[{"id":"semiconductor","title":"半導體製程工藝","titleEn":"Semiconductor Fabrication","category":"semiconductor","summary":"以 20 個模組、520 個學習步驟，拆解晶圓製作、元件、微影、薄膜、蝕刻、互連、量測與製程整合。","summaryEn":"Twenty modules and 520 learning steps explore wafers, devices, lithography, films, etch, interconnects, metrology and integration.","scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學拆解；模組編號是學習順序，製程分支與實際前後關係另有說明。520 步不代表任何廠商的完整量產配方或固定製程數。所有步驟使用明確標示的代表照片；重複使用照片不等於每步專屬實拍。操作為原創概念模擬與工程推理，實驗資料需自行提供或查閱來源。","scopeEn":"Educational subdivisions based on public principles. Module numbers describe learning order; process branches and actual dependencies are identified separately. The 520 steps are not a proprietary manufacturing recipe or universal process count. Every step has a labeled representative photograph; reused images are not step-specific process photography. Activities use original concept simulations and engineering reasoning; measured data must be supplied or obtained from sources.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process","sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-applied-implant","sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop","sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light","scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology","scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization","scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-electroplating","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm","scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models","scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","v3-media-80679a241086"],"diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["基板","隔離","閘極","互連","封裝"],"labelsEn":["Substrate","Isolation","Gate","Interconnect","Package"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"sc-m01","order":1,"title":"製程整合與來料品質","titleEn":"Process integration and incoming quality","description":"建立能連結材料、座標、量測與元件路線的來料證據。26 個操作包含剖面建模與真實量測方法的判讀。","descriptionEn":"Build incoming evidence connecting material, coordinates, metrology and device routes. The 26 operations combine cross-section modeling with interpretation of real measurement methods.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-001","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"建立 CMOS 剖面層序","titleEn":"Build the CMOS cross-section stack","objective":"閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。","objectiveEn":"A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將基板、隔離、井區、閘極與接觸層拖入剖面，標出導電及絕緣區域。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place substrate, isolation, wells, gate and contact layers in a cross-section; mark conducting and insulating regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：介電層遺漏或接觸節點放錯。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Missing dielectric or misassigned contact nodes. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。","checkEn":"A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-001-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。 對應操作：將基板、隔離、井區、閘極與接觸層拖入剖面，標出導電及絕緣區域。","textEn":"A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes. Corresponding operation: Place substrate, isolation, wells, gate and contact layers in a cross-section; mark conducting and insulating regions."},{"id":"sc-001-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：介電層遺漏或接觸節點放錯。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Missing dielectric or misassigned contact nodes."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立 CMOS 剖面層序」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build the CMOS cross-section stack\"?","options":["直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。"],"optionsEn":["Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-002","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"分配光罩圖層","titleEn":"Assign mask layers","objective":"每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把主動區、井區、閘極及接觸的平面圖分開，再疊回同一座標。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Separate active-area, well, gate and contact layouts, then overlay them in one coordinate frame.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：圖層極性、原點或版次混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mixed layer tones, origins or revisions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。","checkEn":"Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-002-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。 對應操作：把主動區、井區、閘極及接觸的平面圖分開，再疊回同一座標。","textEn":"Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin. Corresponding operation: Separate active-area, well, gate and contact layouts, then overlay them in one coordinate frame."},{"id":"sc-002-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：圖層極性、原點或版次混用。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Mixed layer tones, origins or revisions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分配光罩圖層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Assign mask layers\"?","options":["模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。","厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin.","Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-001"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-003","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"辨識製程路線分支","titleEn":"Identify process-route branches","objective":"不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","objectiveEn":"Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：並排平面 CMOS、FinFET 與奈米片剖面，圈出不可直接沿用的幾何。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare planar CMOS, FinFET and nanosheet cross-sections; flag geometry that cannot be transferred unchanged.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把平面尺寸沿用到三維結構。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Planar dimensions carried into three-dimensional structures. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","checkEn":"Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-003-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。 對應操作：並排平面 CMOS、FinFET 與奈米片剖面，圈出不可直接沿用的幾何。","textEn":"Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route. Corresponding operation: Compare planar CMOS, FinFET and nanosheet cross-sections; flag geometry that cannot be transferred unchanged."},{"id":"sc-003-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：把平面尺寸沿用到三維結構。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Planar dimensions carried into three-dimensional structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識製程路線分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify process-route branches\"?","options":["不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。","低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。"],"optionsEn":["Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp.","Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-002"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-004","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"核對基板種類","titleEn":"Verify substrate type","objective":"埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。","objectiveEn":"Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比對塊材矽、磊晶矽與 SOI 的來料截面，選擇與教材路線相符者。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare incoming bulk, epitaxial and SOI wafers and select the substrate matching the exercise route.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：基板產品型號與截面對不上。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Substrate product type mismatches the section. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。","checkEn":"Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-004-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。 對應操作：比對塊材矽、磊晶矽與 SOI 的來料截面，選擇與教材路線相符者。","textEn":"Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness. Corresponding operation: Compare incoming bulk, epitaxial and SOI wafers and select the substrate matching the exercise route."},{"id":"sc-004-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：基板產品型號與截面對不上。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Substrate product type mismatches the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對基板種類」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify substrate type\"?","options":["最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。"],"optionsEn":["The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-003"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-005","order":5,"sequence":5,"title":"比對導電型態","titleEn":"Check conductivity type","objective":"基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。","objectiveEn":"Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用來料證明及示意電性量測判斷 p 型或 n 型，與井區設計交叉核對。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Use the supplier record and schematic electrical measurements to distinguish p-type and n-type material; cross-check the well design.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把導電型態與離子電荷混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Conductivity type confused with ionic charge. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。","checkEn":"Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-005-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。 對應操作：用來料證明及示意電性量測判斷 p 型或 n 型，與井區設計交叉核對。","textEn":"Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions. Corresponding operation: Use the supplier record and schematic electrical measurements to distinguish p-type and n-type material; cross-check the well design."},{"id":"sc-005-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：把導電型態與離子電荷混淆。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Conductivity type confused with ionic charge."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比對導電型態」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check conductivity type\"?","options":["比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。","表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。"],"optionsEn":["The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions.","Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-004"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-006","order":6,"sequence":6,"title":"量測晶圓直徑","titleEn":"Measure wafer diameter","objective":"直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","objectiveEn":"Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在虛擬邊緣掃描圖取多方向直徑，將缺口區排除後檢查圓度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure multiple diameters on an edge-scan map and evaluate roundness while excluding the notch.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：量測跨過缺口或尺度校正錯誤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Measurement crossing the notch or incorrect scale calibration. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","checkEn":"Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-006-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。 對應操作：在虛擬邊緣掃描圖取多方向直徑，將缺口區排除後檢查圓度。","textEn":"Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone. Corresponding operation: Measure multiple diameters on an edge-scan map and evaluate roundness while excluding the notch."},{"id":"sc-006-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：量測跨過缺口或尺度校正錯誤。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Measurement crossing the notch or incorrect scale calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測晶圓直徑」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure wafer diameter\"?","options":["直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。","三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions.","Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-005"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-007","order":7,"sequence":7,"title":"量測總厚度變化","titleEn":"Measure total thickness variation","objective":"厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。","objectiveEn":"Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：從前後表面量測算出局部厚度，製作 TTV 圖並找出極值位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Subtract front and back surface maps to obtain local thickness; map TTV and locate its extrema.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：前後面未對位或彎曲未分離。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unregistered surfaces or unseparated bending. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。","checkEn":"Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-007-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。 對應操作：從前後表面量測算出局部厚度，製作 TTV 圖並找出極值位置。","textEn":"Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow. Corresponding operation: Subtract front and back surface maps to obtain local thickness; map TTV and locate its extrema."},{"id":"sc-007-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：前後面未對位或彎曲未分離。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Unregistered surfaces or unseparated bending."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測總厚度變化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure total thickness variation\"?","options":["粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-006"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-008","order":8,"sequence":8,"title":"區分晶圓彎曲與翹曲","titleEn":"Separate wafer bow from warp","objective":"報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。","objectiveEn":"The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較中心偏移與去除參考平面後的全片形貌，切換支撐條件。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare center deflection with full-wafer shape after reference-plane removal and change the support condition.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：支撐方式不同或參考面不一致。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Changed support conditions or inconsistent reference planes. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。","checkEn":"The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-008-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。 對應操作：比較中心偏移與去除參考平面後的全片形貌，切換支撐條件。","textEn":"The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp. Corresponding operation: Compare center deflection with full-wafer shape after reference-plane removal and change the support condition."},{"id":"sc-008-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：支撐方式不同或參考面不一致。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Changed support conditions or inconsistent reference planes."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「區分晶圓彎曲與翹曲」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate wafer bow from warp\"?","options":["搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。","線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。"],"optionsEn":["Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp.","Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-007"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-009","order":9,"sequence":9,"title":"檢查局部平坦度","titleEn":"Inspect local flatness","objective":"最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","objectiveEn":"The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以曝光場大小的視窗掃描高度圖，比較全片平坦與局部傾斜。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Scan the height map with exposure-field-sized windows and compare global flatness with local slope.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平均化視窗太大而掩蓋局部臺階。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: An averaging window hiding local steps. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","checkEn":"The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-009-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。 對應操作：以曝光場大小的視窗掃描高度圖，比較全片平坦與局部傾斜。","textEn":"The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus. Corresponding operation: Scan the height map with exposure-field-sized windows and compare global flatness with local slope."},{"id":"sc-009-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：平均化視窗太大而掩蓋局部臺階。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: An averaging window hiding local steps."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查局部平坦度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect local flatness\"?","options":["最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。"],"optionsEn":["The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-008"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-010","order":10,"sequence":10,"title":"校核晶向與缺口","titleEn":"Verify crystal orientation and notch","objective":"表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。","objectiveEn":"Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把 X 光晶向報告與缺口方位一起放入晶圓座標，標註表面法向。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place the X-ray orientation report and notch direction in wafer coordinates and label the surface normal.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：表面晶面與晶圓方位標籤互換。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Swapped surface-plane and wafer-azimuth labels. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。","checkEn":"Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-010-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。 對應操作：把 X 光晶向報告與缺口方位一起放入晶圓座標，標註表面法向。","textEn":"Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence. Corresponding operation: Place the X-ray orientation report and notch direction in wafer coordinates and label the surface normal."},{"id":"sc-010-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：表面晶面與晶圓方位標籤互換。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Swapped surface-plane and wafer-azimuth labels."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校核晶向與缺口」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify crystal orientation and notch\"?","options":["模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。"],"optionsEn":["Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-009"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-011","order":11,"sequence":11,"title":"檢查晶圓邊緣輪廓","titleEn":"Inspect wafer edge profile","objective":"夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：放大邊緣截面，標出倒角、崩角與背面磨痕，模擬夾持接觸位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Magnify the edge section, identify bevels, chips and backside grinding marks, and overlay clamp contact locations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：夾持位置與崩角重疊。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Clamping positions overlapping chipped edges. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。","checkEn":"Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-011-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。 對應操作：放大邊緣截面，標出倒角、崩角與背面磨痕，模擬夾持接觸位置。","textEn":"Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions. Corresponding operation: Magnify the edge section, identify bevels, chips and backside grinding marks, and overlay clamp contact locations."},{"id":"sc-011-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：夾持位置與崩角重疊。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Clamping positions overlapping chipped edges."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查晶圓邊緣輪廓」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect wafer edge profile\"?","options":["新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。","低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions.","Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-010"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-012","order":12,"sequence":12,"title":"繪製來料粒子圖","titleEn":"Map incoming particles","objective":"粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","objectiveEn":"Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較明場與散射影像，按大小級距標記粒子並保留檢出門檻。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare bright-field and scattering images, bin particles by size and retain the detection threshold.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：粒子門檻、有效面積或照明改變。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Changed particle threshold, inspected area or illumination. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","checkEn":"Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-012-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。 對應操作：比較明場與散射影像，按大小級距標記粒子並保留檢出門檻。","textEn":"Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison. Corresponding operation: Compare bright-field and scattering images, bin particles by size and retain the detection threshold."},{"id":"sc-012-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：粒子門檻、有效面積或照明改變。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Changed particle threshold, inspected area or illumination."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「繪製來料粒子圖」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Map incoming particles\"?","options":["粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。"],"optionsEn":["Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-011"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-013","order":13,"sequence":13,"title":"區分刮傷與粒子","titleEn":"Distinguish scratches from particles","objective":"線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。","objectiveEn":"Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿缺陷長軸查看連續影像，再與孤立亮點比對。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Follow the major axis of a defect across images and compare it with isolated bright spots.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：線狀缺陷被切成多個粒子。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: A line defect split into several particle detections. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。","checkEn":"Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-013-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。 對應操作：沿缺陷長軸查看連續影像，再與孤立亮點比對。","textEn":"Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology. Corresponding operation: Follow the major axis of a defect across images and compare it with isolated bright spots."},{"id":"sc-013-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：線狀缺陷被切成多個粒子。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: A line defect split into several particle detections."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「區分刮傷與粒子」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Distinguish scratches from particles\"?","options":["比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。"],"optionsEn":["The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-012"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-014","order":14,"sequence":14,"title":"檢查表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughness","objective":"粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","objectiveEn":"Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同掃描尺度的 AFM 高度圖，去除傾斜後再估算粗糙度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare AFM maps at different scan sizes and estimate roughness after tilt removal.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：掃描尺度或傾斜去除方式不同。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Different scan scales or tilt-removal methods. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","checkEn":"Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-014-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。 對應操作：比較不同掃描尺度的 AFM 高度圖，去除傾斜後再估算粗糙度。","textEn":"Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method. Corresponding operation: Compare AFM maps at different scan sizes and estimate roughness after tilt removal."},{"id":"sc-014-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：掃描尺度或傾斜去除方式不同。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Different scan scales or tilt-removal methods."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查表面粗糙度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect surface roughness\"?","options":["閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。","粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。","三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。"],"optionsEn":["A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes.","Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method.","Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：粗糙度數值同時附掃描範圍與去背景方法。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Roughness is accompanied by scan area and background-removal method. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-013"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-015","order":15,"sequence":15,"title":"擬合原生氧化層","titleEn":"Fit native oxide thickness","objective":"模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","objectiveEn":"Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對光學量測分別使用裸矽及矽加氧化層模型，比較殘差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Fit optical data with bare-silicon and silicon-plus-oxide models and compare residuals.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：光學模型簡化過度或參數相關。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Oversimplified optical model or correlated parameters. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","checkEn":"Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-015-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。 對應操作：對光學量測分別使用裸矽及矽加氧化層模型，比較殘差。","textEn":"Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily. Corresponding operation: Fit optical data with bare-silicon and silicon-plus-oxide models and compare residuals."},{"id":"sc-015-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：光學模型簡化過度或參數相關。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Oversimplified optical model or correlated parameters."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「擬合原生氧化層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Fit native oxide thickness\"?","options":["模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。","晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily.","Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：模型選擇有殘差支持，薄膜厚度與折射率不被任意互換。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residuals support the model choice; thickness and refractive index are not exchanged arbitrarily. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-014"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-016","order":16,"sequence":16,"title":"檢查表面金屬污染","titleEn":"Inspect surface metal contamination","objective":"低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。","objectiveEn":"Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比對表面分析空白樣與來料樣訊號，把背景和元素峰分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare a surface-analysis blank with the incoming sample and separate background from elemental peaks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：分析空白污染或量測能力不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Contaminated blanks or insufficient measurement capability. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。","checkEn":"Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-016-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。 對應操作：比對表面分析空白樣與來料樣訊號，把背景和元素峰分開。","textEn":"Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination. Corresponding operation: Compare a surface-analysis blank with the incoming sample and separate background from elemental peaks."},{"id":"sc-016-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：分析空白污染或量測能力不足。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Contaminated blanks or insufficient measurement capability."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查表面金屬污染」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect surface metal contamination\"?","options":["搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。"],"optionsEn":["Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：低於定量能力的結果標示為未能定量，未宣稱絕對零污染。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Signals below quantification capability are reported as unquantified, not absolute zero contamination. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-015"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-017","order":17,"sequence":17,"title":"映射晶圓電阻率","titleEn":"Map wafer resistivity","objective":"電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","objectiveEn":"Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在模擬四點探針地圖上比較中心與邊緣，檢查厚度修正。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare center and edge values on a simulated four-point-probe map and check thickness corrections.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：厚度修正、邊緣修正或接觸失效。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Thickness corrections, edge effects or bad contacts. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","checkEn":"Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-017-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。 對應操作：在模擬四點探針地圖上比較中心與邊緣，檢查厚度修正。","textEn":"Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented. Corresponding operation: Compare center and edge values on a simulated four-point-probe map and check thickness corrections."},{"id":"sc-017-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：厚度修正、邊緣修正或接觸失效。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Thickness corrections, edge effects or bad contacts."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「映射晶圓電阻率」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Map wafer resistivity\"?","options":["埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。","電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。","每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。"],"optionsEn":["Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness.","Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented.","Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：電阻率與片電阻分清，邊界修正及接觸異常另列。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Resistivity is distinguished from sheet resistance; edge corrections and contact artifacts are documented. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-016"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-018","order":18,"sequence":18,"title":"評估磊晶厚度","titleEn":"Evaluate epitaxial thickness","objective":"比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","objectiveEn":"The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將磊晶厚度量測與基板剖面對齊，查找徑向不均勻。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Align epitaxial thickness measurements with the substrate cross-section and identify radial nonuniformity.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把總厚度當作磊晶厚度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Total thickness mistaken for epitaxial thickness. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","checkEn":"The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-018-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。 對應操作：將磊晶厚度量測與基板剖面對齊，查找徑向不均勻。","textEn":"The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness. Corresponding operation: Align epitaxial thickness measurements with the substrate cross-section and identify radial nonuniformity."},{"id":"sc-018-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：把總厚度當作磊晶厚度。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Total thickness mistaken for epitaxial thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估磊晶厚度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate epitaxial thickness\"?","options":["比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。","同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。"],"optionsEn":["The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness.","Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：比較的是磊晶層厚度，非整片晶圓總厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The comparison concerns epitaxial-layer thickness rather than total wafer thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-017"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-019","order":19,"sequence":19,"title":"檢查 SOI 埋氧層","titleEn":"Inspect buried oxide in SOI","objective":"三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。","objectiveEn":"Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在 SOI 分支讀取頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓的獨立量測。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. In the SOI branch, inspect separate measurements for top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：頂矽與埋氧光學參數互相補償。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Compensating optical parameters for top silicon and buried oxide. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。","checkEn":"Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-019-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。 對應操作：在 SOI 分支讀取頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓的獨立量測。","textEn":"Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately. Corresponding operation: In the SOI branch, inspect separate measurements for top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer."},{"id":"sc-019-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：頂矽與埋氧光學參數互相補償。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Compensating optical parameters for top silicon and buried oxide."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查 SOI 埋氧層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect buried oxide in SOI\"?","options":["新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","直徑變化與局部缺口分開記錄，沒有只採單一方向。","三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","Diameter variation is reported separately from the notch rather than from one direction alone.","Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：三層厚度各有量測依據，絕緣層連續性另行檢查。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Each layer has measurement evidence and oxide continuity is evaluated separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-018"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-020","order":20,"sequence":20,"title":"分類晶體缺陷","titleEn":"Classify crystal defects","objective":"晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","objectiveEn":"Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較點狀、線狀及堆疊缺陷示意，追蹤其與表面缺陷圖的關係。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare point, line and stacking-defect representations and relate them to the surface-defect map.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：外來粒子與內部晶體缺陷混類。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: External particles mixed with crystal defects. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","checkEn":"Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-020-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。 對應操作：比較點狀、線狀及堆疊缺陷示意，追蹤其與表面缺陷圖的關係。","textEn":"Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles. Corresponding operation: Compare point, line and stacking-defect representations and relate them to the surface-defect map."},{"id":"sc-020-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：外來粒子與內部晶體缺陷混類。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: External particles mixed with crystal defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分類晶體缺陷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Classify crystal defects\"?","options":["厚度差使用同一座標及單位，未混入整片彎曲。","晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。","監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness differences use consistent coordinates and units without conflating whole-wafer bow.","Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles.","Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：晶格缺陷與外來粒子未合併計數。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Lattice defects are not pooled with external particles. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-019"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-021","order":21,"sequence":21,"title":"建立潔淨搬運接觸面","titleEn":"Define clean handling contacts","objective":"搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","objectiveEn":"Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在搬運模型上標註吸盤、邊緣支撐與感測位置，查看與有效區的交疊。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Mark chuck, edge-support and sensor positions on the handling model and check overlap with the active surface.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：搬運模型未標出實際接觸面。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Handling model omits actual contact surfaces. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","checkEn":"Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-021-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。 對應操作：在搬運模型上標註吸盤、邊緣支撐與感測位置，查看與有效區的交疊。","textEn":"Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas. Corresponding operation: Mark chuck, edge-support and sensor positions on the handling model and check overlap with the active surface."},{"id":"sc-021-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：搬運模型未標出實際接觸面。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Handling model omits actual contact surfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立潔淨搬運接觸面」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Define clean handling contacts\"?","options":["搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。","不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","報告說明支撐方式與參考面，不把 bow 和 warp 當同一量。"],"optionsEn":["Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas.","Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","The report states support conditions and reference planes and distinguishes bow from warp."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：搬運接觸面與產品正面敏感區明確分離。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Handling contact surfaces are explicitly separated from sensitive product-face areas. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-020"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-022","order":22,"sequence":22,"title":"比對 FOUP 槽位圖","titleEn":"Reconcile the FOUP slot map","objective":"每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。","objectiveEn":"Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把晶圓 ID 與槽位讀值配對，模擬一次換槽後重新核對。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Match wafer IDs to slot readings and reconcile the map after a simulated slot change.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：換槽後的 ID 與位置未更新。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wafer IDs and positions not updated after slot changes. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。","checkEn":"Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-022-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。 對應操作：把晶圓 ID 與槽位讀值配對，模擬一次換槽後重新核對。","textEn":"Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs. Corresponding operation: Match wafer IDs to slot readings and reconcile the map after a simulated slot change."},{"id":"sc-022-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：換槽後的 ID 與位置未更新。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Wafer IDs and positions not updated after slot changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比對 FOUP 槽位圖」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Reconcile the FOUP slot map\"?","options":["閘極與通道之間保留介電層，接觸孔只連接指定節點。","最差曝光場被保留，平均值不掩蓋局部失焦區。","每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。"],"optionsEn":["A dielectric separates gate and channel; contacts connect only their assigned nodes.","The worst exposure field is retained; averaging does not hide local defocus.","Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：每片晶圓有唯一位置，空槽不被填成缺失 ID。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Each wafer has one unique location; empty slots are not replaced with missing IDs. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-021"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-023","order":23,"sequence":23,"title":"檢查量測重複性","titleEn":"Check measurement repeatability","objective":"同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","objectiveEn":"Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對同一來料點重複讀值，將儀器散布與晶圓位置差分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Repeat measurements at one incoming location and separate instrument scatter from spatial variation.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：空間變異混入同點重複測試。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Spatial variation included in same-point repeats. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","checkEn":"Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-023-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。 對應操作：對同一來料點重複讀值，將儀器散布與晶圓位置差分開。","textEn":"Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics. Corresponding operation: Repeat measurements at one incoming location and separate instrument scatter from spatial variation."},{"id":"sc-023-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：空間變異混入同點重複測試。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Spatial variation included in same-point repeats."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查量測重複性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check measurement repeatability\"?","options":["表面晶面與平面內方向分開，缺口不被當作完整晶向證據。","同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。","每一圖層的用途、極性與參考原點可追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Surface plane and in-plane direction are distinguished; the notch alone is not treated as complete orientation evidence.","Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics.","Every layer has a traceable purpose, tone and reference origin."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：同點重複與異點變化用不同統計量表示。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Same-point repeatability and between-point variation use separate statistics. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-022"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-024","order":24,"sequence":24,"title":"建立前後測基準對位","titleEn":"Register before-and-after baselines","objective":"新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","objectiveEn":"Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以缺口及固定測點對準來料圖與後續清洗圖，再比較新增缺陷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Register incoming and post-clean maps using the notch and fixed sites before comparing added defects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：座標方向、缺口定位或門檻不一致。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Inconsistent axes, notch registration or thresholds. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","checkEn":"Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-024-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。 對應操作：以缺口及固定測點對準來料圖與後續清洗圖，再比較新增缺陷。","textEn":"Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction. Corresponding operation: Register incoming and post-clean maps using the notch and fixed sites before comparing added defects."},{"id":"sc-024-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：座標方向、缺口定位或門檻不一致。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Inconsistent axes, notch registration or thresholds."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立前後測基準對位」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Register before-and-after baselines\"?","options":["新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。","不同路線的隔離高度與閘極包覆方式分別標示。","夾持點不落在崩角區，邊緣缺陷有位置紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction.","Isolation height and gate enclosure are labeled separately for each route.","Clamp contacts avoid chipped regions and edge defects have recorded positions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：新增缺陷以相同位置與門檻判定，而非總數直接相減。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Added defects are determined with matching locations and thresholds, not simple total-count subtraction. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-023"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-025","order":25,"sequence":25,"title":"分配監控晶圓","titleEn":"Allocate monitor wafers","objective":"監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。","objectiveEn":"Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將破壞性截面、表面檢測及產品晶圓分開，安排可追溯的陪片。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Separate destructive cross-sections, surface tests and product wafers and assign traceable monitor wafers.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：監控片與產品片熱歷史不同。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Monitor and product wafers have different thermal histories. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。","checkEn":"Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-025-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。 對應操作：將破壞性截面、表面檢測及產品晶圓分開，安排可追溯的陪片。","textEn":"Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed. Corresponding operation: Separate destructive cross-sections, surface tests and product wafers and assign traceable monitor wafers."},{"id":"sc-025-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：監控片與產品片熱歷史不同。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Monitor and product wafers have different thermal histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分配監控晶圓」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Allocate monitor wafers\"?","options":["埋氧層或磊晶層沒有被誤當成裸矽厚度。","粒子數附帶有效面積及門檻，不能脫離偵測條件比較。","監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。"],"optionsEn":["Buried oxide and epitaxial layers are not mistaken for bulk silicon thickness.","Particle counts include inspected area and threshold, enabling valid comparison.","Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：監控片的膜層及熱歷史差異被列出。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Differences in monitor-film stacks and thermal history are disclosed. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-024"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-026","order":26,"sequence":26,"title":"判定來料放行","titleEn":"Decide incoming-lot disposition","objective":"不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","objectiveEn":"Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把尺寸、污染與電性證據放在同一批次卡，比較示範規格內與規格外樣本。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine dimensional, contamination and electrical evidence on one lot card and compare examples inside and outside the exercise specification.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：缺測項被默認為合格。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Missing evidence silently treated as passing. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","checkEn":"Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-026-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。 對應操作：把尺寸、污染與電性證據放在同一批次卡，比較示範規格內與規格外樣本。","textEn":"Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes. Corresponding operation: Combine dimensional, contamination and electrical evidence on one lot card and compare examples inside and outside the exercise specification."},{"id":"sc-026-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"量測數字只有在量測位置、參考面、單位與方法一致時才可比較；示範驗收界線由課程情境提供，不是通用產業規格。 本步特別排查：缺測項被默認為合格。","textEn":"Measurements are comparable only with consistent locations, reference planes, units and methods. Exercise acceptance limits are scenario inputs, not universal industry specifications. Specifically examine: Missing evidence silently treated as passing."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判定來料放行」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Decide incoming-lot disposition\"?","options":["線狀刮傷與可移除粒子的分類依形貌證據完成。","不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。","基板導電型態與井區反向接面的安排相符。"],"optionsEn":["Scratch and removable-particle classes are supported by morphology.","Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes.","Substrate conductivity is consistent with the intended reverse-biased well junctions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不合格項有隔離與複測依據，未知值不當成通過。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Nonconformities have segregation and retest evidence; unknown values do not count as passes. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-025"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m02","order":2,"title":"晶體、晶圓製備與清洗","titleEn":"Crystal growth, wafer preparation and cleaning","description":"從晶棒生長到潔淨表面交接，分開材料去除、晶格品質、污染移除與再污染。","descriptionEn":"Follow ingot growth through clean-surface handoff while separating stock removal, crystal quality, decontamination and recontamination.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-027","order":1,"sequence":27,"title":"辨識多晶矽原料品質","titleEn":"Inspect polysilicon feedstock quality","objective":"原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","objectiveEn":"Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較原料純度證明與雜質譜，找出可能影響電性或晶體生長的元素。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare feedstock certificates and impurity spectra to identify species affecting electrical properties or crystal growth.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：總純度標示掩蓋關鍵雜質。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Bulk purity conceals critical impurities. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","checkEn":"Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-027-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。 對應操作：比較原料純度證明與雜質譜，找出可能影響電性或晶體生長的元素。","textEn":"Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately. Corresponding operation: Compare feedstock certificates and impurity spectra to identify species affecting electrical properties or crystal growth."},{"id":"sc-027-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：總純度標示掩蓋關鍵雜質。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Bulk purity conceals critical impurities."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識多晶矽原料品質」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect polysilicon feedstock quality\"?","options":["原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。","兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent.","Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-026"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-028","order":2,"sequence":28,"title":"配置直拉晶體熱場","titleEn":"Configure the CZ thermal field","objective":"界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。","objectiveEn":"Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在熔體剖面調整示意加熱區，觀察固液界面形狀的變化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Adjust schematic heating zones in a melt cross-section and observe the solid-liquid interface.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：局部熱梯度被平均溫度遮蔽。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local gradients hidden by average temperature. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。","checkEn":"Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-028-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。 對應操作：在熔體剖面調整示意加熱區，觀察固液界面形狀的變化。","textEn":"Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together. Corresponding operation: Adjust schematic heating zones in a melt cross-section and observe the solid-liquid interface."},{"id":"sc-028-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：局部熱梯度被平均溫度遮蔽。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Local gradients hidden by average temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置直拉晶體熱場」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure the CZ thermal field\"?","options":["軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-027"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-029","order":3,"sequence":29,"title":"放置籽晶晶向","titleEn":"Orient the seed crystal","objective":"晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。","objectiveEn":"The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：旋轉籽晶晶格，使目標成長方向與拉引軸對準。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Rotate the seed lattice to align the intended growth direction with the pulling axis.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：籽晶方向與拉引軸誤配。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Seed direction mismatched to pulling axis. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。","checkEn":"The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-029-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。 對應操作：旋轉籽晶晶格，使目標成長方向與拉引軸對準。","textEn":"The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction. Corresponding operation: Rotate the seed lattice to align the intended growth direction with the pulling axis."},{"id":"sc-029-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：籽晶方向與拉引軸誤配。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Seed direction mismatched to pulling axis."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「放置籽晶晶向」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Orient the seed crystal\"?","options":["被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。","低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。"],"optionsEn":["The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction.","The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-028"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-030","order":4,"sequence":30,"title":"模擬縮頸排除位錯","titleEn":"Model necking for dislocation control","objective":"判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","objectiveEn":"The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較有縮頸與無縮頸的位錯路徑示意，追蹤位錯是否延續至肩部。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare dislocation paths with and without necking and track their propagation toward the shoulder.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：僅用外徑判斷位錯是否消失。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Using diameter alone to judge dislocation elimination. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","checkEn":"The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-030-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。 對應操作：比較有縮頸與無縮頸的位錯路徑示意，追蹤位錯是否延續至肩部。","textEn":"The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material. Corresponding operation: Compare dislocation paths with and without necking and track their propagation toward the shoulder."},{"id":"sc-030-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：僅用外徑判斷位錯是否消失。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Using diameter alone to judge dislocation elimination."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬縮頸排除位錯」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model necking for dislocation control\"?","options":["判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。","表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。"],"optionsEn":["The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature.","Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-029"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-031","order":5,"sequence":31,"title":"控制晶肩展開","titleEn":"Control shoulder growth","objective":"肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。","objectiveEn":"The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：調整晶肩展開形狀，檢查過渡處的熱梯度與直徑連續性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Adjust the shoulder profile and inspect thermal gradients and diameter continuity at the transition.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：展肩變化過快或熱場不連續。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Abrupt shoulder growth or discontinuous thermal field. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。","checkEn":"The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-031-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。 對應操作：調整晶肩展開形狀，檢查過渡處的熱梯度與直徑連續性。","textEn":"The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity. Corresponding operation: Adjust the shoulder profile and inspect thermal gradients and diameter continuity at the transition."},{"id":"sc-031-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：展肩變化過快或熱場不連續。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Abrupt shoulder growth or discontinuous thermal field."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制晶肩展開」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control shoulder growth\"?","options":["修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。"],"optionsEn":["Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-030"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-032","order":6,"sequence":32,"title":"維持晶棒等徑段","titleEn":"Maintain constant-diameter growth","objective":"直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。","objectiveEn":"The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較拉速變化與直徑監測曲線，辨識延遲控制造成的振盪。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare pull-rate changes with diameter traces and identify oscillations caused by control delay.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：回授延遲或直徑感測雜訊。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Feedback delay or noisy diameter sensing. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。","checkEn":"The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-032-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。 對應操作：比較拉速變化與直徑監測曲線，辨識延遲控制造成的振盪。","textEn":"The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent. Corresponding operation: Compare pull-rate changes with diameter traces and identify oscillations caused by control delay."},{"id":"sc-032-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：回授延遲或直徑感測雜訊。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Feedback delay or noisy diameter sensing."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「維持晶棒等徑段」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Maintain constant-diameter growth\"?","options":["接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。","缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent.","Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-031"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-033","order":7,"sequence":33,"title":"追蹤摻雜偏析","titleEn":"Track dopant segregation","objective":"軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","objectiveEn":"Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿晶棒長度繪出示意摻雜濃度，與熔體剩餘比例比較。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Plot schematic dopant concentration along the ingot and compare it with remaining melt fraction.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略熔體耗用及偏析。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Ignored melt consumption and segregation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","checkEn":"Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-033-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。 對應操作：沿晶棒長度繪出示意摻雜濃度，與熔體剩餘比例比較。","textEn":"Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption. Corresponding operation: Plot schematic dopant concentration along the ingot and compare it with remaining melt fraction."},{"id":"sc-033-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：忽略熔體耗用及偏析。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Ignored melt consumption and segregation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「追蹤摻雜偏析」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Track dopant segregation\"?","options":["軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。","移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness.","Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-032"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-034","order":8,"sequence":34,"title":"比較 CZ 與浮區路線","titleEn":"Compare CZ and float-zone routes","objective":"低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。","objectiveEn":"The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：並排坩堝拉晶與移動熔區模型，標出容器接觸與供料途徑。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare crucible pulling with a moving molten zone and mark container contact and feed paths.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：坩堝接觸差異被遺漏。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Omitted differences in crucible contact. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。","checkEn":"The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-034-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。 對應操作：並排坩堝拉晶與移動熔區模型，標出容器接觸與供料途徑。","textEn":"The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ. Corresponding operation: Compare crucible pulling with a moving molten zone and mark container contact and feed paths."},{"id":"sc-034-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：坩堝接觸差異被遺漏。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Omitted differences in crucible contact."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較 CZ 與浮區路線」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare CZ and float-zone routes\"?","options":["切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。"],"optionsEn":["Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-033"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-035","order":9,"sequence":35,"title":"模擬磁場拉晶作用","titleEn":"Model magnetic CZ effects","objective":"磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。","objectiveEn":"Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：切換磁場作用的熔體流動示意，比較混合強度及熱場穩定性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Toggle magnetic-field effects in the melt-flow model and compare mixing and thermal stability.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把流動控制誤當單純溫度控制。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Flow control mistaken for temperature adjustment. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。","checkEn":"Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-035-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。 對應操作：切換磁場作用的熔體流動示意，比較混合強度及熱場穩定性。","textEn":"Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature. Corresponding operation: Toggle magnetic-field effects in the melt-flow model and compare mixing and thermal stability."},{"id":"sc-035-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：把流動控制誤當單純溫度控制。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Flow control mistaken for temperature adjustment."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬磁場拉晶作用」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model magnetic CZ effects\"?","options":["表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。","兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature.","Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-034"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-036","order":10,"sequence":36,"title":"修整晶棒外徑","titleEn":"Grind the ingot diameter","objective":"修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","objectiveEn":"Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用圓柱量測圖設定修整包絡，估算移除層與剩餘可用半徑。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Set a grinding envelope from cylindrical metrology and estimate removed stock and usable radius.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：偏心修磨造成同軸性不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Eccentric grinding compromises coaxiality. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","checkEn":"Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-036-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。 對應操作：用圓柱量測圖設定修整包絡，估算移除層與剩餘可用半徑。","textEn":"Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately. Corresponding operation: Set a grinding envelope from cylindrical metrology and estimate removed stock and usable radius."},{"id":"sc-036-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：偏心修磨造成同軸性不足。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Eccentric grinding compromises coaxiality."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「修整晶棒外徑」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Grind the ingot diameter\"?","options":["修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。"],"optionsEn":["Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-035"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-037","order":11,"sequence":37,"title":"加工定位缺口","titleEn":"Machine the orientation notch","objective":"缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。","objectiveEn":"Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把缺口放到指定晶向參考，檢查缺口深度與邊緣裂紋示意。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place the notch relative to the crystallographic reference and inspect notch depth and edge-crack indicators.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：缺口未依晶向校核或引入裂紋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unverified notch orientation or introduced cracks. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。","checkEn":"Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-037-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。 對應操作：把缺口放到指定晶向參考，檢查缺口深度與邊緣裂紋示意。","textEn":"Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated. Corresponding operation: Place the notch relative to the crystallographic reference and inspect notch depth and edge-crack indicators."},{"id":"sc-037-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：缺口未依晶向校核或引入裂紋。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Unverified notch orientation or introduced cracks."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「加工定位缺口」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Machine the orientation notch\"?","options":["被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-036"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-038","order":12,"sequence":38,"title":"規劃晶棒切片","titleEn":"Plan ingot slicing","objective":"切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。","objectiveEn":"Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在晶棒模型排列切割面，將鋸縫損耗、成品厚度與後續研磨量分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place slicing planes in the ingot model and separate kerf loss, final thickness and finishing allowance.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忘記鋸縫及精加工餘量。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Omitted kerf and finishing allowances. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。","checkEn":"Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-038-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。 對應操作：在晶棒模型排列切割面，將鋸縫損耗、成品厚度與後續研磨量分開。","textEn":"Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness. Corresponding operation: Place slicing planes in the ingot model and separate kerf loss, final thickness and finishing allowance."},{"id":"sc-038-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：忘記鋸縫及精加工餘量。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Omitted kerf and finishing allowances."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「規劃晶棒切片」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Plan ingot slicing\"?","options":["新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。","表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness.","Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-037"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-039","order":13,"sequence":39,"title":"判讀線鋸切痕","titleEn":"Interpret wire-saw marks","objective":"切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","objectiveEn":"Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比切痕方向與線鋸移動軌跡，標記局部週期紋路。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare saw-mark direction with wire motion and mark local periodic patterns.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：線鋸振動與進給痕混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wire vibration confused with feed marks. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","checkEn":"Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-039-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。 對應操作：對比切痕方向與線鋸移動軌跡，標記局部週期紋路。","textEn":"Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion. Corresponding operation: Compare saw-mark direction with wire motion and mark local periodic patterns."},{"id":"sc-039-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：線鋸振動與進給痕混淆。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Wire vibration confused with feed marks."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判讀線鋸切痕」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Interpret wire-saw marks\"?","options":["切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。"],"optionsEn":["Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-038"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-040","order":14,"sequence":40,"title":"改善切片平行度","titleEn":"Improve slice parallelism","objective":"兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。","objectiveEn":"Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較雙面研磨前後的厚度圖，調整示意壓力分布。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thickness maps before and after double-sided lapping and adjust the schematic pressure distribution.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：局部移除不均造成楔形厚度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Uneven removal creates a wedge-shaped thickness profile. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。","checkEn":"Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-040-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。 對應操作：比較雙面研磨前後的厚度圖，調整示意壓力分布。","textEn":"Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains. Corresponding operation: Compare thickness maps before and after double-sided lapping and adjust the schematic pressure distribution."},{"id":"sc-040-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：局部移除不均造成楔形厚度。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Uneven removal creates a wedge-shaped thickness profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「改善切片平行度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Improve slice parallelism\"?","options":["接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：兩面平行度改善，同時保留足夠成品厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Parallelism improves while sufficient final thickness remains. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-039"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-041","order":15,"sequence":41,"title":"修整晶圓倒角","titleEn":"Shape wafer edge bevels","objective":"倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","objectiveEn":"The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較尖角及圓滑倒角的應力集中圖，將倒角延伸至完整圓周。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare stress concentrations at sharp and rounded edges and extend the bevel around the circumference.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：倒角不連續或邊緣過度移除。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Discontinuous bevel or excessive edge removal. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","checkEn":"The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-041-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。 對應操作：比較尖角及圓滑倒角的應力集中圖，將倒角延伸至完整圓周。","textEn":"The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area. Corresponding operation: Compare stress concentrations at sharp and rounded edges and extend the bevel around the circumference."},{"id":"sc-041-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：倒角不連續或邊緣過度移除。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Discontinuous bevel or excessive edge removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「修整晶圓倒角」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Shape wafer edge bevels\"?","options":["界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。","倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。","移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together.","The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area.","Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：倒角連續且不侵入規劃有效區。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The bevel is continuous and does not invade the planned usable area. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-040"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-042","order":16,"sequence":42,"title":"去除切割損傷層","titleEn":"Remove slicing damage","objective":"被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","objectiveEn":"The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在示意截面逐步移除表層，觀察微裂紋深度與剩餘基板。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Remove the surface layer incrementally in a schematic section and track microcrack depth and remaining substrate.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：可見切痕消失但次表面損傷仍在。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Visible marks removed while subsurface damage remains. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","checkEn":"The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-042-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。 對應操作：在示意截面逐步移除表層，觀察微裂紋深度與剩餘基板。","textEn":"The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks. Corresponding operation: Remove the surface layer incrementally in a schematic section and track microcrack depth and remaining substrate."},{"id":"sc-042-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：可見切痕消失但次表面損傷仍在。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Visible marks removed while subsurface damage remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「去除切割損傷層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove slicing damage\"?","options":["被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。","污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。"],"optionsEn":["The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks.","Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：被移除範圍涵蓋示範損傷層，未僅消除可見切痕。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The removal covers the demonstrated damage layer rather than only visible saw marks. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-041"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-043","order":17,"sequence":43,"title":"執行晶圓精拋模型","titleEn":"Model final wafer polishing","objective":"表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。","objectiveEn":"Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比不同局部接觸壓力下的表面高點移除，觀察微刮傷和邊緣塌陷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare high-point removal under different local contact pressures and inspect microscratches and edge roll-off.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：壓力集中造成微刮傷或邊緣塌陷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Pressure concentration causes scratches or edge roll-off. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。","checkEn":"Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-043-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。 對應操作：對比不同局部接觸壓力下的表面高點移除，觀察微刮傷和邊緣塌陷。","textEn":"Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape. Corresponding operation: Compare high-point removal under different local contact pressures and inspect microscratches and edge roll-off."},{"id":"sc-043-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：壓力集中造成微刮傷或邊緣塌陷。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Pressure concentration causes scratches or edge roll-off."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「執行晶圓精拋模型」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model final wafer polishing\"?","options":["表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。"],"optionsEn":["The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面改善兼顧粗糙度與邊緣形貌。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Surface improvement accounts for both roughness and edge shape. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-042"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-044","order":18,"sequence":44,"title":"分離有機與無機污染","titleEn":"Separate organic and inorganic contamination","objective":"清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","objectiveEn":"The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將示意分析峰分配到有機物、金屬與粒子三類，再選對應清洗功能。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Sort schematic analytical peaks into organic, metallic and particulate contamination before selecting a cleaning function.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：清洗功能與污染類型不符。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Cleaning function mismatches contamination class. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","checkEn":"The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-044-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。 對應操作：將示意分析峰分配到有機物、金屬與粒子三類，再選對應清洗功能。","textEn":"The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything. Corresponding operation: Sort schematic analytical peaks into organic, metallic and particulate contamination before selecting a cleaning function."},{"id":"sc-044-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：清洗功能與污染類型不符。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Cleaning function mismatches contamination class."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分離有機與無機污染」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate organic and inorganic contamination\"?","options":["肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。","清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。","殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。"],"optionsEn":["The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity.","The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything.","Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：清洗選擇針對污染類別，不以單一程序宣稱去除全部。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The cleaning choice targets the contamination class without claiming one process removes everything. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-043"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-045","order":19,"sequence":45,"title":"檢查清洗潤濕性","titleEn":"Inspect cleaning wettability","objective":"接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","objectiveEn":"Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同表面狀態的接觸角圖，檢查液體是否覆蓋圖案凹處。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare contact-angle images for different surface states and inspect wetting inside patterned recesses.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把潤濕性當作全面潔淨指標。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wettability used as a complete cleanliness proxy. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","checkEn":"Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-045-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。 對應操作：比較不同表面狀態的接觸角圖，檢查液體是否覆蓋圖案凹處。","textEn":"Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination. Corresponding operation: Compare contact-angle images for different surface states and inspect wetting inside patterned recesses."},{"id":"sc-045-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：把潤濕性當作全面潔淨指標。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Wettability used as a complete cleanliness proxy."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查清洗潤濕性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect cleaning wettability\"?","options":["接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。","乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","直徑偏差與控制反應的先後順序相符。"],"optionsEn":["Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination.","Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","The timing of diameter errors and control responses is consistent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：接觸角與覆蓋行為一起判讀，未將小角度當成所有污染已清除。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Contact angle and coverage are interpreted together rather than as proof of complete decontamination. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-044"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-046","order":20,"sequence":46,"title":"模擬粒子去除","titleEn":"Model particle removal","objective":"移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。","objectiveEn":"Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在虛擬清洗前後定位相同粒子，分辨脫附、搬移與新沉積。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Locate identical particles before and after virtual cleaning and distinguish detachment, relocation and new deposition.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：粒子搬移或再沉積誤算為去除。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Particle relocation or redeposition counted as removal. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。","checkEn":"Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-046-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。 對應操作：在虛擬清洗前後定位相同粒子，分辨脫附、搬移與新沉積。","textEn":"Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately. Corresponding operation: Locate identical particles before and after virtual cleaning and distinguish detachment, relocation and new deposition."},{"id":"sc-046-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：粒子搬移或再沉積誤算為去除。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Particle relocation or redeposition counted as removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬粒子去除」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model particle removal\"?","options":["新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","軸向不均勻以偏析及熔體演變解釋，而非假設全棒同值。","移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","Axial variation is interpreted through segregation and melt evolution rather than a uniform-ingot assumption.","Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：移走的粒子與重新落回的粒子分開追蹤。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Removed particles and redeposited particles are tracked separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-045"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-047","order":21,"sequence":47,"title":"比較金屬污染清除","titleEn":"Compare metallic-contamination removal","objective":"污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","objectiveEn":"Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對照表面分析的空白、處理前與處理後資料，檢查背景是否漂移。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare blank, pre-treatment and post-treatment surface analyses and inspect background drift.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：空白或背景漂移造成假下降。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Blank or background drift creates a false decrease. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","checkEn":"Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-047-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。 對應操作：對照表面分析的空白、處理前與處理後資料，檢查背景是否漂移。","textEn":"Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions. Corresponding operation: Compare blank, pre-treatment and post-treatment surface analyses and inspect background drift."},{"id":"sc-047-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：空白或背景漂移造成假下降。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Blank or background drift creates a false decrease."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較金屬污染清除」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare metallic-contamination removal\"?","options":["低氧的浮區特徵不被推廣成所有應用都優於 CZ。","污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。","交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。"],"optionsEn":["The low-oxygen character of float-zone growth is not generalized into universal superiority over CZ.","Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions.","Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：污染降低有同一分析條件下的證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Contamination reduction is supported under consistent analytical conditions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-046"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-048","order":22,"sequence":48,"title":"處理原生氧化層分支","titleEn":"Handle native-oxide removal branches","objective":"表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","objectiveEn":"The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比需要親水氧化表面與需要暴露矽表面的後續製程，選擇保留或移除氧化層。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare downstream processes requiring oxidized hydrophilic surfaces or exposed silicon and choose oxide retention or removal.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未考慮下游要求的表面終態。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Downstream surface-state requirements ignored. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","checkEn":"The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-048-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。 對應操作：對比需要親水氧化表面與需要暴露矽表面的後續製程，選擇保留或移除氧化層。","textEn":"The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal. Corresponding operation: Compare downstream processes requiring oxidized hydrophilic surfaces or exposed silicon and choose oxide retention or removal."},{"id":"sc-048-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：未考慮下游要求的表面終態。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Downstream surface-state requirements ignored."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「處理原生氧化層分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handle native-oxide removal branches\"?","options":["表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。","原料總純度與各關鍵金屬含量分開檢核。","磁場改變流動的效果與單纯降低溫度區分。"],"optionsEn":["The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal.","Bulk purity and critical metal concentrations are checked separately.","Magnetic modification of flow is distinguished from merely lowering temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面終態由下一製程需求決定，沒有一律去氧化。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The final surface state follows the next process requirement rather than universal oxide removal. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-047"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-049","order":23,"sequence":49,"title":"檢查沖洗置換","titleEn":"Inspect rinse displacement","objective":"殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。","objectiveEn":"Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在流場示意追蹤殘留液體，比較流動死角與有效置換區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track residual liquid in a flow model and compare stagnant regions with effective displacement.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：流動死角留下殘液。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Stagnant flow regions retain liquid. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。","checkEn":"Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-049-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。 對應操作：在流場示意追蹤殘留液體，比較流動死角與有效置換區。","textEn":"Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface. Corresponding operation: Track residual liquid in a flow model and compare stagnant regions with effective displacement."},{"id":"sc-049-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：流動死角留下殘液。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Stagnant flow regions retain liquid."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查沖洗置換」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect rinse displacement\"?","options":["界面形貌與徑向溫差共同記錄，不只看平均溫度。","修整後的直徑與同軸性分別檢查。","殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。"],"optionsEn":["Interface shape and radial temperature differences are recorded together.","Final diameter and coaxiality are checked separately.","Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：殘留集中區被辨識，出口讀值不等同所有表面都已乾淨。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residual pockets are identified; an outlet reading is not treated as proof of a clean entire surface. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-048"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-050","order":24,"sequence":50,"title":"抑制乾燥水痕","titleEn":"Limit drying marks","objective":"乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","objectiveEn":"Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較液滴滯留與均勻退液的乾燥影像，把水痕位置疊在污染圖上。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare retained-droplet and uniform-meniscus drying images and overlay watermark locations on the contamination map.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：液滴殘留乾燥成局部沉積。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Retained droplets dry into localized deposits. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","checkEn":"Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-050-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。 對應操作：比較液滴滯留與均勻退液的乾燥影像，把水痕位置疊在污染圖上。","textEn":"Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after. Corresponding operation: Compare retained-droplet and uniform-meniscus drying images and overlay watermark locations on the contamination map."},{"id":"sc-050-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：液滴殘留乾燥成局部沉積。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Retained droplets dry into localized deposits."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「抑制乾燥水痕」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Limit drying marks\"?","options":["缺口定位可追溯至晶向量測，無未評估裂紋。","乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。","晶棒軸向與選定晶向一致。"],"optionsEn":["Notch orientation is traceable to crystallographic measurement and cracks are not left unevaluated.","Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after.","The ingot axis matches the selected crystal direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：乾燥後沒有新增局部殘留圈，表面缺陷圖可前後對位。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Drying adds no unexplained residue rings and defect maps can be registered before and after. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-049"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-051","order":25,"sequence":51,"title":"驗證清洗新增缺陷","titleEn":"Verify cleaning-added defects","objective":"新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","objectiveEn":"Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把相同測點的清洗前後圖相減，對新增亮點再分類。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare registered pre-clean and post-clean maps and classify newly appearing bright points.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：前後圖未對位或偵測設定不同。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unregistered maps or changed detection settings. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","checkEn":"Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-051-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。 對應操作：把相同測點的清洗前後圖相減，對新增亮點再分類。","textEn":"Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration. Corresponding operation: Compare registered pre-clean and post-clean maps and classify newly appearing bright points."},{"id":"sc-051-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：前後圖未對位或偵測設定不同。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Unregistered maps or changed detection settings."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「驗證清洗新增缺陷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify cleaning-added defects\"?","options":["新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。","判讀包含位錯路徑，不能僅憑外徑變小宣稱無缺陷。","切片厚度保留後續移除量，不把鋸縫當成產品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration.","The interpretation uses dislocation paths rather than equating a narrower diameter with defect-free material.","Slice thickness includes finishing allowance and excludes kerf loss from product thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：新增缺陷不是由檢出門檻改變或錯位造成。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Added defects are not artifacts of changed detection thresholds or misregistration. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-050"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-052","order":26,"sequence":52,"title":"限制潔淨表面等待","titleEn":"Control clean-surface queue exposure","objective":"交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。","objectiveEn":"Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在等待時間軸上比較表面氧化與吸附指標，對接下一製程的接收條件。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare oxidation and adsorption indicators over queue time against the receiving conditions of the next process.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：表面再氧化或吸附未被追蹤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Untracked reoxidation or adsorption. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。","checkEn":"Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-052-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。 對應操作：在等待時間軸上比較表面氧化與吸附指標，對接下一製程的接收條件。","textEn":"Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time. Corresponding operation: Compare oxidation and adsorption indicators over queue time against the receiving conditions of the next process."},{"id":"sc-052-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"表面製備會改變幾何、化學終態與缺陷；清除一種污染不保證其他類別也已移除，必須以對應量測確認。 本步特別排查：表面再氧化或吸附未被追蹤。","textEn":"Surface preparation changes geometry, termination and defects. Removing one contaminant class does not prove removal of others; corresponding measurements are needed. Specifically examine: Untracked reoxidation or adsorption."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「限制潔淨表面等待」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control clean-surface queue exposure\"?","options":["肩部至等徑段沒有不合理幾何跳變。","切痕方向、週期與機械運動有一致解釋。","交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。"],"optionsEn":["The shoulder-to-body transition has no implausible geometric discontinuity.","Mark direction and periodicity have an explanation consistent with machine motion.","Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：交接依據包含表面狀態及等待歷史，而非僅清洗完成時間。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Handoff evidence includes surface state and queue history, not only the cleaning completion time. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-sumco","sc-mc-prep","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-051"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m03","order":3,"title":"淺溝槽隔離 STI","titleEn":"Shallow-trench isolation","description":"以隔離截面串連硬遮罩、溝槽蝕刻、襯層、填充、研磨與回蝕，保留平面與鰭式元件分支。","descriptionEn":"Link hard masks, trench etching, liners, fill, polishing and recess through isolation sections, with separate planar and fin-device branches.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-053","order":1,"sequence":53,"title":"定位主動區與隔離區","titleEn":"Locate active and isolation regions","objective":"隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。","objectiveEn":"Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把相鄰電晶體平面圖投影至剖面，標出需要電性分隔的位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Project adjacent transistor layouts into a cross-section and mark locations requiring electrical separation.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：隔離邊界侵入通道。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Isolation boundaries intrude into channels. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。","checkEn":"Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-053-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。 對應操作：把相鄰電晶體平面圖投影至剖面，標出需要電性分隔的位置。","textEn":"Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels. Corresponding operation: Project adjacent transistor layouts into a cross-section and mark locations requiring electrical separation."},{"id":"sc-053-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：隔離邊界侵入通道。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Isolation boundaries intrude into channels."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「定位主動區與隔離區」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Locate active and isolation regions\"?","options":["側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。","需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels.","Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-052"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-054","order":2,"sequence":54,"title":"比較 STI 與 LOCOS 分支","titleEn":"Compare STI and LOCOS branches","objective":"鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","objectiveEn":"Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：並排溝槽填充與局部氧化剖面，觀察邊緣侵入及表面形貌。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare trench-fill and local-oxidation cross-sections and inspect lateral encroachment and topography.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：混用 LOCOS 與 STI 的幾何機制。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: LOCOS and STI geometrical mechanisms are mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","checkEn":"Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-054-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。 對應操作：並排溝槽填充與局部氧化剖面，觀察邊緣侵入及表面形貌。","textEn":"Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics. Corresponding operation: Compare trench-fill and local-oxidation cross-sections and inspect lateral encroachment and topography."},{"id":"sc-054-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：混用 LOCOS 與 STI 的幾何機制。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: LOCOS and STI geometrical mechanisms are mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較 STI 與 LOCOS 分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare STI and LOCOS branches\"?","options":["鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。","底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。"],"optionsEn":["Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center.","Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-053"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-055","order":3,"sequence":55,"title":"配置墊氧化層","titleEn":"Configure pad oxide","objective":"墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。","objectiveEn":"Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在矽與氮化層之間插入緩衝氧化層，比較界面應力示意。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Insert a buffer oxide between silicon and nitride and compare interface-stress maps.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：緩衝層位置或材料角色誤標。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Buffer location or material role mislabeled. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。","checkEn":"Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-055-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。 對應操作：在矽與氮化層之間插入緩衝氧化層，比較界面應力示意。","textEn":"Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide. Corresponding operation: Insert a buffer oxide between silicon and nitride and compare interface-stress maps."},{"id":"sc-055-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：緩衝層位置或材料角色誤標。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Buffer location or material role mislabeled."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置墊氧化層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure pad oxide\"?","options":["開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。"],"optionsEn":["Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-054"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-056","order":4,"sequence":56,"title":"沉積隔離硬遮罩","titleEn":"Deposit the isolation hard mask","objective":"硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。","objectiveEn":"Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：選擇示範氮化層覆蓋矽面，查看後續蝕刻及研磨會接觸哪一層。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Cover the surface with the example nitride layer and identify which layer later etch and polishing encounter.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：硬遮罩未兼顧研磨停止需求。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Hard mask ignores polishing-stop requirements. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。","checkEn":"Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-056-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。 對應操作：選擇示範氮化層覆蓋矽面，查看後續蝕刻及研磨會接觸哪一層。","textEn":"Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles. Corresponding operation: Cover the surface with the example nitride layer and identify which layer later etch and polishing encounter."},{"id":"sc-056-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：硬遮罩未兼顧研磨停止需求。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Hard mask ignores polishing-stop requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「沉積隔離硬遮罩」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Deposit the isolation hard mask\"?","options":["襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。","CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。"],"optionsEn":["Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles.","CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-055"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-057","order":5,"sequence":57,"title":"量測硬遮罩膜厚","titleEn":"Measure isolation-mask thickness","objective":"最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","objectiveEn":"The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把多點膜厚放回晶圓圖，比較薄區與預計蝕刻負荷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Map multipoint thickness readings and compare thin areas with expected etch loading.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：以平均膜厚忽略最薄區。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Average thickness hides the thinnest region. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","checkEn":"The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-057-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。 對應操作：把多點膜厚放回晶圓圖，比較薄區與預計蝕刻負荷。","textEn":"The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates. Corresponding operation: Map multipoint thickness readings and compare thin areas with expected etch loading."},{"id":"sc-057-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：以平均膜厚忽略最薄區。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Average thickness hides the thinnest region."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測硬遮罩膜厚」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure isolation-mask thickness\"?","options":["最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。","填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection.","Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-056"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-058","order":6,"sequence":58,"title":"塗佈主動區光阻","titleEn":"Coat the active-area resist","objective":"需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。","objectiveEn":"Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在硬遮罩上覆蓋光阻，查看臺階附近的局部薄化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Coat resist over the hard mask and inspect local thinning near topographic steps.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：臺階薄膜局部露底。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local coating breakthrough at topographic steps. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。","checkEn":"Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-058-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。 對應操作：在硬遮罩上覆蓋光阻，查看臺階附近的局部薄化。","textEn":"Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface. Corresponding operation: Coat resist over the hard mask and inspect local thinning near topographic steps."},{"id":"sc-058-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：臺階薄膜局部露底。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Local coating breakthrough at topographic steps."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「塗佈主動區光阻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Coat the active-area resist\"?","options":["去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。"],"optionsEn":["Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-057"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-059","order":7,"sequence":59,"title":"對準隔離光罩","titleEn":"Align the isolation mask","objective":"殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。","objectiveEn":"Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將隔離光罩對準基準記號，分別調整平移及旋轉。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Align the isolation mask to reference marks with separate translation and rotation adjustments.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只校中心而忽略旋轉。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Center-only alignment ignores rotation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。","checkEn":"Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-059-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。 對應操作：將隔離光罩對準基準記號，分別調整平移及旋轉。","textEn":"Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center. Corresponding operation: Align the isolation mask to reference marks with separate translation and rotation adjustments."},{"id":"sc-059-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：只校中心而忽略旋轉。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Center-only alignment ignores rotation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「對準隔離光罩」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Align the isolation mask\"?","options":["膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。","矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。"],"optionsEn":["Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center.","Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-058"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-060","order":8,"sequence":60,"title":"顯影隔離開口","titleEn":"Develop isolation openings","objective":"開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","objectiveEn":"Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較曝光前後光阻極性，移除指定區並查看主動區是否保留。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Apply the selected resist tone after exposure, remove intended regions and inspect active-area retention.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：曝光極性與保留區相反。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Exposure tone reverses retained regions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","checkEn":"Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-060-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。 對應操作：比較曝光前後光阻極性，移除指定區並查看主動區是否保留。","textEn":"Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal. Corresponding operation: Apply the selected resist tone after exposure, remove intended regions and inspect active-area retention."},{"id":"sc-060-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：曝光極性與保留區相反。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Exposure tone reverses retained regions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「顯影隔離開口」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Develop isolation openings\"?","options":["開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。","停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。"],"optionsEn":["Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point.","The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-059"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-061","order":9,"sequence":61,"title":"量測隔離開口 CD","titleEn":"Measure isolation-opening CD","objective":"CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。","objectiveEn":"CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在密集與孤立區量測相同定義的線寬，標出角部圓化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure identically defined widths in dense and isolated regions and mark corner rounding.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：不同高度的 CD 被直接比較。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: CD values at different heights are compared directly. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。","checkEn":"CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-061-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。 對應操作：在密集與孤立區量測相同定義的線寬，標出角部圓化。","textEn":"CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition. Corresponding operation: Measure identically defined widths in dense and isolated regions and mark corner rounding."},{"id":"sc-061-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：不同高度的 CD 被直接比較。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: CD values at different heights are compared directly."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測隔離開口 CD」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure isolation-opening CD\"?","options":["側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-060"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-062","order":10,"sequence":62,"title":"轉移氮化硬遮罩","titleEn":"Transfer the nitride hard mask","objective":"遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。","objectiveEn":"Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將光阻開口轉到硬遮罩，逐層查看墊氧化層是否被過度消耗。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Transfer resist openings into the hard mask and inspect pad-oxide consumption layer by layer.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：硬遮罩開口伴隨過度底層消耗。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mask opening excessively consumes the underlayer. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。","checkEn":"Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-062-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。 對應操作：將光阻開口轉到硬遮罩，逐層查看墊氧化層是否被過度消耗。","textEn":"Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection. Corresponding operation: Transfer resist openings into the hard mask and inspect pad-oxide consumption layer by layer."},{"id":"sc-062-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：硬遮罩開口伴隨過度底層消耗。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Mask opening excessively consumes the underlayer."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「轉移氮化硬遮罩」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Transfer the nitride hard mask\"?","options":["停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。","底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。"],"optionsEn":["Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection.","Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-061"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-063","order":11,"sequence":63,"title":"去除圖案化光阻","titleEn":"Remove isolation-patterning resist","objective":"去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","objectiveEn":"Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：模擬去膠後檢查硬遮罩側壁，分辨光阻殘留與氮化層輪廓。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect hard-mask sidewalls after simulated resist removal and distinguish residue from nitride geometry.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：去膠殘留與硬遮罩混判。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Resist residue mistaken for hard mask. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","checkEn":"Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-063-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。 對應操作：模擬去膠後檢查硬遮罩側壁，分辨光阻殘留與氮化層輪廓。","textEn":"Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern. Corresponding operation: Inspect hard-mask sidewalls after simulated resist removal and distinguish residue from nitride geometry."},{"id":"sc-063-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：去膠殘留與硬遮罩混判。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Resist residue mistaken for hard mask."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「去除圖案化光阻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove isolation-patterning resist\"?","options":["去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。"],"optionsEn":["Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-062"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-064","order":12,"sequence":64,"title":"開啟墊氧化層窗口","titleEn":"Open the pad-oxide window","objective":"矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。","objectiveEn":"Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿氮化層窗口移除墊氧化層，觀察暴露矽的位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Remove pad oxide through nitride windows and inspect exposed-silicon locations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：墊氧化開口超出遮罩邊界。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Pad-oxide opening extends beyond mask boundaries. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。","checkEn":"Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-064-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。 對應操作：沿氮化層窗口移除墊氧化層，觀察暴露矽的位置。","textEn":"Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening. Corresponding operation: Remove pad oxide through nitride windows and inspect exposed-silicon locations."},{"id":"sc-064-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：墊氧化開口超出遮罩邊界。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Pad-oxide opening extends beyond mask boundaries."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「開啟墊氧化層窗口」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Open the pad-oxide window\"?","options":["襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。"],"optionsEn":["Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-063"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-065","order":13,"sequence":65,"title":"蝕刻 STI 溝槽深度","titleEn":"Etch STI trench depth","objective":"隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。","objectiveEn":"Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在剖面模型增加矽移除量，將最深與最淺溝槽分開標示。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Increase silicon removal in the cross-section and label the deepest and shallowest trenches separately.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：深度分布被單點數據取代。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Depth distribution replaced by one point. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。","checkEn":"Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-065-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。 對應操作：在剖面模型增加矽移除量，將最深與最淺溝槽分開標示。","textEn":"Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point. Corresponding operation: Increase silicon removal in the cross-section and label the deepest and shallowest trenches separately."},{"id":"sc-065-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：深度分布被單點數據取代。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Depth distribution replaced by one point."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「蝕刻 STI 溝槽深度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Etch STI trench depth\"?","options":["交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。","填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。"],"optionsEn":["Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point.","Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-064"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-066","order":14,"sequence":66,"title":"調整 STI 側壁角度","titleEn":"Adjust STI sidewall angle","objective":"側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","objectiveEn":"Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較垂直與略傾斜溝槽，觀察後續填充入口寬度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare vertical and slightly tapered trenches and inspect the opening available for later fill.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：入口輪廓造成填充提早封口。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Entrance profile causes premature fill closure. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","checkEn":"Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-066-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。 對應操作：比較垂直與略傾斜溝槽，觀察後續填充入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together. Corresponding operation: Compare vertical and slightly tapered trenches and inspect the opening available for later fill."},{"id":"sc-066-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：入口輪廓造成填充提早封口。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Entrance profile causes premature fill closure."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整 STI 側壁角度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Adjust STI sidewall angle\"?","options":["側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。","接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together.","Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：側壁形狀與填充可達性一起評估。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Sidewall profile and fill accessibility are evaluated together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-065"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-067","order":15,"sequence":67,"title":"檢查溝槽底角","titleEn":"Inspect trench bottom corners","objective":"底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。","objectiveEn":"Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：放大底角截面，找出尖角、微溝與局部殘留。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Magnify trench-bottom corners and identify sharp edges, microtrenches and residues.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平均深度掩蓋角部微溝。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Average depth hides corner microtrenches. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。","checkEn":"Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-067-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。 對應操作：放大底角截面，找出尖角、微溝與局部殘留。","textEn":"Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data. Corresponding operation: Magnify trench-bottom corners and identify sharp edges, microtrenches and residues."},{"id":"sc-067-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：平均深度掩蓋角部微溝。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Average depth hides corner microtrenches."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查溝槽底角」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect trench bottom corners\"?","options":["膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。"],"optionsEn":["Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：底角異常有局部形貌證據，未以平均深度代替。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Corner anomalies have local-profile evidence rather than only average-depth data. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-066"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-068","order":16,"sequence":68,"title":"移除溝槽蝕刻殘留","titleEn":"Remove trench-etch residues","objective":"殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","objectiveEn":"Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較清洗前後側壁訊號，確認殘留減少時矽輪廓沒有明顯侵蝕。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare sidewall signals before and after cleaning and check that residue removal does not unduly erode silicon.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：殘留清洗侵蝕矽側壁。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Residue cleaning erodes silicon sidewalls. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","checkEn":"Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-068-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。 對應操作：比較清洗前後側壁訊號，確認殘留減少時矽輪廓沒有明顯侵蝕。","textEn":"Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together. Corresponding operation: Compare sidewall signals before and after cleaning and check that residue removal does not unduly erode silicon."},{"id":"sc-068-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：殘留清洗侵蝕矽側壁。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Residue cleaning erodes silicon sidewalls."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「移除溝槽蝕刻殘留」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove trench-etch residues\"?","options":["墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。","殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。","停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。"],"optionsEn":["Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide.","Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together.","The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：殘留去除與尺寸保留同時成立。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residue removal and dimensional preservation are demonstrated together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-067"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-069","order":17,"sequence":69,"title":"形成溝槽襯氧化層","titleEn":"Form the trench liner oxide","objective":"襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","objectiveEn":"Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在溝槽表面加入氧化襯層，追蹤矽消耗與角部圓化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add an oxide liner to trench surfaces and track silicon consumption and corner rounding.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：襯氧化的矽消耗未計入。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Silicon consumption by liner oxidation omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","checkEn":"Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-069-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。 對應操作：在溝槽表面加入氧化襯層，追蹤矽消耗與角部圓化。","textEn":"Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported. Corresponding operation: Add an oxide liner to trench surfaces and track silicon consumption and corner rounding."},{"id":"sc-069-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：襯氧化的矽消耗未計入。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Silicon consumption by liner oxidation omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「形成溝槽襯氧化層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Form the trench liner oxide\"?","options":["襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。","兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。"],"optionsEn":["Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported.","The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：襯層連續性與通道側有效寬度均被保留於報告。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Liner continuity and remaining active-region width are both reported. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-068"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-070","order":18,"sequence":70,"title":"選擇隔離填充路線","titleEn":"Select the isolation-fill route","objective":"填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。","objectiveEn":"Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較共形沉積與改善間隙填充的示意路線，檢查入口提前封閉。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare conformal deposition with gap-fill-oriented routes and inspect premature closure of the opening.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把共形覆蓋直接等同無空洞填充。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Conformal coverage equated with void-free fill. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。","checkEn":"Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-070-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。 對應操作：比較共形沉積與改善間隙填充的示意路線，檢查入口提前封閉。","textEn":"Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone. Corresponding operation: Compare conformal deposition with gap-fill-oriented routes and inspect premature closure of the opening."},{"id":"sc-070-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：把共形覆蓋直接等同無空洞填充。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Conformal coverage equated with void-free fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇隔離填充路線」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select the isolation-fill route\"?","options":["停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。"],"optionsEn":["Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：填充方案不能只靠總沉積厚度判定。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Fill feasibility is not judged from total deposited thickness alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-069"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-071","order":19,"sequence":71,"title":"追蹤溝槽填充接縫","titleEn":"Track trench-fill seams","objective":"接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","objectiveEn":"Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：逐層增加填充材料，觀察兩側成長前緣何處相遇。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add fill material in stages and locate where opposing growth fronts meet.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：兩側生長前緣封住入口。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Opposing growth fronts close the entrance. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","checkEn":"Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-071-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。 對應操作：逐層增加填充材料，觀察兩側成長前緣何處相遇。","textEn":"Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately. Corresponding operation: Add fill material in stages and locate where opposing growth fronts meet."},{"id":"sc-071-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：兩側生長前緣封住入口。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Opposing growth fronts close the entrance."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「追蹤溝槽填充接縫」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Track trench-fill seams\"?","options":["需要保護的位置沒有局部露底。","接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。","回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。"],"optionsEn":["Regions requiring protection have no exposed underlying surface.","Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately.","The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：接縫位置與可能封存空洞分開標記。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Seam locations and potentially trapped voids are labeled separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-070"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-072","order":20,"sequence":72,"title":"檢查隔離層緻密化","titleEn":"Inspect isolation-film densification","objective":"膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","objectiveEn":"Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較緻密化前後膜厚、折射率與應力示意，追蹤收縮。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thickness, refractive index and stress before and after densification and track shrinkage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：膜收縮與材料移除混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Film shrinkage confused with removal. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","checkEn":"Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-072-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。 對應操作：比較緻密化前後膜厚、折射率與應力示意，追蹤收縮。","textEn":"Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching. Corresponding operation: Compare thickness, refractive index and stress before and after densification and track shrinkage."},{"id":"sc-072-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：膜收縮與材料移除混淆。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Film shrinkage confused with removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查隔離層緻密化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect isolation-film densification\"?","options":["膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。","邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","殘差在多個記號上檢查，並非只讓中心對準。"],"optionsEn":["Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching.","Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","Residuals are checked across multiple marks rather than only at the center."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：膜厚收縮不直接等同材料遺失或蝕刻。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Film shrinkage is not automatically interpreted as material removal or etching. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-071"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-073","order":21,"sequence":73,"title":"建立 STI 研磨停止面","titleEn":"Establish the STI polish-stop plane","objective":"停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。","objectiveEn":"The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：設定氮化層作為示範停止層，觀察凸起氧化層逐步移除。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Use nitride as the example stop layer and observe gradual removal of protruding oxide.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：研磨端點與停止層餘量不符。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Polish endpoint conflicts with stop-layer reserve. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。","checkEn":"The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-073-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。 對應操作：設定氮化層作為示範停止層，觀察凸起氧化層逐步移除。","textEn":"The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences. Corresponding operation: Use nitride as the example stop layer and observe gradual removal of protruding oxide."},{"id":"sc-073-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：研磨端點與停止層餘量不符。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Polish endpoint conflicts with stop-layer reserve."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立 STI 研磨停止面」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Establish the STI polish-stop plane\"?","options":["交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","開口與隔離版圖一致，沒有將圖案正負相反。","停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。"],"optionsEn":["Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","Openings match the isolation layout without tone reversal.","The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：停止判據包含剩餘氮化層與區域高度差。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The stop criterion includes remaining nitride and regional height differences. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-072"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-074","order":22,"sequence":74,"title":"診斷隔離凹陷與侵蝕","titleEn":"Diagnose isolation dishing and erosion","objective":"兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","objectiveEn":"The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對照寬隔離區和密集小區的研磨後形貌，分別標註凹陷及區域侵蝕。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare polished wide-isolation and dense-pattern regions and label dishing and regional erosion separately.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：寬圖案凹陷與密集區侵蝕混合。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wide-feature dishing mixed with dense-region erosion. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","checkEn":"The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-074-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。 對應操作：對照寬隔離區和密集小區的研磨後形貌，分別標註凹陷及區域侵蝕。","textEn":"The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value. Corresponding operation: Compare polished wide-isolation and dense-pattern regions and label dishing and regional erosion separately."},{"id":"sc-074-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：寬圖案凹陷與密集區侵蝕混合。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Wide-feature dishing mixed with dense-region erosion."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷隔離凹陷與侵蝕」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose isolation dishing and erosion\"?","options":["CD 比較使用相同量測高度與邊緣定義。","兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。","隔離區位於預定邊界，不切斷有效通道。"],"optionsEn":["CD comparisons use the same measurement height and edge definition.","The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value.","Isolation occupies intended boundaries without cutting active channels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：兩種形貌效應未用同一單點厚度混合描述。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The two topographic effects are not conflated into one point-thickness value. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-073"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-075","order":23,"sequence":75,"title":"去除 STI 停止層","titleEn":"Remove the STI stop layer","objective":"停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","objectiveEn":"Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在模擬截面選擇性移除氮化層，檢查填充氧化層邊緣。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Selectively remove nitride in the model and inspect fill-oxide edges.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：去停止層損耗填充氧化物。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Stop-layer removal also consumes fill oxide. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","checkEn":"Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-075-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。 對應操作：在模擬截面選擇性移除氮化層，檢查填充氧化層邊緣。","textEn":"Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded. Corresponding operation: Selectively remove nitride in the model and inspect fill-oxide edges."},{"id":"sc-075-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：去停止層損耗填充氧化物。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Stop-layer removal also consumes fill oxide."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「去除 STI 停止層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove the STI stop layer\"?","options":["停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。","鳥嘴效應只用於對應局部氧化情境，未套用成 STI 的相同機制。","遮罩開口形成時，非目標層仍符合示範保護需求。"],"optionsEn":["Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded.","Bird's-beak behavior is assigned to the appropriate local-oxidation context rather than identical STI physics.","Mask openings form while non-target layers retain the exercise's required protection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：停止層去除後的氧化層損耗有記錄。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Oxide loss during stop-layer removal is recorded. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-074"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-076","order":24,"sequence":76,"title":"控制隔離表面回蝕","titleEn":"Control isolation recess","objective":"回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。","objectiveEn":"The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：逐步回蝕填充氧化層，比較平面元件和鰭式元件所需的暴露高度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Recess fill oxide incrementally and compare exposure-height needs for planar and fin-based devices.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：對不同元件強制同一回蝕高度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: One recess height imposed on different devices. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。","checkEn":"The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-076-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。 對應操作：逐步回蝕填充氧化層，比較平面元件和鰭式元件所需的暴露高度。","textEn":"The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types. Corresponding operation: Recess fill oxide incrementally and compare exposure-height needs for planar and fin-based devices."},{"id":"sc-076-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：對不同元件強制同一回蝕高度。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: One recess height imposed on different devices."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制隔離表面回蝕」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control isolation recess\"?","options":["墊氧化層的位置及緩衝作用與閘極氧化層區分。","去膠沒有被誤判為硬遮罩圖案消失。","回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。"],"optionsEn":["Pad-oxide location and buffering function are distinguished from gate oxide.","Resist removal is not confused with removal of the hard-mask pattern.","The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：回蝕目標明確標路線，未對所有元件使用同一高度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The recess target is route-specific rather than shared blindly across device types. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-075"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-077","order":25,"sequence":77,"title":"量測隔離邊緣漏電","titleEn":"Measure isolation-edge leakage","objective":"邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","objectiveEn":"Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較示意隔離測試結構的電流曲線，將邊緣長度與面積正規化分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare leakage curves from isolation test structures and distinguish perimeter normalization from area normalization.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：面積與周長正規化混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Area and perimeter normalization mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","checkEn":"Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-077-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。 對應操作：比較示意隔離測試結構的電流曲線，將邊緣長度與面積正規化分開。","textEn":"Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling. Corresponding operation: Compare leakage curves from isolation test structures and distinguish perimeter normalization from area normalization."},{"id":"sc-077-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：面積與周長正規化混用。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Area and perimeter normalization mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測隔離邊緣漏電」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure isolation-edge leakage\"?","options":["矽暴露範圍受硬遮罩約束。","邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。","硬遮罩厚度同時考慮圖案轉移與研磨停止用途。"],"optionsEn":["Exposed silicon remains bounded by the hard-mask opening.","Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling.","Hard-mask thickness considers both pattern transfer and polishing-stop roles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：邊緣主導與面積主導漏電的解釋符合結構尺度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Perimeter-dominated and area-dominated leakage interpretations match structural scaling. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-076"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-078","order":26,"sequence":78,"title":"交接隔離後表面","titleEn":"Handoff the post-isolation surface","objective":"交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","objectiveEn":"Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：疊合隔離深度、表面高度與缺陷圖，確認下一層微影的輸入。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay isolation depth, surface height and defect maps to establish inputs for the next lithography level.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：隔離完成但表面高度仍不合需求。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Isolation complete but surface height remains unsuitable. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","checkEn":"Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-078-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。 對應操作：疊合隔離深度、表面高度與缺陷圖，確認下一層微影的輸入。","textEn":"Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion. Corresponding operation: Overlay isolation depth, surface height and defect maps to establish inputs for the next lithography level."},{"id":"sc-078-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"隔離品質同時受幾何、材料連續性及局部電場影響。俯視開口合格不代表深槽填充、角部或電性也合格。 本步特別排查：隔離完成但表面高度仍不合需求。","textEn":"Isolation quality depends on geometry, material continuity and local fields. A passing top-view opening does not establish acceptable deep fill, corners or electrical behavior. Specifically examine: Isolation complete but surface height remains unsuitable."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接隔離後表面」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handoff the post-isolation surface\"?","options":["交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。","最薄區仍納入遮罩消耗估算。","隔離深度以全片分布評估，而非單點最深值。"],"optionsEn":["Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion.","The thinnest region is included in mask-consumption estimates.","Isolation depth is assessed as a wafer-wide distribution rather than the deepest single point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：交接包含主動區有效尺寸與隔離邊界，而不只填充完成。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Handoff includes active dimensions and isolation boundaries, not merely fill completion. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-077"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m04","order":4,"title":"井區、通道植入與退火","titleEn":"Well and channel implantation and annealing","description":"以濃度剖面、損傷圖與電性地圖區分植入、活化及擴散；通道調整列為傳統平面元件分支。","descriptionEn":"Use concentration profiles, damage maps and electrical maps to distinguish implantation, activation and diffusion; channel adjustment is a conventional planar-device branch.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-079","order":1,"sequence":79,"title":"標示 n 井與 p 井","titleEn":"Label n-wells and p-wells","objective":"井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。","objectiveEn":"Well type is consistent with device-body biasing.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在 CMOS 截面把 PMOS 與 NMOS 所需井區配對，追蹤接面極性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Match PMOS and NMOS devices to their wells in a CMOS section and track junction polarity.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Well type is consistent with device-body biasing.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：井區型態或本體偏壓極性錯誤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wrong well type or body-bias polarity. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。","checkEn":"Well type is consistent with device-body biasing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-079-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。 對應操作：在 CMOS 截面把 PMOS 與 NMOS 所需井區配對，追蹤接面極性。","textEn":"Well type is consistent with device-body biasing. Corresponding operation: Match PMOS and NMOS devices to their wells in a CMOS section and track junction polarity."},{"id":"sc-079-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：井區型態或本體偏壓極性錯誤。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Wrong well type or body-bias polarity."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「標示 n 井與 p 井」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Label n-wells and p-wells\"?","options":["深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。"],"optionsEn":["Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","Well type is consistent with device-body biasing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Well type is consistent with device-body biasing. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-078"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-080","order":2,"sequence":80,"title":"配置深井隔離分支","titleEn":"Configure a deep-well branch","objective":"深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。","objectiveEn":"The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在三重井示意加入深井，畫出隔離邊界及基板耦合路徑。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add a deep well to a triple-well model and draw isolation boundaries and substrate-coupling paths.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：深井邊界沒有形成連續隔離。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Deep-well boundaries fail to form continuous isolation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。","checkEn":"The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-080-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。 對應操作：在三重井示意加入深井，畫出隔離邊界及基板耦合路徑。","textEn":"The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section. Corresponding operation: Add a deep well to a triple-well model and draw isolation boundaries and substrate-coupling paths."},{"id":"sc-080-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：深井邊界沒有形成連續隔離。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Deep-well boundaries fail to form continuous isolation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置深井隔離分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure a deep-well branch\"?","options":["去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。","面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。"],"optionsEn":["Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section.","Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-079"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-081","order":3,"sequence":81,"title":"建立井區植入遮罩","titleEn":"Build the well-implant mask","objective":"未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","objectiveEn":"Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把井區版圖轉為遮罩開口，檢查鄰近器件與重疊裕量。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Convert well layouts into mask openings and inspect adjacent devices and overlap margins.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：植入窗口重疊或保護區缺口。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Overlapping implant windows or gaps in protected areas. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","checkEn":"Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-081-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。 對應操作：把井區版圖轉為遮罩開口，檢查鄰近器件與重疊裕量。","textEn":"Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout. Corresponding operation: Convert well layouts into mask openings and inspect adjacent devices and overlap margins."},{"id":"sc-081-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：植入窗口重疊或保護區缺口。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Overlapping implant windows or gaps in protected areas."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立井區植入遮罩」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build the well-implant mask\"?","options":["未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。","清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。"],"optionsEn":["Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak.","Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-080"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-082","order":4,"sequence":82,"title":"核對遮罩阻擋能力","titleEn":"Check implant-mask stopping capability","objective":"遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。","objectiveEn":"The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較植入深度分布與遮罩等效阻擋厚度，觀察穿透尾端。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare implant-depth distributions with effective mask stopping thickness and inspect penetration tails.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只看平均射程而漏掉穿透尾端。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mean range hides penetration tails. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。","checkEn":"The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-082-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。 對應操作：比較植入深度分布與遮罩等效阻擋厚度，觀察穿透尾端。","textEn":"The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range. Corresponding operation: Compare implant-depth distributions with effective mask stopping thickness and inspect penetration tails."},{"id":"sc-082-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：只看平均射程而漏掉穿透尾端。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Mean range hides penetration tails."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對遮罩阻擋能力」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check implant-mask stopping capability\"?","options":["通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。"],"optionsEn":["Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-081"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-083","order":5,"sequence":83,"title":"選擇植入離子種類","titleEn":"Select implantation species","objective":"所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。","objectiveEn":"The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比示意施體和受體的活化後電性，區分化學元素與電荷狀態。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare activated donor and acceptor behavior and distinguish chemical species from ion charge state.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：摻雜元素與離子電荷態混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Dopant species confused with ion charge state. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。","checkEn":"The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-083-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。 對應操作：對比示意施體和受體的活化後電性，區分化學元素與電荷狀態。","textEn":"The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well. Corresponding operation: Compare activated donor and acceptor behavior and distinguish chemical species from ion charge state."},{"id":"sc-083-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：摻雜元素與離子電荷態混淆。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Dopant species confused with ion charge state."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇植入離子種類」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select implantation species\"?","options":["比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。","降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。"],"optionsEn":["Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well.","A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-082"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-084","order":6,"sequence":84,"title":"設定植入能量比較","titleEn":"Compare implantation energy","objective":"深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","objectiveEn":"Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在教材模型提高或降低能量，觀察投影射程與分布寬度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Vary energy in the educational model and observe projected range and distribution width.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把能量變化當成劑量變化。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Energy variation mistaken for dose variation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","checkEn":"Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-084-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。 對應操作：在教材模型提高或降低能量，觀察投影射程與分布寬度。","textEn":"Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose. Corresponding operation: Vary energy in the educational model and observe projected range and distribution width."},{"id":"sc-084-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：把能量變化當成劑量變化。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Energy variation mistaken for dose variation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「設定植入能量比較」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare implantation energy\"?","options":["深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。","溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。"],"optionsEn":["Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible.","Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-083"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-085","order":7,"sequence":85,"title":"積分植入劑量","titleEn":"Integrate implant dose","objective":"面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。","objectiveEn":"Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把離子流訊號沿時間積分，再與暴露面積的變化比較。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Integrate the ion-current signal over time and compare changes in exposed area.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：積分單位、面積或電荷態錯誤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Incorrect integration units, area or charge state. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。","checkEn":"Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-085-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。 對應操作：把離子流訊號沿時間積分，再與暴露面積的變化比較。","textEn":"Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated. Corresponding operation: Integrate the ion-current signal over time and compare changes in exposed area."},{"id":"sc-085-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：積分單位、面積或電荷態錯誤。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Incorrect integration units, area or charge state."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「積分植入劑量」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Integrate implant dose\"?","options":["掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。"],"optionsEn":["Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-084"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-086","order":8,"sequence":86,"title":"分析多能量井區植入","titleEn":"Analyze multi-energy well implants","objective":"合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。","objectiveEn":"The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：疊合數個示意深度分布，查看合成剖面如何覆蓋目標井區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Superpose several illustrative depth distributions and inspect coverage of the target well.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把多次分布取最大而非相加。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Taking the maximum rather than summing profiles. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。","checkEn":"The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-086-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。 對應操作：疊合數個示意深度分布，查看合成剖面如何覆蓋目標井區。","textEn":"The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak. Corresponding operation: Superpose several illustrative depth distributions and inspect coverage of the target well."},{"id":"sc-086-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：把多次分布取最大而非相加。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Taking the maximum rather than summing profiles."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析多能量井區植入」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze multi-energy well implants\"?","options":["接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。","充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。"],"optionsEn":["Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak.","Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-085"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-087","order":9,"sequence":87,"title":"辨識晶格通道效應","titleEn":"Identify channeling","objective":"通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","objectiveEn":"Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較沿晶軸與偏離晶軸的植入尾端，圈出深層通道化區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare implantation tails along and away from crystal axes and mark deep channeling regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：高斯近似忽略晶向通道化。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Gaussian approximation ignores channeling. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","checkEn":"Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-087-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。 對應操作：比較沿晶軸與偏離晶軸的植入尾端，圈出深層通道化區。","textEn":"Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian. Corresponding operation: Compare implantation tails along and away from crystal axes and mark deep channeling regions."},{"id":"sc-087-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：高斯近似忽略晶向通道化。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Gaussian approximation ignores channeling."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識晶格通道效應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify channeling\"?","options":["通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-086"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-088","order":10,"sequence":88,"title":"調整植入傾角","titleEn":"Adjust implant tilt","objective":"降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。","objectiveEn":"A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在晶格模型改變束流傾角，同時觀察溝槽或遮罩造成的陰影。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Change beam tilt in the lattice model while observing shadowing from trenches or masks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：抑制通道化卻加重幾何遮蔽。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Channeling reduction worsens geometric shadowing. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。","checkEn":"A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-088-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。 對應操作：在晶格模型改變束流傾角，同時觀察溝槽或遮罩造成的陰影。","textEn":"A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing. Corresponding operation: Change beam tilt in the lattice model while observing shadowing from trenches or masks."},{"id":"sc-088-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：抑制通道化卻加重幾何遮蔽。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Channeling reduction worsens geometric shadowing."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整植入傾角」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Adjust implant tilt\"?","options":["去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。"],"optionsEn":["Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-087"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-089","order":11,"sequence":89,"title":"調整植入旋轉角","titleEn":"Adjust implant twist angle","objective":"傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。","objectiveEn":"Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：固定傾角後旋轉晶圓方位，對照晶向與圖案方向。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Hold tilt fixed while rotating wafer azimuth and compare crystal and pattern directions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：傾角與方位角紀錄混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Tilt and azimuth records mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。","checkEn":"Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-089-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。 對應操作：固定傾角後旋轉晶圓方位，對照晶向與圖案方向。","textEn":"Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible. Corresponding operation: Hold tilt fixed while rotating wafer azimuth and compare crystal and pattern directions."},{"id":"sc-089-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：傾角與方位角紀錄混用。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Tilt and azimuth records mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整植入旋轉角」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Adjust implant twist angle\"?","options":["傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。","清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。"],"optionsEn":["Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible.","Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-088"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-090","order":12,"sequence":90,"title":"均化植入掃描","titleEn":"Equalize implant scanning","objective":"掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","objectiveEn":"Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把束流掃描軌跡疊在面劑量圖，找出轉向及邊緣累積。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay beam-scan trajectories on the dose map and identify turnaround and edge accumulation.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：轉向停留造成邊緣劑量異常。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Turnaround dwell creates edge-dose anomalies. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","checkEn":"Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-090-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。 對應操作：把束流掃描軌跡疊在面劑量圖，找出轉向及邊緣累積。","textEn":"Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies. Corresponding operation: Overlay beam-scan trajectories on the dose map and identify turnaround and edge accumulation."},{"id":"sc-090-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：轉向停留造成邊緣劑量異常。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Turnaround dwell creates edge-dose anomalies."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「均化植入掃描」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Equalize implant scanning\"?","options":["掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。"],"optionsEn":["Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-089"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-091","order":13,"sequence":91,"title":"診斷植入充電","titleEn":"Diagnose implant charging","objective":"充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。","objectiveEn":"Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較有無中和作用的表面電位示意，查看介電區和導電區差異。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare surface-potential maps with and without neutralization and inspect dielectric and conducting regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：局部充電被平均束流掩蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local charging hidden by average beam current. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。","checkEn":"Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-091-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。 對應操作：比較有無中和作用的表面電位示意，查看介電區和導電區差異。","textEn":"Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current. Corresponding operation: Compare surface-potential maps with and without neutralization and inspect dielectric and conducting regions."},{"id":"sc-091-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：局部充電被平均束流掩蓋。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Local charging hidden by average beam current."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷植入充電」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose implant charging\"?","options":["比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。"],"optionsEn":["Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-090"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-092","order":14,"sequence":92,"title":"區分植入損傷與摻雜","titleEn":"Separate implant damage from doping","objective":"化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","objectiveEn":"Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將缺陷密度與化學濃度畫在同一深度軸，檢查峰值是否重合。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Plot damage density and chemical concentration on the same depth axis and compare their peaks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：化學濃度直接當成載子濃度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Chemical concentration treated as carrier concentration. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","checkEn":"Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-092-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。 對應操作：將缺陷密度與化學濃度畫在同一深度軸，檢查峰值是否重合。","textEn":"Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration. Corresponding operation: Plot damage density and chemical concentration on the same depth axis and compare their peaks."},{"id":"sc-092-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：化學濃度直接當成載子濃度。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Chemical concentration treated as carrier concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「區分植入損傷與摻雜」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate implant damage from doping\"?","options":["井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。","化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。","溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。"],"optionsEn":["Well type is consistent with device-body biasing.","Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration.","Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：化學摻雜濃度不被直接當成活性載子濃度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Chemical dopant concentration is not treated as active-carrier concentration. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-091"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-093","order":15,"sequence":93,"title":"剝除植入後光阻","titleEn":"Strip post-implant resist","objective":"去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","objectiveEn":"Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：查看植入後表層硬化示意，比較去除前後殘留與基板變化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect an implantation-hardened resist surface and compare residues and substrate changes before and after stripping.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：硬化光阻外觀清除但底層殘留。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Hardened resist appears cleared but residue remains. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","checkEn":"Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-093-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。 對應操作：查看植入後表層硬化示意，比較去除前後殘留與基板變化。","textEn":"Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage. Corresponding operation: Inspect an implantation-hardened resist surface and compare residues and substrate changes before and after stripping."},{"id":"sc-093-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：硬化光阻外觀清除但底層殘留。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Hardened resist appears cleared but residue remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「剝除植入後光阻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Strip post-implant resist\"?","options":["去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。","活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage.","Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：去膠證據包含硬化殘層與表面損傷。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Strip verification includes hardened residue and surface damage. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-092"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-094","order":16,"sequence":94,"title":"清除植入後殘留","titleEn":"Clean post-implant residues","objective":"清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。","objectiveEn":"Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對照元素圖和粒子圖，判別需處理的遮罩殘留或再沉積。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare elemental and particle maps to distinguish mask residue from redeposition.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：透明表面被誤判沒有化學殘留。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Transparent surface misread as chemically clean. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。","checkEn":"Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-094-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。 對應操作：對照元素圖和粒子圖，判別需處理的遮罩殘留或再沉積。","textEn":"Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness. Corresponding operation: Compare elemental and particle maps to distinguish mask residue from redeposition."},{"id":"sc-094-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：透明表面被誤判沒有化學殘留。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Transparent surface misread as chemically clean."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「清除植入後殘留」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Clean post-implant residues\"?","options":["接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。"],"optionsEn":["Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：清潔結果不以外觀透明代替化學分析。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Visual transparency does not substitute for chemical evidence of cleanliness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-093"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-095","order":17,"sequence":95,"title":"模擬井區驅入","titleEn":"Model well drive-in","objective":"垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","objectiveEn":"Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對示意濃度剖面施加擴散演化，查看井深與側向邊界移動。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Apply diffusion evolution to an illustrative concentration profile and track well depth and lateral movement.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略井區側向擴散。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Lateral well diffusion omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","checkEn":"Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-095-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。 對應操作：對示意濃度剖面施加擴散演化，查看井深與側向邊界移動。","textEn":"Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary. Corresponding operation: Apply diffusion evolution to an illustrative concentration profile and track well depth and lateral movement."},{"id":"sc-095-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：忽略井區側向擴散。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Lateral well diffusion omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬井區驅入」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model well drive-in\"?","options":["遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。","垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。","異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。"],"optionsEn":["The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range.","Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary.","Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：垂直和側向擴散一起納入井區邊界。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Both vertical and lateral diffusion are included in the well boundary. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-094"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-096","order":18,"sequence":96,"title":"比較快速與爐管退火","titleEn":"Compare rapid and furnace annealing","objective":"比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","objectiveEn":"Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用兩種時間溫度軌跡驅動同一示意模型，觀察活化及擴散取捨。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Apply two time-temperature histories to the same illustrative model and compare activation with diffusion.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：僅比較最高溫而忽略時間。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Peak temperatures compared without duration. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","checkEn":"Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-096-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。 對應操作：用兩種時間溫度軌跡驅動同一示意模型，觀察活化及擴散取捨。","textEn":"Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone. Corresponding operation: Apply two time-temperature histories to the same illustrative model and compare activation with diffusion."},{"id":"sc-096-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：僅比較最高溫而忽略時間。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Peak temperatures compared without duration."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較快速與爐管退火」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare rapid and furnace annealing\"?","options":["比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。","不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。"],"optionsEn":["Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone.","Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：比較完整熱歷史，不僅比較最高溫度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Complete thermal histories are compared rather than peak temperatures alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-095"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-097","order":19,"sequence":97,"title":"檢查退火溫度均勻性","titleEn":"Inspect anneal temperature uniformity","objective":"溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。","objectiveEn":"Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較晶圓徑向溫度圖與片電阻圖，辨識可能的發射率量測誤差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare radial temperature and sheet-resistance maps and consider emissivity-related measurement error.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：發射率差異造成假溫差。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Emissivity differences create apparent temperature variation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。","checkEn":"Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-097-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。 對應操作：比較晶圓徑向溫度圖與片電阻圖，辨識可能的發射率量測誤差。","textEn":"Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation. Corresponding operation: Compare radial temperature and sheet-resistance maps and consider emissivity-related measurement error."},{"id":"sc-097-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：發射率差異造成假溫差。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Emissivity differences create apparent temperature variation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查退火溫度均勻性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect anneal temperature uniformity\"?","options":["傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","深度趨勢由分布判讀，沒有把能量當作劑量。","溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。"],"optionsEn":["Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","Depth trends are interpreted from the distribution without confusing energy with dose.","Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：溫度偏差與電性散布的相關性有空間對位。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Temperature deviations and electrical variation are spatially registered before correlation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-096"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-098","order":20,"sequence":98,"title":"評估摻雜活化","titleEn":"Evaluate dopant activation","objective":"活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","objectiveEn":"Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將化學剖面積分與電性載子估計對照，判斷活化比例不能超出模型意義。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare integrated chemical profiles with electrically inferred carriers and evaluate the meaning of activation estimates.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：活化估計未納入補償與方法差異。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Activation estimate omits compensation and method differences. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","checkEn":"Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-098-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。 對應操作：將化學剖面積分與電性載子估計對照，判斷活化比例不能超出模型意義。","textEn":"Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions. Corresponding operation: Compare integrated chemical profiles with electrically inferred carriers and evaluate the meaning of activation estimates."},{"id":"sc-098-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：活化估計未納入補償與方法差異。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Activation estimate omits compensation and method differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估摻雜活化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate dopant activation\"?","options":["面劑量與總離子數區分，電荷態假設有標示。","活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。","漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。"],"optionsEn":["Areal dose is distinguished from total ion count and charge-state assumptions are stated.","Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions.","Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：活化估計註明量測方法及補償摻雜假設。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Activation estimates state measurement methods and compensation assumptions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-097"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-099","order":21,"sequence":99,"title":"量測接面深度","titleEn":"Measure junction depth","objective":"接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","objectiveEn":"Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將施體與受體剖面畫在同一圖，以淨摻雜轉換位置辨識接面。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Plot donor and acceptor profiles together and locate the change in net doping.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：植入峰值被當作接面位置。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Implant peak mistaken for junction position. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","checkEn":"Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-099-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。 對應操作：將施體與受體剖面畫在同一圖，以淨摻雜轉換位置辨識接面。","textEn":"Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak. Corresponding operation: Plot donor and acceptor profiles together and locate the change in net doping."},{"id":"sc-099-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：植入峰值被當作接面位置。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Implant peak mistaken for junction position."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測接面深度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure junction depth\"?","options":["接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。","井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","合成濃度以分布相加，非取各次峰值最大者。"],"optionsEn":["Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak.","Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","The combined profile sums distributions rather than taking only the largest peak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：接面深度由淨濃度判定，不等同植入濃度峰值。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Junction depth follows net doping rather than the implant-concentration peak. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-098"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-100","order":22,"sequence":100,"title":"檢查井區片電阻","titleEn":"Inspect well sheet resistance","objective":"異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。","objectiveEn":"Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較同批多點片電阻與植入、退火履歷，排除探針接觸不良。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare within-lot sheet resistance against implant and anneal histories and exclude poor probe contacts.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：探針接觸異常未複測。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Probe-contact outliers not remeasured. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。","checkEn":"Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-100-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。 對應操作：比較同批多點片電阻與植入、退火履歷，排除探針接觸不良。","textEn":"Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts. Corresponding operation: Compare within-lot sheet resistance against implant and anneal histories and exclude poor probe contacts."},{"id":"sc-100-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：探針接觸異常未複測。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Probe-contact outliers not remeasured."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查井區片電阻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect well sheet resistance\"?","options":["井區型態與元件本體電位安排一致。","通道化判斷來自尾端差異，未假設高斯分布永遠成立。","異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Well type is consistent with device-body biasing.","Channeling is diagnosed from tails without assuming every profile is Gaussian.","Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：異常點複測後再決定是否屬製程偏差。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Outliers are remeasured before being classified as process shifts. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-099"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-101","order":23,"sequence":101,"title":"量測井區接面漏電","titleEn":"Measure well-junction leakage","objective":"不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","objectiveEn":"Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較反向偏壓下的示意 I-V，將破壞性崩潰與低場漏電分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare illustrative reverse-bias I-V curves and distinguish breakdown from low-field leakage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：低場漏電與崩潰機制混判。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Low-field leakage confused with breakdown. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","checkEn":"Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-101-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。 對應操作：比較反向偏壓下的示意 I-V，將破壞性崩潰與低場漏電分開。","textEn":"Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms. Corresponding operation: Compare illustrative reverse-bias I-V curves and distinguish breakdown from low-field leakage."},{"id":"sc-101-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：低場漏電與崩潰機制混判。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Low-field leakage confused with breakdown."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測井區接面漏電」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure well-junction leakage\"?","options":["降低通道化的設定仍須檢查幾何遮蔽。","不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。","深井形成的隔離路徑可在剖面連續追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["A channeling-reduction choice is also checked for geometric shadowing.","Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms.","The isolation path created by the deep well can be followed continuously in the section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不同電場區間使用對應失效解釋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Different field regimes are interpreted using their appropriate failure mechanisms. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-100"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-102","order":24,"sequence":102,"title":"建立通道調整植入分支","titleEn":"Build a channel-adjust implant branch","objective":"傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","objectiveEn":"Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在平面 CMOS 分支加入通道調整層，查看閾值與遷移率的取捨。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add a channel-adjust layer to the planar CMOS branch and compare threshold and mobility trade-offs.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：將平面通道植入強套奈米片。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Planar channel implantation imposed on nanosheets. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","checkEn":"Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-102-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。 對應操作：在平面 CMOS 分支加入通道調整層，查看閾值與遷移率的取捨。","textEn":"Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets. Corresponding operation: Add a channel-adjust layer to the planar CMOS branch and compare threshold and mobility trade-offs."},{"id":"sc-102-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：將平面通道植入強套奈米片。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Planar channel implantation imposed on nanosheets."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立通道調整植入分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build a channel-adjust implant branch\"?","options":["傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。","未植入區有連續遮蔽，開口與井區對齊。","傾角與旋轉角分開記錄，遮蔽方向能被重現。"],"optionsEn":["Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets.","Protected regions have continuous masking and openings align with the well layout.","Tilt and twist are recorded separately and shadowing direction is reproducible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：傳統通道植入未被當成低摻雜奈米片的必經步驟。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Conventional channel implantation is not presented as mandatory for lightly doped nanosheets. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-101"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-103","order":25,"sequence":103,"title":"評估井區與隔離交互作用","titleEn":"Evaluate well-isolation interaction","objective":"漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。","objectiveEn":"Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把井區擴散邊界疊在 STI 側壁，檢查角部電場與漏電位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay diffused well boundaries on STI sidewalls and inspect corner fields and leakage locations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：井區邊界與 STI 角部未對位。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Well boundaries not registered to STI corners. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。","checkEn":"Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-103-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。 對應操作：把井區擴散邊界疊在 STI 側壁，檢查角部電場與漏電位置。","textEn":"Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry. Corresponding operation: Overlay diffused well boundaries on STI sidewalls and inspect corner fields and leakage locations."},{"id":"sc-103-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：井區邊界與 STI 角部未對位。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Well boundaries not registered to STI corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估井區與隔離交互作用」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate well-isolation interaction\"?","options":["遮罩下的尾端分布納入評估，不能只看平均射程。","掃描均勻性按有效面積評估且保留邊緣異常。","漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。"],"optionsEn":["The under-mask tail is evaluated rather than only mean projected range.","Uniformity is assessed over the usable area while retaining edge anomalies.","Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：漏電位置與接面、隔離幾何的交集相符。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Leakage locations are consistent with the intersection of junction and isolation geometry. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-102"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-104","order":26,"sequence":104,"title":"交接井區電性地圖","titleEn":"Handoff the well electrical map","objective":"井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","objectiveEn":"Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：彙整濃度剖面、片電阻與漏電三種證據，標出後續熱步驟還會改變的部分。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine concentration, sheet-resistance and leakage evidence and mark features affected by later thermal steps.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：後續熱歷史造成剖面繼續改變。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Later thermal history continues changing the profile. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","checkEn":"Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-104-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。 對應操作：彙整濃度剖面、片電阻與漏電三種證據，標出後續熱步驟還會改變的部分。","textEn":"Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently. Corresponding operation: Combine concentration, sheet-resistance and leakage evidence and mark features affected by later thermal steps."},{"id":"sc-104-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"植入面劑量、深度分布、化學濃度與活性載子濃度是不同量。退火可能修復損傷並活化摻雜，也會改變擴散剖面。 本步特別排查：後續熱歷史造成剖面繼續改變。","textEn":"Implanted areal dose, depth distribution, chemical concentration and active-carrier concentration are different quantities. Annealing can repair damage and activate dopants while also changing diffusion profiles. Specifically examine: Later thermal history continues changing the profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接井區電性地圖」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handoff the well electrical map\"?","options":["充電風險以局部電位差判讀，未只看平均束流。","井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。","所選離子造成的摻雜型態與目標井區相符。"],"optionsEn":["Charging risk is assessed through local potential differences rather than average beam current.","Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently.","The dopant type associated with the species matches the intended well."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：井區驗證保留後續熱預算依賴，未宣稱當下剖面永久固定。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Well verification retains dependence on later thermal budget rather than freezing the current profile permanently. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-applied-implant","sc-mc-index","sc-imec-nanosheet"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-103"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m05","order":5,"title":"閘極介電層與熱氧化","titleEn":"Gate dielectrics and thermal oxidation","description":"分開傳統氧化與高 k 分支，以物理厚度、等效氧化厚度、C-V、漏電及失效分布驗證介電層。","descriptionEn":"Separate conventional oxide and high-k branches and evaluate them with physical thickness, EOT, C-V, leakage and failure distributions.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-105","order":1,"sequence":105,"title":"選擇閘極介電路線","titleEn":"Select the gate-dielectric route","objective":"高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","objectiveEn":"High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較熱氧化矽閘極與高介電常數堆疊，標出各自適用的示範元件。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thermal-silica gates with high-k stacks and label the example devices used for each.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：傳統氧化與高 k 路線混接。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Conventional oxide and high-k routes mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","checkEn":"High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-105-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。 對應操作：比較熱氧化矽閘極與高介電常數堆疊，標出各自適用的示範元件。","textEn":"High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers. Corresponding operation: Compare thermal-silica gates with high-k stacks and label the example devices used for each."},{"id":"sc-105-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：傳統氧化與高 k 路線混接。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Conventional oxide and high-k routes mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇閘極介電路線」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select the gate-dielectric route\"?","options":["高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。","厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。"],"optionsEn":["High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth.","Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-104"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-106","order":2,"sequence":106,"title":"核對前清洗終態","titleEn":"Verify the pre-gate surface state","objective":"起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。","objectiveEn":"The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較表面氧化、碳殘留與等待時間，選取可供閘極形成的起始表面。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare surface oxidation, carbon residue and queue time to select a starting surface for gate formation.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：清洗終態與介電需求不符。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Cleaned surface state mismatches dielectric requirements. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。","checkEn":"The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-106-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。 對應操作：比較表面氧化、碳殘留與等待時間，選取可供閘極形成的起始表面。","textEn":"The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records. Corresponding operation: Compare surface oxidation, carbon residue and queue time to select a starting surface for gate formation."},{"id":"sc-106-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：清洗終態與介電需求不符。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Cleaned surface state mismatches dielectric requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對前清洗終態」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify the pre-gate surface state\"?","options":["新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-105"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-107","order":3,"sequence":107,"title":"映射既有氧化層","titleEn":"Map pre-existing oxide","objective":"初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。","objectiveEn":"Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用多點薄膜模型估計原始氧化層，作為新增成長的初值。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Estimate initial oxide with multipoint film models and use it as the initial condition for growth.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：初始氧化厚度漏算或重算。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Initial oxide omitted or double-counted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。","checkEn":"Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-107-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。 對應操作：用多點薄膜模型估計原始氧化層，作為新增成長的初值。","textEn":"Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence. Corresponding operation: Estimate initial oxide with multipoint film models and use it as the initial condition for growth."},{"id":"sc-107-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：初始氧化厚度漏算或重算。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Initial oxide omitted or double-counted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「映射既有氧化層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Map pre-existing oxide\"?","options":["電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。","晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。"],"optionsEn":["Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence.","Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-106"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-108","order":4,"sequence":108,"title":"比較乾式與濕式氧化","titleEn":"Compare dry and wet oxidation","objective":"成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","objectiveEn":"Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：保持模型其他假設一致，切換氧化物種並比較厚度對時間的曲線。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Keep other assumptions fixed while switching oxidizing species and comparing thickness-time curves.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：以生長速度推斷相同品質。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Growth speed used to infer identical quality. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","checkEn":"Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-108-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。 對應操作：保持模型其他假設一致，切換氧化物種並比較厚度對時間的曲線。","textEn":"Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use. Corresponding operation: Keep other assumptions fixed while switching oxidizing species and comparing thickness-time curves."},{"id":"sc-108-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：以生長速度推斷相同品質。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Growth speed used to infer identical quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較乾式與濕式氧化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare dry and wet oxidation\"?","options":["成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。","EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions.","EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-107"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-109","order":5,"sequence":109,"title":"識別氧化控制區域","titleEn":"Identify oxidation-rate regimes","objective":"同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。","objectiveEn":"One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在薄膜與厚膜區分別查看成長曲線斜率，判讀界面反應或擴散限制。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect growth-curve slopes in thin and thick regimes and identify interface-reaction or diffusion limitations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：常數速率外推超出適用區。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Constant rate extrapolated beyond its regime. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。","checkEn":"One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-109-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。 對應操作：在薄膜與厚膜區分別查看成長曲線斜率，判讀界面反應或擴散限制。","textEn":"One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range. Corresponding operation: Inspect growth-curve slopes in thin and thick regimes and identify interface-reaction or diffusion limitations."},{"id":"sc-109-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：常數速率外推超出適用區。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Constant rate extrapolated beyond its regime."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「識別氧化控制區域」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify oxidation-rate regimes\"?","options":["前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-108"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-110","order":6,"sequence":110,"title":"選擇氧化模型範圍","titleEn":"Choose the oxidation-model range","objective":"模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。","objectiveEn":"Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將示意薄氧化層資料與 Deal-Grove 型擬合比較，圈出系統性偏離。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare illustrative thin-oxide data with a Deal-Grove-type fit and flag systematic deviations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：薄氧化層超出簡化模型有效範圍。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Thin oxide outside simplified-model validity. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。","checkEn":"Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-110-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。 對應操作：將示意薄氧化層資料與 Deal-Grove 型擬合比較，圈出系統性偏離。","textEn":"Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth. Corresponding operation: Compare illustrative thin-oxide data with a Deal-Grove-type fit and flag systematic deviations."},{"id":"sc-110-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：薄氧化層超出簡化模型有效範圍。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Thin oxide outside simplified-model validity."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇氧化模型範圍」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Choose the oxidation-model range\"?","options":["界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。","徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。"],"optionsEn":["Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth.","Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-109"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-111","order":7,"sequence":111,"title":"追蹤氧化消耗矽","titleEn":"Track silicon consumption during oxidation","objective":"新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","objectiveEn":"New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在剖面同時移動氧化層外表面與矽界面，檢查體積成長。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Move both the oxide outer surface and silicon interface in a cross-section to track volume growth.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未計入被氧化消耗的矽。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Oxidation-consumed silicon omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","checkEn":"New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-111-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。 對應操作：在剖面同時移動氧化層外表面與矽界面，檢查體積成長。","textEn":"New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface. Corresponding operation: Move both the oxide outer surface and silicon interface in a cross-section to track volume growth."},{"id":"sc-111-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：未計入被氧化消耗的矽。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Oxidation-consumed silicon omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「追蹤氧化消耗矽」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Track silicon consumption during oxidation\"?","options":["新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。","僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。"],"optionsEn":["New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone.","A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-110"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-112","order":8,"sequence":112,"title":"比較晶面氧化差異","titleEn":"Compare orientation-dependent oxidation","objective":"晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。","objectiveEn":"Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在相同模型條件比較不同晶面，觀察成長曲線差異。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare crystal orientations under the same model conditions and inspect growth-curve differences.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：比較晶向時其他條件同時改變。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Other conditions change during orientation comparison. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。","checkEn":"Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-112-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。 對應操作：在相同模型條件比較不同晶面，觀察成長曲線差異。","textEn":"Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes. Corresponding operation: Compare crystal orientations under the same model conditions and inspect growth-curve differences."},{"id":"sc-112-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：比較晶向時其他條件同時改變。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Other conditions change during orientation comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較晶面氧化差異」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare orientation-dependent oxidation\"?","options":["粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。"],"optionsEn":["Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-111"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-113","order":9,"sequence":113,"title":"評估摻雜對氧化影響","titleEn":"Evaluate doping effects on oxidation","objective":"不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。","objectiveEn":"One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較高摻雜和低摻雜區的示意成長行為，查看模型適用限制。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare illustrative growth behavior in heavily and lightly doped regions and inspect model limitations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略摻雜對成長動力學影響。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Doping effects on growth kinetics ignored. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。","checkEn":"One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-113-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。 對應操作：比較高摻雜和低摻雜區的示意成長行為，查看模型適用限制。","textEn":"One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions. Corresponding operation: Compare illustrative growth behavior in heavily and lightly doped regions and inspect model limitations."},{"id":"sc-113-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：忽略摻雜對成長動力學影響。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Doping effects on growth kinetics ignored."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估摻雜對氧化影響」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate doping effects on oxidation\"?","options":["漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。","厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions.","Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-112"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-114","order":10,"sequence":114,"title":"檢查爐管軸向均勻性","titleEn":"Inspect furnace axial uniformity","objective":"前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","objectiveEn":"Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把陪片位置與膜厚串成軸向圖，分辨裝載位置效應。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Plot monitor positions and oxide thickness along the furnace axis to identify loading-position effects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：批次平均掩蓋晶舟位置差異。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Batch average hides boat-position differences. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","checkEn":"Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-114-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。 對應操作：把陪片位置與膜厚串成軸向圖，分辨裝載位置效應。","textEn":"Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average. Corresponding operation: Plot monitor positions and oxide thickness along the furnace axis to identify loading-position effects."},{"id":"sc-114-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：批次平均掩蓋晶舟位置差異。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Batch average hides boat-position differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查爐管軸向均勻性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect furnace axial uniformity\"?","options":["前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。"],"optionsEn":["Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-113"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-115","order":11,"sequence":115,"title":"檢查徑向氧化均勻性","titleEn":"Inspect radial oxidation uniformity","objective":"徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。","objectiveEn":"Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在同一晶圓比較中心與邊緣膜厚，對照熱場和流場示意。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare center and edge oxide thickness on one wafer against thermal and flow models.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：徑向變化與晶圓間差異混合。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Radial variation pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。","checkEn":"Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-115-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。 對應操作：在同一晶圓比較中心與邊緣膜厚，對照熱場和流場示意。","textEn":"Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences. Corresponding operation: Compare center and edge oxide thickness on one wafer against thermal and flow models."},{"id":"sc-115-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：徑向變化與晶圓間差異混合。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Radial variation pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查徑向氧化均勻性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect radial oxidation uniformity\"?","options":["電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。"],"optionsEn":["Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-114"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-116","order":12,"sequence":116,"title":"記錄氧化升降溫貢獻","titleEn":"Account for oxidation during ramps","objective":"總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。","objectiveEn":"The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將升溫、保持與降溫段的成長貢獻分開積算。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Separate growth contributions during heating, hold and cooling portions of the trajectory.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：升降溫期間成長貢獻漏算。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Growth during heating and cooling omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。","checkEn":"The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-116-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。 對應操作：將升溫、保持與降溫段的成長貢獻分開積算。","textEn":"The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone. Corresponding operation: Separate growth contributions during heating, hold and cooling portions of the trajectory."},{"id":"sc-116-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：升降溫期間成長貢獻漏算。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Growth during heating and cooling omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「記錄氧化升降溫貢獻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Account for oxidation during ramps\"?","options":["電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。","EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone.","EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-115"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-117","order":13,"sequence":117,"title":"檢查氧化層表面形貌","titleEn":"Inspect oxide surface morphology","objective":"粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","objectiveEn":"Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較氧化前後 AFM 圖及局部突點，將粒子與粗糙度分開。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare pre- and post-oxidation AFM maps and separate particles from roughness.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：少量粒子支配粗糙度數值。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: A few particles dominate roughness statistics. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","checkEn":"Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-117-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。 對應操作：比較氧化前後 AFM 圖及局部突點，將粒子與粗糙度分開。","textEn":"Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects. Corresponding operation: Compare pre- and post-oxidation AFM maps and separate particles from roughness."},{"id":"sc-117-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：少量粒子支配粗糙度數值。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: A few particles dominate roughness statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查氧化層表面形貌」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect oxide surface morphology\"?","options":["粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。"],"optionsEn":["Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-116"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-118","order":14,"sequence":118,"title":"量測氧化層光學厚度","titleEn":"Measure oxide optical thickness","objective":"厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。","objectiveEn":"Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對不同波長的反射資料擬合氧化層厚度，檢查擬合殘差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Fit oxide thickness to multiwavelength reflection data and inspect residuals.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：厚度與光學常數參數互補。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Compensating thickness and optical-constant parameters. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。","checkEn":"Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-118-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。 對應操作：對不同波長的反射資料擬合氧化層厚度，檢查擬合殘差。","textEn":"Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality. Corresponding operation: Fit oxide thickness to multiwavelength reflection data and inspect residuals."},{"id":"sc-118-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：厚度與光學常數參數互補。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Compensating thickness and optical-constant parameters."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測氧化層光學厚度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure oxide optical thickness\"?","options":["界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。"],"optionsEn":["Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：厚度估計伴隨模型與擬合品質。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Thickness estimates include the optical model and fit quality. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-117"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-119","order":15,"sequence":119,"title":"建立 MOS 電容測試結構","titleEn":"Build a MOS capacitor test structure","objective":"測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","objectiveEn":"Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在示意氧化層上放置閘極與背接觸，確認量測電場穿過介電層。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place a gate and backside contact on the modeled oxide and verify the measurement field crosses the dielectric.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：電極有效面積或背接觸不明。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unclear effective area or backside contact. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","checkEn":"Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-119-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。 對應操作：在示意氧化層上放置閘極與背接觸，確認量測電場穿過介電層。","textEn":"Test area and electrode contact paths are defined. Corresponding operation: Place a gate and backside contact on the modeled oxide and verify the measurement field crosses the dielectric."},{"id":"sc-119-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：電極有效面積或背接觸不明。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Unclear effective area or backside contact."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立 MOS 電容測試結構」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build a MOS capacitor test structure\"?","options":["起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。","測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。","僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。"],"optionsEn":["The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records.","Test area and electrode contact paths are defined.","A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：測試面積與電極接觸路徑已定義。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Test area and electrode contact paths are defined. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-118"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-120","order":16,"sequence":120,"title":"辨識 MOS 電容區域","titleEn":"Identify MOS capacitance regimes","objective":"電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","objectiveEn":"Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在 C-V 圖依序標記累積、空乏與反轉，與基板型態交叉核對。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Label accumulation, depletion and inversion on a C-V curve and cross-check substrate type.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未依基板型態判讀電壓極性。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Voltage polarity interpreted without substrate type. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","checkEn":"Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-120-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。 對應操作：在 C-V 圖依序標記累積、空乏與反轉，與基板型態交叉核對。","textEn":"Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern. Corresponding operation: Label accumulation, depletion and inversion on a C-V curve and cross-check substrate type."},{"id":"sc-120-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：未依基板型態判讀電壓極性。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Voltage polarity interpreted without substrate type."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識 MOS 電容區域」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify MOS capacitance regimes\"?","options":["電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。","介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。"],"optionsEn":["Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern.","Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：電壓極性依基板型態判讀，而非死記曲線左右。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Voltage polarity follows substrate type rather than a memorized left-right curve pattern. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-119"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-121","order":17,"sequence":121,"title":"萃取等效氧化厚度","titleEn":"Extract equivalent oxide thickness","objective":"EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。","objectiveEn":"EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用面積正規化電容比較不同介電堆疊，區分電性等效與實體厚度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare area-normalized capacitance across stacks and distinguish electrical equivalence from physical thickness.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：EOT 與實體厚度混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: EOT confused with physical thickness. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。","checkEn":"EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-121-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。 對應操作：用面積正規化電容比較不同介電堆疊，區分電性等效與實體厚度。","textEn":"EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness. Corresponding operation: Compare area-normalized capacitance across stacks and distinguish electrical equivalence from physical thickness."},{"id":"sc-121-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：EOT 與實體厚度混用。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: EOT confused with physical thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「萃取等效氧化厚度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Extract equivalent oxide thickness\"?","options":["漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：EOT 不被當成高 k 薄膜的幾何厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: EOT is not interpreted as the high-k film's geometric thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-120"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-122","order":18,"sequence":122,"title":"分析串聯介電層","titleEn":"Analyze series dielectric layers","objective":"最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","objectiveEn":"The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把界面氧化層與高 k 層拆成串聯電容，調整其中一層查看總電容。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Represent interfacial oxide and high-k material as series capacitors and vary one layer to inspect total capacitance.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：串聯電容被誤算成並聯。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Series capacitors treated as parallel. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","checkEn":"The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-122-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。 對應操作：把界面氧化層與高 k 層拆成串聯電容，調整其中一層查看總電容。","textEn":"The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness. Corresponding operation: Represent interfacial oxide and high-k material as series capacitors and vary one layer to inspect total capacitance."},{"id":"sc-122-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：串聯電容被誤算成並聯。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Series capacitors treated as parallel."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析串聯介電層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze series dielectric layers\"?","options":["同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。","最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。","異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。"],"optionsEn":["One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range.","The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness.","Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：最薄幾何層不必然對等效厚度貢獻最小。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The thinnest geometric layer is not automatically the smallest contributor to equivalent thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-121"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-123","order":19,"sequence":123,"title":"形成高 k 界面層分支","titleEn":"Form the high-k interfacial-layer branch","objective":"界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","objectiveEn":"Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在高 k 分支插入受控界面層，觀察表面鈍化和 EOT 的取捨。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Insert a controlled interface layer in the high-k branch and compare passivation with EOT trade-offs.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只看鈍化改善而漏掉電容代價。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Passivation improvement hides capacitance cost. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","checkEn":"Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-123-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。 對應操作：在高 k 分支插入受控界面層，觀察表面鈍化和 EOT 的取捨。","textEn":"Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together. Corresponding operation: Insert a controlled interface layer in the high-k branch and compare passivation with EOT trade-offs."},{"id":"sc-123-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：只看鈍化改善而漏掉電容代價。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Passivation improvement hides capacitance cost."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「形成高 k 界面層分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Form the high-k interfacial-layer branch\"?","options":["界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。","未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","模型失配有標記，未把外推值當成量測真值。"],"optionsEn":["Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together.","Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","Model mismatch is flagged rather than treating extrapolation as measured truth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：界面品質改善與電容代價同時呈現。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Interface-quality improvement and capacitance cost are shown together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-122"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-124","order":20,"sequence":124,"title":"檢查介面電荷位移","titleEn":"Inspect interface-charge shifts","objective":"僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。","objectiveEn":"A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較處理前後 C-V 橫向位移，區分功函數改變與固定電荷可能性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare horizontal C-V shifts and distinguish possible work-function changes from fixed charge.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把平帶位移唯一歸因於固定電荷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Flat-band shift uniquely assigned to fixed charge. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。","checkEn":"A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-124-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。 對應操作：比較處理前後 C-V 橫向位移，區分功函數改變與固定電荷可能性。","textEn":"A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source. Corresponding operation: Compare horizontal C-V shifts and distinguish possible work-function changes from fixed charge."},{"id":"sc-124-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：把平帶位移唯一歸因於固定電荷。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Flat-band shift uniquely assigned to fixed charge."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查介面電荷位移」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect interface-charge shifts\"?","options":["電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","新增氧化層不被畫成全部位於原始矽表面之上。","僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","New oxide is not drawn entirely above the original silicon surface.","A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：僅憑平帶位移不唯一認定某一類電荷來源。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A flat-band shift alone is not treated as unique identification of one charge source. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-123"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-125","order":21,"sequence":125,"title":"診斷介面態響應","titleEn":"Diagnose interface-state response","objective":"介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","objectiveEn":"Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同量測頻率下的 C-V 或導納變化，標記頻率相依區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare C-V or admittance across measurement frequencies and mark frequency-dependent regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未控制頻率與量測條件。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Frequency and measurement conditions uncontrolled. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","checkEn":"Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-125-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。 對應操作：比較不同量測頻率下的 C-V 或導納變化，標記頻率相依區。","textEn":"Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions. Corresponding operation: Compare C-V or admittance across measurement frequencies and mark frequency-dependent regions."},{"id":"sc-125-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：未控制頻率與量測條件。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Frequency and measurement conditions uncontrolled."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷介面態響應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose interface-state response\"?","options":["晶向效果與溫度、初始膜厚變化分開。","介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。","幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。"],"optionsEn":["Orientation effects are separated from temperature and initial-thickness changes.","Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions.","Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：介面態判讀包含頻率及量測條件。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Interface-state interpretation includes frequency and measurement conditions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-124"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-126","order":22,"sequence":126,"title":"檢查閘極漏電","titleEn":"Inspect gate leakage","objective":"漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","objectiveEn":"Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將閘極電流按面積正規化，比較不同電場而非直接比較相同端電壓。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Normalize gate current by area and compare electric fields rather than identical terminal voltages alone.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：相同電壓被當成相同電場。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Same voltage mistaken for the same field. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","checkEn":"Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-126-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。 對應操作：將閘極電流按面積正規化，比較不同電場而非直接比較相同端電壓。","textEn":"Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions. Corresponding operation: Normalize gate current by area and compare electric fields rather than identical terminal voltages alone."},{"id":"sc-126-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：相同電壓被當成相同電場。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Same voltage mistaken for the same field."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查閘極漏電」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect gate leakage\"?","options":["漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。","高 k 與傳統厚氧化層是明示分支，不是依序必做的同一堆疊。","不以單一裸矽模型保證所有摻雜區相同成長。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions.","High-k and conventional thick-oxide routes are explicit branches, not mandatory sequential layers.","One bare-silicon model is not assumed to guarantee identical growth across doped regions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：漏電比較交代有效面積、厚度及場強假設。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Leakage comparisons state effective area, thickness and field assumptions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-125"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-127","order":23,"sequence":127,"title":"辨識局部介電弱點","titleEn":"Identify local dielectric weak spots","objective":"異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。","objectiveEn":"Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把局部缺陷圖與多顆 MOS 電容的漏電分布對照，尋找位置群聚。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare local defect maps with leakage distributions from multiple MOS capacitors and identify spatial clusters.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：空間群聚與孤立離群值混合。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Spatial clusters mixed with isolated outliers. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。","checkEn":"Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-127-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。 對應操作：把局部缺陷圖與多顆 MOS 電容的漏電分布對照，尋找位置群聚。","textEn":"Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately. Corresponding operation: Compare local defect maps with leakage distributions from multiple MOS capacitors and identify spatial clusters."},{"id":"sc-127-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：空間群聚與孤立離群值混合。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Spatial clusters mixed with isolated outliers."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識局部介電弱點」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify local dielectric weak spots\"?","options":["起始表面狀態能連結到前清洗紀錄。","前、中、後位置分別保留，不只報整批平均。","異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。"],"optionsEn":["The initial surface state is traceable to pre-clean records.","Front, middle and rear positions remain visible rather than only a batch average.","Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：異常群聚與孤立離群值分開分析。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Spatial clusters and isolated outliers are analyzed separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-126"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-128","order":24,"sequence":128,"title":"比較介電崩潰分布","titleEn":"Compare dielectric-breakdown distributions","objective":"未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","objectiveEn":"Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較相同應力定義下的樣本分布，保留未失效樣本的截尾資訊。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare sample distributions under a consistent stress definition and retain censoring for unfailed samples.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未失效樣本遭刪除或錯誤編碼。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unfailed samples deleted or miscoded. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","checkEn":"Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-128-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。 對應操作：比較相同應力定義下的樣本分布，保留未失效樣本的截尾資訊。","textEn":"Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime. Corresponding operation: Compare sample distributions under a consistent stress definition and retain censoring for unfailed samples."},{"id":"sc-128-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：未失效樣本遭刪除或錯誤編碼。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Unfailed samples deleted or miscoded."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較介電崩潰分布」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare dielectric-breakdown distributions\"?","options":["徑向趨勢有空間證據且不與晶圓間差異混合。","未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。","初始氧化層未被重複加算或假設為零。"],"optionsEn":["Radial trends have spatial evidence and are not pooled with wafer-to-wafer differences.","Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime.","Initial oxide is neither double-counted nor assumed zero without evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：未失效樣本不被刪除或當作零壽命。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Unfailed samples are neither discarded nor assigned zero lifetime. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-127"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-129","order":25,"sequence":129,"title":"核對介電層熱歷史","titleEn":"Check dielectric thermal history","objective":"電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","objectiveEn":"Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將後續沉積與退火的示意熱歷程加到介電層紀錄，查看界面變化風險。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add downstream deposition and anneal histories to the dielectric record and inspect possible interface changes.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：電性資料對應錯誤熱歷史。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Electrical data paired with wrong thermal history. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","checkEn":"Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-129-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。 對應操作：將後續沉積與退火的示意熱歷程加到介電層紀錄，查看界面變化風險。","textEn":"Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history. Corresponding operation: Add downstream deposition and anneal histories to the dielectric record and inspect possible interface changes."},{"id":"sc-129-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：電性資料對應錯誤熱歷史。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Electrical data paired with wrong thermal history."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對介電層熱歷史」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check dielectric thermal history\"?","options":["電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。","成長速率差異不被誤解為相同品質或相同用途。","總膜厚模型包含適用的過渡段，未只取保持時間。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history.","Growth-rate differences are not equated with identical film quality or use.","The thickness model includes relevant transitions rather than hold time alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：電性驗證狀態對應正確熱歷史。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Electrical verification is associated with the correct thermal history. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-128"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-130","order":26,"sequence":130,"title":"交接閘極介電證據","titleEn":"Handoff gate-dielectric evidence","objective":"幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。","objectiveEn":"Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：整合實體厚度、EOT、漏電與缺陷四種資料，標明分支及模型。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine physical thickness, EOT, leakage and defect data and label the route and model.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：單一厚度合格掩蓋漏電或缺陷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Passing thickness hides leakage or defects. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。","checkEn":"Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-130-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。 對應操作：整合實體厚度、EOT、漏電與缺陷四種資料，標明分支及模型。","textEn":"Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved. Corresponding operation: Combine physical thickness, EOT, leakage and defect data and label the route and model."},{"id":"sc-130-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"介電堆疊的幾何厚度與電性等效厚度不同。光學、電容及漏電各自對材料的不同特性敏感，不能互相完全替代。 本步特別排查：單一厚度合格掩蓋漏電或缺陷。","textEn":"Geometric thickness differs from electrical equivalent thickness. Optical, capacitance and leakage measurements probe different material properties and are not interchangeable. Specifically examine: Passing thickness hides leakage or defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接閘極介電證據」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handoff gate-dielectric evidence\"?","options":["同一常數速率未被套用到全部厚度範圍。","粗糙度評估未被少數異物完全主導。","幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。"],"optionsEn":["One constant rate is not applied across the entire thickness range.","Roughness evaluation is not dominated unknowingly by a few foreign objects.","Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：幾何、電性與可靠度證據互相一致，缺測項保留未決。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Geometric, electrical and reliability evidence are consistent; missing measurements remain unresolved. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-ualberta-oxidation","sc-lam-deposition","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-129"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m06","order":6,"title":"ALD、CVD 與 PVD 薄膜","titleEn":"ALD, CVD and PVD films","description":"拆解成核、供料、表面反應、覆蓋、應力與膜質量測；三種沉積技術是依目的選用的分支。","descriptionEn":"Decompose nucleation, delivery, surface reactions, coverage, stress and film metrology; deposition families are purpose-dependent alternatives.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-131","order":1,"sequence":131,"title":"選擇沉積機制","titleEn":"Select a deposition mechanism","objective":"選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。","objectiveEn":"Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對同一溝槽比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 成長示意，標示方向性與表面反應。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare PVD, CVD and ALD growth in the same trench and label directionality and surface reactions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：沉積機制不符合覆蓋幾何。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Deposition mechanism incompatible with coverage geometry. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。","checkEn":"Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-131-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。 對應操作：對同一溝槽比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 成長示意，標示方向性與表面反應。","textEn":"Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone. Corresponding operation: Compare PVD, CVD and ALD growth in the same trench and label directionality and surface reactions."},{"id":"sc-131-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：沉積機制不符合覆蓋幾何。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Deposition mechanism incompatible with coverage geometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇沉積機制」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select a deposition mechanism\"?","options":["名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。","自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone.","Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-130"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-132","order":2,"sequence":132,"title":"核對沉積表面終態","titleEn":"Verify deposition surface termination","objective":"表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","objectiveEn":"Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較氧化表面、氫終止與污染表面的示意成核行為。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare schematic nucleation on oxidized, hydrogen-terminated and contaminated surfaces.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：成核差異源於表面終態。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Nucleation differences arise from surface termination. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","checkEn":"Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-132-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面終態差異列入成核解釋。 對應操作：比較氧化表面、氫終止與污染表面的示意成核行為。","textEn":"Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation. Corresponding operation: Compare schematic nucleation on oxidized, hydrogen-terminated and contaminated surfaces."},{"id":"sc-132-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：成核差異源於表面終態。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Nucleation differences arise from surface termination."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對沉積表面終態」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify deposition surface termination\"?","options":["表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。","表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。"],"optionsEn":["Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction.","Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面終態差異列入成核解釋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-131"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-133","order":3,"sequence":133,"title":"檢查真空背景","titleEn":"Inspect vacuum background","objective":"基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。","objectiveEn":"Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比對腔體空白壓力曲線與進氣曲線，辨識洩漏及放氣的可能訊號。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare blank-chamber and process-gas pressure traces to identify possible leaks and outgassing.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：總壓力未揭示氣體來源。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Total pressure does not reveal gas origin. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。","checkEn":"Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-133-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。 對應操作：比對腔體空白壓力曲線與進氣曲線，辨識洩漏及放氣的可能訊號。","textEn":"Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition. Corresponding operation: Compare blank-chamber and process-gas pressure traces to identify possible leaks and outgassing."},{"id":"sc-133-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：總壓力未揭示氣體來源。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Total pressure does not reveal gas origin."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查真空背景」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect vacuum background\"?","options":["新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。"],"optionsEn":["The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-132"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-134","order":4,"sequence":134,"title":"校核氣流分配","titleEn":"Check gas-flow distribution","objective":"入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。","objectiveEn":"Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將入口流量與晶圓上方流場示意連接，查看邊緣滯流區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Relate inlet flows to the wafer-level flow model and inspect stagnant edge regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：入口流量未反映表面耗用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Inlet flow does not reflect surface consumption. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。","checkEn":"Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-134-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。 對應操作：將入口流量與晶圓上方流場示意連接，查看邊緣滯流區。","textEn":"Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery. Corresponding operation: Relate inlet flows to the wafer-level flow model and inspect stagnant edge regions."},{"id":"sc-134-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：入口流量未反映表面耗用。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Inlet flow does not reflect surface consumption."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校核氣流分配」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check gas-flow distribution\"?","options":["晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。","兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。"],"optionsEn":["Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery.","The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-133"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-135","order":5,"sequence":135,"title":"評估沉積熱預算","titleEn":"Evaluate deposition thermal budget","objective":"路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","objectiveEn":"Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同沉積路線的熱歷史，與已形成接面及膜層的限制配對。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thermal histories of deposition routes against constraints from existing junctions and films.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：沉積熱歷史超出下層相容範圍。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Deposition thermal history incompatible with underlying layers. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","checkEn":"Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-135-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。 對應操作：比較不同沉積路線的熱歷史，與已形成接面及膜層的限制配對。","textEn":"Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures. Corresponding operation: Compare thermal histories of deposition routes against constraints from existing junctions and films."},{"id":"sc-135-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：沉積熱歷史超出下層相容範圍。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Deposition thermal history incompatible with underlying layers."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估沉積熱預算」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate deposition thermal budget\"?","options":["路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。","低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。"],"optionsEn":["Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","The slope fit is not forced through the origin.","A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-134"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-136","order":6,"sequence":136,"title":"模擬 ALD 首半反應","titleEn":"Model the first ALD half-reaction","objective":"自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。","objectiveEn":"Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在表面位點模型加入第一反應物，查看覆蓋度隨暴露增加的變化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Introduce the first reactant to surface sites and inspect coverage versus exposure.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未達表面飽和或誤認單層成長。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Surface not saturated or monolayer growth assumed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。","checkEn":"Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-136-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。 對應操作：在表面位點模型加入第一反應物，查看覆蓋度隨暴露增加的變化。","textEn":"Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse. Corresponding operation: Introduce the first reactant to surface sites and inspect coverage versus exposure."},{"id":"sc-136-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：未達表面飽和或誤認單層成長。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Surface not saturated or monolayer growth assumed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬 ALD 首半反應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model the first ALD half-reaction\"?","options":["穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","填充結論有截面連續性證據。","自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。"],"optionsEn":["A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-135"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-137","order":7,"sequence":137,"title":"檢查 ALD 第一吹掃","titleEn":"Inspect the first ALD purge","objective":"下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。","objectiveEn":"Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：追蹤多餘反應物與副產物從腔體退出，觀察死角殘留。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track excess reactant and byproducts leaving the chamber and inspect residual material in dead zones.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：反應物與副產物吹掃不完全。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Incomplete purge of reactant and byproducts. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。","checkEn":"Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-137-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。 對應操作：追蹤多餘反應物與副產物從腔體退出，觀察死角殘留。","textEn":"Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction. Corresponding operation: Track excess reactant and byproducts leaving the chamber and inspect residual material in dead zones."},{"id":"sc-137-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：反應物與副產物吹掃不完全。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Incomplete purge of reactant and byproducts."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查 ALD 第一吹掃」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect the first ALD purge\"?","options":["視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。","共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction.","Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-136"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-138","order":8,"sequence":138,"title":"模擬 ALD 次半反應","titleEn":"Model the second ALD half-reaction","objective":"新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","objectiveEn":"The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：讓第二反應物與已吸附表面作用，比較完成反應與未完成區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Let the second reactant interact with the adsorbed surface and compare completed and incomplete regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：表面反應未完成或殘留配基。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Incomplete surface reaction or residual ligands. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","checkEn":"The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-138-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。 對應操作：讓第二反應物與已吸附表面作用，比較完成反應與未完成區。","textEn":"The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately. Corresponding operation: Let the second reactant interact with the adsorbed surface and compare completed and incomplete regions."},{"id":"sc-138-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：表面反應未完成或殘留配基。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Incomplete surface reaction or residual ligands."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬 ALD 次半反應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model the second ALD half-reaction\"?","options":["新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。","靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。"],"optionsEn":["The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together.","Target history and thickness trends have traceable links."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-137"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-139","order":9,"sequence":139,"title":"檢查 ALD 次吹掃","titleEn":"Inspect the second ALD purge","objective":"兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。","objectiveEn":"The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在循環結束追蹤氣相殘留，對照重新開始首反應物的時點。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track gas-phase residue at cycle end against the restart of the first reactant.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：循環間反應物重疊。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Reactant overlap between cycles. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。","checkEn":"The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-139-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。 對應操作：在循環結束追蹤氣相殘留，對照重新開始首反應物的時點。","textEn":"The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions. Corresponding operation: Track gas-phase residue at cycle end against the restart of the first reactant."},{"id":"sc-139-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：循環間反應物重疊。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Reactant overlap between cycles."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查 ALD 次吹掃」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect the second ALD purge\"?","options":["名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-138"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-140","order":10,"sequence":140,"title":"擬合 ALD 每循環成長","titleEn":"Fit ALD growth per cycle","objective":"斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。","objectiveEn":"The slope fit is not forced through the origin.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用厚度對循環數資料分辨初期成核延遲與穩定成長斜率。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Use thickness versus cycle count to separate nucleation delay from steady growth per cycle.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The slope fit is not forced through the origin.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：成核延遲被強制過原點擬合掩蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Nucleation delay hidden by a forced-origin fit. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。","checkEn":"The slope fit is not forced through the origin.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-140-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。 對應操作：用厚度對循環數資料分辨初期成核延遲與穩定成長斜率。","textEn":"The slope fit is not forced through the origin. Corresponding operation: Use thickness versus cycle count to separate nucleation delay from steady growth per cycle."},{"id":"sc-140-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：成核延遲被強制過原點擬合掩蓋。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Nucleation delay hidden by a forced-origin fit."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「擬合 ALD 每循環成長」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Fit ALD growth per cycle\"?","options":["覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。","表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。"],"optionsEn":["The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","The slope fit is not forced through the origin.","Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The slope fit is not forced through the origin. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-139"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-141","order":11,"sequence":141,"title":"分析 ALD 溫度視窗","titleEn":"Analyze the ALD temperature window","objective":"穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","objectiveEn":"A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較覆蓋、成長率及殘留隨溫度的示意資料，找出相對穩定區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare schematic coverage, growth-rate and residue data versus temperature to identify a stable region.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只看成長率而忽略膜質。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Growth rate considered without film quality. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","checkEn":"A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-141-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。 對應操作：比較覆蓋、成長率及殘留隨溫度的示意資料，找出相對穩定區。","textEn":"A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone. Corresponding operation: Compare schematic coverage, growth-rate and residue data versus temperature to identify a stable region."},{"id":"sc-141-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：只看成長率而忽略膜質。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Growth rate considered without film quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析 ALD 溫度視窗」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze the ALD temperature window\"?","options":["穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。"],"optionsEn":["A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-140"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-142","order":12,"sequence":142,"title":"量測 ALD 深孔共形性","titleEn":"Measure ALD high-aspect-ratio conformality","objective":"共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。","objectiveEn":"Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在孔口、中段及底部取截面膜厚，對照反應物耗盡趨勢。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure thickness at the entrance, middle and bottom of a feature and compare reactant-depletion trends.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：孔底反應物不足而陪片正常。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Bottom reactant starvation despite normal planar monitors. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。","checkEn":"Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-142-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。 對應操作：在孔口、中段及底部取截面膜厚，對照反應物耗盡趨勢。","textEn":"Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone. Corresponding operation: Measure thickness at the entrance, middle and bottom of a feature and compare reactant-depletion trends."},{"id":"sc-142-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：孔底反應物不足而陪片正常。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Bottom reactant starvation despite normal planar monitors."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測 ALD 深孔共形性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure ALD high-aspect-ratio conformality\"?","options":["晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-141"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-143","order":13,"sequence":143,"title":"比較熱式與電漿 ALD","titleEn":"Compare thermal and plasma ALD","objective":"電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。","objectiveEn":"Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對同材料目標比較反應活性、方向性與敏感下層的示意影響。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare reactivity, directionality and effects on sensitive underlying layers for the same material target.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：電漿反應改善伴隨下層損傷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Improved plasma reaction accompanies underlayer damage. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。","checkEn":"Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-143-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。 對應操作：對同材料目標比較反應活性、方向性與敏感下層的示意影響。","textEn":"Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together. Corresponding operation: Compare reactivity, directionality and effects on sensitive underlying layers for the same material target."},{"id":"sc-143-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：電漿反應改善伴隨下層損傷。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Improved plasma reaction accompanies underlayer damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較熱式與電漿 ALD」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare thermal and plasma ALD\"?","options":["放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。","低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。"],"optionsEn":["Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together.","A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-142"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-144","order":14,"sequence":144,"title":"診斷 ALD 成核島","titleEn":"Diagnose ALD nucleation islands","objective":"名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","objectiveEn":"Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把早期循環表面影像按時間排列，追蹤島狀區合併為連續膜。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Order early-cycle surface images and track island coalescence into a continuous film.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：島狀膜被名義厚度誤判成連續。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Nominal thickness masks discontinuous islands. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","checkEn":"Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-144-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。 對應操作：把早期循環表面影像按時間排列，追蹤島狀區合併為連續膜。","textEn":"Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity. Corresponding operation: Order early-cycle surface images and track island coalescence into a continuous film."},{"id":"sc-144-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：島狀膜被名義厚度誤判成連續。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Nominal thickness masks discontinuous islands."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷 ALD 成核島」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose ALD nucleation islands\"?","options":["名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。","填充結論有截面連續性證據。","選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity.","The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：名義厚度增加不被當作膜已連續的充分證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Increasing nominal thickness is not sufficient evidence of film continuity. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-143"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-145","order":15,"sequence":145,"title":"模擬 CVD 表面反應","titleEn":"Model CVD surface reactions","objective":"表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。","objectiveEn":"Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較供料固定下不同表面反應速率，追蹤膜厚與前驅物消耗。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare surface-reaction rates under fixed delivery and track thickness and precursor consumption.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：表面反應與供料限制混判。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Surface-reaction and delivery limitations mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。","checkEn":"Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-145-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。 對應操作：比較供料固定下不同表面反應速率，追蹤膜厚與前驅物消耗。","textEn":"Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes. Corresponding operation: Compare surface-reaction rates under fixed delivery and track thickness and precursor consumption."},{"id":"sc-145-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：表面反應與供料限制混判。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Surface-reaction and delivery limitations mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬 CVD 表面反應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model CVD surface reactions\"?","options":["視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。"],"optionsEn":["Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面反應變化與氣相供料變化有分離比較。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Surface-reaction changes are compared separately from gas-delivery changes. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-144"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-146","order":16,"sequence":146,"title":"區分 CVD 傳質限制","titleEn":"Distinguish CVD mass-transfer limitation","objective":"限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","objectiveEn":"The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比提高供料及改變反應活性的兩組結果，判斷限制來源。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare increased delivery with changed reaction activity to diagnose the limiting mechanism.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：未用獨立變量比較限制機制。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Limiting mechanism inferred without independent variables. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","checkEn":"The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-146-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。 對應操作：對比提高供料及改變反應活性的兩組結果，判斷限制來源。","textEn":"The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone. Corresponding operation: Compare increased delivery with changed reaction activity to diagnose the limiting mechanism."},{"id":"sc-146-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：未用獨立變量比較限制機制。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Limiting mechanism inferred without independent variables."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「區分 CVD 傳質限制」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Distinguish CVD mass-transfer limitation\"?","options":["基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。","限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。","靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。"],"optionsEn":["Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition.","The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone.","Target history and thickness trends have traceable links."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：限制機制由敏感度差異判讀，非只憑溫度高低。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The limitation is inferred from sensitivity differences rather than temperature alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-145"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-147","order":17,"sequence":147,"title":"檢查 LPCVD 裝載效應","titleEn":"Inspect LPCVD loading effects","objective":"晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","objectiveEn":"Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同晶舟位置與圖案表面積的膜厚，標註反應物耗用。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thickness across boat positions and patterned surface areas and mark reactant consumption.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：裝載面積或晶舟位置改變。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Changed reactive area or boat position. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","checkEn":"Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-147-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。 對應操作：比較不同晶舟位置與圖案表面積的膜厚，標註反應物耗用。","textEn":"Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation. Corresponding operation: Compare thickness across boat positions and patterned surface areas and mark reactant consumption."},{"id":"sc-147-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：裝載面積或晶舟位置改變。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Changed reactive area or boat position."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查 LPCVD 裝載效應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect LPCVD loading effects\"?","options":["晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。","相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation.","The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：晶舟位置與總反應面積都列入解釋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Both boat position and total reactive area are included in the explanation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-146"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-148","order":18,"sequence":148,"title":"調整 PECVD 膜應力","titleEn":"Compare PECVD film stress","objective":"低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。","objectiveEn":"A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較示意電漿條件下的膜厚、曲率與膜質資料，選擇滿足多目標的狀態。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare thickness, curvature and film-quality data under illustrative plasma conditions and choose a multi-criterion outcome.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：膜應力改善犧牲組成或電性。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Stress improvement sacrifices composition or electrical quality. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。","checkEn":"A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-148-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。 對應操作：比較示意電漿條件下的膜厚、曲率與膜質資料，選擇滿足多目標的狀態。","textEn":"A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior. Corresponding operation: Compare thickness, curvature and film-quality data under illustrative plasma conditions and choose a multi-criterion outcome."},{"id":"sc-148-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：膜應力改善犧牲組成或電性。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Stress improvement sacrifices composition or electrical quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整 PECVD 膜應力」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare PECVD film stress\"?","options":["覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。"],"optionsEn":["The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：低應力方案沒有忽略組成或電性劣化。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A low-stress choice does not ignore degraded composition or electrical behavior. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-147"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-149","order":19,"sequence":149,"title":"檢查 CVD 間隙填充","titleEn":"Inspect CVD gap fill","objective":"填充結論有截面連續性證據。","objectiveEn":"The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿沉積過程觀察入口堆積與底部填充，標示可能的封口空洞。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Observe entrance buildup and bottom fill during deposition and mark possible pinch-off voids.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：填充結論有截面連續性證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：入口封閉留下內部空洞。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Entrance closure traps internal voids. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"填充結論有截面連續性證據。","checkEn":"The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-149-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"填充結論有截面連續性證據。 對應操作：沿沉積過程觀察入口堆積與底部填充，標示可能的封口空洞。","textEn":"The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity. Corresponding operation: Observe entrance buildup and bottom fill during deposition and mark possible pinch-off voids."},{"id":"sc-149-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：入口封閉留下內部空洞。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Entrance closure traps internal voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查 CVD 間隙填充」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect CVD gap fill\"?","options":["自限飽和以曲線趨勢判定，不假定每脈衝恰為完整單原子層。","填充結論有截面連續性證據。","彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。"],"optionsEn":["Self-limiting saturation follows the curve rather than assuming one complete atomic layer per pulse.","The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity.","Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：填充結論有截面連續性證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The fill conclusion is supported by cross-sectional continuity. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-148"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-150","order":20,"sequence":150,"title":"模擬 PVD 入射分布","titleEn":"Model PVD arrival-angle distribution","objective":"視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","objectiveEn":"Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：改變靶材與晶圓相對幾何，觀察沉積粒子的角度分布。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Change target-wafer geometry and inspect the arrival-angle distribution of deposited species.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：視線遮蔽造成側壁或底部薄化。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Line-of-sight shadowing thins sidewalls or bottoms. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","checkEn":"Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-150-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。 對應操作：改變靶材與晶圓相對幾何，觀察沉積粒子的角度分布。","textEn":"Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms. Corresponding operation: Change target-wafer geometry and inspect the arrival-angle distribution of deposited species."},{"id":"sc-150-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：視線遮蔽造成側壁或底部薄化。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Line-of-sight shadowing thins sidewalls or bottoms."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬 PVD 入射分布」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model PVD arrival-angle distribution\"?","options":["視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。","單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","下一反應物進入前的重疊程度被評估。"],"optionsEn":["Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms.","A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","Overlap with the next reactant is evaluated before its introduction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：視線遮蔽對側壁與底部的影響分開評估。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Line-of-sight shadowing is evaluated separately for sidewalls and bottoms. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-149"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-151","order":21,"sequence":151,"title":"檢查濺鍍靶材狀態","titleEn":"Inspect sputtering-target condition","objective":"靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。","objectiveEn":"Target history and thickness trends have traceable links.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較靶材侵蝕溝槽與沉積均勻性圖，追蹤使用歷史。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare target erosion tracks with deposition-uniformity maps and track usage history.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Target history and thickness trends have traceable links.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：靶材侵蝕歷史影響沉積分布。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Target erosion history changes deposition distribution. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。","checkEn":"Target history and thickness trends have traceable links.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-151-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。 對應操作：比較靶材侵蝕溝槽與沉積均勻性圖，追蹤使用歷史。","textEn":"Target history and thickness trends have traceable links. Corresponding operation: Compare target erosion tracks with deposition-uniformity maps and track usage history."},{"id":"sc-151-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：靶材侵蝕歷史影響沉積分布。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Target erosion history changes deposition distribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查濺鍍靶材狀態」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect sputtering-target condition\"?","options":["放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","新表面終態可支持下一循環，殘留配基另列。","靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。"],"optionsEn":["Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","The resulting surface supports the next cycle and remaining ligands are recorded separately.","Target history and thickness trends have traceable links."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：靶材壽命與膜厚趨勢有可追溯關聯。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Target history and thickness trends have traceable links. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-150"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-152","order":22,"sequence":152,"title":"控制反應式濺鍍分支","titleEn":"Analyze reactive sputtering branches","objective":"相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","objectiveEn":"The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較金屬態與反應覆蓋靶面的示意訊號，觀察遲滯及膜組成。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare signals from metallic and compound-covered target states and inspect hysteresis and film composition.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：反應式濺鍍存在歷史遲滯。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Reactive sputtering exhibits history-dependent hysteresis. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","checkEn":"The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-152-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。 對應操作：比較金屬態與反應覆蓋靶面的示意訊號，觀察遲滯及膜組成。","textEn":"The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states. Corresponding operation: Compare signals from metallic and compound-covered target states and inspect hysteresis and film composition."},{"id":"sc-152-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：反應式濺鍍存在歷史遲滯。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Reactive sputtering exhibits history-dependent hysteresis."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制反應式濺鍍分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze reactive sputtering branches\"?","options":["兩個半反應在時間上有足夠分離的示意證據。","相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。","選型根據覆蓋需求與材料限制，不只看沉積速度。"],"optionsEn":["The model provides evidence of temporal separation between half-reactions.","The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states.","Selection follows coverage and material constraints, not deposition speed alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：相同氣體設定可能對應不同歷史狀態。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The same gas setting may correspond to different history-dependent states. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-151"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-153","order":23,"sequence":153,"title":"量測薄膜階梯覆蓋","titleEn":"Measure thin-film step coverage","objective":"覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","objectiveEn":"The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在平面、側壁與底部採相同膜厚定義，計算相對覆蓋。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Use a consistent thickness definition on horizontal, sidewall and bottom surfaces and compare relative coverage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：覆蓋比分母位置未一致。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Coverage-ratio reference locations differ. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","checkEn":"The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-153-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。 對應操作：在平面、側壁與底部採相同膜厚定義，計算相對覆蓋。","textEn":"The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled. Corresponding operation: Use a consistent thickness definition on horizontal, sidewall and bottom surfaces and compare relative coverage."},{"id":"sc-153-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：覆蓋比分母位置未一致。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Coverage-ratio reference locations differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測薄膜階梯覆蓋」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure thin-film step coverage\"?","options":["覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。","表面終態差異列入成核解釋。","斜率擬合不強迫通過原點。"],"optionsEn":["The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled.","Surface-termination differences are included in nucleation interpretation.","The slope fit is not forced through the origin."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：覆蓋比的分子與分母位置標示清楚。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The numerator and denominator locations for coverage ratios are explicitly labeled. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-152"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-154","order":24,"sequence":154,"title":"量測薄膜應力與翹曲","titleEn":"Measure film stress and curvature","objective":"彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。","objectiveEn":"Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較沉積前後晶圓曲率，檢查所用薄膜應力模型的幾何假設。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare wafer curvature before and after deposition and inspect assumptions in the film-stress model.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：曲率公式超出薄膜假設。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Curvature formula used outside thin-film assumptions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。","checkEn":"Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-154-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。 對應操作：比較沉積前後晶圓曲率，檢查所用薄膜應力模型的幾何假設。","textEn":"Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films. Corresponding operation: Compare wafer curvature before and after deposition and inspect assumptions in the film-stress model."},{"id":"sc-154-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：曲率公式超出薄膜假設。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Curvature formula used outside thin-film assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測薄膜應力與翹曲」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure film stress and curvature\"?","options":["基壓與製程壓力分開，不以總壓力唯一判定氣體成分。","穩定成長區還須檢查膜質，不能只靠厚度斜率。","彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。"],"optionsEn":["Base and process pressures are separated; total pressure alone does not identify gas composition.","A stable growth region is also checked for film quality, not thickness slope alone.","Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：彎曲變化未在厚膜或多層情況下盲目套用簡化公式。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Curvature changes are not blindly inserted into simplified formulas for thick or multilayer films. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-153"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-155","order":25,"sequence":155,"title":"分析膜組成與密度","titleEn":"Analyze film composition and density","objective":"單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","objectiveEn":"A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將光學常數、元素分析與厚度資料交叉比對，辨識不同解釋。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Cross-check optical constants, elemental analysis and thickness to distinguish competing interpretations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：單一光學量有多種成分解釋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: One optical measurement permits multiple composition interpretations. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","checkEn":"A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-155-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。 對應操作：將光學常數、元素分析與厚度資料交叉比對，辨識不同解釋。","textEn":"A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity. Corresponding operation: Cross-check optical constants, elemental analysis and thickness to distinguish competing interpretations."},{"id":"sc-155-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：單一光學量有多種成分解釋。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: One optical measurement permits multiple composition interpretations."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析膜組成與密度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze film composition and density\"?","options":["共形性由深度分布評估而非平面陪片厚度。","單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。","入口流量均衡不被直接等同表面供料均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Conformality follows the depth profile rather than planar-monitor thickness alone.","A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity.","Balanced inlet flow is not automatically equated with uniform surface delivery."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：單一折射率變化不足以唯一認定某種雜質。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A refractive-index change alone does not uniquely identify an impurity. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-154"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-156","order":26,"sequence":156,"title":"放行沉積膜層","titleEn":"Release the deposited film","objective":"放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","objectiveEn":"Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：整合連續性、厚度、應力及缺陷證據，檢查對下游蝕刻的影響。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine continuity, thickness, stress and defect evidence and inspect downstream etch implications.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：膜層局部合格但下游不相容。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local film acceptance hides downstream incompatibility. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","checkEn":"Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-156-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。 對應操作：整合連續性、厚度、應力及缺陷證據，檢查對下游蝕刻的影響。","textEn":"Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility. Corresponding operation: Combine continuity, thickness, stress and defect evidence and inspect downstream etch implications."},{"id":"sc-156-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"名義膜厚不足以決定共形性、連續性或材料品質。ALD 的自限半反應可改善控制，但每循環成長量依材料及條件而變。 本步特別排查：膜層局部合格但下游不相容。","textEn":"Nominal thickness does not determine conformality, continuity or material quality. Self-limiting ALD half-reactions improve control, but growth per cycle depends on material and conditions. Specifically examine: Local film acceptance hides downstream incompatibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「放行沉積膜層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Release the deposited film\"?","options":["放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。","路線可行性包含既有結構的熱相容性。","電漿增強的優勢與可能損傷同時說明。"],"optionsEn":["Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility.","Route feasibility includes thermal compatibility with existing structures.","Plasma-enhanced benefits and potential damage are discussed together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：放行判據同時包含膜層本身與下游相容性。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Release criteria include both film properties and downstream compatibility. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-deposition","sc-mc-index","sc-kla-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-155"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m07","order":7,"title":"光阻塗佈、烘烤與顯影","titleEn":"Resist coating, baking and development","description":"以光阻材料相容性串連塗佈至圖案驗收；曝光結果在本模組作為已校核輸入，下一模組深入曝光機制。","descriptionEn":"Connect coating through pattern acceptance using material compatibility. Verified exposure is an input here; the next module examines exposure mechanisms in depth.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-157","order":1,"sequence":157,"title":"選擇光阻極性","titleEn":"Select resist tone","objective":"曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。","objectiveEn":"The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將同一光罩分別套用正性與負性反應，畫出顯影後保留區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Apply positive and negative responses to the same mask and draw the retained regions after development.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：光阻極性與圖案保留區相反。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Resist tone reverses intended retained regions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。","checkEn":"The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-157-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。 對應操作：將同一光罩分別套用正性與負性反應，畫出顯影後保留區。","textEn":"The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone. Corresponding operation: Apply positive and negative responses to the same mask and draw the retained regions after development."},{"id":"sc-157-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：光阻極性與圖案保留區相反。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Resist tone reverses intended retained regions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇光阻極性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select resist tone\"?","options":["脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。"],"optionsEn":["Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-156"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-158","order":2,"sequence":158,"title":"核對光阻適用光譜","titleEn":"Check resist spectral compatibility","objective":"不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。","objectiveEn":"Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較光源波段與光阻吸收示意，選出可對應的材料組合。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare source spectrum with resist absorption and select a compatible material pairing.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：光源與材料吸收波段不匹配。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Source and material absorption bands mismatch. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。","checkEn":"Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-158-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。 對應操作：比較光源波段與光阻吸收示意，選出可對應的材料組合。","textEn":"Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists. Corresponding operation: Compare source spectrum with resist absorption and select a compatible material pairing."},{"id":"sc-158-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：光源與材料吸收波段不匹配。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Source and material absorption bands mismatch."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對光阻適用光譜」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check resist spectral compatibility\"?","options":["熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。","促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。"],"optionsEn":["Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists.","Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-157"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-159","order":3,"sequence":159,"title":"檢查光阻批次與老化","titleEn":"Inspect resist batch and aging","objective":"批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","objectiveEn":"Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較同一材料的新舊批次黏度、粒子與塗膜資料，追蹤保存歷史。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare viscosity, particles and coating data across fresh and aged batches while tracking storage history.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：保存及批次差異未被追蹤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Storage and batch differences untracked. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","checkEn":"Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-159-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。 對應操作：比較同一材料的新舊批次黏度、粒子與塗膜資料，追蹤保存歷史。","textEn":"Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone. Corresponding operation: Compare viscosity, particles and coating data across fresh and aged batches while tracking storage history."},{"id":"sc-159-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：保存及批次差異未被追蹤。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Storage and batch differences untracked."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查光阻批次與老化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect resist batch and aging\"?","options":["批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。","表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。"],"optionsEn":["Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images.","A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-158"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-160","order":4,"sequence":160,"title":"配置抗反射底層","titleEn":"Configure the antireflective underlayer","objective":"反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。","objectiveEn":"Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在高反射基底上加入示意 BARC，對照光場駐波與膜厚。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add a schematic BARC to a reflective substrate and compare standing-wave fields and thickness.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：抗反射層優化忽略後續開口。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Antireflective optimization ignores later opening. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。","checkEn":"Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-160-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。 對應操作：在高反射基底上加入示意 BARC，對照光場駐波與膜厚。","textEn":"Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together. Corresponding operation: Add a schematic BARC to a reflective substrate and compare standing-wave fields and thickness."},{"id":"sc-160-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：抗反射層優化忽略後續開口。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Antireflective optimization ignores later opening."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置抗反射底層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure the antireflective underlayer\"?","options":["加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。"],"optionsEn":["Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-159"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-161","order":5,"sequence":161,"title":"核對塗佈前潔淨度","titleEn":"Verify pre-coat cleanliness","objective":"針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。","objectiveEn":"Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把有機殘留與粒子圖疊在即將塗膜的位置，預測局部缺陷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay organic-residue and particle maps on the coating surface and predict local defects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：基底污染造成針孔或凸點。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Substrate contamination produces pinholes or bumps. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。","checkEn":"Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-161-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。 對應操作：把有機殘留與粒子圖疊在即將塗膜的位置，預測局部缺陷。","textEn":"Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites. Corresponding operation: Overlay organic-residue and particle maps on the coating surface and predict local defects."},{"id":"sc-161-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：基底污染造成針孔或凸點。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Substrate contamination produces pinholes or bumps."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對塗佈前潔淨度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify pre-coat cleanliness\"?","options":["再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。","比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。"],"optionsEn":["Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites.","The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-160"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-162","order":6,"sequence":162,"title":"處理基板脫水","titleEn":"Assess substrate dehydration","objective":"脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","objectiveEn":"Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較表面含水狀態與光阻附著影像，觀察等待後再吸附。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare surface-water state with adhesion images and inspect re-adsorption during waiting.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：脫水後再吸附改變表面。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Re-adsorption changes the dehydrated surface. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","checkEn":"Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-162-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。 對應操作：比較表面含水狀態與光阻附著影像，觀察等待後再吸附。","textEn":"Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history. Corresponding operation: Compare surface-water state with adhesion images and inspect re-adsorption during waiting."},{"id":"sc-162-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：脫水後再吸附改變表面。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Re-adsorption changes the dehydrated surface."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「處理基板脫水」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Assess substrate dehydration\"?","options":["脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。","實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。"],"optionsEn":["Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow.","The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-161"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-163","order":7,"sequence":163,"title":"比較附著促進層","titleEn":"Compare adhesion-promotion layers","objective":"促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。","objectiveEn":"Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在適用基底分支加入示意促進層，對照塗膜完整性與顯影後剝離。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add an illustrative adhesion promoter on a compatible-substrate branch and compare coating integrity and post-develop lifting.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：促進層過量或材料不相容。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Excess promoter or incompatible material. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。","checkEn":"Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-163-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。 對應操作：在適用基底分支加入示意促進層，對照塗膜完整性與顯影後剝離。","textEn":"Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion. Corresponding operation: Add an illustrative adhesion promoter on a compatible-substrate branch and compare coating integrity and post-develop lifting."},{"id":"sc-163-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：促進層過量或材料不相容。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Excess promoter or incompatible material."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較附著促進層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare adhesion-promotion layers\"?","options":["去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。"],"optionsEn":["The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-162"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-164","order":8,"sequence":164,"title":"定位光阻滴注","titleEn":"Position resist dispensing","objective":"有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。","objectiveEn":"Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較中心滴注與偏心滴注後的覆蓋，追蹤初始氣泡。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare coverage after centered and off-center dispensing and track initial bubbles.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：偏心滴注或氣泡造成缺膜。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Off-center dispensing or bubbles cause missing coverage. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。","checkEn":"Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-164-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。 對應操作：比較中心滴注與偏心滴注後的覆蓋，追蹤初始氣泡。","textEn":"Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images. Corresponding operation: Compare coverage after centered and off-center dispensing and track initial bubbles."},{"id":"sc-164-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：偏心滴注或氣泡造成缺膜。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Off-center dispensing or bubbles cause missing coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「定位光阻滴注」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Position resist dispensing\"?","options":["相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。","背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。"],"optionsEn":["Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images.","Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-163"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-165","order":9,"sequence":165,"title":"建立旋塗加速段","titleEn":"Construct the spin-acceleration segment","objective":"加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","objectiveEn":"Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同示意加速曲線下的初始展膜，觀察條紋起點。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare initial spreading under different acceleration profiles and inspect where streaks begin.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：初始展膜缺陷被歸咎最終轉速。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Initial spreading defects blamed on final speed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","checkEn":"Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-165-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。 對應操作：比較不同示意加速曲線下的初始展膜，觀察條紋起點。","textEn":"Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects. Corresponding operation: Compare initial spreading under different acceleration profiles and inspect where streaks begin."},{"id":"sc-165-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：初始展膜缺陷被歸咎最終轉速。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Initial spreading defects blamed on final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立旋塗加速段」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Construct the spin-acceleration segment\"?","options":["加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。"],"optionsEn":["Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-164"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-166","order":10,"sequence":166,"title":"調整旋塗穩態厚度","titleEn":"Compare steady spin-coated thickness","objective":"比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。","objectiveEn":"The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在相同材料與環境假設下改變示意轉速，查看厚度和均勻性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Vary illustrative spin speed under fixed material and ambient assumptions and inspect thickness and uniformity.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：黏度或溶劑變化使經驗曲線失效。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Viscosity or solvent changes invalidate an empirical curve. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。","checkEn":"The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-166-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。 對應操作：在相同材料與環境假設下改變示意轉速，查看厚度和均勻性。","textEn":"The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal. Corresponding operation: Vary illustrative spin speed under fixed material and ambient assumptions and inspect thickness and uniformity."},{"id":"sc-166-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：黏度或溶劑變化使經驗曲線失效。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Viscosity or solvent changes invalidate an empirical curve."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整旋塗穩態厚度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare steady spin-coated thickness\"?","options":["熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。"],"optionsEn":["Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-165"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-167","order":11,"sequence":167,"title":"觀察溶劑揮發效應","titleEn":"Observe solvent-evaporation effects","objective":"厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。","objectiveEn":"Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較相同旋塗曲線但不同揮發程度的膜形，查看乾燥前緣。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare film profiles with the same spin trajectory but different evaporation and inspect drying fronts.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：揮發及乾燥前緣影響膜厚。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Evaporation and drying fronts affect thickness. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。","checkEn":"Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-167-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。 對應操作：比較相同旋塗曲線但不同揮發程度的膜形，查看乾燥前緣。","textEn":"Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow. Corresponding operation: Compare film profiles with the same spin trajectory but different evaporation and inspect drying fronts."},{"id":"sc-167-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：揮發及乾燥前緣影響膜厚。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Evaporation and drying fronts affect thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「觀察溶劑揮發效應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Observe solvent-evaporation effects\"?","options":["倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。","表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。"],"optionsEn":["Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow.","A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-166"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-168","order":12,"sequence":168,"title":"移除邊緣厚珠","titleEn":"Remove the edge bead","objective":"去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","objectiveEn":"The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在旋塗截面辨識邊緣厚珠，設定示意去除區並檢查有效版圖。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Identify edge beads in the coating section, define a removal band and check usable layout coverage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：去邊範圍侵入有效圖案。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Edge removal invades usable patterns. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","checkEn":"The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-168-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。 對應操作：在旋塗截面辨識邊緣厚珠，設定示意去除區並檢查有效版圖。","textEn":"The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region. Corresponding operation: Identify edge beads in the coating section, define a removal band and check usable layout coverage."},{"id":"sc-168-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：去邊範圍侵入有效圖案。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Edge removal invades usable patterns."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「移除邊緣厚珠」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove the edge bead\"?","options":["去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。"],"optionsEn":["The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-167"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-169","order":13,"sequence":169,"title":"檢查背面光阻污染","titleEn":"Inspect backside resist contamination","objective":"背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。","objectiveEn":"Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：查看晶圓背面與夾盤接觸圖，追蹤光阻殘留造成的高度偏差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect the wafer backside and chuck-contact map and track height errors from resist residue.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：背面殘留造成夾盤高度誤差。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Backside residue creates chucking-height errors. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。","checkEn":"Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-169-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。 對應操作：查看晶圓背面與夾盤接觸圖，追蹤光阻殘留造成的高度偏差。","textEn":"Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness. Corresponding operation: Inspect the wafer backside and chuck-contact map and track height errors from resist residue."},{"id":"sc-169-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：背面殘留造成夾盤高度誤差。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Backside residue creates chucking-height errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查背面光阻污染」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect backside resist contamination\"?","options":["再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。"],"optionsEn":["Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-168"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-170","order":14,"sequence":170,"title":"量測軟烤前膜厚","titleEn":"Measure pre-bake film thickness","objective":"軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","objectiveEn":"Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：選擇相同測點建立濕膜基準，記錄量測時距以比較後續收縮。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Establish a pre-bake film baseline at matching sites and record elapsed time for later shrinkage comparison.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：量測時距不同造成表觀厚度差。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Different timing creates apparent thickness changes. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","checkEn":"Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-170-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。 對應操作：選擇相同測點建立濕膜基準，記錄量測時距以比較後續收縮。","textEn":"Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions. Corresponding operation: Establish a pre-bake film baseline at matching sites and record elapsed time for later shrinkage comparison."},{"id":"sc-170-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：量測時距不同造成表觀厚度差。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Different timing creates apparent thickness changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測軟烤前膜厚」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure pre-bake film thickness\"?","options":["曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。","軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。","實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。"],"optionsEn":["The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone.","Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions.","The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：軟烤前後數據有一致測點與時間定義。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Pre- and post-bake data share consistent sites and timing definitions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-169"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-171","order":15,"sequence":171,"title":"比較熱板接觸","titleEn":"Compare hotplate contact","objective":"熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","objectiveEn":"Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在示意熱傳模型改變晶圓與熱板接觸狀態，觀察局部升溫。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Vary wafer-to-hotplate contact in a heat-transfer model and observe local heating.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：接觸熱阻造成局部升溫差。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Contact resistance produces local heating differences. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","checkEn":"Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-171-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。 對應操作：在示意熱傳模型改變晶圓與熱板接觸狀態，觀察局部升溫。","textEn":"Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location. Corresponding operation: Vary wafer-to-hotplate contact in a heat-transfer model and observe local heating."},{"id":"sc-171-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：接觸熱阻造成局部升溫差。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Contact resistance produces local heating differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較熱板接觸」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare hotplate contact\"?","options":["熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。","PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。"],"optionsEn":["Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location.","PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：熱板設定值不被直接當成每點光阻溫度。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Hotplate setpoint is not equated with resist temperature at every location. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-170"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-172","order":16,"sequence":172,"title":"模擬軟烤溶劑移除","titleEn":"Model soft-bake solvent removal","objective":"表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。","objectiveEn":"A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿膜厚方向追蹤溶劑分布，比較表面乾燥與底部殘留。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track solvent concentration through the film and compare surface drying with bottom residue.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：表面乾燥掩蓋底部溶劑。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Surface dryness hides retained bottom solvent. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。","checkEn":"A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-172-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。 對應操作：沿膜厚方向追蹤溶劑分布，比較表面乾燥與底部殘留。","textEn":"A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film. Corresponding operation: Track solvent concentration through the film and compare surface drying with bottom residue."},{"id":"sc-172-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：表面乾燥掩蓋底部溶劑。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Surface dryness hides retained bottom solvent."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬軟烤溶劑移除」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model soft-bake solvent removal\"?","options":["相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。"],"optionsEn":["Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：表面看似乾燥不代表整層溶劑已均勻移除。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A dry-looking surface does not prove uniform solvent removal through the film. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-171"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-173","order":17,"sequence":173,"title":"檢查軟烤後收縮","titleEn":"Inspect post-bake shrinkage","objective":"厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","objectiveEn":"Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對位烘烤前後膜厚圖，辨識均勻收縮與局部裂紋。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Register thickness maps before and after baking and distinguish uniform shrinkage from local cracks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：局部裂紋被平均收縮掩蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local cracks hidden by average shrinkage. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","checkEn":"Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-173-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。 對應操作：對位烘烤前後膜厚圖，辨識均勻收縮與局部裂紋。","textEn":"Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately. Corresponding operation: Register thickness maps before and after baking and distinguish uniform shrinkage from local cracks."},{"id":"sc-173-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：局部裂紋被平均收縮掩蓋。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Local cracks hidden by average shrinkage."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查軟烤後收縮」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect post-bake shrinkage\"?","options":["反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。","厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。","清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。"],"optionsEn":["Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together.","Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately.","Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：厚度收縮和裂紋缺陷分別記錄。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Thickness shrinkage and cracking defects are recorded separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-172"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-174","order":18,"sequence":174,"title":"冷卻及等待控制","titleEn":"Control cooling and queue time","objective":"再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","objectiveEn":"Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較相同材料在不同等待歷史下的曝光起始狀態，標示適用的再吸水分支。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare exposure starting states after different queue histories and label any material-specific rehydration branch.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：錯將材料專屬再吸水套用全部。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Material-specific rehydration imposed universally. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","checkEn":"Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-174-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。 對應操作：比較相同材料在不同等待歷史下的曝光起始狀態，標示適用的再吸水分支。","textEn":"Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists. Corresponding operation: Compare exposure starting states after different queue histories and label any material-specific rehydration branch."},{"id":"sc-174-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：錯將材料專屬再吸水套用全部。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Material-specific rehydration imposed universally."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「冷卻及等待控制」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control cooling and queue time\"?","options":["再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。","沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。"],"optionsEn":["Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists.","Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：再吸水只限需要的光阻體系，未當作所有光阻必做。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Rehydration applies only to compatible resist systems rather than all resists. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-173"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-175","order":19,"sequence":175,"title":"交接已校核曝光結果","titleEn":"Receive verified exposure results","objective":"實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。","objectiveEn":"The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把第八模組的曝光圖與本模組光阻極性結合，確認 PEB 或顯影的輸入。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine the exposure map from module eight with resist tone to establish the input for PEB or development.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：教學模組順序誤當生產順序。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Teaching-module order mistaken for production order. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。","checkEn":"The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-175-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。 對應操作：把第八模組的曝光圖與本模組光阻極性結合，確認 PEB 或顯影的輸入。","textEn":"The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development. Corresponding operation: Combine the exposure map from module eight with resist tone to establish the input for PEB or development."},{"id":"sc-175-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：教學模組順序誤當生產順序。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Teaching-module order mistaken for production order."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接已校核曝光結果」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Receive verified exposure results\"?","options":["倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","脫水後表面狀態包含等待歷史。","實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。"],"optionsEn":["Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","Post-dehydration surface state includes queue history.","The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：實際順序標為塗佈、曝光、適用 PEB、顯影。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The physical sequence is explicitly coating, exposure, applicable PEB, then development. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-174"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-176","order":20,"sequence":176,"title":"控制曝光後烘烤分支","titleEn":"Analyze the post-exposure-bake branch","objective":"PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","objectiveEn":"PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在需要 PEB 的材料模型中比較反應擴散長度與線緣變化。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. For a resist requiring PEB, compare reaction-diffusion length with line-edge changes.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：PEB 與軟烤機制混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: PEB mechanism confused with soft baking. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","checkEn":"PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-176-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。 對應操作：在需要 PEB 的材料模型中比較反應擴散長度與線緣變化。","textEn":"PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking. Corresponding operation: For a resist requiring PEB, compare reaction-diffusion length with line-edge changes."},{"id":"sc-176-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：PEB 與軟烤機制混淆。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: PEB mechanism confused with soft baking."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制曝光後烘烤分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze the post-exposure-bake branch\"?","options":["促進層使用與材料相容，不把過量塗佈當作附著更強。","PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。","圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Promoter use is material-compatible and excess application is not equated with stronger adhesion.","PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking.","Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：PEB 需求依材料機制決定，不與軟烤混淆。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: PEB requirements follow material chemistry and are not confused with soft baking. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-175"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-177","order":21,"sequence":177,"title":"核對顯影液相容性","titleEn":"Check developer compatibility","objective":"相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","objectiveEn":"Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將光阻體系與供應商指定顯影類別配對，比較未曝光區溶失。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Match the resist system to its specified developer class and compare loss from unexposed regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：顯影過度或非目標區溶失。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Overdevelopment or unintended film loss. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","checkEn":"Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-177-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。 對應操作：將光阻體系與供應商指定顯影類別配對，比較未曝光區溶失。","textEn":"Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together. Corresponding operation: Match the resist system to its specified developer class and compare loss from unexposed regions."},{"id":"sc-177-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：顯影過度或非目標區溶失。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Overdevelopment or unintended film loss."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對顯影液相容性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Check developer compatibility\"?","options":["相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。","硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","有效區覆蓋及氣泡位置有影像證據。"],"optionsEn":["Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together.","Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","Coverage of the usable area and bubble locations are supported by images."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：相容性同時檢查目標溶解與非目標膜損耗。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Compatibility considers intended dissolution and unwanted film loss together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-176"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-178","order":22,"sequence":178,"title":"模擬顯影溶解前緣","titleEn":"Model the development front","objective":"清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。","objectiveEn":"Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：觀察開口從表面向下形成，對比線端與密集區溶解差異。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Observe openings forming downward from the surface and compare line ends with dense regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：開口未清底或保留線條過度溶解。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Uncleared openings or excessive retained-line dissolution. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。","checkEn":"Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-178-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。 對應操作：觀察開口從表面向下形成，對比線端與密集區溶解差異。","textEn":"Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together. Corresponding operation: Observe openings forming downward from the surface and compare line ends with dense regions."},{"id":"sc-178-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：開口未清底或保留線條過度溶解。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Uncleared openings or excessive retained-line dissolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬顯影溶解前緣」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model the development front\"?","options":["曝光區與溶解區的對應符合所選極性。","加速段效應與最終轉速效應分開比較。","清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。"],"optionsEn":["The relationship between exposure and dissolution matches the chosen tone.","Acceleration effects are compared separately from final-speed effects.","Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：清底程度與保留光阻尺寸共同評估。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Opening clearance and retained-resist dimensions are evaluated together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-177"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-179","order":23,"sequence":179,"title":"檢查顯影後沖洗","titleEn":"Inspect post-development rinsing","objective":"沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","objectiveEn":"Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：追蹤圖案間殘留顯影液，比較及時終止與持續溶解的示意結果。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track developer retained between features and compare timely termination with continued dissolution.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：殘留顯影液使反應繼續。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Retained developer allows continued dissolution. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","checkEn":"Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-179-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。 對應操作：追蹤圖案間殘留顯影液，比較及時終止與持續溶解的示意結果。","textEn":"Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change. Corresponding operation: Track developer retained between features and compare timely termination with continued dissolution."},{"id":"sc-179-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：殘留顯影液使反應繼續。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Retained developer allows continued dissolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查顯影後沖洗」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect post-development rinsing\"?","options":["比較註明黏度及溶劑條件，不把經驗曲線當普適定律。","沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。","不同曝光波段未被假定能共用任意光阻。"],"optionsEn":["The comparison states viscosity and solvent assumptions rather than treating an empirical curve as universal.","Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change.","Different exposure bands are not assumed to work with arbitrary resists."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：沖洗效果以殘留和尺寸變化確認。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Rinse performance is checked through residue and dimensional change. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-178"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-180","order":24,"sequence":180,"title":"診斷光阻圖案倒塌","titleEn":"Diagnose resist-pattern collapse","objective":"倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","objectiveEn":"Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較細高線條在乾燥前後的位置，檢查毛細作用與附著因素。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare tall slender lines before and after drying and inspect capillary and adhesion effects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：毛細倒塌誤判為曝光橋接。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Capillary collapse mistaken for exposure bridging. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","checkEn":"Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-180-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。 對應操作：比較細高線條在乾燥前後的位置，檢查毛細作用與附著因素。","textEn":"Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging. Corresponding operation: Compare tall slender lines before and after drying and inspect capillary and adhesion effects."},{"id":"sc-180-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：毛細倒塌誤判為曝光橋接。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Capillary collapse mistaken for exposure bridging."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷光阻圖案倒塌」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose resist-pattern collapse\"?","options":["倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。","批次差異有量測支持，未單憑日期推定可用性。","厚度差異不全歸因於離心流動。"],"optionsEn":["Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging.","Batch differences are supported by measurements rather than date alone.","Thickness differences are not attributed entirely to centrifugal flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：倒塌與未曝光橋接在形貌上分開辨識。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Collapse is distinguished morphologically from exposure-related bridging. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-179"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-181","order":25,"sequence":181,"title":"執行顯影後檢查","titleEn":"Perform after-development inspection","objective":"圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。","objectiveEn":"Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較線寬、殘膠、橋接與缺口地圖，選出需返工的示意區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare CD, scum, bridges and missing-feature maps and identify illustrative rework regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平均 CD 掩蓋缺口及殘膠。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mean CD hides missing features and scum. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。","checkEn":"Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-181-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。 對應操作：比較線寬、殘膠、橋接與缺口地圖，選出需返工的示意區。","textEn":"Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone. Corresponding operation: Compare CD, scum, bridges and missing-feature maps and identify illustrative rework regions."},{"id":"sc-181-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：平均 CD 掩蓋缺口及殘膠。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Mean CD hides missing features and scum."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「執行顯影後檢查」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Perform after-development inspection\"?","options":["反射抑制與後續底層開口蝕刻需求一起考慮。","去邊範圍不侵入允許的曝光區。","圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Reflection suppression and later underlayer-opening requirements are considered together.","The edge-removal band does not invade the permitted exposure region.","Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：圖案通過需同時滿足尺寸與完整性，而非僅平均線寬。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Passing patterns satisfy both dimensions and integrity, not average CD alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-180"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-182","order":26,"sequence":182,"title":"判定硬烤或直接轉移","titleEn":"Choose hard bake or direct transfer","objective":"硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","objectiveEn":"Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：依下一蝕刻或其他轉移需求比較硬烤前後輪廓，保留可剝除性資訊。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare pre- and post-hard-bake profiles for the next transfer step and retain stripability information.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：硬烤改變輪廓或降低可剝除性。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Hard bake changes profile or reduces stripability. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","checkEn":"Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-182-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。 對應操作：依下一蝕刻或其他轉移需求比較硬烤前後輪廓，保留可剝除性資訊。","textEn":"Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist. Corresponding operation: Compare pre- and post-hard-bake profiles for the next transfer step and retain stripability information."},{"id":"sc-182-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"光阻極性、吸收、烘烤與顯影彼此耦合。實際先後為塗佈、適用前烤、曝光、適用曝光後烤、顯影；教學模組排序不是生產路由。 本步特別排查：硬烤改變輪廓或降低可剝除性。","textEn":"Resist tone, absorption, baking and development are coupled. Physical order is coating, applicable pre-bake, exposure, applicable post-exposure bake and development; teaching-module order is not a production route. Specifically examine: Hard bake changes profile or reduces stripability."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判定硬烤或直接轉移」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Choose hard bake or direct transfer\"?","options":["背面殘留的機械影響與正面膜厚區分。","硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。","針孔或凸點的預測可追溯至具體污染位置。"],"optionsEn":["Mechanical effects of backside residue are distinguished from frontside film thickness.","Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist.","Predicted pinholes or bumps are traceable to specific contamination sites."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：硬烤是相容性分支，非所有先進光阻的必要固定步驟。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Hard bake is a compatibility branch rather than a mandatory step for every advanced resist. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-mc-prep","sc-mc-spin","sc-mc-softbake","sc-mc-develop"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-181"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"lithography-lab","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影實驗室的黃光照明與工作區；它不是 EUV 掃描機內部或本步光阻反應的照片。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe yellow lighting and the lithography work area; this is not an EUV scanner interior or an image of this step’s resist reaction.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m08","order":8,"title":"曝光、對準、套刻與 EUV","titleEn":"Exposure, alignment, overlay and EUV","description":"用光路、座標、焦距劑量矩陣與誤差向量理解曝光；DUV、浸潤、EUV 與多重圖案化均標為替代情境。","descriptionEn":"Use optical paths, coordinates, focus-exposure matrices and error vectors to understand exposure, with explicit DUV, immersion, EUV and multipatterning alternatives.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-183","order":1,"sequence":183,"title":"配置曝光座標系","titleEn":"Configure exposure coordinates","objective":"平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","objectiveEn":"Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把光罩、平台及晶圓座標箭頭並排，檢查翻轉與縮小倍率方向。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare mask, stage and wafer coordinate axes and inspect inversion and reduction directions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：鏡像、倍率或座標方向混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Confused inversion, reduction or coordinate directions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","checkEn":"Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-183-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。 對應操作：把光罩、平台及晶圓座標箭頭並排，檢查翻轉與縮小倍率方向。","textEn":"Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions. Corresponding operation: Compare mask, stage and wafer coordinate axes and inspect inversion and reduction directions."},{"id":"sc-183-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：鏡像、倍率或座標方向混淆。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Confused inversion, reduction or coordinate directions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置曝光座標系」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure exposure coordinates\"?","options":["平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。","最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。"],"optionsEn":["Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics.","The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-182"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-184","order":2,"sequence":184,"title":"核對光罩版本與極性","titleEn":"Verify reticle revision and tone","objective":"使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。","objectiveEn":"The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：疊合光罩圖案與設計版次，查找版本差異及遮光區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay reticle patterns with the design revision and inspect differences and opaque regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：使用舊版光罩或錯誤極性。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Wrong reticle revision or tone. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。","checkEn":"The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-184-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。 對應操作：疊合光罩圖案與設計版次，查找版本差異及遮光區。","textEn":"The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone. Corresponding operation: Overlay reticle patterns with the design revision and inspect differences and opaque regions."},{"id":"sc-184-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：使用舊版光罩或錯誤極性。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Wrong reticle revision or tone."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對光罩版本與極性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify reticle revision and tone\"?","options":["浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-183"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-185","order":3,"sequence":185,"title":"辨識光罩缺陷","titleEn":"Identify reticle defects","objective":"場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。","objectiveEn":"Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較光罩檢查圖與預期晶圓重複圖案，追蹤缺陷在曝光場中的固定位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare reticle inspection with expected repeated wafer patterns and track fixed within-field defects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：光罩重複缺陷被當成隨機粒子。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Repeating mask defect mistaken for random particles. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。","checkEn":"Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-185-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。 對應操作：比較光罩檢查圖與預期晶圓重複圖案，追蹤缺陷在曝光場中的固定位置。","textEn":"Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination. Corresponding operation: Compare reticle inspection with expected repeated wafer patterns and track fixed within-field defects."},{"id":"sc-185-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：光罩重複缺陷被當成隨機粒子。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Repeating mask defect mistaken for random particles."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「辨識光罩缺陷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Identify reticle defects\"?","options":["視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。","光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。"],"optionsEn":["The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination.","Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-184"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-186","order":4,"sequence":186,"title":"比較光源波長","titleEn":"Compare exposure wavelengths","objective":"比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","objectiveEn":"Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在相同 NA 與示意 k1 下切換波長，比較可分辨特徵尺度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Vary wavelength with fixed NA and illustrative k1 and compare resolvable feature scales.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：波長比較同時改變其他參數。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Other parameters changed during wavelength comparison. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","checkEn":"Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-186-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。 對應操作：在相同 NA 與示意 k1 下切換波長，比較可分辨特徵尺度。","textEn":"Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength. Corresponding operation: Vary wavelength with fixed NA and illustrative k1 and compare resolvable feature scales."},{"id":"sc-186-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：波長比較同時改變其他參數。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Other parameters changed during wavelength comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較光源波長」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare exposure wavelengths\"?","options":["比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。","兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。"],"optionsEn":["Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment.","Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-185"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-187","order":5,"sequence":187,"title":"調整數值孔徑","titleEn":"Vary numerical aperture","objective":"解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。","objectiveEn":"Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較 NA 變化對示意解析度和焦深的相反趨勢。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare how changing NA affects illustrative resolution and depth of focus.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只看解析度忽略焦深。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Resolution considered without depth of focus. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。","checkEn":"Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-187-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。 對應操作：比較 NA 變化對示意解析度和焦深的相反趨勢。","textEn":"Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together. Corresponding operation: Compare how changing NA affects illustrative resolution and depth of focus."},{"id":"sc-187-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：只看解析度忽略焦深。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Resolution considered without depth of focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整數值孔徑」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Vary numerical aperture\"?","options":["修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-186"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-188","order":6,"sequence":188,"title":"區分 DUV 透射與 EUV 反射","titleEn":"Separate DUV transmission from EUV reflection","objective":"EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。","objectiveEn":"The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把透鏡路徑與多鏡反射路徑分開拼裝，標出光罩型態。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Build lens-based and multiple-mirror optical paths separately and label reticle types.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：將 DUV 透鏡模型套到 EUV。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: DUV lens model incorrectly applied to EUV. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。","checkEn":"The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-188-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。 對應操作：把透鏡路徑與多鏡反射路徑分開拼裝，標出光罩型態。","textEn":"The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics. Corresponding operation: Build lens-based and multiple-mirror optical paths separately and label reticle types."},{"id":"sc-188-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：將 DUV 透鏡模型套到 EUV。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: DUV lens model incorrectly applied to EUV."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「區分 DUV 透射與 EUV 反射」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate DUV transmission from EUV reflection\"?","options":["光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。","旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics.","Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-187"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-189","order":7,"sequence":189,"title":"分析浸潤微影分支","titleEn":"Analyze the immersion branch","objective":"浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","objectiveEn":"Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在 DUV 末端加入示意液層，比較折射率對 NA 的影響及液體缺陷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add an illustrative liquid layer to the DUV image space and compare refractive-index effects on NA with liquid-related defects.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把浸潤液路線帶入真空 EUV。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Immersion-fluid route carried into vacuum EUV. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","checkEn":"Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-189-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。 對應操作：在 DUV 末端加入示意液層，比較折射率對 NA 的影響及液體缺陷。","textEn":"Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step. Corresponding operation: Add an illustrative liquid layer to the DUV image space and compare refractive-index effects on NA with liquid-related defects."},{"id":"sc-189-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：把浸潤液路線帶入真空 EUV。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Immersion-fluid route carried into vacuum EUV."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析浸潤微影分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze the immersion branch\"?","options":["浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","倍率項與平移項未互相代替。","邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms.","Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-188"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-190","order":8,"sequence":190,"title":"檢查曝光真空相容性","titleEn":"Inspect exposure-vacuum compatibility","objective":"光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。","objectiveEn":"Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較空氣吸收與真空傳播示意，查看 EUV 光路的表面污染。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare air absorption with vacuum propagation and inspect contamination along EUV optical surfaces.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：傳輸損失與反射損失混計。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Propagation and reflection losses conflated. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。","checkEn":"Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-190-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。 對應操作：比較空氣吸收與真空傳播示意，查看 EUV 光路的表面污染。","textEn":"Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately. Corresponding operation: Compare air absorption with vacuum propagation and inspect contamination along EUV optical surfaces."},{"id":"sc-190-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：傳輸損失與反射損失混計。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Propagation and reflection losses conflated."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查曝光真空相容性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect exposure-vacuum compatibility\"?","options":["插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。"],"optionsEn":["Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-189"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-191","order":9,"sequence":191,"title":"定位晶圓對準記號","titleEn":"Locate wafer alignment marks","objective":"記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。","objectiveEn":"Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把記號影像與背景膜層分開，找出對比不足或被覆蓋的記號。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Separate alignment-mark signals from film background and locate low-contrast or covered marks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：標記被覆蓋或對比不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Marks covered or lacking contrast. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。","checkEn":"Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-191-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。 對應操作：把記號影像與背景膜層分開，找出對比不足或被覆蓋的記號。","textEn":"Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment. Corresponding operation: Separate alignment-mark signals from film background and locate low-contrast or covered marks."},{"id":"sc-191-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：標記被覆蓋或對比不足。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Marks covered or lacking contrast."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「定位晶圓對準記號」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Locate wafer alignment marks\"?","options":["場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。","最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。"],"optionsEn":["Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment.","The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-190"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-192","order":10,"sequence":192,"title":"校正平移誤差","titleEn":"Correct translation error","objective":"修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","objectiveEn":"Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以多個對準記號估計整體位移，再查看修正後的殘差向量。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Estimate global shift from multiple marks and inspect residual vectors after correction.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平移殘差仍有共同方向。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Translation residuals retain a common direction. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","checkEn":"Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-192-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。 對應操作：以多個對準記號估計整體位移，再查看修正後的殘差向量。","textEn":"Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation. Corresponding operation: Estimate global shift from multiple marks and inspect residual vectors after correction."},{"id":"sc-192-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：平移殘差仍有共同方向。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Translation residuals retain a common direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校正平移誤差」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Correct translation error\"?","options":["修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。"],"optionsEn":["Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-191"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-193","order":11,"sequence":193,"title":"校正旋轉誤差","titleEn":"Correct rotational error","objective":"旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。","objectiveEn":"Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較晶圓兩側方向相反的殘差，調整小角度旋轉模型。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare opposing residual directions at wafer edges and adjust a small-angle rotation model.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：旋轉錯誤被平移勉強補償。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Rotation error forced into translation correction. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。","checkEn":"Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-193-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。 對應操作：比較晶圓兩側方向相反的殘差，調整小角度旋轉模型。","textEn":"Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern. Corresponding operation: Compare opposing residual directions at wafer edges and adjust a small-angle rotation model."},{"id":"sc-193-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：旋轉錯誤被平移勉強補償。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Rotation error forced into translation correction."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校正旋轉誤差」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Correct rotational error\"?","options":["視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-192"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-194","order":12,"sequence":194,"title":"校正倍率誤差","titleEn":"Correct magnification error","objective":"倍率項與平移項未互相代替。","objectiveEn":"Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：辨識隨位置半徑放大的殘差，比較 等向 與分軸倍率模型。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Identify residuals growing with position and compare isotropic with axis-dependent scaling models.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：倍率項與平移項未互相代替。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：倍率項與平移項互相代償。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Magnification and translation compensate incorrectly. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"倍率項與平移項未互相代替。","checkEn":"Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-194-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"倍率項與平移項未互相代替。 對應操作：辨識隨位置半徑放大的殘差，比較 等向 與分軸倍率模型。","textEn":"Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms. Corresponding operation: Identify residuals growing with position and compare isotropic with axis-dependent scaling models."},{"id":"sc-194-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：倍率項與平移項互相代償。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Magnification and translation compensate incorrectly."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校正倍率誤差」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Correct magnification error\"?","options":["視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","倍率項與平移項未互相代替。","兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。"],"optionsEn":["Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms.","Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：倍率項與平移項未互相代替。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-193"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-195","order":13,"sequence":195,"title":"建立晶圓高度圖","titleEn":"Build the wafer height map","objective":"插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","objectiveEn":"Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把測高點插值為曝光場高度，保留局部臺階與邊緣。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Interpolate height samples into field-height estimates while retaining local steps and edges.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：插值平滑掉局部臺階。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Interpolation smooths away local steps. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","checkEn":"Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-195-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。 對應操作：把測高點插值為曝光場高度，保留局部臺階與邊緣。","textEn":"Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus. Corresponding operation: Interpolate height samples into field-height estimates while retaining local steps and edges."},{"id":"sc-195-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：插值平滑掉局部臺階。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Interpolation smooths away local steps."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立晶圓高度圖」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build the wafer height map\"?","options":["插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。"],"optionsEn":["Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-194"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-196","order":14,"sequence":196,"title":"校正焦平面與傾斜","titleEn":"Correct focus plane and tilt","objective":"最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。","objectiveEn":"The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對單一曝光場調整焦平面與兩軸傾斜，觀察最差位置的離焦量。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Adjust focus and two-axis tilt for one exposure field and inspect the worst residual defocus.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：最佳平均焦點掩蓋最差位置。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Best average focus hides the worst location. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。","checkEn":"The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-196-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。 對應操作：對單一曝光場調整焦平面與兩軸傾斜，觀察最差位置的離焦量。","textEn":"The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus. Corresponding operation: Adjust focus and two-axis tilt for one exposure field and inspect the worst residual defocus."},{"id":"sc-196-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：最佳平均焦點掩蓋最差位置。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Best average focus hides the worst location."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「校正焦平面與傾斜」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Correct focus plane and tilt\"?","options":["光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。"],"optionsEn":["The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：最佳平均焦點不掩蓋局部超出示範焦深的區域。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The best average focus does not hide regions outside the exercise depth of focus. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-195"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-197","order":15,"sequence":197,"title":"建立焦距劑量矩陣","titleEn":"Build a focus-exposure matrix","objective":"兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","objectiveEn":"The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：排列不同焦距與曝光量的虛擬小區，量測每格線寬和缺陷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Arrange virtual fields across focus and dose and measure CD and defects in each cell.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：焦距與劑量變數未獨立。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Focus and dose variables are not independent. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","checkEn":"The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-197-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。 對應操作：排列不同焦距與曝光量的虛擬小區，量測每格線寬和缺陷。","textEn":"The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged. Corresponding operation: Arrange virtual fields across focus and dose and measure CD and defects in each cell."},{"id":"sc-197-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：焦距與劑量變數未獨立。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Focus and dose variables are not independent."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立焦距劑量矩陣」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build a focus-exposure matrix\"?","options":["使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。","兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。","邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。"],"optionsEn":["The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone.","The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged.","Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：兩個控制軸獨立標示，沒有把焦距與劑量混成一軸。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The two control axes are labeled independently rather than merged. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-196"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-198","order":16,"sequence":198,"title":"判定共同製程視窗","titleEn":"Determine a common process window","objective":"視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","objectiveEn":"The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：疊合線寬、橋接及缺口可接受區，找出共同交集。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay acceptable regions for CD, bridges and missing features to find their intersection.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：單一特徵最佳點取代共同視窗。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: One feature optimum replaces the common window. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","checkEn":"The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-198-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。 對應操作：疊合線寬、橋接及缺口可接受區，找出共同交集。","textEn":"The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum. Corresponding operation: Overlay acceptable regions for CD, bridges and missing features to find their intersection."},{"id":"sc-198-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：單一特徵最佳點取代共同視窗。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: One feature optimum replaces the common window."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判定共同製程視窗」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Determine a common process window\"?","options":["視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。","標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。"],"optionsEn":["The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum.","Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：視窗是多條件交集，不是某一圖案的最佳點。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The window is an intersection of criteria rather than one pattern's optimum. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-197"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-199","order":17,"sequence":199,"title":"比較密集與孤立成像","titleEn":"Compare dense and isolated imaging","objective":"兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。","objectiveEn":"Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以相同設定曝光密集線與孤立線，觀察尺寸偏移。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Expose dense and isolated lines under the same settings and inspect dimensional bias.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只採密集或孤立的一類圖案。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Only dense or isolated patterns sampled. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。","checkEn":"Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-199-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。 對應操作：以相同設定曝光密集線與孤立線，觀察尺寸偏移。","textEn":"Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases. Corresponding operation: Expose dense and isolated lines under the same settings and inspect dimensional bias."},{"id":"sc-199-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：只採密集或孤立的一類圖案。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Only dense or isolated patterns sampled."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較密集與孤立成像」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare dense and isolated imaging\"?","options":["場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。"],"optionsEn":["Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：兩種圖案都在驗證集合中，不能只挑容易成像者。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Both pattern classes remain in the verification set rather than selecting only easy cases. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-198"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-200","order":18,"sequence":200,"title":"分析照明形狀","titleEn":"Analyze illumination shape","objective":"照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","objectiveEn":"Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較示意環形、傳統及多極照明對不同方向圖案的光場。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare schematic annular, conventional and multipole illumination for differently oriented patterns.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：照明優化與圖案方向不匹配。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Illumination optimization mismatches pattern orientation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","checkEn":"Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-200-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。 對應操作：比較示意環形、傳統及多極照明對不同方向圖案的光場。","textEn":"Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch. Corresponding operation: Compare schematic annular, conventional and multipole illumination for differently oriented patterns."},{"id":"sc-200-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：照明優化與圖案方向不匹配。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Illumination optimization mismatches pattern orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析照明形狀」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze illumination shape\"?","options":["解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。","照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。","平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。"],"optionsEn":["Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together.","Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch.","Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：照明優化效果連結到圖案方向與週期。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Illumination benefits are linked to pattern orientation and pitch. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-199"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-201","order":19,"sequence":201,"title":"套用光學鄰近修正","titleEn":"Apply optical proximity correction","objective":"光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","objectiveEn":"The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較未修正與加上修正結構的光罩，查看晶圓目標輪廓誤差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare uncorrected and corrected masks and inspect wafer-contour error relative to target.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只看光罩像不像目標而不看成像。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mask resemblance judged instead of wafer imaging. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","checkEn":"The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-201-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。 對應操作：比較未修正與加上修正結構的光罩，查看晶圓目標輪廓誤差。","textEn":"The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it. Corresponding operation: Compare uncorrected and corrected masks and inspect wafer-contour error relative to target."},{"id":"sc-201-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：只看光罩像不像目標而不看成像。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Mask resemblance judged instead of wafer imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「套用光學鄰近修正」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Apply optical proximity correction\"?","options":["光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。","替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","EUV 路徑沒有插入當作主投影元件的普通透射玻璃透鏡。"],"optionsEn":["The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it.","Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","The EUV path does not use ordinary transmissive glass lenses as its main projection optics."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：光罩外形可偏離目標，但晶圓輪廓需更接近目標。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The mask may differ from the target while the wafer contour should approach it. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-200"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-202","order":20,"sequence":202,"title":"檢查圖案邊緣位置","titleEn":"Inspect pattern edge placement","objective":"邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。","objectiveEn":"Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把設計輪廓、印出輪廓與下層圖案疊合，分開 CD 與位置誤差。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Overlay design, printed contour and the underlying layer and separate CD from placement error.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：CD 與位置誤差未合併判讀。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: CD and placement errors not interpreted together. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。","checkEn":"Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-202-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。 對應操作：把設計輪廓、印出輪廓與下層圖案疊合，分開 CD 與位置誤差。","textEn":"Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment. Corresponding operation: Overlay design, printed contour and the underlying layer and separate CD from placement error."},{"id":"sc-202-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：CD 與位置誤差未合併判讀。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: CD and placement errors not interpreted together."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查圖案邊緣位置」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect pattern edge placement\"?","options":["視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","浸潤路線明示為 DUV 情境，不套用到真空 EUV。","邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。"],"optionsEn":["Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","Immersion is explicitly a DUV context rather than a vacuum-EUV step.","Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：邊緣位置誤差同時考慮尺寸與對位。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Edge-placement error accounts for both size and alignment. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-201"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-203","order":21,"sequence":203,"title":"量測層間套刻","titleEn":"Measure interlayer overlay","objective":"標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","objectiveEn":"Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用上層與下層專用標靶求偏移，對照實際器件敏感位置。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure upper-to-lower-layer offsets with overlay targets and compare device-sensitive locations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：標靶套刻代表性不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Overlay target lacks device representativeness. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","checkEn":"Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-203-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。 對應操作：用上層與下層專用標靶求偏移，對照實際器件敏感位置。","textEn":"Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained. Corresponding operation: Measure upper-to-lower-layer offsets with overlay targets and compare device-sensitive locations."},{"id":"sc-203-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：標靶套刻代表性不足。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Overlay target lacks device representativeness."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測層間套刻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure interlayer overlay\"?","options":["光路傳輸損失與鏡面反射損失分開估算。","標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。","校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。"],"optionsEn":["Propagation loss and mirror-reflection loss are estimated separately.","Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained.","Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：標靶套刻與器件內套刻的差異有保留。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Differences between target overlay and in-device overlay are retained. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-202"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-204","order":22,"sequence":204,"title":"分析場內與場間誤差","titleEn":"Separate intra-field and inter-field error","objective":"場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","objectiveEn":"Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將套刻向量依曝光場分組，再比較場內重複模式與全片漂移。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Group overlay vectors by exposure field and compare repeating field patterns with wafer-wide drift.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：場內模式與全片模式混合。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Intra-field and wafer-level patterns mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","checkEn":"Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-204-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。 對應操作：將套刻向量依曝光場分組，再比較場內重複模式與全片漂移。","textEn":"Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models. Corresponding operation: Group overlay vectors by exposure field and compare repeating field patterns with wafer-wide drift."},{"id":"sc-204-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：場內模式與全片模式混合。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Intra-field and wafer-level patterns mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析場內與場間誤差」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate intra-field and inter-field error\"?","options":["場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。","平面鏡像及座標轉換有一致定義。","記號位置品質有訊號證據，未用不可辨識記號硬對準。"],"optionsEn":["Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models.","Image inversion and coordinate transformations have consistent definitions.","Mark-position quality has signal evidence and unresolved marks are not forced into alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：場內與全片誤差使用對應座標和模型。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Intra-field and wafer-level errors use appropriate coordinates and models. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-203"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-205","order":23,"sequence":205,"title":"診斷 EUV 隨機缺陷","titleEn":"Diagnose EUV stochastic defects","objective":"平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。","objectiveEn":"Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較相同名義圖案多次曝光的缺口、橋接與線緣分布。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare missing features, bridges and edge variation across repeated nominally identical EUV patterns.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平均 CD 掩蓋隨機尾端缺陷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mean CD hides stochastic tail defects. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。","checkEn":"Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-205-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。 對應操作：比較相同名義圖案多次曝光的缺口、橋接與線緣分布。","textEn":"Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk. Corresponding operation: Compare missing features, bridges and edge variation across repeated nominally identical EUV patterns."},{"id":"sc-205-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：平均 CD 掩蓋隨機尾端缺陷。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Mean CD hides stochastic tail defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷 EUV 隨機缺陷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose EUV stochastic defects\"?","options":["使用圖案能追溯至正確版次與曝光極性。","修正後殘差不再包含一致方向的整體偏移。","平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。"],"optionsEn":["The pattern is traceable to the correct revision and exposure tone.","Corrected residuals no longer contain a common global translation.","Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：平均線寬相同不能排除尾端缺陷風險。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Identical mean CD does not rule out tail-related defect risk. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-204"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-206","order":24,"sequence":206,"title":"比較雙重圖案化分支","titleEn":"Compare double-patterning branches","objective":"替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","objectiveEn":"Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把一組密集圖案拆成兩次曝光或間隔層路線，追蹤額外對位需求。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Decompose a dense pattern into two exposures or a spacer-based route and track added alignment needs.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：替代圖案化路線的依賴混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Dependencies from alternative patterning routes mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","checkEn":"Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-206-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。 對應操作：把一組密集圖案拆成兩次曝光或間隔層路線，追蹤額外對位需求。","textEn":"Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence. Corresponding operation: Decompose a dense pattern into two exposures or a spacer-based route and track added alignment needs."},{"id":"sc-206-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：替代圖案化路線的依賴混用。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Dependencies from alternative patterning routes mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較雙重圖案化分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare double-patterning branches\"?","options":["旋轉修正以全片向量模式驗證。","替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。","場內重複缺陷與隨機晶圓污染分開。"],"optionsEn":["Rotation correction is verified from the full-wafer vector pattern.","Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence.","Repeated within-field defects are distinguished from random wafer contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：替代路線明示，不把不同雙圖案化方法混為同一工序。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Alternative routes are labeled rather than merged into one universal double-patterning sequence. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-205"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-207","order":25,"sequence":207,"title":"分析高 NA 視場取捨","titleEn":"Analyze high-NA field trade-offs","objective":"視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","objectiveEn":"Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較示意高 NA 光學與曝光場安排，檢查分場及接縫需求。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare schematic high-NA optics with field placement and inspect partitioning and stitching needs.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略視場、分場與接縫限制。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Field, partitioning and stitching limits omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","checkEn":"Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-207-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。 對應操作：比較示意高 NA 光學與曝光場安排，檢查分場及接縫需求。","textEn":"Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution. Corresponding operation: Compare schematic high-NA optics with field placement and inspect partitioning and stitching needs."},{"id":"sc-207-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：忽略視場、分場與接縫限制。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Field, partitioning and stitching limits omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析高 NA 視場取捨」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze high-NA field trade-offs\"?","options":["視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。","比較控制其他變數，沒有把節點名稱當成波長。","倍率項與平移項未互相代替。"],"optionsEn":["Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution.","Other variables are controlled and a technology-node name is not treated as a wavelength.","Magnification terms are not substituted for translation terms."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：視場與掩模成像限制依選定架構討論，不只標解析度更高。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Field and mask-imaging constraints are discussed for the selected architecture, not only better resolution. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-206"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-208","order":26,"sequence":208,"title":"回傳曝光校正資料","titleEn":"Return exposure-correction data","objective":"校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。","objectiveEn":"Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把焦距、劑量及套刻殘差回傳至虛擬配方卡，標示適用圖層與版次。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Return focus, dose and overlay residuals to the virtual process card and label applicable layer and revision.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：校正資料套用到不同圖層條件。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Corrections applied to incompatible layers or conditions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。","checkEn":"Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-208-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。 對應操作：把焦距、劑量及套刻殘差回傳至虛擬配方卡，標示適用圖層與版次。","textEn":"Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible. Corresponding operation: Return focus, dose and overlay residuals to the virtual process card and label applicable layer and revision."},{"id":"sc-208-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"解析度、焦深、劑量、套刻與隨機缺陷是不同的成像限制。校正平均偏差不能自動消除局部或隨機尾端缺陷。 本步特別排查：校正資料套用到不同圖層條件。","textEn":"Resolution, depth of focus, dose, overlay and stochastic defects impose different imaging limits. Correcting a mean bias does not automatically eliminate local or stochastic-tail defects. Specifically examine: Corrections applied to incompatible layers or conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「回傳曝光校正資料」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Return exposure-correction data\"?","options":["解析度改善與焦深代價同時呈現。","插值沒有平滑掉會造成失焦的實際突起。","校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。"],"optionsEn":["Resolution improvement and depth-of-focus cost are shown together.","Interpolation does not erase protrusions that cause defocus.","Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：校正只套用到相容條件，並保留未改善的殘差。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Corrections apply only to compatible conditions and unresolved residuals remain visible. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-asml-metrology","sc-asml-optics","sc-asml-light"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-207"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"cleanroom","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察微影工作環境；照片不能呈現光阻化學、線寬、套刻或設備內部狀態。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a lithography working environment; the photograph cannot establish resist chemistry, critical dimension, overlay or internal tool state.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m09","order":9,"title":"蝕刻與圖案轉移","titleEn":"Etching and pattern transfer","description":"從遮罩預算到三維剖面驗收，分開反應物供應、離子作用、鈍化、端點及選擇比。","descriptionEn":"Follow mask budgeting through three-dimensional acceptance while separating reactant supply, ion effects, passivation, endpoint and selectivity.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-209","order":1,"sequence":209,"title":"讀取待蝕刻堆疊","titleEn":"Read the etch target stack","objective":"目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。","objectiveEn":"Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在剖面指定目標膜、遮罩及停止層，標出暴露方向。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Identify target film, mask and stop layer in the section and mark exposed directions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：目標材料與停止層標錯。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Target material or stop layer mislabeled. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。","checkEn":"Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-209-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。 對應操作：在剖面指定目標膜、遮罩及停止層，標出暴露方向。","textEn":"Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color. Corresponding operation: Identify target film, mask and stop layer in the section and mark exposed directions."},{"id":"sc-209-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：目標材料與停止層標錯。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Target material or stop layer mislabeled."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「讀取待蝕刻堆疊」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Read the etch target stack\"?","options":["錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。","電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。"],"optionsEn":["Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color.","Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-208"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-210","order":2,"sequence":210,"title":"選擇濕式或乾式路線","titleEn":"Select wet or dry etching","objective":"濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","objectiveEn":"Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較化學移除及電漿移除的輪廓示意，依材料和方向性需求選路線。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare chemical and plasma-removal profiles and choose a route for material and directionality needs.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略晶向選擇性或輪廓需求。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Crystallographic selectivity or profile requirements ignored. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","checkEn":"Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-210-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。 對應操作：比較化學移除及電漿移除的輪廓示意，依材料和方向性需求選路線。","textEn":"Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately. Corresponding operation: Compare chemical and plasma-removal profiles and choose a route for material and directionality needs."},{"id":"sc-210-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：忽略晶向選擇性或輪廓需求。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Crystallographic selectivity or profile requirements ignored."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇濕式或乾式路線」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select wet or dry etching\"?","options":["濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。","中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。"],"optionsEn":["Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","Profile changes support conclusions about directionality.","Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-209"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-211","order":3,"sequence":211,"title":"估算遮罩消耗預算","titleEn":"Estimate mask-consumption budget","objective":"預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。","objectiveEn":"The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以示意選擇比把目標移除量換算成遮罩損失，納入不均勻區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Use illustrative selectivity to estimate mask loss from target removal and include nonuniform regions.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：最薄遮罩或清底餘量未納入。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Thinnest mask or clearing margin omitted. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。","checkEn":"The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-211-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。 對應操作：以示意選擇比把目標移除量換算成遮罩損失，納入不均勻區。","textEn":"The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements. Corresponding operation: Use illustrative selectivity to estimate mask loss from target removal and include nonuniform regions."},{"id":"sc-211-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：最薄遮罩或清底餘量未納入。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Thinnest mask or clearing margin omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「估算遮罩消耗預算」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Estimate mask-consumption budget\"?","options":["深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。"],"optionsEn":["Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-210"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-212","order":4,"sequence":212,"title":"核對蝕刻前圖案","titleEn":"Verify the pre-etch pattern","objective":"已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。","objectiveEn":"Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將顯影後 CD 圖與目标截面對齊，標記橋接與未清底開口。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Register after-development CD data to the target section and mark bridges and uncleared openings.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：前段圖案缺陷誤歸因蝕刻。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Upstream pattern defects blamed on etching. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。","checkEn":"Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-212-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。 對應操作：將顯影後 CD 圖與目标截面對齊，標記橋接與未清底開口。","textEn":"Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward. Corresponding operation: Register after-development CD data to the target section and mark bridges and uncleared openings."},{"id":"sc-212-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：前段圖案缺陷誤歸因蝕刻。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Upstream pattern defects blamed on etching."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對蝕刻前圖案」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify the pre-etch pattern\"?","options":["停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。","最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。"],"optionsEn":["Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward.","The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-211"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-213","order":5,"sequence":213,"title":"執行底層開口分支","titleEn":"Open the underlayer branch","objective":"開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","objectiveEn":"The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：有抗反射底層時先轉移開口，觀察剩餘光阻和下層。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. When an antireflective underlayer is present, open it first and inspect remaining resist and substrate layers.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：底層開口過度消耗光阻。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Underlayer opening excessively consumes resist. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","checkEn":"The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-213-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。 對應操作：有抗反射底層時先轉移開口，觀察剩餘光阻和下層。","textEn":"The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask. Corresponding operation: When an antireflective underlayer is present, open it first and inspect remaining resist and substrate layers."},{"id":"sc-213-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：底層開口過度消耗光阻。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Underlayer opening excessively consumes resist."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「執行底層開口分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Open the underlayer branch\"?","options":["開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。","訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。"],"optionsEn":["The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings.","The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-212"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-214","order":6,"sequence":214,"title":"比較電漿密度與偏壓","titleEn":"Separate plasma density from bias","objective":"電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。","objectiveEn":"Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在示意模型分別變動離子供給與入射能量，對比移除率與損傷。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Vary ion supply and incident energy separately in the model and compare removal with damage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：離子供給與入射能量混為一談。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Ion supply confused with incident energy. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。","checkEn":"Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-214-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。 對應操作：在示意模型分別變動離子供給與入射能量，對比移除率與損傷。","textEn":"Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable. Corresponding operation: Vary ion supply and incident energy separately in the model and compare removal with damage."},{"id":"sc-214-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：離子供給與入射能量混為一談。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Ion supply confused with incident energy."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較電漿密度與偏壓」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Separate plasma density from bias\"?","options":["溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。"],"optionsEn":["Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-213"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-215","order":7,"sequence":215,"title":"觀察離子入射方向","titleEn":"Observe ion-arrival direction","objective":"方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。","objectiveEn":"Profile changes support conclusions about directionality.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較寬與窄角度分布，查看側壁侵蝕及底部移除。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare broad and narrow arrival-angle distributions and inspect sidewall erosion and bottom removal.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Profile changes support conclusions about directionality.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：方向分布改變造成側壁損失。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Changed angular distribution causes sidewall loss. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。","checkEn":"Profile changes support conclusions about directionality.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-215-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。 對應操作：比較寬與窄角度分布，查看側壁侵蝕及底部移除。","textEn":"Profile changes support conclusions about directionality. Corresponding operation: Compare broad and narrow arrival-angle distributions and inspect sidewall erosion and bottom removal."},{"id":"sc-215-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：方向分布改變造成側壁損失。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Changed angular distribution causes sidewall loss."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「觀察離子入射方向」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Observe ion-arrival direction\"?","options":["過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。","深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。"],"optionsEn":["Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","Profile changes support conclusions about directionality.","Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Profile changes support conclusions about directionality. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-214"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-216","order":8,"sequence":216,"title":"檢查中性反應物供應","titleEn":"Inspect neutral-reactant delivery","objective":"深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","objectiveEn":"Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在深孔模型追蹤中性物種到達底部的比例，與表面耗用比較。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track the fraction of neutral species reaching feature bottoms and compare surface consumption.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：深孔供料不足被誤診能量不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Deep-feature starvation misdiagnosed as insufficient energy. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","checkEn":"Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-216-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。 對應操作：在深孔模型追蹤中性物種到達底部的比例，與表面耗用比較。","textEn":"Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy. Corresponding operation: Track the fraction of neutral species reaching feature bottoms and compare surface consumption."},{"id":"sc-216-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：深孔供料不足被誤診能量不足。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Deep-feature starvation misdiagnosed as insufficient energy."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查中性反應物供應」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect neutral-reactant delivery\"?","options":["深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。","每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。"],"optionsEn":["Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects.","Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-215"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-217","order":9,"sequence":217,"title":"平衡側壁鈍化","titleEn":"Balance sidewall passivation","objective":"最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。","objectiveEn":"The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較鈍化較強與較弱的剖面，觀察側蝕、頸縮及底部阻塞。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare stronger and weaker passivation and inspect undercut, necking and bottom blockage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：側壁保護過強堵底或過弱側蝕。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Passivation blocks bottoms or permits undercut. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。","checkEn":"The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-217-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。 對應操作：比較鈍化較強與較弱的剖面，觀察側蝕、頸縮及底部阻塞。","textEn":"The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance. Corresponding operation: Compare stronger and weaker passivation and inspect undercut, necking and bottom blockage."},{"id":"sc-217-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：側壁保護過強堵底或過弱側蝕。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Passivation blocks bottoms or permits undercut."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「平衡側壁鈍化」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Balance sidewall passivation\"?","options":["錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。"],"optionsEn":["Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-216"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-218","order":10,"sequence":218,"title":"調整反應物停留示意","titleEn":"Compare reactant residence time","objective":"停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。","objectiveEn":"Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：改變示意抽氣和供料平衡，觀察副產物殘留與反應物利用。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Change schematic pumping and delivery balance and inspect byproduct retention and reactant utilization.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：用總壓力直接推定停留時間。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Residence time inferred directly from total pressure. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。","checkEn":"Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-218-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。 對應操作：改變示意抽氣和供料平衡，觀察副產物殘留與反應物利用。","textEn":"Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings. Corresponding operation: Change schematic pumping and delivery balance and inspect byproduct retention and reactant utilization."},{"id":"sc-218-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：用總壓力直接推定停留時間。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Residence time inferred directly from total pressure."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「調整反應物停留示意」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare reactant residence time\"?","options":["損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。","中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。"],"optionsEn":["Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings.","Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-217"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-219","order":11,"sequence":219,"title":"檢查晶圓溫度作用","titleEn":"Inspect wafer-temperature effects","objective":"溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","objectiveEn":"Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同表面溫度下的示意吸附與揮發，追蹤殘留及輪廓。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare adsorption and volatility at different surface temperatures and track residue and profile changes.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：溫度改變吸附及副產物揮發。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Temperature changes adsorption and byproduct volatility. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","checkEn":"Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-219-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。 對應操作：比較不同表面溫度下的示意吸附與揮發，追蹤殘留及輪廓。","textEn":"Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented. Corresponding operation: Compare adsorption and volatility at different surface temperatures and track residue and profile changes."},{"id":"sc-219-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：溫度改變吸附及副產物揮發。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Temperature changes adsorption and byproduct volatility."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查晶圓溫度作用」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect wafer-temperature effects\"?","options":["溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。"],"optionsEn":["Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-218"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-220","order":12,"sequence":220,"title":"評估深寬比相依蝕刻","titleEn":"Evaluate aspect-ratio-dependent etching","objective":"深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。","objectiveEn":"Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：同時蝕刻不同寬度但相同起始深度的開口，量測完成深度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Etch openings of different widths from the same starting depth and measure resulting depths.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：窄孔清除落後被平均速率掩蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Narrow-feature lag hidden by average etch rate. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。","checkEn":"Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-220-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。 對應操作：同時蝕刻不同寬度但相同起始深度的開口，量測完成深度。","textEn":"Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate. Corresponding operation: Etch openings of different widths from the same starting depth and measure resulting depths."},{"id":"sc-220-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：窄孔清除落後被平均速率掩蓋。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Narrow-feature lag hidden by average etch rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估深寬比相依蝕刻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate aspect-ratio-dependent etching\"?","options":["停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。"],"optionsEn":["Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-219"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-221","order":13,"sequence":221,"title":"評估圖案密度負載","titleEn":"Evaluate pattern-density loading","objective":"負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。","objectiveEn":"Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較相同線寬在密集與稀疏區的蝕刻深度，保持其他條件一致。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare etch depth at equal widths in dense and sparse regions while holding other conditions fixed.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：圖案密度與深寬比效應混合。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Pattern-density effects mixed with aspect-ratio effects. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。","checkEn":"Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-221-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。 對應操作：比較相同線寬在密集與稀疏區的蝕刻深度，保持其他條件一致。","textEn":"Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects. Corresponding operation: Compare etch depth at equal widths in dense and sparse regions while holding other conditions fixed."},{"id":"sc-221-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：圖案密度與深寬比效應混合。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Pattern-density effects mixed with aspect-ratio effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「評估圖案密度負載」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Evaluate pattern-density loading\"?","options":["圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。","訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects.","The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-220"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-222","order":14,"sequence":222,"title":"量測側壁錐度","titleEn":"Measure sidewall taper","objective":"錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","objectiveEn":"Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在頂部、中段與底部量測寬度，以輪廓定義側壁角度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure widths at top, middle and bottom and define sidewall angle from the profile.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：只有頂部 CD 缺少深度輪廓。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Top CD available without depth-resolved profile. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","checkEn":"Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-222-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。 對應操作：在頂部、中段與底部量測寬度，以輪廓定義側壁角度。","textEn":"Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone. Corresponding operation: Measure widths at top, middle and bottom and define sidewall angle from the profile."},{"id":"sc-222-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：只有頂部 CD 缺少深度輪廓。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Top CD available without depth-resolved profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測側壁錐度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure sidewall taper\"?","options":["錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。","控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。"],"optionsEn":["Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone.","The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：錐度採完整剖面判定，非只用頂部 CD。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Taper is determined from the section rather than top CD alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-221"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-223","order":15,"sequence":223,"title":"診斷側壁弓形","titleEn":"Diagnose sidewall bowing","objective":"中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。","objectiveEn":"Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：放大中段寬度異常的截面，對照側壁保護與入射分布。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Magnify a section with abnormal middle width and compare passivation with arrival-angle distribution.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：中段弓形被當成單純錐度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Mid-depth bowing treated as simple taper. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。","checkEn":"Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-223-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。 對應操作：放大中段寬度異常的截面，對照側壁保護與入射分布。","textEn":"Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper. Corresponding operation: Magnify a section with abnormal middle width and compare passivation with arrival-angle distribution."},{"id":"sc-223-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：中段弓形被當成單純錐度。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Mid-depth bowing treated as simple taper."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷側壁弓形」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose sidewall bowing\"?","options":["過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。"],"optionsEn":["Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：中段外擴與整體錐度分開分類。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Mid-depth widening is classified separately from overall taper. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-222"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-224","order":16,"sequence":224,"title":"診斷底部微溝","titleEn":"Diagnose microtrenching","objective":"局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","objectiveEn":"Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：查看底角局部加深區，對照離子反射及側壁幾何示意。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect locally deepened bottom corners against ion-reflection and sidewall-geometry models.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：底角微溝被平均深度隱藏。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Corner microtrenches hidden by average depth. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","checkEn":"Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-224-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。 對應操作：查看底角局部加深區，對照離子反射及側壁幾何示意。","textEn":"Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth. Corresponding operation: Inspect locally deepened bottom corners against ion-reflection and sidewall-geometry models."},{"id":"sc-224-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：底角微溝被平均深度隱藏。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Corner microtrenches hidden by average depth."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷底部微溝」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose microtrenching\"?","options":["預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。","局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。","每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。"],"optionsEn":["The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements.","Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth.","Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：局部微溝未被平均深度掩蓋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Local microtrenches are not hidden by average depth. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-223"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-225","order":17,"sequence":225,"title":"分析停止層選擇比","titleEn":"Analyze selectivity to the stop layer","objective":"停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","objectiveEn":"Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較目標層清除後停止層的消耗，增加示意清底時間查看代價。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare stop-layer loss after target clearance and extend illustrative overetch to inspect its cost.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：忽略保護層也有有限移除率。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Finite removal of the protected layer ignored. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","checkEn":"Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-225-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。 對應操作：比較目標層清除後停止層的消耗，增加示意清底時間查看代價。","textEn":"Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval. Corresponding operation: Compare stop-layer loss after target clearance and extend illustrative overetch to inspect its cost."},{"id":"sc-225-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：忽略保護層也有有限移除率。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Finite removal of the protected layer ignored."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析停止層選擇比」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze selectivity to the stop layer\"?","options":["停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。","高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。"],"optionsEn":["Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval.","High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：停止層剩餘量與最慢清底區共同決定可用區間。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Remaining stop material and the slowest-clearing region jointly define the feasible interval. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-224"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-226","order":18,"sequence":226,"title":"判讀光學端點訊號","titleEn":"Interpret optical endpoint signals","objective":"訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。","objectiveEn":"The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將發光訊號轉折與材料界面到達時間對照，檢查雜訊和延遲。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Relate emission-signal changes to interface arrival and inspect noise and delay.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：雜訊峰或感測延遲被當真端點。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Noise peaks or sensor delay mistaken for endpoint. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。","checkEn":"The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-226-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。 對應操作：將發光訊號轉折與材料界面到達時間對照，檢查雜訊和延遲。","textEn":"The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak. Corresponding operation: Relate emission-signal changes to interface arrival and inspect noise and delay."},{"id":"sc-226-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：雜訊峰或感測延遲被當真端點。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Noise peaks or sensor delay mistaken for endpoint."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判讀光學端點訊號」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Interpret optical endpoint signals\"?","options":["損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：訊號轉折需與材料轉換一致，不能只用任意峰值。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The signal change must match a material transition rather than an arbitrary peak. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-225"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-227","order":19,"sequence":227,"title":"比較時間式與端點式控制","titleEn":"Compare timed and endpoint control","objective":"控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","objectiveEn":"The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對厚度偏差的兩片虛擬晶圓使用不同停止方式，查看清底與損耗。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Apply different stopping methods to two virtual wafers with thickness variation and inspect clearing and loss.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：厚度差異使固定時間失效。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Thickness variation invalidates fixed timing. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","checkEn":"The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-227-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。 對應操作：對厚度偏差的兩片虛擬晶圓使用不同停止方式，查看清底與損耗。","textEn":"The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation. Corresponding operation: Apply different stopping methods to two virtual wafers with thickness variation and inspect clearing and loss."},{"id":"sc-227-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：厚度差異使固定時間失效。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Thickness variation invalidates fixed timing."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較時間式與端點式控制」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare timed and endpoint control\"?","options":["電漿密度與基板偏壓未當成同一控制量。","控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。","殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。"],"optionsEn":["Plasma density and substrate bias are not treated as the same control variable.","The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation.","Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：控制方式的選擇能解釋厚度變化下的結果。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The control-method choice explains outcomes under thickness variation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-226"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-228","order":20,"sequence":228,"title":"配置有限過蝕刻","titleEn":"Allocate limited overetch","objective":"過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","objectiveEn":"Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以最慢清除區為基準增加示意餘裕，同時查看遮罩與停止層餘量。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Add illustrative margin based on the slowest-clearing region while inspecting mask and stop-layer reserves.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：過長過蝕刻損耗遮罩及停止層。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Excess overetch consumes mask and stop layers. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","checkEn":"Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-228-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。 對應操作：以最慢清除區為基準增加示意餘裕，同時查看遮罩與停止層餘量。","textEn":"Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints. Corresponding operation: Add illustrative margin based on the slowest-clearing region while inspecting mask and stop-layer reserves."},{"id":"sc-228-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：過長過蝕刻損耗遮罩及停止層。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Excess overetch consumes mask and stop layers."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置有限過蝕刻」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Allocate limited overetch\"?","options":["過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。","CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","方向性結論由輪廓變化支持。"],"optionsEn":["Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints.","CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","Profile changes support conclusions about directionality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：過蝕刻不是越長越好，清底與損傷有共同限制。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Overetch is not maximized; clearance and damage impose joint constraints. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-227"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-229","order":21,"sequence":229,"title":"模擬原子層蝕刻循環","titleEn":"Model atomic-layer etch cycles","objective":"每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。","objectiveEn":"Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把表面改質與移除分為兩段，觀察循環間反應是否趨於自限。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Separate surface modification from removal and inspect whether each cycle tends toward self-limitation.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：將每循環移除量當固定整原子層。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Per-cycle removal assumed to equal a whole atomic layer. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。","checkEn":"Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-229-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。 對應操作：把表面改質與移除分為兩段，觀察循環間反應是否趨於自限。","textEn":"Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer. Corresponding operation: Separate surface modification from removal and inspect whether each cycle tends toward self-limitation."},{"id":"sc-229-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：將每循環移除量當固定整原子層。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Per-cycle removal assumed to equal a whole atomic layer."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「模擬原子層蝕刻循環」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Model atomic-layer etch cycles\"?","options":["圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","深孔底部供料不足與離子能量不足分開診斷。","每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。"],"optionsEn":["Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","Bottom reactant starvation is distinguished from insufficient ion energy.","Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：每循環移除量由材料與條件決定，非保證一完整原子層。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Removal per cycle depends on material and conditions rather than guaranteeing a whole atomic layer. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-228"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-230","order":22,"sequence":230,"title":"分析選擇性蝕刻分支","titleEn":"Analyze selective-etch branches","objective":"高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","objectiveEn":"High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在兩種材料相鄰模型中比較移除率，查看高選擇比的有限損耗。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare removal rates in adjacent materials and inspect finite loss even at high selectivity.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：高選擇比被誤當無限選擇比。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: High selectivity mistaken for infinite selectivity. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","checkEn":"High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-230-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。 對應操作：在兩種材料相鄰模型中比較移除率，查看高選擇比的有限損耗。","textEn":"High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material. Corresponding operation: Compare removal rates in adjacent materials and inspect finite loss even at high selectivity."},{"id":"sc-230-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：高選擇比被誤當無限選擇比。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: High selectivity mistaken for infinite selectivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分析選擇性蝕刻分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Analyze selective-etch branches\"?","options":["最佳方案兼顧側壁保護與底部開通。","高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。","目標層與保護層角色清楚，不因顏色相同而混淆材料。"],"optionsEn":["The selected outcome balances sidewall protection with bottom clearance.","High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material.","Target and protected-layer roles are clear and materials are not confused by display color."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：高選擇比不被當作保護材料完全零損耗。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: High selectivity is not interpreted as zero loss of the protected material. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-229"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-231","order":23,"sequence":231,"title":"診斷電漿充電損傷","titleEn":"Diagnose plasma charging damage","objective":"損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","objectiveEn":"Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較連接與浮接圖案的電位示意，定位薄介電層風險。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare potentials in connected and floating patterns and locate thin-dielectric risk areas.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：浮接圖案局部累積電荷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Local charge accumulates on floating patterns. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","checkEn":"Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-231-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。 對應操作：比較連接與浮接圖案的電位示意，定位薄介電層風險。","textEn":"Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths. Corresponding operation: Compare potentials in connected and floating patterns and locate thin-dielectric risk areas."},{"id":"sc-231-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：浮接圖案局部累積電荷。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Local charge accumulates on floating patterns."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷電漿充電損傷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose plasma charging damage\"?","options":["損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。","濕蝕刻不被一律宣稱等向性，晶向選擇性分支另列。","停留時間效果與總壓力讀值不直接等同。"],"optionsEn":["Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths.","Wet etching is not universally called isotropic; crystallographic branches are labeled separately.","Residence-time effects are not equated directly with total-pressure readings."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：損傷位置與電荷累積路徑有對應。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Damage locations correspond to charge-accumulation paths. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-230"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-232","order":24,"sequence":232,"title":"清除蝕刻聚合殘留","titleEn":"Remove etch-polymer residues","objective":"殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。","objectiveEn":"Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較清理前後開口及側壁影像，避免把殘留當成目標膜。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare opening and sidewall images before and after cleaning without confusing residue with target film.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：聚合殘留與材料本體混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Polymer residue confused with the material itself. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。","checkEn":"Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-232-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。 對應操作：比較清理前後開口及側壁影像，避免把殘留當成目標膜。","textEn":"Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced. Corresponding operation: Compare opening and sidewall images before and after cleaning without confusing residue with target film."},{"id":"sc-232-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：聚合殘留與材料本體混淆。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Polymer residue confused with the material itself."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「清除蝕刻聚合殘留」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Remove etch-polymer residues\"?","options":["預算保留最薄遮罩區及額外清底需求。","溫度變化對表面化學的影響有記錄。","殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。"],"optionsEn":["The budget includes the thinnest mask and additional clearing requirements.","Temperature effects on surface chemistry are documented.","Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：殘留降低且圖案尺寸保留有雙重證據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Both residue reduction and dimensional retention are evidenced. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-231"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-233","order":25,"sequence":233,"title":"量測蝕刻偏差","titleEn":"Measure etch bias","objective":"CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","objectiveEn":"CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用相同位置的顯影後及蝕刻後 CD 求變化，保留量測高度差異。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare after-development and after-etch CD at matching sites and retain measurement-height differences.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：CD 的高度或邊緣定義不同。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Different CD heights or edge definitions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","checkEn":"CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-233-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。 對應操作：用相同位置的顯影後及蝕刻後 CD 求變化，保留量測高度差異。","textEn":"CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions. Corresponding operation: Compare after-development and after-etch CD at matching sites and retain measurement-height differences."},{"id":"sc-233-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：CD 的高度或邊緣定義不同。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Different CD heights or edge definitions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測蝕刻偏差」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure etch bias\"?","options":["深度差異與開口深寬比相連，不只平均整片速率。","CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。","已存在的光阻缺陷先記錄，未在蝕刻後才全歸咎蝕刻。"],"optionsEn":["Depth variation is linked to feature aspect ratio rather than only average wafer etch rate.","CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions.","Pre-existing resist defects are recorded rather than all blamed on etching afterward."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：CD 差異在一致邊緣定義下才作為蝕刻偏差。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: CD differences are called etch bias only under consistent edge definitions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-232"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-234","order":26,"sequence":234,"title":"交接轉移後圖案","titleEn":"Handoff the transferred pattern","objective":"圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","objectiveEn":"Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：結合深度、輪廓、缺陷及材料殘留圖，將異常連結到下游風險。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine depth, profile, defect and residue maps and connect anomalies to downstream risks.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：俯視正常但三維輪廓異常。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Normal top view hides abnormal three-dimensional profiles. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","checkEn":"Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-234-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。 對應操作：結合深度、輪廓、缺陷及材料殘留圖，將異常連結到下游風險。","textEn":"Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone. Corresponding operation: Combine depth, profile, defect and residue maps and connect anomalies to downstream risks."},{"id":"sc-234-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"蝕刻速率、方向性與選擇比不是同一性能。材料、尺寸、圖案密度及深寬比會讓同一批次出現不同局部結果。 本步特別排查：俯視正常但三維輪廓異常。","textEn":"Etch rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct properties. Material, size, pattern density and aspect ratio can produce different local outcomes within one batch. Specifically examine: Normal top view hides abnormal three-dimensional profiles."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接轉移後圖案」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handoff the transferred pattern\"?","options":["圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。","開口完成但未過度消耗主要蝕刻遮罩。","負載效應與單一特徵深寬比效應分開。"],"optionsEn":["Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone.","The underlayer is opened without excessive loss of the main etch mask.","Loading effects are distinguished from individual-feature aspect-ratio effects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：圖案轉移驗證涵蓋三維輪廓，不僅俯視影像。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Pattern-transfer verification covers three-dimensional profiles rather than top views alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-lam-etch","sc-mc-index","sc-lam-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-233"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"semiconductor-cleanroom","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m10","order":10,"title":"閘極圖案與內外間隔層","titleEn":"Gate patterning and inner/outer spacers","description":"建立閘極與外間隔層幾何，再比較 FinFET 與奈米片內間隔層分支；不取代後續源汲極及替代閘極模組。","descriptionEn":"Build gate and outer-spacer geometry and compare FinFET and nanosheet inner-spacer branches; later source-drain and replacement-gate modules remain necessary.","route":"教育模組；替代技術依步驟明示為分支，不代表同一片晶圓必須全部依序加工。","routeEn":"Educational module; alternatives are labeled as branches and are not mandatory sequential operations on one wafer.","sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"steps":[{"id":"sc-235","order":1,"sequence":235,"title":"選定先閘或後閘分支","titleEn":"Select gate-first or gate-last branch","objective":"犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。","objectiveEn":"Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：並排最終閘極先形成與替代閘極路線，標出各自後續高溫步驟。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare gate-first and replacement-gate routes and mark later high-temperature steps.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘混淆。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Dummy gate confused with final metal gate. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。","checkEn":"Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-235-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。 對應操作：並排最終閘極先形成與替代閘極路線，標出各自後續高溫步驟。","textEn":"Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished. Corresponding operation: Compare gate-first and replacement-gate routes and mark later high-temperature steps."},{"id":"sc-235-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘混淆。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Dummy gate confused with final metal gate."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選定先閘或後閘分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Select gate-first or gate-last branch\"?","options":["硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。"],"optionsEn":["The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-234"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-236","order":2,"sequence":236,"title":"配置閘極導體堆疊","titleEn":"Configure the gate-conductor stack","objective":"堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。","objectiveEn":"The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把教材分支所需導體及介電層依序放入剖面，查看接觸界面。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place conductors and dielectrics for the selected educational branch in the section and inspect interfaces.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：堆疊組合不屬同一路線。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Stack elements belong to incompatible routes. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。","checkEn":"The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-236-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。 對應操作：把教材分支所需導體及介電層依序放入剖面，查看接觸界面。","textEn":"The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives. Corresponding operation: Place conductors and dielectrics for the selected educational branch in the section and inspect interfaces."},{"id":"sc-236-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：堆疊組合不屬同一路線。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Stack elements belong to incompatible routes."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置閘極導體堆疊」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure the gate-conductor stack\"?","options":["側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。","導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives.","Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-235"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-237","order":3,"sequence":237,"title":"配置閘極頂蓋","titleEn":"Configure the gate cap","objective":"頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","objectiveEn":"Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在導體上放置頂蓋或硬遮罩，觀察後續閘極蝕刻的保護作用。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Place a cap or hard mask above the conductor and inspect its protection during gate etching.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：頂蓋與閘介電層功能混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Gate cap and dielectric functions mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","checkEn":"Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-237-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。 對應操作：在導體上放置頂蓋或硬遮罩，觀察後續閘極蝕刻的保護作用。","textEn":"Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function. Corresponding operation: Place a cap or hard mask above the conductor and inspect its protection during gate etching."},{"id":"sc-237-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：頂蓋與閘介電層功能混用。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Gate cap and dielectric functions mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置閘極頂蓋」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure the gate cap\"?","options":["頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。","水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。"],"optionsEn":["Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone.","Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-236"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-238","order":4,"sequence":238,"title":"建立閘極光阻圖案","titleEn":"Build the gate-resist pattern","objective":"閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。","objectiveEn":"Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將閘極線對準主動區，查看線條是否跨越所需通道。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Align gate lines to active areas and inspect whether they cross the intended channels.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：閘線未跨越預期主動區。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Gate line does not cross the intended active area. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。","checkEn":"Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-238-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。 對應操作：將閘極線對準主動區，查看線條是否跨越所需通道。","textEn":"Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations. Corresponding operation: Align gate lines to active areas and inspect whether they cross the intended channels."},{"id":"sc-238-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：閘線未跨越預期主動區。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Gate line does not cross the intended active area."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立閘極光阻圖案」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Build the gate-resist pattern\"?","options":["不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。"],"optionsEn":["Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-237"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-239","order":5,"sequence":239,"title":"檢查閘長與線端","titleEn":"Inspect gate length and line ends","objective":"線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。","objectiveEn":"Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：分別量測線條中段 CD 與端部縮短，對照器件有效區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure mid-line CD and line-end shortening separately against the active device area.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：線端縮短被中段 CD 掩蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Line-end shortening hidden by mid-line CD. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。","checkEn":"Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-239-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。 對應操作：分別量測線條中段 CD 與端部縮短，對照器件有效區。","textEn":"Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures. Corresponding operation: Measure mid-line CD and line-end shortening separately against the active device area."},{"id":"sc-239-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：線端縮短被中段 CD 掩蓋。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Line-end shortening hidden by mid-line CD."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查閘長與線端」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect gate length and line ends\"?","options":["有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。","閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。"],"optionsEn":["The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures.","Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-238"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-240","order":6,"sequence":240,"title":"轉移閘極硬遮罩","titleEn":"Transfer the gate hard mask","objective":"硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","objectiveEn":"The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把光阻線轉入硬遮罩，檢查側壁粗糙及頂部消耗。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Transfer resist lines into the hard mask and inspect sidewall roughness and top loss.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：硬遮罩粗糙或餘量不足。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Rough hard mask or insufficient thickness reserve. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","checkEn":"The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-240-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。 對應操作：把光阻線轉入硬遮罩，檢查側壁粗糙及頂部消耗。","textEn":"The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness. Corresponding operation: Transfer resist lines into the hard mask and inspect sidewall roughness and top loss."},{"id":"sc-240-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：硬遮罩粗糙或餘量不足。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Rough hard mask or insufficient thickness reserve."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「轉移閘極硬遮罩」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Transfer the gate hard mask\"?","options":["硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。","平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。"],"optionsEn":["The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method.","Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-239"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-241","order":7,"sequence":241,"title":"選擇性蝕刻閘極導體","titleEn":"Selectively etch the gate conductor","objective":"導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。","objectiveEn":"Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在目標導體逐步移除時追蹤底部介電層，查看最慢清底區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track the underlying dielectric while removing the conductor and inspect the slowest-clearing region.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：清底過程損傷下方介電層。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Clearing damages the underlying dielectric. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。","checkEn":"Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-241-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。 對應操作：在目標導體逐步移除時追蹤底部介電層，查看最慢清底區。","textEn":"Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together. Corresponding operation: Track the underlying dielectric while removing the conductor and inspect the slowest-clearing region."},{"id":"sc-241-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：清底過程損傷下方介電層。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Clearing damages the underlying dielectric."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇性蝕刻閘極導體」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Selectively etch the gate conductor\"?","options":["幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-240"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-242","order":8,"sequence":242,"title":"判讀閘極蝕刻端點","titleEn":"Read the gate-etch endpoint","objective":"端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。","objectiveEn":"Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：把材料轉換訊號與截面清底情形對照，檢查訊號延遲。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare material-transition signals with cross-sectional clearing and inspect signal delay.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：端點延遲或材料訊號辨識錯誤。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Endpoint delay or misidentified material signal. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。","checkEn":"Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-242-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。 對應操作：把材料轉換訊號與截面清底情形對照，檢查訊號延遲。","textEn":"Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone. Corresponding operation: Compare material-transition signals with cross-sectional clearing and inspect signal delay."},{"id":"sc-242-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：端點延遲或材料訊號辨識錯誤。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Endpoint delay or misidentified material signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「判讀閘極蝕刻端點」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Read the gate-etch endpoint\"?","options":["三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。","殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。"],"optionsEn":["One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone.","Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-241"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-243","order":9,"sequence":243,"title":"控制閘極底部殘腳","titleEn":"Control gate-foot residues","objective":"不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","objectiveEn":"Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：放大閘極底角，分辨導體殘腳、聚合物及介電層。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Magnify gate-bottom corners and distinguish conductor feet, polymer and dielectric.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：不同材料殘腳被相同處理。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Feet of different materials treated identically. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","checkEn":"Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-243-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。 對應操作：放大閘極底角，分辨導體殘腳、聚合物及介電層。","textEn":"Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone. Corresponding operation: Magnify gate-bottom corners and distinguish conductor feet, polymer and dielectric."},{"id":"sc-243-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：不同材料殘腳被相同處理。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Feet of different materials treated identically."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制閘極底部殘腳」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control gate-foot residues\"?","options":["不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。"],"optionsEn":["Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-242"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-244","order":10,"sequence":244,"title":"檢查閘極側壁斜率","titleEn":"Inspect gate sidewall slope","objective":"閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。","objectiveEn":"Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較上、中、下閘寬，估計輪廓對後續間隔層的影響。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare upper, middle and lower gate widths and assess effects on later spacers.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：側壁角度變化影響間隔層。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Sidewall-angle changes affect spacer formation. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。","checkEn":"Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-244-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。 對應操作：比較上、中、下閘寬，估計輪廓對後續間隔層的影響。","textEn":"Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD. Corresponding operation: Compare upper, middle and lower gate widths and assess effects on later spacers."},{"id":"sc-244-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：側壁角度變化影響間隔層。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Sidewall-angle changes affect spacer formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查閘極側壁斜率」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect gate sidewall slope\"?","options":["側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-243"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-245","order":11,"sequence":245,"title":"量測閘極線緣粗糙","titleEn":"Measure gate line-edge roughness","objective":"粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。","objectiveEn":"Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿閘邊追蹤位置變化，區分整體偏移與局部起伏。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Track edge position along the gate and separate global shift from local fluctuations.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：整體偏移混入局部粗糙統計。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Global shift included in local roughness statistics. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。","checkEn":"Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-245-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。 對應操作：沿閘邊追蹤位置變化，區分整體偏移與局部起伏。","textEn":"Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method. Corresponding operation: Track edge position along the gate and separate global shift from local fluctuations."},{"id":"sc-245-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：整體偏移混入局部粗糙統計。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Global shift included in local roughness statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測閘極線緣粗糙」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure gate line-edge roughness\"?","options":["內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。","水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。"],"optionsEn":["Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method.","Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-244"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-246","order":12,"sequence":246,"title":"檢查閘極下介電損傷","titleEn":"Inspect under-gate dielectric damage","objective":"幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","objectiveEn":"Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：對比閘極加工前後測試結構的漏電與 C-V，定位損傷分支。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare leakage and C-V of test structures before and after gate processing and locate possible damage.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：外觀完整掩蓋介電電性損傷。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Intact appearance hides dielectric electrical damage. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","checkEn":"Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-246-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。 對應操作：對比閘極加工前後測試結構的漏電與 C-V，定位損傷分支。","textEn":"Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior. Corresponding operation: Compare leakage and C-V of test structures before and after gate processing and locate possible damage."},{"id":"sc-246-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：外觀完整掩蓋介電電性損傷。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Intact appearance hides dielectric electrical damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「檢查閘極下介電損傷」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Inspect under-gate dielectric damage\"?","options":["幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-245"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-247","order":13,"sequence":247,"title":"清除閘極加工殘留","titleEn":"Clean gate-processing residues","objective":"殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。","objectiveEn":"Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：將去膠與聚合殘留清理分開觀察，檢查導體及介電層損失。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Observe resist stripping and polymer cleaning separately and inspect conductor and dielectric loss.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：清理造成有效尺寸或介電損耗。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Cleaning causes dimensional or dielectric loss. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。","checkEn":"Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-247-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。 對應操作：將去膠與聚合殘留清理分開觀察，檢查導體及介電層損失。","textEn":"Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness. Corresponding operation: Observe resist stripping and polymer cleaning separately and inspect conductor and dielectric loss."},{"id":"sc-247-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：清理造成有效尺寸或介電損耗。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Cleaning causes dimensional or dielectric loss."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「清除閘極加工殘留」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Clean gate-processing residues\"?","options":["有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。"],"optionsEn":["The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-246"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-248","order":14,"sequence":248,"title":"形成側壁襯層分支","titleEn":"Form a sidewall-liner branch","objective":"襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","objectiveEn":"The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在需要襯層的路線包覆閘極側壁，與不加襯層的剖面對照。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Wrap gate sidewalls with a liner where the route requires it and compare with the unlined section.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：襯層厚度未計入側向尺寸。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Liner thickness omitted from lateral dimensions. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","checkEn":"The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-248-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。 對應操作：在需要襯層的路線包覆閘極側壁，與不加襯層的剖面對照。","textEn":"The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions. Corresponding operation: Wrap gate sidewalls with a liner where the route requires it and compare with the unlined section."},{"id":"sc-248-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：襯層厚度未計入側向尺寸。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Liner thickness omitted from lateral dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「形成側壁襯層分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Form a sidewall-liner branch\"?","options":["犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。","襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。","平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。"],"optionsEn":["Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished.","The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions.","Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：襯層只在適用路線存在，厚度計入側向尺寸。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The liner appears only in applicable routes and its thickness enters lateral dimensions. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-247"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-249","order":15,"sequence":249,"title":"沉積外間隔層薄膜","titleEn":"Deposit the outer-spacer film","objective":"側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","objectiveEn":"Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：以示意共形薄膜覆蓋閘頂、側壁與平面，比較各處厚度。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Cover gate tops, sidewalls and horizontal surfaces with a schematic conformal film and compare thicknesses.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：平面膜厚代表不了角部覆蓋。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Planar thickness does not represent corner coverage. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","checkEn":"Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-249-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。 對應操作：以示意共形薄膜覆蓋閘頂、側壁與平面，比較各處厚度。","textEn":"Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness. Corresponding operation: Cover gate tops, sidewalls and horizontal surfaces with a schematic conformal film and compare thicknesses."},{"id":"sc-249-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：平面膜厚代表不了角部覆蓋。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Planar thickness does not represent corner coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「沉積外間隔層薄膜」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Deposit the outer-spacer film\"?","options":["側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。","低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness.","A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：側壁覆蓋由截面確認，而非只用平面膜厚。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Sidewall coverage is verified in section rather than inferred only from planar thickness. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-248"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-250","order":16,"sequence":250,"title":"建立間隔層回蝕","titleEn":"Form spacers by etch-back","objective":"水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。","objectiveEn":"Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：逐步移除水平面的薄膜，觀察側壁材料如何留下。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Remove film from horizontal surfaces incrementally and observe retention on sidewalls.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：水平清除時側壁也被過度移除。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Sidewalls over-etched during horizontal clearance. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。","checkEn":"Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-250-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。 對應操作：逐步移除水平面的薄膜，觀察側壁材料如何留下。","textEn":"Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain. Corresponding operation: Remove film from horizontal surfaces incrementally and observe retention on sidewalls."},{"id":"sc-250-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：水平清除時側壁也被過度移除。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Sidewalls over-etched during horizontal clearance."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「建立間隔層回蝕」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Form spacers by etch-back\"?","options":["三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。"],"optionsEn":["One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：水平開通時側壁仍保留所需間隔層。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Horizontal surfaces clear while required sidewall spacers remain. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-249"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-251","order":17,"sequence":251,"title":"控制間隔層肩部","titleEn":"Control spacer shoulders","objective":"肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","objectiveEn":"Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：比較不同回蝕程度的頂部肩形與下方隔離距離。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare top-shoulder shapes and lower isolation distances at different etch-back extents.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：肩部修整破壞隔離連續性。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Shoulder trimming breaks isolation continuity. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","checkEn":"Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-251-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。 對應操作：比較不同回蝕程度的頂部肩形與下方隔離距離。","textEn":"Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation. Corresponding operation: Compare top-shoulder shapes and lower isolation distances at different etch-back extents."},{"id":"sc-251-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：肩部修整破壞隔離連續性。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Shoulder trimming breaks isolation continuity."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「控制間隔層肩部」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Control spacer shoulders\"?","options":["閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。","肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。","犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。"],"optionsEn":["Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations.","Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation.","Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：肩部縮小未造成關鍵側壁隔離消失。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Shoulder reduction does not eliminate critical sidewall isolation. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-250"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-252","order":18,"sequence":252,"title":"量測間隔層底部寬度","titleEn":"Measure spacer base width","objective":"有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","objectiveEn":"The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在閘底與中段分別量測間隔層，確認與源汲極邊界的關係。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Measure spacers at gate base and mid-height and relate them to source-drain boundaries.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：不同高度的間隔寬度混用。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Spacer widths at different heights mixed. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","checkEn":"The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-252-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。 對應操作：在閘底與中段分別量測間隔層，確認與源汲極邊界的關係。","textEn":"The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit. Corresponding operation: Measure spacers at gate base and mid-height and relate them to source-drain boundaries."},{"id":"sc-252-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：不同高度的間隔寬度混用。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Spacer widths at different heights mixed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測間隔層底部寬度」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Measure spacer base width\"?","options":["有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。","內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit.","Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：有效隔離寬度的取樣高度明確。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The sampling height for effective isolation width is explicit. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-251"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-253","order":19,"sequence":253,"title":"診斷間隔層殘留薄膜","titleEn":"Diagnose spacer-film residues","objective":"平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。","objectiveEn":"Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：查看應暴露的源汲極平面，分辨連續薄膜與孤立殘粒。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Inspect source-drain surfaces that should be exposed and distinguish continuous film from isolated particles.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：源汲極平面仍有連續殘膜。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Continuous residual film remains on source-drain surfaces. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。","checkEn":"Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-253-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。 對應操作：查看應暴露的源汲極平面，分辨連續薄膜與孤立殘粒。","textEn":"Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria. Corresponding operation: Inspect source-drain surfaces that should be exposed and distinguish continuous film from isolated particles."},{"id":"sc-253-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：源汲極平面仍有連續殘膜。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Continuous residual film remains on source-drain surfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「診斷間隔層殘留薄膜」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Diagnose spacer-film residues\"?","options":["內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","硬遮罩保留所需閘線輪廓及餘量。","平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。"],"optionsEn":["Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","The hard mask retains required gate-line contours and reserve thickness.","Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：平面清除與側壁保留不是同一影像判據。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Horizontal clearance and sidewall retention use different image criteria. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-252"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-254","order":20,"sequence":254,"title":"比較間隔層材料電性","titleEn":"Compare spacer dielectric behavior","objective":"低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","objectiveEn":"A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：用示意低 k 與較高 k 材料比較寄生電容，同時查看機械及蝕刻相容性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Compare parasitic capacitance for illustrative lower-k and higher-k spacers while checking mechanical and etch compatibility.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：低 k 選材忽略結構或可靠度。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Low-k selection ignores structural or reliability costs. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","checkEn":"A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-254-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。 對應操作：用示意低 k 與較高 k 材料比較寄生電容，同時查看機械及蝕刻相容性。","textEn":"A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs. Corresponding operation: Compare parasitic capacitance for illustrative lower-k and higher-k spacers while checking mechanical and etch compatibility."},{"id":"sc-254-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：低 k 選材忽略結構或可靠度。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Low-k selection ignores structural or reliability costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「比較間隔層材料電性」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Compare spacer dielectric behavior\"?","options":["導體清除與介電層保護同時達成。","低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。","內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。"],"optionsEn":["Conductor clearance and dielectric protection are achieved together.","A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs.","The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：低介電常數選擇沒有忽略尺寸或可靠度代價。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: A lower-k choice does not ignore dimensional or reliability costs. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-253"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-255","order":21,"sequence":255,"title":"配置 FinFET 三維間隔層分支","titleEn":"Configure the FinFET spacer branch","objective":"三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","objectiveEn":"One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：讓間隔層包覆鰭與閘極交會的三維角落，檢查盲區。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Wrap spacers around three-dimensional fin-gate intersections and inspect hidden corners.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：二維截面漏掉三維交會盲區。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Two-dimensional section misses hidden three-dimensional intersections. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","checkEn":"One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-255-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。 對應操作：讓間隔層包覆鰭與閘極交會的三維角落，檢查盲區。","textEn":"One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity. Corresponding operation: Wrap spacers around three-dimensional fin-gate intersections and inspect hidden corners."},{"id":"sc-255-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：二維截面漏掉三維交會盲區。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Two-dimensional section misses hidden three-dimensional intersections."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「配置 FinFET 三維間隔層分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Configure the FinFET spacer branch\"?","options":["三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。","完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","端點判斷對應實際界面，而非僅某個時間戳。"],"optionsEn":["One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity.","Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","Endpoint judgment corresponds to the actual interface rather than a timestamp alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：三維角部完整性不能由單一平面截面代替。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: One planar section does not substitute for three-dimensional corner integrity. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-254"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-256","order":22,"sequence":256,"title":"核對奈米片犧牲層分支","titleEn":"Verify the nanosheet sacrificial-layer branch","objective":"犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。","objectiveEn":"Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在奈米片路線辨識 Si 與 SiGe 疊層，標示稍後需保留和移除者。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Identify silicon and silicon-germanium layers in the nanosheet route and label retained and sacrificial layers.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把犧牲 SiGe 層當保留通道。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Sacrificial SiGe mistaken for retained channels. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。","checkEn":"Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-256-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。 對應操作：在奈米片路線辨識 Si 與 SiGe 疊層，標示稍後需保留和移除者。","textEn":"Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel. Corresponding operation: Identify silicon and silicon-germanium layers in the nanosheet route and label retained and sacrificial layers."},{"id":"sc-256-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：把犧牲 SiGe 層當保留通道。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Sacrificial SiGe mistaken for retained channels."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「核對奈米片犧牲層分支」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify the nanosheet sacrificial-layer branch\"?","options":["犧牲閘極與最終金屬閘極明確區分。","不同材料造成的殘腳使用不同診斷，不以外形一概分類。","犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。"],"optionsEn":["Dummy gates and final metal gates are clearly distinguished.","Similar-looking feet are diagnosed by material rather than appearance alone.","Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：犧牲層與通道層角色清楚，非將所有層都當成通道。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Sacrificial and channel-layer roles are clear rather than treating every layer as a channel. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-255"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-257","order":23,"sequence":257,"title":"形成內間隔層凹槽概念","titleEn":"Form the inner-spacer recess concept","objective":"內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","objectiveEn":"Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在奈米片分支於源汲極切面側向回縮犧牲層，追蹤各層均勻性。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. In the nanosheet branch, recess sacrificial layers laterally from the source-drain cut face and track uniformity among layers.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：各層回縮不均或通道侵蝕。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Unequal recess among layers or channel erosion. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","checkEn":"Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-257-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。 對應操作：在奈米片分支於源汲極切面側向回縮犧牲層，追蹤各層均勻性。","textEn":"Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss. Corresponding operation: In the nanosheet branch, recess sacrificial layers laterally from the source-drain cut face and track uniformity among layers."},{"id":"sc-257-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：各層回縮不均或通道侵蝕。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Unequal recess among layers or channel erosion."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「形成內間隔層凹槽概念」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Form the inner-spacer recess concept\"?","options":["閘極輪廓以高度相關 CD 表示。","內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。","堆疊符合所選路線，未同時混用互斥材料安排。"],"optionsEn":["Gate profile is represented with height-dependent CD.","Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss.","The stack matches the selected route without combining incompatible alternatives."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：內間隔凹槽的深度按各層驗證，且通道未被過度損耗。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Recess depth is checked layer by layer without excessive channel loss. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-256"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-258","order":24,"sequence":258,"title":"填充奈米片內間隔層","titleEn":"Fill nanosheet inner spacers","objective":"內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","objectiveEn":"Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：在側向凹槽放入絕緣材料並移除外部多餘材料，查看凹槽殘留。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Fill lateral recesses with dielectric, remove external excess and inspect retained material inside the recesses.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：填充材料殘留堵塞保留通道。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Fill residue obstructs retained channels. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","checkEn":"Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-258-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。 對應操作：在側向凹槽放入絕緣材料並移除外部多餘材料，查看凹槽殘留。","textEn":"Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels. Corresponding operation: Fill lateral recesses with dielectric, remove external excess and inspect retained material inside the recesses."},{"id":"sc-258-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：填充材料殘留堵塞保留通道。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Fill residue obstructs retained channels."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「填充奈米片內間隔層」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Fill nanosheet inner spacers\"?","options":["內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。","頂蓋功能與閘極介電功能分開。","粗糙度估計包含取樣長度與去趨勢方法。"],"optionsEn":["Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels.","Gate-cap function is separated from gate-dielectric function.","Roughness estimates include sampling length and detrending method."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：內間隔層封住預定區域但未堵住保留通道。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Inner spacers occupy intended regions without obstructing retained channels. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-257"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-259","order":25,"sequence":259,"title":"驗證內外間隔層隔離","titleEn":"Verify inner and outer spacer isolation","objective":"內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。","objectiveEn":"The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：沿源汲極至未來閘極的可能路徑追蹤，檢查是否有未隔離缺口。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Trace potential paths from source-drain regions to the future gate and inspect unisolated gaps.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：內外間隔層之間存在未隔離缺口。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: An unisolated gap exists between inner and outer spacers. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。","checkEn":"The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-259-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。 對應操作：沿源汲極至未來閘極的可能路徑追蹤，檢查是否有未隔離缺口。","textEn":"The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained. Corresponding operation: Trace potential paths from source-drain regions to the future gate and inspect unisolated gaps."},{"id":"sc-259-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：內外間隔層之間存在未隔離缺口。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: An unisolated gap exists between inner and outer spacers."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「驗證內外間隔層隔離」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Verify inner and outer spacer isolation\"?","options":["閘極與主動區的交集形成正確通道位置。","幾何完整不被當作介電電性完好的保證。","內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。"],"optionsEn":["Gate-active intersections form the intended channel locations.","Geometric integrity is not treated as proof of intact dielectric behavior.","The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：內外間隔層的不同位置及隔離功能均被說明。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: The distinct locations and isolation functions of inner and outer spacers are explained. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-258"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-260","order":26,"sequence":260,"title":"交接閘極與間隔層幾何","titleEn":"Handoff gate and spacer geometry","objective":"完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","objectiveEn":"Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","instruction":"依示意模型，以自行準備或從參考來源取得的圖、量測資料或試算表進行：整合閘長、線緣、間隔寬度及介電證據，註明源汲極和替代閘極仍待後續完成。","instructionEn":"Use schematic models and diagrams, measurement data or worksheets you supply or obtain from referenced sources. Combine gate length, edge, spacer-width and dielectric evidence and note that source-drain and replacement-gate work follows later.","observation":"保存本步操作前後的對照證據。判讀重點：完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","observationEn":"Keep before-and-after evidence for this operation. Interpret it against this criterion: Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","failure":"若未符合判據，優先檢查：把模組幾何完成誤當電晶體功能完成。這是待驗證的原因；回到相同測點或剖面比對，不能僅據異常外觀定因。","failureEn":"If the criterion is not met, investigate: Module geometry completion mistaken for transistor functionality. This is a hypothesis; compare matching sites or cross-sections before assigning a cause.","check":"完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","checkEn":"Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-260-k1","title":"本步的可檢核證據","titleEn":"Evidence for this operation","text":"完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。 對應操作：整合閘長、線緣、間隔寬度及介電證據，註明源汲極和替代閘極仍待後續完成。","textEn":"Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor. Corresponding operation: Combine gate length, edge, spacer-width and dielectric evidence and note that source-drain and replacement-gate work follows later."},{"id":"sc-260-k2","title":"機制與診斷邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and diagnostic limits","text":"間隔層提供特定位置的電性隔離與幾何間距。奈米片內間隔層位於層間端部，不能用外側側壁間隔層的二維圖替代。 本步特別排查：把模組幾何完成誤當電晶體功能完成。","textEn":"Spacers provide electrical isolation and geometric separation at specific locations. Nanosheet inner spacers occupy interlayer ends and cannot be represented by a two-dimensional outer-spacer diagram. Specifically examine: Module geometry completion mistaken for transistor functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「交接閘極與間隔層幾何」這一步的完成？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports completion of \"Handoff gate and spacer geometry\"?","options":["殘留清除沒有掩蓋有效閘長或介電層改變。","完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。","線端失效未被中段正常 CD 掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Residue removal does not conceal changes in effective gate length or dielectric thickness.","Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor.","Normal mid-line CD does not hide line-end failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本步驗收的是：完成的是本模組幾何，不誤稱整個電晶體已可運作。 其他選項雖可能是有效工程檢查，但不能取代本步證據。","explanationEn":"This operation is accepted against: Completion refers to this module's geometry rather than a fully functioning transistor. The other options may be valid engineering checks but do not replace this evidence."},"sourceIds":["sc-imec-nanosheet","sc-lam-etch","sc-lam-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-259"],"prerequisiteScope":"learning-sequence","activityMode":"guided-worksheet-and-evidence-review","photoTopic":"silicon-wafer","sourceScope":"Principle-level references; exercises and qualitative checks are original educational subdivisions, not vendor recipes.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"sc-m11","title":"源汲極、摻雜與活化","titleEn":"Source/drain, doping and activation","description":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-261","title":"延伸接面剖面建模","titleEn":"Model extension-junction profiles","objective":"完成「延伸接面剖面建模」的證據判讀，辨識『比較淺接面濃度剖面與通道邊界』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate model extension-junction profiles by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare shallow dopant profiles with the channel boundary.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較淺接面濃度剖面與通道邊界。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare shallow dopant profiles with the channel boundary. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只看峰值會漏掉深部尾端。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: peak concentration alone hides deep tails. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只看峰值會漏掉深部尾端」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Peak concentration alone hides deep tails. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-261-k1","title":"延伸接面剖面建模的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of model extension-junction profiles","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較淺接面濃度剖面與通道邊界」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare shallow dopant profiles with the channel boundary. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-261-k2","title":"延伸接面剖面建模的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for model extension-junction profiles","text":"有效證據需支持「接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示」。但只看峰值會漏掉深部尾端；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified. However, peak concentration alone hides deep tails; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「延伸接面剖面建模」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for model extension-junction profiles?","options":["接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示","兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認","低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入"],"optionsEn":["Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified","Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified","Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較淺接面濃度剖面與通道邊界」，因此直接證據是「接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只看峰值會漏掉深部尾端。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare shallow dopant profiles with the channel boundary; the direct criterion is: Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Peak concentration alone hides deep tails."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":261,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-260"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-262","title":"離子種與極性配對","titleEn":"Match dopant species and polarity","objective":"完成「離子種與極性配對」的證據判讀，辨識『將施體與受體分別配置至示意 NMOS 與 PMOS』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate match dopant species and polarity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: assign donors and acceptors to model nmos and pmos regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將施體與受體分別配置至示意 NMOS 與 PMOS。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, assign donors and acceptors to model NMOS and PMOS regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：極性顛倒使接面結構錯置。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: reversed polarity creates the wrong junction structure. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「極性顛倒使接面結構錯置」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Reversed polarity creates the wrong junction structure. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-262-k1","title":"離子種與極性配對的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of match dopant species and polarity","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「將施體與受體分別配置至示意 NMOS 與 PMOS」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Assign donors and acceptors to model NMOS and PMOS regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-262-k2","title":"離子種與極性配對的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for match dopant species and polarity","text":"有效證據需支持「摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致」。但極性顛倒使接面結構錯置；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type. However, reversed polarity creates the wrong junction structure; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「離子種與極性配對」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for match dopant species and polarity?","options":["遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損","摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致","充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現"],"optionsEn":["Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage","Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type","Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將施體與受體分別配置至示意 NMOS 與 PMOS」，因此直接證據是「摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：極性顛倒使接面結構錯置。","explanationEn":"The task is to assign donors and acceptors to model NMOS and PMOS regions; the direct criterion is: Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Reversed polarity creates the wrong junction structure."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":262,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-261"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-263","title":"阻擋光罩覆蓋檢查","titleEn":"Inspect implant-block coverage","objective":"完成「阻擋光罩覆蓋檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『疊合佈植遮罩與有源區圖形』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect implant-block coverage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay the implant mask and active-area geometry.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，疊合佈植遮罩與有源區圖形。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay the implant mask and active-area geometry. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：非目標元件均落在阻擋區內。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: all non-target devices lie inside blocked regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：遮罩缺口造成錯區摻雜。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mask gaps cause unwanted doping. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「非目標元件均落在阻擋區內」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「遮罩缺口造成錯區摻雜」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mask gaps cause unwanted doping. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-263-k1","title":"阻擋光罩覆蓋檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect implant-block coverage","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「疊合佈植遮罩與有源區圖形」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Overlay the implant mask and active-area geometry. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-263-k2","title":"阻擋光罩覆蓋檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect implant-block coverage","text":"有效證據需支持「非目標元件均落在阻擋區內」。但遮罩缺口造成錯區摻雜；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions. However, mask gaps cause unwanted doping; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「阻擋光罩覆蓋檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect implant-block coverage?","options":["遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮","凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整","非目標元件均落在阻擋區內"],"optionsEn":["Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession","Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact","All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「疊合佈植遮罩與有源區圖形」，因此直接證據是「非目標元件均落在阻擋區內」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：遮罩缺口造成錯區摻雜。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay the implant mask and active-area geometry; the direct criterion is: All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mask gaps cause unwanted doping."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":263,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-262"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-264","title":"束流質量分析判讀","titleEn":"Interpret beam mass analysis","objective":"完成「束流質量分析判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『在模擬質譜中辨別目標離子與污染峰』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret beam mass analysis by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish target ions from contaminant peaks in a model spectrum.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在模擬質譜中辨別目標離子與污染峰。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish target ions from contaminant peaks in a model spectrum. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：峰重疊提示離子選擇不足。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: overlapping peaks indicate inadequate species selection. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「峰重疊提示離子選擇不足」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Overlapping peaks indicate inadequate species selection. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-264-k1","title":"束流質量分析判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret beam mass analysis","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「在模擬質譜中辨別目標離子與污染峰」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish target ions from contaminant peaks in a model spectrum. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-264-k2","title":"束流質量分析判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret beam mass analysis","text":"有效證據需支持「目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離」。但峰重疊提示離子選擇不足；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors. However, overlapping peaks indicate inadequate species selection; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「束流質量分析判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret beam mass analysis?","options":["目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離","非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容","外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據"],"optionsEn":["The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors","Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs","The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「在模擬質譜中辨別目標離子與污染峰」，因此直接證據是「目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：峰重疊提示離子選擇不足。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish target ions from contaminant peaks in a model spectrum; the direct criterion is: The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Overlapping peaks indicate inadequate species selection."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":264,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-263"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-265","title":"法拉第杯劑量積分","titleEn":"Integrate Faraday-cup dose","objective":"完成「法拉第杯劑量積分」的證據判讀，辨識『將校正後束流對曝光時間積分』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate integrate faraday-cup dose by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: integrate calibrated beam current over exposure time.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將校正後束流對曝光時間積分。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, integrate calibrated beam current over exposure time. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: integrated charge and scanned area are traceable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：漏算掃描空檔會偏估劑量。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring scan gaps biases dose estimates. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「漏算掃描空檔會偏估劑量」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring scan gaps biases dose estimates. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-265-k1","title":"法拉第杯劑量積分的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of integrate faraday-cup dose","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「將校正後束流對曝光時間積分」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Integrate calibrated beam current over exposure time. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-265-k2","title":"法拉第杯劑量積分的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for integrate faraday-cup dose","text":"有效證據需支持「積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯」。但漏算掃描空檔會偏估劑量；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable. However, ignoring scan gaps biases dose estimates; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「法拉第杯劑量積分」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for integrate faraday-cup dose?","options":["生長侷限於指定晶體開口","積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯","淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區"],"optionsEn":["Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings","Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable","The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將校正後束流對曝光時間積分」，因此直接證據是「積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：漏算掃描空檔會偏估劑量。","explanationEn":"The task is to integrate calibrated beam current over exposure time; the direct criterion is: Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring scan gaps biases dose estimates."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":265,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-264"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-266","title":"束流掃描均勻度","titleEn":"Evaluate beam-scan uniformity","objective":"完成「束流掃描均勻度」的證據判讀，辨識『重建晶圓不同位置的示意劑量圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate beam-scan uniformity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: reconstruct the model dose map across the wafer.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，重建晶圓不同位置的示意劑量圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, reconstruct the model dose map across the wafer. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：條帶紋提示掃描同步異常。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: stripes suggest scan-synchronization errors. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「條帶紋提示掃描同步異常」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Stripes suggest scan-synchronization errors. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-266-k1","title":"束流掃描均勻度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate beam-scan uniformity","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「重建晶圓不同位置的示意劑量圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Reconstruct the model dose map across the wafer. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-266-k2","title":"束流掃描均勻度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate beam-scan uniformity","text":"有效證據需支持「中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍」。但條帶紋提示掃描同步異常；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits. However, stripes suggest scan-synchronization errors; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「束流掃描均勻度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate beam-scan uniformity?","options":["抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道","合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支","中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍"],"optionsEn":["Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel","Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch","Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「重建晶圓不同位置的示意劑量圖」，因此直接證據是「中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：條帶紋提示掃描同步異常。","explanationEn":"The task is to reconstruct the model dose map across the wafer; the direct criterion is: Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Stripes suggest scan-synchronization errors."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":266,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-265"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-267","title":"傾角抑制通道效應","titleEn":"Assess tilt and channeling","objective":"完成「傾角抑制通道效應」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同晶向入射的深度分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess tilt and channeling by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare penetration profiles for different crystal orientations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同晶向入射的深度分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare penetration profiles for different crystal orientations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：深尾端變化與入射方向相關。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略晶向會誤認深尾為擴散。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring orientation can mislabel channeling as diffusion. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「深尾端變化與入射方向相關」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略晶向會誤認深尾為擴散」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring orientation can mislabel channeling as diffusion. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-267-k1","title":"傾角抑制通道效應的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess tilt and channeling","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較不同晶向入射的深度分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare penetration profiles for different crystal orientations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-267-k2","title":"傾角抑制通道效應的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess tilt and channeling","text":"有效證據需支持「深尾端變化與入射方向相關」。但忽略晶向會誤認深尾為擴散；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction. However, ignoring orientation can mislabel channeling as diffusion; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「傾角抑制通道效應」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess tilt and channeling?","options":["深尾端變化與入射方向相關","低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入","應變方向與元件極性需求相容"],"optionsEn":["Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction","Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered","Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同晶向入射的深度分佈」，因此直接證據是「深尾端變化與入射方向相關」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略晶向會誤認深尾為擴散。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare penetration profiles for different crystal orientations; the direct criterion is: Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring orientation can mislabel channeling as diffusion."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":267,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-266"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-268","title":"遮蔽陰影與旋轉","titleEn":"Inspect implant shadowing","objective":"完成「遮蔽陰影與旋轉」的證據判讀，辨識『在閘極立體模型追蹤離子可達區』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect implant shadowing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace ion access around model gate topography.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在閘極立體模型追蹤離子可達區。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace ion access around model gate topography. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: shadowing differences between both junctions are identified. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一方位可能造成非對稱摻雜。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one azimuth can produce asymmetric doping. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一方位可能造成非對稱摻雜」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One azimuth can produce asymmetric doping. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-268-k1","title":"遮蔽陰影與旋轉的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect implant shadowing","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「在閘極立體模型追蹤離子可達區」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Trace ion access around model gate topography. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-268-k2","title":"遮蔽陰影與旋轉的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect implant shadowing","text":"有效證據需支持「兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認」。但單一方位可能造成非對稱摻雜；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified. However, one azimuth can produce asymmetric doping; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「遮蔽陰影與旋轉」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect implant shadowing?","options":["兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持","兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認","遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損"],"optionsEn":["Both distributions have independent measurement support","Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified","Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「在閘極立體模型追蹤離子可達區」，因此直接證據是「兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一方位可能造成非對稱摻雜。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace ion access around model gate topography; the direct criterion is: Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One azimuth can produce asymmetric doping."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":268,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-267"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-269","title":"佈植充電監看","titleEn":"Monitor implant charging","objective":"完成「佈植充電監看」的證據判讀，辨識『比較充電監測結構與束流紀錄』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate monitor implant charging by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare charging monitors with beam records.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較充電監測結構與束流紀錄。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare charging monitors with beam records. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：劑量正常仍可能有閘氧損傷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: correct dose does not exclude gate-oxide damage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「劑量正常仍可能有閘氧損傷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Correct dose does not exclude gate-oxide damage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-269-k1","title":"佈植充電監看的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of monitor implant charging","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較充電監測結構與束流紀錄」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare charging monitors with beam records. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-269-k2","title":"佈植充電監看的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for monitor implant charging","text":"有效證據需支持「充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現」。但劑量正常仍可能有閘氧損傷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals. However, correct dose does not exclude gate-oxide damage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「佈植充電監看」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for monitor implant charging?","options":["凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整","活化改善未超出接面幾何限制","充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現"],"optionsEn":["Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact","Activation improves without excessive junction broadening","Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較充電監測結構與束流紀錄」，因此直接證據是「充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：劑量正常仍可能有閘氧損傷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare charging monitors with beam records; the direct criterion is: Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Correct dose does not exclude gate-oxide damage."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":269,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-268"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-270","title":"光阻熱負載判讀","titleEn":"Assess resist thermal loading","objective":"完成「光阻熱負載判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比對佈植前後光阻輪廓影像』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess resist thermal loading by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare resist profiles before and after model implantation.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比對佈植前後光阻輪廓影像。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare resist profiles before and after model implantation. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: mask edges show no collapse or marked recession. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：熱退縮會改變實際阻擋範圍。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: thermal recession changes the effective blocked region. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「熱退縮會改變實際阻擋範圍」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Thermal recession changes the effective blocked region. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-270-k1","title":"光阻熱負載判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess resist thermal loading","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比對佈植前後光阻輪廓影像」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare resist profiles before and after model implantation. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-270-k2","title":"光阻熱負載判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess resist thermal loading","text":"有效證據需支持「遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮」。但熱退縮會改變實際阻擋範圍；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession. However, thermal recession changes the effective blocked region; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「光阻熱負載判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess resist thermal loading?","options":["遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮","外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據","空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查"],"optionsEn":["Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession","The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence","Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比對佈植前後光阻輪廓影像」，因此直接證據是「遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：熱退縮會改變實際阻擋範圍。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare resist profiles before and after model implantation; the direct criterion is: Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Thermal recession changes the effective blocked region."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":270,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-269"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-271","title":"預非晶化分支評估","titleEn":"Evaluate pre-amorphization","objective":"完成「預非晶化分支評估」的證據判讀，辨識『標示示意非晶層與預定接面的位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate pre-amorphization by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: locate the amorphous layer relative to the intended junction.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，標示示意非晶層與預定接面的位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, locate the amorphous layer relative to the intended junction. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過深損傷可能增加接面附近缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess depth can add defects near the junction. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過深損傷可能增加接面附近缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess depth can add defects near the junction. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-271-k1","title":"預非晶化分支評估的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate pre-amorphization","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「標示示意非晶層與預定接面的位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Locate the amorphous layer relative to the intended junction. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-271-k2","title":"預非晶化分支評估的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate pre-amorphization","text":"有效證據需支持「非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容」。但過深損傷可能增加接面附近缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs. However, excess depth can add defects near the junction; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「預非晶化分支評估」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate pre-amorphization?","options":["活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標","非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容","生長侷限於指定晶體開口"],"optionsEn":["Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics","Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs","Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「標示示意非晶層與預定接面的位置」，因此直接證據是「非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過深損傷可能增加接面附近缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to locate the amorphous layer relative to the intended junction; the direct criterion is: Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess depth can add defects near the junction."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":271,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-270"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-272","title":"延伸接面低能量模擬","titleEn":"Simulate low-energy extensions","objective":"完成「延伸接面低能量模擬」的證據判讀，辨識『比較投影射程與表面損失的相對影響』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate simulate low-energy extensions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare projected range with near-surface dopant loss.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較投影射程與表面損失的相對影響。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare projected range with near-surface dopant loss. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the shallow profile retains a discernible doped region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面損失可使名義劑量高估有效量。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: surface loss can make nominal dose overstate retained dose. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面損失可使名義劑量高估有效量」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Surface loss can make nominal dose overstate retained dose. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-272-k1","title":"延伸接面低能量模擬的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of simulate low-energy extensions","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較投影射程與表面損失的相對影響」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare projected range with near-surface dopant loss. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-272-k2","title":"延伸接面低能量模擬的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for simulate low-energy extensions","text":"有效證據需支持「淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區」。但表面損失可使名義劑量高估有效量；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region. However, surface loss can make nominal dose overstate retained dose; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「延伸接面低能量模擬」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for simulate low-energy extensions?","options":["合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支","保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀","淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區"],"optionsEn":["Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch","Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished","The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較投影射程與表面損失的相對影響」，因此直接證據是「淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面損失可使名義劑量高估有效量。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare projected range with near-surface dopant loss; the direct criterion is: The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Surface loss can make nominal dose overstate retained dose."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":272,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-271"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-273","title":"袋狀摻雜分支定位","titleEn":"Locate pocket-implant branches","objective":"完成「袋狀摻雜分支定位」的證據判讀，辨識『疊合袋狀摻雜與短通道電位模型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate locate pocket-implant branches by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay pocket doping and short-channel potential models.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，疊合袋狀摻雜與短通道電位模型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay pocket doping and short-channel potential models. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過度重疊可能犧牲遷移率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess overlap may reduce mobility. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過度重疊可能犧牲遷移率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess overlap may reduce mobility. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-273-k1","title":"袋狀摻雜分支定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of locate pocket-implant branches","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「疊合袋狀摻雜與短通道電位模型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Overlay pocket doping and short-channel potential models. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-273-k2","title":"袋狀摻雜分支定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for locate pocket-implant branches","text":"有效證據需支持「抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道」。但過度重疊可能犧牲遷移率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel. However, excess overlap may reduce mobility; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「袋狀摻雜分支定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for locate pocket-implant branches?","options":["抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道","應變方向與元件極性需求相容","導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準"],"optionsEn":["Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel","Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective","Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「疊合袋狀摻雜與短通道電位模型」，因此直接證據是「抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過度重疊可能犧牲遷移率。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay pocket doping and short-channel potential models; the direct criterion is: Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess overlap may reduce mobility."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":273,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-272"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-274","title":"源汲極重摻雜分佈","titleEn":"Inspect heavily doped junctions","objective":"完成「源汲極重摻雜分佈」的證據判讀，辨識『分開比較表面濃度與接面梯度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect heavily doped junctions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare surface concentration and junction gradient separately.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分開比較表面濃度與接面梯度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare surface concentration and junction gradient separately. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：提高濃度不保證活化同步提升。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: higher concentration does not guarantee higher activation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「提高濃度不保證活化同步提升」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Higher concentration does not guarantee higher activation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-274-k1","title":"源汲極重摻雜分佈的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect heavily doped junctions","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「分開比較表面濃度與接面梯度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare surface concentration and junction gradient separately. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-274-k2","title":"源汲極重摻雜分佈的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect heavily doped junctions","text":"有效證據需支持「低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入」。但提高濃度不保證活化同步提升；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered. However, higher concentration does not guarantee higher activation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「源汲極重摻雜分佈」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect heavily doped junctions?","options":["接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示","低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入","兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持"],"optionsEn":["Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified","Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered","Both distributions have independent measurement support"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「分開比較表面濃度與接面梯度」，因此直接證據是「低電阻需求與接面漏電限制同時列入」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：提高濃度不保證活化同步提升。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare surface concentration and junction gradient separately; the direct criterion is: Resistance and junction-leakage constraints are both considered. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Higher concentration does not guarantee higher activation."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":274,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-273"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-275","title":"植入後光阻去除檢查","titleEn":"Inspect post-implant resist removal","objective":"完成「植入後光阻去除檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『判讀硬化表層與殘留碳的分析圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect post-implant resist removal by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: interpret hardened-skin and residual-carbon evidence.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，判讀硬化表層與殘留碳的分析圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, interpret hardened-skin and residual-carbon evidence. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: mask residue is removed without active-surface damage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：強行去除可能引入表面粗化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: overaggressive removal can roughen the surface. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「強行去除可能引入表面粗化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Overaggressive removal can roughen the surface. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-275-k1","title":"植入後光阻去除檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect post-implant resist removal","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「判讀硬化表層與殘留碳的分析圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Interpret hardened-skin and residual-carbon evidence. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-275-k2","title":"植入後光阻去除檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect post-implant resist removal","text":"有效證據需支持「遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損」。但強行去除可能引入表面粗化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage. However, overaggressive removal can roughen the surface; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「植入後光阻去除檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect post-implant resist removal?","options":["活化改善未超出接面幾何限制","摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致","遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損"],"optionsEn":["Activation improves without excessive junction broadening","Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type","Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「判讀硬化表層與殘留碳的分析圖」，因此直接證據是「遮罩殘留消失且有源表面未受損」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：強行去除可能引入表面粗化。","explanationEn":"The task is to interpret hardened-skin and residual-carbon evidence; the direct criterion is: Mask residue is removed without active-surface damage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Overaggressive removal can roughen the surface."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":275,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-274"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-276","title":"源汲極凹槽幾何","titleEn":"Measure source/drain recess geometry","objective":"完成「源汲極凹槽幾何」的證據判讀，辨識『在截面圖量取凹槽深度與側壁形狀』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure source/drain recess geometry by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure recess depth and sidewalls in cross sections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在截面圖量取凹槽深度與側壁形狀。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure recess depth and sidewalls in cross sections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：底部尖角可能集中應力或缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: sharp bottom corners may concentrate stress or defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「底部尖角可能集中應力或缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Sharp bottom corners may concentrate stress or defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-276-k1","title":"源汲極凹槽幾何的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure source/drain recess geometry","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「在截面圖量取凹槽深度與側壁形狀」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Measure recess depth and sidewalls in cross sections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-276-k2","title":"源汲極凹槽幾何的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure source/drain recess geometry","text":"有效證據需支持「凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整」。但底部尖角可能集中應力或缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact. However, sharp bottom corners may concentrate stress or defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「源汲極凹槽幾何」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure source/drain recess geometry?","options":["凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整","空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查","非目標元件均落在阻擋區內"],"optionsEn":["Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact","Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field","All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「在截面圖量取凹槽深度與側壁形狀」，因此直接證據是「凹槽接近目標形狀且間隔層完整」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：底部尖角可能集中應力或缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure recess depth and sidewalls in cross sections; the direct criterion is: Recess shape meets the target while spacers remain intact. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Sharp bottom corners may concentrate stress or defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":276,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-275"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-277","title":"外延前界面清潔判讀","titleEn":"Assess the pre-epitaxy interface","objective":"完成「外延前界面清潔判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比較表面氧化與碳污染分析結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess the pre-epitaxy interface by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare surface oxide and carbon-contamination results.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較表面氧化與碳污染分析結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare surface oxide and carbon-contamination results. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：殘氧會破壞外延起始一致性。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: residual oxygen disrupts consistent epitaxial nucleation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「殘氧會破壞外延起始一致性」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Residual oxygen disrupts consistent epitaxial nucleation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-277-k1","title":"外延前界面清潔判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess the pre-epitaxy interface","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較表面氧化與碳污染分析結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare surface oxide and carbon-contamination results. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-277-k2","title":"外延前界面清潔判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess the pre-epitaxy interface","text":"有效證據需支持「外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據」。但殘氧會破壞外延起始一致性；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence. However, residual oxygen disrupts consistent epitaxial nucleation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「外延前界面清潔判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess the pre-epitaxy interface?","options":["目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離","外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據","活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標"],"optionsEn":["The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors","The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence","Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較表面氧化與碳污染分析結果」，因此直接證據是「外延界面具有可追溯的潔淨證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：殘氧會破壞外延起始一致性。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare surface oxide and carbon-contamination results; the direct criterion is: The epitaxial interface has traceable cleanliness evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Residual oxygen disrupts consistent epitaxial nucleation."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":277,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-276"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-278","title":"選擇性外延成核","titleEn":"Inspect selective epitaxial nucleation","objective":"完成「選擇性外延成核」的證據判讀，辨識『區分矽區成長與介電層寄生成核』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect selective epitaxial nucleation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish growth on silicon from parasitic dielectric nucleation.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分矽區成長與介電層寄生成核。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish growth on silicon from parasitic dielectric nucleation. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：生長侷限於指定晶體開口。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: growth is confined to intended crystalline openings. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：介電層上顆粒提示選擇性失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: particles on dielectric indicate lost selectivity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「生長侷限於指定晶體開口」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「介電層上顆粒提示選擇性失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Particles on dielectric indicate lost selectivity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-278-k1","title":"選擇性外延成核的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect selective epitaxial nucleation","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「區分矽區成長與介電層寄生成核」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish growth on silicon from parasitic dielectric nucleation. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-278-k2","title":"選擇性外延成核的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect selective epitaxial nucleation","text":"有效證據需支持「生長侷限於指定晶體開口」。但介電層上顆粒提示選擇性失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings. However, particles on dielectric indicate lost selectivity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「選擇性外延成核」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect selective epitaxial nucleation?","options":["保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀","積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯","生長侷限於指定晶體開口"],"optionsEn":["Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished","Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable","Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分矽區成長與介電層寄生成核」，因此直接證據是「生長侷限於指定晶體開口」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：介電層上顆粒提示選擇性失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish growth on silicon from parasitic dielectric nucleation; the direct criterion is: Growth is confined to intended crystalline openings. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Particles on dielectric indicate lost selectivity."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":278,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-277"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-279","title":"外延晶面與合併","titleEn":"Inspect epitaxial facets and merging","objective":"完成「外延晶面與合併」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤相鄰源汲極外延體的晶面輪廓』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect epitaxial facets and merging by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace facets of neighboring source/drain epitaxial regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤相鄰源汲極外延體的晶面輪廓。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace facets of neighboring source/drain epitaxial regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：非預期合併可能短接獨立節點。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unintended merging can short independent nodes. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「非預期合併可能短接獨立節點」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unintended merging can short independent nodes. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-279-k1","title":"外延晶面與合併的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect epitaxial facets and merging","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「追蹤相鄰源汲極外延體的晶面輪廓」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Trace facets of neighboring source/drain epitaxial regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-279-k2","title":"外延晶面與合併的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect epitaxial facets and merging","text":"有效證據需支持「合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支」。但非預期合併可能短接獨立節點；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch. However, unintended merging can short independent nodes; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「外延晶面與合併」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect epitaxial facets and merging?","options":["合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支","導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準","中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍"],"optionsEn":["Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch","Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria","Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤相鄰源汲極外延體的晶面輪廓」，因此直接證據是「合併或隔離狀態符合版圖分支」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：非預期合併可能短接獨立節點。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace facets of neighboring source/drain epitaxial regions; the direct criterion is: Merged or isolated geometry matches the layout branch. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unintended merging can short independent nodes."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":279,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-278"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-280","title":"應變源材料映射","titleEn":"Map strain-source materials","objective":"完成「應變源材料映射」的證據判讀，辨識『關聯組成圖與通道應變量測』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map strain-source materials by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate composition maps to channel-strain measurements.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，關聯組成圖與通道應變量測。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate composition maps to channel-strain measurements. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：應變方向與元件極性需求相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: strain direction matches the device-polarity objective. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：組成均勻不代表應變未鬆弛。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: uniform composition does not prove unrelaxed strain. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「應變方向與元件極性需求相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「組成均勻不代表應變未鬆弛」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Uniform composition does not prove unrelaxed strain. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-280-k1","title":"應變源材料映射的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map strain-source materials","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「關聯組成圖與通道應變量測」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Relate composition maps to channel-strain measurements. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-280-k2","title":"應變源材料映射的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map strain-source materials","text":"有效證據需支持「應變方向與元件極性需求相容」。但組成均勻不代表應變未鬆弛；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective. However, uniform composition does not prove unrelaxed strain; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「應變源材料映射」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map strain-source materials?","options":["深尾端變化與入射方向相關","應變方向與元件極性需求相容","接面深度與橫向侵入均有標示"],"optionsEn":["Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction","Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective","Both junction depth and lateral encroachment are identified"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「關聯組成圖與通道應變量測」，因此直接證據是「應變方向與元件極性需求相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：組成均勻不代表應變未鬆弛。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate composition maps to channel-strain measurements; the direct criterion is: Strain direction matches the device-polarity objective. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Uniform composition does not prove unrelaxed strain."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":280,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-279"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-281","title":"原位摻雜外延檢查","titleEn":"Assess in-situ doped epitaxy","objective":"完成「原位摻雜外延檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『分開檢視外延厚度與摻雜濃度圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess in-situ doped epitaxy by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect epitaxial thickness and dopant maps separately.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分開檢視外延厚度與摻雜濃度圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect epitaxial thickness and dopant maps separately. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both distributions have independent measurement support. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：厚度穩定仍可能有摻雜漂移。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: stable thickness can coexist with dopant drift. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「厚度穩定仍可能有摻雜漂移」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both distributions have independent measurement support. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Stable thickness can coexist with dopant drift. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-281-k1","title":"原位摻雜外延檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess in-situ doped epitaxy","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「分開檢視外延厚度與摻雜濃度圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Inspect epitaxial thickness and dopant maps separately. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-281-k2","title":"原位摻雜外延檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess in-situ doped epitaxy","text":"有效證據需支持「兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持」。但厚度穩定仍可能有摻雜漂移；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both distributions have independent measurement support. However, stable thickness can coexist with dopant drift; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「原位摻雜外延檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess in-situ doped epitaxy?","options":["摻雜極性與源汲極導電型一致","兩側源汲極的遮蔽差異已辨認","兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持"],"optionsEn":["Dopant polarity matches the intended source/drain type","Shadowing differences between both junctions are identified","Both distributions have independent measurement support"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「分開檢視外延厚度與摻雜濃度圖」，因此直接證據是「兩種分佈均有獨立量測支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：厚度穩定仍可能有摻雜漂移。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect epitaxial thickness and dopant maps separately; the direct criterion is: Both distributions have independent measurement support. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Stable thickness can coexist with dopant drift."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":281,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-280"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-282","title":"活化退火熱預算","titleEn":"Evaluate activation thermal budget","objective":"完成「活化退火熱預算」的證據判讀，辨識『比較示意退火後活化率與接面展寬』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate activation thermal budget by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare activation fraction and junction broadening after model anneals.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較示意退火後活化率與接面展寬。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare activation fraction and junction broadening after model anneals. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：活化改善未超出接面幾何限制。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: activation improves without excessive junction broadening. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：僅追求活化會忽略擴散代價。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: optimizing activation alone ignores diffusion cost. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「活化改善未超出接面幾何限制」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「僅追求活化會忽略擴散代價」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Activation improves without excessive junction broadening. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Optimizing activation alone ignores diffusion cost. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-282-k1","title":"活化退火熱預算的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate activation thermal budget","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比較示意退火後活化率與接面展寬」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare activation fraction and junction broadening after model anneals. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-282-k2","title":"活化退火熱預算的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate activation thermal budget","text":"有效證據需支持「活化改善未超出接面幾何限制」。但僅追求活化會忽略擴散代價；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Activation improves without excessive junction broadening. However, optimizing activation alone ignores diffusion cost; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「活化退火熱預算」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate activation thermal budget?","options":["活化改善未超出接面幾何限制","非目標元件均落在阻擋區內","充電事件與介電層損傷訊號未共現"],"optionsEn":["Activation improves without excessive junction broadening","All non-target devices lie inside blocked regions","Charging events do not coincide with dielectric-damage signals"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較示意退火後活化率與接面展寬」，因此直接證據是「活化改善未超出接面幾何限制」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：僅追求活化會忽略擴散代價。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare activation fraction and junction broadening after model anneals; the direct criterion is: Activation improves without excessive junction broadening. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Optimizing activation alone ignores diffusion cost."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":282,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-281"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-283","title":"快速退火溫度均勻度","titleEn":"Assess rapid-anneal temperature uniformity","objective":"完成「快速退火溫度均勻度」的證據判讀，辨識『對照測溫訊號與晶圓電阻圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess rapid-anneal temperature uniformity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare pyrometry traces and wafer resistance maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照測溫訊號與晶圓電阻圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare pyrometry traces and wafer resistance maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：放射率誤差可冒充真實溫差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: emissivity error can mimic temperature differences. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「放射率誤差可冒充真實溫差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Emissivity error can mimic temperature differences. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-283-k1","title":"快速退火溫度均勻度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess rapid-anneal temperature uniformity","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「對照測溫訊號與晶圓電阻圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare pyrometry traces and wafer resistance maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-283-k2","title":"快速退火溫度均勻度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess rapid-anneal temperature uniformity","text":"有效證據需支持「空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查」。但放射率誤差可冒充真實溫差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field. However, emissivity error can mimic temperature differences; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「快速退火溫度均勻度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess rapid-anneal temperature uniformity?","options":["遮罩邊緣未塌陷或產生顯著退縮","空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查","目標質荷比峰與鄰峰可分離"],"optionsEn":["Mask edges show no collapse or marked recession","Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field","The target mass-to-charge peak is resolved from neighbors"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照測溫訊號與晶圓電阻圖」，因此直接證據是「空間電性變化可與熱場交叉檢查」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：放射率誤差可冒充真實溫差。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare pyrometry traces and wafer resistance maps; the direct criterion is: Spatial electrical variation can be cross-checked against the thermal field. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Emissivity error can mimic temperature differences."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":283,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-282"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-284","title":"毫秒退火分支比較","titleEn":"Compare millisecond-anneal branches","objective":"完成「毫秒退火分支比較」的證據判讀，辨識『對照短熱脈衝與較長熱歷程模型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate compare millisecond-anneal branches by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare short thermal pulses with longer thermal histories.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照短熱脈衝與較長熱歷程模型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare short thermal pulses with longer thermal histories. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：短脈衝不代表所有缺陷皆已修復。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a short pulse does not prove complete defect recovery. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「短脈衝不代表所有缺陷皆已修復」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A short pulse does not prove complete defect recovery. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-284-k1","title":"毫秒退火分支比較的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of compare millisecond-anneal branches","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「對照短熱脈衝與較長熱歷程模型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare short thermal pulses with longer thermal histories. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-284-k2","title":"毫秒退火分支比較的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for compare millisecond-anneal branches","text":"有效證據需支持「活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標」。但短脈衝不代表所有缺陷皆已修復；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics. However, a short pulse does not prove complete defect recovery; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「毫秒退火分支比較」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for compare millisecond-anneal branches?","options":["積分電荷與掃描面積可追溯","非晶化範圍與後續再結晶需求相容","活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標"],"optionsEn":["Integrated charge and scanned area are traceable","Amorphized depth is compatible with recrystallization needs","Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照短熱脈衝與較長熱歷程模型」，因此直接證據是「活化與損傷修復均有驗證指標」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：短脈衝不代表所有缺陷皆已修復。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare short thermal pulses with longer thermal histories; the direct criterion is: Both activation and damage recovery have validation metrics. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A short pulse does not prove complete defect recovery."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":284,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-283"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-285","title":"SIMS 與片電阻交叉驗證","titleEn":"Cross-check SIMS and sheet resistance","objective":"完成「SIMS 與片電阻交叉驗證」的證據判讀，辨識『比對化學摻雜剖面與電性導通量測』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate cross-check sims and sheet resistance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare chemical dopant profiles with electrical conduction.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比對化學摻雜剖面與電性導通量測。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare chemical dopant profiles with electrical conduction. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把化學濃度當活化濃度會誤判。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: equating chemical and active concentration causes misinterpretation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把化學濃度當活化濃度會誤判」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Equating chemical and active concentration causes misinterpretation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-285-k1","title":"SIMS 與片電阻交叉驗證的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of cross-check sims and sheet resistance","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「比對化學摻雜剖面與電性導通量測」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Compare chemical dopant profiles with electrical conduction. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-285-k2","title":"SIMS 與片電阻交叉驗證的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for cross-check sims and sheet resistance","text":"有效證據需支持「保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀」。但把化學濃度當活化濃度會誤判；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished. However, equating chemical and active concentration causes misinterpretation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「SIMS 與片電阻交叉驗證」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for cross-check sims and sheet resistance?","options":["保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀","中心與邊緣分佈皆在題定範圍","淺層分佈仍保留可辨認的有效摻雜區"],"optionsEn":["Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished","Center and edge distributions meet the exercise limits","The shallow profile retains a discernible doped region"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比對化學摻雜剖面與電性導通量測」，因此直接證據是「保留摻雜量與有效活化量分別判讀」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把化學濃度當活化濃度會誤判。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare chemical dopant profiles with electrical conduction; the direct criterion is: Retained dopant and electrically active dopant are distinguished. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Equating chemical and active concentration causes misinterpretation."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":285,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-284"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-286","title":"接面漏電與活化放行","titleEn":"Release junctions using leakage and activation","objective":"完成「接面漏電與活化放行」的證據判讀，辨識『聯合判讀接面漏電、片電阻與缺陷證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release junctions using leakage and activation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: review leakage, sheet resistance and defect evidence together.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，聯合判讀接面漏電、片電阻與缺陷證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, review leakage, sheet resistance and defect evidence together. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：低片電阻仍可能掩蓋接面缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: low sheet resistance can conceal junction defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「低片電阻仍可能掩蓋接面缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Low sheet resistance can conceal junction defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-286-k1","title":"接面漏電與活化放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release junctions using leakage and activation","text":"佈植劑量、深度分佈、晶格損傷與電性活化是不同變量；外延與佈植屬可替代或組合的整合分支。 本題具體操作為「聯合判讀接面漏電、片電阻與缺陷證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Implanted dose, depth distribution, lattice damage and electrical activation are different variables; epitaxy and implantation are alternative or combined integration branches. Here the concrete task is: Review leakage, sheet resistance and defect evidence together. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-286-k2","title":"接面漏電與活化放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release junctions using leakage and activation","text":"有效證據需支持「導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準」。但低片電阻仍可能掩蓋接面缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria. However, low sheet resistance can conceal junction defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接面漏電與活化放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release junctions using leakage and activation?","options":["抑制穿通區未不當侵入導通通道","導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準","深尾端變化與入射方向相關"],"optionsEn":["Punch-through control does not excessively encroach on the channel","Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria","Deep-tail changes correlate with incidence direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「聯合判讀接面漏電、片電阻與缺陷證據」，因此直接證據是「導通改善與漏電風險同時符合題定標準」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：低片電阻仍可能掩蓋接面缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to review leakage, sheet resistance and defect evidence together; the direct criterion is: Conduction improvement and leakage risk meet the stated criteria. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Low sheet resistance can conceal junction defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-modify","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":286,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-285"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafer-foundry","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察無塵室設備與搬運環境；此廠房照片不是任何指定節點或本步製程的實拍證據。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe cleanroom equipment and handling context; this facility photograph does not document a specific node or this process step.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":11},{"id":"sc-m12","title":"矽化物與接觸整合","titleEn":"Silicide and contact integration","description":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-287","title":"矽化物界面氧化檢查","titleEn":"Inspect oxide at silicide interfaces","objective":"完成「矽化物界面氧化檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『辨認接觸區天然氧化層的分析訊號』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect oxide at silicide interfaces by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: identify native-oxide signatures in contact regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，辨認接觸區天然氧化層的分析訊號。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, identify native-oxide signatures in contact regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: interface condition is documented before metal contact. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：殘氧可能造成不連續反應。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: residual oxide can cause discontinuous reaction. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「殘氧可能造成不連續反應」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Interface condition is documented before metal contact. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Residual oxide can cause discontinuous reaction. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-287-k1","title":"矽化物界面氧化檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect oxide at silicide interfaces","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「辨認接觸區天然氧化層的分析訊號」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Identify native-oxide signatures in contact regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-287-k2","title":"矽化物界面氧化檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect oxide at silicide interfaces","text":"有效證據需支持「金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據」。但殘氧可能造成不連續反應；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Interface condition is documented before metal contact. However, residual oxide can cause discontinuous reaction; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「矽化物界面氧化檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect oxide at silicide interfaces?","options":["導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞","停止層清除且落點未過度受損","金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據"],"optionsEn":["Agglomeration has not broken film continuity","The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage","Interface condition is documented before metal contact"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「辨認接觸區天然氧化層的分析訊號」，因此直接證據是「金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：殘氧可能造成不連續反應。","explanationEn":"The task is to identify native-oxide signatures in contact regions; the direct criterion is: Interface condition is documented before metal contact. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Residual oxide can cause discontinuous reaction."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":287,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-286"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-288","title":"矽消耗厚度預算","titleEn":"Budget silicon consumption","objective":"完成「矽消耗厚度預算」的證據判讀，辨識『把矽化物形成所需矽量投影至薄源汲極』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate budget silicon consumption by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: project silicide silicon consumption into a thin junction.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把矽化物形成所需矽量投影至薄源汲極。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, project silicide silicon consumption into a thin junction. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: remaining silicon preserves junction integrity. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略消耗量可能使接觸穿入接面。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignored consumption can drive contact into a junction. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略消耗量可能使接觸穿入接面」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignored consumption can drive contact into a junction. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-288-k1","title":"矽消耗厚度預算的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of budget silicon consumption","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「把矽化物形成所需矽量投影至薄源汲極」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Project silicide silicon consumption into a thin junction. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-288-k2","title":"矽消耗厚度預算的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for budget silicon consumption","text":"有效證據需支持「剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性」。但忽略消耗量可能使接觸穿入接面；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity. However, ignored consumption can drive contact into a junction; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「矽消耗厚度預算」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for budget silicon consumption?","options":["剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性","矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離","孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整"],"optionsEn":["Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity","The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing","Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把矽化物形成所需矽量投影至薄源汲極」，因此直接證據是「剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略消耗量可能使接觸穿入接面。","explanationEn":"The task is to project silicide silicon consumption into a thin junction; the direct criterion is: Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignored consumption can drive contact into a junction."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":288,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-287"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-289","title":"金屬前驅薄膜連續性","titleEn":"Inspect precursor-metal continuity","objective":"完成「金屬前驅薄膜連續性」的證據判讀，辨識『檢視反應前金屬覆蓋的截面與表面圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect precursor-metal continuity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect pre-reaction metal coverage in sections and maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢視反應前金屬覆蓋的截面與表面圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect pre-reaction metal coverage in sections and maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：孤島成膜會形成不均勻矽化物。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: island growth produces nonuniform silicide. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「孤島成膜會形成不均勻矽化物」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Island growth produces nonuniform silicide. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-289-k1","title":"金屬前驅薄膜連續性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect precursor-metal continuity","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「檢視反應前金屬覆蓋的截面與表面圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Inspect pre-reaction metal coverage in sections and maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-289-k2","title":"金屬前驅薄膜連續性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect precursor-metal continuity","text":"有效證據需支持「目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯」。但孤島成膜會形成不均勻矽化物；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation. However, island growth produces nonuniform silicide; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「金屬前驅薄膜連續性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect precursor-metal continuity?","options":["等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化","目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯","粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷"],"optionsEn":["Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution","Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation","Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢視反應前金屬覆蓋的截面與表面圖」，因此直接證據是「目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：孤島成膜會形成不均勻矽化物。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect pre-reaction metal coverage in sections and maps; the direct criterion is: Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Island growth produces nonuniform silicide."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":289,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-288"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-290","title":"自對準反應區辨認","titleEn":"Identify self-aligned reaction regions","objective":"完成「自對準反應區辨認」的證據判讀，辨識『標示金屬在矽與介電層上的不同去向』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify self-aligned reaction regions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map metal behavior over silicon and dielectric regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，標示金屬在矽與介電層上的不同去向。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map metal behavior over silicon and dielectric regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未反應金屬殘留可能跨接間隔層。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unreacted metal residue may bridge spacers. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未反應金屬殘留可能跨接間隔層」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unreacted metal residue may bridge spacers. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-290-k1","title":"自對準反應區辨認的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify self-aligned reaction regions","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「標示金屬在矽與介電層上的不同去向」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Map metal behavior over silicon and dielectric regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-290-k2","title":"自對準反應區辨認的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify self-aligned reaction regions","text":"有效證據需支持「矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成」。但未反應金屬殘留可能跨接間隔層；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts. However, unreacted metal residue may bridge spacers; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「自對準反應區辨認」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify self-aligned reaction regions?","options":["厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型","底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋","矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成"],"optionsEn":["Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model","Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage","Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「標示金屬在矽與介電層上的不同去向」，因此直接證據是「矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未反應金屬殘留可能跨接間隔層。","explanationEn":"The task is to map metal behavior over silicon and dielectric regions; the direct criterion is: Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unreacted metal residue may bridge spacers."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":290,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-289"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-291","title":"首段矽化反應判讀","titleEn":"Interpret initial silicidation","objective":"完成「首段矽化反應判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比較反應前後物相與片電阻訊號』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret initial silicidation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare phase and sheet-resistance evidence before and after reaction.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較反應前後物相與片電阻訊號。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare phase and sheet-resistance evidence before and after reaction. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：電阻變化可由物相轉變支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: phase evidence supports the resistance change. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只看顏色不能證明目標物相。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: color alone does not establish the target phase. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「電阻變化可由物相轉變支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只看顏色不能證明目標物相」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Phase evidence supports the resistance change. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Color alone does not establish the target phase. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-291-k1","title":"首段矽化反應判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret initial silicidation","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較反應前後物相與片電阻訊號」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare phase and sheet-resistance evidence before and after reaction. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-291-k2","title":"首段矽化反應判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret initial silicidation","text":"有效證據需支持「電阻變化可由物相轉變支持」。但只看顏色不能證明目標物相；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Phase evidence supports the resistance change. However, color alone does not establish the target phase; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「首段矽化反應判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret initial silicidation?","options":["電阻變化可由物相轉變支持","最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊","導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈"],"optionsEn":["Phase evidence supports the resistance change","The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap","Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較反應前後物相與片電阻訊號」，因此直接證據是「電阻變化可由物相轉變支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只看顏色不能證明目標物相。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare phase and sheet-resistance evidence before and after reaction; the direct criterion is: Phase evidence supports the resistance change. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Color alone does not establish the target phase."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":291,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-290"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-292","title":"未反應金屬選擇性去除","titleEn":"Assess unreacted-metal removal","objective":"完成「未反應金屬選擇性去除」的證據判讀，辨識『比較介電層殘金屬與矽化物保留量』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess unreacted-metal removal by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dielectric metal residue and silicide retention.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較介電層殘金屬與矽化物保留量。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dielectric metal residue and silicide retention. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：去除不選擇會侵蝕有效接觸。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: nonselective removal erodes useful contacts. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「去除不選擇會侵蝕有效接觸」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Nonselective removal erodes useful contacts. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-292-k1","title":"未反應金屬選擇性去除的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess unreacted-metal removal","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較介電層殘金屬與矽化物保留量」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare dielectric metal residue and silicide retention. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-292-k2","title":"未反應金屬選擇性去除的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess unreacted-metal removal","text":"有效證據需支持「殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失」。但去除不選擇會侵蝕有效接觸；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains. However, nonselective removal erodes useful contacts; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「未反應金屬選擇性去除」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess unreacted-metal removal?","options":["成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長","殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失","底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計"],"optionsEn":["Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth","Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains","Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較介電層殘金屬與矽化物保留量」，因此直接證據是「殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：去除不選擇會侵蝕有效接觸。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dielectric metal residue and silicide retention; the direct criterion is: Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Nonselective removal erodes useful contacts."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":292,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-291"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-293","title":"後段物相穩定化","titleEn":"Assess silicide phase stabilization","objective":"完成「後段物相穩定化」的證據判讀，辨識『判讀後續熱處理的物相與電阻對照』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess silicide phase stabilization by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: interpret phase and resistance after subsequent thermal treatment.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，判讀後續熱處理的物相與電阻對照。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, interpret phase and resistance after subsequent thermal treatment. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：目標相與低電阻區域空間對應。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：相變不完全可能造成雙峰電阻分佈。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: incomplete conversion can cause bimodal resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「目標相與低電阻區域空間對應」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「相變不完全可能造成雙峰電阻分佈」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Incomplete conversion can cause bimodal resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-293-k1","title":"後段物相穩定化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess silicide phase stabilization","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「判讀後續熱處理的物相與電阻對照」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Interpret phase and resistance after subsequent thermal treatment. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-293-k2","title":"後段物相穩定化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess silicide phase stabilization","text":"有效證據需支持「目標相與低電阻區域空間對應」。但相變不完全可能造成雙峰電阻分佈；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions. However, incomplete conversion can cause bimodal resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「後段物相穩定化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess silicide phase stabilization?","options":["停止層清除且落點未過度受損","低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常","目標相與低電阻區域空間對應"],"optionsEn":["The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage","Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies","Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「判讀後續熱處理的物相與電阻對照」，因此直接證據是「目標相與低電阻區域空間對應」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：相變不完全可能造成雙峰電阻分佈。","explanationEn":"The task is to interpret phase and resistance after subsequent thermal treatment; the direct criterion is: Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Incomplete conversion can cause bimodal resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":293,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-292"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-294","title":"矽化物團聚檢查","titleEn":"Inspect silicide agglomeration","objective":"完成「矽化物團聚檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『對照島狀影像與局部電阻異常』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect silicide agglomeration by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate island-like morphology to local resistance anomalies.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照島狀影像與局部電阻異常。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate island-like morphology to local resistance anomalies. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: agglomeration has not broken film continuity. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均厚度合格仍可能局部斷路。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: acceptable mean thickness can conceal local opens. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均厚度合格仍可能局部斷路」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Agglomeration has not broken film continuity. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Acceptable mean thickness can conceal local opens. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-294-k1","title":"矽化物團聚檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect silicide agglomeration","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「對照島狀影像與局部電阻異常」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Relate island-like morphology to local resistance anomalies. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-294-k2","title":"矽化物團聚檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect silicide agglomeration","text":"有效證據需支持「導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞」。但平均厚度合格仍可能局部斷路；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Agglomeration has not broken film continuity. However, acceptable mean thickness can conceal local opens; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「矽化物團聚檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect silicide agglomeration?","options":["導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞","孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整","塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續"],"optionsEn":["Agglomeration has not broken film continuity","Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact","The effective plug conduction path remains continuous"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照島狀影像與局部電阻異常」，因此直接證據是「導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均厚度合格仍可能局部斷路。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate island-like morphology to local resistance anomalies; the direct criterion is: Agglomeration has not broken film continuity. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Acceptable mean thickness can conceal local opens."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":294,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-293"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-295","title":"側向矽化侵入","titleEn":"Inspect lateral silicide encroachment","objective":"完成「側向矽化侵入」的證據判讀，辨識『在閘邊截面標示反應前沿』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect lateral silicide encroachment by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: mark the reaction front near gate edges.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在閘邊截面標示反應前沿。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, mark the reaction front near gate edges. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the reaction front preserves required isolation spacing. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：側向侵入可導致閘極短接。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: lateral encroachment can cause gate shorts. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「側向侵入可導致閘極短接」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Lateral encroachment can cause gate shorts. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-295-k1","title":"側向矽化侵入的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect lateral silicide encroachment","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「在閘邊截面標示反應前沿」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Mark the reaction front near gate edges. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-295-k2","title":"側向矽化侵入的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect lateral silicide encroachment","text":"有效證據需支持「矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離」。但側向侵入可導致閘極短接；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing. However, lateral encroachment can cause gate shorts; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「側向矽化侵入」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect lateral silicide encroachment?","options":["場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷","矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離","等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化"],"optionsEn":["Field metal clears without excessive plug recess","The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing","Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「在閘邊截面標示反應前沿」，因此直接證據是「矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：側向侵入可導致閘極短接。","explanationEn":"The task is to mark the reaction front near gate edges; the direct criterion is: The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Lateral encroachment can cause gate shorts."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":295,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-294"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-296","title":"矽化物表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Measure silicide roughness","objective":"完成「矽化物表面粗糙度」的證據判讀，辨識『比較表面高度圖與後續接觸覆蓋模型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure silicide roughness by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare height maps with subsequent contact coverage.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較表面高度圖與後續接觸覆蓋模型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare height maps with subsequent contact coverage. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：局部突起可能造成高場與覆蓋弱點。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: protrusions can create high-field and coverage weak spots. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「局部突起可能造成高場與覆蓋弱點」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Protrusions can create high-field and coverage weak spots. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-296-k1","title":"矽化物表面粗糙度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure silicide roughness","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較表面高度圖與後續接觸覆蓋模型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare height maps with subsequent contact coverage. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-296-k2","title":"矽化物表面粗糙度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure silicide roughness","text":"有效證據需支持「粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷」。但局部突起可能造成高場與覆蓋弱點；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage. However, protrusions can create high-field and coverage weak spots; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「矽化物表面粗糙度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure silicide roughness?","options":["底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋","階差與後續金屬落點需求相容","粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷"],"optionsEn":["Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage","Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs","Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較表面高度圖與後續接觸覆蓋模型」，因此直接證據是「粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：局部突起可能造成高場與覆蓋弱點。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare height maps with subsequent contact coverage; the direct criterion is: Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Protrusions can create high-field and coverage weak spots."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":296,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-295"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-297","title":"接觸介電層厚度檢查","titleEn":"Inspect contact-dielectric thickness","objective":"完成「接觸介電層厚度檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『量取接觸層介電膜及停止層厚度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect contact-dielectric thickness by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure contact dielectric and stop-layer thicknesses.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取接觸層介電膜及停止層厚度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure contact dielectric and stop-layer thicknesses. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：膜厚漂移會改變蝕刻終點餘裕。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: thickness drift changes etch endpoint margin. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「膜厚漂移會改變蝕刻終點餘裕」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Thickness drift changes etch endpoint margin. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-297-k1","title":"接觸介電層厚度檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect contact-dielectric thickness","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「量取接觸層介電膜及停止層厚度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Measure contact dielectric and stop-layer thicknesses. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-297-k2","title":"接觸介電層厚度檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect contact-dielectric thickness","text":"有效證據需支持「厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型」。但膜厚漂移會改變蝕刻終點餘裕；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model. However, thickness drift changes etch endpoint margin; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸介電層厚度檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect contact-dielectric thickness?","options":["厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型","導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈","接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆"],"optionsEn":["Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model","Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing","Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取接觸層介電膜及停止層厚度」，因此直接證據是「厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：膜厚漂移會改變蝕刻終點餘裕。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure contact dielectric and stop-layer thicknesses; the direct criterion is: Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Thickness drift changes etch endpoint margin."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":297,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-296"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-298","title":"接觸孔套刻裕量","titleEn":"Evaluate contact overlay margin","objective":"完成「接觸孔套刻裕量」的證據判讀，辨識『疊合接觸孔與源汲極落點』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate contact overlay margin by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay contact openings and source/drain landing areas.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，疊合接觸孔與源汲極落點。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay contact openings and source/drain landing areas. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the worst direction preserves the required landing overlap. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均套刻可掩蓋局部錯位。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: average overlay can hide local misalignment. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均套刻可掩蓋局部錯位」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Average overlay can hide local misalignment. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-298-k1","title":"接觸孔套刻裕量的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate contact overlay margin","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「疊合接觸孔與源汲極落點」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Overlay contact openings and source/drain landing areas. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-298-k2","title":"接觸孔套刻裕量的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate contact overlay margin","text":"有效證據需支持「最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊」。但平均套刻可掩蓋局部錯位；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap. However, average overlay can hide local misalignment; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸孔套刻裕量」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate contact overlay margin?","options":["異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區","最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊","成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長"],"optionsEn":["The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region","The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap","Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「疊合接觸孔與源汲極落點」，因此直接證據是「最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均套刻可掩蓋局部錯位。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay contact openings and source/drain landing areas; the direct criterion is: The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Average overlay can hide local misalignment."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":298,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-297"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-299","title":"接觸孔臨界尺寸","titleEn":"Measure contact critical dimensions","objective":"完成「接觸孔臨界尺寸」的證據判讀，辨識『對照頂部孔徑與底部孔徑』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure contact critical dimensions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare contact top and bottom dimensions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照頂部孔徑與底部孔徑。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare contact top and bottom dimensions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: effective bottom contact area is independently estimated. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只量頂部會漏判底部縮口。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: top-only measurement misses bottom narrowing. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只量頂部會漏判底部縮口」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Top-only measurement misses bottom narrowing. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-299-k1","title":"接觸孔臨界尺寸的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure contact critical dimensions","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「對照頂部孔徑與底部孔徑」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare contact top and bottom dimensions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-299-k2","title":"接觸孔臨界尺寸的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure contact critical dimensions","text":"有效證據需支持「底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計」。但只量頂部會漏判底部縮口；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated. However, top-only measurement misses bottom narrowing; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸孔臨界尺寸」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure contact critical dimensions?","options":["低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常","材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致","底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計"],"optionsEn":["Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies","Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch","Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照頂部孔徑與底部孔徑」，因此直接證據是「底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只量頂部會漏判底部縮口。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare contact top and bottom dimensions; the direct criterion is: Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Top-only measurement misses bottom narrowing."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":299,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-298"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-300","title":"接觸孔停止層開口","titleEn":"Inspect contact stop-layer opening","objective":"完成「接觸孔停止層開口」的證據判讀，辨識『區分尚未開口與已傷及落點的截面』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect contact stop-layer opening by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish incomplete opening from landing damage.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分尚未開口與已傷及落點的截面。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish incomplete opening from landing damage. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：停止層清除且落點未過度受損。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the stop layer clears without excessive landing damage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過度蝕刻會增加接觸界面損傷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: overetch can damage the contact interface. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「停止層清除且落點未過度受損」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過度蝕刻會增加接觸界面損傷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Overetch can damage the contact interface. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-300-k1","title":"接觸孔停止層開口的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect contact stop-layer opening","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「區分尚未開口與已傷及落點的截面」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish incomplete opening from landing damage. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-300-k2","title":"接觸孔停止層開口的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect contact stop-layer opening","text":"有效證據需支持「停止層清除且落點未過度受損」。但過度蝕刻會增加接觸界面損傷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage. However, overetch can damage the contact interface; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸孔停止層開口」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect contact stop-layer opening?","options":["停止層清除且落點未過度受損","塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續","金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據"],"optionsEn":["The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage","The effective plug conduction path remains continuous","Interface condition is documented before metal contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分尚未開口與已傷及落點的截面」，因此直接證據是「停止層清除且落點未過度受損」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過度蝕刻會增加接觸界面損傷。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish incomplete opening from landing damage; the direct criterion is: The stop layer clears without excessive landing damage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Overetch can damage the contact interface."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":300,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-299"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-301","title":"孔底殘留清潔判讀","titleEn":"Assess contact-bottom residue","objective":"完成「孔底殘留清潔判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比對孔底元素分析與電阻分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess contact-bottom residue by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare bottom elemental analysis and resistance distribution.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比對孔底元素分析與電阻分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare bottom elemental analysis and resistance distribution. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：薄殘膜可能造成高接觸電阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a thin residue film can raise contact resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「薄殘膜可能造成高接觸電阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A thin residue film can raise contact resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-301-k1","title":"孔底殘留清潔判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess contact-bottom residue","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比對孔底元素分析與電阻分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare bottom elemental analysis and resistance distribution. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-301-k2","title":"孔底殘留清潔判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess contact-bottom residue","text":"有效證據需支持「孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整」。但薄殘膜可能造成高接觸電阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact. However, a thin residue film can raise contact resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「孔底殘留清潔判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess contact-bottom residue?","options":["剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性","孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整","場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷"],"optionsEn":["Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity","Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact","Field metal clears without excessive plug recess"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比對孔底元素分析與電阻分佈」，因此直接證據是「孔底殘留訊號降低且介面保持完整」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：薄殘膜可能造成高接觸電阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare bottom elemental analysis and resistance distribution; the direct criterion is: Bottom residue decreases while the interface remains intact. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A thin residue film can raise contact resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":301,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-300"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-302","title":"原位轉移防再氧化","titleEn":"Assess in-situ transfer protection","objective":"完成「原位轉移防再氧化」的證據判讀，辨識『比較清潔至沉積間界面再氧化證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess in-situ transfer protection by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare reoxidation evidence between cleaning and deposition.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較清潔至沉積間界面再氧化證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare reoxidation evidence between cleaning and deposition. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：乾淨表面可能在轉移時重新氧化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a clean surface can reoxidize during transfer. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「乾淨表面可能在轉移時重新氧化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A clean surface can reoxidize during transfer. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-302-k1","title":"原位轉移防再氧化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess in-situ transfer protection","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較清潔至沉積間界面再氧化證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare reoxidation evidence between cleaning and deposition. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-302-k2","title":"原位轉移防再氧化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess in-situ transfer protection","text":"有效證據需支持「等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化」。但乾淨表面可能在轉移時重新氧化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution. However, a clean surface can reoxidize during transfer; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「原位轉移防再氧化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess in-situ transfer protection?","options":["階差與後續金屬落點需求相容","目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯","等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化"],"optionsEn":["Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs","Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation","Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較清潔至沉積間界面再氧化證據」，因此直接證據是「等待與轉移條件可解釋界面變化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：乾淨表面可能在轉移時重新氧化。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare reoxidation evidence between cleaning and deposition; the direct criterion is: Queue and transfer conditions explain interface evolution. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A clean surface can reoxidize during transfer."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":302,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-301"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-303","title":"接觸襯層底部覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect contact-liner bottom coverage","objective":"完成「接觸襯層底部覆蓋」的證據判讀，辨識『在高深寬比孔截面追蹤襯層連續性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect contact-liner bottom coverage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace liner continuity in high-aspect-ratio contacts.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在高深寬比孔截面追蹤襯層連續性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace liner continuity in high-aspect-ratio contacts. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：頂部成膜正常不保證孔底連續。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: good top coverage does not guarantee bottom continuity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「頂部成膜正常不保證孔底連續」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Good top coverage does not guarantee bottom continuity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-303-k1","title":"接觸襯層底部覆蓋的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect contact-liner bottom coverage","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「在高深寬比孔截面追蹤襯層連續性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Trace liner continuity in high-aspect-ratio contacts. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-303-k2","title":"接觸襯層底部覆蓋的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect contact-liner bottom coverage","text":"有效證據需支持「底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋」。但頂部成膜正常不保證孔底連續；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage. However, good top coverage does not guarantee bottom continuity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸襯層底部覆蓋」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect contact-liner bottom coverage?","options":["底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋","接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆","矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成"],"optionsEn":["Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage","Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution","Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「在高深寬比孔截面追蹤襯層連續性」，因此直接證據是「底部與側壁均有連續覆蓋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：頂部成膜正常不保證孔底連續。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace liner continuity in high-aspect-ratio contacts; the direct criterion is: Both bottom and sidewalls have continuous coverage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Good top coverage does not guarantee bottom continuity."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":303,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-302"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-304","title":"接觸阻障層完整性","titleEn":"Verify contact-barrier integrity","objective":"完成「接觸阻障層完整性」的證據判讀，辨識『比較阻障層截面與元素擴散證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate verify contact-barrier integrity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare barrier sections with elemental diffusion evidence.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較阻障層截面與元素擴散證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare barrier sections with elemental diffusion evidence. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：針孔可能讓局部擴散被平均量測漏掉。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: pinholes can permit diffusion hidden by averages. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「針孔可能讓局部擴散被平均量測漏掉」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Pinholes can permit diffusion hidden by averages. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-304-k1","title":"接觸阻障層完整性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of verify contact-barrier integrity","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較阻障層截面與元素擴散證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare barrier sections with elemental diffusion evidence. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-304-k2","title":"接觸阻障層完整性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for verify contact-barrier integrity","text":"有效證據需支持「導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈」。但針孔可能讓局部擴散被平均量測漏掉；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing. However, pinholes can permit diffusion hidden by averages; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸阻障層完整性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for verify contact-barrier integrity?","options":["電阻變化可由物相轉變支持","導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈","異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區"],"optionsEn":["Phase evidence supports the resistance change","Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing","The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較阻障層截面與元素擴散證據」，因此直接證據是「導體元素未出現非預期越界分佈」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：針孔可能讓局部擴散被平均量測漏掉。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare barrier sections with elemental diffusion evidence; the direct criterion is: Conductor species show no unintended boundary crossing. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Pinholes can permit diffusion hidden by averages."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":304,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-303"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-305","title":"鎢成核分支","titleEn":"Inspect tungsten nucleation","objective":"完成「鎢成核分支」的證據判讀，辨識『辨認示意孔底成核延遲與側壁成長』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect tungsten nucleation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: identify model bottom nucleation delay and sidewall growth.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，辨認示意孔底成核延遲與側壁成長。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, identify model bottom nucleation delay and sidewall growth. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：成核延遲會留下接觸空隙。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: delayed nucleation can leave contact voids. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「成核延遲會留下接觸空隙」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Delayed nucleation can leave contact voids. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-305-k1","title":"鎢成核分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect tungsten nucleation","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「辨認示意孔底成核延遲與側壁成長」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Identify model bottom nucleation delay and sidewall growth. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-305-k2","title":"鎢成核分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect tungsten nucleation","text":"有效證據需支持「成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長」。但成核延遲會留下接觸空隙；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth. However, delayed nucleation can leave contact voids; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鎢成核分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect tungsten nucleation?","options":["材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致","殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失","成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長"],"optionsEn":["Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch","Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains","Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「辨認示意孔底成核延遲與側壁成長」，因此直接證據是「成核均勻性支持連續塞孔成長」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：成核延遲會留下接觸空隙。","explanationEn":"The task is to identify model bottom nucleation delay and sidewall growth; the direct criterion is: Nucleation uniformity supports continuous plug growth. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Delayed nucleation can leave contact voids."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":305,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-304"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-306","title":"鈷填孔分支","titleEn":"Assess cobalt contact filling","objective":"完成「鈷填孔分支」的證據判讀，辨識『比較填充截面與接觸電阻尾端』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess cobalt contact filling by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare fill sections and resistance tails.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較填充截面與接觸電阻尾端。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare fill sections and resistance tails. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: resistance improves without interface or void anomalies. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：更換材料不會自動消除整合缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: changing material does not automatically remove integration defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「更換材料不會自動消除整合缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Changing material does not automatically remove integration defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-306-k1","title":"鈷填孔分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess cobalt contact filling","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較填充截面與接觸電阻尾端」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare fill sections and resistance tails. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-306-k2","title":"鈷填孔分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess cobalt contact filling","text":"有效證據需支持「低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常」。但更換材料不會自動消除整合缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies. However, changing material does not automatically remove integration defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鈷填孔分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess cobalt contact filling?","options":["低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常","金屬接觸前界面狀態有獨立證據","目標相與低電阻區域空間對應"],"optionsEn":["Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies","Interface condition is documented before metal contact","Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較填充截面與接觸電阻尾端」，因此直接證據是「低電阻改善未伴隨界面或空洞異常」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：更換材料不會自動消除整合缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare fill sections and resistance tails; the direct criterion is: Resistance improves without interface or void anomalies. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Changing material does not automatically remove integration defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":306,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-305"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-307","title":"接觸塞孔縫隙辨認","titleEn":"Identify contact-plug seams","objective":"完成「接觸塞孔縫隙辨認」的證據判讀，辨識『在多位置截面區分接合縫與開放空洞』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify contact-plug seams by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish seams from open voids across sections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在多位置截面區分接合縫與開放空洞。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish seams from open voids across sections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the effective plug conduction path remains continuous. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一截面可能漏掉偏心空洞。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one section can miss off-center voids. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一截面可能漏掉偏心空洞」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The effective plug conduction path remains continuous. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One section can miss off-center voids. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-307-k1","title":"接觸塞孔縫隙辨認的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify contact-plug seams","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「在多位置截面區分接合縫與開放空洞」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish seams from open voids across sections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-307-k2","title":"接觸塞孔縫隙辨認的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify contact-plug seams","text":"有效證據需支持「塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續」。但單一截面可能漏掉偏心空洞；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The effective plug conduction path remains continuous. However, one section can miss off-center voids; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸塞孔縫隙辨認」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify contact-plug seams?","options":["導電膜連續性未被團聚破壞","塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續","剩餘矽厚度不侵犯接面完整性"],"optionsEn":["Agglomeration has not broken film continuity","The effective plug conduction path remains continuous","Remaining silicon preserves junction integrity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「在多位置截面區分接合縫與開放空洞」，因此直接證據是「塞孔有效導通路徑保持連續」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一截面可能漏掉偏心空洞。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish seams from open voids across sections; the direct criterion is: The effective plug conduction path remains continuous. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One section can miss off-center voids."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":307,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-306"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-308","title":"塞孔回蝕或研磨終點","titleEn":"Assess plug recess or polish endpoint","objective":"完成「塞孔回蝕或研磨終點」的證據判讀，辨識『比較導體去除量與介電層暴露圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess plug recess or polish endpoint by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare conductor removal and exposed dielectric maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較導體去除量與介電層暴露圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare conductor removal and exposed dielectric maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: field metal clears without excessive plug recess. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：終點太晚會增加塞孔高度損失。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a late endpoint increases plug height loss. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「終點太晚會增加塞孔高度損失」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Field metal clears without excessive plug recess. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A late endpoint increases plug height loss. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-308-k1","title":"塞孔回蝕或研磨終點的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess plug recess or polish endpoint","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「比較導體去除量與介電層暴露圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Compare conductor removal and exposed dielectric maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-308-k2","title":"塞孔回蝕或研磨終點的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess plug recess or polish endpoint","text":"有效證據需支持「場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷」。但終點太晚會增加塞孔高度損失；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Field metal clears without excessive plug recess. However, a late endpoint increases plug height loss; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「塞孔回蝕或研磨終點」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess plug recess or polish endpoint?","options":["目標區金屬連續且厚度分佈可追溯","矽化前沿保留設計所需隔離距離","場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷"],"optionsEn":["Metal is continuous with traceable thickness variation","The reaction front preserves required isolation spacing","Field metal clears without excessive plug recess"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較導體去除量與介電層暴露圖」，因此直接證據是「場區金屬清除且塞孔未過度凹陷」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：終點太晚會增加塞孔高度損失。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare conductor removal and exposed dielectric maps; the direct criterion is: Field metal clears without excessive plug recess. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A late endpoint increases plug height loss."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":308,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-307"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-309","title":"塞孔凹陷高度量測","titleEn":"Measure contact-plug recess","objective":"完成「塞孔凹陷高度量測」的證據判讀，辨識『以高度剖面量取塞孔與介電層階差』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure contact-plug recess by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure plug-to-dielectric height differences.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，以高度剖面量取塞孔與介電層階差。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure plug-to-dielectric height differences. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：階差與後續金屬落點需求相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過深凹陷可能增加下一層接觸阻抗。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: deep recess can increase next-level contact impedance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「階差與後續金屬落點需求相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過深凹陷可能增加下一層接觸阻抗」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Deep recess can increase next-level contact impedance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-309-k1","title":"塞孔凹陷高度量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure contact-plug recess","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「以高度剖面量取塞孔與介電層階差」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Measure plug-to-dielectric height differences. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-309-k2","title":"塞孔凹陷高度量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure contact-plug recess","text":"有效證據需支持「階差與後續金屬落點需求相容」。但過深凹陷可能增加下一層接觸阻抗；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs. However, deep recess can increase next-level contact impedance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「塞孔凹陷高度量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure contact-plug recess?","options":["階差與後續金屬落點需求相容","矽化物僅在指定矽接觸區形成","粗糙度未造成接觸層覆蓋中斷"],"optionsEn":["Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs","Silicide forms only at intended silicon contacts","Roughness does not disrupt contact-layer coverage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「以高度剖面量取塞孔與介電層階差」，因此直接證據是「階差與後續金屬落點需求相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過深凹陷可能增加下一層接觸阻抗。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure plug-to-dielectric height differences; the direct criterion is: Height differences suit subsequent metal landing needs. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Deep recess can increase next-level contact impedance."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":309,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-308"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-310","title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻抽取","titleEn":"Extract Kelvin contact resistance","objective":"完成「Kelvin 接觸電阻抽取」的證據判讀，辨識『用四端結構分離引線與接觸電阻』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate extract kelvin contact resistance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate lead and contact resistance with four terminals.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用四端結構分離引線與接觸電阻。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate lead and contact resistance with four terminals. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：二端量測可能把引線變化當接觸變化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: two-terminal tests can confuse lead and contact changes. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「二端量測可能把引線變化當接觸變化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Two-terminal tests can confuse lead and contact changes. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-310-k1","title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻抽取的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of extract kelvin contact resistance","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「用四端結構分離引線與接觸電阻」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Separate lead and contact resistance with four terminals. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-310-k2","title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻抽取的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for extract kelvin contact resistance","text":"有效證據需支持「接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆」。但二端量測可能把引線變化當接觸變化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution. However, two-terminal tests can confuse lead and contact changes; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「Kelvin 接觸電阻抽取」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for extract kelvin contact resistance?","options":["厚度差異已納入接觸孔深度模型","接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆","電阻變化可由物相轉變支持"],"optionsEn":["Thickness variation is included in the contact-depth model","Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution","Phase evidence supports the resistance change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「用四端結構分離引線與接觸電阻」，因此直接證據是「接觸貢獻不被長引線電阻混淆」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：二端量測可能把引線變化當接觸變化。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate lead and contact resistance with four terminals; the direct criterion is: Lead resistance does not confound the contact contribution. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Two-terminal tests can confuse lead and contact changes."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":310,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-309"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-311","title":"接觸鏈失效定位","titleEn":"Locate contact-chain failures","objective":"完成「接觸鏈失效定位」的證據判讀，辨識『由分段鏈電阻定位高阻接觸群』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate locate contact-chain failures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use segmented chain resistance to locate high-resistance groups.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，由分段鏈電阻定位高阻接觸群。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use segmented chain resistance to locate high-resistance groups. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：整條鏈的總值不能指出單一故障位置。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: total chain resistance cannot identify one failed contact. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「整條鏈的總值不能指出單一故障位置」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Total chain resistance cannot identify one failed contact. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-311-k1","title":"接觸鏈失效定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of locate contact-chain failures","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「由分段鏈電阻定位高阻接觸群」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Use segmented chain resistance to locate high-resistance groups. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-311-k2","title":"接觸鏈失效定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for locate contact-chain failures","text":"有效證據需支持「異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區」。但整條鏈的總值不能指出單一故障位置；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region. However, total chain resistance cannot identify one failed contact; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸鏈失效定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for locate contact-chain failures?","options":["殘金屬清除且有效矽化物未明顯流失","最差方向仍保留題定落點重疊","異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區"],"optionsEn":["Residual metal is removed while useful silicide remains","The worst direction preserves the required landing overlap","The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「由分段鏈電阻定位高阻接觸群」，因此直接證據是「異常可縮小至可再檢測的接觸區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：整條鏈的總值不能指出單一故障位置。","explanationEn":"The task is to use segmented chain resistance to locate high-resistance groups; the direct criterion is: The anomaly is localized to a reviewable contact region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Total chain resistance cannot identify one failed contact."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":311,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-310"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-312","title":"接觸整合分支放行","titleEn":"Release a contact integration branch","objective":"完成「接觸整合分支放行」的證據判讀，辨識『整合界面、塞孔形貌與電阻尾端證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release a contact integration branch by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine interface, plug morphology and resistance-tail evidence.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，整合界面、塞孔形貌與電阻尾端證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine interface, plug morphology and resistance-tail evidence. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：低平均值不能取代缺陷尾端審查。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a low mean cannot replace tail-defect review. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「低平均值不能取代缺陷尾端審查」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A low mean cannot replace tail-defect review. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-312-k1","title":"接觸整合分支放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release a contact integration branch","text":"接觸電阻包含界面與導體貢獻；矽化物、阻障層及塞孔材料依整合路線選擇，不能視為每個節點都使用的固定堆疊。 本題具體操作為「整合界面、塞孔形貌與電阻尾端證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Contact resistance includes interface and conductor contributions; silicides, barriers and plug materials depend on the integration route rather than a universal stack. Here the concrete task is: Combine interface, plug morphology and resistance-tail evidence. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-312-k2","title":"接觸整合分支放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release a contact integration branch","text":"有效證據需支持「材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致」。但低平均值不能取代缺陷尾端審查；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch. However, a low mean cannot replace tail-defect review; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸整合分支放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release a contact integration branch?","options":["材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致","目標相與低電阻區域空間對應","底部有效接觸面積可獨立估計"],"optionsEn":["Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch","Target phase spatially matches low-resistance regions","Effective bottom contact area is independently estimated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「整合界面、塞孔形貌與電阻尾端證據」，因此直接證據是「材料分支的形貌與電性結論一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：低平均值不能取代缺陷尾端審查。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine interface, plug morphology and resistance-tail evidence; the direct criterion is: Morphological and electrical conclusions agree for the material branch. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A low mean cannot replace tail-defect review."},"sourceIds":["scb-silicide","scb-cobalt","scb-metallization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":312,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-311"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":12},{"id":"sc-m13","title":"層間介電膜與化學機械平坦化","titleEn":"Interlayer dielectrics and CMP","description":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-313","title":"層間介電膜間隙映射","titleEn":"Map interlayer dielectric gaps","objective":"完成「層間介電膜間隙映射」的證據判讀，辨識『量取導體間空間與待填充的深寬比』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map interlayer dielectric gaps by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure conductor spacing and gap aspect ratios.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取導體間空間與待填充的深寬比。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure conductor spacing and gap aspect ratios. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只檢查開闊區會漏掉窄縫風險。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: checking open areas misses narrow-gap risks. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只檢查開闊區會漏掉窄縫風險」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Checking open areas misses narrow-gap risks. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-313-k1","title":"層間介電膜間隙映射的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map interlayer dielectric gaps","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「量取導體間空間與待填充的深寬比」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Measure conductor spacing and gap aspect ratios. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-313-k2","title":"層間介電膜間隙映射的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map interlayer dielectric gaps","text":"有效證據需支持「最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估」。但只檢查開闊區會漏掉窄縫風險；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment. However, checking open areas misses narrow-gap risks; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「層間介電膜間隙映射」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map interlayer dielectric gaps?","options":["大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核","最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估","降低電容的收益與強度代價並列"],"optionsEn":["Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching","Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment","Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取導體間空間與待填充的深寬比」，因此直接證據是「最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只檢查開闊區會漏掉窄縫風險。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure conductor spacing and gap aspect ratios; the direct criterion is: Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Checking open areas misses narrow-gap risks."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":313,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-312"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-314","title":"介電膜沉積共形性","titleEn":"Assess dielectric conformality","objective":"完成「介電膜沉積共形性」的證據判讀，辨識『比較階梯頂部、側壁與底部厚度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess dielectric conformality by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare thickness at tops, sidewalls and bottoms.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較階梯頂部、側壁與底部厚度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare thickness at tops, sidewalls and bottoms. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: coverage differences are reproducible across sections. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均膜厚不反映側壁薄弱點。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: average thickness misses thin sidewalls. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均膜厚不反映側壁薄弱點」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Coverage differences are reproducible across sections. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Average thickness misses thin sidewalls. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-314-k1","title":"介電膜沉積共形性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess dielectric conformality","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較階梯頂部、側壁與底部厚度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare thickness at tops, sidewalls and bottoms. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-314-k2","title":"介電膜沉積共形性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess dielectric conformality","text":"有效證據需支持「覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現」。但平均膜厚不反映側壁薄弱點；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Coverage differences are reproducible across sections. However, average thickness misses thin sidewalls; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電膜沉積共形性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess dielectric conformality?","options":["收縮量與材料轉變相互對應","供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性","覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現"],"optionsEn":["Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation","Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample","Coverage differences are reproducible across sections"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較階梯頂部、側壁與底部厚度」，因此直接證據是「覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均膜厚不反映側壁薄弱點。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare thickness at tops, sidewalls and bottoms; the direct criterion is: Coverage differences are reproducible across sections. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Average thickness misses thin sidewalls."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":314,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-313"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-315","title":"間隙填充夾口辨識","titleEn":"Identify gap-fill pinch-off","objective":"完成「間隙填充夾口辨識」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤填充過程中開口縮合的幾何變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify gap-fill pinch-off by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace closure of the gap opening during filling.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤填充過程中開口縮合的幾何變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace closure of the gap opening during filling. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: interior filling precedes closure of the opening. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：先封口會埋入封閉空洞。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: premature closure traps a buried void. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「先封口會埋入封閉空洞」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Interior filling precedes closure of the opening. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Premature closure traps a buried void. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-315-k1","title":"間隙填充夾口辨識的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify gap-fill pinch-off","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「追蹤填充過程中開口縮合的幾何變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Trace closure of the gap opening during filling. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-315-k2","title":"間隙填充夾口辨識的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify gap-fill pinch-off","text":"有效證據需支持「開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充」。但先封口會埋入封閉空洞；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Interior filling precedes closure of the opening. However, premature closure traps a buried void; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「間隙填充夾口辨識」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify gap-fill pinch-off?","options":["開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充","環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯","調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致"],"optionsEn":["Interior filling precedes closure of the opening","Environmental history tracks property changes","Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤填充過程中開口縮合的幾何變化」，因此直接證據是「開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：先封口會埋入封閉空洞。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace closure of the gap opening during filling; the direct criterion is: Interior filling precedes closure of the opening. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Premature closure traps a buried void."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":315,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-314"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-316","title":"可流動介電膜分支","titleEn":"Assess flowable dielectric branches","objective":"完成「可流動介電膜分支」的證據判讀，辨識『比較回流前後窄縫內膜形』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess flowable dielectric branches by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare gap profiles before and after model flow.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較回流前後窄縫內膜形。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare gap profiles before and after model flow. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：填充改善與後續收縮均可量測。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：良好初始填充可能在固化後生裂。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: good initial filling may crack after curing. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「填充改善與後續收縮均可量測」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「良好初始填充可能在固化後生裂」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Good initial filling may crack after curing. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-316-k1","title":"可流動介電膜分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess flowable dielectric branches","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較回流前後窄縫內膜形」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare gap profiles before and after model flow. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-316-k2","title":"可流動介電膜分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess flowable dielectric branches","text":"有效證據需支持「填充改善與後續收縮均可量測」。但良好初始填充可能在固化後生裂；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable. However, good initial filling may crack after curing; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「可流動介電膜分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess flowable dielectric branches?","options":["邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符","填充改善與後續收縮均可量測","待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離"],"optionsEn":["The edge model matches the usable die region","Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable","Removal height is separated from layers that must remain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較回流前後窄縫內膜形」，因此直接證據是「填充改善與後續收縮均可量測」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：良好初始填充可能在固化後生裂。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare gap profiles before and after model flow; the direct criterion is: Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Good initial filling may crack after curing."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":316,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-315"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-317","title":"等離子增強沉積膜質","titleEn":"Inspect PECVD film quality","objective":"完成「等離子增強沉積膜質」的證據判讀，辨識『關聯膜密度、鍵結訊號與漏電樣本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect pecvd film quality by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate film density, bonding signatures and leakage samples.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，關聯膜密度、鍵結訊號與漏電樣本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate film density, bonding signatures and leakage samples. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：疏鬆膜可能增加吸水與漏電。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a porous film may increase moisture uptake and leakage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「疏鬆膜可能增加吸水與漏電」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A porous film may increase moisture uptake and leakage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-317-k1","title":"等離子增強沉積膜質的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect pecvd film quality","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「關聯膜密度、鍵結訊號與漏電樣本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Relate film density, bonding signatures and leakage samples. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-317-k2","title":"等離子增強沉積膜質的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect pecvd film quality","text":"有效證據需支持「膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度」。但疏鬆膜可能增加吸水與漏電；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness. However, a porous film may increase moisture uptake and leakage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「等離子增強沉積膜質」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect pecvd film quality?","options":["墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化","終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應","膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度"],"optionsEn":["Pad-condition changes explain rate variation","Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements","Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「關聯膜密度、鍵結訊號與漏電樣本」，因此直接證據是「膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：疏鬆膜可能增加吸水與漏電。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate film density, bonding signatures and leakage samples; the direct criterion is: Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A porous film may increase moisture uptake and leakage."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":317,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-316"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-318","title":"介電膜折射率映射","titleEn":"Map dielectric refractive index","objective":"完成「介電膜折射率映射」的證據判讀，辨識『用橢圓偏光模型區分厚度與光學常數』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map dielectric refractive index by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate thickness and optical constants in ellipsometry.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用橢圓偏光模型區分厚度與光學常數。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate thickness and optical constants in ellipsometry. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：錯誤光學模型會產生假膜厚差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a wrong optical model creates false thickness differences. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「錯誤光學模型會產生假膜厚差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A wrong optical model creates false thickness differences. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-318-k1","title":"介電膜折射率映射的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map dielectric refractive index","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「用橢圓偏光模型區分厚度與光學常數」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Separate thickness and optical constants in ellipsometry. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-318-k2","title":"介電膜折射率映射的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map dielectric refractive index","text":"有效證據需支持「擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查」。但錯誤光學模型會產生假膜厚差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked. However, a wrong optical model creates false thickness differences; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電膜折射率映射」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map dielectric refractive index?","options":["擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查","修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容","停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動"],"optionsEn":["Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked","Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution","Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「用橢圓偏光模型區分厚度與光學常數」，因此直接證據是「擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：錯誤光學模型會產生假膜厚差。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate thickness and optical constants in ellipsometry; the direct criterion is: Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A wrong optical model creates false thickness differences."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":318,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-317"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-319","title":"介電膜應力曲率量測","titleEn":"Measure dielectric stress by curvature","objective":"完成「介電膜應力曲率量測」的證據判讀，辨識『比較沉積前後晶圓曲率』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure dielectric stress by curvature by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare wafer curvature before and after deposition.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較沉積前後晶圓曲率。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare wafer curvature before and after deposition. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略原始翹曲會誤估薄膜應力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring initial bow biases film-stress estimates. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略原始翹曲會誤估薄膜應力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring initial bow biases film-stress estimates. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-319-k1","title":"介電膜應力曲率量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure dielectric stress by curvature","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較沉積前後晶圓曲率」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare wafer curvature before and after deposition. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-319-k2","title":"介電膜應力曲率量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure dielectric stress by curvature","text":"有效證據需支持「應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設」。但忽略原始翹曲會誤估薄膜應力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions. However, ignoring initial bow biases film-stress estimates; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電膜應力曲率量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure dielectric stress by curvature?","options":["跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制","應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設","大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核"],"optionsEn":["Height differences across pattern densities are controlled","Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions","Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較沉積前後晶圓曲率」，因此直接證據是「應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略原始翹曲會誤估薄膜應力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare wafer curvature before and after deposition; the direct criterion is: Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring initial bow biases film-stress estimates."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":319,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-318"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-320","title":"低介電常數膜孔隙","titleEn":"Assess low-k porosity","objective":"完成「低介電常數膜孔隙」的證據判讀，辨識『對照孔隙特徵、介電常數與機械性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess low-k porosity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare porosity, dielectric constant and mechanical properties.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照孔隙特徵、介電常數與機械性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare porosity, dielectric constant and mechanical properties. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：降低電容的收益與強度代價並列。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：最低介電常數未必適合後續研磨。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: the lowest dielectric constant may not survive CMP. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「降低電容的收益與強度代價並列」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「最低介電常數未必適合後續研磨」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: The lowest dielectric constant may not survive CMP. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-320-k1","title":"低介電常數膜孔隙的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess low-k porosity","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「對照孔隙特徵、介電常數與機械性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare porosity, dielectric constant and mechanical properties. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-320-k2","title":"低介電常數膜孔隙的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess low-k porosity","text":"有效證據需支持「降低電容的收益與強度代價並列」。但最低介電常數未必適合後續研磨；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together. However, the lowest dielectric constant may not survive CMP; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「低介電常數膜孔隙」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess low-k porosity?","options":["供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性","凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據","降低電容的收益與強度代價並列"],"optionsEn":["Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample","Recess and residue have distinct material evidence","Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照孔隙特徵、介電常數與機械性」，因此直接證據是「降低電容的收益與強度代價並列」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：最低介電常數未必適合後續研磨。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare porosity, dielectric constant and mechanical properties; the direct criterion is: Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: The lowest dielectric constant may not survive CMP."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":320,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-319"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-321","title":"低介電膜固化收縮","titleEn":"Measure low-k cure shrinkage","objective":"完成「低介電膜固化收縮」的證據判讀，辨識『比較固化前後膜厚與鍵結變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure low-k cure shrinkage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare thickness and bonding before and after curing.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較固化前後膜厚與鍵結變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare thickness and bonding before and after curing. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：收縮量與材料轉變相互對應。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不均勻固化可造成局部應力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: nonuniform curing can create local stress. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「收縮量與材料轉變相互對應」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不均勻固化可造成局部應力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Nonuniform curing can create local stress. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-321-k1","title":"低介電膜固化收縮的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure low-k cure shrinkage","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較固化前後膜厚與鍵結變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare thickness and bonding before and after curing. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-321-k2","title":"低介電膜固化收縮的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure low-k cure shrinkage","text":"有效證據需支持「收縮量與材料轉變相互對應」。但不均勻固化可造成局部應力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation. However, nonuniform curing can create local stress; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「低介電膜固化收縮」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure low-k cure shrinkage?","options":["收縮量與材料轉變相互對應","調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致","方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說"],"optionsEn":["Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation","Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes","Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較固化前後膜厚與鍵結變化」，因此直接證據是「收縮量與材料轉變相互對應」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不均勻固化可造成局部應力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare thickness and bonding before and after curing; the direct criterion is: Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Nonuniform curing can create local stress."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":321,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-320"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-322","title":"吸濕後膜性質漂移","titleEn":"Assess moisture-induced film drift","objective":"完成「吸濕後膜性質漂移」的證據判讀，辨識『比較乾燥與吸濕樣本的光學及電性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess moisture-induced film drift by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare optical and electrical data for dry and humid samples.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較乾燥與吸濕樣本的光學及電性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare optical and electrical data for dry and humid samples. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: environmental history tracks property changes. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：將吸水漂移當成沉積漂移會誤修機台。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: misreading moisture drift can prompt an incorrect tool adjustment. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「將吸水漂移當成沉積漂移會誤修機台」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Environmental history tracks property changes. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Misreading moisture drift can prompt an incorrect tool adjustment. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-322-k1","title":"吸濕後膜性質漂移的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess moisture-induced film drift","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較乾燥與吸濕樣本的光學及電性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare optical and electrical data for dry and humid samples. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-322-k2","title":"吸濕後膜性質漂移的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess moisture-induced film drift","text":"有效證據需支持「環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯」。但將吸水漂移當成沉積漂移會誤修機台；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Environmental history tracks property changes. However, misreading moisture drift can prompt an incorrect tool adjustment; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「吸濕後膜性質漂移」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess moisture-induced film drift?","options":["顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷","環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯","邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符"],"optionsEn":["Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage","Environmental history tracks property changes","The edge model matches the usable die region"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較乾燥與吸濕樣本的光學及電性」，因此直接證據是「環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：將吸水漂移當成沉積漂移會誤修機台。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare optical and electrical data for dry and humid samples; the direct criterion is: Environmental history tracks property changes. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Misreading moisture drift can prompt an incorrect tool adjustment."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":322,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-321"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-323","title":"CMP 前階差掃描","titleEn":"Scan pre-CMP topography","objective":"完成「CMP 前階差掃描」的證據判讀，辨識『建立高低區高度與圖形密度對照圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate scan pre-cmp topography by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map height differences against pattern density.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，建立高低區高度與圖形密度對照圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map height differences against pattern density. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: removal height is separated from layers that must remain. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未知初始階差會誤導終點判斷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unknown initial topography confuses endpoint decisions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未知初始階差會誤導終點判斷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Removal height is separated from layers that must remain. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unknown initial topography confuses endpoint decisions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-323-k1","title":"CMP 前階差掃描的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of scan pre-cmp topography","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「建立高低區高度與圖形密度對照圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Map height differences against pattern density. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-323-k2","title":"CMP 前階差掃描的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for scan pre-cmp topography","text":"有效證據需支持「待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離」。但未知初始階差會誤導終點判斷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Removal height is separated from layers that must remain. However, unknown initial topography confuses endpoint decisions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「CMP 前階差掃描」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for scan pre-cmp topography?","options":["終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應","污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯","待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離"],"optionsEn":["Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements","Residue morphology correlates with drying locations","Removal height is separated from layers that must remain"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「建立高低區高度與圖形密度對照圖」，因此直接證據是「待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未知初始階差會誤導終點判斷。","explanationEn":"The task is to map height differences against pattern density; the direct criterion is: Removal height is separated from layers that must remain. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unknown initial topography confuses endpoint decisions."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":323,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-322"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-324","title":"研磨墊表面狀態","titleEn":"Inspect polishing-pad condition","objective":"完成「研磨墊表面狀態」的證據判讀，辨識『比較墊面孔隙影像與去除速率趨勢』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect polishing-pad condition by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare pad-pore images and removal-rate trends.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較墊面孔隙影像與去除速率趨勢。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare pad-pore images and removal-rate trends. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: pad-condition changes explain rate variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：釉化墊面可能降低局部去除能力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: pad glazing can reduce local removal capability. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「釉化墊面可能降低局部去除能力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Pad-condition changes explain rate variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Pad glazing can reduce local removal capability. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-324-k1","title":"研磨墊表面狀態的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect polishing-pad condition","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較墊面孔隙影像與去除速率趨勢」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare pad-pore images and removal-rate trends. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-324-k2","title":"研磨墊表面狀態的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect polishing-pad condition","text":"有效證據需支持「墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化」。但釉化墊面可能降低局部去除能力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Pad-condition changes explain rate variation. However, pad glazing can reduce local removal capability; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨墊表面狀態」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect polishing-pad condition?","options":["墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化","停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動","三者在量測不確定度內相互一致"],"optionsEn":["Pad-condition changes explain rate variation","Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation","The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較墊面孔隙影像與去除速率趨勢」，因此直接證據是「墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：釉化墊面可能降低局部去除能力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare pad-pore images and removal-rate trends; the direct criterion is: Pad-condition changes explain rate variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Pad glazing can reduce local removal capability."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":324,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-323"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-325","title":"研磨墊修整一致性","titleEn":"Assess pad conditioning consistency","objective":"完成「研磨墊修整一致性」的證據判讀，辨識『重建修整路徑與墊面磨耗圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess pad conditioning consistency by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: reconstruct conditioning tracks and pad-wear maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，重建修整路徑與墊面磨耗圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, reconstruct conditioning tracks and pad-wear maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不均修整可造成徑向研磨偏差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: uneven conditioning can produce radial polish bias. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不均修整可造成徑向研磨偏差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Uneven conditioning can produce radial polish bias. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-325-k1","title":"研磨墊修整一致性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess pad conditioning consistency","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「重建修整路徑與墊面磨耗圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Reconstruct conditioning tracks and pad-wear maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-325-k2","title":"研磨墊修整一致性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess pad conditioning consistency","text":"有效證據需支持「修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容」。但不均修整可造成徑向研磨偏差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution. However, uneven conditioning can produce radial polish bias; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨墊修整一致性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess pad conditioning consistency?","options":["平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離","修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容","跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制"],"optionsEn":["Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation","Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution","Height differences across pattern densities are controlled"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「重建修整路徑與墊面磨耗圖」，因此直接證據是「修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不均修整可造成徑向研磨偏差。","explanationEn":"The task is to reconstruct conditioning tracks and pad-wear maps; the direct criterion is: Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Uneven conditioning can produce radial polish bias."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":325,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-324"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-326","title":"研磨液粒子聚集檢查","titleEn":"Inspect slurry particle aggregation","objective":"完成「研磨液粒子聚集檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『比較粒徑分佈尾端與刮傷事件』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect slurry particle aggregation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare large-particle tails with scratch events.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較粒徑分佈尾端與刮傷事件。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare large-particle tails with scratch events. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: large-particle excursions are checked against scratching. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均粒徑可能掩蓋少量大聚集物。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mean particle size hides rare large agglomerates. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均粒徑可能掩蓋少量大聚集物」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mean particle size hides rare large agglomerates. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-326-k1","title":"研磨液粒子聚集檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect slurry particle aggregation","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較粒徑分佈尾端與刮傷事件」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare large-particle tails with scratch events. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-326-k2","title":"研磨液粒子聚集檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect slurry particle aggregation","text":"有效證據需支持「大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核」。但平均粒徑可能掩蓋少量大聚集物；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching. However, mean particle size hides rare large agglomerates; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨液粒子聚集檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect slurry particle aggregation?","options":["凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據","最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估","大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核"],"optionsEn":["Recess and residue have distinct material evidence","Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment","Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較粒徑分佈尾端與刮傷事件」，因此直接證據是「大粒子異常與刮傷關聯已查核」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均粒徑可能掩蓋少量大聚集物。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare large-particle tails with scratch events; the direct criterion is: Large-particle excursions are checked against scratching. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mean particle size hides rare large agglomerates."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":326,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-325"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-327","title":"研磨液化學狀態","titleEn":"Assess slurry chemical condition","objective":"完成「研磨液化學狀態」的證據判讀，辨識『關聯供液檢測與材料去除選擇性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess slurry chemical condition by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate slurry measurements to material-removal selectivity.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，關聯供液檢測與材料去除選擇性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate slurry measurements to material-removal selectivity. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：化學漂移可改變去除而非僅改變速率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: chemical drift can change selectivity as well as rate. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「化學漂移可改變去除而非僅改變速率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Chemical drift can change selectivity as well as rate. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-327-k1","title":"研磨液化學狀態的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess slurry chemical condition","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「關聯供液檢測與材料去除選擇性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Relate slurry measurements to material-removal selectivity. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-327-k2","title":"研磨液化學狀態的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess slurry chemical condition","text":"有效證據需支持「供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性」。但化學漂移可改變去除而非僅改變速率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample. However, chemical drift can change selectivity as well as rate; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨液化學狀態」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess slurry chemical condition?","options":["供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性","方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說","覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現"],"optionsEn":["Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample","Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis","Coverage differences are reproducible across sections"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「關聯供液檢測與材料去除選擇性」，因此直接證據是「供液狀態與參考樣本具有可比性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：化學漂移可改變去除而非僅改變速率。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate slurry measurements to material-removal selectivity; the direct criterion is: Slurry condition is comparable with the reference sample. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Chemical drift can change selectivity as well as rate."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":327,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-326"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-328","title":"載具分區壓力響應","titleEn":"Assess carrier-zone response","objective":"完成「載具分區壓力響應」的證據判讀，辨識『比較各區調整後的殘膜徑向分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess carrier-zone response by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare radial residual films after zone adjustments.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較各區調整後的殘膜徑向分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare radial residual films after zone adjustments. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：盲目加壓可能把中央問題轉移至邊緣。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: blind pressure increases can move the problem to the edge. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「盲目加壓可能把中央問題轉移至邊緣」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Blind pressure increases can move the problem to the edge. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-328-k1","title":"載具分區壓力響應的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess carrier-zone response","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較各區調整後的殘膜徑向分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare radial residual films after zone adjustments. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-328-k2","title":"載具分區壓力響應的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess carrier-zone response","text":"有效證據需支持「調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致」。但盲目加壓可能把中央問題轉移至邊緣；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes. However, blind pressure increases can move the problem to the edge; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「載具分區壓力響應」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess carrier-zone response?","options":["開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充","調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致","顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷"],"optionsEn":["Interior filling precedes closure of the opening","Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes","Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較各區調整後的殘膜徑向分佈」，因此直接證據是「調整方向與局部殘膜變化一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：盲目加壓可能把中央問題轉移至邊緣。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare radial residual films after zone adjustments; the direct criterion is: Adjustment direction agrees with local residual-film changes. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Blind pressure increases can move the problem to the edge."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":328,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-327"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-329","title":"晶圓邊緣研磨效應","titleEn":"Inspect CMP edge effects","objective":"完成「晶圓邊緣研磨效應」的證據判讀，辨識『量測邊緣排除區內外的殘膜變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect cmp edge effects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure residual films across the edge-exclusion boundary.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量測邊緣排除區內外的殘膜變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure residual films across the edge-exclusion boundary. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the edge model matches the usable die region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：省略邊緣資料會低估實際不均勻度。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: omitting edge data understates nonuniformity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「省略邊緣資料會低估實際不均勻度」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The edge model matches the usable die region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Omitting edge data understates nonuniformity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-329-k1","title":"晶圓邊緣研磨效應的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect cmp edge effects","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「量測邊緣排除區內外的殘膜變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Measure residual films across the edge-exclusion boundary. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-329-k2","title":"晶圓邊緣研磨效應的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect cmp edge effects","text":"有效證據需支持「邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符」。但省略邊緣資料會低估實際不均勻度；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The edge model matches the usable die region. However, omitting edge data understates nonuniformity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓邊緣研磨效應」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect cmp edge effects?","options":["污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯","填充改善與後續收縮均可量測","邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符"],"optionsEn":["Residue morphology correlates with drying locations","Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable","The edge model matches the usable die region"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「量測邊緣排除區內外的殘膜變化」，因此直接證據是「邊緣模型與可用晶粒範圍相符」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：省略邊緣資料會低估實際不均勻度。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure residual films across the edge-exclusion boundary; the direct criterion is: The edge model matches the usable die region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Omitting edge data understates nonuniformity."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":329,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-328"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-330","title":"光學研磨終點訊號","titleEn":"Interpret optical CMP endpoint","objective":"完成「光學研磨終點訊號」的證據判讀，辨識『比較多波段訊號與薄膜轉換位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret optical cmp endpoint by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare multiband signals with film-transition locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較多波段訊號與薄膜轉換位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare multiband signals with film-transition locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: endpoint features match independent thickness measurements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一波長干涉可能產生假終點。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: single-wavelength interference can produce false endpoints. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一波長干涉可能產生假終點」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Single-wavelength interference can produce false endpoints. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-330-k1","title":"光學研磨終點訊號的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret optical cmp endpoint","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較多波段訊號與薄膜轉換位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare multiband signals with film-transition locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-330-k2","title":"光學研磨終點訊號的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret optical cmp endpoint","text":"有效證據需支持「終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應」。但單一波長干涉可能產生假終點；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements. However, single-wavelength interference can produce false endpoints; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「光學研磨終點訊號」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret optical cmp endpoint?","options":["終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應","三者在量測不確定度內相互一致","膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度"],"optionsEn":["Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements","The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty","Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較多波段訊號與薄膜轉換位置」，因此直接證據是「終點特徵可與獨立膜厚量測對應」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一波長干涉可能產生假終點。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare multiband signals with film-transition locations; the direct criterion is: Endpoint features match independent thickness measurements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Single-wavelength interference can produce false endpoints."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":330,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-329"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-331","title":"介電層停止選擇比","titleEn":"Assess dielectric stop selectivity","objective":"完成「介電層停止選擇比」的證據判讀，辨識『對照介電膜與停止層去除曲線』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess dielectric stop selectivity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare removal curves for dielectric and stop layers.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照介電膜與停止層去除曲線。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare removal curves for dielectric and stop layers. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：高主膜速率不代表良好停止能力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: high main-film removal does not imply good stopping. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「高主膜速率不代表良好停止能力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: High main-film removal does not imply good stopping. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-331-k1","title":"介電層停止選擇比的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess dielectric stop selectivity","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「對照介電膜與停止層去除曲線」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare removal curves for dielectric and stop layers. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-331-k2","title":"介電層停止選擇比的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess dielectric stop selectivity","text":"有效證據需支持「停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動」。但高主膜速率不代表良好停止能力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation. However, high main-film removal does not imply good stopping; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電層停止選擇比」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess dielectric stop selectivity?","options":["擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查","停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動","平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離"],"optionsEn":["Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked","Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation","Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照介電膜與停止層去除曲線」，因此直接證據是「停止層保留量可抵抗題定過研磨變動」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：高主膜速率不代表良好停止能力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare removal curves for dielectric and stop layers; the direct criterion is: Retained stop thickness tolerates the stated overpolish variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: High main-film removal does not imply good stopping."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":331,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-330"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-332","title":"圖形密度侵蝕效應","titleEn":"Assess pattern-density erosion","objective":"完成「圖形密度侵蝕效應」的證據判讀，辨識『對照密集與稀疏區的平坦化結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess pattern-density erosion by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare planarization in dense and sparse regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照密集與稀疏區的平坦化結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare planarization in dense and sparse regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: height differences across pattern densities are controlled. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：均勻空白片不能代表圖形晶圓。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a uniform blanket wafer does not represent patterned wafers. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「均勻空白片不能代表圖形晶圓」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Height differences across pattern densities are controlled. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A uniform blanket wafer does not represent patterned wafers. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-332-k1","title":"圖形密度侵蝕效應的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess pattern-density erosion","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「對照密集與稀疏區的平坦化結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare planarization in dense and sparse regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-332-k2","title":"圖形密度侵蝕效應的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess pattern-density erosion","text":"有效證據需支持「跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制」。但均勻空白片不能代表圖形晶圓；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Height differences across pattern densities are controlled. However, a uniform blanket wafer does not represent patterned wafers; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「圖形密度侵蝕效應」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess pattern-density erosion?","options":["最狹窄區與最深區皆列入填充評估","應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設","跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制"],"optionsEn":["Both narrowest and deepest regions enter the fill assessment","Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions","Height differences across pattern densities are controlled"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照密集與稀疏區的平坦化結果」，因此直接證據是「跨圖形密度的高度差均受控制」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：均勻空白片不能代表圖形晶圓。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare planarization in dense and sparse regions; the direct criterion is: Height differences across pattern densities are controlled. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A uniform blanket wafer does not represent patterned wafers."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":332,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-331"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-333","title":"局部凹陷與殘膜區分","titleEn":"Distinguish recess from residual film","objective":"完成「局部凹陷與殘膜區分」的證據判讀，辨識『用高度及材料訊號分辨過研磨與欠研磨』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate distinguish recess from residual film by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use height and material signals to separate overpolish from underpolish.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用高度及材料訊號分辨過研磨與欠研磨。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use height and material signals to separate overpolish from underpolish. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recess and residue have distinct material evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把兩者混為一談會反向調整製程。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: confusing them can reverse the needed correction. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把兩者混為一談會反向調整製程」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recess and residue have distinct material evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Confusing them can reverse the needed correction. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-333-k1","title":"局部凹陷與殘膜區分的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of distinguish recess from residual film","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「用高度及材料訊號分辨過研磨與欠研磨」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Use height and material signals to separate overpolish from underpolish. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-333-k2","title":"局部凹陷與殘膜區分的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for distinguish recess from residual film","text":"有效證據需支持「凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據」。但把兩者混為一談會反向調整製程；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recess and residue have distinct material evidence. However, confusing them can reverse the needed correction; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「局部凹陷與殘膜區分」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for distinguish recess from residual film?","options":["凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據","覆蓋差異能由多位置截面重現","降低電容的收益與強度代價並列"],"optionsEn":["Recess and residue have distinct material evidence","Coverage differences are reproducible across sections","Capacitance benefit and strength cost are considered together"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「用高度及材料訊號分辨過研磨與欠研磨」，因此直接證據是「凹陷與殘留對應不同的材料證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把兩者混為一談會反向調整製程。","explanationEn":"The task is to use height and material signals to separate overpolish from underpolish; the direct criterion is: Recess and residue have distinct material evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Confusing them can reverse the needed correction."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":333,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-332"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-334","title":"CMP 刮傷方向分析","titleEn":"Analyze CMP scratch direction","objective":"完成「CMP 刮傷方向分析」的證據判讀，辨識『把刮傷方向與墊面運動軌跡對照』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate analyze cmp scratch direction by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare scratch orientation with pad motion tracks.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把刮傷方向與墊面運動軌跡對照。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare scratch orientation with pad motion tracks. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：孤立粒子與連續刮痕不應共用診斷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: isolated particles and continuous scratches need different diagnoses. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「孤立粒子與連續刮痕不應共用診斷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Isolated particles and continuous scratches need different diagnoses. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-334-k1","title":"CMP 刮傷方向分析的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of analyze cmp scratch direction","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「把刮傷方向與墊面運動軌跡對照」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare scratch orientation with pad motion tracks. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-334-k2","title":"CMP 刮傷方向分析的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for analyze cmp scratch direction","text":"有效證據需支持「方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說」。但孤立粒子與連續刮痕不應共用診斷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis. However, isolated particles and continuous scratches need different diagnoses; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「CMP 刮傷方向分析」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for analyze cmp scratch direction?","options":["收縮量與材料轉變相互對應","方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說","開口閉合前內部空間已充分填充"],"optionsEn":["Shrinkage corresponds to the material transformation","Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis","Interior filling precedes closure of the opening"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「把刮傷方向與墊面運動軌跡對照」，因此直接證據是「方向與缺陷形貌支持一致的來源假說」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：孤立粒子與連續刮痕不應共用診斷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare scratch orientation with pad motion tracks; the direct criterion is: Orientation and morphology support a consistent source hypothesis. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Isolated particles and continuous scratches need different diagnoses."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":334,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-333"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-335","title":"研磨後刷洗殘粒","titleEn":"Inspect post-CMP brush-clean residues","objective":"完成「研磨後刷洗殘粒」的證據判讀，辨識『比較清洗前後顆粒地圖與膜損傷』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect post-cmp brush-clean residues by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare particle maps and film damage before and after cleaning.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較清洗前後顆粒地圖與膜損傷。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare particle maps and film damage before and after cleaning. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: particles decrease without added fragile-film damage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：更強刷洗可能增加機械傷害。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: more aggressive brushing can increase mechanical damage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「更強刷洗可能增加機械傷害」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: More aggressive brushing can increase mechanical damage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-335-k1","title":"研磨後刷洗殘粒的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect post-cmp brush-clean residues","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「比較清洗前後顆粒地圖與膜損傷」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare particle maps and film damage before and after cleaning. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-335-k2","title":"研磨後刷洗殘粒的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect post-cmp brush-clean residues","text":"有效證據需支持「顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷」。但更強刷洗可能增加機械傷害；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage. However, more aggressive brushing can increase mechanical damage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨後刷洗殘粒」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect post-cmp brush-clean residues?","options":["填充改善與後續收縮均可量測","環境歷程與膜性質變化可追溯","顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷"],"optionsEn":["Fill improvement and later shrinkage are both measurable","Environmental history tracks property changes","Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較清洗前後顆粒地圖與膜損傷」，因此直接證據是「顆粒減少未增加薄弱膜損傷」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：更強刷洗可能增加機械傷害。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare particle maps and film damage before and after cleaning; the direct criterion is: Particles decrease without added fragile-film damage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: More aggressive brushing can increase mechanical damage."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":335,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-334"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-336","title":"乾燥水痕辨識","titleEn":"Identify post-clean drying marks","objective":"完成「乾燥水痕辨識」的證據判讀，辨識『分辨環狀水痕與研磨殘粒形貌』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify post-clean drying marks by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish ring-shaped drying marks from cmp particles.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分辨環狀水痕與研磨殘粒形貌。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish ring-shaped drying marks from CMP particles. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: residue morphology correlates with drying locations. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：水痕可能被誤判為原始沉積缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: drying marks may be mistaken for deposition defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「水痕可能被誤判為原始沉積缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Residue morphology correlates with drying locations. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Drying marks may be mistaken for deposition defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-336-k1","title":"乾燥水痕辨識的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify post-clean drying marks","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「分辨環狀水痕與研磨殘粒形貌」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish ring-shaped drying marks from CMP particles. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-336-k2","title":"乾燥水痕辨識的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify post-clean drying marks","text":"有效證據需支持「污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯」。但水痕可能被誤判為原始沉積缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Residue morphology correlates with drying locations. However, drying marks may be mistaken for deposition defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「乾燥水痕辨識」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify post-clean drying marks?","options":["污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯","膜質判讀不僅依賴沉積厚度","待去除高度與保留層位置清楚分離"],"optionsEn":["Residue morphology correlates with drying locations","Film quality is assessed beyond deposited thickness","Removal height is separated from layers that must remain"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「分辨環狀水痕與研磨殘粒形貌」，因此直接證據是「污染形貌與乾燥位置具有一致關聯」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：水痕可能被誤判為原始沉積缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish ring-shaped drying marks from CMP particles; the direct criterion is: Residue morphology correlates with drying locations. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Drying marks may be mistaken for deposition defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":336,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-335"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-337","title":"平坦化後膜厚閉合","titleEn":"Close the post-CMP thickness balance","objective":"完成「平坦化後膜厚閉合」的證據判讀，辨識『對照初始膜厚、去除量與最終殘膜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate close the post-cmp thickness balance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare initial film, removed amount and final residual film.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照初始膜厚、去除量與最終殘膜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare initial film, removed amount and final residual film. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：三者在量測不確定度內相互一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不閉合提示量測模型或材料變化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: nonclosure suggests model error or material change. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「三者在量測不確定度內相互一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不閉合提示量測模型或材料變化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Nonclosure suggests model error or material change. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-337-k1","title":"平坦化後膜厚閉合的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of close the post-cmp thickness balance","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「對照初始膜厚、去除量與最終殘膜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Compare initial film, removed amount and final residual film. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-337-k2","title":"平坦化後膜厚閉合的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for close the post-cmp thickness balance","text":"有效證據需支持「三者在量測不確定度內相互一致」。但不閉合提示量測模型或材料變化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty. However, nonclosure suggests model error or material change; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「平坦化後膜厚閉合」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for close the post-cmp thickness balance?","options":["墊面狀態變化可解釋速率變化","三者在量測不確定度內相互一致","擬合殘差與參數相關性均受檢查"],"optionsEn":["Pad-condition changes explain rate variation","The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty","Fit residuals and parameter correlations are checked"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照初始膜厚、去除量與最終殘膜」，因此直接證據是「三者在量測不確定度內相互一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不閉合提示量測模型或材料變化。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare initial film, removed amount and final residual film; the direct criterion is: The three quantities agree within measurement uncertainty. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Nonclosure suggests model error or material change."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":337,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-336"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-338","title":"介電隔離與平坦度放行","titleEn":"Release dielectric isolation and planarity","objective":"完成「介電隔離與平坦度放行」的證據判讀，辨識『整合高度圖、漏電與機械缺陷證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release dielectric isolation and planarity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine height maps, leakage and mechanical-defect evidence.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，整合高度圖、漏電與機械缺陷證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine height maps, leakage and mechanical-defect evidence. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面平坦不能保證介電膜無損傷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a flat surface does not prove an undamaged dielectric. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面平坦不能保證介電膜無損傷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A flat surface does not prove an undamaged dielectric. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-338-k1","title":"介電隔離與平坦度放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release dielectric isolation and planarity","text":"介電膜必須同時提供隔離、機械支撐與可加工性；CMP 的去除速率與圖形密度、膜材及接觸狀態相互耦合。 本題具體操作為「整合高度圖、漏電與機械缺陷證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Dielectrics provide isolation, mechanical support and process compatibility; CMP removal couples material, pattern density and pad contact. Here the concrete task is: Combine height maps, leakage and mechanical-defect evidence. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-338-k2","title":"介電隔離與平坦度放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release dielectric isolation and planarity","text":"有效證據需支持「平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離」。但表面平坦不能保證介電膜無損傷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation. However, a flat surface does not prove an undamaged dielectric; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電隔離與平坦度放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release dielectric isolation and planarity?","options":["應力推估使用相同基板與幾何假設","修整覆蓋與墊面磨耗分佈相容","平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離"],"optionsEn":["Stress inference uses consistent substrate and geometry assumptions","Conditioning coverage matches pad-wear distribution","Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「整合高度圖、漏電與機械缺陷證據」，因此直接證據是「平坦化改善未犧牲電氣隔離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面平坦不能保證介電膜無損傷。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine height maps, leakage and mechanical-defect evidence; the direct criterion is: Planarization improvement preserves electrical isolation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A flat surface does not prove an undamaged dielectric."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-cmp","scb-interconnect"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":338,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-337"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":13},{"id":"sc-m14","title":"鑲嵌式互連圖形與蝕刻","titleEn":"Damascene interconnect patterning and etch","description":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-339","title":"互連層與網路對照","titleEn":"Map interconnect levels to nets","objective":"完成「互連層與網路對照」的證據判讀，辨識『把示意金屬層、導通孔與電路節點逐一對照』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map interconnect levels to nets by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map model metal levels and vias to circuit nodes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把示意金屬層、導通孔與電路節點逐一對照。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map model metal levels and vias to circuit nodes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：層號正確仍可能連到錯誤網路。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a correct layer number can still connect the wrong net. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「層號正確仍可能連到錯誤網路」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A correct layer number can still connect the wrong net. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-339-k1","title":"互連層與網路對照的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map interconnect levels to nets","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「把示意金屬層、導通孔與電路節點逐一對照」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Map model metal levels and vias to circuit nodes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-339-k2","title":"互連層與網路對照的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map interconnect levels to nets","text":"有效證據需支持「每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點」。但層號正確仍可能連到錯誤網路；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint. However, a correct layer number can still connect the wrong net; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「互連層與網路對照」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map interconnect levels to nets?","options":["每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點","孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失","孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積"],"optionsEn":["Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint","The bottom is open without excessive edge loss","Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把示意金屬層、導通孔與電路節點逐一對照」，因此直接證據是「每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：層號正確仍可能連到錯誤網路。","explanationEn":"The task is to map model metal levels and vias to circuit nodes; the direct criterion is: Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A correct layer number can still connect the wrong net."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":339,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-338"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-340","title":"先孔後槽路線選擇","titleEn":"Select a via-first branch","objective":"完成「先孔後槽路線選擇」的證據判讀，辨識『排列先孔後槽的遮罩與保護層示意』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate select a via-first branch by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: arrange masks and protection layers for a via-first model.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，排列先孔後槽的遮罩與保護層示意。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, arrange masks and protection layers for a via-first model. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: vias remain protected during trench patterning. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：省略保護會使孔底受二次攻擊。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: missing protection exposes via bottoms to additional attack. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「省略保護會使孔底受二次攻擊」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Vias remain protected during trench patterning. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Missing protection exposes via bottoms to additional attack. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-340-k1","title":"先孔後槽路線選擇的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of select a via-first branch","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「排列先孔後槽的遮罩與保護層示意」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Arrange masks and protection layers for a via-first model. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-340-k2","title":"先孔後槽路線選擇的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for select a via-first branch","text":"有效證據需支持「導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護」。但省略保護會使孔底受二次攻擊；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Vias remain protected during trench patterning. However, missing protection exposes via bottoms to additional attack; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「先孔後槽路線選擇」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for select a via-first branch?","options":["兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度","導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護","圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化"],"optionsEn":["Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions","Vias remain protected during trench patterning","Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「排列先孔後槽的遮罩與保護層示意」，因此直接證據是「導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：省略保護會使孔底受二次攻擊。","explanationEn":"The task is to arrange masks and protection layers for a via-first model; the direct criterion is: Vias remain protected during trench patterning. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Missing protection exposes via bottoms to additional attack."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":340,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-339"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-341","title":"先槽後孔路線選擇","titleEn":"Select a trench-first branch","objective":"完成「先槽後孔路線選擇」的證據判讀，辨識『排列先槽後孔的對準與底部開口步驟』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate select a trench-first branch by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: arrange alignment and bottom opening in a trench-first model.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，排列先槽後孔的對準與底部開口步驟。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, arrange alignment and bottom opening in a trench-first model. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: vias land within the permitted trench region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：套刻裕量不足可能造成孔槽失配。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: insufficient overlay margin can misregister trench and via. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「套刻裕量不足可能造成孔槽失配」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Vias land within the permitted trench region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Insufficient overlay margin can misregister trench and via. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-341-k1","title":"先槽後孔路線選擇的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of select a trench-first branch","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「排列先槽後孔的對準與底部開口步驟」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Arrange alignment and bottom opening in a trench-first model. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-341-k2","title":"先槽後孔路線選擇的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for select a trench-first branch","text":"有效證據需支持「導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區」。但套刻裕量不足可能造成孔槽失配；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Vias land within the permitted trench region. However, insufficient overlay margin can misregister trench and via; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「先槽後孔路線選擇」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for select a trench-first branch?","options":["孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容","遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性","導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區"],"optionsEn":["Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling","The mask remains intact until trench formation completes","Vias land within the permitted trench region"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「排列先槽後孔的對準與底部開口步驟」，因此直接證據是「導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：套刻裕量不足可能造成孔槽失配。","explanationEn":"The task is to arrange alignment and bottom opening in a trench-first model; the direct criterion is: Vias land within the permitted trench region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Insufficient overlay margin can misregister trench and via."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":341,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-340"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-342","title":"硬遮罩堆疊識別","titleEn":"Identify the hardmask stack","objective":"完成「硬遮罩堆疊識別」的證據判讀，辨識『把圖形轉移層與最終介電膜分開標示』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify the hardmask stack by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate pattern-transfer layers from final dielectric.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把圖形轉移層與最終介電膜分開標示。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate pattern-transfer layers from final dielectric. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：混淆遮罩與介電膜會誤判去除順序。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: confusing masks and dielectric leads to incorrect removal order. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「混淆遮罩與介電膜會誤判去除順序」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Confusing masks and dielectric leads to incorrect removal order. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-342-k1","title":"硬遮罩堆疊識別的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify the hardmask stack","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「把圖形轉移層與最終介電膜分開標示」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Separate pattern-transfer layers from final dielectric. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-342-k2","title":"硬遮罩堆疊識別的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify the hardmask stack","text":"有效證據需支持「每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明」。但混淆遮罩與介電膜會誤判去除順序；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer. However, confusing masks and dielectric leads to incorrect removal order; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「硬遮罩堆疊識別」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify the hardmask stack?","options":["每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明","尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限","溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求"],"optionsEn":["Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer","Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded","Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把圖形轉移層與最終介電膜分開標示」，因此直接證據是「每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：混淆遮罩與介電膜會誤判去除順序。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate pattern-transfer layers from final dielectric; the direct criterion is: Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Confusing masks and dielectric leads to incorrect removal order."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":342,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-341"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-343","title":"底部蝕刻停止層定位","titleEn":"Locate the bottom etch stop","objective":"完成「底部蝕刻停止層定位」的證據判讀，辨識『在多層截面找出下層金屬上的保護層』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate locate the bottom etch stop by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: locate protection above the lower metal in a multilayer section.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在多層截面找出下層金屬上的保護層。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, locate protection above the lower metal in a multilayer section. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：看不清停止層容易接受金屬損傷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: an unresolved stop layer can conceal metal damage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「看不清停止層容易接受金屬損傷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: An unresolved stop layer can conceal metal damage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-343-k1","title":"底部蝕刻停止層定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of locate the bottom etch stop","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「在多層截面找出下層金屬上的保護層」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Locate protection above the lower metal in a multilayer section. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-343-k2","title":"底部蝕刻停止層定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for locate the bottom etch stop","text":"有效證據需支持「開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔」。但看不清停止層容易接受金屬損傷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor. However, an unresolved stop layer can conceal metal damage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「底部蝕刻停止層定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for locate the bottom etch stop?","options":["交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋","開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔","孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽"],"optionsEn":["Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners","The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor","Bottom corners lack unintended grooves"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「在多層截面找出下層金屬上的保護層」，因此直接證據是「開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：看不清停止層容易接受金屬損傷。","explanationEn":"The task is to locate protection above the lower metal in a multilayer section; the direct criterion is: The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: An unresolved stop layer can conceal metal damage."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":343,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-342"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-344","title":"孔層抗反射模型","titleEn":"Assess via-layer antireflection","objective":"完成「孔層抗反射模型」的證據判讀，辨識『比較反射模型與導通孔尺寸變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess via-layer antireflection by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare reflection models with via-size variation.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較反射模型與導通孔尺寸變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare reflection models with via-size variation. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只調曝光可能掩蓋膜堆疊反射差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: exposure-only adjustments can conceal stack-reflection differences. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只調曝光可能掩蓋膜堆疊反射差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Exposure-only adjustments can conceal stack-reflection differences. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-344-k1","title":"孔層抗反射模型的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess via-layer antireflection","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較反射模型與導通孔尺寸變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare reflection models with via-size variation. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-344-k2","title":"孔層抗反射模型的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess via-layer antireflection","text":"有效證據需支持「反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋」。但只調曝光可能掩蓋膜堆疊反射差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation. However, exposure-only adjustments can conceal stack-reflection differences; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「孔層抗反射模型」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess via-layer antireflection?","options":["保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除","殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退","反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋"],"optionsEn":["Protection covers the bottom and remains removable","Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession","Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較反射模型與導通孔尺寸變化」，因此直接證據是「反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只調曝光可能掩蓋膜堆疊反射差。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare reflection models with via-size variation; the direct criterion is: Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Exposure-only adjustments can conceal stack-reflection differences."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":344,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-343"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-345","title":"導通孔曝光焦距裕量","titleEn":"Evaluate via focus margin","objective":"完成「導通孔曝光焦距裕量」的證據判讀，辨識『比較焦距掃描樣本的孔形輪廓』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate via focus margin by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare via profiles across a focus-sweep sample set.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較焦距掃描樣本的孔形輪廓。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare via profiles across a focus-sweep sample set. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一最佳焦點不代表可量產窗口。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one best-focus image does not establish a production window. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一最佳焦點不代表可量產窗口」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One best-focus image does not establish a production window. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-345-k1","title":"導通孔曝光焦距裕量的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate via focus margin","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較焦距掃描樣本的孔形輪廓」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare via profiles across a focus-sweep sample set. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-345-k2","title":"導通孔曝光焦距裕量的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate via focus margin","text":"有效證據需支持「可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容」。但單一最佳焦點不代表可量產窗口；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range. However, one best-focus image does not establish a production window; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔曝光焦距裕量」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate via focus margin?","options":["可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容","孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積","損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range","Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area","Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較焦距掃描樣本的孔形輪廓」，因此直接證據是「可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一最佳焦點不代表可量產窗口。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare via profiles across a focus-sweep sample set; the direct criterion is: Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One best-focus image does not establish a production window."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":345,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-344"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-346","title":"導通孔殘膜辨識","titleEn":"Identify via scum","objective":"完成「導通孔殘膜辨識」的證據判讀，辨識『檢視顯影後孔底殘膜與開口尺寸』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify via scum by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect post-develop bottom scum and opening dimensions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢視顯影後孔底殘膜與開口尺寸。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect post-develop bottom scum and opening dimensions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the bottom is open without excessive edge loss. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面開孔可能仍被薄殘膜封住。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: an apparent opening may retain a thin blocking film. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面開孔可能仍被薄殘膜封住」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The bottom is open without excessive edge loss. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: An apparent opening may retain a thin blocking film. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-346-k1","title":"導通孔殘膜辨識的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify via scum","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「檢視顯影後孔底殘膜與開口尺寸」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Inspect post-develop bottom scum and opening dimensions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-346-k2","title":"導通孔殘膜辨識的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify via scum","text":"有效證據需支持「孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失」。但表面開孔可能仍被薄殘膜封住；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The bottom is open without excessive edge loss. However, an apparent opening may retain a thin blocking film; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔殘膜辨識」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify via scum?","options":["接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控","孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失","兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度"],"optionsEn":["The landing is open with controlled metal loss","The bottom is open without excessive edge loss","Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢視顯影後孔底殘膜與開口尺寸」，因此直接證據是「孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面開孔可能仍被薄殘膜封住。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect post-develop bottom scum and opening dimensions; the direct criterion is: The bottom is open without excessive edge loss. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: An apparent opening may retain a thin blocking film."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":346,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-345"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-347","title":"導通孔硬遮罩轉移","titleEn":"Transfer the via hardmask","objective":"完成「導通孔硬遮罩轉移」的證據判讀，辨識『比較光阻孔形與硬遮罩孔形』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate transfer the via hardmask by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare resist openings with transferred hardmask openings.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較光阻孔形與硬遮罩孔形。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare resist openings with transferred hardmask openings. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只量最上層不能追蹤轉移損失。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: top-layer measurements cannot track transfer loss. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只量最上層不能追蹤轉移損失」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Top-layer measurements cannot track transfer loss. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-347-k1","title":"導通孔硬遮罩轉移的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of transfer the via hardmask","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較光阻孔形與硬遮罩孔形」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare resist openings with transferred hardmask openings. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-347-k2","title":"導通孔硬遮罩轉移的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for transfer the via hardmask","text":"有效證據需支持「圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化」。但只量最上層不能追蹤轉移損失；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers. However, top-layer measurements cannot track transfer loss; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔硬遮罩轉移」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for transfer the via hardmask?","options":["遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性","暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型","圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化"],"optionsEn":["The mask remains intact until trench formation completes","Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model","Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較光阻孔形與硬遮罩孔形」，因此直接證據是「圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只量最上層不能追蹤轉移損失。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare resist openings with transferred hardmask openings; the direct criterion is: Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Top-layer measurements cannot track transfer loss."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":347,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-346"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-348","title":"導通孔側壁角度","titleEn":"Measure via sidewall angle","objective":"完成「導通孔側壁角度」的證據判讀，辨識『從截面分離垂直、錐形與弓形輪廓』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure via sidewall angle by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate vertical, tapered and bowed via profiles.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從截面分離垂直、錐形與弓形輪廓。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate vertical, tapered and bowed via profiles. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：弓形側壁可增加局部薄襯層風險。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: bowed sidewalls can increase local liner-thinning risk. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「弓形側壁可增加局部薄襯層風險」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Bowed sidewalls can increase local liner-thinning risk. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-348-k1","title":"導通孔側壁角度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure via sidewall angle","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「從截面分離垂直、錐形與弓形輪廓」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Separate vertical, tapered and bowed via profiles. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-348-k2","title":"導通孔側壁角度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure via sidewall angle","text":"有效證據需支持「孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容」。但弓形側壁可增加局部薄襯層風險；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling. However, bowed sidewalls can increase local liner-thinning risk; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔側壁角度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure via sidewall angle?","options":["孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容","溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求","導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通"],"optionsEn":["Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling","Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs","Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「從截面分離垂直、錐形與弓形輪廓」，因此直接證據是「孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：弓形側壁可增加局部薄襯層風險。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate vertical, tapered and bowed via profiles; the direct criterion is: Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Bowed sidewalls can increase local liner-thinning risk."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":348,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-347"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-349","title":"深孔蝕刻滯後","titleEn":"Assess aspect-ratio-dependent etch lag","objective":"完成「深孔蝕刻滯後」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同孔寬的實際蝕刻深度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess aspect-ratio-dependent etch lag by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare etched depth across different via widths.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同孔寬的實際蝕刻深度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare etched depth across different via widths. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：大孔到達終點不代表小孔已開通。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: large-via endpoint does not prove small vias are open. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「大孔到達終點不代表小孔已開通」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Large-via endpoint does not prove small vias are open. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-349-k1","title":"深孔蝕刻滯後的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess aspect-ratio-dependent etch lag","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較不同孔寬的實際蝕刻深度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare etched depth across different via widths. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-349-k2","title":"深孔蝕刻滯後的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess aspect-ratio-dependent etch lag","text":"有效證據需支持「尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限」。但大孔到達終點不代表小孔已開通；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded. However, large-via endpoint does not prove small vias are open; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「深孔蝕刻滯後」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess aspect-ratio-dependent etch lag?","options":["最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求","尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限","交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs","Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded","Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同孔寬的實際蝕刻深度」，因此直接證據是「尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：大孔到達終點不代表小孔已開通。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare etched depth across different via widths; the direct criterion is: Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Large-via endpoint does not prove small vias are open."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":349,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-348"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-350","title":"導通孔底部微溝","titleEn":"Inspect via-bottom microtrenching","objective":"完成「導通孔底部微溝」的證據判讀，辨識『在孔底角落尋找局部加深特徵』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect via-bottom microtrenching by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: look for localized deepening at via-bottom corners.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在孔底角落尋找局部加深特徵。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, look for localized deepening at via-bottom corners. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bottom corners lack unintended grooves. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：局部微溝可能被中央深度值掩蓋。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a central depth value can hide corner microtrenches. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「局部微溝可能被中央深度值掩蓋」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bottom corners lack unintended grooves. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A central depth value can hide corner microtrenches. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-350-k1","title":"導通孔底部微溝的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect via-bottom microtrenching","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「在孔底角落尋找局部加深特徵」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Look for localized deepening at via-bottom corners. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-350-k2","title":"導通孔底部微溝的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect via-bottom microtrenching","text":"有效證據需支持「孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽」。但局部微溝可能被中央深度值掩蓋；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bottom corners lack unintended grooves. However, a central depth value can hide corner microtrenches; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔底部微溝」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect via-bottom microtrenching?","options":["殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退","修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站","孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽"],"optionsEn":["Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession","Correction targets the station producing the bias","Bottom corners lack unintended grooves"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「在孔底角落尋找局部加深特徵」，因此直接證據是「孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：局部微溝可能被中央深度值掩蓋。","explanationEn":"The task is to look for localized deepening at via-bottom corners; the direct criterion is: Bottom corners lack unintended grooves. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A central depth value can hide corner microtrenches."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":350,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-349"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-351","title":"孔內犧牲填充","titleEn":"Assess sacrificial via fill","objective":"完成「孔內犧牲填充」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤孔內保護填料的高度與空隙』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess sacrificial via fill by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: track protective via-fill height and voids.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤孔內保護填料的高度與空隙。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, track protective via-fill height and voids. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: protection covers the bottom and remains removable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：填料空洞使孔底仍暴露於槽蝕刻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: fill voids leave via bottoms exposed during trench etch. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「填料空洞使孔底仍暴露於槽蝕刻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Protection covers the bottom and remains removable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Fill voids leave via bottoms exposed during trench etch. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-351-k1","title":"孔內犧牲填充的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess sacrificial via fill","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「追蹤孔內保護填料的高度與空隙」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Track protective via-fill height and voids. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-351-k2","title":"孔內犧牲填充的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess sacrificial via fill","text":"有效證據需支持「保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除」。但填料空洞使孔底仍暴露於槽蝕刻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Protection covers the bottom and remains removable. However, fill voids leave via bottoms exposed during trench etch; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「孔內犧牲填充」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess sacrificial via fill?","options":["保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除","損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證","空腔可填充且接觸面可用"],"optionsEn":["Protection covers the bottom and remains removable","Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence","Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤孔內保護填料的高度與空隙」，因此直接證據是「保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：填料空洞使孔底仍暴露於槽蝕刻。","explanationEn":"The task is to track protective via-fill height and voids; the direct criterion is: Protection covers the bottom and remains removable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Fill voids leave via bottoms exposed during trench etch."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":351,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-350"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-352","title":"溝槽光罩與孔套刻","titleEn":"Align trench masks to vias","objective":"完成「溝槽光罩與孔套刻」的證據判讀，辨識『比較溝槽中心線與導通孔位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate align trench masks to vias by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare trench centerlines and via positions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較溝槽中心線與導通孔位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare trench centerlines and via positions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：中心套刻正常仍可能有場內旋轉誤差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: good center overlay can hide intrafield rotation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「中心套刻正常仍可能有場內旋轉誤差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Good center overlay can hide intrafield rotation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-352-k1","title":"溝槽光罩與孔套刻的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of align trench masks to vias","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較溝槽中心線與導通孔位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare trench centerlines and via positions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-352-k2","title":"溝槽光罩與孔套刻的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for align trench masks to vias","text":"有效證據需支持「孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積」。但中心套刻正常仍可能有場內旋轉誤差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area. However, good center overlay can hide intrafield rotation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「溝槽光罩與孔套刻」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for align trench masks to vias?","options":["每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點","孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積","接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控"],"optionsEn":["Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint","Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area","The landing is open with controlled metal loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較溝槽中心線與導通孔位置」，因此直接證據是「孔槽重疊保留題定連接面積」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：中心套刻正常仍可能有場內旋轉誤差。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare trench centerlines and via positions; the direct criterion is: Trench–via overlap preserves the stated connection area. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Good center overlay can hide intrafield rotation."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":352,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-351"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-353","title":"溝槽線寬與線距","titleEn":"Measure trench width and spacing","objective":"完成「溝槽線寬與線距」的證據判讀，辨識『在密集與孤立線分別量取線槽尺寸』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure trench width and spacing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure dense and isolated trench patterns separately.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在密集與孤立線分別量取線槽尺寸。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure dense and isolated trench patterns separately. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：孤立線合格不能代表密集線不橋接。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: passing isolated lines does not exclude dense-pattern bridging. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「孤立線合格不能代表密集線不橋接」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Passing isolated lines does not exclude dense-pattern bridging. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-353-k1","title":"溝槽線寬與線距的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure trench width and spacing","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「在密集與孤立線分別量取線槽尺寸」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Measure dense and isolated trench patterns separately. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-353-k2","title":"溝槽線寬與線距的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure trench width and spacing","text":"有效證據需支持「兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度」。但孤立線合格不能代表密集線不橋接；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions. However, passing isolated lines does not exclude dense-pattern bridging; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「溝槽線寬與線距」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure trench width and spacing?","options":["暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型","導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護","兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度"],"optionsEn":["Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model","Vias remain protected during trench patterning","Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「在密集與孤立線分別量取線槽尺寸」，因此直接證據是「兩類圖形皆符合各自的題定尺度」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：孤立線合格不能代表密集線不橋接。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure dense and isolated trench patterns separately; the direct criterion is: Both pattern types meet their respective exercise dimensions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Passing isolated lines does not exclude dense-pattern bridging."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":353,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-352"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-354","title":"溝槽硬遮罩選擇性","titleEn":"Assess trench hardmask selectivity","objective":"完成「溝槽硬遮罩選擇性」的證據判讀，辨識『比較溝槽刻深與遮罩剩餘厚度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess trench hardmask selectivity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare trench depth and remaining mask thickness.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較溝槽刻深與遮罩剩餘厚度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare trench depth and remaining mask thickness. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the mask remains intact until trench formation completes. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過早消耗遮罩會放大線寬偏差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: premature mask loss increases linewidth bias. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過早消耗遮罩會放大線寬偏差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The mask remains intact until trench formation completes. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Premature mask loss increases linewidth bias. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-354-k1","title":"溝槽硬遮罩選擇性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess trench hardmask selectivity","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較溝槽刻深與遮罩剩餘厚度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare trench depth and remaining mask thickness. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-354-k2","title":"溝槽硬遮罩選擇性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess trench hardmask selectivity","text":"有效證據需支持「遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性」。但過早消耗遮罩會放大線寬偏差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The mask remains intact until trench formation completes. However, premature mask loss increases linewidth bias; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「溝槽硬遮罩選擇性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess trench hardmask selectivity?","options":["遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性","導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通","導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區"],"optionsEn":["The mask remains intact until trench formation completes","Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry","Vias land within the permitted trench region"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較溝槽刻深與遮罩剩餘厚度」，因此直接證據是「遮罩在溝槽成形前仍保有完整性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過早消耗遮罩會放大線寬偏差。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare trench depth and remaining mask thickness; the direct criterion is: The mask remains intact until trench formation completes. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Premature mask loss increases linewidth bias."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":354,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-353"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-355","title":"溝槽深度終點","titleEn":"Determine trench-depth endpoint","objective":"完成「溝槽深度終點」的證據判讀，辨識『對照截面深度與示意終點訊號』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate determine trench-depth endpoint by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare sectional depth and model endpoint signals.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照截面深度與示意終點訊號。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare sectional depth and model endpoint signals. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只追求深槽可能增加寄生電容。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: deeper trenches can increase parasitic capacitance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只追求深槽可能增加寄生電容」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Deeper trenches can increase parasitic capacitance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-355-k1","title":"溝槽深度終點的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of determine trench-depth endpoint","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「對照截面深度與示意終點訊號」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare sectional depth and model endpoint signals. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-355-k2","title":"溝槽深度終點的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for determine trench-depth endpoint","text":"有效證據需支持「溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求」。但只追求深槽可能增加寄生電容；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs. However, deeper trenches can increase parasitic capacitance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「溝槽深度終點」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for determine trench-depth endpoint?","options":["每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明","溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求","最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求"],"optionsEn":["Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer","Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs","The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照截面深度與示意終點訊號」，因此直接證據是「溝槽深度保留介電隔離與導體截面需求」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只追求深槽可能增加寄生電容。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare sectional depth and model endpoint signals; the direct criterion is: Trench depth preserves insulation and conductor cross-section needs. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Deeper trenches can increase parasitic capacitance."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":355,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-354"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-356","title":"孔槽交會肩部輪廓","titleEn":"Inspect trench–via shoulder profiles","objective":"完成「孔槽交會肩部輪廓」的證據判讀，辨識『檢視孔槽交會處的尖角與肩部殘留』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect trench–via shoulder profiles by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect sharp corners and shoulder residue at trench–via intersections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢視孔槽交會處的尖角與肩部殘留。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect sharp corners and shoulder residue at trench–via intersections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：肩部殘留可能縮小有效導通截面。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: shoulder residue can reduce effective conduction area. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「肩部殘留可能縮小有效導通截面」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Shoulder residue can reduce effective conduction area. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-356-k1","title":"孔槽交會肩部輪廓的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect trench–via shoulder profiles","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「檢視孔槽交會處的尖角與肩部殘留」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Inspect sharp corners and shoulder residue at trench–via intersections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-356-k2","title":"孔槽交會肩部輪廓的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect trench–via shoulder profiles","text":"有效證據需支持「交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋」。但肩部殘留可能縮小有效導通截面；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners. However, shoulder residue can reduce effective conduction area; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「孔槽交會肩部輪廓」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect trench–via shoulder profiles?","options":["修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站","開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔","交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Correction targets the station producing the bias","The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor","Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢視孔槽交會處的尖角與肩部殘留」，因此直接證據是「交會幾何允許後續襯層連續覆蓋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：肩部殘留可能縮小有效導通截面。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect sharp corners and shoulder residue at trench–via intersections; the direct criterion is: Junction geometry permits continuous subsequent liners. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Shoulder residue can reduce effective conduction area."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":356,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-355"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-357","title":"蝕刻後聚合殘留","titleEn":"Inspect post-etch polymer residue","objective":"完成「蝕刻後聚合殘留」的證據判讀，辨識『區分側壁保護膜與應移除殘留』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect post-etch polymer residue by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish protective sidewall films from unwanted residue.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分側壁保護膜與應移除殘留。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish protective sidewall films from unwanted residue. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：殘膜與過度清洗都可損害填充。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: residue and excessive cleaning can both impair filling. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「殘膜與過度清洗都可損害填充」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Residue and excessive cleaning can both impair filling. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-357-k1","title":"蝕刻後聚合殘留的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect post-etch polymer residue","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「區分側壁保護膜與應移除殘留」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish protective sidewall films from unwanted residue. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-357-k2","title":"蝕刻後聚合殘留的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect post-etch polymer residue","text":"有效證據需支持「殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退」。但殘膜與過度清洗都可損害填充；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession. However, residue and excessive cleaning can both impair filling; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「蝕刻後聚合殘留」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect post-etch polymer residue?","options":["殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退","空腔可填充且接觸面可用","反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋"],"optionsEn":["Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession","Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable","Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分側壁保護膜與應移除殘留」，因此直接證據是「殘留清除不使介電側壁明顯後退」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：殘膜與過度清洗都可損害填充。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish protective sidewall films from unwanted residue; the direct criterion is: Residue removal avoids substantial dielectric recession. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Residue and excessive cleaning can both impair filling."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":357,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-356"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-358","title":"低介電膜電漿損傷","titleEn":"Assess plasma damage to low-k films","objective":"完成「低介電膜電漿損傷」的證據判讀，辨識『比較表層化學與介電特性變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess plasma damage to low-k films by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare surface chemistry and dielectric-property changes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較表層化學與介電特性變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare surface chemistry and dielectric-property changes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：外觀正常不表示孔隙結構未改變。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: normal appearance does not imply unchanged porosity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「外觀正常不表示孔隙結構未改變」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Normal appearance does not imply unchanged porosity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-358-k1","title":"低介電膜電漿損傷的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess plasma damage to low-k films","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較表層化學與介電特性變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare surface chemistry and dielectric-property changes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-358-k2","title":"低介電膜電漿損傷的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess plasma damage to low-k films","text":"有效證據需支持「損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證」。但外觀正常不表示孔隙結構未改變；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence. However, normal appearance does not imply unchanged porosity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「低介電膜電漿損傷」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess plasma damage to low-k films?","options":["可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容","損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證","每個跨層連接具有明確的起點與終點"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range","Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence","Each interlevel connection has a defined start and endpoint"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較表層化學與介電特性變化」，因此直接證據是「損傷深度與電容變化有獨立佐證」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：外觀正常不表示孔隙結構未改變。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare surface chemistry and dielectric-property changes; the direct criterion is: Damage depth and capacitance change have independent evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Normal appearance does not imply unchanged porosity."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":358,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-357"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-359","title":"停止層最終開通","titleEn":"Inspect final stop-layer breakthrough","objective":"完成「停止層最終開通」的證據判讀，辨識『比較停止層清除與下層金屬暴露程度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect final stop-layer breakthrough by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare stop-layer removal and lower-metal exposure.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較停止層清除與下層金屬暴露程度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare stop-layer removal and lower-metal exposure. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the landing is open with controlled metal loss. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：延長開通時間可能造成金屬凹蝕。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: longer breakthrough can recess the lower metal. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「延長開通時間可能造成金屬凹蝕」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The landing is open with controlled metal loss. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Longer breakthrough can recess the lower metal. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-359-k1","title":"停止層最終開通的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect final stop-layer breakthrough","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「比較停止層清除與下層金屬暴露程度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare stop-layer removal and lower-metal exposure. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-359-k2","title":"停止層最終開通的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect final stop-layer breakthrough","text":"有效證據需支持「接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控」。但延長開通時間可能造成金屬凹蝕；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The landing is open with controlled metal loss. However, longer breakthrough can recess the lower metal; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「停止層最終開通」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect final stop-layer breakthrough?","options":["導通孔在溝槽圖形化時仍獲保護","孔底實際開放且邊緣未過度流失","接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控"],"optionsEn":["Vias remain protected during trench patterning","The bottom is open without excessive edge loss","The landing is open with controlled metal loss"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較停止層清除與下層金屬暴露程度」，因此直接證據是「接觸落點開放且金屬損失受控」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：延長開通時間可能造成金屬凹蝕。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare stop-layer removal and lower-metal exposure; the direct criterion is: The landing is open with controlled metal loss. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Longer breakthrough can recess the lower metal."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":359,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-358"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-360","title":"下層金屬表面氧化","titleEn":"Assess exposed lower-metal oxidation","objective":"完成「下層金屬表面氧化」的證據判讀，辨識『對照等待時間與孔底金屬表面訊號』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess exposed lower-metal oxidation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare queue time and bottom-metal surface signatures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照等待時間與孔底金屬表面訊號。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare queue time and bottom-metal surface signatures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略再氧化可能錯怪填孔材料。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring reoxidation can misattribute failure to fill material. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略再氧化可能錯怪填孔材料」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring reoxidation can misattribute failure to fill material. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-360-k1","title":"下層金屬表面氧化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess exposed lower-metal oxidation","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「對照等待時間與孔底金屬表面訊號」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Compare queue time and bottom-metal surface signatures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-360-k2","title":"下層金屬表面氧化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess exposed lower-metal oxidation","text":"有效證據需支持「暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型」。但忽略再氧化可能錯怪填孔材料；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model. However, ignoring reoxidation can misattribute failure to fill material; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「下層金屬表面氧化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess exposed lower-metal oxidation?","options":["暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型","導通孔落在已定義溝槽的允許區","圖形偏移與尺寸偏差已逐層量化"],"optionsEn":["Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model","Vias land within the permitted trench region","Shift and dimensional bias are quantified across layers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照等待時間與孔底金屬表面訊號」，因此直接證據是「暴露後的界面狀態可納入接觸模型」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略再氧化可能錯怪填孔材料。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare queue time and bottom-metal surface signatures; the direct criterion is: Post-exposure interface condition enters the contact model. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring reoxidation can misattribute failure to fill material."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":360,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-359"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-361","title":"雙鑲嵌空腔三維重建","titleEn":"Reconstruct dual-damascene cavities","objective":"完成「雙鑲嵌空腔三維重建」的證據判讀，辨識『整合俯視與截面資料重建空腔連通』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate reconstruct dual-damascene cavities by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine plan-view and sectional data to reconstruct cavity connectivity.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，整合俯視與截面資料重建空腔連通。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine plan-view and sectional data to reconstruct cavity connectivity. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：兩張分離截面可能造成假連通印象。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: separate sections can misleadingly suggest connectivity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「兩張分離截面可能造成假連通印象」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Separate sections can misleadingly suggest connectivity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-361-k1","title":"雙鑲嵌空腔三維重建的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of reconstruct dual-damascene cavities","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「整合俯視與截面資料重建空腔連通」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Combine plan-view and sectional data to reconstruct cavity connectivity. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-361-k2","title":"雙鑲嵌空腔三維重建的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for reconstruct dual-damascene cavities","text":"有效證據需支持「導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通」。但兩張分離截面可能造成假連通印象；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry. However, separate sections can misleadingly suggest connectivity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「雙鑲嵌空腔三維重建」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for reconstruct dual-damascene cavities?","options":["孔底可達性與預定填充方式相容","導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通","每層的轉移與停止功能均可說明"],"optionsEn":["Bottom accessibility is compatible with intended filling","Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry","Transfer and stopping roles are explained for each layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「整合俯視與截面資料重建空腔連通」，因此直接證據是「導通孔與溝槽在三維模型中連通」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：兩張分離截面可能造成假連通印象。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine plan-view and sectional data to reconstruct cavity connectivity; the direct criterion is: Vias and trenches connect in the reconstructed geometry. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Separate sections can misleadingly suggest connectivity."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":361,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-360"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-362","title":"線端與孔端最小間距","titleEn":"Inspect line-end and via-end spacing","objective":"完成「線端與孔端最小間距」的證據判讀，辨識『量測線端附近最易失去隔離的區域』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect line-end and via-end spacing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure isolation-critical regions near line ends.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量測線端附近最易失去隔離的區域。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure isolation-critical regions near line ends. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均線距會漏掉線端狹縫。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mean spacing misses line-end pinch points. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均線距會漏掉線端狹縫」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mean spacing misses line-end pinch points. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-362-k1","title":"線端與孔端最小間距的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect line-end and via-end spacing","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「量測線端附近最易失去隔離的區域」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Measure isolation-critical regions near line ends. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-362-k2","title":"線端與孔端最小間距的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect line-end and via-end spacing","text":"有效證據需支持「最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求」。但平均線距會漏掉線端狹縫；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs. However, mean spacing misses line-end pinch points; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「線端與孔端最小間距」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect line-end and via-end spacing?","options":["開孔終點與下層導體保持可辨間隔","尺寸依賴的深度差有可量測上限","最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求"],"optionsEn":["The opening endpoint is distinguished from the lower conductor","Width-dependent depth differences are explicitly bounded","The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「量測線端附近最易失去隔離的區域」，因此直接證據是「最弱局部間距仍符合題定隔離需求」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均線距會漏掉線端狹縫。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure isolation-critical regions near line ends; the direct criterion is: The weakest local spacing meets stated isolation needs. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mean spacing misses line-end pinch points."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":362,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-361"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-363","title":"圖形轉移偏差回饋","titleEn":"Feed back pattern-transfer bias","objective":"完成「圖形轉移偏差回饋」的證據判讀，辨識『分開整理曝光、遮罩與介電蝕刻偏差』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate feed back pattern-transfer bias by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate exposure, hardmask and dielectric-etch biases.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分開整理曝光、遮罩與介電蝕刻偏差。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate exposure, hardmask and dielectric-etch biases. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: correction targets the station producing the bias. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把所有偏差推回曝光會過度補償。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: assigning every bias to exposure overcompensates. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把所有偏差推回曝光會過度補償」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Correction targets the station producing the bias. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Assigning every bias to exposure overcompensates. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-363-k1","title":"圖形轉移偏差回饋的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of feed back pattern-transfer bias","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「分開整理曝光、遮罩與介電蝕刻偏差」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Separate exposure, hardmask and dielectric-etch biases. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-363-k2","title":"圖形轉移偏差回饋的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for feed back pattern-transfer bias","text":"有效證據需支持「修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站」。但把所有偏差推回曝光會過度補償；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Correction targets the station producing the bias. However, assigning every bias to exposure overcompensates; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「圖形轉移偏差回饋」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for feed back pattern-transfer bias?","options":["修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站","反射變化與尺寸偏差有相容解釋","孔底邊角未形成非預期凹槽"],"optionsEn":["Correction targets the station producing the bias","Reflection changes plausibly explain dimension variation","Bottom corners lack unintended grooves"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「分開整理曝光、遮罩與介電蝕刻偏差」，因此直接證據是「修正歸因至造成偏差的具體工站」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把所有偏差推回曝光會過度補償。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate exposure, hardmask and dielectric-etch biases; the direct criterion is: Correction targets the station producing the bias. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Assigning every bias to exposure overcompensates."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":363,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-362"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-364","title":"填金屬前空腔放行","titleEn":"Release cavities before metallization","objective":"完成「填金屬前空腔放行」的證據判讀，辨識『合併空腔形貌、殘留與落點界面證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release cavities before metallization by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine cavity morphology, residue and landing-interface evidence.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，合併空腔形貌、殘留與落點界面證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine cavity morphology, residue and landing-interface evidence. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：空腔可填充且接觸面可用。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：幾何正確但界面污染仍會造成高阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: correct geometry with contamination can still produce high resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「空腔可填充且接觸面可用」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「幾何正確但界面污染仍會造成高阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Correct geometry with contamination can still produce high resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-364-k1","title":"填金屬前空腔放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release cavities before metallization","text":"鑲嵌互連先在介電層形成溝槽或導通孔，再填入導體；先孔後槽、先槽後孔及其他整合路線的順序不可任意混接。 本題具體操作為「合併空腔形貌、殘留與落點界面證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Damascene forms trenches or vias in dielectric before conductor fill; via-first, trench-first and other integration routes cannot be combined arbitrarily. Here the concrete task is: Combine cavity morphology, residue and landing-interface evidence. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-364-k2","title":"填金屬前空腔放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release cavities before metallization","text":"有效證據需支持「空腔可填充且接觸面可用」。但幾何正確但界面污染仍會造成高阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable. However, correct geometry with contamination can still produce high resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「填金屬前空腔放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release cavities before metallization?","options":["保護層覆蓋孔底且可在後續移除","空腔可填充且接觸面可用","可接受孔徑區與焦距變動範圍相容"],"optionsEn":["Protection covers the bottom and remains removable","Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable","Acceptable via dimensions cover the focus-variation range"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「合併空腔形貌、殘留與落點界面證據」，因此直接證據是「空腔可填充且接觸面可用」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：幾何正確但界面污染仍會造成高阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine cavity morphology, residue and landing-interface evidence; the direct criterion is: Cavities are fillable and landing interfaces are usable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Correct geometry with contamination can still produce high resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-interconnect","scb-lam-interconnect","scb-deposition"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":364,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-363"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":14},{"id":"sc-m15","title":"金屬阻障、填充與多層連接","titleEn":"Metal barriers, filling and multilayer connections","description":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-365","title":"阻障厚度與導體截面","titleEn":"Budget barrier thickness and conductor area","objective":"完成「阻障厚度與導體截面」的證據判讀，辨識『從空腔尺寸扣除阻障及襯層佔用面積』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate budget barrier thickness and conductor area by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: subtract barrier and liner area from cavity dimensions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從空腔尺寸扣除阻障及襯層佔用面積。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, subtract barrier and liner area from cavity dimensions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：用外部線寬估算會低估電阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: using outer linewidth underestimates resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「用外部線寬估算會低估電阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Using outer linewidth underestimates resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-365-k1","title":"阻障厚度與導體截面的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of budget barrier thickness and conductor area","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「從空腔尺寸扣除阻障及襯層佔用面積」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Subtract barrier and liner area from cavity dimensions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-365-k2","title":"阻障厚度與導體截面的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for budget barrier thickness and conductor area","text":"有效證據需支持「電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面」。但用外部線寬估算會低估電阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section. However, using outer linewidth underestimates resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「阻障厚度與導體截面」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for budget barrier thickness and conductor area?","options":["高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設","量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄","電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions","Measurement timing is documented with material evolution","Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「從空腔尺寸扣除阻障及襯層佔用面積」，因此直接證據是「電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：用外部線寬估算會低估電阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to subtract barrier and liner area from cavity dimensions; the direct criterion is: Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Using outer linewidth underestimates resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":365,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-364"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-366","title":"擴散阻障材料分支","titleEn":"Compare diffusion-barrier branches","objective":"完成「擴散阻障材料分支」的證據判讀，辨識『對照候選阻障與相鄰金屬介電膜相容性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate compare diffusion-barrier branches by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare barrier compatibility with adjacent metal and dielectric.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照候選阻障與相鄰金屬介電膜相容性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare barrier compatibility with adjacent metal and dielectric. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：低電阻不代表阻擋擴散能力足夠。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: low resistance does not ensure adequate diffusion blocking. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「低電阻不代表阻擋擴散能力足夠」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Low resistance does not ensure adequate diffusion blocking. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-366-k1","title":"擴散阻障材料分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of compare diffusion-barrier branches","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「對照候選阻障與相鄰金屬介電膜相容性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare barrier compatibility with adjacent metal and dielectric. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-366-k2","title":"擴散阻障材料分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for compare diffusion-barrier branches","text":"有效證據需支持「候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈」。但低電阻不代表阻擋擴散能力足夠；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence. However, low resistance does not ensure adequate diffusion blocking; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「擴散阻障材料分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for compare diffusion-barrier branches?","options":["候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈","底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存","電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構"],"optionsEn":["Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence","The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together","Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照候選阻障與相鄰金屬介電膜相容性」，因此直接證據是「候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：低電阻不代表阻擋擴散能力足夠。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare barrier compatibility with adjacent metal and dielectric; the direct criterion is: Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Low resistance does not ensure adequate diffusion blocking."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":366,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-365"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-367","title":"ALD 阻障飽和判讀","titleEn":"Assess ALD barrier saturation","objective":"完成「ALD 阻障飽和判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比較沉積響應與表面位點飽和示意』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess ald barrier saturation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare deposition response with surface-site saturation models.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較沉積響應與表面位點飽和示意。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare deposition response with surface-site saturation models. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未飽和反應會破壞深孔厚度一致性。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unsaturated reactions impair deep-feature uniformity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未飽和反應會破壞深孔厚度一致性」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unsaturated reactions impair deep-feature uniformity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-367-k1","title":"ALD 阻障飽和判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess ald barrier saturation","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較沉積響應與表面位點飽和示意」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare deposition response with surface-site saturation models. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-367-k2","title":"ALD 阻障飽和判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess ald barrier saturation","text":"有效證據需支持「增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量」。但未飽和反應會破壞深孔厚度一致性；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle. However, unsaturated reactions impair deep-feature uniformity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「ALD 阻障飽和判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess ald barrier saturation?","options":["空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應","增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量","待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸"],"optionsEn":["Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks","Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle","Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較沉積響應與表面位點飽和示意」，因此直接證據是「增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未飽和反應會破壞深孔厚度一致性。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare deposition response with surface-site saturation models; the direct criterion is: Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unsaturated reactions impair deep-feature uniformity."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":367,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-366"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-368","title":"阻障層側壁連續性","titleEn":"Inspect barrier sidewall continuity","objective":"完成「阻障層側壁連續性」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤溝槽角落與孔底的連續薄膜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect barrier sidewall continuity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace continuous films at trench corners and via bottoms.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤溝槽角落與孔底的連續薄膜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace continuous films at trench corners and via bottoms. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：一個針孔即可形成局部擴散捷徑。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one pinhole can form a local diffusion shortcut. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「一個針孔即可形成局部擴散捷徑」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One pinhole can form a local diffusion shortcut. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-368-k1","title":"阻障層側壁連續性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect barrier sidewall continuity","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「追蹤溝槽角落與孔底的連續薄膜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Trace continuous films at trench corners and via bottoms. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-368-k2","title":"阻障層側壁連續性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect barrier sidewall continuity","text":"有效證據需支持「最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔」。但一個針孔即可形成局部擴散捷徑；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier. However, one pinhole can form a local diffusion shortcut; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「阻障層側壁連續性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect barrier sidewall continuity?","options":["空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉","場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整","最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔"],"optionsEn":["The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening","Field copper clears while lines remain intact","The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤溝槽角落與孔底的連續薄膜」，因此直接證據是「最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：一個針孔即可形成局部擴散捷徑。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace continuous films at trench corners and via bottoms; the direct criterion is: The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One pinhole can form a local diffusion shortcut."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":368,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-367"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-369","title":"金屬襯層附著評估","titleEn":"Evaluate metal-liner adhesion","objective":"完成「金屬襯層附著評估」的證據判讀，辨識『比較界面剝離位置與材料堆疊』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate metal-liner adhesion by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare delamination locations with the material stack.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較界面剝離位置與材料堆疊。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare delamination locations with the material stack. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：破壞位置與題定附著需求相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把內聚破壞誤判界面破壞會選錯改善項。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: confusing cohesive and interface failure misdirects improvements. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「破壞位置與題定附著需求相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把內聚破壞誤判界面破壞會選錯改善項」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Confusing cohesive and interface failure misdirects improvements. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-369-k1","title":"金屬襯層附著評估的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate metal-liner adhesion","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較界面剝離位置與材料堆疊」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare delamination locations with the material stack. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-369-k2","title":"金屬襯層附著評估的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate metal-liner adhesion","text":"有效證據需支持「破壞位置與題定附著需求相容」。但把內聚破壞誤判界面破壞會選錯改善項；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements. However, confusing cohesive and interface failure misdirects improvements; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「金屬襯層附著評估」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate metal-liner adhesion?","options":["破壞位置與題定附著需求相容","厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋","阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失"],"optionsEn":["Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements","Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation","Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較界面剝離位置與材料堆疊」，因此直接證據是「破壞位置與題定附著需求相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把內聚破壞誤判界面破壞會選錯改善項。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare delamination locations with the material stack; the direct criterion is: Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Confusing cohesive and interface failure misdirects improvements."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":369,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-368"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-370","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect seed coverage at via bottoms","objective":"完成「種子層孔底覆蓋」的證據判讀，辨識『區分連續種子層與局部未覆蓋區』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect seed coverage at via bottoms by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish continuous seed films from uncovered bottom areas.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分連續種子層與局部未覆蓋區。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish continuous seed films from uncovered bottom areas. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：局部斷種會造成延遲成核與空洞。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: seed discontinuities delay nucleation and cause voids. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「局部斷種會造成延遲成核與空洞」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Seed discontinuities delay nucleation and cause voids. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-370-k1","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect seed coverage at via bottoms","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「區分連續種子層與局部未覆蓋區」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish continuous seed films from uncovered bottom areas. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-370-k2","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect seed coverage at via bottoms","text":"有效證據需支持「待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑」。但局部斷種會造成延遲成核與空洞；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths. However, seed discontinuities delay nucleation and cause voids; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「種子層孔底覆蓋」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect seed coverage at via bottoms?","options":["線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計","待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑","過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍"],"optionsEn":["Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates","Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths","Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分連續種子層與局部未覆蓋區」，因此直接證據是「待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：局部斷種會造成延遲成核與空洞。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish continuous seed films from uncovered bottom areas; the direct criterion is: Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Seed discontinuities delay nucleation and cause voids."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":370,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-369"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-371","title":"種子層懸簷遮蔽","titleEn":"Inspect seed-layer overhangs","objective":"完成「種子層懸簷遮蔽」的證據判讀，辨識『量取孔口懸簷與剩餘開口大小』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect seed-layer overhangs by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure opening overhang and remaining aperture.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取孔口懸簷與剩餘開口大小。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure opening overhang and remaining aperture. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：孔口仍允許後續填充傳質。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the opening still permits mass transport during filling. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過厚孔口種子層會提早封口。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess seed at the opening can seal it prematurely. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「孔口仍允許後續填充傳質」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過厚孔口種子層會提早封口」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The opening still permits mass transport during filling. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess seed at the opening can seal it prematurely. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-371-k1","title":"種子層懸簷遮蔽的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect seed-layer overhangs","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「量取孔口懸簷與剩餘開口大小」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Measure opening overhang and remaining aperture. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-371-k2","title":"種子層懸簷遮蔽的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect seed-layer overhangs","text":"有效證據需支持「孔口仍允許後續填充傳質」。但過厚孔口種子層會提早封口；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The opening still permits mass transport during filling. However, excess seed at the opening can seal it prematurely; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「種子層懸簷遮蔽」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect seed-layer overhangs?","options":["量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄","圖形密度造成的高度差已受控","孔口仍允許後續填充傳質"],"optionsEn":["Measurement timing is documented with material evolution","Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled","The opening still permits mass transport during filling"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取孔口懸簷與剩餘開口大小」，因此直接證據是「孔口仍允許後續填充傳質」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過厚孔口種子層會提早封口。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure opening overhang and remaining aperture; the direct criterion is: The opening still permits mass transport during filling. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess seed at the opening can seal it prematurely."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":371,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-370"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-372","title":"種子層片電阻圖","titleEn":"Map seed-layer sheet resistance","objective":"完成「種子層片電阻圖」的證據判讀，辨識『比對種子膜電阻與電鍍供電路徑』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map seed-layer sheet resistance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare seed resistance maps and plating current paths.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比對種子膜電阻與電鍍供電路徑。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare seed resistance maps and plating current paths. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: high-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：厚度正常但污染仍可提高電阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: normal thickness with contamination can still raise resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「厚度正常但污染仍可提高電阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Normal thickness with contamination can still raise resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-372-k1","title":"種子層片電阻圖的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map seed-layer sheet resistance","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比對種子膜電阻與電鍍供電路徑」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare seed resistance maps and plating current paths. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-372-k2","title":"種子層片電阻圖的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map seed-layer sheet resistance","text":"有效證據需支持「高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設」。但厚度正常但污染仍可提高電阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions. However, normal thickness with contamination can still raise resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「種子層片電阻圖」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map seed-layer sheet resistance?","options":["高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設","電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構","蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions","Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure","Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比對種子膜電阻與電鍍供電路徑」，因此直接證據是「高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：厚度正常但污染仍可提高電阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare seed resistance maps and plating current paths; the direct criterion is: High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Normal thickness with contamination can still raise resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":372,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-371"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-373","title":"電鍍液添加劑平衡","titleEn":"Assess plating-additive balance","objective":"完成「電鍍液添加劑平衡」的證據判讀，辨識『比較加速、抑制與整平作用的示意響應』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess plating-additive balance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare accelerator, suppressor and leveler responses.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較加速、抑制與整平作用的示意響應。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare accelerator, suppressor and leveler responses. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單看總沉積量會漏判添加劑失衡。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: total deposition can hide additive imbalance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單看總沉積量會漏判添加劑失衡」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Total deposition can hide additive imbalance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-373-k1","title":"電鍍液添加劑平衡的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess plating-additive balance","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較加速、抑制與整平作用的示意響應」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare accelerator, suppressor and leveler responses. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-373-k2","title":"電鍍液添加劑平衡的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess plating-additive balance","text":"有效證據需支持「底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存」。但單看總沉積量會漏判添加劑失衡；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together. However, total deposition can hide additive imbalance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「電鍍液添加劑平衡」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess plating-additive balance?","options":["高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致","底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存","空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應"],"optionsEn":["High-current regions match geometric constrictions","The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together","Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較加速、抑制與整平作用的示意響應」，因此直接證據是「底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單看總沉積量會漏判添加劑失衡。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare accelerator, suppressor and leveler responses; the direct criterion is: The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Total deposition can hide additive imbalance."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":373,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-372"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-374","title":"電鍍潤濕與困氣","titleEn":"Assess plating wetting and trapped gas","objective":"完成「電鍍潤濕與困氣」的證據判讀，辨識『檢查孔內液體進入與氣泡遮蔽示意』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess plating wetting and trapped gas by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect liquid access and bubble masking within cavities.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢查孔內液體進入與氣泡遮蔽示意。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect liquid access and bubble masking within cavities. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：困氣會造成局部無沉積區。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: trapped gas causes local nondeposition. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「困氣會造成局部無沉積區」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Trapped gas causes local nondeposition. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-374-k1","title":"電鍍潤濕與困氣的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess plating wetting and trapped gas","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「檢查孔內液體進入與氣泡遮蔽示意」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Inspect liquid access and bubble masking within cavities. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-374-k2","title":"電鍍潤濕與困氣的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess plating wetting and trapped gas","text":"有效證據需支持「待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸」。但困氣會造成局部無沉積區；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface. However, trapped gas causes local nondeposition; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「電鍍潤濕與困氣」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess plating wetting and trapped gas?","options":["場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整","替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在","待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸"],"optionsEn":["Field copper clears while lines remain intact","An alternate current path remains after a local failure","Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢查孔內液體進入與氣泡遮蔽示意」，因此直接證據是「待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：困氣會造成局部無沉積區。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect liquid access and bubble masking within cavities; the direct criterion is: Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Trapped gas causes local nondeposition."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":374,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-373"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-375","title":"底部向上填充","titleEn":"Evaluate bottom-up fill","objective":"完成「底部向上填充」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤截面序列的孔底與孔口生長』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate bottom-up fill by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: track bottom and opening growth through section sequences.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤截面序列的孔底與孔口生長。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, track bottom and opening growth through section sequences. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：側壁等速成長可能留下中心縫。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: equal sidewall growth may leave a central seam. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「側壁等速成長可能留下中心縫」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Equal sidewall growth may leave a central seam. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-375-k1","title":"底部向上填充的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate bottom-up fill","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「追蹤截面序列的孔底與孔口生長」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Track bottom and opening growth through section sequences. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-375-k2","title":"底部向上填充的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate bottom-up fill","text":"有效證據需支持「空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉」。但側壁等速成長可能留下中心縫；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening. However, equal sidewall growth may leave a central seam; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「底部向上填充」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate bottom-up fill?","options":["空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉","阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失","累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量"],"optionsEn":["The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening","Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss","Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤截面序列的孔底與孔口生長」，因此直接證據是「空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：側壁等速成長可能留下中心縫。","explanationEn":"The task is to track bottom and opening growth through section sequences; the direct criterion is: The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Equal sidewall growth may leave a central seam."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":375,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-374"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-376","title":"電流分佈邊緣效應","titleEn":"Assess plating edge-current effects","objective":"完成「電流分佈邊緣效應」的證據判讀，辨識『比較邊緣導電接點與鍍層厚度圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess plating edge-current effects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare edge electrical contacts with plated-thickness maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較邊緣導電接點與鍍層厚度圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare edge electrical contacts with plated-thickness maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：邊緣厚膜可能源於電流擁擠。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: thick edges can result from current crowding. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「邊緣厚膜可能源於電流擁擠」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Thick edges can result from current crowding. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-376-k1","title":"電流分佈邊緣效應的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess plating edge-current effects","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較邊緣導電接點與鍍層厚度圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare edge electrical contacts with plated-thickness maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-376-k2","title":"電流分佈邊緣效應的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess plating edge-current effects","text":"有效證據需支持「厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋」。但邊緣厚膜可能源於電流擁擠；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation. However, thick edges can result from current crowding; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「電流分佈邊緣效應」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess plating edge-current effects?","options":["延遲變化可對應至具體導線層","厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋","線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計"],"optionsEn":["Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels","Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation","Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較邊緣導電接點與鍍層厚度圖」，因此直接證據是「厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：邊緣厚膜可能源於電流擁擠。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare edge electrical contacts with plated-thickness maps; the direct criterion is: Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Thick edges can result from current crowding."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":376,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-375"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-377","title":"鍍銅過覆蓋厚度","titleEn":"Measure copper overburden","objective":"完成「鍍銅過覆蓋厚度」的證據判讀，辨識『區分空腔內填充與表面過覆蓋金屬』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure copper overburden by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate cavity fill from surface overburden.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分空腔內填充與表面過覆蓋金屬。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate cavity fill from surface overburden. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：減少表面銅不代表孔內已填滿。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: less surface copper does not prove complete cavity fill. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「減少表面銅不代表孔內已填滿」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Less surface copper does not prove complete cavity fill. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-377-k1","title":"鍍銅過覆蓋厚度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure copper overburden","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「區分空腔內填充與表面過覆蓋金屬」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Separate cavity fill from surface overburden. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-377-k2","title":"鍍銅過覆蓋厚度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure copper overburden","text":"有效證據需支持「過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍」。但減少表面銅不代表孔內已填滿；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability. However, less surface copper does not prove complete cavity fill; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鍍銅過覆蓋厚度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure copper overburden?","options":["圖形密度造成的高度差已受控","導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立","過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍"],"optionsEn":["Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled","Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied","Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分空腔內填充與表面過覆蓋金屬」，因此直接證據是「過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：減少表面銅不代表孔內已填滿。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate cavity fill from surface overburden; the direct criterion is: Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Less surface copper does not prove complete cavity fill."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":377,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-376"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-378","title":"鍍後自退火追蹤","titleEn":"Track post-plating self-annealing","objective":"完成「鍍後自退火追蹤」的證據判讀，辨識『比較存放歷程中的電阻與晶粒變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate track post-plating self-annealing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare resistance and grain changes during storage.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較存放歷程中的電阻與晶粒變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare resistance and grain changes during storage. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: measurement timing is documented with material evolution. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：跨時間比較會把自退火誤當機台漂移。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: time-mismatched comparisons can misread self-annealing as tool drift. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「跨時間比較會把自退火誤當機台漂移」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Measurement timing is documented with material evolution. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Time-mismatched comparisons can misread self-annealing as tool drift. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-378-k1","title":"鍍後自退火追蹤的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of track post-plating self-annealing","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較存放歷程中的電阻與晶粒變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare resistance and grain changes during storage. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-378-k2","title":"鍍後自退火追蹤的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for track post-plating self-annealing","text":"有效證據需支持「量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄」。但跨時間比較會把自退火誤當機台漂移；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Measurement timing is documented with material evolution. However, time-mismatched comparisons can misread self-annealing as tool drift; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鍍後自退火追蹤」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for track post-plating self-annealing?","options":["量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄","蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面","電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面"],"optionsEn":["Measurement timing is documented with material evolution","Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface","Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較存放歷程中的電阻與晶粒變化」，因此直接證據是「量測時間點與材料演化一致記錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：跨時間比較會把自退火誤當機台漂移。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare resistance and grain changes during storage; the direct criterion is: Measurement timing is documented with material evolution. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Time-mismatched comparisons can misread self-annealing as tool drift."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":378,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-377"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-379","title":"金屬晶粒與散射","titleEn":"Assess metal grains and scattering","objective":"完成「金屬晶粒與散射」的證據判讀，辨識『關聯晶粒尺度、線寬與電阻變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess metal grains and scattering by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate grain size, linewidth and resistance changes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，關聯晶粒尺度、線寬與電阻變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate grain size, linewidth and resistance changes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只用塊材電阻率會低估細線效應。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: bulk resistivity alone understates narrow-line effects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只用塊材電阻率會低估細線效應」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Bulk resistivity alone understates narrow-line effects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-379-k1","title":"金屬晶粒與散射的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess metal grains and scattering","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「關聯晶粒尺度、線寬與電阻變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Relate grain size, linewidth and resistance changes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-379-k2","title":"金屬晶粒與散射的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess metal grains and scattering","text":"有效證據需支持「電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構」。但只用塊材電阻率會低估細線效應；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure. However, bulk resistivity alone understates narrow-line effects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「金屬晶粒與散射」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess metal grains and scattering?","options":["候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈","電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構","高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致"],"optionsEn":["Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence","Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure","High-current regions match geometric constrictions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「關聯晶粒尺度、線寬與電阻變化」，因此直接證據是「電阻解釋同時考慮尺寸與微結構」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只用塊材電阻率會低估細線效應。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate grain size, linewidth and resistance changes; the direct criterion is: Resistance interpretation includes size and microstructure. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Bulk resistivity alone understates narrow-line effects."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":379,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-378"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-380","title":"填充空洞三維抽樣","titleEn":"Sample fill voids in three dimensions","objective":"完成「填充空洞三維抽樣」的證據判讀，辨識『比較多方位截面與電性異常區』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate sample fill voids in three dimensions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare sections from multiple orientations with electrical anomalies.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較多方位截面與電性異常區。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare sections from multiple orientations with electrical anomalies. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單張良好截面不足以排除空洞。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one good section does not exclude voids. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單張良好截面不足以排除空洞」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One good section does not exclude voids. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-380-k1","title":"填充空洞三維抽樣的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of sample fill voids in three dimensions","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較多方位截面與電性異常區」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare sections from multiple orientations with electrical anomalies. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-380-k2","title":"填充空洞三維抽樣的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for sample fill voids in three dimensions","text":"有效證據需支持「空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應」。但單張良好截面不足以排除空洞；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks. However, one good section does not exclude voids; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「填充空洞三維抽樣」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for sample fill voids in three dimensions?","options":["替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在","增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量","空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應"],"optionsEn":["An alternate current path remains after a local failure","Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle","Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較多方位截面與電性異常區」，因此直接證據是「空洞位置與可能導通瓶頸相對應」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單張良好截面不足以排除空洞。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare sections from multiple orientations with electrical anomalies; the direct criterion is: Void locations match potential conduction bottlenecks. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One good section does not exclude voids."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":380,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-379"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-381","title":"銅過覆蓋研磨終點","titleEn":"Determine copper-overburden polish endpoint","objective":"完成「銅過覆蓋研磨終點」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤場區銅消失與阻障層暴露』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate determine copper-overburden polish endpoint by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: track field-copper clearance and barrier exposure.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤場區銅消失與阻障層暴露。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, track field-copper clearance and barrier exposure. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: field copper clears while lines remain intact. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：欠研磨可留下連接相鄰線的銅膜。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: underpolish can leave copper bridging neighboring lines. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「欠研磨可留下連接相鄰線的銅膜」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Field copper clears while lines remain intact. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Underpolish can leave copper bridging neighboring lines. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-381-k1","title":"銅過覆蓋研磨終點的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of determine copper-overburden polish endpoint","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「追蹤場區銅消失與阻障層暴露」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Track field-copper clearance and barrier exposure. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-381-k2","title":"銅過覆蓋研磨終點的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for determine copper-overburden polish endpoint","text":"有效證據需支持「場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整」。但欠研磨可留下連接相鄰線的銅膜；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Field copper clears while lines remain intact. However, underpolish can leave copper bridging neighboring lines; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「銅過覆蓋研磨終點」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for determine copper-overburden polish endpoint?","options":["場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整","累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量","最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔"],"optionsEn":["Field copper clears while lines remain intact","Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin","The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤場區銅消失與阻障層暴露」，因此直接證據是「場區銅完全清除而導線仍完整」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：欠研磨可留下連接相鄰線的銅膜。","explanationEn":"The task is to track field-copper clearance and barrier exposure; the direct criterion is: Field copper clears while lines remain intact. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Underpolish can leave copper bridging neighboring lines."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":381,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-380"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-382","title":"阻障去除與低介電保護","titleEn":"Balance barrier removal and low-k protection","objective":"完成「阻障去除與低介電保護」的證據判讀，辨識『比較阻障殘留與介電侵蝕程度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate balance barrier removal and low-k protection by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare residual barrier and dielectric erosion.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較阻障殘留與介電侵蝕程度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare residual barrier and dielectric erosion. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：更久研磨可能造成線間結構受損。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: longer polishing can damage structures between lines. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「更久研磨可能造成線間結構受損」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Longer polishing can damage structures between lines. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-382-k1","title":"阻障去除與低介電保護的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of balance barrier removal and low-k protection","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較阻障殘留與介電侵蝕程度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare residual barrier and dielectric erosion. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-382-k2","title":"阻障去除與低介電保護的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for balance barrier removal and low-k protection","text":"有效證據需支持「阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失」。但更久研磨可能造成線間結構受損；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss. However, longer polishing can damage structures between lines; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「阻障去除與低介電保護」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for balance barrier removal and low-k protection?","options":["破壞位置與題定附著需求相容","阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失","延遲變化可對應至具體導線層"],"optionsEn":["Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements","Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss","Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較阻障殘留與介電侵蝕程度」，因此直接證據是「阻障清除未造成介電支撐明顯損失」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：更久研磨可能造成線間結構受損。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare residual barrier and dielectric erosion; the direct criterion is: Barrier clearance avoids significant dielectric support loss. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Longer polishing can damage structures between lines."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":382,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-381"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-383","title":"寬銅線凹陷量測","titleEn":"Measure dishing in wide copper lines","objective":"完成「寬銅線凹陷量測」的證據判讀，辨識『量取不同線寬中央與邊緣高度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure dishing in wide copper lines by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure center and edge heights across line widths.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取不同線寬中央與邊緣高度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure center and edge heights across line widths. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面平均高度可能掩蓋線中央凹陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mean surface height can hide center-line dishing. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面平均高度可能掩蓋線中央凹陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mean surface height can hide center-line dishing. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-383-k1","title":"寬銅線凹陷量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure dishing in wide copper lines","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「量取不同線寬中央與邊緣高度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Measure center and edge heights across line widths. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-383-k2","title":"寬銅線凹陷量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure dishing in wide copper lines","text":"有效證據需支持「線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計」。但表面平均高度可能掩蓋線中央凹陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates. However, mean surface height can hide center-line dishing; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「寬銅線凹陷量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure dishing in wide copper lines?","options":["導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立","待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑","線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計"],"optionsEn":["Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied","Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths","Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取不同線寬中央與邊緣高度」，因此直接證據是「線寬依賴凹陷被納入導體截面估計」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面平均高度可能掩蓋線中央凹陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure center and edge heights across line widths; the direct criterion is: Width-dependent dishing enters conductor-area estimates. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mean surface height can hide center-line dishing."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":383,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-382"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-384","title":"密集互連區侵蝕","titleEn":"Assess erosion in dense interconnects","objective":"完成「密集互連區侵蝕」的證據判讀，辨識『比較密集陣列與參考區的整體高度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess erosion in dense interconnects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dense arrays and reference-area heights.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較密集陣列與參考區的整體高度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dense arrays and reference-area heights. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：圖形密度造成的高度差已受控。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：線條各自平坦仍可能整區下降。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: individually flat lines can coexist with array-wide erosion. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「圖形密度造成的高度差已受控」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「線條各自平坦仍可能整區下降」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Individually flat lines can coexist with array-wide erosion. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-384-k1","title":"密集互連區侵蝕的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess erosion in dense interconnects","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較密集陣列與參考區的整體高度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare dense arrays and reference-area heights. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-384-k2","title":"密集互連區侵蝕的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess erosion in dense interconnects","text":"有效證據需支持「圖形密度造成的高度差已受控」。但線條各自平坦仍可能整區下降；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled. However, individually flat lines can coexist with array-wide erosion; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「密集互連區侵蝕」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess erosion in dense interconnects?","options":["圖形密度造成的高度差已受控","電阻模型使用剩餘有效導體截面","孔口仍允許後續填充傳質"],"optionsEn":["Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled","Resistance modeling uses the remaining conductor cross-section","The opening still permits mass transport during filling"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較密集陣列與參考區的整體高度」，因此直接證據是「圖形密度造成的高度差已受控」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：線條各自平坦仍可能整區下降。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dense arrays and reference-area heights; the direct criterion is: Pattern-density-dependent height differences are controlled. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Individually flat lines can coexist with array-wide erosion."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":384,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-383"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-385","title":"金屬蓋層完整性","titleEn":"Verify metal capping integrity","objective":"完成「金屬蓋層完整性」的證據判讀，辨識『檢查銅表面蓋層的連續性與界面』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate verify metal capping integrity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect continuity and interfaces of copper caps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢查銅表面蓋層的連續性與界面。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect continuity and interfaces of copper caps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：污染界面可能使蓋層附著失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: contaminated interfaces can impair cap adhesion. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「污染界面可能使蓋層附著失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Contaminated interfaces can impair cap adhesion. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-385-k1","title":"金屬蓋層完整性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of verify metal capping integrity","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「檢查銅表面蓋層的連續性與界面」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Inspect continuity and interfaces of copper caps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-385-k2","title":"金屬蓋層完整性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for verify metal capping integrity","text":"有效證據需支持「蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面」。但污染界面可能使蓋層附著失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface. However, contaminated interfaces can impair cap adhesion; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「金屬蓋層完整性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for verify metal capping integrity?","options":["高電阻區未破壞均勻供電假設","蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面","候選材料具有界面及擴散的證據鏈"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance regions do not invalidate uniform-current assumptions","Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface","Candidate materials have interface and diffusion evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢查銅表面蓋層的連續性與界面」，因此直接證據是「蓋層覆蓋對應已清潔的金屬表面」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：污染界面可能使蓋層附著失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect continuity and interfaces of copper caps; the direct criterion is: Cap coverage matches a verified clean metal surface. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Contaminated interfaces can impair cap adhesion."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":385,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-384"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-386","title":"導通孔電流擁擠","titleEn":"Assess via current crowding","objective":"完成「導通孔電流擁擠」的證據判讀，辨識『將電流密度模型疊合實際孔槽幾何』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess via current crowding by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay current-density models on measured via–trench geometry.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將電流密度模型疊合實際孔槽幾何。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay current-density models on measured via–trench geometry. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: high-current regions match geometric constrictions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只用平均電流密度會漏判局部熱點。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: average current density misses local hotspots. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只用平均電流密度會漏判局部熱點」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: High-current regions match geometric constrictions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Average current density misses local hotspots. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-386-k1","title":"導通孔電流擁擠的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess via current crowding","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「將電流密度模型疊合實際孔槽幾何」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Overlay current-density models on measured via–trench geometry. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-386-k2","title":"導通孔電流擁擠的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess via current crowding","text":"有效證據需支持「高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致」。但只用平均電流密度會漏判局部熱點；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: High-current regions match geometric constrictions. However, average current density misses local hotspots; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔電流擁擠」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess via current crowding?","options":["增加前驅曝露不再改變單循環增量","底部增長與孔口抑制能在模型中共存","高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致"],"optionsEn":["Added precursor exposure no longer changes growth per cycle","The model supports bottom growth and opening suppression together","High-current regions match geometric constrictions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「將電流密度模型疊合實際孔槽幾何」，因此直接證據是「高電流區與幾何收縮位置一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只用平均電流密度會漏判局部熱點。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay current-density models on measured via–trench geometry; the direct criterion is: High-current regions match geometric constrictions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Average current density misses local hotspots."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":386,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-385"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-387","title":"冗餘導通孔連接","titleEn":"Evaluate redundant-via connections","objective":"完成「冗餘導通孔連接」的證據判讀，辨識『比較單孔與多孔連接的失效路徑』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate redundant-via connections by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare failure paths for single- and multi-via connections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較單孔與多孔連接的失效路徑。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare failure paths for single- and multi-via connections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: an alternate current path remains after a local failure. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：多孔共用弱界面可能形成共同失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: multiple vias sharing a weak interface can fail together. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「多孔共用弱界面可能形成共同失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: An alternate current path remains after a local failure. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Multiple vias sharing a weak interface can fail together. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-387-k1","title":"冗餘導通孔連接的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate redundant-via connections","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「比較單孔與多孔連接的失效路徑」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Compare failure paths for single- and multi-via connections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-387-k2","title":"冗餘導通孔連接的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate redundant-via connections","text":"有效證據需支持「替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在」。但多孔共用弱界面可能形成共同失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: An alternate current path remains after a local failure. However, multiple vias sharing a weak interface can fail together; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「冗餘導通孔連接」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate redundant-via connections?","options":["替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在","最薄位置仍具可辨識連續阻隔","待鍍表面可被連續電解液接觸"],"optionsEn":["An alternate current path remains after a local failure","The thinnest location retains a discernible continuous barrier","Electrolyte continuously contacts the intended plating surface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較單孔與多孔連接的失效路徑」，因此直接證據是「替代電流路徑在局部失效後仍存在」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：多孔共用弱界面可能形成共同失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare failure paths for single- and multi-via connections; the direct criterion is: An alternate current path remains after a local failure. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Multiple vias sharing a weak interface can fail together."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":387,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-386"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-388","title":"多層累積套刻","titleEn":"Assess accumulated multilayer overlay","objective":"完成「多層累積套刻」的證據判讀，辨識『疊合多層落點與量測誤差方向』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess accumulated multilayer overlay by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay multilayer landings and error directions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，疊合多層落點與量測誤差方向。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay multilayer landings and error directions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：各層平均合格不保證全堆疊對準。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: passing layer averages does not guarantee stack alignment. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「各層平均合格不保證全堆疊對準」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Passing layer averages does not guarantee stack alignment. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-388-k1","title":"多層累積套刻的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess accumulated multilayer overlay","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「疊合多層落點與量測誤差方向」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Overlay multilayer landings and error directions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-388-k2","title":"多層累積套刻的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess accumulated multilayer overlay","text":"有效證據需支持「累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量」。但各層平均合格不保證全堆疊對準；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin. However, passing layer averages does not guarantee stack alignment; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「多層累積套刻」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess accumulated multilayer overlay?","options":["空腔由底部填滿而非由口部封閉","累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量","破壞位置與題定附著需求相容"],"optionsEn":["The cavity fills from the bottom rather than sealing at the opening","Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin","Failure location is compatible with stated adhesion requirements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「疊合多層落點與量測誤差方向」，因此直接證據是「累積偏差未壓縮最弱層連接裕量」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：各層平均合格不保證全堆疊對準。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay multilayer landings and error directions; the direct criterion is: Accumulated error preserves the weakest layer's landing margin. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Passing layer averages does not guarantee stack alignment."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":388,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-387"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-389","title":"多層 RC 網路量測","titleEn":"Measure multilayer RC networks","objective":"完成「多層 RC 網路量測」的證據判讀，辨識『用鏈路與電容結構分離電阻電容來源』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure multilayer rc networks by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate resistance and capacitance using chain and capacitor structures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用鏈路與電容結構分離電阻電容來源。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate resistance and capacitance using chain and capacitor structures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：延遲變化可對應至具體導線層。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：總延遲不能單獨指出材料或幾何問題。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: total delay alone cannot distinguish material and geometry problems. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「延遲變化可對應至具體導線層」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「總延遲不能單獨指出材料或幾何問題」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Total delay alone cannot distinguish material and geometry problems. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-389-k1","title":"多層 RC 網路量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure multilayer rc networks","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「用鏈路與電容結構分離電阻電容來源」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Separate resistance and capacitance using chain and capacitor structures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-389-k2","title":"多層 RC 網路量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure multilayer rc networks","text":"有效證據需支持「延遲變化可對應至具體導線層」。但總延遲不能單獨指出材料或幾何問題；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels. However, total delay alone cannot distinguish material and geometry problems; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「多層 RC 網路量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure multilayer rc networks?","options":["待電鍍表面具有連續導電路徑","厚度徑向差異有對應的供電解釋","延遲變化可對應至具體導線層"],"optionsEn":["Plating surfaces have continuous conductive paths","Radial thickness variation has a matching electrical explanation","Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「用鏈路與電容結構分離電阻電容來源」，因此直接證據是「延遲變化可對應至具體導線層」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：總延遲不能單獨指出材料或幾何問題。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate resistance and capacitance using chain and capacitor structures; the direct criterion is: Delay changes can be assigned to specific wiring levels. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Total delay alone cannot distinguish material and geometry problems."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":389,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-388"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-390","title":"互連堆疊電性放行","titleEn":"Release the interconnect stack electrically","objective":"完成「互連堆疊電性放行」的證據判讀，辨識『合併開短路、線阻與層間漏電圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release the interconnect stack electrically by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine opens, shorts, line resistance and interlevel leakage maps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，合併開短路、線阻與層間漏電圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine opens, shorts, line resistance and interlevel leakage maps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只測導通會漏掉線間短接風險。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: continuity-only testing misses interline-short risks. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只測導通會漏掉線間短接風險」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Continuity-only testing misses interline-short risks. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-390-k1","title":"互連堆疊電性放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release the interconnect stack electrically","text":"細互連的有效導體截面受阻障與襯層占比影響；成核、填充、退火與研磨需以導通、隔離及可靠度共同驗證。 本題具體操作為「合併開短路、線阻與層間漏電圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Barrier and liner fractions reduce the conducting cross-section of narrow wires; nucleation, filling, annealing and polishing require joint electrical and reliability checks. Here the concrete task is: Combine opens, shorts, line resistance and interlevel leakage maps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-390-k2","title":"互連堆疊電性放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release the interconnect stack electrically","text":"有效證據需支持「導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立」。但只測導通會漏掉線間短接風險；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied. However, continuity-only testing misses interline-short risks; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「互連堆疊電性放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release the interconnect stack electrically?","options":["導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立","孔口仍允許後續填充傳質","過覆蓋量符合後續研磨可處理範圍"],"optionsEn":["Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied","The opening still permits mass transport during filling","Overburden falls within the subsequent polish capability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「合併開短路、線阻與層間漏電圖」，因此直接證據是「導通與隔離兩種要求同時成立」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只測導通會漏掉線間短接風險。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine opens, shorts, line resistance and interlevel leakage maps; the direct criterion is: Conduction and isolation requirements are both satisfied. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Continuity-only testing misses interline-short risks."},"sourceIds":["scb-electroplating","scb-metallization","scb-cobalt","scb-cmp"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":390,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-389"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":15},{"id":"sc-m16","title":"鈍化、背面加工與晶圓完工","titleEn":"Passivation, backside processing and wafer finish","description":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-391","title":"頂層金屬完整性","titleEn":"Inspect top-metal integrity","objective":"完成「頂層金屬完整性」的證據判讀，辨識『檢查最上層導體輪廓與暴露表面』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect top-metal integrity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect top-level conductor profiles and exposed surfaces.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢查最上層導體輪廓與暴露表面。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect top-level conductor profiles and exposed surfaces. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: no unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：蓋上鈍化會使既有缺陷更難定位。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: passivation makes preexisting defects harder to locate. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「蓋上鈍化會使既有缺陷更難定位」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Passivation makes preexisting defects harder to locate. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-391-k1","title":"頂層金屬完整性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect top-metal integrity","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「檢查最上層導體輪廓與暴露表面」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Inspect top-level conductor profiles and exposed surfaces. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-391-k2","title":"頂層金屬完整性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect top-metal integrity","text":"有效證據需支持「最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接」。但蓋上鈍化會使既有缺陷更難定位；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection. However, passivation makes preexisting defects harder to locate; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「頂層金屬完整性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect top-metal integrity?","options":["薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣","最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接","收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求"],"optionsEn":["Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge","No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection","Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢查最上層導體輪廓與暴露表面」，因此直接證據是「最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：蓋上鈍化會使既有缺陷更難定位。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect top-level conductor profiles and exposed surfaces; the direct criterion is: No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Passivation makes preexisting defects harder to locate."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":391,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-390"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-392","title":"鈍化膜水氣阻隔","titleEn":"Assess passivation moisture barriers","objective":"完成「鈍化膜水氣阻隔」的證據判讀，辨識『比較膜結構與示意水氣滲入路徑』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess passivation moisture barriers by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare film structure and model moisture paths.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較膜結構與示意水氣滲入路徑。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare film structure and model moisture paths. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: a continuous barrier covers protected regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：針孔會使平均膜厚失去代表性。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: pinholes undermine average-thickness arguments. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「針孔會使平均膜厚失去代表性」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: A continuous barrier covers protected regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Pinholes undermine average-thickness arguments. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-392-k1","title":"鈍化膜水氣阻隔的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess passivation moisture barriers","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較膜結構與示意水氣滲入路徑」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare film structure and model moisture paths. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-392-k2","title":"鈍化膜水氣阻隔的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess passivation moisture barriers","text":"有效證據需支持「連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區」。但針孔會使平均膜厚失去代表性；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: A continuous barrier covers protected regions. However, pinholes undermine average-thickness arguments; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鈍化膜水氣阻隔」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess passivation moisture barriers?","options":["切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離","粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕","連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區"],"optionsEn":["Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries","Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding","A continuous barrier covers protected regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較膜結構與示意水氣滲入路徑」，因此直接證據是「連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：針孔會使平均膜厚失去代表性。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare film structure and model moisture paths; the direct criterion is: A continuous barrier covers protected regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Pinholes undermine average-thickness arguments."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":392,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-391"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-393","title":"鈍化膜應力配平","titleEn":"Balance passivation stress","objective":"完成「鈍化膜應力配平」的證據判讀，辨識『比較保護膜堆疊與晶圓曲率變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate balance passivation stress by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare passivation stacks and wafer-curvature changes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較保護膜堆疊與晶圓曲率變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare passivation stacks and wafer-curvature changes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: protection and global bow meet their respective requirements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：提高阻隔能力可能增加膜應力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: improved barrier properties can increase film stress. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「提高阻隔能力可能增加膜應力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Improved barrier properties can increase film stress. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-393-k1","title":"鈍化膜應力配平的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of balance passivation stress","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較保護膜堆疊與晶圓曲率變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare passivation stacks and wafer-curvature changes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-393-k2","title":"鈍化膜應力配平的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for balance passivation stress","text":"有效證據需支持「保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求」。但提高阻隔能力可能增加膜應力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements. However, improved barrier properties can increase film stress; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「鈍化膜應力配平」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for balance passivation stress?","options":["保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求","密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷","表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據"],"optionsEn":["Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements","The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions","Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較保護膜堆疊與晶圓曲率變化」，因此直接證據是「保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：提高阻隔能力可能增加膜應力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare passivation stacks and wafer-curvature changes; the direct criterion is: Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Improved barrier properties can increase film stress."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":393,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-392"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-394","title":"焊墊開口光罩對位","titleEn":"Align pad-opening masks","objective":"完成「焊墊開口光罩對位」的證據判讀，辨識『把鈍化開口疊合金屬焊墊與保護邊界』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate align pad-opening masks by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay openings on pads and protective boundaries.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把鈍化開口疊合金屬焊墊與保護邊界。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay openings on pads and protective boundaries. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: openings retain required pad-edge coverage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：開口偏移可能暴露非接合區金屬。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: misalignment can expose nonbonding metal regions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「開口偏移可能暴露非接合區金屬」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Openings retain required pad-edge coverage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Misalignment can expose nonbonding metal regions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-394-k1","title":"焊墊開口光罩對位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of align pad-opening masks","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「把鈍化開口疊合金屬焊墊與保護邊界」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Overlay openings on pads and protective boundaries. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-394-k2","title":"焊墊開口光罩對位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for align pad-opening masks","text":"有效證據需支持「開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋」。但開口偏移可能暴露非接合區金屬；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Openings retain required pad-edge coverage. However, misalignment can expose nonbonding metal regions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「焊墊開口光罩對位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for align pad-opening masks?","options":["量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚","開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋","敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區"],"optionsEn":["The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness","Openings retain required pad-edge coverage","Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「把鈍化開口疊合金屬焊墊與保護邊界」，因此直接證據是「開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：開口偏移可能暴露非接合區金屬。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay openings on pads and protective boundaries; the direct criterion is: Openings retain required pad-edge coverage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Misalignment can expose nonbonding metal regions."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":394,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-393"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-395","title":"焊墊開口蝕刻","titleEn":"Inspect pad-opening etch","objective":"完成「焊墊開口蝕刻」的證據判讀，辨識『對照開口底部清除與金屬表面損傷』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect pad-opening etch by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare bottom clearance and pad-metal damage.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照開口底部清除與金屬表面損傷。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare bottom clearance and pad-metal damage. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過度蝕刻可能降低後續接合品質。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: overetch can reduce subsequent bonding quality. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過度蝕刻可能降低後續接合品質」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Overetch can reduce subsequent bonding quality. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-395-k1","title":"焊墊開口蝕刻的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect pad-opening etch","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「對照開口底部清除與金屬表面損傷」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare bottom clearance and pad-metal damage. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-395-k2","title":"焊墊開口蝕刻的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect pad-opening etch","text":"有效證據需支持「介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整」。但過度蝕刻可能降低後續接合品質；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact. However, overetch can reduce subsequent bonding quality; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「焊墊開口蝕刻」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect pad-opening etch?","options":["氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件","局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現","介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整"],"optionsEn":["Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions","Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported","Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照開口底部清除與金屬表面損傷」，因此直接證據是「介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過度蝕刻可能降低後續接合品質。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare bottom clearance and pad-metal damage; the direct criterion is: Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Overetch can reduce subsequent bonding quality."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":395,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-394"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-396","title":"焊墊表面殘留","titleEn":"Inspect pad-surface residues","objective":"完成「焊墊表面殘留」的證據判讀，辨識『分辨介電殘渣、腐蝕物與有機污染』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect pad-surface residues by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish dielectric residue, corrosion and organic contamination.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分辨介電殘渣、腐蝕物與有機污染。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish dielectric residue, corrosion and organic contamination. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：污染種類由相容的分析證據支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不同殘留混同會選錯清潔策略。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: confusing residue types leads to an unsuitable cleaning strategy. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「污染種類由相容的分析證據支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不同殘留混同會選錯清潔策略」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Confusing residue types leads to an unsuitable cleaning strategy. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-396-k1","title":"焊墊表面殘留的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect pad-surface residues","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「分辨介電殘渣、腐蝕物與有機污染」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish dielectric residue, corrosion and organic contamination. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-396-k2","title":"焊墊表面殘留的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect pad-surface residues","text":"有效證據需支持「污染種類由相容的分析證據支持」。但不同殘留混同會選錯清潔策略；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence. However, confusing residue types leads to an unsuitable cleaning strategy; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「焊墊表面殘留」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect pad-surface residues?","options":["污染種類由相容的分析證據支持","接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離","翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄"],"optionsEn":["Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence","Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable","Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「分辨介電殘渣、腐蝕物與有機污染」，因此直接證據是「污染種類由相容的分析證據支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不同殘留混同會選錯清潔策略。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish dielectric residue, corrosion and organic contamination; the direct criterion is: Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Confusing residue types leads to an unsuitable cleaning strategy."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":396,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-395"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-397","title":"保護聚合物覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess protective polymer coverage","objective":"完成「保護聚合物覆蓋」的證據判讀，辨識『比較聚合膜在階梯與平坦區的厚度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess protective polymer coverage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare polymer coverage over steps and flat regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較聚合膜在階梯與平坦區的厚度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare polymer coverage over steps and flat regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：厚膜跨階梯可能保留氣泡或空隙。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: thick films over steps can trap bubbles or voids. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「厚膜跨階梯可能保留氣泡或空隙」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Thick films over steps can trap bubbles or voids. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-397-k1","title":"保護聚合物覆蓋的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess protective polymer coverage","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較聚合膜在階梯與平坦區的厚度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare polymer coverage over steps and flat regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-397-k2","title":"保護聚合物覆蓋的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess protective polymer coverage","text":"有效證據需支持「機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊」。但厚膜跨階梯可能保留氣泡或空隙；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible. However, thick films over steps can trap bubbles or voids; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「保護聚合物覆蓋」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess protective polymer coverage?","options":["損傷減少與機械強度改善一致","機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊","薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣"],"optionsEn":["Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength","Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible","Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較聚合膜在階梯與平坦區的厚度」，因此直接證據是「機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：厚膜跨階梯可能保留氣泡或空隙。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare polymer coverage over steps and flat regions; the direct criterion is: Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Thick films over steps can trap bubbles or voids."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":397,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-396"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-398","title":"聚合物固化收縮","titleEn":"Assess polymer cure shrinkage","objective":"完成「聚合物固化收縮」的證據判讀，辨識『量取固化後開口尺寸與膜厚變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess polymer cure shrinkage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure opening dimensions and thickness after curing.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取固化後開口尺寸與膜厚變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure opening dimensions and thickness after curing. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：固化前尺寸合格不保證固化後合格。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: pre-cure compliance does not prove post-cure compliance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「固化前尺寸合格不保證固化後合格」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Pre-cure compliance does not prove post-cure compliance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-398-k1","title":"聚合物固化收縮的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess polymer cure shrinkage","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「量取固化後開口尺寸與膜厚變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Measure opening dimensions and thickness after curing. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-398-k2","title":"聚合物固化收縮的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess polymer cure shrinkage","text":"有效證據需支持「收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求」。但固化前尺寸合格不保證固化後合格；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements. However, pre-cure compliance does not prove post-cure compliance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「聚合物固化收縮」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess polymer cure shrinkage?","options":["粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕","背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染","收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求"],"optionsEn":["Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding","Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination","Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取固化後開口尺寸與膜厚變化」，因此直接證據是「收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：固化前尺寸合格不保證固化後合格。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure opening dimensions and thickness after curing; the direct criterion is: Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Pre-cure compliance does not prove post-cure compliance."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":398,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-397"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-399","title":"劃片道結構辨認","titleEn":"Identify structures in dicing streets","objective":"完成「劃片道結構辨認」的證據判讀，辨識『標示測試結構、金屬與允許切割區』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify structures in dicing streets by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map test structures, metal and allowable cut regions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，標示測試結構、金屬與允許切割區。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map test structures, metal and allowable cut regions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：誤切金屬可能增加毛邊與剝離。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: cutting unintended metal can increase burrs and delamination. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「誤切金屬可能增加毛邊與剝離」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Cutting unintended metal can increase burrs and delamination. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-399-k1","title":"劃片道結構辨認的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify structures in dicing streets","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「標示測試結構、金屬與允許切割區」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Map test structures, metal and allowable cut regions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-399-k2","title":"劃片道結構辨認的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify structures in dicing streets","text":"有效證據需支持「切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離」。但誤切金屬可能增加毛邊與剝離；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries. However, cutting unintended metal can increase burrs and delamination; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「劃片道結構辨認」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify structures in dicing streets?","options":["切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離","表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據","搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries","Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement","Support points avoid unintended local bending"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「標示測試結構、金屬與允許切割區」，因此直接證據是「切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：誤切金屬可能增加毛邊與剝離。","explanationEn":"The task is to map test structures, metal and allowable cut regions; the direct criterion is: Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Cutting unintended metal can increase burrs and delamination."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":399,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-398"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-400","title":"密封環連續性","titleEn":"Inspect seal-ring continuity","objective":"完成「密封環連續性」的證據判讀，辨識『沿晶粒邊界追蹤密封環結構』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect seal-ring continuity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace seal-ring structures around die boundaries.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，沿晶粒邊界追蹤密封環結構。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace seal-ring structures around die boundaries. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一邊緣截面不能證明周邊連續。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one edge section cannot prove perimeter continuity. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一邊緣截面不能證明周邊連續」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One edge section cannot prove perimeter continuity. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-400-k1","title":"密封環連續性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect seal-ring continuity","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「沿晶粒邊界追蹤密封環結構」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Trace seal-ring structures around die boundaries. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-400-k2","title":"密封環連續性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect seal-ring continuity","text":"有效證據需支持「密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷」。但單一邊緣截面不能證明周邊連續；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions. However, one edge section cannot prove perimeter continuity; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「密封環連續性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect seal-ring continuity?","options":["分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落","密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷","量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚"],"optionsEn":["Release is complete without removing functional films","The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions","The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「沿晶粒邊界追蹤密封環結構」，因此直接證據是「密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一邊緣截面不能證明周邊連續。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace seal-ring structures around die boundaries; the direct criterion is: The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One edge section cannot prove perimeter continuity."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":400,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-399"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-401","title":"薄化前正面保護","titleEn":"Assess frontside protection before thinning","objective":"完成「薄化前正面保護」的證據判讀，辨識『比較保護膠帶與表面凸起的貼合』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess frontside protection before thinning by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare protective-tape conformity around surface features.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較保護膠帶與表面凸起的貼合。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare protective-tape conformity around surface features. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：局部懸空可放大研磨受力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unsupported areas amplify grinding loads. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「局部懸空可放大研磨受力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unsupported areas amplify grinding loads. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-401-k1","title":"薄化前正面保護的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess frontside protection before thinning","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較保護膠帶與表面凸起的貼合」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare protective-tape conformity around surface features. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-401-k2","title":"薄化前正面保護的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess frontside protection before thinning","text":"有效證據需支持「敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區」。但局部懸空可放大研磨受力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions. However, unsupported areas amplify grinding loads; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「薄化前正面保護」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess frontside protection before thinning?","options":["局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現","只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支","敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區"],"optionsEn":["Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported","The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required","Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較保護膠帶與表面凸起的貼合」，因此直接證據是「敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：局部懸空可放大研磨受力。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare protective-tape conformity around surface features; the direct criterion is: Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unsupported areas amplify grinding loads."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":401,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-400"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-402","title":"保護膠帶氣泡檢查","titleEn":"Inspect protection-tape bubbles","objective":"完成「保護膠帶氣泡檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『建立貼附氣泡與正面結構位置圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect protection-tape bubbles by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map lamination bubbles against frontside structures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，建立貼附氣泡與正面結構位置圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map lamination bubbles against frontside structures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：氣泡可在薄化時引起局部厚度偏差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: bubbles can cause local thickness variation during thinning. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「氣泡可在薄化時引起局部厚度偏差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Bubbles can cause local thickness variation during thinning. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-402-k1","title":"保護膠帶氣泡檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect protection-tape bubbles","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「建立貼附氣泡與正面結構位置圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Map lamination bubbles against frontside structures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-402-k2","title":"保護膠帶氣泡檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect protection-tape bubbles","text":"有效證據需支持「氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件」。但氣泡可在薄化時引起局部厚度偏差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions. However, bubbles can cause local thickness variation during thinning; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「保護膠帶氣泡檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect protection-tape bubbles?","options":["氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件","翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄","晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足"],"optionsEn":["Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions","Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented","Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「建立貼附氣泡與正面結構位置圖」，因此直接證據是「氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：氣泡可在薄化時引起局部厚度偏差。","explanationEn":"The task is to map lamination bubbles against frontside structures; the direct criterion is: Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Bubbles can cause local thickness variation during thinning."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":402,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-401"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-403","title":"臨時載板接合分支","titleEn":"Assess temporary carrier bonding","objective":"完成「臨時載板接合分支」的證據判讀，辨識『判讀接合界面空洞與支撐平整度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess temporary carrier bonding by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: interpret bond voids and support flatness.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，判讀接合界面空洞與支撐平整度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, interpret bond voids and support flatness. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：高接合強度不代表易於安全分離。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: high bond strength does not ensure safe release. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「高接合強度不代表易於安全分離」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: High bond strength does not ensure safe release. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-403-k1","title":"臨時載板接合分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess temporary carrier bonding","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「判讀接合界面空洞與支撐平整度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Interpret bond voids and support flatness. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-403-k2","title":"臨時載板接合分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess temporary carrier bonding","text":"有效證據需支持「接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離」。但高接合強度不代表易於安全分離；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable. However, high bond strength does not ensure safe release; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「臨時載板接合分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess temporary carrier bonding?","options":["封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致","接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離","損傷減少與機械強度改善一致"],"optionsEn":["Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt","Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable","Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「判讀接合界面空洞與支撐平整度」，因此直接證據是「接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：高接合強度不代表易於安全分離。","explanationEn":"The task is to interpret bond voids and support flatness; the direct criterion is: Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: High bond strength does not ensure safe release."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":403,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-402"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-404","title":"晶圓邊緣預修整","titleEn":"Evaluate wafer edge trimming","objective":"完成「晶圓邊緣預修整」的證據判讀，辨識『比較薄化前後邊緣形狀模型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate wafer edge trimming by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare edge-shape models before and after thinning.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較薄化前後邊緣形狀模型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare edge-shape models before and after thinning. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略邊緣形狀會增加崩邊風險。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring edge geometry increases chipping risk. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略邊緣形狀會增加崩邊風險」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring edge geometry increases chipping risk. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-404-k1","title":"晶圓邊緣預修整的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate wafer edge trimming","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較薄化前後邊緣形狀模型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare edge-shape models before and after thinning. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-404-k2","title":"晶圓邊緣預修整的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate wafer edge trimming","text":"有效證據需支持「薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣」。但忽略邊緣形狀會增加崩邊風險；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge. However, ignoring edge geometry increases chipping risk; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓邊緣預修整」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate wafer edge trimming?","options":["背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染","最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接","薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣"],"optionsEn":["Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination","No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection","Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較薄化前後邊緣形狀模型」，因此直接證據是「薄化後不形成易碎尖銳邊緣」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略邊緣形狀會增加崩邊風險。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare edge-shape models before and after thinning; the direct criterion is: Thinning does not create a fragile sharp edge. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring edge geometry increases chipping risk."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":404,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-403"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-405","title":"粗研磨去除模型","titleEn":"Model coarse backgrinding removal","objective":"完成「粗研磨去除模型」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤主要厚度去除與表面損傷層』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate model coarse backgrinding removal by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: track bulk thickness removal and surface-damage layers.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤主要厚度去除與表面損傷層。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, track bulk thickness removal and surface-damage layers. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：追求快速去除可能留下過深損傷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: fast removal can leave excessively deep damage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「追求快速去除可能留下過深損傷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Fast removal can leave excessively deep damage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-405-k1","title":"粗研磨去除模型的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of model coarse backgrinding removal","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「追蹤主要厚度去除與表面損傷層」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Track bulk thickness removal and surface-damage layers. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-405-k2","title":"粗研磨去除模型的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for model coarse backgrinding removal","text":"有效證據需支持「粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕」。但追求快速去除可能留下過深損傷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding. However, fast removal can leave excessively deep damage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「粗研磨去除模型」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for model coarse backgrinding removal?","options":["粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕","搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲","連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區"],"optionsEn":["Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding","Support points avoid unintended local bending","A continuous barrier covers protected regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤主要厚度去除與表面損傷層」，因此直接證據是「粗磨去除量為後續細磨保留餘裕」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：追求快速去除可能留下過深損傷。","explanationEn":"The task is to track bulk thickness removal and surface-damage layers; the direct criterion is: Coarse removal leaves allowance for fine grinding. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Fast removal can leave excessively deep damage."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":405,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-404"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-406","title":"細研磨表面精化","titleEn":"Assess fine-grinding refinement","objective":"完成「細研磨表面精化」的證據判讀，辨識『比較粗細研磨後的粗糙度與損傷深度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess fine-grinding refinement by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare roughness and damage depth after coarse and fine grinding.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較粗細研磨後的粗糙度與損傷深度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare roughness and damage depth after coarse and fine grinding. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: both roughness and damage measurements support improvement. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面光滑不保證次表面無裂紋。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a smooth surface does not exclude subsurface cracks. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面光滑不保證次表面無裂紋」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A smooth surface does not exclude subsurface cracks. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-406-k1","title":"細研磨表面精化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess fine-grinding refinement","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較粗細研磨後的粗糙度與損傷深度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare roughness and damage depth after coarse and fine grinding. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-406-k2","title":"細研磨表面精化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess fine-grinding refinement","text":"有效證據需支持「表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據」。但表面光滑不保證次表面無裂紋；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement. However, a smooth surface does not exclude subsurface cracks; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「細研磨表面精化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess fine-grinding refinement?","options":["保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求","表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據","分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落"],"optionsEn":["Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements","Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement","Release is complete without removing functional films"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較粗細研磨後的粗糙度與損傷深度」，因此直接證據是「表面改善有粗糙度與損傷的雙重證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面光滑不保證次表面無裂紋。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare roughness and damage depth after coarse and fine grinding; the direct criterion is: Both roughness and damage measurements support improvement. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A smooth surface does not exclude subsurface cracks."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":406,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-405"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-407","title":"非接觸厚度量測","titleEn":"Measure thickness without contact","objective":"完成「非接觸厚度量測」的證據判讀，辨識『比較矽厚度量測與膠帶載板厚度』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure thickness without contact by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate silicon thickness from tape and carrier thickness.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較矽厚度量測與膠帶載板厚度。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate silicon thickness from tape and carrier thickness. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：總堆疊厚度會混入膠層變動。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: total stack thickness includes adhesive variation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「總堆疊厚度會混入膠層變動」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Total stack thickness includes adhesive variation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-407-k1","title":"非接觸厚度量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure thickness without contact","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較矽厚度量測與膠帶載板厚度」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Separate silicon thickness from tape and carrier thickness. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-407-k2","title":"非接觸厚度量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure thickness without contact","text":"有效證據需支持「量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚」。但總堆疊厚度會混入膠層變動；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness. However, total stack thickness includes adhesive variation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「非接觸厚度量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure thickness without contact?","options":["只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支","開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋","量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚"],"optionsEn":["The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required","Openings retain required pad-edge coverage","The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較矽厚度量測與膠帶載板厚度」，因此直接證據是「量測指標對應真正的矽殘厚」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：總堆疊厚度會混入膠層變動。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate silicon thickness from tape and carrier thickness; the direct criterion is: The measured variable represents remaining silicon thickness. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Total stack thickness includes adhesive variation."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":407,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-406"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-408","title":"總厚度變異映射","titleEn":"Map total-thickness variation","objective":"完成「總厚度變異映射」的證據判讀，辨識『量測薄化晶圓不同位置的殘厚』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map total-thickness variation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure remaining thickness at multiple wafer locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量測薄化晶圓不同位置的殘厚。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure remaining thickness at multiple wafer locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：僅平均厚度會漏掉薄弱區。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mean thickness alone misses thin weak regions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「僅平均厚度會漏掉薄弱區」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mean thickness alone misses thin weak regions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-408-k1","title":"總厚度變異映射的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map total-thickness variation","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「量測薄化晶圓不同位置的殘厚」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Measure remaining thickness at multiple wafer locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-408-k2","title":"總厚度變異映射的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map total-thickness variation","text":"有效證據需支持「局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現」。但僅平均厚度會漏掉薄弱區；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported. However, mean thickness alone misses thin weak regions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「總厚度變異映射」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map total-thickness variation?","options":["局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現","晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足","介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整"],"optionsEn":["Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported","Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied","Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「量測薄化晶圓不同位置的殘厚」，因此直接證據是「局部極值與全片分佈均有呈現」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：僅平均厚度會漏掉薄弱區。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure remaining thickness at multiple wafer locations; the direct criterion is: Local extremes and wafer-wide distribution are both reported. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mean thickness alone misses thin weak regions."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":408,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-407"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-409","title":"薄化後翹曲量測","titleEn":"Measure bow after thinning","objective":"完成「薄化後翹曲量測」的證據判讀，辨識『區分自由狀態與受夾持狀態的形狀』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure bow after thinning by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: distinguish free-state shape from clamped shape.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分自由狀態與受夾持狀態的形狀。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, distinguish free-state shape from clamped shape. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：受夾持平整不能代表自由晶圓平整。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: clamped flatness does not establish free-wafer flatness. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「受夾持平整不能代表自由晶圓平整」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Clamped flatness does not establish free-wafer flatness. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-409-k1","title":"薄化後翹曲量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure bow after thinning","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「區分自由狀態與受夾持狀態的形狀」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Distinguish free-state shape from clamped shape. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-409-k2","title":"薄化後翹曲量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure bow after thinning","text":"有效證據需支持「翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄」。但受夾持平整不能代表自由晶圓平整；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented. However, clamped flatness does not establish free-wafer flatness; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「薄化後翹曲量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure bow after thinning?","options":["污染種類由相容的分析證據支持","翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄","封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致"],"optionsEn":["Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence","Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented","Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分自由狀態與受夾持狀態的形狀」，因此直接證據是「翹曲量測的邊界條件明確記錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：受夾持平整不能代表自由晶圓平整。","explanationEn":"The task is to distinguish free-state shape from clamped shape; the direct criterion is: Boundary conditions of bow measurement are documented. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Clamped flatness does not establish free-wafer flatness."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":409,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-408"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-410","title":"研磨損傷應力消除","titleEn":"Assess grinding-damage stress relief","objective":"完成「研磨損傷應力消除」的證據判讀，辨識『比較去損傷前後裂紋深度與強度樣本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess grinding-damage stress relief by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare crack depth and strength before and after damage removal.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較去損傷前後裂紋深度與強度樣本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare crack depth and strength before and after damage removal. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：損傷減少與機械強度改善一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只看外觀不能量化強度恢復。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: appearance alone cannot quantify strength recovery. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「損傷減少與機械強度改善一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只看外觀不能量化強度恢復」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Appearance alone cannot quantify strength recovery. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-410-k1","title":"研磨損傷應力消除的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess grinding-damage stress relief","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較去損傷前後裂紋深度與強度樣本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare crack depth and strength before and after damage removal. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-410-k2","title":"研磨損傷應力消除的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess grinding-damage stress relief","text":"有效證據需支持「損傷減少與機械強度改善一致」。但只看外觀不能量化強度恢復；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength. However, appearance alone cannot quantify strength recovery; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「研磨損傷應力消除」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess grinding-damage stress relief?","options":["最終保護前無未解釋裂縫或橋接","機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊","損傷減少與機械強度改善一致"],"optionsEn":["No unexplained cracks or bridges remain before protection","Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible","Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較去損傷前後裂紋深度與強度樣本」，因此直接證據是「損傷減少與機械強度改善一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只看外觀不能量化強度恢復。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare crack depth and strength before and after damage removal; the direct criterion is: Reduced damage agrees with improved mechanical strength. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Appearance alone cannot quantify strength recovery."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":410,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-409"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-411","title":"背面清潔粒子圖","titleEn":"Map backside cleaning particles","objective":"完成「背面清潔粒子圖」的證據判讀，辨識『區分研磨碎屑與外來粒子分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map backside cleaning particles by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate grinding debris from foreign-particle patterns.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，區分研磨碎屑與外來粒子分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate grinding debris from foreign-particle patterns. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：共用清洗路徑可能轉移污染。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: shared cleaning paths can transfer contamination. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「共用清洗路徑可能轉移污染」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Shared cleaning paths can transfer contamination. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-411-k1","title":"背面清潔粒子圖的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map backside cleaning particles","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「區分研磨碎屑與外來粒子分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Separate grinding debris from foreign-particle patterns. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-411-k2","title":"背面清潔粒子圖的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map backside cleaning particles","text":"有效證據需支持「背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染」。但共用清洗路徑可能轉移污染；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination. However, shared cleaning paths can transfer contamination; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面清潔粒子圖」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map backside cleaning particles?","options":["背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染","連續阻隔路徑覆蓋需保護區","收縮後形貌仍符合介面需求"],"optionsEn":["Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination","A continuous barrier covers protected regions","Post-cure geometry still satisfies interface requirements"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「區分研磨碎屑與外來粒子分佈」，因此直接證據是「背面殘粒降低且正面未新增污染」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：共用清洗路徑可能轉移污染。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate grinding debris from foreign-particle patterns; the direct criterion is: Backside particles decrease without new frontside contamination. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Shared cleaning paths can transfer contamination."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":411,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-410"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-412","title":"薄晶圓搬運支撐","titleEn":"Assess thin-wafer handling support","objective":"完成「薄晶圓搬運支撐」的證據判讀，辨識『在示意搬運軌跡分析接觸與彎曲』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess thin-wafer handling support by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: analyze contact and bending along a model handling path.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在示意搬運軌跡分析接觸與彎曲。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, analyze contact and bending along a model handling path. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: support points avoid unintended local bending. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：厚晶圓合格軌跡未必適合薄晶圓。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a thick-wafer handling path may not suit thin wafers. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「厚晶圓合格軌跡未必適合薄晶圓」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Support points avoid unintended local bending. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A thick-wafer handling path may not suit thin wafers. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-412-k1","title":"薄晶圓搬運支撐的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess thin-wafer handling support","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「在示意搬運軌跡分析接觸與彎曲」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Analyze contact and bending along a model handling path. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-412-k2","title":"薄晶圓搬運支撐的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess thin-wafer handling support","text":"有效證據需支持「搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲」。但厚晶圓合格軌跡未必適合薄晶圓；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Support points avoid unintended local bending. However, a thick-wafer handling path may not suit thin wafers; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「薄晶圓搬運支撐」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess thin-wafer handling support?","options":["切割區與晶粒保護邊界清楚分離","搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲","保護能力與整體翹曲同時符合需求"],"optionsEn":["Cut regions are separated from die-protection boundaries","Support points avoid unintended local bending","Protection and global bow meet their respective requirements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「在示意搬運軌跡分析接觸與彎曲」，因此直接證據是「搬運支點不產生非預期局部彎曲」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：厚晶圓合格軌跡未必適合薄晶圓。","explanationEn":"The task is to analyze contact and bending along a model handling path; the direct criterion is: Support points avoid unintended local bending. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A thick-wafer handling path may not suit thin wafers."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":412,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-411"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-413","title":"載板分離後殘膠","titleEn":"Inspect residue after carrier release","objective":"完成「載板分離後殘膠」的證據判讀，辨識『比較分離後表面殘留與膜剝離影像』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect residue after carrier release by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare release residue and film-delamination images.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較分離後表面殘留與膜剝離影像。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare release residue and film-delamination images. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: release is complete without removing functional films. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：乾淨外觀可能掩蓋薄層殘膠。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a clean appearance can conceal thin adhesive residue. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「乾淨外觀可能掩蓋薄層殘膠」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Release is complete without removing functional films. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A clean appearance can conceal thin adhesive residue. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-413-k1","title":"載板分離後殘膠的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect residue after carrier release","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「比較分離後表面殘留與膜剝離影像」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Compare release residue and film-delamination images. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-413-k2","title":"載板分離後殘膠的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect residue after carrier release","text":"有效證據需支持「分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落」。但乾淨外觀可能掩蓋薄層殘膠；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Release is complete without removing functional films. However, a clean appearance can conceal thin adhesive residue; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「載板分離後殘膠」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect residue after carrier release?","options":["開口保留焊墊邊緣所需覆蓋","密封環沒有非設計開口或中斷","分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落"],"optionsEn":["Openings retain required pad-edge coverage","The ring lacks unintended gaps or interruptions","Release is complete without removing functional films"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較分離後表面殘留與膜剝離影像」，因此直接證據是「分離完成且功能膜未隨膠層脫落」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：乾淨外觀可能掩蓋薄層殘膠。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare release residue and film-delamination images; the direct criterion is: Release is complete without removing functional films. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A clean appearance can conceal thin adhesive residue."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":413,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-412"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-414","title":"背面金屬相容分支","titleEn":"Assess optional backside metallization","objective":"完成「背面金屬相容分支」的證據判讀，辨識『對照背面金屬用途與基板電位配置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess optional backside metallization by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: match optional backside metal to substrate-potential requirements.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照背面金屬用途與基板電位配置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, match optional backside metal to substrate-potential requirements. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：所有晶片一律鍍背金屬會引入錯誤假設。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: universal backside metallization is an invalid assumption. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「所有晶片一律鍍背金屬會引入錯誤假設」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Universal backside metallization is an invalid assumption. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-414-k1","title":"背面金屬相容分支的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess optional backside metallization","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「對照背面金屬用途與基板電位配置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Match optional backside metal to substrate-potential requirements. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-414-k2","title":"背面金屬相容分支的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess optional backside metallization","text":"有效證據需支持「只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支」。但所有晶片一律鍍背金屬會引入錯誤假設；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required. However, universal backside metallization is an invalid assumption; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面金屬相容分支」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess optional backside metallization?","options":["只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支","介電殘留清除且焊墊表面完整","敏感結構受支撐且無顯著懸空區"],"optionsEn":["The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required","Dielectric residue clears while the pad surface remains intact","Sensitive features are supported without substantial unsupported regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照背面金屬用途與基板電位配置」，因此直接證據是「只有需要背面電接觸的路線使用此分支」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：所有晶片一律鍍背金屬會引入錯誤假設。","explanationEn":"The task is to match optional backside metal to substrate-potential requirements; the direct criterion is: The branch is used only where backside electrical contact is required. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Universal backside metallization is an invalid assumption."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":414,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-413"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-415","title":"完工晶圓外觀與厚度放行","titleEn":"Release finished-wafer appearance and thickness","objective":"完成「完工晶圓外觀與厚度放行」的證據判讀，辨識『聯合審查崩邊、刮傷、殘厚及翹曲圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate release finished-wafer appearance and thickness by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: review chipping, scratches, thickness and bow together.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，聯合審查崩邊、刮傷、殘厚及翹曲圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, review chipping, scratches, thickness and bow together. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單看良好區域照片會漏掉局部破損。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a good-area photograph can miss local damage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單看良好區域照片會漏掉局部破損」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A good-area photograph can miss local damage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-415-k1","title":"完工晶圓外觀與厚度放行的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of release finished-wafer appearance and thickness","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「聯合審查崩邊、刮傷、殘厚及翹曲圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Review chipping, scratches, thickness and bow together. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-415-k2","title":"完工晶圓外觀與厚度放行的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for release finished-wafer appearance and thickness","text":"有效證據需支持「晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足」。但單看良好區域照片會漏掉局部破損；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied. However, a good-area photograph can miss local damage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「完工晶圓外觀與厚度放行」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for release finished-wafer appearance and thickness?","options":["氣泡位置不破壞題定支撐條件","晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足","污染種類由相容的分析證據支持"],"optionsEn":["Bubble locations preserve the stated support conditions","Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied","Contamination type is supported by suitable analytical evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「聯合審查崩邊、刮傷、殘厚及翹曲圖」，因此直接證據是「晶粒可用區與後續設備夾持需求皆滿足」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單看良好區域照片會漏掉局部破損。","explanationEn":"The task is to review chipping, scratches, thickness and bow together; the direct criterion is: Usable die regions and downstream handling needs are satisfied. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A good-area photograph can miss local damage."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":415,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-414"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-416","title":"完工晶圓與封裝介面交接","titleEn":"Handoff finished wafers to packaging","objective":"完成「完工晶圓與封裝介面交接」的證據判讀，辨識『核對焊墊表面、晶圓厚度及晶粒座標版本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate handoff finished wafers to packaging by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: cross-check pad surfaces, wafer thickness and die-map versions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，核對焊墊表面、晶圓厚度及晶粒座標版本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, cross-check pad surfaces, wafer thickness and die-map versions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：座標版本錯配會把好壞晶粒標反。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a map-version mismatch can misidentify good and bad die. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「座標版本錯配會把好壞晶粒標反」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A map-version mismatch can misidentify good and bad die. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-416-k1","title":"完工晶圓與封裝介面交接的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of handoff finished wafers to packaging","text":"鈍化保護與薄化支撐要一起設計；晶圓厚度、殘餘損傷、翹曲與後續封裝介面是不同放行項。 本題具體操作為「核對焊墊表面、晶圓厚度及晶粒座標版本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Passivation protection and thinning support are designed together; thickness, residual damage, bow and packaging interfaces require separate acceptance evidence. Here the concrete task is: Cross-check pad surfaces, wafer thickness and die-map versions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-416-k2","title":"完工晶圓與封裝介面交接的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for handoff finished wafers to packaging","text":"有效證據需支持「封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致」。但座標版本錯配會把好壞晶粒標反；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt. However, a map-version mismatch can misidentify good and bad die; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「完工晶圓與封裝介面交接」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for handoff finished wafers to packaging?","options":["機械緩衝覆蓋不阻擋必要焊墊","接合區提供連續支撐且可後續分離","封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致"],"optionsEn":["Mechanical buffer coverage leaves required pads accessible","Bonded regions provide continuous support and remain releasable","Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「核對焊墊表面、晶圓厚度及晶粒座標版本」，因此直接證據是「封裝端接收的物理與資料介面一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：座標版本錯配會把好壞晶粒標反。","explanationEn":"The task is to cross-check pad surfaces, wafer thickness and die-map versions; the direct criterion is: Physical and data interfaces agree for packaging receipt. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A map-version mismatch can misidentify good and bad die."},"sourceIds":["scb-deposition","scb-grinding","scb-stressrelief","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":416,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-415"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":16},{"id":"sc-m17","title":"線上檢查、量測與統計製程管制","titleEn":"Inline inspection, metrology and SPC","description":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-417","title":"量測座標重定位","titleEn":"Relocate metrology coordinates","objective":"完成「量測座標重定位」的證據判讀，辨識『把晶圓缺口、晶粒與量測點座標對齊』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate relocate metrology coordinates by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: align wafer-notch, die and measurement-site coordinates.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把晶圓缺口、晶粒與量測點座標對齊。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, align wafer-notch, die and measurement-site coordinates. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：重複量測指向相同實體結構。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: repeated measurements address the same physical structure. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：座標旋轉錯誤會製造假空間漂移。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a coordinate rotation creates false spatial drift. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「重複量測指向相同實體結構」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「座標旋轉錯誤會製造假空間漂移」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Repeated measurements address the same physical structure. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A coordinate rotation creates false spatial drift. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-417-k1","title":"量測座標重定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of relocate metrology coordinates","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「把晶圓缺口、晶粒與量測點座標對齊」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Align wafer-notch, die and measurement-site coordinates. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-417-k2","title":"量測座標重定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for relocate metrology coordinates","text":"有效證據需支持「重複量測指向相同實體結構」。但座標旋轉錯誤會製造假空間漂移；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Repeated measurements address the same physical structure. However, a coordinate rotation creates false spatial drift; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測座標重定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for relocate metrology coordinates?","options":["重複量測指向相同實體結構","粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告","真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分"],"optionsEn":["Repeated measurements address the same physical structure","Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution","Physical anomalies are separated from background variation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把晶圓缺口、晶粒與量測點座標對齊」，因此直接證據是「重複量測指向相同實體結構」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：座標旋轉錯誤會製造假空間漂移。","explanationEn":"The task is to align wafer-notch, die and measurement-site coordinates; the direct criterion is: Repeated measurements address the same physical structure. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A coordinate rotation creates false spatial drift."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":417,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-416"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-418","title":"參考標準片偏差","titleEn":"Assess reference-wafer bias","objective":"完成「參考標準片偏差」的證據判讀，辨識『將儀器讀值與可追溯參考值比對』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess reference-wafer bias by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare instrument readings with traceable reference values.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將儀器讀值與可追溯參考值比對。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare instrument readings with traceable reference values. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把參考值當絕對真值會低估不確定度。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: treating a reference as exact understates uncertainty. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把參考值當絕對真值會低估不確定度」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Treating a reference as exact understates uncertainty. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-418-k1","title":"參考標準片偏差的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess reference-wafer bias","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「將儀器讀值與可追溯參考值比對」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare instrument readings with traceable reference values. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-418-k2","title":"參考標準片偏差的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess reference-wafer bias","text":"有效證據需支持「偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄」。但把參考值當絕對真值會低估不確定度；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty. However, treating a reference as exact understates uncertainty; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「參考標準片偏差」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess reference-wafer bias?","options":["檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估","偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄","多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性"],"optionsEn":["Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter","Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty","The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將儀器讀值與可追溯參考值比對」，因此直接證據是「偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把參考值當絕對真值會低估不確定度。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare instrument readings with traceable reference values; the direct criterion is: Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Treating a reference as exact understates uncertainty."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":418,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-417"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-419","title":"量測重複性試驗","titleEn":"Evaluate measurement repeatability","objective":"完成「量測重複性試驗」的證據判讀，辨識『對同一結構重測並分離短期散布』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate measurement repeatability by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: remeasure one structure to isolate short-term scatter.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對同一結構重測並分離短期散布。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, remeasure one structure to isolate short-term scatter. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：儀器雜訊可冒充晶圓變異。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: instrument noise can mimic wafer variation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「儀器雜訊可冒充晶圓變異」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Instrument noise can mimic wafer variation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-419-k1","title":"量測重複性試驗的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate measurement repeatability","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「對同一結構重測並分離短期散布」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Remeasure one structure to isolate short-term scatter. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-419-k2","title":"量測重複性試驗的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate measurement repeatability","text":"有效證據需支持「重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化」。但儀器雜訊可冒充晶圓變異；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest. However, instrument noise can mimic wafer variation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測重複性試驗」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate measurement repeatability?","options":["模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理","對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋","重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化"],"optionsEn":["Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible","Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation","Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對同一結構重測並分離短期散布」，因此直接證據是「重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：儀器雜訊可冒充晶圓變異。","explanationEn":"The task is to remeasure one structure to isolate short-term scatter; the direct criterion is: Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Instrument noise can mimic wafer variation."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":419,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-418"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-420","title":"量測再現性分解","titleEn":"Separate measurement reproducibility","objective":"完成「量測再現性分解」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同操作者與機台的交叉量測』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate separate measurement reproducibility by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare crossed measurements across operators and tools.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同操作者與機台的交叉量測。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare crossed measurements across operators and tools. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：混用機台會把校正差當製程差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mixed tools can turn calibration differences into apparent process differences. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「混用機台會把校正差當製程差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mixed tools can turn calibration differences into apparent process differences. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-420-k1","title":"量測再現性分解的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of separate measurement reproducibility","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較不同操作者與機台的交叉量測」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare crossed measurements across operators and tools. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-420-k2","title":"量測再現性分解的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for separate measurement reproducibility","text":"有效證據需支持「機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計」。但混用機台會把校正差當製程差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately. However, mixed tools can turn calibration differences into apparent process differences; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測再現性分解」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for separate measurement reproducibility?","options":["機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計","可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定","複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群"],"optionsEn":["Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately","Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified","Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同操作者與機台的交叉量測」，因此直接證據是「機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：混用機台會把校正差當製程差。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare crossed measurements across operators and tools; the direct criterion is: Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mixed tools can turn calibration differences into apparent process differences."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":420,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-419"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-421","title":"量測線性與範圍","titleEn":"Assess metrology linearity and range","objective":"完成「量測線性與範圍」的證據判讀，辨識『用不同尺寸參考結構檢查量測偏差』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess metrology linearity and range by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: check bias using reference structures spanning the range.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用不同尺寸參考結構檢查量測偏差。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, check bias using reference structures spanning the range. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單點校正不能保證全範圍準確。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: single-point calibration does not establish full-range accuracy. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單點校正不能保證全範圍準確」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Single-point calibration does not establish full-range accuracy. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-421-k1","title":"量測線性與範圍的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess metrology linearity and range","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「用不同尺寸參考結構檢查量測偏差」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Check bias using reference structures spanning the range. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-421-k2","title":"量測線性與範圍的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess metrology linearity and range","text":"有效證據需支持「偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢」。但單點校正不能保證全範圍準確；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend. However, single-point calibration does not establish full-range accuracy; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測線性與範圍」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess metrology linearity and range?","options":["漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化","偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢","差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件"],"optionsEn":["Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset","Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend","Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「用不同尺寸參考結構檢查量測偏差」，因此直接證據是「偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單點校正不能保證全範圍準確。","explanationEn":"The task is to check bias using reference structures spanning the range; the direct criterion is: Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Single-point calibration does not establish full-range accuracy."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":421,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-420"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-422","title":"CD-SEM 邊緣判定","titleEn":"Assess CD-SEM edge detection","objective":"完成「CD-SEM 邊緣判定」的證據判讀，辨識『比較閾值與影像邊緣模型的尺寸結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess cd-sem edge detection by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dimensions from threshold and edge-model methods.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較閾值與影像邊緣模型的尺寸結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dimensions from threshold and edge-model methods. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：演算法更換可造成非物理的線寬跳變。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: algorithm changes can cause nonphysical CD jumps. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「演算法更換可造成非物理的線寬跳變」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Algorithm changes can cause nonphysical CD jumps. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-422-k1","title":"CD-SEM 邊緣判定的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess cd-sem edge detection","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較閾值與影像邊緣模型的尺寸結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare dimensions from threshold and edge-model methods. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-422-k2","title":"CD-SEM 邊緣判定的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess cd-sem edge detection","text":"有效證據需支持「尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性」。但演算法更換可造成非物理的線寬跳變；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent. However, algorithm changes can cause nonphysical CD jumps; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「CD-SEM 邊緣判定」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess cd-sem edge detection?","options":["標記結果可由產品區量測支持","空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚","尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性"],"optionsEn":["Target results are supported by product-area measurements","The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters","Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較閾值與影像邊緣模型的尺寸結果」，因此直接證據是「尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：演算法更換可造成非物理的線寬跳變。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dimensions from threshold and edge-model methods; the direct criterion is: Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Algorithm changes can cause nonphysical CD jumps."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":422,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-421"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-423","title":"電子束量測擾動","titleEn":"Assess electron-beam measurement effects","objective":"完成「電子束量測擾動」的證據判讀，辨識『比較連續掃描前後的敏感圖形』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess electron-beam measurement effects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare sensitive patterns before and after repeated scans.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較連續掃描前後的敏感圖形。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare sensitive patterns before and after repeated scans. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：量測本身可能改變待測光阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: measurement itself can alter the resist. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「量測本身可能改變待測光阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Measurement itself can alter the resist. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-423-k1","title":"電子束量測擾動的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess electron-beam measurement effects","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較連續掃描前後的敏感圖形」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare sensitive patterns before and after repeated scans. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-423-k2","title":"電子束量測擾動的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess electron-beam measurement effects","text":"有效證據需支持「重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變」。但量測本身可能改變待測光阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change. However, measurement itself can alter the resist; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「電子束量測擾動」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess electron-beam measurement effects?","options":["重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變","真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分","組內及組間變異對應明確來源"],"optionsEn":["Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change","Physical anomalies are separated from background variation","Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較連續掃描前後的敏感圖形」，因此直接證據是「重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：量測本身可能改變待測光阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare sensitive patterns before and after repeated scans; the direct criterion is: Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Measurement itself can alter the resist."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":423,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-422"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-424","title":"線邊粗糙度頻譜","titleEn":"Analyze line-edge roughness spectra","objective":"完成「線邊粗糙度頻譜」的證據判讀，辨識『將邊緣位置轉為空間頻率分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate analyze line-edge roughness spectra by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: convert edge positions into spatial-frequency distributions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將邊緣位置轉為空間頻率分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, convert edge positions into spatial-frequency distributions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：低解析影像會濾掉高頻粗糙度。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: low-resolution images suppress high-frequency roughness. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「低解析影像會濾掉高頻粗糙度」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Low-resolution images suppress high-frequency roughness. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-424-k1","title":"線邊粗糙度頻譜的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of analyze line-edge roughness spectra","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「將邊緣位置轉為空間頻率分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Convert edge positions into spatial-frequency distributions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-424-k2","title":"線邊粗糙度頻譜的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for analyze line-edge roughness spectra","text":"有效證據需支持「粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告」。但低解析影像會濾掉高頻粗糙度；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution. However, low-resolution images suppress high-frequency roughness; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「線邊粗糙度頻譜」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for analyze line-edge roughness spectra?","options":["特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異","粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告","檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估"],"optionsEn":["Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation","Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution","Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將邊緣位置轉為空間頻率分佈」，因此直接證據是「粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：低解析影像會濾掉高頻粗糙度。","explanationEn":"The task is to convert edge positions into spatial-frequency distributions; the direct criterion is: Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Low-resolution images suppress high-frequency roughness."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":424,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-423"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-425","title":"光學散射模型校驗","titleEn":"Validate scatterometry models","objective":"完成「光學散射模型校驗」的證據判讀，辨識『對照散射模型反演與截面參考資料』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate validate scatterometry models by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare scatterometric inversion with sectional references.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照散射模型反演與截面參考資料。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare scatterometric inversion with sectional references. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不同幾何可能產生相似光學光譜。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: different geometries can produce similar optical spectra. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不同幾何可能產生相似光學光譜」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Different geometries can produce similar optical spectra. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-425-k1","title":"光學散射模型校驗的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of validate scatterometry models","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「對照散射模型反演與截面參考資料」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare scatterometric inversion with sectional references. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-425-k2","title":"光學散射模型校驗的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for validate scatterometry models","text":"有效證據需支持「多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性」。但不同幾何可能產生相似光學光譜；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations. However, different geometries can produce similar optical spectra; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「光學散射模型校驗」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for validate scatterometry models?","options":["對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋","持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分","多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性"],"optionsEn":["Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation","Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise","The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照散射模型反演與截面參考資料」，因此直接證據是「多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不同幾何可能產生相似光學光譜。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare scatterometric inversion with sectional references; the direct criterion is: The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Different geometries can produce similar optical spectra."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":425,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-424"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-426","title":"橢圓偏光多層膜擬合","titleEn":"Fit multilayer ellipsometry","objective":"完成「橢圓偏光多層膜擬合」的證據判讀，辨識『比較單層假設與實際多層膜模型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate fit multilayer ellipsometry by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare a single-layer assumption with the multilayer model.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較單層假設與實際多層膜模型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare a single-layer assumption with the multilayer model. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過多自由參數可能只是在擬合雜訊。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: too many free parameters can fit noise. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過多自由參數可能只是在擬合雜訊」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Too many free parameters can fit noise. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-426-k1","title":"橢圓偏光多層膜擬合的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of fit multilayer ellipsometry","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較單層假設與實際多層膜模型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare a single-layer assumption with the multilayer model. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-426-k2","title":"橢圓偏光多層膜擬合的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for fit multilayer ellipsometry","text":"有效證據需支持「模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理」。但過多自由參數可能只是在擬合雜訊；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible. However, too many free parameters can fit noise; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「橢圓偏光多層膜擬合」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for fit multilayer ellipsometry?","options":["模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理","複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群","穩定性與符合規格分開下結論"],"optionsEn":["Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible","Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups","Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較單層假設與實際多層膜模型」，因此直接證據是「模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過多自由參數可能只是在擬合雜訊。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare a single-layer assumption with the multilayer model; the direct criterion is: Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Too many free parameters can fit noise."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":426,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-425"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-427","title":"AFM 探針形狀影響","titleEn":"Assess AFM tip-shape effects","objective":"完成「AFM 探針形狀影響」的證據判讀，辨識『比較尖端卷積模型與量得的窄溝輪廓』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess afm tip-shape effects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare tip-convolution models with measured narrow trenches.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較尖端卷積模型與量得的窄溝輪廓。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare tip-convolution models with measured narrow trenches. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：探針太鈍會把窄結構量得過寬。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a blunt tip can broaden narrow features. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「探針太鈍會把窄結構量得過寬」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A blunt tip can broaden narrow features. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-427-k1","title":"AFM 探針形狀影響的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess afm tip-shape effects","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較尖端卷積模型與量得的窄溝輪廓」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare tip-convolution models with measured narrow trenches. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-427-k2","title":"AFM 探針形狀影響的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess afm tip-shape effects","text":"有效證據需支持「可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定」。但探針太鈍會把窄結構量得過寬；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified. However, a blunt tip can broaden narrow features; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「AFM 探針形狀影響」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess afm tip-shape effects?","options":["能力指標的分佈假設明確可查","可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定","漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化"],"optionsEn":["Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit","Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified","Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較尖端卷積模型與量得的窄溝輪廓」，因此直接證據是「可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：探針太鈍會把窄結構量得過寬。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare tip-convolution models with measured narrow trenches; the direct criterion is: Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A blunt tip can broaden narrow features."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":427,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-426"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-428","title":"膜應力量測基準扣除","titleEn":"Subtract baseline in stress metrology","objective":"完成「膜應力量測基準扣除」的證據判讀，辨識『以同片沉積前後曲率建立差分』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate subtract baseline in stress metrology by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use same-wafer curvature before and after deposition.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，以同片沉積前後曲率建立差分。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use same-wafer curvature before and after deposition. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：改變夾持條件會混入機械假訊號。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: changed clamping introduces mechanical artifacts. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「改變夾持條件會混入機械假訊號」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Changed clamping introduces mechanical artifacts. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-428-k1","title":"膜應力量測基準扣除的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of subtract baseline in stress metrology","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「以同片沉積前後曲率建立差分」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Use same-wafer curvature before and after deposition. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-428-k2","title":"膜應力量測基準扣除的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for subtract baseline in stress metrology","text":"有效證據需支持「差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件」。但改變夾持條件會混入機械假訊號；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions. However, changed clamping introduces mechanical artifacts; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「膜應力量測基準扣除」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for subtract baseline in stress metrology?","options":["空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚","不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測","差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件"],"optionsEn":["The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters","Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements","Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「以同片沉積前後曲率建立差分」，因此直接證據是「差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：改變夾持條件會混入機械假訊號。","explanationEn":"The task is to use same-wafer curvature before and after deposition; the direct criterion is: Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Changed clamping introduces mechanical artifacts."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":428,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-427"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-429","title":"套刻標記與產品偏差","titleEn":"Assess overlay-target representativeness","objective":"完成「套刻標記與產品偏差」的證據判讀，辨識『比較專用套刻標記與產品圖形的偏差』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess overlay-target representativeness by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dedicated overlay targets with product patterns.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較專用套刻標記與產品圖形的偏差。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dedicated overlay targets with product patterns. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：標記結果可由產品區量測支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: target results are supported by product-area measurements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：標記對準不保證實際元件對準。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: aligned targets do not prove aligned device patterns. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「標記結果可由產品區量測支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「標記對準不保證實際元件對準」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Target results are supported by product-area measurements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Aligned targets do not prove aligned device patterns. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-429-k1","title":"套刻標記與產品偏差的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess overlay-target representativeness","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較專用套刻標記與產品圖形的偏差」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare dedicated overlay targets with product patterns. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-429-k2","title":"套刻標記與產品偏差的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess overlay-target representativeness","text":"有效證據需支持「標記結果可由產品區量測支持」。但標記對準不保證實際元件對準；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Target results are supported by product-area measurements. However, aligned targets do not prove aligned device patterns; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「套刻標記與產品偏差」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess overlay-target representativeness?","options":["標記結果可由產品區量測支持","組內及組間變異對應明確來源","復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持"],"optionsEn":["Target results are supported by product-area measurements","Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings","Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較專用套刻標記與產品圖形的偏差」，因此直接證據是「標記結果可由產品區量測支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：標記對準不保證實際元件對準。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dedicated overlay targets with product patterns; the direct criterion is: Target results are supported by product-area measurements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Aligned targets do not prove aligned device patterns."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":429,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-428"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-430","title":"明場缺陷對比","titleEn":"Inspect bright-field defect contrast","objective":"完成「明場缺陷對比」的證據判讀，辨識『比較明場影像中的圖形差異與參考晶粒』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect bright-field defect contrast by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare bright-field pattern differences with reference dies.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較明場影像中的圖形差異與參考晶粒。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare bright-field pattern differences with reference dies. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: physical anomalies are separated from background variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：照明差異可能增加假缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: illumination differences can increase nuisance detections. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「照明差異可能增加假缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Physical anomalies are separated from background variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Illumination differences can increase nuisance detections. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-430-k1","title":"明場缺陷對比的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect bright-field defect contrast","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較明場影像中的圖形差異與參考晶粒」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare bright-field pattern differences with reference dies. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-430-k2","title":"明場缺陷對比的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect bright-field defect contrast","text":"有效證據需支持「真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分」。但照明差異可能增加假缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Physical anomalies are separated from background variation. However, illumination differences can increase nuisance detections; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「明場缺陷對比」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect bright-field defect contrast?","options":["重複量測指向相同實體結構","真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分","特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異"],"optionsEn":["Repeated measurements address the same physical structure","Physical anomalies are separated from background variation","Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較明場影像中的圖形差異與參考晶粒」，因此直接證據是「真正形貌異常與背景變動可區分」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：照明差異可能增加假缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare bright-field pattern differences with reference dies; the direct criterion is: Physical anomalies are separated from background variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Illumination differences can increase nuisance detections."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":430,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-429"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-431","title":"暗場散射缺陷檢出","titleEn":"Detect dark-field scattering defects","objective":"完成「暗場散射缺陷檢出」的證據判讀，辨識『把散射亮點與表面粒子位置比對』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate detect dark-field scattering defects by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: match scattering spots to surface-particle locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把散射亮點與表面粒子位置比對。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, match scattering spots to surface-particle locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：表面粗糙度可能被分類成顆粒。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: surface roughness can be classified as particles. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「表面粗糙度可能被分類成顆粒」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Surface roughness can be classified as particles. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-431-k1","title":"暗場散射缺陷檢出的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of detect dark-field scattering defects","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「把散射亮點與表面粒子位置比對」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Match scattering spots to surface-particle locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-431-k2","title":"暗場散射缺陷檢出的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for detect dark-field scattering defects","text":"有效證據需支持「檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估」。但表面粗糙度可能被分類成顆粒；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter. However, surface roughness can be classified as particles; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「暗場散射缺陷檢出」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for detect dark-field scattering defects?","options":["持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分","偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄","檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估"],"optionsEn":["Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise","Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty","Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「把散射亮點與表面粒子位置比對」，因此直接證據是「檢出靈敏度與背景散射一同評估」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：表面粗糙度可能被分類成顆粒。","explanationEn":"The task is to match scattering spots to surface-particle locations; the direct criterion is: Detection sensitivity is assessed with background scatter. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Surface roughness can be classified as particles."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":431,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-430"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-432","title":"電子束電壓對比","titleEn":"Interpret e-beam voltage contrast","objective":"完成「電子束電壓對比」的證據判讀，辨識『比較浮接與接地結構的對比圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret e-beam voltage contrast by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare contrast from floating and grounded structures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較浮接與接地結構的對比圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare contrast from floating and grounded structures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：充電狀態不同也可能改變亮度。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: different charging states can change brightness. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「充電狀態不同也可能改變亮度」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Different charging states can change brightness. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-432-k1","title":"電子束電壓對比的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret e-beam voltage contrast","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較浮接與接地結構的對比圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare contrast from floating and grounded structures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-432-k2","title":"電子束電壓對比的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret e-beam voltage contrast","text":"有效證據需支持「對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋」。但充電狀態不同也可能改變亮度；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation. However, different charging states can change brightness; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「電子束電壓對比」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret e-beam voltage contrast?","options":["對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋","穩定性與符合規格分開下結論","重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化"],"optionsEn":["Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation","Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions","Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較浮接與接地結構的對比圖」，因此直接證據是「對比異常具有合理的電連通解釋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：充電狀態不同也可能改變亮度。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare contrast from floating and grounded structures; the direct criterion is: Contrast anomalies have a plausible connectivity explanation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Different charging states can change brightness."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":432,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-431"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-433","title":"缺陷複判抽樣","titleEn":"Sample defects for review","objective":"完成「缺陷複判抽樣」的證據判讀，辨識『從不同分類與尺寸群選擇複判樣本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate sample defects for review by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: select review samples across defect classes and sizes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從不同分類與尺寸群選擇複判樣本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, select review samples across defect classes and sizes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: review includes rare but high-risk defect groups. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只選最顯眼缺陷會造成抽樣偏誤。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: selecting only conspicuous defects biases sampling. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只選最顯眼缺陷會造成抽樣偏誤」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Selecting only conspicuous defects biases sampling. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-433-k1","title":"缺陷複判抽樣的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of sample defects for review","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「從不同分類與尺寸群選擇複判樣本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Select review samples across defect classes and sizes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-433-k2","title":"缺陷複判抽樣的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for sample defects for review","text":"有效證據需支持「複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群」。但只選最顯眼缺陷會造成抽樣偏誤；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups. However, selecting only conspicuous defects biases sampling; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「缺陷複判抽樣」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for sample defects for review?","options":["機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計","複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群","能力指標的分佈假設明確可查"],"optionsEn":["Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately","Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups","Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「從不同分類與尺寸群選擇複判樣本」，因此直接證據是「複判涵蓋少見但高風險缺陷群」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只選最顯眼缺陷會造成抽樣偏誤。","explanationEn":"The task is to select review samples across defect classes and sizes; the direct criterion is: Review includes rare but high-risk defect groups. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Selecting only conspicuous defects biases sampling."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":433,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-432"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-434","title":"假缺陷與漏檢取捨","titleEn":"Balance nuisance detections and misses","objective":"完成「假缺陷與漏檢取捨」的證據判讀，辨識『比較檢出門檻改變時的驗證標籤』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate balance nuisance detections and misses by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare validated labels as detection thresholds change.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較檢出門檻改變時的驗證標籤。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare validated labels as detection thresholds change. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：降低報點數不等同降低真缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: fewer reported sites do not imply fewer true defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「降低報點數不等同降低真缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Fewer reported sites do not imply fewer true defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-434-k1","title":"假缺陷與漏檢取捨的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of balance nuisance detections and misses","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較檢出門檻改變時的驗證標籤」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare validated labels as detection thresholds change. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-434-k2","title":"假缺陷與漏檢取捨的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for balance nuisance detections and misses","text":"有效證據需支持「漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化」。但降低報點數不等同降低真缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset. However, fewer reported sites do not imply fewer true defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「假缺陷與漏檢取捨」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for balance nuisance detections and misses?","options":["不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測","偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢","漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化"],"optionsEn":["Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements","Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend","Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較檢出門檻改變時的驗證標籤」，因此直接證據是「漏檢與誤報以同一資料集量化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：降低報點數不等同降低真缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare validated labels as detection thresholds change; the direct criterion is: Misses and false alarms are quantified on the same dataset. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Fewer reported sites do not imply fewer true defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":434,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-433"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-435","title":"晶圓空間變異分解","titleEn":"Decompose spatial wafer variation","objective":"完成「晶圓空間變異分解」的證據判讀，辨識『分離徑向、方位與局部殘差特徵』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate decompose spatial wafer variation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate radial, azimuthal and local residual features.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分離徑向、方位與局部殘差特徵。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate radial, azimuthal and local residual features. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過度平滑會掩蓋局部異常。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess smoothing hides local excursions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過度平滑會掩蓋局部異常」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess smoothing hides local excursions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-435-k1","title":"晶圓空間變異分解的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of decompose spatial wafer variation","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「分離徑向、方位與局部殘差特徵」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Separate radial, azimuthal and local residual features. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-435-k2","title":"晶圓空間變異分解的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for decompose spatial wafer variation","text":"有效證據需支持「空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚」。但過度平滑會掩蓋局部異常；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters. However, excess smoothing hides local excursions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓空間變異分解」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for decompose spatial wafer variation?","options":["空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚","復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持","尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性"],"optionsEn":["The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters","Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence","Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「分離徑向、方位與局部殘差特徵」，因此直接證據是「空間模型不抹除具有製程意義的群聚」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過度平滑會掩蓋局部異常。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate radial, azimuthal and local residual features; the direct criterion is: The spatial model preserves process-relevant clusters. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess smoothing hides local excursions."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":435,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-434"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-436","title":"合理子群建立","titleEn":"Form rational SPC subgroups","objective":"完成「合理子群建立」的證據判讀，辨識『按相近製程條件分組示意量測序列』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate form rational spc subgroups by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: group measurements under similar process conditions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，按相近製程條件分組示意量測序列。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, group measurements under similar process conditions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：組內及組間變異對應明確來源。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: within- and between-group variation have defined meanings. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：任意混批會扭曲管制界限。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: arbitrary lot mixing distorts control limits. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「組內及組間變異對應明確來源」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「任意混批會扭曲管制界限」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Arbitrary lot mixing distorts control limits. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-436-k1","title":"合理子群建立的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of form rational spc subgroups","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「按相近製程條件分組示意量測序列」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Group measurements under similar process conditions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-436-k2","title":"合理子群建立的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for form rational spc subgroups","text":"有效證據需支持「組內及組間變異對應明確來源」。但任意混批會扭曲管制界限；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings. However, arbitrary lot mixing distorts control limits; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「合理子群建立」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for form rational spc subgroups?","options":["重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變","組內及組間變異對應明確來源","重複量測指向相同實體結構"],"optionsEn":["Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change","Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings","Repeated measurements address the same physical structure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「按相近製程條件分組示意量測序列」，因此直接證據是「組內及組間變異對應明確來源」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：任意混批會扭曲管制界限。","explanationEn":"The task is to group measurements under similar process conditions; the direct criterion is: Within- and between-group variation have defined meanings. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Arbitrary lot mixing distorts control limits."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":436,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-435"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-437","title":"Shewhart 圖基線審查","titleEn":"Review Shewhart-chart baselines","objective":"完成「Shewhart 圖基線審查」的證據判讀，辨識『從穩定歷史段計算中心與散布』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate review shewhart-chart baselines by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: estimate center and spread from stable historical segments.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從穩定歷史段計算中心與散布。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, estimate center and spread from stable historical segments. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: special-cause events are not treated as normal variation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把異常納入基線會放寬警報門檻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: including excursions widens alarm limits. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把異常納入基線會放寬警報門檻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Including excursions widens alarm limits. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-437-k1","title":"Shewhart 圖基線審查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of review shewhart-chart baselines","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「從穩定歷史段計算中心與散布」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Estimate center and spread from stable historical segments. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-437-k2","title":"Shewhart 圖基線審查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for review shewhart-chart baselines","text":"有效證據需支持「特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異」。但把異常納入基線會放寬警報門檻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation. However, including excursions widens alarm limits; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「Shewhart 圖基線審查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for review shewhart-chart baselines?","options":["偏差與參考值不確定度一同記錄","粗糙度頻帶與取樣解析度一起報告","特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異"],"optionsEn":["Bias is recorded together with reference uncertainty","Roughness bands are reported with sampling resolution","Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「從穩定歷史段計算中心與散布」，因此直接證據是「特殊原因事件未被直接當成正常變異」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把異常納入基線會放寬警報門檻。","explanationEn":"The task is to estimate center and spread from stable historical segments; the direct criterion is: Special-cause events are not treated as normal variation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Including excursions widens alarm limits."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":437,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-436"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-438","title":"EWMA 小漂移檢出","titleEn":"Detect small drifts with EWMA","objective":"完成「EWMA 小漂移檢出」的證據判讀，辨識『比較移動加權指標與原始時間序列』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate detect small drifts with ewma by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare exponentially weighted indicators with raw time series.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較移動加權指標與原始時間序列。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare exponentially weighted indicators with raw time series. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略時間相關性可能產生過多警報。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring autocorrelation can create excessive alarms. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略時間相關性可能產生過多警報」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring autocorrelation can create excessive alarms. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-438-k1","title":"EWMA 小漂移檢出的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of detect small drifts with ewma","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較移動加權指標與原始時間序列」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare exponentially weighted indicators with raw time series. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-438-k2","title":"EWMA 小漂移檢出的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for detect small drifts with ewma","text":"有效證據需支持「持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分」。但忽略時間相關性可能產生過多警報；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise. However, ignoring autocorrelation can create excessive alarms; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「EWMA 小漂移檢出」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for detect small drifts with ewma?","options":["持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分","重複散布小於待辨識的製程變化","多參數解沒有未辨識的高度相關性"],"optionsEn":["Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise","Repeatability scatter is below the process change of interest","The solution lacks unrecognized strong parameter correlations"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較移動加權指標與原始時間序列」，因此直接證據是「持續小偏移可與單點雜訊區分」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略時間相關性可能產生過多警報。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare exponentially weighted indicators with raw time series; the direct criterion is: Persistent small shifts are distinguished from isolated noise. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring autocorrelation can create excessive alarms."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":438,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-437"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-439","title":"管制界限與規格分離","titleEn":"Separate control limits from specifications","objective":"完成「管制界限與規格分離」的證據判讀，辨識『將製程分布與設計容許範圍疊合』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate separate control limits from specifications by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay process distributions and design allowances.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將製程分布與設計容許範圍疊合。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay process distributions and design allowances. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：穩定性與符合規格分開下結論。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：穩定製程仍可能持續製造不合格品。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a stable process can consistently produce nonconforming output. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「穩定性與符合規格分開下結論」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「穩定製程仍可能持續製造不合格品」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A stable process can consistently produce nonconforming output. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-439-k1","title":"管制界限與規格分離的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of separate control limits from specifications","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「將製程分布與設計容許範圍疊合」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Overlay process distributions and design allowances. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-439-k2","title":"管制界限與規格分離的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for separate control limits from specifications","text":"有效證據需支持「穩定性與符合規格分開下結論」。但穩定製程仍可能持續製造不合格品；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions. However, a stable process can consistently produce nonconforming output; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「管制界限與規格分離」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for separate control limits from specifications?","options":["模型殘差改善且參數維持物理合理","穩定性與符合規格分開下結論","機台及操作者貢獻可獨立估計"],"optionsEn":["Residuals improve while parameters remain physically plausible","Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions","Tool and operator contributions can be estimated separately"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將製程分布與設計容許範圍疊合」，因此直接證據是「穩定性與符合規格分開下結論」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：穩定製程仍可能持續製造不合格品。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay process distributions and design allowances; the direct criterion is: Stability and specification compliance receive separate conclusions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A stable process can consistently produce nonconforming output."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":439,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-438"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-440","title":"製程能力適用性","titleEn":"Assess capability-index applicability","objective":"完成「製程能力適用性」的證據判讀，辨識『檢查分佈形狀與穩定性再估能力』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess capability-index applicability by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: check distribution shape and stability before estimating capability.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢查分佈形狀與穩定性再估能力。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, check distribution shape and stability before estimating capability. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：能力指標的分佈假設明確可查。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不穩定資料的能力值容易誤導。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: capability estimates from unstable data are misleading. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「能力指標的分佈假設明確可查」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不穩定資料的能力值容易誤導」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Capability estimates from unstable data are misleading. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-440-k1","title":"製程能力適用性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess capability-index applicability","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「檢查分佈形狀與穩定性再估能力」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Check distribution shape and stability before estimating capability. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-440-k2","title":"製程能力適用性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess capability-index applicability","text":"有效證據需支持「能力指標的分佈假設明確可查」。但不穩定資料的能力值容易誤導；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit. However, capability estimates from unstable data are misleading; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「製程能力適用性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess capability-index applicability?","options":["偏差不隨尺度產生未校正趨勢","可達溝底與側壁區域均明確界定","能力指標的分佈假設明確可查"],"optionsEn":["Bias has no uncorrected scale-dependent trend","Accessible bottoms and sidewall regions are identified","Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢查分佈形狀與穩定性再估能力」，因此直接證據是「能力指標的分佈假設明確可查」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不穩定資料的能力值容易誤導。","explanationEn":"The task is to check distribution shape and stability before estimating capability; the direct criterion is: Distribution assumptions behind capability indices are explicit. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Capability estimates from unstable data are misleading."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":440,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-439"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-441","title":"虛擬量測不確定度","titleEn":"Assess virtual-metrology uncertainty","objective":"完成「虛擬量測不確定度」的證據判讀，辨識『比較預測值、實測值與模型信賴區間』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess virtual-metrology uncertainty by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare predictions, measurements and model uncertainty intervals.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較預測值、實測值與模型信賴區間。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare predictions, measurements and model uncertainty intervals. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：模型外推可能給出自信但錯誤的數值。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: extrapolation can yield confident but wrong values. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「模型外推可能給出自信但錯誤的數值」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Extrapolation can yield confident but wrong values. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-441-k1","title":"虛擬量測不確定度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess virtual-metrology uncertainty","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「比較預測值、實測值與模型信賴區間」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Compare predictions, measurements and model uncertainty intervals. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-441-k2","title":"虛擬量測不確定度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess virtual-metrology uncertainty","text":"有效證據需支持「不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測」。但模型外推可能給出自信但錯誤的數值；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements. However, extrapolation can yield confident but wrong values; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「虛擬量測不確定度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess virtual-metrology uncertainty?","options":["不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測","尺寸定義與演算法設定具有一致性","差分扣除保留一致支撐及溫度條件"],"optionsEn":["Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements","Dimension definitions and algorithm settings are consistent","Baseline subtraction preserves support and temperature conditions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較預測值、實測值與模型信賴區間」，因此直接證據是「不確定度增加時會觸發實體量測」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：模型外推可能給出自信但錯誤的數值。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare predictions, measurements and model uncertainty intervals; the direct criterion is: Higher uncertainty triggers physical measurements. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Extrapolation can yield confident but wrong values."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":441,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-440"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-442","title":"量測異常封鎖與復歸","titleEn":"Contain and clear metrology excursions","objective":"完成「量測異常封鎖與復歸」的證據判讀，辨識『用參考片區分量測漂移與真製程漂移』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate contain and clear metrology excursions by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use reference wafers to separate metrology and process drift.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用參考片區分量測漂移與真製程漂移。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use reference wafers to separate metrology and process drift. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recovery is supported by reference and product evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只重設警報會保留未解決根因。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: resetting alarms alone preserves the unresolved cause. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只重設警報會保留未解決根因」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Resetting alarms alone preserves the unresolved cause. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-442-k1","title":"量測異常封鎖與復歸的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of contain and clear metrology excursions","text":"缺陷檢查回答哪裡有異常，量測回答物理量是多少；統計管制需先確認量測系統及穩定基線，管制界限不等同設計規格。 本題具體操作為「用參考片區分量測漂移與真製程漂移」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Inspection locates anomalies while metrology estimates physical quantities; statistical control requires a qualified measurement system and stable baseline, and control limits are not specifications. Here the concrete task is: Use reference wafers to separate metrology and process drift. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-442-k2","title":"量測異常封鎖與復歸的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for contain and clear metrology excursions","text":"有效證據需支持「復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持」。但只重設警報會保留未解決根因；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence. However, resetting alarms alone preserves the unresolved cause; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「量測異常封鎖與復歸」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for contain and clear metrology excursions?","options":["標記結果可由產品區量測支持","復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持","重測未導致可辨識尺寸或充電改變"],"optionsEn":["Target results are supported by product-area measurements","Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence","Repeated scanning causes no discernible size or charging change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「用參考片區分量測漂移與真製程漂移」，因此直接證據是「復歸由獨立參考與產品證據共同支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只重設警報會保留未解決根因。","explanationEn":"The task is to use reference wafers to separate metrology and process drift; the direct criterion is: Recovery is supported by reference and product evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Resetting alarms alone preserves the unresolved cause."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-metrology","scb-spc","scb-virtual","scb-cdsem","scb-afm"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":442,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-441"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":17},{"id":"sc-m18","title":"電性製程監控與晶圓針測","titleEn":"Electrical process control and wafer probing","description":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-443","title":"探針台晶圓座標配準","titleEn":"Register probe-station wafer coordinates","objective":"完成「探針台晶圓座標配準」的證據判讀，辨識『對齊缺口、參考晶粒與探針測試座標』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate register probe-station wafer coordinates by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: align notch, reference die and probe-test coordinates.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對齊缺口、參考晶粒與探針測試座標。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, align notch, reference die and probe-test coordinates. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: every test landing maps to the intended die. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：座標鏡射可把電性結果寫入錯晶粒。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mirrored coordinates assign results to the wrong die. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「座標鏡射可把電性結果寫入錯晶粒」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Every test landing maps to the intended die. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mirrored coordinates assign results to the wrong die. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-443-k1","title":"探針台晶圓座標配準的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of register probe-station wafer coordinates","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「對齊缺口、參考晶粒與探針測試座標」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Align notch, reference die and probe-test coordinates. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-443-k2","title":"探針台晶圓座標配準的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for register probe-station wafer coordinates","text":"有效證據需支持「所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒」。但座標鏡射可把電性結果寫入錯晶粒；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Every test landing maps to the intended die. However, mirrored coordinates assign results to the wrong die; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「探針台晶圓座標配準」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for register probe-station wafer coordinates?","options":["量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性","比較已正規化且未受限流主導","所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒"],"optionsEn":["Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior","The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited","Every test landing maps to the intended die"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對齊缺口、參考晶粒與探針測試座標」，因此直接證據是「所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：座標鏡射可把電性結果寫入錯晶粒。","explanationEn":"The task is to align notch, reference die and probe-test coordinates; the direct criterion is: Every test landing maps to the intended die. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mirrored coordinates assign results to the wrong die."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":443,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-442"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-444","title":"探針焊墊接觸區","titleEn":"Inspect probe-to-pad landing","objective":"完成「探針焊墊接觸區」的證據判讀，辨識『比較針痕位置與焊墊開口邊界』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect probe-to-pad landing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare probe marks with pad-opening boundaries.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較針痕位置與焊墊開口邊界。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare probe marks with pad-opening boundaries. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: probe marks stay within the permitted pad region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：邊緣落針可能造成不穩定接觸或剝膜。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: edge landing can cause unstable contact or delamination. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「邊緣落針可能造成不穩定接觸或剝膜」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Edge landing can cause unstable contact or delamination. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-444-k1","title":"探針焊墊接觸區的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect probe-to-pad landing","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較針痕位置與焊墊開口邊界」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare probe marks with pad-opening boundaries. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-444-k2","title":"探針焊墊接觸區的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect probe-to-pad landing","text":"有效證據需支持「針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界」。但邊緣落針可能造成不穩定接觸或剝膜；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region. However, edge landing can cause unstable contact or delamination; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「探針焊墊接觸區」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect probe-to-pad landing?","options":["針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界","引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理","關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查"],"optionsEn":["Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region","Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately","Off-current is measurable with background verification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較針痕位置與焊墊開口邊界」，因此直接證據是「針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：邊緣落針可能造成不穩定接觸或剝膜。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare probe marks with pad-opening boundaries; the direct criterion is: Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Edge landing can cause unstable contact or delamination."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":444,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-443"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-445","title":"探針平面度","titleEn":"Assess probe coplanarity","objective":"完成「探針平面度」的證據判讀，辨識『檢視多針接觸先後與針痕深淺』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess probe coplanarity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect contact timing and mark depth across probes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢視多針接觸先後與針痕深淺。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect contact timing and mark depth across probes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：所有必要端點具相容接觸條件。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: all required terminals have compatible contact conditions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：部分針未接觸會製造假開路。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: uncontacted probes produce false opens. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「所有必要端點具相容接觸條件」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「部分針未接觸會製造假開路」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: All required terminals have compatible contact conditions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Uncontacted probes produce false opens. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-445-k1","title":"探針平面度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess probe coplanarity","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「檢視多針接觸先後與針痕深淺」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Inspect contact timing and mark depth across probes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-445-k2","title":"探針平面度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess probe coplanarity","text":"有效證據需支持「所有必要端點具相容接觸條件」。但部分針未接觸會製造假開路；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: All required terminals have compatible contact conditions. However, uncontacted probes produce false opens; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「探針平面度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess probe coplanarity?","options":["漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別","所有必要端點具相容接觸條件","各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則"],"optionsEn":["Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path","All required terminals have compatible contact conditions","Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢視多針接觸先後與針痕深淺」，因此直接證據是「所有必要端點具相容接觸條件」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：部分針未接觸會製造假開路。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect contact timing and mark depth across probes; the direct criterion is: All required terminals have compatible contact conditions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Uncontacted probes produce false opens."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":445,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-444"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-446","title":"探針接觸電阻驗證","titleEn":"Verify probe contact resistance","objective":"完成「探針接觸電阻驗證」的證據判讀，辨識『使用參考導通結構重複落針』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate verify probe contact resistance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: repeat touchdowns on reference continuity structures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，使用參考導通結構重複落針。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, repeat touchdowns on reference continuity structures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：接觸漂移可能被誤判為晶片失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: contact drift may be mistaken for device failure. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「接觸漂移可能被誤判為晶片失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Contact drift may be mistaken for device failure. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-446-k1","title":"探針接觸電阻驗證的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of verify probe contact resistance","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「使用參考導通結構重複落針」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Repeat touchdowns on reference continuity structures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-446-k2","title":"探針接觸電阻驗證的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for verify probe contact resistance","text":"有效證據需支持「接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值」。但接觸漂移可能被誤判為晶片失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement. However, contact drift may be mistaken for device failure; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「探針接觸電阻驗證」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for verify probe contact resistance?","options":["擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉","體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分","接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值"],"optionsEn":["The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion","Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable","Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「使用參考導通結構重複落針」，因此直接證據是「接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：接觸漂移可能被誤判為晶片失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to repeat touchdowns on reference continuity structures; the direct criterion is: Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Contact drift may be mistaken for device failure."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":446,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-445"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-447","title":"探針清潔前後比較","titleEn":"Compare probes before and after cleaning","objective":"完成「探針清潔前後比較」的證據判讀，辨識『比較清潔前後接觸散布與針尖影像』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate compare probes before and after cleaning by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare contact scatter and tip images before and after cleaning.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較清潔前後接觸散布與針尖影像。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare contact scatter and tip images before and after cleaning. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：頻繁清潔也可能加速針尖磨耗。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: frequent cleaning can accelerate tip wear. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「頻繁清潔也可能加速針尖磨耗」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Frequent cleaning can accelerate tip wear. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-447-k1","title":"探針清潔前後比較的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of compare probes before and after cleaning","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較清潔前後接觸散布與針尖影像」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare contact scatter and tip images before and after cleaning. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-447-k2","title":"探針清潔前後比較的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for compare probes before and after cleaning","text":"有效證據需支持「改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持」。但頻繁清潔也可能加速針尖磨耗；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement. However, frequent cleaning can accelerate tip wear; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「探針清潔前後比較」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for compare probes before and after cleaning?","options":["改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持","閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得","串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查"],"optionsEn":["Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement","Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature","Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較清潔前後接觸散布與針尖影像」，因此直接證據是「改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：頻繁清潔也可能加速針尖磨耗。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare contact scatter and tip images before and after cleaning; the direct criterion is: Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Frequent cleaning can accelerate tip wear."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":447,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-446"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-448","title":"溫控載台穩定性","titleEn":"Assess thermal-chuck stability","objective":"完成「溫控載台穩定性」的證據判讀，辨識『比較載台設定、實測與晶粒電性時間序列』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess thermal-chuck stability by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare chuck settings, measured temperature and electrical time traces.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較載台設定、實測與晶粒電性時間序列。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare chuck settings, measured temperature and electrical time traces. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未穩態測試會混入溫漂。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: testing before equilibrium introduces thermal drift. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未穩態測試會混入溫漂」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Testing before equilibrium introduces thermal drift. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-448-k1","title":"溫控載台穩定性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess thermal-chuck stability","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較載台設定、實測與晶粒電性時間序列」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare chuck settings, measured temperature and electrical time traces. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-448-k2","title":"溫控載台穩定性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess thermal-chuck stability","text":"有效證據需支持「電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態」。但未穩態測試會混入溫漂；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition. However, testing before equilibrium introduces thermal drift; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「溫控載台穩定性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess thermal-chuck stability?","options":["線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄","電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態","跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制"],"optionsEn":["Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented","Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition","Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較載台設定、實測與晶粒電性時間序列」，因此直接證據是「電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未穩態測試會混入溫漂。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare chuck settings, measured temperature and electrical time traces; the direct criterion is: Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Testing before equilibrium introduces thermal drift."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":448,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-447"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-449","title":"低電流守護與遮蔽","titleEn":"Assess guarding and shielding","objective":"完成「低電流守護與遮蔽」的證據判讀，辨識『比較守護接法前後的空載漏電』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess guarding and shielding by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare open-circuit leakage with and without guarding.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較守護接法前後的空載漏電。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare open-circuit leakage with and without guarding. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: background leakage is below the device signal of interest. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：量測線路漏電可能高於元件漏電。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: fixture leakage can exceed device leakage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「量測線路漏電可能高於元件漏電」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Background leakage is below the device signal of interest. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Fixture leakage can exceed device leakage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-449-k1","title":"低電流守護與遮蔽的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess guarding and shielding","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較守護接法前後的空載漏電」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare open-circuit leakage with and without guarding. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-449-k2","title":"低電流守護與遮蔽的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess guarding and shielding","text":"有效證據需支持「背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號」。但量測線路漏電可能高於元件漏電；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Background leakage is below the device signal of interest. However, fixture leakage can exceed device leakage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「低電流守護與遮蔽」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess guarding and shielding?","options":["比較已正規化且未受限流主導","高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照","背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號"],"optionsEn":["The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited","High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions","Background leakage is below the device signal of interest"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較守護接法前後的空載漏電」，因此直接證據是「背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：量測線路漏電可能高於元件漏電。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare open-circuit leakage with and without guarding; the direct criterion is: Background leakage is below the device signal of interest. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Fixture leakage can exceed device leakage."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":449,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-448"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-450","title":"SMU 量程與限流","titleEn":"Select SMU range and compliance","objective":"完成「SMU 量程與限流」的證據判讀，辨識『核對示意掃描的量程與保護限制』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate select smu range and compliance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: check measurement range and compliance in model sweeps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，核對示意掃描的量程與保護限制。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, check measurement range and compliance in model sweeps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：被截斷曲線不代表物理飽和。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a clipped curve does not establish physical saturation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「被截斷曲線不代表物理飽和」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A clipped curve does not establish physical saturation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-450-k1","title":"SMU 量程與限流的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of select smu range and compliance","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「核對示意掃描的量程與保護限制」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Check measurement range and compliance in model sweeps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-450-k2","title":"SMU 量程與限流的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for select smu range and compliance","text":"有效證據需支持「量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性」。但被截斷曲線不代表物理飽和；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior. However, a clipped curve does not establish physical saturation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「SMU 量程與限流」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for select smu range and compliance?","options":["量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性","關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查","測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配"],"optionsEn":["Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior","Off-current is measurable with background verification","Test structures match the intended failure mode"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「核對示意掃描的量程與保護限制」，因此直接證據是「量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：被截斷曲線不代表物理飽和。","explanationEn":"The task is to check measurement range and compliance in model sweeps; the direct criterion is: Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A clipped curve does not establish physical saturation."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":450,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-449"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-451","title":"四端片電阻量測","titleEn":"Measure four-terminal sheet resistance","objective":"完成「四端片電阻量測」的證據判讀，辨識『由不同接點組合檢查薄膜電阻』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure four-terminal sheet resistance by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: check film resistance with different terminal combinations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，由不同接點組合檢查薄膜電阻。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, check film resistance with different terminal combinations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：忽略幾何因子會把尺寸差當材料差。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ignoring geometry confuses size and material effects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「忽略幾何因子會把尺寸差當材料差」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ignoring geometry confuses size and material effects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-451-k1","title":"四端片電阻量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure four-terminal sheet resistance","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「由不同接點組合檢查薄膜電阻」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Check film resistance with different terminal combinations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-451-k2","title":"四端片電阻量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure four-terminal sheet resistance","text":"有效證據需支持「引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理」。但忽略幾何因子會把尺寸差當材料差；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately. However, ignoring geometry confuses size and material effects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「四端片電阻量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure four-terminal sheet resistance?","options":["延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設","引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理","漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別"],"optionsEn":["Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions","Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately","Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「由不同接點組合檢查薄膜電阻」，因此直接證據是「引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：忽略幾何因子會把尺寸差當材料差。","explanationEn":"The task is to check film resistance with different terminal combinations; the direct criterion is: Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ignoring geometry confuses size and material effects."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":451,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-450"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-452","title":"閾值電壓抽取","titleEn":"Extract threshold voltage","objective":"完成「閾值電壓抽取」的證據判讀，辨識『在相同定義下比較轉移曲線』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate extract threshold voltage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare transfer curves using the same extraction definition.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在相同定義下比較轉移曲線。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare transfer curves using the same extraction definition. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: every sample uses the same stated threshold definition. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不同抽取法可能產生不同但合理的值。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: different extraction methods can yield different valid values. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不同抽取法可能產生不同但合理的值」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Different extraction methods can yield different valid values. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-452-k1","title":"閾值電壓抽取的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of extract threshold voltage","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「在相同定義下比較轉移曲線」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare transfer curves using the same extraction definition. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-452-k2","title":"閾值電壓抽取的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for extract threshold voltage","text":"有效證據需支持「各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則」。但不同抽取法可能產生不同但合理的值；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition. However, different extraction methods can yield different valid values; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「閾值電壓抽取」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for extract threshold voltage?","options":["體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分","列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨","各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則"],"optionsEn":["Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable","Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished","Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「在相同定義下比較轉移曲線」，因此直接證據是「各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不同抽取法可能產生不同但合理的值。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare transfer curves using the same extraction definition; the direct criterion is: Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Different extraction methods can yield different valid values."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":452,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-451"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-453","title":"次臨界擺幅量測","titleEn":"Measure subthreshold swing","objective":"完成「次臨界擺幅量測」的證據判讀，辨識『在對數電流區挑選可信線性區間』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure subthreshold swing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: select a credible linear region in log-current data.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在對數電流區挑選可信線性區間。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, select a credible linear region in log-current data. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把底噪納入擬合會扭曲斜率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: including the noise floor distorts slope. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把底噪納入擬合會扭曲斜率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Including the noise floor distorts slope. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-453-k1","title":"次臨界擺幅量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure subthreshold swing","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「在對數電流區挑選可信線性區間」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Select a credible linear region in log-current data. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-453-k2","title":"次臨界擺幅量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure subthreshold swing","text":"有效證據需支持「擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉」。但把底噪納入擬合會扭曲斜率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion. However, including the noise floor distorts slope; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「次臨界擺幅量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure subthreshold swing?","options":["擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉","串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查","結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄"],"optionsEn":["The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion","Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first","Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「在對數電流區挑選可信線性區間」，因此直接證據是「擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把底噪納入擬合會扭曲斜率。","explanationEn":"The task is to select a credible linear region in log-current data; the direct criterion is: The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Including the noise floor distorts slope."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":453,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-452"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-454","title":"汲極誘發能障降低","titleEn":"Measure drain-induced barrier lowering","objective":"完成「汲極誘發能障降低」的證據判讀，辨識『比較兩種汲極偏壓下的閾值抽取』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure drain-induced barrier lowering by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare threshold extraction at two drain biases.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較兩種汲極偏壓下的閾值抽取。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare threshold extraction at two drain biases. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: threshold shifts use the same method and temperature. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：偏壓與溫度同時改變會混淆原因。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: changing bias and temperature together confounds the cause. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「偏壓與溫度同時改變會混淆原因」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Changing bias and temperature together confounds the cause. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-454-k1","title":"汲極誘發能障降低的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure drain-induced barrier lowering","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較兩種汲極偏壓下的閾值抽取」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare threshold extraction at two drain biases. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-454-k2","title":"汲極誘發能障降低的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure drain-induced barrier lowering","text":"有效證據需支持「閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得」。但偏壓與溫度同時改變會混淆原因；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature. However, changing bias and temperature together confounds the cause; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「汲極誘發能障降低」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure drain-induced barrier lowering?","options":["恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據","閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得","線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄"],"optionsEn":["Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations","Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature","Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較兩種汲極偏壓下的閾值抽取」，因此直接證據是「閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：偏壓與溫度同時改變會混淆原因。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare threshold extraction at two drain biases; the direct criterion is: Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Changing bias and temperature together confounds the cause."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":454,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-453"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-455","title":"跨導與遷移率代理量","titleEn":"Assess transconductance and mobility proxies","objective":"完成「跨導與遷移率代理量」的證據判讀，辨識『從轉移曲線求導並檢查串聯電阻』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess transconductance and mobility proxies by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: differentiate transfer curves and inspect series resistance.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從轉移曲線求導並檢查串聯電阻。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, differentiate transfer curves and inspect series resistance. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：高跨導不能直接等同本徵遷移率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: high transconductance is not directly intrinsic mobility. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「高跨導不能直接等同本徵遷移率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: High transconductance is not directly intrinsic mobility. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-455-k1","title":"跨導與遷移率代理量的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess transconductance and mobility proxies","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「從轉移曲線求導並檢查串聯電阻」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Differentiate transfer curves and inspect series resistance. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-455-k2","title":"跨導與遷移率代理量的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess transconductance and mobility proxies","text":"有效證據需支持「跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制」。但高跨導不能直接等同本徵遷移率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats. However, high transconductance is not directly intrinsic mobility; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「跨導與遷移率代理量」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess transconductance and mobility proxies?","options":["高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照","每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄","跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions","Every good-die decision has a traceable test record","Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「從轉移曲線求導並檢查串聯電阻」，因此直接證據是「跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：高跨導不能直接等同本徵遷移率。","explanationEn":"The task is to differentiate transfer curves and inspect series resistance; the direct criterion is: Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: High transconductance is not directly intrinsic mobility."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":455,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-454"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-456","title":"導通電流比較","titleEn":"Compare on-state current","objective":"完成「導通電流比較」的證據判讀，辨識『在相同偏壓及有效寬度下比較元件』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate compare on-state current by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare devices at matched bias and effective width.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在相同偏壓及有效寬度下比較元件。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare devices at matched bias and effective width. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：比較已正規化且未受限流主導。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未正規化寬度會誤導效能排序。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unnormalized widths distort performance ranking. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「比較已正規化且未受限流主導」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未正規化寬度會誤導效能排序」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unnormalized widths distort performance ranking. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-456-k1","title":"導通電流比較的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of compare on-state current","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「在相同偏壓及有效寬度下比較元件」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare devices at matched bias and effective width. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-456-k2","title":"導通電流比較的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for compare on-state current","text":"有效證據需支持「比較已正規化且未受限流主導」。但未正規化寬度會誤導效能排序；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited. However, unnormalized widths distort performance ranking; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通電流比較」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for compare on-state current?","options":["比較已正規化且未受限流主導","測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配","所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒"],"optionsEn":["The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited","Test structures match the intended failure mode","Every test landing maps to the intended die"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「在相同偏壓及有效寬度下比較元件」，因此直接證據是「比較已正規化且未受限流主導」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未正規化寬度會誤導效能排序。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare devices at matched bias and effective width; the direct criterion is: The comparison is normalized and not compliance-limited. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unnormalized widths distort performance ranking."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":456,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-455"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-457","title":"關斷電流量測","titleEn":"Measure off-state current","objective":"完成「關斷電流量測」的證據判讀，辨識『分離通道關斷與儀器背景漏電』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure off-state current by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: separate channel off-current from background leakage.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分離通道關斷與儀器背景漏電。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, separate channel off-current from background leakage. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: off-current is measurable with background verification. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：背景扣除過度可能產生非物理負值。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess background subtraction can create nonphysical negatives. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「背景扣除過度可能產生非物理負值」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Off-current is measurable with background verification. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess background subtraction can create nonphysical negatives. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-457-k1","title":"關斷電流量測的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure off-state current","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「分離通道關斷與儀器背景漏電」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Separate channel off-current from background leakage. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-457-k2","title":"關斷電流量測的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure off-state current","text":"有效證據需支持「關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查」。但背景扣除過度可能產生非物理負值；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Off-current is measurable with background verification. However, excess background subtraction can create nonphysical negatives; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「關斷電流量測」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure off-state current?","options":["針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界","關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查","延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設"],"optionsEn":["Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region","Off-current is measurable with background verification","Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「分離通道關斷與儀器背景漏電」，因此直接證據是「關斷電流高於可辨識下限並有背景扣查」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：背景扣除過度可能產生非物理負值。","explanationEn":"The task is to separate channel off-current from background leakage; the direct criterion is: Off-current is measurable with background verification. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess background subtraction can create nonphysical negatives."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":457,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-456"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-458","title":"閘極漏電檢查","titleEn":"Inspect gate leakage","objective":"完成「閘極漏電檢查」的證據判讀，辨識『對照閘電流與汲源電流的偏壓依賴』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect gate leakage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare bias dependence of gate and drain/source currents.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照閘電流與汲源電流的偏壓依賴。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare bias dependence of gate and drain/source currents. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只量總電流可能混入接面漏電。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: total current can include junction leakage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只量總電流可能混入接面漏電」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Total current can include junction leakage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-458-k1","title":"閘極漏電檢查的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect gate leakage","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「對照閘電流與汲源電流的偏壓依賴」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare bias dependence of gate and drain/source currents. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-458-k2","title":"閘極漏電檢查的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect gate leakage","text":"有效證據需支持「漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別」。但只量總電流可能混入接面漏電；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path. However, total current can include junction leakage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「閘極漏電檢查」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect gate leakage?","options":["列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨","所有必要端點具相容接觸條件","漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別"],"optionsEn":["Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished","All required terminals have compatible contact conditions","Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照閘電流與汲源電流的偏壓依賴」，因此直接證據是「漏電路徑可由端點電流關係識別」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只量總電流可能混入接面漏電。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare bias dependence of gate and drain/source currents; the direct criterion is: Terminal-current relationships identify the leakage path. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Total current can include junction leakage."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":458,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-457"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-459","title":"接面二極體漏電","titleEn":"Measure junction-diode leakage","objective":"完成「接面二極體漏電」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同面積及周長二極體』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure junction-diode leakage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare diodes with different areas and perimeters.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同面積及周長二極體。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare diodes with different areas and perimeters. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只按面積正規化會漏掉邊緣缺陷。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: area-only normalization hides perimeter defects. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只按面積正規化會漏掉邊緣缺陷」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Area-only normalization hides perimeter defects. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-459-k1","title":"接面二極體漏電的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure junction-diode leakage","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較不同面積及周長二極體」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare diodes with different areas and perimeters. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-459-k2","title":"接面二極體漏電的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure junction-diode leakage","text":"有效證據需支持「體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分」。但只按面積正規化會漏掉邊緣缺陷；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable. However, area-only normalization hides perimeter defects; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接面二極體漏電」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure junction-diode leakage?","options":["體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分","結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄","接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值"],"optionsEn":["Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable","Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately","Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同面積及周長二極體」，因此直接證據是「體積與邊緣漏電貢獻可區分」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只按面積正規化會漏掉邊緣缺陷。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare diodes with different areas and perimeters; the direct criterion is: Bulk-area and edge leakage contributions are distinguishable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Area-only normalization hides perimeter defects."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":459,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-458"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-460","title":"MOS 電容 C–V","titleEn":"Measure MOS capacitor C–V","objective":"完成「MOS 電容 C–V」的證據判讀，辨識『比較頻率掃描的累積與耗盡區』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure mos capacitor c–v by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare accumulation and depletion over frequency sweeps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較頻率掃描的累積與耗盡區。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare accumulation and depletion over frequency sweeps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: series resistance and leakage effects are checked first. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：非理想量測可能模仿界面陷阱。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: measurement artifacts can mimic interface traps. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「非理想量測可能模仿界面陷阱」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Measurement artifacts can mimic interface traps. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-460-k1","title":"MOS 電容 C–V的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure mos capacitor c–v","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較頻率掃描的累積與耗盡區」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare accumulation and depletion over frequency sweeps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-460-k2","title":"MOS 電容 C–V的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure mos capacitor c–v","text":"有效證據需支持「串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查」。但非理想量測可能模仿界面陷阱；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first. However, measurement artifacts can mimic interface traps; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「MOS 電容 C–V」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure mos capacitor c–v?","options":["改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持","串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查","恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據"],"optionsEn":["Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement","Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first","Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較頻率掃描的累積與耗盡區」，因此直接證據是「串聯電阻及漏電影響先被檢查」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：非理想量測可能模仿界面陷阱。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare accumulation and depletion over frequency sweeps; the direct criterion is: Series resistance and leakage effects are checked first. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Measurement artifacts can mimic interface traps."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":460,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-459"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-461","title":"接觸 TLM 結構","titleEn":"Evaluate transmission-line contact structures","objective":"完成「接觸 TLM 結構」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同間距結構的總電阻』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate evaluate transmission-line contact structures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare total resistance across spacing variants.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同間距結構的總電阻。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare total resistance across spacing variants. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不良擬合截距不能當可靠接觸電阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a poor-fit intercept is not reliable contact resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不良擬合截距不能當可靠接觸電阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A poor-fit intercept is not reliable contact resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-461-k1","title":"接觸 TLM 結構的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of evaluate transmission-line contact structures","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較不同間距結構的總電阻」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare total resistance across spacing variants. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-461-k2","title":"接觸 TLM 結構的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for evaluate transmission-line contact structures","text":"有效證據需支持「線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄」。但不良擬合截距不能當可靠接觸電阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented. However, a poor-fit intercept is not reliable contact resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「接觸 TLM 結構」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for evaluate transmission-line contact structures?","options":["每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄","電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態","線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄"],"optionsEn":["Every good-die decision has a traceable test record","Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition","Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同間距結構的總電阻」，因此直接證據是「線性模型適用性與截距不確定度被記錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不良擬合截距不能當可靠接觸電阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare total resistance across spacing variants; the direct criterion is: Model validity and intercept uncertainty are documented. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A poor-fit intercept is not reliable contact resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":461,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-460"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-462","title":"導通孔鏈電性","titleEn":"Test via-chain continuity","objective":"完成「導通孔鏈電性」的證據判讀，辨識『以分段鏈結果定位跨層連接異常』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate test via-chain continuity by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use segmented chains to localize interlevel connection anomalies.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，以分段鏈結果定位跨層連接異常。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use segmented chains to localize interlevel connection anomalies. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: high-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：整體通過不能排除接近失效的尾端。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: overall passing can hide near-failure tails. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「整體通過不能排除接近失效的尾端」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Overall passing can hide near-failure tails. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-462-k1","title":"導通孔鏈電性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of test via-chain continuity","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「以分段鏈結果定位跨層連接異常」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Use segmented chains to localize interlevel connection anomalies. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-462-k2","title":"導通孔鏈電性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for test via-chain continuity","text":"有效證據需支持「高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照」。但整體通過不能排除接近失效的尾端；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions. However, overall passing can hide near-failure tails; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「導通孔鏈電性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for test via-chain continuity?","options":["高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照","所有測試落點皆對應正確晶粒","背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions","Every test landing maps to the intended die","Background leakage is below the device signal of interest"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「以分段鏈結果定位跨層連接異常」，因此直接證據是「高阻段可與幾何或缺陷區相互對照」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：整體通過不能排除接近失效的尾端。","explanationEn":"The task is to use segmented chains to localize interlevel connection anomalies; the direct criterion is: High-resistance segments map to geometry or defect regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Overall passing can hide near-failure tails."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":462,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-461"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-463","title":"梳狀與蛇形互連測試","titleEn":"Test comb and serpentine structures","objective":"完成「梳狀與蛇形互連測試」的證據判讀，辨識『分別用梳狀測短路與蛇形測斷路』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate test comb and serpentine structures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use combs for shorts and serpentines for opens.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，分別用梳狀測短路與蛇形測斷路。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use combs for shorts and serpentines for opens. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: test structures match the intended failure mode. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把兩種結構混用會降低診斷能力。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: confusing the structures reduces diagnostic power. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把兩種結構混用會降低診斷能力」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Test structures match the intended failure mode. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Confusing the structures reduces diagnostic power. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-463-k1","title":"梳狀與蛇形互連測試的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of test comb and serpentine structures","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「分別用梳狀測短路與蛇形測斷路」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Use combs for shorts and serpentines for opens. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-463-k2","title":"梳狀與蛇形互連測試的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for test comb and serpentine structures","text":"有效證據需支持「測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配」。但把兩種結構混用會降低診斷能力；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Test structures match the intended failure mode. However, confusing the structures reduces diagnostic power; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「梳狀與蛇形互連測試」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for test comb and serpentine structures?","options":["量測未因限流而被誤當元件特性","測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配","針痕留在允許區且未穿出保護邊界"],"optionsEn":["Compliance-limited data are not mistaken for device behavior","Test structures match the intended failure mode","Probe marks stay within the permitted pad region"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「分別用梳狀測短路與蛇形測斷路」，因此直接證據是「測試結構與欲辨識故障類型相匹配」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把兩種結構混用會降低診斷能力。","explanationEn":"The task is to use combs for shorts and serpentines for opens; the direct criterion is: Test structures match the intended failure mode. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Confusing the structures reduces diagnostic power."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":463,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-462"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-464","title":"環形振盪器延遲","titleEn":"Measure ring-oscillator delay","objective":"完成「環形振盪器延遲」的證據判讀，辨識『將振盪頻率對照級數與負載』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure ring-oscillator delay by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate oscillation frequency to stage count and load.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將振盪頻率對照級數與負載。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate oscillation frequency to stage count and load. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：頻率變動也可能源於電源或溫度。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: frequency variation can also arise from supply or temperature. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「頻率變動也可能源於電源或溫度」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Frequency variation can also arise from supply or temperature. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-464-k1","title":"環形振盪器延遲的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure ring-oscillator delay","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「將振盪頻率對照級數與負載」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Relate oscillation frequency to stage count and load. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-464-k2","title":"環形振盪器延遲的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure ring-oscillator delay","text":"有效證據需支持「延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設」。但頻率變動也可能源於電源或溫度；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions. However, frequency variation can also arise from supply or temperature; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「環形振盪器延遲」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure ring-oscillator delay?","options":["所有必要端點具相容接觸條件","引線貢獻與幾何修正分別處理","延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設"],"optionsEn":["All required terminals have compatible contact conditions","Lead contribution and geometry correction are treated separately","Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「將振盪頻率對照級數與負載」，因此直接證據是「延遲換算使用正確拓撲與負載假設」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：頻率變動也可能源於電源或溫度。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate oscillation frequency to stage count and load; the direct criterion is: Delay extraction uses correct topology and load assumptions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Frequency variation can also arise from supply or temperature."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":464,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-463"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-465","title":"記憶體位元失效圖","titleEn":"Map memory bit failures","objective":"完成「記憶體位元失效圖」的證據判讀，辨識『把位元錯誤位置還原至列行座標』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate map memory bit failures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map failing bits back to row and column coordinates.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把位元錯誤位置還原至列行座標。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map failing bits back to row and column coordinates. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：地址映射錯誤會製造假失效群聚。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: wrong address mapping creates false failure clusters. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「地址映射錯誤會製造假失效群聚」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Wrong address mapping creates false failure clusters. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-465-k1","title":"記憶體位元失效圖的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of map memory bit failures","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「把位元錯誤位置還原至列行座標」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Map failing bits back to row and column coordinates. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-465-k2","title":"記憶體位元失效圖的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for map memory bit failures","text":"有效證據需支持「列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨」。但地址映射錯誤會製造假失效群聚；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished. However, wrong address mapping creates false failure clusters; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「記憶體位元失效圖」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for map memory bit failures?","options":["列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨","接觸電阻穩定且不主導待測值","各樣本使用一致且明示的閾值規則"],"optionsEn":["Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished","Contact resistance is stable and does not dominate the measurement","Every sample uses the same stated threshold definition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把位元錯誤位置還原至列行座標」，因此直接證據是「列、行與孤立位元失效可分辨」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：地址映射錯誤會製造假失效群聚。","explanationEn":"The task is to map failing bits back to row and column coordinates; the direct criterion is: Row, column and isolated-bit failures are distinguished. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Wrong address mapping creates false failure clusters."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":465,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-464"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-466","title":"數位掃描測試分群","titleEn":"Classify digital scan-test failures","objective":"完成「數位掃描測試分群」的證據判讀，辨識『比較掃描鏈與功能測試失效類型』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate classify digital scan-test failures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare scan-chain and functional failure classes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較掃描鏈與功能測試失效類型。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare scan-chain and functional failure classes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一測試通過不代表全功能覆蓋。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one passing test does not establish full functional coverage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一測試通過不代表全功能覆蓋」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One passing test does not establish full functional coverage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-466-k1","title":"數位掃描測試分群的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of classify digital scan-test failures","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較掃描鏈與功能測試失效類型」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare scan-chain and functional failure classes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-466-k2","title":"數位掃描測試分群的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for classify digital scan-test failures","text":"有效證據需支持「結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄」。但單一測試通過不代表全功能覆蓋；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately. However, one passing test does not establish full functional coverage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「數位掃描測試分群」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for classify digital scan-test failures?","options":["擬合區避開儀器底噪與強反轉","結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄","改善可由污染減少與電阻穩定支持"],"optionsEn":["The fit avoids the noise floor and strong inversion","Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately","Reduced contamination and stable resistance support improvement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較掃描鏈與功能測試失效類型」，因此直接證據是「結構性與功能性故障證據分開記錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一測試通過不代表全功能覆蓋。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare scan-chain and functional failure classes; the direct criterion is: Structural and functional failure evidence is recorded separately. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One passing test does not establish full functional coverage."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":466,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-465"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-467","title":"針測重測與測試接觸區分","titleEn":"Separate retest recovery from contact issues","objective":"完成「針測重測與測試接觸區分」的證據判讀，辨識『比較原測、重落針與重新測試結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate separate retest recovery from contact issues by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare original, retouch and retest outcomes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較原測、重落針與重新測試結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare original, retouch and retest outcomes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：直接以最好一次結果放行會隱藏不穩定。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: passing the best result hides instability. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「直接以最好一次結果放行會隱藏不穩定」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Passing the best result hides instability. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-467-k1","title":"針測重測與測試接觸區分的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of separate retest recovery from contact issues","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「比較原測、重落針與重新測試結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Compare original, retouch and retest outcomes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-467-k2","title":"針測重測與測試接觸區分的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for separate retest recovery from contact issues","text":"有效證據需支持「恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據」。但直接以最好一次結果放行會隱藏不穩定；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations. However, passing the best result hides instability; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「針測重測與測試接觸區分」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for separate retest recovery from contact issues?","options":["電性擷取時溫度已達題定穩態","閾值變化由相同方法與溫度取得","恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據"],"optionsEn":["Temperature reaches the stated steady condition before acquisition","Threshold shifts use the same method and temperature","Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較原測、重落針與重新測試結果」，因此直接證據是「恢復案例可歸因至接觸或元件證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：直接以最好一次結果放行會隱藏不穩定。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare original, retouch and retest outcomes; the direct criterion is: Recovered cases have contact- or device-based explanations. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Passing the best result hides instability."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":467,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-466"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-468","title":"晶圓測試分級與座標輸出","titleEn":"Export wafer-test bins and coordinates","objective":"完成「晶圓測試分級與座標輸出」的證據判讀，辨識『核對分級規則、測試版本與晶粒地圖』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate export wafer-test bins and coordinates by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: check bin rules, test revision and die-map output.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，核對分級規則、測試版本與晶粒地圖。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, check bin rules, test revision and die-map output. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: every good-die decision has a traceable test record. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：檔案格式正確不代表座標與分級正確。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a valid file format does not prove correct coordinates or bins. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「檔案格式正確不代表座標與分級正確」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Every good-die decision has a traceable test record. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A valid file format does not prove correct coordinates or bins. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-468-k1","title":"晶圓測試分級與座標輸出的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of export wafer-test bins and coordinates","text":"電性量測必須控制接觸、漏電、溫度與儀器限制；PCM 結構用於辨識製程參數，晶粒功能測試則回答產品是否完成指定功能。 本題具體操作為「核對分級規則、測試版本與晶粒地圖」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Electrical tests control contact quality, leakage, temperature and instrument limits; PCM structures identify process parameters while functional tests evaluate product behavior. Here the concrete task is: Check bin rules, test revision and die-map output. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-468-k2","title":"晶圓測試分級與座標輸出的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for export wafer-test bins and coordinates","text":"有效證據需支持「每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄」。但檔案格式正確不代表座標與分級正確；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Every good-die decision has a traceable test record. However, a valid file format does not prove correct coordinates or bins; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓測試分級與座標輸出」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for export wafer-test bins and coordinates?","options":["每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄","背景漏電小於要辨識的元件訊號","跨導解釋保留幾何及串聯電阻限制"],"optionsEn":["Every good-die decision has a traceable test record","Background leakage is below the device signal of interest","Transconductance interpretation retains geometry and resistance caveats"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「核對分級規則、測試版本與晶粒地圖」，因此直接證據是「每個良品判定均有可追溯測試紀錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：檔案格式正確不代表座標與分級正確。","explanationEn":"The task is to check bin rules, test revision and die-map output; the direct criterion is: Every good-die decision has a traceable test record. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A valid file format does not prove correct coordinates or bins."},"sourceIds":["scb-probecards","scb-probesystems","scb-metrology","scb-lowlevel","scb-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":468,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-467"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":18},{"id":"sc-m19","title":"良率、可靠度與缺陷失效分析","titleEn":"Yield, reliability and failure analysis","description":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-469","title":"良率分母與重測去重","titleEn":"Define yield denominators and deduplicate retests","objective":"完成「良率分母與重測去重」的證據判讀，辨識『把原始測試紀錄整理成唯一晶粒結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate define yield denominators and deduplicate retests by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: reduce test records to unique die outcomes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把原始測試紀錄整理成唯一晶粒結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, reduce test records to unique die outcomes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：重測重複計數會虛增樣本數。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: counting retests repeatedly inflates sample size. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「重測重複計數會虛增樣本數」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Counting retests repeatedly inflates sample size. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-469-k1","title":"良率分母與重測去重的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of define yield denominators and deduplicate retests","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「把原始測試紀錄整理成唯一晶粒結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Reduce test records to unique die outcomes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-469-k2","title":"良率分母與重測去重的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for define yield denominators and deduplicate retests","text":"有效證據需支持「投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致」。但重測重複計數會虛增樣本數；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions. However, counting retests repeatedly inflates sample size; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「良率分母與重測去重」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for define yield denominators and deduplicate retests?","options":["截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區","投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致","候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆"],"optionsEn":["The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region","Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions","Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「把原始測試紀錄整理成唯一晶粒結果」，因此直接證據是「投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：重測重複計數會虛增樣本數。","explanationEn":"The task is to reduce test records to unique die outcomes; the direct criterion is: Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Counting retests repeatedly inflates sample size."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":469,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-468"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-470","title":"失效分級 Pareto","titleEn":"Build a failure-bin Pareto","objective":"完成「失效分級 Pareto」的證據判讀，辨識『依互斥與重疊失效分類整理數量』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate build a failure-bin pareto by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: count mutually exclusive and overlapping failure classes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，依互斥與重疊失效分類整理數量。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, count mutually exclusive and overlapping failure classes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：圖表分母與多重失效規則明示。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把重疊類別相加可能超過總晶粒數。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: summing overlapping classes can exceed the die count. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「圖表分母與多重失效規則明示」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把重疊類別相加可能超過總晶粒數」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Summing overlapping classes can exceed the die count. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-470-k1","title":"失效分級 Pareto的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of build a failure-bin pareto","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「依互斥與重疊失效分類整理數量」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Count mutually exclusive and overlapping failure classes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-470-k2","title":"失效分級 Pareto的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for build a failure-bin pareto","text":"有效證據需支持「圖表分母與多重失效規則明示」。但把重疊類別相加可能超過總晶粒數；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit. However, summing overlapping classes can exceed the die count; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「失效分級 Pareto」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for build a failure-bin pareto?","options":["結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子","結構異常可與製樣損傷區分","圖表分母與多重失效規則明示"],"optionsEn":["Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor","Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage","Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「依互斥與重疊失效分類整理數量」，因此直接證據是「圖表分母與多重失效規則明示」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把重疊類別相加可能超過總晶粒數。","explanationEn":"The task is to count mutually exclusive and overlapping failure classes; the direct criterion is: Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Summing overlapping classes can exceed the die count."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":470,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-469"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-471","title":"晶圓環狀失效圖","titleEn":"Interpret ring-shaped wafer failures","objective":"完成「晶圓環狀失效圖」的證據判讀，辨識『比較失效環帶與製程徑向量測』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret ring-shaped wafer failures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare failing rings with radial process measurements.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較失效環帶與製程徑向量測。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare failing rings with radial process measurements. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：環狀圖樣不是特定機台的唯一指紋。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a ring is not a unique fingerprint of one tool. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「環狀圖樣不是特定機台的唯一指紋」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A ring is not a unique fingerprint of one tool. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-471-k1","title":"晶圓環狀失效圖的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret ring-shaped wafer failures","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較失效環帶與製程徑向量測」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare failing rings with radial process measurements. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-471-k2","title":"晶圓環狀失效圖的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret ring-shaped wafer failures","text":"有效證據需支持「失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性」。但環狀圖樣不是特定機台的唯一指紋；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism. However, a ring is not a unique fingerprint of one tool; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓環狀失效圖」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret ring-shaped wafer failures?","options":["失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性","後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效","額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對"],"optionsEn":["Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism","Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure","Extra species are checked against location and background"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較失效環帶與製程徑向量測」，因此直接證據是「失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：環狀圖樣不是特定機台的唯一指紋。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare failing rings with radial process measurements; the direct criterion is: Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A ring is not a unique fingerprint of one tool."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":471,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-470"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-472","title":"刮傷型線性失效圖","titleEn":"Interpret scratch-like failure patterns","objective":"完成「刮傷型線性失效圖」的證據判讀，辨識『疊合線性失效與表面刮傷座標』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret scratch-like failure patterns by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: overlay linear failures and surface-scratch coordinates.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，疊合線性失效與表面刮傷座標。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, overlay linear failures and surface-scratch coordinates. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只靠視覺相似不足以證實因果。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: visual similarity alone does not establish causality. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只靠視覺相似不足以證實因果」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Visual similarity alone does not establish causality. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-472-k1","title":"刮傷型線性失效圖的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret scratch-like failure patterns","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「疊合線性失效與表面刮傷座標」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Overlay linear failures and surface-scratch coordinates. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-472-k2","title":"刮傷型線性失效圖的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret scratch-like failure patterns","text":"有效證據需支持「實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關」。但只靠視覺相似不足以證實因果；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations. However, visual similarity alone does not establish causality; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「刮傷型線性失效圖」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret scratch-like failure patterns?","options":["失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留","實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關","開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域"],"optionsEn":["Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained","Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations","Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「疊合線性失效與表面刮傷座標」，因此直接證據是「實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只靠視覺相似不足以證實因果。","explanationEn":"The task is to overlay linear failures and surface-scratch coordinates; the direct criterion is: Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Visual similarity alone does not establish causality."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":472,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-471"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-473","title":"缺陷與電性座標關聯","titleEn":"Correlate defects with electrical failures","objective":"完成「缺陷與電性座標關聯」的證據判讀，辨識『把缺陷座標轉至相同晶粒與結構座標』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate correlate defects with electrical failures by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: transform defect coordinates into the electrical-test frame.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把缺陷座標轉至相同晶粒與結構座標。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, transform defect coordinates into the electrical-test frame. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：重疊率超過適當的隨機對照。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：未校正密度會高估偶然重疊。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: uncorrected defect density exaggerates coincidental overlap. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「重疊率超過適當的隨機對照」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「未校正密度會高估偶然重疊」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Uncorrected defect density exaggerates coincidental overlap. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-473-k1","title":"缺陷與電性座標關聯的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of correlate defects with electrical failures","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「把缺陷座標轉至相同晶粒與結構座標」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Transform defect coordinates into the electrical-test frame. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-473-k2","title":"缺陷與電性座標關聯的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for correlate defects with electrical failures","text":"有效證據需支持「重疊率超過適當的隨機對照」。但未校正密度會高估偶然重疊；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline. However, uncorrected defect density exaggerates coincidental overlap; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「缺陷與電性座標關聯」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for correlate defects with electrical failures?","options":["發光位置對應可重現的失效條件","恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄","重疊率超過適當的隨機對照"],"optionsEn":["Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition","Recovery time is included in post-stress records","Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「把缺陷座標轉至相同晶粒與結構座標」，因此直接證據是「重疊率超過適當的隨機對照」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：未校正密度會高估偶然重疊。","explanationEn":"The task is to transform defect coordinates into the electrical-test frame; the direct criterion is: Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Uncorrected defect density exaggerates coincidental overlap."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":473,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-472"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-474","title":"關鍵面積與缺陷尺寸","titleEn":"Relate critical area to defect size","objective":"完成「關鍵面積與缺陷尺寸」的證據判讀，辨識『用版圖間距估算不同尺寸缺陷的影響』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate relate critical area to defect size by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: estimate defect impact from layout spacing and defect size.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用版圖間距估算不同尺寸缺陷的影響。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, estimate defect impact from layout spacing and defect size. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：良率推估包含幾何敏感度。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: yield estimates include geometric sensitivity. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：相同缺陷數不代表相同晶粒失效率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: equal defect counts do not imply equal die failure rates. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「良率推估包含幾何敏感度」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「相同缺陷數不代表相同晶粒失效率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Equal defect counts do not imply equal die failure rates. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-474-k1","title":"關鍵面積與缺陷尺寸的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of relate critical area to defect size","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「用版圖間距估算不同尺寸缺陷的影響」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Estimate defect impact from layout spacing and defect size. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-474-k2","title":"關鍵面積與缺陷尺寸的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for relate critical area to defect size","text":"有效證據需支持「良率推估包含幾何敏感度」。但相同缺陷數不代表相同晶粒失效率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity. However, equal defect counts do not imply equal die failure rates; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「關鍵面積與缺陷尺寸」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for relate critical area to defect size?","options":["良率推估包含幾何敏感度","熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致","劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容"],"optionsEn":["Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity","Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization","Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「用版圖間距估算不同尺寸缺陷的影響」，因此直接證據是「良率推估包含幾何敏感度」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：相同缺陷數不代表相同晶粒失效率。","explanationEn":"The task is to estimate defect impact from layout spacing and defect size; the direct criterion is: Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Equal defect counts do not imply equal die failure rates."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":474,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-473"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-475","title":"隨機與群聚良率模型","titleEn":"Compare random and clustered yield models","objective":"完成「隨機與群聚良率模型」的證據判讀，辨識『對照均勻與群聚缺陷下的晶粒良率』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate compare random and clustered yield models by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare die yield under uniform and clustered defects.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照均勻與群聚缺陷下的晶粒良率。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare die yield under uniform and clustered defects. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：模型選擇符合空間分佈證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：強群聚資料不適合直接套均勻模型。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: strongly clustered data do not fit a uniform model directly. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「模型選擇符合空間分佈證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「強群聚資料不適合直接套均勻模型」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Strongly clustered data do not fit a uniform model directly. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-475-k1","title":"隨機與群聚良率模型的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of compare random and clustered yield models","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「對照均勻與群聚缺陷下的晶粒良率」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare die yield under uniform and clustered defects. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-475-k2","title":"隨機與群聚良率模型的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for compare random and clustered yield models","text":"有效證據需支持「模型選擇符合空間分佈證據」。但強群聚資料不適合直接套均勻模型；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence. However, strongly clustered data do not fit a uniform model directly; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「隨機與群聚良率模型」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for compare random and clustered yield models?","options":["失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋","模型選擇符合空間分佈證據","截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區"],"optionsEn":["Failure location supports a material-transport explanation","Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence","The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照均勻與群聚缺陷下的晶粒良率」，因此直接證據是「模型選擇符合空間分佈證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：強群聚資料不適合直接套均勻模型。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare die yield under uniform and clustered defects; the direct criterion is: Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Strongly clustered data do not fit a uniform model directly."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":475,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-474"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-476","title":"製程機台履歷交叉表","titleEn":"Cross-tabulate process-tool genealogy","objective":"完成「製程機台履歷交叉表」的證據判讀，辨識『比較共同經過機台的失效群與對照群』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate cross-tabulate process-tool genealogy by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare failed and control groups sharing process tools.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較共同經過機台的失效群與對照群。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare failed and control groups sharing process tools. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：同批共現不等同機台造成失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: co-occurrence in a lot does not prove tool causation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「同批共現不等同機台造成失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Co-occurrence in a lot does not prove tool causation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-476-k1","title":"製程機台履歷交叉表的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of cross-tabulate process-tool genealogy","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較共同經過機台的失效群與對照群」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare failed and control groups sharing process tools. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-476-k2","title":"製程機台履歷交叉表的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for cross-tabulate process-tool genealogy","text":"有效證據需支持「候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆」。但同批共現不等同機台造成失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding. However, co-occurrence in a lot does not prove tool causation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「製程機台履歷交叉表」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for cross-tabulate process-tool genealogy?","options":["結構異常可與製樣損傷區分","可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制","候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆"],"optionsEn":["Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage","Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable","Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較共同經過機台的失效群與對照群」，因此直接證據是「候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：同批共現不等同機台造成失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare failed and control groups sharing process tools; the direct criterion is: Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Co-occurrence in a lot does not prove tool causation."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":476,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-475"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-477","title":"分割實驗根因驗證","titleEn":"Validate causes with split experiments","objective":"完成「分割實驗根因驗證」的證據判讀，辨識『設計僅改變候選因子的示意分組』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate validate causes with split experiments by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: form model groups varying only the candidate factor.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，設計僅改變候選因子的示意分組。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, form model groups varying only the candidate factor. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：多因子同變使改善無法歸因。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: simultaneous changes prevent attribution. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「多因子同變使改善無法歸因」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Simultaneous changes prevent attribution. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-477-k1","title":"分割實驗根因驗證的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of validate causes with split experiments","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「設計僅改變候選因子的示意分組」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Form model groups varying only the candidate factor. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-477-k2","title":"分割實驗根因驗證的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for validate causes with split experiments","text":"有效證據需支持「結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子」。但多因子同變使改善無法歸因；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor. However, simultaneous changes prevent attribution; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「分割實驗根因驗證」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for validate causes with split experiments?","options":["結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子","額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對","漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構"],"optionsEn":["Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor","Extra species are checked against location and background","Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「設計僅改變候選因子的示意分組」，因此直接證據是「結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：多因子同變使改善無法歸因。","explanationEn":"The task is to form model groups varying only the candidate factor; the direct criterion is: Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Simultaneous changes prevent attribution."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":477,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-476"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-478","title":"失效樣本保全","titleEn":"Preserve failure-analysis samples","objective":"完成「失效樣本保全」的證據判讀，辨識『記錄分析前電性、位置與既有加工歷程』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate preserve failure-analysis samples by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: record electrical state, location and prior processing before analysis.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，記錄分析前電性、位置與既有加工歷程。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, record electrical state, location and prior processing before analysis. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：先破壞樣本可能抹除關鍵證據。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: premature destruction can erase crucial evidence. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「先破壞樣本可能抹除關鍵證據」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Premature destruction can erase crucial evidence. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-478-k1","title":"失效樣本保全的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of preserve failure-analysis samples","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「記錄分析前電性、位置與既有加工歷程」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Record electrical state, location and prior processing before analysis. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-478-k2","title":"失效樣本保全的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for preserve failure-analysis samples","text":"有效證據需支持「後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效」。但先破壞樣本可能抹除關鍵證據；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure. However, premature destruction can erase crucial evidence; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「失效樣本保全」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for preserve failure-analysis samples?","options":["腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據","後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效","失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留"],"optionsEn":["The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence","Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure","Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「記錄分析前電性、位置與既有加工歷程」，因此直接證據是「後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：先破壞樣本可能抹除關鍵證據。","explanationEn":"The task is to record electrical state, location and prior processing before analysis; the direct criterion is: Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Premature destruction can erase crucial evidence."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":478,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-477"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-479","title":"非破壞定位順序","titleEn":"Sequence nondestructive localization","objective":"完成「非破壞定位順序」的證據判讀，辨識『比較電性、光學與熱影像定位結果』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate sequence nondestructive localization by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare electrical, optical and thermal localization.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較電性、光學與熱影像定位結果。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare electrical, optical and thermal localization. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：直接廣域切片可能錯過失效位置。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: broad sectioning can miss the failure site. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「直接廣域切片可能錯過失效位置」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Broad sectioning can miss the failure site. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-479-k1","title":"非破壞定位順序的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of sequence nondestructive localization","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較電性、光學與熱影像定位結果」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare electrical, optical and thermal localization. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-479-k2","title":"非破壞定位順序的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for sequence nondestructive localization","text":"有效證據需支持「開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域」。但直接廣域切片可能錯過失效位置；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning. However, broad sectioning can miss the failure site; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「非破壞定位順序」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for sequence nondestructive localization?","options":["恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄","外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間","開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域"],"optionsEn":["Recovery time is included in post-stress records","Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency","Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較電性、光學與熱影像定位結果」，因此直接證據是「開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：直接廣域切片可能錯過失效位置。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare electrical, optical and thermal localization; the direct criterion is: Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Broad sectioning can miss the failure site."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":479,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-478"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-480","title":"發光顯微定位","titleEn":"Localize with emission microscopy","objective":"完成「發光顯微定位」的證據判讀，辨識『把異常發光與電性偏壓狀態對照』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate localize with emission microscopy by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate anomalous emission to electrical bias state.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把異常發光與電性偏壓狀態對照。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate anomalous emission to electrical bias state. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：發光位置對應可重現的失效條件。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：正常元件也可能發光而造成假判。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: healthy devices can also emit and mislead interpretation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「發光位置對應可重現的失效條件」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「正常元件也可能發光而造成假判」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Healthy devices can also emit and mislead interpretation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-480-k1","title":"發光顯微定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of localize with emission microscopy","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「把異常發光與電性偏壓狀態對照」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Relate anomalous emission to electrical bias state. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-480-k2","title":"發光顯微定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for localize with emission microscopy","text":"有效證據需支持「發光位置對應可重現的失效條件」。但正常元件也可能發光而造成假判；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition. However, healthy devices can also emit and mislead interpretation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「發光顯微定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for localize with emission microscopy?","options":["發光位置對應可重現的失效條件","劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容","改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現"],"optionsEn":["Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition","Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism","Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「把異常發光與電性偏壓狀態對照」，因此直接證據是「發光位置對應可重現的失效條件」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：正常元件也可能發光而造成假判。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate anomalous emission to electrical bias state; the direct criterion is: Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Healthy devices can also emit and mislead interpretation."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":480,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-479"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-481","title":"熱點影像判讀","titleEn":"Interpret thermal hotspots","objective":"完成「熱點影像判讀」的證據判讀，辨識『比較熱影像背景與疑似漏電路徑』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate interpret thermal hotspots by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare thermal backgrounds and suspected leakage paths.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較熱影像背景與疑似漏電路徑。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare thermal backgrounds and suspected leakage paths. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：高導熱擴散會使熱點偏離故障源。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: thermal spreading can displace the apparent hotspot. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「高導熱擴散會使熱點偏離故障源」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Thermal spreading can displace the apparent hotspot. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-481-k1","title":"熱點影像判讀的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of interpret thermal hotspots","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較熱影像背景與疑似漏電路徑」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare thermal backgrounds and suspected leakage paths. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-481-k2","title":"熱點影像判讀的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for interpret thermal hotspots","text":"有效證據需支持「熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致」。但高導熱擴散會使熱點偏離故障源；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization. However, thermal spreading can displace the apparent hotspot; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「熱點影像判讀」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for interpret thermal hotspots?","options":["即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論","熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致","失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋"],"optionsEn":["Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions","Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization","Failure location supports a material-transport explanation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較熱影像背景與疑似漏電路徑」，因此直接證據是「熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：高導熱擴散會使熱點偏離故障源。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare thermal backgrounds and suspected leakage paths; the direct criterion is: Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Thermal spreading can displace the apparent hotspot."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":481,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-480"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-482","title":"FIB 截面定位","titleEn":"Target FIB cross sections","objective":"完成「FIB 截面定位」的證據判讀，辨識『以座標轉換把疑似故障切入截面』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate target fib cross sections by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use coordinate transforms to section the suspected defect.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，以座標轉換把疑似故障切入截面。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use coordinate transforms to section the suspected defect. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：切片偏移會造成找不到缺陷的假陰性。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: section misplacement creates a false negative. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「切片偏移會造成找不到缺陷的假陰性」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Section misplacement creates a false negative. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-482-k1","title":"FIB 截面定位的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of target fib cross sections","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「以座標轉換把疑似故障切入截面」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Use coordinate transforms to section the suspected defect. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-482-k2","title":"FIB 截面定位的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for target fib cross sections","text":"有效證據需支持「截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區」。但切片偏移會造成找不到缺陷的假陰性；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region. However, section misplacement creates a false negative; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「FIB 截面定位」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for target fib cross sections?","options":["可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制","投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致","截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區"],"optionsEn":["Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable","Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions","The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「以座標轉換把疑似故障切入截面」，因此直接證據是「截面確實穿過目標故障而非鄰近正常區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：切片偏移會造成找不到缺陷的假陰性。","explanationEn":"The task is to use coordinate transforms to section the suspected defect; the direct criterion is: The section intersects the target rather than an adjacent healthy region. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Section misplacement creates a false negative."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":482,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-481"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-483","title":"TEM 界面證據","titleEn":"Assess TEM interface evidence","objective":"完成「TEM 界面證據」的證據判讀，辨識『檢查界面晶格、空洞與樣品製備假象』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess tem interface evidence by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect lattice, voids and specimen-preparation artifacts.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，檢查界面晶格、空洞與樣品製備假象。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect lattice, voids and specimen-preparation artifacts. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：結構異常可與製樣損傷區分。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：離子製樣可能引入非原始非晶層。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: ion preparation can introduce an artificial amorphous layer. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「結構異常可與製樣損傷區分」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「離子製樣可能引入非原始非晶層」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Ion preparation can introduce an artificial amorphous layer. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-483-k1","title":"TEM 界面證據的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess tem interface evidence","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「檢查界面晶格、空洞與樣品製備假象」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Inspect lattice, voids and specimen-preparation artifacts. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-483-k2","title":"TEM 界面證據的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess tem interface evidence","text":"有效證據需支持「結構異常可與製樣損傷區分」。但離子製樣可能引入非原始非晶層；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage. However, ion preparation can introduce an artificial amorphous layer; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「TEM 界面證據」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess tem interface evidence?","options":["結構異常可與製樣損傷區分","漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構","圖表分母與多重失效規則明示"],"optionsEn":["Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage","Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures","Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「檢查界面晶格、空洞與樣品製備假象」，因此直接證據是「結構異常可與製樣損傷區分」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：離子製樣可能引入非原始非晶層。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect lattice, voids and specimen-preparation artifacts; the direct criterion is: Structural anomalies are separated from preparation damage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Ion preparation can introduce an artificial amorphous layer."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":483,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-482"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-484","title":"元素分析污染辨識","titleEn":"Identify contamination by elemental analysis","objective":"完成「元素分析污染辨識」的證據判讀，辨識『比較失效與正常位置的元素光譜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate identify contamination by elemental analysis by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare elemental spectra at failed and healthy locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較失效與正常位置的元素光譜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare elemental spectra at failed and healthy locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: extra species are checked against location and background. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：分析支架或保護層也可能貢獻訊號。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mounts or protective layers can contribute signals. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「分析支架或保護層也可能貢獻訊號」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Extra species are checked against location and background. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mounts or protective layers can contribute signals. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-484-k1","title":"元素分析污染辨識的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of identify contamination by elemental analysis","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較失效與正常位置的元素光譜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare elemental spectra at failed and healthy locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-484-k2","title":"元素分析污染辨識的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for identify contamination by elemental analysis","text":"有效證據需支持「額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對」。但分析支架或保護層也可能貢獻訊號；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Extra species are checked against location and background. However, mounts or protective layers can contribute signals; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「元素分析污染辨識」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for identify contamination by elemental analysis?","options":["失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性","額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對","腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據"],"optionsEn":["Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism","Extra species are checked against location and background","The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較失效與正常位置的元素光譜」，因此直接證據是「額外元素與空間位置及背景一致核對」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：分析支架或保護層也可能貢獻訊號。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare elemental spectra at failed and healthy locations; the direct criterion is: Extra species are checked against location and background. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mounts or protective layers can contribute signals."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":484,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-483"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-485","title":"閘介電時間相依崩潰","titleEn":"Assess time-dependent dielectric breakdown","objective":"完成「閘介電時間相依崩潰」的證據判讀，辨識『比較示意應力時間與失效分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess time-dependent dielectric breakdown by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare model stress duration and breakdown distributions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較示意應力時間與失效分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare model stress duration and breakdown distributions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: failure definitions and censored survivors are retained. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：刪掉未失效樣本會高估失效率。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: deleting survivors overestimates failure probability. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「刪掉未失效樣本會高估失效率」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Deleting survivors overestimates failure probability. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-485-k1","title":"閘介電時間相依崩潰的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess time-dependent dielectric breakdown","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較示意應力時間與失效分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare model stress duration and breakdown distributions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-485-k2","title":"閘介電時間相依崩潰的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess time-dependent dielectric breakdown","text":"有效證據需支持「失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留」。但刪掉未失效樣本會高估失效率；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained. However, deleting survivors overestimates failure probability; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「閘介電時間相依崩潰」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess time-dependent dielectric breakdown?","options":["外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間","實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關","失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency","Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations","Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較示意應力時間與失效分佈」，因此直接證據是「失效定義與未失效截尾樣本一起保留」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：刪掉未失效樣本會高估失效率。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare model stress duration and breakdown distributions; the direct criterion is: Failure definitions and censored survivors are retained. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Deleting survivors overestimates failure probability."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":485,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-484"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-486","title":"偏壓溫度不穩定性","titleEn":"Assess bias-temperature instability","objective":"完成「偏壓溫度不穩定性」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤閾值漂移與量測間隔中的恢復』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess bias-temperature instability by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: track threshold shifts and recovery during measurement delays.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤閾值漂移與量測間隔中的恢復。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, track threshold shifts and recovery during measurement delays. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recovery time is included in post-stress records. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不同延遲量測會產生不可比漂移。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: different delays produce incomparable shifts. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不同延遲量測會產生不可比漂移」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recovery time is included in post-stress records. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Different delays produce incomparable shifts. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-486-k1","title":"偏壓溫度不穩定性的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess bias-temperature instability","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「追蹤閾值漂移與量測間隔中的恢復」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Track threshold shifts and recovery during measurement delays. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-486-k2","title":"偏壓溫度不穩定性的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess bias-temperature instability","text":"有效證據需支持「恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄」。但不同延遲量測會產生不可比漂移；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recovery time is included in post-stress records. However, different delays produce incomparable shifts; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「偏壓溫度不穩定性」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess bias-temperature instability?","options":["恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄","改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現","重疊率超過適當的隨機對照"],"optionsEn":["Recovery time is included in post-stress records","Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics","Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤閾值漂移與量測間隔中的恢復」，因此直接證據是「恢復時間被納入應力後量測紀錄」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不同延遲量測會產生不可比漂移。","explanationEn":"The task is to track threshold shifts and recovery during measurement delays; the direct criterion is: Recovery time is included in post-stress records. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Different delays produce incomparable shifts."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":486,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-485"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-487","title":"熱載子劣化","titleEn":"Assess hot-carrier degradation","objective":"完成「熱載子劣化」的證據判讀，辨識『比較應力前後跨導與電流變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess hot-carrier degradation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare transconductance and current before and after stress.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較應力前後跨導與電流變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare transconductance and current before and after stress. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單看閾值可能漏掉其他參數劣化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: threshold alone can miss other degradation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單看閾值可能漏掉其他參數劣化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Threshold alone can miss other degradation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-487-k1","title":"熱載子劣化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess hot-carrier degradation","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較應力前後跨導與電流變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare transconductance and current before and after stress. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-487-k2","title":"熱載子劣化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess hot-carrier degradation","text":"有效證據需支持「劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容」。但單看閾值可能漏掉其他參數劣化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism. However, threshold alone can miss other degradation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「熱載子劣化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess hot-carrier degradation?","options":["良率推估包含幾何敏感度","劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容","即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論"],"optionsEn":["Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity","Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism","Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較應力前後跨導與電流變化」，因此直接證據是「劣化指標與選定偏壓機制相容」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單看閾值可能漏掉其他參數劣化。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare transconductance and current before and after stress; the direct criterion is: Degradation metrics match the selected bias mechanism. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Threshold alone can miss other degradation."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":487,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-486"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-488","title":"互連電遷移","titleEn":"Assess interconnect electromigration","objective":"完成「互連電遷移」的證據判讀，辨識『關聯電阻演化、電流方向與空洞位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess interconnect electromigration by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate resistance evolution, current direction and void location.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，關聯電阻演化、電流方向與空洞位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate resistance evolution, current direction and void location. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: failure location supports a material-transport explanation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：自熱造成的可逆電阻上升不等同失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: reversible self-heating resistance is not failure. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「自熱造成的可逆電阻上升不等同失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Failure location supports a material-transport explanation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Reversible self-heating resistance is not failure. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-488-k1","title":"互連電遷移的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess interconnect electromigration","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「關聯電阻演化、電流方向與空洞位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Relate resistance evolution, current direction and void location. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-488-k2","title":"互連電遷移的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess interconnect electromigration","text":"有效證據需支持「失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋」。但自熱造成的可逆電阻上升不等同失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Failure location supports a material-transport explanation. However, reversible self-heating resistance is not failure; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「互連電遷移」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess interconnect electromigration?","options":["投入、有效測試與合格數的定義一致","模型選擇符合空間分佈證據","失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋"],"optionsEn":["Input, valid-test and pass counts use consistent definitions","Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence","Failure location supports a material-transport explanation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「關聯電阻演化、電流方向與空洞位置」，因此直接證據是「失效位置支持材料遷移的物理解釋」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：自熱造成的可逆電阻上升不等同失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate resistance evolution, current direction and void location; the direct criterion is: Failure location supports a material-transport explanation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Reversible self-heating resistance is not failure."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":488,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-487"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-489","title":"應力誘發空洞","titleEn":"Assess stress-induced voiding","objective":"完成「應力誘發空洞」的證據判讀，辨識『比較熱歷程與無外加電流的空洞演化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess stress-induced voiding by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare thermal history and void growth without applied current.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較熱歷程與無外加電流的空洞演化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare thermal history and void growth without applied current. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：所有金屬空洞都歸電遷移會誤診。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: attributing every metal void to electromigration misdiagnoses it. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「所有金屬空洞都歸電遷移會誤診」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Attributing every metal void to electromigration misdiagnoses it. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-489-k1","title":"應力誘發空洞的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess stress-induced voiding","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較熱歷程與無外加電流的空洞演化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare thermal history and void growth without applied current. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-489-k2","title":"應力誘發空洞的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess stress-induced voiding","text":"有效證據需支持「可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制」。但所有金屬空洞都歸電遷移會誤診；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable. However, attributing every metal void to electromigration misdiagnoses it; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「應力誘發空洞」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess stress-induced voiding?","options":["可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制","圖表分母與多重失效規則明示","候選機台關聯已排查批次與時間混淆"],"optionsEn":["Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable","Denominators and multiple-failure rules are explicit","Candidate-tool association is checked for lot and time confounding"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較熱歷程與無外加電流的空洞演化」，因此直接證據是「可區分熱機應力與電流驅動機制」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：所有金屬空洞都歸電遷移會誤診。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare thermal history and void growth without applied current; the direct criterion is: Thermomechanical and current-driven mechanisms are distinguishable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Attributing every metal void to electromigration misdiagnoses it."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":489,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-488"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-490","title":"介電層間漏電劣化","titleEn":"Assess intermetal dielectric degradation","objective":"完成「介電層間漏電劣化」的證據判讀，辨識『比較相鄰導線間漏電與時間變化』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess intermetal dielectric degradation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare leakage between adjacent lines over time.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較相鄰導線間漏電與時間變化。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare leakage between adjacent lines over time. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：探針污染也可能產生假線間漏電。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: probe contamination can mimic interline leakage. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「探針污染也可能產生假線間漏電」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Probe contamination can mimic interline leakage. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-490-k1","title":"介電層間漏電劣化的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess intermetal dielectric degradation","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較相鄰導線間漏電與時間變化」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare leakage between adjacent lines over time. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-490-k2","title":"介電層間漏電劣化的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess intermetal dielectric degradation","text":"有效證據需支持「漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構」。但探針污染也可能產生假線間漏電；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures. However, probe contamination can mimic interline leakage; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「介電層間漏電劣化」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess intermetal dielectric degradation?","options":["結果差異可追溯至受控的分割因子","漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構","失效位置與候選製程機制具空間一致性"],"optionsEn":["Outcome differences trace to the controlled split factor","Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures","Failure locations spatially agree with the candidate mechanism"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較相鄰導線間漏電與時間變化」，因此直接證據是「漏電路徑對應介電隔離結構」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：探針污染也可能產生假線間漏電。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare leakage between adjacent lines over time; the direct criterion is: Leakage paths correspond to dielectric isolation structures. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Probe contamination can mimic interline leakage."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":490,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-489"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-491","title":"濕氣腐蝕機制","titleEn":"Assess moisture-corrosion mechanisms","objective":"完成「濕氣腐蝕機制」的證據判讀，辨識『對照保護層缺口、污染物與腐蝕位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess moisture-corrosion mechanisms by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: relate barrier gaps, contaminants and corrosion locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照保護層缺口、污染物與腐蝕位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, relate barrier gaps, contaminants and corrosion locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只見變色不能證明特定腐蝕機制。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: discoloration alone does not prove a corrosion mechanism. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只見變色不能證明特定腐蝕機制」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Discoloration alone does not prove a corrosion mechanism. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-491-k1","title":"濕氣腐蝕機制的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess moisture-corrosion mechanisms","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「對照保護層缺口、污染物與腐蝕位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Relate barrier gaps, contaminants and corrosion locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-491-k2","title":"濕氣腐蝕機制的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess moisture-corrosion mechanisms","text":"有效證據需支持「腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據」。但只見變色不能證明特定腐蝕機制；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence. However, discoloration alone does not prove a corrosion mechanism; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「濕氣腐蝕機制」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess moisture-corrosion mechanisms?","options":["實體刮傷與失效晶粒位置相關","後續破壞分析可回溯至原始失效","腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據"],"optionsEn":["Physical scratches correlate with failed-die locations","Destructive analysis remains traceable to the original failure","The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照保護層缺口、污染物與腐蝕位置」，因此直接證據是「腐蝕假說同時具有水氣路徑與材料證據」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只見變色不能證明特定腐蝕機制。","explanationEn":"The task is to relate barrier gaps, contaminants and corrosion locations; the direct criterion is: The hypothesis includes moisture pathways and material evidence. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Discoloration alone does not prove a corrosion mechanism."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":491,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-490"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-492","title":"加速模型外推限制","titleEn":"Assess accelerated-model extrapolation","objective":"完成「加速模型外推限制」的證據判讀，辨識『比較不同應力區間的主導失效機制』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess accelerated-model extrapolation by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dominant mechanisms across stress ranges.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較不同應力區間的主導失效機制。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dominant mechanisms across stress ranges. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：高應力可能切換機制使外推失效。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: high stress can switch mechanisms and invalidate extrapolation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「高應力可能切換機制使外推失效」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: High stress can switch mechanisms and invalidate extrapolation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-492-k1","title":"加速模型外推限制的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess accelerated-model extrapolation","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「比較不同應力區間的主導失效機制」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare dominant mechanisms across stress ranges. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-492-k2","title":"加速模型外推限制的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess accelerated-model extrapolation","text":"有效證據需支持「外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間」。但高應力可能切換機制使外推失效；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency. However, high stress can switch mechanisms and invalidate extrapolation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「加速模型外推限制」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess accelerated-model extrapolation?","options":["外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間","重疊率超過適當的隨機對照","開封或切片前已縮小疑似區域"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency","Overlap exceeds an appropriate random baseline","Suspect regions are narrowed before opening or sectioning"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較不同應力區間的主導失效機制」，因此直接證據是「外推只涵蓋已支持的同一機制區間」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：高應力可能切換機制使外推失效。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dominant mechanisms across stress ranges; the direct criterion is: Extrapolation stays within supported mechanism consistency. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: High stress can switch mechanisms and invalidate extrapolation."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":492,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-491"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-493","title":"修正後獨立驗證","titleEn":"Independently verify corrective action","objective":"完成「修正後獨立驗證」的證據判讀，辨識『用未參與調整的對照樣本檢查改善』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate independently verify corrective action by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: use samples excluded from tuning to verify improvement.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，用未參與調整的對照樣本檢查改善。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, use samples excluded from tuning to verify improvement. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：重用調整資料會過度樂觀估計效果。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: reusing tuning data overstates improvement. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「重用調整資料會過度樂觀估計效果」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Reusing tuning data overstates improvement. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-493-k1","title":"修正後獨立驗證的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of independently verify corrective action","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「用未參與調整的對照樣本檢查改善」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Use samples excluded from tuning to verify improvement. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-493-k2","title":"修正後獨立驗證的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for independently verify corrective action","text":"有效證據需支持「改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現」。但重用調整資料會過度樂觀估計效果；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics. However, reusing tuning data overstates improvement; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「修正後獨立驗證」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for independently verify corrective action?","options":["發光位置對應可重現的失效條件","改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現","良率推估包含幾何敏感度"],"optionsEn":["Emission corresponds to a reproducible failure condition","Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics","Yield estimates include geometric sensitivity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「用未參與調整的對照樣本檢查改善」，因此直接證據是「改善可跨獨立批次與指標重現」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：重用調整資料會過度樂觀估計效果。","explanationEn":"The task is to use samples excluded from tuning to verify improvement; the direct criterion is: Improvement reproduces across independent lots and metrics. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Reusing tuning data overstates improvement."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":493,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-492"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-494","title":"良率與可靠度聯合結案","titleEn":"Close yield and reliability investigations","objective":"完成「良率與可靠度聯合結案」的證據判讀，辨識『對照即時合格率與受應力後的失效證據』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate close yield and reliability investigations by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare initial conformance and post-stress failures.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照即時合格率與受應力後的失效證據。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare initial conformance and post-stress failures. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：提高出貨良率不代表壽命已改善。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: higher shipment yield does not establish better lifetime. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「提高出貨良率不代表壽命已改善」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Higher shipment yield does not establish better lifetime. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-494-k1","title":"良率與可靠度聯合結案的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of close yield and reliability investigations","text":"良率描述指定測試下的合格比例，可靠度描述隨時間與應力演變的失效；缺陷相關性需要物理證據才能轉為根因結論。 本題具體操作為「對照即時合格率與受應力後的失效證據」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"Yield describes conformance under specified tests; reliability concerns failure evolution with time and stress. Defect correlations require physical evidence before becoming root-cause conclusions. Here the concrete task is: Compare initial conformance and post-stress failures. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-494-k2","title":"良率與可靠度聯合結案的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for close yield and reliability investigations","text":"有效證據需支持「即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論」。但提高出貨良率不代表壽命已改善；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions. However, higher shipment yield does not establish better lifetime; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「良率與可靠度聯合結案」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for close yield and reliability investigations?","options":["模型選擇符合空間分佈證據","熱點與功耗異常及空間定位一致","即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論"],"optionsEn":["Model choice matches spatial-distribution evidence","Hotspots agree with power anomalies and localization","Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照即時合格率與受應力後的失效證據」，因此直接證據是「即時良率與長期機制風險分別結論」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：提高出貨良率不代表壽命已改善。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare initial conformance and post-stress failures; the direct criterion is: Initial yield and longer-term mechanism risks have separate conclusions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Higher shipment yield does not establish better lifetime."},"sourceIds":["scb-kla","scb-spc","scb-reliability","scb-reliability-models"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":494,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-493"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":19},{"id":"sc-m20","title":"先進電晶體、背面供電與製造交接","titleEn":"Advanced transistors, backside power and handoff","description":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本模組以示意模型、截面判讀及量測資料完成教學任務；此順序為學習編排，不是可直接執行的晶圓製造行程。","descriptionEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Exercises use models, cross sections and measurement datasets. The ordering is pedagogical, not an executable wafer traveler.","sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"sc-495","title":"FinFET 鰭寬與高度","titleEn":"Measure FinFET fin width and height","objective":"完成「FinFET 鰭寬與高度」的證據判讀，辨識『從立體截面比較有效通道尺寸』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate measure finfet fin width and height by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare effective channel dimensions in 3d sections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，從立體截面比較有效通道尺寸。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare effective channel dimensions in 3D sections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: fin width and exposed height are quantified separately. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單一俯視尺寸不能代表通道總寬。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one top-view dimension cannot represent total channel width. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單一俯視尺寸不能代表通道總寬」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One top-view dimension cannot represent total channel width. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-495-k1","title":"FinFET 鰭寬與高度的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of measure finfet fin width and height","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「從立體截面比較有效通道尺寸」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare effective channel dimensions in 3D sections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-495-k2","title":"FinFET 鰭寬與高度的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for measure finfet fin width and height","text":"有效證據需支持「鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化」。但單一俯視尺寸不能代表通道總寬；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately. However, one top-view dimension cannot represent total channel width; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「FinFET 鰭寬與高度」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for measure finfet fin width and height?","options":["鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化","凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存","全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離"],"optionsEn":["Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately","Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation","All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「從立體截面比較有效通道尺寸」，因此直接證據是「鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單一俯視尺寸不能代表通道總寬。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare effective channel dimensions in 3D sections; the direct criterion is: Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One top-view dimension cannot represent total channel width."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":495,"order":1,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-494"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-496","title":"FinFET 隔離層凹回","titleEn":"Assess FinFET isolation recess","objective":"完成「FinFET 隔離層凹回」的證據判讀，辨識『標示隔離層頂部與鰭側壁暴露範圍』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess finfet isolation recess by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: mark isolation height and exposed fin sidewalls.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，標示隔離層頂部與鰭側壁暴露範圍。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, mark isolation height and exposed fin sidewalls. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：凹回過深可能增加不希望的寄生通道。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess recess can expose unwanted parasitic channels. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「凹回過深可能增加不希望的寄生通道」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess recess can expose unwanted parasitic channels. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-496-k1","title":"FinFET 隔離層凹回的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess finfet isolation recess","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「標示隔離層頂部與鰭側壁暴露範圍」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Mark isolation height and exposed fin sidewalls. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-496-k2","title":"FinFET 隔離層凹回的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess finfet isolation recess","text":"有效證據需支持「有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求」。但凹回過深可能增加不希望的寄生通道；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met. However, excess recess can expose unwanted parasitic channels; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「FinFET 隔離層凹回」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess finfet isolation recess?","options":["金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處","有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求","內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除"],"optionsEn":["Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions","Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met","Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「標示隔離層頂部與鰭側壁暴露範圍」，因此直接證據是「有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：凹回過深可能增加不希望的寄生通道。","explanationEn":"The task is to mark isolation height and exposed fin sidewalls; the direct criterion is: Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess recess can expose unwanted parasitic channels."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":496,"order":2,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-495"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-497","title":"FinFET 閘極包覆","titleEn":"Inspect FinFET gate wrapping","objective":"完成「FinFET 閘極包覆」的證據判讀，辨識『比較鰭頂及兩側閘介電層連續性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect finfet gate wrapping by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare gate-dielectric continuity on the fin top and sides.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較鰭頂及兩側閘介電層連續性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare gate-dielectric continuity on the fin top and sides. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：鰭頂完整不能保證側壁界面品質。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: an intact fin top does not prove good sidewall interfaces. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「鰭頂完整不能保證側壁界面品質」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: An intact fin top does not prove good sidewall interfaces. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-497-k1","title":"FinFET 閘極包覆的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect finfet gate wrapping","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較鰭頂及兩側閘介電層連續性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare gate-dielectric continuity on the fin top and sides. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-497-k2","title":"FinFET 閘極包覆的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect finfet gate wrapping","text":"有效證據需支持「三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證」。但鰭頂完整不能保證側壁界面品質；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable. However, an intact fin top does not prove good sidewall interfaces; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「FinFET 閘極包覆」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect finfet gate wrapping?","options":["隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放","閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符","三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證"],"optionsEn":["Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed","Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch","Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較鰭頂及兩側閘介電層連續性」，因此直接證據是「三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：鰭頂完整不能保證側壁界面品質。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare gate-dielectric continuity on the fin top and sides; the direct criterion is: Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: An intact fin top does not prove good sidewall interfaces."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":497,"order":3,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-496"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-498","title":"FinFET 多鰭匹配","titleEn":"Assess matching across multiple fins","objective":"完成「FinFET 多鰭匹配」的證據判讀，辨識『比較同一元件內各鰭的尺寸及連接』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess matching across multiple fins by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare dimensions and connections of fins within one device.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較同一元件內各鰭的尺寸及連接。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare dimensions and connections of fins within one device. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單根缺陷可被總電流平均掩蓋。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: one defective fin can be hidden by total current. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單根缺陷可被總電流平均掩蓋」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: One defective fin can be hidden by total current. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-498-k1","title":"FinFET 多鰭匹配的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess matching across multiple fins","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較同一元件內各鰭的尺寸及連接」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare dimensions and connections of fins within one device. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-498-k2","title":"FinFET 多鰭匹配的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess matching across multiple fins","text":"有效證據需支持「每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻」。但單根缺陷可被總電流平均掩蓋；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current. However, one defective fin can be hidden by total current; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「FinFET 多鰭匹配」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess matching across multiple fins?","options":["每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻","每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接","每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象"],"optionsEn":["Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current","Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections","Each power path has an explicit landing target"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較同一元件內各鰭的尺寸及連接」，因此直接證據是「每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單根缺陷可被總電流平均掩蓋。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare dimensions and connections of fins within one device; the direct criterion is: Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: One defective fin can be hidden by total current."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":498,"order":4,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-497"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-499","title":"GAA 交替外延堆疊","titleEn":"Inspect alternating GAA epitaxial layers","objective":"完成「GAA 交替外延堆疊」的證據判讀，辨識『辨認通道層與犧牲層的週期結構』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect alternating gaa epitaxial layers by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: identify channel and sacrificial layers in the periodic stack.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，辨認通道層與犧牲層的週期結構。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, identify channel and sacrificial layers in the periodic stack. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：層序與材料區分符合釋放路線。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: layer order and material identity match the release route. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：層序錯誤會破壞選擇性釋放假設。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: wrong layer order invalidates selective-release assumptions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「層序與材料區分符合釋放路線」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「層序錯誤會破壞選擇性釋放假設」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Layer order and material identity match the release route. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Wrong layer order invalidates selective-release assumptions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-499-k1","title":"GAA 交替外延堆疊的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect alternating gaa epitaxial layers","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「辨認通道層與犧牲層的週期結構」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Identify channel and sacrificial layers in the periodic stack. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-499-k2","title":"GAA 交替外延堆疊的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect alternating gaa epitaxial layers","text":"有效證據需支持「層序與材料區分符合釋放路線」。但層序錯誤會破壞選擇性釋放假設；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Layer order and material identity match the release route. However, wrong layer order invalidates selective-release assumptions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「GAA 交替外延堆疊」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect alternating gaa epitaxial layers?","options":["薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑","層序與材料區分符合釋放路線","通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留"],"optionsEn":["Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing","Layer order and material identity match the release route","Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「辨認通道層與犧牲層的週期結構」，因此直接證據是「層序與材料區分符合釋放路線」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：層序錯誤會破壞選擇性釋放假設。","explanationEn":"The task is to identify channel and sacrificial layers in the periodic stack; the direct criterion is: Layer order and material identity match the release route. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Wrong layer order invalidates selective-release assumptions."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":499,"order":5,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-498"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-500","title":"奈米片厚度匹配","titleEn":"Assess nanosheet thickness matching","objective":"完成「奈米片厚度匹配」的證據判讀，辨識『逐層量取奈米片厚度及片間間距』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess nanosheet thickness matching by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure each nanosheet thickness and intersheet spacing.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，逐層量取奈米片厚度及片間間距。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure each nanosheet thickness and intersheet spacing. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: differences among sheets at different heights are quantified. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均厚度會掩蓋最薄奈米片。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: average thickness conceals the thinnest sheet. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均厚度會掩蓋最薄奈米片」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Average thickness conceals the thinnest sheet. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-500-k1","title":"奈米片厚度匹配的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess nanosheet thickness matching","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「逐層量取奈米片厚度及片間間距」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Measure each nanosheet thickness and intersheet spacing. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-500-k2","title":"奈米片厚度匹配的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess nanosheet thickness matching","text":"有效證據需支持「不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化」。但平均厚度會掩蓋最薄奈米片；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified. However, average thickness conceals the thinnest sheet; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「奈米片厚度匹配」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess nanosheet thickness matching?","options":["奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構","保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷","不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化"],"optionsEn":["Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports","Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage","Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「逐層量取奈米片厚度及片間間距」，因此直接證據是「不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均厚度會掩蓋最薄奈米片。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure each nanosheet thickness and intersheet spacing; the direct criterion is: Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Average thickness conceals the thinnest sheet."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":500,"order":6,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-499"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-501","title":"GAA 堆疊圖形邊壁","titleEn":"Inspect patterned GAA stack sidewalls","objective":"完成「GAA 堆疊圖形邊壁」的證據判讀，辨識『比較交替材料側壁的蝕刻偏差』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect patterned gaa stack sidewalls by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare sidewall etch bias across alternating materials.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較交替材料側壁的蝕刻偏差。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare sidewall etch bias across alternating materials. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：不同材料速率差可形成鋸齒側壁。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: different material rates can produce serrated sidewalls. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「不同材料速率差可形成鋸齒側壁」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Different material rates can produce serrated sidewalls. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-501-k1","title":"GAA 堆疊圖形邊壁的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect patterned gaa stack sidewalls","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較交替材料側壁的蝕刻偏差」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare sidewall etch bias across alternating materials. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-501-k2","title":"GAA 堆疊圖形邊壁的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect patterned gaa stack sidewalls","text":"有效證據需支持「材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓」。但不同材料速率差可形成鋸齒側壁；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses. However, different material rates can produce serrated sidewalls; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「GAA 堆疊圖形邊壁」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect patterned gaa stack sidewalls?","options":["材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓","全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離","最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區"],"optionsEn":["Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses","All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation","Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較交替材料側壁的蝕刻偏差」，因此直接證據是「材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：不同材料速率差可形成鋸齒側壁。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare sidewall etch bias across alternating materials; the direct criterion is: Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Different material rates can produce serrated sidewalls."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":501,"order":7,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-500"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-502","title":"內間隔層犧牲層凹蝕","titleEn":"Assess inner-spacer recess","objective":"完成「內間隔層犧牲層凹蝕」的證據判讀，辨識『標示犧牲層端部的選擇性橫向凹蝕』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess inner-spacer recess by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map selective lateral recess at sacrificial-layer ends.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，標示犧牲層端部的選擇性橫向凹蝕。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map selective lateral recess at sacrificial-layer ends. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：凹蝕侵入通道層會削弱奈米片。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: recess into the channel layer weakens nanosheets. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「凹蝕侵入通道層會削弱奈米片」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Recess into the channel layer weakens nanosheets. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-502-k1","title":"內間隔層犧牲層凹蝕的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess inner-spacer recess","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「標示犧牲層端部的選擇性橫向凹蝕」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Map selective lateral recess at sacrificial-layer ends. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-502-k2","title":"內間隔層犧牲層凹蝕的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess inner-spacer recess","text":"有效證據需支持「凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存」。但凹蝕侵入通道層會削弱奈米片；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation. However, recess into the channel layer weakens nanosheets; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「內間隔層犧牲層凹蝕」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess inner-spacer recess?","options":["側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立","凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存","金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處"],"optionsEn":["Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts","Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation","Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「標示犧牲層端部的選擇性橫向凹蝕」，因此直接證據是「凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：凹蝕侵入通道層會削弱奈米片。","explanationEn":"The task is to map selective lateral recess at sacrificial-layer ends; the direct criterion is: Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Recess into the channel layer weakens nanosheets."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":502,"order":8,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-501"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-503","title":"內間隔介電填充","titleEn":"Inspect inner-spacer dielectric filling","objective":"完成「內間隔介電填充」的證據判讀，辨識『比較凹槽內填充與外部殘膜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect inner-spacer dielectric filling by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare cavity fill and external dielectric residue.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較凹槽內填充與外部殘膜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare cavity fill and external dielectric residue. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：內間隔空隙可能造成閘源汲耦合異常。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: inner-spacer gaps can disturb gate–source/drain coupling. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「內間隔空隙可能造成閘源汲耦合異常」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Inner-spacer gaps can disturb gate–source/drain coupling. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-503-k1","title":"內間隔介電填充的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect inner-spacer dielectric filling","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較凹槽內填充與外部殘膜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare cavity fill and external dielectric residue. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-503-k2","title":"內間隔介電填充的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect inner-spacer dielectric filling","text":"有效證據需支持「內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除」。但內間隔空隙可能造成閘源汲耦合異常；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable. However, inner-spacer gaps can disturb gate–source/drain coupling; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「內間隔介電填充」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect inner-spacer dielectric filling?","options":["閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符","改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變","內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除"],"optionsEn":["Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch","Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes","Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較凹槽內填充與外部殘膜」，因此直接證據是「內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：內間隔空隙可能造成閘源汲耦合異常。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare cavity fill and external dielectric residue; the direct criterion is: Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Inner-spacer gaps can disturb gate–source/drain coupling."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":503,"order":9,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-502"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-504","title":"內間隔回蝕邊界","titleEn":"Assess inner-spacer etchback boundaries","objective":"完成「內間隔回蝕邊界」的證據判讀，辨識『辨認應保留內層與應移除外膜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess inner-spacer etchback boundaries by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: identify retained inner dielectric and removable outer film.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，辨認應保留內層與應移除外膜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, identify retained inner dielectric and removable outer film. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：過度回蝕會削弱內間隔隔離。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: excess etchback weakens inner-spacer isolation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「過度回蝕會削弱內間隔隔離」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Excess etchback weakens inner-spacer isolation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-504-k1","title":"內間隔回蝕邊界的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess inner-spacer etchback boundaries","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「辨認應保留內層與應移除外膜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Identify retained inner dielectric and removable outer film. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-504-k2","title":"內間隔回蝕邊界的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess inner-spacer etchback boundaries","text":"有效證據需支持「隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放」。但過度回蝕會削弱內間隔隔離；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed. However, excess etchback weakens inner-spacer isolation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「內間隔回蝕邊界」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess inner-spacer etchback boundaries?","options":["隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放","每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象","差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通"],"optionsEn":["Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed","Each power path has an explicit landing target","Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「辨認應保留內層與應移除外膜」，因此直接證據是「隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：過度回蝕會削弱內間隔隔離。","explanationEn":"The task is to identify retained inner dielectric and removable outer film; the direct criterion is: Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Excess etchback weakens inner-spacer isolation."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":504,"order":10,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-503"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-505","title":"GAA 源汲極片端連接","titleEn":"Inspect GAA sheet-end junction connections","objective":"完成「GAA 源汲極片端連接」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤各奈米片與源汲極外延的接合』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect gaa sheet-end junction connections by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace each nanosheet connection to source/drain epitaxy.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤各奈米片與源汲極外延的接合。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace each nanosheet connection to source/drain epitaxy. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：下層接合缺陷可能被上層截面漏掉。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: upper sections can miss defective lower-sheet junctions. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「下層接合缺陷可能被上層截面漏掉」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Upper sections can miss defective lower-sheet junctions. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-505-k1","title":"GAA 源汲極片端連接的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect gaa sheet-end junction connections","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「追蹤各奈米片與源汲極外延的接合」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Trace each nanosheet connection to source/drain epitaxy. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-505-k2","title":"GAA 源汲極片端連接的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect gaa sheet-end junction connections","text":"有效證據需支持「每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接」。但下層接合缺陷可能被上層截面漏掉；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections. However, upper sections can miss defective lower-sheet junctions; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「GAA 源汲極片端連接」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect gaa sheet-end junction connections?","options":["交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭","每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接","薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑"],"optionsEn":["Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures","Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections","Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤各奈米片與源汲極外延的接合」，因此直接證據是「每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：下層接合缺陷可能被上層截面漏掉。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace each nanosheet connection to source/drain epitaxy; the direct criterion is: Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Upper sections can miss defective lower-sheet junctions."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":505,"order":11,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-504"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-506","title":"犧牲層選擇性釋放","titleEn":"Assess selective sacrificial-layer release","objective":"完成「犧牲層選擇性釋放」的證據判讀，辨識『比較犧牲材料殘留與通道材料損失』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess selective sacrificial-layer release by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare sacrificial residue and channel-material loss.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較犧牲材料殘留與通道材料損失。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare sacrificial residue and channel-material loss. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: channels become accessible while retaining their thickness. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：完全去犧牲層不代表通道未被侵蝕。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: complete release does not prove undamaged channels. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「完全去犧牲層不代表通道未被侵蝕」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Complete release does not prove undamaged channels. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-506-k1","title":"犧牲層選擇性釋放的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess selective sacrificial-layer release","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較犧牲材料殘留與通道材料損失」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare sacrificial residue and channel-material loss. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-506-k2","title":"犧牲層選擇性釋放的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess selective sacrificial-layer release","text":"有效證據需支持「通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留」。但完全去犧牲層不代表通道未被侵蝕；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness. However, complete release does not prove undamaged channels; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「犧牲層選擇性釋放」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess selective sacrificial-layer release?","options":["保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷","最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果","通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留"],"optionsEn":["Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage","Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions","Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較犧牲材料殘留與通道材料損失」，因此直接證據是「通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：完全去犧牲層不代表通道未被侵蝕。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare sacrificial residue and channel-material loss; the direct criterion is: Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Complete release does not prove undamaged channels."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":506,"order":12,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-505"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-507","title":"奈米片機械下垂","titleEn":"Inspect nanosheet sagging","objective":"完成「奈米片機械下垂」的證據判讀，辨識『量取釋放後奈米片形狀與相鄰間距』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect nanosheet sagging by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: measure released-sheet shape and neighboring gaps.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，量取釋放後奈米片形狀與相鄰間距。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, measure released-sheet shape and neighboring gaps. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：毛細或殘餘應力可能引起黏附。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: capillary or residual stress can cause sticking. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「毛細或殘餘應力可能引起黏附」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Capillary or residual stress can cause sticking. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-507-k1","title":"奈米片機械下垂的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect nanosheet sagging","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「量取釋放後奈米片形狀與相鄰間距」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Measure released-sheet shape and neighboring gaps. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-507-k2","title":"奈米片機械下垂的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect nanosheet sagging","text":"有效證據需支持「奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構」。但毛細或殘餘應力可能引起黏附；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports. However, capillary or residual stress can cause sticking; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「奈米片機械下垂」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect nanosheet sagging?","options":["奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構","最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區","接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制"],"optionsEn":["Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports","Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings","The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「量取釋放後奈米片形狀與相鄰間距」，因此直接證據是「奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：毛細或殘餘應力可能引起黏附。","explanationEn":"The task is to measure released-sheet shape and neighboring gaps; the direct criterion is: Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Capillary or residual stress can cause sticking."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":507,"order":13,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-506"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-508","title":"環繞閘介電共形覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess wraparound gate-dielectric coverage","objective":"完成「環繞閘介電共形覆蓋」的證據判讀，辨識『追蹤奈米片上、下與側面的薄膜』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess wraparound gate-dielectric coverage by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: trace films above, below and beside each nanosheet.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，追蹤奈米片上、下與側面的薄膜。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, trace films above, below and beside each nanosheet. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: all gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只看頂面無法驗證下表面品質。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: top-surface inspection cannot verify underside quality. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只看頂面無法驗證下表面品質」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Top-surface inspection cannot verify underside quality. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-508-k1","title":"環繞閘介電共形覆蓋的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess wraparound gate-dielectric coverage","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「追蹤奈米片上、下與側面的薄膜」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Trace films above, below and beside each nanosheet. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-508-k2","title":"環繞閘介電共形覆蓋的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess wraparound gate-dielectric coverage","text":"有效證據需支持「全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離」。但只看頂面無法驗證下表面品質；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation. However, top-surface inspection cannot verify underside quality; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「環繞閘介電共形覆蓋」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess wraparound gate-dielectric coverage?","options":["鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化","全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離","側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立"],"optionsEn":["Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately","All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation","Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「追蹤奈米片上、下與側面的薄膜」，因此直接證據是「全部閘控表面均有連續介電隔離」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只看頂面無法驗證下表面品質。","explanationEn":"The task is to trace films above, below and beside each nanosheet; the direct criterion is: All gate-controlled surfaces have continuous dielectric isolation. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Top-surface inspection cannot verify underside quality."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":508,"order":14,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-507"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-509","title":"片間金屬閘填充","titleEn":"Inspect intersheet metal-gate filling","objective":"完成「片間金屬閘填充」的證據判讀，辨識『比較片間剩餘空間與金屬填充截面』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect intersheet metal-gate filling by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare remaining intersheet space and gate-fill sections.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較片間剩餘空間與金屬填充截面。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare remaining intersheet space and gate-fill sections. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：狹窄片間空間增加封口空洞風險。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: narrow intersheet spaces increase pinch-off void risk. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「狹窄片間空間增加封口空洞風險」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Narrow intersheet spaces increase pinch-off void risk. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-509-k1","title":"片間金屬閘填充的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect intersheet metal-gate filling","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較片間剩餘空間與金屬填充截面」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare remaining intersheet space and gate-fill sections. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-509-k2","title":"片間金屬閘填充的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect intersheet metal-gate filling","text":"有效證據需支持「金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處」。但狹窄片間空間增加封口空洞風險；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions. However, narrow intersheet spaces increase pinch-off void risk; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「片間金屬閘填充」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect intersheet metal-gate filling?","options":["改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變","有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求","金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處"],"optionsEn":["Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes","Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met","Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較片間剩餘空間與金屬填充截面」，因此直接證據是「金屬連續且未封住尚未填充的深處」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：狹窄片間空間增加封口空洞風險。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare remaining intersheet space and gate-fill sections; the direct criterion is: Metal stays continuous without trapping unfilled deep regions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Narrow intersheet spaces increase pinch-off void risk."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":509,"order":15,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-508"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-510","title":"GAA 閾值分支與功函數","titleEn":"Assess GAA work-function branches","objective":"完成「GAA 閾值分支與功函數」的證據判讀，辨識『對照功函數層分支與元件閾值分佈』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess gaa work-function branches by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare work-function branches and threshold distributions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照功函數層分支與元件閾值分佈。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare work-function branches and threshold distributions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：用通道尺寸差補償可能掩蓋材料問題。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: geometry compensation can conceal a material problem. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「用通道尺寸差補償可能掩蓋材料問題」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Geometry compensation can conceal a material problem. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-510-k1","title":"GAA 閾值分支與功函數的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess gaa work-function branches","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「對照功函數層分支與元件閾值分佈」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare work-function branches and threshold distributions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-510-k2","title":"GAA 閾值分支與功函數的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess gaa work-function branches","text":"有效證據需支持「閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符」。但用通道尺寸差補償可能掩蓋材料問題；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch. However, geometry compensation can conceal a material problem; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「GAA 閾值分支與功函數」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess gaa work-function branches?","options":["閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符","差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通","三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證"],"optionsEn":["Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch","Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction","Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照功函數層分支與元件閾值分佈」，因此直接證據是「閾值差異與實際閘堆疊分支相符」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：用通道尺寸差補償可能掩蓋材料問題。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare work-function branches and threshold distributions; the direct criterion is: Threshold differences match the actual gate-stack branch. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Geometry compensation can conceal a material problem."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":510,"order":16,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-509"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-511","title":"背面供電拓撲選擇","titleEn":"Select backside-power connectivity topology","objective":"完成「背面供電拓撲選擇」的證據判讀，辨識『比較埋入電源軌與直接背接觸示意』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate select backside-power connectivity topology by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare buried-rail and direct-backside-contact schemes.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較埋入電源軌與直接背接觸示意。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare buried-rail and direct-backside-contact schemes. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: each power path has an explicit landing target. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：把兩種拓撲混接會產生無效連接。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mixing the topologies produces invalid connections. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「把兩種拓撲混接會產生無效連接」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Each power path has an explicit landing target. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mixing the topologies produces invalid connections. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-511-k1","title":"背面供電拓撲選擇的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of select backside-power connectivity topology","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較埋入電源軌與直接背接觸示意」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare buried-rail and direct-backside-contact schemes. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-511-k2","title":"背面供電拓撲選擇的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for select backside-power connectivity topology","text":"有效證據需支持「每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象」。但把兩種拓撲混接會產生無效連接；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Each power path has an explicit landing target. However, mixing the topologies produces invalid connections; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面供電拓撲選擇」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for select backside-power connectivity topology?","options":["每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻","每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象","交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭"],"optionsEn":["Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current","Each power path has an explicit landing target","Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較埋入電源軌與直接背接觸示意」，因此直接證據是「每條電源路徑都有明確接觸對象」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：把兩種拓撲混接會產生無效連接。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare buried-rail and direct-backside-contact schemes; the direct criterion is: Each power path has an explicit landing target. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mixing the topologies produces invalid connections."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":511,"order":17,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-510"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-512","title":"背面加工載板支撐","titleEn":"Assess carriers for backside processing","objective":"完成「背面加工載板支撐」的證據判讀，辨識『在背面路線中標示正面接合及承載結構』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess carriers for backside processing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: map frontside bonding and support in the backside flow.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，在背面路線中標示正面接合及承載結構。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, map frontside bonding and support in the backside flow. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：暫時載板條件不合可損害前端結構。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unsuitable carrier conditions can damage frontside devices. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「暫時載板條件不合可損害前端結構」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unsuitable carrier conditions can damage frontside devices. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-512-k1","title":"背面加工載板支撐的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess carriers for backside processing","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「在背面路線中標示正面接合及承載結構」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Map frontside bonding and support in the backside flow. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-512-k2","title":"背面加工載板支撐的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess carriers for backside processing","text":"有效證據需支持「薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑」。但暫時載板條件不合可損害前端結構；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing. However, unsuitable carrier conditions can damage frontside devices; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面加工載板支撐」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess carriers for backside processing?","options":["最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果","層序與材料區分符合釋放路線","薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑"],"optionsEn":["Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions","Layer order and material identity match the release route","Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「在背面路線中標示正面接合及承載結構」，因此直接證據是「薄化與後續加工期間有連續承載路徑」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：暫時載板條件不合可損害前端結構。","explanationEn":"The task is to map frontside bonding and support in the backside flow; the direct criterion is: Support is maintained through thinning and subsequent processing. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unsuitable carrier conditions can damage frontside devices."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":512,"order":18,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-511"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-513","title":"背面殘矽終點","titleEn":"Determine residual-silicon endpoints","objective":"完成「背面殘矽終點」的證據判讀，辨識『對照背面薄化深度與目標接觸位置』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate determine residual-silicon endpoints by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare thinning depth with intended contact locations.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，對照背面薄化深度與目標接觸位置。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare thinning depth with intended contact locations. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: remaining thickness enables target access without device damage. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：單看平均厚度會漏掉局部過薄。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mean thickness misses local overthinning. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「單看平均厚度會漏掉局部過薄」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mean thickness misses local overthinning. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-513-k1","title":"背面殘矽終點的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of determine residual-silicon endpoints","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「對照背面薄化深度與目標接觸位置」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare thinning depth with intended contact locations. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-513-k2","title":"背面殘矽終點的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for determine residual-silicon endpoints","text":"有效證據需支持「保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷」。但單看平均厚度會漏掉局部過薄；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage. However, mean thickness misses local overthinning; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面殘矽終點」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for determine residual-silicon endpoints?","options":["保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷","接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制","不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化"],"optionsEn":["Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage","The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits","Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「對照背面薄化深度與目標接觸位置」，因此直接證據是「保留厚度足以暴露目標且避免元件損傷」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：單看平均厚度會漏掉局部過薄。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare thinning depth with intended contact locations; the direct criterion is: Remaining thickness enables target access without device damage. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mean thickness misses local overthinning."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":513,"order":19,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-512"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-514","title":"背正面套刻驗證","titleEn":"Verify backside-to-frontside overlay","objective":"完成「背正面套刻驗證」的證據判讀，辨識『將背面標記轉換到前端元件座標』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate verify backside-to-frontside overlay by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: transform backside marks into frontside device coordinates.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，將背面標記轉換到前端元件座標。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, transform backside marks into frontside device coordinates. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：背面鏡像關係處理錯誤會全面錯位。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: incorrect backside mirroring causes systematic misalignment. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「背面鏡像關係處理錯誤會全面錯位」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Incorrect backside mirroring causes systematic misalignment. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-514-k1","title":"背正面套刻驗證的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of verify backside-to-frontside overlay","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「將背面標記轉換到前端元件座標」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Transform backside marks into frontside device coordinates. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-514-k2","title":"背正面套刻驗證的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for verify backside-to-frontside overlay","text":"有效證據需支持「最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區」。但背面鏡像關係處理錯誤會全面錯位；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings. However, incorrect backside mirroring causes systematic misalignment; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背正面套刻驗證」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for verify backside-to-frontside overlay?","options":["材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓","最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區","鰭寬與暴露高度分別量化"],"optionsEn":["Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses","Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings","Fin width and exposed height are quantified separately"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「將背面標記轉換到前端元件座標」，因此直接證據是「最差偏差仍讓導通孔落在允許區」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：背面鏡像關係處理錯誤會全面錯位。","explanationEn":"The task is to transform backside marks into frontside device coordinates; the direct criterion is: Worst-case error keeps vias inside permitted landings. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Incorrect backside mirroring causes systematic misalignment."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":514,"order":20,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-513"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-515","title":"奈米導通孔隔離與落點","titleEn":"Inspect nano-via isolation and landing","objective":"完成「奈米導通孔隔離與落點」的證據判讀，辨識『同時檢查孔壁介電與底部導電連接』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate inspect nano-via isolation and landing by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: inspect via-wall dielectric and bottom electrical connection.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，同時檢查孔壁介電與底部導電連接。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, inspect via-wall dielectric and bottom electrical connection. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：全面金屬接觸可能造成基板短路。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: unisolated metal contact can short the substrate. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「全面金屬接觸可能造成基板短路」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Unisolated metal contact can short the substrate. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-515-k1","title":"奈米導通孔隔離與落點的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of inspect nano-via isolation and landing","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「同時檢查孔壁介電與底部導電連接」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Inspect via-wall dielectric and bottom electrical connection. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-515-k2","title":"奈米導通孔隔離與落點的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for inspect nano-via isolation and landing","text":"有效證據需支持「側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立」。但全面金屬接觸可能造成基板短路；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts. However, unisolated metal contact can short the substrate; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「奈米導通孔隔離與落點」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for inspect nano-via isolation and landing?","options":["有效鰭高與隔離功能同時滿足需求","凹蝕長度兼顧閘極隔離與通道保存","側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立"],"optionsEn":["Effective fin height and isolation requirements are both met","Recess length balances gate isolation and channel preservation","Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「同時檢查孔壁介電與底部導電連接」，因此直接證據是「側壁隔離與底部導通同時成立」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：全面金屬接觸可能造成基板短路。","explanationEn":"The task is to inspect via-wall dielectric and bottom electrical connection; the direct criterion is: Sidewalls isolate while the bottom conducts. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Unisolated metal contact can short the substrate."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":515,"order":21,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-514"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-516","title":"背面配線電壓降","titleEn":"Assess backside-wiring voltage drop","objective":"完成「背面配線電壓降」的證據判讀，辨識『比較前端與背面供電模型的節點電壓』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess backside-wiring voltage drop by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare node voltages in frontside and backside power models.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較前端與背面供電模型的節點電壓。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare node voltages in frontside and backside power models. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只縮短路徑不能忽略接觸電阻。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a shorter path does not remove contact resistance. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只縮短路徑不能忽略接觸電阻」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A shorter path does not remove contact resistance. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-516-k1","title":"背面配線電壓降的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess backside-wiring voltage drop","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較前端與背面供電模型的節點電壓」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare node voltages in frontside and backside power models. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-516-k2","title":"背面配線電壓降的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess backside-wiring voltage drop","text":"有效證據需支持「改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變」。但只縮短路徑不能忽略接觸電阻；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes. However, a shorter path does not remove contact resistance; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面配線電壓降」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess backside-wiring voltage drop?","options":["改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變","三面通道的閘控覆蓋可被驗證","內部隔離連續且外部接觸區可清除"],"optionsEn":["Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes","Gate coverage over the three channel faces is verifiable","Internal isolation is continuous and external contacts remain clearable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較前端與背面供電模型的節點電壓」，因此直接證據是「改善來自明示電阻與電流路徑改變」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只縮短路徑不能忽略接觸電阻。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare node voltages in frontside and backside power models; the direct criterion is: Improvement follows explicit resistance and path changes. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A shorter path does not remove contact resistance."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":516,"order":22,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-515"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-517","title":"背面製程對前端影響","titleEn":"Assess backside-process impact on devices","objective":"完成「背面製程對前端影響」的證據判讀，辨識『比較背面加工前後同一批元件電性』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate assess backside-process impact on devices by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: compare matched devices before and after backside processing.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，比較背面加工前後同一批元件電性。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, compare matched devices before and after backside processing. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：平均不變仍可能有局部尾端劣化。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: an unchanged mean can hide local tail degradation. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「平均不變仍可能有局部尾端劣化」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: An unchanged mean can hide local tail degradation. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-517-k1","title":"背面製程對前端影響的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of assess backside-process impact on devices","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「比較背面加工前後同一批元件電性」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Compare matched devices before and after backside processing. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-517-k2","title":"背面製程對前端影響的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for assess backside-process impact on devices","text":"有效證據需支持「差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通」。但平均不變仍可能有局部尾端劣化；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction. However, an unchanged mean can hide local tail degradation; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「背面製程對前端影響」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for assess backside-process impact on devices?","options":["隔離留在凹槽而源汲極成長面開放","差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通","每根鰭皆對有效電流提供可解釋貢獻"],"optionsEn":["Isolation remains in recesses while growth surfaces are exposed","Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction","Each fin makes an explainable contribution to effective current"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「比較背面加工前後同一批元件電性」，因此直接證據是「差分檢查涵蓋閾值、漏電及導通」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：平均不變仍可能有局部尾端劣化。","explanationEn":"The task is to compare matched devices before and after backside processing; the direct criterion is: Paired checks include threshold, leakage and conduction. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: An unchanged mean can hide local tail degradation."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":517,"order":23,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-516"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-518","title":"製程路線與結構證據交接","titleEn":"Handoff route and structural evidence","objective":"完成「製程路線與結構證據交接」的證據判讀，辨識『把選用分支、剖面及材料標記綁定同一版本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate handoff route and structural evidence by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: bind selected branches, sections and material labels to one revision.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，把選用分支、剖面及材料標記綁定同一版本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, bind selected branches, sections and material labels to one revision. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：漂亮總圖可能包含未製作的分支。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a polished overview may include unbuilt branches. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「漂亮總圖可能包含未製作的分支」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A polished overview may include unbuilt branches. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-518-k1","title":"製程路線與結構證據交接的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of handoff route and structural evidence","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「把選用分支、剖面及材料標記綁定同一版本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Bind selected branches, sections and material labels to one revision. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-518-k2","title":"製程路線與結構證據交接的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for handoff route and structural evidence","text":"有效證據需支持「交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭」。但漂亮總圖可能包含未製作的分支；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures. However, a polished overview may include unbuilt branches; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「製程路線與結構證據交接」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for handoff route and structural evidence?","options":["層序與材料區分符合釋放路線","每片通道均具有連續源汲極連接","交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭"],"optionsEn":["Layer order and material identity match the release route","Each channel sheet has continuous source/drain connections","Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本題操作是「把選用分支、剖面及材料標記綁定同一版本」，因此直接證據是「交接圖與實際分支沒有互斥結構混搭」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：漂亮總圖可能包含未製作的分支。","explanationEn":"The task is to bind selected branches, sections and material labels to one revision; the direct criterion is: Handoff diagrams do not mix mutually exclusive structures. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A polished overview may include unbuilt branches."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"sequence":518,"order":24,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-517"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-519","title":"晶圓放行電性封存","titleEn":"Freeze wafer-release electrical evidence","objective":"完成「晶圓放行電性封存」的證據判讀，辨識『核對 PCM、晶粒分級與可追溯測試版本』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate freeze wafer-release electrical evidence by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: reconcile pcm, die bins and traceable test revisions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，核對 PCM、晶粒分級與可追溯測試版本。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, reconcile PCM, die bins and traceable test revisions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：新舊測試混用會破壞放行可重現性。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: mixing revisions makes release decisions irreproducible. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「新舊測試混用會破壞放行可重現性」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: Mixing revisions makes release decisions irreproducible. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-519-k1","title":"晶圓放行電性封存的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of freeze wafer-release electrical evidence","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「核對 PCM、晶粒分級與可追溯測試版本」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Reconcile PCM, die bins and traceable test revisions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-519-k2","title":"晶圓放行電性封存的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for freeze wafer-release electrical evidence","text":"有效證據需支持「最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果」。但新舊測試混用會破壞放行可重現性；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions. However, mixing revisions makes release decisions irreproducible; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「晶圓放行電性封存」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for freeze wafer-release electrical evidence?","options":["最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果","不同高度奈米片的差異均被量化","通道可自由包覆且自身厚度保留"],"optionsEn":["Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions","Differences among sheets at different heights are quantified","Channels become accessible while retaining their thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本題操作是「核對 PCM、晶粒分級與可追溯測試版本」，因此直接證據是「最終放行使用同一晶圓與有效版本結果」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：新舊測試混用會破壞放行可重現性。","explanationEn":"The task is to reconcile PCM, die bins and traceable test revisions; the direct criterion is: Release uses the same wafer and valid result revisions. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: Mixing revisions makes release decisions irreproducible."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":14,"sequence":519,"order":25,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-518"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"sc-520","title":"良品晶圓製造交接","titleEn":"Handoff qualified wafers","objective":"完成「良品晶圓製造交接」的證據判讀，辨識『整合缺陷位置、封裝介面與未結案限制』所涉及的物理量與整合限制。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate handoff qualified wafers by identifying the physical quantities and integration limits involved in this task: combine defect locations, packaging interfaces and open restrictions.","instruction":"以工程概念模型，或另行提供且已審查的示意截面／量測資料，整合缺陷位置、封裝介面與未結案限制。標出比較基準與量測位置並保留判讀依據；未掛接資料或未給允收數值時，標記定量驗證未完成，不自行編造機台參數。","instructionEn":"Using an engineering concept model, or a separately supplied and reviewed section or measurement dataset, combine defect locations, packaging interfaces and open restrictions. Mark the comparison baseline and measurement locations. If data or numerical acceptance limits are unavailable, mark quantitative validation incomplete rather than inventing tool settings.","observation":"觀察與驗證重點：接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制。這是要檢查的證據條件，並非宣稱已取得真實工廠量測結果。","observationEn":"Observation and validation target: the receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits. This is an evidence criterion, not a claim of measured factory results.","failure":"診斷提醒：只有合格標籤而無證據不足以交接。先用本工序的物理證據確認，再考慮修改上游假設。","failureEn":"Diagnostic consideration: a pass label without evidence is insufficient for handoff. Confirm this with physical evidence before revising upstream assumptions.","check":"提交一項能支持「接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制」的標註圖或量測表；再指出「只有合格標籤而無證據不足以交接」會如何改變判讀。資料缺漏時保持未放行狀態。","checkEn":"Submit an annotated figure or measurement table supporting this criterion: The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits. Then explain the implication of this diagnostic caveat: A pass label without evidence is insufficient for handoff. Keep the task unreleased if evidence is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"sc-520-k1","title":"良品晶圓製造交接的物理定位","titleEn":"Physical role of handoff qualified wafers","text":"本模組是互斥或可組合架構的比較分支：FinFET、GAA 與背面供電並非每條製程都同時存在；學習順序不等於實際晶圓行程。 本題具體操作為「整合缺陷位置、封裝介面與未結案限制」，應先分辨施加的條件、實際量到的變量與推論出的性質。","textEn":"This module compares alternative or combinable architectures: FinFETs, GAA and backside power do not occur together in every flow. Learning order is not a wafer traveler. Here the concrete task is: Combine defect locations, packaging interfaces and open restrictions. Distinguish imposed conditions, measured variables and inferred properties."},{"id":"sc-520-k2","title":"良品晶圓製造交接的證據與失效","titleEn":"Evidence and failure modes for handoff qualified wafers","text":"有效證據需支持「接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制」。但只有合格標籤而無證據不足以交接；因此單一漂亮影像或平均值不能自動取代對本工序目標的檢驗。","textEn":"Evidence should establish the following: The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits. However, a pass label without evidence is insufficient for handoff; an attractive image or a mean value cannot automatically substitute for a task-specific check."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項證據最直接支持「良品晶圓製造交接」這一道教學工序的判定？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports acceptance for handoff qualified wafers?","options":["奈米片未接觸彼此或支撐結構","接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制","材料交界未形成非預期凸凹輪廓"],"optionsEn":["Sheets do not touch neighboring sheets or supports","The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits","Interfaces lack unintended protrusions or recesses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本題操作是「整合缺陷位置、封裝介面與未結案限制」，因此直接證據是「接收端可重建良品判定及剩餘限制」。其他選項屬本模組其他工序，不能單獨取代此項檢查；另需留意：只有合格標籤而無證據不足以交接。","explanationEn":"The task is to combine defect locations, packaging interfaces and open restrictions; the direct criterion is: The receiver can reconstruct good-die decisions and remaining limits. The alternatives concern other operations and cannot alone replace this check. Also note: A pass label without evidence is insufficient for handoff."},"sourceIds":["scb-nanosheet","scb-backside","scb-backside-dtco","scb-epi","scb-metrology"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":8,"sequence":520,"order":26,"prerequisiteIds":["sc-519"],"routeNote":"教育順序；實際晶圓依選定製程分支、核准規格及合格設備行程執行。","routeNoteEn":"Educational ordering; actual wafers follow selected integration branches, approved specifications and qualified equipment travelers.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}],"order":20}],"stepCount":520,"estimatedMinutes":360,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":2,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/semiconductor-flow.svg","subcategory":"integration","subcategoryTitle":"整合流程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Process integration"},{"id":"sub2nm","title":"兩奈米以下製程架構","titleEn":"Sub-2 nm Process Architectures","category":"semiconductor","summary":"以奈米片電晶體、接觸與背面供電建立先進節點概念。節點名稱不是每一個結構的實際幾何尺寸。","summaryEn":"Study nanosheet devices, contacts and backside power delivery. A process-node name is not the physical size of every feature.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["奈米片","全環繞閘極","接觸","背面供電"],"labelsEn":["Nanosheet","GAA gate","Contact","Backside power"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"sub2nm-s01","order":1,"title":"節點與需求","titleEn":"Nodes and requirements","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s01-01","order":1,"title":"解讀節點名稱","titleEn":"Interpret node names","objective":"完成「解讀節點名稱」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for interpret node names.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"節點標籤代表技術世代，應以公開 PPA 與結構資料比較。","textEn":"Node labels identify technology generations; comparisons need public PPA and structural data."},{"id":"sub2nm-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把節點標籤與閘長、接觸間距、金屬間距分成不同欄位。","textEn":"Separate node label, gate length, contact pitch and metal pitch in a table."}],"check":"把節點標籤與閘長、接觸間距、金屬間距分成不同欄位。","checkEn":"Separate node label, gate length, contact pitch and metal pitch in a table.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「解讀節點名稱」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains interpret node names?","options":["節點標籤代表技術世代，應以公開 PPA 與結構資料比較。","動態功耗與切換電容、電壓平方和頻率相關，漏電另有不同來源。","增加閘極對通道的包覆可改善靜電控制，但也提高製程整合複雜度。"],"optionsEn":["Node labels identify technology generations; comparisons need public PPA and structural data.","Dynamic power depends on switched capacitance, voltage squared and frequency; leakage has separate origins.","Greater gate enclosure improves electrostatic control but increases integration complexity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"節點標籤代表技術世代，應以公開 PPA 與結構資料比較。","explanationEn":"Node labels identify technology generations; comparisons need public PPA and structural data."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s01-02","order":2,"title":"建立功耗分解","titleEn":"Decompose power","objective":"完成「建立功耗分解」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for decompose power.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"動態功耗與切換電容、電壓平方和頻率相關，漏電另有不同來源。","textEn":"Dynamic power depends on switched capacitance, voltage squared and frequency; leakage has separate origins."},{"id":"sub2nm-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以符號模型分列動態、短路與漏電功耗。","textEn":"Separate dynamic, short-circuit and leakage power in a symbolic model."}],"check":"以符號模型分列動態、短路與漏電功耗。","checkEn":"Separate dynamic, short-circuit and leakage power in a symbolic model.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立功耗分解」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains decompose power?","options":["增加閘極對通道的包覆可改善靜電控制，但也提高製程整合複雜度。","節點標籤代表技術世代，應以公開 PPA 與結構資料比較。","動態功耗與切換電容、電壓平方和頻率相關，漏電另有不同來源。"],"optionsEn":["Greater gate enclosure improves electrostatic control but increases integration complexity.","Node labels identify technology generations; comparisons need public PPA and structural data.","Dynamic power depends on switched capacitance, voltage squared and frequency; leakage has separate origins."],"answer":2,"explanation":"動態功耗與切換電容、電壓平方和頻率相關，漏電另有不同來源。","explanationEn":"Dynamic power depends on switched capacitance, voltage squared and frequency; leakage has separate origins."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s01-03","order":3,"title":"比較元件架構","titleEn":"Compare device architectures","objective":"完成「比較元件架構」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare device architectures.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"增加閘極對通道的包覆可改善靜電控制，但也提高製程整合複雜度。","textEn":"Greater gate enclosure improves electrostatic control but increases integration complexity."},{"id":"sub2nm-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"繪出平面、鰭式與奈米片的閘極包覆面。","textEn":"Sketch gate coverage for planar, fin and nanosheet devices."}],"check":"繪出平面、鰭式與奈米片的閘極包覆面。","checkEn":"Sketch gate coverage for planar, fin and nanosheet devices.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較元件架構」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare device architectures?","options":["動態功耗與切換電容、電壓平方和頻率相關，漏電另有不同來源。","增加閘極對通道的包覆可改善靜電控制，但也提高製程整合複雜度。","節點標籤代表技術世代，應以公開 PPA 與結構資料比較。"],"optionsEn":["Dynamic power depends on switched capacitance, voltage squared and frequency; leakage has separate origins.","Greater gate enclosure improves electrostatic control but increases integration complexity.","Node labels identify technology generations; comparisons need public PPA and structural data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加閘極對通道的包覆可改善靜電控制，但也提高製程整合複雜度。","explanationEn":"Greater gate enclosure improves electrostatic control but increases integration complexity."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"sub2nm-s02","order":2,"title":"奈米片結構","titleEn":"Nanosheet structure","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s02-01","order":1,"title":"辨識交替材料堆疊","titleEn":"Identify alternating layers","objective":"完成「辨識交替材料堆疊」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify alternating layers.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"交替堆疊提供通道與後續可選擇移除材料，厚度變異會傳遞到元件。","textEn":"Alternating layers provide channels and selectively removable material; thickness variation propagates into the device."},{"id":"sub2nm-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意截面標明保留層與犧牲層。","textEn":"Label retained and sacrificial layers in a schematic section."}],"check":"在示意截面標明保留層與犧牲層。","checkEn":"Label retained and sacrificial layers in a schematic section.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識交替材料堆疊」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify alternating layers?","options":["選擇性移除需保留通道完整性並控制殘留，不能只追求移除速度。","間隔層分隔閘極與源汲區域，寄生電容及漏電取決於幾何與材料。","交替堆疊提供通道與後續可選擇移除材料，厚度變異會傳遞到元件。"],"optionsEn":["Selective removal must preserve channels and control residues rather than maximize removal speed alone.","Spacers separate gate and source/drain regions; geometry and material affect parasitic capacitance and leakage.","Alternating layers provide channels and selectively removable material; thickness variation propagates into the device."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交替堆疊提供通道與後續可選擇移除材料，厚度變異會傳遞到元件。","explanationEn":"Alternating layers provide channels and selectively removable material; thickness variation propagates into the device."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s02-02","order":2,"title":"理解通道釋放","titleEn":"Understand channel release","objective":"完成「理解通道釋放」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand channel release.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"選擇性移除需保留通道完整性並控制殘留，不能只追求移除速度。","textEn":"Selective removal must preserve channels and control residues rather than maximize removal speed alone."},{"id":"sub2nm-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用兩個失效案例說明過蝕刻與釋放不足。","textEn":"Illustrate over-etch and incomplete release with two failure cases."}],"check":"用兩個失效案例說明過蝕刻與釋放不足。","checkEn":"Illustrate over-etch and incomplete release with two failure cases.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解通道釋放」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand channel release?","options":["交替堆疊提供通道與後續可選擇移除材料，厚度變異會傳遞到元件。","選擇性移除需保留通道完整性並控制殘留，不能只追求移除速度。","間隔層分隔閘極與源汲區域，寄生電容及漏電取決於幾何與材料。"],"optionsEn":["Alternating layers provide channels and selectively removable material; thickness variation propagates into the device.","Selective removal must preserve channels and control residues rather than maximize removal speed alone.","Spacers separate gate and source/drain regions; geometry and material affect parasitic capacitance and leakage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇性移除需保留通道完整性並控制殘留，不能只追求移除速度。","explanationEn":"Selective removal must preserve channels and control residues rather than maximize removal speed alone."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s02-03","order":3,"title":"分析內間隔層","titleEn":"Analyze inner spacers","objective":"完成「分析內間隔層」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze inner spacers.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"間隔層分隔閘極與源汲區域，寄生電容及漏電取決於幾何與材料。","textEn":"Spacers separate gate and source/drain regions; geometry and material affect parasitic capacitance and leakage."},{"id":"sub2nm-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在等效電路中標出需抑制的寄生耦合。","textEn":"Mark unwanted parasitic coupling in an equivalent circuit."}],"check":"在等效電路中標出需抑制的寄生耦合。","checkEn":"Mark unwanted parasitic coupling in an equivalent circuit.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析內間隔層」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze inner spacers?","options":["間隔層分隔閘極與源汲區域，寄生電容及漏電取決於幾何與材料。","交替堆疊提供通道與後續可選擇移除材料，厚度變異會傳遞到元件。","選擇性移除需保留通道完整性並控制殘留，不能只追求移除速度。"],"optionsEn":["Spacers separate gate and source/drain regions; geometry and material affect parasitic capacitance and leakage.","Alternating layers provide channels and selectively removable material; thickness variation propagates into the device.","Selective removal must preserve channels and control residues rather than maximize removal speed alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"間隔層分隔閘極與源汲區域，寄生電容及漏電取決於幾何與材料。","explanationEn":"Spacers separate gate and source/drain regions; geometry and material affect parasitic capacitance and leakage."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"sub2nm-s03","order":3,"title":"閘極與接觸","titleEn":"Gate and contacts","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s03-01","order":1,"title":"比較介電層厚度定義","titleEn":"Compare dielectric thickness definitions","objective":"完成「比較介電層厚度定義」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare dielectric thickness definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"高介電常數材料可用較厚實體膜取得較小等效氧化層厚度。","textEn":"A high-k material can use a thicker physical film while achieving a smaller equivalent oxide thickness."},{"id":"sub2nm-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"區分物理厚度與 EOT，勿把兩者視為同一量。","textEn":"Distinguish physical thickness from EOT."}],"check":"區分物理厚度與 EOT，勿把兩者視為同一量。","checkEn":"Distinguish physical thickness from EOT.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較介電層厚度定義」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare dielectric thickness definitions?","options":["尺寸縮小後，接觸與互連的寄生電阻不能被通道改善自動抵銷。","高介電常數材料可用較厚實體膜取得較小等效氧化層厚度。","狹窄間隙中的覆蓋與填充完整性會影響閘極均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["At smaller dimensions, better channels do not automatically offset contact and interconnect resistance.","A high-k material can use a thicker physical film while achieving a smaller equivalent oxide thickness.","Conformality and complete filling in narrow gaps affect gate uniformity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高介電常數材料可用較厚實體膜取得較小等效氧化層厚度。","explanationEn":"A high-k material can use a thicker physical film while achieving a smaller equivalent oxide thickness."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s03-02","order":2,"title":"檢查閘極填充","titleEn":"Review gate fill","objective":"完成「檢查閘極填充」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for review gate fill.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"狹窄間隙中的覆蓋與填充完整性會影響閘極均勻性。","textEn":"Conformality and complete filling in narrow gaps affect gate uniformity."},{"id":"sub2nm-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標示空洞、接縫與厚度偏差的概念位置。","textEn":"Mark conceptual locations of voids, seams and thickness variation."}],"check":"標示空洞、接縫與厚度偏差的概念位置。","checkEn":"Mark conceptual locations of voids, seams and thickness variation.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「檢查閘極填充」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains review gate fill?","options":["狹窄間隙中的覆蓋與填充完整性會影響閘極均勻性。","尺寸縮小後，接觸與互連的寄生電阻不能被通道改善自動抵銷。","高介電常數材料可用較厚實體膜取得較小等效氧化層厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Conformality and complete filling in narrow gaps affect gate uniformity.","At smaller dimensions, better channels do not automatically offset contact and interconnect resistance.","A high-k material can use a thicker physical film while achieving a smaller equivalent oxide thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"狹窄間隙中的覆蓋與填充完整性會影響閘極均勻性。","explanationEn":"Conformality and complete filling in narrow gaps affect gate uniformity."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s03-03","order":3,"title":"追蹤接觸寄生","titleEn":"Track contact parasitics","objective":"完成「追蹤接觸寄生」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for track contact parasitics.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"尺寸縮小後，接觸與互連的寄生電阻不能被通道改善自動抵銷。","textEn":"At smaller dimensions, better channels do not automatically offset contact and interconnect resistance."},{"id":"sub2nm-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立包含源接觸、通道與汲接觸的串聯模型。","textEn":"Build a series model of source contact, channel and drain contact."}],"check":"建立包含源接觸、通道與汲接觸的串聯模型。","checkEn":"Build a series model of source contact, channel and drain contact.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤接觸寄生」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains track contact parasitics?","options":["高介電常數材料可用較厚實體膜取得較小等效氧化層厚度。","狹窄間隙中的覆蓋與填充完整性會影響閘極均勻性。","尺寸縮小後，接觸與互連的寄生電阻不能被通道改善自動抵銷。"],"optionsEn":["A high-k material can use a thicker physical film while achieving a smaller equivalent oxide thickness.","Conformality and complete filling in narrow gaps affect gate uniformity.","At smaller dimensions, better channels do not automatically offset contact and interconnect resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺寸縮小後，接觸與互連的寄生電阻不能被通道改善自動抵銷。","explanationEn":"At smaller dimensions, better channels do not automatically offset contact and interconnect resistance."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"sub2nm-s04","order":4,"title":"背面供電","titleEn":"Backside power delivery","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s04-01","order":1,"title":"分離訊號與電源","titleEn":"Separate signal and power","objective":"完成「分離訊號與電源」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for separate signal and power.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"背面供電把部分電源路徑移到晶圓背側，釋出正面布線資源。","textEn":"Backside power moves part of the power network to the wafer rear and frees front-side routing resources."},{"id":"sub2nm-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在雙面示意圖分別畫出訊號線與供電線。","textEn":"Draw signal and power routes separately on a two-sided schematic."}],"check":"在雙面示意圖分別畫出訊號線與供電線。","checkEn":"Draw signal and power routes separately on a two-sided schematic.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分離訊號與電源」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains separate signal and power?","options":["背面供電把部分電源路徑移到晶圓背側，釋出正面布線資源。","IR 壓降來自電流通過有限電阻，供電路徑長度與截面均有影響。","晶圓薄化、背面連接及對位會新增機械與製程整合挑戰。"],"optionsEn":["Backside power moves part of the power network to the wafer rear and frees front-side routing resources.","IR drop arises from current through finite resistance; path length and cross-section both matter.","Wafer thinning, rear contacts and alignment add mechanical and integration challenges."],"answer":0,"explanation":"背面供電把部分電源路徑移到晶圓背側，釋出正面布線資源。","explanationEn":"Backside power moves part of the power network to the wafer rear and frees front-side routing resources."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s04-02","order":2,"title":"追蹤供電壓降","titleEn":"Track supply voltage drop","objective":"完成「追蹤供電壓降」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for track supply voltage drop.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"IR 壓降來自電流通過有限電阻，供電路徑長度與截面均有影響。","textEn":"IR drop arises from current through finite resistance; path length and cross-section both matter."},{"id":"sub2nm-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用相同負載比較兩種概念供電網路的壓降。","textEn":"Compare voltage drop for two conceptual power networks under equal load."}],"check":"用相同負載比較兩種概念供電網路的壓降。","checkEn":"Compare voltage drop for two conceptual power networks under equal load.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤供電壓降」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains track supply voltage drop?","options":["晶圓薄化、背面連接及對位會新增機械與製程整合挑戰。","背面供電把部分電源路徑移到晶圓背側，釋出正面布線資源。","IR 壓降來自電流通過有限電阻，供電路徑長度與截面均有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Wafer thinning, rear contacts and alignment add mechanical and integration challenges.","Backside power moves part of the power network to the wafer rear and frees front-side routing resources.","IR drop arises from current through finite resistance; path length and cross-section both matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"IR 壓降來自電流通過有限電阻，供電路徑長度與截面均有影響。","explanationEn":"IR drop arises from current through finite resistance; path length and cross-section both matter."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s04-03","order":3,"title":"評估薄化與對位","titleEn":"Assess thinning and alignment","objective":"完成「評估薄化與對位」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for assess thinning and alignment.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"晶圓薄化、背面連接及對位會新增機械與製程整合挑戰。","textEn":"Wafer thinning, rear contacts and alignment add mechanical and integration challenges."},{"id":"sub2nm-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出薄化後需重新驗證的翹曲、支撐及對位項目。","textEn":"List bow, support and alignment checks after thinning."}],"check":"列出薄化後需重新驗證的翹曲、支撐及對位項目。","checkEn":"List bow, support and alignment checks after thinning.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「評估薄化與對位」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains assess thinning and alignment?","options":["IR 壓降來自電流通過有限電阻，供電路徑長度與截面均有影響。","晶圓薄化、背面連接及對位會新增機械與製程整合挑戰。","背面供電把部分電源路徑移到晶圓背側，釋出正面布線資源。"],"optionsEn":["IR drop arises from current through finite resistance; path length and cross-section both matter.","Wafer thinning, rear contacts and alignment add mechanical and integration challenges.","Backside power moves part of the power network to the wafer rear and frees front-side routing resources."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓薄化、背面連接及對位會新增機械與製程整合挑戰。","explanationEn":"Wafer thinning, rear contacts and alignment add mechanical and integration challenges."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"sub2nm-s05","order":5,"title":"變異與量測","titleEn":"Variation and metrology","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s05-01","order":1,"title":"分解尺寸變異","titleEn":"Decompose dimensional variation","objective":"完成「分解尺寸變異」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for decompose dimensional variation.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"片厚、片寬與界面差異會共同造成臨界電壓和電流分布。","textEn":"Sheet thickness, width and interface differences jointly affect threshold and current distributions."},{"id":"sub2nm-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較三個尺寸擾動情境並標明敏感參數。","textEn":"Compare three dimensional-variation scenarios and identify sensitive parameters."}],"check":"比較三個尺寸擾動情境並標明敏感參數。","checkEn":"Compare three dimensional-variation scenarios and identify sensitive parameters.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分解尺寸變異」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains decompose dimensional variation?","options":["間接量測需校準模型與不確定度，單一影像不能證明全部電性。","PDK 規則反映製程可製造性約束，公開示意不能替代實際 PDK。","片厚、片寬與界面差異會共同造成臨界電壓和電流分布。"],"optionsEn":["Indirect metrology requires model calibration and uncertainty; one image cannot establish every electrical property.","PDK rules encode manufacturability constraints; public schematics cannot replace an actual PDK.","Sheet thickness, width and interface differences jointly affect threshold and current distributions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"片厚、片寬與界面差異會共同造成臨界電壓和電流分布。","explanationEn":"Sheet thickness, width and interface differences jointly affect threshold and current distributions."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s05-02","order":2,"title":"建立量測鏈","titleEn":"Build a measurement chain","objective":"完成「建立量測鏈」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a measurement chain.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"間接量測需校準模型與不確定度，單一影像不能證明全部電性。","textEn":"Indirect metrology requires model calibration and uncertainty; one image cannot establish every electrical property."},{"id":"sub2nm-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把結構量測與電性量測連到不同驗證問題。","textEn":"Map structural and electrical measurements to distinct verification questions."}],"check":"把結構量測與電性量測連到不同驗證問題。","checkEn":"Map structural and electrical measurements to distinct verification questions.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立量測鏈」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a measurement chain?","options":["片厚、片寬與界面差異會共同造成臨界電壓和電流分布。","間接量測需校準模型與不確定度，單一影像不能證明全部電性。","PDK 規則反映製程可製造性約束，公開示意不能替代實際 PDK。"],"optionsEn":["Sheet thickness, width and interface differences jointly affect threshold and current distributions.","Indirect metrology requires model calibration and uncertainty; one image cannot establish every electrical property.","PDK rules encode manufacturability constraints; public schematics cannot replace an actual PDK."],"answer":1,"explanation":"間接量測需校準模型與不確定度，單一影像不能證明全部電性。","explanationEn":"Indirect metrology requires model calibration and uncertainty; one image cannot establish every electrical property."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s05-03","order":3,"title":"分析設計規則","titleEn":"Analyze design rules","objective":"完成「分析設計規則」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze design rules.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"PDK 規則反映製程可製造性約束，公開示意不能替代實際 PDK。","textEn":"PDK rules encode manufacturability constraints; public schematics cannot replace an actual PDK."},{"id":"sub2nm-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在教學版版圖標示三個假設規則並註明非晶圓廠資料。","textEn":"Mark three assumed teaching rules on a layout and label them non-foundry data."}],"check":"在教學版版圖標示三個假設規則並註明非晶圓廠資料。","checkEn":"Mark three assumed teaching rules on a layout and label them non-foundry data.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析設計規則」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze design rules?","options":["PDK 規則反映製程可製造性約束，公開示意不能替代實際 PDK。","片厚、片寬與界面差異會共同造成臨界電壓和電流分布。","間接量測需校準模型與不確定度，單一影像不能證明全部電性。"],"optionsEn":["PDK rules encode manufacturability constraints; public schematics cannot replace an actual PDK.","Sheet thickness, width and interface differences jointly affect threshold and current distributions.","Indirect metrology requires model calibration and uncertainty; one image cannot establish every electrical property."],"answer":0,"explanation":"PDK 規則反映製程可製造性約束，公開示意不能替代實際 PDK。","explanationEn":"PDK rules encode manufacturability constraints; public schematics cannot replace an actual PDK."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"sub2nm-s06","order":6,"title":"整合與驗證","titleEn":"Integration and validation","steps":[{"id":"sub2nm-s06-01","order":1,"title":"比較 PPA 取捨","titleEn":"Compare PPA trade-offs","objective":"完成「比較 PPA 取捨」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare ppa trade-offs.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"效能、功耗與面積必須在相同工作條件及工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Performance, power and area must be compared under matching operating conditions and workloads."},{"id":"sub2nm-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"拒絕把不同電壓、頻率的數據直接相除排名。","textEn":"Identify why data at different voltages or frequencies cannot be ranked directly."}],"check":"拒絕把不同電壓、頻率的數據直接相除排名。","checkEn":"Identify why data at different voltages or frequencies cannot be ranked directly.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較 PPA 取捨」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare ppa trade-offs?","options":["論文展示、風險試產與量產資格是不同證據等級。","效能、功耗與面積必須在相同工作條件及工作負載下比較。","專用測試結構有助分離接觸、薄膜、元件與互連的問題。"],"optionsEn":["A paper demonstration, risk production and volume qualification represent different evidence levels.","Performance, power and area must be compared under matching operating conditions and workloads.","Dedicated test structures help separate contact, film, device and interconnect issues."],"answer":1,"explanation":"效能、功耗與面積必須在相同工作條件及工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Performance, power and area must be compared under matching operating conditions and workloads."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s06-02","order":2,"title":"規劃測試結構","titleEn":"Plan test structures","objective":"完成「規劃測試結構」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan test structures.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"專用測試結構有助分離接觸、薄膜、元件與互連的問題。","textEn":"Dedicated test structures help separate contact, film, device and interconnect issues."},{"id":"sub2nm-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為四種問題各選一種概念測試結構。","textEn":"Choose a conceptual test structure for each of four issue classes."}],"check":"為四種問題各選一種概念測試結構。","checkEn":"Choose a conceptual test structure for each of four issue classes.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃測試結構」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan test structures?","options":["專用測試結構有助分離接觸、薄膜、元件與互連的問題。","論文展示、風險試產與量產資格是不同證據等級。","效能、功耗與面積必須在相同工作條件及工作負載下比較。"],"optionsEn":["Dedicated test structures help separate contact, film, device and interconnect issues.","A paper demonstration, risk production and volume qualification represent different evidence levels.","Performance, power and area must be compared under matching operating conditions and workloads."],"answer":0,"explanation":"專用測試結構有助分離接觸、薄膜、元件與互連的問題。","explanationEn":"Dedicated test structures help separate contact, film, device and interconnect issues."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"sub2nm-s06-03","order":3,"title":"建立技術成熟度紀錄","titleEn":"Record technology maturity","objective":"完成「建立技術成熟度紀錄」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for record technology maturity.","knowledge":[{"id":"sub2nm-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"論文展示、風險試產與量產資格是不同證據等級。","textEn":"A paper demonstration, risk production and volume qualification represent different evidence levels."},{"id":"sub2nm-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為每個技術主張附日期、來源及成熟度標籤。","textEn":"Attach a date, source and maturity label to each technology claim."}],"check":"為每個技術主張附日期、來源及成熟度標籤。","checkEn":"Attach a date, source and maturity label to each technology claim.","sourceIds":["tsmc-n2","tsmc-a16"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立技術成熟度紀錄」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains record technology maturity?","options":["效能、功耗與面積必須在相同工作條件及工作負載下比較。","專用測試結構有助分離接觸、薄膜、元件與互連的問題。","論文展示、風險試產與量產資格是不同證據等級。"],"optionsEn":["Performance, power and area must be compared under matching operating conditions and workloads.","Dedicated test structures help separate contact, film, device and interconnect issues.","A paper demonstration, risk production and volume qualification represent different evidence levels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"論文展示、風險試產與量產資格是不同證據等級。","explanationEn":"A paper demonstration, risk production and volume qualification represent different evidence levels."},"prerequisiteIds":["sub2nm-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"asml","title":"ASML 微影機系統工程","titleEn":"ASML Lithography Systems Engineering","category":"instruments","summary":"拆解光源、光學、精密平台、真空與量測的共同設計，深入理解 DUV 透鏡與 EUV 反射鏡為何不同。以公開原理建立原創示意模型。","summaryEn":"Explore the co-design of source, optics, precision stages, vacuum and metrology, including why DUV lenses and EUV mirrors differ. Build an original schematic from public principles.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source","v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"diagram":{"type":"lithography","labels":["光源","照明","光罩","投影光學","晶圓平台"],"labelsEn":["Source","Illuminator","Reticle","Projection optics","Wafer stage"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"asml-s01","order":1,"title":"系統規格","titleEn":"System specification","steps":[{"id":"asml-s01-01","order":1,"title":"拆分解析度指標","titleEn":"Decompose resolution","objective":"完成「拆分解析度指標」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for decompose resolution.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"Rayleigh 形式 CD = k1 λ / NA 連結波長、數值孔徑與製程因子。","textEn":"The Rayleigh form CD = k1 λ / NA connects wavelength, numerical aperture and process factor."},{"id":"asml-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"固定兩個參數，觀察第三個參數對概念解析度的影響。","textEn":"Hold two parameters fixed and vary the third in the conceptual resolution model."}],"check":"固定兩個參數，觀察第三個參數對概念解析度的影響。","checkEn":"Hold two parameters fixed and vary the third in the conceptual resolution model.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「拆分解析度指標」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains decompose resolution?","options":["Rayleigh 形式 CD = k1 λ / NA 連結波長、數值孔徑與製程因子。","印得小與印得準是不同能力，套刻關注不同層的相對位置。","光學、平台、熱漂移與量測誤差會共同影響成像，相關誤差不能任意平方和。"],"optionsEn":["The Rayleigh form CD = k1 λ / NA connects wavelength, numerical aperture and process factor.","Printing small and printing accurately are different capabilities; overlay concerns interlayer position.","Optics, stage, thermal drift and metrology errors combine; correlated errors cannot be blindly combined by root-sum-square."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Rayleigh 形式 CD = k1 λ / NA 連結波長、數值孔徑與製程因子。","explanationEn":"The Rayleigh form CD = k1 λ / NA connects wavelength, numerical aperture and process factor."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s01-02","order":2,"title":"區分解析度與套刻","titleEn":"Separate resolution and overlay","objective":"完成「區分解析度與套刻」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for separate resolution and overlay.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"印得小與印得準是不同能力，套刻關注不同層的相對位置。","textEn":"Printing small and printing accurately are different capabilities; overlay concerns interlayer position."},{"id":"asml-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"各畫一個高解析但套刻差、套刻佳但解析不足的例子。","textEn":"Draw examples of good resolution with poor overlay and the reverse."}],"check":"各畫一個高解析但套刻差、套刻佳但解析不足的例子。","checkEn":"Draw examples of good resolution with poor overlay and the reverse.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分解析度與套刻」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains separate resolution and overlay?","options":["光學、平台、熱漂移與量測誤差會共同影響成像，相關誤差不能任意平方和。","Rayleigh 形式 CD = k1 λ / NA 連結波長、數值孔徑與製程因子。","印得小與印得準是不同能力，套刻關注不同層的相對位置。"],"optionsEn":["Optics, stage, thermal drift and metrology errors combine; correlated errors cannot be blindly combined by root-sum-square.","The Rayleigh form CD = k1 λ / NA connects wavelength, numerical aperture and process factor.","Printing small and printing accurately are different capabilities; overlay concerns interlayer position."],"answer":2,"explanation":"印得小與印得準是不同能力，套刻關注不同層的相對位置。","explanationEn":"Printing small and printing accurately are different capabilities; overlay concerns interlayer position."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s01-03","order":3,"title":"建立誤差預算","titleEn":"Build an error budget","objective":"完成「建立誤差預算」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build an error budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光學、平台、熱漂移與量測誤差會共同影響成像，相關誤差不能任意平方和。","textEn":"Optics, stage, thermal drift and metrology errors combine; correlated errors cannot be blindly combined by root-sum-square."},{"id":"asml-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把各誤差標成系統性、隨機性與可能相關。","textEn":"Classify errors as systematic, random and potentially correlated."}],"check":"把各誤差標成系統性、隨機性與可能相關。","checkEn":"Classify errors as systematic, random and potentially correlated.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立誤差預算」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build an error budget?","options":["印得小與印得準是不同能力，套刻關注不同層的相對位置。","光學、平台、熱漂移與量測誤差會共同影響成像，相關誤差不能任意平方和。","Rayleigh 形式 CD = k1 λ / NA 連結波長、數值孔徑與製程因子。"],"optionsEn":["Printing small and printing accurately are different capabilities; overlay concerns interlayer position.","Optics, stage, thermal drift and metrology errors combine; correlated errors cannot be blindly combined by root-sum-square.","The Rayleigh form CD = k1 λ / NA connects wavelength, numerical aperture and process factor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學、平台、熱漂移與量測誤差會共同影響成像，相關誤差不能任意平方和。","explanationEn":"Optics, stage, thermal drift and metrology errors combine; correlated errors cannot be blindly combined by root-sum-square."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s02","order":2,"title":"光源與能量","titleEn":"Source and energy","steps":[{"id":"asml-s02-01","order":1,"title":"比較 DUV 與 EUV","titleEn":"Compare DUV and EUV","objective":"完成「比較 DUV 與 EUV」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare duv and euv.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"ArF DUV 使用 193 nm 光；EUV 使用約 13.5 nm 光，材料與光路設計因此不同。","textEn":"ArF DUV uses 193 nm light; EUV uses about 13.5 nm, requiring different materials and optical paths."},{"id":"asml-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在波長軸標示兩者，說明不可直接互換光學元件。","textEn":"Place both on a wavelength axis and explain why optics are not interchangeable."}],"check":"在波長軸標示兩者，說明不可直接互換光學元件。","checkEn":"Place both on a wavelength axis and explain why optics are not interchangeable.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較 DUV 與 EUV」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare duv and euv?","options":["EUV 系統可由雷射激發錫電漿產生輻射，再收集可用波段。","每段光學傳輸的效率相乘，單一元件損耗會影響總可用光子數。","ArF DUV 使用 193 nm 光；EUV 使用約 13.5 nm 光，材料與光路設計因此不同。"],"optionsEn":["An EUV system can generate radiation by laser excitation of tin plasma and collect the useful band.","Transmission efficiencies multiply along the path; loss in one component affects total usable photons.","ArF DUV uses 193 nm light; EUV uses about 13.5 nm, requiring different materials and optical paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ArF DUV 使用 193 nm 光；EUV 使用約 13.5 nm 光，材料與光路設計因此不同。","explanationEn":"ArF DUV uses 193 nm light; EUV uses about 13.5 nm, requiring different materials and optical paths."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s02-02","order":2,"title":"理解電漿光源鏈","titleEn":"Understand the plasma source chain","objective":"完成「理解電漿光源鏈」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand the plasma source chain.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"EUV 系統可由雷射激發錫電漿產生輻射，再收集可用波段。","textEn":"An EUV system can generate radiation by laser excitation of tin plasma and collect the useful band."},{"id":"asml-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立能量輸入、電漿、集光與熱負載的功能方塊。","textEn":"Build functional blocks for energy input, plasma, collection and thermal load."}],"check":"建立能量輸入、電漿、集光與熱負載的功能方塊。","checkEn":"Build functional blocks for energy input, plasma, collection and thermal load.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解電漿光源鏈」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand the plasma source chain?","options":["ArF DUV 使用 193 nm 光；EUV 使用約 13.5 nm 光，材料與光路設計因此不同。","EUV 系統可由雷射激發錫電漿產生輻射，再收集可用波段。","每段光學傳輸的效率相乘，單一元件損耗會影響總可用光子數。"],"optionsEn":["ArF DUV uses 193 nm light; EUV uses about 13.5 nm, requiring different materials and optical paths.","An EUV system can generate radiation by laser excitation of tin plasma and collect the useful band.","Transmission efficiencies multiply along the path; loss in one component affects total usable photons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"EUV 系統可由雷射激發錫電漿產生輻射，再收集可用波段。","explanationEn":"An EUV system can generate radiation by laser excitation of tin plasma and collect the useful band."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s02-03","order":3,"title":"追蹤光子損耗","titleEn":"Track photon losses","objective":"完成「追蹤光子損耗」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for track photon losses.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"每段光學傳輸的效率相乘，單一元件損耗會影響總可用光子數。","textEn":"Transmission efficiencies multiply along the path; loss in one component affects total usable photons."},{"id":"asml-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用無因次效率計算三段示意傳輸並檢查範圍。","textEn":"Compute three-stage illustrative transmission using dimensionless efficiencies."}],"check":"用無因次效率計算三段示意傳輸並檢查範圍。","checkEn":"Compute three-stage illustrative transmission using dimensionless efficiencies.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤光子損耗」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains track photon losses?","options":["每段光學傳輸的效率相乘，單一元件損耗會影響總可用光子數。","ArF DUV 使用 193 nm 光；EUV 使用約 13.5 nm 光，材料與光路設計因此不同。","EUV 系統可由雷射激發錫電漿產生輻射，再收集可用波段。"],"optionsEn":["Transmission efficiencies multiply along the path; loss in one component affects total usable photons.","ArF DUV uses 193 nm light; EUV uses about 13.5 nm, requiring different materials and optical paths.","An EUV system can generate radiation by laser excitation of tin plasma and collect the useful band."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每段光學傳輸的效率相乘，單一元件損耗會影響總可用光子數。","explanationEn":"Transmission efficiencies multiply along the path; loss in one component affects total usable photons."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s03","order":3,"title":"DUV 透鏡與色差","titleEn":"DUV lenses and chromatic aberration","steps":[{"id":"asml-s03-01","order":1,"title":"解釋色散","titleEn":"Explain dispersion","objective":"完成「解釋色散」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for explain dispersion.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"材料折射率隨波長改變，使不同波長的焦距可能不同。","textEn":"A material's refractive index varies with wavelength, potentially changing focal length."},{"id":"asml-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出兩個波長的焦點差異，區分色差與球差。","textEn":"Draw focal differences for two wavelengths and distinguish chromatic from spherical aberration."}],"check":"畫出兩個波長的焦點差異，區分色差與球差。","checkEn":"Draw focal differences for two wavelengths and distinguish chromatic from spherical aberration.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「解釋色散」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains explain dispersion?","options":["NA = n sin θ；增加介質折射率可提升 NA，但也新增流體與污染控制需求。","材料折射率隨波長改變，使不同波長的焦距可能不同。","窄頻光源、材料選擇與多元件光學設計可降低色差；沒有通用的零色差配方。"],"optionsEn":["NA = n sin θ; raising medium index can increase NA while adding fluid and contamination constraints.","A material's refractive index varies with wavelength, potentially changing focal length.","Narrowband illumination, material selection and multi-element design reduce chromatic effects; there is no universal zero-aberration recipe."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料折射率隨波長改變，使不同波長的焦距可能不同。","explanationEn":"A material's refractive index varies with wavelength, potentially changing focal length."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s03-02","order":2,"title":"比較色差抑制策略","titleEn":"Compare chromatic-control strategies","objective":"完成「比較色差抑制策略」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare chromatic-control strategies.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"窄頻光源、材料選擇與多元件光學設計可降低色差；沒有通用的零色差配方。","textEn":"Narrowband illumination, material selection and multi-element design reduce chromatic effects; there is no universal zero-aberration recipe."},{"id":"asml-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出每種策略改善的因素及仍保留的誤差。","textEn":"List the factor improved and residual errors for each strategy."}],"check":"列出每種策略改善的因素及仍保留的誤差。","checkEn":"List the factor improved and residual errors for each strategy.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較色差抑制策略」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare chromatic-control strategies?","options":["窄頻光源、材料選擇與多元件光學設計可降低色差；沒有通用的零色差配方。","NA = n sin θ；增加介質折射率可提升 NA，但也新增流體與污染控制需求。","材料折射率隨波長改變，使不同波長的焦距可能不同。"],"optionsEn":["Narrowband illumination, material selection and multi-element design reduce chromatic effects; there is no universal zero-aberration recipe.","NA = n sin θ; raising medium index can increase NA while adding fluid and contamination constraints.","A material's refractive index varies with wavelength, potentially changing focal length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"窄頻光源、材料選擇與多元件光學設計可降低色差；沒有通用的零色差配方。","explanationEn":"Narrowband illumination, material selection and multi-element design reduce chromatic effects; there is no universal zero-aberration recipe."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s03-03","order":3,"title":"理解浸潤式 NA","titleEn":"Understand immersion NA","objective":"完成「理解浸潤式 NA」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand immersion na.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"NA = n sin θ；增加介質折射率可提升 NA，但也新增流體與污染控制需求。","textEn":"NA = n sin θ; raising medium index can increase NA while adding fluid and contamination constraints."},{"id":"asml-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用相同角度比較兩種介質的概念 NA。","textEn":"Compare conceptual NA for two media at the same angle."}],"check":"用相同角度比較兩種介質的概念 NA。","checkEn":"Compare conceptual NA for two media at the same angle.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解浸潤式 NA」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand immersion na?","options":["材料折射率隨波長改變，使不同波長的焦距可能不同。","窄頻光源、材料選擇與多元件光學設計可降低色差；沒有通用的零色差配方。","NA = n sin θ；增加介質折射率可提升 NA，但也新增流體與污染控制需求。"],"optionsEn":["A material's refractive index varies with wavelength, potentially changing focal length.","Narrowband illumination, material selection and multi-element design reduce chromatic effects; there is no universal zero-aberration recipe.","NA = n sin θ; raising medium index can increase NA while adding fluid and contamination constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"NA = n sin θ；增加介質折射率可提升 NA，但也新增流體與污染控制需求。","explanationEn":"NA = n sin θ; raising medium index can increase NA while adding fluid and contamination constraints."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s04","order":4,"title":"EUV 反射光學","titleEn":"EUV reflective optics","steps":[{"id":"asml-s04-01","order":1,"title":"解釋反射鏡選擇","titleEn":"Explain mirror selection","objective":"完成「解釋反射鏡選擇」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for explain mirror selection.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"EUV 在許多材料中強烈吸收，因此投影系統以反射式多層膜光學為核心。","textEn":"EUV is strongly absorbed in many materials, so projection systems rely on multilayer reflective optics."},{"id":"asml-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"將透射式與反射式光路分別標記，指出吸收所在。","textEn":"Label transmissive and reflective paths and identify absorption."}],"check":"將透射式與反射式光路分別標記，指出吸收所在。","checkEn":"Label transmissive and reflective paths and identify absorption.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「解釋反射鏡選擇」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains explain mirror selection?","options":["EUV 在許多材料中強烈吸收，因此投影系統以反射式多層膜光學為核心。","多層界面的反射振幅和相位疊加，產生與波長及角度相關的反射帶。","鏡面形狀偏差及粗糙度分別影響波前和散射，兩種量測不可互相取代。"],"optionsEn":["EUV is strongly absorbed in many materials, so projection systems rely on multilayer reflective optics.","Reflected amplitudes and phases from multilayer interfaces combine into a wavelength- and angle-dependent reflection band.","Mirror figure error and roughness affect wavefront and scattering respectively; one measurement cannot replace the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"EUV 在許多材料中強烈吸收，因此投影系統以反射式多層膜光學為核心。","explanationEn":"EUV is strongly absorbed in many materials, so projection systems rely on multilayer reflective optics."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解多層膜干涉","titleEn":"Understand multilayer interference","objective":"完成「理解多層膜干涉」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand multilayer interference.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"多層界面的反射振幅和相位疊加，產生與波長及角度相關的反射帶。","textEn":"Reflected amplitudes and phases from multilayer interfaces combine into a wavelength- and angle-dependent reflection band."},{"id":"asml-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以相位箭頭示意相長與相消，勿杜撰供應商膜厚配方。","textEn":"Use phase arrows to illustrate constructive and destructive interference without inventing coating recipes."}],"check":"以相位箭頭示意相長與相消，勿杜撰供應商膜厚配方。","checkEn":"Use phase arrows to illustrate constructive and destructive interference without inventing coating recipes.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解多層膜干涉」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand multilayer interference?","options":["鏡面形狀偏差及粗糙度分別影響波前和散射，兩種量測不可互相取代。","EUV 在許多材料中強烈吸收，因此投影系統以反射式多層膜光學為核心。","多層界面的反射振幅和相位疊加，產生與波長及角度相關的反射帶。"],"optionsEn":["Mirror figure error and roughness affect wavefront and scattering respectively; one measurement cannot replace the other.","EUV is strongly absorbed in many materials, so projection systems rely on multilayer reflective optics.","Reflected amplitudes and phases from multilayer interfaces combine into a wavelength- and angle-dependent reflection band."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多層界面的反射振幅和相位疊加，產生與波長及角度相關的反射帶。","explanationEn":"Reflected amplitudes and phases from multilayer interfaces combine into a wavelength- and angle-dependent reflection band."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s04-03","order":3,"title":"分析波前與表面誤差","titleEn":"Analyze wavefront and surface errors","objective":"完成「分析波前與表面誤差」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze wavefront and surface errors.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"鏡面形狀偏差及粗糙度分別影響波前和散射，兩種量測不可互相取代。","textEn":"Mirror figure error and roughness affect wavefront and scattering respectively; one measurement cannot replace the other."},{"id":"asml-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立形狀、粗糙度、反射率三欄檢核表。","textEn":"Build a review table for figure, roughness and reflectivity."}],"check":"建立形狀、粗糙度、反射率三欄檢核表。","checkEn":"Build a review table for figure, roughness and reflectivity.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析波前與表面誤差」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze wavefront and surface errors?","options":["多層界面的反射振幅和相位疊加，產生與波長及角度相關的反射帶。","鏡面形狀偏差及粗糙度分別影響波前和散射，兩種量測不可互相取代。","EUV 在許多材料中強烈吸收，因此投影系統以反射式多層膜光學為核心。"],"optionsEn":["Reflected amplitudes and phases from multilayer interfaces combine into a wavelength- and angle-dependent reflection band.","Mirror figure error and roughness affect wavefront and scattering respectively; one measurement cannot replace the other.","EUV is strongly absorbed in many materials, so projection systems rely on multilayer reflective optics."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鏡面形狀偏差及粗糙度分別影響波前和散射，兩種量測不可互相取代。","explanationEn":"Mirror figure error and roughness affect wavefront and scattering respectively; one measurement cannot replace the other."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s05","order":5,"title":"光罩與運算微影","titleEn":"Reticle and computational lithography","steps":[{"id":"asml-s05-01","order":1,"title":"辨識反射式光罩","titleEn":"Identify a reflective reticle","objective":"完成「辨識反射式光罩」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify a reflective reticle.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"EUV 光罩利用反射結構與吸收圖案調變光場，其成像包含三維效應。","textEn":"An EUV reticle modulates light through reflective structure and absorber patterns, including three-dimensional imaging effects."},{"id":"asml-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在光罩示意剖面標示反射層、吸收區與入射方向。","textEn":"Label reflector, absorber region and incidence direction on a reticle section."}],"check":"在光罩示意剖面標示反射層、吸收區與入射方向。","checkEn":"Label reflector, absorber region and incidence direction on a reticle section.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識反射式光罩」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify a reflective reticle?","options":["光學鄰近效應修正預先調整光罩圖形，使印製輪廓更接近目標。","有限光子與材料反應的統計起伏會造成局部成像變異。","EUV 光罩利用反射結構與吸收圖案調變光場，其成像包含三維效應。"],"optionsEn":["Optical proximity correction modifies mask patterns so printed contours better approach the target.","Finite photon counts and material-response fluctuations cause local imaging variation.","An EUV reticle modulates light through reflective structure and absorber patterns, including three-dimensional imaging effects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"EUV 光罩利用反射結構與吸收圖案調變光場，其成像包含三維效應。","explanationEn":"An EUV reticle modulates light through reflective structure and absorber patterns, including three-dimensional imaging effects."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s05-02","order":2,"title":"理解 OPC 修正","titleEn":"Understand OPC corrections","objective":"完成「理解 OPC 修正」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand opc corrections.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光學鄰近效應修正預先調整光罩圖形，使印製輪廓更接近目標。","textEn":"Optical proximity correction modifies mask patterns so printed contours better approach the target."},{"id":"asml-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較直角目標、未修正像與概念修正像。","textEn":"Compare target corners, uncorrected image and conceptually corrected image."}],"check":"比較直角目標、未修正像與概念修正像。","checkEn":"Compare target corners, uncorrected image and conceptually corrected image.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解 OPC 修正」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand opc corrections?","options":["EUV 光罩利用反射結構與吸收圖案調變光場，其成像包含三維效應。","光學鄰近效應修正預先調整光罩圖形，使印製輪廓更接近目標。","有限光子與材料反應的統計起伏會造成局部成像變異。"],"optionsEn":["An EUV reticle modulates light through reflective structure and absorber patterns, including three-dimensional imaging effects.","Optical proximity correction modifies mask patterns so printed contours better approach the target.","Finite photon counts and material-response fluctuations cause local imaging variation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學鄰近效應修正預先調整光罩圖形，使印製輪廓更接近目標。","explanationEn":"Optical proximity correction modifies mask patterns so printed contours better approach the target."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s05-03","order":3,"title":"評估隨機缺陷","titleEn":"Assess stochastic defects","objective":"完成「評估隨機缺陷」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for assess stochastic defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"有限光子與材料反應的統計起伏會造成局部成像變異。","textEn":"Finite photon counts and material-response fluctuations cause local imaging variation."},{"id":"asml-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"區分平均輪廓偏差與隨機缺陷率，兩者分開記錄。","textEn":"Record mean contour error separately from stochastic defect rate."}],"check":"區分平均輪廓偏差與隨機缺陷率，兩者分開記錄。","checkEn":"Record mean contour error separately from stochastic defect rate.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「評估隨機缺陷」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains assess stochastic defects?","options":["有限光子與材料反應的統計起伏會造成局部成像變異。","EUV 光罩利用反射結構與吸收圖案調變光場，其成像包含三維效應。","光學鄰近效應修正預先調整光罩圖形，使印製輪廓更接近目標。"],"optionsEn":["Finite photon counts and material-response fluctuations cause local imaging variation.","An EUV reticle modulates light through reflective structure and absorber patterns, including three-dimensional imaging effects.","Optical proximity correction modifies mask patterns so printed contours better approach the target."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有限光子與材料反應的統計起伏會造成局部成像變異。","explanationEn":"Finite photon counts and material-response fluctuations cause local imaging variation."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s06","order":6,"title":"精密機電平台","titleEn":"Precision mechatronic stages","steps":[{"id":"asml-s06-01","order":1,"title":"畫出定位閉迴路","titleEn":"Draw the positioning loop","objective":"完成「畫出定位閉迴路」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for draw the positioning loop.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"感測器、控制器與致動器組成閉迴路，感測延遲與結構共振限制性能。","textEn":"Sensors, controller and actuator form a feedback loop whose performance is limited by delay and structural resonance."},{"id":"asml-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"將命令、量測及誤差信號連到正確方塊。","textEn":"Connect command, measurement and error signals to the correct blocks."}],"check":"將命令、量測及誤差信號連到正確方塊。","checkEn":"Connect command, measurement and error signals to the correct blocks.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「畫出定位閉迴路」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains draw the positioning loop?","options":["光罩與晶圓的相對掃描需符合投影縮放及時序關係。","感測器、控制器與致動器組成閉迴路，感測延遲與結構共振限制性能。","快速振動與慢速熱漂移有不同頻率特徵，通常需要不同抑制方法。"],"optionsEn":["Relative reticle and wafer scanning must follow the projection scaling and timing relationship.","Sensors, controller and actuator form a feedback loop whose performance is limited by delay and structural resonance.","Fast vibration and slow thermal drift occupy different frequency ranges and usually need different mitigation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測器、控制器與致動器組成閉迴路，感測延遲與結構共振限制性能。","explanationEn":"Sensors, controller and actuator form a feedback loop whose performance is limited by delay and structural resonance."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s06-02","order":2,"title":"分離振動與漂移","titleEn":"Separate vibration and drift","objective":"完成「分離振動與漂移」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for separate vibration and drift.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"快速振動與慢速熱漂移有不同頻率特徵，通常需要不同抑制方法。","textEn":"Fast vibration and slow thermal drift occupy different frequency ranges and usually need different mitigation."},{"id":"asml-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把示意時間序列拆為快速分量與慢變分量。","textEn":"Separate a schematic time series into fast and slowly varying components."}],"check":"把示意時間序列拆為快速分量與慢變分量。","checkEn":"Separate a schematic time series into fast and slowly varying components.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分離振動與漂移」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains separate vibration and drift?","options":["快速振動與慢速熱漂移有不同頻率特徵，通常需要不同抑制方法。","光罩與晶圓的相對掃描需符合投影縮放及時序關係。","感測器、控制器與致動器組成閉迴路，感測延遲與結構共振限制性能。"],"optionsEn":["Fast vibration and slow thermal drift occupy different frequency ranges and usually need different mitigation.","Relative reticle and wafer scanning must follow the projection scaling and timing relationship.","Sensors, controller and actuator form a feedback loop whose performance is limited by delay and structural resonance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"快速振動與慢速熱漂移有不同頻率特徵，通常需要不同抑制方法。","explanationEn":"Fast vibration and slow thermal drift occupy different frequency ranges and usually need different mitigation."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s06-03","order":3,"title":"檢查掃描同步","titleEn":"Review scan synchronization","objective":"完成「檢查掃描同步」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for review scan synchronization.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光罩與晶圓的相對掃描需符合投影縮放及時序關係。","textEn":"Relative reticle and wafer scanning must follow the projection scaling and timing relationship."},{"id":"asml-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以無單位動畫檢查兩平台相對位移是否一致。","textEn":"Use a dimensionless animation to check relative platform displacement."}],"check":"以無單位動畫檢查兩平台相對位移是否一致。","checkEn":"Use a dimensionless animation to check relative platform displacement.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「檢查掃描同步」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains review scan synchronization?","options":["感測器、控制器與致動器組成閉迴路，感測延遲與結構共振限制性能。","快速振動與慢速熱漂移有不同頻率特徵，通常需要不同抑制方法。","光罩與晶圓的相對掃描需符合投影縮放及時序關係。"],"optionsEn":["Sensors, controller and actuator form a feedback loop whose performance is limited by delay and structural resonance.","Fast vibration and slow thermal drift occupy different frequency ranges and usually need different mitigation.","Relative reticle and wafer scanning must follow the projection scaling and timing relationship."],"answer":2,"explanation":"光罩與晶圓的相對掃描需符合投影縮放及時序關係。","explanationEn":"Relative reticle and wafer scanning must follow the projection scaling and timing relationship."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s07","order":7,"title":"真空熱與污染","titleEn":"Vacuum thermal and contamination control","steps":[{"id":"asml-s07-01","order":1,"title":"理解真空必要性","titleEn":"Understand vacuum requirements","objective":"完成「理解真空必要性」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand vacuum requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s07-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"EUV 光路需降低氣體吸收；真空也改變散熱及材料逸氣條件。","textEn":"EUV paths reduce gas absorption through vacuum, which also changes heat transfer and outgassing conditions."},{"id":"asml-s07-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較空氣與真空中可用的散熱路徑。","textEn":"Compare available heat-transfer paths in air and vacuum."}],"check":"比較空氣與真空中可用的散熱路徑。","checkEn":"Compare available heat-transfer paths in air and vacuum.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解真空必要性」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand vacuum requirements?","options":["EUV 光路需降低氣體吸收；真空也改變散熱及材料逸氣條件。","吸收能量引起溫升，溫升經熱膨脹改變幾何，最終影響光學誤差。","污染會降低反射率或增加缺陷，潔淨控制必須連結可量測的退化。"],"optionsEn":["EUV paths reduce gas absorption through vacuum, which also changes heat transfer and outgassing conditions.","Absorption causes heating, thermal expansion changes geometry and geometry affects optical error.","Contamination can reduce reflectivity or add defects; cleanliness controls must link to measurable degradation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"EUV 光路需降低氣體吸收；真空也改變散熱及材料逸氣條件。","explanationEn":"EUV paths reduce gas absorption through vacuum, which also changes heat transfer and outgassing conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s06-03"],"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s07-02","order":2,"title":"追蹤熱變形鏈","titleEn":"Trace thermal deformation","objective":"完成「追蹤熱變形鏈」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for trace thermal deformation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s07-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"吸收能量引起溫升，溫升經熱膨脹改變幾何，最終影響光學誤差。","textEn":"Absorption causes heating, thermal expansion changes geometry and geometry affects optical error."},{"id":"asml-s07-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"連結吸收功率、溫度、位移與波前四個量。","textEn":"Connect absorbed power, temperature, displacement and wavefront error."}],"check":"連結吸收功率、溫度、位移與波前四個量。","checkEn":"Connect absorbed power, temperature, displacement and wavefront error.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤熱變形鏈」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains trace thermal deformation?","options":["污染會降低反射率或增加缺陷，潔淨控制必須連結可量測的退化。","EUV 光路需降低氣體吸收；真空也改變散熱及材料逸氣條件。","吸收能量引起溫升，溫升經熱膨脹改變幾何，最終影響光學誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Contamination can reduce reflectivity or add defects; cleanliness controls must link to measurable degradation.","EUV paths reduce gas absorption through vacuum, which also changes heat transfer and outgassing conditions.","Absorption causes heating, thermal expansion changes geometry and geometry affects optical error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸收能量引起溫升，溫升經熱膨脹改變幾何，最終影響光學誤差。","explanationEn":"Absorption causes heating, thermal expansion changes geometry and geometry affects optical error."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s07-01"],"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s07-03","order":3,"title":"建立污染監測項","titleEn":"Define contamination monitoring","objective":"完成「建立污染監測項」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define contamination monitoring.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s07-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"污染會降低反射率或增加缺陷，潔淨控制必須連結可量測的退化。","textEn":"Contamination can reduce reflectivity or add defects; cleanliness controls must link to measurable degradation."},{"id":"asml-s07-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"指定反射率趨勢與缺陷趨勢的追蹤欄位。","textEn":"Define monitoring fields for reflectivity and defect trends."}],"check":"指定反射率趨勢與缺陷趨勢的追蹤欄位。","checkEn":"Define monitoring fields for reflectivity and defect trends.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立污染監測項」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define contamination monitoring?","options":["吸收能量引起溫升，溫升經熱膨脹改變幾何，最終影響光學誤差。","污染會降低反射率或增加缺陷，潔淨控制必須連結可量測的退化。","EUV 光路需降低氣體吸收；真空也改變散熱及材料逸氣條件。"],"optionsEn":["Absorption causes heating, thermal expansion changes geometry and geometry affects optical error.","Contamination can reduce reflectivity or add defects; cleanliness controls must link to measurable degradation.","EUV paths reduce gas absorption through vacuum, which also changes heat transfer and outgassing conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"污染會降低反射率或增加缺陷，潔淨控制必須連結可量測的退化。","explanationEn":"Contamination can reduce reflectivity or add defects; cleanliness controls must link to measurable degradation."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s07-02"],"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-s08","order":8,"title":"整機整合與驗收","titleEn":"System integration and acceptance","steps":[{"id":"asml-s08-01","order":1,"title":"整合焦距與劑量窗口","titleEn":"Integrate focus and dose windows","objective":"完成「整合焦距與劑量窗口」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for integrate focus and dose windows.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s08-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"焦距與曝光劑量共同決定可接受圖案的製程窗口。","textEn":"Focus and exposure dose jointly define the process window for acceptable patterns."},{"id":"asml-s08-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在二維參數圖標出符合概念規格的區域。","textEn":"Mark the acceptable region on a two-parameter conceptual map."}],"check":"在二維參數圖標出符合概念規格的區域。","checkEn":"Mark the acceptable region on a two-parameter conceptual map.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「整合焦距與劑量窗口」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains integrate focus and dose windows?","options":["單一模組合格不代表整機合格，介面誤差需透過整合測試暴露。","公開系統原理可以支援工程學習，不能補齊未公開的製造公差與製程。","焦距與曝光劑量共同決定可接受圖案的製程窗口。"],"optionsEn":["Passing individual modules does not prove the whole system; interface errors require integration tests.","Public system principles support engineering learning but do not supply undisclosed manufacturing tolerances or processes.","Focus and exposure dose jointly define the process window for acceptable patterns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"焦距與曝光劑量共同決定可接受圖案的製程窗口。","explanationEn":"Focus and exposure dose jointly define the process window for acceptable patterns."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s07-03"],"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s08-02","order":2,"title":"制定跨模組測試","titleEn":"Define cross-module tests","objective":"完成「制定跨模組測試」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define cross-module tests.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s08-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"單一模組合格不代表整機合格，介面誤差需透過整合測試暴露。","textEn":"Passing individual modules does not prove the whole system; interface errors require integration tests."},{"id":"asml-s08-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為光源到光學、光學到平台各設定一個介面測試。","textEn":"Specify one interface test for source-to-optics and optics-to-stage."}],"check":"為光源到光學、光學到平台各設定一個介面測試。","checkEn":"Specify one interface test for source-to-optics and optics-to-stage.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「制定跨模組測試」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define cross-module tests?","options":["焦距與曝光劑量共同決定可接受圖案的製程窗口。","單一模組合格不代表整機合格，介面誤差需透過整合測試暴露。","公開系統原理可以支援工程學習，不能補齊未公開的製造公差與製程。"],"optionsEn":["Focus and exposure dose jointly define the process window for acceptable patterns.","Passing individual modules does not prove the whole system; interface errors require integration tests.","Public system principles support engineering learning but do not supply undisclosed manufacturing tolerances or processes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一模組合格不代表整機合格，介面誤差需透過整合測試暴露。","explanationEn":"Passing individual modules does not prove the whole system; interface errors require integration tests."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s08-01"],"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"asml-s08-03","order":3,"title":"交付證據與限制","titleEn":"Deliver evidence and limits","objective":"完成「交付證據與限制」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver evidence and limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-s08-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"公開系統原理可以支援工程學習，不能補齊未公開的製造公差與製程。","textEn":"Public system principles support engineering learning but do not supply undisclosed manufacturing tolerances or processes."},{"id":"asml-s08-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交方塊圖、誤差預算及待驗證清單，清楚標示示意模型。","textEn":"Submit the block diagram, error budget and open questions, clearly labeled as a schematic model."}],"check":"提交方塊圖、誤差預算及待驗證清單，清楚標示示意模型。","checkEn":"Submit the block diagram, error budget and open questions, clearly labeled as a schematic model.","sourceIds":["asml-principles","asml-optics","asml-source"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付證據與限制」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver evidence and limits?","options":["公開系統原理可以支援工程學習，不能補齊未公開的製造公差與製程。","焦距與曝光劑量共同決定可接受圖案的製程窗口。","單一模組合格不代表整機合格，介面誤差需透過整合測試暴露。"],"optionsEn":["Public system principles support engineering learning but do not supply undisclosed manufacturing tolerances or processes.","Focus and exposure dose jointly define the process window for acceptable patterns.","Passing individual modules does not prove the whole system; interface errors require integration tests."],"answer":0,"explanation":"公開系統原理可以支援工程學習，不能補齊未公開的製造公差與製程。","explanationEn":"Public system principles support engineering learning but do not supply undisclosed manufacturing tolerances or processes."},"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s08-02"],"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"asml-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光」與「8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field\" and \"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"asml-v12-01","title":"High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-s08-03"],"objective":"說明「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"把 NA 從 0.33 提高到 0.55，光罩端的光錐也跟著變寬。EUV 光罩是反射式，入射錐與反射錐不能重疊，而且必須落在光罩多層膜的角度接受範圍內；以光罩上約 6° 的主光線角計算，若仍用等向 4× 縮小，光錐半角會超過 6°，入射與反射光互相干涉。ASML 的 EXE 平台因此採用變形光學：垂直掃描方向（x，沿狹縫）縮小 4×，掃描方向（y）縮小 8×，掃描方向的光罩端光錐減半。代價是標準 6 吋光罩的 104 × 132 mm 圖案區在晶圓上只剩 26 × 16.5 mm，即半場，每片晶圓曝光次數加倍，大晶粒需要拼接，光罩資料也必須在 y 方向拉長 2 倍。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Raising NA from 0.33 to 0.55 widens the cone of light at the reticle as well. The EUV reticle is reflective, so the incident and reflected cones must not overlap and must stay within the angular acceptance of the mask multilayer; with a chief-ray angle of about 6° on the mask, keeping an isotropic 4× reduction would push the cone half-angle beyond 6° and the incident and reflected light would collide. ASML's EXE platform therefore uses anamorphic optics: 4× reduction across the scan (x, along the slit) and 8× in the scan direction (y), halving the mask-side cone in y. The price is that the 104 × 132 mm pattern area of a standard 6-inch mask covers only 26 × 16.5 mm on the wafer, a half field, so each wafer needs twice as many exposures, large dies must be stitched, and mask data are stretched 2× in y. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：光罩端 NA = NA/M：NXE 為 0.33/4 = 0.0825（4.7°），光錐在 1.3° 到 10.7° 之間；0.55/4 = 0.1375（7.9°）超過 6° 主光線角，光錐跨越法線（−1.9° 到 13.9°）；y 方向 8× 時 0.0688（3.9°），光錐回到 2.1° 到 9.9°。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Mask-side NA = NA/M: NXE has 0.33/4 = 0.0825 (4.7°), a cone from 1.3° to 10.7°; 0.55/4 = 0.1375 (7.9°) exceeds the 6° chief-ray angle and the cone crosses the normal (−1.9° to 13.9°); with 8× in y it is 0.0688 (3.9°), back to 2.1° to 9.9°.","failure":"常見誤解：「High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-01-k1","title":"High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光","titleEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field","text":"把 NA 從 0.33 提高到 0.55，光罩端的光錐也跟著變寬。EUV 光罩是反射式，入射錐與反射錐不能重疊，而且必須落在光罩多層膜的角度接受範圍內；以光罩上約 6° 的主光線角計算，若仍用等向 4× 縮小，光錐半角會超過 6°，入射與反射光互相干涉。","textEn":"Raising NA from 0.33 to 0.55 widens the cone of light at the reticle as well. The EUV reticle is reflective, so the incident and reflected cones must not overlap and must stay within the angular acceptance of the mask multilayer; with a chief-ray angle of about 6° on the mask, keeping an isotropic 4× reduction would push the cone half-angle beyond 6° and the incident and reflected light would collide.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field\" is correct?","options":["High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","把 NA 從 0.33 提高到 0.55，光罩端的光錐也跟著變寬。","光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","Raising NA from 0.33 to 0.55 widens the cone of light at the reticle as well.","Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把 NA 從 0.33 提高到 0.55，光罩端的光錐也跟著變寬。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Raising NA from 0.33 to 0.55 widens the cone of light at the reticle as well. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"asml-v12-02","title":"High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光：定量估算","titleEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：光罩端 NA = NA/M：NXE 為 0.33/4 = 0.0825（4.7°），光錐在 1.3° 到 10.7° 之間；0.55/4 = 0.1375（7.9°）超過 6° 主光線角，光錐跨越法線（−1.9° 到 13.9°）；y 方向 8× 時 0.0688（3.9°），光錐回到 2.1° 到 9.9°。場大小：x = 104/4 = 26 mm、y = 132/8 = 16.5 mm，面積 429 mm² 對 858 mm²；300 mm 晶圓含部分場約由 96 場增為約 186 場。k₁ = 0.33 時 CD = 0.33 × 13.5/0.55 ≈ 8.1 nm，而 λ/NA² 景深由 124 nm 降到 44.6 nm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Mask-side NA = NA/M: NXE has 0.33/4 = 0.0825 (4.7°), a cone from 1.3° to 10.7°; 0.55/4 = 0.1375 (7.9°) exceeds the 6° chief-ray angle and the cone crosses the normal (−1.9° to 13.9°); with 8× in y it is 0.0688 (3.9°), back to 2.1° to 9.9°. Field size: x = 104/4 = 26 mm and y = 132/8 = 16.5 mm, 429 mm² against 858 mm²; a 300 mm wafer goes from about 96 to about 186 fields including partials. With k₁ = 0.33, CD = 0.33 × 13.5/0.55 ≈ 8.1 nm, while the λ/NA² depth of focus falls from 124 nm to 44.6 nm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以含 x 與 y 兩種方向線距的測試光罩曝光，確認晶圓上兩方向的 CD 與圖案位置一致，儘管光罩上的尺寸相差 2 倍；量測場尺寸與兩個半場交界處的拼接套刻；做焦距—劑量矩陣，比較實測景深與 44.6 nm 等級的預測；再量不同節距與方向的最佳焦距差，評估光罩三維陰影效應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Expose a test reticle with line-space patterns in both x and y and confirm that wafer CD and placement match in both orientations even though the mask features differ by 2×; measure field dimensions and the stitching overlay where two half fields meet; run a focus–exposure matrix and compare the measured depth of focus with the 44.6 nm-scale prediction; then measure best-focus differences across pitch and orientation to assess mask 3D shadowing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"光罩端 NA = NA/M：NXE 為 0.33/4 = 0.0825（4.7°），光錐在 1.3° 到 10.7° 之間；0.55/4 = 0.1375（7.9°）超過 6° 主光線角，光錐跨越法線（−1.9° 到 13.9°）；y 方向 8× 時 0.0688（3.9°），光錐回到 2.1° 到 9.9°。場大小：x = 104/4 = 26 mm、y = 132/8 = 16.5 mm，面積 429 mm² 對 858 mm²；300 mm 晶圓含部分場約由 96 場增為約 186 場。k₁ = 0.33 時 CD = 0.33 × 13.5/0.55 ≈ 8.1 nm，而 λ/NA² 景深由 124 nm 降到 44.6 nm。","textEn":"Mask-side NA = NA/M: NXE has 0.33/4 = 0.0825 (4.7°), a cone from 1.3° to 10.7°; 0.55/4 = 0.1375 (7.9°) exceeds the 6° chief-ray angle and the cone crosses the normal (−1.9° to 13.9°); with 8× in y it is 0.0688 (3.9°), back to 2.1° to 9.9°. Field size: x = 104/4 = 26 mm and y = 132/8 = 16.5 mm, 429 mm² against 858 mm²; a 300 mm wafer goes from about 96 to about 186 fields including partials. With k₁ = 0.33, CD = 0.33 × 13.5/0.55 ≈ 8.1 nm, while the λ/NA² depth of focus falls from 124 nm to 44.6 nm.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field\", which statement holds?","options":["集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。","晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。","光罩端 NA = NA/M：NXE 為 0.33/4 = 0.0825（4.7°），光錐在 1.3° 到 10.7° 之間。"],"optionsEn":["A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.","Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.","Mask-side NA = NA/M: NXE has 0.33/4 = 0.0825 (4.7°), a cone from 1.3° to 10.7°."],"answer":2,"explanation":"光罩端 NA = NA/M：NXE 為 0.33/4 = 0.0825（4.7°），光錐在 1.3° 到 10.7° 之間；0.55/4 = 0.1375（7.9°）超過 6° 主光線角，光錐跨越法線（−1.9° 到 13.9°）；y 方向 8× 時 0.0688（3.9°），光錐回到 2.1° 到 9.9°。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Mask-side NA = NA/M: NXE has 0.33/4 = 0.0825 (4.7°), a cone from 1.3° to 10.7°; 0.55/4 = 0.1375 (7.9°) exceeds the 6° chief-ray angle and the cone crosses the normal (−1.9° to 13.9°); with 8× in y it is 0.0688 (3.9°), back to 2.1° to 9.9°. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"asml-v12-03","title":"High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光：量測與驗證","titleEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以含 x 與 y 兩種方向線距的測試光罩曝光，確認晶圓上兩方向的 CD 與圖案位置一致，儘管光罩上的尺寸相差 2 倍；量測場尺寸與兩個半場交界處的拼接套刻；做焦距—劑量矩陣，比較實測景深與 44.6 nm 等級的預測；再量不同節距與方向的最佳焦距差，評估光罩三維陰影效應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Expose a test reticle with line-space patterns in both x and y and confirm that wafer CD and placement match in both orientations even though the mask features differ by 2×; measure field dimensions and the stitching overlay where two half fields meet; run a focus–exposure matrix and compare the measured depth of focus with the 44.6 nm-scale prediction; then measure best-focus differences across pitch and orientation to assess mask 3D shadowing. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：超過 26 × 16.5 mm 的晶粒必須拆成兩個半場，交界處的套刻與 CD 不連續會讓跨越邊界的導線斷開或變細；若光罩資料的 y 方向縮放處理錯誤，整片圖案失真；光罩三維陰影造成與方向有關的影像位移，表現為無法用單一焦距修正的系統套刻。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A die larger than 26 × 16.5 mm must be split into two half fields, and overlay or CD discontinuity at the seam can open or neck lines that cross it; mishandled y scaling in the mask data distorts the whole pattern; mask 3D shadowing shifts images depending on orientation, showing up as systematic overlay that no single focus setting can correct.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以含 x 與 y 兩種方向線距的測試光罩曝光，確認晶圓上兩方向的 CD 與圖案位置一致，儘管光罩上的尺寸相差 2 倍；量測場尺寸與兩個半場交界處的拼接套刻；做焦距—劑量矩陣，比較實測景深與 44.6 nm 等級的預測；再量不同節距與方向的最佳焦距差，評估光罩三維陰影效應。","textEn":"Expose a test reticle with line-space patterns in both x and y and confirm that wafer CD and placement match in both orientations even though the mask features differ by 2×; measure field dimensions and the stitching overlay where two half fields meet; run a focus–exposure matrix and compare the measured depth of focus with the 44.6 nm-scale prediction; then measure best-focus differences across pitch and orientation to assess mask 3D shadowing.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field\"?","options":["以含 x 與 y 兩種方向線距的測試光罩曝光，確認晶圓上兩方向的 CD 與圖案位置一致，儘管光罩上的尺寸相差 2 倍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。"],"optionsEn":["Expose a test reticle with line-space patterns in both x and y and confirm that wafer CD and placement match in both orientations even though the mask features differ by 2×.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以含 x 與 y 兩種方向線距的測試光罩曝光，確認晶圓上兩方向的 CD 與圖案位置一致，儘管光罩上的尺寸相差 2 倍；量測場尺寸與兩個半場交界處的拼接套刻；做焦距—劑量矩陣，比較實測景深與 44.6 nm 等級的預測；再量不同節距與方向的最佳焦距差，評估光罩三維陰影效應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Expose a test reticle with line-space patterns in both x and y and confirm that wafer CD and placement match in both orientations even though the mask features differ by 2×; measure field dimensions and the stitching overlay where two half fields meet; run a focus–exposure matrix and compare the measured depth of focus with the 44.6 nm-scale prediction; then measure best-focus differences across pitch and orientation to assess mask 3D shadowing. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"asml-v12-04","title":"High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「0.55 NA 變形投影光學」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “0.55 NA anamorphic projection optics” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"超過 26 × 16.5 mm 的晶粒必須拆成兩個半場，交界處的套刻與 CD 不連續會讓跨越邊界的導線斷開或變細；若光罩資料的 y 方向縮放處理錯誤，整片圖案失真；光罩三維陰影造成與方向有關的影像位移，表現為無法用單一焦距修正的系統套刻。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A die larger than 26 × 16.5 mm must be split into two half fields, and overlay or CD discontinuity at the seam can open or neck lines that cross it; mishandled y scaling in the mask data distorts the whole pattern; mask 3D shadowing shifts images depending on orientation, showing up as systematic overlay that no single focus setting can correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：代價是標準 6 吋光罩的 104 × 132 mm 圖案區在晶圓上只剩 26 × 16.5 mm，即半場，每片晶圓曝光次數加倍，大晶粒需要拼接，光罩資料也必須在 y 方向拉長 2 倍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The price is that the 104 × 132 mm pattern area of a standard 6-inch mask covers only 26 × 16.5 mm on the wafer, a half field, so each wafer needs twice as many exposures, large dies must be stitched, and mask data are stretched 2× in y.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"超過 26 × 16.5 mm 的晶粒必須拆成兩個半場，交界處的套刻與 CD 不連續會讓跨越邊界的導線斷開或變細；若光罩資料的 y 方向縮放處理錯誤，整片圖案失真；光罩三維陰影造成與方向有關的影像位移，表現為無法用單一焦距修正的系統套刻。","textEn":"A die larger than 26 × 16.5 mm must be split into two half fields, and overlay or CD discontinuity at the seam can open or neck lines that cross it; mishandled y scaling in the mask data distorts the whole pattern; mask 3D shadowing shifts images depending on orientation, showing up as systematic overlay that no single focus setting can correct.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「High-NA 變形光學與半場曝光」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-NA anamorphic optics and the half field\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","超過 26 × 16.5 mm 的晶粒必須拆成兩個半場，交界處的套刻與 CD 不連續會讓跨越邊界的導線斷開或變細。","光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","A die larger than 26 × 16.5 mm must be split into two half fields, and overlay or CD discontinuity at the seam can open or neck lines that cross it.","Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"超過 26 × 16.5 mm 的晶粒必須拆成兩個半場，交界處的套刻與 CD 不連續會讓跨越邊界的導線斷開或變細；若光罩資料的 y 方向縮放處理錯誤，整片圖案失真；光罩三維陰影造成與方向有關的影像位移，表現為無法用單一焦距修正的系統套刻。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A die larger than 26 × 16.5 mm must be split into two half fields, and overlay or CD discontinuity at the seam can open or neck lines that cross it; mishandled y scaling in the mask data distorts the whole pattern; mask 3D shadowing shifts images depending on orientation, showing up as systematic overlay that no single focus setting can correct. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"asml-v12-05","title":"8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「光罩台與晶圓台同步」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"掃描曝光時光罩與晶圓反向運動，速度比等於掃描方向的縮小倍率：NXE 為 4，EXE 為 8。同樣的晶圓掃描速度下，EXE 的光罩台要跑 NXE 的兩倍快，而且曝光場數加倍，加減速時間必須更短；ASML 公開的數字是 EXE 光罩台 32 g（NXE 的四倍）、晶圓台 8 g。8× 倍率也有好處：光罩在掃描方向的位置誤差到晶圓上縮小 8 倍，垂直方向縮小 4 倍。代價是慣性力：真空中的光罩靠靜電夾盤的摩擦力固定，加速度越大越容易微滑，而光罩滑移會直接變成影像位移。同步誤差的移動平均（MA）與移動標準差（MSD）以晶圓座標、在狹縫曝光窗內計算。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「光罩台與晶圓台同步」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During a scan the reticle and wafer move in opposite directions with a speed ratio equal to the scan-direction reduction: 4 for NXE and 8 for EXE. For the same wafer scan speed the EXE reticle stage must run twice as fast as NXE's, and with twice as many fields the ramps must be shorter; ASML publishes 32 g for the EXE reticle stage, four times NXE, and 8 g for the wafer stage. The 8× ratio also helps: reticle position errors in the scan direction shrink 8× at the wafer and cross-scan errors 4×. The price is inertial force: in vacuum the reticle is held by friction on an electrostatic clamp, higher acceleration invites micro-slip, and any reticle slip becomes image displacement. Moving-average (MA) and moving-standard-deviation (MSD) synchronisation errors are computed in wafer coordinates over the slit exposure window. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：晶圓 0.4 m/s 時光罩 3.2 m/s；以 32 g（313.8 m/s²）加速需 10.2 ms、16.3 mm，同步加速段晶圓只需 32/8 = 4 g；若光罩台只有 8 g，則需 40.8 ms。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At a wafer speed of 0.4 m/s the reticle runs 3.2 m/s; at 32 g (313.8 m/s²) the ramp takes 10.2 ms and 16.3 mm, during which the wafer needs only 32/8 = 4 g, whereas an 8 g reticle stage would need 40.8 ms.","failure":"常見誤解：「光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「光罩台與晶圓台同步」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-05-k1","title":"8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學","titleEn":"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification","text":"掃描曝光時光罩與晶圓反向運動，速度比等於掃描方向的縮小倍率：NXE 為 4，EXE 為 8。同樣的晶圓掃描速度下，EXE 的光罩台要跑 NXE 的兩倍快，而且曝光場數加倍，加減速時間必須更短；ASML 公開的數字是 EXE 光罩台 32 g（NXE 的四倍）、晶圓台 8 g。","textEn":"During a scan the reticle and wafer move in opposite directions with a speed ratio equal to the scan-direction reduction: 4 for NXE and 8 for EXE. For the same wafer scan speed the EXE reticle stage must run twice as fast as NXE's, and with twice as many fields the ramps must be shorter; ASML publishes 32 g for the EXE reticle stage, four times NXE, and 8 g for the wafer stage.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification\" is correct?","options":["光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。","掃描曝光時光罩與晶圓反向運動，速度比等於掃描方向的縮小倍率：NXE 為 4，EXE 為 8。"],"optionsEn":["Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.","During a scan the reticle and wafer move in opposite directions with a speed ratio equal to the scan-direction reduction: 4 for NXE and 8 for EXE."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃描曝光時光罩與晶圓反向運動，速度比等於掃描方向的縮小倍率：NXE 為 4，EXE 為 8。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During a scan the reticle and wafer move in opposite directions with a speed ratio equal to the scan-direction reduction: 4 for NXE and 8 for EXE. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"asml-v12-06","title":"8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學：定量估算","titleEn":"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「光罩台與晶圓台同步」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：晶圓 0.4 m/s 時光罩 3.2 m/s；以 32 g（313.8 m/s²）加速需 10.2 ms、16.3 mm，同步加速段晶圓只需 32/8 = 4 g；若光罩台只有 8 g，則需 40.8 ms。光罩 152 × 152 × 6.35 mm、密度 2210 kg/m³，質量 0.324 kg，慣性力 0.324 × 313.8 ≈ 102 N；摩擦係數 0.25 時夾持正向力至少 407 N，安全係數 2 取 814 N；靜電壓力 ½ε₀E² 在 E ≈ 10⁸ V/m 時約 44 kPa，以 40 kPa 計需約 0.020 m² 夾持面積。光罩端 4 nm 的 MA 在晶圓掃描方向只剩 0.5 nm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At a wafer speed of 0.4 m/s the reticle runs 3.2 m/s; at 32 g (313.8 m/s²) the ramp takes 10.2 ms and 16.3 mm, during which the wafer needs only 32/8 = 4 g, whereas an 8 g reticle stage would need 40.8 ms. A 152 × 152 × 6.35 mm mask at 2210 kg/m³ weighs 0.324 kg, so the inertial force is 0.324 × 313.8 ≈ 102 N; with friction coefficient 0.25 the clamp normal force must be at least 407 N, 814 N with a safety factor of 2; electrostatic pressure ½ε₀E² is about 44 kPa at E ≈ 10⁸ V/m, so at 40 kPa about 0.020 m² of clamp area is needed. A 4 nm reticle MA becomes only 0.5 nm at the wafer in the scan direction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以載台編碼器在不同掃描速度與加速度下記錄同步誤差，計算 MA 與 MSD 並與預算比較；在大量加減速循環前後，以光罩對準感測器重複量測光罩基準標記位置，確認累積滑移低於允收值；同時記錄馬達電流與光罩台溫度，因為馬達發熱與力的平方成正比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record synchronisation error from stage encoders at several scan speeds and accelerations, compute MA and MSD and compare with the budget; measure reticle fiducial positions with the reticle alignment sensors before and after many acceleration cycles to confirm that accumulated slip stays below allowance; log motor current and reticle-stage temperature at the same time, because motor heating scales with the square of force.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"晶圓 0.4 m/s 時光罩 3.2 m/s；以 32 g（313.8 m/s²）加速需 10.2 ms、16.3 mm，同步加速段晶圓只需 32/8 = 4 g；若光罩台只有 8 g，則需 40.8 ms。光罩 152 × 152 × 6.35 mm、密度 2210 kg/m³，質量 0.324 kg，慣性力 0.324 × 313.8 ≈ 102 N；摩擦係數 0.25 時夾持正向力至少 407 N，安全係數 2 取 814 N；靜電壓力 ½ε₀E² 在 E ≈ 10⁸ V/m 時約 44 kPa，以 40 kPa 計需約 0.020 m² 夾持面積。光罩端 4 nm 的 MA 在晶圓掃描方向只剩 0.5 nm。","textEn":"At a wafer speed of 0.4 m/s the reticle runs 3.2 m/s; at 32 g (313.8 m/s²) the ramp takes 10.2 ms and 16.3 mm, during which the wafer needs only 32/8 = 4 g, whereas an 8 g reticle stage would need 40.8 ms. A 152 × 152 × 6.35 mm mask at 2210 kg/m³ weighs 0.324 kg, so the inertial force is 0.324 × 313.8 ≈ 102 N; with friction coefficient 0.25 the clamp normal force must be at least 407 N, 814 N with a safety factor of 2; electrostatic pressure ½ε₀E² is about 44 kPa at E ≈ 10⁸ V/m, so at 40 kPa about 0.020 m² of clamp area is needed. A 4 nm reticle MA becomes only 0.5 nm at the wafer in the scan direction.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification\", which statement holds?","options":["晶圓 0.4 m/s 時光罩 3.2 m/s。","水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。","模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。"],"optionsEn":["At a wafer speed of 0.4 m/s the reticle runs 3.2 m/s.","The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack.","More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶圓 0.4 m/s 時光罩 3.2 m/s；以 32 g（313.8 m/s²）加速需 10.2 ms、16.3 mm，同步加速段晶圓只需 32/8 = 4 g；若光罩台只有 8 g，則需 40.8 ms。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At a wafer speed of 0.4 m/s the reticle runs 3.2 m/s; at 32 g (313.8 m/s²) the ramp takes 10.2 ms and 16.3 mm, during which the wafer needs only 32/8 = 4 g, whereas an 8 g reticle stage would need 40.8 ms. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"asml-v12-07","title":"8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「光罩台與晶圓台同步」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以載台編碼器在不同掃描速度與加速度下記錄同步誤差，計算 MA 與 MSD 並與預算比較；在大量加減速循環前後，以光罩對準感測器重複量測光罩基準標記位置，確認累積滑移低於允收值；同時記錄馬達電流與光罩台溫度，因為馬達發熱與力的平方成正比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record synchronisation error from stage encoders at several scan speeds and accelerations, compute MA and MSD and compare with the budget; measure reticle fiducial positions with the reticle alignment sensors before and after many acceleration cycles to confirm that accumulated slip stays below allowance; log motor current and reticle-stage temperature at the same time, because motor heating scales with the square of force. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：光罩每數千次掃描微滑零點幾奈米，累積成場內套刻漂移，晶圓間的對準無法完全抓到；夾盤凸點上的顆粒降低接觸面積與摩擦力，同時造成局部變形；32 g 下馬達發熱提高光罩台溫度，使量測框架漂移。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A reticle that slips a fraction of a nanometre every few thousand scans accumulates intra-field overlay drift that wafer-to-wafer alignment cannot fully capture; particles on clamp burls reduce contact area and friction while locally deforming the mask; motor heating at 32 g warms the reticle stage and drifts the metrology frame.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以載台編碼器在不同掃描速度與加速度下記錄同步誤差，計算 MA 與 MSD 並與預算比較；在大量加減速循環前後，以光罩對準感測器重複量測光罩基準標記位置，確認累積滑移低於允收值；同時記錄馬達電流與光罩台溫度，因為馬達發熱與力的平方成正比。","textEn":"Record synchronisation error from stage encoders at several scan speeds and accelerations, compute MA and MSD and compare with the budget; measure reticle fiducial positions with the reticle alignment sensors before and after many acceleration cycles to confirm that accumulated slip stays below allowance; log motor current and reticle-stage temperature at the same time, because motor heating scales with the square of force.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","以載台編碼器在不同掃描速度與加速度下記錄同步誤差，計算 MA 與 MSD 並與預算比較。","光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Record synchronisation error from stage encoders at several scan speeds and accelerations, compute MA and MSD and compare with the budget.","Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以載台編碼器在不同掃描速度與加速度下記錄同步誤差，計算 MA 與 MSD 並與預算比較；在大量加減速循環前後，以光罩對準感測器重複量測光罩基準標記位置，確認累積滑移低於允收值；同時記錄馬達電流與光罩台溫度，因為馬達發熱與力的平方成正比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record synchronisation error from stage encoders at several scan speeds and accelerations, compute MA and MSD and compare with the budget; measure reticle fiducial positions with the reticle alignment sensors before and after many acceleration cycles to confirm that accumulated slip stays below allowance; log motor current and reticle-stage temperature at the same time, because motor heating scales with the square of force. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"asml-v12-08","title":"8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「光罩台與晶圓台同步」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Reticle-stage and wafer-stage synchronisation” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"光罩每數千次掃描微滑零點幾奈米，累積成場內套刻漂移，晶圓間的對準無法完全抓到；夾盤凸點上的顆粒降低接觸面積與摩擦力，同時造成局部變形；32 g 下馬達發熱提高光罩台溫度，使量測框架漂移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A reticle that slips a fraction of a nanometre every few thousand scans accumulates intra-field overlay drift that wafer-to-wafer alignment cannot fully capture; particles on clamp burls reduce contact area and friction while locally deforming the mask; motor heating at 32 g warms the reticle stage and drifts the metrology frame. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：同步誤差的移動平均（MA）與移動標準差（MSD）以晶圓座標、在狹縫曝光窗內計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Moving-average (MA) and moving-standard-deviation (MSD) synchronisation errors are computed in wafer coordinates over the slit exposure window.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"光罩每數千次掃描微滑零點幾奈米，累積成場內套刻漂移，晶圓間的對準無法完全抓到；夾盤凸點上的顆粒降低接觸面積與摩擦力，同時造成局部變形；32 g 下馬達發熱提高光罩台溫度，使量測框架漂移。","textEn":"A reticle that slips a fraction of a nanometre every few thousand scans accumulates intra-field overlay drift that wafer-to-wafer alignment cannot fully capture; particles on clamp burls reduce contact area and friction while locally deforming the mask; motor heating at 32 g warms the reticle stage and drifts the metrology frame.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「8× 掃描倍率下的光罩台動力學」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reticle-stage dynamics under 8× scan magnification\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。","光罩每數千次掃描微滑零點幾奈米，累積成場內套刻漂移，晶圓間的對準無法完全抓到。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.","A reticle that slips a fraction of a nanometre every few thousand scans accumulates intra-field overlay drift that wafer-to-wafer alignment cannot fully capture."],"answer":2,"explanation":"光罩每數千次掃描微滑零點幾奈米，累積成場內套刻漂移，晶圓間的對準無法完全抓到；夾盤凸點上的顆粒降低接觸面積與摩擦力，同時造成局部變形；32 g 下馬達發熱提高光罩台溫度，使量測框架漂移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A reticle that slips a fraction of a nanometre every few thousand scans accumulates intra-field overlay drift that wafer-to-wafer alignment cannot fully capture; particles on clamp burls reduce contact area and friction while locally deforming the mask; motor heating at 32 g warms the reticle stage and drifts the metrology frame. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":9},{"id":"asml-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷」與「集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity\" and \"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"asml-v12-09","title":"EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “EUV pellicle and reticle front side” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"護膜是一張只有數十奈米厚的自撐薄膜，裝在光罩前方數毫米處；落在護膜上的顆粒嚴重離焦而不成像，但若直接落在光罩上，會在每個場的每顆晶粒重複印出。EUV 下薄膜本身會吸收，而且光線來回穿過兩次，所以單程穿透率 T 對產能的影響是 T²；吸收的功率在真空中只能靠輻射散熱，光源功率越高薄膜溫度可達數百 °C。ASML 公開的第一代護膜約 50 nm 厚、單程損失約 10%，後續的矽化物、碳奈米管等材料在穿透率、強度與熱穩定性之間取捨。數微米以上的顆粒仍不能留在護膜上，抽真空與破真空時的壓差也是薄膜破裂的風險。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A pellicle is a free-standing membrane only tens of nanometres thick mounted a few millimetres in front of the reticle; particles landing on it are far out of focus and do not print, whereas a particle on the mask itself repeats in every die of every field. In EUV the membrane absorbs and the light crosses it twice, so a single-pass transmission T costs throughput as T²; the absorbed power can leave only by radiation in vacuum, and at higher source powers the film reaches several hundred °C. ASML's published first-generation pellicle was about 50 nm thick with roughly 10% single-pass loss, and later silicide and carbon-nanotube materials trade transmission, strength and thermal stability. Particles larger than a few micrometres must still be kept off the film, and pressure differences during pump-down and venting are a rupture risk. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “EUV pellicle and reticle front side”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：T = 0.90 時雙程 0.81，曝光受限下產能損失 19%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With T = 0.90 the double pass is 0.81, a 19% throughput loss when exposure-limited.","failure":"常見誤解：「護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “EUV pellicle and reticle front side”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-09-k1","title":"EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷","titleEn":"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity","text":"護膜是一張只有數十奈米厚的自撐薄膜，裝在光罩前方數毫米處；落在護膜上的顆粒嚴重離焦而不成像，但若直接落在光罩上，會在每個場的每顆晶粒重複印出。EUV 下薄膜本身會吸收，而且光線來回穿過兩次，所以單程穿透率 T 對產能的影響是 T²；吸收的功率在真空中只能靠輻射散熱，光源功率越高薄膜溫度可達數百 °C。","textEn":"A pellicle is a free-standing membrane only tens of nanometres thick mounted a few millimetres in front of the reticle; particles landing on it are far out of focus and do not print, whereas a particle on the mask itself repeats in every die of every field. In EUV the membrane absorbs and the light crosses it twice, so a single-pass transmission T costs throughput as T²; the absorbed power can leave only by radiation in vacuum, and at higher source powers the film reaches several hundred °C.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity\" is correct?","options":["護膜是一張只有數十奈米厚的自撐薄膜，裝在光罩前方數毫米處；落在護膜上的顆粒嚴重離焦而不成像，但若直接落在光罩上，會在每個場的每顆晶粒重複印出。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。","集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["A pellicle is a free-standing membrane only tens of nanometres thick mounted a few millimetres in front of the reticle.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.","A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"護膜是一張只有數十奈米厚的自撐薄膜，裝在光罩前方數毫米處；落在護膜上的顆粒嚴重離焦而不成像，但若直接落在光罩上，會在每個場的每顆晶粒重複印出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A pellicle is a free-standing membrane only tens of nanometres thick mounted a few millimetres in front of the reticle; particles landing on it are far out of focus and do not print, whereas a particle on the mask itself repeats in every die of every field. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"asml-v12-10","title":"EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷：定量估算","titleEn":"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “EUV pellicle and reticle front side” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：T = 0.90 時雙程 0.81，曝光受限下產能損失 19%。熱負載：20 W EUV 照在 104 × 8 mm 狹縫區（8.32 cm²），第一程吸收 2.0 W，經光罩 0.65 反射後第二程吸收 1.17 W，共 3.17 W、3.8 kW/m²；雙面輻射 q = 2εσT⁴，ε = 0.3 時 T ≈ 578 K（305 °C），功率加倍升到約 415 °C。顆粒陰影：間距 2.5 mm、光罩端 NA 0.0825，模糊直徑 2h·NA ≈ 0.41 mm，10 µm 顆粒只遮掉 (10/412)² ≈ 6×10⁻⁴。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With T = 0.90 the double pass is 0.81, a 19% throughput loss when exposure-limited. Heat load: 20 W of EUV on a 104 × 8 mm slit area (8.32 cm²) deposits 2.0 W on the first pass and, after 0.65 mask reflectance, 1.17 W on the second, 3.17 W or 3.8 kW/m²; two-sided radiation q = 2εσT⁴ with ε = 0.3 gives T ≈ 578 K (305 °C), about 415 °C if power doubles. Particle shadow: at 2.5 mm standoff and mask-side NA 0.0825 the blur is 2h·NA ≈ 0.41 mm, so a 10 µm particle blocks only (10/412)² ≈ 6×10⁻⁴. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：安裝前以 13.5 nm 反射／穿透量測確認單程穿透率與均勻性；上機後比較有無護膜時晶圓端的劑量感測器讀值，並以紅外熱像追蹤曝光中的薄膜溫度；定期以散射式檢測檢查護膜顆粒，並在固定晶圓數後檢查光罩正面新增顆粒；最後以晶粒對晶粒比對找出重複性缺陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before mounting confirm single-pass transmission and uniformity by 13.5 nm reflectometry and transmission measurement; on the tool compare wafer-level dose-sensor readings with and without the pellicle and track film temperature during exposure by infrared imaging; inspect the pellicle for particles with scatter-based inspection and check the reticle front side for adders after fixed wafer counts; finally search for repeating defects by die-to-die comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"T = 0.90 時雙程 0.81，曝光受限下產能損失 19%。熱負載：20 W EUV 照在 104 × 8 mm 狹縫區（8.32 cm²），第一程吸收 2.0 W，經光罩 0.65 反射後第二程吸收 1.17 W，共 3.17 W、3.8 kW/m²；雙面輻射 q = 2εσT⁴，ε = 0.3 時 T ≈ 578 K（305 °C），功率加倍升到約 415 °C。顆粒陰影：間距 2.5 mm、光罩端 NA 0.0825，模糊直徑 2h·NA ≈ 0.41 mm，10 µm 顆粒只遮掉 (10/412)² ≈ 6×10⁻⁴。","textEn":"With T = 0.90 the double pass is 0.81, a 19% throughput loss when exposure-limited. Heat load: 20 W of EUV on a 104 × 8 mm slit area (8.32 cm²) deposits 2.0 W on the first pass and, after 0.65 mask reflectance, 1.17 W on the second, 3.17 W or 3.8 kW/m²; two-sided radiation q = 2εσT⁴ with ε = 0.3 gives T ≈ 578 K (305 °C), about 415 °C if power doubles. Particle shadow: at 2.5 mm standoff and mask-side NA 0.0825 the blur is 2h·NA ≈ 0.41 mm, so a 10 µm particle blocks only (10/412)² ≈ 6×10⁻⁴.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity\", which statement holds?","options":["晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。","T = 0.90 時雙程 0.81，曝光受限下產能損失 19%。","光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.","With T = 0.90 the double pass is 0.81, a 19% throughput loss when exposure-limited.","Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"T = 0.90 時雙程 0.81，曝光受限下產能損失 19%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With T = 0.90 the double pass is 0.81, a 19% throughput loss when exposure-limited. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"asml-v12-11","title":"EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷：量測與驗證","titleEn":"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “EUV pellicle and reticle front side” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"安裝前以 13.5 nm 反射／穿透量測確認單程穿透率與均勻性；上機後比較有無護膜時晶圓端的劑量感測器讀值，並以紅外熱像追蹤曝光中的薄膜溫度；定期以散射式檢測檢查護膜顆粒，並在固定晶圓數後檢查光罩正面新增顆粒；最後以晶粒對晶粒比對找出重複性缺陷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before mounting confirm single-pass transmission and uniformity by 13.5 nm reflectometry and transmission measurement; on the tool compare wafer-level dose-sensor readings with and without the pellicle and track film temperature during exposure by infrared imaging; inspect the pellicle for particles with scatter-based inspection and check the reticle front side for adders after fixed wafer counts; finally search for repeating defects by die-to-die comparison. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：高功率或抽氣壓差使薄膜破裂，碎片污染光罩與機台內部；長期加熱使薄膜起皺或氧化，穿透率緩慢下降，造成劑量漂移；沒有護膜時，一顆 100 nm 顆粒落在光罩上就會在每顆晶粒印出重複缺陷，直到被檢出前整批產品良率受損。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: High power or a pump-down pressure difference ruptures the film and its fragments contaminate the reticle and tool interior; prolonged heating wrinkles or oxidises the film so transmission slowly falls and dose drifts; without a pellicle a single 100 nm particle on the mask prints a repeating defect in every die, damaging the yield of whole lots until it is caught.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝前以 13.5 nm 反射／穿透量測確認單程穿透率與均勻性；上機後比較有無護膜時晶圓端的劑量感測器讀值，並以紅外熱像追蹤曝光中的薄膜溫度；定期以散射式檢測檢查護膜顆粒，並在固定晶圓數後檢查光罩正面新增顆粒；最後以晶粒對晶粒比對找出重複性缺陷。","textEn":"Before mounting confirm single-pass transmission and uniformity by 13.5 nm reflectometry and transmission measurement; on the tool compare wafer-level dose-sensor readings with and without the pellicle and track film temperature during exposure by infrared imaging; inspect the pellicle for particles with scatter-based inspection and check the reticle front side for adders after fixed wafer counts; finally search for repeating defects by die-to-die comparison.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","安裝前以 13.5 nm 反射／穿透量測確認單程穿透率與均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","Before mounting confirm single-pass transmission and uniformity by 13.5 nm reflectometry and transmission measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安裝前以 13.5 nm 反射／穿透量測確認單程穿透率與均勻性；上機後比較有無護膜時晶圓端的劑量感測器讀值，並以紅外熱像追蹤曝光中的薄膜溫度；定期以散射式檢測檢查護膜顆粒，並在固定晶圓數後檢查光罩正面新增顆粒；最後以晶粒對晶粒比對找出重複性缺陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before mounting confirm single-pass transmission and uniformity by 13.5 nm reflectometry and transmission measurement; on the tool compare wafer-level dose-sensor readings with and without the pellicle and track film temperature during exposure by infrared imaging; inspect the pellicle for particles with scatter-based inspection and check the reticle front side for adders after fixed wafer counts; finally search for repeating defects by die-to-die comparison. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"asml-v12-12","title":"EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷：失效診斷","titleEn":"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「EUV 護膜與光罩正面」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “EUV pellicle and reticle front side” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"高功率或抽氣壓差使薄膜破裂，碎片污染光罩與機台內部；長期加熱使薄膜起皺或氧化，穿透率緩慢下降，造成劑量漂移；沒有護膜時，一顆 100 nm 顆粒落在光罩上就會在每顆晶粒印出重複缺陷，直到被檢出前整批產品良率受損。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"High power or a pump-down pressure difference ruptures the film and its fragments contaminate the reticle and tool interior; prolonged heating wrinkles or oxidises the film so transmission slowly falls and dose drifts; without a pellicle a single 100 nm particle on the mask prints a repeating defect in every die, damaging the yield of whole lots until it is caught. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：數微米以上的顆粒仍不能留在護膜上，抽真空與破真空時的壓差也是薄膜破裂的風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Particles larger than a few micrometres must still be kept off the film, and pressure differences during pump-down and venting are a rupture risk.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高功率或抽氣壓差使薄膜破裂，碎片污染光罩與機台內部；長期加熱使薄膜起皺或氧化，穿透率緩慢下降，造成劑量漂移；沒有護膜時，一顆 100 nm 顆粒落在光罩上就會在每顆晶粒印出重複缺陷，直到被檢出前整批產品良率受損。","textEn":"High power or a pump-down pressure difference ruptures the film and its fragments contaminate the reticle and tool interior; prolonged heating wrinkles or oxidises the film so transmission slowly falls and dose drifts; without a pellicle a single 100 nm particle on the mask prints a repeating defect in every die, damaging the yield of whole lots until it is caught.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「EUV 護膜穿透率、熱負載與光罩缺陷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"EUV pellicle transmission, heat load and reticle defectivity\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高功率或抽氣壓差使薄膜破裂，碎片污染光罩與機台內部。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["High power or a pump-down pressure difference ruptures the film and its fragments contaminate the reticle and tool interior.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高功率或抽氣壓差使薄膜破裂，碎片污染光罩與機台內部；長期加熱使薄膜起皺或氧化，穿透率緩慢下降，造成劑量漂移；沒有護膜時，一顆 100 nm 顆粒落在光罩上就會在每顆晶粒印出重複缺陷，直到被檢出前整批產品良率受損。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High power or a pump-down pressure difference ruptures the film and its fragments contaminate the reticle and tool interior; prolonged heating wrinkles or oxidises the film so transmission slowly falls and dose drifts; without a pellicle a single 100 nm particle on the mask prints a repeating defect in every die, damaging the yield of whole lots until it is caught. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"asml-v12-13","title":"集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"集光鏡是一面大型橢球 Mo/Si 多層膜反射鏡，距錫電漿僅數百毫米，把電漿成像到中間焦點。每一發脈衝都噴出錫離子、中性原子與微小碎屑；約百帕的氫氣緩衝層讓離子減速，EUV 光子與電漿則產生氫自由基，把沉積的錫蝕刻成可揮發的 SnH₄，由氣流帶到真空泵。集光鏡反射率由沉積與蝕刻的平衡決定：SnH₄ 若在熱表面分解會把錫再沉積回去，氫滲入多層膜則可能起泡。壽命以每十億發（gigapulse）的相對反射率損失追蹤，光源以提高驅動雷射功率或掃描機延長曝光來維持劑量，最後排定更換。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The collector is a large ellipsoidal Mo/Si multilayer mirror only a few hundred millimetres from the tin plasma, imaging the plasma onto the intermediate focus. Every pulse throws out tin ions, neutral atoms and fine debris; a hydrogen buffer of order a hundred pascals slows the ions, while EUV photons and the plasma create hydrogen radicals that etch deposited tin into volatile SnH₄, which the gas flow carries to the pumps. Collector reflectance is set by the balance of deposition and etching: SnH₄ that decomposes on hot surfaces puts tin back, and hydrogen penetrating the multilayer can raise blisters. Lifetime is tracked as relative reflectance loss per gigapulse, the source holds dose by raising drive-laser power or the scanner by lengthening exposure, and a replacement is eventually scheduled. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：50 kHz 時 1 Gpulse = 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h，每天 4.32 Gpulse。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At 50 kHz one gigapulse is 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h, or 4.32 Gpulse per day.","failure":"常見誤解：「集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-13-k1","title":"集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔","titleEn":"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning","text":"集光鏡是一面大型橢球 Mo/Si 多層膜反射鏡，距錫電漿僅數百毫米，把電漿成像到中間焦點。每一發脈衝都噴出錫離子、中性原子與微小碎屑；約百帕的氫氣緩衝層讓離子減速，EUV 光子與電漿則產生氫自由基，把沉積的錫蝕刻成可揮發的 SnH₄，由氣流帶到真空泵。","textEn":"The collector is a large ellipsoidal Mo/Si multilayer mirror only a few hundred millimetres from the tin plasma, imaging the plasma onto the intermediate focus. Every pulse throws out tin ions, neutral atoms and fine debris; a hydrogen buffer of order a hundred pascals slows the ions, while EUV photons and the plasma create hydrogen radicals that etch deposited tin into volatile SnH₄, which the gas flow carries to the pumps.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning\" is correct?","options":["集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。","集光鏡是一面大型橢球 Mo/Si 多層膜反射鏡，距錫電漿僅數百毫米，把電漿成像到中間焦點。","水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。"],"optionsEn":["A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.","The collector is a large ellipsoidal Mo/Si multilayer mirror only a few hundred millimetres from the tin plasma, imaging the plasma onto the intermediate focus.","The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack."],"answer":1,"explanation":"集光鏡是一面大型橢球 Mo/Si 多層膜反射鏡，距錫電漿僅數百毫米，把電漿成像到中間焦點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The collector is a large ellipsoidal Mo/Si multilayer mirror only a few hundred millimetres from the tin plasma, imaging the plasma onto the intermediate focus. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"asml-v12-14","title":"集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔：定量估算","titleEn":"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：50 kHz 時 1 Gpulse = 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h，每天 4.32 Gpulse。教學假設衰減 0.04%/Gpulse，每天 0.17%；允許損失 15% 時可用 375 Gpulse，約 87 天。曝光受限時每小時晶圓數與反射率成正比，損失 15% 而不補償就少 15% 產能；若要維持產能，中間焦點功率需提高到 1/0.85 ≈ 1.18 倍。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At 50 kHz one gigapulse is 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h, or 4.32 Gpulse per day. With an assumed loss of 0.04% per Gpulse, reflectance falls 0.17% per day; a 15% allowance lasts 375 Gpulse, about 87 days. When exposure-limited, wafers per hour scale with reflectance, so an uncompensated 15% loss costs 15% throughput, and keeping throughput requires intermediate-focus power raised to 1/0.85 ≈ 1.18 times. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以光源內的能量感測器量中間焦點功率，除以驅動雷射能量得到轉換效率乘集光鏡反射率的趨勢，並與掃描機劑量感測器交叉比對；以中間焦點遠場影像看反射率的空間分佈，找出不均勻沉積；以殘氣分析追蹤 SnH₄ 與水氣分壓；把每 Gpulse 的衰減斜率記錄成維修預測的依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure intermediate-focus power with in-source energy sensors and divide by drive-laser energy to trend conversion efficiency times collector reflectance, cross-checking with the scanner dose sensor; use far-field images of the intermediate focus to map reflectance spatially and reveal uneven deposition; follow SnH₄ and water partial pressures by residual-gas analysis; log the per-gigapulse decay slope as the basis for maintenance forecasting.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"50 kHz 時 1 Gpulse = 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h，每天 4.32 Gpulse。教學假設衰減 0.04%/Gpulse，每天 0.17%；允許損失 15% 時可用 375 Gpulse，約 87 天。曝光受限時每小時晶圓數與反射率成正比，損失 15% 而不補償就少 15% 產能；若要維持產能，中間焦點功率需提高到 1/0.85 ≈ 1.18 倍。","textEn":"At 50 kHz one gigapulse is 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h, or 4.32 Gpulse per day. With an assumed loss of 0.04% per Gpulse, reflectance falls 0.17% per day; a 15% allowance lasts 375 Gpulse, about 87 days. When exposure-limited, wafers per hour scale with reflectance, so an uncompensated 15% loss costs 15% throughput, and keeping throughput requires intermediate-focus power raised to 1/0.85 ≈ 1.18 times.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning\", which statement holds?","options":["模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。","High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","50 kHz 時 1 Gpulse = 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h，每天 4.32 Gpulse。"],"optionsEn":["More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals.","High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","At 50 kHz one gigapulse is 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h, or 4.32 Gpulse per day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"50 kHz 時 1 Gpulse = 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h，每天 4.32 Gpulse。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At 50 kHz one gigapulse is 20 000 s ≈ 5.6 h, or 4.32 Gpulse per day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"asml-v12-15","title":"集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以光源內的能量感測器量中間焦點功率，除以驅動雷射能量得到轉換效率乘集光鏡反射率的趨勢，並與掃描機劑量感測器交叉比對；以中間焦點遠場影像看反射率的空間分佈，找出不均勻沉積；以殘氣分析追蹤 SnH₄ 與水氣分壓；把每 Gpulse 的衰減斜率記錄成維修預測的依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure intermediate-focus power with in-source energy sensors and divide by drive-laser energy to trend conversion efficiency times collector reflectance, cross-checking with the scanner dose sensor; use far-field images of the intermediate focus to map reflectance spatially and reveal uneven deposition; follow SnH₄ and water partial pressures by residual-gas analysis; log the per-gigapulse decay slope as the basis for maintenance forecasting. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：錫在集光鏡周邊再沉積，使光瞳填充不均，照明均勻度與成像隨之改變；覆蓋層因氫起泡造成不可逆的反射率損失；若只看劑量是否合格而不追蹤衰減斜率，某天會突然需要更換集光鏡，造成數天停機。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Tin redeposited around the collector periphery fills the pupil unevenly, changing illumination uniformity and imaging; hydrogen blistering of the cap causes irreversible reflectance loss; watching only whether dose passes, without trending the decay slope, leads to a sudden collector swap and days of downtime.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以光源內的能量感測器量中間焦點功率，除以驅動雷射能量得到轉換效率乘集光鏡反射率的趨勢，並與掃描機劑量感測器交叉比對；以中間焦點遠場影像看反射率的空間分佈，找出不均勻沉積；以殘氣分析追蹤 SnH₄ 與水氣分壓；把每 Gpulse 的衰減斜率記錄成維修預測的依據。","textEn":"Measure intermediate-focus power with in-source energy sensors and divide by drive-laser energy to trend conversion efficiency times collector reflectance, cross-checking with the scanner dose sensor; use far-field images of the intermediate focus to map reflectance spatially and reveal uneven deposition; follow SnH₄ and water partial pressures by residual-gas analysis; log the per-gigapulse decay slope as the basis for maintenance forecasting.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning\"?","options":["以光源內的能量感測器量中間焦點功率，除以驅動雷射能量得到轉換效率乘集光鏡反射率的趨勢，並與掃描機劑量感測器交叉比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Measure intermediate-focus power with in-source energy sensors and divide by drive-laser energy to trend conversion efficiency times collector reflectance, cross-checking with the scanner dose sensor.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以光源內的能量感測器量中間焦點功率，除以驅動雷射能量得到轉換效率乘集光鏡反射率的趨勢，並與掃描機劑量感測器交叉比對；以中間焦點遠場影像看反射率的空間分佈，找出不均勻沉積；以殘氣分析追蹤 SnH₄ 與水氣分壓；把每 Gpulse 的衰減斜率記錄成維修預測的依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure intermediate-focus power with in-source energy sensors and divide by drive-laser energy to trend conversion efficiency times collector reflectance, cross-checking with the scanner dose sensor; use far-field images of the intermediate focus to map reflectance spatially and reveal uneven deposition; follow SnH₄ and water partial pressures by residual-gas analysis; log the per-gigapulse decay slope as the basis for maintenance forecasting. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"asml-v12-16","title":"集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集光鏡與氫氣緩衝」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Collector mirror and hydrogen buffer” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"錫在集光鏡周邊再沉積，使光瞳填充不均，照明均勻度與成像隨之改變；覆蓋層因氫起泡造成不可逆的反射率損失；若只看劑量是否合格而不追蹤衰減斜率，某天會突然需要更換集光鏡，造成數天停機。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Tin redeposited around the collector periphery fills the pupil unevenly, changing illumination uniformity and imaging; hydrogen blistering of the cap causes irreversible reflectance loss; watching only whether dose passes, without trending the decay slope, leads to a sudden collector swap and days of downtime. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：壽命以每十億發（gigapulse）的相對反射率損失追蹤，光源以提高驅動雷射功率或掃描機延長曝光來維持劑量，最後排定更換。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lifetime is tracked as relative reflectance loss per gigapulse, the source holds dose by raising drive-laser power or the scanner by lengthening exposure, and a replacement is eventually scheduled.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錫在集光鏡周邊再沉積，使光瞳填充不均，照明均勻度與成像隨之改變；覆蓋層因氫起泡造成不可逆的反射率損失；若只看劑量是否合格而不追蹤衰減斜率，某天會突然需要更換集光鏡，造成數天停機。","textEn":"Tin redeposited around the collector periphery fills the pupil unevenly, changing illumination uniformity and imaging; hydrogen blistering of the cap causes irreversible reflectance loss; watching only whether dose passes, without trending the decay slope, leads to a sudden collector swap and days of downtime.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集光鏡壽命：錫沉積與氫自由基清潔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Collector lifetime: tin deposition and hydrogen-radical cleaning\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","錫在集光鏡周邊再沉積，使光瞳填充不均，照明均勻度與成像隨之改變。","水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Tin redeposited around the collector periphery fills the pupil unevenly, changing illumination uniformity and imaging.","The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack."],"answer":1,"explanation":"錫在集光鏡周邊再沉積，使光瞳填充不均，照明均勻度與成像隨之改變；覆蓋層因氫起泡造成不可逆的反射率損失；若只看劑量是否合格而不追蹤衰減斜率，某天會突然需要更換集光鏡，造成數天停機。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tin redeposited around the collector periphery fills the pupil unevenly, changing illumination uniformity and imaging; hydrogen blistering of the cap causes irreversible reflectance loss; watching only whether dose passes, without trending the decay slope, leads to a sudden collector swap and days of downtime. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":10},{"id":"asml-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「焦面與對準標記的量測物理」與「晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors\" and \"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"asml-v12-17","title":"焦面與對準標記的量測物理：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「水平感測器與對準感測器」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level sensor and alignment sensor” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"雙載台掃描機在量測側先量晶圓：水平感測器以掠射角把光柵圖樣投到晶圓上，反射像的橫移正比於高度，逐場繪出地形與晶圓不平度，曝光時載台沿此焦面追蹤。因為光從多層透明膜反射，量到的「表觀高度」與膜層結構有關，這種製程相依偏差要用氣壓式量規或選擇波長、偏振來校正。對準感測器量繞射光柵標記的位置：±1 階干涉的相位就是位置；化學機械研磨或蝕刻使標記不對稱時，誤差隨波長改變，因此用多波長量測並比較色間差異來偵測不對稱。0.55 NA 的景深只剩約 45 nm，焦距預算縮到數奈米。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「水平感測器與對準感測器」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"On the measure side of a dual-stage scanner the wafer is mapped first: the level sensor projects a grating pattern onto the wafer at grazing incidence, and the lateral shift of the reflected image is proportional to height, so each field's topography and wafer unflatness are mapped for the stage to follow during exposure. Because the light reflects from a stack of transparent films, the apparent height depends on the stack, and this process dependency is calibrated with an air gauge or by choice of wavelength and polarisation. The alignment sensor locates diffraction-grating marks, where the phase of the ±1-order interference is the position; marks made asymmetric by CMP or etch give wavelength-dependent errors, so multi-wavelength readings and colour-to-colour differences expose asymmetry. At 0.55 NA the depth of focus is only about 45 nm and the focus budget shrinks to a few nanometres. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Level sensor and alignment sensor”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：三角量測：入射角 θ 時反射光橫移 Δ = 2h·sinθ，θ = 80° 得 Δ ≈ 1.97h，1 nm 高度只移 1.97 nm，須靠大面積光柵平均才能解析次奈米。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Triangulation: at incidence θ the reflected beam shifts Δ = 2h·sinθ, so θ = 80° gives Δ ≈ 1.97h and 1 nm of height moves the beam only 1.97 nm, resolvable at sub-nanometre level only by averaging over a large grating.","failure":"常見誤解：「水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「水平感測器與對準感測器」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Level sensor and alignment sensor”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-17-k1","title":"焦面與對準標記的量測物理","titleEn":"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors","text":"雙載台掃描機在量測側先量晶圓：水平感測器以掠射角把光柵圖樣投到晶圓上，反射像的橫移正比於高度，逐場繪出地形與晶圓不平度，曝光時載台沿此焦面追蹤。因為光從多層透明膜反射，量到的「表觀高度」與膜層結構有關，這種製程相依偏差要用氣壓式量規或選擇波長、偏振來校正。","textEn":"On the measure side of a dual-stage scanner the wafer is mapped first: the level sensor projects a grating pattern onto the wafer at grazing incidence, and the lateral shift of the reflected image is proportional to height, so each field's topography and wafer unflatness are mapped for the stage to follow during exposure. Because the light reflects from a stack of transparent films, the apparent height depends on the stack, and this process dependency is calibrated with an air gauge or by choice of wavelength and polarisation.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焦面與對準標記的量測物理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors\" is correct?","options":["水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。","晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。","雙載台掃描機在量測側先量晶圓：水平感測器以掠射角把光柵圖樣投到晶圓上，反射像的橫移正比於高度，逐場繪出地形與晶圓不平度，曝光時載台沿此焦面追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack.","Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.","On the measure side of a dual-stage scanner the wafer is mapped first: the level sensor projects a grating pattern onto the wafer at grazing incidence, and the lateral shift of the reflected image is proportional to height, so each field's topography and wafer unflatness are mapped for the stage to follow during exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙載台掃描機在量測側先量晶圓：水平感測器以掠射角把光柵圖樣投到晶圓上，反射像的橫移正比於高度，逐場繪出地形與晶圓不平度，曝光時載台沿此焦面追蹤。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"On the measure side of a dual-stage scanner the wafer is mapped first: the level sensor projects a grating pattern onto the wafer at grazing incidence, and the lateral shift of the reflected image is proportional to height, so each field's topography and wafer unflatness are mapped for the stage to follow during exposure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"asml-v12-18","title":"焦面與對準標記的量測物理：定量估算","titleEn":"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水平感測器與對準感測器」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level sensor and alignment sensor” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：三角量測：入射角 θ 時反射光橫移 Δ = 2h·sinθ，θ = 80° 得 Δ ≈ 1.97h，1 nm 高度只移 1.97 nm，須靠大面積光柵平均才能解析次奈米。景深 λ/NA²：0.33 NA 為 124 nm、0.55 NA 為 44.6 nm。對準：±1 階干涉 x = P·φ/(4π)，P = 1.6 µm 時 10 mrad 相位雜訊為 1.27 nm；標記不對稱額外造成 0.02 rad 相位，位置誤差 2.5 nm，與整個產品套刻預算同級。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Triangulation: at incidence θ the reflected beam shifts Δ = 2h·sinθ, so θ = 80° gives Δ ≈ 1.97h and 1 nm of height moves the beam only 1.97 nm, resolvable at sub-nanometre level only by averaging over a large grating. Depth of focus λ/NA² is 124 nm at 0.33 NA and 44.6 nm at 0.55 NA. Alignment: ±1-order interference gives x = P·φ/(4π), so with P = 1.6 µm a 10 mrad phase noise is 1.27 nm; mark asymmetry adding 0.02 rad of phase gives a 2.5 nm position error, the same size as the whole on-product overlay budget. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在不同膜層的產品晶圓上比較水平感測器與氣壓式量規讀值，建立每種膜層的製程修正；以焦距敏感標記或焦距—劑量矩陣量出實際最佳焦距圖，與水平感測器圖比較；對準方面，用多個波長量同一組標記，色間偏差超過門檻即標記為不對稱，再把預測套刻與曝光後套刻量測比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare level-sensor and air-gauge readings on product wafers with different stacks to build a process correction per stack; measure the true best-focus map with focus-sensitive targets or a focus–exposure matrix and compare with the level-sensor map; for alignment read the same marks at several wavelengths, flag marks whose colour-to-colour deviation exceeds a threshold as asymmetric, and compare predicted overlay with post-exposure overlay metrology.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"三角量測：入射角 θ 時反射光橫移 Δ = 2h·sinθ，θ = 80° 得 Δ ≈ 1.97h，1 nm 高度只移 1.97 nm，須靠大面積光柵平均才能解析次奈米。景深 λ/NA²：0.33 NA 為 124 nm、0.55 NA 為 44.6 nm。對準：±1 階干涉 x = P·φ/(4π)，P = 1.6 µm 時 10 mrad 相位雜訊為 1.27 nm；標記不對稱額外造成 0.02 rad 相位，位置誤差 2.5 nm，與整個產品套刻預算同級。","textEn":"Triangulation: at incidence θ the reflected beam shifts Δ = 2h·sinθ, so θ = 80° gives Δ ≈ 1.97h and 1 nm of height moves the beam only 1.97 nm, resolvable at sub-nanometre level only by averaging over a large grating. Depth of focus λ/NA² is 124 nm at 0.33 NA and 44.6 nm at 0.55 NA. Alignment: ±1-order interference gives x = P·φ/(4π), so with P = 1.6 µm a 10 mrad phase noise is 1.27 nm; mark asymmetry adding 0.02 rad of phase gives a 2.5 nm position error, the same size as the whole on-product overlay budget.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焦面與對準標記的量測物理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors\", which statement holds?","options":["三角量測：入射角 θ 時反射光橫移 Δ = 2h·sinθ，θ = 80° 得 Δ ≈ 1.97h，1 nm 高度只移 1.97 nm，須靠大面積光柵平均才能解析次奈米。","光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。","光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Triangulation: at incidence θ the reflected beam shifts Δ = 2h·sinθ, so θ = 80° gives Δ ≈ 1.97h and 1 nm of height moves the beam only 1.97 nm, resolvable at sub-nanometre level only by averaging over a large grating.","Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour.","Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"三角量測：入射角 θ 時反射光橫移 Δ = 2h·sinθ，θ = 80° 得 Δ ≈ 1.97h，1 nm 高度只移 1.97 nm，須靠大面積光柵平均才能解析次奈米。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Triangulation: at incidence θ the reflected beam shifts Δ = 2h·sinθ, so θ = 80° gives Δ ≈ 1.97h and 1 nm of height moves the beam only 1.97 nm, resolvable at sub-nanometre level only by averaging over a large grating. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"asml-v12-19","title":"焦面與對準標記的量測物理：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「水平感測器與對準感測器」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Level sensor and alignment sensor” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在不同膜層的產品晶圓上比較水平感測器與氣壓式量規讀值，建立每種膜層的製程修正；以焦距敏感標記或焦距—劑量矩陣量出實際最佳焦距圖，與水平感測器圖比較；對準方面，用多個波長量同一組標記，色間偏差超過門檻即標記為不對稱，再把預測套刻與曝光後套刻量測比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare level-sensor and air-gauge readings on product wafers with different stacks to build a process correction per stack; measure the true best-focus map with focus-sensitive targets or a focus–exposure matrix and compare with the level-sensor map; for alignment read the same marks at several wavelengths, flag marks whose colour-to-colour deviation exceeds a threshold as asymmetric, and compare predicted overlay with post-exposure overlay metrology. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：新膜層的製程相依偏差未校正，晶圓邊緣或特定區域焦距偏數十奈米，造成 CD 變異與缺陷；對準到不對稱的標記，整片晶圓帶有數奈米的系統偏移，看起來卻像隨機套刻雜訊。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: An uncalibrated process dependency on a new stack shifts focus by tens of nanometres at the wafer edge or in particular regions, causing CD variation and defects; aligning to asymmetric marks gives the whole wafer a systematic offset of a few nanometres that looks like random overlay noise.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同膜層的產品晶圓上比較水平感測器與氣壓式量規讀值，建立每種膜層的製程修正；以焦距敏感標記或焦距—劑量矩陣量出實際最佳焦距圖，與水平感測器圖比較；對準方面，用多個波長量同一組標記，色間偏差超過門檻即標記為不對稱，再把預測套刻與曝光後套刻量測比對。","textEn":"Compare level-sensor and air-gauge readings on product wafers with different stacks to build a process correction per stack; measure the true best-focus map with focus-sensitive targets or a focus–exposure matrix and compare with the level-sensor map; for alignment read the same marks at several wavelengths, flag marks whose colour-to-colour deviation exceeds a threshold as asymmetric, and compare predicted overlay with post-exposure overlay metrology.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焦面與對準標記的量測物理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在不同膜層的產品晶圓上比較水平感測器與氣壓式量規讀值，建立每種膜層的製程修正。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare level-sensor and air-gauge readings on product wafers with different stacks to build a process correction per stack.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在不同膜層的產品晶圓上比較水平感測器與氣壓式量規讀值，建立每種膜層的製程修正；以焦距敏感標記或焦距—劑量矩陣量出實際最佳焦距圖，與水平感測器圖比較；對準方面，用多個波長量同一組標記，色間偏差超過門檻即標記為不對稱，再把預測套刻與曝光後套刻量測比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare level-sensor and air-gauge readings on product wafers with different stacks to build a process correction per stack; measure the true best-focus map with focus-sensitive targets or a focus–exposure matrix and compare with the level-sensor map; for alignment read the same marks at several wavelengths, flag marks whose colour-to-colour deviation exceeds a threshold as asymmetric, and compare predicted overlay with post-exposure overlay metrology. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"asml-v12-20","title":"焦面與對準標記的量測物理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水平感測器與對準感測器」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Level sensor and alignment sensor” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"新膜層的製程相依偏差未校正，晶圓邊緣或特定區域焦距偏數十奈米，造成 CD 變異與缺陷；對準到不對稱的標記，整片晶圓帶有數奈米的系統偏移，看起來卻像隨機套刻雜訊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"An uncalibrated process dependency on a new stack shifts focus by tens of nanometres at the wafer edge or in particular regions, causing CD variation and defects; aligning to asymmetric marks gives the whole wafer a systematic offset of a few nanometres that looks like random overlay noise. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：0.55 NA 的景深只剩約 45 nm，焦距預算縮到數奈米。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At 0.55 NA the depth of focus is only about 45 nm and the focus budget shrinks to a few nanometres.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新膜層的製程相依偏差未校正，晶圓邊緣或特定區域焦距偏數十奈米，造成 CD 變異與缺陷；對準到不對稱的標記，整片晶圓帶有數奈米的系統偏移，看起來卻像隨機套刻雜訊。","textEn":"An uncalibrated process dependency on a new stack shifts focus by tens of nanometres at the wafer edge or in particular regions, causing CD variation and defects; aligning to asymmetric marks gives the whole wafer a systematic offset of a few nanometres that looks like random overlay noise.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焦面與對準標記的量測物理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measurement physics of focus and alignment sensors\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。","新膜層的製程相依偏差未校正，晶圓邊緣或特定區域焦距偏數十奈米，造成 CD 變異與缺陷；對準到不對稱的標記，整片晶圓帶有數奈米的系統偏移，看起來卻像隨機套刻雜訊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.","An uncalibrated process dependency on a new stack shifts focus by tens of nanometres at the wafer edge or in particular regions, causing CD variation and defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新膜層的製程相依偏差未校正，晶圓邊緣或特定區域焦距偏數十奈米，造成 CD 變異與缺陷；對準到不對稱的標記，整片晶圓帶有數奈米的系統偏移，看起來卻像隨機套刻雜訊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An uncalibrated process dependency on a new stack shifts focus by tens of nanometres at the wafer edge or in particular regions, causing CD variation and defects; aligning to asymmetric marks gives the whole wafer a systematic offset of a few nanometres that looks like random overlay noise. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"asml-v12-21","title":"晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"EUV 晶圓在真空中由靜電夾盤固定，夾盤表面是數千個微小凸點，以減少接觸面積、降低顆粒造成的局部變形，熱量經由凸點與背面氣體傳到台面。每次曝光把劑量能量與吸收的帶外紅外線留在該場，局部升溫使晶圓想要膨脹；凸點的摩擦力先抵抗，當剪力超過摩擦力時晶圓局部滑移，形成與曝光順序有關的場間變形。晶圓上機前的溫度必須與台面差在毫開爾文等級，台面以水循環控溫，並以前饋的晶圓加熱模型預測每場膨脹、調整倍率與平移。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An EUV wafer is held in vacuum by an electrostatic clamp whose surface consists of thousands of small burls, reducing contact area and particle-induced deformation, and heat leaves through the burls and backside gas into the table. Each exposure leaves its dose energy plus absorbed out-of-band infrared in that field, and the local temperature rise makes the wafer want to expand; burl friction resists at first, but once shear exceeds friction the wafer slips locally, producing field-to-field distortion that depends on exposure order. The wafer must arrive within millikelvins of the table temperature, the table is water-conditioned, and a feedforward wafer-heating model predicts expansion per field to adjust magnification and translation. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：50 mJ/cm² 乘半場 26 × 16.5 mm 得每場 0.2145 J；若絕熱地留在場下方 775 µm 厚的矽（2330 kg/m³、c = 700 J/kg·K，質量 0.775 g），ΔT ≈ 0.40 K；自由膨脹在 26 mm 上為 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm，是套刻預算的十倍，凸點夾持與熱傳導必須壓掉九成以上。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: 50 mJ/cm² over a 26 × 16.5 mm half field is 0.2145 J per field; held adiabatically in the 775 µm of silicon under the field (2330 kg/m³, c = 700 J/kg·K, mass 0.775 g) it gives ΔT ≈ 0.40 K, and free expansion across 26 mm is 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm, ten times the overlay budget, so burl clamping and conduction must suppress more than 90%.","failure":"常見誤解：「晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-21-k1","title":"晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控","titleEn":"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control","text":"EUV 晶圓在真空中由靜電夾盤固定，夾盤表面是數千個微小凸點，以減少接觸面積、降低顆粒造成的局部變形，熱量經由凸點與背面氣體傳到台面。每次曝光把劑量能量與吸收的帶外紅外線留在該場，局部升溫使晶圓想要膨脹；凸點的摩擦力先抵抗，當剪力超過摩擦力時晶圓局部滑移，形成與曝光順序有關的場間變形。","textEn":"An EUV wafer is held in vacuum by an electrostatic clamp whose surface consists of thousands of small burls, reducing contact area and particle-induced deformation, and heat leaves through the burls and backside gas into the table. Each exposure leaves its dose energy plus absorbed out-of-band infrared in that field, and the local temperature rise makes the wafer want to expand; burl friction resists at first, but once shear exceeds friction the wafer slips locally, producing field-to-field distortion that depends on exposure order.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control\" is correct?","options":["EUV 晶圓在真空中由靜電夾盤固定，夾盤表面是數千個微小凸點，以減少接觸面積、降低顆粒造成的局部變形，熱量經由凸點與背面氣體傳到台面。","晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。","模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。"],"optionsEn":["An EUV wafer is held in vacuum by an electrostatic clamp whose surface consists of thousands of small burls, reducing contact area and particle-induced deformation, and heat leaves through the burls and backside gas into the table.","Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.","More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"EUV 晶圓在真空中由靜電夾盤固定，夾盤表面是數千個微小凸點，以減少接觸面積、降低顆粒造成的局部變形，熱量經由凸點與背面氣體傳到台面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An EUV wafer is held in vacuum by an electrostatic clamp whose surface consists of thousands of small burls, reducing contact area and particle-induced deformation, and heat leaves through the burls and backside gas into the table. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"asml-v12-22","title":"晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控：定量估算","titleEn":"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：50 mJ/cm² 乘半場 26 × 16.5 mm 得每場 0.2145 J；若絕熱地留在場下方 775 µm 厚的矽（2330 kg/m³、c = 700 J/kg·K，質量 0.775 g），ΔT ≈ 0.40 K；自由膨脹在 26 mm 上為 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm，是套刻預算的十倍，凸點夾持與熱傳導必須壓掉九成以上。晶圓上機溫差 10 mK 時，半徑 150 mm 處膨脹 150 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.01 K = 3.9 nm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: 50 mJ/cm² over a 26 × 16.5 mm half field is 0.2145 J per field; held adiabatically in the 775 µm of silicon under the field (2330 kg/m³, c = 700 J/kg·K, mass 0.775 g) it gives ΔT ≈ 0.40 K, and free expansion across 26 mm is 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm, ten times the overlay budget, so burl clamping and conduction must suppress more than 90%. A 10 mK loading offset expands the wafer at 150 mm radius by 150 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.01 K = 3.9 nm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以高劑量與低劑量曝光同一佈局，量出與曝光順序相關的套刻圖，與晶圓加熱模型的預測比較；以台面溫度感測器追蹤每片晶圓的升溫曲線；夾持前後各量一次晶圓形狀與對準標記，分離夾持變形；定期量夾盤平坦度圖，檢查凸點磨耗或污染。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Expose the same layout at high and low dose, measure the overlay pattern correlated with exposure order and compare it with the wafer-heating model; follow each wafer's temperature rise with table sensors; measure wafer shape and alignment marks before and after clamping to separate clamp-induced distortion; map clamp flatness periodically to check for burl wear or contamination.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"50 mJ/cm² 乘半場 26 × 16.5 mm 得每場 0.2145 J；若絕熱地留在場下方 775 µm 厚的矽（2330 kg/m³、c = 700 J/kg·K，質量 0.775 g），ΔT ≈ 0.40 K；自由膨脹在 26 mm 上為 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm，是套刻預算的十倍，凸點夾持與熱傳導必須壓掉九成以上。晶圓上機溫差 10 mK 時，半徑 150 mm 處膨脹 150 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.01 K = 3.9 nm。","textEn":"50 mJ/cm² over a 26 × 16.5 mm half field is 0.2145 J per field; held adiabatically in the 775 µm of silicon under the field (2330 kg/m³, c = 700 J/kg·K, mass 0.775 g) it gives ΔT ≈ 0.40 K, and free expansion across 26 mm is 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm, ten times the overlay budget, so burl clamping and conduction must suppress more than 90%. A 10 mK loading offset expands the wafer at 150 mm radius by 150 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.01 K = 3.9 nm.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control\", which statement holds?","options":["High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","50 mJ/cm² 乘半場 26 × 16.5 mm 得每場 0.2145 J。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","50 mJ/cm² over a 26 × 16.5 mm half field is 0.2145 J per field.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput."],"answer":1,"explanation":"50 mJ/cm² 乘半場 26 × 16.5 mm 得每場 0.2145 J；若絕熱地留在場下方 775 µm 厚的矽（2330 kg/m³、c = 700 J/kg·K，質量 0.775 g），ΔT ≈ 0.40 K；自由膨脹在 26 mm 上為 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm，是套刻預算的十倍，凸點夾持與熱傳導必須壓掉九成以上。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"50 mJ/cm² over a 26 × 16.5 mm half field is 0.2145 J per field; held adiabatically in the 775 µm of silicon under the field (2330 kg/m³, c = 700 J/kg·K, mass 0.775 g) it gives ΔT ≈ 0.40 K, and free expansion across 26 mm is 26 mm × 2.6 ppm/K × 0.40 K ≈ 27 nm, ten times the overlay budget, so burl clamping and conduction must suppress more than 90%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"asml-v12-23","title":"晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以高劑量與低劑量曝光同一佈局，量出與曝光順序相關的套刻圖，與晶圓加熱模型的預測比較；以台面溫度感測器追蹤每片晶圓的升溫曲線；夾持前後各量一次晶圓形狀與對準標記，分離夾持變形；定期量夾盤平坦度圖，檢查凸點磨耗或污染。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Expose the same layout at high and low dose, measure the overlay pattern correlated with exposure order and compare it with the wafer-heating model; follow each wafer's temperature rise with table sensors; measure wafer shape and alignment marks before and after clamping to separate clamp-induced distortion; map clamp flatness periodically to check for burl wear or contamination. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：凸點磨耗或沾上顆粒，局部高度突起造成焦距熱點，摩擦力也改變，使晶圓加熱模型失效，晶圓邊緣套刻變差；高翹曲晶圓（例如多層堆疊記憶體）無法完全吸平，夾持本身就引入數奈米變形。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Worn or particle-contaminated burls create local height bumps that become focus hot spots and change friction so the wafer-heating model no longer holds and edge overlay degrades; highly warped wafers such as deep-stack memory cannot be fully flattened, so clamping itself introduces nanometres of distortion.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以高劑量與低劑量曝光同一佈局，量出與曝光順序相關的套刻圖，與晶圓加熱模型的預測比較；以台面溫度感測器追蹤每片晶圓的升溫曲線；夾持前後各量一次晶圓形狀與對準標記，分離夾持變形；定期量夾盤平坦度圖，檢查凸點磨耗或污染。","textEn":"Expose the same layout at high and low dose, measure the overlay pattern correlated with exposure order and compare it with the wafer-heating model; follow each wafer's temperature rise with table sensors; measure wafer shape and alignment marks before and after clamping to separate clamp-induced distortion; map clamp flatness periodically to check for burl wear or contamination.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。","以高劑量與低劑量曝光同一佈局，量出與曝光順序相關的套刻圖，與晶圓加熱模型的預測比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.","Expose the same layout at high and low dose, measure the overlay pattern correlated with exposure order and compare it with the wafer-heating model."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以高劑量與低劑量曝光同一佈局，量出與曝光順序相關的套刻圖，與晶圓加熱模型的預測比較；以台面溫度感測器追蹤每片晶圓的升溫曲線；夾持前後各量一次晶圓形狀與對準標記，分離夾持變形；定期量夾盤平坦度圖，檢查凸點磨耗或污染。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Expose the same layout at high and low dose, measure the overlay pattern correlated with exposure order and compare it with the wafer-heating model; follow each wafer's temperature rise with table sensors; measure wafer shape and alignment marks before and after clamping to separate clamp-induced distortion; map clamp flatness periodically to check for burl wear or contamination. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"asml-v12-24","title":"晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「晶圓夾盤、凸點與溫控」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Wafer clamp, burls and thermal conditioning” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"凸點磨耗或沾上顆粒，局部高度突起造成焦距熱點，摩擦力也改變，使晶圓加熱模型失效，晶圓邊緣套刻變差；高翹曲晶圓（例如多層堆疊記憶體）無法完全吸平，夾持本身就引入數奈米變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Worn or particle-contaminated burls create local height bumps that become focus hot spots and change friction so the wafer-heating model no longer holds and edge overlay degrades; highly warped wafers such as deep-stack memory cannot be fully flattened, so clamping itself introduces nanometres of distortion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：晶圓上機前的溫度必須與台面差在毫開爾文等級，台面以水循環控溫，並以前饋的晶圓加熱模型預測每場膨脹、調整倍率與平移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The wafer must arrive within millikelvins of the table temperature, the table is water-conditioned, and a feedforward wafer-heating model predicts expansion per field to adjust magnification and translation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"凸點磨耗或沾上顆粒，局部高度突起造成焦距熱點，摩擦力也改變，使晶圓加熱模型失效，晶圓邊緣套刻變差；高翹曲晶圓（例如多層堆疊記憶體）無法完全吸平，夾持本身就引入數奈米變形。","textEn":"Worn or particle-contaminated burls create local height bumps that become focus hot spots and change friction so the wafer-heating model no longer holds and edge overlay degrades; highly warped wafers such as deep-stack memory cannot be fully flattened, so clamping itself introduces nanometres of distortion.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶圓加熱、夾持與晶圓台熱控」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wafer heating, clamping and wafer-table thermal control\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["凸點磨耗或沾上顆粒，局部高度突起造成焦距熱點，摩擦力也改變，使晶圓加熱模型失效，晶圓邊緣套刻變差。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。"],"optionsEn":["Worn or particle-contaminated burls create local height bumps that become focus hot spots and change friction so the wafer-heating model no longer holds and edge overlay degrades.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"凸點磨耗或沾上顆粒，局部高度突起造成焦距熱點，摩擦力也改變，使晶圓加熱模型失效，晶圓邊緣套刻變差；高翹曲晶圓（例如多層堆疊記憶體）無法完全吸平，夾持本身就引入數奈米變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Worn or particle-contaminated burls create local height bumps that become focus hot spots and change friction so the wafer-heating model no longer holds and edge overlay degrades; highly warped wafers such as deep-stack memory cannot be fully flattened, so clamping itself introduces nanometres of distortion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":11},{"id":"asml-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正」與「每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure\" and \"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"asml-v12-25","title":"場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「套刻量測與逐場修正」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"套刻誤差可拆成：晶圓層級（場間）的平移、旋轉、倍率與非正交（六參數線性模型）及高階多項式；場內的倍率、旋轉與非對稱項（十參數模型）以及鏡頭與光罩特徵；還有無法修正的隨機殘差。以繞射式套刻標記量測後，先進製程控制把修正量回饋給掃描機致動器：載台負責平移與旋轉，鏡頭與光罩台負責倍率；逐曝光修正（CPE）讓每一場都有自己的一組小修正。參數越多能吃掉越多系統特徵，但也會把量測雜訊擬合進去，參數數與取樣點數共同決定雜訊放大。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「套刻量測與逐場修正」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Overlay error splits into wafer-level (inter-field) translation, rotation, magnification and non-orthogonality, the six-parameter linear model, plus higher-order polynomials; intra-field magnification, rotation and asymmetric terms, the ten-parameter model, plus lens and reticle signatures; and a non-correctable random residual. After measurement on diffraction-based overlay targets, advanced process control feeds corrections to scanner actuators: the stage handles translation and rotation and the lens and reticle stage handle magnification, while corrections per exposure (CPE) give every field its own small set. More parameters absorb more systematic signature but also fit measurement noise, and the parameter count together with sampling density sets noise amplification. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學分解（3σ）：晶圓線性 2.5 nm、晶圓高階 1.8 nm、場內 1.5 nm、隨機 1.2 nm，總計 √13.18 = 3.63 nm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching decomposition (3σ): wafer linear 2.5 nm, wafer higher-order 1.8 nm, intra-field 1.5 nm and random 1.2 nm, total √13.18 = 3.63 nm.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「套刻量測與逐場修正」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-25-k1","title":"場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正","titleEn":"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure","text":"套刻誤差可拆成：晶圓層級（場間）的平移、旋轉、倍率與非正交（六參數線性模型）及高階多項式；場內的倍率、旋轉與非對稱項（十參數模型）以及鏡頭與光罩特徵；還有無法修正的隨機殘差。以繞射式套刻標記量測後，先進製程控制把修正量回饋給掃描機致動器：載台負責平移與旋轉，鏡頭與光罩台負責倍率；逐曝光修正（CPE）讓每一場都有自己的一組小修正。","textEn":"Overlay error splits into wafer-level (inter-field) translation, rotation, magnification and non-orthogonality, the six-parameter linear model, plus higher-order polynomials; intra-field magnification, rotation and asymmetric terms, the ten-parameter model, plus lens and reticle signatures; and a non-correctable random residual. After measurement on diffraction-based overlay targets, advanced process control feeds corrections to scanner actuators: the stage handles translation and rotation and the lens and reticle stage handle magnification, while corrections per exposure (CPE) give every field its own small set.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure\" is correct?","options":["模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。","套刻誤差可拆成：晶圓層級（場間）的平移、旋轉、倍率與非正交（六參數線性模型）及高階多項式。","光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。"],"optionsEn":["More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals.","Overlay error splits into wafer-level (inter-field) translation, rotation, magnification and non-orthogonality, the six-parameter linear model, plus higher-order polynomials.","Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"套刻誤差可拆成：晶圓層級（場間）的平移、旋轉、倍率與非正交（六參數線性模型）及高階多項式；場內的倍率、旋轉與非對稱項（十參數模型）以及鏡頭與光罩特徵；還有無法修正的隨機殘差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Overlay error splits into wafer-level (inter-field) translation, rotation, magnification and non-orthogonality, the six-parameter linear model, plus higher-order polynomials; intra-field magnification, rotation and asymmetric terms, the ten-parameter model, plus lens and reticle signatures; and a non-correctable random residual. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"asml-v12-26","title":"場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「套刻量測與逐場修正」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學分解（3σ）：晶圓線性 2.5 nm、晶圓高階 1.8 nm、場內 1.5 nm、隨機 1.2 nm，總計 √13.18 = 3.63 nm。去除線性後 2.63 nm；CPE 吃掉高階與場內 80% 變異後為 √(0.2×1.8² + 0.2×1.5² + 1.2²) = 1.59 nm。雜訊代價：量測雜訊 0.3 nm、p = 300 參數、n = 600 點時加入約 0.3·√(p/n) = 0.21 nm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching decomposition (3σ): wafer linear 2.5 nm, wafer higher-order 1.8 nm, intra-field 1.5 nm and random 1.2 nm, total √13.18 = 3.63 nm. Removing the linear part leaves 2.63 nm; CPE capturing 80% of higher-order and intra-field variance leaves √(0.2×1.8² + 0.2×1.5² + 1.2²) = 1.59 nm. Noise cost: with 0.3 nm measurement noise, p = 300 parameters and n = 600 points, about 0.3·√(p/n) = 0.21 nm is added. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在監控晶圓上做高密度套刻取樣，以保留點交叉驗證選擇模型階數，確認殘差接近量測雜訊而非更低；把修正量套用到下一批後再量，比較預測與實際；並定期量測多台掃描機之間的匹配套刻，確認修正在機台間可轉移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample overlay densely on monitor wafers and choose model order by cross-validation on held-out points, confirming that residuals approach measurement noise rather than fall below it; apply the corrections to the next lot, re-measure and compare prediction with result; measure matched-machine overlay between scanners periodically to confirm that corrections transfer across tools.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學分解（3σ）：晶圓線性 2.5 nm、晶圓高階 1.8 nm、場內 1.5 nm、隨機 1.2 nm，總計 √13.18 = 3.63 nm。去除線性後 2.63 nm；CPE 吃掉高階與場內 80% 變異後為 √(0.2×1.8² + 0.2×1.5² + 1.2²) = 1.59 nm。雜訊代價：量測雜訊 0.3 nm、p = 300 參數、n = 600 點時加入約 0.3·√(p/n) = 0.21 nm。","textEn":"Teaching decomposition (3σ): wafer linear 2.5 nm, wafer higher-order 1.8 nm, intra-field 1.5 nm and random 1.2 nm, total √13.18 = 3.63 nm. Removing the linear part leaves 2.63 nm; CPE capturing 80% of higher-order and intra-field variance leaves √(0.2×1.8² + 0.2×1.5² + 1.2²) = 1.59 nm. Noise cost: with 0.3 nm measurement noise, p = 300 parameters and n = 600 points, about 0.3·√(p/n) = 0.21 nm is added.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure\", which statement holds?","options":["光罩誤差到晶圓會縮小 8 倍，所以光罩台的動態要求可以放寬。","集光鏡反射率慢慢下降只影響光源亮度，不影響每小時晶圓數。","教學分解（3σ）：晶圓線性 2.5 nm、晶圓高階 1.8 nm、場內 1.5 nm、隨機 1.2 nm，總計 √13.18 = 3.63 nm。"],"optionsEn":["Reticle errors shrink 8× at the wafer, so reticle-stage dynamics can be relaxed.","A slowly falling collector reflectance only dims the source and does not affect wafers per hour.","Teaching decomposition (3σ): wafer linear 2.5 nm, wafer higher-order 1.8 nm, intra-field 1.5 nm and random 1.2 nm, total √13.18 = 3.63 nm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學分解（3σ）：晶圓線性 2.5 nm、晶圓高階 1.8 nm、場內 1.5 nm、隨機 1.2 nm，總計 √13.18 = 3.63 nm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching decomposition (3σ): wafer linear 2.5 nm, wafer higher-order 1.8 nm, intra-field 1.5 nm and random 1.2 nm, total √13.18 = 3.63 nm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"asml-v12-27","title":"場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「套刻量測與逐場修正」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在監控晶圓上做高密度套刻取樣，以保留點交叉驗證選擇模型階數，確認殘差接近量測雜訊而非更低；把修正量套用到下一批後再量，比較預測與實際；並定期量測多台掃描機之間的匹配套刻，確認修正在機台間可轉移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample overlay densely on monitor wafers and choose model order by cross-validation on held-out points, confirming that residuals approach measurement noise rather than fall below it; apply the corrections to the next lot, re-measure and compare prediction with result; measure matched-machine overlay between scanners periodically to confirm that corrections transfer across tools. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：以稀疏而吵雜的資料擬合 CPE，等於把雜訊寫回機台；製程路徑改變（例如換了蝕刻腔）後仍用舊修正，套刻反而變差；修正量超出致動器範圍被截斷；套刻標記與元件圖案的偏差未校正，量測合格但元件不合格。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Fitting CPE to sparse, noisy data writes noise back into the tool; keeping old corrections after the process route changes, such as a different etch chamber, makes overlay worse; corrections beyond actuator range are clipped; an uncalibrated target-to-device offset lets metrology pass while devices fail.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在監控晶圓上做高密度套刻取樣，以保留點交叉驗證選擇模型階數，確認殘差接近量測雜訊而非更低；把修正量套用到下一批後再量，比較預測與實際；並定期量測多台掃描機之間的匹配套刻，確認修正在機台間可轉移。","textEn":"Sample overlay densely on monitor wafers and choose model order by cross-validation on held-out points, confirming that residuals approach measurement noise rather than fall below it; apply the corrections to the next lot, re-measure and compare prediction with result; measure matched-machine overlay between scanners periodically to confirm that corrections transfer across tools.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure\"?","options":["在監控晶圓上做高密度套刻取樣，以保留點交叉驗證選擇模型階數，確認殘差接近量測雜訊而非更低。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。"],"optionsEn":["Sample overlay densely on monitor wafers and choose model order by cross-validation on held-out points, confirming that residuals approach measurement noise rather than fall below it.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在監控晶圓上做高密度套刻取樣，以保留點交叉驗證選擇模型階數，確認殘差接近量測雜訊而非更低；把修正量套用到下一批後再量，比較預測與實際；並定期量測多台掃描機之間的匹配套刻，確認修正在機台間可轉移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample overlay densely on monitor wafers and choose model order by cross-validation on held-out points, confirming that residuals approach measurement noise rather than fall below it; apply the corrections to the next lot, re-measure and compare prediction with result; measure matched-machine overlay between scanners periodically to confirm that corrections transfer across tools. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"asml-v12-28","title":"場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「套刻量測與逐場修正」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Overlay metrology and per-exposure corrections” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"以稀疏而吵雜的資料擬合 CPE，等於把雜訊寫回機台；製程路徑改變（例如換了蝕刻腔）後仍用舊修正，套刻反而變差；修正量超出致動器範圍被截斷；套刻標記與元件圖案的偏差未校正，量測合格但元件不合格。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Fitting CPE to sparse, noisy data writes noise back into the tool; keeping old corrections after the process route changes, such as a different etch chamber, makes overlay worse; corrections beyond actuator range are clipped; an uncalibrated target-to-device offset lets metrology pass while devices fail. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：參數越多能吃掉越多系統特徵，但也會把量測雜訊擬合進去，參數數與取樣點數共同決定雜訊放大。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: More parameters absorb more systematic signature but also fit measurement noise, and the parameter count together with sampling density sets noise amplification.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型參數越多，套刻殘差一定越小。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More model parameters always give smaller overlay residuals.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以稀疏而吵雜的資料擬合 CPE，等於把雜訊寫回機台；製程路徑改變（例如換了蝕刻腔）後仍用舊修正，套刻反而變差；修正量超出致動器範圍被截斷；套刻標記與元件圖案的偏差未校正，量測合格但元件不合格。","textEn":"Fitting CPE to sparse, noisy data writes noise back into the tool; keeping old corrections after the process route changes, such as a different etch chamber, makes overlay worse; corrections beyond actuator range are clipped; an uncalibrated target-to-device offset lets metrology pass while devices fail.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「場間套刻建模與逐曝光修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Field-to-field overlay modelling and corrections per exposure\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","以稀疏而吵雜的資料擬合 CPE，等於把雜訊寫回機台。","光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Fitting CPE to sparse, noisy data writes noise back into the tool.","Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以稀疏而吵雜的資料擬合 CPE，等於把雜訊寫回機台；製程路徑改變（例如換了蝕刻腔）後仍用舊修正，套刻反而變差；修正量超出致動器範圍被截斷；套刻標記與元件圖案的偏差未校正，量測合格但元件不合格。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fitting CPE to sparse, noisy data writes noise back into the tool; keeping old corrections after the process route changes, such as a different etch chamber, makes overlay worse; corrections beyond actuator range are clipped; an uncalibrated target-to-device offset lets metrology pass while devices fail. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"asml-v12-29","title":"每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「產能、可用度與交接」如何決定ASML 微影機系統工程的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Throughput, availability and handoff” determines the key performance of “ASML Lithography Systems Engineering”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"產能是在指定劑量與佈局下每小時能曝多少片晶圓。單片時間由三部分組成：曝光時間（晶圓端功率除以劑量決定）、每場的額外時間（加速、減速、穩定與步進）、以及雙載台無法隱藏的晶圓交換時間。產出量等於每小時晶圓數乘可用度與使用率；可用度受計畫保養（集光鏡、錫滴產生器更換）與非計畫停機（平均故障間隔與修復時間）限制。驗收時以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉，記錄每小時晶圓數、劑量穩定度、套刻、焦距與可用度，交接時附上光源功率趨勢、集光鏡反射率與護膜狀態。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「產能、可用度與交接」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Throughput is how many wafers per hour the tool exposes at a specified dose and layout. Wafer time has three parts: exposure time, set by wafer-level power divided by dose; per-field overhead for acceleration, deceleration, settling and stepping; and wafer exchange that the dual stage cannot hide. Output equals wafers per hour times availability and utilisation, and availability is limited by planned maintenance such as collector and droplet-generator swaps and by unplanned downtime governed by mean time between failures and mean time to repair. Acceptance runs the specified dose and layout continuously, logging wafers per hour, dose stability, overlay, focus and availability, and the handoff carries source-power trends, collector reflectance and pellicle status. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Throughput, availability and handoff”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：NXE 類教學：中間焦點 250 W、光學 1.5%、護膜 0.81，晶圓端 3.04 W；掃描速度 v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s；96 場 × 858 mm² = 824 cm²，30 mJ/cm² 需 24.7 J、曝光 8.13 s；每場額外 60 ms 共 5.76 s；晶圓額外 2.0 s；合計 15.9 s，約 226 片/小時。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: NXE-like teaching case: 250 W at intermediate focus, 1.5% optics and 0.81 pellicle give 3.04 W at the wafer; scan speed v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s; 96 fields × 858 mm² = 824 cm² needs 24.7 J at 30 mJ/cm², 8.13 s of exposure; 60 ms overhead per field adds 5.76 s and wafer overhead 2.0 s, totalling 15.9 s or about 226 wafers per hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「產能、可用度與交接」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Throughput, availability and handoff”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-29-k1","title":"每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收","titleEn":"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability","text":"產能是在指定劑量與佈局下每小時能曝多少片晶圓。單片時間由三部分組成：曝光時間（晶圓端功率除以劑量決定）、每場的額外時間（加速、減速、穩定與步進）、以及雙載台無法隱藏的晶圓交換時間。","textEn":"Throughput is how many wafers per hour the tool exposes at a specified dose and layout. Wafer time has three parts: exposure time, set by wafer-level power divided by dose; per-field overhead for acceleration, deceleration, settling and stepping; and wafer exchange that the dual stage cannot hide.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability\" is correct?","options":["光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。","High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","產能是在指定劑量與佈局下每小時能曝多少片晶圓。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour.","High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","Throughput is how many wafers per hour the tool exposes at a specified dose and layout."],"answer":2,"explanation":"產能是在指定劑量與佈局下每小時能曝多少片晶圓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Throughput is how many wafers per hour the tool exposes at a specified dose and layout. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"asml-v12-30","title":"每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收：定量估算","titleEn":"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「產能、可用度與交接」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Throughput, availability and handoff” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：NXE 類教學：中間焦點 250 W、光學 1.5%、護膜 0.81，晶圓端 3.04 W；掃描速度 v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s；96 場 × 858 mm² = 824 cm²，30 mJ/cm² 需 24.7 J、曝光 8.13 s；每場額外 60 ms 共 5.76 s；晶圓額外 2.0 s；合計 15.9 s，約 226 片/小時。可用度：每週計畫保養 6 h（3.6%）、MTBF 150 h 且 MTTR 5 h（3.2%），A = 93.2%，每天 226 × 24 × 0.932 ≈ 5055 片。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: NXE-like teaching case: 250 W at intermediate focus, 1.5% optics and 0.81 pellicle give 3.04 W at the wafer; scan speed v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s; 96 fields × 858 mm² = 824 cm² needs 24.7 J at 30 mJ/cm², 8.13 s of exposure; 60 ms overhead per field adds 5.76 s and wafer overhead 2.0 s, totalling 15.9 s or about 226 wafers per hour. Availability: 6 h weekly planned maintenance (3.6%) plus MTBF 150 h with MTTR 5 h (3.2%) gives A = 93.2%, or 226 × 24 × 0.932 ≈ 5055 wafers per day. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉至少 24 小時，從機台紀錄拆解每片晶圓的曝光、每場額外與晶圓交換時間，與模型逐項比較；依 SEMI E10 的設備狀態定義，以數週的事件紀錄計算可用度、MTBF 與 MTTR；同時統計每場劑量穩定度，確認產能不是以犧牲劑量控制換來的。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run the specified dose and layout continuously for at least 24 hours, break each wafer's time into exposure, per-field overhead and exchange from machine logs and compare item by item with the model; compute availability, MTBF and MTTR from weeks of event logs using SEMI E10 equipment-state definitions; tally per-field dose stability at the same time to confirm that throughput was not bought by loosening dose control.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"NXE 類教學：中間焦點 250 W、光學 1.5%、護膜 0.81，晶圓端 3.04 W；掃描速度 v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s；96 場 × 858 mm² = 824 cm²，30 mJ/cm² 需 24.7 J、曝光 8.13 s；每場額外 60 ms 共 5.76 s；晶圓額外 2.0 s；合計 15.9 s，約 226 片/小時。可用度：每週計畫保養 6 h（3.6%）、MTBF 150 h 且 MTTR 5 h（3.2%），A = 93.2%，每天 226 × 24 × 0.932 ≈ 5055 片。","textEn":"NXE-like teaching case: 250 W at intermediate focus, 1.5% optics and 0.81 pellicle give 3.04 W at the wafer; scan speed v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s; 96 fields × 858 mm² = 824 cm² needs 24.7 J at 30 mJ/cm², 8.13 s of exposure; 60 ms overhead per field adds 5.76 s and wafer overhead 2.0 s, totalling 15.9 s or about 226 wafers per hour. Availability: 6 h weekly planned maintenance (3.6%) plus MTBF 150 h with MTTR 5 h (3.2%) gives A = 93.2%, or 226 × 24 × 0.932 ≈ 5055 wafers per day.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability\", which statement holds?","options":["NXE 類教學：中間焦點 250 W、光學 1.5%、護膜 0.81，晶圓端 3.04 W。","護膜只是透明保護層，對產能沒有影響。","水平感測器量到的就是光阻表面真實高度，與下層膜無關。"],"optionsEn":["NXE-like teaching case: 250 W at intermediate focus, 1.5% optics and 0.81 pellicle give 3.04 W at the wafer.","A pellicle is just a transparent cover with no effect on throughput.","The level sensor reads the true resist height regardless of the underlying film stack."],"answer":0,"explanation":"NXE 類教學：中間焦點 250 W、光學 1.5%、護膜 0.81，晶圓端 3.04 W；掃描速度 v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s；96 場 × 858 mm² = 824 cm²，30 mJ/cm² 需 24.7 J、曝光 8.13 s；每場額外 60 ms 共 5.76 s；晶圓額外 2.0 s；合計 15.9 s，約 226 片/小時。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"NXE-like teaching case: 250 W at intermediate focus, 1.5% optics and 0.81 pellicle give 3.04 W at the wafer; scan speed v = P/(D·W) = 3.04/(300 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.39 m/s; 96 fields × 858 mm² = 824 cm² needs 24.7 J at 30 mJ/cm², 8.13 s of exposure; 60 ms overhead per field adds 5.76 s and wafer overhead 2.0 s, totalling 15.9 s or about 226 wafers per hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"asml-v12-31","title":"每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收：量測與驗證","titleEn":"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「產能、可用度與交接」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Throughput, availability and handoff” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉至少 24 小時，從機台紀錄拆解每片晶圓的曝光、每場額外與晶圓交換時間，與模型逐項比較；依 SEMI E10 的設備狀態定義，以數週的事件紀錄計算可用度、MTBF 與 MTTR；同時統計每場劑量穩定度，確認產能不是以犧牲劑量控制換來的。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run the specified dose and layout continuously for at least 24 hours, break each wafer's time into exposure, per-field overhead and exchange from machine logs and compare item by item with the model; compute availability, MTBF and MTTR from weeks of event logs using SEMI E10 equipment-state definitions; tally per-field dose stability at the same time to confirm that throughput was not bought by loosening dose control. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：規格產能是在參考佈局與劑量下量得，客戶佈局若有更多部分場或更高劑量，實際產能明顯較低；可用度宣稱若未計入排定的集光鏡更換，產線排程會在保養週失準；短時間的最佳紀錄被誤當成長期持續產能。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Specified throughput is measured at a reference layout and dose, so customer layouts with more partial fields or higher dose run noticeably slower; availability claims that leave out scheduled collector swaps derail fab scheduling in maintenance weeks; a short best-case run is mistaken for sustained long-term throughput.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉至少 24 小時，從機台紀錄拆解每片晶圓的曝光、每場額外與晶圓交換時間，與模型逐項比較；依 SEMI E10 的設備狀態定義，以數週的事件紀錄計算可用度、MTBF 與 MTTR；同時統計每場劑量穩定度，確認產能不是以犧牲劑量控制換來的。","textEn":"Run the specified dose and layout continuously for at least 24 hours, break each wafer's time into exposure, per-field overhead and exchange from machine logs and compare item by item with the model; compute availability, MTBF and MTTR from weeks of event logs using SEMI E10 equipment-state definitions; tally per-field dose stability at the same time to confirm that throughput was not bought by loosening dose control.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉至少 24 小時，從機台紀錄拆解每片晶圓的曝光、每場額外與晶圓交換時間，與模型逐項比較。","晶圓被靜電夾緊後就不會熱膨脹。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Run the specified dose and layout continuously for at least 24 hours, break each wafer's time into exposure, per-field overhead and exchange from machine logs and compare item by item with the model.","Once electrostatically clamped, a wafer cannot expand thermally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉至少 24 小時，從機台紀錄拆解每片晶圓的曝光、每場額外與晶圓交換時間，與模型逐項比較；依 SEMI E10 的設備狀態定義，以數週的事件紀錄計算可用度、MTBF 與 MTTR；同時統計每場劑量穩定度，確認產能不是以犧牲劑量控制換來的。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run the specified dose and layout continuously for at least 24 hours, break each wafer's time into exposure, per-field overhead and exchange from machine logs and compare item by item with the model; compute availability, MTBF and MTTR from weeks of event logs using SEMI E10 equipment-state definitions; tally per-field dose stability at the same time to confirm that throughput was not bought by loosening dose control. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"asml-v12-32","title":"每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收：失效診斷","titleEn":"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"],"prerequisiteIds":["asml-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「產能、可用度與交接」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Throughput, availability and handoff” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"規格產能是在參考佈局與劑量下量得，客戶佈局若有更多部分場或更高劑量，實際產能明顯較低；可用度宣稱若未計入排定的集光鏡更換，產線排程會在保養週失準；短時間的最佳紀錄被誤當成長期持續產能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Specified throughput is measured at a reference layout and dose, so customer layouts with more partial fields or higher dose run noticeably slower; availability claims that leave out scheduled collector swaps derail fab scheduling in maintenance weeks; a short best-case run is mistaken for sustained long-term throughput. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：驗收時以指定劑量與佈局連續運轉，記錄每小時晶圓數、劑量穩定度、套刻、焦距與可用度，交接時附上光源功率趨勢、集光鏡反射率與護膜狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Acceptance runs the specified dose and layout continuously, logging wafers per hour, dose stability, overlay, focus and availability, and the handoff carries source-power trends, collector reflectance and pellicle status.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「光源功率加倍，每小時晶圓數就一定加倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling source power always doubles wafers per hour.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"asml-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"規格產能是在參考佈局與劑量下量得，客戶佈局若有更多部分場或更高劑量，實際產能明顯較低；可用度宣稱若未計入排定的集光鏡更換，產線排程會在保養週失準；短時間的最佳紀錄被誤當成長期持續產能。","textEn":"Specified throughput is measured at a reference layout and dose, so customer layouts with more partial fields or higher dose run noticeably slower; availability claims that leave out scheduled collector swaps derail fab scheduling in maintenance weeks; a short best-case run is mistaken for sustained long-term throughput.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]},{"id":"asml-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-asml-twinscan-exe-5000","v12o-asml-high-na-5-things","v12o-brouns-2017-euv-pellicles","v12o-asml-twinscan-nxe-3800e"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「每小時晶圓數與可用度的系統驗收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"System acceptance of wafers per hour and availability\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","High-NA 只是換上更大的反射鏡，曝光場大小與 NXE 相同。","規格產能是在參考佈局與劑量下量得，客戶佈局若有更多部分場或更高劑量，實際產能明顯較低。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","High-NA simply uses bigger mirrors and keeps the same exposure field as NXE.","Specified throughput is measured at a reference layout and dose, so customer layouts with more partial fields or higher dose run noticeably slower."],"answer":2,"explanation":"規格產能是在參考佈局與劑量下量得，客戶佈局若有更多部分場或更高劑量，實際產能明顯較低；可用度宣稱若未計入排定的集光鏡更換，產線排程會在保養週失準；短時間的最佳紀錄被誤當成長期持續產能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Specified throughput is measured at a reference layout and dose, so customer layouts with more partial fields or higher dose run noticeably slower; availability claims that leave out scheduled collector swaps derail fab scheduling in maintenance weeks; a short best-case run is mistaken for sustained long-term throughput. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":12}],"stepCount":56,"estimatedMinutes":1160,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","enrichmentVersion":12,"v12Extension":{"stages":4,"steps":32,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"High-NA 產能練習：劑量 50 mJ/cm²，300 mm 晶圓含部分場共 186 個半場，面積 186 × 429 mm² = 798 cm²，需能量 39.9 J；假設晶圓端功率 4.0 W，曝光時間 10.0 s。掃描速度 v = 4.0/(500 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.31 m/s，光罩速度 8 × 0.31 ≈ 2.46 m/s。光罩台 32 g 時加速 2.46/313.8 ≈ 7.8 ms，每場額外時間取加速加減速再加 20 ms 穩定與步進，共 35.7 ms，186 場為 6.64 s；晶圓額外 2.0 s，合計 18.6 s，約 193 片/小時。若光罩台只有 8 g，加速 31.4 ms，每場 82.8 ms，186 場為 15.4 s，合計 27.4 s，只剩約 131 片/小時，說明半場加倍後高加速度載台對產能的關鍵性。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實機規格。","textEn":"High-NA throughput exercise: at 50 mJ/cm² a 300 mm wafer holds 186 half fields including partials, 186 × 429 mm² = 798 cm², needing 39.9 J; assuming 4.0 W at the wafer the exposure time is 10.0 s. Scan speed v = 4.0/(500 J/m² × 0.026 m) ≈ 0.31 m/s and the reticle runs 8 × 0.31 ≈ 2.46 m/s. With a 32 g reticle stage the ramp takes 2.46/313.8 ≈ 7.8 ms; taking per-field overhead as acceleration plus deceleration plus 20 ms for settling and stepping gives 35.7 ms, or 6.64 s for 186 fields; adding 2.0 s of wafer overhead totals 18.6 s, about 193 wafers per hour. With only 8 g the ramp is 31.4 ms, each field costs 82.8 ms, 186 fields take 15.4 s, the total is 27.4 s and throughput falls to about 131 wafers per hour, showing why high-acceleration stages are essential once fields are halved. Values are teaching assumptions, not any tool's specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"focus":"High-NA 變形光學、高加速度光罩台、EUV 護膜與集光鏡壽命、焦面對準量測、晶圓熱控、逐場套刻與產能可用度","focusEn":"High-NA anamorphic optics, high-acceleration reticle stages, pellicle and collector life, focus and alignment sensing, wafer thermal control, per-field overlay and productivity"},"learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-lithography","learningTags":["optics","optics-lithography","lithography"],"subcategory":"optics-lithography","subcategoryTitle":"微影光學與精密定位","subcategoryTitleEn":"Lithography optics and precision positioning"},{"id":"idf","title":"經國號與航空製造概念","titleEn":"IDF and Aircraft Manufacturing Concepts","category":"aerospace","summary":"以經國號研製歷史為起點，學習通用飛機結構、材料追溯、系統整合與驗證管理。","summaryEn":"Use the IDF development history to study general aircraft structures, material traceability, integration and verification management.","scope":"航空史與通用工程概念；不含武器、火控、戰術、作戰性能優化或真機建造指示。","scopeEn":"Aviation history and general engineering concepts only; excludes weapons, fire control, tactics, combat optimization and instructions to construct an operational aircraft.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"diagram":{"type":"aircraft","labels":["需求","機翼","機身","系統","驗證"],"labelsEn":["Requirements","Wing","Fuselage","Systems","Verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"idf-s01","order":1,"title":"任務與歷史","titleEn":"Purpose and history","steps":[{"id":"idf-s01-01","order":1,"title":"定位研製歷程","titleEn":"Place development milestones","objective":"完成「定位研製歷程」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for place development milestones.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"原型出廠、首飛與量產是不同里程碑，不能用單一日期代表完整研製。","textEn":"Prototype rollout, first flight and production are different milestones in aircraft development."},{"id":"idf-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"依公開資料建立三類里程碑時間軸。","textEn":"Build a timeline with three distinct milestone types from public sources."}],"check":"依公開資料建立三類里程碑時間軸。","checkEn":"Build a timeline with three distinct milestone types from public sources.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「定位研製歷程」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains place development milestones?","options":["原型出廠、首飛與量產是不同里程碑，不能用單一日期代表完整研製。","結構與品質管理概念可用非飛行比例模型表達，不需要作戰功能。","每項需求應連到設計決策與驗證證據，避免只有漂亮外形。"],"optionsEn":["Prototype rollout, first flight and production are different milestones in aircraft development.","Structural and quality concepts can be represented by a non-flying scale model without combat functions.","Each requirement should link to a design decision and verification evidence."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原型出廠、首飛與量產是不同里程碑，不能用單一日期代表完整研製。","explanationEn":"Prototype rollout, first flight and production are different milestones in aircraft development."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s01-02","order":2,"title":"界定學習模型","titleEn":"Define the learning model","objective":"完成「界定學習模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define the learning model.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"結構與品質管理概念可用非飛行比例模型表達，不需要作戰功能。","textEn":"Structural and quality concepts can be represented by a non-flying scale model without combat functions."},{"id":"idf-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"定義模型包含的結構方塊和不採用的真實性能數據。","textEn":"Define structural blocks and identify real performance data outside the model."}],"check":"定義模型包含的結構方塊和不採用的真實性能數據。","checkEn":"Define structural blocks and identify real performance data outside the model.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「界定學習模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define the learning model?","options":["每項需求應連到設計決策與驗證證據，避免只有漂亮外形。","原型出廠、首飛與量產是不同里程碑，不能用單一日期代表完整研製。","結構與品質管理概念可用非飛行比例模型表達，不需要作戰功能。"],"optionsEn":["Each requirement should link to a design decision and verification evidence.","Prototype rollout, first flight and production are different milestones in aircraft development.","Structural and quality concepts can be represented by a non-flying scale model without combat functions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結構與品質管理概念可用非飛行比例模型表達，不需要作戰功能。","explanationEn":"Structural and quality concepts can be represented by a non-flying scale model without combat functions."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s01-03","order":3,"title":"建立需求追溯","titleEn":"Trace requirements","objective":"完成「建立需求追溯」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for trace requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"每項需求應連到設計決策與驗證證據，避免只有漂亮外形。","textEn":"Each requirement should link to a design decision and verification evidence."},{"id":"idf-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以重量、可檢查性、介面一致性建立三條追溯鏈。","textEn":"Create traceability chains for mass, inspectability and interface consistency."}],"check":"以重量、可檢查性、介面一致性建立三條追溯鏈。","checkEn":"Create traceability chains for mass, inspectability and interface consistency.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立需求追溯」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains trace requirements?","options":["結構與品質管理概念可用非飛行比例模型表達，不需要作戰功能。","每項需求應連到設計決策與驗證證據，避免只有漂亮外形。","原型出廠、首飛與量產是不同里程碑，不能用單一日期代表完整研製。"],"optionsEn":["Structural and quality concepts can be represented by a non-flying scale model without combat functions.","Each requirement should link to a design decision and verification evidence.","Prototype rollout, first flight and production are different milestones in aircraft development."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每項需求應連到設計決策與驗證證據，避免只有漂亮外形。","explanationEn":"Each requirement should link to a design decision and verification evidence."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"idf-s02","order":2,"title":"通用結構力學","titleEn":"General structural mechanics","steps":[{"id":"idf-s02-01","order":1,"title":"辨識機翼承載概念","titleEn":"Identify wing load paths","objective":"完成「辨識機翼承載概念」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify wing load paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"翼樑、翼肋與蒙皮共同傳遞載荷，外形相同不保證剛性相同。","textEn":"Spars, ribs and skin share loads; identical shape does not ensure equal stiffness."},{"id":"idf-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在無比例示意翼標出彎曲與剪力傳遞方向。","textEn":"Mark bending and shear load paths on a not-to-scale wing schematic."}],"check":"在無比例示意翼標出彎曲與剪力傳遞方向。","checkEn":"Mark bending and shear load paths on a not-to-scale wing schematic.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識機翼承載概念」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify wing load paths?","options":["薄板可能在材料破壞前屈曲，加筋會改變穩定性與重量。","接頭會傳遞載荷並造成局部應力集中，需考慮檢查及可維修性。","翼樑、翼肋與蒙皮共同傳遞載荷，外形相同不保證剛性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thin panels can buckle before material failure; stiffening changes stability and mass.","Joints transfer load and create local stress concentrations, requiring inspection and maintainability considerations.","Spars, ribs and skin share loads; identical shape does not ensure equal stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"翼樑、翼肋與蒙皮共同傳遞載荷，外形相同不保證剛性相同。","explanationEn":"Spars, ribs and skin share loads; identical shape does not ensure equal stiffness."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s02-02","order":2,"title":"分析薄殼穩定性","titleEn":"Analyze shell stability","objective":"完成「分析薄殼穩定性」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze shell stability.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"薄板可能在材料破壞前屈曲，加筋會改變穩定性與重量。","textEn":"Thin panels can buckle before material failure; stiffening changes stability and mass."},{"id":"idf-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較紙板平板與折邊模型的定性剛性。","textEn":"Compare qualitative stiffness of flat and folded card models."}],"check":"比較紙板平板與折邊模型的定性剛性。","checkEn":"Compare qualitative stiffness of flat and folded card models.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析薄殼穩定性」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze shell stability?","options":["翼樑、翼肋與蒙皮共同傳遞載荷，外形相同不保證剛性相同。","薄板可能在材料破壞前屈曲，加筋會改變穩定性與重量。","接頭會傳遞載荷並造成局部應力集中，需考慮檢查及可維修性。"],"optionsEn":["Spars, ribs and skin share loads; identical shape does not ensure equal stiffness.","Thin panels can buckle before material failure; stiffening changes stability and mass.","Joints transfer load and create local stress concentrations, requiring inspection and maintainability considerations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄板可能在材料破壞前屈曲，加筋會改變穩定性與重量。","explanationEn":"Thin panels can buckle before material failure; stiffening changes stability and mass."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s02-03","order":3,"title":"評估連接介面","titleEn":"Evaluate joint interfaces","objective":"完成「評估連接介面」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for evaluate joint interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"接頭會傳遞載荷並造成局部應力集中，需考慮檢查及可維修性。","textEn":"Joints transfer load and create local stress concentrations, requiring inspection and maintainability considerations."},{"id":"idf-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出三個接頭的載荷路徑與可檢查方向。","textEn":"Mark load paths and inspection directions for three schematic joints."}],"check":"標出三個接頭的載荷路徑與可檢查方向。","checkEn":"Mark load paths and inspection directions for three schematic joints.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「評估連接介面」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains evaluate joint interfaces?","options":["接頭會傳遞載荷並造成局部應力集中，需考慮檢查及可維修性。","翼樑、翼肋與蒙皮共同傳遞載荷，外形相同不保證剛性相同。","薄板可能在材料破壞前屈曲，加筋會改變穩定性與重量。"],"optionsEn":["Joints transfer load and create local stress concentrations, requiring inspection and maintainability considerations.","Spars, ribs and skin share loads; identical shape does not ensure equal stiffness.","Thin panels can buckle before material failure; stiffening changes stability and mass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭會傳遞載荷並造成局部應力集中，需考慮檢查及可維修性。","explanationEn":"Joints transfer load and create local stress concentrations, requiring inspection and maintainability considerations."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"idf-s03","order":3,"title":"材料與製造品質","titleEn":"Materials and manufacturing quality","steps":[{"id":"idf-s03-01","order":1,"title":"比較金屬與複材","titleEn":"Compare metals and composites","objective":"完成「比較金屬與複材」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare metals and composites.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"複合材料具方向性，金屬與複材的缺陷和檢查方法不同。","textEn":"Composites are directional, and metals and composites differ in defect types and inspection methods."},{"id":"idf-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出兩類材料的方向性與典型缺陷。","textEn":"List directionality and typical defects for both material classes."}],"check":"列出兩類材料的方向性與典型缺陷。","checkEn":"List directionality and typical defects for both material classes.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較金屬與複材」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare metals and composites?","options":["目視、超音波與射線觀察不同類型缺陷，各有偵測限制。","複合材料具方向性，金屬與複材的缺陷和檢查方法不同。","材料批號和製程版本讓異常能追溯到來源與受影響零件。"],"optionsEn":["Visual, ultrasonic and radiographic methods observe different defects and have detection limits.","Composites are directional, and metals and composites differ in defect types and inspection methods.","Material lot and process revision connect anomalies to sources and affected parts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"複合材料具方向性，金屬與複材的缺陷和檢查方法不同。","explanationEn":"Composites are directional, and metals and composites differ in defect types and inspection methods."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s03-02","order":2,"title":"建立材料履歷","titleEn":"Build material records","objective":"完成「建立材料履歷」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build material records.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"材料批號和製程版本讓異常能追溯到來源與受影響零件。","textEn":"Material lot and process revision connect anomalies to sources and affected parts."},{"id":"idf-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"替教學模型建立材料、零件與組裝的編號關係。","textEn":"Create relationships among material, part and assembly identifiers."}],"check":"替教學模型建立材料、零件與組裝的編號關係。","checkEn":"Create relationships among material, part and assembly identifiers.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立材料履歷」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build material records?","options":["材料批號和製程版本讓異常能追溯到來源與受影響零件。","目視、超音波與射線觀察不同類型缺陷，各有偵測限制。","複合材料具方向性，金屬與複材的缺陷和檢查方法不同。"],"optionsEn":["Material lot and process revision connect anomalies to sources and affected parts.","Visual, ultrasonic and radiographic methods observe different defects and have detection limits.","Composites are directional, and metals and composites differ in defect types and inspection methods."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料批號和製程版本讓異常能追溯到來源與受影響零件。","explanationEn":"Material lot and process revision connect anomalies to sources and affected parts."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s03-03","order":3,"title":"理解非破壞檢測","titleEn":"Understand nondestructive inspection","objective":"完成「理解非破壞檢測」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand nondestructive inspection.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"目視、超音波與射線觀察不同類型缺陷，各有偵測限制。","textEn":"Visual, ultrasonic and radiographic methods observe different defects and have detection limits."},{"id":"idf-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為表面裂紋與內部脫層分別選擇概念檢查方法。","textEn":"Select conceptual inspections for surface cracks and internal delamination."}],"check":"為表面裂紋與內部脫層分別選擇概念檢查方法。","checkEn":"Select conceptual inspections for surface cracks and internal delamination.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解非破壞檢測」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand nondestructive inspection?","options":["複合材料具方向性，金屬與複材的缺陷和檢查方法不同。","材料批號和製程版本讓異常能追溯到來源與受影響零件。","目視、超音波與射線觀察不同類型缺陷，各有偵測限制。"],"optionsEn":["Composites are directional, and metals and composites differ in defect types and inspection methods.","Material lot and process revision connect anomalies to sources and affected parts.","Visual, ultrasonic and radiographic methods observe different defects and have detection limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"目視、超音波與射線觀察不同類型缺陷，各有偵測限制。","explanationEn":"Visual, ultrasonic and radiographic methods observe different defects and have detection limits."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"idf-s04","order":4,"title":"系統介面","titleEn":"System interfaces","steps":[{"id":"idf-s04-01","order":1,"title":"建立能源方塊圖","titleEn":"Build an energy block diagram","objective":"完成「建立能源方塊圖」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build an energy block diagram.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"能源、訊號與機械載荷是不同介面，混淆會掩蓋整合風險。","textEn":"Energy, signals and mechanical loads are different interfaces; conflating them hides integration risks."},{"id":"idf-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用三種線型畫出非作戰教學模型介面。","textEn":"Use three line styles for interfaces in a non-combat learning model."}],"check":"用三種線型畫出非作戰教學模型介面。","checkEn":"Use three line styles for interfaces in a non-combat learning model.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立能源方塊圖」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build an energy block diagram?","options":["能源、訊號與機械載荷是不同介面，混淆會掩蓋整合風險。","多個感測器需要交叉核對與共同失效分析，數量增加不等於可靠度保證。","清楚的狀態、警示與單位能降低誤讀，資訊過多也會增加負擔。"],"optionsEn":["Energy, signals and mechanical loads are different interfaces; conflating them hides integration risks.","Multiple sensors need cross-checking and common-cause analysis; more sensors alone do not guarantee reliability.","Clear states, warnings and units reduce misinterpretation, while excess information increases burden."],"answer":0,"explanation":"能源、訊號與機械載荷是不同介面，混淆會掩蓋整合風險。","explanationEn":"Energy, signals and mechanical loads are different interfaces; conflating them hides integration risks."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解感測冗餘","titleEn":"Understand sensor redundancy","objective":"完成「理解感測冗餘」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand sensor redundancy.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"多個感測器需要交叉核對與共同失效分析，數量增加不等於可靠度保證。","textEn":"Multiple sensors need cross-checking and common-cause analysis; more sensors alone do not guarantee reliability."},{"id":"idf-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立三個虛擬感測器不同讀值時的診斷表。","textEn":"Build a diagnostic table for three disagreeing virtual sensors."}],"check":"建立三個虛擬感測器不同讀值時的診斷表。","checkEn":"Build a diagnostic table for three disagreeing virtual sensors.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解感測冗餘」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand sensor redundancy?","options":["清楚的狀態、警示與單位能降低誤讀，資訊過多也會增加負擔。","能源、訊號與機械載荷是不同介面，混淆會掩蓋整合風險。","多個感測器需要交叉核對與共同失效分析，數量增加不等於可靠度保證。"],"optionsEn":["Clear states, warnings and units reduce misinterpretation, while excess information increases burden.","Energy, signals and mechanical loads are different interfaces; conflating them hides integration risks.","Multiple sensors need cross-checking and common-cause analysis; more sensors alone do not guarantee reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多個感測器需要交叉核對與共同失效分析，數量增加不等於可靠度保證。","explanationEn":"Multiple sensors need cross-checking and common-cause analysis; more sensors alone do not guarantee reliability."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s04-03","order":3,"title":"檢查人機資訊","titleEn":"Review human-machine information","objective":"完成「檢查人機資訊」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for review human-machine information.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"清楚的狀態、警示與單位能降低誤讀，資訊過多也會增加負擔。","textEn":"Clear states, warnings and units reduce misinterpretation, while excess information increases burden."},{"id":"idf-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"設計只顯示必要狀態的地面教學儀表。","textEn":"Design a ground-training display showing essential states only."}],"check":"設計只顯示必要狀態的地面教學儀表。","checkEn":"Design a ground-training display showing essential states only.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「檢查人機資訊」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains review human-machine information?","options":["多個感測器需要交叉核對與共同失效分析，數量增加不等於可靠度保證。","清楚的狀態、警示與單位能降低誤讀，資訊過多也會增加負擔。","能源、訊號與機械載荷是不同介面，混淆會掩蓋整合風險。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple sensors need cross-checking and common-cause analysis; more sensors alone do not guarantee reliability.","Clear states, warnings and units reduce misinterpretation, while excess information increases burden.","Energy, signals and mechanical loads are different interfaces; conflating them hides integration risks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清楚的狀態、警示與單位能降低誤讀，資訊過多也會增加負擔。","explanationEn":"Clear states, warnings and units reduce misinterpretation, while excess information increases burden."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"idf-s05","order":5,"title":"驗證與風險管理","titleEn":"Verification and risk management","steps":[{"id":"idf-s05-01","order":1,"title":"分辨驗證與確認","titleEn":"Distinguish verification and validation","objective":"完成「分辨驗證與確認」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish verification and validation.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"驗證檢查是否符合規格，確認檢查是否符合用途。","textEn":"Verification checks specifications; validation checks fitness for intended use."},{"id":"idf-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把五個教學測試問題分到兩類。","textEn":"Classify five learning-model test questions into the two categories."}],"check":"把五個教學測試問題分到兩類。","checkEn":"Classify five learning-model test questions into the two categories.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分辨驗證與確認」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish verification and validation?","options":["失效模式分析需連結原因、影響、偵測及緩解，不能只列風險名稱。","小零件改動可能改變重量、介面與檢驗需求，因此變更需重新評估。","驗證檢查是否符合規格，確認檢查是否符合用途。"],"optionsEn":["Failure-mode analysis links causes, effects, detection and mitigation rather than only naming risks.","A small part change can affect mass, interfaces and inspection needs, requiring reassessment.","Verification checks specifications; validation checks fitness for intended use."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗證檢查是否符合規格，確認檢查是否符合用途。","explanationEn":"Verification checks specifications; validation checks fitness for intended use."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s05-02","order":2,"title":"建立失效模式表","titleEn":"Build a failure-mode table","objective":"完成「建立失效模式表」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a failure-mode table.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"失效模式分析需連結原因、影響、偵測及緩解，不能只列風險名稱。","textEn":"Failure-mode analysis links causes, effects, detection and mitigation rather than only naming risks."},{"id":"idf-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為感測斷線與模型接頭鬆脫建立完整紀錄。","textEn":"Create complete records for sensor disconnection and loose model joints."}],"check":"為感測斷線與模型接頭鬆脫建立完整紀錄。","checkEn":"Create complete records for sensor disconnection and loose model joints.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立失效模式表」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a failure-mode table?","options":["驗證檢查是否符合規格，確認檢查是否符合用途。","失效模式分析需連結原因、影響、偵測及緩解，不能只列風險名稱。","小零件改動可能改變重量、介面與檢驗需求，因此變更需重新評估。"],"optionsEn":["Verification checks specifications; validation checks fitness for intended use.","Failure-mode analysis links causes, effects, detection and mitigation rather than only naming risks.","A small part change can affect mass, interfaces and inspection needs, requiring reassessment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"失效模式分析需連結原因、影響、偵測及緩解，不能只列風險名稱。","explanationEn":"Failure-mode analysis links causes, effects, detection and mitigation rather than only naming risks."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s05-03","order":3,"title":"管理設計變更","titleEn":"Manage design changes","objective":"完成「管理設計變更」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for manage design changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"小零件改動可能改變重量、介面與檢驗需求，因此變更需重新評估。","textEn":"A small part change can affect mass, interfaces and inspection needs, requiring reassessment."},{"id":"idf-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提出一次模型材料替換並列出受影響證據。","textEn":"Propose a model material substitution and list affected evidence."}],"check":"提出一次模型材料替換並列出受影響證據。","checkEn":"Propose a model material substitution and list affected evidence.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「管理設計變更」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains manage design changes?","options":["小零件改動可能改變重量、介面與檢驗需求，因此變更需重新評估。","驗證檢查是否符合規格，確認檢查是否符合用途。","失效模式分析需連結原因、影響、偵測及緩解，不能只列風險名稱。"],"optionsEn":["A small part change can affect mass, interfaces and inspection needs, requiring reassessment.","Verification checks specifications; validation checks fitness for intended use.","Failure-mode analysis links causes, effects, detection and mitigation rather than only naming risks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"小零件改動可能改變重量、介面與檢驗需求，因此變更需重新評估。","explanationEn":"A small part change can affect mass, interfaces and inspection needs, requiring reassessment."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"idf-s06","order":6,"title":"交付與維護概念","titleEn":"Handover and maintenance concepts","steps":[{"id":"idf-s06-01","order":1,"title":"完成構型清單","titleEn":"Complete the configuration list","objective":"完成「完成構型清單」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for complete the configuration list.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"構型清單需確保圖面版本與實物版本一致。","textEn":"A configuration list must align drawing revisions with the physical model."},{"id":"idf-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"核對模型、零件表與示意圖的版本。","textEn":"Check versions across model, bill of materials and schematic."}],"check":"核對模型、零件表與示意圖的版本。","checkEn":"Check versions across model, bill of materials and schematic.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「完成構型清單」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains complete the configuration list?","options":["開放問題與未驗證假設應隨交付物保留，避免把模型能力誤當真機能力。","構型清單需確保圖面版本與實物版本一致。","可維修設計讓檢查點能接近、辨識及記錄。"],"optionsEn":["Open questions and unverified assumptions belong with deliverables to avoid mistaking model capability for aircraft capability.","A configuration list must align drawing revisions with the physical model.","Maintainable design makes inspection points accessible, identifiable and recordable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"構型清單需確保圖面版本與實物版本一致。","explanationEn":"A configuration list must align drawing revisions with the physical model."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s06-02","order":2,"title":"規劃檢查可及性","titleEn":"Plan inspection access","objective":"完成「規劃檢查可及性」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan inspection access.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"可維修設計讓檢查點能接近、辨識及記錄。","textEn":"Maintainable design makes inspection points accessible, identifiable and recordable."},{"id":"idf-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在模型上標出不拆解即可檢查的位置。","textEn":"Mark locations inspectable without disassembling the model."}],"check":"在模型上標出不拆解即可檢查的位置。","checkEn":"Mark locations inspectable without disassembling the model.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃檢查可及性」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan inspection access?","options":["可維修設計讓檢查點能接近、辨識及記錄。","開放問題與未驗證假設應隨交付物保留，避免把模型能力誤當真機能力。","構型清單需確保圖面版本與實物版本一致。"],"optionsEn":["Maintainable design makes inspection points accessible, identifiable and recordable.","Open questions and unverified assumptions belong with deliverables to avoid mistaking model capability for aircraft capability.","A configuration list must align drawing revisions with the physical model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可維修設計讓檢查點能接近、辨識及記錄。","explanationEn":"Maintainable design makes inspection points accessible, identifiable and recordable."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"idf-s06-03","order":3,"title":"撰寫工程回顧","titleEn":"Write the engineering review","objective":"完成「撰寫工程回顧」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for write the engineering review.","knowledge":[{"id":"idf-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"開放問題與未驗證假設應隨交付物保留，避免把模型能力誤當真機能力。","textEn":"Open questions and unverified assumptions belong with deliverables to avoid mistaking model capability for aircraft capability."},{"id":"idf-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交非飛行模型報告和未驗證項目表。","textEn":"Submit a non-flying model report and unresolved verification list."}],"check":"提交非飛行模型報告和未驗證項目表。","checkEn":"Submit a non-flying model report and unresolved verification list.","sourceIds":["aidc-idf","faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「撰寫工程回顧」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains write the engineering review?","options":["構型清單需確保圖面版本與實物版本一致。","可維修設計讓檢查點能接近、辨識及記錄。","開放問題與未驗證假設應隨交付物保留，避免把模型能力誤當真機能力。"],"optionsEn":["A configuration list must align drawing revisions with the physical model.","Maintainable design makes inspection points accessible, identifiable and recordable.","Open questions and unverified assumptions belong with deliverables to avoid mistaking model capability for aircraft capability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開放問題與未驗證假設應隨交付物保留，避免把模型能力誤當真機能力。","explanationEn":"Open questions and unverified assumptions belong with deliverables to avoid mistaking model capability for aircraft capability."},"prerequisiteIds":["idf-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course"},{"id":"apache","title":"阿帕契案例與旋翼機原理","titleEn":"Apache Context and Rotorcraft Principles","category":"aerospace","summary":"以公開案例認識旋翼機，透過非飛行模型學習升力、傳動概念、振動及適航安全。","summaryEn":"Use public context and non-flying models to study rotorcraft lift, transmission concepts, vibration and airworthiness safety.","scope":"旋翼機物理與安全教育；不含武器、瞄準、軍用性能設計、飛行操作或真機組裝。","scopeEn":"Rotorcraft physics and safety education only; excludes weapons, targeting, military-performance design, flight operations and operational aircraft assembly.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter","v5-place-746229a483ea"],"diagram":{"type":"rotorcraft","labels":["旋翼","傳動","機體","感測","安全"],"labelsEn":["Rotor","Transmission","Airframe","Sensing","Safety"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"apache-s01","order":1,"title":"旋翼機系統地圖","titleEn":"Rotorcraft system map","steps":[{"id":"apache-s01-01","order":1,"title":"辨識旋翼與機身","titleEn":"Identify rotor and fuselage","objective":"完成「辨識旋翼與機身」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify rotor and fuselage.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"旋翼同時影響升力與機體反作用，不能只把它當作向上的風扇。","textEn":"A rotor affects lift and airframe reaction, rather than acting merely as an upward fan."},{"id":"apache-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意圖上標出旋翼、機身與反作用方向。","textEn":"Mark rotor, fuselage and reaction directions on a schematic."}],"check":"在示意圖上標出旋翼、機身與反作用方向。","checkEn":"Mark rotor, fuselage and reaction directions on a schematic.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識旋翼與機身」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify rotor and fuselage?","options":["旋翼同時影響升力與機體反作用，不能只把它當作向上的風扇。","能源經動力來源與傳動到旋翼，其中每一段都存在效率損失。","靜態模型可展示機械關係，而真實飛行需要獨立適航驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A rotor affects lift and airframe reaction, rather than acting merely as an upward fan.","Energy passes through power source and transmission to the rotor, with losses at each stage.","A static model illustrates mechanical relationships; actual flight needs independent airworthiness validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"旋翼同時影響升力與機體反作用，不能只把它當作向上的風扇。","explanationEn":"A rotor affects lift and airframe reaction, rather than acting merely as an upward fan."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s01-02","order":2,"title":"建立能源流概念","titleEn":"Map energy flow","objective":"完成「建立能源流概念」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map energy flow.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"能源經動力來源與傳動到旋翼，其中每一段都存在效率損失。","textEn":"Energy passes through power source and transmission to the rotor, with losses at each stage."},{"id":"apache-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"使用無因次效率繪出能源流向。","textEn":"Diagram energy flow with dimensionless efficiencies."}],"check":"使用無因次效率繪出能源流向。","checkEn":"Diagram energy flow with dimensionless efficiencies.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立能源流概念」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map energy flow?","options":["靜態模型可展示機械關係，而真實飛行需要獨立適航驗證。","旋翼同時影響升力與機體反作用，不能只把它當作向上的風扇。","能源經動力來源與傳動到旋翼，其中每一段都存在效率損失。"],"optionsEn":["A static model illustrates mechanical relationships; actual flight needs independent airworthiness validation.","A rotor affects lift and airframe reaction, rather than acting merely as an upward fan.","Energy passes through power source and transmission to the rotor, with losses at each stage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"能源經動力來源與傳動到旋翼，其中每一段都存在效率損失。","explanationEn":"Energy passes through power source and transmission to the rotor, with losses at each stage."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s01-03","order":3,"title":"界定展示邊界","titleEn":"Define display boundaries","objective":"完成「界定展示邊界」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define display boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"靜態模型可展示機械關係，而真實飛行需要獨立適航驗證。","textEn":"A static model illustrates mechanical relationships; actual flight needs independent airworthiness validation."},{"id":"apache-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列明模型只檢查幾何及概念連接。","textEn":"State that the model tests geometry and conceptual connections only."}],"check":"列明模型只檢查幾何及概念連接。","checkEn":"State that the model tests geometry and conceptual connections only.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「界定展示邊界」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define display boundaries?","options":["能源經動力來源與傳動到旋翼，其中每一段都存在效率損失。","靜態模型可展示機械關係，而真實飛行需要獨立適航驗證。","旋翼同時影響升力與機體反作用，不能只把它當作向上的風扇。"],"optionsEn":["Energy passes through power source and transmission to the rotor, with losses at each stage.","A static model illustrates mechanical relationships; actual flight needs independent airworthiness validation.","A rotor affects lift and airframe reaction, rather than acting merely as an upward fan."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜態模型可展示機械關係，而真實飛行需要獨立適航驗證。","explanationEn":"A static model illustrates mechanical relationships; actual flight needs independent airworthiness validation."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"apache-s02","order":2,"title":"空氣動力學概念","titleEn":"Aerodynamic concepts","steps":[{"id":"apache-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解升力方向","titleEn":"Understand lift direction","objective":"完成「理解升力方向」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand lift direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"升力相對局部氣流定義，旋轉葉片不同半徑處的相對速度不同。","textEn":"Lift is defined relative to local airflow; blade sections at different radii have different relative speeds."},{"id":"apache-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在靜態葉片圖標出局部相對速度方向。","textEn":"Mark local relative velocity on a static blade diagram."}],"check":"在靜態葉片圖標出局部相對速度方向。","checkEn":"Mark local relative velocity on a static blade diagram.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解升力方向」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand lift direction?","options":["總距改變葉片整體槳距，周期變距隨旋轉方位改變槳距分布。","主旋翼扭矩對機身有反作用，需要系統層級的平衡機制。","升力相對局部氣流定義，旋轉葉片不同半徑處的相對速度不同。"],"optionsEn":["Collective changes overall blade pitch; cyclic varies pitch with rotor azimuth.","Main-rotor torque creates an airframe reaction that needs a system-level balancing mechanism.","Lift is defined relative to local airflow; blade sections at different radii have different relative speeds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"升力相對局部氣流定義，旋轉葉片不同半徑處的相對速度不同。","explanationEn":"Lift is defined relative to local airflow; blade sections at different radii have different relative speeds."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s02-02","order":2,"title":"比較總距與周期概念","titleEn":"Compare collective and cyclic concepts","objective":"完成「比較總距與周期概念」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare collective and cyclic concepts.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"總距改變葉片整體槳距，周期變距隨旋轉方位改變槳距分布。","textEn":"Collective changes overall blade pitch; cyclic varies pitch with rotor azimuth."},{"id":"apache-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用紙板姿態標記比較兩種概念，不提供操作參數。","textEn":"Compare the concepts with card orientation markers without operating settings."}],"check":"用紙板姿態標記比較兩種概念，不提供操作參數。","checkEn":"Compare the concepts with card orientation markers without operating settings.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較總距與周期概念」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare collective and cyclic concepts?","options":["升力相對局部氣流定義，旋轉葉片不同半徑處的相對速度不同。","總距改變葉片整體槳距，周期變距隨旋轉方位改變槳距分布。","主旋翼扭矩對機身有反作用，需要系統層級的平衡機制。"],"optionsEn":["Lift is defined relative to local airflow; blade sections at different radii have different relative speeds.","Collective changes overall blade pitch; cyclic varies pitch with rotor azimuth.","Main-rotor torque creates an airframe reaction that needs a system-level balancing mechanism."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總距改變葉片整體槳距，周期變距隨旋轉方位改變槳距分布。","explanationEn":"Collective changes overall blade pitch; cyclic varies pitch with rotor azimuth."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s02-03","order":3,"title":"理解扭矩反作用","titleEn":"Understand torque reaction","objective":"完成「理解扭矩反作用」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand torque reaction.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"主旋翼扭矩對機身有反作用，需要系統層級的平衡機制。","textEn":"Main-rotor torque creates an airframe reaction that needs a system-level balancing mechanism."},{"id":"apache-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出成對作用與反作用力矩箭頭。","textEn":"Draw paired action and reaction torque arrows."}],"check":"畫出成對作用與反作用力矩箭頭。","checkEn":"Draw paired action and reaction torque arrows.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解扭矩反作用」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand torque reaction?","options":["主旋翼扭矩對機身有反作用，需要系統層級的平衡機制。","升力相對局部氣流定義，旋轉葉片不同半徑處的相對速度不同。","總距改變葉片整體槳距，周期變距隨旋轉方位改變槳距分布。"],"optionsEn":["Main-rotor torque creates an airframe reaction that needs a system-level balancing mechanism.","Lift is defined relative to local airflow; blade sections at different radii have different relative speeds.","Collective changes overall blade pitch; cyclic varies pitch with rotor azimuth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主旋翼扭矩對機身有反作用，需要系統層級的平衡機制。","explanationEn":"Main-rotor torque creates an airframe reaction that needs a system-level balancing mechanism."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"apache-s03","order":3,"title":"結構與傳動概念","titleEn":"Structure and transmission concepts","steps":[{"id":"apache-s03-01","order":1,"title":"辨識傳動功能","titleEn":"Identify transmission functions","objective":"完成「辨識傳動功能」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify transmission functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"傳動系統分配轉速與扭矩，軸承及潤滑也參與可靠度。","textEn":"Transmission distributes speed and torque; bearings and lubrication affect reliability."},{"id":"apache-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用功能方塊連接動力來源、傳動與旋翼。","textEn":"Link power source, transmission and rotor with functional blocks."}],"check":"用功能方塊連接動力來源、傳動與旋翼。","checkEn":"Link power source, transmission and rotor with functional blocks.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識傳動功能」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify transmission functions?","options":["重心位置依每個部件的質量與位置決定，總重量相同也可能重心不同。","傳動系統分配轉速與扭矩，軸承及潤滑也參與可靠度。","旋轉結構承受反覆載荷，疲勞損傷與最大靜態載荷是不同問題。"],"optionsEn":["Center of gravity depends on component masses and positions; equal total mass can yield different centers.","Transmission distributes speed and torque; bearings and lubrication affect reliability.","Rotating structures experience repeated loads; fatigue differs from maximum static loading."],"answer":1,"explanation":"傳動系統分配轉速與扭矩，軸承及潤滑也參與可靠度。","explanationEn":"Transmission distributes speed and torque; bearings and lubrication affect reliability."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s03-02","order":2,"title":"辨識周期載荷","titleEn":"Identify cyclic loads","objective":"完成「辨識周期載荷」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify cyclic loads.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"旋轉結構承受反覆載荷，疲勞損傷與最大靜態載荷是不同問題。","textEn":"Rotating structures experience repeated loads; fatigue differs from maximum static loading."},{"id":"apache-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較靜態載荷圖與周期載荷圖。","textEn":"Compare static and cyclic loading plots."}],"check":"比較靜態載荷圖與周期載荷圖。","checkEn":"Compare static and cyclic loading plots.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識周期載荷」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify cyclic loads?","options":["旋轉結構承受反覆載荷，疲勞損傷與最大靜態載荷是不同問題。","重心位置依每個部件的質量與位置決定，總重量相同也可能重心不同。","傳動系統分配轉速與扭矩，軸承及潤滑也參與可靠度。"],"optionsEn":["Rotating structures experience repeated loads; fatigue differs from maximum static loading.","Center of gravity depends on component masses and positions; equal total mass can yield different centers.","Transmission distributes speed and torque; bearings and lubrication affect reliability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"旋轉結構承受反覆載荷，疲勞損傷與最大靜態載荷是不同問題。","explanationEn":"Rotating structures experience repeated loads; fatigue differs from maximum static loading."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s03-03","order":3,"title":"檢查重量配置","titleEn":"Review mass distribution","objective":"完成「檢查重量配置」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for review mass distribution.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"重心位置依每個部件的質量與位置決定，總重量相同也可能重心不同。","textEn":"Center of gravity depends on component masses and positions; equal total mass can yield different centers."},{"id":"apache-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用低風險桌面模型比較移動配重前後的平衡。","textEn":"Compare balance before and after moving a weight on a safe desktop model."}],"check":"用低風險桌面模型比較移動配重前後的平衡。","checkEn":"Compare balance before and after moving a weight on a safe desktop model.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「檢查重量配置」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains review mass distribution?","options":["傳動系統分配轉速與扭矩，軸承及潤滑也參與可靠度。","旋轉結構承受反覆載荷，疲勞損傷與最大靜態載荷是不同問題。","重心位置依每個部件的質量與位置決定，總重量相同也可能重心不同。"],"optionsEn":["Transmission distributes speed and torque; bearings and lubrication affect reliability.","Rotating structures experience repeated loads; fatigue differs from maximum static loading.","Center of gravity depends on component masses and positions; equal total mass can yield different centers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重心位置依每個部件的質量與位置決定，總重量相同也可能重心不同。","explanationEn":"Center of gravity depends on component masses and positions; equal total mass can yield different centers."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"apache-s04","order":4,"title":"振動與量測","titleEn":"Vibration and measurement","steps":[{"id":"apache-s04-01","order":1,"title":"區分不平衡與共振","titleEn":"Distinguish imbalance and resonance","objective":"完成「區分不平衡與共振」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish imbalance and resonance.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"不平衡提供周期激勵，共振則是結構對特定頻率反應放大。","textEn":"Imbalance provides periodic excitation; resonance amplifies response near certain frequencies."},{"id":"apache-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意頻譜分別標出激勵和模態概念。","textEn":"Identify excitation and modal concepts on a schematic spectrum."}],"check":"在示意頻譜分別標出激勵和模態概念。","checkEn":"Identify excitation and modal concepts on a schematic spectrum.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分不平衡與共振」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish imbalance and resonance?","options":["不平衡提供周期激勵，共振則是結構對特定頻率反應放大。","取樣頻率不足可能產生混疊，使低頻假象掩蓋真實振動。","狀態監測需在可比較工作條件下觀察趨勢。"],"optionsEn":["Imbalance provides periodic excitation; resonance amplifies response near certain frequencies.","Insufficient sampling can alias vibration into misleading lower frequencies.","Condition monitoring requires trends under comparable operating conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不平衡提供周期激勵，共振則是結構對特定頻率反應放大。","explanationEn":"Imbalance provides periodic excitation; resonance amplifies response near certain frequencies."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解感測器取樣","titleEn":"Understand sensor sampling","objective":"完成「理解感測器取樣」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand sensor sampling.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"取樣頻率不足可能產生混疊，使低頻假象掩蓋真實振動。","textEn":"Insufficient sampling can alias vibration into misleading lower frequencies."},{"id":"apache-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較同一虛擬正弦訊號的兩種取樣結果。","textEn":"Compare two sampling rates for the same virtual sinusoid."}],"check":"比較同一虛擬正弦訊號的兩種取樣結果。","checkEn":"Compare two sampling rates for the same virtual sinusoid.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解感測器取樣」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand sensor sampling?","options":["狀態監測需在可比較工作條件下觀察趨勢。","不平衡提供周期激勵，共振則是結構對特定頻率反應放大。","取樣頻率不足可能產生混疊，使低頻假象掩蓋真實振動。"],"optionsEn":["Condition monitoring requires trends under comparable operating conditions.","Imbalance provides periodic excitation; resonance amplifies response near certain frequencies.","Insufficient sampling can alias vibration into misleading lower frequencies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"取樣頻率不足可能產生混疊，使低頻假象掩蓋真實振動。","explanationEn":"Insufficient sampling can alias vibration into misleading lower frequencies."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s04-03","order":3,"title":"建立趨勢基準","titleEn":"Establish a trend baseline","objective":"完成「建立趨勢基準」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for establish a trend baseline.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"狀態監測需在可比較工作條件下觀察趨勢。","textEn":"Condition monitoring requires trends under comparable operating conditions."},{"id":"apache-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為虛擬資料標記工況與量測日期。","textEn":"Annotate virtual data with condition and measurement date."}],"check":"為虛擬資料標記工況與量測日期。","checkEn":"Annotate virtual data with condition and measurement date.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立趨勢基準」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains establish a trend baseline?","options":["取樣頻率不足可能產生混疊，使低頻假象掩蓋真實振動。","狀態監測需在可比較工作條件下觀察趨勢。","不平衡提供周期激勵，共振則是結構對特定頻率反應放大。"],"optionsEn":["Insufficient sampling can alias vibration into misleading lower frequencies.","Condition monitoring requires trends under comparable operating conditions.","Imbalance provides periodic excitation; resonance amplifies response near certain frequencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"狀態監測需在可比較工作條件下觀察趨勢。","explanationEn":"Condition monitoring requires trends under comparable operating conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"apache-s05","order":5,"title":"安全與人因","titleEn":"Safety and human factors","steps":[{"id":"apache-s05-01","order":1,"title":"識別旋轉部件危害","titleEn":"Identify rotating-part hazards","objective":"完成「識別旋轉部件危害」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify rotating-part hazards.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"旋轉件儲存動能，靜態外觀無法反映其運動風險。","textEn":"Rotating components store kinetic energy not apparent from their stationary appearance."},{"id":"apache-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在教學展示中以靜態圖替代裸露高速轉件。","textEn":"Use static diagrams instead of exposed high-speed parts in the display."}],"check":"在教學展示中以靜態圖替代裸露高速轉件。","checkEn":"Use static diagrams instead of exposed high-speed parts in the display.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「識別旋轉部件危害」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify rotating-part hazards?","options":["警示需區分故障、量測失真與通訊中斷，避免錯誤因果。","維護紀錄應包含觀察、來源和處置，不能靠記憶推定完成。","旋轉件儲存動能，靜態外觀無法反映其運動風險。"],"optionsEn":["Warnings should distinguish failure, measurement error and lost communication.","Maintenance records need observations, sources and disposition rather than assumed completion.","Rotating components store kinetic energy not apparent from their stationary appearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"旋轉件儲存動能，靜態外觀無法反映其運動風險。","explanationEn":"Rotating components store kinetic energy not apparent from their stationary appearance."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s05-02","order":2,"title":"分析警示資訊","titleEn":"Analyze warning information","objective":"完成「分析警示資訊」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze warning information.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"警示需區分故障、量測失真與通訊中斷，避免錯誤因果。","textEn":"Warnings should distinguish failure, measurement error and lost communication."},{"id":"apache-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為三類虛擬異常設計不同狀態標籤。","textEn":"Create distinct state labels for three virtual anomaly types."}],"check":"為三類虛擬異常設計不同狀態標籤。","checkEn":"Create distinct state labels for three virtual anomaly types.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析警示資訊」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze warning information?","options":["旋轉件儲存動能，靜態外觀無法反映其運動風險。","警示需區分故障、量測失真與通訊中斷，避免錯誤因果。","維護紀錄應包含觀察、來源和處置，不能靠記憶推定完成。"],"optionsEn":["Rotating components store kinetic energy not apparent from their stationary appearance.","Warnings should distinguish failure, measurement error and lost communication.","Maintenance records need observations, sources and disposition rather than assumed completion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"警示需區分故障、量測失真與通訊中斷，避免錯誤因果。","explanationEn":"Warnings should distinguish failure, measurement error and lost communication."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s05-03","order":3,"title":"建立維護證據","titleEn":"Build maintenance evidence","objective":"完成「建立維護證據」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build maintenance evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"維護紀錄應包含觀察、來源和處置，不能靠記憶推定完成。","textEn":"Maintenance records need observations, sources and disposition rather than assumed completion."},{"id":"apache-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"完成模型檢查清單並保留未完成項目。","textEn":"Complete the model inspection checklist and retain open items."}],"check":"完成模型檢查清單並保留未完成項目。","checkEn":"Complete the model inspection checklist and retain open items.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立維護證據」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build maintenance evidence?","options":["維護紀錄應包含觀察、來源和處置，不能靠記憶推定完成。","旋轉件儲存動能，靜態外觀無法反映其運動風險。","警示需區分故障、量測失真與通訊中斷，避免錯誤因果。"],"optionsEn":["Maintenance records need observations, sources and disposition rather than assumed completion.","Rotating components store kinetic energy not apparent from their stationary appearance.","Warnings should distinguish failure, measurement error and lost communication."],"answer":0,"explanation":"維護紀錄應包含觀察、來源和處置，不能靠記憶推定完成。","explanationEn":"Maintenance records need observations, sources and disposition rather than assumed completion."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"apache-s06","order":6,"title":"模型驗收","titleEn":"Model acceptance","steps":[{"id":"apache-s06-01","order":1,"title":"核對部件接口","titleEn":"Check component interfaces","objective":"完成「核對部件接口」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for check component interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"模型接口需符合幾何相容性，視覺相鄰不代表正確连接。","textEn":"Model interfaces require geometric compatibility; visual proximity is not a valid connection."},{"id":"apache-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"核對三組靜態部件接口與定位標記。","textEn":"Check three static interfaces and their alignment markers."}],"check":"核對三組靜態部件接口與定位標記。","checkEn":"Check three static interfaces and their alignment markers.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「核對部件接口」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains check component interfaces?","options":["教育展示的成功指標是概念清晰和證據可追溯。","模型接口需符合幾何相容性，視覺相鄰不代表正確连接。","能分辨氣動、結構與控制問題，才有合理的系統分工。"],"optionsEn":["A successful educational display makes concepts clear and evidence traceable.","Model interfaces require geometric compatibility; visual proximity is not a valid connection.","Distinguishing aerodynamic, structural and control questions enables sensible system allocation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型接口需符合幾何相容性，視覺相鄰不代表正確连接。","explanationEn":"Model interfaces require geometric compatibility; visual proximity is not a valid connection."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s06-02","order":2,"title":"完成概念測驗","titleEn":"Complete conceptual review","objective":"完成「完成概念測驗」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for complete conceptual review.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"能分辨氣動、結構與控制問題，才有合理的系統分工。","textEn":"Distinguishing aerodynamic, structural and control questions enables sensible system allocation."},{"id":"apache-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"將六個問題分配到正確工程領域。","textEn":"Assign six questions to the correct engineering domains."}],"check":"將六個問題分配到正確工程領域。","checkEn":"Assign six questions to the correct engineering domains.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「完成概念測驗」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains complete conceptual review?","options":["能分辨氣動、結構與控制問題，才有合理的系統分工。","教育展示的成功指標是概念清晰和證據可追溯。","模型接口需符合幾何相容性，視覺相鄰不代表正確连接。"],"optionsEn":["Distinguishing aerodynamic, structural and control questions enables sensible system allocation.","A successful educational display makes concepts clear and evidence traceable.","Model interfaces require geometric compatibility; visual proximity is not a valid connection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"能分辨氣動、結構與控制問題，才有合理的系統分工。","explanationEn":"Distinguishing aerodynamic, structural and control questions enables sensible system allocation."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"apache-s06-03","order":3,"title":"交付非飛行展示","titleEn":"Deliver the non-flying display","objective":"完成「交付非飛行展示」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver the non-flying display.","knowledge":[{"id":"apache-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"教育展示的成功指標是概念清晰和證據可追溯。","textEn":"A successful educational display makes concepts clear and evidence traceable."},{"id":"apache-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交方塊圖與學習紀錄，標明不能用於飛行。","textEn":"Submit the block diagram and learning record, labeled unsuitable for flight."}],"check":"提交方塊圖與學習紀錄，標明不能用於飛行。","checkEn":"Submit the block diagram and learning record, labeled unsuitable for flight.","sourceIds":["faa-helicopter"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付非飛行展示」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver the non-flying display?","options":["模型接口需符合幾何相容性，視覺相鄰不代表正確连接。","能分辨氣動、結構與控制問題，才有合理的系統分工。","教育展示的成功指標是概念清晰和證據可追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Model interfaces require geometric compatibility; visual proximity is not a valid connection.","Distinguishing aerodynamic, structural and control questions enables sensible system allocation.","A successful educational display makes concepts clear and evidence traceable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教育展示的成功指標是概念清晰和證據可追溯。","explanationEn":"A successful educational display makes concepts clear and evidence traceable."},"prerequisiteIds":["apache-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course"},{"id":"submarine","title":"國造潛艦案例與水下載具工程","titleEn":"Submarine Context and Underwater Vehicle Engineering","category":"marine","summary":"以浮力、壓力與生命安全概念認識水下載具；採用民用研究潛器資料及不加壓桌面示意模型。","summaryEn":"Study underwater vehicles through buoyancy, pressure and life safety using civilian research-submersible sources and unpressurized desktop models.","scope":"民用水下載具與常壓模型概念；不含武器、匿蹤、軍用作戰系統、耐壓艙製造或載人下潛指示。","scopeEn":"Civilian underwater-vehicle and open-tank model concepts; excludes weapons, stealth, military operational systems, pressure-hull fabrication and crewed diving instructions.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["whoi-safety","v10-other-vendor-submarine"],"diagram":{"type":"submarine","labels":["外形","浮力","艙體","能源","監測"],"labelsEn":["Shape","Buoyancy","Hull","Energy","Monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"submarine-s01","order":1,"title":"任務與功能","titleEn":"Purpose and functions","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s01-01","order":1,"title":"區分水面與水下浮態","titleEn":"Distinguish surface and submerged buoyancy","objective":"完成「區分水面與水下浮態」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish surface and submerged buoyancy.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"浮力等於排開流體的重量，完全浸沒時體積變化與密度變化都重要。","textEn":"Buoyancy equals displaced-fluid weight; volume and density changes matter when fully submerged."},{"id":"submarine-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以常壓容器中的密封浮體比較浮起與下沉。","textEn":"Compare floating and sinking sealed objects in an unpressurized container."}],"check":"以常壓容器中的密封浮體比較浮起與下沉。","checkEn":"Compare floating and sinking sealed objects in an unpressurized container.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分水面與水下浮態」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish surface and submerged buoyancy?","options":["浮力等於排開流體的重量，完全浸沒時體積變化與密度變化都重要。","觀測、取樣與回收是民用研究潛器的系統任務。","零件質量、排水量及配置共同決定整體浮態。"],"optionsEn":["Buoyancy equals displaced-fluid weight; volume and density changes matter when fully submerged.","Observation, sampling and recovery are system functions of civilian research submersibles.","Component mass, displaced volume and placement jointly determine buoyancy state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"浮力等於排開流體的重量，完全浸沒時體積變化與密度變化都重要。","explanationEn":"Buoyancy equals displaced-fluid weight; volume and density changes matter when fully submerged."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s01-02","order":2,"title":"定義民用教學載具","titleEn":"Define a civilian learning vehicle","objective":"完成「定義民用教學載具」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define a civilian learning vehicle.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"觀測、取樣與回收是民用研究潛器的系統任務。","textEn":"Observation, sampling and recovery are system functions of civilian research submersibles."},{"id":"submarine-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出觀測與回收功能，不引入武裝或匿蹤功能。","textEn":"Diagram observation and recovery functions without weapons or stealth functions."}],"check":"畫出觀測與回收功能，不引入武裝或匿蹤功能。","checkEn":"Diagram observation and recovery functions without weapons or stealth functions.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「定義民用教學載具」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define a civilian learning vehicle?","options":["零件質量、排水量及配置共同決定整體浮態。","浮力等於排開流體的重量，完全浸沒時體積變化與密度變化都重要。","觀測、取樣與回收是民用研究潛器的系統任務。"],"optionsEn":["Component mass, displaced volume and placement jointly determine buoyancy state.","Buoyancy equals displaced-fluid weight; volume and density changes matter when fully submerged.","Observation, sampling and recovery are system functions of civilian research submersibles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"觀測、取樣與回收是民用研究潛器的系統任務。","explanationEn":"Observation, sampling and recovery are system functions of civilian research submersibles."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s01-03","order":3,"title":"建立質量清單","titleEn":"Build a mass list","objective":"完成「建立質量清單」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a mass list.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"零件質量、排水量及配置共同決定整體浮態。","textEn":"Component mass, displaced volume and placement jointly determine buoyancy state."},{"id":"submarine-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立桌面模型各部件的質量與體積表。","textEn":"Create a component mass and volume table for a desktop model."}],"check":"建立桌面模型各部件的質量與體積表。","checkEn":"Create a component mass and volume table for a desktop model.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立質量清單」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a mass list?","options":["觀測、取樣與回收是民用研究潛器的系統任務。","零件質量、排水量及配置共同決定整體浮態。","浮力等於排開流體的重量，完全浸沒時體積變化與密度變化都重要。"],"optionsEn":["Observation, sampling and recovery are system functions of civilian research submersibles.","Component mass, displaced volume and placement jointly determine buoyancy state.","Buoyancy equals displaced-fluid weight; volume and density changes matter when fully submerged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"零件質量、排水量及配置共同決定整體浮態。","explanationEn":"Component mass, displaced volume and placement jointly determine buoyancy state."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"submarine-s02","order":2,"title":"浮力與穩定性","titleEn":"Buoyancy and stability","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s02-01","order":1,"title":"比較正負與中性浮力","titleEn":"Compare buoyancy states","objective":"完成「比較正負與中性浮力」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare buoyancy states.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"重量與浮力大小關係決定浮起、下沉或近中性狀態。","textEn":"The relation between weight and buoyancy determines rising, sinking or near-neutral behavior."},{"id":"submarine-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"計算無單位示意例子的淨向上力。","textEn":"Calculate net upward force in a dimensionless illustrative example."}],"check":"計算無單位示意例子的淨向上力。","checkEn":"Calculate net upward force in a dimensionless illustrative example.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較正負與中性浮力」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare buoyancy states?","options":["重心由質量分布決定，浮心由排水體積分布決定。","浮力與重力作用線的相對位置會形成恢復或翻轉力矩。","重量與浮力大小關係決定浮起、下沉或近中性狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Center of gravity follows mass distribution; center of buoyancy follows displaced volume.","Relative lines of action of weight and buoyancy can create restoring or overturning moments.","The relation between weight and buoyancy determines rising, sinking or near-neutral behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重量與浮力大小關係決定浮起、下沉或近中性狀態。","explanationEn":"The relation between weight and buoyancy determines rising, sinking or near-neutral behavior."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s02-02","order":2,"title":"區分重心與浮心","titleEn":"Distinguish mass and buoyancy centers","objective":"完成「區分重心與浮心」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish mass and buoyancy centers.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"重心由質量分布決定，浮心由排水體積分布決定。","textEn":"Center of gravity follows mass distribution; center of buoyancy follows displaced volume."},{"id":"submarine-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在模型截面標出兩者並說明位置差異。","textEn":"Mark both centers in the model section and explain the difference."}],"check":"在模型截面標出兩者並說明位置差異。","checkEn":"Mark both centers in the model section and explain the difference.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分重心與浮心」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish mass and buoyancy centers?","options":["重量與浮力大小關係決定浮起、下沉或近中性狀態。","重心由質量分布決定，浮心由排水體積分布決定。","浮力與重力作用線的相對位置會形成恢復或翻轉力矩。"],"optionsEn":["The relation between weight and buoyancy determines rising, sinking or near-neutral behavior.","Center of gravity follows mass distribution; center of buoyancy follows displaced volume.","Relative lines of action of weight and buoyancy can create restoring or overturning moments."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重心由質量分布決定，浮心由排水體積分布決定。","explanationEn":"Center of gravity follows mass distribution; center of buoyancy follows displaced volume."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s02-03","order":3,"title":"觀察姿態恢復","titleEn":"Observe restoring tendency","objective":"完成「觀察姿態恢復」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for observe restoring tendency.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"浮力與重力作用線的相對位置會形成恢復或翻轉力矩。","textEn":"Relative lines of action of weight and buoyancy can create restoring or overturning moments."},{"id":"submarine-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在小型常壓水槽中只觀察模型的定性姿態。","textEn":"Observe only qualitative model attitude in a small open tank."}],"check":"在小型常壓水槽中只觀察模型的定性姿態。","checkEn":"Observe only qualitative model attitude in a small open tank.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「觀察姿態恢復」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains observe restoring tendency?","options":["浮力與重力作用線的相對位置會形成恢復或翻轉力矩。","重量與浮力大小關係決定浮起、下沉或近中性狀態。","重心由質量分布決定，浮心由排水體積分布決定。"],"optionsEn":["Relative lines of action of weight and buoyancy can create restoring or overturning moments.","The relation between weight and buoyancy determines rising, sinking or near-neutral behavior.","Center of gravity follows mass distribution; center of buoyancy follows displaced volume."],"answer":0,"explanation":"浮力與重力作用線的相對位置會形成恢復或翻轉力矩。","explanationEn":"Relative lines of action of weight and buoyancy can create restoring or overturning moments."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"submarine-s03","order":3,"title":"壓力概念與界面","titleEn":"Pressure concepts and interfaces","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s03-01","order":1,"title":"理解靜水壓","titleEn":"Understand hydrostatic pressure","objective":"完成「理解靜水壓」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand hydrostatic pressure.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"靜水壓隨密度、重力加速度及深度增加，絕對壓力還包括表面壓力。","textEn":"Hydrostatic pressure rises with density, gravity and depth; absolute pressure includes surface pressure."},{"id":"submarine-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用符號 p = p0 + ρgh 標出各項與單位。","textEn":"Label terms and units in p = p0 + ρgh."}],"check":"用符號 p = p0 + ρgh 標出各項與單位。","checkEn":"Label terms and units in p = p0 + ρgh.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解靜水壓」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand hydrostatic pressure?","options":["每個開口與穿艙連接都增加密封及檢查需求。","靜水壓隨密度、重力加速度及深度增加，絕對壓力還包括表面壓力。","外壓下的殼體可能因失穩而破壞，不能只用拉伸強度推論安全。"],"optionsEn":["Each opening and penetration adds sealing and inspection requirements.","Hydrostatic pressure rises with density, gravity and depth; absolute pressure includes surface pressure.","A shell under external pressure can fail by instability, so tensile strength alone cannot prove safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜水壓隨密度、重力加速度及深度增加，絕對壓力還包括表面壓力。","explanationEn":"Hydrostatic pressure rises with density, gravity and depth; absolute pressure includes surface pressure."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s03-02","order":2,"title":"辨識外壓失穩","titleEn":"Identify external-pressure instability","objective":"完成「辨識外壓失穩」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify external-pressure instability.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"外壓下的殼體可能因失穩而破壞，不能只用拉伸強度推論安全。","textEn":"A shell under external pressure can fail by instability, so tensile strength alone cannot prove safety."},{"id":"submarine-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以無尺寸示意圖區分材料破壞與殼體失穩。","textEn":"Distinguish material failure from shell instability in a dimensionless sketch."}],"check":"以無尺寸示意圖區分材料破壞與殼體失穩。","checkEn":"Distinguish material failure from shell instability in a dimensionless sketch.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識外壓失穩」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify external-pressure instability?","options":["外壓下的殼體可能因失穩而破壞，不能只用拉伸強度推論安全。","每個開口與穿艙連接都增加密封及檢查需求。","靜水壓隨密度、重力加速度及深度增加，絕對壓力還包括表面壓力。"],"optionsEn":["A shell under external pressure can fail by instability, so tensile strength alone cannot prove safety.","Each opening and penetration adds sealing and inspection requirements.","Hydrostatic pressure rises with density, gravity and depth; absolute pressure includes surface pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外壓下的殼體可能因失穩而破壞，不能只用拉伸強度推論安全。","explanationEn":"A shell under external pressure can fail by instability, so tensile strength alone cannot prove safety."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s03-03","order":3,"title":"建立穿艙介面概念","titleEn":"Map hull interfaces","objective":"完成「建立穿艙介面概念」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map hull interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"每個開口與穿艙連接都增加密封及檢查需求。","textEn":"Each opening and penetration adds sealing and inspection requirements."},{"id":"submarine-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意圖上列出需檢查的接口類型，不設計實體耐壓件。","textEn":"List interface types needing inspection without designing pressure hardware."}],"check":"在示意圖上列出需檢查的接口類型，不設計實體耐壓件。","checkEn":"List interface types needing inspection without designing pressure hardware.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立穿艙介面概念」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map hull interfaces?","options":["靜水壓隨密度、重力加速度及深度增加，絕對壓力還包括表面壓力。","外壓下的殼體可能因失穩而破壞，不能只用拉伸強度推論安全。","每個開口與穿艙連接都增加密封及檢查需求。"],"optionsEn":["Hydrostatic pressure rises with density, gravity and depth; absolute pressure includes surface pressure.","A shell under external pressure can fail by instability, so tensile strength alone cannot prove safety.","Each opening and penetration adds sealing and inspection requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每個開口與穿艙連接都增加密封及檢查需求。","explanationEn":"Each opening and penetration adds sealing and inspection requirements."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"submarine-s04","order":4,"title":"能源與環境","titleEn":"Energy and environment","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s04-01","order":1,"title":"分解能源需求","titleEn":"Decompose energy needs","objective":"完成「分解能源需求」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for decompose energy needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"推进、感測、運算與環境維持會競爭有限能源。","textEn":"Propulsion, sensing, computation and environmental support compete for finite energy."},{"id":"submarine-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立純教學功率預算並注明假設數值。","textEn":"Create a teaching power budget with clearly labeled assumptions."}],"check":"建立純教學功率預算並注明假設數值。","checkEn":"Create a teaching power budget with clearly labeled assumptions.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分解能源需求」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains decompose energy needs?","options":["推进、感測、運算與環境維持會競爭有限能源。","電子設備產熱需經導熱與外界換熱排出，封閉空間仍需熱分析。","載人空間的環境監測屬生命安全系統，需要獨立設計與驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Propulsion, sensing, computation and environmental support compete for finite energy.","Electronic heat must leave through conduction and external heat transfer even in an enclosed volume.","Environmental monitoring in a crewed space is a life-safety system needing independent design and verification."],"answer":0,"explanation":"推进、感測、運算與環境維持會競爭有限能源。","explanationEn":"Propulsion, sensing, computation and environmental support compete for finite energy."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解散熱路徑","titleEn":"Understand heat paths","objective":"完成「理解散熱路徑」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand heat paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"電子設備產熱需經導熱與外界換熱排出，封閉空間仍需熱分析。","textEn":"Electronic heat must leave through conduction and external heat transfer even in an enclosed volume."},{"id":"submarine-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出元件到外界的概念熱阻鏈。","textEn":"Mark a conceptual thermal-resistance chain to the environment."}],"check":"標出元件到外界的概念熱阻鏈。","checkEn":"Mark a conceptual thermal-resistance chain to the environment.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解散熱路徑」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand heat paths?","options":["載人空間的環境監測屬生命安全系統，需要獨立設計與驗證。","推进、感測、運算與環境維持會競爭有限能源。","電子設備產熱需經導熱與外界換熱排出，封閉空間仍需熱分析。"],"optionsEn":["Environmental monitoring in a crewed space is a life-safety system needing independent design and verification.","Propulsion, sensing, computation and environmental support compete for finite energy.","Electronic heat must leave through conduction and external heat transfer even in an enclosed volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電子設備產熱需經導熱與外界換熱排出，封閉空間仍需熱分析。","explanationEn":"Electronic heat must leave through conduction and external heat transfer even in an enclosed volume."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s04-03","order":3,"title":"辨識環境監測目的","titleEn":"Identify environmental monitoring","objective":"完成「辨識環境監測目的」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify environmental monitoring.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"載人空間的環境監測屬生命安全系統，需要獨立設計與驗證。","textEn":"Environmental monitoring in a crewed space is a life-safety system needing independent design and verification."},{"id":"submarine-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"只列監測量及異常資訊流，不提供載人建造指示。","textEn":"List monitored quantities and alarm information flow without crewed construction instructions."}],"check":"只列監測量及異常資訊流，不提供載人建造指示。","checkEn":"List monitored quantities and alarm information flow without crewed construction instructions.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識環境監測目的」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify environmental monitoring?","options":["電子設備產熱需經導熱與外界換熱排出，封閉空間仍需熱分析。","載人空間的環境監測屬生命安全系統，需要獨立設計與驗證。","推进、感測、運算與環境維持會競爭有限能源。"],"optionsEn":["Electronic heat must leave through conduction and external heat transfer even in an enclosed volume.","Environmental monitoring in a crewed space is a life-safety system needing independent design and verification.","Propulsion, sensing, computation and environmental support compete for finite energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"載人空間的環境監測屬生命安全系統，需要獨立設計與驗證。","explanationEn":"Environmental monitoring in a crewed space is a life-safety system needing independent design and verification."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"submarine-s05","order":5,"title":"可靠度與回收","titleEn":"Reliability and recovery","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s05-01","order":1,"title":"分析共同失效","titleEn":"Analyze common-cause failures","objective":"完成「分析共同失效」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze common-cause failures.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"共用能源或通訊可能使多個看似獨立的系統同時失效。","textEn":"Shared power or communication can defeat apparently independent systems together."},{"id":"submarine-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在概念圖標記共用節點與依賴關係。","textEn":"Mark shared nodes and dependencies in a conceptual diagram."}],"check":"在概念圖標記共用節點與依賴關係。","checkEn":"Mark shared nodes and dependencies in a conceptual diagram.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析共同失效」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze common-cause failures?","options":["民用潛器需將定位、回收與安全狀態視為整體任務的一部分。","反覆使用的設備需要比對基準紀錄與變化。","共用能源或通訊可能使多個看似獨立的系統同時失效。"],"optionsEn":["Civilian submersibles include location, recovery and safe state as part of the overall mission.","Repeatedly used equipment needs comparison with baseline records and changes.","Shared power or communication can defeat apparently independent systems together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用能源或通訊可能使多個看似獨立的系統同時失效。","explanationEn":"Shared power or communication can defeat apparently independent systems together."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s05-02","order":2,"title":"建立回收功能","titleEn":"Define recovery functions","objective":"完成「建立回收功能」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define recovery functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"民用潛器需將定位、回收與安全狀態視為整體任務的一部分。","textEn":"Civilian submersibles include location, recovery and safe state as part of the overall mission."},{"id":"submarine-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為桌面模型設計清楚的人工取回方式。","textEn":"Define a clear manual retrieval method for the desktop model."}],"check":"為桌面模型設計清楚的人工取回方式。","checkEn":"Define a clear manual retrieval method for the desktop model.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立回收功能」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define recovery functions?","options":["共用能源或通訊可能使多個看似獨立的系統同時失效。","民用潛器需將定位、回收與安全狀態視為整體任務的一部分。","反覆使用的設備需要比對基準紀錄與變化。"],"optionsEn":["Shared power or communication can defeat apparently independent systems together.","Civilian submersibles include location, recovery and safe state as part of the overall mission.","Repeatedly used equipment needs comparison with baseline records and changes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"民用潛器需將定位、回收與安全狀態視為整體任務的一部分。","explanationEn":"Civilian submersibles include location, recovery and safe state as part of the overall mission."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s05-03","order":3,"title":"規劃檢查紀錄","titleEn":"Plan inspection records","objective":"完成「規劃檢查紀錄」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan inspection records.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"反覆使用的設備需要比對基準紀錄與變化。","textEn":"Repeatedly used equipment needs comparison with baseline records and changes."},{"id":"submarine-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為模型每次展示記錄外觀、浮態與異常。","textEn":"Record appearance, buoyancy state and anomalies at each demonstration."}],"check":"為模型每次展示記錄外觀、浮態與異常。","checkEn":"Record appearance, buoyancy state and anomalies at each demonstration.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃檢查紀錄」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan inspection records?","options":["反覆使用的設備需要比對基準紀錄與變化。","共用能源或通訊可能使多個看似獨立的系統同時失效。","民用潛器需將定位、回收與安全狀態視為整體任務的一部分。"],"optionsEn":["Repeatedly used equipment needs comparison with baseline records and changes.","Shared power or communication can defeat apparently independent systems together.","Civilian submersibles include location, recovery and safe state as part of the overall mission."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反覆使用的設備需要比對基準紀錄與變化。","explanationEn":"Repeatedly used equipment needs comparison with baseline records and changes."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"submarine-s06","order":6,"title":"教育模型驗收","titleEn":"Educational model acceptance","steps":[{"id":"submarine-s06-01","order":1,"title":"核對浮力預測","titleEn":"Check buoyancy predictions","objective":"完成「核對浮力預測」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for check buoyancy predictions.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"實測與計算差異可能來自體積估算、附著氣泡或材料吸水。","textEn":"Prediction differences may arise from volume estimates, attached bubbles or water absorption."},{"id":"submarine-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"解釋模型兩次量測不一致的可能原因。","textEn":"Explain possible causes of disagreement between two model measurements."}],"check":"解釋模型兩次量測不一致的可能原因。","checkEn":"Explain possible causes of disagreement between two model measurements.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「核對浮力預測」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains check buoyancy predictions?","options":["安全的教育成果應明確區分常壓模型與真實耐壓載具。","實測與計算差異可能來自體積估算、附著氣泡或材料吸水。","民用研究潛器的特定認證資料不能直接轉用為其他載具的設計依據。"],"optionsEn":["Educational results must clearly distinguish an open-tank model from a real pressure-rated vehicle.","Prediction differences may arise from volume estimates, attached bubbles or water absorption.","Certification data for one civilian submersible cannot be directly reused to design another vehicle."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實測與計算差異可能來自體積估算、附著氣泡或材料吸水。","explanationEn":"Prediction differences may arise from volume estimates, attached bubbles or water absorption."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s06-02","order":2,"title":"檢查資料可信度","titleEn":"Review evidence quality","objective":"完成「檢查資料可信度」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for review evidence quality.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"民用研究潛器的特定認證資料不能直接轉用為其他載具的設計依據。","textEn":"Certification data for one civilian submersible cannot be directly reused to design another vehicle."},{"id":"submarine-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在報告區分一般原理與特定載具資料。","textEn":"Separate general principles from vehicle-specific data in the report."}],"check":"在報告區分一般原理與特定載具資料。","checkEn":"Separate general principles from vehicle-specific data in the report.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「檢查資料可信度」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains review evidence quality?","options":["民用研究潛器的特定認證資料不能直接轉用為其他載具的設計依據。","安全的教育成果應明確區分常壓模型與真實耐壓載具。","實測與計算差異可能來自體積估算、附著氣泡或材料吸水。"],"optionsEn":["Certification data for one civilian submersible cannot be directly reused to design another vehicle.","Educational results must clearly distinguish an open-tank model from a real pressure-rated vehicle.","Prediction differences may arise from volume estimates, attached bubbles or water absorption."],"answer":0,"explanation":"民用研究潛器的特定認證資料不能直接轉用為其他載具的設計依據。","explanationEn":"Certification data for one civilian submersible cannot be directly reused to design another vehicle."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"submarine-s06-03","order":3,"title":"完成學習交付","titleEn":"Complete learning handover","objective":"完成「完成學習交付」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for complete learning handover.","knowledge":[{"id":"submarine-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"安全的教育成果應明確區分常壓模型與真實耐壓載具。","textEn":"Educational results must clearly distinguish an open-tank model from a real pressure-rated vehicle."},{"id":"submarine-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交浮力模型、系統圖與未涵蓋的驗證清單。","textEn":"Submit the buoyancy model, system diagram and excluded verification tasks."}],"check":"提交浮力模型、系統圖與未涵蓋的驗證清單。","checkEn":"Submit the buoyancy model, system diagram and excluded verification tasks.","sourceIds":["whoi-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「完成學習交付」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains complete learning handover?","options":["實測與計算差異可能來自體積估算、附著氣泡或材料吸水。","民用研究潛器的特定認證資料不能直接轉用為其他載具的設計依據。","安全的教育成果應明確區分常壓模型與真實耐壓載具。"],"optionsEn":["Prediction differences may arise from volume estimates, attached bubbles or water absorption.","Certification data for one civilian submersible cannot be directly reused to design another vehicle.","Educational results must clearly distinguish an open-tank model from a real pressure-rated vehicle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安全的教育成果應明確區分常壓模型與真實耐壓載具。","explanationEn":"Educational results must clearly distinguish an open-tank model from a real pressure-rated vehicle."},"prerequisiteIds":["submarine-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course"},{"id":"danjiang","title":"淡江大橋工程","titleEn":"Danjiang Bridge Engineering","category":"structures","summary":"以單塔不對稱斜張橋認識載荷路徑、施工階段、耐久性及長期監測。","summaryEn":"Study load paths, construction stages, durability and monitoring through a single-pylon asymmetric cable-stayed bridge.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang","v10-other-vendor-danjiang","v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"diagram":{"type":"bridge","labels":["地盤","基礎","主塔","斜索","橋面"],"labelsEn":["Ground","Foundation","Pylon","Cables","Deck"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"danjiang-s01","order":1,"title":"需求與場址","titleEn":"Requirements and site","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s01-01","order":1,"title":"界定交通與環境需求","titleEn":"Define transport and environmental needs","objective":"完成「界定交通與環境需求」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define transport and environmental needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"橋梁服務需求包括交通、航道與環境，不能只以跨距衡量。","textEn":"Bridge requirements include traffic, navigation and environment, not span alone."},{"id":"danjiang-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立各需求對應的利害關係人與證據。","textEn":"Map stakeholders and evidence to each requirement."}],"check":"建立各需求對應的利害關係人與證據。","checkEn":"Map stakeholders and evidence to each requirement.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「界定交通與環境需求」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define transport and environmental needs?","options":["橋梁服務需求包括交通、航道與環境，不能只以跨距衡量。","地形、地質、水文與風場會影響結構選型。","主橋、引道與基礎的介面需要一致的座標和標高。"],"optionsEn":["Bridge requirements include traffic, navigation and environment, not span alone.","Topography, geology, hydrology and wind influence structural choices.","Main span, approaches and foundations need consistent coordinates and elevations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"橋梁服務需求包括交通、航道與環境，不能只以跨距衡量。","explanationEn":"Bridge requirements include traffic, navigation and environment, not span alone."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s01-02","order":2,"title":"閱讀場址資料","titleEn":"Read site data","objective":"完成「閱讀場址資料」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for read site data.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"地形、地質、水文與風場會影響結構選型。","textEn":"Topography, geology, hydrology and wind influence structural choices."},{"id":"danjiang-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在場址示意圖標出四種資料來源。","textEn":"Mark four data sources on a site schematic."}],"check":"在場址示意圖標出四種資料來源。","checkEn":"Mark four data sources on a site schematic.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「閱讀場址資料」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains read site data?","options":["主橋、引道與基礎的介面需要一致的座標和標高。","橋梁服務需求包括交通、航道與環境，不能只以跨距衡量。","地形、地質、水文與風場會影響結構選型。"],"optionsEn":["Main span, approaches and foundations need consistent coordinates and elevations.","Bridge requirements include traffic, navigation and environment, not span alone.","Topography, geology, hydrology and wind influence structural choices."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地形、地質、水文與風場會影響結構選型。","explanationEn":"Topography, geology, hydrology and wind influence structural choices."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s01-03","order":3,"title":"建立系統邊界","titleEn":"Set system boundaries","objective":"完成「建立系統邊界」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for set system boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"主橋、引道與基礎的介面需要一致的座標和標高。","textEn":"Main span, approaches and foundations need consistent coordinates and elevations."},{"id":"danjiang-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"核對概念模型的基準點與單位。","textEn":"Check reference points and units in the conceptual model."}],"check":"核對概念模型的基準點與單位。","checkEn":"Check reference points and units in the conceptual model.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立系統邊界」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains set system boundaries?","options":["地形、地質、水文與風場會影響結構選型。","主橋、引道與基礎的介面需要一致的座標和標高。","橋梁服務需求包括交通、航道與環境，不能只以跨距衡量。"],"optionsEn":["Topography, geology, hydrology and wind influence structural choices.","Main span, approaches and foundations need consistent coordinates and elevations.","Bridge requirements include traffic, navigation and environment, not span alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主橋、引道與基礎的介面需要一致的座標和標高。","explanationEn":"Main span, approaches and foundations need consistent coordinates and elevations."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-s02","order":2,"title":"基礎與地盤","titleEn":"Foundations and ground","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解地盤承載","titleEn":"Understand ground support","objective":"完成「理解地盤承載」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand ground support.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"基礎把結構載荷傳到地盤，承載力和變形都需考慮。","textEn":"Foundations transfer loads to ground; both capacity and deformation matter."},{"id":"danjiang-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出塔柱到地盤的載荷路徑。","textEn":"Draw the load path from pylon to ground."}],"check":"畫出塔柱到地盤的載荷路徑。","checkEn":"Draw the load path from pylon to ground.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解地盤承載」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand ground support?","options":["水流可能改變橋墩周圍河床，影響有效支承條件。","施工期間的位移及地下水變化可提供地盤反應證據。","基礎把結構載荷傳到地盤，承載力和變形都需考慮。"],"optionsEn":["Flow can alter the bed around piers and affect support conditions.","Displacement and groundwater changes provide evidence of ground response during construction.","Foundations transfer loads to ground; both capacity and deformation matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基礎把結構載荷傳到地盤，承載力和變形都需考慮。","explanationEn":"Foundations transfer loads to ground; both capacity and deformation matter."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s02-02","order":2,"title":"分析水流沖刷","titleEn":"Analyze scour conceptually","objective":"完成「分析水流沖刷」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze scour conceptually.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"水流可能改變橋墩周圍河床，影響有效支承條件。","textEn":"Flow can alter the bed around piers and affect support conditions."},{"id":"danjiang-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出需長期觀測的河床區域。","textEn":"Mark riverbed areas needing long-term observation."}],"check":"標出需長期觀測的河床區域。","checkEn":"Mark riverbed areas needing long-term observation.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析水流沖刷」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze scour conceptually?","options":["基礎把結構載荷傳到地盤，承載力和變形都需考慮。","水流可能改變橋墩周圍河床，影響有效支承條件。","施工期間的位移及地下水變化可提供地盤反應證據。"],"optionsEn":["Foundations transfer loads to ground; both capacity and deformation matter.","Flow can alter the bed around piers and affect support conditions.","Displacement and groundwater changes provide evidence of ground response during construction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水流可能改變橋墩周圍河床，影響有效支承條件。","explanationEn":"Flow can alter the bed around piers and affect support conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s02-03","order":3,"title":"建立施工監測點","titleEn":"Plan construction monitoring","objective":"完成「建立施工監測點」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan construction monitoring.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"施工期間的位移及地下水變化可提供地盤反應證據。","textEn":"Displacement and groundwater changes provide evidence of ground response during construction."},{"id":"danjiang-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立量測量、頻率概念及異常處置欄位。","textEn":"Define measurement, sampling concept and anomaly-response fields."}],"check":"建立量測量、頻率概念及異常處置欄位。","checkEn":"Define measurement, sampling concept and anomaly-response fields.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立施工監測點」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan construction monitoring?","options":["施工期間的位移及地下水變化可提供地盤反應證據。","基礎把結構載荷傳到地盤，承載力和變形都需考慮。","水流可能改變橋墩周圍河床，影響有效支承條件。"],"optionsEn":["Displacement and groundwater changes provide evidence of ground response during construction.","Foundations transfer loads to ground; both capacity and deformation matter.","Flow can alter the bed around piers and affect support conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工期間的位移及地下水變化可提供地盤反應證據。","explanationEn":"Displacement and groundwater changes provide evidence of ground response during construction."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-s03","order":3,"title":"主塔與橋面","titleEn":"Pylon and deck","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s03-01","order":1,"title":"辨識斜張受力","titleEn":"Identify cable-stayed load paths","objective":"完成「辨識斜張受力」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify cable-stayed load paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"橋面載荷經斜索傳到主塔和基礎，索力與幾何相互關聯。","textEn":"Deck loads pass through stays to pylon and foundations; cable force and geometry interact."},{"id":"danjiang-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在原創示意圖標出力的方向。","textEn":"Mark force directions on an original schematic."}],"check":"在原創示意圖標出力的方向。","checkEn":"Mark force directions on an original schematic.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識斜張受力」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify cable-stayed load paths?","options":["車流反覆載荷使接頭與細節的疲勞成為耐久議題。","橋面載荷經斜索傳到主塔和基礎，索力與幾何相互關聯。","不對稱跨徑需要整體平衡分析，不能只把兩側當相同結構。"],"optionsEn":["Repeated traffic loading makes fatigue at joints and details a durability issue.","Deck loads pass through stays to pylon and foundations; cable force and geometry interact.","Asymmetric spans require overall equilibrium rather than identical treatment of both sides."],"answer":1,"explanation":"橋面載荷經斜索傳到主塔和基礎，索力與幾何相互關聯。","explanationEn":"Deck loads pass through stays to pylon and foundations; cable force and geometry interact."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s03-02","order":2,"title":"比較不對稱配置","titleEn":"Compare asymmetric layouts","objective":"完成「比較不對稱配置」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare asymmetric layouts.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"不對稱跨徑需要整體平衡分析，不能只把兩側當相同結構。","textEn":"Asymmetric spans require overall equilibrium rather than identical treatment of both sides."},{"id":"danjiang-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較左右跨的概念載荷與支承。","textEn":"Compare conceptual loading and supports of the two spans."}],"check":"比較左右跨的概念載荷與支承。","checkEn":"Compare conceptual loading and supports of the two spans.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較不對稱配置」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare asymmetric layouts?","options":["不對稱跨徑需要整體平衡分析，不能只把兩側當相同結構。","車流反覆載荷使接頭與細節的疲勞成為耐久議題。","橋面載荷經斜索傳到主塔和基礎，索力與幾何相互關聯。"],"optionsEn":["Asymmetric spans require overall equilibrium rather than identical treatment of both sides.","Repeated traffic loading makes fatigue at joints and details a durability issue.","Deck loads pass through stays to pylon and foundations; cable force and geometry interact."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不對稱跨徑需要整體平衡分析，不能只把兩側當相同結構。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric spans require overall equilibrium rather than identical treatment of both sides."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s03-03","order":3,"title":"理解鋼橋面疲勞","titleEn":"Understand steel-deck fatigue","objective":"完成「理解鋼橋面疲勞」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand steel-deck fatigue.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"車流反覆載荷使接頭與細節的疲勞成為耐久議題。","textEn":"Repeated traffic loading makes fatigue at joints and details a durability issue."},{"id":"danjiang-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出應檢查的局部細節而非只看最大應力。","textEn":"Identify local details needing inspection beyond peak stress."}],"check":"標出應檢查的局部細節而非只看最大應力。","checkEn":"Identify local details needing inspection beyond peak stress.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解鋼橋面疲勞」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand steel-deck fatigue?","options":["橋面載荷經斜索傳到主塔和基礎，索力與幾何相互關聯。","不對稱跨徑需要整體平衡分析，不能只把兩側當相同結構。","車流反覆載荷使接頭與細節的疲勞成為耐久議題。"],"optionsEn":["Deck loads pass through stays to pylon and foundations; cable force and geometry interact.","Asymmetric spans require overall equilibrium rather than identical treatment of both sides.","Repeated traffic loading makes fatigue at joints and details a durability issue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"車流反覆載荷使接頭與細節的疲勞成為耐久議題。","explanationEn":"Repeated traffic loading makes fatigue at joints and details a durability issue."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-s04","order":4,"title":"施工階段概念","titleEn":"Construction-stage concepts","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s04-01","order":1,"title":"安排節塊順序","titleEn":"Sequence conceptual segments","objective":"完成「安排節塊順序」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for sequence conceptual segments.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"施工中的結構系統會變化，完成狀態安全不代表每個階段都安全。","textEn":"The structural system changes during construction; final safety does not prove stage safety."},{"id":"danjiang-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用桌面模型比較三個中間狀態。","textEn":"Compare three intermediate states with a desktop model."}],"check":"用桌面模型比較三個中間狀態。","checkEn":"Compare three intermediate states with a desktop model.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「安排節塊順序」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains sequence conceptual segments?","options":["施工中的結構系統會變化，完成狀態安全不代表每個階段都安全。","臨時支承承擔未完成結構的載荷，移除會改變受力。","溫度、變形與累積誤差會影響合龍位置。"],"optionsEn":["The structural system changes during construction; final safety does not prove stage safety.","Temporary supports carry incomplete structures; removal changes the load distribution.","Temperature, deformation and accumulated error affect closure alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工中的結構系統會變化，完成狀態安全不代表每個階段都安全。","explanationEn":"The structural system changes during construction; final safety does not prove stage safety."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解臨時支承","titleEn":"Understand temporary support","objective":"完成「理解臨時支承」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand temporary support.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"臨時支承承擔未完成結構的載荷，移除會改變受力。","textEn":"Temporary supports carry incomplete structures; removal changes the load distribution."},{"id":"danjiang-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出移除支承前後的受力差異。","textEn":"Draw load differences before and after support removal."}],"check":"畫出移除支承前後的受力差異。","checkEn":"Draw load differences before and after support removal.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解臨時支承」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand temporary support?","options":["溫度、變形與累積誤差會影響合龍位置。","施工中的結構系統會變化，完成狀態安全不代表每個階段都安全。","臨時支承承擔未完成結構的載荷，移除會改變受力。"],"optionsEn":["Temperature, deformation and accumulated error affect closure alignment.","The structural system changes during construction; final safety does not prove stage safety.","Temporary supports carry incomplete structures; removal changes the load distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"臨時支承承擔未完成結構的載荷，移除會改變受力。","explanationEn":"Temporary supports carry incomplete structures; removal changes the load distribution."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s04-03","order":3,"title":"核對合龍幾何","titleEn":"Check closure geometry","objective":"完成「核對合龍幾何」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for check closure geometry.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"溫度、變形與累積誤差會影響合龍位置。","textEn":"Temperature, deformation and accumulated error affect closure alignment."},{"id":"danjiang-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出合龍概念檢核的座標、溫度和量測時間。","textEn":"List coordinates, temperature and measurement time for conceptual closure review."}],"check":"列出合龍概念檢核的座標、溫度和量測時間。","checkEn":"List coordinates, temperature and measurement time for conceptual closure review.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「核對合龍幾何」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains check closure geometry?","options":["臨時支承承擔未完成結構的載荷，移除會改變受力。","溫度、變形與累積誤差會影響合龍位置。","施工中的結構系統會變化，完成狀態安全不代表每個階段都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Temporary supports carry incomplete structures; removal changes the load distribution.","Temperature, deformation and accumulated error affect closure alignment.","The structural system changes during construction; final safety does not prove stage safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度、變形與累積誤差會影響合龍位置。","explanationEn":"Temperature, deformation and accumulated error affect closure alignment."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-s05","order":5,"title":"耐久與防護","titleEn":"Durability and protection","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s05-01","order":1,"title":"追蹤腐蝕路徑","titleEn":"Trace corrosion paths","objective":"完成「追蹤腐蝕路徑」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for trace corrosion paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"水分與鹽分進入可能影響鋼材及鋼筋耐久性。","textEn":"Water and salts can affect the durability of steel and reinforcement."},{"id":"danjiang-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把暴露環境連到防護層與檢查方式。","textEn":"Link exposure to protection layers and inspection methods."}],"check":"把暴露環境連到防護層與檢查方式。","checkEn":"Link exposure to protection layers and inspection methods.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤腐蝕路徑」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains trace corrosion paths?","options":["鋪面需與鋼橋面變形及防水需求相容。","阻尼消散振動能量，剛度調整與阻尼增加不是同一作用。","水分與鹽分進入可能影響鋼材及鋼筋耐久性。"],"optionsEn":["Paving must accommodate steel-deck deformation and waterproofing needs.","Damping dissipates vibration energy; changing stiffness is a different mechanism.","Water and salts can affect the durability of steel and reinforcement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水分與鹽分進入可能影響鋼材及鋼筋耐久性。","explanationEn":"Water and salts can affect the durability of steel and reinforcement."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s05-02","order":2,"title":"理解鋪面與防水","titleEn":"Understand paving and waterproofing","objective":"完成「理解鋪面與防水」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand paving and waterproofing.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"鋪面需與鋼橋面變形及防水需求相容。","textEn":"Paving must accommodate steel-deck deformation and waterproofing needs."},{"id":"danjiang-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在剖面標出橋面、防水與鋪面功能。","textEn":"Label deck, waterproofing and pavement functions in a section."}],"check":"在剖面標出橋面、防水與鋪面功能。","checkEn":"Label deck, waterproofing and pavement functions in a section.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解鋪面與防水」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand paving and waterproofing?","options":["水分與鹽分進入可能影響鋼材及鋼筋耐久性。","鋪面需與鋼橋面變形及防水需求相容。","阻尼消散振動能量，剛度調整與阻尼增加不是同一作用。"],"optionsEn":["Water and salts can affect the durability of steel and reinforcement.","Paving must accommodate steel-deck deformation and waterproofing needs.","Damping dissipates vibration energy; changing stiffness is a different mechanism."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鋪面需與鋼橋面變形及防水需求相容。","explanationEn":"Paving must accommodate steel-deck deformation and waterproofing needs."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s05-03","order":3,"title":"分析減振目的","titleEn":"Analyze damping purpose","objective":"完成「分析減振目的」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze damping purpose.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"阻尼消散振動能量，剛度調整與阻尼增加不是同一作用。","textEn":"Damping dissipates vibration energy; changing stiffness is a different mechanism."},{"id":"danjiang-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較兩條示意自由衰減曲線。","textEn":"Compare two schematic free-decay curves."}],"check":"比較兩條示意自由衰減曲線。","checkEn":"Compare two schematic free-decay curves.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析減振目的」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze damping purpose?","options":["阻尼消散振動能量，剛度調整與阻尼增加不是同一作用。","水分與鹽分進入可能影響鋼材及鋼筋耐久性。","鋪面需與鋼橋面變形及防水需求相容。"],"optionsEn":["Damping dissipates vibration energy; changing stiffness is a different mechanism.","Water and salts can affect the durability of steel and reinforcement.","Paving must accommodate steel-deck deformation and waterproofing needs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼消散振動能量，剛度調整與阻尼增加不是同一作用。","explanationEn":"Damping dissipates vibration energy; changing stiffness is a different mechanism."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-s06","order":6,"title":"驗收與維護","titleEn":"Acceptance and maintenance","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-s06-01","order":1,"title":"建立量測基準","titleEn":"Establish measurement baselines","objective":"完成「建立量測基準」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for establish measurement baselines.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"竣工幾何與初始監測值支援後續變化判讀。","textEn":"As-built geometry and initial measurements support future change interpretation."},{"id":"danjiang-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立基準日期、環境及感測器欄位。","textEn":"Record baseline date, environment and sensors."}],"check":"建立基準日期、環境及感測器欄位。","checkEn":"Record baseline date, environment and sensors.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立量測基準」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains establish measurement baselines?","options":["載重、耐久與運營需求需要不同驗證證據。","竣工幾何與初始監測值支援後續變化判讀。","可達性影響索、接頭及排水設施的維護品質。"],"optionsEn":["Load, durability and operation needs require different evidence.","As-built geometry and initial measurements support future change interpretation.","Access affects maintenance of cables, joints and drainage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"竣工幾何與初始監測值支援後續變化判讀。","explanationEn":"As-built geometry and initial measurements support future change interpretation."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s06-02","order":2,"title":"規劃巡檢路徑","titleEn":"Plan inspection routes","objective":"完成「規劃巡檢路徑」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan inspection routes.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"可達性影響索、接頭及排水設施的維護品質。","textEn":"Access affects maintenance of cables, joints and drainage."},{"id":"danjiang-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意模型上安排安全可及的檢查區域。","textEn":"Mark conceptually accessible inspection areas on the model."}],"check":"在示意模型上安排安全可及的檢查區域。","checkEn":"Mark conceptually accessible inspection areas on the model.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃巡檢路徑」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan inspection routes?","options":["可達性影響索、接頭及排水設施的維護品質。","載重、耐久與運營需求需要不同驗證證據。","竣工幾何與初始監測值支援後續變化判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Access affects maintenance of cables, joints and drainage.","Load, durability and operation needs require different evidence.","As-built geometry and initial measurements support future change interpretation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可達性影響索、接頭及排水設施的維護品質。","explanationEn":"Access affects maintenance of cables, joints and drainage."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"danjiang-s06-03","order":3,"title":"交付證據矩陣","titleEn":"Deliver an evidence matrix","objective":"完成「交付證據矩陣」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver an evidence matrix.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"載重、耐久與運營需求需要不同驗證證據。","textEn":"Load, durability and operation needs require different evidence."},{"id":"danjiang-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為三類需求各填一項證據及尚待確認事項。","textEn":"Give evidence and open questions for each requirement class."}],"check":"為三類需求各填一項證據及尚待確認事項。","checkEn":"Give evidence and open questions for each requirement class.","sourceIds":["thb-danjiang"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付證據矩陣」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver an evidence matrix?","options":["竣工幾何與初始監測值支援後續變化判讀。","可達性影響索、接頭及排水設施的維護品質。","載重、耐久與運營需求需要不同驗證證據。"],"optionsEn":["As-built geometry and initial measurements support future change interpretation.","Access affects maintenance of cables, joints and drainage.","Load, durability and operation needs require different evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"載重、耐久與運營需求需要不同驗證證據。","explanationEn":"Load, durability and operation needs require different evidence."},"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固」與「縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout\" and \"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-01","title":"不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-s06-03"],"objective":"說明「背跨錨墩拉力」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Back-span anchor-pier force” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋的單塔位於河道偏淡水側，主跨 450 m 伸向八里，背跨只有 175 m。斜拉索把橋面重量吊到塔頂，塔頂兩側斜索的水平分力必須互相抵銷，否則橋塔會被拉彎；主跨長、背跨短，背索因此比前索陡，同樣的水平力在背跨端產生更大的向下拉力。若背跨本身不夠重，這個差額就要由背跨端的錨墩以拉力（或壓重）承受，背跨橋墩的支承因此可能出現上拔。設計者調整背跨壓重、錨墩配置與背索角度，就是在決定橋塔彎矩、錨墩反力與主跨撓度之間的分配。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「背跨錨墩拉力」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Danjiang Bridge’s single pylon stands toward the Tamsui side of the channel; the 450 m main span reaches toward Bali while the back span is only 175 m. Stays lift the deck weight to the pylon head, and the horizontal components of the stays on both sides must cancel or the pylon is bent. Because the main span is long and the back span short, the back stays are steeper, so the same horizontal force produces a larger downward pull at the back-span end. If the back span is not heavy enough, the difference must be carried as tension (or ballast) at the anchor pier, and back-span bearings may see uplift. Adjusting back-span ballast, anchor-pier layout and back-stay angles is how the designer distributes demand among pylon bending, anchor-pier reaction and main-span deflection. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Back-span anchor-pier force” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：把全橋視為以塔為支點的槓桿：R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Treat the bridge as a lever about the pylon: R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b.","failure":"常見誤解：「單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「背跨錨墩拉力」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Back-span anchor-pier force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-01-k1","title":"不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固","titleEn":"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout","text":"淡江大橋的單塔位於河道偏淡水側，主跨 450 m 伸向八里，背跨只有 175 m。斜拉索把橋面重量吊到塔頂，塔頂兩側斜索的水平分力必須互相抵銷，否則橋塔會被拉彎；主跨長、背跨短，背索因此比前索陡，同樣的水平力在背跨端產生更大的向下拉力。","textEn":"The Danjiang Bridge’s single pylon stands toward the Tamsui side of the channel; the 450 m main span reaches toward Bali while the back span is only 175 m. Stays lift the deck weight to the pylon head, and the horizontal components of the stays on both sides must cancel or the pylon is bent.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout\" is correct?","options":["單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。","淡江大橋的單塔位於河道偏淡水側，主跨 450 m 伸向八里，背跨只有 175 m。","阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。"],"optionsEn":["In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough.","The Danjiang Bridge’s single pylon stands toward the Tamsui side of the channel; the 450 m main span reaches toward Bali while the back span is only 175 m.","The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淡江大橋的單塔位於河道偏淡水側，主跨 450 m 伸向八里，背跨只有 175 m。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Danjiang Bridge’s single pylon stands toward the Tamsui side of the channel; the 450 m main span reaches toward Bali while the back span is only 175 m. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":19},{"id":"danjiang-v13-02","title":"不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固：定量估算","titleEn":"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背跨錨墩拉力」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Back-span anchor-pier force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：把全橋視為以塔為支點的槓桿：R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b。取 w_m = w_b = 300 kN/m、L_m = 450 m、L_b = 175 m：R = (30,375,000 − 4,593,750)/175 ≈ 147,300 kN；若背跨壓重使 w_b = 1,000 kN/m，R 降為約 86,100 kN。數值為教學假設，非本橋設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Treat the bridge as a lever about the pylon: R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b. With w_m = w_b = 300 kN/m, L_m = 450 m and L_b = 175 m, R = (30,375,000 − 4,593,750)/175 ≈ 147,300 kN; ballasting the back span to w_b = 1,000 kN/m lowers R to about 86,100 kN. Values are teaching assumptions, not this bridge’s design values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在施工各階段以背跨錨墩支承的荷重計或千斤頂讀值，比對施工階段分析預測的反力；同時量測塔頂縱向偏位與背索索力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At each construction stage compare load-cell or jack readings at the back-span anchor-pier bearings with reactions predicted by the staged analysis, while measuring longitudinal pylon-head displacement and back-stay forces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"把全橋視為以塔為支點的槓桿：R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b。取 w_m = w_b = 300 kN/m、L_m = 450 m、L_b = 175 m：R = (30,375,000 − 4,593,750)/175 ≈ 147,300 kN；若背跨壓重使 w_b = 1,000 kN/m，R 降為約 86,100 kN。數值為教學假設，非本橋設計值。","textEn":"Treat the bridge as a lever about the pylon: R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b. With w_m = w_b = 300 kN/m, L_m = 450 m and L_b = 175 m, R = (30,375,000 − 4,593,750)/175 ≈ 147,300 kN; ballasting the back span to w_b = 1,000 kN/m lowers R to about 86,100 kN. Values are teaching assumptions, not this bridge’s design values.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout\", which statement holds?","options":["大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。","合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","把全橋視為以塔為支點的槓桿：R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b。"],"optionsEn":["As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability.","A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","Treat the bridge as a lever about the pylon: R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把全橋視為以塔為支點的槓桿：R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Treat the bridge as a lever about the pylon: R = (w_m·L_m²/2 − w_b·L_b²/2)/L_b. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":20},{"id":"danjiang-v13-03","title":"不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背跨錨墩拉力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Back-span anchor-pier force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在施工各階段以背跨錨墩支承的荷重計或千斤頂讀值，比對施工階段分析預測的反力；同時量測塔頂縱向偏位與背索索力。若反力偏低而塔頂往主跨側偏，表示背跨壓重或背索力不足，需在合龍前調整。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At each construction stage compare load-cell or jack readings at the back-span anchor-pier bearings with reactions predicted by the staged analysis, while measuring longitudinal pylon-head displacement and back-stay forces. A low reaction together with pylon sway toward the main span indicates insufficient ballast or back-stay force, to be corrected before closure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：計算書應列出背跨壓重、錨墩拉力與背索力在每一施工階段與成橋狀態的包絡值，並把錨墩支承反力列為合龍前的停留檢查點，由設計單位簽認後才可進行下一階段。","observationEn":"Site practice: The calculations should tabulate envelopes of back-span ballast, anchor-pier tension and back-stay force for every construction stage and the completed state, and anchor-pier bearing reactions should be a hold point before closure, released only after the designer signs off.","failure":"注意干擾：背跨壓重估算過輕或錨墩拉力構件設計不足時，滿載的主跨會把背跨支承拉離，產生支承上拔與反覆碰撞，塔頂偏位與主跨撓度同時超出預測，伸縮縫與支承提前損壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If back-span ballast is underestimated or the anchor-pier tie is undersized, a fully loaded main span lifts the back-span bearings off their seats, causing uplift and repeated impact; pylon-head sway and main-span deflection both exceed predictions, and joints and bearings wear out early. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在施工各階段以背跨錨墩支承的荷重計或千斤頂讀值，比對施工階段分析預測的反力；同時量測塔頂縱向偏位與背索索力。若反力偏低而塔頂往主跨側偏，表示背跨壓重或背索力不足，需在合龍前調整。","textEn":"At each construction stage compare load-cell or jack readings at the back-span anchor-pier bearings with reactions predicted by the staged analysis, while measuring longitudinal pylon-head displacement and back-stay forces. A low reaction together with pylon sway toward the main span indicates insufficient ballast or back-stay force, to be corrected before closure.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"計算書應列出背跨壓重、錨墩拉力與背索力在每一施工階段與成橋狀態的包絡值，並把錨墩支承反力列為合龍前的停留檢查點，由設計單位簽認後才可進行下一階段。","textEn":"The calculations should tabulate envelopes of back-span ballast, anchor-pier tension and back-stay force for every construction stage and the completed state, and anchor-pier bearing reactions should be a hold point before closure, released only after the designer signs off.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout\"?","options":["在施工各階段以背跨錨墩支承的荷重計或千斤頂讀值，比對施工階段分析預測的反力；同時量測塔頂縱向偏位與背索索力。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。"],"optionsEn":["At each construction stage compare load-cell or jack readings at the back-span anchor-pier bearings with reactions predicted by the staged analysis, while measuring longitudinal pylon-head displacement and back-stay forces.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在施工各階段以背跨錨墩支承的荷重計或千斤頂讀值，比對施工階段分析預測的反力；同時量測塔頂縱向偏位與背索索力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At each construction stage compare load-cell or jack readings at the back-span anchor-pier bearings with reactions predicted by the staged analysis, while measuring longitudinal pylon-head displacement and back-stay forces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":21},{"id":"danjiang-v13-04","title":"不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背跨錨墩拉力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Back-span anchor-pier force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"背跨壓重估算過輕或錨墩拉力構件設計不足時，滿載的主跨會把背跨支承拉離，產生支承上拔與反覆碰撞，塔頂偏位與主跨撓度同時超出預測，伸縮縫與支承提前損壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If back-span ballast is underestimated or the anchor-pier tie is undersized, a fully loaded main span lifts the back-span bearings off their seats, causing uplift and repeated impact; pylon-head sway and main-span deflection both exceed predictions, and joints and bearings wear out early. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計者調整背跨壓重、錨墩配置與背索角度，就是在決定橋塔彎矩、錨墩反力與主跨撓度之間的分配。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adjusting back-span ballast, anchor-pier layout and back-stay angles is how the designer distributes demand among pylon bending, anchor-pier reaction and main-span deflection.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"背跨壓重估算過輕或錨墩拉力構件設計不足時，滿載的主跨會把背跨支承拉離，產生支承上拔與反覆碰撞，塔頂偏位與主跨撓度同時超出預測，伸縮縫與支承提前損壞。","textEn":"If back-span ballast is underestimated or the anchor-pier tie is undersized, a fully loaded main span lifts the back-span bearings off their seats, causing uplift and repeated impact; pylon-head sway and main-span deflection both exceed predictions, and joints and bearings wear out early.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不對稱跨徑的槓桿平衡與背跨錨固」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lever balance and back-span anchorage of an asymmetric layout\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","背跨壓重估算過輕或錨墩拉力構件設計不足時，滿載的主跨會把背跨支承拉離，產生支承上拔與反覆碰撞，塔頂偏位與主跨撓度同時超出預測，伸縮縫與支承提前損壞。","阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If back-span ballast is underestimated or the anchor-pier tie is undersized, a fully loaded main span lifts the back-span bearings off their seats, causing uplift and repeated impact.","The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"背跨壓重估算過輕或錨墩拉力構件設計不足時，滿載的主跨會把背跨支承拉離，產生支承上拔與反覆碰撞，塔頂偏位與主跨撓度同時超出預測，伸縮縫與支承提前損壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If back-span ballast is underestimated or the anchor-pier tie is undersized, a fully loaded main span lifts the back-span bearings off their seats, causing uplift and repeated impact; pylon-head sway and main-span deflection both exceed predictions, and joints and bearings wear out early. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":22},{"id":"danjiang-v13-05","title":"縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydraulic fuse restraints” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋縱向在主橋塔設 7 支 HFR、橋梁兩端設 4 支 FVD；橫向以內側橋墩頂的 FPB 鋼製摩擦單擺支承與八里側合成橡膠墊消能。HFR 在平時像剛性保險栓，承受煞車與風力而不讓橋面漂移；地震力超過臨界值時保險動作，轉為黏滯阻尼器，讓橋面在約 40 cm 可消能位移內擺動，最後 5 cm 作為防止橋面撞擊橋塔的止擋。這種先剛後柔的安排，把常時的使用性與大地震的消能分開設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Published Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has 7 HFR units at the main pylon and 4 FVD units at the bridge ends in the longitudinal direction, while transversely friction-pendulum steel bearings on the inner pier tops and elastomeric pads on the Bali side dissipate energy. In service the HFR behaves like a rigid fuse, carrying braking and wind forces so the deck does not drift; when seismic force exceeds the threshold, the fuse releases and the unit becomes a viscous damper, letting the deck move within roughly 40 cm of dissipative travel, with a final 5 cm acting as a stop that keeps the deck from striking the pylon. Stiff-then-soft behaviour separates everyday serviceability from energy dissipation in a large earthquake. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Hydraulic fuse restraints” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：公開資料 7 支 HFR 合計約 5,250 t，平均每支約 750 t（約 7,360 kN）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The published total of about 5,250 t for 7 HFR units averages about 750 t (about 7,360 kN) each.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Hydraulic fuse restraints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-05-k1","title":"縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限","titleEn":"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits","text":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋縱向在主橋塔設 7 支 HFR、橋梁兩端設 4 支 FVD；橫向以內側橋墩頂的 FPB 鋼製摩擦單擺支承與八里側合成橡膠墊消能。HFR 在平時像剛性保險栓，承受煞車與風力而不讓橋面漂移；地震力超過臨界值時保險動作，轉為黏滯阻尼器，讓橋面在約 40 cm 可消能位移內擺動，最後 5 cm 作為防止橋面撞擊橋塔的止擋。","textEn":"Published Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has 7 HFR units at the main pylon and 4 FVD units at the bridge ends in the longitudinal direction, while transversely friction-pendulum steel bearings on the inner pier tops and elastomeric pads on the Bali side dissipate energy. In service the HFR behaves like a rigid fuse, carrying braking and wind forces so the deck does not drift; when seismic force exceeds the threshold, the fuse releases and the unit becomes a viscous damper, letting the deck move within roughly 40 cm of dissipative travel, with a final 5 cm acting as a stop that keeps the deck from striking the pylon.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。","斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。","公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋縱向在主橋塔設 7 支 HFR、橋梁兩端設 4 支 FVD；橫向以內側橋墩頂的 FPB 鋼製摩擦單擺支承與八里側合成橡膠墊消能。"],"optionsEn":["The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake.","Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.","Published Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has 7 HFR units at the main pylon and 4 FVD units at the bridge ends in the longitudinal direction, while transversely friction-pendulum steel bearings on the inner pier tops and elastomeric pads on the Bali side dissipate energy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋縱向在主橋塔設 7 支 HFR、橋梁兩端設 4 支 FVD；橫向以內側橋墩頂的 FPB 鋼製摩擦單擺支承與八里側合成橡膠墊消能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Published Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has 7 HFR units at the main pylon and 4 FVD units at the bridge ends in the longitudinal direction, while transversely friction-pendulum steel bearings on the inner pier tops and elastomeric pads on the Bali side dissipate energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":23},{"id":"danjiang-v13-06","title":"縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限：定量估算","titleEn":"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydraulic fuse restraints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：公開資料 7 支 HFR 合計約 5,250 t，平均每支約 750 t（約 7,360 kN）。端部 FVD 取 F = C·v^α，若設計力 9,810 kN 發生在 v = 0.8 m/s、α = 0.3，C = 9,810/0.8^0.3 ≈ 10,490 kN/(m/s)^0.3；v 只有 0.2 m/s 時 F ≈ 10,490×0.617 ≈ 6,470 kN。α 與速度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The published total of about 5,250 t for 7 HFR units averages about 750 t (about 7,360 kN) each. For an end FVD with F = C·v^α, a design force of 9,810 kN at v = 0.8 m/s with α = 0.3 gives C = 9,810/0.8^0.3 ≈ 10,490 kN/(m/s)^0.3; at only 0.2 m/s, F ≈ 10,490×0.617 ≈ 6,470 kN. α and velocities are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每支阻尼器出廠前做原型與逐件試驗：HFR 驗證保險觸發力與觸發後的力—速度曲線，FVD 在多個速度與溫度下繪製遲滯迴圈；安裝後量測橋面與橋塔間的實際間隙，確認 40 cm 消能行程與 5 cm 止擋皆符合圖說。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Each device receives prototype and production tests before delivery: for the HFR, verify the fuse release force and the post-release force–velocity curve; for the FVD, plot hysteresis loops at several velocities and temperatures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"公開資料 7 支 HFR 合計約 5,250 t，平均每支約 750 t（約 7,360 kN）。端部 FVD 取 F = C·v^α，若設計力 9,810 kN 發生在 v = 0.8 m/s、α = 0.3，C = 9,810/0.8^0.3 ≈ 10,490 kN/(m/s)^0.3；v 只有 0.2 m/s 時 F ≈ 10,490×0.617 ≈ 6,470 kN。α 與速度為教學假設。","textEn":"The published total of about 5,250 t for 7 HFR units averages about 750 t (about 7,360 kN) each. For an end FVD with F = C·v^α, a design force of 9,810 kN at v = 0.8 m/s with α = 0.3 gives C = 9,810/0.8^0.3 ≈ 10,490 kN/(m/s)^0.3; at only 0.2 m/s, F ≈ 10,490×0.617 ≈ 6,470 kN. α and velocities are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits\", which statement holds?","options":["公開資料 7 支 HFR 合計約 5,250 t，平均每支約 750 t（約 7,360 kN）。","塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。","風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。"],"optionsEn":["The published total of about 5,250 t for 7 HFR units averages about 750 t (about 7,360 kN) each.","Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once.","Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"公開資料 7 支 HFR 合計約 5,250 t，平均每支約 750 t（約 7,360 kN）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The published total of about 5,250 t for 7 HFR units averages about 750 t (about 7,360 kN) each. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":24},{"id":"danjiang-v13-07","title":"縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydraulic fuse restraints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每支阻尼器出廠前做原型與逐件試驗：HFR 驗證保險觸發力與觸發後的力—速度曲線，FVD 在多個速度與溫度下繪製遲滯迴圈；安裝後量測橋面與橋塔間的實際間隙，確認 40 cm 消能行程與 5 cm 止擋皆符合圖說。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Each device receives prototype and production tests before delivery: for the HFR, verify the fuse release force and the post-release force–velocity curve; for the FVD, plot hysteresis loops at several velocities and temperatures. After installation measure the actual deck-to-pylon gaps and confirm the 40 cm dissipative travel and 5 cm stop match the drawings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保險觸發力、阻尼係數與行程必須同時列在設計圖與採購規範，並與風、煞車、溫度與地震的荷載組合逐一對照；HFR 與 FVD 的更換程序與臨時固定方式要在交接文件中寫明。","observationEn":"Site practice: Fuse release force, damping coefficient and stroke must all appear on the drawings and in the procurement specification and be checked against each wind, braking, temperature and seismic combination; replacement procedures and temporary restraint methods for the HFR and FVD units belong in the handover documents.","failure":"注意干擾：若保險觸發力設定太低，強烈東北季風或煞車就可能誤觸發，使橋面在常時漂移；設定太高則地震時不觸發，地震力直接灌入橋塔基礎。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A fuse set too low can be triggered by strong northeast-monsoon wind or braking, letting the deck drift in service; set too high it does not release in an earthquake and the full seismic force goes into the pylon foundation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每支阻尼器出廠前做原型與逐件試驗：HFR 驗證保險觸發力與觸發後的力—速度曲線，FVD 在多個速度與溫度下繪製遲滯迴圈；安裝後量測橋面與橋塔間的實際間隙，確認 40 cm 消能行程與 5 cm 止擋皆符合圖說。","textEn":"Each device receives prototype and production tests before delivery: for the HFR, verify the fuse release force and the post-release force–velocity curve; for the FVD, plot hysteresis loops at several velocities and temperatures. After installation measure the actual deck-to-pylon gaps and confirm the 40 cm dissipative travel and 5 cm stop match the drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保險觸發力、阻尼係數與行程必須同時列在設計圖與採購規範，並與風、煞車、溫度與地震的荷載組合逐一對照；HFR 與 FVD 的更換程序與臨時固定方式要在交接文件中寫明。","textEn":"Fuse release force, damping coefficient and stroke must all appear on the drawings and in the procurement specification and be checked against each wind, braking, temperature and seismic combination; replacement procedures and temporary restraint methods for the HFR and FVD units belong in the handover documents.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","每支阻尼器出廠前做原型與逐件試驗：HFR 驗證保險觸發力與觸發後的力—速度曲線，FVD 在多個速度與溫度下繪製遲滯迴圈。","鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Each device receives prototype and production tests before delivery: for the HFR, verify the fuse release force and the post-release force–velocity curve.","Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每支阻尼器出廠前做原型與逐件試驗：HFR 驗證保險觸發力與觸發後的力—速度曲線，FVD 在多個速度與溫度下繪製遲滯迴圈；安裝後量測橋面與橋塔間的實際間隙，確認 40 cm 消能行程與 5 cm 止擋皆符合圖說。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Each device receives prototype and production tests before delivery: for the HFR, verify the fuse release force and the post-release force–velocity curve; for the FVD, plot hysteresis loops at several velocities and temperatures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":25},{"id":"danjiang-v13-08","title":"縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「HFR 液壓保險阻尼器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydraulic fuse restraints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若保險觸發力設定太低，強烈東北季風或煞車就可能誤觸發，使橋面在常時漂移；設定太高則地震時不觸發，地震力直接灌入橋塔基礎。行程不足時橋面在大地震末段撞擊止擋，產生衝擊力與局部損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A fuse set too low can be triggered by strong northeast-monsoon wind or braking, letting the deck drift in service; set too high it does not release in an earthquake and the full seismic force goes into the pylon foundation. Insufficient stroke lets the deck hit the stops late in a large earthquake, producing impact forces and local damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這種先剛後柔的安排，把常時的使用性與大地震的消能分開設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stiff-then-soft behaviour separates everyday serviceability from energy dissipation in a large earthquake.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若保險觸發力設定太低，強烈東北季風或煞車就可能誤觸發，使橋面在常時漂移；設定太高則地震時不觸發，地震力直接灌入橋塔基礎。行程不足時橋面在大地震末段撞擊止擋，產生衝擊力與局部損傷。","textEn":"A fuse set too low can be triggered by strong northeast-monsoon wind or braking, letting the deck drift in service; set too high it does not release in an earthquake and the full seismic force goes into the pylon foundation. Insufficient stroke lets the deck hit the stops late in a large earthquake, producing impact forces and local damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「縱向浮動體系：HFR、FVD 與位移上限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Longitudinal floating system: HFR, FVD and displacement limits\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。","若保險觸發力設定太低，強烈東北季風或煞車就可能誤觸發，使橋面在常時漂移；設定太高則地震時不觸發，地震力直接灌入橋塔基礎。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.","A fuse set too low can be triggered by strong northeast-monsoon wind or braking, letting the deck drift in service."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若保險觸發力設定太低，強烈東北季風或煞車就可能誤觸發，使橋面在常時漂移；設定太高則地震時不觸發，地震力直接灌入橋塔基礎。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A fuse set too low can be triggered by strong northeast-monsoon wind or braking, letting the deck drift in service; set too high it does not release in an earthquake and the full seismic force goes into the pylon foundation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":26}],"order":7},{"id":"danjiang-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力」與「58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stay force, strand count and service stress\" and \"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-09","title":"斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Stay force, strand count and service stress: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「主跨遠端長索」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Far main-span stay” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋以 94 根斜拉索把鋼箱梁吊到單一橋塔，主跨遠端的索最長、最平。每根索要承擔所在節塊的分擔長度內的橋面重、鋪面與活載，但索越平，相同垂直分力需要的索力越大，所以遠端長索通常是鋼絞線數最多的一組。設計時以使用狀態的索力除以每股容許力決定股數，並按標準錨具規格向上取整，同時保留更換單股與日後調索的裕度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主跨遠端長索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Danjiang Bridge hangs its steel box girder from a single pylon with 94 stays, and the stays at the far end of the main span are the longest and flattest. Each stay carries the deck weight, surfacing and live load over its tributary length, but the flatter the stay, the larger the force needed for the same vertical component, so the far long stays usually have the most strands. The strand count is set by dividing the service force by the allowable force per strand and rounding up to a standard anchorage size, leaving margin for single-strand replacement and future force adjustment. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Far main-span stay” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：取塔頂高出橋面 185 m、錨點水平距 430 m，sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395；分擔 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN，T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN，乘 1.25 計活載與附加靜載得約 14,230 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With the anchorage 185 m below the pylon head and 430 m away horizontally, sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395; a tributary load of 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN gives T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN, and a 1.25 factor for live and superimposed load gives about 14,230 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主跨遠端長索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Far main-span stay”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-09-k1","title":"斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力","titleEn":"Stay force, strand count and service stress","text":"淡江大橋以 94 根斜拉索把鋼箱梁吊到單一橋塔，主跨遠端的索最長、最平。每根索要承擔所在節塊的分擔長度內的橋面重、鋪面與活載，但索越平，相同垂直分力需要的索力越大，所以遠端長索通常是鋼絞線數最多的一組。","textEn":"The Danjiang Bridge hangs its steel box girder from a single pylon with 94 stays, and the stays at the far end of the main span are the longest and flattest. Each stay carries the deck weight, surfacing and live load over its tributary length, but the flatter the stay, the larger the force needed for the same vertical component, so the far long stays usually have the most strands.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stay force, strand count and service stress\" is correct?","options":["淡江大橋以 94 根斜拉索把鋼箱梁吊到單一橋塔，主跨遠端的索最長、最平。","斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。","大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。"],"optionsEn":["The Danjiang Bridge hangs its steel box girder from a single pylon with 94 stays, and the stays at the far end of the main span are the longest and flattest.","Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.","As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淡江大橋以 94 根斜拉索把鋼箱梁吊到單一橋塔，主跨遠端的索最長、最平。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Danjiang Bridge hangs its steel box girder from a single pylon with 94 stays, and the stays at the far end of the main span are the longest and flattest. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":27},{"id":"danjiang-v13-10","title":"斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Stay force, strand count and service stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主跨遠端長索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Far main-span stay” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：取塔頂高出橋面 185 m、錨點水平距 430 m，sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395；分擔 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN，T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN，乘 1.25 計活載與附加靜載得約 14,230 kN。15.7 mm 鋼絞線 GUTS = 150×1,860 = 279 kN，0.45 GUTS = 125.6 kN，需 14,230/125.6 ≈ 114 股，取 127 股錨具。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With the anchorage 185 m below the pylon head and 430 m away horizontally, sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395; a tributary load of 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN gives T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN, and a 1.25 factor for live and superimposed load gives about 14,230 kN. A 15.7 mm strand has GUTS = 150×1,860 = 279 kN and 0.45 GUTS = 125.6 kN, so 14,230/125.6 ≈ 114 strands are needed and a 127-strand anchorage is chosen. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對設計索力表與鋼絞線出廠拉伸、鬆弛與疲勞試驗報告，確認每批鋼絞線的破斷力與彈性模數；錨具系統依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞與破斷試驗，並在張拉紀錄中逐根核對最終索力與使用應力比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare the design stay-force table with mill tensile, relaxation and fatigue reports for the strand, confirming breaking force and modulus for each lot; the anchorage system receives assembly fatigue and ultimate tests under stay-cable recommendations, and the stressing records are checked stay by stay for final force and service stress ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"取塔頂高出橋面 185 m、錨點水平距 430 m，sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395；分擔 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN，T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN，乘 1.25 計活載與附加靜載得約 14,230 kN。15.7 mm 鋼絞線 GUTS = 150×1,860 = 279 kN，0.45 GUTS = 125.6 kN，需 14,230/125.6 ≈ 114 股，取 127 股錨具。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With the anchorage 185 m below the pylon head and 430 m away horizontally, sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395; a tributary load of 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN gives T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN, and a 1.25 factor for live and superimposed load gives about 14,230 kN. A 15.7 mm strand has GUTS = 150×1,860 = 279 kN and 0.45 GUTS = 125.6 kN, so 14,230/125.6 ≈ 114 strands are needed and a 127-strand anchorage is chosen. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stay force, strand count and service stress\", which statement holds?","options":["合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","取塔頂高出橋面 185 m、錨點水平距 430 m，sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395。","載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。"],"optionsEn":["A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","With the anchorage 185 m below the pylon head and 430 m away horizontally, sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395.","A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取塔頂高出橋面 185 m、錨點水平距 430 m，sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395；分擔 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN，T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN，乘 1.25 計活載與附加靜載得約 14,230 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With the anchorage 185 m below the pylon head and 430 m away horizontally, sinθ = 185/√(185²+430²) = 185/468.1 ≈ 0.395; a tributary load of 15 m×300 kN/m = 4,500 kN gives T = 4,500/0.395 ≈ 11,390 kN, and a 1.25 factor for live and superimposed load gives about 14,230 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":28},{"id":"danjiang-v13-11","title":"斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stay force, strand count and service stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主跨遠端長索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Far main-span stay” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對設計索力表與鋼絞線出廠拉伸、鬆弛與疲勞試驗報告，確認每批鋼絞線的破斷力與彈性模數；錨具系統依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞與破斷試驗，並在張拉紀錄中逐根核對最終索力與使用應力比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare the design stay-force table with mill tensile, relaxation and fatigue reports for the strand, confirming breaking force and modulus for each lot; the anchorage system receives assembly fatigue and ultimate tests under stay-cable recommendations, and the stressing records are checked stay by stay for final force and service stress ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：索力表要同時列出成橋索力、使用最大索力、單索斷失工況與更換工況，錨具尺寸按最不利者決定；圖說應註明每根索的股數、錨具型號與預留調整量。","observationEn":"Site practice: The stay-force table should list completed-state force, maximum service force, stay-loss and replacement cases, with anchorage size governed by the worst; drawings should state each stay’s strand count, anchorage type and reserved adjustment.","failure":"注意干擾：若只按恆載挑選股數而忽略活載、溫差與單索斷失的重分配，使用應力可能接近或超過容許值，長期在錨頭產生較大的疲勞應力幅，並使日後無法安全地單股更換。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting strands for dead load only, ignoring live load, temperature and redistribution after a stay loss, can push service stress close to or beyond the limit, raising fatigue stress ranges at the anchor heads and making later single-strand replacement unsafe. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對設計索力表與鋼絞線出廠拉伸、鬆弛與疲勞試驗報告，確認每批鋼絞線的破斷力與彈性模數；錨具系統依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞與破斷試驗，並在張拉紀錄中逐根核對最終索力與使用應力比。","textEn":"Compare the design stay-force table with mill tensile, relaxation and fatigue reports for the strand, confirming breaking force and modulus for each lot; the anchorage system receives assembly fatigue and ultimate tests under stay-cable recommendations, and the stressing records are checked stay by stay for final force and service stress ratio.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"索力表要同時列出成橋索力、使用最大索力、單索斷失工況與更換工況，錨具尺寸按最不利者決定；圖說應註明每根索的股數、錨具型號與預留調整量。","textEn":"The stay-force table should list completed-state force, maximum service force, stay-loss and replacement cases, with anchorage size governed by the worst; drawings should state each stay’s strand count, anchorage type and reserved adjustment.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stay force, strand count and service stress\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。","比對設計索力表與鋼絞線出廠拉伸、鬆弛與疲勞試驗報告，確認每批鋼絞線的破斷力與彈性模數。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection.","Compare the design stay-force table with mill tensile, relaxation and fatigue reports for the strand, confirming breaking force and modulus for each lot."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比對設計索力表與鋼絞線出廠拉伸、鬆弛與疲勞試驗報告，確認每批鋼絞線的破斷力與彈性模數；錨具系統依斜索規範做組裝體疲勞與破斷試驗，並在張拉紀錄中逐根核對最終索力與使用應力比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare the design stay-force table with mill tensile, relaxation and fatigue reports for the strand, confirming breaking force and modulus for each lot; the anchorage system receives assembly fatigue and ultimate tests under stay-cable recommendations, and the stressing records are checked stay by stay for final force and service stress ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":29},{"id":"danjiang-v13-12","title":"斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stay force, strand count and service stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主跨遠端長索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Far main-span stay” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只按恆載挑選股數而忽略活載、溫差與單索斷失的重分配，使用應力可能接近或超過容許值，長期在錨頭產生較大的疲勞應力幅，並使日後無法安全地單股更換。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting strands for dead load only, ignoring live load, temperature and redistribution after a stay loss, can push service stress close to or beyond the limit, raising fatigue stress ranges at the anchor heads and making later single-strand replacement unsafe. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計時以使用狀態的索力除以每股容許力決定股數，並按標準錨具規格向上取整，同時保留更換單股與日後調索的裕度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The strand count is set by dividing the service force by the allowable force per strand and rounding up to a standard anchorage size, leaving margin for single-strand replacement and future force adjustment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只按恆載挑選股數而忽略活載、溫差與單索斷失的重分配，使用應力可能接近或超過容許值，長期在錨頭產生較大的疲勞應力幅，並使日後無法安全地單股更換。","textEn":"Selecting strands for dead load only, ignoring live load, temperature and redistribution after a stay loss, can push service stress close to or beyond the limit, raising fatigue stress ranges at the anchor heads and making later single-strand replacement unsafe.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斜拉索力、鋼絞線數與使用應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stay force, strand count and service stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只按恆載挑選股數而忽略活載、溫差與單索斷失的重分配，使用應力可能接近或超過容許值，長期在錨頭產生較大的疲勞應力幅，並使日後無法安全地單股更換。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。"],"optionsEn":["Selecting strands for dead load only, ignoring live load, temperature and redistribution after a stay loss, can push service stress close to or beyond the limit, raising fatigue stress ranges at the anchor heads and making later single-strand replacement unsafe.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只按恆載挑選股數而忽略活載、溫差與單索斷失的重分配，使用應力可能接近或超過容許值，長期在錨頭產生較大的疲勞應力幅，並使日後無法安全地單股更換。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting strands for dead load only, ignoring live load, temperature and redistribution after a stay loss, can push service stress close to or beyond the limit, raising fatigue stress ranges at the anchor heads and making later single-strand replacement unsafe. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":30},{"id":"danjiang-v13-13","title":"58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「P130 大體積樁帽」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “P130 mass-concrete pile cap” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主塔基礎由 58 支直徑 2.5 m、長約 65 m 的全套管基樁貫入大南灣層，上方是平面約 77 m × 45 m 的大型樁帽，依公開報導約 15,000 m³ 混凝土連續澆置約 93 小時。樁群把塔與斜索的巨大垂直力分散到深層地盤，樁帽頂設在既有河床以下以減輕沖刷。如此厚的樁帽在水化期間核心溫度上升遠高於表面，內外溫差造成的拉應力若超過早齡期混凝土抗拉強度，就會出現溫度裂縫，成為日後鹽害侵入的通道。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「P130 大體積樁帽」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main-pylon foundation uses 58 fully cased bored piles, 2.5 m in diameter and about 65 m long, driven into the Dananwan layer, under a pile cap of about 77 m × 45 m in plan; public reports describe about 15,000 m³ of concrete placed continuously over about 93 hours. The pile group spreads the large vertical forces of pylon and stays into deep ground, and the cap top lies below the existing riverbed to reduce scour. In a cap this thick the core temperature during hydration rises far above the surface, and if the tensile stress from the temperature difference exceeds the early-age tensile strength, thermal cracks form and later become paths for chloride ingress. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “P130 mass-concrete pile cap” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：絕熱溫升 ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Adiabatic temperature rise ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c).","failure":"常見誤解：「大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「P130 大體積樁帽」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “P130 mass-concrete pile cap”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-13-k1","title":"58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱","titleEn":"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration","text":"主塔基礎由 58 支直徑 2.5 m、長約 65 m 的全套管基樁貫入大南灣層，上方是平面約 77 m × 45 m 的大型樁帽，依公開報導約 15,000 m³ 混凝土連續澆置約 93 小時。樁群把塔與斜索的巨大垂直力分散到深層地盤，樁帽頂設在既有河床以下以減輕沖刷。","textEn":"The main-pylon foundation uses 58 fully cased bored piles, 2.5 m in diameter and about 65 m long, driven into the Dananwan layer, under a pile cap of about 77 m × 45 m in plan; public reports describe about 15,000 m³ of concrete placed continuously over about 93 hours. The pile group spreads the large vertical forces of pylon and stays into deep ground, and the cap top lies below the existing riverbed to reduce scour.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration\" is correct?","options":["大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。","主塔基礎由 58 支直徑 2.5 m、長約 65 m 的全套管基樁貫入大南灣層，上方是平面約 77 m × 45 m 的大型樁帽，依公開報導約 15,000 m³ 混凝土連續澆置約 93 小時。","塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。"],"optionsEn":["As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability.","The main-pylon foundation uses 58 fully cased bored piles, 2.5 m in diameter and about 65 m long, driven into the Dananwan layer, under a pile cap of about 77 m × 45 m in plan.","Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主塔基礎由 58 支直徑 2.5 m、長約 65 m 的全套管基樁貫入大南灣層，上方是平面約 77 m × 45 m 的大型樁帽，依公開報導約 15,000 m³ 混凝土連續澆置約 93 小時。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main-pylon foundation uses 58 fully cased bored piles, 2.5 m in diameter and about 65 m long, driven into the Dananwan layer, under a pile cap of about 77 m × 45 m in plan; public reports describe about 15,000 m³ of concrete placed continuously over about 93 hours. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":31},{"id":"danjiang-v13-14","title":"58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱：定量估算","titleEn":"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「P130 大體積樁帽」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “P130 mass-concrete pile cap” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：絕熱溫升 ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)。取有效水泥量 C = 350 kg/m³、Q = 300 kJ/kg、ρ·c = 2,400 kJ/(m³·K)：ΔT = 350×300/2,400 ≈ 44 °C；改用摻料使有效水泥量降為 250 kg/m³，ΔT ≈ 31 °C。93 小時澆置 15,000 m³ 需平均約 161 m³/h 的供料率。配比數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Adiabatic temperature rise ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c). With effective cement C = 350 kg/m³, Q = 300 kJ/kg and ρ·c = 2,400 kJ/(m³·K), ΔT = 350×300/2,400 ≈ 44 °C; lowering effective cement to 250 kg/m³ with supplementary materials gives ΔT ≈ 31 °C. Placing 15,000 m³ in 93 hours needs an average supply of about 161 m³/h. Mix values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：澆置前做溫度應力分析並訂出核心與表面溫差上限（例如 20 °C 等級），樁帽內埋設多層熱電偶連續記錄；基樁以靜載或雙向載重試驗與完整性檢測（聲波或熱完整性）驗收，比對設計承載與沉陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before casting, run a thermal-stress analysis and set a core-to-surface limit (for example of the order of 20 °C), embedding thermocouples at several levels in the cap with continuous logging; accept piles with static or bidirectional load tests and integrity tests (sonic or thermal) compared against design capacity and settlement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"絕熱溫升 ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)。取有效水泥量 C = 350 kg/m³、Q = 300 kJ/kg、ρ·c = 2,400 kJ/(m³·K)：ΔT = 350×300/2,400 ≈ 44 °C；改用摻料使有效水泥量降為 250 kg/m³，ΔT ≈ 31 °C。93 小時澆置 15,000 m³ 需平均約 161 m³/h 的供料率。配比數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Adiabatic temperature rise ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c). With effective cement C = 350 kg/m³, Q = 300 kJ/kg and ρ·c = 2,400 kJ/(m³·K), ΔT = 350×300/2,400 ≈ 44 °C; lowering effective cement to 250 kg/m³ with supplementary materials gives ΔT ≈ 31 °C. Placing 15,000 m³ in 93 hours needs an average supply of about 161 m³/h. Mix values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration\", which statement holds?","options":["風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。","鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。","絕熱溫升 ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)。"],"optionsEn":["Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter.","Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.","Adiabatic temperature rise ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"絕熱溫升 ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Adiabatic temperature rise ΔT = C·Q/(ρ·c). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":32},{"id":"danjiang-v13-15","title":"58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「P130 大體積樁帽」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “P130 mass-concrete pile cap” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"澆置前做溫度應力分析並訂出核心與表面溫差上限（例如 20 °C 等級），樁帽內埋設多層熱電偶連續記錄；基樁以靜載或雙向載重試驗與完整性檢測（聲波或熱完整性）驗收，比對設計承載與沉陷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before casting, run a thermal-stress analysis and set a core-to-surface limit (for example of the order of 20 °C), embedding thermocouples at several levels in the cap with continuous logging; accept piles with static or bidirectional load tests and integrity tests (sonic or thermal) compared against design capacity and settlement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：大體積澆置前要有供料、泵送與備援計畫（第二座拌合廠、備用泵車）、分層澆置順序、測溫與保溫措施，並把溫差超限列為停止與通報條件，由監造與設計單位共同認可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before a mass pour require a supply, pumping and backup plan (second batching plant, standby pumps), a layer sequence, temperature monitoring and insulation, with exceedance of the temperature difference as a stop-and-report condition approved by both the supervising engineer and the designer.","failure":"注意干擾：連續澆置中斷形成冷縫，或保溫不足使表面急冷，樁帽會出現貫穿或表層溫度裂縫；在河口鹽害與潮汐乾濕交替下，裂縫加速氯離子侵入，使鋼筋提前腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An interrupted pour that leaves a cold joint, or poor insulation that chills the surface, produces through or surface thermal cracks in the cap; under estuary salt exposure and tidal wetting and drying, the cracks accelerate chloride ingress and early corrosion of the reinforcement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"澆置前做溫度應力分析並訂出核心與表面溫差上限（例如 20 °C 等級），樁帽內埋設多層熱電偶連續記錄；基樁以靜載或雙向載重試驗與完整性檢測（聲波或熱完整性）驗收，比對設計承載與沉陷。","textEn":"Before casting, run a thermal-stress analysis and set a core-to-surface limit (for example of the order of 20 °C), embedding thermocouples at several levels in the cap with continuous logging; accept piles with static or bidirectional load tests and integrity tests (sonic or thermal) compared against design capacity and settlement.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"大體積澆置前要有供料、泵送與備援計畫（第二座拌合廠、備用泵車）、分層澆置順序、測溫與保溫措施，並把溫差超限列為停止與通報條件，由監造與設計單位共同認可。","textEn":"Before a mass pour require a supply, pumping and backup plan (second batching plant, standby pumps), a layer sequence, temperature monitoring and insulation, with exceedance of the temperature difference as a stop-and-report condition approved by both the supervising engineer and the designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration\"?","options":["澆置前做溫度應力分析並訂出核心與表面溫差上限（例如 20 °C 等級），樁帽內埋設多層熱電偶連續記錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Before casting, run a thermal-stress analysis and set a core-to-surface limit (for example of the order of 20 °C), embedding thermocouples at several levels in the cap with continuous logging.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"澆置前做溫度應力分析並訂出核心與表面溫差上限（例如 20 °C 等級），樁帽內埋設多層熱電偶連續記錄；基樁以靜載或雙向載重試驗與完整性檢測（聲波或熱完整性）驗收，比對設計承載與沉陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before casting, run a thermal-stress analysis and set a core-to-surface limit (for example of the order of 20 °C), embedding thermocouples at several levels in the cap with continuous logging; accept piles with static or bidirectional load tests and integrity tests (sonic or thermal) compared against design capacity and settlement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":33},{"id":"danjiang-v13-16","title":"58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「P130 大體積樁帽」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “P130 mass-concrete pile cap” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"連續澆置中斷形成冷縫，或保溫不足使表面急冷，樁帽會出現貫穿或表層溫度裂縫；在河口鹽害與潮汐乾濕交替下，裂縫加速氯離子侵入，使鋼筋提前腐蝕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An interrupted pour that leaves a cold joint, or poor insulation that chills the surface, produces through or surface thermal cracks in the cap; under estuary salt exposure and tidal wetting and drying, the cracks accelerate chloride ingress and early corrosion of the reinforcement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：如此厚的樁帽在水化期間核心溫度上升遠高於表面，內外溫差造成的拉應力若超過早齡期混凝土抗拉強度，就會出現溫度裂縫，成為日後鹽害侵入的通道。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In a cap this thick the core temperature during hydration rises far above the surface, and if the tensile stress from the temperature difference exceeds the early-age tensile strength, thermal cracks form and later become paths for chloride ingress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"連續澆置中斷形成冷縫，或保溫不足使表面急冷，樁帽會出現貫穿或表層溫度裂縫；在河口鹽害與潮汐乾濕交替下，裂縫加速氯離子侵入，使鋼筋提前腐蝕。","textEn":"An interrupted pour that leaves a cold joint, or poor insulation that chills the surface, produces through or surface thermal cracks in the cap; under estuary salt exposure and tidal wetting and drying, the cracks accelerate chloride ingress and early corrosion of the reinforcement.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「58 支全套管基樁與大體積樁帽水化熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The 58-pile foundation and mass-concrete cap hydration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","連續澆置中斷形成冷縫，或保溫不足使表面急冷，樁帽會出現貫穿或表層溫度裂縫；在河口鹽害與潮汐乾濕交替下，裂縫加速氯離子侵入，使鋼筋提前腐蝕。","塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An interrupted pour that leaves a cold joint, or poor insulation that chills the surface, produces through or surface thermal cracks in the cap.","Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連續澆置中斷形成冷縫，或保溫不足使表面急冷，樁帽會出現貫穿或表層溫度裂縫；在河口鹽害與潮汐乾濕交替下，裂縫加速氯離子侵入，使鋼筋提前腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An interrupted pour that leaves a cold joint, or poor insulation that chills the surface, produces through or surface thermal cracks in the cap; under estuary salt exposure and tidal wetting and drying, the cracks accelerate chloride ingress and early corrosion of the reinforcement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":34}],"order":8},{"id":"danjiang-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位」與「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon\" and \"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-17","title":"211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「橋塔 53 個昇層」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “The 53 pylon lifts” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋橋塔高約 211 m，是三維曲面的單柱混凝土塔，公開報導指出以 53 個每層約 4 m 的昇層施築。曲面塔每一層的斷面形狀與中心都不同，模板必須逐層變形，且自重偏心會讓塔身在施工中逐漸彎曲；同時，太陽照射一側使塔身兩面溫差數度，就足以讓塔頂偏移十幾到數十公分。因此測量定位不能只看當下讀數，而要把溫度、自重偏心與後續斜索張拉造成的變形一起預測，才能讓完成時的塔軸落在設計位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「橋塔 53 個昇層」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Danjiang pylon is about 211 m tall, a single concrete mast with a three-dimensional curved surface, and public reports state it was built in 53 lifts of about 4 m. Each lift of a curved pylon has a different shape and centroid, so the formwork must change lift by lift, and the self-weight eccentricity gradually bends the shaft during construction. At the same time, sunlight on one side creates a temperature difference of a few degrees across the section, enough to move the top by tens of centimetres. Setting-out therefore cannot rely on the instantaneous reading; temperature, self-weight eccentricity and later stay stressing must be predicted together so that the completed axis lands in its design position. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “The 53 pylon lifts” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：線性溫差下懸臂塔頂偏位 Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a linear temperature difference the cantilever tip displacement is Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b).","failure":"常見誤解：「塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「橋塔 53 個昇層」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “The 53 pylon lifts”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-17-k1","title":"211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位","titleEn":"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon","text":"淡江大橋橋塔高約 211 m，是三維曲面的單柱混凝土塔，公開報導指出以 53 個每層約 4 m 的昇層施築。曲面塔每一層的斷面形狀與中心都不同，模板必須逐層變形，且自重偏心會讓塔身在施工中逐漸彎曲；同時，太陽照射一側使塔身兩面溫差數度，就足以讓塔頂偏移十幾到數十公分。","textEn":"The Danjiang pylon is about 211 m tall, a single concrete mast with a three-dimensional curved surface, and public reports state it was built in 53 lifts of about 4 m. Each lift of a curved pylon has a different shape and centroid, so the formwork must change lift by lift, and the self-weight eccentricity gradually bends the shaft during construction.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon\" is correct?","options":["塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。","合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","淡江大橋橋塔高約 211 m，是三維曲面的單柱混凝土塔，公開報導指出以 53 個每層約 4 m 的昇層施築。"],"optionsEn":["Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once.","A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","The Danjiang pylon is about 211 m tall, a single concrete mast with a three-dimensional curved surface, and public reports state it was built in 53 lifts of about 4 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"淡江大橋橋塔高約 211 m，是三維曲面的單柱混凝土塔，公開報導指出以 53 個每層約 4 m 的昇層施築。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Danjiang pylon is about 211 m tall, a single concrete mast with a three-dimensional curved surface, and public reports state it was built in 53 lifts of about 4 m. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":35},{"id":"danjiang-v13-18","title":"211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位：定量估算","titleEn":"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋塔 53 個昇層」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “The 53 pylon lifts” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：線性溫差下懸臂塔頂偏位 Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b)。取 α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C、斷面兩側溫差 ΔT = 10 °C、塔高 H = 200 m、斷面深 b = 8 m：Δ = 10⁻⁵×10×200²/(2×8) = 0.25 m；溫差降為 5 °C 時約 0.125 m。53 層×4 m = 212 m，與公開塔高約 211 m 一致。斷面與溫差為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a linear temperature difference the cantilever tip displacement is Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b). With α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C, a 10 °C difference across the section, H = 200 m and section depth b = 8 m, Δ = 10⁻⁵×10×200²/(2×8) = 0.25 m; a 5 °C difference gives about 0.125 m. 53 lifts × 4 m = 212 m, consistent with the published height of about 211 m. Section and temperature values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每一昇層在清晨溫度均勻時以全站儀與 GNSS 量測控制點，並同步讀取塔身溫度計；把實測與施工階段分析的預測偏位比對，再以三維雷射掃描與 BIM 模型比對曲面形狀，偏差超過允許值時調整下一層模板定位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: For each lift survey the control points at dawn, when temperature is uniform, with total station and GNSS while reading embedded thermometers; compare measured with predicted displacements from the staged analysis, compare the curved surface with the BIM model by 3D laser scanning, and adjust the next lift’s formwork when deviations exceed tolerance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"線性溫差下懸臂塔頂偏位 Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b)。取 α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C、斷面兩側溫差 ΔT = 10 °C、塔高 H = 200 m、斷面深 b = 8 m：Δ = 10⁻⁵×10×200²/(2×8) = 0.25 m；溫差降為 5 °C 時約 0.125 m。53 層×4 m = 212 m，與公開塔高約 211 m 一致。斷面與溫差為教學假設。","textEn":"For a linear temperature difference the cantilever tip displacement is Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b). With α = 1.0×10⁻⁵/°C, a 10 °C difference across the section, H = 200 m and section depth b = 8 m, Δ = 10⁻⁵×10×200²/(2×8) = 0.25 m; a 5 °C difference gives about 0.125 m. 53 lifts × 4 m = 212 m, consistent with the published height of about 211 m. Section and temperature values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon\", which statement holds?","options":["線性溫差下懸臂塔頂偏位 Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b)。","載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。","裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。"],"optionsEn":["For a linear temperature difference the cantilever tip displacement is Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b).","A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful.","A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線性溫差下懸臂塔頂偏位 Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a linear temperature difference the cantilever tip displacement is Δ = α·ΔT·H²/(2b). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":36},{"id":"danjiang-v13-19","title":"211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋塔 53 個昇層」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “The 53 pylon lifts” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每一昇層在清晨溫度均勻時以全站儀與 GNSS 量測控制點，並同步讀取塔身溫度計；把實測與施工階段分析的預測偏位比對，再以三維雷射掃描與 BIM 模型比對曲面形狀，偏差超過允許值時調整下一層模板定位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"For each lift survey the control points at dawn, when temperature is uniform, with total station and GNSS while reading embedded thermometers; compare measured with predicted displacements from the staged analysis, compare the curved surface with the BIM model by 3D laser scanning, and adjust the next lift’s formwork when deviations exceed tolerance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量程序應規定量測時段、溫度紀錄與預拱值表，模板定位以預測的「施工時應在位置」放樣而非設計最終座標；曲面塔每批昇層的掃描比對結果要經測量技師與設計單位共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey procedure should specify measurement times, temperature records and a pre-set table, setting formwork to the predicted as-built-at-this-stage position rather than final design coordinates; scan comparisons for each batch of curved lifts are co-signed by the surveyor and the designer.","failure":"注意干擾：若在午後量測並直接以讀數修正模板，會把暫時的日照偏位當成永久誤差，累積數層後塔軸偏離設計線；曲面模板定位錯誤還會使鋼筋保護層不足或錨固箱位置偏移，影響斜索角度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Surveying in the afternoon and correcting the formwork directly from the reading treats temporary solar sway as permanent error, and after several lifts the axis drifts off the design line; mispositioned curved formwork can also reduce cover or shift anchor boxes, changing stay angles. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每一昇層在清晨溫度均勻時以全站儀與 GNSS 量測控制點，並同步讀取塔身溫度計；把實測與施工階段分析的預測偏位比對，再以三維雷射掃描與 BIM 模型比對曲面形狀，偏差超過允許值時調整下一層模板定位。","textEn":"For each lift survey the control points at dawn, when temperature is uniform, with total station and GNSS while reading embedded thermometers; compare measured with predicted displacements from the staged analysis, compare the curved surface with the BIM model by 3D laser scanning, and adjust the next lift’s formwork when deviations exceed tolerance.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量程序應規定量測時段、溫度紀錄與預拱值表，模板定位以預測的「施工時應在位置」放樣而非設計最終座標；曲面塔每批昇層的掃描比對結果要經測量技師與設計單位共同簽認。","textEn":"The survey procedure should specify measurement times, temperature records and a pre-set table, setting formwork to the predicted as-built-at-this-stage position rather than final design coordinates; scan comparisons for each batch of curved lifts are co-signed by the surveyor and the designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每一昇層在清晨溫度均勻時以全站儀與 GNSS 量測控制點，並同步讀取塔身溫度計。","阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","For each lift survey the control points at dawn, when temperature is uniform, with total station and GNSS while reading embedded thermometers.","The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每一昇層在清晨溫度均勻時以全站儀與 GNSS 量測控制點，並同步讀取塔身溫度計；把實測與施工階段分析的預測偏位比對，再以三維雷射掃描與 BIM 模型比對曲面形狀，偏差超過允許值時調整下一層模板定位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"For each lift survey the control points at dawn, when temperature is uniform, with total station and GNSS while reading embedded thermometers; compare measured with predicted displacements from the staged analysis, compare the curved surface with the BIM model by 3D laser scanning, and adjust the next lift’s formwork when deviations exceed tolerance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":37},{"id":"danjiang-v13-20","title":"211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋塔 53 個昇層」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “The 53 pylon lifts” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在午後量測並直接以讀數修正模板，會把暫時的日照偏位當成永久誤差，累積數層後塔軸偏離設計線；曲面模板定位錯誤還會使鋼筋保護層不足或錨固箱位置偏移，影響斜索角度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Surveying in the afternoon and correcting the formwork directly from the reading treats temporary solar sway as permanent error, and after several lifts the axis drifts off the design line; mispositioned curved formwork can also reduce cover or shift anchor boxes, changing stay angles. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此測量定位不能只看當下讀數，而要把溫度、自重偏心與後續斜索張拉造成的變形一起預測，才能讓完成時的塔軸落在設計位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Setting-out therefore cannot rely on the instantaneous reading; temperature, self-weight eccentricity and later stay stressing must be predicted together so that the completed axis lands in its design position.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在午後量測並直接以讀數修正模板，會把暫時的日照偏位當成永久誤差，累積數層後塔軸偏離設計線；曲面模板定位錯誤還會使鋼筋保護層不足或錨固箱位置偏移，影響斜索角度。","textEn":"Surveying in the afternoon and correcting the formwork directly from the reading treats temporary solar sway as permanent error, and after several lifts the axis drifts off the design line; mispositioned curved formwork can also reduce cover or shift anchor boxes, changing stay angles.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「211 m 曲面橋塔的昇層施工與日照偏位」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lift-by-lift construction and solar sway of the 211 m curved pylon\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","若在午後量測並直接以讀數修正模板，會把暫時的日照偏位當成永久誤差，累積數層後塔軸偏離設計線；曲面模板定位錯誤還會使鋼筋保護層不足或錨固箱位置偏移，影響斜索角度。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","Surveying in the afternoon and correcting the formwork directly from the reading treats temporary solar sway as permanent error, and after several lifts the axis drifts off the design line."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若在午後量測並直接以讀數修正模板，會把暫時的日照偏位當成永久誤差，累積數層後塔軸偏離設計線；曲面模板定位錯誤還會使鋼筋保護層不足或錨固箱位置偏移，影響斜索角度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Surveying in the afternoon and correcting the formwork directly from the reading treats temporary solar sway as permanent error, and after several lifts the axis drifts off the design line; mispositioned curved formwork can also reduce cover or shift anchor boxes, changing stay angles. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":38},{"id":"danjiang-v13-21","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「26 號合龍節塊」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closure segment no. 26” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁以船運到橋下、由懸臂端吊裝，公開報導指出一般節塊約 400 至 500 t，全橋採全焊接以減輕約一成重量。最後的八里側 26 號合龍節塊長約 15.2 m、寬約 51.3 m、重約 390 t，選在漲潮時段吊裝以免駁船擱淺，吊裝前一天早、中、晚量測橋面高程與伸縮。懸臂鋼梁會隨溫度伸縮與起伏，合龍口的長度與高差在一天內持續改變；合龍前的大懸臂在強風下也曾出現約 40 cm 的擺動，所以合龍必須在溫度與風況都穩定的窗口完成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「26 號合龍節塊」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder segments were barged to the site and lifted at the cantilever tips; public reports cite typical segments of about 400 to 500 t, with full welding saving about a tenth of the weight. The final closure segment no. 26 on the Bali side is about 15.2 m long, 51.3 m wide and 390 t, lifted at high tide so the barge would not ground, after deck levels and expansion were measured morning, noon and evening the day before. A steel cantilever lengthens and rises or falls with temperature, so the closure gap’s length and level difference change throughout the day; before closure the long cantilever was also reported to sway about 40 cm in strong wind, so closure must be completed in a window of stable temperature and wind. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Closure segment no. 26” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：合龍口長度變化 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Change in closure-gap length ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","failure":"常見誤解：「合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「26 號合龍節塊」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Closure segment no. 26”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-21-k1","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口","titleEn":"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window","text":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁以船運到橋下、由懸臂端吊裝，公開報導指出一般節塊約 400 至 500 t，全橋採全焊接以減輕約一成重量。最後的八里側 26 號合龍節塊長約 15.2 m、寬約 51.3 m、重約 390 t，選在漲潮時段吊裝以免駁船擱淺，吊裝前一天早、中、晚量測橋面高程與伸縮。","textEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder segments were barged to the site and lifted at the cantilever tips; public reports cite typical segments of about 400 to 500 t, with full welding saving about a tenth of the weight. The final closure segment no.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window\" is correct?","options":["淡江大橋鋼箱梁以船運到橋下、由懸臂端吊裝，公開報導指出一般節塊約 400 至 500 t，全橋採全焊接以減輕約一成重量。","合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。"],"optionsEn":["The Danjiang steel box girder segments were barged to the site and lifted at the cantilever tips.","A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁以船運到橋下、由懸臂端吊裝，公開報導指出一般節塊約 400 至 500 t，全橋採全焊接以減輕約一成重量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder segments were barged to the site and lifted at the cantilever tips; public reports cite typical segments of about 400 to 500 t, with full welding saving about a tenth of the weight. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":39},{"id":"danjiang-v13-22","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口：定量估算","titleEn":"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「26 號合龍節塊」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closure segment no. 26” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：合龍口長度變化 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。取鋼 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、自固定點起算 L = 430 m、早晚溫差 ΔT = 15 °C：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×430×15 ≈ 0.077 m，即約 77 mm；若只差 5 °C 則約 26 mm。溫度與長度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Change in closure-gap length ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With steel α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 430 m from the fixed point and a 15 °C morning-to-afternoon difference, ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×430×15 ≈ 0.077 m, about 77 mm; a 5 °C difference gives about 26 mm. Temperatures and length are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：合龍前連續 24 至 72 小時記錄合龍口長度、高差、橋面溫度與風速，回歸出長度—溫度關係，選定合龍溫度並據以決定節塊配切長度；吊裝後先以臨時鎖定裝置固定，再於預定溫度區間內完成焊接，並複量全橋線形與索力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record gap length, level difference, deck temperature and wind speed continuously for 24 to 72 hours before closure, regress length against temperature, choose the closure temperature and set the segment’s trimmed length; after lifting, lock the segment with temporary devices, complete welding within the chosen temperature band and re-survey the profile and stay forces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"合龍口長度變化 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。取鋼 α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C、自固定點起算 L = 430 m、早晚溫差 ΔT = 15 °C：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×430×15 ≈ 0.077 m，即約 77 mm；若只差 5 °C 則約 26 mm。溫度與長度為教學假設。","textEn":"Change in closure-gap length ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With steel α = 1.2×10⁻⁵/°C, L = 430 m from the fixed point and a 15 °C morning-to-afternoon difference, ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×430×15 ≈ 0.077 m, about 77 mm; a 5 °C difference gives about 26 mm. Temperatures and length are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。","合龍口長度變化 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.","Change in closure-gap length ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"合龍口長度變化 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Change in closure-gap length ΔL = α·L·ΔT. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":40},{"id":"danjiang-v13-23","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「26 號合龍節塊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closure segment no. 26” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"合龍前連續 24 至 72 小時記錄合龍口長度、高差、橋面溫度與風速，回歸出長度—溫度關係，選定合龍溫度並據以決定節塊配切長度；吊裝後先以臨時鎖定裝置固定，再於預定溫度區間內完成焊接，並複量全橋線形與索力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record gap length, level difference, deck temperature and wind speed continuously for 24 to 72 hours before closure, regress length against temperature, choose the closure temperature and set the segment’s trimmed length; after lifting, lock the segment with temporary devices, complete welding within the chosen temperature band and re-survey the profile and stay forces. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合龍作業應有獨立的施工計畫：量測期、溫度與風速作業門檻、潮位窗口、臨時鎖定順序、焊接程序與中止條件，並由監造單位設為停留檢查點，未經簽認不得解除臨時鎖定。","observationEn":"Site practice: Closure needs its own method statement: measurement period, temperature and wind thresholds, tidal window, temporary locking sequence, welding procedure and abort criteria, with the supervising engineer holding a hold point so temporary locks are not released without sign-off.","failure":"注意干擾：未依溫度窗口配切或鎖定，合龍口在焊接期間張開或擠壓，造成焊道開裂、內應力殘留或強迫頂推；若在強風擺動中強行對位，吊具與臨時連接可能承受衝擊，危及作業人員。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without trimming and locking to the temperature window, the gap opens or closes during welding, cracking welds, leaving residual stress or forcing the cantilevers apart; forcing alignment while the cantilever sways in wind can shock-load rigging and temporary connections and endanger the crew. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"合龍前連續 24 至 72 小時記錄合龍口長度、高差、橋面溫度與風速，回歸出長度—溫度關係，選定合龍溫度並據以決定節塊配切長度；吊裝後先以臨時鎖定裝置固定，再於預定溫度區間內完成焊接，並複量全橋線形與索力。","textEn":"Record gap length, level difference, deck temperature and wind speed continuously for 24 to 72 hours before closure, regress length against temperature, choose the closure temperature and set the segment’s trimmed length; after lifting, lock the segment with temporary devices, complete welding within the chosen temperature band and re-survey the profile and stay forces.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合龍作業應有獨立的施工計畫：量測期、溫度與風速作業門檻、潮位窗口、臨時鎖定順序、焊接程序與中止條件，並由監造單位設為停留檢查點，未經簽認不得解除臨時鎖定。","textEn":"Closure needs its own method statement: measurement period, temperature and wind thresholds, tidal window, temporary locking sequence, welding procedure and abort criteria, with the supervising engineer holding a hold point so temporary locks are not released without sign-off.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。","合龍前連續 24 至 72 小時記錄合龍口長度、高差、橋面溫度與風速，回歸出長度—溫度關係，選定合龍溫度並據以決定節塊配切長度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.","Record gap length, level difference, deck temperature and wind speed continuously for 24 to 72 hours before closure, regress length against temperature, choose the closure temperature and set the segment’s trimmed length."],"answer":2,"explanation":"合龍前連續 24 至 72 小時記錄合龍口長度、高差、橋面溫度與風速，回歸出長度—溫度關係，選定合龍溫度並據以決定節塊配切長度；吊裝後先以臨時鎖定裝置固定，再於預定溫度區間內完成焊接，並複量全橋線形與索力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record gap length, level difference, deck temperature and wind speed continuously for 24 to 72 hours before closure, regress length against temperature, choose the closure temperature and set the segment’s trimmed length; after lifting, lock the segment with temporary devices, complete welding within the chosen temperature band and re-survey the profile and stay forces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":41},{"id":"danjiang-v13-24","title":"鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「26 號合龍節塊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closure segment no. 26” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未依溫度窗口配切或鎖定，合龍口在焊接期間張開或擠壓，造成焊道開裂、內應力殘留或強迫頂推；若在強風擺動中強行對位，吊具與臨時連接可能承受衝擊，危及作業人員。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without trimming and locking to the temperature window, the gap opens or closes during welding, cracking welds, leaving residual stress or forcing the cantilevers apart; forcing alignment while the cantilever sways in wind can shock-load rigging and temporary connections and endanger the crew. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：懸臂鋼梁會隨溫度伸縮與起伏，合龍口的長度與高差在一天內持續改變；合龍前的大懸臂在強風下也曾出現約 40 cm 的擺動，所以合龍必須在溫度與風況都穩定的窗口完成。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A steel cantilever lengthens and rises or falls with temperature, so the closure gap’s length and level difference change throughout the day; before closure the long cantilever was also reported to sway about 40 cm in strong wind, so closure must be completed in a window of stable temperature and wind.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未依溫度窗口配切或鎖定，合龍口在焊接期間張開或擠壓，造成焊道開裂、內應力殘留或強迫頂推；若在強風擺動中強行對位，吊具與臨時連接可能承受衝擊，危及作業人員。","textEn":"Without trimming and locking to the temperature window, the gap opens or closes during welding, cracking welds, leaving residual stress or forcing the cantilevers apart; forcing alignment while the cantilever sways in wind can shock-load rigging and temporary connections and endanger the crew.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼箱梁懸臂吊裝與合龍溫度窗口」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cantilever erection and the closure temperature window\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未依溫度窗口配切或鎖定，合龍口在焊接期間張開或擠壓，造成焊道開裂、內應力殘留或強迫頂推；若在強風擺動中強行對位，吊具與臨時連接可能承受衝擊，危及作業人員。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。"],"optionsEn":["Without trimming and locking to the temperature window, the gap opens or closes during welding, cracking welds, leaving residual stress or forcing the cantilevers apart.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未依溫度窗口配切或鎖定，合龍口在焊接期間張開或擠壓，造成焊道開裂、內應力殘留或強迫頂推；若在強風擺動中強行對位，吊具與臨時連接可能承受衝擊，危及作業人員。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without trimming and locking to the temperature window, the gap opens or closes during welding, cracking welds, leaving residual stress or forcing the cantilevers apart; forcing alignment while the cantilever sways in wind can shock-load rigging and temporary connections and endanger the crew. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":42}],"order":9},{"id":"danjiang-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀」與「載重試驗與實測勁度比對」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration\" and \"Load testing and measured stiffness\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-25","title":"風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「斷面與全橋風洞模型」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Section and full-bridge wind models” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋以斷面模型與全橋模型風洞試驗輔以數值分析，檢查施工階段與完工後的穩定、車輛與行人舒適性及纜索風致振動，並以 1:200 模型測試獨立橋塔，結果未見氣動或氣彈不穩定。鋼箱梁在中低風速下最常見的問題是渦致振動：氣流在箱梁下游交替脫落渦流，頻率接近橋面的垂直或扭轉頻率時產生有限振幅的鎖定振動。欄杆、防風屏與檢修車軌道都會改變斷面形狀，因此試驗模型必須包含這些附屬物。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「斷面與全橋風洞模型」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge was checked by section-model and full-bridge wind-tunnel tests supported by numerical analysis for stability during construction and in service, vehicle and pedestrian comfort and wind-induced cable vibration, with a 1:200 model of the free-standing pylon, and that no aerodynamic or aeroelastic instability was found. The commonest problem for a steel box deck at low and moderate wind is vortex-induced vibration: vortices shed alternately behind the box and, when their frequency approaches a vertical or torsional deck frequency, cause limited-amplitude lock-in. Railings, wind screens and inspection-gantry rails all change the section shape, so test models must include them. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Section and full-bridge wind models” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：渦流脫落鎖定風速 U = f·D/St。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Vortex lock-in wind speed U = f·D/St. With vertical bending frequency f = 0.35 Hz, characteristic depth including attachments D = 3.5 m and St = 0.10, U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s; if railings change St to 0.12, U ≈ 10.2 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「斷面與全橋風洞模型」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Section and full-bridge wind models”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-25-k1","title":"風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration","text":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋以斷面模型與全橋模型風洞試驗輔以數值分析，檢查施工階段與完工後的穩定、車輛與行人舒適性及纜索風致振動，並以 1:200 模型測試獨立橋塔，結果未見氣動或氣彈不穩定。鋼箱梁在中低風速下最常見的問題是渦致振動：氣流在箱梁下游交替脫落渦流，頻率接近橋面的垂直或扭轉頻率時產生有限振幅的鎖定振動。","textEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge was checked by section-model and full-bridge wind-tunnel tests supported by numerical analysis for stability during construction and in service, vehicle and pedestrian comfort and wind-induced cable vibration, with a 1:200 model of the free-standing pylon, and that no aerodynamic or aeroelastic instability was found. The commonest problem for a steel box deck at low and moderate wind is vortex-induced vibration: vortices shed alternately behind the box and, when their frequency approaches a vertical or torsional deck frequency, cause limited-amplitude lock-in.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration\" is correct?","options":["風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。","公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋以斷面模型與全橋模型風洞試驗輔以數值分析，檢查施工階段與完工後的穩定、車輛與行人舒適性及纜索風致振動，並以 1:200 模型測試獨立橋塔，結果未見氣動或氣彈不穩定。","載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。"],"optionsEn":["Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter.","Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge was checked by section-model and full-bridge wind-tunnel tests supported by numerical analysis for stability during construction and in service, vehicle and pedestrian comfort and wind-induced cable vibration, with a 1:200 model of the free-standing pylon, and that no aerodynamic or aeroelastic instability was found.","A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公路局公開資料指出，淡江大橋以斷面模型與全橋模型風洞試驗輔以數值分析，檢查施工階段與完工後的穩定、車輛與行人舒適性及纜索風致振動，並以 1:200 模型測試獨立橋塔，結果未見氣動或氣彈不穩定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge was checked by section-model and full-bridge wind-tunnel tests supported by numerical analysis for stability during construction and in service, vehicle and pedestrian comfort and wind-induced cable vibration, with a 1:200 model of the free-standing pylon, and that no aerodynamic or aeroelastic instability was found. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":43},{"id":"danjiang-v13-26","title":"風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面與全橋風洞模型」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Section and full-bridge wind models” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：渦流脫落鎖定風速 U = f·D/St。取垂直彎曲頻率 f = 0.35 Hz、箱梁含附屬物的特徵高度 D = 3.5 m、St = 0.10：U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s；若欄杆改變使 St 變為 0.12，U ≈ 10.2 m/s。這屬日常季風風速範圍，所以要靠試驗確認振幅。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Vortex lock-in wind speed U = f·D/St. With vertical bending frequency f = 0.35 Hz, characteristic depth including attachments D = 3.5 m and St = 0.10, U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s; if railings change St to 0.12, U ≈ 10.2 m/s. These are everyday monsoon wind speeds, so amplitudes must be confirmed by testing. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：斷面模型以彈簧懸掛做自由振動與風速掃描，記錄振幅—風速曲線並換算成實橋加速度，與行人與行車舒適準則比較；全橋氣彈模型檢查施工最長懸臂與成橋狀態；完工後以橋面加速度計與風速計長期紀錄，比對實測鎖定風速與振幅。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Spring-mount the section model for free-vibration and wind-speed sweeps, record amplitude versus wind speed, scale to full-size acceleration and compare with pedestrian and driving comfort criteria; use the full aeroelastic model for the longest construction cantilever and the completed state; after completion log deck accelerometers and anemometers long term and compare measured lock-in speeds and amplitudes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"渦流脫落鎖定風速 U = f·D/St。取垂直彎曲頻率 f = 0.35 Hz、箱梁含附屬物的特徵高度 D = 3.5 m、St = 0.10：U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s；若欄杆改變使 St 變為 0.12，U ≈ 10.2 m/s。這屬日常季風風速範圍，所以要靠試驗確認振幅。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Vortex lock-in wind speed U = f·D/St. With vertical bending frequency f = 0.35 Hz, characteristic depth including attachments D = 3.5 m and St = 0.10, U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s; if railings change St to 0.12, U ≈ 10.2 m/s. These are everyday monsoon wind speeds, so amplitudes must be confirmed by testing. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration\", which statement holds?","options":["裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。","阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。","渦流脫落鎖定風速 U = f·D/St。"],"optionsEn":["A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection.","The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake.","Vortex lock-in wind speed U = f·D/St. With vertical bending frequency f = 0.35 Hz, characteristic depth including attachments D = 3.5 m and St = 0.10, U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"渦流脫落鎖定風速 U = f·D/St。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Vortex lock-in wind speed U = f·D/St. With vertical bending frequency f = 0.35 Hz, characteristic depth including attachments D = 3.5 m and St = 0.10, U = 0.35×3.5/0.10 ≈ 12.3 m/s; if railings change St to 0.12, U ≈ 10.2 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":44},{"id":"danjiang-v13-27","title":"風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面與全橋風洞模型」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Section and full-bridge wind models” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"斷面模型以彈簧懸掛做自由振動與風速掃描，記錄振幅—風速曲線並換算成實橋加速度，與行人與行車舒適準則比較；全橋氣彈模型檢查施工最長懸臂與成橋狀態；完工後以橋面加速度計與風速計長期紀錄，比對實測鎖定風速與振幅。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Spring-mount the section model for free-vibration and wind-speed sweeps, record amplitude versus wind speed, scale to full-size acceleration and compare with pedestrian and driving comfort criteria; use the full aeroelastic model for the longest construction cantilever and the completed state; after completion log deck accelerometers and anemometers long term and compare measured lock-in speeds and amplitudes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何欄杆、防風屏、燈桿或標誌的形狀變更，都應回送風工程顧問評估是否需補做斷面試驗；施工最長懸臂狀態要訂出停工風速與臨時抗風措施。","observationEn":"Site practice: Any change to railings, wind screens, lighting columns or signs should go back to the wind consultant to decide whether further section tests are needed; the longest-cantilever stage needs a stop-work wind speed and temporary wind measures.","failure":"注意干擾：完工後更換欄杆或加裝屏障而未重新評估，可能讓原本安全的斷面出現渦振或噪音；淡江大橋通車後曾有東北季風吹過欄杆產生低頻聲響的反映，顯示附屬物的氣動細節同樣影響使用性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Changing railings or adding screens after completion without re-evaluation can introduce vortex vibration or noise in a previously safe section; after the Danjiang Bridge opened, low-frequency sound from northeast-monsoon wind passing the railings was reported, showing that attachment details also affect serviceability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"斷面模型以彈簧懸掛做自由振動與風速掃描，記錄振幅—風速曲線並換算成實橋加速度，與行人與行車舒適準則比較；全橋氣彈模型檢查施工最長懸臂與成橋狀態；完工後以橋面加速度計與風速計長期紀錄，比對實測鎖定風速與振幅。","textEn":"Spring-mount the section model for free-vibration and wind-speed sweeps, record amplitude versus wind speed, scale to full-size acceleration and compare with pedestrian and driving comfort criteria; use the full aeroelastic model for the longest construction cantilever and the completed state; after completion log deck accelerometers and anemometers long term and compare measured lock-in speeds and amplitudes.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何欄杆、防風屏、燈桿或標誌的形狀變更，都應回送風工程顧問評估是否需補做斷面試驗；施工最長懸臂狀態要訂出停工風速與臨時抗風措施。","textEn":"Any change to railings, wind screens, lighting columns or signs should go back to the wind consultant to decide whether further section tests are needed; the longest-cantilever stage needs a stop-work wind speed and temporary wind measures.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration\"?","options":["斷面模型以彈簧懸掛做自由振動與風速掃描，記錄振幅—風速曲線並換算成實橋加速度，與行人與行車舒適準則比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。"],"optionsEn":["Spring-mount the section model for free-vibration and wind-speed sweeps, record amplitude versus wind speed, scale to full-size acceleration and compare with pedestrian and driving comfort criteria.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"斷面模型以彈簧懸掛做自由振動與風速掃描，記錄振幅—風速曲線並換算成實橋加速度，與行人與行車舒適準則比較；全橋氣彈模型檢查施工最長懸臂與成橋狀態；完工後以橋面加速度計與風速計長期紀錄，比對實測鎖定風速與振幅。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Spring-mount the section model for free-vibration and wind-speed sweeps, record amplitude versus wind speed, scale to full-size acceleration and compare with pedestrian and driving comfort criteria; use the full aeroelastic model for the longest construction cantilever and the completed state; after completion log deck accelerometers and anemometers long term and compare measured lock-in speeds and amplitudes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":45},{"id":"danjiang-v13-28","title":"風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面與全橋風洞模型」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Section and full-bridge wind models” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"完工後更換欄杆或加裝屏障而未重新評估，可能讓原本安全的斷面出現渦振或噪音；淡江大橋通車後曾有東北季風吹過欄杆產生低頻聲響的反映，顯示附屬物的氣動細節同樣影響使用性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Changing railings or adding screens after completion without re-evaluation can introduce vortex vibration or noise in a previously safe section; after the Danjiang Bridge opened, low-frequency sound from northeast-monsoon wind passing the railings was reported, showing that attachment details also affect serviceability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：欄杆、防風屏與檢修車軌道都會改變斷面形狀，因此試驗模型必須包含這些附屬物。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Railings, wind screens and inspection-gantry rails all change the section shape, so test models must include them.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"完工後更換欄杆或加裝屏障而未重新評估，可能讓原本安全的斷面出現渦振或噪音；淡江大橋通車後曾有東北季風吹過欄杆產生低頻聲響的反映，顯示附屬物的氣動細節同樣影響使用性。","textEn":"Changing railings or adding screens after completion without re-evaluation can introduce vortex vibration or noise in a previously safe section; after the Danjiang Bridge opened, low-frequency sound from northeast-monsoon wind passing the railings was reported, showing that attachment details also affect serviceability.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「風洞試驗與渦致振動判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind-tunnel testing and vortex-induced vibration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","完工後更換欄杆或加裝屏障而未重新評估，可能讓原本安全的斷面出現渦振或噪音。","載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Changing railings or adding screens after completion without re-evaluation can introduce vortex vibration or noise in a previously safe section.","A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful."],"answer":1,"explanation":"完工後更換欄杆或加裝屏障而未重新評估，可能讓原本安全的斷面出現渦振或噪音；淡江大橋通車後曾有東北季風吹過欄杆產生低頻聲響的反映，顯示附屬物的氣動細節同樣影響使用性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Changing railings or adding screens after completion without re-evaluation can introduce vortex vibration or noise in a previously safe section; after the Danjiang Bridge opened, low-frequency sound from northeast-monsoon wind passing the railings was reported, showing that attachment details also affect serviceability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":46},{"id":"danjiang-v13-29","title":"載重試驗與實測勁度比對：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Load testing and measured stiffness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「通車前載重試驗」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pre-opening load test” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋在通車前安排斜拉索重新張拉檢查與載重試驗。載重試驗以已知重量的卡車車隊在預定位置停放，量測主跨撓度、塔頂偏位、索力增量與關鍵斷面應變，再與結構模型在相同載重下的預測比較。實測撓度略小於預測通常代表實際勁度較高（鋪面、欄杆參與），若明顯大於預測或卸載後殘留變形過大，則可能有支承、索力或連接的問題。這些結果也成為日後監測的基準狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「通車前載重試驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before opening, the Danjiang Bridge scheduled stay re-tensioning checks and a load test. A load test parks a fleet of trucks of known weight at planned positions and measures main-span deflection, pylon-top displacement, stay-force increments and strains at key sections, compared with the structural model’s predictions under the same load. Measured deflection slightly below prediction usually means real stiffness is higher (surfacing and railings participate); deflection clearly above prediction, or large residual deformation after unloading, may point to bearing, stay-force or connection problems. The results also become the baseline for later monitoring. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pre-opening load test” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：16 輛 35 t 卡車合計 560 t（約 5,494 kN）置於主跨中段，模型預測撓度 0.45 m，等效勁度 k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m；實測 0.40 m，實測／計算比 = 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89；卸載後殘留 0.03 m，殘留率 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Sixteen 35 t trucks, 560 t in total (about 5,494 kN), are placed near mid main span; the model predicts 0.45 m of deflection, an equivalent stiffness k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「通車前載重試驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pre-opening load test”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-29-k1","title":"載重試驗與實測勁度比對","titleEn":"Load testing and measured stiffness","text":"淡江大橋在通車前安排斜拉索重新張拉檢查與載重試驗。載重試驗以已知重量的卡車車隊在預定位置停放，量測主跨撓度、塔頂偏位、索力增量與關鍵斷面應變，再與結構模型在相同載重下的預測比較。","textEn":"Before opening, the Danjiang Bridge scheduled stay re-tensioning checks and a load test. A load test parks a fleet of trucks of known weight at planned positions and measures main-span deflection, pylon-top displacement, stay-force increments and strains at key sections, compared with the structural model’s predictions under the same load.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「載重試驗與實測勁度比對」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Load testing and measured stiffness\" is correct?","options":["載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。","鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。","淡江大橋在通車前安排斜拉索重新張拉檢查與載重試驗。"],"optionsEn":["A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful.","Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.","Before opening, the Danjiang Bridge scheduled stay re-tensioning checks and a load test."],"answer":2,"explanation":"淡江大橋在通車前安排斜拉索重新張拉檢查與載重試驗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before opening, the Danjiang Bridge scheduled stay re-tensioning checks and a load test. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":47},{"id":"danjiang-v13-30","title":"載重試驗與實測勁度比對：定量估算","titleEn":"Load testing and measured stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通車前載重試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pre-opening load test” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：16 輛 35 t 卡車合計 560 t（約 5,494 kN）置於主跨中段，模型預測撓度 0.45 m，等效勁度 k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m；實測 0.40 m，實測／計算比 = 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89；卸載後殘留 0.03 m，殘留率 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Sixteen 35 t trucks, 560 t in total (about 5,494 kN), are placed near mid main span; the model predicts 0.45 m of deflection, an equivalent stiffness k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m. Measured deflection is 0.40 m, a measured-to-calculated ratio of 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89; a residual of 0.03 m after unloading is 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗計畫事先列出載重位置、分級加載、量測點（GNSS、水準、應變計、索力計）、穩定判定與允收準則（例如實測／計算比落在約 0.7 至 1.0、殘留率低於約 20%）；量測同步記錄溫度，必要時以空載基準扣除溫度變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The test plan lists load positions, load steps, measurement points (GNSS, levelling, strain gauges, stay-force sensors), stabilisation criteria and acceptance limits (for example a measured-to-calculated ratio of about 0.7 to 1.0 and residual below about 20%), with temperature recorded simultaneously so thermal deformation can be removed against an unloaded baseline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"16 輛 35 t 卡車合計 560 t（約 5,494 kN）置於主跨中段，模型預測撓度 0.45 m，等效勁度 k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m；實測 0.40 m，實測／計算比 = 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89；卸載後殘留 0.03 m，殘留率 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Sixteen 35 t trucks, 560 t in total (about 5,494 kN), are placed near mid main span; the model predicts 0.45 m of deflection, an equivalent stiffness k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m. Measured deflection is 0.40 m, a measured-to-calculated ratio of 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89; a residual of 0.03 m after unloading is 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「載重試驗與實測勁度比對」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Load testing and measured stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["16 輛 35 t 卡車合計 560 t（約 5,494 kN）置於主跨中段，模型預測撓度 0.45 m，等效勁度 k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m。","單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。","斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。"],"optionsEn":["Sixteen 35 t trucks, 560 t in total (about 5,494 kN), are placed near mid main span.","In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough.","Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones."],"answer":0,"explanation":"16 輛 35 t 卡車合計 560 t（約 5,494 kN）置於主跨中段，模型預測撓度 0.45 m，等效勁度 k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m；實測 0.40 m，實測／計算比 = 0.40/0.45 ≈ 0.89；卸載後殘留 0.03 m，殘留率 0.03/0.40 = 7.5%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Sixteen 35 t trucks, 560 t in total (about 5,494 kN), are placed near mid main span; the model predicts 0.45 m of deflection, an equivalent stiffness k = 5,494/0.45 ≈ 12,200 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":48},{"id":"danjiang-v13-31","title":"載重試驗與實測勁度比對：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Load testing and measured stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通車前載重試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pre-opening load test” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗計畫事先列出載重位置、分級加載、量測點（GNSS、水準、應變計、索力計）、穩定判定與允收準則（例如實測／計算比落在約 0.7 至 1.0、殘留率低於約 20%）；量測同步記錄溫度，必要時以空載基準扣除溫度變形。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The test plan lists load positions, load steps, measurement points (GNSS, levelling, strain gauges, stay-force sensors), stabilisation criteria and acceptance limits (for example a measured-to-calculated ratio of about 0.7 to 1.0 and residual below about 20%), with temperature recorded simultaneously so thermal deformation can be removed against an unloaded baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：載重試驗要與索力復測、支承與伸縮縫位置紀錄一起做成成橋基準檔案；卡車重量需經地磅秤重並存證，試驗期間封閉交通並由專人指揮車隊定位。","observationEn":"Site practice: Combine the load test with stay-force re-measurement and records of bearing and joint positions into the as-completed baseline file; weigh each truck on a certified weighbridge, keep the tickets, close the bridge during the test and have a marshal position the trucks.","failure":"注意干擾：若試驗在日照強烈時進行且未修正溫度，橋面熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，使判讀失真；若比值異常卻直接放行通車，可能錯過支承卡死、索力分配錯誤或焊接缺陷等早期問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing in strong sunshine without temperature correction lets thermal deck movement reach the same order as load deflection and distorts interpretation; opening the bridge despite abnormal ratios can miss early problems such as seized bearings, misallocated stay forces or weld defects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗計畫事先列出載重位置、分級加載、量測點（GNSS、水準、應變計、索力計）、穩定判定與允收準則（例如實測／計算比落在約 0.7 至 1.0、殘留率低於約 20%）；量測同步記錄溫度，必要時以空載基準扣除溫度變形。","textEn":"The test plan lists load positions, load steps, measurement points (GNSS, levelling, strain gauges, stay-force sensors), stabilisation criteria and acceptance limits (for example a measured-to-calculated ratio of about 0.7 to 1.0 and residual below about 20%), with temperature recorded simultaneously so thermal deformation can be removed against an unloaded baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"載重試驗要與索力復測、支承與伸縮縫位置紀錄一起做成成橋基準檔案；卡車重量需經地磅秤重並存證，試驗期間封閉交通並由專人指揮車隊定位。","textEn":"Combine the load test with stay-force re-measurement and records of bearing and joint positions into the as-completed baseline file; weigh each truck on a certified weighbridge, keep the tickets, close the bridge during the test and have a marshal position the trucks.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「載重試驗與實測勁度比對」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Load testing and measured stiffness\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","試驗計畫事先列出載重位置、分級加載、量測點（GNSS、水準、應變計、索力計）、穩定判定與允收準則（例如實測／計算比落在約 0.7 至 1.0、殘留率低於約 20%）。","塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","The test plan lists load positions, load steps, measurement points (GNSS, levelling, strain gauges, stay-force sensors), stabilisation criteria and acceptance limits (for example a measured-to-calculated ratio of about 0.7 to 1.0 and residual below about 20%), with temperature recorded simultaneously so thermal deformation can be removed against an unloaded baseline.","Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試驗計畫事先列出載重位置、分級加載、量測點（GNSS、水準、應變計、索力計）、穩定判定與允收準則（例如實測／計算比落在約 0.7 至 1.0、殘留率低於約 20%）；量測同步記錄溫度，必要時以空載基準扣除溫度變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The test plan lists load positions, load steps, measurement points (GNSS, levelling, strain gauges, stay-force sensors), stabilisation criteria and acceptance limits (for example a measured-to-calculated ratio of about 0.7 to 1.0 and residual below about 20%), with temperature recorded simultaneously so thermal deformation can be removed against an unloaded baseline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":49},{"id":"danjiang-v13-32","title":"載重試驗與實測勁度比對：失效診斷","titleEn":"Load testing and measured stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通車前載重試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pre-opening load test” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若試驗在日照強烈時進行且未修正溫度，橋面熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，使判讀失真；若比值異常卻直接放行通車，可能錯過支承卡死、索力分配錯誤或焊接缺陷等早期問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing in strong sunshine without temperature correction lets thermal deck movement reach the same order as load deflection and distorts interpretation; opening the bridge despite abnormal ratios can miss early problems such as seized bearings, misallocated stay forces or weld defects. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些結果也成為日後監測的基準狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The results also become the baseline for later monitoring.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「載重試驗撓度比計算值小，就代表設計太保守、浪費材料。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A load-test deflection smaller than calculated means the design was overly conservative and wasteful.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若試驗在日照強烈時進行且未修正溫度，橋面熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，使判讀失真；若比值異常卻直接放行通車，可能錯過支承卡死、索力分配錯誤或焊接缺陷等早期問題。","textEn":"Testing in strong sunshine without temperature correction lets thermal deck movement reach the same order as load deflection and distorts interpretation; opening the bridge despite abnormal ratios can miss early problems such as seized bearings, misallocated stay forces or weld defects.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載重試驗與實測勁度比對」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Load testing and measured stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。","若試驗在日照強烈時進行且未修正溫度，橋面熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，使判讀失真；若比值異常卻直接放行通車，可能錯過支承卡死、索力分配錯誤或焊接缺陷等早期問題。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.","Testing in strong sunshine without temperature correction lets thermal deck movement reach the same order as load deflection and distorts interpretation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若試驗在日照強烈時進行且未修正溫度，橋面熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，使判讀失真；若比值異常卻直接放行通車，可能錯過支承卡死、索力分配錯誤或焊接缺陷等早期問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing in strong sunshine without temperature correction lets thermal deck movement reach the same order as load deflection and distorts interpretation; opening the bridge despite abnormal ratios can miss early problems such as seized bearings, misallocated stay forces or weld defects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":50}],"order":10},{"id":"danjiang-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度」與「監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness\" and \"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-33","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「U 肋與橫隔板交接」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rib-to-diaphragm joints” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁採全焊接，橋面板上鋪 GUSS 澆注式瀝青。正交異性橋面的疲勞熱點集中在輪載正下方：U 肋與面板的縱向焊道、U 肋穿過橫隔板的切口，以及現場對接的 U 肋接頭。鋪面不是只有防水與行車舒適的功能，它與鋼板共同受力時能明顯降低局部應力幅；但瀝青模數隨溫度大幅下降，夏季高溫時鋪面參與度變低，焊道承受的應力幅變大。疲勞評估因此必須同時考慮細節分類、交通量與鋪面溫度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「U 肋與橫隔板交接」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder is fully welded and its deck plate is surfaced with GUSS mastic asphalt. Fatigue hot spots in an orthotropic deck concentrate under the wheels: longitudinal rib-to-deck welds, the cut-outs where U-ribs pass through diaphragms, and site butt splices of the ribs. The surfacing is not only for waterproofing and ride; acting together with the plate it markedly lowers local stress ranges. Asphalt stiffness, however, drops sharply with temperature, so in hot summers the surfacing contributes less and the welds see larger stress ranges. Fatigue assessment must therefore combine detail category, traffic volume and surfacing temperature. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Rib-to-diaphragm joints” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：S–N 曲線 N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: S–N curve N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「U 肋與橫隔板交接」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Rib-to-diaphragm joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-33-k1","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度","titleEn":"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness","text":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁採全焊接，橋面板上鋪 GUSS 澆注式瀝青。正交異性橋面的疲勞熱點集中在輪載正下方：U 肋與面板的縱向焊道、U 肋穿過橫隔板的切口，以及現場對接的 U 肋接頭。","textEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder is fully welded and its deck plate is surfaced with GUSS mastic asphalt. Fatigue hot spots in an orthotropic deck concentrate under the wheels: longitudinal rib-to-deck welds, the cut-outs where U-ribs pass through diaphragms, and site butt splices of the ribs.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness\" is correct?","options":["淡江大橋鋼箱梁採全焊接，橋面板上鋪 GUSS 澆注式瀝青。","鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。","裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。"],"optionsEn":["The Danjiang steel box girder is fully welded and its deck plate is surfaced with GUSS mastic asphalt.","Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.","A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淡江大橋鋼箱梁採全焊接，橋面板上鋪 GUSS 澆注式瀝青。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Danjiang steel box girder is fully welded and its deck plate is surfaced with GUSS mastic asphalt. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":51},{"id":"danjiang-v13-34","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度：定量估算","titleEn":"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「U 肋與橫隔板交接」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rib-to-diaphragm joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：S–N 曲線 N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³。取細節類別 Δσ_C = 71 MPa：夏季鋪面軟化時 Δσ = 60 MPa，N ≈ 2×10⁶×1.657 ≈ 3.3×10⁶ 次；冬季鋪面參與時 Δσ = 40 MPa，N ≈ 2×10⁶×5.59 ≈ 1.1×10⁷ 次，壽命比為 (60/40)³ ≈ 3.4。應力幅為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: S–N curve N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³. With detail category Δσ_C = 71 MPa, a summer stress range of 60 MPa with softened surfacing gives N ≈ 2×10⁶×1.657 ≈ 3.3×10⁶ cycles, while a winter range of 40 MPa with the surfacing acting gives N ≈ 2×10⁶×5.59 ≈ 1.1×10⁷ cycles, a life ratio of (60/40)³ ≈ 3.4. Stress ranges are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：現場對接焊道以超音波或相位陣列檢測驗收，並以應變計在重車道下方量測不同季節的應力幅，配合動態地磅的軸重頻譜，以 Miner 累積損傷法比對設計假設；定期以目視與磁粒檢測巡查 U 肋切口與焊趾。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Accept site butt welds by ultrasonic or phased-array testing, gauge stress ranges under the heavy-vehicle lane in different seasons, combine them with axle-load spectra from weigh-in-motion and compare with design assumptions using Miner’s cumulative damage; inspect rib cut-outs and weld toes periodically by visual and magnetic-particle testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"S–N 曲線 N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³。取細節類別 Δσ_C = 71 MPa：夏季鋪面軟化時 Δσ = 60 MPa，N ≈ 2×10⁶×1.657 ≈ 3.3×10⁶ 次；冬季鋪面參與時 Δσ = 40 MPa，N ≈ 2×10⁶×5.59 ≈ 1.1×10⁷ 次，壽命比為 (60/40)³ ≈ 3.4。應力幅為教學假設。","textEn":"S–N curve N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³. With detail category Δσ_C = 71 MPa, a summer stress range of 60 MPa with softened surfacing gives N ≈ 2×10⁶×1.657 ≈ 3.3×10⁶ cycles, while a winter range of 40 MPa with the surfacing acting gives N ≈ 2×10⁶×5.59 ≈ 1.1×10⁷ cycles, a life ratio of (60/40)³ ≈ 3.4. Stress ranges are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器裝得越多越硬，橋梁在地震中就越安全。","S–N 曲線 N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³。","大體積混凝土只要強度夠，水化熱不會影響耐久性。"],"optionsEn":["The more and stiffer the dampers, the safer the bridge is in an earthquake.","S–N curve N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³.","As long as mass concrete reaches its strength, hydration heat does not affect durability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"S–N 曲線 N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"S–N curve N = 2×10⁶×(Δσ_C/Δσ)³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":52},{"id":"danjiang-v13-35","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「U 肋與橫隔板交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rib-to-diaphragm joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"現場對接焊道以超音波或相位陣列檢測驗收，並以應變計在重車道下方量測不同季節的應力幅，配合動態地磅的軸重頻譜，以 Miner 累積損傷法比對設計假設；定期以目視與磁粒檢測巡查 U 肋切口與焊趾。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Accept site butt welds by ultrasonic or phased-array testing, gauge stress ranges under the heavy-vehicle lane in different seasons, combine them with axle-load spectra from weigh-in-motion and compare with design assumptions using Miner’s cumulative damage; inspect rib cut-outs and weld toes periodically by visual and magnetic-particle testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：鋪面更換或改用不同材料前，必須評估其模數與溫度特性對鋼橋面應力幅的影響；巡檢計畫應把重車道下方的 U 肋接頭列為優先檢查區，並保存每次檢測的裂縫位置圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before resurfacing or changing material, assess how its modulus and temperature behaviour change deck stress ranges; the inspection plan should prioritise rib splices under the heavy-vehicle lane and keep a crack-location map from each inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：U 肋與面板焊道的根部裂縫可能向面板內擴展，在鋪面下方難以發現，直到鋪面出現縱向裂紋或滲水；高溫季節長期重車會加速裂縫成長，修補需要封閉車道並刨除鋪面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Root cracks in rib-to-deck welds can grow into the deck plate, hidden beneath the surfacing until longitudinal cracks or water seepage appear in the pavement; sustained heavy traffic in hot seasons accelerates growth, and repair requires lane closures and removal of the surfacing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"現場對接焊道以超音波或相位陣列檢測驗收，並以應變計在重車道下方量測不同季節的應力幅，配合動態地磅的軸重頻譜，以 Miner 累積損傷法比對設計假設；定期以目視與磁粒檢測巡查 U 肋切口與焊趾。","textEn":"Accept site butt welds by ultrasonic or phased-array testing, gauge stress ranges under the heavy-vehicle lane in different seasons, combine them with axle-load spectra from weigh-in-motion and compare with design assumptions using Miner’s cumulative damage; inspect rib cut-outs and weld toes periodically by visual and magnetic-particle testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"鋪面更換或改用不同材料前，必須評估其模數與溫度特性對鋼橋面應力幅的影響；巡檢計畫應把重車道下方的 U 肋接頭列為優先檢查區，並保存每次檢測的裂縫位置圖。","textEn":"Before resurfacing or changing material, assess how its modulus and temperature behaviour change deck stress ranges; the inspection plan should prioritise rib splices under the heavy-vehicle lane and keep a crack-location map from each inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","合龍節塊只要照設計圖長度製造，任何時間都能吊上去對接。","現場對接焊道以超音波或相位陣列檢測驗收，並以應變計在重車道下方量測不同季節的應力幅，配合動態地磅的軸重頻譜，以 Miner 累積損傷法比對設計假設。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A closure segment made to the drawing length can be lifted and joined at any time of day.","Accept site butt welds by ultrasonic or phased-array testing, gauge stress ranges under the heavy-vehicle lane in different seasons, combine them with axle-load spectra from weigh-in-motion and compare with design assumptions using Miner’s cumulative damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"現場對接焊道以超音波或相位陣列檢測驗收，並以應變計在重車道下方量測不同季節的應力幅，配合動態地磅的軸重頻譜，以 Miner 累積損傷法比對設計假設；定期以目視與磁粒檢測巡查 U 肋切口與焊趾。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Accept site butt welds by ultrasonic or phased-array testing, gauge stress ranges under the heavy-vehicle lane in different seasons, combine them with axle-load spectra from weigh-in-motion and compare with design assumptions using Miner’s cumulative damage; inspect rib cut-outs and weld toes periodically by visual and magnetic-particle testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":53},{"id":"danjiang-v13-36","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「U 肋與橫隔板交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rib-to-diaphragm joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"U 肋與面板焊道的根部裂縫可能向面板內擴展，在鋪面下方難以發現，直到鋪面出現縱向裂紋或滲水；高溫季節長期重車會加速裂縫成長，修補需要封閉車道並刨除鋪面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Root cracks in rib-to-deck welds can grow into the deck plate, hidden beneath the surfacing until longitudinal cracks or water seepage appear in the pavement; sustained heavy traffic in hot seasons accelerates growth, and repair requires lane closures and removal of the surfacing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：疲勞評估因此必須同時考慮細節分類、交通量與鋪面溫度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Fatigue assessment must therefore combine detail category, traffic volume and surfacing temperature.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼橋面疲勞只跟鋼板厚度有關，鋪面材料和季節溫度不影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steel-deck fatigue depends only on plate thickness; surfacing material and seasonal temperature have no effect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"U 肋與面板焊道的根部裂縫可能向面板內擴展，在鋪面下方難以發現，直到鋪面出現縱向裂紋或滲水；高溫季節長期重車會加速裂縫成長，修補需要封閉車道並刨除鋪面。","textEn":"Root cracks in rib-to-deck welds can grow into the deck plate, hidden beneath the surfacing until longitudinal cracks or water seepage appear in the pavement; sustained heavy traffic in hot seasons accelerates growth, and repair requires lane closures and removal of the surfacing.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞壽命與鋪面勁度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Orthotropic-deck fatigue life and surfacing stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["U 肋與面板焊道的根部裂縫可能向面板內擴展，在鋪面下方難以發現，直到鋪面出現縱向裂紋或滲水；高溫季節長期重車會加速裂縫成長，修補需要封閉車道並刨除鋪面。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。"],"optionsEn":["Root cracks in rib-to-deck welds can grow into the deck plate, hidden beneath the surfacing until longitudinal cracks or water seepage appear in the pavement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"U 肋與面板焊道的根部裂縫可能向面板內擴展，在鋪面下方難以發現，直到鋪面出現縱向裂紋或滲水；高溫季節長期重車會加速裂縫成長，修補需要封閉車道並刨除鋪面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Root cracks in rib-to-deck welds can grow into the deck plate, hidden beneath the surfacing until longitudinal cracks or water seepage appear in the pavement; sustained heavy traffic in hot seasons accelerates growth, and repair requires lane closures and removal of the surfacing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":54},{"id":"danjiang-v13-37","title":"監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「24 小時監測系統」如何影響淡江大橋工程的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “24-hour monitoring system” governs force, deformation or durability in “Danjiang Bridge Engineering”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公路局資料指出，淡江大橋設有橋檢桁架，並對橋塔、斜拉索、鋼箱梁與 P120、P140 墩進行 24 小時監測；斜拉索、支承、阻尼器與伸縮縫都設計為可更換，以配合 120 年使用年限。監測數據最大的干擾來自溫度：一天內索力、塔頂偏位與伸縮縫開口都隨溫度變化，若直接拿原始讀數與基準比較，會把正常的熱效應誤判為損傷。工程師要先建立每個量測值與溫度的回歸關係，把讀數換算到基準溫度，再以偏差趨勢決定是否調索、檢修或更換構件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「24 小時監測系統」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has an inspection gantry and 24-hour monitoring of the pylon, stays, steel box girder and piers P120 and P140, and that stays, bearings, dampers and expansion joints are designed to be replaceable for a 120-year service life. The largest disturbance in the data is temperature: stay forces, pylon-top displacement and joint openings all change through the day, and comparing raw readings directly with the baseline mistakes normal thermal effects for damage. Engineers first regress each measured quantity against temperature, convert readings to a reference temperature, then use the trend of deviations to decide on force adjustment, repair or replacement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “24-hour monitoring system” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：溫度修正 T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Temperature correction T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref).","failure":"常見誤解：「裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「24 小時監測系統」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “24-hour monitoring system”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-37-k1","title":"監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策","titleEn":"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions","text":"公路局資料指出，淡江大橋設有橋檢桁架，並對橋塔、斜拉索、鋼箱梁與 P120、P140 墩進行 24 小時監測；斜拉索、支承、阻尼器與伸縮縫都設計為可更換，以配合 120 年使用年限。監測數據最大的干擾來自溫度：一天內索力、塔頂偏位與伸縮縫開口都隨溫度變化，若直接拿原始讀數與基準比較，會把正常的熱效應誤判為損傷。","textEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has an inspection gantry and 24-hour monitoring of the pylon, stays, steel box girder and piers P120 and P140, and that stays, bearings, dampers and expansion joints are designed to be replaceable for a 120-year service life. The largest disturbance in the data is temperature: stay forces, pylon-top displacement and joint openings all change through the day, and comparing raw readings directly with the baseline mistakes normal thermal effects for damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions\" is correct?","options":["裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。","公路局資料指出，淡江大橋設有橋檢桁架，並對橋塔、斜拉索、鋼箱梁與 P120、P140 墩進行 24 小時監測。","單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection.","Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has an inspection gantry and 24-hour monitoring of the pylon, stays, steel box girder and piers P120 and P140, and that stays, bearings, dampers and expansion joints are designed to be replaceable for a 120-year service life.","In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公路局資料指出，淡江大橋設有橋檢桁架，並對橋塔、斜拉索、鋼箱梁與 P120、P140 墩進行 24 小時監測；斜拉索、支承、阻尼器與伸縮縫都設計為可更換，以配合 120 年使用年限。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Highway Bureau data state that the Danjiang Bridge has an inspection gantry and 24-hour monitoring of the pylon, stays, steel box girder and piers P120 and P140, and that stays, bearings, dampers and expansion joints are designed to be replaceable for a 120-year service life. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":55},{"id":"danjiang-v13-38","title":"監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策：定量估算","titleEn":"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「24 小時監測系統」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “24-hour monitoring system” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：溫度修正 T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)。某索溫度係數 k = −8 kN/°C，32 °C 時實測 5,960 kN，換算到 20 °C：T_20 = 5,960 − (−8)×(32 − 20) = 6,056 kN；與基準 6,100 kN 相差 −44 kN，約 −0.7%，在 ±5% 警戒內。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Temperature correction T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref). For a stay with k = −8 kN/°C measuring 5,960 kN at 32 °C, the 20 °C value is T_20 = 5,960 − (−8)×(32 − 20) = 6,056 kN; against a 6,100 kN baseline the difference is −44 kN, about −0.7%, inside a ±5% alert band. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以通車初期至少一整年的資料建立各感測器的溫度回歸與季節基準，設定警戒與行動兩級門檻；異常時先檢查感測器漂移與時間同步，再以人工量測（例如振動法索力或精密水準）複核，最後才判定結構變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use at least one full year of early-service data to build temperature regressions and seasonal baselines for each sensor, with alert and action thresholds; on an anomaly first check sensor drift and time synchronisation, then confirm by independent manual measurement such as vibration-based stay force or precise levelling, and only then conclude a structural change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"溫度修正 T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)。某索溫度係數 k = −8 kN/°C，32 °C 時實測 5,960 kN，換算到 20 °C：T_20 = 5,960 − (−8)×(32 − 20) = 6,056 kN；與基準 6,100 kN 相差 −44 kN，約 −0.7%，在 ±5% 警戒內。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Temperature correction T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref). For a stay with k = −8 kN/°C measuring 5,960 kN at 32 °C, the 20 °C value is T_20 = 5,960 − (−8)×(32 − 20) = 6,056 kN; against a 6,100 kN baseline the difference is −44 kN, about −0.7%, inside a ±5% alert band. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions\", which statement holds?","options":["斜拉索越陡越省鋼，所以長索的股數應該比短索少。","塔頂量到偏位，就代表施工做歪了，必須立即拉回。","溫度修正 T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)。"],"optionsEn":["Steeper stays use less steel, so long stays should have fewer strands than short ones.","Any measured pylon-top offset means the pylon was built crooked and must be pulled back at once.","Temperature correction T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度修正 T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Temperature correction T_ref = T_meas − k·(t − t_ref). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":56},{"id":"danjiang-v13-39","title":"監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「24 小時監測系統」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “24-hour monitoring system” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以通車初期至少一整年的資料建立各感測器的溫度回歸與季節基準，設定警戒與行動兩級門檻；異常時先檢查感測器漂移與時間同步，再以人工量測（例如振動法索力或精密水準）複核，最後才判定結構變化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use at least one full year of early-service data to build temperature regressions and seasonal baselines for each sensor, with alert and action thresholds; on an anomaly first check sensor drift and time synchronisation, then confirm by independent manual measurement such as vibration-based stay force or precise levelling, and only then conclude a structural change. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要包含感測器清單與位置、校正紀錄、溫度回歸係數、門檻值與通報流程，並規定任何構件更換（索、支承、阻尼器、伸縮縫）前後都要重做局部基準量測與紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents should include the sensor list and locations, calibration records, temperature regression coefficients, thresholds and reporting procedure, and require new local baseline measurements before and after any replacement of stays, bearings, dampers or joints.","failure":"注意干擾：未做溫度修正時，夏季索力下降可能被誤判為索力損失而進行不必要的調索；反之真正的錨具滑移或阻尼器失效可能被季節波動掩蓋，等到出現明顯變形才發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without temperature correction, a summer drop in stay force can be misread as force loss and trigger unnecessary re-tensioning; conversely real anchor slip or damper failure can hide inside seasonal swings until visible deformation appears. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以通車初期至少一整年的資料建立各感測器的溫度回歸與季節基準，設定警戒與行動兩級門檻；異常時先檢查感測器漂移與時間同步，再以人工量測（例如振動法索力或精密水準）複核，最後才判定結構變化。","textEn":"Use at least one full year of early-service data to build temperature regressions and seasonal baselines for each sensor, with alert and action thresholds; on an anomaly first check sensor drift and time synchronisation, then confirm by independent manual measurement such as vibration-based stay force or precise levelling, and only then conclude a structural change.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要包含感測器清單與位置、校正紀錄、溫度回歸係數、門檻值與通報流程，並規定任何構件更換（索、支承、阻尼器、伸縮縫）前後都要重做局部基準量測與紀錄。","textEn":"Handover documents should include the sensor list and locations, calibration records, temperature regression coefficients, thresholds and reporting procedure, and require new local baseline measurements before and after any replacement of stays, bearings, dampers or joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions\"?","options":["以通車初期至少一整年的資料建立各感測器的溫度回歸與季節基準，設定警戒與行動兩級門檻。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","風洞試驗只需要檢查颱風時會不會顫振，中低風速不必關心。"],"optionsEn":["Use at least one full year of early-service data to build temperature regressions and seasonal baselines for each sensor, with alert and action thresholds.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Wind-tunnel testing only needs to check flutter in typhoons; low and moderate wind speeds do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以通車初期至少一整年的資料建立各感測器的溫度回歸與季節基準，設定警戒與行動兩級門檻；異常時先檢查感測器漂移與時間同步，再以人工量測（例如振動法索力或精密水準）複核，最後才判定結構變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use at least one full year of early-service data to build temperature regressions and seasonal baselines for each sensor, with alert and action thresholds; on an anomaly first check sensor drift and time synchronisation, then confirm by independent manual measurement such as vibration-based stay force or precise levelling, and only then conclude a structural change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":57},{"id":"danjiang-v13-40","title":"監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"],"prerequisiteIds":["danjiang-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「24 小時監測系統」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “24-hour monitoring system” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未做溫度修正時，夏季索力下降可能被誤判為索力損失而進行不必要的調索；反之真正的錨具滑移或阻尼器失效可能被季節波動掩蓋，等到出現明顯變形才發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without temperature correction, a summer drop in stay force can be misread as force loss and trigger unnecessary re-tensioning; conversely real anchor slip or damper failure can hide inside seasonal swings until visible deformation appears. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：工程師要先建立每個量測值與溫度的回歸關係，把讀數換算到基準溫度，再以偏差趨勢決定是否調索、檢修或更換構件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Engineers first regress each measured quantity against temperature, convert readings to a reference temperature, then use the trend of deviations to decide on force adjustment, repair or replacement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝了 24 小時監測系統，就可以取代人工巡檢。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A 24-hour monitoring system can replace manual inspection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"danjiang-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未做溫度修正時，夏季索力下降可能被誤判為索力損失而進行不必要的調索；反之真正的錨具滑移或阻尼器失效可能被季節波動掩蓋，等到出現明顯變形才發現。","textEn":"Without temperature correction, a summer drop in stay force can be misread as force loss and trigger unnecessary re-tensioning; conversely real anchor slip or damper failure can hide inside seasonal swings until visible deformation appears.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]},{"id":"danjiang-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-thb-djbridge-features","v13s-thb-djbridge-basic-data","v13s-zha-danjiang-bridge","v13s-cie-danjiang-pdf","v13s-cna-danjiang-2026"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「監測資料的溫度修正與構件更換決策」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temperature-corrected monitoring and component replacement decisions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","未做溫度修正時，夏季索力下降可能被誤判為索力損失而進行不必要的調索；反之真正的錨具滑移或阻尼器失效可能被季節波動掩蓋，等到出現明顯變形才發現。","單塔斜張橋只要把橋塔做得夠粗，背跨長短就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without temperature correction, a summer drop in stay force can be misread as force loss and trigger unnecessary re-tensioning.","In a single-pylon cable-stayed bridge the back-span length does not matter as long as the pylon is massive enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未做溫度修正時，夏季索力下降可能被誤判為索力損失而進行不必要的調索；反之真正的錨具滑移或阻尼器失效可能被季節波動掩蓋，等到出現明顯變形才發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without temperature correction, a summer drop in stay force can be misread as force loss and trigger unnecessary re-tensioning; conversely real anchor slip or damper failure can hide inside seasonal swings until visible deformation appears. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":58}],"order":11}],"stepCount":58,"estimatedMinutes":1270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","enrichmentVersion":13,"learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-cable-stayed","learningTags":["structures","st-cable-stayed","cablestayed"],"subcategory":"st-cable-stayed","subcategoryTitle":"斜張橋與斜索系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Cable-stayed bridges and stay systems","v13Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"cablestayed","architectureNodes":[["曲面混凝土主塔與基樁","Curved concrete pylon and piles"],["94 根斜拉索","94 stay cables"],["全焊鋼箱梁橋面","Fully welded steel box deck"],["背跨錨墩與支承","Back-span anchor piers and bearings"],["HFR 與 FVD 縱向消能","HFR and FVD longitudinal dissipation"],["24 小時監測與檢修","24-hour monitoring and inspection"]],"architectureEdges":[[2,1],[1,0],[2,3],[2,4],[4,0],[1,5],[2,5]]},"v13Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某長索使用索力 T = 6,000 kN，以 61 股 15.7 mm 鋼絞線組成，A = 61×150 = 9,150 mm²，E = 195 GPa，索長 L = 300 m，水平投影 L_h = 280 m。使用應力 σ = 6,000,000/9,150 ≈ 656 MPa，約為 GUTS 1,860 MPa 的 35%。張拉伸長量 ΔL = T·L/(E·A) = 6,000,000×300,000/(195,000×9,150) ≈ 1,009 mm。考慮垂度的 Ernst 等效模數 E_eq = E/[1 + (γ·L_h)²·E/(12σ³)]，取含套管的等效單位重 γ = 1.02×10⁻⁴ N/mm³：(γ·L_h)² = (1.02×10⁻⁴×280,000)² ≈ 816 N²/mm⁴，乘 E 再除以 12σ³ 得 0.047，E_eq ≈ 195/1.047 ≈ 186 GPa。若在施工早期索力只有一半（σ ≈ 328 MPa），比值變為 0.376，E_eq ≈ 142 GPa，長索明顯變軟，施工階段分析必須逐階段更新等效模數。數值為教學假設，不代表淡江大橋的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a long stay carries a service force T = 6,000 kN with 61 strands of 15.7 mm, A = 61×150 = 9,150 mm², E = 195 GPa, length L = 300 m and horizontal projection L_h = 280 m. The service stress is σ = 6,000,000/9,150 ≈ 656 MPa, about 35% of the 1,860 MPa GUTS. The stressing elongation is ΔL = T·L/(E·A) = 6,000,000×300,000/(195,000×9,150) ≈ 1,009 mm. The Ernst equivalent modulus for sag is E_eq = E/[1 + (γ·L_h)²·E/(12σ³)]; with an equivalent unit weight including the duct of γ = 1.02×10⁻⁴ N/mm³, (γ·L_h)² = (1.02×10⁻⁴×280,000)² ≈ 816 N²/mm⁴, and multiplying by E and dividing by 12σ³ gives 0.047, so E_eq ≈ 195/1.047 ≈ 186 GPa. If the force is only half during early erection (σ ≈ 328 MPa), the ratio becomes 0.376 and E_eq ≈ 142 GPa: the long stay is much softer, so the staged analysis must update the equivalent modulus stage by stage. Values are teaching assumptions, not the Danjiang Bridge design.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"以背跨錨固、縱向消能、索力與疲勞量化淡江大橋 450 m 單塔不對稱斜張橋的設計與驗證","focusEn":"Quantifying back-span anchorage, longitudinal energy dissipation, stay forces and fatigue for the 450 m single-pylon asymmetric Danjiang Bridge"}},{"id":"hsuehshan","title":"雪山隧道工程","titleEn":"Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering","category":"underground","summary":"認識複雜地質、地下水、開挖支護與營運安全如何共同決定長隧道工程。","summaryEn":"Learn how complex geology, groundwater, excavation support and operational safety shape long tunnels.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan","v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["地質","探查","開挖","支護","機電"],"labelsEn":["Geology","Investigation","Excavation","Support","Services"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s01","order":1,"title":"路線與地質","titleEn":"Alignment and geology","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-01","order":1,"title":"比較路線約束","titleEn":"Compare alignment constraints","objective":"完成「比較路線約束」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare alignment constraints.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"路線需同時考慮地形、交通連接與地質風險。","textEn":"Alignment balances terrain, transport links and geological risk."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立兩條概念路線的比較表。","textEn":"Compare two conceptual alignments in a table."}],"check":"建立兩條概念路線的比較表。","checkEn":"Compare two conceptual alignments in a table.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較路線約束」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare alignment constraints?","options":["路線需同時考慮地形、交通連接與地質風險。","鑽孔與地表資料只能取樣，地層模型帶有不確定度。","施工中的探查可更新前方地質判斷。"],"optionsEn":["Alignment balances terrain, transport links and geological risk.","Boreholes and surface observations sample ground; geological models contain uncertainty.","Investigation during construction updates understanding of the ground ahead."],"answer":0,"explanation":"路線需同時考慮地形、交通連接與地質風險。","explanationEn":"Alignment balances terrain, transport links and geological risk."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-02","order":2,"title":"建立地質模型","titleEn":"Build a geological model","objective":"完成「建立地質模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a geological model.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"鑽孔與地表資料只能取樣，地層模型帶有不確定度。","textEn":"Boreholes and surface observations sample ground; geological models contain uncertainty."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以不同透明度標示已知與推估地層。","textEn":"Use different opacity for observed and inferred strata."}],"check":"以不同透明度標示已知與推估地層。","checkEn":"Use different opacity for observed and inferred strata.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立地質模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a geological model?","options":["施工中的探查可更新前方地質判斷。","路線需同時考慮地形、交通連接與地質風險。","鑽孔與地表資料只能取樣，地層模型帶有不確定度。"],"optionsEn":["Investigation during construction updates understanding of the ground ahead.","Alignment balances terrain, transport links and geological risk.","Boreholes and surface observations sample ground; geological models contain uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鑽孔與地表資料只能取樣，地層模型帶有不確定度。","explanationEn":"Boreholes and surface observations sample ground; geological models contain uncertainty."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-03","order":3,"title":"規劃前進探查","titleEn":"Plan forward investigation","objective":"完成「規劃前進探查」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan forward investigation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"施工中的探查可更新前方地質判斷。","textEn":"Investigation during construction updates understanding of the ground ahead."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"說明新增資料如何改變概念風險圖。","textEn":"Explain how new data changes the conceptual risk map."}],"check":"說明新增資料如何改變概念風險圖。","checkEn":"Explain how new data changes the conceptual risk map.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃前進探查」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan forward investigation?","options":["鑽孔與地表資料只能取樣，地層模型帶有不確定度。","施工中的探查可更新前方地質判斷。","路線需同時考慮地形、交通連接與地質風險。"],"optionsEn":["Boreholes and surface observations sample ground; geological models contain uncertainty.","Investigation during construction updates understanding of the ground ahead.","Alignment balances terrain, transport links and geological risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工中的探查可更新前方地質判斷。","explanationEn":"Investigation during construction updates understanding of the ground ahead."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"hsuehshan-s02","order":2,"title":"地下水與風險","titleEn":"Groundwater and risk","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解水壓與滲流","titleEn":"Understand pressure and seepage","objective":"完成「理解水壓與滲流」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand pressure and seepage.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"地下水流動取決於水力梯度及地層透水性。","textEn":"Groundwater flow depends on hydraulic gradient and permeability."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"區分水壓量測與出水量量測。","textEn":"Distinguish pressure measurement from inflow measurement."}],"check":"區分水壓量測與出水量量測。","checkEn":"Distinguish pressure measurement from inflow measurement.","sourceIds":