ehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「觀察收斂趨勢」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains observe convergence trends?","options":["防水限制滲入，排水管理水的去向，兩者功能不同。","支護與圍岩共同承載，時間效應會改變變形。","隧道收斂量隨時間的趨勢可協助辨識穩定化或持續變形。"],"optionsEn":["Waterproofing limits ingress; drainage manages water pathways.","Support and ground carry loads together; time effects change deformation.","Convergence trends help distinguish stabilization from continuing deformation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隧道收斂量隨時間的趨勢可協助辨識穩定化或持續變形。","explanationEn":"Convergence trends help distinguish stabilization from continuing deformation."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s04-03","order":3,"title":"理解防排水層","titleEn":"Understand waterproofing and drainage","objective":"完成「理解防排水層」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand waterproofing and drainage.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"防水限制滲入，排水管理水的去向，兩者功能不同。","textEn":"Waterproofing limits ingress; drainage manages water pathways."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在襯砌剖面標出兩種功能。","textEn":"Label both functions on a lining section."}],"check":"在襯砌剖面標出兩種功能。","checkEn":"Label both functions on a lining section.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解防排水層」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand waterproofing and drainage?","options":["隧道收斂量隨時間的趨勢可協助辨識穩定化或持續變形。","防水限制滲入，排水管理水的去向，兩者功能不同。","支護與圍岩共同承載，時間效應會改變變形。"],"optionsEn":["Convergence trends help distinguish stabilization from continuing deformation.","Waterproofing limits ingress; drainage manages water pathways.","Support and ground carry loads together; time effects change deformation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防水限制滲入，排水管理水的去向，兩者功能不同。","explanationEn":"Waterproofing limits ingress; drainage manages water pathways."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05","order":5,"title":"營運機電","titleEn":"Operational systems","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-01","order":1,"title":"畫出通風網路","titleEn":"Draw ventilation topology","objective":"完成「畫出通風網路」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for draw ventilation topology.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"通風配置需服務空氣品質及緊急情境，不能只計平均流量。","textEn":"Ventilation serves air quality and emergency scenarios, not average airflow alone."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以概念方塊圖區分正常與異常情境。","textEn":"Use blocks to distinguish normal and abnormal scenarios."}],"check":"以概念方塊圖區分正常與異常情境。","checkEn":"Use blocks to distinguish normal and abnormal scenarios.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「畫出通風網路」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains draw ventilation topology?","options":["入口與內部亮度變化影響視覺適應。","方向、距離與可用出口資訊需清楚且一致。","通風配置需服務空氣品質及緊急情境，不能只計平均流量。"],"optionsEn":["Brightness changes between portals and interior affect visual adaptation.","Direction, distance and available-exit information need clarity and consistency.","Ventilation serves air quality and emergency scenarios, not average airflow alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"通風配置需服務空氣品質及緊急情境，不能只計平均流量。","explanationEn":"Ventilation serves air quality and emergency scenarios, not average airflow alone."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-02","order":2,"title":"規劃照明過渡","titleEn":"Plan lighting transitions","objective":"完成「規劃照明過渡」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan lighting transitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"入口與內部亮度變化影響視覺適應。","textEn":"Brightness changes between portals and interior affect visual adaptation."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出定性亮度過渡曲線。","textEn":"Draw a qualitative brightness-transition curve."}],"check":"畫出定性亮度過渡曲線。","checkEn":"Draw a qualitative brightness-transition curve.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃照明過渡」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan lighting transitions?","options":["通風配置需服務空氣品質及緊急情境，不能只計平均流量。","入口與內部亮度變化影響視覺適應。","方向、距離與可用出口資訊需清楚且一致。"],"optionsEn":["Ventilation serves air quality and emergency scenarios, not average airflow alone.","Brightness changes between portals and interior affect visual adaptation.","Direction, distance and available-exit information need clarity and consistency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口與內部亮度變化影響視覺適應。","explanationEn":"Brightness changes between portals and interior affect visual adaptation."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-03","order":3,"title":"辨識疏散資訊","titleEn":"Identify evacuation information","objective":"完成「辨識疏散資訊」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify evacuation information.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"方向、距離與可用出口資訊需清楚且一致。","textEn":"Direction, distance and available-exit information need clarity and consistency."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"檢查虛擬標示是否互相矛盾。","textEn":"Check virtual signs for inconsistent instructions."}],"check":"檢查虛擬標示是否互相矛盾。","checkEn":"Check virtual signs for inconsistent instructions.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識疏散資訊」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify evacuation information?","options":["方向、距離與可用出口資訊需清楚且一致。","通風配置需服務空氣品質及緊急情境，不能只計平均流量。","入口與內部亮度變化影響視覺適應。"],"optionsEn":["Direction, distance and available-exit information need clarity and consistency.","Ventilation serves air quality and emergency scenarios, not average airflow alone.","Brightness changes between portals and interior affect visual adaptation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向、距離與可用出口資訊需清楚且一致。","explanationEn":"Direction, distance and available-exit information need clarity and consistency."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06","order":6,"title":"系統驗證","titleEn":"System validation","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-01","order":1,"title":"測試跨系統介面","titleEn":"Test cross-system interfaces","objective":"完成「測試跨系統介面」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for test cross-system interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"感測、通訊與控制的交互作用需整合測試。","textEn":"Interactions among sensing, communication and control require integration tests."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為一個虛擬告警追蹤完整資訊鏈。","textEn":"Trace the full information chain for one virtual alarm."}],"check":"為一個虛擬告警追蹤完整資訊鏈。","checkEn":"Trace the full information chain for one virtual alarm.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「測試跨系統介面」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains test cross-system interfaces?","options":["實際施工需場址專業判斷，教育模型只能展示相依關係。","感測、通訊與控制的交互作用需整合測試。","設備老化與環境影響需要定期檢查及替換規劃。"],"optionsEn":["Actual construction needs site-specific expertise; an educational model demonstrates dependencies.","Interactions among sensing, communication and control require integration tests.","Aging and environment require inspection and replacement planning."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測、通訊與控制的交互作用需整合測試。","explanationEn":"Interactions among sensing, communication and control require integration tests."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-02","order":2,"title":"建立維護計畫","titleEn":"Build a maintenance plan","objective":"完成「建立維護計畫」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a maintenance plan.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"設備老化與環境影響需要定期檢查及替換規劃。","textEn":"Aging and environment require inspection and replacement planning."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立設備功能、檢查方式與紀錄欄位。","textEn":"Define equipment function, inspection method and record fields."}],"check":"建立設備功能、檢查方式與紀錄欄位。","checkEn":"Define equipment function, inspection method and record fields.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立維護計畫」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a maintenance plan?","options":["設備老化與環境影響需要定期檢查及替換規劃。","實際施工需場址專業判斷，教育模型只能展示相依關係。","感測、通訊與控制的交互作用需整合測試。"],"optionsEn":["Aging and environment require inspection and replacement planning.","Actual construction needs site-specific expertise; an educational model demonstrates dependencies.","Interactions among sensing, communication and control require integration tests."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設備老化與環境影響需要定期檢查及替換規劃。","explanationEn":"Aging and environment require inspection and replacement planning."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-03","order":3,"title":"提交工程學習記錄","titleEn":"Submit the engineering learning record","objective":"完成「提交工程學習記錄」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for submit the engineering learning record.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"實際施工需場址專業判斷，教育模型只能展示相依關係。","textEn":"Actual construction needs site-specific expertise; an educational model demonstrates dependencies."},{"id":"hsuehshan-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交地質假設、系統圖與未驗證限制。","textEn":"Submit geological assumptions, system diagrams and verification limits."}],"check":"提交地質假設、系統圖與未驗證限制。","checkEn":"Submit geological assumptions, system diagrams and verification limits.","sourceIds":["freeway-hsuehshan"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「提交工程學習記錄」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains submit the engineering learning record?","options":["感測、通訊與控制的交互作用需整合測試。","設備老化與環境影響需要定期檢查及替換規劃。","實際施工需場址專業判斷，教育模型只能展示相依關係。"],"optionsEn":["Interactions among sensing, communication and control require integration tests.","Aging and environment require inspection and replacement planning.","Actual construction needs site-specific expertise; an educational model demonstrates dependencies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"實際施工需場址專業判斷，教育模型只能展示相依關係。","explanationEn":"Actual construction needs site-specific expertise; an educational model demonstrates dependencies."},"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「破碎帶連通與預報更新」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-01","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-s06-03"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將雪山山區破碎帶視為多條可能連通水路，研究先進孔揭露的新裂隙如何修正主孔前方預測；不能以已排出的水量推定剩餘岩體必然乾燥。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Treat the mountain fault zone as several potentially connected pathways and examine how a newly intercepted fracture changes the forecast ahead of the main bore. Water already drained does not prove the remaining ground is dry. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2 無因次；通水面積=200 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2 dimensionless; flow area=200 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-01-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"將雪山山區破碎帶視為多條可能連通水路，研究先進孔揭露的新裂隙如何修正主孔前方預測；不能以已排出的水量推定剩餘岩體必然乾燥。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Treat the mountain fault zone as several potentially connected pathways and examine how a newly intercepted fracture changes the forecast ahead of the main bore. Water already drained does not prove the remaining ground is dry.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","將雪山山區破碎帶視為多條可能連通水路，研究先進孔揭露的新裂隙如何修正主孔前方預測；不能以已排出的水量推定剩餘岩體必然乾燥。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Treat the mountain fault zone as several potentially connected pathways and examine how a newly intercepted fracture changes the forecast ahead of the main bore.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將雪山山區破碎帶視為多條可能連通水路，研究先進孔揭露的新裂隙如何修正主孔前方預測；不能以已排出的水量推定剩餘岩體必然乾燥。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Treat the mountain fault zone as several potentially connected pathways and examine how a newly intercepted fracture changes the forecast ahead of the main bore. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":19},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-02","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2 無因次；通水面積=200 m²。Q=k i A=0.0004 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00044 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2 dimensionless; flow area=200 m². Q=k i A=0.0004 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00044 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2 無因次；通水面積=200 m²。Q=k i A=0.0004 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00044 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2 dimensionless; flow area=200 m². Q=k i A=0.0004 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00044 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2 無因次；通水面積=200 m²。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2 dimensionless; flow area=200 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2 無因次；通水面積=200 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2 dimensionless; flow area=200 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":20},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-03","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：若抽水後短暫衰減被誤判為水源耗盡，進入另一連通裂隙時水量可能回升；應用壓力回復試驗區分補注。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A temporary decline mistaken for exhaustion can be followed by renewed inflow from another fracture; pressure recovery helps distinguish recharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較同里程先進孔的出水衰減與主孔後續入流，保留孔口壓力及時間基準，檢查兩者是否同受降雨控制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare probe-flow decay with later main-bore inflow at matching chainage, preserving collar pressure and timing to test whether both respond to rainfall. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":21},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-04","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若抽水後短暫衰減被誤判為水源耗盡，進入另一連通裂隙時水量可能回升；應用壓力回復試驗區分補注。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A temporary decline mistaken for exhaustion can be followed by renewed inflow from another fracture; pressure recovery helps distinguish recharge. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若抽水後短暫衰減被誤判為水源耗盡，進入另一連通裂隙時水量可能回升；應用壓力回復試驗區分補注。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"A temporary decline mistaken for exhaustion can be followed by renewed inflow from another fracture; pressure recovery helps distinguish recharge. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若抽水後短暫衰減被誤判為水源耗盡，進入另一連通裂隙時水量可能回升；應用壓力回復試驗區分補注。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A temporary decline mistaken for exhaustion can be followed by renewed inflow from another fracture; pressure recovery helps distinguish recharge.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若抽水後短暫衰減被誤判為水源耗盡，進入另一連通裂隙時水量可能回升；應用壓力回復試驗區分補注。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A temporary decline mistaken for exhaustion can be followed by renewed inflow from another fracture; pressure recovery helps distinguish recharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":22},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-05","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以雪山兩孔及探勘坑之間的水頭差建立假想分層模型，分辨局部排水效果與整座山體地下水位下降；永久襯砌還要承受排水失效狀態。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Build a hypothetical layered head model between the two bores and exploratory gallery, separating local drainage from regional drawdown. Permanent lining must also be assessed when the drainage path is unavailable. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-05-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"以雪山兩孔及探勘坑之間的水頭差建立假想分層模型，分辨局部排水效果與整座山體地下水位下降；永久襯砌還要承受排水失效狀態。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Build a hypothetical layered head model between the two bores and exploratory gallery, separating local drainage from regional drawdown. Permanent lining must also be assessed when the drainage path is unavailable.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","以雪山兩孔及探勘坑之間的水頭差建立假想分層模型，分辨局部排水效果與整座山體地下水位下降；永久襯砌還要承受排水失效狀態。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Build a hypothetical layered head model between the two bores and exploratory gallery, separating local drainage from regional drawdown."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以雪山兩孔及探勘坑之間的水頭差建立假想分層模型，分辨局部排水效果與整座山體地下水位下降；永久襯砌還要承受排水失效狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Build a hypothetical layered head model between the two bores and exploratory gallery, separating local drainage from regional drawdown. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":23},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-06","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為334.521 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 334.521 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為334.521 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 334.521 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":24},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-07","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：一孔排水可能讓另一孔水位同步變化，若當作兩次獨立事件會誤估滲透性；需先查共同補注和管路連通。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Drainage in one bore may alter the other; treating these as independent events biases permeability estimates, so investigate shared recharge and connections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把各孔測壓管高程校至同一基準，分開穩態水位、降雨尖峰與停泵回升；讀值低於洞頂時仍檢查其他含水層。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Level piezometers to one datum and separate steady head, rainfall peaks and outage recovery; low readings in one layer do not exclude pressure elsewhere. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":25},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-08","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一孔排水可能讓另一孔水位同步變化，若當作兩次獨立事件會誤估滲透性；需先查共同補注和管路連通。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Drainage in one bore may alter the other; treating these as independent events biases permeability estimates, so investigate shared recharge and connections. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一孔排水可能讓另一孔水位同步變化，若當作兩次獨立事件會誤估滲透性；需先查共同補注和管路連通。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Drainage in one bore may alter the other; treating these as independent events biases permeability estimates, so investigate shared recharge and connections. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","一孔排水可能讓另一孔水位同步變化，若當作兩次獨立事件會誤估滲透性；需先查共同補注和管路連通。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Drainage in one bore may alter the other; treating these as independent events biases permeability estimates, so investigate shared recharge and connections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一孔排水可能讓另一孔水位同步變化，若當作兩次獨立事件會誤估滲透性；需先查共同補注和管路連通。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Drainage in one bore may alter the other; treating these as independent events biases permeability estimates, so investigate shared recharge and connections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":26}],"order":7},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」與「支護啟動與變形容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" and \"Support activation and deformation capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-09","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"將雪山覆土與破碎帶交界分開，檢查高應力岩塊旁的低剛度帶是否使洞壁變形集中；覆土相近的兩個斷面不一定採相同材料模型。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate cover effects from the fault transition and examine whether a compliant band beside stressed blocks concentrates wall movement. Two sections with similar cover need not share the same constitutive model. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=500 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=500 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-09-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"將雪山覆土與破碎帶交界分開，檢查高應力岩塊旁的低剛度帶是否使洞壁變形集中；覆土相近的兩個斷面不一定採相同材料模型。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"Separate cover effects from the fault transition and examine whether a compliant band beside stressed blocks concentrates wall movement. Two sections with similar cover need not share the same constitutive model.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["將雪山覆土與破碎帶交界分開，檢查高應力岩塊旁的低剛度帶是否使洞壁變形集中；覆土相近的兩個斷面不一定採相同材料模型。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Separate cover effects from the fault transition and examine whether a compliant band beside stressed blocks concentrates wall movement.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將雪山覆土與破碎帶交界分開，檢查高應力岩塊旁的低剛度帶是否使洞壁變形集中；覆土相近的兩個斷面不一定採相同材料模型。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate cover effects from the fault transition and examine whether a compliant band beside stressed blocks concentrates wall movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":27},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-10","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=500 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.9 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=500 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.9 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=500 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.9 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=500 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.9 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：覆土深度=500 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: cover=500 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=500 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=500 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=39 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":28},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-11","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：若只按平均岩級分段，局部剝落與擠壓可被混為同一機制，導致支護剛度增加卻無法容納位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaged ground classes can confuse spalling with squeezing, increasing stiffness without providing the needed displacement capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在岩塊與破碎帶兩側設多點伸長計，將破壞方位、開挖距離和支護受力同步比較，以辨認彈性回彈或持續塑性變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare extensometers on both sides with damage orientation, face distance and support force to distinguish elastic rebound from continuing plastic deformation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":29},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-12","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只按平均岩級分段，局部剝落與擠壓可被混為同一機制，導致支護剛度增加卻無法容納位移。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaged ground classes can confuse spalling with squeezing, increasing stiffness without providing the needed displacement capacity. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只按平均岩級分段，局部剝落與擠壓可被混為同一機制，導致支護剛度增加卻無法容納位移。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Averaged ground classes can confuse spalling with squeezing, increasing stiffness without providing the needed displacement capacity. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只按平均岩級分段，局部剝落與擠壓可被混為同一機制，導致支護剛度增加卻無法容納位移。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Averaged ground classes can confuse spalling with squeezing, increasing stiffness without providing the needed displacement capacity.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只按平均岩級分段，局部剝落與擠壓可被混為同一機制，導致支護剛度增加卻無法容納位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaged ground classes can confuse spalling with squeezing, increasing stiffness without providing the needed displacement capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":30},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-13","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以雪山長隧道施工的支護封閉時序為題，分析掌子面前進後尚未形成閉合環的暫時狀態；開挖面距離與支護齡期要與最終尺寸同時保留。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Study the temporary condition before support closes into a ring as the heading advances. Face distance and support age must remain visible alongside final dimensions when interpreting loads and convergence. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=30 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=30 kN/mm; movement=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-13-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"以雪山長隧道施工的支護封閉時序為題，分析掌子面前進後尚未形成閉合環的暫時狀態；開挖面距離與支護齡期要與最終尺寸同時保留。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Study the temporary condition before support closes into a ring as the heading advances. Face distance and support age must remain visible alongside final dimensions when interpreting loads and convergence.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","以雪山長隧道施工的支護封閉時序為題，分析掌子面前進後尚未形成閉合環的暫時狀態；開挖面距離與支護齡期要與最終尺寸同時保留。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Study the temporary condition before support closes into a ring as the heading advances.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以雪山長隧道施工的支護封閉時序為題，分析掌子面前進後尚未形成閉合環的暫時狀態；開挖面距離與支護齡期要與最終尺寸同時保留。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Study the temporary condition before support closes into a ring as the heading advances. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":31},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-14","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=30 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=240 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為264 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=30 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=240 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 264 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=30 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=240 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為264 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=30 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=240 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 264 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=30 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=30 kN/mm; movement=8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=30 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=30 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":32},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-15","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：位移趨緩可能只是量測點移出活躍區，若未記錄掌子面位置會過早認定整段已穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slower movement may mean the point has left the active zone; without face position it can be misread as stability of the whole section. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將每次封閉時間標在收斂曲線，檢查速率改變是否發生於同一施工事件，再比較支護荷重是否有對應反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark each closure time on convergence histories and test whether rate changes coincide with construction events and corresponding support-load changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":33},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-16","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"位移趨緩可能只是量測點移出活躍區，若未記錄掌子面位置會過早認定整段已穩定。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slower movement may mean the point has left the active zone; without face position it can be misread as stability of the whole section. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"位移趨緩可能只是量測點移出活躍區，若未記錄掌子面位置會過早認定整段已穩定。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Slower movement may mean the point has left the active zone; without face position it can be misread as stability of the whole section. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","位移趨緩可能只是量測點移出活躍區，若未記錄掌子面位置會過早認定整段已穩定。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Slower movement may mean the point has left the active zone; without face position it can be misread as stability of the whole section.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"位移趨緩可能只是量測點移出活躍區，若未記錄掌子面位置會過早認定整段已穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slower movement may mean the point has left the active zone; without face position it can be misread as stability of the whole section. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":34}],"order":8},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「掘進利用率與設備停時」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-17","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪山案例用來比較受地質限制的掘進循環：刀具切削時間、檢查修理及出渣等待必須分開，才能判定設備瓶頸或破碎帶風險誰先控制進度。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use the Hsuehshan context to separate cutting, inspection and spoil queues in a geologically constrained cycle, determining whether machinery or fault-zone uncertainty controls progress before proposing a production change. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.5 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.5 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-17-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"雪山案例用來比較受地質限制的掘進循環：刀具切削時間、檢查修理及出渣等待必須分開，才能判定設備瓶頸或破碎帶風險誰先控制進度。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Use the Hsuehshan context to separate cutting, inspection and spoil queues in a geologically constrained cycle, determining whether machinery or fault-zone uncertainty controls progress before proposing a production change. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","雪山案例用來比較受地質限制的掘進循環：刀具切削時間、檢查修理及出渣等待必須分開，才能判定設備瓶頸或破碎帶風險誰先控制進度。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Use the Hsuehshan context to separate cutting, inspection and spoil queues in a geologically constrained cycle, determining whether machinery or fault-zone uncertainty controls progress before proposing a production change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雪山案例用來比較受地質限制的掘進循環：刀具切削時間、檢查修理及出渣等待必須分開，才能判定設備瓶頸或破碎帶風險誰先控制進度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use the Hsuehshan context to separate cutting, inspection and spoil queues in a geologically constrained cycle, determining whether machinery or fault-zone uncertainty controls progress before proposing a production change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":35},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-18","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.5 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.16 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.276 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.5 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.16 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.276 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.5 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.16 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.276 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.5 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.16 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.276 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：切削速率=1.5 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.5 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.5 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.5 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":36},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-19","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：出渣等待若被列為地質停工，會把後勤問題誤判成岩石太硬，導致無效更換刀具或修改推進策略。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Spoil queues classified as ground delay falsely suggest hard rock and prompt ineffective cutter replacement or advance changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把停機原因碼對齊刀具檢查和地質里程，另以完整班次的時間收支核對日報，避免只選高產時段評估機器。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align downtime causes with cutter inspection and geological chainage, checking a complete shift time balance rather than selecting high-output intervals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":37},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-20","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出渣等待若被列為地質停工，會把後勤問題誤判成岩石太硬，導致無效更換刀具或修改推進策略。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Spoil queues classified as ground delay falsely suggest hard rock and prompt ineffective cutter replacement or advance changes. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出渣等待若被列為地質停工，會把後勤問題誤判成岩石太硬，導致無效更換刀具或修改推進策略。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Spoil queues classified as ground delay falsely suggest hard rock and prompt ineffective cutter replacement or advance changes. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","出渣等待若被列為地質停工，會把後勤問題誤判成岩石太硬，導致無效更換刀具或修改推進策略。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Spoil queues classified as ground delay falsely suggest hard rock and prompt ineffective cutter replacement or advance changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"出渣等待若被列為地質停工，會把後勤問題誤判成岩石太硬，導致無效更換刀具或修改推進策略。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Spoil queues classified as ground delay falsely suggest hard rock and prompt ineffective cutter replacement or advance changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":38},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-21","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪山山區工址的長距離運輸使裝載、交會與卸料相互制約，假想多工作面同時出渣時需檢查共同通道容量，不能只按各面最佳日進尺配置車隊。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Long access distances couple loading, passing and unloading. For simultaneous hypothetical headings, test the shared route against combined demand rather than sizing fleets from each face best daily advance. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-21-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"雪山山區工址的長距離運輸使裝載、交會與卸料相互制約，假想多工作面同時出渣時需檢查共同通道容量，不能只按各面最佳日進尺配置車隊。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Long access distances couple loading, passing and unloading. For simultaneous hypothetical headings, test the shared route against combined demand rather than sizing fleets from each face best daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["雪山山區工址的長距離運輸使裝載、交會與卸料相互制約，假想多工作面同時出渣時需檢查共同通道容量，不能只按各面最佳日進尺配置車隊。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Long access distances couple loading, passing and unloading.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雪山山區工址的長距離運輸使裝載、交會與卸料相互制約，假想多工作面同時出渣時需檢查共同通道容量，不能只按各面最佳日進尺配置車隊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Long access distances couple loading, passing and unloading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":39},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-22","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為124.675 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 124.675 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為124.675 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 124.675 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":40},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-23","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：增加車輛若堵住單線交會點，總運量反而下降，且材料補給可能與撤離需求競爭同一空間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: More vehicles can block passing locations and reduce throughput while material deliveries compete with evacuation access. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按車次配對裝載重量和到卸料點時間，找出排隊集中區；比較維修期間與正常時段的有效循環。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair payloads with arrival times at unloading, locate queue concentration and compare effective cycles during maintenance and ordinary service. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":41},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-24","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"增加車輛若堵住單線交會點，總運量反而下降，且材料補給可能與撤離需求競爭同一空間。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"More vehicles can block passing locations and reduce throughput while material deliveries compete with evacuation access. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"增加車輛若堵住單線交會點，總運量反而下降，且材料補給可能與撤離需求競爭同一空間。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"More vehicles can block passing locations and reduce throughput while material deliveries compete with evacuation access. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["增加車輛若堵住單線交會點，總運量反而下降，且材料補給可能與撤離需求競爭同一空間。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["More vehicles can block passing locations and reduce throughput while material deliveries compete with evacuation access.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增加車輛若堵住單線交會點，總運量反而下降，且材料補給可能與撤離需求競爭同一空間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"More vehicles can block passing locations and reduce throughput while material deliveries compete with evacuation access. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":42}],"order":9},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪山長距離貫通的教學情境著重方向傳遞：將洞口地表基準、導坑及主孔控制網分開覆核，找出共用基準偏差無法靠重複量測自行消除的原因。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For long-distance breakthrough, independently examine surface control, pilot-gallery transfer and the main-bore network. Identify why repeated measurements cannot remove a bias inherited from a shared starting datum. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3000 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3000 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"雪山長距離貫通的教學情境著重方向傳遞：將洞口地表基準、導坑及主孔控制網分開覆核，找出共用基準偏差無法靠重複量測自行消除的原因。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"For long-distance breakthrough, independently examine surface control, pilot-gallery transfer and the main-bore network. Identify why repeated measurements cannot remove a bias inherited from a shared starting datum.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","雪山長距離貫通的教學情境著重方向傳遞：將洞口地表基準、導坑及主孔控制網分開覆核，找出共用基準偏差無法靠重複量測自行消除的原因。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","For long-distance breakthrough, independently examine surface control, pilot-gallery transfer and the main-bore network.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雪山長距離貫通的教學情境著重方向傳遞：將洞口地表基準、導坑及主孔控制網分開覆核，找出共用基準偏差無法靠重複量測自行消除的原因。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For long-distance breakthrough, independently examine surface control, pilot-gallery transfer and the main-bore network. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":43},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3000 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.041597 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3000 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.041597 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3000 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.041597 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3000 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.041597 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3000 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3000 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3000 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3000 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0378155 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":44},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：若把導坑成果當絕對真值，主孔與導坑可以共同偏離正確方向，兩者彼此吻合仍會錯過預定貫通位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating pilot control as exact can make both networks agree while both deviate from the intended breakthrough point. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從另一地表控制線重新傳遞方向，對照不同溫度時段的角距原始值，再把閉合差拆成水平與高程分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Transfer orientation from another surface control route, compare raw observations across temperature periods and separate horizontal and vertical closure components. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":45},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把導坑成果當絕對真值，主孔與導坑可以共同偏離正確方向，兩者彼此吻合仍會錯過預定貫通位置。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating pilot control as exact can make both networks agree while both deviate from the intended breakthrough point. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把導坑成果當絕對真值，主孔與導坑可以共同偏離正確方向，兩者彼此吻合仍會錯過預定貫通位置。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Treating pilot control as exact can make both networks agree while both deviate from the intended breakthrough point. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若把導坑成果當絕對真值，主孔與導坑可以共同偏離正確方向，兩者彼此吻合仍會錯過預定貫通位置。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating pilot control as exact can make both networks agree while both deviate from the intended breakthrough point.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把導坑成果當絕對真值，主孔與導坑可以共同偏離正確方向，兩者彼此吻合仍會錯過預定貫通位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating pilot control as exact can make both networks agree while both deviate from the intended breakthrough point. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":46},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-29","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以雪山雙孔道路的一孔維修為情境，分析風門、橫通道及車流邊界如何共同改變網路；不能把施工通風模型直接移作營運控煙模型。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use maintenance in one road bore to examine changes in dampers, passages and traffic boundaries. Construction ventilation cannot be transferred directly into an operational smoke-control model with different occupants and sources. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=500 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=500 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-29-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"以雪山雙孔道路的一孔維修為情境，分析風門、橫通道及車流邊界如何共同改變網路；不能把施工通風模型直接移作營運控煙模型。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Use maintenance in one road bore to examine changes in dampers, passages and traffic boundaries. Construction ventilation cannot be transferred directly into an operational smoke-control model with different occupants and sources.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","以雪山雙孔道路的一孔維修為情境，分析風門、橫通道及車流邊界如何共同改變網路；不能把施工通風模型直接移作營運控煙模型。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Use maintenance in one road bore to examine changes in dampers, passages and traffic boundaries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以雪山雙孔道路的一孔維修為情境，分析風門、橫通道及車流邊界如何共同改變網路；不能把施工通風模型直接移作營運控煙模型。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use maintenance in one road bore to examine changes in dampers, passages and traffic boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":47},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-30","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=500 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為31.0592 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=500 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 31.0592 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=500 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為31.0592 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=500 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 31.0592 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=500 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=500 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=500 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=25.6688 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":48},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-31","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：橫通道門位資料若過期，模型可能預測隔離但現場形成短路風流，關鍵區段抽排效果便被高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Outdated passage-door states may predict isolation while a real airflow shortcut reduces extraction in the critical zone. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步記錄兩孔風速、壓差與門位，先比正常工況再比核准異常工況，辨認風量減少來自漏風還是阻力增加。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise both-bore flow, pressure and door states, comparing normal and approved degraded cases to distinguish leakage from increased resistance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":49},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-32","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"橫通道門位資料若過期，模型可能預測隔離但現場形成短路風流，關鍵區段抽排效果便被高估。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Outdated passage-door states may predict isolation while a real airflow shortcut reduces extraction in the critical zone. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"橫通道門位資料若過期，模型可能預測隔離但現場形成短路風流，關鍵區段抽排效果便被高估。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Outdated passage-door states may predict isolation while a real airflow shortcut reduces extraction in the critical zone. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","橫通道門位資料若過期，模型可能預測隔離但現場形成短路風流，關鍵區段抽排效果便被高估。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Outdated passage-door states may predict isolation while a real airflow shortcut reduces extraction in the critical zone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橫通道門位資料若過期，模型可能預測隔離但現場形成短路風流，關鍵區段抽排效果便被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Outdated passage-door states may predict isolation while a real airflow shortcut reduces extraction in the critical zone. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":50}],"order":10},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-33","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「剩餘集水容積」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remaining sump volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪山排水教學把斷層入流和機電故障合併：若雨後淨入流提高同時一台泵維修，剩餘容積與警報延遲要放在同一時間線，不把名義備援當保證。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘集水容積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Combine fault inflow and equipment state: after rainfall, increased net inflow can coincide with pump maintenance. Place usable volume and alarm delay on one timeline rather than treating nominal redundancy as guaranteed service. A sump offers finite buffering after pumps stop, with usable volume reduced by initial water, sediment and dead spaces. Buffer time depends on net inflow rather than pump nameplate capacity. Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Remaining sump volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=300 m³；淨入流=0.2 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=300 m³; net inflow=0.2 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=25 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘集水容積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Remaining sump volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-33-k1","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume","text":"雪山排水教學把斷層入流和機電故障合併：若雨後淨入流提高同時一台泵維修，剩餘容積與警報延遲要放在同一時間線，不把名義備援當保證。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。","textEn":"Combine fault inflow and equipment state: after rainfall, increased net inflow can coincide with pump maintenance. Place usable volume and alarm delay on one timeline rather than treating nominal redundancy as guaranteed service.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" is correct?","options":["雪山排水教學把斷層入流和機電故障合併：若雨後淨入流提高同時一台泵維修，剩餘容積與警報延遲要放在同一時間線，不把名義備援當保證。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Combine fault inflow and equipment state: after rainfall, increased net inflow can coincide with pump maintenance.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雪山排水教學把斷層入流和機電故障合併：若雨後淨入流提高同時一台泵維修，剩餘容積與警報延遲要放在同一時間線，不把名義備援當保證。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Combine fault inflow and equipment state: after rainfall, increased net inflow can coincide with pump maintenance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":51},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-34","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：定量估算","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘集水容積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remaining sump volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=300 m³；淨入流=0.2 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=25 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為22.7273 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=300 m³; net inflow=0.2 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=25 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 22.7273 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=300 m³；淨入流=0.2 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=25 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為22.7273 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=300 m³; net inflow=0.2 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=25 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 22.7273 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=300 m³；淨入流=0.2 m³/s。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=300 m³; net inflow=0.2 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=25 min.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=300 m³；淨入流=0.2 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=300 m³; net inflow=0.2 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=25 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":52},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-35","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘集水容積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remaining sump volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","failure":"注意干擾：若雨後水量超過平日平均而沿用舊緩衝時間，故障處理可能尚未完成水位已達設備區，形成連鎖失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using an ordinary-day buffer after rainfall can let water reach equipment before recovery is complete, producing cascading failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用實測集水坑水位容積曲線核對流量，再將維修隔離狀態和警報傳輸延遲加入緩衝計算，確認淤積已扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check flow against the measured sump curve, then include isolated equipment and alarm-transmission delay in the buffer calculation with sediment deducted. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":53},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-36","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘集水容積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remaining sump volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若雨後水量超過平日平均而沿用舊緩衝時間，故障處理可能尚未完成水位已達設備區，形成連鎖失效。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using an ordinary-day buffer after rainfall can let water reach equipment before recovery is complete, producing cascading failure. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若雨後水量超過平日平均而沿用舊緩衝時間，故障處理可能尚未完成水位已達設備區，形成連鎖失效。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。","textEn":"Using an ordinary-day buffer after rainfall can let water reach equipment before recovery is complete, producing cascading failure. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若雨後水量超過平日平均而沿用舊緩衝時間，故障處理可能尚未完成水位已達設備區，形成連鎖失效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Using an ordinary-day buffer after rainfall can let water reach equipment before recovery is complete, producing cascading failure.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若雨後水量超過平日平均而沿用舊緩衝時間，故障處理可能尚未完成水位已達設備區，形成連鎖失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using an ordinary-day buffer after rainfall can let water reach equipment before recovery is complete, producing cascading failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":54},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響雪山隧道工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雪山營運交接以排水及通風共同介面為核心，要求一項告警能追到設備位置、供電來源和最後校正；改名或設備更換不能切斷原始趨勢。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Handover focuses on drainage-ventilation interfaces: each alarm must trace to location, supply and last calibration. Renaming or replacement must preserve the ability to interpret historical trends and distinguish renewal from deterioration. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=100 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=100 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"雪山營運交接以排水及通風共同介面為核心，要求一項告警能追到設備位置、供電來源和最後校正；改名或設備更換不能切斷原始趨勢。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Handover focuses on drainage-ventilation interfaces: each alarm must trace to location, supply and last calibration. Renaming or replacement must preserve the ability to interpret historical trends and distinguish renewal from deterioration.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","雪山營運交接以排水及通風共同介面為核心，要求一項告警能追到設備位置、供電來源和最後校正；改名或設備更換不能切斷原始趨勢。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Handover focuses on drainage-ventilation interfaces: each alarm must trace to location, supply and last calibration.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雪山營運交接以排水及通風共同介面為核心，要求一項告警能追到設備位置、供電來源和最後校正；改名或設備更換不能切斷原始趨勢。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Handover focuses on drainage-ventilation interfaces: each alarm must trace to location, supply and last calibration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":55},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=100 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.4 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=100 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.4 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=100 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.4 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=100 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.4 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","原創教學假設：設備總數=100 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=100 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=100 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=100 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":56},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：若新水位計沿用舊零點卻換了安裝高程，趨勢可能顯示假的水量增加；先核對基準而非立刻擴泵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A replacement level sensor at a new elevation with an old zero creates false rising-water trends; check datum before increasing pumping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Hsuehshan Tunnel Engineering, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查低點水位告警與風機故障各一例，從控制畫面找到工單及現場標籤，重算設備更換前後是否可直接比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample a low-point alarm and fan fault from screen to work order and physical tag, testing comparability across equipment replacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":57},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["hsuehshan-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若新水位計沿用舊零點卻換了安裝高程，趨勢可能顯示假的水量增加；先核對基準而非立刻擴泵。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A replacement level sensor at a new elevation with an old zero creates false rising-water trends; check datum before increasing pumping. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若新水位計沿用舊零點卻換了安裝高程，趨勢可能顯示假的水量增加；先核對基準而非立刻擴泵。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"A replacement level sensor at a new elevation with an old zero creates false rising-water trends; check datum before increasing pumping. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"hsuehshan-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-hsuehshan","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若新水位計沿用舊零點卻換了安裝高程，趨勢可能顯示假的水量增加；先核對基準而非立刻擴泵。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A replacement level sensor at a new elevation with an old zero creates false rising-water trends; check datum before increasing pumping.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若新水位計沿用舊零點卻換了安裝高程，趨勢可能顯示假的水量增加；先核對基準而非立刻擴泵。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A replacement level sensor at a new elevation with an old zero creates false rising-water trends; check datum before increasing pumping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":58}],"order":11}],"stepCount":58,"estimatedMinutes":1270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","enrichmentVersion":14,"learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","v14Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["支護安裝時點","Support activation time"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]]},"v14Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，再獨立計算「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」。原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=31 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為334.521 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=20 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為124.675 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate piezometric head and lining pressure, then independently calculate shared access and transport bottlenecks. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=31 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=304.11 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 334.521 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=20 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=137.143 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 124.675 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"破碎帶水壓、長距離探勘與雙孔道路防災","focusEn":"Fault-zone water pressure, long-distance investigation and twin-bore road resilience"}},{"id":"steam-locomotive","title":"蒸汽火車頭工程","titleEn":"Steam Locomotive Engineering","category":"rail","summary":"用熱力循環和非加壓機構模型理解鍋爐、汽缸、連桿、輪軌與維修。","summaryEn":"Use thermodynamic concepts and unpressurized mechanism models to understand boiler, cylinder, rods, wheel-rail interaction and maintenance.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["nps-steam","v10-other-vendor-steam-locomotive"],"diagram":{"type":"locomotive","labels":["熱源","蒸汽","汽缸","連桿","動輪"],"labelsEn":["Heat","Steam","Cylinder","Rods","Driving wheels"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01","order":1,"title":"能源與系統","titleEn":"Energy and system","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-01","order":1,"title":"建立能量轉換圖","titleEn":"Map energy conversion","objective":"完成「建立能量轉換圖」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map energy conversion.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"燃料熱能經蒸汽與活塞轉為機械功，其中存在多種損失。","textEn":"Fuel heat becomes mechanical work through steam and pistons, with multiple losses."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出熱、功與排熱三種能量路徑。","textEn":"Draw heat, work and rejected-heat paths."}],"check":"畫出熱、功與排熱三種能量路徑。","checkEn":"Draw heat, work and rejected-heat paths.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立能量轉換圖」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map energy conversion?","options":["燃料熱能經蒸汽與活塞轉為機械功，其中存在多種損失。","壓力和溫度是不同狀態量，關係取決於工質狀態。","連桿運動可用手動模型展示，無需蒸汽或燃燒。"],"optionsEn":["Fuel heat becomes mechanical work through steam and pistons, with multiple losses.","Pressure and temperature are distinct state variables related through fluid state.","Rod motion can be demonstrated by a hand-operated model without steam or combustion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"燃料熱能經蒸汽與活塞轉為機械功，其中存在多種損失。","explanationEn":"Fuel heat becomes mechanical work through steam and pistons, with multiple losses."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-02","order":2,"title":"區分壓力與溫度","titleEn":"Distinguish pressure and temperature","objective":"完成「區分壓力與溫度」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish pressure and temperature.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"壓力和溫度是不同狀態量，關係取決於工質狀態。","textEn":"Pressure and temperature are distinct state variables related through fluid state."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意狀態表分別列出兩者及單位。","textEn":"List both variables and units separately in a state table."}],"check":"在示意狀態表分別列出兩者及單位。","checkEn":"List both variables and units separately in a state table.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分壓力與溫度」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish pressure and temperature?","options":["連桿運動可用手動模型展示，無需蒸汽或燃燒。","燃料熱能經蒸汽與活塞轉為機械功，其中存在多種損失。","壓力和溫度是不同狀態量，關係取決於工質狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Rod motion can be demonstrated by a hand-operated model without steam or combustion.","Fuel heat becomes mechanical work through steam and pistons, with multiple losses.","Pressure and temperature are distinct state variables related through fluid state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓力和溫度是不同狀態量，關係取決於工質狀態。","explanationEn":"Pressure and temperature are distinct state variables related through fluid state."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-03","order":3,"title":"設定非加壓模型","titleEn":"Define an unpressurized model","objective":"完成「設定非加壓模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define an unpressurized model.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"連桿運動可用手動模型展示，無需蒸汽或燃燒。","textEn":"Rod motion can be demonstrated by a hand-operated model without steam or combustion."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"確定教具沒有壓力源與熱源。","textEn":"Verify the teaching model has no pressure or heat source."}],"check":"確定教具沒有壓力源與熱源。","checkEn":"Verify the teaching model has no pressure or heat source.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「設定非加壓模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define an unpressurized model?","options":["壓力和溫度是不同狀態量，關係取決於工質狀態。","連桿運動可用手動模型展示，無需蒸汽或燃燒。","燃料熱能經蒸汽與活塞轉為機械功，其中存在多種損失。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure and temperature are distinct state variables related through fluid state.","Rod motion can be demonstrated by a hand-operated model without steam or combustion.","Fuel heat becomes mechanical work through steam and pistons, with multiple losses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連桿運動可用手動模型展示，無需蒸汽或燃燒。","explanationEn":"Rod motion can be demonstrated by a hand-operated model without steam or combustion."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02","order":2,"title":"熱交換概念","titleEn":"Heat-exchange concepts","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解受熱與汽化","titleEn":"Understand heating and vaporization","objective":"完成「理解受熱與汽化」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand heating and vaporization.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"顯熱改變溫度，潛熱對應相變能量。","textEn":"Sensible heat changes temperature; latent heat accompanies phase change."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在概念加熱曲線標示兩個區段。","textEn":"Mark both regions on a conceptual heating curve."}],"check":"在概念加熱曲線標示兩個區段。","checkEn":"Mark both regions on a conceptual heating curve.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解受熱與汽化」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand heating and vaporization?","options":["鍋爐把熱傳給水，真實設備的安全依賴專業設計和檢驗。","水垢影響熱傳，腐蝕可能降低材料完整性。","顯熱改變溫度，潛熱對應相變能量。"],"optionsEn":["A boiler transfers heat to water; real equipment safety requires professional design and inspection.","Scale affects heat transfer and corrosion can reduce material integrity.","Sensible heat changes temperature; latent heat accompanies phase change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"顯熱改變溫度，潛熱對應相變能量。","explanationEn":"Sensible heat changes temperature; latent heat accompanies phase change."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-02","order":2,"title":"辨識鍋爐功能","titleEn":"Identify boiler functions","objective":"完成「辨識鍋爐功能」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify boiler functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"鍋爐把熱傳給水，真實設備的安全依賴專業設計和檢驗。","textEn":"A boiler transfers heat to water; real equipment safety requires professional design and inspection."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"只畫功能方塊，不製作任何耐壓部件。","textEn":"Draw functional blocks only and fabricate no pressure components."}],"check":"只畫功能方塊，不製作任何耐壓部件。","checkEn":"Draw functional blocks only and fabricate no pressure components.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識鍋爐功能」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify boiler functions?","options":["顯熱改變溫度，潛熱對應相變能量。","鍋爐把熱傳給水，真實設備的安全依賴專業設計和檢驗。","水垢影響熱傳，腐蝕可能降低材料完整性。"],"optionsEn":["Sensible heat changes temperature; latent heat accompanies phase change.","A boiler transfers heat to water; real equipment safety requires professional design and inspection.","Scale affects heat transfer and corrosion can reduce material integrity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鍋爐把熱傳給水，真實設備的安全依賴專業設計和檢驗。","explanationEn":"A boiler transfers heat to water; real equipment safety requires professional design and inspection."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-03","order":3,"title":"分析水質影響","titleEn":"Analyze water-quality effects","objective":"完成「分析水質影響」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze water-quality effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"水垢影響熱傳，腐蝕可能降低材料完整性。","textEn":"Scale affects heat transfer and corrosion can reduce material integrity."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立水質、熱傳及檢查的關係圖。","textEn":"Map water quality to heat transfer and inspection."}],"check":"建立水質、熱傳及檢查的關係圖。","checkEn":"Map water quality to heat transfer and inspection.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析水質影響」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze water-quality effects?","options":["水垢影響熱傳，腐蝕可能降低材料完整性。","顯熱改變溫度，潛熱對應相變能量。","鍋爐把熱傳給水，真實設備的安全依賴專業設計和檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["Scale affects heat transfer and corrosion can reduce material integrity.","Sensible heat changes temperature; latent heat accompanies phase change.","A boiler transfers heat to water; real equipment safety requires professional design and inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水垢影響熱傳，腐蝕可能降低材料完整性。","explanationEn":"Scale affects heat transfer and corrosion can reduce material integrity."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03","order":3,"title":"汽缸與連桿","titleEn":"Cylinder and rods","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-01","order":1,"title":"理解壓差做功","titleEn":"Understand pressure work","objective":"完成「理解壓差做功」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand pressure work.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"活塞兩側壓差可產生力，位移把力轉成機械功。","textEn":"Pressure difference across a piston produces force, and displacement produces work."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以符號 F = Δp A 檢查單位。","textEn":"Check units in F = Δp A."}],"check":"以符號 F = Δp A 檢查單位。","checkEn":"Check units in F = Δp A.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解壓差做功」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand pressure work?","options":["進汽與排汽的相對時序影響循環，不等同於單純開關。","活塞兩側壓差可產生力，位移把力轉成機械功。","曲柄滑塊把往復運動轉成旋轉，幾何決定位移關係。"],"optionsEn":["Admission and exhaust timing affect the cycle rather than acting as a simple switch.","Pressure difference across a piston produces force, and displacement produces work.","A crank-slider converts reciprocation to rotation, with motion set by geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"活塞兩側壓差可產生力，位移把力轉成機械功。","explanationEn":"Pressure difference across a piston produces force, and displacement produces work."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-02","order":2,"title":"建立曲柄滑塊模型","titleEn":"Build a crank-slider model","objective":"完成「建立曲柄滑塊模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a crank-slider model.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"曲柄滑塊把往復運動轉成旋轉，幾何決定位移關係。","textEn":"A crank-slider converts reciprocation to rotation, with motion set by geometry."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以手動紙板模型觀察一圈的往復次數。","textEn":"Observe reciprocation over one turn using a hand-operated card model."}],"check":"以手動紙板模型觀察一圈的往復次數。","checkEn":"Observe reciprocation over one turn using a hand-operated card model.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立曲柄滑塊模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a crank-slider model?","options":["曲柄滑塊把往復運動轉成旋轉，幾何決定位移關係。","進汽與排汽的相對時序影響循環，不等同於單純開關。","活塞兩側壓差可產生力，位移把力轉成機械功。"],"optionsEn":["A crank-slider converts reciprocation to rotation, with motion set by geometry.","Admission and exhaust timing affect the cycle rather than acting as a simple switch.","Pressure difference across a piston produces force, and displacement produces work."],"answer":0,"explanation":"曲柄滑塊把往復運動轉成旋轉，幾何決定位移關係。","explanationEn":"A crank-slider converts reciprocation to rotation, with motion set by geometry."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-03","order":3,"title":"理解配氣概念","titleEn":"Understand valve-timing concepts","objective":"完成「理解配氣概念」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand valve-timing concepts.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"進汽與排汽的相對時序影響循環，不等同於單純開關。","textEn":"Admission and exhaust timing affect the cycle rather than acting as a simple switch."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意週期圖標示不同功能區段。","textEn":"Mark functional regions on a schematic cycle."}],"check":"在示意週期圖標示不同功能區段。","checkEn":"Mark functional regions on a schematic cycle.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解配氣概念」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand valve-timing concepts?","options":["活塞兩側壓差可產生力，位移把力轉成機械功。","曲柄滑塊把往復運動轉成旋轉，幾何決定位移關係。","進汽與排汽的相對時序影響循環，不等同於單純開關。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure difference across a piston produces force, and displacement produces work.","A crank-slider converts reciprocation to rotation, with motion set by geometry.","Admission and exhaust timing affect the cycle rather than acting as a simple switch."],"answer":2,"explanation":"進汽與排汽的相對時序影響循環，不等同於單純開關。","explanationEn":"Admission and exhaust timing affect the cycle rather than acting as a simple switch."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04","order":4,"title":"輪軌與結構","titleEn":"Wheels rails and structure","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-01","order":1,"title":"辨識牽引與黏著","titleEn":"Identify traction and adhesion","objective":"完成「辨識牽引與黏著」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify traction and adhesion.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"輪軌可傳遞的牽引力受黏著條件限制。","textEn":"Wheel-rail traction is limited by adhesion conditions."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較理想驅動力與可用黏著力。","textEn":"Compare ideal drive force with available adhesion."}],"check":"比較理想驅動力與可用黏著力。","checkEn":"Compare ideal drive force with available adhesion.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識牽引與黏著」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify traction and adhesion?","options":["輪軌可傳遞的牽引力受黏著條件限制。","連桿可協調多個動輪運動，但也帶來幾何和載荷要求。","摩擦與磨耗會改變運動阻力及間隙。"],"optionsEn":["Wheel-rail traction is limited by adhesion conditions.","Coupling rods coordinate driving wheels while adding geometric and load constraints.","Friction and wear change motion resistance and clearance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"輪軌可傳遞的牽引力受黏著條件限制。","explanationEn":"Wheel-rail traction is limited by adhesion conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解連動輪功能","titleEn":"Understand coupled wheels","objective":"完成「理解連動輪功能」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand coupled wheels.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"連桿可協調多個動輪運動，但也帶來幾何和載荷要求。","textEn":"Coupling rods coordinate driving wheels while adding geometric and load constraints."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在低速手動模型檢查是否卡住。","textEn":"Check for binding in a slow hand-operated model."}],"check":"在低速手動模型檢查是否卡住。","checkEn":"Check for binding in a slow hand-operated model.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解連動輪功能」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand coupled wheels?","options":["摩擦與磨耗會改變運動阻力及間隙。","輪軌可傳遞的牽引力受黏著條件限制。","連桿可協調多個動輪運動，但也帶來幾何和載荷要求。"],"optionsEn":["Friction and wear change motion resistance and clearance.","Wheel-rail traction is limited by adhesion conditions.","Coupling rods coordinate driving wheels while adding geometric and load constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"連桿可協調多個動輪運動，但也帶來幾何和載荷要求。","explanationEn":"Coupling rods coordinate driving wheels while adding geometric and load constraints."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-03","order":3,"title":"觀察軸承與潤滑","titleEn":"Observe bearings and lubrication","objective":"完成「觀察軸承與潤滑」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for observe bearings and lubrication.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"摩擦與磨耗會改變運動阻力及間隙。","textEn":"Friction and wear change motion resistance and clearance."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"記錄模型運動阻力前後差異。","textEn":"Record changes in model motion resistance."}],"check":"記錄模型運動阻力前後差異。","checkEn":"Record changes in model motion resistance.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「觀察軸承與潤滑」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains observe bearings and lubrication?","options":["連桿可協調多個動輪運動，但也帶來幾何和載荷要求。","摩擦與磨耗會改變運動阻力及間隙。","輪軌可傳遞的牽引力受黏著條件限制。"],"optionsEn":["Coupling rods coordinate driving wheels while adding geometric and load constraints.","Friction and wear change motion resistance and clearance.","Wheel-rail traction is limited by adhesion conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"摩擦與磨耗會改變運動阻力及間隙。","explanationEn":"Friction and wear change motion resistance and clearance."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05","order":5,"title":"制動與維護概念","titleEn":"Braking and maintenance concepts","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-01","order":1,"title":"理解制動能量","titleEn":"Understand braking energy","objective":"完成「理解制動能量」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand braking energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"減速需移除動能，制動過程會把能量轉到其他形式。","textEn":"Deceleration removes kinetic energy by converting it into other forms."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用能量圖解釋速度增加對動能的影響。","textEn":"Use an energy diagram to explain speed's effect on kinetic energy."}],"check":"用能量圖解釋速度增加對動能的影響。","checkEn":"Use an energy diagram to explain speed's effect on kinetic energy.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解制動能量」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand braking energy?","options":["連桿和輪軸的反覆載荷需要定期檢查。","異常阻力、鬆脫或破損應觸發停止展示及檢查。","減速需移除動能，制動過程會把能量轉到其他形式。"],"optionsEn":["Repeated loading of rods and axles motivates periodic inspection.","Abnormal resistance, loosening or damage should stop the demonstration for inspection.","Deceleration removes kinetic energy by converting it into other forms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"減速需移除動能，制動過程會把能量轉到其他形式。","explanationEn":"Deceleration removes kinetic energy by converting it into other forms."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-02","order":2,"title":"辨識疲勞檢查","titleEn":"Identify fatigue inspections","objective":"完成「辨識疲勞檢查」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify fatigue inspections.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"連桿和輪軸的反覆載荷需要定期檢查。","textEn":"Repeated loading of rods and axles motivates periodic inspection."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為桌面模型列出可觀察鬆動與裂損點。","textEn":"List observable looseness and damage points on the model."}],"check":"為桌面模型列出可觀察鬆動與裂損點。","checkEn":"List observable looseness and damage points on the model.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識疲勞檢查」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify fatigue inspections?","options":["減速需移除動能，制動過程會把能量轉到其他形式。","連桿和輪軸的反覆載荷需要定期檢查。","異常阻力、鬆脫或破損應觸發停止展示及檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Deceleration removes kinetic energy by converting it into other forms.","Repeated loading of rods and axles motivates periodic inspection.","Abnormal resistance, loosening or damage should stop the demonstration for inspection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連桿和輪軸的反覆載荷需要定期檢查。","explanationEn":"Repeated loading of rods and axles motivates periodic inspection."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-03","order":3,"title":"建立停用條件","titleEn":"Set out-of-service conditions","objective":"完成「建立停用條件」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for set out-of-service conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"異常阻力、鬆脫或破損應觸發停止展示及檢查。","textEn":"Abnormal resistance, loosening or damage should stop the demonstration for inspection."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為教具設定明確的停止條件。","textEn":"Define clear stop conditions for the teaching model."}],"check":"為教具設定明確的停止條件。","checkEn":"Define clear stop conditions for the teaching model.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立停用條件」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains set out-of-service conditions?","options":["異常阻力、鬆脫或破損應觸發停止展示及檢查。","減速需移除動能，制動過程會把能量轉到其他形式。","連桿和輪軸的反覆載荷需要定期檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal resistance, loosening or damage should stop the demonstration for inspection.","Deceleration removes kinetic energy by converting it into other forms.","Repeated loading of rods and axles motivates periodic inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"異常阻力、鬆脫或破損應觸發停止展示及檢查。","explanationEn":"Abnormal resistance, loosening or damage should stop the demonstration for inspection."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06","order":6,"title":"模型驗收","titleEn":"Model acceptance","steps":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-01","order":1,"title":"核對機構連續性","titleEn":"Check mechanism continuity","objective":"完成「核對機構連續性」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for check mechanism continuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"一整圈平順轉動可檢查幾何相容性，但不能證明真車安全。","textEn":"Smooth full rotation checks geometric compatibility but does not establish full-scale safety."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以手動完成一圈並記錄卡滯位置。","textEn":"Turn one cycle by hand and record binding locations."}],"check":"以手動完成一圈並記錄卡滯位置。","checkEn":"Turn one cycle by hand and record binding locations.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「核對機構連續性」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains check mechanism continuity?","options":["機構示意及熱力概念可以分開驗證再整合解說。","一整圈平順轉動可檢查幾何相容性，但不能證明真車安全。","排熱、摩擦與不完全熱利用使實際效率低於理想。"],"optionsEn":["Mechanism and thermodynamic concepts can be checked separately before combined explanation.","Smooth full rotation checks geometric compatibility but does not establish full-scale safety.","Heat rejection, friction and imperfect heat use lower real efficiency below ideal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一整圈平順轉動可檢查幾何相容性，但不能證明真車安全。","explanationEn":"Smooth full rotation checks geometric compatibility but does not establish full-scale safety."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-02","order":2,"title":"整理效率限制","titleEn":"Summarize efficiency limits","objective":"完成「整理效率限制」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for summarize efficiency limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"排熱、摩擦與不完全熱利用使實際效率低於理想。","textEn":"Heat rejection, friction and imperfect heat use lower real efficiency below ideal."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為各損失指定其所在功能方塊。","textEn":"Assign each loss to a functional block."}],"check":"為各損失指定其所在功能方塊。","checkEn":"Assign each loss to a functional block.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「整理效率限制」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains summarize efficiency limits?","options":["排熱、摩擦與不完全熱利用使實際效率低於理想。","機構示意及熱力概念可以分開驗證再整合解說。","一整圈平順轉動可檢查幾何相容性，但不能證明真車安全。"],"optionsEn":["Heat rejection, friction and imperfect heat use lower real efficiency below ideal.","Mechanism and thermodynamic concepts can be checked separately before combined explanation.","Smooth full rotation checks geometric compatibility but does not establish full-scale safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"排熱、摩擦與不完全熱利用使實際效率低於理想。","explanationEn":"Heat rejection, friction and imperfect heat use lower real efficiency below ideal."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-03","order":3,"title":"交付教學示意","titleEn":"Deliver the teaching schematic","objective":"完成「交付教學示意」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver the teaching schematic.","knowledge":[{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"機構示意及熱力概念可以分開驗證再整合解說。","textEn":"Mechanism and thermodynamic concepts can be checked separately before combined explanation."},{"id":"steam-locomotive-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交無壓力模型照片、能源圖及學習心得。","textEn":"Submit a photo of the unpressurized model, energy diagram and learning notes."}],"check":"提交無壓力模型照片、能源圖及學習心得。","checkEn":"Submit a photo of the unpressurized model, energy diagram and learning notes.","sourceIds":["nps-steam"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付教學示意」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver the teaching schematic?","options":["一整圈平順轉動可檢查幾何相容性，但不能證明真車安全。","排熱、摩擦與不完全熱利用使實際效率低於理想。","機構示意及熱力概念可以分開驗證再整合解說。"],"optionsEn":["Smooth full rotation checks geometric compatibility but does not establish full-scale safety.","Heat rejection, friction and imperfect heat use lower real efficiency below ideal.","Mechanism and thermodynamic concepts can be checked separately before combined explanation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"機構示意及熱力概念可以分開驗證再整合解說。","explanationEn":"Mechanism and thermodynamic concepts can be checked separately before combined explanation."},"prerequisiteIds":["steam-locomotive-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course"},{"id":"ferrari","title":"法拉利與精密汽車製造","titleEn":"Ferrari and Precision Automotive Manufacturing","category":"automotive","summary":"以公開工廠案例理解車身、動力、底盤、塗裝與品質追溯；所有組裝動作以虛擬模型呈現。","summaryEn":"Use public factory examples to study body, powertrain, chassis, finishing and quality traceability through virtual assembly.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["ferrari-body"],"diagram":{"type":"car","labels":["車身","動力","懸吊","線束","檢驗"],"labelsEn":["Body","Powertrain","Suspension","Harness","Inspection"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"ferrari-s01","order":1,"title":"需求與平台","titleEn":"Requirements and platform","steps":[{"id":"ferrari-s01-01","order":1,"title":"定義車輛使用情境","titleEn":"Define vehicle use","objective":"完成「定義車輛使用情境」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define vehicle use.","knowledge":[{"id":"ferrari-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"性能、舒適、排放與成本形成互相牽制的需求。","textEn":"Performance, comfort, emissions and cost create interacting requirements."},{"id":"ferrari-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立城市與長途兩種情境比較。","textEn":"Compare urban and long-distance use cases."}],"check":"建立城市與長途兩種情境比較。","checkEn":"Compare urban and long-distance use cases.","sourceIds":["ferrari-body"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「定義車輛使用情境」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define vehicle use?","options":["性能、舒適、排放與成本形成互相牽制的需求。","車身、底盤及動力系統的介面決定整車整合。","零件批號與裝配紀錄可定位受影響車輛。"],"optionsEn":["Performance, comfort, emissions and cost create interacting requirements.","Body, chassis and powertrain interfaces determine vehicle integration.","Part lots and assembly records identify affected vehicles."],"answer":0,"explanation":"性能、舒適、排放與成本形成互相牽制的需求。","explanationEn":"Performance, comfort, emissions and cost create interacting requirements."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"seq