ceptual hydraulic power is ρgQH; output also depends on efficiency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"發電機把機械能轉為電能，並網涉及電氣同步及保護。","explanationEn":"A generator converts mechanical to electrical energy; grid connection involves synchronization and protection."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"three-gorges-s05","order":5,"title":"航運與環境","titleEn":"Navigation and environment","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-s05-01","order":1,"title":"理解船閘水位轉換","titleEn":"Understand lock-level transitions","objective":"完成「理解船閘水位轉換」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand lock-level transitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"船閘透過分段改變水位讓船舶跨越高差。","textEn":"Locks change water level in stages to move vessels across elevation differences."},{"id":"three-gorges-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以無流速參數動畫展示概念水位變化。","textEn":"Animate conceptual water levels without operational flow settings."}],"check":"以無流速參數動畫展示概念水位變化。","checkEn":"Animate conceptual water levels without operational flow settings.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解船閘水位轉換」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand lock-level transitions?","options":["水庫改變流速和沉積分布，需長期監測。","工程效益評估需同時考慮移民、生態及下游影響。","船閘透過分段改變水位讓船舶跨越高差。"],"optionsEn":["A reservoir changes velocity and sediment distribution, requiring long-term monitoring.","Benefit assessment also considers resettlement, ecology and downstream impacts.","Locks change water level in stages to move vessels across elevation differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"船閘透過分段改變水位讓船舶跨越高差。","explanationEn":"Locks change water level in stages to move vessels across elevation differences."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"three-gorges-s05-02","order":2,"title":"分析泥砂輸移","titleEn":"Analyze sediment transport","objective":"完成「分析泥砂輸移」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze sediment transport.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"水庫改變流速和沉積分布，需長期監測。","textEn":"A reservoir changes velocity and sediment distribution, requiring long-term monitoring."},{"id":"three-gorges-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出可能沉積與侵蝕區域及不確定度。","textEn":"Mark possible deposition and erosion areas with uncertainty."}],"check":"標出可能沉積與侵蝕區域及不確定度。","checkEn":"Mark possible deposition and erosion areas with uncertainty.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析泥砂輸移」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze sediment transport?","options":["船閘透過分段改變水位讓船舶跨越高差。","水庫改變流速和沉積分布，需長期監測。","工程效益評估需同時考慮移民、生態及下游影響。"],"optionsEn":["Locks change water level in stages to move vessels across elevation differences.","A reservoir changes velocity and sediment distribution, requiring long-term monitoring.","Benefit assessment also considers resettlement, ecology and downstream impacts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水庫改變流速和沉積分布，需長期監測。","explanationEn":"A reservoir changes velocity and sediment distribution, requiring long-term monitoring."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"three-gorges-s05-03","order":3,"title":"納入社會與生態影響","titleEn":"Include social and ecological impacts","objective":"完成「納入社會與生態影響」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for include social and ecological impacts.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"工程效益評估需同時考慮移民、生態及下游影響。","textEn":"Benefit assessment also considers resettlement, ecology and downstream impacts."},{"id":"three-gorges-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立影響、證據與補救追蹤表。","textEn":"Create an impact, evidence and mitigation tracking table."}],"check":"建立影響、證據與補救追蹤表。","checkEn":"Create an impact, evidence and mitigation tracking table.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「納入社會與生態影響」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains include social and ecological impacts?","options":["工程效益評估需同時考慮移民、生態及下游影響。","船閘透過分段改變水位讓船舶跨越高差。","水庫改變流速和沉積分布，需長期監測。"],"optionsEn":["Benefit assessment also considers resettlement, ecology and downstream impacts.","Locks change water level in stages to move vessels across elevation differences.","A reservoir changes velocity and sediment distribution, requiring long-term monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"工程效益評估需同時考慮移民、生態及下游影響。","explanationEn":"Benefit assessment also considers resettlement, ecology and downstream impacts."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"three-gorges-s06","order":6,"title":"監測與資產管理","titleEn":"Monitoring and asset management","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-s06-01","order":1,"title":"建立結構監測基準","titleEn":"Set structural monitoring baselines","objective":"完成「建立結構監測基準」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for set structural monitoring baselines.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"位移、滲流與溫度需連結環境條件解讀。","textEn":"Displacement, seepage and temperature need environmental context."},{"id":"three-gorges-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為虛擬資料記錄水位與季節。","textEn":"Annotate virtual data with reservoir level and season."}],"check":"為虛擬資料記錄水位與季節。","checkEn":"Annotate virtual data with reservoir level and season.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立結構監測基準」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains set structural monitoring baselines?","options":["發電量不能單獨代表整項工程的成功。","位移、滲流與溫度需連結環境條件解讀。","大型壩體的安全判斷需要多種證據及獨立專業審查。"],"optionsEn":["Generation alone does not represent overall project success.","Displacement, seepage and temperature need environmental context.","Large-dam safety needs multiple evidence types and independent expertise."],"answer":1,"explanation":"位移、滲流與溫度需連結環境條件解讀。","explanationEn":"Displacement, seepage and temperature need environmental context."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"three-gorges-s06-02","order":2,"title":"理解獨立安全審查","titleEn":"Understand independent safety review","objective":"完成「理解獨立安全審查」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand independent safety review.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"大型壩體的安全判斷需要多種證據及獨立專業審查。","textEn":"Large-dam safety needs multiple evidence types and independent expertise."},{"id":"three-gorges-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把模型、量測與巡檢列成不同證據來源。","textEn":"Separate models, instruments and inspections as evidence sources."}],"check":"把模型、量測與巡檢列成不同證據來源。","checkEn":"Separate models, instruments and inspections as evidence sources.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解獨立安全審查」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand independent safety review?","options":["大型壩體的安全判斷需要多種證據及獨立專業審查。","發電量不能單獨代表整項工程的成功。","位移、滲流與溫度需連結環境條件解讀。"],"optionsEn":["Large-dam safety needs multiple evidence types and independent expertise.","Generation alone does not represent overall project success.","Displacement, seepage and temperature need environmental context."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大型壩體的安全判斷需要多種證據及獨立專業審查。","explanationEn":"Large-dam safety needs multiple evidence types and independent expertise."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"three-gorges-s06-03","order":3,"title":"交付多目標回顧","titleEn":"Deliver a multi-objective review","objective":"完成「交付多目標回顧」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver a multi-objective review.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"發電量不能單獨代表整項工程的成功。","textEn":"Generation alone does not represent overall project success."},{"id":"three-gorges-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"交付能源圖、影響矩陣及未解問題。","textEn":"Deliver the energy map, impact matrix and open questions."}],"check":"交付能源圖、影響矩陣及未解問題。","checkEn":"Deliver the energy map, impact matrix and open questions.","sourceIds":["ctg-three-gorges"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付多目標回顧」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver a multi-objective review?","options":["位移、滲流與溫度需連結環境條件解讀。","大型壩體的安全判斷需要多種證據及獨立專業審查。","發電量不能單獨代表整項工程的成功。"],"optionsEn":["Displacement, seepage and temperature need environmental context.","Large-dam safety needs multiple evidence types and independent expertise.","Generation alone does not represent overall project success."],"answer":2,"explanation":"發電量不能單獨代表整項工程的成功。","explanationEn":"Generation alone does not represent overall project success."},"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「洪峰預報偏差帳」與「分段庫容積分」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Flood forecast bias account\" and \"Piecewise storage integration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-01","title":"洪峰預報偏差帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flood forecast bias account: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-s06-03"],"objective":"說明「洪峰預報偏差帳」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flood forecast bias account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大型水庫調度先把預報入流與可控制出流分開。入流偏差會隨時間積分成庫容偏差，即使瞬時流量差看似不大，也可能持續耗用預留空間。模型必須以相同時間窗對齊雨量預報、支流到達與下游限制，不能把更新前後的預報當成兩股來水。 逐時正負誤差可能在期末抵消，但最大累積偏差仍決定需要保留的暫時空間，應同時報告兩種量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪峰預報偏差帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reservoir scheduling separates forecast inflow from controllable release. Inflow bias integrates over time into storage error, so a modest flow discrepancy can consume reserved space when it persists. Rainfall predictions, tributary arrival and downstream restrictions must share a time window; forecast revisions are alternative estimates, not additional streams of water. Positive and negative hourly errors may cancel at the endpoint, while the maximum cumulative error still determines temporary space requirements; report both quantities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flood forecast bias account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洪峰預報偏差帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flood forecast bias account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-01-k1","title":"洪峰預報偏差帳","titleEn":"Flood forecast bias account","text":"大型水庫調度先把預報入流與可控制出流分開。入流偏差會隨時間積分成庫容偏差，即使瞬時流量差看似不大，也可能持續耗用預留空間。","textEn":"Reservoir scheduling separates forecast inflow from controllable release. Inflow bias integrates over time into storage error, so a modest flow discrepancy can consume reserved space when it persists.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「洪峰預報偏差帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flood forecast bias account\" is correct?","options":["每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水","大型水庫調度先把預報入流與可控制出流分開。","相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容"],"optionsEn":["Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow.","Reservoir scheduling separates forecast inflow from controllable release.","Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大型水庫調度先把預報入流與可控制出流分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reservoir scheduling separates forecast inflow from controllable release. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":19},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-02","title":"洪峰預報偏差帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Flood forecast bias account: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洪峰預報偏差帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flood forecast bias account” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。模型邊界：偏差在整段期間固定，忽略水面雨量蒸發及取水；只計預報誤差體積。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3. Model boundary: constant bias throughout the interval, omitting surface rainfall, evaporation and withdrawals; this is forecast error volume only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將逐時預報與事後入流各列一欄，以相同起訖時間積分並核對水位庫容表推算的增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tabulate hourly forecasts beside reconstructed inflow, integrate over identical limits and compare the increment with the stage-storage relation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。模型邊界：偏差在整段期間固定，忽略水面雨量蒸發及取水；只計預報誤差體積。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3. Model boundary: constant bias throughout the interval, omitting surface rainfall, evaporation and withdrawals; this is forecast error volume only.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「洪峰預報偏差帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flood forecast bias account\", which statement holds?","options":["出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度","大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。"],"optionsEn":["The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach.","A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":20},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-03","title":"洪峰預報偏差帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flood forecast bias account: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洪峰預報偏差帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flood forecast bias account” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將逐時預報與事後入流各列一欄，以相同起訖時間積分並核對水位庫容表推算的增量。另查出流儀表是否延遲，若流量偏差與水位變化不閉合，先排除時間戳及曲線版本不同，不直接調整防洪限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tabulate hourly forecasts beside reconstructed inflow, integrate over identical limits and compare the increment with the stage-storage relation. Check release-meter delay separately. If flow imbalance and level change disagree, investigate timestamps and curve versions before interpreting the discrepancy as lost flood space. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立六小時誤差帳，再把偏差改成前半正值、後半負值，分別比較最大暫存量與期末淨增量，說明兩者對預留空間的意義不同。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build a six-hour error account, then reverse the bias sign halfway through. Compare maximum temporary storage with the final net increment and explain why they imply different space requirements.","failure":"注意干擾：預報低估若與出流受限同時發生，庫容偏差會持續累積；但水位異常也可能來自回水或量測基準漂移，必須以第二種水量證據區分，不能只憑單站水位判斷預報失準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Underprediction combined with constrained release accumulates storage error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將逐時預報與事後入流各列一欄，以相同起訖時間積分並核對水位庫容表推算的增量。另查出流儀表是否延遲，若流量偏差與水位變化不閉合，先排除時間戳及曲線版本不同，不直接調整防洪限制。","textEn":"Tabulate hourly forecasts beside reconstructed inflow, integrate over identical limits and compare the increment with the stage-storage relation. Check release-meter delay separately. If flow imbalance and level change disagree, investigate timestamps and curve versions before interpreting the discrepancy as lost flood space.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立六小時誤差帳，再把偏差改成前半正值、後半負值，分別比較最大暫存量與期末淨增量，說明兩者對預留空間的意義不同。","textEn":"Build a six-hour error account, then reverse the bias sign halfway through. Compare maximum temporary storage with the final net increment and explain why they imply different space requirements.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「洪峰預報偏差帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flood forecast bias account\"?","options":["將逐時預報與事後入流各列一欄，以相同起訖時間積分並核對水位庫容表推算的增量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同"],"optionsEn":["Tabulate hourly forecasts beside reconstructed inflow, integrate over identical limits and compare the increment with the stage-storage relation.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將逐時預報與事後入流各列一欄，以相同起訖時間積分並核對水位庫容表推算的增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tabulate hourly forecasts beside reconstructed inflow, integrate over identical limits and compare the increment with the stage-storage relation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":21},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-04","title":"洪峰預報偏差帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flood forecast bias account: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洪峰預報偏差帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flood forecast bias account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"預報低估若與出流受限同時發生，庫容偏差會持續累積；但水位異常也可能來自回水或量測基準漂移，必須以第二種水量證據區分，不能只憑單站水位判斷預報失準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Underprediction combined with constrained release accumulates storage error. An unusual level can also reflect backwater or datum drift, so a second water-balance observation is needed before assigning the discrepancy to forecast failure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：逐時正負誤差可能在期末抵消，但最大累積偏差仍決定需要保留的暫時空間，應同時報告兩種量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Positive and negative hourly errors may cancel at the endpoint, while the maximum cumulative error still determines temporary space requirements; report both quantities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"預報低估若與出流受限同時發生，庫容偏差會持續累積；但水位異常也可能來自回水或量測基準漂移，必須以第二種水量證據區分，不能只憑單站水位判斷預報失準。","textEn":"Underprediction combined with constrained release accumulates storage error. An unusual level can also reflect backwater or datum drift, so a second water-balance observation is needed before assigning the discrepancy to forecast failure.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「洪峰預報偏差帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flood forecast bias account\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","預報低估若與出流受限同時發生，庫容偏差會持續累積；但水位異常也可能來自回水或量測基準漂移，必須以第二種水量證據區分，不能只憑單站水位判斷預報失準。","相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Underprediction combined with constrained release accumulates storage error.","Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"預報低估若與出流受限同時發生，庫容偏差會持續累積；但水位異常也可能來自回水或量測基準漂移，必須以第二種水量證據區分，不能只憑單站水位判斷預報失準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Underprediction combined with constrained release accumulates storage error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":22},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-05","title":"分段庫容積分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piecewise storage integration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「分段庫容積分」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piecewise storage integration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。用相鄰高程的水面面積做梯形積分，是資料稀疏時可檢查的近似；但支流庫灣及回水的空間差異仍須另外處理，不能把單站水位當成全庫水平面的證明。 若測深採用的水位基準與岸線高程不同，整張容量曲線會偏移，因此測量基準屬於模型輸入的一部分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分段庫容積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area. A widening valley gives different volumes for equal level increments. Trapezoidal integration between surveyed areas provides a transparent approximation when data are sparse, but tributary bays and backwater remain spatial effects that a single gauge cannot resolve. A mismatch between bathymetric water-level datum and shoreline elevations shifts the capacity curve; reference control is therefore part of the model input. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piecewise storage integration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分段庫容積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piecewise storage integration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-05-k1","title":"分段庫容積分","titleEn":"Piecewise storage integration","text":"水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。用相鄰高程的水面面積做梯形積分，是資料稀疏時可檢查的近似；但支流庫灣及回水的空間差異仍須另外處理，不能把單站水位當成全庫水平面的證明。","textEn":"Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area. A widening valley gives different volumes for equal level increments.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分段庫容積分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piecewise storage integration\" is correct?","options":["相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容","沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算","水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。"],"optionsEn":["Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.","Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.","Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":23},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-06","title":"分段庫容積分：定量估算","titleEn":"Piecewise storage integration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分段庫容積分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piecewise storage integration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。模型邊界：相鄰斷面的面積隨高程線性變化且假設靜水面；不是完整庫容曲線。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3. Model boundary: area changes linearly with elevation between observations and the surface is level; this is not a complete capacity curve. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以相同垂直基準疊合兩次測量輪廓，檢查支流庫灣是否被遺漏，再把高程間距減半比較積分變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Overlay survey contours in one vertical datum and check missing tributary bays.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。模型邊界：相鄰斷面的面積隨高程線性變化且假設靜水面；不是完整庫容曲線。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3. Model boundary: area changes linearly with elevation between observations and the surface is level; this is not a complete capacity curve.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分段庫容積分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piecewise storage integration\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。","通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數","壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3.","Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles.","Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":24},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-07","title":"分段庫容積分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piecewise storage integration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分段庫容積分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piecewise storage integration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以相同垂直基準疊合兩次測量輪廓，檢查支流庫灣是否被遺漏，再把高程間距減半比較積分變化。若細分結果差異集中在一段高程，應補查地形轉折，而非以整庫平均面積掩蓋局部誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Overlay survey contours in one vertical datum and check missing tributary bays. Halve the elevation interval and compare integrated volumes. If the change concentrates in one elevation band, investigate a terrain transition rather than hiding local error behind a reservoir-wide mean area. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出三個高程的面積曲線，加入中間面積與端點線性值不同的情境，計算粗細兩種積分差並提出最值得補測的高程區間。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot areas at three elevations and make the middle area differ from linear interpolation. Calculate coarse and refined volumes, then identify the elevation band where another survey would be most valuable.","failure":"注意干擾：岸線插值錯誤會讓可用庫容被高估，尤其在淹沒平台突然展寬的位置；這類幾何誤差與蒸發損失的時間特徵不同，可用靜水測量及多次水量閉合分辨。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incorrect shoreline interpolation can overstate usable storage, especially where a submerged terrace widens abruptly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以相同垂直基準疊合兩次測量輪廓，檢查支流庫灣是否被遺漏，再把高程間距減半比較積分變化。若細分結果差異集中在一段高程，應補查地形轉折，而非以整庫平均面積掩蓋局部誤差。","textEn":"Overlay survey contours in one vertical datum and check missing tributary bays. Halve the elevation interval and compare integrated volumes. If the change concentrates in one elevation band, investigate a terrain transition rather than hiding local error behind a reservoir-wide mean area.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出三個高程的面積曲線，加入中間面積與端點線性值不同的情境，計算粗細兩種積分差並提出最值得補測的高程區間。","textEn":"Plot areas at three elevations and make the middle area differ from linear interpolation. Calculate coarse and refined volumes, then identify the elevation band where another survey would be most valuable.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分段庫容積分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piecewise storage integration\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以相同垂直基準疊合兩次測量輪廓，檢查支流庫灣是否被遺漏，再把高程間距減半比較積分變化。","水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Overlay survey contours in one vertical datum and check missing tributary bays.","A reservoir surface is level at every discharge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以相同垂直基準疊合兩次測量輪廓，檢查支流庫灣是否被遺漏，再把高程間距減半比較積分變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Overlay survey contours in one vertical datum and check missing tributary bays. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":25},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-08","title":"分段庫容積分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piecewise storage integration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分段庫容積分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piecewise storage integration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"岸線插值錯誤會讓可用庫容被高估，尤其在淹沒平台突然展寬的位置；這類幾何誤差與蒸發損失的時間特徵不同，可用靜水測量及多次水量閉合分辨。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incorrect shoreline interpolation can overstate usable storage, especially where a submerged terrace widens abruptly. This geometric error behaves differently from evaporation loss and can be distinguished using static surveys and repeated balance closure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若測深採用的水位基準與岸線高程不同，整張容量曲線會偏移，因此測量基準屬於模型輸入的一部分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A mismatch between bathymetric water-level datum and shoreline elevations shifts the capacity curve; reference control is therefore part of the model input.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"岸線插值錯誤會讓可用庫容被高估，尤其在淹沒平台突然展寬的位置；這類幾何誤差與蒸發損失的時間特徵不同，可用靜水測量及多次水量閉合分辨。","textEn":"Incorrect shoreline interpolation can overstate usable storage, especially where a submerged terrace widens abruptly. This geometric error behaves differently from evaporation loss and can be distinguished using static surveys and repeated balance closure.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分段庫容積分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piecewise storage integration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算","岸線插值錯誤會讓可用庫容被高估，尤其在淹沒平台突然展寬的位置；這類幾何誤差與蒸發損失的時間特徵不同，可用靜水測量及多次水量閉合分辨。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.","Incorrect shoreline interpolation can overstate usable storage, especially where a submerged terrace widens abruptly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"岸線插值錯誤會讓可用庫容被高估，尤其在淹沒平台突然展寬的位置；這類幾何誤差與蒸發損失的時間特徵不同，可用靜水測量及多次水量閉合分辨。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incorrect shoreline interpolation can overstate usable storage, especially where a submerged terrace widens abruptly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":26}],"order":7},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「泥砂質量與淤積」與「分層取水混溫」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sediment mass and deposition\" and \"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-09","title":"泥砂質量與淤積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment mass and deposition: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「泥砂質量與淤積」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment mass and deposition” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"懸浮泥砂先以乾質量守恆，沉積後再透過乾容重轉成體積，兩個步驟不可混用水的密度。流量、濃度與攔砂比例共同控制入庫及留庫質量；細粒壓密會隨時間改變體積，因此一次估算的體積不能直接當成永久損失曲線。 乾容重包含沉積孔隙的體積效應，壓密後即使乾質量不變，對應占據庫容仍可能減少，需明示測量齡期。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥砂質量與淤積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Suspended sediment is first conserved as dry mass and then converted to deposited volume using dry bulk density, not water density. Discharge, concentration and trapping fraction jointly control incoming and retained mass. Fine material consolidates over time, so one volume estimate does not establish a permanent capacity-loss curve. Dry bulk density includes pore-volume effects, so consolidation can reduce occupied storage without changing dry mass; specify the age of the surveyed deposit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment mass and deposition” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泥砂質量與淤積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment mass and deposition”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-09-k1","title":"泥砂質量與淤積","titleEn":"Sediment mass and deposition","text":"懸浮泥砂先以乾質量守恆，沉積後再透過乾容重轉成體積，兩個步驟不可混用水的密度。流量、濃度與攔砂比例共同控制入庫及留庫質量；細粒壓密會隨時間改變體積，因此一次估算的體積不能直接當成永久損失曲線。","textEn":"Suspended sediment is first conserved as dry mass and then converted to deposited volume using dry bulk density, not water density. Discharge, concentration and trapping fraction jointly control incoming and retained mass.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泥砂質量與淤積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment mass and deposition\" is correct?","options":["懸浮泥砂先以乾質量守恆，沉積後再透過乾容重轉成體積，兩個步驟不可混用水的密度。","沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算","出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度"],"optionsEn":["Suspended sediment is first conserved as dry mass and then converted to deposited volume using dry bulk density, not water density.","Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.","The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach."],"answer":0,"explanation":"懸浮泥砂先以乾質量守恆，沉積後再透過乾容重轉成體積，兩個步驟不可混用水的密度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Suspended sediment is first conserved as dry mass and then converted to deposited volume using dry bulk density, not water density. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":27},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-10","title":"泥砂質量與淤積：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment mass and deposition: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泥砂質量與淤積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment mass and deposition” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3。模型邊界：流量濃度及截留比例皆固定；不含床載、再懸浮及後續壓密。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3. Model boundary: constant flow, concentration and trapping fraction; excludes bed load, resuspension and subsequent consolidation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時採集不同水深的濃度樣本，核對濁度換算是否跨越粒徑改變，再用沉積岩心乾重與體積估算容重。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3。模型邊界：流量濃度及截留比例皆固定；不含床載、再懸浮及後續壓密。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3. Model boundary: constant flow, concentration and trapping fraction; excludes bed load, resuspension and subsequent consolidation.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泥砂質量與淤積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment mass and deposition\", which statement holds?","options":["大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3。","總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同"],"optionsEn":["A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","Original hypothetical example.","Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=2000 m3/s; C=0.30 kg/m3; t=86400 s; f=0.60 (dimensionless); rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; V=Q*C*t*f/rhoDry=25920 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":28},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-11","title":"泥砂質量與淤積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment mass and deposition: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泥砂質量與淤積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment mass and deposition” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時採集不同水深的濃度樣本，核對濁度換算是否跨越粒徑改變，再用沉積岩心乾重與體積估算容重。將質量帳與測深體積比較時必須採相同期間，否則洪水後壓密會被誤認為泥砂離庫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores. Compare mass and bathymetric volume over the same period; otherwise consolidation after a flood may be mistaken for sediment leaving the reservoir. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以兩種乾容重重算同一留庫質量，再令洪水濃度隨流量先升後降，繪出質量輸入曲線，說明單一平均濃度會遺失哪些時序資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate one retained mass using two dry bulk densities, then make concentration rise and fall around the flood peak. Plot incoming mass and identify timing information lost by one average concentration.","failure":"注意干擾：只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Surface samples can miss concentrated near-bed flow and understate retained mass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時採集不同水深的濃度樣本，核對濁度換算是否跨越粒徑改變，再用沉積岩心乾重與體積估算容重。將質量帳與測深體積比較時必須採相同期間，否則洪水後壓密會被誤認為泥砂離庫。","textEn":"Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores. Compare mass and bathymetric volume over the same period; otherwise consolidation after a flood may be mistaken for sediment leaving the reservoir.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以兩種乾容重重算同一留庫質量，再令洪水濃度隨流量先升後降，繪出質量輸入曲線，說明單一平均濃度會遺失哪些時序資訊。","textEn":"Recalculate one retained mass using two dry bulk densities, then make concentration rise and fall around the flood peak. Plot incoming mass and identify timing information lost by one average concentration.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泥砂質量與淤積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment mass and deposition\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分","同時採集不同水深的濃度樣本，核對濁度換算是否跨越粒徑改變，再用沉積岩心乾重與體積估算容重。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score.","Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同時採集不同水深的濃度樣本，核對濁度換算是否跨越粒徑改變，再用沉積岩心乾重與體積估算容重。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":29},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-12","title":"泥砂質量與淤積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment mass and deposition: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泥砂質量與淤積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment mass and deposition” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Surface samples can miss concentrated near-bed flow and understate retained mass. Converting with particle density also ignores pore space and understates deposited volume, allowing both errors to reinforce one another. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：乾容重包含沉積孔隙的體積效應，壓密後即使乾質量不變，對應占據庫容仍可能減少，需明示測量齡期。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dry bulk density includes pore-volume effects, so consolidation can reduce occupied storage without changing dry mass; specify the age of the surveyed deposit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。","textEn":"Surface samples can miss concentrated near-bed flow and understate retained mass. Converting with particle density also ignores pore space and understates deposited volume, allowing both errors to reinforce one another.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泥砂質量與淤積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment mass and deposition\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度"],"optionsEn":["Surface samples can miss concentrated near-bed flow and understate retained mass.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Surface samples can miss concentrated near-bed flow and understate retained mass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":30},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-13","title":"分層取水混溫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「分層取水混溫」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"深庫水溫分層會讓相同總流量具有不同下游熱負荷。理想混合先以各支流質量流率乘比熱與溫度作能量守恆，再求共同出口溫度；開口所在高程不等於實際吸入水層，因取水流束可能跨越密度界面，必須量測垂向剖面。 熱量帳應明示共同參考溫度；在相同比熱近似下參考值會相消，但水流的實際來源與交換路徑不能省略。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層取水混溫」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Thermal stratification allows equal total releases to carry different downstream heat loads. Ideal mixing conserves each stream mass flow multiplied by heat capacity and temperature. The elevation of an opening does not uniquely identify the withdrawn layer, because the intake flow can entrain water across a density interface. The heat account needs a common reference temperature; it cancels under equal heat capacities, while stream origins and exchange paths still require explicit identification. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC.","failure":"常見誤解：「出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分層取水混溫」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-13-k1","title":"分層取水混溫","titleEn":"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing","text":"深庫水溫分層會讓相同總流量具有不同下游熱負荷。理想混合先以各支流質量流率乘比熱與溫度作能量守恆，再求共同出口溫度；開口所在高程不等於實際吸入水層，因取水流束可能跨越密度界面，必須量測垂向剖面。","textEn":"Thermal stratification allows equal total releases to carry different downstream heat loads. Ideal mixing conserves each stream mass flow multiplied by heat capacity and temperature.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分層取水混溫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing\" is correct?","options":["出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度","深庫水溫分層會讓相同總流量具有不同下游熱負荷。","通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數"],"optionsEn":["The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach.","Thermal stratification allows equal total releases to carry different downstream heat loads.","Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深庫水溫分層會讓相同總流量具有不同下游熱負荷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Thermal stratification allows equal total releases to carry different downstream heat loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":31},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-14","title":"分層取水混溫：定量估算","titleEn":"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分層取水混溫」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC。模型邊界：兩水流密度比熱相同、完全混合且無外界熱交換；不代表生態合格溫度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC. Model boundary: equal density and heat capacity, complete mixing and no external heat exchange; not an ecological compliance temperature. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在取水口上游布設垂向溫度剖面，並量測混合後斷面的橫向差異。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure an upstream vertical temperature profile and lateral differences after mixing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC。模型邊界：兩水流密度比熱相同、完全混合且無外界熱交換；不代表生態合格溫度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC. Model boundary: equal density and heat capacity, complete mixing and no external heat exchange; not an ecological compliance temperature.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分層取水混溫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing\", which statement holds?","options":["壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭","水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC。"],"optionsEn":["Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head.","A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.","Original hypothetical example."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qwarm=120 m3/s; Twarm=22 degC; Qcold=80 m3/s; Tcold=12 degC; Tout=(Qwarm*Twarm+Qcold*Tcold)/(Qwarm+Qcold)=18 degC. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":32},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-15","title":"分層取水混溫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分層取水混溫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在取水口上游布設垂向溫度剖面，並量測混合後斷面的橫向差異。以總流量與熱量殘差檢查混合是否完成；若出口單點溫度符合算值而橫向差異仍大，不能宣稱整個河段具有同一熱環境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure an upstream vertical temperature profile and lateral differences after mixing. Check total flow and heat residuals. If one outlet sensor matches the calculation while lateral differences remain large, the entire receiving reach cannot be described by that single temperature. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定總出流，求得另一目標溫度所需冷暖流量比例，再列出若冷水層厚度不足時模型失效的證據，以及需補充的剖面量測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold total release constant and solve the warm-to-cold flow ratio for another target temperature. List observations showing that insufficient cold-layer thickness invalidates the assumption and specify additional profile measurements.","failure":"注意干擾：水躍或分層流可能使冷水沿底部延伸，表面測值會掩蓋底層熱衝擊；感測器反應慢也可能削弱短時變化，應將空間不均與儀器滯後分別辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stratified release can carry cold water along the bed while surface readings hide the thermal change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在取水口上游布設垂向溫度剖面，並量測混合後斷面的橫向差異。以總流量與熱量殘差檢查混合是否完成；若出口單點溫度符合算值而橫向差異仍大，不能宣稱整個河段具有同一熱環境。","textEn":"Measure an upstream vertical temperature profile and lateral differences after mixing. Check total flow and heat residuals. If one outlet sensor matches the calculation while lateral differences remain large, the entire receiving reach cannot be described by that single temperature.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定總出流，求得另一目標溫度所需冷暖流量比例，再列出若冷水層厚度不足時模型失效的證據，以及需補充的剖面量測。","textEn":"Hold total release constant and solve the warm-to-cold flow ratio for another target temperature. List observations showing that insufficient cold-layer thickness invalidates the assumption and specify additional profile measurements.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分層取水混溫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing\"?","options":["在取水口上游布設垂向溫度剖面，並量測混合後斷面的橫向差異。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水"],"optionsEn":["Measure an upstream vertical temperature profile and lateral differences after mixing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在取水口上游布設垂向溫度剖面，並量測混合後斷面的橫向差異。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure an upstream vertical temperature profile and lateral differences after mixing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":33},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-16","title":"分層取水混溫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分層取水混溫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Layered withdrawal temperature mixing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水躍或分層流可能使冷水沿底部延伸，表面測值會掩蓋底層熱衝擊；感測器反應慢也可能削弱短時變化，應將空間不均與儀器滯後分別辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stratified release can carry cold water along the bed while surface readings hide the thermal change. Slow sensor response can also suppress short events, so spatial nonuniformity and instrument lag require separate diagnosis. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：熱量帳應明示共同參考溫度；在相同比熱近似下參考值會相消，但水流的實際來源與交換路徑不能省略。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The heat account needs a common reference temperature; it cancels under equal heat capacities, while stream origins and exchange paths still require explicit identification.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水躍或分層流可能使冷水沿底部延伸，表面測值會掩蓋底層熱衝擊；感測器反應慢也可能削弱短時變化，應將空間不均與儀器滯後分別辨識。","textEn":"Stratified release can carry cold water along the bed while surface readings hide the thermal change. Slow sensor response can also suppress short events, so spatial nonuniformity and instrument lag require separate diagnosis.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層取水混溫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Layered withdrawal temperature mixing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","水躍或分層流可能使冷水沿底部延伸，表面測值會掩蓋底層熱衝擊；感測器反應慢也可能削弱短時變化，應將空間不均與儀器滯後分別辨識。","通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Stratified release can carry cold water along the bed while surface readings hide the thermal change.","Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水躍或分層流可能使冷水沿底部延伸，表面測值會掩蓋底層熱衝擊；感測器反應慢也可能削弱短時變化，應將空間不均與儀器滯後分別辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stratified release can carry cold water along the bed while surface readings hide the thermal change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":34}],"order":8},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「船閘用水時序」與「升船機平衡偏差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lockage water timing\" and \"Ship lift balance imbalance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-17","title":"船閘用水時序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lockage water timing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「船閘用水時序」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lockage water timing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船閘升降依靠閘室水位變化，船隻排水量在同船進出且水位轉換完整時不應重複計入。教材先用閘室平面積乘水位差建立一個升降階段的幾何水量，再把循環次數放到時段帳中；多級閘室之間的共享水及回收系統必須另建連接關係。 每個閘室都應有控制體，級間移轉在整體帳內會互相抵消，只有跨越外部邊界的水量才形成淨耗用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船閘用水時序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A lock changes chamber level to move vessels. Vessel displacement must not be counted repeatedly when the same vessel enters and leaves a complete level-change cycle. Chamber area times lift gives one stage geometric volume; the number and timing of cycles then enter the water account. Shared water between stages requires an explicit connection model. Each chamber needs a control volume; interstage transfers cancel in the overall account, and only flow crossing its external boundary contributes to net use. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lockage water timing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「船閘用水時序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lockage water timing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-17-k1","title":"船閘用水時序","titleEn":"Lockage water timing","text":"船閘升降依靠閘室水位變化，船隻排水量在同船進出且水位轉換完整時不應重複計入。教材先用閘室平面積乘水位差建立一個升降階段的幾何水量，再把循環次數放到時段帳中；多級閘室之間的共享水及回收系統必須另建連接關係。","textEn":"A lock changes chamber level to move vessels. Vessel displacement must not be counted repeatedly when the same vessel enters and leaves a complete level-change cycle.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「船閘用水時序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lockage water timing\" is correct?","options":["通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數","大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","船閘升降依靠閘室水位變化，船隻排水量在同船進出且水位轉換完整時不應重複計入。"],"optionsEn":["Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles.","A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","A lock changes chamber level to move vessels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"船閘升降依靠閘室水位變化，船隻排水量在同船進出且水位轉換完整時不應重複計入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A lock changes chamber level to move vessels. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":35},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-18","title":"船閘用水時序：定量估算","titleEn":"Lockage water timing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「船閘用水時序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lockage water timing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day。模型邊界：單獨閘室每次完全換水且無回收；不能乘上所有級數當作實際多級閘耗水。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day. Model boundary: one isolated chamber exchanges a full volume each cycle without recovery; do not multiply by every stage to infer actual multistage consumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用閘室水位曲線識別充水與排水開始時間，核對閥門流量積分與幾何體積，再追蹤水究竟來自上游庫區或鄰室。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify filling and emptying from chamber level traces, compare integrated valve flow with geometric volume, and track whether water comes from the reservoir or a neighboring chamber.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day。模型邊界：單獨閘室每次完全換水且無回收；不能乘上所有級數當作實際多級閘耗水。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day. Model boundary: one isolated chamber exchanges a full volume each cycle without recovery; do not multiply by every stage to infer actual multistage consumption.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「船閘用水時序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lockage water timing\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day。","總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同","標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day.","Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects.","A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=4200 m2; dh=18 m; N=12 cycles/day; V=A*dh*N=907200 m3/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":36},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-19","title":"船閘用水時序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lockage water timing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「船閘用水時序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lockage water timing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用閘室水位曲線識別充水與排水開始時間，核對閥門流量積分與幾何體積，再追蹤水究竟來自上游庫區或鄰室。若只記錄通船艘數而未記實際升降循環，共閘通行會使估計耗水失真。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify filling and emptying from chamber level traces, compare integrated valve flow with geometric volume, and track whether water comes from the reservoir or a neighboring chamber. Vessel count alone misstates water use when several vessels share one actual lockage cycle. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計一張十二次升降的時程表，加入兩次共閘與一次漏水事件，分別用艘數法和循環積分法估算水量，指出應由哪個感測器辨識差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create a schedule of twelve cycles with two shared lockages and one leakage event. Compare vessel counting with cycle integration and identify which measurement distinguishes the resulting water-account differences.","failure":"注意干擾：閥門漏水會使停等期間仍有水量移轉，幾何升降帳因而不能閉合；但多艘共閘與級間調水也會造成表面差異，應先辨認流程再指認設備洩漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Valve leakage transfers water during waiting periods and prevents geometric closure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用閘室水位曲線識別充水與排水開始時間，核對閥門流量積分與幾何體積，再追蹤水究竟來自上游庫區或鄰室。若只記錄通船艘數而未記實際升降循環，共閘通行會使估計耗水失真。","textEn":"Identify filling and emptying from chamber level traces, compare integrated valve flow with geometric volume, and track whether water comes from the reservoir or a neighboring chamber. Vessel count alone misstates water use when several vessels share one actual lockage cycle.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計一張十二次升降的時程表，加入兩次共閘與一次漏水事件，分別用艘數法和循環積分法估算水量，指出應由哪個感測器辨識差異。","textEn":"Create a schedule of twelve cycles with two shared lockages and one leakage event. Compare vessel counting with cycle integration and identify which measurement distinguishes the resulting water-account differences.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「船閘用水時序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lockage water timing\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用閘室水位曲線識別充水與排水開始時間，核對閥門流量積分與幾何體積，再追蹤水究竟來自上游庫區或鄰室。","相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Identify filling and emptying from chamber level traces, compare integrated valve flow with geometric volume, and track whether water comes from the reservoir or a neighboring chamber.","Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用閘室水位曲線識別充水與排水開始時間，核對閥門流量積分與幾何體積，再追蹤水究竟來自上游庫區或鄰室。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify filling and emptying from chamber level traces, compare integrated valve flow with geometric volume, and track whether water comes from the reservoir or a neighboring chamber. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":37},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-20","title":"船閘用水時序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lockage water timing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「船閘用水時序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lockage water timing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"閥門漏水會使停等期間仍有水量移轉，幾何升降帳因而不能閉合；但多艘共閘與級間調水也會造成表面差異，應先辨認流程再指認設備洩漏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Valve leakage transfers water during waiting periods and prevents geometric closure. Shared lockages and interstage transfers can produce similar apparent differences, so the operating sequence must be reconstructed before diagnosing equipment leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：每個閘室都應有控制體，級間移轉在整體帳內會互相抵消，只有跨越外部邊界的水量才形成淨耗用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Each chamber needs a control volume; interstage transfers cancel in the overall account, and only flow crossing its external boundary contributes to net use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"閥門漏水會使停等期間仍有水量移轉，幾何升降帳因而不能閉合；但多艘共閘與級間調水也會造成表面差異，應先辨認流程再指認設備洩漏。","textEn":"Valve leakage transfers water during waiting periods and prevents geometric closure. Shared lockages and interstage transfers can produce similar apparent differences, so the operating sequence must be reconstructed before diagnosing equipment leakage.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「船閘用水時序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lockage water timing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","閥門漏水會使停等期間仍有水量移轉，幾何升降帳因而不能閉合；但多艘共閘與級間調水也會造成表面差異，應先辨認流程再指認設備洩漏。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","Valve leakage transfers water during waiting periods and prevents geometric closure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閥門漏水會使停等期間仍有水量移轉，幾何升降帳因而不能閉合；但多艘共閘與級間調水也會造成表面差異，應先辨認流程再指認設備洩漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Valve leakage transfers water during waiting periods and prevents geometric closure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":38},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-21","title":"升船機平衡偏差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ship lift balance imbalance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「升船機平衡偏差」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ship lift balance imbalance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。浮船進槽時通常排出相應水量，若槽內水位維持不變，載船前後總重近似不變。教材把殘餘不平衡質量與摩擦分開，藉此辨認驅動功率、制動及結構載重是不同問題。 船仍漂浮時排水質量與船重相等，若船體接觸槽底則浮力條件改變，不能再使用原先重量替代關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「升船機平衡偏差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone. A floating vessel displaces approximately its own weight of water when the trough level is maintained. Separate residual imbalance from friction to distinguish driving power, braking requirements and structural load, which are different engineering questions. Displaced water mass equals vessel mass while the vessel floats; grounding changes that buoyancy condition and invalidates the original weight-substitution relationship for the trough. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ship lift balance imbalance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「升船機平衡偏差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ship lift balance imbalance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-21-k1","title":"升船機平衡偏差","titleEn":"Ship lift balance imbalance","text":"水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。浮船進槽時通常排出相應水量，若槽內水位維持不變，載船前後總重近似不變。","textEn":"A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone. A floating vessel displaces approximately its own weight of water when the trough level is maintained.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「升船機平衡偏差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ship lift balance imbalance\" is correct?","options":["水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。","大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭"],"optionsEn":["A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone.","A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":39},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-22","title":"升船機平衡偏差：定量估算","titleEn":"Ship lift balance imbalance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「升船機平衡偏差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ship lift balance imbalance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。模型邊界：僅算固定速度下不平衡重力功率，不含摩擦加速及制動冗餘。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W. Model boundary: gravitational imbalance power at constant speed only; excludes friction, acceleration and braking redundancy. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以槽水位、排出水量和稱重記錄核對浮力替代關係，再比較空槽與載船的同速電流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare trough level, displaced water and weighing records, then compare empty and occupied trough current at equal speed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。模型邊界：僅算固定速度下不平衡重力功率，不含摩擦加速及制動冗餘。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W. Model boundary: gravitational imbalance power at constant speed only; excludes friction, acceleration and braking redundancy.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「升船機平衡偏差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ship lift balance imbalance\", which statement holds?","options":["水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。","每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水"],"optionsEn":["A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.","Original hypothetical example.","Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":40},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-23","title":"升船機平衡偏差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ship lift balance imbalance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「升船機平衡偏差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ship lift balance imbalance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以槽水位、排出水量和稱重記錄核對浮力替代關係，再比較空槽與載船的同速電流。若差值隨運動方向改變，應檢查摩擦與導向偏載；若與水位偏差一致，才支持殘餘重量解釋。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare trough level, displaced water and weighing records, then compare empty and occupied trough current at equal speed. Direction-dependent differences suggest friction or guide loading, whereas a consistent relation with level error supports an imbalance-weight explanation for the extra demand. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把水位誤差換算成新增水重，與給定不平衡質量比較，再列出加速度與導向摩擦所需額外資料，繪製完整功率帳而不把缺項設成零。","observationEn":"Site practice: Convert a level error into added water mass and compare it with the stated imbalance. List additional data needed for acceleration and guide friction, and build a complete power account without silently setting missing terms to zero.","failure":"注意干擾：水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以槽水位、排出水量和稱重記錄核對浮力替代關係，再比較空槽與載船的同速電流。若差值隨運動方向改變，應檢查摩擦與導向偏載；若與水位偏差一致，才支持殘餘重量解釋。","textEn":"Compare trough level, displaced water and weighing records, then compare empty and occupied trough current at equal speed. Direction-dependent differences suggest friction or guide loading, whereas a consistent relation with level error supports an imbalance-weight explanation for the extra demand.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把水位誤差換算成新增水重，與給定不平衡質量比較，再列出加速度與導向摩擦所需額外資料，繪製完整功率帳而不把缺項設成零。","textEn":"Convert a level error into added water mass and compare it with the stated imbalance. List additional data needed for acceleration and guide friction, and build a complete power account without silently setting missing terms to zero.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「升船機平衡偏差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ship lift balance imbalance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算","以槽水位、排出水量和稱重記錄核對浮力替代關係，再比較空槽與載船的同速電流。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.","Compare trough level, displaced water and weighing records, then compare empty and occupied trough current at equal speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以槽水位、排出水量和稱重記錄核對浮力替代關係，再比較空槽與載船的同速電流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare trough level, displaced water and weighing records, then compare empty and occupied trough current at equal speed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":41},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-24","title":"升船機平衡偏差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ship lift balance imbalance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「升船機平衡偏差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ship lift balance imbalance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption. A binding guide also raises current without the same static weight change, allowing weighing and direction tests to distinguish the two mechanisms. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：船仍漂浮時排水質量與船重相等，若船體接觸槽底則浮力條件改變，不能再使用原先重量替代關係。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Displaced water mass equals vessel mass while the vessel floats; grounding changes that buoyancy condition and invalidates the original weight-substitution relationship for the trough.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。","textEn":"Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption. A binding guide also raises current without the same static weight change, allowing weighing and direction tests to distinguish the two mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「升船機平衡偏差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ship lift balance imbalance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭"],"optionsEn":["Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":42}],"order":9},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「淨水頭功率帳」與「電力爬坡能量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Net head power account\" and \"Electrical ramp energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-25","title":"淨水頭功率帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Net head power account: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「淨水頭功率帳」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Net head power account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"發電水頭是能量高程差扣除引水系統損失，不是壩高或水庫高程的同義詞。尾水抬升與攔污柵阻塞都會降低淨水頭，卻有不同的量測位置及維修責任。把水力功率、軸功率與電功率依效率串接，才能避免在不同儀表邊界間重複扣損。 速度水頭必須和壓力水頭使用相容斷面，若兩端斷面差異很大，僅以靜水位差代替能量差會有偏差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淨水頭功率帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Generating head is the energy-level difference after conveyance losses, not dam height or reservoir elevation. Tailwater rise and trash-rack blockage both reduce net head but have different measurement locations and maintenance implications. Distinguish hydraulic, shaft and electrical power when applying efficiencies so that losses are not deducted twice across instrument boundaries. Velocity and pressure heads require compatible sections; markedly different inlet and outlet sections make a simple static-level difference an incomplete estimate of energy difference. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Net head power account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淨水頭功率帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Net head power account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-25-k1","title":"淨水頭功率帳","titleEn":"Net head power account","text":"發電水頭是能量高程差扣除引水系統損失，不是壩高或水庫高程的同義詞。尾水抬升與攔污柵阻塞都會降低淨水頭，卻有不同的量測位置及維修責任。","textEn":"Generating head is the energy-level difference after conveyance losses, not dam height or reservoir elevation. Tailwater rise and trash-rack blockage both reduce net head but have different measurement locations and maintenance implications.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淨水頭功率帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Net head power account\" is correct?","options":["壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭","發電水頭是能量高程差扣除引水系統損失，不是壩高或水庫高程的同義詞。","總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同"],"optionsEn":["Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head.","Generating head is the energy-level difference after conveyance losses, not dam height or reservoir elevation.","Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"發電水頭是能量高程差扣除引水系統損失，不是壩高或水庫高程的同義詞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Generating head is the energy-level difference after conveyance losses, not dam height or reservoir elevation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":43},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-26","title":"淨水頭功率帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Net head power account: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淨水頭功率帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Net head power account” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW。模型邊界：穩態不可壓縮流，效率為水力輸入至電端總效率；未計暫態及可用率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW. Model boundary: steady incompressible flow with overall hydraulic-to-electrical efficiency; transients and availability are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步讀取進出口能量高程、流量與電端功率，以同一時段計算效率，並核對壓力計高程補償。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize inlet and outlet energy levels, discharge and terminal power, including pressure-tap elevation corrections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW。模型邊界：穩態不可壓縮流，效率為水力輸入至電端總效率；未計暫態及可用率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW. Model boundary: steady incompressible flow with overall hydraulic-to-electrical efficiency; transients and availability are excluded.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「淨水頭功率帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Net head power account\", which statement holds?","options":["標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分","相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW。"],"optionsEn":["A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score.","Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.","Original hypothetical example."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Q=650 m3/s; Hg=92 m; hL=4 m; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; eta=0.91 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(Hg-hL)*eta/1e6=510.63012 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":44},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-27","title":"淨水頭功率帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Net head power account: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淨水頭功率帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Net head power account” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步讀取進出口能量高程、流量與電端功率，以同一時段計算效率，並核對壓力計高程補償。若損失隨流量平方增加而機組效率曲線正常，先查引水阻力，不把全部差值歸因於轉輪劣化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize inlet and outlet energy levels, discharge and terminal power, including pressure-tap elevation corrections. If loss grows approximately with flow squared while the turbine efficiency trend remains normal, investigate conveyance resistance before assigning the entire discrepancy to runner deterioration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別增加尾水高程及柵損失，保持其他輸入不變重算功率，再畫出兩個情境所需量測位置，說明相同功率下降為何需要不同處理。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase tailwater level and rack loss in separate scenarios while holding other inputs constant. Recalculate power and locate the measurements needed to explain why equal power reductions require different responses.","failure":"注意干擾：尾水資料延遲會造成虛假的效率升降，尤其在快速增載後；堵塞柵前後的壓差才是局部損失證據，不能僅由電力降低推定必須更換機組。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delayed tailwater data create artificial efficiency changes after load increases. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步讀取進出口能量高程、流量與電端功率，以同一時段計算效率，並核對壓力計高程補償。若損失隨流量平方增加而機組效率曲線正常，先查引水阻力，不把全部差值歸因於轉輪劣化。","textEn":"Synchronize inlet and outlet energy levels, discharge and terminal power, including pressure-tap elevation corrections. If loss grows approximately with flow squared while the turbine efficiency trend remains normal, investigate conveyance resistance before assigning the entire discrepancy to runner deterioration.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別增加尾水高程及柵損失，保持其他輸入不變重算功率，再畫出兩個情境所需量測位置，說明相同功率下降為何需要不同處理。","textEn":"Increase tailwater level and rack loss in separate scenarios while holding other inputs constant. Recalculate power and locate the measurements needed to explain why equal power reductions require different responses.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「淨水頭功率帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Net head power account\"?","options":["同步讀取進出口能量高程、流量與電端功率，以同一時段計算效率，並核對壓力計高程補償。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize inlet and outlet energy levels, discharge and terminal power, including pressure-tap elevation corrections.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步讀取進出口能量高程、流量與電端功率，以同一時段計算效率，並核對壓力計高程補償。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize inlet and outlet energy levels, discharge and terminal power, including pressure-tap elevation corrections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":45},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-28","title":"淨水頭功率帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Net head power account: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淨水頭功率帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Net head power account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尾水資料延遲會造成虛假的效率升降，尤其在快速增載後；堵塞柵前後的壓差才是局部損失證據，不能僅由電力降低推定必須更換機組。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delayed tailwater data create artificial efficiency changes after load increases. Differential pressure across a blocked rack is evidence of local loss; reduced electrical output alone does not establish that the generating unit needs replacement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度水頭必須和壓力水頭使用相容斷面，若兩端斷面差異很大，僅以靜水位差代替能量差會有偏差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Velocity and pressure heads require compatible sections; markedly different inlet and outlet sections make a simple static-level difference an incomplete estimate of energy difference.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尾水資料延遲會造成虛假的效率升降，尤其在快速增載後；堵塞柵前後的壓差才是局部損失證據，不能僅由電力降低推定必須更換機組。","textEn":"Delayed tailwater data create artificial efficiency changes after load increases. Differential pressure across a blocked rack is evidence of local loss; reduced electrical output alone does not establish that the generating unit needs replacement.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「淨水頭功率帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Net head power account\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","尾水資料延遲會造成虛假的效率升降，尤其在快速增載後；堵塞柵前後的壓差才是局部損失證據，不能僅由電力降低推定必須更換機組。","總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Delayed tailwater data create artificial efficiency changes after load increases.","Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾水資料延遲會造成虛假的效率升降，尤其在快速增載後；堵塞柵前後的壓差才是局部損失證據，不能僅由電力降低推定必須更換機組。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delayed tailwater data create artificial efficiency changes after load increases. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":46},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-29","title":"電力爬坡能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Electrical ramp energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「電力爬坡能量」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Electrical ramp energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電網要求的功率爬坡會沿水力傳動鏈改變流量及壓力，但功率斜率與累計能量是不同維度。先以功率時間曲線求能量，再檢查水量及暫態約束是否容許該曲線；額外能量只是相對基線的面積，不能將爬坡末值乘全時段而忽略初值。 功率曲線下面積的單位是能量，曲線斜率則是功率每時間，將兩者分開才能對照不同調度合約要求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電力爬坡能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A grid power ramp changes flow and pressure through the hydraulic chain, but ramp rate and accumulated energy have different dimensions. Integrate the power-time curve first, then check water and transient constraints. Additional energy is the area above a baseline, not the final power multiplied by the whole ramp duration. Area under a power curve is energy, whereas its slope is power per time; separating them permits comparison with different dispatch requirements and limits. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Electrical ramp energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電力爬坡能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Electrical ramp energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-29-k1","title":"電力爬坡能量","titleEn":"Electrical ramp energy","text":"電網要求的功率爬坡會沿水力傳動鏈改變流量及壓力，但功率斜率與累計能量是不同維度。先以功率時間曲線求能量，再檢查水量及暫態約束是否容許該曲線；額外能量只是相對基線的面積，不能將爬坡末值乘全時段而忽略初值。","textEn":"A grid power ramp changes flow and pressure through the hydraulic chain, but ramp rate and accumulated energy have different dimensions. Integrate the power-time curve first, then check water and transient constraints.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電力爬坡能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Electrical ramp energy\" is correct?","options":["總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同","水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平","電網要求的功率爬坡會沿水力傳動鏈改變流量及壓力，但功率斜率與累計能量是不同維度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects.","A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.","A grid power ramp changes flow and pressure through the hydraulic chain, but ramp rate and accumulated energy have different dimensions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電網要求的功率爬坡會沿水力傳動鏈改變流量及壓力，但功率斜率與累計能量是不同維度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A grid power ramp changes flow and pressure through the hydraulic chain, but ramp rate and accumulated energy have different dimensions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":47},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-30","title":"電力爬坡能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Electrical ramp energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電力爬坡能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Electrical ramp energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh。模型邊界：假設電端功率線性爬坡，不表示水力暫態或電網限制已獲滿足。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh. Model boundary: linear electrical power ramp only; hydraulic transient and grid constraints are not thereby satisfied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以秒級電功率積分核對時段電表，再將調度命令、導葉位置與壓力峰值按時間對齊。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate second-scale terminal power and compare the interval meter, then align dispatch commands, guide-vane position and pressure peaks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh。模型邊界：假設電端功率線性爬坡，不表示水力暫態或電網限制已獲滿足。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh. Model boundary: linear electrical power ramp only; hydraulic transient and grid constraints are not thereby satisfied.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電力爬坡能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Electrical ramp energy\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh。","每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水","沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh.","Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow.","Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P0=400 MW; P1=700 MW; dt=0.25 h; E=(P0+P1)/2*dt=137.5 MWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":48},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-31","title":"電力爬坡能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Electrical ramp energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電力爬坡能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Electrical ramp energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以秒級電功率積分核對時段電表，再將調度命令、導葉位置與壓力峰值按時間對齊。若總電量正確但壓力有尖峰，問題屬爬坡形狀而非能量帳；應保留原始波形，不只保存十五分鐘平均值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate second-scale terminal power and compare the interval meter, then align dispatch commands, guide-vane position and pressure peaks. Correct total energy with a pressure spike indicates a ramp-shape problem, so retain raw waveforms instead of only fifteen-minute averages for the diagnosis. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較線性爬坡與先快後慢的兩段曲線，使兩者總電量相同，再指出哪幾個水力與電氣量必須高頻記錄才能判斷各自限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare a linear ramp with a two-stage fast-then-slow ramp having equal energy. Identify the hydraulic and electrical variables requiring rapid recording to determine the different constraints on each trajectory.","failure":"注意干擾：只核對時段電量會漏掉短時壓力超越或機組振動，因正負功率偏差可能互相抵消；若時間戳錯位，也會把先前的壓力事件錯配到後續命令。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking interval energy alone can miss brief pressure or vibration excursions because positive and negative power errors cancel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以秒級電功率積分核對時段電表，再將調度命令、導葉位置與壓力峰值按時間對齊。若總電量正確但壓力有尖峰，問題屬爬坡形狀而非能量帳；應保留原始波形，不只保存十五分鐘平均值。","textEn":"Integrate second-scale terminal power and compare the interval meter, then align dispatch commands, guide-vane position and pressure peaks. Correct total energy with a pressure spike indicates a ramp-shape problem, so retain raw waveforms instead of only fifteen-minute averages for the diagnosis.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較線性爬坡與先快後慢的兩段曲線，使兩者總電量相同，再指出哪幾個水力與電氣量必須高頻記錄才能判斷各自限制。","textEn":"Compare a linear ramp with a two-stage fast-then-slow ramp having equal energy. Identify the hydraulic and electrical variables requiring rapid recording to determine the different constraints on each trajectory.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電力爬坡能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Electrical ramp energy\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以秒級電功率積分核對時段電表，再將調度命令、導葉位置與壓力峰值按時間對齊。","通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Integrate second-scale terminal power and compare the interval meter, then align dispatch commands, guide-vane position and pressure peaks.","Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以秒級電功率積分核對時段電表，再將調度命令、導葉位置與壓力峰值按時間對齊。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate second-scale terminal power and compare the interval meter, then align dispatch commands, guide-vane position and pressure peaks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":49},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-32","title":"電力爬坡能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Electrical ramp energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電力爬坡能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Electrical ramp energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只核對時段電量會漏掉短時壓力超越或機組振動，因正負功率偏差可能互相抵消；若時間戳錯位，也會把先前的壓力事件錯配到後續命令。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking interval energy alone can miss brief pressure or vibration excursions because positive and negative power errors cancel. Timestamp misalignment can additionally attach an earlier pressure event to a later dispatch command. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：功率曲線下面積的單位是能量，曲線斜率則是功率每時間，將兩者分開才能對照不同調度合約要求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Area under a power curve is energy, whereas its slope is power per time; separating them permits comparison with different dispatch requirements and limits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總電量相同就代表爬坡影響相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal total energy means that ramp trajectories have equivalent effects.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只核對時段電量會漏掉短時壓力超越或機組振動，因正負功率偏差可能互相抵消；若時間戳錯位，也會把先前的壓力事件錯配到後續命令。","textEn":"Checking interval energy alone can miss brief pressure or vibration excursions because positive and negative power errors cancel. Timestamp misalignment can additionally attach an earlier pressure event to a later dispatch command.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電力爬坡能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Electrical ramp energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平","只核對時段電量會漏掉短時壓力超越或機組振動，因正負功率偏差可能互相抵消；若時間戳錯位，也會把先前的壓力事件錯配到後續命令。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.","Checking interval energy alone can miss brief pressure or vibration excursions because positive and negative power errors cancel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只核對時段電量會漏掉短時壓力超越或機組振動，因正負功率偏差可能互相抵消；若時間戳錯位，也會把先前的壓力事件錯配到後續命令。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking interval energy alone can miss brief pressure or vibration excursions because positive and negative power errors cancel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":50}],"order":10},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「長庫區回水高差」與「多感測殘差判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Long reservoir backwater difference\" and \"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-33","title":"長庫區回水高差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Long reservoir backwater difference: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「長庫區回水高差」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long reservoir backwater difference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有持續流量通過的長庫區並非處處靜水面，水面坡度同時受斷面、摩阻與下游控制影響。教材先以已量測平均坡度換算兩站高差，建立空間尺度感；真正回水分析仍需能量方程及各斷面資料，不能用一條坡線外推所有支流。 水面坡度與能量坡度並不總相等，流速水頭沿程改變時需要補入能量方程，尤其在斷面突變附近。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「長庫區回水高差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long reservoir carrying flow does not have a level surface everywhere. Section geometry, friction and downstream control jointly influence the water-surface slope. A measured mean slope can estimate the difference between two stations, but actual backwater analysis requires energy equations and cross sections rather than one line extrapolated through every tributary. Water-surface slope and energy slope are not always equal; changing velocity head requires an energy correction, particularly near abrupt changes in cross-sectional geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long reservoir backwater difference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「長庫區回水高差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Long reservoir backwater difference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-33-k1","title":"長庫區回水高差","titleEn":"Long reservoir backwater difference","text":"有持續流量通過的長庫區並非處處靜水面，水面坡度同時受斷面、摩阻與下游控制影響。教材先以已量測平均坡度換算兩站高差，建立空間尺度感；真正回水分析仍需能量方程及各斷面資料，不能用一條坡線外推所有支流。","textEn":"A long reservoir carrying flow does not have a level surface everywhere. Section geometry, friction and downstream control jointly influence the water-surface slope.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A reservoir surface is level at every discharge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長庫區回水高差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long reservoir backwater difference\" is correct?","options":["有持續流量通過的長庫區並非處處靜水面，水面坡度同時受斷面、摩阻與下游控制影響。","水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平","標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分"],"optionsEn":["A long reservoir carrying flow does not have a level surface everywhere.","A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.","A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有持續流量通過的長庫區並非處處靜水面，水面坡度同時受斷面、摩阻與下游控制影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long reservoir carrying flow does not have a level surface everywhere. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":51},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-34","title":"長庫區回水高差：定量估算","titleEn":"Long reservoir backwater difference: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長庫區回水高差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long reservoir backwater difference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m。模型邊界：坡度為無因次且只代表該時段兩站平均水面坡度；不是摩阻坡度定律。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m. Model boundary: dimensionless slope represents the observed mean water-surface gradient between two stations in one interval, not a friction-slope law. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先統一兩站水準基準並校正訊號時間，再比較低流量與洪水時的高差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Unify gauge datums and synchronize signals before comparing low-flow and flood differences.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m。模型邊界：坡度為無因次且只代表該時段兩站平均水面坡度；不是摩阻坡度定律。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m. Model boundary: dimensionless slope represents the observed mean water-surface gradient between two stations in one interval, not a friction-slope law.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長庫區回水高差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long reservoir backwater difference\", which statement holds?","options":["相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m。","出口平均溫度就是整段河川溫度"],"optionsEn":["Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m.","The average outlet temperature represents the entire receiving river reach."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Sw=0.000012 (dimensionless); L=80000 m; dh=Sw*L=0.96 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":52},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-35","title":"長庫區回水高差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long reservoir backwater difference: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長庫區回水高差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long reservoir backwater difference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先統一兩站水準基準並校正訊號時間，再比較低流量與洪水時的高差。若高差會隨流量改變而基準點穩定，支持水力回水解釋；若所有流量下都出現固定偏移，應先檢查測站基準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Unify gauge datums and synchronize signals before comparing low-flow and flood differences. A flow-dependent difference with stable benchmarks supports a hydraulic explanation. A fixed offset across all flow conditions instead calls for checking the reference elevations and calibration of the gauges. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一長度下試算兩倍坡度的高差，並畫出支流匯入口前後應設的測站，說明哪些資料可檢查平均坡度假設，哪些需一維或二維模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double the slope over the same length, then locate gauges around a tributary junction. Explain which observations test the mean-slope assumption and which questions require a one- or two-dimensional hydraulic model.","failure":"注意干擾：把上游洪水抬升全歸因於壩前水位，會漏掉沿程壅水及支流匯入作用；反之，基準錯差也可能偽裝成坡度，必須用獨立水準測量拆解。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing all upstream flood rise to the dam-front level overlooks reach backwater and tributary inputs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先統一兩站水準基準並校正訊號時間，再比較低流量與洪水時的高差。若高差會隨流量改變而基準點穩定，支持水力回水解釋；若所有流量下都出現固定偏移，應先檢查測站基準。","textEn":"Unify gauge datums and synchronize signals before comparing low-flow and flood differences. A flow-dependent difference with stable benchmarks supports a hydraulic explanation. A fixed offset across all flow conditions instead calls for checking the reference elevations and calibration of the gauges.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一長度下試算兩倍坡度的高差，並畫出支流匯入口前後應設的測站，說明哪些資料可檢查平均坡度假設，哪些需一維或二維模型。","textEn":"Double the slope over the same length, then locate gauges around a tributary junction. Explain which observations test the mean-slope assumption and which questions require a one- or two-dimensional hydraulic model.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長庫區回水高差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long reservoir backwater difference\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重","先統一兩站水準基準並校正訊號時間，再比較低流量與洪水時的高差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.","Unify gauge datums and synchronize signals before comparing low-flow and flood differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先統一兩站水準基準並校正訊號時間，再比較低流量與洪水時的高差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Unify gauge datums and synchronize signals before comparing low-flow and flood differences. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":53},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-36","title":"長庫區回水高差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long reservoir backwater difference: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長庫區回水高差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long reservoir backwater difference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把上游洪水抬升全歸因於壩前水位，會漏掉沿程壅水及支流匯入作用；反之，基準錯差也可能偽裝成坡度，必須用獨立水準測量拆解。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing all upstream flood rise to the dam-front level overlooks reach backwater and tributary inputs. Conversely, a datum error can imitate a water-surface gradient and requires independent leveling to separate it from hydraulics. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：水面坡度與能量坡度並不總相等，流速水頭沿程改變時需要補入能量方程，尤其在斷面突變附近。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Water-surface slope and energy slope are not always equal; changing velocity head requires an energy correction, particularly near abrupt changes in cross-sectional geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水庫水面在任何流量下皆為水平」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A reservoir surface is level at every discharge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把上游洪水抬升全歸因於壩前水位，會漏掉沿程壅水及支流匯入作用；反之，基準錯差也可能偽裝成坡度，必須用獨立水準測量拆解。","textEn":"Attributing all upstream flood rise to the dam-front level overlooks reach backwater and tributary inputs. Conversely, a datum error can imitate a water-surface gradient and requires independent leveling to separate it from hydraulics.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長庫區回水高差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long reservoir backwater difference\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把上游洪水抬升全歸因於壩前水位，會漏掉沿程壅水及支流匯入作用；反之，基準錯差也可能偽裝成坡度，必須用獨立水準測量拆解。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all upstream flood rise to the dam-front level overlooks reach backwater and tributary inputs.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把上游洪水抬升全歸因於壩前水位，會漏掉沿程壅水及支流匯入作用；反之，基準錯差也可能偽裝成坡度，必須用獨立水準測量拆解。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing all upstream flood rise to the dam-front level overlooks reach backwater and tributary inputs. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":54},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-37","title":"多感測殘差判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「多感測殘差判讀」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"監測值可先扣除已校準的水位與季節效應，留下用來追查異常的殘差。標準化殘差有助比較不同單位的量測，但前提是基線期間與變異估計有效；相鄰感測器常受共同環境影響，不能把相關訊號誤當成多份獨立證據。 標準差估計須對應同一殘差定義，原始位移的季節變幅不能直接充當去季節後模型誤差的標準差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「多感測殘差判讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A monitoring model can remove calibrated reservoir-level and seasonal effects to expose residuals for investigation. Standardization helps compare variables with different units only when the baseline period and variance estimate are valid. Nearby instruments often share environmental effects, so correlated signals must not be counted as several independent confirmations. The standard deviation must match the residual definition; seasonal variation in raw displacement cannot directly represent uncertainty after those seasonal effects have been removed. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3.","failure":"常見誤解：「標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「多感測殘差判讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-37-k1","title":"多感測殘差判讀","titleEn":"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis","text":"監測值可先扣除已校準的水位與季節效應，留下用來追查異常的殘差。標準化殘差有助比較不同單位的量測，但前提是基線期間與變異估計有效；相鄰感測器常受共同環境影響，不能把相關訊號誤當成多份獨立證據。","textEn":"A monitoring model can remove calibrated reservoir-level and seasonal effects to expose residuals for investigation. Standardization helps compare variables with different units only when the baseline period and variance estimate are valid.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多感測殘差判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis\" is correct?","options":["標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分","監測值可先扣除已校準的水位與季節效應，留下用來追查異常的殘差。","每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水"],"optionsEn":["A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score.","A monitoring model can remove calibrated reservoir-level and seasonal effects to expose residuals for investigation.","Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"監測值可先扣除已校準的水位與季節效應，留下用來追查異常的殘差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A monitoring model can remove calibrated reservoir-level and seasonal effects to expose residuals for investigation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":55},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-38","title":"多感測殘差判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「多感測殘差判讀」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3。模型邊界：正常基線的標準差固定；數值僅示範殘差，並非本壩警報或安全判準。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3. Model boundary: fixed standard deviation from an assumed baseline; the result illustrates a residual, not a project alarm or safety criterion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時檢查溫度、庫水位、量測基準及維修紀錄，將殘差與附近不同原理儀器比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review temperature, reservoir level, reference control and maintenance records together, then compare residuals with nearby instruments using different physical principles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3。模型邊界：正常基線的標準差固定；數值僅示範殘差，並非本壩警報或安全判準。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3. Model boundary: fixed standard deviation from an assumed baseline; the result illustrates a residual, not a project alarm or safety criterion.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多感測殘差判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis\", which statement holds?","options":["沉積體積可以直接用顆粒密度換算","通船艘數就是獨立升降循環數","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3。"],"optionsEn":["Deposited volume can be calculated directly using particle density.","Vessel count is the same as the number of independent lockage cycles.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: y=7.2 mm; yhat=5.4 mm; sigma=0.6 mm; z=(y-yhat)/sigma=3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":56},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-39","title":"多感測殘差判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「多感測殘差判讀」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時檢查溫度、庫水位、量測基準及維修紀錄，將殘差與附近不同原理儀器比較。若僅單一通道偏離而獨立測量穩定，先查儀器；若多種原理同時偏離，再追查共同結構或水力原因。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review temperature, reservoir level, reference control and maintenance records together, then compare residuals with nearby instruments using different physical principles. An isolated channel suggests an instrument issue; coherent changes across independent methods justify investigating a shared structural or hydraulic mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立包含季節項的假想量測序列，分別加入感測器跳值與緩慢結構位移，畫出原始值和殘差，提出可區分兩種原因的獨立觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create a hypothetical seasonal series and separately insert a sensor jump and slow structural movement. Plot observations and residuals, then propose an independent measurement that can distinguish the two underlying causes.","failure":"注意干擾：基線若含長期漂移，標準差會被放大而掩蓋新異常；若校準資料只涵蓋低水位，外推至高水位也會產生假殘差，不能直接宣告壩體劣化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A drifting baseline inflates the standard deviation and can conceal new changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時檢查溫度、庫水位、量測基準及維修紀錄，將殘差與附近不同原理儀器比較。若僅單一通道偏離而獨立測量穩定，先查儀器；若多種原理同時偏離，再追查共同結構或水力原因。","textEn":"Review temperature, reservoir level, reference control and maintenance records together, then compare residuals with nearby instruments using different physical principles. An isolated channel suggests an instrument issue; coherent changes across independent methods justify investigating a shared structural or hydraulic mechanism.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立包含季節項的假想量測序列，分別加入感測器跳值與緩慢結構位移，畫出原始值和殘差，提出可區分兩種原因的獨立觀測。","textEn":"Create a hypothetical seasonal series and separately insert a sensor jump and slow structural movement. Plot observations and residuals, then propose an independent measurement that can distinguish the two underlying causes.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多感測殘差判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis\"?","options":["同時檢查溫度、庫水位、量測基準及維修紀錄，將殘差與附近不同原理儀器比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","壩高可直接當作機組淨水頭"],"optionsEn":["Review temperature, reservoir level, reference control and maintenance records together, then compare residuals with nearby instruments using different physical principles.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Dam height can be used directly as turbine net head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時檢查溫度、庫水位、量測基準及維修紀錄，將殘差與附近不同原理儀器比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review temperature, reservoir level, reference control and maintenance records together, then compare residuals with nearby instruments using different physical principles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":57},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-40","title":"多感測殘差判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"],"prerequisiteIds":["three-gorges-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「多感測殘差判讀」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Multiple sensor residual diagnosis” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基線若含長期漂移，標準差會被放大而掩蓋新異常；若校準資料只涵蓋低水位，外推至高水位也會產生假殘差，不能直接宣告壩體劣化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A drifting baseline inflates the standard deviation and can conceal new changes. A model trained only at low reservoir levels can also create false residuals at high levels, which do not alone demonstrate dam deterioration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：標準差估計須對應同一殘差定義，原始位移的季節變幅不能直接充當去季節後模型誤差的標準差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The standard deviation must match the residual definition; seasonal variation in raw displacement cannot directly represent uncertainty after those seasonal effects have been removed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「標準化殘差可直接當通用安全評分」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A standardized residual directly provides a universal safety score.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"three-gorges-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基線若含長期漂移，標準差會被放大而掩蓋新異常；若校準資料只涵蓋低水位，外推至高水位也會產生假殘差，不能直接宣告壩體劣化。","textEn":"A drifting baseline inflates the standard deviation and can conceal new changes. A model trained only at low reservoir levels can also create false residuals at high levels, which do not alone demonstrate dam deterioration.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]},{"id":"three-gorges-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v5-place-c445157198d7","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多感測殘差判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multiple sensor residual diagnosis\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","基線若含長期漂移，標準差會被放大而掩蓋新異常；若校準資料只涵蓋低水位，外推至高水位也會產生假殘差，不能直接宣告壩體劣化。","每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A drifting baseline inflates the standard deviation and can conceal new changes.","Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基線若含長期漂移，標準差會被放大而掩蓋新異常；若校準資料只涵蓋低水位，外推至高水位也會產生假殘差，不能直接宣告壩體劣化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A drifting baseline inflates the standard deviation and can conceal new changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":58}],"order":11}],"stepCount":58,"estimatedMinutes":1270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","enrichmentVersion":15,"learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","v15Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["洪峰預報偏差帳","Flood forecast bias account"],["泥砂質量與淤積","Sediment mass and deposition"],["船閘用水時序","Lockage water timing"],["淨水頭功率帳","Net head power account"],["多感測殘差判讀","Multiple sensor residual diagnosis"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]]},"v15Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為本課原創情境串接，所有數值是假設，不能視為業主設計圖或操作許可。先完成「洪峰預報偏差帳」的守恆與邊界檢核，再比較「分段庫容積分」及「泥砂質量與淤積」的不同控制量。第一組計算為 dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3；第二組為 A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。學員須保留量綱、資料時間與量測位置，討論誤差如何傳到結果，將第三單元的限制寫入同一張決策表。任何未納入的結構、河道或機組耦合都列為下一階段工作，不由單一得數推論全工程安全。","textEn":"This original sequence connects the first three units using assumed inputs; none is an owner drawing or an operating authorization. First establish conservation and boundaries for Flood forecast bias account, then compare the controlling variables in Piecewise storage integration and Sediment mass and deposition. The first calculation is dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3; the second is A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3. Preserve dimensions, observation times, and measurement locations in the working sheet. Explain how input uncertainty changes each conclusion and include the third unit limitations in the same decision table. Structural, river, and machine interactions omitted by a model remain subsequent work; a single numerical answer cannot demonstrate safety of the complete project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"長庫區洪水預報與航運發電耦合","focusEn":"Flood forecasting and navigation generation coupling in a long reservoir"}},{"id":"metro","title":"捷運車輛與控制系統","titleEn":"Metro Vehicles and Control Systems","category":"rail","summary":"連結車體、轉向架、牽引、制動、號誌及維修，學習整套大眾運輸系統的相依關係。","summaryEn":"Connect body, bogie, traction, braking, signalling and maintenance to study mass-transit system dependencies.","scope":"公開原理的分層工程教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務，並非原廠配方、施工圖或操作許可。","scopeEn":"A layered course in public engineering principles. Steps are verifiable learning tasks, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"diagram":{"type":"metro","labels":["車體","轉向架","牽引","車載控制","號誌"],"labelsEn":["Body","Bogie","Traction","Onboard control","Signalling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"metro-s01","order":1,"title":"運輸需求","titleEn":"Transport requirements","steps":[{"id":"metro-s01-01","order":1,"title":"定義運能與班距","titleEn":"Define capacity and headway","objective":"完成「定義運能與班距」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for define capacity and headway.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"每列容量與班距共同影響運能，但月台和疏散也形成限制。","textEn":"Train capacity and headway affect throughput, while platforms and evacuation impose constraints."},{"id":"metro-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用假設值比較兩種概念服務方案。","textEn":"Compare two conceptual services using assumed values."}],"check":"用假設值比較兩種概念服務方案。","checkEn":"Compare two conceptual services using assumed values.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「定義運能與班距」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains define capacity and headway?","options":["每列容量與班距共同影響運能，但月台和疏散也形成限制。","車輛、供電、軌道及號誌需共同設計介面。","可用性取決於故障和修復，不能只看平均故障間隔。"],"optionsEn":["Train capacity and headway affect throughput, while platforms and evacuation impose constraints.","Vehicles, power, track and signalling need coordinated interfaces.","Availability depends on failure and repair, not failure interval alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每列容量與班距共同影響運能，但月台和疏散也形成限制。","explanationEn":"Train capacity and headway affect throughput, while platforms and evacuation impose constraints."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s01-02","order":2,"title":"建立系統分工","titleEn":"Map system responsibilities","objective":"完成「建立系統分工」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map system responsibilities.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"車輛、供電、軌道及號誌需共同設計介面。","textEn":"Vehicles, power, track and signalling need coordinated interfaces."},{"id":"metro-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出四個系統的雙向依賴。","textEn":"Draw dependencies among the four systems."}],"check":"畫出四個系統的雙向依賴。","checkEn":"Draw dependencies among the four systems.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立系統分工」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map system responsibilities?","options":["可用性取決於故障和修復，不能只看平均故障間隔。","每列容量與班距共同影響運能，但月台和疏散也形成限制。","車輛、供電、軌道及號誌需共同設計介面。"],"optionsEn":["Availability depends on failure and repair, not failure interval alone.","Train capacity and headway affect throughput, while platforms and evacuation impose constraints.","Vehicles, power, track and signalling need coordinated interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"車輛、供電、軌道及號誌需共同設計介面。","explanationEn":"Vehicles, power, track and signalling need coordinated interfaces."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s01-03","order":3,"title":"制定可用性需求","titleEn":"Set availability needs","objective":"完成「制定可用性需求」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for set availability needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"可用性取決於故障和修復，不能只看平均故障間隔。","textEn":"Availability depends on failure and repair, not failure interval alone."},{"id":"metro-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較相同故障率不同修復時間的情境。","textEn":"Compare equal failure rates with different repair times."}],"check":"比較相同故障率不同修復時間的情境。","checkEn":"Compare equal failure rates with different repair times.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「制定可用性需求」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains set availability needs?","options":["車輛、供電、軌道及號誌需共同設計介面。","可用性取決於故障和修復，不能只看平均故障間隔。","每列容量與班距共同影響運能，但月台和疏散也形成限制。"],"optionsEn":["Vehicles, power, track and signalling need coordinated interfaces.","Availability depends on failure and repair, not failure interval alone.","Train capacity and headway affect throughput, while platforms and evacuation impose constraints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可用性取決於故障和修復，不能只看平均故障間隔。","explanationEn":"Availability depends on failure and repair, not failure interval alone."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"metro-s02","order":2,"title":"車體與轉向架","titleEn":"Body and bogie","steps":[{"id":"metro-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解車體承載","titleEn":"Understand body load paths","objective":"完成「理解車體承載」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand body load paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"乘客、設備和運動載荷經車體與轉向架傳到軌道。","textEn":"Passenger, equipment and dynamic loads pass through body and bogies to track."},{"id":"metro-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在示意圖追蹤垂直載荷路徑。","textEn":"Trace vertical load paths on a schematic."}],"check":"在示意圖追蹤垂直載荷路徑。","checkEn":"Trace vertical load paths on a schematic.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解車體承載」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand body load paths?","options":["一次與二次懸吊處理不同結構間的振動與位移。","接觸幾何與黏著影響導向、牽引及磨耗。","乘客、設備和運動載荷經車體與轉向架傳到軌道。"],"optionsEn":["Primary and secondary suspension manage vibration and motion between different structures.","Contact geometry and adhesion affect guidance, traction and wear.","Passenger, equipment and dynamic loads pass through body and bogies to track."],"answer":2,"explanation":"乘客、設備和運動載荷經車體與轉向架傳到軌道。","explanationEn":"Passenger, equipment and dynamic loads pass through body and bogies to track."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s02-02","order":2,"title":"理解懸吊層級","titleEn":"Understand suspension stages","objective":"完成「理解懸吊層級」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand suspension stages.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"一次與二次懸吊處理不同結構間的振動與位移。","textEn":"Primary and secondary suspension manage vibration and motion between different structures."},{"id":"metro-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"以質量彈簧圖標出各層。","textEn":"Mark stages on a mass-spring diagram."}],"check":"以質量彈簧圖標出各層。","checkEn":"Mark stages on a mass-spring diagram.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解懸吊層級」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand suspension stages?","options":["乘客、設備和運動載荷經車體與轉向架傳到軌道。","一次與二次懸吊處理不同結構間的振動與位移。","接觸幾何與黏著影響導向、牽引及磨耗。"],"optionsEn":["Passenger, equipment and dynamic loads pass through body and bogies to track.","Primary and secondary suspension manage vibration and motion between different structures.","Contact geometry and adhesion affect guidance, traction and wear."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一次與二次懸吊處理不同結構間的振動與位移。","explanationEn":"Primary and secondary suspension manage vibration and motion between different structures."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s02-03","order":3,"title":"辨識輪軌接觸","titleEn":"Identify wheel-rail contact","objective":"完成「辨識輪軌接觸」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify wheel-rail contact.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"接觸幾何與黏著影響導向、牽引及磨耗。","textEn":"Contact geometry and adhesion affect guidance, traction and wear."},{"id":"metro-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出牽引與維護各需的觀察量。","textEn":"List observations for traction and maintenance."}],"check":"列出牽引與維護各需的觀察量。","checkEn":"List observations for traction and maintenance.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識輪軌接觸」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify wheel-rail contact?","options":["接觸幾何與黏著影響導向、牽引及磨耗。","乘客、設備和運動載荷經車體與轉向架傳到軌道。","一次與二次懸吊處理不同結構間的振動與位移。"],"optionsEn":["Contact geometry and adhesion affect guidance, traction and wear.","Passenger, equipment and dynamic loads pass through body and bogies to track.","Primary and secondary suspension manage vibration and motion between different structures."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸幾何與黏著影響導向、牽引及磨耗。","explanationEn":"Contact geometry and adhesion affect guidance, traction and wear."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"metro-s03","order":3,"title":"牽引與制動","titleEn":"Traction and braking","steps":[{"id":"metro-s03-01","order":1,"title":"建立牽引能源圖","titleEn":"Map traction energy","objective":"完成「建立牽引能源圖」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map traction energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"供電、變流器與馬達共同完成能量轉換。","textEn":"Power supply, converter and motor jointly convert energy."},{"id":"metro-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"追蹤電網到輪端的能源路徑。","textEn":"Trace energy from grid to wheels."}],"check":"追蹤電網到輪端的能源路徑。","checkEn":"Trace energy from grid to wheels.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立牽引能源圖」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map traction energy?","options":["輪軌黏著不足會限制可用制動力。","供電、變流器與馬達共同完成能量轉換。","不同制動方式需協同，回生可用性受系統條件限制。"],"optionsEn":["Low wheel-rail adhesion limits available braking force.","Power supply, converter and motor jointly convert energy.","Braking modes coordinate, and regeneration depends on system conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"供電、變流器與馬達共同完成能量轉換。","explanationEn":"Power supply, converter and motor jointly convert energy."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s03-02","order":2,"title":"理解回生與摩擦制動","titleEn":"Understand regenerative and friction braking","objective":"完成「理解回生與摩擦制動」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand regenerative and friction braking.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"不同制動方式需協同，回生可用性受系統條件限制。","textEn":"Braking modes coordinate, and regeneration depends on system conditions."},{"id":"metro-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出能源可回收及不可回收情境。","textEn":"Diagram recoverable and non-recoverable energy cases."}],"check":"畫出能源可回收及不可回收情境。","checkEn":"Diagram recoverable and non-recoverable energy cases.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解回生與摩擦制動」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand regenerative and friction braking?","options":["不同制動方式需協同，回生可用性受系統條件限制。","輪軌黏著不足會限制可用制動力。","供電、變流器與馬達共同完成能量轉換。"],"optionsEn":["Braking modes coordinate, and regeneration depends on system conditions.","Low wheel-rail adhesion limits available braking force.","Power supply, converter and motor jointly convert energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同制動方式需協同，回生可用性受系統條件限制。","explanationEn":"Braking modes coordinate, and regeneration depends on system conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s03-03","order":3,"title":"分析滑行與黏著","titleEn":"Analyze sliding and adhesion","objective":"完成「分析滑行與黏著」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze sliding and adhesion.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"輪軌黏著不足會限制可用制動力。","textEn":"Low wheel-rail adhesion limits available braking force."},{"id":"metro-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用抽象圖比較高低黏著的限制。","textEn":"Compare high- and low-adhesion limits abstractly."}],"check":"用抽象圖比較高低黏著的限制。","checkEn":"Compare high- and low-adhesion limits abstractly.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析滑行與黏著」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze sliding and adhesion?","options":["供電、變流器與馬達共同完成能量轉換。","不同制動方式需協同，回生可用性受系統條件限制。","輪軌黏著不足會限制可用制動力。"],"optionsEn":["Power supply, converter and motor jointly convert energy.","Braking modes coordinate, and regeneration depends on system conditions.","Low wheel-rail adhesion limits available braking force."],"answer":2,"explanation":"輪軌黏著不足會限制可用制動力。","explanationEn":"Low wheel-rail adhesion limits available braking force."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"metro-s04","order":4,"title":"車載設備與人因","titleEn":"Onboard equipment and human factors","steps":[{"id":"metro-s04-01","order":1,"title":"整合車門狀態","titleEn":"Integrate door status","objective":"完成「整合車門狀態」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for integrate door status.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"車門狀態需要可靠感知並與列車控制相互核對。","textEn":"Door state needs reliable sensing and checking against train control."},{"id":"metro-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在虛擬模型定義開、關、未知三種狀態。","textEn":"Define open, closed and unknown states in the virtual model."}],"check":"在虛擬模型定義開、關、未知三種狀態。","checkEn":"Define open, closed and unknown states in the virtual model.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「整合車門狀態」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains integrate door status?","options":["車門狀態需要可靠感知並與列車控制相互核對。","資訊需清楚傳達位置、方向及異常，不只顯示廣告。","空調、照明和控制會消耗牽引以外的能量。"],"optionsEn":["Door state needs reliable sensing and checking against train control.","Information needs to communicate location, direction and abnormal conditions.","HVAC, lighting and control use energy beyond traction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"車門狀態需要可靠感知並與列車控制相互核對。","explanationEn":"Door state needs reliable sensing and checking against train control."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s04-02","order":2,"title":"規劃乘客資訊","titleEn":"Plan passenger information","objective":"完成「規劃乘客資訊」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan passenger information.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"資訊需清楚傳達位置、方向及異常，不只顯示廣告。","textEn":"Information needs to communicate location, direction and abnormal conditions."},{"id":"metro-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"檢查兩種語系的站名與方向一致。","textEn":"Check station names and directions across two languages."}],"check":"檢查兩種語系的站名與方向一致。","checkEn":"Check station names and directions across two languages.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃乘客資訊」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan passenger information?","options":["空調、照明和控制會消耗牽引以外的能量。","車門狀態需要可靠感知並與列車控制相互核對。","資訊需清楚傳達位置、方向及異常，不只顯示廣告。"],"optionsEn":["HVAC, lighting and control use energy beyond traction.","Door state needs reliable sensing and checking against train control.","Information needs to communicate location, direction and abnormal conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"資訊需清楚傳達位置、方向及異常，不只顯示廣告。","explanationEn":"Information needs to communicate location, direction and abnormal conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s04-03","order":3,"title":"建立設備電力需求","titleEn":"Map auxiliary power needs","objective":"完成「建立設備電力需求」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map auxiliary power needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"空調、照明和控制會消耗牽引以外的能量。","textEn":"HVAC, lighting and control use energy beyond traction."},{"id":"metro-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立輔助負載的概念功率表。","textEn":"Create a conceptual auxiliary-power table."}],"check":"建立輔助負載的概念功率表。","checkEn":"Create a conceptual auxiliary-power table.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立設備電力需求」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map auxiliary power needs?","options":["資訊需清楚傳達位置、方向及異常，不只顯示廣告。","空調、照明和控制會消耗牽引以外的能量。","車門狀態需要可靠感知並與列車控制相互核對。"],"optionsEn":["Information needs to communicate location, direction and abnormal conditions.","HVAC, lighting and control use energy beyond traction.","Door state needs reliable sensing and checking against train control."],"answer":1,"explanation":"空調、照明和控制會消耗牽引以外的能量。","explanationEn":"HVAC, lighting and control use energy beyond traction."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"metro-s05","order":5,"title":"號誌與通訊概念","titleEn":"Signalling and communication concepts","steps":[{"id":"metro-s05-01","order":1,"title":"區分定位與授權","titleEn":"Distinguish location and movement authority","objective":"完成「區分定位與授權」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish location and movement authority.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"知道列車位置與允許列車移動是不同功能。","textEn":"Knowing train location and authorizing movement are different functions."},{"id":"metro-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在概念圖分開位置量測與許可訊息。","textEn":"Separate position measurement and authority messages."}],"check":"在概念圖分開位置量測與許可訊息。","checkEn":"Separate position measurement and authority messages.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分定位與授權」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish location and movement authority?","options":["CBTC 以連續通訊及列車定位支援控制，安全需整體驗證。","缺少可靠資訊時，系統需進入預定安全狀態。","知道列車位置與允許列車移動是不同功能。"],"optionsEn":["CBTC uses continuous communication and localization for control, requiring system-wide safety validation.","Loss of reliable information requires a predefined safe state.","Knowing train location and authorizing movement are different functions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"知道列車位置與允許列車移動是不同功能。","explanationEn":"Knowing train location and authorizing movement are different functions."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s05-02","order":2,"title":"理解 CBTC 架構","titleEn":"Understand CBTC architecture","objective":"完成「理解 CBTC 架構」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand cbtc architecture.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"CBTC 以連續通訊及列車定位支援控制，安全需整體驗證。","textEn":"CBTC uses continuous communication and localization for control, requiring system-wide safety validation."},{"id":"metro-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出車載、地面與控制中心功能。","textEn":"Draw onboard, wayside and control-center functions."}],"check":"畫出車載、地面與控制中心功能。","checkEn":"Draw onboard, wayside and control-center functions.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解 CBTC 架構」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand cbtc architecture?","options":["知道列車位置與允許列車移動是不同功能。","CBTC 以連續通訊及列車定位支援控制，安全需整體驗證。","缺少可靠資訊時，系統需進入預定安全狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Knowing train location and authorizing movement are different functions.","CBTC uses continuous communication and localization for control, requiring system-wide safety validation.","Loss of reliable information requires a predefined safe state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"CBTC 以連續通訊及列車定位支援控制，安全需整體驗證。","explanationEn":"CBTC uses continuous communication and localization for control, requiring system-wide safety validation."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s05-03","order":3,"title":"模擬通訊失效狀態","titleEn":"Simulate communication failure states","objective":"完成「模擬通訊失效狀態」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for simulate communication failure states.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"缺少可靠資訊時，系統需進入預定安全狀態。","textEn":"Loss of reliable information requires a predefined safe state."},{"id":"metro-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"只在隔離模擬器中畫出狀態轉移，不接實際號誌。","textEn":"Model transitions only in an isolated simulator, never connected to real signalling."}],"check":"只在隔離模擬器中畫出狀態轉移，不接實際號誌。","checkEn":"Model transitions only in an isolated simulator, never connected to real signalling.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「模擬通訊失效狀態」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains simulate communication failure states?","options":["缺少可靠資訊時，系統需進入預定安全狀態。","知道列車位置與允許列車移動是不同功能。","CBTC 以連續通訊及列車定位支援控制，安全需整體驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Loss of reliable information requires a predefined safe state.","Knowing train location and authorizing movement are different functions.","CBTC uses continuous communication and localization for control, requiring system-wide safety validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺少可靠資訊時，系統需進入預定安全狀態。","explanationEn":"Loss of reliable information requires a predefined safe state."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":15}]},{"id":"metro-s06","order":6,"title":"驗證與營運維護","titleEn":"Verification and operational maintenance","steps":[{"id":"metro-s06-01","order":1,"title":"建立整合測試矩陣","titleEn":"Build integration tests","objective":"完成「建立整合測試矩陣」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build integration tests.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"車門、牽引與號誌的介面需測試正常和異常情境。","textEn":"Door, traction and signalling interfaces need normal and abnormal scenario tests."},{"id":"metro-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立虛擬輸入、預期狀態與結果表。","textEn":"Tabulate virtual inputs, expected states and results."}],"check":"建立虛擬輸入、預期狀態與結果表。","checkEn":"Tabulate virtual inputs, expected states and results.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立整合測試矩陣」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build integration tests?","options":["教育控制模型不能直接用於真實載客系統。","車門、牽引與號誌的介面需測試正常和異常情境。","檢查點位置和模組更換方式影響修復時間。"],"optionsEn":["An educational control model cannot be directly used for real passenger service.","Door, traction and signalling interfaces need normal and abnormal scenario tests.","Inspection access and module replacement affect repair time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"車門、牽引與號誌的介面需測試正常和異常情境。","explanationEn":"Door, traction and signalling interfaces need normal and abnormal scenario tests."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s06-02","order":2,"title":"規劃維修可及性","titleEn":"Plan maintainability","objective":"完成「規劃維修可及性」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan maintainability.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"檢查點位置和模組更換方式影響修復時間。","textEn":"Inspection access and module replacement affect repair time."},{"id":"metro-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較兩個模型布局的維修路徑。","textEn":"Compare service paths in two model layouts."}],"check":"比較兩個模型布局的維修路徑。","checkEn":"Compare service paths in two model layouts.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃維修可及性」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan maintainability?","options":["檢查點位置和模組更換方式影響修復時間。","教育控制模型不能直接用於真實載客系統。","車門、牽引與號誌的介面需測試正常和異常情境。"],"optionsEn":["Inspection access and module replacement affect repair time.","An educational control model cannot be directly used for real passenger service.","Door, traction and signalling interfaces need normal and abnormal scenario tests."],"answer":0,"explanation":"檢查點位置和模組更換方式影響修復時間。","explanationEn":"Inspection access and module replacement affect repair time."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":15},{"id":"metro-s06-03","order":3,"title":"交付運輸系統模型","titleEn":"Deliver the transit-system model","objective":"完成「交付運輸系統模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for deliver the transit-system model.","knowledge":[{"id":"metro-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"教育控制模型不能直接用於真實載客系統。","textEn":"An educational control model cannot be directly used for real passenger service."},{"id":"metro-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"提交系統圖、測試紀錄與適用範圍。","textEn":"Submit diagrams, test records and scope limits."}],"check":"提交系統圖、測試紀錄與適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit diagrams, test records and scope limits.","sourceIds":["alstom-cbtc"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「交付運輸系統模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains deliver the transit-system model?","options":["車門、牽引與號誌的介面需測試正常和異常情境。","檢查點位置和模組更換方式影響修復時間。","教育控制模型不能直接用於真實載客系統。"],"optionsEn":["Door, traction and signalling interfaces need normal and abnormal scenario tests.","Inspection access and module replacement affect repair time.","An educational control model cannot be directly used for real passenger service."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教育控制模型不能直接用於真實載客系統。","explanationEn":"An educational control model cannot be directly used for real passenger service."},"prerequisiteIds":["metro-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":15}]}],"stepCount":18,"estimatedMinutes":270,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course"},{"id":"a004","title":"晶圓研磨與拋光","titleEn":"Wafer lapping and polishing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"從鋸切晶圓的厚度與損傷開始，建立研磨、鏡面拋光、清潔與放行之間的證據鏈。","summaryEn":"Build an evidence chain from thickness and saw damage through lapping, mirror polishing, cleaning and release.","sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["來料","研磨","損傷整備","鏡面拋光","清潔量測"],"labelsEn":["Incoming","Lapping","Damage preparation","Polishing","Clean and measure"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a004-stage01","order":1,"title":"來料與幾何基準","titleEn":"Incoming material and geometry","description":"先辨認材料狀態與量測定義，再規劃可用的去除量。","descriptionEn":"Identify material condition and measurement definitions before allocating removal.","steps":[{"id":"a004-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨認裸矽晶圓與薄膜 CMP 的邊界","titleEn":"Distinguish bare-wafer finishing from film CMP","objective":"界定本批晶圓的材料層與後續用途。","objectiveEn":"Identify the material stack and intended next process.","instruction":"畫出鋸切裸矽與已有金屬圖案晶圓的兩種截面；在各截面標記可移除材料、保留材料及下一站需要的表面。比較兩者為何不能共用同一終點判據。","instructionEn":"Draw cross-sections of sawn bare silicon and a patterned metal wafer. Mark removable and retained material and the surface required next. Compare why the two need different endpoint criteria.","observation":"觀察「厚度達標」與「保留薄膜達標」是否指向不同的量測。","observationEn":"Notice whether target wafer thickness and target remaining film require different measurements.","failure":"若把金屬 CMP 的選擇性直接當成裸矽拋光規格，先退回材料清單重新界定。","failureEn":"If metal-CMP selectivity is treated as a bare-silicon specification, revisit the material inventory.","check":"交出兩張截面並為每張指定一項厚度和一項表面驗證。","checkEn":"Submit both cross-sections with one thickness and one surface check for each.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-01-k1","title":"加工對象","titleEn":"Processing target","text":"裸矽整備處理基板本體；薄膜 CMP 還須保護已形成的材料與圖案。","textEn":"Bare-wafer finishing shapes the substrate; film CMP must also preserve existing layers and patterns."},{"id":"a004-v6-01-k2","title":"終點的意義","titleEn":"Meaning of an endpoint","text":"停止條件取決於下一製程需求，不能只以外觀發亮決定。","textEn":"Stopping depends on the next process, not just a shiny appearance."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩片晶圓同樣發亮，為何仍不能用相同終點放行？","questionEn":"Why can two equally shiny wafers require different release endpoints?","options":["它們需要保留的材料和量測對象不同。","兩種終點都只由晶圓直徑決定。","只需反轉研磨方向，便可共用剩餘材料要求。"],"optionsEn":["They retain different materials and require different measurements.","Both endpoints depend only on wafer diameter.","Reversing polishing direction makes remaining-material requirements interchangeable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"它們需要保留的材料和量測對象不同。 裸矽整備處理基板本體；薄膜 CMP 還須保護已形成的材料與圖案。","explanationEn":"They retain different materials and require different measurements. Bare-wafer finishing shapes the substrate; film CMP must also preserve existing layers and patterns."}},{"id":"a004-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-01"],"title":"建立厚度、彎曲與粗糙度量測圖","titleEn":"Map thickness, bow and roughness","objective":"把不同尺度的表面問題分開記錄。","objectiveEn":"Record surface problems at distinct spatial scales.","instruction":"在自行繪製的九點厚度表填入假設值並註明單位，計算最大與最小差值；另畫整片彎曲輪廓和局部粗糙度截線，避免把三種圖合成單一分數。","instructionEn":"Enter labeled hypothetical values in a nine-point thickness table and compute the maximum-minus-minimum difference. Separately sketch whole-wafer bow and local roughness rather than merging them into one score.","observation":"比較厚度一致但彎曲的晶圓，以及不彎曲但厚度不均的晶圓。","observationEn":"Compare a uniformly thick bowed wafer with a flat-looking wafer of uneven thickness.","failure":"若換夾持方式便改變結果，記錄支撐條件；不要把受力展平當成本體已修正。","failureEn":"If support changes the result, record the fixture condition; forced flattening is not permanent correction.","check":"清楚標明厚度差、整體形狀和局部表面三種證據的量測範圍。","checkEn":"Label the measurement extent of thickness variation, overall shape and local surface texture.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-02-k1","title":"空間尺度","titleEn":"Spatial scale","text":"平行度、整體形狀與局部粗糙度回答不同問題。","textEn":"Parallelism, overall shape and local roughness answer different questions."},{"id":"a004-v6-02-k2","title":"量測基準","titleEn":"Measurement reference","text":"夾持狀態、取樣位置和邊緣排除區須隨結果保存。","textEn":"Support condition, sampling positions and edge exclusion belong with the result."}],"quiz":{"question":"局部粗糙度降低，能否直接證明全片厚度更均勻？","questionEn":"Does lower local roughness prove improved full-wafer thickness uniformity?","options":["能，局部粗糙度就等於全片平行度。","不能，還需要厚度分布量測。","能，固定放大倍率已足以取代厚度取樣。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; local roughness is the same as full-wafer parallelism.","No; a thickness map is still required.","Yes; fixed magnification replaces thickness sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不能，還需要厚度分布量測。 平行度、整體形狀與局部粗糙度回答不同問題。","explanationEn":"No; a thickness map is still required. Parallelism, overall shape and local roughness answer different questions."}},{"id":"a004-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-02"],"title":"分配鋸切後的材料去除預算","titleEn":"Allocate removal after slicing","objective":"在厚度限制內保留後續整備的餘量。","objectiveEn":"Reserve finishing allowance within the thickness constraint.","instruction":"用紙上厚度帳本列出來料、研磨後、損傷去除後與拋光後四個狀態；自行設定教學數值並逐站相減，檢查最後仍留有修整餘量。","instructionEn":"Build a paper thickness ledger for incoming, lapped, damage-removed and polished states. Use explicitly hypothetical values, subtract each allowance and check that finishing margin remains.","observation":"比較平均厚度足夠但局部最薄點已不足的情況。","observationEn":"Compare an acceptable average thickness with an already insufficient local minimum.","failure":"若預算只用平均值，可能忽略最薄區；回到來料地圖調整分配。","failureEn":"An average-only budget can hide a thin region; revise the allocation using the incoming map.","check":"每一站的移除量與最薄位置均可追溯，且沒有負的剩餘餘量。","checkEn":"Trace every removal allocation and the thinnest location, with no negative remaining allowance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-03-k1","title":"去除不可逆","titleEn":"Irreversible removal","text":"後段不能靠拋光補回已移除的矽。","textEn":"Later polishing cannot restore silicon already removed."},{"id":"a004-v6-03-k2","title":"最薄區控制","titleEn":"Minimum-thickness control","text":"放行需考慮局部限制，平均值只能作整體摘要。","textEn":"Local limits matter for release; the average is only a summary."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均厚度尚可，但一區已低於最終要求，應如何判斷？","questionEn":"The average is acceptable but one region is below the final requirement. What follows?","options":["只要中心點達標，其他位置可用平均值代替。","繼續全片均勻去除，直到最薄區回到厚度要求。","不能以平均值掩蓋局部不足，需重新判定可加工性。"],"optionsEn":["If the center passes, other locations may be replaced by the average.","Continue uniform removal until the thinnest region returns to the required thickness.","Reassess processability; the average cannot hide the local shortfall."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不能以平均值掩蓋局部不足，需重新判定可加工性。 後段不能靠拋光補回已移除的矽。","explanationEn":"Reassess processability; the average cannot hide the local shortfall. Later polishing cannot restore silicon already removed."}},{"id":"a004-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-03"],"title":"檢查邊緣完整性與搬運接觸","titleEn":"Inspect edge integrity and handling contact","objective":"辨認可能形成碎屑或後續破片的邊緣狀況。","objectiveEn":"Recognize edge conditions that can generate debris or later fracture.","instruction":"在晶圓圓周示意圖標出缺角、裂紋與正常倒角，另畫載具接觸位置。比較缺陷是否靠近支撐點；只制定影像複查與隔離決策，不實作破壞試驗。","instructionEn":"Mark chips, cracks and normal bevels on an edge diagram, then add carrier contact locations. Compare defects with support points and define image review or quarantine decisions without destructive testing.","observation":"注意「平滑倒角」與不規則缺口的形狀差異，以及缺口附近的散落粒子。","observationEn":"Distinguish a smooth bevel from an irregular chip and look for nearby debris.","failure":"把正常倒角誤判為缺角會造成誤剔除；只看中心表面則可能漏掉裂紋。","failureEn":"Mistaking a bevel for a chip causes false rejects; viewing only the center can miss cracks.","check":"缺陷紀錄包含圓周位置、形貌與處置理由，而非只有合格勾選。","checkEn":"Record edge position, morphology and disposition reasoning rather than a pass check alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-04-k1","title":"邊緣應力","titleEn":"Edge stress","text":"邊緣形貌影響接觸與應力集中，也可能成為粒子來源。","textEn":"Edge geometry influences contact and stress concentration and can become a particle source."},{"id":"a004-v6-04-k2","title":"缺陷定位","titleEn":"Defect localization","text":"同一方位重複出現缺口可提示搬運或載具接觸問題。","textEn":"Repeated chips at the same orientation can suggest a handling or carrier-contact issue."}],"quiz":{"question":"缺口總在同一載具接觸附近出現，優先比較什麼？","questionEn":"Chips repeatedly occur near one carrier contact. What should be compared first?","options":["接觸位置與缺陷方位的關聯。","僅比較中心粗糙度，因為邊緣缺陷一定來自中心。","直接歸因於來料批次，不核對載具方位。"],"optionsEn":["The relationship between contact position and defect orientation.","Compare center roughness only, assuming every edge defect originates at the center.","Attribute it to incoming lots without checking carrier orientation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸位置與缺陷方位的關聯。 邊緣形貌影響接觸與應力集中，也可能成為粒子來源。","explanationEn":"The relationship between contact position and defect orientation. Edge geometry influences contact and stress concentration and can become a particle source."}}]},{"id":"a004-stage02","order":2,"title":"研磨與表面整備","titleEn":"Lapping and surface preparation","description":"比較厚度修正、邊緣完整性與表面損傷，避免把粗加工當鏡面加工。","descriptionEn":"Separate thickness correction, edge integrity and damage removal from mirror finishing.","steps":[{"id":"a004-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-04"],"title":"推演雙面研磨的厚度修正","titleEn":"Model thickness correction during lapping","objective":"理解兩面去除如何改善厚度與平行度。","objectiveEn":"Understand how removal from both faces changes thickness and parallelism.","instruction":"在截面模型將上、下研磨面分別標色，畫出厚端與薄端的去除趨勢。比較均勻去除和偏一側去除兩種假設，不把壓力示意值當作設備設定。","instructionEn":"Color the upper and lower lapping interfaces in a section model. Sketch removal trends at thick and thin regions and compare uniform versus one-sided removal assumptions without turning schematic pressure into machine settings.","observation":"觀察兩面總去除量相同時，偏斜是否仍可能殘留。","observationEn":"Check whether tilt can remain even when total removal from both faces is equal.","failure":"只追求總去除量會漏掉局部平行度；需返回厚度地圖，而非只看加工時間。","failureEn":"Total removal alone misses local parallelism; return to the thickness map rather than processing time.","check":"說明一個厚度改善但平行度未改善的案例。","checkEn":"Explain a case where thickness improves but parallelism does not.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-05-k1","title":"相對去除","titleEn":"Relative removal","text":"厚度與兩面相對形狀由材料去除的空間分布共同決定。","textEn":"Thickness and relative face shape depend on the spatial distribution of removal."},{"id":"a004-v6-05-k2","title":"時間不是品質","titleEn":"Time is not quality","text":"相同時間不保證相同去除分布，工具與接觸狀態也需追蹤。","textEn":"Equal time does not guarantee equal removal distribution; tool and contact condition also matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"研磨時間相同的兩批厚度分布不同，哪種說法較合理？","questionEn":"Two equally timed lots have different thickness maps. Which explanation is reasonable?","options":["相同時間必須對應相同去除，應先排除所有工具因素。","接觸與去除分布可能不同。","只要平均來料厚度相同，局部接觸就必然相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal time requires equal removal, so all tool factors should be excluded.","Contact and removal distributions may differ.","Equal incoming average thickness guarantees identical local contact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸與去除分布可能不同。 厚度與兩面相對形狀由材料去除的空間分布共同決定。","explanationEn":"Contact and removal distributions may differ. Thickness and relative face shape depend on the spatial distribution of removal."}},{"id":"a004-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-05"],"title":"區分機械損傷去除與鏡面外觀","titleEn":"Separate damage removal from mirror appearance","objective":"把次表面損傷列為獨立整備問題。","objectiveEn":"Treat subsurface damage as a separate preparation concern.","instruction":"在鋸切與研磨後的剖面下方加上受損層，再畫去除後剖面。對照來源的加工順序，說明為何損傷整備不能僅由一張反光照片驗證；不配置蝕刻化學品。","instructionEn":"Add a damaged layer beneath sawn and lapped surfaces, then draw the section after its removal. Use the referenced sequence to explain why a reflective photograph cannot verify damage preparation; do not mix etchants.","observation":"觀察外觀粗糙度和損傷深度是否被誤畫為同一條界線。","observationEn":"Check whether surface roughness and damage depth have been incorrectly represented as the same boundary.","failure":"若以光澤代替損傷證據，列出仍未知的部分並保留待驗證狀態。","failureEn":"If gloss substitutes for damage evidence, list what remains unknown and keep the status unverified.","check":"在流程圖中標出損傷來源、去除目的及後續證據，沒有宣稱鏡面等於無損傷。","checkEn":"Mark the damage source, removal purpose and later evidence without equating a mirror finish with no damage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-06-k1","title":"次表面層","titleEn":"Subsurface layer","text":"機械加工的影響可延伸到可見表面以下。","textEn":"Mechanical processing can affect material below the visible surface."},{"id":"a004-v6-06-k2","title":"證據範圍","titleEn":"Evidence scope","text":"外觀影像能說明可見缺陷，不能單獨涵蓋所有材料狀態。","textEn":"Appearance images show visible defects but cannot alone establish every material condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"晶圓很亮但沒有損傷去除紀錄，能否直接宣告無損傷？","questionEn":"A wafer is shiny but lacks damage-removal evidence. Can it be declared damage-free?","options":["能，鏡面粗糙度已完整代表次表面狀態。","能，研磨後平均厚度合格即代表所有損傷去除。","不能，外觀與材料損傷需要不同證據。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; mirror-surface roughness completely represents subsurface condition.","Yes; acceptable average thickness after lapping proves all damage was removed.","No; appearance and material damage require different evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不能，外觀與材料損傷需要不同證據。 機械加工的影響可延伸到可見表面以下。","explanationEn":"No; appearance and material damage require different evidence. Mechanical processing can affect material below the visible surface."}},{"id":"a004-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-06"],"title":"分解研磨墊、漿料與相對運動","titleEn":"Separate pad, slurry and relative motion","objective":"建立化學與機械作用共同去除材料的模型。","objectiveEn":"Model removal as coupled chemical and mechanical action.","instruction":"畫出晶圓、研磨墊與漿料三個界面，逐一改變示意中的接觸、供液或相對運動；在紙上預測哪種改變會造成去除變慢或局部不均。","instructionEn":"Draw wafer, pad and slurry interfaces. Change contact, liquid supply or relative motion one at a time in the sketch and predict slower removal or local nonuniformity.","observation":"比較材料容易反應但接觸不良，以及接觸充分但漿料狀態不合適的兩種情境。","observationEn":"Compare a reactive surface with poor contact against good contact with unsuitable slurry condition.","failure":"把所有變化歸因於轉速會忽略墊面或漿料；重新建立一因一變的比較。","failureEn":"Attributing every change to speed ignores the pad or slurry; restore a one-factor comparison.","check":"因果圖同時包含表面反應、接觸與帶走材料三條路徑。","checkEn":"Include surface reaction, contact and material removal pathways in the causal diagram.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-07-k1","title":"耦合作用","titleEn":"Coupled action","text":"CMP 同時依靠化學環境與機械接觸，不能僅視為乾磨。","textEn":"CMP couples a chemical environment with mechanical contact; it is not simply dry abrasion."},{"id":"a004-v6-07-k2","title":"變因隔離","titleEn":"Isolating variables","text":"一次比較一個變因，才容易判別局部不均的來源。","textEn":"Comparing one variable at a time helps identify the origin of nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何不能只提高轉速來解決每種拋光缺陷？","questionEn":"Why is increasing speed not a universal polishing fix?","options":["缺陷也可能來自接觸、墊面或漿料條件。","提高轉速會自動保持所有區域的接觸壓力一致。","所有缺陷都是去除量不足，延長加工即可解決。"],"optionsEn":["Defects can also arise from contact, pad condition or slurry.","Higher speed automatically equalizes pressure in every region.","Every defect is insufficient removal and can be fixed by longer processing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷也可能來自接觸、墊面或漿料條件。 CMP 同時依靠化學環境與機械接觸，不能僅視為乾磨。","explanationEn":"Defects can also arise from contact, pad condition or slurry. CMP couples a chemical environment with mechanical contact; it is not simply dry abrasion."}},{"id":"a004-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-07"],"title":"追蹤工具狀態與批次漂移","titleEn":"Track tool condition and lot drift","objective":"把工具變化與晶圓差異分開比較。","objectiveEn":"Separate tool changes from wafer-to-wafer differences.","instruction":"自行建立三批假設紀錄，包含初始厚度、去除量與工具使用順序。將結果按時間與來料條件分別排序，判斷趨勢更像來料偏移還是工具狀態漂移。","instructionEn":"Create three hypothetical lots with starting thickness, removal and tool-use order. Sort results by time and incoming condition separately to distinguish material shift from tool-condition drift.","observation":"注意是否從某次工具狀態改變後，所有晶圓都出現相似偏移。","observationEn":"Look for a common shift across wafers after a tool-condition change.","failure":"混合不同來料規格可能製造假的時間趨勢；先分組再比較。","failureEn":"Mixing incoming specifications can create a false time trend; stratify before comparison.","check":"提出一項可區分兩種假說的追加觀察，並保留批次識別。","checkEn":"Propose an additional observation that distinguishes the hypotheses and retain lot identities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-08-k1","title":"共同原因","titleEn":"Shared cause","text":"同一工具狀態可影響多片晶圓，因此需要批次與時間關聯。","textEn":"A shared tool condition can affect many wafers, making lot and time associations useful."},{"id":"a004-v6-08-k2","title":"分組比較","titleEn":"Stratified comparison","text":"相似來料的前後比較，比混合所有晶圓平均值更容易解讀。","textEn":"Before-and-after comparisons of similar inputs are easier to interpret than a mixed average."}],"quiz":{"question":"發現時間趨勢前，為何先確認來料規格一致？","questionEn":"Why check comparable incoming specifications before interpreting a time trend?","options":["因為不同來料只影響產量，從不影響去除結果。","避免把材料差異誤當成工具漂移。","因為分組後便不需要保留工具時間順序。"],"optionsEn":["Different incoming material affects output quantity but never removal results.","To avoid mistaking material differences for tool drift.","Stratification eliminates the need to retain tool-use order."],"answer":1,"explanation":"避免把材料差異誤當成工具漂移。 同一工具狀態可影響多片晶圓，因此需要批次與時間關聯。","explanationEn":"To avoid mistaking material differences for tool drift. A shared tool condition can affect many wafers, making lot and time associations useful."}}]},{"id":"a004-stage03","order":3,"title":"拋光與驗證","titleEn":"Polishing and verification","description":"以分布、缺陷與污染證據共同判定是否可交付下一製程。","descriptionEn":"Combine spatial profiles, defects and contamination evidence before release.","steps":[{"id":"a004-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-cmp-applied","v6-wafer-sumco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-08"],"title":"評估中心與邊緣去除分布","titleEn":"Evaluate center-to-edge removal","objective":"以徑向地圖識別過度與不足去除。","objectiveEn":"Identify over-removal and under-removal on a radial map.","instruction":"將自己設定的拋光前後九點厚度相減，畫成中心、過渡區和邊緣三區。先描述哪區去除較多，再提出壓力或接觸假說；不替未知設備填入壓力數值。","instructionEn":"Subtract your hypothetical before-and-after nine-point maps and group removal into center, transition and edge. Describe the pattern before proposing pressure or contact hypotheses; do not invent machine pressures.","observation":"平均去除量相同的兩片，可能有相反的中心與邊緣分布。","observationEn":"Equal average removal can hide opposite center-to-edge patterns.","failure":"若只量中心，就無法確認邊緣過拋；補上邊緣取樣並標明排除範圍。","failureEn":"Center-only sampling misses edge overpolish; add edge sampling and label exclusions.","check":"交出分區去除圖及一個可被後續量測推翻的假說。","checkEn":"Submit a zonal removal map and a hypothesis that later measurements could disprove.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-09-k1","title":"分布回授","titleEn":"Profile feedback","text":"局部去除差異需要空間回授，單一平均厚度不足。","textEn":"Local removal differences need spatial feedback; one average thickness is insufficient."},{"id":"a004-v6-09-k2","title":"假說與觀察","titleEn":"Hypothesis versus observation","text":"「邊緣較薄」是觀察；「接觸壓力造成」仍需驗證。","textEn":"A thinner edge is an observation; a contact-pressure explanation still needs testing."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均去除達標但邊緣明顯過薄，應如何放行？","questionEn":"Average removal meets target but the edge is clearly too thin. How should release be judged?","options":["依平均值放行，局部不足可由中心厚度補償。","只重新定義排除區，不檢查這是否符合原規格。","依局部規格重新判定，不能只以平均值放行。"],"optionsEn":["Release by the average; center thickness compensates for a local deficit.","Redefine the excluded region without checking the original specification.","Reassess local specifications rather than release by the average alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"依局部規格重新判定，不能只以平均值放行。 局部去除差異需要空間回授，單一平均厚度不足。","explanationEn":"Reassess local specifications rather than release by the average alone. Local removal differences need spatial feedback; one average thickness is insufficient."}},{"id":"a004-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-09"],"title":"建立拋光終點與過拋辨識","titleEn":"Define a polishing endpoint","objective":"用目標剩餘量和缺陷條件共同決定停止。","objectiveEn":"Combine remaining-material targets and defect conditions when deciding to stop.","instruction":"在紙上比較提早停止、剛好達標及持續去除三個情境。為每一情境記錄剩餘厚度、均勻度和表面狀態；說明為何延長時間不能無限改善品質。","instructionEn":"Compare early stopping, target completion and continued removal on paper. Record remaining thickness, uniformity and surface condition for each, explaining why more time cannot improve quality indefinitely.","observation":"觀察缺陷改善與厚度損失可能同時發生，兩者需共同判讀。","observationEn":"Observe that defect improvement and thickness loss can occur together and must be interpreted jointly.","failure":"將時間到達視為唯一終點時，工具漂移會被漏掉；要求相應的量測佐證。","failureEn":"A time-only endpoint can miss tool drift; require matching measurement evidence.","check":"列出停止條件、超出條件與需要保留的驗證紀錄。","checkEn":"List stop criteria, out-of-limit conditions and the verification record to retain.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-10-k1","title":"多條件終點","titleEn":"Multiple endpoint conditions","text":"終點是符合要求的狀態，不只是計時器結束。","textEn":"An endpoint is a required state, not merely the end of a timer."},{"id":"a004-v6-10-k2","title":"過拋代價","titleEn":"Cost of overpolishing","text":"額外去除可能消耗幾何餘量，不能假定越久越好。","textEn":"Extra removal can consume geometric margin; longer is not automatically better."}],"quiz":{"question":"延長拋光使局部表面變好，卻低於厚度下限，結果為何？","questionEn":"Longer polishing improves a local surface but violates minimum thickness. What is the result?","options":["仍不符合整體放行要求。","表面要求優先時，厚度下限便自動失效。","用較低的平均去除率重算報告，就可視為沒有超限。"],"optionsEn":["It still fails the combined release requirements.","Giving surface quality priority automatically removes the thickness limit.","Recalculate the report with a lower average removal rate to erase the violation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"仍不符合整體放行要求。 終點是符合要求的狀態，不只是計時器結束。","explanationEn":"It still fails the combined release requirements. An endpoint is a required state, not merely the end of a timer."}},{"id":"a004-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-10"],"title":"追蹤拋光後粒子與再污染","titleEn":"Trace particles and recontamination","objective":"區分去除缺陷與清潔後新增污染。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish polishing defects from contamination introduced after cleaning.","instruction":"畫出拋光出口、清洗、乾燥與載具四個交接點，為每點建立假設粒子位置圖。比較同一晶圓前後地圖，找出首次出現新粒子的交接位置。","instructionEn":"Draw handoffs from polishing to cleaning, drying and carrier storage. Create hypothetical particle maps at each and compare the same wafer over time to locate where new particles first appear.","observation":"查看粒子是否跟著固定方位、液滴痕跡或載具接觸分布出現。","observationEn":"Look for patterns tied to orientation, drying marks or carrier contacts.","failure":"最後一張地圖只能證明最終狀態，不能單獨證明哪個站點造成污染。","failureEn":"A final map establishes the final state but cannot alone identify the contaminating station.","check":"提出保留污染追溯能力的前後比對方案，不假定清洗必然成功。","checkEn":"Propose before-and-after comparisons that preserve traceability without assuming cleaning succeeded.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-11-k1","title":"交接污染","titleEn":"Handoff contamination","text":"已拋光表面仍可能在清潔與搬運之間重新受到污染。","textEn":"A polished surface can be recontaminated during cleaning and handling handoffs."},{"id":"a004-v6-11-k2","title":"同片追蹤","titleEn":"Same-wafer tracking","text":"同片同方位的比較有助於區別舊缺陷與新缺陷。","textEn":"Comparing the same wafer and orientation helps distinguish old and new defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"如何較有力地判斷污染是否在載具交接後出現？","questionEn":"What better supports a conclusion that contamination appeared after carrier handoff?","options":["比較不同批次的最終平均粒子數即可定位本站責任。","比較同一晶圓交接前後、相同方位的粒子圖。","只查看清洗設備的完成訊號即可排除搬運污染。"],"optionsEn":["Comparing final average particle counts from different lots identifies this station’s responsibility.","Compare aligned particle maps of the same wafer before and after handoff.","A cleaning-complete signal rules out handling contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較同一晶圓交接前後、相同方位的粒子圖。 已拋光表面仍可能在清潔與搬運之間重新受到污染。","explanationEn":"Compare aligned particle maps of the same wafer before and after handoff. A polished surface can be recontaminated during cleaning and handling handoffs."}},{"id":"a004-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-wafer-sumco","v6-cmp-applied"],"prerequisiteIds":["a004-v6-11"],"title":"整合晶圓放行與異常處置","titleEn":"Integrate wafer release and disposition","objective":"用可追溯證據決定放行、複查或隔離。","objectiveEn":"Decide release, review or quarantine using traceable evidence.","instruction":"整理前十一項產物，將厚度、形狀、表面缺陷與清潔證據放在同一張放行表。加入一個缺少量測的案例及一個確認超限案例，分別說明下一個行動。","instructionEn":"Combine the prior outputs into a release sheet covering thickness, shape, surface defects and cleanliness. Add one missing-measurement case and one confirmed out-of-limit case and assign different next actions.","observation":"確認「尚無證據」沒有被寫成「已證明合格」，不同量測仍保留其基準。","observationEn":"Ensure missing evidence is not recorded as demonstrated compliance and each measurement retains its reference.","failure":"若重工會超出剩餘厚度預算，就不能僅因想降低報廢率而批准。","failureEn":"Do not authorize rework that exceeds the remaining thickness budget just to reduce rejects.","check":"每個結論都有批次、量測與處置理由，且下一站知道未解問題。","checkEn":"Link every conclusion to lot, measurement and disposition reasoning, with unresolved issues visible to the next stage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a004-v6-12-k1","title":"放行證據鏈","titleEn":"Release evidence chain","text":"產品放行需要相互一致的多項證據，而非挑選最漂亮的一項。","textEn":"Release needs consistent evidence across criteria, not selection of the most favorable result."},{"id":"a004-v6-12-k2","title":"重工可行性","titleEn":"Rework feasibility","text":"重工決策仍受材料餘量與缺陷機制限制。","textEn":"Rework remains constrained by material allowance and the defect mechanism."}],"quiz":{"question":"一項必要量測尚未取得時，正確狀態是什麼？","questionEn":"What status is appropriate when a required measurement is missing?","options":["直接合格，因為沒有超限數字。","用另一批的平均值補入，再視為本批已量測。","待驗證，先補齊證據再決定放行。"],"optionsEn":["Pass, because no out-of-limit number is present.","Fill in another lot’s average and treat this lot as measured.","Unverified; obtain the evidence before release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"待驗證，先補齊證據再決定放行。 產品放行需要相互一致的多項證據，而非挑選最漂亮的一項。","explanationEn":"Unverified; obtain the evidence before release. Release needs consistent evidence across criteria, not selection of the most favorable result."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的十二項教學任務，以自行繪製的示意模型、試算及來源資料進行；未提供工廠實測資料、專有配方或設備操作許可。","scopeEn":"Twelve educational tasks based on public principles, using original schematic models, calculations and referenced material. No factory measurement dataset, proprietary recipe or equipment operating authorization is supplied.","curriculumVersion":6,"subcategory":"substrate","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓與基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafers and substrates"},{"id":"a405","title":"消色差透鏡設計","titleEn":"Achromatic lens design","category":"instruments","kind":"course","summary":"用玻璃色散、光焦度分配與成像驗證，理解雙合透鏡如何降低色差，以及仍須處理的像差與公差。","summaryEn":"Use glass dispersion, optical-power allocation and imaging checks to understand chromatic correction and its remaining aberrations and tolerances.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund","v6-glass-schott","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":44,"estimatedMinutes":1040,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"diagram":{"type":"photonics","labels":["波段","玻璃配對","光焦度","組裝","成像驗證"],"labelsEn":["Spectrum","Glass pair","Optical power","Assembly","Image verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a405-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求與材料","titleEn":"Requirements and materials","description":"先固定波段及共軛，再建立薄透鏡的初步設計。","descriptionEn":"Fix spectrum and conjugates before building a preliminary thin-lens design.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"界定波段、共軛與成像需求","titleEn":"Define spectrum, conjugates and imaging needs","objective":"定義消色差設計要同時服務的波長與物像條件。","objectiveEn":"Define the wavelengths and object-image conditions the achromat must serve.","instruction":"畫出紅、綠、藍三條代表光路和一個共同像面，再分別標記遠方物體與近距物體。為比較選定相同的光圈與成像尺度，避免一邊改波長一邊改物距。","instructionEn":"Draw representative red, green and blue paths and one image plane, then label distant and near objects. Hold aperture and image scale consistent so spectrum and object distance are not changed together.","observation":"單色清楚與多色共同成像是不同要求；物距改變也會改變成像條件。","observationEn":"Single-color sharpness and common multicolor imaging are different requirements; object distance also changes the conjugates.","failure":"若只寫「影像清晰」，便無法區分波段、視場或解析度要求。","failureEn":"A requirement of merely clear imaging cannot distinguish spectrum, field or resolution.","check":"需求表包含波段、物像條件、光圈及需要比較的像面。","checkEn":"Record spectrum, conjugates, aperture and the image plane used for comparison.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-01-k1","title":"共軛條件","titleEn":"Conjugate conditions","text":"同一透鏡在不同物距下，不一定具有相同像差表現。","textEn":"One lens does not necessarily have the same aberration behavior at different object distances."},{"id":"a405-v6-01-k2","title":"共同像面","titleEn":"Common image plane","text":"消色差評估要比較多個波長，不可只挑最好的一色。","textEn":"Chromatic evaluation compares multiple wavelengths rather than selecting the best-performing color."}],"quiz":{"question":"只展示綠光的清晰影像，能否證明消色差符合需求？","questionEn":"Does one sharp green image prove chromatic requirements are met?","options":["不能，還需在相同條件下比較其他指定波長。","能，只要綠光的焦點正好在感測器平面。","能，只要使用相同玻璃材料，波長不需另測。"],"optionsEn":["No; compare the other specified wavelengths under the same conditions.","Yes, if green focus lies exactly at the sensor plane.","Yes; the same glass removes the need for separate wavelengths."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，還需在相同條件下比較其他指定波長。 同一透鏡在不同物距下，不一定具有相同像差表現。","explanationEn":"No; compare the other specified wavelengths under the same conditions. One lens does not necessarily have the same aberration behavior at different object distances."}},{"id":"a405-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-glass-schott"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-01"],"title":"閱讀折射率與阿貝數資料","titleEn":"Read refractive-index and Abbe-number data","objective":"區分折射能力與色散的材料指標。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish material measures of refraction and dispersion.","instruction":"從 SCHOTT 資料選兩種玻璃，記下折射率、阿貝數及其光譜線定義。以同一參考線比較，圈出高折射率但不必然低色散的情況。","instructionEn":"Choose two glasses from SCHOTT data and record refractive index, Abbe number and spectral-line definitions. Compare using the same reference line and identify why high index does not necessarily mean low dispersion.","observation":"注意 nd、ne 或不同阿貝數定義不可不經轉換便混用。","observationEn":"Do not mix nd, ne or differently defined Abbe numbers without accounting for their definitions.","failure":"只挑折射率最大的材料，可能使色差配置更困難。","failureEn":"Choosing the highest-index material alone may make chromatic balancing harder.","check":"材料表保留資料來源、參考波長和色散定義。","checkEn":"Retain data source, reference wavelength and dispersion definition in the material table.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-02-k1","title":"色散指標","titleEn":"Dispersion measure","text":"阿貝數描述指定光譜線間的相對色散，不能等同折射率。","textEn":"Abbe number describes relative dispersion across specified spectral lines, not refractive index itself."},{"id":"a405-v6-02-k2","title":"定義一致","titleEn":"Consistent definitions","text":"比較材料前先對齊參考光譜線與溫度等條件。","textEn":"Align reference spectral lines and conditions such as temperature before comparing materials."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩張表分別使用 nd/Vd 與 ne/Ve，最佳做法是什麼？","questionEn":"Two tables use nd/Vd and ne/Ve respectively. What is the best approach?","options":["只比較數字大小，忽略其參考光譜線。","先核對光譜線定義，再作一致條件比較。","只要兩者皆稱阿貝數，就可以直接互換定義。"],"optionsEn":["Compare numerical values while ignoring their reference spectral lines.","Check spectral-line definitions before making a consistent comparison.","Since both are called Abbe numbers, their definitions are interchangeable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先核對光譜線定義，再作一致條件比較。 阿貝數描述指定光譜線間的相對色散，不能等同折射率。","explanationEn":"Check spectral-line definitions before making a consistent comparison. Abbe number describes relative dispersion across specified spectral lines, not refractive index itself."}},{"id":"a405-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-glass-schott","v6-achromat-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-02"],"title":"分配正負光焦度","titleEn":"Allocate positive and negative optical power","objective":"以薄透鏡近似建立一階消色差條件。","objectiveEn":"Establish first-order achromatization using a thin-lens approximation.","instruction":"以明確假設的 V1=60、V2=30、總光焦度 10 m⁻¹ 試算。聯立 Φ1+Φ2=10 與 Φ1/V1+Φ2/V2=0，求兩片光焦度，再換算焦距並標註接觸薄透鏡假設。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical V1=60, V2=30 and total power 10 m⁻¹. Solve Φ1+Φ2=10 and Φ1/V1+Φ2/V2=0, convert the powers to focal lengths and label the contacting-thin-lens assumption.","observation":"所得正片光焦度大於總光焦度，負片抵銷部分光焦度與色散。","observationEn":"The positive element has more power than the total; the negative element cancels part of its power and dispersion.","failure":"混用毫米與公尺會造成千倍焦距錯誤；每行試算保留單位。","failureEn":"Mixing millimeters and meters causes a factor-of-one-thousand focal-length error; keep units on every line.","check":"得到 Φ1=20、Φ2=-10 m⁻¹，且能說明厚度與間隙尚未納入。","checkEn":"Obtain Φ1=20 and Φ2=-10 m⁻¹ and explain that thickness and spacing are not yet included.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-03-k1","title":"光焦度平衡","titleEn":"Optical-power balance","text":"接觸薄透鏡的總光焦度為各片光焦度之和；色散需另滿足平衡。","textEn":"Contacting thin-lens powers add, while dispersion needs a separate balance."},{"id":"a405-v6-03-k2","title":"近似範圍","titleEn":"Approximation scope","text":"一階試算是起點，不能取代實際厚透鏡追跡。","textEn":"First-order calculation is a starting point, not a replacement for thick-lens ray tracing."}],"quiz":{"question":"本例兩片光焦度應為哪組？","questionEn":"Which pair of powers satisfies the example?","options":["5 與 5 m⁻¹。","10 與 10 m⁻¹。","20 與 -10 m⁻¹。"],"optionsEn":["5 and 5 m⁻¹.","10 and 10 m⁻¹.","20 and -10 m⁻¹."],"answer":2,"explanation":"20 與 -10 m⁻¹。 接觸薄透鏡的總光焦度為各片光焦度之和；色散需另滿足平衡。","explanationEn":"20 and -10 m⁻¹. Contacting thin-lens powers add, while dispersion needs a separate balance."}},{"id":"a405-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund","v6-glass-schott"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-03"],"title":"檢查兩色重合與次級光譜","titleEn":"Check two-color correction and residual spectrum","objective":"理解雙合透鏡仍可能保留中間波長的焦移。","objectiveEn":"Understand why an achromat can retain intermediate-wavelength focus shifts.","instruction":"畫出焦點位置隨波長的示意曲線，將兩個設計波長調至同一焦點，再保留中間波長的偏差。比較「兩點重合」與「整條曲線為零」的差異。","instructionEn":"Draw a schematic focus-versus-wavelength curve, bring two design wavelengths to a common focus and retain an intermediate offset. Compare two-point coincidence with a curve that is zero everywhere.","observation":"兩色對齊不代表所有可見光或紅外線都同樣對齊。","observationEn":"Correcting two colors does not align every visible or infrared wavelength equally.","failure":"將名稱中的「消色差」解讀成零色差，會提出不合理驗收。","failureEn":"Reading achromatic as zero chromatic error creates unrealistic acceptance criteria.","check":"明確標記設計波段和剩餘焦移，而非只畫兩條重合光線。","checkEn":"Mark the design band and remaining focus shift, not only two coincident rays.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-04-k1","title":"次級光譜","titleEn":"Secondary spectrum","text":"兩波長的一階修正通常仍留下其他波長的殘差。","textEn":"First-order correction at two wavelengths generally leaves residuals at others."},{"id":"a405-v6-04-k2","title":"波段限制","titleEn":"Spectral limits","text":"材料與設計波段共同限定可宣稱的表現。","textEn":"Materials and the design band limit the performance claim."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩個設計波長焦點重合，哪個結論仍不成立？","questionEn":"Two design wavelengths share a focus. Which conclusion is still unsupported?","options":["所有波長都完全沒有色差。","指定兩波長的一階焦移已降低。","仍須查看其他指定波長。"],"optionsEn":["Every wavelength is completely free of chromatic error.","First-order focus separation for the specified pair is reduced.","Other specified wavelengths still need checking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"「所有波長都完全沒有色差」超出兩色焦點重合所能證明的範圍；中間或其他波長仍可能留下次級光譜。","explanationEn":"The claim that every wavelength is free of chromatic error exceeds what two coincident focal positions prove; intermediate and other wavelengths can retain secondary spectrum."}}]},{"id":"a405-stage02","order":2,"title":"形狀與組裝","titleEn":"Shape and assembly","description":"比較表面彎曲、光圈、方向與偏心對成像的影響。","descriptionEn":"Compare curvature, aperture, orientation and decentration effects.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-04"],"title":"比較曲率配置與透鏡形狀","titleEn":"Compare curvature allocation and lens shape","objective":"分辨相同光焦度下不同形狀的像差。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish aberrations of different shapes with similar power.","instruction":"保持材料與近似總光焦度不變，畫出較對稱與較彎曲的兩組表面。標示中心與邊緣光線，討論為何一階焦距相近仍需進一步追跡。","instructionEn":"Hold materials and approximate total power fixed and draw more symmetric and more strongly bent surface pairs. Mark central and marginal rays and explain why similar paraxial focal length still requires ray tracing.","observation":"表面彎曲的分配會影響邊緣光線，而不只改變透鏡外觀。","observationEn":"Allocation of surface curvature affects marginal rays, not just appearance.","failure":"只保留焦距欄位會漏掉形狀資訊；補上曲率符號和光行方向。","failureEn":"A focal-length-only record omits shape; add curvature signs and propagation direction.","check":"兩個候選均保留表面順序、曲率符號與比較條件。","checkEn":"Retain surface order, curvature signs and comparison conditions for both candidates.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-05-k1","title":"彎曲自由度","titleEn":"Lens-bending freedom","text":"相近一階光焦度可由不同曲率分配實現。","textEn":"Similar paraxial power can arise from different curvature distributions."},{"id":"a405-v6-05-k2","title":"邊緣光線","titleEn":"Marginal rays","text":"有限光圈下的光線不一定遵循近軸近似。","textEn":"Rays at finite aperture need not follow the paraxial approximation."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩個設計焦距相同，能否因此判定成像品質相同？","questionEn":"Do equal focal lengths prove equal image quality?","options":["能，一階焦距已完整決定有限光圈像差。","不能，表面形狀和有限光圈像差仍可能不同。","能，只要兩者玻璃相同，曲率分配就沒有作用。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; paraxial focal length fully determines finite-aperture aberrations.","No; surface shape and finite-aperture aberrations may differ.","Yes; with identical glass, curvature allocation has no effect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不能，表面形狀和有限光圈像差仍可能不同。 相近一階光焦度可由不同曲率分配實現。","explanationEn":"No; surface shape and finite-aperture aberrations may differ. Similar paraxial power can arise from different curvature distributions."}},{"id":"a405-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-aberrations-edmund","v6-achromat-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-05"],"title":"區分球差、彗差與色差","titleEn":"Separate spherical aberration, coma and color","objective":"避免用改變波長解釋所有模糊。","objectiveEn":"Avoid attributing every blur to wavelength changes.","instruction":"分別畫單一波長的軸上邊緣光線、離軸光束和多波長軸上光束。為每張圖只改變一種因素：光圈、視場或波長，對應可能的像差類型。","instructionEn":"Draw on-axis marginal rays at one wavelength, an off-axis bundle and a multicolor on-axis bundle. Change only aperture, field or wavelength in each to associate the relevant aberration.","observation":"單色仍有模糊時，不能全歸因於玻璃色散。","observationEn":"Blur that remains in monochromatic light cannot all be attributed to dispersion.","failure":"多因素同時改變會讓診斷失去可比性；返回一因素比較。","failureEn":"Changing multiple factors at once destroys diagnostic comparability; return to one-factor comparisons.","check":"能為三種模糊各指定不同的控制變因與觀察。","checkEn":"Assign a distinct control variable and observation to each blur type.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-06-k1","title":"像差分類","titleEn":"Aberration classification","text":"色差與單色像差有不同來源，修正一種不代表全部修正。","textEn":"Chromatic and monochromatic aberrations have different origins; correcting one does not correct all."},{"id":"a405-v6-06-k2","title":"控制變因","titleEn":"Controlled variables","text":"波長固定後改變光圈，可把部分幾何像差與色差分開比較。","textEn":"Varying aperture at fixed wavelength helps separate geometric aberrations from color."}],"quiz":{"question":"固定單一波長後，縮小光圈使軸上模糊改善，優先懷疑什麼？","questionEn":"At one wavelength, stopping down improves on-axis blur. What is a plausible concern?","options":["必定是不同波長之間的焦移，即使測試只有單一波長。","必定只有鍍膜透射率改變，光線幾何不需檢查。","與邊緣光線相關的單色像差。"],"optionsEn":["It must be inter-wavelength focus shift even in a single-wavelength test.","It must be coating transmission alone, so ray geometry needs no review.","A monochromatic aberration involving marginal rays."],"answer":2,"explanation":"與邊緣光線相關的單色像差。 色差與單色像差有不同來源，修正一種不代表全部修正。","explanationEn":"A monochromatic aberration involving marginal rays. Chromatic and monochromatic aberrations have different origins; correcting one does not correct all."}},{"id":"a405-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-06"],"title":"確認雙合透鏡的安裝方向","titleEn":"Check doublet orientation","objective":"將標示方向與設計共軛對應。","objectiveEn":"Match mounting orientation to the design conjugates.","instruction":"為同一雙合透鏡畫正反兩種安裝圖，固定物距與像面。查閱所選元件的供應商方向說明，將實際朝向與設計條件對應，不假定每款雙合透鏡都可任意翻轉。","instructionEn":"Draw both mounting orientations for one doublet at fixed object distance and image plane. Consult the chosen component’s orientation guidance and match it to design conditions rather than assuming every doublet is reversible.","observation":"焦距可能相近，但翻轉後的像差表現仍可改變。","observationEn":"Focal length may remain similar while aberration performance changes after reversal.","failure":"只看外徑選方向會忽略光學表面配置；回查圖面和共軛。","failureEn":"Choosing orientation by diameter ignores surface arrangement; revisit the drawing and conjugates.","check":"組裝圖有光行方向、元件朝向及依據來源。","checkEn":"Include propagation direction, component orientation and its supporting reference.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-07-k1","title":"方向與共軛","titleEn":"Orientation and conjugates","text":"透鏡方向應配合設計的物像條件。","textEn":"Lens orientation should match its intended object-image conditions."},{"id":"a405-v6-07-k2","title":"標記追溯","titleEn":"Marking traceability","text":"機械可裝入不等於光學方向正確。","textEn":"Mechanical fit does not establish correct optical orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"透鏡正反都能裝入鏡筒，下一步應做什麼？","questionEn":"The lens fits the barrel in either direction. What should happen next?","options":["核對元件圖面與設計共軛的方向。","只比較兩面直徑，直徑相同就可任選。","只測一次近軸焦距，就宣稱正反像差相同。"],"optionsEn":["Check orientation against the component drawing and design conjugates.","Compare face diameters only; equal diameters allow either orientation.","Measure paraxial focal length once and declare equal aberrations both ways."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對元件圖面與設計共軛的方向。 透鏡方向應配合設計的物像條件。","explanationEn":"Check orientation against the component drawing and design conjugates. Lens orientation should match its intended object-image conditions."}},{"id":"a405-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-glass-schott"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-07"],"title":"評估偏心、傾斜與膠合界面","titleEn":"Evaluate decentration, tilt and the cemented interface","objective":"辨認組裝幾何與材料界面的不同風險。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish assembly geometry from interface-material risks.","instruction":"在剖面上各加入一次偏心、傾斜及膠層不均，保持其他條件不變。畫出可能的光束偏轉或界面問題，並把膠合型與空氣間隔型設計分開記錄。","instructionEn":"Introduce decentration, tilt and uneven cement separately in a cross-section while holding other conditions fixed. Sketch beam deviation or interface issues and record cemented and air-spaced designs separately.","observation":"裝配誤差可能呈現左右不對稱，不能只用軸上單點焦距判斷。","observationEn":"Assembly error can create asymmetry that one on-axis focal-length value misses.","failure":"把空氣間隔直接替換為膠層會改變光學模型，不是單純更換固定方式。","failureEn":"Replacing an air gap with cement changes the optical model, not just the mounting method.","check":"列出至少一項幾何與一項界面材料的驗證。","checkEn":"Identify at least one geometric and one interface-material verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-08-k1","title":"共同光軸","titleEn":"Shared optical axis","text":"雙片的相對光軸與傾角影響組合後的表現。","textEn":"Relative element axes and tilt affect the assembled performance."},{"id":"a405-v6-08-k2","title":"界面介質","titleEn":"Interface medium","text":"膠層或空氣間隙具有光學角色，應納入設計資料。","textEn":"Cement or an air gap has an optical role and belongs in the design data."}],"quiz":{"question":"將空氣間隔雙片直接膠合，為何需重新評估？","questionEn":"Why reassess an air-spaced pair before cementing it?","options":["膠合只改變固定方式，不必修改任何光學模型。","界面介質與間距已改變。","只要兩片外徑相同，空氣與膠層可完全互換。"],"optionsEn":["Cementing changes only mounting and requires no optical-model change.","Interface medium and spacing change.","Equal diameters make air and cement fully interchangeable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"界面介質與間距已改變。 雙片的相對光軸與傾角影響組合後的表現。","explanationEn":"Interface medium and spacing change. Relative element axes and tilt affect the assembled performance."}}]},{"id":"a405-stage03","order":3,"title":"公差與驗收","titleEn":"Tolerances and acceptance","description":"把鍍膜、製造差異與多波長量測整合成可追溯驗收。","descriptionEn":"Combine coatings, manufacturing variation and multiwavelength measurements in traceable acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund","v6-glass-schott"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-08"],"title":"區分抗反射鍍膜與色差修正","titleEn":"Separate antireflection coating from chromatic correction","objective":"避免將透光率改善誤當作焦移消除。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mistaking improved transmission for eliminated focal shift.","instruction":"在同一透鏡模型上比較有無抗反射鍍膜的光能路徑，另保留多波長焦點位置圖。分開記錄透射、反射鬼影與焦距，不用亮度替代成像量測。","instructionEn":"Compare light-energy paths with and without an antireflection coating while retaining a separate multicolor focus diagram. Record transmission, reflected ghosts and focal position independently.","observation":"影像變亮或反光減少，不必然代表色差已降低。","observationEn":"A brighter image or reduced reflection does not necessarily indicate lower chromatic aberration.","failure":"超出鍍膜設計波段的表現不可從單一波長外推。","failureEn":"Do not extrapolate one wavelength’s coating performance beyond its design band.","check":"驗收表分開列出光譜透射與多色焦移。","checkEn":"Separate spectral transmission and multicolor focus shift in acceptance records.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-09-k1","title":"反射與折射","titleEn":"Reflection and refraction","text":"抗反射鍍膜主要控制界面反射；雙合材料配置負責主要色差平衡。","textEn":"Antireflection coatings primarily control interface reflection; doublet material allocation provides the main chromatic balance."},{"id":"a405-v6-09-k2","title":"亮度誤判","titleEn":"Brightness misinterpretation","text":"亮度受到光源與曝光影響，不能單獨代表解析品質。","textEn":"Brightness depends on illumination and exposure and is not an independent measure of resolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"鍍膜後影像更亮，是否足以證明兩色焦點更接近？","questionEn":"The coated lens produces a brighter image. Does that prove closer two-color focus?","options":["足夠，較高透射率必然代表較小軸向色差。","足夠，只要鍍膜顏色符合設計波段。","不足，需另測多波長焦點。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; higher transmission necessarily means smaller axial color.","Yes, if the coating’s visible color matches the design band.","No; multiwavelength focus needs separate measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不足，需另測多波長焦點。 抗反射鍍膜主要控制界面反射；雙合材料配置負責主要色差平衡。","explanationEn":"No; multiwavelength focus needs separate measurement. Antireflection coatings primarily control interface reflection; doublet material allocation provides the main chromatic balance."}},{"id":"a405-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-glass-schott","v6-aberrations-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-09"],"title":"建立尺寸與材料的公差敏感度","titleEn":"Build tolerance sensitivity for geometry and glass","objective":"找出值得優先控制的設計變因。","objectiveEn":"Identify design variables that deserve priority control.","instruction":"建立曲率、厚度、間距、折射率與偏心五欄。用模型或來源資料逐一施加小變化，記錄焦位或影像指標的變化方向；明確註明不是工廠統計分布。","instructionEn":"Create columns for curvature, thickness, spacing, refractive index and decentration. Apply small changes individually in a model or referenced data and record response direction, explicitly distinguishing this from factory statistics.","observation":"相同百分比變化對不同變因，不一定造成相同影像影響。","observationEn":"Equal percentage changes in different variables need not produce equal image effects.","failure":"把單因子結果直接相加成量產良率會超出資料能力。","failureEn":"Turning one-factor results directly into production yield exceeds the evidence.","check":"指出最敏感的候選變因及其比較尺度，保留尚未評估的耦合。","checkEn":"Identify candidate sensitive variables and comparison scales while retaining untested couplings.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-10-k1","title":"敏感度","titleEn":"Sensitivity","text":"公差評估關心輸入偏差如何傳到成像結果。","textEn":"Tolerance analysis asks how input deviations propagate into imaging results."},{"id":"a405-v6-10-k2","title":"分布假設","titleEn":"Distribution assumptions","text":"良率推估另需合理的製造分布及變因相關性。","textEn":"Yield estimates additionally need defensible manufacturing distributions and correlations."}],"quiz":{"question":"只有單因子敏感度表，能否直接宣稱量產良率？","questionEn":"Can a one-factor sensitivity table directly establish production yield?","options":["不能，仍缺製造分布和相關性資料。","能，把各變因造成的偏差百分比平均即可。","能，單因子分析已包含變因之間的相關性。"],"optionsEn":["No; manufacturing distributions and correlations are missing.","Yes; average the deviation percentages from all variables.","Yes; one-factor analysis already includes inter-variable correlations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，仍缺製造分布和相關性資料。 公差評估關心輸入偏差如何傳到成像結果。","explanationEn":"No; manufacturing distributions and correlations are missing. Tolerance analysis asks how input deviations propagate into imaging results."}},{"id":"a405-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-10"],"title":"比較多波長焦點與離軸影像","titleEn":"Compare multicolor focus and off-axis images","objective":"用一致條件檢查軸上與視場邊緣。","objectiveEn":"Check on-axis and field-edge behavior under consistent conditions.","instruction":"用紙上光線模型或自行取得的合適測量資料，固定物體、光圈與參考位置；分別記錄指定波長的最佳焦位，再在共同像面比較中心和邊緣。","instructionEn":"Using a paper ray model or suitable measurements you obtain, hold object, aperture and reference position fixed. Record best focus for each wavelength, then compare center and edge at one common image plane.","observation":"各色各自重新對焦可掩蓋共同像面上的實際色差。","observationEn":"Refocusing separately for each color can hide the actual chromatic error at a shared image plane.","failure":"更改曝光或物距而未記錄，會破壞不同影像之間的比較。","failureEn":"Unrecorded exposure or object-distance changes undermine comparisons.","check":"結果同時包含各色最佳焦位與共同像面表現。","checkEn":"Include both per-color best-focus positions and common-plane performance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-11-k1","title":"共同條件比較","titleEn":"Like-for-like comparison","text":"驗收需與實際使用條件一致，不能為每個結果換一組最佳條件。","textEn":"Acceptance should match use conditions rather than optimize conditions independently for each result."},{"id":"a405-v6-11-k2","title":"視場取樣","titleEn":"Field sampling","text":"軸上良好不保證離軸同樣良好。","textEn":"Good on-axis performance does not guarantee good off-axis performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"為每種顏色各自重新對焦後都很清楚，還缺什麼？","questionEn":"Every color is sharp after separate refocusing. What evidence is missing?","options":["只比較各色在自己的最佳像面所得影像。","在同一像面上的多色比較。","只比較總透光率，無需保留焦位差。"],"optionsEn":["Compare each color only at its own best image plane.","A multicolor comparison at one image plane.","Compare total transmission without retaining focus offsets."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一像面上的多色比較。 驗收需與實際使用條件一致，不能為每個結果換一組最佳條件。","explanationEn":"A multicolor comparison at one image plane. Acceptance should match use conditions rather than optimize conditions independently for each result."}},{"id":"a405-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v6-aberrations-edmund","v6-glass-schott"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-11"],"title":"整理光學組件的驗收與追溯","titleEn":"Assemble optical acceptance and traceability","objective":"讓材料、設計版本與實測條件可互相對應。","objectiveEn":"Link materials, design revision and measurement conditions.","instruction":"把玻璃資料、表面順序、方向、公差與成像結果組成一份交接表。加入一個可接受殘差與一個超限案例，分別寫出接受理由及需要改善的變因。","instructionEn":"Combine glass data, surface order, orientation, tolerances and imaging results in a handoff record. Add an acceptable residual and an out-of-limit case, stating acceptance reasoning and the variable to investigate.","observation":"聲稱「完全不散色」通常超出有限波段與有限公差的證據。","observationEn":"A claim of absolutely no dispersion generally exceeds evidence limited by spectrum and tolerances.","failure":"若測試版本與製造圖面不同，先修正版本對應再作判定。","failureEn":"If tested and manufactured revisions differ, restore revision correspondence before judgment.","check":"交付文件說明適用波段、殘餘像差、組裝方向及未驗證條件。","checkEn":"State the applicable band, residual aberrations, mounting orientation and unverified conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v6-12-k1","title":"規格化性能","titleEn":"Specified performance","text":"工程驗收依明確條件下的性能，而不是無限範圍的完美宣稱。","textEn":"Engineering acceptance uses performance under stated conditions rather than unlimited perfection claims."},{"id":"a405-v6-12-k2","title":"版本控制","titleEn":"Revision control","text":"材料批次、設計處方與測試條件需可追溯到同一組件。","textEn":"Material lot, prescription and test conditions should trace to the same assembly."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個交付描述最可驗證？","questionEn":"Which delivery statement is most verifiable?","options":["在未指定波段下，單一焦距正確即代表全面合格。","外徑與中心厚度合格即可取代所有成像驗收。","在列明波段與共軛下符合指定焦移和成像要求。"],"optionsEn":["Correct focal length alone proves complete compliance without a specified spectrum.","Diameter and center-thickness compliance replace all imaging acceptance.","Meets stated focus-shift and imaging requirements over the listed band and conjugates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在列明波段與共軛下符合指定焦移和成像要求。 工程驗收依明確條件下的性能，而不是無限範圍的完美宣稱。","explanationEn":"Meets stated focus-shift and imaging requirements over the listed band and conjugates. Engineering acceptance uses performance under stated conditions rather than unlimited perfection claims."}}]},{"id":"a405-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「部分色散與三片式複消色差解」與「熱離焦與光熱係數」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution\" and \"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v12-01","title":"部分色散與三片式複消色差解：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v6-12"],"objective":"說明「三片式複消色差組」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Three-glass apochromatic group” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"兩片玻璃的消色差只能讓 C 與 F 線共焦；一般玻璃的相對部分色散落在正常線 P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d 上，其他波長仍各自聚焦，留下二級光譜。要讓第三個波長也共焦，需同時滿足三個條件：總光焦度 Σφᵢ = φ、一級色差 Σφᵢ/νᵢ = 0、二級色差 Σφᵢ·Pᵢ/νᵢ = 0。三種玻璃在 (1/ν, P) 平面上必須圍成三角形，三角形面積越小，各片光焦度越大；正常線之外的異常色散玻璃（如 N-FK51A 的 ΔP_gF = +0.034、N-KZFS4 的 −0.010）可以把三角形撐開。三片式的代價是單片光焦度變大、曲率變陡，高階像差與定心敏感度隨之上升。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「三片式複消色差組」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A two-glass achromat can only bring the C and F lines to a common focus; ordinary glasses have relative partial dispersions on the normal line P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d, so other wavelengths still focus elsewhere and leave the secondary spectrum. Bringing a third wavelength to the same focus requires three conditions at once: total power Σφᵢ = φ, zero primary colour Σφᵢ/νᵢ = 0 and zero secondary colour Σφᵢ·Pᵢ/νᵢ = 0. The three glasses must form a triangle in the (1/ν, P) plane, and the smaller its area the larger the individual element powers; anomalous-dispersion glasses off the normal line, such as N-FK51A with ΔP_gF = +0.034 and N-KZFS4 with −0.010, open the triangle up. The price of a triplet is larger element powers and steeper curves, so higher-order aberrations and centring sensitivity grow. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Three-glass apochromatic group”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：由 Sellmeier 係數算得 N-FK51A（ν = 84.47、P = 0.5359）、N-KZFS4（44.49、0.5590）、N-SF5（32.25、0.5984）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: From Sellmeier coefficients: N-FK51A (ν = 84.47, P = 0.5359), N-KZFS4 (44.49, 0.5590) and N-SF5 (32.25, 0.5984).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「三片式複消色差組」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Three-glass apochromatic group”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-01-k1","title":"部分色散與三片式複消色差解","titleEn":"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution","text":"兩片玻璃的消色差只能讓 C 與 F 線共焦；一般玻璃的相對部分色散落在正常線 P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d 上，其他波長仍各自聚焦，留下二級光譜。要讓第三個波長也共焦，需同時滿足三個條件：總光焦度 Σφᵢ = φ、一級色差 Σφᵢ/νᵢ = 0、二級色差 Σφᵢ·Pᵢ/νᵢ = 0。","textEn":"A two-glass achromat can only bring the C and F lines to a common focus; ordinary glasses have relative partial dispersions on the normal line P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d, so other wavelengths still focus elsewhere and leave the secondary spectrum. Bringing a third wavelength to the same focus requires three conditions at once: total power Σφᵢ = φ, zero primary colour Σφᵢ/νᵢ = 0 and zero secondary colour Σφᵢ·Pᵢ/νᵢ = 0.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「部分色散與三片式複消色差解」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution\" is correct?","options":["只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","兩片玻璃的消色差只能讓 C 與 F 線共焦。","玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。"],"optionsEn":["A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","A two-glass achromat can only bring the C and F lines to a common focus.","Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩片玻璃的消色差只能讓 C 與 F 線共焦；一般玻璃的相對部分色散落在正常線 P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d 上，其他波長仍各自聚焦，留下二級光譜。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A two-glass achromat can only bring the C and F lines to a common focus; ordinary glasses have relative partial dispersions on the normal line P_gF ≈ 0.6438 − 0.001682·ν_d, so other wavelengths still focus elsewhere and leave the secondary spectrum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":13},{"id":"a405-v12-02","title":"部分色散與三片式複消色差解：定量估算","titleEn":"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「三片式複消色差組」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Three-glass apochromatic group” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：由 Sellmeier 係數算得 N-FK51A（ν = 84.47、P = 0.5359）、N-KZFS4（44.49、0.5590）、N-SF5（32.25、0.5984）。f = 100 mm 解三式：φ₁ = 2.576φ（f₁ = 38.8 mm）、φ₂ = −2.153φ（f₂ = −46.4 mm）、φ₃ = 0.577φ（f₃ = 173.3 mm）；以實際折射率逐線計算，C、F、g 焦點都落在 d 焦點 0.15 µm 以內。對照 N-BK7/F2 雙合：C、F 在 d 後 50 µm、g 在 223 µm；但三片式 Σ|φᵢ| = 5.31φ，雙合只有 3.62φ。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: From Sellmeier coefficients: N-FK51A (ν = 84.47, P = 0.5359), N-KZFS4 (44.49, 0.5590) and N-SF5 (32.25, 0.5984). Solving the three equations for f = 100 mm gives φ₁ = 2.576φ (f₁ = 38.8 mm), φ₂ = −2.153φ (f₂ = −46.4 mm) and φ₃ = 0.577φ (f₃ = 173.3 mm); tracing with real indices line by line puts the C, F and g foci within 0.15 µm of the d focus. For comparison an N-BK7/F2 doublet leaves C and F 50 µm behind d and g at 223 µm, but the triplet carries Σ|φᵢ| = 5.31φ against 3.62φ for the doublet. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以實際熔煉批的熔次資料（n_d、ν_d、P_gF）取代型錄值重新解光焦度；組裝後用單色儀或窄帶濾光片在 C、d、F、g 各波長量軸向最佳焦點，確認焦點散佈小於景深，並與模型的 0.15 µm 等級殘差比較；同時量各片偏心，因為大光焦度讓同樣的偏心產生更大的彗差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Re-solve the powers with melt-sheet data (n_d, ν_d, P_gF) from the actual glass lots instead of catalogue values; after assembly measure the axial best focus at C, d, F and g with a monochromator or narrow-band filters, confirm the spread is smaller than the depth of focus and compare with the modelled 0.15 µm-level residual; measure element decentration as well, because large powers turn the same decentre into more coma.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"由 Sellmeier 係數算得 N-FK51A（ν = 84.47、P = 0.5359）、N-KZFS4（44.49、0.5590）、N-SF5（32.25、0.5984）。f = 100 mm 解三式：φ₁ = 2.576φ（f₁ = 38.8 mm）、φ₂ = −2.153φ（f₂ = −46.4 mm）、φ₃ = 0.577φ（f₃ = 173.3 mm）；以實際折射率逐線計算，C、F、g 焦點都落在 d 焦點 0.15 µm 以內。對照 N-BK7/F2 雙合：C、F 在 d 後 50 µm、g 在 223 µm；但三片式 Σ|φᵢ| = 5.31φ，雙合只有 3.62φ。","textEn":"From Sellmeier coefficients: N-FK51A (ν = 84.47, P = 0.5359), N-KZFS4 (44.49, 0.5590) and N-SF5 (32.25, 0.5984). Solving the three equations for f = 100 mm gives φ₁ = 2.576φ (f₁ = 38.8 mm), φ₂ = −2.153φ (f₂ = −46.4 mm) and φ₃ = 0.577φ (f₃ = 173.3 mm); tracing with real indices line by line puts the C, F and g foci within 0.15 µm of the d focus. For comparison an N-BK7/F2 doublet leaves C and F 50 µm behind d and g at 223 µm, but the triplet carries Σ|φᵢ| = 5.31φ against 3.62φ for the doublet.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「部分色散與三片式複消色差解」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution\", which statement holds?","options":["鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。","HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。","由 Sellmeier 係數算得 N-FK51A（ν = 84.47、P = 0.5359）、N-KZFS4（44.49、0.5590）、N-SF5（32.25、0.5984）。"],"optionsEn":["A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.","A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.","From Sellmeier coefficients: N-FK51A (ν = 84.47, P = 0.5359), N-KZFS4 (44.49, 0.5590) and N-SF5 (32.25, 0.5984)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"由 Sellmeier 係數算得 N-FK51A（ν = 84.47、P = 0.5359）、N-KZFS4（44.49、0.5590）、N-SF5（32.25、0.5984）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"From Sellmeier coefficients: N-FK51A (ν = 84.47, P = 0.5359), N-KZFS4 (44.49, 0.5590) and N-SF5 (32.25, 0.5984). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":14},{"id":"a405-v12-03","title":"部分色散與三片式複消色差解：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「三片式複消色差組」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Three-glass apochromatic group” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以實際熔煉批的熔次資料（n_d、ν_d、P_gF）取代型錄值重新解光焦度；組裝後用單色儀或窄帶濾光片在 C、d、F、g 各波長量軸向最佳焦點，確認焦點散佈小於景深，並與模型的 0.15 µm 等級殘差比較；同時量各片偏心，因為大光焦度讓同樣的偏心產生更大的彗差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Re-solve the powers with melt-sheet data (n_d, ν_d, P_gF) from the actual glass lots instead of catalogue values; after assembly measure the axial best focus at C, d, F and g with a monochromator or narrow-band filters, confirm the spread is smaller than the depth of focus and compare with the modelled 0.15 µm-level residual; measure element decentration as well, because large powers turn the same decentre into more coma. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：FK51A 類氟磷冠玻璃硬度低、膨脹係數大、耐候性差，拋光或膠合時容易出現裂紋與表面污斑；若沿用型錄 P_gF 而不看熔次資料，三色共焦點偏移，實際殘餘色差可能比設計大一個數量級，而大光焦度也讓軸上彗差對定心誤差極為敏感。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Fluorophosphate crowns of the FK51A type are soft, high-expansion and weather poorly, so they crack or stain during polishing or cementing; using catalogue P_gF instead of melt data shifts the three-colour focus so the real residual colour can be an order of magnitude above design, and the large powers make on-axis coma extremely sensitive to centring error.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以實際熔煉批的熔次資料（n_d、ν_d、P_gF）取代型錄值重新解光焦度；組裝後用單色儀或窄帶濾光片在 C、d、F、g 各波長量軸向最佳焦點，確認焦點散佈小於景深，並與模型的 0.15 µm 等級殘差比較；同時量各片偏心，因為大光焦度讓同樣的偏心產生更大的彗差。","textEn":"Re-solve the powers with melt-sheet data (n_d, ν_d, P_gF) from the actual glass lots instead of catalogue values; after assembly measure the axial best focus at C, d, F and g with a monochromator or narrow-band filters, confirm the spread is smaller than the depth of focus and compare with the modelled 0.15 µm-level residual; measure element decentration as well, because large powers turn the same decentre into more coma.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「部分色散與三片式複消色差解」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution\"?","options":["以實際熔煉批的熔次資料（n_d、ν_d、P_gF）取代型錄值重新解光焦度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。"],"optionsEn":["Re-solve the powers with melt-sheet data (n_d, ν_d, P_gF) from the actual glass lots instead of catalogue values.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以實際熔煉批的熔次資料（n_d、ν_d、P_gF）取代型錄值重新解光焦度；組裝後用單色儀或窄帶濾光片在 C、d、F、g 各波長量軸向最佳焦點，確認焦點散佈小於景深，並與模型的 0.15 µm 等級殘差比較；同時量各片偏心，因為大光焦度讓同樣的偏心產生更大的彗差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Re-solve the powers with melt-sheet data (n_d, ν_d, P_gF) from the actual glass lots instead of catalogue values; after assembly measure the axial best focus at C, d, F and g with a monochromator or narrow-band filters, confirm the spread is smaller than the depth of focus and compare with the modelled 0.15 µm-level residual; measure element decentration as well, because large powers turn the same decentre into more coma. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":15},{"id":"a405-v12-04","title":"部分色散與三片式複消色差解：失效診斷","titleEn":"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「三片式複消色差組」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Three-glass apochromatic group” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"FK51A 類氟磷冠玻璃硬度低、膨脹係數大、耐候性差，拋光或膠合時容易出現裂紋與表面污斑；若沿用型錄 P_gF 而不看熔次資料，三色共焦點偏移，實際殘餘色差可能比設計大一個數量級，而大光焦度也讓軸上彗差對定心誤差極為敏感。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Fluorophosphate crowns of the FK51A type are soft, high-expansion and weather poorly, so they crack or stain during polishing or cementing; using catalogue P_gF instead of melt data shifts the three-colour focus so the real residual colour can be an order of magnitude above design, and the large powers make on-axis coma extremely sensitive to centring error. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：三片式的代價是單片光焦度變大、曲率變陡，高階像差與定心敏感度隨之上升。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The price of a triplet is larger element powers and steeper curves, so higher-order aberrations and centring sensitivity grow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"FK51A 類氟磷冠玻璃硬度低、膨脹係數大、耐候性差，拋光或膠合時容易出現裂紋與表面污斑；若沿用型錄 P_gF 而不看熔次資料，三色共焦點偏移，實際殘餘色差可能比設計大一個數量級，而大光焦度也讓軸上彗差對定心誤差極為敏感。","textEn":"Fluorophosphate crowns of the FK51A type are soft, high-expansion and weather poorly, so they crack or stain during polishing or cementing; using catalogue P_gF instead of melt data shifts the three-colour focus so the real residual colour can be an order of magnitude above design, and the large powers make on-axis coma extremely sensitive to centring error.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「部分色散與三片式複消色差解」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Partial dispersion and the three-glass apochromatic solution\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","FK51A 類氟磷冠玻璃硬度低、膨脹係數大、耐候性差，拋光或膠合時容易出現裂紋與表面污斑。","玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Fluorophosphate crowns of the FK51A type are soft, high-expansion and weather poorly, so they crack or stain during polishing or cementing.","Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"FK51A 類氟磷冠玻璃硬度低、膨脹係數大、耐候性差，拋光或膠合時容易出現裂紋與表面污斑；若沿用型錄 P_gF 而不看熔次資料，三色共焦點偏移，實際殘餘色差可能比設計大一個數量級，而大光焦度也讓軸上彗差對定心誤差極為敏感。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fluorophosphate crowns of the FK51A type are soft, high-expansion and weather poorly, so they crack or stain during polishing or cementing; using catalogue P_gF instead of melt data shifts the three-colour focus so the real residual colour can be an order of magnitude above design, and the large powers make on-axis coma extremely sensitive to centring error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":16},{"id":"a405-v12-05","title":"熱離焦與光熱係數：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"溫度同時改變折射率（dn/dT）與鏡片尺寸（膨脹係數 α），薄透鏡在空氣中的焦距變化率為 (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1)，稱為光熱係數。型錄的 dn/dT 是相對於空氣的值，SCHOTT 另以 G = α(n − 1) + dn/dT 表示玻璃的熱光常數。雙合透鏡的光熱係數按各片光焦度加權相加；同時鏡片到感測器之間的鏡筒或隔圈以 α_h·L 伸長。無熱化設計要讓像面移動與機構伸長相等，即 γ·f ≈ α_h·L，這對戶外相機、車載與太空光學尤其關鍵。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Temperature changes both the refractive index (dn/dT) and the lens dimensions (expansion coefficient α), and for a thin lens in air the focal-length change rate is (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1), the opto-thermal coefficient. Catalogue dn/dT values are relative to air, and SCHOTT also expresses the thermo-optical constant as G = α(n − 1) + dn/dT. A doublet's opto-thermal coefficient is the power-weighted sum of its elements, while the barrel or spacer between lens and sensor grows by α_h·L. Athermal design makes image-plane motion equal mount growth, γ·f ≈ α_h·L, which is critical for outdoor, automotive and space cameras. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：N-BK7：α = 7.1 ppm/K、相對 dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K（e 線）、n_e − 1 = 0.5187，γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K；F2：8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: N-BK7: α = 7.1 ppm/K, relative dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K (e-line), n_e − 1 = 0.5187, so γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K; F2: 8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K.","failure":"常見誤解：「玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-05-k1","title":"熱離焦與光熱係數","titleEn":"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient","text":"溫度同時改變折射率（dn/dT）與鏡片尺寸（膨脹係數 α），薄透鏡在空氣中的焦距變化率為 (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1)，稱為光熱係數。型錄的 dn/dT 是相對於空氣的值，SCHOTT 另以 G = α(n − 1) + dn/dT 表示玻璃的熱光常數。","textEn":"Temperature changes both the refractive index (dn/dT) and the lens dimensions (expansion coefficient α), and for a thin lens in air the focal-length change rate is (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1), the opto-thermal coefficient. Catalogue dn/dT values are relative to air, and SCHOTT also expresses the thermo-optical constant as G = α(n − 1) + dn/dT.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱離焦與光熱係數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient\" is correct?","options":["玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。","溫度同時改變折射率（dn/dT）與鏡片尺寸（膨脹係數 α），薄透鏡在空氣中的焦距變化率為 (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1)，稱為光熱係數。"],"optionsEn":["Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.","Temperature changes both the refractive index (dn/dT) and the lens dimensions (expansion coefficient α), and for a thin lens in air the focal-length change rate is (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1), the opto-thermal coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度同時改變折射率（dn/dT）與鏡片尺寸（膨脹係數 α），薄透鏡在空氣中的焦距變化率為 (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1)，稱為光熱係數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Temperature changes both the refractive index (dn/dT) and the lens dimensions (expansion coefficient α), and for a thin lens in air the focal-length change rate is (1/f)·df/dT = α − (dn/dT)/(n − 1), the opto-thermal coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":17},{"id":"a405-v12-06","title":"熱離焦與光熱係數：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：N-BK7：α = 7.1 ppm/K、相對 dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K（e 線）、n_e − 1 = 0.5187，γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K；F2：8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K。雙合權重 2.308 與 −1.308，γ = 2.308 × 1.32 − 1.308 × 1.15 ≈ 1.53 ppm/K。f = 100 mm、ΔT = 40 K：焦距伸長 6.1 µm；鋁鏡筒 100 mm × 23.6 ppm/K × 40 K = 94.4 µm，失配 88 µm，是 f/4 景深 ±2λN² = ±17.6 µm 的 5 倍；改用 Invar（1.2 ppm/K）隔圈伸長 4.8 µm，殘差僅 1.3 µm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: N-BK7: α = 7.1 ppm/K, relative dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K (e-line), n_e − 1 = 0.5187, so γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K; F2: 8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K. With doublet weights 2.308 and −1.308, γ = 2.308 × 1.32 − 1.308 × 1.15 ≈ 1.53 ppm/K. For f = 100 mm and ΔT = 40 K the focal length grows 6.1 µm, while an aluminium barrel grows 100 mm × 23.6 ppm/K × 40 K = 94.4 µm, a mismatch of 88 µm, five times the f/4 depth of focus ±2λN² = ±17.6 µm; an Invar spacer (1.2 ppm/K) grows 4.8 µm, leaving only 1.3 µm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：把鏡頭與感測器裝在溫控箱中，於 −20、20、60 °C 各浸泡到熱平衡後量穿焦 MTF 求最佳焦距，算出 Δz/ΔT 與模型比較；另以千分錶或干涉測長單獨量鏡筒伸長，分離光學項與機構項；再做快速升溫測試，觀察徑向溫度梯度造成的暫態離焦與球差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mount lens and sensor in a thermal chamber, soak to equilibrium at −20, 20 and 60 °C, measure through-focus MTF to find best focus and compare the resulting Δz/ΔT with the model; measure barrel growth separately with a dial gauge or interferometric length measurement to separate optical and mechanical terms; then run a fast ramp to observe transient defocus and spherical aberration from radial temperature gradients.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"N-BK7：α = 7.1 ppm/K、相對 dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K（e 線）、n_e − 1 = 0.5187，γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K；F2：8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K。雙合權重 2.308 與 −1.308，γ = 2.308 × 1.32 − 1.308 × 1.15 ≈ 1.53 ppm/K。f = 100 mm、ΔT = 40 K：焦距伸長 6.1 µm；鋁鏡筒 100 mm × 23.6 ppm/K × 40 K = 94.4 µm，失配 88 µm，是 f/4 景深 ±2λN² = ±17.6 µm 的 5 倍；改用 Invar（1.2 ppm/K）隔圈伸長 4.8 µm，殘差僅 1.3 µm。","textEn":"N-BK7: α = 7.1 ppm/K, relative dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K (e-line), n_e − 1 = 0.5187, so γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K; F2: 8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K. With doublet weights 2.308 and −1.308, γ = 2.308 × 1.32 − 1.308 × 1.15 ≈ 1.53 ppm/K. For f = 100 mm and ΔT = 40 K the focal length grows 6.1 µm, while an aluminium barrel grows 100 mm × 23.6 ppm/K × 40 K = 94.4 µm, a mismatch of 88 µm, five times the f/4 depth of focus ±2λN² = ±17.6 µm; an Invar spacer (1.2 ppm/K) grows 4.8 µm, leaving only 1.3 µm.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱離焦與光熱係數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient\", which statement holds?","options":["N-BK7：α = 7.1 ppm/K、相對 dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K（e 線）、n_e − 1 = 0.5187，γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K。","只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。","只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。"],"optionsEn":["N-BK7: α = 7.1 ppm/K, relative dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K (e-line), n_e − 1 = 0.5187, so γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K; F2: 8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K.","If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp.","Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear."],"answer":0,"explanation":"N-BK7：α = 7.1 ppm/K、相對 dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K（e 線）、n_e − 1 = 0.5187，γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K；F2：8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"N-BK7: α = 7.1 ppm/K, relative dn/dT = 3.0 ppm/K (e-line), n_e − 1 = 0.5187, so γ = 7.1 − 5.78 = 1.32 ppm/K; F2: 8.2 − 4.4/0.6241 = 1.15 ppm/K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":18},{"id":"a405-v12-07","title":"熱離焦與光熱係數：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"把鏡頭與感測器裝在溫控箱中，於 −20、20、60 °C 各浸泡到熱平衡後量穿焦 MTF 求最佳焦距，算出 Δz/ΔT 與模型比較；另以千分錶或干涉測長單獨量鏡筒伸長，分離光學項與機構項；再做快速升溫測試，觀察徑向溫度梯度造成的暫態離焦與球差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mount lens and sensor in a thermal chamber, soak to equilibrium at −20, 20 and 60 °C, measure through-focus MTF to find best focus and compare the resulting Δz/ΔT with the model; measure barrel growth separately with a dial gauge or interferometric length measurement to separate optical and mechanical terms; then run a fast ramp to observe transient defocus and spherical aberration from radial temperature gradients. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：鋁鏡筒在低溫收縮壓迫玻璃，產生應力雙折射與像散，嚴重時崩邊或破裂；黏著劑在高溫蠕變，鏡片位置不回復；溫度快速變化時徑向梯度造成暫態離焦，影像在數分鐘內忽清忽糊。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: An aluminium barrel shrinking at low temperature squeezes the glass, causing stress birefringence and astigmatism and in severe cases edge chipping or fracture; adhesive creeps at high temperature so the lens does not return to position; rapid temperature change creates radial gradients and transient defocus, so the image drifts in and out of focus for minutes.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把鏡頭與感測器裝在溫控箱中，於 −20、20、60 °C 各浸泡到熱平衡後量穿焦 MTF 求最佳焦距，算出 Δz/ΔT 與模型比較；另以千分錶或干涉測長單獨量鏡筒伸長，分離光學項與機構項；再做快速升溫測試，觀察徑向溫度梯度造成的暫態離焦與球差。","textEn":"Mount lens and sensor in a thermal chamber, soak to equilibrium at −20, 20 and 60 °C, measure through-focus MTF to find best focus and compare the resulting Δz/ΔT with the model; measure barrel growth separately with a dial gauge or interferometric length measurement to separate optical and mechanical terms; then run a fast ramp to observe transient defocus and spherical aberration from radial temperature gradients.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱離焦與光熱係數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","把鏡頭與感測器裝在溫控箱中，於 −20、20、60 °C 各浸泡到熱平衡後量穿焦 MTF 求最佳焦距，算出 Δz/ΔT 與模型比較。","量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Mount lens and sensor in a thermal chamber, soak to equilibrium at −20, 20 and 60 °C, measure through-focus MTF to find best focus and compare the resulting Δz/ΔT with the model.","A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把鏡頭與感測器裝在溫控箱中，於 −20、20、60 °C 各浸泡到熱平衡後量穿焦 MTF 求最佳焦距，算出 Δz/ΔT 與模型比較；另以千分錶或干涉測長單獨量鏡筒伸長，分離光學項與機構項；再做快速升溫測試，觀察徑向溫度梯度造成的暫態離焦與球差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mount lens and sensor in a thermal chamber, soak to equilibrium at −20, 20 and 60 °C, measure through-focus MTF to find best focus and compare the resulting Δz/ΔT with the model; measure barrel growth separately with a dial gauge or interferometric length measurement to separate optical and mechanical terms; then run a fast ramp to observe transient defocus and spherical aberration from radial temperature gradients. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":19},{"id":"a405-v12-08","title":"熱離焦與光熱係數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「熱光係數與鏡筒膨脹」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Thermo-optic coefficient and barrel expansion” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"鋁鏡筒在低溫收縮壓迫玻璃，產生應力雙折射與像散，嚴重時崩邊或破裂；黏著劑在高溫蠕變，鏡片位置不回復；溫度快速變化時徑向梯度造成暫態離焦，影像在數分鐘內忽清忽糊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"An aluminium barrel shrinking at low temperature squeezes the glass, causing stress birefringence and astigmatism and in severe cases edge chipping or fracture; adhesive creeps at high temperature so the lens does not return to position; rapid temperature change creates radial gradients and transient defocus, so the image drifts in and out of focus for minutes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：無熱化設計要讓像面移動與機構伸長相等，即 γ·f ≈ α_h·L，這對戶外相機、車載與太空光學尤其關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Athermal design makes image-plane motion equal mount growth, γ·f ≈ α_h·L, which is critical for outdoor, automotive and space cameras.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鋁鏡筒在低溫收縮壓迫玻璃，產生應力雙折射與像散，嚴重時崩邊或破裂；黏著劑在高溫蠕變，鏡片位置不回復；溫度快速變化時徑向梯度造成暫態離焦，影像在數分鐘內忽清忽糊。","textEn":"An aluminium barrel shrinking at low temperature squeezes the glass, causing stress birefringence and astigmatism and in severe cases edge chipping or fracture; adhesive creeps at high temperature so the lens does not return to position; rapid temperature change creates radial gradients and transient defocus, so the image drifts in and out of focus for minutes.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱離焦與光熱係數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal defocus and the opto-thermal coefficient\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。","鋁鏡筒在低溫收縮壓迫玻璃，產生應力雙折射與像散，嚴重時崩邊或破裂；黏著劑在高溫蠕變，鏡片位置不回復；溫度快速變化時徑向梯度造成暫態離焦，影像在數分鐘內忽清忽糊。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.","An aluminium barrel shrinking at low temperature squeezes the glass, causing stress birefringence and astigmatism and in severe cases edge chipping or fracture."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋁鏡筒在低溫收縮壓迫玻璃，產生應力雙折射與像散，嚴重時崩邊或破裂；黏著劑在高溫蠕變，鏡片位置不回復；溫度快速變化時徑向梯度造成暫態離焦，影像在數分鐘內忽清忽糊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An aluminium barrel shrinking at low temperature squeezes the glass, causing stress birefringence and astigmatism and in severe cases edge chipping or fracture; adhesive creeps at high temperature so the lens does not return to position; rapid temperature change creates radial gradients and transient defocus, so the image drifts in and out of focus for minutes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":20}],"order":4},{"id":"a405-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨」與「生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs\" and \"Production centring, edging and cementing\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v12-09","title":"膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「膠合界面與空氣間隔」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cemented interface and air gap” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"膠合雙合透鏡兩片內曲率相同，只有三個面，界面以折射率接近的膠填滿，反射極低、對位穩固、鬼影路徑少；但只有三個曲率，用來定光焦度、消色差與彎曲修正球差後就沒有自由度處理大孔徑下的色球差與彗差。膠層還要承受兩種玻璃膨脹係數差造成的剪應變，限制了口徑與玻璃組合，紫外與高功率雷射下膠也會吸收老化。空氣間隔版有四個曲率加一個間距，可在兩個波長同時修正球差並控制彗差，適合更快的 f 數與更大口徑，代價是間距與偏心公差、多兩個需鍍膜的空氣界面，以及間距誤差直接改變焦距。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「膠合界面與空氣間隔」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A cemented doublet has equal inner radii and only three surfaces; the interface is filled with index-matched cement, so reflection is very low, alignment is robust and there are few ghost paths. But three curvatures are used up setting power, correcting colour and bending for spherical aberration, leaving no freedom for spherochromatism and coma at large aperture. The cement layer must also absorb the shear strain from the two glasses' expansion mismatch, which limits diameter and glass pairs, and cement absorbs and ages under UV and high-power lasers. An air-spaced version has four curvatures plus a gap, so it can correct spherical aberration at two wavelengths and control coma, suiting faster f-numbers and larger apertures, at the cost of spacing and decentre tolerances, two more air–glass surfaces to coat, and a gap error that changes focal length directly. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Cemented interface and air gap”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：間距敏感度：φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂，∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Gap sensitivity: φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂, so ∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂.","failure":"常見誤解：「空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「膠合界面與空氣間隔」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Cemented interface and air gap”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-09-k1","title":"膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨","titleEn":"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs","text":"膠合雙合透鏡兩片內曲率相同，只有三個面，界面以折射率接近的膠填滿，反射極低、對位穩固、鬼影路徑少；但只有三個曲率，用來定光焦度、消色差與彎曲修正球差後就沒有自由度處理大孔徑下的色球差與彗差。膠層還要承受兩種玻璃膨脹係數差造成的剪應變，限制了口徑與玻璃組合，紫外與高功率雷射下膠也會吸收老化。","textEn":"A cemented doublet has equal inner radii and only three surfaces; the interface is filled with index-matched cement, so reflection is very low, alignment is robust and there are few ghost paths. But three curvatures are used up setting power, correcting colour and bending for spherical aberration, leaving no freedom for spherochromatism and coma at large aperture.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs\" is correct?","options":["膠合雙合透鏡兩片內曲率相同，只有三個面，界面以折射率接近的膠填滿，反射極低、對位穩固、鬼影路徑少。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。","鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。"],"optionsEn":["A cemented doublet has equal inner radii and only three surfaces.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.","A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred."],"answer":0,"explanation":"膠合雙合透鏡兩片內曲率相同，只有三個面，界面以折射率接近的膠填滿，反射極低、對位穩固、鬼影路徑少；但只有三個曲率，用來定光焦度、消色差與彎曲修正球差後就沒有自由度處理大孔徑下的色球差與彗差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A cemented doublet has equal inner radii and only three surfaces; the interface is filled with index-matched cement, so reflection is very low, alignment is robust and there are few ghost paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":21},{"id":"a405-v12-10","title":"膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨：定量估算","titleEn":"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「膠合界面與空氣間隔」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cemented interface and air gap” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：間距敏感度：φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂，∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 時 f₁ = 43.3 mm、f₂ = −76.4 mm，−φ₁φ₂ = 3.02×10⁻⁴ mm⁻²，Δf = −f²·Δφ ≈ −3.02·Δd，隔圈差 10 µm 焦距就變 −30 µm。膠合界面反射：BK7/膠 (n = 1.56) 為 2.0×10⁻⁴、膠/F2 為 3.6×10⁻⁴，未鍍膜空氣界面約 4.3%。Ø50 mm 在 ΔT = 40 K 時邊緣錯位：BK7/F2（Δα = 1.1 ppm/K）1.1 µm，15 µm 膠層剪應變 0.07；CaF₂（18.9 ppm/K）配約 8 ppm/K 的火石 10.9 µm，剪應變 0.73。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Gap sensitivity: φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂, so ∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂. For N-BK7/F2 at f = 100 mm, f₁ = 43.3 mm and f₂ = −76.4 mm give −φ₁φ₂ = 3.02×10⁻⁴ mm⁻² and Δf = −f²·Δφ ≈ −3.02·Δd, so a 10 µm spacer error moves focal length by −30 µm. Cement-interface reflectance: BK7 to cement (n = 1.56) 2.0×10⁻⁴ and cement to F2 3.6×10⁻⁴, against about 4.3% for an uncoated air surface. Edge mismatch for Ø50 mm over ΔT = 40 K: BK7/F2 (Δα = 1.1 ppm/K) 1.1 µm, a 0.07 shear strain in a 15 µm cement layer; CaF₂ (18.9 ppm/K) against a flint near 8 ppm/K gives 10.9 µm and 0.73. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：空氣間隔版在組裝時以焦距量測台量有效焦距對隔圈厚度的變化，驗證 −3 µm/µm 的敏感度；以干涉儀或波前感測器在兩個波長量球差，確認色球差被修正；膠合版做 −40 到 +70 °C 熱循環，之後以斜射光檢查邊緣是否出現牛頓環或銀白脫膠，並以偏光儀檢查應力雙折射。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: For the air-spaced version measure effective focal length against spacer thickness on a focal-length bench during assembly to confirm the −3 µm/µm sensitivity, and measure spherical aberration at two wavelengths with an interferometer or wavefront sensor to confirm spherochromatism is corrected; cycle the cemented version from −40 to +70 °C, then inspect the edge under oblique light for Newton rings or silvery delamination and check stress birefringence with a polariscope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"間距敏感度：φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂，∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 時 f₁ = 43.3 mm、f₂ = −76.4 mm，−φ₁φ₂ = 3.02×10⁻⁴ mm⁻²，Δf = −f²·Δφ ≈ −3.02·Δd，隔圈差 10 µm 焦距就變 −30 µm。膠合界面反射：BK7/膠 (n = 1.56) 為 2.0×10⁻⁴、膠/F2 為 3.6×10⁻⁴，未鍍膜空氣界面約 4.3%。Ø50 mm 在 ΔT = 40 K 時邊緣錯位：BK7/F2（Δα = 1.1 ppm/K）1.1 µm，15 µm 膠層剪應變 0.07；CaF₂（18.9 ppm/K）配約 8 ppm/K 的火石 10.9 µm，剪應變 0.73。","textEn":"Gap sensitivity: φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂, so ∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂. For N-BK7/F2 at f = 100 mm, f₁ = 43.3 mm and f₂ = −76.4 mm give −φ₁φ₂ = 3.02×10⁻⁴ mm⁻² and Δf = −f²·Δφ ≈ −3.02·Δd, so a 10 µm spacer error moves focal length by −30 µm. Cement-interface reflectance: BK7 to cement (n = 1.56) 2.0×10⁻⁴ and cement to F2 3.6×10⁻⁴, against about 4.3% for an uncoated air surface. Edge mismatch for Ø50 mm over ΔT = 40 K: BK7/F2 (Δα = 1.1 ppm/K) 1.1 µm, a 0.07 shear strain in a 15 µm cement layer; CaF₂ (18.9 ppm/K) against a flint near 8 ppm/K gives 10.9 µm and 0.73.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs\", which statement holds?","options":["HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。","間距敏感度：φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂，∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂。","量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。"],"optionsEn":["A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.","Gap sensitivity: φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂, so ∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂.","A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released."],"answer":1,"explanation":"間距敏感度：φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂，∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Gap sensitivity: φ = φ₁ + φ₂ − dφ₁φ₂, so ∂φ/∂d = −φ₁φ₂. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":22},{"id":"a405-v12-11","title":"膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「膠合界面與空氣間隔」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Cemented interface and air gap” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"空氣間隔版在組裝時以焦距量測台量有效焦距對隔圈厚度的變化，驗證 −3 µm/µm 的敏感度；以干涉儀或波前感測器在兩個波長量球差，確認色球差被修正；膠合版做 −40 到 +70 °C 熱循環，之後以斜射光檢查邊緣是否出現牛頓環或銀白脫膠，並以偏光儀檢查應力雙折射。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"For the air-spaced version measure effective focal length against spacer thickness on a focal-length bench during assembly to confirm the −3 µm/µm sensitivity, and measure spherical aberration at two wavelengths with an interferometer or wavefront sensor to confirm spherochromatism is corrected; cycle the cemented version from −40 to +70 °C, then inspect the edge under oblique light for Newton rings or silvery delamination and check stress birefringence with a polariscope. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：膨脹係數差大的膠合組在低溫脫膠，邊緣出現牛頓環與銀白反光，波前與穿透率同時劣化；空氣間隔版的隔圈鬆動，受衝擊後間距與偏心改變，焦距與軸上彗差漂移；膠層在紫外光下黃化，藍端穿透率下降。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A cemented pair with a large expansion mismatch delaminates in the cold, showing Newton rings and silvery reflections at the edge as wavefront and transmission degrade together; a loose spacer in an air-spaced doublet lets gap and decentre change after shock so focal length and on-axis coma drift; cement yellows under UV and blue transmission falls.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"空氣間隔版在組裝時以焦距量測台量有效焦距對隔圈厚度的變化，驗證 −3 µm/µm 的敏感度；以干涉儀或波前感測器在兩個波長量球差，確認色球差被修正；膠合版做 −40 到 +70 °C 熱循環，之後以斜射光檢查邊緣是否出現牛頓環或銀白脫膠，並以偏光儀檢查應力雙折射。","textEn":"For the air-spaced version measure effective focal length against spacer thickness on a focal-length bench during assembly to confirm the −3 µm/µm sensitivity, and measure spherical aberration at two wavelengths with an interferometer or wavefront sensor to confirm spherochromatism is corrected; cycle the cemented version from −40 to +70 °C, then inspect the edge under oblique light for Newton rings or silvery delamination and check stress birefringence with a polariscope.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","空氣間隔版在組裝時以焦距量測台量有效焦距對隔圈厚度的變化，驗證 −3 µm/µm 的敏感度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","For the air-spaced version measure effective focal length against spacer thickness on a focal-length bench during assembly to confirm the −3 µm/µm sensitivity, and measure spherical aberration at two wavelengths with an interferometer or wavefront sensor to confirm spherochromatism is corrected."],"answer":2,"explanation":"空氣間隔版在組裝時以焦距量測台量有效焦距對隔圈厚度的變化，驗證 −3 µm/µm 的敏感度；以干涉儀或波前感測器在兩個波長量球差，確認色球差被修正；膠合版做 −40 到 +70 °C 熱循環，之後以斜射光檢查邊緣是否出現牛頓環或銀白脫膠，並以偏光儀檢查應力雙折射。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"For the air-spaced version measure effective focal length against spacer thickness on a focal-length bench during assembly to confirm the −3 µm/µm sensitivity, and measure spherical aberration at two wavelengths with an interferometer or wavefront sensor to confirm spherochromatism is corrected; cycle the cemented version from −40 to +70 °C, then inspect the edge under oblique light for Newton rings or silvery delamination and check stress birefringence with a polariscope. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":23},{"id":"a405-v12-12","title":"膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「膠合界面與空氣間隔」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Cemented interface and air gap” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"膨脹係數差大的膠合組在低溫脫膠，邊緣出現牛頓環與銀白反光，波前與穿透率同時劣化；空氣間隔版的隔圈鬆動，受衝擊後間距與偏心改變，焦距與軸上彗差漂移；膠層在紫外光下黃化，藍端穿透率下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A cemented pair with a large expansion mismatch delaminates in the cold, showing Newton rings and silvery reflections at the edge as wavefront and transmission degrade together; a loose spacer in an air-spaced doublet lets gap and decentre change after shock so focal length and on-axis coma drift; cement yellows under UV and blue transmission falls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：空氣間隔版有四個曲率加一個間距，可在兩個波長同時修正球差並控制彗差，適合更快的 f 數與更大口徑，代價是間距與偏心公差、多兩個需鍍膜的空氣界面，以及間距誤差直接改變焦距。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An air-spaced version has four curvatures plus a gap, so it can correct spherical aberration at two wavelengths and control coma, suiting faster f-numbers and larger apertures, at the cost of spacing and decentre tolerances, two more air–glass surfaces to coat, and a gap error that changes focal length directly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"膨脹係數差大的膠合組在低溫脫膠，邊緣出現牛頓環與銀白反光，波前與穿透率同時劣化；空氣間隔版的隔圈鬆動，受衝擊後間距與偏心改變，焦距與軸上彗差漂移；膠層在紫外光下黃化，藍端穿透率下降。","textEn":"A cemented pair with a large expansion mismatch delaminates in the cold, showing Newton rings and silvery reflections at the edge as wavefront and transmission degrade together; a loose spacer in an air-spaced doublet lets gap and decentre change after shock so focal length and on-axis coma drift; cement yellows under UV and blue transmission falls.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膠合與空氣間隔雙合透鏡的取捨」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cemented versus air-spaced doublet trade-offs\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["膨脹係數差大的膠合組在低溫脫膠，邊緣出現牛頓環與銀白反光，波前與穿透率同時劣化。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。"],"optionsEn":["A cemented pair with a large expansion mismatch delaminates in the cold, showing Newton rings and silvery reflections at the edge as wavefront and transmission degrade together.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred."],"answer":0,"explanation":"膨脹係數差大的膠合組在低溫脫膠，邊緣出現牛頓環與銀白反光，波前與穿透率同時劣化；空氣間隔版的隔圈鬆動，受衝擊後間距與偏心改變，焦距與軸上彗差漂移；膠層在紫外光下黃化，藍端穿透率下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A cemented pair with a large expansion mismatch delaminates in the cold, showing Newton rings and silvery reflections at the edge as wavefront and transmission degrade together; a loose spacer in an air-spaced doublet lets gap and decentre change after shock so focal length and on-axis coma drift; cement yellows under UV and blue transmission falls. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":24},{"id":"a405-v12-13","title":"生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Production centring, edging and cementing: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「定心磨邊與膠合治具」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"拋光完成的鏡片，其光軸（兩曲率中心的連線）通常不與外徑同軸。定心磨邊時把鏡片裝在主軸上，先讓光軸對準旋轉軸：曲率夠大的鏡片可用鐘形夾頭自動定心，曲率淺的彎月或弱負透鏡夾持角不足，必須以自準直儀觀察反射像隨旋轉的晃動做光學定心，再把外徑磨成與光軸同心，殘差以楔角或邊厚差表示。膠合時兩片在 10 到 20 µm 的膠層上相對移動，同時觀察各面反射像使它們同心，再以紫外或加熱固化；膠的固化收縮會拉動鏡片，所以固化後必須再量一次整組的定心。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「定心磨邊與膠合治具」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A polished element's optical axis, the line through its two centres of curvature, generally does not coincide with its outer diameter. In centring and edging the element sits on a spindle and its optical axis is first aligned to the rotation axis: strongly curved elements self-centre in bell chucks, while shallow menisci and weak negative lenses lack clamping angle and must be centred optically by watching the reflected image wobble in an autocollimator; the edge is then ground concentric with the optical axis, and the residual is stated as wedge or edge-thickness variation. In cementing the two elements are slid on a 10 to 20 µm cement layer while the reflected images of all surfaces are made concentric, then cured by UV or heat; cure shrinkage pulls the elements, so the centring of the finished pair must be measured again after cure. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：半徑 R = 60 mm 的面偏心 c = 10 µm，傾斜 ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad（0.57′）；Ø25 mm 的邊厚差 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm；光束偏折 (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″，在 f = 100 mm 像面造成 8.6 µm 的視軸偏移，約 2.5 個 3.45 µm 像素。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A surface of radius R = 60 mm decentred by c = 10 µm tilts by ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad (0.57′); over Ø25 mm the edge-thickness variation is 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm; the beam deviates by (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″, shifting the boresight by 8.6 µm at f = 100 mm, about 2.5 pixels of 3.45 µm.","failure":"常見誤解：「鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「定心磨邊與膠合治具」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-13-k1","title":"生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序","titleEn":"Production centring, edging and cementing","text":"拋光完成的鏡片，其光軸（兩曲率中心的連線）通常不與外徑同軸。定心磨邊時把鏡片裝在主軸上，先讓光軸對準旋轉軸：曲率夠大的鏡片可用鐘形夾頭自動定心，曲率淺的彎月或弱負透鏡夾持角不足，必須以自準直儀觀察反射像隨旋轉的晃動做光學定心，再把外徑磨成與光軸同心，殘差以楔角或邊厚差表示。","textEn":"A polished element's optical axis, the line through its two centres of curvature, generally does not coincide with its outer diameter. In centring and edging the element sits on a spindle and its optical axis is first aligned to the rotation axis: strongly curved elements self-centre in bell chucks, while shallow menisci and weak negative lenses lack clamping angle and must be centred optically by watching the reflected image wobble in an autocollimator; the edge is then ground concentric with the optical axis, and the residual is stated as wedge or edge-thickness variation.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Production centring, edging and cementing\" is correct?","options":["鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。","拋光完成的鏡片，其光軸（兩曲率中心的連線）通常不與外徑同軸。","只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。"],"optionsEn":["A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.","A polished element's optical axis, the line through its two centres of curvature, generally does not coincide with its outer diameter.","If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拋光完成的鏡片，其光軸（兩曲率中心的連線）通常不與外徑同軸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A polished element's optical axis, the line through its two centres of curvature, generally does not coincide with its outer diameter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":25},{"id":"a405-v12-14","title":"生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序：定量估算","titleEn":"Production centring, edging and cementing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「定心磨邊與膠合治具」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：半徑 R = 60 mm 的面偏心 c = 10 µm，傾斜 ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad（0.57′）；Ø25 mm 的邊厚差 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm；光束偏折 (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″，在 f = 100 mm 像面造成 8.6 µm 的視軸偏移，約 2.5 個 3.45 µm 像素。曲率中心自準直時，偏心 c 在主軸旋轉下表現為半徑 2c = 20 µm 的圓。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A surface of radius R = 60 mm decentred by c = 10 µm tilts by ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad (0.57′); over Ø25 mm the edge-thickness variation is 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm; the beam deviates by (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″, shifting the boresight by 8.6 µm at f = 100 mm, about 2.5 pixels of 3.45 µm. In centre-of-curvature autocollimation the decentre c appears as a circle of radius 2c = 20 µm as the spindle turns. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：單片以迴轉台與千分錶量邊厚差，或以定心儀量各面曲率中心相對基準軸的偏移；膠合固化後用多面定心量測儀透過所有面量整組偏心，並以平行光管比較光學視軸與機械軸；把每片的偏心、邊厚差與固化前後差值記錄到序號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure each element's edge-thickness variation with a rotary table and dial gauge, or the offset of each surface's centre of curvature from the datum axis with a centring instrument; after cure measure the pair's decentration through all surfaces with a multi-surface centring instrument and compare optical boresight with the mechanical axis using a collimator; log each element's decentre, edge variation and pre- and post-cure difference against its serial number.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"半徑 R = 60 mm 的面偏心 c = 10 µm，傾斜 ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad（0.57′）；Ø25 mm 的邊厚差 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm；光束偏折 (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″，在 f = 100 mm 像面造成 8.6 µm 的視軸偏移，約 2.5 個 3.45 µm 像素。曲率中心自準直時，偏心 c 在主軸旋轉下表現為半徑 2c = 20 µm 的圓。","textEn":"A surface of radius R = 60 mm decentred by c = 10 µm tilts by ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad (0.57′); over Ø25 mm the edge-thickness variation is 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm; the beam deviates by (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″, shifting the boresight by 8.6 µm at f = 100 mm, about 2.5 pixels of 3.45 µm. In centre-of-curvature autocollimation the decentre c appears as a circle of radius 2c = 20 µm as the spindle turns.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Production centring, edging and cementing\", which statement holds?","options":["只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。","只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","半徑 R = 60 mm 的面偏心 c = 10 µm，傾斜 ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad（0.57′）。"],"optionsEn":["Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear.","A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","A surface of radius R = 60 mm decentred by c = 10 µm tilts by ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad (0.57′)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"半徑 R = 60 mm 的面偏心 c = 10 µm，傾斜 ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad（0.57′）；Ø25 mm 的邊厚差 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm；光束偏折 (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″，在 f = 100 mm 像面造成 8.6 µm 的視軸偏移，約 2.5 個 3.45 µm 像素。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A surface of radius R = 60 mm decentred by c = 10 µm tilts by ε = c/R = 0.167 mrad (0.57′); over Ø25 mm the edge-thickness variation is 25 mm × 0.167 mrad = 4.2 µm; the beam deviates by (n − 1)ε = 0.517 × 0.167 mrad = 86 µrad = 17.8″, shifting the boresight by 8.6 µm at f = 100 mm, about 2.5 pixels of 3.45 µm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":26},{"id":"a405-v12-15","title":"生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Production centring, edging and cementing: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「定心磨邊與膠合治具」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"單片以迴轉台與千分錶量邊厚差，或以定心儀量各面曲率中心相對基準軸的偏移；膠合固化後用多面定心量測儀透過所有面量整組偏心，並以平行光管比較光學視軸與機械軸；把每片的偏心、邊厚差與固化前後差值記錄到序號。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure each element's edge-thickness variation with a rotary table and dial gauge, or the offset of each surface's centre of curvature from the datum axis with a centring instrument; after cure measure the pair's decentration through all surfaces with a multi-surface centring instrument and compare optical boresight with the mechanical axis using a collimator; log each element's decentre, edge variation and pre- and post-cure difference against its serial number. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：膠層厚度不均使固化收縮不對稱，濕膠時對準良好的組件固化後出現楔角；膠中氣泡或灰塵成為散射點；磨邊崩角成為應力集中處，熱循環時裂紋由此擴展；邊厚差超規使軸上出現彗差，影像清晰度在視場兩側不對稱。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven cement thickness makes cure shrinkage asymmetric, so a pair aligned perfectly while wet acquires a wedge after cure; bubbles or dust in the cement become scatter points; edge chips from edging concentrate stress and cracks grow from them during thermal cycling; out-of-spec edge variation puts coma on axis and makes sharpness asymmetric across the field.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"單片以迴轉台與千分錶量邊厚差，或以定心儀量各面曲率中心相對基準軸的偏移；膠合固化後用多面定心量測儀透過所有面量整組偏心，並以平行光管比較光學視軸與機械軸；把每片的偏心、邊厚差與固化前後差值記錄到序號。","textEn":"Measure each element's edge-thickness variation with a rotary table and dial gauge, or the offset of each surface's centre of curvature from the datum axis with a centring instrument; after cure measure the pair's decentration through all surfaces with a multi-surface centring instrument and compare optical boresight with the mechanical axis using a collimator; log each element's decentre, edge variation and pre- and post-cure difference against its serial number.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Production centring, edging and cementing\"?","options":["單片以迴轉台與千分錶量邊厚差，或以定心儀量各面曲率中心相對基準軸的偏移。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。"],"optionsEn":["Measure each element's edge-thickness variation with a rotary table and dial gauge, or the offset of each surface's centre of curvature from the datum axis with a centring instrument.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單片以迴轉台與千分錶量邊厚差，或以定心儀量各面曲率中心相對基準軸的偏移；膠合固化後用多面定心量測儀透過所有面量整組偏心，並以平行光管比較光學視軸與機械軸；把每片的偏心、邊厚差與固化前後差值記錄到序號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure each element's edge-thickness variation with a rotary table and dial gauge, or the offset of each surface's centre of curvature from the datum axis with a centring instrument; after cure measure the pair's decentration through all surfaces with a multi-surface centring instrument and compare optical boresight with the mechanical axis using a collimator; log each element's decentre, edge variation and pre- and post-cure difference against its serial number. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":27},{"id":"a405-v12-16","title":"生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Production centring, edging and cementing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「定心磨邊與膠合治具」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Centring, edging and cementing fixtures” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"膠層厚度不均使固化收縮不對稱，濕膠時對準良好的組件固化後出現楔角；膠中氣泡或灰塵成為散射點；磨邊崩角成為應力集中處，熱循環時裂紋由此擴展；邊厚差超規使軸上出現彗差，影像清晰度在視場兩側不對稱。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Uneven cement thickness makes cure shrinkage asymmetric, so a pair aligned perfectly while wet acquires a wedge after cure; bubbles or dust in the cement become scatter points; edge chips from edging concentrate stress and cracks grow from them during thermal cycling; out-of-spec edge variation puts coma on axis and makes sharpness asymmetric across the field. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：膠合時兩片在 10 到 20 µm 的膠層上相對移動，同時觀察各面反射像使它們同心，再以紫外或加熱固化；膠的固化收縮會拉動鏡片，所以固化後必須再量一次整組的定心。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In cementing the two elements are slid on a 10 to 20 µm cement layer while the reflected images of all surfaces are made concentric, then cured by UV or heat; cure shrinkage pulls the elements, so the centring of the finished pair must be measured again after cure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"膠層厚度不均使固化收縮不對稱，濕膠時對準良好的組件固化後出現楔角；膠中氣泡或灰塵成為散射點；磨邊崩角成為應力集中處，熱循環時裂紋由此擴展；邊厚差超規使軸上出現彗差，影像清晰度在視場兩側不對稱。","textEn":"Uneven cement thickness makes cure shrinkage asymmetric, so a pair aligned perfectly while wet acquires a wedge after cure; bubbles or dust in the cement become scatter points; edge chips from edging concentrate stress and cracks grow from them during thermal cycling; out-of-spec edge variation puts coma on axis and makes sharpness asymmetric across the field.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「生產定心、磨邊與膠合工序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Production centring, edging and cementing\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","膠層厚度不均使固化收縮不對稱，濕膠時對準良好的組件固化後出現楔角。","只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uneven cement thickness makes cure shrinkage asymmetric, so a pair aligned perfectly while wet acquires a wedge after cure.","If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp."],"answer":1,"explanation":"膠層厚度不均使固化收縮不對稱，濕膠時對準良好的組件固化後出現楔角；膠中氣泡或灰塵成為散射點；磨邊崩角成為應力集中處，熱循環時裂紋由此擴展；邊厚差超規使軸上出現彗差，影像清晰度在視場兩側不對稱。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven cement thickness makes cure shrinkage asymmetric, so a pair aligned perfectly while wet acquires a wedge after cure; bubbles or dust in the cement become scatter points; edge chips from edging concentrate stress and cracks grow from them during thermal cycling; out-of-spec edge variation puts coma on axis and makes sharpness asymmetric across the field. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":28}],"order":5},{"id":"a405-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準」與「干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria\" and \"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v12-17","title":"依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「感測器像素與 MTF」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sensor pixels and MTF” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"相機用的消色差透鏡要以感測器取樣來評判：像素間距 p 決定 Nyquist 頻率 ν_N = 1/(2p)，系統 MTF 等於鏡頭 MTF 乘像素孔徑的 sinc 響應；鏡頭在 f 數 N 的繞射截止頻率為 1/(λN)。殘餘的二級光譜就是隨波長變化的離焦，多色 MTF 要以感測器光譜響應加權；拜耳濾色片讓紅藍通道的取樣頻率再減半。因此規格應寫成在 Nyquist 或其一半、中心與邊緣的多色 MTF，並要求各色焦點散佈落在 ±2λN² 的像素尺度景深內。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「感測器像素與 MTF」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An achromat for a camera must be judged against sensor sampling: pixel pitch p sets the Nyquist frequency ν_N = 1/(2p), and system MTF is lens MTF times the sinc response of the pixel aperture, with the lens's diffraction cutoff at 1/(λN) for f-number N. Residual secondary spectrum is a wavelength-dependent defocus, so polychromatic MTF must be weighted by the sensor's spectral response, and a Bayer filter halves the sampling rate again for the red and blue channels. The specification should therefore state polychromatic MTF at Nyquist or half Nyquist at centre and edge, and require the colour focus spread to fall within the pixel-scale depth of focus ±2λN². Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Sensor pixels and MTF”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：p = 3.45 µm，ν_N = 145 lp/mm；f/4、0.55 µm 截止 455 lp/mm，繞射 MTF(145) ≈ 0.60，像素 sinc 0.64，未計像差已只剩 0.38。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: p = 3.45 µm gives ν_N = 145 lp/mm; at f/4 and 0.55 µm the cutoff is 455 lp/mm, diffraction MTF(145) ≈ 0.60 and pixel sinc 0.64, already 0.38 before aberrations.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「感測器像素與 MTF」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Sensor pixels and MTF”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-17-k1","title":"依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準","titleEn":"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria","text":"相機用的消色差透鏡要以感測器取樣來評判：像素間距 p 決定 Nyquist 頻率 ν_N = 1/(2p)，系統 MTF 等於鏡頭 MTF 乘像素孔徑的 sinc 響應；鏡頭在 f 數 N 的繞射截止頻率為 1/(λN)。殘餘的二級光譜就是隨波長變化的離焦，多色 MTF 要以感測器光譜響應加權；拜耳濾色片讓紅藍通道的取樣頻率再減半。","textEn":"An achromat for a camera must be judged against sensor sampling: pixel pitch p sets the Nyquist frequency ν_N = 1/(2p), and system MTF is lens MTF times the sinc response of the pixel aperture, with the lens's diffraction cutoff at 1/(λN) for f-number N. Residual secondary spectrum is a wavelength-dependent defocus, so polychromatic MTF must be weighted by the sensor's spectral response, and a Bayer filter halves the sampling rate again for the red and blue channels.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria\" is correct?","options":["只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。","HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。","相機用的消色差透鏡要以感測器取樣來評判：像素間距 p 決定 Nyquist 頻率 ν_N = 1/(2p)，系統 MTF 等於鏡頭 MTF 乘像素孔徑的 sinc 響應。"],"optionsEn":["If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp.","A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.","An achromat for a camera must be judged against sensor sampling: pixel pitch p sets the Nyquist frequency ν_N = 1/(2p), and system MTF is lens MTF times the sinc response of the pixel aperture, with the lens's diffraction cutoff at 1/(λN) for f-number N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相機用的消色差透鏡要以感測器取樣來評判：像素間距 p 決定 Nyquist 頻率 ν_N = 1/(2p)，系統 MTF 等於鏡頭 MTF 乘像素孔徑的 sinc 響應；鏡頭在 f 數 N 的繞射截止頻率為 1/(λN)。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An achromat for a camera must be judged against sensor sampling: pixel pitch p sets the Nyquist frequency ν_N = 1/(2p), and system MTF is lens MTF times the sinc response of the pixel aperture, with the lens's diffraction cutoff at 1/(λN) for f-number N. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":29},{"id":"a405-v12-18","title":"依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準：定量估算","titleEn":"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「感測器像素與 MTF」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sensor pixels and MTF” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：p = 3.45 µm，ν_N = 145 lp/mm；f/4、0.55 µm 截止 455 lp/mm，繞射 MTF(145) ≈ 0.60，像素 sinc 0.64，未計像差已只剩 0.38。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 對焦在 d 線時，C、F 離焦 50 µm，W₀₂₀ = Δz/(8N²λ) 分別為 0.60λ 與 0.80λ，Nyquist MTF 只剩 0.05 與 0.02；改用 N-FK51A/N-KZFS4 雙合，色焦差 14.2 µm，C、F 為 0.47 與 0.55。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: p = 3.45 µm gives ν_N = 145 lp/mm; at f/4 and 0.55 µm the cutoff is 455 lp/mm, diffraction MTF(145) ≈ 0.60 and pixel sinc 0.64, already 0.38 before aberrations. An N-BK7/F2 doublet at f = 100 mm focused on the d line leaves C and F 50 µm out, W₀₂₀ = Δz/(8N²λ) of 0.60λ and 0.80λ, so their Nyquist MTF falls to 0.05 and 0.02; an N-FK51A/N-KZFS4 doublet has a 14.2 µm colour spread and gives 0.47 and 0.55. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以斜邊法在實際感測器上量 MTF，分別取紅、綠、藍通道，或在 MTF 量測台上配窄帶濾光片逐波長量；每個波長做穿焦掃描求最佳焦點位置，直接量出色焦差並與 50 µm 或 14.2 µm 的設計值比較；量測頻率至少涵蓋 Nyquist 與其一半，並在中心與 70% 視場各量一次。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure MTF on the actual sensor by the slanted-edge method for the red, green and blue channels separately, or on an MTF bench with narrow-band filters wavelength by wavelength; run a through-focus scan per wavelength to locate best focus, measuring the colour focus spread directly against the 50 µm or 14.2 µm design value; cover at least Nyquist and half Nyquist, at the centre and at 70% field.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"p = 3.45 µm，ν_N = 145 lp/mm；f/4、0.55 µm 截止 455 lp/mm，繞射 MTF(145) ≈ 0.60，像素 sinc 0.64，未計像差已只剩 0.38。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 對焦在 d 線時，C、F 離焦 50 µm，W₀₂₀ = Δz/(8N²λ) 分別為 0.60λ 與 0.80λ，Nyquist MTF 只剩 0.05 與 0.02；改用 N-FK51A/N-KZFS4 雙合，色焦差 14.2 µm，C、F 為 0.47 與 0.55。","textEn":"p = 3.45 µm gives ν_N = 145 lp/mm; at f/4 and 0.55 µm the cutoff is 455 lp/mm, diffraction MTF(145) ≈ 0.60 and pixel sinc 0.64, already 0.38 before aberrations. An N-BK7/F2 doublet at f = 100 mm focused on the d line leaves C and F 50 µm out, W₀₂₀ = Δz/(8N²λ) of 0.60λ and 0.80λ, so their Nyquist MTF falls to 0.05 and 0.02; an N-FK51A/N-KZFS4 doublet has a 14.2 µm colour spread and gives 0.47 and 0.55.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria\", which statement holds?","options":["p = 3.45 µm，ν_N = 145 lp/mm。","量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。","玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。"],"optionsEn":["p = 3.45 µm gives ν_N = 145 lp/mm; at f/4 and 0.55 µm the cutoff is 455 lp/mm, diffraction MTF(145) ≈ 0.60 and pixel sinc 0.64, already 0.38 before aberrations.","A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released.","Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"p = 3.45 µm，ν_N = 145 lp/mm；f/4、0.55 µm 截止 455 lp/mm，繞射 MTF(145) ≈ 0.60，像素 sinc 0.64，未計像差已只剩 0.38。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"p = 3.45 µm gives ν_N = 145 lp/mm; at f/4 and 0.55 µm the cutoff is 455 lp/mm, diffraction MTF(145) ≈ 0.60 and pixel sinc 0.64, already 0.38 before aberrations. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":30},{"id":"a405-v12-19","title":"依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「感測器像素與 MTF」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Sensor pixels and MTF” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以斜邊法在實際感測器上量 MTF，分別取紅、綠、藍通道，或在 MTF 量測台上配窄帶濾光片逐波長量；每個波長做穿焦掃描求最佳焦點位置，直接量出色焦差並與 50 µm 或 14.2 µm 的設計值比較；量測頻率至少涵蓋 Nyquist 與其一半，並在中心與 70% 視場各量一次。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure MTF on the actual sensor by the slanted-edge method for the red, green and blue channels separately, or on an MTF bench with narrow-band filters wavelength by wavelength; run a through-focus scan per wavelength to locate best focus, measuring the colour focus spread directly against the 50 µm or 14.2 µm design value; cover at least Nyquist and half Nyquist, at the centre and at 70% field. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：以 N-BK7/F2 雙合搭配 3.45 µm 像素與 f/4，紅藍通道模糊，高對比邊緣出現紫邊；若規格只寫 546 nm 單色 MTF，鏡頭在檢驗台上全數合格，裝上相機後彩色影像卻不合格，責任在規格而非製造。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Pairing an N-BK7/F2 doublet with 3.45 µm pixels at f/4 blurs the red and blue channels and puts purple fringes on high-contrast edges; a specification written only as 546 nm monochromatic MTF lets every lens pass on the bench while colour images fail in the camera, a fault of the specification rather than manufacturing.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以斜邊法在實際感測器上量 MTF，分別取紅、綠、藍通道，或在 MTF 量測台上配窄帶濾光片逐波長量；每個波長做穿焦掃描求最佳焦點位置，直接量出色焦差並與 50 µm 或 14.2 µm 的設計值比較；量測頻率至少涵蓋 Nyquist 與其一半，並在中心與 70% 視場各量一次。","textEn":"Measure MTF on the actual sensor by the slanted-edge method for the red, green and blue channels separately, or on an MTF bench with narrow-band filters wavelength by wavelength; run a through-focus scan per wavelength to locate best focus, measuring the colour focus spread directly against the 50 µm or 14.2 µm design value; cover at least Nyquist and half Nyquist, at the centre and at 70% field.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以斜邊法在實際感測器上量 MTF，分別取紅、綠、藍通道，或在 MTF 量測台上配窄帶濾光片逐波長量。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure MTF on the actual sensor by the slanted-edge method for the red, green and blue channels separately, or on an MTF bench with narrow-band filters wavelength by wavelength.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以斜邊法在實際感測器上量 MTF，分別取紅、綠、藍通道，或在 MTF 量測台上配窄帶濾光片逐波長量；每個波長做穿焦掃描求最佳焦點位置，直接量出色焦差並與 50 µm 或 14.2 µm 的設計值比較；量測頻率至少涵蓋 Nyquist 與其一半，並在中心與 70% 視場各量一次。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure MTF on the actual sensor by the slanted-edge method for the red, green and blue channels separately, or on an MTF bench with narrow-band filters wavelength by wavelength; run a through-focus scan per wavelength to locate best focus, measuring the colour focus spread directly against the 50 µm or 14.2 µm design value; cover at least Nyquist and half Nyquist, at the centre and at 70% field. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":31},{"id":"a405-v12-20","title":"依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「感測器像素與 MTF」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Sensor pixels and MTF” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"以 N-BK7/F2 雙合搭配 3.45 µm 像素與 f/4，紅藍通道模糊，高對比邊緣出現紫邊；若規格只寫 546 nm 單色 MTF，鏡頭在檢驗台上全數合格，裝上相機後彩色影像卻不合格，責任在規格而非製造。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Pairing an N-BK7/F2 doublet with 3.45 µm pixels at f/4 blurs the red and blue channels and puts purple fringes on high-contrast edges; a specification written only as 546 nm monochromatic MTF lets every lens pass on the bench while colour images fail in the camera, a fault of the specification rather than manufacturing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：因此規格應寫成在 Nyquist 或其一半、中心與邊緣的多色 MTF，並要求各色焦點散佈落在 ±2λN² 的像素尺度景深內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The specification should therefore state polychromatic MTF at Nyquist or half Nyquist at centre and edge, and require the colour focus spread to fall within the pixel-scale depth of focus ±2λN².","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以 N-BK7/F2 雙合搭配 3.45 µm 像素與 f/4，紅藍通道模糊，高對比邊緣出現紫邊；若規格只寫 546 nm 單色 MTF，鏡頭在檢驗台上全數合格，裝上相機後彩色影像卻不合格，責任在規格而非製造。","textEn":"Pairing an N-BK7/F2 doublet with 3.45 µm pixels at f/4 blurs the red and blue channels and puts purple fringes on high-contrast edges; a specification written only as 546 nm monochromatic MTF lets every lens pass on the bench while colour images fail in the camera, a fault of the specification rather than manufacturing.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「依感測器匹配設計與 MTF 判準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sensor-matched design and MTF criteria\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。","以 N-BK7/F2 雙合搭配 3.45 µm 像素與 f/4，紅藍通道模糊，高對比邊緣出現紫邊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.","Pairing an N-BK7/F2 doublet with 3.45 µm pixels at f/4 blurs the red and blue channels and puts purple fringes on high-contrast edges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 N-BK7/F2 雙合搭配 3.45 µm 像素與 f/4，紅藍通道模糊，高對比邊緣出現紫邊；若規格只寫 546 nm 單色 MTF，鏡頭在檢驗台上全數合格，裝上相機後彩色影像卻不合格，責任在規格而非製造。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pairing an N-BK7/F2 doublet with 3.45 µm pixels at f/4 blurs the red and blue channels and puts purple fringes on high-contrast edges; a specification written only as 546 nm monochromatic MTF lets every lens pass on the bench while colour images fail in the camera, a fault of the specification rather than manufacturing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":32},{"id":"a405-v12-21","title":"干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"穿透波前誤差通常用 632.8 nm 的 Fizeau 或 Twyman–Green 干涉儀量：平行測試光穿過鏡片聚焦到參考返回球，原路折返再穿過鏡片一次，所以量到的光程差是單程的兩倍。Zernike 擬合可把傾斜與離焦移除，剩下的像散、彗差與球差分別指向應力、定心與曲率或間距問題。但 HeNe 測試是單色的，看不到色差；它的焦點位置也與設計波長不同，球差還會隨波長改變（色球差），所以 632.8 nm 的合格判定必須依設計模型換算到使用波段。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Transmitted wavefront error is usually measured with a 632.8 nm Fizeau or Twyman–Green interferometer: the collimated test beam passes through the lens to focus on a reference return sphere and comes back through the lens, so the measured optical path difference is twice the single-pass value. A Zernike fit removes tilt and focus, and the remaining astigmatism, coma and spherical terms point to stress, centring and radius or spacing problems respectively. But a HeNe test is monochromatic and blind to colour; its focus differs from the design wavelength's, and spherical aberration varies with wavelength (spherochromatism), so a pass at 632.8 nm must be converted to the working band through the design model. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：雙程量得 0.10λ rms（632.8 nm），單程 0.05λ = 31.6 nm；換到 546 nm 為 0.058λ，Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876；Maréchal 0.8 要求在 546 nm ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A double-pass reading of 0.10λ rms at 632.8 nm is 0.05λ = 31.6 nm single pass, or 0.058λ at 546 nm, giving Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876; a Maréchal 0.8 requires ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm at 546 nm.","failure":"常見誤解：「HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-21-k1","title":"干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算","titleEn":"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion","text":"穿透波前誤差通常用 632.8 nm 的 Fizeau 或 Twyman–Green 干涉儀量：平行測試光穿過鏡片聚焦到參考返回球，原路折返再穿過鏡片一次，所以量到的光程差是單程的兩倍。Zernike 擬合可把傾斜與離焦移除，剩下的像散、彗差與球差分別指向應力、定心與曲率或間距問題。","textEn":"Transmitted wavefront error is usually measured with a 632.8 nm Fizeau or Twyman–Green interferometer: the collimated test beam passes through the lens to focus on a reference return sphere and comes back through the lens, so the measured optical path difference is twice the single-pass value. A Zernike fit removes tilt and focus, and the remaining astigmatism, coma and spherical terms point to stress, centring and radius or spacing problems respectively.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion\" is correct?","options":["穿透波前誤差通常用 632.8 nm 的 Fizeau 或 Twyman–Green 干涉儀量：平行測試光穿過鏡片聚焦到參考返回球，原路折返再穿過鏡片一次，所以量到的光程差是單程的兩倍。","HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。","只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。"],"optionsEn":["Transmitted wavefront error is usually measured with a 632.8 nm Fizeau or Twyman–Green interferometer: the collimated test beam passes through the lens to focus on a reference return sphere and comes back through the lens, so the measured optical path difference is twice the single-pass value.","A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.","Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear."],"answer":0,"explanation":"穿透波前誤差通常用 632.8 nm 的 Fizeau 或 Twyman–Green 干涉儀量：平行測試光穿過鏡片聚焦到參考返回球，原路折返再穿過鏡片一次，所以量到的光程差是單程的兩倍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Transmitted wavefront error is usually measured with a 632.8 nm Fizeau or Twyman–Green interferometer: the collimated test beam passes through the lens to focus on a reference return sphere and comes back through the lens, so the measured optical path difference is twice the single-pass value. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":33},{"id":"a405-v12-22","title":"干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：雙程量得 0.10λ rms（632.8 nm），單程 0.05λ = 31.6 nm；換到 546 nm 為 0.058λ，Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876；Maréchal 0.8 要求在 546 nm ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 雙合在 632.8 nm 的焦點位於 d 焦點後 28.8 µm，返回球須放在此處，這個焦點偏移本身也能核對玻璃組合是否正確。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A double-pass reading of 0.10λ rms at 632.8 nm is 0.05λ = 31.6 nm single pass, or 0.058λ at 546 nm, giving Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876; a Maréchal 0.8 requires ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm at 546 nm. The 632.8 nm focus of an N-BK7/F2 f = 100 mm doublet lies 28.8 µm behind the d focus, so the return sphere must sit there, and that offset itself checks that the glass pair is right. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：先以旋轉或隨機球平均法校正返回球與參考面的誤差；鏡片在夾具中量 0° 與 180° 兩個方位，相減分離鏡片與系統誤差；把 Zernike 彗差與定心量測結果交叉比對；記錄多次量測的平均與標準差，並把量得的 632.8 nm 焦點位置與模型的 28.8 µm 預測比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate the return sphere and reference surface first by rotation or random-ball averaging; measure the lens at 0° and 180° in its fixture and difference the results to separate lens from system error; cross-check Zernike coma with centring measurements; log the mean and standard deviation of repeated measurements, and compare the measured 632.8 nm focus position with the modelled 28.8 µm offset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"雙程量得 0.10λ rms（632.8 nm），單程 0.05λ = 31.6 nm；換到 546 nm 為 0.058λ，Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876；Maréchal 0.8 要求在 546 nm ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm。N-BK7/F2、f = 100 mm 雙合在 632.8 nm 的焦點位於 d 焦點後 28.8 µm，返回球須放在此處，這個焦點偏移本身也能核對玻璃組合是否正確。","textEn":"A double-pass reading of 0.10λ rms at 632.8 nm is 0.05λ = 31.6 nm single pass, or 0.058λ at 546 nm, giving Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876; a Maréchal 0.8 requires ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm at 546 nm. The 632.8 nm focus of an N-BK7/F2 f = 100 mm doublet lies 28.8 µm behind the d focus, so the return sphere must sit there, and that offset itself checks that the glass pair is right.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","雙程量得 0.10λ rms（632.8 nm），單程 0.05λ = 31.6 nm。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","A double-pass reading of 0.10λ rms at 632.8 nm is 0.05λ = 31.6 nm single pass, or 0.058λ at 546 nm, giving Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙程量得 0.10λ rms（632.8 nm），單程 0.05λ = 31.6 nm；換到 546 nm 為 0.058λ，Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876；Maréchal 0.8 要求在 546 nm ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A double-pass reading of 0.10λ rms at 632.8 nm is 0.05λ = 31.6 nm single pass, or 0.058λ at 546 nm, giving Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π × 0.058)²] ≈ 0.876; a Maréchal 0.8 requires ≤ λ/14 = 39 nm at 546 nm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":34},{"id":"a405-v12-23","title":"干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"先以旋轉或隨機球平均法校正返回球與參考面的誤差；鏡片在夾具中量 0° 與 180° 兩個方位，相減分離鏡片與系統誤差；把 Zernike 彗差與定心量測結果交叉比對；記錄多次量測的平均與標準差，並把量得的 632.8 nm 焦點位置與模型的 28.8 µm 預測比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate the return sphere and reference surface first by rotation or random-ball averaging; measure the lens at 0° and 180° in its fixture and difference the results to separate lens from system error; cross-check Zernike coma with centring measurements; log the mean and standard deviation of repeated measurements, and compare the measured 632.8 nm focus position with the modelled 28.8 µm offset. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：忘記把雙程結果除以 2 或沒扣除參考面誤差，合格鏡片被誤判報廢；鏡片在 632.8 nm 合格卻在 486 nm 因色球差不合格；測試夾具夾得太緊，量到的像散其實是夾持應力，卻被歸咎於拋光。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Forgetting to halve the double-pass result or to subtract reference error scraps good lenses; a lens passes at 632.8 nm but fails at 486 nm through spherochromatism; an over-tight test fixture produces astigmatism that is really clamping stress yet is blamed on polishing.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以旋轉或隨機球平均法校正返回球與參考面的誤差；鏡片在夾具中量 0° 與 180° 兩個方位，相減分離鏡片與系統誤差；把 Zernike 彗差與定心量測結果交叉比對；記錄多次量測的平均與標準差，並把量得的 632.8 nm 焦點位置與模型的 28.8 µm 預測比較。","textEn":"Calibrate the return sphere and reference surface first by rotation or random-ball averaging; measure the lens at 0° and 180° in its fixture and difference the results to separate lens from system error; cross-check Zernike coma with centring measurements; log the mean and standard deviation of repeated measurements, and compare the measured 632.8 nm focus position with the modelled 28.8 µm offset.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。","先以旋轉或隨機球平均法校正返回球與參考面的誤差。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.","Calibrate the return sphere and reference surface first by rotation or random-ball averaging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先以旋轉或隨機球平均法校正返回球與參考面的誤差；鏡片在夾具中量 0° 與 180° 兩個方位，相減分離鏡片與系統誤差；把 Zernike 彗差與定心量測結果交叉比對；記錄多次量測的平均與標準差，並把量得的 632.8 nm 焦點位置與模型的 28.8 µm 預測比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate the return sphere and reference surface first by rotation or random-ball averaging; measure the lens at 0° and 180° in its fixture and difference the results to separate lens from system error; cross-check Zernike coma with centring measurements; log the mean and standard deviation of repeated measurements, and compare the measured 632.8 nm focus position with the modelled 28.8 µm offset. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":35},{"id":"a405-v12-24","title":"干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙程 Fizeau 穿透波前」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Double-pass Fizeau transmitted wavefront” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"忘記把雙程結果除以 2 或沒扣除參考面誤差，合格鏡片被誤判報廢；鏡片在 632.8 nm 合格卻在 486 nm 因色球差不合格；測試夾具夾得太緊，量到的像散其實是夾持應力，卻被歸咎於拋光。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Forgetting to halve the double-pass result or to subtract reference error scraps good lenses; a lens passes at 632.8 nm but fails at 486 nm through spherochromatism; an over-tight test fixture produces astigmatism that is really clamping stress yet is blamed on polishing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：但 HeNe 測試是單色的，看不到色差；它的焦點位置也與設計波長不同，球差還會隨波長改變（色球差），所以 632.8 nm 的合格判定必須依設計模型換算到使用波段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: But a HeNe test is monochromatic and blind to colour; its focus differs from the design wavelength's, and spherical aberration varies with wavelength (spherochromatism), so a pass at 632.8 nm must be converted to the working band through the design model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忘記把雙程結果除以 2 或沒扣除參考面誤差，合格鏡片被誤判報廢；鏡片在 632.8 nm 合格卻在 486 nm 因色球差不合格；測試夾具夾得太緊，量到的像散其實是夾持應力，卻被歸咎於拋光。","textEn":"Forgetting to halve the double-pass result or to subtract reference error scraps good lenses; a lens passes at 632.8 nm but fails at 486 nm through spherochromatism; an over-tight test fixture produces astigmatism that is really clamping stress yet is blamed on polishing.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「干涉儀穿透波前量測與波長換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Interferometric transmitted-wavefront test and wavelength conversion\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忘記把雙程結果除以 2 或沒扣除參考面誤差，合格鏡片被誤判報廢。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。"],"optionsEn":["Forgetting to halve the double-pass result or to subtract reference error scraps good lenses.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忘記把雙程結果除以 2 或沒扣除參考面誤差，合格鏡片被誤判報廢；鏡片在 632.8 nm 合格卻在 486 nm 因色球差不合格；測試夾具夾得太緊，量到的像散其實是夾持應力，卻被歸咎於拋光。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Forgetting to halve the double-pass result or to subtract reference error scraps good lenses; a lens passes at 632.8 nm but fails at 486 nm through spherochromatism; an over-tight test fixture produces astigmatism that is really clamping stress yet is blamed on polishing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":36}],"order":6},{"id":"a405-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「雜散光與鬼影分析」與「量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stray-light and ghost analysis\" and \"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a405-v12-25","title":"雜散光與鬼影分析：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Stray-light and ghost analysis: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ghost paths and edge stray light” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"每個折射面都會反射一點光，經過兩次反射的光又朝感測器前進，形成亮光源的離焦複本，即鬼影。N 個面之間的二次反射路徑共有 N(N − 1)/2 條；膠合雙合有 3 個面，空氣間隔版有 4 個，再加上感測器保護玻璃與感測器本身，而感測器往往是最強的反射面。鬼影照度取決於兩面反射率與鬼影在感測器上的離焦程度，聚焦在感測器附近的鬼影最危險。另一類雜散光來自研磨鏡緣散射、鏡筒內壁與螺紋，以及膠中的氣泡。分析時先用近軸鬼影追跡找出鬼影焦點，再以非序列光線追跡估算照度。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every refracting surface reflects a little light, and light reflected twice heads back toward the sensor as an out-of-focus copy of a bright source, a ghost. Among N surfaces there are N(N − 1)/2 two-bounce paths; a cemented doublet has 3 surfaces and an air-spaced one 4, plus the sensor cover glass and the sensor itself, which is often the strongest reflector. Ghost irradiance depends on the two reflectances and how defocused the ghost is at the sensor, and a ghost that focuses near the sensor is the most dangerous. Other stray light comes from scatter off ground lens edges, barrel walls and threads, and bubbles in the cement. Analysis starts with paraxial ghost tracing to locate ghost foci and then estimates irradiance by non-sequential ray tracing. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Ghost paths and edge stray light”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：路徑數：膠合 3 面有 3 條、空氣間隔 4 面有 6 條；雙合加 2 面保護玻璃與感測器共 6 面，15 條。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Paths: 3 for a cemented 3-surface doublet and 6 for an air-spaced 4-surface one; a doublet plus a 2-surface cover glass and the sensor makes 6 surfaces and 15 paths.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Ghost paths and edge stray light”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-25-k1","title":"雜散光與鬼影分析","titleEn":"Stray-light and ghost analysis","text":"每個折射面都會反射一點光，經過兩次反射的光又朝感測器前進，形成亮光源的離焦複本，即鬼影。N 個面之間的二次反射路徑共有 N(N − 1)/2 條；膠合雙合有 3 個面，空氣間隔版有 4 個，再加上感測器保護玻璃與感測器本身，而感測器往往是最強的反射面。","textEn":"Every refracting surface reflects a little light, and light reflected twice heads back toward the sensor as an out-of-focus copy of a bright source, a ghost. Among N surfaces there are N(N − 1)/2 two-bounce paths; a cemented doublet has 3 surfaces and an air-spaced one 4, plus the sensor cover glass and the sensor itself, which is often the strongest reflector.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雜散光與鬼影分析」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stray-light and ghost analysis\" is correct?","options":["只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。","每個折射面都會反射一點光，經過兩次反射的光又朝感測器前進，形成亮光源的離焦複本，即鬼影。","量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。"],"optionsEn":["Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear.","Every refracting surface reflects a little light, and light reflected twice heads back toward the sensor as an out-of-focus copy of a bright source, a ghost.","A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每個折射面都會反射一點光，經過兩次反射的光又朝感測器前進，形成亮光源的離焦複本，即鬼影。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every refracting surface reflects a little light, and light reflected twice heads back toward the sensor as an out-of-focus copy of a bright source, a ghost. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":37},{"id":"a405-v12-26","title":"雜散光與鬼影分析：定量估算","titleEn":"Stray-light and ghost analysis: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ghost paths and edge stray light” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：路徑數：膠合 3 面有 3 條、空氣間隔 4 面有 6 條；雙合加 2 面保護玻璃與感測器共 6 面，15 條。感測器（R = 4%）與鏡頭後表面（鍍膜 R = 0.5%）之間的鬼影能量比 2×10⁻⁴；若 50 µm 的 LED 像變成 0.5 mm 的鬼影圓盤，峰值比 2×10⁻⁴ × (50/500)² = 2×10⁻⁶；LED 超出滿井 1000 倍時，鬼影達滿井的 0.2%，在 12 位元感測器約 8 LSB，肉眼可見。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Paths: 3 for a cemented 3-surface doublet and 6 for an air-spaced 4-surface one; a doublet plus a 2-surface cover glass and the sensor makes 6 surfaces and 15 paths. A ghost between the sensor (R = 4%) and the rear lens surface (coated R = 0.5%) carries an energy ratio of 2×10⁻⁴; if a 50 µm LED image becomes a 0.5 mm ghost disc the peak ratio is 2×10⁻⁴ × (50/500)² = 2×10⁻⁶, and with the LED 1000 times over full well the ghost reaches 0.2% of full well, about 8 LSB on a 12-bit sensor and visible. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以準直的強光源在多個視場角掃描，用長曝光或高動態範圍拍攝鏡頭加感測器的影像，標出鬼影位置與大小並與鬼影追跡比較；以積分球加黑點的方法量面眩光指數；檢查鏡緣是否塗黑、鏡筒內壁是否有消光螺紋，並在紅外波段重複測試，確認鍍膜在感測器全響應範圍內都有效。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Scan a bright collimated source across several field angles and record lens plus sensor with long exposures or high dynamic range, mark ghost positions and sizes and compare with the ghost trace; measure the veiling-glare index with an integrating sphere and black spot; check that lens edges are blackened and barrel walls carry baffling threads, and repeat in the near infrared to confirm the coating works across the sensor's full response.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"路徑數：膠合 3 面有 3 條、空氣間隔 4 面有 6 條；雙合加 2 面保護玻璃與感測器共 6 面，15 條。感測器（R = 4%）與鏡頭後表面（鍍膜 R = 0.5%）之間的鬼影能量比 2×10⁻⁴；若 50 µm 的 LED 像變成 0.5 mm 的鬼影圓盤，峰值比 2×10⁻⁴ × (50/500)² = 2×10⁻⁶；LED 超出滿井 1000 倍時，鬼影達滿井的 0.2%，在 12 位元感測器約 8 LSB，肉眼可見。","textEn":"Paths: 3 for a cemented 3-surface doublet and 6 for an air-spaced 4-surface one; a doublet plus a 2-surface cover glass and the sensor makes 6 surfaces and 15 paths. A ghost between the sensor (R = 4%) and the rear lens surface (coated R = 0.5%) carries an energy ratio of 2×10⁻⁴; if a 50 µm LED image becomes a 0.5 mm ghost disc the peak ratio is 2×10⁻⁴ × (50/500)² = 2×10⁻⁶, and with the LED 1000 times over full well the ghost reaches 0.2% of full well, about 8 LSB on a 12-bit sensor and visible.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雜散光與鬼影分析」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stray-light and ghost analysis\", which statement holds?","options":["玻璃的熱膨脹很小，所以溫度變化不會讓焦點移動。","鏡片拋光到正確曲率後自然就是同心的，不需要另外定心。","路徑數：膠合 3 面有 3 條、空氣間隔 4 面有 6 條；雙合加 2 面保護玻璃與感測器共 6 面，15 條。"],"optionsEn":["Glass expands so little that temperature changes cannot move the focus.","A lens polished to the right radii is automatically centred.","Paths: 3 for a cemented 3-surface doublet and 6 for an air-spaced 4-surface one."],"answer":2,"explanation":"路徑數：膠合 3 面有 3 條、空氣間隔 4 面有 6 條；雙合加 2 面保護玻璃與感測器共 6 面，15 條。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Paths: 3 for a cemented 3-surface doublet and 6 for an air-spaced 4-surface one; a doublet plus a 2-surface cover glass and the sensor makes 6 surfaces and 15 paths. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":38},{"id":"a405-v12-27","title":"雜散光與鬼影分析：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Stray-light and ghost analysis: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Ghost paths and edge stray light” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以準直的強光源在多個視場角掃描，用長曝光或高動態範圍拍攝鏡頭加感測器的影像，標出鬼影位置與大小並與鬼影追跡比較；以積分球加黑點的方法量面眩光指數；檢查鏡緣是否塗黑、鏡筒內壁是否有消光螺紋，並在紅外波段重複測試，確認鍍膜在感測器全響應範圍內都有效。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Scan a bright collimated source across several field angles and record lens plus sensor with long exposures or high dynamic range, mark ghost positions and sizes and compare with the ghost trace; measure the veiling-glare index with an integrating sphere and black spot; check that lens edges are blackened and barrel walls carry baffling threads, and repeat in the near infrared to confirm the coating works across the sensor's full response. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：未塗黑的研磨鏡緣把視場外的強光散射成整片霧光，對比下降；抗反射膜只針對可見光最佳化，感測器在近紅外仍有響應，夜間模式鬼影突然明顯；聚焦在感測器上的鬼影成為與光源反向移動的亮點，被誤判為缺陷像素或目標。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: An unblackened ground edge scatters a bright out-of-field source into a veil of haze that lowers contrast; a coating optimised only for the visible leaves high near-infrared reflectance where the sensor still responds, so ghosts suddenly appear in night mode; a ghost focused on the sensor becomes a bright spot moving opposite to the source, mistaken for a defective pixel or a target.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以準直的強光源在多個視場角掃描，用長曝光或高動態範圍拍攝鏡頭加感測器的影像，標出鬼影位置與大小並與鬼影追跡比較；以積分球加黑點的方法量面眩光指數；檢查鏡緣是否塗黑、鏡筒內壁是否有消光螺紋，並在紅外波段重複測試，確認鍍膜在感測器全響應範圍內都有效。","textEn":"Scan a bright collimated source across several field angles and record lens plus sensor with long exposures or high dynamic range, mark ghost positions and sizes and compare with the ghost trace; measure the veiling-glare index with an integrating sphere and black spot; check that lens edges are blackened and barrel walls carry baffling threads, and repeat in the near infrared to confirm the coating works across the sensor's full response.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雜散光與鬼影分析」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stray-light and ghost analysis\"?","options":["以準直的強光源在多個視場角掃描，用長曝光或高動態範圍拍攝鏡頭加感測器的影像，標出鬼影位置與大小並與鬼影追跡比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。"],"optionsEn":["Scan a bright collimated source across several field angles and record lens plus sensor with long exposures or high dynamic range, mark ghost positions and sizes and compare with the ghost trace.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以準直的強光源在多個視場角掃描，用長曝光或高動態範圍拍攝鏡頭加感測器的影像，標出鬼影位置與大小並與鬼影追跡比較；以積分球加黑點的方法量面眩光指數；檢查鏡緣是否塗黑、鏡筒內壁是否有消光螺紋，並在紅外波段重複測試，確認鍍膜在感測器全響應範圍內都有效。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Scan a bright collimated source across several field angles and record lens plus sensor with long exposures or high dynamic range, mark ghost positions and sizes and compare with the ghost trace; measure the veiling-glare index with an integrating sphere and black spot; check that lens edges are blackened and barrel walls carry baffling threads, and repeat in the near infrared to confirm the coating works across the sensor's full response. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":39},{"id":"a405-v12-28","title":"雜散光與鬼影分析：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stray-light and ghost analysis: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鬼影路徑與邊緣雜散光」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Ghost paths and edge stray light” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"未塗黑的研磨鏡緣把視場外的強光散射成整片霧光，對比下降；抗反射膜只針對可見光最佳化，感測器在近紅外仍有響應，夜間模式鬼影突然明顯；聚焦在感測器上的鬼影成為與光源反向移動的亮點，被誤判為缺陷像素或目標。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"An unblackened ground edge scatters a bright out-of-field source into a veil of haze that lowers contrast; a coating optimised only for the visible leaves high near-infrared reflectance where the sensor still responds, so ghosts suddenly appear in night mode; a ghost focused on the sensor becomes a bright spot moving opposite to the source, mistaken for a defective pixel or a target. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：分析時先用近軸鬼影追跡找出鬼影焦點，再以非序列光線追跡估算照度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Analysis starts with paraxial ghost tracing to locate ghost foci and then estimates irradiance by non-sequential ray tracing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要鍍了抗反射膜，就不會出現鬼影。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once an antireflection coating is applied, ghosts cannot appear.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未塗黑的研磨鏡緣把視場外的強光散射成整片霧光，對比下降；抗反射膜只針對可見光最佳化，感測器在近紅外仍有響應，夜間模式鬼影突然明顯；聚焦在感測器上的鬼影成為與光源反向移動的亮點，被誤判為缺陷像素或目標。","textEn":"An unblackened ground edge scatters a bright out-of-field source into a veil of haze that lowers contrast; a coating optimised only for the visible leaves high near-infrared reflectance where the sensor still responds, so ghosts suddenly appear in night mode; a ghost focused on the sensor becomes a bright spot moving opposite to the source, mistaken for a defective pixel or a target.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雜散光與鬼影分析」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stray-light and ghost analysis\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","未塗黑的研磨鏡緣把視場外的強光散射成整片霧光，對比下降。","量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","An unblackened ground edge scatters a bright out-of-field source into a veil of haze that lowers contrast.","A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未塗黑的研磨鏡緣把視場外的強光散射成整片霧光，對比下降；抗反射膜只針對可見光最佳化，感測器在近紅外仍有響應，夜間模式鬼影突然明顯；聚焦在感測器上的鬼影成為與光源反向移動的亮點，被誤判為缺陷像素或目標。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An unblackened ground edge scatters a bright out-of-field source into a veil of haze that lowers contrast; a coating optimised only for the visible leaves high near-infrared reflectance where the sensor still responds, so ghosts suddenly appear in night mode; a ghost focused on the sensor becomes a bright spot moving opposite to the source, mistaken for a defective pixel or a target. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":40},{"id":"a405-v12-29","title":"量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「驗收矩陣與保護帶」如何決定消色差透鏡設計的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Acceptance matrix and guard band” determines the key performance of “Achromatic lens design”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"量產驗收把設計轉成可量的門檻：有效焦距與後焦、指定頻率與視場的多色 MTF、軸向色焦差、632.8 nm 穿透波前、定心與視軸、鬼影檢查、熱離焦，以及依 ISO 10110-7 標示的表面瑕疵。量測不確定度必須遠小於公差，測試不確定度比至少 4；下限規格的允收門檻要加上保護帶，即門檻 = 規格 + U，在生產者風險（誤拒好件）與使用者風險（誤收壞件）之間取捨。量測台本身要做重複性與再現性研究，並以標準鏡每日校驗。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「驗收矩陣與保護帶」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Production acceptance turns the design into measurable gates: effective and back focal length, polychromatic MTF at specified frequencies and fields, axial colour focus spread, 632.8 nm transmitted wavefront, centring and boresight, ghost checks, thermal defocus and surface imperfections stated per ISO 10110-7. Measurement uncertainty must be well below tolerance, with a test uncertainty ratio of at least 4; for a lower-limit specification the acceptance threshold is guard-banded as threshold = spec + U, trading producer risk of rejecting good parts against consumer risk of accepting bad ones. The test bench itself needs a repeatability and reproducibility study and a daily check against a reference lens. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Acceptance matrix and guard band”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：規格：72 lp/mm 多色 MTF ≥ 0.30；量測擴充不確定度 U = 0.03（k = 2），保護帶門檻 0.33。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Specification: polychromatic MTF ≥ 0.30 at 72 lp/mm with expanded uncertainty U = 0.03 (k = 2), so the guard-banded threshold is 0.33.","failure":"常見誤解：「量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「驗收矩陣與保護帶」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Acceptance matrix and guard band”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-29-k1","title":"量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接","titleEn":"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff","text":"量產驗收把設計轉成可量的門檻：有效焦距與後焦、指定頻率與視場的多色 MTF、軸向色焦差、632.8 nm 穿透波前、定心與視軸、鬼影檢查、熱離焦，以及依 ISO 10110-7 標示的表面瑕疵。量測不確定度必須遠小於公差，測試不確定度比至少 4；下限規格的允收門檻要加上保護帶，即門檻 = 規格 + U，在生產者風險（誤拒好件）與使用者風險（誤收壞件）之間取捨。","textEn":"Production acceptance turns the design into measurable gates: effective and back focal length, polychromatic MTF at specified frequencies and fields, axial colour focus spread, 632.8 nm transmitted wavefront, centring and boresight, ghost checks, thermal defocus and surface imperfections stated per ISO 10110-7. Measurement uncertainty must be well below tolerance, with a test uncertainty ratio of at least 4; for a lower-limit specification the acceptance threshold is guard-banded as threshold = spec + U, trading producer risk of rejecting good parts against consumer risk of accepting bad ones.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff\" is correct?","options":["量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。","只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","量產驗收把設計轉成可量的門檻：有效焦距與後焦、指定頻率與視場的多色 MTF、軸向色焦差、632.8 nm 穿透波前、定心與視軸、鬼影檢查、熱離焦，以及依 ISO 10110-7 標示的表面瑕疵。"],"optionsEn":["A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released.","A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","Production acceptance turns the design into measurable gates: effective and back focal length, polychromatic MTF at specified frequencies and fields, axial colour focus spread, 632.8 nm transmitted wavefront, centring and boresight, ghost checks, thermal defocus and surface imperfections stated per ISO 10110-7."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量產驗收把設計轉成可量的門檻：有效焦距與後焦、指定頻率與視場的多色 MTF、軸向色焦差、632.8 nm 穿透波前、定心與視軸、鬼影檢查、熱離焦，以及依 ISO 10110-7 標示的表面瑕疵。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Production acceptance turns the design into measurable gates: effective and back focal length, polychromatic MTF at specified frequencies and fields, axial colour focus spread, 632.8 nm transmitted wavefront, centring and boresight, ghost checks, thermal defocus and surface imperfections stated per ISO 10110-7. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":41},{"id":"a405-v12-30","title":"量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「驗收矩陣與保護帶」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Acceptance matrix and guard band” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：規格：72 lp/mm 多色 MTF ≥ 0.30；量測擴充不確定度 U = 0.03（k = 2），保護帶門檻 0.33。若量產平均 0.38、標準差 0.025，有保護帶的良率 Φ((0.38 − 0.33)/0.025) = Φ(2.0) = 97.7%，不加保護帶為 Φ(3.2) = 99.93%，但會放行真值略低於 0.30 的鏡頭。焦距公差 ±0.5 mm、U = 0.1 mm，測試不確定度比 5，符合 ≥ 4 的要求。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Specification: polychromatic MTF ≥ 0.30 at 72 lp/mm with expanded uncertainty U = 0.03 (k = 2), so the guard-banded threshold is 0.33. With a production mean of 0.38 and standard deviation 0.025, guard-banded yield is Φ((0.38 − 0.33)/0.025) = Φ(2.0) = 97.7%, against Φ(3.2) = 99.93% without a guard band, which would release lenses whose true MTF lies just below 0.30. A focal-length tolerance of ±0.5 mm with U = 0.1 mm gives a test uncertainty ratio of 5, meeting the ≥ 4 requirement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：對 MTF 量測台做量測系統分析：10 顆鏡頭 × 3 位操作員 × 3 次重複，計算重複性與再現性佔公差的百分比；每日以標準鏡確認讀值在管制界限內；與客戶的量測台做相關性比對，找出系統偏差；把每顆鏡頭的量測值、玻璃熔次、膠批號與設計模型版本一併記錄到序號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run a measurement-system analysis on the MTF bench with 10 lenses × 3 operators × 3 repeats and compute repeatability and reproducibility as a percentage of tolerance; check daily that the reference lens reads within control limits; correlate with the customer's bench to find systematic bias; record each lens's results with glass melt lot, cement batch and design-model version under its serial number.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"規格：72 lp/mm 多色 MTF ≥ 0.30；量測擴充不確定度 U = 0.03（k = 2），保護帶門檻 0.33。若量產平均 0.38、標準差 0.025，有保護帶的良率 Φ((0.38 − 0.33)/0.025) = Φ(2.0) = 97.7%，不加保護帶為 Φ(3.2) = 99.93%，但會放行真值略低於 0.30 的鏡頭。焦距公差 ±0.5 mm、U = 0.1 mm，測試不確定度比 5，符合 ≥ 4 的要求。","textEn":"Specification: polychromatic MTF ≥ 0.30 at 72 lp/mm with expanded uncertainty U = 0.03 (k = 2), so the guard-banded threshold is 0.33. With a production mean of 0.38 and standard deviation 0.025, guard-banded yield is Φ((0.38 − 0.33)/0.025) = Φ(2.0) = 97.7%, against Φ(3.2) = 99.93% without a guard band, which would release lenses whose true MTF lies just below 0.30. A focal-length tolerance of ±0.5 mm with U = 0.1 mm gives a test uncertainty ratio of 5, meeting the ≥ 4 requirement.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["規格：72 lp/mm 多色 MTF ≥ 0.30；量測擴充不確定度 U = 0.03（k = 2），保護帶門檻 0.33。","空氣間隔雙合只是沒上膠的膠合透鏡，光學性能完全相同。","只要鏡頭在綠光達到繞射極限，彩色影像就一定清晰。"],"optionsEn":["Specification: polychromatic MTF ≥ 0.30 at 72 lp/mm with expanded uncertainty U = 0.03 (k = 2), so the guard-banded threshold is 0.33.","An air-spaced doublet is just an uncemented cemented doublet with identical optics.","If the lens is diffraction-limited in green, colour images will be sharp."],"answer":0,"explanation":"規格：72 lp/mm 多色 MTF ≥ 0.30；量測擴充不確定度 U = 0.03（k = 2），保護帶門檻 0.33。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Specification: polychromatic MTF ≥ 0.30 at 72 lp/mm with expanded uncertainty U = 0.03 (k = 2), so the guard-banded threshold is 0.33. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":42},{"id":"a405-v12-31","title":"量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「驗收矩陣與保護帶」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Acceptance matrix and guard band” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"對 MTF 量測台做量測系統分析：10 顆鏡頭 × 3 位操作員 × 3 次重複，計算重複性與再現性佔公差的百分比；每日以標準鏡確認讀值在管制界限內；與客戶的量測台做相關性比對，找出系統偏差；把每顆鏡頭的量測值、玻璃熔次、膠批號與設計模型版本一併記錄到序號。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run a measurement-system analysis on the MTF bench with 10 lenses × 3 operators × 3 repeats and compute repeatability and reproducibility as a percentage of tolerance; check daily that the reference lens reads within control limits; correlate with the customer's bench to find systematic bias; record each lens's results with glass melt lot, cement batch and design-model version under its serial number. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：供應商與客戶的 MTF 量測台相差 0.04，整批在進料檢驗被退回；未設保護帶，邊緣件流入產品造成客訴；標準鏡在搬運中受損而讀值偏高，未被察覺下所有鏡頭都被高估。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Supplier and customer MTF benches differ by 0.04 and whole lots are rejected at incoming inspection; without a guard band marginal parts reach products and return as complaints; a reference lens damaged in handling reads high unnoticed, so every lens is overestimated.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對 MTF 量測台做量測系統分析：10 顆鏡頭 × 3 位操作員 × 3 次重複，計算重複性與再現性佔公差的百分比；每日以標準鏡確認讀值在管制界限內；與客戶的量測台做相關性比對，找出系統偏差；把每顆鏡頭的量測值、玻璃熔次、膠批號與設計模型版本一併記錄到序號。","textEn":"Run a measurement-system analysis on the MTF bench with 10 lenses × 3 operators × 3 repeats and compute repeatability and reproducibility as a percentage of tolerance; check daily that the reference lens reads within control limits; correlate with the customer's bench to find systematic bias; record each lens's results with glass melt lot, cement batch and design-model version under its serial number.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","對 MTF 量測台做量測系統分析：10 顆鏡頭 × 3 位操作員 × 3 次重複，計算重複性與再現性佔公差的百分比。","HeNe 干涉儀量到的波前合格，就代表整個可見光波段都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Run a measurement-system analysis on the MTF bench with 10 lenses × 3 operators × 3 repeats and compute repeatability and reproducibility as a percentage of tolerance.","A wavefront pass at 632.8 nm means the lens passes across the visible band."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對 MTF 量測台做量測系統分析：10 顆鏡頭 × 3 位操作員 × 3 次重複，計算重複性與再現性佔公差的百分比；每日以標準鏡確認讀值在管制界限內；與客戶的量測台做相關性比對，找出系統偏差；把每顆鏡頭的量測值、玻璃熔次、膠批號與設計模型版本一併記錄到序號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run a measurement-system analysis on the MTF bench with 10 lenses × 3 operators × 3 repeats and compute repeatability and reproducibility as a percentage of tolerance; check daily that the reference lens reads within control limits; correlate with the customer's bench to find systematic bias; record each lens's results with glass melt lot, cement batch and design-model version under its serial number. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":43},{"id":"a405-v12-32","title":"量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"],"prerequisiteIds":["a405-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「驗收矩陣與保護帶」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Acceptance matrix and guard band” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"供應商與客戶的 MTF 量測台相差 0.04，整批在進料檢驗被退回；未設保護帶，邊緣件流入產品造成客訴；標準鏡在搬運中受損而讀值偏高，未被察覺下所有鏡頭都被高估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Supplier and customer MTF benches differ by 0.04 and whole lots are rejected at incoming inspection; without a guard band marginal parts reach products and return as complaints; a reference lens damaged in handling reads high unnoticed, so every lens is overestimated. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：量測台本身要做重複性與再現性研究，並以標準鏡每日校驗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The test bench itself needs a repeatability and reproducibility study and a daily check against a reference lens.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量到的 MTF 只要比規格高一點點，就一定可以放行。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lens whose measured MTF is just above spec can always be released.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a405-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"供應商與客戶的 MTF 量測台相差 0.04，整批在進料檢驗被退回；未設保護帶，邊緣件流入產品造成客訴；標準鏡在搬運中受損而讀值偏高，未被察覺下所有鏡頭都被高估。","textEn":"Supplier and customer MTF benches differ by 0.04 and whole lots are rejected at incoming inspection; without a guard band marginal parts reach products and return as complaints; a reference lens damaged in handling reads high unnoticed, so every lens is overestimated.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]},{"id":"a405-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-achromat-edmund","v12o-schott-tie-29-refractive-index","v12o-schott-tie-19-dn-dt"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量產驗收矩陣、保護帶與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Production acceptance matrix, guard bands and handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","只要兩片玻璃的阿貝數差夠大，就能完全消除二級光譜。","供應商與客戶的 MTF 量測台相差 0.04，整批在進料檢驗被退回。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","A large enough Abbe-number difference between two glasses eliminates the secondary spectrum.","Supplier and customer MTF benches differ by 0.04 and whole lots are rejected at incoming inspection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"供應商與客戶的 MTF 量測台相差 0.04，整批在進料檢驗被退回；未設保護帶，邊緣件流入產品造成客訴；標準鏡在搬運中受損而讀值偏高，未被察覺下所有鏡頭都被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Supplier and customer MTF benches differ by 0.04 and whole lots are rejected at incoming inspection; without a guard band marginal parts reach products and return as complaints; a reference lens damaged in handling reads high unnoticed, so every lens is overestimated. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":44}],"order":7}],"scope":"公開原理的十二項教學任務，以自行繪製的示意模型、試算及來源資料進行；未提供工廠實測資料、專有配方或設備操作許可。","scopeEn":"Twelve educational tasks based on public principles, using original schematic models, calculations and referenced material. No factory measurement dataset, proprietary recipe or equipment operating authorization is supplied.","curriculumVersion":6,"enrichmentVersion":12,"v12Extension":{"stages":4,"steps":32,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"焦點預算練習：f = 100 mm、f/4 的 N-BK7/F2 膠合雙合，f₁ = 43.3 mm、f₂ = −76.4 mm，搭配 3.45 µm 像素（Nyquist 145 lp/mm）。二級光譜使 C、F 焦點在 d 後 50 µm；把感測器放在中間 +25 µm，d、C、F 各離焦 25 µm，W₀₂₀ 為 0.33λ、0.30λ、0.40λ，Nyquist MTF 約 0.36、0.35、0.37，乘像素 sinc 0.64 後約 0.23。溫度上升 40 K：鏡片焦距伸長 100 × 1.53×10⁻⁶ × 40 = 6.1 µm，鋁鏡筒伸長 94.4 µm，失配 88 µm 遠超 ±17.6 µm 景深；改用 Invar 隔圈後殘差 1.3 µm。若改用 N-FK51A/N-KZFS4（f₁ = 47.3 mm、f₂ = −89.8 mm），色焦差降為 14.2 µm，置中後各色離焦 7.1 µm，Nyquist MTF 約 0.51 到 0.62，乘像素響應後約 0.33 到 0.39，足以通過 0.30 的規格。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際產品規格。","textEn":"Focus-budget exercise: an f = 100 mm, f/4 cemented N-BK7/F2 doublet with f₁ = 43.3 mm and f₂ = −76.4 mm on 3.45 µm pixels (Nyquist 145 lp/mm). Secondary spectrum puts the C and F foci 50 µm behind d; placing the sensor midway at +25 µm defocuses d, C and F by 25 µm each, W₀₂₀ of 0.33λ, 0.30λ and 0.40λ, giving Nyquist MTF near 0.36, 0.35 and 0.37, about 0.23 after the 0.64 pixel sinc. A 40 K rise lengthens the lens focal length by 100 × 1.53×10⁻⁶ × 40 = 6.1 µm while an aluminium barrel grows 94.4 µm, an 88 µm mismatch far beyond the ±17.6 µm depth of focus; an Invar spacer leaves 1.3 µm. Switching to N-FK51A/N-KZFS4 (f₁ = 47.3 mm, f₂ = −89.8 mm) cuts the colour spread to 14.2 µm, so centred focus leaves each colour 7.1 µm out, Nyquist MTF about 0.51 to 0.62 and roughly 0.33 to 0.39 with the pixel response, enough to pass a 0.30 specification. Values are teaching assumptions, not any product's specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"focus":"三片式複消色差、熱離焦、膠合與空氣間隔取捨、定心膠合工序、感測器匹配 MTF、波前與鬼影驗收","focusEn":"Three-glass apochromats, thermal defocus, cemented versus air-spaced trade-offs, centring and cementing, sensor-matched MTF, wavefront and ghost acceptance"},"learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-design-fabrication","learningTags":["optics","optics-design-fabrication","imaging"],"subcategory":"optics-design-fabrication","subcategoryTitle":"光學設計與精密加工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Optical design and precision fabrication"},{"id":"b003","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview","v6-akashi-engineering","v6-akashi-maintenance","v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"stages":[{"id":"b003-stage01","order":1,"steps":[{"id":"b003-v6-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview","v6-akashi-engineering"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出海峽限制圖","titleEn":"Map strait constraints","objective":"區分航道淨空與結構跨距的需求。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish navigation-clearance needs from structural span requirements.","instruction":"自繪兩岸、航道和候選塔位，另以符號標出深水與強潮流區。為每一個塔位寫出一項須由海事或地質資料確認的限制。","instructionEn":"Sketch the shores, navigation corridor and candidate tower locations; mark deep water and strong currents separately. For each tower location, name a constraint requiring marine or geological evidence.","observation":"比較塔位移動是否同時改變航道餘裕、側跨與施工可達性。","observationEn":"Observe whether moving a tower changes navigation space, side spans and construction access together.","failure":"只保留最短跨距，卻把基礎放入航道或未調查地層。","failureEn":"Minimizing span alone can place foundations in a navigation corridor or uninvestigated ground.","check":"提交有圖例的限制圖，至少保留兩項尚待查證的資料。","checkEn":"Submit a keyed constraint map with at least two unresolved evidence needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-01-k1","title":"多目標選址","titleEn":"Multi-objective siting","text":"塔位同時影響結構、航運和施工；跨距不是唯一決策量。","textEn":"Tower placement affects structure, navigation and construction; span is only one decision variable."},{"id":"b003-v6-01-k2","title":"資料不確定性","titleEn":"Data uncertainty","text":"未量測的水深或地層不能因示意圖畫得完整就視為已確認。","textEn":"A complete-looking sketch does not verify unmeasured depth or ground conditions."}],"quiz":{"options":["航道、地盤與施工限制是否不同","只比較總橋重，認為其可代表所有場址限制","先假定兩地地盤完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Differences in navigation, ground and construction constraints","Compare total bridge weight as if it represented every site constraint","Assume identical ground conditions first"],"answer":0,"question":"兩個塔位方案跨距相近，下一個合理比較是什麼？","questionEn":"Two tower layouts have similar spans. What should be compared next?","explanation":"相近的跨距不代表相同的外部條件，必須比較限制與證據缺口。","explanationEn":"Similar spans do not imply similar external conditions; compare constraints and evidence gaps."}},{"id":"b003-v6-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-01"],"title":"追蹤懸索橋載荷路徑","titleEn":"Trace the suspension load path","objective":"辨認吊索、主纜、塔與錨碇的不同角色。","objectiveEn":"Identify the distinct roles of hangers, main cables, towers and anchorages.","instruction":"在自繪側視圖把一個橋面載荷依序連到吊索及主纜，再分別追蹤塔的支承和端部錨碇的反力。另畫一條溫度伸縮方向箭頭。","instructionEn":"On a side-view sketch, trace a deck load through hangers and main cables, then identify tower support and end-anchorage reactions. Add a separate thermal-movement arrow.","observation":"注意吊索大致垂直，而主纜曲線連續通過塔頂。","observationEn":"Notice the approximately vertical hangers and the main cable continuing over the towers.","failure":"把主纜當成從塔頂直接放射到橋面的斜張索。","failureEn":"Mistaking the main cable for separate stays radiating directly from a tower to the deck.","check":"載荷路徑須包含錨碇，且與伸縮箭頭使用不同圖例。","checkEn":"Include anchorages in the load path and distinguish force arrows from movement arrows.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-02-k1","title":"懸索與斜張","titleEn":"Suspension versus cable-stayed","text":"懸索橋以主纜與吊索承托橋面；斜張橋的斜索直接連結塔與梁。","textEn":"A suspension bridge supports its deck through main cables and hangers; stays connect a cable-stayed deck directly to towers."},{"id":"b003-v6-02-k2","title":"反力閉合","titleEn":"Reaction closure","text":"辨識拉力仍須追查由哪個支承或地盤提供平衡反力。","textEn":"Identifying tension also requires locating the support or ground that balances it."}],"quiz":{"options":["吊索到橋面的局部傳力已完整，所以不需其他反力","主纜端部拉力的反力路徑","主塔承受壓力即可代替所有端部反力"],"optionsEn":["Local hanger-to-deck transfer is complete, so no further reaction is needed","The reaction path for end cable tension","Tower compression can replace all end reactions"],"answer":1,"question":"如果示意圖刪掉主纜端部的錨碇，主要遺漏是什麼？","questionEn":"What is chiefly missing if a sketch omits the main-cable anchorages?","explanation":"錨碇是懸索系統的受力邊界，不能只畫橋面、塔和吊索。","explanationEn":"Anchorages define the suspension system’s force boundary; deck, towers and hangers alone are incomplete."}},{"id":"b003-v6-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-engineering","v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-02"],"title":"拆解海中基礎介面","titleEn":"Separate marine-foundation interfaces","objective":"辨識海床、基礎與橋塔交界各需什麼證據。","objectiveEn":"Identify evidence needed at seabed, foundation and tower interfaces.","instruction":"畫出海床剖面、基礎底面與塔座，列出承載、變形、海床變化三類問題。將施工定位紀錄與營運期海床觀測分成兩欄。","instructionEn":"Draw seabed, foundation base and tower seat. List bearing, deformation and bed-change questions, separating construction-position records from operational seabed observations.","observation":"觀察同一塔頂位移可能來自基礎轉動或塔本身變形。","observationEn":"Recognize that tower-top movement may result from foundation rotation or tower deformation.","failure":"把單一塔頂讀數直接認定為海床承載失效。","failureEn":"Treating one tower-top reading as proof of seabed bearing failure.","check":"為三類問題各指定一種觀察量，並寫明無法由它單獨判定的事項。","checkEn":"Assign one observable to each question and state what it cannot establish alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-03-k1","title":"支承條件","titleEn":"Support conditions","text":"基礎的受力與變形都會影響上部結構的邊界條件。","textEn":"Foundation forces and deformations both affect superstructure boundary conditions."},{"id":"b003-v6-03-k2","title":"分層量測","titleEn":"Measurements at multiple levels","text":"塔頂、塔座及地盤的相對量測有助於區分變形來源。","textEn":"Relative measurements at tower top, base and ground help distinguish deformation sources."}],"quiz":{"options":["只增加同一位置讀數次數，不核對支承","另一次未註記時間的塔頂照片","塔座位移與環境條件的同期紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Repeat readings at the same point without checking support","Another tower-top photograph with no timestamp","Concurrent tower-base displacement and environmental records"],"answer":2,"question":"塔頂偏移增加時，哪組補充資料最有助診斷？","questionEn":"Which additional data best helps diagnose increased tower-top displacement?","explanation":"同步的支承與環境紀錄可檢查不同假說，單點讀數不能定位原因。","explanationEn":"Synchronized support and environmental records test competing explanations; one reading cannot locate the cause."}},{"id":"b003-v6-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview","v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-03"],"title":"核對錨碇與纜索交接","titleEn":"Review anchorage–cable interfaces","objective":"將端部受力模型連結到幾何與耐久檢查。","objectiveEn":"Connect an end-force model to geometry and durability checks.","instruction":"自繪主纜進入錨碇的簡圖，標出拉力傳遞、可檢查空間與水分進入方向。把錨碇和橋塔基礎列成兩個不同構件。","instructionEn":"Sketch a main cable entering an anchorage; mark force transfer, inspection space and possible moisture entry. List the anchorage separately from the tower foundation.","observation":"檢查力能否從纜索一路追蹤到錨碇與地盤。","observationEn":"Check whether the force path can be followed continuously from cable to anchorage and ground.","failure":"以表面塗層完好推論整個錨碇內部都乾燥且健全。","failureEn":"Inferring a dry, sound anchorage interior solely from intact surface coating.","check":"交付受力圖與耐久疑問各一張，註明需要的內部證據。","checkEn":"Provide a force sketch and a durability-question sheet naming the necessary internal evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-04-k1","title":"構件職責","titleEn":"Component roles","text":"主塔支承主纜，端部錨碇承接纜索端力；兩者不應混為一談。","textEn":"Towers support main cables while end anchorages resist end forces; these roles differ."},{"id":"b003-v6-04-k2","title":"可檢查性","titleEn":"Inspectability","text":"無法直接看見的介面，需要事先規劃可追溯的檢查方法。","textEn":"Hidden interfaces require planned, traceable inspection methods."}],"quiz":{"options":["有位置與日期的內部檢查及濕度紀錄","只增加外表面檢查，假定內部條件一致","以當日車流估算內部濕度"],"optionsEn":["Located, dated internal inspection and humidity records","Increase external inspection and assume the interior matches","Infer internal humidity from the day’s traffic"],"answer":0,"question":"哪項證據最能補足錨碇外觀照片的限制？","questionEn":"Which evidence best supplements external anchorage photographs?","explanation":"內部環境和檢查位置才直接對應隱蔽介面的疑問。","explanationEn":"Internal conditions and inspection locations directly address hidden-interface questions."}}],"title":"海峽與受力系統","titleEn":"Strait and structural system","description":"先把航道、地盤與懸索受力放在同一概念模型中。","descriptionEn":"Put navigation, ground conditions and suspension load paths in one conceptual model."},{"id":"b003-stage02","order":2,"steps":[{"id":"b003-v6-05","sequence":5,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview","v6-akashi-engineering"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-04"],"title":"比較主纜形狀與載荷","titleEn":"Compare cable shape and loading","objective":"理解纜索幾何與張力不能分開指定。","objectiveEn":"Understand why cable geometry and tension cannot be specified independently.","instruction":"以鬆弛繩模型或自繪曲線比較兩種下垂程度，在圖上放入相同的示意橋面載荷。只作定性判讀，列出求數值時還缺的材料和邊界資料。","instructionEn":"Compare two cable sags using loose string or sketches under the same illustrative deck load. Keep conclusions qualitative and list missing material and boundary data for numerical analysis.","observation":"觀察曲線變平時，端部力的方向也改變。","observationEn":"Observe that flattening the cable changes the end-force direction.","failure":"把下垂量減少誤認為必然能降低所有纜索力。","failureEn":"Assuming reduced sag necessarily reduces every cable force.","check":"圖中保留相同載荷假設，並說明不能由外形直接求出張力。","checkEn":"Keep the load assumption identical and explain why shape alone cannot give tension.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-05-k1","title":"柔性纜索","titleEn":"Flexible cable","text":"纜索主要以拉力傳力，平衡形狀會隨載荷與支承位置改變。","textEn":"A cable primarily carries tension; its equilibrium shape depends on loading and support positions."},{"id":"b003-v6-05-k2","title":"模型限制","titleEn":"Model limits","text":"繩模型未重現鋼纜剛度、溫度與橋面剛性，只展示幾何關係。","textEn":"A string model illustrates geometry without reproducing steel-cable stiffness, temperature effects or deck rigidity."}],"quiz":{"options":["只控制圖上的跨度，允許載荷不同","載荷與支承條件的假設","只控制纜索材料，忽略支承位置"],"optionsEn":["Hold only drawn span constant while changing the load","Assumptions about loading and supports","Hold only cable material constant and ignore support positions"],"answer":1,"question":"想比較兩種垂度的受力，哪項必須先控制一致？","questionEn":"What should first be held consistent when comparing forces for two sags?","explanation":"在不同載荷或支承下看到的差異不能只歸因於垂度。","explanationEn":"Differences under changed loads or supports cannot be attributed to sag alone."}},{"id":"b003-v6-06","sequence":6,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-engineering"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-05"],"title":"追蹤分段架設狀態","titleEn":"Track staged deck erection","objective":"區分施工中與完工後的平衡系統。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish construction-stage equilibrium from the completed system.","instruction":"把橋面分成六個示意區段，自選兩種安裝先後並逐格畫出已連接構件。每一格標記不平衡載荷與尚未形成的連續性，不安排真實吊裝。","instructionEn":"Divide the deck into six illustrative segments and sketch two assembly sequences. For each state mark unbalanced loads and missing continuity; do not plan an actual lift.","observation":"比較單側增加一段橋面時，主纜和鄰近吊索的受力路徑如何改變。","observationEn":"Compare load-path changes in the main cable and adjacent hangers when a segment is added on one side.","failure":"直接套用完工橋的支承與連續性來評估每個施工格。","failureEn":"Applying completed-bridge support and continuity assumptions to every construction state.","check":"選出一個最需要重新分析的中間狀態，說明理由與缺少資料。","checkEn":"Select an intermediate state needing renewed analysis and explain why and what data is missing.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-06-k1","title":"階段結構","titleEn":"Stage-dependent structure","text":"構件尚未連接時，完工後的載荷重分配途徑可能不存在。","textEn":"Load redistribution available after completion may not exist before components are connected."},{"id":"b003-v6-06-k2","title":"工序依賴","titleEn":"Sequence dependency","text":"幾何調整和構件接合的結果會成為下一階段的初始條件。","textEn":"Geometry adjustment and connection outcomes become initial conditions for the next stage."}],"quiz":{"options":["中間狀態可直接沿用完工載荷分配","每個中間狀態都必定比完工更安全","未完成結構的連接與載荷不同"],"optionsEn":["Intermediate states can use final load distribution unchanged","Every intermediate state is necessarily safer than completion","Connections and loads differ in an incomplete structure"],"answer":2,"question":"哪個理由最能說明需要施工階段分析？","questionEn":"What best explains the need for construction-stage analysis?","explanation":"需要檢查的是當時實際存在的結構系統，而非只看終態。","explanationEn":"The relevant structure is the one that exists at that stage, not only the final state."}},{"id":"b003-v6-07","sequence":7,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-engineering"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-06"],"title":"重建地震後測量基準","titleEn":"Reconcile post-earthquake geometry","objective":"理解基準變動如何影響尚未製造的構件。","objectiveEn":"Understand how changed reference geometry affects unfabricated components.","instruction":"依 1995 年事件畫出「地震前控制點—震後復測—更新模型—複核構件」流程。用自設的小位移示例，分開記錄地盤移動與構件相對變形。","instructionEn":"Based on the 1995 event, map pre-event controls, resurvey, model update and component review. In a clearly invented displacement example, separate ground movement from relative component deformation.","observation":"比較兩塔間距變化與塔本身損傷是否是不同證據問題。","observationEn":"Distinguish a changed tower spacing from evidence of damage within a tower.","failure":"控制點移動後，仍把舊座標當成固定真值調整構件。","failureEn":"Adjusting components to old coordinates after the control points have moved.","check":"記錄示例新舊基準、相對距離與待重審構件，禁止把示例值當實測。","checkEn":"Record old and new references, relative distances and components needing review; label every example value as invented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-07-k1","title":"共同位移","titleEn":"Common movement","text":"地盤與基礎共同移動，與基礎對地盤滑動，是不同的機制。","textEn":"Ground and foundation moving together differs from a foundation sliding relative to ground."},{"id":"b003-v6-07-k2","title":"版本追溯","titleEn":"Version traceability","text":"幾何基準修訂要能追溯到分析模型與待製構件版本。","textEn":"A revised geometric reference must be traceable to model and component versions."}],"quiz":{"options":["仍須復測並檢查模型與構件介面","外觀正常即可忽略幾何改變","立即判定所有基礎已滑動"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey and review model and component interfaces","Normal appearance makes geometry changes irrelevant","Conclude immediately that all foundations slid"],"answer":0,"question":"震後塔距改變，但構件外觀無明顯損傷，應如何解讀？","questionEn":"Tower spacing changes after an earthquake without visible member damage. What follows?","explanation":"外觀、相對位移與受力是不同證據層次，須整合後判斷。","explanationEn":"Appearance, relative displacement and force behavior are different evidence layers that must be reconciled."}},{"id":"b003-v6-08","sequence":8,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-engineering","v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-07"],"title":"分辨靜風與振動問題","titleEn":"Distinguish static wind and vibration","objective":"識別風力、變形與振動穩定性所需的不同模型。","objectiveEn":"Identify different models for wind force, deformation and dynamic stability.","instruction":"為靜態側向風力、渦激反應與扭轉振動各寫一個研究問題。以自繪位移—時間曲線比較衰減、持續與增長，避免賦予真實橋梁限值。","instructionEn":"Write separate questions about static crosswind force, vortex-induced response and torsional vibration. Sketch decaying, sustained and growing motion without assigning real-bridge limits.","observation":"觀察平均位移相近的曲線，振幅隨時間的變化仍可能不同。","observationEn":"Curves with similar mean displacement can have different amplitude trends over time.","failure":"只檢查最大靜態撓度，就宣稱已驗證所有風振現象。","failureEn":"Claiming all wind behavior is verified by checking maximum static deflection alone.","check":"將三種問題配對到合適的觀察量，標示定性曲線。","checkEn":"Match the three questions to suitable observables and label curves as qualitative.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-08-k1","title":"時間尺度","titleEn":"Time scale","text":"穩定平均風荷載與反覆振動需要不同的證據描述。","textEn":"Steady mean wind loading and repeated oscillation require different evidence descriptions."},{"id":"b003-v6-08-k2","title":"能量與阻尼","titleEn":"Energy and damping","text":"阻尼消散振動能量；它與單純提高靜態剛度的作用不同。","textEn":"Damping dissipates vibration energy, which differs from simply increasing static stiffness."}],"quiz":{"options":["圖上平均位移的方向","振幅是否隨時間增長","圖中使用的長度單位"],"optionsEn":["Direction of the plotted mean displacement","Whether vibration amplitude grows over time","Length units shown on the plot"],"answer":1,"question":"哪個現象無法由一張平均撓度圖充分判斷？","questionEn":"What cannot be adequately judged from a mean-deflection plot?","explanation":"振動增長需要時間或動態穩定性資訊；平均量會隱藏它。","explanationEn":"Growth requires time-dependent or stability information; averages can hide it."}}],"title":"架設與幾何控制","titleEn":"Erection and geometric control","description":"比較未完成結構的平衡、基準變更與風振假設。","descriptionEn":"Compare incomplete-structure equilibrium, changed survey references and wind-response assumptions."},{"id":"b003-stage03","order":3,"steps":[{"id":"b003-v6-09","sequence":9,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-08"],"title":"畫出主纜乾燥屏障","titleEn":"Map the cable drying barrier","objective":"說明外包覆與內部乾燥的互補關係。","objectiveEn":"Explain how wrapping and internal drying complement each other.","instruction":"自繪主纜包覆、送氣、排氣及濕度觀測點的功能圖。為「包覆局部進水」與「送氣中斷」各列一項可觀察證據，不指定設備參數。","instructionEn":"Sketch functional roles of cable wrapping, air supply, exhaust and humidity observations. For local water ingress and interrupted air supply, name evidence without specifying operating parameters.","observation":"檢查進氣正常是否仍可能與局部高濕並存。","observationEn":"Ask whether normal inlet air can coexist with a locally humid region.","failure":"以乾燥機正在運轉，取代主纜內部環境的證據。","failureEn":"Substituting evidence that a dryer is running for evidence about conditions inside the cable.","check":"圖上須有兩個不同失效路徑與對應觀察點。","checkEn":"Include two distinct failure paths and corresponding observation locations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-09-k1","title":"防蝕多重屏障","titleEn":"Complementary corrosion barriers","text":"外包覆抑制水分進入，乾燥系統改善內部環境；兩者提供不同功能。","textEn":"Wrapping limits moisture entry while drying changes internal conditions; the functions differ."},{"id":"b003-v6-09-k2","title":"代表性採樣","titleEn":"Representative sampling","text":"一個位置的濕度，不能自動代表整條纜索的狀態。","textEn":"Humidity measured at one point does not automatically represent the entire cable."}],"quiz":{"options":["直接把遠端讀值刪除","用乾燥機功率證明全纜乾燥","核對量測與局部氣流或包覆異常"],"optionsEn":["Delete the distant reading","Use dryer power as proof the entire cable is dry","Check measurements and local airflow or wrapping anomalies"],"answer":2,"question":"送氣端讀值正常而遠端濕度偏高，最合理的下一步是什麼？","questionEn":"Inlet readings are normal but a distant point is humid. What is the best next review?","explanation":"不同位置的差異可能提供局部失效線索，須先查證。","explanationEn":"Differences between locations may reveal local failure and require verification."}},{"id":"b003-v6-10","sequence":10,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-09"],"title":"辨認重複載荷與接頭","titleEn":"Identify repeated loading at connections","objective":"區分疲勞、腐蝕與單次超載的證據。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish evidence of fatigue, corrosion and one-time overload.","instruction":"在自繪鋼橋面接頭示意上標記幾何變化處，建立三欄：反覆交通載荷、水分滯留、單次異常事件。為每欄列一種需要查證的紀錄。","instructionEn":"Mark geometric changes on a steel-deck connection sketch. Create columns for repeated traffic loading, trapped moisture and a single abnormal event, assigning evidence to each.","observation":"留意細小裂紋的位置及歷次變化，比單一遠景照片更具診斷性。","observationEn":"Crack location and change over time are more diagnostic than one distant photograph.","failure":"看到鏽色就把所有裂紋歸因於腐蝕，忽略載荷歷程。","failureEn":"Attributing every crack to corrosion because rust is visible, without considering load history.","check":"完成三種機制的證據表，至少列一項仍不能排除的替代解釋。","checkEn":"Complete the three-mechanism evidence table and retain at least one alternative explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-10-k1","title":"局部細節","titleEn":"Local details","text":"幾何不連續可能集中應力；整體受力正常不保證每個接頭無問題。","textEn":"Geometric discontinuities can concentrate stress; normal global behavior does not prove every connection sound."},{"id":"b003-v6-10-k2","title":"機制辨識","titleEn":"Mechanism identification","text":"裂紋形態、環境與載荷歷程應一起判讀，不能只靠顏色。","textEn":"Crack form, environment and load history should be interpreted together rather than from color alone."}],"quiz":{"options":["同位置、同尺度的歷次量測","不同位置的裂紋照片但沒有時間對照","只記錄當日總車流，不核對裂紋位置"],"optionsEn":["Repeated measurements at the same location and scale","Crack photographs from different locations without time comparison","Record only daily traffic without locating the crack"],"answer":0,"question":"哪項資料最有助區分持續發展的裂紋與穩定表面痕跡？","questionEn":"Which data best distinguishes a developing crack from a stable surface mark?","explanation":"可比較的時間序列才提供變化證據；外觀單照缺少發展資訊。","explanationEn":"Comparable time-series observations provide change evidence that a single image lacks."}},{"id":"b003-v6-11","sequence":11,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-10"],"title":"校正監測比較條件","titleEn":"Normalize monitoring comparisons","objective":"避免把溫度或儀器差異誤認為結構劣化。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mistaking environmental or instrument differences for structural deterioration.","instruction":"自行製作含時間、溫度、風況、感測器和位移的六列示例表。選出可直接比較的兩列，再為其餘列註記需校正或補查的條件。","instructionEn":"Create a six-row example table with time, temperature, wind, sensor and displacement. Select two comparable rows and mark conditions requiring adjustment or investigation in the others.","observation":"觀察位移異常是否與換感測器或環境改變同時發生。","observationEn":"See whether displacement changes coincide with sensor replacement or environmental changes.","failure":"把不同零點或不同溫度的資料直接相減，產生假趨勢。","failureEn":"Direct subtraction across different zero references or temperatures creates a false trend.","check":"保留原始示例值、比較依據與未解釋的殘差，不覆寫原紀錄。","checkEn":"Retain original example values, comparison criteria and unexplained residuals without overwriting records.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-11-k1","title":"基線條件","titleEn":"Baseline conditions","text":"基線不只是單一數值，還包括量測時間、環境、設備與基準。","textEn":"A baseline includes time, environment, instrument and reference, not just one value."},{"id":"b003-v6-11-k2","title":"可重現性","titleEn":"Reproducibility","text":"他人應能利用相同選取規則重建你的比較結果。","textEn":"Another reviewer should reproduce the comparison using the same selection rules."}],"quiz":{"options":["直接宣告主纜斷裂","新舊感測器的零點和交接紀錄","把前後資料平均後忽略跳變"],"optionsEn":["Immediately declare main-cable rupture","Old and new sensor zero references and handover records","Average the records and disregard the jump"],"answer":1,"question":"更換感測器當天出現位移跳變，應優先核對什麼？","questionEn":"A displacement jump appears on the day a sensor is replaced. What should be checked first?","explanation":"先排查量測系統變動，再結合結構和環境證據判讀。","explanationEn":"Check measurement-system changes before interpreting structural and environmental evidence."}},{"id":"b003-v6-12","sequence":12,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-akashi-overview","v6-akashi-engineering","v6-akashi-maintenance"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-11"],"title":"交付懸索橋證據卷宗","titleEn":"Deliver a suspension-bridge evidence dossier","objective":"把結構、施工與維護的未解問題交接清楚。","objectiveEn":"Clearly hand over unresolved structural, construction and maintenance questions.","instruction":"把前述圖表整理成索引：載荷路徑、基準版本、架設狀態、風振問題及纜索防蝕。對每份資料註明來源、假設與支持的判斷範圍。","instructionEn":"Index your load-path, reference-version, erection-state, wind-response and corrosion records. For each, identify source, assumptions and the conclusion it can support.","observation":"檢查是否把某一階段的分析誤用為整橋所有狀態的證明。","observationEn":"Check whether evidence for one stage has been mistaken for proof of every bridge state.","failure":"只交付漂亮模型，沒有資料版本、量測條件或待確認事項。","failureEn":"Delivering an attractive model without versions, measurement conditions or unresolved items.","check":"以「已支持／未支持／需專業複核」分類至少五項判斷。","checkEn":"Classify at least five conclusions as supported, unsupported or requiring professional review.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v6-12-k1","title":"證據對應","titleEn":"Evidence matching","text":"每項結論需對應適用狀態與資料，不能用一張圖概括全生命週期。","textEn":"Each conclusion requires applicable conditions and evidence; one sketch cannot cover an entire life cycle."},{"id":"b003-v6-12-k2","title":"教育交付","titleEn":"Educational deliverable","text":"課程完成代表學習證據齊備，不等於取得真橋施工或通行安全認證。","textEn":"Course completion records learning evidence, not construction or operational safety certification for the real bridge."}],"quiz":{"options":["只保留沒有圖例的完工圖像","刪除所有不確定事項以顯得完整","含來源版本、假設與未解問題的索引"],"optionsEn":["Only a finished image without a key","Delete uncertainties to make the work look complete","An index with source versions, assumptions and open questions"],"answer":2,"question":"哪份交付最適合另一位工程學徒接續？","questionEn":"Which handover best enables another learner to continue?","explanation":"可追溯性使下一位能看出已知與未知，避免把示意當定案。","explanationEn":"Traceability distinguishes known from unknown and prevents treating a sketch as an approved design."}}],"title":"耐久與營運證據","titleEn":"Durability and operating evidence","description":"把纜索、鋼構與感測紀錄連結到可追溯的維護判斷。","descriptionEn":"Connect cable, steelwork and sensor records to traceable maintenance decisions."},{"id":"b003-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速」與「長週期模態與地震輸入」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder\" and \"Long-period modes and seismic input\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b003-v13-01","title":"桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v6-12"],"objective":"說明「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Truss flutter margin” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主跨接近 2 km 時，加勁梁的扭轉頻率與豎彎頻率都很低，風在某一速度下會讓兩者耦合成自激的顫振：氣動力隨扭轉角輸入能量，總阻尼由正轉負，振幅在數個週期內發散。明石海峽大橋採用約 35.5 m 寬、14 m 深的開放式鋼桁架，橋面設置格柵開口與中央垂直穩定板，目的是打亂橋面上下的壓力差、提高顫振臨界風速。桁架斷面的氣動導數與流線形箱梁差異很大，只能靠斷面模型與全橋模型試驗確定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When the main span approaches 2 km, both the torsional and the vertical bending frequencies of the stiffening girder are very low, and at some wind speed the two couple into self-excited flutter: aerodynamic forces feed energy through the twist angle, total damping turns negative and the amplitude diverges within a few cycles. Akashi Kaikyo uses an open steel truss about 35.5 m wide and 14 m deep, with gratings in the deck and a central vertical stabiliser, to disrupt the pressure difference across the deck and raise the flutter onset speed. The aerodynamic derivatives of a truss differ greatly from those of a streamlined box, so they can only be fixed by section-model and full-bridge model tests. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Truss flutter margin” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Selberg 平板估算 U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Selberg flat-plate estimate U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)].","failure":"常見誤解：「桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Truss flutter margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-01-k1","title":"桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速","titleEn":"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder","text":"主跨接近 2 km 時，加勁梁的扭轉頻率與豎彎頻率都很低，風在某一速度下會讓兩者耦合成自激的顫振：氣動力隨扭轉角輸入能量，總阻尼由正轉負，振幅在數個週期內發散。明石海峽大橋採用約 35.5 m 寬、14 m 深的開放式鋼桁架，橋面設置格柵開口與中央垂直穩定板，目的是打亂橋面上下的壓力差、提高顫振臨界風速。","textEn":"When the main span approaches 2 km, both the torsional and the vertical bending frequencies of the stiffening girder are very low, and at some wind speed the two couple into self-excited flutter: aerodynamic forces feed energy through the twist angle, total damping turns negative and the amplitude diverges within a few cycles. Akashi Kaikyo uses an open steel truss about 35.5 m wide and 14 m deep, with gratings in the deck and a central vertical stabiliser, to disrupt the pressure difference across the deck and raise the flutter onset speed.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder\" is correct?","options":["桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。","主跨接近 2 km 時，加勁梁的扭轉頻率與豎彎頻率都很低，風在某一速度下會讓兩者耦合成自激的顫振：氣動力隨扭轉角輸入能量，總阻尼由正轉負，振幅在數個週期內發散。","懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter.","When the main span approaches 2 km, both the torsional and the vertical bending frequencies of the stiffening girder are very low, and at some wind speed the two couple into self-excited flutter: aerodynamic forces feed energy through the twist angle, total damping turns negative and the amplitude diverges within a few cycles.","A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主跨接近 2 km 時，加勁梁的扭轉頻率與豎彎頻率都很低，風在某一速度下會讓兩者耦合成自激的顫振：氣動力隨扭轉角輸入能量，總阻尼由正轉負，振幅在數個週期內發散。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When the main span approaches 2 km, both the torsional and the vertical bending frequencies of the stiffening girder are very low, and at some wind speed the two couple into self-excited flutter: aerodynamic forces feed energy through the twist angle, total damping turns negative and the amplitude diverges within a few cycles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":13},{"id":"b003-v13-02","title":"桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速：定量估算","titleEn":"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Truss flutter margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Selberg 平板估算 U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]。取 B = 35.5 m、m = 44,000 kg/m、I = 6.0×10⁶ kg·m²/m、f_B = 0.065 Hz、f_T = 0.16 Hz、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：ω_T = 1.005 rad/s，√(m·I)/(ρB³) = 513,800/55,920 = 9.19，U_F = 0.44×35.5×1.005×√(0.835×9.19) ≈ 43 m/s；f_T 提高到 0.18 Hz 時約 50 m/s。數值為教學假設，平板公式對桁架只作量級比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Selberg flat-plate estimate U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]. With B = 35.5 m, m = 44,000 kg/m, I = 6.0×10⁶ kg·m²/m, f_B = 0.065 Hz, f_T = 0.16 Hz and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³: ω_T = 1.005 rad/s, √(m·I)/(ρB³) = 513,800/55,920 = 9.19, so U_F = 0.44×35.5×1.005×√(0.835×9.19) ≈ 43 m/s; raising f_T to 0.18 Hz gives about 50 m/s. Values are teaching assumptions; for a truss the flat-plate formula only gives an order of magnitude. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以斷面模型強迫振動試驗量測 Scanlan 氣動導數 H*、A*，代入多模態顫振分析求臨界風速，再與全橋氣彈模型在紊流中的發散風速比較；驗收以顫振臨界風速高於規範的照查風速（設計風速乘陣風與安全係數）為準，並檢查不同風攻角（例如 ±3°）下的最低值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure Scanlan aerodynamic derivatives H* and A* with forced-oscillation section-model tests, feed them into a multi-mode flutter analysis, and compare the predicted onset speed with the divergence speed of a full aeroelastic model in turbulent flow; acceptance requires the flutter onset to exceed the code verification speed (design wind times gust and safety factors), checking the lowest value over angles of attack such as ±3°.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Selberg 平板估算 U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]。取 B = 35.5 m、m = 44,000 kg/m、I = 6.0×10⁶ kg·m²/m、f_B = 0.065 Hz、f_T = 0.16 Hz、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：ω_T = 1.005 rad/s，√(m·I)/(ρB³) = 513,800/55,920 = 9.19，U_F = 0.44×35.5×1.005×√(0.835×9.19) ≈ 43 m/s；f_T 提高到 0.18 Hz 時約 50 m/s。數值為教學假設，平板公式對桁架只作量級比較。","textEn":"Selberg flat-plate estimate U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]. With B = 35.5 m, m = 44,000 kg/m, I = 6.0×10⁶ kg·m²/m, f_B = 0.065 Hz, f_T = 0.16 Hz and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³: ω_T = 1.005 rad/s, √(m·I)/(ρB³) = 513,800/55,920 = 9.19, so U_F = 0.44×35.5×1.005×√(0.835×9.19) ≈ 43 m/s; raising f_T to 0.18 Hz gives about 50 m/s. Values are teaching assumptions; for a truss the flat-plate formula only gives an order of magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder\", which statement holds?","options":["水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。","地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","Selberg 平板估算 U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]。"],"optionsEn":["If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality.","After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","Selberg flat-plate estimate U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Selberg 平板估算 U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Selberg flat-plate estimate U_F = 0.44·B·ω_T·√[(1 − (f_B/f_T)²)·√(m·I)/(ρB³)]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":14},{"id":"b003-v13-03","title":"桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Truss flutter margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以斷面模型強迫振動試驗量測 Scanlan 氣動導數 H*、A*，代入多模態顫振分析求臨界風速，再與全橋氣彈模型在紊流中的發散風速比較；驗收以顫振臨界風速高於規範的照查風速（設計風速乘陣風與安全係數）為準，並檢查不同風攻角（例如 ±3°）下的最低值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure Scanlan aerodynamic derivatives H* and A* with forced-oscillation section-model tests, feed them into a multi-mode flutter analysis, and compare the predicted onset speed with the divergence speed of a full aeroelastic model in turbulent flow; acceptance requires the flutter onset to exceed the code verification speed (design wind times gust and safety factors), checking the lowest value over angles of attack such as ±3°. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何在加勁桁架上新增的檢修走道、管線或防護網，都要先由風工程師評估對格柵開孔率與穩定板的影響，必要時補做斷面模型試驗；維護計畫須把格柵清潔列為定期項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: Any walkway, duct or screen added to the stiffening truss must first be assessed by the wind engineer for its effect on grating porosity and the stabiliser, with a new section-model test if needed; the maintenance plan must list grating cleaning as a routine item.","failure":"注意干擾：若沿用平板或箱梁的經驗值而未針對桁架做試驗，可能高估臨界風速；顫振一旦發生，扭轉振幅在數分鐘內增長，1940 年塔科馬海峽橋就是以扭轉發散破壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Borrowing flat-plate or box-girder values without testing the truss can overestimate the onset speed; once flutter starts, torsional amplitude grows within minutes, as in the torsional collapse of the Tacoma Narrows Bridge in 1940. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以斷面模型強迫振動試驗量測 Scanlan 氣動導數 H*、A*，代入多模態顫振分析求臨界風速，再與全橋氣彈模型在紊流中的發散風速比較；驗收以顫振臨界風速高於規範的照查風速（設計風速乘陣風與安全係數）為準，並檢查不同風攻角（例如 ±3°）下的最低值。","textEn":"Measure Scanlan aerodynamic derivatives H* and A* with forced-oscillation section-model tests, feed them into a multi-mode flutter analysis, and compare the predicted onset speed with the divergence speed of a full aeroelastic model in turbulent flow; acceptance requires the flutter onset to exceed the code verification speed (design wind times gust and safety factors), checking the lowest value over angles of attack such as ±3°.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何在加勁桁架上新增的檢修走道、管線或防護網，都要先由風工程師評估對格柵開孔率與穩定板的影響，必要時補做斷面模型試驗；維護計畫須把格柵清潔列為定期項目。","textEn":"Any walkway, duct or screen added to the stiffening truss must first be assessed by the wind engineer for its effect on grating porosity and the stabiliser, with a new section-model test if needed; the maintenance plan must list grating cleaning as a routine item.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder\"?","options":["以斷面模型強迫振動試驗量測 Scanlan 氣動導數 H*、A*，代入多模態顫振分析求臨界風速，再與全橋氣彈模型在紊流中的發散風速比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。"],"optionsEn":["Measure Scanlan aerodynamic derivatives H* and A* with forced-oscillation section-model tests, feed them into a multi-mode flutter analysis, and compare the predicted onset speed with the divergence speed of a full aeroelastic model in turbulent flow.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以斷面模型強迫振動試驗量測 Scanlan 氣動導數 H*、A*，代入多模態顫振分析求臨界風速，再與全橋氣彈模型在紊流中的發散風速比較；驗收以顫振臨界風速高於規範的照查風速（設計風速乘陣風與安全係數）為準，並檢查不同風攻角（例如 ±3°）下的最低值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure Scanlan aerodynamic derivatives H* and A* with forced-oscillation section-model tests, feed them into a multi-mode flutter analysis, and compare the predicted onset speed with the divergence speed of a full aeroelastic model in turbulent flow; acceptance requires the flutter onset to exceed the code verification speed (design wind times gust and safety factors), checking the lowest value over angles of attack such as ±3°. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":15},{"id":"b003-v13-04","title":"桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「桁架加勁梁顫振裕度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Truss flutter margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沿用平板或箱梁的經驗值而未針對桁架做試驗，可能高估臨界風速；顫振一旦發生，扭轉振幅在數分鐘內增長，1940 年塔科馬海峽橋就是以扭轉發散破壞。格柵被雜物或後加設備堵塞，也會讓實橋氣動特性偏離試驗斷面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Borrowing flat-plate or box-girder values without testing the truss can overestimate the onset speed; once flutter starts, torsional amplitude grows within minutes, as in the torsional collapse of the Tacoma Narrows Bridge in 1940. Gratings blocked by debris or later-added equipment also move the real deck away from the tested section. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：桁架斷面的氣動導數與流線形箱梁差異很大，只能靠斷面模型與全橋模型試驗確定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The aerodynamic derivatives of a truss differ greatly from those of a streamlined box, so they can only be fixed by section-model and full-bridge model tests.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沿用平板或箱梁的經驗值而未針對桁架做試驗，可能高估臨界風速；顫振一旦發生，扭轉振幅在數分鐘內增長，1940 年塔科馬海峽橋就是以扭轉發散破壞。格柵被雜物或後加設備堵塞，也會讓實橋氣動特性偏離試驗斷面。","textEn":"Borrowing flat-plate or box-girder values without testing the truss can overestimate the onset speed; once flutter starts, torsional amplitude grows within minutes, as in the torsional collapse of the Tacoma Narrows Bridge in 1940. Gratings blocked by debris or later-added equipment also move the real deck away from the tested section.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「桁架加勁梁的顫振臨界風速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flutter onset of the truss stiffening girder\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若沿用平板或箱梁的經驗值而未針對桁架做試驗，可能高估臨界風速；顫振一旦發生，扭轉振幅在數分鐘內增長，1940 年塔科馬海峽橋就是以扭轉發散破壞。","懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Borrowing flat-plate or box-girder values without testing the truss can overestimate the onset speed.","A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若沿用平板或箱梁的經驗值而未針對桁架做試驗，可能高估臨界風速；顫振一旦發生，扭轉振幅在數分鐘內增長，1940 年塔科馬海峽橋就是以扭轉發散破壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Borrowing flat-plate or box-girder values without testing the truss can overestimate the onset speed; once flutter starts, torsional amplitude grows within minutes, as in the torsional collapse of the Tacoma Narrows Bridge in 1940. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":16},{"id":"b003-v13-05","title":"長週期模態與地震輸入：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-period modes and seismic input: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「長週期豎彎模態」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-period vertical modes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"懸索橋的豎向勁度主要來自主纜的重力張力，而不是加勁梁的彎曲勁度，因此低階模態週期可長達十秒以上，像一條張緊的弦。這使主跨對短週期地震加速度不敏感，卻對長週期地震波、海峽地盤的大變位與基礎間的相對位移很敏感。明石海峽大橋的耐震設計考慮規模 8.5 級的板塊交界地震，並把基礎設在避開活動斷層的位置；但 1995 年兵庫縣南部地震的斷層錯動仍使地盤與基礎一起移動，提醒設計者：相對位移與絕對加速度是兩個不同的設計問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「長週期豎彎模態」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The vertical stiffness of a suspension bridge comes mainly from the gravity tension in its main cables rather than the bending stiffness of the stiffening girder, so the lowest modes can have periods of more than ten seconds, like a taut string. The main span is therefore insensitive to short-period ground acceleration but sensitive to long-period waves, large ground displacement in the strait and relative movement between foundations. The Akashi Kaikyo design considered a magnitude 8.5 interplate earthquake and sited foundations away from active faults, yet in the 1995 Hyogo-ken Nanbu earthquake fault movement still carried the ground and foundations together, a reminder that relative displacement and absolute acceleration are two separate design problems. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Long-period vertical modes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以弦近似，反對稱第一豎彎頻率 f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: In the string approximation the first antisymmetric vertical frequency is f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m).","failure":"常見誤解：「懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「長週期豎彎模態」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Long-period vertical modes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-05-k1","title":"長週期模態與地震輸入","titleEn":"Long-period modes and seismic input","text":"懸索橋的豎向勁度主要來自主纜的重力張力，而不是加勁梁的彎曲勁度，因此低階模態週期可長達十秒以上，像一條張緊的弦。這使主跨對短週期地震加速度不敏感，卻對長週期地震波、海峽地盤的大變位與基礎間的相對位移很敏感。","textEn":"The vertical stiffness of a suspension bridge comes mainly from the gravity tension in its main cables rather than the bending stiffness of the stiffening girder, so the lowest modes can have periods of more than ten seconds, like a taut string. The main span is therefore insensitive to short-period ground acceleration but sensitive to long-period waves, large ground displacement in the strait and relative movement between foundations.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長週期模態與地震輸入」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-period modes and seismic input\" is correct?","options":["懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。","鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。","懸索橋的豎向勁度主要來自主纜的重力張力，而不是加勁梁的彎曲勁度，因此低階模態週期可長達十秒以上，像一條張緊的弦。"],"optionsEn":["A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it.","The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.","The vertical stiffness of a suspension bridge comes mainly from the gravity tension in its main cables rather than the bending stiffness of the stiffening girder, so the lowest modes can have periods of more than ten seconds, like a taut string."],"answer":2,"explanation":"懸索橋的豎向勁度主要來自主纜的重力張力，而不是加勁梁的彎曲勁度，因此低階模態週期可長達十秒以上，像一條張緊的弦。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The vertical stiffness of a suspension bridge comes mainly from the gravity tension in its main cables rather than the bending stiffness of the stiffening girder, so the lowest modes can have periods of more than ten seconds, like a taut string. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":17},{"id":"b003-v13-06","title":"長週期模態與地震輸入：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-period modes and seismic input: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長週期豎彎模態」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-period vertical modes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以弦近似，反對稱第一豎彎頻率 f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m)。取兩纜合計 H = 1,074 MN、m = 44,000 kg/m、l = 1,991 m：√(1.074×10⁹/44,000) = 156 m/s，f ≈ 156/1,991 = 0.078 Hz，週期約 12.7 s。若 m 增加 10%，週期增為約 13.4 s。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: In the string approximation the first antisymmetric vertical frequency is f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m). With H = 1,074 MN for both cables, m = 44,000 kg/m and l = 1,991 m: √(1.074×10⁹/44,000) = 156 m/s, f ≈ 156/1,991 = 0.078 Hz and the period is about 12.7 s. A 10% increase in m lengthens the period to about 13.4 s. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把手算弦頻率與有限元素模態分析比較，確認前幾個模態的形狀（對稱、反對稱、側向、扭轉）與排序；耐震檢核需同時輸入長週期設計波與各基礎不同步的地盤位移，並把塔頂、索鞍與伸縮縫的相對位移與容許值逐一比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare the hand string frequency with finite-element modal analysis, confirming the shape and order of the first modes (symmetric, antisymmetric, lateral, torsional); seismic checks must input long-period design motions and non-synchronous ground displacement at each foundation, comparing relative displacement at tower tops, saddles and expansion joints with their allowances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以弦近似，反對稱第一豎彎頻率 f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m)。取兩纜合計 H = 1,074 MN、m = 44,000 kg/m、l = 1,991 m：√(1.074×10⁹/44,000) = 156 m/s，f ≈ 156/1,991 = 0.078 Hz，週期約 12.7 s。若 m 增加 10%，週期增為約 13.4 s。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"In the string approximation the first antisymmetric vertical frequency is f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m). With H = 1,074 MN for both cables, m = 44,000 kg/m and l = 1,991 m: √(1.074×10⁹/44,000) = 156 m/s, f ≈ 156/1,991 = 0.078 Hz and the period is about 12.7 s. A 10% increase in m lengthens the period to about 13.4 s. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長週期模態與地震輸入」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-period modes and seismic input\", which statement holds?","options":["以弦近似，反對稱第一豎彎頻率 f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m)。","索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。","全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["In the string approximation the first antisymmetric vertical frequency is f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m).","Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces.","A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以弦近似，反對稱第一豎彎頻率 f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"In the string approximation the first antisymmetric vertical frequency is f ≈ (1/l)·√(H/m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":18},{"id":"b003-v13-07","title":"長週期模態與地震輸入：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-period modes and seismic input: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長週期豎彎模態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-period vertical modes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把手算弦頻率與有限元素模態分析比較，確認前幾個模態的形狀（對稱、反對稱、側向、扭轉）與排序；耐震檢核需同時輸入長週期設計波與各基礎不同步的地盤位移，並把塔頂、索鞍與伸縮縫的相對位移與容許值逐一比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare the hand string frequency with finite-element modal analysis, confirming the shape and order of the first modes (symmetric, antisymmetric, lateral, torsional); seismic checks must input long-period design motions and non-synchronous ground displacement at each foundation, comparing relative displacement at tower tops, saddles and expansion joints with their allowances. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：耐震設計書應列出各基礎的地盤位移假設與斷層位置圖，並把相對位移需求寫進伸縮縫、支承與索鞍的採購規格；完工後的模態實測要回饋修正模型，作為日後事件評估的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: The seismic design report should list ground-displacement assumptions for each foundation with a fault-location map, and write the relative-displacement demand into expansion-joint, bearing and saddle specifications; measured modes after completion must update the model as the baseline for future event assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：只用單一同步地震波分析時，會低估塔與錨碇之間的相對位移，伸縮縫、支承與索鞍可能超出行程；長週期波若與主跨低階模態接近，加勁梁位移可能遠大於以加速度反應譜估算的結果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Analysing with a single synchronous record underestimates relative movement between towers and anchorages, so expansion joints, bearings and saddles may exceed their travel; long-period waves near the low modes of the main span can produce girder displacements far larger than an acceleration-spectrum estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把手算弦頻率與有限元素模態分析比較，確認前幾個模態的形狀（對稱、反對稱、側向、扭轉）與排序；耐震檢核需同時輸入長週期設計波與各基礎不同步的地盤位移，並把塔頂、索鞍與伸縮縫的相對位移與容許值逐一比對。","textEn":"Compare the hand string frequency with finite-element modal analysis, confirming the shape and order of the first modes (symmetric, antisymmetric, lateral, torsional); seismic checks must input long-period design motions and non-synchronous ground displacement at each foundation, comparing relative displacement at tower tops, saddles and expansion joints with their allowances.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"耐震設計書應列出各基礎的地盤位移假設與斷層位置圖，並把相對位移需求寫進伸縮縫、支承與索鞍的採購規格；完工後的模態實測要回饋修正模型，作為日後事件評估的基準。","textEn":"The seismic design report should list ground-displacement assumptions for each foundation with a fault-location map, and write the relative-displacement demand into expansion-joint, bearing and saddle specifications; measured modes after completion must update the model as the baseline for future event assessments.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長週期模態與地震輸入」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-period modes and seismic input\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把手算弦頻率與有限元素模態分析比較，確認前幾個模態的形狀（對稱、反對稱、側向、扭轉）與排序。","主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Compare the hand string frequency with finite-element modal analysis, confirming the shape and order of the first modes (symmetric, antisymmetric, lateral, torsional).","With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把手算弦頻率與有限元素模態分析比較，確認前幾個模態的形狀（對稱、反對稱、側向、扭轉）與排序；耐震檢核需同時輸入長週期設計波與各基礎不同步的地盤位移，並把塔頂、索鞍與伸縮縫的相對位移與容許值逐一比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare the hand string frequency with finite-element modal analysis, confirming the shape and order of the first modes (symmetric, antisymmetric, lateral, torsional); seismic checks must input long-period design motions and non-synchronous ground displacement at each foundation, comparing relative displacement at tower tops, saddles and expansion joints with their allowances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":19},{"id":"b003-v13-08","title":"長週期模態與地震輸入：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-period modes and seismic input: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長週期豎彎模態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-period vertical modes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用單一同步地震波分析時，會低估塔與錨碇之間的相對位移，伸縮縫、支承與索鞍可能超出行程；長週期波若與主跨低階模態接近，加勁梁位移可能遠大於以加速度反應譜估算的結果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Analysing with a single synchronous record underestimates relative movement between towers and anchorages, so expansion joints, bearings and saddles may exceed their travel; long-period waves near the low modes of the main span can produce girder displacements far larger than an acceleration-spectrum estimate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：明石海峽大橋的耐震設計考慮規模 8.5 級的板塊交界地震，並把基礎設在避開活動斷層的位置；但 1995 年兵庫縣南部地震的斷層錯動仍使地盤與基礎一起移動，提醒設計者：相對位移與絕對加速度是兩個不同的設計問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Akashi Kaikyo design considered a magnitude 8.5 interplate earthquake and sited foundations away from active faults, yet in the 1995 Hyogo-ken Nanbu earthquake fault movement still carried the ground and foundations together, a reminder that relative displacement and absolute acceleration are two separate design problems.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用單一同步地震波分析時，會低估塔與錨碇之間的相對位移，伸縮縫、支承與索鞍可能超出行程；長週期波若與主跨低階模態接近，加勁梁位移可能遠大於以加速度反應譜估算的結果。","textEn":"Analysing with a single synchronous record underestimates relative movement between towers and anchorages, so expansion joints, bearings and saddles may exceed their travel; long-period waves near the low modes of the main span can produce girder displacements far larger than an acceleration-spectrum estimate.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長週期模態與地震輸入」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-period modes and seismic input\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。","只用單一同步地震波分析時，會低估塔與錨碇之間的相對位移，伸縮縫、支承與索鞍可能超出行程。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.","Analysing with a single synchronous record underestimates relative movement between towers and anchorages, so expansion joints, bearings and saddles may exceed their travel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用單一同步地震波分析時，會低估塔與錨碇之間的相對位移，伸縮縫、支承與索鞍可能超出行程；長週期波若與主跨低階模態接近，加勁梁位移可能遠大於以加速度反應譜估算的結果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Analysing with a single synchronous record underestimates relative movement between towers and anchorages, so expansion joints, bearings and saddles may exceed their travel; long-period waves near the low modes of the main span can produce girder displacements far larger than an acceleration-spectrum estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":20}],"order":4},{"id":"b003-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面」與「設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"High-strength wire and the single-cable section\" and \"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b003-v13-09","title":"高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"High-strength wire and the single-cable section: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主纜是懸索橋最難更換的構件，其強度決定跨度上限。本州四國連絡橋公團公開說明：若沿用 160 kgf/mm²（約 1,570 N/mm²）鋼絲，明石海峽大橋每側需要兩條約 1,000 mm 的主纜；開發 180 kgf/mm²（約 1,760 N/mm²，製造商資料稱 1,770 MPa 級）鋼絲後，每側只需一條約 1,100 mm 主纜。每條主纜由 290 股、每股 127 根 5.23 mm 鍍鋅鋼絲組成。鋼絲強度提高也提高了工作應力，因此鍍鋅層、乾燥空氣與疲勞細部變得更關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main cable is the hardest member of a suspension bridge to replace, and its strength sets the span limit. The Honshu-Shikoku authority states that with 160 kgf/mm² wire (about 1,570 N/mm²) Akashi Kaikyo would have needed two cables of about 1,000 mm on each side; with newly developed 180 kgf/mm² wire (about 1,760 N/mm², quoted by the steelmaker as the 1,770 MPa class) one cable of about 1,100 mm per side sufficed. Each cable has 290 strands of 127 galvanised wires of 5.23 mm. Higher wire strength also raises working stress, so the zinc coating, dry air and fatigue details become more critical. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單絲面積 a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm²，每纜 290×127 = 36,830 根，A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²；破斷力 = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Wire area a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm², with 290×127 = 36,830 wires per cable, A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²; breaking force = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-09-k1","title":"高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面","titleEn":"High-strength wire and the single-cable section","text":"主纜是懸索橋最難更換的構件，其強度決定跨度上限。本州四國連絡橋公團公開說明：若沿用 160 kgf/mm²（約 1,570 N/mm²）鋼絲，明石海峽大橋每側需要兩條約 1,000 mm 的主纜；開發 180 kgf/mm²（約 1,760 N/mm²，製造商資料稱 1,770 MPa 級）鋼絲後，每側只需一條約 1,100 mm 主纜。","textEn":"The main cable is the hardest member of a suspension bridge to replace, and its strength sets the span limit. The Honshu-Shikoku authority states that with 160 kgf/mm² wire (about 1,570 N/mm²) Akashi Kaikyo would have needed two cables of about 1,000 mm on each side; with newly developed 180 kgf/mm² wire (about 1,760 N/mm², quoted by the steelmaker as the 1,770 MPa class) one cable of about 1,100 mm per side sufficed.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-strength wire and the single-cable section\" is correct?","options":["主纜是懸索橋最難更換的構件，其強度決定跨度上限。","鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。","水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。"],"optionsEn":["The main cable is the hardest member of a suspension bridge to replace, and its strength sets the span limit.","The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.","If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主纜是懸索橋最難更換的構件，其強度決定跨度上限。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main cable is the hardest member of a suspension bridge to replace, and its strength sets the span limit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":21},{"id":"b003-v13-10","title":"高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"High-strength wire and the single-cable section: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單絲面積 a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm²，每纜 290×127 = 36,830 根，A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²；破斷力 = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN。若用 1,570 N/mm² 鋼絲提供相同破斷力需 886,900 mm²，多約 12%。主纜外徑約 1.122 m，毛面積 0.989 m²，空隙率 = 1 − 0.791/0.989 ≈ 20%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Wire area a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm², with 290×127 = 36,830 wires per cable, A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²; breaking force = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN. Supplying the same force with 1,570 N/mm² wire needs 886,900 mm², about 12% more. With an outer diameter of about 1.122 m the gross area is 0.989 m² and the void ratio = 1 − 0.791/0.989 ≈ 20%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鋼絲出廠要逐捲抽驗抗拉強度、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗及鍍鋅附著量（製造商資料指出長大橋鋼絲鍍鋅量常在 300 g/m² 以上），索股完成後量測長度標記與直徑；架設後以纜徑量測與空隙率計算確認擠壓品質。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample every coil for tensile strength, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests and zinc coating mass (the steelmaker notes that long-span bridge wire is usually coated with 300 g/m² or more), check length marks and diameter on each finished strand, and after erection confirm squeezing quality by measured cable diameter and computed void ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單絲面積 a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm²，每纜 290×127 = 36,830 根，A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²；破斷力 = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN。若用 1,570 N/mm² 鋼絲提供相同破斷力需 886,900 mm²，多約 12%。主纜外徑約 1.122 m，毛面積 0.989 m²，空隙率 = 1 − 0.791/0.989 ≈ 20%。","textEn":"Wire area a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm², with 290×127 = 36,830 wires per cable, A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²; breaking force = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN. Supplying the same force with 1,570 N/mm² wire needs 886,900 mm², about 12% more. With an outer diameter of about 1.122 m the gross area is 0.989 m² and the void ratio = 1 − 0.791/0.989 ≈ 20%.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-strength wire and the single-cable section\", which statement holds?","options":["地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","單絲面積 a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm²，每纜 290×127 = 36,830 根，A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²。","只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。"],"optionsEn":["After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","Wire area a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm², with 290×127 = 36,830 wires per cable, A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²; breaking force = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN.","Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單絲面積 a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm²，每纜 290×127 = 36,830 根，A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²；破斷力 = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Wire area a = π/4×5.23² = 21.48 mm², with 290×127 = 36,830 wires per cable, A = 36,830×21.48 ≈ 791,200 mm²; breaking force = 791,200×1,760 ≈ 1,393 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":22},{"id":"b003-v13-11","title":"高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High-strength wire and the single-cable section: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鋼絲出廠要逐捲抽驗抗拉強度、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗及鍍鋅附著量（製造商資料指出長大橋鋼絲鍍鋅量常在 300 g/m² 以上），索股完成後量測長度標記與直徑；架設後以纜徑量測與空隙率計算確認擠壓品質。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample every coil for tensile strength, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests and zinc coating mass (the steelmaker notes that long-span bridge wire is usually coated with 300 g/m² or more), check length marks and diameter on each finished strand, and after erection confirm squeezing quality by measured cable diameter and computed void ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：鋼絲規格要同時規定強度、韌性指標（扭轉次數）與鍍鋅量，並要求每捲可追溯到爐號；擠壓與纏絲作業須設保護措施避免刮傷鍍鋅層，損傷處的修補方法與允收須事先核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: Wire specifications must set strength, ductility indicators such as torsion turns and zinc mass together, with every coil traceable to its heat; squeezing and wrapping must protect the zinc from scratches, and repair methods and acceptance for damaged spots must be approved in advance.","failure":"注意干擾：高強度鋼絲對氫脆與應力腐蝕更敏感，鍍鋅層若在運輸或擠壓時刮傷，加上潮濕空氣，就可能出現局部腐蝕坑與脆性斷絲；斷絲在纜內不易察覺，累積到一定比例才顯現為安全係數下降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High-strength wire is more sensitive to hydrogen embrittlement and stress corrosion; zinc scratched during transport or squeezing, combined with humid air, can start local pits and brittle wire breaks that are hard to see inside the cable and only appear as a loss of safety factor once enough have accumulated. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鋼絲出廠要逐捲抽驗抗拉強度、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗及鍍鋅附著量（製造商資料指出長大橋鋼絲鍍鋅量常在 300 g/m² 以上），索股完成後量測長度標記與直徑；架設後以纜徑量測與空隙率計算確認擠壓品質。","textEn":"Sample every coil for tensile strength, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests and zinc coating mass (the steelmaker notes that long-span bridge wire is usually coated with 300 g/m² or more), check length marks and diameter on each finished strand, and after erection confirm squeezing quality by measured cable diameter and computed void ratio.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"鋼絲規格要同時規定強度、韌性指標（扭轉次數）與鍍鋅量，並要求每捲可追溯到爐號；擠壓與纏絲作業須設保護措施避免刮傷鍍鋅層，損傷處的修補方法與允收須事先核准。","textEn":"Wire specifications must set strength, ductility indicators such as torsion turns and zinc mass together, with every coil traceable to its heat; squeezing and wrapping must protect the zinc from scratches, and repair methods and acceptance for damaged spots must be approved in advance.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-strength wire and the single-cable section\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。","鋼絲出廠要逐捲抽驗抗拉強度、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗及鍍鋅附著量（製造商資料指出長大橋鋼絲鍍鋅量常在 300 g/m² 以上），索股完成後量測長度標記與直徑。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be.","Sample every coil for tensile strength, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests and zinc coating mass (the steelmaker notes that long-span bridge wire is usually coated with 300 g/m² or more), check length marks and diameter on each finished strand, and after erection confirm squeezing quality by measured cable diameter and computed void ratio."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼絲出廠要逐捲抽驗抗拉強度、伸長率、扭轉與捲繞試驗及鍍鋅附著量（製造商資料指出長大橋鋼絲鍍鋅量常在 300 g/m² 以上），索股完成後量測長度標記與直徑；架設後以纜徑量測與空隙率計算確認擠壓品質。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample every coil for tensile strength, elongation, torsion and wrapping tests and zinc coating mass (the steelmaker notes that long-span bridge wire is usually coated with 300 g/m² or more), check length marks and diameter on each finished strand, and after erection confirm squeezing quality by measured cable diameter and computed void ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":23},{"id":"b003-v13-12","title":"高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-strength wire and the single-cable section: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「1,760 N/mm² 鍍鋅鋼絲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “1,760 N/mm² galvanised wire” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高強度鋼絲對氫脆與應力腐蝕更敏感，鍍鋅層若在運輸或擠壓時刮傷，加上潮濕空氣，就可能出現局部腐蝕坑與脆性斷絲；斷絲在纜內不易察覺，累積到一定比例才顯現為安全係數下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High-strength wire is more sensitive to hydrogen embrittlement and stress corrosion; zinc scratched during transport or squeezing, combined with humid air, can start local pits and brittle wire breaks that are hard to see inside the cable and only appear as a loss of safety factor once enough have accumulated. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鋼絲強度提高也提高了工作應力，因此鍍鋅層、乾燥空氣與疲勞細部變得更關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Higher wire strength also raises working stress, so the zinc coating, dry air and fatigue details become more critical.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高強度鋼絲對氫脆與應力腐蝕更敏感，鍍鋅層若在運輸或擠壓時刮傷，加上潮濕空氣，就可能出現局部腐蝕坑與脆性斷絲；斷絲在纜內不易察覺，累積到一定比例才顯現為安全係數下降。","textEn":"High-strength wire is more sensitive to hydrogen embrittlement and stress corrosion; zinc scratched during transport or squeezing, combined with humid air, can start local pits and brittle wire breaks that are hard to see inside the cable and only appear as a loss of safety factor once enough have accumulated.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高強度鋼絲與單纜斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-strength wire and the single-cable section\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高強度鋼絲對氫脆與應力腐蝕更敏感，鍍鋅層若在運輸或擠壓時刮傷，加上潮濕空氣，就可能出現局部腐蝕坑與脆性斷絲。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。"],"optionsEn":["High-strength wire is more sensitive to hydrogen embrittlement and stress corrosion.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高強度鋼絲對氫脆與應力腐蝕更敏感，鍍鋅層若在運輸或擠壓時刮傷，加上潮濕空氣，就可能出現局部腐蝕坑與脆性斷絲；斷絲在纜內不易察覺，累積到一定比例才顯現為安全係數下降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High-strength wire is more sensitive to hydrogen embrittlement and stress corrosion; zinc scratched during transport or squeezing, combined with humid air, can start local pits and brittle wire breaks that are hard to see inside the cable and only appear as a loss of safety factor once enough have accumulated. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":24},{"id":"b003-v13-13","title":"設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主塔基礎位於水深約 60 m、潮流最大約 8 節的海峽中，無法築圍堰抽乾。做法是先開挖整平海床，再把工廠製造的雙壁圓形鋼沉箱拖航到位、灌水沉放（設置沉箱工法），然後在沉箱內以抗水洗水中混凝土分層澆置，讓鋼殼成為永久模板。2P 沉箱外徑 80 m、內徑 56 m、高約 65 m，內核混凝土約 270,000 m³；基礎周邊再鋪濾層與拋石防止強潮流沖刷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The tower foundations sit in about 60 m of water with tidal currents up to about 8 knots, where no cofferdam can be pumped dry. The seabed is excavated and levelled, a factory-built double-walled circular steel caisson is towed into place and ballasted down (the laying-down caisson method), and antiwashout underwater concrete is then placed in layers inside it, the steel shell acting as permanent formwork. The 2P caisson is 80 m in outer diameter, 56 m inner, about 65 m high, with about 270,000 m³ of core concrete; filter layers and rock armour around it resist scour by the strong currents. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：內核面積 = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²，每層 4 m，單次澆置約 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³，連續約 72 h，平均 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h；六台泵各 110 m³/h，總能力 660 m³/h，平均利用率約 21%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Core area = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²; with 4 m layers each pour is about 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³, placed continuously over about 72 h, an average of 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h; six pumps of 110 m³/h give 660 m³/h of capacity, about 21% average utilisation.","failure":"常見誤解：「水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-13-k1","title":"設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土","titleEn":"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete","text":"主塔基礎位於水深約 60 m、潮流最大約 8 節的海峽中，無法築圍堰抽乾。做法是先開挖整平海床，再把工廠製造的雙壁圓形鋼沉箱拖航到位、灌水沉放（設置沉箱工法），然後在沉箱內以抗水洗水中混凝土分層澆置，讓鋼殼成為永久模板。","textEn":"The tower foundations sit in about 60 m of water with tidal currents up to about 8 knots, where no cofferdam can be pumped dry. The seabed is excavated and levelled, a factory-built double-walled circular steel caisson is towed into place and ballasted down (the laying-down caisson method), and antiwashout underwater concrete is then placed in layers inside it, the steel shell acting as permanent formwork.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete\" is correct?","options":["水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。","主塔基礎位於水深約 60 m、潮流最大約 8 節的海峽中，無法築圍堰抽乾。","索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。"],"optionsEn":["If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality.","The tower foundations sit in about 60 m of water with tidal currents up to about 8 knots, where no cofferdam can be pumped dry.","Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主塔基礎位於水深約 60 m、潮流最大約 8 節的海峽中，無法築圍堰抽乾。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The tower foundations sit in about 60 m of water with tidal currents up to about 8 knots, where no cofferdam can be pumped dry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":25},{"id":"b003-v13-14","title":"設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土：定量估算","titleEn":"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：內核面積 = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²，每層 4 m，單次澆置約 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³，連續約 72 h，平均 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h；六台泵各 110 m³/h，總能力 660 m³/h，平均利用率約 21%。24 支澆置管平均各負責 2,463/24 ≈ 103 m²，等效半徑 √(103/π) ≈ 5.7 m，小於 8 m 流動距離上限。面積與層厚引自公開論文，其餘為推算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Core area = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²; with 4 m layers each pour is about 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³, placed continuously over about 72 h, an average of 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h; six pumps of 110 m³/h give 660 m³/h of capacity, about 21% average utilisation. Each of 24 tremie pipes serves about 2,463/24 ≈ 103 m², an equivalent radius of √(103/π) ≈ 5.7 m, within the 8 m flow-distance limit. Area and layer thickness come from a published paper; the rest is derived. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：澆置中以測深錘或感測器追蹤各管周邊混凝土面高程，確保管口埋入深度與層面平整；試體量測水中與氣中強度比、坍流度與凝結時間；完成後鑽心取樣檢查層間結合與空洞，並以海床測深監測沉箱周邊沖刷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During placement track the concrete surface around each pipe with sounding weights or sensors to keep pipe embedment and a level surface; test specimens for the underwater-to-air strength ratio, slump flow and setting time; afterwards core through layers to check bond and voids, and monitor scour around the caisson by seabed soundings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"內核面積 = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²，每層 4 m，單次澆置約 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³，連續約 72 h，平均 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h；六台泵各 110 m³/h，總能力 660 m³/h，平均利用率約 21%。24 支澆置管平均各負責 2,463/24 ≈ 103 m²，等效半徑 √(103/π) ≈ 5.7 m，小於 8 m 流動距離上限。面積與層厚引自公開論文，其餘為推算。","textEn":"Core area = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²; with 4 m layers each pour is about 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³, placed continuously over about 72 h, an average of 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h; six pumps of 110 m³/h give 660 m³/h of capacity, about 21% average utilisation. Each of 24 tremie pipes serves about 2,463/24 ≈ 103 m², an equivalent radius of √(103/π) ≈ 5.7 m, within the 8 m flow-distance limit. Area and layer thickness come from a published paper; the rest is derived.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete\", which statement holds?","options":["全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。","主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。","內核面積 = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²，每層 4 m，單次澆置約 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³，連續約 72 h，平均 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h。"],"optionsEn":["A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge.","With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.","Core area = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"內核面積 = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²，每層 4 m，單次澆置約 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³，連續約 72 h，平均 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h；六台泵各 110 m³/h，總能力 660 m³/h，平均利用率約 21%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Core area = π/4×56² ≈ 2,463 m²; with 4 m layers each pour is about 2,463×4 ≈ 9,850 m³, placed continuously over about 72 h, an average of 9,850/72 ≈ 137 m³/h; six pumps of 110 m³/h give 660 m³/h of capacity, about 21% average utilisation. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":26},{"id":"b003-v13-15","title":"設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"澆置中以測深錘或感測器追蹤各管周邊混凝土面高程，確保管口埋入深度與層面平整；試體量測水中與氣中強度比、坍流度與凝結時間；完成後鑽心取樣檢查層間結合與空洞，並以海床測深監測沉箱周邊沖刷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During placement track the concrete surface around each pipe with sounding weights or sensors to keep pipe embedment and a level surface; test specimens for the underwater-to-air strength ratio, slump flow and setting time; afterwards core through layers to check bond and voids, and monitor scour around the caisson by seabed soundings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：水中混凝土計畫應規定管口最小埋深、最大流動距離、層間間隔時間與停止條件，並在試驗槽先做足尺試澆；沉箱就位精度與海床整平度列為進入澆置前的停留點，由監造簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The underwater concreting plan must fix minimum pipe embedment, maximum flow distance, layer interval and stop conditions, with a full-scale trial pour in a test tank; caisson positioning accuracy and seabed levelness are hold points signed by the supervising engineer before placement begins.","failure":"注意干擾：水中混凝土若抗水洗性不足或管口拔出，水泥漿被潮流帶走，形成骨材鬆散層與層間弱面；某一區流動距離過長則產生材料分離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concrete with poor washout resistance, or a pipe lifted out of the mass, lets the current strip the paste and leaves loose aggregate and weak layer joints; excessive flow distance in one zone causes segregation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"澆置中以測深錘或感測器追蹤各管周邊混凝土面高程，確保管口埋入深度與層面平整；試體量測水中與氣中強度比、坍流度與凝結時間；完成後鑽心取樣檢查層間結合與空洞，並以海床測深監測沉箱周邊沖刷。","textEn":"During placement track the concrete surface around each pipe with sounding weights or sensors to keep pipe embedment and a level surface; test specimens for the underwater-to-air strength ratio, slump flow and setting time; afterwards core through layers to check bond and voids, and monitor scour around the caisson by seabed soundings.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"水中混凝土計畫應規定管口最小埋深、最大流動距離、層間間隔時間與停止條件，並在試驗槽先做足尺試澆；沉箱就位精度與海床整平度列為進入澆置前的停留點，由監造簽認。","textEn":"The underwater concreting plan must fix minimum pipe embedment, maximum flow distance, layer interval and stop conditions, with a full-scale trial pour in a test tank; caisson positioning accuracy and seabed levelness are hold points signed by the supervising engineer before placement begins.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete\"?","options":["澆置中以測深錘或感測器追蹤各管周邊混凝土面高程，確保管口埋入深度與層面平整。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。"],"optionsEn":["During placement track the concrete surface around each pipe with sounding weights or sensors to keep pipe embedment and a level surface.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"澆置中以測深錘或感測器追蹤各管周邊混凝土面高程，確保管口埋入深度與層面平整；試體量測水中與氣中強度比、坍流度與凝結時間；完成後鑽心取樣檢查層間結合與空洞，並以海床測深監測沉箱周邊沖刷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During placement track the concrete surface around each pipe with sounding weights or sensors to keep pipe embedment and a level surface; test specimens for the underwater-to-air strength ratio, slump flow and setting time; afterwards core through layers to check bond and voids, and monitor scour around the caisson by seabed soundings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":27},{"id":"b003-v13-16","title":"設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土：失效診斷","titleEn":"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「2P 鋼沉箱與水中混凝土」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “2P steel caisson and underwater concrete” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水中混凝土若抗水洗性不足或管口拔出，水泥漿被潮流帶走，形成骨材鬆散層與層間弱面；某一區流動距離過長則產生材料分離。基礎周邊沖刷若未及時防護，可能淘空沉箱邊緣、降低承載與抗傾覆能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concrete with poor washout resistance, or a pipe lifted out of the mass, lets the current strip the paste and leaves loose aggregate and weak layer joints; excessive flow distance in one zone causes segregation. Unchecked scour around the foundation can undermine the caisson edge and reduce bearing and overturning capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：2P 沉箱外徑 80 m、內徑 56 m、高約 65 m，內核混凝土約 270,000 m³；基礎周邊再鋪濾層與拋石防止強潮流沖刷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The 2P caisson is 80 m in outer diameter, 56 m inner, about 65 m high, with about 270,000 m³ of core concrete; filter layers and rock armour around it resist scour by the strong currents.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水中混凝土若抗水洗性不足或管口拔出，水泥漿被潮流帶走，形成骨材鬆散層與層間弱面；某一區流動距離過長則產生材料分離。基礎周邊沖刷若未及時防護，可能淘空沉箱邊緣、降低承載與抗傾覆能力。","textEn":"Concrete with poor washout resistance, or a pipe lifted out of the mass, lets the current strip the paste and leaves loose aggregate and weak layer joints; excessive flow distance in one zone causes segregation. Unchecked scour around the foundation can undermine the caisson edge and reduce bearing and overturning capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設置沉箱與抗水洗混凝土」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Laying-down caisson and antiwashout concrete\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","水中混凝土若抗水洗性不足或管口拔出，水泥漿被潮流帶走，形成骨材鬆散層與層間弱面；某一區流動距離過長則產生材料分離。","索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Concrete with poor washout resistance, or a pipe lifted out of the mass, lets the current strip the paste and leaves loose aggregate and weak layer joints.","Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水中混凝土若抗水洗性不足或管口拔出，水泥漿被潮流帶走，形成骨材鬆散層與層間弱面；某一區流動距離過長則產生材料分離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concrete with poor washout resistance, or a pipe lifted out of the mass, lets the current strip the paste and leaves loose aggregate and weak layer joints; excessive flow distance in one zone causes segregation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":28}],"order":5},{"id":"b003-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「索股垂度的溫度敏感度」與「跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag\" and \"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b003-v13-17","title":"索股垂度的溫度敏感度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “PWS strand sag” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"明石海峽大橋以預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）架設主纜：每股 127 根鋼絲在工廠成束、端部預裝錨頭，再沿導索與貓道牽引過海峽，290 股依序放入索鞍。每一股都必須調整到與基準索股相同的垂度，否則擠壓成纜後各股受力不均。由於主纜長度隨溫度伸縮，而垂度對長度變化極為敏感，調整通常安排在夜間溫度穩定、索股內外溫差小的時段，並以溫度修正量測值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Akashi Kaikyo's main cables were erected with prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS): each bundle of 127 wires is made in the factory with sockets fitted at the ends, hauled across the strait along guide ropes and catwalks, and the 290 strands are placed in the saddles in sequence. Every strand must be adjusted to the same sag as the reference strand, otherwise the wires share load unequally after squeezing. Because cable length changes with temperature and sag is very sensitive to length, adjustment is usually done at night when temperatures are stable and the difference between strand surface and core is small, with temperature-corrected readings. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “PWS strand sag” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：拋物線纜長 S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Parabolic cable length S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l).","failure":"常見誤解：「索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “PWS strand sag”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-17-k1","title":"索股垂度的溫度敏感度","titleEn":"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag","text":"明石海峽大橋以預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）架設主纜：每股 127 根鋼絲在工廠成束、端部預裝錨頭，再沿導索與貓道牽引過海峽，290 股依序放入索鞍。每一股都必須調整到與基準索股相同的垂度，否則擠壓成纜後各股受力不均。","textEn":"Akashi Kaikyo's main cables were erected with prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS): each bundle of 127 wires is made in the factory with sockets fitted at the ends, hauled across the strait along guide ropes and catwalks, and the 290 strands are placed in the saddles in sequence. Every strand must be adjusted to the same sag as the reference strand, otherwise the wires share load unequally after squeezing.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「索股垂度的溫度敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag\" is correct?","options":["索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。","地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","明石海峽大橋以預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）架設主纜：每股 127 根鋼絲在工廠成束、端部預裝錨頭，再沿導索與貓道牽引過海峽，290 股依序放入索鞍。"],"optionsEn":["Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces.","After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","Akashi Kaikyo's main cables were erected with prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS): each bundle of 127 wires is made in the factory with sockets fitted at the ends, hauled across the strait along guide ropes and catwalks, and the 290 strands are placed in the saddles in sequence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明石海峽大橋以預製平行鋼絲索股（PWS）架設主纜：每股 127 根鋼絲在工廠成束、端部預裝錨頭，再沿導索與貓道牽引過海峽，290 股依序放入索鞍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Akashi Kaikyo's main cables were erected with prefabricated parallel-wire strands (PWS): each bundle of 127 wires is made in the factory with sockets fitted at the ends, hauled across the strait along guide ropes and catwalks, and the 290 strands are placed in the saddles in sequence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":29},{"id":"b003-v13-18","title":"索股垂度的溫度敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “PWS strand sag” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：拋物線纜長 S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l)。取 l = 1,991 m、f = 199.1 m（垂跨比 1/10）：S ≈ 1,991 + 53.1 = 2,044.1 m。溫度上升 1 °C，ΔS = 1.2×10⁻⁵×2,044.1 ≈ 0.0245 m，Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS = 1.875×0.0245 ≈ 0.046 m。也就是每 1 °C 垂度約改變 46 mm，5 °C 溫差即約 230 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Parabolic cable length S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l). With l = 1,991 m and f = 199.1 m (sag ratio 1/10): S ≈ 1,991 + 53.1 = 2,044.1 m. A 1 °C rise gives ΔS = 1.2×10⁻⁵×2,044.1 ≈ 0.0245 m and Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS = 1.875×0.0245 ≈ 0.046 m, so sag changes by about 46 mm per °C and a 5 °C error means about 230 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：基準索股以全站儀或水準量測跨中與邊跨垂度，配合多點索股溫度計取平均溫度修正；其他索股以相對於基準股的高差量測調整，允收以修正後高差在數毫米至十餘毫米內為準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure mid-span and side-span sag of the reference strand by total station or levelling with multi-point strand thermometers for temperature correction; adjust other strands by their height difference relative to the reference, accepting corrected differences within a few to about a dozen millimetres.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"拋物線纜長 S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l)。取 l = 1,991 m、f = 199.1 m（垂跨比 1/10）：S ≈ 1,991 + 53.1 = 2,044.1 m。溫度上升 1 °C，ΔS = 1.2×10⁻⁵×2,044.1 ≈ 0.0245 m，Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS = 1.875×0.0245 ≈ 0.046 m。也就是每 1 °C 垂度約改變 46 mm，5 °C 溫差即約 230 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Parabolic cable length S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l). With l = 1,991 m and f = 199.1 m (sag ratio 1/10): S ≈ 1,991 + 53.1 = 2,044.1 m. A 1 °C rise gives ΔS = 1.2×10⁻⁵×2,044.1 ≈ 0.0245 m and Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS = 1.875×0.0245 ≈ 0.046 m, so sag changes by about 46 mm per °C and a 5 °C error means about 230 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「索股垂度的溫度敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag\", which statement holds?","options":["拋物線纜長 S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l)。","只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。","減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Parabolic cable length S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l).","Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration.","The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拋物線纜長 S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Parabolic cable length S ≈ l + 8f²/(3l). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":30},{"id":"b003-v13-19","title":"索股垂度的溫度敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “PWS strand sag” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"基準索股以全站儀或水準量測跨中與邊跨垂度，配合多點索股溫度計取平均溫度修正；其他索股以相對於基準股的高差量測調整，允收以修正後高差在數毫米至十餘毫米內為準。每日記錄氣溫、風速與量測時間，作為異常時的回溯依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure mid-span and side-span sag of the reference strand by total station or levelling with multi-point strand thermometers for temperature correction; adjust other strands by their height difference relative to the reference, accepting corrected differences within a few to about a dozen millimetres. Log air temperature, wind speed and time daily as a trace for anomalies. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：索股調整的量測時段、溫度計位置與修正公式應寫入施工規範；基準索股須定期複測，若連續數股偏差同向，先停工檢查基準點與溫度修正，再繼續牽引。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification should fix the measuring window, thermometer positions and correction formula for strand adjustment; the reference strand must be re-surveyed periodically, and if several strands deviate in the same direction, stop to check the benchmarks and temperature correction before hauling more.","failure":"注意干擾：日間陽光照射使上層索股比下層熱數度，若此時調整，夜間冷卻後各股垂度不一，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲長期過載、部分鬆弛；鬆弛鋼絲在纜內會形成鼓起，影響索夾夾緊與防護包覆。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adjusting in daytime sun, when top strands run several degrees warmer than lower ones, leaves unequal sags after night cooling; once squeezed, some wires are permanently overloaded and others slack, and slack wires bulge inside the cable, spoiling cable-band clamping and wrapping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"基準索股以全站儀或水準量測跨中與邊跨垂度，配合多點索股溫度計取平均溫度修正；其他索股以相對於基準股的高差量測調整，允收以修正後高差在數毫米至十餘毫米內為準。每日記錄氣溫、風速與量測時間，作為異常時的回溯依據。","textEn":"Measure mid-span and side-span sag of the reference strand by total station or levelling with multi-point strand thermometers for temperature correction; adjust other strands by their height difference relative to the reference, accepting corrected differences within a few to about a dozen millimetres. Log air temperature, wind speed and time daily as a trace for anomalies.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"索股調整的量測時段、溫度計位置與修正公式應寫入施工規範；基準索股須定期複測，若連續數股偏差同向，先停工檢查基準點與溫度修正，再繼續牽引。","textEn":"The specification should fix the measuring window, thermometer positions and correction formula for strand adjustment; the reference strand must be re-surveyed periodically, and if several strands deviate in the same direction, stop to check the benchmarks and temperature correction before hauling more.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「索股垂度的溫度敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","基準索股以全站儀或水準量測跨中與邊跨垂度，配合多點索股溫度計取平均溫度修正；其他索股以相對於基準股的高差量測調整，允收以修正後高差在數毫米至十餘毫米內為準。","懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure mid-span and side-span sag of the reference strand by total station or levelling with multi-point strand thermometers for temperature correction.","A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基準索股以全站儀或水準量測跨中與邊跨垂度，配合多點索股溫度計取平均溫度修正；其他索股以相對於基準股的高差量測調整，允收以修正後高差在數毫米至十餘毫米內為準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure mid-span and side-span sag of the reference strand by total station or levelling with multi-point strand thermometers for temperature correction; adjust other strands by their height difference relative to the reference, accepting corrected differences within a few to about a dozen millimetres. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":31},{"id":"b003-v13-20","title":"索股垂度的溫度敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預製平行鋼絲索股垂度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “PWS strand sag” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"日間陽光照射使上層索股比下層熱數度，若此時調整，夜間冷卻後各股垂度不一，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲長期過載、部分鬆弛；鬆弛鋼絲在纜內會形成鼓起，影響索夾夾緊與防護包覆。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adjusting in daytime sun, when top strands run several degrees warmer than lower ones, leaves unequal sags after night cooling; once squeezed, some wires are permanently overloaded and others slack, and slack wires bulge inside the cable, spoiling cable-band clamping and wrapping. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：由於主纜長度隨溫度伸縮，而垂度對長度變化極為敏感，調整通常安排在夜間溫度穩定、索股內外溫差小的時段，並以溫度修正量測值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Because cable length changes with temperature and sag is very sensitive to length, adjustment is usually done at night when temperatures are stable and the difference between strand surface and core is small, with temperature-corrected readings.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"日間陽光照射使上層索股比下層熱數度，若此時調整，夜間冷卻後各股垂度不一，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲長期過載、部分鬆弛；鬆弛鋼絲在纜內會形成鼓起，影響索夾夾緊與防護包覆。","textEn":"Adjusting in daytime sun, when top strands run several degrees warmer than lower ones, leaves unequal sags after night cooling; once squeezed, some wires are permanently overloaded and others slack, and slack wires bulge inside the cable, spoiling cable-band clamping and wrapping.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「索股垂度的溫度敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temperature sensitivity of strand sag\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","日間陽光照射使上層索股比下層熱數度，若此時調整，夜間冷卻後各股垂度不一，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲長期過載、部分鬆弛；鬆弛鋼絲在纜內會形成鼓起，影響索夾夾緊與防護包覆。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","Adjusting in daytime sun, when top strands run several degrees warmer than lower ones, leaves unequal sags after night cooling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"日間陽光照射使上層索股比下層熱數度，若此時調整，夜間冷卻後各股垂度不一，擠壓成纜後部分鋼絲長期過載、部分鬆弛；鬆弛鋼絲在纜內會形成鼓起，影響索夾夾緊與防護包覆。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adjusting in daytime sun, when top strands run several degrees warmer than lower ones, leaves unequal sags after night cooling; once squeezed, some wires are permanently overloaded and others slack, and slack wires bulge inside the cable, spoiling cable-band clamping and wrapping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":32},{"id":"b003-v13-21","title":"跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「1995 年地震後桁段加長」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-1995 truss lengthening” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"1995 年 1 月 17 日地震發生時，主塔已完成、所有索股已架設，正在進行主纜擠壓，加勁桁尚未架設。斷層錯動使基礎隨地盤移動，中央跨徑約增加 0.8 m。由於主纜長度已固定，跨徑變長意味著垂度變小、張力略增；設計團隊重新計算後，把尚未製造的加勁桁構件在中央跨加長 800 mm、淡路側邊跨加長 340 mm，使完工線形仍與主纜幾何相容。公開論文指出中央跨垂度約減少 1.3 m，主纜張力增加約為原設計最大張力的 0.6%，仍在容許範圍內。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「1995 年地震後桁段加長」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When the earthquake struck on 17 January 1995 the towers were complete and all strands erected, cable squeezing was in progress and the stiffening truss had not yet been erected. Fault movement carried the foundations with the ground and lengthened the centre span by about 0.8 m. With the cable length already fixed, a longer span means less sag and slightly more tension; after re-analysis the team lengthened truss members not yet fabricated by 800 mm in the centre span and 340 mm in the Awaji side span so that the completed profile stayed compatible with the cable geometry. The published paper reports a centre-span sag reduction of about 1.3 m and an extra cable tension of about 0.6% of the original maximum, within the allowable. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Post-1995 truss lengthening” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：纜長固定時 dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0，故 df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With fixed cable length dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0, so df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f).","failure":"常見誤解：「地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「1995 年地震後桁段加長」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Post-1995 truss lengthening”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-21-k1","title":"跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正","titleEn":"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew","text":"1995 年 1 月 17 日地震發生時，主塔已完成、所有索股已架設，正在進行主纜擠壓，加勁桁尚未架設。斷層錯動使基礎隨地盤移動，中央跨徑約增加 0.8 m。","textEn":"When the earthquake struck on 17 January 1995 the towers were complete and all strands erected, cable squeezing was in progress and the stiffening truss had not yet been erected. Fault movement carried the foundations with the ground and lengthened the centre span by about 0.8 m.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew\" is correct?","options":["1995 年 1 月 17 日地震發生時，主塔已完成、所有索股已架設，正在進行主纜擠壓，加勁桁尚未架設。","地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["When the earthquake struck on 17 January 1995 the towers were complete and all strands erected, cable squeezing was in progress and the stiffening truss had not yet been erected.","After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"1995 年 1 月 17 日地震發生時，主塔已完成、所有索股已架設，正在進行主纜擠壓，加勁桁尚未架設。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When the earthquake struck on 17 January 1995 the towers were complete and all strands erected, cable squeezing was in progress and the stiffening truss had not yet been erected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":33},{"id":"b003-v13-22","title":"跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「1995 年地震後桁段加長」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-1995 truss lengthening” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：纜長固定時 dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0，故 df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f)。取 n = 0.1、l = 1,991 m、f = 199.1 m、dl = 0.8 m：df = −0.8×0.973×1.875 ≈ −1.46 m。不可伸長假設高估了垂度變化；實際張力增加使主纜彈性伸長、塔頂也有變位，公開報告值約 1.3 m。n 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With fixed cable length dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0, so df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f). With n = 0.1, l = 1,991 m, f = 199.1 m and dl = 0.8 m: df = −0.8×0.973×1.875 ≈ −1.46 m. The inextensible assumption overestimates the change; the extra tension stretches the cable elastically and the tower tops also move, and the published value is about 1.3 m. n is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：事件後以 GPS 與精密測量重新建立各基礎與塔頂座標，量測主纜各跨垂度與索鞍位置，回饋到完工線形分析；加長的桁段在工廠以修正圖說製造，架設中逐段比對節點高程與預測值，最終與設計車道縱斷面比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After the event re-establish coordinates of every foundation and tower top by GPS and precise survey, measure cable sag in each span and saddle positions, and feed them into the final-profile analysis; fabricate the lengthened members to revised drawings and compare node levels with predictions segment by segment during erection, finally checking against the design road profile.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"纜長固定時 dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0，故 df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f)。取 n = 0.1、l = 1,991 m、f = 199.1 m、dl = 0.8 m：df = −0.8×0.973×1.875 ≈ −1.46 m。不可伸長假設高估了垂度變化；實際張力增加使主纜彈性伸長、塔頂也有變位，公開報告值約 1.3 m。n 為教學假設。","textEn":"With fixed cable length dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0, so df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f). With n = 0.1, l = 1,991 m, f = 199.1 m and dl = 0.8 m: df = −0.8×0.973×1.875 ≈ −1.46 m. The inextensible assumption overestimates the change; the extra tension stretches the cable elastically and the tower tops also move, and the published value is about 1.3 m. n is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew\", which statement holds?","options":["主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。","纜長固定時 dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0，故 df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f)。","桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。"],"optionsEn":["With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.","With fixed cable length dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0, so df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f).","A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"纜長固定時 dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0，故 df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With fixed cable length dS = (1 − 8n²/3)·dl + (16f/(3l))·df = 0, so df = −dl·(1 − 8n²/3)·3l/(16f). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":34},{"id":"b003-v13-23","title":"跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「1995 年地震後桁段加長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-1995 truss lengthening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"事件後以 GPS 與精密測量重新建立各基礎與塔頂座標，量測主纜各跨垂度與索鞍位置，回饋到完工線形分析；加長的桁段在工廠以修正圖說製造，架設中逐段比對節點高程與預測值，最終與設計車道縱斷面比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After the event re-establish coordinates of every foundation and tower top by GPS and precise survey, measure cable sag in each span and saddle positions, and feed them into the final-profile analysis; fabricate the lengthened members to revised drawings and compare node levels with predictions segment by segment during erection, finally checking against the design road profile. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：大型懸索橋施工期間應持續保存基礎、塔頂與主纜的測量基準與時間序列，並預先規劃「事件後重新測量—重算線形—修正未製構件」的決策流程與核准層級；修正圖說須由設計者簽認後才可投料。","observationEn":"Site practice: During construction of a major suspension bridge keep survey baselines and time series for foundations, tower tops and cables, and plan in advance the decision path of post-event survey, profile re-analysis and revision of unfabricated members with its approval levels; revised drawings must be signed by the designer before steel is cut.","failure":"注意干擾：若沿用原設計長度製造加勁桁，桁段與吊索幾何不相容，合龍時會出現強迫的拉壓力與伸縮縫錯位；未重新檢核塔底應力與主纜張力，也可能低估地震造成的永久附加應力（公開論文報告塔底附加應力最大約 18.2 N/mm²）。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fabricating the truss to the original lengths would make segments incompatible with hanger geometry, forcing tension and compression at closure and misaligning expansion joints; skipping a re-check of tower-base stress and cable tension could miss the permanent added stress from the quake (the paper reports up to about 18.2 N/mm² at the tower base). A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"事件後以 GPS 與精密測量重新建立各基礎與塔頂座標，量測主纜各跨垂度與索鞍位置，回饋到完工線形分析；加長的桁段在工廠以修正圖說製造，架設中逐段比對節點高程與預測值，最終與設計車道縱斷面比較。","textEn":"After the event re-establish coordinates of every foundation and tower top by GPS and precise survey, measure cable sag in each span and saddle positions, and feed them into the final-profile analysis; fabricate the lengthened members to revised drawings and compare node levels with predictions segment by segment during erection, finally checking against the design road profile.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"大型懸索橋施工期間應持續保存基礎、塔頂與主纜的測量基準與時間序列，並預先規劃「事件後重新測量—重算線形—修正未製構件」的決策流程與核准層級；修正圖說須由設計者簽認後才可投料。","textEn":"During construction of a major suspension bridge keep survey baselines and time series for foundations, tower tops and cables, and plan in advance the decision path of post-event survey, profile re-analysis and revision of unfabricated members with its approval levels; revised drawings must be signed by the designer before steel is cut.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。","事件後以 GPS 與精密測量重新建立各基礎與塔頂座標，量測主纜各跨垂度與索鞍位置，回饋到完工線形分析。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.","After the event re-establish coordinates of every foundation and tower top by GPS and precise survey, measure cable sag in each span and saddle positions, and feed them into the final-profile analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"事件後以 GPS 與精密測量重新建立各基礎與塔頂座標，量測主纜各跨垂度與索鞍位置，回饋到完工線形分析；加長的桁段在工廠以修正圖說製造，架設中逐段比對節點高程與預測值，最終與設計車道縱斷面比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After the event re-establish coordinates of every foundation and tower top by GPS and precise survey, measure cable sag in each span and saddle positions, and feed them into the final-profile analysis; fabricate the lengthened members to revised drawings and compare node levels with predictions segment by segment during erection, finally checking against the design road profile. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":35},{"id":"b003-v13-24","title":"跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「1995 年地震後桁段加長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-1995 truss lengthening” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沿用原設計長度製造加勁桁，桁段與吊索幾何不相容，合龍時會出現強迫的拉壓力與伸縮縫錯位；未重新檢核塔底應力與主纜張力，也可能低估地震造成的永久附加應力（公開論文報告塔底附加應力最大約 18.2 N/mm²）。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fabricating the truss to the original lengths would make segments incompatible with hanger geometry, forcing tension and compression at closure and misaligning expansion joints; skipping a re-check of tower-base stress and cable tension could miss the permanent added stress from the quake (the paper reports up to about 18.2 N/mm² at the tower base). Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：公開論文指出中央跨垂度約減少 1.3 m，主纜張力增加約為原設計最大張力的 0.6%，仍在容許範圍內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The published paper reports a centre-span sag reduction of about 1.3 m and an extra cable tension of about 0.6% of the original maximum, within the allowable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沿用原設計長度製造加勁桁，桁段與吊索幾何不相容，合龍時會出現強迫的拉壓力與伸縮縫錯位；未重新檢核塔底應力與主纜張力，也可能低估地震造成的永久附加應力（公開論文報告塔底附加應力最大約 18.2 N/mm²）。","textEn":"Fabricating the truss to the original lengths would make segments incompatible with hanger geometry, forcing tension and compression at closure and misaligning expansion joints; skipping a re-check of tower-base stress and cable tension could miss the permanent added stress from the quake (the paper reports up to about 18.2 N/mm² at the tower base).","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨徑變化後的垂度與桁段修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sag change and truss correction after the span grew\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若沿用原設計長度製造加勁桁，桁段與吊索幾何不相容，合龍時會出現強迫的拉壓力與伸縮縫錯位。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["Fabricating the truss to the original lengths would make segments incompatible with hanger geometry, forcing tension and compression at closure and misaligning expansion joints.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若沿用原設計長度製造加勁桁，桁段與吊索幾何不相容，合龍時會出現強迫的拉壓力與伸縮縫錯位；未重新檢核塔底應力與主纜張力，也可能低估地震造成的永久附加應力（公開論文報告塔底附加應力最大約 18.2 N/mm²）。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fabricating the truss to the original lengths would make segments incompatible with hanger geometry, forcing tension and compression at closure and misaligning expansion joints; skipping a re-check of tower-base stress and cable tension could miss the permanent added stress from the quake (the paper reports up to about 18.2 N/mm² at the tower base). Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":36}],"order":6},{"id":"b003-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對」與「長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records\" and \"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b003-v13-25","title":"全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Full model and typhoon records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"斷面模型只能代表二維流場，懸索橋的顫振與抖振卻牽涉多個三維模態、主纜與塔的氣動力，以及沿跨長變化的紊流。明石海峽大橋因此在大型風洞中做全橋氣彈模型試驗，模型需同時滿足幾何、質量、勁度與重力相似，以 Froude 相似律換算風速與頻率；完工後研究者再以颱風期間的風速計、加速度計與 GPS 實測，比對抖振位移與模態阻尼，驗證設計假設。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A section model represents only two-dimensional flow, while flutter and buffeting of a suspension bridge involve several three-dimensional modes, aerodynamic forces on cables and towers, and turbulence that varies along the span. Akashi Kaikyo was therefore tested with a full aeroelastic model in a large wind tunnel, which must reproduce geometry, mass, stiffness and gravity together, with wind speed and frequency scaled by Froude similarity; after completion researchers compared buffeting displacement and modal damping with anemometer, accelerometer and GPS records from typhoons to validate the design assumptions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Full model and typhoon records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Froude 相似：長度比 λ = 1/100 時，風速比 √λ = 1/10、頻率比 1/√λ = 10、單位長質量比 λ² = 1/10,000。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Froude similarity: with length scale λ = 1/100, velocity scales by √λ = 1/10, frequency by 1/√λ = 10 and mass per length by λ² = 1/10,000.","failure":"常見誤解：「全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Full model and typhoon records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-25-k1","title":"全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對","titleEn":"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records","text":"斷面模型只能代表二維流場，懸索橋的顫振與抖振卻牽涉多個三維模態、主纜與塔的氣動力，以及沿跨長變化的紊流。明石海峽大橋因此在大型風洞中做全橋氣彈模型試驗，模型需同時滿足幾何、質量、勁度與重力相似，以 Froude 相似律換算風速與頻率；完工後研究者再以颱風期間的風速計、加速度計與 GPS 實測，比對抖振位移與模態阻尼，驗證設計假設。","textEn":"A section model represents only two-dimensional flow, while flutter and buffeting of a suspension bridge involve several three-dimensional modes, aerodynamic forces on cables and towers, and turbulence that varies along the span. Akashi Kaikyo was therefore tested with a full aeroelastic model in a large wind tunnel, which must reproduce geometry, mass, stiffness and gravity together, with wind speed and frequency scaled by Froude similarity; after completion researchers compared buffeting displacement and modal damping with anemometer, accelerometer and GPS records from typhoons to validate the design assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records\" is correct?","options":["全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。","斷面模型只能代表二維流場，懸索橋的顫振與抖振卻牽涉多個三維模態、主纜與塔的氣動力，以及沿跨長變化的紊流。","只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。"],"optionsEn":["A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge.","A section model represents only two-dimensional flow, while flutter and buffeting of a suspension bridge involve several three-dimensional modes, aerodynamic forces on cables and towers, and turbulence that varies along the span.","Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斷面模型只能代表二維流場，懸索橋的顫振與抖振卻牽涉多個三維模態、主纜與塔的氣動力，以及沿跨長變化的紊流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A section model represents only two-dimensional flow, while flutter and buffeting of a suspension bridge involve several three-dimensional modes, aerodynamic forces on cables and towers, and turbulence that varies along the span. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":37},{"id":"b003-v13-26","title":"全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對：定量估算","titleEn":"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Full model and typhoon records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Froude 相似：長度比 λ = 1/100 時，風速比 √λ = 1/10、頻率比 1/√λ = 10、單位長質量比 λ² = 1/10,000。實橋 80 m/s 對應模型 8 m/s；0.065 Hz 對應 0.65 Hz；44,000 kg/m 對應 4.4 kg/m；全長 3,911 m 的模型約 39 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Froude similarity: with length scale λ = 1/100, velocity scales by √λ = 1/10, frequency by 1/√λ = 10 and mass per length by λ² = 1/10,000. A full-scale 80 m/s maps to 8 m/s in the model, 0.065 Hz to 0.65 Hz, 44,000 kg/m to 4.4 kg/m, and the 3,911 m bridge becomes a model about 39 m long. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：模型先做自由振動試驗確認各模態頻率與阻尼符合相似要求，再在均勻流與紊流中逐級提高風速記錄位移與發散點；實橋比對時把颱風紀錄依平均風速分段，以頻譜辨識模態頻率與阻尼，並比較量測抖振位移與預測值的比值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: First run free-vibration tests on the model to confirm modal frequencies and damping meet similarity, then raise wind speed step by step in smooth and turbulent flow, recording displacement and divergence; for full-scale comparison bin typhoon records by mean wind speed, identify frequencies and damping from spectra, and compare the ratio of measured to predicted buffeting displacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Froude 相似：長度比 λ = 1/100 時，風速比 √λ = 1/10、頻率比 1/√λ = 10、單位長質量比 λ² = 1/10,000。實橋 80 m/s 對應模型 8 m/s；0.065 Hz 對應 0.65 Hz；44,000 kg/m 對應 4.4 kg/m；全長 3,911 m 的模型約 39 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Froude similarity: with length scale λ = 1/100, velocity scales by √λ = 1/10, frequency by 1/√λ = 10 and mass per length by λ² = 1/10,000. A full-scale 80 m/s maps to 8 m/s in the model, 0.065 Hz to 0.65 Hz, 44,000 kg/m to 4.4 kg/m, and the 3,911 m bridge becomes a model about 39 m long. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records\", which statement holds?","options":["減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。","懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。","Froude 相似：長度比 λ = 1/100 時，風速比 √λ = 1/10、頻率比 1/√λ = 10、單位長質量比 λ² = 1/10,000。"],"optionsEn":["The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be.","A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it.","Froude similarity: with length scale λ = 1/100, velocity scales by √λ = 1/10, frequency by 1/√λ = 10 and mass per length by λ² = 1/10,000."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Froude 相似：長度比 λ = 1/100 時，風速比 √λ = 1/10、頻率比 1/√λ = 10、單位長質量比 λ² = 1/10,000。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Froude similarity: with length scale λ = 1/100, velocity scales by √λ = 1/10, frequency by 1/√λ = 10 and mass per length by λ² = 1/10,000. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":38},{"id":"b003-v13-27","title":"全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Full model and typhoon records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"模型先做自由振動試驗確認各模態頻率與阻尼符合相似要求，再在均勻流與紊流中逐級提高風速記錄位移與發散點；實橋比對時把颱風紀錄依平均風速分段，以頻譜辨識模態頻率與阻尼，並比較量測抖振位移與預測值的比值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"First run free-vibration tests on the model to confirm modal frequencies and damping meet similarity, then raise wind speed step by step in smooth and turbulent flow, recording displacement and divergence; for full-scale comparison bin typhoon records by mean wind speed, identify frequencies and damping from spectra, and compare the ratio of measured to predicted buffeting displacement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：試驗計畫應明列相似律、模型頻率與阻尼的允差、紊流條件與試驗風攻角；完工監測報告要附原始資料與處理參數，讓日後研究者能以新方法重新分析並與風洞結果比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: The test plan must state the similarity law, tolerances on model frequency and damping, turbulence conditions and angles of attack; completion monitoring reports should include raw data and processing parameters so later researchers can reanalyse them and compare with the tunnel results.","failure":"注意干擾：模型阻尼過高或質量分布不符，會使顫振風速被高估；紊流強度與積分尺度若與海峽實況不同，抖振預測可能偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excess damping or wrong mass distribution in the model overestimates the flutter speed; turbulence intensity and integral scale unlike the strait's can bias buffeting predictions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"模型先做自由振動試驗確認各模態頻率與阻尼符合相似要求，再在均勻流與紊流中逐級提高風速記錄位移與發散點；實橋比對時把颱風紀錄依平均風速分段，以頻譜辨識模態頻率與阻尼，並比較量測抖振位移與預測值的比值。","textEn":"First run free-vibration tests on the model to confirm modal frequencies and damping meet similarity, then raise wind speed step by step in smooth and turbulent flow, recording displacement and divergence; for full-scale comparison bin typhoon records by mean wind speed, identify frequencies and damping from spectra, and compare the ratio of measured to predicted buffeting displacement.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"試驗計畫應明列相似律、模型頻率與阻尼的允差、紊流條件與試驗風攻角；完工監測報告要附原始資料與處理參數，讓日後研究者能以新方法重新分析並與風洞結果比較。","textEn":"The test plan must state the similarity law, tolerances on model frequency and damping, turbulence conditions and angles of attack; completion monitoring reports should include raw data and processing parameters so later researchers can reanalyse them and compare with the tunnel results.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records\"?","options":["模型先做自由振動試驗確認各模態頻率與阻尼符合相似要求，再在均勻流與紊流中逐級提高風速記錄位移與發散點。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。"],"optionsEn":["First run free-vibration tests on the model to confirm modal frequencies and damping meet similarity, then raise wind speed step by step in smooth and turbulent flow, recording displacement and divergence.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模型先做自由振動試驗確認各模態頻率與阻尼符合相似要求，再在均勻流與紊流中逐級提高風速記錄位移與發散點；實橋比對時把颱風紀錄依平均風速分段，以頻譜辨識模態頻率與阻尼，並比較量測抖振位移與預測值的比值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"First run free-vibration tests on the model to confirm modal frequencies and damping meet similarity, then raise wind speed step by step in smooth and turbulent flow, recording displacement and divergence; for full-scale comparison bin typhoon records by mean wind speed, identify frequencies and damping from spectra, and compare the ratio of measured to predicted buffeting displacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":39},{"id":"b003-v13-28","title":"全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對：失效診斷","titleEn":"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「全橋氣彈模型與颱風實測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Full model and typhoon records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模型阻尼過高或質量分布不符，會使顫振風速被高估；紊流強度與積分尺度若與海峽實況不同，抖振預測可能偏差。實測時若 GPS 多路徑誤差或風速計受橋體遮蔽未修正，也會錯誤地「驗證」或否定設計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excess damping or wrong mass distribution in the model overestimates the flutter speed; turbulence intensity and integral scale unlike the strait's can bias buffeting predictions. In field data, uncorrected GPS multipath or anemometers shielded by the deck can falsely confirm or reject the design. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：明石海峽大橋因此在大型風洞中做全橋氣彈模型試驗，模型需同時滿足幾何、質量、勁度與重力相似，以 Froude 相似律換算風速與頻率；完工後研究者再以颱風期間的風速計、加速度計與 GPS 實測，比對抖振位移與模態阻尼，驗證設計假設。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Akashi Kaikyo was therefore tested with a full aeroelastic model in a large wind tunnel, which must reproduce geometry, mass, stiffness and gravity together, with wind speed and frequency scaled by Froude similarity; after completion researchers compared buffeting displacement and modal damping with anemometer, accelerometer and GPS records from typhoons to validate the design assumptions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模型阻尼過高或質量分布不符，會使顫振風速被高估；紊流強度與積分尺度若與海峽實況不同，抖振預測可能偏差。實測時若 GPS 多路徑誤差或風速計受橋體遮蔽未修正，也會錯誤地「驗證」或否定設計。","textEn":"Excess damping or wrong mass distribution in the model overestimates the flutter speed; turbulence intensity and integral scale unlike the strait's can bias buffeting predictions. In field data, uncorrected GPS multipath or anemometers shielded by the deck can falsely confirm or reject the design.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「全橋模型試驗與颱風實測比對」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Full-bridge model tests versus typhoon records\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","模型阻尼過高或質量分布不符，會使顫振風速被高估；紊流強度與積分尺度若與海峽實況不同，抖振預測可能偏差。","只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Excess damping or wrong mass distribution in the model overestimates the flutter speed.","Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型阻尼過高或質量分布不符，會使顫振風速被高估；紊流強度與積分尺度若與海峽實況不同，抖振預測可能偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excess damping or wrong mass distribution in the model overestimates the flutter speed; turbulence intensity and integral scale unlike the strait's can bias buffeting predictions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":40},{"id":"b003-v13-29","title":"長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「長吊索尾流振動」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-hanger wake vibration” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"明石海峽大橋部分吊索長度超過 200 m，每個索夾處有並排的平行鋼絲吊索，間距約為吊索直徑的 9 倍。完工後觀察到在約 20 m/s 的風中，背風側吊索因位於迎風吊索的尾流中而大幅振動；過去一般認為這類尾流馳振只在間距小於約 5 倍直徑時發生。風洞試驗顯示，在吊索表面螺旋纏繞直徑 10 mm 的鋼絲可打亂尾流與表面分離，降低振動，營運單位並開發了纏絲機械施作。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「長吊索尾流振動」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Some Akashi Kaikyo hangers exceed 200 m, and at each cable band parallel-wire hanger ropes run side by side at a spacing of about nine rope diameters. After completion the leeward ropes were seen vibrating strongly in winds of about 20 m/s because they sat in the wake of the windward ropes; such wake galloping had previously been thought to occur only at spacings below about five diameters. Wind-tunnel tests showed that winding 10 mm wire helically around the rope disrupts the wake and surface separation and reduces the vibration, and the operator developed a winding machine to install it. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Long-hanger wake vibration” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：弦頻率 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: String frequency f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「長吊索尾流振動」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Long-hanger wake vibration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-29-k1","title":"長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲","titleEn":"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire","text":"明石海峽大橋部分吊索長度超過 200 m，每個索夾處有並排的平行鋼絲吊索，間距約為吊索直徑的 9 倍。完工後觀察到在約 20 m/s 的風中，背風側吊索因位於迎風吊索的尾流中而大幅振動；過去一般認為這類尾流馳振只在間距小於約 5 倍直徑時發生。","textEn":"Some Akashi Kaikyo hangers exceed 200 m, and at each cable band parallel-wire hanger ropes run side by side at a spacing of about nine rope diameters. After completion the leeward ropes were seen vibrating strongly in winds of about 20 m/s because they sat in the wake of the windward ropes; such wake galloping had previously been thought to occur only at spacings below about five diameters.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire\" is correct?","options":["只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。","主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。","明石海峽大橋部分吊索長度超過 200 m，每個索夾處有並排的平行鋼絲吊索，間距約為吊索直徑的 9 倍。"],"optionsEn":["Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration.","With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.","Some Akashi Kaikyo hangers exceed 200 m, and at each cable band parallel-wire hanger ropes run side by side at a spacing of about nine rope diameters."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明石海峽大橋部分吊索長度超過 200 m，每個索夾處有並排的平行鋼絲吊索，間距約為吊索直徑的 9 倍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Some Akashi Kaikyo hangers exceed 200 m, and at each cable band parallel-wire hanger ropes run side by side at a spacing of about nine rope diameters. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":41},{"id":"b003-v13-30","title":"長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長吊索尾流振動」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-hanger wake vibration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：弦頻率 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。取 L = 200 m、T = 1.6 MN、m = 40 kg/m：√(T/m) = 200 m/s，f₁ = 200/400 = 0.5 Hz。直徑 D = 0.09 m、風速 20 m/s 時折減風速 U/(f·D) = 20/(0.5×0.09) ≈ 444，遠高於渦振範圍，屬尾流馳振區；間距 9D ≈ 0.81 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: String frequency f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). With L = 200 m, T = 1.6 MN and m = 40 kg/m: √(T/m) = 200 m/s and f₁ = 200/400 = 0.5 Hz. With D = 0.09 m at 20 m/s the reduced velocity U/(f·D) = 20/(0.5×0.09) ≈ 444, far above the vortex range and in the wake-galloping regime; the spacing 9D ≈ 0.81 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表性吊索上安裝加速度計與風速風向計，記錄振幅與風向、風速的關係，辨識振動只出現在特定風向與背風索；風洞中以成對索段試驗有無纏絲、不同纏繞節距的反應，選定方案後再在實橋試裝並比較前後振幅。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fit accelerometers and anemometers to representative hangers and relate amplitude to wind speed and direction, confirming that vibration appears only for certain directions and on the leeward rope; in the wind tunnel test paired rope segments with and without wire and with different pitches, then trial-fit the chosen scheme on the bridge and compare amplitudes before and after.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"弦頻率 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。取 L = 200 m、T = 1.6 MN、m = 40 kg/m：√(T/m) = 200 m/s，f₁ = 200/400 = 0.5 Hz。直徑 D = 0.09 m、風速 20 m/s 時折減風速 U/(f·D) = 20/(0.5×0.09) ≈ 444，遠高於渦振範圍，屬尾流馳振區；間距 9D ≈ 0.81 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"String frequency f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). With L = 200 m, T = 1.6 MN and m = 40 kg/m: √(T/m) = 200 m/s and f₁ = 200/400 = 0.5 Hz. With D = 0.09 m at 20 m/s the reduced velocity U/(f·D) = 20/(0.5×0.09) ≈ 444, far above the vortex range and in the wake-galloping regime; the spacing 9D ≈ 0.81 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire\", which statement holds?","options":["弦頻率 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。","桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。","鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。"],"optionsEn":["String frequency f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m).","A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter.","The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"弦頻率 f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"String frequency f₁ = (1/2L)·√(T/m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":42},{"id":"b003-v13-31","title":"長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長吊索尾流振動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-hanger wake vibration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表性吊索上安裝加速度計與風速風向計，記錄振幅與風向、風速的關係，辨識振動只出現在特定風向與背風索；風洞中以成對索段試驗有無纏絲、不同纏繞節距的反應，選定方案後再在實橋試裝並比較前後振幅。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fit accelerometers and anemometers to representative hangers and relate amplitude to wind speed and direction, confirming that vibration appears only for certain directions and on the leeward rope; in the wind tunnel test paired rope segments with and without wire and with different pitches, then trial-fit the chosen scheme on the bridge and compare amplitudes before and after. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：長吊索的振動觀測應從完工初期就納入監測計畫，特定風向的異常振動要記錄並回報設計者；纏絲、阻尼器或連結件等對策必須先經風洞或試裝驗證，並確認不妨礙日後的磁通檢測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Observation of long-hanger vibration should be in the monitoring plan from the first year, recording and reporting unusual vibration in particular wind directions; wire winding, dampers or ties must be proven by wind-tunnel tests or trial fitting and must not obstruct later magnetic-flux inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：長吊索反覆大振幅擺動會使索夾出口與錨頭處彎曲應力集中、鋼絲磨損與疲勞，兩索相互碰撞也會損傷護套與防蝕層，讓水分進入吊索內部。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated large swings of long hangers concentrate bending stress where the rope exits the cable band and at its socket, wearing and fatiguing the wires; ropes striking each other also damage sheathing and corrosion protection and let water into the rope. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表性吊索上安裝加速度計與風速風向計，記錄振幅與風向、風速的關係，辨識振動只出現在特定風向與背風索；風洞中以成對索段試驗有無纏絲、不同纏繞節距的反應，選定方案後再在實橋試裝並比較前後振幅。","textEn":"Fit accelerometers and anemometers to representative hangers and relate amplitude to wind speed and direction, confirming that vibration appears only for certain directions and on the leeward rope; in the wind tunnel test paired rope segments with and without wire and with different pitches, then trial-fit the chosen scheme on the bridge and compare amplitudes before and after.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"長吊索的振動觀測應從完工初期就納入監測計畫，特定風向的異常振動要記錄並回報設計者；纏絲、阻尼器或連結件等對策必須先經風洞或試裝驗證，並確認不妨礙日後的磁通檢測。","textEn":"Observation of long-hanger vibration should be in the monitoring plan from the first year, recording and reporting unusual vibration in particular wind directions; wire winding, dampers or ties must be proven by wind-tunnel tests or trial fitting and must not obstruct later magnetic-flux inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在代表性吊索上安裝加速度計與風速風向計，記錄振幅與風向、風速的關係，辨識振動只出現在特定風向與背風索。","索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Fit accelerometers and anemometers to representative hangers and relate amplitude to wind speed and direction, confirming that vibration appears only for certain directions and on the leeward rope.","Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在代表性吊索上安裝加速度計與風速風向計，記錄振幅與風向、風速的關係，辨識振動只出現在特定風向與背風索；風洞中以成對索段試驗有無纏絲、不同纏繞節距的反應，選定方案後再在實橋試裝並比較前後振幅。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fit accelerometers and anemometers to representative hangers and relate amplitude to wind speed and direction, confirming that vibration appears only for certain directions and on the leeward rope; in the wind tunnel test paired rope segments with and without wire and with different pitches, then trial-fit the chosen scheme on the bridge and compare amplitudes before and after. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":43},{"id":"b003-v13-32","title":"長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長吊索尾流振動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-hanger wake vibration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"長吊索反覆大振幅擺動會使索夾出口與錨頭處彎曲應力集中、鋼絲磨損與疲勞，兩索相互碰撞也會損傷護套與防蝕層，讓水分進入吊索內部。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated large swings of long hangers concentrate bending stress where the rope exits the cable band and at its socket, wearing and fatiguing the wires; ropes striking each other also damage sheathing and corrosion protection and let water into the rope. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：風洞試驗顯示，在吊索表面螺旋纏繞直徑 10 mm 的鋼絲可打亂尾流與表面分離，降低振動，營運單位並開發了纏絲機械施作。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wind-tunnel tests showed that winding 10 mm wire helically around the rope disrupts the wake and surface separation and reduces the vibration, and the operator developed a winding machine to install it.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要吊索間距大於 5 倍直徑，就不會有尾流振動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hangers spaced more than five diameters apart can never suffer wake vibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"長吊索反覆大振幅擺動會使索夾出口與錨頭處彎曲應力集中、鋼絲磨損與疲勞，兩索相互碰撞也會損傷護套與防蝕層，讓水分進入吊索內部。","textEn":"Repeated large swings of long hangers concentrate bending stress where the rope exits the cable band and at its socket, wearing and fatiguing the wires; ropes striking each other also damage sheathing and corrosion protection and let water into the rope.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長吊索尾流振動與螺旋纏絲」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-hanger wake vibration and helical wire\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。","長吊索反覆大振幅擺動會使索夾出口與錨頭處彎曲應力集中、鋼絲磨損與疲勞，兩索相互碰撞也會損傷護套與防蝕層，讓水分進入吊索內部。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.","Repeated large swings of long hangers concentrate bending stress where the rope exits the cable band and at its socket, wearing and fatiguing the wires."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長吊索反覆大振幅擺動會使索夾出口與錨頭處彎曲應力集中、鋼絲磨損與疲勞，兩索相互碰撞也會損傷護套與防蝕層，讓水分進入吊索內部。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated large swings of long hangers concentrate bending stress where the rope exits the cable band and at its socket, wearing and fatiguing the wires; ropes striking each other also damage sheathing and corrosion protection and let water into the rope. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":44}],"order":7},{"id":"b003-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支」與「減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection\" and \"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b003-v13-33","title":"主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「主纜送氣出口濕度」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cable exhaust humidity” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"本州四國連絡橋的檢查發現，舊有懸索橋拆開鍍鋅纏絲後鋼絲已有鏽蝕，因此開發了將乾燥空氣送入主纜內部的系統，並以世界首創的形式用於明石海峽大橋與其他懸索橋。管理目標是纜內相對濕度 40%，比會發生腐蝕的約 60% 留有安全餘裕；夏季高濕時另加預冷設備除濕。乾燥空氣沿主纜空隙流動，一路蒸發並帶走殘留水分，最後從排氣口排出，排氣口的濕度就是纜內是否已乾燥的指標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主纜送氣出口濕度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inspections of older Honshu-Shikoku suspension bridges found rust on wires once the galvanised wrapping was removed, so a system injecting dry air into the main cable was developed and used, as a world first, on Akashi Kaikyo and the other suspension bridges. The management target is 40% relative humidity inside the cable, a margin below the roughly 60% at which corrosion occurs; pre-coolers dehumidify humid summer air. The dry air travels through the cable voids, evaporating and carrying away trapped moisture before leaving at exhaust points, so exhaust humidity is the indicator of whether the cable interior is dry. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cable exhaust humidity” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：25 °C 飽和水氣密度約 23.0 g/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Saturated vapour density at 25 °C is about 23.0 g/m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主纜送氣出口濕度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cable exhaust humidity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-33-k1","title":"主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支","titleEn":"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection","text":"本州四國連絡橋的檢查發現，舊有懸索橋拆開鍍鋅纏絲後鋼絲已有鏽蝕，因此開發了將乾燥空氣送入主纜內部的系統，並以世界首創的形式用於明石海峽大橋與其他懸索橋。管理目標是纜內相對濕度 40%，比會發生腐蝕的約 60% 留有安全餘裕；夏季高濕時另加預冷設備除濕。","textEn":"Inspections of older Honshu-Shikoku suspension bridges found rust on wires once the galvanised wrapping was removed, so a system injecting dry air into the main cable was developed and used, as a world first, on Akashi Kaikyo and the other suspension bridges. The management target is 40% relative humidity inside the cable, a margin below the roughly 60% at which corrosion occurs; pre-coolers dehumidify humid summer air.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection\" is correct?","options":["本州四國連絡橋的檢查發現，舊有懸索橋拆開鍍鋅纏絲後鋼絲已有鏽蝕，因此開發了將乾燥空氣送入主纜內部的系統，並以世界首創的形式用於明石海峽大橋與其他懸索橋。","主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。","減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Inspections of older Honshu-Shikoku suspension bridges found rust on wires once the galvanised wrapping was removed, so a system injecting dry air into the main cable was developed and used, as a world first, on Akashi Kaikyo and the other suspension bridges.","With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.","The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本州四國連絡橋的檢查發現，舊有懸索橋拆開鍍鋅纏絲後鋼絲已有鏽蝕，因此開發了將乾燥空氣送入主纜內部的系統，並以世界首創的形式用於明石海峽大橋與其他懸索橋。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inspections of older Honshu-Shikoku suspension bridges found rust on wires once the galvanised wrapping was removed, so a system injecting dry air into the main cable was developed and used, as a world first, on Akashi Kaikyo and the other suspension bridges. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":45},{"id":"b003-v13-34","title":"主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主纜送氣出口濕度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cable exhaust humidity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：25 °C 飽和水氣密度約 23.0 g/m³。送入 15% RH 空氣（3.5 g/m³），出口 40% RH（9.2 g/m³），每立方公尺帶走約 5.7 g。流量 1.0 m³/min 時每日 1,440 m³，約 8.2 kg 水；若段內殘留 50 kg 水，約 6 天才能排除。主纜空隙約 0.989×20% ≈ 0.198 m³/m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Saturated vapour density at 25 °C is about 23.0 g/m³. Injecting air at 15% RH (3.5 g/m³) with exhaust at 40% RH (9.2 g/m³) removes about 5.7 g per cubic metre. At 1.0 m³/min, 1,440 m³ a day carries about 8.2 kg of water, so 50 kg trapped in a section takes about 6 days to clear. Cable voids are about 0.989×20% ≈ 0.198 m³ per metre. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在每個送氣與排氣口連續記錄溫度、相對濕度與流量，計算各段的露點與水分移除量；排氣濕度持續高於目標時，先檢查包覆氣密與送氣壓力，再於低點開窗目視檢查鋼絲鍍鋅狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Log temperature, relative humidity and flow continuously at every injection and exhaust point, computing dew point and moisture removal per section; if exhaust humidity stays above target, first check wrapping airtightness and supply pressure, then open an inspection window at a low point to inspect the zinc on the wires.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"25 °C 飽和水氣密度約 23.0 g/m³。送入 15% RH 空氣（3.5 g/m³），出口 40% RH（9.2 g/m³），每立方公尺帶走約 5.7 g。流量 1.0 m³/min 時每日 1,440 m³，約 8.2 kg 水；若段內殘留 50 kg 水，約 6 天才能排除。主纜空隙約 0.989×20% ≈ 0.198 m³/m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Saturated vapour density at 25 °C is about 23.0 g/m³. Injecting air at 15% RH (3.5 g/m³) with exhaust at 40% RH (9.2 g/m³) removes about 5.7 g per cubic metre. At 1.0 m³/min, 1,440 m³ a day carries about 8.2 kg of water, so 50 kg trapped in a section takes about 6 days to clear. Cable voids are about 0.989×20% ≈ 0.198 m³ per metre. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection\", which statement holds?","options":["懸索橋很柔，所以地震對它幾乎沒有影響。","25 °C 飽和水氣密度約 23.0 g/m³。","水中混凝土只要配比強度夠高，澆置方式不影響品質。"],"optionsEn":["A suspension bridge is so flexible that earthquakes hardly affect it.","Saturated vapour density at 25 °C is about 23.0 g/m³.","If the underwater mix is strong enough, the placing method does not affect quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"25 °C 飽和水氣密度約 23.0 g/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Saturated vapour density at 25 °C is about 23.0 g/m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":46},{"id":"b003-v13-35","title":"主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主纜送氣出口濕度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cable exhaust humidity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在每個送氣與排氣口連續記錄溫度、相對濕度與流量，計算各段的露點與水分移除量；排氣濕度持續高於目標時，先檢查包覆氣密與送氣壓力，再於低點開窗目視檢查鋼絲鍍鋅狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Log temperature, relative humidity and flow continuously at every injection and exhaust point, computing dew point and moisture removal per section; if exhaust humidity stays above target, first check wrapping airtightness and supply pressure, then open an inspection window at a low point to inspect the zinc on the wires. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把每個區段的排氣濕度、流量與設備運轉狀態納入中央監控與警報，維修紀錄須連結到區段編號；包覆修補、索夾更換等作業後要重新做氣密與流量確認，才算結案。","observationEn":"Site practice: Bring exhaust humidity, flow and equipment status for every section into central monitoring with alarms, link maintenance records to section numbers, and close out wrapping repairs or cable-band work only after airtightness and flow are re-verified.","failure":"注意干擾：包覆破損或索夾密封失效會讓乾燥空氣從近端漏出，遠端仍潮濕，平均讀值卻看似正常；送氣設備故障未被警報偵測時，纜內濕度數週內就可能回升到腐蝕門檻以上。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Damaged wrapping or failed cable-band seals let dry air escape near the inlet while the far end stays wet, even though average readings look normal; an equipment fault not caught by alarms can let internal humidity climb above the corrosion threshold within weeks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在每個送氣與排氣口連續記錄溫度、相對濕度與流量，計算各段的露點與水分移除量；排氣濕度持續高於目標時，先檢查包覆氣密與送氣壓力，再於低點開窗目視檢查鋼絲鍍鋅狀態。","textEn":"Log temperature, relative humidity and flow continuously at every injection and exhaust point, computing dew point and moisture removal per section; if exhaust humidity stays above target, first check wrapping airtightness and supply pressure, then open an inspection window at a low point to inspect the zinc on the wires.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把每個區段的排氣濕度、流量與設備運轉狀態納入中央監控與警報，維修紀錄須連結到區段編號；包覆修補、索夾更換等作業後要重新做氣密與流量確認，才算結案。","textEn":"Bring exhaust humidity, flow and equipment status for every section into central monitoring with alarms, link maintenance records to section numbers, and close out wrapping repairs or cable-band work only after airtightness and flow are re-verified.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地震後只要把橋塔推回原位，就能維持原設計線形。","在每個送氣與排氣口連續記錄溫度、相對濕度與流量，計算各段的露點與水分移除量；排氣濕度持續高於目標時，先檢查包覆氣密與送氣壓力，再於低點開窗目視檢查鋼絲鍍鋅狀態。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","After an earthquake you simply push the towers back to restore the design profile.","Log temperature, relative humidity and flow continuously at every injection and exhaust point, computing dew point and moisture removal per section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在每個送氣與排氣口連續記錄溫度、相對濕度與流量，計算各段的露點與水分移除量；排氣濕度持續高於目標時，先檢查包覆氣密與送氣壓力，再於低點開窗目視檢查鋼絲鍍鋅狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Log temperature, relative humidity and flow continuously at every injection and exhaust point, computing dew point and moisture removal per section; if exhaust humidity stays above target, first check wrapping airtightness and supply pressure, then open an inspection window at a low point to inspect the zinc on the wires. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":47},{"id":"b003-v13-36","title":"主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主纜送氣出口濕度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cable exhaust humidity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"包覆破損或索夾密封失效會讓乾燥空氣從近端漏出，遠端仍潮濕，平均讀值卻看似正常；送氣設備故障未被警報偵測時，纜內濕度數週內就可能回升到腐蝕門檻以上。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Damaged wrapping or failed cable-band seals let dry air escape near the inlet while the far end stays wet, even though average readings look normal; an equipment fault not caught by alarms can let internal humidity climb above the corrosion threshold within weeks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：乾燥空氣沿主纜空隙流動，一路蒸發並帶走殘留水分，最後從排氣口排出，排氣口的濕度就是纜內是否已乾燥的指標。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The dry air travels through the cable voids, evaporating and carrying away trapped moisture before leaving at exhaust points, so exhaust humidity is the indicator of whether the cable interior is dry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主纜外面有鍍鋅纏絲與塗裝，內部就不會潮濕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With galvanised wrapping and paint outside, the cable interior cannot get wet.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"包覆破損或索夾密封失效會讓乾燥空氣從近端漏出，遠端仍潮濕，平均讀值卻看似正常；送氣設備故障未被警報偵測時，纜內濕度數週內就可能回升到腐蝕門檻以上。","textEn":"Damaged wrapping or failed cable-band seals let dry air escape near the inlet while the far end stays wet, even though average readings look normal; an equipment fault not caught by alarms can let internal humidity climb above the corrosion threshold within weeks.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜乾燥空氣的水分收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moisture budget of cable dry-air injection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["包覆破損或索夾密封失效會讓乾燥空氣從近端漏出，遠端仍潮濕，平均讀值卻看似正常；送氣設備故障未被警報偵測時，纜內濕度數週內就可能回升到腐蝕門檻以上。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Damaged wrapping or failed cable-band seals let dry air escape near the inlet while the far end stays wet, even though average readings look normal.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be."],"answer":0,"explanation":"包覆破損或索夾密封失效會讓乾燥空氣從近端漏出，遠端仍潮濕，平均讀值卻看似正常；送氣設備故障未被警報偵測時，纜內濕度數週內就可能回升到腐蝕門檻以上。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Damaged wrapping or failed cable-band seals let dry air escape near the inlet while the far end stays wet, even though average readings look normal; an equipment fault not caught by alarms can let internal humidity climb above the corrosion threshold within weeks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":48},{"id":"b003-v13-37","title":"減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」如何影響明石海峽大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tower TMDs and 200-year target” governs force, deformation or durability in “Akashi Kaikyo Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"本州四國連絡橋的維護方針以 200 年以上的長期使用為目標，以預防保全與資產管理把生命週期成本降到最低。明石海峽主塔為十字形斷面，風洞試驗顯示若無減振裝置，塔在橫向風中振幅可達約 95 cm，裝設 TMD 與附加阻尼器後約 10 cm，容許值 30 cm；公開簡報列出共約 40 組 TMD 與 8 組附加阻尼器。營運後實測塔位移小於約 2 cm，營運單位因而研究把減振裝置的維護週期由每 5 年延長到約 14 年。這是以監測數據調整維護投入的典型案例。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Honshu-Shikoku maintenance policy targets service of 200 years or more, minimising life-cycle cost through preventive maintenance and asset management. The Akashi Kaikyo towers have a cruciform section; wind-tunnel tests showed transverse-wind amplitudes of about 95 cm without dampers and about 10 cm with TMDs and additional dampers, against an allowable 30 cm, and a public presentation lists about 40 TMDs and 8 additional dampers. Measured tower displacement in service stayed below about 2 cm, so the operator studied extending the damper maintenance interval from every 5 years to about 14 years, a typical case of using monitoring data to tune maintenance effort. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tower TMDs and 200-year target” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：渦振振幅約與總阻尼成反比。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Vortex-induced amplitude is roughly inversely proportional to total damping.","failure":"常見誤解：「減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tower TMDs and 200-year target”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-37-k1","title":"減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理","titleEn":"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management","text":"本州四國連絡橋的維護方針以 200 年以上的長期使用為目標，以預防保全與資產管理把生命週期成本降到最低。明石海峽主塔為十字形斷面，風洞試驗顯示若無減振裝置，塔在橫向風中振幅可達約 95 cm，裝設 TMD 與附加阻尼器後約 10 cm，容許值 30 cm；公開簡報列出共約 40 組 TMD 與 8 組附加阻尼器。","textEn":"The Honshu-Shikoku maintenance policy targets service of 200 years or more, minimising life-cycle cost through preventive maintenance and asset management. The Akashi Kaikyo towers have a cruciform section; wind-tunnel tests showed transverse-wind amplitudes of about 95 cm without dampers and about 10 cm with TMDs and additional dampers, against an allowable 30 cm, and a public presentation lists about 40 TMDs and 8 additional dampers.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management\" is correct?","options":["減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。","本州四國連絡橋的維護方針以 200 年以上的長期使用為目標，以預防保全與資產管理把生命週期成本降到最低。","桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。"],"optionsEn":["The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be.","The Honshu-Shikoku maintenance policy targets service of 200 years or more, minimising life-cycle cost through preventive maintenance and asset management.","A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本州四國連絡橋的維護方針以 200 年以上的長期使用為目標，以預防保全與資產管理把生命週期成本降到最低。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Honshu-Shikoku maintenance policy targets service of 200 years or more, minimising life-cycle cost through preventive maintenance and asset management. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":49},{"id":"b003-v13-38","title":"減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理：定量估算","titleEn":"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tower TMDs and 200-year target” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：渦振振幅約與總阻尼成反比。設塔結構阻尼 ζ_s = 0.5%，95 cm 降到 10 cm 需總阻尼 0.5%×95/10 ≈ 4.75%，即 TMD 附加約 4.25%；要符合 30 cm 只需 0.5%×95/30 ≈ 1.58%。若 TMD 劣化使附加阻尼減半，總阻尼約 2.6%，振幅約 95×0.5/2.6 ≈ 18 cm，仍低於容許值。阻尼比為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Vortex-induced amplitude is roughly inversely proportional to total damping. With tower damping ζ_s = 0.5%, cutting 95 cm to 10 cm needs about 0.5%×95/10 ≈ 4.75% in total, so the TMDs add about 4.25%; meeting 30 cm needs only 0.5%×95/30 ≈ 1.58%. If TMD ageing halves the added damping, the total is about 2.6% and the amplitude about 95×0.5/2.6 ≈ 18 cm, still within the limit. Damping ratios are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以塔內加速度與位移長期紀錄，篩選可能引發振動的強風事件，比較實測振幅與設計預測；定期抽驗 TMD 的頻率與阻尼係數，並做阻尼變化 ±20%、±50% 的敏感度分析，確認延長維護週期後仍滿足容許位移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use long-term tower acceleration and displacement records to pick out strong-wind events capable of exciting vibration and compare measured amplitudes with design predictions; periodically spot-check TMD frequency and damping coefficient, and run sensitivity analyses for ±20% and ±50% damping changes to confirm that the allowable displacement is still met with a longer interval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"渦振振幅約與總阻尼成反比。設塔結構阻尼 ζ_s = 0.5%，95 cm 降到 10 cm 需總阻尼 0.5%×95/10 ≈ 4.75%，即 TMD 附加約 4.25%；要符合 30 cm 只需 0.5%×95/30 ≈ 1.58%。若 TMD 劣化使附加阻尼減半，總阻尼約 2.6%，振幅約 95×0.5/2.6 ≈ 18 cm，仍低於容許值。阻尼比為教學假設。","textEn":"Vortex-induced amplitude is roughly inversely proportional to total damping. With tower damping ζ_s = 0.5%, cutting 95 cm to 10 cm needs about 0.5%×95/10 ≈ 4.75% in total, so the TMDs add about 4.25%; meeting 30 cm needs only 0.5%×95/30 ≈ 1.58%. If TMD ageing halves the added damping, the total is about 2.6% and the amplitude about 95×0.5/2.6 ≈ 18 cm, still within the limit. Damping ratios are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼絲強度越高，主纜就越不需要防蝕。","索股垂度只要白天量一次，誤差幾公分不影響主纜受力。","渦振振幅約與總阻尼成反比。"],"optionsEn":["The stronger the wire, the less corrosion protection the cable needs.","Measuring strand sag once in daytime is fine; a few centimetres of error do not affect cable forces.","Vortex-induced amplitude is roughly inversely proportional to total damping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"渦振振幅約與總阻尼成反比。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Vortex-induced amplitude is roughly inversely proportional to total damping. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":50},{"id":"b003-v13-39","title":"減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tower TMDs and 200-year target” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以塔內加速度與位移長期紀錄，篩選可能引發振動的強風事件，比較實測振幅與設計預測；定期抽驗 TMD 的頻率與阻尼係數，並做阻尼變化 ±20%、±50% 的敏感度分析，確認延長維護週期後仍滿足容許位移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use long-term tower acceleration and displacement records to pick out strong-wind events capable of exciting vibration and compare measured amplitudes with design predictions; periodically spot-check TMD frequency and damping coefficient, and run sensitivity analyses for ±20% and ±50% damping changes to confirm that the allowable displacement is still met with a longer interval. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何維護週期的延長都要附上監測證據、敏感度分析與重新評估的觸發條件（例如觀測到某風速以上的事件或振幅超過門檻），並由業主的技術委員會核准；檢查與修繕紀錄納入資料庫以 PDCA 循環更新計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Any extension of a maintenance interval must come with monitoring evidence, sensitivity analysis and re-assessment triggers (such as an event above a given wind speed or amplitude above a threshold), approved by the owner's technical committee; inspection and repair records go into the database so the plan is updated through a PDCA cycle.","failure":"注意干擾：若不看監測數據而一律縮短週期，維護成本與封閉作業增加卻無性能收益；反之若沒有敏感度分析就延長週期，TMD 卡滯或失調可能在下一次強風時才被發現，塔與索鞍承受未預期的反覆應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shortening intervals regardless of monitoring data adds cost and closures for no performance gain; extending them without sensitivity analysis can leave a stuck or detuned TMD undiscovered until the next strong wind, exposing towers and saddles to unexpected cyclic stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以塔內加速度與位移長期紀錄，篩選可能引發振動的強風事件，比較實測振幅與設計預測；定期抽驗 TMD 的頻率與阻尼係數，並做阻尼變化 ±20%、±50% 的敏感度分析，確認延長維護週期後仍滿足容許位移。","textEn":"Use long-term tower acceleration and displacement records to pick out strong-wind events capable of exciting vibration and compare measured amplitudes with design predictions; periodically spot-check TMD frequency and damping coefficient, and run sensitivity analyses for ±20% and ±50% damping changes to confirm that the allowable displacement is still met with a longer interval.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何維護週期的延長都要附上監測證據、敏感度分析與重新評估的觸發條件（例如觀測到某風速以上的事件或振幅超過門檻），並由業主的技術委員會核准；檢查與修繕紀錄納入資料庫以 PDCA 循環更新計畫。","textEn":"Any extension of a maintenance interval must come with monitoring evidence, sensitivity analysis and re-assessment triggers (such as an event above a given wind speed or amplitude above a threshold), approved by the owner's technical committee; inspection and repair records go into the database so the plan is updated through a PDCA cycle.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management\"?","options":["以塔內加速度與位移長期紀錄，篩選可能引發振動的強風事件，比較實測振幅與設計預測。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","全橋模型的風速必須和實橋一樣，試驗才有意義。"],"optionsEn":["Use long-term tower acceleration and displacement records to pick out strong-wind events capable of exciting vibration and compare measured amplitudes with design predictions.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A full-bridge model is only meaningful if tested at the same wind speed as the real bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以塔內加速度與位移長期紀錄，篩選可能引發振動的強風事件，比較實測振幅與設計預測；定期抽驗 TMD 的頻率與阻尼係數，並做阻尼變化 ±20%、±50% 的敏感度分析，確認延長維護週期後仍滿足容許位移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use long-term tower acceleration and displacement records to pick out strong-wind events capable of exciting vibration and compare measured amplitudes with design predictions; periodically spot-check TMD frequency and damping coefficient, and run sensitivity analyses for ±20% and ±50% damping changes to confirm that the allowable displacement is still met with a longer interval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":51},{"id":"b003-v13-40","title":"減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"],"prerequisiteIds":["b003-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塔內 TMD 與 200 年目標」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tower TMDs and 200-year target” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若不看監測數據而一律縮短週期，維護成本與封閉作業增加卻無性能收益；反之若沒有敏感度分析就延長週期，TMD 卡滯或失調可能在下一次強風時才被發現，塔與索鞍承受未預期的反覆應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shortening intervals regardless of monitoring data adds cost and closures for no performance gain; extending them without sensitivity analysis can leave a stuck or detuned TMD undiscovered until the next strong wind, exposing towers and saddles to unexpected cyclic stress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這是以監測數據調整維護投入的典型案例。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measured tower displacement in service stayed below about 2 cm, so the operator studied extending the damper maintenance interval from every 5 years to about 14 years, a typical case of using monitoring data to tune maintenance effort.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「減振裝置維護得越頻繁，橋梁一定越安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The more often dampers are serviced, the safer the bridge must be.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b003-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若不看監測數據而一律縮短週期，維護成本與封閉作業增加卻無性能收益；反之若沒有敏感度分析就延長週期，TMD 卡滯或失調可能在下一次強風時才被發現，塔與索鞍承受未預期的反覆應力。","textEn":"Shortening intervals regardless of monitoring data adds cost and closures for no performance gain; extending them without sensitivity analysis can leave a stuck or detuned TMD undiscovered until the next strong wind, exposing towers and saddles to unexpected cyclic stress.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]},{"id":"b003-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-jb-honshi-maintenance-super","v13s-jb-honshi-construction-material","v13s-wcee-akashi-seismic","v13s-iaarc-akashi-caisson-concrete","v13s-piarc-akashi-tower-dampers"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「減振裝置維護與 200 年資產管理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damper upkeep and 200-year asset management\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若不看監測數據而一律縮短週期，維護成本與封閉作業增加卻無性能收益。","桁架加勁梁很深很重，所以不會發生顫振。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shortening intervals regardless of monitoring data adds cost and closures for no performance gain.","A truss stiffening girder is deep and heavy, so it cannot flutter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若不看監測數據而一律縮短週期，維護成本與封閉作業增加卻無性能收益；反之若沒有敏感度分析就延長週期，TMD 卡滯或失調可能在下一次強風時才被發現，塔與索鞍承受未預期的反覆應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shortening intervals regardless of monitoring data adds cost and closures for no performance gain; extending them without sensitivity analysis can leave a stuck or detuned TMD undiscovered until the next strong wind, exposing towers and saddles to unexpected cyclic stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":52}],"order":8}],"title":"明石海峽大橋","titleEn":"Akashi Kaikyo Bridge","summary":"從海峽條件到主纜防蝕，拆解懸索橋的受力、施工幾何與營運證據。","summaryEn":"Trace a suspension bridge from strait conditions to cable corrosion protection through load paths, construction geometry and operating evidence.","scope":"以公開資料建立的原創教學分解；所有步驟為紙上、數位模型與證據判讀練習。自繪的示意與自設資料必須標示假設；本站未提供現地工程資料，亦不是核准施工、設備操作或水質放行程序。","scopeEn":"Original educational decomposition of public information. Every step is a paper, digital-model or evidence-interpretation exercise. Label assumptions in self-drawn diagrams and invented data; this site does not supply field engineering records or approved construction, operating or water-release procedures.","diagram":{"type":"suspension","labels":["地盤與錨碇","橋塔","主纜","吊索與橋面","監測"],"labelsEn":["Ground and anchorages","Towers","Main cables","Hangers and deck","Monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":52,"estimatedMinutes":1240,"curriculumVersion":6,"enrichmentVersion":13,"learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-suspension","learningTags":["structures","st-suspension","suspension"],"subcategory":"st-suspension","subcategoryTitle":"懸索橋巨作與主纜系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Suspension bridges and main-cable systems","v13Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"suspension","architectureNodes":[["主塔與塔內 TMD","Towers and tower TMDs"],["PWS 主纜","PWS main cables"],["吊索與螺旋纏絲","Hangers and helical wire"],["桁架加勁梁","Truss stiffening girder"],["設置沉箱與錨碇","Laid-down caissons and anchorages"],["乾燥空氣與監測","Dry air and monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[1,0],[0,4],[1,4],[5,1],[5,0]]},"v13Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"延伸練習：假設主跨 l = 1,991 m、垂跨比 n = 1/10（f = 199.1 m），兩條主纜與加勁梁合計恆載 w = 431.6 kN/m（44 t/m）。水平張力 H = w·l²/(8f) = 431.6×1,991²/(8×199.1) ≈ 1,074,000 kN，每纜 537 MN；塔頂最大張力 T = H·√(1+16n²) = 537×1.077 ≈ 578 MN。每纜鋼絲面積 0.791 m²，恆載應力 = 578/0.791 ≈ 731 N/mm²，對 1,760 N/mm² 鋼絲的恆載安全係數約 2.41；若活載與溫度再使張力增加 10%，係數降為約 2.19。若改用 1,570 N/mm² 鋼絲而面積不變，恆載係數只剩約 2.15，這正是公開資料說需要每側兩條纜的原因。地震後跨徑若增加 0.8 m，不可伸長估算垂度減少約 1.46 m。數值為教學假設，不代表明石海峽大橋的設計計算。","textEn":"Extension exercise: assume l = 1,991 m, sag ratio n = 1/10 (f = 199.1 m) and a dead load for both cables and the girder of w = 431.6 kN/m (44 t/m). Horizontal tension H = w·l²/(8f) = 431.6×1,991²/(8×199.1) ≈ 1,074,000 kN, or 537 MN per cable; maximum tension at the tower T = H·√(1+16n²) = 537×1.077 ≈ 578 MN. With 0.791 m² of wire per cable the dead-load stress is 578/0.791 ≈ 731 N/mm², a dead-load safety factor of about 2.41 on 1,760 N/mm² wire; if live load and temperature add 10% to tension the factor drops to about 2.19. With 1,570 N/mm² wire and the same area the dead-load factor would be only about 2.15, which is why the public account says two cables per side would have been needed. A 0.8 m span increase after the earthquake reduces sag by about 1.46 m in the inextensible estimate. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design calculations of the Akashi Kaikyo Bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"以數字深入明石海峽大橋：顫振裕度、高強度鋼絲、設置沉箱、地震後幾何修正與主纜乾燥空氣","focusEn":"Numbers behind Akashi Kaikyo: flutter margin, high-strength wire, laid-down caissons, post-quake geometry correction and dry-air cables"}},{"id":"b102","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure","v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction","v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"stages":[{"id":"b102-stage01","order":1,"steps":[{"id":"b102-v6-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"建立地層與路線剖面","titleEn":"Build a ground–alignment section","objective":"分開已觀測地層與推估延伸。","objectiveEn":"Separate observed strata from inferred continuity.","instruction":"自繪兩岸及海床，將白堊泥灰岩畫成有厚度的帶狀層。以實線代表假設鑽孔位置、虛線表示孔間推論，另標出可能含水或破碎區。","instructionEn":"Sketch both coasts and seabed with a chalk-marl band. Mark hypothetical boreholes with solid symbols and inferred continuity with dashed lines; add potentially wet or fractured zones.","observation":"觀察最短直線是否始終位於選定地層內。","observationEn":"Check whether the shortest straight alignment stays inside the selected layer.","failure":"把「主要穿越某地層」誤解成全線均質且不會滲水。","failureEn":"Treating a dominant stratum as proof of uniform, watertight conditions everywhere.","check":"剖面須有觀測／推論圖例及兩處需補充調查的位置。","checkEn":"Include an observation/inference key and two locations needing further investigation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-01-k1","title":"地層追蹤","titleEn":"Stratum following","text":"路線可以為了維持較合適地層而調整，不必是兩點最短連線。","textEn":"Alignment may follow favorable ground rather than the shortest line between two points."},{"id":"b102-v6-01-k2","title":"局部差異","titleEn":"Local variation","text":"斷層、褶皺和含水差異會使同名岩層的施工表現不同。","textEn":"Faults, folding and water conditions can change behavior within a named rock layer."}],"quiz":{"options":["標成推論並列出驗證需求","延用最近鑽孔結果當成全段實測","從剖面刪掉不確定區"],"optionsEn":["As an inference with a verification need","Treat the nearest borehole as measurement of the whole interval","Remove the uncertain area from the section"],"answer":0,"question":"鑽孔間出現未確認的構造，應如何標記？","questionEn":"How should an unconfirmed feature between boreholes be shown?","explanation":"地質模型應保留不確定性，讓後續觀察能修正它。","explanationEn":"A geological model should preserve uncertainty so subsequent observations can revise it."}},{"id":"b102-v6-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-01"],"title":"連結兩岸測量基準","titleEn":"Connect survey references on both shores","objective":"理解長距離對向掘進的基準一致性。","objectiveEn":"Understand reference consistency in long opposing drives.","instruction":"畫出地面控制網、井下傳遞點與隧道導線的關係。用自設兩岸座標示例，先核對單位、方向與高程基準，再比較預期會合位置。","instructionEn":"Diagram surface controls, underground transfer points and tunnel traverses. With invented coordinates from both shores, reconcile units, orientation and height datum before comparing predicted meeting positions.","observation":"比較共同偏移和兩側相向軸線不一致造成的不同結果。","observationEn":"Compare a common offset with disagreement between opposing drive axes.","failure":"未統一高程基準，就把兩側標高差當成施工誤差。","failureEn":"Treating height differences as construction error before reconciling datums.","check":"交付一張基準對照表及一個可重現的示例閉合檢查。","checkEn":"Submit a reference table and a reproducible example closure check.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-02-k1","title":"基準傳遞","titleEn":"Reference transfer","text":"地面控制需經過可追溯的傳遞才能用於地下方向判讀。","textEn":"Surface control must be transferred traceably before underground directions can be interpreted."},{"id":"b102-v6-02-k2","title":"誤差累積","titleEn":"Error accumulation","text":"長距離測量的小方向誤差可能累積成明顯位置差。","textEn":"Small directional errors over long distances can accumulate into substantial positional differences."}],"quiz":{"options":["立即修改襯砌環直徑","單位、基準面及控制點版本","只採用數字較小的一組"],"optionsEn":["Immediately change lining-ring diameter","Units, datum and control-point versions","Use whichever numbers are smaller"],"answer":1,"question":"兩隊高程數字不一致時，第一項核對是什麼？","questionEn":"Two teams report different elevations. What should be checked first?","explanation":"先確定數據在同一參考系，才能判斷幾何偏差。","explanationEn":"Data must share a reference system before geometric discrepancies are assessed."}},{"id":"b102-v6-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-02"],"title":"選擇開挖配置的證據","titleEn":"Identify evidence for excavation configuration","objective":"把機台功能與地層及地下水問題配對。","objectiveEn":"Match machine functions to ground and groundwater questions.","instruction":"建立硬度、裂隙、含水與出碴四列需求表，分別說明刀盤、工作面支承、密封與運輸的角色。比較英法兩側條件可能不同的理由，不填操作壓力。","instructionEn":"Create a table for strength, fractures, water and spoil handling; identify cutting, face support, sealing and transport roles. Explain why the two shores may need different configurations without specifying operating pressures.","observation":"觀察「能切削岩石」與「能管理水及出碴」是否是不同能力。","observationEn":"Distinguish ability to cut rock from ability to manage water and spoil.","failure":"只以隧道直徑挑選機台，忽略地層與水壓條件。","failureEn":"Selecting a machine by tunnel diameter alone while ignoring ground and water conditions.","check":"每項功能至少連到一項地質證據或待調查事項。","checkEn":"Link each function to geological evidence or an investigation need.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-03-k1","title":"適地配置","titleEn":"Ground-specific configuration","text":"同一工程可採用不同配置，以回應各段地層與地下水差異。","textEn":"One project may use different configurations to address sectional ground and groundwater differences."},{"id":"b102-v6-03-k2","title":"連續物流","titleEn":"Continuous logistics","text":"切削、出碴與環片供應互相制約；單一速度不能代表整體能力。","textEn":"Cutting, spoil removal and segment supply constrain one another; one speed does not represent total capability."}],"quiz":{"options":["直徑相同就必須使用相同配置","只需改變列車速度","工作面支承與密封需求仍可能不同"],"optionsEn":["Equal diameter requires identical configuration","Only train speed needs changing","Face-support and sealing requirements may still differ"],"answer":2,"question":"兩段隧道直徑相同但含水條件不同，哪個結論合理？","questionEn":"Two sections share a diameter but differ in water conditions. Which conclusion is reasonable?","explanation":"直徑只是幾何要求；地下水和地層決定另外的功能需求。","explanationEn":"Diameter defines geometry; ground and groundwater impose additional functional requirements."}},{"id":"b102-v6-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-03"],"title":"用開挖觀察修訂地質模型","titleEn":"Update the ground model from excavation observations","objective":"建立預測與現地觀察不一致時的判讀流程。","objectiveEn":"Define a response when predictions and field observations disagree.","instruction":"自行寫三則示例觀察：出碴性質改變、滲水增加、測量方向偏移。分別列出可能機制、需補查紀錄與模型要修訂的欄位。","instructionEn":"Invent three observations: changed spoil, increased ingress and a survey-direction shift. For each, list candidate mechanisms, records to check and model fields to revise.","observation":"注意相同表徵可以有地質、設備或量測等不同原因。","observationEn":"Recognize that the same symptom may have geological, equipment or measurement causes.","failure":"因原模型標示低透水，就把新增滲水當成量測錯誤刪除。","failureEn":"Discarding increased ingress as measurement error because the original model predicts low permeability.","check":"至少保留兩種競爭假說，並寫出可區分它們的證據。","checkEn":"Retain at least two competing explanations and evidence that could distinguish them.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-04-k1","title":"觀察回饋","titleEn":"Observational feedback","text":"地質預測應接受新證據檢驗；模型不是現地狀態的保證。","textEn":"Geological predictions must be tested against new evidence; a model does not guarantee field conditions."},{"id":"b102-v6-04-k2","title":"可區分證據","titleEn":"Discriminating evidence","text":"有用的補查應能讓不同假說產生不同預期結果。","textEn":"Useful follow-up evidence produces different expected results under competing explanations."}],"quiz":{"options":["保留原版本，加入新觀察並重新評估","只保留原先最有利的假設","把兩種現象平均成一個正常值"],"optionsEn":["Preserve the old version, add observations and reassess","Retain only the original favorable assumption","Average both symptoms into a normal value"],"answer":0,"question":"出碴變化與新滲水同時發生時，應如何處理模型？","questionEn":"Spoil changes and new water ingress occur together. How should the model be treated?","explanation":"版本化修訂保留決策依據，並讓新增證據改變推論。","explanationEn":"Versioned revision preserves decision context while allowing new evidence to change conclusions."}}],"title":"地質、測量與開挖","titleEn":"Geology, survey and excavation","description":"把預期地層、實際觀察與開挖配置建立可修訂的對照。","descriptionEn":"Build a revisable comparison between expected ground, observations and excavation configuration."},{"id":"b102-stage02","order":2,"steps":[{"id":"b102-v6-05","sequence":5,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-04"],"title":"檢查襯砌環與接縫","titleEn":"Review lining rings and joints","objective":"分清承載、防水與幾何接合證據。","objectiveEn":"Separate evidence for load support, water control and geometric fit.","instruction":"畫一圈分片襯砌及相鄰兩環，標記接縫、接觸面與可能漏水路徑。建立環片識別、位置、缺損和接縫觀察的記錄欄位。","instructionEn":"Draw a segmented ring and two adjacent rings, marking joints, contacts and potential ingress paths. Define records for segment identity, location, defects and joint observations.","observation":"比較環片本體完整與接縫完整是否能互相替代。","observationEn":"Ask whether sound segment bodies and sound joints provide interchangeable evidence.","failure":"環片外表沒有裂縫，就認定所有接縫都止水良好。","failureEn":"Assuming every joint is watertight because segment faces have no visible cracks.","check":"為承載、幾何、防水各列一種不同的檢核證據。","checkEn":"Name distinct evidence for support, geometry and water control.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-05-k1","title":"系統接縫","titleEn":"System joints","text":"襯砌不是孤立環片的集合；環內與環間接合會影響整體性能。","textEn":"Lining behavior depends on within-ring and between-ring joints, not only isolated segments."},{"id":"b102-v6-05-k2","title":"位置追溯","titleEn":"Location traceability","text":"缺陷紀錄須能回到具體環號與方位，才能比較後續變化。","textEn":"Defect records need ring identity and orientation to support later comparisons."}],"quiz":{"options":["全隧道環片總數","同環號、方位及時間的觀察序列","未註位置的零散照片"],"optionsEn":["Total number of tunnel segments","Observations with matching ring, orientation and timestamps","Unlocated photographs"],"answer":1,"question":"哪項記錄最適合追蹤接縫漏水是否擴大？","questionEn":"Which record best tracks whether joint leakage is spreading?","explanation":"可定位、可比較的紀錄才支持變化判斷。","explanationEn":"Located and comparable records support judgments about change."}},{"id":"b102-v6-06","sequence":6,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-05"],"title":"區分漏水來源與排水路徑","titleEn":"Distinguish ingress sources from drainage paths","objective":"解釋抽排能力不等於止水成功。","objectiveEn":"Explain why pumping capacity does not prove successful water exclusion.","instruction":"自繪接縫、集水溝、集水井和抽排出口，分別用箭頭表示外水進入與收集輸送。以示例時間表比較降雨、漏水位置及抽排量。","instructionEn":"Sketch joints, drains, sumps and discharge, using different arrows for water ingress and collection. Compare rainfall, leak locations and pumping in an invented timeline.","observation":"觀察集水量變化可能來自入流改變，也可能來自排水路徑堵塞。","observationEn":"Changes in collected flow may reflect altered inflow or blocked drainage routes.","failure":"抽水機仍運轉就推論沒有漏水，或流量下降就推論問題改善。","failureEn":"Inferring no ingress because pumps run, or improvement because measured flow falls.","check":"指出兩種使觀測流量下降的不同情境與辨別資料。","checkEn":"Identify two different causes of reduced measured flow and evidence distinguishing them.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-06-k1","title":"入流與輸送","titleEn":"Inflow versus conveyance","text":"滲入隧道的水與被量測到的排水，可能因蓄積或堵塞而不同。","textEn":"Ingress and measured drainage can differ because of storage or obstruction."},{"id":"b102-v6-06-k2","title":"水量平衡","titleEn":"Water balance","text":"在有明確時間範圍的模型中，入流、出流和蓄積須互相一致。","textEn":"In a time-bounded model, inflow, outflow and storage change must be consistent."}],"quiz":{"options":["只確認供電存在，便排除所有排水問題","直接宣告外水已減少","收集及輸送路徑是否受阻"],"optionsEn":["Confirm supply power and rule out all drainage problems","Immediately conclude external ingress has decreased","Whether collection or conveyance is obstructed"],"answer":2,"question":"排水量下降但局部積水升高，最應檢查什麼？","questionEn":"Drainage flow falls while local ponding rises. What most needs checking?","explanation":"流量與積水相反變化提示輸送問題，需核查路徑和量測。","explanationEn":"Opposing flow and ponding trends suggest a conveyance issue requiring route and measurement checks."}},{"id":"b102-v6-07","sequence":7,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-06"],"title":"辨認三條隧道的功能","titleEn":"Distinguish the three tunnel roles","objective":"將交通、維護與避難功能在圖中分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate traffic, maintenance and refuge functions on a diagram.","instruction":"自繪兩條行車隧道和中央服務隧道，再加入聯絡通道。用三種線型表示列車路線、維護通行與示意撤離方向，避免填入真實緊急操作命令。","instructionEn":"Sketch two running tunnels and a central service tunnel with cross-passages. Use distinct line styles for trains, maintenance and illustrative evacuation, without issuing real emergency instructions.","observation":"觀察聯絡通道與供列車換線的橫渡洞室是否是不同構造。","observationEn":"Distinguish pedestrian/service cross-passages from rail crossover caverns.","failure":"把服務隧道畫成第三條正常載客鐵路。","failureEn":"Drawing the service tunnel as a third regular passenger railway.","check":"圖例應能一眼分辨三種功能與兩種橫向連接。","checkEn":"The key must distinguish the three functions and the two types of lateral connection.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-07-k1","title":"功能隔離","titleEn":"Functional separation","text":"中央服務隧道提供維護與緊急支援，與行車隧道用途不同。","textEn":"The central service tunnel supports maintenance and emergencies rather than normal rail traffic."},{"id":"b102-v6-07-k2","title":"連接類型","titleEn":"Connection types","text":"聯絡通道服務人員移動；橫渡洞室則提供列車跨線能力。","textEn":"Cross-passages support movement of people; crossover caverns allow trains to change running tunnels."}],"quiz":{"options":["設有軌道的橫渡洞室","一般人行聯絡通道","服務隧道內的排水溝"],"optionsEn":["A rail crossover cavern","An ordinary pedestrian cross-passage","A service-tunnel drain"],"answer":0,"question":"需要列車從一條行車隧道移到另一條時，對應哪個構造？","questionEn":"Which structure allows a train to change from one running tunnel to the other?","explanation":"不同橫向連接有不同尺寸和用途，不能在系統圖上混用。","explanationEn":"Different lateral connections serve different functions and must not be conflated."}},{"id":"b102-v6-08","sequence":8,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-07"],"title":"讀懂服務隧道壓差概念","titleEn":"Interpret service-tunnel pressure differences","objective":"理解保護空間與門、通風的相互依賴。","objectiveEn":"Understand dependencies among protected space, doors and ventilation.","instruction":"以兩個箱體代表服務與行車隧道，畫出正常示意氣流和門開啟時的可能路徑。列出判斷氣流方向需要的資料，不自行設定火災排煙程序。","instructionEn":"Represent service and running tunnels as two boxes. Sketch intended airflow and possible paths when a door opens. List data needed to judge flow without defining fire-smoke operating procedures.","observation":"注意風機狀態、壓差與門的位置並非同一個訊號。","observationEn":"Fan status, pressure difference and door position are different signals.","failure":"只因風機顯示開啟，就認定保護空間一定維持壓差。","failureEn":"Assuming a protected space maintains pressure simply because a fan indicates running.","check":"列出至少三個互相核對的狀態或觀察量。","checkEn":"List at least three states or observations to cross-check.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-08-k1","title":"壓差屏障","titleEn":"Pressure barrier","text":"適當的壓差可引導氣流；實際效果仍受開口與系統狀態影響。","textEn":"Pressure differences can direct flow; openings and system state affect actual performance."},{"id":"b102-v6-08-k2","title":"功能驗證","titleEn":"Functional verification","text":"設備運转訊號只能證明部分狀態，不能代替完整功能證據。","textEn":"A running indication establishes only part of the state, not complete functional performance."}],"quiz":{"options":["忽略壓差，因馬達已運轉","核對開口、氣流及感測狀態","立即認定所有門都關妥"],"optionsEn":["Ignore pressure because motors are running","Check openings, airflow and sensor state","Assume all doors are properly closed"],"answer":1,"question":"風機開啟但保護區壓差不足，哪個判斷較合理？","questionEn":"Fans run but protected-zone pressure is insufficient. Which judgment is sound?","explanation":"保護功能依賴整體狀態，必須把設備與環境證據合看。","explanationEn":"Protection depends on system state, so equipment and environmental evidence must be combined."}}],"title":"襯砌與三隧道介面","titleEn":"Lining and three-bore interfaces","description":"追蹤環片接合、排水與聯絡通道在不同狀態的功能。","descriptionEn":"Trace segment joints, drainage and cross-passages under different system states."},{"id":"b102-stage03","order":3,"steps":[{"id":"b102-v6-09","sequence":9,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-08"],"title":"整理軌道與機電淨空","titleEn":"Coordinate track and service clearances","objective":"看出斷面配置中的安裝與維護衝突。","objectiveEn":"Identify installation and maintenance conflicts in a cross-section.","instruction":"在自繪圓形斷面放入列車包絡、步道、電車線、冷卻管與電纜。再畫一個設備維護所需空間，以虛線標記尚無尺寸資料的部分。","instructionEn":"Place a train envelope, walkway, catenary, cooling pipes and cables in a circular sketch. Add maintenance space and use dashed boundaries where dimensional evidence is missing.","observation":"比較「裝得下」與「仍可檢查、撤離和維護」是否不同。","observationEn":"Distinguish physical fit from retained inspection, egress and maintenance access.","failure":"只畫設備外形，忽略人員通行及拆換路徑。","failureEn":"Drawing equipment outlines without access or replacement paths.","check":"找出兩個潛在介面衝突並列明需向哪個專業取得資料。","checkEn":"Identify two potential conflicts and the disciplines that must provide missing data.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-09-k1","title":"包絡介面","titleEn":"Envelope interfaces","text":"設備配置須同時考慮車輛動態、結構和通行空間。","textEn":"Equipment layout must account for vehicle motion, structure and access together."},{"id":"b102-v6-09-k2","title":"維護空間","titleEn":"Maintenance space","text":"正常運轉不碰撞，不等於能安全拆換或檢查設備。","textEn":"Collision-free operation does not establish that equipment can be inspected or replaced safely."}],"quiz":{"options":["是，唯一條件是不碰列車","只要管線顏色不同即可","尚未，通行與維護需求仍未滿足"],"optionsEn":["Yes; avoiding the train is the only condition","Yes, if the pipe has a different color","No; access and maintenance requirements remain unresolved"],"answer":2,"question":"一條新管線不碰列車但占用步道，是否已完成介面檢核？","questionEn":"A new pipe avoids the train but occupies the walkway. Is interface review complete?","explanation":"斷面有多種功能包絡，不能只檢查車輛外形。","explanationEn":"The cross-section contains multiple functional envelopes, not only a train outline."}},{"id":"b102-v6-10","sequence":10,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-09"],"title":"檢查供電與服務依賴","titleEn":"Review power and service dependencies","objective":"說明冗餘電源不等於所有設備都無中斷。","objectiveEn":"Explain why redundant supplies do not prove uninterrupted service for every load.","instruction":"畫出兩岸電源、供電分段及列車、排水、照明三類負載。以紙上情境移除一個來源，標記哪些功能仍需切換與控制證據。","instructionEn":"Diagram power from both shores, supply sections and train, drainage and lighting loads. Remove one source in a paper scenario and mark functions requiring transfer and control evidence.","observation":"比較電源存在、路徑可用與末端設備運轉三種狀態。","observationEn":"Distinguish source availability, path availability and operation of the final device.","failure":"把圖上有兩個電源直接視為所有故障情況都有備援。","failureEn":"Treating two drawn power sources as proof of redundancy for every failure case.","check":"為一個負載畫出完整替代路徑，並列一個共同失效點的疑問。","checkEn":"Trace an alternative path to one load and identify a possible common failure point.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-10-k1","title":"端到端功能","titleEn":"End-to-end function","text":"備援需要從來源到負載的完整可用路徑。","textEn":"Redundancy requires a complete available path from source to load."},{"id":"b102-v6-10-k2","title":"共同依賴","titleEn":"Shared dependencies","text":"兩條供電路徑仍可能共用控制、保護或連接設備。","textEn":"Two supply paths may still share control, protection or connection equipment."}],"quiz":{"options":["替代來源到排水設備的整條路徑是否可用","只核對備援來源額定容量，不追蹤配電路徑","以其他負載正常推論排水設備必定可用"],"optionsEn":["Is the complete alternative path to drainage equipment available?","Check backup source rating without tracing distribution","Infer drainage availability because other loads work"],"answer":0,"question":"確認排水備援時，哪個問題最重要？","questionEn":"Which question matters most when verifying drainage backup?","explanation":"功能驗證必須追到負載，不能停在上游電源。","explanationEn":"Verification must reach the load rather than stop at the upstream source."}},{"id":"b102-v6-11","sequence":11,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-10"],"title":"組織維護占用與復歸證據","titleEn":"Organize maintenance possession and return evidence","objective":"辨認施工完成與恢復運行間的交接責任。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish completion of work from authorization to resume service.","instruction":"建立示意交接表，含區段、受影響設備、隔離狀態、檢查結果及未結案項。用「換線維護」桌上情境辨認交通與設備團隊的交界，不模擬真實控制指令。","instructionEn":"Build an illustrative handover sheet with section, affected equipment, isolation state, checks and open items. Use a crossover-maintenance tabletop scenario to identify team interfaces without simulating real control commands.","observation":"觀察工件安裝完成是否仍有功能測試與文件核對未完成。","observationEn":"Notice whether physical completion still leaves functional tests or document reconciliation pending.","failure":"以工時結束代替設備復歸與路線交接確認。","failureEn":"Treating the end of a work shift as confirmation of equipment restoration and route handover.","check":"將施工完成、測試完成與授權狀態分成獨立欄位。","checkEn":"Keep work completion, test completion and authorization state in separate fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-11-k1","title":"狀態交接","titleEn":"State handover","text":"跨班或跨專業交接應描述實際設備狀態及尚未解除的限制。","textEn":"Cross-shift or cross-discipline handover must describe actual equipment state and remaining restrictions."},{"id":"b102-v6-11-k2","title":"責任邊界","titleEn":"Responsibility boundaries","text":"驗證證據與運行授權由不同角色承擔時，介面必須清楚。","textEn":"Interfaces must be explicit when verification and operating authority belong to different roles."}],"quiz":{"options":["直接填寫已全面復歸","機械完成與功能未驗證分別列示","刪除測試欄以免混淆"],"optionsEn":["Mark fully restored","Record mechanical completion and unverified function separately","Remove the test field"],"answer":1,"question":"工件已裝回但功能測試未完成，交接表應如何表示？","questionEn":"A component is reinstalled but functional testing is incomplete. How should it be recorded?","explanation":"不同完成層次不能互相替代，否則會掩蓋未結案工作。","explanationEn":"Different completion levels are not interchangeable and must not hide unfinished work."}},{"id":"b102-v6-12","sequence":12,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-channel-infrastructure","v6-channel-tbm","v6-channel-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-11"],"title":"交付三隧道整合模型","titleEn":"Deliver the integrated three-bore model","objective":"將土建與機電證據連成可查核的系統。","objectiveEn":"Connect civil and service-system evidence into an auditable model.","instruction":"把地質、襯砌、漏水、通風和供電圖表整理成同一介面索引。選一個「供電中斷伴隨滲水」假想情境，指出需聯合查證的兩個系統與資料缺口。","instructionEn":"Index ground, lining, ingress, ventilation and power records together. For an invented power-loss-plus-ingress scenario, identify two systems requiring joint review and remaining evidence gaps.","observation":"檢查每個功能主張是否有可定位的圖表或紀錄支持。","observationEn":"Check that each functional claim has a located diagram or record behind it.","failure":"各專業圖表單獨完整，卻無法對齊區段名稱與狀態。","failureEn":"Individually complete discipline records cannot be reconciled by location or state.","check":"提交共享區段索引、假設清單與至少三項未解介面問題。","checkEn":"Submit a common section index, assumptions and at least three unresolved interface questions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v6-12-k1","title":"系統整合","titleEn":"Systems integration","text":"隧道能否服務取決於土建、設備、交通與維護的共同狀態。","textEn":"Tunnel service depends on combined civil, equipment, traffic and maintenance states."},{"id":"b102-v6-12-k2","title":"共同識別","titleEn":"Common identifiers","text":"一致的區段與設備識別可防止把不同位置的證據錯接。","textEn":"Consistent section and equipment identifiers prevent mismatching evidence from different locations."}],"quiz":{"options":["只核對總設備數量是否相同","只比較各自最後一次正常結果","區段、設備識別、時間及狀態"],"optionsEn":["Whether total equipment counts match","Compare only each system’s latest normal result","Section, equipment identity, time and state"],"answer":2,"question":"整合兩份排水與供電紀錄前，最先應核對什麼？","questionEn":"What should first be reconciled when integrating drainage and power records?","explanation":"共同識別與時間狀態使不同專業證據可以正確連結。","explanationEn":"Shared identifiers and time/state information allow evidence from different disciplines to be connected correctly."}}],"title":"機電整合與交付","titleEn":"Systems integration and handover","description":"以桌上情境檢查通風、供電、交通和維護的依賴。","descriptionEn":"Use tabletop scenarios to review dependencies among ventilation, power, traffic and maintenance."},{"id":"b102-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b102-v14-01","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v6-12"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法海底案例先區分海面水深與岩層測壓水頭，避免把海床幾何直接當襯砌各處水壓；服務通道排水也會影響局部梯度。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish seawater depth from rock piezometric head, including local gradients affected by service-gallery drainage rather than equating seabed geometry with pressure everywhere. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=34 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=34 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-01-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"英法海底案例先區分海面水深與岩層測壓水頭，避免把海床幾何直接當襯砌各處水壓；服務通道排水也會影響局部梯度。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Distinguish seawater depth from rock piezometric head, including local gradients affected by service-gallery drainage rather than equating seabed geometry with pressure everywhere. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","英法海底案例先區分海面水深與岩層測壓水頭，避免把海床幾何直接當襯砌各處水壓；服務通道排水也會影響局部梯度。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Distinguish seawater depth from rock piezometric head, including local gradients affected by service-gallery drainage rather than equating seabed geometry with pressure everywhere.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"英法海底案例先區分海面水深與岩層測壓水頭，避免把海床幾何直接當襯砌各處水壓；服務通道排水也會影響局部梯度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish seawater depth from rock piezometric head, including local gradients affected by service-gallery drainage rather than equating seabed geometry with pressure everywhere. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":13},{"id":"b102-v14-02","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=34 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為366.894 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=34 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 366.894 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=34 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為366.894 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=34 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 366.894 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=34 m。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=34 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=34 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=34 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=333.54 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":14},{"id":"b102-v14-03","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：潮汐反應滯後若當成儀器故障，會錯過含水層傳遞時間與排水邊界變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking tidal lag for sensor failure loses information about aquifer response time and drainage-boundary changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將主孔與服務孔測壓點用同一高程和潮位基準比較，檢查水頭相位差是否支持連通假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare bore and service-gallery piezometers on one elevation and tide datum, testing whether phase differences support hydraulic connectivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":15},{"id":"b102-v14-04","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"潮汐反應滯後若當成儀器故障，會錯過含水層傳遞時間與排水邊界變化。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking tidal lag for sensor failure loses information about aquifer response time and drainage-boundary changes. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"潮汐反應滯後若當成儀器故障，會錯過含水層傳遞時間與排水邊界變化。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Mistaking tidal lag for sensor failure loses information about aquifer response time and drainage-boundary changes. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","潮汐反應滯後若當成儀器故障，會錯過含水層傳遞時間與排水邊界變化。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mistaking tidal lag for sensor failure loses information about aquifer response time and drainage-boundary changes.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潮汐反應滯後若當成儀器故障，會錯過含水層傳遞時間與排水邊界變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking tidal lag for sensor failure loses information about aquifer response time and drainage-boundary changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":16},{"id":"b102-v14-05","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比較英法主孔及服務通道的襯砌尺度，幾何縮小雖改變膜應力量級，接頭轉角、局部荷載及維修開口仍須獨立評估。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare lining scales in running bores and service access; geometric scaling changes membrane stress but does not preserve joint rotations, local loads or maintenance-opening behaviour. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-05-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"比較英法主孔及服務通道的襯砌尺度，幾何縮小雖改變膜應力量級，接頭轉角、局部荷載及維修開口仍須獨立評估。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Compare lining scales in running bores and service access; geometric scaling changes membrane stress but does not preserve joint rotations, local loads or maintenance-opening behaviour. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","比較英法主孔及服務通道的襯砌尺度，幾何縮小雖改變膜應力量級，接頭轉角、局部荷載及維修開口仍須獨立評估。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Compare lining scales in running bores and service access."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較英法主孔及服務通道的襯砌尺度，幾何縮小雖改變膜應力量級，接頭轉角、局部荷載及維修開口仍須獨立評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare lining scales in running bores and service access; geometric scaling changes membrane stress but does not preserve joint rotations, local loads or maintenance-opening behaviour. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":17},{"id":"b102-v14-06","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.11771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.11771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.11771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.11771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":18},{"id":"b102-v14-07","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：把小孔的接縫性能按比例套到大孔，可能忽略更大的絕對張開和局部偏心。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scaling small-bore sealing performance to the larger bore can miss increased absolute opening and local eccentricity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分別建立兩種斷面的接頭模型，將同水頭下環向變形與開口附近局部應變對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Model both jointed sections separately and compare circumferential movement with local strains near openings under matched head. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":19},{"id":"b102-v14-08","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把小孔的接縫性能按比例套到大孔，可能忽略更大的絕對張開和局部偏心。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scaling small-bore sealing performance to the larger bore can miss increased absolute opening and local eccentricity. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把小孔的接縫性能按比例套到大孔，可能忽略更大的絕對張開和局部偏心。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Scaling small-bore sealing performance to the larger bore can miss increased absolute opening and local eccentricity. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","把小孔的接縫性能按比例套到大孔，可能忽略更大的絕對張開和局部偏心。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Scaling small-bore sealing performance to the larger bore can miss increased absolute opening and local eccentricity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把小孔的接縫性能按比例套到大孔，可能忽略更大的絕對張開和局部偏心。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scaling small-bore sealing performance to the larger bore can miss increased absolute opening and local eccentricity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":20}],"order":4},{"id":"b102-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b102-v14-09","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"服務通道與主孔間的連接令止水介面不只沿圓環分布，教學比較規則接縫和分岔部位的變形相容，不能只按平均寬度分類。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connections between service access and running bores create nonuniform interfaces; compare regular joints with branch movement compatibility rather than classifying seals by mean gap alone. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=3.4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=3.4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-09-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"服務通道與主孔間的連接令止水介面不只沿圓環分布，教學比較規則接縫和分岔部位的變形相容，不能只按平均寬度分類。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Connections between service access and running bores create nonuniform interfaces; compare regular joints with branch movement compatibility rather than classifying seals by mean gap alone. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["服務通道與主孔間的連接令止水介面不只沿圓環分布，教學比較規則接縫和分岔部位的變形相容，不能只按平均寬度分類。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Connections between service access and running bores create nonuniform interfaces.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"服務通道與主孔間的連接令止水介面不只沿圓環分布，教學比較規則接縫和分岔部位的變形相容，不能只按平均寬度分類。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connections between service access and running bores create nonuniform interfaces; compare regular joints with branch movement compatibility rather than classifying seals by mean gap alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":21},{"id":"b102-v14-10","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=3.4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.26 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=3.4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.26 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=3.4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.26 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=3.4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.26 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=3.4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=3.4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=3.4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=3.4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13.6 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":22},{"id":"b102-v14-11","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：不同方向錯台可能讓密封接觸區遷移，單一正向試驗合格不能證明反向循環後仍水密。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Opposite offsets can shift the sealing contact zone; passing one-direction tests does not prove tightness after reversed cycles. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在接縫轉角及分岔附近保存錯台方向，選全尺寸測試中真正對應的組合，而非只比水壓。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain offset direction at rotated and branched interfaces and select the matching full-size test combination, not pressure alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":23},{"id":"b102-v14-12","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同方向錯台可能讓密封接觸區遷移，單一正向試驗合格不能證明反向循環後仍水密。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Opposite offsets can shift the sealing contact zone; passing one-direction tests does not prove tightness after reversed cycles. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同方向錯台可能讓密封接觸區遷移，單一正向試驗合格不能證明反向循環後仍水密。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Opposite offsets can shift the sealing contact zone; passing one-direction tests does not prove tightness after reversed cycles. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["不同方向錯台可能讓密封接觸區遷移，單一正向試驗合格不能證明反向循環後仍水密。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Opposite offsets can shift the sealing contact zone; passing one-direction tests does not prove tightness after reversed cycles.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同方向錯台可能讓密封接觸區遷移，單一正向試驗合格不能證明反向循環後仍水密。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Opposite offsets can shift the sealing contact zone; passing one-direction tests does not prove tightness after reversed cycles. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":24},{"id":"b102-v14-13","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長海底隧道的維修物流需在列車服務與服務通道使用間協調，備料的距離和返回時間會影響實際工作窗口，不只看工具進入時間。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintenance logistics must fit railway service and service-access use; material distance and return time constrain the window beyond the time needed to bring tools inside. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=21 t；往返週期=33 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=21 t; cycle=33 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-13-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"長海底隧道的維修物流需在列車服務與服務通道使用間協調，備料的距離和返回時間會影響實際工作窗口，不只看工具進入時間。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Maintenance logistics must fit railway service and service-access use; material distance and return time constrain the window beyond the time needed to bring tools inside. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","長海底隧道的維修物流需在列車服務與服務通道使用間協調，備料的距離和返回時間會影響實際工作窗口，不只看工具進入時間。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Maintenance logistics must fit railway service and service-access use.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長海底隧道的維修物流需在列車服務與服務通道使用間協調，備料的距離和返回時間會影響實際工作窗口，不只看工具進入時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintenance logistics must fit railway service and service-access use; material distance and return time constrain the window beyond the time needed to bring tools inside. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":25},{"id":"b102-v14-14","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=21 t；往返週期=33 min。C=N payload 60/T=152.727 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為138.843 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=21 t; cycle=33 min. C=N payload 60/T=152.727 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 138.843 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=21 t；往返週期=33 min。C=N payload 60/T=152.727 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為138.843 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=21 t; cycle=33 min. C=N payload 60/T=152.727 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 138.843 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=21 t；往返週期=33 min。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=21 t; cycle=33 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=21 t；往返週期=33 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=21 t; cycle=33 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":26},{"id":"b102-v14-15","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：只安排作業時間而不留撤出驗證，會把未清空的工作面錯報成可恢復列車服務。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scheduling work without verified withdrawal time can incorrectly report an occupied worksite as ready for railway service. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用工單時間戳分開進入、作業、清點及撤出，核對共用路線是否在同一窗口被另一任務占用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate access, work, inventory checks and withdrawal in work-order timestamps and identify overlapping use of shared routes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":27},{"id":"b102-v14-16","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只安排作業時間而不留撤出驗證，會把未清空的工作面錯報成可恢復列車服務。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scheduling work without verified withdrawal time can incorrectly report an occupied worksite as ready for railway service. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只安排作業時間而不留撤出驗證，會把未清空的工作面錯報成可恢復列車服務。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Scheduling work without verified withdrawal time can incorrectly report an occupied worksite as ready for railway service. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只安排作業時間而不留撤出驗證，會把未清空的工作面錯報成可恢復列車服務。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Scheduling work without verified withdrawal time can incorrectly report an occupied worksite as ready for railway service.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只安排作業時間而不留撤出驗證，會把未清空的工作面錯報成可恢復列車服務。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scheduling work without verified withdrawal time can incorrectly report an occupied worksite as ready for railway service. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":28}],"order":5},{"id":"b102-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」與「列車壓力波與動壓量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" and \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b102-v14-17","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「通風顯熱量」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ventilation sensible heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法列車與設備熱源會隨服務密度改變，分析正常高峰和一條冷卻路徑維修時的空氣及水側熱帳，避免把裝置容量直接視為可移除熱量。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通風顯熱量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Traffic-dependent heat must be reconciled across air and water during peaks and cooling-path maintenance rather than equating installed capacity with removable heat. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise. Equal volumetric flow at different density does not provide equal cooling. Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ventilation sensible heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=82 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=12 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=82 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=12 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通風顯熱量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ventilation sensible heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-17-k1","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal","text":"英法列車與設備熱源會隨服務密度改變，分析正常高峰和一條冷卻路徑維修時的空氣及水側熱帳，避免把裝置容量直接視為可移除熱量。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。","textEn":"Traffic-dependent heat must be reconciled across air and water during peaks and cooling-path maintenance rather than equating installed capacity with removable heat. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" is correct?","options":["只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","英法列車與設備熱源會隨服務密度改變，分析正常高峰和一條冷卻路徑維修時的空氣及水側熱帳，避免把裝置容量直接視為可移除熱量。"],"optionsEn":["Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Traffic-dependent heat must be reconciled across air and water during peaks and cooling-path maintenance rather than equating installed capacity with removable heat."],"answer":2,"explanation":"英法列車與設備熱源會隨服務密度改變，分析正常高峰和一條冷卻路徑維修時的空氣及水側熱帳，避免把裝置容量直接視為可移除熱量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Traffic-dependent heat must be reconciled across air and water during peaks and cooling-path maintenance rather than equating installed capacity with removable heat. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":29},{"id":"b102-v14-18","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通風顯熱量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ventilation sensible heat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=82 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=12 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1186.7 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1305.37 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=82 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=12 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1186.7 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1305.37 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=82 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=12 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1186.7 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1305.37 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=82 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=12 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1186.7 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1305.37 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=82 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=12 K。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=82 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=12 K.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=82 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=12 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=82 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=12 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":30},{"id":"b102-v14-19","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通風顯熱量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ventilation sensible heat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","failure":"注意干擾：平均日溫度正常可能遮住列車連續通過的局部熱峰，需保留時間解析度再判斷冷卻不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A normal daily mean can conceal local peaks during successive train passages; retain time resolution before judging cooling adequacy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配對列車通過時段、設備功率、進出口溫差和流量，檢查熱量殘差是否集中在服務高峰。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair train passages, equipment power, temperature rise and flow, checking whether energy residuals cluster during peak service. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":31},{"id":"b102-v14-20","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通風顯熱量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ventilation sensible heat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均日溫度正常可能遮住列車連續通過的局部熱峰，需保留時間解析度再判斷冷卻不足。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A normal daily mean can conceal local peaks during successive train passages; retain time resolution before judging cooling adequacy. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均日溫度正常可能遮住列車連續通過的局部熱峰，需保留時間解析度再判斷冷卻不足。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。","textEn":"A normal daily mean can conceal local peaks during successive train passages; retain time resolution before judging cooling adequacy. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","平均日溫度正常可能遮住列車連續通過的局部熱峰，需保留時間解析度再判斷冷卻不足。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","A normal daily mean can conceal local peaks during successive train passages; retain time resolution before judging cooling adequacy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均日溫度正常可能遮住列車連續通過的局部熱峰，需保留時間解析度再判斷冷卻不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A normal daily mean can conceal local peaks during successive train passages; retain time resolution before judging cooling adequacy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":32},{"id":"b102-v14-21","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法主孔的列車種類與速度不同，阻塞比和交會情境應分案；服務通道門位又會改變壓力反射邊界，不能用單一動壓替代波動歷程。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different train types, speeds and encounter cases change blockage and wave behaviour; service-access door states also alter reflections beyond a single dynamic-pressure estimate. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-21-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"英法主孔的列車種類與速度不同，阻塞比和交會情境應分案；服務通道門位又會改變壓力反射邊界，不能用單一動壓替代波動歷程。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Different train types, speeds and encounter cases change blockage and wave behaviour; service-access door states also alter reflections beyond a single dynamic-pressure estimate. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["英法主孔的列車種類與速度不同，阻塞比和交會情境應分案；服務通道門位又會改變壓力反射邊界，不能用單一動壓替代波動歷程。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Different train types, speeds and encounter cases change blockage and wave behaviour.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"英法主孔的列車種類與速度不同，阻塞比和交會情境應分案；服務通道門位又會改變壓力反射邊界，不能用單一動壓替代波動歷程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different train types, speeds and encounter cases change blockage and wave behaviour; service-access door states also alter reflections beyond a single dynamic-pressure estimate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":33},{"id":"b102-v14-22","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1220.41 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1220.41 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1220.41 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1220.41 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":34},{"id":"b102-v14-23","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：只存最大壓力不存升壓時間，可能漏掉設備密封與乘客感受所受的快速變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Saving only peak pressure loses rapid changes relevant to seals and passenger comfort. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在列車通過前後同步量測門兩側壓力，將列車編組與門位一起保存，檢查反射峰抵達時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise pressure across doors before and after passage, retaining formation and door state to check reflected-wave arrival. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":35},{"id":"b102-v14-24","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只存最大壓力不存升壓時間，可能漏掉設備密封與乘客感受所受的快速變化。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Saving only peak pressure loses rapid changes relevant to seals and passenger comfort. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只存最大壓力不存升壓時間，可能漏掉設備密封與乘客感受所受的快速變化。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"Saving only peak pressure loses rapid changes relevant to seals and passenger comfort. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只存最大壓力不存升壓時間，可能漏掉設備密封與乘客感受所受的快速變化。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Saving only peak pressure loses rapid changes relevant to seals and passenger comfort.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只存最大壓力不存升壓時間，可能漏掉設備密封與乘客感受所受的快速變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Saving only peak pressure loses rapid changes relevant to seals and passenger comfort. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":36}],"order":6},{"id":"b102-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b102-v14-25","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法服務通道提供不同於運行孔的接收空間，疏散模型需確認到達之後的人流容量與可用狀態，不能在越過第一道門時就結束計時。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Service access provides a receiving space distinct from the running bore; evacuation modelling must include capacity and availability after the first doorway, not stop its clock there. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=82 s；行走距離=320 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=82 s; travel distance=320 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-25-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"英法服務通道提供不同於運行孔的接收空間，疏散模型需確認到達之後的人流容量與可用狀態，不能在越過第一道門時就結束計時。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Service access provides a receiving space distinct from the running bore; evacuation modelling must include capacity and availability after the first doorway, not stop its clock there. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","英法服務通道提供不同於運行孔的接收空間，疏散模型需確認到達之後的人流容量與可用狀態，不能在越過第一道門時就結束計時。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Service access provides a receiving space distinct from the running bore.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"英法服務通道提供不同於運行孔的接收空間，疏散模型需確認到達之後的人流容量與可用狀態，不能在越過第一道門時就結束計時。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Service access provides a receiving space distinct from the running bore; evacuation modelling must include capacity and availability after the first doorway, not stop its clock there. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":37},{"id":"b102-v14-26","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=82 s；行走距離=320 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=482 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為522 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=82 s; travel distance=320 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=482 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 522 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=82 s；行走距離=320 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=482 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為522 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=82 s; travel distance=320 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=482 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 522 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：前置時間=82 s；行走距離=320 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=82 s; travel distance=320 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=82 s；行走距離=320 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=82 s; travel distance=320 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":38},{"id":"b102-v14-27","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：通道本身可用但接收區壅塞時，隊列會回堵主孔，使用單一平均步速會低估所需時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Congestion in an otherwise accessible receiving zone can queue people back into the running bore and defeat an average-speed estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"演練或模擬分開通過橫通道門與後續移動時間，核對接收區人數及通訊延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate doorway crossing from onward movement in drills or models, checking receiving-zone occupancy and communication delays. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":39},{"id":"b102-v14-28","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"通道本身可用但接收區壅塞時，隊列會回堵主孔，使用單一平均步速會低估所需時間。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Congestion in an otherwise accessible receiving zone can queue people back into the running bore and defeat an average-speed estimate. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"通道本身可用但接收區壅塞時，隊列會回堵主孔，使用單一平均步速會低估所需時間。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Congestion in an otherwise accessible receiving zone can queue people back into the running bore and defeat an average-speed estimate. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","通道本身可用但接收區壅塞時，隊列會回堵主孔，使用單一平均步速會低估所需時間。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Congestion in an otherwise accessible receiving zone can queue people back into the running bore and defeat an average-speed estimate.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通道本身可用但接收區壅塞時，隊列會回堵主孔，使用單一平均步速會低估所需時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Congestion in an otherwise accessible receiving zone can queue people back into the running bore and defeat an average-speed estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":40},{"id":"b102-v14-29","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「剩餘集水容積」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remaining sump volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海底排水的可靠性需連結低點集水、供電與維修隔離，假想兩台泵中一台退出時，分析淨入流與警報延遲而不把原容量沿用。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘集水容積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Link low-point sumps, power and maintenance isolation; when one hypothetical pump is unavailable, recalculate net inflow and alarm delay rather than retaining the original capacity. A sump offers finite buffering after pumps stop, with usable volume reduced by initial water, sediment and dead spaces. Buffer time depends on net inflow rather than pump nameplate capacity. Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Remaining sump volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=320 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=320 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘集水容積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Remaining sump volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-29-k1","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume","text":"海底排水的可靠性需連結低點集水、供電與維修隔離，假想兩台泵中一台退出時，分析淨入流與警報延遲而不把原容量沿用。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。","textEn":"Link low-point sumps, power and maintenance isolation; when one hypothetical pump is unavailable, recalculate net inflow and alarm delay rather than retaining the original capacity. A sump offers finite buffering after pumps stop, with usable volume reduced by initial water, sediment and dead spaces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" is correct?","options":["集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","海底排水的可靠性需連結低點集水、供電與維修隔離，假想兩台泵中一台退出時，分析淨入流與警報延遲而不把原容量沿用。"],"optionsEn":["Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Link low-point sumps, power and maintenance isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海底排水的可靠性需連結低點集水、供電與維修隔離，假想兩台泵中一台退出時，分析淨入流與警報延遲而不把原容量沿用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Link low-point sumps, power and maintenance isolation; when one hypothetical pump is unavailable, recalculate net inflow and alarm delay rather than retaining the original capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":41},{"id":"b102-v14-30","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：定量估算","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘集水容積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remaining sump volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=320 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為25.5183 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=320 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 25.5183 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=320 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為25.5183 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=320 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 25.5183 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=320 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=320 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=320 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=320 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=28.0702 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":42},{"id":"b102-v14-31","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘集水容積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remaining sump volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","failure":"注意干擾：名義備泵若共用堵塞出口，切換成功但水位仍升；應查管路而非反覆切換泵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A spare sharing a blocked outlet can transfer successfully while water keeps rising; diagnose the route instead of repeatedly switching pumps. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將水位上升曲線與當時泵啟停、閥位及出水流量同步，區分閥路阻塞和機械輸出不足。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise level rise with pump state, valves and discharge, distinguishing blocked routing from deficient mechanical output. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":43},{"id":"b102-v14-32","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘集水容積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remaining sump volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"名義備泵若共用堵塞出口，切換成功但水位仍升；應查管路而非反覆切換泵。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A spare sharing a blocked outlet can transfer successfully while water keeps rising; diagnose the route instead of repeatedly switching pumps. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"名義備泵若共用堵塞出口，切換成功但水位仍升；應查管路而非反覆切換泵。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。","textEn":"A spare sharing a blocked outlet can transfer successfully while water keeps rising; diagnose the route instead of repeatedly switching pumps. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","名義備泵若共用堵塞出口，切換成功但水位仍升；應查管路而非反覆切換泵。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","A spare sharing a blocked outlet can transfer successfully while water keeps rising; diagnose the route instead of repeatedly switching pumps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"名義備泵若共用堵塞出口，切換成功但水位仍升；應查管路而非反覆切換泵。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A spare sharing a blocked outlet can transfer successfully while water keeps rising; diagnose the route instead of repeatedly switching pumps. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":44}],"order":7},{"id":"b102-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b102-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法跨境服務把電力、控制、冷卻與維修責任放在多個介面，設備重複不能消除共用軟體或配電故障，需以功能可用性定義頂事件。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border service couples power, controls, cooling and maintenance responsibilities; duplicated equipment does not eliminate shared software or distribution faults, so define top events by lost function. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.011 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.011 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"英法跨境服務把電力、控制、冷卻與維修責任放在多個介面，設備重複不能消除共用軟體或配電故障，需以功能可用性定義頂事件。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Cross-border service couples power, controls, cooling and maintenance responsibilities; duplicated equipment does not eliminate shared software or distribution faults, so define top events by lost function. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["英法跨境服務把電力、控制、冷卻與維修責任放在多個介面，設備重複不能消除共用軟體或配電故障，需以功能可用性定義頂事件。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-border service couples power, controls, cooling and maintenance responsibilities.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"英法跨境服務把電力、控制、冷卻與維修責任放在多個介面，設備重複不能消除共用軟體或配電故障，需以功能可用性定義頂事件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border service couples power, controls, cooling and maintenance responsibilities; duplicated equipment does not eliminate shared software or distribution faults, so define top events by lost function. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":45},{"id":"b102-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.011 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000121 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00014641 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.011 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000121 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00014641 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.011 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000121 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00014641 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.011 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000121 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00014641 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.011 無因次。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.011 dimensionless.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.011 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.011 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":46},{"id":"b102-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：把同一次共同電源故障拆成兩個獨立事件會嚴重低估並聯不可用率，且掩蓋責任介面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Splitting one common-supply fault into independent events understates parallel unavailability and hides interface responsibility. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從一項失去服務的事件反向追到共用電源和控制版本，再比對維修時設備是否真的獨立。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace one loss-of-service event back to common supply and control revisions and test independence during maintenance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":47},{"id":"b102-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把同一次共同電源故障拆成兩個獨立事件會嚴重低估並聯不可用率，且掩蓋責任介面。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Splitting one common-supply fault into independent events understates parallel unavailability and hides interface responsibility. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把同一次共同電源故障拆成兩個獨立事件會嚴重低估並聯不可用率，且掩蓋責任介面。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Splitting one common-supply fault into independent events understates parallel unavailability and hides interface responsibility. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把同一次共同電源故障拆成兩個獨立事件會嚴重低估並聯不可用率，且掩蓋責任介面。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Splitting one common-supply fault into independent events understates parallel unavailability and hides interface responsibility.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把同一次共同電源故障拆成兩個獨立事件會嚴重低估並聯不可用率，且掩蓋責任介面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Splitting one common-supply fault into independent events understates parallel unavailability and hides interface responsibility. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":48},{"id":"b102-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響英法海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Channel Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"英法長期營運需要把更新設備與原設施共同管理，資料交接必須保留新舊版本適用里程及日期，不能讓歷史趨勢因供應商更換而中斷。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Long-term renewal requires old and new systems to coexist in records, with chainage and dates defining each revision rather than losing historical trends when suppliers change. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=101 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=101 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"英法長期營運需要把更新設備與原設施共同管理，資料交接必須保留新舊版本適用里程及日期，不能讓歷史趨勢因供應商更換而中斷。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Long-term renewal requires old and new systems to coexist in records, with chainage and dates defining each revision rather than losing historical trends when suppliers change. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","英法長期營運需要把更新設備與原設施共同管理，資料交接必須保留新舊版本適用里程及日期，不能讓歷史趨勢因供應商更換而中斷。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Long-term renewal requires old and new systems to coexist in records, with chainage and dates defining each revision rather than losing historical trends when suppliers change.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"英法長期營運需要把更新設備與原設施共同管理，資料交接必須保留新舊版本適用里程及日期，不能讓歷史趨勢因供應商更換而中斷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Long-term renewal requires old and new systems to coexist in records, with chainage and dates defining each revision rather than losing historical trends when suppliers change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":49},{"id":"b102-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=101 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.5743 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=101 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.5743 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=101 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.5743 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=101 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.5743 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","原創教學假設：設備總數=101 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=101 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=101 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=101 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.1584 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":50},{"id":"b102-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Channel Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：設備ID重用但未保留更換日期，會把新感測器的偏移解讀成隧道結構突然改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reusing an asset ID without replacement dates can turn a new-sensor offset into a false sudden structural change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Channel Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查更換過的感測器，從現行標籤追到舊型號校正與工單，驗證量程和零點是否可比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample a replaced sensor from its current tag back to previous calibration and work orders, checking range and zero comparability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":51},{"id":"b102-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b102-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"設備ID重用但未保留更換日期，會把新感測器的偏移解讀成隧道結構突然改變。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reusing an asset ID without replacement dates can turn a new-sensor offset into a false sudden structural change. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b102-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"設備ID重用但未保留更換日期，會把新感測器的偏移解讀成隧道結構突然改變。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Reusing an asset ID without replacement dates can turn a new-sensor offset into a false sudden structural change. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b102-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b102","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","設備ID重用但未保留更換日期，會把新感測器的偏移解讀成隧道結構突然改變。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Reusing an asset ID without replacement dates can turn a new-sensor offset into a false sudden structural change.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備ID重用但未保留更換日期，會把新感測器的偏移解讀成隧道結構突然改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reusing an asset ID without replacement dates can turn a new-sensor offset into a false sudden structural change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":52}],"order":8}],"title":"英法海底隧道","titleEn":"Channel Tunnel","summary":"從白堊泥灰岩選線到三隧道營運系統，練習地質推論、支承、防水與機電整合。","summaryEn":"Study geological inference, support, water control and systems integration from chalk-marl alignment to three-bore operation.","scope":"以公開資料建立的原創教學分解；所有步驟為紙上、數位模型與證據判讀練習。自繪的示意與自設資料必須標示假設；本站未提供現地工程資料，亦不是核准施工、設備操作或水質放行程序。","scopeEn":"Original educational decomposition of public information. Every step is a paper, digital-model or evidence-interpretation exercise. Label assumptions in self-drawn diagrams and invented data; this site does not supply field engineering records or approved construction, operating or water-release procedures.","diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["地層","開挖與襯砌","聯絡通道","機電","監測"],"labelsEn":["Ground","Excavation and lining","Cross-passages","Services","Monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":52,"estimatedMinutes":1240,"curriculumVersion":6,"enrichmentVersion":14,"learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","v14Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["入口壓力擾動","Portal pressure disturbance"],["剩餘集水容積","Remaining sump volume"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]]},"v14Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「環向受力與接縫柔度」，再獨立計算「列車壓力波與動壓量級」。原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.32 MPa；半徑=3.1 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.11771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=41 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1220.41 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate ring force and joint flexibility, then independently calculate train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale. Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.32 MPa; radius=3.1 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=2.83429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.11771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=41 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1008.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1220.41 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"主孔服務孔介面、壓力波與長期可維護性","focusEn":"Running-bore and service-gallery interfaces, pressure waves and maintainability"}},{"id":"b202","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-spillways","v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"stages":[{"id":"b202-stage01","order":1,"steps":[{"id":"b202-v6-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-spillways"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分開水庫、壩體與洩流路徑","titleEn":"Separate reservoir, dam and release paths","objective":"分辨擋水、蓄水、發電和溢洪功能。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish retention, storage, generation and spillway functions.","instruction":"自繪水庫、壩體、進水塔、壓力管、電廠及兩側溢洪路徑。以不同線型追蹤發電水路與溢洪水路到下游，標出它們與壩體的介面。","instructionEn":"Sketch reservoir, dam, intake towers, penstocks, powerhouse and side spillways. Trace generation and spillway routes to downstream using distinct line styles and mark dam interfaces.","observation":"確認溢洪水路並非越過壩頂流向電廠。","observationEn":"Confirm that the spillway route does not pass over the dam crest onto the powerhouse.","failure":"將所有放流水都畫成穿過水輪機，忽略獨立洩流功能。","failureEn":"Drawing all released water through turbines and overlooking separate release functions.","check":"圖中須有兩條可獨立追蹤的水路及各自功能。","checkEn":"Show two independently traceable water routes and their functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-01-k1","title":"功能分流","titleEn":"Functional separation","text":"蓄水結構與不同出流路徑共同構成水庫系統。","textEn":"The retaining structure and different outlet routes jointly form the reservoir system."},{"id":"b202-v6-01-k2","title":"介面辨識","titleEn":"Interface identification","text":"進水、管路、發電與下游水流的交界需要清楚定義。","textEn":"Interfaces among intakes, conduits, generation and downstream flow need clear definitions."}],"quiz":{"options":["溢洪道","水輪機壓力管，所有溢洪都必須經過它","壩頂道路，作為預定水流越頂路徑"],"optionsEn":["Spillway","Turbine penstocks, which all spill flow must use","The crest road as the intended overtopping route"],"answer":0,"question":"哪個構造最直接提供與發電水路分開的高水位洩流途徑？","questionEn":"Which structure most directly provides a high-water release path separate from generation?","explanation":"溢洪系統有獨立的水流路徑，不能以水輪機水路代替。","explanationEn":"The spillway has its own hydraulic path and cannot be represented by the turbine route."}},{"id":"b202-v6-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-01"],"title":"追蹤拱壩與重力作用","titleEn":"Trace arch and gravity action","objective":"解釋壩體、基底與兩岸岩體如何共同受力。","objectiveEn":"Explain joint load transfer through dam body, base and canyon rock.","instruction":"畫平面與剖面兩張示意：平面標水壓與向兩岸傳力，剖面標自重、基底及水壓。註明這是厚拱壩的定性模型，不能用箭頭直接判定安全。","instructionEn":"Draw plan and section: show pressure and transfer toward abutments in plan, then weight, base and water pressure in section. Label this a qualitative thick-arch model, not a safety calculation.","observation":"觀察只畫剖面是否會遺漏兩岸岩體的作用。","observationEn":"Notice what abutment action is lost when only a section is drawn.","failure":"將壩的全部抵抗能力只歸因於重量或只歸因於拱形。","failureEn":"Attributing all resistance solely to weight or solely to curvature.","check":"兩張圖應共同包含水、壩體、基底和兩岸的力路徑。","checkEn":"Together, the sketches must include water, dam, base and abutment force paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-02-k1","title":"三維受力","titleEn":"Three-dimensional behavior","text":"厚拱壩的行為需同時考慮壩體與岩體支承，單一剖面不完整。","textEn":"A thick arch dam requires consideration of dam and rock support; one section is incomplete."},{"id":"b202-v6-02-k2","title":"邊界可靠性","titleEn":"Boundary reliability","text":"理想模型假設的支承能力需要地質與變形證據支持。","textEn":"Support capacity assumed in an ideal model needs geological and deformation evidence."}],"quiz":{"options":["兩岸只限制滲水，不參與傳力","拱作用把部分荷載傳入兩岸","拱形會使地基完全不受力"],"optionsEn":["Abutments only limit seepage and carry no structural load","Arch action transfers part of the load into the abutments","Curvature makes the foundation entirely unloaded"],"answer":1,"question":"兩岸岩體的條件為何影響拱作用判讀？","questionEn":"Why do abutment-rock conditions matter for arch action?","explanation":"受力路徑需要能承接反力的岩體邊界。","explanationEn":"The load path needs rock boundaries capable of providing reactions."}},{"id":"b202-v6-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-02"],"title":"重建導流與乾地作業依賴","titleEn":"Reconstruct diversion dependencies","objective":"理解臨時導流如何提供永久工程的作業條件。","objectiveEn":"Understand how temporary diversion enables permanent works.","instruction":"依歷史資料畫出原河道、導流隧道與壩基作業區。用三格示意比較導流前、導流中和永久水路形成後，記錄每格水流去向。","instructionEn":"From historical accounts, sketch the river, diversion tunnels and foundation work area. Compare pre-diversion, diversion and permanent-waterway states, recording the flow destination in each.","observation":"檢查某一格是否意外把所有流路同時關閉。","observationEn":"Check whether a state inadvertently closes every flow route.","failure":"把圍堰視為不受來水影響的永久邊界，省略施工期洪水疑問。","failureEn":"Treating cofferdams as permanent, flow-independent boundaries and omitting construction-flood questions.","check":"每一格都保留連續水路及尚待專業分析的施工期風險。","checkEn":"Preserve a continuous water route and a construction-risk question in each state.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-03-k1","title":"臨時工程","titleEn":"Temporary works","text":"臨時設施的功能與失效會直接影響永久工程的施工條件。","textEn":"Temporary-work functions and failures directly affect conditions for permanent construction."},{"id":"b202-v6-03-k2","title":"狀態轉換","titleEn":"State transitions","text":"由導流到蓄水是系統邊界的變更，需要另行驗證。","textEn":"Transition from diversion to impoundment changes system boundaries and needs separate verification."}],"quiz":{"options":["尚未列出最後一台發電機的安裝日期","沒有先列出永久工程總材料量","某階段沒有說明來水可往何處流"],"optionsEn":["The last generator’s installation date is not yet given","Permanent-work material totals are not listed first","A stage gives no destination for incoming water"],"answer":2,"question":"在導流轉換圖中最嚴重的缺漏是什麼？","questionEn":"What is the most significant omission in a diversion-transition diagram?","explanation":"轉換階段仍須追蹤水流，不能因圖是中間狀態就忽略。","explanationEn":"Flow must remain accounted for even during an intermediate state."}},{"id":"b202-v6-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-03"],"title":"整理壩基與裂隙證據","titleEn":"Organize foundation and discontinuity evidence","objective":"分開岩石材料、接觸面與滲流路徑問題。","objectiveEn":"Separate rock-material, contact and seepage-path questions.","instruction":"在假想基岩剖面標記裂隙、壩基接觸面、排水與觀測位置。建立「材料強度」「接面狀態」「水壓」三欄，為每欄列出不同證據。","instructionEn":"On an invented rock section, mark discontinuities, dam contact, drains and observations. Create separate material-strength, contact-condition and water-pressure columns with distinct evidence needs.","observation":"注意堅硬岩石仍可能包含需要調查的裂隙與水路。","observationEn":"Recognize that strong rock may still contain discontinuities and water paths needing investigation.","failure":"只用岩石名稱或表面硬度，就認定壩基介面完整。","failureEn":"Declaring the foundation interface sound from rock name or surface hardness alone.","check":"三欄均須有觀察量與至少一項無法單獨推論的結論。","checkEn":"Give an observable and a conclusion it cannot establish alone in each column.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-04-k1","title":"岩體與岩塊","titleEn":"Rock mass versus intact rock","text":"岩塊性質不能完整代表含裂隙岩體的行為。","textEn":"Intact-rock properties do not fully describe a fractured rock mass."},{"id":"b202-v6-04-k2","title":"水壓與接觸","titleEn":"Water pressure and contact","text":"滲流條件會影響接觸面的有效受力，需與結構資料一起判讀。","textEn":"Seepage conditions affect effective contact loading and must be interpreted with structural evidence."}],"quiz":{"options":["該試體在試驗條件下的材料表現","整個壩基所有裂隙均不透水","任何水位下都不需監測"],"optionsEn":["Material behavior of that specimen under test conditions","Every foundation discontinuity is watertight","Monitoring is unnecessary at any reservoir level"],"answer":0,"question":"完整岩心強度良好，可直接證明什麼？","questionEn":"Good intact-core strength directly establishes what?","explanation":"試體證據有取樣與尺度範圍，不能無條件推廣到整個岩體。","explanationEn":"Specimen evidence has sampling and scale limits and cannot automatically represent the whole rock mass."}}],"title":"河谷與施工邊界","titleEn":"Canyon and construction boundaries","description":"分清永久工程的受力、水路與臨時導流。","descriptionEn":"Distinguish permanent load paths, water routes and temporary diversion."},{"id":"b202-stage02","order":2,"steps":[{"id":"b202-v6-05","sequence":5,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-04"],"title":"閱讀分塊澆置的介面","titleEn":"Read block-construction interfaces","objective":"辨認分塊施工與最終整體作用的差別。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish block construction from final integrated behavior.","instruction":"把壩體畫成少量教學用方塊，標記不同完成高度與接縫。比較「單塊已有強度」和「相鄰區塊已形成設計傳力」兩種判斷所需的證據。","instructionEn":"Draw a few educational dam blocks with unequal completion heights and joints. Compare evidence for one block gaining strength with evidence for intended transfer between adjacent blocks.","observation":"觀察接縫狀態改變時，整體模型的連續性假設也需變更。","observationEn":"Notice how joint-state changes alter assumptions about structural continuity.","failure":"因所有塊體都已澆完，就視為接縫與整體作用自動完成。","failureEn":"Assuming joints and integrated action are complete because all blocks have been poured.","check":"標記每個示意接縫的狀態與尚缺驗證，避免填施工尺寸。","checkEn":"Mark each joint state and missing verification without assigning construction dimensions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-05-k1","title":"分塊邏輯","titleEn":"Block logic","text":"分塊可管理施工與熱行為；最終整體作用仍須處理接縫。","textEn":"Blocks organize construction and thermal behavior; final integrated action still depends on joints."},{"id":"b202-v6-05-k2","title":"狀態紀錄","titleEn":"State records","text":"施工紀錄須能說明各區塊在同一時間的實際成熟與接合狀態。","textEn":"Records should identify each block’s maturity and connection state at a common time."}],"quiz":{"options":["以最後澆置日期代替所有接合驗證","接縫處理與整體傳力條件","以各塊外觀完整代替整體作用查證"],"optionsEn":["Use the last pour date in place of all joint verification","Joint treatment and conditions for integrated load transfer","Use intact block appearance as proof of integrated action"],"answer":1,"question":"所有壩塊已澆置，哪項仍須單獨查證？","questionEn":"All blocks are poured. What still requires independent verification?","explanation":"材料放置完成不等於所有介面功能完成。","explanationEn":"Completion of material placement does not establish completion of every interface function."}},{"id":"b202-v6-06","sequence":6,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-05"],"title":"比較水化熱與冷卻歷程","titleEn":"Compare hydration heat and cooling histories","objective":"理解溫度梯度、收縮與裂縫的關係。","objectiveEn":"Understand relationships among thermal gradients, contraction and cracking.","instruction":"自繪混凝土核心與表面兩條溫度—時間曲線，再畫冷卻較快的比較曲線。標記水化放熱、散熱及相對收縮，不採用歷史設備數值作今日設定。","instructionEn":"Sketch core and surface temperature histories and a faster-cooling comparison. Mark hydration heat, heat loss and relative contraction without using historical equipment values as present settings.","observation":"比較最高溫相近但內外溫差不同的情況。","observationEn":"Compare cases with similar peak temperature but different internal-to-surface gradients.","failure":"把快速降溫一概當作越快越好，忽略拘束與梯度。","failureEn":"Assuming faster cooling is always better while ignoring restraint and gradients.","check":"解釋為何峰值、梯度與時間歷程都需保留。","checkEn":"Explain why peak, gradient and time history all need to be retained.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-06-k1","title":"熱源與尺度","titleEn":"Heat source and scale","text":"大體積混凝土的內部熱不易迅速逸散，溫度分布會不均勻。","textEn":"Heat within mass concrete does not escape quickly, producing nonuniform temperatures."},{"id":"b202-v6-06-k2","title":"拘束收縮","titleEn":"Restrained contraction","text":"自由收縮受到相鄰材料或幾何拘束時，可能產生應力。","textEn":"Contraction restrained by adjacent material or geometry can generate stress."}],"quiz":{"options":["是，最高溫是唯一需要的資料","只需表面溫度相同即可認定等效","不一定，梯度、拘束與材料歷程也影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Yes; peak temperature is the only relevant data","Equal surface temperature alone establishes equivalence","No; gradients, restraint and material history also matter"],"answer":2,"question":"相同最高溫的兩塊混凝土，裂縫風險必定相同嗎？","questionEn":"Do two concrete blocks with the same peak temperature necessarily share cracking risk?","explanation":"最高溫只描述熱歷程的一部分，無法取代梯度和拘束證據。","explanationEn":"Peak temperature captures only part of thermal history and cannot replace gradient and restraint evidence."}},{"id":"b202-v6-07","sequence":7,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-06"],"title":"分清接縫灌漿與排水","titleEn":"Distinguish joint grouting from drainage","objective":"避免把填充接縫與降低滲流水壓混成同一功能。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating joint filling with management of seepage pressure.","instruction":"在兩張小圖分別畫壩塊接縫與壩基排水路徑。用功能敘述解釋灌漿、止水與排水各想改變什麼，再列出需查證的效果。","instructionEn":"Draw block joints and foundation drainage in separate sketches. Explain what grouting, water barriers and drainage seek to change, then identify evidence of their effects.","observation":"觀察流量減少是否同時需要查看水壓，而非單獨判為改善。","observationEn":"Check whether reduced flow also requires pressure data before it is called an improvement.","failure":"把排水孔流量變小直接認定為止水良好，忽略可能堵塞。","failureEn":"Treating falling drain flow as proof of improved water exclusion while overlooking possible blockage.","check":"提交功能對照與一組「流量下降」的兩種替代解釋。","checkEn":"Provide a function comparison and two alternative explanations for falling flow.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-07-k1","title":"功能區別","titleEn":"Different functions","text":"填充或接合、限制入流與引導排水，是不同工程功能。","textEn":"Filling or joining, limiting ingress and conveying drainage are different engineering functions."},{"id":"b202-v6-07-k2","title":"組合證據","titleEn":"Combined evidence","text":"流量與壓力一起看，比只看其中一項更能限制錯誤推論。","textEn":"Flow and pressure considered together constrain interpretations better than either alone."}],"quiz":{"options":["排水路徑受阻等替代原因","整體止水效果必然變好","只增加流量讀數次數，忽略壓力上升"],"optionsEn":["Alternative causes such as obstructed drainage","Water exclusion has necessarily improved","Repeat flow readings while ignoring rising pressure"],"answer":0,"question":"排水流量下降而附近水壓升高，應優先考慮什麼？","questionEn":"Drain flow falls while nearby water pressure rises. What warrants consideration?","explanation":"相反的水壓與流量趨勢不能只解讀為漏水減少。","explanationEn":"Opposing pressure and flow trends cannot be interpreted solely as reduced leakage."}},{"id":"b202-v6-08","sequence":8,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-07"],"title":"連結進水、管路與水輪機","titleEn":"Link intake, conduit and turbine interfaces","objective":"辨識高程差、流量與瞬變的不同問題。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish head, flow and transient-response questions.","instruction":"自繪水面、進水口、壓力管和水輪機的高程關係。用兩格比較穩定流動與流量改變的概念，註明沒有進行真實閥門操作或壓力計算。","instructionEn":"Sketch elevations of reservoir surface, intake, penstock and turbine. Compare steady flow and changing flow in two panels, explicitly excluding real valve operation or pressure calculations.","observation":"注意管路不是只把水運送到機組，也承受壓力與約束反力。","observationEn":"A conduit transports water while also carrying pressure and restraint forces.","failure":"只用高程差估算發電概念，就宣稱已驗證管路所有受力。","failureEn":"Claiming complete conduit verification from an elevation-based generation estimate alone.","check":"列出穩態與瞬變各需的資料，並保留未知邊界條件。","checkEn":"List data needed for steady and transient states, keeping unknown boundary conditions explicit.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-08-k1","title":"能量路徑","titleEn":"Energy path","text":"水位差提供能量潛力；實際輸出還受流量與損失影響。","textEn":"Water-level difference provides energy potential; output also depends on flow and losses."},{"id":"b202-v6-08-k2","title":"瞬變效應","titleEn":"Transient effects","text":"流速改變會引起隨時間變化的壓力，不能只用穩態圖描述。","textEn":"Changing velocity produces time-varying pressure that a steady-state diagram cannot fully describe."}],"quiz":{"options":["穩態平均壓力必定等於所有瞬時峰值","流量變化可能造成動態壓力反應","只要高程不變，壓力就不可能隨時間變化"],"optionsEn":["Steady mean pressure necessarily equals every transient peak","Changing flow can create a dynamic pressure response","If elevation stays fixed, pressure cannot change with time"],"answer":1,"question":"為何穩態壓力資料不能單獨代表快速流量變化時的狀態？","questionEn":"Why cannot steady pressure alone represent a rapid flow change?","explanation":"瞬變是時間相關的系統反應，需要額外的模型及資料。","explanationEn":"A transient is a time-dependent system response requiring additional modeling and evidence."}}],"title":"壩體與水工介面","titleEn":"Dam body and hydraulic interfaces","description":"追蹤分塊、熱變形、接縫與管路的相互影響。","descriptionEn":"Trace interactions among blocks, thermal movement, joints and conduits."},{"id":"b202-stage03","order":3,"steps":[{"id":"b202-v6-09","sequence":9,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-spillways"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-08"],"title":"從溢洪道侵蝕追查水流","titleEn":"Trace spillway erosion to flow behavior","objective":"區分看到的損傷與尚未確定的侵蝕機制。","objectiveEn":"Separate observed damage from an unconfirmed erosion mechanism.","instruction":"依歷史案例自繪溢洪道至斜隧道的路徑，在一處標示假想侵蝕。列出流路幾何、接縫、流量歷程與表面調查等需查證資料，不直接指定修補材料。","instructionEn":"Sketch the historical spillway-to-inclined-tunnel path and mark hypothetical erosion. List geometry, joints, flow history and surface evidence to investigate without prescribing repair materials.","observation":"比較同樣「混凝土缺損」可能具有不同位置、發展速度及成因。","observationEn":"Similar concrete loss may differ in location, growth rate and cause.","failure":"看見侵蝕就套用單一成因，或把修補完成當成成因已排除。","failureEn":"Assigning one cause from appearance or treating a completed repair as proof the cause is removed.","check":"建立損傷地圖，明確分出已觀察事實與待驗證機制。","checkEn":"Create a damage map distinguishing observed facts from mechanisms requiring verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-09-k1","title":"水工損傷","titleEn":"Hydraulic damage","text":"高速水流與局部幾何可能形成複雜作用；外觀不足以單獨辨因。","textEn":"High-speed flow and local geometry can interact in complex ways; appearance alone is insufficient for diagnosis."},{"id":"b202-v6-09-k2","title":"歷史回饋","titleEn":"Historical feedback","text":"既有侵蝕與修復紀錄提供檢查重點，但不能直接代替新事件調查。","textEn":"Historical erosion and repairs guide inspection but do not replace investigation of a new event."}],"quiz":{"options":["只核對修補材料強度，不檢查流路","沿用前次成因，不核對本次事件條件","事件流量歷程、幾何和局部表面狀態"],"optionsEn":["Check repair strength without examining the water route","Reuse the previous diagnosis without checking this event","Event flow history, geometry and local surface conditions"],"answer":2,"question":"修補區再次出現侵蝕，最應補查哪類證據？","questionEn":"Erosion reappears near a repair. What evidence most needs review?","explanation":"反覆損傷需要回到水流與局部介面的機制，而非只記錄修補外觀。","explanationEn":"Repeated damage requires review of flow and interface mechanisms, not only repaired appearance."}},{"id":"b202-v6-10","sequence":10,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-09"],"title":"建立壩體監測比較窗","titleEn":"Establish comparable dam-monitoring windows","objective":"把水位、溫度與變形的時間關係分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate time relationships among reservoir level, temperature and deformation.","instruction":"自行製作六列示例水位、氣溫、位移與排水紀錄，標記季節性變化。挑出兩組相近條件資料，比較剩餘差異並保留儀器核對欄。","instructionEn":"Invent six records of reservoir level, temperature, movement and drainage, marking seasonal variation. Compare two matched-condition groups and retain an instrument-check field.","observation":"觀察同一位移數字可能對應不同水位或溫度狀態。","observationEn":"The same displacement value may occur under different water-level or temperature conditions.","failure":"把正常環境循環或感測器零點變更直接當成永久損傷。","failureEn":"Treating environmental cycles or sensor-zero changes as permanent damage.","check":"為一個異常保留環境、儀器與結構三種可能解釋。","checkEn":"Retain environmental, instrument and structural explanations for one anomaly.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-10-k1","title":"條件化比較","titleEn":"Conditional comparison","text":"跨時比較應記錄荷載與環境，避免將不同條件混成趨勢。","textEn":"Comparisons over time should retain load and environment rather than merge different conditions into one trend."},{"id":"b202-v6-10-k2","title":"證據交叉核對","titleEn":"Cross-checking evidence","text":"位移、滲流和目視紀錄各有盲點，組合使用有助限制誤判。","textEn":"Movement, seepage and visual records have different blind spots; combining them limits misinterpretation."}],"quiz":{"options":["有需要進一步檢驗的相關性","已證明全部由溫度造成","已證明壩體永久失效"],"optionsEn":["A correlation requiring further examination","Temperature has been proven the sole cause","Permanent dam failure has been proven"],"answer":0,"question":"位移季節性變化與氣溫同步，能直接推論什麼？","questionEn":"Displacement varies seasonally with temperature. What can be inferred directly?","explanation":"同步變化是線索，並非單獨的因果或安全證明。","explanationEn":"Synchronous variation is a clue, not standalone causal or safety proof."}},{"id":"b202-v6-11","sequence":11,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-spillways"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-10"],"title":"做有邊界的水量收支","titleEn":"Construct a bounded water balance","objective":"區分蓄水變化與不同出流用途。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish storage change from different outflow uses.","instruction":"自設一個單日水量例子，列入入流、放流、蒸發與蓄水變化。再畫兩個不同放流分配的教學情境，只比較質量守恆，不提出真實調度建議。","instructionEn":"Invent a one-day example with inflow, release, evaporation and storage change. Compare two illustrative release allocations for mass balance only, without recommending real reservoir operations.","observation":"檢查發電流量與總放流是否被重複計入。","observationEn":"Check whether generation flow is double-counted within total release.","failure":"將通過水輪機的水當成消失，或忽略水庫蓄積。","failureEn":"Treating turbine flow as consumed water or omitting storage change.","check":"收支需閉合，並標明全部數字是自設例子及尚缺用途限制。","checkEn":"Close the balance and label all numbers as invented, with unmodeled use constraints.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-11-k1","title":"守恆邊界","titleEn":"Conservation boundary","text":"在選定空間與時間內，水量入出與蓄積必須一致。","textEn":"Within defined space and time, inflow, outflow and storage must balance."},{"id":"b202-v6-11-k2","title":"多重目標","titleEn":"Multiple objectives","text":"供水、發電、洪水與環境問題不會被單一水量平衡自動解決。","textEn":"A water balance alone does not resolve supply, energy, flood and environmental objectives."}],"quiz":{"options":["同時列為兩次出流","作為出流，不再另列一次消耗","從所有收支欄刪除"],"optionsEn":["As two separate outflows","As outflow, without counting a second consumption","Omit it from the balance"],"answer":1,"question":"水流經水輪機後到達下游，在水庫收支中應如何處理？","questionEn":"Water passes through turbines to downstream. How is it represented in the reservoir balance?","explanation":"同一水量不能因用途名稱不同而重複計算。","explanationEn":"The same water must not be counted twice because it has different use labels."}},{"id":"b202-v6-12","sequence":12,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-history","v6-hoover-dam","v6-hoover-spillways"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-11"],"title":"編成壩工證據與限制清單","titleEn":"Compile dam-engineering evidence and limits","objective":"交付能區分歷史案例、模型與實測需求的資料。","objectiveEn":"Deliver records distinguishing historical cases, models and measurement needs.","instruction":"整理水路圖、受力圖、施工狀態、熱曲線與監測表。為每項結論註記它屬歷史事實、教學假設或仍需實測，並列出專業複核邊界。","instructionEn":"Organize route, force, construction-state, thermal and monitoring records. Label each conclusion as historical fact, educational assumption or needing measurement, and identify professional-review boundaries.","observation":"核對舊施工記錄是否被誤寫成現行通用規格。","observationEn":"Check whether a historical construction record has been misrepresented as a current universal specification.","failure":"把課程示意數值寫入真實施工、設備或放流水量設定。","failureEn":"Transferring illustrative course values into actual construction, equipment or release settings.","check":"至少五項判斷可回查到來源或自設假設，未解問題單獨列出。","checkEn":"Make at least five conclusions traceable to sources or declared assumptions, with open issues listed separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v6-12-k1","title":"歷史與規範","titleEn":"History versus specifications","text":"歷史工程能提供思考案例，但今日設計需另外的資料與程序。","textEn":"Historical engineering provides cases for reasoning; present design requires additional evidence and procedures."},{"id":"b202-v6-12-k2","title":"範圍宣告","titleEn":"Scope declaration","text":"證據能支持什麼及不能支持什麼，都應出現在交付中。","textEn":"A handover should state both what evidence supports and what it does not."}],"quiz":{"options":["已完成課程，所以真壩可按此圖操作","歷史數字可直接套用任何新壩","本模型展示功能與依賴，尚非壩體安全鑑定"],"optionsEn":["Course completion authorizes operation from this sketch","Historical values apply directly to any new dam","This model shows functions and dependencies, not a dam-safety assessment"],"answer":2,"question":"哪項交付敘述最合適？","questionEn":"Which handover statement is most appropriate?","explanation":"學習模型的可審查性不等於真實工程驗證完成。","explanationEn":"A reviewable learning model is not completed validation of a real engineering system."}}],"title":"洩流與長期判讀","titleEn":"Releases and long-term interpretation","description":"以侵蝕、監測與水量證據檢查工程的運作邊界。","descriptionEn":"Review operating boundaries using erosion, monitoring and water-balance evidence."},{"id":"b202-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「拱座相容與分力」與「裂縫連通與揚壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Abutment compatibility and load sharing\" and \"Crack connectivity and uplift\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b202-v15-01","title":"拱座相容與分力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Abutment compatibility and load sharing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v6-12"],"objective":"說明「拱座相容與分力」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拱重力壩把一部分水平荷載沿拱圈送到兩岸，也把一部分荷載透過壩底傳入基礎。教材以同位移的平行彈簧理解剛度與分力，不把它當成真實拱壩公式。岩體節理、施工縫及溫度會改變相容條件，所以增加某路徑剛度也會改變其他路徑分擔。 平行彈簧共同位移來自相容條件，若兩岸支承本身移動，需把支承位移加入，分力比例就不再只由剛度決定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拱座相容與分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An arch-gravity dam transfers some horizontal load toward the abutments and some through its base. Parallel springs with equal displacement illustrate stiffness-controlled sharing, not a real arch-dam design equation. Rock joints, construction joints and temperature alter compatibility, so stiffening one path changes the load carried by the other path as well. Equal spring displacement follows compatibility; moving supports introduce imposed displacements, after which stiffness ratios alone no longer determine the force shares between the paths. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dam height alone determines the arch load share.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拱座相容與分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Abutment compatibility and load sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-01-k1","title":"拱座相容與分力","titleEn":"Abutment compatibility and load sharing","text":"拱重力壩把一部分水平荷載沿拱圈送到兩岸，也把一部分荷載透過壩底傳入基礎。教材以同位移的平行彈簧理解剛度與分力，不把它當成真實拱壩公式。","textEn":"An arch-gravity dam transfers some horizontal load toward the abutments and some through its base. Parallel springs with equal displacement illustrate stiffness-controlled sharing, not a real arch-dam design equation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dam height alone determines the arch load share. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「拱座相容與分力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Abutment compatibility and load sharing\" is correct?","options":["只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力","拱重力壩把一部分水平荷載沿拱圈送到兩岸，也把一部分荷載透過壩底傳入基礎。","只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Dam height alone determines the arch load share.","An arch-gravity dam transfers some horizontal load toward the abutments and some through its base.","Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拱重力壩把一部分水平荷載沿拱圈送到兩岸，也把一部分荷載透過壩底傳入基礎。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An arch-gravity dam transfers some horizontal load toward the abutments and some through its base. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":13},{"id":"b202-v15-02","title":"拱座相容與分力：定量估算","titleEn":"Abutment compatibility and load sharing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拱座相容與分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN。模型邊界：線彈性且兩路徑同位移；未模擬三維拱殼、開裂或接觸滑移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN. Model boundary: linear elasticity and equal displacement in both paths; excludes three-dimensional shell action, cracking and contact slip. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一水位下比較壩體位移、拱座變形及溫度，避免用不同季節的位移直接反推剛度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare dam displacement, abutment deformation and temperature at the same reservoir level before inferring stiffness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN。模型邊界：線彈性且兩路徑同位移；未模擬三維拱殼、開裂或接觸滑移。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN. Model boundary: linear elasticity and equal displacement in both paths; excludes three-dimensional shell action, cracking and contact slip.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「拱座相容與分力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Abutment compatibility and load sharing\", which statement holds?","options":["自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量","所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint.","One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":14},{"id":"b202-v15-03","title":"拱座相容與分力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Abutment compatibility and load sharing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拱座相容與分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一水位下比較壩體位移、拱座變形及溫度，避免用不同季節的位移直接反推剛度。以改變一個路徑剛度的敏感度分析檢查分力總和是否保持外力，並用多點量測辨認左右岸反應不對稱。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare dam displacement, abutment deformation and temperature at the same reservoir level before inferring stiffness. Change one path stiffness and confirm that load shares still sum to the applied force. Use several observations to distinguish an asymmetric abutment response from a uniform translation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把拱座路徑剛度減半，重算兩種分力與共同位移，畫出每個路徑的自由體圖，列出需要岩體試驗才能確認的模型參數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve the abutment-path stiffness and recalculate both load shares and common displacement. Draw a free-body diagram for each path and identify the parameters that require rock-mass testing before interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一水位下比較壩體位移、拱座變形及溫度，避免用不同季節的位移直接反推剛度。以改變一個路徑剛度的敏感度分析檢查分力總和是否保持外力，並用多點量測辨認左右岸反應不對稱。","textEn":"Compare dam displacement, abutment deformation and temperature at the same reservoir level before inferring stiffness. Change one path stiffness and confirm that load shares still sum to the applied force. Use several observations to distinguish an asymmetric abutment response from a uniform translation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把拱座路徑剛度減半，重算兩種分力與共同位移，畫出每個路徑的自由體圖，列出需要岩體試驗才能確認的模型參數。","textEn":"Halve the abutment-path stiffness and recalculate both load shares and common displacement. Draw a free-body diagram for each path and identify the parameters that require rock-mass testing before interpretation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「拱座相容與分力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Abutment compatibility and load sharing\"?","options":["在同一水位下比較壩體位移、拱座變形及溫度，避免用不同季節的位移直接反推剛度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離"],"optionsEn":["Compare dam displacement, abutment deformation and temperature at the same reservoir level before inferring stiffness.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一水位下比較壩體位移、拱座變形及溫度，避免用不同季節的位移直接反推剛度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare dam displacement, abutment deformation and temperature at the same reservoir level before inferring stiffness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":15},{"id":"b202-v15-04","title":"拱座相容與分力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Abutment compatibility and load sharing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拱座相容與分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. Calibrating only one crest displacement may reproduce overall stiffness while completely misrepresenting local stress concentrations and the distribution of support reactions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平行彈簧共同位移來自相容條件，若兩岸支承本身移動，需把支承位移加入，分力比例就不再只由剛度決定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal spring displacement follows compatibility; moving supports introduce imposed displacements, after which stiffness ratios alone no longer determine the force shares between the paths.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dam height alone determines the arch load share.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。","textEn":"Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. Calibrating only one crest displacement may reproduce overall stiffness while completely misrepresenting local stress concentrations and the distribution of support reactions.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拱座相容與分力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Abutment compatibility and load sharing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。","只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere.","Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":16},{"id":"b202-v15-05","title":"裂縫連通與揚壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crack connectivity and uplift: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「裂縫連通與揚壓」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crack connectivity and uplift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。教材把已假設的壓力分布積分成向上合力，再討論裂縫開口與排水能力對分布的影響。裂縫長度不能獨立決定壓力，因流動阻力、下游水位與排水孔都參與控制。 排水點可能讓壓力圖出現折線，積分時應按各段面積相加，作用點也必須用各段力矩求得。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂縫連通與揚壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area. Integrating an explicitly assumed pressure diagram gives the upward resultant; crack aperture and drainage then explain possible changes to that diagram. Crack length alone cannot determine pressure because flow resistance, tailwater and drains also control it. A drain may introduce a breakpoint in the pressure diagram; sum segment areas for force and segment moments for the resultant location on the base. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crack connectivity and uplift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「裂縫連通與揚壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crack connectivity and uplift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-05-k1","title":"裂縫連通與揚壓","titleEn":"Crack connectivity and uplift","text":"基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。教材把已假設的壓力分布積分成向上合力，再討論裂縫開口與排水能力對分布的影響。","textEn":"Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area. Integrating an explicitly assumed pressure diagram gives the upward resultant; crack aperture and drainage then explain possible changes to that diagram.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裂縫連通與揚壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crack connectivity and uplift\" is correct?","options":["只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓","平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險","基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。"],"optionsEn":["Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.","Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.","Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":17},{"id":"b202-v15-06","title":"裂縫連通與揚壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Crack connectivity and uplift: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裂縫連通與揚壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crack connectivity and uplift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。模型邊界：沿基底壓力線性且以一米壩長計算；不代表裂縫內實際壓力分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN. Model boundary: linear basal pressure over a one-metre dam strip; not the measured distribution within an actual crack. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各測壓孔換算至共同基準的壓力水頭，再檢查高低庫水位期間的反應與時間差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。模型邊界：沿基底壓力線性且以一米壩長計算；不代表裂縫內實際壓力分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN. Model boundary: linear basal pressure over a one-metre dam strip; not the measured distribution within an actual crack.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裂縫連通與揚壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crack connectivity and uplift\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。","首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力","低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN.","The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.","Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":18},{"id":"b202-v15-07","title":"裂縫連通與揚壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crack connectivity and uplift: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裂縫連通與揚壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crack connectivity and uplift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各測壓孔換算至共同基準的壓力水頭，再檢查高低庫水位期間的反應與時間差。以排水流量配對判讀：壓力上升但流量下降支持堵塞假說，壓力與流量同升則須追查新增連通路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels. Pair pressure with drainage flow: rising pressure with falling flow supports blockage, while simultaneous increases require investigation of a newly connected seepage path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較線性分布與上游半段保持高壓的分段分布，分別求合力及作用點，說明相同上游水位下為何抗滑與傾覆判斷都會改變。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare the linear diagram with a piecewise diagram retaining high pressure over the upstream half. Find each resultant and its location, then explain changes in both sliding and overturning interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：未辨認堵塞仍沿用原先低揚壓分布，會高估有效壩重與抗滑餘量；但測管氣泡或堵管也能產生假訊號，需以沖洗紀錄及鄰孔讀值交叉確認。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using an old low-uplift diagram after drainage blockage overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各測壓孔換算至共同基準的壓力水頭，再檢查高低庫水位期間的反應與時間差。以排水流量配對判讀：壓力上升但流量下降支持堵塞假說，壓力與流量同升則須追查新增連通路徑。","textEn":"Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels. Pair pressure with drainage flow: rising pressure with falling flow supports blockage, while simultaneous increases require investigation of a newly connected seepage path.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較線性分布與上游半段保持高壓的分段分布，分別求合力及作用點，說明相同上游水位下為何抗滑與傾覆判斷都會改變。","textEn":"Compare the linear diagram with a piecewise diagram retaining high pressure over the upstream half. Find each resultant and its location, then explain changes in both sliding and overturning interpretation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裂縫連通與揚壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crack connectivity and uplift\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將各測壓孔換算至共同基準的壓力水頭，再檢查高低庫水位期間的反應與時間差。","溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels.","Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將各測壓孔換算至共同基準的壓力水頭，再檢查高低庫水位期間的反應與時間差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":19},{"id":"b202-v15-08","title":"裂縫連通與揚壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crack connectivity and uplift: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裂縫連通與揚壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crack connectivity and uplift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未辨認堵塞仍沿用原先低揚壓分布，會高估有效壩重與抗滑餘量；但測管氣泡或堵管也能產生假訊號，需以沖洗紀錄及鄰孔讀值交叉確認。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using an old low-uplift diagram after drainage blockage overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Air or blockage in the measuring tube can also create false signals, so maintenance records and neighboring readings must corroborate the interpretation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水點可能讓壓力圖出現折線，積分時應按各段面積相加，作用點也必須用各段力矩求得。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A drain may introduce a breakpoint in the pressure diagram; sum segment areas for force and segment moments for the resultant location on the base.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未辨認堵塞仍沿用原先低揚壓分布，會高估有效壩重與抗滑餘量；但測管氣泡或堵管也能產生假訊號，需以沖洗紀錄及鄰孔讀值交叉確認。","textEn":"Using an old low-uplift diagram after drainage blockage overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Air or blockage in the measuring tube can also create false signals, so maintenance records and neighboring readings must corroborate the interpretation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裂縫連通與揚壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crack connectivity and uplift\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險","未辨認堵塞仍沿用原先低揚壓分布，會高估有效壩重與抗滑餘量；但測管氣泡或堵管也能產生假訊號，需以沖洗紀錄及鄰孔讀值交叉確認。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.","Using an old low-uplift diagram after drainage blockage overstates effective weight and sliding resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未辨認堵塞仍沿用原先低揚壓分布，會高估有效壩重與抗滑餘量；但測管氣泡或堵管也能產生假訊號，需以沖洗紀錄及鄰孔讀值交叉確認。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using an old low-uplift diagram after drainage blockage overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":20}],"order":4},{"id":"b202-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「混凝土冷卻熱量」與「接縫閉合與溫度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Concrete cooling heat account\" and \"Joint closure and temperature\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b202-v15-09","title":"混凝土冷卻熱量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Concrete cooling heat account: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「混凝土冷卻熱量」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete cooling heat account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大體積混凝土降溫同時涉及熱量移除與空間溫差，兩者不可互相代替。比熱模型能估算均勻降溫所需移除的顯熱，但表面冷得過快可能提高內外約束應力。需把水化熱產生、冷卻水帶走熱量與周邊散熱分列，才能判斷熱量帳是否閉合。 熱擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，縮小試件的冷卻曲線不能直接按時間等比例搬到大體積壩塊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土冷卻熱量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cooling mass concrete involves both heat removal and spatial gradients, which are not interchangeable. Heat capacity estimates sensible energy for uniform cooling, while rapid surface cooling can increase restraint stresses. Separate hydration heat, heat carried by cooling water and environmental exchange to establish whether the thermal account actually closes. Thermal diffusion time scales with characteristic length squared, so cooling observations from small specimens cannot be transferred to massive blocks by simple linear time scaling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete cooling heat account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混凝土冷卻熱量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concrete cooling heat account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-09-k1","title":"混凝土冷卻熱量","titleEn":"Concrete cooling heat account","text":"大體積混凝土降溫同時涉及熱量移除與空間溫差，兩者不可互相代替。比熱模型能估算均勻降溫所需移除的顯熱，但表面冷得過快可能提高內外約束應力。","textEn":"Cooling mass concrete involves both heat removal and spatial gradients, which are not interchangeable. Heat capacity estimates sensible energy for uniform cooling, while rapid surface cooling can increase restraint stresses.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土冷卻熱量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concrete cooling heat account\" is correct?","options":["大體積混凝土降溫同時涉及熱量移除與空間溫差，兩者不可互相代替。","平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險","自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量"],"optionsEn":["Cooling mass concrete involves both heat removal and spatial gradients, which are not interchangeable.","Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.","Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大體積混凝土降溫同時涉及熱量移除與空間溫差，兩者不可互相代替。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cooling mass concrete involves both heat removal and spatial gradients, which are not interchangeable. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":21},{"id":"b202-v15-10","title":"混凝土冷卻熱量：定量估算","titleEn":"Concrete cooling heat account: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混凝土冷卻熱量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete cooling heat account” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。模型邊界：常數比熱與均勻溫降；未計持續水化熱及熱應力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ. Model boundary: constant heat capacity and uniform cooling; continuing hydration heat and thermal stress are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以核心、中間和表面溫度檢查均勻假設，再用冷卻水流量乘進出口溫差積分熱量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the uniform-temperature assumption using core, intermediate and surface readings, then integrate cooling-water flow times temperature rise.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。模型邊界：常數比熱與均勻溫降；未計持續水化熱及熱應力。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ. Model boundary: constant heat capacity and uniform cooling; continuing hydration heat and thermal stress are excluded.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土冷卻熱量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concrete cooling heat account\", which statement holds?","options":["所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。","岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離"],"optionsEn":["One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ.","Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":22},{"id":"b202-v15-11","title":"混凝土冷卻熱量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete cooling heat account: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混凝土冷卻熱量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete cooling heat account” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以核心、中間和表面溫度檢查均勻假設，再用冷卻水流量乘進出口溫差積分熱量。若水側移熱量大於混凝土顯熱減少，應查水化熱與邊界交換，不可立即認定溫度儀表故障。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the uniform-temperature assumption using core, intermediate and surface readings, then integrate cooling-water flow times temperature rise. If water-side heat removal exceeds the concrete sensible-energy decrease, investigate hydration and boundary exchange before assuming the temperature instruments are defective. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對同一熱量設計均勻與偏側冷卻兩個假想溫度剖面，指出哪些測點能區分兩者，再估算多移除一開爾文顯熱所需的額外能量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct uniform and one-sided cooling profiles with the same total heat removal. Identify sensors that distinguish them, then calculate the additional sensible energy associated with one more kelvin of cooling.","failure":"注意干擾：冷卻太集中會造成局部溫度梯度及裂縫，即使平均溫度下降符合目標也可能出現問題；裂縫又改變水密與局部傳熱，因此不能只以總移熱量驗收冷卻品質。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concentrated cooling can create local gradients and cracking even when average temperature meets its target. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以核心、中間和表面溫度檢查均勻假設，再用冷卻水流量乘進出口溫差積分熱量。若水側移熱量大於混凝土顯熱減少，應查水化熱與邊界交換，不可立即認定溫度儀表故障。","textEn":"Check the uniform-temperature assumption using core, intermediate and surface readings, then integrate cooling-water flow times temperature rise. If water-side heat removal exceeds the concrete sensible-energy decrease, investigate hydration and boundary exchange before assuming the temperature instruments are defective.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對同一熱量設計均勻與偏側冷卻兩個假想溫度剖面，指出哪些測點能區分兩者，再估算多移除一開爾文顯熱所需的額外能量。","textEn":"Construct uniform and one-sided cooling profiles with the same total heat removal. Identify sensors that distinguish them, then calculate the additional sensible energy associated with one more kelvin of cooling.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土冷卻熱量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concrete cooling heat account\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援","以核心、中間和表面溫度檢查均勻假設，再用冷卻水流量乘進出口溫差積分熱量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.","Check the uniform-temperature assumption using core, intermediate and surface readings, then integrate cooling-water flow times temperature rise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以核心、中間和表面溫度檢查均勻假設，再用冷卻水流量乘進出口溫差積分熱量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the uniform-temperature assumption using core, intermediate and surface readings, then integrate cooling-water flow times temperature rise. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":23},{"id":"b202-v15-12","title":"混凝土冷卻熱量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concrete cooling heat account: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混凝土冷卻熱量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete cooling heat account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"冷卻太集中會造成局部溫度梯度及裂縫，即使平均溫度下降符合目標也可能出現問題；裂縫又改變水密與局部傳熱，因此不能只以總移熱量驗收冷卻品質。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concentrated cooling can create local gradients and cracking even when average temperature meets its target. Cracks subsequently alter watertightness and heat transfer, so total extracted energy alone cannot establish the quality of the cooling process. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：熱擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，縮小試件的冷卻曲線不能直接按時間等比例搬到大體積壩塊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Thermal diffusion time scales with characteristic length squared, so cooling observations from small specimens cannot be transferred to massive blocks by simple linear time scaling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冷卻太集中會造成局部溫度梯度及裂縫，即使平均溫度下降符合目標也可能出現問題；裂縫又改變水密與局部傳熱，因此不能只以總移熱量驗收冷卻品質。","textEn":"Concentrated cooling can create local gradients and cracking even when average temperature meets its target. Cracks subsequently alter watertightness and heat transfer, so total extracted energy alone cannot establish the quality of the cooling process.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土冷卻熱量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concrete cooling heat account\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["冷卻太集中會造成局部溫度梯度及裂縫，即使平均溫度下降符合目標也可能出現問題；裂縫又改變水密與局部傳熱，因此不能只以總移熱量驗收冷卻品質。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量"],"optionsEn":["Concentrated cooling can create local gradients and cracking even when average temperature meets its target.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"冷卻太集中會造成局部溫度梯度及裂縫，即使平均溫度下降符合目標也可能出現問題；裂縫又改變水密與局部傳熱，因此不能只以總移熱量驗收冷卻品質。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concentrated cooling can create local gradients and cracking even when average temperature meets its target. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":24},{"id":"b202-v15-13","title":"接縫閉合與溫度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint closure and temperature: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「接縫閉合與溫度」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint closure and temperature” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分塊澆置留下的接縫，其開合取決於塊體自由熱變形、相鄰約束與水壓。線膨脹模型只描述未受約束的長度變化，接縫灌漿後的應力則需用實際約束分析。不能把某溫度下的縫寬直接解讀為永久缺陷，也不能把所有縫寬變化都歸於氣溫。 接縫量測方向若與縫面法線不一致，需將位移投影分解，否則剪切位移也可能混入開合讀值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接縫閉合與溫度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A joint between concrete blocks opens or closes through thermal strain, neighboring restraint and water loading. Linear expansion describes free length change only; stress after grouting depends on actual restraint. Joint width at one temperature is not automatically a permanent defect, and not every width change can be attributed to air temperature. A gauge not aligned with the joint normal requires displacement projection; otherwise tangential movement can contaminate the apparent opening or closure of the joint. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint closure and temperature” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接縫閉合與溫度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint closure and temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-13-k1","title":"接縫閉合與溫度","titleEn":"Joint closure and temperature","text":"分塊澆置留下的接縫，其開合取決於塊體自由熱變形、相鄰約束與水壓。線膨脹模型只描述未受約束的長度變化，接縫灌漿後的應力則需用實際約束分析。","textEn":"A joint between concrete blocks opens or closes through thermal strain, neighboring restraint and water loading. Linear expansion describes free length change only; stress after grouting depends on actual restraint.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接縫閉合與溫度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint closure and temperature\" is correct?","options":["自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量","分塊澆置留下的接縫，其開合取決於塊體自由熱變形、相鄰約束與水壓。","首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力"],"optionsEn":["Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint.","A joint between concrete blocks opens or closes through thermal strain, neighboring restraint and water loading.","The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分塊澆置留下的接縫，其開合取決於塊體自由熱變形、相鄰約束與水壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A joint between concrete blocks opens or closes through thermal strain, neighboring restraint and water loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":25},{"id":"b202-v15-14","title":"接縫閉合與溫度：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint closure and temperature: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接縫閉合與溫度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint closure and temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm。模型邊界：單一塊體沿量測方向自由膨脹；不是受約束接縫的實際閉合量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm. Model boundary: free expansion of one block along the measurement axis; not the actual closure of a restrained joint. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將接縫計讀值與塊體內部溫度及庫水位同步繪圖，查看升溫與降溫路徑是否重合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot joint readings with internal block temperature and reservoir level, checking whether warming and cooling paths coincide.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm。模型邊界：單一塊體沿量測方向自由膨脹；不是受約束接縫的實際閉合量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm. Model boundary: free expansion of one block along the measurement axis; not the actual closure of a restrained joint.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接縫閉合與溫度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint closure and temperature\", which statement holds?","options":["低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償","溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge.","Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: alpha=0.00001 1/K; L=18 m; dT=12 K; dL=alpha*L*dT*1000=2.16 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":26},{"id":"b202-v15-15","title":"接縫閉合與溫度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint closure and temperature: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接縫閉合與溫度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint closure and temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將接縫計讀值與塊體內部溫度及庫水位同步繪圖，查看升溫與降溫路徑是否重合。若有遲滯，再查接觸摩擦與裂縫連通；量測基座本身的熱伸縮也必須先校正，避免誤判壩體變形。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot joint readings with internal block temperature and reservoir level, checking whether warming and cooling paths coincide. Hysteresis calls for investigating contact friction or crack connectivity. Correct thermal movement of the instrument mounting itself before assigning the observed change to the dam. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用三種熱膨脹係數重算自由伸長，另畫受約束與無約束兩個自由體圖，列出從位移轉成應力還缺少的剛度及接觸條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate free extension for three thermal expansion coefficients. Draw restrained and unrestrained free-body diagrams, then list stiffness and contact information still needed to convert displacement into a stress estimate.","failure":"注意干擾：灌漿溫度與後續運轉溫度不相容時，可能造成過高接觸壓力或縫面重新張開；但單支接縫計也可能因固定端鬆動而跳值，需以附近位移證據區分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incompatible grouting and service-temperature range can produce excessive contact pressure or reopening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將接縫計讀值與塊體內部溫度及庫水位同步繪圖，查看升溫與降溫路徑是否重合。若有遲滯，再查接觸摩擦與裂縫連通；量測基座本身的熱伸縮也必須先校正，避免誤判壩體變形。","textEn":"Plot joint readings with internal block temperature and reservoir level, checking whether warming and cooling paths coincide. Hysteresis calls for investigating contact friction or crack connectivity. Correct thermal movement of the instrument mounting itself before assigning the observed change to the dam.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用三種熱膨脹係數重算自由伸長，另畫受約束與無約束兩個自由體圖，列出從位移轉成應力還缺少的剛度及接觸條件。","textEn":"Recalculate free extension for three thermal expansion coefficients. Draw restrained and unrestrained free-body diagrams, then list stiffness and contact information still needed to convert displacement into a stress estimate.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接縫閉合與溫度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint closure and temperature\"?","options":["將接縫計讀值與塊體內部溫度及庫水位同步繪圖，查看升溫與降溫路徑是否重合。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力"],"optionsEn":["Plot joint readings with internal block temperature and reservoir level, checking whether warming and cooling paths coincide.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Dam height alone determines the arch load share."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將接縫計讀值與塊體內部溫度及庫水位同步繪圖，查看升溫與降溫路徑是否重合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot joint readings with internal block temperature and reservoir level, checking whether warming and cooling paths coincide. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":27},{"id":"b202-v15-16","title":"接縫閉合與溫度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint closure and temperature: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接縫閉合與溫度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint closure and temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"灌漿溫度與後續運轉溫度不相容時，可能造成過高接觸壓力或縫面重新張開；但單支接縫計也可能因固定端鬆動而跳值，需以附近位移證據區分。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incompatible grouting and service-temperature range can produce excessive contact pressure or reopening. A loose gauge anchor can also cause a sudden reading change, requiring neighboring displacement evidence to distinguish the instrument fault from physical joint behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：接縫量測方向若與縫面法線不一致，需將位移投影分解，否則剪切位移也可能混入開合讀值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A gauge not aligned with the joint normal requires displacement projection; otherwise tangential movement can contaminate the apparent opening or closure of the joint.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"灌漿溫度與後續運轉溫度不相容時，可能造成過高接觸壓力或縫面重新張開；但單支接縫計也可能因固定端鬆動而跳值，需以附近位移證據區分。","textEn":"An incompatible grouting and service-temperature range can produce excessive contact pressure or reopening. A loose gauge anchor can also cause a sudden reading change, requiring neighboring displacement evidence to distinguish the instrument fault from physical joint behavior.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接縫閉合與溫度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint closure and temperature\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","灌漿溫度與後續運轉溫度不相容時，可能造成過高接觸壓力或縫面重新張開；但單支接縫計也可能因固定端鬆動而跳值，需以附近位移證據區分。","首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An incompatible grouting and service-temperature range can produce excessive contact pressure or reopening.","The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"灌漿溫度與後續運轉溫度不相容時，可能造成過高接觸壓力或縫面重新張開；但單支接縫計也可能因固定端鬆動而跳值，需以附近位移證據區分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incompatible grouting and service-temperature range can produce excessive contact pressure or reopening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":28}],"order":5},{"id":"b202-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「壓力鋼管水錘」與「溢洪面汽蝕指標」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Penstock water hammer\" and \"Spillway cavitation indicator\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b202-v15-17","title":"壓力鋼管水錘：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Penstock water hammer: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「壓力鋼管水錘」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Penstock water hammer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。焦科夫斯基關係適合估計快速速度改變的首波幅度；反射、分岔與調壓設施會改變後續波形，因此單一首波不能取代整段管路的暫態包絡。 反射的符號取決於邊界阻抗，水庫端與封閉閥端可能產生不同反射，因此應在時空圖標明每個邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力鋼管水錘」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity. The Joukowsky relation estimates the first wave from a rapid velocity change. Reflections, branches and surge facilities alter later waves, so one first-wave estimate is not a full transient envelope. Reflection sign depends on boundary impedance; reservoir and closed-valve ends can reflect differently, so every boundary must be identified on the space-time diagram. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Penstock water hammer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力鋼管水錘」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Penstock water hammer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-17-k1","title":"壓力鋼管水錘","titleEn":"Penstock water hammer","text":"導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。焦科夫斯基關係適合估計快速速度改變的首波幅度；反射、分岔與調壓設施會改變後續波形，因此單一首波不能取代整段管路的暫態包絡。","textEn":"Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity. The Joukowsky relation estimates the first wave from a rapid velocity change.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力鋼管水錘」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Penstock water hammer\" is correct?","options":["首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力","所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。"],"optionsEn":["The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.","One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":29},{"id":"b202-v15-18","title":"壓力鋼管水錘：定量估算","titleEn":"Penstock water hammer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力鋼管水錘」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Penstock water hammer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。模型邊界：速度變化快於相關往返波時間，單相彈性首波；未含汽穴與反射疊加。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa. Model boundary: velocity change is faster than the relevant wave round-trip time; single-phase elastic first wave without cavitation or reflected-wave superposition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先以管長與波速估算往返時間，再比較控制動作時間及高速壓力記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate round-trip time from pipe length and wave speed, then compare actuator timing with rapid pressure records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。模型邊界：速度變化快於相關往返波時間，單相彈性首波；未含汽穴與反射疊加。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa. Model boundary: velocity change is faster than the relevant wave round-trip time; single-phase elastic first wave without cavitation or reflected-wave superposition.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力鋼管水錘」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Penstock water hammer\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。","岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離","每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa.","Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.","Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":30},{"id":"b202-v15-19","title":"壓力鋼管水錘：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Penstock water hammer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力鋼管水錘」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Penstock water hammer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先以管長與波速估算往返時間，再比較控制動作時間及高速壓力記錄。用兩測點峰值到達差檢查波速，若訊號含低壓平台或不連續回升，應追查汽穴及氣體效應，而非只修改阻力係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate round-trip time from pipe length and wave speed, then compare actuator timing with rapid pressure records. Arrival differences between two sensors test wave speed. Low-pressure plateaus or abrupt recovery warrant investigation of cavitation and gas effects rather than merely changing friction coefficients. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別把速度變化減半及波速降低，計算首波幅度，再用示意時空圖標出反射路徑，寫明何時必須改用完整特徵線暫態模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve the velocity change and reduce wave speed in separate cases. Calculate first-wave amplitudes, mark reflection paths on a space-time diagram, and state when a full method-of-characteristics transient model is required.","failure":"注意干擾：延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以管長與波速估算往返時間，再比較控制動作時間及高速壓力記錄。用兩測點峰值到達差檢查波速，若訊號含低壓平台或不連續回升，應追查汽穴及氣體效應，而非只修改阻力係數。","textEn":"Estimate round-trip time from pipe length and wave speed, then compare actuator timing with rapid pressure records. Arrival differences between two sensors test wave speed. Low-pressure plateaus or abrupt recovery warrant investigation of cavitation and gas effects rather than merely changing friction coefficients.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別把速度變化減半及波速降低，計算首波幅度，再用示意時空圖標出反射路徑，寫明何時必須改用完整特徵線暫態模型。","textEn":"Halve the velocity change and reduce wave speed in separate cases. Calculate first-wave amplitudes, mark reflection paths on a space-time diagram, and state when a full method-of-characteristics transient model is required.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力鋼管水錘」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Penstock water hammer\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","先以管長與波速估算往返時間，再比較控制動作時間及高速壓力記錄。","只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Estimate round-trip time from pipe length and wave speed, then compare actuator timing with rapid pressure records.","Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先以管長與波速估算往返時間，再比較控制動作時間及高速壓力記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate round-trip time from pipe length and wave speed, then compare actuator timing with rapid pressure records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":31},{"id":"b202-v15-20","title":"壓力鋼管水錘：失效診斷","titleEn":"Penstock water hammer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力鋼管水錘」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Penstock water hammer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. Column separation on the low-pressure side can generate a larger impact when the separated liquid columns rejoin. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：反射的符號取決於邊界阻抗，水庫端與封閉閥端可能產生不同反射，因此應在時空圖標明每個邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reflection sign depends on boundary impedance; reservoir and closed-valve ends can reflect differently, so every boundary must be identified on the space-time diagram.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。","textEn":"Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. Column separation on the low-pressure side can generate a larger impact when the separated liquid columns rejoin.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力鋼管水錘」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Penstock water hammer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave."],"answer":2,"explanation":"延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":32},{"id":"b202-v15-21","title":"溢洪面汽蝕指標：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Spillway cavitation indicator: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「溢洪面汽蝕指標」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Spillway cavitation indicator” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。汽蝕數把可用壓力差除以動壓，便於比較流況，但臨界值仍依表面幾何、含氣與尺度而異。以平均壓力計算只能作初步篩查。 蒸氣壓取決於水溫，而局部絕對壓也受大氣壓影響，兩者均應使用與事件同時的條件比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溢洪面汽蝕指標」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities. Vapor formation depends on absolute pressure relative to vapor pressure. A cavitation number normalizes available pressure by dynamic pressure, but its critical value depends on geometry, aeration and scale. A value based on mean pressure is therefore a preliminary indicator only. Vapor pressure depends on water temperature and absolute local pressure depends on atmospheric conditions; both should represent the same event rather than unrelated reference conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Spillway cavitation indicator” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「溢洪面汽蝕指標」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Spillway cavitation indicator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-21-k1","title":"溢洪面汽蝕指標","titleEn":"Spillway cavitation indicator","text":"高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。汽蝕數把可用壓力差除以動壓，便於比較流況，但臨界值仍依表面幾何、含氣與尺度而異。","textEn":"High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities. Vapor formation depends on absolute pressure relative to vapor pressure.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溢洪面汽蝕指標」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Spillway cavitation indicator\" is correct?","options":["高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。","所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償"],"optionsEn":["High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities.","One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":33},{"id":"b202-v15-22","title":"溢洪面汽蝕指標：定量估算","titleEn":"Spillway cavitation indicator: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「溢洪面汽蝕指標」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Spillway cavitation indicator” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。模型邊界：使用局部平均絕對壓力；未給臨界汽蝕數或損傷速率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264. Model boundary: uses local mean absolute pressure; no critical cavitation value or erosion rate is supplied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對壓力感測器是表壓還是絕對壓，並量測水溫以選取蒸氣壓。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm whether the sensor reports gauge or absolute pressure and measure water temperature for vapor pressure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。模型邊界：使用局部平均絕對壓力；未給臨界汽蝕數或損傷速率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264. Model boundary: uses local mean absolute pressure; no critical cavitation value or erosion rate is supplied.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溢洪面汽蝕指標」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Spillway cavitation indicator\", which statement holds?","options":["溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。","只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力"],"optionsEn":["Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.","Original hypothetical example.","Dam height alone determines the arch load share."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":34},{"id":"b202-v15-23","title":"溢洪面汽蝕指標：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Spillway cavitation indicator: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「溢洪面汽蝕指標」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Spillway cavitation indicator” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對壓力感測器是表壓還是絕對壓，並量測水溫以選取蒸氣壓。將壓力波動、表面缺口及含氣記錄對齊，若平均值平穩但瞬時低壓頻繁，應分析低尾分布，不能以平均汽蝕數排除損傷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm whether the sensor reports gauge or absolute pressure and measure water temperature for vapor pressure. Align pressure fluctuations with surface defects and aeration observations. Frequent low-pressure excursions require analysis of the lower distribution tail even if the mean cavitation number appears steady. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在固定壓力下把流速提高兩成，重算指標並說明平方效應，再列出判斷實際損傷還需的粗糙度、含氣與壓力波動證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase velocity by twenty percent at fixed pressure and recompute the indicator, explaining the squared effect. List roughness, aeration and pressure-fluctuation evidence still needed before assessing actual surface damage.","failure":"注意干擾：錯把表壓當絕對壓會嚴重改變指標，表面錯台又可能使局部最低壓遠低於平均值；若只看總流量，就無法區分幾何缺陷與通氣不足的來源。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing gauge with absolute pressure distorts the indicator, while a surface offset can make minimum pressure much lower than its mean. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對壓力感測器是表壓還是絕對壓，並量測水溫以選取蒸氣壓。將壓力波動、表面缺口及含氣記錄對齊，若平均值平穩但瞬時低壓頻繁，應分析低尾分布，不能以平均汽蝕數排除損傷。","textEn":"Confirm whether the sensor reports gauge or absolute pressure and measure water temperature for vapor pressure. Align pressure fluctuations with surface defects and aeration observations. Frequent low-pressure excursions require analysis of the lower distribution tail even if the mean cavitation number appears steady.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在固定壓力下把流速提高兩成，重算指標並說明平方效應，再列出判斷實際損傷還需的粗糙度、含氣與壓力波動證據。","textEn":"Increase velocity by twenty percent at fixed pressure and recompute the indicator, explaining the squared effect. List roughness, aeration and pressure-fluctuation evidence still needed before assessing actual surface damage.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溢洪面汽蝕指標」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Spillway cavitation indicator\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險","核對壓力感測器是表壓還是絕對壓，並量測水溫以選取蒸氣壓。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.","Confirm whether the sensor reports gauge or absolute pressure and measure water temperature for vapor pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對壓力感測器是表壓還是絕對壓，並量測水溫以選取蒸氣壓。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm whether the sensor reports gauge or absolute pressure and measure water temperature for vapor pressure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":35},{"id":"b202-v15-24","title":"溢洪面汽蝕指標：失效診斷","titleEn":"Spillway cavitation indicator: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「溢洪面汽蝕指標」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Spillway cavitation indicator” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯把表壓當絕對壓會嚴重改變指標，表面錯台又可能使局部最低壓遠低於平均值；若只看總流量，就無法區分幾何缺陷與通氣不足的來源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing gauge with absolute pressure distorts the indicator, while a surface offset can make minimum pressure much lower than its mean. Total discharge alone cannot distinguish a geometric defect from inadequate air supply as the cause of damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：蒸氣壓取決於水溫，而局部絕對壓也受大氣壓影響，兩者均應使用與事件同時的條件比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Vapor pressure depends on water temperature and absolute local pressure depends on atmospheric conditions; both should represent the same event rather than unrelated reference conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯把表壓當絕對壓會嚴重改變指標，表面錯台又可能使局部最低壓遠低於平均值；若只看總流量，就無法區分幾何缺陷與通氣不足的來源。","textEn":"Confusing gauge with absolute pressure distorts the indicator, while a surface offset can make minimum pressure much lower than its mean. Total discharge alone cannot distinguish a geometric defect from inadequate air supply as the cause of damage.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溢洪面汽蝕指標」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Spillway cavitation indicator\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["錯把表壓當絕對壓會嚴重改變指標，表面錯台又可能使局部最低壓遠低於平均值；若只看總流量，就無法區分幾何缺陷與通氣不足的來源。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償"],"optionsEn":["Confusing gauge with absolute pressure distorts the indicator, while a surface offset can make minimum pressure much lower than its mean.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯把表壓當絕對壓會嚴重改變指標，表面錯台又可能使局部最低壓遠低於平均值；若只看總流量，就無法區分幾何缺陷與通氣不足的來源。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing gauge with absolute pressure distorts the indicator, while a surface offset can make minimum pressure much lower than its mean. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":36}],"order":6},{"id":"b202-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「低水頭機組出力」與「沉積三角洲前移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Low head generating output\" and \"Sediment delta advance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b202-v15-25","title":"低水頭機組出力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low head generating output: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「低水頭機組出力」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low head generating output” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"庫水位下降使可用水頭改變，維持同一功率可能需要增加流量，但管路損失和機組運轉範圍限制這種補償。教材先固定流量與效率比較水頭對出力的直接作用，再要求用機組特性曲線檢查效率假設，不能線性外推至所有低水位。 導葉開度與流量的關係隨水頭改變，固定開度不等於固定流量，比較模型時必須明確哪一項受到控制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低水頭機組出力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Falling reservoir level changes available head, and maintaining power may require more discharge. Conveyance losses and the machine operating range limit that compensation. First hold flow and efficiency constant to isolate the direct head effect, then consult machine characteristics; the assumed efficiency cannot be extrapolated to every low-water condition. The relation between guide-vane opening and discharge changes with head; fixed opening is not fixed flow, so the controlled quantity must be stated explicitly. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low head generating output” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低水頭機組出力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low head generating output”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-25-k1","title":"低水頭機組出力","titleEn":"Low head generating output","text":"庫水位下降使可用水頭改變，維持同一功率可能需要增加流量，但管路損失和機組運轉範圍限制這種補償。教材先固定流量與效率比較水頭對出力的直接作用，再要求用機組特性曲線檢查效率假設，不能線性外推至所有低水位。","textEn":"Falling reservoir level changes available head, and maintaining power may require more discharge. Conveyance losses and the machine operating range limit that compensation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低水頭機組出力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low head generating output\" is correct?","options":["低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償","庫水位下降使可用水頭改變，維持同一功率可能需要增加流量，但管路損失和機組運轉範圍限制這種補償。","岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離"],"optionsEn":["Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge.","Falling reservoir level changes available head, and maintaining power may require more discharge.","Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front."],"answer":1,"explanation":"庫水位下降使可用水頭改變，維持同一功率可能需要增加流量，但管路損失和機組運轉範圍限制這種補償。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Falling reservoir level changes available head, and maintaining power may require more discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":37},{"id":"b202-v15-26","title":"低水頭機組出力：定量估算","titleEn":"Low head generating output: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低水頭機組出力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low head generating output” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW。模型邊界：淨水頭已扣引水損失且效率固定；未保證機組在該工況允許運行。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW. Model boundary: net head already excludes conveyance loss and efficiency is fixed; operation at this point is not thereby authorized. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將同步流量、淨水頭與電功率換算成效率，並按導葉開度分類比較，避免把不同工況混成一條趨勢。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calculate efficiency from synchronized discharge, net head and terminal power, grouping observations by guide-vane position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW。模型邊界：淨水頭已扣引水損失且效率固定；未保證機組在該工況允許運行。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW. Model boundary: net head already excludes conveyance loss and efficiency is fixed; operation at this point is not thereby authorized.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低水頭機組出力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low head generating output\", which statement holds?","options":["每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援","只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW。"],"optionsEn":["Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.","Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.","Original hypothetical example."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=180 m3/s; H=70 m; eta=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*H*eta/1e6=111.2454 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":38},{"id":"b202-v15-27","title":"低水頭機組出力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low head generating output: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低水頭機組出力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low head generating output” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將同步流量、淨水頭與電功率換算成效率，並按導葉開度分類比較，避免把不同工況混成一條趨勢。另查振動與壓力脈動，若功率模型符合而脈動增大，仍須研究運轉區域限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calculate efficiency from synchronized discharge, net head and terminal power, grouping observations by guide-vane position. Check vibration and pressure pulsation separately. Agreement with the power equation does not resolve an increasing pulsation level or establish suitability of that operating region. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以相同效率計算恢復原功率所需流量，再加入與流量平方相關的損失重算，繪出補償效果遞減的原因並列出機組曲線的必要資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate the discharge needed to restore original power at fixed efficiency, then introduce flow-squared losses. Show why compensation diminishes and list the machine-curve data required to assess the revised point.","failure":"注意干擾：為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將同步流量、淨水頭與電功率換算成效率，並按導葉開度分類比較，避免把不同工況混成一條趨勢。另查振動與壓力脈動，若功率模型符合而脈動增大，仍須研究運轉區域限制。","textEn":"Calculate efficiency from synchronized discharge, net head and terminal power, grouping observations by guide-vane position. Check vibration and pressure pulsation separately. Agreement with the power equation does not resolve an increasing pulsation level or establish suitability of that operating region.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以相同效率計算恢復原功率所需流量，再加入與流量平方相關的損失重算，繪出補償效果遞減的原因並列出機組曲線的必要資料。","textEn":"Calculate the discharge needed to restore original power at fixed efficiency, then introduce flow-squared losses. Show why compensation diminishes and list the machine-curve data required to assess the revised point.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低水頭機組出力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low head generating output\"?","options":["將同步流量、淨水頭與電功率換算成效率，並按導葉開度分類比較，避免把不同工況混成一條趨勢。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量"],"optionsEn":["Calculate efficiency from synchronized discharge, net head and terminal power, grouping observations by guide-vane position.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將同步流量、淨水頭與電功率換算成效率，並按導葉開度分類比較，避免把不同工況混成一條趨勢。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calculate efficiency from synchronized discharge, net head and terminal power, grouping observations by guide-vane position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":39},{"id":"b202-v15-28","title":"低水頭機組出力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low head generating output: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低水頭機組出力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low head generating output” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain. A meter affected by altered flow patterns can also indicate a false efficiency improvement, requiring independent verification. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：導葉開度與流量的關係隨水頭改變，固定開度不等於固定流量，比較模型時必須明確哪一項受到控制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The relation between guide-vane opening and discharge changes with head; fixed opening is not fixed flow, so the controlled quantity must be stated explicitly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。","textEn":"Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain. A meter affected by altered flow patterns can also indicate a false efficiency improvement, requiring independent verification.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低水頭機組出力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low head generating output\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。","岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain.","Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":40},{"id":"b202-v15-29","title":"沉積三角洲前移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment delta advance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「沉積三角洲前移」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment delta advance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"入庫流速降低使較粗顆粒優先沉降，三角洲前緣位置影響取水與通道幾何。簡化的體積除以橫截面積只能估算平均前移距離，不能描述底坡、粒徑分選及潛流。應把泥砂供給與可容納空間分開，避免把局部淤高等同全庫均勻填滿。 沉積前緣可能沿舊河槽形成狹長分支，使用全庫平均寬度會稀釋這種集中前移，需要保留局部地形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積三角洲前移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deceleration at reservoir entry deposits coarse material preferentially, and delta position affects intake and channel geometry. Deposited volume divided by a representative cross-sectional area estimates mean advance only; it omits bed slope, sorting and density currents. Sediment supply and accommodation space must be distinguished from uniform filling of the reservoir. A depositional front may advance as a narrow lobe along the old channel; reservoir-average width conceals that concentration and should not replace local geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment delta advance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉積三角洲前移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment delta advance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-29-k1","title":"沉積三角洲前移","titleEn":"Sediment delta advance","text":"入庫流速降低使較粗顆粒優先沉降，三角洲前緣位置影響取水與通道幾何。簡化的體積除以橫截面積只能估算平均前移距離，不能描述底坡、粒徑分選及潛流。","textEn":"Deceleration at reservoir entry deposits coarse material preferentially, and delta position affects intake and channel geometry. Deposited volume divided by a representative cross-sectional area estimates mean advance only; it omits bed slope, sorting and density currents.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉積三角洲前移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment delta advance\" is correct?","options":["岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離","溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移","入庫流速降低使較粗顆粒優先沉降，三角洲前緣位置影響取水與通道幾何。"],"optionsEn":["Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.","Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.","Deceleration at reservoir entry deposits coarse material preferentially, and delta position affects intake and channel geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"入庫流速降低使較粗顆粒優先沉降，三角洲前緣位置影響取水與通道幾何。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deceleration at reservoir entry deposits coarse material preferentially, and delta position affects intake and channel geometry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":41},{"id":"b202-v15-30","title":"沉積三角洲前移：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment delta advance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉積三角洲前移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment delta advance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。模型邊界：假設矩形沉積前緣且全數體積推進前緣；不含壓密及側向擴展。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m. Model boundary: rectangular depositional front with all volume advancing that front; excludes consolidation and lateral spreading. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重複測量同一基準的縱剖面及橫斷面，將前緣位置、頂積層厚度與粒徑一起比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat longitudinal and cross-sectional surveys on one datum, comparing front position, topset thickness and grain size.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。模型邊界：假設矩形沉積前緣且全數體積推進前緣；不含壓密及側向擴展。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m. Model boundary: rectangular depositional front with all volume advancing that front; excludes consolidation and lateral spreading.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉積三角洲前移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment delta advance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。","只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力","平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m.","Dam height alone determines the arch load share.","Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":42},{"id":"b202-v15-31","title":"沉積三角洲前移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment delta advance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉積三角洲前移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment delta advance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重複測量同一基準的縱剖面及橫斷面，將前緣位置、頂積層厚度與粒徑一起比較。若測得體積增加但前緣未動，應查垂向加積或側向展寬，不能因簡式預測前移便宣稱測量錯誤。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat longitudinal and cross-sectional surveys on one datum, comparing front position, topset thickness and grain size. If volume rises without front advance, investigate vertical aggradation or lateral widening rather than rejecting measurements because the simple translation model predicted movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持沉積體積不變，分別加倍前緣寬度與厚度，計算前移距離，再規劃足以分辨前移和垂向加積的三條重複測線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep deposited volume fixed and separately double front width and thickness. Calculate advance distances, then plan three repeat survey lines that distinguish frontal translation from vertical accumulation.","failure":"注意干擾：只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重複測量同一基準的縱剖面及橫斷面，將前緣位置、頂積層厚度與粒徑一起比較。若測得體積增加但前緣未動，應查垂向加積或側向展寬，不能因簡式預測前移便宣稱測量錯誤。","textEn":"Repeat longitudinal and cross-sectional surveys on one datum, comparing front position, topset thickness and grain size. If volume rises without front advance, investigate vertical aggradation or lateral widening rather than rejecting measurements because the simple translation model predicted movement.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持沉積體積不變，分別加倍前緣寬度與厚度，計算前移距離，再規劃足以分辨前移和垂向加積的三條重複測線。","textEn":"Keep deposited volume fixed and separately double front width and thickness. Calculate advance distances, then plan three repeat survey lines that distinguish frontal translation from vertical accumulation.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉積三角洲前移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment delta advance\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","重複測量同一基準的縱剖面及橫斷面，將前緣位置、頂積層厚度與粒徑一起比較。","首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Repeat longitudinal and cross-sectional surveys on one datum, comparing front position, topset thickness and grain size.","The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重複測量同一基準的縱剖面及橫斷面，將前緣位置、頂積層厚度與粒徑一起比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat longitudinal and cross-sectional surveys on one datum, comparing front position, topset thickness and grain size. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":43},{"id":"b202-v15-32","title":"沉積三角洲前移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment delta advance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉積三角洲前移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment delta advance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. Conversely, level-driven shoreline movement may be mistaken for deposition; submerged topography referenced to a fixed elevation is needed to distinguish them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：沉積前緣可能沿舊河槽形成狹長分支，使用全庫平均寬度會稀釋這種集中前移，需要保留局部地形。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A depositional front may advance as a narrow lobe along the old channel; reservoir-average width conceals that concentration and should not replace local geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。","textEn":"Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. Conversely, level-driven shoreline movement may be mistaken for deposition; submerged topography referenced to a fixed elevation is needed to distinguish them.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉積三角洲前移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment delta advance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移","只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.","Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":44}],"order":7},{"id":"b202-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「垂線監測溫漂」與「排水備援共同原因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift\" and \"Drainage redundancy common causes\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b202-v15-33","title":"垂線監測溫漂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「垂線監測溫漂」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"垂線觀測相對位置時，量測支架與讀數裝置也會受到溫度影響。把已校準的儀器溫度係數乘溫差，可估算需扣除的儀器漂移，但不能順便移除壩體真正熱變形。兩種效應必須以獨立基準、內部溫度與不同原理位移儀共同辨識。 溫漂係數具有量測軸向與安裝條件，儀器移位或更換支架後須重新檢查，不能沿用舊校準而未記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂線監測溫漂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pendulum observations include temperature effects in mounting and readout hardware as well as movement of the structure. A calibrated instrument coefficient estimates instrumental drift, but must not remove genuine thermal deformation of the dam. Independent reference control, internal temperature and another displacement principle are needed to separate the effects. A drift coefficient belongs to a measurement axis and mounting arrangement; relocation or replacement of the support requires renewed checks and documented calibration continuity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「垂線監測溫漂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-33-k1","title":"垂線監測溫漂","titleEn":"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift","text":"垂線觀測相對位置時，量測支架與讀數裝置也會受到溫度影響。把已校準的儀器溫度係數乘溫差，可估算需扣除的儀器漂移，但不能順便移除壩體真正熱變形。","textEn":"Pendulum observations include temperature effects in mounting and readout hardware as well as movement of the structure. A calibrated instrument coefficient estimates instrumental drift, but must not remove genuine thermal deformation of the dam.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂線監測溫漂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift\" is correct?","options":["垂線觀測相對位置時，量測支架與讀數裝置也會受到溫度影響。","溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移","每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援"],"optionsEn":["Pendulum observations include temperature effects in mounting and readout hardware as well as movement of the structure.","Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.","Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup."],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂線觀測相對位置時，量測支架與讀數裝置也會受到溫度影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pendulum observations include temperature effects in mounting and readout hardware as well as movement of the structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":45},{"id":"b202-v15-34","title":"垂線監測溫漂：定量估算","titleEn":"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂線監測溫漂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm。模型邊界：儀器漂移係數由獨立校準取得且線性；未扣除壩體物理熱位移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm. Model boundary: instrument drift coefficient comes from independent linear calibration; actual thermal movement of the dam is not removed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在儀器不移動的控制條件下校準溫度係數，再用現地獨立測量檢查修正後殘差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate temperature sensitivity under controlled fixed-position conditions, then compare corrected residuals with independent field observations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm。模型邊界：儀器漂移係數由獨立校準取得且線性；未扣除壩體物理熱位移。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm. Model boundary: instrument drift coefficient comes from independent linear calibration; actual thermal movement of the dam is not removed.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂線監測溫漂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift\", which statement holds?","options":["只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm。","自由熱伸長就是受約束接縫閉合量"],"optionsEn":["Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm.","Free thermal extension equals closure of a restrained joint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: yraw=4.8 mm; k=0.04 mm/K; dT=15 K; ycorr=yraw-k*dT=4.2 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":46},{"id":"b202-v15-35","title":"垂線監測溫漂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂線監測溫漂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在儀器不移動的控制條件下校準溫度係數，再用現地獨立測量檢查修正後殘差。若季節訊號在不同原理儀器都出現，不應全部當成儀器漂移；並記錄更換支架前後的零點差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate temperature sensitivity under controlled fixed-position conditions, then compare corrected residuals with independent field observations. Seasonal signals shared by different instrument principles should not all be removed as drift. Record zero shifts before and after replacement of mounting components as a separate effect. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：產生同時含壩體季節位移和儀器溫漂的序列，分別用獨立係數及錯誤回歸係數校正，展示兩種方法對異常偵測的不同結果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Generate a series containing structural seasonal movement and instrument thermal drift. Correct it using an independent calibration and an incorrect regression coefficient, then demonstrate how the two approaches alter anomaly detection.","failure":"注意干擾：用壩體量測本身回歸儀器溫度係數，可能把真正結構反應吸收到校正項而掩蓋變化；固定端鬆動則可能造成非線性跳值，線性溫漂公式無法修復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Regressing instrument sensitivity from dam movement itself can absorb genuine structural behavior into a correction term and conceal changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在儀器不移動的控制條件下校準溫度係數，再用現地獨立測量檢查修正後殘差。若季節訊號在不同原理儀器都出現，不應全部當成儀器漂移；並記錄更換支架前後的零點差。","textEn":"Calibrate temperature sensitivity under controlled fixed-position conditions, then compare corrected residuals with independent field observations. Seasonal signals shared by different instrument principles should not all be removed as drift. Record zero shifts before and after replacement of mounting components as a separate effect.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"產生同時含壩體季節位移和儀器溫漂的序列，分別用獨立係數及錯誤回歸係數校正，展示兩種方法對異常偵測的不同結果。","textEn":"Generate a series containing structural seasonal movement and instrument thermal drift. Correct it using an independent calibration and an incorrect regression coefficient, then demonstrate how the two approaches alter anomaly detection.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂線監測溫漂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線","在儀器不移動的控制條件下校準溫度係數，再用現地獨立測量檢查修正後殘差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.","Calibrate temperature sensitivity under controlled fixed-position conditions, then compare corrected residuals with independent field observations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在儀器不移動的控制條件下校準溫度係數，再用現地獨立測量檢查修正後殘差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate temperature sensitivity under controlled fixed-position conditions, then compare corrected residuals with independent field observations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":47},{"id":"b202-v15-36","title":"垂線監測溫漂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂線監測溫漂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用壩體量測本身回歸儀器溫度係數，可能把真正結構反應吸收到校正項而掩蓋變化；固定端鬆動則可能造成非線性跳值，線性溫漂公式無法修復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Regressing instrument sensitivity from dam movement itself can absorb genuine structural behavior into a correction term and conceal changes. A loose mounting point can cause nonlinear jumps that a linear thermal-drift equation cannot repair. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：溫漂係數具有量測軸向與安裝條件，儀器移位或更換支架後須重新檢查，不能沿用舊校準而未記錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A drift coefficient belongs to a measurement axis and mounting arrangement; relocation or replacement of the support requires renewed checks and documented calibration continuity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「溫漂校正應消除所有壩體季節位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thermal drift correction should remove all seasonal movement of the dam.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用壩體量測本身回歸儀器溫度係數，可能把真正結構反應吸收到校正項而掩蓋變化；固定端鬆動則可能造成非線性跳值，線性溫漂公式無法修復。","textEn":"Regressing instrument sensitivity from dam movement itself can absorb genuine structural behavior into a correction term and conceal changes. A loose mounting point can cause nonlinear jumps that a linear thermal-drift equation cannot repair.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂線監測溫漂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pendulum monitoring thermal drift\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用壩體量測本身回歸儀器溫度係數，可能把真正結構反應吸收到校正項而掩蓋變化；固定端鬆動則可能造成非線性跳值，線性溫漂公式無法修復。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援"],"optionsEn":["Regressing instrument sensitivity from dam movement itself can absorb genuine structural behavior into a correction term and conceal changes.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用壩體量測本身回歸儀器溫度係數，可能把真正結構反應吸收到校正項而掩蓋變化；固定端鬆動則可能造成非線性跳值，線性溫漂公式無法修復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Regressing instrument sensitivity from dam movement itself can absorb genuine structural behavior into a correction term and conceal changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":48},{"id":"b202-v15-37","title":"排水備援共同原因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drainage redundancy common causes: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「排水備援共同原因」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drainage redundancy common causes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"備援只有在失效機制足夠獨立時才能降低同時失效機率。兩部泵可能共用電源、進水池或控制器，因此把單機失效機率直接相乘會過度樂觀。教材先建立明示獨立的基準，再加入共同原因事件，強調可靠度數值取決於系統邊界與資料期間。 故障機率須附需求期間與成功功能定義，短時啟動成功與長時持續抽水成功是兩個不同的事件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水備援共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Redundancy reduces simultaneous failure only when failure mechanisms are sufficiently independent. Two pumps may share power, a sump or controls, making a simple product of individual probabilities optimistic. Establish an explicitly independent baseline before adding a common-cause event, and define the system boundary and observation period for every probability. A probability needs a demand interval and a defined success function; successful starting and sustained pumping throughout a long event are different reliability questions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drainage redundancy common causes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012.","failure":"常見誤解：「每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水備援共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drainage redundancy common causes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-37-k1","title":"排水備援共同原因","titleEn":"Drainage redundancy common causes","text":"備援只有在失效機制足夠獨立時才能降低同時失效機率。兩部泵可能共用電源、進水池或控制器，因此把單機失效機率直接相乘會過度樂觀。","textEn":"Redundancy reduces simultaneous failure only when failure mechanisms are sufficiently independent. Two pumps may share power, a sump or controls, making a simple product of individual probabilities optimistic.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水備援共同原因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drainage redundancy common causes\" is correct?","options":["每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援","備援只有在失效機制足夠獨立時才能降低同時失效機率。","只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力"],"optionsEn":["Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.","Redundancy reduces simultaneous failure only when failure mechanisms are sufficiently independent.","Dam height alone determines the arch load share."],"answer":1,"explanation":"備援只有在失效機制足夠獨立時才能降低同時失效機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Redundancy reduces simultaneous failure only when failure mechanisms are sufficiently independent. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":49},{"id":"b202-v15-38","title":"排水備援共同原因：定量估算","titleEn":"Drainage redundancy common causes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水備援共同原因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drainage redundancy common causes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。模型邊界：兩泵同一需求期間的失效事件假設獨立；不是現場可靠度或年失效率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012. Model boundary: independent failure events over the same demand interval; not field reliability or an annual failure rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。模型邊界：兩泵同一需求期間的失效事件假設獨立；不是現場可靠度或年失效率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012. Model boundary: independent failure events over the same demand interval; not field reliability or an annual failure rate.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水備援共同原因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drainage redundancy common causes\", which statement holds?","options":["平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險","首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力","原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.","The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.","Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":50},{"id":"b202-v15-39","title":"排水備援共同原因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage redundancy common causes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水備援共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drainage redundancy common causes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。把無需求時停機與有需求時失效分開統計；若兩泵常在同一事件失效，就不能保留獨立假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer. Distinguish planned idle states from failures on demand. Repeated simultaneous failures during one event invalidate the independence assumption used by the simple probability product. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加入一個共同電源失效事件，畫故障樹並計算條件機率，指出何種改造可切斷共同原因，以及需要哪些需求紀錄才能更新估計。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a common power-failure event, draw a fault tree and calculate conditional probabilities. Identify a modification that removes the shared cause and the demand records needed to update the estimate.","failure":"注意干擾：淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。把無需求時停機與有需求時失效分開統計；若兩泵常在同一事件失效，就不能保留獨立假設。","textEn":"Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer. Distinguish planned idle states from failures on demand. Repeated simultaneous failures during one event invalidate the independence assumption used by the simple probability product.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加入一個共同電源失效事件，畫故障樹並計算條件機率，指出何種改造可切斷共同原因，以及需要哪些需求紀錄才能更新估計。","textEn":"Add a common power-failure event, draw a fault tree and calculate conditional probabilities. Identify a modification that removes the shared cause and the demand records needed to update the estimate.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水備援共同原因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drainage redundancy common causes\"?","options":["用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償"],"optionsEn":["Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":51},{"id":"b202-v15-40","title":"排水備援共同原因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drainage redundancy common causes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"],"prerequisiteIds":["b202-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水備援共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drainage redundancy common causes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. Testing unloaded motor starts does not reveal a blocked common intake, so the actual drainage path and electrical separation must be verified together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：故障機率須附需求期間與成功功能定義，短時啟動成功與長時持續抽水成功是兩個不同的事件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A probability needs a demand interval and a defined success function; successful starting and sustained pumping throughout a long event are different reliability questions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b202-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。","textEn":"Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. Testing unloaded motor starts does not reveal a blocked common intake, so the actual drainage path and electrical separation must be verified together.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]},{"id":"b202-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v6-hoover-dam","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usbr-instruments","v15s-usace-catalog"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水備援共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drainage redundancy common causes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。","只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy.","Dam height alone determines the arch load share."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":52}],"order":8}],"title":"胡佛壩","titleEn":"Hoover Dam","summary":"以導流、大體積混凝土、壩基及洩流系統理解大型壩工的工序依賴與證據。","summaryEn":"Understand dependencies and evidence in large-dam engineering through diversion, mass concrete, foundations and water-release systems.","scope":"以公開資料建立的原創教學分解；所有步驟為紙上、數位模型與證據判讀練習。自繪的示意與自設資料必須標示假設；本站未提供現地工程資料，亦不是核准施工、設備操作或水質放行程序。","scopeEn":"Original educational decomposition of public information. Every step is a paper, digital-model or evidence-interpretation exercise. Label assumptions in self-drawn diagrams and invented data; this site does not supply field engineering records or approved construction, operating or water-release procedures.","diagram":{"type":"dam","labels":["河谷與基岩","壩體","進水與壓力管","溢洪道","監測"],"labelsEn":["Canyon and rock","Dam body","Intake and penstocks","Spillways","Monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":52,"estimatedMinutes":1240,"curriculumVersion":6,"enrichmentVersion":15,"learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","v15Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["拱座相容與分力","Abutment compatibility and load sharing"],["混凝土冷卻熱量","Concrete cooling heat account"],["壓力鋼管水錘","Penstock water hammer"],["低水頭機組出力","Low head generating output"],["排水備援共同原因","Drainage redundancy common causes"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]]},"v15Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為本課原創情境串接，所有數值是假設，不能視為業主設計圖或操作許可。先完成「拱座相容與分力」的守恆與邊界檢核，再比較「裂縫連通與揚壓」及「混凝土冷卻熱量」的不同控制量。第一組計算為 ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN；第二組為 pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。學員須保留量綱、資料時間與量測位置，討論誤差如何傳到結果，將第三單元的限制寫入同一張決策表。任何未納入的結構、河道或機組耦合都列為下一階段工作，不由單一得數推論全工程安全。","textEn":"This original sequence connects the first three units using assumed inputs; none is an owner drawing or an operating authorization. First establish conservation and boundaries for Abutment compatibility and load sharing, then compare the controlling variables in Crack connectivity and uplift and Concrete cooling heat account. The first calculation is ka=8 GN/m; kg=12 GN/m; F=100 MN; Fa=F*ka/(ka+kg)=40 MN; the second is pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN. Preserve dimensions, observation times, and measurement locations in the working sheet. Explain how input uncertainty changes each conclusion and include the third unit limitations in the same decision table. Structural, river, and machine interactions omitted by a model remain subsequent work; a single numerical answer cannot demonstrate safety of the complete project.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"拱重力壩熱力水力與監測交互診斷","focusEn":"Arch gravity dam thermal hydraulic and monitoring diagnosis"}},{"id":"b301","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-route-safety","v6-thsr-disaster"],"stages":[{"id":"b301-stage01","order":1,"steps":[{"id":"b301-v6-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-route-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"建立高鐵系統邊界","titleEn":"Map high-speed-rail system boundaries","objective":"分開土建、軌道、供電、車輛、控制及營運介面。","objectiveEn":"Separate civil, track, power, vehicle, control and operations interfaces.","instruction":"畫出土建承托軌道、軌道導引車輛的主鏈，再加供電與控制連到車輛。以不同箭頭表示力、能量與資訊，為每種介面列一項驗證問題。","instructionEn":"Draw civil support to track to vehicle, then connect power and control to the vehicle. Use distinct arrows for force, energy and information, with one verification question per interface.","observation":"觀察車輛能運轉是否仍不足以證明軌道與控制整合已完成。","observationEn":"Recognize that a moving train alone does not establish completed track and control integration.","failure":"把高鐵等同於一列高速列車，省略路線與控制條件。","failureEn":"Equating a high-speed railway with a fast train while omitting route and control conditions.","check":"六個子系統都有介面，且箭頭的物理意義清楚。","checkEn":"Connect all six subsystems and explain the physical meaning of each arrow.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-01-k1","title":"跨專業系統","titleEn":"Multidiscipline system","text":"高速運行取決於車輛與路線、供電、控制及營運的一致性。","textEn":"High-speed operation depends on compatibility among vehicles, route, power, control and operations."},{"id":"b301-v6-01-k2","title":"不同傳遞量","titleEn":"Different transferred quantities","text":"力、電能與控制資訊需要不同驗證，不能用同一箭頭含糊表示。","textEn":"Force, electrical energy and control information require different verification and should not share an ambiguous arrow."}],"quiz":{"options":["與路線動態及控制系統相容","列車靜態寬度已被量測","尺寸文件有可比對的幾何內容"],"optionsEn":["Compatibility with route dynamics and control","That static train width was measured","That the dimensional record contains comparable geometry"],"answer":0,"question":"列車靜態尺寸合格，還不能單獨證明哪件事？","questionEn":"A train meets static dimensional requirements. What does that not establish by itself?","explanation":"靜態幾何只是整合條件的一部分，仍需動態與控制證據。","explanationEn":"Static geometry is only part of integration; dynamic and control evidence remains necessary."}},{"id":"b301-v6-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-01"],"title":"比較曲線與行車需求","titleEn":"Compare alignment curves and service needs","objective":"理解速度、曲線與舒適性的相互約束。","objectiveEn":"Understand relationships among speed, curvature and ride requirements.","instruction":"自繪直線、緩和曲線與圓曲線的概念路線，標出方向變化。比較兩種示意速度下需要關注的橫向反應，不指定實線設計半徑或超高。","instructionEn":"Sketch straight, transition and circular alignment sections, marking direction changes. Compare lateral-response concerns at two illustrative speeds without assigning real design radius or cant.","observation":"觀察平面方向平順，是否仍有垂向坡度或接續問題。","observationEn":"Check whether a smooth plan alignment still leaves vertical-gradient or transition issues.","failure":"只看列車最高速度，就認定所有曲線都能以同速通過。","failureEn":"Assuming every curve supports a train’s maximum rated speed.","check":"交付平面及縱向問題各一項，說明缺少的驗證資料。","checkEn":"Provide one plan and one vertical-profile question with missing verification data.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-02-k1","title":"速度與曲率","titleEn":"Speed and curvature","text":"橫向運動反應取決於速度與曲率的組合，而非車輛標稱速度。","textEn":"Lateral motion depends on the combination of speed and curvature, not the vehicle’s rated speed alone."},{"id":"b301-v6-02-k2","title":"平順接續","titleEn":"Smooth transitions","text":"方向或坡度變化需要連續性考量，不能只把直線片段接起來。","textEn":"Direction and gradient changes require continuity considerations rather than simply joining straight segments."}],"quiz":{"options":["車輛靜態長度是否自行縮短","橫向動態反應與舒適性如何改變","既有曲線的幾何是否因速度而自動改變"],"optionsEn":["Whether static vehicle length automatically shortens","How lateral response and comfort change","Whether curve geometry automatically changes with speed"],"answer":1,"question":"同一曲線提高示意速度時，最合理的研究問題是什麼？","questionEn":"If illustrative speed increases on the same curve, which question is most relevant?","explanation":"速度變動改變動態需求；不能假定幾何或車輛尺寸會自行補償。","explanationEn":"Changing speed alters dynamic demands; geometry and vehicle dimensions do not automatically compensate."}},{"id":"b301-v6-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-disaster"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-02"],"title":"追蹤地層下陷到軌道","titleEn":"Trace subsidence to track geometry","objective":"分辨均勻沉降與差異沉降的介面影響。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish interface effects of uniform and differential settlement.","instruction":"用同一條示意軌道畫均勻下降與局部下降兩種剖面。將地面觀測、橋墩位移與軌道高低資料列成三層，說明不能互相替代的理由。","instructionEn":"Draw uniform and localized settlement beneath the same illustrative track. Separate ground observations, pier movement and track levels into three evidence layers and explain their limits.","observation":"比較總沉降相近的兩例，局部坡折是否不同。","observationEn":"Compare local gradient changes in examples with similar total settlement.","failure":"以沿線平均沉降值代表所有局部軌道變化。","failureEn":"Using average line-wide settlement to represent every local track change.","check":"指出最需補充局部量測的位置，並維持共同高程基準。","checkEn":"Identify locations needing local measurements and retain a common elevation datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-03-k1","title":"差異變形","titleEn":"Differential movement","text":"鄰近支承的相對變形會影響幾何連續性，不能只看平均值。","textEn":"Relative movement of neighboring supports affects geometric continuity and is not captured by an average."},{"id":"b301-v6-03-k2","title":"跨層證據","titleEn":"Evidence across levels","text":"地盤、土建與軌道的反應需對齊位置和時間才可比較。","textEn":"Ground, civil and track responses must share location and time references to be compared."}],"quiz":{"options":["所有支承一起均勻下降的一段必定較差","僅憑總沉降即可判定兩者完全相同","沉降集中在短距離內的一段"],"optionsEn":["The uniformly settling section must be worse","Total settlement alone proves the sections identical","The section where settlement is concentrated over a short distance"],"answer":2,"question":"兩段總沉降相同，哪段仍可能有較大的幾何變化？","questionEn":"Two sections have equal total settlement. Which may still have greater geometric change?","explanation":"沉降的空間分布會改變坡度與曲率，即使總量相同。","explanationEn":"Spatial distribution changes slope and curvature even when total settlement is equal."}},{"id":"b301-v6-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-disaster"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-03"],"title":"檢查橋梁與軌道支承介面","titleEn":"Review bridge–track support interfaces","objective":"把預鑄構件交接連到軌道幾何基準。","objectiveEn":"Connect precast-member handover to track-geometry references.","instruction":"以自繪高架橋分開橋墩、支承、梁體與軌道層，標出縱向伸縮和量測基準。列出梁體就位後，軌道專業仍需取得的幾何與狀態資料。","instructionEn":"Separate piers, bearings, girders and track layers in a viaduct sketch. Mark longitudinal movement and survey references; list geometry and state records needed by the track team after girder placement.","observation":"注意梁體就位合格不等於軌道精度與長期位移已被驗證。","observationEn":"Accepted girder placement does not establish track precision or long-term movement behavior.","failure":"將橋梁竣工標高直接當成最終鋼軌標高，忽略中間構造。","failureEn":"Treating bridge as-built level as final rail level while omitting intermediate layers.","check":"完成土建到軌道的介面表，至少含基準、可動方向與待補資料。","checkEn":"Complete a civil-to-track interface sheet including reference, movement direction and missing records.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-04-k1","title":"層間累積","titleEn":"Layer accumulation","text":"各層厚度、調整與變形共同決定鋼軌最終幾何。","textEn":"Layer thickness, adjustment and deformation together determine final rail geometry."},{"id":"b301-v6-04-k2","title":"可動支承","titleEn":"Movable supports","text":"設計允許的伸縮與需要限制的位移，應在模型中分清。","textEn":"Intended movement and movement that must be restrained should be distinguished in the model."}],"quiz":{"options":["中間層與調整量共同決定軌面位置","梁頂標高與軌面必定相同","軌道幾何與土建從不互相影響"],"optionsEn":["Intermediate layers and adjustments determine rail position","Girder-top and rail elevations are necessarily identical","Track geometry and civil works never interact"],"answer":0,"question":"梁頂標高正確，為何還需軌道層交接資料？","questionEn":"Why are track-layer records needed even if girder-top elevation is correct?","explanation":"交接要追蹤完整尺寸鏈，而不是只驗證其中一層。","explanationEn":"Handover must trace the full dimensional chain, not only one layer."}}],"title":"路線與土建介面","titleEn":"Alignment and civil interfaces","description":"將路線幾何、地盤與橋梁條件連到軌道需求。","descriptionEn":"Connect alignment, ground and bridge conditions to track requirements."},{"id":"b301-stage02","order":2,"steps":[{"id":"b301-v6-05","sequence":5,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-04"],"title":"比較軌道形式及轉換區","titleEn":"Compare track forms and transition zones","objective":"理解不同軌道形式回應不同介面要求。","objectiveEn":"Understand how track forms respond to different interface needs.","instruction":"依探索館說明，整理版式軌道、道岔附近的配置和低振動軌道三種功能重點。畫兩種剛度不同的軌道相接，列出需量測的幾何與動態反應。","instructionEn":"Using the museum overview, compare slab-track, turnout-area and low-vibration functions. Sketch a transition between track forms of different stiffness and identify geometric and dynamic observations.","observation":"觀察靜態軌面平順是否仍可能有支承剛度變化。","observationEn":"Recognize that a smooth static rail profile can still cross a stiffness change.","failure":"把全線軌道假定為單一材料與單一剛度。","failureEn":"Assuming one material and stiffness for the entire line.","check":"比較表須有功能、支承差異及轉換區待驗證事項。","checkEn":"Include purpose, support differences and transition-zone verification needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-05-k1","title":"功能選型","titleEn":"Function-led selection","text":"道岔定位、一般正線與振動控制可能需要不同構造組合。","textEn":"Turnout positioning, ordinary main line and vibration control can require different structural arrangements."},{"id":"b301-v6-05-k2","title":"過渡反應","titleEn":"Transition response","text":"支承特性突變可影響輪軌互動，需與幾何一起檢查。","textEn":"Abrupt support-property changes can affect wheel–rail interaction and should be examined with geometry."}],"quiz":{"options":["有，軌頂相同即代表剛度相同","沒有，支承特性與動態反應仍需證據","只要列車靜止不晃就已足夠"],"optionsEn":["Yes; equal rail elevation means equal stiffness","No; support properties and dynamic response still need evidence","A stationary train not rocking is sufficient"],"answer":1,"question":"兩段軌頂高程相同，是否已證明轉換區動態相容？","questionEn":"Two sections have equal rail elevation. Does that prove dynamic compatibility at the transition?","explanation":"高程只描述幾何的一部分，無法取代動態介面檢核。","explanationEn":"Elevation describes only part of geometry and does not replace dynamic interface review."}},{"id":"b301-v6-06","sequence":6,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-route-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-05"],"title":"分開道岔位置與路線確認","titleEn":"Separate turnout position from route confirmation","objective":"辨識機械位置、位置證據與通行授權。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish mechanical position, position evidence and movement authority.","instruction":"畫一個簡化分岔軌道，用不同符號表示移動部件、位置回報和控制狀態。寫出「位置未知」的桌上案例，說明為何不能只看遠景照片決定路線。","instructionEn":"Sketch a turnout with separate symbols for moving components, position indication and control state. Describe an unknown-position tabletop case and why a distant photograph cannot establish a route.","observation":"觀察部件看似靠妥與完整位置證據是否為不同層次。","observationEn":"Distinguish apparent mechanical closure from complete position evidence.","failure":"將目視位置直接等同於系統已確認且允許列車通行。","failureEn":"Equating visual position with system confirmation and authority to move.","check":"表格保留機械、檢知、控制三欄，未知狀態不得寫成已驗證。","checkEn":"Keep mechanical, detection and control columns separate; do not relabel unknown states as verified.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-06-k1","title":"證據鏈","titleEn":"Evidence chain","text":"幾何位置、檢知資訊和系統授權屬於不同介面。","textEn":"Physical position, detection information and system authority are different interfaces."},{"id":"b301-v6-06-k2","title":"未知狀態","titleEn":"Unknown state","text":"資料不足不是正常的同義詞，應保留為待查證。","textEn":"Insufficient information is not equivalent to normal operation and must remain unresolved."}],"quiz":{"options":["外觀可替代全部系統證據","可直接推論控制授權已成立","機械觀察已記錄，系統位置仍未驗證"],"optionsEn":["Appearance replaces all system evidence","Movement authority can be inferred directly","Mechanical observation recorded; system position unverified"],"answer":2,"question":"道岔外觀位置正確但位置回報未確認，最合適的課程記錄是什麼？","questionEn":"A turnout looks aligned but its position indication is unconfirmed. What is the best learning record?","explanation":"不同證據欄位不能互相冒充，未知應清楚留下。","explanationEn":"Different evidence fields are not interchangeable; unknowns must remain visible."}},{"id":"b301-v6-07","sequence":7,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-06"],"title":"建立集電與供電介面圖","titleEn":"Map current-collection and power interfaces","objective":"分辨供電存在與受電弓接觸品質。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish supply availability from pantograph contact quality.","instruction":"自繪變電、電車線、受電弓與車輛用電鏈，另加接觸幾何示意。以「有電但接觸不穩」假想例子列出電氣與機械兩類證據，不提供接近帶電設備的作業。","instructionEn":"Sketch supply, catenary, pantograph and vehicle demand, adding contact geometry. For an invented energized-but-unstable-contact case, list electrical and mechanical evidence without field work near live equipment.","observation":"比較上游供電量測與車上集電狀態能回答的不同問題。","observationEn":"Compare the questions answered by upstream supply readings and onboard collection observations.","failure":"看到上游電壓正常就排除所有集電介面問題。","failureEn":"Ruling out every collection-interface problem because upstream voltage is normal.","check":"每一個假說須連到電氣或機械證據，並註明位置與時間。","checkEn":"Link each hypothesis to electrical or mechanical evidence with location and time.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-07-k1","title":"機電接觸","titleEn":"Electromechanical contact","text":"集電同時是電能傳遞與運動接觸問題。","textEn":"Current collection involves both electrical transfer and moving mechanical contact."},{"id":"b301-v6-07-k2","title":"觀測位置","titleEn":"Observation location","text":"不同測點位於不同系統邊界，不能隨意互相替代。","textEn":"Measurements at different system boundaries cannot be substituted indiscriminately."}],"quiz":{"options":["該測點電壓在觀察期間穩定","受電弓全程接觸品質必定良好","所有車上負載均無異常"],"optionsEn":["Voltage at that location was stable during observation","Pantograph contact was necessarily good throughout","Every onboard load was fault-free"],"answer":0,"question":"上游電壓穩定能直接證明哪項？","questionEn":"What does stable upstream voltage directly establish?","explanation":"測量只能先支持其所在邊界與時間範圍內的結論。","explanationEn":"A measurement initially supports conclusions within its own location and time boundary."}},{"id":"b301-v6-08","sequence":8,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-route-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-07"],"title":"理解ATC速度防護證據","titleEn":"Interpret ATC speed-protection evidence","objective":"區分行車計畫、允許速度與實際速度。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish timetable intent, permitted speed and actual speed.","instruction":"自繪三條明確標成假想的曲線：計畫速度、允許速度、實際速度。找出實際速度接近或超出允許範圍的區域，說明需要防護而非只調整時刻表。","instructionEn":"Sketch explicitly fictional planned, permitted and actual speed curves. Identify where actual speed approaches or exceeds permission and explain the need for protection rather than merely changing the timetable.","observation":"觀察晚點與違反速度限制是不同問題。","observationEn":"Distinguish lateness from violation of a speed limit.","failure":"因列車晚點就把時刻表目標速度當成可突破的安全限制。","failureEn":"Treating a timetable target as permission to exceed a safety limit because the train is late.","check":"標示三種曲線的來源角色與一個資料不足的區段。","checkEn":"Identify the role behind each curve and one section with insufficient information.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-08-k1","title":"控制約束","titleEn":"Control constraints","text":"允許速度受前方路線與行車條件影響，不只取決於車輛能力。","textEn":"Permitted speed depends on route and traffic conditions, not only vehicle capability."},{"id":"b301-v6-08-k2","title":"安全與服務","titleEn":"Safety and service","text":"準點目標與防護約束不是同一層級的判斷。","textEn":"Punctuality objectives and protection constraints are different decision layers."}],"quiz":{"options":["計畫速度自動覆蓋允許速度","計畫需受當時允許範圍約束","只要實際速度低於車輛最高速度即可"],"optionsEn":["Planned speed automatically overrides permission","The plan remains constrained by current permission","Actual speed need only remain below vehicle maximum"],"answer":1,"question":"計畫速度高於當時允許速度，應如何解讀課程圖？","questionEn":"Planned speed exceeds current permitted speed. How should the diagram be interpreted?","explanation":"車輛能力與時刻表不能取代路線與行車防護條件。","explanationEn":"Vehicle capability and timetable goals do not replace route and traffic protection conditions."}}],"title":"軌道與機電整合","titleEn":"Track and electromechanical integration","description":"辨識軌道形式、道岔、集電與控制的不同證據。","descriptionEn":"Identify distinct evidence for track forms, turnouts, current collection and control."},{"id":"b301-stage03","order":3,"steps":[{"id":"b301-v6-09","sequence":9,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-disaster"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-08"],"title":"配對災害與偵測位置","titleEn":"Match hazards to detector locations","objective":"說明不同災害需要不同觀察量與布設邏輯。","objectiveEn":"Explain why hazards require different observables and siting logic.","instruction":"自繪隧道口、跨河橋、邊坡及一般路段，將落石、水位、地滑、風與地震觀察配到合理區域。為每一配對補一句不能保證偵測所有事件的理由。","instructionEn":"Sketch a portal, river bridge, slope and ordinary section. Assign rockfall, water level, slope movement, wind and earthquake observations, noting one limitation for each.","observation":"觀察單一感測器位置能代表的空間範圍是否有限。","observationEn":"Consider the spatial limits of any one detector location.","failure":"認定只要全線裝有同一類感測器，就能覆蓋所有災害。","failureEn":"Assuming one detector type across the line covers every hazard.","check":"完成至少四個「災害—位置—觀察量—盲點」配對。","checkEn":"Complete at least four hazard–location–observable–blind-spot mappings.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-09-k1","title":"需求導向偵測","titleEn":"Hazard-led detection","text":"偵測器選擇與位置應回應特定事件如何影響路線。","textEn":"Detector type and location should respond to how a particular event affects the route."},{"id":"b301-v6-09-k2","title":"覆蓋限制","titleEn":"Coverage limits","text":"沒有告警可能是未發生，也可能是超出覆蓋或設備狀態問題。","textEn":"No alarm may mean no event, an event outside coverage, or a device-state problem."}],"quiz":{"options":["遠方車站的室內溫度","其他路段道岔的位置回報","相關河段的水位與流況"],"optionsEn":["Indoor temperature at a distant station","Turnout indication in another section","Water level and flow conditions in the relevant reach"],"answer":2,"question":"跨河橋的洪水風險，哪個觀察最直接相關？","questionEn":"Which observation is most directly relevant to flooding at a river bridge?","explanation":"觀察量需對應災害機制與位置；不相關的正常訊號不能替代。","explanationEn":"Observables must match hazard mechanism and location; unrelated normal readings are no substitute."}},{"id":"b301-v6-10","sequence":10,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-disaster"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-09"],"title":"拆解地震後查證鏈","titleEn":"Decompose post-earthquake verification","objective":"區分告警、停止、檢查與恢復狀態。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish alarm, stop, inspection and restoration states.","instruction":"以紙上流程排列事件紀錄、影響區段、設施檢查、資料複核與授權交接。為每一節點寫出輸入證據與未完成時的標記，不填真實復駛速度或門檻。","instructionEn":"Arrange event records, affected sections, inspections, evidence review and authorization handover on paper. Name input evidence and incomplete-state labels without actual restart speeds or thresholds.","observation":"觀察地震訊號結束與設施已確認可用是否是不同時點。","observationEn":"Distinguish the end of shaking from confirmation that facilities are usable.","failure":"因感測器恢復正常，就省略受影響土建與軌道的查證。","failureEn":"Skipping civil and track checks because sensor readings have returned to normal.","check":"流程需顯示至少一個不能由感測器單獨證明的節點。","checkEn":"Show at least one stage that a sensor reading alone cannot verify.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-10-k1","title":"事件與狀態","titleEn":"Event versus condition","text":"告警描述事件或觀察；設施狀態仍需其他證據確認。","textEn":"An alarm describes an event or observation; facility condition requires additional evidence."},{"id":"b301-v6-10-k2","title":"分階段復核","titleEn":"Staged review","text":"停止、檢查與運行授權是不同責任，應各自留下紀錄。","textEn":"Stopping, inspection and operating authority are distinct responsibilities requiring records."}],"quiz":{"options":["不能，受影響設施與授權仍需查證","可以，事件結束等於設施無損","可以，只要列車沒有明顯外觀損傷"],"optionsEn":["No; affected facilities and authorization still require verification","Yes; an ended event means undamaged facilities","Yes, if trains show no visible damage"],"answer":0,"question":"地震波已停止，能否單憑此資訊判定全線可恢復？","questionEn":"Shaking has stopped. Does that alone establish line-wide readiness?","explanation":"事件停止不能證明每個結構、軌道與系統介面都仍符合要求。","explanationEn":"An ended event does not establish that every structure, track and system interface meets requirements."}},{"id":"b301-v6-11","sequence":11,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-route-safety"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-10"],"title":"管理維護與零件變更證據","titleEn":"Manage maintenance and component-change evidence","objective":"理解相容性需要超過外形與料號。","objectiveEn":"Understand why compatibility needs more than appearance and part numbers.","instruction":"自設一個更換感測器的紀錄，包含功能、接線介面、校正、版本與測試結果。比較新舊元件，在每個差異旁列出需更新的文件。","instructionEn":"Invent a sensor-replacement record with function, connection interface, calibration, version and test result. Compare old and new items, noting documents that each difference requires updating.","observation":"注意外形相同但量程、輸出定義或版本不同的情境。","observationEn":"Consider identical-looking parts with different ranges, output meanings or versions.","failure":"只因安裝孔位相同，就認定替代零件已完成相容驗證。","failureEn":"Declaring a replacement compatible solely because mounting holes match.","check":"交付功能差異表與可追溯的測試／文件清單。","checkEn":"Deliver a functional-difference table and a traceable test/document list.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-11-k1","title":"配置管理","titleEn":"Configuration management","text":"實際安裝狀態應與圖紙、設定及維護紀錄相符。","textEn":"Installed configuration should match drawings, settings and maintenance records."},{"id":"b301-v6-11-k2","title":"相容性驗證","titleEn":"Compatibility verification","text":"機械裝得上不代表電氣、資訊或功能語意相同。","textEn":"Mechanical fit does not establish electrical, information or functional equivalence."}],"quiz":{"options":["僅沿用原先的單位標籤","核對接收端解讀、校正與文件","只確認外殼沒有損傷"],"optionsEn":["Simply retain the old unit label","Review receiver interpretation, calibration and documentation","Only inspect the housing for damage"],"answer":1,"question":"新感測器孔位相同但輸出單位不同，最需要什麼？","questionEn":"A new sensor fits mechanically but uses different output units. What is most needed?","explanation":"輸出語意是系統介面的一部分，不能由機械相容取代。","explanationEn":"Output meaning is part of the system interface and is not verified by mechanical fit."}},{"id":"b301-v6-12","sequence":12,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-thsr-discovery","v6-thsr-route-safety","v6-thsr-disaster"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b301-v6-11"],"title":"交付高鐵整合證據矩陣","titleEn":"Deliver the high-speed-rail integration matrix","objective":"讓跨專業判斷有一致位置、版本與完成狀態。","objectiveEn":"Give cross-discipline judgments consistent location, version and completion state.","instruction":"將土建、軌道、集電、ATC及災害圖表列成需求—證據矩陣。選一個橋梁沉降情境，追蹤它可能影響哪些介面，註明只屬學習分析。","instructionEn":"Build a requirement–evidence matrix for civil works, track, collection, ATC and hazards. Trace interfaces potentially affected by a bridge-settlement scenario, labeling it as a learning analysis.","observation":"檢查某一系統的正常證據是否被誤用來替其他系統背書。","observationEn":"Check whether normal evidence for one subsystem is being used to certify another.","failure":"只有各專業合格結論，缺乏交界處相容性的證據。","failureEn":"Collecting individual discipline approvals without evidence of compatibility at their interfaces.","check":"每個介面都有來源、適用情境、未解問題及後續責任。","checkEn":"Give each interface a source, applicable scenario, open issue and follow-up responsibility.","knowledge":[{"id":"b301-v6-12-k1","title":"整合驗證","titleEn":"Integration verification","text":"子系統各自符合要求，仍須檢查連接後的共同功能。","textEn":"Individually compliant subsystems still require verification of their connected functions."},{"id":"b301-v6-12-k2","title":"可追溯交付","titleEn":"Traceable handover","text":"共享位置與版本使不同團隊能重建同一項判斷。","textEn":"Shared location and version identifiers allow teams to reconstruct the same judgment."}],"quiz":{"options":["是否可以刪除全部介面測試","是否已證明所有未測情境都合格","相互連接後是否滿足共同功能"],"optionsEn":["Whether every interface test can be removed","Whether all untested scenarios are thereby proven acceptable","Whether their connections meet shared functional requirements"],"answer":2,"question":"五個子系統各自通過單機測試，下一個合理問題是什麼？","questionEn":"Five subsystems pass standalone tests. What is the next reasonable question?","explanation":"整合行為可能不是單機測試的範圍，需另外的對應證據。","explanationEn":"Integrated behavior may lie outside standalone tests and needs evidence of its own."}}],"title":"災害、維護與交付","titleEn":"Hazards, maintenance and handover","description":"把偵測、決策、現地複核與變更管理分成可追溯步驟。","descriptionEn":"Separate detection, decisions, inspection and configuration changes into traceable stages."}],"title":"台灣高速鐵路","titleEn":"Taiwan High Speed Rail","summary":"以路線、橋隧、軌道、列車與安全控制的介面，理解高速鐵路整合與長期維護。","summaryEn":"Understand high-speed railway integration and maintenance through interfaces among alignment, civil works, track, trains and safety control.","scope":"以公開資料建立的原創教學分解；所有步驟為紙上、數位模型與證據判讀練習。自繪的示意與自設資料必須標示假設；本站未提供現地工程資料，亦不是核准施工、設備操作或水質放行程序。","scopeEn":"Original educational decomposition of public information. Every step is a paper, digital-model or evidence-interpretation exercise. Label assumptions in self-drawn diagrams and invented data; this site does not supply field engineering records or approved construction, operating or water-release procedures.","diagram":{"type":"rail","labels":["土建","軌道","車輛","供電與控制","驗證"],"labelsEn":["Civil works","Track","Rolling stock","Power and control","Verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240,"curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"b401","category":"environment","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality","v6-newater-parameters","v6-video-P7UDE2cISPQ"],"stages":[{"id":"b401-stage01","order":1,"steps":[{"id":"b401-v6-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"閉合回用水流程","titleEn":"Close the reclaimed-water loop","objective":"區分已處理用水、再生水與最終使用。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish treated used water, reclaimed product and final use.","instruction":"畫出已處理用水→MF/UF→RO→UV的概念流程，另分工業專管與水庫→淨水場→自來水兩條用途支路。標示這是一般教學路線，MBR等實廠配置可能不同。","instructionEn":"Draw treated used water to MF/UF, RO and UV. Add industrial dedicated supply and reservoir-to-waterworks-to-taps branches. Label this a general teaching route; actual configurations such as MBR may differ.","observation":"確認原污水並未直接接入再生水產品端，間接飲用支路也沒有略過淨水場。","observationEn":"Confirm raw sewage is not connected directly to product and the indirect-potable branch does not omit waterworks.","failure":"把NEWater等同未處理污水，或把間接飲用畫成直接供水。","failureEn":"Equating NEWater with untreated sewage or drawing indirect reuse as direct tap supply.","check":"每個水質邊界都有名稱，兩條使用支路可獨立追蹤。","checkEn":"Name each water-quality boundary and make both use branches traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-01-k1","title":"水質邊界","titleEn":"Water-quality boundaries","text":"已處理用水仍需後續純化；不同水流名稱代表不同處理狀態。","textEn":"Treated used water still requires further purification; stream names indicate different treatment states."},{"id":"b401-v6-01-k2","title":"用途路徑","titleEn":"Use pathways","text":"工業供水與間接飲用回用有不同的下游系統介面。","textEn":"Industrial supply and indirect potable reuse connect to different downstream systems."}],"quiz":{"options":["淨水場再處理後才供應自來水","直接跳過任何後續處理","改由工業專管自動變成家戶管線"],"optionsEn":["Waterworks treatment before tap-water supply","Bypass all subsequent treatment","Automatically turn an industrial main into household supply"],"answer":0,"question":"在PUB描述的間接飲用路徑中，水庫之後還有什麼？","questionEn":"In PUB’s described indirect-potable route, what follows the reservoir?","explanation":"「間接」包含水庫混合與後續淨水處理，不能刪除。","explanationEn":"Indirect reuse includes reservoir blending and subsequent waterworks treatment."}},{"id":"b401-v6-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-01"],"title":"建立進流水的資料邊界","titleEn":"Define the feedwater data boundary","objective":"把上游處理狀態與下游膜系統需求對齊。","objectiveEn":"Match upstream treatment status with downstream membrane evidence needs.","instruction":"自設一張進流水紀錄表，分別列流量、混濁、溶解物及微生物資料欄。對缺少數據的欄位保留未知，說明它可能影響哪一道後續屏障。","instructionEn":"Create a feedwater-record template for flow, turbidity, dissolved substances and microbiological evidence. Keep missing fields unknown and identify the downstream barrier each may affect.","observation":"比較水看起來透明與已取得化學或微生物證據的差別。","observationEn":"Distinguish visual clarity from chemical or microbiological evidence.","failure":"以肉眼清澈取代進流水品質與處理狀態確認。","failureEn":"Substituting visual clarity for feed-quality and treatment-status verification.","check":"至少四個資料欄各連到一項後續功能或驗證需求。","checkEn":"Link at least four fields to a downstream function or verification need.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-02-k1","title":"污染物類別","titleEn":"Contaminant classes","text":"粒子、溶解成分與微生物需要不同的量測與處理觀點。","textEn":"Particles, dissolved constituents and microorganisms require different measurement and treatment perspectives."},{"id":"b401-v6-02-k2","title":"上游依賴","titleEn":"Upstream dependency","text":"後段設備的表現受進流水條件影響，不能只看設備名稱。","textEn":"Downstream performance depends on feed conditions, not just equipment names."}],"quiz":{"options":["透明等於所有溶解物已去除","外觀已觀察，化學條件仍未知","可用出水流量代替化學資料"],"optionsEn":["Clarity means all dissolved substances are removed","Appearance observed; chemical conditions unknown","Product flow can replace chemical data"],"answer":1,"question":"進流水透明但化學資料缺漏，最適合的記錄是什麼？","questionEn":"Feedwater looks clear but chemical data is missing. What should be recorded?","explanation":"外觀只能描述有限性質，不能補出未量測的污染物資料。","explanationEn":"Appearance describes limited properties and cannot supply missing contaminant measurements."}},{"id":"b401-v6-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-02"],"title":"分辨MF/UF與RO的任務","titleEn":"Distinguish MF/UF and RO roles","objective":"用污染物類型理解不同膜屏障的互補。","objectiveEn":"Use contaminant classes to understand complementary membrane barriers.","instruction":"畫三類符號代表粒子、微生物與溶解離子，將MF/UF與RO畫成不同功能方塊。用「可能被截留／仍需下段處理／需量測確認」標記，不填通用百分之百去除承諾。","instructionEn":"Represent particles, microorganisms and dissolved ions with symbols, and draw separate MF/UF and RO blocks. Label retained, requiring downstream treatment and needing measurement without universal 100-percent removal claims.","observation":"注意前段粒子控制可改善後段條件，但不是所有溶解物的證明。","observationEn":"Particle control upstream can improve downstream conditions without proving removal of every dissolved constituent.","failure":"把所有膜都當成同一種細篩，認為第一道即可取代全部後段。","failureEn":"Treating all membranes as the same fine sieve and assuming the first replaces every later barrier.","check":"三類符號均有去向與未確認項，且MF/UF和RO功能可區分。","checkEn":"Give each symbol a destination and unresolved point, with distinguishable MF/UF and RO roles.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-03-k1","title":"互補屏障","titleEn":"Complementary barriers","text":"不同單元針對不同性質的污染物，串接可處理不同風險。","textEn":"Different units address different contaminant properties; a train combines complementary functions."},{"id":"b401-v6-03-k2","title":"簡化限制","titleEn":"Limits of simplification","text":"圖上符號只教分類，不代表特定膜在所有條件下的截留率。","textEn":"Diagram symbols teach categories, not rejection rates of a particular membrane under all conditions."}],"quiz":{"options":["所有溶解鹽類都已移除","後段RO和UV永遠可以取消","該量測條件下粒子相關指標較低"],"optionsEn":["All dissolved salts have been removed","RO and UV can always be omitted","A low particle-related indicator under those measurement conditions"],"answer":2,"question":"MF/UF出水低濁度能單獨證明什麼？","questionEn":"What does low MF/UF product turbidity establish on its own?","explanation":"低濁度不是所有化學與微生物條件的完整證明。","explanationEn":"Low turbidity is not complete evidence of every chemical and microbiological condition."}},{"id":"b401-v6-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-03"],"title":"檢查第一道膜屏障的完整性","titleEn":"Review first-barrier integrity evidence","objective":"辨認產水量與膜屏障完整性不同。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish water production from membrane-barrier integrity.","instruction":"自繪膜模組及密封介面，標出穿膜與繞過密封的兩種可能路徑。建立完整性證據、出水觀察與設備狀態三欄，所有數據留作自設教學示例。","instructionEn":"Sketch a membrane module and seals, marking passage through the membrane and possible seal bypass. Create integrity-evidence, product-observation and equipment-state columns using only labeled example data.","observation":"觀察出水量正常是否仍可能有旁通或局部缺陷。","observationEn":"Consider whether normal product flow can coexist with bypass or a local defect.","failure":"以流量正常或馬達運轉，替代屏障完整性證據。","failureEn":"Using normal flow or a running motor as proof of barrier integrity.","check":"列出兩種缺陷假說及能區分它們的觀察，不能只寫「正常」。","checkEn":"List two defect hypotheses and observations distinguishing them rather than simply writing normal.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-04-k1","title":"完整性與通量","titleEn":"Integrity versus throughput","text":"流得過去說明有產水，不等於水只經過預期的屏障。","textEn":"Flow establishes production, not that all water passed through the intended barrier."},{"id":"b401-v6-04-k2","title":"繞流介面","titleEn":"Bypass interfaces","text":"接合或密封也屬屏障的一部分，不能只檢查膜材料。","textEn":"Joints and seals are part of the barrier, not just the membrane material."}],"quiz":{"options":["產量有證據，屏障完整性尚未驗證","產量正常已足以證明完整性","可直接視為所有污染物都不存在"],"optionsEn":["Production evidenced; barrier integrity unverified","Normal production proves integrity","All contaminants can be considered absent"],"answer":0,"question":"流量正常但完整性證據不明，應如何分類？","questionEn":"Flow is normal but integrity evidence is unclear. How should the result be classified?","explanation":"功能宣稱需要對應證據，產量不能替代完整性。","explanationEn":"Functional claims need matching evidence; output quantity cannot substitute for integrity."}}],"title":"回用水邊界與前處理","titleEn":"Reuse boundaries and pretreatment","description":"辨認進流水、不同污染物與第一道膜屏障的證據。","descriptionEn":"Identify feedwater, contaminant classes and evidence for the first membrane barrier."},{"id":"b401-stage02","order":2,"steps":[{"id":"b401-v6-05","sequence":5,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-04"],"title":"閉合RO三股水的物料平衡","titleEn":"Balance the three RO streams","objective":"區分進水、透過水與濃縮水的數量。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish feed, permeate and concentrate quantities.","instruction":"用自設且標明假想的單位流量，畫進水分成透過水和濃縮水。先檢查水量加總，再比較溶質去向，不把濃縮水當作消失或無污染的水。","instructionEn":"Use explicitly invented unit flows to split feed into permeate and concentrate. Check the water balance, then trace solutes without treating concentrate as vanished or contaminant-free.","observation":"觀察透過水比例提高時，濃縮側需要重新檢查哪些假設。","observationEn":"Consider which concentrate-side assumptions need review as the permeate fraction rises.","failure":"只報告產水量，遺漏濃縮水量及所攜帶的物質。","failureEn":"Reporting product flow without concentrate flow or transported substances.","check":"水量收支閉合，並標記尚未納入的溶質與實際設備限制。","checkEn":"Close the water balance and identify unmodeled solutes and actual equipment limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-05-k1","title":"分離不是消滅","titleEn":"Separation is not destruction","text":"膜分離改變物質分配，並不使被排除的物質憑空消失。","textEn":"Membrane separation redistributes substances rather than making rejected material disappear."},{"id":"b401-v6-05-k2","title":"比例與條件","titleEn":"Fractions and conditions","text":"水量回收比例只描述部分績效，須與品質和濃縮側條件一起看。","textEn":"Water recovery describes only part of performance and must be considered with quality and concentrate conditions."}],"quiz":{"options":["75單位，因與產水相同","25單位","0單位，因被膜去除"],"optionsEn":["75 units, because it equals product flow","25 units","0 units, because the membrane removes it"],"answer":1,"question":"假想進水100單位、透過水75單位，在忽略蓄積下濃縮水多少？","questionEn":"For invented feed of 100 units and permeate of 75, with no storage, what is concentrate flow?","explanation":"水量守恆給出100−75＝25；這只是教學收支，未代表可用操作比例。","explanationEn":"Conservation gives 100−75=25; this teaching balance does not define an operating recovery."}},{"id":"b401-v6-06","sequence":6,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-quality","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-05"],"title":"解讀導電度而不過度推論","titleEn":"Interpret conductivity without overclaiming","objective":"區分離子相關指標與完整水質。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish an ion-related indicator from complete water quality.","instruction":"閱讀PUB水質表的導電度、濁度和有機碳欄位，分開記下單位與描述性質。自設兩份導電度相近但其他欄位不同的示例，比較可以及不可以下的結論。","instructionEn":"Read conductivity, turbidity and organic-carbon fields in PUB’s table, recording units and properties separately. Invent two samples with similar conductivity but differing other fields and compare valid and invalid conclusions.","observation":"注意單一低讀值不能補出未測項目。","observationEn":"A single low reading cannot supply unmeasured parameters.","failure":"用低導電度直接證明無微生物或所有有機污染物。","failureEn":"Using low conductivity as proof of no microorganisms or all organic contaminants.","check":"為三個指標各寫出一項能回答與不能回答的問題。","checkEn":"For each indicator, state one question it can and cannot answer.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-06-k1","title":"代理指標","titleEn":"Proxy indicators","text":"導電度反映水中導電性成分的綜合影響，不是每種污染物的直接濃度。","textEn":"Conductivity reflects combined conductive constituents, not direct concentration of every contaminant."},{"id":"b401-v6-06-k2","title":"單位語意","titleEn":"Meaning of units","text":"不同量測單位代表不同性質，不能因數字小就彼此比較優劣。","textEn":"Different units describe different properties; small numbers cannot be compared indiscriminately."}],"quiz":{"options":["低導電度證明微生物為零","可把導電度單位換成菌落數","離子相關指標已有資料，微生物狀態仍待驗證"],"optionsEn":["Low conductivity proves zero microorganisms","Conductivity units can be relabeled as colony counts","Ion-related evidence exists; microbial status remains unverified"],"answer":2,"question":"導電度很低而微生物結果尚未取得，最合理的結論是什麼？","questionEn":"Conductivity is low but microbiological results are unavailable. What follows?","explanation":"不同指標不能互相替代，尤其不能把物理電性當成微生物檢驗。","explanationEn":"Indicators are not interchangeable, particularly electrical properties and microbial testing."}},{"id":"b401-v6-07","sequence":7,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-06"],"title":"診斷膜效能趨勢","titleEn":"Diagnose membrane-performance trends","objective":"在比較膜效能前檢查進水與量測條件。","objectiveEn":"Check feed and measurement conditions before comparing membrane performance.","instruction":"自行建立兩段時間的流量、壓差、溫度與進水品質示例。先標記條件差異，再為產水下降列出積垢、進水變化與儀器偏差等假說，不指定清洗藥劑。","instructionEn":"Create example flow, differential pressure, temperature and feed-quality records for two periods. Mark condition changes before considering fouling, changed feed or instrument bias for lower output; prescribe no cleaning chemicals.","observation":"比較是否在相近條件下仍有持續偏差。","observationEn":"Check whether persistent differences remain under comparable conditions.","failure":"只用產量降低就斷定膜已損壞，忽略溫度、進水與量測。","failureEn":"Declaring membrane damage from lower output alone while ignoring temperature, feed and measurements.","check":"至少保留三種原因與一項可區分它們的補充資料。","checkEn":"Retain three candidate causes and a discriminating additional observation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-07-k1","title":"條件化趨勢","titleEn":"Condition-aware trends","text":"性能比較需保留進水與環境條件，避免把條件變化當設備退化。","textEn":"Performance comparisons require feed and environmental context to distinguish condition changes from deterioration."},{"id":"b401-v6-07-k2","title":"診斷而非猜測","titleEn":"Diagnosis rather than guessing","text":"同一現象可能有多因；查證計畫應讓假說可被反駁。","textEn":"One symptom can have multiple causes; investigation should make hypotheses testable."}],"quiz":{"options":["核對比較條件與量測，再評估設備趨勢","直接認定膜完整性破壞","刪除溫度資料以保持表格簡單"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile conditions and measurements before judging equipment trends","Immediately conclude loss of membrane integrity","Delete temperature to simplify the table"],"answer":0,"question":"兩次產水量不同，但進水溫度也不同，應先做什麼？","questionEn":"Product flow differs between periods with different feed temperatures. What comes first?","explanation":"先控制比較範圍，才能讓效能趨勢具有可解釋性。","explanationEn":"Establishing comparable conditions makes performance trends interpretable."}},{"id":"b401-v6-08","sequence":8,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-07"],"title":"辨認UV屏障與驗證量","titleEn":"Identify the UV barrier and its evidence","objective":"說明消毒與物質分離的不同任務。","objectiveEn":"Explain the different tasks of disinfection and separation.","instruction":"在RO後方加入UV功能方塊，分別記錄光源狀態、水流與水的透光相關證據。畫出「燈亮但驗證不完整」情境，不自行提供飲用水消毒劑量。","instructionEn":"Add a UV block after RO, separating light-source state, flow and transmission-related evidence. Illustrate a lamp-on-but-unverified case without specifying drinking-water disinfection doses.","observation":"觀察光源通電是否能直接證明所有水得到足夠作用。","observationEn":"Ask whether an energized source proves adequate treatment of all passing water.","failure":"把燈亮等同消毒已驗證，或認為UV會把溶解鹽類分走。","failureEn":"Equating a lit lamp with verified disinfection or assuming UV separates dissolved salts.","check":"用不同證據欄位分開設備狀態、處理條件與水質驗證。","checkEn":"Separate equipment state, treatment conditions and quality verification in the record.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-08-k1","title":"功能差異","titleEn":"Functional difference","text":"UV作用於微生物失活；它不是RO式的溶質分流。","textEn":"UV targets microbial inactivation rather than RO-like solute separation."},{"id":"b401-v6-08-k2","title":"完整作用條件","titleEn":"Complete treatment conditions","text":"光源、流動與水的光學條件共同影響處理，不能只看開關。","textEn":"Source, flow and optical conditions jointly affect treatment; an on/off signal is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"options":["出水所有化學成分均已去除","設備有開啟指示，處理效果仍需對應證據","全部水質項目已通過檢驗"],"optionsEn":["Every chemical constituent has been removed","An on indication exists; treatment performance still needs evidence","All water-quality parameters have passed"],"answer":1,"question":"UV燈顯示開啟，可直接證明哪項？","questionEn":"A UV lamp indicates on. What does that directly prove?","explanation":"設備狀態不是完整水質結果，必須保留各自的驗證。","explanationEn":"Equipment state is not a complete quality result; each requires its own verification."}}],"title":"分離、診斷與消毒","titleEn":"Separation, diagnosis and disinfection","description":"把逆滲透的水量與水質、膜狀態及UV功能分開判讀。","descriptionEn":"Interpret RO flow and quality, membrane condition and UV function separately."},{"id":"b401-stage03","order":3,"steps":[{"id":"b401-v6-09","sequence":9,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-quality","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-08"],"title":"建立採樣追溯鏈","titleEn":"Establish sample traceability","objective":"讓結果對應到正確位置、時間與樣品。","objectiveEn":"Link results to the correct location, time and sample.","instruction":"設計樣品表單，包含編號、取樣位置、時間、分析項目、方法和結果狀態。用兩個假想相近編號，演練如何辨認進水樣被誤標為出水樣。","instructionEn":"Design a sample form with ID, location, time, analyte, method and result state. Use two similar invented IDs to detect feedwater mislabeled as product.","observation":"檢查只有檢驗數字、沒有樣品身分時是否仍能解讀。","observationEn":"Assess whether a result remains interpretable without sample identity.","failure":"將不同時間、位置或方法的結果拼成同一批水的證明。","failureEn":"Combining results from different times, locations or methods as proof about one water batch.","check":"每筆示例結果可反查完整身分，錯置樣品須保留更正紀錄。","checkEn":"Trace each example result to its identity and retain correction records for mislabeling.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-09-k1","title":"代表性","titleEn":"Representativeness","text":"樣品能代表的水流與時間範圍，取決於採樣設計及紀錄。","textEn":"The stream and time represented by a sample depend on sampling design and records."},{"id":"b401-v6-09-k2","title":"結果狀態","titleEn":"Result status","text":"待分析、低於檢出能力及未檢測是不同狀態，不應都填成零。","textEn":"Pending, below detection capability and not tested are different states and should not all become zero."}],"quiz":{"options":["0，表示沒有檢出","以另一位置的結果自動補入","未檢測，保留待取得證據"],"optionsEn":["Zero, meaning not detected","Automatically fill with a result from another location","Not tested; evidence pending"],"answer":2,"question":"某項分析尚未執行，表格應怎麼填？","questionEn":"How should an analysis that has not been performed be recorded?","explanation":"未檢測並不等於未檢出；誠實的狀態是追溯鏈的一部分。","explanationEn":"Not tested is not equivalent to not detected; accurate status is part of traceability."}},{"id":"b401-v6-10","sequence":10,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-09"],"title":"核對工業與間接回用介面","titleEn":"Review industrial and indirect-reuse interfaces","objective":"把目的地要求連到對應供水路徑。","objectiveEn":"Connect destination requirements to the appropriate supply route.","instruction":"建立兩欄：工業專管與水庫後接淨水場。為兩欄分別列交付點、後續處理與需確認的品質責任；不把工業廠內額外純化假定為PUB已完成。","instructionEn":"Compare dedicated industrial supply with reservoir-to-waterworks reuse. List handover point, further treatment and quality responsibility, without assuming PUB performs every customer’s additional purification.","observation":"觀察相同再生水來源在不同使用者端是否仍有不同後續需求。","observationEn":"The same reclaimed source may face different downstream needs at different users.","failure":"把NEWater典型值直接視為每一家工業製程的完整規格。","failureEn":"Treating NEWater typical values as complete specifications for every industrial process.","check":"兩條路徑各保留一項使用端需另行確認的介面條件。","checkEn":"Retain one destination-specific condition requiring separate confirmation for each route.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-10-k1","title":"適用途徑","titleEn":"Fit-for-purpose pathways","text":"水的目的地與後續處理會影響應驗證的介面，不能只看名稱。","textEn":"Destination and subsequent treatment influence the interface to verify, not just the water’s name."},{"id":"b401-v6-10-k2","title":"交付邊界","titleEn":"Handover boundary","text":"公用供水與客戶製程之間的品質責任須明確，不能隱含轉移。","textEn":"Quality responsibilities between utility supply and customer processes must be explicit."}],"quiz":{"options":["在客戶端增加明確的處理與驗證邊界","將供水典型值改成客戶所有需求","假定所有再生水用途完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Add an explicit customer treatment and verification boundary","Relabel typical supply values as all customer requirements","Assume every reuse application is identical"],"answer":0,"question":"某晶圓廠需要額外純化，合理的模型表示是什麼？","questionEn":"A wafer fab requires further purification. How should the model show it?","explanation":"上游供水與下游製程需求是不同邊界，需分開交代。","explanationEn":"Utility supply and downstream process needs are different boundaries that must be stated separately."}},{"id":"b401-v6-11","sequence":11,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-quality","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-10"],"title":"記錄異常與未驗證狀態","titleEn":"Record anomalies and unverified states","objective":"避免在證據矛盾時給出過度的品質結論。","objectiveEn":"Avoid overclaiming quality when evidence conflicts.","instruction":"自行寫一個導電度趨勢改變但重測尚未完成的案例。列出感測器、取樣身分、進水條件與處理狀態的核對清單，交付狀態標成待驗證，不作真實放水指令。","instructionEn":"Invent a changed conductivity trend with repeat analysis pending. List sensor, sample identity, feed and treatment checks; label the learning handover unverified without issuing actual release commands.","observation":"注意一次正常重測是否足以解釋先前異常與整段時間。","observationEn":"Consider whether one normal repeat explains the prior anomaly and the entire affected period.","failure":"只留下正常讀值、刪除異常資料，造成虛假的連續合格紀錄。","failureEn":"Keeping normal readings while deleting anomalies to create a falsely continuous acceptable record.","check":"保留事件時間線、原始異常與待取得資料，結論不得超出觀察期間。","checkEn":"Preserve the timeline, original anomaly and missing evidence; limit conclusions to observed periods.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-11-k1","title":"偏差追查","titleEn":"Deviation investigation","text":"異常應有可追溯的查證與結案理由，不能只靠後續正常值覆蓋。","textEn":"Anomalies need traceable investigation and closure reasons rather than being overwritten by later normal values."},{"id":"b401-v6-11-k2","title":"時間範圍","titleEn":"Time scope","text":"採樣結果有其時間與位置範圍，不自動涵蓋未觀測時段。","textEn":"Sample results have time and location scope and do not automatically cover unobserved periods."}],"quiz":{"options":["直接刪除，僅保留最後結果","保留並查明適用範圍與原因","用兩次平均值宣告整段正常"],"optionsEn":["Delete it and retain only the latest result","Preserve it and investigate its scope and cause","Average the two and declare the entire interval normal"],"answer":1,"question":"後一次樣品正常，先前異常應如何處理？","questionEn":"A later sample is normal. What should happen to the earlier anomaly?","explanation":"後續結果不會自動解釋前次異常或填補時間空白。","explanationEn":"A later result does not automatically explain an earlier anomaly or fill a time gap."}},{"id":"b401-v6-12","sequence":12,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v6-newater-process","v6-newater-quality","v6-newater-parameters"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["b401-v6-11"],"title":"交付多重屏障品質卷宗","titleEn":"Deliver the multiple-barrier quality dossier","objective":"區分典型資料、操作準則與產品驗證證據。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish typical data, operating criteria and product-verification evidence.","instruction":"整理流程、物料平衡、屏障狀態、採樣紀錄與目的地介面。閱讀PUB典型值表的欄名及日期，為每個課程結論標上来源或自設假設，不把典型值轉成自行放行標準。","instructionEn":"Organize process, balance, barrier, sampling and destination records. Read the headings and date of PUB’s typical-values table; label sources or invented assumptions without converting typical values into self-authorized release criteria.","observation":"核對「典型」「指引」「本次實測」是否在文件中被混用。","observationEn":"Check whether typical, guideline and current measurement are being conflated.","failure":"拿公開典型值表代替當批水的實測與完整驗證。","failureEn":"Substituting a public typical-values table for measurements and verification of a specific batch.","check":"交付三類資料的區分表及至少四項可追溯證據，明示這不是飲水安全認證。","checkEn":"Submit a distinction table and at least four traceable evidence items, explicitly identifying this as no drinking-water safety certification.","knowledge":[{"id":"b401-v6-12-k1","title":"資料類別","titleEn":"Data categories","text":"典型值描述通常表現；指引、操作判準與特定樣品結果有不同角色。","textEn":"Typical values describe usual performance; guidelines, operating criteria and sample results have distinct roles."},{"id":"b401-v6-12-k2","title":"多重證據","titleEn":"Multiple evidence layers","text":"屏障、監測、採樣與目的地需求需相互吻合，單一指標無法概括。","textEn":"Barriers, monitoring, sampling and destination requirements must agree; one indicator cannot represent them all."}],"quiz":{"options":["使用者自行處理的水已通過全部驗證","任何實廠都可照表自行設定放行門檻","官方描述的通常水質表現與資料範圍"],"optionsEn":["User-treated water has passed all verification","Every plant may adopt the table as release settings","The authority’s described usual quality and data scope"],"answer":2,"question":"一張標示「典型值」的官方表格能直接證明哪件事？","questionEn":"What does an official table labeled typical values directly establish?","explanation":"公開典型資料是背景證據，不是特定樣品、設備或操作授權。","explanationEn":"Public typical data is background evidence, not verification or authorization for a particular sample, device or operation."}}],"title":"採樣、用途與品質交付","titleEn":"Sampling, uses and quality handover","description":"將追溯、異常處置概念及目的地要求連成驗證鏈。","descriptionEn":"Connect traceability, anomaly-handling concepts and destination requirements into an evidence chain."}],"title":"新加坡新生水系統","titleEn":"Singapore NEWater System","summary":"以多重處理屏障、物料平衡與水質證據，理解再生水如何連接城市與工業用水。","summaryEn":"Understand how reclaimed water links cities and industry through multiple treatment barriers, mass balance and water-quality evidence.","scope":"以公開資料建立的原創教學分解；所有步驟為紙上、數位模型與證據判讀練習。自繪的示意與自設資料必須標示假設；本站未提供現地工程資料，亦不是核准施工、設備操作或水質放行程序。","scopeEn":"Original educational decomposition of public information. Every step is a paper, digital-model or evidence-interpretation exercise. Label assumptions in self-drawn diagrams and invented data; this site does not supply field engineering records or approved construction, operating or water-release procedures.","diagram":{"type":"water-treatment","labels":["已處理用水","MF/UF","逆滲透","紫外線","用途與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Treated used water","MF/UF","Reverse osmosis","Ultraviolet","Use and verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240,"curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"c001","title":"Airbus A350 複材客機系統工程","titleEn":"Airbus A350 composite airliner systems","category":"aerospace","summary":"從機翼載荷、複材方向、公差鏈到配置變更，用原創示意與紙上算例學習A350類客機的系統整合。","summaryEn":"Study A350-class airliner integration through original sketches and paper exercises on wing loads, composite directionality, tolerance chains and configuration change.","scope":"12道入門工程學習任務；引用A350公開背景，力學數值為明示教學假設。不是原廠鋪層表、裝配SOP、維修手冊、適航符合性證明或製造授權。","scopeEn":"Twelve introductory engineering tasks grounded in public A350 background, with explicitly hypothetical mechanics values. Not manufacturer layup schedules, assembly SOPs, maintenance instructions, airworthiness substantiation or manufacturing authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-a350-family","v6-a350-milestones","v6-faa-composites","v6-video-W0jlu0ghNIg"],"diagram":{"type":"aircraft","labels":["機身","機翼","接合介面","系統通道","驗證證據"],"labelsEn":["Fuselage","Wing","Joint interface","System routes","Verification evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"c001-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、載荷與基準","titleEn":"Requirements, loads and datums","description":"先定義系統邊界，再用質量、力矩及座標建立可追溯的整合問題。","descriptionEn":"Define boundaries, then use mass, moments and coordinates to establish traceable integration questions.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c001-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":[],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family"],"title":"分配客機系統邊界","titleEn":"Allocate airliner system boundaries","objective":"把機體、動力、供電與控制的介面分開記錄。","objectiveEn":"Separate interfaces among airframe, propulsion, power and control.","instruction":"在紙上畫四個系統方塊，分別用實線、虛線表示載荷與資訊交換。以A350公開介紹辨識用途，再為每條箭頭寫下輸入、輸出與責任者；圖是你的原創示意。","instructionEn":"Draw four system blocks, using solid and dashed arrows for loads and information. Identify purposes from the public A350 overview, then label each interface with its input, output and owner. This is your own schematic.","observation":"觀察一條電源線與一項結構支承是否被錯當成同一種介面。","observationEn":"Check whether an electrical supply and a structural support have been treated as the same interface.","failure":"只列零件名稱而沒有交換量，會隱藏整合問題。","failureEn":"A parts list without exchanged quantities hides integration problems.","check":"至少列出一項機械、一項電力及一項資訊介面，各有可檢查的量。","checkEn":"Identify mechanical, electrical and information interfaces, each with a checkable quantity.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-01-k1","title":"功能與實體","titleEn":"Function and hardware","text":"一個功能可能跨越多個實體零件；方塊邊界是分析選擇。","textEn":"One function may span several physical parts; block boundaries are analytical choices."},{"id":"c001-v6-01-k2","title":"介面責任","titleEn":"Interface ownership","text":"輸出符合自己的規格，仍須與接收端假設相容。","textEn":"Meeting an output specification still requires compatibility with the receiving side."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩團隊零件各自合格，整合卻失敗，先查什麼？","questionEn":"Two teams pass their component checks but integration fails. What should be checked first?","options":["只確認各零件單獨合格即可接受整合","只核對總質量是否與原計畫相同","介面的交換量與假設是否一致"],"optionsEn":["Accept integration as soon as the individual parts pass","Check only whether total mass matches the original plan","Whether exchanged quantities and interface assumptions agree"],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部合格不自動證明跨系統相容。","explanationEn":"Local compliance does not automatically establish system compatibility."}},{"id":"c001-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-01"],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family"],"title":"計算示意配重的重心","titleEn":"Calculate a schematic mass balance","objective":"以位置加權理解配置變更對重心的影響。","objectiveEn":"Use position-weighted mass to understand configuration changes.","instruction":"設兩個教學質量：2單位位於x=1，1單位位於x=4。算總質量與重心，再把後者移到x=7重算；所有數值均為無因次例題，不是飛機限制。","instructionEn":"Use teaching masses of 2 units at x=1 and 1 unit at x=4. Calculate total mass and center of mass, then move the latter to x=7 and recalculate. All values are dimensionless examples, not aircraft limits.","observation":"總質量不變，重心卻由2移到3。","observationEn":"Total mass stays constant while the center moves from 2 to 3.","failure":"直接平均兩個位置，等於錯把不同質量視為相等。","failureEn":"Averaging positions directly wrongly assigns equal weight to unequal masses.","check":"保留兩次力矩和，並用總質量除回重心。","checkEn":"Retain both moment sums and divide by total mass to recover the center.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-02-k1","title":"一階質量矩","titleEn":"First mass moment","text":"重心由Σmx／Σm求得，必須使用共同原點。","textEn":"The center is Σmx/Σm, using a common origin."},{"id":"c001-v6-02-k2","title":"配置管理","titleEn":"Configuration control","text":"搬動設備可能改變重心，即使沒有新增重量。","textEn":"Relocating equipment can change balance without adding mass."}],"quiz":{"question":"把同一設備往後移，哪項必然不變？","questionEn":"When the same item is moved aft, which quantity necessarily stays unchanged?","options":["重心位置","總質量","總質量矩"],"optionsEn":["Center-of-mass position","Total mass","Total mass moment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"位置改變影響力矩，不改變該設備質量。","explanationEn":"Changing position alters the moment, not the item’s mass."}},{"id":"c001-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-02"],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family","v6-faa-composites"],"title":"追蹤機翼到機身的載荷路徑","titleEn":"Trace the wing-to-fuselage load path","objective":"區分分布載荷、接合處反力與局部應力。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish distributed load, joint reaction and local stress.","instruction":"畫一根固定端示意樑，把三支向上箭頭分布在翼展上。先令總力相同，再把箭頭外移；比较固定端彎矩。僅做紙上力學，不推算真機強度。","instructionEn":"Draw a fixed-end teaching beam with three upward arrows along its span. Keep total force unchanged, move the arrows outward and compare root bending moments. Use paper mechanics only, without inferring aircraft strength.","observation":"相同升力總和，作用點更遠時根部力矩增加。","observationEn":"The same total lift produces a larger root moment when applied farther out.","failure":"只比較總力會漏掉力臂，接頭也不能用外觀大小判定安全。","failureEn":"Comparing total force alone misses the lever arm; joint appearance cannot establish safety.","check":"每支箭頭標出到根部的距離，列出ΣFr。","checkEn":"Label each lever arm and calculate ΣFr.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-03-k1","title":"力臂","titleEn":"Lever arm","text":"力矩取決於力與其垂直作用距離。","textEn":"Moment depends on force and its perpendicular lever arm."},{"id":"c001-v6-03-k2","title":"局部與整體","titleEn":"Local and global response","text":"整體平衡提供反力，局部接頭仍需獨立驗證。","textEn":"Global equilibrium gives reactions; local joints still require separate substantiation."}],"quiz":{"question":"總升力不變、向翼尖移動，根部彎矩如何變化？","questionEn":"With total lift unchanged but moved toward the tip, how does root bending moment change?","options":["增大","必定降為零","因總力相同而不變"],"optionsEn":["It increases","It necessarily becomes zero","It is unchanged because total force is unchanged"],"answer":0,"explanation":"外移增加力臂，因此增加根部力矩。","explanationEn":"Moving the load outward increases its lever arm and root moment."}},{"id":"c001-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-03"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"核對裝配基準與公差鏈","titleEn":"Check assembly datums and tolerance chains","objective":"讓兩個分段使用一致的座標與驗收基準。","objectiveEn":"Give two sections consistent coordinates and acceptance datums.","instruction":"在兩張原創機身分段圖標出共同原點、軸向和接合平面。假設兩段偏差各為±0.4示意單位，求最壞相對錯位，再與假設允收±0.6比較。","instructionEn":"Mark a shared origin, axes and mating plane on two original fuselage-section sketches. Assume each has an error of ±0.4 teaching units. Find the worst relative mismatch and compare with an assumed ±0.6 allowance.","observation":"單段各自合格，反向偏差仍可能造成0.8錯位。","observationEn":"Individually acceptable sections can still mismatch by 0.8 when errors oppose.","failure":"混用機身座標與局部治具座標，會產生看似固定的系統偏差。","failureEn":"Mixing body and fixture frames can create an apparently fixed systematic offset.","check":"指出最壞組合，且圖上所有尺寸可追溯到相同基準。","checkEn":"Identify the worst combination and trace every dimension to the common datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-04-k1","title":"基準","titleEn":"Datum","text":"尺寸的意義依賴其參考平面與方向。","textEn":"A dimension depends on its reference plane and direction."},{"id":"c001-v6-04-k2","title":"公差累積","titleEn":"Tolerance accumulation","text":"最壞相對誤差需考慮兩零件朝相反方向偏移。","textEn":"Worst relative error includes opposite deviations of the two parts."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩段各±0.4，最壞相對錯位是多少？","questionEn":"For two sections each at ±0.4, what is the worst relative mismatch?","options":["0.4","0.16","0.8"],"optionsEn":["0.4","0.16","0.8"],"answer":2,"explanation":"一段+0.4、另一段−0.4，差為0.8。","explanationEn":"One at +0.4 and the other at −0.4 differ by 0.8."}}]},{"id":"c001-stage02","order":2,"title":"材料回應與損傷證據","titleEn":"Material response and damage evidence","description":"比较方向性、熱相容、檢測範圍與循環載荷；不替代任何實機材料試驗。","descriptionEn":"Compare directionality, thermal compatibility, inspection scope and cyclic loading without replacing aircraft material tests.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c001-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-04"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"辨識複材方向性","titleEn":"Identify composite directionality","objective":"把纖維方向與載荷方向連在一起。","objectiveEn":"Relate fiber direction to loading direction.","instruction":"畫三張試片示意：纖維沿0°、90°及混合方向。對同一軸向拉力標出纖維與基材可能扮演的角色；只提出待測假設，不自填材料強度。","instructionEn":"Sketch coupons with fibers at 0°, 90° and mixed orientations. Under the same axial load, identify possible fiber and matrix roles. Record hypotheses requiring tests instead of inventing strength values.","observation":"旋轉試片方向會改變材料回應，即使外形與厚度相同。","observationEn":"Rotating the material direction can alter response despite identical shape and thickness.","failure":"把複材當作各方向相同的金屬，會掩蓋方向性與層間問題。","failureEn":"Treating a laminate as direction-independent metal hides anisotropy and interlaminar issues.","check":"每張試片都有載荷箭頭、纖維方向及一項待驗證假設。","checkEn":"Each coupon shows a load arrow, fiber orientation and a testable hypothesis.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-05-k1","title":"異向性","titleEn":"Anisotropy","text":"複材性質可能隨方向改變，不能只用單一強度數字描述。","textEn":"Composite properties can vary by direction and cannot be described by one strength value alone."},{"id":"c001-v6-05-k2","title":"基材功能","titleEn":"Matrix role","text":"基材保持纖維配置並傳遞載荷，不能視為無功能的填充物。","textEn":"The matrix maintains fiber arrangement and transfers load; it is not an inert filler."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩試片外形一樣卻反應不同，哪項應優先核對？","questionEn":"Two equal-shaped coupons respond differently. Which factor should be checked first?","options":["只比較外形與厚度是否相同","纖維方向與鋪層資訊","只核對總質量，不看鋪層"],"optionsEn":["Compare only external shape and thickness","Fiber orientation and laminate information","Check only mass without examining the layup"],"answer":1,"explanation":"方向與鋪層直接影響複材力學回應。","explanationEn":"Orientation and layup directly affect composite mechanical response."}},{"id":"c001-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-05"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"比較異材接合的熱伸長","titleEn":"Compare thermal expansion at a mixed-material joint","objective":"理解相連材料自由伸長不同的後果。","objectiveEn":"Understand consequences of unequal free thermal expansion.","instruction":"假設兩條等長教學材料的熱膨脹係數為2與10個相同單位，在相同升溫下比較自由伸長比。再畫出端部被共同約束的情境，列出需要分析的接頭反力。","instructionEn":"Assume equal-length teaching strips with expansion coefficients of 2 and 10 in the same units. Compare free expansion under equal heating, then sketch a shared end restraint and identify joint reactions needing analysis.","observation":"較大係數的自由伸長為另一條的5倍；接合後不能各自自由伸長。","observationEn":"The higher-coefficient strip expands five times as much freely; joined strips cannot both follow their free expansion.","failure":"把自由熱伸長直接當作受約束後的實際位移，忽略了相容条件。","failureEn":"Using free expansion as constrained displacement ignores compatibility.","check":"分別列出自由伸長與約束後需解的未知量，不猜接頭應力值。","checkEn":"Separate free expansion from unknown constrained quantities without guessing joint stress.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-06-k1","title":"熱應變","titleEn":"Thermal strain","text":"自由熱應變由膨脹係數乘溫度變化得到。","textEn":"Free thermal strain is expansion coefficient times temperature change."},{"id":"c001-v6-06-k2","title":"相容條件","titleEn":"Compatibility","text":"被接在一起的部位須同時滿足幾何相容與力平衡。","textEn":"Connected parts must satisfy both geometric compatibility and force equilibrium."}],"quiz":{"question":"自由伸長不同的材料被接合後，還需加入什麼？","questionEn":"What must be added when joining materials with different free expansions?","options":["約束與相容條件","把較小伸長直接刪掉","假設接頭永遠沒有反力"],"optionsEn":["Restraints and compatibility conditions","Discard the smaller expansion","Assume the joint never develops a reaction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭限制相對移動，可能因此產生內力。","explanationEn":"The joint limits relative movement and can generate internal forces."}},{"id":"c001-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-06"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"建立複材檢查的證據地圖","titleEn":"Map composite inspection evidence","objective":"區分表面觀察與內部損傷的證據。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish surface observation from internal-damage evidence.","instruction":"畫一片有表面撞痕與假設層間缺陷的示意板。把目視、適用的非破壞檢測與後續工程評估放在不同欄位；為每種方法註明它能回答與不能回答的問題。","instructionEn":"Draw a panel with a surface impact mark and a hypothetical internal defect. Separate visual inspection, applicable nondestructive inspection and engineering assessment into columns, stating what each can and cannot answer.","observation":"外表平整不能排除內部異常，檢測訊號也不自動等於可放行。","observationEn":"A smooth surface cannot rule out internal anomalies, and a signal alone does not authorize release.","failure":"用照片替代經核准的檢測與判讀，會把未知狀態誤標合格。","failureEn":"Substituting a photo for approved inspection and interpretation mislabels uncertainty as acceptance.","check":"至少一項未知量保留為待確認，並列出需要的合格判讀證據。","checkEn":"Retain at least one unresolved question and identify the qualified interpretation needed.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-07-k1","title":"損傷容限","titleEn":"Damage tolerance","text":"發現、評估和處置損傷是不同工作。","textEn":"Detecting, assessing and dispositioning damage are separate tasks."},{"id":"c001-v6-07-k2","title":"檢測範圍","titleEn":"Inspection coverage","text":"每種方法有適用材料、幾何與缺陷範圍。","textEn":"Every method has applicable materials, geometries and defect classes."}],"quiz":{"question":"沒有看見裂痕，能直接得出哪個結論？","questionEn":"No crack is visible. Which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有內部層間皆完整","已符合真機放行要求","目前目視範圍沒有可見裂痕"],"optionsEn":["All internal interfaces are intact","The aircraft release requirements are satisfied","No visible crack was found within the visual inspection scope"],"answer":2,"explanation":"證據只能支援其觀察範圍內的結論。","explanationEn":"Evidence supports conclusions only within its observation scope."}},{"id":"c001-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-07"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"區分靜態強度與循環疲勞","titleEn":"Separate static strength from cyclic fatigue","objective":"用載荷歷程而非一次峰值描述耐久問題。","objectiveEn":"Describe durability through load history rather than one peak.","instruction":"自畫兩條無因次載荷曲線：一次峰值與多次較低振幅循環。標記循環數、平均值和振幅，列出需要何種試驗資料才能比較壽命；不自行推算服役年限。","instructionEn":"Draw dimensionless load histories: one peak and repeated lower-amplitude cycles. Mark cycle count, mean and amplitude, then identify test data needed to compare life. Do not infer service years.","observation":"低於一次試驗峰值的循環載荷，仍可能累積損傷。","observationEn":"Repeated loading below a single-test peak can still accumulate damage.","failure":"一次靜載通過就宣稱無限壽命，混淆了不同驗證目的。","failureEn":"Claiming unlimited life after one static pass confuses different verification purposes.","check":"報告分開寫靜態判定、循環資料與尚未回答的壽命問題。","checkEn":"Report static assessment, cyclic data and unanswered life questions separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-08-k1","title":"载荷歷程","titleEn":"Load history","text":"疲勞問題包含次數、振幅、平均值與順序。","textEn":"Fatigue problems include count, amplitude, mean and sequence."},{"id":"c001-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證範圍","titleEn":"Verification scope","text":"一種試驗合格不自動覆蓋所有失效機制。","textEn":"Passing one test does not cover every failure mechanism."}],"quiz":{"question":"靜載測試通過後，仍不能直接宣稱什麼？","questionEn":"After passing a static test, what still cannot be claimed directly?","options":["仍需要辨識使用載荷歷程","已證明所有循環疲勞壽命","該靜載情境已取得一項證據"],"optionsEn":["The service-load history still needs identification","Every cyclic-fatigue life requirement is proven","Evidence exists for that static-load case"],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜態與疲勞的驗證對象不同。","explanationEn":"Static and fatigue verification address different behavior."}}]},{"id":"c001-stage03","order":3,"title":"系統整合與配置交付","titleEn":"System integration and configuration handover","description":"把冗餘、空間、變更及證據成熟度納入同一份工程紀錄。","descriptionEn":"Bring redundancy, space, change and evidence maturity into one engineering record.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c001-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-08"],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family"],"title":"檢查冗餘電源的共同依賴","titleEn":"Check shared dependencies in redundant power","objective":"避免把兩條線路誤認成兩套獨立供電。","objectiveEn":"Avoid confusing two wires with two independent supplies.","instruction":"畫两路教學電源供應同一感測器，先讓它們共用一個上游開關，再另畫分開的上游路徑。用紙上斷點逐一追蹤失效影響，不模擬真機電路。","instructionEn":"Draw two teaching supplies feeding one sensor, first sharing an upstream switch and then using separate upstream paths. Trace failures with paper break points, without simulating an aircraft circuit.","observation":"共用開關失效可同時切斷兩條下游線路。","observationEn":"A shared switch failure can interrupt both downstream paths.","failure":"只數備份元件，未檢查共同依賴，會高估可用性。","failureEn":"Counting backup components without shared-dependency analysis overstates availability.","check":"標出至少一個共同失效點及其影響，將未知獨立性列為待驗證。","checkEn":"Mark a common failure point and its effect, retaining unproven independence as an open item.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-09-k1","title":"共同原因","titleEn":"Common cause","text":"相同來源或環境可能同時影響看似分開的設備。","textEn":"A shared source or environment can affect apparently separate equipment."},{"id":"c001-v6-09-k2","title":"失效傳播","titleEn":"Failure propagation","text":"系統邊界上的依賴決定故障如何擴散。","textEn":"Dependencies across boundaries determine how faults propagate."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩路電源共用上游開關，該開關失效代表什麼？","questionEn":"Two supplies share an upstream switch. What does its failure imply?","options":["兩路可能同時失去供電","必定只有一路受影響","下游有兩條線就不受影響"],"optionsEn":["Both paths may lose power together","Only one path can be affected","Two downstream wires prevent any effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"路徑數量不能取代獨立性分析。","explanationEn":"Path count is not a substitute for independence analysis."}},{"id":"c001-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-09"],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family","v6-faa-composites"],"title":"審查管線與維修可達性","titleEn":"Review routing and maintenance access","objective":"在原創配置圖上辨識跨系統的空間衝突。","objectiveEn":"Identify cross-system spatial conflicts on an original layout.","instruction":"畫一段機身設備艙示意，放入管線、線束、支承與可拆面板。先標運動及熱源區，再安排檢查視線和拆卸路徑；尺寸只用自訂教學單位。","instructionEn":"Sketch a fuselage equipment bay with pipes, wiring, supports and a removable panel. Mark moving and hot zones, then inspection sightlines and removal paths. Use invented teaching units only.","observation":"在安裝時放得進去，不代表日後能安全檢查或取出。","observationEn":"Fitting during installation does not ensure later inspection or removal access.","failure":"只看靜止的正視圖，可能漏掉運動包络或拆卸空間。","failureEn":"A static front view may hide motion envelopes or removal clearances.","check":"為一項元件畫出完整移出路徑，並列出至少一項介面衝突。","checkEn":"Draw a complete removal path for one item and identify an interface conflict.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-10-k1","title":"維護設計","titleEn":"Design for maintenance","text":"可達性是生命周期需求，不是完工後才處理的附加項。","textEn":"Access is a lifecycle requirement rather than an afterthought."},{"id":"c001-v6-10-k2","title":"空間包络","titleEn":"Spatial envelope","text":"位置、運動、工具與拆卸路徑佔用不同空間。","textEn":"Installed position, motion, tools and removal paths occupy different spaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"元件安裝後被固定管線擋住，主要漏了什麼？","questionEn":"A fixed pipe blocks an installed component’s removal. What was omitted?","options":["只確認最初裝配時元件放得進去","只比較檢修口面積而不檢查移出路徑","維修拆卸的空間介面"],"optionsEn":["Confirm only that the component fitted during initial assembly","Compare access-panel area without checking the removal path","The maintenance-removal spatial interface"],"answer":2,"explanation":"維修需要考慮整條拆卸路徑。","explanationEn":"Maintenance requires considering the entire removal path."}},{"id":"c001-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-10"],"sourceIds":["v6-faa-composites"],"title":"追蹤設計變更的影響鏈","titleEn":"Trace a design-change impact chain","objective":"讓一項材料變更連回所有受影響的證據。","objectiveEn":"Connect a material change to every affected evidence item.","instruction":"設想教學支架由材料甲改為乙。建立變更卡，逐欄檢查質量、熱膨脹、接合、檢測方式及圖面版本；未知欄寫待確認，不自行批准替代。","instructionEn":"Imagine changing a teaching bracket from material A to B. Create a change card covering mass, thermal expansion, joining, inspection and drawing revision. Mark unknowns for review rather than approving substitution.","observation":"外形相同的支架仍可能改變負載與檢驗需求。","observationEn":"An equal-shaped bracket may still change loads and inspection needs.","failure":"只更新採購名稱而保留舊驗證結論，會切斷配置追溯。","failureEn":"Updating only the purchase name while keeping old verification breaks configuration traceability.","check":"變更卡至少連到兩項需重新審查的既有證據。","checkEn":"Link the change card to at least two existing evidence items requiring review.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-11-k1","title":"配置基線","titleEn":"Configuration baseline","text":"驗證結果只對特定版本與假設成立。","textEn":"Verification results apply to a particular revision and assumptions."},{"id":"c001-v6-11-k2","title":"變更影響","titleEn":"Change impact","text":"一項局部替換可能跨越結構、熱與維護介面。","textEn":"A local substitution may cross structural, thermal and maintenance interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"材料已更換、外形不變，舊驗證可以如何處理？","questionEn":"Material changes but shape does not. How should previous verification be treated?","options":["外形相同就自動沿用所有舊證據","先審查適用性與影響，再決定需重做部分","僅比較新舊材料密度，不審查其他介面"],"optionsEn":["Automatically reuse every old result because shape is unchanged","Review applicability and impact before selecting re-verification","Compare only density without reviewing other interfaces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"外形一致不足以證明材料變更沒有影響。","explanationEn":"Equal geometry does not establish that a material change has no effect."}},{"id":"c001-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c001-v6-11"],"sourceIds":["v6-a350-family","v6-a350-milestones","v6-faa-composites"],"title":"組成分層驗證證據包","titleEn":"Assemble a layered verification dossier","objective":"把分析、試片、分系統與整合的證據分層。","objectiveEn":"Separate analysis, coupon, subsystem and integration evidence.","instruction":"將前十一道工序的筆記排成矩陣，每列是一項需求，每欄是一種證據。明確標示教學推論、引用事實與尚缺測試；選一項接合需求追蹤到底。","instructionEn":"Arrange the previous eleven task notes in a matrix with requirements as rows and evidence types as columns. Mark teaching deductions, cited facts and missing tests. Trace one joint requirement through the layers.","observation":"完整欄位不代表實際取得證據，空缺應維持可見。","observationEn":"A filled form does not mean evidence was obtained; gaps must remain visible.","failure":"用漂亮模型截圖代替結構試驗或審查紀錄，會高估完成度。","failureEn":"Replacing structural tests or review records with attractive model screenshots overstates completion.","check":"交付一條可追溯證據鏈，且沒有把本課程當作真機製造放行。","checkEn":"Deliver a traceable evidence chain without treating the course as an aircraft manufacturing release.","knowledge":[{"id":"c001-v6-12-k1","title":"驗證階層","titleEn":"Verification hierarchy","text":"局部材料表現與整機整合是不同尺度的問題。","textEn":"Local material behavior and aircraft integration are different scales of problem."},{"id":"c001-v6-12-k2","title":"證據成熟度","titleEn":"Evidence maturity","text":"假設、計畫與已完成量測應有不同狀態。","textEn":"Assumptions, plans and completed measurements need distinct status labels."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項最適合標為「待取得證據」？","questionEn":"Which item should be marked as evidence still to obtain?","options":["已規劃但尚未執行的試驗","已引用並核對的公開首飛日期","已算出的教學重心例題"],"optionsEn":["A planned but unperformed test","A checked and cited public first-flight date","A completed classroom center-of-mass calculation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗計畫不等於試驗結果。","explanationEn":"A test plan is not a test result."}}]}],"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":216,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"c101","title":"Alvin 載人科學潛器","titleEn":"Alvin human-occupied research submersible","category":"marine","summary":"以Alvin公開科學任務為背景，拆解浮力、縱傾、觀測幾何、樣本識別及資料驗證，理解深海研究平台如何服務科學問題。","summaryEn":"Use Alvin’s public science mission to study buoyancy, trim, viewing geometry, sample identity and data verification, linking an ocean platform to scientific questions.","scope":"12道紙上與示意模型任務，數值均為明示教學假設；不提供耐壓艙設計、生命維持規格、載人試驗、真實下潛計畫或操作許可。","scopeEn":"Twelve paper and schematic-model tasks with explicitly hypothetical values. No pressure-hull design, life-support specifications, crewed tests, actual dive planning or operating authorization.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-alvin-history","v6-alvin-systems","v6-alvin-verification"],"diagram":{"type":"submarine","labels":["科學需求","浮力與配平","觀測與取樣","通訊與定位","資料證據"],"labelsEn":["Science requirements","Buoyancy and trim","Observation and sampling","Communication and positioning","Data evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"c101-stage01","order":1,"title":"科學目的與靜力模型","titleEn":"Science purpose and static models","description":"把觀測需求連到壓差、浮力與力矩，區分平台功能與科學目的。","descriptionEn":"Connect observation needs to pressure difference, buoyancy and moments, separating platform function from science purpose.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c101-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":[],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems","v6-alvin-verification"],"title":"把科學問題轉成觀測需求","titleEn":"Turn a science question into observation requirements","objective":"定義潛器要取得的資料，而非只列設備。","objectiveEn":"Define the required data rather than merely listing instruments.","instruction":"設定虛構任務：比較兩處海底岩石外觀。列出影像、樣本識別、位置及時間四欄，說明每欄如何回答問題；不規劃真實下潛。","instructionEn":"Set a fictional mission comparing rock appearance at two seafloor sites. List imagery, sample identity, position and time, explaining how each answers the question. Do not plan an actual dive.","observation":"缺少位置或樣本識別的照片，難以連回同一觀測對象。","observationEn":"A photograph without location or sample identity is difficult to connect to its observation target.","failure":"把相機解析度當成整個任務成功標準，忽略資料脈絡。","failureEn":"Treating camera resolution as the entire success criterion ignores data context.","check":"每項資料均對應科學問題，且有識別與時間欄位。","checkEn":"Each datum maps to the science question and has identity and time fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-01-k1","title":"需求分配","titleEn":"Requirements allocation","text":"科學目的必須轉成可收集、可追溯的資料。","textEn":"A scientific purpose must become collectible, traceable data."},{"id":"c101-v6-01-k2","title":"任務邊界","titleEn":"Mission boundary","text":"教育案例只討論資料需求，不授權現場操作。","textEn":"The educational case addresses data requirements, not operational authorization."}],"quiz":{"question":"要把岩石照片與實體樣本對上，最缺不得的是什麼？","questionEn":"What is essential for matching a rock photograph to its physical sample?","options":["只依相近拍攝時間猜測配對","只依容器擺放順序配對","共同樣本識別碼與記錄"],"optionsEn":["Infer the pairing only from similar capture times","Match only by container placement order","A shared sample identifier and record"],"answer":2,"explanation":"共同識別碼維持影像與樣本間的關聯。","explanationEn":"A shared identifier preserves the image-to-sample relationship."}},{"id":"c101-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-01"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"區分水深與壓差","titleEn":"Distinguish depth from pressure difference","objective":"用靜水概念標記外部與內部環境。","objectiveEn":"Use hydrostatics to label exterior and interior environments.","instruction":"畫一個封閉教學球體，分別標示外部水壓及內部壓力。以p外=p表面+ρgh比較h與2h的水柱貢獻；保持ρ與g不變，不計算艙壁厚度。","instructionEn":"Sketch a closed teaching sphere and label external and internal pressures. Use p_external=p_surface+ρgh to compare water-column contributions at h and 2h with constant density and gravity. Do not calculate wall thickness.","observation":"加倍深度使水柱壓力項加倍，但不使含表面壓力的絕對壓力恰好加倍。","observationEn":"Doubling depth doubles the water-column term, not necessarily the absolute pressure including surface pressure.","failure":"混用絕對壓力與壓差，會使載荷敘述不清。","failureEn":"Mixing absolute pressure with differential pressure obscures the load definition.","check":"圖上同時標出內壓、外壓及兩者差，寫明模型假設。","checkEn":"Label internal, external and differential pressures and state the assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-02-k1","title":"靜水壓力","titleEn":"Hydrostatic pressure","text":"在密度近似固定時，水柱壓力隨深度線性增加。","textEn":"With approximately constant density, water-column pressure grows linearly with depth."},{"id":"c101-v6-02-k2","title":"壓差","titleEn":"Differential pressure","text":"結構兩側環境的差異決定相應載荷問題。","textEn":"The difference between environments on either side defines the corresponding load problem."}],"quiz":{"question":"將h變為2h，哪一項恰好加倍？","questionEn":"When h becomes 2h, which term doubles exactly in this model?","options":["內部壓力必然","ρgh水柱項","所有絕對壓力"],"optionsEn":["The internal pressure necessarily","The ρgh water-column term","Every absolute pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面壓力項不隨水深加倍。","explanationEn":"The surface-pressure term does not double with depth."}},{"id":"c101-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-02"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"建立浮力與重量帳","titleEn":"Build a buoyancy and weight balance","objective":"以排水體積與總質量判斷淨垂直力。","objectiveEn":"Use displaced volume and total mass to determine net vertical force.","instruction":"使用紙上假設ρ=1、g=1、排水體積V=12、質量m=10，算B−W。再加入3單位質量而不改體積，重新判讀；這不是Alvin的實際數值。","instructionEn":"Use paper assumptions ρ=1, g=1, displaced volume V=12 and mass m=10 to compute B−W. Add 3 mass units without changing volume and reassess. These are not Alvin’s actual values.","observation":"初始淨力為+2，增加載重後變成−1。","observationEn":"The initial net force is +2 and becomes −1 after adding the load.","failure":"用物體外觀大小代替實際排水體積，或漏算工具重量，都會改變判定。","failureEn":"Substituting apparent size for displaced volume or omitting tool mass changes the result.","check":"兩種狀態各寫出浮力、重量與淨力符號。","checkEn":"Record buoyancy, weight and net-force sign for both states.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-03-k1","title":"阿基米德原理","titleEn":"Archimedes’ principle","text":"浮力等於排開流體的重量。","textEn":"Buoyancy equals the weight of displaced fluid."},{"id":"c101-v6-03-k2","title":"載荷清單","titleEn":"Payload inventory","text":"新增樣本與工具會改變質量帳，未必等量增加排水體積。","textEn":"Samples and tools change mass without necessarily adding proportional displaced volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"此模型增加3單位質量後，淨力為何？","questionEn":"After adding 3 mass units in this model, what is the net force?","options":["−1，向下","+2，向上","0，必定中性"],"optionsEn":["−1, downward","+2, upward","0, necessarily neutral"],"answer":0,"explanation":"浮力12不變，重量由10變13，淨力為−1。","explanationEn":"Buoyancy stays 12 while weight becomes 13, giving −1."}},{"id":"c101-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-03"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"用力矩理解縱傾","titleEn":"Understand trim through moments","objective":"分開判斷中性浮力與姿態平衡。","objectiveEn":"Separate neutral buoyancy from attitude balance.","instruction":"画側視圖，讓總浮力與重量相等，但兩作用線前後錯開。標出可能的轉動方向，再將一個小教學載荷沿前後移動，觀察力矩符號如何改變。","instructionEn":"Draw a side view with equal buoyancy and weight but fore-aft separation of their lines of action. Mark the possible rotation, then move a small teaching load along the vehicle and examine the moment sign.","observation":"垂直合力為零時，仍可能存在使潛器俯仰的力矩。","observationEn":"Zero vertical resultant can coexist with a pitching moment.","failure":"只檢查重量等於浮力，不能證明姿態已平衡。","failureEn":"Checking weight equals buoyancy alone does not establish attitude equilibrium.","check":"同時列出合力與合力矩兩個條件。","checkEn":"State both force and moment equilibrium conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-04-k1","title":"浮心與重心","titleEn":"Centers of buoyancy and mass","text":"兩者的相對位置影響姿態回應。","textEn":"Their relative locations influence attitude response."},{"id":"c101-v6-04-k2","title":"力偶","titleEn":"Force couple","text":"大小相等、方向相反但作用線不同的力可形成力偶。","textEn":"Equal opposite forces on different lines can form a couple."}],"quiz":{"question":"浮力等於重量但作用線錯開，能否保證不轉動？","questionEn":"If buoyancy equals weight but the lines differ, is no rotation guaranteed?","options":["能，合力零就足夠","只有相機關閉才不能","不能，還要檢查力矩"],"optionsEn":["Yes; zero resultant force is sufficient","Only if the camera is off","No; moments must also be checked"],"answer":2,"explanation":"平移與轉動是不同平衡條件。","explanationEn":"Translational and rotational equilibrium are separate conditions."}}]},{"id":"c101-stage02","order":2,"title":"浮材、能量與取樣介面","titleEn":"Buoyancy material, energy and sampling interfaces","description":"以公開功能介紹和原創案例，檢查材料、照明及工具的相互限制。","descriptionEn":"Use public functions and original examples to examine material, lighting and tool constraints.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c101-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-04"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"比較浮材的功能與限制","titleEn":"Compare buoyancy-material functions and limits","objective":"區分低密度與環境耐受的證據。","objectiveEn":"Separate low density from environmental qualification.","instruction":"依WHOI公開介紹畫浮材、框架與附件的功能圖。對兩種假設材料建立密度、吸水或壓縮行為、固定介面三欄；沒有公開資料的格子保留未知，不提供配方。","instructionEn":"Use WHOI’s overview to sketch buoyancy material, frame and attachments. Compare two hypothetical materials by density, water uptake or compression behavior, and mounting interfaces. Leave unavailable data unknown and supply no formulation.","observation":"材料在表面能浮，不足以證明深水環境中功能維持。","observationEn":"Floating at the surface does not prove retained function in a deep-water environment.","failure":"把低密度視為唯一選材條件，会漏掉環境與連接需求。","failureEn":"Using low density as the sole criterion omits environment and attachment needs.","check":"至少提出一項材料性能及一項固定介面需取得的驗證證據。","checkEn":"Identify evidence needed for one material property and one attachment interface.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-05-k1","title":"功能分工","titleEn":"Functional allocation","text":"浮材提供浮力，框架與附件承擔不同的結構功能。","textEn":"Buoyancy material, frame and attachments perform different functions."},{"id":"c101-v6-05-k2","title":"環境相容","titleEn":"Environmental compatibility","text":"性能需要連同環境及使用時間定義。","textEn":"Performance must be defined together with environment and duration."}],"quiz":{"question":"桌上浮水測試能直接證明哪件事？","questionEn":"What can a tabletop flotation test directly establish?","options":["真實載人任務可用","該次表面條件下的浮水表現","所有深度下的耐久性"],"optionsEn":["Suitability for an actual crewed mission","Flotation behavior under those surface conditions","Durability at every depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"測試結論不能超出其條件。","explanationEn":"A test conclusion cannot exceed its conditions."}},{"id":"c101-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-05"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"編製科學設備能量預算","titleEn":"Budget energy for scientific equipment","objective":"區分功率需求與任務能量需求。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish power demand from mission energy demand.","instruction":"用自訂例題：相機10W開2小時，燈30W開半小時。求總Wh，再加入一項待查的待機消耗；把未知量獨立列出，不宣稱已估算整艇續航。","instructionEn":"Use an invented example: a 10 W camera for two hours and a 30 W light for half an hour. Sum Wh and add an unknown standby term separately. Do not claim to have estimated vehicle endurance.","observation":"相機用20Wh，燈用15Wh；高功率不一定意味較大總能耗。","observationEn":"The camera uses 20 Wh and the light 15 Wh; higher power need not mean higher total energy.","failure":"把W直接相加當作Wh，或漏掉待機時間，會破壞能量帳。","failureEn":"Adding watts as if they were watt-hours or omitting standby time breaks the energy balance.","check":"列出35Wh已知部分、未知待機項及單位。","checkEn":"Report the known 35 Wh subtotal, unknown standby term and units.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-06-k1","title":"功與率","titleEn":"Energy and power","text":"能量是功率對時間的累積。","textEn":"Energy accumulates power over time."},{"id":"c101-v6-06-k2","title":"預算邊界","titleEn":"Budget boundary","text":"科學負載能量不等於全部系統能量。","textEn":"Science-payload energy is not total system energy."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個设备在此例耗能較多？","questionEn":"Which device uses more energy in this example?","options":["相機，20Wh","燈，因為30W較大","兩者相同"],"optionsEn":["Camera, 20 Wh","Light, because 30 W is larger","They use the same energy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"必須同時考慮功率與使用時間。","explanationEn":"Both power and duration matter."}},{"id":"c101-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-06"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"安排照明與影像幾何","titleEn":"Arrange lighting and imaging geometry","objective":"理解照明方向與懸浮粒子對影像的影響。","objectiveEn":"Understand lighting direction and suspended-particle effects.","instruction":"畫相機、目標及兩個不同方向的燈位。用示意光線標出直接照明與可能回到鏡頭的散射路徑；比較目標對比與陰影，不把示意圖當作已取得的水下照片。","instructionEn":"Sketch a camera, target and two lighting positions. Trace direct illumination and possible particle-scattered paths into the lens. Compare contrast and shadows without treating the diagram as acquired underwater photography.","observation":"更多光不一定帶来更多可辨識細節，散射也可能增加。","observationEn":"More light does not necessarily reveal more detail; scattering may also increase.","failure":"只提高亮度而不查光路，會把曝光與可辨識度混為一談。","failureEn":"Increasing brightness without checking geometry confuses exposure with interpretability.","check":"在兩張圖上各標出一項改善及一項代價。","checkEn":"Mark one benefit and one trade-off on each diagram.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-07-k1","title":"散射","titleEn":"Scattering","text":"水中粒子可把光送回相機，降低目標對比。","textEn":"Particles can scatter light back toward the camera and reduce target contrast."},{"id":"c101-v6-07-k2","title":"幾何證據","titleEn":"Geometric evidence","text":"影像判讀需要相機、光源與目標的相對位置。","textEn":"Image interpretation benefits from relative camera, source and target positions."}],"quiz":{"question":"燈變亮但目標更難辨識，合理的下一步是？","questionEn":"The light is brighter but the target is harder to distinguish. What is a reasonable next step?","options":["只用相機的標稱像素數解釋影像品質","只繼續增加亮度，不檢查光路","檢查散射與照明幾何"],"optionsEn":["Explain quality only from the camera pixel count","Continue increasing brightness without checking optical paths","Inspect scattering and lighting geometry"],"answer":2,"explanation":"亮度與有用影像資訊不是同一量。","explanationEn":"Brightness and useful image information are not the same quantity."}},{"id":"c101-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-07"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems","v6-alvin-verification"],"title":"檢查取樣工具的可達範圍","titleEn":"Check sampling-tool reach","objective":"把觀測視野、工具路徑與樣本容器接起來。","objectiveEn":"Connect viewing field, tool path and sample container.","instruction":"用平面示意圖放置相機視野、兩節教學手臂、樣本與容器。画取樣前後的工具姿態，检查路径是否遮住視野或碰到其他設備；不使用真機關節設定。","instructionEn":"On a plan-view schematic, place a camera field, a two-link teaching arm, a sample and a container. Draw before/after tool poses and inspect obscured views or equipment intersections, without using real joint settings.","observation":"端點能碰到樣本，不代表整段手臂路徑無衝突。","observationEn":"Reaching the sample with the endpoint does not prove the whole arm path is clear.","failure":"忽略手臂中間連桿或樣本外形，會低估碰撞範圍。","failureEn":"Ignoring intermediate links or sample shape underestimates collision extent.","check":"保留起點、過渡點及終點三個姿態，皆核對視野與空間。","checkEn":"Retain start, intermediate and end poses, checking view and clearance at each.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-08-k1","title":"可達與可行","titleEn":"Reachable and feasible","text":"幾何可達只是任務可行的必要條件之一。","textEn":"Geometric reachability is only one condition for task feasibility."},{"id":"c101-v6-08-k2","title":"樣本脈絡","titleEn":"Sample context","text":"取樣前影像與容器識別維持科學證據鏈。","textEn":"Pre-sampling imagery and container identity preserve scientific context."}],"quiz":{"question":"工具端點路徑無碰撞，還要看什麼？","questionEn":"The tool endpoint path is clear. What else must be checked?","options":["只比較起點與終點的工具位置","所有連桿及樣本的掃掠空間","只檢查空載手臂，不納入樣本外形"],"optionsEn":["Compare only initial and final tool positions","Swept space of every link and the sample","Check only the empty arm, excluding the sample shape"],"answer":1,"explanation":"碰撞可發生在端點以外的任何部分。","explanationEn":"Collision can occur on parts other than the endpoint."}}]},{"id":"c101-stage03","order":3,"title":"定位、紀錄與科學驗證","titleEn":"Positioning, records and science verification","description":"用量測模型與資料流程檢查樣本是否能連回原問題。","descriptionEn":"Use measurement models and data flows to check whether samples can be traced to the original question.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c101-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-08"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"閱讀聲學測距的不確定性","titleEn":"Read uncertainty in acoustic ranging","objective":"區分傳播時間、距離與位置估計。","objectiveEn":"Separate travel time, range and position estimation.","instruction":"假設聲速c固定、量得雙程時間t，寫出距離r=ct/2。再將時間誤差寫成±Δt，求距離誤差項；全部符號計算，不假裝提供航次數據。","instructionEn":"Assume constant sound speed c and measured round-trip time t, giving r=ct/2. Introduce timing error ±Δt and derive the range-error term. Use symbolic calculations without implying expedition data are supplied.","observation":"單一距離只限制在等距位置集合上，不能獨立決定完整位置。","observationEn":"One range constrains a set of equal-distance positions, not a complete position.","failure":"漏除以2會把雙程路徑當作單程距離。","failureEn":"Omitting division by two treats the round-trip path as one-way range.","check":"寫出r及±cΔt/2，並列出還缺的幾何或量測資訊。","checkEn":"Write r and ±cΔt/2, then list missing geometry or measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-09-k1","title":"雙程時間","titleEn":"Round-trip timing","text":"發送到回收的時間包含去程與回程。","textEn":"Transmit-to-return time includes outward and return travel."},{"id":"c101-v6-09-k2","title":"量測到定位","titleEn":"Measurement to position","text":"定位需要足夠幾何約束，也受環境模型影響。","textEn":"Positioning requires sufficient geometric constraints and depends on environmental models."}],"quiz":{"question":"用雙程時間求單程距離，為何除以2？","questionEn":"Why divide round-trip travel time by two when finding one-way range?","options":["聲音走了來回兩段","為了把時鐘誤差直接減半","為了補償往返的聲能損失"],"optionsEn":["The sound travels outward and back","To halve the clock error directly","To compensate for acoustic energy lost on the return trip"],"answer":0,"explanation":"距離為 r=ct/2；聲速固定時，時間誤差對應距離誤差 ±cΔt/2。雙程時間包含去程與回程，除以2是路徑換算，不是消除時鐘誤差。","explanationEn":"Range is r=ct/2. With fixed sound speed, a time error gives range error ±cΔt/2. Round-trip time includes outward and return paths; dividing by two converts path length, not clock error."}},{"id":"c101-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-09"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-systems"],"title":"建立水下訊息的確認流程","titleEn":"Build an underwater-message acknowledgment flow","objective":"在有限通訊下分辨已送出與已收到。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish sent from received under constrained communication.","instruction":"為虛構科學任務畫三個訊息狀態：待送、已送、已確認。给影像摘要加序號與時間；假設一則確認遺失，安排重傳時如何避免重複記錄。","instructionEn":"Create pending, sent and acknowledged states for a fictional science message. Add sequence and time to an image summary. Assume an acknowledgment is lost and specify how retransmission avoids duplicate records.","observation":"發送端沒有確認，不等於接收端一定沒收到。","observationEn":"Lack of acknowledgment does not prove the receiver got nothing.","failure":"重傳訊息沒有識別碼，可能被當作第二筆觀測。","failureEn":"Retransmission without an identifier may be mistaken for a second observation.","check":"用同一序號演練一次確認遺失，接收紀錄只保留一筆邏輯資料。","checkEn":"Walk through one lost acknowledgment using the same sequence ID, retaining one logical record.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-10-k1","title":"通訊狀態","titleEn":"Communication state","text":"傳送成功、接收成功與應用處理完成並不相同。","textEn":"Transmission, reception and application processing are distinct successes."},{"id":"c101-v6-10-k2","title":"冪等處理","titleEn":"Idempotent handling","text":"重複收到同一識別訊息，不應重複產生相同資料事件。","textEn":"Receiving the same identified message repeatedly should not duplicate its data event."}],"quiz":{"question":"確認遺失後重傳，最有用的欄位是？","questionEn":"Which field is most useful when retransmitting after a lost acknowledgment?","options":["每次重傳都產生新的訊息識別碼","只依接收時間判斷是否重複","穩定的訊息識別碼"],"optionsEn":["Generate a new message identifier for every retransmission","Determine duplicates solely from reception time","A stable message identifier"],"answer":2,"explanation":"穩定識別有助於區分重傳與新資料。","explanationEn":"Stable identity distinguishes retransmission from new data."}},{"id":"c101-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-10"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-verification"],"title":"核對影像、樣本與時間鏈","titleEn":"Reconcile image, sample and time records","objective":"讓不同設備資料能對應同一事件。","objectiveEn":"Associate records from different devices with one event.","instruction":"自製三筆示意觀測，記錄相機時間、採样時間及樣本編號。刻意讓一台時鐘快2分鐘，計算校正後配對，再保留原始時間與校正說明。","instructionEn":"Create three synthetic observations with camera time, sampling time and sample ID. Make one clock two minutes fast, pair events after correction, and retain raw times and the correction note.","observation":"時間一致應指同一基準，而非只看數字接近。","observationEn":"Time consistency means a common reference, not merely similar numbers.","failure":"直接覆寫原始時間會失去重建判讀過程的線索。","failureEn":"Overwriting raw timestamps removes evidence needed to reconstruct interpretation.","check":"每組配對能追到原始紀錄、時間偏移與樣本識別。","checkEn":"Trace each pairing to raw records, clock offset and sample identity.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-11-k1","title":"溯源","titleEn":"Provenance","text":"保留原始值與處理步驟，才能重現結果。","textEn":"Retaining raw values and processing steps enables reproducibility."},{"id":"c101-v6-11-k2","title":"同步誤差","titleEn":"Synchronization error","text":"設備時鐘偏差可能造成事件錯配。","textEn":"Clock offsets can misassociate events."}],"quiz":{"question":"發現固定2分鐘偏差，較好的紀錄方法是？","questionEn":"A constant two-minute offset is discovered. What is the better record practice?","options":["忽略偏差只看檔案順序","保留原始時間並另存校正值與方法","直接覆寫所有原始時間"],"optionsEn":["Ignore it and rely on file order","Keep raw time and separately record corrected time and method","Overwrite all raw timestamps"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分開保存原始與處理後資料可重建證據鏈。","explanationEn":"Keeping raw and processed data separately preserves the evidence chain."}},{"id":"c101-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c101-v6-11"],"sourceIds":["v6-alvin-history","v6-alvin-systems","v6-alvin-verification"],"title":"區分工程驗證與科學驗證","titleEn":"Separate engineering and science verification","objective":"把平台可用與資料可用分成不同證據。","objectiveEn":"Separate platform readiness from data usability.","instruction":"閱讀WHOI的2022年科學驗證公開說明。將本課程成果分成平台概念、工具功能及資料品質三欄，為每欄寫一項已完成紙上檢查與一項仍需專業實測的問題。","instructionEn":"Read WHOI’s public account of 2022 science verification. Sort course outcomes into platform concepts, tool functions and data quality, giving one completed paper check and one question requiring professional measurement in each.","observation":"平台完成某項測試，並不自動證明所有樣本與影像符合科學目的。","observationEn":"Passing one platform test does not automatically establish that all samples and images meet scientific goals.","failure":"將公開認證深度當作本課程模型的操作許可，是範圍錯置。","failureEn":"Treating a publicly reported depth certification as operating permission for a teaching model is a scope error.","check":"交付三欄驗證表，清楚標示本課程只完成教育分析。","checkEn":"Deliver the three-column matrix, clearly identifying the work as educational analysis only.","knowledge":[{"id":"c101-v6-12-k1","title":"分層驗證","titleEn":"Layered verification","text":"系統安全、工具功能與資料適用性需要各自的證據。","textEn":"System safety, tool function and data fitness need their own evidence."},{"id":"c101-v6-12-k2","title":"科學可用性","titleEn":"Scientific usability","text":"資料必須能回答原定問題，才算有用的觀測。","textEn":"Data must answer the intended question to be a useful observation."}],"quiz":{"question":"工具動作正常，但樣本標籤混亂，哪項仍未通過？","questionEn":"The tool works, but sample labels are confused. Which aspect remains unverified?","options":["科學資料的可追溯性","工具一定無法移動","所有工程测试均失敗"],"optionsEn":["Scientific-data traceability","The tool necessarily cannot move","Every engineering test has failed"],"answer":0,"explanation":"功能正常與資料追溯是不同驗證項。","explanationEn":"Functional operation and data traceability are distinct checks."}}]}],"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":216,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"c213","title":"Toyota Prius 油電混合車","titleEn":"Toyota Prius hybrid vehicle","category":"automotive","summary":"從公開THS架構出發，用能量帳、理想齒輪、回生與儲能例題理解Prius油電整合，並練習公平比較不同駕駛與世代條件。","summaryEn":"Start from the public THS architecture and use energy balances, ideal gearing, regeneration and storage exercises to understand Prius hybrid integration and fair comparisons.","scope":"12道原創概念任務；1997與2003資料僅用於架構及歷史。數值不是任何Prius的ECU標定、電池規格或制動設定；不進行高壓系統拆裝或車輛改裝。","scopeEn":"Twelve original conceptual tasks; 1997 and 2003 sources support architecture and history. Values are not Prius ECU calibration, battery specifications or brake settings. No high-voltage disassembly or vehicle modification.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths","v6-prius-2003","v6-toyota-kaikan"],"diagram":{"type":"car","labels":["燃油與引擎","功率分流","電池與電機","車輪與制動","能量與熱帳"],"labelsEn":["Fuel and engine","Power split","Battery and machines","Wheels and braking","Energy and heat balance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"c213-stage01","order":1,"title":"能量邊界與分流原理","titleEn":"Energy boundaries and power-split principles","description":"先畫能量流，再以功率、時間和理想速度約束檢查單位與邊界。","descriptionEn":"Map energy flows, then check units and boundaries through power, time and ideal speed constraints.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c213-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":[],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"界定油電系統的能量邊界","titleEn":"Define the hybrid energy boundary","objective":"辨識燃油、電池、車輪功與熱的能量角色。","objectiveEn":"Identify the energy roles of fuel, battery, wheel work and heat.","instruction":"畫燃油、引擎、發電機、電池、馬達與車輪方塊。以箭頭連接可能能量流，另畫散熱出口；比較行程時保留電池起終儲能，避免把回生當成新能量來源。","instructionEn":"Draw fuel, engine, generator, battery, motor and wheel blocks. Connect possible energy paths and add heat exits. Retain initial and final battery energy when comparing trips, rather than treating regeneration as a new energy source.","observation":"電池可在不同時刻吸收或釋放能量，其起終差影響比較。","observationEn":"The battery can absorb or release energy at different times; its net change affects comparisons.","failure":"只看燃油消耗，卻忽略行程結束時電池少了能量，會偏估效率。","failureEn":"Comparing fuel alone while ignoring a depleted battery biases the efficiency assessment.","check":"圖上有能量輸入、儲存、有用輸出與損失四類。","checkEn":"Show energy input, storage, useful output and losses.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-01-k1","title":"能量守恆","titleEn":"Energy conservation","text":"能量轉換會改變形式，回生不會憑空創造能量。","textEn":"Conversion changes energy form; regeneration does not create energy."},{"id":"c213-v6-01-k2","title":"比較邊界","titleEn":"Comparison boundary","text":"相同行程也要比較電池儲能變化，才有一致邊界。","textEn":"Even equal trips require battery-energy changes to establish a consistent boundary."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項必須納入兩次行程的公平能量比較？","questionEn":"What must be included for a fair energy comparison between two trips?","options":["只比較燃油消耗，即使電池終點不同","把回生當成系統外新增的能量輸入","電池起點與終點的儲能差"],"optionsEn":["Compare fuel alone even when final battery states differ","Treat regeneration as new energy entering from outside the system","The initial-to-final battery-energy change"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電池能量差代表行程使用或留下的儲能。","explanationEn":"Battery-energy change represents stored energy used or retained by the trip."}},{"id":"c213-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-01"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"把功率曲線換成能量","titleEn":"Convert a power profile into energy","objective":"用時間積分分清kW與kWh。","objectiveEn":"Separate kW and kWh through time integration.","instruction":"使用虛構輪端需求：10kW維持6分鐘、20kW維持3分鐘。各自換算小時後求能量，再畫等能量但不同峰值的另一條曲線。","instructionEn":"Use fictional wheel demand of 10 kW for 6 minutes and 20 kW for 3 minutes. Convert time to hours, calculate each energy and sketch another profile with equal energy but a different peak.","observation":"兩段各1kWh，總計2kWh；峰值與累積量不同。","observationEn":"Each interval is 1 kWh, totaling 2 kWh; peak and accumulation differ.","failure":"把分鐘直接乘上kW卻標成kWh，會產生60倍單位錯誤。","failureEn":"Multiplying minutes by kW and labeling the result kWh creates a factor-of-60 error.","check":"每段保留時間換算，總面積為2kWh。","checkEn":"Retain each time conversion and obtain a total area of 2 kWh.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-02-k1","title":"功率積分","titleEn":"Power integration","text":"固定功率下E=Pt，變動功率則累加分段面積。","textEn":"For constant power E=Pt; varying power requires summing interval areas."},{"id":"c213-v6-02-k2","title":"峰值需求","titleEn":"Peak demand","text":"相同總能量仍可能需要不同的峰值供能能力。","textEn":"Equal total energy can require different peak power capability."}],"quiz":{"question":"20kW維持3分鐘的能量是多少？","questionEn":"How much energy is 20 kW sustained for 3 minutes?","options":["0.15kWh","1kWh","60kWh"],"optionsEn":["0.15 kWh","1 kWh","60 kWh"],"answer":1,"explanation":"3分鐘是0.05小時，20×0.05=1。","explanationEn":"Three minutes is 0.05 hours; 20×0.05=1."}},{"id":"c213-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-02"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"畫出功率分流的两條路徑","titleEn":"Draw two power-split paths","objective":"區分機械傳遞與電力轉換路徑。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish mechanical transmission from electrical conversion.","instruction":"參照Toyota公開系統圖，原創重畫引擎到車輪的機械路徑及經發電機、電力系統、馬達的路徑。再畫電池可接入的位置，不把某次分流比例寫成固定常數。","instructionEn":"Using Toyota’s public system diagram as a reference, redraw the engine-to-wheel mechanical path and the path through generator, electrical system and motor. Add the battery connection without treating one power split as a fixed ratio.","observation":"車輪可由不同能量路徑共同驅動，路徑需隨情境辨識。","observationEn":"Different energy paths can contribute to wheel drive and must be identified by scenario.","failure":"把所有引擎能量都畫成先進電池，混淆功率分流與純串聯系統。","failureEn":"Routing all engine energy through the battery confuses power splitting with a purely series system.","check":"兩條路徑都可從引擎追蹤到車輪，電池為儲能分支。","checkEn":"Trace both paths from engine to wheels, showing the battery as storage.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-03-k1","title":"分流裝置","titleEn":"Power-split device","text":"公開THS架構把引擎功率分配到機械與發電路徑。","textEn":"The public THS architecture distributes engine power between mechanical and generation paths."},{"id":"c213-v6-03-k2","title":"轉換損失","titleEn":"Conversion loss","text":"經過不同轉換次數的路徑，損失與限制不一定相同。","textEn":"Paths with different conversion stages need not have equal losses or limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪張圖較符合公開THS分流概念？","questionEn":"Which diagram better matches the public THS power-split concept?","options":["引擎同時可連向車輪及發電機","引擎所有能量都必須先存入電池","引擎僅機械驅動車輪，電機僅用於起動"],"optionsEn":["The engine can connect toward both wheels and generator","All engine energy must first be stored in the battery","The engine only drives mechanically and the electrical machine only starts it"],"answer":0,"explanation":"功率分流包含機械路徑，不是所有能量都必經電池。","explanationEn":"Power splitting includes a mechanical path; not all energy must pass through the battery."}},{"id":"c213-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-03"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"閱讀行星齒輪的速度約束","titleEn":"Read a planetary-gear speed constraint","objective":"理解三個轉速並非可任意獨立選擇。","objectiveEn":"Understand that three rotational speeds are not independent.","instruction":"用理想教學齒輪關係(Ns+Nr)ωc=Nsωs+Nrωr，假設Ns=1、Nr=2，令ωs=0、ωr=3，求ωc。圖上只標太陽輪、環齒輪及行星架，不聲稱這是任一Prius的齒數。","instructionEn":"Use the ideal teaching relation (Ns+Nr)ωc=Nsωs+Nrωr with Ns=1, Nr=2, ωs=0 and ωr=3. Solve for ωc. Label sun, ring and carrier without claiming these are Prius tooth counts.","observation":"三項轉速受同一幾何關係約束，結果ωc=2。","observationEn":"The three speeds share one kinematic constraint, giving ωc=2.","failure":"把三個轉速各自任意設置，通常無法同時符合齒輪嚙合關係。","failureEn":"Arbitrarily choosing all three speeds generally violates the gear constraint.","check":"將結果代回等式，左右兩側皆為6。","checkEn":"Substitute the result and obtain 6 on both sides.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-04-k1","title":"運動約束","titleEn":"Kinematic constraint","text":"齒輪嚙合限制相對運動，不等於固定所有軸的轉速比例。","textEn":"Gear engagement constrains relative motion without fixing every shaft-speed ratio."},{"id":"c213-v6-04-k2","title":"模型層級","titleEn":"Model level","text":"理想速度方程未包含損失、控制器或實際零件限制。","textEn":"An ideal speed equation excludes losses, controllers and actual component limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"此例的行星架轉速ωc為多少？","questionEn":"What is the carrier speed ωc in this example?","options":["3","6","2"],"optionsEn":["3","6","2"],"answer":2,"explanation":"3ωc=1×0+2×3，故ωc=2。","explanationEn":"3ωc=1×0+2×3, so ωc=2."}}]},{"id":"c213-stage02","order":2,"title":"駕駛情境與儲能變化","titleEn":"Driving scenarios and stored energy","description":"使用虛構加速、制動與儲能案例，避免把效率、功率和能量混為一談。","descriptionEn":"Use fictional acceleration, braking and storage cases to distinguish efficiency, power and energy.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c213-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-04"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"核對加速時的瞬時功率帳","titleEn":"Check an acceleration power balance","objective":"辨識多來源供能與轉換損失。","objectiveEn":"Identify multiple power contributions and conversion losses.","instruction":"設教學時刻輪端需30kW，引擎路徑提供18kW、電池經馬達提供15kW。計算總輸入與差額，將差額列為簡化損失項；不要當作車輛效率實測。兩項功率是同一共同邊界的上游輸入，假設邊界內儲能不變且無其他功率流。","instructionEn":"At a teaching instant, assume wheel demand is 30 kW, with 18 kW from an engine path and 15 kW from a battery/motor path. Calculate total input and the residual as a simplified loss term, not measured vehicle efficiency. Both inputs cross the same system boundary; assume no change in stored energy inside that boundary and no other power flows.","observation":"供能33kW與輪端30kW之間有3kW差額。","observationEn":"There is a 3 kW residual between 33 kW supplied and 30 kW at the wheels.","failure":"把不同介面量到的功率直接當同一位置，會重複計算或漏算損失。","failureEn":"Treating power measured at different interfaces as one location can double-count or omit losses.","check":"各功率標清量測邊界，帳目以同一時刻平衡。","checkEn":"Label the boundary for each power and balance one instant consistently.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-05-k1","title":"瞬時平衡","titleEn":"Instantaneous balance","text":"功率帳必須對應相同時刻與清楚的系統邊界。","textEn":"A power balance requires the same instant and clear system boundaries."},{"id":"c213-v6-05-k2","title":"殘差判讀","titleEn":"Residual interpretation","text":"帳目差可能代表損失、儲能變化或量測不一致，需先定義模型。","textEn":"A residual may represent loss, storage change or inconsistent measurement; define the model first."}],"quiz":{"question":"在已定義的簡化例題中，損失項是多少？","questionEn":"In this defined simplified example, what is the loss term?","options":["63kW","3kW","12kW"],"optionsEn":["63 kW","3 kW","12 kW"],"answer":1,"explanation":"18+15−30=3kW。","explanationEn":"18+15−30=3 kW."}},{"id":"c213-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-05"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"比較效率點與整體油耗","titleEn":"Compare operating efficiency with trip fuel use","objective":"避免把引擎最佳效率點當作永遠可用的答案。","objectiveEn":"Avoid treating an engine’s best-efficiency point as always available.","instruction":"自畫兩個假設運轉點：A的需求10、效率0.25，B的需求20、效率0.40。比較輸入需求P/η，再列出多餘能量是否可儲存及何時需要它；不使用OEM效率圖。","instructionEn":"Invent operating points A with output 10 and efficiency 0.25, and B with output 20 and efficiency 0.40. Compare input P/η, then ask whether surplus energy can be stored and when it is needed. Use no OEM efficiency map.","observation":"效率較高的B，其瞬時輸入仍可能較大。","observationEn":"The more efficient point B can still have higher instantaneous input.","failure":"只看效率百分比而忽略需求與儲能限制，會選錯比較邊界。","failureEn":"Looking only at efficiency percentage ignores demand and storage constraints.","check":"列出A輸入40、B輸入50，以及不能直接比較全程油耗的原因。","checkEn":"Report inputs of 40 and 50 and explain why they do not directly compare trip fuel use.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-06-k1","title":"效率定義","titleEn":"Efficiency definition","text":"效率是有用輸出與輸入的比值，不是輸入的絕對大小。","textEn":"Efficiency is useful output divided by input, not the absolute input magnitude."},{"id":"c213-v6-06-k2","title":"時間協調","titleEn":"Time coordination","text":"混合動力可跨時間安排能量，但仍受儲能與損失限制。","textEn":"A hybrid can coordinate energy over time, subject to storage and loss constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"較高效率點一定消耗較少瞬時輸入嗎？","questionEn":"Does a higher-efficiency point always use less instantaneous input?","options":["不一定，還要看輸出需求","一定，只要效率百分比較高","只要兩點的時間相同就一定較少"],"optionsEn":["No; output demand also matters","Yes, whenever its efficiency percentage is higher","Yes, as long as both points last equally long"],"answer":0,"explanation":"輸入等於輸出除以效率，兩個量都影響結果。","explanationEn":"Input equals output divided by efficiency, so both quantities matter."}},{"id":"c213-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-06"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"分析回生制動的能量上限","titleEn":"Analyze an energy limit for regeneration","objective":"區分可回收動能與实际儲存能量。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish recoverable kinetic energy from stored energy.","instruction":"以E=mv²/2比較同質量在v與2v時的動能。假設某次減速有100教學能量單位、總回收比例0.6，求儲存與未回收部分；這不是真車制動設定。","instructionEn":"Use E=mv²/2 to compare kinetic energy at v and 2v for equal mass. For a fictional slowdown with 100 energy units and a total recovery fraction of 0.6, calculate stored and unrecovered portions. This is not a brake setting.","observation":"速度加倍使動能成4倍；例題只能存回60單位。","observationEn":"Doubling speed quadruples kinetic energy; the example stores only 60 units.","failure":"把每次制動的全部動能都算入電池，忽略轉換與接收限制。","failureEn":"Counting all braking energy as battery storage ignores conversion and acceptance limits.","check":"能量帳為60回收加40未回收，且不超過100。","checkEn":"Show 60 recovered plus 40 unrecovered, never exceeding 100.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-07-k1","title":"動能平方律","titleEn":"Kinetic-energy square law","text":"質量固定時，動能與速度平方成正比。","textEn":"At fixed mass, kinetic energy is proportional to speed squared."},{"id":"c213-v6-07-k2","title":"回收限制","titleEn":"Recovery limits","text":"電池接收能力、系統損失與行駛情境限制回生。","textEn":"Battery acceptance, system losses and driving conditions limit regeneration."}],"quiz":{"question":"同質量速度加倍，動能變為多少倍？","questionEn":"For the same mass, doubling speed multiplies kinetic energy by what?","options":["2倍","1/2倍","4倍"],"optionsEn":["2","1/2","4"],"answer":2,"explanation":"動能包含v²項。","explanationEn":"Kinetic energy contains v²."}},{"id":"c213-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-07"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"追蹤電池儲能狀態","titleEn":"Track battery stored-energy state","objective":"把充放電事件排成可核對的能量序列。","objectiveEn":"Arrange charge/discharge events into an auditable energy sequence.","instruction":"假設可用儲能窗10單位，起始6；先放出2，再接收1.2。計算各時刻存量並對照0至10示意範圍；不把百分比當成真實電池電壓。","instructionEn":"Assume a usable 10-unit storage window starting at 6. Discharge 2, then receive 1.2. Compute each state within the teaching range 0–10, without equating a percentage to actual battery voltage.","observation":"最終為5.2，與起點差−0.8。","observationEn":"The final state is 5.2, a change of −0.8 from the start.","failure":"用總充電量當最終存量，會漏掉初始條件與放電。","failureEn":"Using total charge received as final stored energy omits the initial state and discharge.","check":"列出6→4→5.2，能量增減與每個事件一致。","checkEn":"Show 6→4→5.2 with changes matching each event.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-08-k1","title":"狀態量","titleEn":"State variable","text":"儲能取決於初始狀態與之後累積的能量變化。","textEn":"Stored energy depends on the initial state and accumulated changes."},{"id":"c213-v6-08-k2","title":"估計與量測","titleEn":"Estimation and measurement","text":"電池狀態估計不能僅靠任意單一百分比推回完整物理狀態。","textEn":"A battery-state estimate cannot be reconstructed fully from an arbitrary percentage alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"例題行程結束，比起點少多少儲能？","questionEn":"How much stored energy is lost relative to the start in this example?","options":["5.2單位","0.8單位","1.2單位"],"optionsEn":["5.2 units","0.8 units","1.2 units"],"answer":1,"explanation":"6−5.2=0.8。","explanationEn":"6−5.2=0.8."}}]},{"id":"c213-stage03","order":3,"title":"熱、功能與比較證據","titleEn":"Heat, function and comparison evidence","description":"從熱帳與回生受限情境走向條件一致、版本明確的工程比較。","descriptionEn":"Move from heat balance and limited regeneration to comparisons with matched conditions and explicit versions.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c213-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-08"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"建立損失到散熱的路徑","titleEn":"Trace losses into thermal management","objective":"把電力與機械損失連到熱負荷。","objectiveEn":"Connect electrical and mechanical losses to heat loads.","instruction":"在原創能量圖上標出馬達、電力轉換與電池的假設損失位置。使用簡化熱帳：產熱8單位、散熱5單位，標示內能增加方向；不指定真車冷卻液或溫度。","instructionEn":"Mark hypothetical motor, power-conversion and battery losses on your energy diagram. Use a simplified heat balance with 8 units generated and 5 removed, indicating the direction of internal-energy change. Specify no vehicle coolant or temperature.","observation":"持續產熱大於散熱時，儲存熱能會增加。","observationEn":"Stored thermal energy increases when generation persistently exceeds removal.","failure":"只查瞬時電功率而忽略時間累積，可能漏掉熱負荷。","failureEn":"Checking instantaneous electrical power alone can miss accumulated thermal loading.","check":"寫出+3單位內能變化，並指出還缺熱容量才能估溫升。","checkEn":"Record +3 units of internal-energy change and identify heat capacity as needed for temperature rise.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-09-k1","title":"熱平衡","titleEn":"Thermal balance","text":"產熱、散熱與儲熱需同時納入。","textEn":"Generation, removal and storage all belong in the heat balance."},{"id":"c213-v6-09-k2","title":"模型不足","titleEn":"Model incompleteness","text":"沒有熱容量與邊界條件，不能由能量差直接得溫度。","textEn":"Without heat capacity and boundary conditions, an energy difference does not determine temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"產熱8、散熱5，能否直接知道溫度？","questionEn":"With generation 8 and removal 5, can temperature be known directly?","options":["不能，尚需熱容量等條件","能，必定是3°C","能，必定維持不變"],"optionsEn":["No; heat capacity and other conditions are needed","Yes, it must be 3°C","Yes, it must stay unchanged"],"answer":0,"explanation":"能量差與溫度差的單位和意義不同。","explanationEn":"Energy difference and temperature difference have different units and meanings."}},{"id":"c213-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-09"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths"],"title":"分析回生受限時的制動需求","titleEn":"Analyze braking demand when regeneration is limited","objective":"分開處理車輛減速需求與能量回收能力。","objectiveEn":"Separate required deceleration from energy-recovery capability.","instruction":"在紙上列出假設減速需求與可用回生兩欄。安排一個電池暫不能接收能量的情境，指出總制動功能仍需由合格整車系統滿足；僅做功能分析，不改制動控制。","instructionEn":"On paper, list hypothetical deceleration demand and available regeneration. Introduce a battery-unavailable-for-charging scenario and identify that overall braking must still be met by the qualified vehicle system. Analyze functions only; do not alter brake control.","observation":"回生降低不代表駕駛的減速需求同時消失。","observationEn":"Reduced regeneration does not remove the driver’s braking demand.","failure":"把回收能量視為唯一制動能力，會混淆安全功能與效率功能。","failureEn":"Treating recovery as the sole braking capability confuses safety and efficiency functions.","check":"列出能量回收、總減速及狀態提示三項不同需求。","checkEn":"List energy recovery, total deceleration and status indication as distinct requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-10-k1","title":"功能協調","titleEn":"Functional coordination","text":"多種制動作用需在整車層級協調驗證。","textEn":"Different braking contributions require vehicle-level coordination and verification."},{"id":"c213-v6-10-k2","title":"受限狀態","titleEn":"Limited availability","text":"能量儲存的限制可能改變回收能力。","textEn":"Storage constraints can change recovery capability."}],"quiz":{"question":"電池不能接收回生能量時，仍須满足什麼？","questionEn":"When the battery cannot accept regenerated energy, what remains necessary?","options":["保持與電池可充電時完全相同的回收量","把回生能力當成唯一總制動需求","整車規定的減速功能"],"optionsEn":["Maintain exactly the same recovery as when charging was available","Treat regeneration capability as the sole overall braking requirement","The vehicle’s required deceleration function"],"answer":2,"explanation":"效率功能受限不能取代總制動需求。","explanationEn":"A recovery limitation does not replace the overall braking requirement."}},{"id":"c213-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-10"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths","v6-prius-2003"],"title":"設計公平的行程比較","titleEn":"Design a fair trip comparison","objective":"控制影響油耗比較的條件。","objectiveEn":"Control conditions that affect fuel-use comparisons.","instruction":"自製兩次虛構行程紀錄欄位：距離、速度歷程、坡度、載重、環境與電池起終狀態。找出其中一項不一致時應如何限制結論；不自填真實油耗數據。","instructionEn":"Create fields for two fictional trips: distance, speed profile, grade, payload, environment and initial/final battery state. Explain how a mismatch in one field limits conclusions, without inventing measured fuel data.","observation":"相同距離並不保证相同交通、載荷或能量邊界。","observationEn":"Equal distance does not guarantee equal traffic, load or energy boundaries.","failure":"把不同測試循環的公開數字直接排名，可能比較的是條件而非技術。","failureEn":"Ranking numbers from different test cycles may compare conditions rather than technology.","check":"列出至少三個需一致的條件及一項仍存在的不確定性。","checkEn":"List at least three conditions to match and one remaining uncertainty.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-11-k1","title":"實驗控制","titleEn":"Experimental control","text":"比較需要限定變動因素，並記錄無法控制的因素。","textEn":"Comparison requires limiting changing factors and recording uncontrolled ones."},{"id":"c213-v6-11-k2","title":"重複性","titleEn":"Repeatability","text":"單次結果不足以描述變動範圍。","textEn":"A single result does not describe variability."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩次行程距離相同，就能直接比較技術效率嗎？","questionEn":"Are equal trip distances enough to compare technical efficiency directly?","options":["只要車款名稱相同就能","不能，還需匹配其他條件與能量邊界","能，距離是唯一因素"],"optionsEn":["Only matching the model name is needed","No; other conditions and energy boundaries must match","Yes; distance is the only factor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"公平比較涉及負载、速度、環境與儲能狀態。","explanationEn":"A fair comparison involves load, speed, environment and stored-energy state."}},{"id":"c213-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c213-v6-11"],"sourceIds":["v6-prius-ths","v6-prius-2003","v6-toyota-kaikan"],"title":"交付分世代的油電證據圖","titleEn":"Deliver a generation-specific hybrid evidence map","objective":"區分跨世代原理與某一車型的具體實作。","objectiveEn":"Separate cross-generation principles from model-specific implementation.","instruction":"把1997公開THS架構與2003 THS II發表放在时间線。將本課程的能量守恆、分流、回生和熱帳標為可轉移原理；把硬體數值及控制標定列為需按年份查證。","instructionEn":"Place the 1997 public THS architecture and 2003 THS II announcement on a timeline. Mark conservation, power splitting, regeneration and heat balance as transferable principles; mark hardware values and control calibration for model-year verification.","observation":"名字延續不代表每代的電池、電機與控制設定相同。","observationEn":"A continuing model name does not mean identical batteries, machines or controls across generations.","failure":"將一代技術資料與另一代型號混在同一張表而未標年分，會造成錯引。","failureEn":"Mixing one generation’s technical data with another model without dates creates misattribution.","check":"提交有來源年份、假設標記與待查欄位的系統圖。","checkEn":"Submit a system map with source years, assumption labels and open verification fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"c213-v6-12-k1","title":"技術傳承","titleEn":"Technical continuity","text":"物理原理可延續，工程實作仍會演進。","textEn":"Physical principles can persist while implementation evolves."},{"id":"c213-v6-12-k2","title":"版本溯源","titleEn":"Version provenance","text":"年份、市場與產品版本是技術資料的一部分。","textEn":"Year, market and product revision are part of technical provenance."}],"quiz":{"question":"閱讀不同世代Prius資料，哪種做法最好？","questionEn":"What is the best practice when reading different Prius generations?","options":["標明年份與版本再比較相同功能","所有資料合併為一套固定參數","以較新的照片證明舊規格"],"optionsEn":["Mark year and revision before comparing the same function","Merge all data into one fixed parameter set","Use a newer photo to prove an older specification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"版本明確，才不會將架構原理誤當固定實作。","explanationEn":"Explicit versions prevent confusing architectural principles with fixed implementation."}}]}],"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":216,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"c307","title":"Landsat 地球觀測計畫","titleEn":"Landsat Earth-observation program","category":"space","summary":"以Landsat 8作主要儀器例子，學習軌道、波段、DN換算、品質遮罩與時間序列，區分原始觀測、處理结果及環境推論。","summaryEn":"Use Landsat 8 as the main instrument example to study orbit, bands, DN conversion, quality masks and time series, separating observations, processing and environmental inference.","scope":"12道原創遙測入門任務；課程沒有預載實景或實測表格。小算例係數為教學假設；實際分析需自行取得資料及其版本相符的中繼資料，不把单一衛星規格套用所有世代。","scopeEn":"Twelve original introductory remote-sensing tasks, without preloaded scenes or measured tables. Small-example coefficients are hypothetical. Actual analysis requires acquired data and matching metadata; one satellite’s specifications do not apply to every generation.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-landsat8","v6-landsat-level1","v6-eros-legacy","v6-video-0rVQHFPZfJk","v10-other-vendor-c307"],"diagram":{"type":"satellite","labels":["觀測需求","軌道與波段","影像與中繼資料","校準與遮罩","變化證據"],"labelsEn":["Observation needs","Orbit and bands","Imagery and metadata","Calibration and masks","Change evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"c307-stage01","order":1,"title":"觀測設計與取樣尺度","titleEn":"Observation design and sampling scale","description":"從地表問題選擇時間、波段和空間尺度，再區分取樣與顯示。","descriptionEn":"Choose time, bands and spatial scale from the land question, then separate sampling from display.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c307-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":[],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8"],"title":"把地表問題轉成觀測需求","titleEn":"Translate a land question into observation requirements","objective":"為植被比較選定波段、時段與品質條件。","objectiveEn":"Choose bands, periods and quality conditions for a vegetation comparison.","instruction":"設定虛構問題：同一地區兩個時段的植被是否改變？列出紅光、近紅外、可比日期、地理範圍及雲遮狀態；先定義資料需求，不把網站示意圖當作已下載影像。","instructionEn":"Set a fictional question: did vegetation change between two periods in one area? List red and near-infrared bands, comparable dates, geographic extent and cloud status. Define data requirements without treating site diagrams as downloaded imagery.","observation":"漂亮彩圖不代表兩期具備相同觀測條件。","observationEn":"An attractive color image does not establish comparable conditions between dates.","failure":"不同季節或雲遮的差異可能被錯認為地表變化。","failureEn":"Seasonal or cloud differences can be mistaken for surface change.","check":"每項比較需求都有資料欄位與排除條件。","checkEn":"Give each comparison requirement a data field and an exclusion condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-01-k1","title":"觀測設計","titleEn":"Observation design","text":"研究問題決定時間、波段與空間範圍。","textEn":"The question determines time, bands and spatial extent."},{"id":"c307-v6-01-k2","title":"可比性","titleEn":"Comparability","text":"比較之前需確認資料代表相近的觀測情境。","textEn":"Comparison first requires checking that observations represent compatible conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"要比較植被變化，哪組條件較完整？","questionEn":"Which set is more complete for comparing vegetation change?","options":["使用同一衛星便不需核對季節與雲","像元間距相同便不需核對地點與日期","同地範圍、可比時段、紅光/NIR與雲狀態"],"optionsEn":["Use the same satellite without checking season or cloud","Match pixel spacing without checking location or date","Same area, comparable periods, red/NIR and cloud status"],"answer":2,"explanation":"資料的可比性比展示色彩更接近科學問題。","explanationEn":"Data comparability addresses the scientific question more directly than display colors."}},{"id":"c307-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-01"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8"],"title":"區分繞行週期與重訪週期","titleEn":"Distinguish orbital period from repeat cycle","objective":"避免把繞地球一圈當作回到同一觀測軌跡。","objectiveEn":"Avoid equating one orbit with a repeat of the same observation track.","instruction":"依USGS對Landsat 8的介紹，分別記錄約99分鐘繞行與16日重複週期。畫旋轉地球下的相鄰地面軌跡，說明為何兩種時間不能互換；不將數字套用全部Landsat世代。","instructionEn":"From USGS’s Landsat 8 overview, separately record the approximately 99-minute orbit and 16-day repeat cycle. Sketch adjacent tracks over a rotating Earth and explain why the intervals differ. Do not apply them to every Landsat generation.","observation":"衛星每圈經過不同地面經度，還需考慮地球自轉。","observationEn":"Successive orbits cross different ground longitudes because Earth rotates.","failure":"把99分鐘說成同一地點必定有新影像，混淆軌道與覆盖。","failureEn":"Claiming a new image of the same site every 99 minutes confuses orbit with coverage.","check":"筆記分開列出兩種週期、對應事件及Landsat 8限定。","checkEn":"Record both intervals, their events and the Landsat 8 limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-02-k1","title":"地面軌跡","titleEn":"Ground track","text":"軌道運動與地球自轉共同決定地面投影。","textEn":"Orbital motion and Earth’s rotation jointly determine the ground projection."},{"id":"c307-v6-02-k2","title":"重訪與可用","titleEn":"Revisit and usability","text":"軌跡重訪也不保證無雲或符合研究需求。","textEn":"A repeated track does not guarantee cloud-free or suitable data."}],"quiz":{"question":"Landsat 8的99分鐘與16日分别描述什麼？","questionEn":"What do Landsat 8’s 99 minutes and 16 days describe?","options":["同地重訪與繞行一圈，順序與前項相反","繞行一圈與地面軌跡重複","資料處理時間與感測器曝光週期"],"optionsEn":["Site revisit and one orbit, in the reverse order","One orbit and ground-track repetition","Data processing duration and sensor exposure period"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同週期對應不同幾何事件。","explanationEn":"The intervals describe different geometric events."}},{"id":"c307-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-02"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8"],"title":"閱讀多光譜波段的物理用途","titleEn":"Read the physical purposes of spectral bands","objective":"把感測波段與可觀察現象對應。","objectiveEn":"Relate spectral bands to observable phenomena.","instruction":"畫可見光、近紅外、短波紅外及熱紅外的概念區帶。將反射太陽光與熱放射分成兩類，再列植被、水分及熱狀態需要哪些額外判讀條件。","instructionEn":"Sketch conceptual visible, near-infrared, shortwave-infrared and thermal-infrared regions. Separate reflected sunlight from thermal emission, then list additional interpretation conditions for vegetation, moisture and thermal state.","observation":"不同波段不是相同照片換顏色，而是不同的光譜量測。","observationEn":"Bands are different spectral measurements, not the same photo recolored.","failure":"把熱紅外亮度直接當成可見光顏色，會用錯物理解釋。","failureEn":"Interpreting thermal-infrared brightness as visible color applies the wrong physics.","check":"至少把一個反射波段與一個熱波段對應到各自觀測機制。","checkEn":"Associate at least one reflected and one thermal band with their mechanisms.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-03-k1","title":"光譜選擇","titleEn":"Spectral selection","text":"感測器只量到其波段響應範圍內的資訊。","textEn":"A sensor measures information within its spectral response range."},{"id":"c307-v6-03-k2","title":"顯示與量測","titleEn":"Display versus measurement","text":"偽彩色把波段映射成螢幕色彩，不等於肉眼所見。","textEn":"False color maps bands to screen colors and need not match human vision."}],"quiz":{"question":"偽彩色中的紅色區域，必定是地表真實紅色嗎？","questionEn":"Must a red area in a false-color image be physically red?","options":["不一定，要查波段到色彩的映射","一定，每個顯示通道都等於相同的可見光顏色","只要像元更密，就可忽略波段映射"],"optionsEn":["No; inspect the band-to-color mapping","Yes; each display channel always equals the corresponding visible color","A denser pixel grid makes band mapping irrelevant"],"answer":0,"explanation":"顯示通道由使用者或產品設定。","explanationEn":"Display channels are set by the user or product."}},{"id":"c307-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-03"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8"],"title":"分開像元間距與可辨細節","titleEn":"Separate pixel spacing from resolved detail","objective":"理解取樣、混合像元與重取樣的差別。","objectiveEn":"Understand sampling, mixed pixels and resampling.","instruction":"在紙上畫30m網格與一條10m寬的假設河道，標出被河道和岸地共同占據的格子。再把網格細分成10m顯示格，指出哪些資訊仍無法由插值新增。","instructionEn":"Draw a 30 m grid and a hypothetical 10 m-wide river. Mark cells mixing water and banks, then subdivide the display grid to 10 m and identify information that interpolation cannot create.","observation":"更密的顯示格並不自動增加原始感測細節。","observationEn":"A denser display grid does not automatically add original sensor detail.","failure":"把輸出像元變小當作感測器解析度變高，會誇大辨識能力。","failureEn":"Treating smaller output pixels as better sensor resolution overstates resolving ability.","check":"指出一個混合像元，並註明重取樣只改資料表示。","checkEn":"Identify a mixed pixel and state that resampling changes representation.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-04-k1","title":"混合像元","titleEn":"Mixed pixel","text":"一個像元可能同時包含多種地表。","textEn":"One pixel may contain several surface types."},{"id":"c307-v6-04-k2","title":"取樣限制","titleEn":"Sampling limits","text":"後處理不能無條件恢復原始未量到的高頻資訊。","textEn":"Post-processing cannot unconditionally recover spatial information never measured."}],"quiz":{"question":"30m影像重取樣成10m格，能保證什麼？","questionEn":"Resampling a 30 m image to a 10 m grid guarantees what?","options":["新增真實10m感測細節","所有混合像元消失","輸出格網間距變小"],"optionsEn":["New genuine 10 m sensor detail","Removal of all mixed pixels","Smaller output-grid spacing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"格網間距與實際可辨識細節不同。","explanationEn":"Grid spacing differs from genuinely resolved detail."}}]},{"id":"c307-stage02","order":2,"title":"產品識別與物理換算","titleEn":"Product identity and physical conversion","description":"使用來源中的換算形式，搭配明示教學值與待填場景卡。","descriptionEn":"Use conversion forms from the references with explicit teaching values and pending scene cards.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c307-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-04"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"核對場景與中繼資料版本","titleEn":"Check scene and metadata identity","objective":"在轉換數值前確認資料產品與係數來源。","objectiveEn":"Confirm product and coefficient identity before conversion.","instruction":"建立一張空白場景卡，欄位含衛星、感測器、日期、產品層級、Collection、波段與中繼資料檔名。若自行從USGS取得資料，逐項抄錄；未取得時標為待填，不虛構場景編號。","instructionEn":"Create a blank scene card with satellite, sensor, date, product level, collection, band and metadata filename. If you obtain USGS data, transcribe them; otherwise mark fields pending rather than inventing a scene ID.","observation":"相同波段號碼在不同產品世代可能不代表相同用途。","observationEn":"The same band number can have different meaning across product generations.","failure":"拿另一場景或不同產品層級的係數換算，會失去可追溯性。","failureEn":"Using coefficients from another scene or product level breaks traceability.","check":"每項係數能連回同一產品的中繼資料，未知項明示。","checkEn":"Trace each coefficient to the same product’s metadata and mark unknowns.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-05-k1","title":"產品層級","titleEn":"Product level","text":"原始量化值與不同處理產品有不同解釋。","textEn":"Quantized values and differently processed products have different interpretations."},{"id":"c307-v6-05-k2","title":"參數溯源","titleEn":"Parameter provenance","text":"係數、版本與資料日期共同決定換算適用性。","textEn":"Coefficients, revision and date jointly determine conversion applicability."}],"quiz":{"question":"進行DN換算前，哪項最應先確認？","questionEn":"Before converting DN, what should be confirmed first?","options":["任意相鄰日期的係數都可直接沿用","係數屬於同一產品與波段","所有波段共用同一係數即可"],"optionsEn":["Coefficients from any nearby date can be reused directly","Coefficients belong to the same product and band","One coefficient set can be used for all bands"],"answer":1,"explanation":"正確公式搭配錯誤係數仍會得到錯誤結果。","explanationEn":"A correct formula with wrong coefficients still gives a wrong result."}},{"id":"c307-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-05"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"用教學係數換算輻亮度","titleEn":"Convert radiance using teaching coefficients","objective":"把DN與有物理單位的輻亮度分開。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish DN from radiance with physical units.","instruction":"使用USGS的線性形式L=M×DN+A，另設教學係數M=0.02、A=−1、DN=100，計算L。明寫係數虛構，實景必須使用該產品MTL檔的係數。","instructionEn":"Use the USGS linear form L=M×DN+A with invented teaching coefficients M=0.02, A=−1 and DN=100. Compute L and label the coefficients fictional; real scenes require their product’s MTL coefficients.","observation":"結果為1個相應輻亮度單位，不能把DN=100直接標作輻亮度。","observationEn":"The result is 1 in corresponding radiance units; DN=100 is not itself radiance.","failure":"漏掉加法項A，會得到不同且帶系統偏差的結果。","failureEn":"Omitting additive term A produces a systematic difference.","check":"保留乘法、加法與單位標記，且係數標為教學假設。","checkEn":"Retain multiplication, addition and units, with coefficients marked as assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-06-k1","title":"線性縮放","titleEn":"Linear scaling","text":"斜率與截距共同把量化值對應到物理量。","textEn":"Slope and intercept jointly map a quantized value to a physical quantity."},{"id":"c307-v6-06-k2","title":"資料解釋","titleEn":"Data interpretation","text":"儲存位元數不等於物理單位或精確度。","textEn":"Storage bit depth is not a physical unit or an accuracy guarantee."}],"quiz":{"question":"此例L=0.02×100−1等於多少？","questionEn":"What is L=0.02×100−1 in this example?","options":["1","2","100"],"optionsEn":["1","2","100"],"answer":0,"explanation":"乘法得2，再加−1得1。","explanationEn":"Multiplication gives 2; adding −1 gives 1."}},{"id":"c307-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-06"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"套用太陽角的反射率修正","titleEn":"Apply the solar-angle reflectance correction","objective":"區分未修正與太陽角修正的TOA反射率。","objectiveEn":"Separate uncorrected and solar-angle-corrected TOA reflectance.","instruction":"在紙上設未修正反射率ρ′=0.2、太陽高度30°，用ρ=ρ′/sin(θ)求值。另畫高度角與天頂角互補的圖；不把TOA反射率稱為地表反射率。","instructionEn":"Assume uncorrected reflectance ρ′=0.2 and solar elevation 30°, then apply ρ=ρ′/sin(θ). Sketch complementary elevation and zenith angles. Do not label TOA reflectance as surface reflectance.","observation":"本例sin30°=0.5，修正後為0.4。","observationEn":"Here sin30°=0.5, giving corrected reflectance 0.4.","failure":"混用高度角的cos與天頂角的sin，會套錯幾何。","failureEn":"Using cosine of elevation or sine of zenith applies the wrong geometry.","check":"同時標明角度定義、計算結果與TOA層級。","checkEn":"State the angle definition, result and TOA product level.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-07-k1","title":"角度定義","titleEn":"Angle definition","text":"太陽高度與天頂角互補，公式必須對應使用。","textEn":"Solar elevation and zenith are complementary, so formulas must match definitions."},{"id":"c307-v6-07-k2","title":"大氣層頂","titleEn":"Top of atmosphere","text":"太陽角修正不等於已消除所有大氣影響。","textEn":"Solar-angle correction does not remove every atmospheric effect."}],"quiz":{"question":"修正太陽高度後，能否直接稱為地表反射率？","questionEn":"After solar-elevation correction, can the result be called surface reflectance directly?","options":["能，太陽角修正已消除所有大氣影響","能，只要另外用了相同雲遮罩","不能，仍是TOA層級"],"optionsEn":["Yes; solar-angle correction removes every atmospheric effect","Yes, provided the same cloud mask is also used","No; it remains TOA reflectance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何修正與大氣校正不同。","explanationEn":"Geometric correction differs from atmospheric correction."}},{"id":"c307-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-07"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8","v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"分辨亮溫與地表溫度","titleEn":"Distinguish brightness temperature from surface temperature","objective":"理解熱波段換算結果的物理層級。","objectiveEn":"Understand the physical level of a thermal-band conversion.","instruction":"畫熱放射從地表到感測器的路徑，列出放射率與大氣影響。閱讀USGS亮溫公式所需K1、K2及輻亮度欄位，建立空白計算表；無實景係數時不產生真實溫度地圖。","instructionEn":"Sketch thermal radiation traveling from surface to sensor and list emissivity and atmospheric effects. Identify K1, K2 and radiance required by the USGS brightness-temperature formula, creating a blank worksheet rather than a real temperature map without scene coefficients.","observation":"感測器亮溫不直接等於每一地物的實際表面溫度。","observationEn":"Sensor brightness temperature is not automatically the physical temperature of every surface.","failure":"忽略放射率或把K當°C，會造成不同類型的錯誤。","failureEn":"Ignoring emissivity or treating kelvin as Celsius creates different errors.","check":"表格清楚標K、產品層級及需另處理的環境因素。","checkEn":"Label kelvin, product level and environmental factors requiring further treatment.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-08-k1","title":"亮溫","titleEn":"Brightness temperature","text":"亮溫以輻射模型表達觀測到的熱訊號。","textEn":"Brightness temperature expresses an observed thermal signal through a radiative model."},{"id":"c307-v6-08-k2","title":"放射率","titleEn":"Emissivity","text":"不同表面的放射特性會影響溫度反推。","textEn":"Surface emission properties affect temperature inference."}],"quiz":{"question":"熱波段換出的亮溫要用於地表研究，還需注意什麼？","questionEn":"What still matters when using thermal brightness temperature for surface studies?","options":["只需從K值扣273.15就成為地表溫度","放射率、大氣與產品處理層級","同一熱波段的所有地物可共用相同放射特性"],"optionsEn":["Only subtract 273.15 from kelvin to obtain surface temperature","Emissivity, atmosphere and product-processing level","Every surface in one thermal band has the same emission properties"],"answer":1,"explanation":"亮溫與地表溫度具有不同假設。","explanationEn":"Brightness and surface temperature involve different assumptions."}}]},{"id":"c307-stage03","order":3,"title":"品質、對準與變化判讀","titleEn":"Quality, registration and change interpretation","description":"將遮罩、幾何、指標及跨感測器限制帶入可重現的比較。","descriptionEn":"Include masks, geometry, indices and cross-sensor limitations in reproducible comparisons.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c307-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-08"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8","v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"先遮罩再解讀有效像元","titleEn":"Mask before interpreting valid pixels","objective":"把雲、缺值與飽和等品質狀態保留在分析中。","objectiveEn":"Retain quality states such as cloud, missing data and saturation.","instruction":"自製一個3×3示意格，明確指定兩格雲、一格缺值，其餘為假設反射率。只對有效格計算平均，並記錄被排除數；真實產品須查其QA定義。","instructionEn":"Create a synthetic 3×3 grid with two cloud cells, one missing cell and assumed reflectance elsewhere. Average only valid cells and record exclusions; real products require their QA definitions.","observation":"有效像元數為6，不是9。","observationEn":"The valid-pixel count is 6, not 9.","failure":"把缺值當零加入平均，會人為降低結果。","failureEn":"Averaging missing data as zero artificially lowers the result.","check":"交付有效遮罩、平均分母與排除理由。","checkEn":"Provide the validity mask, averaging denominator and exclusion reasons.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-09-k1","title":"品質旗標","titleEn":"Quality flags","text":"品質資訊屬於資料解釋的一部分，而非可忽略附件。","textEn":"Quality information is part of data interpretation, not optional decoration."},{"id":"c307-v6-09-k2","title":"缺值語意","titleEn":"Missing-value meaning","text":"沒有觀測不等於觀測值為零。","textEn":"No observation is not an observed zero."}],"quiz":{"question":"9格中2格雲、1格缺值，平均分母應是多少？","questionEn":"With 2 cloudy and 1 missing cell among 9, what is the averaging denominator?","options":["6","9","3"],"optionsEn":["6","9","3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"排除三個無效觀測後剩六格。","explanationEn":"Excluding three invalid observations leaves six."}},{"id":"c307-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-09"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8"],"title":"核對兩期影像的幾何對準","titleEn":"Check registration between two dates","objective":"避免把位置錯位誤判為地表改變。","objectiveEn":"Avoid interpreting misregistration as surface change.","instruction":"畫兩張相同地物邊界的方格圖，讓第二張故意位移一格。做逐格差異標記，再恢復對準比較；說明真實資料還需核對投影、格網與重取樣方法。","instructionEn":"Draw two grid maps of identical boundaries and shift the second by one cell. Mark cellwise differences, then realign and compare. Explain that real data also require projection, grid and resampling checks.","observation":"位移能在邊緣製造一圈假變化。","observationEn":"A shift can create a band of false change around boundaries.","failure":"只檢查日期相近，卻未核對座標系，會留下空間錯配。","failureEn":"Checking similar dates without coordinate systems leaves spatial mismatch.","check":"列出對準前後差異，並標示共同格網基準。","checkEn":"Report differences before and after alignment and label the shared grid.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-10-k1","title":"配準","titleEn":"Registration","text":"比較像元需要代表相同或可對應的地面位置。","textEn":"Compared pixels must represent the same or corresponding ground locations."},{"id":"c307-v6-10-k2","title":"邊緣敏感性","titleEn":"Edge sensitivity","text":"地物邊界對小位移通常比均勻區域更敏感。","textEn":"Boundaries are usually more sensitive to small shifts than uniform areas."}],"quiz":{"question":"差異只集中在所有地物邊緣，優先檢查什麼？","questionEn":"Differences cluster around every boundary. What should be checked first?","options":["直接認定所有地物都同時發生邊緣變化","先對兩期影像各自加強銳化","影像配準與格網"],"optionsEn":["Assume every feature experienced simultaneous boundary change","First sharpen each date independently","Image registration and grids"],"answer":2,"explanation":"規律邊缘差異可能來自幾何錯位。","explanationEn":"Systematic edge differences may arise from geometric misregistration."}},{"id":"c307-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-10"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8","v6-landsat-level1"],"title":"計算並限制植被指標的結論","titleEn":"Calculate a vegetation index and limit its interpretation","objective":"用簡單比值連接波段，同時保留限制。","objectiveEn":"Connect bands with a simple ratio while retaining limitations.","instruction":"使用教學反射率NIR=0.6、Red=0.2，計算NDVI=(NIR−Red)/(NIR+Red)。再用NIR=Red=0討論分母問題；先確認兩波段同層級、同位置且有效。","instructionEn":"Use teaching reflectances NIR=0.6 and Red=0.2 to calculate NDVI=(NIR−Red)/(NIR+Red). Then consider NIR=Red=0 and the denominator problem. First ensure both bands share processing level, location and validity.","observation":"例題NDVI為0.5，但無法僅凭這個數值指定植物種類。","observationEn":"The example NDVI is 0.5, but that value alone cannot identify a plant species.","failure":"不同單位或無效像元直接相除，会得到無法解釋的指標。","failureEn":"Combining inconsistent units or invalid pixels produces an uninterpretable index.","check":"保存算式、有效性條件與至少一項不能支持的結論。","checkEn":"Retain the calculation, validity conditions and at least one unsupported conclusion.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-11-k1","title":"正規化差值","titleEn":"Normalized difference","text":"分子表示波段差，分母提供尺度正規化。","textEn":"The numerator expresses a band difference and the denominator normalizes scale."},{"id":"c307-v6-11-k2","title":"指標非診斷","titleEn":"Index is not a diagnosis","text":"指標是線索，仍需環境、時間及地面證據。","textEn":"An index is evidence to interpret alongside environment, time and ground information."}],"quiz":{"question":"NIR=0.6、Red=0.2時NDVI為何？","questionEn":"What is NDVI for NIR=0.6 and Red=0.2?","options":["2","0.5","0.8"],"optionsEn":["2","0.5","0.8"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(0.6−0.2)/(0.6+0.2)=0.4/0.8=0.5。","explanationEn":"(0.6−0.2)/(0.6+0.2)=0.4/0.8=0.5."}},{"id":"c307-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c307-v6-11"],"sourceIds":["v6-landsat8","v6-landsat-level1","v6-eros-legacy"],"title":"整理長期序列的校準證據","titleEn":"Organize calibration evidence for a long-term series","objective":"把真實地表變化與感測器、處理變化分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate surface change from sensor and processing changes.","instruction":"建立跨三期的空白比較表，列衛星、波段定義、產品版本、雲遮、幾何對準及處理步驟。若不同感測器的波段響應不完全相同，將可比性列為需驗證，不自行宣布趨勢成立。","instructionEn":"Create a three-period comparison table with satellite, band definition, product revision, cloud, registration and processing steps. If sensor band responses differ, mark comparability for verification rather than declaring a trend.","observation":"產品值可換算到相同單位，仍可能受光譜響應差異影響。","observationEn":"Values in common units can still differ because spectral responses differ.","failure":"把處理版本改變造成的階躍當作環境突變，會誤導長期結論。","failureEn":"A processing-revision discontinuity can be misread as an environmental event.","check":"交付可重現的資料清單與限制，不虛構已取得的Landsat實景。","checkEn":"Deliver a reproducible data inventory and limitations without implying actual scenes were acquired.","knowledge":[{"id":"c307-v6-12-k1","title":"跨感測器比較","titleEn":"Cross-sensor comparison","text":"相同波段名稱不保證完全相同的光譜響應。","textEn":"Matching band names do not guarantee identical spectral responses."},{"id":"c307-v6-12-k2","title":"重現性","titleEn":"Reproducibility","text":"資料版本、係數與處理順序應一併保留。","textEn":"Retain data revisions, coefficients and processing order together."}],"quiz":{"question":"時間序列突變剛好遇到產品版本更新，應先做什麼？","questionEn":"A time-series jump coincides with a product update. What should be done first?","options":["檢查處理與校準差異再判讀環境","直接宣布地表突然變化","先將新版數值全部平移到舊資料平均值"],"optionsEn":["Check processing and calibration differences before environmental interpretation","Immediately declare abrupt surface change","Shift all new-product values to the old mean before investigation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"觀測與處理鏈的變化是需排除的替代解釋。","explanationEn":"Changes in observation and processing are alternative explanations to evaluate."}}]}],"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":216,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"c407","title":"Universal Robots UR5 協作手臂","titleEn":"Universal Robots UR5 collaborative arm","category":"manufacturing","summary":"以UR5系列的公開歷史為入口，透過紙上六軸工作站概念學習座標框、TCP、負載力矩、路徑與狀態確認，先掌握整合問題。","summaryEn":"Enter through the public history of the UR5 family and use paper workcell concepts to study frames, TCP, payload moments, paths and state confirmation before integration.","scope":"12道紙上與示意任務，不操作實體機器。UR5e公開手冊僅支援通用概念，不能直接當作原始UR5或其他版本SOP；實際應用仍需對應手冊、合格整合及現場風險驗證。","scopeEn":"Twelve paper and schematic tasks without physical robot operation. UR5e documentation supports general concepts and is not an SOP for the original UR5 or other revisions. Actual applications require matching manuals, qualified integration and on-site risk validation.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-ur-history","v6-ur5e-manual","v6-ur-odense"],"diagram":{"type":"robot","labels":["工作站需求","座標與TCP","負載與路徑","事件與停止","配置證據"],"labelsEn":["Workcell needs","Frames and TCP","Payload and path","Events and stopping","Configuration evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"c407-stage01","order":1,"title":"應用邊界、座標與工具","titleEn":"Application boundary, frames and tool","description":"先辨識整個工作站，再分清參考框架、工具中心及負載。","descriptionEn":"Identify the whole workcell, then distinguish reference frames, TCP and payload.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c407-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":[],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"界定協作工作站的風險邊界","titleEn":"Define the collaborative workcell risk boundary","objective":"把手臂、工具、工件與人員入口共同納入場域圖。","objectiveEn":"Include the arm, tool, workpiece and human access in the workcell map.","instruction":"在原創紙上工作站放置六軸手臂、夾具、假設工件與人員入口。以不同標記圈出掃掠、夾擠與掉落情境；閱讀公開手冊的應用風險觀念，不啟動實體機器。","instructionEn":"On an original paper workcell, place a six-axis arm, fixture, hypothetical part and human entrance. Mark swept-space, trapping and dropped-object scenarios. Study public application-risk concepts without powering physical machinery.","observation":"協作手臂的名稱不會消除末端工具與周邊設備造成的危害。","observationEn":"A collaborative-arm label does not remove hazards from tools and surrounding equipment.","failure":"只圈手臂本體、漏掉工件及夾具，會縮小了風險分析邊界。","failureEn":"Mapping only the arm omits workpiece and fixture hazards from the assessment boundary.","check":"至少標出三類危害及暴露情境，列明需由合格整合者評估。","checkEn":"Mark at least three hazard types and exposure scenarios, identifying the need for qualified integration assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-01-k1","title":"應用層級","titleEn":"Application level","text":"機器人安全與工具、工件、環境及使用方式共同相關。","textEn":"Application safety depends on tools, workpieces, environment and use as well as the robot."},{"id":"c407-v6-01-k2","title":"生命周期","titleEn":"Lifecycle","text":"示教、正常運轉與維修可能有不同的暴露情境。","textEn":"Teaching, normal operation and maintenance can create different exposures."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項判斷應退回重新評估？","questionEn":"Which conclusion should be rejected for reassessment?","options":["工具及工件危害需一併辨識","維修暴露情境需另外列入評估","因產品名稱含「協作」，所以不需應用風險評估"],"optionsEn":["Tool and workpiece hazards need to be identified together","Maintenance exposure scenarios need explicit assessment","Because the product is called collaborative, no application risk assessment is needed"],"answer":2,"explanation":"名稱不能取代應用風險評估與驗證。","explanationEn":"A label cannot replace application risk assessment and validation."}},{"id":"c407-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-01"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"建立基座與工件座標框","titleEn":"Establish base and workpiece frames","objective":"用明確原點與方向描述同一位置。","objectiveEn":"Describe one position with explicit origins and axes.","instruction":"畫基座XY與旋轉90°的工件XY座標。用同一支向右的世界方向箭頭，分別表示它在兩個框架的分量；標明正轉方向，先做平面概念再談六軸。","instructionEn":"Draw base XY axes and a workpiece frame rotated 90°. Express one rightward world arrow in both frames, stating positive rotation. Begin with planar concepts before considering six axes.","observation":"同一實體方向的座標分量會隨參考框架改變。","observationEn":"Coordinates of the same physical direction change with the reference frame.","failure":"切換框架卻沿用舊分量，會讓工具朝錯誤方向移動。","failureEn":"Changing frames while reusing old components moves the tool in the wrong direction.","check":"兩套箭頭都有原點、軸名與旋轉定義，能描述同一實體方向。","checkEn":"Both frames have origins, axis names and rotation definitions representing the same direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-02-k1","title":"座標與物理","titleEn":"Coordinates and physics","text":"座標是描述方式，切換座標不代表物件自己移動。","textEn":"Coordinates are a description; changing them does not itself move an object."},{"id":"c407-v6-02-k2","title":"參考框架","titleEn":"Reference frame","text":"指令的方向必須和其使用的框架一起解讀。","textEn":"A commanded direction must be interpreted with its frame."}],"quiz":{"question":"座標值改變就必然代表工具移動了嗎？","questionEn":"Do changed coordinate values necessarily mean the tool moved?","options":["一定，任何座標數字變化都是實體位移","不一定，可能只是換了參考框架","只有平移原點會改座標，旋轉軸向不會"],"optionsEn":["Yes; every coordinate change is physical displacement","No; the reference frame may have changed","Only moving the origin changes coordinates, not rotating the axes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一姿態可以有不同框架下的描述。","explanationEn":"One pose can have different descriptions in different frames."}},{"id":"c407-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-02"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"標定工具中心的概念偏移","titleEn":"Model a tool-center offset","objective":"把法蘭位置與实际工作點分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate flange position from the working point.","instruction":"畫末端法蘭與向前延伸2教學單位的工具尖端。保持法蘭位置不變，將工具方向在紙上轉90°，比較尖端位置；用此說明為何TCP定義包含相對位置。","instructionEn":"Sketch a flange and tool tip extending 2 teaching units. Hold flange position fixed and rotate the tool orientation by 90° on paper. Compare tip locations to explain why TCP definition includes an offset.","observation":"法蘭中心不移動，偏置工具尖端仍會移動。","observationEn":"An offset tool tip moves even if the flange center does not.","failure":"把法蘭原點當作所有工具的尖端，会造成系統性定位誤差。","failureEn":"Treating the flange origin as every tool’s tip creates systematic positioning error.","check":"兩種方向都畫出法蘭、偏移向量及TCP位置。","checkEn":"Show flange, offset vector and TCP in both orientations.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-03-k1","title":"TCP","titleEn":"Tool center point","text":"TCP是所選工具工作點的座標定義，不一定在法蘭中心。","textEn":"A TCP defines a selected working point and need not lie at the flange center."},{"id":"c407-v6-03-k2","title":"姿態影響","titleEn":"Orientation effect","text":"偏移向量需隨工具方向轉換到基座框架。","textEn":"The offset vector must be transformed with tool orientation into the base frame."}],"quiz":{"question":"換上更長工具而未更新TCP，最可能出現什麼？","questionEn":"A longer tool is fitted without updating TCP. What is a likely result?","options":["實際工作點偏離預期位置","工具長度不影響幾何","所有關節角自動歸零"],"optionsEn":["The physical working point misses the intended location","Tool length has no geometric effect","All joint angles automatically become zero"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TCP錯誤直接影響工作點的幾何描述。","explanationEn":"An incorrect TCP directly affects the working-point geometry."}},{"id":"c407-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-03"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"比較負載質量與重心位置","titleEn":"Compare payload mass and center of mass","objective":"理解相同質量在不同偏移下的力矩差異。","objectiveEn":"Understand different moments from equal mass at different offsets.","instruction":"用平面示意將同一教學負載放在距法蘭1與3單位的位置，保持重力方向不變。比較力矩倍率，再列出工具、工件與夾具是否都已計入；不選實機負載參數。","instructionEn":"Place the same teaching load at offsets 1 and 3 from a flange in a planar sketch, keeping gravity direction fixed. Compare moments and check inclusion of tool, part and gripper mass. Do not select physical robot payload settings.","observation":"垂直力臂增加3倍，靜態重力矩也增加3倍。","observationEn":"Tripling the perpendicular lever arm triples the static gravitational moment.","failure":"只輸入工件重量卻漏掉夾具，會錯估負載。","failureEn":"Entering only workpiece mass while omitting the gripper misrepresents the load.","check":"負載表包含各物件質量與相對重心，未有數值者標待查。","checkEn":"Include each item’s mass and relative center, marking unavailable values pending.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-04-k1","title":"質量與力矩","titleEn":"Mass and moment","text":"質量相同不代表關節承受相同力矩。","textEn":"Equal mass does not imply equal joint moment."},{"id":"c407-v6-04-k2","title":"組合負載","titleEn":"Combined payload","text":"工具與工件共同形成末端負載及重心。","textEn":"Tool and workpiece jointly define payload and its center."}],"quiz":{"question":"同一重量離支點的垂直距離從1變3，靜態力矩如何變？","questionEn":"For equal weight, perpendicular offset increases from 1 to 3. How does static moment change?","options":["保持不變","變成1/3","成為3倍"],"optionsEn":["It stays unchanged","It becomes one third","It triples"],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜態力矩等於力乘垂直力臂。","explanationEn":"Static moment equals force times perpendicular lever arm."}}]},{"id":"c407-stage02","order":2,"title":"運動幾何與可行路徑","titleEn":"Motion geometry and feasible paths","description":"用平面例子檢查插補、掃掠空間、奇異性與姿態可行性。","descriptionEn":"Use planar examples to examine interpolation, swept space, singularity and pose feasibility.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c407-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-04"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"分辨關節運動與工具直線","titleEn":"Distinguish joint motion from a straight tool path","objective":"理解端點軌跡與關節插補不是同一問題。","objectiveEn":"Understand that tool trajectory and joint interpolation differ.","instruction":"用兩節平面手臂畫起終姿態。先讓兩關節角均勻改變，標出中間工具位置；再畫工具沿直線的目標路徑，比較兩條曲線，不宣稱已解真機逆運動學。","instructionEn":"Use a two-link planar arm with start and end poses. Vary joint angles uniformly and mark intermediate tool positions, then draw a desired straight tool path and compare. Do not claim to solve the real robot’s inverse kinematics.","observation":"關節平順變化不保證工具端點走直線。","observationEn":"Smooth joint changes do not guarantee a straight endpoint path.","failure":"只核對起终點而忽略中間軌跡，可能漏掉障礙碰撞。","failureEn":"Checking only endpoints can miss intermediate collisions.","check":"兩種路徑至少各有一個中間姿態，並記錄差異。","checkEn":"Include at least one intermediate pose for each path and record the difference.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-05-k1","title":"正運動學","titleEn":"Forward kinematics","text":"關節配置映射到工具姿態，映射通常不是線性的。","textEn":"Joint configuration maps to tool pose, generally nonlinearly."},{"id":"c407-v6-05-k2","title":"路徑要求","titleEn":"Path requirement","text":"應用可能要求端點幾何路徑，而非只要求抵達終點。","textEn":"An application may require a particular tool path, not just an endpoint."}],"quiz":{"question":"關節角等速改變，工具必定走直線嗎？","questionEn":"Do uniformly changing joint angles guarantee a straight tool path?","options":["必然，關節插補與工具直線完全相同","不必然","只要兩關節角速度相同就保證直線"],"optionsEn":["Yes; joint interpolation and a tool straight line are identical","No","Equal joint angular speeds guarantee a straight tool path"],"answer":1,"explanation":"關節空間到工具空間的映射通常非線性。","explanationEn":"The joint-to-tool mapping is generally nonlinear."}},{"id":"c407-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-05"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"用過渡點檢查完整掃掠空間","titleEn":"Check swept space with intermediate poses","objective":"把工具與每節連桿都納入路徑檢查。","objectiveEn":"Include the tool and every link in path checks.","instruction":"在紙上加入一個障礙物，畫出起點、過渡點與終點的完整手臂。給工具加上假設工件輪廓，逐一比較掃掠空間；所有距離均為教學示意。","instructionEn":"Add an obstacle to the paper workcell and draw the complete arm at start, intermediate and end poses. Include a hypothetical carried part and compare swept spaces using teaching distances only.","observation":"工具尖端避開障礙，手肘或工件仍可能相交。","observationEn":"The tip may clear an obstacle while an elbow or carried part intersects it.","failure":"只檢查TCP軌跡，會忽略其他運動部位。","failureEn":"Checking only TCP trajectory omits other moving parts.","check":"每個姿態都標出最接近障礙的部位及尚未驗證的連續區間。","checkEn":"Identify the closest part at each pose and any continuous intervals not yet checked.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-06-k1","title":"掃掠體積","titleEn":"Swept volume","text":"運動物件沿路徑占據的空間超過一條端點線。","textEn":"The space occupied by a moving body exceeds an endpoint line."},{"id":"c407-v6-06-k2","title":"離散檢查限制","titleEn":"Discrete-check limitation","text":"少量姿態快照不能保證中間所有位置安全。","textEn":"A few pose snapshots cannot establish safety at every intermediate point."}],"quiz":{"question":"三張姿態圖都沒碰撞，能否保證整條路徑無碰撞？","questionEn":"If three pose snapshots are clear, is the entire path guaranteed collision-free?","options":["不能，中間區間仍需檢查","能，起點、中點及終點一定涵蓋全部軌跡","只需確認起終點高度相同"],"optionsEn":["No; intermediate intervals still need checking","Yes; start, middle and end always cover the whole path","Only equal start/end heights need confirmation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"離散取樣可能漏掉中間的相交。","explanationEn":"Discrete sampling can miss intersections between samples."}},{"id":"c407-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-06"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"辨識接近奇異姿態的訊號","titleEn":"Recognize signs of a near-singular configuration","objective":"理解微小工具運動可能需要較大關節變化。","objectiveEn":"Understand why small tool motion can require large joint changes.","instruction":"以兩節平面手臂比較彎曲與幾乎伸直兩種姿態，畫出小幅工具位移，特別標示沿手臂伸展方向的分量。比較所需關節改變的敏感性；不計算或修改實機速度限制。","instructionEn":"Compare bent and nearly straight configurations of a two-link planar arm. Sketch a small tool displacement, explicitly marking its component along the extension direction. Compare sensitivity of required joint changes without calculating or changing real speed limits.","observation":"接近特定幾何排列時，位置與關節變化的關係可能變得敏感。","observationEn":"Near particular geometric alignments, the relation between position and joint changes can become sensitive.","failure":"把工具速度看似很小當作關節速度一定很小，會漏看幾何放大。","failureEn":"Assuming low tool speed guarantees low joint speeds overlooks geometric amplification.","check":"說明哪種姿態較需檢查敏感性，並記錄這只是平面示意。","checkEn":"Identify which configuration needs sensitivity review and label the planar simplification.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-07-k1","title":"奇異性","titleEn":"Singularity","text":"某些配置會使可用瞬時運動方向或逆解行為退化。","textEn":"Certain configurations degrade available instantaneous motion directions or inverse behavior."},{"id":"c407-v6-07-k2","title":"速度映射","titleEn":"Velocity mapping","text":"工具速度與關節速度經由姿態相關的映射連結。","textEn":"Tool and joint velocities are linked by a configuration-dependent mapping."}],"quiz":{"question":"接近奇異姿態時，哪個判斷最可靠？","questionEn":"Near a singular configuration, which judgment is most reliable?","options":["工具慢就保證所有關節慢","只要終點可達就忽略路徑","需檢查關節與工具運動的敏感性"],"optionsEn":["A slow tool guarantees every joint is slow","Ignore the path if the endpoint is reachable","Check sensitivity between joint and tool motion"],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何映射可能放大關節運動需求。","explanationEn":"The geometric mapping can amplify joint-motion demand."}},{"id":"c407-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-07"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"比較可達範圍與工作姿態","titleEn":"Compare reachability with working pose","objective":"把位置、方向與周邊限制分開核對。","objectiveEn":"Check position, orientation and surrounding constraints separately.","instruction":"畫一個可到達的目標點，再要求工具以指定方向接近。以兩個假設姿態比較是否同時滿足方向、工件空間與關節範圍；不推定任何UR5版本的實際可達界限。","instructionEn":"Draw a reachable target point and then require a specified approach orientation. Compare two hypothetical poses for orientation, part clearance and joint range, without inferring actual reach limits for any UR5 version.","observation":"同一位置可能只有部分工具方向可用。","observationEn":"Only some tool orientations may be usable at the same position.","failure":"把手臂最大伸展半徑當作完整可工作空間，忽略了姿態與障礙。","failureEn":"Treating maximum reach radius as the full usable workspace omits orientation and obstacles.","check":"對兩個姿態分別填入位置、方向、空間與關節條件。","checkEn":"Record position, orientation, clearance and joint conditions for both poses.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-08-k1","title":"姿態","titleEn":"Pose","text":"姿態包含位置及方向，不能只給三個位置座標。","textEn":"Pose includes position and orientation, not only three position coordinates."},{"id":"c407-v6-08-k2","title":"任務空間","titleEn":"Task workspace","text":"可工作的區域由應用條件共同限制。","textEn":"Usable workspace is constrained by the application’s combined conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何只看伸展半徑不足以證明目標可作業？","questionEn":"Why is reach radius alone insufficient to establish task feasibility?","options":["半徑內所有工具方向均已被保證","還需找到符合方向、關節及空間條件的姿態","TCP到基座的距離會決定唯一關節配置"],"optionsEn":["Every tool orientation inside the radius is already guaranteed","A pose satisfying orientation, joint and clearance conditions is still needed","TCP distance from the base determines a unique joint configuration"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可達位置不等於可執行指定任務。","explanationEn":"Reaching a position does not mean performing the required task is feasible."}}]},{"id":"c407-stage03","order":3,"title":"確認、恢復與版本交付","titleEn":"Confirmation, recovery and version handover","description":"將感測握手、節拍、停止後狀態及配置紀錄組成可審查流程。","descriptionEn":"Build an auditable workflow from sensor handshakes, cycle time, post-stop state and configuration records.","route":"原創概念學習路線；工序編號是教學順序，不是原廠連續製造或操作程序。","routeEn":"An original conceptual learning route; numbering indicates teaching order, not a continuous manufacturer production or operating procedure.","steps":[{"id":"c407-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-08"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"建立夾取與感測的握手流程","titleEn":"Build a grasp-and-sensor handshake","objective":"讓指令與已確認的物件狀態分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate commands from confirmed object state.","instruction":"用紙上狀態圖表示待命、夾取指令、等待確認、搬移與異常。設一個感測確認未到的情境，停留在等待或異常分支；不寫入真實控制器。","instructionEn":"Create a paper state diagram for idle, grasp command, waiting for confirmation, transfer and fault. Withhold a sensor acknowledgment and remain in a waiting or fault branch. Do not program a physical controller.","observation":"已送出夾取指令不代表物件已被可靠握住。","observationEn":"Issuing a grasp command does not establish that the part is securely held.","failure":"固定等一小段時間就搬移，可能把未知狀態誤判成功。","failureEn":"Moving after a fixed short delay may mistake uncertainty for success.","check":"圖上每條搬移轉移都有確認條件，並有未確認分支。","checkEn":"Give each transfer transition a confirmation condition and an unconfirmed branch.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-09-k1","title":"狀態機","titleEn":"State machine","text":"流程依狀態與事件轉移，不只依時間順序。","textEn":"A process transitions through states and events, not just elapsed time."},{"id":"c407-v6-09-k2","title":"確認證據","titleEn":"Confirmation evidence","text":"感測回覆也有適用範圍與可能故障，需納入驗證。","textEn":"Sensor acknowledgment also has scope and failure modes requiring validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"夾取指令已送出但未收到確認，紙上流程應如何？","questionEn":"A grasp command is sent but unconfirmed. What should the paper workflow do?","options":["走等待或異常分支，不宣稱夾取完成","直接搬移並假設已夾住","固定等待後一律判為成功"],"optionsEn":["Follow a waiting or fault branch without declaring success","Move immediately and assume a successful grasp","Always declare success after a fixed delay"],"answer":0,"explanation":"指令不是完成證據。","explanationEn":"A command is not completion evidence."}},{"id":"c407-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-09"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"比較節拍與驗證覆蓋","titleEn":"Compare cycle time with verification coverage","objective":"在簡化流程中辨識等待與搬移成本。","objectiveEn":"Identify waiting and motion costs in a simplified cycle.","instruction":"自訂教學週期：接近2秒、確認1秒、搬移3秒、放置2秒。計算總時間，再提出一個只改布局的縮時假設；保留確認步驟並標示尚需驗證。","instructionEn":"Use a teaching cycle of 2 s approach, 1 s confirmation, 3 s transfer and 2 s placement. Sum the time and propose a layout-only improvement, retaining confirmation and marking the proposal for validation.","observation":"總時間8秒；刪除確認雖縮時，卻改變功能保證。","observationEn":"Total time is 8 s; deleting confirmation reduces time but changes functional assurance.","failure":"為了節拍省略安全或品質關卡，不能算等條件改善。","failureEn":"Removing safety or quality gates is not a like-for-like improvement.","check":"比較前後需求相同，所有時間與新增假設明列。","checkEn":"Keep requirements equal and list timings and added assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-10-k1","title":"節拍分解","titleEn":"Cycle-time decomposition","text":"總時間由動作、等待與確認共同組成。","textEn":"Total time includes motion, waiting and confirmation."},{"id":"c407-v6-10-k2","title":"等條件比較","titleEn":"Like-for-like comparison","text":"改善必須保留原有需求，否則比較對象已改變。","textEn":"An improvement must retain requirements or the comparison target has changed."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪種縮時方案較適合先作紙上評估？","questionEn":"Which time-reduction idea is more suitable for initial paper evaluation?","options":["刪除夾取確認以縮短等待","未收到確認時直接略過該狀態","縮短布局搬移距離但保留驗證關卡"],"optionsEn":["Delete grasp confirmation to reduce waiting","Skip the state whenever confirmation is missing","Shorten transfer distance while retaining verification gates"],"answer":2,"explanation":"布局改善可在保留功能需求下提出，但仍需驗證。","explanationEn":"Layout changes can preserve functional requirements, but still require validation."}},{"id":"c407-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-10"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur5e-manual"],"title":"分析停止後的狀態與恢復","titleEn":"Analyze state after stopping and recovery","objective":"把停止命令與已停止、可重新啟動分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate a stop command, stopped state and restart readiness.","instruction":"在紙上選一個搬移中的時刻，標出工具、工件與外部設備的狀態。列出停止後仍需確認的位置、握持與人員情境，再畫「重新確認後」的恢復分支；不測試實機停距。","instructionEn":"Choose a point during the paper transfer cycle and mark tool, part and external-equipment states. List position, grasp and human-context checks after a stop, then draw a revalidated recovery branch. Do not test physical stopping distance.","observation":"停止運動不必然代表工件已穩定或周邊設備已處於相同狀態。","observationEn":"Stopped motion does not necessarily mean the part is secure or surrounding equipment is in a matching state.","failure":"直接回到原流程下一行，可能沿用已失效的狀態假設。","failureEn":"Resuming at the next program line may reuse invalid state assumptions.","check":"恢復分支包含重新確認條件與不確定時的處置。","checkEn":"Include revalidation conditions and an uncertainty response in recovery.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-11-k1","title":"停止過程","titleEn":"Stopping process","text":"發出停止指令與實際停止之間仍有動態過程。","textEn":"A dynamic process exists between a stop command and actual standstill."},{"id":"c407-v6-11-k2","title":"狀態恢復","titleEn":"State recovery","text":"恢復需要確認系統狀態，而非只記住程式位置。","textEn":"Recovery requires confirming system state, not just program position."}],"quiz":{"question":"停止後重新啟動前，哪個做法較完整？","questionEn":"Before restarting after a stop, which approach is more complete?","options":["假設所有外部設備同步停止","重新確認工件、設備與人員狀態","只讀取程式行號"],"optionsEn":["Assume every external device stopped synchronously","Reconfirm part, equipment and human states","Read only the program line number"],"answer":1,"explanation":"程式位置不足以代表實體系統狀態。","explanationEn":"Program position does not fully represent physical system state."}},{"id":"c407-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c407-v6-11"],"sourceIds":["v6-ur-history","v6-ur5e-manual","v6-ur-odense"],"title":"整理工具與程式的版本證據","titleEn":"Organize tool and program version evidence","objective":"避免把一個機型或工具的設定直接移植。","objectiveEn":"Avoid directly transplanting settings between models or tools.","instruction":"建立交付表，列手臂型號、手冊版本、工具TCP、負載假設、工件框架、程式版本與紙上驗證結果。注明UR5歷史課程引用UR5e手冊僅為概念參考，實際機型需另核對。","instructionEn":"Create a handover table with arm model, manual revision, TCP, payload assumptions, workpiece frame, program revision and paper-validation results. State that the historical UR5 course uses UR5e documentation conceptually; actual model compatibility needs separate checking.","observation":"程式檔一致而工具或安裝設定不同，仍可能產生不同運動。","observationEn":"Equal program files can produce different behavior with changed tool or installation settings.","failure":"只備份程式、不記錄安裝與工具配置，會留下復現缺口。","failureEn":"Backing up only the program without installation and tool configuration leaves a reproducibility gap.","check":"交付表能指出每一設定的來源與適用版本，不宣稱課程等於現場驗收。","checkEn":"Trace each setting to a source and applicable revision without equating the course to on-site acceptance.","knowledge":[{"id":"c407-v6-12-k1","title":"配置組合","titleEn":"Configuration set","text":"程式、工具、座標與負載設定共同定義應用。","textEn":"Program, tool, frames and payload settings jointly define the application."},{"id":"c407-v6-12-k2","title":"版本適用性","titleEn":"Version applicability","text":"相近產品名稱不保證介面、限制或程序相同。","textEn":"Similar product names do not guarantee identical interfaces, limits or procedures."}],"quiz":{"question":"只帶走程式檔，為何可能無法重現工作站？","questionEn":"Why may a program file alone fail to reproduce a workcell?","options":["工具與安裝設定也是應用的一部分","程式檔必定已包含所有機械工具尺寸","相同檔名就能保證相同安裝設定"],"optionsEn":["Tool and installation settings are also part of the application","A program file necessarily contains every physical tool dimension","An equal filename guarantees identical installation settings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"應用行為由整個配置組合決定。","explanationEn":"Application behavior depends on the complete configuration set."}}]}],"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":216,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":6},{"id":"d002","title":"伊泰普水電站","titleEn":"Itaipu Hydroelectric Power Plant","category":"energy","kind":"course","summary":"以十二個概念任務串起水量、水力能、旋轉機械與雙頻電網介面。","summaryEn":"Twelve conceptual tasks connect water balance, hydraulic energy, rotating machinery and two-frequency grid interfaces.","scope":"以伊泰普為案例的公開原理課程；所有自設數字均標為教學假設。三階段十二步不是實際施工順序、完整設備製造 SOP 或水門／送電操作指示。","scopeEn":"A public-principles course using Itaipu as its case. All invented numbers are labeled teaching assumptions. Three stages and twelve steps are not a construction sequence, complete manufacturing SOP, or gate/energization instructions.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-history","v6-science-itaipu-energy","v6-science-hydropower"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"energy","labels":["水庫","壓力管","水輪機","發電機","電網介面"],"labelsEn":["Reservoir","Penstock","Turbine","Generator","Grid interface"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d002-stage01","order":1,"title":"水力邊界與介面","titleEn":"Hydraulic boundaries and interfaces","description":"先把水、能量與責任邊界分開。","descriptionEn":"First separate water, energy and responsibility boundaries.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d002-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-history","v6-science-itaipu-energy"],"title":"劃定雙國電站系統邊界","titleEn":"Define the binational plant boundary","objective":"分清電站、輸電與兩國電網的責任。","objectiveEn":"Separate plant, transmission and national-grid responsibilities.","instruction":"畫出水庫、機組、變壓器與兩國電網四類節點；用不同箭頭標示水流及電力。","instructionEn":"Draw reservoir, generating-unit, transformer and national-grid nodes; distinguish water and electricity arrows.","observation":"同一水力來源可以對接不同電力系統。","observationEn":"One hydraulic resource can interface with different power systems.","failure":"把國界當作物理能量終點，會遺漏輸電介面。","failureEn":"Treating the border as an energy endpoint omits transmission interfaces.","check":"逐一標出每條跨邊界箭頭的輸入、輸出與負責者。","checkEn":"Identify the input, output and owner of every boundary-crossing arrow.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"系統邊界決定哪些功率、損失與責任需要計入。","textEn":"System boundaries determine which powers, losses and responsibilities must be counted."},{"id":"d002-v6-01-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"雙國所有權與電氣連接方式是兩個不同層次的問題。","textEn":"Binational ownership and electrical connection are different layers of the system."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個圖最適合進行介面審查？","questionEn":"Which diagram best supports interface review?","options":["同時標示物理流向與各介面責任","只畫國旗與總裝置容量","把所有輸出合併成沒有單位的箭頭"],"optionsEn":["It shows physical flows and interface responsibilities","It shows only flags and installed capacity","It combines outputs into an arrow without units"],"answer":0,"explanation":"系統邊界決定哪些功率、損失與責任需要計入。 雙國所有權與電氣連接方式是兩個不同層次的問題。","explanationEn":"System boundaries determine which powers, losses and responsibilities must be counted. Binational ownership and electrical connection are different layers of the system."}},{"id":"d002-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-01"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"分辨毛水頭與有效水頭","titleEn":"Separate gross and effective head","objective":"說明水位差與可用水力能的關係。","objectiveEn":"Explain the relationship between elevation difference and usable hydraulic energy.","instruction":"在自畫剖面標出上游、下游水位與管路損失；用假設的 10 單位水頭減去 2 單位損失。","instructionEn":"Mark upstream and downstream levels and conduit losses; subtract an assumed loss of 2 from a gross head of 10 units.","observation":"有效水頭為 8 個示例單位，不能再把損失扣第二次。","observationEn":"Effective head is 8 example units; losses must not be subtracted twice.","failure":"直接把壩體高度當有效水頭，會混淆結構尺度與水力條件。","failureEn":"Using dam height as effective head confuses structural dimensions with hydraulic conditions.","check":"指出兩個水位基準，並保留損失的計算位置。","checkEn":"Identify both level references and show where losses enter the calculation.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"可用水頭取決於上下游能量差及沿途損失。","textEn":"Usable head depends on the upstream–downstream energy difference and intervening losses."},{"id":"d002-v6-02-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"示例單位只用來練習能量帳，不是伊泰普的實際水頭。","textEn":"The example units teach energy accounting; they are not Itaipu’s actual head."}],"quiz":{"question":"例子中應採用多少有效水頭？","questionEn":"What effective head should the example use?","options":["12 個示例單位","8 個示例單位","只由壩體高度決定"],"optionsEn":["12 example units","8 example units","A value determined solely by dam height"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可用水頭取決於上下游能量差及沿途損失。 示例單位只用來練習能量帳，不是伊泰普的實際水頭。","explanationEn":"Usable head depends on the upstream–downstream energy difference and intervening losses. The example units teach energy accounting; they are not Itaipu’s actual head."}},{"id":"d002-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-02"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"閉合水量收支","titleEn":"Close the water balance","objective":"檢查入流、出流與庫存變化是否相容。","objectiveEn":"Check whether inflow, outflow and storage change are consistent.","instruction":"建立假設一小時帳：入流 12、發電用水 8、其他出流 3，全部採同一體積單位。","instructionEn":"Create an assumed one-hour account: inflow 12, turbine discharge 8 and other outflow 3, all in one volume unit.","observation":"庫存增加 1 單位；用水並未因發電而消失。","observationEn":"Storage increases by 1 unit; generation does not destroy the water.","failure":"忽略其他出流會高估庫存增加，進而誤判可用水量。","failureEn":"Omitting other outflow overstates storage growth and available water.","check":"驗證入流減總出流等於庫存變化，並註明時間窗。","checkEn":"Verify that inflow minus total outflow equals storage change and state the time window.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"守恆帳必須同時包含流量路徑與儲存項。","textEn":"A conservation account includes both flow paths and storage."},{"id":"d002-v6-03-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"瞬時流量與一段時間的總體積不能直接相減。","textEn":"An instantaneous flow rate cannot be subtracted directly from a time-integrated volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"這一小時庫存如何改變？","questionEn":"How does storage change during this hour?","options":["增加 4 單位","減少 11 單位","增加 1 單位"],"optionsEn":["It increases by 4 units","It decreases by 11 units","It increases by 1 unit"],"answer":2,"explanation":"守恆帳必須同時包含流量路徑與儲存項。 瞬時流量與一段時間的總體積不能直接相減。","explanationEn":"A conservation account includes both flow paths and storage. An instantaneous flow rate cannot be subtracted directly from a time-integrated volume."}},{"id":"d002-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-03"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"追蹤壓力管與機組介面","titleEn":"Trace penstock-to-unit interfaces","objective":"識別水力、結構與維修介面。","objectiveEn":"Identify hydraulic, structural and maintenance interfaces.","instruction":"在概念圖依序連接進水口、壓力管、水輪機與尾水；另畫承重與檢修邊界。","instructionEn":"Connect intake, penstock, turbine and tailwater on a concept diagram; add support and maintenance boundaries.","observation":"水路連續不代表支承與隔離責任已經完整。","observationEn":"A continuous water path does not by itself define support or isolation responsibilities.","failure":"只檢查管徑接得上，會漏掉位移、載荷與可維護性。","failureEn":"Checking only matching pipe sizes misses displacement, load and maintainability.","check":"為每個介面列一項幾何資料與一項需由專業團隊確認的載荷資料。","checkEn":"List one geometry item and one professionally reviewed load item for each interface.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"設備介面同時傳遞物質、力與資訊。","textEn":"Equipment interfaces carry matter, forces and information."},{"id":"d002-v6-04-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"此圖用來辨識資料缺口，不授權開關水門或拆卸受壓部件。","textEn":"The diagram identifies missing information; it does not authorize gate operation or disassembly of pressurized components."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項資訊不能因水路連通而省略？","questionEn":"Which information cannot be omitted merely because the water path connects?","options":["支承載荷與維修隔離邊界","概念圖的裝飾色彩","各節點相同的字體"],"optionsEn":["Support loads and maintenance isolation boundaries","Decorative diagram colours","Matching fonts at every node"],"answer":0,"explanation":"設備介面同時傳遞物質、力與資訊。 此圖用來辨識資料缺口，不授權開關水門或拆卸受壓部件。","explanationEn":"Equipment interfaces carry matter, forces and information. The diagram identifies missing information; it does not authorize gate operation or disassembly of pressurized components."}}]},{"id":"d002-stage02","order":2,"title":"機電能量轉換","titleEn":"Electromechanical conversion","description":"把水輪機、軸、發電機及頻率需求連起來。","descriptionEn":"Connect turbine, shaft, generator and frequency requirements.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d002-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-04"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"連接水輪機與發電機能量帳","titleEn":"Connect turbine and generator energy accounts","objective":"把水力功率分解為軸功率與電功率。","objectiveEn":"Separate hydraulic power into shaft and electrical power.","instruction":"用假設水力輸入 100、軸輸出 90、電輸出 85 個功率單位畫出三段能量帳。","instructionEn":"Draw three energy stages with assumed hydraulic input 100, shaft output 90 and electrical output 85 power units.","observation":"水輪機損失 10、發電機損失 5；總效率為 85%。","observationEn":"Turbine loss is 10 and generator loss is 5; overall efficiency is 85%.","failure":"相加各段效率會得到沒有物理意義的總效率。","failureEn":"Adding stage efficiencies produces a physically meaningless overall efficiency.","check":"核對輸入等於有效輸出加所有損失，並說明效率應相乘。","checkEn":"Check input against useful output plus losses and explain why stage efficiencies multiply.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"串聯能量轉換的總效率是各段效率的乘積。","textEn":"Overall efficiency of serial energy conversion is the product of stage efficiencies."},{"id":"d002-v6-05-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"例子的數值是學習用假設，不是廠商保證值。","textEn":"The numbers are teaching assumptions, not vendor guarantees."}],"quiz":{"question":"例子的水力到電力總效率是多少？","questionEn":"What is the example’s hydraulic-to-electrical efficiency?","options":["175%","85%","只看軸輸出，為 90%"],"optionsEn":["175%","85%","90%, considering shaft output only"],"answer":1,"explanation":"串聯能量轉換的總效率是各段效率的乘積。 例子的數值是學習用假設，不是廠商保證值。","explanationEn":"Overall efficiency of serial energy conversion is the product of stage efficiencies. The numbers are teaching assumptions, not vendor guarantees."}},{"id":"d002-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-05"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-energy"],"title":"分組 50 Hz 與 60 Hz 電氣介面","titleEn":"Group 50 Hz and 60 Hz electrical interfaces","objective":"理解伊泰普機組分組為何需要電網介面規劃。","objectiveEn":"Understand why Itaipu’s unit groups need deliberate grid interfaces.","instruction":"依官方資料把二十部機組卡分成十部 50 Hz 與十部 60 Hz；把各組接到相應頻率標籤。","instructionEn":"Use the official account to sort twenty unit cards into ten 50 Hz and ten 60 Hz units, then match frequency labels.","observation":"同樣的容量單位不表示兩種頻率可直接並聯。","observationEn":"Identical power units do not imply that different frequencies can be directly paralleled.","failure":"把容量相等誤當同步條件，會漏掉頻率與相位相容性。","failureEn":"Treating equal capacity as synchronization overlooks frequency and phase compatibility.","check":"在任何跨頻率連線旁標記需要明確轉換介面，而非直接電線。","checkEn":"Mark every cross-frequency link as requiring a defined conversion interface, not a direct wire.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"交流並聯系統需要相容的頻率、相位與電壓條件。","textEn":"Parallel AC systems require compatible frequency, phase and voltage conditions."},{"id":"d002-v6-06-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本步只辨識介面；不提供實際送電或同步操作指令。","textEn":"This task identifies interfaces only; it gives no energization or synchronization instructions."}],"quiz":{"question":"50 Hz 與 60 Hz 標籤的主要工程意義為何？","questionEn":"What is the main engineering implication of the 50 Hz and 60 Hz labels?","options":["只要功率相同即可直接相連","表示兩種水的流動速度","必須審查跨系統的頻率相容與轉換"],"optionsEn":["Equal power alone permits direct connection","They identify two water velocities","Cross-system frequency compatibility and conversion need review"],"answer":2,"explanation":"交流並聯系統需要相容的頻率、相位與電壓條件。 本步只辨識介面；不提供實際送電或同步操作指令。","explanationEn":"Parallel AC systems require compatible frequency, phase and voltage conditions. This task identifies interfaces only; it gives no energization or synchronization instructions."}},{"id":"d002-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-06"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"辨識扭矩與轉速的角色","titleEn":"Identify the roles of torque and speed","objective":"區分旋轉機械的運動與傳能量。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish rotational motion from mechanical energy transfer.","instruction":"比較兩個假設軸工況：相同轉速、不同扭矩；用 P=Tω 標示功率比例。","instructionEn":"Compare two assumed shaft cases at equal speed but different torque; use P=Tω to mark the power ratio.","observation":"轉速相同時，扭矩加倍會使軸功率加倍。","observationEn":"At equal speed, doubling torque doubles shaft power.","failure":"把轉速直接當作功率讀值，會忽略負載變化。","failureEn":"Using speed alone as a power reading ignores changes in load.","check":"列出扭矩、角速度與功率的不同單位。","checkEn":"List distinct units for torque, angular speed and power.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"軸功率同時取決於扭矩與角速度。","textEn":"Shaft power depends on both torque and angular speed."},{"id":"d002-v6-07-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"此比例比較不需要也不代表真實機組的額定軸參數。","textEn":"The ratio comparison neither needs nor represents real rated shaft parameters."}],"quiz":{"question":"相同轉速下，哪項變化會增加軸功率？","questionEn":"At the same speed, which change increases shaft power?","options":["增加傳遞扭矩","只更換轉速表標籤","把角速度的單位省略"],"optionsEn":["Increasing transmitted torque","Relabelling the speed gauge","Omitting angular-speed units"],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸功率同時取決於扭矩與角速度。 此比例比較不需要也不代表真實機組的額定軸參數。","explanationEn":"Shaft power depends on both torque and angular speed. The ratio comparison neither needs nor represents real rated shaft parameters."}},{"id":"d002-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-07"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-energy","v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"畫出調節與回授概念","titleEn":"Draw regulation and feedback concepts","objective":"分開量測、設定與致動的訊號路徑。","objectiveEn":"Separate measurement, setpoint and actuation signal paths.","instruction":"建立紙上控制方塊圖：假設目標功率、量測功率、誤差比較與水量調節；加入延遲方塊。","instructionEn":"Build a paper block diagram with assumed target power, measured power, error comparison, water regulation and a delay block.","observation":"量測與致動延遲能讓同一設定產生不同暫態。","observationEn":"Measurement and actuation delays can produce different transients for the same target.","failure":"看到誤差就假定設備立即到位，會錯過振盪與過度調節。","failureEn":"Assuming instantaneous response to error misses oscillation and overcorrection.","check":"以箭頭區分能量流與回授訊號，並圈出尚未建模的延遲。","checkEn":"Distinguish energy and feedback arrows and circle unmodelled delays.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"回授根據量測與目標的差異修正動作，實際系統具有動態。","textEn":"Feedback adjusts action from measured error, while real systems have dynamics."},{"id":"d002-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不給控制器增益；有效增益需要設備模型及正式驗證。","textEn":"No controller gains are supplied; valid gains require equipment models and formal verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個方塊不能由「理想即時反應」取代？","questionEn":"Which block should not be replaced by an assumption of instant response?","options":["圖紙名稱","量測與致動延遲","步驟頁碼"],"optionsEn":["The diagram title","Measurement and actuation delays","The lesson page number"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回授根據量測與目標的差異修正動作，實際系統具有動態。 本課不給控制器增益；有效增益需要設備模型及正式驗證。","explanationEn":"Feedback adjusts action from measured error, while real systems have dynamics. No controller gains are supplied; valid gains require equipment models and formal verification."}}]},{"id":"d002-stage03","order":3,"title":"證據與交接","titleEn":"Evidence and handover","description":"用量綱、可用率與可追溯資料完成概念審查。","descriptionEn":"Complete a conceptual review using dimensions, availability and traceability.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d002-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-08"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-energy","v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"區別容量、功率與電量","titleEn":"Distinguish capacity, power and energy","objective":"避免把 MW 與 MWh 混為一談。","objectiveEn":"Avoid confusing MW with MWh.","instruction":"對假設平均輸出 2 MW、持續 3 小時的機組計算電量，並另列裝置容量欄。","instructionEn":"Calculate energy for an assumed average output of 2 MW over 3 hours and keep installed capacity in a separate field.","observation":"電量為 6 MWh；裝置容量不等於每小時必達的輸出。","observationEn":"Energy is 6 MWh; installed capacity is not an hourly output guarantee.","failure":"直接把官方容量當年電量，會造成量綱錯誤。","failureEn":"Treating official capacity as annual energy causes a dimensional error.","check":"確認每個值均有單位與時間範圍，並標示假設平均值。","checkEn":"Check units and time ranges and label the assumed average.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"電量是功率對時間的累積。","textEn":"Energy is power accumulated over time."},{"id":"d002-v6-09-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"官方年度產量應連同年份閱讀，不能當作永久固定值。","textEn":"Official annual generation belongs to its stated year, not a permanent fixed output."}],"quiz":{"question":"示例產生多少電量？","questionEn":"How much energy does the example produce?","options":["6 MW","2 MWh，與時間無關","6 MWh"],"optionsEn":["6 MW","2 MWh, independent of time","6 MWh"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電量是功率對時間的累積。 官方年度產量應連同年份閱讀，不能當作永久固定值。","explanationEn":"Energy is power accumulated over time. Official annual generation belongs to its stated year, not a permanent fixed output."}},{"id":"d002-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-09"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-energy","v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"分開效率與可用率","titleEn":"Separate efficiency and availability","objective":"判斷同樣高效的設備為何年度輸出仍不同。","objectiveEn":"Explain why equally efficient equipment can have different annual outputs.","instruction":"用假設機組 A 與 B：運轉效率相同，但可用時數分別為 8 與 6；在相同平均功率下比較電量。","instructionEn":"Compare assumed units A and B with equal operating efficiency but 8 and 6 available hours at the same average power.","observation":"停機時數改變電量，即使運轉期間效率不變。","observationEn":"Downtime changes energy output even when operating efficiency is unchanged.","failure":"只報最佳效率會掩蓋停機與維修造成的交付差異。","failureEn":"Reporting only peak efficiency hides delivery differences caused by outages and maintenance.","check":"把損失帳與可用時數帳分成兩張表。","checkEn":"Separate conversion-loss and available-hours accounts.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"效率描述運轉時的能量轉換，可用率描述可服務時間比例。","textEn":"Efficiency describes energy conversion while operating; availability describes the fraction of serviceable time."},{"id":"d002-v6-10-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"年度比較還要控制來水條件，不能把所有差異都歸因於維修。","textEn":"Annual comparisons also need inflow context; not every difference is caused by maintenance."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一項可直接解釋示例兩機組的電量差異？","questionEn":"What directly explains the example’s energy difference?","options":["可用時數不同","效率一定不同","電量與時間無關"],"optionsEn":["Different available hours","Efficiency must differ","Energy is independent of time"],"answer":0,"explanation":"效率描述運轉時的能量轉換，可用率描述可服務時間比例。 年度比較還要控制來水條件，不能把所有差異都歸因於維修。","explanationEn":"Efficiency describes energy conversion while operating; availability describes the fraction of serviceable time. Annual comparisons also need inflow context; not every difference is caused by maintenance."}},{"id":"d002-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-10"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"建立異常證據的關聯圖","titleEn":"Map relationships among anomaly evidence","objective":"用多個觀察量區分假設故障。","objectiveEn":"Use multiple observations to separate hypothetical faults.","instruction":"設計兩張虛構事件卡：功率下降但水頭不變，以及水頭下降且功率下降；列出下一個需核對的量測。","instructionEn":"Create two fictional event cards: falling power with steady head, and falling head with falling power; list the next measurement to check.","observation":"相同功率症狀可能來自不同上游條件。","observationEn":"The same power symptom can arise from different upstream conditions.","failure":"只憑單一曲線宣判機組損壞，會把外部條件當成內部故障。","failureEn":"Declaring damage from one curve can mistake an external condition for an internal fault.","check":"每個判斷附上證據、替代解釋與未確認項，不自行解除保護。","checkEn":"Attach evidence, alternatives and unknowns to each judgment without overriding protections.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"故障診斷需要一致的時間基準及多訊號交叉檢查。","textEn":"Fault diagnosis needs aligned timestamps and cross-checking of multiple signals."},{"id":"d002-v6-11-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"事件卡是教學假設，並非電站事故紀錄或處置命令。","textEn":"The event cards are teaching assumptions, not plant incident records or response orders."}],"quiz":{"question":"單一功率下降曲線能確定什麼？","questionEn":"What can a single falling-power curve establish?","options":["水輪機必然已損壞","輸出下降，原因仍需其他證據","所有保護都應關閉"],"optionsEn":["The turbine is certainly damaged","Output fell; its cause still needs other evidence","All protections should be disabled"],"answer":1,"explanation":"故障診斷需要一致的時間基準及多訊號交叉檢查。 事件卡是教學假設，並非電站事故紀錄或處置命令。","explanationEn":"Fault diagnosis needs aligned timestamps and cross-checking of multiple signals. The event cards are teaching assumptions, not plant incident records or response orders."}},{"id":"d002-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d002-v6-11"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-itaipu-history","v6-science-itaipu-energy","v6-science-hydropower"],"title":"完成機電系統概念交接","titleEn":"Complete a conceptual electromechanical handover","objective":"把守恆、電網介面與驗證缺口合成可審查文件。","objectiveEn":"Combine conservation accounts, grid interfaces and evidence gaps into a reviewable package.","instruction":"提交一頁系統圖、兩張水量／能量帳、頻率分組表及三項待查證問題。","instructionEn":"Submit a one-page system diagram, water and energy accounts, a frequency-group table and three unresolved questions.","observation":"不同表格使用同一邊界與時間基準時，結論才可互相比較。","observationEn":"Conclusions become comparable when the tables share boundaries and time bases.","failure":"刪除假設標籤會讓教學計算看似正式設計。","failureEn":"Removing assumption labels makes teaching calculations look like formal design.","check":"為每張圖列來源與假設，並由另一位學徒重新核算一個量綱。","checkEn":"Label sources and assumptions and ask another learner to recheck one dimensional calculation.","knowledge":[{"id":"d002-v6-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"交接品質取決於可追溯的假設、介面與驗證證據。","textEn":"Handover quality depends on traceable assumptions, interfaces and verification evidence."},{"id":"d002-v6-12-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"完成課程表示通過概念審查，不表示有權建造或操作水電站。","textEn":"Course completion means passing a conceptual review, not authorization to construct or operate a plant."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪份交接資料最可審查？","questionEn":"Which handover package is most reviewable?","options":["只列總容量且沒有邊界","把所有假設改寫為實測值","保留來源、單位、假設及未解問題"],"optionsEn":["It lists capacity without boundaries","It relabels assumptions as measurements","It retains sources, units, assumptions and open questions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"交接品質取決於可追溯的假設、介面與驗證證據。 完成課程表示通過概念審查，不表示有權建造或操作水電站。","explanationEn":"Handover quality depends on traceable assumptions, interfaces and verification evidence. Course completion means passing a conceptual review, not authorization to construct or operate a plant."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":6,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240},{"id":"d107","title":"呂勒奧HYBRIT試驗工程","titleEn":"Lulea HYBRIT Pilot Engineering","category":"materials","kind":"course","summary":"以呂勒奧試驗設施理解氫還原、製氫、儲存與材料證據的系統關係。","summaryEn":"Use the Luleå pilots to understand hydrogen reduction, electrolysis, storage and material evidence as connected systems.","scope":"以公開試驗原理與紙上物料帳進行十二個概念任務。呂勒奧為試驗設施；耶利瓦勒的工業示範規劃為另一地點與尺度。本課不含化學製備、氫氣設備建造、操作參數或完整量產 SOP。","scopeEn":"Twelve conceptual tasks use public pilot principles and paper material accounts. Luleå hosts pilots; the Gällivare industrial-demonstration plan is a different site and scale. No chemical preparation, hydrogen equipment construction, operating settings or complete production SOP is provided.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-milestones","v6-science-hybrit-reduction","v6-science-hybrit-storage"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"materials","labels":["礦石球團","電解製氫","直接還原","儲存緩衝","產品證據"],"labelsEn":["Ore pellets","Electrolysis","Direct reduction","Storage buffer","Product evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d107-stage01","order":1,"title":"試驗邊界與投入","titleEn":"Pilot boundaries and inputs","description":"分清設施成熟度、物料與能源投入。","descriptionEn":"Separate facility maturity, material inputs and energy inputs.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d107-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-milestones","v6-science-hybrit-storage"],"title":"區分試驗與工業示範邊界","titleEn":"Separate pilot and industrial demonstration boundaries","objective":"分清呂勒奧試驗設施與耶利瓦勒工業示範規劃。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish the Luleå pilots from the planned Gällivare industrial demonstration.","instruction":"將呂勒奧還原試驗、呂勒奧儲氫試驗、耶利瓦勒示範規劃三張卡按地點與成熟度分類。","instructionEn":"Sort Luleå reduction, Luleå storage and planned Gällivare demonstration cards by location and maturity.","observation":"一項技術可以在不同城市、不同規模分階段驗證。","observationEn":"One technology can undergo staged verification at different scales and locations.","failure":"將試驗成功直接等同商業量產，會遺漏放大與整合的證據。","failureEn":"Equating pilot success with commercial production omits scale-up and integration evidence.","check":"每張卡均列地點、年份與已驗證的範圍，規劃不標為完工。","checkEn":"Give each card a location, date and verified scope; do not label plans as completed.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"試驗設施與工業示範的設備尺度和證據範圍不同。","textEn":"Pilot and industrial-demonstration facilities differ in scale and evidential scope."},{"id":"d107-v6-01-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課以呂勒奧公開試驗原理為案例，不宣稱耶利瓦勒設施已完工。","textEn":"This course uses public Luleå pilot principles without claiming completion at Gällivare."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個分類符合官方地點區分？","questionEn":"Which classification follows the official location distinction?","options":["呂勒奧是試驗案例，耶利瓦勒是另項示範規劃","三張卡均代表同一座已量產工廠","只要名稱相近就不需地點證據"],"optionsEn":["Luleå is the pilot case; Gällivare is a separate demonstration plan","All three cards represent one operating commercial factory","Similar names remove the need for location evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗設施與工業示範的設備尺度和證據範圍不同。 本課以呂勒奧公開試驗原理為案例，不宣稱耶利瓦勒設施已完工。","explanationEn":"Pilot and industrial-demonstration facilities differ in scale and evidential scope. This course uses public Luleå pilot principles without claiming completion at Gällivare."}},{"id":"d107-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-01"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"追蹤礦石中的鐵與氧","titleEn":"Track iron and oxygen in the ore","objective":"把還原反應理解為移除氧而保留鐵的物料變化。","objectiveEn":"Understand reduction as oxygen removal while retaining iron.","instruction":"用紙卡表示鐵、氧與氫，把反應前後的元素分別對帳；不配置化學品。","instructionEn":"Represent iron, oxygen and hydrogen with paper cards and balance each element before and after reaction; use no chemicals.","observation":"產物的鐵與被帶走的氧都有對應來源。","observationEn":"Both product iron and removed oxygen have identifiable origins.","failure":"只比較總質量而忽略含氧量，會把失重誤當鐵流失。","failureEn":"Comparing total mass without oxygen content can mistake oxygen removal for lost iron.","check":"各元素卡片數量守恆，並把水標在產物側。","checkEn":"Conserve the count of each element and place water on the product side.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"氫還原鐵氧化物時，氧與氫形成水。","textEn":"During hydrogen reduction of iron oxide, oxygen combines with hydrogen to form water."},{"id":"d107-v6-02-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"紙卡表達元素守恆，不提供實際反應條件或氣體配比。","textEn":"Cards express elemental conservation, not reaction conditions or gas-mixture recipes."}],"quiz":{"question":"還原後少掉的氧應如何交代？","questionEn":"How should removed oxygen be accounted for?","options":["當作質量憑空消失","追蹤到含氧產物流，例如水","假定所有失重都是鐵被消耗"],"optionsEn":["Treat it as mass that vanished","Trace it into an oxygen-containing product such as water","Assume all mass loss is consumed iron"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氫還原鐵氧化物時，氧與氫形成水。 紙卡表達元素守恆，不提供實際反應條件或氣體配比。","explanationEn":"During hydrogen reduction of iron oxide, oxygen combines with hydrogen to form water. Cards express elemental conservation, not reaction conditions or gas-mixture recipes."}},{"id":"d107-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-02"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"比較球團孔隙與反應介面","titleEn":"Compare pellet porosity and reaction interfaces","objective":"理解固體形狀與氣體接觸路徑的關係。","objectiveEn":"Relate solid structure to gas-access paths.","instruction":"畫兩個同外徑的概念球團剖面，一個連通孔隙較多、一個孔隙封閉；標示可接觸區。","instructionEn":"Draw two equal-diameter conceptual pellets, one with connected pores and one with closed pores; mark accessible regions.","observation":"外徑相同的球團未必具有相同內部可接觸面。","observationEn":"Equal external diameters do not imply equal internal accessibility.","failure":"只看外形就推定還原程度一致，會忽略傳質差異。","failureEn":"Inferring equal reduction from appearance ignores mass-transfer differences.","check":"明確區分外部尺寸、孔隙連通性與尚未量測的內部狀態。","checkEn":"Distinguish external dimensions, pore connectivity and unmeasured internal condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"固體內部的傳質路徑影響反應物能否抵達反應介面。","textEn":"Internal transport paths influence whether reactants reach reaction interfaces."},{"id":"d107-v6-03-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"示意圖只能提出假說，真實球團性能需適用量測與材料資料。","textEn":"A sketch proposes a hypothesis; real pellet performance needs suitable measurements and material data."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個推論最可靠？","questionEn":"Which inference is most defensible?","options":["相同外徑保證完全相同的還原表現","孔隙圖足以取代所有材料驗證","相同外徑仍可能具有不同氣體可達性"],"optionsEn":["Equal diameters guarantee identical reduction performance","A pore sketch replaces all material verification","Equal diameters can still have different gas accessibility"],"answer":2,"explanation":"固體內部的傳質路徑影響反應物能否抵達反應介面。 示意圖只能提出假說，真實球團性能需適用量測與材料資料。","explanationEn":"Internal transport paths influence whether reactants reach reaction interfaces. A sketch proposes a hypothesis; real pellet performance needs suitable measurements and material data."}},{"id":"d107-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-03"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"標示製氫的能源與水介面","titleEn":"Mark electricity and water interfaces for hydrogen","objective":"區分電解的物料投入與能源投入。","objectiveEn":"Separate material inputs from energy inputs in electrolysis.","instruction":"畫水與電力進入電解方塊、氫與氧離開的流程；把電力畫成能量箭頭。","instructionEn":"Draw water and electricity entering an electrolysis block and hydrogen and oxygen leaving; use an energy arrow for electricity.","observation":"電力供應來源會影響整體能源與排放評估。","observationEn":"The electricity source affects the overall energy and emissions assessment.","failure":"把電力寫成反應物質量，會混淆能量帳與物料帳。","failureEn":"Recording electricity as reactant mass confuses energy and material accounts.","check":"為水、氫、氧使用物料單位，為電力使用功率或電量單位。","checkEn":"Use material units for water, hydrogen and oxygen, and power or energy units for electricity.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"電解需要外部能量，不能僅由水的質量推算完整能耗。","textEn":"Electrolysis requires external energy; water mass alone cannot determine total energy demand."},{"id":"d107-v6-04-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"課程不含自製電解設備、氣體收集或通電操作。","textEn":"The course includes no homemade electrolyzer, gas collection or energization procedure."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪組資訊應放在不同帳表？","questionEn":"Which information belongs in separate accounts?","options":["水的質量與用電量","兩次以同單位量得的水質量","同一時間窗的氫氣投入與產出"],"optionsEn":["Water mass and electricity consumption","Two water masses measured in the same units","Hydrogen input and output over one time window"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電解需要外部能量，不能僅由水的質量推算完整能耗。 課程不含自製電解設備、氣體收集或通電操作。","explanationEn":"Electrolysis requires external energy; water mass alone cannot determine total energy demand. The course includes no homemade electrolyzer, gas collection or energization procedure."}}]},{"id":"d107-stage02","order":2,"title":"還原與循環介面","titleEn":"Reduction and recycle interfaces","description":"追蹤氧、水、固體產品與熱收支。","descriptionEn":"Trace oxygen, water, solid products and heat accounts.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d107-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-04"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-milestones","v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"比較氫還原的流程邊界","titleEn":"Compare the hydrogen-reduction process boundary","objective":"避免把局部反應與全生命週期排放混同。","objectiveEn":"Avoid confusing a local reaction with lifecycle emissions.","instruction":"畫氫直接還原與以碳作還原劑的概念路徑；另列電力、礦石與運輸的上游欄。","instructionEn":"Sketch hydrogen and carbon-reductant routes and add upstream electricity, ore and transport columns.","observation":"反應出口的差異不會自動消除上游影響。","observationEn":"Differences at the reaction outlet do not automatically eliminate upstream impacts.","failure":"只看水蒸氣出口就宣稱任何電源皆零排放，會越過證據邊界。","failureEn":"Claiming zero emissions for any electricity source from a water outlet exceeds the evidence.","check":"結論標明局部製程或生命週期邊界，不把二者混寫。","checkEn":"Label conclusions as process-level or lifecycle-level and keep the boundaries distinct.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"直接還原路徑的反應產物與能源供應排放需分開核算。","textEn":"Reaction products and energy-supply emissions require separate accounting."},{"id":"d107-v6-05-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"官方化石燃料替代目標不是本課自行計算出的完整碳盤查結果。","textEn":"Official fossil-fuel replacement goals are not a lifecycle inventory calculated by this lesson."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個主張需要額外上游資料？","questionEn":"Which claim requires additional upstream data?","options":["氫還原能形成水","全生命週期排放為零","電解需要電力"],"optionsEn":["Hydrogen reduction can form water","Lifecycle emissions are zero","Electrolysis needs electricity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"直接還原路徑的反應產物與能源供應排放需分開核算。 官方化石燃料替代目標不是本課自行計算出的完整碳盤查結果。","explanationEn":"Reaction products and energy-supply emissions require separate accounting. Official fossil-fuel replacement goals are not a lifecycle inventory calculated by this lesson."}},{"id":"d107-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-05"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"追蹤回流氣與水分離","titleEn":"Trace gas recirculation and water separation","objective":"識別循環物流及其累積項。","objectiveEn":"Identify recycle streams and accumulation terms.","instruction":"在概念圖把反應後氣流接到水分離方塊，再畫回流與補充物流；所有數值留白待證據填入。","instructionEn":"Connect reactor outlet gas to a water-separation block, then draw recycle and make-up streams; leave values blank pending evidence.","observation":"回流可以重用未反應物，但不等同沒有損失。","observationEn":"Recycle can reuse unreacted material but does not imply zero losses.","failure":"把回流當新的外部投入重複相加，會高估資源使用。","failureEn":"Counting recycle again as external input overstates resource use.","check":"分別圈出整廠邊界與回流迴路，確認每條外部物流只記一次。","checkEn":"Circle plant and recycle boundaries separately and count each external stream once.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"循環製程的總帳與單元帳具有不同邊界。","textEn":"Overall and unit-level accounts use different boundaries in a recycle process."},{"id":"d107-v6-06-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本圖只表達流程邏輯，不提供分離器設計或氫氣操作條件。","textEn":"The diagram expresses process logic, not separator design or hydrogen operating conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"整廠資源帳中應如何處理內部回流？","questionEn":"How should internal recycle appear in a plant-wide resource account?","options":["每循環一次都算全新外購量","認定有回流就不會有損失","不重複算成新的外部供應"],"optionsEn":["Count every pass as new purchased supply","Assume recycle eliminates all losses","Do not count it again as new external supply"],"answer":2,"explanation":"循環製程的總帳與單元帳具有不同邊界。 本圖只表達流程邏輯，不提供分離器設計或氫氣操作條件。","explanationEn":"Overall and unit-level accounts use different boundaries in a recycle process. The diagram expresses process logic, not separator design or hydrogen operating conditions."}},{"id":"d107-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-06"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"區分海綿鐵與完成鋼品","titleEn":"Distinguish sponge iron from finished steel","objective":"辨識直接還原產物與後續熔煉的介面。","objectiveEn":"Identify the interface between direct-reduced material and downstream steelmaking.","instruction":"將鐵礦球團、海綿鐵、後續熔煉與鋼品四張卡排序；在海綿鐵旁標固體與多孔。","instructionEn":"Order ore pellet, sponge iron, downstream melting and steel-product cards; mark sponge iron as solid and porous.","observation":"取得金屬鐵不代表合金成分與最終形狀已完成。","observationEn":"Producing metallic iron does not finish alloy composition or final shape.","failure":"把還原產物直接標為完成鋼材，會略過下游品質需求。","failureEn":"Labelling reduced material as finished steel skips downstream quality requirements.","check":"在兩個製程間列成分、物理狀態與可追溯批次三項交接資料。","checkEn":"List composition, physical state and traceable batch as three handover fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"直接還原可在不熔化鐵的條件下形成海綿鐵。","textEn":"Direct reduction can form sponge iron without melting the iron."},{"id":"d107-v6-07-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課沒有鋼廠配料或熔煉程序，僅辨識產品階段。","textEn":"This course identifies product stages without steelmaking recipes or melting procedures."}],"quiz":{"question":"海綿鐵卡應放在哪裡？","questionEn":"Where does the sponge-iron card belong?","options":["直接還原之後、後續鋼品製造之前","最終塗裝包裝之後","取代整個鋼材品質驗證程序"],"optionsEn":["After direct reduction and before downstream steel production","After final coating and packaging","In place of the entire steel-quality verification process"],"answer":0,"explanation":"直接還原可在不熔化鐵的條件下形成海綿鐵。 本課沒有鋼廠配料或熔煉程序，僅辨識產品階段。","explanationEn":"Direct reduction can form sponge iron without melting the iron. This course identifies product stages without steelmaking recipes or melting procedures."}},{"id":"d107-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-07"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"分離熱需求與化學轉化","titleEn":"Separate heat demand from chemical conversion","objective":"理解反應完成度與熱收支是不同檢查。","objectiveEn":"Understand reaction completion and heat balance as separate checks.","instruction":"畫物料流和熱流兩層圖；把加熱、散熱與熱回收放入能量層，不填實際溫度。","instructionEn":"Draw material-flow and heat-flow layers; place heating, losses and recovery in the energy layer without assigning real temperatures.","observation":"同一物料路線可以因熱損失而有不同外部能源需求。","observationEn":"The same material route can require different external energy because of heat losses.","failure":"只有元素守恆就宣稱能源足夠，會漏掉熱需求。","failureEn":"Declaring energy sufficiency from elemental balance alone omits heat demand.","check":"每一個熱流都有方向，回收熱不重複計作新供應。","checkEn":"Give each heat flow a direction and avoid counting recovered heat as new supply twice.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"物料守恆與能量守恆必須各自閉合。","textEn":"Material and energy conservation must each close independently."},{"id":"d107-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"沒有完整設備資料時，只能列需求項與未知量。","textEn":"Without complete equipment data, the result can only list requirements and unknowns."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪份證據不能單獨證明熱收支閉合？","questionEn":"Which evidence alone cannot establish a closed heat balance?","options":["完整且同邊界的能量帳","元素數量守恆表","帶單位的熱輸入與損失核對"],"optionsEn":["A complete energy account with consistent boundaries","An elemental conservation table","A unit-labelled comparison of heat input and losses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"物料守恆與能量守恆必須各自閉合。 沒有完整設備資料時，只能列需求項與未知量。","explanationEn":"Material and energy conservation must each close independently. Without complete equipment data, the result can only list requirements and unknowns."}}]},{"id":"d107-stage03","order":3,"title":"時間緩衝與證據交接","titleEn":"Time buffering and evidence handover","description":"以庫存模型與批次證據審視整合。","descriptionEn":"Review integration through inventory models and batch evidence.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d107-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-08"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-storage"],"title":"建立儲氫庫存的概念帳","titleEn":"Build a conceptual hydrogen inventory account","objective":"理解儲存如何緩衝產需時間差。","objectiveEn":"Understand how storage buffers timing differences between supply and demand.","instruction":"使用假設庫存 5、同時段流入 4、流出 3 個抽象單位，計算期末庫存。","instructionEn":"Use assumed inventory 5, inflow 4 and outflow 3 abstract units over one period to calculate ending inventory.","observation":"期末為 6 單位，儲存改變供應時間而非製造額外氫。","observationEn":"Ending inventory is 6 units; storage changes supply timing rather than creating hydrogen.","failure":"把充入量當作淨庫存增加會漏算同期取用。","failureEn":"Treating inflow as net inventory growth omits simultaneous withdrawal.","check":"驗證期初加流入減流出等於期末，並保留假設標籤。","checkEn":"Check opening plus inflow minus outflow against closing inventory and retain assumption labels.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"儲存設備連接製氫供給與還原需求的時間尺度。","textEn":"Storage connects the time scales of hydrogen supply and reduction demand."},{"id":"d107-v6-09-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"抽象單位不是壓力、容量設計或儲氫操作建議。","textEn":"Abstract units are not pressure settings, capacity designs or storage operating advice."}],"quiz":{"question":"假設期末庫存是多少？","questionEn":"What is the assumed ending inventory?","options":["9 個抽象單位","2 個抽象單位","6 個抽象單位"],"optionsEn":["9 abstract units","2 abstract units","6 abstract units"],"answer":2,"explanation":"儲存設備連接製氫供給與還原需求的時間尺度。 抽象單位不是壓力、容量設計或儲氫操作建議。","explanationEn":"Storage connects the time scales of hydrogen supply and reduction demand. Abstract units are not pressure settings, capacity designs or storage operating advice."}},{"id":"d107-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-09"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-storage"],"title":"比較兩段供需時間曲線","titleEn":"Compare supply and demand over two periods","objective":"區分平均供需平衡與每時段可供性。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish average balance from availability in each period.","instruction":"假設兩時段供應為 8、2，需求為 5、5；從零庫存開始，以紙上帳記錄可轉移的餘量。","instructionEn":"Assume supply of 8 and 2 and demand of 5 and 5 across two periods; track transferable surplus from zero opening inventory.","observation":"第一段餘量 3 可以在理想無損概念模型中補第二段缺口 3。","observationEn":"A surplus of 3 can fill the later deficit of 3 in an ideal lossless concept model.","failure":"只看總量 10 等於 10 就忽略時序，會錯判無儲存情況也可連續供應。","failureEn":"Looking only at equal totals of 10 misses timing and falsely implies continuous supply without storage.","check":"比較有儲存與無儲存兩張表，寫明模型忽略容量及速率限制。","checkEn":"Compare accounts with and without storage and state that the model omits capacity and rate limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"平均平衡不能保證每個時間窗皆平衡。","textEn":"Average balance does not guarantee balance in every time window."},{"id":"d107-v6-10-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"實際儲存還有損失、充放速率、容量與專業安全限制。","textEn":"Real storage also has losses, transfer-rate, capacity and professionally assessed safety limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何總供應等於總需求仍可能短缺？","questionEn":"Why can shortages occur despite equal total supply and demand?","options":["供需發生時間不同且缺少可用緩衝","守恆定律因此失效","只要總量相同就永遠不會短缺"],"optionsEn":["Supply and demand occur at different times without available buffering","Conservation therefore fails","Equal totals always eliminate shortages"],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均平衡不能保證每個時間窗皆平衡。 實際儲存還有損失、充放速率、容量與專業安全限制。","explanationEn":"Average balance does not guarantee balance in every time window. Real storage also has losses, transfer-rate, capacity and professionally assessed safety limits."}},{"id":"d107-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-10"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-milestones","v6-science-hybrit-reduction"],"title":"設計批次證據與材料交接","titleEn":"Design batch evidence and material handover","objective":"把材料身份與品質聲明連接到證據。","objectiveEn":"Link material identity and quality claims to evidence.","instruction":"製作虛構批次卡，列原料批號、還原產品身份、檢驗方法引用與未驗證欄。","instructionEn":"Create a fictional batch card with feed ID, reduced-product identity, test-method reference and unverified fields.","observation":"沒有批號的數據無法可靠連回特定材料。","observationEn":"Data without a batch identity cannot reliably be linked to a particular material.","failure":"將別批次數值複製成當批驗證，會破壞可追溯性。","failureEn":"Copying another batch’s values as current verification breaks traceability.","check":"所有數值標為自設示例或附來源，不把空欄當通過。","checkEn":"Label every value as hypothetical or sourced, and do not treat blanks as passes.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"批次追溯把原料、處理歷史與產品證據連為一體。","textEn":"Batch traceability links feedstock, processing history and product evidence."},{"id":"d107-v6-11-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不設定商業鋼材驗收規格；接受條件需由適用標準與買方定義。","textEn":"The lesson sets no commercial steel acceptance specification; applicable standards and buyers define those conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢驗欄空白時，最適合的狀態為何？","questionEn":"What is the appropriate status for a blank test field?","options":["自動通過","尚未驗證","以其他批次最高分代替"],"optionsEn":["Automatically passed","Not yet verified","Replace it with the highest score from another batch"],"answer":1,"explanation":"批次追溯把原料、處理歷史與產品證據連為一體。 本課不設定商業鋼材驗收規格；接受條件需由適用標準與買方定義。","explanationEn":"Batch traceability links feedstock, processing history and product evidence. The lesson sets no commercial steel acceptance specification; applicable standards and buyers define those conditions."}},{"id":"d107-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d107-v6-11"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hybrit-milestones","v6-science-hybrit-reduction","v6-science-hybrit-storage"],"title":"審查試驗工程的放大證據","titleEn":"Review evidence for pilot scale-up","objective":"完成區分已證實、假設與待驗證的系統交接。","objectiveEn":"Complete a handover distinguishing demonstrated facts, assumptions and open verification.","instruction":"提交地點成熟度表、物料與能量圖、儲存兩時段帳，以及三項放大後需再驗證的介面。","instructionEn":"Submit the location/maturity table, material and energy diagrams, two-period storage account and three interfaces needing scale-up verification.","observation":"放大問題包含傳熱、傳質、連續性與供應介面的共同變化。","observationEn":"Scale-up involves coupled changes in heat transfer, mass transfer, continuity and supply interfaces.","failure":"把小規模證據直接當成所有尺度保證，會超出資料支援範圍。","failureEn":"Treating small-scale evidence as a guarantee at every scale exceeds its support.","check":"逐句標註已證實、教學假設或待查證，並保留來源日期。","checkEn":"Label each claim as demonstrated, teaching assumption or unverified, retaining source dates.","knowledge":[{"id":"d107-v6-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"工程成熟度依賴可轉移的證據，而非僅依賴項目名稱。","textEn":"Engineering maturity depends on transferable evidence, not the project name alone."},{"id":"d107-v6-12-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"完成十二步代表概念審查，不代表完成氫系統設計或商業生產認證。","textEn":"Completing twelve tasks is a conceptual review, not hydrogen-system design or commercial-production certification."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個交接最能避免誇大試驗成果？","questionEn":"Which handover best avoids overstating pilot results?","options":["只寫技術已完全成熟","刪除地點與年份以免比較","明列規模、邊界與尚需驗證的介面"],"optionsEn":["State only that the technology is fully mature","Remove locations and dates to prevent comparison","State scale, boundaries and interfaces still requiring verification"],"answer":2,"explanation":"工程成熟度依賴可轉移的證據，而非僅依賴項目名稱。 完成十二步代表概念審查，不代表完成氫系統設計或商業生產認證。","explanationEn":"Engineering maturity depends on transferable evidence, not the project name alone. Completing twelve tasks is a conceptual review, not hydrogen-system design or commercial-production certification."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":6,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240},{"id":"d201","title":"EMI早期電腦斷層掃描器工程","titleEn":"EMI Early Computed Tomography Scanner Engineering","category":"biomedical","kind":"course","summary":"從 EMI 早期設備史出發，以數位假體拆解投影、重建與影像品質。","summaryEn":"Start with early EMI equipment history and use digital phantoms to study projections, reconstruction and image quality.","scope":"十二步限於設備物理、數位假體與品質追溯。歷史設備與現代 QA 來源分別標示，不推定規格相同。不操作輻射設備、不使用病人資料、不提供診斷、治療或臨床掃描設定；不是醫療設備製造或驗收 SOP。","scopeEn":"Twelve tasks cover equipment physics, digital phantoms and quality traceability. Historical equipment and modern QA sources are distinguished without assuming identical specifications. No radiation equipment, patient data, diagnosis, treatment or clinical scan settings are used; this is not a medical-device manufacturing or acceptance SOP.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-science-emi-object","v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality","v10-other-vendor-d201"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"biomedical","labels":["數位假體","投影","資料索引","重建","品質比較"],"labelsEn":["Digital phantom","Projections","Data indexing","Reconstruction","Quality comparison"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d201-stage01","order":1,"title":"證據、假體與投影","titleEn":"Evidence, phantoms and projections","description":"用已知數位矩陣建立可追溯的反問題。","descriptionEn":"Build a traceable inverse problem from a known digital matrix.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d201-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-emi-object","v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"建立早期 CT 的證據與功能邊界","titleEn":"Establish evidence and function boundaries for early CT","objective":"區分歷史設備事實、重建原理與現代品質方法。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish historical equipment facts, reconstruction principles and modern quality methods.","instruction":"排列多角度衰減投影、重建、影像三張卡；將 EMI 典藏紀錄與現代品質指南分欄。","instructionEn":"Order multi-angle attenuation projections, reconstruction and image cards; separate the EMI collection record from modern quality guidance.","observation":"歷史設備與現代品質原理可以互相說明，但不能假定規格完全相同。","observationEn":"Historical equipment and modern quality principles can inform each other without implying identical specifications.","failure":"把現代指南中的性能值套回 1971 年設備，會造成時代錯置。","failureEn":"Assigning modern performance values to the 1971 instrument creates an anachronism.","check":"每項主張都有歷史或原理標籤，並附相對應來源。","checkEn":"Label every claim as historical or conceptual and attach the appropriate source.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"CT 從多方向的衰減資訊推估物體內部的空間分布。","textEn":"CT estimates internal spatial distributions from attenuation information collected in multiple directions."},{"id":"d201-v6-01-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課只使用數位假體，不操作 X 光設備或解讀病人影像。","textEn":"This course uses digital phantoms only, without operating X-ray equipment or interpreting patient images."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪條資訊鏈最符合 CT 的基本原理？","questionEn":"Which information chain best describes CT?","options":["多角度投影→計算重建→影像","單張外觀照片→直接得知所有內部細節","先指定診斷→再修改投影符合答案"],"optionsEn":["Multi-angle projections → computational reconstruction → image","One external photograph → complete internal detail","Assign diagnosis → alter projections to match it"],"answer":0,"explanation":"CT 從多方向的衰減資訊推估物體內部的空間分布。 本課只使用數位假體，不操作 X 光設備或解讀病人影像。","explanationEn":"CT estimates internal spatial distributions from attenuation information collected in multiple directions. This course uses digital phantoms only, without operating X-ray equipment or interpreting patient images."}},{"id":"d201-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-01"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"建立帶座標的數位假體","titleEn":"Build a coordinate-labelled digital phantom","objective":"使像素位置、數值與已知真值可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Make pixel location, value and known ground truth traceable.","instruction":"畫 2×2 假體，第一列 1、2，第二列 3、4；標列、欄與任意衰減單位。","instructionEn":"Draw a 2×2 phantom with rows [1,2] and [3,4]; label rows, columns and arbitrary attenuation units.","observation":"四個像素的座標與數值具有確定對應。","observationEn":"Each of the four pixel coordinates has a defined value.","failure":"轉置陣列但不改座標標示，會讓方向判讀錯誤。","failureEn":"Transposing the array without relabelling coordinates causes orientation errors.","check":"請另一位學徒按座標重建同一矩陣，核對四個位置。","checkEn":"Ask another learner to reproduce the matrix from coordinates and check all four positions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"數位假體提供已知真值，便於測試演算法而不涉及人體。","textEn":"A digital phantom provides known ground truth for testing algorithms without human subjects."},{"id":"d201-v6-02-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"任意單位不是人體組織的 CT 值，也沒有診斷意義。","textEn":"Arbitrary units are not tissue CT values and have no diagnostic meaning."}],"quiz":{"question":"為什麼假體必須標座標？","questionEn":"Why must the phantom have coordinate labels?","options":["使所有像素自動變得相同","讓位置與數值對應可以重現","讓任意數字成為病人測量值"],"optionsEn":["To make all pixels identical automatically","To reproduce the mapping between location and value","To turn arbitrary numbers into patient measurements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"數位假體提供已知真值，便於測試演算法而不涉及人體。 任意單位不是人體組織的 CT 值，也沒有診斷意義。","explanationEn":"A digital phantom provides known ground truth for testing algorithms without human subjects. Arbitrary units are not tissue CT values and have no diagnostic meaning."}},{"id":"d201-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-02"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture"],"title":"計算兩方向的線積分近似","titleEn":"Calculate two-direction line-sum approximations","objective":"理解投影如何壓縮沿路徑的資訊。","objectiveEn":"Understand how projections combine information along paths.","instruction":"對前步 2×2 假體算列和 3、7 與欄和 4、6，保留其方向標籤。","instructionEn":"Calculate row sums 3,7 and column sums 4,6 for the previous 2×2 phantom, retaining direction labels.","observation":"每個和只保留沿一條路徑的總貢獻。","observationEn":"Each sum retains only the total contribution along one path.","failure":"把某條投影和當成單一像素值，會混淆量測與未知量。","failureEn":"Treating a projection sum as one pixel confuses measurements with unknowns.","check":"確認兩方向的總和都為 10，並註明這是簡化線和模型。","checkEn":"Confirm both directions total 10 and label this as a simplified line-sum model.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"理想化 CT 投影可用沿射線的衰減積分表示。","textEn":"Idealized CT projections can be represented by attenuation integrals along rays."},{"id":"d201-v6-03-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本例略去射束能譜、散射與探測器效應，只教幾何與守恆。","textEn":"This example omits spectra, scatter and detector effects to teach geometry and conservation."}],"quiz":{"question":"第一列的投影和是多少？","questionEn":"What is the first row’s projection sum?","options":["1","10","3"],"optionsEn":["1","10","3"],"answer":2,"explanation":"理想化 CT 投影可用沿射線的衰減積分表示。 本例略去射束能譜、散射與探測器效應，只教幾何與守恆。","explanationEn":"Idealized CT projections can be represented by attenuation integrals along rays. This example omits spectra, scatter and detector effects to teach geometry and conservation."}},{"id":"d201-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-03"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture"],"title":"辨識有限角度的不唯一性","titleEn":"Identify ambiguity from limited directions","objective":"說明少量投影不能唯一決定內部矩陣。","objectiveEn":"Explain why a few projections need not uniquely determine an internal matrix.","instruction":"比較矩陣 [1,2;3,4] 與 [2,1;2,5] 的列和及欄和。","instructionEn":"Compare row and column sums of matrices [1,2;3,4] and [2,1;2,5].","observation":"兩矩陣都有列和 3、7 與欄和 4、6，但內部數值不同。","observationEn":"Both have row sums 3,7 and column sums 4,6 despite different internal values.","failure":"只匹配兩方向投影就宣稱真值唯一，會掩蓋資料不足。","failureEn":"Claiming unique truth from two matching directions hides insufficient data.","check":"列出另一方向或額外限制可能補充的資訊，不憑空假設真值。","checkEn":"List information another direction or constraint could add without assuming the true answer.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"反問題可能有多個符合少量量測的解。","textEn":"An inverse problem can have multiple solutions consistent with limited measurements."},{"id":"d201-v6-04-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"資料一致性是必要檢查，但不自動等於唯一或正確重建。","textEn":"Data consistency is necessary but does not automatically imply a unique or correct reconstruction."}],"quiz":{"question":"相同兩方向投影可以證明什麼？","questionEn":"What do equal projections in two directions establish?","options":["在這些量測下相容，但不保證內部唯一","每個內部像素必定相同","多角度量測毫無價值"],"optionsEn":["Consistency with those measurements, without guaranteeing a unique interior","Every internal pixel must be identical","Additional angles have no value"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反問題可能有多個符合少量量測的解。 資料一致性是必要檢查，但不自動等於唯一或正確重建。","explanationEn":"An inverse problem can have multiple solutions consistent with limited measurements. Data consistency is necessary but does not automatically imply a unique or correct reconstruction."}}]},{"id":"d201-stage02","order":2,"title":"資料鏈與重建","titleEn":"Data chain and reconstruction","description":"比較正規化、角度索引、反投影與前向檢查。","descriptionEn":"Compare normalization, angle indexing, backprojection and forward checks.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d201-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-04"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"區分原始訊號與正規化資料","titleEn":"Separate raw signals from normalized data","objective":"理解參考訊號與探測器偏差的角色。","objectiveEn":"Understand reference signals and detector bias.","instruction":"製作兩個虛構探測器卡，寫相同物體訊號但不同空白參考；標示需要校正的比較。","instructionEn":"Make two fictional detector cards with equal object signals but different blank references; mark the comparison needing correction.","observation":"原始數值相同不一定代表相同衰減比例。","observationEn":"Equal raw values do not necessarily represent equal attenuation ratios.","failure":"忽略參考值漂移，可能把儀器差異誤認為物體差異。","failureEn":"Ignoring reference drift can mistake instrumental differences for object differences.","check":"在資料表保留原始值、參考值、校正版本三欄。","checkEn":"Retain raw value, reference value and calibration version in separate columns.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"量測需相對適當參考解讀，探測器偏差會傳到重建結果。","textEn":"Measurements require suitable references, and detector bias propagates into reconstruction."},{"id":"d201-v6-05-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課僅分類校正資料，不提供醫療設備現場校正操作。","textEn":"This task classifies calibration information without instructing onsite medical-equipment calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"相同原始讀值、不同參考值時，應先做什麼？","questionEn":"With equal raw readings but different references, what comes first?","options":["直接宣稱兩個衰減量完全相同","審查正規化及參考一致性","刪除參考值以方便比較"],"optionsEn":["Declare the attenuation values identical","Review normalization and reference consistency","Delete references to simplify comparison"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測需相對適當參考解讀，探測器偏差會傳到重建結果。 本課僅分類校正資料，不提供醫療設備現場校正操作。","explanationEn":"Measurements require suitable references, and detector bias propagates into reconstruction. This task classifies calibration information without instructing onsite medical-equipment calibration."}},{"id":"d201-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-05"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture"],"title":"組織投影角度索引","titleEn":"Organize projection-angle indexing","objective":"保持角度、探測器位置與量測值同步。","objectiveEn":"Keep angle, detector position and measurement value synchronized.","instruction":"以三個假設角度與兩個探測器位置製作六格資料表，給每格唯一索引。","instructionEn":"Make a six-cell table for three assumed angles and two detector positions, assigning a unique index to each cell.","observation":"重排角度列時，對應數值必須一起移動。","observationEn":"Reordering angle rows requires moving the corresponding values with them.","failure":"只排序角度標籤而不移動數值，會造成錯誤幾何配對。","failureEn":"Sorting angle labels alone creates incorrect geometry–value pairings.","check":"隨機挑一格，能追溯其角度、位置與來源是假設還是引用。","checkEn":"Trace one selected cell to its angle, position and hypothetical or cited origin.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"投影集合的幾何索引是重建輸入的一部分。","textEn":"Geometric indexing is part of the reconstruction input."},{"id":"d201-v6-06-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"這是自建小型資料表，不代表課程提供真實掃描器量測資料。","textEn":"This is a learner-built small table, not a supplied real-scanner dataset."}],"quiz":{"question":"排序投影時哪些資料必須一起移動？","questionEn":"What must move together when projections are sorted?","options":["只有角度文字","只有表格顏色","角度、位置與其對應數值"],"optionsEn":["Angle text alone","Table colours alone","Angle, position and associated value"],"answer":2,"explanation":"投影集合的幾何索引是重建輸入的一部分。 這是自建小型資料表，不代表課程提供真實掃描器量測資料。","explanationEn":"Geometric indexing is part of the reconstruction input. This is a learner-built small table, not a supplied real-scanner dataset."}},{"id":"d201-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-06"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"觀察簡單反投影的模糊","titleEn":"Observe blur in simple backprojection","objective":"理解把投影展回路徑不會立即恢復真值。","objectiveEn":"Understand why spreading projections back along paths does not immediately recover ground truth.","instruction":"把列和與欄和以半透明色帶展回 2×2 格線；與原假體逐格比較。","instructionEn":"Spread row and column sums back onto a 2×2 grid as translucent bands, then compare with the original phantom.","observation":"不同路徑的貢獻疊加，但細節不必等於原矩陣。","observationEn":"Contributions from different paths overlap without necessarily reproducing the original matrix.","failure":"把較亮的疊加圖直接稱為準確重建，會忽略模糊與正規化。","failureEn":"Calling a brighter overlay accurate reconstruction ignores blur and normalization.","check":"列出至少兩格差異，明確標為未濾波概念反投影。","checkEn":"List at least two cell differences and label the result conceptual unfiltered backprojection.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"反投影把投影資訊分配回空間，仍需適當重建方法控制模糊。","textEn":"Backprojection redistributes projection information into space; suitable reconstruction methods are still needed to manage blur."},{"id":"d201-v6-07-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"少量角度的手繪示例不能用來評價臨床影像性能。","textEn":"A few-angle sketch cannot assess clinical image performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"反投影疊加後應先檢查什麼？","questionEn":"What should be checked after backprojection overlap?","options":["與已知假體的差異及所用方法限制","影像顏色是否好看","是否可直接作診斷"],"optionsEn":["Differences from known ground truth and method limitations","Whether the colours are attractive","Whether it can immediately support diagnosis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反投影把投影資訊分配回空間，仍需適當重建方法控制模糊。 少量角度的手繪示例不能用來評價臨床影像性能。","explanationEn":"Backprojection redistributes projection information into space; suitable reconstruction methods are still needed to manage blur. A few-angle sketch cannot assess clinical image performance."}},{"id":"d201-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-07"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-hounsfield-lecture"],"title":"用前向投影檢查候選重建","titleEn":"Check a candidate reconstruction by forward projection","objective":"將候選影像重新投影以檢查資料一致性。","objectiveEn":"Reproject a candidate image to check measurement consistency.","instruction":"對候選矩陣 [1,1;3,4] 算列和與欄和，與目標 3、7 與 4、6 比較。","instructionEn":"Compute row and column sums for candidate [1,1;3,4] and compare with targets 3,7 and 4,6.","observation":"第一列與第二欄各少 1，顯示候選未符合全部資料。","observationEn":"The first row and second column are each short by 1, so the candidate does not fit all data.","failure":"只比較總亮度可能漏掉哪條路徑不一致。","failureEn":"Comparing total brightness alone can miss which path is inconsistent.","check":"逐路徑列殘差並保留正負號，不擅自更改目標資料。","checkEn":"List signed residuals for each path without changing the target data.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"前向模型把候選解轉回量測空間，便於比較殘差。","textEn":"A forward model maps a candidate solution back into measurement space for residual comparison."},{"id":"d201-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"殘差為零仍受有限角度的不唯一性限制。","textEn":"Zero residual still does not resolve ambiguity from limited angles."}],"quiz":{"question":"示例候選哪裡不符合目標？","questionEn":"Where does the candidate fail to match the target?","options":["每條路徑都完全符合","第一列與第二欄各少 1","只有顏色不同，數值都相同"],"optionsEn":["Every path matches exactly","The first row and second column are each short by 1","Only colours differ; all values agree"],"answer":1,"explanation":"前向模型把候選解轉回量測空間，便於比較殘差。 殘差為零仍受有限角度的不唯一性限制。","explanationEn":"A forward model maps a candidate solution back into measurement space for residual comparison. Zero residual still does not resolve ambiguity from limited angles."}}]},{"id":"d201-stage03","order":3,"title":"品質特徵與驗證報告","titleEn":"Quality characteristics and verification","description":"分別審視偏差、雜訊、細節與可重現性。","descriptionEn":"Review bias, noise, detail and reproducibility separately.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d201-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-08"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"比較均勻區的偏差與雜訊","titleEn":"Compare bias and noise in a uniform region","objective":"區分整體偏移與數值分散。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish overall offset from spread.","instruction":"以已知示例真值 10，比較區域 A=[10,10,10] 與 B=[9,10,11]，再比較 C=[12,12,12]。","instructionEn":"With example truth 10, compare regions A=[10,10,10], B=[9,10,11] and C=[12,12,12].","observation":"B 有分散但平均為 10；C 一致但有偏差。","observationEn":"B has spread with mean 10; C is consistent but biased.","failure":"把低雜訊直接當作準確，會忽略系統性偏移。","failureEn":"Treating low noise as accuracy ignores systematic bias.","check":"分開寫平均差與數值分散，全部標任意教學單位。","checkEn":"Report mean error and spread separately, using arbitrary teaching units.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"準確度、均勻性與雜訊描述不同品質特徵。","textEn":"Accuracy, uniformity and noise describe different quality characteristics."},{"id":"d201-v6-09-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"示例不含人體 CT 值或臨床合格門檻。","textEn":"The example contains no tissue CT values or clinical acceptance thresholds."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個區域示範一致但有偏差？","questionEn":"Which region is consistent but biased?","options":["A=[10,10,10]","只要一致就不可能有偏差","C=[12,12,12]"],"optionsEn":["A=[10,10,10]","Consistency makes bias impossible","C=[12,12,12]"],"answer":2,"explanation":"準確度、均勻性與雜訊描述不同品質特徵。 示例不含人體 CT 值或臨床合格門檻。","explanationEn":"Accuracy, uniformity and noise describe different quality characteristics. The example contains no tissue CT values or clinical acceptance thresholds."}},{"id":"d201-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-09"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"辨識解析度與平滑的取捨","titleEn":"Identify the resolution–smoothing trade-off","objective":"說明降低波動可能同時抹去細節。","objectiveEn":"Explain how reducing variation can also erase detail.","instruction":"畫一條含單格窄峰的數位剖面，與三格移動平均後的剖面比較峰寬與峰高。","instructionEn":"Draw a digital profile with a one-cell narrow peak and compare peak width and height after a three-cell moving average.","observation":"平滑可能降低局部波動，也使窄峰展寬。","observationEn":"Smoothing can reduce local variation while broadening a narrow peak.","failure":"只以平滑外觀評分，會忽略小特徵辨識能力。","failureEn":"Scoring only smooth appearance ignores small-feature visibility.","check":"同時記錄波動改變與峰形改變，說明選用方法的目的。","checkEn":"Record both variation and peak-shape changes and explain the method’s purpose.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"處理方法可以在雜訊與空間細節之間產生取捨。","textEn":"Processing methods can create a trade-off between noise and spatial detail."},{"id":"d201-v6-10-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"這是訊號處理練習，不建議病人掃描參數或影像診斷設定。","textEn":"This is signal-processing practice, not advice on patient scanning or diagnostic settings."}],"quiz":{"question":"平滑後圖更平順能證明什麼？","questionEn":"What does a smoother result establish?","options":["波動改變了，仍需檢查細節損失","所有影像品質都一定提高","可忽略解析度評估"],"optionsEn":["Variation changed; detail loss still needs checking","Every aspect of image quality improved","Resolution assessment is unnecessary"],"answer":0,"explanation":"處理方法可以在雜訊與空間細節之間產生取捨。 這是訊號處理練習，不建議病人掃描參數或影像診斷設定。","explanationEn":"Processing methods can create a trade-off between noise and spatial detail. This is signal-processing practice, not advice on patient scanning or diagnostic settings."}},{"id":"d201-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-10"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"把假體異常連回資料鏈","titleEn":"Trace phantom anomalies through the data chain","objective":"用可測假說區分物體、探測器與重建問題。","objectiveEn":"Separate object, detector and reconstruction issues using testable hypotheses.","instruction":"製作虛構案例：同一資料用兩個重建版本得到不同條紋；列出版本、校正與角度索引檢查。","instructionEn":"Create a fictional case where one dataset produces different streaks with two reconstruction versions; list version, calibration and angle-index checks.","observation":"資料相同而處理結果不同，應先審查處理鏈差異。","observationEn":"When identical data produce different outputs, processing-chain differences deserve initial review.","failure":"看到條紋就宣告病理異常，會越過設備品質課程的用途。","failureEn":"Declaring pathology from streaks exceeds the purpose of an equipment-quality lesson.","check":"每個假說附可重現比較，不對病人作任何結論。","checkEn":"Attach a reproducible comparison to each hypothesis and make no patient conclusions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"品質調查需要控制變因，才能把差異連回資料鏈。","textEn":"Quality investigation needs controlled variables to link differences to the data chain."},{"id":"d201-v6-11-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"此處所有案例為虛構數位假體，不是臨床判讀。","textEn":"Every case here is a fictional digital phantom, not clinical interpretation."}],"quiz":{"question":"同資料但不同重建版本出現差異時，首先應保留什麼？","questionEn":"With one dataset and different reconstruction outputs, what should be retained first?","options":["只保留較漂亮的圖","輸入資料與軟體版本的可追溯紀錄","任意修改資料直到兩圖相同"],"optionsEn":["Only the more attractive image","Traceable records of input data and software versions","Arbitrarily alter data until the images agree"],"answer":1,"explanation":"品質調查需要控制變因，才能把差異連回資料鏈。 此處所有案例為虛構數位假體，不是臨床判讀。","explanationEn":"Quality investigation needs controlled variables to link differences to the data chain. Every case here is a fictional digital phantom, not clinical interpretation."}},{"id":"d201-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d201-v6-11"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-emi-object","v6-science-hounsfield-lecture","v6-science-ct-quality"],"title":"完成無輻射的重建品質報告","titleEn":"Complete a radiation-free reconstruction quality report","objective":"交付可重現、有限度的數位假體驗證。","objectiveEn":"Deliver reproducible, bounded digital-phantom verification.","instruction":"整理假體矩陣、投影索引、候選殘差、偏差雜訊比較與方法版本，附來源和限制。","instructionEn":"Compile the phantom matrix, projection indices, candidate residuals, bias/noise comparison and method version, with sources and limitations.","observation":"已知真值、輸入與方法同時保存，才容易獨立重現。","observationEn":"Independent reproduction requires preserved ground truth, inputs and methods together.","failure":"把概念測試通過寫成醫療設備合格，會誇大驗證範圍。","failureEn":"Calling a passed concept test medical-device approval exaggerates verification scope.","check":"讓另一位學徒重算一條投影；報告明言沒有真實掃描、診斷或治療。","checkEn":"Have another learner recalculate one projection; state that no real scan, diagnosis or treatment occurred.","knowledge":[{"id":"d201-v6-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"可重現報告應保留資料來源、方法、版本與適用邊界。","textEn":"A reproducible report preserves data origin, method, version and applicability boundaries."},{"id":"d201-v6-12-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"完成本課只表示掌握影像物理的概念證據，不構成臨床能力認證。","textEn":"Completion demonstrates conceptual evidence in imaging physics, not certification of clinical competence."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪份報告的結論符合證據？","questionEn":"Which report conclusion matches the evidence?","options":["所有 CT 設備均已通過驗收","可直接替代醫療專業判讀","此數位假體在指定模型下通過已列檢查"],"optionsEn":["All CT devices have passed acceptance","It can replace professional clinical interpretation","This digital phantom passed the listed checks under the stated model"],"answer":2,"explanation":"可重現報告應保留資料來源、方法、版本與適用邊界。 完成本課只表示掌握影像物理的概念證據，不構成臨床能力認證。","explanationEn":"A reproducible report preserves data origin, method, version and applicability boundaries. Completion demonstrates conceptual evidence in imaging physics, not certification of clinical competence."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":6,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240},{"id":"d310","title":"卡倫堡工業共生系統","titleEn":"Kalundborg Industrial Symbiosis","category":"process","kind":"course","summary":"以卡倫堡為背景，從資源盤點、介面計量到合作治理建立工業共生概念方案。","summaryEn":"Use Kalundborg as context for a conceptual industrial-symbiosis proposal covering resource inventories, metering interfaces and cooperation.","scope":"三階段十二步以原創虛構企業與明示假設帳進行概念規劃；官方案例支持原理與歷史，不代表提供現行合約或實際管網數據。不是工廠連接、處理配方、法律合約或完整操作 SOP。","scopeEn":"Three stages and twelve tasks use fictional firms and explicitly assumed accounts for conceptual planning. Official cases support principles and history, not current contracts or real pipeline data. This is not a plant-connection procedure, treatment recipe, legal contract or complete operating SOP.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"process","labels":["來源廠","資源卡","交換介面","接收用途","共同治理"],"labelsEn":["Source plant","Resource card","Exchange interface","Receiving use","Joint governance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d310-stage01","order":1,"title":"邊界與資源適配","titleEn":"Boundaries and resource fit","description":"建立組織網路、盤點欄位與比較基準。","descriptionEn":"Establish the organizational network, inventory fields and baseline.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d310-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-kalundborg-about"],"title":"劃定跨企業資源交換網路","titleEn":"Define an inter-company resource network","objective":"將供應者、使用者與資源責任畫在同一系統圖。","objectiveEn":"Put suppliers, users and resource responsibilities on one system diagram.","instruction":"畫來源廠 A、接收廠 B 與第三方設施 C；分別標水、能源、物料箭頭及跨企業負責者。","instructionEn":"Draw source plant A, receiving plant B and third-party facility C; label water, energy and material arrows and inter-company owners.","observation":"資源可以跨企業循環，但品質與交付責任仍需明確。","observationEn":"Resources can circulate across firms while quality and delivery responsibilities still need definition.","failure":"只畫循環箭頭不標所有者，會隱藏跨企業介面。","failureEn":"Drawing loops without owners hides inter-company interfaces.","check":"每條交換線均有來源、接收者、資源類型與責任欄。","checkEn":"Give each exchange a source, receiver, resource type and responsibility field.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"工業共生將一個參與者的剩餘資源連到另一個參與者的需求。","textEn":"Industrial symbiosis links one participant’s surplus resources to another participant’s needs."},{"id":"d310-v6-01-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"A、B、C 是原創教學角色，不代表官方網路的特定現行合約。","textEn":"A, B and C are original teaching roles, not specific current contracts in the official network."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪條連接最容易進行介面審查？","questionEn":"Which connection is easiest to review?","options":["同時標示資源、兩端組織與責任","只有箭頭，沒有資源類別","把所有公司合併成無責任單一節點"],"optionsEn":["One naming the resource, both organizations and responsibility","An arrow without a resource type","All companies merged into an ownerless node"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工業共生將一個參與者的剩餘資源連到另一個參與者的需求。 A、B、C 是原創教學角色，不代表官方網路的特定現行合約。","explanationEn":"Industrial symbiosis links one participant’s surplus resources to another participant’s needs. A, B and C are original teaching roles, not specific current contracts in the official network."}},{"id":"d310-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-01"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"建立資源盤點欄位","titleEn":"Build a resource inventory","objective":"讓數量、時間與品質資訊可以比較。","objectiveEn":"Make quantity, timing and quality information comparable.","instruction":"設計三張資源卡，欄位包括名稱、數量單位、時段、品質限制與資料來源。","instructionEn":"Design three resource cards with name, quantity unit, time window, quality constraints and data source.","observation":"同名資源可能因濃度、溫度或供應時段不同而不可互換。","observationEn":"Resources with the same name may not be interchangeable because of composition, temperature or timing.","failure":"只記年總量會漏掉季節性與品質差異。","failureEn":"Recording annual totals alone misses seasonality and quality differences.","check":"每張卡均能回答多少、何時、何種品質與由誰提供證據。","checkEn":"Each card must answer how much, when, at what quality and who provides evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"交換可行性需要數量、品質、時間與位置同時匹配。","textEn":"Exchange feasibility requires matching quantity, quality, timing and location."},{"id":"d310-v6-02-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"未知資料應標待查證，不以零或最高品質代填。","textEn":"Unknown information should be marked unverified, not replaced with zero or the highest quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"只有資源名稱與年總量時，還缺什麼？","questionEn":"What is missing when only a resource name and annual total are known?","options":["更多裝飾圖示","時間分布、品質與介面資料","相同數值再重複一次"],"optionsEn":["More decorative icons","Timing, quality and interface information","The same value repeated once more"],"answer":1,"explanation":"交換可行性需要數量、品質、時間與位置同時匹配。 未知資料應標待查證，不以零或最高品質代填。","explanationEn":"Exchange feasibility requires matching quantity, quality, timing and location. Unknown information should be marked unverified, not replaced with zero or the highest quality."}},{"id":"d310-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-02"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"保存交換前的比較基準","titleEn":"Preserve the pre-exchange baseline","objective":"定義節省量所比較的原始情境。","objectiveEn":"Define the original scenario against which savings are compared.","instruction":"分開列出無交換與有交換兩種情境的外購資源、處理需求與共同產出邊界。","instructionEn":"List purchased resources, treatment needs and common output boundaries for scenarios without and with exchange.","observation":"只有產出與時間窗一致，節省量才有明確意義。","observationEn":"Savings are meaningful only when outputs and time windows are consistent.","failure":"把低產量年度與高產量年度直接比較，會把減產誤當效率改善。","failureEn":"Comparing low- and high-output years directly can mistake reduced production for efficiency gains.","check":"確認兩情境交付同等功能，並記錄所有假設差異。","checkEn":"Confirm equivalent delivered function and record all differing assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"基準情境決定效益計算的比較對象。","textEn":"The baseline defines the comparison used to calculate benefits."},{"id":"d310-v6-03-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不重算官方減碳宣稱，只建立可審查比較方法。","textEn":"This course builds a reviewable comparison method rather than recalculating official carbon claims."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪兩個情境最適合比較交換效益？","questionEn":"Which scenarios best support comparison of exchange benefits?","options":["產量和季節都不同且不作校正","只比較公司名稱長短","相同功能與時間窗，僅交換安排不同"],"optionsEn":["Different outputs and seasons without adjustment","Compare company-name lengths only","Same function and time window, with exchange arrangements differing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"基準情境決定效益計算的比較對象。 本課不重算官方減碳宣稱，只建立可審查比較方法。","explanationEn":"The baseline defines the comparison used to calculate benefits. This course builds a reviewable comparison method rather than recalculating official carbon claims."}},{"id":"d310-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-03"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"篩選來源與需求的匹配","titleEn":"Screen source–demand matches","objective":"識別數量吻合但品質不合的假匹配。","objectiveEn":"Identify false matches where quantity fits but quality does not.","instruction":"設計來源卡「可供 10、品質未驗證」與需求卡「需要 8、品質需確認」，以紅黃綠分類但不批准連接。","instructionEn":"Create source card “10 available, quality unverified” and demand card “8 needed, quality confirmation required”; classify readiness without approving a connection.","observation":"數量看似足夠，品質未知仍是未完成的匹配。","observationEn":"Quantity may appear sufficient while unknown quality leaves the match incomplete.","failure":"只因 10 大於 8 就判定可直接使用，會漏掉適用性。","failureEn":"Approving use because 10 exceeds 8 overlooks fitness for purpose.","check":"為數量、品質、時間、地點各列一個獨立狀態。","checkEn":"Give quantity, quality, timing and location separate status fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"工業交換需要滿足接收用途的條件，不能只看供應量。","textEn":"Industrial exchange must satisfy receiving-use conditions, not only supply volume."},{"id":"d310-v6-04-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"分類是概念篩選，實際連接需專業評估、協議與適用許可。","textEn":"Classification is conceptual screening; real connections need professional assessment, agreements and applicable permissions."}],"quiz":{"question":"上述來源與需求應如何標示？","questionEn":"How should the source and demand be marked?","options":["數量初步足夠，品質仍待確認","所有條件自動通過","接收端需求完全不重要"],"optionsEn":["Quantity provisionally sufficient; quality still unverified","All conditions automatically passed","Receiving requirements do not matter"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工業交換需要滿足接收用途的條件，不能只看供應量。 分類是概念篩選，實際連接需專業評估、協議與適用許可。","explanationEn":"Industrial exchange must satisfy receiving-use conditions, not only supply volume. Classification is conceptual screening; real connections need professional assessment, agreements and applicable permissions."}}]},{"id":"d310-stage02","order":2,"title":"守恆與交換介面","titleEn":"Conservation and exchange interfaces","description":"審查物料、熱、水與計量邊界。","descriptionEn":"Review material, heat, water and metering boundaries.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d310-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-04"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"閉合單一物料交換帳","titleEn":"Close a single-material exchange account","objective":"把接收量、剩餘量與損失分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate received quantity, remainder and losses.","instruction":"用同一時段的假設帳：來源 10、接收 7、已知其他去向 1，求尚待交代的餘量。","instructionEn":"Use an assumed same-period account: source 10, received 7 and known other destination 1; calculate the unaccounted remainder.","observation":"餘量為 2；不能因畫了交換箭頭就假設全部被利用。","observationEn":"The remainder is 2; an exchange arrow does not imply complete utilization.","failure":"把來源 10 與接收 7 都算為節省 17，會重複計數。","failureEn":"Counting source 10 and receipt 7 as savings of 17 double-counts the transfer.","check":"來源等於接收加其他去向加餘量，並檢查單位一致。","checkEn":"Verify source equals received plus other destinations plus remainder, using consistent units.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"物料在網路中的內部移轉不會創造額外物質。","textEn":"Internal transfers within a network do not create additional material."},{"id":"d310-v6-05-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本帳為自設例題，未交代餘量不是官方網路的實際排放或損失。","textEn":"This invented exercise does not identify real emissions or losses in the official network."}],"quiz":{"question":"例題尚待交代的餘量是多少？","questionEn":"What remainder is still unaccounted for?","options":["17","2","0，因為資源已經循環"],"optionsEn":["17","2","0, because the resource circulates"],"answer":1,"explanation":"物料在網路中的內部移轉不會創造額外物質。 本帳為自設例題，未交代餘量不是官方網路的實際排放或損失。","explanationEn":"Internal transfers within a network do not create additional material. This invented exercise does not identify real emissions or losses in the official network."}},{"id":"d310-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-05"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"區分熱量與溫度適用性","titleEn":"Distinguish heat quantity from temperature suitability","objective":"理解餘熱總量不能單獨決定用途。","objectiveEn":"Understand why total surplus heat alone cannot determine its use.","instruction":"畫來源熱流與兩個需求端，一個需求溫度較低、一個較高；用概念箭頭標出需進一步評估的提升介面。","instructionEn":"Draw a heat source and two demands at lower and higher temperature requirements; mark any upgrading interface needing evaluation.","observation":"熱量相同的來源，因溫度不同而可能適合不同需求。","observationEn":"Sources with equal heat quantities can suit different demands because their temperatures differ.","failure":"只看能量總數相等就宣告可直接替代，會忽略熱品位。","failureEn":"Declaring direct substitution from equal energy totals ignores heat quality.","check":"同時列熱量單位與溫度條件，未知者保留空缺說明。","checkEn":"Record both heat quantity units and temperature conditions, explaining unknowns.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"熱的可利用性取決於溫差、需求與轉換介面。","textEn":"Heat usefulness depends on temperature difference, demand and conversion interfaces."},{"id":"d310-v6-06-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不提供蒸汽管線、熱泵或受壓設備的設計操作參數。","textEn":"The lesson provides no design or operating settings for steam lines, heat pumps or pressure equipment."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估餘熱交換時，除了熱量還需什麼？","questionEn":"What is needed besides heat quantity when assessing heat exchange?","options":["只需來源廠商標誌","把熱量全部改成沒有單位的分數","來源與需求的溫度及介面條件"],"optionsEn":["Only the source company’s logo","Convert all heat quantities to unitless scores","Source and demand temperatures and interface conditions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱的可利用性取決於溫差、需求與轉換介面。 本課不提供蒸汽管線、熱泵或受壓設備的設計操作參數。","explanationEn":"Heat usefulness depends on temperature difference, demand and conversion interfaces. The lesson provides no design or operating settings for steam lines, heat pumps or pressure equipment."}},{"id":"d310-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-06"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"確認水的用途適配","titleEn":"Check water fitness for purpose","objective":"避免把回用水標籤當作所有用途都合格。","objectiveEn":"Avoid treating a reused-water label as approval for every use.","instruction":"以三張虛構需求卡列冷卻、清洗與更高品質製程用水；分別列待驗證的品質項。","instructionEn":"Create fictional cooling, washing and higher-quality process-water demand cards, listing quality evidence needed for each.","observation":"同一水源可以適合一種用途而不適合另一種用途。","observationEn":"One water source can fit one use while failing another.","failure":"把所有水需求合成單一容量欄會掩蓋交叉污染風險與品質限制。","failureEn":"Merging all water demands into one capacity field hides contamination concerns and quality constraints.","check":"每個用途有獨立品質欄、來源與未驗證標記，不設定飲用安全結論。","checkEn":"Give every use a separate quality field, source and verification status without declaring drinking-water safety.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"資源循環需要符合接收用途，回用本身不保證品質。","textEn":"Circular use must meet receiving requirements; reuse alone does not guarantee quality."},{"id":"d310-v6-07-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"這是用途分類練習，不是水處理配方或供水驗收規範。","textEn":"This is a use-classification exercise, not a treatment recipe or water-supply acceptance specification."}],"quiz":{"question":"「可回用」標籤能否證明所有用途都適合？","questionEn":"Does a “reusable” label establish suitability for every use?","options":["不能，需逐用途核對品質條件","可以，只要數量足夠","可以，水的用途不影響要求"],"optionsEn":["No; quality conditions must be checked for each use","Yes, if the quantity is sufficient","Yes; water use does not affect requirements"],"answer":0,"explanation":"資源循環需要符合接收用途，回用本身不保證品質。 這是用途分類練習，不是水處理配方或供水驗收規範。","explanationEn":"Circular use must meet receiving requirements; reuse alone does not guarantee quality. This is a use-classification exercise, not a treatment recipe or water-supply acceptance specification."}},{"id":"d310-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-07"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"界定計量與所有權交接點","titleEn":"Define metering and ownership-transfer points","objective":"使雙方對交換數量採一致邊界。","objectiveEn":"Give both parties a consistent boundary for exchanged quantities.","instruction":"在 A 到 B 的概念線上畫兩個計量點與一個交接點，標時間窗與誰保管讀值。","instructionEn":"Draw two meter points and one handover point on an A-to-B concept line, marking time windows and record owners.","observation":"兩端讀值差異可能涉及時間、庫存、損失或儀表偏差。","observationEn":"Differences between end readings can involve timing, storage, losses or meter bias.","failure":"未對齊時間就直接歸咎某一方，會把記帳差異誤判為違約。","failureEn":"Blaming one party before aligning time windows can mistake accounting differences for non-compliance.","check":"比較前先統一單位與時間，再列差值的替代解釋。","checkEn":"Align units and time before comparison, then list alternative explanations for differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"計量點與責任交接點可能不同，必須明確記錄。","textEn":"Metering and responsibility-transfer points can differ and must be documented."},{"id":"d310-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"概念線不揭示真實管線位置，也不授權接管或調整儀表。","textEn":"The concept line reveals no real pipeline route and authorizes no connection or meter adjustment."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩端讀值不同時第一步應是什麼？","questionEn":"What comes first when endpoint readings differ?","options":["立刻宣告其中一方違約","核對時間窗、單位與計量邊界","任選一個數字刪掉另一個"],"optionsEn":["Immediately declare one party in breach","Check time windows, units and metering boundaries","Keep either number and delete the other"],"answer":1,"explanation":"計量點與責任交接點可能不同，必須明確記錄。 概念線不揭示真實管線位置，也不授權接管或調整儀表。","explanationEn":"Metering and responsibility-transfer points can differ and must be documented. The concept line reveals no real pipeline route and authorizes no connection or meter adjustment."}}]},{"id":"d310-stage03","order":3,"title":"合作、韌性與交接","titleEn":"Cooperation, resilience and handover","description":"處理時間承諾、中斷依賴與效益歸屬。","descriptionEn":"Address time commitments, interruption dependencies and benefit attribution.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d310-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-08"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"比較承諾供應與實際可用性","titleEn":"Compare committed supply with actual availability","objective":"辨識長期合作中時間與品質承諾的作用。","objectiveEn":"Identify the role of timing and quality commitments in cooperation.","instruction":"建立虛構交換協議欄：資源品質、交付時窗、資料責任、異常通知與變更審查。","instructionEn":"Create fictional agreement fields for quality, delivery windows, data ownership, incident notification and change review.","observation":"年度總量承諾不能取代停機期間的供應安排。","observationEn":"An annual quantity commitment cannot replace arrangements for outages.","failure":"只寫平均供應量卻不說中斷，會使接收端高估連續性。","failureEn":"Listing only average supply without interruptions overstates continuity for the receiver.","check":"為供應中斷情境列通知對象與需共同決策的資料，不寫現場處置命令。","checkEn":"For an interruption scenario, list recipients and information for joint decisions, without field-response instructions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"跨企業合作需要共享資訊與清楚的責任安排。","textEn":"Inter-company cooperation needs shared information and clear responsibilities."},{"id":"d310-v6-09-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"協議欄是教學框架，不是可直接簽署的法律合約。","textEn":"These agreement fields are a teaching framework, not a ready-to-sign legal contract."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項最能補足平均供應量的不足？","questionEn":"What best complements an average supply quantity?","options":["更大的公司名稱字體","刪除所有異常情境","供應時窗、中斷通知與品質責任"],"optionsEn":["A larger company-name font","Removing all exception scenarios","Supply windows, interruption notification and quality responsibilities"],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨企業合作需要共享資訊與清楚的責任安排。 協議欄是教學框架，不是可直接簽署的法律合約。","explanationEn":"Inter-company cooperation needs shared information and clear responsibilities. These agreement fields are a teaching framework, not a ready-to-sign legal contract."}},{"id":"d310-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-09"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"推演一條交換中斷的影響","titleEn":"Trace the effects of an interrupted exchange","objective":"辨識依賴關係與備援需求。","objectiveEn":"Identify dependencies and fallback needs.","instruction":"在 A→B→C 的教學網路移除 A→B，標示直接與間接受影響節點；列替代供應待驗證欄。","instructionEn":"Remove A→B from the teaching network A→B→C, mark direct and indirect effects, and list alternative-supply verification needs.","observation":"下游依賴可能讓一次中斷影響多個參與者。","observationEn":"Downstream dependencies can spread one interruption across several participants.","failure":"假定備援資源必然相容，可能把品質不合的物料送入下游。","failureEn":"Assuming fallback compatibility can pass unsuitable material downstream.","check":"每個替代方案重新核對數量、品質、時間與責任，不自動繞過檢查。","checkEn":"Recheck quantity, quality, timing and responsibility for each alternative without bypassing checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"網路韌性取決於依賴結構與已驗證的替代路徑。","textEn":"Network resilience depends on dependencies and verified alternatives."},{"id":"d310-v6-10-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"推演只在紙上進行，不要求改動任何現場管網或供應。","textEn":"This is a paper exercise and requires no changes to real networks or supplies."}],"quiz":{"question":"A→B 中斷後，哪個判斷最合理？","questionEn":"After A→B fails, which judgment is most reasonable?","options":["B 直接受影響，C 可能因依賴而受影響","只有 A 的圖示需要改色","任意資源都可立即取代原供應"],"optionsEn":["B is directly affected; C may be affected through dependence","Only A’s icon needs recolouring","Any resource can immediately replace the original supply"],"answer":0,"explanation":"網路韌性取決於依賴結構與已驗證的替代路徑。 推演只在紙上進行，不要求改動任何現場管網或供應。","explanationEn":"Network resilience depends on dependencies and verified alternatives. This is a paper exercise and requires no changes to real networks or supplies."}},{"id":"d310-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-10"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"避免節省量重複歸屬","titleEn":"Avoid double attribution of savings","objective":"區分公司個別效益與網路總效益。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish individual benefits from network-wide benefits.","instruction":"假設一筆交換替代 7 單位外購資源；分列供應者、接收者與網路總帳，標明共同受益。","instructionEn":"Assume one exchange replaces 7 units of purchased resource; separate supplier, receiver and network accounts and mark shared benefits.","observation":"雙方均可受益，但同一筆物理替代量在總帳只計一次。","observationEn":"Both parties can benefit, but the same physical substitution is counted once in the total.","failure":"把兩家都報的 7 相加為 14，會高估網路節省。","failureEn":"Adding the 7 reported by each firm into 14 overstates network savings.","check":"每筆效益都有唯一交換編號、基準與歸屬規則。","checkEn":"Give each benefit a unique exchange ID, baseline and attribution rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"聚合效益需排除重複計數並維持一致邊界。","textEn":"Aggregated benefits require removing double-counting and keeping consistent boundaries."},{"id":"d310-v6-11-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"物料節省不是自動等同碳減量，後者還需適用係數與邊界。","textEn":"Material savings do not automatically equal carbon reductions, which need suitable factors and boundaries."}],"quiz":{"question":"同一筆 7 單位替代在網路總帳應記多少？","questionEn":"How much should the network count for one 7-unit substitution?","options":["14 單位，因為有兩家公司","7 單位，並揭露歸屬方式","沒有單位，只寫效益很大"],"optionsEn":["14 units, because two companies are involved","7 units, with attribution disclosed","No units; simply state large benefits"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聚合效益需排除重複計數並維持一致邊界。 物料節省不是自動等同碳減量，後者還需適用係數與邊界。","explanationEn":"Aggregated benefits require removing double-counting and keeping consistent boundaries. Material savings do not automatically equal carbon reductions, which need suitable factors and boundaries."}},{"id":"d310-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d310-v6-11"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-kalundborg","v6-science-kalundborg-about","v6-science-symbiosis-facilitation"],"title":"完成共生網路的分期交接","titleEn":"Complete a staged symbiosis-network handover","objective":"把資源適配、治理與證據整合為可審查方案。","objectiveEn":"Integrate resource fit, governance and evidence into a reviewable proposal.","instruction":"提交網路圖、資源卡、基準與交換帳、異常推演及資料缺口清單；為每項指派驗證責任。","instructionEn":"Submit the network map, resource cards, baseline and exchange accounts, interruption exercise and data gaps, assigning verification responsibility.","observation":"方案成熟度由已確認的介面與合作證據決定，不能只看連線數量。","observationEn":"Proposal maturity depends on verified interfaces and collaboration evidence, not the number of links alone.","failure":"把未驗證交換全部標成完成，會讓後續決策失去依據。","failureEn":"Marking every unverified exchange as complete removes the basis for later decisions.","check":"按已知、假設、待確認三類審查，讓另一位學徒追算一次總帳。","checkEn":"Review known, assumed and unverified items, and have another learner trace one total account.","knowledge":[{"id":"d310-v6-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"工業共生是持續協調的社會與工程系統。","textEn":"Industrial symbiosis is an engineering and social system requiring continuing coordination."},{"id":"d310-v6-12-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"十二步是概念規劃，不代表已取得真實資源、商業協議或運作許可。","textEn":"These twelve tasks are conceptual planning, not access to real resources, commercial agreements or operating permissions."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪份方案最適合交給下一位工程師？","questionEn":"Which proposal is best for the next engineer?","options":["只有漂亮循環圖而沒有資料","把所有缺漏標成不重要","附證據、責任與未解介面的版本"],"optionsEn":["An attractive loop diagram without data","One labelling every gap unimportant","A version with evidence, responsibilities and unresolved interfaces"],"answer":2,"explanation":"工業共生是持續協調的社會與工程系統。 十二步是概念規劃，不代表已取得真實資源、商業協議或運作許可。","explanationEn":"Industrial symbiosis is an engineering and social system requiring continuing coordination. These twelve tasks are conceptual planning, not access to real resources, commercial agreements or operating permissions."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":6,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240},{"id":"d401","title":"大型強子對撞機LHC","titleEn":"Large Hadron Collider LHC","category":"megascience","kind":"course","summary":"以 LHC 的公開系統介紹拆解束流導引、RF、低溫、真空與探測資料介面。","summaryEn":"Use public LHC system descriptions to examine beam guidance, RF, cryogenics, vacuum and detector-data interfaces.","scope":"十二步是紙上模型與原創示意圖的概念課程，不提供真實機器設定、束流操作、聯鎖解除或繞過方式。教學事件卡不是真實 LHC 量測，也不作新物理結論；不是加速器設計或運轉 SOP。","scopeEn":"Twelve tasks use paper models and original concept diagrams. They provide no real machine settings, beam operations, interlock releases or bypass methods. Teaching event cards are not LHC measurements and support no new-physics conclusions; this is not an accelerator design or operating SOP.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc","v6-science-lhc-magnets","v6-science-lhc-rf","v6-video-6UqW4GEla3Q"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"megascience","labels":["束流","磁鐵","RF 共振腔","低溫／真空","探測與資料"],"labelsEn":["Beam","Magnets","RF cavities","Cryogenics / vacuum","Detection and data"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d401-stage01","order":1,"title":"職責與束流幾何","titleEn":"Responsibilities and beam geometry","description":"區分加速器、探測器、束團與彎轉。","descriptionEn":"Distinguish accelerator, detector, bunches and bending.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d401-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc"],"title":"分開加速器與探測器職責","titleEn":"Separate accelerator and detector responsibilities","objective":"辨識導引加速束流與記錄碰撞的不同系統。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish systems that guide and accelerate beams from systems that record collisions.","instruction":"把磁鐵導引、射頻加速、真空保持放入加速器欄；把碰撞訊號與事件紀錄放入探測器欄，畫交會介面。","instructionEn":"Place magnetic guidance, RF acceleration and vacuum maintenance under accelerator; place collision signals and event records under detector and draw their interface.","observation":"加速器與探測器緊密協作，但交付內容不同。","observationEn":"Accelerator and detector cooperate closely but deliver different functions.","failure":"把所有設備都稱作探測器，會隱藏束流條件與量測的分工。","failureEn":"Calling every component a detector hides the distinction between beam conditions and measurements.","check":"每張卡都有主責系統，並標示碰撞點的共同介面。","checkEn":"Assign a primary system to every card and mark the shared collision-point interface.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"加速器建立粒子束條件；探測器把相互作用轉為可分析訊號。","textEn":"Accelerators establish beam conditions; detectors turn interactions into analyzable signals."},{"id":"d401-v6-01-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課是公開系統原理分類，不控制任何束流或真實設施。","textEn":"This is public system-principle classification, not control of beams or real facilities."}],"quiz":{"question":"「事件紀錄」最主要屬於哪一側？","questionEn":"Which side primarily owns event recording?","options":["探測器與資料取得系統","磁鐵支架的外觀設計","僅真空管的幾何外形"],"optionsEn":["Detector and data-acquisition systems","The visual design of magnet supports","Vacuum-pipe geometry alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"加速器建立粒子束條件；探測器把相互作用轉為可分析訊號。 本課是公開系統原理分類，不控制任何束流或真實設施。","explanationEn":"Accelerators establish beam conditions; detectors turn interactions into analyzable signals. This is public system-principle classification, not control of beams or real facilities."}},{"id":"d401-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-01"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc"],"title":"畫出環形束流的介面","titleEn":"Map interfaces around a beam ring","objective":"區分環形路徑、注入連接與碰撞區域。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish ring paths, injection connections and collision regions.","instruction":"畫原創不按比例環圖，標兩方向束流、外部注入來源與碰撞點；所有箭頭標方向。","instructionEn":"Draw an original not-to-scale ring with two beam directions, external injection interfaces and collision points; label every arrow direction.","observation":"一個環形設施仍有多個跨系統的輸入與量測介面。","observationEn":"A ring facility still has multiple cross-system input and measurement interfaces.","failure":"把所有箭頭合併為單一方向，會失去兩束相向運動的意義。","failureEn":"Merging all arrows into one direction loses the meaning of counter-rotating beams.","check":"辨認兩條束流路徑，並明說概念圖不是地下設施地圖。","checkEn":"Identify both beam paths and state that the concept diagram is not a map of underground facilities.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"LHC 的相向束流在分離束管中運行，於指定區域相遇。","textEn":"LHC counter-rotating beams travel in separate beam pipes and meet in designated regions."},{"id":"d401-v6-02-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"不按比例圖用於介面理解，不提供通行、安裝或運轉座標。","textEn":"The not-to-scale map teaches interfaces, not access, installation or operating coordinates."}],"quiz":{"question":"概念環圖必須保留什麼？","questionEn":"What must the conceptual ring retain?","options":["所有地下設備的精確位置","兩束流方向與碰撞介面","把兩束流畫成同一根無方向線"],"optionsEn":["Exact locations of all underground equipment","Both beam directions and collision interfaces","Both beams as one directionless line"],"answer":1,"explanation":"LHC 的相向束流在分離束管中運行，於指定區域相遇。 不按比例圖用於介面理解，不提供通行、安裝或運轉座標。","explanationEn":"LHC counter-rotating beams travel in separate beam pipes and meet in designated regions. The not-to-scale map teaches interfaces, not access, installation or operating coordinates."}},{"id":"d401-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-02"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc","v6-science-lhc-rf"],"title":"區分單粒子、束團與平均量","titleEn":"Distinguish particles, bunches and averages","objective":"理解離散粒子束與連續平均表示的差別。","objectiveEn":"Understand the difference between discrete bunches and continuous averages.","instruction":"用三群紙點代表三個束團；比較「每群點數」與「整段時間總點數」兩種描述。","instructionEn":"Use three groups of paper dots as bunches; compare dots per bunch with total dots over a time interval.","observation":"相同總點數可以具有不同的時間分布。","observationEn":"Equal total dot counts can have different time distributions.","failure":"把平均量當作每個瞬間都相同，會抹去束團結構。","failureEn":"Treating averages as identical at every instant erases bunch structure.","check":"給每個量附時間窗或束團索引，不加入真實機器設定。","checkEn":"Attach a time window or bunch index to every quantity without using real machine settings.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"束團結構把粒子分布與射頻時間關係連在一起。","textEn":"Bunch structure links particle distributions to RF timing."},{"id":"d401-v6-03-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"紙點不代表真實粒子數、束流強度或操作要求。","textEn":"Paper dots do not represent actual particle counts, beam intensity or operating requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"相同總點數可否代表相同時間分布？","questionEn":"Do equal total dot counts guarantee identical timing?","options":["可以，總數決定所有時間細節","只有紙的顏色決定時間分布","不能，還需要束團與時間資訊"],"optionsEn":["Yes; the total determines all timing detail","Only paper colour determines timing","No; bunch and timing information is also needed"],"answer":2,"explanation":"束團結構把粒子分布與射頻時間關係連在一起。 紙點不代表真實粒子數、束流強度或操作要求。","explanationEn":"Bunch structure links particle distributions to RF timing. Paper dots do not represent actual particle counts, beam intensity or operating requirements."}},{"id":"d401-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-03"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc-magnets","v6-science-lhc-rf"],"title":"辨識二極磁鐵的彎轉角色","titleEn":"Identify the bending role of dipole magnets","objective":"把改變方向與增加能量分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate changing direction from adding energy.","instruction":"在概念束流路徑加入二極磁鐵方塊；以相同速度長度的箭頭表示方向改變。","instructionEn":"Add dipole blocks to a conceptual beam path; use equal-length velocity arrows to represent a change of direction.","observation":"理想磁力的彎轉作用不等於射頻電場的加速作用。","observationEn":"Ideal magnetic bending is distinct from acceleration by an RF electric field.","failure":"把彎得更明顯直接當成能量增加，會混淆方向與動能。","failureEn":"Treating greater bending as energy gain confuses direction with kinetic energy.","check":"圖上分別標出方向改變與能量轉移的位置。","checkEn":"Mark direction changes and energy-transfer locations separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"磁場可以改變帶電粒子的運動方向，RF 電場用於能量轉移。","textEn":"Magnetic fields can change charged-particle direction, while RF electric fields transfer energy."},{"id":"d401-v6-04-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"示意箭頭不是磁場強度或真實束流調整建議。","textEn":"Diagram arrows are not magnetic-field settings or real beam-adjustment advice."}],"quiz":{"question":"二極磁鐵在本圖的主要作用為何？","questionEn":"What is the dipole’s primary role in this diagram?","options":["彎轉束流方向","記錄碰撞事件的影像","直接替代所有射頻能量輸入"],"optionsEn":["Bending the beam direction","Recording images of collision events","Replacing all RF energy input"],"answer":0,"explanation":"磁場可以改變帶電粒子的運動方向，RF 電場用於能量轉移。 示意箭頭不是磁場強度或真實束流調整建議。","explanationEn":"Magnetic fields can change charged-particle direction, while RF electric fields transfer energy. Diagram arrows are not magnetic-field settings or real beam-adjustment advice."}}]},{"id":"d401-stage02","order":2,"title":"束流支援介面","titleEn":"Beam-support interfaces","description":"理解兩平面聚焦、射頻、熱與真空。","descriptionEn":"Understand two-plane focusing, RF, heat and vacuum.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d401-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-04"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc-magnets"],"title":"理解四極的兩平面作用","titleEn":"Understand quadrupole action in two planes","objective":"辨識單一四極不能同時簡化為兩方向都聚焦。","objectiveEn":"Recognize that one quadrupole cannot simply be treated as focusing in both planes.","instruction":"畫水平與垂直兩個束流剖面，標同一概念四極在一平面聚焦、另一平面散焦。","instructionEn":"Draw horizontal and vertical beam views, marking conceptual focusing in one plane and defocusing in the other.","observation":"只看一個投影可能誤以為束流已全面收斂。","observationEn":"A single projection can misleadingly suggest convergence in every direction.","failure":"用一個「聚焦」箭頭概括兩平面，會漏掉耦合的設計需求。","failureEn":"One generic focusing arrow hides the need to consider both planes.","check":"成對保存兩平面圖，說明整體磁鐵配置需系統設計。","checkEn":"Keep both plane views and explain that the overall magnet arrangement needs system design.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"四極磁鐵在一個橫向平面聚焦、在另一平面散焦。","textEn":"A quadrupole focuses in one transverse plane and defocuses in the other."},{"id":"d401-v6-05-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不計算機器光學設定或提供磁鐵電流。","textEn":"The lesson does not calculate machine-optics settings or provide magnet currents."}],"quiz":{"question":"只檢查水平束寬的主要缺陷是什麼？","questionEn":"What is the main limitation of checking only horizontal beam width?","options":["無法知道圖紙顏色","可能漏掉垂直平面的散焦","可自動證明兩方向都已最佳化"],"optionsEn":["It does not reveal paper colour","It can miss defocusing in the vertical plane","It automatically proves both directions are optimized"],"answer":1,"explanation":"四極磁鐵在一個橫向平面聚焦、在另一平面散焦。 本課不計算機器光學設定或提供磁鐵電流。","explanationEn":"A quadrupole focuses in one transverse plane and defocuses in the other. The lesson does not calculate machine-optics settings or provide magnet currents."}},{"id":"d401-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-05"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc-rf"],"title":"用相位圖辨識射頻能量轉移","titleEn":"Identify RF energy transfer with a phase diagram","objective":"理解到達時刻與振盪電場方向的關係。","objectiveEn":"Relate arrival time to the direction of an oscillating electric field.","instruction":"畫正弦概念波與三個到達時刻標記，分辨場方向相同、反向及接近零的區段。","instructionEn":"Draw a conceptual sine wave and three arrival markers, distinguishing same-direction, opposite-direction and near-zero field regions.","observation":"相同位置但不同時刻到達，可能得到不同的能量改變。","observationEn":"Arrival at the same location at different times can produce different energy changes.","failure":"只記共振腔存在就假定所有粒子等量增能，會忽略相位。","failureEn":"Assuming equal energy gain merely because a cavity exists ignores phase.","check":"每個到達點都有時間或相位標籤，結論限於概念方向。","checkEn":"Give each arrival point a time or phase label and limit conclusions to conceptual direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"射頻加速取決於粒子通過時的電場相位。","textEn":"RF acceleration depends on electric-field phase when particles pass."},{"id":"d401-v6-06-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"波形不代表 LHC 頻率、相位設定或啟動程序。","textEn":"The waveform does not represent LHC frequency, phase settings or startup procedures."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何相同共振腔可能產生不同能量改變？","questionEn":"Why can the same cavity produce different energy changes?","options":["只因共振腔名字不同","相位與能量轉移完全無關","粒子到達時的電場相位不同"],"optionsEn":["Only because the cavity names differ","Phase has no relation to energy transfer","Particles encounter different electric-field phases"],"answer":2,"explanation":"射頻加速取決於粒子通過時的電場相位。 波形不代表 LHC 頻率、相位設定或啟動程序。","explanationEn":"RF acceleration depends on electric-field phase when particles pass. The waveform does not represent LHC frequency, phase settings or startup procedures."}},{"id":"d401-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-06"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc","v6-science-lhc-magnets"],"title":"畫出低溫系統的熱路徑","titleEn":"Map heat paths in the cryogenic system","objective":"理解超導設備與環境熱負荷的介面。","objectiveEn":"Understand interfaces between superconducting equipment and environmental heat loads.","instruction":"畫冷端、外殼、支承與電流引入概念方塊，標出可能傳熱路徑及冷卻移除箭頭。","instructionEn":"Draw cold mass, enclosure, support and current-entry blocks, marking possible heat paths and heat-removal arrows.","observation":"機械連接與電氣連接同時可能形成熱路徑。","observationEn":"Mechanical and electrical connections can also form thermal paths.","failure":"只畫冷卻機而不畫熱流入，會讓能量帳看似沒有負荷。","failureEn":"Drawing cooling alone without heat ingress makes the energy account appear load-free.","check":"每條熱流有方向與來源，未知大小不自行填成實測值。","checkEn":"Give every heat flow a direction and origin; do not label unknown magnitudes as measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"低溫工程需管理外部熱流入與內部負荷。","textEn":"Cryogenic engineering must manage external heat ingress and internal loads."},{"id":"d401-v6-07-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本步不教低溫流體操作、壓力調整或真實超導磁鐵通電。","textEn":"This task does not teach cryogen handling, pressure adjustment or real superconducting-magnet energization."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個項目應納入低溫概念帳？","questionEn":"Which item belongs in the cryogenic concept account?","options":["支承及電氣介面的熱流入","只有設備名稱","假定所有連接都完全絕熱"],"optionsEn":["Heat ingress through supports and electrical interfaces","Equipment names alone","Assume every connection is perfectly insulating"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低溫工程需管理外部熱流入與內部負荷。 本步不教低溫流體操作、壓力調整或真實超導磁鐵通電。","explanationEn":"Cryogenic engineering must manage external heat ingress and internal loads. This task does not teach cryogen handling, pressure adjustment or real superconducting-magnet energization."}},{"id":"d401-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-07"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc"],"title":"辨識束管真空的系統角色","titleEn":"Identify the system role of beam-pipe vacuum","objective":"將束流環境與機械連接的要求分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate beam-environment requirements from mechanical connections.","instruction":"在概念束管圖標接頭、量測與抽氣介面；用虛構「資料缺漏」標記說明不能據此判定就緒。","instructionEn":"Mark joints, measurement and pumping interfaces on a concept beam pipe; use a fictional missing-data flag to explain why readiness is unknown.","observation":"機械上連通不等於真空狀態已被確認。","observationEn":"Mechanical continuity does not establish a verified vacuum condition.","failure":"看到圖上管道封閉就宣稱真空合格，會把外觀當量測。","failureEn":"Declaring acceptable vacuum from a closed pipe drawing mistakes appearance for measurement.","check":"區分圖示連接、量測證據與正式授權三種不同欄位。","checkEn":"Separate drawn connectivity, measurement evidence and formal authorization into distinct fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"真空環境減少束流與殘餘氣體的相互作用。","textEn":"A vacuum environment reduces interactions between the beam and residual gas."},{"id":"d401-v6-08-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"本課不提供真空門檻、閥件操作或現場排故程序。","textEn":"This lesson provides no vacuum thresholds, valve operations or onsite troubleshooting procedures."}],"quiz":{"question":"封閉束管的示意圖能證明什麼？","questionEn":"What does a closed beam-pipe sketch establish?","options":["所有量測都已通過","概念連接關係，不能證明實際真空品質","可以省略真空監測"],"optionsEn":["All measurements have passed","Conceptual connectivity, not actual vacuum quality","Vacuum monitoring can be omitted"],"answer":1,"explanation":"真空環境減少束流與殘餘氣體的相互作用。 本課不提供真空門檻、閥件操作或現場排故程序。","explanationEn":"A vacuum environment reduces interactions between the beam and residual gas. This lesson provides no vacuum thresholds, valve operations or onsite troubleshooting procedures."}}]},{"id":"d401-stage03","order":3,"title":"狀態證據與科研資料","titleEn":"State evidence and research data","description":"保留未知、版本及選取規則，完成概念交接。","descriptionEn":"Preserve unknowns, versions and selection rules for conceptual handover.","route":"依學習相依關係閱讀；這四步是公開原理的概念任務，不是現場施工、操作或量產程序。","routeEn":"Follow the learning dependencies. These four tasks explore public principles; they are not field, operating or production procedures.","steps":[{"id":"d401-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-08"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc","v6-science-lhc-magnets"],"title":"把未知狀態保留為未就緒","titleEn":"Keep unknown states as not ready","objective":"區分量測、狀態確認與操作許可。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish measurements, state verification and operating authorization.","instruction":"用紙上表格列真空、低溫、磁鐵與 RF 四列；其中一列資料缺漏，將整體標為待查證。","instructionEn":"Make a paper table for vacuum, cryogenics, magnets and RF; leave one row missing data and mark the overall result unverified.","observation":"其他列正常不能補足缺漏系統的證據。","observationEn":"Normal entries elsewhere cannot substitute for evidence from the missing subsystem.","failure":"把未知狀態當通過會破壞保護與就緒判斷。","failureEn":"Treating unknown as passed undermines protection and readiness assessment.","check":"缺漏欄保留未知，列所需證據與負責角色，不給任何解除或繞過方法。","checkEn":"Preserve unknowns and list required evidence and responsible roles, without release or bypass methods.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"系統就緒需要適用且完整的狀態證據。","textEn":"System readiness requires applicable and complete state evidence."},{"id":"d401-v6-09-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"這是紙上證據分類；真正保護與操作許可由正式系統與授權人員管理。","textEn":"This is paper evidence classification; real protection and authorization remain with formal systems and authorized staff."}],"quiz":{"question":"一個必要欄位資料缺漏時應如何標示？","questionEn":"How should a required field with missing data be marked?","options":["因其他欄正常所以通過","直接停用該檢查","未知／待查證，不視為通過"],"optionsEn":["Passed because other fields look normal","Disable the check","Unknown/unverified, not passed"],"answer":2,"explanation":"系統就緒需要適用且完整的狀態證據。 這是紙上證據分類；真正保護與操作許可由正式系統與授權人員管理。","explanationEn":"System readiness requires applicable and complete state evidence. This is paper evidence classification; real protection and authorization remain with formal systems and authorized staff."}},{"id":"d401-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-09"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc"],"title":"連接探測器訊號與校正版本","titleEn":"Link detector signals to calibration versions","objective":"使數據可追溯至儀器條件與處理方法。","objectiveEn":"Make data traceable to instrument conditions and processing methods.","instruction":"建立虛構事件卡，包含事件編號、時間標記、探測器子系統、校正版本與原始／處理標籤。","instructionEn":"Create a fictional event card with event ID, timestamp, detector subsystem, calibration version and raw/processed label.","observation":"同一原始訊號經不同校正可能產生不同表示。","observationEn":"Different calibrations can produce different representations of the same raw signal.","failure":"只保存漂亮圖像不保留版本，會阻礙重現與比較。","failureEn":"Keeping only attractive images without versions prevents reproduction and comparison.","check":"每張卡能連回輸入與處理版本，示例不冒充實驗公開事件。","checkEn":"Every card traces back to input and processing version; examples must not masquerade as published experimental events.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"探測器把相互作用轉為電氣或其他可處理訊號，解讀需量測脈絡。","textEn":"Detectors convert interactions into electrical or other processable signals whose interpretation needs measurement context."},{"id":"d401-v6-10-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"這是資料管理概念，沒有提供 LHC 原始事件資料或物理發現證據。","textEn":"This is a data-management concept, not supplied raw LHC event data or evidence of a physics discovery."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個欄位最有助重現處理結果？","questionEn":"Which field most directly supports reproducing processing results?","options":["校正與處理版本","只記圖片檔名長度","只記展示頁面的背景色"],"optionsEn":["Calibration and processing versions","Image filename length only","Display-page background colour only"],"answer":0,"explanation":"探測器把相互作用轉為電氣或其他可處理訊號，解讀需量測脈絡。 這是資料管理概念，沒有提供 LHC 原始事件資料或物理發現證據。","explanationEn":"Detectors convert interactions into electrical or other processable signals whose interpretation needs measurement context. This is a data-management concept, not supplied raw LHC event data or evidence of a physics discovery."}},{"id":"d401-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-10"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc"],"title":"分開事件選取與物理結論","titleEn":"Separate event selection from physics conclusions","objective":"避免把可見事件或自設樣本當成發現。","objectiveEn":"Avoid treating visible events or invented samples as discoveries.","instruction":"對十張自行編號的事件卡設定公開的教學選取規則；保留選中與未選中的數量及理由。","instructionEn":"Set an explicit teaching selection rule for ten self-numbered event cards; retain selected and rejected counts and reasons.","observation":"選取規則會改變所看到的樣本，必須揭露。","observationEn":"Selection rules change the observed sample and must be disclosed.","failure":"只展示符合預期的卡片而隱藏規則，會造成選擇偏差。","failureEn":"Showing only expected cards while hiding rules creates selection bias.","check":"列完整起始數、選取條件與剩餘數，聲明不推論新粒子。","checkEn":"Record starting count, selection conditions and remaining count, stating that no new particle is inferred.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"科學結論需要可檢驗方法與充分證據，不能由單一示意事件直接推出。","textEn":"Scientific conclusions require testable methods and sufficient evidence, not a single illustrative event."},{"id":"d401-v6-11-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"教學卡只用來練習透明篩選，沒有實際碰撞量測。","textEn":"Teaching cards practice transparent selection and contain no actual collision measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪個作法可降低選取偏差的隱藏風險？","questionEn":"Which practice reduces hidden selection bias?","options":["只展示最符合期待的一張","公開起始樣本與選取規則","選完後改規則但不記錄"],"optionsEn":["Show only the single most expected card","Disclose the starting sample and selection rules","Change rules afterward without documenting them"],"answer":1,"explanation":"科學結論需要可檢驗方法與充分證據，不能由單一示意事件直接推出。 教學卡只用來練習透明篩選，沒有實際碰撞量測。","explanationEn":"Scientific conclusions require testable methods and sufficient evidence, not a single illustrative event. Teaching cards practice transparent selection and contain no actual collision measurements."}},{"id":"d401-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d401-v6-11"],"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-science-lhc","v6-science-lhc-magnets","v6-science-lhc-rf"],"title":"完成大型科研系統概念審查","titleEn":"Complete a conceptual review of a large research system","objective":"把束流、支援系統與數據證據整合交接。","objectiveEn":"Integrate beam, support-system and data evidence into a handover.","instruction":"提交責任圖、磁鐵與 RF 概念圖、熱／真空介面表、未就緒清單及事件版本表。","instructionEn":"Submit the responsibility map, magnet and RF concept diagrams, thermal/vacuum interface table, unready-state list and event-version table.","observation":"大型科學設施的可靠性依賴跨系統一致的證據與責任。","observationEn":"Reliability in a large research facility depends on consistent evidence and responsibilities across systems.","failure":"只展示壯觀設備而省略未知與版本，會讓整合無法審查。","failureEn":"Showing impressive equipment while omitting unknowns and versions makes integration unreviewable.","check":"由另一位學徒選一條介面追查來源、假設與責任，保留所有未知項。","checkEn":"Have another learner trace one interface to its sources, assumptions and owner, retaining every unknown.","knowledge":[{"id":"d401-v6-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"系統整合需要功能、介面、證據與授權的清楚區分。","textEn":"System integration needs clear distinctions among functions, interfaces, evidence and authorization."},{"id":"d401-v6-12-k2","title":"驗證與適用界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"完成課程不構成粒子加速器設計審查、操作培訓或任何保護系統變更許可。","textEn":"Course completion is not accelerator design approval, operational training or permission to modify protection systems."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪份審查結果最符合本課程？","questionEn":"Which review outcome fits this course?","options":["已獲准實際啟動束流","可以移除任何未通過的保護要求","能說明公共原理與未驗證介面，未聲稱操作授權"],"optionsEn":["It grants permission to start a real beam","It permits removal of unmet protection requirements","It explains public principles and unverified interfaces without claiming operational authorization"],"answer":2,"explanation":"系統整合需要功能、介面、證據與授權的清楚區分。 完成課程不構成粒子加速器設計審查、操作培訓或任何保護系統變更許可。","explanationEn":"System integration needs clear distinctions among functions, interfaces, evidence and authorization. Course completion is not accelerator design approval, operational training or permission to modify protection systems."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":6,"stepCount":12,"estimatedMinutes":240},{"id":"b015","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"title":"舊金山金門大橋","titleEn":"Golden Gate Bridge","summary":"從海峽選址、懸索受力到橋面更換與耐震改造，用 24 道概念模型練習理解一座仍在使用的大跨橋梁。","summaryEn":"Use 24 conceptual exercises to connect strait constraints and suspension forces with deck replacement and seismic rehabilitation of a working long-span bridge.","scope":"以公開一次資料為背景的原創工程判讀課程；每步在紙上或數位示意模型中完成。自設數值、構形與工序不得當成原工程的設計、施工、設備操作或驗收程序。","scopeEn":"Original engineering interpretation exercises grounded in public primary sources. Complete each step on paper or in a schematic digital model. Invented values, geometry and sequences are not the original project’s design, construction, operating or acceptance procedures.","diagram":{"type":"suspension","labels":["需求與場址","結構與介面","施工狀態","驗證與維護"],"labelsEn":["Requirements and site","Structures and interfaces","Construction states","Verification and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":64,"estimatedMinutes":1600,"stages":[{"id":"b015-stage01","order":1,"title":"場址、邊界與受力","titleEn":"Site, boundaries and force paths","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「場址、邊界與受力」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on site, boundaries and force paths, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v7-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把海峽需求放進場址圖","titleEn":"Map the strait requirements","objective":"辨認航道、岸線與跨越位置的共同限制。","objectiveEn":"Identify joint constraints from navigation, shorelines and crossing location.","instruction":"1. 自繪兩岸與航道；2. 分別標示塔位及錨碇區；3. 列出水深、地盤與航道資料缺口。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch shores and navigation corridor; 2. mark tower and anchorage zones separately; 3. list missing depth, ground and navigation evidence.","observation":"跨距相近的方案仍可能有不同的基礎及航運限制。","observationEn":"Similar spans may still imply different foundation and navigation constraints.","failure":"僅以最短跨距判定塔位可行。","failureEn":"Choose tower locations from the shortest span alone.","check":"提交有圖例的場址圖及三個待查資料欄。","checkEn":"Submit a keyed site map and three evidence gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-01-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"選址同時改變側跨比例、施工可達性及支承條件，不能只比跨距。","textEn":"Siting changes side-span proportions, access and support conditions, so span alone is insufficient."},{"id":"b015-v7-01-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"地圖座標只定位工程背景；地質與海事邊界需要專門調查。","textEn":"A map pin locates project context; ground and marine boundaries require dedicated investigation."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把海峽需求放進場址圖」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map the strait requirements”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["跨距相近的方案仍可能有不同的基礎及航運限制。","僅以最短跨距判定塔位可行。","塔位只影響外觀，不會改變側跨與反力。"],"optionsEn":["Similar spans may still imply different foundation and navigation constraints.","Choose tower locations from the shortest span alone.","Tower locations affect appearance only, not side spans or reactions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選址同時改變側跨比例、施工可達性及支承條件，不能只比跨距。 地圖座標只定位工程背景；地質與海事邊界需要專門調查。","explanationEn":"Siting changes side-span proportions, access and support conditions, so span alone is insufficient. A map pin locates project context; ground and marine boundaries require dedicated investigation."}},{"id":"b015-v7-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-01"],"title":"區分全橋與主跨尺寸","titleEn":"Separate overall and main-span dimensions","objective":"避免把不同統計邊界混成同一個橋長。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating different definitions of bridge length.","instruction":"1. 畫全橋、懸吊區、主跨三條尺寸線；2. 依官方表標記各自端點；3. 記錄單位與是否包含引橋。","instructionEn":"1. Draw overall, suspended and main-span dimension lines; 2. mark their endpoints from the official table; 3. record units and whether approaches are included.","observation":"尺寸比較只有在端點與單位一致時才成立。","observationEn":"Dimensions are comparable only when endpoints and units agree.","failure":"把包含引橋的長度當成兩塔之間的距離。","failureEn":"Treat a length including approaches as the distance between towers.","check":"繳交三條尺寸線和各自的邊界定義。","checkEn":"Provide three dimension lines with their boundary definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-02-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"主跨是兩座主塔間的跨度；全橋長度可包含側跨及引橋。","textEn":"The main span lies between the main towers; overall length can include side spans and approaches."},{"id":"b015-v7-02-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"統計資料的精確位數不能修正錯誤的量測邊界。","textEn":"Numerical precision cannot correct an incorrectly defined measurement boundary."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分全橋與主跨尺寸」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate overall and main-span dimensions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把包含引橋的長度當成兩塔之間的距離。","尺寸比較只有在端點與單位一致時才成立。","單位一致時便可以忽略兩個尺寸的起訖位置。"],"optionsEn":["Treat a length including approaches as the distance between towers.","Dimensions are comparable only when endpoints and units agree.","Matching units make dimension endpoints irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"主跨是兩座主塔間的跨度；全橋長度可包含側跨及引橋。 統計資料的精確位數不能修正錯誤的量測邊界。","explanationEn":"The main span lies between the main towers; overall length can include side spans and approaches. Numerical precision cannot correct an incorrectly defined measurement boundary."}},{"id":"b015-v7-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-02"],"title":"追蹤橋面重力至地盤","titleEn":"Trace deck gravity to the ground","objective":"區分吊索、主纜、塔與錨碇的作用。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish the roles of hangers, main cables, towers and anchorages.","instruction":"1. 在橋面放一個假想載荷；2. 畫到吊索及主纜的傳力箭頭；3. 分別追到塔基與端部錨碇反力。","instructionEn":"1. Place a hypothetical deck load; 2. trace force arrows through hangers and main cables; 3. close the paths through tower foundations and end anchorages.","observation":"完整力路徑必須包含主纜端部的水平反力。","observationEn":"A complete force path includes horizontal reactions at the main-cable ends.","failure":"只畫塔的壓力就認為所有纜索拉力已平衡。","failureEn":"Assume tower compression alone balances every cable force.","check":"提交一張閉合到地盤的受力圖。","checkEn":"Submit a force diagram closed through the ground.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-03-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"柔性纜索主要承受拉力，塔與錨碇分擔不同方向的支承反力。","textEn":"Flexible cables act mainly in tension; towers and anchorages provide different support reactions."},{"id":"b015-v7-03-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"受力箭頭與位移箭頭應分色，否則容易把作用與反應混淆。","textEn":"Use separate symbols for forces and movements to avoid confusing actions with responses."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「追蹤橋面重力至地盤」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Trace deck gravity to the ground”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只畫塔的壓力就認為所有纜索拉力已平衡。","端部錨碇只供裝飾，主纜不會把力傳到它。","完整力路徑必須包含主纜端部的水平反力。"],"optionsEn":["Assume tower compression alone balances every cable force.","End anchorages are decorative and receive no cable force.","A complete force path includes horizontal reactions at the main-cable ends."],"answer":2,"explanation":"柔性纜索主要承受拉力，塔與錨碇分擔不同方向的支承反力。 受力箭頭與位移箭頭應分色，否則容易把作用與反應混淆。","explanationEn":"Flexible cables act mainly in tension; towers and anchorages provide different support reactions. Use separate symbols for forces and movements to avoid confusing actions with responses."}},{"id":"b015-v7-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-03"],"title":"比較橋型與反力邊界","titleEn":"Compare bridge forms and reactions","objective":"看出懸索、斜張與拱橋的力學差別。","objectiveEn":"Recognize mechanical differences between suspension, cable-stayed and arch bridges.","instruction":"1. 自繪三種橋型；2. 標出主要拉力或壓力構件；3. 保持相同跨越需求，列出各型式需要的支承證據。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch three bridge forms; 2. label principal tension or compression members; 3. keep the crossing requirement fixed and list support evidence for each.","observation":"外形相似的跨越構造不一定具有相同反力方向。","observationEn":"Similar crossing silhouettes need not produce the same reaction directions.","failure":"把斜張索當成懸索橋主纜下的垂直吊索。","failureEn":"Treat cable stays as vertical hangers below a suspension main cable.","check":"提交橋型、力型與地盤需求的三欄比較表。","checkEn":"Submit a table of bridge form, force type and ground requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-04-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"懸索經主纜與吊索承托橋面；斜張索則直接連接橋塔與橋面。","textEn":"Suspension decks hang from main cables through hangers; stays directly connect a tower and deck."},{"id":"b015-v7-04-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"倒置纜索曲線可幫助理解拱的壓力，但不能取代拱橋穩定分析。","textEn":"An inverted cable curve illustrates arch compression but does not replace arch stability analysis."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較橋型與反力邊界」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare bridge forms and reactions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["外形相似的跨越構造不一定具有相同反力方向。","把斜張索當成懸索橋主纜下的垂直吊索。","拱橋與懸索橋的主要承重構件都只承受拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Similar crossing silhouettes need not produce the same reaction directions.","Treat cable stays as vertical hangers below a suspension main cable.","The principal members of arches and suspension bridges both carry tension only."],"answer":0,"explanation":"懸索經主纜與吊索承托橋面；斜張索則直接連接橋塔與橋面。 倒置纜索曲線可幫助理解拱的壓力，但不能取代拱橋穩定分析。","explanationEn":"Suspension decks hang from main cables through hangers; stays directly connect a tower and deck. An inverted cable curve illustrates arch compression but does not replace arch stability analysis."}},{"id":"b015-v7-05","sequence":5,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-04"],"title":"建立溫度與車流情境","titleEn":"Define temperature and traffic cases","objective":"把不同荷載組合當成不同模型狀態。","objectiveEn":"Treat different load combinations as distinct model states.","instruction":"1. 定義無量綱的冷、暖兩情境；2. 分配主跨或側跨假想車流；3. 先預測再比較橋面位移方向。","instructionEn":"1. Define dimensionless cool and warm cases; 2. distribute hypothetical traffic on main or side spans; 3. predict then compare deck-movement directions.","observation":"橋面位移同時受纜長變化與載荷分布影響。","observationEn":"Deck movement depends on cable-length changes and load distribution together.","failure":"只看車輛總數就斷言主跨一定向下同樣多。","failureEn":"Use vehicle count alone to assert identical downward main-span movement.","check":"繳交至少四個有邊界條件的情境卡。","checkEn":"Provide at least four scenario cards with boundary conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-05-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"加熱造成的纜索伸長會改變懸吊幾何；活載位置也改變力的平衡。","textEn":"Thermal cable expansion changes suspension geometry, while live-load position changes equilibrium."},{"id":"b015-v7-05-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"簡化模型的位移方向可作概念比較，不能作真橋變形限值。","textEn":"A simplified model can compare movement directions, not set real-bridge deformation limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立溫度與車流情境」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Define temperature and traffic cases”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只看車輛總數就斷言主跨一定向下同樣多。","橋面位移同時受纜長變化與載荷分布影響。","主纜溫度改變不可能影響橋面位置。"],"optionsEn":["Use vehicle count alone to assert identical downward main-span movement.","Deck movement depends on cable-length changes and load distribution together.","Cable-temperature changes cannot affect deck position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加熱造成的纜索伸長會改變懸吊幾何；活載位置也改變力的平衡。 簡化模型的位移方向可作概念比較，不能作真橋變形限值。","explanationEn":"Thermal cable expansion changes suspension geometry, while live-load position changes equilibrium. A simplified model can compare movement directions, not set real-bridge deformation limits."}},{"id":"b015-v7-06","sequence":6,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-05"],"title":"做場址階段設計審查","titleEn":"Review the site-stage model","objective":"整合第一階段的尺寸、反力與不確定性。","objectiveEn":"Integrate dimensions, reactions and uncertainties from the first stage.","instruction":"1. 將場址圖與受力圖並排；2. 逐一核對尺寸端點和反力落點；3. 指定一個必須補資料才能決定的選項。","instructionEn":"1. Compare site and force diagrams; 2. audit dimension endpoints and reaction locations; 3. identify one choice that requires further evidence.","observation":"未知地盤條件應保留為待查項，而非被漂亮圖面掩蓋。","observationEn":"Unknown ground conditions should remain unresolved rather than disappear behind a polished drawing.","failure":"把所有未確認欄位填成與另一座橋相同。","failureEn":"Fill every unverified field with values borrowed from another bridge.","check":"輸出含假設、證據、待查項的三欄審查單。","checkEn":"Produce a review sheet separating assumptions, evidence and open items.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-06-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"設計審查要檢查介面是否一致，不只檢查單一構件有無畫出。","textEn":"Design review checks interface consistency, not merely whether every component is drawn."},{"id":"b015-v7-06-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"可追溯的未知項比沒有來源的確定數字更有助於後續決策。","textEn":"Traceable unknowns support later decisions better than unsupported precise numbers."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「做場址階段設計審查」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review the site-stage model”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把所有未確認欄位填成與另一座橋相同。","圖畫越精細，未知地盤條件就越少。","未知地盤條件應保留為待查項，而非被漂亮圖面掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Fill every unverified field with values borrowed from another bridge.","More detailed drawing automatically reduces unknown ground conditions.","Unknown ground conditions should remain unresolved rather than disappear behind a polished drawing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設計審查要檢查介面是否一致，不只檢查單一構件有無畫出。 可追溯的未知項比沒有來源的確定數字更有助於後續決策。","explanationEn":"Design review checks interface consistency, not merely whether every component is drawn. Traceable unknowns support later decisions better than unsupported precise numbers."}}]},{"id":"b015-stage02","order":2,"title":"基礎、橋塔與主纜","titleEn":"Foundations, towers and main cables","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「基礎、橋塔與主纜」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on foundations, towers and main cables, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v7-07","sequence":7,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-06"],"title":"分開海床與塔基變形","titleEn":"Separate seabed and foundation movements","objective":"辨認基礎平移、轉動和橋塔彎曲。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish foundation translation, rotation and tower bending.","instruction":"1. 畫海床、基礎與橋塔三層；2. 分別施加假想平移與轉角；3. 比較相同塔頂位移可能對應的不同原因。","instructionEn":"1. Draw seabed, foundation and tower layers; 2. apply hypothetical translations and rotations separately; 3. compare different causes of the same tower-top displacement.","observation":"單一塔頂位移不能唯一識別基礎或塔身的變化。","observationEn":"One tower-top reading cannot uniquely identify foundation or tower changes.","failure":"塔頂偏移便直接證明海床承載失效。","failureEn":"A shifted tower top directly proves seabed bearing failure.","check":"提交兩種具有相同塔頂位移的概念反例。","checkEn":"Submit two conceptual cases with the same tower-top displacement.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-07-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"剛體轉動與構件彎曲在局部量測上可能相似，需多點觀測分辨。","textEn":"Rigid rotation and member bending may appear similar locally; multiple observations help distinguish them."},{"id":"b015-v7-07-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"把測点放在不同高度及基礎附近，可增加辨識不同變形模式的資訊。","textEn":"Observations at different heights and near foundations improve discrimination between movement modes."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開海床與塔基變形」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate seabed and foundation movements”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["單一塔頂位移不能唯一識別基礎或塔身的變化。","塔頂偏移便直接證明海床承載失效。","剛體轉動與塔身彎曲在任何測點都能用單一讀數區分。"],"optionsEn":["One tower-top reading cannot uniquely identify foundation or tower changes.","A shifted tower top directly proves seabed bearing failure.","One reading anywhere always separates rigid rotation from tower bending."],"answer":0,"explanation":"剛體轉動與構件彎曲在局部量測上可能相似，需多點觀測分辨。 把測点放在不同高度及基礎附近，可增加辨識不同變形模式的資訊。","explanationEn":"Rigid rotation and member bending may appear similar locally; multiple observations help distinguish them. Observations at different heights and near foundations improve discrimination between movement modes."}},{"id":"b015-v7-08","sequence":8,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-07"],"title":"拆解塔座的介面資料","titleEn":"Separate tower-base interface records","objective":"連接地質、混凝土與鋼構三種證據。","objectiveEn":"Connect ground, concrete and steel-interface evidence.","instruction":"1. 畫地盤至塔腳的剖面；2. 在每個交界列出幾何與材料紀錄；3. 將缺失資料標成不能放行的模型介面。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a section from ground to tower foot; 2. list geometry and material records at each interface; 3. flag missing records as unresolved model interfaces.","observation":"上下構件各自合格仍不保證接觸介面吻合。","observationEn":"Individually acceptable components do not guarantee a compatible interface.","failure":"上下材料強度足夠便可忽略幾何及接觸條件。","failureEn":"Adequate material strengths make geometry and contact conditions irrelevant.","check":"繳交三層介面表，至少列出一項幾何衝突。","checkEn":"Provide a three-layer interface table with at least one geometric conflict.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-08-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"介面會傳遞力、約束位移並影響施工定位，因此必須獨立檢查。","textEn":"Interfaces transmit forces, constrain movement and affect positioning, so they require explicit review."},{"id":"b015-v7-08-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"示意圖中的完美貼合是假設，不是現場接觸品質的證據。","textEn":"Perfect contact in a schematic is an assumption, not evidence of field contact quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆解塔座的介面資料」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate tower-base interface records”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["上下材料強度足夠便可忽略幾何及接觸條件。","上下構件各自合格仍不保證接觸介面吻合。","材料來源相同就表示上下構件的幾何一定吻合。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate material strengths make geometry and contact conditions irrelevant.","Individually acceptable components do not guarantee a compatible interface.","A shared material supplier guarantees matching component geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"介面會傳遞力、約束位移並影響施工定位，因此必須獨立檢查。 示意圖中的完美貼合是假設，不是現場接觸品質的證據。","explanationEn":"Interfaces transmit forces, constrain movement and affect positioning, so they require explicit review. Perfect contact in a schematic is an assumption, not evidence of field contact quality."}},{"id":"b015-v7-09","sequence":9,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-08"],"title":"辨認橋塔節間與側向支撐","titleEn":"Identify tower panels and lateral bracing","objective":"理解細長塔腿如何形成整體側向系統。","objectiveEn":"Understand how slender tower legs form a lateral system.","instruction":"1. 畫兩條塔腿及連接節間；2. 用不同顏色標出縱向與橫向變形；3. 比較移除一組概念支撐前後的變形趨勢。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two tower legs and connecting panels; 2. distinguish longitudinal and transverse deformation; 3. compare trends before and after removing a conceptual brace.","observation":"同樣塔高的模型可因支撐配置不同而有不同側向剛度。","observationEn":"Equal-height models can have different lateral stiffness because of bracing layout.","failure":"塔高相同就保證風中位移相同。","failureEn":"Identical tower height guarantees identical wind displacement.","check":"提交兩種配置的變形草圖及固定邊界。","checkEn":"Submit deformation sketches and support assumptions for two layouts.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-09-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"細長結構的穩定性取決於約束與構件共同作用，不能只比較截面面積。","textEn":"Slender-structure stability depends on restraints and member interaction, not cross-sectional area alone."},{"id":"b015-v7-09-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"移除支撐的數位試驗只用於概念辨識，不對應實橋可容許損傷。","textEn":"Digital brace-removal exercises explain mechanisms, not permissible damage to the actual bridge."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認橋塔節間與側向支撐」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Identify tower panels and lateral bracing”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["塔高相同就保證風中位移相同。","塔腿的連接配置不會改變整體變形。","同樣塔高的模型可因支撐配置不同而有不同側向剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Identical tower height guarantees identical wind displacement.","Connections between tower legs cannot affect overall deformation.","Equal-height models can have different lateral stiffness because of bracing layout."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細長結構的穩定性取決於約束與構件共同作用，不能只比較截面面積。 移除支撐的數位試驗只用於概念辨識，不對應實橋可容許損傷。","explanationEn":"Slender-structure stability depends on restraints and member interaction, not cross-sectional area alone. Digital brace-removal exercises explain mechanisms, not permissible damage to the actual bridge."}},{"id":"b015-v7-10","sequence":10,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-09"],"title":"把單絲、索股與主纜分層","titleEn":"Separate wire, strand and main cable","objective":"辨認多尺度的纜索品質紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Recognize cable-quality records at multiple scales.","instruction":"1. 畫單絲、索股、主纜三級樹；2. 把材料試驗、集束幾何與外包保護分配到各級；3. 保留批次追溯連結。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a wire–strand–cable tree; 2. assign material tests, bundle geometry and wrapping to the appropriate levels; 3. retain batch-traceability links.","observation":"單絲試驗只描述局部材料，不直接證明整條主纜狀態。","observationEn":"A wire test characterizes local material, not the condition of an entire main cable.","failure":"抽到一根合格單絲即可認定所有索股與接合均正常。","failureEn":"One acceptable wire establishes that all strands and connections are sound.","check":"繳交三級追溯樹及每級一種證據。","checkEn":"Provide a three-level traceability tree with one evidence type per level.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-10-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"主纜由多根鋼絲組成，局部材料、幾何分布與防護狀態影響不同問題。","textEn":"Main cables comprise many wires; local material, geometric distribution and protection address different questions."},{"id":"b015-v7-10-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"抽樣結果必須連同抽樣位置及代表範圍解讀。","textEn":"Sampling results must be interpreted with their locations and representativeness."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把單絲、索股與主纜分層」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate wire, strand and main cable”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["單絲試驗只描述局部材料，不直接證明整條主纜狀態。","抽到一根合格單絲即可認定所有索股與接合均正常。","主纜外包保護的檢查可以直接取代鋼絲材料追溯。"],"optionsEn":["A wire test characterizes local material, not the condition of an entire main cable.","One acceptable wire establishes that all strands and connections are sound.","Cable-wrap inspection directly replaces wire-material traceability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主纜由多根鋼絲組成，局部材料、幾何分布與防護狀態影響不同問題。 抽樣結果必須連同抽樣位置及代表範圍解讀。","explanationEn":"Main cables comprise many wires; local material, geometric distribution and protection address different questions. Sampling results must be interpreted with their locations and representativeness."}},{"id":"b015-v7-11","sequence":11,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-10"],"title":"讀懂索鞍與主纜轉向","titleEn":"Interpret cable saddles and redirection","objective":"把主纜的拉力方向與橋塔反力連起來。","objectiveEn":"Connect main-cable tension directions with tower reactions.","instruction":"1. 畫主纜通過塔頂的兩側切線；2. 合成一組自設向量；3. 在索鞍與塔上標記相反作用力。","instructionEn":"1. Draw cable tangents on both sides of a tower; 2. combine a hypothetical vector pair; 3. mark opposite forces on saddle and tower.","observation":"塔頂反力來自兩側纜索拉力的向量合成。","observationEn":"Tower-top reaction follows the vector combination of cable tensions on both sides.","failure":"兩側纜索張力相等就表示塔頂沒有任何受力。","failureEn":"Equal tensions on both sides imply zero force on the tower top.","check":"輸出有方向、比例假設與反力的向量圖。","checkEn":"Provide a vector diagram with directions, scale assumptions and reaction.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-11-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"相同大小的斜向力仍可能形成明顯合力，方向比數字相等更重要。","textEn":"Equal-magnitude inclined forces can produce a substantial resultant; equal numbers do not erase direction."},{"id":"b015-v7-11-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"索鞍接觸與主纜轉折是局部介面問題，整橋模型通常需另外簡化。","textEn":"Saddle contact and cable redirection are local interface problems simplified separately in whole-bridge models."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「讀懂索鞍與主纜轉向」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret cable saddles and redirection”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["兩側纜索張力相等就表示塔頂沒有任何受力。","塔頂反力來自兩側纜索拉力的向量合成。","兩個拉力的大小可以直接相減而不考慮方向。"],"optionsEn":["Equal tensions on both sides imply zero force on the tower top.","Tower-top reaction follows the vector combination of cable tensions on both sides.","Two tension magnitudes can be subtracted without considering direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同大小的斜向力仍可能形成明顯合力，方向比數字相等更重要。 索鞍接觸與主纜轉折是局部介面問題，整橋模型通常需另外簡化。","explanationEn":"Equal-magnitude inclined forces can produce a substantial resultant; equal numbers do not erase direction. Saddle contact and cable redirection are local interface problems simplified separately in whole-bridge models."}},{"id":"b015-v7-12","sequence":12,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-11"],"title":"標示索夾、吊索與防護分工","titleEn":"Distinguish cable bands, hangers and protection","objective":"理解傳力連接與腐蝕防護不是同一種功能。","objectiveEn":"Understand that load transfer and corrosion protection are different functions.","instruction":"1. 畫主纜、索夾與垂直吊索；2. 標示傳力及排水路徑；3. 將機械連接紀錄與塗覆檢查分成兩份清單。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch main cable, band and vertical hanger; 2. mark force and drainage paths; 3. separate mechanical-connection and coating-inspection records.","observation":"外表塗層完整不能單獨證明連接的機械狀態。","observationEn":"An intact surface coating alone does not establish mechanical connection condition.","failure":"外觀沒有鏽色就可省略索夾及吊索端部檢查。","failureEn":"No visible rust makes cable-band and hanger-end checks unnecessary.","check":"繳交分開力路徑與水路徑的節點圖。","checkEn":"Submit a node sketch separating force and water paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-12-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"局部積水及隙縫環境可能與可見大面積塗層具有不同的腐蝕條件。","textEn":"Trapped water and crevices can create corrosion conditions different from broad exposed coating surfaces."},{"id":"b015-v7-12-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"維護紀錄必須指出檢查範圍，不能把外觀檢查擴大為內部健康保證。","textEn":"Maintenance records must state inspection scope rather than turn surface observations into internal-health guarantees."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「標示索夾、吊索與防護分工」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish cable bands, hangers and protection”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["外觀沒有鏽色就可省略索夾及吊索端部檢查。","排水路徑和傳力路徑完全相同，所以不需分開標記。","外表塗層完整不能單獨證明連接的機械狀態。"],"optionsEn":["No visible rust makes cable-band and hanger-end checks unnecessary.","Drainage and force paths are identical and need no separate labels.","An intact surface coating alone does not establish mechanical connection condition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部積水及隙縫環境可能與可見大面積塗層具有不同的腐蝕條件。 維護紀錄必須指出檢查範圍，不能把外觀檢查擴大為內部健康保證。","explanationEn":"Trapped water and crevices can create corrosion conditions different from broad exposed coating surfaces. Maintenance records must state inspection scope rather than turn surface observations into internal-health guarantees."}}]},{"id":"b015-stage03","order":3,"title":"橋面架設與變形","titleEn":"Deck erection and deformation","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「橋面架設與變形」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on deck erection and deformation, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v7-13","sequence":13,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-12"],"title":"比較架設前後的受力狀態","titleEn":"Compare construction and completed states","objective":"識別未閉合系統中的臨時邊界。","objectiveEn":"Identify temporary boundaries in an incomplete system.","instruction":"1. 畫未掛橋面、部分掛設、完成三狀態；2. 在每張圖列出仍缺少的構件；3. 逐一追查剩餘支承與反力。","instructionEn":"1. Draw bare-cable, partly decked and completed states; 2. list absent components in each; 3. trace the remaining supports and reactions.","observation":"完工橋的力路徑不能直接套到尚未完成的架設狀態。","observationEn":"Completed-bridge force paths cannot simply be applied to incomplete erection states.","failure":"完工結構安全就代表每個中間狀態也必然安全。","failureEn":"A satisfactory completed structure guarantees every intermediate state.","check":"提交三張有缺件與邊界註記的狀態圖。","checkEn":"Submit three state diagrams identifying missing members and boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-13-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"施工階段的剛度、約束及荷載都會變動；臨時系統有自己的分析需求。","textEn":"Construction-stage stiffness, restraints and loads change; temporary systems need their own analysis."},{"id":"b015-v7-13-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程的狀態排序用來檢查依賴關係，不是吊裝作業程序。","textEn":"The educational state sequence checks dependencies and is not a lifting procedure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較架設前後的受力狀態」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare construction and completed states”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["完工橋的力路徑不能直接套到尚未完成的架設狀態。","完工結構安全就代表每個中間狀態也必然安全。","未安裝的構件仍可在施工模型中提供實際剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Completed-bridge force paths cannot simply be applied to incomplete erection states.","A satisfactory completed structure guarantees every intermediate state.","Uninstalled members still provide actual stiffness in construction models."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工階段的剛度、約束及荷載都會變動；臨時系統有自己的分析需求。 課程的狀態排序用來檢查依賴關係，不是吊裝作業程序。","explanationEn":"Construction-stage stiffness, restraints and loads change; temporary systems need their own analysis. The educational state sequence checks dependencies and is not a lifting procedure."}},{"id":"b015-v7-14","sequence":14,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-13"],"title":"追蹤橋面節段幾何累積","titleEn":"Track accumulated deck-segment geometry","objective":"理解局部尺寸誤差與全跨閉合的關係。","objectiveEn":"Relate local dimension errors to whole-span closure.","instruction":"1. 排列六個自設長度節段；2. 分別加入同向及交錯誤差；3. 比較末端閉合偏差並記錄基準。","instructionEn":"1. Arrange six hypothetical deck lengths; 2. add same-direction and alternating errors; 3. compare end closure and record the reference frame.","observation":"相同單節誤差上限可能形成不同的累積閉合差。","observationEn":"The same per-segment error bound can yield different accumulated closure errors.","failure":"每段誤差不大就不需要檢查整跨累積。","failureEn":"Small individual errors eliminate the need to check span-wide accumulation.","check":"輸出節段表、累積曲線及一個可追溯基準。","checkEn":"Provide a segment table, accumulation plot and traceable datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-14-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"系統性偏差會沿序列累積，不能當成互相抵消的隨機誤差。","textEn":"Systematic bias accumulates along a sequence and cannot be treated as canceling random error."},{"id":"b015-v7-14-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"幾何比較應指定溫度與模型狀態，避免把環境變化誤認為製作誤差。","textEn":"Geometry comparisons should specify temperature and model state to avoid mistaking environmental movement for fabrication error."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「追蹤橋面節段幾何累積」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Track accumulated deck-segment geometry”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["每段誤差不大就不需要檢查整跨累積。","相同單節誤差上限可能形成不同的累積閉合差。","相同方向的節段偏差必然互相抵消。"],"optionsEn":["Small individual errors eliminate the need to check span-wide accumulation.","The same per-segment error bound can yield different accumulated closure errors.","Same-direction segment errors necessarily cancel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"系統性偏差會沿序列累積，不能當成互相抵消的隨機誤差。 幾何比較應指定溫度與模型狀態，避免把環境變化誤認為製作誤差。","explanationEn":"Systematic bias accumulates along a sequence and cannot be treated as canceling random error. Geometry comparisons should specify temperature and model state to avoid mistaking environmental movement for fabrication error."}},{"id":"b015-v7-15","sequence":15,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-14"],"title":"區分橋面彎曲與扭轉","titleEn":"Distinguish deck bending and torsion","objective":"看出左右側位移組合代表的變形模式。","objectiveEn":"Identify deformation modes from paired edge movements.","instruction":"1. 在同一斷面設左右觀察點；2. 繪同向與反向位移；3. 比較中線升降與斷面轉角。","instructionEn":"1. Place observation points at both deck edges; 2. draw same-direction and opposite-direction movements; 3. compare centerline motion and section rotation.","observation":"兩側反向位移可能代表扭轉而非單純整體升降。","observationEn":"Opposite edge movements can indicate torsion rather than uniform vertical motion.","failure":"只量一側橋面即可完整區分所有變形模式。","failureEn":"One deck-edge measurement fully distinguishes all deformation modes.","check":"提交兩組邊緣位移及對應的模式標籤。","checkEn":"Provide two paired edge-motion cases with mode labels.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-15-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"彎曲與扭轉是不同的變形自由度；橋面橫向連接會影響兩者的耦合。","textEn":"Bending and torsion are distinct degrees of freedom; transverse connections influence their coupling."},{"id":"b015-v7-15-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"一個感測器的時間曲線不足以唯一判斷整個斷面的運動。","textEn":"One sensor time history cannot uniquely identify the motion of an entire cross-section."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分橋面彎曲與扭轉」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish deck bending and torsion”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只量一側橋面即可完整區分所有變形模式。","兩側反向位移代表橋面只做剛體平移。","兩側反向位移可能代表扭轉而非單純整體升降。"],"optionsEn":["One deck-edge measurement fully distinguishes all deformation modes.","Opposite edge movements indicate pure rigid translation.","Opposite edge movements can indicate torsion rather than uniform vertical motion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"彎曲與扭轉是不同的變形自由度；橋面橫向連接會影響兩者的耦合。 一個感測器的時間曲線不足以唯一判斷整個斷面的運動。","explanationEn":"Bending and torsion are distinct degrees of freedom; transverse connections influence their coupling. One sensor time history cannot uniquely identify the motion of an entire cross-section."}},{"id":"b015-v7-16","sequence":16,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-15"],"title":"用風案例比較剛度與阻尼","titleEn":"Compare stiffness and damping in wind cases","objective":"避免把降低位移與消耗振動能量混為一談。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating reduced displacement with dissipation of vibration energy.","instruction":"1. 畫兩個自設振動衰減曲線；2. 分別改變頻率及衰減快慢；3. 標註剛度改變與阻尼改變的差別。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two hypothetical vibration-decay curves; 2. vary frequency and decay rate separately; 3. distinguish stiffness changes from damping changes.","observation":"頻率改變與衰減加快是不同的模型特徵。","observationEn":"A changed frequency and faster decay are different model features.","failure":"振幅較小就一定證明材料強度提高。","failureEn":"A smaller amplitude necessarily proves higher material strength.","check":"繳交頻率、振幅及衰減三個獨立觀察欄。","checkEn":"Provide separate observations for frequency, amplitude and decay.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-16-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"剛度影響固有頻率，阻尼描述能量耗散；兩者不能從單一最大振幅直接互換。","textEn":"Stiffness affects natural frequency while damping describes dissipation; one peak amplitude does not identify both."},{"id":"b015-v7-16-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"橋梁的風反應還受氣動形狀與來流條件影響，簡單振子只是概念工具。","textEn":"Bridge wind response also depends on aerodynamics and inflow; a simple oscillator is only a conceptual tool."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用風案例比較剛度與阻尼」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare stiffness and damping in wind cases”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["頻率改變與衰減加快是不同的模型特徵。","振幅較小就一定證明材料強度提高。","衰減曲線變快就唯一證明固有頻率提高。"],"optionsEn":["A changed frequency and faster decay are different model features.","A smaller amplitude necessarily proves higher material strength.","Faster decay uniquely proves an increased natural frequency."],"answer":0,"explanation":"剛度影響固有頻率，阻尼描述能量耗散；兩者不能從單一最大振幅直接互換。 橋梁的風反應還受氣動形狀與來流條件影響，簡單振子只是概念工具。","explanationEn":"Stiffness affects natural frequency while damping describes dissipation; one peak amplitude does not identify both. Bridge wind response also depends on aerodynamics and inflow; a simple oscillator is only a conceptual tool."}},{"id":"b015-v7-17","sequence":17,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-16"],"title":"讀取橋面更換的介面變化","titleEn":"Interpret deck-replacement interfaces","objective":"理解更換橋面會改變質量與接合需求。","objectiveEn":"Understand how deck replacement changes mass and connection requirements.","instruction":"1. 並排畫原混凝土橋面與鋼橋面概念截面；2. 標示重量、局部剛度及排水介面；3. 列出需要重新核對的吊索與支承資料。","instructionEn":"1. Compare conceptual concrete and steel deck sections; 2. mark mass, local stiffness and drainage interfaces; 3. list hanger and support records needing review.","observation":"減輕橋面重量不表示所有結構反應都按同一比例減少。","observationEn":"Reduced deck weight does not reduce every structural response by the same proportion.","failure":"換成較輕橋面後即可沿用全部舊的動態與接合判斷。","failureEn":"A lighter deck permits every old dynamic and connection assumption to remain unchanged.","check":"輸出更換前後的介面差異清單。","checkEn":"Provide an interface-change register for the replacement.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-17-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"質量、剛度與載荷分配共同決定反應，改變其中一項便可能需要重新評估。","textEn":"Mass, stiffness and load distribution jointly govern response; changing one may require reassessment."},{"id":"b015-v7-17-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方記錄的橋面更換是歷史案例；本練習不重建其夜間施工安排。","textEn":"The documented deck replacement is a historical case; this exercise does not reconstruct its night-work plan."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「讀取橋面更換的介面變化」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret deck-replacement interfaces”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["換成較輕橋面後即可沿用全部舊的動態與接合判斷。","減輕橋面重量不表示所有結構反應都按同一比例減少。","重量變少就不必再核對任何橋面連接。"],"optionsEn":["A lighter deck permits every old dynamic and connection assumption to remain unchanged.","Reduced deck weight does not reduce every structural response by the same proportion.","Lower weight eliminates every deck-connection recheck."],"answer":1,"explanation":"質量、剛度與載荷分配共同決定反應，改變其中一項便可能需要重新評估。 官方記錄的橋面更換是歷史案例；本練習不重建其夜間施工安排。","explanationEn":"Mass, stiffness and load distribution jointly govern response; changing one may require reassessment. The documented deck replacement is a historical case; this exercise does not reconstruct its night-work plan."}},{"id":"b015-v7-18","sequence":18,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-17"],"title":"做橋面階段幾何審查","titleEn":"Review deck-stage geometry","objective":"讓架設狀態與量測資料具有一致版本。","objectiveEn":"Keep construction states and measurement data under consistent versions.","instruction":"1. 選一個部分完成狀態；2. 檢查節段、溫度與基準的版本；3. 用新舊兩張圖指出一個不能直接比較的量測。","instructionEn":"1. Select a partially complete state; 2. check segment, temperature and datum versions; 3. identify one observation that cannot be directly compared across two revisions.","observation":"同一位置的讀數在不同邊界條件下不一定可直接相減。","observationEn":"Readings at the same location are not necessarily directly comparable under different boundaries.","failure":"測點名稱相同便代表兩次量測具有相同條件。","failureEn":"An identical point name guarantees identical measurement conditions.","check":"提交一份帶版本及不適用說明的比較表。","checkEn":"Submit a versioned comparison table with applicability notes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-18-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"量測可追溯性包含儀器與模型狀態；只保留數字會丟失工程意義。","textEn":"Measurement traceability includes instruments and model state; retaining numbers alone loses engineering meaning."},{"id":"b015-v7-18-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"介面修訂應通知依賴該資料的後續判讀，否則局部正確仍可造成整體不一致。","textEn":"Interface revisions must propagate to dependent interpretations or locally correct work can remain globally inconsistent."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「做橋面階段幾何審查」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review deck-stage geometry”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["測點名稱相同便代表兩次量測具有相同條件。","測量紀錄只保留數字比保留溫度與版本更完整。","同一位置的讀數在不同邊界條件下不一定可直接相減。"],"optionsEn":["An identical point name guarantees identical measurement conditions.","Numbers alone are a more complete measurement record than numbers with temperature and versions.","Readings at the same location are not necessarily directly comparable under different boundaries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測可追溯性包含儀器與模型狀態；只保留數字會丟失工程意義。 介面修訂應通知依賴該資料的後續判讀，否則局部正確仍可造成整體不一致。","explanationEn":"Measurement traceability includes instruments and model state; retaining numbers alone loses engineering meaning. Interface revisions must propagate to dependent interpretations or locally correct work can remain globally inconsistent."}}]},{"id":"b015-stage04","order":4,"title":"維護、改造與工程移轉","titleEn":"Maintenance, rehabilitation and transfer","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「維護、改造與工程移轉」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on maintenance, rehabilitation and transfer, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v7-19","sequence":19,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-18"],"title":"制定分區腐蝕觀察表","titleEn":"Create a corrosion-observation map","objective":"區分腐蝕環境與可見缺陷的證據層級。","objectiveEn":"Separate exposure conditions from observed-defect evidence.","instruction":"1. 在示意橋上分出海霧、排水與接頭區；2. 各列一種可觀察現象；3. 加入照片日期、位置與不可見範圍欄。","instructionEn":"1. Divide a schematic into marine-fog, drainage and joint zones; 2. list one observable condition per zone; 3. add photo date, location and unseen-scope fields.","observation":"相同外觀缺陷在不同排水與暴露條件下可能有不同進展。","observationEn":"Similar visible defects can progress differently under different drainage and exposure conditions.","failure":"只用照片顏色就判定剩餘承載能力。","failureEn":"Infer remaining load capacity from photograph color alone.","check":"提交分區觀察表並標示不能由照片推出的結論。","checkEn":"Provide a zoned observation register and conclusions photographs cannot establish.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-19-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"腐蝕評估需連接環境、材料損失與構件功能；外觀是證據的一部分。","textEn":"Corrosion assessment links exposure, material loss and function; appearance supplies only part of the evidence."},{"id":"b015-v7-19-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"照片適合做位置與變化追蹤，但沒有比例與時間基準時不能直接量化損失。","textEn":"Photos track location and change, but cannot quantify loss without scale and time references."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「制定分區腐蝕觀察表」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a corrosion-observation map”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["相同外觀缺陷在不同排水與暴露條件下可能有不同進展。","只用照片顏色就判定剩餘承載能力。","所有暴露區都能由同一張近照推定腐蝕狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Similar visible defects can progress differently under different drainage and exposure conditions.","Infer remaining load capacity from photograph color alone.","One close-up establishes corrosion conditions in every exposure zone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"腐蝕評估需連接環境、材料損失與構件功能；外觀是證據的一部分。 照片適合做位置與變化追蹤，但沒有比例與時間基準時不能直接量化損失。","explanationEn":"Corrosion assessment links exposure, material loss and function; appearance supplies only part of the evidence. Photos track location and change, but cannot quantify loss without scale and time references."}},{"id":"b015-v7-20","sequence":20,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-19"],"title":"拆解吊索更新的依賴關係","titleEn":"Map hanger-renewal dependencies","objective":"看出構件更換前後的負載轉移問題。","objectiveEn":"Recognize load-transfer questions around component replacement.","instruction":"1. 在模型標示待更新吊索；2. 畫出可能受影響的相鄰橋面區；3. 列出臨時狀態分析與復核紀錄兩類先決證據。","instructionEn":"1. Mark a hypothetical renewal hanger; 2. map adjacent deck areas potentially affected; 3. list temporary-state analysis and verification records as prerequisites.","observation":"更換一個局部承重元件會影響鄰近系統的受力與幾何。","observationEn":"Replacing one local load-bearing element affects neighboring forces and geometry.","failure":"零件尺寸相同就可忽略更換時的負載轉移。","failureEn":"Matching component dimensions makes load transfer during replacement irrelevant.","check":"輸出依賴圖，明確區分概念審查與現場作業。","checkEn":"Produce a dependency map distinguishing conceptual review from field work.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-20-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"承重構件不能被視為隨意可抽換的積木，臨時平衡也是設計問題。","textEn":"Load-bearing components are not freely removable blocks; temporary equilibrium is a design question."},{"id":"b015-v7-20-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"歷史更新案例可提示應查哪些證據，但不提供今天可直接照做的工序。","textEn":"Historical renewal cases suggest evidence needs but do not supply present-day executable procedures."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆解吊索更新的依賴關係」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map hanger-renewal dependencies”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["零件尺寸相同就可忽略更換時的負載轉移。","更換一個局部承重元件會影響鄰近系統的受力與幾何。","吊索更換只影響新吊索，不影響鄰近橋面。"],"optionsEn":["Matching component dimensions makes load transfer during replacement irrelevant.","Replacing one local load-bearing element affects neighboring forces and geometry.","Hanger replacement affects only the new hanger, not adjacent deck areas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"承重構件不能被視為隨意可抽換的積木，臨時平衡也是設計問題。 歷史更新案例可提示應查哪些證據，但不提供今天可直接照做的工序。","explanationEn":"Load-bearing components are not freely removable blocks; temporary equilibrium is a design question. Historical renewal cases suggest evidence needs but do not supply present-day executable procedures."}},{"id":"b015-v7-21","sequence":21,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-20"],"title":"建立耐震改造的性能矩陣","titleEn":"Build a seismic-performance matrix","objective":"區分構件加強、位移容許及能量耗散。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish strengthening, movement accommodation and energy dissipation.","instruction":"1. 列出橋塔、橋面連接及引橋；2. 對每項寫下力、位移與功能問題；3. 比較三種概念改造目的而不設定實橋參數。","instructionEn":"1. List towers, deck connections and approaches; 2. identify force, displacement and function questions; 3. compare three rehabilitation aims without assigning real-bridge settings.","observation":"更強的局部構件可能把更多地震作用傳到相鄰介面。","observationEn":"A stronger local member can transfer more seismic demand into adjacent interfaces.","failure":"提高局部剛度就保證整座橋所有部位的需求都降低。","failureEn":"Increasing local stiffness guarantees lower demand everywhere in the bridge.","check":"繳交性能目標、介面影響與查證方式的矩陣。","checkEn":"Submit a matrix of performance aims, interface effects and verification methods.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-21-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"耐震性能同時包含強度、變形能力與功能維持；單一安全係數不能描述全部。","textEn":"Seismic performance involves strength, deformation capacity and function; one safety factor cannot describe all of it."},{"id":"b015-v7-21-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"營運者的分期改造提供案例背景，課程不宣稱任一期在今天已完工。","textEn":"The operator’s phased rehabilitation provides context; this course makes no claim that a particular phase is complete today."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立耐震改造的性能矩陣」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Build a seismic-performance matrix”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["提高局部剛度就保證整座橋所有部位的需求都降低。","能量耗散與局部材料強度是完全相同的性能量。","更強的局部構件可能把更多地震作用傳到相鄰介面。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing local stiffness guarantees lower demand everywhere in the bridge.","Energy dissipation and local material strength are identical performance quantities.","A stronger local member can transfer more seismic demand into adjacent interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"耐震性能同時包含強度、變形能力與功能維持；單一安全係數不能描述全部。 營運者的分期改造提供案例背景，課程不宣稱任一期在今天已完工。","explanationEn":"Seismic performance involves strength, deformation capacity and function; one safety factor cannot describe all of it. The operator’s phased rehabilitation provides context; this course makes no claim that a particular phase is complete today."}},{"id":"b015-v7-22","sequence":22,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-21"],"title":"辨識量測漂移與結構變化","titleEn":"Distinguish sensor drift from structural change","objective":"避免把單一異常訊號當成唯一原因。","objectiveEn":"Avoid treating a single anomalous signal as a unique diagnosis.","instruction":"1. 自設兩個位移與一個溫度序列；2. 加入單點偏移及共同趨勢；3. 列出交叉感測與基準複測的查證次序。","instructionEn":"1. Create two displacement series and one temperature series; 2. add a single-point offset and shared trend; 3. define cross-sensor and datum rechecks.","observation":"多個獨立訊號的一致趨勢比單點跳動更能支持系統性變化。","observationEn":"Consistent trends across independent signals support system-wide change better than one jump.","failure":"任何超出過去範圍的數字都能直接定位受損構件。","failureEn":"Any reading outside its historical range directly identifies a damaged component.","check":"提交包含至少兩個替代解釋的異常判讀單。","checkEn":"Submit an anomaly review with at least two alternative explanations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-22-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"感測器漂移、環境影響與真實變形都可能產生異常；需辨識而非只報警。","textEn":"Sensor drift, environmental effects and real deformation can all create anomalies; interpretation is needed beyond an alarm."},{"id":"b015-v7-22-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設數據只能驗證判讀方法，不能估計真橋的當前健康狀態。","textEn":"Synthetic data test interpretation methods and cannot estimate the actual bridge’s current condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨識量測漂移與結構變化」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish sensor drift from structural change”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["多個獨立訊號的一致趨勢比單點跳動更能支持系統性變化。","任何超出過去範圍的數字都能直接定位受損構件。","同一感測器重複輸出的數字就等同多個獨立證據。"],"optionsEn":["Consistent trends across independent signals support system-wide change better than one jump.","Any reading outside its historical range directly identifies a damaged component.","Repeated output from one sensor equals multiple independent evidence sources."],"answer":0,"explanation":"感測器漂移、環境影響與真實變形都可能產生異常；需辨識而非只報警。 自設數據只能驗證判讀方法，不能估計真橋的當前健康狀態。","explanationEn":"Sensor drift, environmental effects and real deformation can all create anomalies; interpretation is needed beyond an alarm. Synthetic data test interpretation methods and cannot estimate the actual bridge’s current condition."}},{"id":"b015-v7-23","sequence":23,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-22"],"title":"比較明石海峽與淡江大橋","titleEn":"Compare Akashi Kaikyo and Danjiang bridges","objective":"辨認可轉移工法與不可直接移植的假設。","objectiveEn":"Identify transferable methods and nontransferable assumptions.","instruction":"1. 並排畫金門、明石與淡江橋型；2. 對比主纜吊索與斜張索力路徑；3. 列出場址、風與基礎必須重新查證的差異。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch Golden Gate, Akashi Kaikyo and Danjiang forms; 2. contrast main-cable/hanger and stay force paths; 3. list site, wind and foundation differences needing new evidence.","observation":"量測追溯與介面審查可轉移，但橋型和場址參數須重新建立。","observationEn":"Measurement traceability and interface review transfer, but bridge form and site parameters require rebuilding.","failure":"同為跨水大橋便能沿用同一組索力與基礎條件。","failureEn":"Every water-crossing bridge can reuse identical cable forces and foundation conditions.","check":"繳交三項相似處與三項禁止直接套用的差異。","checkEn":"Provide three similarities and three differences that prevent direct reuse.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-23-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"比較工程的價值在辨認相同問題的不同解法，不在尋找外觀最相近的照片。","textEn":"Engineering comparison identifies different solutions to related problems rather than merely similar photographs."},{"id":"b015-v7-23-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"懸索與斜張橋都需幾何及張力協調，但力路徑和施工狀態不同。","textEn":"Suspension and cable-stayed bridges both coordinate geometry and tension but have different force paths and construction states."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較明石海峽與淡江大橋」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare Akashi Kaikyo and Danjiang bridges”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["同為跨水大橋便能沿用同一組索力與基礎條件。","量測追溯與介面審查可轉移，但橋型和場址參數須重新建立。","不同場址的風與地質條件可由橋梁外觀相似程度換算。"],"optionsEn":["Every water-crossing bridge can reuse identical cable forces and foundation conditions.","Measurement traceability and interface review transfer, but bridge form and site parameters require rebuilding.","Visual similarity between bridges determines corresponding wind and ground conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較工程的價值在辨認相同問題的不同解法，不在尋找外觀最相近的照片。 懸索與斜張橋都需幾何及張力協調，但力路徑和施工狀態不同。","explanationEn":"Engineering comparison identifies different solutions to related problems rather than merely similar photographs. Suspension and cable-stayed bridges both coordinate geometry and tension but have different force paths and construction states."}},{"id":"b015-v7-24","sequence":24,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-improvements","v7-golden-seismic","v7-golden-history"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-23"],"title":"總工程師交付證據包","titleEn":"Deliver the chief-engineer evidence pack","objective":"把完整課程整理成可複查的工程論證。","objectiveEn":"Turn the course into an auditable engineering argument.","instruction":"1. 彙整場址、受力、狀態及維護圖；2. 給每個結論連上一個來源或模型假設；3. 保留三個仍需專業調查才能回答的問題。","instructionEn":"1. Assemble site, force, state and maintenance diagrams; 2. attach a source or model assumption to every conclusion; 3. retain three questions requiring professional investigation.","observation":"完整交付包含未解問題和適用範圍，而非只有通過標記。","observationEn":"A complete handover includes unresolved questions and applicability limits, not just pass marks.","failure":"課程操作完成就等於具備現地橋梁施工資格。","failureEn":"Completing the course establishes qualification to construct a real bridge.","check":"提交帶版本、來源及限制的四頁概念工程包。","checkEn":"Submit a four-page conceptual engineering pack with versions, sources and limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v7-24-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"工程論證由要求、模型、證據及限制串起來；漂亮圖面本身不是驗證。","textEn":"An engineering argument joins requirements, models, evidence and limits; a polished diagram is not verification."},{"id":"b015-v7-24-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程完成的是概念與證據組織能力，不是金門大橋的原始施工設計。","textEn":"This course develops conceptual and evidence-organizing skills, not the Golden Gate Bridge’s original construction design."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「總工程師交付證據包」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Deliver the chief-engineer evidence pack”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["課程操作完成就等於具備現地橋梁施工資格。","未解問題應從交付資料刪除，以免影響完整性。","完整交付包含未解問題和適用範圍，而非只有通過標記。"],"optionsEn":["Completing the course establishes qualification to construct a real bridge.","Open questions should be removed from handover records to preserve completeness.","A complete handover includes unresolved questions and applicability limits, not just pass marks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工程論證由要求、模型、證據及限制串起來；漂亮圖面本身不是驗證。 本課程完成的是概念與證據組織能力，不是金門大橋的原始施工設計。","explanationEn":"An engineering argument joins requirements, models, evidence and limits; a polished diagram is not verification. This course develops conceptual and evidence-organizing skills, not the Golden Gate Bridge’s original construction design."}}]},{"id":"b015-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力」與「主纜重力勁度與橫向變位」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load\" and \"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v13-01","title":"由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v7-24"],"objective":"說明「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “61,500-ton cable load per tower” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主資料指出兩條主纜施加在每座橋塔的荷重約 61,500 噸（美噸）。這個豎向力等於主跨與邊跨主纜在索鞍兩側的豎向分量之和，因此只要知道兩側主纜在塔頂的傾角，就能反推主纜水平張力與最大張力，再與鋼絲面積及強度比較得到安全係數。這種「由支承反力反推內力」的檢核，是評估既有懸索橋時最常用的獨立驗算，可與原始計算書或有限元素模型相互印證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Owner data state that the two main cables place about 61,500 tons (short tons) on each tower. This vertical force is the sum of the vertical components of the main-span and side-span cables on either side of the saddle, so knowing the cable angles at the tower top gives the horizontal and maximum tensions, which can then be compared with wire area and strength for a safety factor. Back-calculating internal forces from support reactions is the most common independent check when evaluating an existing suspension bridge, cross-checking the original calculations or a finite-element model. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “61,500-ton cable load per tower” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：V = 61,500 short ton×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: V = 61,500 short tons×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The load on the tower equals the cable tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “61,500-ton cable load per tower”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-01-k1","title":"由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力","titleEn":"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load","text":"業主資料指出兩條主纜施加在每座橋塔的荷重約 61,500 噸（美噸）。這個豎向力等於主跨與邊跨主纜在索鞍兩側的豎向分量之和，因此只要知道兩側主纜在塔頂的傾角，就能反推主纜水平張力與最大張力，再與鋼絲面積及強度比較得到安全係數。","textEn":"Owner data state that the two main cables place about 61,500 tons (short tons) on each tower. This vertical force is the sum of the vertical components of the main-span and side-span cables on either side of the saddle, so knowing the cable angles at the tower top gives the horizontal and maximum tensions, which can then be compared with wire area and strength for a safety factor.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The load on the tower equals the cable tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load\" is correct?","options":["塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。","業主資料指出兩條主纜施加在每座橋塔的荷重約 61,500 噸（美噸）。","懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。"],"optionsEn":["The load on the tower equals the cable tension.","Owner data state that the two main cables place about 61,500 tons (short tons) on each tower.","A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"業主資料指出兩條主纜施加在每座橋塔的荷重約 61,500 噸（美噸）。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Owner data state that the two main cables place about 61,500 tons (short tons) on each tower. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b015-v13-02","title":"由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力：定量估算","titleEn":"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “61,500-ton cable load per tower” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：V = 61,500 short ton×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN。取主跨 tanθ_m = 0.44、邊跨 tanθ_s = 0.40：H = V/(0.44+0.40) ≈ 651 MN（兩纜），每纜 326 MN；T = 326×√(1+0.44²) ≈ 356 MN。每纜鋼絲面積 27,572×18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm²，應力 ≈ 691 N/mm²，對最低強度 1,517 N/mm² 的係數約 2.19。傾角為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: V = 61,500 short tons×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN. Taking tanθ_m = 0.44 for the main span and tanθ_s = 0.40 for the side span: H = V/(0.44+0.40) ≈ 651 MN for both cables, 326 MN each; T = 326×√(1+0.44²) ≈ 356 MN. Wire area per cable 27,572×18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm² gives a stress of about 691 N/mm², a factor of about 2.19 on the 1,517 N/mm² minimum strength. The angles are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以竣工測量或光達掃描取得塔頂兩側主纜實際傾角，代回計算 H 與 T，並與原設計值和有限元素模型比較；若三者差異超過約定範圍，檢查恆載假設（例如 1986 年更換後的橋面重量）與塔頂索鞍位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain actual cable angles on both sides of the tower top from as-built survey or lidar, recompute H and T, and compare with original design values and the finite-element model; if the three differ beyond an agreed band, check dead-load assumptions such as the deck weight after the 1986 replacement and the saddle positions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"V = 61,500 short ton×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN。取主跨 tanθ_m = 0.44、邊跨 tanθ_s = 0.40：H = V/(0.44+0.40) ≈ 651 MN（兩纜），每纜 326 MN；T = 326×√(1+0.44²) ≈ 356 MN。每纜鋼絲面積 27,572×18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm²，應力 ≈ 691 N/mm²，對最低強度 1,517 N/mm² 的係數約 2.19。傾角為教學假設。","textEn":"V = 61,500 short tons×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN. Taking tanθ_m = 0.44 for the main span and tanθ_s = 0.40 for the side span: H = V/(0.44+0.40) ≈ 651 MN for both cables, 326 MN each; T = 326×√(1+0.44²) ≈ 356 MN. Wire area per cable 27,572×18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm² gives a stress of about 691 N/mm², a factor of about 2.19 on the 1,517 N/mm² minimum strength. The angles are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load\", which statement holds?","options":["吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。","把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","V = 61,500 short ton×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter.","A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","V = 61,500 short tons×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"V = 61,500 short ton×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"V = 61,500 short tons×907.2 kg×9.81 ≈ 547 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b015-v13-03","title":"由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “61,500-ton cable load per tower” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以竣工測量或光達掃描取得塔頂兩側主纜實際傾角，代回計算 H 與 T，並與原設計值和有限元素模型比較；若三者差異超過約定範圍，檢查恆載假設（例如 1986 年更換後的橋面重量）與塔頂索鞍位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain actual cable angles on both sides of the tower top from as-built survey or lidar, recompute H and T, and compare with original design values and the finite-element model; if the three differ beyond an agreed band, check dead-load assumptions such as the deck weight after the 1986 replacement and the saddle positions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：既有懸索橋的評估報告應附一份「恆載履歷表」，逐項列出歷次改造增減的重量與日期，並以塔頂反力與主纜幾何做獨立驗算，作為與有限元素模型比對的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: An evaluation of an existing suspension bridge should include a dead-load history listing the weight added or removed by each modification with dates, and an independent check from tower reactions and cable geometry as the benchmark for the finite-element model.","failure":"注意干擾：若評估仍沿用 1937 年的恆載而忽略後來的橋面更換、加勁與附加設施，計算出的主纜應力與安全係數會偏離實際；反過來若遺漏新增荷重（防墜網、抗風整流板），可能高估剩餘容量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An evaluation still using 1937 dead loads, ignoring later deck replacement, bracing and attachments, misstates cable stress and safety factor; conversely, missing added loads such as the deterrent net or wind fairings can overstate remaining capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以竣工測量或光達掃描取得塔頂兩側主纜實際傾角，代回計算 H 與 T，並與原設計值和有限元素模型比較；若三者差異超過約定範圍，檢查恆載假設（例如 1986 年更換後的橋面重量）與塔頂索鞍位置。","textEn":"Obtain actual cable angles on both sides of the tower top from as-built survey or lidar, recompute H and T, and compare with original design values and the finite-element model; if the three differ beyond an agreed band, check dead-load assumptions such as the deck weight after the 1986 replacement and the saddle positions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"既有懸索橋的評估報告應附一份「恆載履歷表」，逐項列出歷次改造增減的重量與日期，並以塔頂反力與主纜幾何做獨立驗算，作為與有限元素模型比對的基準。","textEn":"An evaluation of an existing suspension bridge should include a dead-load history listing the weight added or removed by each modification with dates, and an independent check from tower reactions and cable geometry as the benchmark for the finite-element model.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load\"?","options":["以竣工測量或光達掃描取得塔頂兩側主纜實際傾角，代回計算 H 與 T，並與原設計值和有限元素模型比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。"],"optionsEn":["Obtain actual cable angles on both sides of the tower top from as-built survey or lidar, recompute H and T, and compare with original design values and the finite-element model.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以竣工測量或光達掃描取得塔頂兩側主纜實際傾角，代回計算 H 與 T，並與原設計值和有限元素模型比較；若三者差異超過約定範圍，檢查恆載假設（例如 1986 年更換後的橋面重量）與塔頂索鞍位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain actual cable angles on both sides of the tower top from as-built survey or lidar, recompute H and T, and compare with original design values and the finite-element model; if the three differ beyond an agreed band, check dead-load assumptions such as the deck weight after the 1986 replacement and the saddle positions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b015-v13-04","title":"由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「每塔 61,500 噸纜力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “61,500-ton cable load per tower” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若評估仍沿用 1937 年的恆載而忽略後來的橋面更換、加勁與附加設施，計算出的主纜應力與安全係數會偏離實際；反過來若遺漏新增荷重（防墜網、抗風整流板），可能高估剩餘容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An evaluation still using 1937 dead loads, ignoring later deck replacement, bracing and attachments, misstates cable stress and safety factor; conversely, missing added loads such as the deterrent net or wind fairings can overstate remaining capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這種「由支承反力反推內力」的檢核，是評估既有懸索橋時最常用的獨立驗算，可與原始計算書或有限元素模型相互印證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Back-calculating internal forces from support reactions is the most common independent check when evaluating an existing suspension bridge, cross-checking the original calculations or a finite-element model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The load on the tower equals the cable tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若評估仍沿用 1937 年的恆載而忽略後來的橋面更換、加勁與附加設施，計算出的主纜應力與安全係數會偏離實際；反過來若遺漏新增荷重（防墜網、抗風整流板），可能高估剩餘容量。","textEn":"An evaluation still using 1937 dead loads, ignoring later deck replacement, bracing and attachments, misstates cable stress and safety factor; conversely, missing added loads such as the deterrent net or wind fairings can overstate remaining capacity.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「由塔頂荷重反推主纜張力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Back-calculating cable tension from tower load\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若評估仍沿用 1937 年的恆載而忽略後來的橋面更換、加勁與附加設施，計算出的主纜應力與安全係數會偏離實際。","懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An evaluation still using 1937 dead loads, ignoring later deck replacement, bracing and attachments, misstates cable stress and safety factor.","A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若評估仍沿用 1937 年的恆載而忽略後來的橋面更換、加勁與附加設施，計算出的主纜應力與安全係數會偏離實際；反過來若遺漏新增荷重（防墜網、抗風整流板），可能高估剩餘容量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An evaluation still using 1937 dead loads, ignoring later deck replacement, bracing and attachments, misstates cable stress and safety factor; conversely, missing added loads such as the deterrent net or wind fairings can overstate remaining capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b015-v13-05","title":"主纜重力勁度與橫向變位：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「27.7 ft 橫向變位」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “27.7 ft lateral deflection” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主資料列出主跨中央最大橫向變位約 27.7 ft（約 8.4 m），遠大於最大下垂 10.8 ft 與上揚 5.8 ft。懸索橋抵抗側風的勁度主要不是來自加勁桁架的側向彎曲，而是來自主纜的「重力勁度」：受張的主纜像鐘擺一樣，被側向推開時，張力的水平分量會把它拉回中心。張力越大、跨徑越短，回復力越強；1950 年代增設的下層橫向斜撐則提高了橋面本身的側向與扭轉勁度，兩者共同決定側風下的變位與振動特性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「27.7 ft 橫向變位」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Owner data list a maximum transverse deflection at mid-span of about 27.7 ft (about 8.4 m), far more than the maximum downward 10.8 ft and upward 5.8 ft. A suspension bridge resists crosswind mainly not through lateral bending of the stiffening truss but through the gravity stiffness of the cables: like a pendulum, a tensioned cable pushed sideways is pulled back by the horizontal component of its tension. Higher tension and shorter span give stronger restoring force; the lower lateral bracing added in the 1950s raised the deck's own lateral and torsional stiffness, and the two together set deflection and vibration in crosswinds. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “27.7 ft lateral deflection” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以弦受側向均布力估算 δ = w_L·l²/(8H)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate with a string under uniform lateral load δ = w_L·l²/(8H).","failure":"常見誤解：「懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「27.7 ft 橫向變位」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “27.7 ft lateral deflection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-05-k1","title":"主纜重力勁度與橫向變位","titleEn":"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection","text":"業主資料列出主跨中央最大橫向變位約 27.7 ft（約 8.4 m），遠大於最大下垂 10.8 ft 與上揚 5.8 ft。懸索橋抵抗側風的勁度主要不是來自加勁桁架的側向彎曲，而是來自主纜的「重力勁度」：受張的主纜像鐘擺一樣，被側向推開時，張力的水平分量會把它拉回中心。","textEn":"Owner data list a maximum transverse deflection at mid-span of about 27.7 ft (about 8.4 m), far more than the maximum downward 10.8 ft and upward 5.8 ft. A suspension bridge resists crosswind mainly not through lateral bending of the stiffening truss but through the gravity stiffness of the cables: like a pendulum, a tensioned cable pushed sideways is pulled back by the horizontal component of its tension.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主纜重力勁度與橫向變位」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection\" is correct?","options":["懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。","老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。","業主資料列出主跨中央最大橫向變位約 27.7 ft（約 8.4 m），遠大於最大下垂 10.8 ft 與上揚 5.8 ft。"],"optionsEn":["A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load.","Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.","Owner data list a maximum transverse deflection at mid-span of about 27.7 ft (about 8.4 m), far more than the maximum downward 10.8 ft and upward 5.8 ft."],"answer":2,"explanation":"業主資料列出主跨中央最大橫向變位約 27.7 ft（約 8.4 m），遠大於最大下垂 10.8 ft 與上揚 5.8 ft。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Owner data list a maximum transverse deflection at mid-span of about 27.7 ft (about 8.4 m), far more than the maximum downward 10.8 ft and upward 5.8 ft. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b015-v13-06","title":"主纜重力勁度與橫向變位：定量估算","titleEn":"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「27.7 ft 橫向變位」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “27.7 ft lateral deflection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以弦受側向均布力估算 δ = w_L·l²/(8H)。取 H = 651 MN（兩纜合計）、l = 1,280 m、側向風力 w_L = 15 kN/m：δ = 15×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 4.7 m；反算達到 8.4 m 需 w_L ≈ 8×651,000×8.44/1,280² ≈ 26.9 kN/m。忽略桁架側向勁度，為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate with a string under uniform lateral load δ = w_L·l²/(8H). With H = 651 MN for both cables, l = 1,280 m and lateral wind load w_L = 15 kN/m: δ = 15×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 4.7 m; reaching 8.4 m would need w_L ≈ 8×651,000×8.44/1,280² ≈ 26.9 kN/m. Truss lateral stiffness is ignored; values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以 GNSS 在跨中與四分點量測強風中的側向位移，同步記錄橋面高度的風速風向，將位移對風壓（∝U²）作圖，檢查斜率是否符合重力勁度加桁架勁度的模型；並比較伸縮縫與風支承在側向位移時的行程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure lateral displacement in strong wind with GNSS at mid-span and quarter points, recording deck-level wind speed and direction, plot displacement against wind pressure (∝U²) and check the slope against a gravity-plus-truss stiffness model; also compare the travel of expansion joints and wind shoes during lateral movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以弦受側向均布力估算 δ = w_L·l²/(8H)。取 H = 651 MN（兩纜合計）、l = 1,280 m、側向風力 w_L = 15 kN/m：δ = 15×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 4.7 m；反算達到 8.4 m 需 w_L ≈ 8×651,000×8.44/1,280² ≈ 26.9 kN/m。忽略桁架側向勁度，為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate with a string under uniform lateral load δ = w_L·l²/(8H). With H = 651 MN for both cables, l = 1,280 m and lateral wind load w_L = 15 kN/m: δ = 15×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 4.7 m; reaching 8.4 m would need w_L ≈ 8×651,000×8.44/1,280² ≈ 26.9 kN/m. Truss lateral stiffness is ignored; values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主纜重力勁度與橫向變位」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection\", which statement holds?","options":["以弦受側向均布力估算 δ = w_L·l²/(8H)。","空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。","只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate with a string under uniform lateral load δ = w_L·l²/(8H).","Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run.","If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以弦受側向均布力估算 δ = w_L·l²/(8H)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate with a string under uniform lateral load δ = w_L·l²/(8H). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b015-v13-07","title":"主纜重力勁度與橫向變位：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「27.7 ft 橫向變位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “27.7 ft lateral deflection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以 GNSS 在跨中與四分點量測強風中的側向位移，同步記錄橋面高度的風速風向，將位移對風壓（∝U²）作圖，檢查斜率是否符合重力勁度加桁架勁度的模型；並比較伸縮縫與風支承在側向位移時的行程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure lateral displacement in strong wind with GNSS at mid-span and quarter points, recording deck-level wind speed and direction, plot displacement against wind pressure (∝U²) and check the slope against a gravity-plus-truss stiffness model; also compare the travel of expansion joints and wind shoes during lateral movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何會增加橋面受風面積或改變斷面形狀的工程，都要在設計階段提出側風變位與氣動穩定的評估，並由業主的風工程顧問核可；評估須同時列出伸縮縫、風支承與管線的位移容量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Any work that adds wind area or changes the deck section must come with an assessment of lateral deflection and aerodynamic stability at design stage, approved by the owner's wind consultant, listing the displacement capacity of joints, wind shoes and services.","failure":"注意干擾：若改造增加了橋面側向受風面積（例如加裝圍欄或設備）而未更新側風分析，實際橫向變位與伸縮縫行程需求可能超出原設計；側向勁度不足也會讓渦振與扭轉耦合更容易發生。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If a modification increases the deck's lateral wind area, such as new fencing or equipment, without updating the crosswind analysis, actual lateral deflection and joint travel demand may exceed design; low lateral stiffness also makes vortex and torsional coupling easier. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 GNSS 在跨中與四分點量測強風中的側向位移，同步記錄橋面高度的風速風向，將位移對風壓（∝U²）作圖，檢查斜率是否符合重力勁度加桁架勁度的模型；並比較伸縮縫與風支承在側向位移時的行程。","textEn":"Measure lateral displacement in strong wind with GNSS at mid-span and quarter points, recording deck-level wind speed and direction, plot displacement against wind pressure (∝U²) and check the slope against a gravity-plus-truss stiffness model; also compare the travel of expansion joints and wind shoes during lateral movement.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何會增加橋面受風面積或改變斷面形狀的工程，都要在設計階段提出側風變位與氣動穩定的評估，並由業主的風工程顧問核可；評估須同時列出伸縮縫、風支承與管線的位移容量。","textEn":"Any work that adds wind area or changes the deck section must come with an assessment of lateral deflection and aerodynamic stability at design stage, approved by the owner's wind consultant, listing the displacement capacity of joints, wind shoes and services.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主纜重力勁度與橫向變位」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以 GNSS 在跨中與四分點量測強風中的側向位移，同步記錄橋面高度的風速風向，將位移對風壓（∝U²）作圖，檢查斜率是否符合重力勁度加桁架勁度的模型。","1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Measure lateral displacement in strong wind with GNSS at mid-span and quarter points, recording deck-level wind speed and direction, plot displacement against wind pressure (∝U²) and check the slope against a gravity-plus-truss stiffness model.","Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以 GNSS 在跨中與四分點量測強風中的側向位移，同步記錄橋面高度的風速風向，將位移對風壓（∝U²）作圖，檢查斜率是否符合重力勁度加桁架勁度的模型；並比較伸縮縫與風支承在側向位移時的行程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure lateral displacement in strong wind with GNSS at mid-span and quarter points, recording deck-level wind speed and direction, plot displacement against wind pressure (∝U²) and check the slope against a gravity-plus-truss stiffness model; also compare the travel of expansion joints and wind shoes during lateral movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b015-v13-08","title":"主纜重力勁度與橫向變位：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「27.7 ft 橫向變位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “27.7 ft lateral deflection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若改造增加了橋面側向受風面積（例如加裝圍欄或設備）而未更新側風分析，實際橫向變位與伸縮縫行程需求可能超出原設計；側向勁度不足也會讓渦振與扭轉耦合更容易發生。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If a modification increases the deck's lateral wind area, such as new fencing or equipment, without updating the crosswind analysis, actual lateral deflection and joint travel demand may exceed design; low lateral stiffness also makes vortex and torsional coupling easier. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：張力越大、跨徑越短，回復力越強；1950 年代增設的下層橫向斜撐則提高了橋面本身的側向與扭轉勁度，兩者共同決定側風下的變位與振動特性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Higher tension and shorter span give stronger restoring force; the lower lateral bracing added in the 1950s raised the deck's own lateral and torsional stiffness, and the two together set deflection and vibration in crosswinds.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若改造增加了橋面側向受風面積（例如加裝圍欄或設備）而未更新側風分析，實際橫向變位與伸縮縫行程需求可能超出原設計；側向勁度不足也會讓渦振與扭轉耦合更容易發生。","textEn":"If a modification increases the deck's lateral wind area, such as new fencing or equipment, without updating the crosswind analysis, actual lateral deflection and joint travel demand may exceed design; low lateral stiffness also makes vortex and torsional coupling easier.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主纜重力勁度與橫向變位」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cable gravity stiffness and lateral deflection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。","若改造增加了橋面側向受風面積（例如加裝圍欄或設備）而未更新側風分析，實際橫向變位與伸縮縫行程需求可能超出原設計；側向勁度不足也會讓渦振與扭轉耦合更容易發生。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.","If a modification increases the deck's lateral wind area, such as new fencing or equipment, without updating the crosswind analysis, actual lateral deflection and joint travel demand may exceed design."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若改造增加了橋面側向受風面積（例如加裝圍欄或設備）而未更新側風分析，實際橫向變位與伸縮縫行程需求可能超出原設計；側向勁度不足也會讓渦振與扭轉耦合更容易發生。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If a modification increases the deck's lateral wind area, such as new fencing or equipment, without updating the crosswind analysis, actual lateral deflection and joint travel demand may exceed design; low lateral stiffness also makes vortex and torsional coupling easier. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":5},{"id":"b015-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性」與「吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire\" and \"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v13-09","title":"1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “0.192 in galvanised wire” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"金門大橋每條主纜含 27,572 根直徑 0.192 in（約 4.88 mm）的鍍鋅鋼絲，分成 61 束、平均每束約 452 根，連同纏繞外徑約 36⅜ in（0.92 m）。業主公布的鋼絲平均抗拉強度 235,600 psi（規格最低 220,000 psi）、降伏強度 182,600 psi、斷裂伸長率 6.3%（最低 4.0%）。與現代 1,770 至 1,960 MPa 級鋼絲相比強度較低，但延性與降伏比較寬裕；評估既有主纜時，要用當時規格的最低值與實際抽樣結果，而不是現代鋼絲的數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each Golden Gate cable contains 27,572 galvanised wires of 0.192 in (about 4.88 mm) diameter in 61 strands averaging about 452 wires, about 36⅜ in (0.92 m) in diameter with wrapping. The owner lists average wire tensile strength of 235,600 psi (220,000 psi specified minimum), yield of 182,600 psi and elongation at rupture of 6.3% (4.0% minimum). The strength is lower than modern 1,770 to 1,960 MPa wire, but ductility and yield ratio are generous; evaluating an existing cable must use the period specification minimum and actual sample results, not modern wire figures. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “0.192 in galvanised wire” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：換算：235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm²、220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm²、182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm²，降伏比 ≈ 0.775。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Conversions: 235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm², 220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm², 182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm², a yield ratio ≈ 0.775.","failure":"常見誤解：「老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “0.192 in galvanised wire”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-09-k1","title":"1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性","titleEn":"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire","text":"金門大橋每條主纜含 27,572 根直徑 0.192 in（約 4.88 mm）的鍍鋅鋼絲，分成 61 束、平均每束約 452 根，連同纏繞外徑約 36⅜ in（0.92 m）。業主公布的鋼絲平均抗拉強度 235,600 psi（規格最低 220,000 psi）、降伏強度 182,600 psi、斷裂伸長率 6.3%（最低 4.0%）。","textEn":"Each Golden Gate cable contains 27,572 galvanised wires of 0.192 in (about 4.88 mm) diameter in 61 strands averaging about 452 wires, about 36⅜ in (0.92 m) in diameter with wrapping. The owner lists average wire tensile strength of 235,600 psi (220,000 psi specified minimum), yield of 182,600 psi and elongation at rupture of 6.3% (4.0% minimum).","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire\" is correct?","options":["金門大橋每條主纜含 27,572 根直徑 0.192 in（約 4.88 mm）的鍍鋅鋼絲，分成 61 束、平均每束約 452 根，連同纏繞外徑約 36⅜ in（0.92 m）。","老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。","吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。"],"optionsEn":["Each Golden Gate cable contains 27,572 galvanised wires of 0.192 in (about 4.88 mm) diameter in 61 strands averaging about 452 wires, about 36⅜ in (0.92 m) in diameter with wrapping.","Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.","Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"金門大橋每條主纜含 27,572 根直徑 0.192 in（約 4.88 mm）的鍍鋅鋼絲，分成 61 束、平均每束約 452 根，連同纏繞外徑約 36⅜ in（0.92 m）。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each Golden Gate cable contains 27,572 galvanised wires of 0.192 in (about 4.88 mm) diameter in 61 strands averaging about 452 wires, about 36⅜ in (0.92 m) in diameter with wrapping. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b015-v13-10","title":"1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性：定量估算","titleEn":"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “0.192 in galvanised wire” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：換算：235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm²、220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm²、182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm²，降伏比 ≈ 0.775。單絲面積 π/4×4.877² ≈ 18.68 mm²，每纜面積 ≈ 515,000 mm²，以最低強度計破斷力 ≈ 781 MN。兩纜總長核算：2×27,572×2,332 m ≈ 128,600 km，與公布的約 129,000 km 一致。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Conversions: 235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm², 220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm², 182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm², a yield ratio ≈ 0.775. Wire area π/4×4.877² ≈ 18.68 mm², about 515,000 mm² per cable, for a minimum breaking force ≈ 781 MN. Total length check: 2×27,572×2,332 m ≈ 128,600 km, matching the published 129,000 km or so. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：開纜檢查時取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸、伸長率與扭轉試驗，並以金相與鍍鋅層量測判斷腐蝕階段；依試驗結果與斷絲統計建立剩餘強度模型，比較設計時的最低強度與實際分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During cable openings remove representative wires for tensile, elongation and torsion tests, and assess corrosion stage by metallography and zinc measurement; build a remaining-strength model from test results and broken-wire counts, comparing the original specified minimum with the actual distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"換算：235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm²、220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm²、182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm²，降伏比 ≈ 0.775。單絲面積 π/4×4.877² ≈ 18.68 mm²，每纜面積 ≈ 515,000 mm²，以最低強度計破斷力 ≈ 781 MN。兩纜總長核算：2×27,572×2,332 m ≈ 128,600 km，與公布的約 129,000 km 一致。","textEn":"Conversions: 235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm², 220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm², 182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm², a yield ratio ≈ 0.775. Wire area π/4×4.877² ≈ 18.68 mm², about 515,000 mm² per cable, for a minimum breaking force ≈ 781 MN. Total length check: 2×27,572×2,332 m ≈ 128,600 km, matching the published 129,000 km or so.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire\", which statement holds?","options":["把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","換算：235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm²、220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm²、182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm²，降伏比 ≈ 0.775。","螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。"],"optionsEn":["A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","Conversions: 235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm², 220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm², 182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm², a yield ratio ≈ 0.775.","Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever."],"answer":1,"explanation":"換算：235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm²、220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm²、182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm²，降伏比 ≈ 0.775。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Conversions: 235,600 psi ≈ 1,624 N/mm², 220,000 psi ≈ 1,517 N/mm², 182,600 psi ≈ 1,259 N/mm², a yield ratio ≈ 0.775. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b015-v13-11","title":"1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “0.192 in galvanised wire” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"開纜檢查時取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸、伸長率與扭轉試驗，並以金相與鍍鋅層量測判斷腐蝕階段；依試驗結果與斷絲統計建立剩餘強度模型，比較設計時的最低強度與實際分布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During cable openings remove representative wires for tensile, elongation and torsion tests, and assess corrosion stage by metallography and zinc measurement; build a remaining-strength model from test results and broken-wire counts, comparing the original specified minimum with the actual distribution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保存原始鋼絲規格與出廠試驗紀錄，每次開纜取樣都要記錄位置、束號與試驗結果，納入同一資料庫，讓日後的剩餘強度評估能追溯並比較趨勢。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep the original wire specification and mill test records, and log location, strand number and results for every cable sample in one database so later remaining-strength evaluations can trace and compare trends.","failure":"注意干擾：若評估直接套用現代鋼絲強度，主纜安全係數會被高估；反之若只依外觀判斷而不做試驗，可能忽略內部鋼絲的脆化或腐蝕裂縫，延誤除濕或補強決策。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying modern wire strengths overstates the cable's safety factor; judging only by appearance without testing can miss embrittlement or corrosion cracking of inner wires and delay dehumidification or strengthening decisions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"開纜檢查時取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸、伸長率與扭轉試驗，並以金相與鍍鋅層量測判斷腐蝕階段；依試驗結果與斷絲統計建立剩餘強度模型，比較設計時的最低強度與實際分布。","textEn":"During cable openings remove representative wires for tensile, elongation and torsion tests, and assess corrosion stage by metallography and zinc measurement; build a remaining-strength model from test results and broken-wire counts, comparing the original specified minimum with the actual distribution.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保存原始鋼絲規格與出廠試驗紀錄，每次開纜取樣都要記錄位置、束號與試驗結果，納入同一資料庫，讓日後的剩餘強度評估能追溯並比較趨勢。","textEn":"Keep the original wire specification and mill test records, and log location, strand number and results for every cable sample in one database so later remaining-strength evaluations can trace and compare trends.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。","開纜檢查時取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸、伸長率與扭轉試驗，並以金相與鍍鋅層量測判斷腐蝕階段；依試驗結果與斷絲統計建立剩餘強度模型，比較設計時的最低強度與實際分布。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability.","During cable openings remove representative wires for tensile, elongation and torsion tests, and assess corrosion stage by metallography and zinc measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開纜檢查時取出代表性鋼絲做拉伸、伸長率與扭轉試驗，並以金相與鍍鋅層量測判斷腐蝕階段；依試驗結果與斷絲統計建立剩餘強度模型，比較設計時的最低強度與實際分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During cable openings remove representative wires for tensile, elongation and torsion tests, and assess corrosion stage by metallography and zinc measurement; build a remaining-strength model from test results and broken-wire counts, comparing the original specified minimum with the actual distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b015-v13-12","title":"1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「0.192 in 鍍鋅鋼絲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “0.192 in galvanised wire” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若評估直接套用現代鋼絲強度，主纜安全係數會被高估；反之若只依外觀判斷而不做試驗，可能忽略內部鋼絲的脆化或腐蝕裂縫，延誤除濕或補強決策。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying modern wire strengths overstates the cable's safety factor; judging only by appearance without testing can miss embrittlement or corrosion cracking of inner wires and delay dehumidification or strengthening decisions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：與現代 1,770 至 1,960 MPa 級鋼絲相比強度較低，但延性與降伏比較寬裕；評估既有主纜時，要用當時規格的最低值與實際抽樣結果，而不是現代鋼絲的數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The strength is lower than modern 1,770 to 1,960 MPa wire, but ductility and yield ratio are generous; evaluating an existing cable must use the period specification minimum and actual sample results, not modern wire figures.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若評估直接套用現代鋼絲強度，主纜安全係數會被高估；反之若只依外觀判斷而不做試驗，可能忽略內部鋼絲的脆化或腐蝕裂縫，延誤除濕或補強決策。","textEn":"Applying modern wire strengths overstates the cable's safety factor; judging only by appearance without testing can miss embrittlement or corrosion cracking of inner wires and delay dehumidification or strengthening decisions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「1930 年代鋼絲的強度與延性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Strength and ductility of the 1930s wire\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若評估直接套用現代鋼絲強度，主纜安全係數會被高估；反之若只依外觀判斷而不做試驗，可能忽略內部鋼絲的脆化或腐蝕裂縫，延誤除濕或補強決策。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。"],"optionsEn":["Applying modern wire strengths overstates the cable's safety factor.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若評估直接套用現代鋼絲強度，主纜安全係數會被高估；反之若只依外觀判斷而不做試驗，可能忽略內部鋼絲的脆化或腐蝕裂縫，延誤除濕或補強決策。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying modern wire strengths overstates the cable's safety factor; judging only by appearance without testing can miss embrittlement or corrosion cracking of inner wires and delay dehumidification or strengthening decisions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b015-v13-13","title":"吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「250 對吊索」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “250 pairs of suspenders” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"金門大橋有 250 對豎向吊索，間距 50 ft，每根直徑 2-11/16 in；原吊索於 1972 至 1976 年間全部更換，最後一根於 1976 年 5 月 4 日完成。吊索把橋面荷重傳到索夾與主纜，最脆弱的部位通常是下端錨頭附近：雨水沿吊索流下積聚、海鹽與鋼絲彎曲應力在此疊加。更換吊索時，必須在不中斷交通的情況下以臨時吊具分擔荷重，逐根卸載、拆除與張拉，並控制橋面高程與相鄰吊索的受力變化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「250 對吊索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Golden Gate has 250 pairs of vertical suspender ropes at 50 ft spacing, each 2-11/16 in in diameter; the originals were all replaced between 1972 and 1976, the last on 4 May 1976. Suspenders carry deck load to the cable bands and main cables, and the weakest zone is usually near the lower socket, where rainwater running down the rope collects and salt and wire bending stress combine. Replacing suspenders without stopping traffic means sharing load through temporary hangers, then unloading, removing and tensioning ropes one at a time while controlling deck level and force changes in neighbouring suspenders. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “250 pairs of suspenders” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：每對吊索承擔 50 ft（15.24 m）橋面。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Each pair carries 50 ft (15.24 m) of deck.","failure":"常見誤解：「吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「250 對吊索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “250 pairs of suspenders”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-13-k1","title":"吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換","titleEn":"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement","text":"金門大橋有 250 對豎向吊索，間距 50 ft，每根直徑 2-11/16 in；原吊索於 1972 至 1976 年間全部更換，最後一根於 1976 年 5 月 4 日完成。吊索把橋面荷重傳到索夾與主纜，最脆弱的部位通常是下端錨頭附近：雨水沿吊索流下積聚、海鹽與鋼絲彎曲應力在此疊加。","textEn":"Golden Gate has 250 pairs of vertical suspender ropes at 50 ft spacing, each 2-11/16 in in diameter; the originals were all replaced between 1972 and 1976, the last on 4 May 1976. Suspenders carry deck load to the cable bands and main cables, and the weakest zone is usually near the lower socket, where rainwater running down the rope collects and salt and wire bending stress combine.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement\" is correct?","options":["吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。","金門大橋有 250 對豎向吊索，間距 50 ft，每根直徑 2-11/16 in。","空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。"],"optionsEn":["Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter.","Golden Gate has 250 pairs of vertical suspender ropes at 50 ft spacing, each 2-11/16 in in diameter.","Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"金門大橋有 250 對豎向吊索，間距 50 ft，每根直徑 2-11/16 in；原吊索於 1972 至 1976 年間全部更換，最後一根於 1976 年 5 月 4 日完成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Golden Gate has 250 pairs of vertical suspender ropes at 50 ft spacing, each 2-11/16 in in diameter; the originals were all replaced between 1972 and 1976, the last on 4 May 1976. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b015-v13-14","title":"吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換：定量估算","titleEn":"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「250 對吊索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “250 pairs of suspenders” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：每對吊索承擔 50 ft（15.24 m）橋面。若每側橋面恆載 100 kN/m，每對受力 100×15.24 ≈ 1,524 kN，每根 762 kN。直徑 68.3 mm 鋼索若金屬面積約為毛面積的 60%，A ≈ 0.6×π/4×68.3² ≈ 2,196 mm²，應力 ≈ 347 N/mm²。恆載與填充率為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Each pair carries 50 ft (15.24 m) of deck. With 100 kN/m of dead load per side, a pair carries 100×15.24 ≈ 1,524 kN, or 762 kN per rope. For a 68.3 mm rope with metallic area about 60% of gross, A ≈ 0.6×π/4×68.3² ≈ 2,196 mm², a stress of about 347 N/mm². Dead load and fill factor are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：更換時以千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計量測新舊吊索受力轉移，量測橋面高程變化與相鄰吊索力，確保偏差在容許範圍；完成後以振動法或荷重計抽測吊索力，並以磁通檢測建立新吊索的基準剖面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During replacement measure the force transfer between old and new ropes with jack readings and strain gauges, monitoring deck level and neighbouring forces within tolerance; afterwards spot-check forces by vibration method or load cell and record a magnetic-flux baseline for each new rope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"每對吊索承擔 50 ft（15.24 m）橋面。若每側橋面恆載 100 kN/m，每對受力 100×15.24 ≈ 1,524 kN，每根 762 kN。直徑 68.3 mm 鋼索若金屬面積約為毛面積的 60%，A ≈ 0.6×π/4×68.3² ≈ 2,196 mm²，應力 ≈ 347 N/mm²。恆載與填充率為教學假設。","textEn":"Each pair carries 50 ft (15.24 m) of deck. With 100 kN/m of dead load per side, a pair carries 100×15.24 ≈ 1,524 kN, or 762 kN per rope. For a 68.3 mm rope with metallic area about 60% of gross, A ≈ 0.6×π/4×68.3² ≈ 2,196 mm², a stress of about 347 N/mm². Dead load and fill factor are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement\", which statement holds?","options":["只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。","1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。","每對吊索承擔 50 ft（15.24 m）橋面。"],"optionsEn":["If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems.","Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.","Each pair carries 50 ft (15.24 m) of deck."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每對吊索承擔 50 ft（15.24 m）橋面。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Each pair carries 50 ft (15.24 m) of deck. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b015-v13-15","title":"吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「250 對吊索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “250 pairs of suspenders” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"更換時以千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計量測新舊吊索受力轉移，量測橋面高程變化與相鄰吊索力，確保偏差在容許範圍；完成後以振動法或荷重計抽測吊索力，並以磁通檢測建立新吊索的基準剖面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During replacement measure the force transfer between old and new ropes with jack readings and strain gauges, monitoring deck level and neighbouring forces within tolerance; afterwards spot-check forces by vibration method or load cell and record a magnetic-flux baseline for each new rope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：吊索更換計畫應列出臨時吊具容量、逐根卸載與張拉的停留點、橋面高程允差與停止條件，並由結構工程師現場核可；新吊索要建立可追溯的出廠證明與安裝張力紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: A suspender replacement plan should list temporary hanger capacity, hold points for unloading and tensioning each rope, deck-level tolerance and stop conditions, approved on site by the structural engineer; new ropes need traceable mill certificates and installation tension records.","failure":"注意干擾：下端錨頭附近的腐蝕斷絲常被護套或塗裝遮蔽，若只做目視檢查可能延誤更換；更換時若荷重轉移順序錯誤，相鄰吊索過載或橋面局部下陷，可能造成桁架構件附加應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Broken wires near lower sockets are often hidden under sleeves or paint, so visual inspection alone can delay replacement; a wrong load-transfer order during replacement can overload neighbouring ropes or locally drop the deck, adding stress to truss members. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"更換時以千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計量測新舊吊索受力轉移，量測橋面高程變化與相鄰吊索力，確保偏差在容許範圍；完成後以振動法或荷重計抽測吊索力，並以磁通檢測建立新吊索的基準剖面。","textEn":"During replacement measure the force transfer between old and new ropes with jack readings and strain gauges, monitoring deck level and neighbouring forces within tolerance; afterwards spot-check forces by vibration method or load cell and record a magnetic-flux baseline for each new rope.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"吊索更換計畫應列出臨時吊具容量、逐根卸載與張拉的停留點、橋面高程允差與停止條件，並由結構工程師現場核可；新吊索要建立可追溯的出廠證明與安裝張力紀錄。","textEn":"A suspender replacement plan should list temporary hanger capacity, hold points for unloading and tensioning each rope, deck-level tolerance and stop conditions, approved on site by the structural engineer; new ropes need traceable mill certificates and installation tension records.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement\"?","options":["更換時以千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計量測新舊吊索受力轉移，量測橋面高程變化與相鄰吊索力，確保偏差在容許範圍。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。"],"optionsEn":["During replacement measure the force transfer between old and new ropes with jack readings and strain gauges, monitoring deck level and neighbouring forces within tolerance.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The load on the tower equals the cable tension."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更換時以千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計量測新舊吊索受力轉移，量測橋面高程變化與相鄰吊索力，確保偏差在容許範圍；完成後以振動法或荷重計抽測吊索力，並以磁通檢測建立新吊索的基準剖面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During replacement measure the force transfer between old and new ropes with jack readings and strain gauges, monitoring deck level and neighbouring forces within tolerance; afterwards spot-check forces by vibration method or load cell and record a magnetic-flux baseline for each new rope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b015-v13-16","title":"吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換：失效診斷","titleEn":"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「250 對吊索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “250 pairs of suspenders” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"下端錨頭附近的腐蝕斷絲常被護套或塗裝遮蔽，若只做目視檢查可能延誤更換；更換時若荷重轉移順序錯誤，相鄰吊索過載或橋面局部下陷，可能造成桁架構件附加應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Broken wires near lower sockets are often hidden under sleeves or paint, so visual inspection alone can delay replacement; a wrong load-transfer order during replacement can overload neighbouring ropes or locally drop the deck, adding stress to truss members. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：更換吊索時，必須在不中斷交通的情況下以臨時吊具分擔荷重，逐根卸載、拆除與張拉，並控制橋面高程與相鄰吊索的受力變化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Replacing suspenders without stopping traffic means sharing load through temporary hangers, then unloading, removing and tensioning ropes one at a time while controlling deck level and force changes in neighbouring suspenders.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"下端錨頭附近的腐蝕斷絲常被護套或塗裝遮蔽，若只做目視檢查可能延誤更換；更換時若荷重轉移順序錯誤，相鄰吊索過載或橋面局部下陷，可能造成桁架構件附加應力。","textEn":"Broken wires near lower sockets are often hidden under sleeves or paint, so visual inspection alone can delay replacement; a wrong load-transfer order during replacement can overload neighbouring ropes or locally drop the deck, adding stress to truss members.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吊索受力與 1970 年代全面更換」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Suspender forces and the 1970s full replacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","下端錨頭附近的腐蝕斷絲常被護套或塗裝遮蔽，若只做目視檢查可能延誤更換；更換時若荷重轉移順序錯誤，相鄰吊索過載或橋面局部下陷，可能造成桁架構件附加應力。","空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Broken wires near lower sockets are often hidden under sleeves or paint, so visual inspection alone can delay replacement.","Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"下端錨頭附近的腐蝕斷絲常被護套或塗裝遮蔽，若只做目視檢查可能延誤更換；更換時若荷重轉移順序錯誤，相鄰吊索過載或橋面局部下陷，可能造成桁架構件附加應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Broken wires near lower sockets are often hidden under sleeves or paint, so visual inspection alone can delay replacement; a wrong load-transfer order during replacement can overload neighbouring ropes or locally drop the deck, adding stress to truss members. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":6},{"id":"b015-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算」與「橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress\" and \"Cable rise after the lighter deck\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v13-17","title":"1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Six months and nine days of spinning” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主資料記載金門大橋主纜鋼絲紡線在 6 個月又 9 天內完成，兩條主纜共用約 80,000 mi（約 129,000 km）的鍍鋅鋼絲。空中紡線讓紡線輪沿貓道上方來回運行，每趟把鋼絲環從一座錨碇帶到另一座，在兩端錨碇的索靴上繞回；工人在塔頂與跨中逐根調整鋼絲垂度，使每束鋼絲受力一致。速度受限於紡線輪數量、運行速度、調整垂度所需的時間與風。這個進度數字可以用來回推每天必須鋪設的鋼絲長度與每束完成所需時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Owner data record that wire spinning for the Golden Gate cables was completed in six months and nine days, using about 80,000 mi (about 129,000 km) of galvanised wire for both cables. Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, where it turns around strand shoes; crews at the towers and mid-span adjust wire sag one by one so every wire in a strand carries the same force. Speed is limited by the number of wheels, their travel speed, the time to adjust sag, and wind. The progress figure lets us back-calculate the wire length that had to be laid each day and the time per strand. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Six months and nine days of spinning” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：總長 129,000 km ÷ 190 天 ≈ 679 km/天。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Total 129,000 km ÷ 190 days ≈ 679 km a day.","failure":"常見誤解：「空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Six months and nine days of spinning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-17-k1","title":"1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算","titleEn":"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress","text":"業主資料記載金門大橋主纜鋼絲紡線在 6 個月又 9 天內完成，兩條主纜共用約 80,000 mi（約 129,000 km）的鍍鋅鋼絲。空中紡線讓紡線輪沿貓道上方來回運行，每趟把鋼絲環從一座錨碇帶到另一座，在兩端錨碇的索靴上繞回；工人在塔頂與跨中逐根調整鋼絲垂度，使每束鋼絲受力一致。","textEn":"Owner data record that wire spinning for the Golden Gate cables was completed in six months and nine days, using about 80,000 mi (about 129,000 km) of galvanised wire for both cables. Aerial spinning runs spinning wheels back and forth above the catwalk, each trip carrying a loop of wire from one anchorage to the other, where it turns around strand shoes; crews at the towers and mid-span adjust wire sag one by one so every wire in a strand carries the same force.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress\" is correct?","options":["空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。","把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","業主資料記載金門大橋主纜鋼絲紡線在 6 個月又 9 天內完成，兩條主纜共用約 80,000 mi（約 129,000 km）的鍍鋅鋼絲。"],"optionsEn":["Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run.","A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","Owner data record that wire spinning for the Golden Gate cables was completed in six months and nine days, using about 80,000 mi (about 129,000 km) of galvanised wire for both cables."],"answer":2,"explanation":"業主資料記載金門大橋主纜鋼絲紡線在 6 個月又 9 天內完成，兩條主纜共用約 80,000 mi（約 129,000 km）的鍍鋅鋼絲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Owner data record that wire spinning for the Golden Gate cables was completed in six months and nine days, using about 80,000 mi (about 129,000 km) of galvanised wire for both cables. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"b015-v13-18","title":"1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算：定量估算","titleEn":"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Six months and nine days of spinning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：總長 129,000 km ÷ 190 天 ≈ 679 km/天。單根主纜鋼絲長約 2,332 m，相當於每天約 679,000/2,332 ≈ 291 根全長鋼絲；兩纜共 122 束，平均每束約 190/122 ≈ 1.6 天完成（忽略並行作業）。若因強風停工 20 天，日進度需提高到約 129,000/170 ≈ 759 km/天。工作日假設為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Total 129,000 km ÷ 190 days ≈ 679 km a day. With each cable wire about 2,332 m long, that is about 679,000/2,332 ≈ 291 full-length wires a day; across 122 strands in both cables, about 190/122 ≈ 1.6 days per strand on average (ignoring parallel work). Losing 20 days to wind would require about 129,000/170 ≈ 759 km a day. Working-day assumptions are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：紡線期間每日記錄各紡線輪趟數、完成鋼絲數、停工時間與天氣，並以每束完成後的垂度量測確認品質；進度曲線與計畫比較，落後時優先檢討停工原因而不是縮短垂度調整時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During spinning log trips per wheel, wires completed, downtime and weather daily, confirming quality by sag survey after each strand; compare the progress curve with the plan and, when behind, examine causes of downtime first rather than shortening sag adjustment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"總長 129,000 km ÷ 190 天 ≈ 679 km/天。單根主纜鋼絲長約 2,332 m，相當於每天約 679,000/2,332 ≈ 291 根全長鋼絲；兩纜共 122 束，平均每束約 190/122 ≈ 1.6 天完成（忽略並行作業）。若因強風停工 20 天，日進度需提高到約 129,000/170 ≈ 759 km/天。工作日假設為教學假設。","textEn":"Total 129,000 km ÷ 190 days ≈ 679 km a day. With each cable wire about 2,332 m long, that is about 679,000/2,332 ≈ 291 full-length wires a day; across 122 strands in both cables, about 190/122 ≈ 1.6 days per strand on average (ignoring parallel work). Losing 20 days to wind would require about 129,000/170 ≈ 759 km a day. Working-day assumptions are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress\", which statement holds?","options":["總長 129,000 km ÷ 190 天 ≈ 679 km/天。","螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。","防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Total 129,000 km ÷ 190 days ≈ 679 km a day.","Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever.","The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總長 129,000 km ÷ 190 天 ≈ 679 km/天。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Total 129,000 km ÷ 190 days ≈ 679 km a day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"b015-v13-19","title":"1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Six months and nine days of spinning” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"紡線期間每日記錄各紡線輪趟數、完成鋼絲數、停工時間與天氣，並以每束完成後的垂度量測確認品質；進度曲線與計畫比較，落後時優先檢討停工原因而不是縮短垂度調整時間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During spinning log trips per wheel, wires completed, downtime and weather daily, confirming quality by sag survey after each strand; compare the progress curve with the plan and, when behind, examine causes of downtime first rather than shortening sag adjustment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：紡線施工規範要寫明每束垂度允差、量測時段與溫度修正，以及停工風速；進度壓力下任何放寬品質門檻的提議都必須經設計者書面核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The spinning specification should state sag tolerance per strand, survey windows and temperature correction, and the stop-work wind speed; any proposal to relax quality thresholds under schedule pressure needs the designer's written approval.","failure":"注意干擾：為追趕進度而縮短垂度調整，會讓同一束鋼絲受力不均，壓擠後產生鬆弛絲，長期影響主纜耐久與索夾夾緊；強風中強行紡線則可能使鋼絲纏繞或斷裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cutting sag adjustment to catch up leaves uneven forces in a strand and slack wires after compaction, harming long-term durability and cable-band grip; spinning in strong wind can tangle or break wires. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"紡線期間每日記錄各紡線輪趟數、完成鋼絲數、停工時間與天氣，並以每束完成後的垂度量測確認品質；進度曲線與計畫比較，落後時優先檢討停工原因而不是縮短垂度調整時間。","textEn":"During spinning log trips per wheel, wires completed, downtime and weather daily, confirming quality by sag survey after each strand; compare the progress curve with the plan and, when behind, examine causes of downtime first rather than shortening sag adjustment.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"紡線施工規範要寫明每束垂度允差、量測時段與溫度修正，以及停工風速；進度壓力下任何放寬品質門檻的提議都必須經設計者書面核可。","textEn":"The spinning specification should state sag tolerance per strand, survey windows and temperature correction, and the stop-work wind speed; any proposal to relax quality thresholds under schedule pressure needs the designer's written approval.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","紡線期間每日記錄各紡線輪趟數、完成鋼絲數、停工時間與天氣，並以每束完成後的垂度量測確認品質；進度曲線與計畫比較，落後時優先檢討停工原因而不是縮短垂度調整時間。","懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","During spinning log trips per wheel, wires completed, downtime and weather daily, confirming quality by sag survey after each strand.","A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"紡線期間每日記錄各紡線輪趟數、完成鋼絲數、停工時間與天氣，並以每束完成後的垂度量測確認品質；進度曲線與計畫比較，落後時優先檢討停工原因而不是縮短垂度調整時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During spinning log trips per wheel, wires completed, downtime and weather daily, confirming quality by sag survey after each strand; compare the progress curve with the plan and, when behind, examine causes of downtime first rather than shortening sag adjustment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"b015-v13-20","title":"1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「6 個月又 9 天的紡線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Six months and nine days of spinning” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為追趕進度而縮短垂度調整，會讓同一束鋼絲受力不均，壓擠後產生鬆弛絲，長期影響主纜耐久與索夾夾緊；強風中強行紡線則可能使鋼絲纏繞或斷裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cutting sag adjustment to catch up leaves uneven forces in a strand and slack wires after compaction, harming long-term durability and cable-band grip; spinning in strong wind can tangle or break wires. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這個進度數字可以用來回推每天必須鋪設的鋼絲長度與每束完成所需時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The progress figure lets us back-calculate the wire length that had to be laid each day and the time per strand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為追趕進度而縮短垂度調整，會讓同一束鋼絲受力不均，壓擠後產生鬆弛絲，長期影響主纜耐久與索夾夾緊；強風中強行紡線則可能使鋼絲纏繞或斷裂。","textEn":"Cutting sag adjustment to catch up leaves uneven forces in a strand and slack wires after compaction, harming long-term durability and cable-band grip; spinning in strong wind can tangle or break wires.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「1930 年代空中紡線的進度估算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Estimating 1930s aerial-spinning progress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","為追趕進度而縮短垂度調整，會讓同一束鋼絲受力不均，壓擠後產生鬆弛絲，長期影響主纜耐久與索夾夾緊；強風中強行紡線則可能使鋼絲纏繞或斷裂。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","Cutting sag adjustment to catch up leaves uneven forces in a strand and slack wires after compaction, harming long-term durability and cable-band grip."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為追趕進度而縮短垂度調整，會讓同一束鋼絲受力不均，壓擠後產生鬆弛絲，長期影響主纜耐久與索夾夾緊；強風中強行紡線則可能使鋼絲纏繞或斷裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cutting sag adjustment to catch up leaves uneven forces in a strand and slack wires after compaction, harming long-term durability and cable-band grip; spinning in strong wind can tangle or break wires. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"b015-v13-21","title":"橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cable rise after the lighter deck: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"1980 年代金門大橋把原有鋼筋混凝土橋面與縱梁更換為正交異性鋼橋面，業主資料記載重量減少約 12,300 噸，相當於每延英尺約 1.37 噸。施工多在夜間分段進行，每天早上恢復通車。橋面變輕後主纜張力下降、彈性伸長減少，主跨垂度隨之變小，橋面整體抬升；同時塔頂索鞍兩側的平衡改變，塔頂可能朝邊跨方向移動。因此更換順序必須控制左右對稱與跨間平衡，並預先計算完工後的路面縱斷面與伸縮縫位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In the 1980s the original reinforced-concrete deck and stringers were replaced with an orthotropic steel deck; owner data record a weight reduction of about 12,300 tons, about 1.37 tons per lineal foot. Work was done mostly at night in sections, reopening to traffic each morning. A lighter deck lowers cable tension and elastic stretch, so main-span sag decreases and the deck rises; the balance on either side of the tower saddles also changes and tower tops may move toward the side spans. The replacement sequence therefore had to control symmetry and balance between spans, and the final road profile and joint positions had to be predicted in advance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Δw = 1.37 short ton/ft ≈ 40 kN/m（兩纜合計）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Δw = 1.37 short tons/ft ≈ 40 kN/m for both cables.","failure":"常見誤解：「把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-21-k1","title":"橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升","titleEn":"Cable rise after the lighter deck","text":"1980 年代金門大橋把原有鋼筋混凝土橋面與縱梁更換為正交異性鋼橋面，業主資料記載重量減少約 12,300 噸，相當於每延英尺約 1.37 噸。施工多在夜間分段進行，每天早上恢復通車。","textEn":"In the 1980s the original reinforced-concrete deck and stringers were replaced with an orthotropic steel deck; owner data record a weight reduction of about 12,300 tons, about 1.37 tons per lineal foot. Work was done mostly at night in sections, reopening to traffic each morning.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cable rise after the lighter deck\" is correct?","options":["1980 年代金門大橋把原有鋼筋混凝土橋面與縱梁更換為正交異性鋼橋面，業主資料記載重量減少約 12,300 噸，相當於每延英尺約 1.37 噸。","把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。"],"optionsEn":["In the 1980s the original reinforced-concrete deck and stringers were replaced with an orthotropic steel deck.","A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"1980 年代金門大橋把原有鋼筋混凝土橋面與縱梁更換為正交異性鋼橋面，業主資料記載重量減少約 12,300 噸，相當於每延英尺約 1.37 噸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In the 1980s the original reinforced-concrete deck and stringers were replaced with an orthotropic steel deck; owner data record a weight reduction of about 12,300 tons, about 1.37 tons per lineal foot. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"b015-v13-22","title":"橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升：定量估算","titleEn":"Cable rise after the lighter deck: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Δw = 1.37 short ton/ft ≈ 40 kN/m（兩纜合計）。取 f = 142 m：ΔH = Δw·l²/(8f) = 40×1,280²/(8×142) ≈ 57,700 kN，每纜 28.8 MN；主跨主纜縮短 ΔS ≈ 28.8×10⁶×1,320/(2×10¹¹×0.515) ≈ 0.37 m；Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS ≈ 1.69×0.37 ≈ 0.62 m 抬升。垂度、E 與纜長為教學假設，忽略塔頂位移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Δw = 1.37 short tons/ft ≈ 40 kN/m for both cables. With f = 142 m: ΔH = Δw·l²/(8f) = 40×1,280²/(8×142) ≈ 57,700 kN, or 28.8 MN per cable; the main-span cable shortens by ΔS ≈ 28.8×10⁶×1,320/(2×10¹¹×0.515) ≈ 0.37 m, and Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS ≈ 1.69×0.37 ≈ 0.62 m of rise. Sag, E and cable length are teaching assumptions; tower-top movement is ignored. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每一施工段完成後量測橋面高程、塔頂位移與主纜垂度，並與分段更換分析比較；全部完成後重新測量路面縱斷面、伸縮縫開口與吊索力，更新恆載履歷與結構模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each section measure deck levels, tower-top movement and cable sag against the staged-replacement analysis; at completion re-survey the road profile, joint openings and suspender forces, updating the dead-load history and structural model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Δw = 1.37 short ton/ft ≈ 40 kN/m（兩纜合計）。取 f = 142 m：ΔH = Δw·l²/(8f) = 40×1,280²/(8×142) ≈ 57,700 kN，每纜 28.8 MN；主跨主纜縮短 ΔS ≈ 28.8×10⁶×1,320/(2×10¹¹×0.515) ≈ 0.37 m；Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS ≈ 1.69×0.37 ≈ 0.62 m 抬升。垂度、E 與纜長為教學假設，忽略塔頂位移。","textEn":"Δw = 1.37 short tons/ft ≈ 40 kN/m for both cables. With f = 142 m: ΔH = Δw·l²/(8f) = 40×1,280²/(8×142) ≈ 57,700 kN, or 28.8 MN per cable; the main-span cable shortens by ΔS ≈ 28.8×10⁶×1,320/(2×10¹¹×0.515) ≈ 0.37 m, and Δf = (3l/(16f))·ΔS ≈ 1.69×0.37 ≈ 0.62 m of rise. Sag, E and cable length are teaching assumptions; tower-top movement is ignored.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cable rise after the lighter deck\", which statement holds?","options":["1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。","Δw = 1.37 short ton/ft ≈ 40 kN/m（兩纜合計）。","塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。"],"optionsEn":["Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.","Δw = 1.37 short tons/ft ≈ 40 kN/m for both cables.","The load on the tower equals the cable tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Δw = 1.37 short ton/ft ≈ 40 kN/m（兩纜合計）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Δw = 1.37 short tons/ft ≈ 40 kN/m for both cables. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"b015-v13-23","title":"橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cable rise after the lighter deck: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每一施工段完成後量測橋面高程、塔頂位移與主纜垂度，並與分段更換分析比較；全部完成後重新測量路面縱斷面、伸縮縫開口與吊索力，更新恆載履歷與結構模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each section measure deck levels, tower-top movement and cable sag against the staged-replacement analysis; at completion re-survey the road profile, joint openings and suspender forces, updating the dead-load history and structural model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：大規模恆載改變的工程，應事先完成分段施工分析、列出每階段允許的不平衡重量與幾何監測點，並在每夜施工結束時核對量測值；超出觸發值即停止下一段，由設計者評估後才繼續。","observationEn":"Site practice: Major dead-load changes require a staged analysis listing the allowable unbalanced weight and geometric checkpoints for each stage, with readings checked at the end of every night shift; exceeding a trigger stops the next section until the designer has assessed it.","failure":"注意干擾：若更換不對稱推進，單側或單跨減重過多，塔頂索鞍兩側張力差增大，塔身彎矩與伸縮縫偏位可能超限；未預先調整路面高程則完工後出現縱斷面不平順與排水問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Asymmetric progress that lightens one side or span too much increases the tension difference across the saddles, possibly overstressing tower bending and shifting joints beyond limits; failing to plan road levels leaves an uneven profile and drainage problems after completion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每一施工段完成後量測橋面高程、塔頂位移與主纜垂度，並與分段更換分析比較；全部完成後重新測量路面縱斷面、伸縮縫開口與吊索力，更新恆載履歷與結構模型。","textEn":"After each section measure deck levels, tower-top movement and cable sag against the staged-replacement analysis; at completion re-survey the road profile, joint openings and suspender forces, updating the dead-load history and structural model.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"大規模恆載改變的工程，應事先完成分段施工分析、列出每階段允許的不平衡重量與幾何監測點，並在每夜施工結束時核對量測值；超出觸發值即停止下一段，由設計者評估後才繼續。","textEn":"Major dead-load changes require a staged analysis listing the allowable unbalanced weight and geometric checkpoints for each stage, with readings checked at the end of every night shift; exceeding a trigger stops the next section until the designer has assessed it.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cable rise after the lighter deck\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。","每一施工段完成後量測橋面高程、塔頂位移與主纜垂度，並與分段更換分析比較；全部完成後重新測量路面縱斷面、伸縮縫開口與吊索力，更新恆載履歷與結構模型。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.","After each section measure deck levels, tower-top movement and cable sag against the staged-replacement analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每一施工段完成後量測橋面高程、塔頂位移與主纜垂度，並與分段更換分析比較；全部完成後重新測量路面縱斷面、伸縮縫開口與吊索力，更新恆載履歷與結構模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each section measure deck levels, tower-top movement and cable sag against the staged-replacement analysis; at completion re-survey the road profile, joint openings and suspender forces, updating the dead-load history and structural model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"b015-v13-24","title":"橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cable rise after the lighter deck: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「1986 年橋面減重 12,300 噸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “1986 deck lightening of 12,300 tons” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若更換不對稱推進，單側或單跨減重過多，塔頂索鞍兩側張力差增大，塔身彎矩與伸縮縫偏位可能超限；未預先調整路面高程則完工後出現縱斷面不平順與排水問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Asymmetric progress that lightens one side or span too much increases the tension difference across the saddles, possibly overstressing tower bending and shifting joints beyond limits; failing to plan road levels leaves an uneven profile and drainage problems after completion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此更換順序必須控制左右對稱與跨間平衡，並預先計算完工後的路面縱斷面與伸縮縫位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The replacement sequence therefore had to control symmetry and balance between spans, and the final road profile and joint positions had to be predicted in advance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若更換不對稱推進，單側或單跨減重過多，塔頂索鞍兩側張力差增大，塔身彎矩與伸縮縫偏位可能超限；未預先調整路面高程則完工後出現縱斷面不平順與排水問題。","textEn":"Asymmetric progress that lightens one side or span too much increases the tension difference across the saddles, possibly overstressing tower bending and shifting joints beyond limits; failing to plan road levels leaves an uneven profile and drainage problems after completion.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋面更換減重後的主纜抬升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cable rise after the lighter deck\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若更換不對稱推進，單側或單跨減重過多，塔頂索鞍兩側張力差增大，塔身彎矩與伸縮縫偏位可能超限；未預先調整路面高程則完工後出現縱斷面不平順與排水問題。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。"],"optionsEn":["Asymmetric progress that lightens one side or span too much increases the tension difference across the saddles, possibly overstressing tower bending and shifting joints beyond limits.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若更換不對稱推進，單側或單跨減重過多，塔頂索鞍兩側張力差增大，塔身彎矩與伸縮縫偏位可能超限；未預先調整路面高程則完工後出現縱斷面不平順與排水問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric progress that lightens one side or span too much increases the tension difference across the saddles, possibly overstressing tower bending and shifting joints beyond limits; failing to plan road levels leaves an uneven profile and drainage problems after completion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":7},{"id":"b015-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗」與「索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing\" and \"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v13-25","title":"抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “West railing slat tones” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"為了讓金門大橋在持續 100 mph 的風中保持結構完整，並承擔新增防墜網帶來的風阻，抗風改造把兩塔之間的西側人行道欄杆換成較透風的細長直立鋼條，並在人行道下方的桁架加裝整流板。2020 年春天起，強風中出現明顯的鳴聲：風以某些角度穿過鋼條時，渦流脫落頻率與鋼條或條間空氣的自然振動吻合。業主公布兩種音調：西風垂直吹向欄杆且達 22 mph 以上時約 280 至 700 Hz，風以小角度吹來且達 27 mph 以上時約 1.1 kHz。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"To keep the Golden Gate structurally sound in sustained winds up to 100 mph and to carry the extra wind resistance of the new deterrent net, the wind retrofit replaced the west sidewalk railing between the towers with thin vertical slats that let more air through, and added a wind fairing on the truss below the sidewalk. From spring 2020 a distinct tone was heard in strong wind: as wind passed through the slats at certain angles, the vortex-shedding frequency matched the natural vibration of the slats or of the air between them. The owner reports two tones: about 280 to 700 Hz with west wind perpendicular to the railing at 22 mph or more, and about 1.1 kHz with wind at a slight angle at 27 mph or more. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “West railing slat tones” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：渦流脫落 f = St·U/d。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Vortex shedding f = St·U/d.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “West railing slat tones”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-25-k1","title":"抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing","text":"為了讓金門大橋在持續 100 mph 的風中保持結構完整，並承擔新增防墜網帶來的風阻，抗風改造把兩塔之間的西側人行道欄杆換成較透風的細長直立鋼條，並在人行道下方的桁架加裝整流板。2020 年春天起，強風中出現明顯的鳴聲：風以某些角度穿過鋼條時，渦流脫落頻率與鋼條或條間空氣的自然振動吻合。","textEn":"To keep the Golden Gate structurally sound in sustained winds up to 100 mph and to carry the extra wind resistance of the new deterrent net, the wind retrofit replaced the west sidewalk railing between the towers with thin vertical slats that let more air through, and added a wind fairing on the truss below the sidewalk. From spring 2020 a distinct tone was heard in strong wind: as wind passed through the slats at certain angles, the vortex-shedding frequency matched the natural vibration of the slats or of the air between them.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing\" is correct?","options":["只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。","為了讓金門大橋在持續 100 mph 的風中保持結構完整，並承擔新增防墜網帶來的風阻，抗風改造把兩塔之間的西側人行道欄杆換成較透風的細長直立鋼條，並在人行道下方的桁架加裝整流板。","螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。"],"optionsEn":["If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems.","To keep the Golden Gate structurally sound in sustained winds up to 100 mph and to carry the extra wind resistance of the new deterrent net, the wind retrofit replaced the west sidewalk railing between the towers with thin vertical slats that let more air through, and added a wind fairing on the truss below the sidewalk.","Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為了讓金門大橋在持續 100 mph 的風中保持結構完整，並承擔新增防墜網帶來的風阻，抗風改造把兩塔之間的西側人行道欄杆換成較透風的細長直立鋼條，並在人行道下方的桁架加裝整流板。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"To keep the Golden Gate structurally sound in sustained winds up to 100 mph and to carry the extra wind resistance of the new deterrent net, the wind retrofit replaced the west sidewalk railing between the towers with thin vertical slats that let more air through, and added a wind fairing on the truss below the sidewalk. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"b015-v13-26","title":"抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “West railing slat tones” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：渦流脫落 f = St·U/d。U = 22 mph ≈ 9.8 m/s、f = 280 Hz、St = 0.2 時，對應特徵尺寸 d = St·U/f ≈ 0.2×9.8/280 ≈ 7.0 mm；27 mph（12.1 m/s）、1.1 kHz 則 d ≈ 2.2 mm，暗示高音調來自不同的流動特徵（例如邊緣或條間間隙）。St 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Vortex shedding f = St·U/d. With U = 22 mph ≈ 9.8 m/s, f = 280 Hz and St = 0.2, the implied characteristic size is d = St·U/f ≈ 0.2×9.8/280 ≈ 7.0 mm; 27 mph (12.1 m/s) at 1.1 kHz gives d ≈ 2.2 mm, suggesting the higher tone comes from a different flow feature such as an edge or the gap between slats. St is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：業主自 2020 年秋以足尺欄杆模型做風洞試驗，比較橫桿、粗糙膠帶、U 形夾、紋理塗料與填頂等方案，最後以附薄橡膠墊的 U 形夾在 110 種風速與風向組合中消除或大幅降低聲音；剩餘情境預估每年平均約 70 小時與 18 小時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: From autumn 2020 the owner tested a full-scale railing model in a wind tunnel, comparing horizontal bars, coarse tape, U-shaped clips, textured paint and top fillers; U-shaped clips with a thin rubber insert eliminated or greatly reduced sound across 110 wind speed and direction combinations, with the remaining cases expected for about 70 and 18 hours a year on average.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"渦流脫落 f = St·U/d。U = 22 mph ≈ 9.8 m/s、f = 280 Hz、St = 0.2 時，對應特徵尺寸 d = St·U/f ≈ 0.2×9.8/280 ≈ 7.0 mm；27 mph（12.1 m/s）、1.1 kHz 則 d ≈ 2.2 mm，暗示高音調來自不同的流動特徵（例如邊緣或條間間隙）。St 為教學假設。","textEn":"Vortex shedding f = St·U/d. With U = 22 mph ≈ 9.8 m/s, f = 280 Hz and St = 0.2, the implied characteristic size is d = St·U/f ≈ 0.2×9.8/280 ≈ 7.0 mm; 27 mph (12.1 m/s) at 1.1 kHz gives d ≈ 2.2 mm, suggesting the higher tone comes from a different flow feature such as an edge or the gap between slats. St is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing\", which statement holds?","options":["防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。","懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。","渦流脫落 f = St·U/d。"],"optionsEn":["The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability.","A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load.","Vortex shedding f = St·U/d."],"answer":2,"explanation":"渦流脫落 f = St·U/d。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Vortex shedding f = St·U/d. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"b015-v13-27","title":"抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “West railing slat tones” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"業主自 2020 年秋以足尺欄杆模型做風洞試驗，比較橫桿、粗糙膠帶、U 形夾、紋理塗料與填頂等方案，最後以附薄橡膠墊的 U 形夾在 110 種風速與風向組合中消除或大幅降低聲音；剩餘情境預估每年平均約 70 小時與 18 小時。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"From autumn 2020 the owner tested a full-scale railing model in a wind tunnel, comparing horizontal bars, coarse tape, U-shaped clips, textured paint and top fillers; U-shaped clips with a thin rubber insert eliminated or greatly reduced sound across 110 wind speed and direction combinations, with the remaining cases expected for about 70 and 18 hours a year on average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：改變橋面細部的工程，風洞試驗範圍應包含局部構件的渦振與聲學，並在合約中訂出可接受的聲音與振動準則；改善措施（例如 12,000 根鋼條的夾具）須有安裝品質抽查與維修計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: For work that changes deck details, wind-tunnel scope should include local vortex shedding and acoustics, with acceptable sound and vibration criteria in the contract; remedies such as clips on 12,000 slats need installation sampling and a maintenance plan.","failure":"注意干擾：若改造只檢核結構氣動穩定而未評估聲學與局部渦振，細長構件可能在常見風速下鳴響並承受高頻應力循環；高頻振動長期也可能使鋼條銲道或螺栓疲勞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only global aerodynamic stability without assessing acoustics and local vortex shedding can leave slender parts singing at common wind speeds and seeing high-frequency stress cycles, which over time can fatigue slat welds or bolts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"業主自 2020 年秋以足尺欄杆模型做風洞試驗，比較橫桿、粗糙膠帶、U 形夾、紋理塗料與填頂等方案，最後以附薄橡膠墊的 U 形夾在 110 種風速與風向組合中消除或大幅降低聲音；剩餘情境預估每年平均約 70 小時與 18 小時。","textEn":"From autumn 2020 the owner tested a full-scale railing model in a wind tunnel, comparing horizontal bars, coarse tape, U-shaped clips, textured paint and top fillers; U-shaped clips with a thin rubber insert eliminated or greatly reduced sound across 110 wind speed and direction combinations, with the remaining cases expected for about 70 and 18 hours a year on average.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"改變橋面細部的工程，風洞試驗範圍應包含局部構件的渦振與聲學，並在合約中訂出可接受的聲音與振動準則；改善措施（例如 12,000 根鋼條的夾具）須有安裝品質抽查與維修計畫。","textEn":"For work that changes deck details, wind-tunnel scope should include local vortex shedding and acoustics, with acceptable sound and vibration criteria in the contract; remedies such as clips on 12,000 slats need installation sampling and a maintenance plan.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing\"?","options":["業主自 2020 年秋以足尺欄杆模型做風洞試驗，比較橫桿、粗糙膠帶、U 形夾、紋理塗料與填頂等方案，最後以附薄橡膠墊的 U 形夾在 110 種風速與風向組合中消除或大幅降低聲音。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。"],"optionsEn":["From autumn 2020 the owner tested a full-scale railing model in a wind tunnel, comparing horizontal bars, coarse tape, U-shaped clips, textured paint and top fillers.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"業主自 2020 年秋以足尺欄杆模型做風洞試驗，比較橫桿、粗糙膠帶、U 形夾、紋理塗料與填頂等方案，最後以附薄橡膠墊的 U 形夾在 110 種風速與風向組合中消除或大幅降低聲音；剩餘情境預估每年平均約 70 小時與 18 小時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"From autumn 2020 the owner tested a full-scale railing model in a wind tunnel, comparing horizontal bars, coarse tape, U-shaped clips, textured paint and top fillers; U-shaped clips with a thin rubber insert eliminated or greatly reduced sound across 110 wind speed and direction combinations, with the remaining cases expected for about 70 and 18 hours a year on average. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"b015-v13-28","title":"抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「西側欄杆鋼條風鳴」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “West railing slat tones” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若改造只檢核結構氣動穩定而未評估聲學與局部渦振，細長構件可能在常見風速下鳴響並承受高頻應力循環；高頻振動長期也可能使鋼條銲道或螺栓疲勞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only global aerodynamic stability without assessing acoustics and local vortex shedding can leave slender parts singing at common wind speeds and seeing high-frequency stress cycles, which over time can fatigue slat welds or bolts. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：業主公布兩種音調：西風垂直吹向欄杆且達 22 mph 以上時約 280 至 700 Hz，風以小角度吹來且達 27 mph 以上時約 1.1 kHz。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The owner reports two tones: about 280 to 700 Hz with west wind perpendicular to the railing at 22 mph or more, and about 1.1 kHz with wind at a slight angle at 27 mph or more.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若改造只檢核結構氣動穩定而未評估聲學與局部渦振，細長構件可能在常見風速下鳴響並承受高頻應力循環；高頻振動長期也可能使鋼條銲道或螺栓疲勞。","textEn":"Checking only global aerodynamic stability without assessing acoustics and local vortex shedding can leave slender parts singing at common wind speeds and seeing high-frequency stress cycles, which over time can fatigue slat welds or bolts.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「抗風改造欄杆的風鳴試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind-tunnel tests of the singing retrofit railing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若改造只檢核結構氣動穩定而未評估聲學與局部渦振，細長構件可能在常見風速下鳴響並承受高頻應力循環；高頻振動長期也可能使鋼條銲道或螺栓疲勞。","螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Checking only global aerodynamic stability without assessing acoustics and local vortex shedding can leave slender parts singing at common wind speeds and seeing high-frequency stress cycles, which over time can fatigue slat welds or bolts.","Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若改造只檢核結構氣動穩定而未評估聲學與局部渦振，細長構件可能在常見風速下鳴響並承受高頻應力循環；高頻振動長期也可能使鋼條銲道或螺栓疲勞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only global aerodynamic stability without assessing acoustics and local vortex shedding can leave slender parts singing at common wind speeds and seeing high-frequency stress cycles, which over time can fatigue slat welds or bolts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"b015-v13-29","title":"索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「索夾螺栓預力」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cable-band bolt preload” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"索夾靠螺栓夾緊主纜，以摩擦力抵抗吊索力沿主纜方向的下滑分量。業主資料記載，1953 至 1954 年增設下層橫向斜撐時發現索夾螺栓最多損失了規定張力的 50%，1954 年重新張拉，1970 年代再張拉至 90,000 lb；1999 年做過張力檢查，2000 至 2001 年把 256 根直徑 2⅛ in、長 3 ft 的繫固螺栓再張拉至 92,000 lb。預力流失的主因是主纜鋼絲在夾壓下逐漸重新排列與壓密、鍍鋅層潛變，以及溫度循環；螺栓伸長量只有零點幾毫米，因此很小的直徑變化就能吃掉大半預力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「索夾螺栓預力」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cable bands grip the main cable by bolt clamping, using friction to resist the component of suspender force acting down the cable slope. Owner data record that when the lower lateral bracing was added in 1953–1954, cable-band bolts were found to have lost as much as 50% of their specified tension; they were re-tensioned in 1954, again to 90,000 lb in the 1970s, checked in 1999, and in 2000–2001 the 256 tie-down bolts, each 2⅛ in in diameter and 3 ft long, were re-tensioned to 92,000 lb. Preload is lost mainly as cable wires rearrange and compact under clamping, as zinc creeps and through thermal cycles; bolt elongation is only fractions of a millimetre, so a tiny diameter change can consume most of the preload. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cable-band bolt preload” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN，2⅛ in 螺栓毛面積 ≈ 2,288 mm²，應力 ≈ 175 N/mm²；夾緊長度取 0.6 m，彈性伸長 = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: 90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN; a 2⅛ in bolt has a gross area ≈ 2,288 mm², a stress ≈ 175 N/mm²; with a 0.6 m grip the elastic elongation = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm, so just 0.26 mm of cable compaction under the band loses about 50% of preload.","failure":"常見誤解：「螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「索夾螺栓預力」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cable-band bolt preload”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-29-k1","title":"索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉","titleEn":"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning","text":"索夾靠螺栓夾緊主纜，以摩擦力抵抗吊索力沿主纜方向的下滑分量。業主資料記載，1953 至 1954 年增設下層橫向斜撐時發現索夾螺栓最多損失了規定張力的 50%，1954 年重新張拉，1970 年代再張拉至 90,000 lb；1999 年做過張力檢查，2000 至 2001 年把 256 根直徑 2⅛ in、長 3 ft 的繫固螺栓再張拉至 92,000 lb。","textEn":"Cable bands grip the main cable by bolt clamping, using friction to resist the component of suspender force acting down the cable slope. Owner data record that when the lower lateral bracing was added in 1953–1954, cable-band bolts were found to have lost as much as 50% of their specified tension; they were re-tensioned in 1954, again to 90,000 lb in the 1970s, checked in 1999, and in 2000–2001 the 256 tie-down bolts, each 2⅛ in in diameter and 3 ft long, were re-tensioned to 92,000 lb.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning\" is correct?","options":["螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。","1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。","索夾靠螺栓夾緊主纜，以摩擦力抵抗吊索力沿主纜方向的下滑分量。"],"optionsEn":["Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever.","Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.","Cable bands grip the main cable by bolt clamping, using friction to resist the component of suspender force acting down the cable slope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"索夾靠螺栓夾緊主纜，以摩擦力抵抗吊索力沿主纜方向的下滑分量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cable bands grip the main cable by bolt clamping, using friction to resist the component of suspender force acting down the cable slope. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"b015-v13-30","title":"索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉：定量估算","titleEn":"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「索夾螺栓預力」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cable-band bolt preload” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN，2⅛ in 螺栓毛面積 ≈ 2,288 mm²，應力 ≈ 175 N/mm²；夾緊長度取 0.6 m，彈性伸長 = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm。只要主纜在索夾處壓密約 0.26 mm，預力即損失約 50%。3 ft 長、92,000 lb 的繫固螺栓伸長約 179×914/200,000 ≈ 0.82 mm。夾緊長度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: 90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN; a 2⅛ in bolt has a gross area ≈ 2,288 mm², a stress ≈ 175 N/mm²; with a 0.6 m grip the elastic elongation = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm, so just 0.26 mm of cable compaction under the band loses about 50% of preload. A 3 ft tie-down bolt at 92,000 lb stretches about 179×914/200,000 ≈ 0.82 mm. The grip length is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以超音波量測螺栓伸長或以液壓張拉器做起始脫離（lift-off）試驗求現有預力，抽樣範圍涵蓋不同跨段與坡度；再張拉後記錄每根螺栓的目標值與實際值，數年後複測以求預力流失曲線，並檢查索夾是否有滑移痕跡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure existing preload by ultrasonic bolt elongation or hydraulic lift-off tests on a sample covering different spans and slopes; after re-tensioning record target and achieved values for each bolt, re-test after some years to derive the preload-loss curve, and inspect bands for slip marks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN，2⅛ in 螺栓毛面積 ≈ 2,288 mm²，應力 ≈ 175 N/mm²；夾緊長度取 0.6 m，彈性伸長 = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm。只要主纜在索夾處壓密約 0.26 mm，預力即損失約 50%。3 ft 長、92,000 lb 的繫固螺栓伸長約 179×914/200,000 ≈ 0.82 mm。夾緊長度為教學假設。","textEn":"90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN; a 2⅛ in bolt has a gross area ≈ 2,288 mm², a stress ≈ 175 N/mm²; with a 0.6 m grip the elastic elongation = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm, so just 0.26 mm of cable compaction under the band loses about 50% of preload. A 3 ft tie-down bolt at 92,000 lb stretches about 179×914/200,000 ≈ 0.82 mm. The grip length is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning\", which statement holds?","options":["90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN，2⅛ in 螺栓毛面積 ≈ 2,288 mm²，應力 ≈ 175 N/mm²。","塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。","老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。"],"optionsEn":["90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN.","The load on the tower equals the cable tension.","Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless."],"answer":0,"explanation":"90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN，2⅛ in 螺栓毛面積 ≈ 2,288 mm²，應力 ≈ 175 N/mm²；夾緊長度取 0.6 m，彈性伸長 = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"90,000 lb ≈ 400 kN; a 2⅛ in bolt has a gross area ≈ 2,288 mm², a stress ≈ 175 N/mm²; with a 0.6 m grip the elastic elongation = 175×600/200,000 ≈ 0.52 mm, so just 0.26 mm of cable compaction under the band loses about 50% of preload. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"b015-v13-31","title":"索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「索夾螺栓預力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cable-band bolt preload” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以超音波量測螺栓伸長或以液壓張拉器做起始脫離（lift-off）試驗求現有預力，抽樣範圍涵蓋不同跨段與坡度；再張拉後記錄每根螺栓的目標值與實際值，數年後複測以求預力流失曲線，並檢查索夾是否有滑移痕跡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure existing preload by ultrasonic bolt elongation or hydraulic lift-off tests on a sample covering different spans and slopes; after re-tensioning record target and achieved values for each bolt, re-test after some years to derive the preload-loss curve, and inspect bands for slip marks. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：索夾螺栓應列入定期抽測的檢查項目，訂出觸發全面再張拉的預力門檻；任何會增加吊索力或改變主纜壓密狀態的工程（加撐、換橋面、除濕包覆）完成後，都要安排一次螺栓預力複測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make cable-band bolts a periodic sampling item with a preload threshold that triggers full re-tensioning; after any work that raises suspender forces or changes cable compaction, such as bracing, deck replacement or dehumidification wrapping, schedule a preload re-check.","failure":"注意干擾：預力流失到摩擦力不足時，陡坡段的索夾會沿主纜下滑，吊索偏斜、索夾邊緣刮傷鋼絲並破壞防護包覆，水分隨之進入主纜；滑移也會改變吊索長度分配與橋面線形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: When preload falls until friction is inadequate, bands on steep cable slopes slide down, tilting suspenders, scoring wires at band edges and breaking the wrapping so water enters the cable; slip also redistributes suspender lengths and alters the deck profile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以超音波量測螺栓伸長或以液壓張拉器做起始脫離（lift-off）試驗求現有預力，抽樣範圍涵蓋不同跨段與坡度；再張拉後記錄每根螺栓的目標值與實際值，數年後複測以求預力流失曲線，並檢查索夾是否有滑移痕跡。","textEn":"Measure existing preload by ultrasonic bolt elongation or hydraulic lift-off tests on a sample covering different spans and slopes; after re-tensioning record target and achieved values for each bolt, re-test after some years to derive the preload-loss curve, and inspect bands for slip marks.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"索夾螺栓應列入定期抽測的檢查項目，訂出觸發全面再張拉的預力門檻；任何會增加吊索力或改變主纜壓密狀態的工程（加撐、換橋面、除濕包覆）完成後，都要安排一次螺栓預力複測。","textEn":"Make cable-band bolts a periodic sampling item with a preload threshold that triggers full re-tensioning; after any work that raises suspender forces or changes cable compaction, such as bracing, deck replacement or dehumidification wrapping, schedule a preload re-check.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以超音波量測螺栓伸長或以液壓張拉器做起始脫離（lift-off）試驗求現有預力，抽樣範圍涵蓋不同跨段與坡度。","空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Measure existing preload by ultrasonic bolt elongation or hydraulic lift-off tests on a sample covering different spans and slopes.","Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以超音波量測螺栓伸長或以液壓張拉器做起始脫離（lift-off）試驗求現有預力，抽樣範圍涵蓋不同跨段與坡度；再張拉後記錄每根螺栓的目標值與實際值，數年後複測以求預力流失曲線，並檢查索夾是否有滑移痕跡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure existing preload by ultrasonic bolt elongation or hydraulic lift-off tests on a sample covering different spans and slopes; after re-tensioning record target and achieved values for each bolt, re-test after some years to derive the preload-loss curve, and inspect bands for slip marks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"b015-v13-32","title":"索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「索夾螺栓預力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cable-band bolt preload” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"預力流失到摩擦力不足時，陡坡段的索夾會沿主纜下滑，吊索偏斜、索夾邊緣刮傷鋼絲並破壞防護包覆，水分隨之進入主纜；滑移也會改變吊索長度分配與橋面線形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"When preload falls until friction is inadequate, bands on steep cable slopes slide down, tilting suspenders, scoring wires at band edges and breaking the wrapping so water enters the cable; slip also redistributes suspender lengths and alters the deck profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：預力流失的主因是主纜鋼絲在夾壓下逐漸重新排列與壓密、鍍鋅層潛變，以及溫度循環；螺栓伸長量只有零點幾毫米，因此很小的直徑變化就能吃掉大半預力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preload is lost mainly as cable wires rearrange and compact under clamping, as zinc creeps and through thermal cycles; bolt elongation is only fractions of a millimetre, so a tiny diameter change can consume most of the preload.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「螺栓一旦鎖到規定張力，就能永久保持。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once bolts are tightened to the specified tension, they keep it forever.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"預力流失到摩擦力不足時，陡坡段的索夾會沿主纜下滑，吊索偏斜、索夾邊緣刮傷鋼絲並破壞防護包覆，水分隨之進入主纜；滑移也會改變吊索長度分配與橋面線形。","textEn":"When preload falls until friction is inadequate, bands on steep cable slopes slide down, tilting suspenders, scoring wires at band edges and breaking the wrapping so water enters the cable; slip also redistributes suspender lengths and alters the deck profile.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「索夾螺栓預力損失與再張拉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cable-band bolt preload loss and re-tensioning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。","預力流失到摩擦力不足時，陡坡段的索夾會沿主纜下滑，吊索偏斜、索夾邊緣刮傷鋼絲並破壞防護包覆，水分隨之進入主纜；滑移也會改變吊索長度分配與橋面線形。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.","When preload falls until friction is inadequate, bands on steep cable slopes slide down, tilting suspenders, scoring wires at band edges and breaking the wrapping so water enters the cable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"預力流失到摩擦力不足時，陡坡段的索夾會沿主纜下滑，吊索偏斜、索夾邊緣刮傷鋼絲並破壞防護包覆，水分隨之進入主纜；滑移也會改變吊索長度分配與橋面線形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"When preload falls until friction is inadequate, bands on steep cable slopes slide down, tilting suspenders, scoring wires at band edges and breaking the wrapping so water enters the cable; slip also redistributes suspender lengths and alters the deck profile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":8},{"id":"b015-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「第 3B 期主橋耐震改造」與「防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge\" and \"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b015-v13-33","title":"第 3B 期主橋耐震改造：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「38 組消能裝置」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “38 energy-dissipation devices” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震後的脆弱度研究指出，近距離 7.0 級以上地震可能造成嚴重損壞，8.0 級以上則可能使引橋與 Fort Point 拱段倒塌。改造以 10% 50 年超越機率（約 0.46 g）的中度地震與 1,000 年回歸期（約 0.65 g、相當於 1906 年舊金山地震）的最大可信地震為準則，分三期進行；第 2 期於 2008 年 7 月完成，消除了引橋倒塌風險。第 3B 期涵蓋主跨、兩邊跨、兩座橋塔與南塔基座：塔底以大型鋼板補強、塔內桁架補強、更換橋面與主塔及混凝土塔柱交接處的伸縮縫以容納三維位移、補強橋面橫向斜撐、改造 255 根橫梁，並安裝 38 組消能裝置，大幅減少傳入橋梁的地震能量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「38 組消能裝置」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A vulnerability study after the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake found that a nearby magnitude 7.0 or larger event could cause severe damage, and one of 8.0 or larger could collapse the approach viaducts and Fort Point Arch. The retrofit uses a moderate earthquake with 10% exceedance in 50 years (about 0.46 g) and a maximum credible earthquake with a 1,000-year return period (about 0.65 g, equivalent to the 1906 San Francisco earthquake), in three phases; Phase 2, finished in July 2008, removed the approach collapse risk. Phase 3B covers the main span, both side spans, both towers and the South Tower pier: steel plates at the tower bases, strengthened tower trusses, new expansion joints at the towers and pylons for three-dimensional movement, reinforced roadway lateral bracing, 255 retrofitted floor beams and 38 energy-dissipation devices that greatly reduce seismic energy entering the bridge. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “38 energy-dissipation devices” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以非線性黏滯阻尼器說明消能：F = C·v^α。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Illustrate dissipation with a nonlinear viscous damper F = C·v^α.","failure":"常見誤解：「1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「38 組消能裝置」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “38 energy-dissipation devices”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-33-k1","title":"第 3B 期主橋耐震改造","titleEn":"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge","text":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震後的脆弱度研究指出，近距離 7.0 級以上地震可能造成嚴重損壞，8.0 級以上則可能使引橋與 Fort Point 拱段倒塌。改造以 10% 50 年超越機率（約 0.46 g）的中度地震與 1,000 年回歸期（約 0.65 g、相當於 1906 年舊金山地震）的最大可信地震為準則，分三期進行；第 2 期於 2008 年 7 月完成，消除了引橋倒塌風險。","textEn":"A vulnerability study after the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake found that a nearby magnitude 7.0 or larger event could cause severe damage, and one of 8.0 or larger could collapse the approach viaducts and Fort Point Arch. The retrofit uses a moderate earthquake with 10% exceedance in 50 years (about 0.46 g) and a maximum credible earthquake with a 1,000-year return period (about 0.65 g, equivalent to the 1906 San Francisco earthquake), in three phases; Phase 2, finished in July 2008, removed the approach collapse risk.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「第 3B 期主橋耐震改造」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge\" is correct?","options":["1989 年洛馬普列塔地震後的脆弱度研究指出，近距離 7.0 級以上地震可能造成嚴重損壞，8.0 級以上則可能使引橋與 Fort Point 拱段倒塌。","1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。","防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["A vulnerability study after the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake found that a nearby magnitude 7.0 or larger event could cause severe damage, and one of 8.0 or larger could collapse the approach viaducts and Fort Point Arch.","Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.","The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震後的脆弱度研究指出，近距離 7.0 級以上地震可能造成嚴重損壞，8.0 級以上則可能使引橋與 Fort Point 拱段倒塌。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A vulnerability study after the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake found that a nearby magnitude 7.0 or larger event could cause severe damage, and one of 8.0 or larger could collapse the approach viaducts and Fort Point Arch. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":57},{"id":"b015-v13-34","title":"第 3B 期主橋耐震改造：定量估算","titleEn":"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「38 組消能裝置」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “38 energy-dissipation devices” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以非線性黏滯阻尼器說明消能：F = C·v^α。取 C = 3,000 kN·(s/m)^0.4、α = 0.4、振幅 X = 0.5 m、週期 4 s（ω = 1.571 rad/s）：峰值速度 0.785 m/s，F ≈ 3,000×0.785^0.4 ≈ 2,720 kN；每循環耗能 E = λ·C·X^(1+α)·ω^α，λ ≈ 3.58，E ≈ 4,880 kJ。裝置型式與參數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Illustrate dissipation with a nonlinear viscous damper F = C·v^α. With C = 3,000 kN·(s/m)^0.4, α = 0.4, amplitude X = 0.5 m and a 4 s period (ω = 1.571 rad/s): peak velocity 0.785 m/s and F ≈ 3,000×0.785^0.4 ≈ 2,720 kN; energy per cycle E = λ·C·X^(1+α)·ω^α with λ ≈ 3.58 gives E ≈ 4,880 kJ. Device type and parameters are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：消能裝置須做原型與逐件試驗，涵蓋設計速度範圍、溫度與循環次數，力—位移遲滯迴圈的耗能與規格比較；全橋以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層紀錄，檢查塔底應力、伸縮縫三維位移與橋面斜撐受力是否符合兩級地震的性能目標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Damping devices need prototype and production tests over the design velocity range, temperatures and cycle counts, comparing hysteresis-loop energy with the specification; the whole bridge is analysed by nonlinear time history with several near-fault records to check tower-base stress, three-dimensional joint movement and lateral-bracing forces against the performance goals for both earthquake levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以非線性黏滯阻尼器說明消能：F = C·v^α。取 C = 3,000 kN·(s/m)^0.4、α = 0.4、振幅 X = 0.5 m、週期 4 s（ω = 1.571 rad/s）：峰值速度 0.785 m/s，F ≈ 3,000×0.785^0.4 ≈ 2,720 kN；每循環耗能 E = λ·C·X^(1+α)·ω^α，λ ≈ 3.58，E ≈ 4,880 kJ。裝置型式與參數為教學假設。","textEn":"Illustrate dissipation with a nonlinear viscous damper F = C·v^α. With C = 3,000 kN·(s/m)^0.4, α = 0.4, amplitude X = 0.5 m and a 4 s period (ω = 1.571 rad/s): peak velocity 0.785 m/s and F ≈ 3,000×0.785^0.4 ≈ 2,720 kN; energy per cycle E = λ·C·X^(1+α)·ω^α with λ ≈ 3.58 gives E ≈ 4,880 kJ. Device type and parameters are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「第 3B 期主橋耐震改造」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge\", which statement holds?","options":["懸索橋的橫向勁度主要來自橋面桁架，主纜只負責垂直荷重。","以非線性黏滯阻尼器說明消能：F = C·v^α。","吊索只是把橋面掛起來的細鋼索，壞一兩根不影響整體。"],"optionsEn":["A suspension bridge's lateral stiffness comes mainly from the deck truss; the cables only carry vertical load.","Illustrate dissipation with a nonlinear viscous damper F = C·v^α.","Suspenders are just thin ropes hanging the deck; losing one or two does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以非線性黏滯阻尼器說明消能：F = C·v^α。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Illustrate dissipation with a nonlinear viscous damper F = C·v^α. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":58},{"id":"b015-v13-35","title":"第 3B 期主橋耐震改造：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「38 組消能裝置」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “38 energy-dissipation devices” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"消能裝置須做原型與逐件試驗，涵蓋設計速度範圍、溫度與循環次數，力—位移遲滯迴圈的耗能與規格比較；全橋以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層紀錄，檢查塔底應力、伸縮縫三維位移與橋面斜撐受力是否符合兩級地震的性能目標。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Damping devices need prototype and production tests over the design velocity range, temperatures and cycle counts, comparing hysteresis-loop energy with the specification; the whole bridge is analysed by nonlinear time history with several near-fault records to check tower-base stress, three-dimensional joint movement and lateral-bracing forces against the performance goals for both earthquake levels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：耐震改造的分期順序應依構件勁度與倒塌後果排定（業主先做較不柔的橋塔與邊跨），每期完工都要更新全橋模型與性能矩陣；消能裝置需納入定期檢查與抽測計畫，並保存原型試驗曲線作為基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: Sequence retrofit phases by stiffness and collapse consequence (the owner starts with the less flexible towers and side spans), updating the whole-bridge model and performance matrix at the end of each phase; put damping devices on a periodic inspection and sampling programme with prototype test curves kept as the baseline.","failure":"注意干擾：只補強主橋而不處理伸縮縫，大地震時橋面與塔之間的相對位移可能使伸縮縫破壞、支承脫落；消能裝置若在長期風與交通的小振幅循環中磨耗而未檢查，地震時的耗能可能遠低於設計。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Strengthening the main bridge without new joints lets relative movement between deck and towers in a large earthquake destroy joints and unseat bearings; dampers worn by years of small wind and traffic cycles without inspection may dissipate far less energy than designed in an earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"消能裝置須做原型與逐件試驗，涵蓋設計速度範圍、溫度與循環次數，力—位移遲滯迴圈的耗能與規格比較；全橋以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層紀錄，檢查塔底應力、伸縮縫三維位移與橋面斜撐受力是否符合兩級地震的性能目標。","textEn":"Damping devices need prototype and production tests over the design velocity range, temperatures and cycle counts, comparing hysteresis-loop energy with the specification; the whole bridge is analysed by nonlinear time history with several near-fault records to check tower-base stress, three-dimensional joint movement and lateral-bracing forces against the performance goals for both earthquake levels.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"耐震改造的分期順序應依構件勁度與倒塌後果排定（業主先做較不柔的橋塔與邊跨），每期完工都要更新全橋模型與性能矩陣；消能裝置需納入定期檢查與抽測計畫，並保存原型試驗曲線作為基準。","textEn":"Sequence retrofit phases by stiffness and collapse consequence (the owner starts with the less flexible towers and side spans), updating the whole-bridge model and performance matrix at the end of each phase; put damping devices on a periodic inspection and sampling programme with prototype test curves kept as the baseline.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「第 3B 期主橋耐震改造」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","把橋面換輕只會讓橋更安全，不會改變幾何。","消能裝置須做原型與逐件試驗，涵蓋設計速度範圍、溫度與循環次數，力—位移遲滯迴圈的耗能與規格比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A lighter deck only makes the bridge safer; it does not change the geometry.","Damping devices need prototype and production tests over the design velocity range, temperatures and cycle counts, comparing hysteresis-loop energy with the specification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"消能裝置須做原型與逐件試驗，涵蓋設計速度範圍、溫度與循環次數，力—位移遲滯迴圈的耗能與規格比較；全橋以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層紀錄，檢查塔底應力、伸縮縫三維位移與橋面斜撐受力是否符合兩級地震的性能目標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Damping devices need prototype and production tests over the design velocity range, temperatures and cycle counts, comparing hysteresis-loop energy with the specification; the whole bridge is analysed by nonlinear time history with several near-fault records to check tower-base stress, three-dimensional joint movement and lateral-bracing forces against the performance goals for both earthquake levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":59},{"id":"b015-v13-36","title":"第 3B 期主橋耐震改造：失效診斷","titleEn":"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「38 組消能裝置」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “38 energy-dissipation devices” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只補強主橋而不處理伸縮縫，大地震時橋面與塔之間的相對位移可能使伸縮縫破壞、支承脫落；消能裝置若在長期風與交通的小振幅循環中磨耗而未檢查，地震時的耗能可能遠低於設計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Strengthening the main bridge without new joints lets relative movement between deck and towers in a large earthquake destroy joints and unseat bearings; dampers worn by years of small wind and traffic cycles without inspection may dissipate far less energy than designed in an earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：第 3B 期涵蓋主跨、兩邊跨、兩座橋塔與南塔基座：塔底以大型鋼板補強、塔內桁架補強、更換橋面與主塔及混凝土塔柱交接處的伸縮縫以容納三維位移、補強橋面橫向斜撐、改造 255 根橫梁，並安裝 38 組消能裝置，大幅減少傳入橋梁的地震能量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Phase 3B covers the main span, both side spans, both towers and the South Tower pier: steel plates at the tower bases, strengthened tower trusses, new expansion joints at the towers and pylons for three-dimensional movement, reinforced roadway lateral bracing, 255 retrofitted floor beams and 38 energy-dissipation devices that greatly reduce seismic energy entering the bridge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「1989 年地震中金門大橋沒有損壞，代表它不需要耐震改造。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because the bridge was undamaged in 1989, it does not need seismic retrofit.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只補強主橋而不處理伸縮縫，大地震時橋面與塔之間的相對位移可能使伸縮縫破壞、支承脫落；消能裝置若在長期風與交通的小振幅循環中磨耗而未檢查，地震時的耗能可能遠低於設計。","textEn":"Strengthening the main bridge without new joints lets relative movement between deck and towers in a large earthquake destroy joints and unseat bearings; dampers worn by years of small wind and traffic cycles without inspection may dissipate far less energy than designed in an earthquake.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「第 3B 期主橋耐震改造」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Phase 3B seismic retrofit of the main bridge\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只補強主橋而不處理伸縮縫，大地震時橋面與塔之間的相對位移可能使伸縮縫破壞、支承脫落。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Strengthening the main bridge without new joints lets relative movement between deck and towers in a large earthquake destroy joints and unseat bearings.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只補強主橋而不處理伸縮縫，大地震時橋面與塔之間的相對位移可能使伸縮縫破壞、支承脫落；消能裝置若在長期風與交通的小振幅循環中磨耗而未檢查，地震時的耗能可能遠低於設計。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Strengthening the main bridge without new joints lets relative movement between deck and towers in a large earthquake destroy joints and unseat bearings; dampers worn by years of small wind and traffic cycles without inspection may dissipate far less energy than designed in an earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":60},{"id":"b015-v13-37","title":"防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「防墜網與整流板」如何影響舊金山金門大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deterrent net and wind fairing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Golden Gate Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"防墜系統在東西兩側人行道下方 20 ft 處裝設海洋級不鏽鋼網，向外伸出 20 ft，沿 1.7 mi 全長連續，2018 年動工、2024 年初完成。網片與支架改變了橋面邊緣的流場並增加風阻，因此必須搭配抗風改造：透風的西側欄杆與人行道下方整流板，確保橋梁在持續 100 mph 的風中仍保有結構完整與氣動穩定。這說明一座 1937 年的懸索橋，每次在斷面上加東西，都要重新回答「顫振、抖振、渦振與側向變位是否仍可接受」的問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「防墜網與整流板」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The deterrent system hangs marine-grade stainless-steel netting 20 ft below the sidewalks on both sides, extending 20 ft out and running continuously for the full 1.7 miles; it began in 2018 and was complete in early 2024. The netting and its supports change the flow at the deck edges and add wind resistance, so it had to be paired with the wind retrofit, the more porous west railing and a fairing below the sidewalk, to keep the bridge structurally sound and aerodynamically stable in sustained winds up to 100 mph. It shows that every addition to the section of a 1937 suspension bridge reopens the question of whether flutter, buffeting, vortex shedding and lateral deflection remain acceptable. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Deterrent net and wind fairing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：100 mph（44.7 m/s）風壓 q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At 100 mph (44.7 m/s) the wind pressure q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「防墜網與整流板」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Deterrent net and wind fairing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-37-k1","title":"防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理","titleEn":"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management","text":"防墜系統在東西兩側人行道下方 20 ft 處裝設海洋級不鏽鋼網，向外伸出 20 ft，沿 1.7 mi 全長連續，2018 年動工、2024 年初完成。網片與支架改變了橋面邊緣的流場並增加風阻，因此必須搭配抗風改造：透風的西側欄杆與人行道下方整流板，確保橋梁在持續 100 mph 的風中仍保有結構完整與氣動穩定。","textEn":"The deterrent system hangs marine-grade stainless-steel netting 20 ft below the sidewalks on both sides, extending 20 ft out and running continuously for the full 1.7 miles; it began in 2018 and was complete in early 2024. The netting and its supports change the flow at the deck edges and add wind resistance, so it had to be paired with the wind retrofit, the more porous west railing and a fairing below the sidewalk, to keep the bridge structurally sound and aerodynamically stable in sustained winds up to 100 mph.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management\" is correct?","options":["防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。","防墜系統在東西兩側人行道下方 20 ft 處裝設海洋級不鏽鋼網，向外伸出 20 ft，沿 1.7 mi 全長連續，2018 年動工、2024 年初完成。","塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。"],"optionsEn":["The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability.","The deterrent system hangs marine-grade stainless-steel netting 20 ft below the sidewalks on both sides, extending 20 ft out and running continuously for the full 1.7 miles.","The load on the tower equals the cable tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防墜系統在東西兩側人行道下方 20 ft 處裝設海洋級不鏽鋼網，向外伸出 20 ft，沿 1.7 mi 全長連續，2018 年動工、2024 年初完成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The deterrent system hangs marine-grade stainless-steel netting 20 ft below the sidewalks on both sides, extending 20 ft out and running continuously for the full 1.7 miles; it began in 2018 and was complete in early 2024. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":61},{"id":"b015-v13-38","title":"防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理：定量估算","titleEn":"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「防墜網與整流板」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deterrent net and wind fairing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：100 mph（44.7 m/s）風壓 q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa。若網片與支架在兩側合計增加等效投影深度 0.6 m、阻力係數 1.2：ΔF ≈ 1,249×1.2×0.6 ≈ 0.90 kN/m；以重力勁度估算跨中附加側向變位 Δδ = ΔF·l²/(8H) ≈ 0.90×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 0.28 m。投影深度與係數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At 100 mph (44.7 m/s) the wind pressure q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa. If the net and supports add an equivalent projected depth of 0.6 m in total with a drag coefficient of 1.2: ΔF ≈ 1,249×1.2×0.6 ≈ 0.90 kN/m; the gravity-stiffness estimate of added mid-span lateral deflection is Δδ = ΔF·l²/(8H) ≈ 0.90×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 0.28 m. Projected depth and coefficient are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以含網片、整流板與新欄杆的斷面模型重新量測靜力係數與氣動導數，檢查顫振臨界風速、抖振反應與渦振；施工後以監測資料比較改造前後同風況下的位移與加速度，並持續記錄網片與支架的腐蝕與鬆動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Re-measure static coefficients and aerodynamic derivatives on a section model including the net, fairing and new railing, checking flutter onset, buffeting and vortex shedding; after construction compare monitored displacement and acceleration before and after under similar winds, and keep recording corrosion and loosening of the net and supports.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"100 mph（44.7 m/s）風壓 q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa。若網片與支架在兩側合計增加等效投影深度 0.6 m、阻力係數 1.2：ΔF ≈ 1,249×1.2×0.6 ≈ 0.90 kN/m；以重力勁度估算跨中附加側向變位 Δδ = ΔF·l²/(8H) ≈ 0.90×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 0.28 m。投影深度與係數為教學假設。","textEn":"At 100 mph (44.7 m/s) the wind pressure q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa. If the net and supports add an equivalent projected depth of 0.6 m in total with a drag coefficient of 1.2: ΔF ≈ 1,249×1.2×0.6 ≈ 0.90 kN/m; the gravity-stiffness estimate of added mid-span lateral deflection is Δδ = ΔF·l²/(8H) ≈ 0.90×1,280²/(8×651,000) ≈ 0.28 m. Projected depth and coefficient are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management\", which statement holds?","options":["老橋的鋼絲強度一定比規格值低很多，所以不值得試驗。","空中紡線的速度只取決於紡線輪跑多快。","100 mph（44.7 m/s）風壓 q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa。"],"optionsEn":["Old bridge wire is always far below its specification, so testing is pointless.","Aerial-spinning speed depends only on how fast the wheels run.","At 100 mph (44.7 m/s) the wind pressure q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"100 mph（44.7 m/s）風壓 q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At 100 mph (44.7 m/s) the wind pressure q = ½ρU² ≈ 1,249 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":62},{"id":"b015-v13-39","title":"防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「防墜網與整流板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deterrent net and wind fairing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以含網片、整流板與新欄杆的斷面模型重新量測靜力係數與氣動導數，檢查顫振臨界風速、抖振反應與渦振；施工後以監測資料比較改造前後同風況下的位移與加速度，並持續記錄網片與支架的腐蝕與鬆動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Re-measure static coefficients and aerodynamic derivatives on a section model including the net, fairing and new railing, checking flutter onset, buffeting and vortex shedding; after construction compare monitored displacement and acceleration before and after under similar winds, and keep recording corrosion and loosening of the net and supports. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主應建立「斷面變更管理」制度：任何附加於橋面或桁架的設施，先登錄重量、受風面積與連接細部，由結構與風工程顧問評估並核准，完工後更新恆載履歷、風洞基準與檢查清單，作為交接文件的一部分。","observationEn":"Site practice: The owner should run section-change management: any attachment to deck or truss is first registered with its weight, wind area and connection details, assessed and approved by structural and wind consultants, and after completion the dead-load history, wind-tunnel baseline and inspection checklist are updated as part of the handover record.","failure":"注意干擾：若附加物在未經氣動評估下裝上，可能降低顫振裕度或在某風向引發新的渦振；網片支架與桁架的連接若疲勞或腐蝕鬆脫，部件墜落還會危及航道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attachments installed without aerodynamic assessment can lower flutter margin or start new vortex vibration in some wind directions; fatigued or corroded connections between net supports and the truss can loosen and drop parts into the shipping channel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以含網片、整流板與新欄杆的斷面模型重新量測靜力係數與氣動導數，檢查顫振臨界風速、抖振反應與渦振；施工後以監測資料比較改造前後同風況下的位移與加速度，並持續記錄網片與支架的腐蝕與鬆動。","textEn":"Re-measure static coefficients and aerodynamic derivatives on a section model including the net, fairing and new railing, checking flutter onset, buffeting and vortex shedding; after construction compare monitored displacement and acceleration before and after under similar winds, and keep recording corrosion and loosening of the net and supports.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主應建立「斷面變更管理」制度：任何附加於橋面或桁架的設施，先登錄重量、受風面積與連接細部，由結構與風工程顧問評估並核准，完工後更新恆載履歷、風洞基準與檢查清單，作為交接文件的一部分。","textEn":"The owner should run section-change management: any attachment to deck or truss is first registered with its weight, wind area and connection details, assessed and approved by structural and wind consultants, and after completion the dead-load history, wind-tunnel baseline and inspection checklist are updated as part of the handover record.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management\"?","options":["以含網片、整流板與新欄杆的斷面模型重新量測靜力係數與氣動導數，檢查顫振臨界風速、抖振反應與渦振。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要整座橋在強風中穩定，欄杆的振動與聲音就不是工程問題。"],"optionsEn":["Re-measure static coefficients and aerodynamic derivatives on a section model including the net, fairing and new railing, checking flutter onset, buffeting and vortex shedding.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If the whole bridge is stable in strong wind, railing vibration and noise are not engineering problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以含網片、整流板與新欄杆的斷面模型重新量測靜力係數與氣動導數，檢查顫振臨界風速、抖振反應與渦振；施工後以監測資料比較改造前後同風況下的位移與加速度，並持續記錄網片與支架的腐蝕與鬆動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Re-measure static coefficients and aerodynamic derivatives on a section model including the net, fairing and new railing, checking flutter onset, buffeting and vortex shedding; after construction compare monitored displacement and acceleration before and after under similar winds, and keep recording corrosion and loosening of the net and supports. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":63},{"id":"b015-v13-40","title":"防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"],"prerequisiteIds":["b015-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「防墜網與整流板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deterrent net and wind fairing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若附加物在未經氣動評估下裝上，可能降低顫振裕度或在某風向引發新的渦振；網片支架與桁架的連接若疲勞或腐蝕鬆脫，部件墜落還會危及航道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attachments installed without aerodynamic assessment can lower flutter margin or start new vortex vibration in some wind directions; fatigued or corroded connections between net supports and the truss can loosen and drop parts into the shipping channel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這說明一座 1937 年的懸索橋，每次在斷面上加東西，都要重新回答「顫振、抖振、渦振與側向變位是否仍可接受」的問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It shows that every addition to the section of a 1937 suspension bridge reopens the question of whether flutter, buffeting, vortex shedding and lateral deflection remain acceptable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防墜網是輕量的附屬設施，對橋梁的結構與風穩定沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The deterrent net is a light accessory with no effect on structure or wind stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b015-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若附加物在未經氣動評估下裝上，可能降低顫振裕度或在某風向引發新的渦振；網片支架與桁架的連接若疲勞或腐蝕鬆脫，部件墜落還會危及航道。","textEn":"Attachments installed without aerodynamic assessment can lower flutter margin or start new vortex vibration in some wind directions; fatigued or corroded connections between net supports and the truss can loosen and drop parts into the shipping channel.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]},{"id":"b015-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-golden-stats","v7-golden-seismic","v13s-ggb-seismic-phase-3","v13s-ggb-high-wind-sounds","v13s-ggb-deterrent-net"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防墜網、整流板與斷面變更管理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deterrent net, fairing and section-change management\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若附加物在未經氣動評估下裝上，可能降低顫振裕度或在某風向引發新的渦振；網片支架與桁架的連接若疲勞或腐蝕鬆脫，部件墜落還會危及航道。","塔頂荷重就等於主纜張力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Attachments installed without aerodynamic assessment can lower flutter margin or start new vortex vibration in some wind directions.","The load on the tower equals the cable tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若附加物在未經氣動評估下裝上，可能降低顫振裕度或在某風向引發新的渦振；網片支架與桁架的連接若疲勞或腐蝕鬆脫，部件墜落還會危及航道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attachments installed without aerodynamic assessment can lower flutter margin or start new vortex vibration in some wind directions; fatigued or corroded connections between net supports and the truss can loosen and drop parts into the shipping channel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":64}],"order":9}],"curriculumVersion":7,"enrichmentVersion":13,"learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-suspension","learningTags":["structures","st-suspension","suspension"],"subcategory":"st-suspension","subcategoryTitle":"懸索橋巨作與主纜系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Suspension bridges and main-cable systems","v13Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"suspension","architectureNodes":[["鋼塔與塔底補強","Steel towers and base strengthening"],["空中紡線主纜","Air-spun main cables"],["索夾螺栓與吊索","Cable-band bolts and suspenders"],["加勁桁架與正交異性橋面","Stiffening truss and orthotropic deck"],["消能裝置與伸縮縫","Dampers and expansion joints"],["欄杆、整流板與防墜網","Railing, fairing and deterrent net"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[1,0],[3,4],[4,0],[5,3]]},"v13Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"延伸練習：以業主公開數據核算主纜安全係數的變化。每座塔承受主纜荷重約 61,500 short ton（≈ 547 MN）；假設塔頂兩側 tanθ 為 0.44 與 0.40，H ≈ 651 MN（兩纜），每纜最大張力 T ≈ 356 MN。每纜鋼絲 27,572 根 × 18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm²，以規格最低強度 220,000 psi（1,517 N/mm²）計破斷力 ≈ 781 MN，安全係數 ≈ 781/356 ≈ 2.19；以實測平均 235,600 psi（1,624 N/mm²）計 ≈ 2.35。若 1986 年橋面減重使每纜張力減少約 28.8 MN 的水平分量（最大張力約減 31.5 MN），係數提高到約 781/324.5 ≈ 2.41；若腐蝕使有效鋼絲面積減少 5%，係數回落到約 2.29。數值除業主公布者外均為教學假設，不代表金門大橋的評估結果。","textEn":"Extension exercise: check the change in cable safety factor with the owner's data. Each tower carries about 61,500 short tons (≈ 547 MN) from the cables; assuming tanθ of 0.44 and 0.40 on either side of the tower, H ≈ 651 MN for both cables and the maximum tension per cable T ≈ 356 MN. Each cable has 27,572 wires × 18.68 mm² ≈ 515,000 mm²; at the specified minimum 220,000 psi (1,517 N/mm²) the breaking force is ≈ 781 MN and the safety factor ≈ 781/356 ≈ 2.19, or about 2.35 at the average 235,600 psi (1,624 N/mm²). If the 1986 deck lightening reduced the horizontal tension per cable by about 28.8 MN (about 31.5 MN off the maximum tension), the factor rises to about 781/324.5 ≈ 2.41; a 5% loss of effective wire area from corrosion brings it back to about 2.29. Apart from the owner's published figures, values are teaching assumptions, not the Golden Gate Bridge's evaluation results.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"以業主公開數據做定量延伸：主纜張力、側向重力勁度、索夾螺栓預力損失、橋面減重抬升、欄杆風鳴與第 3B 期耐震改造","focusEn":"Quantitative extension from owner data: cable tension, lateral gravity stiffness, cable-band bolt preload loss, deck-lightening rise, railing wind tones and Phase 3B seismic retrofit"}},{"id":"b021","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"title":"台北 101","titleEn":"Taipei 101","summary":"用 24 步拆解超高層建築的核心、外伸桁架、基礎、風振控制與營運介面，將外觀地標轉成可解釋的工程系統。","summaryEn":"Use 24 steps to unpack the core, outriggers, foundations, wind-motion control and operating interfaces of a supertall building.","scope":"以公開一次資料為背景的原創工程判讀課程；每步在紙上或數位示意模型中完成。自設數值、構形與工序不得當成原工程的設計、施工、設備操作或驗收程序。","scopeEn":"Original engineering interpretation exercises grounded in public primary sources. Complete each step on paper or in a schematic digital model. Invented values, geometry and sequences are not the original project’s design, construction, operating or acceptance procedures.","diagram":{"type":"structure","labels":["需求與場址","結構與介面","施工狀態","驗證與維護"],"labelsEn":["Requirements and site","Structures and interfaces","Construction states","Verification and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":64,"estimatedMinutes":1600,"stages":[{"id":"b021-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、場址與荷載","titleEn":"Requirements, site and loads","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「需求、場址與荷載」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on requirements, site and loads, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v7-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分清高度與使用需求","titleEn":"Separate height from functional requirements","objective":"把地標高度轉成結構與使用性能問題。","objectiveEn":"Translate landmark height into structural and service-performance questions.","instruction":"1. 畫辦公、機械及觀景用途區；2. 分列承載、舒適與維護需求；3. 為每類寫一種需要的證據。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch office, mechanical and observation zones; 2. separate capacity, comfort and maintenance needs; 3. name evidence for each.","observation":"足夠承載能力不會自動保證高樓使用者感到舒適。","observationEn":"Adequate load capacity does not automatically establish occupant comfort.","failure":"只以總高度判定建築性能是否良好。","failureEn":"Assess building performance from total height alone.","check":"提交三類需求和對應證據矩陣。","checkEn":"Submit a matrix of three requirement classes and their evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-01-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"極限承載與日常服務性能回答不同問題，風中加速度常與使用感受有關。","textEn":"Ultimate capacity and everyday serviceability answer different questions; wind acceleration can matter to occupants."},{"id":"b021-v7-01-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"建築高度是幾何背景，不是風、地震或舒適性能的直接評分。","textEn":"Building height is geometric context, not a direct wind, seismic or comfort score."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分清高度與使用需求」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate height from functional requirements”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["足夠承載能力不會自動保證高樓使用者感到舒適。","只以總高度判定建築性能是否良好。","一棟樓有足夠承載能力就不會產生令人不適的加速度。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate load capacity does not automatically establish occupant comfort.","Assess building performance from total height alone.","Adequate capacity guarantees absence of uncomfortable acceleration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"極限承載與日常服務性能回答不同問題，風中加速度常與使用感受有關。 建築高度是幾何背景，不是風、地震或舒適性能的直接評分。","explanationEn":"Ultimate capacity and everyday serviceability answer different questions; wind acceleration can matter to occupants. Building height is geometric context, not a direct wind, seismic or comfort score."}},{"id":"b021-v7-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-01"],"title":"標記都市場址介面","titleEn":"Map urban-site interfaces","objective":"理解基地邊界以外仍有工程依賴。","objectiveEn":"Understand dependencies beyond the property boundary.","instruction":"1. 畫基地、周邊道路及鄰房；2. 標示地下水與管線資料空白；3. 區分公開地址、假設範圍與待調查範圍。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch site, roads and neighboring buildings; 2. mark gaps in groundwater and utility knowledge; 3. distinguish the public address, assumptions and investigation scope.","observation":"精確街址不能取代地下管線及地層調查。","observationEn":"A precise street address does not replace utility and ground investigation.","failure":"Google 地圖看到建築輪廓便可推知地下基礎範圍。","failureEn":"A visible building outline on Google Maps establishes its underground foundation extent.","check":"輸出含三個地下未知項的基地圖。","checkEn":"Produce a site plan with three underground unknowns.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-02-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"深基礎與地下室的變形或水位影響可能跨越地籍邊界。","textEn":"Deep-foundation and basement deformation or water effects can extend beyond cadastral boundaries."},{"id":"b021-v7-02-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"公開地圖適合建立背景與方位，不能當作現地測量控制資料。","textEn":"Public maps establish context and orientation, not field survey control."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「標記都市場址介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map urban-site interfaces”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["Google 地圖看到建築輪廓便可推知地下基礎範圍。","精確街址不能取代地下管線及地層調查。","地下室與基礎的影響必然止於地籍邊界。"],"optionsEn":["A visible building outline on Google Maps establishes its underground foundation extent.","A precise street address does not replace utility and ground investigation.","Basement and foundation effects necessarily stop at cadastral boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深基礎與地下室的變形或水位影響可能跨越地籍邊界。 公開地圖適合建立背景與方位，不能當作現地測量控制資料。","explanationEn":"Deep-foundation and basement deformation or water effects can extend beyond cadastral boundaries. Public maps establish context and orientation, not field survey control."}},{"id":"b021-v7-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-02"],"title":"區分重力與水平力路徑","titleEn":"Separate gravity and lateral force paths","objective":"把樓板、核心與周邊柱接成不同力路徑。","objectiveEn":"Connect floors, core and perimeter columns through distinct force paths.","instruction":"1. 畫一個概念標準層；2. 以兩色分別追蹤重力及水平力；3. 在基礎處關閉兩條反力路徑。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a conceptual typical floor; 2. trace gravity and lateral forces in two colors; 3. close both reaction paths at foundations.","observation":"同一樓板可以同時承受重力並傳遞平面內水平作用。","observationEn":"A floor can support gravity and transmit in-plane lateral action simultaneously.","failure":"重力傳到柱子後就不需要考慮樓板的水平傳力。","failureEn":"Once gravity reaches columns, floor-level lateral transfer can be ignored.","check":"提交包含樓板平面內作用的雙色受力圖。","checkEn":"Provide a two-color force map including floor in-plane action.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-03-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"樓板作為水平傳力構件時需要足夠連接；畫成剛性平面是一種模型假設。","textEn":"Floors require connections to transfer lateral action; drawing a rigid diaphragm is a modeling assumption."},{"id":"b021-v7-03-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"核心、周邊框架與基礎的分工取決於整體配置，不能從立面照片唯一推導。","textEn":"The roles of core, perimeter framing and foundations depend on the system and cannot be uniquely inferred from a façade photo."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分重力與水平力路徑」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate gravity and lateral force paths”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["重力傳到柱子後就不需要考慮樓板的水平傳力。","樓板的平面內作用與其連接條件完全無關。","同一樓板可以同時承受重力並傳遞平面內水平作用。"],"optionsEn":["Once gravity reaches columns, floor-level lateral transfer can be ignored.","In-plane floor action is entirely independent of connections.","A floor can support gravity and transmit in-plane lateral action simultaneously."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樓板作為水平傳力構件時需要足夠連接；畫成剛性平面是一種模型假設。 核心、周邊框架與基礎的分工取決於整體配置，不能從立面照片唯一推導。","explanationEn":"Floors require connections to transfer lateral action; drawing a rigid diaphragm is a modeling assumption. The roles of core, perimeter framing and foundations depend on the system and cannot be uniquely inferred from a façade photo."}},{"id":"b021-v7-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-03"],"title":"拆出質量、剛度與阻尼","titleEn":"Separate mass, stiffness and damping","objective":"建立高樓振動的最小概念模型。","objectiveEn":"Build a minimal conceptual model of tall-building motion.","instruction":"1. 畫單自由度質量彈簧模型；2. 分別改變一個無量綱參數；3. 比較頻率及衰減形狀。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a one-degree-of-freedom mass-spring model; 2. change one dimensionless parameter at a time; 3. compare frequency and decay shape.","observation":"增加質量與增加剛度通常對頻率產生不同方向的影響。","observationEn":"Increasing mass and increasing stiffness generally shift frequency in different directions.","failure":"只看振幅較小便確定質量、剛度與阻尼都提高。","failureEn":"A smaller amplitude proves that mass, stiffness and damping all increased.","check":"繳交三個單參數變更的對照圖。","checkEn":"Provide three comparisons changing one parameter at a time.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-04-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"理想線性振子頻率與剛度和質量的比值有關，阻尼控制能量消散。","textEn":"Ideal linear-oscillator frequency depends on stiffness relative to mass; damping governs dissipation."},{"id":"b021-v7-04-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"單自由度模型省略高階與扭轉模態，只適合說明機理。","textEn":"A one-degree model omits higher and torsional modes and is suitable only for explaining mechanisms."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆出質量、剛度與阻尼」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate mass, stiffness and damping”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["增加質量與增加剛度通常對頻率產生不同方向的影響。","只看振幅較小便確定質量、剛度與阻尼都提高。","剛度加倍一定使理想振子的頻率加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing mass and increasing stiffness generally shift frequency in different directions.","A smaller amplitude proves that mass, stiffness and damping all increased.","Doubling stiffness necessarily doubles ideal oscillator frequency."],"answer":0,"explanation":"理想線性振子頻率與剛度和質量的比值有關，阻尼控制能量消散。 單自由度模型省略高階與扭轉模態，只適合說明機理。","explanationEn":"Ideal linear-oscillator frequency depends on stiffness relative to mass; damping governs dissipation. A one-degree model omits higher and torsional modes and is suitable only for explaining mechanisms."}},{"id":"b021-v7-05","sequence":5,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-04"],"title":"比較風與地震輸入","titleEn":"Compare wind and earthquake inputs","objective":"辨認外力激振與基底運動的差別。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish applied-force excitation from base motion.","instruction":"1. 在樓身畫風作用分布；2. 在基礎畫假想地盤移動；3. 列出兩情境不同的輸入與輸出量。","instructionEn":"1. Draw wind actions along the tower; 2. draw hypothetical ground movement at the base; 3. list distinct inputs and outputs for both cases.","observation":"風與地震都能引起振動，但輸入位置與時間特徵不同。","observationEn":"Wind and earthquakes both induce motion but differ in input location and time characteristics.","failure":"兩者最大位移相同就代表每層受力及使用感受相同。","failureEn":"Equal peak displacement implies equal story forces and occupant experience.","check":"提交兩個輸入—系統—觀察量的方塊圖。","checkEn":"Submit two input–system–observation diagrams.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-05-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"外力與基底運動使用不同邊界描述；比較時必須先對齊量的定義。","textEn":"Applied forces and base motion use different boundary descriptions; comparisons require aligned definitions."},{"id":"b021-v7-05-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本練習不把任一自設時程當成台北 101 的設計地震或風場。","textEn":"No synthetic time history in this exercise is a Taipei 101 design earthquake or wind field."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較風與地震輸入」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare wind and earthquake inputs”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["兩者最大位移相同就代表每層受力及使用感受相同。","風與地震都能引起振動，但輸入位置與時間特徵不同。","地震輸入只能畫成樓頂的一個靜態水平力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak displacement implies equal story forces and occupant experience.","Wind and earthquakes both induce motion but differ in input location and time characteristics.","Earthquake input can only be represented by one static roof force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外力與基底運動使用不同邊界描述；比較時必須先對齊量的定義。 本練習不把任一自設時程當成台北 101 的設計地震或風場。","explanationEn":"Applied forces and base motion use different boundary descriptions; comparisons require aligned definitions. No synthetic time history in this exercise is a Taipei 101 design earthquake or wind field."}},{"id":"b021-v7-06","sequence":6,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-05"],"title":"審查地基與結構需求","titleEn":"Review ground and structural requirements","objective":"把上部結構反力連接到基礎證據。","objectiveEn":"Connect superstructure reactions to foundation evidence.","instruction":"1. 畫壓力、拔力及水平反力箭頭；2. 對應樁、承台及地層概念區；3. 分開承載與沉陷兩類問題。","instructionEn":"1. Draw compression, uplift and horizontal reactions; 2. connect them to conceptual piles, caps and strata; 3. separate capacity from settlement questions.","observation":"足夠承載與可接受差異沉陷是兩個不同檢查。","observationEn":"Adequate capacity and acceptable differential settlement are separate checks.","failure":"樁數足夠就能忽略群樁及沉陷差異。","failureEn":"A sufficient pile count makes group effects and differential settlement irrelevant.","check":"輸出一張反力對證據需求的配對表。","checkEn":"Produce a reaction-to-evidence matching table.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-06-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"基礎設計需處理荷載分配與變形相容；不能只將總重除以樁數。","textEn":"Foundation design addresses load distribution and deformation compatibility, not simply total weight divided by pile count."},{"id":"b021-v7-06-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方基礎概要提供系統背景，不提供可用於新基地的承載設計值。","textEn":"The owner’s foundation overview supplies system context, not bearing design values for another site."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「審查地基與結構需求」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review ground and structural requirements”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["樁數足夠就能忽略群樁及沉陷差異。","總重除以樁數即可完整預測每根樁的受力與沉陷。","足夠承載與可接受差異沉陷是兩個不同檢查。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficient pile count makes group effects and differential settlement irrelevant.","Total weight divided by pile count fully predicts each pile’s load and settlement.","Adequate capacity and acceptable differential settlement are separate checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基礎設計需處理荷載分配與變形相容；不能只將總重除以樁數。 官方基礎概要提供系統背景，不提供可用於新基地的承載設計值。","explanationEn":"Foundation design addresses load distribution and deformation compatibility, not simply total weight divided by pile count. The owner’s foundation overview supplies system context, not bearing design values for another site."}}]},{"id":"b021-stage02","order":2,"title":"核心、外伸桁架與介面","titleEn":"Core, outriggers and interfaces","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「核心、外伸桁架與介面」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on core, outriggers and interfaces, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v7-07","sequence":7,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-06"],"title":"辨認斜撐核心系統","titleEn":"Identify the braced core","objective":"將核心視為具有連接與變形的結構。","objectiveEn":"Treat the core as a structure with connections and deformation.","instruction":"1. 畫核心框架與假想斜撐；2. 標記軸力及層間側移；3. 比較連接完整與鬆開的概念模型。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch core framing and conceptual braces; 2. mark axial forces and story drift; 3. compare connected and released idealized models.","observation":"核心的側向作用依賴構件與連接共同形成傳力系統。","observationEn":"Core lateral action depends on members and connections forming a continuous system.","failure":"只要核心外框封閉就一定具有相同剛度。","failureEn":"Any closed core outline necessarily has identical stiffness.","check":"提供構件、連接與層間位移三種標記。","checkEn":"Provide member, connection and story-drift annotations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-07-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"斜撐利用軸向作用參與側向抵抗，但連接假設會改變整體變形。","textEn":"Braces participate through axial action, while connection assumptions affect overall deformation."},{"id":"b021-v7-07-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"示意模型不還原實樓所有斜撐位置，細節須由工程圖及專業分析確認。","textEn":"The schematic does not reproduce every real brace location; details require engineering drawings and analysis."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認斜撐核心系統」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Identify the braced core”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["核心的側向作用依賴構件與連接共同形成傳力系統。","只要核心外框封閉就一定具有相同剛度。","核心構件只要存在，連接方式就不影響變形。"],"optionsEn":["Core lateral action depends on members and connections forming a continuous system.","Any closed core outline necessarily has identical stiffness.","Core-member presence makes connection details irrelevant to deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"斜撐利用軸向作用參與側向抵抗，但連接假設會改變整體變形。 示意模型不還原實樓所有斜撐位置，細節須由工程圖及專業分析確認。","explanationEn":"Braces participate through axial action, while connection assumptions affect overall deformation. The schematic does not reproduce every real brace location; details require engineering drawings and analysis."}},{"id":"b021-v7-08","sequence":8,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-07"],"title":"理解外伸桁架如何連接周邊柱","titleEn":"Understand outrigger-to-perimeter coupling","objective":"追蹤核心傾轉與周邊軸力的關係。","objectiveEn":"Trace the relationship between core rotation and perimeter axial forces.","instruction":"1. 畫核心、外伸桁架及兩側柱；2. 施加小幅概念側移；3. 標記兩側柱軸力增減及基礎反力。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a core, outrigger and two perimeter columns; 2. apply a small conceptual sway; 3. mark changes in column axial forces and foundation reactions.","observation":"外伸桁架透過周邊柱的軸向作用協助抵抗核心傾轉。","observationEn":"An outrigger engages perimeter-column axial action to help resist core rotation.","failure":"外伸桁架只承受自重，不影響周邊柱的受力。","failureEn":"An outrigger carries only its own weight and does not affect perimeter-column forces.","check":"提交可追蹤到基礎的外伸桁架力路徑。","checkEn":"Submit an outrigger force path traceable to foundations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-08-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"增加有效抵抗力臂可以改變抗傾覆分工，但必須包含連接與基礎。","textEn":"Engaging a wider resisting lever arm changes overturning resistance but must include connections and foundations."},{"id":"b021-v7-08-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"台北 101 的多層外伸系統有特定配置；本模型只是解釋作用原理。","textEn":"Taipei 101 has a specific multi-outrigger layout; this model only explains the mechanism."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「理解外伸桁架如何連接周邊柱」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Understand outrigger-to-perimeter coupling”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["外伸桁架只承受自重，不影響周邊柱的受力。","外伸桁架透過周邊柱的軸向作用協助抵抗核心傾轉。","外伸桁架不需要把作用追蹤到基礎。"],"optionsEn":["An outrigger carries only its own weight and does not affect perimeter-column forces.","An outrigger engages perimeter-column axial action to help resist core rotation.","Outrigger action need not be traced to foundations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加有效抵抗力臂可以改變抗傾覆分工，但必須包含連接與基礎。 台北 101 的多層外伸系統有特定配置；本模型只是解釋作用原理。","explanationEn":"Engaging a wider resisting lever arm changes overturning resistance but must include connections and foundations. Taipei 101 has a specific multi-outrigger layout; this model only explains the mechanism."}},{"id":"b021-v7-09","sequence":9,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-08"],"title":"核對機械層的多系統介面","titleEn":"Audit mechanical-floor interfaces","objective":"辨識設備、結構與維修空間的衝突。","objectiveEn":"Identify conflicts among equipment, structure and maintenance space.","instruction":"1. 畫一層概念機械層；2. 疊放桁架、管線及維修通道；3. 為每個相交處建立介面問題卡。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a conceptual mechanical floor; 2. overlay trusses, services and maintenance routes; 3. create an interface issue card at each conflict.","observation":"管線能穿過圖面空白不代表現場具有維修及結構許可空間。","observationEn":"A service passing through blank drawing space does not establish maintenance clearance or structural permission.","failure":"只檢查設備外框不相交就能完成機械層協調。","failureEn":"Nonintersecting equipment outlines alone complete mechanical-floor coordination.","check":"提交至少三個介面衝突及其責任資料欄。","checkEn":"Submit at least three interface conflicts with responsible-data fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-09-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"結構及設備系統共用空間，維護可達性與施工順序也是介面條件。","textEn":"Structure and services share space; maintenance access and construction sequence are interface conditions too."},{"id":"b021-v7-09-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"數位碰撞檢查能找幾何衝突，但不能自行批准結構開孔。","textEn":"Digital clash detection finds geometric conflicts but cannot authorize structural penetrations."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「核對機械層的多系統介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Audit mechanical-floor interfaces”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只檢查設備外框不相交就能完成機械層協調。","維修人員所需空間不是設備與結構協調的一部分。","管線能穿過圖面空白不代表現場具有維修及結構許可空間。"],"optionsEn":["Nonintersecting equipment outlines alone complete mechanical-floor coordination.","Maintenance access is outside structural-equipment coordination.","A service passing through blank drawing space does not establish maintenance clearance or structural permission."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結構及設備系統共用空間，維護可達性與施工順序也是介面條件。 數位碰撞檢查能找幾何衝突，但不能自行批准結構開孔。","explanationEn":"Structure and services share space; maintenance access and construction sequence are interface conditions too. Digital clash detection finds geometric conflicts but cannot authorize structural penetrations."}},{"id":"b021-v7-10","sequence":10,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-09"],"title":"比較周邊框架與核心分工","titleEn":"Compare perimeter-frame and core roles","objective":"避免將所有水平荷載只分配給核心。","objectiveEn":"Avoid assigning every lateral action to the core alone.","instruction":"1. 畫核心及周邊兩個平行子系統；2. 分別設定相對軟硬的示意值；3. 比較分力與變形相容條件。","instructionEn":"1. Draw core and perimeter as parallel subsystems; 2. assign illustrative relative stiffnesses; 3. compare load sharing and deformation compatibility.","observation":"相連子系統的相對剛度會影響分力，而非只看構件數量。","observationEn":"Relative stiffness of connected subsystems affects force sharing, not merely member count.","failure":"核心較粗就能將周邊框架在模型中全部刪除。","failureEn":"A large core justifies deleting all perimeter framing from the model.","check":"輸出兩種剛度比例下的定性分力圖。","checkEn":"Provide qualitative force-sharing diagrams for two stiffness ratios.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-10-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"相容變形與力平衡必須同時滿足；各系統不能獨立任意分配荷載。","textEn":"Deformation compatibility and force equilibrium must hold together; loads cannot be assigned arbitrarily to isolated systems."},{"id":"b021-v7-10-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"設計者的系統概要可指引模型邊界，但不提供完整分析矩陣。","textEn":"The designer’s system overview guides model boundaries but does not supply a full analysis matrix."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較周邊框架與核心分工」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare perimeter-frame and core roles”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["相連子系統的相對剛度會影響分力，而非只看構件數量。","核心較粗就能將周邊框架在模型中全部刪除。","周邊框架與核心可以各自任意分配水平荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Relative stiffness of connected subsystems affects force sharing, not merely member count.","A large core justifies deleting all perimeter framing from the model.","Perimeter frames and core can allocate lateral loads arbitrarily and independently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相容變形與力平衡必須同時滿足；各系統不能獨立任意分配荷載。 設計者的系統概要可指引模型邊界，但不提供完整分析矩陣。","explanationEn":"Deformation compatibility and force equilibrium must hold together; loads cannot be assigned arbitrarily to isolated systems. The designer’s system overview guides model boundaries but does not supply a full analysis matrix."}},{"id":"b021-v7-11","sequence":11,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-10"],"title":"檢查樓板開口的傳力繞道","titleEn":"Review load paths around floor openings","objective":"理解管道及電梯開口對傳力的影響。","objectiveEn":"Understand how service and elevator openings affect force transfer.","instruction":"1. 在概念樓板畫兩個開口；2. 繪出繞過開口的平面內力路徑；3. 標記需要連接細節的邊緣。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two openings in a conceptual floor; 2. trace in-plane force paths around them; 3. identify edges needing connection details.","observation":"局部開口可能改變傳力集中位置，不能只扣除面積。","observationEn":"An opening can change force concentration locations rather than simply subtract area.","failure":"樓板總面積差不多便代表開口位置不重要。","failureEn":"Similar total floor area makes opening location irrelevant.","check":"提交含邊緣與連接需求的樓板力路徑圖。","checkEn":"Submit a floor force-path map with edge and connection needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-11-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水平傳力須繞過不連續處，幾何與連接決定可用路徑。","textEn":"Lateral force transfer must bypass discontinuities; geometry and connections determine available paths."},{"id":"b021-v7-11-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步示意開口是教學自設，不是台北 101 的實際樓層平面。","textEn":"Openings in this exercise are invented teaching geometry, not an actual Taipei 101 floor plan."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檢查樓板開口的傳力繞道」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review load paths around floor openings”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["樓板總面積差不多便代表開口位置不重要。","局部開口可能改變傳力集中位置，不能只扣除面積。","相同開口總面積保證相同的局部傳力路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Similar total floor area makes opening location irrelevant.","An opening can change force concentration locations rather than simply subtract area.","Equal total opening area guarantees identical local force paths."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水平傳力須繞過不連續處，幾何與連接決定可用路徑。 本步示意開口是教學自設，不是台北 101 的實際樓層平面。","explanationEn":"Lateral force transfer must bypass discontinuities; geometry and connections determine available paths. Openings in this exercise are invented teaching geometry, not an actual Taipei 101 floor plan."}},{"id":"b021-v7-12","sequence":12,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-concept","v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-11"],"title":"用介面矩陣完成結構複核","titleEn":"Complete a structural-interface review","objective":"讓核心、桁架、樓板與基礎使用一致假設。","objectiveEn":"Align assumptions across core, outriggers, floors and foundations.","instruction":"1. 列出四類子系統；2. 每對介面填入力、位移及資料版本；3. 將一個矛盾假設回溯到受影響的步驟。","instructionEn":"1. List four subsystem classes; 2. record forces, movements and data versions at each interface; 3. trace one inconsistent assumption to affected steps.","observation":"單一子系統看似合理仍可能與相鄰系統的邊界不一致。","observationEn":"A plausible subsystem may still conflict with adjacent boundary assumptions.","failure":"各張圖都沒有畫錯元件就表示整體模型一定相容。","failureEn":"Correctly drawn components on every sheet guarantee global compatibility.","check":"繳交一份包含修訂紀錄的四系統矩陣。","checkEn":"Provide a four-system matrix with a revision record.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-12-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"工程介面需要雙方共享相同的力與位移定義，否則資料無法直接串接。","textEn":"Engineering interfaces require shared force and movement definitions for usable data exchange."},{"id":"b021-v7-12-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"複核應記錄哪些下游結論需要重做，不能只修改衝突那一張圖。","textEn":"Review records should identify downstream conclusions needing revision, not only the conflicting drawing."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用介面矩陣完成結構複核」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Complete a structural-interface review”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["各張圖都沒有畫錯元件就表示整體模型一定相容。","不同專業採用不同位移定義不影響介面資料交換。","單一子系統看似合理仍可能與相鄰系統的邊界不一致。"],"optionsEn":["Correctly drawn components on every sheet guarantee global compatibility.","Different displacement definitions do not affect interface data exchange.","A plausible subsystem may still conflict with adjacent boundary assumptions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工程介面需要雙方共享相同的力與位移定義，否則資料無法直接串接。 複核應記錄哪些下游結論需要重做，不能只修改衝突那一張圖。","explanationEn":"Engineering interfaces require shared force and movement definitions for usable data exchange. Review records should identify downstream conclusions needing revision, not only the conflicting drawing."}}]},{"id":"b021-stage03","order":3,"title":"風振、量測與機電","titleEn":"Wind motion, measurement and services","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「風振、量測與機電」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on wind motion, measurement and services, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v7-13","sequence":13,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-12"],"title":"畫出調諧質量阻尼器雙系統","titleEn":"Draw a tuned-mass-damper model","objective":"區分建築本體與輔助質量的相對運動。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish building motion from auxiliary-mass relative motion.","instruction":"1. 畫建築與懸吊質量兩個自由度；2. 標示兩者位移及相對位移；3. 畫出阻尼作用連接的位置。","instructionEn":"1. Draw building and suspended-mass degrees of freedom; 2. mark both displacements and their relative displacement; 3. locate the damping connection.","observation":"阻尼器的相對運動與建築的絕對位移不是同一個量。","observationEn":"Damper relative motion and building absolute displacement are different quantities.","failure":"擺錘移動很大就表示建築一定失去承載能力。","failureEn":"Large pendulum motion necessarily means the building has lost load capacity.","check":"提交兩自由度示意及三種位移定義。","checkEn":"Submit a two-degree schematic and three displacement definitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-13-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"調諧質量阻尼器是耦合動力系統；它利用相對運動調整主系統反應。","textEn":"A tuned mass damper is a coupled dynamic system that uses relative motion to modify primary-system response."},{"id":"b021-v7-13-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"觀景照片只能顯示裝置外形，不能直接給出控制性能或當時荷載。","textEn":"Observation-deck photos show device appearance, not control performance or concurrent loading."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「畫出調諧質量阻尼器雙系統」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Draw a tuned-mass-damper model”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["阻尼器的相對運動與建築的絕對位移不是同一個量。","擺錘移動很大就表示建築一定失去承載能力。","擺錘的相對位移就是地面量到的建築位移。"],"optionsEn":["Damper relative motion and building absolute displacement are different quantities.","Large pendulum motion necessarily means the building has lost load capacity.","Pendulum relative displacement equals building displacement measured from the ground."],"answer":0,"explanation":"調諧質量阻尼器是耦合動力系統；它利用相對運動調整主系統反應。 觀景照片只能顯示裝置外形，不能直接給出控制性能或當時荷載。","explanationEn":"A tuned mass damper is a coupled dynamic system that uses relative motion to modify primary-system response. Observation-deck photos show device appearance, not control performance or concurrent loading."}},{"id":"b021-v7-14","sequence":14,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-13"],"title":"理解調諧與離調的差異","titleEn":"Understand tuning and detuning","objective":"用比較而非實樓設定值理解頻率匹配。","objectiveEn":"Understand frequency matching through comparison rather than real-building settings.","instruction":"1. 建立無量綱兩振子示例；2. 比較接近及偏離主頻率的輔助振子；3. 保持激振條件一致再比較反應曲線。","instructionEn":"1. Create a dimensionless two-oscillator example; 2. compare near-tuned and detuned auxiliary oscillators; 3. hold excitation fixed before comparing responses.","observation":"調諧效果取決於頻率關係與阻尼，不能只看質量大小。","observationEn":"Tuning performance depends on frequency relationships and damping, not mass alone.","failure":"阻尼球越重就能在所有頻率下消除全部晃動。","failureEn":"A heavier damper ball eliminates all motion at every frequency.","check":"繳交一致激振下的兩條比較曲線與假設。","checkEn":"Provide two response comparisons under identical excitation with assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-14-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"調諧具有頻率範圍；真實建築存在多模態，單一裝置不是所有反應的萬能解。","textEn":"Tuning is frequency-dependent; real buildings have multiple modes, so one device is not a universal remedy."},{"id":"b021-v7-14-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設模型只能展示參數敏感度，不能回推原裝置的調整方法。","textEn":"An invented model illustrates parameter sensitivity and cannot reconstruct adjustment procedures for the actual device."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「理解調諧與離調的差異」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Understand tuning and detuning”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["阻尼球越重就能在所有頻率下消除全部晃動。","調諧效果取決於頻率關係與阻尼，不能只看質量大小。","調諧裝置只影響單一時刻，與激振頻率無關。"],"optionsEn":["A heavier damper ball eliminates all motion at every frequency.","Tuning performance depends on frequency relationships and damping, not mass alone.","A tuned device affects only one instant and is independent of excitation frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"調諧具有頻率範圍；真實建築存在多模態，單一裝置不是所有反應的萬能解。 自設模型只能展示參數敏感度，不能回推原裝置的調整方法。","explanationEn":"Tuning is frequency-dependent; real buildings have multiple modes, so one device is not a universal remedy. An invented model illustrates parameter sensitivity and cannot reconstruct adjustment procedures for the actual device."}},{"id":"b021-v7-15","sequence":15,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-14"],"title":"拆解黏滯耗能與行程邊界","titleEn":"Separate viscous dissipation from stroke limits","objective":"理解阻尼與碰撞限制各自的功能。","objectiveEn":"Understand separate functions of damping and travel limits.","instruction":"1. 在雙振子圖標出相對速度；2. 用概念迴圈畫能量消散；3. 另以虛線標出有限行程而不設定實際數值。","instructionEn":"1. Mark relative velocity in the two-oscillator diagram; 2. sketch a conceptual dissipation loop; 3. mark finite travel separately without actual settings.","observation":"限制行程與消耗振動能量是不同但需協調的功能。","observationEn":"Limiting travel and dissipating vibration energy are distinct coordinated functions.","failure":"只要有止擋就不需要分析相對運動及耗能。","failureEn":"A stop makes relative-motion and energy-dissipation analysis unnecessary.","check":"提供耗能路徑及行程邊界的分色圖。","checkEn":"Provide a color-separated diagram of dissipation and travel boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-15-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"黏滯裝置可把機械能轉為熱；碰撞或止擋會改變系統的非線性反應。","textEn":"Viscous devices convert mechanical energy to heat; contact or stops change nonlinear system response."},{"id":"b021-v7-15-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"看見止擋或阻尼器的存在並不等於已驗證其安裝及可用狀態。","textEn":"The visible presence of stops or dampers does not verify their installation or availability."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆解黏滯耗能與行程邊界」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate viscous dissipation from stroke limits”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只要有止擋就不需要分析相對運動及耗能。","止擋接觸只限制位置，絕不改變系統動態反應。","限制行程與消耗振動能量是不同但需協調的功能。"],"optionsEn":["A stop makes relative-motion and energy-dissipation analysis unnecessary.","Stop contact only limits position and never changes system dynamics.","Limiting travel and dissipating vibration energy are distinct coordinated functions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"黏滯裝置可把機械能轉為熱；碰撞或止擋會改變系統的非線性反應。 看見止擋或阻尼器的存在並不等於已驗證其安裝及可用狀態。","explanationEn":"Viscous devices convert mechanical energy to heat; contact or stops change nonlinear system response. The visible presence of stops or dampers does not verify their installation or availability."}},{"id":"b021-v7-16","sequence":16,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-15"],"title":"比較位移、速度與加速度","titleEn":"Compare displacement, velocity and acceleration","objective":"選擇能回答問題的量測量。","objectiveEn":"Select observations that answer the intended question.","instruction":"1. 畫一條平滑概念位移曲線；2. 標出速度與加速度較大的區段；3. 將舒適與間隙問題配到不同觀察量。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a smooth conceptual displacement curve; 2. identify high-speed and high-acceleration portions; 3. map comfort and clearance questions to different observations.","observation":"相同峰值位移的兩段振動可能具有不同峰值加速度。","observationEn":"Two motions with equal peak displacement can have different peak accelerations.","failure":"最大位移相同便能保證使用者感受完全相同。","failureEn":"Equal maximum displacement guarantees identical occupant experience.","check":"繳交問題、觀察量與量測限制的三欄表。","checkEn":"Provide a table of questions, observations and measurement limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-16-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"對相同振幅的正弦運動，頻率改變會顯著影響加速度；不能只看位移。","textEn":"For equal-amplitude sinusoidal motion, frequency changes strongly affect acceleration; displacement alone is insufficient."},{"id":"b021-v7-16-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"數值微分會放大量測雜訊，觀察量轉換需要處理誤差。","textEn":"Numerical differentiation amplifies measurement noise, so converting observations requires error treatment."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較位移、速度與加速度」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare displacement, velocity and acceleration”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["相同峰值位移的兩段振動可能具有不同峰值加速度。","最大位移相同便能保證使用者感受完全相同。","將位移曲線微分不會增加量測雜訊影響。"],"optionsEn":["Two motions with equal peak displacement can have different peak accelerations.","Equal maximum displacement guarantees identical occupant experience.","Differentiating displacement never increases the effect of measurement noise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對相同振幅的正弦運動，頻率改變會顯著影響加速度；不能只看位移。 數值微分會放大量測雜訊，觀察量轉換需要處理誤差。","explanationEn":"For equal-amplitude sinusoidal motion, frequency changes strongly affect acceleration; displacement alone is insufficient. Numerical differentiation amplifies measurement noise, so converting observations requires error treatment."}},{"id":"b021-v7-17","sequence":17,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-16"],"title":"協調電梯與結構位移","titleEn":"Coordinate elevators with structural movement","objective":"理解垂直運輸設備也有結構介面。","objectiveEn":"Understand structural interfaces of vertical transportation.","instruction":"1. 畫電梯井與樓層連接；2. 標出樓層相對移動及設備固定點；3. 分列行車舒適、間隙與維修可達性的問題。","instructionEn":"1. Draw an elevator shaft and floor connections; 2. mark relative floor movement and fixing points; 3. separate ride comfort, clearance and maintenance-access questions.","observation":"結構能承載仍不代表所有設備介面在移動後保持功能。","observationEn":"Structural capacity does not establish continued function of every moving equipment interface.","failure":"電梯速度規格可以取代結構與設備介面的核對。","failureEn":"Elevator speed specifications replace structural-equipment interface checks.","check":"提交不含設備調整參數的介面核對清單。","checkEn":"Submit an interface checklist without equipment-adjustment settings.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-17-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"非結構設備的功能依賴固定方式、間隙及供電等條件，需與結構一起協調。","textEn":"Equipment function depends on fixings, clearances and power among other conditions, requiring coordination with structure."},{"id":"b021-v7-17-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"公開高速電梯資料是技術背景，不能用來指導現場調整或維修。","textEn":"Public high-speed-elevator information provides context, not field-adjustment or maintenance instructions."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「協調電梯與結構位移」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Coordinate elevators with structural movement”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["電梯速度規格可以取代結構與設備介面的核對。","結構能承載仍不代表所有設備介面在移動後保持功能。","電梯和樓層的固定點沒有任何結構作用。"],"optionsEn":["Elevator speed specifications replace structural-equipment interface checks.","Structural capacity does not establish continued function of every moving equipment interface.","Elevator-to-floor fixings have no structural role."],"answer":1,"explanation":"非結構設備的功能依賴固定方式、間隙及供電等條件，需與結構一起協調。 公開高速電梯資料是技術背景，不能用來指導現場調整或維修。","explanationEn":"Equipment function depends on fixings, clearances and power among other conditions, requiring coordination with structure. Public high-speed-elevator information provides context, not field-adjustment or maintenance instructions."}},{"id":"b021-v7-18","sequence":18,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-17"],"title":"完成風振證據審查","titleEn":"Review wind-motion evidence","objective":"區分裝置展示、模型結果與實測證據。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish device displays, model outputs and measurements.","instruction":"1. 選一張裝置照片與自設曲線；2. 為每項結論標記照片、模型或實測需求；3. 刪除超出現有證據範圍的性能宣稱。","instructionEn":"1. Select a device photo and synthetic response curve; 2. label conclusions as photo-based, model-based or requiring measurement; 3. remove unsupported performance claims.","observation":"模型顯示反應下降仍需實際條件與量測驗證才能推論真樓性能。","observationEn":"Reduced model response still needs actual conditions and measurements before inferring real-building performance.","failure":"阻尼球照片足以量出任一次颱風中的減振百分比。","failureEn":"A damper-ball photo establishes the vibration-reduction percentage in any typhoon.","check":"提交每項結論均有證據層級的審查表。","checkEn":"Submit a review table assigning an evidence level to every conclusion.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-18-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"公開展示能解釋裝置用途，但定量驗證需要輸入、感測器、分析方法與誤差。","textEn":"A public display explains purpose, while quantitative verification needs inputs, sensors, analysis and uncertainty."},{"id":"b021-v7-18-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"沒有實測資料時應保留待查項，不能用自設數據填補成真實表現。","textEn":"Without measurements, retain evidence gaps instead of presenting synthetic data as actual performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「完成風振證據審查」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review wind-motion evidence”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["阻尼球照片足以量出任一次颱風中的減振百分比。","從裝置質量可直接推出所有颱風的減振比例。","模型顯示反應下降仍需實際條件與量測驗證才能推論真樓性能。"],"optionsEn":["A damper-ball photo establishes the vibration-reduction percentage in any typhoon.","Device mass directly determines the reduction ratio for every typhoon.","Reduced model response still needs actual conditions and measurements before inferring real-building performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公開展示能解釋裝置用途，但定量驗證需要輸入、感測器、分析方法與誤差。 沒有實測資料時應保留待查項，不能用自設數據填補成真實表現。","explanationEn":"A public display explains purpose, while quantitative verification needs inputs, sensors, analysis and uncertainty. Without measurements, retain evidence gaps instead of presenting synthetic data as actual performance."}}]},{"id":"b021-stage04","order":4,"title":"施工證據與全生命週期","titleEn":"Construction evidence and lifecycle","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「施工證據與全生命週期」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on construction evidence and lifecycle, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v7-19","sequence":19,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-18"],"title":"拆分施工階段與完成狀態","titleEn":"Separate construction and completed states","objective":"辨認逐層建造時尚未形成的系統。","objectiveEn":"Identify systems not yet established during staged construction.","instruction":"1. 畫三個不同完成高度；2. 標示各自已連接的核心與周邊部分；3. 對未形成的外伸系統列出概念邊界問題。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch three completion heights; 2. mark connected core and perimeter portions; 3. list boundary questions for incomplete outrigger systems.","observation":"未完成外伸系統時的荷載分配可能不同於竣工模型。","observationEn":"Load sharing before outrigger completion may differ from the completed model.","failure":"竣工分析通過即可直接證明所有樓層施工狀態。","failureEn":"A completed-state analysis directly verifies every construction stage.","check":"輸出三個狀態的系統有無及證據需求表。","checkEn":"Provide a system-presence and evidence table for three states.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-19-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"建造順序會改變暫時剛度、荷載與約束，施工狀態需獨立辨識。","textEn":"Construction sequence changes temporary stiffness, loads and constraints; each state needs identification."},{"id":"b021-v7-19-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程不提供吊裝或臨時支撐方案，只訓練閱讀依賴關係。","textEn":"This course provides no lifting or temporary-support scheme; it teaches dependency interpretation."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆分施工階段與完成狀態」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate construction and completed states”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["未完成外伸系統時的荷載分配可能不同於竣工模型。","竣工分析通過即可直接證明所有樓層施工狀態。","不同完成高度必然具有同一組剛度與約束。"],"optionsEn":["Load sharing before outrigger completion may differ from the completed model.","A completed-state analysis directly verifies every construction stage.","Different completion heights necessarily share identical stiffness and restraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建造順序會改變暫時剛度、荷載與約束，施工狀態需獨立辨識。 本課程不提供吊裝或臨時支撐方案，只訓練閱讀依賴關係。","explanationEn":"Construction sequence changes temporary stiffness, loads and constraints; each state needs identification. This course provides no lifting or temporary-support scheme; it teaches dependency interpretation."}},{"id":"b021-v7-20","sequence":20,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-19"],"title":"追蹤差異縮短與量測基準","titleEn":"Track differential shortening and datums","objective":"理解垂直構件並非以相同比例縮短。","objectiveEn":"Understand why vertical members need not shorten equally.","instruction":"1. 畫核心與周邊柱兩條高度線；2. 加入不同的自設縮短曲線；3. 比較樓層接合及設備介面的相對偏差。","instructionEn":"1. Draw core and perimeter height lines; 2. add different synthetic shortening curves; 3. compare relative offsets at floor and equipment interfaces.","observation":"共同的總樓高不會消除核心與周邊之間的差異縮短。","observationEn":"A common total height does not eliminate differential shortening between core and perimeter.","failure":"把頂樓高度調齊就能保證每層介面都一致。","failureEn":"Aligning the roof height guarantees alignment at every floor interface.","check":"提交相對縮短圖並標明時間與基準假設。","checkEn":"Provide a relative-shortening plot with time and datum assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-20-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"彈性壓縮、材料長期變形與施工加載歷程都可影響垂直變形。","textEn":"Elastic compression, long-term material behavior and construction loading history can affect vertical deformation."},{"id":"b021-v7-20-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"需比較同一基準及時間狀態的數據，否則可能把正常歷程誤判成偏差。","textEn":"Compare data under the same datum and time state to avoid mistaking normal evolution for error."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「追蹤差異縮短與量測基準」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Track differential shortening and datums”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把頂樓高度調齊就能保證每層介面都一致。","共同的總樓高不會消除核心與周邊之間的差異縮短。","只有最高樓層才會受到垂直縮短影響。"],"optionsEn":["Aligning the roof height guarantees alignment at every floor interface.","A common total height does not eliminate differential shortening between core and perimeter.","Only the top floor is affected by vertical shortening."],"answer":1,"explanation":"彈性壓縮、材料長期變形與施工加載歷程都可影響垂直變形。 需比較同一基準及時間狀態的數據，否則可能把正常歷程誤判成偏差。","explanationEn":"Elastic compression, long-term material behavior and construction loading history can affect vertical deformation. Compare data under the same datum and time state to avoid mistaking normal evolution for error."}},{"id":"b021-v7-21","sequence":21,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-20"],"title":"檢查帷幕牆與樓層移動相容","titleEn":"Review façade and floor-movement compatibility","objective":"辨認非結構外牆與承重骨架的相對位移。","objectiveEn":"Identify relative movement between a nonstructural façade and the load-bearing frame.","instruction":"1. 畫跨越兩層的概念帷幕單元；2. 分別加入層間側移與差異縮短；3. 標示接頭、固定點及需查證的空間。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a conceptual façade unit spanning two floors; 2. add story drift and differential shortening separately; 3. mark joints, fixings and clearances requiring evidence.","observation":"結構保持承載功能仍需另外核對外牆接頭的位移相容。","observationEn":"Retained structural capacity still requires separate verification of movement compatibility at façade joints.","failure":"樓層位移在結構模型中合理就表示每個外牆接頭都不會受影響。","failureEn":"Acceptable floor movements in a structural model guarantee that every façade joint remains unaffected.","check":"提交兩種位移模式與外牆介面的配對圖。","checkEn":"Submit a diagram matching two movement modes to façade interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-21-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"帷幕牆的固定與接縫需要容納相關移動，非承重不代表沒有工程性能需求。","textEn":"Façade fixings and joints must accommodate relevant movement; non-load-bearing does not mean free of performance requirements."},{"id":"b021-v7-21-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步單元為自繪示意，不代表台北 101 實際外牆固定細節或容許位移。","textEn":"The teaching unit does not represent Taipei 101’s actual façade fixing details or permissible movements."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檢查帷幕牆與樓層移動相容」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review façade and floor-movement compatibility”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["樓層位移在結構模型中合理就表示每個外牆接頭都不會受影響。","非承重外牆不需要任何位移相容要求。","結構保持承載功能仍需另外核對外牆接頭的位移相容。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable floor movements in a structural model guarantee that every façade joint remains unaffected.","A non-load-bearing façade needs no movement-compatibility requirements.","Retained structural capacity still requires separate verification of movement compatibility at façade joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"帷幕牆的固定與接縫需要容納相關移動，非承重不代表沒有工程性能需求。 本步單元為自繪示意，不代表台北 101 實際外牆固定細節或容許位移。","explanationEn":"Façade fixings and joints must accommodate relevant movement; non-load-bearing does not mean free of performance requirements. The teaching unit does not represent Taipei 101’s actual façade fixing details or permissible movements."}},{"id":"b021-v7-22","sequence":22,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-21"],"title":"建立結構與營運變更紀錄","titleEn":"Create a structural and operational change log","objective":"讓改裝及設備更新留下可追溯介面。","objectiveEn":"Preserve traceable interfaces through refits and equipment changes.","instruction":"1. 提出一個假想機械層設備更新；2. 列出質量、振動及維修空間改變；3. 指向必須重新審查的結構與機電資料。","instructionEn":"1. Propose a hypothetical mechanical-floor equipment replacement; 2. list mass, vibration and maintenance-space changes; 3. identify structural and service records needing review.","observation":"用途或設備改變可能影響既有結構假設，即使建築外觀不變。","observationEn":"Changes in use or equipment can affect structural assumptions even when the exterior is unchanged.","failure":"室內改裝不改外牆就不必做任何介面審查。","failureEn":"An interior refit leaving the façade unchanged needs no interface review.","check":"提交一筆包含原因、影響、版本與待核事項的變更紀錄。","checkEn":"Submit a change record with rationale, impacts, versions and open checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-22-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"全生命週期管理需要保留原假設與變更後條件，才能判斷資料是否仍適用。","textEn":"Lifecycle management retains original assumptions and changed conditions to judge continued applicability."},{"id":"b021-v7-22-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程假想更新並不表示台北 101 正在進行該項改裝。","textEn":"The hypothetical replacement does not imply Taipei 101 is undertaking that refit."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立結構與營運變更紀錄」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a structural and operational change log”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["用途或設備改變可能影響既有結構假設，即使建築外觀不變。","室內改裝不改外牆就不必做任何介面審查。","更新設備重量相同就能省略所有振動和維修介面。"],"optionsEn":["Changes in use or equipment can affect structural assumptions even when the exterior is unchanged.","An interior refit leaving the façade unchanged needs no interface review.","Equal replacement-equipment weight removes every vibration and maintenance interface question."],"answer":0,"explanation":"全生命週期管理需要保留原假設與變更後條件，才能判斷資料是否仍適用。 課程假想更新並不表示台北 101 正在進行該項改裝。","explanationEn":"Lifecycle management retains original assumptions and changed conditions to judge continued applicability. The hypothetical replacement does not imply Taipei 101 is undertaking that refit."}},{"id":"b021-v7-23","sequence":23,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-22"],"title":"比較其他超高層的抗側系統","titleEn":"Compare lateral systems in other towers","objective":"建立台北 101 與其他巨作的可比問題。","objectiveEn":"Create comparable questions for Taipei 101 and other landmark towers.","instruction":"1. 選上海中心或哈里發塔作延伸研究；2. 先查其主要結構系統；3. 比較核心、周邊及氣動外形的分工並標示未知。","instructionEn":"1. Select Shanghai Tower or Burj Khalifa for further study; 2. verify its main structural system; 3. compare core, perimeter and aerodynamic-form roles while marking unknowns.","observation":"同為超高層建築不代表阻尼器、核心或外伸系統配置相同。","observationEn":"Supertall status does not imply identical damper, core or outrigger layouts.","failure":"外觀都逐層收分就能推定使用同一套抗側系統。","failureEn":"Tapered silhouettes establish identical lateral systems.","check":"提交兩項可比問題及至少三項需另查的設計差異。","checkEn":"Submit two comparable questions and at least three design differences needing evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-23-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"比較先對齊需求與模型邊界，再討論幾何或構件，才能避免用外觀取代機理。","textEn":"Align requirements and model boundaries before comparing geometry or members to avoid substituting appearance for mechanism."},{"id":"b021-v7-23-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"延伸項目是下一個資料查證任務；沒有來源支持的細節應明確留白。","textEn":"The related project begins a new evidence task; leave unsupported details explicitly unknown."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較其他超高層的抗側系統」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare lateral systems in other towers”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["外觀都逐層收分就能推定使用同一套抗側系統。","同為超高層建築不代表阻尼器、核心或外伸系統配置相同。","所有超高層都有與台北 101 完全相同的調諧質量阻尼器。"],"optionsEn":["Tapered silhouettes establish identical lateral systems.","Supertall status does not imply identical damper, core or outrigger layouts.","Every supertall has exactly the same tuned mass damper as Taipei 101."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較先對齊需求與模型邊界，再討論幾何或構件，才能避免用外觀取代機理。 延伸項目是下一個資料查證任務；沒有來源支持的細節應明確留白。","explanationEn":"Align requirements and model boundaries before comparing geometry or members to avoid substituting appearance for mechanism. The related project begins a new evidence task; leave unsupported details explicitly unknown."}},{"id":"b021-v7-24","sequence":24,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-taipei-engineer","v7-taipei-damper","v7-taipei-history","v7-taipei-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-23"],"title":"審查全生命週期證據包","titleEn":"Review the lifecycle evidence pack","objective":"把地標學習轉成可重複使用的工程查證方法。","objectiveEn":"Turn landmark study into a reusable engineering-verification method.","instruction":"1. 彙整場址、力路徑、動力及介面圖；2. 為每張圖標記來源與假設；3. 用一個新設備情境測試是否能追到受影響結論。","instructionEn":"1. Assemble site, force, dynamics and interface diagrams; 2. label sources and assumptions; 3. use one new-equipment scenario to trace affected conclusions.","observation":"有版本的圖與假設清單比單一漂亮模型更便於維護與複查。","observationEn":"Versioned diagrams and assumption registers support maintenance and review better than one polished model.","failure":"只要動態示意看起來平穩，就能作為真樓性能認證。","failureEn":"A stable-looking animation constitutes certification of actual building performance.","check":"提交含未解問題的四階段學習報告。","checkEn":"Submit a four-stage learning report including unresolved questions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v7-24-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"高樓工程把結構、機電、使用與維護連在一起，任何一個層面的成功都不能代替整體驗證。","textEn":"Tall-building engineering connects structure, services, use and maintenance; success in one area does not replace system verification."},{"id":"b021-v7-24-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"學習報告記錄概念能力與查證方法，不是結構設計或設備維修的執業證明。","textEn":"The report records conceptual skills and verification methods, not professional authorization for design or equipment maintenance."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「審查全生命週期證據包」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review the lifecycle evidence pack”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只要動態示意看起來平穩，就能作為真樓性能認證。","結構、設備與使用三者可以完全獨立驗證而忽略交界。","有版本的圖與假設清單比單一漂亮模型更便於維護與複查。"],"optionsEn":["A stable-looking animation constitutes certification of actual building performance.","Structure, equipment and use can be verified independently while ignoring their interfaces.","Versioned diagrams and assumption registers support maintenance and review better than one polished model."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高樓工程把結構、機電、使用與維護連在一起，任何一個層面的成功都不能代替整體驗證。 學習報告記錄概念能力與查證方法，不是結構設計或設備維修的執業證明。","explanationEn":"Tall-building engineering connects structure, services, use and maintenance; success in one area does not replace system verification. The report records conceptual skills and verification methods, not professional authorization for design or equipment maintenance."}}]},{"id":"b021-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「三級風力準則與角隅修形」與「外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping\" and \"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v13-01","title":"三級風力準則與角隅修形：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v7-24"],"objective":"說明「角隅鋸齒缺角」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sawtooth corner notches” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 的風工程不是單一設計風速，而是三組回歸期各管一件事：約半年回歸期檢核居住舒適度、50 年回歸期檢核變位、100 年回歸期檢核構材強度。風洞試驗後，建築在四個角隅做出鋸齒狀缺角，讓氣流在角部提早分離並打亂整齊的渦流脫落，使橫風向反應明顯降低。角隅修形同時改變帷幕牆的局部風壓分布，因此構架、阻尼器與外牆三方都必須使用同一份風洞資料，而不是各自套用規範公式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「角隅鋸齒缺角」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101's wind engineering is not one design wind speed but three return periods, each governing a different check: roughly a half-year event for occupant comfort, a 50-year event for drift and a 100-year event for member strength. After wind-tunnel testing, the four corners were given sawtooth notches that trigger early flow separation and break up organised vortex shedding, clearly reducing across-wind response. Corner shaping also changes local cladding pressures, so the frame, damper and façade teams must all work from the same wind-tunnel dataset rather than each applying code formulas on their own. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Sawtooth corner notches” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以均布等效風壓估計基底彎矩 M = ½·q·C·B·H²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate the base moment from a uniform equivalent pressure, M = ½·q·C·B·H².","failure":"常見誤解：「角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「角隅鋸齒缺角」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Sawtooth corner notches”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-01-k1","title":"三級風力準則與角隅修形","titleEn":"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping","text":"台北 101 的風工程不是單一設計風速，而是三組回歸期各管一件事：約半年回歸期檢核居住舒適度、50 年回歸期檢核變位、100 年回歸期檢核構材強度。風洞試驗後，建築在四個角隅做出鋸齒狀缺角，讓氣流在角部提早分離並打亂整齊的渦流脫落，使橫風向反應明顯降低。","textEn":"Taipei 101's wind engineering is not one design wind speed but three return periods, each governing a different check: roughly a half-year event for occupant comfort, a 50-year event for drift and a 100-year event for member strength. After wind-tunnel testing, the four corners were given sawtooth notches that trigger early flow separation and break up organised vortex shedding, clearly reducing across-wind response.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「三級風力準則與角隅修形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping\" is correct?","options":["角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。","台北 101 的風工程不是單一設計風速，而是三組回歸期各管一件事：約半年回歸期檢核居住舒適度、50 年回歸期檢核變位、100 年回歸期檢核構材強度。","外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。"],"optionsEn":["Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads.","Taipei 101's wind engineering is not one design wind speed but three return periods, each governing a different check: roughly a half-year event for occupant comfort, a 50-year event for drift and a 100-year event for member strength.","The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most."],"answer":1,"explanation":"台北 101 的風工程不是單一設計風速，而是三組回歸期各管一件事：約半年回歸期檢核居住舒適度、50 年回歸期檢核變位、100 年回歸期檢核構材強度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101's wind engineering is not one design wind speed but three return periods, each governing a different check: roughly a half-year event for occupant comfort, a 50-year event for drift and a 100-year event for member strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b021-v13-02","title":"三級風力準則與角隅修形：定量估算","titleEn":"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「角隅鋸齒缺角」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sawtooth corner notches” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以均布等效風壓估計基底彎矩 M = ½·q·C·B·H²。取 q = 2.5 kPa、C = 1.3、B = 50 m、H = 500 m，M = 0.5×2,500×1.3×50×500² ≈ 20.3 GN·m；若角隅修形使等效係數降低 25%，M 約降為 15.2 GN·m，基礎與巨柱軸力隨之同比例減少。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate the base moment from a uniform equivalent pressure, M = ½·q·C·B·H². With q = 2.5 kPa, C = 1.3, B = 50 m and H = 500 m, M = 0.5×2,500×1.3×50×500² ≈ 20.3 GN·m; if corner shaping lowers the equivalent coefficient by 25%, M falls to about 15.2 GN·m and foundation and mega-column forces drop in proportion. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：要求風洞報告分別列出三種回歸期的基底彎矩、變位與頂層加速度，並附角隅修形與未修形的比較試驗；高頻力平衡結果要以結構實際模態重新組合，再與規範公式估算比對，差異超過約兩成時必須查明原因並書面說明。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Require the wind-tunnel report to list base moments, drifts and top-floor accelerations separately for the three return periods, with comparative tests of notched and unnotched corners; recombine force-balance results with the structure's actual modes, compare with code-formula estimates, and investigate and document any difference larger than about 20%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以均布等效風壓估計基底彎矩 M = ½·q·C·B·H²。取 q = 2.5 kPa、C = 1.3、B = 50 m、H = 500 m，M = 0.5×2,500×1.3×50×500² ≈ 20.3 GN·m；若角隅修形使等效係數降低 25%，M 約降為 15.2 GN·m，基礎與巨柱軸力隨之同比例減少。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate the base moment from a uniform equivalent pressure, M = ½·q·C·B·H². With q = 2.5 kPa, C = 1.3, B = 50 m and H = 500 m, M = 0.5×2,500×1.3×50×500² ≈ 20.3 GN·m; if corner shaping lowers the equivalent coefficient by 25%, M falls to about 15.2 GN·m and foundation and mega-column forces drop in proportion. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「三級風力準則與角隅修形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。","塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","以均布等效風壓估計基底彎矩 M = ½·q·C·B·H²。"],"optionsEn":["The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter.","Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","Estimate the base moment from a uniform equivalent pressure, M = ½·q·C·B·H²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以均布等效風壓估計基底彎矩 M = ½·q·C·B·H²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate the base moment from a uniform equivalent pressure, M = ½·q·C·B·H². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b021-v13-03","title":"三級風力準則與角隅修形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「角隅鋸齒缺角」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sawtooth corner notches” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"要求風洞報告分別列出三種回歸期的基底彎矩、變位與頂層加速度，並附角隅修形與未修形的比較試驗；高頻力平衡結果要以結構實際模態重新組合，再與規範公式估算比對，差異超過約兩成時必須查明原因並書面說明。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Require the wind-tunnel report to list base moments, drifts and top-floor accelerations separately for the three return periods, with comparative tests of notched and unnotched corners; recombine force-balance results with the structure's actual modes, compare with code-formula estimates, and investigate and document any difference larger than about 20%. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把三級風力準則與允收值寫入結構設計基準書，任何外形變更（角隅尺寸、塔頂與帷幕牆突出物）都必須回送風工程顧問評估，並在變更紀錄中保留風洞比對資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write the three-tier wind criteria and acceptance values into the structural design basis, send any change of external form (corner dimensions, crown, façade projections) back to the wind consultant for assessment, and keep the wind-tunnel comparison in the change record.","failure":"注意干擾：若只拿 100 年強度風載設計構架而未檢核半年回歸期加速度，結構雖安全，常見颱風時高樓層使用者仍會明顯不適；若角隅缺角在施工中為了帷幕牆單元化而被簡化，實際風力可能回到未修形的較高水準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Designing the frame only for 100-year strength loads without checking half-year accelerations leaves a safe structure that still makes upper-floor occupants uncomfortable in common typhoons; if the corner notches are simplified during construction to ease unitised cladding, actual wind forces can revert to the higher unnotched level. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"要求風洞報告分別列出三種回歸期的基底彎矩、變位與頂層加速度，並附角隅修形與未修形的比較試驗；高頻力平衡結果要以結構實際模態重新組合，再與規範公式估算比對，差異超過約兩成時必須查明原因並書面說明。","textEn":"Require the wind-tunnel report to list base moments, drifts and top-floor accelerations separately for the three return periods, with comparative tests of notched and unnotched corners; recombine force-balance results with the structure's actual modes, compare with code-formula estimates, and investigate and document any difference larger than about 20%.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把三級風力準則與允收值寫入結構設計基準書，任何外形變更（角隅尺寸、塔頂與帷幕牆突出物）都必須回送風工程顧問評估，並在變更紀錄中保留風洞比對資料。","textEn":"Write the three-tier wind criteria and acceptance values into the structural design basis, send any change of external form (corner dimensions, crown, façade projections) back to the wind consultant for assessment, and keep the wind-tunnel comparison in the change record.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「三級風力準則與角隅修形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping\"?","options":["要求風洞報告分別列出三種回歸期的基底彎矩、變位與頂層加速度，並附角隅修形與未修形的比較試驗。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。"],"optionsEn":["Require the wind-tunnel report to list base moments, drifts and top-floor accelerations separately for the three return periods, with comparative tests of notched and unnotched corners.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"要求風洞報告分別列出三種回歸期的基底彎矩、變位與頂層加速度，並附角隅修形與未修形的比較試驗；高頻力平衡結果要以結構實際模態重新組合，再與規範公式估算比對，差異超過約兩成時必須查明原因並書面說明。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Require the wind-tunnel report to list base moments, drifts and top-floor accelerations separately for the three return periods, with comparative tests of notched and unnotched corners; recombine force-balance results with the structure's actual modes, compare with code-formula estimates, and investigate and document any difference larger than about 20%. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b021-v13-04","title":"三級風力準則與角隅修形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「角隅鋸齒缺角」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sawtooth corner notches” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只拿 100 年強度風載設計構架而未檢核半年回歸期加速度，結構雖安全，常見颱風時高樓層使用者仍會明顯不適；若角隅缺角在施工中為了帷幕牆單元化而被簡化，實際風力可能回到未修形的較高水準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Designing the frame only for 100-year strength loads without checking half-year accelerations leaves a safe structure that still makes upper-floor occupants uncomfortable in common typhoons; if the corner notches are simplified during construction to ease unitised cladding, actual wind forces can revert to the higher unnotched level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：角隅修形同時改變帷幕牆的局部風壓分布，因此構架、阻尼器與外牆三方都必須使用同一份風洞資料，而不是各自套用規範公式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Corner shaping also changes local cladding pressures, so the frame, damper and façade teams must all work from the same wind-tunnel dataset rather than each applying code formulas on their own.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只拿 100 年強度風載設計構架而未檢核半年回歸期加速度，結構雖安全，常見颱風時高樓層使用者仍會明顯不適；若角隅缺角在施工中為了帷幕牆單元化而被簡化，實際風力可能回到未修形的較高水準。","textEn":"Designing the frame only for 100-year strength loads without checking half-year accelerations leaves a safe structure that still makes upper-floor occupants uncomfortable in common typhoons; if the corner notches are simplified during construction to ease unitised cladding, actual wind forces can revert to the higher unnotched level.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「三級風力準則與角隅修形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Three-tier wind criteria and corner shaping\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只拿 100 年強度風載設計構架而未檢核半年回歸期加速度，結構雖安全，常見颱風時高樓層使用者仍會明顯不適。","外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Designing the frame only for 100-year strength loads without checking half-year accelerations leaves a safe structure that still makes upper-floor occupants uncomfortable in common typhoons.","The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只拿 100 年強度風載設計構架而未檢核半年回歸期加速度，結構雖安全，常見颱風時高樓層使用者仍會明顯不適；若角隅缺角在施工中為了帷幕牆單元化而被簡化，實際風力可能回到未修形的較高水準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Designing the frame only for 100-year strength loads without checking half-year accelerations leaves a safe structure that still makes upper-floor occupants uncomfortable in common typhoons; if the corner notches are simplified during construction to ease unitised cladding, actual wind forces can revert to the higher unnotched level. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b021-v13-05","title":"外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「八支巨柱的力偶」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eight-mega-column couple” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 周邊有八支巨柱（每面兩支），26 樓以下每面另有次巨柱與角柱經帶狀桁架加入；外伸桁架約每 8 至 10 層一道，依位置做成單層、雙層或三層高。核心筒受風彎曲時，外伸桁架像槓桿一樣把核心的轉角變成巨柱軸力：一側減壓、另一側增壓，形成力偶抵抗大部分傾覆彎矩。因為巨柱本身已承受很大的重力壓力，風或地震造成的軸力變化多半只是減少壓力，但柱續接仍須檢核少量的淨上拉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「八支巨柱的力偶」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101 has eight perimeter mega-columns, two per face; below level 26, sub-super columns and corner columns on each face are engaged through belt trusses. Outriggers occur about every 8 to 10 floors and are one, two or three storeys deep depending on location. When the core bends in wind, the outriggers act as levers that turn core rotation into mega-column axial force, unloading one side and adding compression to the other, so a couple resists most of the overturning moment. Because the mega-columns already carry heavy gravity compression, wind or seismic axial changes mostly reduce compression, yet column splices must still be checked for small net uplift. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Eight-mega-column couple” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：巨柱力偶 ΔN = M_col/(a·n)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Mega-column couple ΔN = M_col/(a·n).","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「八支巨柱的力偶」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Eight-mega-column couple”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-05-k1","title":"外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力","titleEn":"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force","text":"台北 101 周邊有八支巨柱（每面兩支），26 樓以下每面另有次巨柱與角柱經帶狀桁架加入；外伸桁架約每 8 至 10 層一道，依位置做成單層、雙層或三層高。核心筒受風彎曲時，外伸桁架像槓桿一樣把核心的轉角變成巨柱軸力：一側減壓、另一側增壓，形成力偶抵抗大部分傾覆彎矩。","textEn":"Taipei 101 has eight perimeter mega-columns, two per face; below level 26, sub-super columns and corner columns on each face are engaged through belt trusses. Outriggers occur about every 8 to 10 floors and are one, two or three storeys deep depending on location.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force\" is correct?","options":["外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。","鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。","台北 101 周邊有八支巨柱（每面兩支），26 樓以下每面另有次巨柱與角柱經帶狀桁架加入；外伸桁架約每 8 至 10 層一道，依位置做成單層、雙層或三層高。"],"optionsEn":["The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most.","The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.","Taipei 101 has eight perimeter mega-columns, two per face; below level 26, sub-super columns and corner columns on each face are engaged through belt trusses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"台北 101 周邊有八支巨柱（每面兩支），26 樓以下每面另有次巨柱與角柱經帶狀桁架加入；外伸桁架約每 8 至 10 層一道，依位置做成單層、雙層或三層高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101 has eight perimeter mega-columns, two per face; below level 26, sub-super columns and corner columns on each face are engaged through belt trusses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b021-v13-06","title":"外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力：定量估算","titleEn":"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「八支巨柱的力偶」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eight-mega-column couple” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：巨柱力偶 ΔN = M_col/(a·n)。若外伸桁架交給巨柱的彎矩 M_col = 12 GN·m，受拉側與受壓側巨柱群形心距 a = 40 m、每側 n = 4 支，ΔN = 12×10⁹/(40×4) = 75 MN；重力軸力若為 350 MN，風作用時兩側分別為 275 MN 與 425 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Mega-column couple ΔN = M_col/(a·n). If the outriggers deliver M_col = 12 GN·m to the columns, with a = 40 m between tension-side and compression-side group centroids and n = 4 columns per side, ΔN = 12×10⁹/(40×4) = 75 MN; with 350 MN of gravity load, the two sides carry 275 MN and 425 MN under wind. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在三維模型中分別輸出核心與巨柱各自承擔的傾覆彎矩比例，並與只有核心時的頂層變位比較；再以手算力偶核對各道外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿力，確認每一道外伸桁架的分擔比例與其勁度排序一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Output from the three-dimensional model the share of overturning carried by the core and by the mega-columns, and compare top drift with a core-only model; then check the chord and diagonal forces in each outrigger level with a hand couple calculation, confirming that each level's share matches its stiffness ranking.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"巨柱力偶 ΔN = M_col/(a·n)。若外伸桁架交給巨柱的彎矩 M_col = 12 GN·m，受拉側與受壓側巨柱群形心距 a = 40 m、每側 n = 4 支，ΔN = 12×10⁹/(40×4) = 75 MN；重力軸力若為 350 MN，風作用時兩側分別為 275 MN 與 425 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Mega-column couple ΔN = M_col/(a·n). If the outriggers deliver M_col = 12 GN·m to the columns, with a = 40 m between tension-side and compression-side group centroids and n = 4 columns per side, ΔN = 12×10⁹/(40×4) = 75 MN; with 350 MN of gravity load, the two sides carry 275 MN and 425 MN under wind. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force\", which statement holds?","options":["巨柱力偶 ΔN = M_col/(a·n)。","只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。","自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。"],"optionsEn":["Mega-column couple ΔN = M_col/(a·n).","Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored.","Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"巨柱力偶 ΔN = M_col/(a·n)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Mega-column couple ΔN = M_col/(a·n). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b021-v13-07","title":"外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「八支巨柱的力偶」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eight-mega-column couple” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在三維模型中分別輸出核心與巨柱各自承擔的傾覆彎矩比例，並與只有核心時的頂層變位比較；再以手算力偶核對各道外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿力，確認每一道外伸桁架的分擔比例與其勁度排序一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Output from the three-dimensional model the share of overturning carried by the core and by the mega-columns, and compare top drift with a core-only model; then check the chord and diagonal forces in each outrigger level with a hand couple calculation, confirming that each level's share matches its stiffness ranking. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在設計書中列出每一道外伸桁架的樓層、深度、所連接的巨柱與分擔比例，柱續接處標明最大淨上拉的載重組合，並要求鋼構製造圖保留這些標記以便現場查核。","observationEn":"Site practice: List in the design report each outrigger's level, depth, connected mega-columns and share of overturning, mark the governing net-uplift load combination at column splices, and require shop drawings to carry these marks for site checking.","failure":"注意干擾：若外伸桁架與巨柱接合的勁度被高估，模型中的力偶會比實際大，核心筒承受的彎矩被低估；反之若接合過早鎖固而未考慮差異縮短，巨柱與外伸桁架會在完工後承受額外的重力附加力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overestimating the stiffness of outrigger-to-column joints makes the modelled couple larger than reality and understates core bending; conversely, locking the joints too early without allowing for differential shortening imposes additional gravity-induced forces on columns and outriggers after completion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在三維模型中分別輸出核心與巨柱各自承擔的傾覆彎矩比例，並與只有核心時的頂層變位比較；再以手算力偶核對各道外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿力，確認每一道外伸桁架的分擔比例與其勁度排序一致。","textEn":"Output from the three-dimensional model the share of overturning carried by the core and by the mega-columns, and compare top drift with a core-only model; then check the chord and diagonal forces in each outrigger level with a hand couple calculation, confirming that each level's share matches its stiffness ranking.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在設計書中列出每一道外伸桁架的樓層、深度、所連接的巨柱與分擔比例，柱續接處標明最大淨上拉的載重組合，並要求鋼構製造圖保留這些標記以便現場查核。","textEn":"List in the design report each outrigger's level, depth, connected mega-columns and share of overturning, mark the governing net-uplift load combination at column splices, and require shop drawings to carry these marks for site checking.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在三維模型中分別輸出核心與巨柱各自承擔的傾覆彎矩比例，並與只有核心時的頂層變位比較。","阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Output from the three-dimensional model the share of overturning carried by the core and by the mega-columns, and compare top drift with a core-only model.","A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在三維模型中分別輸出核心與巨柱各自承擔的傾覆彎矩比例，並與只有核心時的頂層變位比較；再以手算力偶核對各道外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿力，確認每一道外伸桁架的分擔比例與其勁度排序一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Output from the three-dimensional model the share of overturning carried by the core and by the mega-columns, and compare top drift with a core-only model; then check the chord and diagonal forces in each outrigger level with a hand couple calculation, confirming that each level's share matches its stiffness ranking. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b021-v13-08","title":"外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「八支巨柱的力偶」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eight-mega-column couple” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若外伸桁架與巨柱接合的勁度被高估，模型中的力偶會比實際大，核心筒承受的彎矩被低估；反之若接合過早鎖固而未考慮差異縮短，巨柱與外伸桁架會在完工後承受額外的重力附加力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overestimating the stiffness of outrigger-to-column joints makes the modelled couple larger than reality and understates core bending; conversely, locking the joints too early without allowing for differential shortening imposes additional gravity-induced forces on columns and outriggers after completion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因為巨柱本身已承受很大的重力壓力，風或地震造成的軸力變化多半只是減少壓力，但柱續接仍須檢核少量的淨上拉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Because the mega-columns already carry heavy gravity compression, wind or seismic axial changes mostly reduce compression, yet column splices must still be checked for small net uplift.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若外伸桁架與巨柱接合的勁度被高估，模型中的力偶會比實際大，核心筒承受的彎矩被低估；反之若接合過早鎖固而未考慮差異縮短，巨柱與外伸桁架會在完工後承受額外的重力附加力。","textEn":"Overestimating the stiffness of outrigger-to-column joints makes the modelled couple larger than reality and understates core bending; conversely, locking the joints too early without allowing for differential shortening imposes additional gravity-induced forces on columns and outriggers after completion.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸桁架把傾覆彎矩轉成巨柱軸力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outriggers turn overturning into mega-column axial force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。","若外伸桁架與巨柱接合的勁度被高估，模型中的力偶會比實際大，核心筒承受的彎矩被低估。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.","Overestimating the stiffness of outrigger-to-column joints makes the modelled couple larger than reality and understates core bending."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若外伸桁架與巨柱接合的勁度被高估，模型中的力偶會比實際大，核心筒承受的彎矩被低估；反之若接合過早鎖固而未考慮差異縮短，巨柱與外伸桁架會在完工後承受額外的重力附加力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overestimating the stiffness of outrigger-to-column joints makes the modelled couple larger than reality and understates core bending; conversely, locking the joints too early without allowing for differential shortening imposes additional gravity-induced forces on columns and outriggers after completion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":5},{"id":"b021-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量」與「高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity\" and \"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v13-09","title":"巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 的巨柱底部約 2.4 m × 3.0 m，由厚 50 至 80 mm 的鋼板焊成箱形，內灌設計強度約 10,000 psi（約 69 MPa）的高強度混凝土，並以內部繫材防止鋼板外鼓。鋼箱提供模板、圍束與抗拉能力，混凝土提供大部分軸壓勁度並阻止鋼板向內挫屈，兩者合作的效率高於各自單獨使用。斷面隨高度逐段縮小，填充高度也分段結束（核心箱形柱與巨柱填至約 62 層），每一段的合成比例不同，計算必須逐段進行。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101's mega-columns are about 2.4 m × 3.0 m at the base, welded into boxes from 50 to 80 mm plates and filled with high-strength concrete of about 10,000 psi (about 69 MPa) design strength, with internal ties preventing the plates from bulging. The steel box provides formwork, confinement and tension capacity, while the concrete supplies most of the axial stiffness and stops the plates buckling inwards, so together they outperform either material alone. The section shrinks with height and the fill stops at different levels (core box columns and super columns are filled to about level 62), so the composite proportions change and must be checked segment by segment. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：名目擠壓強度 N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Nominal squash load N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-09-k1","title":"巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量","titleEn":"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity","text":"台北 101 的巨柱底部約 2.4 m × 3.0 m，由厚 50 至 80 mm 的鋼板焊成箱形，內灌設計強度約 10,000 psi（約 69 MPa）的高強度混凝土，並以內部繫材防止鋼板外鼓。鋼箱提供模板、圍束與抗拉能力，混凝土提供大部分軸壓勁度並阻止鋼板向內挫屈，兩者合作的效率高於各自單獨使用。","textEn":"Taipei 101's mega-columns are about 2.4 m × 3.0 m at the base, welded into boxes from 50 to 80 mm plates and filled with high-strength concrete of about 10,000 psi (about 69 MPa) design strength, with internal ties preventing the plates from bulging. The steel box provides formwork, confinement and tension capacity, while the concrete supplies most of the axial stiffness and stops the plates buckling inwards, so together they outperform either material alone.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity\" is correct?","options":["台北 101 的巨柱底部約 2.4 m × 3.0 m，由厚 50 至 80 mm 的鋼板焊成箱形，內灌設計強度約 10,000 psi（約 69 MPa）的高強度混凝土，並以內部繫材防止鋼板外鼓。","鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。","鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。"],"optionsEn":["Taipei 101's mega-columns are about 2.4 m × 3.0 m at the base, welded into boxes from 50 to 80 mm plates and filled with high-strength concrete of about 10,000 psi (about 69 MPa) design strength, with internal ties preventing the plates from bulging.","The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.","The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"台北 101 的巨柱底部約 2.4 m × 3.0 m，由厚 50 至 80 mm 的鋼板焊成箱形，內灌設計強度約 10,000 psi（約 69 MPa）的高強度混凝土，並以內部繫材防止鋼板外鼓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101's mega-columns are about 2.4 m × 3.0 m at the base, welded into boxes from 50 to 80 mm plates and filled with high-strength concrete of about 10,000 psi (about 69 MPa) design strength, with internal ties preventing the plates from bulging. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b021-v13-10","title":"巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：名目擠壓強度 N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c。2.4 m × 3.0 m、板厚 80 mm：A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m²、A_s = 7.20 − 6.36 = 0.84 m²；f_y = 414 MPa、f_c = 69 MPa，N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 347 + 373 = 720 MN。若混凝土只有 41 MPa，N₀ 約 569 MN，下降約 21%。數值為教學假設，未計長細比與強度折減。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Nominal squash load N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c. For 2.4 m × 3.0 m with 80 mm plate: A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m² and A_s = 7.20 − 6.36 = 0.84 m²; with f_y = 414 MPa and f_c = 69 MPa, N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 347 + 373 = 720 MN. With only 41 MPa concrete N₀ is about 569 MN, roughly 21% less. Teaching assumptions, ignoring slenderness and resistance factors. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐段建立巨柱斷面表（外尺寸、板厚、填充起訖樓層、混凝土強度），以合成柱公式與有限元素斷面分析互相核對；確認重力加風或地震組合下的軸力比在允許範圍，並檢查柱續接與隔板位置與製造圖一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a segment-by-segment mega-column schedule (outer size, plate thickness, fill start and end levels, concrete strength), cross-check composite-column formulas with finite-element section analysis, confirm the axial-load ratio under gravity plus wind or earthquake is within limits, and check that splice and diaphragm locations match the shop drawings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"名目擠壓強度 N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c。2.4 m × 3.0 m、板厚 80 mm：A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m²、A_s = 7.20 − 6.36 = 0.84 m²；f_y = 414 MPa、f_c = 69 MPa，N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 347 + 373 = 720 MN。若混凝土只有 41 MPa，N₀ 約 569 MN，下降約 21%。數值為教學假設，未計長細比與強度折減。","textEn":"Nominal squash load N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c. For 2.4 m × 3.0 m with 80 mm plate: A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m² and A_s = 7.20 − 6.36 = 0.84 m²; with f_y = 414 MPa and f_c = 69 MPa, N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 347 + 373 = 720 MN. With only 41 MPa concrete N₀ is about 569 MN, roughly 21% less. Teaching assumptions, ignoring slenderness and resistance factors.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","名目擠壓強度 N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c。","雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。"],"optionsEn":["Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","Nominal squash load N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c.","In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"名目擠壓強度 N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Nominal squash load N₀ = A_s·f_y + 0.85·f_c·A_c. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b021-v13-11","title":"巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐段建立巨柱斷面表（外尺寸、板厚、填充起訖樓層、混凝土強度），以合成柱公式與有限元素斷面分析互相核對；確認重力加風或地震組合下的軸力比在允許範圍，並檢查柱續接與隔板位置與製造圖一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a segment-by-segment mega-column schedule (outer size, plate thickness, fill start and end levels, concrete strength), cross-check composite-column formulas with finite-element section analysis, confirm the axial-load ratio under gravity plus wind or earthquake is within limits, and check that splice and diaphragm locations match the shop drawings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：巨柱斷面表要同時出現在結構圖、鋼構製造圖與混凝土澆置計畫，每一段標明填充起訖樓層與強度；每次澆置前由監造確認隔板排氣孔與灌注孔位置，列為停止點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Show the mega-column schedule on the structural drawings, steel shop drawings and concrete placement plan, marking fill start and end levels and strength for each segment; before every pour the resident engineer confirms diaphragm vent and filling holes as a hold point.","failure":"注意干擾：若圖面上的填充高度與實際澆置高度不符，未填充段只能靠鋼板單獨受力，容量可能比計算值少兩成以上；混凝土收縮在隔板下方留下空隙時，該處的圍束與傳力也會局部失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the drawn fill level differs from the actual pour, unfilled segments rely on the steel plates alone and can fall more than 20% below the calculated capacity; shrinkage voids under diaphragm plates also locally defeat confinement and load transfer. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐段建立巨柱斷面表（外尺寸、板厚、填充起訖樓層、混凝土強度），以合成柱公式與有限元素斷面分析互相核對；確認重力加風或地震組合下的軸力比在允許範圍，並檢查柱續接與隔板位置與製造圖一致。","textEn":"Build a segment-by-segment mega-column schedule (outer size, plate thickness, fill start and end levels, concrete strength), cross-check composite-column formulas with finite-element section analysis, confirm the axial-load ratio under gravity plus wind or earthquake is within limits, and check that splice and diaphragm locations match the shop drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"巨柱斷面表要同時出現在結構圖、鋼構製造圖與混凝土澆置計畫，每一段標明填充起訖樓層與強度；每次澆置前由監造確認隔板排氣孔與灌注孔位置，列為停止點。","textEn":"Show the mega-column schedule on the structural drawings, steel shop drawings and concrete placement plan, marking fill start and end levels and strength for each segment; before every pour the resident engineer confirms diaphragm vent and filling holes as a hold point.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。","逐段建立巨柱斷面表（外尺寸、板厚、填充起訖樓層、混凝土強度），以合成柱公式與有限元素斷面分析互相核對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement.","Build a segment-by-segment mega-column schedule (outer size, plate thickness, fill start and end levels, concrete strength), cross-check composite-column formulas with finite-element section analysis, confirm the axial-load ratio under gravity plus wind or earthquake is within limits, and check that splice and diaphragm locations match the shop drawings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐段建立巨柱斷面表（外尺寸、板厚、填充起訖樓層、混凝土強度），以合成柱公式與有限元素斷面分析互相核對；確認重力加風或地震組合下的軸力比在允許範圍，並檢查柱續接與隔板位置與製造圖一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a segment-by-segment mega-column schedule (outer size, plate thickness, fill start and end levels, concrete strength), cross-check composite-column formulas with finite-element section analysis, confirm the axial-load ratio under gravity plus wind or earthquake is within limits, and check that splice and diaphragm locations match the shop drawings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b021-v13-12","title":"巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete-filled steel box mega-column” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若圖面上的填充高度與實際澆置高度不符，未填充段只能靠鋼板單獨受力，容量可能比計算值少兩成以上；混凝土收縮在隔板下方留下空隙時，該處的圍束與傳力也會局部失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the drawn fill level differs from the actual pour, unfilled segments rely on the steel plates alone and can fall more than 20% below the calculated capacity; shrinkage voids under diaphragm plates also locally defeat confinement and load transfer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：斷面隨高度逐段縮小，填充高度也分段結束（核心箱形柱與巨柱填至約 62 層），每一段的合成比例不同，計算必須逐段進行。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The section shrinks with height and the fill stops at different levels (core box columns and super columns are filled to about level 62), so the composite proportions change and must be checked segment by segment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若圖面上的填充高度與實際澆置高度不符，未填充段只能靠鋼板單獨受力，容量可能比計算值少兩成以上；混凝土收縮在隔板下方留下空隙時，該處的圍束與傳力也會局部失效。","textEn":"If the drawn fill level differs from the actual pour, unfilled segments rely on the steel plates alone and can fall more than 20% below the calculated capacity; shrinkage voids under diaphragm plates also locally defeat confinement and load transfer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨柱合成斷面與軸壓容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Composite mega-column section and axial capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若圖面上的填充高度與實際澆置高度不符，未填充段只能靠鋼板單獨受力，容量可能比計算值少兩成以上；混凝土收縮在隔板下方留下空隙時，該處的圍束與傳力也會局部失效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。"],"optionsEn":["If the drawn fill level differs from the actual pour, unfilled segments rely on the steel plates alone and can fall more than 20% below the calculated capacity.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若圖面上的填充高度與實際澆置高度不符，未填充段只能靠鋼板單獨受力，容量可能比計算值少兩成以上；混凝土收縮在隔板下方留下空隙時，該處的圍束與傳力也會局部失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the drawn fill level differs from the actual pour, unfilled segments rely on the steel plates alone and can fall more than 20% below the calculated capacity; shrinkage voids under diaphragm plates also locally defeat confinement and load transfer. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b021-v13-13","title":"高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “SM570M thick plates and column splices” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 的主要鋼構使用 SM570M 等級鋼材，降伏強度約 60 ksi 以上，板厚可達 80 mm。厚板焊接時冷卻快、拘束大，容易產生氫致裂紋與層狀撕裂，因此規格同時限制碳當量（板厚 40 mm 以下約 0.44%、40 mm 以上約 0.47%）與降伏比（較厚的梁與斜撐約 80%、較薄者約 85%），確保焊接性與塑性變形能力。柱續接採全滲透焊，以抵抗風與地震下可能出現的少量淨上拉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101's main steelwork uses SM570M steel with a yield strength of about 60 ksi or more and plates up to 80 mm thick. Thick plates cool quickly and are highly restrained during welding, inviting hydrogen cracking and lamellar tearing, so the specification limited both the carbon equivalent (about 0.44% for plates under 40 mm and about 0.47% for 40 mm and thicker) and the yield ratio (about 80% for thicker girders and braces, about 85% for thinner ones) to secure weldability and plastic deformation capacity. Column splices are full-penetration welds to resist the small net uplift that wind and earthquakes can produce. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “SM570M thick plates and column splices” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：碳當量 Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Carbon equivalent Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “SM570M thick plates and column splices”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-13-k1","title":"高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接","titleEn":"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding","text":"台北 101 的主要鋼構使用 SM570M 等級鋼材，降伏強度約 60 ksi 以上，板厚可達 80 mm。厚板焊接時冷卻快、拘束大，容易產生氫致裂紋與層狀撕裂，因此規格同時限制碳當量（板厚 40 mm 以下約 0.44%、40 mm 以上約 0.47%）與降伏比（較厚的梁與斜撐約 80%、較薄者約 85%），確保焊接性與塑性變形能力。","textEn":"Taipei 101's main steelwork uses SM570M steel with a yield strength of about 60 ksi or more and plates up to 80 mm thick. Thick plates cool quickly and are highly restrained during welding, inviting hydrogen cracking and lamellar tearing, so the specification limited both the carbon equivalent (about 0.44% for plates under 40 mm and about 0.47% for 40 mm and thicker) and the yield ratio (about 80% for thicker girders and braces, about 85% for thinner ones) to secure weldability and plastic deformation capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding\" is correct?","options":["鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。","台北 101 的主要鋼構使用 SM570M 等級鋼材，降伏強度約 60 ksi 以上，板厚可達 80 mm。","只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter.","Taipei 101's main steelwork uses SM570M steel with a yield strength of about 60 ksi or more and plates up to 80 mm thick.","Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"台北 101 的主要鋼構使用 SM570M 等級鋼材，降伏強度約 60 ksi 以上，板厚可達 80 mm。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101's main steelwork uses SM570M steel with a yield strength of about 60 ksi or more and plates up to 80 mm thick. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b021-v13-14","title":"高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接：定量估算","titleEn":"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “SM570M thick plates and column splices” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：碳當量 Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。取 C 0.16、Mn 1.45、Cr 0.02、Mo 0、V 0.04、Ni 0.02、Cu 0.02，Ceq = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.012 + 0.003 ≈ 0.42%，低於 0.47% 上限；降伏比 440/600 ≈ 0.73，低於 0.80。數值為教學假設，不是實際鋼廠成分。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Carbon equivalent Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. With C 0.16, Mn 1.45, Cr 0.02, Mo 0, V 0.04, Ni 0.02 and Cu 0.02, Ceq = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.012 + 0.003 ≈ 0.42%, below the 0.47% limit; the yield ratio 440/600 ≈ 0.73 is below 0.80. Teaching assumptions, not actual mill chemistry. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每一爐號的鋼材證明書都要核對化學成分、降伏比與板厚方向性能（Z 向斷面收縮率），焊接程序以實際板厚做資格檢定；施焊時記錄預熱與層間溫度，完成後以超音波檢測全滲透焊並依規範判定合格與否。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check every heat's mill certificate for chemistry, yield ratio and through-thickness (Z-direction reduction of area) properties, qualify welding procedures on the actual plate thickness, record preheat and interpass temperatures during welding, and ultrasonically test every full-penetration weld against the code acceptance criteria.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"碳當量 Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。取 C 0.16、Mn 1.45、Cr 0.02、Mo 0、V 0.04、Ni 0.02、Cu 0.02，Ceq = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.012 + 0.003 ≈ 0.42%，低於 0.47% 上限；降伏比 440/600 ≈ 0.73，低於 0.80。數值為教學假設，不是實際鋼廠成分。","textEn":"Carbon equivalent Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. With C 0.16, Mn 1.45, Cr 0.02, Mo 0, V 0.04, Ni 0.02 and Cu 0.02, Ceq = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.012 + 0.003 ≈ 0.42%, below the 0.47% limit; the yield ratio 440/600 ≈ 0.73 is below 0.80. Teaching assumptions, not actual mill chemistry.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding\", which statement holds?","options":["自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。","阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。","碳當量 Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。"],"optionsEn":["Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed.","A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.","Carbon equivalent Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15."],"answer":2,"explanation":"碳當量 Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Carbon equivalent Ceq = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b021-v13-15","title":"高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “SM570M thick plates and column splices” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每一爐號的鋼材證明書都要核對化學成分、降伏比與板厚方向性能（Z 向斷面收縮率），焊接程序以實際板厚做資格檢定；施焊時記錄預熱與層間溫度，完成後以超音波檢測全滲透焊並依規範判定合格與否。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check every heat's mill certificate for chemistry, yield ratio and through-thickness (Z-direction reduction of area) properties, qualify welding procedures on the actual plate thickness, record preheat and interpass temperatures during welding, and ultrasonically test every full-penetration weld against the code acceptance criteria. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對厚板全滲透焊設定「冷卻 48 小時後才做超音波檢測」的停止點，保留每道焊道的焊工代號、預熱紀錄與檢測報告；任何補焊都要重新檢測，並經設計單位同意後才可覆蓋。","observationEn":"Site practice: Set a hold point of ultrasonic testing no earlier than 48 hours after cooling for thick full-penetration welds, keep the welder ID, preheat record and test report for each weld, and re-test every repair weld, covering it only after the designer approves.","failure":"注意干擾：厚板未充分預熱或焊材含氫量過高時，焊後數小時至數天才出現的延遲裂紋可能在檢測前就被覆蓋；層狀撕裂常出現在 T 形接頭的母材內部，在地震反覆載重下會成為斷裂起點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without adequate preheat or with high-hydrogen consumables, delayed cracks that appear hours or days after welding may be covered before inspection; lamellar tears form inside the base metal of T-joints and become fracture initiation points under cyclic seismic loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每一爐號的鋼材證明書都要核對化學成分、降伏比與板厚方向性能（Z 向斷面收縮率），焊接程序以實際板厚做資格檢定；施焊時記錄預熱與層間溫度，完成後以超音波檢測全滲透焊並依規範判定合格與否。","textEn":"Check every heat's mill certificate for chemistry, yield ratio and through-thickness (Z-direction reduction of area) properties, qualify welding procedures on the actual plate thickness, record preheat and interpass temperatures during welding, and ultrasonically test every full-penetration weld against the code acceptance criteria.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對厚板全滲透焊設定「冷卻 48 小時後才做超音波檢測」的停止點，保留每道焊道的焊工代號、預熱紀錄與檢測報告；任何補焊都要重新檢測，並經設計單位同意後才可覆蓋。","textEn":"Set a hold point of ultrasonic testing no earlier than 48 hours after cooling for thick full-penetration welds, keep the welder ID, preheat record and test report for each weld, and re-test every repair weld, covering it only after the designer approves.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding\"?","options":["每一爐號的鋼材證明書都要核對化學成分、降伏比與板厚方向性能（Z 向斷面收縮率），焊接程序以實際板厚做資格檢定。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。"],"optionsEn":["Check every heat's mill certificate for chemistry, yield ratio and through-thickness (Z-direction reduction of area) properties, qualify welding procedures on the actual plate thickness, record preheat and interpass temperatures during welding, and ultrasonically test every full-penetration weld against the code acceptance criteria.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每一爐號的鋼材證明書都要核對化學成分、降伏比與板厚方向性能（Z 向斷面收縮率），焊接程序以實際板厚做資格檢定；施焊時記錄預熱與層間溫度，完成後以超音波檢測全滲透焊並依規範判定合格與否。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check every heat's mill certificate for chemistry, yield ratio and through-thickness (Z-direction reduction of area) properties, qualify welding procedures on the actual plate thickness, record preheat and interpass temperatures during welding, and ultrasonically test every full-penetration weld against the code acceptance criteria. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b021-v13-16","title":"高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「SM570M 厚鋼板與柱續接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “SM570M thick plates and column splices” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"厚板未充分預熱或焊材含氫量過高時，焊後數小時至數天才出現的延遲裂紋可能在檢測前就被覆蓋；層狀撕裂常出現在 T 形接頭的母材內部，在地震反覆載重下會成為斷裂起點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without adequate preheat or with high-hydrogen consumables, delayed cracks that appear hours or days after welding may be covered before inspection; lamellar tears form inside the base metal of T-joints and become fracture initiation points under cyclic seismic loading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：柱續接採全滲透焊，以抵抗風與地震下可能出現的少量淨上拉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Column splices are full-penetration welds to resist the small net uplift that wind and earthquakes can produce.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"厚板未充分預熱或焊材含氫量過高時，焊後數小時至數天才出現的延遲裂紋可能在檢測前就被覆蓋；層狀撕裂常出現在 T 形接頭的母材內部，在地震反覆載重下會成為斷裂起點。","textEn":"Without adequate preheat or with high-hydrogen consumables, delayed cracks that appear hours or days after welding may be covered before inspection; lamellar tears form inside the base metal of T-joints and become fracture initiation points under cyclic seismic loading.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高強度厚板鋼材與全滲透焊接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-strength thick plate and full-penetration welding\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","厚板未充分預熱或焊材含氫量過高時，焊後數小時至數天才出現的延遲裂紋可能在檢測前就被覆蓋；層狀撕裂常出現在 T 形接頭的母材內部，在地震反覆載重下會成為斷裂起點。","只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without adequate preheat or with high-hydrogen consumables, delayed cracks that appear hours or days after welding may be covered before inspection.","Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚板未充分預熱或焊材含氫量過高時，焊後數小時至數天才出現的延遲裂紋可能在檢測前就被覆蓋；層狀撕裂常出現在 T 形接頭的母材內部，在地震反覆載重下會成為斷裂起點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without adequate preheat or with high-hydrogen consumables, delayed cracks that appear hours or days after welding may be covered before inspection; lamellar tears form inside the base metal of T-joints and become fracture initiation points under cyclic seismic loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":6},{"id":"b021-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基」與「331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin\" and \"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v13-17","title":"台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 基地上方約 30 m 為湖積粉土質黏土（上部約 20 m 很軟），其下為崩積層，岩盤（桂竹林層）約在地表下 40 至 65 m，頂部約 10 m 膠結不良。塔樓下設 380 支直徑 1.5 m、中心距約 3.96 m 的反循環鑽掘基樁，嵌入岩盤 15 至 33 m，上方為厚 3.0 至 4.7 m 的筏基，配合約 22 m 深的五層地下室開挖。基樁主要靠岩盤段的側摩擦承載，筏基則把巨柱與核心的集中力分配到整個樁群。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At the Taipei 101 site the top 30 m or so is lacustrine silty clay, the upper 20 m very soft, over colluvium, with bedrock of the Kueichulin Formation at about 40 to 65 m below ground and a poorly cemented top 10 m. Under the tower, 380 reverse-circulation bored piles of 1.5 m diameter at about 3.96 m centres are socketed 15 to 33 m into rock, capped by a raft 3.0 to 4.7 m thick within an excavation about 22 m deep for the five-level basement. The piles carry load mainly by side friction in the rock socket, while the raft spreads the concentrated mega-column and core loads across the whole group. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：岩盤段側摩擦 Q = π·D·L·f_s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Rock-socket side resistance Q = π·D·L·f_s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-17-k1","title":"台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基","titleEn":"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin","text":"台北 101 基地上方約 30 m 為湖積粉土質黏土（上部約 20 m 很軟），其下為崩積層，岩盤（桂竹林層）約在地表下 40 至 65 m，頂部約 10 m 膠結不良。塔樓下設 380 支直徑 1.5 m、中心距約 3.96 m 的反循環鑽掘基樁，嵌入岩盤 15 至 33 m，上方為厚 3.0 至 4.7 m 的筏基，配合約 22 m 深的五層地下室開挖。","textEn":"At the Taipei 101 site the top 30 m or so is lacustrine silty clay, the upper 20 m very soft, over colluvium, with bedrock of the Kueichulin Formation at about 40 to 65 m below ground and a poorly cemented top 10 m. Under the tower, 380 reverse-circulation bored piles of 1.5 m diameter at about 3.96 m centres are socketed 15 to 33 m into rock, capped by a raft 3.0 to 4.7 m thick within an excavation about 22 m deep for the five-level basement.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin\" is correct?","options":["只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。","塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","台北 101 基地上方約 30 m 為湖積粉土質黏土（上部約 20 m 很軟），其下為崩積層，岩盤（桂竹林層）約在地表下 40 至 65 m，頂部約 10 m 膠結不良。"],"optionsEn":["Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored.","Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","At the Taipei 101 site the top 30 m or so is lacustrine silty clay, the upper 20 m very soft, over colluvium, with bedrock of the Kueichulin Formation at about 40 to 65 m below ground and a poorly cemented top 10 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"台北 101 基地上方約 30 m 為湖積粉土質黏土（上部約 20 m 很軟），其下為崩積層，岩盤（桂竹林層）約在地表下 40 至 65 m，頂部約 10 m 膠結不良。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At the Taipei 101 site the top 30 m or so is lacustrine silty clay, the upper 20 m very soft, over colluvium, with bedrock of the Kueichulin Formation at about 40 to 65 m below ground and a poorly cemented top 10 m. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"b021-v13-18","title":"台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基：定量估算","titleEn":"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：岩盤段側摩擦 Q = π·D·L·f_s。取 D = 1.5 m、嵌入長 L = 20 m、單位側摩擦 f_s = 0.30 MPa，Q = π×1.5×20×0.30 ≈ 28.3 MN，安全係數 2 時容許約 14.1 MN。樁距 3.96/1.5 ≈ 2.6 倍樁徑，群樁效應會增加沉陷。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Rock-socket side resistance Q = π·D·L·f_s. With D = 1.5 m, socket length L = 20 m and unit side friction f_s = 0.30 MPa, Q = π×1.5×20×0.30 ≈ 28.3 MN, about 14.1 MN allowable with a factor of safety of 2. The spacing of 3.96/1.5 ≈ 2.6 diameters means group effects increase settlement. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以試驗樁做靜載試驗：公開論文記載壓力試驗最大約 40.6 MN、拉拔試驗最大約 22 MN，並在塔樓區做生產樁驗證試驗；以應變計分段量測側摩擦、回推 t–z 曲線，再與群樁沉陷分析比較（計算長期最大沉陷約 65 mm，施工期間量得塔中心沉陷小於約 20 mm）。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Load-test trial piles statically; the published paper records compression tests up to about 40.6 MN and pull-out tests up to about 22 MN, plus proof tests on production piles in the tower area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"岩盤段側摩擦 Q = π·D·L·f_s。取 D = 1.5 m、嵌入長 L = 20 m、單位側摩擦 f_s = 0.30 MPa，Q = π×1.5×20×0.30 ≈ 28.3 MN，安全係數 2 時容許約 14.1 MN。樁距 3.96/1.5 ≈ 2.6 倍樁徑，群樁效應會增加沉陷。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Rock-socket side resistance Q = π·D·L·f_s. With D = 1.5 m, socket length L = 20 m and unit side friction f_s = 0.30 MPa, Q = π×1.5×20×0.30 ≈ 28.3 MN, about 14.1 MN allowable with a factor of safety of 2. The spacing of 3.96/1.5 ≈ 2.6 diameters means group effects increase settlement. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin\", which statement holds?","options":["岩盤段側摩擦 Q = π·D·L·f_s。","雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。","帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。"],"optionsEn":["Rock-socket side resistance Q = π·D·L·f_s.","In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone.","A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩盤段側摩擦 Q = π·D·L·f_s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Rock-socket side resistance Q = π·D·L·f_s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"b021-v13-19","title":"台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以試驗樁做靜載試驗：公開論文記載壓力試驗最大約 40.6 MN、拉拔試驗最大約 22 MN，並在塔樓區做生產樁驗證試驗；以應變計分段量測側摩擦、回推 t–z 曲線，再與群樁沉陷分析比較（計算長期最大沉陷約 65 mm，施工期間量得塔中心沉陷小於約 20 mm）。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Load-test trial piles statically; the published paper records compression tests up to about 40.6 MN and pull-out tests up to about 22 MN, plus proof tests on production piles in the tower area. Measure side friction segment by segment with strain gauges, back-calculate t–z curves and compare with group-settlement analysis, which predicted about 65 mm long-term maximum while under about 20 mm was measured at the tower centre during construction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每支樁記錄鑽掘深度、入岩長度、孔底清理與穩定液性質，澆置前以測深與超音波檢查孔形；開挖期間同步監測鄰房與地下水位，任何異常即暫停開挖，由大地工程顧問判斷後才可續作。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record drilled depth, socket length, base cleaning and drilling-fluid properties for each pile, sound and ultrasonically profile the hole before concreting, and monitor neighbouring buildings and groundwater during excavation, stopping work on any anomaly until the geotechnical consultant decides.","failure":"注意干擾：反循環鑽掘時若孔壁在軟黏土段坍落或孔底沉泥未清除，岩盤段的側摩擦與端承都會大幅下降；樁群中少數樁偏軟會讓筏基不均勻沉陷，使高聳結構傾斜，並在巨柱與核心之間產生附加內力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the borehole wall collapses in the soft clay or bottom slime is not cleaned during reverse-circulation drilling, socket friction and end bearing drop sharply; a few soft piles in the group cause uneven raft settlement, tilting the tall structure and inducing extra forces between mega-columns and core. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以試驗樁做靜載試驗：公開論文記載壓力試驗最大約 40.6 MN、拉拔試驗最大約 22 MN，並在塔樓區做生產樁驗證試驗；以應變計分段量測側摩擦、回推 t–z 曲線，再與群樁沉陷分析比較（計算長期最大沉陷約 65 mm，施工期間量得塔中心沉陷小於約 20 mm）。","textEn":"Load-test trial piles statically; the published paper records compression tests up to about 40.6 MN and pull-out tests up to about 22 MN, plus proof tests on production piles in the tower area. Measure side friction segment by segment with strain gauges, back-calculate t–z curves and compare with group-settlement analysis, which predicted about 65 mm long-term maximum while under about 20 mm was measured at the tower centre during construction.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每支樁記錄鑽掘深度、入岩長度、孔底清理與穩定液性質，澆置前以測深與超音波檢查孔形；開挖期間同步監測鄰房與地下水位，任何異常即暫停開挖，由大地工程顧問判斷後才可續作。","textEn":"Record drilled depth, socket length, base cleaning and drilling-fluid properties for each pile, sound and ultrasonically profile the hole before concreting, and monitor neighbouring buildings and groundwater during excavation, stopping work on any anomaly until the geotechnical consultant decides.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以試驗樁做靜載試驗：公開論文記載壓力試驗最大約 40.6 MN、拉拔試驗最大約 22 MN，並在塔樓區做生產樁驗證試驗。","外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Load-test trial piles statically.","The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以試驗樁做靜載試驗：公開論文記載壓力試驗最大約 40.6 MN、拉拔試驗最大約 22 MN，並在塔樓區做生產樁驗證試驗；以應變計分段量測側摩擦、回推 t–z 曲線，再與群樁沉陷分析比較（計算長期最大沉陷約 65 mm，施工期間量得塔中心沉陷小於約 20 mm）。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Load-test trial piles statically; the published paper records compression tests up to about 40.6 MN and pull-out tests up to about 22 MN, plus proof tests on production piles in the tower area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"b021-v13-20","title":"台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反循環基樁與岩盤嵌入」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reverse-circulation piles and rock sockets” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"反循環鑽掘時若孔壁在軟黏土段坍落或孔底沉泥未清除，岩盤段的側摩擦與端承都會大幅下降；樁群中少數樁偏軟會讓筏基不均勻沉陷，使高聳結構傾斜，並在巨柱與核心之間產生附加內力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the borehole wall collapses in the soft clay or bottom slime is not cleaned during reverse-circulation drilling, socket friction and end bearing drop sharply; a few soft piles in the group cause uneven raft settlement, tilting the tall structure and inducing extra forces between mega-columns and core. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：基樁主要靠岩盤段的側摩擦承載，筏基則把巨柱與核心的集中力分配到整個樁群。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The piles carry load mainly by side friction in the rock socket, while the raft spreads the concentrated mega-column and core loads across the whole group.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"反循環鑽掘時若孔壁在軟黏土段坍落或孔底沉泥未清除，岩盤段的側摩擦與端承都會大幅下降；樁群中少數樁偏軟會讓筏基不均勻沉陷，使高聳結構傾斜，並在巨柱與核心之間產生附加內力。","textEn":"If the borehole wall collapses in the soft clay or bottom slime is not cleaned during reverse-circulation drilling, socket friction and end bearing drop sharply; a few soft piles in the group cause uneven raft settlement, tilting the tall structure and inducing extra forces between mega-columns and core.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「台北盆地軟黏土上的基樁與筏基」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piles and raft in the soft Taipei basin\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","反循環鑽掘時若孔壁在軟黏土段坍落或孔底沉泥未清除，岩盤段的側摩擦與端承都會大幅下降。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","If the borehole wall collapses in the soft clay or bottom slime is not cleaned during reverse-circulation drilling, socket friction and end bearing drop sharply."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反循環鑽掘時若孔壁在軟黏土段坍落或孔底沉泥未清除，岩盤段的側摩擦與端承都會大幅下降；樁群中少數樁偏軟會讓筏基不均勻沉陷，使高聳結構傾斜，並在巨柱與核心之間產生附加內力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the borehole wall collapses in the soft clay or bottom slime is not cleaned during reverse-circulation drilling, socket friction and end bearing drop sharply; a few soft piles in the group cause uneven raft settlement, tilting the tall structure and inducing extra forces between mega-columns and core. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"b021-v13-21","title":"331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「爬升式塔吊支承點」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Climbing tower-crane supports” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"2002 年 3 月 31 日花蓮外海規模 6.8 地震時，施工中的台北 101 有兩部位於 56 樓的塔吊被震落，造成五人死亡。當時鋼構約施工到 53 至 56 樓、樓板混凝土約到 34 樓、柱內填充約到 32 樓，塔吊支承在 47 與 51 樓；未完成的結構缺少樓板隔膜與填充混凝土，比完工狀態更柔、更不均勻，高處又會放大地表加速度。塔吊及其支承與繫結屬於臨時工程，卻同樣需要以地震力檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「爬升式塔吊支承點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In the magnitude 6.8 earthquake off Hualien on 31 March 2002, two tower cranes at level 56 of the unfinished Taipei 101 were shaken loose, killing five people. Steel was then erected to about levels 53 to 56, slab concrete to about level 34 and column infill to about level 32, with crane supports at levels 47 and 51; the incomplete frame lacked floor diaphragms and infill, so it was more flexible and less regular than the finished building, and height amplified the ground acceleration. Cranes, their supports and ties are temporary works, yet they must be checked for seismic forces just like the permanent structure. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Climbing tower-crane supports” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：附近測站東西向尖峰約 193 gal，即 0.197 g；若施工中高樓層放大 2.5 倍，塔吊處約 0.49 g。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A nearby station recorded about 193 gal east–west, or 0.197 g; with 2.5 times amplification at the upper construction levels the crane sees about 0.49 g.","failure":"常見誤解：「塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「爬升式塔吊支承點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Climbing tower-crane supports”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-21-k1","title":"331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震","titleEn":"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works","text":"2002 年 3 月 31 日花蓮外海規模 6.8 地震時，施工中的台北 101 有兩部位於 56 樓的塔吊被震落，造成五人死亡。當時鋼構約施工到 53 至 56 樓、樓板混凝土約到 34 樓、柱內填充約到 32 樓，塔吊支承在 47 與 51 樓；未完成的結構缺少樓板隔膜與填充混凝土，比完工狀態更柔、更不均勻，高處又會放大地表加速度。","textEn":"In the magnitude 6.8 earthquake off Hualien on 31 March 2002, two tower cranes at level 56 of the unfinished Taipei 101 were shaken loose, killing five people. Steel was then erected to about levels 53 to 56, slab concrete to about level 34 and column infill to about level 32, with crane supports at levels 47 and 51; the incomplete frame lacked floor diaphragms and infill, so it was more flexible and less regular than the finished building, and height amplified the ground acceleration.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works\" is correct?","options":["2002 年 3 月 31 日花蓮外海規模 6.8 地震時，施工中的台北 101 有兩部位於 56 樓的塔吊被震落，造成五人死亡。","塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。"],"optionsEn":["In the magnitude 6.8 earthquake off Hualien on 31 March 2002, two tower cranes at level 56 of the unfinished Taipei 101 were shaken loose, killing five people.","Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"2002 年 3 月 31 日花蓮外海規模 6.8 地震時，施工中的台北 101 有兩部位於 56 樓的塔吊被震落，造成五人死亡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In the magnitude 6.8 earthquake off Hualien on 31 March 2002, two tower cranes at level 56 of the unfinished Taipei 101 were shaken loose, killing five people. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"b021-v13-22","title":"331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震：定量估算","titleEn":"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「爬升式塔吊支承點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Climbing tower-crane supports” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：附近測站東西向尖峰約 193 gal，即 0.197 g；若施工中高樓層放大 2.5 倍，塔吊處約 0.49 g。塔吊質量 120 t 時水平慣性力 F = m·a = 120,000×0.49×9.81 ≈ 579 kN，作用於支承上方 20 m 時彎矩約 11,580 kN·m，支承間距 4 m 時繫結力約 2,895 kN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A nearby station recorded about 193 gal east–west, or 0.197 g; with 2.5 times amplification at the upper construction levels the crane sees about 0.49 g. For a 120 t crane the horizontal inertia force is F = m·a = 120,000×0.49×9.81 ≈ 579 kN; acting 20 m above the supports it gives about 11,580 kN·m, or a tie force of about 2,895 kN for supports 4 m apart. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：塔吊基座、爬升框與繫結要以施工階段結構模型分析，輸入當地設計地震與颱風風速，並檢查支承樓層在該階段的實際強度（混凝土是否已澆置、構件是否已鎖固）；地震後由專業技師檢查繫結螺栓、焊道與爬升楔塊，確認無損後才可恢復吊裝。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Analyse crane bases, climbing frames and ties with a construction-stage model using the local design earthquake and typhoon wind, checking the supporting floors at their actual stage of completion (concrete placed or not, members fully connected or not); after any earthquake, have a professional engineer inspect tie bolts, welds and climbing wedges and confirm no damage before lifting resumes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"附近測站東西向尖峰約 193 gal，即 0.197 g；若施工中高樓層放大 2.5 倍，塔吊處約 0.49 g。塔吊質量 120 t 時水平慣性力 F = m·a = 120,000×0.49×9.81 ≈ 579 kN，作用於支承上方 20 m 時彎矩約 11,580 kN·m，支承間距 4 m 時繫結力約 2,895 kN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A nearby station recorded about 193 gal east–west, or 0.197 g; with 2.5 times amplification at the upper construction levels the crane sees about 0.49 g. For a 120 t crane the horizontal inertia force is F = m·a = 120,000×0.49×9.81 ≈ 579 kN; acting 20 m above the supports it gives about 11,580 kN·m, or a tie force of about 2,895 kN for supports 4 m apart. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。","附近測站東西向尖峰約 193 gal，即 0.197 g；若施工中高樓層放大 2.5 倍，塔吊處約 0.49 g。","角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。"],"optionsEn":["A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.","A nearby station recorded about 193 gal east–west, or 0.197 g; with 2.5 times amplification at the upper construction levels the crane sees about 0.49 g.","Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"附近測站東西向尖峰約 193 gal，即 0.197 g；若施工中高樓層放大 2.5 倍，塔吊處約 0.49 g。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A nearby station recorded about 193 gal east–west, or 0.197 g; with 2.5 times amplification at the upper construction levels the crane sees about 0.49 g. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"b021-v13-23","title":"331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「爬升式塔吊支承點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Climbing tower-crane supports” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"塔吊基座、爬升框與繫結要以施工階段結構模型分析，輸入當地設計地震與颱風風速，並檢查支承樓層在該階段的實際強度（混凝土是否已澆置、構件是否已鎖固）；地震後由專業技師檢查繫結螺栓、焊道與爬升楔塊，確認無損後才可恢復吊裝。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Analyse crane bases, climbing frames and ties with a construction-stage model using the local design earthquake and typhoon wind, checking the supporting floors at their actual stage of completion (concrete placed or not, members fully connected or not); after any earthquake, have a professional engineer inspect tie bolts, welds and climbing wedges and confirm no damage before lifting resumes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：塔吊的地震與颱風作業限制、強制停機與吊臂放鬆迴轉程序要寫入施工計畫；每次爬升前後各設停止點，由結構設計者確認支承樓層的施工階段強度並簽認，未簽認不得爬升。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write the earthquake and typhoon operating limits, mandatory shutdown and free-slew procedures for cranes into the construction plan; set hold points before and after each climb at which the structural designer confirms and signs off the stage strength of the supporting floors, with no climbing until signed.","failure":"注意干擾：公開資料指出，事故後檢方調查是否有疏失，工程停工約三個月並依委員會建議復工。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Public records state that prosecutors investigated possible negligence and that work stopped for about three months before resuming on a committee's recommendation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"塔吊基座、爬升框與繫結要以施工階段結構模型分析，輸入當地設計地震與颱風風速，並檢查支承樓層在該階段的實際強度（混凝土是否已澆置、構件是否已鎖固）；地震後由專業技師檢查繫結螺栓、焊道與爬升楔塊，確認無損後才可恢復吊裝。","textEn":"Analyse crane bases, climbing frames and ties with a construction-stage model using the local design earthquake and typhoon wind, checking the supporting floors at their actual stage of completion (concrete placed or not, members fully connected or not); after any earthquake, have a professional engineer inspect tie bolts, welds and climbing wedges and confirm no damage before lifting resumes.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"塔吊的地震與颱風作業限制、強制停機與吊臂放鬆迴轉程序要寫入施工計畫；每次爬升前後各設停止點，由結構設計者確認支承樓層的施工階段強度並簽認，未簽認不得爬升。","textEn":"Write the earthquake and typhoon operating limits, mandatory shutdown and free-slew procedures for cranes into the construction plan; set hold points before and after each climb at which the structural designer confirms and signs off the stage strength of the supporting floors, with no climbing until signed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。","塔吊基座、爬升框與繫結要以施工階段結構模型分析，輸入當地設計地震與颱風風速，並檢查支承樓層在該階段的實際強度（混凝土是否已澆置、構件是否已鎖固）。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.","Analyse crane bases, climbing frames and ties with a construction-stage model using the local design earthquake and typhoon wind, checking the supporting floors at their actual stage of completion (concrete placed or not, members fully connected or not)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塔吊基座、爬升框與繫結要以施工階段結構模型分析，輸入當地設計地震與颱風風速，並檢查支承樓層在該階段的實際強度（混凝土是否已澆置、構件是否已鎖固）；地震後由專業技師檢查繫結螺栓、焊道與爬升楔塊，確認無損後才可恢復吊裝。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Analyse crane bases, climbing frames and ties with a construction-stage model using the local design earthquake and typhoon wind, checking the supporting floors at their actual stage of completion (concrete placed or not, members fully connected or not); after any earthquake, have a professional engineer inspect tie bolts, welds and climbing wedges and confirm no damage before lifting resumes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"b021-v13-24","title":"331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震：失效診斷","titleEn":"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「爬升式塔吊支承點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Climbing tower-crane supports” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"公開資料指出，事故後檢方調查是否有疏失，工程停工約三個月並依委員會建議復工。一般而言，塔吊繫結與爬升支承若只按吊重與風力設計，強震時可能在支承點或塔身斷面先破壞，墜落物又會撞擊下方樓板與人員。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Public records state that prosecutors investigated possible negligence and that work stopped for about three months before resuming on a committee's recommendation. In general, crane ties and climbing supports designed only for lifted load and wind can fail first at supports or tower sections in a strong earthquake, and falling parts then strike the floors and people below. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塔吊及其支承與繫結屬於臨時工程，卻同樣需要以地震力檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cranes, their supports and ties are temporary works, yet they must be checked for seismic forces just like the permanent structure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"公開資料指出，事故後檢方調查是否有疏失，工程停工約三個月並依委員會建議復工。一般而言，塔吊繫結與爬升支承若只按吊重與風力設計，強震時可能在支承點或塔身斷面先破壞，墜落物又會撞擊下方樓板與人員。","textEn":"Public records state that prosecutors investigated possible negligence and that work stopped for about three months before resuming on a committee's recommendation. In general, crane ties and climbing supports designed only for lifted load and wind can fail first at supports or tower sections in a strong earthquake, and falling parts then strike the floors and people below.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「331 地震塔吊墜落與臨時結構耐震」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The 2002 crane collapse and seismic design of temporary works\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["公開資料指出，事故後檢方調查是否有疏失，工程停工約三個月並依委員會建議復工。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。"],"optionsEn":["Public records state that prosecutors investigated possible negligence and that work stopped for about three months before resuming on a committee's recommendation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"公開資料指出，事故後檢方調查是否有疏失，工程停工約三個月並依委員會建議復工。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Public records state that prosecutors investigated possible negligence and that work stopped for about three months before resuming on a committee's recommendation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":7},{"id":"b021-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收」與「兩級地震性能與非線性驗證」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance\" and \"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v13-25","title":"巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「隔板下方空隙檢測」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Voids under diaphragm plates” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"箱形巨柱內有水平隔板與繫材，混凝土必須流過狹窄孔口填滿每個角落，又無法振動搗實，因此採用高流動、自充填的配比。台北 101 的規格要求 90 天設計強度 10,000 psi、坍度約 250 ± 20 mm、坍流度約 600 ± 20 mm，隔板下方空隙不超過面積的 5%，並限制 90 天自體收縮約 300 × 10⁻⁶。隔板下的空隙最難避免，因為氣泡與泌水會集中在板底。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔板下方空隙檢測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A box mega-column contains horizontal diaphragms and ties, so concrete must flow through narrow openings to fill every corner without vibration, which calls for a highly fluid self-consolidating mix. Taipei 101's specification called for 10,000 psi design strength at 90 days, slump about 250 ± 20 mm, slump flow about 600 ± 20 mm, voids under diaphragm plates of no more than 5% of the area, and autogenous shrinkage limited to about 300 × 10⁻⁶ at 90 days. Voids under diaphragms are the hardest to avoid because air bubbles and bleed water collect beneath the plate. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Voids under diaphragm plates” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：隔板下淨面積 A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²，若檢測到空隙 0.25 m²，比例 = 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%，低於 5% 上限；自體收縮 300 × 10⁻⁶ 在 4.2 m 樓高內造成約 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm 的縮短，足以在板底拉開一道縫。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The net area under a diaphragm is A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²; a detected void of 0.25 m² gives 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%, below the 5% limit.","failure":"常見誤解：「自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔板下方空隙檢測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Voids under diaphragm plates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-25-k1","title":"巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收","titleEn":"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance","text":"箱形巨柱內有水平隔板與繫材，混凝土必須流過狹窄孔口填滿每個角落，又無法振動搗實，因此採用高流動、自充填的配比。台北 101 的規格要求 90 天設計強度 10,000 psi、坍度約 250 ± 20 mm、坍流度約 600 ± 20 mm，隔板下方空隙不超過面積的 5%，並限制 90 天自體收縮約 300 × 10⁻⁶。","textEn":"A box mega-column contains horizontal diaphragms and ties, so concrete must flow through narrow openings to fill every corner without vibration, which calls for a highly fluid self-consolidating mix. Taipei 101's specification called for 10,000 psi design strength at 90 days, slump about 250 ± 20 mm, slump flow about 600 ± 20 mm, voids under diaphragm plates of no more than 5% of the area, and autogenous shrinkage limited to about 300 × 10⁻⁶ at 90 days.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance\" is correct?","options":["自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。","箱形巨柱內有水平隔板與繫材，混凝土必須流過狹窄孔口填滿每個角落，又無法振動搗實，因此採用高流動、自充填的配比。","雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。"],"optionsEn":["Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed.","A box mega-column contains horizontal diaphragms and ties, so concrete must flow through narrow openings to fill every corner without vibration, which calls for a highly fluid self-consolidating mix.","In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"箱形巨柱內有水平隔板與繫材，混凝土必須流過狹窄孔口填滿每個角落，又無法振動搗實，因此採用高流動、自充填的配比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A box mega-column contains horizontal diaphragms and ties, so concrete must flow through narrow openings to fill every corner without vibration, which calls for a highly fluid self-consolidating mix. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"b021-v13-26","title":"巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收：定量估算","titleEn":"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔板下方空隙檢測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Voids under diaphragm plates” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：隔板下淨面積 A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²，若檢測到空隙 0.25 m²，比例 = 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%，低於 5% 上限；自體收縮 300 × 10⁻⁶ 在 4.2 m 樓高內造成約 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm 的縮短，足以在板底拉開一道縫。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The net area under a diaphragm is A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²; a detected void of 0.25 m² gives 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%, below the 5% limit. Autogenous shrinkage of 300 × 10⁻⁶ over a 4.2 m storey shortens the fill by about 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm, enough to open a gap under a plate. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先以足尺模型柱試灌，硬化後切開量測隔板下空隙並調整配比與排氣孔；正式施工時以敲擊或超音波檢查隔板附近是否空洞，記錄每一車的坍流度與溫度並取圓柱試體，空隙超標處鑽孔注漿補強並重新檢測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: First cast a full-scale mock-up column and cut it open after hardening to measure voids under diaphragms, adjusting the mix and vent holes; during production check around diaphragms by tapping or ultrasonic testing, record slump flow and temperature of every truck with cylinders taken, and drill, grout and re-test wherever voids exceed the limit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"隔板下淨面積 A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²，若檢測到空隙 0.25 m²，比例 = 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%，低於 5% 上限；自體收縮 300 × 10⁻⁶ 在 4.2 m 樓高內造成約 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm 的縮短，足以在板底拉開一道縫。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The net area under a diaphragm is A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²; a detected void of 0.25 m² gives 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%, below the 5% limit. Autogenous shrinkage of 300 × 10⁻⁶ over a 4.2 m storey shortens the fill by about 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm, enough to open a gap under a plate. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance\", which statement holds?","options":["帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。","外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。","隔板下淨面積 A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²，若檢測到空隙 0.25 m²，比例 = 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%，低於 5% 上限。"],"optionsEn":["A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement.","The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most.","The net area under a diaphragm is A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²; a detected void of 0.25 m² gives 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%, below the 5% limit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔板下淨面積 A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²，若檢測到空隙 0.25 m²，比例 = 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%，低於 5% 上限；自體收縮 300 × 10⁻⁶ 在 4.2 m 樓高內造成約 300×10⁻⁶×4,200 ≈ 1.3 mm 的縮短，足以在板底拉開一道縫。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The net area under a diaphragm is A_d = 2.24×2.84 ≈ 6.36 m²; a detected void of 0.25 m² gives 0.25/6.36 ≈ 3.9%, below the 5% limit. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"b021-v13-27","title":"巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔板下方空隙檢測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Voids under diaphragm plates” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先以足尺模型柱試灌，硬化後切開量測隔板下空隙並調整配比與排氣孔；正式施工時以敲擊或超音波檢查隔板附近是否空洞，記錄每一車的坍流度與溫度並取圓柱試體，空隙超標處鑽孔注漿補強並重新檢測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"First cast a full-scale mock-up column and cut it open after hardening to measure voids under diaphragms, adjusting the mix and vent holes; during production check around diaphragms by tapping or ultrasonic testing, record slump flow and temperature of every truck with cylinders taken, and drill, grout and re-test wherever voids exceed the limit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每一段巨柱澆置前確認排氣孔暢通與澆置管位置，並設「模型柱試驗合格」與「前一段空隙檢測完成」兩個停止點；檢測結果標註在巨柱斷面表上，成為竣工紀錄的一部分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before each mega-column pour confirm clear vent holes and placement-pipe positions, with two hold points per segment, mock-up approval and completion of void checks on the previous segment; mark the results on the mega-column schedule as part of the as-built record.","failure":"注意干擾：坍流度不足或澆置速度過快會把空氣封在隔板下，形成大面積空洞；過度泌水則在板底留下弱化水膜，地震時巨柱局部的圍束與剪力傳遞降低，鋼板可能向內挫屈。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inadequate slump flow or too fast a placement traps air under diaphragms in large voids; excessive bleeding leaves a weak water film under the plate, so in an earthquake local confinement and shear transfer in the mega-column drop and the plate may buckle inwards. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以足尺模型柱試灌，硬化後切開量測隔板下空隙並調整配比與排氣孔；正式施工時以敲擊或超音波檢查隔板附近是否空洞，記錄每一車的坍流度與溫度並取圓柱試體，空隙超標處鑽孔注漿補強並重新檢測。","textEn":"First cast a full-scale mock-up column and cut it open after hardening to measure voids under diaphragms, adjusting the mix and vent holes; during production check around diaphragms by tapping or ultrasonic testing, record slump flow and temperature of every truck with cylinders taken, and drill, grout and re-test wherever voids exceed the limit.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每一段巨柱澆置前確認排氣孔暢通與澆置管位置，並設「模型柱試驗合格」與「前一段空隙檢測完成」兩個停止點；檢測結果標註在巨柱斷面表上，成為竣工紀錄的一部分。","textEn":"Before each mega-column pour confirm clear vent holes and placement-pipe positions, with two hold points per segment, mock-up approval and completion of void checks on the previous segment; mark the results on the mega-column schedule as part of the as-built record.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance\"?","options":["先以足尺模型柱試灌，硬化後切開量測隔板下空隙並調整配比與排氣孔。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。"],"optionsEn":["First cast a full-scale mock-up column and cut it open after hardening to measure voids under diaphragms, adjusting the mix and vent holes.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先以足尺模型柱試灌，硬化後切開量測隔板下空隙並調整配比與排氣孔；正式施工時以敲擊或超音波檢查隔板附近是否空洞，記錄每一車的坍流度與溫度並取圓柱試體，空隙超標處鑽孔注漿補強並重新檢測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"First cast a full-scale mock-up column and cut it open after hardening to measure voids under diaphragms, adjusting the mix and vent holes; during production check around diaphragms by tapping or ultrasonic testing, record slump flow and temperature of every truck with cylinders taken, and drill, grout and re-test wherever voids exceed the limit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"b021-v13-28","title":"巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收：失效診斷","titleEn":"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔板下方空隙檢測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Voids under diaphragm plates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"坍流度不足或澆置速度過快會把空氣封在隔板下，形成大面積空洞；過度泌水則在板底留下弱化水膜，地震時巨柱局部的圍束與剪力傳遞降低，鋼板可能向內挫屈。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inadequate slump flow or too fast a placement traps air under diaphragms in large voids; excessive bleeding leaves a weak water film under the plate, so in an earthquake local confinement and shear transfer in the mega-column drop and the plate may buckle inwards. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：隔板下的空隙最難避免，因為氣泡與泌水會集中在板底。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Voids under diaphragms are the hardest to avoid because air bubbles and bleed water collect beneath the plate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"坍流度不足或澆置速度過快會把空氣封在隔板下，形成大面積空洞；過度泌水則在板底留下弱化水膜，地震時巨柱局部的圍束與剪力傳遞降低，鋼板可能向內挫屈。","textEn":"Inadequate slump flow or too fast a placement traps air under diaphragms in large voids; excessive bleeding leaves a weak water film under the plate, so in an earthquake local confinement and shear transfer in the mega-column drop and the plate may buckle inwards.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨柱填充混凝土的配比與充填驗收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Infill concrete mix and fill acceptance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","坍流度不足或澆置速度過快會把空氣封在隔板下，形成大面積空洞；過度泌水則在板底留下弱化水膜，地震時巨柱局部的圍束與剪力傳遞降低，鋼板可能向內挫屈。","雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Inadequate slump flow or too fast a placement traps air under diaphragms in large voids.","In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone."],"answer":1,"explanation":"坍流度不足或澆置速度過快會把空氣封在隔板下，形成大面積空洞；過度泌水則在板底留下弱化水膜，地震時巨柱局部的圍束與剪力傳遞降低，鋼板可能向內挫屈。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inadequate slump flow or too fast a placement traps air under diaphragms in large voids; excessive bleeding leaves a weak water film under the plate, so in an earthquake local confinement and shear transfer in the mega-column drop and the plate may buckle inwards. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"b021-v13-29","title":"兩級地震性能與非線性驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 的耐震設計以兩級地震檢核：約 100 年回歸期地震下結構保持彈性，約 950 年回歸期地震下維持穩定不倒塌，並以非線性時間歷程分析驗證。周邊抗彎構架須能獨立承擔規範要求的 25% 地震力，形成雙重系統；分析中梁端塑性轉角超過約 0.005 弧度的位置改用減弱斷面梁（狗骨頭切削），把塑性鉸從柱面移開，以保護焊接接頭。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101's seismic design checks two levels: the structure stays elastic in an earthquake of roughly 100-year return period and remains stable without collapse in one of roughly 950 years, verified by nonlinear time-history analysis. The perimeter moment frames must independently carry the code-required 25% of the seismic force, forming a dual system; where analysis shows beam-end plastic rotations above about 0.005 rad, reduced beam sections (dogbone cuts) move the plastic hinge away from the column face to protect the welded joint. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：塑性轉角 θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Plastic rotation θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-29-k1","title":"兩級地震性能與非線性驗證","titleEn":"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks","text":"台北 101 的耐震設計以兩級地震檢核：約 100 年回歸期地震下結構保持彈性，約 950 年回歸期地震下維持穩定不倒塌，並以非線性時間歷程分析驗證。周邊抗彎構架須能獨立承擔規範要求的 25% 地震力，形成雙重系統；分析中梁端塑性轉角超過約 0.005 弧度的位置改用減弱斷面梁（狗骨頭切削），把塑性鉸從柱面移開，以保護焊接接頭。","textEn":"Taipei 101's seismic design checks two levels: the structure stays elastic in an earthquake of roughly 100-year return period and remains stable without collapse in one of roughly 950 years, verified by nonlinear time-history analysis. The perimeter moment frames must independently carry the code-required 25% of the seismic force, forming a dual system; where analysis shows beam-end plastic rotations above about 0.005 rad, reduced beam sections (dogbone cuts) move the plastic hinge away from the column face to protect the welded joint.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「兩級地震性能與非線性驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks\" is correct?","options":["雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。","阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。","台北 101 的耐震設計以兩級地震檢核：約 100 年回歸期地震下結構保持彈性，約 950 年回歸期地震下維持穩定不倒塌，並以非線性時間歷程分析驗證。"],"optionsEn":["In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone.","A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.","Taipei 101's seismic design checks two levels: the structure stays elastic in an earthquake of roughly 100-year return period and remains stable without collapse in one of roughly 950 years, verified by nonlinear time-history analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"台北 101 的耐震設計以兩級地震檢核：約 100 年回歸期地震下結構保持彈性，約 950 年回歸期地震下維持穩定不倒塌，並以非線性時間歷程分析驗證。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101's seismic design checks two levels: the structure stays elastic in an earthquake of roughly 100-year return period and remains stable without collapse in one of roughly 950 years, verified by nonlinear time-history analysis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"b021-v13-30","title":"兩級地震性能與非線性驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：塑性轉角 θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y。若層間變位角 1/90 = 0.0111 rad、梁降伏轉角 0.0060 rad，θ_p ≈ 0.0051 rad，超過 0.005 rad 門檻，需改用減弱斷面；雙重系統下若總基底剪力 V = 100 MN，抗彎構架單獨須能承擔 0.25×100 = 25 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Plastic rotation θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y. With a storey drift angle of 1/90 = 0.0111 rad and a beam yield rotation of 0.0060 rad, θ_p ≈ 0.0051 rad, above the 0.005 rad threshold, so a reduced beam section is needed; in the dual system, if total base shear V = 100 MN, the moment frame alone must carry 0.25×100 = 25 MN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多組符合場址條件的地震紀錄做非線性時間歷程分析，逐層輸出層間變位角與梁端塑性轉角分布，並與兩級性能目標比對；再把核心斜撐移除、只留抗彎構架做一次分析，確認 25% 的獨立承載要求。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several site-appropriate records, output storey drift angles and beam-end plastic rotations floor by floor and compare them with the two performance targets; then analyse the moment frame alone with the core bracing removed to confirm the independent 25% requirement, and support reduced-section cut dimensions with full-scale or published test data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"塑性轉角 θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y。若層間變位角 1/90 = 0.0111 rad、梁降伏轉角 0.0060 rad，θ_p ≈ 0.0051 rad，超過 0.005 rad 門檻，需改用減弱斷面；雙重系統下若總基底剪力 V = 100 MN，抗彎構架單獨須能承擔 0.25×100 = 25 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Plastic rotation θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y. With a storey drift angle of 1/90 = 0.0111 rad and a beam yield rotation of 0.0060 rad, θ_p ≈ 0.0051 rad, above the 0.005 rad threshold, so a reduced beam section is needed; in the dual system, if total base shear V = 100 MN, the moment frame alone must carry 0.25×100 = 25 MN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「兩級地震性能與非線性驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks\", which statement holds?","options":["塑性轉角 θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y。","角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。","鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。"],"optionsEn":["Plastic rotation θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y.","Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads.","The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"塑性轉角 θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Plastic rotation θ_p ≈ θ_total − θ_y. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"b021-v13-31","title":"兩級地震性能與非線性驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多組符合場址條件的地震紀錄做非線性時間歷程分析，逐層輸出層間變位角與梁端塑性轉角分布，並與兩級性能目標比對；再把核心斜撐移除、只留抗彎構架做一次分析，確認 25% 的獨立承載要求。減弱斷面的切削尺寸以實尺寸試驗或文獻試驗資料佐證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several site-appropriate records, output storey drift angles and beam-end plastic rotations floor by floor and compare them with the two performance targets; then analyse the moment frame alone with the core bracing removed to confirm the independent 25% requirement, and support reduced-section cut dimensions with full-scale or published test data. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：減弱斷面梁的切削尺寸、位置與表面粗糙度列為檢驗項目，以樣板量測並拍照紀錄；任何因管線而修改梁翼的現場要求，都必須回到設計單位重新檢核塑性鉸位置後才可施作。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make reduced-section cut dimensions, location and surface roughness inspection items, measured with templates and photographed; any field request to modify beam flanges for services must go back to the designer to re-check the plastic hinge location before work proceeds.","failure":"注意干擾：1994 年美國北嶺地震中，許多鋼構抗彎接頭在梁翼焊道附近脆性斷裂，促成減弱斷面梁等改良接頭；若切削位置錯誤或圓弧加工粗糙，塑性鉸仍可能回到柱面，或在切削處提早斷裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: In the 1994 Northridge earthquake many steel moment connections fractured in a brittle manner near the beam-flange welds, prompting improved details such as the reduced beam section; if the cut is mislocated or its radius poorly finished, the hinge can migrate back to the column face or fracture prematurely at the cut. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多組符合場址條件的地震紀錄做非線性時間歷程分析，逐層輸出層間變位角與梁端塑性轉角分布，並與兩級性能目標比對；再把核心斜撐移除、只留抗彎構架做一次分析，確認 25% 的獨立承載要求。減弱斷面的切削尺寸以實尺寸試驗或文獻試驗資料佐證。","textEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several site-appropriate records, output storey drift angles and beam-end plastic rotations floor by floor and compare them with the two performance targets; then analyse the moment frame alone with the core bracing removed to confirm the independent 25% requirement, and support reduced-section cut dimensions with full-scale or published test data.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"減弱斷面梁的切削尺寸、位置與表面粗糙度列為檢驗項目，以樣板量測並拍照紀錄；任何因管線而修改梁翼的現場要求，都必須回到設計單位重新檢核塑性鉸位置後才可施作。","textEn":"Make reduced-section cut dimensions, location and surface roughness inspection items, measured with templates and photographed; any field request to modify beam flanges for services must go back to the designer to re-check the plastic hinge location before work proceeds.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「兩級地震性能與非線性驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以多組符合場址條件的地震紀錄做非線性時間歷程分析，逐層輸出層間變位角與梁端塑性轉角分布，並與兩級性能目標比對。","只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several site-appropriate records, output storey drift angles and beam-end plastic rotations floor by floor and compare them with the two performance targets.","Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以多組符合場址條件的地震紀錄做非線性時間歷程分析，逐層輸出層間變位角與梁端塑性轉角分布，並與兩級性能目標比對；再把核心斜撐移除、只留抗彎構架做一次分析，確認 25% 的獨立承載要求。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several site-appropriate records, output storey drift angles and beam-end plastic rotations floor by floor and compare them with the two performance targets; then analyse the moment frame alone with the core bracing removed to confirm the independent 25% requirement, and support reduced-section cut dimensions with full-scale or published test data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"b021-v13-32","title":"兩級地震性能與非線性驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「減弱斷面梁與塑性轉角」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reduced beam sections and plastic rotation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"1994 年美國北嶺地震中，許多鋼構抗彎接頭在梁翼焊道附近脆性斷裂，促成減弱斷面梁等改良接頭；若切削位置錯誤或圓弧加工粗糙，塑性鉸仍可能回到柱面，或在切削處提早斷裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"In the 1994 Northridge earthquake many steel moment connections fractured in a brittle manner near the beam-flange welds, prompting improved details such as the reduced beam section; if the cut is mislocated or its radius poorly finished, the hinge can migrate back to the column face or fracture prematurely at the cut. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：周邊抗彎構架須能獨立承擔規範要求的 25% 地震力，形成雙重系統；分析中梁端塑性轉角超過約 0.005 弧度的位置改用減弱斷面梁（狗骨頭切削），把塑性鉸從柱面移開，以保護焊接接頭。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The perimeter moment frames must independently carry the code-required 25% of the seismic force, forming a dual system; where analysis shows beam-end plastic rotations above about 0.005 rad, reduced beam sections (dogbone cuts) move the plastic hinge away from the column face to protect the welded joint.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙重系統中的抗彎構架只是分擔核心剩下的力，從不需要單獨承擔。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"In a dual system the moment frame only shares what the core leaves over and never needs to stand alone.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"1994 年美國北嶺地震中，許多鋼構抗彎接頭在梁翼焊道附近脆性斷裂，促成減弱斷面梁等改良接頭；若切削位置錯誤或圓弧加工粗糙，塑性鉸仍可能回到柱面，或在切削處提早斷裂。","textEn":"In the 1994 Northridge earthquake many steel moment connections fractured in a brittle manner near the beam-flange welds, prompting improved details such as the reduced beam section; if the cut is mislocated or its radius poorly finished, the hinge can migrate back to the column face or fracture prematurely at the cut.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「兩級地震性能與非線性驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Two-level seismic performance and nonlinear checks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。","1994 年美國北嶺地震中，許多鋼構抗彎接頭在梁翼焊道附近脆性斷裂，促成減弱斷面梁等改良接頭。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.","In the 1994 Northridge earthquake many steel moment connections fractured in a brittle manner near the beam-flange welds, prompting improved details such as the reduced beam section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"1994 年美國北嶺地震中，許多鋼構抗彎接頭在梁翼焊道附近脆性斷裂，促成減弱斷面梁等改良接頭；若切削位置錯誤或圓弧加工粗糙，塑性鉸仍可能回到柱面，或在切削處提早斷裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"In the 1994 Northridge earthquake many steel moment connections fractured in a brittle manner near the beam-flange welds, prompting improved details such as the reduced beam section; if the cut is mislocated or its radius poorly finished, the hinge can migrate back to the column face or fracture prematurely at the cut. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":8},{"id":"b021-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查」與「颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes\" and \"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b021-v13-33","title":"颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damper event-swing records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 的主擺錘在營運期間累積了一系列事件紀錄：2015 年 8 月蘇迪勒颱風時擺幅約 100 cm，為歷來最大；2019 年 4 月規模 6.1 地震時約 20 cm，是當時地震造成的最大擺幅。這些紀錄是結構健康的證據：擺幅、方向與持續時間可與同時段的風速及地震紀錄比對，判斷阻尼器是否仍在調頻範圍、緩衝系統是否被碰觸，並決定事件後的檢查深度。本單元把阻尼器當作監測儀器使用，不重複其調頻原理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101's main pendulum has built up a record of events in service: about 100 cm of swing in Typhoon Soudelor in August 2015, the largest so far, and about 20 cm in a magnitude 6.1 earthquake in April 2019, then the largest earthquake-induced swing. These records are structural-health evidence: amplitude, direction and duration can be compared with concurrent wind and earthquake records to judge whether the damper is still in tune and whether the bumper system was touched, and to set the depth of post-event inspection. This unit uses the damper as a monitoring instrument rather than revisiting its tuning theory. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Damper event-swing records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：擺錘簡諧運動的最大速度 v = 2π·f·A。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For harmonic pendulum motion the peak velocity is v = 2π·f·A.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Damper event-swing records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-33-k1","title":"颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查","titleEn":"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes","text":"台北 101 的主擺錘在營運期間累積了一系列事件紀錄：2015 年 8 月蘇迪勒颱風時擺幅約 100 cm，為歷來最大；2019 年 4 月規模 6.1 地震時約 20 cm，是當時地震造成的最大擺幅。這些紀錄是結構健康的證據：擺幅、方向與持續時間可與同時段的風速及地震紀錄比對，判斷阻尼器是否仍在調頻範圍、緩衝系統是否被碰觸，並決定事件後的檢查深度。","textEn":"Taipei 101's main pendulum has built up a record of events in service: about 100 cm of swing in Typhoon Soudelor in August 2015, the largest so far, and about 20 cm in a magnitude 6.1 earthquake in April 2019, then the largest earthquake-induced swing. These records are structural-health evidence: amplitude, direction and duration can be compared with concurrent wind and earthquake records to judge whether the damper is still in tune and whether the bumper system was touched, and to set the depth of post-event inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes\" is correct?","options":["台北 101 的主擺錘在營運期間累積了一系列事件紀錄：2015 年 8 月蘇迪勒颱風時擺幅約 100 cm，為歷來最大。","阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。","帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。"],"optionsEn":["Taipei 101's main pendulum has built up a record of events in service: about 100 cm of swing in Typhoon Soudelor in August 2015, the largest so far, and about 20 cm in a magnitude 6.1 earthquake in April 2019, then the largest earthquake-induced swing.","A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.","A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"台北 101 的主擺錘在營運期間累積了一系列事件紀錄：2015 年 8 月蘇迪勒颱風時擺幅約 100 cm，為歷來最大；2019 年 4 月規模 6.1 地震時約 20 cm，是當時地震造成的最大擺幅。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101's main pendulum has built up a record of events in service: about 100 cm of swing in Typhoon Soudelor in August 2015, the largest so far, and about 20 cm in a magnitude 6.1 earthquake in April 2019, then the largest earthquake-induced swing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":57},{"id":"b021-v13-34","title":"颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damper event-swing records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：擺錘簡諧運動的最大速度 v = 2π·f·A。取 f = 0.14 Hz、A = 1.0 m，v = 2π×0.14×1.0 ≈ 0.88 m/s，660 t 擺錘的動能 ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×660,000×0.88² ≈ 256 kJ；若設計行程為 ±1.5 m，行程使用率約 1.0/1.5 ≈ 67%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For harmonic pendulum motion the peak velocity is v = 2π·f·A. With f = 0.14 Hz and A = 1.0 m, v = 2π×0.14×1.0 ≈ 0.88 m/s and a 660 t pendulum carries ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×660,000×0.88² ≈ 256 kJ; against a design stroke of ±1.5 m the stroke utilisation is about 1.0/1.5 ≈ 67%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：事件後先調出擺錘位移、樓層加速度與風速或地震紀錄，確認最大擺幅與行程限制之間的餘裕；接著目視檢查緩衝環接觸痕跡、阻尼器漏油、吊索與吊點，必要時以自由擺動量測頻率是否仍與基準值相符，結果寫入事件報告。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After an event, retrieve pendulum displacement, floor acceleration and wind or earthquake records and confirm the margin between peak swing and stroke limits; then inspect bumper-ring contact marks, damper leaks, hangers and pick points, and if needed measure the free-swing frequency against the baseline, recording the results in an event report.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"擺錘簡諧運動的最大速度 v = 2π·f·A。取 f = 0.14 Hz、A = 1.0 m，v = 2π×0.14×1.0 ≈ 0.88 m/s，660 t 擺錘的動能 ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×660,000×0.88² ≈ 256 kJ；若設計行程為 ±1.5 m，行程使用率約 1.0/1.5 ≈ 67%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For harmonic pendulum motion the peak velocity is v = 2π·f·A. With f = 0.14 Hz and A = 1.0 m, v = 2π×0.14×1.0 ≈ 0.88 m/s and a 660 t pendulum carries ½·m·v² ≈ 0.5×660,000×0.88² ≈ 256 kJ; against a design stroke of ±1.5 m the stroke utilisation is about 1.0/1.5 ≈ 67%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸桁架設得越多越好，每層都設最能減少變位。","擺錘簡諧運動的最大速度 v = 2π·f·A。","鋼材強度等級越高越好，降伏比高一點也沒有關係。"],"optionsEn":["The more outriggers the better; one on every floor reduces drift most.","For harmonic pendulum motion the peak velocity is v = 2π·f·A.","The higher the steel grade the better, and a high yield ratio does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擺錘簡諧運動的最大速度 v = 2π·f·A。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For harmonic pendulum motion the peak velocity is v = 2π·f·A. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":58},{"id":"b021-v13-35","title":"颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damper event-swing records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"事件後先調出擺錘位移、樓層加速度與風速或地震紀錄，確認最大擺幅與行程限制之間的餘裕；接著目視檢查緩衝環接觸痕跡、阻尼器漏油、吊索與吊點，必要時以自由擺動量測頻率是否仍與基準值相符，結果寫入事件報告。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After an event, retrieve pendulum displacement, floor acceleration and wind or earthquake records and confirm the margin between peak swing and stroke limits; then inspect bumper-ring contact marks, damper leaks, hangers and pick points, and if needed measure the free-swing frequency against the baseline, recording the results in an event report. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立事件分級：擺幅或樓層加速度超過設定門檻即啟動詳細檢查；每次事件的擺幅、風速、處置與檢查結果累積成趨勢表，提供結構顧問年度審查並作為調頻複核的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Set event tiers in which swing or floor acceleration above set thresholds triggers a detailed inspection, and accumulate each event's swing, wind speed, actions and findings into a trend table for the structural consultant's annual review and as the basis for re-checking the tuning.","failure":"注意干擾：若事件紀錄沒有時間同步，擺錘位移無法對應風速，就分不出大擺幅來自強風還是阻尼器失調；事件後若省略緩衝器檢查，隱藏的損傷可能要到下一次颱風才顯現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without time-synchronised records, pendulum displacement cannot be matched to wind speed, so a large swing cannot be attributed to strong wind or to detuning; skipping the post-event bumper inspection lets hidden damage surface only in the next typhoon. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"事件後先調出擺錘位移、樓層加速度與風速或地震紀錄，確認最大擺幅與行程限制之間的餘裕；接著目視檢查緩衝環接觸痕跡、阻尼器漏油、吊索與吊點，必要時以自由擺動量測頻率是否仍與基準值相符，結果寫入事件報告。","textEn":"After an event, retrieve pendulum displacement, floor acceleration and wind or earthquake records and confirm the margin between peak swing and stroke limits; then inspect bumper-ring contact marks, damper leaks, hangers and pick points, and if needed measure the free-swing frequency against the baseline, recording the results in an event report.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立事件分級：擺幅或樓層加速度超過設定門檻即啟動詳細檢查；每次事件的擺幅、風速、處置與檢查結果累積成趨勢表，提供結構顧問年度審查並作為調頻複核的依據。","textEn":"Set event tiers in which swing or floor acceleration above set thresholds triggers a detailed inspection, and accumulate each event's swing, wind speed, actions and findings into a trend table for the structural consultant's annual review and as the basis for re-checking the tuning.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","塔吊是臨時設備，不需要考慮地震力。","事件後先調出擺錘位移、樓層加速度與風速或地震紀錄，確認最大擺幅與行程限制之間的餘裕。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Tower cranes are temporary equipment and need not be designed for earthquakes.","After an event, retrieve pendulum displacement, floor acceleration and wind or earthquake records and confirm the margin between peak swing and stroke limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"事件後先調出擺錘位移、樓層加速度與風速或地震紀錄，確認最大擺幅與行程限制之間的餘裕；接著目視檢查緩衝環接觸痕跡、阻尼器漏油、吊索與吊點，必要時以自由擺動量測頻率是否仍與基準值相符，結果寫入事件報告。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After an event, retrieve pendulum displacement, floor acceleration and wind or earthquake records and confirm the margin between peak swing and stroke limits; then inspect bumper-ring contact marks, damper leaks, hangers and pick points, and if needed measure the free-swing frequency against the baseline, recording the results in an event report. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":59},{"id":"b021-v13-36","title":"颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「阻尼器事件擺幅紀錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damper event-swing records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若事件紀錄沒有時間同步，擺錘位移無法對應風速，就分不出大擺幅來自強風還是阻尼器失調；事件後若省略緩衝器檢查，隱藏的損傷可能要到下一次颱風才顯現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without time-synchronised records, pendulum displacement cannot be matched to wind speed, so a large swing cannot be attributed to strong wind or to detuning; skipping the post-event bumper inspection lets hidden damage surface only in the next typhoon. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本單元把阻尼器當作監測儀器使用，不重複其調頻原理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This unit uses the damper as a monitoring instrument rather than revisiting its tuning theory.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器擺幅創紀錄，就代表大樓結構出了問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A record damper swing means something is wrong with the building structure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若事件紀錄沒有時間同步，擺錘位移無法對應風速，就分不出大擺幅來自強風還是阻尼器失調；事件後若省略緩衝器檢查，隱藏的損傷可能要到下一次颱風才顯現。","textEn":"Without time-synchronised records, pendulum displacement cannot be matched to wind speed, so a large swing cannot be attributed to strong wind or to detuning; skipping the post-event bumper inspection lets hidden damage surface only in the next typhoon.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「颱風與地震後的阻尼器紀錄與檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damper records and inspection after typhoons and earthquakes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若事件紀錄沒有時間同步，擺錘位移無法對應風速，就分不出大擺幅來自強風還是阻尼器失調；事件後若省略緩衝器檢查，隱藏的損傷可能要到下一次颱風才顯現。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。"],"optionsEn":["Without time-synchronised records, pendulum displacement cannot be matched to wind speed, so a large swing cannot be attributed to strong wind or to detuning.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若事件紀錄沒有時間同步，擺錘位移無法對應風速，就分不出大擺幅來自強風還是阻尼器失調；事件後若省略緩衝器檢查，隱藏的損傷可能要到下一次颱風才顯現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without time-synchronised records, pendulum displacement cannot be matched to wind speed, so a large swing cannot be attributed to strong wind or to detuning; skipping the post-event bumper inspection lets hidden damage surface only in the next typhoon. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":60},{"id":"b021-v13-37","title":"颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」如何影響台北 101的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift” governs force, deformation or durability in “Taipei 101”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"台北 101 位於颱風區，帷幕單元面積大，玻璃供應商指出必須使用比一般更厚的玻璃基板，單片面積平均約 40 平方英尺（約 3.7 m²），窗間牆部位則使用客製的陶瓷釉面玻璃。帷幕牆同時承受正負風壓與樓層間的相對變位：風壓使玻璃彎曲，層間變位則讓框架變成平行四邊形，必須靠框內間隙與可滑動的連接件吸收。長期維護的重點是密封膠、墊片、破損玻璃更換，以及外牆維護設備的可達性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipei 101 stands in a typhoon zone with large curtain-wall units; its glass supplier states that thicker-than-typical glass substrates were needed, with individual units averaging about 40 ft² (about 3.7 m²) and custom ceramic-frit glass in the spandrels. The curtain wall must resist positive and negative wind pressure and relative storey movement at the same time: pressure bends the glass, while drift racks the frame into a parallelogram that edge clearances and sliding connections must absorb. Long-term upkeep centres on sealants, gaskets, broken-glass replacement and access for façade maintenance equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：四邊簡支玻璃板最大應力 σ = β·p·a²/t²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Peak stress in a four-side-supported glass plate is σ = β·p·a²/t².","failure":"常見誤解：「帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-37-k1","title":"颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護","titleEn":"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep","text":"台北 101 位於颱風區，帷幕單元面積大，玻璃供應商指出必須使用比一般更厚的玻璃基板，單片面積平均約 40 平方英尺（約 3.7 m²），窗間牆部位則使用客製的陶瓷釉面玻璃。帷幕牆同時承受正負風壓與樓層間的相對變位：風壓使玻璃彎曲，層間變位則讓框架變成平行四邊形，必須靠框內間隙與可滑動的連接件吸收。","textEn":"Taipei 101 stands in a typhoon zone with large curtain-wall units; its glass supplier states that thicker-than-typical glass substrates were needed, with individual units averaging about 40 ft² (about 3.7 m²) and custom ceramic-frit glass in the spandrels. The curtain wall must resist positive and negative wind pressure and relative storey movement at the same time: pressure bends the glass, while drift racks the frame into a parallelogram that edge clearances and sliding connections must absorb.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep\" is correct?","options":["帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。","台北 101 位於颱風區，帷幕單元面積大，玻璃供應商指出必須使用比一般更厚的玻璃基板，單片面積平均約 40 平方英尺（約 3.7 m²），窗間牆部位則使用客製的陶瓷釉面玻璃。","角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。"],"optionsEn":["A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement.","Taipei 101 stands in a typhoon zone with large curtain-wall units.","Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"台北 101 位於颱風區，帷幕單元面積大，玻璃供應商指出必須使用比一般更厚的玻璃基板，單片面積平均約 40 平方英尺（約 3.7 m²），窗間牆部位則使用客製的陶瓷釉面玻璃。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipei 101 stands in a typhoon zone with large curtain-wall units; its glass supplier states that thicker-than-typical glass substrates were needed, with individual units averaging about 40 ft² (about 3.7 m²) and custom ceramic-frit glass in the spandrels. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":61},{"id":"b021-v13-38","title":"颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：四邊簡支玻璃板最大應力 σ = β·p·a²/t²。短邊 a = 1.5 m、厚 t = 12 mm、風壓 p = 4.0 kPa、β = 0.48，σ = 0.48×4,000×1.5²/0.012² = 30 MPa；層間變位角 1/200、樓高 4.2 m 時，框架水平錯動 4,200/200 = 21 mm，需由框內間隙與滑動連接吸收。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Peak stress in a four-side-supported glass plate is σ = β·p·a²/t². With short side a = 1.5 m, thickness t = 12 mm, pressure p = 4.0 kPa and β = 0.48, σ = 0.48×4,000×1.5²/0.012² = 30 MPa; a drift angle of 1/200 over a 4.2 m storey racks the frame 4,200/200 = 21 mm, which edge clearances and sliding connections must absorb. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以實尺寸帷幕牆試體做風壓（含颱風循環）、水密、氣密與層間變位試驗，確認玻璃不破、密封不漏水；完工後定期以目視與望遠鏡檢查密封膠劣化與玻璃自爆，並記錄每片更換玻璃的位置、原因與規格。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test full-scale curtain-wall mock-ups for wind pressure including typhoon cycles, water and air tightness and storey-drift racking, confirming no glass breakage or leakage; after completion inspect visually and with binoculars for sealant ageing and spontaneous glass breakage, recording the location, cause and specification of every replaced pane.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"四邊簡支玻璃板最大應力 σ = β·p·a²/t²。短邊 a = 1.5 m、厚 t = 12 mm、風壓 p = 4.0 kPa、β = 0.48，σ = 0.48×4,000×1.5²/0.012² = 30 MPa；層間變位角 1/200、樓高 4.2 m 時，框架水平錯動 4,200/200 = 21 mm，需由框內間隙與滑動連接吸收。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Peak stress in a four-side-supported glass plate is σ = β·p·a²/t². With short side a = 1.5 m, thickness t = 12 mm, pressure p = 4.0 kPa and β = 0.48, σ = 0.48×4,000×1.5²/0.012² = 30 MPa; a drift angle of 1/200 over a 4.2 m storey racks the frame 4,200/200 = 21 mm, which edge clearances and sliding connections must absorb. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼箱巨柱裡的混凝土只是為了增加重量與防火。","只要基樁打到岩盤，沉陷就可以忽略。","四邊簡支玻璃板最大應力 σ = β·p·a²/t²。"],"optionsEn":["The concrete inside a steel-box mega-column is only there to add weight and fire protection.","Once piles reach bedrock, settlement can be ignored.","Peak stress in a four-side-supported glass plate is σ = β·p·a²/t²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"四邊簡支玻璃板最大應力 σ = β·p·a²/t²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Peak stress in a four-side-supported glass plate is σ = β·p·a²/t². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":62},{"id":"b021-v13-39","title":"颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以實尺寸帷幕牆試體做風壓（含颱風循環）、水密、氣密與層間變位試驗，確認玻璃不破、密封不漏水；完工後定期以目視與望遠鏡檢查密封膠劣化與玻璃自爆，並記錄每片更換玻璃的位置、原因與規格。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test full-scale curtain-wall mock-ups for wind pressure including typhoon cycles, water and air tightness and storey-drift racking, confirming no glass breakage or leakage; after completion inspect visually and with binoculars for sealant ageing and spontaneous glass breakage, recording the location, cause and specification of every replaced pane. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要附帷幕牆試驗報告、各樓層允許層間變位、連接件滑動方向圖與備品玻璃清單；颱風季前檢查外牆維護設備的固定與停放，颱風後逐層巡檢，並把破損紀錄回饋給結構與帷幕顧問。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include curtain-wall test reports, allowable storey drift per floor, sliding-direction diagrams for connections and a spare-glass list; before typhoon season check the securing and parking of façade maintenance equipment, and after typhoons inspect floor by floor, feeding breakage records back to the structural and façade consultants.","failure":"注意干擾：若帷幕牆連接件在安裝時被誤鎖死，層間變位會直接擠壓玻璃，造成角部破裂；颱風期間一片玻璃破損會讓室內受壓，進而吹落隔間與天花板，碎片也成為高空墜落物。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If curtain-wall connections are mistakenly locked during installation, storey drift squeezes the glass directly and cracks the corners; one broken pane in a typhoon pressurises the interior, blowing out partitions and ceilings and turning fragments into falling debris. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以實尺寸帷幕牆試體做風壓（含颱風循環）、水密、氣密與層間變位試驗，確認玻璃不破、密封不漏水；完工後定期以目視與望遠鏡檢查密封膠劣化與玻璃自爆，並記錄每片更換玻璃的位置、原因與規格。","textEn":"Test full-scale curtain-wall mock-ups for wind pressure including typhoon cycles, water and air tightness and storey-drift racking, confirming no glass breakage or leakage; after completion inspect visually and with binoculars for sealant ageing and spontaneous glass breakage, recording the location, cause and specification of every replaced pane.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要附帷幕牆試驗報告、各樓層允許層間變位、連接件滑動方向圖與備品玻璃清單；颱風季前檢查外牆維護設備的固定與停放，颱風後逐層巡檢，並把破損紀錄回饋給結構與帷幕顧問。","textEn":"Handover should include curtain-wall test reports, allowable storey drift per floor, sliding-direction diagrams for connections and a spare-glass list; before typhoon season check the securing and parking of façade maintenance equipment, and after typhoons inspect floor by floor, feeding breakage records back to the structural and façade consultants.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep\"?","options":["以實尺寸帷幕牆試體做風壓（含颱風循環）、水密、氣密與層間變位試驗，確認玻璃不破、密封不漏水。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","自充填混凝土會自動填滿鋼箱，不需要開孔排氣或檢測。"],"optionsEn":["Test full-scale curtain-wall mock-ups for wind pressure including typhoon cycles, water and air tightness and storey-drift racking, confirming no glass breakage or leakage.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Self-consolidating concrete fills a steel box automatically, so no vent holes or testing are needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以實尺寸帷幕牆試體做風壓（含颱風循環）、水密、氣密與層間變位試驗，確認玻璃不破、密封不漏水；完工後定期以目視與望遠鏡檢查密封膠劣化與玻璃自爆，並記錄每片更換玻璃的位置、原因與規格。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test full-scale curtain-wall mock-ups for wind pressure including typhoon cycles, water and air tightness and storey-drift racking, confirming no glass breakage or leakage; after completion inspect visually and with binoculars for sealant ageing and spontaneous glass breakage, recording the location, cause and specification of every replaced pane. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":63},{"id":"b021-v13-40","title":"颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"],"prerequisiteIds":["b021-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「帷幕牆玻璃與層間變位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Curtain-wall glass and storey drift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若帷幕牆連接件在安裝時被誤鎖死，層間變位會直接擠壓玻璃，造成角部破裂；颱風期間一片玻璃破損會讓室內受壓，進而吹落隔間與天花板，碎片也成為高空墜落物。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If curtain-wall connections are mistakenly locked during installation, storey drift squeezes the glass directly and cracks the corners; one broken pane in a typhoon pressurises the interior, blowing out partitions and ceilings and turning fragments into falling debris. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：長期維護的重點是密封膠、墊片、破損玻璃更換，以及外牆維護設備的可達性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Long-term upkeep centres on sealants, gaskets, broken-glass replacement and access for façade maintenance equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「帷幕牆只是外觀，不需要配合結構的變位來設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A curtain wall is cosmetic and need not be designed for structural movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b021-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若帷幕牆連接件在安裝時被誤鎖死，層間變位會直接擠壓玻璃，造成角部破裂；颱風期間一片玻璃破損會讓室內受壓，進而吹落隔間與天花板，碎片也成為高空墜落物。","textEn":"If curtain-wall connections are mistakenly locked during installation, storey drift squeezes the glass directly and cracks the corners; one broken pane in a typhoon pressurises the interior, blowing out partitions and ceilings and turning fragments into falling debris.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]},{"id":"b021-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-seags-taipei-101-piles","v13s-ntu-chang-taipei-101","v13s-taipeitimes-2002-cranes"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「颱風風壓下的帷幕玻璃與長期維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Curtain-wall glass under typhoon pressure and long-term upkeep\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若帷幕牆連接件在安裝時被誤鎖死，層間變位會直接擠壓玻璃，造成角部破裂；颱風期間一片玻璃破損會讓室內受壓，進而吹落隔間與天花板，碎片也成為高空墜落物。","角隅缺角主要是造型裝飾，對結構風力沒有實質影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If curtain-wall connections are mistakenly locked during installation, storey drift squeezes the glass directly and cracks the corners.","Corner notches are mainly decorative and have no real effect on structural wind loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若帷幕牆連接件在安裝時被誤鎖死，層間變位會直接擠壓玻璃，造成角部破裂；颱風期間一片玻璃破損會讓室內受壓，進而吹落隔間與天花板，碎片也成為高空墜落物。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If curtain-wall connections are mistakenly locked during installation, storey drift squeezes the glass directly and cracks the corners; one broken pane in a typhoon pressurises the interior, blowing out partitions and ceilings and turning fragments into falling debris. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":64}],"order":9}],"curriculumVersion":7,"enrichmentVersion":13,"learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-supertall","learningTags":["structures","st-supertall","tower"],"subcategory":"st-supertall","subcategoryTitle":"超高層建築巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"Supertall building landmarks","v13Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"tower","architectureNodes":[["鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱","Concrete-filled mega-columns"],["外伸桁架與帶狀桁架","Outriggers and belt trusses"],["斜撐核心筒","Braced core"],["周邊抗彎構架","Perimeter moment frames"],["筏基與岩盤嵌入基樁","Raft and rock-socketed piles"],["阻尼器與事件紀錄","Damper and event records"]],"architectureEdges":[[2,1],[1,0],[3,0],[0,4],[2,4],[2,5]]},"v13Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"巨柱檢核練習：某鋼箱填充混凝土巨柱 2.4 m × 3.0 m、板厚 80 mm，f_y = 414 MPa、f_c = 69 MPa。A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m²、A_s = 0.84 m²，名目擠壓強度 N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 720 MN，取強度折減 0.75 得設計容量約 540 MN。外伸桁架傳來的彎矩 12 GN·m 由力臂 40 m、每側 4 支巨柱分擔，ΔN = 12,000/(40×4) = 75 MN；重力軸力 350 MN 時受壓側合計 425 MN，使用率 425/540 ≈ 0.79。若填充混凝土只達 41 MPa，N₀ 約 569 MN、設計容量約 427 MN，使用率升到約 1.00，已無餘裕；若外伸桁架勁度不足使 M_col 降為 8 GN·m，ΔN 減為 50 MN，但核心筒須多承擔 4 GN·m。數值為教學假設，不代表台北 101 的設計值。","textEn":"Mega-column check: a concrete-filled steel box 2.4 m × 3.0 m with 80 mm plate, f_y = 414 MPa and f_c = 69 MPa. A_c = 2.24×2.84 = 6.36 m² and A_s = 0.84 m², so the nominal squash load is N₀ = 0.84×414 + 0.85×69×6.36 ≈ 720 MN, or about 540 MN design capacity with a resistance factor of 0.75. An outrigger moment of 12 GN·m shared over a 40 m lever arm by 4 columns per side gives ΔN = 12,000/(40×4) = 75 MN; with 350 MN of gravity load the compression side carries 425 MN, a utilisation of 425/540 ≈ 0.79. If the infill reaches only 41 MPa, N₀ is about 569 MN and design capacity about 427 MN, pushing utilisation to about 1.00 with no margin left; if softer outriggers reduce M_col to 8 GN·m, ΔN drops to 50 MN but the core must carry an extra 4 GN·m. Values are teaching assumptions, not Taipei 101's design values.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"以巨柱合成斷面、外伸桁架力偶、台北盆地基樁與施工期臨時結構的實際數字，深化台北 101 的結構檢核","focusEn":"Deepening Taipei 101 checks with real numbers on composite mega-columns, outrigger couples, basin piles and construction-stage temporary works"}},{"id":"b103","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical","v10-other-vendor-b103","v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"title":"哥達基線隧道","titleEn":"Gotthard Base Tunnel","summary":"沿 24 個判讀步驟研究阿爾卑斯基線鐵路的路線、地質、施工物流、防水與鐵路系統整合；以可查證的證據代替想像中的挖掘配方。","summaryEn":"Study alignment, geology, construction logistics, waterproofing and railway integration of an Alpine base tunnel through 24 evidence-led exercises.","scope":"以公開一次資料為背景的原創工程判讀課程；每步在紙上或數位示意模型中完成。自設數值、構形與工序不得當成原工程的設計、施工、設備操作或驗收程序。","scopeEn":"Original engineering interpretation exercises grounded in public primary sources. Complete each step on paper or in a schematic digital model. Invented values, geometry and sequences are not the original project’s design, construction, operating or acceptance procedures.","diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["需求與場址","結構與介面","施工狀態","驗證與維護"],"labelsEn":["Requirements and site","Structures and interfaces","Construction states","Verification and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":64,"estimatedMinutes":1600,"stages":[{"id":"b103-stage01","order":1,"title":"路線、地質與不確定性","titleEn":"Alignment, geology and uncertainty","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「路線、地質與不確定性」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on alignment, geology and uncertainty, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把基線路線放回鐵路網","titleEn":"Place the base alignment in its network","objective":"理解隧道長度以外的運輸目的。","objectiveEn":"Understand the transport purpose beyond tunnel length.","instruction":"1. 畫跨山舊線與概念基線；2. 分列坡度、距離及連接路段；3. 指出一個仍可能限制全線容量的外部瓶頸。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch the mountain route and conceptual base route; 2. separate gradient, distance and connecting sections; 3. identify an external bottleneck that could still limit capacity.","observation":"隧道本身能力提高不會自動消除連接鐵路的瓶頸。","observationEn":"Improved tunnel capability does not automatically remove bottlenecks on connecting railways.","failure":"只要隧道更長就一定使整條運輸走廊更有效率。","failureEn":"A longer tunnel necessarily makes the entire transport corridor more efficient.","check":"繳交含兩端連接線的需求圖。","checkEn":"Provide a requirements map including both connecting routes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-01-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"基線路線以較低高程穿越山體，坡度及路線條件影響列車牽引與運輸安排。","textEn":"A base route crosses at a lower elevation; gradients and alignment affect traction and transport planning."},{"id":"b103-v7-01-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方長度及運輸背景是比較起點，不能直接用來計算今天的班表能力。","textEn":"Official length and transport context begin the comparison but do not directly determine present timetable capacity."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把基線路線放回鐵路網」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Place the base alignment in its network”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["隧道本身能力提高不會自動消除連接鐵路的瓶頸。","只要隧道更長就一定使整條運輸走廊更有效率。","增加一段隧道的能力就保證所有連接路段同步增加能力。"],"optionsEn":["Improved tunnel capability does not automatically remove bottlenecks on connecting railways.","A longer tunnel necessarily makes the entire transport corridor more efficient.","Increasing one tunnel’s capacity guarantees matching gains on all connecting routes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基線路線以較低高程穿越山體，坡度及路線條件影響列車牽引與運輸安排。 官方長度及運輸背景是比較起點，不能直接用來計算今天的班表能力。","explanationEn":"A base route crosses at a lower elevation; gradients and alignment affect traction and transport planning. Official length and transport context begin the comparison but do not directly determine present timetable capacity."}},{"id":"b103-v7-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-01"],"title":"分開雙管與連通設施","titleEn":"Separate running tubes and connections","objective":"辨認列車路徑與橫向連通功能。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish train paths from transverse connections.","instruction":"1. 畫兩條單線主隧道；2. 用不同符號標示橫坑及多功能區；3. 分開列車通道與人員通行的概念圖例。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two single-track running tubes; 2. mark cross-passages and multifunction areas with different symbols; 3. separate train paths from conceptual pedestrian connections.","observation":"兩條主隧道與橫坑具有不同功能，不能都視為可行車路線。","observationEn":"Running tubes and cross-passages have different functions and are not all train routes.","failure":"圖上只要連通就能讓列車任意從一管換到另一管。","failureEn":"Any connection drawn between tubes permits trains to change tubes there.","check":"提供至少三種連通功能的圖例。","checkEn":"Provide a legend distinguishing at least three connection functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-02-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"交通路徑、設備空間與逃生連通各有不同幾何及系統需求。","textEn":"Traffic paths, equipment spaces and escape connections have different geometric and system requirements."},{"id":"b103-v7-02-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"示意圖的連線不等於具備軌道、控制或可使用狀態。","textEn":"A connecting line in a schematic does not establish track, control or availability."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開雙管與連通設施」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate running tubes and connections”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["圖上只要連通就能讓列車任意從一管換到另一管。","兩條主隧道與橫坑具有不同功能，不能都視為可行車路線。","所有橫坑都具有列車軌道及轉轍功能。"],"optionsEn":["Any connection drawn between tubes permits trains to change tubes there.","Running tubes and cross-passages have different functions and are not all train routes.","Every cross-passage contains tracks and train-switching functions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交通路徑、設備空間與逃生連通各有不同幾何及系統需求。 示意圖的連線不等於具備軌道、控制或可使用狀態。","explanationEn":"Traffic paths, equipment spaces and escape connections have different geometric and system requirements. A connecting line in a schematic does not establish track, control or availability."}},{"id":"b103-v7-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-02"],"title":"建立地質預測與實證兩欄","titleEn":"Separate predicted geology from observations","objective":"把地質模型當成需持續更新的假說。","objectiveEn":"Treat the geological model as a hypothesis requiring updates.","instruction":"1. 畫含三種自設岩性區的縱斷面；2. 另列鑽孔與掌子面觀察欄；3. 將未驗證區段以虛線保留。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a longitudinal section with three hypothetical rock zones; 2. separate borehole and face observations; 3. keep unverified sections dashed.","observation":"地質預測必須隨新觀察更新，不能等同沿線已完全確認。","observationEn":"Geological predictions need updating with observations and do not establish complete route knowledge.","failure":"已有一張縱斷面就表示兩個鑽孔之間的岩體全部已證實。","failureEn":"One section drawing verifies every rock volume between two boreholes.","check":"提交預測、觀察與信心水準分開的剖面。","checkEn":"Submit a section separating predictions, observations and confidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-03-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"鑽孔只直接觀察有限空間，向外延伸的解釋具有不確定性。","textEn":"Boreholes directly sample limited space; extrapolated interpretations carry uncertainty."},{"id":"b103-v7-03-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"工程判讀重點是預測與實際差異如何影響模型，而非把地層畫得整齊。","textEn":"Engineering interpretation asks how prediction–observation differences affect the model, not how tidy the strata look."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立地質預測與實證兩欄」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate predicted geology from observations”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["已有一張縱斷面就表示兩個鑽孔之間的岩體全部已證實。","鑽孔間的地層圖是直接觀察全部地下空間的紀錄。","地質預測必須隨新觀察更新，不能等同沿線已完全確認。"],"optionsEn":["One section drawing verifies every rock volume between two boreholes.","A section between boreholes directly records the entire underground volume.","Geological predictions need updating with observations and do not establish complete route knowledge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鑽孔只直接觀察有限空間，向外延伸的解釋具有不確定性。 工程判讀重點是預測與實際差異如何影響模型，而非把地層畫得整齊。","explanationEn":"Boreholes directly sample limited space; extrapolated interpretations carry uncertainty. Engineering interpretation asks how prediction–observation differences affect the model, not how tidy the strata look."}},{"id":"b103-v7-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-03"],"title":"解讀斷層與破碎帶","titleEn":"Interpret faults and fractured zones","objective":"辨識岩石種類與岩體結構的不同。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish rock type from rock-mass structure.","instruction":"1. 用同一岩性畫完整及節理密集兩模型；2. 標出節理方向與水的可能路徑；3. 比較需要補充的觀察資料。","instructionEn":"1. Draw intact and heavily jointed examples of the same rock type; 2. mark joint directions and possible water paths; 3. compare required observations.","observation":"相同岩石名稱可能對應不同節理、水文及變形條件。","observationEn":"The same rock name may conceal different jointing, groundwater and deformation conditions.","failure":"只知道岩石硬度即可選定所有支護需求。","failureEn":"Rock hardness alone determines every support requirement.","check":"繳交岩性、構造與含水條件的分欄表。","checkEn":"Provide separate fields for lithology, structure and groundwater.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-04-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"岩體行為不只由完整岩塊強度決定，也受不連續面與水影響。","textEn":"Rock-mass behavior depends on discontinuities and water as well as intact-rock strength."},{"id":"b103-v7-04-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步不提供支護尺寸或挖掘設定，而是建立需由地質證據回答的問題。","textEn":"This step gives no support dimensions or excavation settings; it defines questions requiring geological evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「解讀斷層與破碎帶」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret faults and fractured zones”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["相同岩石名稱可能對應不同節理、水文及變形條件。","只知道岩石硬度即可選定所有支護需求。","完整岩塊的強度可以取代節理與地下水資料。"],"optionsEn":["The same rock name may conceal different jointing, groundwater and deformation conditions.","Rock hardness alone determines every support requirement.","Intact-rock strength replaces joint and groundwater information."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩體行為不只由完整岩塊強度決定，也受不連續面與水影響。 本步不提供支護尺寸或挖掘設定，而是建立需由地質證據回答的問題。","explanationEn":"Rock-mass behavior depends on discontinuities and water as well as intact-rock strength. This step gives no support dimensions or excavation settings; it defines questions requiring geological evidence."}},{"id":"b103-v7-05","sequence":5,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-04"],"title":"辨認覆土、地應力與溫度","titleEn":"Distinguish cover, stress and temperature","objective":"避免用單一深度數字概括地下條件。","objectiveEn":"Avoid reducing underground conditions to one depth number.","instruction":"1. 在斷面分別標示地表及隧道標高；2. 畫假想覆土變化；3. 將應力、熱與地下水證據列成不同需求。","instructionEn":"1. Mark surface and tunnel elevations separately; 2. draw hypothetical cover variation; 3. list separate stress, heat and groundwater evidence needs.","observation":"覆土深度增加不等於所有位置具有同樣應力方向或水壓。","observationEn":"Greater cover does not imply identical stress directions or water pressures everywhere.","failure":"地表到隧道的距離可以直接替代完整地應力與水文資料。","failureEn":"Surface-to-tunnel distance replaces complete stress and hydrogeological information.","check":"提交三類環境條件及各自需量測的資料。","checkEn":"Submit three environmental conditions with their measurement needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-05-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地形、構造歷史與岩體性質會使應力場偏離簡單垂直自重估算。","textEn":"Topography, tectonic history and rock properties can make stress fields differ from simple overburden estimates."},{"id":"b103-v7-05-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"熱、水與力學資料具有不同量測方法，不能因共用一張剖面就互相代替。","textEn":"Thermal, hydraulic and mechanical conditions require different observations despite sharing a section drawing."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認覆土、地應力與溫度」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish cover, stress and temperature”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["地表到隧道的距離可以直接替代完整地應力與水文資料。","覆土深度增加不等於所有位置具有同樣應力方向或水壓。","熱環境與水壓可從覆土深度唯一決定。"],"optionsEn":["Surface-to-tunnel distance replaces complete stress and hydrogeological information.","Greater cover does not imply identical stress directions or water pressures everywhere.","Cover depth uniquely determines temperature and water pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地形、構造歷史與岩體性質會使應力場偏離簡單垂直自重估算。 熱、水與力學資料具有不同量測方法，不能因共用一張剖面就互相代替。","explanationEn":"Topography, tectonic history and rock properties can make stress fields differ from simple overburden estimates. Thermal, hydraulic and mechanical conditions require different observations despite sharing a section drawing."}},{"id":"b103-v7-06","sequence":6,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-05"],"title":"制定勘察更新的決策紀錄","titleEn":"Create an investigation-update decision record","objective":"讓新地質證據影響後續模型。","objectiveEn":"Make new geological evidence propagate into downstream models.","instruction":"1. 設定一個與預測不同的假想觀察；2. 列出受影響的支護、物流與防水問題；3. 標記哪些結論需重做而哪些仍有效。","instructionEn":"1. Introduce a hypothetical observation inconsistent with prediction; 2. list affected support, logistics and waterproofing questions; 3. mark conclusions needing revision and those still valid.","observation":"新證據的價值在修正相依判斷，不能只新增一張地質照片。","observationEn":"New evidence should revise dependent judgments rather than merely add a geological photograph.","failure":"把差異記錄存檔後即可繼續沿用全部舊假設。","failureEn":"Filing a discrepancy permits all old assumptions to remain unchanged.","check":"繳交一份有上游證據及下游影響的變更單。","checkEn":"Provide a change record linking upstream evidence to downstream impacts.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-06-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"觀測與決策之間需要明確連結，否則資料很多也無法降低模型風險。","textEn":"Observations need explicit links to decisions; more data alone do not reduce modeling risk."},{"id":"b103-v7-06-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"未知條件可導致暫停判斷與補資料，這是工程品質控制的一部分。","textEn":"Unknown conditions can require pausing a judgment and gathering evidence as part of quality control."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「制定勘察更新的決策紀錄」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create an investigation-update decision record”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把差異記錄存檔後即可繼續沿用全部舊假設。","地質模型一旦發布就不應因新觀察而修改。","新證據的價值在修正相依判斷，不能只新增一張地質照片。"],"optionsEn":["Filing a discrepancy permits all old assumptions to remain unchanged.","A published geological model should never change after new observations.","New evidence should revise dependent judgments rather than merely add a geological photograph."],"answer":2,"explanation":"觀測與決策之間需要明確連結，否則資料很多也無法降低模型風險。 未知條件可導致暫停判斷與補資料，這是工程品質控制的一部分。","explanationEn":"Observations need explicit links to decisions; more data alone do not reduce modeling risk. Unknown conditions can require pausing a judgment and gathering evidence as part of quality control."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage02","order":2,"title":"開挖狀態與施工物流","titleEn":"Excavation states and logistics","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「開挖狀態與施工物流」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on excavation states and logistics, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-07","sequence":7,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-06"],"title":"比較機械掘進與分部開挖概念","titleEn":"Compare mechanized and staged excavation concepts","objective":"理解工法選擇取決於地質、斷面與物流。","objectiveEn":"Understand that methods depend on ground, geometry and logistics.","instruction":"1. 畫機械掘進與分部開挖的概念狀態；2. 比較斷面自由度、設備空間及出碴介面；3. 列出不能從照片推定的條件。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch mechanized and staged excavation concepts; 2. compare geometric flexibility, equipment space and muck interfaces; 3. list conditions that photographs cannot establish.","observation":"設備外觀相似不代表不同地質區段可沿用同一作業設定。","observationEn":"Similar equipment appearance does not justify identical settings in different ground.","failure":"只要使用最大掘進機就能解決所有地質問題。","failureEn":"The largest tunnel-boring machine solves every geological problem.","check":"提交三個工法比較維度與各自資料缺口。","checkEn":"Submit three method-comparison dimensions with evidence gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-07-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"施工方法是系統選擇，需要處理掌子面、支護、設備與物流的相容性。","textEn":"An excavation method is a system choice involving compatibility among face, support, equipment and logistics."},{"id":"b103-v7-07-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程不提供爆破參數或掘進機操作值，只比較公開工法機理。","textEn":"The course provides no blasting parameters or machine settings and compares only public method concepts."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較機械掘進與分部開挖概念」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare mechanized and staged excavation concepts”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["設備外觀相似不代表不同地質區段可沿用同一作業設定。","只要使用最大掘進機就能解決所有地質問題。","施工方法只取決於隧道的總長度。"],"optionsEn":["Similar equipment appearance does not justify identical settings in different ground.","The largest tunnel-boring machine solves every geological problem.","Excavation method depends only on total tunnel length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工方法是系統選擇，需要處理掌子面、支護、設備與物流的相容性。 本課程不提供爆破參數或掘進機操作值，只比較公開工法機理。","explanationEn":"An excavation method is a system choice involving compatibility among face, support, equipment and logistics. The course provides no blasting parameters or machine settings and compares only public method concepts."}},{"id":"b103-v7-08","sequence":8,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-07"],"title":"分辨開挖面與後方工作區","titleEn":"Separate the face from trailing work zones","objective":"把掘進視為串接工序而非單一刀盤。","objectiveEn":"Treat tunnelling as a connected process rather than one cutterhead.","instruction":"1. 畫掌子面、支護及後方輸送三區；2. 標示人、材料與碴料的不同流線；3. 找出一個可能阻塞其他區的介面。","instructionEn":"1. Draw face, support and trailing-conveyor zones; 2. separate people, material and muck flows; 3. identify an interface that can block other zones.","observation":"前端掘進加快若超過後端能力，整體進度未必提高。","observationEn":"Faster advance need not improve progress when downstream capacity is insufficient.","failure":"只提高刀盤理論效率就可保證全隧道工期等比例縮短。","failureEn":"Higher theoretical cutterhead efficiency guarantees proportional schedule reduction.","check":"提交三區流線圖及一個瓶頸說明。","checkEn":"Provide a three-zone flow map and one bottleneck explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-08-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"串联系統的能力受限制環節影響，停機與交界等待不能在總體模型中省略。","textEn":"A serial system is constrained by limiting stages; downtime and interface waits matter to the overall model."},{"id":"b103-v7-08-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"教學流線只顯示相依關係，不是現地通行或施工配置圖。","textEn":"The teaching flow map shows dependencies, not a field traffic or construction layout."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分辨開挖面與後方工作區」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate the face from trailing work zones”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只提高刀盤理論效率就可保證全隧道工期等比例縮短。","前端掘進加快若超過後端能力，整體進度未必提高。","後方輸送能力不會限制前端掘進的總產出。"],"optionsEn":["Higher theoretical cutterhead efficiency guarantees proportional schedule reduction.","Faster advance need not improve progress when downstream capacity is insufficient.","Trailing transport capacity cannot limit overall advance output."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串联系統的能力受限制環節影響，停機與交界等待不能在總體模型中省略。 教學流線只顯示相依關係，不是現地通行或施工配置圖。","explanationEn":"A serial system is constrained by limiting stages; downtime and interface waits matter to the overall model. The teaching flow map shows dependencies, not a field traffic or construction layout."}},{"id":"b103-v7-09","sequence":9,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-08"],"title":"拆出臨時支護與永久襯砌","titleEn":"Separate temporary support and final lining","objective":"辨認不同時間狀態下的承載機理。","objectiveEn":"Recognize load-resistance mechanisms at different times.","instruction":"1. 畫剛開挖、初期支護及完成襯砌三狀態；2. 記錄各狀態已存在的構件；3. 比較岩體與結構的相互作用假設。","instructionEn":"1. Draw freshly excavated, initially supported and finally lined states; 2. list components present in each; 3. compare ground–structure interaction assumptions.","observation":"永久襯砌的存在不能回頭證明未完成階段的穩定性。","observationEn":"A final lining does not retrospectively verify stability before its completion.","failure":"將完工襯砌放入所有施工狀態即可簡化而不影響判斷。","failureEn":"Adding the completed lining to every construction state simplifies analysis without consequence.","check":"提交三狀態構件與反力表。","checkEn":"Submit a table of components and reactions for three states.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-09-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地下結構與岩體共同變形；支護安裝時機及邊界是模型的一部分。","textEn":"Underground structures and ground deform together; installation timing and boundaries are part of the model."},{"id":"b103-v7-09-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"概念狀態分析不能直接決定現場支護間距或施工時序。","textEn":"Conceptual state analysis cannot directly determine field support spacing or work sequence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆出臨時支護與永久襯砌」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate temporary support and final lining”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["將完工襯砌放入所有施工狀態即可簡化而不影響判斷。","臨時支護的安裝時間不會改變岩體與結構互動。","永久襯砌的存在不能回頭證明未完成階段的穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Adding the completed lining to every construction state simplifies analysis without consequence.","Temporary-support timing does not affect ground–structure interaction.","A final lining does not retrospectively verify stability before its completion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地下結構與岩體共同變形；支護安裝時機及邊界是模型的一部分。 概念狀態分析不能直接決定現場支護間距或施工時序。","explanationEn":"Underground structures and ground deform together; installation timing and boundaries are part of the model. Conceptual state analysis cannot directly determine field support spacing or work sequence."}},{"id":"b103-v7-10","sequence":10,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-09"],"title":"讀取收斂量測的時間曲線","titleEn":"Interpret convergence time histories","objective":"區分變形速率、總量與量測重置。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish deformation rate, total movement and datum resets.","instruction":"1. 建立三條自設收斂曲線；2. 分別加入趨穩、加速與基準跳點；3. 對每條列出下一個應查證的資料。","instructionEn":"1. Create three synthetic convergence curves; 2. include stabilization, acceleration and a datum jump; 3. specify the next evidence check for each.","observation":"曲線跳點可能來自量測基準變更，需先查紀錄再判斷岩體突變。","observationEn":"A curve jump can result from a datum change and requires record checks before inferring abrupt ground behavior.","failure":"量測跳點必然表示隧道立即發生同等變形。","failureEn":"Every measurement jump necessarily indicates equal immediate tunnel movement.","check":"繳交三曲線的候選解釋及查證表。","checkEn":"Provide candidate explanations and checks for three curves.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-10-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"變形量及其時間趨勢傳達不同資訊；單一讀數缺少速率與背景。","textEn":"Movement magnitude and time trend convey different information; one reading lacks rate and context."},{"id":"b103-v7-10-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"所有警戒值在本練習都保持未指定，不以自設曲線設定真實工地限值。","textEn":"Alert thresholds remain unspecified; synthetic curves do not establish real construction limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「讀取收斂量測的時間曲線」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret convergence time histories”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["曲線跳點可能來自量測基準變更，需先查紀錄再判斷岩體突變。","量測跳點必然表示隧道立即發生同等變形。","變形總量相同就表示各曲線的速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["A curve jump can result from a datum change and requires record checks before inferring abrupt ground behavior.","Every measurement jump necessarily indicates equal immediate tunnel movement.","Equal total movement implies equal rates in every curve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"變形量及其時間趨勢傳達不同資訊；單一讀數缺少速率與背景。 所有警戒值在本練習都保持未指定，不以自設曲線設定真實工地限值。","explanationEn":"Movement magnitude and time trend convey different information; one reading lacks rate and context. Alert thresholds remain unspecified; synthetic curves do not establish real construction limits."}},{"id":"b103-v7-11","sequence":11,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-10"],"title":"建立出碴與材料再利用帳","titleEn":"Create a muck and reuse ledger","objective":"追蹤材料品質、去向與物流守恆。","objectiveEn":"Track material quality, destination and logistics conservation.","instruction":"1. 對自設碴料批次建立重量欄；2. 依待檢、可用、不可用分流；3. 核對庫存變化與運出入是否平衡。","instructionEn":"1. Assign masses to hypothetical muck batches; 2. separate pending, suitable and unsuitable streams; 3. reconcile inventory with inflows and outflows.","observation":"材料數量平衡成立仍不代表每批都適合再利用。","observationEn":"A balanced material ledger does not establish suitability of every batch for reuse.","failure":"所有挖出的岩石都能直接當成同等級混凝土骨材。","failureEn":"Every excavated rock batch can directly serve as equivalent concrete aggregate.","check":"輸出有品質狀態及去向的批次守恆表。","checkEn":"Produce a batch balance with quality status and destinations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-11-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"材料再利用需要性質與污染等證據，不能僅依岩石外觀決定用途。","textEn":"Reuse requires property and contamination evidence rather than appearance alone."},{"id":"b103-v7-11-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"庫存、運輸與品質結果是不同資料流，需要共同批次識別碼才能追溯。","textEn":"Inventory, transport and quality results require common batch identifiers for traceability."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立出碴與材料再利用帳」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a muck and reuse ledger”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有挖出的岩石都能直接當成同等級混凝土骨材。","材料數量平衡成立仍不代表每批都適合再利用。","出碴重量相同就代表所有批次具有相同材料品質。"],"optionsEn":["Every excavated rock batch can directly serve as equivalent concrete aggregate.","A balanced material ledger does not establish suitability of every batch for reuse.","Equal muck masses establish identical quality in every batch."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料再利用需要性質與污染等證據，不能僅依岩石外觀決定用途。 庫存、運輸與品質結果是不同資料流，需要共同批次識別碼才能追溯。","explanationEn":"Reuse requires property and contamination evidence rather than appearance alone. Inventory, transport and quality results require common batch identifiers for traceability."}},{"id":"b103-v7-12","sequence":12,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-11"],"title":"協調多工作面的共同介面","titleEn":"Coordinate multiple work fronts","objective":"理解平行開挖如何共享基準與資源。","objectiveEn":"Understand shared datums and resources in parallel drives.","instruction":"1. 畫兩個假想工作面與共同出入口；2. 設定共用運輸及測量介面；3. 模擬其中一區延後時的相依影響。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two hypothetical faces and a shared access; 2. define shared transport and survey interfaces; 3. trace consequences when one area is delayed.","observation":"增加工作面會增加並行能力，也可能增加共用資源衝突。","observationEn":"Additional faces increase parallel opportunities but can create shared-resource conflicts.","failure":"工作面數量加倍就一定使完工時間減半。","failureEn":"Doubling work fronts necessarily halves completion time.","check":"提交資源與基準的兩類相依圖。","checkEn":"Provide separate dependency maps for resources and datums.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-12-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"平行任務需共享可靠的幾何基準，否則速度提升可能累積到貫通誤差。","textEn":"Parallel tasks need reliable shared geometry or faster progress can accumulate breakthrough mismatch."},{"id":"b103-v7-12-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"施工組織比較需考慮資源限制及介面等待，不能只加總理論掘進率。","textEn":"Construction organization must consider resource limits and interface waits, not only theoretical advance rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「協調多工作面的共同介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Coordinate multiple work fronts”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["工作面數量加倍就一定使完工時間減半。","平行工作面不需共同測量基準，只需各自前進。","增加工作面會增加並行能力，也可能增加共用資源衝突。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling work fronts necessarily halves completion time.","Parallel work fronts need no shared survey datum, only local advance.","Additional faces increase parallel opportunities but can create shared-resource conflicts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行任務需共享可靠的幾何基準，否則速度提升可能累積到貫通誤差。 施工組織比較需考慮資源限制及介面等待，不能只加總理論掘進率。","explanationEn":"Parallel tasks need reliable shared geometry or faster progress can accumulate breakthrough mismatch. Construction organization must consider resource limits and interface waits, not only theoretical advance rates."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage03","order":3,"title":"襯砌、防水與鐵路介面","titleEn":"Lining, waterproofing and railway interfaces","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「襯砌、防水與鐵路介面」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on lining, waterproofing and railway interfaces, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-13","sequence":13,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-12"],"title":"檢查雙向貫通的誤差鏈","titleEn":"Review breakthrough error chains","objective":"理解方向、距離與座標基準的累積。","objectiveEn":"Understand accumulation of direction, distance and reference errors.","instruction":"1. 畫兩端向中間延伸的測線；2. 加入小幅自設角度及距離偏差；3. 比較閉合差並註明同一座標基準。","instructionEn":"1. Draw survey chains advancing from opposite ends; 2. introduce small hypothetical angle and distance errors; 3. compare closure under one reference frame.","observation":"很小的方向偏差沿長距離延伸可能形成明顯橫向閉合差。","observationEn":"A small directional error over a long distance can create substantial lateral closure error.","failure":"只要每段距離量得精確就可忽略方向與座標轉換。","failureEn":"Accurate segment distances make direction and coordinate transformations irrelevant.","check":"輸出兩條誤差鏈及一份閉合差來源表。","checkEn":"Provide two error chains and a closure-error source table.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-13-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"測量誤差可含系統性與隨機部分，方向偏差不能用距離精度掩蓋。","textEn":"Survey errors include systematic and random components; distance precision does not hide direction bias."},{"id":"b103-v7-13-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"公開地圖座標不是隧道貫通測量基準，本步使用自設平面座標。","textEn":"Public map coordinates are not tunnel breakthrough control; this exercise uses an invented planar frame."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檢查雙向貫通的誤差鏈」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review breakthrough error chains”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["很小的方向偏差沿長距離延伸可能形成明顯橫向閉合差。","只要每段距離量得精確就可忽略方向與座標轉換。","測線方向偏差只影響起點，不會隨距離累積。"],"optionsEn":["A small directional error over a long distance can create substantial lateral closure error.","Accurate segment distances make direction and coordinate transformations irrelevant.","Survey-direction bias affects only the starting point and cannot accumulate with distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"測量誤差可含系統性與隨機部分，方向偏差不能用距離精度掩蓋。 公開地圖座標不是隧道貫通測量基準，本步使用自設平面座標。","explanationEn":"Survey errors include systematic and random components; distance precision does not hide direction bias. Public map coordinates are not tunnel breakthrough control; this exercise uses an invented planar frame."}},{"id":"b103-v7-14","sequence":14,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-13"],"title":"分開滲水來源與排水去向","titleEn":"Separate seepage sources and drainage destinations","objective":"建立水路與結構邊界的概念模型。","objectiveEn":"Build a conceptual model of water paths and structural boundaries.","instruction":"1. 畫岩體、支護、防水層及內襯；2. 用箭頭標示假想滲水；3. 分列清水、可能污染水與未知來源。","instructionEn":"1. Draw ground, support, waterproofing and inner lining; 2. mark hypothetical seepage; 3. separate clean, potentially contaminated and unknown sources.","observation":"不同來源的水應先辨識，不能直接假設具有相同排放條件。","observationEn":"Water sources need identification before assuming identical discharge conditions.","failure":"水都是透明就能合併成同一條無需檢測的排水線。","failureEn":"All clear-looking water can share one untested discharge route.","check":"提交標示未知水源及去向的水路圖。","checkEn":"Submit a water-path diagram with unknown sources and destinations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-14-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地下水、施工用水與污染事件可能需要不同處理，外觀不足以判定品質。","textEn":"Groundwater, process water and contamination events can require different treatment; appearance is insufficient."},{"id":"b103-v7-14-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"防水與排水需協調，堵住可見水路不一定解決上游壓力問題。","textEn":"Waterproofing and drainage must be coordinated; blocking visible flow does not necessarily address upstream pressure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開滲水來源與排水去向」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate seepage sources and drainage destinations”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["水都是透明就能合併成同一條無需檢測的排水線。","不同來源的水應先辨識，不能直接假設具有相同排放條件。","封住可見漏水就能保證上游水壓也消失。"],"optionsEn":["All clear-looking water can share one untested discharge route.","Water sources need identification before assuming identical discharge conditions.","Blocking visible leakage guarantees upstream water pressure disappears."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地下水、施工用水與污染事件可能需要不同處理，外觀不足以判定品質。 防水與排水需協調，堵住可見水路不一定解決上游壓力問題。","explanationEn":"Groundwater, process water and contamination events can require different treatment; appearance is insufficient. Waterproofing and drainage must be coordinated; blocking visible flow does not necessarily address upstream pressure."}},{"id":"b103-v7-15","sequence":15,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-14"],"title":"核對襯砌接縫與連通口","titleEn":"Check lining joints and connection openings","objective":"把局部細節視為連續系統的弱點候選。","objectiveEn":"Treat local details as potential discontinuities in a continuous system.","instruction":"1. 畫襯砌、接縫與橫坑開口；2. 標記水、力及電纜三種跨界路徑；3. 列出各自需保留的施工與檢查紀錄。","instructionEn":"1. Draw lining, joints and a cross-passage opening; 2. mark water, force and cable crossings; 3. list installation and inspection records for each.","observation":"連續壁面模型不能自動代表接縫與穿透部位的行為。","observationEn":"A continuous-wall model does not automatically represent joints and penetrations.","failure":"大部分襯砌沒有滲水就能證明每個接縫都具有相同品質。","failureEn":"A mostly dry lining proves identical quality at every joint.","check":"輸出至少三種跨界介面的證據清單。","checkEn":"Provide evidence lists for at least three crossing interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-15-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"幾何不連續會改變局部變形、水路及應力分布，因此需要具體細節資料。","textEn":"Geometric discontinuities change local deformation, flow and stresses and require detail-specific evidence."},{"id":"b103-v7-15-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"照片與示意圖有助於定位，但不能代替隱蔽工程及材料紀錄。","textEn":"Photos and schematics locate details but do not replace concealed-work and material records."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「核對襯砌接縫與連通口」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Check lining joints and connection openings”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["大部分襯砌沒有滲水就能證明每個接縫都具有相同品質。","整段襯砌看似連續即可刪除接縫與開口模型。","連續壁面模型不能自動代表接縫與穿透部位的行為。"],"optionsEn":["A mostly dry lining proves identical quality at every joint.","An apparently continuous lining permits deletion of joint and opening models.","A continuous-wall model does not automatically represent joints and penetrations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何不連續會改變局部變形、水路及應力分布，因此需要具體細節資料。 照片與示意圖有助於定位，但不能代替隱蔽工程及材料紀錄。","explanationEn":"Geometric discontinuities change local deformation, flow and stresses and require detail-specific evidence. Photos and schematics locate details but do not replace concealed-work and material records."}},{"id":"b103-v7-16","sequence":16,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-15"],"title":"把軌道幾何連到結構空間","titleEn":"Connect track geometry to structural space","objective":"辨識行車界限、軌道基準與維修空間。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish vehicle clearance, track datums and maintenance space.","instruction":"1. 在隧道斷面畫概念軌道及車輛包絡；2. 另畫架空線與走道；3. 比較軌道偏移對各介面空間的影響。","instructionEn":"1. Draw conceptual track and vehicle envelopes; 2. add overhead equipment and walkways; 3. compare effects of track offsets on interface space.","observation":"隧道淨空合適仍需核對軌道位置與設備包絡的共同條件。","observationEn":"Adequate tunnel size still requires compatible track position and equipment envelopes.","failure":"土建斷面容得下車體就代表全部鐵路設備都可直接安裝。","failureEn":"A civil section containing the vehicle body guarantees fit for all railway equipment.","check":"提供三種包絡及共同基準的斷面圖。","checkEn":"Provide a section with three envelopes and a common datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-16-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"土建及鐵路設備使用同一幾何空間，但各自有安裝、運動與維護需求。","textEn":"Civil works and railway equipment share space but have distinct installation, movement and maintenance needs."},{"id":"b103-v7-16-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步包絡為教學自繪，不提供真實鐵路通行或設備淨空批准值。","textEn":"Teaching envelopes are original sketches, not approved railway or equipment-clearance values."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把軌道幾何連到結構空間」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Connect track geometry to structural space”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["隧道淨空合適仍需核對軌道位置與設備包絡的共同條件。","土建斷面容得下車體就代表全部鐵路設備都可直接安裝。","車輛包絡與設備維修包絡永遠相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate tunnel size still requires compatible track position and equipment envelopes.","A civil section containing the vehicle body guarantees fit for all railway equipment.","Vehicle and equipment-maintenance envelopes are always identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"土建及鐵路設備使用同一幾何空間，但各自有安裝、運動與維護需求。 本步包絡為教學自繪，不提供真實鐵路通行或設備淨空批准值。","explanationEn":"Civil works and railway equipment share space but have distinct installation, movement and maintenance needs. Teaching envelopes are original sketches, not approved railway or equipment-clearance values."}},{"id":"b103-v7-17","sequence":17,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-16"],"title":"區分供電、通訊與控制介面","titleEn":"Separate power, communications and control","objective":"理解鐵路營運是多系統整合。","objectiveEn":"Understand railway operation as multisystem integration.","instruction":"1. 畫供電、通訊與列車控制三條功能鏈；2. 標示資訊及能源流向；3. 列出中斷任一鏈時需要查證的狀態。","instructionEn":"1. Draw power, communications and train-control chains; 2. distinguish information and energy flows; 3. list states needing verification if one chain is interrupted.","observation":"通訊連通並不單獨證明電力或列車控制功能可用。","observationEn":"Communication connectivity alone does not establish power or train-control availability.","failure":"所有設備都回應網路訊息就可判定隧道已具備行車條件。","failureEn":"Network responses from every device establish train-operating readiness.","check":"提交三條功能鏈及至少三個交界問題。","checkEn":"Submit three functional chains and at least three interface questions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-17-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"子系統可用與系統整合可用是不同層級，必須對應到服務功能。","textEn":"Subsystem availability and integrated readiness are different levels and must map to service functions."},{"id":"b103-v7-17-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程只討論功能邊界，不提供真實列車控制配置或現地操作指令。","textEn":"The course discusses functional boundaries, not actual train-control configurations or field commands."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分供電、通訊與控制介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate power, communications and control”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有設備都回應網路訊息就可判定隧道已具備行車條件。","通訊連通並不單獨證明電力或列車控制功能可用。","能源流與資訊流可用同一條線不加區分地驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Network responses from every device establish train-operating readiness.","Communication connectivity alone does not establish power or train-control availability.","Energy and information flows can be verified as one indistinguishable line."],"answer":1,"explanation":"子系統可用與系統整合可用是不同層級，必須對應到服務功能。 課程只討論功能邊界，不提供真實列車控制配置或現地操作指令。","explanationEn":"Subsystem availability and integrated readiness are different levels and must map to service functions. The course discusses functional boundaries, not actual train-control configurations or field commands."}},{"id":"b103-v7-18","sequence":18,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-17"],"title":"建立土建移交的證據索引","titleEn":"Create a civil-to-systems handover index","objective":"防止已完工與已適合安裝的概念混淆。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating construction completion with installation readiness.","instruction":"1. 列出斷面、滲水、基準及預留介面；2. 為每項配一種紀錄與版本；3. 標記尚未解決、會阻礙設備安裝的缺項。","instructionEn":"1. List geometry, seepage, datums and reserved interfaces; 2. assign a record and version to each; 3. flag unresolved items preventing installation readiness.","observation":"土建完成日期不是每個機電介面已驗證的替代證據。","observationEn":"A civil completion date does not substitute for verified service interfaces.","failure":"開挖貫通就表示所有後續安裝與營運驗證都已完成。","failureEn":"Breakthrough means all installation and operational verification are complete.","check":"繳交可追到位置及版本的移交索引。","checkEn":"Submit a handover index traceable to location and version.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-18-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"移交將幾何、品質及限制資訊交給下一專業，是功能整合的一部分。","textEn":"Handover transfers geometry, quality and limitations to the next discipline as part of functional integration."},{"id":"b103-v7-18-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"證據應明確標示驗證範圍，不能把一段合格延伸為全線合格。","textEn":"Evidence must state verified scope rather than extend one accepted section to the whole route."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立土建移交的證據索引」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a civil-to-systems handover index”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["開挖貫通就表示所有後續安裝與營運驗證都已完成。","移交只需要完成日期，不需要資料位置與版本。","土建完成日期不是每個機電介面已驗證的替代證據。"],"optionsEn":["Breakthrough means all installation and operational verification are complete.","Handover needs only a completion date, not data location and version.","A civil completion date does not substitute for verified service interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移交將幾何、品質及限制資訊交給下一專業，是功能整合的一部分。 證據應明確標示驗證範圍，不能把一段合格延伸為全線合格。","explanationEn":"Handover transfers geometry, quality and limitations to the next discipline as part of functional integration. Evidence must state verified scope rather than extend one accepted section to the whole route."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage04","order":4,"title":"系統驗證與衍生工程","titleEn":"System verification and related projects","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「系統驗證與衍生工程」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on system verification and related projects, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-19","sequence":19,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-18"],"title":"分開局部試驗與整合試驗","titleEn":"Separate local and integrated tests","objective":"建立從設備功能到服務功能的證據鏈。","objectiveEn":"Build an evidence chain from device function to service function.","instruction":"1. 為一個概念通訊節點列出局部測試；2. 加入跨區端到端情境；3. 標記局部通過仍無法回答的整體問題。","instructionEn":"1. Define a local test for a conceptual communication node; 2. add an end-to-end cross-zone scenario; 3. identify system questions not answered by local success.","observation":"各設備單獨通過並不保證跨系統的功能與時序相容。","observationEn":"Independent device passes do not establish compatible cross-system functions and timing.","failure":"把各廠商測試報告相加即可取代所有整合驗證。","failureEn":"Adding supplier reports replaces every integration test.","check":"提交要求、測試範圍及缺口三欄矩陣。","checkEn":"Provide a requirements, test-scope and gap matrix.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-19-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"整合驗證針對介面與共同情境，與單體功能試驗具有不同覆蓋範圍。","textEn":"Integration verification covers interfaces and shared scenarios distinct from standalone function tests."},{"id":"b103-v7-19-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設案例用於查漏，不宣稱重現哥達隧道的正式驗收程序。","textEn":"Synthetic cases expose gaps and do not reproduce Gotthard’s formal acceptance process."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開局部試驗與整合試驗」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate local and integrated tests”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["各設備單獨通過並不保證跨系統的功能與時序相容。","把各廠商測試報告相加即可取代所有整合驗證。","整合試驗只是單體試驗更換名稱，覆蓋範圍完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Independent device passes do not establish compatible cross-system functions and timing.","Adding supplier reports replaces every integration test.","Integration testing merely renames component testing with identical coverage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"整合驗證針對介面與共同情境，與單體功能試驗具有不同覆蓋範圍。 自設案例用於查漏，不宣稱重現哥達隧道的正式驗收程序。","explanationEn":"Integration verification covers interfaces and shared scenarios distinct from standalone function tests. Synthetic cases expose gaps and do not reproduce Gotthard’s formal acceptance process."}},{"id":"b103-v7-20","sequence":20,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-19"],"title":"用非操作方式檢查可達性","titleEn":"Review access without issuing operating instructions","objective":"辨識平面連通與實際可使用的差異。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish drawn connectivity from practical availability.","instruction":"1. 在雙管圖標出概念人員路徑；2. 另列門、照明及資訊需求；3. 以缺少一項資訊的例子說明不能直接判定可達。","instructionEn":"1. Mark conceptual pedestrian routes on the twin-tube diagram; 2. list door, lighting and information needs; 3. show why one missing item prevents an availability judgment.","observation":"圖上路徑連通仍需設備、資訊與狀態證據才能判斷可使用。","observationEn":"A connected path still requires equipment, information and state evidence before judging usability.","failure":"橫坑存在就自動代表任何情境下都可自由通行。","failureEn":"The existence of a cross-passage implies free passage in every scenario.","check":"提交功能需求清單，保留現地程序為未提供。","checkEn":"Submit functional requirements while leaving field procedures unspecified.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-20-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"可達性包含幾何與狀態；一條線無法表達門、環境及設備可用性。","textEn":"Access includes geometry and state; one line cannot represent doors, environment and equipment availability."},{"id":"b103-v7-20-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本練習不提供火災、疏散或列車事故處置程序，實務須遵循營運者指引。","textEn":"This exercise supplies no fire, evacuation or train-incident procedure; actual practice follows operator guidance."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用非操作方式檢查可達性」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review access without issuing operating instructions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["橫坑存在就自動代表任何情境下都可自由通行。","圖上路徑連通仍需設備、資訊與狀態證據才能判斷可使用。","一張平面圖可完整表達門的狀態、照明及設備可用性。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of a cross-passage implies free passage in every scenario.","A connected path still requires equipment, information and state evidence before judging usability.","One plan fully represents door states, lighting and equipment availability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可達性包含幾何與狀態；一條線無法表達門、環境及設備可用性。 本練習不提供火災、疏散或列車事故處置程序，實務須遵循營運者指引。","explanationEn":"Access includes geometry and state; one line cannot represent doors, environment and equipment availability. This exercise supplies no fire, evacuation or train-incident procedure; actual practice follows operator guidance."}},{"id":"b103-v7-21","sequence":21,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-20"],"title":"建立維護窗口的介面問題","titleEn":"Map maintenance-window interface questions","objective":"辨識單一設備維修與鐵路服務之間的依賴。","objectiveEn":"Identify dependencies between equipment maintenance and railway service.","instruction":"1. 選一個假想設備維護項；2. 標出共用供電、通訊及接近路徑；3. 區分設備完成、功能複核及服務恢復三種狀態。","instructionEn":"1. Select a hypothetical equipment-maintenance task; 2. mark shared power, communications and access paths; 3. distinguish task completion, functional recheck and service restoration.","observation":"維修工作結束與整個相關功能已恢復是不同的證據判斷。","observationEn":"Finishing a maintenance task and restoring the associated integrated function are different evidence judgments.","failure":"單一設備修好就能自行判定所有相關鐵路服務已恢復。","failureEn":"Repairing one device independently establishes that every related railway service has been restored.","check":"提交三種狀態及交界證據的相依圖。","checkEn":"Submit a dependency map of three states and interface evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-21-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"共享資源會使維護影響跨越單一設備邊界，因此應追蹤相關功能。","textEn":"Shared resources let maintenance effects cross device boundaries, so related functions must be traced."},{"id":"b103-v7-21-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程只建立工程問題，不指定封鎖、隔離、復電或列車營運程序。","textEn":"The exercise defines engineering questions and specifies no possession, isolation, reenergization or train-operating procedure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立維護窗口的介面問題」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map maintenance-window interface questions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["單一設備修好就能自行判定所有相關鐵路服務已恢復。","共用資源只影響被維護的設備，不會影響相鄰功能。","維修工作結束與整個相關功能已恢復是不同的證據判斷。"],"optionsEn":["Repairing one device independently establishes that every related railway service has been restored.","Shared resources affect only maintained equipment and never adjacent functions.","Finishing a maintenance task and restoring the associated integrated function are different evidence judgments."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共享資源會使維護影響跨越單一設備邊界，因此應追蹤相關功能。 課程只建立工程問題，不指定封鎖、隔離、復電或列車營運程序。","explanationEn":"Shared resources let maintenance effects cross device boundaries, so related functions must be traced. The exercise defines engineering questions and specifies no possession, isolation, reenergization or train-operating procedure."}},{"id":"b103-v7-22","sequence":22,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-21"],"title":"比較缺陷、環境與感測器異常","titleEn":"Compare defects, environment and sensor anomalies","objective":"為維護觀察保留多個候選解釋。","objectiveEn":"Retain multiple explanations for maintenance observations.","instruction":"1. 自設一段滲水及位移紀錄；2. 加入感測器維修與降雨時間；3. 分列可能關係、尚未證實關係及補測需求。","instructionEn":"1. Create synthetic seepage and movement records; 2. add sensor-service and rainfall times; 3. separate possible relations, unproven relations and further evidence.","observation":"同時發生的變化只能提出關聯假說，不能直接證明單一成因。","observationEn":"Coincident changes suggest a relationship but do not prove a single cause.","failure":"降雨後讀數改變便能排除所有設備與基準因素。","failureEn":"A post-rainfall change excludes every equipment and datum explanation.","check":"輸出至少三項候選原因的證據評分表。","checkEn":"Provide an evidence table for at least three candidate causes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-22-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"因果判讀需要時間、空間及獨立證據一致；單一相關不足以診斷。","textEn":"Causal interpretation needs consistent temporal, spatial and independent evidence; correlation alone is insufficient."},{"id":"b103-v7-22-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"維護資料的缺漏與感測器更換必須保留在時間軸上，避免假趨勢。","textEn":"Data gaps and sensor replacements belong on the timeline to avoid false trends."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較缺陷、環境與感測器異常」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare defects, environment and sensor anomalies”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["同時發生的變化只能提出關聯假說，不能直接證明單一成因。","降雨後讀數改變便能排除所有設備與基準因素。","兩條曲線同時變動足以證明其中一條必然造成另一條。"],"optionsEn":["Coincident changes suggest a relationship but do not prove a single cause.","A post-rainfall change excludes every equipment and datum explanation.","Simultaneous changes prove one curve necessarily causes the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"因果判讀需要時間、空間及獨立證據一致；單一相關不足以診斷。 維護資料的缺漏與感測器更換必須保留在時間軸上，避免假趨勢。","explanationEn":"Causal interpretation needs consistent temporal, spatial and independent evidence; correlation alone is insufficient. Data gaps and sensor replacements belong on the timeline to avoid false trends."}},{"id":"b103-v7-23","sequence":23,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-22"],"title":"比較海峽、山岳與都市隧道","titleEn":"Compare strait, mountain and urban tunnels","objective":"找出哥達、英法與雪山隧道可互學的問題。","objectiveEn":"Identify transferable questions among Gotthard, Channel and Hsuehshan tunnels.","instruction":"1. 查各隧道用途與場址；2. 比較水、地質、運輸及連通需求；3. 列出共同的證據管理方法與不可沿用的參數。","instructionEn":"1. Verify each tunnel’s use and setting; 2. compare water, geology, transport and connection requirements; 3. separate shared evidence methods from nontransferable parameters.","observation":"地質更新及介面追溯可互學，但鐵路與公路的營運需求不同。","observationEn":"Geological updating and interface traceability transfer, but rail and road operational requirements differ.","failure":"都是長隧道就可套用同一通風、斷面與行車模型。","failureEn":"All long tunnels can share the same ventilation, section and traffic model.","check":"提交三隧道的相似處與差異表。","checkEn":"Provide a three-tunnel similarity and difference table.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-23-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"工程比較要保持系統邊界清楚，不能把隧道長度當成唯一難度指標。","textEn":"Comparisons need clear system boundaries and cannot use length as the sole complexity measure."},{"id":"b103-v7-23-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"延伸研究應從各營運者與業主資料重新建模，而非將本課程假設直接複製。","textEn":"Related research should rebuild from operator and owner evidence rather than copy this course’s assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較海峽、山岳與都市隧道」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare strait, mountain and urban tunnels”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["都是長隧道就可套用同一通風、斷面與行車模型。","地質更新及介面追溯可互學，但鐵路與公路的營運需求不同。","公路與鐵路隧道可直接共用全部營運假設。"],"optionsEn":["All long tunnels can share the same ventilation, section and traffic model.","Geological updating and interface traceability transfer, but rail and road operational requirements differ.","Road and railway tunnels can directly reuse every operating assumption."],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程比較要保持系統邊界清楚，不能把隧道長度當成唯一難度指標。 延伸研究應從各營運者與業主資料重新建模，而非將本課程假設直接複製。","explanationEn":"Comparisons need clear system boundaries and cannot use length as the sole complexity measure. Related research should rebuild from operator and owner evidence rather than copy this course’s assumptions."}},{"id":"b103-v7-24","sequence":24,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-23"],"title":"交付隧道系統學習檔案","titleEn":"Deliver the tunnel-system learning dossier","objective":"把地質到鐵路服務串成可追溯鏈。","objectiveEn":"Connect geology to railway service through a traceable chain.","instruction":"1. 整合路線、地質、狀態及系統圖；2. 每個判讀連接來源與假設；3. 用一項地質變更重新追查下游影響。","instructionEn":"1. Integrate route, geology, state and system diagrams; 2. link each interpretation to sources and assumptions; 3. trace downstream impacts of one ground-model change.","observation":"可追溯檔案能指出證據改變後哪些結論需重驗。","observationEn":"A traceable dossier identifies conclusions requiring recheck after evidence changes.","failure":"所有課程步驟打勾就代表真實隧道具備營運安全認證。","failureEn":"Checking every lesson step certifies an actual tunnel’s operational safety.","check":"繳交四階段索引、未解問題與一次修訂演練。","checkEn":"Submit a four-stage index, unresolved questions and one revision exercise.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-24-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"隧道是地盤、結構、設備及營運共同組成的系統，驗證必須跨越專業邊界。","textEn":"A tunnel combines ground, structures, equipment and operations, so verification crosses disciplinary boundaries."},{"id":"b103-v7-24-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"學習完成表示已建立概念與證據組織，不表示具備現地挖掘或營運權限。","textEn":"Completion demonstrates conceptual and evidence organization, not permission for field excavation or operation."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「交付隧道系統學習檔案」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Deliver the tunnel-system learning dossier”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有課程步驟打勾就代表真實隧道具備營運安全認證。","新證據不應改變先前已完成的任何模型結論。","可追溯檔案能指出證據改變後哪些結論需重驗。"],"optionsEn":["Checking every lesson step certifies an actual tunnel’s operational safety.","New evidence should never change a previously completed model conclusion.","A traceable dossier identifies conclusions requiring recheck after evidence changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隧道是地盤、結構、設備及營運共同組成的系統，驗證必須跨越專業邊界。 學習完成表示已建立概念與證據組織，不表示具備現地挖掘或營運權限。","explanationEn":"A tunnel combines ground, structures, equipment and operations, so verification crosses disciplinary boundaries. Completion demonstrates conceptual and evidence organization, not permission for field excavation or operation."}}]},{"id":"b103-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「基線縱坡與牽引需求」與「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" and \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-01","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-24"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-01-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b103-v14-02","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1338.08 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1338.08 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1338.08 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1338.08 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b103-v14-03","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b103-v14-04","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b103-v14-05","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-05-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b103-v14-06","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b103-v14-07","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b103-v14-08","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":5},{"id":"b103-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-09","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-09-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b103-v14-10","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=224 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為246.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=224 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 246.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=224 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為246.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=224 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 246.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b103-v14-11","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b103-v14-12","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b103-v14-13","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-13-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b103-v14-14","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.52629 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.52629 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.52629 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.52629 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b103-v14-15","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b103-v14-16","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":6},{"id":"b103-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「掘進利用率與設備停時」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-17","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-17-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"b103-v14-18","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.6064 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.767 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6064 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.767 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.6064 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.767 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6064 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.767 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"b103-v14-19","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"b103-v14-20","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"b103-v14-21","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-21-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"b103-v14-22","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"b103-v14-23","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"b103-v14-24","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":7},{"id":"b103-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"b103-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0449248 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0449248 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0449248 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0449248 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"b103-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"b103-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"b103-v14-29","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「通風顯熱量」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ventilation sensible heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通風顯熱量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise. Equal volumetric flow at different density does not provide equal cooling. Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ventilation sensible heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通風顯熱量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ventilation sensible heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-29-k1","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal","text":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。","textEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" is correct?","options":["只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"b103-v14-30","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通風顯熱量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ventilation sensible heat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1671.52 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1671.52 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1671.52 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1671.52 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"b103-v14-31","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通風顯熱量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ventilation sensible heat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","failure":"注意干擾：停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"b103-v14-32","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通風顯熱量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ventilation sensible heat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。","textEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":8},{"id":"b103-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「列車壓力波與動壓量級」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-33","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-33-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":57},{"id":"b103-v14-34","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1280.66 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1280.66 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1280.66 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1280.66 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":58},{"id":"b103-v14-35","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":59},{"id":"b103-v14-36","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":60},{"id":"b103-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":61},{"id":"b103-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.7451 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.7451 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.7451 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.7451 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":62},{"id":"b103-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":63},{"id":"b103-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":64}],"order":9}],"curriculumVersion":7,"enrichmentVersion":14,"learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","v14Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["坡度阻力功率","Grade-resistance power"],["洞壁切向應力","Tangential wall stress"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["通風顯熱量","Ventilation sensible heat"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]]},"v14Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，再獨立計算「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」。原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate cover stress and wall redistribution, then independently calculate shared access and transport bottlenecks. Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"深覆土地應力、基線牽引與多工作面整合","focusEn":"Deep-cover stress, base-railway traction and multiple-heading integration"}},{"id":"b226","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor","v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"title":"巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘","titleEn":"Panama Canal expansion locks","summary":"透過 24 個概念工序認識三階船閘、節水池、滾動閘門、土建與控制介面，連結通航能力、淡水資源與維護證據。","summaryEn":"Use 24 conceptual steps to connect three-chamber locks, water-saving basins, rolling gates and civil-control interfaces with navigation, freshwater and maintenance evidence.","scope":"以公開一次資料為背景的原創工程判讀課程；每步在紙上或數位示意模型中完成。自設數值、構形與工序不得當成原工程的設計、施工、設備操作或驗收程序。","scopeEn":"Original engineering interpretation exercises grounded in public primary sources. Complete each step on paper or in a schematic digital model. Invented values, geometry and sequences are not the original project’s design, construction, operating or acceptance procedures.","diagram":{"type":"water","labels":["需求與場址","結構與介面","施工狀態","驗證與維護"],"labelsEn":["Requirements and site","Structures and interfaces","Construction states","Verification and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":64,"estimatedMinutes":1600,"stages":[{"id":"b226-stage01","order":1,"title":"通航需求與水量邊界","titleEn":"Navigation requirements and water balance","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「通航需求與水量邊界」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on navigation requirements and water balance, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v7-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出兩洋與湖泊的高程關係","titleEn":"Map ocean and lake level relationships","objective":"理解船閘如何連接不同水位。","objectiveEn":"Understand how locks connect different water levels.","instruction":"1. 畫海洋、閘室及加通湖三類區域；2. 用高程線區分水面；3. 將船移動路線與水移動路線分色。","instructionEn":"1. Draw ocean, lock chambers and Gatun Lake; 2. distinguish water levels with elevation lines; 3. separate vessel and water routes by color.","observation":"船的前進方向與水流方向不是必然相同。","observationEn":"Vessel direction and water-flow direction are not necessarily the same.","failure":"船閘是把海水連續向前推動船舶的單向水管。","failureEn":"A lock is a one-way pipe continuously pushing ships forward with seawater.","check":"提交含兩類路徑和水位基準的概念剖面。","checkEn":"Submit a conceptual section with two route types and a water-level datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-01-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"浮船的升降依靠所在水面的變化；閘室是調整水位的空間。","textEn":"A floating vessel rises or falls with its water surface; a lock chamber provides the changing-level space."},{"id":"b226-v7-01-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"水位圖描述功能概念，不是實際閘門開閉或通航程序。","textEn":"The level diagram explains function and is not an actual gate or transit procedure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「畫出兩洋與湖泊的高程關係」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map ocean and lake level relationships”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["船的前進方向與水流方向不是必然相同。","船閘是把海水連續向前推動船舶的單向水管。","船舶高度由閘門馬達直接托舉，不受閘室水面影響。"],"optionsEn":["Vessel direction and water-flow direction are not necessarily the same.","A lock is a one-way pipe continuously pushing ships forward with seawater.","Gate motors directly lift vessel elevation independently of chamber water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"浮船的升降依靠所在水面的變化；閘室是調整水位的空間。 水位圖描述功能概念，不是實際閘門開閉或通航程序。","explanationEn":"A floating vessel rises or falls with its water surface; a lock chamber provides the changing-level space. The level diagram explains function and is not an actual gate or transit procedure."}},{"id":"b226-v7-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-01"],"title":"比較原船閘與擴建船閘","titleEn":"Compare original and expanded locks","objective":"避免把兩代設備與尺寸混用。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mixing two generations of equipment and dimensions.","instruction":"1. 分別建立原閘與新閘資料卡；2. 標示人字閘門與滾動閘門；3. 記錄每個尺寸所描述的是閘室還是船舶。","instructionEn":"1. Create separate original-lock and expanded-lock records; 2. distinguish miter and rolling gates; 3. identify whether each dimension describes chamber or vessel.","observation":"閘室尺寸與可通航船舶限制不是完全相同的量。","observationEn":"Chamber dimensions and permitted vessel limits are not identical quantities.","failure":"把新閘室寬度直接當成任何情境下的允許船寬。","failureEn":"Treat new-chamber width as the permissible vessel beam in every circumstance.","check":"輸出含設備世代與資料邊界的比較表。","checkEn":"Provide a comparison with equipment generation and data boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-02-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"擴建工程增加新的通航設施；原閘與新閘採用不同閘門及水管理配置。","textEn":"The expansion added facilities with gate and water-management arrangements different from the original locks."},{"id":"b226-v7-02-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"船舶限制需額外考慮通航要求，不能只從土建空間推算。","textEn":"Vessel limits involve navigation requirements beyond the physical civil-work space."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較原船閘與擴建船閘」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare original and expanded locks”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把新閘室寬度直接當成任何情境下的允許船寬。","閘室尺寸與可通航船舶限制不是完全相同的量。","原運河人字門與新閘滾動門具有相同運動幾何。"],"optionsEn":["Treat new-chamber width as the permissible vessel beam in every circumstance.","Chamber dimensions and permitted vessel limits are not identical quantities.","Original miter gates and new rolling gates have identical movement geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擴建工程增加新的通航設施；原閘與新閘採用不同閘門及水管理配置。 船舶限制需額外考慮通航要求，不能只從土建空間推算。","explanationEn":"The expansion added facilities with gate and water-management arrangements different from the original locks. Vessel limits involve navigation requirements beyond the physical civil-work space."}},{"id":"b226-v7-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-02"],"title":"拆出三階閘室系統","titleEn":"Decompose the three-chamber system","objective":"辨識單一閘室與整組船閘的關係。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish one chamber from a complete lock flight.","instruction":"1. 串接三個概念閘室；2. 標出相鄰水位邊界；3. 列出每個邊界需協調的水力及設備資訊。","instructionEn":"1. Connect three conceptual chambers; 2. mark adjacent water-level boundaries; 3. list hydraulic and equipment information needed at each boundary.","observation":"一個閘室的狀態可能改變相鄰區的可用條件。","observationEn":"The state of one chamber can affect conditions available to neighboring sections.","failure":"三個閘室可以忽略共同邊界而各自獨立任意運作。","failureEn":"Three chambers can operate arbitrarily and independently without shared boundaries.","check":"繳交三室及四個邊界的系統圖。","checkEn":"Provide a three-chamber diagram with four boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-03-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"串聯系統共享水位與通航介面，局部功能成立不代表整組時序相容。","textEn":"Series systems share level and navigation interfaces; local function does not establish compatible system timing."},{"id":"b226-v7-03-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本圖只表達依賴關係，不給出真實操作順序或設定值。","textEn":"The diagram expresses dependencies without real operating sequences or settings."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆出三階閘室系統」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Decompose the three-chamber system”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["三個閘室可以忽略共同邊界而各自獨立任意運作。","相鄰閘室的水位邊界對彼此沒有影響。","一個閘室的狀態可能改變相鄰區的可用條件。"],"optionsEn":["Three chambers can operate arbitrarily and independently without shared boundaries.","Adjacent chamber-level boundaries have no mutual effect.","The state of one chamber can affect conditions available to neighboring sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"串聯系統共享水位與通航介面，局部功能成立不代表整組時序相容。 本圖只表達依賴關係，不給出真實操作順序或設定值。","explanationEn":"Series systems share level and navigation interfaces; local function does not establish compatible system timing. The diagram expresses dependencies without real operating sequences or settings."}},{"id":"b226-v7-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-03"],"title":"建立一個完整的水量邊界","titleEn":"Define a complete water-balance boundary","objective":"把閘室、節水池與外部水源放入守恆框架。","objectiveEn":"Place chambers, saving basins and external water in a conservation framework.","instruction":"1. 選定包住閘室與節水池的邊界；2. 列出進入、流出及儲水變化；3. 用自設體積核對平衡並標示未計入項。","instructionEn":"1. Enclose a chamber and its basins in a boundary; 2. list inflow, outflow and storage change; 3. reconcile invented volumes and identify omitted terms.","observation":"內部回用流量不應再次計為從湖泊新增取水。","observationEn":"Internal reuse should not be counted again as new withdrawal from the lake.","failure":"把每一段內部水流都加進外部耗水量。","failureEn":"Add every internal transfer to external water consumption.","check":"提交一次守恆計算與明確的系統邊界。","checkEn":"Submit one conservation calculation with an explicit system boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-04-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水量守恆取決於邊界定義，內部轉移在整體帳中應相互抵消。","textEn":"Water conservation depends on boundary definition; internal transfers cancel in the overall balance."},{"id":"b226-v7-04-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設例子不對應真實航次用水，實況還需水位及營運資料。","textEn":"The invented example is not real transit consumption, which requires level and operating data."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立一個完整的水量邊界」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Define a complete water-balance boundary”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["內部回用流量不應再次計為從湖泊新增取水。","把每一段內部水流都加進外部耗水量。","內部轉移與外部取水在任何邊界下都是同一項。"],"optionsEn":["Internal reuse should not be counted again as new withdrawal from the lake.","Add every internal transfer to external water consumption.","Internal transfer and external withdrawal are identical under every boundary definition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水量守恆取決於邊界定義，內部轉移在整體帳中應相互抵消。 自設例子不對應真實航次用水，實況還需水位及營運資料。","explanationEn":"Water conservation depends on boundary definition; internal transfers cancel in the overall balance. The invented example is not real transit consumption, which requires level and operating data."}},{"id":"b226-v7-05","sequence":5,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-04"],"title":"辨認節水比例的分母","titleEn":"Identify the denominator in a saving ratio","objective":"區分回用比例、耗水差異與總取水。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish reuse fraction, consumption difference and total withdrawal.","instruction":"1. 寫出原始取水及回用的假想數據；2. 用兩個不同分母計算百分比；3. 說明為何不能把百分比直接相加。","instructionEn":"1. Write hypothetical withdrawal and reuse values; 2. calculate percentages using two denominators; 3. explain why those percentages cannot simply be added.","observation":"節水百分比需要交代比較對象與分母才具有意義。","observationEn":"A saving percentage needs a comparison basis and denominator to be meaningful.","failure":"兩份資料都寫節水就可把百分比相加得到總效果。","failureEn":"Two reported saving percentages can be added to obtain total benefit.","check":"輸出每個百分比的公式、分母及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Provide a formula, denominator and scope for each percentage.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-05-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"回用同一水體與減少外部取水是相關但不相同的指標。","textEn":"Reusing water and reducing external withdrawal are related but distinct metrics."},{"id":"b226-v7-05-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方發表的回用性能應連同測試或設計背景閱讀，不能推成每次航行保證。","textEn":"Published reuse performance needs its design or test context and is not a guarantee for every transit."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認節水比例的分母」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Identify the denominator in a saving ratio”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["兩份資料都寫節水就可把百分比相加得到總效果。","節水百分比需要交代比較對象與分母才具有意義。","同樣百分比在不同分母下代表相同節水體積。"],"optionsEn":["Two reported saving percentages can be added to obtain total benefit.","A saving percentage needs a comparison basis and denominator to be meaningful.","The same percentage under different denominators means the same saved volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回用同一水體與減少外部取水是相關但不相同的指標。 官方發表的回用性能應連同測試或設計背景閱讀，不能推成每次航行保證。","explanationEn":"Reusing water and reducing external withdrawal are related but distinct metrics. Published reuse performance needs its design or test context and is not a guarantee for every transit."}},{"id":"b226-v7-06","sequence":6,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-05"],"title":"審查通航與水資源需求","titleEn":"Review navigation and water-resource needs","objective":"理解航運服務與流域其他用途的共同依賴。","objectiveEn":"Understand shared dependence of shipping and other watershed uses.","instruction":"1. 畫通航、居民用水及湖泊蓄水三個需求節點；2. 連到共同水源；3. 列出一項增加通航能力仍不能回答的資源問題。","instructionEn":"1. Draw navigation, public-water and storage demand nodes; 2. connect them to shared water; 3. identify a resource question increased navigation capacity cannot answer.","observation":"更大的船閘不能單獨保證任何乾旱條件下都有足夠淡水。","observationEn":"Larger locks alone cannot guarantee sufficient freshwater under every drought condition.","failure":"增加閘室尺寸會自動增加流域可用水量。","failureEn":"Increasing chamber size automatically increases available watershed water.","check":"繳交通航、儲水及供水需求矩陣。","checkEn":"Provide a navigation, storage and water-supply requirements matrix.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-06-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"工程容量與自然資源供給屬不同約束，兩者需在同一系統範圍下協調。","textEn":"Engineering capacity and natural supply are different constraints requiring coordination within one system boundary."},{"id":"b226-v7-06-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程不推定當前水位、通航限額或政策；這些需查最新營運公告。","textEn":"The course does not infer current levels, transit limits or policy, which require current operator notices."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「審查通航與水資源需求」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review navigation and water-resource needs”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["增加閘室尺寸會自動增加流域可用水量。","自然降雨與工程容量是可以互相替代的相同約束。","更大的船閘不能單獨保證任何乾旱條件下都有足夠淡水。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing chamber size automatically increases available watershed water.","Natural rainfall and engineering capacity are interchangeable constraints.","Larger locks alone cannot guarantee sufficient freshwater under every drought condition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工程容量與自然資源供給屬不同約束，兩者需在同一系統範圍下協調。 本課程不推定當前水位、通航限額或政策；這些需查最新營運公告。","explanationEn":"Engineering capacity and natural supply are different constraints requiring coordination within one system boundary. The course does not infer current levels, transit limits or policy, which require current operator notices."}}]},{"id":"b226-stage02","order":2,"title":"閘室土建與大型閘門","titleEn":"Lock civil works and large gates","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「閘室土建與大型閘門」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on lock civil works and large gates, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v7-07","sequence":7,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-06"],"title":"拆出開挖、地盤與閘室底板","titleEn":"Separate excavation, ground and lock floor","objective":"辨識擋土、地下水與承載的不同問題。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish retaining, groundwater and bearing questions.","instruction":"1. 畫概念基坑與閘室底板；2. 標出土水壓與結構自重方向；3. 分別列出地盤、地下水及結構證據需求。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a conceptual excavation and lock floor; 2. mark earth, water and self-weight directions; 3. list ground, groundwater and structural evidence separately.","observation":"水位改變會影響地下結構受力，不能只考慮上部船閘重量。","observationEn":"Water-level changes affect underground structural actions beyond the weight of the lock.","failure":"底板很厚就可以忽略地下水及地盤變形。","failureEn":"A thick floor slab makes groundwater and ground deformation irrelevant.","check":"提交一張含水壓及地盤反力的概念剖面。","checkEn":"Submit a conceptual section with water pressure and ground reactions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-07-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"基坑與完工閘室具有不同水位及支承狀態，應分開建模。","textEn":"Excavations and completed locks have different water levels and supports and require separate models."},{"id":"b226-v7-07-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步不提供降水、支撐或開挖方案，而是列出必須具備的設計證據。","textEn":"This step supplies no dewatering, support or excavation scheme; it identifies necessary design evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆出開挖、地盤與閘室底板」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate excavation, ground and lock floor”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["水位改變會影響地下結構受力，不能只考慮上部船閘重量。","底板很厚就可以忽略地下水及地盤變形。","基坑與完工閘室可以假定永遠具有同一水位與支承。"],"optionsEn":["Water-level changes affect underground structural actions beyond the weight of the lock.","A thick floor slab makes groundwater and ground deformation irrelevant.","Excavations and completed locks can always share identical levels and support conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基坑與完工閘室具有不同水位及支承狀態，應分開建模。 本步不提供降水、支撐或開挖方案，而是列出必須具備的設計證據。","explanationEn":"Excavations and completed locks have different water levels and supports and require separate models. This step supplies no dewatering, support or excavation scheme; it identifies necessary design evidence."}},{"id":"b226-v7-08","sequence":8,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-07"],"title":"理解大體積混凝土的溫度歷程","titleEn":"Understand mass-concrete temperature history","objective":"將材料強度與溫度變形分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate material strength from thermal deformation.","instruction":"1. 畫一塊概念厚牆的中心與表面；2. 自設兩條溫度曲線；3. 比較溫差、約束與裂縫風險之間的關係。","instructionEn":"1. Draw the core and surface of a conceptual thick wall; 2. create two temperature histories; 3. relate temperature difference, restraint and cracking risk.","observation":"強度資料合格不會自動消除受約束溫度變形的問題。","observationEn":"Acceptable strength data do not automatically eliminate restrained thermal-deformation issues.","failure":"混凝土越厚就一定越不需考慮內外溫差。","failureEn":"Thicker concrete necessarily needs less consideration of internal temperature differences.","check":"輸出溫度歷程與約束位置的配對圖。","checkEn":"Provide paired temperature histories and restraint locations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-08-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水化產熱、散熱及約束會共同影響溫度應力，不能只看單點最高溫。","textEn":"Hydration heat, cooling and restraint jointly influence thermal stress, beyond one peak temperature."},{"id":"b226-v7-08-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程的溫度曲線是教學自設，不提供實際混凝土配比或養護設定。","textEn":"Teaching temperature curves provide no actual mix design or curing settings."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「理解大體積混凝土的溫度歷程」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Understand mass-concrete temperature history”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["混凝土越厚就一定越不需考慮內外溫差。","強度資料合格不會自動消除受約束溫度變形的問題。","只記最高溫度就能完整描述受約束溫度應力。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker concrete necessarily needs less consideration of internal temperature differences.","Acceptable strength data do not automatically eliminate restrained thermal-deformation issues.","One maximum temperature completely describes restrained thermal stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水化產熱、散熱及約束會共同影響溫度應力，不能只看單點最高溫。 課程的溫度曲線是教學自設，不提供實際混凝土配比或養護設定。","explanationEn":"Hydration heat, cooling and restraint jointly influence thermal stress, beyond one peak temperature. Teaching temperature curves provide no actual mix design or curing settings."}},{"id":"b226-v7-09","sequence":9,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-08"],"title":"核對施工縫與止水介面","titleEn":"Review joints and waterstops","objective":"理解連續防水依賴局部接合品質。","objectiveEn":"Understand how continuous water control depends on local joints.","instruction":"1. 畫底板、牆及一條概念施工縫；2. 標出水的可能穿越路徑；3. 建立位置、材料及隱蔽檢查的追溯表。","instructionEn":"1. Draw floor, wall and a conceptual construction joint; 2. mark possible water crossings; 3. create a location, material and concealed-inspection record.","observation":"大面積混凝土完整不等於每一條接縫都已驗證水密。","observationEn":"Intact bulk concrete does not establish watertightness at every joint.","failure":"表面無裂痕就能證明所有隱蔽止水構件正確安裝。","failureEn":"A crack-free surface proves correct installation of all concealed waterstops.","check":"提交至少三類接縫證據與各自限制。","checkEn":"Provide at least three joint-evidence types with their limitations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-09-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"防水介面是連續路徑問題，局部缺口可能主導整體滲漏。","textEn":"Water control is a continuity problem in which a local gap can dominate leakage."},{"id":"b226-v7-09-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"照片可協助追溯位置，但材料識別與施工紀錄仍需各自保留。","textEn":"Photos help trace locations, while material identification and installation records remain separate needs."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「核對施工縫與止水介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review joints and waterstops”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["表面無裂痕就能證明所有隱蔽止水構件正確安裝。","隱蔽止水細節能由完工外觀唯一推定。","大面積混凝土完整不等於每一條接縫都已驗證水密。"],"optionsEn":["A crack-free surface proves correct installation of all concealed waterstops.","Concealed waterstop details can be uniquely inferred from finished appearance.","Intact bulk concrete does not establish watertightness at every joint."],"answer":2,"explanation":"防水介面是連續路徑問題，局部缺口可能主導整體滲漏。 照片可協助追溯位置，但材料識別與施工紀錄仍需各自保留。","explanationEn":"Water control is a continuity problem in which a local gap can dominate leakage. Photos help trace locations, while material identification and installation records remain separate needs."}},{"id":"b226-v7-10","sequence":10,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-09"],"title":"辨認滾動閘門的空間包絡","titleEn":"Identify rolling-gate movement envelopes","objective":"區分閘門封水、移動及檢修空間。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish sealing, movement and maintenance spaces.","instruction":"1. 畫閘室與側向閘門凹槽；2. 以虛線標出概念移動包絡；3. 列出結構、驅動及維護三類介面。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a chamber and lateral gate recess; 2. mark a conceptual movement envelope; 3. list structural, drive and maintenance interfaces.","observation":"閘門能放入凹槽不等於移動、密封及維護條件全部成立。","observationEn":"A gate fitting its recess does not establish movement, sealing and maintenance requirements.","failure":"只要閘門外形吻合開口，所有機械介面便可省略。","failureEn":"A gate outline matching the opening makes every mechanical interface unnecessary.","check":"輸出三種空間與介面分色的平面圖。","checkEn":"Produce a plan separating three spaces and interface types by color.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-10-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"滾動門的側向移動與原運河人字門的旋轉不同，不能沿用相同幾何模型。","textEn":"Rolling-gate translation differs from original miter-gate rotation and needs a different geometric model."},{"id":"b226-v7-10-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本圖不提供運動速度、驅動力或現場維護操作值。","textEn":"The diagram supplies no movement speeds, drive forces or field maintenance settings."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認滾動閘門的空間包絡」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Identify rolling-gate movement envelopes”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["閘門能放入凹槽不等於移動、密封及維護條件全部成立。","只要閘門外形吻合開口，所有機械介面便可省略。","滾動門的檢修空間可由封水位置的外框直接代替。"],"optionsEn":["A gate fitting its recess does not establish movement, sealing and maintenance requirements.","A gate outline matching the opening makes every mechanical interface unnecessary.","A rolling gate’s closed outline directly substitutes for its maintenance space."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滾動門的側向移動與原運河人字門的旋轉不同，不能沿用相同幾何模型。 本圖不提供運動速度、驅動力或現場維護操作值。","explanationEn":"Rolling-gate translation differs from original miter-gate rotation and needs a different geometric model. The diagram supplies no movement speeds, drive forces or field maintenance settings."}},{"id":"b226-v7-11","sequence":11,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-10"],"title":"追溯大型閘門製造與運輸","titleEn":"Trace gate fabrication and transport evidence","objective":"理解製造完成與現地適合安裝的差別。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish fabrication completion from site installation readiness.","instruction":"1. 畫製造、海運、暫存及安裝四個資料節點；2. 每段列出幾何與狀態紀錄；3. 加入到場損傷及版本不符的假想例子。","instructionEn":"1. Draw fabrication, sea transport, storage and installation records; 2. list geometry and condition evidence at each stage; 3. introduce hypothetical arrival damage and revision mismatch.","observation":"出廠驗證不會自動覆蓋運輸及到場後的狀態變化。","observationEn":"Factory verification does not automatically cover transport and post-arrival condition changes.","failure":"供應商出廠合格即可刪除所有到場介面複核。","failureEn":"Supplier factory acceptance eliminates every arrival-interface review.","check":"提交一件構件從出廠到移交的資料鏈。","checkEn":"Provide one component’s evidence chain from factory to handover.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-11-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"大型構件的品質包含幾何、材料、運輸支承及狀態追溯，不能只看重量。","textEn":"Large-component quality involves geometry, material, transport support and condition traceability, not weight alone."},{"id":"b226-v7-11-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"歷史運輸照片可說明尺度及物流背景，不是可複製的吊運計畫。","textEn":"Historical transport photographs explain scale and logistics context, not a reusable lifting plan."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「追溯大型閘門製造與運輸」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Trace gate fabrication and transport evidence”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["供應商出廠合格即可刪除所有到場介面複核。","出廠驗證不會自動覆蓋運輸及到場後的狀態變化。","大型構件重量一致就表示運輸後幾何與狀態未改變。"],"optionsEn":["Supplier factory acceptance eliminates every arrival-interface review.","Factory verification does not automatically cover transport and post-arrival condition changes.","Equal component weight proves geometry and condition are unchanged after transport."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大型構件的品質包含幾何、材料、運輸支承及狀態追溯，不能只看重量。 歷史運輸照片可說明尺度及物流背景，不是可複製的吊運計畫。","explanationEn":"Large-component quality involves geometry, material, transport support and condition traceability, not weight alone. Historical transport photographs explain scale and logistics context, not a reusable lifting plan."}},{"id":"b226-v7-12","sequence":12,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-expanded","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-11"],"title":"審查閘門—土建的公差鏈","titleEn":"Review gate-to-civil tolerance chains","objective":"把零件尺寸轉成整體介面配合。","objectiveEn":"Translate component dimensions into assembled interface compatibility.","instruction":"1. 自設閘門、凹槽及導向三個尺寸；2. 分別加入同向及反向偏差；3. 比較剩餘間隙並記錄共同基準。","instructionEn":"1. Invent gate, recess and guide dimensions; 2. apply same-direction and opposite-direction deviations; 3. compare remaining clearances under one datum.","observation":"各零件在自有公差內仍可能組成不相容的介面。","observationEn":"Individually in-tolerance parts can still create an incompatible assembly.","failure":"每個供應商都合格就代表組合間隙一定合適。","failureEn":"Every supplier passing guarantees acceptable assembly clearance.","check":"輸出有單位、基準及最不利組合的公差表。","checkEn":"Provide a tolerance table with units, datums and adverse combinations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-12-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"配合由多項尺寸共同決定，系統性偏差與不同基準會增加閉合問題。","textEn":"Fit depends on multiple dimensions; systematic bias and inconsistent datums can worsen closure."},{"id":"b226-v7-12-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設間隙只用於理解累積，不是實際閘門可接受偏差。","textEn":"Invented clearances explain accumulation and are not permissible real-gate tolerances."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「審查閘門—土建的公差鏈」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review gate-to-civil tolerance chains”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["每個供應商都合格就代表組合間隙一定合適。","相同方向的公差一定會互相抵消並增加間隙。","各零件在自有公差內仍可能組成不相容的介面。"],"optionsEn":["Every supplier passing guarantees acceptable assembly clearance.","Same-direction tolerances necessarily cancel and increase clearance.","Individually in-tolerance parts can still create an incompatible assembly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配合由多項尺寸共同決定，系統性偏差與不同基準會增加閉合問題。 自設間隙只用於理解累積，不是實際閘門可接受偏差。","explanationEn":"Fit depends on multiple dimensions; systematic bias and inconsistent datums can worsen closure. Invented clearances explain accumulation and are not permissible real-gate tolerances."}}]},{"id":"b226-stage03","order":3,"title":"水力與功能介面驗證","titleEn":"Hydraulic and functional interfaces","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「水力與功能介面驗證」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on hydraulic and functional interfaces, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v7-13","sequence":13,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-12"],"title":"畫出節水池的儲水層級","titleEn":"Draw the water-saving basin levels","objective":"理解多池系統如何提供不同儲水位置。","objectiveEn":"Understand distinct storage levels in a multiple-basin system.","instruction":"1. 畫一個閘室及三個概念節水池；2. 標出水面高程及連通關係；3. 將內部轉移與外部供水箭頭分開。","instructionEn":"1. Draw one chamber and three conceptual saving basins; 2. mark levels and connections; 3. separate internal transfers from external supply.","observation":"節水池回用作用需要水位及連通條件，不能只靠池子的存在。","observationEn":"Basin reuse requires level and connection conditions, not merely the presence of basins.","failure":"新增池子但不核對高程及連通仍能保證相同節水效果。","failureEn":"Adding basins without checking levels and connections guarantees identical savings.","check":"提交有高程基準的池室連通圖。","checkEn":"Submit a basin-chamber connection map with a level datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-13-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水的可轉移量受幾何與水位差影響，儲水總容量不能直接當成每次回用量。","textEn":"Transferable water depends on geometry and head difference; total storage is not automatically reused per cycle."},{"id":"b226-v7-13-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步僅建立水力概念，不提供真實節水池閥門時序。","textEn":"This step builds hydraulic concepts and provides no actual basin-valve sequence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「畫出節水池的儲水層級」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Draw the water-saving basin levels”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["節水池回用作用需要水位及連通條件，不能只靠池子的存在。","新增池子但不核對高程及連通仍能保證相同節水效果。","節水池總容量就是每個航次必定回用的水量。"],"optionsEn":["Basin reuse requires level and connection conditions, not merely the presence of basins.","Adding basins without checking levels and connections guarantees identical savings.","Total basin capacity equals water necessarily reused on every transit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水的可轉移量受幾何與水位差影響，儲水總容量不能直接當成每次回用量。 本步僅建立水力概念，不提供真實節水池閥門時序。","explanationEn":"Transferable water depends on geometry and head difference; total storage is not automatically reused per cycle. This step builds hydraulic concepts and provides no actual basin-valve sequence."}},{"id":"b226-v7-14","sequence":14,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-13"],"title":"區分靜水壓與流動瞬變","titleEn":"Distinguish hydrostatic and transient effects","objective":"避免用靜止水面推定所有充排水現象。","objectiveEn":"Avoid inferring every filling or emptying effect from still-water levels.","instruction":"1. 畫靜止水面下的壓力趨勢；2. 另畫概念管路流量變化；3. 分列穩態、瞬變及結構反應三種問題。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch pressure trends beneath a still surface; 2. separately sketch changing conduit flow; 3. distinguish steady, transient and structural-response questions.","observation":"相同起訖水位不保證過程中的流量及壓力歷程相同。","observationEn":"Identical initial and final levels do not guarantee identical flow or pressure histories.","failure":"只知道最後水位即可證明整段充水過程沒有瞬變問題。","failureEn":"Knowing the final level proves the filling process has no transient issues.","check":"繳交狀態量與過程量的比較表。","checkEn":"Provide a comparison of state quantities and process quantities.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-14-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"靜水壓描述近乎靜止條件；改變流速涉及動量及時間效應。","textEn":"Hydrostatic pressure describes near-stationary conditions; changing velocity introduces momentum and time effects."},{"id":"b226-v7-14-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"概念曲線不設定流速、開關速率或設備極限，也不取代水力試驗。","textEn":"Conceptual curves set no velocities, actuation rates or equipment limits and do not replace hydraulic tests."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分靜水壓與流動瞬變」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish hydrostatic and transient effects”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只知道最後水位即可證明整段充水過程沒有瞬變問題。","相同起訖水位不保證過程中的流量及壓力歷程相同。","靜水壓圖已包含全部流速變化的時間效應。"],"optionsEn":["Knowing the final level proves the filling process has no transient issues.","Identical initial and final levels do not guarantee identical flow or pressure histories.","A hydrostatic-pressure diagram already includes all time effects of changing velocity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜水壓描述近乎靜止條件；改變流速涉及動量及時間效應。 概念曲線不設定流速、開關速率或設備極限，也不取代水力試驗。","explanationEn":"Hydrostatic pressure describes near-stationary conditions; changing velocity introduces momentum and time effects. Conceptual curves set no velocities, actuation rates or equipment limits and do not replace hydraulic tests."}},{"id":"b226-v7-15","sequence":15,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-14"],"title":"檢查船舶包絡與水位情境","titleEn":"Check vessel envelopes across level cases","objective":"把吃水、浮體及閘室幾何分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate draft, floating-body geometry and chamber dimensions.","instruction":"1. 畫一個假想船體及水線；2. 比較兩個自設水位情境；3. 將船舶尺度與通航核准資料分成不同欄。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a hypothetical hull and waterline; 2. compare two invented level cases; 3. separate vessel dimensions from navigation-approval data.","observation":"船體在示意圖內放得下不代表符合實際通航條件。","observationEn":"A vessel fitting inside a drawing does not establish actual navigation eligibility.","failure":"以滑鼠把船放入閘室就等於完成吃水與通航驗證。","failureEn":"Dragging a ship into a chamber completes draft and navigation verification.","check":"提交幾何假設、情境與未知條件三欄表。","checkEn":"Provide geometric assumptions, scenarios and unknown conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-15-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"船舶浮態與可用水深具有共同邊界，通航評估還需要營運及船舶資料。","textEn":"Vessel flotation and available depth share boundaries; navigation review also needs operating and vessel information."},{"id":"b226-v7-15-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本模型不提供允許吃水、船寬或實際航行建議。","textEn":"The model provides no permissible draft, beam or actual navigation advice."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檢查船舶包絡與水位情境」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Check vessel envelopes across level cases”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["以滑鼠把船放入閘室就等於完成吃水與通航驗證。","閘室土建尺寸可以直接取代營運者的船舶核准條件。","船體在示意圖內放得下不代表符合實際通航條件。"],"optionsEn":["Dragging a ship into a chamber completes draft and navigation verification.","Chamber civil dimensions directly replace operator vessel-approval conditions.","A vessel fitting inside a drawing does not establish actual navigation eligibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"船舶浮態與可用水深具有共同邊界，通航評估還需要營運及船舶資料。 本模型不提供允許吃水、船寬或實際航行建議。","explanationEn":"Vessel flotation and available depth share boundaries; navigation review also needs operating and vessel information. The model provides no permissible draft, beam or actual navigation advice."}},{"id":"b226-v7-16","sequence":16,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-15"],"title":"把水位感測與設備狀態分開","titleEn":"Separate level sensing from equipment state","objective":"理解量測與命令確認的不同證據。","objectiveEn":"Understand separate evidence for measurement and command confirmation.","instruction":"1. 畫水位感測、控制判斷及設備回饋三個節點；2. 用不同箭頭標記資料和命令；3. 加入一個感測器失準的假想案例。","instructionEn":"1. Draw level sensing, control decision and equipment-feedback nodes; 2. distinguish data from commands; 3. introduce a hypothetical sensor bias.","observation":"發出命令與設備達到所需狀態是兩件需分別證實的事。","observationEn":"Issuing a command and reaching the required equipment state need separate evidence.","failure":"控制畫面顯示命令已送出就能證明閘門機械位置正確。","failureEn":"A sent-command display proves the gate’s mechanical position is correct.","check":"提供命令、回饋及獨立查證的功能圖。","checkEn":"Provide a function map of command, feedback and independent verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-16-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"控制系統依靠狀態資訊，感測偏差與回饋缺失需在概念驗證中區分。","textEn":"Controls rely on state information; biased sensing and missing feedback are distinct verification questions."},{"id":"b226-v7-16-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"此圖僅為一般工程原理，不揭示或模擬真實船閘控制邏輯。","textEn":"The diagram teaches general principles and neither reveals nor simulates actual lock-control logic."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把水位感測與設備狀態分開」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate level sensing from equipment state”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["發出命令與設備達到所需狀態是兩件需分別證實的事。","控制畫面顯示命令已送出就能證明閘門機械位置正確。","水位感測器正常就能證明閘門機械回饋也正常。"],"optionsEn":["Issuing a command and reaching the required equipment state need separate evidence.","A sent-command display proves the gate’s mechanical position is correct.","A functioning level sensor proves correct mechanical gate feedback."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制系統依靠狀態資訊，感測偏差與回饋缺失需在概念驗證中區分。 此圖僅為一般工程原理，不揭示或模擬真實船閘控制邏輯。","explanationEn":"Controls rely on state information; biased sensing and missing feedback are distinct verification questions. The diagram teaches general principles and neither reveals nor simulates actual lock-control logic."}},{"id":"b226-v7-17","sequence":17,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-16"],"title":"建立水密試驗的證據結構","titleEn":"Structure evidence for a watertightness test","objective":"區分試驗結果與試驗覆蓋範圍。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish a test result from its coverage.","instruction":"1. 選一個概念節水池邊界；2. 列出初始狀態、觀察量及資料期間；3. 明確寫下此次測試未涵蓋的介面。","instructionEn":"1. Select a conceptual basin boundary; 2. list initial state, observations and record duration; 3. state interfaces outside this test.","observation":"一次局部水密結果不能直接證明整個閘室系統所有功能。","observationEn":"One local watertightness result does not verify every function of the complete lock system.","failure":"節水池不漏水便表示閘門、控制及通航全部已驗收。","failureEn":"A watertight basin means gates, controls and navigation are fully accepted.","check":"輸出含邊界與不適用範圍的試驗摘要範本。","checkEn":"Provide a test-summary template with boundaries and exclusions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-17-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"試驗論證需描述狀態、量測及判定依據；只有通過二字不足以追溯。","textEn":"A test argument needs state, observations and judgment basis; a bare pass label is not traceable."},{"id":"b226-v7-17-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方試水新聞提供建設里程碑，課程不由新聞反推實際驗收限值。","textEn":"Official filling-test news provides a milestone; this course does not infer acceptance limits from it."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立水密試驗的證據結構」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Structure evidence for a watertightness test”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["節水池不漏水便表示閘門、控制及通航全部已驗收。","一次局部水密結果不能直接證明整個閘室系統所有功能。","試驗只需保留通過標記，不需保留當時邊界。"],"optionsEn":["A watertight basin means gates, controls and navigation are fully accepted.","One local watertightness result does not verify every function of the complete lock system.","Testing needs only a pass label and no record of boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試驗論證需描述狀態、量測及判定依據；只有通過二字不足以追溯。 官方試水新聞提供建設里程碑，課程不由新聞反推實際驗收限值。","explanationEn":"A test argument needs state, observations and judgment basis; a bare pass label is not traceable. Official filling-test news provides a milestone; this course does not infer acceptance limits from it."}},{"id":"b226-v7-18","sequence":18,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-17"],"title":"做跨專業整合審查","titleEn":"Review multidisciplinary integration","objective":"讓土建、水力、機械與控制使用同一套邊界。","objectiveEn":"Align boundaries across civil, hydraulic, mechanical and control disciplines.","instruction":"1. 把四類系統放進介面矩陣；2. 每對介面填入共享量與版本；3. 追查一個水位基準變更的全部影響。","instructionEn":"1. Place four system classes in an interface matrix; 2. record shared quantities and versions; 3. trace all effects of one level-datum change.","observation":"共享水位基準不一致可能讓各自正確的子系統產生整體衝突。","observationEn":"Inconsistent shared level datums can make individually correct subsystems incompatible.","failure":"每一專業自己的圖面通過就保證交界完全一致。","failureEn":"Every discipline’s drawing approval guarantees compatible interfaces.","check":"提交一份含跨專業問題及修訂欄的矩陣。","checkEn":"Submit a matrix with multidisciplinary issues and revision fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-18-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"大型水工工程的錯誤常落在介面與資料定義，需明確協調責任與版本。","textEn":"Large hydraulic works need explicit responsibility and version control at interfaces and data definitions."},{"id":"b226-v7-18-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"介面審查不是實際系統投運許可；後者還需正式程序與專業驗證。","textEn":"Interface review is not permission to commission a real system, which requires formal procedures and professional verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「做跨專業整合審查」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review multidisciplinary integration”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["每一專業自己的圖面通過就保證交界完全一致。","土建與控制採用不同水位零點不會影響結果。","共享水位基準不一致可能讓各自正確的子系統產生整體衝突。"],"optionsEn":["Every discipline’s drawing approval guarantees compatible interfaces.","Different level zero points in civil and control systems cannot affect results.","Inconsistent shared level datums can make individually correct subsystems incompatible."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大型水工工程的錯誤常落在介面與資料定義，需明確協調責任與版本。 介面審查不是實際系統投運許可；後者還需正式程序與專業驗證。","explanationEn":"Large hydraulic works need explicit responsibility and version control at interfaces and data definitions. Interface review is not permission to commission a real system, which requires formal procedures and professional verification."}}]},{"id":"b226-stage04","order":4,"title":"維護、流域與衍生工程","titleEn":"Maintenance, watershed and related works","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「維護、流域與衍生工程」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on maintenance, watershed and related works, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v7-19","sequence":19,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-18"],"title":"辨識密封劣化與量測誤差","titleEn":"Distinguish seal degradation and observation errors","objective":"避免從單一滲漏數字推定唯一故障。","objectiveEn":"Avoid inferring a unique fault from one leakage value.","instruction":"1. 自設三段水位與流量紀錄；2. 分別加入密封變化、量測偏移及水位差變化；3. 找出需要獨立查證的訊號。","instructionEn":"1. Create three level and flow records; 2. introduce seal changes, sensor offsets and changed head; 3. identify signals needing independent confirmation.","observation":"流量增加可能來自水位差或量測改變，不一定只有密封劣化。","observationEn":"Higher flow can reflect changed head or measurements, not only seal degradation.","failure":"只要漏水數字上升就能確定是哪一段密封失效。","failureEn":"An increased leakage number uniquely identifies the failed seal segment.","check":"輸出至少三種原因的辨識表。","checkEn":"Produce a discrimination table for at least three causes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-19-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"診斷需要把驅動條件與設備狀態一起比較，不能只看輸出數字。","textEn":"Diagnosis compares driving conditions with equipment state rather than output numbers alone."},{"id":"b226-v7-19-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設紀錄用於練習排除混淆因素，不代表任一真實閘門有缺陷。","textEn":"Synthetic records practice separating confounders and imply no defect in any real gate."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨識密封劣化與量測誤差」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish seal degradation and observation errors”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["流量增加可能來自水位差或量測改變，不一定只有密封劣化。","只要漏水數字上升就能確定是哪一段密封失效。","水位差改變不可能影響量到的漏水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Higher flow can reflect changed head or measurements, not only seal degradation.","An increased leakage number uniquely identifies the failed seal segment.","Changed water head cannot affect observed leakage flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"診斷需要把驅動條件與設備狀態一起比較，不能只看輸出數字。 自設紀錄用於練習排除混淆因素，不代表任一真實閘門有缺陷。","explanationEn":"Diagnosis compares driving conditions with equipment state rather than output numbers alone. Synthetic records practice separating confounders and imply no defect in any real gate."}},{"id":"b226-v7-20","sequence":20,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-19"],"title":"建立維護可達性與備援觀點","titleEn":"Review maintenance access and redundancy","objective":"理解能維修與仍有服務能力是不同問題。","objectiveEn":"Understand that maintainability and retained service are separate questions.","instruction":"1. 在概念系統標出待維護設備；2. 列出接近、隔離及其他路徑的證據需求；3. 分开局部備援與共同依賴。","instructionEn":"1. Mark equipment for hypothetical maintenance; 2. list evidence needs for access, separation and alternate paths; 3. distinguish local redundancy from shared dependencies.","observation":"兩套設備若共用同一個關鍵依賴，不代表完全獨立備援。","observationEn":"Two equipment sets sharing a critical dependency are not fully independent redundancy.","failure":"設備數量加倍便可忽略共同供電或共同土建介面。","failureEn":"Doubling equipment count makes shared power or civil interfaces irrelevant.","check":"繳交備援、共同原因與待查資料表。","checkEn":"Provide a table of redundancy, common causes and evidence gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-20-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"可靠性要看功能路徑及共同失效因素，而非只數設備件數。","textEn":"Reliability depends on functional paths and common-cause factors, not equipment count alone."},{"id":"b226-v7-20-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步不提供隔離、檢修或現場替代操作方法，只建立審查問題。","textEn":"This step provides no isolation, servicing or substitute operating method; it defines review questions."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立維護可達性與備援觀點」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review maintenance access and redundancy”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["設備數量加倍便可忽略共同供電或共同土建介面。","兩套設備若共用同一個關鍵依賴，不代表完全獨立備援。","兩個設備共用同一依賴仍必定構成完全獨立備援。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling equipment count makes shared power or civil interfaces irrelevant.","Two equipment sets sharing a critical dependency are not fully independent redundancy.","Two devices sharing one dependency necessarily form fully independent redundancy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可靠性要看功能路徑及共同失效因素，而非只數設備件數。 本步不提供隔離、檢修或現場替代操作方法，只建立審查問題。","explanationEn":"Reliability depends on functional paths and common-cause factors, not equipment count alone. This step provides no isolation, servicing or substitute operating method; it defines review questions."}},{"id":"b226-v7-21","sequence":21,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-20"],"title":"把航次與流域資料分層","titleEn":"Separate transit and watershed records","objective":"連結局部節水與長期水資源帳。","objectiveEn":"Connect local reuse with long-term water-resource accounting.","instruction":"1. 建立一次概念航次水帳；2. 另建月尺度入流、蒸發與取水帳；3. 標記兩者可比較與不可直接相加的量。","instructionEn":"1. Create a conceptual transit water ledger; 2. create a monthly inflow, evaporation and withdrawal ledger; 3. mark comparable and nonadditive quantities.","observation":"單次回用表現不能單獨代表整個流域的長期供需平衡。","observationEn":"Per-transit reuse alone does not establish long-term watershed balance.","failure":"一個航次節水就能推出整個月水庫蓄水必然增加。","failureEn":"Water saving on one transit proves reservoir storage must rise over the month.","check":"提交兩個時間尺度的守恆表與連結項。","checkEn":"Provide balances at two time scales with their connecting terms.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-21-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水資源分析的時間與空間邊界必須一致；不同尺度的指標不能直接混算。","textEn":"Water-resource analysis needs consistent temporal and spatial boundaries; metrics at different scales cannot be mixed directly."},{"id":"b226-v7-21-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"長期判讀需資料完整性與不確定性，不由單次示範動畫推論。","textEn":"Long-term interpretation requires complete records and uncertainty treatment, not one demonstration animation."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把航次與流域資料分層」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate transit and watershed records”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["一個航次節水就能推出整個月水庫蓄水必然增加。","月尺度入流可以直接加到單次航次回用百分比。","單次回用表現不能單獨代表整個流域的長期供需平衡。"],"optionsEn":["Water saving on one transit proves reservoir storage must rise over the month.","Monthly inflow can be added directly to a per-transit reuse percentage.","Per-transit reuse alone does not establish long-term watershed balance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水資源分析的時間與空間邊界必須一致；不同尺度的指標不能直接混算。 長期判讀需資料完整性與不確定性，不由單次示範動畫推論。","explanationEn":"Water-resource analysis needs consistent temporal and spatial boundaries; metrics at different scales cannot be mixed directly. Long-term interpretation requires complete records and uncertainty treatment, not one demonstration animation."}},{"id":"b226-v7-22","sequence":22,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-21"],"title":"比較原運河與其他升船工程","titleEn":"Compare the original canal and other ship-lifting works","objective":"找出相近目的下不同水力與機械解法。","objectiveEn":"Identify different hydraulic and mechanical solutions to related aims.","instruction":"1. 比較原巴拿馬船閘與擴建新閘；2. 再選三峽船閘或升船機查證；3. 分開水位調節、機械升降及資源需求。","instructionEn":"1. Compare original and expanded Panama locks; 2. select Three Gorges locks or its ship lift for further evidence; 3. separate level adjustment, mechanical lifting and resource needs.","observation":"都能升降船舶的工程仍可能有完全不同的承載與能源路徑。","observationEn":"Works that all raise vessels can have very different load and energy paths.","failure":"所有升船設施都可用相同閘門及節水池模型表示。","failureEn":"Every ship-lifting facility can use the same gate and basin model.","check":"繳交三個相似需求與三個不同機理。","checkEn":"Provide three shared needs and three different mechanisms.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-22-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"衍生學習應比較要解決的問題，再查證各工程使用的具體方案。","textEn":"Related learning compares the problem first, then verifies the particular solution used by each project."},{"id":"b226-v7-22-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"原運河歷史是比較背景，不能把早期設備敘述當成擴建新閘的現況。","textEn":"Original-canal history provides comparison and must not be presented as current expanded-lock equipment."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較原運河與其他升船工程」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare the original canal and other ship-lifting works”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["都能升降船舶的工程仍可能有完全不同的承載與能源路徑。","所有升船設施都可用相同閘門及節水池模型表示。","機械升船與調整閘室水位具有完全相同的能源路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Works that all raise vessels can have very different load and energy paths.","Every ship-lifting facility can use the same gate and basin model.","Mechanical vessel lifting and chamber-level adjustment have identical energy paths."],"answer":0,"explanation":"衍生學習應比較要解決的問題，再查證各工程使用的具體方案。 原運河歷史是比較背景，不能把早期設備敘述當成擴建新閘的現況。","explanationEn":"Related learning compares the problem first, then verifies the particular solution used by each project. Original-canal history provides comparison and must not be presented as current expanded-lock equipment."}},{"id":"b226-v7-23","sequence":23,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-22"],"title":"查核節水與容量宣稱","titleEn":"Audit water-saving and capacity claims","objective":"把宣傳數字轉成可核對的工程敘述。","objectiveEn":"Turn headline numbers into checkable engineering statements.","instruction":"1. 選一個官方容量或節水敘述；2. 摘出日期、比較對象與條件；3. 改寫成保留限制與未知的學習筆記。","instructionEn":"1. Select an official capacity or saving statement; 2. extract date, comparison basis and conditions; 3. rewrite it as a note retaining limits and unknowns.","observation":"有來源的數字仍需保留日期與適用條件才不會被誤用。","observationEn":"A sourced number still needs its date and applicability conditions to avoid misuse.","failure":"數字來自官方頁面就能不加條件套用到任何年份和航次。","failureEn":"An official number applies unconditionally to every year and transit.","check":"提交一條原意不變且明示範圍的摘要。","checkEn":"Submit one faithful summary with explicit scope.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-23-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"資料可信與適用於當前問題是兩個不同檢查；來源權威不能取代邊界核對。","textEn":"Credibility and applicability are separate checks; source authority does not replace boundary review."},{"id":"b226-v7-23-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"使用者自設模擬結果不能偽裝成營運者的實際效率或性能保證。","textEn":"User-generated simulation results must not masquerade as operator efficiency data or performance guarantees."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「查核節水與容量宣稱」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Audit water-saving and capacity claims”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["數字來自官方頁面就能不加條件套用到任何年份和航次。","有來源的數字仍需保留日期與適用條件才不會被誤用。","資料的發布日期與比較基準不影響工程宣稱的適用性。"],"optionsEn":["An official number applies unconditionally to every year and transit.","A sourced number still needs its date and applicability conditions to avoid misuse.","Publication date and comparison basis do not affect a claim’s applicability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料可信與適用於當前問題是兩個不同檢查；來源權威不能取代邊界核對。 使用者自設模擬結果不能偽裝成營運者的實際效率或性能保證。","explanationEn":"Credibility and applicability are separate checks; source authority does not replace boundary review. User-generated simulation results must not masquerade as operator efficiency data or performance guarantees."}},{"id":"b226-v7-24","sequence":24,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-gates","v7-panama-original","v7-panama-visitor"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-23"],"title":"完成水工系統交付報告","titleEn":"Complete the hydraulic-system learning report","objective":"讓幾何、水量、設備與資料保持一致。","objectiveEn":"Align geometry, water balance, equipment and evidence.","instruction":"1. 彙整四階段模型及矩陣；2. 逐一連結來源、假設與未解項；3. 選一個介面變更演練資料更新的傳播。","instructionEn":"1. Assemble four-stage models and matrices; 2. link sources, assumptions and open items; 3. rehearse propagation of one interface revision.","observation":"可複查報告會清楚指出自設模型與真實工程證據的分界。","observationEn":"An auditable report clearly separates invented models from real-project evidence.","failure":"完成全部動畫就可宣稱已掌握真實船閘的投運與操控。","failureEn":"Completing all animations establishes mastery of real lock commissioning and control.","check":"提交含版本、圖例、來源與待查問題的學習檔。","checkEn":"Submit a learning dossier with versions, legends, sources and open questions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v7-24-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"水工巨作需要土建、機械、水力、控制及流域共同成立，局部示範不等於整體驗證。","textEn":"Major hydraulic works depend on civil, mechanical, hydraulic, control and watershed systems together; a local demo is not system verification."},{"id":"b226-v7-24-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程交付的是工程概念與證據組織能力，不是現場建造或操作資格。","textEn":"The deliverable is engineering understanding and evidence organization, not field construction or operating qualification."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「完成水工系統交付報告」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Complete the hydraulic-system learning report”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["完成全部動畫就可宣稱已掌握真實船閘的投運與操控。","每個局部功能動畫成功就等同整體正式驗收完成。","可複查報告會清楚指出自設模型與真實工程證據的分界。"],"optionsEn":["Completing all animations establishes mastery of real lock commissioning and control.","Successful local animations equal completion of formal system acceptance.","An auditable report clearly separates invented models from real-project evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水工巨作需要土建、機械、水力、控制及流域共同成立，局部示範不等於整體驗證。 本課程交付的是工程概念與證據組織能力，不是現場建造或操作資格。","explanationEn":"Major hydraulic works depend on civil, mechanical, hydraulic, control and watershed systems together; a local demo is not system verification. The deliverable is engineering understanding and evidence organization, not field construction or operating qualification."}}]},{"id":"b226-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「雙池水位均衡」與「充水歷線與慣性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equalization between two pools\" and \"Filling hydrograph and inertia\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v15-01","title":"雙池水位均衡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equalization between two pools: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v7-24"],"objective":"說明「雙池水位均衡」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equalization between two pools” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。守恆終點只由初始體積與面積決定，達到終點的時間則另受管路控制。 假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。 把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙池水位均衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir. Conservation determines the equilibrium endpoint from initial storage and areas, while conduits separately determine how quickly it is approached. Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m. Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equalization between two pools” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas.","failure":"常見誤解：「節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙池水位均衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equalization between two pools”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-01-k1","title":"雙池水位均衡","titleEn":"Equalization between two pools","text":"兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。守恆終點只由初始體積與面積決定，達到終點的時間則另受管路控制。","textEn":"Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir. Conservation determines the equilibrium endpoint from initial storage and areas, while conduits separately determine how quickly it is approached.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙池水位均衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equalization between two pools\" is correct?","options":["節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。","兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。","充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。"],"optionsEn":["A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.","Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir.","Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b226-v15-02","title":"雙池水位均衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Equalization between two pools: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙池水位均衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equalization between two pools” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙池水位均衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equalization between two pools\", which statement holds?","options":["兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。","慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定。"],"optionsEn":["Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal.","A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b226-v15-03","title":"雙池水位均衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equalization between two pools: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙池水位均衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equalization between two pools” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。另算閘室下降水量與池體上升水量，核對共同終點能同時滿足兩個控制體的守恆。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone. Separately calculate chamber loss and basin gain and verify that the shared endpoint closes both control-volume balances. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以雙池水位均衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for equalization between two pools, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone.","failure":"注意干擾：把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。另算閘室下降水量與池體上升水量，核對共同終點能同時滿足兩個控制體的守恆。","textEn":"Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone. Separately calculate chamber loss and basin gain and verify that the shared endpoint closes both control-volume balances.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以雙池水位均衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for equalization between two pools, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙池水位均衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equalization between two pools\"?","options":["各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。"],"optionsEn":["Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route."],"answer":0,"explanation":"各自積分水位變化乘面積，檢查兩側交換體積是否相反相等；再用閥位和流量時序辨識接近均衡時變慢的原因，不能只比較終點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b226-v15-04","title":"雙池水位均衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equalization between two pools: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙池水位均衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equalization between two pools” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。","textEn":"Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙池水位均衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equalization between two pools\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。","充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water.","Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b226-v15-05","title":"充水歷線與慣性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filling hydrograph and inertia: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「充水歷線與慣性」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filling hydrograph and inertia” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。平均充水時間無法表示瞬時最大流量。 假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。 同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「充水歷線與慣性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. Early acceleration and late deceleration also create surface slopes affecting vessels, so average filling time cannot represent peak discharge. Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph. Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filling hydrograph and inertia” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「充水歷線與慣性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filling hydrograph and inertia”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-05-k1","title":"充水歷線與慣性","titleEn":"Filling hydrograph and inertia","text":"船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。平均充水時間無法表示瞬時最大流量。","textEn":"Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. Early acceleration and late deceleration also create surface slopes affecting vessels, so average filling time cannot represent peak discharge.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「充水歷線與慣性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filling hydrograph and inertia\" is correct?","options":["充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。","閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。","船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.","A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.","Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b226-v15-06","title":"充水歷線與慣性：定量估算","titleEn":"Filling hydrograph and inertia: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「充水歷線與慣性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filling hydrograph and inertia” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「充水歷線與慣性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filling hydrograph and inertia\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³。","平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。","兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s.","Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group.","Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b226-v15-07","title":"充水歷線與慣性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filling hydrograph and inertia: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「充水歷線與慣性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filling hydrograph and inertia” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。把高頻流量歷線重新取樣後積分，檢查峰值保存程度與總水量的數值收斂。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Preserve the rising limb resolution instead of smoothing inertial effects into a full-cycle average. Resample the high-frequency hydrograph and integrate it, checking both peak preservation and numerical convergence of total volume. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以充水歷線與慣性編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for filling hydrograph and inertia, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Preserve the rising limb resolution instead of smoothing inertial effects into a full-cycle average.","failure":"注意干擾：同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。把高頻流量歷線重新取樣後積分，檢查峰值保存程度與總水量的數值收斂。","textEn":"Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Preserve the rising limb resolution instead of smoothing inertial effects into a full-cycle average. Resample the high-frequency hydrograph and integrate it, checking both peak preservation and numerical convergence of total volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以充水歷線與慣性編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for filling hydrograph and inertia, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Preserve the rising limb resolution instead of smoothing inertial effects into a full-cycle average.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「充水歷線與慣性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filling hydrograph and inertia\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。","百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads.","Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用流量積分對照水位升幅，並比較室內前後水位差與船舶繫纜負荷；保留流量上升段解析度，避免用整段平均掩蓋慣性效應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare integrated flow with level rise and relate longitudinal level differences to mooring loads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b226-v15-08","title":"充水歷線與慣性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filling hydrograph and inertia: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「充水歷線與慣性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filling hydrograph and inertia” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。","textEn":"Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「充水歷線與慣性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filling hydrograph and inertia\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。","同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.","Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":5},{"id":"b226-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「縱向水面坡度推力」與「密度交換前緣」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Longitudinal water-slope force\" and \"Density-exchange front\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v15-09","title":"縱向水面坡度推力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Longitudinal water-slope force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「縱向水面坡度推力」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Longitudinal water-slope force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"充水不均會使閘室水面形成坡度，船體承受對應的長向壓力差。以排水重量乘小坡度可估算準靜態推力，但需另外處理流速阻力和繫纜動力。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設船舶排水質量50000 t、閘內坡度0.0002，長向力約mgS=98.1 kN；小坡度準靜態，不含阻力與加速度。 單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。若將全部張力歸於水面坡度，可能掩蓋局部射流或不對稱流入。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「縱向水面坡度推力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uneven filling creates a longitudinal surface slope and pressure imbalance on a vessel. Displacement weight times small slope estimates quasi-static force, with current drag and mooring dynamics treated separately. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume vessel displacement mass 50000 t and longitudinal slope 0.0002. Approximate force mgS=98.1 kN, for a small quasi-static slope without drag or acceleration. A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. Attributing all tension to slope may conceal a local jet or asymmetric inflow acting on the hull. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Longitudinal water-slope force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「縱向水面坡度推力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Longitudinal water-slope force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-09-k1","title":"縱向水面坡度推力","titleEn":"Longitudinal water-slope force","text":"充水不均會使閘室水面形成坡度，船體承受對應的長向壓力差。以排水重量乘小坡度可估算準靜態推力，但需另外處理流速阻力和繫纜動力。","textEn":"Uneven filling creates a longitudinal surface slope and pressure imbalance on a vessel. Displacement weight times small slope estimates quasi-static force, with current drag and mooring dynamics treated separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「縱向水面坡度推力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Longitudinal water-slope force\" is correct?","options":["充水不均會使閘室水面形成坡度，船體承受對應的長向壓力差。","閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。","兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。"],"optionsEn":["Uneven filling creates a longitudinal surface slope and pressure imbalance on a vessel.","A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.","Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"充水不均會使閘室水面形成坡度，船體承受對應的長向壓力差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uneven filling creates a longitudinal surface slope and pressure imbalance on a vessel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b226-v15-10","title":"縱向水面坡度推力：定量估算","titleEn":"Longitudinal water-slope force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「縱向水面坡度推力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Longitudinal water-slope force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設船舶排水質量50000 t、閘內坡度0.0002，長向力約mgS=98.1 kN；小坡度準靜態，不含阻力與加速度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume vessel displacement mass 50000 t and longitudinal slope 0.0002. Approximate force mgS=98.1 kN, for a small quasi-static slope without drag or acceleration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設船舶排水質量50000 t、閘內坡度0.0002，長向力約mgS=98.1 kN；小坡度準靜態，不含阻力與加速度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume vessel displacement mass 50000 t and longitudinal slope 0.0002. Approximate force mgS=98.1 kN, for a small quasi-static slope without drag or acceleration.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「縱向水面坡度推力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Longitudinal water-slope force\", which statement holds?","options":["慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。"],"optionsEn":["A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b226-v15-11","title":"縱向水面坡度推力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Longitudinal water-slope force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「縱向水面坡度推力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Longitudinal water-slope force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。將船舶質量與坡度推力獨立重算，並檢查繫纜負荷是否存在不屬於水面坡度的相位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Separate wind, propulsion effects and line stiffness to define reproducible comparison conditions. Independently recalculate displacement-slope force and check whether mooring loads contain phases inconsistent with the measured surface slope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以縱向水面坡度推力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for longitudinal water-slope force, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Separate wind, propulsion effects and line stiffness to define reproducible comparison conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。將船舶質量與坡度推力獨立重算，並檢查繫纜負荷是否存在不屬於水面坡度的相位。","textEn":"Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Separate wind, propulsion effects and line stiffness to define reproducible comparison conditions. Independently recalculate displacement-slope force and check whether mooring loads contain phases inconsistent with the measured surface slope.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以縱向水面坡度推力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for longitudinal water-slope force, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Separate wind, propulsion effects and line stiffness to define reproducible comparison conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「縱向水面坡度推力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Longitudinal water-slope force\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。","在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.","Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在船首船尾及中段量測水位與流速，校核坡度估算和繫纜張力相位；將風力、推進器影響與繫纜剛度分離，建立可重現的比較工況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure levels and currents at bow, stern and midship, comparing inferred slope with mooring-tension phase. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b226-v15-12","title":"縱向水面坡度推力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Longitudinal water-slope force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「縱向水面坡度推力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Longitudinal water-slope force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。若將全部張力歸於水面坡度，可能掩蓋局部射流或不對稱流入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. Attributing all tension to slope may conceal a local jet or asymmetric inflow acting on the hull. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若將全部張力歸於水面坡度，可能掩蓋局部射流或不對稱流入。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Attributing all tension to slope may conceal a local jet or asymmetric inflow acting on the hull.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。若將全部張力歸於水面坡度，可能掩蓋局部射流或不對稱流入。","textEn":"A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. Attributing all tension to slope may conceal a local jet or asymmetric inflow acting on the hull.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「縱向水面坡度推力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Longitudinal water-slope force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。"],"optionsEn":["A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一水位站無法辨認室內坡度，繫纜伸長也會造成船體動態放大。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A single gauge cannot resolve chamber slope, and elastic mooring lines can amplify motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b226-v15-13","title":"密度交換前緣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Density-exchange front: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「密度交換前緣」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Density-exchange front” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。這種交換不能用零淨流量判定不存在。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設密度差25 kg/m³、基準1000 kg/m³、水深5 m，約化重力g′=0.24525 m/s²，速度尺度√(g′h)=1.107 m/s；非精確前緣速度。 表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度交換前緣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations. Zero net discharge therefore does not establish absence of density-driven exchange. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume density difference 25 kg/m³, reference density 1000 kg/m³ and depth 5 m. Reduced gravity is 0.24525 m/s² and √(g′h)=1.107 m/s, a scale rather than an exact front speed. Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density-exchange front” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「密度交換前緣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Density-exchange front”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-13-k1","title":"密度交換前緣","titleEn":"Density-exchange front","text":"海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。這種交換不能用零淨流量判定不存在。","textEn":"Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations. Zero net discharge therefore does not establish absence of density-driven exchange.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密度交換前緣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Density-exchange front\" is correct?","options":["兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。","海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。","平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。"],"optionsEn":["Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal.","Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations.","Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b226-v15-14","title":"密度交換前緣：定量估算","titleEn":"Density-exchange front: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「密度交換前緣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Density-exchange front” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設密度差25 kg/m³、基準1000 kg/m³、水深5 m，約化重力g′=0.24525 m/s²，速度尺度√(g′h)=1.107 m/s；非精確前緣速度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume density difference 25 kg/m³, reference density 1000 kg/m³ and depth 5 m. Reduced gravity is 0.24525 m/s² and √(g′h)=1.107 m/s, a scale rather than an exact front speed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設密度差25 kg/m³、基準1000 kg/m³、水深5 m，約化重力g′=0.24525 m/s²，速度尺度√(g′h)=1.107 m/s；非精確前緣速度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume density difference 25 kg/m³, reference density 1000 kg/m³ and depth 5 m. Reduced gravity is 0.24525 m/s² and √(g′h)=1.107 m/s, a scale rather than an exact front speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密度交換前緣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Density-exchange front\", which statement holds?","options":["兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。","百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk.","Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b226-v15-15","title":"密度交換前緣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Density-exchange front: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「密度交換前緣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Density-exchange front” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。以分層流量乘鹽度積分鹽通量，確認正負體積流量抵銷時仍可能輸送淨鹽量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Track interactions with vessel displacement and avoid treating turbidity as direct evidence of salinity. Integrate layer flow times salinity and verify that cancelling volume flows can still carry a net salt flux. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以密度交換前緣編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for density-exchange front, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Track interactions with vessel displacement and avoid treating turbidity as direct evidence of salinity.","failure":"注意干擾：表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。以分層流量乘鹽度積分鹽通量，確認正負體積流量抵銷時仍可能輸送淨鹽量。","textEn":"Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Track interactions with vessel displacement and avoid treating turbidity as direct evidence of salinity. Integrate layer flow times salinity and verify that cancelling volume flows can still carry a net salt flux.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以密度交換前緣編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for density-exchange front, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Track interactions with vessel displacement and avoid treating turbidity as direct evidence of salinity.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密度交換前緣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Density-exchange front\"?","options":["同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量測上下層流向及鹽度，計算鹽通量而非只積分總流量；追蹤前緣與船舶排水的交互作用，避免把短時混濁當作鹽分證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure upper and lower currents and salinity together, calculating salt flux rather than total discharge alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b226-v15-16","title":"密度交換前緣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Density-exchange front: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「密度交換前緣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Density-exchange front” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。","textEn":"Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密度交換前緣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Density-exchange front\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。","平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate.","Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":6},{"id":"b226-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「閘門浮力與輪載」與「管路快速減速壓峰」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads\" and \"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v15-17","title":"閘門浮力與輪載：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「閘門浮力與輪載」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。減輕平均輪載有利移動，但偏心、軌道沉降和門體變形仍可能使個別輪子受力集中。 假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。 某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閘門浮力與輪載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads. Lower mean loading aids movement, but eccentricity, rail settlement and deformation can still concentrate reactions on individual wheels. Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Mean wheel load is (40−28)/8=1.5 MN, excluding eccentricity, dynamics and rail-level differences. A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閘門浮力與輪載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-17-k1","title":"閘門浮力與輪載","titleEn":"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads","text":"滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。減輕平均輪載有利移動，但偏心、軌道沉降和門體變形仍可能使個別輪子受力集中。","textEn":"Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads. Lower mean loading aids movement, but eccentricity, rail settlement and deformation can still concentrate reactions on individual wheels.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘門浮力與輪載」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads\" is correct?","options":["平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。","慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group.","A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"b226-v15-18","title":"閘門浮力與輪載：定量估算","titleEn":"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閘門浮力與輪載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Mean wheel load is (40−28)/8=1.5 MN, excluding eccentricity, dynamics and rail-level differences. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Mean wheel load is (40−28)/8=1.5 MN, excluding eccentricity, dynamics and rail-level differences.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閘門浮力與輪載」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。","平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。","設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels.","Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route.","After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"b226-v15-19","title":"閘門浮力與輪載：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閘門浮力與輪載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。比較各輪反力總和與扣除浮力後的重量，另檢查最大輪載是否隨軌道高點移動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verify total reaction equilibrium before evaluating maximum individual loads rather than averages. Compare summed reactions with weight minus buoyancy and check whether maximum wheel load follows rail high spots. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以閘門浮力與輪載編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gate buoyancy and wheel loads, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verify total reaction equilibrium before evaluating maximum individual loads rather than averages.","failure":"注意干擾：某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。比較各輪反力總和與扣除浮力後的重量，另檢查最大輪載是否隨軌道高點移動。","textEn":"Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verify total reaction equilibrium before evaluating maximum individual loads rather than averages. Compare summed reactions with weight minus buoyancy and check whether maximum wheel load follows rail high spots.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以閘門浮力與輪載編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gate buoyancy and wheel loads, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verify total reaction equilibrium before evaluating maximum individual loads rather than averages.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閘門浮力與輪載」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。","充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact.","Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將輪載或軸承應變與水位、門位一起比對，檢查軌道高程和各輪接觸；以總反力守恆確認量測，再評估最大輪載而非平均值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wheel loads or bearing strains with water level and position, checking rail elevation and wheel contact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"b226-v15-20","title":"閘門浮力與輪載：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閘門浮力與輪載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。","textEn":"A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閘門浮力與輪載」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gate buoyancy and wheel loads\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"b226-v15-21","title":"管路快速減速壓峰：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「管路快速減速壓峰」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"充洩水管路的速度改變會形成壓力波，反射邊界和含氣量決定波速與衰減。Joukowsky式適合快速改變的初估，慢速閥動作須用歷時模型。 假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。 若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。把壓力計阻尼造成的平滑當成真實衰減也會低估荷載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「管路快速減速壓峰」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Velocity changes in filling conduits create pressure waves whose speed and decay depend on boundaries and air content. Joukowsky gives a rapid-change estimate; slower valve motion requires time-dependent analysis. Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting. Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. Sensor damping mistaken for physical decay can also underestimate the actual transient load. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting.","failure":"常見誤解：「慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「管路快速減速壓峰」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-21-k1","title":"管路快速減速壓峰","titleEn":"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure","text":"充洩水管路的速度改變會形成壓力波，反射邊界和含氣量決定波速與衰減。Joukowsky式適合快速改變的初估，慢速閥動作須用歷時模型。","textEn":"Velocity changes in filling conduits create pressure waves whose speed and decay depend on boundaries and air content. Joukowsky gives a rapid-change estimate; slower valve motion requires time-dependent analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「管路快速減速壓峰」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure\" is correct?","options":["充洩水管路的速度改變會形成壓力波，反射邊界和含氣量決定波速與衰減。","慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Velocity changes in filling conduits create pressure waves whose speed and decay depend on boundaries and air content.","A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"充洩水管路的速度改變會形成壓力波，反射邊界和含氣量決定波速與衰減。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Velocity changes in filling conduits create pressure waves whose speed and decay depend on boundaries and air content. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"b226-v15-22","title":"管路快速減速壓峰：定量估算","titleEn":"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「管路快速減速壓峰」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「管路快速減速壓峰」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa。","節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting.","A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、波速800 m/s、速度減少0.3 m/s且變化快於2L/a，Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa；非閥門操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume density 1000 kg/m³, wave speed 800 m/s and velocity change 0.3 m/s occurring faster than 2L/a. Δp=ρaΔv=240 kPa, not a valve operating setting. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"b226-v15-23","title":"管路快速減速壓峰：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「管路快速減速壓峰」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。以壓波往返時間核對閥動作快慢分類，並用多站到達時差反算有效波速。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verify adequate sampling and distinguish vapor cavities from the single-phase elastic model. Compare valve movement time with wave round-trip time and infer effective wave speed from multi-station arrival differences. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以管路快速減速壓峰編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rapid conduit deceleration pressure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verify adequate sampling and distinguish vapor cavities from the single-phase elastic model.","failure":"注意干擾：若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。以壓波往返時間核對閥動作快慢分類，並用多站到達時差反算有效波速。","textEn":"Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verify adequate sampling and distinguish vapor cavities from the single-phase elastic model. Compare valve movement time with wave round-trip time and infer effective wave speed from multi-station arrival differences.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以管路快速減速壓峰編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rapid conduit deceleration pressure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verify adequate sampling and distinguish vapor cavities from the single-phase elastic model.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「管路快速減速壓峰」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。","核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.","Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對管長、波速和動作歷時，再比較多點壓力到達時間與反射；檢查記錄取樣率足以看到波峰，並辨識氣穴與單相彈性模型的差別。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check pipe length, wave speed and movement duration, comparing pressure arrival and reflection at several locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"b226-v15-24","title":"管路快速減速壓峰：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「管路快速減速壓峰」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rapid conduit deceleration pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。把壓力計阻尼造成的平滑當成真實衰減也會低估荷載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. Sensor damping mistaken for physical decay can also underestimate the actual transient load. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把壓力計阻尼造成的平滑當成真實衰減也會低估荷載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sensor damping mistaken for physical decay can also underestimate the actual transient load.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。把壓力計阻尼造成的平滑當成真實衰減也會低估荷載。","textEn":"Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. Sensor damping mistaken for physical decay can also underestimate the actual transient load.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管路快速減速壓峰」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rapid conduit deceleration pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若壓力降至汽化壓以下，水柱分離後再碰撞可能產生不同峰值，單次線性式失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Column separation below vapor pressure and subsequent recombination can create different peaks, invalidating a single linear estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":7},{"id":"b226-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「混凝土溫差拘束」與「船底餘裕與沉降量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Concrete thermal restraint\" and \"Under-keel clearance and squat\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v15-25","title":"混凝土溫差拘束：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Concrete thermal restraint: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「混凝土溫差拘束」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete thermal restraint” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。只看最高溫度會漏掉冷卻過程的拉應力。 假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。 表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土溫差拘束」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks. Crack risk depends on restraint and developing early-age strength, so peak temperature alone misses tensile demand during cooling. Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Stress REαΔT=1.5 MPa, an elastic estimate without creep relaxation. Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete thermal restraint” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混凝土溫差拘束」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concrete thermal restraint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-25-k1","title":"混凝土溫差拘束","titleEn":"Concrete thermal restraint","text":"大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。只看最高溫度會漏掉冷卻過程的拉應力。","textEn":"Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks. Crack risk depends on restraint and developing early-age strength, so peak temperature alone misses tensile demand during cooling.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土溫差拘束」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concrete thermal restraint\" is correct?","options":["兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。","大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。","平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。"],"optionsEn":["Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk.","Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks.","Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"b226-v15-26","title":"混凝土溫差拘束：定量估算","titleEn":"Concrete thermal restraint: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混凝土溫差拘束」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete thermal restraint” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Stress REαΔT=1.5 MPa, an elastic estimate without creep relaxation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Stress REαΔT=1.5 MPa, an elastic estimate without creep relaxation.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土溫差拘束」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concrete thermal restraint\", which statement holds?","options":["設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。","充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.","Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"b226-v15-27","title":"混凝土溫差拘束：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete thermal restraint: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混凝土溫差拘束」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete thermal restraint” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。以齡期相符的模數與拉伸資料重新計算，檢查溫降、拘束與開裂時間是否一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Distinguish internal gradients from overall restraint and use material tests to update modulus and curing boundaries. Recalculate using age-matched modulus and tensile data and check consistency between cooling, restraint and observed crack timing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以混凝土溫差拘束編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for concrete thermal restraint, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Distinguish internal gradients from overall restraint and use material tests to update modulus and curing boundaries.","failure":"注意干擾：表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。以齡期相符的模數與拉伸資料重新計算，檢查溫降、拘束與開裂時間是否一致。","textEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Distinguish internal gradients from overall restraint and use material tests to update modulus and curing boundaries. Recalculate using age-matched modulus and tensile data and check consistency between cooling, restraint and observed crack timing.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以混凝土溫差拘束編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for concrete thermal restraint, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Distinguish internal gradients from overall restraint and use material tests to update modulus and curing boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土溫差拘束」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concrete thermal restraint\"?","options":["將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。"],"optionsEn":["Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將核心與表面溫度、接縫位移和齡期強度同步比較，辨認內外溫差與整體拘束；使用實際材料試驗修正模數，保留養護期間邊界。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures, joint movement and age-dependent strength synchronously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"b226-v15-28","title":"混凝土溫差拘束：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concrete thermal restraint: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混凝土溫差拘束」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete thermal restraint” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。","textEn":"Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土溫差拘束」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concrete thermal restraint\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。","平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop.","Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"b226-v15-29","title":"船底餘裕與沉降量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance and squat: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「船底餘裕與沉降量」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Under-keel clearance and squat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船底淨空由水深減吃水和動態變化決定，載重、鹽度和航速都會影響結果。幾何餘裕不是可直接使用的航行餘裕，須分列波動與量測不確定度。 假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。 沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。若把固定吃水值用於所有載重與水質，會產生不實的可用餘裕。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船底餘裕與沉降量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Under-keel clearance subtracts draft and dynamic effects from depth, with loading, salinity and speed all relevant. Geometric clearance differs from usable navigation margin, requiring separate motion and measurement allowances. Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m. Available margin is 16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m, with all values assumed. A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. Fixed draft across different loads and water conditions creates a misleading available margin. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Under-keel clearance and squat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「船底餘裕與沉降量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Under-keel clearance and squat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-29-k1","title":"船底餘裕與沉降量","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance and squat","text":"船底淨空由水深減吃水和動態變化決定，載重、鹽度和航速都會影響結果。幾何餘裕不是可直接使用的航行餘裕，須分列波動與量測不確定度。","textEn":"Under-keel clearance subtracts draft and dynamic effects from depth, with loading, salinity and speed all relevant. Geometric clearance differs from usable navigation margin, requiring separate motion and measurement allowances.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「船底餘裕與沉降量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Under-keel clearance and squat\" is correct?","options":["平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。","百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。","船底淨空由水深減吃水和動態變化決定，載重、鹽度和航速都會影響結果。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route.","Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.","Under-keel clearance subtracts draft and dynamic effects from depth, with loading, salinity and speed all relevant."],"answer":2,"explanation":"船底淨空由水深減吃水和動態變化決定，載重、鹽度和航速都會影響結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Under-keel clearance subtracts draft and dynamic effects from depth, with loading, salinity and speed all relevant. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"b226-v15-30","title":"船底餘裕與沉降量：定量估算","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance and squat: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「船底餘裕與沉降量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Under-keel clearance and squat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m. Available margin is 16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m, with all values assumed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m. Available margin is 16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m, with all values assumed.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「船底餘裕與沉降量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Under-keel clearance and squat\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m。","節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。","閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m.","A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.","A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設水深16 m、吃水14.5 m、動態下沉0.25 m、其他保留0.35 m，可用餘裕16−14.5−0.25−0.35=0.90 m；全部為假設。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume depth 16 m, draft 14.5 m, squat 0.25 m and other allowance 0.35 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"b226-v15-31","title":"船底餘裕與沉降量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance and squat: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「船底餘裕與沉降量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Under-keel clearance and squat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。對測深誤差和吃水變化分別作敏感度分析，核對最不利位置而非只有代表斷面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Retain trim, motion and sounding uncertainty separately to avoid duplicated or omitted deductions. Test sounding-error and draft sensitivities separately and assess the controlling location rather than one representative section. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以船底餘裕與沉降量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for under-keel clearance and squat, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Retain trim, motion and sounding uncertainty separately to avoid duplicated or omitted deductions.","failure":"注意干擾：沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。對測深誤差和吃水變化分別作敏感度分析，核對最不利位置而非只有代表斷面。","textEn":"Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Retain trim, motion and sounding uncertainty separately to avoid duplicated or omitted deductions. Test sounding-error and draft sensitivities separately and assess the controlling location rather than one representative section.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以船底餘裕與沉降量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for under-keel clearance and squat, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Retain trim, motion and sounding uncertainty separately to avoid duplicated or omitted deductions.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「船底餘裕與沉降量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Under-keel clearance and squat\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。","平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth.","Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group."],"answer":1,"explanation":"統一水深、吃水和潮位的基準與時刻，查底床最高點而非平均深度；將船體縱傾、波動和測深誤差分別保存，避免重複或遺漏扣減。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align depth, draft and tide references and times, checking highest bed points rather than mean depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"b226-v15-32","title":"船底餘裕與沉降量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance and squat: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「船底餘裕與沉降量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Under-keel clearance and squat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。若把固定吃水值用於所有載重與水質，會產生不實的可用餘裕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. Fixed draft across different loads and water conditions creates a misleading available margin. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把固定吃水值用於所有載重與水質，會產生不實的可用餘裕。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Fixed draft across different loads and water conditions creates a misleading available margin.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均水深足夠就能保證整條船底通道都有足夠淨空。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate mean depth guarantees clearance along the entire hull route.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。若把固定吃水值用於所有載重與水質，會產生不實的可用餘裕。","textEn":"A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. Fixed draft across different loads and water conditions creates a misleading available margin.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「船底餘裕與沉降量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Under-keel clearance and squat\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。","沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.","A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉積高點可能在水深平均值仍足夠時造成局部淺區，密度改變亦會增加吃水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A deposit high spot can create a shallow patch despite adequate mean depth, and density changes alter draft. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":8},{"id":"b226-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「回用率與淨淡水耗用」與「故障停航與水源緩衝」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use\" and \"Outage backlog and water reserve\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b226-v15-33","title":"回用率與淨淡水耗用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「回用率與淨淡水耗用」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回用百分比必須有明確分母，閘室交換量、從湖取水量與全年水源消耗並不相同。漏流、蒸發與鹽分管理可能改變系統邊界內的淨耗用。 假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。 只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。閘次船型差異和不完整循環又可能造成看似改善卻不可比較的績效數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回用率與淨淡水耗用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A reuse percentage requires an explicit denominator. Chamber exchange, lake withdrawal and annual water-resource consumption differ, while leakage, evaporation and salinity management can change net use within the chosen boundary. Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³. Freshwater makeup is (1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³, not an official lockage demand. Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. Vessel differences and incomplete cycles can produce apparently improved performance values that are not comparable across the measurement period. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回用率與淨淡水耗用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-33-k1","title":"回用率與淨淡水耗用","titleEn":"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use","text":"回用百分比必須有明確分母，閘室交換量、從湖取水量與全年水源消耗並不相同。漏流、蒸發與鹽分管理可能改變系統邊界內的淨耗用。","textEn":"A reuse percentage requires an explicit denominator. Chamber exchange, lake withdrawal and annual water-resource consumption differ, while leakage, evaporation and salinity management can change net use within the chosen boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回用率與淨淡水耗用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use\" is correct?","options":["回用百分比必須有明確分母，閘室交換量、從湖取水量與全年水源消耗並不相同。","百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。","設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。"],"optionsEn":["A reuse percentage requires an explicit denominator.","Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.","After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput."],"answer":0,"explanation":"回用百分比必須有明確分母，閘室交換量、從湖取水量與全年水源消耗並不相同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A reuse percentage requires an explicit denominator. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":57},{"id":"b226-v15-34","title":"回用率與淨淡水耗用：定量估算","titleEn":"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回用率與淨淡水耗用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³. Freshwater makeup is (1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³, not an official lockage demand. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³. Freshwater makeup is (1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³, not an official lockage demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回用率與淨淡水耗用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use\", which statement holds?","options":["充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³。","兩側水面相同時，不同密度水體就不會互相交換。"],"optionsEn":["Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³.","Different-density waters stop exchanging when their surface elevations are equal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一次交換量200000 m³、回用率0.6、另有損失5000 m³，淡水補充=(1−0.6)200000+5000=85000 m³；非官方每次用水量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume cycle exchange 200000 m³, reuse fraction 0.6 and other losses 5000 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":58},{"id":"b226-v15-35","title":"回用率與淨淡水耗用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回用率與淨淡水耗用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。以完整週期的池位回復確認沒有借用下一循環庫容，將蒸發漏流另列為水源負擔。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Cover a complete cycle and state whether vessel displacement is included in the metering boundary. Confirm basin-level recovery over a complete cycle to exclude borrowing future storage and list evaporation and leakage separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以回用率與淨淡水耗用編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for reuse ratio and net freshwater use, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Cover a complete cycle and state whether vessel displacement is included in the metering boundary.","failure":"注意干擾：只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。以完整週期的池位回復確認沒有借用下一循環庫容，將蒸發漏流另列為水源負擔。","textEn":"Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Cover a complete cycle and state whether vessel displacement is included in the metering boundary. Confirm basin-level recovery over a complete cycle to exclude borrowing future storage and list evaporation and leakage separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以回用率與淨淡水耗用編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for reuse ratio and net freshwater use, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Cover a complete cycle and state whether vessel displacement is included in the metering boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回用率與淨淡水耗用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","慢速改變流量也必須產生完整的快速水錘壓峰。","為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A slow flow change must generate the full rapid-waterhammer pressure peak.","Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為每個水量畫清楚來源與去向，將暫存池、外海與淡水湖分成控制體；確認計量時間覆蓋完整循環，並說明船舶排水體積是否納入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map every water source and destination, separating basins, sea and freshwater lake into control volumes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":59},{"id":"b226-v15-36","title":"回用率與淨淡水耗用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回用率與淨淡水耗用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reuse ratio and net freshwater use” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。閘次船型差異和不完整循環又可能造成看似改善卻不可比較的績效數字。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. Vessel differences and incomplete cycles can produce apparently improved performance values that are not comparable across the measurement period. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閘次船型差異和不完整循環又可能造成看似改善卻不可比較的績效數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Vessel differences and incomplete cycles can produce apparently improved performance values that are not comparable across the measurement period.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「百分之六十回用一定讓全年淡水需求直接減少六成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sixty percent reuse necessarily reduces annual freshwater demand by sixty percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。閘次船型差異和不完整循環又可能造成看似改善卻不可比較的績效數字。","textEn":"Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. Vessel differences and incomplete cycles can produce apparently improved performance values that are not comparable across the measurement period.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回用率與淨淡水耗用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reuse ratio and net freshwater use\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。"],"optionsEn":["Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只引用回用率而省略其他損失，會把單次水力效率誤當流域節水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Quoting reuse alone confuses cycle hydraulics with watershed savings. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":60},{"id":"b226-v15-37","title":"故障停航與水源緩衝：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outage backlog and water reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「故障停航與水源緩衝」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outage backlog and water reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。系統復原應同時盤點通行和水量資源。 假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。 機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「故障停航與水源緩衝」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. Recovery therefore requires both transit and water-resource accounting. Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Extra demand is 680000 m³; allocation 170000 m³/day requires at least four days, excluding new arrivals. Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outage backlog and water reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「故障停航與水源緩衝」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Outage backlog and water reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-37-k1","title":"故障停航與水源緩衝","titleEn":"Outage backlog and water reserve","text":"容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。系統復原應同時盤點通行和水量資源。","textEn":"Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. Recovery therefore requires both transit and water-resource accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「故障停航與水源緩衝」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outage backlog and water reserve\" is correct?","options":["設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。","容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。","節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.","Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time.","A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water."],"answer":1,"explanation":"容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":61},{"id":"b226-v15-38","title":"故障停航與水源緩衝：定量估算","titleEn":"Outage backlog and water reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「故障停航與水源緩衝」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outage backlog and water reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Extra demand is 680000 m³; allocation 170000 m³/day requires at least four days, excluding new arrivals. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Extra demand is 680000 m³; allocation 170000 m³/day requires at least four days, excluding new arrivals.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「故障停航與水源緩衝」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outage backlog and water reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["閘室平均水位平穩就表示船首船尾沒有壓力差。","平均輪載足夠低就能排除任何個別輪組超載。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³。"],"optionsEn":["A steady mean chamber level means there is no bow-to-stern pressure difference.","Low mean wheel load rules out overload in every individual wheel group.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":62},{"id":"b226-v15-39","title":"故障停航與水源緩衝：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outage backlog and water reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「故障停航與水源緩衝」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outage backlog and water reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。將每天新增通行需求加入排程重算，檢查水源可分配量是否仍足以逐日減少積壓。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Separate confirmed supply constraints from adjustable schedules and check that demands are not counted twice. Add newly arriving demand to the daily schedule and check whether allocated water still reduces the backlog each day. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以故障停航與水源緩衝編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for outage backlog and water reserve, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Separate confirmed supply constraints from adjustable schedules and check that demands are not counted twice.","failure":"注意干擾：機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。將每天新增通行需求加入排程重算，檢查水源可分配量是否仍足以逐日減少積壓。","textEn":"Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Separate confirmed supply constraints from adjustable schedules and check that demands are not counted twice. Add newly arriving demand to the daily schedule and check whether allocated water still reduces the backlog each day.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以故障停航與水源緩衝編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for outage backlog and water reserve, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Separate confirmed supply constraints from adjustable schedules and check that demands are not counted twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「故障停航與水源緩衝」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outage backlog and water reserve\"?","options":["用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two blocks with the same peak temperature have identical thermal-cracking risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用匿名化通行隊列、可分配水量與其他取水用途建立共同日曆；將已確認的供水約束和可調整排程分開，核對每項需求是否重複計列。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a common calendar of anonymous transit queues, available water and other withdrawals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":63},{"id":"b226-v15-40","title":"故障停航與水源緩衝：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outage backlog and water reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b226-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「故障停航與水源緩衝」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outage backlog and water reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b226-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。","textEn":"Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b226-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-acp-open","v7-panama-basins","v7-panama-expanded","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「故障停航與水源緩衝」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outage backlog and water reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。","節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible.","A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water."],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":64}],"order":9}],"curriculumVersion":7,"enrichmentVersion":15,"learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","v15Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"water-lock","architectureNodes":[["雙池水位均衡","Equalization between two pools"],["縱向水面坡度推力","Longitudinal water-slope force"],["閘門浮力與輪載","Gate buoyancy and wheel loads"],["混凝土溫差拘束","Concrete thermal restraint"],["故障停航與水源緩衝","Outage backlog and water reserve"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]]},"v15Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 均衡水位的單參數比較固定閘室面積20000 m²、初始水位10 m及池面積10000 m²，只將池初始水位由4升至6 m。同基準下最終水位由8 m升為(20000×10+10000×6)/30000=8.6667 m；池升2 m只令共同水位升0.6667 m。這是兩固定面積水體的封閉體積平衡，未計船舶移動、漏水或外部補水。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. For equalization sensitivity, keep chamber area 20000 m², initial chamber level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² fixed, raising only initial basin level from 4 m to 6 m. On the common datum, final level rises from 8 m to (20000×10+10000×6)/30000=8.6667 m. A 2 m basin change raises the common level only 0.6667 m. This closed-volume comparison excludes vessel movement, leakage and external supply.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"節水池耦合、非恆定充洩水與滾動閘門的定量深化","focusEn":"Quantitative extension of basin coupling, unsteady filling and rolling-gate mechanics"}},{"id":"a025","title":"背面供電網路製程","titleEn":"Backside power-delivery processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco","v7-bspdn-demo","v7-bspdn-flow","v7-bspdn-building","v7-bspdn-esd","v7-bspdn-intel","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"拆解前後側供電分工、鍵合與薄化、奈米通孔連接，再以壓降、熱與可靠度證據審查整合方案。","summaryEn":"Separate signal and power routing, plan bonding, thinning and backside contacts, then review the integration using voltage-drop, thermal and reliability evidence.","scope":"依公開原理編寫的四階段、24 個教學工作包；每步需交出模型、判讀或驗證紀錄。數值練習為自訂教學案例，不是廠商製程配方、現場操作許可或專業設計認證。","scopeEn":"Four stages and 24 educational work packages based on public principles. Each step produces a model, interpretation or verification record. Numerical exercises are hypothetical, not manufacturer recipes, field operating authorization or professional design certification.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["訊號層","元件","背面接觸","電源網路","封裝"],"labelsEn":["Signal layers","Devices","Backside contacts","Power network","Package"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a025-stage01","order":1,"title":"系統需求與電源路徑","titleEn":"Requirements and power paths","description":"先建立電源與訊號、電阻與暫態的不同證據。","descriptionEn":"Separate power from signals and resistive from transient evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a025-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出電源與訊號的兩條路徑","titleEn":"Draw separate power and signal paths","objective":"區分供電網路與訊號傳播。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish power distribution from signal propagation.","instruction":"先畫封裝、正面金屬及電晶體；用另一色畫背面電源進入點；追蹤 VDD 與 VSS 完整回路；圈出仍留在正面的訊號。","instructionEn":"Sketch the package, frontside metals and transistor; add backside power entry in another color; trace the complete VDD and VSS loop; circle signals remaining on the front.","observation":"供電轉到背面後，訊號層並未消失。","observationEn":"Moving power does not eliminate signal layers.","failure":"若只畫 VDD，補回回流路徑後再分析壓降。","failureEn":"If only VDD is drawn, add the return path before analyzing drop.","check":"交出含兩種網路與回流的截面。","checkEn":"Submit a section with both networks and the return path.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-01-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"背面供電改變配線分工，不代表把所有訊號移到背面。","textEn":"Backside power changes routing allocation; it does not move every signal backside."},{"id":"a025-v7-01-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"電壓是兩點之差，供電與回流都影響元件實際供應。","textEn":"Voltage is a difference between points; both supply and return affect the device."}],"quiz":{"question":"背面供電截面應保留什麼？","questionEn":"What should a backside-power section retain?","options":["正面訊號及完整供電回路。","只有單一 VDD 箭頭。","完全刪除正面互連。"],"optionsEn":["Frontside signals and the complete power loop.","Only one VDD arrow.","All frontside interconnect removed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"正面訊號及完整供電回路。 背面供電改變配線分工，不代表把所有訊號移到背面。","explanationEn":"Frontside signals and the complete power loop. Backside power changes routing allocation; it does not move every signal backside."}},{"id":"a025-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-01"],"title":"比較三種電源軌配置","titleEn":"Compare three rail configurations","objective":"把幾何改善與供電改善分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate geometry gains from delivery gains.","instruction":"畫傳統正面、正面連接埋藏軌、背面連接埋藏軌三圖；逐圖標出接觸點；比較訊號可用空間；列出每種新增介面。","instructionEn":"Draw conventional frontside, frontside-connected buried rails and backside-connected buried rails; mark contacts; compare signal space; list added interfaces.","observation":"埋藏軌與背面供電不是完全同義。","observationEn":"Buried rails and backside delivery are not synonymous.","failure":"若三圖只換顏色，重新追蹤封裝到元件的連通性。","failureEn":"If only colors differ, retrace connectivity from package to device.","check":"表格能分辨軌位置與供電進入側。","checkEn":"The table distinguishes rail position from power-entry side.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-02-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"電源軌位置和電源進入側是兩個設計選項。","textEn":"Rail location and power-entry side are separate choices."},{"id":"a025-v7-02-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"介面增加可能帶來新的對準與可靠度要求。","textEn":"Additional interfaces can create alignment and reliability requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"有埋藏電源軌就一定由背面供電嗎？","questionEn":"Do buried rails necessarily imply backside delivery?","options":["一定，兩者是同一名詞。","不一定，須追蹤電源連接。","只要有埋藏軌便沒有接觸電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; the terms are identical.","No; trace the power connection.","Buried rails eliminate contact resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不一定，須追蹤電源連接。 電源軌位置和電源進入側是兩個設計選項。","explanationEn":"No; trace the power connection. Rail location and power-entry side are separate choices."}},{"id":"a025-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-02"],"title":"建立直流壓降帳本","titleEn":"Build a DC voltage-drop ledger","objective":"用簡化電阻網路定位主要損耗。","objectiveEn":"Locate losses with a simplified resistive network.","instruction":"自行設定三段串聯電阻與電流並註明是假設；分別計算 I×R；把各段壓降相加；比較加寬其中一段前後結果。","instructionEn":"Choose hypothetical current and three series resistances; calculate each I×R drop; sum the drops; compare widening one segment.","observation":"改善最小電阻段不一定改善整體瓶頸。","observationEn":"Improving the smallest resistance may barely change the bottleneck.","failure":"勿把示例電阻當成某節點的實測值；補上假設標籤。","failureEn":"Do not present example resistances as measurements of a named node.","check":"每段單位、總壓降及最大貢獻可追溯。","checkEn":"Units, total drop and largest contributor are traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-03-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"串聯路徑的電阻貢獻需逐段相加。","textEn":"Series-path resistance contributions add."},{"id":"a025-v7-03-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"R 的變化與 I 的變化都會改變壓降，不能只比較線寬。","textEn":"Both resistance and current change drop; width alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪一段先值得改善？","questionEn":"Which segment warrants attention first?","options":["顏色最深的段。","永遠是最靠近封裝的一段。","在同一電流條件下壓降最大的段。"],"optionsEn":["The darkest-colored segment.","Always the segment nearest the package.","The largest-drop segment at the same current."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在同一電流條件下壓降最大的段。 串聯路徑的電阻貢獻需逐段相加。","explanationEn":"The largest-drop segment at the same current. Series-path resistance contributions add."}},{"id":"a025-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-03"],"title":"分開靜態壓降與瞬態下陷","titleEn":"Separate static drop from transient droop","objective":"辨識負載突變造成的時間效應。","objectiveEn":"Identify time-dependent effects of load changes.","instruction":"畫穩定負載與階躍負載兩條曲線；標出電流變化時刻；把穩態壓降與短暫谷值分別量測；比較兩種去耦配置的假設波形。","instructionEn":"Draw steady and stepped loads; mark the current transition; measure steady drop separately from the temporary minimum; compare two hypothetical decoupling waveforms.","observation":"相同直流電阻仍可能有不同瞬態谷值。","observationEn":"Equal DC resistance can coexist with different transient minima.","failure":"只用平均電壓會漏掉谷值；保留時間尺度。","failureEn":"Average voltage can conceal minima; retain the time scale.","check":"報告同時列出穩態值、最小值及恢復時間。","checkEn":"Report steady value, minimum and recovery time.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-04-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"電源網路有寄生電感與電容，暫態不能只用電阻描述。","textEn":"Parasitic inductance and capacitance make transient behavior more than resistance."},{"id":"a025-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"不同量測頻寬會改變可見的快速事件。","textEn":"Measurement bandwidth changes which fast events are visible."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均電壓相同能證明瞬態相同嗎？","questionEn":"Does equal average voltage prove equal transients?","options":["不能，需比較谷值與時間響應。","能，平均值涵蓋全部頻率。","能，只要晶片尺寸相同。"],"optionsEn":["No; compare minima and timing.","Yes; averages capture every frequency.","Yes, if die size matches."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，需比較谷值與時間響應。 電源網路有寄生電感與電容，暫態不能只用電阻描述。","explanationEn":"No; compare minima and timing. Parasitic inductance and capacitance make transient behavior more than resistance."}},{"id":"a025-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-04"],"title":"檢查標準元件配線容量","titleEn":"Inspect standard-cell routing capacity","objective":"評估釋放電源軌空間的實際收益。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate usable space released by power routing.","instruction":"畫四個相鄰標準元件；分開標記電源軌與訊號軌；移動電源後重新連接訊號；記錄仍因通孔或禁佈區受限的位置。","instructionEn":"Draw four adjacent cells; mark power and signal tracks separately; reroute signals after relocating power; record remaining via and keep-out constraints.","observation":"可用面積增加不等於所有線都能順利佈完。","observationEn":"More area does not guarantee routability.","failure":"若只按面積比例推算頻率，增加實際線長與擁塞比較。","failureEn":"If frequency is inferred from area alone, add route-length and congestion checks.","check":"交付前後配置及一處仍未解決的擁塞。","checkEn":"Submit before/after layouts and one remaining congestion point.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-05-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"設計與技術協同最佳化需同時考慮元件與配線限制。","textEn":"Design-technology co-optimization considers cells and routing together."},{"id":"a025-v7-05-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"面積、速度、功耗的比較必須使用一致工作負載與限制。","textEn":"Area, speed and power comparisons need matching workloads and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"釋放面積後應再驗證什麼？","questionEn":"What should be checked after space is released?","options":["只看空白面積就宣告性能提升。","訊號能否佈通以及路徑延遲。","刪除所有禁佈區以完成比較。"],"optionsEn":["Declare performance from blank area alone.","Signal routability and path delay.","Remove all keep-outs to finish comparison."],"answer":1,"explanation":"訊號能否佈通以及路徑延遲。 設計與技術協同最佳化需同時考慮元件與配線限制。","explanationEn":"Signal routability and path delay. Design-technology co-optimization considers cells and routing together."}},{"id":"a025-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-intel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-05"],"title":"選擇測試載具與對照組","titleEn":"Select test vehicles and controls","objective":"把新供電技術與電晶體改版的影響分離。","objectiveEn":"Separate delivery changes from transistor changes.","instruction":"列出電晶體、電源網路及工作負載三項變因；設計只改供電的對照；指定前後量測；記錄尚不能歸因的差異。","instructionEn":"List transistor, delivery network and workload variables; design a delivery-only comparison; specify before/after measurements; record unattributable differences.","observation":"同時更改多項技術會混淆原因。","observationEn":"Changing several technologies confounds attribution.","failure":"若對照的尺寸與溫度不同，先統一條件再比較。","failureEn":"Match geometry and temperature before comparing controls.","check":"一張實驗矩陣說明固定、改變及量測項。","checkEn":"Provide a matrix of fixed, changed and measured items.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-06-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"測試載具可先驗證單一整合風險。","textEn":"A test vehicle can isolate an integration risk."},{"id":"a025-v7-06-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"研究晶片的改善不自動等於產品在所有負載下的改善。","textEn":"Test-chip gains are not automatic product gains under every workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"只想判斷背面供電效益，應如何設計？","questionEn":"How should a delivery-specific benefit be tested?","options":["同時更换架構與工作負載。","只挑表現最好的一筆數據。","保持其他主要變因一致。"],"optionsEn":["Change architecture and workload simultaneously.","Select only the best measurement.","Keep other major variables comparable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保持其他主要變因一致。 測試載具可先驗證單一整合風險。","explanationEn":"Keep other major variables comparable. A test vehicle can isolate an integration risk."}}]},{"id":"a025-stage02","order":2,"title":"鍵合、薄化與前後對準","titleEn":"Bonding, thinning and alignment","description":"用截面與誤差帳本理解背面加工的依存關係。","descriptionEn":"Use sections and error budgets to understand backside integration dependencies.","steps":[{"id":"a025-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-flow"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-06"],"title":"建立前後面方向與標記","titleEn":"Establish front/back orientation and marks","objective":"避免翻面後座標與極性誤判。","objectiveEn":"Avoid coordinate and polarity errors after flipping.","instruction":"畫俯視與截面基準；標出缺口與三個不對稱標記；紙上翻面後重標座標；追蹤同一 VDD 接點的位置。","instructionEn":"Draw plan and section references; add a notch and three asymmetric marks; relabel coordinates after a paper flip; track the same VDD contact.","observation":"翻轉與平面旋轉對圖案的影響不同。","observationEn":"A flip and an in-plane rotation transform patterns differently.","failure":"對稱標記無法辨認鏡像時，增加不對稱識別。","failureEn":"Add an asymmetric identifier if marks cannot distinguish mirroring.","check":"兩視圖間同一接點能唯一對應。","checkEn":"Each contact has one unambiguous cross-view match.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-07-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"背面加工需要將量測座標連回正面元件。","textEn":"Backside processing must relate measurements to frontside devices."},{"id":"a025-v7-07-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"標記本身也需在薄化及堆疊後可辨識。","textEn":"Marks must remain identifiable after thinning and stacking."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪種標記較能揭露翻面錯誤？","questionEn":"Which mark best exposes a flip error?","options":["可區分鏡像的不對稱標記。","完全均勻的圓。","沒有方向定義的網格。"],"optionsEn":["An asymmetric mark that distinguishes mirrors.","A uniform circle.","A grid without orientation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可區分鏡像的不對稱標記。 背面加工需要將量測座標連回正面元件。","explanationEn":"An asymmetric mark that distinguishes mirrors. Backside processing must relate measurements to frontside devices."}},{"id":"a025-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-flow"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-07"],"title":"規劃載板鍵合的支撐","titleEn":"Plan carrier-bond support","objective":"理解薄晶圓加工的機械邊界。","objectiveEn":"Understand mechanical boundaries during thin-wafer processing.","instruction":"畫主動晶圓與載板的接合面；標出後續加工施力位置；比較完全支撐與局部空隙；建立加工前空隙檢查清單。","instructionEn":"Draw active wafer and carrier interfaces; mark later loading locations; compare full support with a local void; create a pre-processing void check.","observation":"局部失去支撐可能造成厚度或應力異常。","observationEn":"A local support gap can produce thickness or stress anomalies.","failure":"不能以外側貼合外觀證明內部無空隙；指定適合的非破壞檢查。","failureEn":"Outer appearance does not establish void-free bonding; specify suitable nondestructive inspection.","check":"示意圖標明支撐、空隙與驗證位置。","checkEn":"Label support, voids and inspection positions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-08-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"載板提供薄化期間的機械支撐。","textEn":"A carrier provides support during thinning."},{"id":"a025-v7-08-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"鍵合平整度也會影響後續對準與量測。","textEn":"Bond geometry also affects later alignment and measurement."}],"quiz":{"question":"局部空隙最先影響哪種假設？","questionEn":"Which assumption is challenged by a local void?","options":["電晶體數量固定。","晶圓各處具有一致支撐。","所有訊號都在背面。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed transistor count.","Uniform support across the wafer.","All signals being backside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓各處具有一致支撐。 載板提供薄化期間的機械支撐。","explanationEn":"Uniform support across the wafer. A carrier provides support during thinning."}},{"id":"a025-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-flow"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-08"],"title":"分配薄化餘量","titleEn":"Allocate thinning margin","objective":"用最薄區而非平均值控制去除預算。","objectiveEn":"Budget removal using local minima, not only averages.","instruction":"建立九點假設厚度圖；列出粗去除、精修與終點餘量；逐點相減；標記最先失去餘量的區域。","instructionEn":"Create a hypothetical nine-point thickness map; allocate coarse removal, finishing and endpoint margin; subtract pointwise; mark the first region to lose margin.","observation":"平均厚度合格時仍可能有局部過薄。","observationEn":"Local over-thinning can occur despite an acceptable average.","failure":"若用單一平均值，回到位置配對的前後圖。","failureEn":"Replace an average-only analysis with paired spatial maps.","check":"每區剩餘量非負，且列出需重檢的極值。","checkEn":"Each region retains nonnegative margin and flagged extrema are listed.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-09-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"材料去除不可由後續拋光補回。","textEn":"Subsequent polishing cannot restore removed material."},{"id":"a025-v7-09-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"終點需符合元件與接觸設計，不是越薄越好。","textEn":"The endpoint must suit device and contact design; thinner is not always better."}],"quiz":{"question":"薄化應優先留意哪項？","questionEn":"What deserves priority during thinning review?","options":["照片最亮的區域。","僅全片平均加工時間。","局部最小剩餘厚度。"],"optionsEn":["The brightest photo region.","Only average processing time.","Minimum local remaining thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部最小剩餘厚度。 材料去除不可由後續拋光補回。","explanationEn":"Minimum local remaining thickness. Subsequent polishing cannot restore removed material."}},{"id":"a025-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-building"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-09"],"title":"辨認薄化終點證據","titleEn":"Identify thinning-endpoint evidence","objective":"區分厚度讀值與露出目標層。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish thickness readings from target-layer exposure.","instruction":"畫三種截面：未到、剛到與過度去除；為各截面選擇厚度或材料辨識證據；比較中心與邊緣結果；標示不能由光澤判定的部分。","instructionEn":"Draw under-thinned, target and over-thinned sections; choose thickness or material-identification evidence; compare center and edge; mark what gloss cannot establish.","observation":"幾何厚度與材料種類回答不同問題。","observationEn":"Geometry and material identity answer different questions.","failure":"未證實目標層前，不把時間到了當成終點。","failureEn":"Do not treat elapsed time as proof of target-layer exposure.","check":"三種截面各有可區分的量測判據。","checkEn":"Each section has a discriminating measurement criterion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-10-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"薄化流程需要可重複的終點指標。","textEn":"A thinning flow needs a reproducible endpoint indicator."},{"id":"a025-v7-10-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"量測需保留校正與空間範圍，才能比較不同區域。","textEn":"Calibration and spatial extent are needed to compare regions."}],"quiz":{"question":"只看加工時間可否證明已露出目標層？","questionEn":"Does processing time prove the target layer is exposed?","options":["不能，需材料或厚度證據。","可以，相同時間一定相同厚度。","可以，背面顏色一定唯一。"],"optionsEn":["No; material or thickness evidence is needed.","Yes; equal time guarantees equal thickness.","Yes; backside color is always unique."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，需材料或厚度證據。 薄化流程需要可重複的終點指標。","explanationEn":"No; material or thickness evidence is needed. A thinning flow needs a reproducible endpoint indicator."}},{"id":"a025-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-flow"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-10"],"title":"分解前後側對準誤差","titleEn":"Decompose front-to-back overlay error","objective":"辨認全片位移與局部形變。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish global offsets from local distortion.","instruction":"在九個位置畫設計與實測標記；先扣除共同平移；再比較旋轉與殘差；把局部不規則量保留為未解釋項。","instructionEn":"Draw designed and measured marks at nine sites; remove common translation; compare rotation and residuals; retain irregular local errors as unexplained.","observation":"消除平均偏差後仍可能有局部錯位。","observationEn":"Local misalignment can remain after average offset removal.","failure":"只報平均誤差可能抵消正負值；增加最大值與位置圖。","failureEn":"Signed errors can cancel in averages; add maxima and maps.","check":"提交原始、校正後及殘差三張圖。","checkEn":"Submit raw, corrected and residual maps.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-11-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"鍵合形變可能影響後續微影對準。","textEn":"Bond-induced distortion can affect later lithographic alignment."},{"id":"a025-v7-11-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"誤差預算應保留量測不確定度。","textEn":"An error budget should retain measurement uncertainty."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均位移為零代表全部對準嗎？","questionEn":"Does zero mean offset prove alignment everywhere?","options":["代表，正負誤差已物理消失。","不代表，局部殘差可能存在。","代表，旋轉不影响接點。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; opposite errors have physically vanished.","No; local residuals may remain.","Yes; rotation cannot affect contacts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不代表，局部殘差可能存在。 鍵合形變可能影響後續微影對準。","explanationEn":"No; local residuals may remain. Bond-induced distortion can affect later lithographic alignment."}},{"id":"a025-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo","v7-bspdn-building"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-11"],"title":"審查前段元件相容性","titleEn":"Review compatibility with frontside devices","objective":"將新增加工視為可驗證的應力來源。","objectiveEn":"Treat additional processing as a testable stress source.","instruction":"列出鍵合、薄化、背面加工三個節點；為每節點指定前後電性量測；固定量測溫度；對照一組未做新增流程的測試元件。","instructionEn":"List bonding, thinning and backside-processing checkpoints; assign before/after electrical tests; fix test temperature; compare controls without the added flow.","observation":"結果變化應與流程節點和量測條件關聯。","observationEn":"Changes should be related to process checkpoints and measurement conditions.","failure":"不同量測溫度可能製造假退化；先核對測試條件。","failureEn":"Different test temperatures can mimic degradation; verify conditions first.","check":"差異表能區分元件變化與量測漂移。","checkEn":"The comparison distinguishes device changes from measurement drift.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-12-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"未退化的研究展示只適用其測試條件。","textEn":"A non-degradation result applies to its tested conditions."},{"id":"a025-v7-12-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"前後配對比獨立批次平均更能定位變化。","textEn":"Paired before/after data can localize changes better than separate batch averages."}],"quiz":{"question":"某研究元件未退化，可否保證所有產品？","questionEn":"Does one non-degraded research device guarantee every product?","options":["可以，薄化永遠無影響。","可以，電性只由正面尺寸決定。","不能，需依各整合條件再驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; thinning never matters.","Yes; frontside dimensions alone determine behavior.","No; each integration needs verification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不能，需依各整合條件再驗證。 未退化的研究展示只適用其測試條件。","explanationEn":"No; each integration needs verification. A non-degradation result applies to its tested conditions."}}]},{"id":"a025-stage03","order":3,"title":"背面接觸與配線整合","titleEn":"Backside contacts and routing","description":"檢查連接、絕緣、熱路徑及製程相容性。","descriptionEn":"Review connectivity, insulation, thermal paths and process compatibility.","steps":[{"id":"a025-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-12"],"title":"比較埋藏軌與直接接觸","titleEn":"Compare buried-rail and direct-contact schemes","objective":"辨識不同背面連接策略的介面。","objectiveEn":"Identify interfaces in alternative backside connections.","instruction":"畫背面通孔接埋藏軌的路徑；另畫直接接近源汲極的概念路徑；比較落點面積；列出隔離與對準問題，避免混用兩種流程。","instructionEn":"Draw a backside via landing on a buried rail; sketch a conceptual direct device connection; compare landing areas; list isolation and alignment concerns without mixing flows.","observation":"不同方案可共享目標但不共享所有步驟。","observationEn":"Schemes can share goals without sharing every process step.","failure":"若移植一個方案的規則，先確認結構是否相同。","failureEn":"Check structural equivalence before transferring a rule.","check":"以介面表說明兩者共同點與差異。","checkEn":"Provide an interface table of similarities and differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-13-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"背面連接不是單一固定架構。","textEn":"Backside connectivity is not one fixed architecture."},{"id":"a025-v7-13-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"較短路徑仍需付出可製造性與隔離驗證。","textEn":"A shorter path still requires manufacturability and isolation verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩種方案可直接共用完整流程嗎？","questionEn":"Can both schemes use an identical complete flow?","options":["不能，落點與隔離結構不同。","可以，只需更改名稱。","可以，通孔不需要對準。"],"optionsEn":["No; landing and isolation structures differ.","Yes; rename the process.","Yes; vias need no alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，落點與隔離結構不同。 背面連接不是單一固定架構。","explanationEn":"No; landing and isolation structures differ. Backside connectivity is not one fixed architecture."}},{"id":"a025-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-13"],"title":"檢查通孔的絕緣與導通","titleEn":"Inspect via isolation and continuity","objective":"分開開路、短路與高阻三種缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Separate open, shorted and high-resistance faults.","instruction":"畫正常、填充空隙、側壁隔離破損三個截面；逐一預測導通與漏電結果；把電性結果配回截面；提出可排除另一原因的追加檢查。","instructionEn":"Draw sound, voided and insulation-damaged vias; predict continuity and leakage; match results to sections; propose a check excluding an alternative cause.","observation":"導通良好不代表與鄰近結構隔離良好。","observationEn":"Good continuity does not prove isolation from neighbors.","failure":"若只測通斷，增加隔離證據，不據此猜測材料配方。","failureEn":"Add isolation evidence to continuity testing; do not infer a recipe.","check":"缺陷矩陣包含導通、電阻及隔離三欄。","checkEn":"The fault matrix includes continuity, resistance and isolation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-14-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"導電路徑與隔離邊界需同時成立。","textEn":"The conductive path and insulating boundary must both work."},{"id":"a025-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"不同缺陷可能有相同單一測試結果。","textEn":"Different defects can share a single test signature."}],"quiz":{"question":"只測到導通足以放行嗎？","questionEn":"Is continuity alone enough for release?","options":["足夠，短路也算完成連接。","不足，還須檢查電阻及隔離。","足夠，漏電只發生於正面。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; a short also counts as connection.","No; resistance and isolation also matter.","Yes; leakage occurs only on the front."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不足，還須檢查電阻及隔離。 導電路徑與隔離邊界需同時成立。","explanationEn":"No; resistance and isolation also matter. The conductive path and insulating boundary must both work."}},{"id":"a025-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-14"],"title":"建立接觸電阻的比較","titleEn":"Build a contact-resistance comparison","objective":"避免把線路電阻誤當成接觸電阻。","objectiveEn":"Avoid confusing line resistance with contact resistance.","instruction":"畫兩端量測含引線的模型；再畫四端感測的概念配置；給引線相同假設增量；比較兩種讀值受影響程度。","instructionEn":"Draw a two-terminal model including leads; sketch conceptual four-terminal sensing; add the same hypothetical lead resistance; compare measurement sensitivity.","observation":"測到的總阻值可能含測試結構本身。","observationEn":"Measured resistance can include the test structure.","failure":"若沒有結構資訊，將結果標為總路徑阻值。","failureEn":"Without structure information, label the value total-path resistance.","check":"報告說明感測點與未扣除的寄生項。","checkEn":"State sensing locations and unremoved parasitics.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-15-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"接觸、通孔與金屬線共同形成路徑電阻。","textEn":"Contacts, vias and lines contribute to path resistance."},{"id":"a025-v7-15-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"量測方法影響可分離出的物理量。","textEn":"The measurement method determines which quantities can be isolated."}],"quiz":{"question":"兩端讀值增加一定代表接觸退化嗎？","questionEn":"Does higher two-terminal resistance prove contact degradation?","options":["一定，線路不可能有電阻。","一定，探針接觸永遠理想。","不一定，引線與通孔也可能改變。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; lines cannot have resistance.","Yes; probe contact is always ideal.","No; leads or vias may also have changed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不一定，引線與通孔也可能改變。 接觸、通孔與金屬線共同形成路徑電阻。","explanationEn":"No; leads or vias may also have changed. Contacts, vias and lines contribute to path resistance."}},{"id":"a025-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-15"],"title":"規劃背面金屬網路","titleEn":"Plan the backside metal network","objective":"平衡供電覆蓋、壓降與區域需求。","objectiveEn":"Balance power coverage, drop and regional demand.","instruction":"把假設晶片分成四個負載區；分配電源入口與網格；用相同總金屬量比較均勻與偏重熱點的方案；檢查最遠路徑。","instructionEn":"Divide a hypothetical die into four load zones; place entries and a grid; compare uniform and hotspot-weighted metal at equal total amount; inspect the longest path.","observation":"相同金屬總量可以有不同最差壓降。","observationEn":"Equal metal quantity can produce different worst-case drops.","failure":"若只最佳化平均值，重新檢查最高負載與邊角區。","failureEn":"After average-only optimization, revisit peak-load and corner regions.","check":"交出兩方案的負載圖、路徑與取捨。","checkEn":"Submit load maps, paths and tradeoffs for both schemes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-16-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"供電網路需配合負載空間分布。","textEn":"Power routing should match spatial load demand."},{"id":"a025-v7-16-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"電源入口位置與網格密度共同影響路徑。","textEn":"Entry locations and grid density jointly shape paths."}],"quiz":{"question":"相同總金屬量是否代表相同供電品質？","questionEn":"Does equal metal quantity imply equal delivery quality?","options":["否，配置與負載分布仍不同。","是，只要面積相同。","是，電流均勻分配與負載無關。"],"optionsEn":["No; topology and load distribution differ.","Yes, provided area matches.","Yes; current divides independently of load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"否，配置與負載分布仍不同。 供電網路需配合負載空間分布。","explanationEn":"No; topology and load distribution differ. Power routing should match spatial load demand."}},{"id":"a025-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-16"],"title":"追蹤去耦電容的作用","titleEn":"Trace the role of decoupling capacitance","objective":"把暫態支援與直流供電分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate transient support from steady power supply.","instruction":"畫負載、寄生路徑與去耦支路；假設同一電流脈衝；比較電容靠近與遠離負載的回路；標出寄生電感可能削弱效果的位置。","instructionEn":"Draw the load, parasitic path and decoupling branch; apply the same hypothetical current pulse; compare near and distant loops; mark where inductance weakens the response.","observation":"加大電容不能自動消除所有頻率的阻抗。","observationEn":"Increasing capacitance does not eliminate impedance at every frequency.","failure":"若只列電容量，補回連接路徑及頻率條件。","failureEn":"Add connection-path and frequency conditions to capacitance alone.","check":"以回路圖解释一種配置較有效的原因。","checkEn":"Explain a configuration advantage using a loop diagram.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-17-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"去耦提供短時間能量緩衝。","textEn":"Decoupling provides a short-term energy buffer."},{"id":"a025-v7-17-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"電容位置、連接寄生與負載頻譜同樣重要。","textEn":"Location, connection parasitics and load spectrum also matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"比較去耦方案時還需什麼？","questionEn":"What else matters when comparing decoupling?","options":["只有標稱電容量。","連接回路與頻率範圍。","只看電容顏色。"],"optionsEn":["Only nominal capacitance.","Connection loop and frequency range.","Only capacitor color."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連接回路與頻率範圍。 去耦提供短時間能量緩衝。","explanationEn":"Connection loop and frequency range. Decoupling provides a short-term energy buffer."}},{"id":"a025-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-esd"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-17"],"title":"審查散熱與薄基板","titleEn":"Review heat flow through a thin substrate","objective":"辨認薄化如何改變熱擴散路徑。","objectiveEn":"Identify how thinning changes heat spreading.","instruction":"畫元件、薄矽、背面金屬與封裝的熱路徑；分別標熱源及散熱邊界；比較兩種金屬分布；列出需模擬的局部溫升。","instructionEn":"Draw thermal paths through devices, thin silicon, backside metal and package; mark sources and sinks; compare two metal layouts; list local temperature rises needing simulation.","observation":"較低電阻不保證每個熱點都更冷。","observationEn":"Lower resistance does not guarantee every hotspot is cooler.","failure":"若宣稱薄化一定改善散熱，重新比較垂直與橫向路徑。","failureEn":"Revisit vertical and lateral paths before claiming thinning always improves cooling.","check":"熱路徑圖清楚區分電性收益與熱風險。","checkEn":"The diagram separates electrical benefits from thermal risks.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-18-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"薄化會改變原本矽基板的熱擴散能力。","textEn":"Thinning changes heat spreading through silicon."},{"id":"a025-v7-18-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"背面金屬可能提供新熱路徑，但需依幾何驗證。","textEn":"Backside metal can provide new thermal paths, subject to geometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"背面供電電阻降低就一定不過熱嗎？","questionEn":"Does lower delivery resistance rule out overheating?","options":["一定，電阻是唯一熱參數。","一定，薄矽沒有熱容量。","不一定，仍需熱模型與邊界條件。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; resistance is the only thermal parameter.","Yes; thin silicon has no heat capacity.","No; a thermal model and boundaries are needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不一定，仍需熱模型與邊界條件。 薄化會改變原本矽基板的熱擴散能力。","explanationEn":"No; a thermal model and boundaries are needed. Thinning changes heat spreading through silicon."}}]},{"id":"a025-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性、可靠度與設計審查","titleEn":"Electrical, reliability and design review","description":"以對照組、失效定位與交付證據判讀方案。","descriptionEn":"Evaluate the design through controls, failure localization and release evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a025-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-building"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-18"],"title":"建立晶圓內電性地圖","titleEn":"Build a within-wafer electrical map","objective":"區分共同偏移與局部缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Separate shared shifts from local faults.","instruction":"在九點地圖填假設通孔電阻；標記加工前後差值；比較邊緣與中心；檢查異常是否與厚度或對準殘差共位。","instructionEn":"Place hypothetical via resistances on a nine-site map; calculate before/after changes; compare edge and center; check co-location with thickness or overlay residuals.","observation":"相關位置可提出假說，不能單獨證明原因。","observationEn":"Spatial correlation suggests a hypothesis but does not prove causation.","failure":"若只挑單點最佳結果，恢復全圖及失敗點。","failureEn":"Restore the full map and failures if only the best point was selected.","check":"每個異常有位置、對照項及追加檢查。","checkEn":"Each anomaly has a location, comparator and follow-up check.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-19-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"位置配對能串接多種量測證據。","textEn":"Spatial pairing connects different measurement evidence."},{"id":"a025-v7-19-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"全片均值會掩蓋局部短路或高阻。","textEn":"A whole-wafer average can hide local shorts or high resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"異常電阻和薄區重疊代表什麼？","questionEn":"What does resistance/thickness co-location establish?","options":["值得追查的關聯，尚非因果證明。","已證明唯一失效原因。","所有其他量測都不必要。"],"optionsEn":["A useful association, not yet causation.","The sole failure cause is proven.","All other measurements are unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"值得追查的關聯，尚非因果證明。 位置配對能串接多種量測證據。","explanationEn":"A useful association, not yet causation. Spatial pairing connects different measurement evidence."}},{"id":"a025-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-19"],"title":"比較電流密度與可靠度","titleEn":"Compare current density and reliability","objective":"將截面瓶頸與壽命評估連起來。","objectiveEn":"Connect cross-sectional bottlenecks to reliability review.","instruction":"畫兩種不同截面接點；用假設 I/A 比較平均電流密度；圈出轉角及縮頸；列出溫度與時間需一併記錄的理由。","instructionEn":"Draw contacts with two cross-sections; compare hypothetical I/A averages; circle corners and necks; explain why temperature and duration must also be recorded.","observation":"平均密度未反映所有局部擁擠。","observationEn":"Average density does not capture all local crowding.","failure":"勿把簡化比值直接換成壽命；保留材料與幾何未知項。","failureEn":"Do not convert a simple ratio into lifetime; retain material and geometry uncertainties.","check":"結果只排序風險，不虛構產品壽命。","checkEn":"Results rank concerns without inventing product lifetime.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-20-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"較小有效截面在相同電流下有較高平均電流密度。","textEn":"A smaller effective area has higher average density at equal current."},{"id":"a025-v7-20-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"可靠度需要時間、溫度與局部結構的聯合證據。","textEn":"Reliability needs evidence about duration, temperature and local structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"I/A 可以直接算出產品壽命嗎？","questionEn":"Can I/A alone determine product lifetime?","options":["可以，與溫度無關。","不能，它只是風險分析的一部分。","可以，所有材料完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; temperature is irrelevant.","No; it is one part of the analysis.","Yes; all materials behave identically."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不能，它只是風險分析的一部分。 較小有效截面在相同電流下有較高平均電流密度。","explanationEn":"No; it is one part of the analysis. A smaller effective area has higher average density at equal current."}},{"id":"a025-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-esd"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-20"],"title":"規劃 ESD 保護路徑","titleEn":"Plan the ESD protection path","objective":"理解保護導通與熱承受是不同條件。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish protection conduction from thermal survival.","instruction":"畫正常供電與瞬態放電路徑；標出保護元件及回流；比較薄化前後的散熱體積；建立僅供模型審查的失效假說。","instructionEn":"Draw normal power and transient discharge paths; mark protection devices and return; compare heat-spreading volume before/after thinning; form model-review failure hypotheses.","observation":"保護元件能導通仍可能局部過熱。","observationEn":"A conducting protection device can still overheat locally.","failure":"不在真實晶片施加放電；用公開原理及假設模型討論。","failureEn":"Do not discharge real chips; discuss public principles and hypothetical models.","check":"圖中同時標示電流與熱兩條路徑。","checkEn":"The diagram includes electrical and thermal paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-21-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"ESD 防護需同時處理電流分流與能量散逸。","textEn":"ESD protection addresses both current diversion and energy dissipation."},{"id":"a025-v7-21-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"薄基板的保護策略需重新檢查熱限制。","textEn":"Thin-substrate protection requires renewed thermal review."}],"quiz":{"question":"導通測試通過便代表 ESD 保護完整嗎？","questionEn":"Does passing continuity establish complete ESD protection?","options":["代表，放電完全沒有熱。","代表，薄化不改變材料體積。","不代表，熱承受與路徑仍需驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; discharge produces no heat.","Yes; thinning changes no volume.","No; thermal survival and pathways still need checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不代表，熱承受與路徑仍需驗證。 ESD 防護需同時處理電流分流與能量散逸。","explanationEn":"No; thermal survival and pathways still need checks. ESD protection addresses both current diversion and energy dissipation."}},{"id":"a025-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-dtco","v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-21"],"title":"建立失效定位決策樹","titleEn":"Build a failure-localization tree","objective":"以最少追加證據分辨可能原因。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish causes with targeted additional evidence.","instruction":"從高壓降案例出發列出高負載、高阻與量測偏移；為每支假說選一個可否證觀察；依非破壞性排檢查順序；記錄哪些結論仍不確定。","instructionEn":"Start with excessive drop and list high load, high resistance and measurement offset; choose a falsifying observation per branch; order nondestructive checks; record unresolved conclusions.","observation":"同一症狀可以來自不同子系統。","observationEn":"One symptom can originate in different subsystems.","failure":"若直接把異常歸為薄化失敗，補上排除負載及測試偏差的證據。","failureEn":"Exclude load and measurement changes before blaming thinning.","check":"每支分支有輸入、判据與後續動作。","checkEn":"Each branch has input, criterion and follow-up action.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-22-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"診斷流程應區分症狀與物理原因。","textEn":"Diagnosis distinguishes symptoms from physical causes."},{"id":"a025-v7-22-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"有效檢查需能改變判斷，而非重複同一讀值。","textEn":"A useful check changes the inference instead of repeating the same value."}],"quiz":{"question":"高壓降首先證明哪件事？","questionEn":"What does excessive drop establish first?","options":["供電表現異常，原因仍需區分。","一定是通孔空隙。","一定是背面微影失效。"],"optionsEn":["Delivery is abnormal; the cause remains to be distinguished.","It must be a via void.","It must be backside lithography failure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"供電表現異常，原因仍需區分。 診斷流程應區分症狀與物理原因。","explanationEn":"Delivery is abnormal; the cause remains to be distinguished. Diagnosis distinguishes symptoms from physical causes."}},{"id":"a025-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-flow","v7-bspdn-dtco"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-22"],"title":"連結混合鍵合與封裝課程","titleEn":"Connect hybrid bonding and packaging","objective":"比較共享的介面問題與不同功能。","objectiveEn":"Compare shared interface problems and different functions.","instruction":"把背面供電、晶圓混合鍵合及先進封裝排在一張介面圖；圈出對準、平坦度與連接電阻共同項；標示訊號與電源目標差異；選一個衍生課程繼續。","instructionEn":"Place backside power, wafer hybrid bonding and advanced packaging on one interface map; circle alignment, flatness and resistance concerns; distinguish signal and power goals; choose a related course.","observation":"共用量測觀念不表示可互換流程。","observationEn":"Shared metrology concepts do not make flows interchangeable.","failure":"若直接套用鍵合間距，先核對接點用途與結構。","failureEn":"Verify contact purpose and structure before transferring a bonding pitch.","check":"比較表至少列出兩共同點與一差異。","checkEn":"List at least two similarities and one difference.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-23-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"多層整合共同依賴清楚的介面定義。","textEn":"Multilevel integration relies on clear interface definitions."},{"id":"a025-v7-23-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"同一量測名稱在不同尺度下仍需重新定義取樣範圍。","textEn":"The same measurement name still needs a scale-specific sampling definition."}],"quiz":{"question":"相似工法最適合轉移什麼？","questionEn":"What transfers best between related processes?","options":["整套未知設備設定。","問題分析與驗證方法，再確認適用條件。","所有幾何尺寸直接照搬。"],"optionsEn":["An entire unknown equipment setup.","Analysis and verification methods, with applicability checked.","Every geometry copied unchanged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"問題分析與驗證方法，再確認適用條件。 多層整合共同依賴清楚的介面定義。","explanationEn":"Analysis and verification methods, with applicability checked. Multilevel integration relies on clear interface definitions."}},{"id":"a025-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-bspdn-intel","v7-bspdn-demo"],"prerequisiteIds":["a025-v7-23"],"title":"完成總工程師整合審查","titleEn":"Complete the chief-engineer integration review","objective":"建立可追溯且不誇大結論的交付包。","objectiveEn":"Produce a traceable review package without overstating results.","instruction":"整理截面、壓降帳本與對準地圖；列出三項已驗證及三項未知；提出下一輪對照實驗；用一頁說明放行或暫緩的理由。","instructionEn":"Collect sections, drop ledger and overlay maps; list three verified and three unknown items; propose the next controlled comparison; justify release or hold on one page.","observation":"證據完整度與性能數字大小是兩回事。","observationEn":"Evidence completeness differs from the size of a performance gain.","failure":"沒有實測或有效模型的項目維持待驗證，不填入廠商保證。","failureEn":"Keep unsupported items unverified rather than adding manufacturer guarantees.","check":"每项結論可連回來源、假設或自己的計算。","checkEn":"Every conclusion traces to a source, assumption or calculation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a025-v7-24-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"設計審查評估證據與限制，不只展示最漂亮的結果。","textEn":"Design review evaluates evidence and limits, not only favorable results."},{"id":"a025-v7-24-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"教育模型可訓練判讀，但不取代製程資格認證。","textEn":"Educational models train interpretation but do not replace process qualification."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪種交付最能支持下一步決策？","questionEn":"Which deliverable best supports the next decision?","options":["只列最高改善百分比。","把所有待驗證項改成通過。","包含假設、失敗與未知項的證據包。"],"optionsEn":["Only the largest improvement percentage.","Mark every unverified item passed.","Evidence including assumptions, failures and unknowns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"包含假設、失敗與未知項的證據包。 設計審查評估證據與限制，不只展示最漂亮的結果。","explanationEn":"Evidence including assumptions, failures and unknowns. Design review evaluates evidence and limits, not only favorable results."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":7,"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a042","title":"高數值孔徑 EUV 成像","titleEn":"High-numerical-aperture EUV imaging","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml","v7-highna-rayleigh","v7-highna-optics","v7-highna-lab","v7-highna-ecosystem","v7-highna-process","v7-highna-metrology","v7-highna-motion","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從解析度、非等倍率光學、光罩與薄光阻，到接縫、焦距控制及缺陷量測，完成 High-NA EUV 成像整合審查。","summaryEn":"Review High-NA EUV imaging from resolution and anamorphic optics through masks, thin resist, field stitching, focus control and defect metrology.","scope":"依公開原理編寫的四階段、24 個教學工作包；每步需交出模型、判讀或驗證紀錄。數值練習為自訂教學案例，不是廠商製程配方、現場操作許可或專業設計認證。","scopeEn":"Four stages and 24 educational work packages based on public principles. Each step produces a model, interpretation or verification record. Numerical exercises are hypothetical, not manufacturer recipes, field operating authorization or professional design certification.","diagram":{"type":"lithography","labels":["光源","反射光罩","非等倍率反射鏡","光阻","量測"],"labelsEn":["Source","Reflective mask","Anamorphic mirrors","Resist","Metrology"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a042-stage01","order":1,"title":"成像與光學預算","titleEn":"Imaging and optical budgets","description":"比較解析度、焦深、反射光路與非等倍率。","descriptionEn":"Compare resolution, depth of focus, reflective paths and anamorphic scaling.","steps":[{"id":"a042-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml","v7-highna-rayleigh"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分開節點名稱與實際線寬","titleEn":"Separate node labels from feature dimensions","objective":"建立不混淆的尺度表。","objectiveEn":"Build an unambiguous scale table.","instruction":"列出節點名稱、線寬、節距與波長四欄；畫兩條線標出線寬與節距；把公開光學解析度放在正確欄位；標記未公開的元件尺寸。","instructionEn":"List node label, linewidth, pitch and wavelength; draw two lines with width and pitch; place published optical resolution in its proper column; mark unpublished device dimensions.","observation":"節點名稱不能直接代入每個幾何尺寸。","observationEn":"A node label is not every physical dimension.","failure":"若把「2 nm」當成所有線寬，退回欄位定義。","failureEn":"Revisit definitions if a 2 nm label is treated as every linewidth.","check":"示意圖清楚區分至少三種尺度。","checkEn":"The diagram clearly distinguishes at least three scales.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-01-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"微影解析度與半導體節點命名描述不同層面。","textEn":"Lithographic resolution and node naming describe different aspects."},{"id":"a042-v7-01-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"節距包含線與間距，不能只報線寬。","textEn":"Pitch includes a line and space; linewidth alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"節點名稱能直接代表所有線寬嗎？","questionEn":"Does a node name directly specify all linewidths?","options":["不能，需使用各層實際尺寸定義。","可以，每一條線都等於節點數字。","可以，節距與波長也相同。"],"optionsEn":["No; use layer-specific dimensions.","Yes; every line equals the node number.","Yes; pitch and wavelength are identical too."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，需使用各層實際尺寸定義。 微影解析度與半導體節點命名描述不同層面。","explanationEn":"No; use layer-specific dimensions. Lithographic resolution and node naming describe different aspects."}},{"id":"a042-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-rayleigh"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-01"],"title":"用 Rayleigh 關係比較 NA","titleEn":"Compare numerical aperture with Rayleigh scaling","objective":"在固定條件下判斷解析度趨勢。","objectiveEn":"Assess resolution trends under fixed conditions.","instruction":"寫出 R=k1×λ/NA；固定 k1 與波長；比較 NA 0.33 與 0.55 的比值；列出不能保持固定時需重新建模的項目。","instructionEn":"Write R=k1×wavelength/NA; hold k1 and wavelength fixed; compare NA 0.33 and 0.55; list what must be remodeled if assumptions change.","observation":"NA 增大使理想化可解析尺寸減小。","observationEn":"Higher NA reduces the idealized resolvable size.","failure":"不把此比例直接當成晶片效能倍數。","failureEn":"Do not convert this ratio directly into a chip-performance multiplier.","check":"計算含無因次比值及固定條件。","checkEn":"Provide the dimensionless ratio and held conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-02-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"Rayleigh 關係提供光學解析度的尺度估算。","textEn":"The Rayleigh relationship estimates resolution scaling."},{"id":"a042-v7-02-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"k1 代表製程與成像因素，不是永遠相同的常數。","textEn":"k1 captures imaging and process factors and need not stay constant."}],"quiz":{"question":"固定 λ 與 k1 時，提高 NA 如何影響 R？","questionEn":"At fixed wavelength and k1, what does higher NA do to R?","options":["使 R 同比例變大。","使 R 變小。","完全沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["It increases R proportionally.","It decreases R.","It has no effect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使 R 變小。 Rayleigh 關係提供光學解析度的尺度估算。","explanationEn":"It decreases R. The Rayleigh relationship estimates resolution scaling."}},{"id":"a042-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-02"],"title":"建立焦深取捨","titleEn":"Build the depth-of-focus tradeoff","objective":"比較横向解析度與垂直容忍度。","objectiveEn":"Compare lateral resolution with vertical tolerance.","instruction":"以 DOF 與 λ/NA² 的比例畫趨勢；比較兩種 NA；把晶圓高度誤差放入焦深帶；標記離焦風險區。","instructionEn":"Plot the DOF proportionality to wavelength/NA squared; compare two NAs; place wafer-height errors inside the focus band; mark defocus-risk regions.","observation":"更細的成像通常伴隨更小的高度容忍度。","observationEn":"Finer imaging generally comes with tighter height tolerance.","failure":"若只看解析度，補上焦深及表面高度誤差預算。","failureEn":"Add focus depth and height-error budgets to resolution-only analysis.","check":"一圖同時顯示解析度收益與焦深代價。","checkEn":"One figure shows both resolution benefit and focus-depth cost.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-03-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"固定其他因素時，焦深對 NA 的平方敏感。","textEn":"With other factors fixed, focus depth scales inversely with NA squared."},{"id":"a042-v7-03-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"真實製程視窗仍受光阻、圖案及量測定義影響。","textEn":"Actual process windows also depend on resist, pattern and measurement definition."}],"quiz":{"question":"提高 NA 後哪項控制更重要？","questionEn":"What control becomes more demanding as NA increases?","options":["任意放寬表面起伏。","完全取消光阻厚度檢查。","焦距與晶圓高度控制。"],"optionsEn":["Freely allowing surface variation.","Removing resist-thickness checks.","Focus and wafer-height control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"焦距與晶圓高度控制。 固定其他因素時，焦深對 NA 的平方敏感。","explanationEn":"Focus and wafer-height control. With other factors fixed, focus depth scales inversely with NA squared."}},{"id":"a042-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-optics"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-03"],"title":"追蹤反射式 EUV 光路","titleEn":"Trace the reflective EUV optical path","objective":"理解光源到光阻的損耗介面。","objectiveEn":"Understand loss interfaces from source to resist.","instruction":"畫光源、照明鏡、光罩及投影鏡；在每次反射標能量流向；用假設反射率連乘比較損耗；說明為何使用真空。","instructionEn":"Draw source, illumination mirrors, mask and projection mirrors; mark energy flow at each reflection; multiply hypothetical reflectivities; explain the vacuum path.","observation":"多次反射的損耗會累積。","observationEn":"Losses accumulate across reflections.","failure":"勿以可見光玻璃透鏡取代 EUV 反射光學。","failureEn":"Do not substitute visible-light glass lenses for EUV reflective optics.","check":"光路圖包含真空邊界及逐段損耗。","checkEn":"Include vacuum boundaries and segment losses.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-04-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"EUV 易被材料吸收，因此系統採用反射鏡與真空。","textEn":"EUV absorption motivates mirrors and vacuum."},{"id":"a042-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"單一元件的反射率不等於整機傳輸率。","textEn":"One mirror's reflectivity is not the system transmission."}],"quiz":{"question":"多面鏡的總傳輸如何估計？","questionEn":"How is transmission across mirrors estimated?","options":["在簡化模型中連乘各段傳輸率。","把百分比直接相加。","只看最後一面鏡。"],"optionsEn":["Multiply segment transmissions in a simplified model.","Add the percentages.","Use only the last mirror."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在簡化模型中連乘各段傳輸率。 EUV 易被材料吸收，因此系統採用反射鏡與真空。","explanationEn":"Multiply segment transmissions in a simplified model. EUV absorption motivates mirrors and vacuum."}},{"id":"a042-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-04"],"title":"驗證非等倍率縮小","titleEn":"Verify anamorphic demagnification","objective":"把光罩座標正確轉到晶圓。","objectiveEn":"Map mask coordinates correctly to wafer coordinates.","instruction":"畫長方形光罩圖案；在兩軸分別用 4× 與 8× 縮小；計算四角座標；反算光罩尺寸以得到指定晶圓長寬。","instructionEn":"Draw a rectangular mask pattern; apply 4x and 8x demagnification on separate axes; calculate all corners; invert the mapping for a target wafer rectangle.","observation":"相同光罩邊長在兩方向產生不同晶圓尺寸。","observationEn":"Equal mask lengths produce different wafer lengths along the two axes.","failure":"如果成像比例錯，先核對軸定義而非旋轉圖形掩飾。","failureEn":"Check axis definitions rather than rotating a wrongly scaled image.","check":"正向與反向座標轉換互相一致。","checkEn":"Forward and inverse coordinate transforms agree.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-05-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"High-NA 光學採用兩方向不同縮小倍率。","textEn":"High-NA optics use unequal demagnification along two axes."},{"id":"a042-v7-05-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"非等倍率影響光罩資料、曝光場與接縫規劃。","textEn":"Anamorphic scaling affects mask data, exposure fields and stitching."}],"quiz":{"question":"同一光罩正方形必然成為晶圓正方形嗎？","questionEn":"Must a square mask feature remain square on the wafer?","options":["一定，只要使用 EUV。","不一定，兩軸倍率不同。","一定，倍率不影响形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Yes, whenever EUV is used.","No; the axis magnifications differ.","Yes; magnification cannot affect shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不一定，兩軸倍率不同。 High-NA 光學採用兩方向不同縮小倍率。","explanationEn":"No; the axis magnifications differ. High-NA optics use unequal demagnification along two axes."}},{"id":"a042-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-lab"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-05"],"title":"建立光學與製程責任界面","titleEn":"Define optical and process interfaces","objective":"避免把全部圖案問題歸給投影鏡。","objectiveEn":"Avoid assigning every pattern error to projection optics.","instruction":"列出光源、光罩、光阻與平台四介面；為各介面指定可觀測量；畫資料交接箭頭；給一個線寬偏差案例分配排查順序。","instructionEn":"List source, mask, resist and stage interfaces; assign observables; draw data handoffs; order checks for a linewidth-deviation case.","observation":"同樣的線寬偏差可來自多種因素。","observationEn":"Similar width errors can have several causes.","failure":"沒有隔離證據時，不把相關性寫成單一根因。","failureEn":"Without isolation evidence, do not state a single root cause.","check":"介面表含輸入、輸出及責任量測。","checkEn":"The interface table includes inputs, outputs and assigned measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-06-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"成像品質由光學、材料及機電共同形成。","textEn":"Imaging quality emerges from optics, materials and mechatronics."},{"id":"a042-v7-06-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"跨設備資料必須使用可對應的位置與時間標記。","textEn":"Cross-tool data need matching spatial and time identifiers."}],"quiz":{"question":"圖案偏差可以僅憑照片判定鏡面故障嗎？","questionEn":"Can a pattern photo alone establish mirror failure?","options":["可以，光阻不影响圖案。","可以，所有誤差都源自光源。","不能，需分離其他介面因素。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; resist cannot affect patterns.","Yes; every error originates at the source.","No; other interface factors need isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不能，需分離其他介面因素。 成像品質由光學、材料及機電共同形成。","explanationEn":"No; other interface factors need isolation. Imaging quality emerges from optics, materials and mechatronics."}}]},{"id":"a042-stage02","order":2,"title":"光罩、光阻與圖案轉移","titleEn":"Mask, resist and pattern transfer","description":"將光罩幾何與光阻、底層、蝕刻聯合判讀。","descriptionEn":"Interpret mask geometry together with resist, underlayers and etch.","steps":[{"id":"a042-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-06"],"title":"辨認光罩三維效應","titleEn":"Identify mask three-dimensional effects","objective":"區分平面設計與真實吸收層。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish layout from a physical absorber stack.","instruction":"畫反射多層膜與吸收層截面；加入斜入射光；比較兩個圖案方向；標記可能造成位置或最佳焦距差異的介面。","instructionEn":"Draw reflector and absorber sections; add oblique incidence; compare pattern orientations; mark interfaces that may shift position or best focus.","observation":"光罩不是沒有厚度的黑白投影片。","observationEn":"A mask is not a thickness-free black-and-white transparency.","failure":"若平面模型無法說明方向差異，列入三維光學效應。","failureEn":"Consider 3D optics when a planar model cannot explain orientation effects.","check":"說明一項平面模型遺漏的效應及驗證方法。","checkEn":"Explain one effect missing from a planar model and how to check it.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-07-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"吸收層與多層膜可改變相位及影像對比。","textEn":"Absorber and multilayer structures can affect phase and contrast."},{"id":"a042-v7-07-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"不同圖案方向可能需要分開評估。","textEn":"Different pattern orientations may need separate evaluation."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何需要光罩截面？","questionEn":"Why is a mask section needed?","options":["厚度與斜入射會影響成像。","光罩沒有任何反射。","平面尺寸永遠不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness and oblique illumination affect imaging.","Masks have no reflection.","Planar dimensions never matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度與斜入射會影響成像。 吸收層與多層膜可改變相位及影像對比。","explanationEn":"Thickness and oblique illumination affect imaging. Absorber and multilayer structures can affect phase and contrast."}},{"id":"a042-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-07"],"title":"比較光罩補償前後輪廓","titleEn":"Compare compensated mask contours","objective":"理解光學鄰近修正的目的。","objectiveEn":"Understand the purpose of optical proximity correction.","instruction":"畫目標轉角與未補償成像輪廓；添加原創示意補償形狀；比較孤立線與密集線；標註仍須以模型及晶圓驗證。","instructionEn":"Draw target corners and uncorrected contours; add an original schematic compensation; compare isolated and dense lines; mark the need for model and wafer validation.","observation":"光罩形狀不必與最終圖案完全相同。","observationEn":"Mask shape need not duplicate the final pattern.","failure":"不要把手畫補償尺寸當成可製造光罩資料。","failureEn":"Do not treat hand-drawn compensation dimensions as mask-production data.","check":"示意圖清楚分開目標、光罩及預測影像。","checkEn":"Separate target, mask and predicted image.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-08-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"補償藉由改變輸入形狀改善印出的目標輪廓。","textEn":"Compensation changes input geometry to improve printed contours."},{"id":"a042-v7-08-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"同一補償可能受鄰近圖案及照明條件影響。","textEn":"Compensation depends on neighboring patterns and illumination."}],"quiz":{"question":"補償成功的判據是什麼？","questionEn":"What determines successful compensation?","options":["光罩看起來和目標完全相同。","晶圓輪廓更接近目標且視窗可接受。","只增加所有圖案面積。"],"optionsEn":["The mask looks identical to the target.","Wafer contours approach target within an acceptable window.","Every pattern area is enlarged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓輪廓更接近目標且視窗可接受。 補償藉由改變輸入形狀改善印出的目標輪廓。","explanationEn":"Wafer contours approach target within an acceptable window. Compensation changes input geometry to improve printed contours."}},{"id":"a042-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-08"],"title":"比較光阻厚度與倒塌風險","titleEn":"Compare resist thickness and collapse risk","objective":"用高寬比理解結構穩定。","objectiveEn":"Use aspect ratio to discuss feature stability.","instruction":"畫同寬不同高的三條光阻線；計算高度除以寬度；比較離焦與倒塌風險；列出薄化後圖案轉移的新要求。","instructionEn":"Draw equal-width resist lines at three heights; calculate height/width; compare focus and collapse concerns; list transfer demands after thinning.","observation":"較薄光阻可能有利成像但留下更少蝕刻餘量。","observationEn":"Thinner resist can help imaging while reducing etch margin.","failure":"若只追求低高寬比，補上後續轉移厚度預算。","failureEn":"Add transfer-thickness budgeting to aspect-ratio optimization.","check":"比較表含焦深、穩定與轉移三面向。","checkEn":"Compare focus depth, stability and transfer.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-09-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"高寬比把厚度與線寬連結到結構問題。","textEn":"Aspect ratio relates height and width to structural concerns."},{"id":"a042-v7-09-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"光阻最佳厚度須與底層及蝕刻共同設計。","textEn":"Resist thickness must be designed with underlayers and etch."}],"quiz":{"question":"光阻越薄是否必然越好？","questionEn":"Is thinner resist always better?","options":["是，蝕刻不需要任何遮罩。","是，薄膜不可能有缺陷。","否，還要滿足圖案轉移要求。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; etch needs no mask.","Yes; thin films cannot have defects.","No; pattern transfer must still work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"否，還要滿足圖案轉移要求。 高寬比把厚度與線寬連結到結構問題。","explanationEn":"No; pattern transfer must still work. Aspect ratio relates height and width to structural concerns."}},{"id":"a042-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-09"],"title":"建立光阻與底層介面圖","titleEn":"Map the resist-underlayer interface","objective":"把黏附、形貌與轉移一起審查。","objectiveEn":"Review adhesion, morphology and transfer together.","instruction":"畫光阻、底層與目標膜；標示各層作用；比較兩種假設底層造成的線形差異；規劃只改底層的對照組。","instructionEn":"Draw resist, underlayer and target film; label roles; compare hypothetical line-shape changes for two underlayers; design an underlayer-only control.","observation":"相同光阻不保證在不同底層有相同結果。","observationEn":"The same resist need not behave identically on different underlayers.","failure":"同時換光阻與底層會混淆原因，拆成實驗矩陣。","failureEn":"Separate simultaneous resist and underlayer changes into a matrix.","check":"每層有功能、關鍵介面與觀察項。","checkEn":"Each layer has a function, interface and observable.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-10-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"光阻與底層需共同最佳化。","textEn":"Resist and underlayer require co-optimization."},{"id":"a042-v7-10-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"單一材料排名不能取代堆疊整合驗證。","textEn":"A material ranking cannot replace stack-integration verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"如何先辨認底層影響？","questionEn":"How can underlayer effects first be isolated?","options":["固定光阻及其他條件比較底層。","同時更改所有堆疊。","只比較材料商品名稱。"],"optionsEn":["Hold resist and other conditions fixed.","Change every layer at once.","Compare product names only."],"answer":0,"explanation":"固定光阻及其他條件比較底層。 光阻與底層需共同最佳化。","explanationEn":"Hold resist and other conditions fixed. Resist and underlayer require co-optimization."}},{"id":"a042-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-10"],"title":"區分光子與材料隨機性","titleEn":"Distinguish photon and material stochasticity","objective":"理解少數缺陷與平均線寬的差異。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish rare defects from average linewidth.","instruction":"畫相同目標的二十個接觸孔；加入自訂缺孔與尺寸擾動；分別統計平均尺寸及缺孔數；比較兩批平均相同的資料。","instructionEn":"Draw twenty target contacts; add hypothetical missing holes and size variations; count mean size and missing holes separately; compare batches with equal means.","observation":"平均尺寸一致仍可能有不同失敗率。","observationEn":"Equal mean size can coexist with different failure rates.","failure":"不要以二十個樣本推估量產極低缺陷率；註明樣本限制。","failureEn":"Do not infer production-scale rare-event rates from twenty samples.","check":"同時報告平均、散布、缺陷數與樣本數。","checkEn":"Report mean, spread, defect count and sample size.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-11-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷需用分布及事件數評估。","textEn":"Stochastic defects require distributions and event counts."},{"id":"a042-v7-11-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"看不到缺陷不等於缺陷機率為零。","textEn":"Observing no defects does not establish zero probability."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均線寬正常就可排除缺孔嗎？","questionEn":"Does a normal mean linewidth rule out missing holes?","options":["可以，平均值涵蓋所有拓撲。","不能，需單獨檢查缺陷事件。","可以，只需增加影像亮度。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; a mean captures all topology.","No; defect events need separate inspection.","Yes; just brighten the image."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不能，需單獨檢查缺陷事件。 隨機缺陷需用分布及事件數評估。","explanationEn":"No; defect events need separate inspection. Stochastic defects require distributions and event counts."}},{"id":"a042-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-11"],"title":"追蹤顯影到蝕刻的圖案變化","titleEn":"Track patterns from development to etch","objective":"避免只用光阻圖案評估最終結構。","objectiveEn":"Avoid assessing final structures from resist alone.","instruction":"畫顯影後、硬遮罩後與目標膜後三個輪廓；逐站標線寬變化；比較斜壁與頂視影像；分配每站允許的教學誤差預算。","instructionEn":"Draw post-develop, hard-mask and target-film contours; mark width changes; compare sloped walls with top views; allocate hypothetical error budgets by stage.","observation":"頂視線寬相同可對應不同側壁。","observationEn":"Equal top-view widths can hide different sidewalls.","failure":"未取得蝕刻後證據時，結論只限光阻階段。","failureEn":"Without after-etch evidence, limit conclusions to the resist stage.","check":"三站輪廓與每次轉移偏差可對應。","checkEn":"Match three contours and transfer deviations.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-12-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"最終圖案是曝光、顯影與轉移共同結果。","textEn":"The final pattern combines exposure, development and transfer."},{"id":"a042-v7-12-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"每次轉移可能改變尺寸與形貌。","textEn":"Each transfer can change dimensions and morphology."}],"quiz":{"question":"光阻照片能否保證目標膜形貌？","questionEn":"Can a resist photo guarantee target-film geometry?","options":["能，所有層必定等比例複製。","能，只要曝光一次。","不能，需蝕刻後量測。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; every layer replicates perfectly.","Yes, after a single exposure.","No; after-etch metrology is needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不能，需蝕刻後量測。 最終圖案是曝光、顯影與轉移共同結果。","explanationEn":"No; after-etch metrology is needed. The final pattern combines exposure, development and transfer."}}]},{"id":"a042-stage03","order":3,"title":"平台、焦距與曝光場","titleEn":"Stages, focus and exposure fields","description":"建立定位、場接縫與時間預算。","descriptionEn":"Build positioning, stitching and timing budgets.","steps":[{"id":"a042-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-motion"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-12"],"title":"推演晶圓與光罩同步掃描","titleEn":"Model synchronized wafer and mask scanning","objective":"建立兩平台相對運動的概念。","objectiveEn":"Model relative motion of both stages.","instruction":"畫曝光狹縫與兩平台；指定示意縮小倍率；推演對應位移；加入一段速度誤差並標記其影像方向。","instructionEn":"Draw an exposure slit and both stages; choose a schematic demagnification; derive corresponding displacements; add a velocity error and mark its image direction.","observation":"平台各自位置正確仍須保持相對同步。","observationEn":"Individually correct positions still require relative synchronization.","failure":"若兩平台使用相同位移卻倍率不同，重算對應關係。","failureEn":"Recalculate mapping if both stages move equally despite demagnification.","check":"時間圖顯示兩平台與相對誤差。","checkEn":"A time plot shows both stages and relative error.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-13-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"掃描成像需要平台運動與光學倍率一致。","textEn":"Scanning requires motion consistent with optical scaling."},{"id":"a042-v7-13-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"同步誤差需按曝光時刻評估。","textEn":"Synchronization error must be evaluated during exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"只檢查平台終點位置足夠嗎？","questionEn":"Is checking only final stage position enough?","options":["不夠，曝光期間同步也重要。","足夠，中途軌跡不影響影像。","足夠，兩平台不需配合。"],"optionsEn":["No; synchronization during exposure matters.","Yes; the intermediate path cannot affect imaging.","Yes; stages need no coordination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不夠，曝光期間同步也重要。 掃描成像需要平台運動與光學倍率一致。","explanationEn":"No; synchronization during exposure matters. Scanning requires motion consistent with optical scaling."}},{"id":"a042-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml","v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-13"],"title":"規劃半曝光場拼接","titleEn":"Plan half-field stitching","objective":"辨認接縫處的對準與連接問題。","objectiveEn":"Identify alignment and continuity at field seams.","instruction":"把示意晶片切成兩個場；畫一條跨接縫導線；分別加入平移與縮放偏差；比較開路、短路及重疊情境。","instructionEn":"Split a schematic die into two fields; draw a crossing line; add translation and scaling errors separately; compare open, short and overlap cases.","observation":"接縫不是把兩張圖靠近就完成。","observationEn":"Stitching is more than placing images side by side.","failure":"不要假設每個晶片都需拼接；先比較晶片與曝光場大小。","failureEn":"Compare die and field sizes before assuming stitching is required.","check":"說明何時需要拼接及如何檢查邊界。","checkEn":"Explain when stitching is needed and how boundaries are checked.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-14-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"非等倍率使曝光場規劃改變。","textEn":"Anamorphic optics change exposure-field planning."},{"id":"a042-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"跨場圖案需額外檢查位置與連續性。","textEn":"Cross-field patterns need alignment and continuity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"所有晶片一定需兩場拼接嗎？","questionEn":"Must every die use two stitched fields?","options":["一定，與晶片大小無關。","不一定，取決於晶片與場的尺寸。","不必，接縫永遠沒有誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Yes, regardless of die size.","No; it depends on die and field size.","No, because seams can never have errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不一定，取決於晶片與場的尺寸。 非等倍率使曝光場規劃改變。","explanationEn":"No; it depends on die and field size. Anamorphic optics change exposure-field planning."}},{"id":"a042-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-14"],"title":"建立晶圓高度與焦距圖","titleEn":"Build a wafer-height and focus map","objective":"把形貌轉為可校正的誤差。","objectiveEn":"Translate topography into correctable errors.","instruction":"畫九點高度圖；扣除整體傾斜平面；將殘差與假設焦深範圍比較；標記需重測或限制曝光的位置。","instructionEn":"Draw a nine-point height map; subtract a best-fit tilt plane; compare residuals with a hypothetical focus range; flag sites for remeasurement or exposure limits.","observation":"平面傾斜校正後仍可能有局部起伏。","observationEn":"Local topography can remain after tilt correction.","failure":"若只用中心點對焦，增加邊緣與局部高點取樣。","failureEn":"Add edge and local-high sampling to center-only focusing.","check":"原始高度、校正量與殘差均有紀錄。","checkEn":"Record raw heights, corrections and residuals.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-15-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"焦距控制依賴可追溯的高度量測。","textEn":"Focus control depends on traceable height measurements."},{"id":"a042-v7-15-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"校正模型的自由度有限，不能消除所有形貌。","textEn":"A correction model has finite freedom and cannot erase all topography."}],"quiz":{"question":"扣除傾斜後還應看什麼？","questionEn":"What remains to inspect after removing tilt?","options":["只看全片平均高度。","刪除不符合平面的數據。","局部殘差是否超出焦距容忍。"],"optionsEn":["Only mean wafer height.","Delete data not fitting the plane.","Whether local residuals exceed focus tolerance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部殘差是否超出焦距容忍。 焦距控制依賴可追溯的高度量測。","explanationEn":"Whether local residuals exceed focus tolerance. Focus control depends on traceable height measurements."}},{"id":"a042-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-motion"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-15"],"title":"比較熱漂移與隨機振動","titleEn":"Compare thermal drift and random vibration","objective":"按時間尺度分類位置誤差。","objectiveEn":"Classify positioning error by time scale.","instruction":"畫緩慢漂移及快速擾動兩條假設訊號；選不同取樣間隔；比較可觀測成分；為兩類問題分別指定溫度或位置證據。","instructionEn":"Draw slow drift and fast disturbance signals; choose sampling intervals; compare observable components; assign temperature or position evidence to each.","observation":"相同誤差幅度不一定需要相同校正。","observationEn":"Equal error amplitudes can require different corrections.","failure":"過慢取樣可能漏掉快速擾動；保留量測頻寬。","failureEn":"Slow sampling can miss fast disturbances; retain bandwidth information.","check":"分類含時間尺度、感測量與修正假說。","checkEn":"Classify time scale, sensing quantity and correction hypothesis.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-16-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"機電精度同時受環境與運動狀態影響。","textEn":"Mechatronic precision depends on environment and motion."},{"id":"a042-v7-16-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"量測頻率必須適合欲觀察的變化。","textEn":"Sampling must suit the changes being observed."}],"quiz":{"question":"慢速溫度紀錄能否排除快速振動？","questionEn":"Can slow temperature logging exclude fast vibration?","options":["不能，需適當頻寬的位置量測。","能，所有誤差都有同一頻率。","能，只要平均溫度固定。"],"optionsEn":["No; position measurement with suitable bandwidth is needed.","Yes; all errors share one frequency.","Yes, if average temperature is fixed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，需適當頻寬的位置量測。 機電精度同時受環境與運動狀態影響。","explanationEn":"No; position measurement with suitable bandwidth is needed. Mechatronic precision depends on environment and motion."}},{"id":"a042-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-16"],"title":"拆解曝光時間與產能","titleEn":"Decompose exposure time and throughput","objective":"避免以曝光次數直接判定總產能。","objectiveEn":"Avoid deriving total throughput from exposure count alone.","instruction":"列出對準、移動、曝光與換片時間；建立兩種假設排程；分別增加場數及縮短平台時間；比較總時間及瓶頸。","instructionEn":"List alignment, motion, exposure and exchange times; create two hypothetical schedules; vary field count and stage time separately; compare totals and bottlenecks.","observation":"場數增加不等於總時間必然成同比例增加。","observationEn":"More fields do not force total time to increase proportionally.","failure":"不要用公開峰值代替實際光阻劑量與排程條件。","failureEn":"Do not substitute peak claims for dose and scheduling conditions.","check":"以同條件時間帳本比較方案。","checkEn":"Compare schemes using a timing ledger under matching conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-17-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"產能由多個時間項及重疊作業共同決定。","textEn":"Throughput depends on several time terms and overlap."},{"id":"a042-v7-17-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"劑量、場數與平台速度的取捨需共同審查。","textEn":"Dose, field count and stage speed require joint review."}],"quiz":{"question":"半場是否必然使每片時間加倍？","questionEn":"Does a half field necessarily double wafer time?","options":["必然，其他動作時間為零。","不必然，要看完整時間預算。","完全不影响任何時間項。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; all other actions take zero time.","Not necessarily; inspect the full timing budget.","It cannot affect any time term."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不必然，要看完整時間預算。 產能由多個時間項及重疊作業共同決定。","explanationEn":"Not necessarily; inspect the full timing budget. Throughput depends on several time terms and overlap."}},{"id":"a042-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-17"],"title":"追蹤曝光場內的劑量分布","titleEn":"Track dose distribution within a field","objective":"區分平均能量與局部曝光均勻性。","objectiveEn":"Separate average energy from local exposure uniformity.","instruction":"畫中心與兩側三區曝光圖；指定相同平均但不同分布的假設劑量；比較每區線寬回應；列出感測器位置及校正證據。","instructionEn":"Draw center and two edge exposure zones; assign equal-average but differently distributed hypothetical doses; compare local linewidth responses; list sensor positions and calibration evidence.","observation":"平均曝光量相同仍可能有場內差異。","observationEn":"Equal average exposure can conceal within-field differences.","failure":"若只看總能量，補上位置分布，避免把光阻差異全部歸因於光源。","failureEn":"Add spatial distribution to total energy and avoid attributing every resist difference to the source.","check":"交出每區劑量、觀察及可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Report dose, observation and potential confounders by zone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-18-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"曝光品質包含空間與時間的均勻性。","textEn":"Exposure quality includes spatial and temporal uniformity."},{"id":"a042-v7-18-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"量測點的覆蓋範圍會限制對全場的結論。","textEn":"Measurement coverage limits conclusions about the whole field."}],"quiz":{"question":"平均劑量相同是否證明全場曝光一致？","questionEn":"Does equal average dose prove uniform field exposure?","options":["是，平均值等於每個點。","是，場邊永遠沒有誤差。","否，還需檢查空間分布。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; the average equals every point.","Yes; field edges never have errors.","No; inspect spatial distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"否，還需檢查空間分布。 曝光品質包含空間與時間的均勻性。","explanationEn":"No; inspect spatial distribution. Exposure quality includes spatial and temporal uniformity."}}]},{"id":"a042-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測、缺陷與整合驗證","titleEn":"Metrology, defects and integrated verification","description":"把影像、製程視窗與電性測試連接成證據鏈。","descriptionEn":"Connect images, process windows and electrical tests into an evidence chain.","steps":[{"id":"a042-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-18"],"title":"建立焦距與劑量矩陣","titleEn":"Build a focus-exposure matrix","objective":"以多條件找可接受製程區域。","objectiveEn":"Find acceptable regions across conditions.","instruction":"畫三個焦距×三個相對劑量的假設矩陣；填入示意線寬及缺陷觀察；圈出同時符合兩條件的區域；標明數值不供設備設定。","instructionEn":"Draw a hypothetical three-focus by three-relative-dose matrix; enter illustrative widths and defects; outline the region meeting both conditions; label values as non-operational.","observation":"單一最佳點不代表有寬廣製程視窗。","observationEn":"One optimum point does not establish a broad process window.","failure":"若只選線寬最接近的一格，加入缺陷與鄰近格穩定性。","failureEn":"Add defects and neighboring-condition stability to closest-width selection.","check":"判定使用至少兩項品質指標。","checkEn":"Use at least two quality criteria.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-19-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"製程視窗是同時滿足條件的範圍。","textEn":"A process window is a range satisfying joint conditions."},{"id":"a042-v7-19-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"裕量比單次最佳結果更有助於穩定性判讀。","textEn":"Margin is more informative about robustness than one optimum result."}],"quiz":{"question":"只有一格合格代表什麼？","questionEn":"What does only one passing matrix cell indicate?","options":["可能視窗狹窄，需更多驗證。","已證明任何條件都穩定。","可刪除所有失敗格。"],"optionsEn":["A potentially narrow window needing more checks.","Stability under every condition is proven.","All failing cells may be removed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可能視窗狹窄，需更多驗證。 製程視窗是同時滿足條件的範圍。","explanationEn":"A potentially narrow window needing more checks. A process window is a range satisfying joint conditions."}},{"id":"a042-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-19"],"title":"分辨 CD、疊對與邊緣位置","titleEn":"Separate CD, overlay and edge placement","objective":"避免不同誤差指標互相替代。","objectiveEn":"Avoid substituting one error metric for another.","instruction":"畫上下兩層線路；分別改變寬度與平移；量出 CD、層間偏移與目標邊緣差；比較兩項誤差相加的情況。","instructionEn":"Draw lines on two layers; vary width and translation separately; measure CD, layer offset and target-edge difference; compare combined errors.","observation":"CD 合格仍可能因疊對偏差造成連接失敗。","observationEn":"Passing CD can coexist with failed connections from overlay error.","failure":"若只報單一「精度」，指定其物理定義與位置。","failureEn":"Replace a generic accuracy number with a physical definition and location.","check":"三種指標各有圖示與量測基準。","checkEn":"Illustrate all three metrics with measurement references.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-20-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"尺寸與位置是不同的品質維度。","textEn":"Size and position are distinct quality dimensions."},{"id":"a042-v7-20-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"邊緣位置可能同時受尺寸與疊對影響。","textEn":"Edge position can reflect both size and overlay."}],"quiz":{"question":"CD 合格能否證明層間對準？","questionEn":"Does passing CD prove interlayer alignment?","options":["能，寬度就是位置。","不能，疊對需另測。","能，只要線條發亮。"],"optionsEn":["Yes; width is position.","No; overlay requires separate measurement.","Yes, if lines appear bright."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不能，疊對需另測。 尺寸與位置是不同的品質維度。","explanationEn":"No; overlay requires separate measurement. Size and position are distinct quality dimensions."}},{"id":"a042-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-20"],"title":"規劃光學與電子束互補檢查","titleEn":"Plan complementary optical and e-beam checks","objective":"匹配檢查速度與缺陷解析度。","objectiveEn":"Match inspection speed and defect resolution.","instruction":"列出全片趨勢與局部缺陷兩類問題；為各類選量測工具；設計熱點加隨機位置取樣；比較只查熱點會漏掉的情況。","instructionEn":"Separate whole-wafer trends from local defects; assign tools; sample hotspots plus random sites; compare what hotspot-only inspection could miss.","observation":"快速取樣與高解析檢查需互相補充。","observationEn":"Fast sampling and high-resolution inspection complement each other.","failure":"不宣稱取樣等於全片每一結構檢查。","failureEn":"Do not equate sampling with inspection of every structure.","check":"計畫列出覆蓋範圍、解析能力與未覆蓋區。","checkEn":"State coverage, resolving capability and gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-21-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"光學量測與電子束檢查具有不同速度與資訊特性。","textEn":"Optical metrology and e-beam inspection differ in speed and information."},{"id":"a042-v7-21-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"取樣策略會影響可發現的缺陷種類。","textEn":"Sampling strategy changes the defects likely to be found."}],"quiz":{"question":"只檢查已知熱點有何限制？","questionEn":"What limits hotspot-only inspection?","options":["能保證沒有任何缺陷。","使儀器解析度無限大。","可能漏掉未知位置的缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["It guarantees no defects anywhere.","It gives infinite resolution.","It may miss defects in unexpected locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可能漏掉未知位置的缺陷。 光學量測與電子束檢查具有不同速度與資訊特性。","explanationEn":"It may miss defects in unexpected locations. Optical metrology and e-beam inspection differ in speed and information."}},{"id":"a042-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-ecosystem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-21"],"title":"建立缺陷分類與電性對照","titleEn":"Classify defects against electrical outcomes","objective":"把影像異常轉成可驗證的功能假說。","objectiveEn":"Translate image anomalies into testable functional hypotheses.","instruction":"畫橋接、缺孔及線頸三種原創示意；預測短路、開路或高阻；配對假設電性結果；列出影像不足以判斷的案例。","instructionEn":"Draw original bridge, missing-contact and necking examples; predict short, open or high resistance; pair hypothetical electrical results; list cases images cannot resolve.","observation":"可見形貌與電性失敗需建立對照。","observationEn":"Visible morphology and electrical failure need correlation.","failure":"不要將每個影像雜點都標成失效；先查成像與樣品條件。","failureEn":"Check imaging and sample conditions before treating every speck as a defect.","check":"分類表包含形貌、功能假說與追加證據。","checkEn":"Include morphology, functional hypothesis and additional evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-22-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"缺陷的功能影響取決於位置及連接關係。","textEn":"Functional impact depends on location and connectivity."},{"id":"a042-v7-22-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"影像分類須與其他證據交叉確認。","textEn":"Image classification needs cross-checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"一個雜點能直接證明短路嗎？","questionEn":"Does a speck directly prove a short?","options":["不能，需確認形貌與電性。","能，任何雜點都導電。","能，影像不可能有雜訊。"],"optionsEn":["No; morphology and electrical evidence are needed.","Yes; every speck conducts.","Yes; images cannot contain noise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，需確認形貌與電性。 缺陷的功能影響取決於位置及連接關係。","explanationEn":"No; morphology and electrical evidence are needed. Functional impact depends on location and connectivity."}},{"id":"a042-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-asml","v7-highna-lab"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-22"],"title":"比較 DUV、多重圖案化與 High NA","titleEn":"Compare DUV, multipatterning and High NA","objective":"依圖層需求選擇方法而非技術排名。","objectiveEn":"Select methods by layer requirements rather than prestige.","instruction":"為三種示意圖層列出節距、場大小及產能需求；比較單次與多次圖案化的步驟；標出疊對及成本項；說明一個不需 High NA 的案例。","instructionEn":"Specify pitch, field size and throughput for three illustrative layers; compare single and multiple patterning; mark overlay and cost terms; explain a layer not requiring High NA.","observation":"不同圖層可使用不同微影策略。","observationEn":"Different layers can use different lithography strategies.","failure":"不能把所有舊設備視為失效；先看需求匹配。","failureEn":"Match requirements before treating older tools as unsuitable.","check":"選擇表有需求、收益、限制與衍生課程。","checkEn":"The selection table includes needs, benefits, limits and related study.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-23-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"製程選擇需整合解析度、成本與圖案轉移。","textEn":"Process selection integrates resolution, cost and transfer."},{"id":"a042-v7-23-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"更高 NA 不自動成為每層的最佳選項。","textEn":"Higher NA is not automatically best for every layer."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪種比較最合理？","questionEn":"Which comparison is most useful?","options":["單純依設備新舊排名。","在同一圖層需求下比較完整流程。","只看最小公開線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Rank solely by equipment age.","Compare complete flows for the same layer requirements.","Use only minimum advertised linewidth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一圖層需求下比較完整流程。 製程選擇需整合解析度、成本與圖案轉移。","explanationEn":"Compare complete flows for the same layer requirements. Process selection integrates resolution, cost and transfer."}},{"id":"a042-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-highna-lab","v7-highna-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a042-v7-23"],"title":"完成成像整合交付","titleEn":"Complete the imaging-integration dossier","objective":"用完整證據支持下一輪試驗。","objectiveEn":"Support the next experiment with complete evidence.","instruction":"收集尺度表、焦距矩陣與缺陷分類；標記每張圖是自繪、假設或實測來源；列出三個未解問題；提出優先驗證的介面。","instructionEn":"Collect scale definitions, focus matrix and defect classification; label original, hypothetical and sourced evidence; list three unresolved questions; prioritize an interface for verification.","observation":"漂亮影像不能取代統計與流程相容證據。","observationEn":"Attractive images cannot replace statistics and integration evidence.","failure":"缺乏電性或轉移結果時，限制結論到已驗證階段。","failureEn":"Limit conclusions to verified stages when electrical or transfer evidence is absent.","check":"交付包含可重現假設、資料對應與下一步。","checkEn":"Deliver reproducible assumptions, data mapping and a next step.","knowledge":[{"id":"a042-v7-24-k1","title":"原理與限制","titleEn":"Principle and limits","text":"整合成熟度需要多種證據互相支持。","textEn":"Integration maturity requires mutually supporting evidence."},{"id":"a042-v7-24-k2","title":"驗證與判讀","titleEn":"Verification and interpretation","text":"本課程是成像原理審查，不是光刻機建造藍圖。","textEn":"This course reviews imaging principles, not lithography-machine construction blueprints."}],"quiz":{"question":"哪項最能支持總工程師決策？","questionEn":"What best supports a chief engineer's decision?","options":["只展示單張最佳照片。","宣稱公開原理等於完整量產配方。","可追溯的視窗、缺陷與未知項。"],"optionsEn":["Show only one best photograph.","Claim public principles are a complete production recipe.","Traceable windows, defects and unknowns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可追溯的視窗、缺陷與未知項。 整合成熟度需要多種證據互相支持。","explanationEn":"Traceable windows, defects and unknowns. Integration maturity requires mutually supporting evidence."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":7,"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography"},{"id":"c005","title":"Boeing 787 複材與電力系統","titleEn":"Boeing 787 composites and electrical integration","category":"aerospace","kind":"course","summary":"以二十四個設計審查任務連結材料、機身接合、更多電力架構與試驗證據。","summaryEn":"Twenty-four design-review tasks connect materials, fuselage joins, more-electric architecture and test evidence.","scope":"以公開資料建立的概念工程課程，練習件、載荷與數字均為教學假設。不是波音製造圖、維修指令、飛行操作或適航放行程序。","scopeEn":"A conceptual engineering course based on public sources; specimens, loads and numbers are teaching assumptions. It is not Boeing manufacturing data, maintenance instructions, flight procedures or an airworthiness release process.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production","v7-science-787-history","v7-science-787-address"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"aircraft","labels":["需求","複材結構","系統整合","試驗證據"],"labelsEn":["Requirements","Composite structure","Systems integration","Test evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"c005-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求與材料邊界","titleEn":"Requirements and material boundaries","description":"把航程與重量需求轉成可追溯的結構問題。","descriptionEn":"Translate range and mass needs into traceable structural questions.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c005-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"建立任務與重量權衡圖","titleEn":"Build a mission and mass trade map","objective":"分清航程、酬載與能源需求。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish range, payload and energy demands.","instruction":"列出假想航線的距離與酬載；畫出空機、酬載與燃油三格；調高其中一格並記錄其他限制。","instructionEn":"List distance and payload for an imaginary route; draw empty-mass, payload and fuel boxes; increase one and record the other constraints.","observation":"航程目標牽動結構重量與攜帶能源。","observationEn":"A range target couples structural mass to carried energy.","failure":"只比較座位數會漏掉任務差異。","failureEn":"Comparing seat counts alone misses mission differences.","check":"交出有單位、假設及兩個權衡方案的表。","checkEn":"Submit a table with units, assumptions and two trade alternatives.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"重量預算是跨系統分配，某一部件減重不等於相同幅度的全機油耗改善。","textEn":"A mass budget spans systems; a component mass reduction does not imply an equal percentage aircraft fuel reduction."},{"id":"c005-v7-01-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"酬載、攜帶能源與結構質量相互耦合；比較航線時要固定氣象與保留量假設。","textEn":"Payload, carried energy and structural mass are coupled; route comparisons need consistent weather and reserve assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立任務與重量權衡圖」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a mission and mass trade map’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["同時列出任務與質量假設","只看最多座位數","把所有 787 型號視為同一性能"],"optionsEn":["State mission and mass assumptions together","Use maximum seat count alone","Treat every 787 variant as identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重量預算是跨系統分配，某一部件減重不等於相同幅度的全機油耗改善。 酬載、攜帶能源與結構質量相互耦合；比較航線時要固定氣象與保留量假設。","explanationEn":"A mass budget spans systems; a component mass reduction does not imply an equal percentage aircraft fuel reduction. Payload, carried energy and structural mass are coupled; route comparisons need consistent weather and reserve assumptions."}},{"id":"c005-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-01"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"畫出機身與機翼載荷路徑","titleEn":"Trace fuselage and wing load paths","objective":"把外力連到承載結構。","objectiveEn":"Connect external forces to load-carrying structure.","instruction":"在原創側視圖標重力與升力；沿機翼盒、接頭與機身畫反力；再加入客艙壓差並用另一顏色標示。","instructionEn":"Mark gravity and lift on an original side view; trace reactions through wing box, joints and fuselage; add cabin pressure using a different color.","observation":"同一接頭可能承受多種載荷。","observationEn":"A joint may carry several load components.","failure":"把蒙皮當裝飾會切斷載荷路徑。","failureEn":"Treating skin as decorative breaks the load path.","check":"每個外力都要有連續的反力路徑。","checkEn":"Every external load needs a continuous reaction path.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"平衡條件是力與力矩守恆，並不單獨證明剛度、疲勞或穩定性。","textEn":"Force and moment equilibrium alone do not establish stiffness, fatigue resistance or stability."},{"id":"c005-v7-02-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"機身框、長桁與蒙皮分擔承載；簡圖省略了真實接頭細節。","textEn":"Frames, stringers and skin share loads; a schematic omits actual joint details."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「畫出機身與機翼載荷路徑」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Trace fuselage and wing load paths’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只需計算重量而不考慮壓差","需要追蹤力與力矩的傳遞","箭頭終止在外觀表面即可"],"optionsEn":["Consider weight but ignore pressure","Trace both forces and moments","End arrows at the outer appearance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平衡條件是力與力矩守恆，並不單獨證明剛度、疲勞或穩定性。 機身框、長桁與蒙皮分擔承載；簡圖省略了真實接頭細節。","explanationEn":"Force and moment equilibrium alone do not establish stiffness, fatigue resistance or stability. Frames, stringers and skin share loads; a schematic omits actual joint details."}},{"id":"c005-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-02"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"辨識層合板方向性","titleEn":"Identify laminate directionality","objective":"理解纖維方向如何改變剛度。","objectiveEn":"Understand how fiber orientation changes stiffness.","instruction":"畫兩片等厚試片；一片纖維平行拉力、一片垂直；再加入斜向層並預測剪切反應。","instructionEn":"Draw two equal-thickness coupons; align fibers with the load in one and across it in the other; add angled plies and predict shear response.","observation":"等厚材料未必有相同方向剛度。","observationEn":"Equal thickness does not imply equal directional stiffness.","failure":"把複材當各向同性金屬會誤判。","failureEn":"Treating composites as isotropic metal misleads.","check":"說明至少兩個方向的負載差異。","checkEn":"Explain loading differences in at least two directions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"纖維、樹脂與鋪層共同決定層合板行為，不能只引用單一纖維強度。","textEn":"Fibers, matrix and stacking jointly determine laminate behavior; fiber strength alone is insufficient."},{"id":"c005-v7-03-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"橫向與層間行為更依賴基材和介面；沿纖維強度高不能代表所有方向都同樣強。","textEn":"Transverse and interlaminar behavior depend more on matrix and interfaces; high fiber-direction strength does not imply equal strength everywhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「辨識層合板方向性」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Identify laminate directionality’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["同厚度必然同強度","只要增加樹脂就一定更強","應比較鋪層與載荷方向"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness guarantees equal strength","More resin always means stronger material","Compare stacking with load direction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"纖維、樹脂與鋪層共同決定層合板行為，不能只引用單一纖維強度。 橫向與層間行為更依賴基材和介面；沿纖維強度高不能代表所有方向都同樣強。","explanationEn":"Fibers, matrix and stacking jointly determine laminate behavior; fiber strength alone is insufficient. Transverse and interlaminar behavior depend more on matrix and interfaces; high fiber-direction strength does not imply equal strength everywhere."}},{"id":"c005-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-03"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"建立材料批次追溯卡","titleEn":"Build material-lot traceability","objective":"讓材料身分連到試件與紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Connect material identity to specimens and records.","instruction":"為兩個假想批次編號；記錄收料、儲存與出庫事件；把每張教學試片連回批次並標出缺資料處。","instructionEn":"Number two hypothetical lots; record receipt, storage and issue events; link each teaching coupon to a lot and flag missing data.","observation":"外觀相同不代表材料履歷相同。","observationEn":"Similar appearance does not establish identical history.","failure":"把失去標籤的試片重新猜成某批次會破壞追溯。","failureEn":"Guessing a lost coupon identity breaks traceability.","check":"從試片能回查批次，從批次能找到全部試片。","checkEn":"Trace specimens to lots and lots to all their specimens.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"材料狀態包含時間與環境歷程，不是只有供應商名稱。","textEn":"Material state includes time and environmental history, not just supplier name."},{"id":"c005-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"追溯能界定受影響範圍，但不能取代材料本身的驗證。","textEn":"Traceability identifies affected scope but does not replace material verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立材料批次追溯卡」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build material-lot traceability’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["未知資料應明確標示與隔離審查","可用相似外觀補寫批號","總裝後不必保留批次關係"],"optionsEn":["Flag unknown data for separate review","Infer lot identity from appearance","Discard lot links after assembly"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料狀態包含時間與環境歷程，不是只有供應商名稱。 追溯能界定受影響範圍，但不能取代材料本身的驗證。","explanationEn":"Material state includes time and environmental history, not just supplier name. Traceability identifies affected scope but does not replace material verification."}},{"id":"c005-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-04"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"規劃製造與檢測分工","titleEn":"Plan production and inspection roles","objective":"區分做出零件與證明零件合格。","objectiveEn":"Separate making a part from proving conformity.","instruction":"畫供應商、加工、檢驗與總裝四站；為每站指定輸入證據；加入不合格返工路徑並檢查版本回流。","instructionEn":"Draw supplier, fabrication, inspection and assembly stations; assign input evidence to each; add a nonconformance loop and inspect revision feedback.","observation":"品質證據需要隨零件一起交接。","observationEn":"Quality evidence must travel with the part.","failure":"只安排物流而沒有文件介面容易漏驗。","failureEn":"Logistics without documentation interfaces can omit inspections.","check":"列出每個交接點的零件身分與可接受證據。","checkEn":"Identify part identity and acceptable evidence at every handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"分散製造可並行工作，但把介面控制、運輸保護與一致性問題放大。","textEn":"Distributed manufacture enables parallel work but magnifies interface, transport-protection and consistency challenges."},{"id":"c005-v7-05-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"返工會改變狀態；舊檢驗結果不能自動覆蓋修改後配置。","textEn":"Rework changes state; old inspection results do not automatically cover a modified configuration."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規劃製造與檢測分工」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Plan production and inspection roles’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["返工後可永遠沿用舊證明","交付必須含配置與檢測證據","運到總裝線即代表品質合格"],"optionsEn":["Reuse old evidence indefinitely after rework","Deliver configuration and inspection evidence","Arrival at assembly proves conformity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分散製造可並行工作，但把介面控制、運輸保護與一致性問題放大。 返工會改變狀態；舊檢驗結果不能自動覆蓋修改後配置。","explanationEn":"Distributed manufacture enables parallel work but magnifies interface, transport-protection and consistency challenges. Rework changes state; old inspection results do not automatically cover a modified configuration."}},{"id":"c005-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-05"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"建立需求—驗證矩陣","titleEn":"Build a requirement–verification matrix","objective":"為不同主張選擇正確證據。","objectiveEn":"Select appropriate evidence for different claims.","instruction":"寫下質量、尺寸與承載三項假想要求；分配量測、分析或試驗方法；列出無法僅靠外觀證明的項目。","instructionEn":"Write hypothetical mass, dimensional and load requirements; assign measurement, analysis or test; list claims that appearance alone cannot establish.","observation":"漂亮模型與可驗證工程是不同產物。","observationEn":"An attractive model and verified engineering are different outputs.","failure":"把所有欄位都填「目視通過」沒有意義。","failureEn":"Marking every field as visual pass is uninformative.","check":"每項要求有條件、方法與結果欄位。","checkEn":"Every requirement has conditions, a method and a result field.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"驗證問題是是否符合要求；確認用途則問要求是否解決正確任務。","textEn":"Verification asks whether requirements are met; validation asks whether those requirements address the right mission."},{"id":"c005-v7-06-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"未測項目應保留為未決，不能由其他通過項目推定。","textEn":"Untested items remain open; unrelated passes do not close them."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立需求—驗證矩陣」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a requirement–verification matrix’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["漂亮外觀能證明承載","有一項通過即可全部放行","尺寸與承載需要不同的證據"],"optionsEn":["Appearance proves load capability","One pass releases every requirement","Dimensions and load capability need different evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗證問題是是否符合要求；確認用途則問要求是否解決正確任務。 未測項目應保留為未決，不能由其他通過項目推定。","explanationEn":"Verification asks whether requirements are met; validation asks whether those requirements address the right mission. Untested items remain open; unrelated passes do not close them."}}]},{"id":"c005-stage02","order":2,"title":"複材製程與接合證據","titleEn":"Composite processing and joint evidence","description":"用教學試片了解層合、成形、缺陷與接合。","descriptionEn":"Use teaching coupons to understand laminates, forming, defects and joints.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c005-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-06"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"比較鋪層對稱與翹曲","titleEn":"Compare layup symmetry and warping","objective":"把堆疊順序連到熱變形。","objectiveEn":"Link stacking order to thermal deformation.","instruction":"畫對稱與不對稱層序；標每層方向；以紙片示意受熱後的彎曲可能性並註記只是類比。","instructionEn":"Draw symmetric and asymmetric stacks; mark ply directions; use paper to illustrate possible thermal curvature and label the analogy.","observation":"相同材料用量仍可能有不同耦合行為。","observationEn":"Equal material amounts may have different coupling behavior.","failure":"把紙模型變形量當真實碳纖維數值不成立。","failureEn":"Paper curvature is not a carbon-composite measurement.","check":"解釋層序與總厚度各自影響什麼。","checkEn":"Explain the distinct effects of stacking and total thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"不對稱層合可使面內負載與彎曲耦合；對稱並不自動保證所有性能合格。","textEn":"Unsymmetric laminates can couple in-plane loads to bending; symmetry alone does not ensure all requirements are met."},{"id":"c005-v7-07-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"熱膨脹、工具約束與固化收縮都可能影響成形幾何。","textEn":"Thermal expansion, tooling constraints and cure shrinkage can all affect final geometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較鋪層對稱與翹曲」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare layup symmetry and warping’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["比較層序而非只比較厚度","只要厚度相同就不會翹曲","紙模型可給出飛機零件公差"],"optionsEn":["Compare stacking as well as thickness","Equal thickness prevents warping","A paper model specifies aircraft tolerances"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不對稱層合可使面內負載與彎曲耦合；對稱並不自動保證所有性能合格。 熱膨脹、工具約束與固化收縮都可能影響成形幾何。","explanationEn":"Unsymmetric laminates can couple in-plane loads to bending; symmetry alone does not ensure all requirements are met. Thermal expansion, tooling constraints and cure shrinkage can all affect final geometry."}},{"id":"c005-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-07"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"標記鋪帶間隙與重疊","titleEn":"Mark layup gaps and overlaps","objective":"辨認製程缺陷對幾何的影響。","objectiveEn":"Recognize process defects affecting geometry.","instruction":"在示意鋪帶圖標出間隙、重疊與轉向；用同一比例尺比較面積；寫出需要檢查的位置而不自行訂適航允收值。","instructionEn":"Mark gaps, overlaps and turns in a tape schematic; compare areas at one scale; identify inspection locations without inventing airworthiness limits.","observation":"局部增厚與樹脂區可能出現在不同位置。","observationEn":"Local thickening and resin-rich regions may occur separately.","failure":"只看總覆蓋率會漏掉集中缺陷。","failureEn":"Overall coverage can hide clustered defects.","check":"提交缺陷位置圖與待查設計依據。","checkEn":"Submit a defect-location map and required design references.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"幾何不連續可能改變局部纖維方向與載荷傳遞。","textEn":"Geometric discontinuities may change local fiber orientation and load transfer."},{"id":"c005-v7-08-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"允收取決於材料、位置與核准工程依據，不能由課程圖決定。","textEn":"Acceptance depends on material, location and approved engineering data, not this illustration."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「標記鋪帶間隙與重疊」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Mark layup gaps and overlaps’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任意修補就能恢復核准狀態","缺陷的位置和形態都重要","覆蓋率高即可忽略局部缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Any patch restores approval","Defect location and shape both matter","High coverage permits all local defects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何不連續可能改變局部纖維方向與載荷傳遞。 允收取決於材料、位置與核准工程依據，不能由課程圖決定。","explanationEn":"Geometric discontinuities may change local fiber orientation and load transfer. Acceptance depends on material, location and approved engineering data, not this illustration."}},{"id":"c005-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-08"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"檢查工具面與定位基準","titleEn":"Review tooling and datums","objective":"避免把量測座標系混在一起。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mixing measurement frames.","instruction":"在模具圖定義基準面與兩軸；把三個測點投影至同一座標系；再改一個基準並比較報表變化。","instructionEn":"Define a datum plane and two axes on a mold sketch; project three points into that frame; change a datum and compare reports.","observation":"不同基準可讓同一件看起來不同。","observationEn":"Different datums can make one part appear different.","failure":"比較沒有基準註記的數字會誤判。","failureEn":"Numbers without datum definitions mislead comparisons.","check":"所有測點都附座標框架與單位。","checkEn":"Attach a frame and units to every point.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"基準建立可重複的幾何參考，不等於工具永遠不會熱變形。","textEn":"Datums establish repeatable geometry references, not thermally invariant tooling."},{"id":"c005-v7-09-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"工具、零件與量測裝置各有不確定度，應分開列帳。","textEn":"Tooling, parts and instruments have separate uncertainties that should be accounted for."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「檢查工具面與定位基準」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review tooling and datums’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["座標數字越多越準","工具基準不需記錄","先統一基準再比較量測"],"optionsEn":["More coordinate digits guarantee accuracy","Tool datums need no record","Unify datums before comparing measurements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"基準建立可重複的幾何參考，不等於工具永遠不會熱變形。 工具、零件與量測裝置各有不確定度，應分開列帳。","explanationEn":"Datums establish repeatable geometry references, not thermally invariant tooling. Tooling, parts and instruments have separate uncertainties that should be accounted for."}},{"id":"c005-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-09"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"閱讀固化歷程而不配製配方","titleEn":"Read cure histories without prescribing a recipe","objective":"辨認歷程資料與合格判定的關係。","objectiveEn":"Relate history records to conformity decisions.","instruction":"畫無量綱的溫度與時間示意；標感測器位置、資料空缺與升降段；比較兩條歷程並提出待查問題。","instructionEn":"Draw a dimensionless temperature-time sketch; mark sensor positions, gaps and ramps; compare two histories and list questions for review.","observation":"單一最高溫度無法描述整段歷程。","observationEn":"A peak temperature does not describe a full history.","failure":"將教學曲線當真實固化設定會誤用。","failureEn":"Treating the teaching curve as a production cure schedule is misuse.","check":"說明為何需要位置、時間與材料對應。","checkEn":"Explain why location, time and material identity matter.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"固化涉及樹脂反應、熱傳與壓實，過程證據應連回特定材料系統。","textEn":"Cure involves resin reaction, heat transfer and consolidation; evidence must link to a particular material system."},{"id":"c005-v7-10-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"感測點量到的是局部歷程，厚度與熱邊界差異可能造成零件內部溫度梯度；代表性須另驗證。","textEn":"Sensors record local histories; thickness and thermal boundaries can create internal gradients, so representativeness needs verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「閱讀固化歷程而不配製配方」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Read cure histories without prescribing a recipe’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["完整歷程比單一峰值更有資訊","最高溫相同就完全等效","任一教學曲線可套用所有樹脂"],"optionsEn":["Full histories carry more information than peaks","Equal peak temperatures mean equivalence","One teaching curve suits every resin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"固化涉及樹脂反應、熱傳與壓實，過程證據應連回特定材料系統。 感測點量到的是局部歷程，厚度與熱邊界差異可能造成零件內部溫度梯度；代表性須另驗證。","explanationEn":"Cure involves resin reaction, heat transfer and consolidation; evidence must link to a particular material system. Sensors record local histories; thickness and thermal boundaries can create internal gradients, so representativeness needs verification."}},{"id":"c005-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-10"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"比較非破壞檢測訊號","titleEn":"Compare nondestructive inspection signals","objective":"把可見表面與內部缺陷分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate surface appearance from internal defects.","instruction":"畫完好與疑似分層的教學截面；為每個截面配一條虛構回波；列出參考試塊與訊號不確定因素。","instructionEn":"Draw sound and suspected-delamination sections; attach invented echo traces; list reference-block and uncertainty factors.","observation":"訊號差異需要校準與幾何背景。","observationEn":"Signal differences need calibration and geometry context.","failure":"把每個回波都當缺陷會誤報。","failureEn":"Treating every echo as a defect creates false alarms.","check":"指出一個可能真缺陷與一個幾何干擾。","checkEn":"Identify a possible defect and a geometric confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"非破壞檢測仍有可偵測性限制；沒有指示不等於不存在任何缺陷。","textEn":"Nondestructive inspection has detection limits; no indication does not prove the absence of every defect."},{"id":"c005-v7-11-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"參考試件讓設備響應與材料幾何建立對照；參考件與受檢區差異越大，判讀適用性越需審查。","textEn":"Reference specimens connect instrument response with geometry and material; larger differences from inspected regions require closer applicability review."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較非破壞檢測訊號」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare nondestructive inspection signals’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任何回波都代表分層","判讀需要參考件與位置資訊","表面平整證明內部無缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Every echo is delamination","Interpretation needs references and location","A smooth surface proves no internal defect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"非破壞檢測仍有可偵測性限制；沒有指示不等於不存在任何缺陷。 參考試件讓設備響應與材料幾何建立對照；參考件與受檢區差異越大，判讀適用性越需審查。","explanationEn":"Nondestructive inspection has detection limits; no indication does not prove the absence of every defect. Reference specimens connect instrument response with geometry and material; larger differences from inspected regions require closer applicability review."}},{"id":"c005-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-11"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"分析複材接頭的載荷轉移","titleEn":"Analyze load transfer in composite joints","objective":"區分接頭整體力與局部應力。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish overall joint force from local stress.","instruction":"畫簡化搭接與對接兩種模型；標出剪力、承壓與偏心；比較改變接合長度的可能影響。","instructionEn":"Draw simplified lap and butt joints; mark shear, bearing and eccentricity; compare possible effects of changing joint length.","observation":"受力可能集中於接頭端部。","observationEn":"Loads may concentrate near joint ends.","failure":"把平均應力當所有位置應力會漏判。","failureEn":"Treating average stress as local stress misses concentrations.","check":"交出載荷路徑與一個偏心造成的問題。","checkEn":"Submit a load path and one eccentricity-related issue.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"膠接、機械接合與混合接頭具有不同失效模式，不能只用接合面積比較。","textEn":"Bonded, mechanical and hybrid joints have different failure modes; area alone is insufficient."},{"id":"c005-v7-12-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"偏心搭接會引入彎曲與剝離效應，增加接合長度不保證端部應力按同一比例下降。","textEn":"Eccentric lap joints introduce bending and peel; increasing overlap does not guarantee proportional reduction in end stresses."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分析複材接頭的載荷轉移」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Analyze load transfer in composite joints’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["平均應力即可預測所有失效","接合面積加倍保證強度加倍","接頭需檢查局部與整體行為"],"optionsEn":["Average stress predicts every failure","Doubling area guarantees double strength","Review both local and overall joint behavior"],"answer":2,"explanation":"膠接、機械接合與混合接頭具有不同失效模式，不能只用接合面積比較。 偏心搭接會引入彎曲與剝離效應，增加接合長度不保證端部應力按同一比例下降。","explanationEn":"Bonded, mechanical and hybrid joints have different failure modes; area alone is insufficient. Eccentric lap joints introduce bending and peel; increasing overlap does not guarantee proportional reduction in end stresses."}}]},{"id":"c005-stage03","order":3,"title":"總裝與機電整合","titleEn":"Final assembly and electromechanical integration","description":"分開幾何介面、電力供應、散熱與資料責任。","descriptionEn":"Separate geometry, power, cooling and data responsibilities.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c005-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-12"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"對齊機身段的共同座標","titleEn":"Align fuselage sections in a common frame","objective":"理解大型總裝的幾何介面。","objectiveEn":"Understand geometry interfaces in large assembly.","instruction":"畫兩段圓筒與各自基準；轉成共同軸線；加入平移、傾角兩種偏差並分別記錄。","instructionEn":"Draw two cylinders with local datums; transform to a common axis; introduce translation and tilt and record them separately.","observation":"角度偏差隨距離放大為位置偏差。","observationEn":"Angular errors grow into positional errors over distance.","failure":"只對齊一個點不能確定整段姿態。","failureEn":"Aligning one point cannot define a whole section attitude.","check":"用三個不共線參考點說明姿態。","checkEn":"Explain attitude using three non-collinear references.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-13-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"大型零件對接同時管理位置與姿態；局部貼合不代表整體軸線一致。","textEn":"Large-part mating controls position and attitude; local contact does not establish global alignment."},{"id":"c005-v7-13-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"剛體模型忽略零件彈性，實際量測應考慮支撐與溫度。","textEn":"A rigid model omits elasticity; real metrology must consider support and temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「對齊機身段的共同座標」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Align fuselage sections in a common frame’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["需要共同基準及姿態資訊","接觸一點即完全對齊","可忽略支撐造成變形"],"optionsEn":["Use common datums and attitude information","One touching point proves alignment","Support deformation is irrelevant"],"answer":0,"explanation":"大型零件對接同時管理位置與姿態；局部貼合不代表整體軸線一致。 剛體模型忽略零件彈性，實際量測應考慮支撐與溫度。","explanationEn":"Large-part mating controls position and attitude; local contact does not establish global alignment. A rigid model omits elasticity; real metrology must consider support and temperature."}},{"id":"c005-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-13"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"建立公差與不確定度預算","titleEn":"Build tolerance and uncertainty budgets","objective":"分開設計範圍與量測能力。","objectiveEn":"Separate design allowance from measurement capability.","instruction":"給三個教學尺寸各一個假設範圍；計算最差方向疊加；另列儀器不確定度並說明不能混稱公差。","instructionEn":"Assign assumed ranges to three dimensions; sum worst-case directions; list instrument uncertainty separately and explain the distinction.","observation":"名義尺寸吻合不保證所有組合可裝配。","observationEn":"Matching nominal dimensions does not guarantee assembly in every combination.","failure":"把量測解析度當不確定度不成立。","failureEn":"Display resolution is not measurement uncertainty.","check":"保留名義值、允許範圍及量測不確定度三欄。","checkEn":"Keep nominal value, allowance and uncertainty in separate columns.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-14-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"公差是設計容許範圍，不確定度是對測量結果的認識限制。","textEn":"Tolerance is a design allowance; uncertainty describes limits of knowledge about a measurement."},{"id":"c005-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"統計疊加要有分布與相關性假設，不能盲目替代最差情境。","textEn":"Statistical stacks need distribution and correlation assumptions and cannot blindly replace worst-case analysis."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立公差與不確定度預算」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build tolerance and uncertainty budgets’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有尺寸誤差一定互相抵消","公差與不確定度應分列","顯示更多小數即可保證裝配"],"optionsEn":["All dimensional errors cancel","List tolerance and uncertainty separately","More displayed decimals guarantee assembly"],"answer":1,"explanation":"公差是設計容許範圍，不確定度是對測量結果的認識限制。 統計疊加要有分布與相關性假設，不能盲目替代最差情境。","explanationEn":"Tolerance is a design allowance; uncertainty describes limits of knowledge about a measurement. Statistical stacks need distribution and correlation assumptions and cannot blindly replace worst-case analysis."}},{"id":"c005-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-14"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"辨識異材接觸與雷擊路徑","titleEn":"Identify material interfaces and lightning paths","objective":"把環境保護連到結構與導電介面。","objectiveEn":"Link environmental protection to structural and conductive interfaces.","instruction":"標示碳纖維與金屬接合處；另畫示意電流路徑；圈出需查隔離、搭接與檢驗證據的地方。","instructionEn":"Mark carbon-fiber–metal interfaces; draw a separate illustrative current path; circle locations needing isolation, bonding and inspection evidence.","observation":"機械接合與電氣連續性不能互相代替。","observationEn":"Mechanical attachment and electrical continuity are different properties.","failure":"以外觀漆面判定防雷能力會誤導。","failureEn":"Paint appearance cannot establish lightning protection.","check":"區分腐蝕問題與瞬態導電問題。","checkEn":"Distinguish corrosion from transient-current problems.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-15-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"異材接觸可能引入電化學腐蝕條件；防護設計需要環境與材料相容性評估。","textEn":"Dissimilar materials can create galvanic conditions; protection needs environmental and compatibility assessment."},{"id":"c005-v7-15-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"導電路徑的不連續可能造成局部電位差與發熱；機械牢固不能替代電气連續性證據。","textEn":"Discontinuous conducting paths can create local potential differences and heating; mechanical attachment does not establish electrical continuity."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「辨識異材接觸與雷擊路徑」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Identify material interfaces and lightning paths’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["有金屬螺栓就完成全部防雷","碳纖維不必考虑電性","分別檢查材料相容性與導電路徑"],"optionsEn":["Metal bolts complete all lightning protection","Carbon composites have no electrical considerations","Check compatibility and current paths separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"異材接觸可能引入電化學腐蝕條件；防護設計需要環境與材料相容性評估。 導電路徑的不連續可能造成局部電位差與發熱；機械牢固不能替代電气連續性證據。","explanationEn":"Dissimilar materials can create galvanic conditions; protection needs environmental and compatibility assessment. Discontinuous conducting paths can create local potential differences and heating; mechanical attachment does not establish electrical continuity."}},{"id":"c005-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-15"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"拆解更多電力架構","titleEn":"Decompose more-electric architecture","objective":"理解來源、匯流排與負載分工。","objectiveEn":"Understand sources, buses and load allocation.","instruction":"畫發電來源、轉換器與三組教學負載；以不同色標示獨立通道；移除一個來源後檢查哪些功能仍有供應。","instructionEn":"Draw sources, converters and three teaching loads; color independent channels; remove one source and inspect remaining supplied functions.","observation":"冗餘需要避免共用單點故障。","observationEn":"Redundancy must avoid shared single-point failures.","failure":"畫兩條線但共用同一失效點不是有效獨立。","failureEn":"Two lines sharing one failure point are not effectively independent.","check":"標出正常與單點故障下的功能狀態。","checkEn":"Mark functional states in normal and single-failure cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-16-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"更多電力架構把部分功能的能源需求轉給電系，也提高轉換與熱管理的重要性。","textEn":"More-electric architecture shifts some energy demands to electrical systems and raises conversion and thermal-management importance."},{"id":"c005-v7-16-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"故障後可維持的功能取決於剩餘來源能力與負載優先序；備援數量不能取代功率平衡。","textEn":"Retained functions after failure depend on remaining source capacity and load priorities; backup count cannot replace power balance."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「拆解更多電力架構」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Decompose more-electric architecture’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["檢查兩通道是否共享失效點","所有負載都可任意接同一來源","線條數量就是可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Check channels for shared failure points","Arbitrarily connect every load to one source","Line count alone determines reliability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"更多電力架構把部分功能的能源需求轉給電系，也提高轉換與熱管理的重要性。 故障後可維持的功能取決於剩餘來源能力與負載優先序；備援數量不能取代功率平衡。","explanationEn":"More-electric architecture shifts some energy demands to electrical systems and raises conversion and thermal-management importance. Retained functions after failure depend on remaining source capacity and load priorities; backup count cannot replace power balance."}},{"id":"c005-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-16"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"連結電力損失與散熱","titleEn":"Connect electrical losses to cooling","objective":"把效率與熱流納入同一預算。","objectiveEn":"Include efficiency and heat flow in one budget.","instruction":"為假想轉換器設定輸入與輸出功率；相減得到損失；把熱流箭頭連至冷卻介面並註明例子非機型數據。","instructionEn":"Assign hypothetical converter input and output powers; subtract for loss; connect heat arrows to a cooling interface and label the example non-aircraft-specific.","observation":"電力沒有消失，損失多轉成熱。","observationEn":"Electrical losses often become heat rather than disappearing.","failure":"把效率百分比直接當瓦數是單位錯誤。","failureEn":"Treating an efficiency percentage as watts is a unit error.","check":"完成輸入等於輸出加損失的平衡。","checkEn":"Close input = output + loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-17-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"效率需指定負載條件；高效率不代表在高功率下可忽略散熱。","textEn":"Efficiency needs a load condition; high efficiency does not make cooling negligible at high power."},{"id":"c005-v7-17-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"熱界面能力還受溫差、流阻與環境條件限制。","textEn":"Thermal interfaces also depend on temperature differences, flow resistance and environment."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「連結電力損失與散熱」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Connect electrical losses to cooling’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["輸出功率一定大於輸入","仍需依實際損失量設計散熱","效率高於九成就完全不發熱"],"optionsEn":["Output must exceed input","Size cooling for actual losses","Above ninety percent efficiency means no heat"],"answer":1,"explanation":"效率需指定負載條件；高效率不代表在高功率下可忽略散熱。 熱界面能力還受溫差、流阻與環境條件限制。","explanationEn":"Efficiency needs a load condition; high efficiency does not make cooling negligible at high power. Thermal interfaces also depend on temperature differences, flow resistance and environment."}},{"id":"c005-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-17"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"審查資料介面與故障隔離","titleEn":"Review data interfaces and fault isolation","objective":"讓控制資訊有明確來源與時效。","objectiveEn":"Give control information explicit origin and freshness.","instruction":"建立教學感測資料表，含單位與時間戳；模擬延遲及失聯；替每種狀況定義待查訊息與降級狀態。","instructionEn":"Create a teaching sensor table with units and timestamps; simulate delay and loss; define review messages and degraded states for each.","observation":"數值合理仍可能是過期資料。","observationEn":"A plausible value may still be stale.","failure":"只驗證資料有到達會漏掉語意錯誤。","failureEn":"Arrival checks alone miss semantic errors.","check":"逐欄核對單位、時基、來源與失效狀態。","checkEn":"Check units, timebase, origin and failure state for each field.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-18-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"介面契約同時包含格式、時序與失效行為。","textEn":"An interface contract includes format, timing and failure behavior."},{"id":"c005-v7-18-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"故障隔離需要獨立證據，不能讓同一錯誤訊號自我證明正確。","textEn":"Fault isolation needs independent evidence; one faulty signal cannot certify itself."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「審查資料介面與故障隔離」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review data interfaces and fault isolation’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["收到任意數字即代表正常","延遲永遠不影響控制","時效與單位也是介面要求"],"optionsEn":["Any received number proves health","Delay never affects control","Freshness and units are interface requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"介面契約同時包含格式、時序與失效行為。 故障隔離需要獨立證據，不能讓同一錯誤訊號自我證明正確。","explanationEn":"An interface contract includes format, timing and failure behavior. Fault isolation needs independent evidence; one faulty signal cannot certify itself."}}]},{"id":"c005-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證、可靠度與交付","titleEn":"Verification, reliability and delivery","description":"讓每項設計主張都能指向合適的試驗證據。","descriptionEn":"Link each design claim to appropriate test evidence.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c005-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-18"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"區分靜力與疲勞證據","titleEn":"Distinguish static and fatigue evidence","objective":"避免一次承載取代壽命主張。","objectiveEn":"Avoid substituting one load test for lifetime evidence.","instruction":"畫單次載荷與重複載荷兩種時間圖；為兩圖寫不同問題；列出需記錄的破壞與損傷指標。","instructionEn":"Draw single-load and repeated-load histories; write a different question for each; list damage and failure indicators to record.","observation":"可承受一次負載不代表可承受所有循環。","observationEn":"Surviving one load does not establish cyclic capability.","failure":"宣稱複材完全不會疲勞或損傷不正確。","failureEn":"Claiming composites cannot fatigue or damage is incorrect.","check":"用一句話各界定強度與耐久性。","checkEn":"Define strength and durability separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-19-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"複材可能出現基材裂紋、分層等損傷，機制與金屬裂紋並不完全相同。","textEn":"Composites may develop matrix cracks and delamination; their mechanisms differ from metal cracking."},{"id":"c005-v7-19-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"試驗結論依載荷譜、環境與試件配置而定；改變其中一項後，原有壽命結論須重新檢查。","textEn":"Test conclusions depend on load spectrum, environment and specimen configuration; changing any of them requires reviewing lifetime conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「區分靜力與疲勞證據」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Distinguish static and fatigue evidence’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["靜力通過不能取代疲勞評估","碳纖維結構絕不會累積損傷","一次高載荷代表全部壽命"],"optionsEn":["Static success cannot replace fatigue evaluation","Carbon structures never accumulate damage","One high load proves full lifetime"],"answer":0,"explanation":"複材可能出現基材裂紋、分層等損傷，機制與金屬裂紋並不完全相同。 試驗結論依載荷譜、環境與試件配置而定；改變其中一項後，原有壽命結論須重新檢查。","explanationEn":"Composites may develop matrix cracks and delamination; their mechanisms differ from metal cracking. Test conclusions depend on load spectrum, environment and specimen configuration; changing any of them requires reviewing lifetime conclusions."}},{"id":"c005-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-19"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"分析壓力循環與局部開口","titleEn":"Analyze pressure cycles and cutouts","objective":"看見孔口附近的受力轉移。","objectiveEn":"Recognize force transfer around openings.","instruction":"畫完整圓筒與有窗孔圓筒；在孔周追蹤膜力；標出加強區並比較循環壓差的問題。","instructionEn":"Draw intact and windowed cylinders; trace membrane forces around the opening; mark reinforcement and compare cyclic-pressure concerns.","observation":"開口迫使載荷繞行。","observationEn":"Openings redirect loads.","failure":"只用完整薄殼公式評估孔邊會漏掉局部效應。","failureEn":"An intact-shell formula misses opening-edge effects.","check":"提交局部載荷繞行圖及限制註記。","checkEn":"Submit a local load-bypass sketch with limitations.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-20-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"薄殼公式可作遠離不連續處的初步估算，但接頭、孔口與局部屈曲需更細模型。","textEn":"Thin-shell formulas give preliminary estimates away from discontinuities; joints, cutouts and buckling need finer models."},{"id":"c005-v7-20-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"壓力循環、濕熱與缺陷可能耦合；示意模型不能給飛行壽命。","textEn":"Pressure cycles, moisture, temperature and defects can interact; a sketch cannot establish flight life."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分析壓力循環與局部開口」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Analyze pressure cycles and cutouts’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只有外形最漂亮的窗才安全","需要補充孔邊的局部分析","孔洞不會改變應力"],"optionsEn":["Window appearance determines safety","Add local analysis around openings","Openings cannot alter stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄殼公式可作遠離不連續處的初步估算，但接頭、孔口與局部屈曲需更細模型。 壓力循環、濕熱與缺陷可能耦合；示意模型不能給飛行壽命。","explanationEn":"Thin-shell formulas give preliminary estimates away from discontinuities; joints, cutouts and buckling need finer models. Pressure cycles, moisture, temperature and defects can interact; a sketch cannot establish flight life."}},{"id":"c005-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-20"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"解釋氣動彈性耦合","titleEn":"Explain aeroelastic coupling","objective":"區分剛體氣動與柔性回饋。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish rigid aerodynamics from flexible feedback.","instruction":"畫氣流、機翼變形與載荷三節點；連成回饋環；改變假想剛度，說明需要哪些試驗而不推算真機邊界。","instructionEn":"Draw airflow, wing deformation and load nodes; connect a feedback loop; change assumed stiffness and identify required tests without predicting aircraft limits.","observation":"變形可以反過來改變氣動載荷。","observationEn":"Deformation can change aerodynamic loading.","failure":"只看靜態撓度不能確定動態穩定。","failureEn":"Static deflection alone cannot establish dynamic stability.","check":"指出回饋鏈中至少兩個不確定因素。","checkEn":"Identify at least two uncertainties in the feedback chain.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-21-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"氣動彈性涉及結構、慣性與氣動的耦合，穩定性需條件完整的分析與驗證。","textEn":"Aeroelasticity couples structure, inertia and aerodynamics; stability needs fully specified analysis and validation."},{"id":"c005-v7-21-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"縮尺試驗涉及相似律，不能僅按長度比例複製。","textEn":"Scale tests require similarity considerations, not just geometric scaling."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「解釋氣動彈性耦合」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Explain aeroelastic coupling’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["靜止時不晃動就永不顫振","縮小尺寸即可保持所有動態特性","柔性與氣動必須一起評估"],"optionsEn":["No motion at rest proves no flutter","Shrinking dimensions preserves all dynamics","Evaluate flexibility and aerodynamics together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣動彈性涉及結構、慣性與氣動的耦合，穩定性需條件完整的分析與驗證。 縮尺試驗涉及相似律，不能僅按長度比例複製。","explanationEn":"Aeroelasticity couples structure, inertia and aerodynamics; stability needs fully specified analysis and validation. Scale tests require similarity considerations, not just geometric scaling."}},{"id":"c005-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-21"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"設計軟體與硬體整合案例","titleEn":"Design software–hardware integration cases","objective":"測到正常與異常介面行為。","objectiveEn":"Exercise nominal and abnormal interface behavior.","instruction":"寫三個模擬案例：正常、延遲、錯誤單位；指定預期輸出；比較實際記錄與預期並保存配置。","instructionEn":"Write nominal, delayed and wrong-unit simulation cases; specify expected outputs; compare results against expectations and record configuration.","observation":"可重現故障比偶然成功更能定位問題。","observationEn":"Reproducible faults localize issues better than accidental success.","failure":"只有正常案例無法覆蓋例外行為。","failureEn":"Nominal cases alone do not cover exceptions.","check":"每個案例含輸入、預期、實際與版本。","checkEn":"Include input, expected result, actual result and version in each case.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-22-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"整合試驗驗證介面假設；單元測試通過不表示完整系統必然正常。","textEn":"Integration tests check interface assumptions; passing unit tests does not guarantee system success."},{"id":"c005-v7-22-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"模擬覆蓋率不等於真機驗證完備，模型本身也需確認。","textEn":"Simulation coverage does not equal complete aircraft verification; models require validation too."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「設計軟體與硬體整合案例」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Design software–hardware integration cases’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["故障注入應有明確預期結果","只跑一次正常輸入即可","模型通過即可免除其他驗證"],"optionsEn":["Fault injection needs explicit expected results","One nominal input is sufficient","Model success eliminates all other verification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"整合試驗驗證介面假設；單元測試通過不表示完整系統必然正常。 模擬覆蓋率不等於真機驗證完備，模型本身也需確認。","explanationEn":"Integration tests check interface assumptions; passing unit tests does not guarantee system success. Simulation coverage does not equal complete aircraft verification; models require validation too."}},{"id":"c005-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-22"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"整理不合格與設計變更鏈","titleEn":"Organize nonconformance and design changes","objective":"避免修改破壞既有驗證。","objectiveEn":"Prevent changes from invalidating prior evidence.","instruction":"假設一個接頭材料改版；列受影響的圖、分析與試驗；標出要重驗、可沿用及待證明的項目。","instructionEn":"Assume a joint material revision; list affected drawings, analyses and tests; mark retest, reusable and unresolved evidence.","observation":"小改動也可能跨越材料與電性介面。","observationEn":"A small change can cross material and electrical interfaces.","failure":"只改圖號不檢查證據適用性不完整。","failureEn":"Changing a drawing number without reviewing evidence is incomplete.","check":"用影響矩陣連接改動與全部相關主張。","checkEn":"Link the change to relevant claims in an impact matrix.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-23-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"配置控制讓證據對應到真正受驗的物件，而不是抽象的產品名稱。","textEn":"Configuration control ties evidence to the item actually tested, not an abstract product name."},{"id":"c005-v7-23-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"重用證據需說明等效性；無理由的沿用是未決風險。","textEn":"Reusing evidence requires an equivalence argument; unexplained reuse remains unresolved."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「整理不合格與設計變更鏈」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Organize nonconformance and design changes’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["材料改變不會影響電氣介面","變更後重新判斷證據適用性","只要產品名稱相同即可沿用"],"optionsEn":["Material changes never affect electrical interfaces","Reassess evidence applicability after change","A shared product name justifies all reuse"],"answer":1,"explanation":"配置控制讓證據對應到真正受驗的物件，而不是抽象的產品名稱。 重用證據需說明等效性；無理由的沿用是未決風險。","explanationEn":"Configuration control ties evidence to the item actually tested, not an abstract product name. Reusing evidence requires an equivalence argument; unexplained reuse remains unresolved."}},{"id":"c005-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"prerequisiteIds":["c005-v7-23"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-787-design","v7-science-composite-handbook","v7-science-787-production"],"title":"完成總工程師交付審查","titleEn":"Complete the chief-engineer review","objective":"以可追溯證據說明能與不能主張的事。","objectiveEn":"State what evidence does and does not support.","instruction":"彙整材料、結構、電力三份圖；把每個結論連至檢核紀錄；列三個尚需專業驗證的問題並比較 A350 相近課程。","instructionEn":"Collect material, structure and power diagrams; link conclusions to review records; list three questions needing professional verification and compare the related A350 course.","observation":"總裝完成與適航放行是不同里程碑。","observationEn":"Assembly completion and airworthiness release are different milestones.","failure":"把完成學習勾選當真實製造資格會誤解。","failureEn":"Course completion is not manufacturing qualification.","check":"審查表中包含證據、限制、未決事項與相似工法。","checkEn":"Include evidence, limits, open issues and related methods.","knowledge":[{"id":"c005-v7-24-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"大型客機共同面對複材、系統介面及試驗追溯；各型號實作不能直接互換。","textEn":"Large airliners share composite, interface and test-traceability problems; implementations are not interchangeable."},{"id":"c005-v7-24-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"交付審查可用主張—證據—未決事項矩陣，避免把缺資料誤寫為零風險，並保留責任與版本。","textEn":"Delivery review can use a claim–evidence–open-item matrix to avoid mistaking missing information for zero risk and to preserve responsibility and version."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「完成總工程師交付審查」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Complete the chief-engineer review’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有相似飛機可共用維修方法","完成課程即可核准真機放行","結論應與配置及證據一起呈現"],"optionsEn":["Similar aircraft share all maintenance methods","Course completion authorizes aircraft release","Present conclusions with configuration and evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"大型客機共同面對複材、系統介面及試驗追溯；各型號實作不能直接互換。 交付審查可用主張—證據—未決事項矩陣，避免把缺資料誤寫為零風險，並保留責任與版本。","explanationEn":"Large airliners share composite, interface and test-traceability problems; implementations are not interchangeable. Delivery review can use a claim–evidence–open-item matrix to avoid mistaking missing information for zero risk and to preserve responsibility and version."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":7,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":600},{"id":"c325","title":"James Webb 太空望遠鏡","titleEn":"James Webb Space Telescope","category":"space","kind":"course","summary":"以二十四步拆解紅外觀測、分段鏡對準、遮陽隔熱、展開與地面驗證。","summaryEn":"Twenty-four steps examine infrared observation, mirror phasing, shielding, deployment and ground verification.","scope":"所有圖解與數值為公開原理的教學模型；不是 NASA 操作程序、飛行軟體或可製造的望遠鏡圖。地圖指向 Goddard 地面機構，Webb 本體位於日地 L2 附近軌道。","scopeEn":"Diagrams and numbers are teaching models of public principles, not NASA procedures, flight software or buildable telescope drawings. The map marks Goddard on Earth; Webb itself orbits near Sun–Earth L2.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-wavefront","v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-launch","v7-science-webb-first-images","v7-science-goddard-address","v10-other-vendor-c325"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"space","labels":["入射光","分段鏡","冷儀器","地面資料"],"labelsEn":["Incoming light","Segmented mirror","Cold instruments","Ground data"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"c325-stage01","order":1,"title":"觀測需求與系統分界","titleEn":"Observation needs and system boundaries","description":"由光子、熱與幾何理解太空望遠鏡。","descriptionEn":"Understand the telescope through photons, heat and geometry.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c325-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-mirrors"],"title":"把科學問題轉成觀測量","titleEn":"Translate science questions into observables","objective":"區分亮度、位置與光譜問題。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish brightness, position and spectral questions.","instruction":"選星系與系外行星兩種假想問題；寫出要量的物理量；為每個量指定成像或光譜並標記未知條件。","instructionEn":"Choose hypothetical galaxy and exoplanet questions; write the measured quantities; assign imaging or spectroscopy and mark unknown conditions.","observation":"不同科學問題需要不同資料產品。","observationEn":"Different science questions need different data products.","failure":"把所有觀測都稱為拍照會遺漏光譜。","failureEn":"Calling every observation a photograph omits spectroscopy.","check":"交出問題、觀測量、儀器功能三欄表。","checkEn":"Submit question, observable and instrument-function columns.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"成像保留空間分布；光譜把光分到波長座標以分析訊號。","textEn":"Imaging preserves spatial distribution; spectroscopy separates light by wavelength for analysis."},{"id":"c325-v7-01-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"科學結論需要校準與模型，不能由單一美化影像直接推出。","textEn":"Scientific conclusions need calibration and models, not a single presentation image."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「把科學問題轉成觀測量」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Translate science questions into observables’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["先決定觀測量再選資料形式","所有問題只需要彩色圖片","亮點的顏色可直接等同物質成分"],"optionsEn":["Define observables before selecting data form","Every question needs only a color picture","A bright spot’s displayed color directly identifies composition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"成像保留空間分布；光譜把光分到波長座標以分析訊號。 科學結論需要校準與模型，不能由單一美化影像直接推出。","explanationEn":"Imaging preserves spatial distribution; spectroscopy separates light by wavelength for analysis. Scientific conclusions need calibration and models, not a single presentation image."}},{"id":"c325-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-01"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-instruments"],"title":"辨識紅外波段與熱背景","titleEn":"Identify infrared bands and thermal background","objective":"理解儀器自身也會產生背景。","objectiveEn":"Understand that the instrument also contributes background.","instruction":"畫目標光與望遠鏡熱輻射兩條路；用相同單位標示概念訊號；比較冷卻前後的背景比例。","instructionEn":"Draw target-light and telescope-emission paths; label conceptual signals in matching units; compare background fractions before and after cooling.","observation":"降低背景可改善微弱訊號的辨識。","observationEn":"Lower background can improve detection of faint signals.","failure":"把冷卻等同增加目標亮度不正確。","failureEn":"Cooling does not brighten the target itself.","check":"分別說明訊號來源與背景來源。","checkEn":"Explain signal and background origins separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"紅外偵測中，儀器熱輻射可能與天體訊號競爭。","textEn":"Instrumental thermal emission may compete with astronomical infrared signals."},{"id":"c325-v7-02-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"冷卻效果受波段、探測器與熱路徑影響，不能只用一個溫度概括。","textEn":"Cooling effects depend on band, detector and thermal paths, not one temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「辨識紅外波段與熱背景」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Identify infrared bands and thermal background’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有波長有相同熱背景","冷卻主要改變儀器背景","冷卻會讓遠方天體本身更亮"],"optionsEn":["Every wavelength has identical thermal background","Cooling mainly changes instrumental background","Cooling makes distant objects intrinsically brighter"],"answer":1,"explanation":"紅外偵測中，儀器熱輻射可能與天體訊號競爭。 冷卻效果受波段、探測器與熱路徑影響，不能只用一個溫度概括。","explanationEn":"Instrumental thermal emission may compete with astronomical infrared signals. Cooling effects depend on band, detector and thermal paths, not one temperature alone."}},{"id":"c325-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-02"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-launch","v7-science-goddard-address","v7-science-webb-shield"],"title":"分開 L2 軌道與地面座標","titleEn":"Separate L2 orbit from ground coordinates","objective":"避免用地圖標記誤解太空位置。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mistaking a map marker for a space position.","instruction":"畫太陽、地球與 L2 概念圖；另開 Goddard 的地圖卡；為兩圖標不同座標系與物件名稱。","instructionEn":"Sketch Sun, Earth and L2; open the separate Goddard map card; label different frames and objects on the two diagrams.","observation":"地理地址表示機構，不表示太空載具位置。","observationEn":"A street address locates an institution, not the spacecraft.","failure":"將地圖經緯度寫成 Webb 本體座標會誤導。","failureEn":"Calling map latitude/longitude the Webb position is misleading.","check":"能清楚解釋地面點與軌道示意的差別。","checkEn":"Explain the difference between a ground marker and an orbit schematic.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"L2 附近的軌道不是停在一個固定點；日地幾何與控制共同影響任務條件。","textEn":"An orbit near L2 is not a stationary point; Sun–Earth geometry and control influence mission conditions."},{"id":"c325-v7-03-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"地球經緯度與太空星曆使用不同座標系；位置還需時間、原點與座標方向，單有一對數字無法定位。","textEn":"Terrestrial coordinates and space ephemerides use different frames; position also needs time, origin and axes, not just two numbers."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分開 L2 軌道與地面座標」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate L2 orbit from ground coordinates’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["Webb 停在 Goddard 屋頂","L2 是地球上一個經緯度","Goddard 標記代表地面研發管理機構"],"optionsEn":["Webb sits on Goddard’s roof","L2 is a terrestrial latitude/longitude","The Goddard marker represents a ground research and management institution"],"answer":2,"explanation":"L2 附近的軌道不是停在一個固定點；日地幾何與控制共同影響任務條件。 地球經緯度與太空星曆使用不同座標系；位置還需時間、原點與座標方向，單有一對數字無法定位。","explanationEn":"An orbit near L2 is not a stationary point; Sun–Earth geometry and control influence mission conditions. Terrestrial coordinates and space ephemerides use different frames; position also needs time, origin and axes, not just two numbers."}},{"id":"c325-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-03"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-instruments"],"title":"分配收光面積與解析能力","titleEn":"Separate collecting area from resolution","objective":"辨識口徑影響的不同指標。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish the different effects of aperture.","instruction":"畫兩種假想口徑；用面積比較收光；再討論波長改變時繞射尺度如何變化。","instructionEn":"Draw two hypothetical apertures; compare area for light collection; discuss how diffraction scale changes with wavelength.","observation":"收光量與角解析力相互關聯但不是同一數值。","observationEn":"Light collection and angular resolution are related but distinct.","failure":"只用像素數代表光學解析力不成立。","failureEn":"Pixel count alone does not determine optical resolution.","check":"表格分列面積、波長、像素與角尺度。","checkEn":"List area, wavelength, pixels and angular scale separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"理想繞射尺度與波長成正比、口徑成反比；真實像質還受像差與取樣影響。","textEn":"Ideal diffraction scale grows with wavelength and decreases with aperture; real quality also depends on aberrations and sampling."},{"id":"c325-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"增加收光面積改善光子數，卻不能修正失焦或姿態抖動。","textEn":"More collecting area improves photon counts but does not correct defocus or pointing jitter."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分配收光面積與解析能力」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate collecting area from resolution’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["像質需同時看口徑、波長與取樣","增加像素即可無限提高解析度","收光面積就是角解析力的單位"],"optionsEn":["Assess aperture, wavelength and sampling together","More pixels provide unlimited resolution","Collecting area is a unit of angular resolution"],"answer":0,"explanation":"理想繞射尺度與波長成正比、口徑成反比；真實像質還受像差與取樣影響。 增加收光面積改善光子數，卻不能修正失焦或姿態抖動。","explanationEn":"Ideal diffraction scale grows with wavelength and decreases with aperture; real quality also depends on aberrations and sampling. More collecting area improves photon counts but does not correct defocus or pointing jitter."}},{"id":"c325-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-04"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-instruments"],"title":"繪製熱端與冷端介面","titleEn":"Draw hot-side and cold-side interfaces","objective":"找到跨越隔熱邊界的路徑。","objectiveEn":"Locate paths crossing thermal boundaries.","instruction":"將電源、通訊、鏡面與儀器分類；畫穿越遮陽板邊界的線；標記結構、電線與輻射三種熱路徑。","instructionEn":"Classify power, communications, mirrors and instruments; draw boundary-crossing links; mark structural, wiring and radiation heat paths.","observation":"遮住陽光不會消除所有熱傳。","observationEn":"Blocking sunlight does not remove every heat-transfer path.","failure":"忽略電纜導熱會漏掉跨界熱負載。","failureEn":"Ignoring cable conduction omits cross-boundary heat load.","check":"每條跨界線都有功能與熱影響註記。","checkEn":"Annotate function and thermal effect on each crossing.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"真空中沒有一般空氣對流，但仍有固體導熱與輻射。","textEn":"Vacuum removes ordinary air convection but not conduction or radiation."},{"id":"c325-v7-05-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"功能與隔熱要求可能衝突，需跨系統預算而不是單一零件最優化。","textEn":"Functional and isolation requirements may conflict, requiring a system budget rather than one-part optimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「繪製熱端與冷端介面」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Draw hot-side and cold-side interfaces’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["遮陽板可隔絕所有電線導熱","需同時檢查導熱與輻射","真空中完全沒有熱傳"],"optionsEn":["A sunshield blocks all cable conduction","Check conduction and radiation","Vacuum prevents all heat transfer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"真空中沒有一般空氣對流，但仍有固體導熱與輻射。 功能與隔熱要求可能衝突，需跨系統預算而不是單一零件最優化。","explanationEn":"Vacuum removes ordinary air convection but not conduction or radiation. Functional and isolation requirements may conflict, requiring a system budget rather than one-part optimization."}},{"id":"c325-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-05"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-launch"],"title":"建立收納與展開依賴圖","titleEn":"Build a stowage and deployment dependency graph","objective":"用先後條件理解複雜機構。","objectiveEn":"Understand complex mechanisms through prerequisites.","instruction":"畫收納外形與展開外形；列出三種假想先決條件；畫無循環依賴圖並標出不可逆動作。","instructionEn":"Draw stowed and deployed envelopes; list three hypothetical prerequisites; create an acyclic dependency graph and mark irreversible actions.","observation":"最後形狀可行不保證展開路徑可行。","observationEn":"A feasible final shape does not prove a feasible deployment path.","failure":"用動畫外觀取代接觸與相依分析會漏判。","failureEn":"Appearance-only animation misses contacts and dependencies.","check":"每個動作有前置狀態與完成證據。","checkEn":"Each action needs a prior state and completion evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"展開工程同時處理包絡、機構自由度與狀態確認。","textEn":"Deployment engineering addresses envelopes, mechanism degrees of freedom and state confirmation."},{"id":"c325-v7-06-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"若依賴圖出現循環，必須重新定義可達狀態；前置動作完成應有獨立狀態證據。","textEn":"Cycles in a dependency graph require redefining reachable states; prerequisite completion needs independent state evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立收納與展開依賴圖」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a stowage and deployment dependency graph’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只要終點正確就能任意展開","動作可全部同時執行","檢查整段路徑與先決條件"],"optionsEn":["Any deployment path works if the final shape is right","Every action can occur simultaneously","Check the entire path and prerequisites"],"answer":2,"explanation":"展開工程同時處理包絡、機構自由度與狀態確認。 若依賴圖出現循環，必須重新定義可達狀態；前置動作完成應有獨立狀態證據。","explanationEn":"Deployment engineering addresses envelopes, mechanism degrees of freedom and state confirmation. Cycles in a dependency graph require redefining reachable states; prerequisite completion needs independent state evidence."}}]},{"id":"c325-stage02","order":2,"title":"分段光學與波前","titleEn":"Segmented optics and wavefronts","description":"分清成像位置、相位與視場一致性。","descriptionEn":"Separate image position, phase and field consistency.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c325-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-06"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"理解分段鏡面的鋪排","titleEn":"Understand segmented-mirror tiling","objective":"把機械分段與光學整體分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate mechanical segments from optical unity.","instruction":"畫六角鏡片與間隙；標每片獨立身分；追蹤同一星光如何由多片鏡面貢獻。","instructionEn":"Draw hexagonal segments and gaps; identify each segment; trace how many segments contribute to one star image.","observation":"分段數不等於獨立望遠鏡數。","observationEn":"Segment count is not the number of separate telescopes.","failure":"把接縫抹掉並不代表光學已對準。","failureEn":"Removing drawn seams does not establish optical phasing.","check":"同時保留零件身分與共同波前概念。","checkEn":"Preserve part identity and the shared-wavefront concept.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"Webb 主鏡由十八片鏡段構成；能否形成共同波前取決於相對對準。","textEn":"Webb’s primary has eighteen segments; a common wavefront depends on relative alignment."},{"id":"c325-v7-07-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"分段形式解決尺寸與展開問題，也增加控制與驗證介面。","textEn":"Segmentation addresses packaging and deployment while adding control and verification interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「理解分段鏡面的鋪排」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Understand segmented-mirror tiling’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["多片鏡面需要共同的光學對準","每片只拍自己的天空區塊","接縫不見即代表相位一致"],"optionsEn":["Multiple segments need common optical alignment","Each segment photographs its own sky region","Invisible seams prove matched phase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Webb 主鏡由十八片鏡段構成；能否形成共同波前取決於相對對準。 分段形式解決尺寸與展開問題，也增加控制與驗證介面。","explanationEn":"Webb’s primary has eighteen segments; a common wavefront depends on relative alignment. Segmentation addresses packaging and deployment while adding control and verification interfaces."}},{"id":"c325-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-07"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"區分活塞與傾斜誤差","titleEn":"Distinguish piston and tilt errors","objective":"辨認不同自由度造成的像差。","objectiveEn":"Recognize errors from different degrees of freedom.","instruction":"畫兩片教學鏡面；一片只前後移、一片只旋轉；比較路徑長與光線方向並作註記。","instructionEn":"Draw two teaching mirror segments; translate one and rotate the other; compare path length and ray direction.","observation":"位置與傾角錯誤需要不同解釋。","observationEn":"Position and tilt errors require different interpretations.","failure":"只看光點中心無法涵蓋所有波前誤差。","failureEn":"Image-center position does not capture every wavefront error.","check":"圖中分別標出平移與旋轉。","checkEn":"Label translation and rotation separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"活塞改變相對光程，傾斜改變光線方向；二者不能視為同一調整量。","textEn":"Piston changes relative optical path; tilt changes ray direction; they are not the same adjustment."},{"id":"c325-v7-08-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"真實調整受多自由度耦合與感測可觀測性限制。","textEn":"Real alignment is limited by coupled degrees of freedom and observability."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「區分活塞與傾斜誤差」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Distinguish piston and tilt errors’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["平移與旋轉是同一自由度","需分辨位置與角度誤差","光點重疊即保證所有波前都一致"],"optionsEn":["Translation and rotation are identical","Distinguish positional and angular errors","Overlapping spots guarantee perfect wavefronts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"活塞改變相對光程，傾斜改變光線方向；二者不能視為同一調整量。 真實調整受多自由度耦合與感測可觀測性限制。","explanationEn":"Piston changes relative optical path; tilt changes ray direction; they are not the same adjustment. Real alignment is limited by coupled degrees of freedom and observability."}},{"id":"c325-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-08"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-wavefront","v7-science-webb-mirrors"],"title":"比較像點重疊與相位一致","titleEn":"Compare image stacking and phase agreement","objective":"了解幾何對準之後仍有光程問題。","objectiveEn":"Understand remaining optical-path issues after geometric alignment.","instruction":"將虛構星點移到同一中心；畫兩條不同相位的波形；列出中心重疊仍無法證明的事項。","instructionEn":"Move simulated star spots to one center; draw two waveforms with different phases; list what common centering does not establish.","observation":"同位置強度圖仍可能隱藏相位差。","observationEn":"Co-located intensity patterns may hide phase differences.","failure":"只用紅箭頭中心作相位驗證會誤導。","failureEn":"A centered guidance arrow is not a phase measurement.","check":"說明位置、相位與波前三者關係。","checkEn":"Explain image position, phase and wavefront relationships.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"光學相干疊加涉及相位；簡單幾何光線圖無法表達全部繞射行為。","textEn":"Coherent optical addition depends on phase; ray sketches cannot describe all diffraction effects."},{"id":"c325-v7-09-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"相位量測可能有週期性歧義；不同尺度的誤差估計能幫助區分大偏差與精細對準。","textEn":"Phase measurements can have periodic ambiguity; different error scales help distinguish large offsets from fine alignment."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較像點重疊與相位一致」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare image stacking and phase agreement’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["中心重疊就是全部對準完成","相位差等於鏡片顏色差","中心重疊之後仍需波前證據"],"optionsEn":["Center overlap completes all alignment","Phase difference is a color difference","Wavefront evidence is still needed after image stacking"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光學相干疊加涉及相位；簡單幾何光線圖無法表達全部繞射行為。 相位量測可能有週期性歧義；不同尺度的誤差估計能幫助區分大偏差與精細對準。","explanationEn":"Coherent optical addition depends on phase; ray sketches cannot describe all diffraction effects. Phase measurements can have periodic ambiguity; different error scales help distinguish large offsets from fine alignment."}},{"id":"c325-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-09"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"建立量測—修正回饋迴路","titleEn":"Build a measurement–correction loop","objective":"把誤差估計與機構調整分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate error estimation from actuator adjustment.","instruction":"畫影像、估計、命令與再量測四節點；加入一個假想偏差；以小幅修正示例檢查誤差是否下降。","instructionEn":"Draw image, estimate, command and remeasurement nodes; introduce an assumed bias; use a small correction example and inspect error reduction.","observation":"修正後必須再次觀察。","observationEn":"A correction needs remeasurement.","failure":"把估計值當絕對真值可能造成過度修正。","failureEn":"Treating estimates as truth can overcorrect.","check":"記錄每輪前後誤差與不確定度。","checkEn":"Record before/after error and uncertainty each cycle.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"閉迴路依賴可量測的誤差與適當增益，控制命令並不等於結果。","textEn":"Closed loops need observable errors and suitable gain; commands are not outcomes."},{"id":"c325-v7-10-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"高增益可能放大量測雜訊或引發振盪；控制效果須用收斂速度、殘差與穩定度共同比較。","textEn":"High gain can amplify noise or induce oscillation; compare convergence, residual error and stability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立量測—修正回饋迴路」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a measurement–correction loop’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["調整後重新量測才知道效果","發出命令即證明誤差歸零","增益越大一定越穩定"],"optionsEn":["Remeasure after adjustment to establish effect","Sending a command proves zero error","Higher gain always improves stability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"閉迴路依賴可量測的誤差與適當增益，控制命令並不等於結果。 高增益可能放大量測雜訊或引發振盪；控制效果須用收斂速度、殘差與穩定度共同比較。","explanationEn":"Closed loops need observable errors and suitable gain; commands are not outcomes. High gain can amplify noise or induce oscillation; compare convergence, residual error and stability together."}},{"id":"c325-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-10"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"檢查視場與儀器的一致性","titleEn":"Review field and instrument consistency","objective":"避免只在一個位置最佳化。","objectiveEn":"Avoid optimizing only one field point.","instruction":"在教學視場標中心及四角；記錄假想像質指標；比較單點最佳與多點折衷方案。","instructionEn":"Mark a center and four field corners; record hypothetical quality metrics; compare single-point optimization with a multi-point compromise.","observation":"中心像質好不等於全視場一致。","observationEn":"Good central quality does not establish field-wide consistency.","failure":"將一個儀器結果套到所有儀器不成立。","failureEn":"One instrument’s result cannot cover all instruments.","check":"報表包含視場位置及測試模式。","checkEn":"Include field position and test mode in the report.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"光學系統的像差可能隨視場變化，多儀器介面增加一致性要求。","textEn":"Aberrations may vary across a field; multiple instruments add consistency requirements."},{"id":"c325-v7-11-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"比較需固定波段、焦點條件與定義，否則指標不一定可比。","textEn":"Comparisons need fixed band, focus conditions and definitions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「檢查視場與儀器的一致性」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review field and instrument consistency’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["不同波段的任何指標可直接相加","應跨視場與模式保留量測條件","中心測一次即可代表全場"],"optionsEn":["Arbitrary metrics from different bands can be added","Preserve conditions across field points and modes","One center test represents the entire field"],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學系統的像差可能隨視場變化，多儀器介面增加一致性要求。 比較需固定波段、焦點條件與定義，否則指標不一定可比。","explanationEn":"Aberrations may vary across a field; multiple instruments add consistency requirements. Comparisons need fixed band, focus conditions and definitions."}},{"id":"c325-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-11"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"建立低溫光學誤差預算","titleEn":"Build a cold-optics error budget","objective":"區分製造、對準與環境變化。","objectiveEn":"Separate manufacture, alignment and environmental change.","instruction":"列出面形、定位與熱變形三種誤差；以相同波前單位表達；標示哪些可校正及哪些須重新驗證。","instructionEn":"List figure, alignment and thermal errors; express them in a common wavefront unit; identify correctable and re-verification items.","observation":"單一漂亮面形無法保證全系統像質。","observationEn":"An excellent surface alone cannot guarantee system image quality.","failure":"不同單位直接相加會產生假精準。","failureEn":"Adding incompatible units creates false precision.","check":"每項誤差都有來源、單位與條件。","checkEn":"Each error has origin, units and conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"誤差預算的合成方式依相關性而定，不是所有項目都可平方和開根號。","textEn":"Error-budget combination depends on correlation; root-sum-square is not universally valid."},{"id":"c325-v7-12-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"低溫材料行為與結構穩定度需要環境試驗支持。","textEn":"Cryogenic material behavior and structural stability need environmental-test support."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立低溫光學誤差預算」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a cold-optics error budget’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有誤差必然互不相關","室溫檢查可完全取代低溫驗證","先統一量的定義再合成"],"optionsEn":["All errors are automatically independent","Room-temperature inspection replaces cryogenic verification","Unify definitions before combining errors"],"answer":2,"explanation":"誤差預算的合成方式依相關性而定，不是所有項目都可平方和開根號。 低溫材料行為與結構穩定度需要環境試驗支持。","explanationEn":"Error-budget combination depends on correlation; root-sum-square is not universally valid. Cryogenic material behavior and structural stability need environmental-test support."}}]},{"id":"c325-stage03","order":3,"title":"遮陽、展開與穩定度","titleEn":"Shielding, deployment and stability","description":"把熱路徑與機構相依關係視為共同問題。","descriptionEn":"Treat thermal paths and mechanism dependencies together.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c325-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-12"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield"],"title":"繪製五層遮陽板的熱流","titleEn":"Draw heat flow through five shield layers","objective":"理解分層與間距的功能。","objectiveEn":"Understand layering and separation.","instruction":"畫五片不相碰的薄膜；標入射與向外散熱箭頭；比較層間保持分離與局部接觸的差異。","instructionEn":"Draw five separated membranes; mark incoming and outgoing radiation; compare separated layers with local contact.","observation":"薄膜分層不只是增加材料厚度。","observationEn":"Multiple membranes do more than increase material thickness.","failure":"把五層壓成一片會改變熱路徑。","failureEn":"Pressing layers together changes heat paths.","check":"說明層間間距為何影響隔熱。","checkEn":"Explain why layer separation matters thermally.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-13-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"多層設計利用輻射交換與幾何把熱導向太空，接觸則可能增加導熱。","textEn":"Multiple layers use radiative exchange and geometry to reject heat; contact may increase conduction."},{"id":"c325-v7-13-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"各層互相看見的面積與角度決定輻射交換比例；遮陽效果因此和形狀及相對位置相連。","textEn":"Relative visible areas and angles determine radiative exchange; shielding therefore depends on shape and placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「繪製五層遮陽板的熱流」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Draw heat flow through five shield layers’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["層間幾何是熱設計的一部分","五層只為了讓顏色漂亮","接觸與分離的熱效果完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Interlayer geometry is part of thermal design","Five layers are purely decorative","Contact and separation are thermally identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層設計利用輻射交換與幾何把熱導向太空，接觸則可能增加導熱。 各層互相看見的面積與角度決定輻射交換比例；遮陽效果因此和形狀及相對位置相連。","explanationEn":"Multiple layers use radiative exchange and geometry to reject heat; contact may increase conduction. Relative visible areas and angles determine radiative exchange; shielding therefore depends on shape and placement."}},{"id":"c325-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-13"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield"],"title":"分開反射率與放射率","titleEn":"Separate reflectance from emittance","objective":"避免用可見顏色推論全部熱性能。","objectiveEn":"Avoid inferring all thermal properties from visible color.","instruction":"畫太陽波段與紅外波段兩欄；分別註記吸收與放射；比較兩種假想塗層並列出需要測量的光譜資料。","instructionEn":"Draw solar and infrared columns; note absorption and emission separately; compare hypothetical coatings and list required spectral measurements.","observation":"不同波段的表面行為可能不同。","observationEn":"Surface behavior may differ by spectral band.","failure":"看起來亮就等於所有波段都低吸收不正確。","failureEn":"A shiny appearance does not prove low absorption in every band.","check":"評估表保留波長範圍與溫度條件。","checkEn":"Keep wavelength range and temperature conditions in the table.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-14-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"光譜選擇性使太陽吸收與熱放射不能只用肉眼顏色判定。","textEn":"Spectral selectivity prevents visual color from determining solar absorption and thermal emission."},{"id":"c325-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"熱平衡還受視角、面積與周遭輻射環境影響。","textEn":"Thermal balance also depends on view geometry, area and surrounding radiation."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分開反射率與放射率」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate reflectance from emittance’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只看可見光照片即可選航天塗層","需要光譜與環境條件","所有銀色物體熱性能相同"],"optionsEn":["A visible photograph is enough to select spacecraft coatings","Spectral and environmental conditions are needed","All silver-colored objects have identical thermal behavior"],"answer":1,"explanation":"光譜選擇性使太陽吸收與熱放射不能只用肉眼顏色判定。 熱平衡還受視角、面積與周遭輻射環境影響。","explanationEn":"Spectral selectivity prevents visual color from determining solar absorption and thermal emission. Thermal balance also depends on view geometry, area and surrounding radiation."}},{"id":"c325-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-14"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield"],"title":"審查薄膜張力與邊界條件","titleEn":"Review membrane tension and boundaries","objective":"把形狀維持與熱功能連起來。","objectiveEn":"Connect shape retention to thermal function.","instruction":"用紙面示意膜邊固定點；加入一個鬆弛區；比較局部皺摺如何改變間距與視角。","instructionEn":"Sketch membrane boundary attachments; add a slack region; compare how wrinkles change spacing and view geometry.","observation":"機械形狀改變也可能影響熱路徑。","observationEn":"Mechanical shape changes may alter thermal paths.","failure":"只確認固定點存在不足以證明整面形狀。","failureEn":"Attachment existence does not establish membrane shape.","check":"標出固定、可動與未知邊界。","checkEn":"Mark fixed, movable and unknown boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-15-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"薄膜主要透過面內張力維持形狀，其行為與抗彎板不同。","textEn":"Membranes retain shape mainly through in-plane tension and differ from bending plates."},{"id":"c325-v7-15-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"邊界固定方式改變張力分布；皺摺會同時改變局部應力和層間幾何，因此不能分開最佳化。","textEn":"Boundary restraints change tension distribution; wrinkles affect local stress and interlayer geometry and cannot be optimized independently."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「審查薄膜張力與邊界條件」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review membrane tension and boundaries’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["薄膜與厚鋼板的力學完全相同","增加張力永遠沒有副作用","應把形狀與熱效果一起審查"],"optionsEn":["Membranes behave exactly like thick steel plates","Increasing tension never has trade-offs","Review shape and thermal effects together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄膜主要透過面內張力維持形狀，其行為與抗彎板不同。 邊界固定方式改變張力分布；皺摺會同時改變局部應力和層間幾何，因此不能分開最佳化。","explanationEn":"Membranes retain shape mainly through in-plane tension and differ from bending plates. Boundary restraints change tension distribution; wrinkles affect local stress and interlayer geometry and cannot be optimized independently."}},{"id":"c325-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-15"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-launch"],"title":"建立展開完成的證據表","titleEn":"Build deployment-completion evidence","objective":"分辨發令、移動與鎖定。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish command, movement and latch.","instruction":"為假想鉸鏈定義三種狀態；列位置與狀態兩類證據；模擬命令已送但未確認到位的情況。","instructionEn":"Define three states for a hypothetical hinge; list position and state evidence; simulate a sent command without confirmed arrival.","observation":"命令成功送出不等於機構完成。","observationEn":"A sent command does not prove mechanism completion.","failure":"沒有獨立確認就前進可能掩蓋未決狀態。","failureEn":"Advancing without independent confirmation hides uncertainty.","check":"狀態表包含未知而非強迫二選一。","checkEn":"Include unknown states rather than forced binary choices.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-16-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"複雜機構的狀態估計依多個觀察來源，證據相依性需透明。","textEn":"Complex mechanism states use multiple observations whose dependencies must be explicit."},{"id":"c325-v7-16-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"互相獨立的觀察能降低共因誤判；若兩個指示都依同一感測器，數量增加並未增加獨立證據。","textEn":"Independent observations reduce common-cause misinterpretation; two indicators using one sensor do not provide independent evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立展開完成的證據表」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build deployment-completion evidence’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["未確認到位應保留未知狀態","命令送出就一定完成","未知必須直接改成正常"],"optionsEn":["Preserve an unknown state when arrival is unconfirmed","Sending a command guarantees completion","Unknown must be relabeled normal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"複雜機構的狀態估計依多個觀察來源，證據相依性需透明。 互相獨立的觀察能降低共因誤判；若兩個指示都依同一感測器，數量增加並未增加獨立證據。","explanationEn":"Complex mechanism states use multiple observations whose dependencies must be explicit. Independent observations reduce common-cause misinterpretation; two indicators using one sensor do not provide independent evidence."}},{"id":"c325-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-16"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"評估熱漂移對鏡面影響","titleEn":"Assess thermal drift effects on mirrors","objective":"連結緩慢熱變化與光學誤差。","objectiveEn":"Connect slow thermal changes to optical error.","instruction":"畫溫度與像質兩條假想時間序列；標示時間延遲；提出相關與因果需要的額外證據。","instructionEn":"Draw hypothetical temperature and image-quality timelines; mark delay; identify extra evidence needed to distinguish correlation from causation.","observation":"光學誤差不一定立即跟隨溫度改變。","observationEn":"Optical error may lag temperature changes.","failure":"看到兩條曲線同向就直接宣稱因果不充分。","failureEn":"Correlated curves alone do not establish causation.","check":"提出一個替代原因與一個驗證方法。","checkEn":"Offer an alternative cause and a verification method.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-17-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"結構熱膨脹與熱時間常數會影響定位穩定度。","textEn":"Structural expansion and thermal time constants affect alignment stability."},{"id":"c325-v7-17-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"追蹤資料需保留姿態、時間與配置，否則不同情境難以比較。","textEn":"Trending needs attitude, time and configuration to compare conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「評估熱漂移對鏡面影響」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Assess thermal drift effects on mirrors’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任一溫度變化都立即同幅改變焦點","應保留時間延遲及其他條件","相關係數等於因果證明"],"optionsEn":["Every temperature change causes an instant proportional focus change","Preserve delays and contextual conditions","Correlation proves causation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"結構熱膨脹與熱時間常數會影響定位穩定度。 追蹤資料需保留姿態、時間與配置，否則不同情境難以比較。","explanationEn":"Structural expansion and thermal time constants affect alignment stability. Trending needs attitude, time and configuration to compare conditions."}},{"id":"c325-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-17"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"分配姿態抖動與曝光誤差","titleEn":"Allocate jitter and exposure errors","objective":"理解動態穩定度如何影響影像。","objectiveEn":"Understand how dynamic stability affects images.","instruction":"畫固定星點與抖動軌跡；疊加短與長曝光；比較位移模糊及光子雜訊的權衡。","instructionEn":"Draw a stationary star and jitter path; overlay short and long exposures; compare motion blur and photon-noise trade-offs.","observation":"延長曝光可能增加訊號，也累積運動影響。","observationEn":"Longer exposure can add signal while integrating motion effects.","failure":"把曝光拉長視為萬用改善方法會失誤。","failureEn":"Longer exposure is not a universal remedy.","check":"把光學失焦與姿態模糊分成兩欄。","checkEn":"Separate optical defocus from pointing blur.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-18-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"影像品質是光學、取樣與時間穩定度共同結果。","textEn":"Image quality combines optics, sampling and temporal stability."},{"id":"c325-v7-18-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"曝光影像整合了一段時間內的位置分布；不同頻率的抖動可能在同一平均偏差下產生不同模糊。","textEn":"An exposure integrates a distribution of positions; different jitter frequencies can produce different blur despite equal mean error."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分配姿態抖動與曝光誤差」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Allocate jitter and exposure errors’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["曝光無限延長一定最佳","所有模糊都是鏡面形狀問題","曝光應與穩定度一起權衡"],"optionsEn":["Infinite exposure is always optimal","All blur comes from mirror figure","Trade exposure against stability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"影像品質是光學、取樣與時間穩定度共同結果。 曝光影像整合了一段時間內的位置分布；不同頻率的抖動可能在同一平均偏差下產生不同模糊。","explanationEn":"Image quality combines optics, sampling and temporal stability. An exposure integrates a distribution of positions; different jitter frequencies can produce different blur despite equal mean error."}}]},{"id":"c325-stage04","order":4,"title":"試驗、校準與科學資料","titleEn":"Testing, calibration and science data","description":"讓地面證據與在軌資料互相對照。","descriptionEn":"Relate ground evidence to on-orbit data.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"c325-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-18"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-shield","v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"設計地面驗證矩陣","titleEn":"Design a ground-verification matrix","objective":"把環境條件與驗證項目對應。","objectiveEn":"Map environmental conditions to verification items.","instruction":"列振動、真空、低溫三種條件；為每項寫一個可驗證主張；指出地面不能完全重現的情況。","instructionEn":"List vibration, vacuum and cryogenic conditions; assign a verifiable claim to each; identify conditions not fully reproduced on Earth.","observation":"多個試驗互補，沒有單一全能試驗。","observationEn":"Tests complement one another; none establishes everything.","failure":"室溫成功不能直接代表真空低溫成功。","failureEn":"Room-temperature success does not prove cryogenic-vacuum success.","check":"每項試驗有配置、環境與接受證據。","checkEn":"State configuration, environment and acceptance evidence for each test.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-19-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"環境試驗應與分析、檢驗及模型校準共同形成證據鏈。","textEn":"Environmental tests join analysis, inspection and model calibration in an evidence chain."},{"id":"c325-v7-19-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"地面重力與邊界條件會引入修正需求；模型誤差仍須列入。","textEn":"Ground gravity and boundaries require corrections; model error remains part of the assessment."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「設計地面驗證矩陣」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Design a ground-verification matrix’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["不同條件需不同驗證證據","漂亮展開動畫可取代真空試驗","一次試驗可覆蓋所有配置"],"optionsEn":["Different conditions need appropriate evidence","Deployment animation replaces vacuum tests","One test covers every configuration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"環境試驗應與分析、檢驗及模型校準共同形成證據鏈。 地面重力與邊界條件會引入修正需求；模型誤差仍須列入。","explanationEn":"Environmental tests join analysis, inspection and model calibration in an evidence chain. Ground gravity and boundaries require corrections; model error remains part of the assessment."}},{"id":"c325-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-19"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-wavefront"],"title":"比較縮尺測試與全尺寸系統","titleEn":"Compare scaled tests with full-scale systems","objective":"理解縮尺保留與改變的物理量。","objectiveEn":"Understand which quantities scaling preserves or changes.","instruction":"選光路、質量與熱時間三個量；列幾何縮小後的變化；標出能直接驗證的演算法問題與不能直接外推的環境問題。","instructionEn":"Choose optical path, mass and thermal time; list changes under geometric scaling; distinguish algorithm checks from non-transferable environmental behavior.","observation":"相似外觀不代表所有物理行為相似。","observationEn":"Similar appearance does not imply full physical similarity.","failure":"單憑縮尺比例推定全機熱穩定不成立。","failureEn":"Scale ratio alone cannot predict full-system thermal stability.","check":"提交一張可外推與不可直接外推表。","checkEn":"Submit a transferable/non-directly-transferable table.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-20-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"縮尺試驗可隔離演算法或介面問題；全尺寸載荷與材料效應仍需其他證據。","textEn":"Scaled tests isolate algorithms or interfaces; full-size loads and material effects need additional evidence."},{"id":"c325-v7-20-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"相似律取決於要驗證的主導物理；幾何縮尺可保留光路概念，卻不自動保留熱時間與重力變形。","textEn":"Similarity depends on the governing physics; geometric scaling can preserve optical concepts without preserving thermal time or gravitational deformation."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較縮尺測試與全尺寸系統」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare scaled tests with full-scale systems’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["外型相似即可免除全尺寸驗證","縮尺試驗需明確界定驗證範圍","縮小六倍就讓所有量都縮小六倍"],"optionsEn":["Similar shape removes full-scale verification needs","Define the scope of scaled validation","A sixfold scale change scales every quantity sixfold"],"answer":1,"explanation":"縮尺試驗可隔離演算法或介面問題；全尺寸載荷與材料效應仍需其他證據。 相似律取決於要驗證的主導物理；幾何縮尺可保留光路概念，卻不自動保留熱時間與重力變形。","explanationEn":"Scaled tests isolate algorithms or interfaces; full-size loads and material effects need additional evidence. Similarity depends on the governing physics; geometric scaling can preserve optical concepts without preserving thermal time or gravitational deformation."}},{"id":"c325-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-20"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments"],"title":"建立暗訊號與平場校準概念","titleEn":"Build dark and flat-field calibration concepts","objective":"把探測器差異與天體訊號分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate detector variation from astronomical signal.","instruction":"建立小型虛構像素矩陣；加入固定偏移與增益差；逐項校正並保留未處理影像作比較。","instructionEn":"Create a small synthetic pixel array; add offsets and gain differences; correct them separately and keep the original for comparison.","observation":"相同照明下像素響應可能不同。","observationEn":"Pixel responses may differ under equal illumination.","failure":"把所有背景都減成零可能抹掉訊號。","failureEn":"Forcing every background to zero can erase signal.","check":"清楚標示原始、校準與顯示轉換三層。","checkEn":"Label raw, calibrated and display-transformed layers.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-21-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"暗訊號與平場處理針對不同誤差來源，校準必須匹配狀態與波段。","textEn":"Dark and flat-field corrections address different errors and must match state and band."},{"id":"c325-v7-21-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"校準參數應保留取得條件與版本；保存原始影像讓日後能檢查校準改動是否引入新的結構。","textEn":"Keep calibration conditions and versions; retaining raw images allows checking whether calibration changes introduce new structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立暗訊號與平場校準概念」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build dark and flat-field calibration concepts’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任何漂亮圖片都已科學校準","可以刪掉原始數據只留成圖","校準與美化顯示應分開"],"optionsEn":["Every attractive image is scientifically calibrated","Discard raw data and keep only the final image","Separate calibration from display enhancement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"暗訊號與平場處理針對不同誤差來源，校準必須匹配狀態與波段。 校準參數應保留取得條件與版本；保存原始影像讓日後能檢查校準改動是否引入新的結構。","explanationEn":"Dark and flat-field corrections address different errors and must match state and band. Keep calibration conditions and versions; retaining raw images allows checking whether calibration changes introduce new structure."}},{"id":"c325-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-21"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-launch"],"title":"追蹤資料封包到科學產品","titleEn":"Trace packets to science products","objective":"讓每個處理結果都可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Make processing results traceable.","instruction":"建立假想資料編號；連結接收時間、校準版本與處理設定；修改一個設定並比較結果及歷程。","instructionEn":"Create hypothetical data IDs; link receipt time, calibration version and processing settings; change one setting and compare output and provenance.","observation":"結果變化可能來自處理版本而非天體。","observationEn":"Output changes may come from processing rather than the sky.","failure":"只保存最後圖片無法重現推論。","failureEn":"A final image alone cannot reproduce an inference.","check":"記錄輸入、版本、設定與輸出校驗碼。","checkEn":"Record inputs, versions, settings and output checksums.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-22-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"資料履歷讓科學與軟體變更可區分，並支持重新處理。","textEn":"Provenance separates scientific changes from software changes and supports reprocessing."},{"id":"c325-v7-22-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"保留處理歷程不會自動證明模型正確，仍需獨立校準驗證。","textEn":"Provenance does not itself prove model correctness; independent calibration checks remain necessary."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「追蹤資料封包到科學產品」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Trace packets to science products’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["版本與輸入應伴隨輸出保存","檔名相同代表內容不變","重新處理一定代表觀測錯誤"],"optionsEn":["Preserve versions and inputs with outputs","Matching filenames prove identical content","Reprocessing always means the observation was wrong"],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料履歷讓科學與軟體變更可區分，並支持重新處理。 保留處理歷程不會自動證明模型正確，仍需獨立校準驗證。","explanationEn":"Provenance separates scientific changes from software changes and supports reprocessing. Provenance does not itself prove model correctness; independent calibration checks remain necessary."}},{"id":"c325-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-22"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-instruments","v7-science-webb-first-images"],"title":"用誤差與反證閱讀科學影像","titleEn":"Read images with uncertainty and counterchecks","objective":"避免把處理痕跡當新天體。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mistaking processing artifacts for objects.","instruction":"在虛構影像加入一個異常像素；比較相鄰曝光；提出訊號、儀器與處理三種解釋並標證據不足處。","instructionEn":"Add one anomalous pixel to a synthetic image; compare adjacent exposures; propose sky, detector and processing explanations and mark evidence gaps.","observation":"異常特徵需要跨資料交叉檢查。","observationEn":"Anomalies need checks across data.","failure":"只選最漂亮的一張支持結論會偏誤。","failureEn":"Selecting only the most attractive image biases conclusions.","check":"至少列兩個競爭解釋及可區分的觀測。","checkEn":"List competing explanations and a discriminating observation.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-23-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"科學影像包含噪聲、偵測器效應與處理選擇，不能把每個像素當確定物理物件。","textEn":"Images include noise, detector effects and processing choices; not every pixel is a certain physical object."},{"id":"c325-v7-23-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"不確定性與重複觀察是推論的一部分，不是失敗的裝飾。","textEn":"Uncertainty and repeat observation are part of inference, not decorative caveats."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「用誤差與反證閱讀科學影像」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Read images with uncertainty and counterchecks’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["調色後變明顯就能證明真實","跨曝光與處理條件核對異常","單一亮點必然是新發現"],"optionsEn":["Greater visibility after recoloring proves reality","Check anomalies across exposures and processing conditions","One bright pixel guarantees a discovery"],"answer":1,"explanation":"科學影像包含噪聲、偵測器效應與處理選擇，不能把每個像素當確定物理物件。 不確定性與重複觀察是推論的一部分，不是失敗的裝飾。","explanationEn":"Images include noise, detector effects and processing choices; not every pixel is a certain physical object. Uncertainty and repeat observation are part of inference, not decorative caveats."}},{"id":"c325-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"prerequisiteIds":["c325-v7-23"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-webb-mirrors","v7-science-webb-instruments"],"title":"審查 Webb 與相關光學工程","titleEn":"Review Webb and related optical engineering","objective":"找出可遷移原理與不能照搬的条件。","objectiveEn":"Identify transferable principles and non-transferable conditions.","instruction":"比較 Webb、Landsat 與地面消色差鏡頭；列出共同的光學校準問題；再分開波段、環境與熱設計差異。","instructionEn":"Compare Webb, Landsat and an achromatic lens; list shared calibration problems; separate spectral, environmental and thermal differences.","observation":"都用光學不表示材料、鍍膜或校準完全相同。","observationEn":"Shared optics do not imply identical materials, coatings or calibration.","failure":"把太空紅外方法直接當地面鏡頭配方會誤用。","failureEn":"Applying space-infrared methods as terrestrial lens recipes misuses the comparison.","check":"總結必須含共同原理、差異與證據界限。","checkEn":"Include common principles, differences and evidence limits in the review.","knowledge":[{"id":"c325-v7-24-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"收光、像差、熱漂移與可追溯校準是跨工程的共通問題。","textEn":"Collection, aberration, thermal drift and traceable calibration recur across optical projects."},{"id":"c325-v7-24-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"Webb 採反射式分段主鏡；消色差折射鏡靠不同色散材料處理另一類問題。","textEn":"Webb uses a segmented reflecting primary; achromatic refractors use different dispersions to address a different problem."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「審查 Webb 與相關光學工程」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review Webb and related optical engineering’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有光學器件可用同一材料配方","反射鏡與折射鏡的色散機制相同","比較原理時也要標明環境差異"],"optionsEn":["Every optic uses the same material recipe","Mirrors and refractors have identical dispersion mechanisms","Mark environmental differences when comparing principles"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收光、像差、熱漂移與可追溯校準是跨工程的共通問題。 Webb 採反射式分段主鏡；消色差折射鏡靠不同色散材料處理另一類問題。","explanationEn":"Collection, aberration, thermal drift and traceable calibration recur across optical projects. Webb uses a segmented reflecting primary; achromatic refractors use different dispersions to address a different problem."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":7,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":600},{"id":"d036","title":"道格灘離岸風電場","titleEn":"Dogger Bank offshore wind farm","category":"energy","kind":"course","summary":"以二十四個工程任務串接場址、單樁、轉子、海纜、HVDC 與可維護性。","summaryEn":"Twenty-four tasks connect site conditions, monopiles, rotors, cables, HVDC and maintainability.","scope":"以 Dogger Bank 分期工程公開資料為案例，數值與載荷圖均是教學假設；不是打樁、起重、海事作業或高壓送電指令。歷史只引用已公布里程碑，不宣稱全風場現已完工。","scopeEn":"Uses public information about phased Dogger Bank construction; numerical examples and loads are teaching assumptions, not piling, lifting, marine-operation or high-voltage energization instructions. History states published milestones without claiming whole-farm completion.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-firstpower","v7-science-dogger-base","v7-science-wind-principles","v7-science-dogger-address"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"wind","labels":["風資源","風機與基礎","海纜與換流","陸上電網"],"labelsEn":["Wind resource","Turbine and foundation","Cable and conversion","Onshore grid"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d036-stage01","order":1,"title":"風況、場址與設計邊界","titleEn":"Wind, site and design boundaries","description":"將自然條件轉成可追溯的設計假設。","descriptionEn":"Translate natural conditions into traceable assumptions.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d036-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-wind-principles","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"讀取風速分布而非單一平均","titleEn":"Read wind distributions rather than one mean","objective":"了解平均風速不足以描述發電。","objectiveEn":"Understand why mean wind alone is insufficient.","instruction":"建立低、中、高三段假想風速頻率；比較平均值相同的兩組分布；寫下發電估算仍缺的資料。","instructionEn":"Build low, medium and high hypothetical wind bins; compare distributions with equal means; list missing generation-estimation data.","observation":"相同平均值可能對應不同能量機會。","observationEn":"Equal means can correspond to different energy opportunities.","failure":"用平均風速直接代入全年輸出會偏差。","failureEn":"Using mean speed directly for annual output can bias estimates.","check":"保留頻率、時間範圍與量測高度。","checkEn":"Preserve frequency, period and measurement height.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"風中可用功率理想上與風速立方相關，但真實風機有功率曲線與運作限制。","textEn":"Ideal available wind power scales with speed cubed, but real turbines have power curves and operating limits."},{"id":"d036-v7-01-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"風資源估計還需空氣密度、方向與長期代表性。","textEn":"Resource estimates also need air density, direction and long-term representativeness."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「讀取風速分布而非單一平均」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Read wind distributions rather than one mean’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應用風速分布與適用功率曲線","平均風速就是全年發電量","風越強就可無限制輸出"],"optionsEn":["Use wind distributions and an applicable power curve","Mean speed equals annual generation","Stronger wind allows unlimited output"],"answer":0,"explanation":"風中可用功率理想上與風速立方相關，但真實風機有功率曲線與運作限制。 風資源估計還需空氣密度、方向與長期代表性。","explanationEn":"Ideal available wind power scales with speed cubed, but real turbines have power curves and operating limits. Resource estimates also need air density, direction and long-term representativeness."}},{"id":"d036-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-01"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-firstpower","v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-foundation"],"title":"區分風場分期與發電里程碑","titleEn":"Distinguish phases from generation milestones","objective":"正確閱讀大型工程進度。","objectiveEn":"Read major-project progress correctly.","instruction":"畫 A、B、C 三區；為首次發電、單區完成與全部完成建立不同欄位；把有日期的官方公告對應到正確欄。","instructionEn":"Draw A, B and C; separate first power, phase completion and whole-project completion; assign dated official announcements to the correct fields.","observation":"一台發電不代表所有風機均已運轉。","observationEn":"One generating turbine does not establish fleet-wide operation.","failure":"把首電新聞標題改寫成全案完工不正確。","failureEn":"Rewriting first-power news as whole-project completion is wrong.","check":"每個進度主張都附區別與日期。","checkEn":"Attach scope and date to each progress claim.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"分期工程有不同土建、機電與併網進度，容量目標不等於已投運容量。","textEn":"Phases have different civil, mechanical and grid milestones; target capacity is not commissioned capacity."},{"id":"d036-v7-02-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"2023 年首電是歷史事實，本課未據此推定 2026 年全部完工。","textEn":"First power in 2023 is a historical event, not evidence here of complete delivery in 2026."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「區分風場分期與發電里程碑」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Distinguish phases from generation milestones’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["A 區海纜完工代表 C 區也完工","首次發電與全案完成應分開","總規劃容量就是目前輸出"],"optionsEn":["Phase A cables imply phase C completion","Separate first power from total completion","Planned capacity equals current output"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分期工程有不同土建、機電與併網進度，容量目標不等於已投運容量。 2023 年首電是歷史事實，本課未據此推定 2026 年全部完工。","explanationEn":"Phases have different civil, mechanical and grid milestones; target capacity is not commissioned capacity. First power in 2023 is a historical event, not evidence here of complete delivery in 2026."}},{"id":"d036-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-02"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation"],"title":"建立海床地形與地層剖面","titleEn":"Build bathymetry and soil profiles","objective":"分清水深與基礎承載條件。","objectiveEn":"Separate water depth from foundation conditions.","instruction":"畫三個假想測點的海床高程；另畫分層土壤；標出點間推估區域與需補勘的空白。","instructionEn":"Draw seabed elevations at three hypothetical points; add soil layers; mark interpolated areas and investigation gaps.","observation":"海床平坦不代表地層均勻。","observationEn":"A flat seabed does not imply uniform soil.","failure":"把一個鑽孔套用全風場會過度推論。","failureEn":"Applying one borehole to an entire farm overreaches.","check":"剖面明確區分已量測與推估。","checkEn":"Distinguish measured and inferred profile portions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"基礎反應涉及地層剛度、強度與循環行為，而不只是水深。","textEn":"Foundation response involves soil stiffness, strength and cyclic behavior, not depth alone."},{"id":"d036-v7-03-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"測點間的地層推估包含空間不確定度；差異較大的區域可能需要更多勘查以降低模型風險。","textEn":"Soil interpolation between points carries spatial uncertainty; highly variable areas may need more investigation to reduce model risk."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立海床地形與地層剖面」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build bathymetry and soil profiles’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["水深相同代表所有地層相同","一個測點足以代表所有樁位","地形與地質要分開檢查"],"optionsEn":["Equal depth proves identical soil","One point represents every pile location","Review bathymetry and geology separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"基礎反應涉及地層剛度、強度與循環行為，而不只是水深。 測點間的地層推估包含空間不確定度；差異較大的區域可能需要更多勘查以降低模型風險。","explanationEn":"Foundation response involves soil stiffness, strength and cyclic behavior, not depth alone. Soil interpolation between points carries spatial uncertainty; highly variable areas may need more investigation to reduce model risk."}},{"id":"d036-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-03"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-wind-principles","v7-science-dogger-cables"],"title":"比較風機間距與尾流","titleEn":"Compare spacing and wakes","objective":"了解上游風機改變下游條件。","objectiveEn":"Understand upstream effects on downstream turbines.","instruction":"畫兩列教學風機與主風向；標尾流陰影；轉換風向再比較受影響機位與海纜長度。","instructionEn":"Draw two teaching rows and prevailing wind; shade wakes; rotate the wind and compare affected positions and cable lengths.","observation":"發電、載荷與海纜成本可能互相牽動。","observationEn":"Energy, loads and cable cost may interact.","failure":"只追求最近距離可能增加尾流損失。","failureEn":"Minimizing spacing can increase wake losses.","check":"列出兩個布局方案及各自權衡。","checkEn":"List two layouts and their trade-offs.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"尾流包含速度虧損與湍流變化，並非固定不變的幾何陰影。","textEn":"Wakes involve velocity deficits and turbulence changes, not fixed geometric shadows."},{"id":"d036-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"真實布局需風況、環境、海床與電氣整合模型；簡圖僅供比較。","textEn":"Real layouts need wind, environment, seabed and electrical models; sketches support comparison only."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較風機間距與尾流」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare spacing and wakes’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["布局要同時比較風向與電氣距離","每台額定功率直接相加就是年發電","尾流永遠朝同一方向"],"optionsEn":["Compare wind direction and electrical distance","Summed ratings equal annual energy","Wakes always point in one direction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"尾流包含速度虧損與湍流變化，並非固定不變的幾何陰影。 真實布局需風況、環境、海床與電氣整合模型；簡圖僅供比較。","explanationEn":"Wakes involve velocity deficits and turbulence changes, not fixed geometric shadows. Real layouts need wind, environment, seabed and electrical models; sketches support comparison only."}},{"id":"d036-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-04"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-wind-principles"],"title":"畫出風浪流的共同載荷路徑","titleEn":"Trace combined wind, wave and current loads","objective":"把自然作用連到塔架與地基。","objectiveEn":"Connect natural actions to tower and soil.","instruction":"在風機剖面標風、浪與流；追蹤力矩至單樁；列出同向與不同向的假想組合。","instructionEn":"Mark wind, waves and current on a section; trace moments to the monopile; list hypothetical aligned and misaligned combinations.","observation":"最大單一載荷不必出现在同一時刻。","observationEn":"Individual load maxima need not occur simultaneously.","failure":"任意相加所有最大值可能失真。","failureEn":"Arbitrarily summing all maxima can misrepresent conditions.","check":"保留載荷方向、時序與組合假設。","checkEn":"Preserve direction, timing and combination assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"海上結構面對多源動態作用，組合需物理與機率背景。","textEn":"Offshore structures face multiple dynamic actions whose combinations need physical and probabilistic context."},{"id":"d036-v7-05-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"載荷的方向與相位影響合力矩，設計情境應區分極端事件與長期循環，因為兩者回答不同問題。","textEn":"Load direction and phase affect resultant moments; extreme-event and long-term cyclic scenarios address different questions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「畫出風浪流的共同載荷路徑」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Trace combined wind, wave and current loads’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["海流只影響發電不影響基礎","載荷組合需說明相依性","所有最大值必然同時發生"],"optionsEn":["Current affects generation but not foundations","State dependencies in load combinations","All maxima necessarily coincide"],"answer":1,"explanation":"海上結構面對多源動態作用，組合需物理與機率背景。 載荷的方向與相位影響合力矩，設計情境應區分極端事件與長期循環，因為兩者回答不同問題。","explanationEn":"Offshore structures face multiple dynamic actions whose combinations need physical and probabilistic context. Load direction and phase affect resultant moments; extreme-event and long-term cyclic scenarios address different questions."}},{"id":"d036-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-05"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-wind-principles","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"界定能源與可用率預算","titleEn":"Define energy and availability budgets","objective":"分清功率、電量與停機損失。","objectiveEn":"Separate power, energy and downtime losses.","instruction":"用假設額定功率乘時間建立上限；分列尾流、電損與停機；檢查各項是否重複扣除。","instructionEn":"Form an upper bound from assumed rating and time; separate wake, electrical and downtime losses; check for double counting.","observation":"MW 與 MWh 表達不同物理量。","observationEn":"MW and MWh represent different quantities.","failure":"把裝置容量當全年電量會單位錯誤。","failureEn":"Treating capacity as annual energy is a unit error.","check":"完成有單位與損失定義的預算。","checkEn":"Produce a budget with units and defined losses.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"容量因數與可用率不同；可用但無風的風機仍可能不發電。","textEn":"Capacity factor differs from availability; an available turbine may produce nothing in calm conditions."},{"id":"d036-v7-06-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"發電估計必須標期間與假設，不能當固定收益保證。","textEn":"Generation estimates need a period and assumptions and are not guaranteed returns."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「界定能源與可用率預算」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Define energy and availability budgets’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["可用率百分之百就一定滿發","MW 與 MWh 可互相替代","分開容量因數與設備可用率"],"optionsEn":["Full availability implies full-rated output","MW and MWh are interchangeable","Separate capacity factor from availability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"容量因數與可用率不同；可用但無風的風機仍可能不發電。 發電估計必須標期間與假設，不能當固定收益保證。","explanationEn":"Capacity factor differs from availability; an available turbine may produce nothing in calm conditions. Generation estimates need a period and assumptions and are not guaranteed returns."}}]},{"id":"d036-stage02","order":2,"title":"基礎、轉子與機械可靠度","titleEn":"Foundations, rotors and mechanical reliability","description":"追蹤受力、疲勞、腐蝕與維護介面。","descriptionEn":"Trace loading, fatigue, corrosion and maintenance interfaces.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d036-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-06"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation"],"title":"檢查單樁的結構與土壤介面","titleEn":"Review the monopile–soil interface","objective":"理解基礎固定並非理想剛接。","objectiveEn":"Understand that foundation restraint is not perfectly rigid.","instruction":"畫單樁與分布土反力；比較軟硬兩種假想地層；標塔頂位移與固有頻率可能改變的方向。","instructionEn":"Draw a monopile and distributed soil reactions; compare hypothetical soft and stiff soils; mark possible changes in tower-top motion and natural frequency.","observation":"土壤反應會影響整體動態。","observationEn":"Soil response affects whole-system dynamics.","failure":"把海床下端永遠視為完全固定會簡化過度。","failureEn":"Assuming a perfectly fixed buried end can oversimplify.","check":"列出模型邊界及敏感參數。","checkEn":"List model boundaries and sensitive parameters.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"樁土互制把基礎與上部結構耦合，循環載荷可能改變有效反應。","textEn":"Soil–pile interaction couples foundation and superstructure; cycles may alter effective response."},{"id":"d036-v7-07-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"海床附近的側向反力分布影響彎矩與轉角；土層厚度相同也不保證具有相同的等效剛度。","textEn":"Lateral reaction distribution near the seabed affects moment and rotation; equal layer thickness does not imply equal effective stiffness."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「檢查單樁的結構與土壤介面」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review the monopile–soil interface’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應檢查土壤假設對動態的影響","基礎永遠不動所以不需建模","只看樁重即可決定承載"],"optionsEn":["Examine soil assumptions in dynamic behavior","Foundations never move and need no model","Pile weight alone determines capacity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"樁土互制把基礎與上部結構耦合，循環載荷可能改變有效反應。 海床附近的側向反力分布影響彎矩與轉角；土層厚度相同也不保證具有相同的等效剛度。","explanationEn":"Soil–pile interaction couples foundation and superstructure; cycles may alter effective response. Lateral reaction distribution near the seabed affects moment and rotation; equal layer thickness does not imply equal effective stiffness."}},{"id":"d036-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-07"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation"],"title":"追蹤過渡段與塔架接合","titleEn":"Trace transition-piece and tower interfaces","objective":"辨識接頭、通行與設備介面。","objectiveEn":"Identify joint, access and equipment interfaces.","instruction":"在剖面中分出單樁、過渡段與塔架；標載荷傳遞；另用虛線標設備與人員通行路徑。","instructionEn":"Separate monopile, transition piece and tower in a section; mark load transfer; use dashed lines for equipment and access paths.","observation":"同一幾何介面同時服務結構與維護。","observationEn":"One geometric interface can serve structure and maintenance.","failure":"只畫載荷不留可檢查性會造成設計盲點。","failureEn":"Load-only drawings can overlook inspectability.","check":"至少指出一處需同時滿足承載與維護的區域。","checkEn":"Identify an area serving both load and maintenance needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"接合細節需管理接觸、預力與疲勞等問題，不能只靠外形吻合。","textEn":"Joint detail must address contact, preload and fatigue, not appearance alone."},{"id":"d036-v7-08-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"接頭的局部接觸狀態可能影響載荷分配；圖面審查需同時保留連接區與量測可達性的描述。","textEn":"Local joint contact can alter load sharing; reviews should preserve both connection details and measurement access."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「追蹤過渡段與塔架接合」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Trace transition-piece and tower interfaces’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["維護通道永遠與結構無關","結構與維護需求要共同審查","接頭看起來密合就代表全部合格"],"optionsEn":["Access never interacts with structure","Review structural and maintenance needs together","A close-looking fit proves full compliance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接合細節需管理接觸、預力與疲勞等問題，不能只靠外形吻合。 接頭的局部接觸狀態可能影響載荷分配；圖面審查需同時保留連接區與量測可達性的描述。","explanationEn":"Joint detail must address contact, preload and fatigue, not appearance alone. Local joint contact can alter load sharing; reviews should preserve both connection details and measurement access."}},{"id":"d036-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-08"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-wind-principles","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"分解葉片的升力與彎曲","titleEn":"Decompose blade lift and bending","objective":"把氣動力連到葉根載荷。","objectiveEn":"Connect aerodynamic forces to root loads.","instruction":"在示意葉片標三段分布力；畫合力與葉根力矩；改變外段力並比較對根部的影響。","instructionEn":"Mark loads on three blade spans; draw resultant and root moment; change an outer-span load and compare root effects.","observation":"遠端載荷因力臂而影響彎矩。","observationEn":"Outboard loads influence bending through leverage.","failure":"只比合力會忽略分布位置。","failureEn":"Comparing resultant force alone ignores distribution.","check":"能說明相同合力為何產生不同力矩。","checkEn":"Explain why equal forces can produce different moments.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"葉片需要在氣動效率、剛度、重量與疲勞間權衡。","textEn":"Blades trade aerodynamic efficiency, stiffness, mass and fatigue performance."},{"id":"d036-v7-09-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"葉片扭轉會改變局部迎角，再回饋到氣動力；只用剛性直梁模型會遺漏這類耦合。","textEn":"Blade twist changes local angle of attack and aerodynamic force; a rigid straight-beam model misses this coupling."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分解葉片的升力與彎曲」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Decompose blade lift and bending’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只有合力大小重要","葉片越重就永遠效率越好","分布位置影響根部彎矩"],"optionsEn":["Only total force matters","Heavier blades always improve efficiency","Load position affects root moment"],"answer":2,"explanation":"葉片需要在氣動效率、剛度、重量與疲勞間權衡。 葉片扭轉會改變局部迎角，再回饋到氣動力；只用剛性直梁模型會遺漏這類耦合。","explanationEn":"Blades trade aerodynamic efficiency, stiffness, mass and fatigue performance. Blade twist changes local angle of attack and aerodynamic force; a rigid straight-beam model misses this coupling."}},{"id":"d036-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-09"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-wind-principles"],"title":"比較模態與週期激振","titleEn":"Compare modes and periodic excitation","objective":"了解動態頻率避開的重要性。","objectiveEn":"Understand dynamic frequency separation.","instruction":"畫一條假想結構頻率與轉速區間；加入轉動及葉片通過頻率概念線；標出需詳細分析的接近區域。","instructionEn":"Draw an assumed structural frequency and speed range; add conceptual rotor and blade-passing frequency lines; flag close approaches for analysis.","observation":"頻率接近可能增加振動風險。","observationEn":"Nearby frequencies can increase vibration risk.","failure":"只驗證靜態承載不足以涵蓋共振問題。","failureEn":"Static load checks do not cover resonance.","check":"所有頻率均標單位與假設。","checkEn":"Label units and assumptions on every frequency.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"模態反映質量與剛度分布，基礎、塔架與轉子共同影響系統。","textEn":"Modes reflect mass and stiffness distribution across foundation, tower and rotor."},{"id":"d036-v7-10-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"頻率接近不等於必然失效，仍需阻尼、激振與響應評估。","textEn":"Frequency proximity does not guarantee failure; damping, excitation and response matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較模態與週期激振」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare modes and periodic excitation’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["需進一步檢查阻尼與激振","頻率接近就能直接宣判倒塌","靜態強度足夠就沒有動態問題"],"optionsEn":["Examine damping and excitation further","Frequency proximity alone proves collapse","Static strength eliminates dynamic concerns"],"answer":0,"explanation":"模態反映質量與剛度分布，基礎、塔架與轉子共同影響系統。 頻率接近不等於必然失效，仍需阻尼、激振與響應評估。","explanationEn":"Modes reflect mass and stiffness distribution across foundation, tower and rotor. Frequency proximity does not guarantee failure; damping, excitation and response matter."}},{"id":"d036-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-10"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-wind-principles"],"title":"建立疲勞事件與量測紀錄","titleEn":"Build fatigue-event and measurement records","objective":"將重複載荷轉為可追蹤問題。","objectiveEn":"Turn repeated loads into traceable questions.","instruction":"畫兩段不同幅度的虛構應變歷程；標記循環範例；列感測器漂移與資料缺漏對解釋的影響。","instructionEn":"Draw two synthetic strain histories with different amplitudes; mark example cycles; list effects of drift and missing data.","observation":"小載荷大量循環也可能影響壽命。","observationEn":"Many small cycles can affect lifetime.","failure":"只保存最大值會丟失循環歷史。","failureEn":"Saving only maxima loses cyclic history.","check":"保留時間序列、校準與工況標記。","checkEn":"Preserve time series, calibration and operating-state labels.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"疲勞評估需載荷譜與材料/接頭資料，不能僅靠一個峰值。","textEn":"Fatigue assessment needs load spectra and material/joint data, not one peak."},{"id":"d036-v7-11-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"循環計數必須連到應力估計與材料資料；感測位置不同，即使峰值相同也未必代表相同損傷。","textEn":"Cycle counts must link to stress estimates and material data; equal peaks at different sensor positions need not imply equal damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立疲勞事件與量測紀錄」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build fatigue-event and measurement records’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["感測器漂移與壽命估計無關","循環幅度與次數都要考慮","只要最大值未超限就不會疲勞"],"optionsEn":["Sensor drift never affects life estimates","Consider cycle magnitude and count","No overload means no fatigue"],"answer":1,"explanation":"疲勞評估需載荷譜與材料/接頭資料，不能僅靠一個峰值。 循環計數必須連到應力估計與材料資料；感測位置不同，即使峰值相同也未必代表相同損傷。","explanationEn":"Fatigue assessment needs load spectra and material/joint data, not one peak. Cycle counts must link to stress estimates and material data; equal peaks at different sensor positions need not imply equal damage."}},{"id":"d036-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-11"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation"],"title":"比較防蝕與可檢查性","titleEn":"Compare corrosion protection and inspectability","objective":"把海洋環境納入材料證據。","objectiveEn":"Include the marine environment in material evidence.","instruction":"在潮差、飛濺與浸水區分色；列各區觀察項目；比較完好與破損塗層的假想檢查紀錄。","instructionEn":"Color tidal, splash and submerged zones; list observations for each; compare hypothetical intact and damaged coating records.","observation":"不同環境區需要不同觀察重點。","observationEn":"Environmental zones need different inspection emphasis.","failure":"只看塔頂照片無法代表水下狀態。","failureEn":"A tower-top photo cannot establish underwater condition.","check":"指出不可直接觀察的部位及所需證據。","checkEn":"Identify inaccessible areas and required evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"腐蝕防護涉及材料、塗層、電化學保護與可維護性等系統因素。","textEn":"Corrosion protection combines material, coatings, electrochemical protection and maintainability."},{"id":"d036-v7-12-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"表面觀察不能單獨量化全部剩餘厚度或內部損傷。","textEn":"Surface observation alone cannot quantify all remaining thickness or internal damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較防蝕與可檢查性」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare corrosion protection and inspectability’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任何白色塗層都完全等效","沒有表面鏽斑就一定毫無損傷","不同海洋區域應分別記錄"],"optionsEn":["Every white coating is equivalent","No surface rust guarantees no damage","Record marine zones separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"腐蝕防護涉及材料、塗層、電化學保護與可維護性等系統因素。 表面觀察不能單獨量化全部剩餘厚度或內部損傷。","explanationEn":"Corrosion protection combines material, coatings, electrochemical protection and maintainability. Surface observation alone cannot quantify all remaining thickness or internal damage."}}]},{"id":"d036-stage03","order":3,"title":"集電、海纜與 HVDC","titleEn":"Collection, submarine cables and HVDC","description":"分清交流集電與直流輸電的不同功能。","descriptionEn":"Separate AC collection from DC export.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d036-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-12"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"畫出交流集電拓樸","titleEn":"Draw AC collection topology","objective":"理解多風機與海上站的連接。","objectiveEn":"Understand turbine-to-offshore-station connections.","instruction":"用五台假想風機畫兩種集電支路；標每段功率匯集；移除一段海纜並比較受影響機位。","instructionEn":"Draw two collection branches for five hypothetical turbines; mark accumulated power; remove one cable segment and compare affected turbines.","observation":"靠近匯集點的線段可能承擔更多輸送。","observationEn":"Segments near collection points may carry more power.","failure":"把每段電纜負載都當一台風機會低估。","failureEn":"Assuming one-turbine loading on every segment underestimates aggregation.","check":"每條支路具輸入、匯流與失效影響。","checkEn":"Show inputs, aggregation and failure impact on each branch.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-13-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"Dogger Bank A 公開資料區分陣列交流海纜與後續直流外送。","textEn":"Public Dogger Bank A material distinguishes AC array cables from subsequent DC export."},{"id":"d036-v7-13-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"不同集電拓樸改變單點故障的影響範圍與電纜長度；供電冗餘與維修成本需一起比較。","textEn":"Collection topology changes single-failure scope and cable length; redundancy and repair cost must be compared together."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「畫出交流集電拓樸」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Draw AC collection topology’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["線段負載需按上游匯流計算","每條海纜永遠只載一台容量","所有海纜都是同一種直流功能"],"optionsEn":["Account for aggregated upstream loading","Every cable always carries one turbine’s rating","All cables have the same DC function"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Dogger Bank A 公開資料區分陣列交流海纜與後續直流外送。 不同集電拓樸改變單點故障的影響範圍與電纜長度；供電冗餘與維修成本需一起比較。","explanationEn":"Public Dogger Bank A material distinguishes AC array cables from subsequent DC export. Collection topology changes single-failure scope and cable length; redundancy and repair cost must be compared together."}},{"id":"d036-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-13"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables"],"title":"分開電纜電流與熱限制","titleEn":"Separate cable current and thermal limits","objective":"把導體損失連到海床散熱。","objectiveEn":"Link conductor loss to seabed heat transfer.","instruction":"設兩個假想電流值；用 I²R 比較同阻抗損失；再改海床熱條件並列出載流量仍缺的資料。","instructionEn":"Choose two hypothetical currents; compare I²R losses at one resistance; change seabed thermal conditions and list missing ampacity inputs.","observation":"同一電纜在不同散熱條件下限制可能不同。","observationEn":"One cable can have different limits under different cooling conditions.","failure":"只憑導體截面判定所有場址載流量不夠。","failureEn":"Cross-section alone does not establish ampacity at every site.","check":"報表列電流、阻值、熱邊界與假設。","checkEn":"Report current, resistance, thermal boundary and assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-14-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"電阻損失隨電流平方增長，溫度又可能改變導體電阻。","textEn":"Resistive loss scales with current squared, and temperature can alter resistance."},{"id":"d036-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"海纜設計還需埋設、交越與材料資料；此處不提供實際額定值。","textEn":"Cable design needs burial, crossing and material data; no real ratings are supplied."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分開電纜電流與熱限制」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate cable current and thermal limits’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["電流加倍損失永遠只加倍","熱邊界與電流都會影響限制","截面相同就處處同額定值"],"optionsEn":["Doubling current only doubles loss","Thermal boundaries and current both affect limits","Equal sections have equal ratings everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電阻損失隨電流平方增長，溫度又可能改變導體電阻。 海纜設計還需埋設、交越與材料資料；此處不提供實際額定值。","explanationEn":"Resistive loss scales with current squared, and temperature can alter resistance. Cable design needs burial, crossing and material data; no real ratings are supplied."}},{"id":"d036-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-14"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables"],"title":"辨識海纜路由與機械保護","titleEn":"Identify cable routing and mechanical protection","objective":"了解路由是多因素約束。","objectiveEn":"Understand routing as a multi-constraint problem.","instruction":"在示意海圖標海床起伏與交越；畫兩條候選路由；比較長度、維修可達性及需要補查的環境資料。","instructionEn":"Mark relief and crossings on a schematic chart; draw candidate routes; compare length, repair access and missing environmental data.","observation":"最短路由未必是最低整體風險。","observationEn":"The shortest route may not minimize overall risk.","failure":"忽略交越或可維修性會失去關鍵約束。","failureEn":"Ignoring crossings or repair access loses key constraints.","check":"每條路由至少列三項權衡。","checkEn":"List at least three trade-offs per route.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-15-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"海纜同時承擔電氣、機械與環境要求；路由選擇不能只最佳化距離。","textEn":"Cables carry electrical, mechanical and environmental requirements; distance alone is insufficient."},{"id":"d036-v7-15-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"彎曲、局部支撐與交越可能改變機械負擔及散熱；地圖距離相同的路徑仍可能有不同工程難度。","textEn":"Bending, support and crossings affect mechanical loading and cooling; equal map distances can have different engineering difficulty."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「辨識海纜路由與機械保護」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Identify cable routing and mechanical protection’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["最短路線必然最佳","海床資訊只影響外觀","應同時比較交越與維修條件"],"optionsEn":["The shortest route is always best","Seabed data only affects appearance","Compare crossing and repair conditions together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"海纜同時承擔電氣、機械與環境要求；路由選擇不能只最佳化距離。 彎曲、局部支撐與交越可能改變機械負擔及散熱；地圖距離相同的路徑仍可能有不同工程難度。","explanationEn":"Cables carry electrical, mechanical and environmental requirements; distance alone is insufficient. Bending, support and crossings affect mechanical loading and cooling; equal map distances can have different engineering difficulty."}},{"id":"d036-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-15"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"說明 AC—DC—AC 能量鏈","titleEn":"Explain the AC–DC–AC energy chain","objective":"辨識換流器與變壓器的不同。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish converters from transformers.","instruction":"畫交流集電、海上換流、直流輸送與陸上換流；為各節點標電能形式；另畫變壓器並說明功能差異。","instructionEn":"Draw AC collection, offshore conversion, DC export and onshore conversion; label electrical form at each node; add a transformer and distinguish its role.","observation":"改變電壓與改變交流/直流形式不是同一件事。","observationEn":"Changing voltage and converting AC/DC are different functions.","failure":"只放變壓器就聲稱產生 HVDC 不成立。","failureEn":"A transformer alone does not create HVDC.","check":"完整鏈含轉換與輸送損失註記。","checkEn":"Annotate conversion and transmission losses along the chain.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-16-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"HVDC 在長距離海纜工程中可提供系統選擇，但換流站增加成本、控制與散熱要求。","textEn":"HVDC offers an option for long submarine links, with converter cost, control and cooling needs."},{"id":"d036-v7-16-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"換流站也有電能損失與散熱負載；完整效率預算應包含兩端站與外送線，不只算海纜。","textEn":"Converter stations add losses and cooling loads; the efficiency budget includes both terminals and the export link, not just cable."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「說明 AC—DC—AC 能量鏈」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Explain the AC–DC–AC energy chain’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["變壓器與換流器需分開表示","變壓器即可把所有 AC 變成 DC","直流輸送沒有任何損失"],"optionsEn":["Represent transformers and converters separately","A transformer alone converts AC to DC","DC transmission has no losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"HVDC 在長距離海纜工程中可提供系統選擇，但換流站增加成本、控制與散熱要求。 換流站也有電能損失與散熱負載；完整效率預算應包含兩端站與外送線，不只算海纜。","explanationEn":"HVDC offers an option for long submarine links, with converter cost, control and cooling needs. Converter stations add losses and cooling loads; the efficiency budget includes both terminals and the export link, not just cable."}},{"id":"d036-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-16"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"分析保護分區與失效隔離","titleEn":"Analyze protection zones and fault isolation","objective":"理解故障影響的邊界。","objectiveEn":"Understand fault-containment boundaries.","instruction":"在教學能量鏈畫三個分區；標故障觀察與隔離邊界；模擬一個區域不可用時哪些資料需再確認。","instructionEn":"Draw three zones on the teaching chain; mark observations and isolation boundaries; simulate one unavailable zone and list data to reconfirm.","observation":"隔離設備動作仍需狀態證據。","observationEn":"Isolation action still needs state evidence.","failure":"把畫面變灰當成真實斷電會混淆。","failureEn":"A gray display is not proof of de-energization.","check":"分開教學狀態、現場電氣狀態與未知。","checkEn":"Separate teaching state, physical state and unknown status.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-17-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"保護協調要讓選擇性、快速性與系統穩定互相配合。","textEn":"Protection coordination balances selectivity, speed and system stability."},{"id":"d036-v7-17-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"監控電源或通訊的共用故障可能同時影響多區觀察；分區圖應標示這些非主功率依賴。","textEn":"Shared monitoring-power or communication failures can affect several zones; diagrams should show these non-power dependencies."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分析保護分區與失效隔離」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Analyze protection zones and fault isolation’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有分區永遠可各自無依賴運作","隔離主張需要獨立狀態證據","畫面不亮就能判定無電"],"optionsEn":["All zones operate without dependencies","Isolation claims need independent state evidence","A dark display proves no voltage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護協調要讓選擇性、快速性與系統穩定互相配合。 監控電源或通訊的共用故障可能同時影響多區觀察；分區圖應標示這些非主功率依賴。","explanationEn":"Protection coordination balances selectivity, speed and system stability. Shared monitoring-power or communication failures can affect several zones; diagrams should show these non-power dependencies."}},{"id":"d036-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-17"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-firstpower"],"title":"建立併網與電能品質問題單","titleEn":"Build grid-interface and power-quality questions","objective":"把能送電與符合介面要求分開。","objectiveEn":"Separate power delivery from interface compliance.","instruction":"列頻率、電壓、功率與諧波四項；為每項選觀測方式；加入一個虛構擾動並記錄恢復行為。","instructionEn":"List frequency, voltage, power and harmonics; assign observations; introduce a fictional disturbance and record recovery behavior.","observation":"瞬間有功輸出不代表所有電網要求已滿足。","observationEn":"Instantaneous real-power output does not establish all grid requirements.","failure":"只看發電量而不看介面條件會漏驗。","failureEn":"Energy-only checks miss interface conditions.","check":"每項主張都有量測條件及未決事項。","checkEn":"Each claim has measurement conditions and open issues.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-18-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"電網介面涉及動態與波形品質，不只是平均功率。","textEn":"Grid interfaces involve dynamics and waveform quality, not average power alone."},{"id":"d036-v7-18-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"適用要求與測試須以具體電網規範為準，本課未代替併網審查。","textEn":"Applicable requirements depend on the specific grid code; this course does not replace interconnection review."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立併網與電能品質問題單」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build grid-interface and power-quality questions’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["發電量大即可忽略波形","任何電壓可直接接任何電網","併網需多項條件共同驗證"],"optionsEn":["High energy output makes waveform irrelevant","Any voltage can connect directly to any grid","Verify multiple grid-interface conditions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電網介面涉及動態與波形品質，不只是平均功率。 適用要求與測試須以具體電網規範為準，本課未代替併網審查。","explanationEn":"Grid interfaces involve dynamics and waveform quality, not average power alone. Applicable requirements depend on the specific grid code; this course does not replace interconnection review."}}]},{"id":"d036-stage04","order":4,"title":"安裝、運維與全生命週期","titleEn":"Installation, operations and lifecycle","description":"以資源、天候、量測與環境證據完成整合。","descriptionEn":"Integrate resources, weather, measurement and environmental evidence.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d036-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-18"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-dogger-base"],"title":"規劃港口與安裝資源相依","titleEn":"Plan port and installation dependencies","objective":"將大型零件物流與工序連結。","objectiveEn":"Connect large-component logistics to work dependencies.","instruction":"列葉片、塔段與機艙三類物流；畫港口暫存及船舶時程；加入一項延誤並重排依賴。","instructionEn":"List blade, tower and nacelle logistics; draw port storage and vessel schedules; insert a delay and revise dependencies.","observation":"進料節奏與海上資源需要同步。","observationEn":"Delivery rhythm must match offshore resources.","failure":"假設所有大型件可無限暫存會失真。","failureEn":"Assuming unlimited storage distorts the plan.","check":"排程標容量限制及關鍵等待點。","checkEn":"Mark capacity limits and critical waits.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-19-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"海上建造是物流、氣候與專用資源共同約束的系統。","textEn":"Offshore construction is constrained by logistics, weather and specialized resources."},{"id":"d036-v7-19-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"大型零件的存放方向、尺寸與交接順序會限制可用場地；物流資料需要和工序版本一致。","textEn":"Component orientation, size and handoff order constrain space; logistics information must match the work-sequence version."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規劃港口與安裝資源相依」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Plan port and installation dependencies’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應同時管理暫存與船期","零件到港即等於可立即安裝","專用船永遠不會成為瓶頸"],"optionsEn":["Manage storage and vessel timing together","Port arrival guarantees immediate installation","Specialized vessels never constrain progress"],"answer":0,"explanation":"海上建造是物流、氣候與專用資源共同約束的系統。 大型零件的存放方向、尺寸與交接順序會限制可用場地；物流資料需要和工序版本一致。","explanationEn":"Offshore construction is constrained by logistics, weather and specialized resources. Component orientation, size and handoff order constrain space; logistics information must match the work-sequence version."}},{"id":"d036-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-19"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-dogger-base"],"title":"比較天候窗口與延誤風險","titleEn":"Compare weather windows and delay risk","objective":"避免把平均天氣當連續可作業時段。","objectiveEn":"Avoid treating average weather as continuous availability.","instruction":"建一串可用與不可用的假想日曆；插入需連續數日的教學活動；比較相同可用天數但不同排列的日曆。","instructionEn":"Build hypothetical available/unavailable calendars; insert an activity needing consecutive days; compare equal availability with different ordering.","observation":"可用天數相同不保證可完成同一工序。","observationEn":"Equal available days may not complete the same task.","failure":"只用年度平均值安排連續活動會低估等待。","failureEn":"Annual averages can underestimate waiting for continuous tasks.","check":"指出至少一個連續窗口不足的情況。","checkEn":"Identify a case with insufficient continuous window.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-20-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"天候風險依活動持續時間與限制條件變化，不是單一百分比。","textEn":"Weather risk depends on activity duration and constraints, not one percentage."},{"id":"d036-v7-20-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"預報不確定度會隨時間與情境改變；排程宜保留備選序列，並區分平均延誤與尾端風險。","textEn":"Forecast uncertainty varies with horizon and conditions; schedules need alternatives and should distinguish mean delay from tail risk."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較天候窗口與延誤風險」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare weather windows and delay risk’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任何活動使用相同天候條件","應分析連續可用窗口","全年有一半好天就隨時可作業"],"optionsEn":["Every activity has identical weather limits","Analyze continuous usable windows","Half-year good weather permits work anytime"],"answer":1,"explanation":"天候風險依活動持續時間與限制條件變化，不是單一百分比。 預報不確定度會隨時間與情境改變；排程宜保留備選序列，並區分平均延誤與尾端風險。","explanationEn":"Weather risk depends on activity duration and constraints, not one percentage. Forecast uncertainty varies with horizon and conditions; schedules need alternatives and should distinguish mean delay from tail risk."}},{"id":"d036-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-20"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-base","v7-science-wind-principles"],"title":"解讀 SCADA 與狀態監測","titleEn":"Interpret SCADA and condition monitoring","objective":"把異常訊號連到工況與校準。","objectiveEn":"Relate anomalies to operating conditions and calibration.","instruction":"建立風速、功率與振動三條假想曲線；標停機與量測缺漏；提出感測器問題與設備問題兩種解釋。","instructionEn":"Create synthetic wind, power and vibration curves; mark stops and missing readings; propose sensor and equipment explanations.","observation":"資料异常不一定等於設備故障。","observationEn":"An anomalous reading is not necessarily a machine fault.","failure":"只依一點尖峰判定更換零件不可靠。","failureEn":"One spike cannot reliably justify component replacement.","check":"至少用兩個相互獨立線索支持判斷。","checkEn":"Support interpretation with two independent clues.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-21-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"狀態監測需要基準、趨勢與工況正規化，不能只靠顏色燈號。","textEn":"Monitoring needs baselines, trends and operating normalization, not just colored indicators."},{"id":"d036-v7-21-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"多個感測器若共享處理程式或電源，其錯誤可能相關；判讀需檢查證據的獨立程度。","textEn":"Sensors sharing processing or power may have correlated errors; interpretation needs to examine evidence independence."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「解讀 SCADA 與狀態監測」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Interpret SCADA and condition monitoring’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["紅色尖峰必然代表軸承損壞","缺資料應直接補成零發電","先排除資料與工況差異"],"optionsEn":["A red spike necessarily proves bearing damage","Missing readings should always become zero power","First review data quality and operating differences"],"answer":2,"explanation":"狀態監測需要基準、趨勢與工況正規化，不能只靠顏色燈號。 多個感測器若共享處理程式或電源，其錯誤可能相關；判讀需檢查證據的獨立程度。","explanationEn":"Monitoring needs baselines, trends and operating normalization, not just colored indicators. Sensors sharing processing or power may have correlated errors; interpretation needs to examine evidence independence."}},{"id":"d036-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-21"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-base"],"title":"估算可維護性與備件影響","titleEn":"Estimate maintainability and spare effects","objective":"分清故障率與修復等待。","objectiveEn":"Separate failures from restoration delay.","instruction":"假設同樣故障但不同備件等待時間；畫停機時間組成；比較基地、船期與替換件對可用率的影響。","instructionEn":"Assume equal faults with different spare delays; break downtime into components; compare base, vessel and replacement effects.","observation":"修復時間包含等待，不只是工具作業。","observationEn":"Restoration time includes waiting, not just hands-on repair.","failure":"只記實際維修工時會低估停機。","failureEn":"Hands-on hours alone underestimate downtime.","check":"表格含偵測、等待、移動、修復與確認。","checkEn":"Include detection, waiting, travel, repair and verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-22-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"可維護性是設計、接近性、資源與證據交接共同結果。","textEn":"Maintainability combines design, access, resources and evidence handoff."},{"id":"d036-v7-22-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"備件數量與成本的最適化依故障模型，不能由單次案例推廣全風場。","textEn":"Spare optimization depends on failure models; one case cannot represent the whole farm."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「估算可維護性與備件影響」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Estimate maintainability and spare effects’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["停機應包含物流與驗證時間","維修扳手使用時間就是全部停機","任何備件永遠越多越好"],"optionsEn":["Downtime includes logistics and verification","Tool time equals total downtime","More of every spare is always optimal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"可維護性是設計、接近性、資源與證據交接共同結果。 備件數量與成本的最適化依故障模型，不能由單次案例推廣全風場。","explanationEn":"Maintainability combines design, access, resources and evidence handoff. Spare optimization depends on failure models; one case cannot represent the whole farm."}},{"id":"d036-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-22"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-dogger-base"],"title":"把環境監測納入生命週期","titleEn":"Include environmental monitoring in lifecycle","objective":"區分施工影響、營運影響與監測證據。","objectiveEn":"Separate construction, operational impacts and evidence.","instruction":"列噪音、棲地與海床擾動三項問題；為各項分配前後期觀察；寫出自然變動可能造成的混淆。","instructionEn":"List noise, habitat and seabed-disturbance questions; assign before/after observations; identify confounding natural variation.","observation":"清潔能源目標不等於沒有局部影響。","observationEn":"Clean-energy aims do not imply zero local impact.","failure":"只觀察施工後而沒有基準會難以歸因。","failureEn":"Post-construction observation without a baseline weakens attribution.","check":"至少列一個基準、一個對照與一個限制。","checkEn":"Identify a baseline, comparison and limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-23-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"環境評估需要時空尺度與因果設計，單張照片不能代表生態狀態。","textEn":"Environmental assessment needs spatial/temporal scales and causal design; one photo cannot represent ecological state."},{"id":"d036-v7-23-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"季節變化可能同時影響處理區與對照區；保留跨時期與跨位置資料能協助分辨工程影響。","textEn":"Seasonal variation can affect both project and comparison areas; time and location coverage helps distinguish project effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「把環境監測納入生命週期」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Include environmental monitoring in lifecycle’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["一張照片足以代表整片海域","監測應保留施工前基準與限制","再生能源項目絕無環境影響"],"optionsEn":["One photograph represents an entire sea area","Preserve pre-construction baselines and limits","Renewable projects have no environmental impacts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"環境評估需要時空尺度與因果設計，單張照片不能代表生態狀態。 季節變化可能同時影響處理區與對照區；保留跨時期與跨位置資料能協助分辨工程影響。","explanationEn":"Environmental assessment needs spatial/temporal scales and causal design; one photo cannot represent ecological state. Seasonal variation can affect both project and comparison areas; time and location coverage helps distinguish project effects."}},{"id":"d036-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"prerequisiteIds":["d036-v7-23"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-dogger-foundation","v7-science-dogger-cables","v7-science-dogger-base"],"title":"完成風電—電網整合審查","titleEn":"Complete a wind–grid integration review","objective":"把機械、電氣與營運證據合在一起。","objectiveEn":"Combine mechanical, electrical and operational evidence.","instruction":"彙整載荷路徑、集電圖與停機預算；找出跨領域矛盾；比較變壓器與伊泰普課程的共同電網介面及不同能源輸入。","instructionEn":"Gather load paths, collection topology and downtime budgets; find cross-domain conflicts; compare transformer and Itaipu courses for shared grid interfaces and different inputs.","observation":"同為發電工程，資源與動態條件仍不同。","observationEn":"Generating projects still differ in resources and dynamics.","failure":"直接把水電調度概念套到風電會忽略可控制程度。","failureEn":"Transferring hydropower dispatch directly to wind ignores controllability differences.","check":"提交含相似處、差異、未決項與來源日期的審查。","checkEn":"Submit similarities, differences, open issues and source dates.","knowledge":[{"id":"d036-v7-24-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"大型能源工程共用功率平衡、設備可靠度與電網介面，但水、風與儲能的控制自由度不同。","textEn":"Energy projects share balance, reliability and grid interfaces, but water, wind and storage offer different control freedoms."},{"id":"d036-v7-24-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"能源輸入的可控制程度會影響調度與備援策略；比較不同電廠時要將儲能、資源和電網條件分列。","textEn":"Input controllability affects dispatch and backup strategies; separate storage, resource and grid conditions when comparing plants."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「完成風電—電網整合審查」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Complete a wind–grid integration review’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有發電廠可用完全相同控制","設計容量越大就完全不需要電網審查","比較時保留不同能源的控制限制"],"optionsEn":["All plants use identical control","Larger capacity eliminates grid review","Preserve source-specific control limits when comparing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"大型能源工程共用功率平衡、設備可靠度與電網介面，但水、風與儲能的控制自由度不同。 能源輸入的可控制程度會影響調度與備援策略；比較不同電廠時要將儲能、資源和電網條件分列。","explanationEn":"Energy projects share balance, reliability and grid interfaces, but water, wind and storage offer different control freedoms. Input controllability affects dispatch and backup strategies; separate storage, resource and grid conditions when comparing plants."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":7,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":600},{"id":"d202","title":"EXPLORER 全身正子影像系統","titleEn":"EXPLORER total-body PET imaging system","category":"biomedical","kind":"course","summary":"以二十四步拆解光子偵測、符合事件、時間同步、校正、重建與研究品質證據。","summaryEn":"Twenty-four steps examine photon detection, coincidences, synchronization, correction, reconstruction and research-quality evidence.","scope":"僅以虛構事件表與非人體教學影像學習醫學影像工程，不提供病人診斷、放射性藥物製備、注射量、掃描處方或設備操作。實際醫療由合格專業人員執行。","scopeEn":"Learn imaging engineering with synthetic event tables and non-patient teaching images only. No diagnosis, radiopharmaceutical preparation, administered activity, scan prescription or equipment operation is provided; real care requires qualified professionals.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-about","v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic","v7-science-pet-completed","v7-science-pet-address","v7-science-pet-publications","v10-other-vendor-d202"],"depth":4,"diagram":{"type":"medical","labels":["光子事件","偵測與計時","校正重建","研究證據"],"labelsEn":["Photon events","Detection and timing","Correction and reconstruction","Research evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"d202-stage01","order":1,"title":"成像物理與系統分界","titleEn":"Imaging physics and system boundaries","description":"從觀測量區分 PET、CT 與全身視野。","descriptionEn":"Distinguish PET, CT and total-body coverage by observables.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d202-v7-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-about","v7-science-pet-completed"],"title":"界定 PET 與 CT 的不同觀測","titleEn":"Define different PET and CT observables","objective":"避免把功能影像與結構影像混為一談。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating functional and structural imaging.","instruction":"畫 PET 訊號來源與 CT 外部照射兩條概念鏈；列出各自量測量；標出影像融合仍需的座標資訊。","instructionEn":"Draw conceptual PET-emission and external CT-illumination chains; list their measurements; identify coordinate data needed for fusion.","observation":"相同外形的設備可能包含不同成像原理。","observationEn":"One enclosure may contain different imaging principles.","failure":"把 PET 視為另一台普通照相機會誤解。","failureEn":"Treating PET as an ordinary camera misleads.","check":"表格分列訊號來源、量測與輸出用途。","checkEn":"Separate source, measurement and output role.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-01-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"PET 偵測體內放射性示蹤訊號的分布；CT 量測 X 光穿透相關資訊，原理不同。","textEn":"PET detects distributions of radiotracer emissions; CT measures X-ray transmission-related information."},{"id":"d202-v7-01-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"融合影像須保留各模態的單位與物理意義；幾何重疊不會把發射與穿透測量變成同一種量。","textEn":"Fused images must retain modality-specific units and meaning; spatial overlap does not make emission and transmission identical measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「界定 PET 與 CT 的不同觀測」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Define different PET and CT observables’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["兩種影像需依各自物理量解釋","PET 與 CT 完全同一物理量","顏色亮就能直接判定疾病"],"optionsEn":["Interpret each modality through its own measured quantity","PET and CT measure an identical quantity","Bright colors directly diagnose disease"],"answer":0,"explanation":"PET 偵測體內放射性示蹤訊號的分布；CT 量測 X 光穿透相關資訊，原理不同。 融合影像須保留各模態的單位與物理意義；幾何重疊不會把發射與穿透測量變成同一種量。","explanationEn":"PET detects distributions of radiotracer emissions; CT measures X-ray transmission-related information. Fused images must retain modality-specific units and meaning; spatial overlap does not make emission and transmission identical measurements."}},{"id":"d202-v7-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-01"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-about","v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"建立正子湮滅的簡化幾何","titleEn":"Build simplified annihilation geometry","objective":"理解光子對與量測事件的關係。","objectiveEn":"Understand photon pairs and measured events.","instruction":"在虛構圓環中央放一個事件點；畫兩個近反向光子；標示源位置、湮滅點與偵測點並說明簡化。","instructionEn":"Place a synthetic event inside a ring; draw near-opposite photons; label origin, annihilation and detections and explain the simplification.","observation":"偵測點不是放射源本身的位置。","observationEn":"Detection points are not source positions.","failure":"把每次事件看成精準無誤差直線會過度理想化。","failureEn":"Treating every event as an exact line overidealizes.","check":"區分示蹤源、湮滅事件與探測器。","checkEn":"Distinguish tracer origin, annihilation and detector.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-02-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"正子行程與光子非完全共線性等物理因素會限制定位。","textEn":"Positron range and photon non-collinearity contribute localization limits."},{"id":"d202-v7-02-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"兩個光子都被偵測到才形成可用配對的候選事件；接受角度與材料效率會限制幾何理想值。","textEn":"Detecting both photons creates a candidate pair; acceptance angles and material efficiency limit ideal geometric performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立正子湮滅的簡化幾何」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build simplified annihilation geometry’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["幾何直線可消除所有物理不確定度","需分清事件發生處與被偵測處","兩個光子必然在探測器內才產生"],"optionsEn":["A geometric line removes all physical uncertainty","Separate event origin from detection","Both photons necessarily originate inside detectors"],"answer":1,"explanation":"正子行程與光子非完全共線性等物理因素會限制定位。 兩個光子都被偵測到才形成可用配對的候選事件；接受角度與材料效率會限制幾何理想值。","explanationEn":"Positron range and photon non-collinearity contribute localization limits. Detecting both photons creates a candidate pair; acceptance angles and material efficiency limit ideal geometric performance."}},{"id":"d202-v7-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-02"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"由符合對建立響應線","titleEn":"Build lines of response from coincidences","objective":"了解一筆事件不等於一個完整像素。","objectiveEn":"Understand that one event is not a complete image pixel.","instruction":"在八個虛構偵測位置中配對；連接符合對成直線；疊加多條線並標出資訊仍不足的地方。","instructionEn":"Pair eight hypothetical detector positions; join coincidences with lines; overlay many lines and mark remaining ambiguity.","observation":"多事件統計才支持空間分布估計。","observationEn":"Many events support distribution estimation.","failure":"把一條響應線的中點當必然源位置不正確。","failureEn":"A response-line midpoint is not necessarily the source location.","check":"能說明為何需更多方向與事件。","checkEn":"Explain the need for more directions and events.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-03-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"不使用時間資訊時，符合對主要約束一條響應線附近，而不是唯一位置。","textEn":"Without timing information, a coincidence constrains a region near a response line rather than one point."},{"id":"d202-v7-03-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"響應線受偵測器尺寸、散射與幾何模型影響。","textEn":"Detector size, scattering and geometry affect response lines."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「由符合對建立響應線」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build lines of response from coincidences’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["中點必定就是來源","單一事件就能生成完整全身影像","一對偵測主要提供線上位置約束"],"optionsEn":["The midpoint is always the origin","One event produces a complete total-body image","A pair mainly supplies a line-location constraint"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不使用時間資訊時，符合對主要約束一條響應線附近，而不是唯一位置。 響應線受偵測器尺寸、散射與幾何模型影響。","explanationEn":"Without timing information, a coincidence constrains a region near a response line rather than one point. Detector size, scattering and geometry affect response lines."}},{"id":"d202-v7-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-03"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-about"],"title":"比較短軸向與長軸向視野","titleEn":"Compare short and long axial coverage","objective":"理解幾何涵蓋與同時觀測。","objectiveEn":"Understand geometry coverage and simultaneous observation.","instruction":"畫短圓環與長圓筒偵測範圍；把三個教學物件放在不同軸向位置；比較分段觀測與同時觀測的時間差。","instructionEn":"Draw short-ring and long-cylinder coverage; place three teaching objects at different axial positions; compare sequential and simultaneous observations.","observation":"長視野可同時涵蓋更多位置。","observationEn":"A long field can observe more locations simultaneously.","failure":"增加長度不代表所有情況同倍率改善。","failureEn":"More length does not guarantee the same gain in every case.","check":"比較表分列幾何涵蓋、時間與偵測效率。","checkEn":"Separate coverage, timing and detection efficiency.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-04-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"uEXPLORER 原始研究描述約 194 cm 軸向視野；改善幅度仍依任務與測試條件而定。","textEn":"Original uEXPLORER research reports about 194 cm axial coverage; benefit depends on task and test conditions."},{"id":"d202-v7-04-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"全身同時觀測與多床位依序拼接具有不同時間資訊。","textEn":"Simultaneous total-body observation and sequential bed-position assembly contain different timing information."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較短軸向與長軸向視野」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare short and long axial coverage’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應比較空間與時間涵蓋","長一倍就必然所有性能都兩倍","全身影像一定全在同一時刻量到"],"optionsEn":["Compare spatial and temporal coverage","Doubling length doubles every performance metric","Any whole-body image was measured simultaneously"],"answer":0,"explanation":"uEXPLORER 原始研究描述約 194 cm 軸向視野；改善幅度仍依任務與測試條件而定。 全身同時觀測與多床位依序拼接具有不同時間資訊。","explanationEn":"Original uEXPLORER research reports about 194 cm axial coverage; benefit depends on task and test conditions. Simultaneous total-body observation and sequential bed-position assembly contain different timing information."}},{"id":"d202-v7-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-04"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-publications"],"title":"分開靈敏度、解析度與雜訊","titleEn":"Separate sensitivity, resolution and noise","objective":"建立多指標評估而非單一排名。","objectiveEn":"Evaluate multiple metrics rather than one ranking.","instruction":"列三個指標並各寫量測問題；在兩個虛構系統間比較；找出某一指標改善但另一指標不變的情況。","instructionEn":"List three metrics and their measurement questions; compare hypothetical systems; find a case where one improves while another does not.","observation":"偵測更多事件不必然讓點擴散更窄。","observationEn":"More detected events do not necessarily narrow spatial response.","failure":"把靈敏度倍數當成解析度倍數是錯誤。","failureEn":"Sensitivity gains are not resolution gains.","check":"每個指標附定義、條件與單位。","checkEn":"Attach definition, conditions and units to every metric.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-05-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"靈敏度描述偵測能力，解析度描述空間分辨，雜訊描述隨機變異。","textEn":"Sensitivity concerns detection, resolution spatial separation and noise random variability."},{"id":"d202-v7-05-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"不同研究若使用不同幾何或重建設定，數值不可不加說明地直接排名。","textEn":"Results with different geometry or reconstruction settings cannot be ranked without qualification."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分開靈敏度、解析度與雜訊」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate sensitivity, resolution and noise’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["無單位百分比可代表所有品質","應同時評估三個不同指標","最高靈敏度必定最高解析度"],"optionsEn":["One unitless percentage represents all quality","Assess the three distinct metrics together","Highest sensitivity guarantees highest resolution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"靈敏度描述偵測能力，解析度描述空間分辨，雜訊描述隨機變異。 不同研究若使用不同幾何或重建設定，數值不可不加說明地直接排名。","explanationEn":"Sensitivity concerns detection, resolution spatial separation and noise random variability. Results with different geometry or reconstruction settings cannot be ranked without qualification."}},{"id":"d202-v7-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-05"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"繪製成像系統介面","titleEn":"Draw the imaging-system interfaces","objective":"區分物理偵測、計算與研究輸出。","objectiveEn":"Separate detection, computation and research output.","instruction":"畫探測器、計時、事件表、重建四節點；標資料型態；替每條介面寫來源、版本與時間要求。","instructionEn":"Draw detector, timing, event-table and reconstruction nodes; label data types; state origin, version and time requirements for each interface.","observation":"影像品質依整條資料鏈而定。","observationEn":"Image quality depends on the full data chain.","failure":"只檢查最終影像外觀會漏掉資料遺失。","failureEn":"Final-image appearance may hide data loss.","check":"所有箭頭都寫清輸入、輸出及責任。","checkEn":"Label input, output and responsibility on every arrow.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-06-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"大量探測事件需一致的幾何、時基與校準，才能整合為可解釋資料。","textEn":"Many detector events need consistent geometry, timing and calibration to become interpretable data."},{"id":"d202-v7-06-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"幾何表和校準表是事件解讀的一部分；只保存數字而不保存通道定義，日後可能無法正確重建。","textEn":"Geometry and calibration tables are part of event interpretation; numbers without channel definitions may become unreconstructable."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「繪製成像系統介面」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Draw the imaging-system interfaces’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["只要終圖好看資料必定完整","廠商名稱相同即代表所有版本等效","整條鏈都需可追溯的介面資料"],"optionsEn":["An attractive final image proves complete data","A shared vendor name proves all versions equivalent","Make interfaces traceable throughout the chain"],"answer":2,"explanation":"大量探測事件需一致的幾何、時基與校準，才能整合為可解釋資料。 幾何表和校準表是事件解讀的一部分；只保存數字而不保存通道定義，日後可能無法正確重建。","explanationEn":"Many detector events need consistent geometry, timing and calibration to become interpretable data. Geometry and calibration tables are part of event interpretation; numbers without channel definitions may become unreconstructable."}}]},{"id":"d202-stage02","order":2,"title":"偵測器與資料擷取","titleEn":"Detectors and acquisition","description":"把閃爍訊號轉成可追蹤的數位事件。","descriptionEn":"Turn scintillation signals into traceable digital events.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d202-v7-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-06"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"拆解閃爍體到光電訊號","titleEn":"Decompose scintillation-to-electrical conversion","objective":"理解能量轉換與波形觀測。","objectiveEn":"Understand energy conversion and waveform observation.","instruction":"畫光子、閃爍光與光感測器三級；配一條虛構脈衝；標幅度、到達時間與雜訊基線。","instructionEn":"Draw photon, scintillation light and photosensor stages; add a synthetic pulse; label amplitude, arrival and noise baseline.","observation":"同一脈衝包含多種估計資訊。","observationEn":"One pulse supports several estimates.","failure":"把脈衝高度直接當來源位置不成立。","failureEn":"Pulse height does not directly locate the source.","check":"在波形上分開時間與能量代理量。","checkEn":"Separate timing and energy proxies on the waveform.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-07-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"閃爍晶體與感測器將能量沉積轉為電訊號，轉換本身有統計變異。","textEn":"Scintillator and sensor convert energy deposition to electrical signals with statistical variation."},{"id":"d202-v7-07-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"光的收集效率與感測器增益都影響脈衝統計，能量解析與時間解析因此需要分別量測。","textEn":"Light-collection efficiency and sensor gain affect pulse statistics, so energy and timing resolution need separate measurement."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「拆解閃爍體到光電訊號」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Decompose scintillation-to-electrical conversion’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["幅度與時間需分開估計","波形高度就是空間座標","能量轉換完全沒有雜訊"],"optionsEn":["Estimate amplitude and time separately","Waveform height is a spatial coordinate","Energy conversion has no noise"],"answer":0,"explanation":"閃爍晶體與感測器將能量沉積轉為電訊號，轉換本身有統計變異。 光的收集效率與感測器增益都影響脈衝統計，能量解析與時間解析因此需要分別量測。","explanationEn":"Scintillator and sensor convert energy deposition to electrical signals with statistical variation. Light-collection efficiency and sensor gain affect pulse statistics, so energy and timing resolution need separate measurement."}},{"id":"d202-v7-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-07"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"檢查通道增益與能量標定","titleEn":"Check channel gain and energy calibration","objective":"避免把通道差異當物理差異。","objectiveEn":"Avoid mistaking channel variation for physics.","instruction":"給三個虛構通道相同輸入；記錄不同輸出幅度；建立相對校準並保留校準前後圖。","instructionEn":"Give three synthetic channels the same input; record differing amplitudes; form a relative calibration and keep before/after plots.","observation":"等能量事件可能產生不同數位幅度。","observationEn":"Equal-energy events may yield different digital amplitudes.","failure":"直接比較未校準通道會形成系統偏差。","failureEn":"Comparing uncalibrated channels creates systematic bias.","check":"每個校準係數附通道與版本。","checkEn":"Attach channel identity and version to coefficients.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-08-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"增益校準建立可比性；校準仍有漂移與不確定度。","textEn":"Gain calibration establishes comparability but still has drift and uncertainty."},{"id":"d202-v7-08-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"溫度或電子學狀態改變可能讓通道增益漂移；校準的有效期間需以穩定性資料支持。","textEn":"Temperature or electronics changes can shift gain; calibration validity periods need stability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「檢查通道增益與能量標定」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Check channel gain and energy calibration’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["校準一次即可永遠不變","相同輸入應以校準後量比較","通道原始數字必然可直接比較"],"optionsEn":["One calibration lasts unchanged forever","Compare calibrated values for equal inputs","Raw channel numbers are always directly comparable"],"answer":1,"explanation":"增益校準建立可比性；校準仍有漂移與不確定度。 溫度或電子學狀態改變可能讓通道增益漂移；校準的有效期間需以穩定性資料支持。","explanationEn":"Gain calibration establishes comparability but still has drift and uncertainty. Temperature or electronics changes can shift gain; calibration validity periods need stability evidence."}},{"id":"d202-v7-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-08"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"辨識時間偏移與時鐘漂移","titleEn":"Identify timing offsets and clock drift","objective":"區分固定差值與逐漸變化。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish constant offsets from changing drift.","instruction":"建立兩條虛構時間戳序列；先加入固定差值再加入斜率差；用圖分辨兩種誤差並提出校正證據。","instructionEn":"Create two synthetic timestamp streams; add an offset then a slope difference; distinguish them graphically and propose calibration evidence.","observation":"對齊一次不保證長時間同步。","observationEn":"One alignment does not ensure lasting synchronization.","failure":"把所有時間差都當固定偏移會留下殘差。","failureEn":"Treating all timing error as fixed offset leaves residuals.","check":"報告同時列偏移、漂移及觀測區間。","checkEn":"Report offset, drift and observation duration.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-09-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"時間同步影響符合配對與飛行時間定位，不只是檔案排序。","textEn":"Timing affects coincidence pairing and time-of-flight localization, not just sorting."},{"id":"d202-v7-09-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"時間戳的單位、解析度與共同時基必須一致；增加儲存位數不能修正不同時鐘的物理偏差。","textEn":"Timestamp units, resolution and timebase must agree; more stored digits do not correct physical clock differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「辨識時間偏移與時鐘漂移」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Identify timing offsets and clock drift’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["一次零點重設能永久消除漂移","時間戳與成像位置無關","需分別評估偏移與漂移"],"optionsEn":["One reset permanently removes drift","Timestamps cannot affect image localization","Assess offset and drift separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間同步影響符合配對與飛行時間定位，不只是檔案排序。 時間戳的單位、解析度與共同時基必須一致；增加儲存位數不能修正不同時鐘的物理偏差。","explanationEn":"Timing affects coincidence pairing and time-of-flight localization, not just sorting. Timestamp units, resolution and timebase must agree; more stored digits do not correct physical clock differences."}},{"id":"d202-v7-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-09"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"建立符合事件的判別表","titleEn":"Build a coincidence classification table","objective":"理解配對条件與誤配問題。","objectiveEn":"Understand pairing criteria and false pairings.","instruction":"產生帶通道與時間的虛構事件表；用任意教學窗口配對；比較窗口變寬後真配對與誤配對可能變化。","instructionEn":"Generate synthetic channel/time events; pair them using an arbitrary teaching window; compare possible true and false pairing changes when it widens.","observation":"接受更多事件也可能接受更多誤配。","observationEn":"Accepting more events may admit more false pairs.","failure":"窗口越大影像一定越好不成立。","failureEn":"A wider window does not guarantee better images.","check":"明確標出窗口只作教學且非設備設定。","checkEn":"Label the window as a teaching value, not an equipment setting.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-10-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"符合條件需要時間與幾何相容；偶然同時事件也可能被誤配。","textEn":"Coincidences need temporal and geometric compatibility; unrelated events can pair accidentally."},{"id":"d202-v7-10-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"最佳參數依系統與測試任務，本課不提供臨床取得條件。","textEn":"Appropriate parameters depend on system and task; no clinical acquisition conditions are supplied."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立符合事件的判別表」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a coincidence classification table’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應權衡保留事件與誤配","越寬窗口永遠越準","只要時間接近必然同一事件"],"optionsEn":["Balance retained events against false pairs","Wider windows are always more accurate","Nearby times guarantee one physical event"],"answer":0,"explanation":"符合條件需要時間與幾何相容；偶然同時事件也可能被誤配。 最佳參數依系統與測試任務，本課不提供臨床取得條件。","explanationEn":"Coincidences need temporal and geometric compatibility; unrelated events can pair accidentally. Appropriate parameters depend on system and task; no clinical acquisition conditions are supplied."}},{"id":"d202-v7-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-10"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"把時間差換成位置區間","titleEn":"Relate time difference to a position interval","objective":"理解 TOF 提供的是有限精度約束。","objectiveEn":"Understand TOF as a finite-precision constraint.","instruction":"畫一條響應線與兩端探測器；標時間差正負；以 Δx=cΔt/2 的理想式畫出含不確定度的位置區間。","instructionEn":"Draw a response line with two detectors; label time-difference sign; use ideal Δx=cΔt/2 to mark a location interval with uncertainty.","observation":"時間解析度有限，所以位置是區間而非無誤差點。","observationEn":"Finite timing resolution gives an interval, not an exact point.","failure":"把一個 TOF 事件當精準像素會過度解讀。","failureEn":"Treating one TOF event as an exact pixel overinterprets it.","check":"公式中的秒、米與二分之一都有說明。","checkEn":"Explain seconds, meters and the factor of two.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-11-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"兩光子的路徑差隨事件位置變化兩倍，因此理想位置差含二分之一。","textEn":"The difference of the two path lengths changes twice as fast as position, giving the factor one-half."},{"id":"d202-v7-11-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"真實 TOF 還有校準、探測器和統計效應，這不是診斷定位計算器。","textEn":"Real TOF includes calibration, detector and statistical effects; this is not a diagnostic locator."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「把時間差換成位置區間」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Relate time difference to a position interval’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["位置差必定等於 cΔt 而沒有除二","應報告位置區間與時間不確定度","飛行時間完全消除所有模糊"],"optionsEn":["Position difference is always cΔt without halving","Report a location interval and timing uncertainty","TOF eliminates all blur"],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩光子的路徑差隨事件位置變化兩倍，因此理想位置差含二分之一。 真實 TOF 還有校準、探測器和統計效應，這不是診斷定位計算器。","explanationEn":"The difference of the two path lengths changes twice as fast as position, giving the factor one-half. Real TOF includes calibration, detector and statistical effects; this is not a diagnostic locator."}},{"id":"d202-v7-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-11"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"評估事件吞吐與遺失","titleEn":"Assess event throughput and loss","objective":"把資料量與可追蹤完整性連結。","objectiveEn":"Connect data volume to traceable completeness.","instruction":"建立假想每秒事件量；乘上每筆資料大小估算流量；加入緩衝溢出事件並比較輸入與輸出計數。","instructionEn":"Set synthetic events per second; multiply by record size for data rate; add buffer overflow and compare input/output counts.","observation":"高靈敏度也增加資料處理需求。","observationEn":"High sensitivity also increases processing demand.","failure":"檔案可打開不代表事件完全保留。","failureEn":"A readable file does not prove complete events.","check":"保留丟棄計數、序號與時間區段。","checkEn":"Keep dropped counts, sequence numbers and time intervals.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-12-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"吞吐瓶頸可能位於電子學、網路或儲存；必須沿全鏈檢查。","textEn":"Bottlenecks can lie in electronics, networking or storage and need end-to-end checks."},{"id":"d202-v7-12-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"資料缺失若與事件率相關，可能引入非隨機偏差。","textEn":"Loss correlated with event rate can introduce nonrandom bias."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「評估事件吞吐與遺失」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Assess event throughput and loss’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["儲存空間夠大就不會掉事件","遺失事件永遠都是無害的隨機樣本","需核對輸入輸出與丟失紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Ample disk space guarantees no event loss","Lost events are always harmless random samples","Compare input, output and loss logs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"吞吐瓶頸可能位於電子學、網路或儲存；必須沿全鏈檢查。 資料缺失若與事件率相關，可能引入非隨機偏差。","explanationEn":"Bottlenecks can lie in electronics, networking or storage and need end-to-end checks. Loss correlated with event rate can introduce nonrandom bias."}}]},{"id":"d202-stage03","order":3,"title":"校正與影像重建","titleEn":"Corrections and reconstruction","description":"理解量測偏差、統計與重建模型。","descriptionEn":"Understand measurement bias, statistics and reconstruction models.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d202-v7-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-12"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-completed"],"title":"理解衰減與 CT 對位","titleEn":"Understand attenuation and CT registration","objective":"分開光子損失與位置對應。","objectiveEn":"Separate photon loss from spatial registration.","instruction":"畫均勻教學物件中的兩條不同長度路徑；標相對穿透差；把衰減圖平移一格，觀察校正套錯位置的問題。","instructionEn":"Draw two path lengths through a uniform teaching object; mark transmission differences; shift an attenuation map one cell and inspect misapplied correction.","observation":"同一發射強度可能因路徑而有不同偵測量。","observationEn":"Equal emission can yield different detections because of path length.","failure":"把衰減差異直接解讀為生理差異不合適。","failureEn":"Attenuation differences should not directly become physiological interpretations.","check":"分列衰減模型與影像對位兩種誤差。","checkEn":"Separate attenuation-model and registration errors.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-13-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"PET 校正需描述光子沿路徑的損失；CT 資訊的使用還需能量轉換與座標一致性。","textEn":"PET attenuation correction models path losses; using CT also needs energy conversion and coordinate consistency."},{"id":"d202-v7-13-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"衰減係數依光子能量與材料而變；影像座標一致仍不保證物理係數轉換正確，兩者需分別驗證。","textEn":"Attenuation depends on photon energy and material; aligned coordinates do not guarantee correct coefficient conversion, so both require verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「理解衰減與 CT 對位」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Understand attenuation and CT registration’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["對位錯誤可能污染校正結果","衰減圖放任何位置都相同","CT 亮度直接等於 PET 放射強度"],"optionsEn":["Misregistration can corrupt correction","Attenuation-map position never matters","CT brightness equals PET activity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"PET 校正需描述光子沿路徑的損失；CT 資訊的使用還需能量轉換與座標一致性。 衰減係數依光子能量與材料而變；影像座標一致仍不保證物理係數轉換正確，兩者需分別驗證。","explanationEn":"PET attenuation correction models path losses; using CT also needs energy conversion and coordinate consistency. Attenuation depends on photon energy and material; aligned coordinates do not guarantee correct coefficient conversion, so both require verification."}},{"id":"d202-v7-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-13"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"分開散射與隨機符合","titleEn":"Separate scatter from random coincidences","objective":"辨認不同污染來源需要不同模型。","objectiveEn":"Recognize different contamination mechanisms.","instruction":"畫一個轉向光子案例；另畫兩個無關事件的誤配；在事件表分別標真、散射、隨機三類教學標籤。","instructionEn":"Draw one deflected photon case and one pairing from unrelated events; label true, scattered and random cases in a teaching table.","observation":"錯誤配對與路徑改變不是同一機制。","observationEn":"False pairing and path deflection are different mechanisms.","failure":"把所有背景用同一常數扣除可能失真。","failureEn":"Subtracting one constant for all backgrounds can distort data.","check":"以圖解說明兩種污染的差別。","checkEn":"Explain both mechanisms with diagrams.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-14-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"散射改變光子能量和方向；隨機符合把無關光子當成一對。","textEn":"Scatter changes photon energy/direction; random coincidences pair unrelated photons."},{"id":"d202-v7-14-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"實際事件真值不可直接觀測，校正依統計模型與驗證。","textEn":"Real event truth is not directly observable; correction depends on statistical models and validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「分開散射與隨機符合」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Separate scatter from random coincidences’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["散射事件一定能憑照片肉眼辨認","不同機制需各自校正與驗證","所有背景都是同一種噪聲常數"],"optionsEn":["Scatter is always visually identifiable in a photograph","Different mechanisms need appropriate correction and validation","All background is one constant noise term"],"answer":1,"explanation":"散射改變光子能量和方向；隨機符合把無關光子當成一對。 實際事件真值不可直接觀測，校正依統計模型與驗證。","explanationEn":"Scatter changes photon energy/direction; random coincidences pair unrelated photons. Real event truth is not directly observable; correction depends on statistical models and validation."}},{"id":"d202-v7-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-14"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"校準幾何響應與通道效率","titleEn":"Normalize geometry and channel efficiency","objective":"避免把探測器差異當物件差異。","objectiveEn":"Avoid turning detector differences into object differences.","instruction":"給均勻教學物件設定相同發射；讓某通道效率降低；比較未校正與校正後分布並標出殘差。","instructionEn":"Set uniform synthetic emission; reduce one channel’s efficiency; compare corrected and uncorrected distributions and mark residuals.","observation":"假結構可能來自通道響應。","observationEn":"Apparent structure may come from channel response.","failure":"一次校準不涵蓋所有配置與時間。","failureEn":"One calibration does not cover every configuration or time.","check":"校準記錄含幾何版本、日期與測試條件。","checkEn":"Record geometry version, date and test conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-15-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"正規化補償系統響應差異，需要與實際偵測器配置一致。","textEn":"Normalization compensates response differences and must match detector configuration."},{"id":"d202-v7-15-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"壞通道、漂移與缺資料須顯式處理，不能任意補成理想數值。","textEn":"Bad channels, drift and missing data need explicit treatment, not invented ideal values."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「校準幾何響應與通道效率」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Normalize geometry and channel efficiency’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["均勻物件出現條紋一定是物件真實結構","更換通道後可無條件沿用校準","校準需對應幾何與通道狀態"],"optionsEn":["Stripes in a uniform object must be real structure","Calibration always remains valid after replacing a channel","Match calibration to geometry and channel state"],"answer":2,"explanation":"正規化補償系統響應差異，需要與實際偵測器配置一致。 壞通道、漂移與缺資料須顯式處理，不能任意補成理想數值。","explanationEn":"Normalization compensates response differences and must match detector configuration. Bad channels, drift and missing data need explicit treatment, not invented ideal values."}},{"id":"d202-v7-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-15"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"比較死時間與隨機雜訊","titleEn":"Compare dead time with random noise","objective":"理解高事件率的非線性。","objectiveEn":"Understand high-rate nonlinearity.","instruction":"畫理想輸入對輸出直線；加入假想飽和彎曲；比較兩段事件率下比例是否一致。","instructionEn":"Draw an ideal input/output line; add hypothetical saturation curvature; compare proportionality at two event rates.","observation":"輸入增加不保證輸出等比例增加。","observationEn":"More input need not produce proportional output.","failure":"把所有低計數都當低來源強度會誤判。","failureEn":"Low recorded counts need not mean low source strength.","check":"報告明確分開事件率損失與統計波動。","checkEn":"Separate rate losses from statistical fluctuation.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-16-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"死時間是系統處理後暫時不能記錄另一事件的效應，可造成率相依損失。","textEn":"Dead time describes temporary inability to record another event, producing rate-dependent loss."},{"id":"d202-v7-16-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"率校正模型也帶入不確定度；接近飽和時，反推失去的事件資訊可能變得不穩定。","textEn":"Rate-correction models add uncertainty; near saturation, inferring lost events can become unstable."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較死時間與隨機雜訊」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare dead time with random noise’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["應檢查計數響應是否仍近似線性","輸入加倍輸出必定加倍","可用任意更大輸入克服所有雜訊"],"optionsEn":["Check whether count response remains approximately linear","Twice the input always means twice the output","Arbitrarily increasing input overcomes all noise"],"answer":0,"explanation":"死時間是系統處理後暫時不能記錄另一事件的效應，可造成率相依損失。 率校正模型也帶入不確定度；接近飽和時，反推失去的事件資訊可能變得不穩定。","explanationEn":"Dead time describes temporary inability to record another event, producing rate-dependent loss. Rate-correction models add uncertainty; near saturation, inferring lost events can become unstable."}},{"id":"d202-v7-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-16"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-dynamic","v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"建立前向模型與迭代重建","titleEn":"Build a forward model and iterative reconstruction","objective":"理解影像是由量測估計而來。","objectiveEn":"Understand images as estimates from measurements.","instruction":"畫四格教學影像與幾條投影；由影像預測事件量；比較預測與虛構量測，再做一次非負更新並保存殘差。","instructionEn":"Draw a four-cell image and projections; predict event counts; compare with synthetic measurements, make one nonnegative update and keep residuals.","observation":"可見影像取決於模型與量測共同作用。","observationEn":"The visible image depends on model and data together.","failure":"迭代次數越多必然越真實不成立。","failureEn":"More iterations do not guarantee greater truth.","check":"提交初值、預測、殘差及更新後結果。","checkEn":"Submit initialization, prediction, residual and updated result.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-17-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"前向模型把候選分布映到觀測，重建則用差異修正估計。","textEn":"A forward model maps candidate distributions to observations; reconstruction updates estimates using disagreement."},{"id":"d202-v7-17-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"正則化與停止條件改變偏差—雜訊權衡；四格例子非臨床演算法。","textEn":"Regularization and stopping affect bias–noise trade-offs; the four-cell example is not a clinical algorithm."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立前向模型與迭代重建」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build a forward model and iterative reconstruction’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["影像每一格都是直接拍到的真值","重建需同時檢查模型與殘差","更多迭代永遠等於更正確"],"optionsEn":["Every voxel is directly photographed truth","Examine the model and residuals during reconstruction","More iterations are always more correct"],"answer":1,"explanation":"前向模型把候選分布映到觀測，重建則用差異修正估計。 正則化與停止條件改變偏差—雜訊權衡；四格例子非臨床演算法。","explanationEn":"A forward model maps candidate distributions to observations; reconstruction updates estimates using disagreement. Regularization and stopping affect bias–noise trade-offs; the four-cell example is not a clinical algorithm."}},{"id":"d202-v7-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-17"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-dynamic","v7-science-pet-about"],"title":"設計動態影像的時間分箱","titleEn":"Design time framing for dynamic images","objective":"比較時間解析與統計精度。","objectiveEn":"Compare temporal resolution with statistical precision.","instruction":"把同一虛構事件流切為短框與長框；繪出兩種時間曲線；比較短框波動與長框平滑的代價。","instructionEn":"Split one synthetic stream into short and long frames; plot both curves; compare short-frame variation and long-frame smoothing costs.","observation":"較短時間框可看快速變化但事件較少。","observationEn":"Shorter frames resolve change but contain fewer events.","failure":"曲線越平滑就必然越真實不正確。","failureEn":"Smoother curves are not necessarily truer.","check":"說明選框長度與研究問題的關係。","checkEn":"Explain frame duration relative to the research question.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-18-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"動態 PET 的優勢包含同時觀察多位置的時間變化；時間分箱仍影響可辨識特徵。","textEn":"Dynamic PET can observe multiple locations over time; framing affects detectable features."},{"id":"d202-v7-18-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"不同時間框的計數可能受同一校準偏差影響；時間曲線比較需區分隨機波動與共享的系統誤差。","textEn":"Frames may share calibration bias; time-curve comparisons must separate random fluctuation from shared systematic error."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「設計動態影像的時間分箱」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Design time framing for dynamic images’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["框越短所有性能都越好","平滑即可證明模型正確","框長度需權衡時間與統計"],"optionsEn":["Shorter frames improve every metric","Smoothing proves model correctness","Frame duration trades timing against statistics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"動態 PET 的優勢包含同時觀察多位置的時間變化；時間分箱仍影響可辨識特徵。 不同時間框的計數可能受同一校準偏差影響；時間曲線比較需區分隨機波動與共享的系統誤差。","explanationEn":"Dynamic PET can observe multiple locations over time; framing affects detectable features. Frames may share calibration bias; time-curve comparisons must separate random fluctuation from shared systematic error."}}]},{"id":"d202-stage04","order":4,"title":"品質驗證與研究資料","titleEn":"Quality verification and research data","description":"用可重現的非臨床證據檢查成像系統。","descriptionEn":"Evaluate imaging systems using reproducible nonclinical evidence.","route":"先完成前置學習，再提交圖解、推理與檢核證據；每一步均為原創教育任務。","routeEn":"Complete the prerequisites, then submit diagrams, reasoning and review evidence; each step is an original educational exercise.","steps":[{"id":"d202-v7-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-18"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-publications"],"title":"建立非人體測試物的品質計畫","titleEn":"Plan quality checks using non-patient objects","objective":"讓性能主張對應可重現物件。","objectiveEn":"Link performance claims to reproducible objects.","instruction":"用數位幾何建立均勻、點狀及不同大小三種教學物件；各配一項品質問題；保存物件定義與評估腳本。","instructionEn":"Define uniform, point-like and varying-size digital objects; assign quality questions; preserve object definitions and evaluation scripts.","observation":"不同測試物揭露不同性能面向。","observationEn":"Different objects reveal different performance aspects.","failure":"用單一精美影像代表所有性能會不足。","failureEn":"One attractive image cannot establish all performance.","check":"每項結論連到測試物、條件及方法。","checkEn":"Link claims to object, conditions and method.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-19-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"模型測試可分開均勻性、空間響應與對比，但不能直接等同臨床效益。","textEn":"Phantom-like tests separate uniformity, spatial response and contrast but do not directly establish clinical benefit."},{"id":"d202-v7-19-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"數位物件有已知真值，適合檢查演算法；但無法單獨涵蓋硬體漂移與真實量測環境。","textEn":"Digital objects provide known truth for algorithm checks but cannot alone capture hardware drift and real measurement conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立非人體測試物的品質計畫」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Plan quality checks using non-patient objects’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["用合適物件評估不同主張","一張清楚圖就代表全部合格","數位測試直接等於臨床效果證明"],"optionsEn":["Use suitable objects for different claims","One clear image proves total conformity","Digital tests directly prove clinical benefit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"模型測試可分開均勻性、空間響應與對比，但不能直接等同臨床效益。 數位物件有已知真值，適合檢查演算法；但無法單獨涵蓋硬體漂移與真實量測環境。","explanationEn":"Phantom-like tests separate uniformity, spatial response and contrast but do not directly establish clinical benefit. Digital objects provide known truth for algorithm checks but cannot alone capture hardware drift and real measurement conditions."}},{"id":"d202-v7-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-19"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance"],"title":"比較對比恢復與背景變異","titleEn":"Compare contrast recovery and background variability","objective":"理解看得清與量得準未必相同。","objectiveEn":"Understand visibility and quantitative accuracy as different.","instruction":"在虛構影像設同濃度不同大小區塊；量中心平均與背景變動；比較平滑前後對小區塊的影響。","instructionEn":"Place equal-intensity regions of different sizes in a synthetic image; measure regional means and background variation; compare smoothing effects on small regions.","observation":"小物件可能因空間混合被低估。","observationEn":"Small objects can be underestimated through spatial mixing.","failure":"平滑降低噪聲也可能降低小物件對比。","failureEn":"Smoothing may reduce both noise and small-object contrast.","check":"結果同時保留對比與變異指標。","checkEn":"Preserve both contrast and variability metrics.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-20-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"部分容積效應使有限解析度混合鄰近訊號；視覺輪廓不等於真實邊界。","textEn":"Partial-volume effects mix neighboring signals; visual contours are not exact boundaries."},{"id":"d202-v7-20-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"背景變異的估計取決於區域大小與取樣數；比較對比時也要固定同一種背景定義。","textEn":"Background-variability estimates depend on region size and sample count; contrast comparisons need consistent background definitions."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較對比恢復與背景變異」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare contrast recovery and background variability’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["任何大小區塊都必須同樣恢復","應同時看對比與背景變異","平滑後沒噪點即量測完全準確"],"optionsEn":["Every region size has identical recovery","Assess contrast and background variability together","No visible noise means perfect quantitative accuracy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"部分容積效應使有限解析度混合鄰近訊號；視覺輪廓不等於真實邊界。 背景變異的估計取決於區域大小與取樣數；比較對比時也要固定同一種背景定義。","explanationEn":"Partial-volume effects mix neighboring signals; visual contours are not exact boundaries. Background-variability estimates depend on region size and sample count; contrast comparisons need consistent background definitions."}},{"id":"d202-v7-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-20"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"檢查運動與模態對位誤差","titleEn":"Review motion and multimodality misregistration","objective":"辨識時間與空間不一致的影響。","objectiveEn":"Recognize temporal and spatial inconsistency.","instruction":"將教學物件在兩時刻平移；疊加 PET 與衰減示意；比較未對位與對位後殘差並記錄插值。","instructionEn":"Translate a teaching object between two times; overlay PET and attenuation sketches; compare residuals before/after alignment and record interpolation.","observation":"對位改善外觀仍需檢查量化影響。","observationEn":"Better-looking registration still needs quantitative checks.","failure":"把所有邊界硬拉重合可能造成失真。","failureEn":"Forcing every boundary to match may distort data.","check":"報告原始、轉換與未解決區域。","checkEn":"Report original data, transformation and unresolved regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-21-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"不同模態可能在不同時間測得，運動會影響融合與校正。","textEn":"Modalities acquired at different times may mismatch through motion, affecting fusion and correction."},{"id":"d202-v7-21-k2","title":"驗證與界限","titleEn":"Verification and limits","text":"配準演算法不能自動保證生理對應正確，需相應驗證。","textEn":"Registration does not automatically establish correct physiological correspondence; validation is required."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「檢查運動與模態對位誤差」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Review motion and multimodality misregistration’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["圖像重疊即代表全部正確","可用任意變形消除任何差異","對位後仍要驗證量化影響"],"optionsEn":["Visual overlap proves all correctness","Any deformation may erase any discrepancy","Check quantitative effects after registration"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同模態可能在不同時間測得，運動會影響融合與校正。 配準演算法不能自動保證生理對應正確，需相應驗證。","explanationEn":"Modalities acquired at different times may mismatch through motion, affecting fusion and correction. Registration does not automatically establish correct physiological correspondence; validation is required."}},{"id":"d202-v7-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-21"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-dynamic","v7-science-pet-publications"],"title":"建立研究資料與版本履歷","titleEn":"Build research-data provenance","objective":"讓結果可以重現且不混入身分資料。","objectiveEn":"Make results reproducible without identity data.","instruction":"為合成事件檔建立隨機案例編號；記錄幾何、校準與軟體版本；匯出不含個人欄位的重現清單。","instructionEn":"Give a synthetic event file a random case ID; record geometry, calibration and software versions; export a reproducibility manifest without personal fields.","observation":"相同資料用不同校準可能產生不同結果。","observationEn":"Different calibrations can change results from the same data.","failure":"刪除姓名不一定足以去識別真實醫療資料。","failureEn":"Removing names alone may not de-identify real medical data.","check":"清單能重現合成結果，且沒有個人資訊。","checkEn":"The manifest reproduces synthetic results and contains no personal data.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-22-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"可重現性需要輸入、演算法、參數與校準的完整關係。","textEn":"Reproducibility needs relationships among input, algorithm, parameters and calibration."},{"id":"d202-v7-22-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"醫療資料的身分線索可能出現在標頭、影像文字與時間資訊；研究資料治理需處理整個資料結構。","textEn":"Identity clues can appear in headers, image text and timing; research-data governance must address the full data structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「建立研究資料與版本履歷」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Build research-data provenance’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["版本與校準應連結到每個結果","刪名字即可公開全部醫療檔案","程式相同就不用記校準"],"optionsEn":["Link versions and calibration to each result","Removing names makes all medical files public","Identical code removes the need to record calibration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"可重現性需要輸入、演算法、參數與校準的完整關係。 醫療資料的身分線索可能出現在標頭、影像文字與時間資訊；研究資料治理需處理整個資料結構。","explanationEn":"Reproducibility needs relationships among input, algorithm, parameters and calibration. Identity clues can appear in headers, image text and timing; research-data governance must address the full data structure."}},{"id":"d202-v7-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-22"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic","v7-science-pet-publications"],"title":"比較原始研究的測試條件","titleEn":"Compare conditions across original studies","objective":"避免拼湊出不存在的性能組合。","objectiveEn":"Avoid inventing a composite performance claim.","instruction":"從兩篇研究各摘記題名與測試範圍；分列幾何、重建與指標；標出不可直接比較的欄位並解釋原因。","instructionEn":"Record titles and scope from two original studies; separate geometry, reconstruction and metrics; flag incomparable fields and explain why.","observation":"不同論文的最佳數值未必可同時達到。","observationEn":"Best values from different papers may not be simultaneously attainable.","failure":"把各研究最佳值拼成一台新系統會誤導。","failureEn":"Combining best values into an imaginary system misleads.","check":"所有比較都附來源及原始條件。","checkEn":"Attach sources and original conditions to comparisons.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-23-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"物理性能報告依標準、測試物與重建選擇而定，不能脫離條件使用。","textEn":"Physical performance depends on standards, objects and reconstruction choices."},{"id":"d202-v7-23-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"測試可重現性和可推廣性是不同問題；在同一物件重現結果，不代表所有樣本與用途都等效。","textEn":"Reproducibility and generalizability are different; reproducing a test object does not establish equivalence for all samples and uses."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「比較原始研究的測試條件」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Compare conditions across original studies’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["有論文就代表對每個人效果相同","比較時保留各研究條件","可任意合併所有最佳數字"],"optionsEn":["A paper guarantees identical benefit for everyone","Preserve study conditions when comparing","Arbitrarily combine all best numbers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"物理性能報告依標準、測試物與重建選擇而定，不能脫離條件使用。 測試可重現性和可推廣性是不同問題；在同一物件重現結果，不代表所有樣本與用途都等效。","explanationEn":"Physical performance depends on standards, objects and reconstruction choices. Reproducibility and generalizability are different; reproducing a test object does not establish equivalence for all samples and uses."}},{"id":"d202-v7-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"prerequisiteIds":["d202-v7-23"],"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-science-pet-about","v7-science-pet-performance","v7-science-pet-dynamic"],"title":"完成 PET、CT 與科學儀器比較","titleEn":"Complete PET, CT and scientific-instrument comparison","objective":"遷移偵測、校準與證據推理。","objectiveEn":"Transfer detection, calibration and evidence reasoning.","instruction":"對照 EXPLORER、早期 EMI CT 與大型探測器；列相同的時間、幾何及校準問題；再分開粒子來源、用途與驗證界限。","instructionEn":"Compare EXPLORER, early EMI CT and large detectors; list shared timing, geometry and calibration questions; separate particle sources, purposes and validation limits.","observation":"共通資料原理不表示設備或用途可互換。","observationEn":"Shared data principles do not make devices or purposes interchangeable.","failure":"將高能物理探測器的條件照搬到醫療系統不成立。","failureEn":"High-energy detector conditions cannot simply transfer to medical systems.","check":"審查包含物理鏈、資料鏈、品質與未決事項。","checkEn":"Review the physics chain, data chain, quality and open issues.","knowledge":[{"id":"d202-v7-24-k1","title":"工程原理","titleEn":"Engineering principle","text":"科學儀器共用訊號轉換、校準與反問題，但量測物理與適用要求各異。","textEn":"Scientific instruments share transduction, calibration and inverse problems while differing in physics and requirements."},{"id":"d202-v7-24-k2","title":"模型與驗證","titleEn":"Model and verification","text":"反問題可有多個與量測相容的解；加入先驗會改變估計，必須交代來源與對結論的敏感度。","textEn":"Inverse problems may have several data-compatible solutions; priors alter estimates and need documented origins and sensitivity analysis."}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「完成 PET、CT 與科學儀器比較」，哪個判斷正確？","questionEn":"For ‘Complete PET, CT and scientific-instrument comparison’, which conclusion is justified?","options":["所有環形探測器都能互換用途","完成重建練習即具診斷資格","共同原理與用途界限需一起說明"],"optionsEn":["All ring detectors are interchangeable","Completing reconstruction exercises qualifies one to diagnose","Explain common principles with use boundaries"],"answer":2,"explanation":"科學儀器共用訊號轉換、校準與反問題，但量測物理與適用要求各異。 反問題可有多個與量測相容的解；加入先驗會改變估計，必須交代來源與對結論的敏感度。","explanationEn":"Scientific instruments share transduction, calibration and inverse problems while differing in physics and requirements. Inverse problems may have several data-compatible solutions; priors alter estimates and need documented origins and sensitivity analysis."}}]}],"status":"guided","languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"curriculumVersion":7,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":600},{"id":"a003","title":"矽晶圓線鋸切片","titleEn":"Silicon wafer wire sawing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解切縫、TTV、次表面損傷，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore kerf, ttv and subsurface damage through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["晶棒與切片預算","線網與切削互動","片形與損傷證據","良率與後段交接"],"labelsEn":["Ingot and slicing budget","Wire web and cutting","Geometry and damage","Yield and downstream handoff"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a003-stage01","order":1,"title":"晶棒與切片預算","titleEn":"Ingot and slicing budget","description":"在「晶棒與切片預算」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for ingot and slicing budget, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a003-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨識晶向","titleEn":"Identify crystal orientation","objective":"完成「辨識晶向」的因果圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify crystal orientation, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：辨識晶向。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：晶向標記要連到晶棒座標，不能以外觀代替繞射證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify crystal orientation. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Orientation marks require ingot coordinates and diffraction evidence, not appearance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「晶向標記要連到晶棒座標，不能以外觀代替繞射證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Orientation marks require ingot coordinates and diffraction evidence, not appearance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「辨識晶向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify crystal orientation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「辨識晶向」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify crystal orientation: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-01-k1","title":"辨識晶向的原理","titleEn":"Identify crystal orientation principle","text":"晶向標記要連到晶棒座標，不能以外觀代替繞射證據。","textEn":"Orientation marks require ingot coordinates and diffraction evidence, not appearance."},{"id":"a003-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「辨識晶向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify crystal orientation?","options":["晶向標記要連到晶棒座標，不能以外觀代替繞射證據。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Orientation marks require ingot coordinates and diffraction evidence, not appearance.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶向標記要連到晶棒座標，不能以外觀代替繞射證據。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"Orientation marks require ingot coordinates and diffraction evidence, not appearance. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}},{"id":"a003-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-01"],"title":"定義可用晶棒長","titleEn":"Define usable ingot length","objective":"完成「定義可用晶棒長」的對照表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for define usable ingot length, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：定義可用晶棒長。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：頭尾排除長度會改變可用片數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define usable ingot length. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Head and tail exclusions change usable wafer count. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頭尾排除長度會改變可用片數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Head and tail exclusions change usable wafer count. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「定義可用晶棒長」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define usable ingot length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「定義可用晶棒長」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for define usable ingot length: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-02-k1","title":"定義可用晶棒長的原理","titleEn":"Define usable ingot length principle","text":"頭尾排除長度會改變可用片數。","textEn":"Head and tail exclusions change usable wafer count."},{"id":"a003-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「定義可用晶棒長」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define usable ingot length?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","頭尾排除長度會改變可用片數。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Head and tail exclusions change usable wafer count.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"頭尾排除長度會改變可用片數。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"Head and tail exclusions change usable wafer count. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}},{"id":"a003-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-02"],"title":"切縫預算","titleEn":"Budget kerf","objective":"完成「切縫預算」的敏感度草圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget kerf, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：切縫預算。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：每片占用長度包含晶圓厚度與切縫。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂算例：可用晶棒長 100 mm、切片厚 0.8 mm、切縫 0.2 mm；先求理想片數，再將切縫改為 0.25 mm 比較整數片數，列出尚未納入的端損與不良片。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget kerf. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Length consumed per slice includes wafer thickness and kerf. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical exercise: usable ingot length 100 mm, slice thickness 0.8 mm and kerf 0.2 mm. Calculate ideal integer count, change kerf to 0.25 mm and list excluded end losses and rejects.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「每片占用長度包含晶圓厚度與切縫。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Length consumed per slice includes wafer thickness and kerf. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「切縫預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget kerf and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「切縫預算」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget kerf: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-03-k1","title":"切縫預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget kerf principle","text":"每片占用長度包含晶圓厚度與切縫。","textEn":"Length consumed per slice includes wafer thickness and kerf."},{"id":"a003-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「切縫預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget kerf?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","每片占用長度包含晶圓厚度與切縫。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Length consumed per slice includes wafer thickness and kerf."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每片占用長度包含晶圓厚度與切縫。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"Length consumed per slice includes wafer thickness and kerf. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}},{"id":"a003-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-03"],"title":"厚度留量","titleEn":"Reserve thickness allowance","objective":"完成「厚度留量」的故障判別表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for reserve thickness allowance, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：厚度留量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：切片厚度還須支付損傷移除與拋光留量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reserve thickness allowance. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Sliced thickness must cover damage removal and polishing allowance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「切片厚度還須支付損傷移除與拋光留量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sliced thickness must cover damage removal and polishing allowance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「厚度留量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reserve thickness allowance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「厚度留量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for reserve thickness allowance: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-04-k1","title":"厚度留量的原理","titleEn":"Reserve thickness allowance principle","text":"切片厚度還須支付損傷移除與拋光留量。","textEn":"Sliced thickness must cover damage removal and polishing allowance."},{"id":"a003-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「厚度留量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reserve thickness allowance?","options":["切片厚度還須支付損傷移除與拋光留量。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Sliced thickness must cover damage removal and polishing allowance.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"切片厚度還須支付損傷移除與拋光留量。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"Sliced thickness must cover damage removal and polishing allowance. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}},{"id":"a003-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-04"],"title":"固定端受力圖","titleEn":"Draw mounting loads","objective":"完成「固定端受力圖」的量測規劃，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for draw mounting loads, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：固定端受力圖。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：偏心固定會讓進給負荷在切片中不均。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw mounting loads. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Eccentric mounting makes feed loading asymmetric. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「偏心固定會讓進給負荷在切片中不均。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Eccentric mounting makes feed loading asymmetric. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「固定端受力圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw mounting loads and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「固定端受力圖」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for draw mounting loads: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-05-k1","title":"固定端受力圖的原理","titleEn":"Draw mounting loads principle","text":"偏心固定會讓進給負荷在切片中不均。","textEn":"Eccentric mounting makes feed loading asymmetric."},{"id":"a003-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「固定端受力圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw mounting loads?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","偏心固定會讓進給負荷在切片中不均。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Eccentric mounting makes feed loading asymmetric.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏心固定會讓進給負荷在切片中不均。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"Eccentric mounting makes feed loading asymmetric. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}},{"id":"a003-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-05"],"title":"來料電阻率分區","titleEn":"Map incoming resistivity","objective":"完成「來料電阻率分區」的工程驗收單，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for map incoming resistivity, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：來料電阻率分區。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：沿晶棒的電阻率變化不能用單片平均值代表。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map incoming resistivity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: One wafer average cannot describe axial resistivity variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沿晶棒的電阻率變化不能用單片平均值代表。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One wafer average cannot describe axial resistivity variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「來料電阻率分區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map incoming resistivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「來料電阻率分區」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for map incoming resistivity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-06-k1","title":"來料電阻率分區的原理","titleEn":"Map incoming resistivity principle","text":"沿晶棒的電阻率變化不能用單片平均值代表。","textEn":"One wafer average cannot describe axial resistivity variation."},{"id":"a003-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","textEn":"Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「來料電阻率分區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map incoming resistivity?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","沿晶棒的電阻率變化不能用單片平均值代表。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","One wafer average cannot describe axial resistivity variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿晶棒的電阻率變化不能用單片平均值代表。 可用片數的理想上限為可用長度除以每片厚度加切縫，實際還須扣除端損及不良片。","explanationEn":"One wafer average cannot describe axial resistivity variation. Ideal slice count divides usable length by thickness plus kerf; real yield additionally loses end material and rejects."}}]},{"id":"a003-stage02","order":2,"title":"線網與切削互動","titleEn":"Wire web and cutting","description":"在「線網與切削互動」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for wire web and cutting, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a003-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-06"],"title":"線徑與槽距","titleEn":"Separate wire diameter and pitch","objective":"完成「線徑與槽距」的因果圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate wire diameter and pitch, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：線徑與槽距。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：線徑、切縫與導輪槽距是不同幾何量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate wire diameter and pitch. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Wire diameter, kerf and guide-groove pitch differ. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「線徑、切縫與導輪槽距是不同幾何量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wire diameter, kerf and guide-groove pitch differ. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「線徑與槽距」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate wire diameter and pitch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「線徑與槽距」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate wire diameter and pitch: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-07-k1","title":"線徑與槽距的原理","titleEn":"Separate wire diameter and pitch principle","text":"線徑、切縫與導輪槽距是不同幾何量。","textEn":"Wire diameter, kerf and guide-groove pitch differ."},{"id":"a003-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「線徑與槽距」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate wire diameter and pitch?","options":["線徑、切縫與導輪槽距是不同幾何量。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Wire diameter, kerf and guide-groove pitch differ.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線徑、切縫與導輪槽距是不同幾何量。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Wire diameter, kerf and guide-groove pitch differ. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}},{"id":"a003-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-07"],"title":"張力與撓曲","titleEn":"Relate tension and deflection","objective":"完成「張力與撓曲」的對照表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for relate tension and deflection, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：張力與撓曲。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：同一橫向負荷下張力改變線網撓曲。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate tension and deflection. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Wire tension changes deflection under the same transverse load. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「同一橫向負荷下張力改變線網撓曲。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wire tension changes deflection under the same transverse load. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「張力與撓曲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate tension and deflection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「張力與撓曲」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for relate tension and deflection: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-08-k1","title":"張力與撓曲的原理","titleEn":"Relate tension and deflection principle","text":"同一橫向負荷下張力改變線網撓曲。","textEn":"Wire tension changes deflection under the same transverse load."},{"id":"a003-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「張力與撓曲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate tension and deflection?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","同一橫向負荷下張力改變線網撓曲。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Wire tension changes deflection under the same transverse load.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一橫向負荷下張力改變線網撓曲。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Wire tension changes deflection under the same transverse load. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}},{"id":"a003-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-08"],"title":"進給與線速分工","titleEn":"Separate feed and wire speed","objective":"完成「進給與線速分工」的敏感度草圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate feed and wire speed, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：進給與線速分工。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：進給速度決定進入速率，線速影響磨粒接觸歷程。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate feed and wire speed. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Feed controls penetration while wire speed changes abrasive contact history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「進給速度決定進入速率，線速影響磨粒接觸歷程。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Feed controls penetration while wire speed changes abrasive contact history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「進給與線速分工」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate feed and wire speed and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「進給與線速分工」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate feed and wire speed: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-09-k1","title":"進給與線速分工的原理","titleEn":"Separate feed and wire speed principle","text":"進給速度決定進入速率，線速影響磨粒接觸歷程。","textEn":"Feed controls penetration while wire speed changes abrasive contact history."},{"id":"a003-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「進給與線速分工」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate feed and wire speed?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","進給速度決定進入速率，線速影響磨粒接觸歷程。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Feed controls penetration while wire speed changes abrasive contact history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"進給速度決定進入速率，線速影響磨粒接觸歷程。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Feed controls penetration while wire speed changes abrasive contact history. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}},{"id":"a003-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-09"],"title":"磨粒分布","titleEn":"Inspect abrasive distribution","objective":"完成「磨粒分布」的故障判別表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect abrasive distribution, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：磨粒分布。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：少數過大磨粒可能留下深損傷，平均粒徑不足以判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect abrasive distribution. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Oversized abrasive tails can cause deep damage despite a stable mean size. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「少數過大磨粒可能留下深損傷，平均粒徑不足以判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oversized abrasive tails can cause deep damage despite a stable mean size. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「磨粒分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect abrasive distribution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「磨粒分布」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect abrasive distribution: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-10-k1","title":"磨粒分布的原理","titleEn":"Inspect abrasive distribution principle","text":"少數過大磨粒可能留下深損傷，平均粒徑不足以判讀。","textEn":"Oversized abrasive tails can cause deep damage despite a stable mean size."},{"id":"a003-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「磨粒分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect abrasive distribution?","options":["少數過大磨粒可能留下深損傷，平均粒徑不足以判讀。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Oversized abrasive tails can cause deep damage despite a stable mean size.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"少數過大磨粒可能留下深損傷，平均粒徑不足以判讀。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Oversized abrasive tails can cause deep damage despite a stable mean size. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}},{"id":"a003-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-10"],"title":"排屑路徑","titleEn":"Trace debris removal","objective":"完成「排屑路徑」的量測規劃，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace debris removal, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：排屑路徑。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：排屑不足會改變接觸與局部熱負荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace debris removal. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Poor debris removal changes contact and local heating. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「排屑不足會改變接觸與局部熱負荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Poor debris removal changes contact and local heating. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「排屑路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace debris removal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「排屑路徑」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace debris removal: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-11-k1","title":"排屑路徑的原理","titleEn":"Trace debris removal principle","text":"排屑不足會改變接觸與局部熱負荷。","textEn":"Poor debris removal changes contact and local heating."},{"id":"a003-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「排屑路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace debris removal?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","排屑不足會改變接觸與局部熱負荷。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Poor debris removal changes contact and local heating.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"排屑不足會改變接觸與局部熱負荷。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Poor debris removal changes contact and local heating. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}},{"id":"a003-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-11"],"title":"斷線事件","titleEn":"Reconstruct wire breakage","objective":"完成「斷線事件」的工程驗收單，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for reconstruct wire breakage, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：斷線事件。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：斷線前的張力尖峰與片序能限定受影響區域。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reconstruct wire breakage. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Pre-break tension spikes and slice order delimit affected material. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「斷線前的張力尖峰與片序能限定受影響區域。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pre-break tension spikes and slice order delimit affected material. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「斷線事件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reconstruct wire breakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「斷線事件」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for reconstruct wire breakage: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-12-k1","title":"斷線事件的原理","titleEn":"Reconstruct wire breakage principle","text":"斷線前的張力尖峰與片序能限定受影響區域。","textEn":"Pre-break tension spikes and slice order delimit affected material."},{"id":"a003-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","textEn":"Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「斷線事件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reconstruct wire breakage?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","斷線前的張力尖峰與片序能限定受影響區域。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Pre-break tension spikes and slice order delimit affected material."],"answer":2,"explanation":"斷線前的張力尖峰與片序能限定受影響區域。 線網的機械耦合使單條線受力改變可能影響相鄰切面，進給穩定性需與導輪狀態一起看。","explanationEn":"Pre-break tension spikes and slice order delimit affected material. Mechanical coupling in a wire web means one load change can affect neighboring cuts; inspect feed stability with guide condition."}}]},{"id":"a003-stage03","order":3,"title":"片形與損傷證據","titleEn":"Geometry and damage","description":"在「片形與損傷證據」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for geometry and damage, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a003-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-12"],"title":"總厚度變異","titleEn":"Measure total thickness variation","objective":"完成「總厚度變異」的因果圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for measure total thickness variation, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：總厚度變異。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：TTV 是厚度最大與最小之差，不是表面粗糙度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure total thickness variation. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: TTV is maximum minus minimum thickness, not roughness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「TTV 是厚度最大與最小之差，不是表面粗糙度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: TTV is maximum minus minimum thickness, not roughness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「總厚度變異」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure total thickness variation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「總厚度變異」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for measure total thickness variation: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-13-k1","title":"總厚度變異的原理","titleEn":"Measure total thickness variation principle","text":"TTV 是厚度最大與最小之差，不是表面粗糙度。","textEn":"TTV is maximum minus minimum thickness, not roughness."},{"id":"a003-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「總厚度變異」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure total thickness variation?","options":["TTV 是厚度最大與最小之差，不是表面粗糙度。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["TTV is maximum minus minimum thickness, not roughness.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"TTV 是厚度最大與最小之差，不是表面粗糙度。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"TTV is maximum minus minimum thickness, not roughness. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}},{"id":"a003-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-13"],"title":"翹曲與弓形","titleEn":"Separate warp and bow","objective":"完成「翹曲與弓形」的對照表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate warp and bow, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：翹曲與弓形。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：自由狀態形貌與夾持後平坦度不可混用。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate warp and bow. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Free-state shape differs from clamped flatness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「自由狀態形貌與夾持後平坦度不可混用。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Free-state shape differs from clamped flatness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「翹曲與弓形」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate warp and bow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「翹曲與弓形」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate warp and bow: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-14-k1","title":"翹曲與弓形的原理","titleEn":"Separate warp and bow principle","text":"自由狀態形貌與夾持後平坦度不可混用。","textEn":"Free-state shape differs from clamped flatness."},{"id":"a003-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「翹曲與弓形」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate warp and bow?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","自由狀態形貌與夾持後平坦度不可混用。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Free-state shape differs from clamped flatness.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"自由狀態形貌與夾持後平坦度不可混用。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"Free-state shape differs from clamped flatness. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}},{"id":"a003-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-14"],"title":"鋸痕方向","titleEn":"Register saw-mark direction","objective":"完成「鋸痕方向」的敏感度草圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for register saw-mark direction, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鋸痕方向。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：鋸痕方向應與線運動及進給座標一起比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Register saw-mark direction. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Saw marks need registration to wire and feed directions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鋸痕方向應與線運動及進給座標一起比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Saw marks need registration to wire and feed directions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「鋸痕方向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for register saw-mark direction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鋸痕方向」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for register saw-mark direction: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-15-k1","title":"鋸痕方向的原理","titleEn":"Register saw-mark direction principle","text":"鋸痕方向應與線運動及進給座標一起比較。","textEn":"Saw marks need registration to wire and feed directions."},{"id":"a003-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鋸痕方向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating register saw-mark direction?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","鋸痕方向應與線運動及進給座標一起比較。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Saw marks need registration to wire and feed directions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋸痕方向應與線運動及進給座標一起比較。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"Saw marks need registration to wire and feed directions. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}},{"id":"a003-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-15"],"title":"次表面損傷","titleEn":"Estimate subsurface damage","objective":"完成「次表面損傷」的故障判別表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for estimate subsurface damage, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：次表面損傷。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：表面看似光滑仍可能保有次表面裂紋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate subsurface damage. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: An apparently smooth surface can retain subsurface cracks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面看似光滑仍可能保有次表面裂紋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An apparently smooth surface can retain subsurface cracks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「次表面損傷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate subsurface damage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「次表面損傷」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for estimate subsurface damage: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-16-k1","title":"次表面損傷的原理","titleEn":"Estimate subsurface damage principle","text":"表面看似光滑仍可能保有次表面裂紋。","textEn":"An apparently smooth surface can retain subsurface cracks."},{"id":"a003-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「次表面損傷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate subsurface damage?","options":["表面看似光滑仍可能保有次表面裂紋。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["An apparently smooth surface can retain subsurface cracks.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面看似光滑仍可能保有次表面裂紋。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"An apparently smooth surface can retain subsurface cracks. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}},{"id":"a003-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-16"],"title":"邊緣崩缺","titleEn":"Classify edge chips","objective":"完成「邊緣崩缺」的量測規劃，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for classify edge chips, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊緣崩缺。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：邊緣缺口尺寸及位置共同影響後續破片風險。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify edge chips. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Edge-chip size and position influence subsequent fracture risk. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊緣缺口尺寸及位置共同影響後續破片風險。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Edge-chip size and position influence subsequent fracture risk. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「邊緣崩缺」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify edge chips and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊緣崩缺」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for classify edge chips: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-17-k1","title":"邊緣崩缺的原理","titleEn":"Classify edge chips principle","text":"邊緣缺口尺寸及位置共同影響後續破片風險。","textEn":"Edge-chip size and position influence subsequent fracture risk."},{"id":"a003-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊緣崩缺」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify edge chips?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","邊緣缺口尺寸及位置共同影響後續破片風險。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Edge-chip size and position influence subsequent fracture risk.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣缺口尺寸及位置共同影響後續破片風險。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"Edge-chip size and position influence subsequent fracture risk. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}},{"id":"a003-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-17"],"title":"量測重複性","titleEn":"Check measurement repeatability","objective":"完成「量測重複性」的工程驗收單，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for check measurement repeatability, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：量測重複性。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：重新放片的變異應先與片間差異分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check measurement repeatability. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Repositioning variation must be separated from wafer variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「重新放片的變異應先與片間差異分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Repositioning variation must be separated from wafer variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「量測重複性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check measurement repeatability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「量測重複性」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for check measurement repeatability: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-18-k1","title":"量測重複性的原理","titleEn":"Check measurement repeatability principle","text":"重新放片的變異應先與片間差異分開。","textEn":"Repositioning variation must be separated from wafer variation."},{"id":"a003-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","textEn":"TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「量測重複性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check measurement repeatability?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","重新放片的變異應先與片間差異分開。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Repositioning variation must be separated from wafer variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重新放片的變異應先與片間差異分開。 TTV 用兩面的局部間距計算；弓形用中面相對參考面計算，因此厚度均勻的片仍可能彎曲。","explanationEn":"Repositioning variation must be separated from wafer variation. TTV measures local separation of both faces while bow describes the median surface; uniform thickness can coexist with curvature."}}]},{"id":"a003-stage04","order":4,"title":"良率與後段交接","titleEn":"Yield and downstream handoff","description":"在「良率與後段交接」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for yield and downstream handoff, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a003-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-18"],"title":"材料利用率","titleEn":"Compute material utilization","objective":"完成「材料利用率」的因果圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compute material utilization, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：材料利用率。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：提高片數若同時增加報廢，未必提高有效矽利用率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compute material utilization. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: More slices may not improve usable silicon yield if rejects increase. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提高片數若同時增加報廢，未必提高有效矽利用率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: More slices may not improve usable silicon yield if rejects increase. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「材料利用率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compute material utilization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「材料利用率」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compute material utilization: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-19-k1","title":"材料利用率的原理","titleEn":"Compute material utilization principle","text":"提高片數若同時增加報廢，未必提高有效矽利用率。","textEn":"More slices may not improve usable silicon yield if rejects increase."},{"id":"a003-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「材料利用率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compute material utilization?","options":["提高片數若同時增加報廢，未必提高有效矽利用率。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["More slices may not improve usable silicon yield if rejects increase.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高片數若同時增加報廢，未必提高有效矽利用率。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"More slices may not improve usable silicon yield if rejects increase. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}},{"id":"a003-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-19"],"title":"線耗追蹤","titleEn":"Track wire consumption","objective":"完成「線耗追蹤」的對照表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for track wire consumption, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：線耗追蹤。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：線耗量需按合格片數正規化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track wire consumption. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Wire consumption should be normalized by accepted wafers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「線耗量需按合格片數正規化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wire consumption should be normalized by accepted wafers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：只要每批總線耗下降，即使合格片數下降更多，也可判定單位合格片的線耗改善。 應回到「線耗追蹤」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower total wire use per batch proves better wire use per accepted wafer even if accepted output falls by a larger fraction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track wire consumption and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「線耗追蹤」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for track wire consumption: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-20-k1","title":"線耗追蹤的原理","titleEn":"Track wire consumption principle","text":"線耗量需按合格片數正規化。","textEn":"Wire consumption should be normalized by accepted wafers."},{"id":"a003-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「線耗追蹤」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track wire consumption?","options":["只要每批總線耗下降，即使合格片數下降更多，也可判定單位合格片的線耗改善。","線耗量需按合格片數正規化。","比較線耗時只需計入切出的片數，不必區分後續判退與合格片。"],"optionsEn":["Lower total wire use per batch proves better wire use per accepted wafer even if accepted output falls by a larger fraction.","Wire consumption should be normalized by accepted wafers.","Wire-use comparisons need only the number of sliced wafers, without separating subsequent rejects from accepted wafers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"線耗量需按合格片數正規化。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"Wire consumption should be normalized by accepted wafers. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}},{"id":"a003-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-20"],"title":"切片序列圖","titleEn":"Plot slice-order trends","objective":"完成「切片序列圖」的敏感度草圖，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for plot slice-order trends, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：切片序列圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：連續片的週期性厚度誤差可提示導輪相關因素。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plot slice-order trends. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Periodic slice-thickness errors can suggest guide-related causes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「連續片的週期性厚度誤差可提示導輪相關因素。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Periodic slice-thickness errors can suggest guide-related causes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「切片序列圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plot slice-order trends and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「切片序列圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for plot slice-order trends: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-21-k1","title":"切片序列圖的原理","titleEn":"Plot slice-order trends principle","text":"連續片的週期性厚度誤差可提示導輪相關因素。","textEn":"Periodic slice-thickness errors can suggest guide-related causes."},{"id":"a003-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「切片序列圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plot slice-order trends?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","連續片的週期性厚度誤差可提示導輪相關因素。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Periodic slice-thickness errors can suggest guide-related causes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"連續片的週期性厚度誤差可提示導輪相關因素。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"Periodic slice-thickness errors can suggest guide-related causes. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}},{"id":"a003-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-21"],"title":"移除留量交接","titleEn":"Transfer removal allowance","objective":"完成「移除留量交接」的故障判別表，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for transfer removal allowance, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：移除留量交接。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：研磨端需要最深損傷估計而不只是平均厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Transfer removal allowance. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Lapping needs estimated deepest damage, not just mean thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「研磨端需要最深損傷估計而不只是平均厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lapping needs estimated deepest damage, not just mean thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「移除留量交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for transfer removal allowance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「移除留量交接」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for transfer removal allowance: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-22-k1","title":"移除留量交接的原理","titleEn":"Transfer removal allowance principle","text":"研磨端需要最深損傷估計而不只是平均厚度。","textEn":"Lapping needs estimated deepest damage, not just mean thickness."},{"id":"a003-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「移除留量交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating transfer removal allowance?","options":["研磨端需要最深損傷估計而不只是平均厚度。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Lapping needs estimated deepest damage, not just mean thickness.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"研磨端需要最深損傷估計而不只是平均厚度。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"Lapping needs estimated deepest damage, not just mean thickness. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}},{"id":"a003-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-22"],"title":"盲樣重驗","titleEn":"Recheck blinded samples","objective":"完成「盲樣重驗」的量測規劃，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for recheck blinded samples, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：盲樣重驗。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：對邊界片重驗須保留原片序與量測版本。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Recheck blinded samples. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Boundary-sample retests need original slice identity and measurement version. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「對邊界片重驗須保留原片序與量測版本。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Boundary-sample retests need original slice identity and measurement version. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「盲樣重驗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for recheck blinded samples and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「盲樣重驗」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for recheck blinded samples: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-23-k1","title":"盲樣重驗的原理","titleEn":"Recheck blinded samples principle","text":"對邊界片重驗須保留原片序與量測版本。","textEn":"Boundary-sample retests need original slice identity and measurement version."},{"id":"a003-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「盲樣重驗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating recheck blinded samples?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","對邊界片重驗須保留原片序與量測版本。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Boundary-sample retests need original slice identity and measurement version.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對邊界片重驗須保留原片序與量測版本。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"Boundary-sample retests need original slice identity and measurement version. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}},{"id":"a003-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a003-v8-23"],"title":"切片批次放行","titleEn":"Release a slicing lot","objective":"完成「切片批次放行」的工程驗收單，把切縫、TTV、次表面損傷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release a slicing lot, connecting relevant limits in kerf, ttv and subsurface damage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：切片批次放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：厚度、損傷、邊緣與追溯證據須同時交付。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release a slicing lot. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Release requires thickness, damage, edge and traceability evidence together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度、損傷、邊緣與追溯證據須同時交付。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Release requires thickness, damage, edge and traceability evidence together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「切片批次放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release a slicing lot and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「切片批次放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release a slicing lot: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a003-v8-24-k1","title":"切片批次放行的原理","titleEn":"Release a slicing lot principle","text":"厚度、損傷、邊緣與追溯證據須同時交付。","textEn":"Release requires thickness, damage, edge and traceability evidence together."},{"id":"a003-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","textEn":"A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「切片批次放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release a slicing lot?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","厚度、損傷、邊緣與追溯證據須同時交付。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Release requires thickness, damage, edge and traceability evidence together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度、損傷、邊緣與追溯證據須同時交付。 切片端減少切縫的收益，若被後段新增的損傷移除量抵銷，整體矽利用率可能沒有增加。","explanationEn":"Release requires thickness, damage, edge and traceability evidence together. A smaller kerf may not improve overall silicon utilization if it requires more downstream damage removal."}}]}],"subcategory":"substrate","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓與基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafers and substrates"},{"id":"a005","title":"矽磊晶層生長","titleEn":"Silicon epitaxial growth","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["基板與磊晶目標","反應與傳輸","晶體及摻雜判讀","整合與放行"],"labelsEn":["Substrate and epitaxy target","Reaction and transport","Crystal and doping evidence","Integration and release"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a005-stage01","order":1,"title":"基板與磊晶目標","titleEn":"Substrate and epitaxy target","description":"在「基板與磊晶目標」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for substrate and epitaxy target, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a005-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"區分磊晶與沉積","titleEn":"Distinguish epitaxy from deposition","objective":"完成「區分磊晶與沉積」的因果圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for distinguish epitaxy from deposition, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：區分磊晶與沉積。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：磊晶需要與基板有確定晶體關係。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish epitaxy from deposition. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Epitaxy requires a defined crystallographic relationship to the substrate. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「磊晶需要與基板有確定晶體關係。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Epitaxy requires a defined crystallographic relationship to the substrate. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「區分磊晶與沉積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish epitaxy from deposition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「區分磊晶與沉積」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for distinguish epitaxy from deposition: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-01-k1","title":"區分磊晶與沉積的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish epitaxy from deposition principle","text":"磊晶需要與基板有確定晶體關係。","textEn":"Epitaxy requires a defined crystallographic relationship to the substrate."},{"id":"a005-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「區分磊晶與沉積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish epitaxy from deposition?","options":["磊晶需要與基板有確定晶體關係。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Epitaxy requires a defined crystallographic relationship to the substrate.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"磊晶需要與基板有確定晶體關係。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"Epitaxy requires a defined crystallographic relationship to the substrate. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}},{"id":"a005-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-01"],"title":"基板電性階梯","titleEn":"Define substrate-layer electrical contrast","objective":"完成「基板電性階梯」的對照表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for define substrate-layer electrical contrast, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基板電性階梯。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：磊晶層與基板可有不同摻雜濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define substrate-layer electrical contrast. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: The epitaxial layer and substrate can have different doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「磊晶層與基板可有不同摻雜濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The epitaxial layer and substrate can have different doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「基板電性階梯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define substrate-layer electrical contrast and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基板電性階梯」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for define substrate-layer electrical contrast: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-02-k1","title":"基板電性階梯的原理","titleEn":"Define substrate-layer electrical contrast principle","text":"磊晶層與基板可有不同摻雜濃度。","textEn":"The epitaxial layer and substrate can have different doping."},{"id":"a005-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基板電性階梯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define substrate-layer electrical contrast?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","磊晶層與基板可有不同摻雜濃度。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","The epitaxial layer and substrate can have different doping.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"磊晶層與基板可有不同摻雜濃度。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"The epitaxial layer and substrate can have different doping. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}},{"id":"a005-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-02"],"title":"晶向與台階","titleEn":"Read orientation and terraces","objective":"完成「晶向與台階」的敏感度草圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for read orientation and terraces, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶向與台階。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：微偏角影響表面台階密度及成長形貌。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read orientation and terraces. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Miscut changes terrace density and growth morphology. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「微偏角影響表面台階密度及成長形貌。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Miscut changes terrace density and growth morphology. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「晶向與台階」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read orientation and terraces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶向與台階」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for read orientation and terraces: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-03-k1","title":"晶向與台階的原理","titleEn":"Read orientation and terraces principle","text":"微偏角影響表面台階密度及成長形貌。","textEn":"Miscut changes terrace density and growth morphology."},{"id":"a005-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶向與台階」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read orientation and terraces?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","微偏角影響表面台階密度及成長形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Miscut changes terrace density and growth morphology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"微偏角影響表面台階密度及成長形貌。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"Miscut changes terrace density and growth morphology. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}},{"id":"a005-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-03"],"title":"原生氧化層","titleEn":"Assess native oxide","objective":"完成「原生氧化層」的故障判別表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess native oxide, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：原生氧化層。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：殘留氧化物會中斷外延晶格的延續。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess native oxide. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Residual oxide interrupts crystalline registry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「殘留氧化物會中斷外延晶格的延續。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual oxide interrupts crystalline registry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「原生氧化層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess native oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「原生氧化層」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess native oxide: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-04-k1","title":"原生氧化層的原理","titleEn":"Assess native oxide principle","text":"殘留氧化物會中斷外延晶格的延續。","textEn":"Residual oxide interrupts crystalline registry."},{"id":"a005-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「原生氧化層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess native oxide?","options":["殘留氧化物會中斷外延晶格的延續。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Residual oxide interrupts crystalline registry.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留氧化物會中斷外延晶格的延續。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"Residual oxide interrupts crystalline registry. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}},{"id":"a005-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-04"],"title":"表面潔淨交接","titleEn":"Specify the clean-to-growth handoff","objective":"完成「表面潔淨交接」的量測規劃，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for specify the clean-to-growth handoff, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面潔淨交接。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：清洗後等待時間可能改變再氧化與吸附。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Specify the clean-to-growth handoff. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Queue time after cleaning can change reoxidation and adsorption. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清洗後等待時間可能改變再氧化與吸附。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Queue time after cleaning can change reoxidation and adsorption. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「表面潔淨交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for specify the clean-to-growth handoff and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面潔淨交接」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for specify the clean-to-growth handoff: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-05-k1","title":"表面潔淨交接的原理","titleEn":"Specify the clean-to-growth handoff principle","text":"清洗後等待時間可能改變再氧化與吸附。","textEn":"Queue time after cleaning can change reoxidation and adsorption."},{"id":"a005-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面潔淨交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating specify the clean-to-growth handoff?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","清洗後等待時間可能改變再氧化與吸附。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Queue time after cleaning can change reoxidation and adsorption.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清洗後等待時間可能改變再氧化與吸附。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"Queue time after cleaning can change reoxidation and adsorption. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}},{"id":"a005-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-05"],"title":"截面厚度目標","titleEn":"Set cross-section targets","objective":"完成「截面厚度目標」的工程驗收單，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for set cross-section targets, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：截面厚度目標。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：膜厚目標應與電性用途及後段熱歷程連結。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set cross-section targets. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thickness targets require electrical purpose and later thermal history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「膜厚目標應與電性用途及後段熱歷程連結。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness targets require electrical purpose and later thermal history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「截面厚度目標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set cross-section targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「截面厚度目標」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for set cross-section targets: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-06-k1","title":"截面厚度目標的原理","titleEn":"Set cross-section targets principle","text":"膜厚目標應與電性用途及後段熱歷程連結。","textEn":"Thickness targets require electrical purpose and later thermal history."},{"id":"a005-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","textEn":"The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「截面厚度目標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set cross-section targets?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","膜厚目標應與電性用途及後段熱歷程連結。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Thickness targets require electrical purpose and later thermal history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜厚目標應與電性用途及後段熱歷程連結。 基板提供晶格模板，但摻雜、殘留氧化物與缺陷會改變新生晶層的電性與完整性。","explanationEn":"Thickness targets require electrical purpose and later thermal history. The substrate provides lattice registry, but doping, oxide and defects affect the new layer’s electrical and structural quality."}}]},{"id":"a005-stage02","order":2,"title":"反應與傳輸","titleEn":"Reaction and transport","description":"在「反應與傳輸」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for reaction and transport, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a005-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-06"],"title":"反應控制區","titleEn":"Identify reaction-limited growth","objective":"完成「反應控制區」的因果圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify reaction-limited growth, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：反應控制區。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：反應受限區對表面溫度較敏感。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify reaction-limited growth. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Reaction-limited growth is more sensitive to surface temperature. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應受限區對表面溫度較敏感。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reaction-limited growth is more sensitive to surface temperature. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「反應控制區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify reaction-limited growth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「反應控制區」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify reaction-limited growth: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-07-k1","title":"反應控制區的原理","titleEn":"Identify reaction-limited growth principle","text":"反應受限區對表面溫度較敏感。","textEn":"Reaction-limited growth is more sensitive to surface temperature."},{"id":"a005-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「反應控制區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify reaction-limited growth?","options":["反應受限區對表面溫度較敏感。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Reaction-limited growth is more sensitive to surface temperature.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反應受限區對表面溫度較敏感。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Reaction-limited growth is more sensitive to surface temperature. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}},{"id":"a005-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-07"],"title":"傳質控制區","titleEn":"Identify transport-limited growth","objective":"完成「傳質控制區」的對照表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify transport-limited growth, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：傳質控制區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：傳輸受限時增加表面反應速率未必增加成長。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify transport-limited growth. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Faster surface reaction need not accelerate transport-limited growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「傳輸受限時增加表面反應速率未必增加成長。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Faster surface reaction need not accelerate transport-limited growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「傳質控制區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify transport-limited growth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「傳質控制區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify transport-limited growth: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-08-k1","title":"傳質控制區的原理","titleEn":"Identify transport-limited growth principle","text":"傳輸受限時增加表面反應速率未必增加成長。","textEn":"Faster surface reaction need not accelerate transport-limited growth."},{"id":"a005-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「傳質控制區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify transport-limited growth?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","傳輸受限時增加表面反應速率未必增加成長。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Faster surface reaction need not accelerate transport-limited growth.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"傳輸受限時增加表面反應速率未必增加成長。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Faster surface reaction need not accelerate transport-limited growth. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}},{"id":"a005-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-08"],"title":"入口耗盡","titleEn":"Trace inlet depletion","objective":"完成「入口耗盡」的敏感度草圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace inlet depletion, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：入口耗盡。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：反應物沿流向耗盡可形成厚度梯度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace inlet depletion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Reactant depletion along flow can create thickness gradients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應物沿流向耗盡可形成厚度梯度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reactant depletion along flow can create thickness gradients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「入口耗盡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace inlet depletion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「入口耗盡」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace inlet depletion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-09-k1","title":"入口耗盡的原理","titleEn":"Trace inlet depletion principle","text":"反應物沿流向耗盡可形成厚度梯度。","textEn":"Reactant depletion along flow can create thickness gradients."},{"id":"a005-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「入口耗盡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace inlet depletion?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","反應物沿流向耗盡可形成厚度梯度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Reactant depletion along flow can create thickness gradients."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應物沿流向耗盡可形成厚度梯度。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Reactant depletion along flow can create thickness gradients. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}},{"id":"a005-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-09"],"title":"旋轉平均效果","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging","objective":"完成「旋轉平均效果」的故障判別表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess rotation averaging, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：旋轉平均效果。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：旋轉能平均角向不均，未必消除徑向梯度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess rotation averaging. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Rotation averages azimuthal variations but may preserve radial gradients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「旋轉能平均角向不均，未必消除徑向梯度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rotation averages azimuthal variations but may preserve radial gradients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「旋轉平均效果」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess rotation averaging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「旋轉平均效果」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess rotation averaging: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-10-k1","title":"旋轉平均效果的原理","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging principle","text":"旋轉能平均角向不均，未必消除徑向梯度。","textEn":"Rotation averages azimuthal variations but may preserve radial gradients."},{"id":"a005-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「旋轉平均效果」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess rotation averaging?","options":["旋轉能平均角向不均，未必消除徑向梯度。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Rotation averages azimuthal variations but may preserve radial gradients.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"旋轉能平均角向不均，未必消除徑向梯度。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Rotation averages azimuthal variations but may preserve radial gradients. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}},{"id":"a005-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-10"],"title":"自摻雜","titleEn":"Trace autodoping","objective":"完成「自摻雜」的量測規劃，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace autodoping, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自摻雜。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：基板釋出摻雜可污染原本設定的磊晶濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace autodoping. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Substrate dopants can alter intended epitaxial doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「基板釋出摻雜可污染原本設定的磊晶濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Substrate dopants can alter intended epitaxial doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「自摻雜」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace autodoping and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自摻雜」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace autodoping: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-11-k1","title":"自摻雜的原理","titleEn":"Trace autodoping principle","text":"基板釋出摻雜可污染原本設定的磊晶濃度。","textEn":"Substrate dopants can alter intended epitaxial doping."},{"id":"a005-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自摻雜」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace autodoping?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","基板釋出摻雜可污染原本設定的磊晶濃度。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Substrate dopants can alter intended epitaxial doping.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板釋出摻雜可污染原本設定的磊晶濃度。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Substrate dopants can alter intended epitaxial doping. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}},{"id":"a005-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-11"],"title":"腔體記憶","titleEn":"Identify chamber memory","objective":"完成「腔體記憶」的工程驗收單，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for identify chamber memory, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：腔體記憶。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：前批材料可能影響後批背景濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify chamber memory. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Previous chamber history can affect subsequent background doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前批材料可能影響後批背景濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Previous chamber history can affect subsequent background doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「腔體記憶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify chamber memory and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「腔體記憶」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for identify chamber memory: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-12-k1","title":"腔體記憶的原理","titleEn":"Identify chamber memory principle","text":"前批材料可能影響後批背景濃度。","textEn":"Previous chamber history can affect subsequent background doping."},{"id":"a005-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","textEn":"Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「腔體記憶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify chamber memory?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","前批材料可能影響後批背景濃度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Previous chamber history can affect subsequent background doping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"前批材料可能影響後批背景濃度。 表面反應與邊界層傳質是串聯的限制；改善其中較快一項可能無法增加總成長速率。","explanationEn":"Previous chamber history can affect subsequent background doping. Surface reaction and boundary-layer transport impose serial limits; accelerating the faster process may not raise growth rate."}}]},{"id":"a005-stage03","order":3,"title":"晶體及摻雜判讀","titleEn":"Crystal and doping evidence","description":"在「晶體及摻雜判讀」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for crystal and doping evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a005-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-12"],"title":"厚度均勻圖","titleEn":"Map thickness uniformity","objective":"完成「厚度均勻圖」的因果圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map thickness uniformity, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：厚度均勻圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：中心邊緣與方位點都需納入採樣。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map thickness uniformity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Sampling should include radial and azimuthal positions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中心邊緣與方位點都需納入採樣。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sampling should include radial and azimuthal positions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「厚度均勻圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map thickness uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「厚度均勻圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map thickness uniformity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-13-k1","title":"厚度均勻圖的原理","titleEn":"Map thickness uniformity principle","text":"中心邊緣與方位點都需納入採樣。","textEn":"Sampling should include radial and azimuthal positions."},{"id":"a005-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「厚度均勻圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map thickness uniformity?","options":["中心邊緣與方位點都需納入採樣。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Sampling should include radial and azimuthal positions.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中心邊緣與方位點都需納入採樣。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Sampling should include radial and azimuthal positions. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}},{"id":"a005-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-13"],"title":"摻雜深度輪廓","titleEn":"Read doping depth profiles","objective":"完成「摻雜深度輪廓」的對照表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for read doping depth profiles, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜深度輪廓。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：濃度輪廓的陡峭程度會受量測解析度限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read doping depth profiles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Measured profile abruptness is limited by instrument resolution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濃度輪廓的陡峭程度會受量測解析度限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Measured profile abruptness is limited by instrument resolution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「摻雜深度輪廓」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read doping depth profiles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜深度輪廓」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for read doping depth profiles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-14-k1","title":"摻雜深度輪廓的原理","titleEn":"Read doping depth profiles principle","text":"濃度輪廓的陡峭程度會受量測解析度限制。","textEn":"Measured profile abruptness is limited by instrument resolution."},{"id":"a005-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜深度輪廓」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read doping depth profiles?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","濃度輪廓的陡峭程度會受量測解析度限制。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Measured profile abruptness is limited by instrument resolution.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"濃度輪廓的陡峭程度會受量測解析度限制。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Measured profile abruptness is limited by instrument resolution. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}},{"id":"a005-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-14"],"title":"電阻率與活化","titleEn":"Relate resistivity and activation","objective":"完成「電阻率與活化」的敏感度草圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for relate resistivity and activation, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電阻率與活化。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：電阻率取決於載子濃度及遷移率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂算例：假設同一材料的活化載子濃度加倍、遷移率降為原來的 0.8；以電導率與兩者乘積成正比估算變化，再說明為何仍需深度輪廓。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate resistivity and activation. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Resistivity depends on both carrier density and mobility. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical exercise: active carrier density doubles while mobility becomes 0.8 of its original value. Estimate conductivity change from their product and explain why a depth profile is still needed.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電阻率取決於載子濃度及遷移率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Resistivity depends on both carrier density and mobility. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「電阻率與活化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate resistivity and activation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電阻率與活化」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for relate resistivity and activation: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-15-k1","title":"電阻率與活化的原理","titleEn":"Relate resistivity and activation principle","text":"電阻率取決於載子濃度及遷移率。","textEn":"Resistivity depends on both carrier density and mobility."},{"id":"a005-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電阻率與活化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate resistivity and activation?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","電阻率取決於載子濃度及遷移率。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Resistivity depends on both carrier density and mobility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電阻率取決於載子濃度及遷移率。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Resistivity depends on both carrier density and mobility. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}},{"id":"a005-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-15"],"title":"堆疊錯誤","titleEn":"Classify stacking defects","objective":"完成「堆疊錯誤」的故障判別表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for classify stacking defects, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：堆疊錯誤。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：局部晶體缺陷應與基板缺陷座標配對。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify stacking defects. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Local crystal defects should be registered to substrate defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部晶體缺陷應與基板缺陷座標配對。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local crystal defects should be registered to substrate defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「堆疊錯誤」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify stacking defects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「堆疊錯誤」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for classify stacking defects: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-16-k1","title":"堆疊錯誤的原理","titleEn":"Classify stacking defects principle","text":"局部晶體缺陷應與基板缺陷座標配對。","textEn":"Local crystal defects should be registered to substrate defects."},{"id":"a005-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「堆疊錯誤」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify stacking defects?","options":["局部晶體缺陷應與基板缺陷座標配對。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Local crystal defects should be registered to substrate defects.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部晶體缺陷應與基板缺陷座標配對。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Local crystal defects should be registered to substrate defects. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}},{"id":"a005-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-16"],"title":"粗糙度尺度","titleEn":"Compare roughness scales","objective":"完成「粗糙度尺度」的量測規劃，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare roughness scales, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粗糙度尺度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同掃描面積可能得到不同粗糙度統計。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare roughness scales. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Roughness statistics depend on scan area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同掃描面積可能得到不同粗糙度統計。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Roughness statistics depend on scan area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「粗糙度尺度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare roughness scales and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粗糙度尺度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare roughness scales: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-17-k1","title":"粗糙度尺度的原理","titleEn":"Compare roughness scales principle","text":"不同掃描面積可能得到不同粗糙度統計。","textEn":"Roughness statistics depend on scan area."},{"id":"a005-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粗糙度尺度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare roughness scales?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","不同掃描面積可能得到不同粗糙度統計。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Roughness statistics depend on scan area.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同掃描面積可能得到不同粗糙度統計。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Roughness statistics depend on scan area. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}},{"id":"a005-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-17"],"title":"界面擴散","titleEn":"Estimate interface broadening","objective":"完成「界面擴散」的工程驗收單，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for estimate interface broadening, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面擴散。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：後續熱處理會改變原先的摻雜階梯。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate interface broadening. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Later heating can broaden an initially abrupt doping transition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「後續熱處理會改變原先的摻雜階梯。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Later heating can broaden an initially abrupt doping transition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「界面擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate interface broadening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面擴散」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for estimate interface broadening: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-18-k1","title":"界面擴散的原理","titleEn":"Estimate interface broadening principle","text":"後續熱處理會改變原先的摻雜階梯。","textEn":"Later heating can broaden an initially abrupt doping transition."},{"id":"a005-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate interface broadening?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","後續熱處理會改變原先的摻雜階梯。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Later heating can broaden an initially abrupt doping transition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"後續熱處理會改變原先的摻雜階梯。 電阻率近似由載子濃度與遷移率乘積決定，因此只量電阻率無法唯一重建深度摻雜輪廓。","explanationEn":"Later heating can broaden an initially abrupt doping transition. Resistivity depends approximately on carrier density times mobility, so resistivity alone cannot reconstruct a unique doping profile."}}]},{"id":"a005-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與放行","titleEn":"Integration and release","description":"在「整合與放行」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for integration and release, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a005-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-18"],"title":"熱預算帳本","titleEn":"Build a thermal-budget ledger","objective":"完成「熱預算帳本」的因果圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for build a thermal-budget ledger, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算帳本。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：相同最終膜厚不代表相同熱歷程。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a thermal-budget ledger. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Equal final thickness does not imply equal thermal history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同最終膜厚不代表相同熱歷程。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal final thickness does not imply equal thermal history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「熱預算帳本」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a thermal-budget ledger and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算帳本」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for build a thermal-budget ledger: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-19-k1","title":"熱預算帳本的原理","titleEn":"Build a thermal-budget ledger principle","text":"相同最終膜厚不代表相同熱歷程。","textEn":"Equal final thickness does not imply equal thermal history."},{"id":"a005-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算帳本」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a thermal-budget ledger?","options":["相同最終膜厚不代表相同熱歷程。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final thickness does not imply equal thermal history.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同最終膜厚不代表相同熱歷程。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"Equal final thickness does not imply equal thermal history. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}},{"id":"a005-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-19"],"title":"圖案負載效應","titleEn":"Assess pattern loading","objective":"完成「圖案負載效應」的對照表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess pattern loading, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案負載效應。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：裸片結果不能直接代替有圖案表面的成長結果。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pattern loading. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Blanket-wafer results do not directly predict patterned growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「裸片結果不能直接代替有圖案表面的成長結果。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Blanket-wafer results do not directly predict patterned growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「圖案負載效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pattern loading and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案負載效應」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess pattern loading: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-20-k1","title":"圖案負載效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess pattern loading principle","text":"裸片結果不能直接代替有圖案表面的成長結果。","textEn":"Blanket-wafer results do not directly predict patterned growth."},{"id":"a005-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案負載效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pattern loading?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","裸片結果不能直接代替有圖案表面的成長結果。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Blanket-wafer results do not directly predict patterned growth.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"裸片結果不能直接代替有圖案表面的成長結果。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"Blanket-wafer results do not directly predict patterned growth. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}},{"id":"a005-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-20"],"title":"粒子與成長缺陷","titleEn":"Distinguish particles from growth defects","objective":"完成「粒子與成長缺陷」的敏感度草圖，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles from growth defects, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子與成長缺陷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：粒子沉積與晶格成長缺陷需要不同分析證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish particles from growth defects. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Deposited particles and crystalline growth defects require different evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子沉積與晶格成長缺陷需要不同分析證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Deposited particles and crystalline growth defects require different evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「粒子與成長缺陷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish particles from growth defects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子與成長缺陷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles from growth defects: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-21-k1","title":"粒子與成長缺陷的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish particles from growth defects principle","text":"粒子沉積與晶格成長缺陷需要不同分析證據。","textEn":"Deposited particles and crystalline growth defects require different evidence."},{"id":"a005-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子與成長缺陷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish particles from growth defects?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","粒子沉積與晶格成長缺陷需要不同分析證據。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Deposited particles and crystalline growth defects require different evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粒子沉積與晶格成長缺陷需要不同分析證據。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"Deposited particles and crystalline growth defects require different evidence. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}},{"id":"a005-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-21"],"title":"雙因子實驗","titleEn":"Design a two-factor study","objective":"完成「雙因子實驗」的故障判別表，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for design a two-factor study, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：雙因子實驗。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：改變溫度與流量時要保留交互作用判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design a two-factor study. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A temperature-flow study should preserve interaction effects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「改變溫度與流量時要保留交互作用判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A temperature-flow study should preserve interaction effects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「雙因子實驗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design a two-factor study and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「雙因子實驗」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for design a two-factor study: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-22-k1","title":"雙因子實驗的原理","titleEn":"Design a two-factor study principle","text":"改變溫度與流量時要保留交互作用判讀。","textEn":"A temperature-flow study should preserve interaction effects."},{"id":"a005-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「雙因子實驗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design a two-factor study?","options":["改變溫度與流量時要保留交互作用判讀。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["A temperature-flow study should preserve interaction effects.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"改變溫度與流量時要保留交互作用判讀。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"A temperature-flow study should preserve interaction effects. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}},{"id":"a005-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-22"],"title":"電性見證片","titleEn":"Choose electrical witnesses","objective":"完成「電性見證片」的量測規劃，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose electrical witnesses, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電性見證片。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：只量膜厚不能保證電性符合要求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose electrical witnesses. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Thickness alone cannot establish electrical suitability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只量膜厚不能保證電性符合要求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness alone cannot establish electrical suitability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「電性見證片」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose electrical witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電性見證片」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose electrical witnesses: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-23-k1","title":"電性見證片的原理","titleEn":"Choose electrical witnesses principle","text":"只量膜厚不能保證電性符合要求。","textEn":"Thickness alone cannot establish electrical suitability."},{"id":"a005-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電性見證片」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose electrical witnesses?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","只量膜厚不能保證電性符合要求。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Thickness alone cannot establish electrical suitability.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量膜厚不能保證電性符合要求。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"Thickness alone cannot establish electrical suitability. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}},{"id":"a005-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sumco","v8a-epi","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a005-v8-23"],"title":"磊晶交接檔","titleEn":"Assemble the epitaxy dossier","objective":"完成「磊晶交接檔」的工程驗收單，把膜厚、摻雜階梯、晶體缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assemble the epitaxy dossier, connecting relevant limits in thickness, doping transitions and crystalline defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：磊晶交接檔。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：膜厚、摻雜、缺陷與熱歷程共同定義材料品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assemble the epitaxy dossier. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thickness, doping, defects and thermal history jointly define quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「膜厚、摻雜、缺陷與熱歷程共同定義材料品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness, doping, defects and thermal history jointly define quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「磊晶交接檔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assemble the epitaxy dossier and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「磊晶交接檔」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assemble the epitaxy dossier: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a005-v8-24-k1","title":"磊晶交接檔的原理","titleEn":"Assemble the epitaxy dossier principle","text":"膜厚、摻雜、缺陷與熱歷程共同定義材料品質。","textEn":"Thickness, doping, defects and thermal history jointly define quality."},{"id":"a005-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","textEn":"Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「磊晶交接檔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assemble the epitaxy dossier?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","膜厚、摻雜、缺陷與熱歷程共同定義材料品質。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Thickness, doping, defects and thermal history jointly define quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜厚、摻雜、缺陷與熱歷程共同定義材料品質。 磊晶層的初始缺陷、後段擴散及接觸加工會共同決定元件結果，材料放行需保留熱歷程版本。","explanationEn":"Thickness, doping, defects and thermal history jointly define quality. Initial epitaxial defects, subsequent diffusion and contact processing jointly determine device outcomes; retain thermal-history versions."}}]}],"subcategory":"substrate","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓與基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafers and substrates"},{"id":"a006","title":"絕緣層上覆矽晶圓製造","titleEn":"Silicon-on-insulator wafer fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["SOI 結構分工","鍵合與層轉移","薄層量測","元件相容性"],"labelsEn":["SOI layer functions","Bonding and layer transfer","Thin-layer measurements","Device compatibility"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a006-stage01","order":1,"title":"SOI 結構分工","titleEn":"SOI layer functions","description":"在「SOI 結構分工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for soi layer functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨認三層結構","titleEn":"Identify the three-layer stack","objective":"完成「辨認三層結構」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify the three-layer stack, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：辨認三層結構。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the three-layer stack. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「辨認三層結構」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the three-layer stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「辨認三層結構」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify the three-layer stack: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-01-k1","title":"辨認三層結構的原理","titleEn":"Identify the three-layer stack principle","text":"頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。","textEn":"Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles."},{"id":"a006-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「辨認三層結構」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the three-layer stack?","options":["頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-01"],"title":"選擇層轉移路徑","titleEn":"Compare layer-transfer routes","objective":"完成「選擇層轉移路徑」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare layer-transfer routes, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇層轉移路徑。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare layer-transfer routes. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「選擇層轉移路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare layer-transfer routes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇層轉移路徑」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare layer-transfer routes: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-02-k1","title":"選擇層轉移路徑的原理","titleEn":"Compare layer-transfer routes principle","text":"鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。","textEn":"Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms."},{"id":"a006-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇層轉移路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare layer-transfer routes?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-02"],"title":"頂矽厚度預算","titleEn":"Budget top-silicon thickness","objective":"完成「頂矽厚度預算」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget top-silicon thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：頂矽厚度預算。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂厚度帳：頂矽轉移後 120 個任意厚度單位、修整消耗 15、後續氧化消耗矽 5；求剩餘量，再檢查是否有把氧化物厚度誤當成矽消耗。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget top-silicon thickness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical thickness ledger: transferred top silicon 120 arbitrary units, finishing consumes 15 and later oxidation consumes 5 silicon units. Compute the remainder and check that oxide thickness was not confused with silicon consumption.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「頂矽厚度預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget top-silicon thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「頂矽厚度預算」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget top-silicon thickness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-03-k1","title":"頂矽厚度預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget top-silicon thickness principle","text":"分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。","textEn":"Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance."},{"id":"a006-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「頂矽厚度預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget top-silicon thickness?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-03"],"title":"埋氧厚度作用","titleEn":"Assess buried-oxide thickness","objective":"完成「埋氧厚度作用」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess buried-oxide thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋氧厚度作用。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess buried-oxide thickness. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「埋氧厚度作用」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess buried-oxide thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋氧厚度作用」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess buried-oxide thickness: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-04-k1","title":"埋氧厚度作用的原理","titleEn":"Assess buried-oxide thickness principle","text":"埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。","textEn":"Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow."},{"id":"a006-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋氧厚度作用」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess buried-oxide thickness?","options":["埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-04"],"title":"供體可回收性","titleEn":"Plan donor reuse","objective":"完成「供體可回收性」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for plan donor reuse, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：供體可回收性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan donor reuse. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「供體可回收性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan donor reuse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「供體可回收性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for plan donor reuse: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-05-k1","title":"供體可回收性的原理","titleEn":"Plan donor reuse principle","text":"供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。","textEn":"Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting."},{"id":"a006-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「供體可回收性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan donor reuse?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-05"],"title":"晶圓配對","titleEn":"Pair donor and handle wafers","objective":"完成「晶圓配對」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for pair donor and handle wafers, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶圓配對。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Pair donor and handle wafers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「晶圓配對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for pair donor and handle wafers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶圓配對」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for pair donor and handle wafers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-06-k1","title":"晶圓配對的原理","titleEn":"Pair donor and handle wafers principle","text":"熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。","textEn":"Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding."},{"id":"a006-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶圓配對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating pair donor and handle wafers?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage02","order":2,"title":"鍵合與層轉移","titleEn":"Bonding and layer transfer","description":"在「鍵合與層轉移」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for bonding and layer transfer, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-06"],"title":"離子層深度","titleEn":"Locate the implanted split layer","objective":"完成「離子層深度」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for locate the implanted split layer, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離子層深度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate the implanted split layer. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「離子層深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate the implanted split layer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離子層深度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for locate the implanted split layer: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-07-k1","title":"離子層深度的原理","titleEn":"Locate the implanted split layer principle","text":"佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。","textEn":"Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty."},{"id":"a006-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離子層深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate the implanted split layer?","options":["佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-07"],"title":"活化表面","titleEn":"Compare activated surfaces","objective":"完成「活化表面」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare activated surfaces, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化表面。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare activated surfaces. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「活化表面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare activated surfaces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化表面」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare activated surfaces: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-08-k1","title":"活化表面的原理","titleEn":"Compare activated surfaces principle","text":"表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。","textEn":"Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness."},{"id":"a006-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化表面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare activated surfaces?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-08"],"title":"顆粒與空洞","titleEn":"Connect particles to voids","objective":"完成「顆粒與空洞」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for connect particles to voids, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：顆粒與空洞。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect particles to voids. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「顆粒與空洞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect particles to voids and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「顆粒與空洞」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for connect particles to voids: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-09-k1","title":"顆粒與空洞的原理","titleEn":"Connect particles to voids principle","text":"單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。","textEn":"One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself."},{"id":"a006-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「顆粒與空洞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect particles to voids?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-09"],"title":"鍵合波前","titleEn":"Track bonding-front propagation","objective":"完成「鍵合波前」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for track bonding-front propagation, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍵合波前。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bonding-front propagation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「鍵合波前」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bonding-front propagation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍵合波前」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for track bonding-front propagation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-10-k1","title":"鍵合波前的原理","titleEn":"Track bonding-front propagation principle","text":"波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。","textEn":"Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems."},{"id":"a006-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍵合波前」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bonding-front propagation?","options":["波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-10"],"title":"分裂與熱處理","titleEn":"Separate splitting from strengthening","objective":"完成「分裂與熱處理」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate splitting from strengthening, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分裂與熱處理。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate splitting from strengthening. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「分裂與熱處理」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate splitting from strengthening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分裂與熱處理」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate splitting from strengthening: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-11-k1","title":"分裂與熱處理的原理","titleEn":"Separate splitting from strengthening principle","text":"分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。","textEn":"Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface."},{"id":"a006-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分裂與熱處理」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate splitting from strengthening?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-11"],"title":"供體修復","titleEn":"Define donor refresh evidence","objective":"完成「供體修復」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for define donor refresh evidence, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：供體修復。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define donor refresh evidence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「供體修復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define donor refresh evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「供體修復」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for define donor refresh evidence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-12-k1","title":"供體修復的原理","titleEn":"Define donor refresh evidence principle","text":"再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。","textEn":"Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment."},{"id":"a006-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「供體修復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define donor refresh evidence?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage03","order":3,"title":"薄層量測","titleEn":"Thin-layer measurements","description":"在「薄層量測」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for thin-layer measurements, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-12"],"title":"頂矽厚度圖","titleEn":"Map top-silicon thickness","objective":"完成「頂矽厚度圖」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map top-silicon thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：頂矽厚度圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map top-silicon thickness. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「頂矽厚度圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map top-silicon thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「頂矽厚度圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map top-silicon thickness: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-13-k1","title":"頂矽厚度圖的原理","titleEn":"Map top-silicon thickness principle","text":"厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。","textEn":"Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation."},{"id":"a006-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「頂矽厚度圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map top-silicon thickness?","options":["厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-13"],"title":"埋氧連續性","titleEn":"Inspect buried-oxide continuity","objective":"完成「埋氧連續性」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect buried-oxide continuity, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋氧連續性。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect buried-oxide continuity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「埋氧連續性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect buried-oxide continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋氧連續性」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect buried-oxide continuity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-14-k1","title":"埋氧連續性的原理","titleEn":"Inspect buried-oxide continuity principle","text":"局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。","textEn":"Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths."},{"id":"a006-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋氧連續性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect buried-oxide continuity?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-14"],"title":"鍵合強度分布","titleEn":"Map bond strength","objective":"完成「鍵合強度分布」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map bond strength, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍵合強度分布。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map bond strength. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「鍵合強度分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map bond strength and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍵合強度分布」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map bond strength: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-15-k1","title":"鍵合強度分布的原理","titleEn":"Map bond strength principle","text":"局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。","textEn":"One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength."},{"id":"a006-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍵合強度分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map bond strength?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-15"],"title":"界面陷阱","titleEn":"Assess interface traps","objective":"完成「界面陷阱」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess interface traps, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面陷阱。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess interface traps. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「界面陷阱」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess interface traps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面陷阱」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess interface traps: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-16-k1","title":"界面陷阱的原理","titleEn":"Assess interface traps principle","text":"幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。","textEn":"Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality."},{"id":"a006-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面陷阱」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess interface traps?","options":["幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-16"],"title":"表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Check transferred-surface roughness","objective":"完成「表面粗糙度」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for check transferred-surface roughness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面粗糙度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check transferred-surface roughness. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「表面粗糙度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check transferred-surface roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面粗糙度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for check transferred-surface roughness: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-17-k1","title":"表面粗糙度的原理","titleEn":"Check transferred-surface roughness principle","text":"分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。","textEn":"The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons."},{"id":"a006-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面粗糙度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check transferred-surface roughness?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-17"],"title":"缺陷邊緣排除","titleEn":"Specify edge exclusion","objective":"完成「缺陷邊緣排除」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for specify edge exclusion, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺陷邊緣排除。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Specify edge exclusion. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「缺陷邊緣排除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for specify edge exclusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺陷邊緣排除」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for specify edge exclusion: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-18-k1","title":"缺陷邊緣排除的原理","titleEn":"Specify edge exclusion principle","text":"邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。","textEn":"Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area."},{"id":"a006-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺陷邊緣排除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating specify edge exclusion?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage04","order":4,"title":"元件相容性","titleEn":"Device compatibility","description":"在「元件相容性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for device compatibility, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-18"],"title":"自熱效應","titleEn":"Analyze self-heating","objective":"完成「自熱效應」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for analyze self-heating, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自熱效應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze self-heating. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「自熱效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze self-heating and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自熱效應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for analyze self-heating: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-19-k1","title":"自熱效應的原理","titleEn":"Analyze self-heating principle","text":"埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。","textEn":"Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating."},{"id":"a006-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自熱效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze self-heating?","options":["埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-19"],"title":"背閘耦合","titleEn":"Trace back-gate coupling","objective":"完成「背閘耦合」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace back-gate coupling, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背閘耦合。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace back-gate coupling. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「背閘耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace back-gate coupling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背閘耦合」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace back-gate coupling: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-20-k1","title":"背閘耦合的原理","titleEn":"Trace back-gate coupling principle","text":"支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。","textEn":"Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel."},{"id":"a006-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背閘耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace back-gate coupling?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-20"],"title":"RF 基板差異","titleEn":"Compare RF substrate needs","objective":"完成「RF 基板差異」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare rf substrate needs, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：RF 基板差異。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare RF substrate needs. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「RF 基板差異」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare rf substrate needs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「RF 基板差異」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare rf substrate needs: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-21-k1","title":"RF 基板差異的原理","titleEn":"Compare RF substrate needs principle","text":"高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。","textEn":"High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements."},{"id":"a006-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「RF 基板差異」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare rf substrate needs?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-21"],"title":"應力翹曲","titleEn":"Assess stress-induced bow","objective":"完成「應力翹曲」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess stress-induced bow, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力翹曲。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess stress-induced bow. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「應力翹曲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess stress-induced bow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力翹曲」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess stress-induced bow: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-22-k1","title":"應力翹曲的原理","titleEn":"Assess stress-induced bow principle","text":"多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。","textEn":"Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice."},{"id":"a006-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力翹曲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess stress-induced bow?","options":["多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-22"],"title":"分層追溯","titleEn":"Trace layer provenance","objective":"完成「分層追溯」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace layer provenance, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分層追溯。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace layer provenance. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「分層追溯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace layer provenance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分層追溯」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace layer provenance: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-23-k1","title":"分層追溯的原理","titleEn":"Trace layer provenance principle","text":"頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。","textEn":"Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable."},{"id":"a006-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分層追溯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace layer provenance?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-23"],"title":"SOI 放行矩陣","titleEn":"Release the SOI stack","objective":"完成「SOI 放行矩陣」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the soi stack, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SOI 放行矩陣。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the SOI stack. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「SOI 放行矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the soi stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SOI 放行矩陣」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the soi stack: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-24-k1","title":"SOI 放行矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Release the SOI stack principle","text":"隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。","textEn":"Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review."},{"id":"a006-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SOI 放行矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the soi stack?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}}]}],"subcategory":"substrate","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓與基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafers and substrates"},{"id":"a007","title":"晶圓表面清洗","titleEn":"Wafer surface cleaning","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解去污效果、材料損失、再污染，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore removal, material loss and recontamination through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["污染與表面目標","清洗路徑","沖洗乾燥","潔淨證據"],"labelsEn":["Contaminants and surface targets","Cleaning pathways","Rinsing and drying","Cleanliness evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a007-stage01","order":1,"title":"污染與表面目標","titleEn":"Contaminants and surface targets","description":"在「污染與表面目標」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contaminants and surface targets, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"污染分類","titleEn":"Classify contaminants","objective":"完成「污染分類」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for classify contaminants, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染分類。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify contaminants. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「污染分類」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify contaminants and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染分類」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for classify contaminants: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-01-k1","title":"污染分類的原理","titleEn":"Classify contaminants principle","text":"粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。","textEn":"Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence."},{"id":"a007-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染分類」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify contaminants?","options":["粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-01"],"title":"基底相容表","titleEn":"Build substrate compatibility tables","objective":"完成「基底相容表」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for build substrate compatibility tables, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基底相容表。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build substrate compatibility tables. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「基底相容表」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build substrate compatibility tables and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基底相容表」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for build substrate compatibility tables: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-02-k1","title":"基底相容表的原理","titleEn":"Build substrate compatibility tables principle","text":"能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。","textEn":"A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films."},{"id":"a007-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基底相容表」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build substrate compatibility tables?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-02"],"title":"先後順序圖","titleEn":"Map cleaning order","objective":"完成「先後順序圖」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map cleaning order, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：先後順序圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map cleaning order. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「先後順序圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map cleaning order and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「先後順序圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map cleaning order: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-03-k1","title":"先後順序圖的原理","titleEn":"Map cleaning order principle","text":"前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。","textEn":"Each surface state affects the next cleaning step."},{"id":"a007-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「先後順序圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map cleaning order?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Each surface state affects the next cleaning step."],"answer":2,"explanation":"前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-03"],"title":"空白見證片","titleEn":"Choose blank witnesses","objective":"完成「空白見證片」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for choose blank witnesses, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：空白見證片。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose blank witnesses. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Containers and handling contribute background contamination. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Containers and handling contribute background contamination. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「空白見證片」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose blank witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「空白見證片」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for choose blank witnesses: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-04-k1","title":"空白見證片的原理","titleEn":"Choose blank witnesses principle","text":"容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。","textEn":"Containers and handling contribute background contamination."},{"id":"a007-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「空白見證片」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose blank witnesses?","options":["容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Containers and handling contribute background contamination.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Containers and handling contribute background contamination. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-04"],"title":"潔淨程度指標","titleEn":"Select cleanliness metrics","objective":"完成「潔淨程度指標」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for select cleanliness metrics, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：潔淨程度指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Select cleanliness metrics. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「潔淨程度指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for select cleanliness metrics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「潔淨程度指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for select cleanliness metrics: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-05-k1","title":"潔淨程度指標的原理","titleEn":"Select cleanliness metrics principle","text":"粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。","textEn":"Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration."},{"id":"a007-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「潔淨程度指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating select cleanliness metrics?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-05"],"title":"接觸角限制","titleEn":"Bound contact-angle interpretation","objective":"完成「接觸角限制」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for bound contact-angle interpretation, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸角限制。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Bound contact-angle interpretation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「接觸角限制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for bound contact-angle interpretation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸角限制」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for bound contact-angle interpretation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-06-k1","title":"接觸角限制的原理","titleEn":"Bound contact-angle interpretation principle","text":"接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。","textEn":"Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence."},{"id":"a007-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸角限制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating bound contact-angle interpretation?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage02","order":2,"title":"清洗路徑","titleEn":"Cleaning pathways","description":"在「清洗路徑」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cleaning pathways, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-06"],"title":"化學選擇性","titleEn":"Assess chemical selectivity","objective":"完成「化學選擇性」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess chemical selectivity, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：化學選擇性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess chemical selectivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「化學選擇性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess chemical selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「化學選擇性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess chemical selectivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-07-k1","title":"化學選擇性的原理","titleEn":"Assess chemical selectivity principle","text":"選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。","textEn":"Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「化學選擇性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess chemical selectivity?","options":["選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-07"],"title":"粒子附著力","titleEn":"Draw particle adhesion forces","objective":"完成「粒子附著力」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw particle adhesion forces, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子附著力。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw particle adhesion forces. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「粒子附著力」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw particle adhesion forces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子附著力」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw particle adhesion forces: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-08-k1","title":"粒子附著力的原理","titleEn":"Draw particle adhesion forces principle","text":"粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。","textEn":"Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty."},{"id":"a007-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子附著力」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw particle adhesion forces?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-08"],"title":"邊界層更新","titleEn":"Analyze boundary-layer renewal","objective":"完成「邊界層更新」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for analyze boundary-layer renewal, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊界層更新。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze boundary-layer renewal. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「邊界層更新」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze boundary-layer renewal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊界層更新」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for analyze boundary-layer renewal: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-09-k1","title":"邊界層更新的原理","titleEn":"Analyze boundary-layer renewal principle","text":"流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。","textEn":"Flow affects reactant supply and product removal."},{"id":"a007-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊界層更新」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze boundary-layer renewal?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Flow affects reactant supply and product removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-09"],"title":"超音波副作用","titleEn":"Assess acoustic side effects","objective":"完成「超音波副作用」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess acoustic side effects, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：超音波副作用。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess acoustic side effects. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「超音波副作用」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess acoustic side effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「超音波副作用」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess acoustic side effects: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-10-k1","title":"超音波副作用的原理","titleEn":"Assess acoustic side effects principle","text":"提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。","textEn":"Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures."},{"id":"a007-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「超音波副作用」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess acoustic side effects?","options":["提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-10"],"title":"槽液老化","titleEn":"Track bath aging","objective":"完成「槽液老化」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track bath aging, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：槽液老化。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bath aging. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「槽液老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bath aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「槽液老化」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track bath aging: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-11-k1","title":"槽液老化的原理","titleEn":"Track bath aging principle","text":"溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。","textEn":"Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry."},{"id":"a007-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「槽液老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bath aging?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-11"],"title":"單片與批次","titleEn":"Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning","objective":"完成「單片與批次」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：單片與批次。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「單片與批次」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「單片與批次」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-12-k1","title":"單片與批次的原理","titleEn":"Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning principle","text":"批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。","textEn":"Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis."},{"id":"a007-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「單片與批次」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare single-wafer and batch cleaning?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage03","order":3,"title":"沖洗乾燥","titleEn":"Rinsing and drying","description":"在「沖洗乾燥」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for rinsing and drying, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-12"],"title":"沖洗置換模型","titleEn":"Model rinse displacement","objective":"完成「沖洗置換模型」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for model rinse displacement, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沖洗置換模型。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model rinse displacement. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「沖洗置換模型」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model rinse displacement and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沖洗置換模型」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for model rinse displacement: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-13-k1","title":"沖洗置換模型的原理","titleEn":"Model rinse displacement principle","text":"僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。","textEn":"Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions."},{"id":"a007-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沖洗置換模型」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model rinse displacement?","options":["僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-13"],"title":"水質進入點","titleEn":"Check incoming rinse quality","objective":"完成「水質進入點」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for check incoming rinse quality, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：水質進入點。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check incoming rinse quality. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「水質進入點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check incoming rinse quality and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「水質進入點」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for check incoming rinse quality: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-14-k1","title":"水質進入點的原理","titleEn":"Check incoming rinse quality principle","text":"清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。","textEn":"Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality."},{"id":"a007-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「水質進入點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check incoming rinse quality?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-14"],"title":"殘液乾燥痕","titleEn":"Interpret drying marks","objective":"完成「殘液乾燥痕」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret drying marks, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：殘液乾燥痕。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret drying marks. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「殘液乾燥痕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret drying marks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「殘液乾燥痕」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret drying marks: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-15-k1","title":"殘液乾燥痕的原理","titleEn":"Interpret drying marks principle","text":"水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。","textEn":"Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects."},{"id":"a007-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「殘液乾燥痕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret drying marks?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-15"],"title":"毛細倒塌","titleEn":"Assess capillary collapse","objective":"完成「毛細倒塌」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess capillary collapse, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：毛細倒塌。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess capillary collapse. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「毛細倒塌」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess capillary collapse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「毛細倒塌」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess capillary collapse: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-16-k1","title":"毛細倒塌的原理","titleEn":"Assess capillary collapse principle","text":"液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。","textEn":"Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features."},{"id":"a007-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「毛細倒塌」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess capillary collapse?","options":["液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-16"],"title":"等待時間控制","titleEn":"Control queue-time evidence","objective":"完成「等待時間控制」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for control queue-time evidence, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：等待時間控制。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Control queue-time evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「等待時間控制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for control queue-time evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「等待時間控制」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for control queue-time evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-17-k1","title":"等待時間控制的原理","titleEn":"Control queue-time evidence principle","text":"乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。","textEn":"Post-dry exposure changes readsorption."},{"id":"a007-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「等待時間控制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating control queue-time evidence?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Post-dry exposure changes readsorption.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-17"],"title":"搬運接觸點","titleEn":"Trace handling contact points","objective":"完成「搬運接觸點」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace handling contact points, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運接觸點。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace handling contact points. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「搬運接觸點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace handling contact points and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運接觸點」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace handling contact points: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-18-k1","title":"搬運接觸點的原理","titleEn":"Trace handling contact points principle","text":"背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。","textEn":"Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment."},{"id":"a007-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運接觸點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace handling contact points?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage04","order":4,"title":"潔淨證據","titleEn":"Cleanliness evidence","description":"在「潔淨證據」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cleanliness evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-18"],"title":"前後粒子差","titleEn":"Calculate particle adders","objective":"完成「前後粒子差」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for calculate particle adders, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前後粒子差。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂缺陷圖：同一掃描區清洗前 40 顆、後 18 顆，其中 10 顆位置重合。分開計算留存、移除與新生顆粒；說明為何只相減會漏掉新增污染。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calculate particle adders. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical matched defect maps: 40 particles before, 18 after, with 10 co-located. Separate retained, removed and added particles and explain why simple subtraction hides new contamination.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「前後粒子差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calculate particle adders and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前後粒子差」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for calculate particle adders: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-19-k1","title":"前後粒子差的原理","titleEn":"Calculate particle adders principle","text":"比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。","textEn":"Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds."},{"id":"a007-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前後粒子差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calculate particle adders?","options":["比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-19"],"title":"金屬分析空白","titleEn":"Audit metal-analysis blanks","objective":"完成「金屬分析空白」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for audit metal-analysis blanks, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬分析空白。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit metal-analysis blanks. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「金屬分析空白」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit metal-analysis blanks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬分析空白」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for audit metal-analysis blanks: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-20-k1","title":"金屬分析空白的原理","titleEn":"Audit metal-analysis blanks principle","text":"低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。","textEn":"Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits."},{"id":"a007-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬分析空白」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit metal-analysis blanks?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-20"],"title":"表面損失圖","titleEn":"Map substrate loss","objective":"完成「表面損失圖」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map substrate loss, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面損失圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map substrate loss. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「表面損失圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map substrate loss and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面損失圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map substrate loss: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-21-k1","title":"表面損失圖的原理","titleEn":"Map substrate loss principle","text":"去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。","textEn":"Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面損失圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map substrate loss?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-21"],"title":"缺陷空間關聯","titleEn":"Correlate defect locations","objective":"完成「缺陷空間關聯」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for correlate defect locations, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺陷空間關聯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Correlate defect locations. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「缺陷空間關聯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for correlate defect locations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺陷空間關聯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for correlate defect locations: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-22-k1","title":"缺陷空間關聯的原理","titleEn":"Correlate defect locations principle","text":"位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。","textEn":"Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone."},{"id":"a007-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺陷空間關聯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating correlate defect locations?","options":["位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-22"],"title":"重工邊界","titleEn":"Define rework limits","objective":"完成「重工邊界」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define rework limits, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重工邊界。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define rework limits. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「重工邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define rework limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重工邊界」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define rework limits: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-23-k1","title":"重工邊界的原理","titleEn":"Define rework limits principle","text":"反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。","textEn":"Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重工邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define rework limits?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-23"],"title":"潔淨交接單","titleEn":"Complete the cleanliness handoff","objective":"完成「潔淨交接單」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for complete the cleanliness handoff, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：潔淨交接單。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Complete the cleanliness handoff. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「潔淨交接單」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for complete the cleanliness handoff and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「潔淨交接單」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for complete the cleanliness handoff: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-24-k1","title":"潔淨交接單的原理","titleEn":"Complete the cleanliness handoff principle","text":"移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。","textEn":"Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff."},{"id":"a007-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「潔淨交接單」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating complete the cleanliness handoff?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a008","title":"超純水供應系統","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water supply systems","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解水質多指標、使用點、滯留，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["用水需求與污染","純化系統分工","循環與監測","異常及永續"],"labelsEn":["Water demand and contaminants","Purification functions","Distribution and monitoring","Excursions and sustainability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a008-stage01","order":1,"title":"用水需求與污染","titleEn":"Water demand and contaminants","description":"在「用水需求與污染」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for water demand and contaminants, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"界定使用點","titleEn":"Define points of use","objective":"完成「界定使用點」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define points of use, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界定使用點。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define points of use. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「界定使用點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define points of use and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界定使用點」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define points of use: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-01-k1","title":"界定使用點的原理","titleEn":"Define points of use principle","text":"沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。","textEn":"Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality."},{"id":"a008-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界定使用點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define points of use?","options":["沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-01"],"title":"峰值與平均流量","titleEn":"Separate peak and average flow","objective":"完成「峰值與平均流量」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate peak and average flow, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與平均流量。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate peak and average flow. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「峰值與平均流量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate peak and average flow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與平均流量」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate peak and average flow: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-02-k1","title":"峰值與平均流量的原理","titleEn":"Separate peak and average flow principle","text":"只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。","textEn":"Average demand misses coincident usage peaks."},{"id":"a008-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與平均流量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate peak and average flow?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Average demand misses coincident usage peaks.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-02"],"title":"污染質量帳","titleEn":"Build contaminant mass balances","objective":"完成「污染質量帳」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for build contaminant mass balances, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染質量帳。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build contaminant mass balances. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「污染質量帳」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build contaminant mass balances and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染質量帳」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for build contaminant mass balances: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-03-k1","title":"污染質量帳的原理","titleEn":"Build contaminant mass balances principle","text":"濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。","textEn":"Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux."},{"id":"a008-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染質量帳」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build contaminant mass balances?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux."],"answer":2,"explanation":"濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-03"],"title":"電阻率盲區","titleEn":"Identify resistivity blind spots","objective":"完成「電阻率盲區」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for identify resistivity blind spots, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電阻率盲區。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify resistivity blind spots. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「電阻率盲區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify resistivity blind spots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電阻率盲區」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for identify resistivity blind spots: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-04-k1","title":"電阻率盲區的原理","titleEn":"Identify resistivity blind spots principle","text":"高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。","textEn":"High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles."},{"id":"a008-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電阻率盲區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify resistivity blind spots?","options":["高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-04"],"title":"TOC 指標","titleEn":"Interpret total organic carbon","objective":"完成「TOC 指標」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for interpret total organic carbon, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：TOC 指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret total organic carbon. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「TOC 指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret total organic carbon and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「TOC 指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for interpret total organic carbon: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-05-k1","title":"TOC 指標的原理","titleEn":"Interpret total organic carbon principle","text":"TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。","textEn":"TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity."},{"id":"a008-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「TOC 指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret total organic carbon?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-05"],"title":"回用水分流","titleEn":"Segregate recovery streams","objective":"完成「回用水分流」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for segregate recovery streams, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：回用水分流。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Segregate recovery streams. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「回用水分流」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for segregate recovery streams and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「回用水分流」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for segregate recovery streams: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-06-k1","title":"回用水分流的原理","titleEn":"Segregate recovery streams principle","text":"回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。","textEn":"Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load."},{"id":"a008-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「回用水分流」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating segregate recovery streams?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage02","order":2,"title":"純化系統分工","titleEn":"Purification functions","description":"在「純化系統分工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for purification functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-06"],"title":"前處理功能","titleEn":"Assign pretreatment functions","objective":"完成「前處理功能」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assign pretreatment functions, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前處理功能。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign pretreatment functions. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「前處理功能」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign pretreatment functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前處理功能」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assign pretreatment functions: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-07-k1","title":"前處理功能的原理","titleEn":"Assign pretreatment functions principle","text":"前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。","textEn":"Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing."},{"id":"a008-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前處理功能」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign pretreatment functions?","options":["前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-07"],"title":"逆滲透物料平衡","titleEn":"Balance reverse-osmosis streams","objective":"完成「逆滲透物料平衡」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for balance reverse-osmosis streams, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：逆滲透物料平衡。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂守恆題：進水 100 L/min、產水 75 L/min、濃水 25 L/min；在無其他支流假設下檢查流量守恆及回收率，另列污染濃度資料才能求質量流率。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Balance reverse-osmosis streams. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical balance: feed 100 L/min, permeate 75 L/min and concentrate 25 L/min. Check flow conservation and recovery assuming no other streams; list concentration data needed for contaminant mass balance.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「逆滲透物料平衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for balance reverse-osmosis streams and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「逆滲透物料平衡」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for balance reverse-osmosis streams: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-08-k1","title":"逆滲透物料平衡的原理","titleEn":"Balance reverse-osmosis streams principle","text":"產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。","textEn":"Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance."},{"id":"a008-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「逆滲透物料平衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating balance reverse-osmosis streams?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-08"],"title":"離子交換突破","titleEn":"Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough","objective":"完成「離子交換突破」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離子交換突破。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「離子交換突破」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離子交換突破」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-09-k1","title":"離子交換突破的原理","titleEn":"Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough principle","text":"樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。","textEn":"Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion."},{"id":"a008-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離子交換突破」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret ion-exchange breakthrough?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-09"],"title":"有機物分解","titleEn":"Assess organic-removal stages","objective":"完成「有機物分解」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess organic-removal stages, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：有機物分解。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess organic-removal stages. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「有機物分解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess organic-removal stages and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「有機物分解」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess organic-removal stages: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-10-k1","title":"有機物分解的原理","titleEn":"Assess organic-removal stages principle","text":"分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。","textEn":"Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal."},{"id":"a008-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「有機物分解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess organic-removal stages?","options":["分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-10"],"title":"脫氣模組","titleEn":"Evaluate degassing","objective":"完成「脫氣模組」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for evaluate degassing, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：脫氣模組。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate degassing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「脫氣模組」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate degassing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「脫氣模組」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for evaluate degassing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-11-k1","title":"脫氣模組的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate degassing principle","text":"溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。","textEn":"Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms."},{"id":"a008-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「脫氣模組」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate degassing?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-11"],"title":"終端過濾","titleEn":"Review final filtration","objective":"完成「終端過濾」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review final filtration, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：終端過濾。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review final filtration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「終端過濾」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review final filtration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「終端過濾」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review final filtration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-12-k1","title":"終端過濾的原理","titleEn":"Review final filtration principle","text":"標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。","textEn":"Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency."},{"id":"a008-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「終端過濾」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review final filtration?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage03","order":3,"title":"循環與監測","titleEn":"Distribution and monitoring","description":"在「循環與監測」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for distribution and monitoring, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-12"],"title":"循環管網","titleEn":"Trace the recirculation loop","objective":"完成「循環管網」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace the recirculation loop, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：循環管網。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the recirculation loop. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「循環管網」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the recirculation loop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「循環管網」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace the recirculation loop: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-13-k1","title":"循環管網的原理","titleEn":"Trace the recirculation loop principle","text":"持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。","textEn":"Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness."},{"id":"a008-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「循環管網」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the recirculation loop?","options":["持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-13"],"title":"死角支管","titleEn":"Find dead legs","objective":"完成「死角支管」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for find dead legs, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：死角支管。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Find dead legs. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「死角支管」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for find dead legs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「死角支管」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for find dead legs: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-14-k1","title":"死角支管的原理","titleEn":"Find dead legs principle","text":"低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。","textEn":"Stagnant branches can become contamination sources."},{"id":"a008-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「死角支管」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating find dead legs?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stagnant branches can become contamination sources.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-14"],"title":"壓差與濾芯","titleEn":"Interpret filter pressure drop","objective":"完成「壓差與濾芯」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret filter pressure drop, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：壓差與濾芯。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret filter pressure drop. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「壓差與濾芯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret filter pressure drop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「壓差與濾芯」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret filter pressure drop: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-15-k1","title":"壓差與濾芯的原理","titleEn":"Interpret filter pressure drop principle","text":"壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。","textEn":"Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass."},{"id":"a008-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「壓差與濾芯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret filter pressure drop?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-15"],"title":"使用點採樣","titleEn":"Design point-of-use sampling","objective":"完成「使用點採樣」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for design point-of-use sampling, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：使用點採樣。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design point-of-use sampling. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「使用點採樣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design point-of-use sampling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「使用點採樣」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for design point-of-use sampling: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-16-k1","title":"使用點採樣的原理","titleEn":"Design point-of-use sampling principle","text":"中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。","textEn":"Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements."},{"id":"a008-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「使用點採樣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design point-of-use sampling?","options":["中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-16"],"title":"感測器延遲","titleEn":"Account for sensor delay","objective":"完成「感測器延遲」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for account for sensor delay, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：感測器延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Account for sensor delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「感測器延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for account for sensor delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「感測器延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for account for sensor delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-17-k1","title":"感測器延遲的原理","titleEn":"Account for sensor delay principle","text":"採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。","textEn":"Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm."},{"id":"a008-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「感測器延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating account for sensor delay?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-17"],"title":"溫度補償","titleEn":"Review temperature compensation","objective":"完成「溫度補償」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review temperature compensation, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度補償。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review temperature compensation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「溫度補償」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review temperature compensation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度補償」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review temperature compensation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-18-k1","title":"溫度補償的原理","titleEn":"Review temperature compensation principle","text":"電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。","textEn":"Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata."},{"id":"a008-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度補償」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review temperature compensation?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage04","order":4,"title":"異常及永續","titleEn":"Excursions and sustainability","description":"在「異常及永續」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for excursions and sustainability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-18"],"title":"異常隔離區","titleEn":"Define excursion boundaries","objective":"完成「異常隔離區」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define excursion boundaries, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：異常隔離區。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define excursion boundaries. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「異常隔離區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define excursion boundaries and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「異常隔離區」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define excursion boundaries: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-19-k1","title":"異常隔離區的原理","titleEn":"Define excursion boundaries principle","text":"受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。","textEn":"Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window."},{"id":"a008-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「異常隔離區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define excursion boundaries?","options":["受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-19"],"title":"維護沖洗證據","titleEn":"Verify maintenance flushing","objective":"完成「維護沖洗證據」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for verify maintenance flushing, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：維護沖洗證據。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Verify maintenance flushing. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「維護沖洗證據」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for verify maintenance flushing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「維護沖洗證據」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for verify maintenance flushing: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-20-k1","title":"維護沖洗證據的原理","titleEn":"Verify maintenance flushing principle","text":"更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。","textEn":"After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline."},{"id":"a008-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「維護沖洗證據」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating verify maintenance flushing?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-20"],"title":"多指標交叉驗證","titleEn":"Cross-check quality indicators","objective":"完成「多指標交叉驗證」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for cross-check quality indicators, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：多指標交叉驗證。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check quality indicators. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「多指標交叉驗證」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check quality indicators and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「多指標交叉驗證」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for cross-check quality indicators: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-21-k1","title":"多指標交叉驗證的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check quality indicators principle","text":"單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。","textEn":"A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor."},{"id":"a008-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「多指標交叉驗證」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check quality indicators?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-21"],"title":"回收率權衡","titleEn":"Assess recovery tradeoffs","objective":"完成「回收率權衡」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess recovery tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：回收率權衡。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess recovery tradeoffs. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「回收率權衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess recovery tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「回收率權衡」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess recovery tradeoffs: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-22-k1","title":"回收率權衡的原理","titleEn":"Assess recovery tradeoffs principle","text":"提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。","textEn":"Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden."},{"id":"a008-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「回收率權衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess recovery tradeoffs?","options":["提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-22"],"title":"停機重啟","titleEn":"Plan restart qualification","objective":"完成「停機重啟」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for plan restart qualification, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：停機重啟。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan restart qualification. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「停機重啟」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan restart qualification and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「停機重啟」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for plan restart qualification: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-23-k1","title":"停機重啟的原理","titleEn":"Plan restart qualification principle","text":"停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。","textEn":"Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence."},{"id":"a008-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「停機重啟」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan restart qualification?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-23"],"title":"水務放行報告","titleEn":"Assemble water-system acceptance","objective":"完成「水務放行報告」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assemble water-system acceptance, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：水務放行報告。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assemble water-system acceptance. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「水務放行報告」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assemble water-system acceptance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「水務放行報告」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assemble water-system acceptance: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-24-k1","title":"水務放行報告的原理","titleEn":"Assemble water-system acceptance principle","text":"品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。","textEn":"Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability."},{"id":"a008-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「水務放行報告」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assemble water-system acceptance?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a009","title":"晶圓廠微污染控制","titleEn":"Microcontamination control in fabs","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore sources, transport and defect maps through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["污染源與路徑","空氣與微環境","液體接觸鏈","缺陷歸因"],"labelsEn":["Sources and pathways","Air and microenvironments","Liquid-contact chains","Defect attribution"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a009-stage01","order":1,"title":"污染源與路徑","titleEn":"Sources and pathways","description":"在「污染源與路徑」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for sources and pathways, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"建立污染源地圖","titleEn":"Map contamination sources","objective":"完成「建立污染源地圖」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map contamination sources, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：建立污染源地圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map contamination sources. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「建立污染源地圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map contamination sources and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「建立污染源地圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map contamination sources: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-01-k1","title":"建立污染源地圖的原理","titleEn":"Map contamination sources principle","text":"人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。","textEn":"People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources."},{"id":"a009-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「建立污染源地圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map contamination sources?","options":["人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-01"],"title":"尺寸與危害","titleEn":"Separate size and hazard","objective":"完成「尺寸與危害」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate size and hazard, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：尺寸與危害。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate size and hazard. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「尺寸與危害」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate size and hazard and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「尺寸與危害」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate size and hazard: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-02-k1","title":"尺寸與危害的原理","titleEn":"Separate size and hazard principle","text":"相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。","textEn":"Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects."},{"id":"a009-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「尺寸與危害」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate size and hazard?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-02"],"title":"粒子與分子","titleEn":"Distinguish particles and molecules","objective":"完成「粒子與分子」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles and molecules, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子與分子。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish particles and molecules. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「粒子與分子」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish particles and molecules and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子與分子」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles and molecules: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-03-k1","title":"粒子與分子的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish particles and molecules principle","text":"粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。","textEn":"Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control."},{"id":"a009-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子與分子」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish particles and molecules?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-03"],"title":"暴露劑量","titleEn":"Estimate contamination exposure","objective":"完成「暴露劑量」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for estimate contamination exposure, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：暴露劑量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂暴露模型：先假設沉積通量與濃度成正比。案例甲濃度 2、時間 3，案例乙濃度 1、時間 8；比較相對暴露，再列使此線性模型失效的吸附飽和情況。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate contamination exposure. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical exposure model: deposition flux is proportional to concentration. Compare relative exposures for concentration/time pairs (2,3) and (1,8), then state how adsorption saturation could invalidate linearity.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「暴露劑量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate contamination exposure and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「暴露劑量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for estimate contamination exposure: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-04-k1","title":"暴露劑量的原理","titleEn":"Estimate contamination exposure principle","text":"表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。","textEn":"Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration."},{"id":"a009-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「暴露劑量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate contamination exposure?","options":["表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-04"],"title":"沉積與再懸浮","titleEn":"Trace deposition and resuspension","objective":"完成「沉積與再懸浮」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace deposition and resuspension, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沉積與再懸浮。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace deposition and resuspension. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「沉積與再懸浮」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace deposition and resuspension and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沉積與再懸浮」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace deposition and resuspension: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-05-k1","title":"沉積與再懸浮的原理","titleEn":"Trace deposition and resuspension principle","text":"清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。","textEn":"Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles."},{"id":"a009-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沉積與再懸浮」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace deposition and resuspension?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-05"],"title":"監控片安排","titleEn":"Choose monitoring wafers","objective":"完成「監控片安排」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for choose monitoring wafers, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：監控片安排。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose monitoring wafers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「監控片安排」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose monitoring wafers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「監控片安排」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for choose monitoring wafers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-06-k1","title":"監控片安排的原理","titleEn":"Choose monitoring wafers principle","text":"監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。","textEn":"Monitor wafers need representative handling histories."},{"id":"a009-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「監控片安排」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose monitoring wafers?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Monitor wafers need representative handling histories."],"answer":2,"explanation":"監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage02","order":2,"title":"空氣與微環境","titleEn":"Air and microenvironments","description":"在「空氣與微環境」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for air and microenvironments, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-06"],"title":"氣流方向","titleEn":"Map airflow direction","objective":"完成「氣流方向」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map airflow direction, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣流方向。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map airflow direction. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「氣流方向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map airflow direction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣流方向」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map airflow direction: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-07-k1","title":"氣流方向的原理","titleEn":"Map airflow direction principle","text":"平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。","textEn":"Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation."},{"id":"a009-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣流方向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map airflow direction?","options":["平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-07"],"title":"濾材功能","titleEn":"Compare filter functions","objective":"完成「濾材功能」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare filter functions, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濾材功能。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare filter functions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「濾材功能」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare filter functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濾材功能」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare filter functions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-08-k1","title":"濾材功能的原理","titleEn":"Compare filter functions principle","text":"粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。","textEn":"Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria."},{"id":"a009-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濾材功能」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare filter functions?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-08"],"title":"壓差邊界","titleEn":"Set pressure-boundary evidence","objective":"完成「壓差邊界」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for set pressure-boundary evidence, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：壓差邊界。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set pressure-boundary evidence. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「壓差邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set pressure-boundary evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「壓差邊界」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for set pressure-boundary evidence: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-09-k1","title":"壓差邊界的原理","titleEn":"Set pressure-boundary evidence principle","text":"壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。","textEn":"Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport."},{"id":"a009-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「壓差邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set pressure-boundary evidence?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-09"],"title":"微環境開口","titleEn":"Assess minienvironment openings","objective":"完成「微環境開口」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess minienvironment openings, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：微環境開口。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess minienvironment openings. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「微環境開口」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess minienvironment openings and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「微環境開口」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess minienvironment openings: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-10-k1","title":"微環境開口的原理","titleEn":"Assess minienvironment openings principle","text":"開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。","textEn":"Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure."},{"id":"a009-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「微環境開口」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess minienvironment openings?","options":["開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-10"],"title":"FOUP 釋氣","titleEn":"Assess FOUP outgassing","objective":"完成「FOUP 釋氣」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess foup outgassing, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：FOUP 釋氣。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess FOUP outgassing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「FOUP 釋氣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess foup outgassing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「FOUP 釋氣」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess foup outgassing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-11-k1","title":"FOUP 釋氣的原理","titleEn":"Assess FOUP outgassing principle","text":"載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。","textEn":"Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants."},{"id":"a009-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「FOUP 釋氣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess foup outgassing?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-11"],"title":"濕度耦合","titleEn":"Study humidity coupling","objective":"完成「濕度耦合」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for study humidity coupling, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濕度耦合。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Study humidity coupling. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「濕度耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for study humidity coupling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濕度耦合」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for study humidity coupling: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-12-k1","title":"濕度耦合的原理","titleEn":"Study humidity coupling principle","text":"吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。","textEn":"Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity."},{"id":"a009-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濕度耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating study humidity coupling?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage03","order":3,"title":"液體接觸鏈","titleEn":"Liquid-contact chains","description":"在「液體接觸鏈」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for liquid-contact chains, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-12"],"title":"容器浸出物","titleEn":"Audit container extractables","objective":"完成「容器浸出物」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for audit container extractables, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：容器浸出物。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit container extractables. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「容器浸出物」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit container extractables and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「容器浸出物」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for audit container extractables: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-13-k1","title":"容器浸出物的原理","titleEn":"Audit container extractables principle","text":"化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。","textEn":"Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration."},{"id":"a009-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「容器浸出物」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit container extractables?","options":["化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-13"],"title":"管線顆粒脫落","titleEn":"Trace tubing particle shedding","objective":"完成「管線顆粒脫落」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace tubing particle shedding, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：管線顆粒脫落。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace tubing particle shedding. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「管線顆粒脫落」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace tubing particle shedding and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「管線顆粒脫落」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace tubing particle shedding: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-14-k1","title":"管線顆粒脫落的原理","titleEn":"Trace tubing particle shedding principle","text":"機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。","textEn":"Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding."},{"id":"a009-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「管線顆粒脫落」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace tubing particle shedding?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-14"],"title":"閥件死腔","titleEn":"Locate valve dead volumes","objective":"完成「閥件死腔」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for locate valve dead volumes, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閥件死腔。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate valve dead volumes. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「閥件死腔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate valve dead volumes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閥件死腔」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for locate valve dead volumes: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-15-k1","title":"閥件死腔的原理","titleEn":"Locate valve dead volumes principle","text":"局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。","textEn":"Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels."},{"id":"a009-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閥件死腔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate valve dead volumes?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-15"],"title":"濾芯旁通","titleEn":"Check filtration bypass","objective":"完成「濾芯旁通」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for check filtration bypass, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濾芯旁通。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check filtration bypass. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「濾芯旁通」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check filtration bypass and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濾芯旁通」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for check filtration bypass: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-16-k1","title":"濾芯旁通的原理","titleEn":"Check filtration bypass principle","text":"濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。","textEn":"A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass."},{"id":"a009-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濾芯旁通」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check filtration bypass?","options":["濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-16"],"title":"靜電與吸附","titleEn":"Link electrostatics and attraction","objective":"完成「靜電與吸附」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for link electrostatics and attraction, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：靜電與吸附。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Link electrostatics and attraction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「靜電與吸附」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for link electrostatics and attraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「靜電與吸附」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for link electrostatics and attraction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-17-k1","title":"靜電與吸附的原理","titleEn":"Link electrostatics and attraction principle","text":"帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。","textEn":"Charged surfaces can increase particle capture."},{"id":"a009-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「靜電與吸附」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating link electrostatics and attraction?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Charged surfaces can increase particle capture.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-17"],"title":"化學批次更換","titleEn":"Compare chemical-lot transitions","objective":"完成「化學批次更換」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare chemical-lot transitions, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：化學批次更換。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare chemical-lot transitions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「化學批次更換」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare chemical-lot transitions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「化學批次更換」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare chemical-lot transitions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-18-k1","title":"化學批次更換的原理","titleEn":"Compare chemical-lot transitions principle","text":"更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。","textEn":"Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages."},{"id":"a009-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「化學批次更換」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare chemical-lot transitions?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage04","order":4,"title":"缺陷歸因","titleEn":"Defect attribution","description":"在「缺陷歸因」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for defect attribution, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-18"],"title":"檢出限標示","titleEn":"Report detection limits","objective":"完成「檢出限標示」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for report detection limits, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：檢出限標示。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report detection limits. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「檢出限標示」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report detection limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「檢出限標示」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for report detection limits: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-19-k1","title":"檢出限標示的原理","titleEn":"Report detection limits principle","text":"未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。","textEn":"Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination."},{"id":"a009-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「檢出限標示」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report detection limits?","options":["未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-19"],"title":"空間缺陷圖","titleEn":"Register defect maps","objective":"完成「空間缺陷圖」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for register defect maps, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：空間缺陷圖。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Register defect maps. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「空間缺陷圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for register defect maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「空間缺陷圖」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for register defect maps: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-20-k1","title":"空間缺陷圖的原理","titleEn":"Register defect maps principle","text":"缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。","textEn":"Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration."},{"id":"a009-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「空間缺陷圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating register defect maps?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-20"],"title":"時間序列比對","titleEn":"Align event timelines","objective":"完成「時間序列比對」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for align event timelines, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：時間序列比對。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Align event timelines. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「時間序列比對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for align event timelines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「時間序列比對」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for align event timelines: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-21-k1","title":"時間序列比對的原理","titleEn":"Align event timelines principle","text":"維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。","textEn":"Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock."},{"id":"a009-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「時間序列比對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating align event timelines?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock."],"answer":2,"explanation":"維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-21"],"title":"單因素隔離","titleEn":"Isolate a contamination hypothesis","objective":"完成「單因素隔離」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for isolate a contamination hypothesis, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：單因素隔離。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Isolate a contamination hypothesis. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「單因素隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for isolate a contamination hypothesis and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「單因素隔離」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for isolate a contamination hypothesis: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-22-k1","title":"單因素隔離的原理","titleEn":"Isolate a contamination hypothesis principle","text":"同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。","textEn":"Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution."},{"id":"a009-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「單因素隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating isolate a contamination hypothesis?","options":["同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-22"],"title":"恢復與放行","titleEn":"Define recovery evidence","objective":"完成「恢復與放行」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define recovery evidence, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：恢復與放行。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define recovery evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「恢復與放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define recovery evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「恢復與放行」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define recovery evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-23-k1","title":"恢復與放行的原理","titleEn":"Define recovery evidence principle","text":"恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。","textEn":"Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms."},{"id":"a009-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「恢復與放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define recovery evidence?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-23"],"title":"污染控制報告","titleEn":"Compile the control dossier","objective":"完成「污染控制報告」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compile the control dossier, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染控制報告。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compile the control dossier. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「污染控制報告」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compile the control dossier and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染控制報告」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compile the control dossier: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-24-k1","title":"污染控制報告的原理","titleEn":"Compile the control dossier principle","text":"來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。","textEn":"Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately."},{"id":"a009-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染控制報告」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compile the control dossier?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a010","title":"晶圓廠自動搬運系統","titleEn":"Automated material handling in fabs","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["搬運圖與產能","任務與交握","壅塞及故障","驗收與資料"],"labelsEn":["Transport graph and capacity","Tasks and handshakes","Congestion and faults","Acceptance and data"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a010-stage01","order":1,"title":"搬運圖與產能","titleEn":"Transport graph and capacity","description":"在「搬運圖與產能」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for transport graph and capacity, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨識載具與批號","titleEn":"Identify carriers and lots","objective":"完成「辨識載具與批號」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify carriers and lots, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：辨識載具與批號。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify carriers and lots. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「辨識載具與批號」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify carriers and lots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「辨識載具與批號」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify carriers and lots: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-01-k1","title":"辨識載具與批號的原理","titleEn":"Identify carriers and lots principle","text":"載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。","textEn":"Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields."},{"id":"a010-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「辨識載具與批號」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify carriers and lots?","options":["載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。","平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields.","Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-01"],"title":"建立有向路網","titleEn":"Build the directed route graph","objective":"完成「建立有向路網」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for build the directed route graph, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：建立有向路網。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build the directed route graph. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「建立有向路網」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build the directed route graph and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「建立有向路網」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for build the directed route graph: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-02-k1","title":"建立有向路網的原理","titleEn":"Build the directed route graph principle","text":"單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。","textEn":"Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance."},{"id":"a010-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「建立有向路網」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build the directed route graph?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-02"],"title":"工具負載埠","titleEn":"Represent load ports","objective":"完成「工具負載埠」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for represent load ports, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：工具負載埠。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Represent load ports. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「工具負載埠」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for represent load ports and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「工具負載埠」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for represent load ports: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-03-k1","title":"工具負載埠的原理","titleEn":"Represent load ports principle","text":"設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。","textEn":"Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models."},{"id":"a010-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「工具負載埠」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating represent load ports?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。","設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved.","Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-03"],"title":"搬運需求矩陣","titleEn":"Build a transport-demand matrix","objective":"完成「搬運需求矩陣」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for build a transport-demand matrix, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運需求矩陣。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a transport-demand matrix. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「搬運需求矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a transport-demand matrix and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運需求矩陣」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for build a transport-demand matrix: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-04-k1","title":"搬運需求矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Build a transport-demand matrix principle","text":"製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。","textEn":"Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line."},{"id":"a010-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運需求矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a transport-demand matrix?","options":["製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。","平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line.","Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-04"],"title":"儲位與緩衝","titleEn":"Allocate storage buffers","objective":"完成「儲位與緩衝」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for allocate storage buffers, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：儲位與緩衝。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Allocate storage buffers. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「儲位與緩衝」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for allocate storage buffers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「儲位與緩衝」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for allocate storage buffers: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-05-k1","title":"儲位與緩衝的原理","titleEn":"Allocate storage buffers principle","text":"緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。","textEn":"Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting."},{"id":"a010-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「儲位與緩衝」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating allocate storage buffers?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-05"],"title":"搬運時間拆解","titleEn":"Decompose transport time","objective":"完成「搬運時間拆解」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for decompose transport time, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運時間拆解。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Decompose transport time. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「搬運時間拆解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for decompose transport time and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運時間拆解」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for decompose transport time: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-06-k1","title":"搬運時間拆解的原理","titleEn":"Decompose transport time principle","text":"等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。","textEn":"Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies."},{"id":"a010-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運時間拆解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating decompose transport time?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。","等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved.","Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage02","order":2,"title":"任務與交握","titleEn":"Tasks and handshakes","description":"在「任務與交握」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for tasks and handshakes, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-06"],"title":"任務狀態機","titleEn":"Draw the task state machine","objective":"完成「任務狀態機」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw the task state machine, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：任務狀態機。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw the task state machine. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「任務狀態機」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw the task state machine and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「任務狀態機」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw the task state machine: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-07-k1","title":"任務狀態機的原理","titleEn":"Draw the task state machine principle","text":"已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。","textEn":"Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states."},{"id":"a010-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「任務狀態機」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw the task state machine?","options":["已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。","任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states.","Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-07"],"title":"載入前交握","titleEn":"Validate the loading handshake","objective":"完成「載入前交握」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for validate the loading handshake, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：載入前交握。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Validate the loading handshake. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「載入前交握」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for validate the loading handshake and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「載入前交握」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for validate the loading handshake: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-08-k1","title":"載入前交握的原理","titleEn":"Validate the loading handshake principle","text":"設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。","textEn":"Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity."},{"id":"a010-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「載入前交握」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating validate the loading handshake?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-08"],"title":"路段保留","titleEn":"Reserve track segments","objective":"完成「路段保留」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for reserve track segments, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：路段保留。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reserve track segments. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「路段保留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reserve track segments and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「路段保留」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for reserve track segments: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-09-k1","title":"路段保留的原理","titleEn":"Reserve track segments principle","text":"避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。","textEn":"Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing."},{"id":"a010-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「路段保留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reserve track segments?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。","避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock.","Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-09"],"title":"優先權與飢餓","titleEn":"Balance priority and starvation","objective":"完成「優先權與飢餓」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for balance priority and starvation, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：優先權與飢餓。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Balance priority and starvation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「優先權與飢餓」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for balance priority and starvation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「優先權與飢餓」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for balance priority and starvation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-10-k1","title":"優先權與飢餓的原理","titleEn":"Balance priority and starvation principle","text":"高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。","textEn":"High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots."},{"id":"a010-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「優先權與飢餓」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating balance priority and starvation?","options":["高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。","任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots.","Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-10"],"title":"重試冪等性","titleEn":"Make retries idempotent","objective":"完成「重試冪等性」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for make retries idempotent, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重試冪等性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Make retries idempotent. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「重試冪等性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for make retries idempotent and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重試冪等性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for make retries idempotent: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-11-k1","title":"重試冪等性的原理","titleEn":"Make retries idempotent principle","text":"重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。","textEn":"Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks."},{"id":"a010-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重試冪等性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating make retries idempotent?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-11"],"title":"超時狀態","titleEn":"Handle timeout ambiguity","objective":"完成「超時狀態」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for handle timeout ambiguity, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：超時狀態。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Handle timeout ambiguity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「超時狀態」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for handle timeout ambiguity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「超時狀態」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for handle timeout ambiguity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-12-k1","title":"超時狀態的原理","titleEn":"Handle timeout ambiguity principle","text":"超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。","textEn":"Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action."},{"id":"a010-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「超時狀態」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating handle timeout ambiguity?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。","超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock.","Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage03","order":3,"title":"壅塞及故障","titleEn":"Congestion and faults","description":"在「壅塞及故障」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for congestion and faults, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-12"],"title":"瓶頸利用率","titleEn":"Measure bottleneck utilization","objective":"完成「瓶頸利用率」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for measure bottleneck utilization, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：瓶頸利用率。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure bottleneck utilization. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「瓶頸利用率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure bottleneck utilization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「瓶頸利用率」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for measure bottleneck utilization: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-13-k1","title":"瓶頸利用率的原理","titleEn":"Measure bottleneck utilization principle","text":"高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。","textEn":"High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment."},{"id":"a010-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「瓶頸利用率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure bottleneck utilization?","options":["高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。","已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment.","Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-13"],"title":"路口壅塞","titleEn":"Inspect junction queues","objective":"完成「路口壅塞」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect junction queues, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：路口壅塞。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect junction queues. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「路口壅塞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect junction queues and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「路口壅塞」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect junction queues: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-14-k1","title":"路口壅塞的原理","titleEn":"Inspect junction queues principle","text":"合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。","textEn":"Junction service limits propagate queues upstream."},{"id":"a010-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「路口壅塞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect junction queues?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Junction service limits propagate queues upstream.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-14"],"title":"故障車阻擋","titleEn":"Model a blocked vehicle","objective":"完成「故障車阻擋」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for model a blocked vehicle, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：故障車阻擋。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model a blocked vehicle. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「故障車阻擋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model a blocked vehicle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「故障車阻擋」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for model a blocked vehicle: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-15-k1","title":"故障車阻擋的原理","titleEn":"Model a blocked vehicle principle","text":"停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。","textEn":"A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability."},{"id":"a010-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「故障車阻擋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model a blocked vehicle?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。","停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks.","A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-15"],"title":"負載埠拒收","titleEn":"Recover from port rejection","objective":"完成「負載埠拒收」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for recover from port rejection, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：負載埠拒收。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Recover from port rejection. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「負載埠拒收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for recover from port rejection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「負載埠拒收」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for recover from port rejection: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-16-k1","title":"負載埠拒收的原理","titleEn":"Recover from port rejection principle","text":"目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。","textEn":"Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task."},{"id":"a010-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「負載埠拒收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating recover from port rejection?","options":["目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。","已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task.","Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-16"],"title":"掉線與恢復","titleEn":"Reconcile network recovery","objective":"完成「掉線與恢復」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for reconcile network recovery, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掉線與恢復。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reconcile network recovery. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「掉線與恢復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reconcile network recovery and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掉線與恢復」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for reconcile network recovery: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-17-k1","title":"掉線與恢復的原理","titleEn":"Reconcile network recovery principle","text":"恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。","textEn":"Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states."},{"id":"a010-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掉線與恢復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reconcile network recovery?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-17"],"title":"地震或急停","titleEn":"Model emergency-stop states","objective":"完成「地震或急停」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for model emergency-stop states, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：地震或急停。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model emergency-stop states. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「地震或急停」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model emergency-stop states and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「地震或急停」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for model emergency-stop states: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-18-k1","title":"地震或急停的原理","titleEn":"Model emergency-stop states principle","text":"安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。","textEn":"Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation."},{"id":"a010-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「地震或急停」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model emergency-stop states?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。","安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks.","Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗收與資料","titleEn":"Acceptance and data","description":"在「驗收與資料」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for acceptance and data, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-18"],"title":"搬運振動","titleEn":"Assess transport vibration","objective":"完成「搬運振動」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess transport vibration, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運振動。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess transport vibration. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「搬運振動」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess transport vibration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運振動」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess transport vibration: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-19-k1","title":"搬運振動的原理","titleEn":"Assess transport vibration principle","text":"峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。","textEn":"Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads."},{"id":"a010-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運振動」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess transport vibration?","options":["峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。","中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads.","An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-19"],"title":"粒子增量","titleEn":"Measure transport particle adders","objective":"完成「粒子增量」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure transport particle adders, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子增量。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure transport particle adders. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「粒子增量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure transport particle adders and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子增量」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure transport particle adders: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-20-k1","title":"粒子增量的原理","titleEn":"Measure transport particle adders principle","text":"潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。","textEn":"Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories."},{"id":"a010-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子增量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure transport particle adders?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-20"],"title":"尾端延遲","titleEn":"Report tail latency","objective":"完成「尾端延遲」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for report tail latency, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：尾端延遲。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂延遲資料：九次任務均 20 s，一次 200 s；計算平均與中位數，保留最大值，再設計會揭露尾端問題的報表欄位。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report tail latency. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical latency data: nine tasks take 20 s and one takes 200 s. Compute mean and median, retain the maximum, and design a report exposing tail delays.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「尾端延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report tail latency and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「尾端延遲」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for report tail latency: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-21-k1","title":"尾端延遲的原理","titleEn":"Report tail latency principle","text":"中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。","textEn":"Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays."},{"id":"a010-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「尾端延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report tail latency?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。","中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions.","Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-21"],"title":"事件追溯","titleEn":"Audit event traceability","objective":"完成「事件追溯」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for audit event traceability, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：事件追溯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit event traceability. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「事件追溯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit event traceability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「事件追溯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for audit event traceability: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-22-k1","title":"事件追溯的原理","titleEn":"Audit event traceability principle","text":"每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。","textEn":"Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity."},{"id":"a010-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「事件追溯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit event traceability?","options":["每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。","中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity.","An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-22"],"title":"離散事件模擬","titleEn":"Build a discrete-event experiment","objective":"完成「離散事件模擬」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for build a discrete-event experiment, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離散事件模擬。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a discrete-event experiment. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「離散事件模擬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a discrete-event experiment and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離散事件模擬」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for build a discrete-event experiment: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-23-k1","title":"離散事件模擬的原理","titleEn":"Build a discrete-event experiment principle","text":"相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。","textEn":"Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison."},{"id":"a010-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離散事件模擬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a discrete-event experiment?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-23"],"title":"搬運系統驗收","titleEn":"Accept the transport system","objective":"完成「搬運系統驗收」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the transport system, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運系統驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the transport system. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「搬運系統驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the transport system and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運系統驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the transport system: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-24-k1","title":"搬運系統驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the transport system principle","text":"產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。","textEn":"Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence."},{"id":"a010-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運系統驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the transport system?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。","產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions.","Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a011","title":"熱氧化閘極介電層","titleEn":"Thermally grown gate dielectrics","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["界面與氧化目的","成長動力學","厚度與電性","元件熱整合"],"labelsEn":["Interface and oxidation purpose","Growth kinetics","Thickness and electrical evidence","Device thermal integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a011-stage01","order":1,"title":"界面與氧化目的","titleEn":"Interface and oxidation purpose","description":"在「界面與氧化目的」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for interface and oxidation purpose, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分辨成長與沉積","titleEn":"Separate growth and deposition","objective":"完成「分辨成長與沉積」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate growth and deposition, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分辨成長與沉積。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate growth and deposition. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「分辨成長與沉積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate growth and deposition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分辨成長與沉積」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate growth and deposition: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-01-k1","title":"分辨成長與沉積的原理","titleEn":"Separate growth and deposition principle","text":"熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。","textEn":"Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source."},{"id":"a011-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分辨成長與沉積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate growth and deposition?","options":["熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-01"],"title":"界面位置移動","titleEn":"Track the moving interface","objective":"完成「界面位置移動」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for track the moving interface, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面位置移動。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂幾何模型：假設氧化物厚度 100 個單位、矽消耗為其 0.44 倍；以原表面為零畫出新界面與外表面。0.44 是近似體積換算，非本課量測值。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track the moving interface. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical geometry: oxide thickness 100 units and silicon consumption 0.44 times that thickness. Mark the new interface and outer surface relative to the original surface. The 0.44 is an approximate volume conversion, not course measurement data.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「界面位置移動」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track the moving interface and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面位置移動」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for track the moving interface: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-02-k1","title":"界面位置移動的原理","titleEn":"Track the moving interface principle","text":"氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。","textEn":"The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface."},{"id":"a011-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面位置移動」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track the moving interface?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-02"],"title":"閘氧與場氧","titleEn":"Separate gate and field oxide","objective":"完成「閘氧與場氧」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate gate and field oxide, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘氧與場氧。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate gate and field oxide. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘氧與場氧」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate gate and field oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘氧與場氧」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate gate and field oxide: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-03-k1","title":"閘氧與場氧的原理","titleEn":"Separate gate and field oxide principle","text":"電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。","textEn":"Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets."},{"id":"a011-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘氧與場氧」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate gate and field oxide?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-03"],"title":"乾氧與濕氧","titleEn":"Compare dry and wet oxidation","objective":"完成「乾氧與濕氧」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare dry and wet oxidation, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：乾氧與濕氧。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare dry and wet oxidation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「乾氧與濕氧」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare dry and wet oxidation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「乾氧與濕氧」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare dry and wet oxidation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-04-k1","title":"乾氧與濕氧的原理","titleEn":"Compare dry and wet oxidation principle","text":"氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。","textEn":"Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties."},{"id":"a011-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「乾氧與濕氧」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare dry and wet oxidation?","options":["氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-04"],"title":"原生氧化前史","titleEn":"Record initial oxide history","objective":"完成「原生氧化前史」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for record initial oxide history, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：原生氧化前史。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Record initial oxide history. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「原生氧化前史」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for record initial oxide history and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「原生氧化前史」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for record initial oxide history: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-05-k1","title":"原生氧化前史的原理","titleEn":"Record initial oxide history principle","text":"初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。","textEn":"Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth."},{"id":"a011-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「原生氧化前史」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating record initial oxide history?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-05"],"title":"清洗後等待","titleEn":"Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay","objective":"完成「清洗後等待」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：清洗後等待。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「清洗後等待」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「清洗後等待」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-06-k1","title":"清洗後等待的原理","titleEn":"Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay principle","text":"吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。","textEn":"Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface."},{"id":"a011-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「清洗後等待」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess the clean-to-oxidation delay?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage02","order":2,"title":"成長動力學","titleEn":"Growth kinetics","description":"在「成長動力學」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for growth kinetics, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-06"],"title":"線性成長區","titleEn":"Identify the linear regime","objective":"完成「線性成長區」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify the linear regime, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：線性成長區。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the linear regime. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「線性成長區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the linear regime and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「線性成長區」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify the linear regime: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-07-k1","title":"線性成長區的原理","titleEn":"Identify the linear regime principle","text":"薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。","textEn":"Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited."},{"id":"a011-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「線性成長區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the linear regime?","options":["薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-07"],"title":"拋物線成長區","titleEn":"Identify the parabolic regime","objective":"完成「拋物線成長區」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify the parabolic regime, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：拋物線成長區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the parabolic regime. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「拋物線成長區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the parabolic regime and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「拋物線成長區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify the parabolic regime: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-08-k1","title":"拋物線成長區的原理","titleEn":"Identify the parabolic regime principle","text":"厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。","textEn":"Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide."},{"id":"a011-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「拋物線成長區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the parabolic regime?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-08"],"title":"模型初始條件","titleEn":"Set model initial conditions","objective":"完成「模型初始條件」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for set model initial conditions, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：模型初始條件。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set model initial conditions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「模型初始條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set model initial conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「模型初始條件」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for set model initial conditions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-09-k1","title":"模型初始條件的原理","titleEn":"Set model initial conditions principle","text":"套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。","textEn":"Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition."},{"id":"a011-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「模型初始條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set model initial conditions?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-09"],"title":"晶向效應","titleEn":"Assess orientation effects","objective":"完成「晶向效應」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess orientation effects, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶向效應。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess orientation effects. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶向效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess orientation effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶向效應」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess orientation effects: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-10-k1","title":"晶向效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess orientation effects principle","text":"不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。","textEn":"Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates."},{"id":"a011-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶向效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess orientation effects?","options":["不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-10"],"title":"摻雜效應","titleEn":"Assess doping effects","objective":"完成「摻雜效應」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess doping effects, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜效應。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess doping effects. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「摻雜效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess doping effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜效應」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess doping effects: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-11-k1","title":"摻雜效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess doping effects principle","text":"重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。","textEn":"Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves."},{"id":"a011-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess doping effects?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-11"],"title":"應力耦合","titleEn":"Trace oxidation stress","objective":"完成「應力耦合」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace oxidation stress, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力耦合。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace oxidation stress. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「應力耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace oxidation stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力耦合」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace oxidation stress: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-12-k1","title":"應力耦合的原理","titleEn":"Trace oxidation stress principle","text":"氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。","textEn":"Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress."},{"id":"a011-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace oxidation stress?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage03","order":3,"title":"厚度與電性","titleEn":"Thickness and electrical evidence","description":"在「厚度與電性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for thickness and electrical evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-12"],"title":"橢偏膜厚","titleEn":"Interpret ellipsometric thickness","objective":"完成「橢偏膜厚」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for interpret ellipsometric thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：橢偏膜厚。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret ellipsometric thickness. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「橢偏膜厚」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret ellipsometric thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「橢偏膜厚」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for interpret ellipsometric thickness: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-13-k1","title":"橢偏膜厚的原理","titleEn":"Interpret ellipsometric thickness principle","text":"光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。","textEn":"Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions."},{"id":"a011-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「橢偏膜厚」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret ellipsometric thickness?","options":["光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-13"],"title":"截面校對","titleEn":"Cross-check section thickness","objective":"完成「截面校對」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for cross-check section thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：截面校對。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check section thickness. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「截面校對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check section thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「截面校對」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for cross-check section thickness: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-14-k1","title":"截面校對的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check section thickness principle","text":"局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。","textEn":"A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity."},{"id":"a011-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「截面校對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check section thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-14"],"title":"電容等效厚度","titleEn":"Infer electrical thickness","objective":"完成「電容等效厚度」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for infer electrical thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電容等效厚度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Infer electrical thickness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「電容等效厚度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for infer electrical thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電容等效厚度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for infer electrical thickness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-15-k1","title":"電容等效厚度的原理","titleEn":"Infer electrical thickness principle","text":"介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。","textEn":"Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness."},{"id":"a011-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電容等效厚度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating infer electrical thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-15"],"title":"漏電曲線","titleEn":"Read leakage curves","objective":"完成「漏電曲線」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for read leakage curves, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：漏電曲線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read leakage curves. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「漏電曲線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read leakage curves and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「漏電曲線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for read leakage curves: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-16-k1","title":"漏電曲線的原理","titleEn":"Read leakage curves principle","text":"比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。","textEn":"Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity."},{"id":"a011-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「漏電曲線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read leakage curves?","options":["比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-16"],"title":"界面陷阱指標","titleEn":"Inspect interface-trap evidence","objective":"完成「界面陷阱指標」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect interface-trap evidence, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面陷阱指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect interface-trap evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「界面陷阱指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect interface-trap evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面陷阱指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect interface-trap evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-17-k1","title":"界面陷阱指標的原理","titleEn":"Inspect interface-trap evidence principle","text":"C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。","textEn":"C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics."},{"id":"a011-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面陷阱指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect interface-trap evidence?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-17"],"title":"擊穿分布","titleEn":"Analyze breakdown distributions","objective":"完成「擊穿分布」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for analyze breakdown distributions, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：擊穿分布。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze breakdown distributions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「擊穿分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze breakdown distributions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「擊穿分布」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for analyze breakdown distributions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-18-k1","title":"擊穿分布的原理","titleEn":"Analyze breakdown distributions principle","text":"單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。","textEn":"One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability."},{"id":"a011-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「擊穿分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze breakdown distributions?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage04","order":4,"title":"元件熱整合","titleEn":"Device thermal integration","description":"在「元件熱整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for device thermal integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-18"],"title":"熱預算累加","titleEn":"Accumulate thermal history","objective":"完成「熱預算累加」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for accumulate thermal history, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算累加。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accumulate thermal history. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「熱預算累加」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accumulate thermal history and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算累加」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for accumulate thermal history: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-19-k1","title":"熱預算累加的原理","titleEn":"Accumulate thermal history principle","text":"長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles."},{"id":"a011-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算累加」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accumulate thermal history?","options":["長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-19"],"title":"邊角氧化","titleEn":"Assess corner oxidation","objective":"完成「邊角氧化」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess corner oxidation, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊角氧化。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess corner oxidation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「邊角氧化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess corner oxidation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊角氧化」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess corner oxidation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-20-k1","title":"邊角氧化的原理","titleEn":"Assess corner oxidation principle","text":"二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。","textEn":"Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth."},{"id":"a011-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊角氧化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess corner oxidation?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-20"],"title":"固定電荷","titleEn":"Separate fixed charge","objective":"完成「固定電荷」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate fixed charge, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：固定電荷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate fixed charge. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「固定電荷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate fixed charge and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「固定電荷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate fixed charge: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-21-k1","title":"固定電荷的原理","titleEn":"Separate fixed charge principle","text":"固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。","textEn":"Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences."},{"id":"a011-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「固定電荷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate fixed charge?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-21"],"title":"氮化選項","titleEn":"Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs","objective":"完成「氮化選項」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氮化選項。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「氮化選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氮化選項」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-22-k1","title":"氮化選項的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs principle","text":"介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。","textEn":"Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together."},{"id":"a011-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氮化選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate nitridation tradeoffs?","options":["介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-22"],"title":"模型失效界線","titleEn":"State model limits","objective":"完成「模型失效界線」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for state model limits, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：模型失效界線。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: State model limits. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「模型失效界線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for state model limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「模型失效界線」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for state model limits: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-23-k1","title":"模型失效界線的原理","titleEn":"State model limits principle","text":"經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。","textEn":"Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces."},{"id":"a011-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「模型失效界線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating state model limits?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-23"],"title":"閘氧驗收","titleEn":"Accept the gate oxide","objective":"完成「閘氧驗收」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the gate oxide, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘氧驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the gate oxide. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閘氧驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the gate oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘氧驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the gate oxide: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-24-k1","title":"閘氧驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the gate oxide principle","text":"厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。","textEn":"Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability."},{"id":"a011-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘氧驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the gate oxide?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a012","title":"高介電常數原子層沉積","titleEn":"High-k atomic layer deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["介電層與電容","表面循環","三維覆蓋","電性及整合"],"labelsEn":["Dielectric and capacitance","Surface cycles","Three-dimensional coverage","Electrical behavior and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a012-stage01","order":1,"title":"介電層與電容","titleEn":"Dielectric and capacitance","description":"在「介電層與電容」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for dielectric and capacitance, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"物理厚度與 EOT","titleEn":"Separate thickness and EOT","objective":"完成「物理厚度與 EOT」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate thickness and eot, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：物理厚度與 EOT。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate thickness and EOT. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「物理厚度與 EOT」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate thickness and eot and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「物理厚度與 EOT」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate thickness and eot: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-01-k1","title":"物理厚度與 EOT的原理","titleEn":"Separate thickness and EOT principle","text":"較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。","textEn":"Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance."},{"id":"a012-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「物理厚度與 EOT」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate thickness and eot?","options":["較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-01"],"title":"串聯介面電容","titleEn":"Calculate series interface capacitance","objective":"完成「串聯介面電容」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for calculate series interface capacitance, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：串聯介面電容。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂電容模型：令介面與上層電容分別為 2 與 8 個單位；算串聯總電容，再將上層增為 16。比較收益並說明瓶頸。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calculate series interface capacitance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical capacitance model: interface and upper-layer capacitances are 2 and 8 units. Calculate series capacitance, increase the upper layer to 16 and identify the limiting contribution.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「串聯介面電容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calculate series interface capacitance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「串聯介面電容」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for calculate series interface capacitance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-02-k1","title":"串聯介面電容的原理","titleEn":"Calculate series interface capacitance principle","text":"薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。","textEn":"A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness."},{"id":"a012-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「串聯介面電容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calculate series interface capacitance?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-02"],"title":"基底終端基團","titleEn":"Identify surface termination","objective":"完成「基底終端基團」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify surface termination, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基底終端基團。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify surface termination. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「基底終端基團」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify surface termination and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基底終端基團」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify surface termination: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-03-k1","title":"基底終端基團的原理","titleEn":"Identify surface termination principle","text":"表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。","textEn":"Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation."},{"id":"a012-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基底終端基團」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify surface termination?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-03"],"title":"前驅物相容性","titleEn":"Review precursor compatibility","objective":"完成「前驅物相容性」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for review precursor compatibility, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前驅物相容性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review precursor compatibility. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「前驅物相容性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review precursor compatibility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前驅物相容性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for review precursor compatibility: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-04-k1","title":"前驅物相容性的原理","titleEn":"Review precursor compatibility principle","text":"揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。","textEn":"Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together."},{"id":"a012-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前驅物相容性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review precursor compatibility?","options":["揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-04"],"title":"成核延遲","titleEn":"Measure nucleation delay","objective":"完成「成核延遲」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for measure nucleation delay, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：成核延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure nucleation delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「成核延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure nucleation delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「成核延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for measure nucleation delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-05-k1","title":"成核延遲的原理","titleEn":"Measure nucleation delay principle","text":"最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。","textEn":"Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth."},{"id":"a012-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「成核延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure nucleation delay?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-05"],"title":"熱式與電漿式","titleEn":"Compare thermal and plasma ALD","objective":"完成「熱式與電漿式」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare thermal and plasma ald, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱式與電漿式。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare thermal and plasma ALD. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「熱式與電漿式」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare thermal and plasma ald and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱式與電漿式」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare thermal and plasma ald: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-06-k1","title":"熱式與電漿式的原理","titleEn":"Compare thermal and plasma ALD principle","text":"活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。","textEn":"Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden."},{"id":"a012-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱式與電漿式」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare thermal and plasma ald?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面循環","titleEn":"Surface cycles","description":"在「表面循環」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for surface cycles, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-06"],"title":"第一半反應","titleEn":"Trace the first half-reaction","objective":"完成「第一半反應」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace the first half-reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：第一半反應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the first half-reaction. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「第一半反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the first half-reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「第一半反應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace the first half-reaction: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-07-k1","title":"第一半反應的原理","titleEn":"Trace the first half-reaction principle","text":"飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。","textEn":"After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth."},{"id":"a012-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「第一半反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the first half-reaction?","options":["飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-07"],"title":"清除殘留氣體","titleEn":"Separate purge from reaction","objective":"完成「清除殘留氣體」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate purge from reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：清除殘留氣體。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate purge from reaction. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「清除殘留氣體」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate purge from reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「清除殘留氣體」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate purge from reaction: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-08-k1","title":"清除殘留氣體的原理","titleEn":"Separate purge from reaction principle","text":"不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。","textEn":"Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling."},{"id":"a012-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「清除殘留氣體」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate purge from reaction?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-08"],"title":"第二半反應","titleEn":"Trace the second half-reaction","objective":"完成「第二半反應」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace the second half-reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：第二半反應。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the second half-reaction. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「第二半反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the second half-reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「第二半反應」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace the second half-reaction: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-09-k1","title":"第二半反應的原理","titleEn":"Trace the second half-reaction principle","text":"共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。","textEn":"The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface."},{"id":"a012-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「第二半反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the second half-reaction?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-09"],"title":"飽和曲線","titleEn":"Construct saturation curves","objective":"完成「飽和曲線」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for construct saturation curves, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：飽和曲線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Construct saturation curves. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「飽和曲線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for construct saturation curves and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「飽和曲線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for construct saturation curves: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-10-k1","title":"飽和曲線的原理","titleEn":"Construct saturation curves principle","text":"證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。","textEn":"Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point."},{"id":"a012-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「飽和曲線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating construct saturation curves?","options":["證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-10"],"title":"循環與膜厚","titleEn":"Relate cycles to thickness","objective":"完成「循環與膜厚」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for relate cycles to thickness, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：循環與膜厚。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate cycles to thickness. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「循環與膜厚」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate cycles to thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「循環與膜厚」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for relate cycles to thickness: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-11-k1","title":"循環與膜厚的原理","titleEn":"Relate cycles to thickness principle","text":"線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。","textEn":"Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks."},{"id":"a012-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「循環與膜厚」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate cycles to thickness?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-11"],"title":"溫度窗","titleEn":"Identify the temperature window","objective":"完成「溫度窗」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for identify the temperature window, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度窗。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the temperature window. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「溫度窗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the temperature window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度窗」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for identify the temperature window: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-12-k1","title":"溫度窗的原理","titleEn":"Identify the temperature window principle","text":"太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。","textEn":"Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition."},{"id":"a012-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度窗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the temperature window?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage03","order":3,"title":"三維覆蓋","titleEn":"Three-dimensional coverage","description":"在「三維覆蓋」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for three-dimensional coverage, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-12"],"title":"深槽反應物耗盡","titleEn":"Assess feature-scale depletion","objective":"完成「深槽反應物耗盡」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess feature-scale depletion, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：深槽反應物耗盡。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess feature-scale depletion. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「深槽反應物耗盡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess feature-scale depletion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「深槽反應物耗盡」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess feature-scale depletion: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-13-k1","title":"深槽反應物耗盡的原理","titleEn":"Assess feature-scale depletion principle","text":"入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。","textEn":"Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features."},{"id":"a012-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「深槽反應物耗盡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess feature-scale depletion?","options":["入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-13"],"title":"側壁與底部比","titleEn":"Compare sidewall and bottom thickness","objective":"完成「側壁與底部比」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare sidewall and bottom thickness, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：側壁與底部比。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sidewall and bottom thickness. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「側壁與底部比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sidewall and bottom thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「側壁與底部比」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare sidewall and bottom thickness: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-14-k1","title":"側壁與底部比的原理","titleEn":"Compare sidewall and bottom thickness principle","text":"覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。","textEn":"Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations."},{"id":"a012-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「側壁與底部比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sidewall and bottom thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-14"],"title":"成分均勻性","titleEn":"Map composition uniformity","objective":"完成「成分均勻性」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map composition uniformity, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：成分均勻性。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map composition uniformity. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「成分均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map composition uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「成分均勻性」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map composition uniformity: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-15-k1","title":"成分均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Map composition uniformity principle","text":"厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。","textEn":"Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition."},{"id":"a012-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「成分均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map composition uniformity?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-15"],"title":"針孔與漏電","titleEn":"Connect pinholes and leakage","objective":"完成「針孔與漏電」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for connect pinholes and leakage, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：針孔與漏電。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect pinholes and leakage. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「針孔與漏電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect pinholes and leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「針孔與漏電」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for connect pinholes and leakage: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-16-k1","title":"針孔與漏電的原理","titleEn":"Connect pinholes and leakage principle","text":"少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。","textEn":"A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage."},{"id":"a012-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「針孔與漏電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect pinholes and leakage?","options":["少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-16"],"title":"晶化風險","titleEn":"Assess crystallization","objective":"完成「晶化風險」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess crystallization, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶化風險。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess crystallization. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「晶化風險」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess crystallization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶化風險」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess crystallization: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-17-k1","title":"晶化風險的原理","titleEn":"Assess crystallization principle","text":"後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。","textEn":"Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways."},{"id":"a012-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶化風險」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess crystallization?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-17"],"title":"殘碳分析","titleEn":"Interpret residual carbon","objective":"完成「殘碳分析」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for interpret residual carbon, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：殘碳分析。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret residual carbon. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「殘碳分析」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret residual carbon and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「殘碳分析」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for interpret residual carbon: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-18-k1","title":"殘碳分析的原理","titleEn":"Interpret residual carbon principle","text":"成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。","textEn":"Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata."},{"id":"a012-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「殘碳分析」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret residual carbon?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性及整合","titleEn":"Electrical behavior and integration","description":"在「電性及整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for electrical behavior and integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-18"],"title":"介面偶極","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles","objective":"完成「介面偶極」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace interface dipoles, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介面偶極。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace interface dipoles. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「介面偶極」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace interface dipoles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介面偶極」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace interface dipoles: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-19-k1","title":"介面偶極的原理","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles principle","text":"介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。","textEn":"Interface chemistry can also change effective work function."},{"id":"a012-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介面偶極」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace interface dipoles?","options":["介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Interface chemistry can also change effective work function.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-19"],"title":"遷移率代價","titleEn":"Assess mobility tradeoffs","objective":"完成「遷移率代價」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess mobility tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遷移率代價。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess mobility tradeoffs. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：閘極電容提高就足以證明載子遷移率提高，不必檢查散射或陷阱。 應回到「遷移率代價」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher gate capacitance alone proves higher carrier mobility without checking scattering or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess mobility tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遷移率代價」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess mobility tradeoffs: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-20-k1","title":"遷移率代價的原理","titleEn":"Assess mobility tradeoffs principle","text":"高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。","textEn":"Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties."},{"id":"a012-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遷移率代價」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess mobility tradeoffs?","options":["閘極電容提高就足以證明載子遷移率提高，不必檢查散射或陷阱。","高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。","兩種介電堆疊只要 EOT 相同，其介面散射與有效遷移率就必定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Higher gate capacitance alone proves higher carrier mobility without checking scattering or traps.","Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties.","Two dielectric stacks with equal EOT must have identical interface scattering and effective mobility."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-20"],"title":"閘極填充空間","titleEn":"Budget gate-cavity volume","objective":"完成「閘極填充空間」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget gate-cavity volume, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘極填充空間。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget gate-cavity volume. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閘極填充空間」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget gate-cavity volume and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘極填充空間」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget gate-cavity volume: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-21-k1","title":"閘極填充空間的原理","titleEn":"Budget gate-cavity volume principle","text":"介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。","textEn":"Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume."},{"id":"a012-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘極填充空間」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget gate-cavity volume?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-21"],"title":"偏壓穩定性","titleEn":"Assess bias stability","objective":"完成「偏壓穩定性」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess bias stability, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：偏壓穩定性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess bias stability. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「偏壓穩定性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess bias stability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「偏壓穩定性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess bias stability: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-22-k1","title":"偏壓穩定性的原理","titleEn":"Assess bias stability principle","text":"初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。","textEn":"Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability."},{"id":"a012-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「偏壓穩定性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess bias stability?","options":["初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-22"],"title":"配方變更見證","titleEn":"Define change-control witnesses","objective":"完成「配方變更見證」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define change-control witnesses, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：配方變更見證。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define change-control witnesses. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「配方變更見證」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define change-control witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「配方變更見證」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define change-control witnesses: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-23-k1","title":"配方變更見證的原理","titleEn":"Define change-control witnesses principle","text":"換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。","textEn":"A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks."},{"id":"a012-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「配方變更見證」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define change-control witnesses?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-23"],"title":"高介電層放行","titleEn":"Release the high-k layer","objective":"完成「高介電層放行」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the high-k layer, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：高介電層放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the high-k layer. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「高介電層放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the high-k layer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「高介電層放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the high-k layer: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-24-k1","title":"高介電層放行的原理","titleEn":"Release the high-k layer principle","text":"EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。","textEn":"Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly."},{"id":"a012-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「高介電層放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the high-k layer?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a013","title":"金屬閘極功函數工程","titleEn":"Metal-gate work-function engineering","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["能帶與閘極","材料堆疊","選擇性加工","閾值與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Band alignment and gates","Material stacks","Selective processing","Threshold and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a013-stage01","order":1,"title":"能帶與閘極","titleEn":"Band alignment and gates","description":"在「能帶與閘極」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for band alignment and gates, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義真空功函數","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function","objective":"完成「定義真空功函數」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define vacuum work function, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：定義真空功函數。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define vacuum work function. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「定義真空功函數」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define vacuum work function and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「定義真空功函數」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define vacuum work function: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-01-k1","title":"定義真空功函數的原理","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function principle","text":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","textEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device."},{"id":"a013-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「定義真空功函數」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define vacuum work function?","options":["金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-01"],"title":"平帶條件","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions","objective":"完成「平帶條件」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：平帶條件。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw flat-band conditions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「平帶條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw flat-band conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「平帶條件」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-02-k1","title":"平帶條件的原理","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions principle","text":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","textEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge."},{"id":"a013-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「平帶條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw flat-band conditions?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-02"],"title":"NMOS 與 PMOS","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets","objective":"完成「NMOS 與 PMOS」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：NMOS 與 PMOS。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate NMOS and PMOS targets. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「NMOS 與 PMOS」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate nmos and pmos targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「NMOS 與 PMOS」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-03-k1","title":"NMOS 與 PMOS的原理","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets principle","text":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。","textEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."},{"id":"a013-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「NMOS 與 PMOS」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate nmos and pmos targets?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-03"],"title":"閘介電層串聯","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack","objective":"完成「閘介電層串聯」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘介電層串聯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include the dielectric stack. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘介電層串聯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include the dielectric stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘介電層串聯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-04-k1","title":"閘介電層串聯的原理","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack principle","text":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","textEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks."},{"id":"a013-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘介電層串聯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include the dielectric stack?","options":["相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-04"],"title":"閾值抽取定義","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction","objective":"完成「閾值抽取定義」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose threshold extraction, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值抽取定義。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose threshold extraction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閾值抽取定義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose threshold extraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值抽取定義」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose threshold extraction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-05-k1","title":"閾值抽取定義的原理","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction principle","text":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","textEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds."},{"id":"a013-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值抽取定義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose threshold extraction?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-05"],"title":"厚度空間預算","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness","objective":"完成「厚度空間預算」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：厚度空間預算。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget gate-stack thickness. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「厚度空間預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget gate-stack thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「厚度空間預算」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-06-k1","title":"厚度空間預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness principle","text":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。","textEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."},{"id":"a013-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「厚度空間預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget gate-stack thickness?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage02","order":2,"title":"材料堆疊","titleEn":"Material stacks","description":"在「材料堆疊」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for material stacks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-06"],"title":"薄金屬連續性","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity","objective":"完成「薄金屬連續性」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：薄金屬連續性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thin-metal continuity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「薄金屬連續性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thin-metal continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「薄金屬連續性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-07-k1","title":"薄金屬連續性的原理","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity principle","text":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","textEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous."},{"id":"a013-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「薄金屬連續性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thin-metal continuity?","options":["極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-07"],"title":"介面偶極形成","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles","objective":"完成「介面偶極形成」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介面偶極形成。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace interface dipoles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「介面偶極形成」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace interface dipoles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介面偶極形成」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-08-k1","title":"介面偶極形成的原理","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles principle","text":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","textEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts."},{"id":"a013-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介面偶極形成」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace interface dipoles?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Interface reactions can create additional band shifts.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-08"],"title":"氮含量與成分","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition","objective":"完成「氮含量與成分」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氮含量與成分。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare nitrogen and composition. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「氮含量與成分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare nitrogen and composition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氮含量與成分」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-09-k1","title":"氮含量與成分的原理","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition principle","text":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。","textEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."},{"id":"a013-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氮含量與成分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare nitrogen and composition?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-09"],"title":"晶粒與取向","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation","objective":"完成「晶粒與取向」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶粒與取向。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess grain orientation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶粒與取向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess grain orientation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶粒與取向」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-10-k1","title":"晶粒與取向的原理","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation principle","text":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","textEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences."},{"id":"a013-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶粒與取向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess grain orientation?","options":["多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-10"],"title":"沉積成核","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation","objective":"完成「沉積成核」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect nucleation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沉積成核。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect nucleation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「沉積成核」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect nucleation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沉積成核」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect nucleation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-11-k1","title":"沉積成核的原理","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation principle","text":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","textEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior."},{"id":"a013-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沉積成核」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect nucleation?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-11"],"title":"熱處理重分布","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution","objective":"完成「熱處理重分布」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱處理重分布。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track thermal redistribution. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「熱處理重分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track thermal redistribution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱處理重分布」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-12-k1","title":"熱處理重分布的原理","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution principle","text":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。","textEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱處理重分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track thermal redistribution?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."],"answer":2,"explanation":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage03","order":3,"title":"選擇性加工","titleEn":"Selective processing","description":"在「選擇性加工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for selective processing, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-12"],"title":"區域保護層","titleEn":"Plan regional protection","objective":"完成「區域保護層」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for plan regional protection, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：區域保護層。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan regional protection. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「區域保護層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan regional protection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「區域保護層」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for plan regional protection: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-13-k1","title":"區域保護層的原理","titleEn":"Plan regional protection principle","text":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","textEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「區域保護層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan regional protection?","options":["選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-13"],"title":"金屬回蝕","titleEn":"Assess metal recess","objective":"完成「金屬回蝕」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess metal recess, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬回蝕。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess metal recess. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬回蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess metal recess and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬回蝕」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess metal recess: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-14-k1","title":"金屬回蝕的原理","titleEn":"Assess metal recess principle","text":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","textEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage."},{"id":"a013-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬回蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess metal recess?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-14"],"title":"選擇性去除","titleEn":"Check selective removal","objective":"完成「選擇性去除」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for check selective removal, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性去除。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check selective removal. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「選擇性去除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check selective removal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性去除」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for check selective removal: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-15-k1","title":"選擇性去除的原理","titleEn":"Check selective removal principle","text":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。","textEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."},{"id":"a013-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性去除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check selective removal?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-15"],"title":"窄腔填充","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill","objective":"完成「窄腔填充」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：窄腔填充。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect narrow-cavity fill. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「窄腔填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect narrow-cavity fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「窄腔填充」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-16-k1","title":"窄腔填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill principle","text":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","textEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids."},{"id":"a013-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「窄腔填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect narrow-cavity fill?","options":["外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Premature closure can conceal internal voids.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-16"],"title":"閘極電阻","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance","objective":"完成「閘極電阻」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate gate resistance, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘極電阻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate gate resistance. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「閘極電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate gate resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘極電阻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate gate resistance: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-17-k1","title":"閘極電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance principle","text":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","textEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria."},{"id":"a013-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘極電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate gate resistance?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-17"],"title":"金屬殘留短路","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges","objective":"完成「金屬殘留短路」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬殘留短路。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 做一張閾值歸因表：列金屬功函數、介面電荷及通道摻雜三個可能原因；為各原因分別指定材料分析、C-V 或摻雜輪廓的辨別證據。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate residual-metal bridges. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Build a threshold-attribution table for metal work function, interface charge and channel doping. Assign discriminating materials, C-V or doping-profile evidence to each.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬殘留短路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate residual-metal bridges and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬殘留短路」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-18-k1","title":"金屬殘留短路的原理","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges principle","text":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。","textEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."},{"id":"a013-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬殘留短路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate residual-metal bridges?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage04","order":4,"title":"閾值與可靠度","titleEn":"Threshold and reliability","description":"在「閾值與可靠度」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for threshold and reliability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-18"],"title":"C-V 與 I-V","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V","objective":"完成「C-V 與 I-V」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：C-V 與 I-V。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check C-V and I-V. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「C-V 與 I-V」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check c-v and i-v and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「C-V 與 I-V」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-19-k1","title":"C-V 與 I-V的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V principle","text":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","textEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities."},{"id":"a013-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「C-V 與 I-V」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check c-v and i-v?","options":["兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-19"],"title":"閾值空間圖","titleEn":"Map threshold variation","objective":"完成「閾值空間圖」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for map threshold variation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值空間圖。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map threshold variation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閾值空間圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map threshold variation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值空間圖」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for map threshold variation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-20-k1","title":"閾值空間圖的原理","titleEn":"Map threshold variation principle","text":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","textEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures."},{"id":"a013-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值空間圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map threshold variation?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-20"],"title":"溫度依賴","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence","objective":"完成「溫度依賴」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度依賴。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare temperature dependence. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「溫度依賴」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare temperature dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度依賴」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-21-k1","title":"溫度依賴的原理","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence principle","text":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。","textEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."},{"id":"a013-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度依賴」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare temperature dependence?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-21"],"title":"偏壓老化","titleEn":"Track bias aging","objective":"完成「偏壓老化」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for track bias aging, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：偏壓老化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bias aging. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「偏壓老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bias aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「偏壓老化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for track bias aging: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-22-k1","title":"偏壓老化的原理","titleEn":"Track bias aging principle","text":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","textEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets."},{"id":"a013-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「偏壓老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bias aging?","options":["閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-22"],"title":"雙極性整合","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration","objective":"完成「雙極性整合」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：雙極性整合。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review dual-polarity integration. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「雙極性整合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review dual-polarity integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「雙極性整合」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-23-k1","title":"雙極性整合的原理","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration principle","text":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","textEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation."},{"id":"a013-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「雙極性整合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review dual-polarity integration?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-23"],"title":"金屬閘極驗收","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate","objective":"完成「金屬閘極驗收」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬閘極驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the metal gate. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「金屬閘極驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the metal gate and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬閘極驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-24-k1","title":"金屬閘極驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate principle","text":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。","textEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."},{"id":"a013-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬閘極驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the metal gate?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a014","title":"離子佈植摻雜","titleEn":"Ion implantation doping","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解劑量、射程、損傷及活化，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore dose, range, damage and activation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["佈植目的與輪廓","束流與遮罩","損傷與活化","量測及整合"],"labelsEn":["Implant purpose and profiles","Beam and masks","Damage and activation","Measurement and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a014-stage01","order":1,"title":"佈植目的與輪廓","titleEn":"Implant purpose and profiles","description":"在「佈植目的與輪廓」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for implant purpose and profiles, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"劑量與濃度","titleEn":"Separate dose and concentration","objective":"完成「劑量與濃度」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate dose and concentration, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：劑量與濃度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂積分題：假設一段厚 10 nm 的均勻區濃度為 10^19 cm^-3；先把厚度換成 cm，再求面劑量，並解釋此方盒輪廓不是實際佈植高斯輪廓。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate dose and concentration. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical integral: a uniform 10 nm region has concentration 10^19 cm^-3. Convert thickness to cm and compute areal dose; explain why this box profile is not a real implantation Gaussian.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「劑量與濃度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate dose and concentration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「劑量與濃度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate dose and concentration: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-01-k1","title":"劑量與濃度的原理","titleEn":"Separate dose and concentration principle","text":"面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。","textEn":"Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings."},{"id":"a014-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「劑量與濃度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate dose and concentration?","options":["面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-01"],"title":"摻雜種類","titleEn":"Choose dopant roles","objective":"完成「摻雜種類」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for choose dopant roles, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜種類。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose dopant roles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「摻雜種類」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose dopant roles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜種類」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for choose dopant roles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-02-k1","title":"摻雜種類的原理","titleEn":"Choose dopant roles principle","text":"摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。","textEn":"Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior."},{"id":"a014-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜種類」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose dopant roles?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-02"],"title":"投影射程","titleEn":"Read projected range","objective":"完成「投影射程」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for read projected range, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：投影射程。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read projected range. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「投影射程」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read projected range and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「投影射程」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for read projected range: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-03-k1","title":"投影射程的原理","titleEn":"Read projected range principle","text":"射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。","textEn":"Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail."},{"id":"a014-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「投影射程」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read projected range?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail."],"answer":2,"explanation":"射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-03"],"title":"能量與深度","titleEn":"Relate energy and depth","objective":"完成「能量與深度」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for relate energy and depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：能量與深度。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate energy and depth. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「能量與深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate energy and depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「能量與深度」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for relate energy and depth: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-04-k1","title":"能量與深度的原理","titleEn":"Relate energy and depth principle","text":"能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。","textEn":"Energy affects both depth and damage distribution."},{"id":"a014-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「能量與深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate energy and depth?","options":["能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Energy affects both depth and damage distribution.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-04"],"title":"接面位置","titleEn":"Define junction depth","objective":"完成「接面位置」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define junction depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面位置。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define junction depth. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「接面位置」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define junction depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面位置」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define junction depth: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-05-k1","title":"接面位置的原理","titleEn":"Define junction depth principle","text":"接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。","textEn":"Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping."},{"id":"a014-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面位置」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define junction depth?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-05"],"title":"遮罩止擋條件","titleEn":"Set mask-stopping evidence","objective":"完成「遮罩止擋條件」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for set mask-stopping evidence, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遮罩止擋條件。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set mask-stopping evidence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「遮罩止擋條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set mask-stopping evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遮罩止擋條件」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for set mask-stopping evidence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-06-k1","title":"遮罩止擋條件的原理","titleEn":"Set mask-stopping evidence principle","text":"遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。","textEn":"Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions."},{"id":"a014-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遮罩止擋條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set mask-stopping evidence?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage02","order":2,"title":"束流與遮罩","titleEn":"Beam and masks","description":"在「束流與遮罩」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for beam and masks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-06"],"title":"質量分析","titleEn":"Trace mass selection","objective":"完成「質量分析」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace mass selection, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：質量分析。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace mass selection. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「質量分析」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace mass selection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「質量分析」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace mass selection: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-07-k1","title":"質量分析的原理","titleEn":"Trace mass selection principle","text":"電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。","textEn":"Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species."},{"id":"a014-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「質量分析」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace mass selection?","options":["電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-07"],"title":"束流積分","titleEn":"Integrate beam dose","objective":"完成「束流積分」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for integrate beam dose, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：束流積分。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Integrate beam dose. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「束流積分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for integrate beam dose and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「束流積分」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for integrate beam dose: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-08-k1","title":"束流積分的原理","titleEn":"Integrate beam dose principle","text":"電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。","textEn":"Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area."},{"id":"a014-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「束流積分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating integrate beam dose?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-08"],"title":"掃描均勻性","titleEn":"Assess scan uniformity","objective":"完成「掃描均勻性」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess scan uniformity, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掃描均勻性。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess scan uniformity. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「掃描均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess scan uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掃描均勻性」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess scan uniformity: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-09-k1","title":"掃描均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Assess scan uniformity principle","text":"掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。","textEn":"Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose."},{"id":"a014-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掃描均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess scan uniformity?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-09"],"title":"晶向通道效應","titleEn":"Assess channeling","objective":"完成「晶向通道效應」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess channeling, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶向通道效應。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess channeling. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「晶向通道效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess channeling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶向通道效應」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess channeling: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-10-k1","title":"晶向通道效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess channeling principle","text":"沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。","textEn":"Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails."},{"id":"a014-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶向通道效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess channeling?","options":["沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-10"],"title":"傾角與陰影","titleEn":"Assess tilt and shadowing","objective":"完成「傾角與陰影」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess tilt and shadowing, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：傾角與陰影。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess tilt and shadowing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「傾角與陰影」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess tilt and shadowing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「傾角與陰影」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess tilt and shadowing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-11-k1","title":"傾角與陰影的原理","titleEn":"Assess tilt and shadowing principle","text":"抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。","textEn":"Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing."},{"id":"a014-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「傾角與陰影」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess tilt and shadowing?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-11"],"title":"晶圓充電","titleEn":"Assess wafer charging","objective":"完成「晶圓充電」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess wafer charging, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶圓充電。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess wafer charging. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「晶圓充電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess wafer charging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶圓充電」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess wafer charging: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-12-k1","title":"晶圓充電的原理","titleEn":"Assess wafer charging principle","text":"絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。","textEn":"Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage."},{"id":"a014-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶圓充電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess wafer charging?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage03","order":3,"title":"損傷與活化","titleEn":"Damage and activation","description":"在「損傷與活化」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for damage and activation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-12"],"title":"碰撞損傷","titleEn":"Map collision damage","objective":"完成「碰撞損傷」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map collision damage, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：碰撞損傷。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map collision damage. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「碰撞損傷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map collision damage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「碰撞損傷」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map collision damage: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-13-k1","title":"碰撞損傷的原理","titleEn":"Map collision damage principle","text":"佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。","textEn":"Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration."},{"id":"a014-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「碰撞損傷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map collision damage?","options":["佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-13"],"title":"非晶化區","titleEn":"Identify amorphized regions","objective":"完成「非晶化區」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify amorphized regions, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：非晶化區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify amorphized regions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「非晶化區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify amorphized regions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「非晶化區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify amorphized regions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-14-k1","title":"非晶化區的原理","titleEn":"Identify amorphized regions principle","text":"非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。","textEn":"Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing."},{"id":"a014-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「非晶化區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify amorphized regions?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-14"],"title":"暫態增強擴散","titleEn":"Identify transient enhanced diffusion","objective":"完成「暫態增強擴散」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify transient enhanced diffusion, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：暫態增強擴散。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify transient enhanced diffusion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「暫態增強擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify transient enhanced diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「暫態增強擴散」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify transient enhanced diffusion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-15-k1","title":"暫態增強擴散的原理","titleEn":"Identify transient enhanced diffusion principle","text":"過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。","textEn":"Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion."},{"id":"a014-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「暫態增強擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify transient enhanced diffusion?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-15"],"title":"活化比例","titleEn":"Estimate activation fraction","objective":"完成「活化比例」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for estimate activation fraction, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化比例。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate activation fraction. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「活化比例」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate activation fraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化比例」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for estimate activation fraction: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-16-k1","title":"活化比例的原理","titleEn":"Estimate activation fraction principle","text":"活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。","textEn":"Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence."},{"id":"a014-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化比例」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate activation fraction?","options":["活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-16"],"title":"聚集與失活","titleEn":"Assess clustering and deactivation","objective":"完成「聚集與失活」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess clustering and deactivation, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：聚集與失活。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess clustering and deactivation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「聚集與失活」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess clustering and deactivation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「聚集與失活」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess clustering and deactivation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-17-k1","title":"聚集與失活的原理","titleEn":"Assess clustering and deactivation principle","text":"更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。","textEn":"More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers."},{"id":"a014-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「聚集與失活」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess clustering and deactivation?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-17"],"title":"遮罩去除風險","titleEn":"Review mask stripping","objective":"完成「遮罩去除風險」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review mask stripping, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遮罩去除風險。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review mask stripping. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「遮罩去除風險」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review mask stripping and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遮罩去除風險」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review mask stripping: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-18-k1","title":"遮罩去除風險的原理","titleEn":"Review mask stripping principle","text":"高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。","textEn":"High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty."},{"id":"a014-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遮罩去除風險」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review mask stripping?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測及整合","titleEn":"Measurement and integration","description":"在「量測及整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for measurement and integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-18"],"title":"SIMS 深度校準","titleEn":"Calibrate SIMS depth","objective":"完成「SIMS 深度校準」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for calibrate sims depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SIMS 深度校準。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calibrate SIMS depth. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「SIMS 深度校準」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calibrate sims depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SIMS 深度校準」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for calibrate sims depth: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-19-k1","title":"SIMS 深度校準的原理","titleEn":"Calibrate SIMS depth principle","text":"濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。","textEn":"Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration."},{"id":"a014-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SIMS 深度校準」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calibrate sims depth?","options":["濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-19"],"title":"片電阻判讀","titleEn":"Interpret sheet resistance","objective":"完成「片電阻判讀」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for interpret sheet resistance, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片電阻判讀。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret sheet resistance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「片電阻判讀」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret sheet resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片電阻判讀」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for interpret sheet resistance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-20-k1","title":"片電阻判讀的原理","titleEn":"Interpret sheet resistance principle","text":"片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。","textEn":"Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth."},{"id":"a014-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片電阻判讀」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret sheet resistance?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-20"],"title":"接面漏電","titleEn":"Inspect junction leakage","objective":"完成「接面漏電」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect junction leakage, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面漏電。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect junction leakage. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「接面漏電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect junction leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面漏電」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect junction leakage: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-21-k1","title":"接面漏電的原理","titleEn":"Inspect junction leakage principle","text":"低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。","textEn":"Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal."},{"id":"a014-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面漏電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect junction leakage?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-21"],"title":"多重能量設計","titleEn":"Compare multi-energy profiles","objective":"完成「多重能量設計」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare multi-energy profiles, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：多重能量設計。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare multi-energy profiles. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「多重能量設計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare multi-energy profiles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「多重能量設計」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare multi-energy profiles: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-22-k1","title":"多重能量設計的原理","titleEn":"Compare multi-energy profiles principle","text":"多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。","textEn":"Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate."},{"id":"a014-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「多重能量設計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare multi-energy profiles?","options":["多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-22"],"title":"熱歷程追蹤","titleEn":"Track subsequent heat treatments","objective":"完成「熱歷程追蹤」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track subsequent heat treatments, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱歷程追蹤。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track subsequent heat treatments. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「熱歷程追蹤」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track subsequent heat treatments and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱歷程追蹤」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track subsequent heat treatments: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-23-k1","title":"熱歷程追蹤的原理","titleEn":"Track subsequent heat treatments principle","text":"佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。","textEn":"Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing."},{"id":"a014-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱歷程追蹤」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track subsequent heat treatments?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-23"],"title":"佈植批次審查","titleEn":"Review the implant lot","objective":"完成「佈植批次審查」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review the implant lot, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：佈植批次審查。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review the implant lot. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「佈植批次審查」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review the implant lot and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「佈植批次審查」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review the implant lot: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-24-k1","title":"佈植批次審查的原理","titleEn":"Review the implant lot principle","text":"劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。","textEn":"Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together."},{"id":"a014-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「佈植批次審查」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review the implant lot?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a015","title":"快速熱退火","titleEn":"Rapid thermal annealing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["退火需求","升降溫控制","電性與形貌","製程窗口"],"labelsEn":["Annealing requirements","Heating and cooling","Electrical and structural outcomes","Process-window evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a015-stage01","order":1,"title":"退火需求","titleEn":"Annealing requirements","description":"在「退火需求」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for annealing requirements, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"活化與擴散","titleEn":"Separate activation and diffusion","objective":"完成「活化與擴散」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate activation and diffusion, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化與擴散。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate activation and diffusion. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「活化與擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate activation and diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化與擴散」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate activation and diffusion: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-01-k1","title":"活化與擴散的原理","titleEn":"Separate activation and diffusion principle","text":"活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。","textEn":"Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution."},{"id":"a015-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化與擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate activation and diffusion?","options":["活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-01"],"title":"溫度時間軌跡","titleEn":"Draw temperature-time trajectories","objective":"完成「溫度時間軌跡」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw temperature-time trajectories, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度時間軌跡。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw temperature-time trajectories. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「溫度時間軌跡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw temperature-time trajectories and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度時間軌跡」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw temperature-time trajectories: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-02-k1","title":"溫度時間軌跡的原理","titleEn":"Draw temperature-time trajectories principle","text":"峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。","textEn":"Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure."},{"id":"a015-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度時間軌跡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw temperature-time trajectories?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-02"],"title":"熱預算積分","titleEn":"Construct a thermal-budget integral","objective":"完成「熱預算積分」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for construct a thermal-budget integral, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算積分。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂兩段熱歷程：用任意擴散係數 D1=1、D2=4 與時間 t1=4、t2=1 比較 D×t；說明同一擴散積分仍不證明活化或缺陷演化相同。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Construct a thermal-budget integral. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical thermal histories: compare D×t for arbitrary diffusivities D1=1, D2=4 and times t1=4, t2=1. Explain why equal integrated diffusion does not prove equal activation or defect evolution.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱預算積分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for construct a thermal-budget integral and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算積分」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for construct a thermal-budget integral: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-03-k1","title":"熱預算積分的原理","titleEn":"Construct a thermal-budget integral principle","text":"擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。","textEn":"Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone."},{"id":"a015-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算積分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating construct a thermal-budget integral?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-03"],"title":"損傷恢復","titleEn":"Define damage-recovery targets","objective":"完成「損傷恢復」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define damage-recovery targets, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：損傷恢復。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define damage-recovery targets. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「損傷恢復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define damage-recovery targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「損傷恢復」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define damage-recovery targets: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-04-k1","title":"損傷恢復的原理","titleEn":"Define damage-recovery targets principle","text":"缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。","textEn":"Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales."},{"id":"a015-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「損傷恢復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define damage-recovery targets?","options":["缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-04"],"title":"前段堆疊","titleEn":"Inventory the incoming stack","objective":"完成「前段堆疊」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inventory the incoming stack, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前段堆疊。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inventory the incoming stack. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「前段堆疊」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inventory the incoming stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前段堆疊」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inventory the incoming stack: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-05-k1","title":"前段堆疊的原理","titleEn":"Inventory the incoming stack principle","text":"表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。","textEn":"Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer."},{"id":"a015-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前段堆疊」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inventory the incoming stack?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-05"],"title":"氣氛角色","titleEn":"Assign ambient functions","objective":"完成「氣氛角色」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assign ambient functions, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣氛角色。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign ambient functions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「氣氛角色」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign ambient functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣氛角色」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assign ambient functions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-06-k1","title":"氣氛角色的原理","titleEn":"Assign ambient functions principle","text":"氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。","textEn":"Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport."},{"id":"a015-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣氛角色」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign ambient functions?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage02","order":2,"title":"升降溫控制","titleEn":"Heating and cooling","description":"在「升降溫控制」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for heating and cooling, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-06"],"title":"燈區分配","titleEn":"Allocate heating zones","objective":"完成「燈區分配」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for allocate heating zones, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：燈區分配。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Allocate heating zones. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「燈區分配」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for allocate heating zones and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「燈區分配」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for allocate heating zones: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-07-k1","title":"燈區分配的原理","titleEn":"Allocate heating zones principle","text":"多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。","textEn":"Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling."},{"id":"a015-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「燈區分配」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating allocate heating zones?","options":["多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-07"],"title":"高溫計發射率","titleEn":"Assess pyrometer emissivity","objective":"完成「高溫計發射率」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess pyrometer emissivity, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：高溫計發射率。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pyrometer emissivity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「高溫計發射率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pyrometer emissivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「高溫計發射率」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess pyrometer emissivity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-08-k1","title":"高溫計發射率的原理","titleEn":"Assess pyrometer emissivity principle","text":"亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。","textEn":"Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model."},{"id":"a015-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「高溫計發射率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pyrometer emissivity?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-08"],"title":"背面狀態","titleEn":"Check backside conditions","objective":"完成「背面狀態」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for check backside conditions, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背面狀態。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check backside conditions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「背面狀態」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check backside conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背面狀態」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for check backside conditions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-09-k1","title":"背面狀態的原理","titleEn":"Check backside conditions principle","text":"背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。","textEn":"Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings."},{"id":"a015-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背面狀態」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check backside conditions?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-09"],"title":"升溫斜率","titleEn":"Compare ramp rates","objective":"完成「升溫斜率」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare ramp rates, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：升溫斜率。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare ramp rates. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「升溫斜率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare ramp rates and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「升溫斜率」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare ramp rates: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-10-k1","title":"升溫斜率的原理","titleEn":"Compare ramp rates principle","text":"快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。","textEn":"Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients."},{"id":"a015-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「升溫斜率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare ramp rates?","options":["快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-10"],"title":"旋轉與均勻","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging","objective":"完成「旋轉與均勻」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess rotation averaging, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：旋轉與均勻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess rotation averaging. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「旋轉與均勻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess rotation averaging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「旋轉與均勻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess rotation averaging: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-11-k1","title":"旋轉與均勻的原理","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging principle","text":"旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。","textEn":"Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations."},{"id":"a015-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「旋轉與均勻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess rotation averaging?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-11"],"title":"冷卻尾端","titleEn":"Include the cooling tail","objective":"完成「冷卻尾端」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for include the cooling tail, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：冷卻尾端。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include the cooling tail. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Diffusion can continue during cooling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Diffusion can continue during cooling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「冷卻尾端」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include the cooling tail and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「冷卻尾端」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for include the cooling tail: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-12-k1","title":"冷卻尾端的原理","titleEn":"Include the cooling tail principle","text":"降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。","textEn":"Diffusion can continue during cooling."},{"id":"a015-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「冷卻尾端」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include the cooling tail?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Diffusion can continue during cooling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Diffusion can continue during cooling. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage03","order":3,"title":"電性與形貌","titleEn":"Electrical and structural outcomes","description":"在「電性與形貌」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for electrical and structural outcomes, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-12"],"title":"片電阻前後","titleEn":"Compare sheet resistance","objective":"完成「片電阻前後」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare sheet resistance, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片電阻前後。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sheet resistance. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「片電阻前後」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sheet resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片電阻前後」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare sheet resistance: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-13-k1","title":"片電阻前後的原理","titleEn":"Compare sheet resistance principle","text":"片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。","textEn":"Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth."},{"id":"a015-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片電阻前後」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sheet resistance?","options":["片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-13"],"title":"濃度輪廓展寬","titleEn":"Measure profile broadening","objective":"完成「濃度輪廓展寬」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure profile broadening, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濃度輪廓展寬。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure profile broadening. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「濃度輪廓展寬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure profile broadening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濃度輪廓展寬」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure profile broadening: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-14-k1","title":"濃度輪廓展寬的原理","titleEn":"Measure profile broadening principle","text":"較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。","textEn":"Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control."},{"id":"a015-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濃度輪廓展寬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure profile broadening?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-14"],"title":"接面漏電圖","titleEn":"Map junction leakage","objective":"完成「接面漏電圖」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map junction leakage, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面漏電圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map junction leakage. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「接面漏電圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map junction leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面漏電圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map junction leakage: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-15-k1","title":"接面漏電圖的原理","titleEn":"Map junction leakage principle","text":"漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。","textEn":"Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage."},{"id":"a015-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面漏電圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map junction leakage?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-15"],"title":"滑移線","titleEn":"Inspect slip lines","objective":"完成「滑移線」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect slip lines, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：滑移線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect slip lines. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「滑移線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect slip lines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「滑移線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect slip lines: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-16-k1","title":"滑移線的原理","titleEn":"Inspect slip lines principle","text":"熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。","textEn":"Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects."},{"id":"a015-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「滑移線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect slip lines?","options":["熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-16"],"title":"翹曲回復","titleEn":"Measure bow evolution","objective":"完成「翹曲回復」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for measure bow evolution, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：翹曲回復。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure bow evolution. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「翹曲回復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure bow evolution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「翹曲回復」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for measure bow evolution: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-17-k1","title":"翹曲回復的原理","titleEn":"Measure bow evolution principle","text":"退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。","textEn":"Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions."},{"id":"a015-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「翹曲回復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure bow evolution?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-17"],"title":"圖案吸收差","titleEn":"Assess pattern-dependent absorption","objective":"完成「圖案吸收差」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess pattern-dependent absorption, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案吸收差。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pattern-dependent absorption. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「圖案吸收差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pattern-dependent absorption and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案吸收差」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess pattern-dependent absorption: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-18-k1","title":"圖案吸收差的原理","titleEn":"Assess pattern-dependent absorption principle","text":"裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。","textEn":"Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity."},{"id":"a015-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案吸收差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pattern-dependent absorption?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage04","order":4,"title":"製程窗口","titleEn":"Process-window evidence","description":"在「製程窗口」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for process-window evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-18"],"title":"峰值與停留權衡","titleEn":"Trade peak temperature against dwell","objective":"完成「峰值與停留權衡」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trade peak temperature against dwell, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與停留權衡。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trade peak temperature against dwell. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「峰值與停留權衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trade peak temperature against dwell and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與停留權衡」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trade peak temperature against dwell: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-19-k1","title":"峰值與停留權衡的原理","titleEn":"Trade peak temperature against dwell principle","text":"更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。","textEn":"Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks."},{"id":"a015-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與停留權衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trade peak temperature against dwell?","options":["更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-19"],"title":"不確定度傳播","titleEn":"Propagate temperature uncertainty","objective":"完成「不確定度傳播」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for propagate temperature uncertainty, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：不確定度傳播。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Propagate temperature uncertainty. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「不確定度傳播」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for propagate temperature uncertainty and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「不確定度傳播」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for propagate temperature uncertainty: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-20-k1","title":"不確定度傳播的原理","titleEn":"Propagate temperature uncertainty principle","text":"小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。","textEn":"Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes."},{"id":"a015-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「不確定度傳播」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating propagate temperature uncertainty?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-20"],"title":"監控片轉移","titleEn":"Transfer monitor calibration","objective":"完成「監控片轉移」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for transfer monitor calibration, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：監控片轉移。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Transfer monitor calibration. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「監控片轉移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for transfer monitor calibration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「監控片轉移」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for transfer monitor calibration: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-21-k1","title":"監控片轉移的原理","titleEn":"Transfer monitor calibration principle","text":"監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。","textEn":"Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers."},{"id":"a015-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「監控片轉移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating transfer monitor calibration?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-21"],"title":"批間漂移","titleEn":"Detect run-to-run drift","objective":"完成「批間漂移」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for detect run-to-run drift, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：批間漂移。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Detect run-to-run drift. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「批間漂移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for detect run-to-run drift and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「批間漂移」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for detect run-to-run drift: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-22-k1","title":"批間漂移的原理","titleEn":"Detect run-to-run drift principle","text":"燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。","textEn":"Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift."},{"id":"a015-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「批間漂移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating detect run-to-run drift?","options":["燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-22"],"title":"跨模組交接","titleEn":"Handoff thermal constraints","objective":"完成「跨模組交接」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for handoff thermal constraints, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：跨模組交接。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Handoff thermal constraints. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「跨模組交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for handoff thermal constraints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「跨模組交接」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for handoff thermal constraints: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-23-k1","title":"跨模組交接的原理","titleEn":"Handoff thermal constraints principle","text":"閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。","textEn":"Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits."},{"id":"a015-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「跨模組交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating handoff thermal constraints?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-23"],"title":"退火窗口放行","titleEn":"Accept the annealing window","objective":"完成「退火窗口放行」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the annealing window, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：退火窗口放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the annealing window. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「退火窗口放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the annealing window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「退火窗口放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the annealing window: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-24-k1","title":"退火窗口放行的原理","titleEn":"Accept the annealing window principle","text":"活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。","textEn":"Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria."},{"id":"a015-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「退火窗口放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the annealing window?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a016","title":"雷射尖峰退火","titleEn":"Laser spike annealing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["雷射熱歷程","光束與掃描","局部反應","圖案相容性"],"labelsEn":["Laser thermal history","Beam and scanning","Localized response","Pattern compatibility"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a016-stage01","order":1,"title":"雷射熱歷程","titleEn":"Laser thermal history","description":"在「雷射熱歷程」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for laser thermal history, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"毫秒與奈秒","titleEn":"Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes","objective":"完成「毫秒與奈秒」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：毫秒與奈秒。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「毫秒與奈秒」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「毫秒與奈秒」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-01-k1","title":"毫秒與奈秒的原理","titleEn":"Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes principle","text":"不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。","textEn":"Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process."},{"id":"a016-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「毫秒與奈秒」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes?","options":["不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-01"],"title":"光吸收深度","titleEn":"Assess optical penetration","objective":"完成「光吸收深度」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess optical penetration, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光吸收深度。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess optical penetration. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「光吸收深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess optical penetration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光吸收深度」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess optical penetration: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-02-k1","title":"光吸收深度的原理","titleEn":"Assess optical penetration principle","text":"光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。","textEn":"Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth."},{"id":"a016-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光吸收深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess optical penetration?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-02"],"title":"熱擴散尺度","titleEn":"Estimate thermal diffusion length","objective":"完成「熱擴散尺度」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for estimate thermal diffusion length, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱擴散尺度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate thermal diffusion length. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱擴散尺度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate thermal diffusion length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱擴散尺度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for estimate thermal diffusion length: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-03-k1","title":"熱擴散尺度的原理","titleEn":"Estimate thermal diffusion length principle","text":"熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time."},{"id":"a016-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱擴散尺度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate thermal diffusion length?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-03"],"title":"峰值與積分能量","titleEn":"Separate peak and integrated energy","objective":"完成「峰值與積分能量」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate peak and integrated energy, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與積分能量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate peak and integrated energy. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「峰值與積分能量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate peak and integrated energy and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與積分能量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate peak and integrated energy: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-04-k1","title":"峰值與積分能量的原理","titleEn":"Separate peak and integrated energy principle","text":"相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。","textEn":"Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures."},{"id":"a016-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與積分能量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate peak and integrated energy?","options":["相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-04"],"title":"熔融與非熔融","titleEn":"Distinguish melting regimes","objective":"完成「熔融與非熔融」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for distinguish melting regimes, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熔融與非熔融。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish melting regimes. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熔融與非熔融」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish melting regimes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熔融與非熔融」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for distinguish melting regimes: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-05-k1","title":"熔融與非熔融的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish melting regimes principle","text":"是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。","textEn":"Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms."},{"id":"a016-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熔融與非熔融」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish melting regimes?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-05"],"title":"熱敏感下層","titleEn":"Identify sensitive underlying layers","objective":"完成「熱敏感下層」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for identify sensitive underlying layers, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱敏感下層。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify sensitive underlying layers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱敏感下層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify sensitive underlying layers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱敏感下層」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for identify sensitive underlying layers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-06-k1","title":"熱敏感下層的原理","titleEn":"Identify sensitive underlying layers principle","text":"表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。","textEn":"Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment."},{"id":"a016-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱敏感下層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify sensitive underlying layers?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}}]},{"id":"a016-stage02","order":2,"title":"光束與掃描","titleEn":"Beam and scanning","description":"在「光束與掃描」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for beam and scanning, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-06"],"title":"光斑強度剖面","titleEn":"Read the beam profile","objective":"完成「光斑強度剖面」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for read the beam profile, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光斑強度剖面。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read the beam profile. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「光斑強度剖面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read the beam profile and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光斑強度剖面」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for read the beam profile: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-07-k1","title":"光斑強度剖面的原理","titleEn":"Read the beam profile principle","text":"平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。","textEn":"Mean power does not describe local beam intensity."},{"id":"a016-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光斑強度剖面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read the beam profile?","options":["平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Mean power does not describe local beam intensity.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-07"],"title":"掃描速度","titleEn":"Relate scan speed and dwell","objective":"完成「掃描速度」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for relate scan speed and dwell, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掃描速度。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂掃描幾何：光斑寬 0.1 mm、掃速 100 mm/s；求單點名義停留時間，再把掃速加倍，並列出需另外處理的重疊與光斑非均勻。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate scan speed and dwell. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical scan: beam width 0.1 mm and speed 100 mm/s. Compute nominal dwell, double the speed, and list overlap and beam nonuniformity effects requiring separate treatment.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「掃描速度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate scan speed and dwell and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掃描速度」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for relate scan speed and dwell: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-08-k1","title":"掃描速度的原理","titleEn":"Relate scan speed and dwell principle","text":"固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。","textEn":"With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell."},{"id":"a016-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掃描速度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate scan speed and dwell?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-08"],"title":"重疊帶","titleEn":"Assess scan overlap","objective":"完成「重疊帶」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess scan overlap, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重疊帶。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess scan overlap. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「重疊帶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess scan overlap and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重疊帶」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess scan overlap: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-09-k1","title":"重疊帶的原理","titleEn":"Assess scan overlap principle","text":"相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。","textEn":"Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure."},{"id":"a016-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重疊帶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess scan overlap?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-09"],"title":"邊緣轉向","titleEn":"Inspect scan turnarounds","objective":"完成「邊緣轉向」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect scan turnarounds, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊緣轉向。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect scan turnarounds. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「邊緣轉向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect scan turnarounds and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊緣轉向」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect scan turnarounds: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-10-k1","title":"邊緣轉向的原理","titleEn":"Inspect scan turnarounds principle","text":"掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。","textEn":"Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area."},{"id":"a016-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊緣轉向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect scan turnarounds?","options":["掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-10"],"title":"溫度回授延遲","titleEn":"Account for thermal-feedback delay","objective":"完成「溫度回授延遲」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for account for thermal-feedback delay, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度回授延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Account for thermal-feedback delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「溫度回授延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for account for thermal-feedback delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度回授延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for account for thermal-feedback delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-11-k1","title":"溫度回授延遲的原理","titleEn":"Account for thermal-feedback delay principle","text":"感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。","textEn":"Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks."},{"id":"a016-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度回授延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating account for thermal-feedback delay?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-11"],"title":"功率漂移","titleEn":"Track laser-power drift","objective":"完成「功率漂移」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for track laser-power drift, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：功率漂移。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track laser-power drift. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「功率漂移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track laser-power drift and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「功率漂移」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for track laser-power drift: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-12-k1","title":"功率漂移的原理","titleEn":"Track laser-power drift principle","text":"校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。","textEn":"Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions."},{"id":"a016-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「功率漂移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track laser-power drift?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}}]},{"id":"a016-stage03","order":3,"title":"局部反應","titleEn":"Localized response","description":"在「局部反應」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for localized response, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-12"],"title":"摻雜活化","titleEn":"Evaluate dopant activation","objective":"完成「摻雜活化」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for evaluate dopant activation, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜活化。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate dopant activation. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「摻雜活化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate dopant activation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜活化」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for evaluate dopant activation: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-13-k1","title":"摻雜活化的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate dopant activation principle","text":"短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。","textEn":"Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion."},{"id":"a016-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜活化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate dopant activation?","options":["短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-13"],"title":"接觸電阻改善","titleEn":"Assess contact-resistance change","objective":"完成「接觸電阻改善」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess contact-resistance change, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸電阻改善。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess contact-resistance change. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「接觸電阻改善」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess contact-resistance change and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸電阻改善」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess contact-resistance change: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸電阻改善的原理","titleEn":"Assess contact-resistance change principle","text":"總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。","textEn":"Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface."},{"id":"a016-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸電阻改善」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess contact-resistance change?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-14"],"title":"再結晶前緣","titleEn":"Trace recrystallization fronts","objective":"完成「再結晶前緣」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace recrystallization fronts, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：再結晶前緣。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace recrystallization fronts. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「再結晶前緣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace recrystallization fronts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「再結晶前緣」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace recrystallization fronts: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-15-k1","title":"再結晶前緣的原理","titleEn":"Trace recrystallization fronts principle","text":"結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。","textEn":"Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality."},{"id":"a016-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「再結晶前緣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace recrystallization fronts?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-15"],"title":"表面粗糙化","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening","objective":"完成「表面粗糙化」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect surface roughening, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面粗糙化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect surface roughening. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「表面粗糙化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect surface roughening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面粗糙化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect surface roughening: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-16-k1","title":"表面粗糙化的原理","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening principle","text":"電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。","textEn":"Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation."},{"id":"a016-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面粗糙化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect surface roughening?","options":["電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-16"],"title":"應力尖峰","titleEn":"Assess transient stress","objective":"完成「應力尖峰」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess transient stress, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力尖峰。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess transient stress. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「應力尖峰」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess transient stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力尖峰」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess transient stress: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-17-k1","title":"應力尖峰的原理","titleEn":"Assess transient stress principle","text":"局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。","textEn":"Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming."},{"id":"a016-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力尖峰」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess transient stress?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-17"],"title":"量測空間解析","titleEn":"Check spatial resolution","objective":"完成「量測空間解析」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for check spatial resolution, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：量測空間解析。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：量測光斑過大會平均掉掃描邊界異常。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check spatial resolution. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Large measurement spots can average out scan-boundary anomalies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「量測光斑過大會平均掉掃描邊界異常。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Large measurement spots can average out scan-boundary anomalies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「量測空間解析」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check spatial resolution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「量測空間解析」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for check spatial resolution: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-18-k1","title":"量測空間解析的原理","titleEn":"Check spatial resolution principle","text":"量測光斑過大會平均掉掃描邊界異常。","textEn":"Large measurement spots can average out scan-boundary anomalies."},{"id":"a016-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「量測空間解析」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check spatial resolution?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","量測光斑過大會平均掉掃描邊界異常。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Large measurement spots can average out scan-boundary anomalies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測光斑過大會平均掉掃描邊界異常。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Large measurement spots can average out scan-boundary anomalies. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}}]},{"id":"a016-stage04","order":4,"title":"圖案相容性","titleEn":"Pattern compatibility","description":"在「圖案相容性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for pattern compatibility, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-18"],"title":"金屬圖案吸收","titleEn":"Compare patterned absorption","objective":"完成「金屬圖案吸收」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare patterned absorption, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬圖案吸收。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：反射率差異使不同區塊接受不同熱負荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare patterned absorption. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Reflectivity variations give different blocks different thermal loads. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反射率差異使不同區塊接受不同熱負荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reflectivity variations give different blocks different thermal loads. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「金屬圖案吸收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare patterned absorption and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬圖案吸收」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare patterned absorption: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-19-k1","title":"金屬圖案吸收的原理","titleEn":"Compare patterned absorption principle","text":"反射率差異使不同區塊接受不同熱負荷。","textEn":"Reflectivity variations give different blocks different thermal loads."},{"id":"a016-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬圖案吸收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare patterned absorption?","options":["反射率差異使不同區塊接受不同熱負荷。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Reflectivity variations give different blocks different thermal loads.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反射率差異使不同區塊接受不同熱負荷。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Reflectivity variations give different blocks different thermal loads. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}},{"id":"a016-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-19"],"title":"圖案密度分組","titleEn":"Stratify pattern density","objective":"完成「圖案密度分組」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for stratify pattern density, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案密度分組。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：需分組比較圖案密度與溫度或電性偏移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Stratify pattern density. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Compare temperature or electrical shifts by pattern-density group. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需分組比較圖案密度與溫度或電性偏移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Compare temperature or electrical shifts by pattern-density group. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「圖案密度分組」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for stratify pattern density and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案密度分組」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for stratify pattern density: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-20-k1","title":"圖案密度分組的原理","titleEn":"Stratify pattern density principle","text":"需分組比較圖案密度與溫度或電性偏移。","textEn":"Compare temperature or electrical shifts by pattern-density group."},{"id":"a016-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案密度分組」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating stratify pattern density?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","需分組比較圖案密度與溫度或電性偏移。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Compare temperature or electrical shifts by pattern-density group.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"需分組比較圖案密度與溫度或電性偏移。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Compare temperature or electrical shifts by pattern-density group. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}},{"id":"a016-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-20"],"title":"多次通過","titleEn":"Assess repeated passes","objective":"完成「多次通過」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess repeated passes, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：多次通過。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：多次低能量不保證等同單次高能量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess repeated passes. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Several low-energy passes need not equal one high-energy pass. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多次低能量不保證等同單次高能量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Several low-energy passes need not equal one high-energy pass. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「多次通過」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess repeated passes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「多次通過」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess repeated passes: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-21-k1","title":"多次通過的原理","titleEn":"Assess repeated passes principle","text":"多次低能量不保證等同單次高能量。","textEn":"Several low-energy passes need not equal one high-energy pass."},{"id":"a016-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「多次通過」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess repeated passes?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","多次低能量不保證等同單次高能量。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Several low-energy passes need not equal one high-energy pass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多次低能量不保證等同單次高能量。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Several low-energy passes need not equal one high-energy pass. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}},{"id":"a016-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-21"],"title":"下層見證結構","titleEn":"Choose buried-layer witnesses","objective":"完成「下層見證結構」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for choose buried-layer witnesses, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：下層見證結構。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：只量表面活化無法證明下層未受損。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose buried-layer witnesses. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Surface activation alone cannot prove buried layers remain undamaged. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只量表面活化無法證明下層未受損。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface activation alone cannot prove buried layers remain undamaged. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「下層見證結構」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose buried-layer witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「下層見證結構」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for choose buried-layer witnesses: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-22-k1","title":"下層見證結構的原理","titleEn":"Choose buried-layer witnesses principle","text":"只量表面活化無法證明下層未受損。","textEn":"Surface activation alone cannot prove buried layers remain undamaged."},{"id":"a016-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「下層見證結構」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose buried-layer witnesses?","options":["只量表面活化無法證明下層未受損。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Surface activation alone cannot prove buried layers remain undamaged.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只量表面活化無法證明下層未受損。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Surface activation alone cannot prove buried layers remain undamaged. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}},{"id":"a016-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-22"],"title":"失效區回溯","titleEn":"Trace failed scan regions","objective":"完成「失效區回溯」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace failed scan regions, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：失效區回溯。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：缺陷圖需轉到掃描時間與光斑座標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace failed scan regions. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Defect maps should be registered to scan time and beam coordinates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「缺陷圖需轉到掃描時間與光斑座標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Defect maps should be registered to scan time and beam coordinates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「失效區回溯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace failed scan regions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「失效區回溯」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace failed scan regions: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-23-k1","title":"失效區回溯的原理","titleEn":"Trace failed scan regions principle","text":"缺陷圖需轉到掃描時間與光斑座標。","textEn":"Defect maps should be registered to scan time and beam coordinates."},{"id":"a016-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「失效區回溯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace failed scan regions?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","缺陷圖需轉到掃描時間與光斑座標。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Defect maps should be registered to scan time and beam coordinates.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷圖需轉到掃描時間與光斑座標。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Defect maps should be registered to scan time and beam coordinates. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}},{"id":"a016-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-23"],"title":"雷射退火審查","titleEn":"Review laser-anneal evidence","objective":"完成「雷射退火審查」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review laser-anneal evidence, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：雷射退火審查。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活化收益需與熱峰值、均勻性及下層相容性一起評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review laser-anneal evidence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Assess activation gain with thermal peaks, uniformity and buried-layer compatibility. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化收益需與熱峰值、均勻性及下層相容性一起評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Assess activation gain with thermal peaks, uniformity and buried-layer compatibility. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「雷射退火審查」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review laser-anneal evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「雷射退火審查」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review laser-anneal evidence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-24-k1","title":"雷射退火審查的原理","titleEn":"Review laser-anneal evidence principle","text":"活化收益需與熱峰值、均勻性及下層相容性一起評估。","textEn":"Assess activation gain with thermal peaks, uniformity and buried-layer compatibility."},{"id":"a016-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","textEn":"Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「雷射退火審查」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review laser-anneal evidence?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","活化收益需與熱峰值、均勻性及下層相容性一起評估。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Assess activation gain with thermal peaks, uniformity and buried-layer compatibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活化收益需與熱峰值、均勻性及下層相容性一起評估。 金屬與介電圖案的反射及吸收不同，代表性驗證應包含圖案晶圓而非僅有裸矽校準片。","explanationEn":"Assess activation gain with thermal peaks, uniformity and buried-layer compatibility. Metal and dielectric patterns differ optically, so representative validation needs patterned wafers beyond bare-silicon calibration."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a017","title":"擴散爐均勻性控制","titleEn":"Diffusion-furnace uniformity control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["爐管與邊界","熱場與傳輸","擴散輪廓","均勻性驗收"],"labelsEn":["Furnace and boundaries","Thermal field and transport","Diffusion profiles","Uniformity acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a017-stage01","order":1,"title":"爐管與邊界","titleEn":"Furnace and boundaries","description":"在「爐管與邊界」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for furnace and boundaries, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a017-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"批次位置圖","titleEn":"Map batch positions","objective":"完成「批次位置圖」的因果圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map batch positions, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：批次位置圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：前中後片位是不同的熱與流體採樣位置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map batch positions. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Front, middle and rear slots sample different thermal and flow conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前中後片位是不同的熱與流體採樣位置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Front, middle and rear slots sample different thermal and flow conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「批次位置圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map batch positions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「批次位置圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map batch positions: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-01-k1","title":"批次位置圖的原理","titleEn":"Map batch positions principle","text":"前中後片位是不同的熱與流體採樣位置。","textEn":"Front, middle and rear slots sample different thermal and flow conditions."},{"id":"a017-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「批次位置圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map batch positions?","options":["前中後片位是不同的熱與流體採樣位置。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Front, middle and rear slots sample different thermal and flow conditions.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"前中後片位是不同的熱與流體採樣位置。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Front, middle and rear slots sample different thermal and flow conditions. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}},{"id":"a017-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-01"],"title":"晶舟載量","titleEn":"Specify boat loading","objective":"完成「晶舟載量」的對照表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for specify boat loading, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶舟載量。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：裝片數量及間距改變熱容量與流場。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Specify boat loading. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Wafer count and spacing change thermal mass and flow. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「裝片數量及間距改變熱容量與流場。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wafer count and spacing change thermal mass and flow. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「晶舟載量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for specify boat loading and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶舟載量」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for specify boat loading: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-02-k1","title":"晶舟載量的原理","titleEn":"Specify boat loading principle","text":"裝片數量及間距改變熱容量與流場。","textEn":"Wafer count and spacing change thermal mass and flow."},{"id":"a017-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶舟載量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating specify boat loading?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","裝片數量及間距改變熱容量與流場。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Wafer count and spacing change thermal mass and flow.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"裝片數量及間距改變熱容量與流場。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Wafer count and spacing change thermal mass and flow. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}},{"id":"a017-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-02"],"title":"爐溫與片溫","titleEn":"Separate furnace and wafer temperature","objective":"完成「爐溫與片溫」的敏感度草圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate furnace and wafer temperature, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：爐溫與片溫。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：爐壁設定值不能直接當作晶圓瞬時溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate furnace and wafer temperature. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Wall setpoint is not instantaneous wafer temperature. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「爐壁設定值不能直接當作晶圓瞬時溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wall setpoint is not instantaneous wafer temperature. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「爐溫與片溫」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate furnace and wafer temperature and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「爐溫與片溫」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate furnace and wafer temperature: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-03-k1","title":"爐溫與片溫的原理","titleEn":"Separate furnace and wafer temperature principle","text":"爐壁設定值不能直接當作晶圓瞬時溫度。","textEn":"Wall setpoint is not instantaneous wafer temperature."},{"id":"a017-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「爐溫與片溫」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate furnace and wafer temperature?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","爐壁設定值不能直接當作晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Wall setpoint is not instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"爐壁設定值不能直接當作晶圓瞬時溫度。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Wall setpoint is not instantaneous wafer temperature. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}},{"id":"a017-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-03"],"title":"固定源與有限源","titleEn":"Separate constant and finite sources","objective":"完成「固定源與有限源」的故障判別表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate constant and finite sources, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：固定源與有限源。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：邊界供應條件決定擴散解的形式。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate constant and finite sources. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Source boundary conditions determine the diffusion solution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊界供應條件決定擴散解的形式。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source boundary conditions determine the diffusion solution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「固定源與有限源」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate constant and finite sources and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「固定源與有限源」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate constant and finite sources: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-04-k1","title":"固定源與有限源的原理","titleEn":"Separate constant and finite sources principle","text":"邊界供應條件決定擴散解的形式。","textEn":"Source boundary conditions determine the diffusion solution."},{"id":"a017-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「固定源與有限源」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate constant and finite sources?","options":["邊界供應條件決定擴散解的形式。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Source boundary conditions determine the diffusion solution.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊界供應條件決定擴散解的形式。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Source boundary conditions determine the diffusion solution. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}},{"id":"a017-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-04"],"title":"濃度守恆","titleEn":"Check concentration conservation","objective":"完成「濃度守恆」的量測規劃，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for check concentration conservation, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濃度守恆。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：有限劑量擴散應保持總量，除非另有損失通量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check concentration conservation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Finite-dose diffusion conserves total dose unless a loss flux is specified. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「有限劑量擴散應保持總量，除非另有損失通量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Finite-dose diffusion conserves total dose unless a loss flux is specified. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「濃度守恆」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check concentration conservation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濃度守恆」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for check concentration conservation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-05-k1","title":"濃度守恆的原理","titleEn":"Check concentration conservation principle","text":"有限劑量擴散應保持總量，除非另有損失通量。","textEn":"Finite-dose diffusion conserves total dose unless a loss flux is specified."},{"id":"a017-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濃度守恆」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check concentration conservation?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","有限劑量擴散應保持總量，除非另有損失通量。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Finite-dose diffusion conserves total dose unless a loss flux is specified.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有限劑量擴散應保持總量，除非另有損失通量。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Finite-dose diffusion conserves total dose unless a loss flux is specified. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}},{"id":"a017-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-05"],"title":"熱預算累計","titleEn":"Accumulate diffusion budgets","objective":"完成「熱預算累計」的工程驗收單，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accumulate diffusion budgets, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算累計。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：非恆溫歷程需積分溫度相關擴散係數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accumulate diffusion budgets. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nonisothermal histories require integrating temperature-dependent diffusivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「非恆溫歷程需積分溫度相關擴散係數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nonisothermal histories require integrating temperature-dependent diffusivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱預算累計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accumulate diffusion budgets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算累計」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accumulate diffusion budgets: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-06-k1","title":"熱預算累計的原理","titleEn":"Accumulate diffusion budgets principle","text":"非恆溫歷程需積分溫度相關擴散係數。","textEn":"Nonisothermal histories require integrating temperature-dependent diffusivity."},{"id":"a017-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","textEn":"Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算累計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accumulate diffusion budgets?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","非恆溫歷程需積分溫度相關擴散係數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Nonisothermal histories require integrating temperature-dependent diffusivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"非恆溫歷程需積分溫度相關擴散係數。 有限源保持總劑量，固定表面源持續補充摻雜；兩種擴散模型採用不同守恆及邊界條件。","explanationEn":"Nonisothermal histories require integrating temperature-dependent diffusivity. Finite sources conserve dose while fixed-surface sources replenish dopants; the models have different conservation and boundary conditions."}}]},{"id":"a017-stage02","order":2,"title":"熱場與傳輸","titleEn":"Thermal field and transport","description":"在「熱場與傳輸」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for thermal field and transport, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a017-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-06"],"title":"加熱區校準","titleEn":"Calibrate heating zones","objective":"完成「加熱區校準」的因果圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for calibrate heating zones, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：加熱區校準。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：各區控制需要考慮相鄰區熱耦合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calibrate heating zones. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Zone control requires adjacent-zone thermal coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「各區控制需要考慮相鄰區熱耦合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Zone control requires adjacent-zone thermal coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「加熱區校準」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calibrate heating zones and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「加熱區校準」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for calibrate heating zones: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-07-k1","title":"加熱區校準的原理","titleEn":"Calibrate heating zones principle","text":"各區控制需要考慮相鄰區熱耦合。","textEn":"Zone control requires adjacent-zone thermal coupling."},{"id":"a017-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「加熱區校準」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calibrate heating zones?","options":["各區控制需要考慮相鄰區熱耦合。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Zone control requires adjacent-zone thermal coupling.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"各區控制需要考慮相鄰區熱耦合。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Zone control requires adjacent-zone thermal coupling. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}},{"id":"a017-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-07"],"title":"端部熱損","titleEn":"Assess end losses","objective":"完成「端部熱損」的對照表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess end losses, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：端部熱損。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：爐管入口出口常與中心區有不同熱邊界。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess end losses. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Tube ends often have different thermal boundaries from the center. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「爐管入口出口常與中心區有不同熱邊界。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Tube ends often have different thermal boundaries from the center. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「端部熱損」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess end losses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「端部熱損」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess end losses: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-08-k1","title":"端部熱損的原理","titleEn":"Assess end losses principle","text":"爐管入口出口常與中心區有不同熱邊界。","textEn":"Tube ends often have different thermal boundaries from the center."},{"id":"a017-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「端部熱損」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess end losses?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐管入口出口常與中心區有不同熱邊界。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Tube ends often have different thermal boundaries from the center.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"爐管入口出口常與中心區有不同熱邊界。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Tube ends often have different thermal boundaries from the center. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}},{"id":"a017-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-08"],"title":"氣體耗盡","titleEn":"Track gas depletion","objective":"完成「氣體耗盡」的敏感度草圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for track gas depletion, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣體耗盡。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：反應物沿爐長的消耗可造成片位差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track gas depletion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Reactant consumption along the furnace can cause slot dependence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應物沿爐長的消耗可造成片位差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reactant consumption along the furnace can cause slot dependence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「氣體耗盡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track gas depletion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣體耗盡」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for track gas depletion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-09-k1","title":"氣體耗盡的原理","titleEn":"Track gas depletion principle","text":"反應物沿爐長的消耗可造成片位差。","textEn":"Reactant consumption along the furnace can cause slot dependence."},{"id":"a017-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣體耗盡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track gas depletion?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","反應物沿爐長的消耗可造成片位差。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Reactant consumption along the furnace can cause slot dependence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應物沿爐長的消耗可造成片位差。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Reactant consumption along the furnace can cause slot dependence. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}},{"id":"a017-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-09"],"title":"載入暫態","titleEn":"Model loading transients","objective":"完成「載入暫態」的故障判別表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for model loading transients, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：載入暫態。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：載入冷晶舟會暫時擾動穩態熱場。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model loading transients. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Loading a cold boat temporarily disturbs a steady thermal field. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「載入冷晶舟會暫時擾動穩態熱場。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Loading a cold boat temporarily disturbs a steady thermal field. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「載入暫態」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model loading transients and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「載入暫態」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for model loading transients: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-10-k1","title":"載入暫態的原理","titleEn":"Model loading transients principle","text":"載入冷晶舟會暫時擾動穩態熱場。","textEn":"Loading a cold boat temporarily disturbs a steady thermal field."},{"id":"a017-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「載入暫態」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model loading transients?","options":["載入冷晶舟會暫時擾動穩態熱場。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Loading a cold boat temporarily disturbs a steady thermal field.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"載入冷晶舟會暫時擾動穩態熱場。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Loading a cold boat temporarily disturbs a steady thermal field. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}},{"id":"a017-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-10"],"title":"升降溫對稱性","titleEn":"Compare heating and cooling","objective":"完成「升降溫對稱性」的量測規劃，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare heating and cooling, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：升降溫對稱性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：升溫與降溫的熱傳條件不必對稱。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare heating and cooling. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Heating and cooling heat-transfer conditions need not be symmetric. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「升溫與降溫的熱傳條件不必對稱。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Heating and cooling heat-transfer conditions need not be symmetric. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「升降溫對稱性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare heating and cooling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「升降溫對稱性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare heating and cooling: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-11-k1","title":"升降溫對稱性的原理","titleEn":"Compare heating and cooling principle","text":"升溫與降溫的熱傳條件不必對稱。","textEn":"Heating and cooling heat-transfer conditions need not be symmetric."},{"id":"a017-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「升降溫對稱性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare heating and cooling?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","升溫與降溫的熱傳條件不必對稱。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Heating and cooling heat-transfer conditions need not be symmetric.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"升溫與降溫的熱傳條件不必對稱。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Heating and cooling heat-transfer conditions need not be symmetric. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}},{"id":"a017-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-11"],"title":"空載與滿載","titleEn":"Compare empty and full loads","objective":"完成「空載與滿載」的工程驗收單，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare empty and full loads, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：空載與滿載。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：空載均溫不能代替滿載產品驗證。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare empty and full loads. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity cannot replace loaded validation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「空載均溫不能代替滿載產品驗證。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Empty-furnace uniformity cannot replace loaded validation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「空載與滿載」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare empty and full loads and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「空載與滿載」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare empty and full loads: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-12-k1","title":"空載與滿載的原理","titleEn":"Compare empty and full loads principle","text":"空載均溫不能代替滿載產品驗證。","textEn":"Empty-furnace uniformity cannot replace loaded validation."},{"id":"a017-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","textEn":"Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「空載與滿載」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare empty and full loads?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","空載均溫不能代替滿載產品驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Empty-furnace uniformity cannot replace loaded validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"空載均溫不能代替滿載產品驗證。 晶舟和晶圓增加熱容量，也改變氣流與熱輻射遮蔽，因此空爐校準須經負載條件驗證。","explanationEn":"Empty-furnace uniformity cannot replace loaded validation. Boats and wafers add thermal mass and change flow and radiation shielding; empty-furnace calibration needs loaded verification."}}]},{"id":"a017-stage03","order":3,"title":"擴散輪廓","titleEn":"Diffusion profiles","description":"在「擴散輪廓」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for diffusion profiles, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a017-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-12"],"title":"Fick 通量方向","titleEn":"Draw Fickian flux","objective":"完成「Fick 通量方向」的因果圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw fickian flux, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：Fick 通量方向。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：擴散通量由濃度梯度而不是濃度本身決定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw Fickian flux. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Diffusion flux depends on concentration gradient rather than concentration alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「擴散通量由濃度梯度而不是濃度本身決定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Diffusion flux depends on concentration gradient rather than concentration alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「Fick 通量方向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw fickian flux and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「Fick 通量方向」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw fickian flux: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-13-k1","title":"Fick 通量方向的原理","titleEn":"Draw Fickian flux principle","text":"擴散通量由濃度梯度而不是濃度本身決定。","textEn":"Diffusion flux depends on concentration gradient rather than concentration alone."},{"id":"a017-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「Fick 通量方向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw fickian flux?","options":["擴散通量由濃度梯度而不是濃度本身決定。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion flux depends on concentration gradient rather than concentration alone.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"擴散通量由濃度梯度而不是濃度本身決定。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"Diffusion flux depends on concentration gradient rather than concentration alone. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}},{"id":"a017-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-13"],"title":"高斯有限源","titleEn":"Model a finite-source Gaussian","objective":"完成「高斯有限源」的對照表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for model a finite-source gaussian, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：高斯有限源。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：輪廓展寬時峰值降低以維持總劑量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂有限源擴散：總劑量固定時，將高斯標準差加倍；推導峰值應如何變化，並用積分面積檢查。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model a finite-source Gaussian. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A finite-source profile broadens while its peak falls to conserve dose. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical finite-source diffusion: double Gaussian standard deviation at fixed total dose. Derive the peak change and verify by integrated area.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「輪廓展寬時峰值降低以維持總劑量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A finite-source profile broadens while its peak falls to conserve dose. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「高斯有限源」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model a finite-source gaussian and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「高斯有限源」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for model a finite-source gaussian: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-14-k1","title":"高斯有限源的原理","titleEn":"Model a finite-source Gaussian principle","text":"輪廓展寬時峰值降低以維持總劑量。","textEn":"A finite-source profile broadens while its peak falls to conserve dose."},{"id":"a017-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「高斯有限源」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model a finite-source gaussian?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","輪廓展寬時峰值降低以維持總劑量。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","A finite-source profile broadens while its peak falls to conserve dose.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輪廓展寬時峰值降低以維持總劑量。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"A finite-source profile broadens while its peak falls to conserve dose. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}},{"id":"a017-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-14"],"title":"互補誤差函數","titleEn":"Model constant-surface diffusion","objective":"完成「互補誤差函數」的敏感度草圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for model constant-surface diffusion, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：互補誤差函數。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：維持表面濃度需要持續供應摻雜原子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model constant-surface diffusion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Constant surface concentration requires continued dopant supply. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「維持表面濃度需要持續供應摻雜原子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Constant surface concentration requires continued dopant supply. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「互補誤差函數」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model constant-surface diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「互補誤差函數」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for model constant-surface diffusion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-15-k1","title":"互補誤差函數的原理","titleEn":"Model constant-surface diffusion principle","text":"維持表面濃度需要持續供應摻雜原子。","textEn":"Constant surface concentration requires continued dopant supply."},{"id":"a017-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「互補誤差函數」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model constant-surface diffusion?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","維持表面濃度需要持續供應摻雜原子。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Constant surface concentration requires continued dopant supply."],"answer":2,"explanation":"維持表面濃度需要持續供應摻雜原子。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"Constant surface concentration requires continued dopant supply. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}},{"id":"a017-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-15"],"title":"接面交點","titleEn":"Locate the junction intersection","objective":"完成「接面交點」的故障判別表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for locate the junction intersection, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面交點。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：接面深度需與基底背景濃度一起決定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate the junction intersection. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Junction depth is determined with the background doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接面深度需與基底背景濃度一起決定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Junction depth is determined with the background doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「接面交點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate the junction intersection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面交點」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for locate the junction intersection: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-16-k1","title":"接面交點的原理","titleEn":"Locate the junction intersection principle","text":"接面深度需與基底背景濃度一起決定。","textEn":"Junction depth is determined with the background doping."},{"id":"a017-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面交點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate the junction intersection?","options":["接面深度需與基底背景濃度一起決定。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Junction depth is determined with the background doping.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接面深度需與基底背景濃度一起決定。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"Junction depth is determined with the background doping. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}},{"id":"a017-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-16"],"title":"濃度依賴擴散","titleEn":"Identify concentration dependence","objective":"完成「濃度依賴擴散」的量測規劃，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for identify concentration dependence, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濃度依賴擴散。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：高摻雜時常數擴散係數可能失去適用性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify concentration dependence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Constant diffusivity can fail at high doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高摻雜時常數擴散係數可能失去適用性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Constant diffusivity can fail at high doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「濃度依賴擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify concentration dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濃度依賴擴散」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for identify concentration dependence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-17-k1","title":"濃度依賴擴散的原理","titleEn":"Identify concentration dependence principle","text":"高摻雜時常數擴散係數可能失去適用性。","textEn":"Constant diffusivity can fail at high doping."},{"id":"a017-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濃度依賴擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify concentration dependence?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","高摻雜時常數擴散係數可能失去適用性。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Constant diffusivity can fail at high doping.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高摻雜時常數擴散係數可能失去適用性。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"Constant diffusivity can fail at high doping. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}},{"id":"a017-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-17"],"title":"缺陷促進擴散","titleEn":"Assess defect-assisted diffusion","objective":"完成「缺陷促進擴散」的工程驗收單，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess defect-assisted diffusion, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺陷促進擴散。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：點缺陷前史會改變有效擴散行為。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess defect-assisted diffusion. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Point-defect history changes effective diffusion behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「點缺陷前史會改變有效擴散行為。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Point-defect history changes effective diffusion behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「缺陷促進擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess defect-assisted diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺陷促進擴散」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess defect-assisted diffusion: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-18-k1","title":"缺陷促進擴散的原理","titleEn":"Assess defect-assisted diffusion principle","text":"點缺陷前史會改變有效擴散行為。","textEn":"Point-defect history changes effective diffusion behavior."},{"id":"a017-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","textEn":"Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺陷促進擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess defect-assisted diffusion?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","點缺陷前史會改變有效擴散行為。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Point-defect history changes effective diffusion behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"點缺陷前史會改變有效擴散行為。 Fick 模型的通量取決於梯度，均勻高濃度區可有低通量，而低濃度但陡梯度區可有顯著通量。","explanationEn":"Point-defect history changes effective diffusion behavior. Fickian flux follows gradients: uniform high concentration can have little flux while a low but steep profile can have substantial flux."}}]},{"id":"a017-stage04","order":4,"title":"均勻性驗收","titleEn":"Uniformity acceptance","description":"在「均勻性驗收」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for uniformity acceptance, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a017-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-18"],"title":"徑向與軸向圖","titleEn":"Separate radial and axial maps","objective":"完成「徑向與軸向圖」的因果圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate radial and axial maps, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：徑向與軸向圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：片內徑向變異與片間軸向變異應分開報告。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate radial and axial maps. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Report within-wafer radial and slot-to-slot axial variation separately. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片內徑向變異與片間軸向變異應分開報告。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report within-wafer radial and slot-to-slot axial variation separately. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「徑向與軸向圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate radial and axial maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「徑向與軸向圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate radial and axial maps: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-19-k1","title":"徑向與軸向圖的原理","titleEn":"Separate radial and axial maps principle","text":"片內徑向變異與片間軸向變異應分開報告。","textEn":"Report within-wafer radial and slot-to-slot axial variation separately."},{"id":"a017-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「徑向與軸向圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate radial and axial maps?","options":["片內徑向變異與片間軸向變異應分開報告。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Report within-wafer radial and slot-to-slot axial variation separately.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"片內徑向變異與片間軸向變異應分開報告。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Report within-wafer radial and slot-to-slot axial variation separately. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}},{"id":"a017-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-19"],"title":"片電阻映射","titleEn":"Map sheet resistance","objective":"完成「片電阻映射」的對照表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for map sheet resistance, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片電阻映射。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：同一電阻結果可能來自不同濃度輪廓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map sheet resistance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal resistance can arise from different concentration profiles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「同一電阻結果可能來自不同濃度輪廓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal resistance can arise from different concentration profiles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「片電阻映射」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map sheet resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片電阻映射」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for map sheet resistance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-20-k1","title":"片電阻映射的原理","titleEn":"Map sheet resistance principle","text":"同一電阻結果可能來自不同濃度輪廓。","textEn":"Equal resistance can arise from different concentration profiles."},{"id":"a017-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片電阻映射」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map sheet resistance?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","同一電阻結果可能來自不同濃度輪廓。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal resistance can arise from different concentration profiles.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一電阻結果可能來自不同濃度輪廓。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Equal resistance can arise from different concentration profiles. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}},{"id":"a017-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-20"],"title":"校準熱電偶","titleEn":"Assess thermocouple calibration","objective":"完成「校準熱電偶」的敏感度草圖，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess thermocouple calibration, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：校準熱電偶。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：感測器漂移可能被誤判為製程漂移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermocouple calibration. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Sensor drift can be mistaken for process drift. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「感測器漂移可能被誤判為製程漂移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sensor drift can be mistaken for process drift. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「校準熱電偶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermocouple calibration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「校準熱電偶」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess thermocouple calibration: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-21-k1","title":"校準熱電偶的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermocouple calibration principle","text":"感測器漂移可能被誤判為製程漂移。","textEn":"Sensor drift can be mistaken for process drift."},{"id":"a017-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「校準熱電偶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermocouple calibration?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","感測器漂移可能被誤判為製程漂移。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Sensor drift can be mistaken for process drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"感測器漂移可能被誤判為製程漂移。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Sensor drift can be mistaken for process drift. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}},{"id":"a017-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-21"],"title":"設備清潔週期","titleEn":"Assess maintenance cycles","objective":"完成「設備清潔週期」的故障判別表，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess maintenance cycles, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：設備清潔週期。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：管壁沉積狀態可能影響批次間重現性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess maintenance cycles. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Tube-wall deposits can affect run-to-run repeatability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「管壁沉積狀態可能影響批次間重現性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Tube-wall deposits can affect run-to-run repeatability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「設備清潔週期」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess maintenance cycles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「設備清潔週期」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess maintenance cycles: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-22-k1","title":"設備清潔週期的原理","titleEn":"Assess maintenance cycles principle","text":"管壁沉積狀態可能影響批次間重現性。","textEn":"Tube-wall deposits can affect run-to-run repeatability."},{"id":"a017-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「設備清潔週期」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess maintenance cycles?","options":["管壁沉積狀態可能影響批次間重現性。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Tube-wall deposits can affect run-to-run repeatability.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"管壁沉積狀態可能影響批次間重現性。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Tube-wall deposits can affect run-to-run repeatability. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}},{"id":"a017-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-22"],"title":"最差片位","titleEn":"Select worst-case slots","objective":"完成「最差片位」的量測規劃，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for select worst-case slots, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：最差片位。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：中心片合格不代表端部片位合格。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Select worst-case slots. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Center-wafer acceptance does not prove end-slot acceptance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中心片合格不代表端部片位合格。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Center-wafer acceptance does not prove end-slot acceptance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「最差片位」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for select worst-case slots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「最差片位」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for select worst-case slots: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-23-k1","title":"最差片位的原理","titleEn":"Select worst-case slots principle","text":"中心片合格不代表端部片位合格。","textEn":"Center-wafer acceptance does not prove end-slot acceptance."},{"id":"a017-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「最差片位」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating select worst-case slots?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","中心片合格不代表端部片位合格。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Center-wafer acceptance does not prove end-slot acceptance.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"中心片合格不代表端部片位合格。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Center-wafer acceptance does not prove end-slot acceptance. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}},{"id":"a017-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a017-v8-23"],"title":"批次擴散驗收","titleEn":"Accept batch diffusion","objective":"完成「批次擴散驗收」的工程驗收單，把片位熱場、邊界條件、擴散輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept batch diffusion, connecting relevant limits in slot thermal fields, boundary conditions and diffusion profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：批次擴散驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：熱場、濃度輪廓、位置差異及量測校準需一併審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept batch diffusion. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review thermal field, profiles, position effects and calibration together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱場、濃度輪廓、位置差異及量測校準需一併審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review thermal field, profiles, position effects and calibration together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「批次擴散驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept batch diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「批次擴散驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept batch diffusion: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a017-v8-24-k1","title":"批次擴散驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept batch diffusion principle","text":"熱場、濃度輪廓、位置差異及量測校準需一併審查。","textEn":"Review thermal field, profiles, position effects and calibration together."},{"id":"a017-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","textEn":"Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「批次擴散驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept batch diffusion?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","熱場、濃度輪廓、位置差異及量測校準需一併審查。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Review thermal field, profiles, position effects and calibration together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱場、濃度輪廓、位置差異及量測校準需一併審查。 爐管軸向變異與片內徑向變異對應不同邊界，將兩者混成單一標準差可能遮蔽故障來源。","explanationEn":"Review thermal field, profiles, position effects and calibration together. Axial furnace and radial wafer variation reflect different boundaries; merging them into one deviation can hide fault causes."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a018","title":"淺溝槽隔離製作","titleEn":"Shallow-trench isolation fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore trench fill, isolation leakage and stress through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["隔離幾何","溝槽與襯層","填充與平坦化","漏電與應力"],"labelsEn":["Isolation geometry","Trench and liner","Fill and planarization","Leakage and stress"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a018-stage01","order":1,"title":"隔離幾何","titleEn":"Isolation geometry","description":"在「隔離幾何」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for isolation geometry, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a018-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"主動區邊界","titleEn":"Draw active-area boundaries","objective":"完成「主動區邊界」的因果圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw active-area boundaries, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：主動區邊界。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：隔離區定義元件間電性邊界而非閘長。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw active-area boundaries. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Isolation defines electrical boundaries between devices, not gate length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離區定義元件間電性邊界而非閘長。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation defines electrical boundaries between devices, not gate length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「主動區邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw active-area boundaries and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「主動區邊界」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw active-area boundaries: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-01-k1","title":"主動區邊界的原理","titleEn":"Draw active-area boundaries principle","text":"隔離區定義元件間電性邊界而非閘長。","textEn":"Isolation defines electrical boundaries between devices, not gate length."},{"id":"a018-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「主動區邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw active-area boundaries?","options":["隔離區定義元件間電性邊界而非閘長。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Isolation defines electrical boundaries between devices, not gate length.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隔離區定義元件間電性邊界而非閘長。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Isolation defines electrical boundaries between devices, not gate length. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}},{"id":"a018-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-01"],"title":"溝槽深度預算","titleEn":"Budget trench depth","objective":"完成「溝槽深度預算」的對照表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for budget trench depth, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溝槽深度預算。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：隔離深度需與接面及漏電路徑一起評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget trench depth. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Isolation depth must be assessed against junctions and leakage paths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離深度需與接面及漏電路徑一起評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation depth must be assessed against junctions and leakage paths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「溝槽深度預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget trench depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溝槽深度預算」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for budget trench depth: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-02-k1","title":"溝槽深度預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget trench depth principle","text":"隔離深度需與接面及漏電路徑一起評估。","textEn":"Isolation depth must be assessed against junctions and leakage paths."},{"id":"a018-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溝槽深度預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget trench depth?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","隔離深度需與接面及漏電路徑一起評估。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Isolation depth must be assessed against junctions and leakage paths.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離深度需與接面及漏電路徑一起評估。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Isolation depth must be assessed against junctions and leakage paths. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}},{"id":"a018-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-02"],"title":"硬遮罩分工","titleEn":"Assign hard-mask functions","objective":"完成「硬遮罩分工」的敏感度草圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assign hard-mask functions, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：硬遮罩分工。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：遮罩要兼顧蝕刻保護及後續平坦化停止。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign hard-mask functions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Masks may provide both etch protection and a planarization stop. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「遮罩要兼顧蝕刻保護及後續平坦化停止。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Masks may provide both etch protection and a planarization stop. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「硬遮罩分工」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign hard-mask functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「硬遮罩分工」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assign hard-mask functions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-03-k1","title":"硬遮罩分工的原理","titleEn":"Assign hard-mask functions principle","text":"遮罩要兼顧蝕刻保護及後續平坦化停止。","textEn":"Masks may provide both etch protection and a planarization stop."},{"id":"a018-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「硬遮罩分工」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign hard-mask functions?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","遮罩要兼顧蝕刻保護及後續平坦化停止。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Masks may provide both etch protection and a planarization stop."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩要兼顧蝕刻保護及後續平坦化停止。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Masks may provide both etch protection and a planarization stop. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}},{"id":"a018-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-03"],"title":"襯墊氧化層","titleEn":"Assess pad oxide","objective":"完成「襯墊氧化層」的故障判別表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess pad oxide, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：襯墊氧化層。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：襯墊層可改變應力傳遞與移除選擇性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pad oxide. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Pad layers alter stress transfer and removal selectivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「襯墊層可改變應力傳遞與移除選擇性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pad layers alter stress transfer and removal selectivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「襯墊氧化層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pad oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「襯墊氧化層」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess pad oxide: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-04-k1","title":"襯墊氧化層的原理","titleEn":"Assess pad oxide principle","text":"襯墊層可改變應力傳遞與移除選擇性。","textEn":"Pad layers alter stress transfer and removal selectivity."},{"id":"a018-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「襯墊氧化層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pad oxide?","options":["襯墊層可改變應力傳遞與移除選擇性。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Pad layers alter stress transfer and removal selectivity.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"襯墊層可改變應力傳遞與移除選擇性。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Pad layers alter stress transfer and removal selectivity. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}},{"id":"a018-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-04"],"title":"圖案密度","titleEn":"Compare pattern density","objective":"完成「圖案密度」的量測規劃，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare pattern density, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案密度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：稀疏與密集區可能有不同蝕刻及填充負載。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare pattern density. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sparse and dense regions can have different etch and fill loading. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「稀疏與密集區可能有不同蝕刻及填充負載。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sparse and dense regions can have different etch and fill loading. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「圖案密度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare pattern density and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案密度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare pattern density: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-05-k1","title":"圖案密度的原理","titleEn":"Compare pattern density principle","text":"稀疏與密集區可能有不同蝕刻及填充負載。","textEn":"Sparse and dense regions can have different etch and fill loading."},{"id":"a018-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案密度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare pattern density?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","稀疏與密集區可能有不同蝕刻及填充負載。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Sparse and dense regions can have different etch and fill loading.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀疏與密集區可能有不同蝕刻及填充負載。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Sparse and dense regions can have different etch and fill loading. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}},{"id":"a018-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-05"],"title":"邊角電場","titleEn":"Locate corner fields","objective":"完成「邊角電場」的工程驗收單，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate corner fields, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊角電場。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：尖角可能集中電場而增加局部漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate corner fields. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Sharp corners can concentrate fields and increase local leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「尖角可能集中電場而增加局部漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sharp corners can concentrate fields and increase local leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「邊角電場」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate corner fields and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊角電場」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate corner fields: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-06-k1","title":"邊角電場的原理","titleEn":"Locate corner fields principle","text":"尖角可能集中電場而增加局部漏電。","textEn":"Sharp corners can concentrate fields and increase local leakage."},{"id":"a018-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","textEn":"Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊角電場」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate corner fields?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","尖角可能集中電場而增加局部漏電。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Sharp corners can concentrate fields and increase local leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尖角可能集中電場而增加局部漏電。 隔離必須在截面上切斷非預期導通路徑，溝槽名稱或深度單一數值無法完整描述電性隔離。","explanationEn":"Sharp corners can concentrate fields and increase local leakage. Isolation must interrupt unintended conduction paths in section; a trench label or single depth cannot fully describe it."}}]},{"id":"a018-stage02","order":2,"title":"溝槽與襯層","titleEn":"Trench and liner","description":"在「溝槽與襯層」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for trench and liner, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a018-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-06"],"title":"溝槽側壁角","titleEn":"Measure trench sidewall angle","objective":"完成「溝槽側壁角」的因果圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for measure trench sidewall angle, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溝槽側壁角。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：側壁形狀會改變入口封閉與填充風險。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure trench sidewall angle. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Sidewall shape changes opening closure and fill risk. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「側壁形狀會改變入口封閉與填充風險。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sidewall shape changes opening closure and fill risk. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「溝槽側壁角」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure trench sidewall angle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溝槽側壁角」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for measure trench sidewall angle: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-07-k1","title":"溝槽側壁角的原理","titleEn":"Measure trench sidewall angle principle","text":"側壁形狀會改變入口封閉與填充風險。","textEn":"Sidewall shape changes opening closure and fill risk."},{"id":"a018-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溝槽側壁角」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure trench sidewall angle?","options":["側壁形狀會改變入口封閉與填充風險。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall shape changes opening closure and fill risk.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"側壁形狀會改變入口封閉與填充風險。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Sidewall shape changes opening closure and fill risk. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}},{"id":"a018-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-07"],"title":"底部殘留","titleEn":"Inspect trench-bottom residue","objective":"完成「底部殘留」的對照表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect trench-bottom residue, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部殘留。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：殘留物可能阻礙襯層與填充界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect trench-bottom residue. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Residues can compromise liner and fill interfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「殘留物可能阻礙襯層與填充界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residues can compromise liner and fill interfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「底部殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect trench-bottom residue and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部殘留」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect trench-bottom residue: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-08-k1","title":"底部殘留的原理","titleEn":"Inspect trench-bottom residue principle","text":"殘留物可能阻礙襯層與填充界面。","textEn":"Residues can compromise liner and fill interfaces."},{"id":"a018-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect trench-bottom residue?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","殘留物可能阻礙襯層與填充界面。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Residues can compromise liner and fill interfaces.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘留物可能阻礙襯層與填充界面。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Residues can compromise liner and fill interfaces. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}},{"id":"a018-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-08"],"title":"蝕刻損傷","titleEn":"Assess etch damage","objective":"完成「蝕刻損傷」的敏感度草圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess etch damage, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：蝕刻損傷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：幾何正確仍可能存在電漿損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess etch damage. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Correct geometry can still contain plasma damage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何正確仍可能存在電漿損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Correct geometry can still contain plasma damage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「蝕刻損傷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess etch damage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「蝕刻損傷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess etch damage: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-09-k1","title":"蝕刻損傷的原理","titleEn":"Assess etch damage principle","text":"幾何正確仍可能存在電漿損傷。","textEn":"Correct geometry can still contain plasma damage."},{"id":"a018-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「蝕刻損傷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess etch damage?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","幾何正確仍可能存在電漿損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Correct geometry can still contain plasma damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何正確仍可能存在電漿損傷。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Correct geometry can still contain plasma damage. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}},{"id":"a018-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-09"],"title":"角落圓化","titleEn":"Compare corner rounding","objective":"完成「角落圓化」的故障判別表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare corner rounding, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：角落圓化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：圓化會改變電場及可用主動區尺寸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare corner rounding. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Rounding changes fields and usable active dimensions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「圓化會改變電場及可用主動區尺寸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rounding changes fields and usable active dimensions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「角落圓化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare corner rounding and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「角落圓化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare corner rounding: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-10-k1","title":"角落圓化的原理","titleEn":"Compare corner rounding principle","text":"圓化會改變電場及可用主動區尺寸。","textEn":"Rounding changes fields and usable active dimensions."},{"id":"a018-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「角落圓化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare corner rounding?","options":["圓化會改變電場及可用主動區尺寸。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Rounding changes fields and usable active dimensions.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"圓化會改變電場及可用主動區尺寸。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Rounding changes fields and usable active dimensions. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}},{"id":"a018-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-10"],"title":"襯層氧化消耗","titleEn":"Budget liner oxidation","objective":"完成「襯層氧化消耗」的量測規劃，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for budget liner oxidation, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：襯層氧化消耗。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：襯層成長會消耗溝槽壁矽並改變寬度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget liner oxidation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Liner growth consumes silicon walls and changes trench width. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「襯層成長會消耗溝槽壁矽並改變寬度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Liner growth consumes silicon walls and changes trench width. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「襯層氧化消耗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget liner oxidation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「襯層氧化消耗」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for budget liner oxidation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-11-k1","title":"襯層氧化消耗的原理","titleEn":"Budget liner oxidation principle","text":"襯層成長會消耗溝槽壁矽並改變寬度。","textEn":"Liner growth consumes silicon walls and changes trench width."},{"id":"a018-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「襯層氧化消耗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget liner oxidation?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","襯層成長會消耗溝槽壁矽並改變寬度。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Liner growth consumes silicon walls and changes trench width.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"襯層成長會消耗溝槽壁矽並改變寬度。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Liner growth consumes silicon walls and changes trench width. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}},{"id":"a018-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-11"],"title":"襯層應力","titleEn":"Inspect liner stress","objective":"完成「襯層應力」的工程驗收單，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for inspect liner stress, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：襯層應力。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：氧化與拘束產生的應力會傳到鄰近通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect liner stress. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Oxidation and confinement stress can reach adjacent channels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化與拘束產生的應力會傳到鄰近通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oxidation and confinement stress can reach adjacent channels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「襯層應力」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect liner stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「襯層應力」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for inspect liner stress: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-12-k1","title":"襯層應力的原理","titleEn":"Inspect liner stress principle","text":"氧化與拘束產生的應力會傳到鄰近通道。","textEn":"Oxidation and confinement stress can reach adjacent channels."},{"id":"a018-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","textEn":"Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「襯層應力」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect liner stress?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","氧化與拘束產生的應力會傳到鄰近通道。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Oxidation and confinement stress can reach adjacent channels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氧化與拘束產生的應力會傳到鄰近通道。 側壁形狀與襯層消耗會改變填充前的實際開口，所以設計圖寬度不能直接代替沉積入口寬度。","explanationEn":"Oxidation and confinement stress can reach adjacent channels. Sidewall shape and liner consumption change the prefill opening, so layout width is not necessarily deposition-entry width."}}]},{"id":"a018-stage03","order":3,"title":"填充與平坦化","titleEn":"Fill and planarization","description":"在「填充與平坦化」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for fill and planarization, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a018-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-12"],"title":"底部與側壁成長","titleEn":"Compare bottom and sidewall growth","objective":"完成「底部與側壁成長」的因果圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare bottom and sidewall growth, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部與側壁成長。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：不均勻成長可能造成入口先封閉。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare bottom and sidewall growth. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Uneven growth can close the opening prematurely. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不均勻成長可能造成入口先封閉。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Uneven growth can close the opening prematurely. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「底部與側壁成長」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare bottom and sidewall growth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部與側壁成長」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare bottom and sidewall growth: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-13-k1","title":"底部與側壁成長的原理","titleEn":"Compare bottom and sidewall growth principle","text":"不均勻成長可能造成入口先封閉。","textEn":"Uneven growth can close the opening prematurely."},{"id":"a018-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部與側壁成長」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare bottom and sidewall growth?","options":["不均勻成長可能造成入口先封閉。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Uneven growth can close the opening prematurely.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不均勻成長可能造成入口先封閉。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"Uneven growth can close the opening prematurely. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}},{"id":"a018-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-13"],"title":"接縫空洞","titleEn":"Identify seams and voids","objective":"完成「接縫空洞」的對照表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify seams and voids, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接縫空洞。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：表面平坦不保證溝槽內部無空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify seams and voids. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A flat surface does not prove void-free trench fill. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面平坦不保證溝槽內部無空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A flat surface does not prove void-free trench fill. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接縫空洞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify seams and voids and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接縫空洞」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify seams and voids: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-14-k1","title":"接縫空洞的原理","titleEn":"Identify seams and voids principle","text":"表面平坦不保證溝槽內部無空洞。","textEn":"A flat surface does not prove void-free trench fill."},{"id":"a018-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接縫空洞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify seams and voids?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","表面平坦不保證溝槽內部無空洞。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","A flat surface does not prove void-free trench fill.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面平坦不保證溝槽內部無空洞。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"A flat surface does not prove void-free trench fill. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}},{"id":"a018-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-14"],"title":"填充緻密化","titleEn":"Assess fill densification","objective":"完成「填充緻密化」的敏感度草圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess fill densification, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：填充緻密化。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：退火收縮可能改變應力及表面凹陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 畫四張原創截面：完整填充、內部空洞、表面碟形凹陷、兩者同時存在；為每張安排截面及表面量測，不能只憑頂視放行。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess fill densification. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Anneal shrinkage can change stress and surface recess. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Draw four original sections: sound fill, internal void, surface dishing, and both. Assign cross-sectional and surface measurements without accepting from top view alone.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「退火收縮可能改變應力及表面凹陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Anneal shrinkage can change stress and surface recess. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「填充緻密化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess fill densification and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「填充緻密化」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess fill densification: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-15-k1","title":"填充緻密化的原理","titleEn":"Assess fill densification principle","text":"退火收縮可能改變應力及表面凹陷。","textEn":"Anneal shrinkage can change stress and surface recess."},{"id":"a018-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「填充緻密化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess fill densification?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","退火收縮可能改變應力及表面凹陷。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Anneal shrinkage can change stress and surface recess."],"answer":2,"explanation":"退火收縮可能改變應力及表面凹陷。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"Anneal shrinkage can change stress and surface recess. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}},{"id":"a018-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-15"],"title":"CMP 停止層","titleEn":"Define the CMP stop","objective":"完成「CMP 停止層」的故障判別表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define the cmp stop, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：CMP 停止層。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：停止層剩餘量必須與過拋光風險一起考量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define the CMP stop. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Remaining stop-layer thickness must be assessed with overpolish risk. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「停止層剩餘量必須與過拋光風險一起考量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Remaining stop-layer thickness must be assessed with overpolish risk. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「CMP 停止層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define the cmp stop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「CMP 停止層」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define the cmp stop: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-16-k1","title":"CMP 停止層的原理","titleEn":"Define the CMP stop principle","text":"停止層剩餘量必須與過拋光風險一起考量。","textEn":"Remaining stop-layer thickness must be assessed with overpolish risk."},{"id":"a018-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「CMP 停止層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define the cmp stop?","options":["停止層剩餘量必須與過拋光風險一起考量。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Remaining stop-layer thickness must be assessed with overpolish risk.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"停止層剩餘量必須與過拋光風險一起考量。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"Remaining stop-layer thickness must be assessed with overpolish risk. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}},{"id":"a018-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-16"],"title":"碟形與侵蝕","titleEn":"Separate dishing and erosion","objective":"完成「碟形與侵蝕」的量測規劃，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate dishing and erosion, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：碟形與侵蝕。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：局部填充凹陷與大範圍材料侵蝕不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate dishing and erosion. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Local fill recess differs from broad-area erosion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部填充凹陷與大範圍材料侵蝕不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local fill recess differs from broad-area erosion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「碟形與侵蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate dishing and erosion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「碟形與侵蝕」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate dishing and erosion: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-17-k1","title":"碟形與侵蝕的原理","titleEn":"Separate dishing and erosion principle","text":"局部填充凹陷與大範圍材料侵蝕不同。","textEn":"Local fill recess differs from broad-area erosion."},{"id":"a018-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「碟形與侵蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate dishing and erosion?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","局部填充凹陷與大範圍材料侵蝕不同。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Local fill recess differs from broad-area erosion.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部填充凹陷與大範圍材料侵蝕不同。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"Local fill recess differs from broad-area erosion. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}},{"id":"a018-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-17"],"title":"隔離高度","titleEn":"Measure isolation height","objective":"完成「隔離高度」的工程驗收單，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for measure isolation height, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離高度。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：隔離頂部高度會影響後續閘堆疊形貌。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure isolation height. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Isolation height affects subsequent gate-stack topography. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離頂部高度會影響後續閘堆疊形貌。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation height affects subsequent gate-stack topography. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「隔離高度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure isolation height and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離高度」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for measure isolation height: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-18-k1","title":"隔離高度的原理","titleEn":"Measure isolation height principle","text":"隔離頂部高度會影響後續閘堆疊形貌。","textEn":"Isolation height affects subsequent gate-stack topography."},{"id":"a018-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","textEn":"Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離高度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure isolation height?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","隔離頂部高度會影響後續閘堆疊形貌。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Isolation height affects subsequent gate-stack topography."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離頂部高度會影響後續閘堆疊形貌。 填充空洞是內部缺陷，CMP 凹陷是表面形貌；兩者可同時存在，需截面與表面量測各自確認。","explanationEn":"Isolation height affects subsequent gate-stack topography. Fill voids are internal defects while CMP recess is surface topography; both may coexist and need separate measurements."}}]},{"id":"a018-stage04","order":4,"title":"漏電與應力","titleEn":"Leakage and stress","description":"在「漏電與應力」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for leakage and stress, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a018-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-18"],"title":"窄寬效應","titleEn":"Assess narrow-width effects","objective":"完成「窄寬效應」的因果圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess narrow-width effects, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：窄寬效應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：通道靠近隔離邊界時邊緣影響比例增加。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess narrow-width effects. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Edge effects become proportionally larger near isolation boundaries. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「通道靠近隔離邊界時邊緣影響比例增加。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Edge effects become proportionally larger near isolation boundaries. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「窄寬效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess narrow-width effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「窄寬效應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess narrow-width effects: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-19-k1","title":"窄寬效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess narrow-width effects principle","text":"通道靠近隔離邊界時邊緣影響比例增加。","textEn":"Edge effects become proportionally larger near isolation boundaries."},{"id":"a018-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「窄寬效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess narrow-width effects?","options":["通道靠近隔離邊界時邊緣影響比例增加。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Edge effects become proportionally larger near isolation boundaries.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"通道靠近隔離邊界時邊緣影響比例增加。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Edge effects become proportionally larger near isolation boundaries. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}},{"id":"a018-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-19"],"title":"寄生通道","titleEn":"Trace parasitic channels","objective":"完成「寄生通道」的對照表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace parasitic channels, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：寄生通道。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：隔離邊緣可能形成不同於主通道的導通路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace parasitic channels. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Isolation edges can support conduction distinct from the main channel. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離邊緣可能形成不同於主通道的導通路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation edges can support conduction distinct from the main channel. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「寄生通道」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace parasitic channels and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「寄生通道」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace parasitic channels: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-20-k1","title":"寄生通道的原理","titleEn":"Trace parasitic channels principle","text":"隔離邊緣可能形成不同於主通道的導通路徑。","textEn":"Isolation edges can support conduction distinct from the main channel."},{"id":"a018-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「寄生通道」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace parasitic channels?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","隔離邊緣可能形成不同於主通道的導通路徑。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Isolation edges can support conduction distinct from the main channel.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離邊緣可能形成不同於主通道的導通路徑。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Isolation edges can support conduction distinct from the main channel. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}},{"id":"a018-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-20"],"title":"漏電測試結構","titleEn":"Choose isolation test structures","objective":"完成「漏電測試結構」的敏感度草圖，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for choose isolation test structures, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：漏電測試結構。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：元件間隔離需要跨隔離區的測試配置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose isolation test structures. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Interdevice isolation needs test structures spanning the isolation region. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元件間隔離需要跨隔離區的測試配置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interdevice isolation needs test structures spanning the isolation region. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「漏電測試結構」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose isolation test structures and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「漏電測試結構」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for choose isolation test structures: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-21-k1","title":"漏電測試結構的原理","titleEn":"Choose isolation test structures principle","text":"元件間隔離需要跨隔離區的測試配置。","textEn":"Interdevice isolation needs test structures spanning the isolation region."},{"id":"a018-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「漏電測試結構」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose isolation test structures?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","元件間隔離需要跨隔離區的測試配置。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Interdevice isolation needs test structures spanning the isolation region."],"answer":2,"explanation":"元件間隔離需要跨隔離區的測試配置。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Interdevice isolation needs test structures spanning the isolation region. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}},{"id":"a018-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-21"],"title":"應力距離效應","titleEn":"Assess distance-to-isolation stress","objective":"完成「應力距離效應」的故障判別表，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess distance-to-isolation stress, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力距離效應。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同元件尺寸可能因到隔離邊界距離不同而有不同表現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess distance-to-isolation stress. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Equal devices can differ because of distance to isolation boundaries. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同元件尺寸可能因到隔離邊界距離不同而有不同表現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal devices can differ because of distance to isolation boundaries. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「應力距離效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess distance-to-isolation stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力距離效應」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess distance-to-isolation stress: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-22-k1","title":"應力距離效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess distance-to-isolation stress principle","text":"相同元件尺寸可能因到隔離邊界距離不同而有不同表現。","textEn":"Equal devices can differ because of distance to isolation boundaries."},{"id":"a018-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力距離效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess distance-to-isolation stress?","options":["相同元件尺寸可能因到隔離邊界距離不同而有不同表現。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Equal devices can differ because of distance to isolation boundaries.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同元件尺寸可能因到隔離邊界距離不同而有不同表現。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Equal devices can differ because of distance to isolation boundaries. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}},{"id":"a018-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-22"],"title":"截面抽樣","titleEn":"Choose section locations","objective":"完成「截面抽樣」的量測規劃，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose section locations, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：截面抽樣。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：需包含密集、稀疏及最窄溝槽。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose section locations. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sections should include dense, sparse and narrowest trenches. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需包含密集、稀疏及最窄溝槽。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sections should include dense, sparse and narrowest trenches. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「截面抽樣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose section locations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「截面抽樣」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose section locations: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-23-k1","title":"截面抽樣的原理","titleEn":"Choose section locations principle","text":"需包含密集、稀疏及最窄溝槽。","textEn":"Sections should include dense, sparse and narrowest trenches."},{"id":"a018-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「截面抽樣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose section locations?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","需包含密集、稀疏及最窄溝槽。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Sections should include dense, sparse and narrowest trenches.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"需包含密集、稀疏及最窄溝槽。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Sections should include dense, sparse and narrowest trenches. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}},{"id":"a018-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-frontend","v8a-legacy","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a018-v8-23"],"title":"STI 整合放行","titleEn":"Accept STI integration","objective":"完成「STI 整合放行」的工程驗收單，把溝槽填充、隔離漏電、應力中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept sti integration, connecting relevant limits in trench fill, isolation leakage and stress to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：STI 整合放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：填充、平坦、漏電與通道應力需共同符合要求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept STI integration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Fill, planarity, leakage and channel stress require joint acceptance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「填充、平坦、漏電與通道應力需共同符合要求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fill, planarity, leakage and channel stress require joint acceptance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「STI 整合放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept sti integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「STI 整合放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept sti integration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a018-v8-24-k1","title":"STI 整合放行的原理","titleEn":"Accept STI integration principle","text":"填充、平坦、漏電與通道應力需共同符合要求。","textEn":"Fill, planarity, leakage and channel stress require joint acceptance."},{"id":"a018-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","textEn":"STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「STI 整合放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept sti integration?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","填充、平坦、漏電與通道應力需共同符合要求。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Fill, planarity, leakage and channel stress require joint acceptance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填充、平坦、漏電與通道應力需共同符合要求。 STI 應力可依主動區到隔離邊界的距離改變元件特性，因此驗收需涵蓋版圖而不只是材料樣片。","explanationEn":"Fill, planarity, leakage and channel stress require joint acceptance. STI stress can change devices with distance to isolation; acceptance therefore needs layout coverage beyond material coupons."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a019","title":"應變矽通道整合","titleEn":"Strained-silicon channel integration","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["應變與輸運","應力來源","量測與校準","效能及可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Strain and transport","Stress sources","Measurement and calibration","Performance and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a019-stage01","order":1,"title":"應變與輸運","titleEn":"Strain and transport","description":"在「應變與輸運」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for strain and transport, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a019-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"應力與應變","titleEn":"Separate stress and strain","objective":"完成「應力與應變」的因果圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate stress and strain, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力與應變。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：應力是力學載荷，應變是相對形變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂小應變：長度由 100.00 變為 100.10 單位；計算軸向應變，再說明為何缺少彈性常數及邊界條件時不能唯一求應力。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate stress and strain. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Stress describes loading while strain describes relative deformation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical small strain: length changes from 100.00 to 100.10 units. Calculate axial strain and explain why stress is not uniquely known without elastic constants and boundaries.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「應力是力學載荷，應變是相對形變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stress describes loading while strain describes relative deformation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「應力與應變」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate stress and strain and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力與應變」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate stress and strain: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-01-k1","title":"應力與應變的原理","titleEn":"Separate stress and strain principle","text":"應力是力學載荷，應變是相對形變。","textEn":"Stress describes loading while strain describes relative deformation."},{"id":"a019-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力與應變」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate stress and strain?","options":["應力是力學載荷，應變是相對形變。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Stress describes loading while strain describes relative deformation.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應力是力學載荷，應變是相對形變。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"Stress describes loading while strain describes relative deformation. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}},{"id":"a019-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-01"],"title":"通道晶向","titleEn":"Register channel orientation","objective":"完成「通道晶向」的對照表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for register channel orientation, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：通道晶向。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：遷移率對應變的反應依賴晶向與載子種類。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Register channel orientation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Mobility response depends on orientation and carrier type. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「遷移率對應變的反應依賴晶向與載子種類。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mobility response depends on orientation and carrier type. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「通道晶向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for register channel orientation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「通道晶向」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for register channel orientation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-02-k1","title":"通道晶向的原理","titleEn":"Register channel orientation principle","text":"遷移率對應變的反應依賴晶向與載子種類。","textEn":"Mobility response depends on orientation and carrier type."},{"id":"a019-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「通道晶向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating register channel orientation?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","遷移率對應變的反應依賴晶向與載子種類。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Mobility response depends on orientation and carrier type.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"遷移率對應變的反應依賴晶向與載子種類。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"Mobility response depends on orientation and carrier type. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}},{"id":"a019-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-02"],"title":"拉伸與壓縮","titleEn":"Compare tension and compression","objective":"完成「拉伸與壓縮」的敏感度草圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare tension and compression, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：拉伸與壓縮。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：同一應變符號對電子與電洞未必同樣有利。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare tension and compression. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: One strain sign need not benefit electrons and holes equally. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「同一應變符號對電子與電洞未必同樣有利。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One strain sign need not benefit electrons and holes equally. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「拉伸與壓縮」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare tension and compression and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「拉伸與壓縮」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare tension and compression: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-03-k1","title":"拉伸與壓縮的原理","titleEn":"Compare tension and compression principle","text":"同一應變符號對電子與電洞未必同樣有利。","textEn":"One strain sign need not benefit electrons and holes equally."},{"id":"a019-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「拉伸與壓縮」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare tension and compression?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","同一應變符號對電子與電洞未必同樣有利。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","One strain sign need not benefit electrons and holes equally."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一應變符號對電子與電洞未必同樣有利。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"One strain sign need not benefit electrons and holes equally. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}},{"id":"a019-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-03"],"title":"張量分量","titleEn":"Resolve strain components","objective":"完成「張量分量」的故障判別表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for resolve strain components, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：張量分量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：單一數值不能代表完整三維應變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Resolve strain components. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: One scalar cannot represent full three-dimensional strain. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一數值不能代表完整三維應變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One scalar cannot represent full three-dimensional strain. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「張量分量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for resolve strain components and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「張量分量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for resolve strain components: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-04-k1","title":"張量分量的原理","titleEn":"Resolve strain components principle","text":"單一數值不能代表完整三維應變。","textEn":"One scalar cannot represent full three-dimensional strain."},{"id":"a019-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「張量分量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating resolve strain components?","options":["單一數值不能代表完整三維應變。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["One scalar cannot represent full three-dimensional strain.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一數值不能代表完整三維應變。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"One scalar cannot represent full three-dimensional strain. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}},{"id":"a019-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-04"],"title":"基準元件","titleEn":"Choose a reference device","objective":"完成「基準元件」的量測規劃，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose a reference device, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基準元件。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：比較需維持幾何、電壓與接觸條件一致。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose a reference device. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Comparisons require matched geometry, voltage and contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較需維持幾何、電壓與接觸條件一致。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Comparisons require matched geometry, voltage and contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「基準元件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose a reference device and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基準元件」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose a reference device: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-05-k1","title":"基準元件的原理","titleEn":"Choose a reference device principle","text":"比較需維持幾何、電壓與接觸條件一致。","textEn":"Comparisons require matched geometry, voltage and contacts."},{"id":"a019-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基準元件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose a reference device?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","比較需維持幾何、電壓與接觸條件一致。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Comparisons require matched geometry, voltage and contacts.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較需維持幾何、電壓與接觸條件一致。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"Comparisons require matched geometry, voltage and contacts. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}},{"id":"a019-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-05"],"title":"效能指標","titleEn":"Separate mobility and drive current","objective":"完成「效能指標」的工程驗收單，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for separate mobility and drive current, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：效能指標。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：驅動電流還受到串聯電阻與電容限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate mobility and drive current. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Drive current is also constrained by series resistance and capacitance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「驅動電流還受到串聯電阻與電容限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Drive current is also constrained by series resistance and capacitance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「效能指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate mobility and drive current and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「效能指標」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for separate mobility and drive current: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-06-k1","title":"效能指標的原理","titleEn":"Separate mobility and drive current principle","text":"驅動電流還受到串聯電阻與電容限制。","textEn":"Drive current is also constrained by series resistance and capacitance."},{"id":"a019-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","textEn":"Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「效能指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate mobility and drive current?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","驅動電流還受到串聯電阻與電容限制。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Drive current is also constrained by series resistance and capacitance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驅動電流還受到串聯電阻與電容限制。 應變對輸運的作用依賴方向、載子及能帶；「增加應力」沒有脫離方向與材料的普遍正面意義。","explanationEn":"Drive current is also constrained by series resistance and capacitance. Strain effects depend on direction, carriers and bands; increasing stress has no universal benefit independent of material and direction."}}]},{"id":"a019-stage02","order":2,"title":"應力來源","titleEn":"Stress sources","description":"在「應力來源」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for stress sources, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a019-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-06"],"title":"嵌入式源汲極","titleEn":"Trace embedded stressors","objective":"完成「嵌入式源汲極」的因果圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace embedded stressors, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：嵌入式源汲極。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：源汲極材料晶格差可透過拘束把應力傳入通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace embedded stressors. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Source-drain lattice mismatch can transfer stress into a constrained channel. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「源汲極材料晶格差可透過拘束把應力傳入通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source-drain lattice mismatch can transfer stress into a constrained channel. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「嵌入式源汲極」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace embedded stressors and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「嵌入式源汲極」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace embedded stressors: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-07-k1","title":"嵌入式源汲極的原理","titleEn":"Trace embedded stressors principle","text":"源汲極材料晶格差可透過拘束把應力傳入通道。","textEn":"Source-drain lattice mismatch can transfer stress into a constrained channel."},{"id":"a019-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「嵌入式源汲極」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace embedded stressors?","options":["源汲極材料晶格差可透過拘束把應力傳入通道。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Source-drain lattice mismatch can transfer stress into a constrained channel.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"源汲極材料晶格差可透過拘束把應力傳入通道。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Source-drain lattice mismatch can transfer stress into a constrained channel. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}},{"id":"a019-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-07"],"title":"接觸蝕刻停止層","titleEn":"Assess stress liners","objective":"完成「接觸蝕刻停止層」的對照表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess stress liners, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸蝕刻停止層。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：應力薄膜的效果依賴厚度、覆蓋及幾何。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess stress liners. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Stress-liner effects depend on thickness, coverage and geometry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「應力薄膜的效果依賴厚度、覆蓋及幾何。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stress-liner effects depend on thickness, coverage and geometry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「接觸蝕刻停止層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess stress liners and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸蝕刻停止層」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess stress liners: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-08-k1","title":"接觸蝕刻停止層的原理","titleEn":"Assess stress liners principle","text":"應力薄膜的效果依賴厚度、覆蓋及幾何。","textEn":"Stress-liner effects depend on thickness, coverage and geometry."},{"id":"a019-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸蝕刻停止層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess stress liners?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","應力薄膜的效果依賴厚度、覆蓋及幾何。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Stress-liner effects depend on thickness, coverage and geometry.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應力薄膜的效果依賴厚度、覆蓋及幾何。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Stress-liner effects depend on thickness, coverage and geometry. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}},{"id":"a019-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-08"],"title":"緩衝層鬆弛","titleEn":"Assess buffer relaxation","objective":"完成「緩衝層鬆弛」的敏感度草圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess buffer relaxation, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：緩衝層鬆弛。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：緩衝層鬆弛與缺陷生成需要一起評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess buffer relaxation. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Buffer relaxation must be considered alongside defect generation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「緩衝層鬆弛與缺陷生成需要一起評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buffer relaxation must be considered alongside defect generation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「緩衝層鬆弛」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess buffer relaxation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「緩衝層鬆弛」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess buffer relaxation: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-09-k1","title":"緩衝層鬆弛的原理","titleEn":"Assess buffer relaxation principle","text":"緩衝層鬆弛與缺陷生成需要一起評估。","textEn":"Buffer relaxation must be considered alongside defect generation."},{"id":"a019-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「緩衝層鬆弛」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess buffer relaxation?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","緩衝層鬆弛與缺陷生成需要一起評估。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Buffer relaxation must be considered alongside defect generation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"緩衝層鬆弛與缺陷生成需要一起評估。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Buffer relaxation must be considered alongside defect generation. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}},{"id":"a019-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-09"],"title":"隔離區拘束","titleEn":"Include isolation constraints","objective":"完成「隔離區拘束」的故障判別表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for include isolation constraints, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離區拘束。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：隔離材料的拘束會改變通道應變分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include isolation constraints. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Isolation constraints change channel strain distribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離材料的拘束會改變通道應變分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation constraints change channel strain distribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「隔離區拘束」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include isolation constraints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離區拘束」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for include isolation constraints: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-10-k1","title":"隔離區拘束的原理","titleEn":"Include isolation constraints principle","text":"隔離材料的拘束會改變通道應變分布。","textEn":"Isolation constraints change channel strain distribution."},{"id":"a019-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離區拘束」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include isolation constraints?","options":["隔離材料的拘束會改變通道應變分布。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Isolation constraints change channel strain distribution.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隔離材料的拘束會改變通道應變分布。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Isolation constraints change channel strain distribution. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}},{"id":"a019-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-10"],"title":"圖案切割","titleEn":"Compare patterned relaxation","objective":"完成「圖案切割」的量測規劃，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare patterned relaxation, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案切割。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：圖案化後自由邊界增加，應變可能部分釋放。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare patterned relaxation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Patterning introduces free boundaries that can release strain. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「圖案化後自由邊界增加，應變可能部分釋放。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Patterning introduces free boundaries that can release strain. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「圖案切割」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare patterned relaxation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案切割」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare patterned relaxation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-11-k1","title":"圖案切割的原理","titleEn":"Compare patterned relaxation principle","text":"圖案化後自由邊界增加，應變可能部分釋放。","textEn":"Patterning introduces free boundaries that can release strain."},{"id":"a019-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案切割」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare patterned relaxation?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","圖案化後自由邊界增加，應變可能部分釋放。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Patterning introduces free boundaries that can release strain.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圖案化後自由邊界增加，應變可能部分釋放。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Patterning introduces free boundaries that can release strain. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}},{"id":"a019-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-11"],"title":"熱膨脹失配","titleEn":"Assess thermal mismatch","objective":"完成「熱膨脹失配」的工程驗收單，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess thermal mismatch, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱膨脹失配。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：冷卻過程的膨脹係數差可形成額外應力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermal mismatch. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thermal-expansion mismatch during cooling adds stress. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「冷卻過程的膨脹係數差可形成額外應力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal-expansion mismatch during cooling adds stress. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「熱膨脹失配」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermal mismatch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱膨脹失配」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess thermal mismatch: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-12-k1","title":"熱膨脹失配的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermal mismatch principle","text":"冷卻過程的膨脹係數差可形成額外應力。","textEn":"Thermal-expansion mismatch during cooling adds stress."},{"id":"a019-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","textEn":"Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱膨脹失配」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermal mismatch?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","冷卻過程的膨脹係數差可形成額外應力。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Thermal-expansion mismatch during cooling adds stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"冷卻過程的膨脹係數差可形成額外應力。 晶格失配可先以彈性形變承受，超出可維持範圍後可能藉位錯鬆弛，必須同看應變與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Thermal-expansion mismatch during cooling adds stress. Lattice mismatch can remain elastic before relaxing through dislocations; inspect strain and defects together."}}]},{"id":"a019-stage03","order":3,"title":"量測與校準","titleEn":"Measurement and calibration","description":"在「量測與校準」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for measurement and calibration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a019-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-12"],"title":"拉曼位移","titleEn":"Interpret Raman shifts","objective":"完成「拉曼位移」的因果圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for interpret raman shifts, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：拉曼位移。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：峰位變化也需排除溫度及成分影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret Raman shifts. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Peak shifts require separating temperature and composition effects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「峰位變化也需排除溫度及成分影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Peak shifts require separating temperature and composition effects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「拉曼位移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret raman shifts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「拉曼位移」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for interpret raman shifts: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-13-k1","title":"拉曼位移的原理","titleEn":"Interpret Raman shifts principle","text":"峰位變化也需排除溫度及成分影響。","textEn":"Peak shifts require separating temperature and composition effects."},{"id":"a019-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「拉曼位移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret raman shifts?","options":["峰位變化也需排除溫度及成分影響。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Peak shifts require separating temperature and composition effects.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"峰位變化也需排除溫度及成分影響。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"Peak shifts require separating temperature and composition effects. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}},{"id":"a019-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-13"],"title":"XRD 倒易空間","titleEn":"Read reciprocal-space maps","objective":"完成「XRD 倒易空間」的對照表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for read reciprocal-space maps, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：XRD 倒易空間。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：成分與鬆弛不能只由單一峰位置唯一決定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read reciprocal-space maps. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: One peak position does not uniquely determine composition and relaxation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「成分與鬆弛不能只由單一峰位置唯一決定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One peak position does not uniquely determine composition and relaxation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「XRD 倒易空間」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read reciprocal-space maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「XRD 倒易空間」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for read reciprocal-space maps: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-14-k1","title":"XRD 倒易空間的原理","titleEn":"Read reciprocal-space maps principle","text":"成分與鬆弛不能只由單一峰位置唯一決定。","textEn":"One peak position does not uniquely determine composition and relaxation."},{"id":"a019-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「XRD 倒易空間」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read reciprocal-space maps?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","成分與鬆弛不能只由單一峰位置唯一決定。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","One peak position does not uniquely determine composition and relaxation.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"成分與鬆弛不能只由單一峰位置唯一決定。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"One peak position does not uniquely determine composition and relaxation. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}},{"id":"a019-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-14"],"title":"局部 TEM 應變","titleEn":"Interpret local strain maps","objective":"完成「局部 TEM 應變」的敏感度草圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret local strain maps, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：局部 TEM 應變。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：局部薄片製備可能改變原結構拘束。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret local strain maps. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thin-lamella preparation can change the original constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部薄片製備可能改變原結構拘束。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thin-lamella preparation can change the original constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「局部 TEM 應變」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret local strain maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「局部 TEM 應變」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret local strain maps: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-15-k1","title":"局部 TEM 應變的原理","titleEn":"Interpret local strain maps principle","text":"局部薄片製備可能改變原結構拘束。","textEn":"Thin-lamella preparation can change the original constraints."},{"id":"a019-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「局部 TEM 應變」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret local strain maps?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","局部薄片製備可能改變原結構拘束。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Thin-lamella preparation can change the original constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部薄片製備可能改變原結構拘束。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"Thin-lamella preparation can change the original constraints. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}},{"id":"a019-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-15"],"title":"有限元素邊界","titleEn":"Set finite-element boundaries","objective":"完成「有限元素邊界」的故障判別表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for set finite-element boundaries, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：有限元素邊界。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：錯誤固定邊界可能人為放大通道應力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set finite-element boundaries. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Incorrect fixed boundaries can artificially amplify channel stress. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「錯誤固定邊界可能人為放大通道應力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Incorrect fixed boundaries can artificially amplify channel stress. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「有限元素邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set finite-element boundaries and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「有限元素邊界」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for set finite-element boundaries: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-16-k1","title":"有限元素邊界的原理","titleEn":"Set finite-element boundaries principle","text":"錯誤固定邊界可能人為放大通道應力。","textEn":"Incorrect fixed boundaries can artificially amplify channel stress."},{"id":"a019-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「有限元素邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set finite-element boundaries?","options":["錯誤固定邊界可能人為放大通道應力。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Incorrect fixed boundaries can artificially amplify channel stress.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯誤固定邊界可能人為放大通道應力。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"Incorrect fixed boundaries can artificially amplify channel stress. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}},{"id":"a019-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-16"],"title":"網格收斂","titleEn":"Check mesh convergence","objective":"完成「網格收斂」的量測規劃，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for check mesh convergence, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：網格收斂。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：尖角應力峰值需檢查網格依賴。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check mesh convergence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Corner stress peaks require mesh-dependence checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「尖角應力峰值需檢查網格依賴。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Corner stress peaks require mesh-dependence checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「網格收斂」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check mesh convergence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「網格收斂」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for check mesh convergence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-17-k1","title":"網格收斂的原理","titleEn":"Check mesh convergence principle","text":"尖角應力峰值需檢查網格依賴。","textEn":"Corner stress peaks require mesh-dependence checks."},{"id":"a019-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「網格收斂」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check mesh convergence?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","尖角應力峰值需檢查網格依賴。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Corner stress peaks require mesh-dependence checks.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尖角應力峰值需檢查網格依賴。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"Corner stress peaks require mesh-dependence checks. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}},{"id":"a019-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-17"],"title":"量測與模擬對齊","titleEn":"Register measurement and simulation","objective":"完成「量測與模擬對齊」的工程驗收單，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for register measurement and simulation, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：量測與模擬對齊。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：比較需採相同空間平均範圍及方向。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Register measurement and simulation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Comparisons need matching spatial averaging and directions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較需採相同空間平均範圍及方向。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Comparisons need matching spatial averaging and directions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「量測與模擬對齊」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for register measurement and simulation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「量測與模擬對齊」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for register measurement and simulation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-18-k1","title":"量測與模擬對齊的原理","titleEn":"Register measurement and simulation principle","text":"比較需採相同空間平均範圍及方向。","textEn":"Comparisons need matching spatial averaging and directions."},{"id":"a019-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","textEn":"Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「量測與模擬對齊」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating register measurement and simulation?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","比較需採相同空間平均範圍及方向。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Comparisons need matching spatial averaging and directions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較需採相同空間平均範圍及方向。 實際量測具有有限空間平均範圍，模擬的單點峰值需經相同空間平均才適合與量測比較。","explanationEn":"Comparisons need matching spatial averaging and directions. Measurements have finite spatial averaging; simulated point peaks need equivalent averaging before comparison."}}]},{"id":"a019-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能及可靠度","titleEn":"Performance and reliability","description":"在「效能及可靠度」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for performance and reliability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a019-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-18"],"title":"有效遷移率","titleEn":"Extract effective mobility","objective":"完成「有效遷移率」的因果圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for extract effective mobility, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：有效遷移率。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：抽取結果需控制閘電容與串聯電阻假設。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Extract effective mobility. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Extraction depends on gate-capacitance and series-resistance assumptions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「抽取結果需控制閘電容與串聯電阻假設。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Extraction depends on gate-capacitance and series-resistance assumptions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「有效遷移率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for extract effective mobility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「有效遷移率」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for extract effective mobility: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-19-k1","title":"有效遷移率的原理","titleEn":"Extract effective mobility principle","text":"抽取結果需控制閘電容與串聯電阻假設。","textEn":"Extraction depends on gate-capacitance and series-resistance assumptions."},{"id":"a019-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「有效遷移率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating extract effective mobility?","options":["抽取結果需控制閘電容與串聯電阻假設。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Extraction depends on gate-capacitance and series-resistance assumptions.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽取結果需控制閘電容與串聯電阻假設。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Extraction depends on gate-capacitance and series-resistance assumptions. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}},{"id":"a019-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-19"],"title":"漏電代價","titleEn":"Assess leakage tradeoffs","objective":"完成「漏電代價」的對照表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess leakage tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：漏電代價。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：提高導通電流仍需維持關斷電流限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess leakage tradeoffs. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Higher on-current must still satisfy off-current constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提高導通電流仍需維持關斷電流限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher on-current must still satisfy off-current constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「漏電代價」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess leakage tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「漏電代價」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess leakage tradeoffs: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-20-k1","title":"漏電代價的原理","titleEn":"Assess leakage tradeoffs principle","text":"提高導通電流仍需維持關斷電流限制。","textEn":"Higher on-current must still satisfy off-current constraints."},{"id":"a019-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「漏電代價」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess leakage tradeoffs?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","提高導通電流仍需維持關斷電流限制。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Higher on-current must still satisfy off-current constraints.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"提高導通電流仍需維持關斷電流限制。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Higher on-current must still satisfy off-current constraints. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}},{"id":"a019-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-20"],"title":"接面缺陷","titleEn":"Inspect junction defects","objective":"完成「接面缺陷」的敏感度草圖，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect junction defects, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面缺陷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：增加失配可能帶來鬆弛缺陷及漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect junction defects. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Greater mismatch can introduce relaxation defects and leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「增加失配可能帶來鬆弛缺陷及漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Greater mismatch can introduce relaxation defects and leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「接面缺陷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect junction defects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面缺陷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect junction defects: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-21-k1","title":"接面缺陷的原理","titleEn":"Inspect junction defects principle","text":"增加失配可能帶來鬆弛缺陷及漏電。","textEn":"Greater mismatch can introduce relaxation defects and leakage."},{"id":"a019-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面缺陷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect junction defects?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","增加失配可能帶來鬆弛缺陷及漏電。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Greater mismatch can introduce relaxation defects and leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"增加失配可能帶來鬆弛缺陷及漏電。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Greater mismatch can introduce relaxation defects and leakage. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}},{"id":"a019-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-21"],"title":"熱穩定性","titleEn":"Assess thermal stability","objective":"完成「熱穩定性」的故障判別表，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess thermal stability, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱穩定性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：後續熱循環可能改變應變保持程度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermal stability. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Later thermal cycles can change retained strain. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「後續熱循環可能改變應變保持程度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Later thermal cycles can change retained strain. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「熱穩定性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermal stability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱穩定性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess thermal stability: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-22-k1","title":"熱穩定性的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermal stability principle","text":"後續熱循環可能改變應變保持程度。","textEn":"Later thermal cycles can change retained strain."},{"id":"a019-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱穩定性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermal stability?","options":["後續熱循環可能改變應變保持程度。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Later thermal cycles can change retained strain.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"後續熱循環可能改變應變保持程度。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Later thermal cycles can change retained strain. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}},{"id":"a019-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-22"],"title":"版圖相依性","titleEn":"Assess layout dependence","objective":"完成「版圖相依性」的量測規劃，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess layout dependence, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：版圖相依性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：鄰近結構可能改變相同元件的應力環境。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess layout dependence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Neighboring structures can change stress around otherwise equal devices. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鄰近結構可能改變相同元件的應力環境。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Neighboring structures can change stress around otherwise equal devices. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「版圖相依性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess layout dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「版圖相依性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess layout dependence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-23-k1","title":"版圖相依性的原理","titleEn":"Assess layout dependence principle","text":"鄰近結構可能改變相同元件的應力環境。","textEn":"Neighboring structures can change stress around otherwise equal devices."},{"id":"a019-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「版圖相依性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess layout dependence?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","鄰近結構可能改變相同元件的應力環境。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Neighboring structures can change stress around otherwise equal devices.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鄰近結構可能改變相同元件的應力環境。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Neighboring structures can change stress around otherwise equal devices. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}},{"id":"a019-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-strain","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a019-v8-23"],"title":"應變整合結論","titleEn":"Review strain integration","objective":"完成「應變整合結論」的工程驗收單，把應變張量、載子輸運、鬆弛中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review strain integration, connecting relevant limits in strain tensors, carrier transport and relaxation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應變整合結論。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：需將輸運收益與缺陷、漏電及版圖變異一起呈現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review strain integration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Report transport gains with defects, leakage and layout variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需將輸運收益與缺陷、漏電及版圖變異一起呈現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report transport gains with defects, leakage and layout variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「應變整合結論」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review strain integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應變整合結論」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review strain integration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a019-v8-24-k1","title":"應變整合結論的原理","titleEn":"Review strain integration principle","text":"需將輸運收益與缺陷、漏電及版圖變異一起呈現。","textEn":"Report transport gains with defects, leakage and layout variation."},{"id":"a019-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","textEn":"Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應變整合結論」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review strain integration?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","需將輸運收益與缺陷、漏電及版圖變異一起呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Report transport gains with defects, leakage and layout variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"需將輸運收益與缺陷、漏電及版圖變異一起呈現。 遷移率提高的收益會受接觸及互連限制；元件電流與電路延遲應分層驗證而非直接同比換算。","explanationEn":"Report transport gains with defects, leakage and layout variation. Contact and interconnect limits constrain mobility gains; validate device current and circuit delay separately rather than scaling them proportionally."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a020","title":"矽鍺選擇性磊晶","titleEn":"Selective silicon-germanium epitaxy","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["選擇性與晶格","表面與成長","成分及形貌","接觸與整合"],"labelsEn":["Selectivity and lattice","Surface and growth","Composition and morphology","Contacts and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a020-stage01","order":1,"title":"選擇性與晶格","titleEn":"Selectivity and lattice","description":"在「選擇性與晶格」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for selectivity and lattice, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a020-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"選擇性定義","titleEn":"Define selectivity","objective":"完成「選擇性定義」的因果圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define selectivity, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性定義。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：在矽上成長且在介電層抑制成核是兩個需驗證的條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define selectivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Growth on silicon and suppressed dielectric nucleation both need evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「在矽上成長且在介電層抑制成核是兩個需驗證的條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Growth on silicon and suppressed dielectric nucleation both need evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「選擇性定義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性定義」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define selectivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-01-k1","title":"選擇性定義的原理","titleEn":"Define selectivity principle","text":"在矽上成長且在介電層抑制成核是兩個需驗證的條件。","textEn":"Growth on silicon and suppressed dielectric nucleation both need evidence."},{"id":"a020-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性定義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define selectivity?","options":["在矽上成長且在介電層抑制成核是兩個需驗證的條件。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Growth on silicon and suppressed dielectric nucleation both need evidence.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在矽上成長且在介電層抑制成核是兩個需驗證的條件。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"Growth on silicon and suppressed dielectric nucleation both need evidence. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}},{"id":"a020-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-01"],"title":"鍺比例","titleEn":"Set germanium fraction","objective":"完成「鍺比例」的對照表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for set germanium fraction, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍺比例。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：鍺比例同時影響晶格、能帶及材料穩定性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set germanium fraction. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Germanium fraction affects lattice, bands and material stability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鍺比例同時影響晶格、能帶及材料穩定性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Germanium fraction affects lattice, bands and material stability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「鍺比例」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set germanium fraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍺比例」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for set germanium fraction: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-02-k1","title":"鍺比例的原理","titleEn":"Set germanium fraction principle","text":"鍺比例同時影響晶格、能帶及材料穩定性。","textEn":"Germanium fraction affects lattice, bands and material stability."},{"id":"a020-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍺比例」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set germanium fraction?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","鍺比例同時影響晶格、能帶及材料穩定性。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Germanium fraction affects lattice, bands and material stability.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鍺比例同時影響晶格、能帶及材料穩定性。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"Germanium fraction affects lattice, bands and material stability. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}},{"id":"a020-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-02"],"title":"種晶表面","titleEn":"Identify seed surfaces","objective":"完成「種晶表面」的敏感度草圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify seed surfaces, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：種晶表面。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：殘氧化層會阻礙預期晶體延續。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify seed surfaces. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Residual oxide impedes intended crystalline continuation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「殘氧化層會阻礙預期晶體延續。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual oxide impedes intended crystalline continuation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「種晶表面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify seed surfaces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「種晶表面」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify seed surfaces: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-03-k1","title":"種晶表面的原理","titleEn":"Identify seed surfaces principle","text":"殘氧化層會阻礙預期晶體延續。","textEn":"Residual oxide impedes intended crystalline continuation."},{"id":"a020-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「種晶表面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify seed surfaces?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","殘氧化層會阻礙預期晶體延續。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Residual oxide impedes intended crystalline continuation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘氧化層會阻礙預期晶體延續。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"Residual oxide impedes intended crystalline continuation. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}},{"id":"a020-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-03"],"title":"開口幾何","titleEn":"Define opening geometry","objective":"完成「開口幾何」的故障判別表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define opening geometry, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：開口幾何。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：側壁角及暴露晶面會影響最終晶面形貌。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define opening geometry. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Sidewall angle and exposed planes affect final facets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「側壁角及暴露晶面會影響最終晶面形貌。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sidewall angle and exposed planes affect final facets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「開口幾何」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define opening geometry and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「開口幾何」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define opening geometry: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-04-k1","title":"開口幾何的原理","titleEn":"Define opening geometry principle","text":"側壁角及暴露晶面會影響最終晶面形貌。","textEn":"Sidewall angle and exposed planes affect final facets."},{"id":"a020-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「開口幾何」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define opening geometry?","options":["側壁角及暴露晶面會影響最終晶面形貌。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall angle and exposed planes affect final facets.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"側壁角及暴露晶面會影響最終晶面形貌。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"Sidewall angle and exposed planes affect final facets. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}},{"id":"a020-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-04"],"title":"摻雜與成長","titleEn":"Couple doping and growth","objective":"完成「摻雜與成長」的量測規劃，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for couple doping and growth, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜與成長。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：原位摻雜可能改變成長動力學。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Couple doping and growth. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: In-situ doping can change growth kinetics. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「原位摻雜可能改變成長動力學。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: In-situ doping can change growth kinetics. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「摻雜與成長」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for couple doping and growth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜與成長」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for couple doping and growth: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-05-k1","title":"摻雜與成長的原理","titleEn":"Couple doping and growth principle","text":"原位摻雜可能改變成長動力學。","textEn":"In-situ doping can change growth kinetics."},{"id":"a020-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜與成長」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating couple doping and growth?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","原位摻雜可能改變成長動力學。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","In-situ doping can change growth kinetics.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原位摻雜可能改變成長動力學。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"In-situ doping can change growth kinetics. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}},{"id":"a020-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-05"],"title":"熱預算限制","titleEn":"Set thermal-budget bounds","objective":"完成「熱預算限制」的工程驗收單，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for set thermal-budget bounds, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算限制。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：鄰近閘與底層材料限制可採用的熱歷程。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set thermal-budget bounds. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Adjacent gates and underlying materials constrain thermal history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鄰近閘與底層材料限制可採用的熱歷程。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adjacent gates and underlying materials constrain thermal history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「熱預算限制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set thermal-budget bounds and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算限制」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for set thermal-budget bounds: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-06-k1","title":"熱預算限制的原理","titleEn":"Set thermal-budget bounds principle","text":"鄰近閘與底層材料限制可採用的熱歷程。","textEn":"Adjacent gates and underlying materials constrain thermal history."},{"id":"a020-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","textEn":"Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算限制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set thermal-budget bounds?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","鄰近閘與底層材料限制可採用的熱歷程。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Adjacent gates and underlying materials constrain thermal history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鄰近閘與底層材料限制可採用的熱歷程。 選擇性磊晶同時追求目標表面成長及非目標表面不成核，必須報告兩種表面的結果。","explanationEn":"Adjacent gates and underlying materials constrain thermal history. Selective epitaxy requires growth on target surfaces and suppressed nucleation elsewhere; report both surface outcomes."}}]},{"id":"a020-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面與成長","titleEn":"Surface and growth","description":"在「表面與成長」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for surface and growth, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a020-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-06"],"title":"表面前清潔","titleEn":"Assess pre-epitaxy cleaning","objective":"完成「表面前清潔」的因果圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess pre-epitaxy cleaning, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面前清潔。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：清潔需移除阻礙物而保留種晶幾何。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pre-epitaxy cleaning. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Cleaning must remove barriers while preserving seed geometry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清潔需移除阻礙物而保留種晶幾何。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Cleaning must remove barriers while preserving seed geometry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「表面前清潔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pre-epitaxy cleaning and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面前清潔」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess pre-epitaxy cleaning: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-07-k1","title":"表面前清潔的原理","titleEn":"Assess pre-epitaxy cleaning principle","text":"清潔需移除阻礙物而保留種晶幾何。","textEn":"Cleaning must remove barriers while preserving seed geometry."},{"id":"a020-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面前清潔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pre-epitaxy cleaning?","options":["清潔需移除阻礙物而保留種晶幾何。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Cleaning must remove barriers while preserving seed geometry.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清潔需移除阻礙物而保留種晶幾何。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Cleaning must remove barriers while preserving seed geometry. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}},{"id":"a020-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-07"],"title":"成長與蝕刻競爭","titleEn":"Balance deposition and etching","objective":"完成「成長與蝕刻競爭」的對照表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for balance deposition and etching, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：成長與蝕刻競爭。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：選擇性可來自成長與去除速率的競爭。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Balance deposition and etching. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Selectivity can arise from competing growth and removal rates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇性可來自成長與去除速率的競爭。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Selectivity can arise from competing growth and removal rates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「成長與蝕刻競爭」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for balance deposition and etching and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「成長與蝕刻競爭」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for balance deposition and etching: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-08-k1","title":"成長與蝕刻競爭的原理","titleEn":"Balance deposition and etching principle","text":"選擇性可來自成長與去除速率的競爭。","textEn":"Selectivity can arise from competing growth and removal rates."},{"id":"a020-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「成長與蝕刻競爭」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating balance deposition and etching?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","選擇性可來自成長與去除速率的競爭。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Selectivity can arise from competing growth and removal rates.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇性可來自成長與去除速率的競爭。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Selectivity can arise from competing growth and removal rates. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}},{"id":"a020-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-08"],"title":"介電層成核延遲","titleEn":"Assess dielectric nucleation delay","objective":"完成「介電層成核延遲」的敏感度草圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess dielectric nucleation delay, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介電層成核延遲。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：短時間選擇性不證明長時間仍無寄生成核。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess dielectric nucleation delay. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Short-term selectivity does not prove absence of later parasitic nuclei. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「短時間選擇性不證明長時間仍無寄生成核。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Short-term selectivity does not prove absence of later parasitic nuclei. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「介電層成核延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess dielectric nucleation delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介電層成核延遲」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess dielectric nucleation delay: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-09-k1","title":"介電層成核延遲的原理","titleEn":"Assess dielectric nucleation delay principle","text":"短時間選擇性不證明長時間仍無寄生成核。","textEn":"Short-term selectivity does not prove absence of later parasitic nuclei."},{"id":"a020-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介電層成核延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess dielectric nucleation delay?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","短時間選擇性不證明長時間仍無寄生成核。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Short-term selectivity does not prove absence of later parasitic nuclei."],"answer":2,"explanation":"短時間選擇性不證明長時間仍無寄生成核。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Short-term selectivity does not prove absence of later parasitic nuclei. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}},{"id":"a020-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-09"],"title":"圖案負載","titleEn":"Assess pattern loading","objective":"完成「圖案負載」的故障判別表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess pattern loading, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案負載。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：不同開口密度可能改變局部反應物供應。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pattern loading. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Opening density can change local reactant availability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同開口密度可能改變局部反應物供應。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Opening density can change local reactant availability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「圖案負載」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pattern loading and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案負載」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess pattern loading: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-10-k1","title":"圖案負載的原理","titleEn":"Assess pattern loading principle","text":"不同開口密度可能改變局部反應物供應。","textEn":"Opening density can change local reactant availability."},{"id":"a020-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案負載」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pattern loading?","options":["不同開口密度可能改變局部反應物供應。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Opening density can change local reactant availability.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同開口密度可能改變局部反應物供應。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Opening density can change local reactant availability. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}},{"id":"a020-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-10"],"title":"晶面演化","titleEn":"Track facet evolution","objective":"完成「晶面演化」的量測規劃，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track facet evolution, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶面演化。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：晶面成長速率差會改變截面外形。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track facet evolution. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Different facet growth rates change cross-section shape. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「晶面成長速率差會改變截面外形。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different facet growth rates change cross-section shape. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶面演化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track facet evolution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶面演化」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track facet evolution: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-11-k1","title":"晶面演化的原理","titleEn":"Track facet evolution principle","text":"晶面成長速率差會改變截面外形。","textEn":"Different facet growth rates change cross-section shape."},{"id":"a020-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶面演化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track facet evolution?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","晶面成長速率差會改變截面外形。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Different facet growth rates change cross-section shape.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶面成長速率差會改變截面外形。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Different facet growth rates change cross-section shape. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}},{"id":"a020-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-11"],"title":"相鄰結構合併","titleEn":"Inspect coalescence","objective":"完成「相鄰結構合併」的工程驗收單，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for inspect coalescence, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：相鄰結構合併。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：兩側成長前緣相遇可能留下晶體缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect coalescence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Merging growth fronts can leave crystalline defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩側成長前緣相遇可能留下晶體缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Merging growth fronts can leave crystalline defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「相鄰結構合併」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect coalescence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「相鄰結構合併」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for inspect coalescence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-12-k1","title":"相鄰結構合併的原理","titleEn":"Inspect coalescence principle","text":"兩側成長前緣相遇可能留下晶體缺陷。","textEn":"Merging growth fronts can leave crystalline defects."},{"id":"a020-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","textEn":"Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「相鄰結構合併」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect coalescence?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","兩側成長前緣相遇可能留下晶體缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Merging growth fronts can leave crystalline defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩側成長前緣相遇可能留下晶體缺陷。 晶面速度不同造成外形演化，圖案密度又改變局部供料，因此截面形貌不能只由沉積時間決定。","explanationEn":"Merging growth fronts can leave crystalline defects. Facet-dependent rates and pattern-dependent supply govern shape, so deposition time alone cannot determine the section."}}]},{"id":"a020-stage03","order":3,"title":"成分及形貌","titleEn":"Composition and morphology","description":"在「成分及形貌」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for composition and morphology, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a020-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-12"],"title":"鍺深度分布","titleEn":"Map germanium depth profiles","objective":"完成「鍺深度分布」的因果圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map germanium depth profiles, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍺深度分布。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：表面平均成分不能代表整層成分梯度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 設計兩張同平均鍺比例、不同深度梯度的示意圖；指出平均成分量測無法區分之處，再選深度或繞射證據進行辨別。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map germanium depth profiles. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean surface composition cannot represent a depth gradient. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Sketch two depth profiles with equal mean germanium fraction but different gradients. Identify what average composition cannot distinguish and choose depth-resolved or diffraction evidence.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面平均成分不能代表整層成分梯度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean surface composition cannot represent a depth gradient. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「鍺深度分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map germanium depth profiles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍺深度分布」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map germanium depth profiles: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-13-k1","title":"鍺深度分布的原理","titleEn":"Map germanium depth profiles principle","text":"表面平均成分不能代表整層成分梯度。","textEn":"Mean surface composition cannot represent a depth gradient."},{"id":"a020-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍺深度分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map germanium depth profiles?","options":["表面平均成分不能代表整層成分梯度。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Mean surface composition cannot represent a depth gradient.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面平均成分不能代表整層成分梯度。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"Mean surface composition cannot represent a depth gradient. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}},{"id":"a020-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-13"],"title":"摻雜活化","titleEn":"Assess dopant activation","objective":"完成「摻雜活化」的對照表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess dopant activation, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜活化。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：化學摻雜濃度與活化濃度需分開量測。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess dopant activation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Chemical and activated dopant concentrations need separate measurements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「化學摻雜濃度與活化濃度需分開量測。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chemical and activated dopant concentrations need separate measurements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「摻雜活化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess dopant activation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜活化」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess dopant activation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-14-k1","title":"摻雜活化的原理","titleEn":"Assess dopant activation principle","text":"化學摻雜濃度與活化濃度需分開量測。","textEn":"Chemical and activated dopant concentrations need separate measurements."},{"id":"a020-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜活化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess dopant activation?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","化學摻雜濃度與活化濃度需分開量測。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Chemical and activated dopant concentrations need separate measurements.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"化學摻雜濃度與活化濃度需分開量測。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"Chemical and activated dopant concentrations need separate measurements. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}},{"id":"a020-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-14"],"title":"應變保持","titleEn":"Measure retained strain","objective":"完成「應變保持」的敏感度草圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for measure retained strain, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應變保持。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：成長更厚不一定保留更多彈性應變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure retained strain. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thicker growth need not retain more elastic strain. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「成長更厚不一定保留更多彈性應變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thicker growth need not retain more elastic strain. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「應變保持」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure retained strain and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應變保持」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for measure retained strain: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-15-k1","title":"應變保持的原理","titleEn":"Measure retained strain principle","text":"成長更厚不一定保留更多彈性應變。","textEn":"Thicker growth need not retain more elastic strain."},{"id":"a020-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應變保持」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure retained strain?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","成長更厚不一定保留更多彈性應變。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Thicker growth need not retain more elastic strain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成長更厚不一定保留更多彈性應變。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"Thicker growth need not retain more elastic strain. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}},{"id":"a020-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-15"],"title":"失配位錯","titleEn":"Locate misfit dislocations","objective":"完成「失配位錯」的故障判別表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for locate misfit dislocations, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：失配位錯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：位錯可釋放應變並形成漏電來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate misfit dislocations. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Dislocations can relax strain and introduce leakage paths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「位錯可釋放應變並形成漏電來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dislocations can relax strain and introduce leakage paths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「失配位錯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate misfit dislocations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「失配位錯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for locate misfit dislocations: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-16-k1","title":"失配位錯的原理","titleEn":"Locate misfit dislocations principle","text":"位錯可釋放應變並形成漏電來源。","textEn":"Dislocations can relax strain and introduce leakage paths."},{"id":"a020-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「失配位錯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate misfit dislocations?","options":["位錯可釋放應變並形成漏電來源。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Dislocations can relax strain and introduce leakage paths.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"位錯可釋放應變並形成漏電來源。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"Dislocations can relax strain and introduce leakage paths. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}},{"id":"a020-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-16"],"title":"表面粗糙化","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening","objective":"完成「表面粗糙化」的量測規劃，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect surface roughening, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面粗糙化。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：高成長速率可能伴隨形貌失控。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect surface roughening. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: High growth rate can coexist with morphology degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高成長速率可能伴隨形貌失控。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High growth rate can coexist with morphology degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「表面粗糙化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect surface roughening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面粗糙化」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect surface roughening: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-17-k1","title":"表面粗糙化的原理","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening principle","text":"高成長速率可能伴隨形貌失控。","textEn":"High growth rate can coexist with morphology degradation."},{"id":"a020-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面粗糙化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect surface roughening?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","高成長速率可能伴隨形貌失控。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","High growth rate can coexist with morphology degradation.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高成長速率可能伴隨形貌失控。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"High growth rate can coexist with morphology degradation. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}},{"id":"a020-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-17"],"title":"選擇性檢出限","titleEn":"Report selectivity detection limits","objective":"完成「選擇性檢出限」的工程驗收單，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for report selectivity detection limits, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性檢出限。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：未看到寄生核需附檢測面積及解析度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report selectivity detection limits. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: No observed nuclei requires stated inspection area and resolution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「未看到寄生核需附檢測面積及解析度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: No observed nuclei requires stated inspection area and resolution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「選擇性檢出限」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report selectivity detection limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性檢出限」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for report selectivity detection limits: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-18-k1","title":"選擇性檢出限的原理","titleEn":"Report selectivity detection limits principle","text":"未看到寄生核需附檢測面積及解析度。","textEn":"No observed nuclei requires stated inspection area and resolution."},{"id":"a020-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","textEn":"Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性檢出限」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report selectivity detection limits?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","未看到寄生核需附檢測面積及解析度。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","No observed nuclei requires stated inspection area and resolution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未看到寄生核需附檢測面積及解析度。 鍺比例、活化與晶格鬆弛相互耦合；更高名義摻雜或成分不保證更低接觸電阻及更低漏電。","explanationEn":"No observed nuclei requires stated inspection area and resolution. Germanium fraction, activation and relaxation interact; higher nominal doping or composition does not guarantee lower contact resistance or leakage."}}]},{"id":"a020-stage04","order":4,"title":"接觸與整合","titleEn":"Contacts and integration","description":"在「接觸與整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contacts and integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a020-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-18"],"title":"接觸金屬反應","titleEn":"Assess metal reaction","objective":"完成「接觸金屬反應」的因果圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess metal reaction, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸金屬反應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：接觸形成後的界面成分可能不同於原磊晶表面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess metal reaction. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: The contact interface can differ from the original epitaxial surface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸形成後的界面成分可能不同於原磊晶表面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The contact interface can differ from the original epitaxial surface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「接觸金屬反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess metal reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸金屬反應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess metal reaction: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-19-k1","title":"接觸金屬反應的原理","titleEn":"Assess metal reaction principle","text":"接觸形成後的界面成分可能不同於原磊晶表面。","textEn":"The contact interface can differ from the original epitaxial surface."},{"id":"a020-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸金屬反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess metal reaction?","options":["接觸形成後的界面成分可能不同於原磊晶表面。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["The contact interface can differ from the original epitaxial surface.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸形成後的界面成分可能不同於原磊晶表面。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"The contact interface can differ from the original epitaxial surface. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}},{"id":"a020-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-19"],"title":"接觸面積預算","titleEn":"Budget contact area","objective":"完成「接觸面積預算」的對照表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for budget contact area, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸面積預算。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：晶面形貌會改變可利用的接觸面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget contact area. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Facet geometry changes available contact area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「晶面形貌會改變可利用的接觸面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Facet geometry changes available contact area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「接觸面積預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget contact area and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸面積預算」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for budget contact area: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-20-k1","title":"接觸面積預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget contact area principle","text":"晶面形貌會改變可利用的接觸面積。","textEn":"Facet geometry changes available contact area."},{"id":"a020-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸面積預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget contact area?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","晶面形貌會改變可利用的接觸面積。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Facet geometry changes available contact area.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶面形貌會改變可利用的接觸面積。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"Facet geometry changes available contact area. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}},{"id":"a020-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-20"],"title":"奈米片端點","titleEn":"Analyze nanosheet endpoints","objective":"完成「奈米片端點」的敏感度草圖，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for analyze nanosheet endpoints, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：奈米片端點。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：每層奈米片的暴露端點可能有不同成長條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze nanosheet endpoints. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Each nanosheet endpoint can experience different growth conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「每層奈米片的暴露端點可能有不同成長條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Each nanosheet endpoint can experience different growth conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「奈米片端點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze nanosheet endpoints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「奈米片端點」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for analyze nanosheet endpoints: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-21-k1","title":"奈米片端點的原理","titleEn":"Analyze nanosheet endpoints principle","text":"每層奈米片的暴露端點可能有不同成長條件。","textEn":"Each nanosheet endpoint can experience different growth conditions."},{"id":"a020-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「奈米片端點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze nanosheet endpoints?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","每層奈米片的暴露端點可能有不同成長條件。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Each nanosheet endpoint can experience different growth conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每層奈米片的暴露端點可能有不同成長條件。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"Each nanosheet endpoint can experience different growth conditions. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}},{"id":"a020-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-21"],"title":"後續選蝕耐受","titleEn":"Assess later selective-etch survival","objective":"完成「後續選蝕耐受」的故障判別表，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess later selective-etch survival, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：後續選蝕耐受。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：源汲極需要在犧牲層移除時被保護。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess later selective-etch survival. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Source-drain material needs protection during sacrificial-layer removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「源汲極需要在犧牲層移除時被保護。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source-drain material needs protection during sacrificial-layer removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「後續選蝕耐受」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess later selective-etch survival and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「後續選蝕耐受」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess later selective-etch survival: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-22-k1","title":"後續選蝕耐受的原理","titleEn":"Assess later selective-etch survival principle","text":"源汲極需要在犧牲層移除時被保護。","textEn":"Source-drain material needs protection during sacrificial-layer removal."},{"id":"a020-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「後續選蝕耐受」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess later selective-etch survival?","options":["源汲極需要在犧牲層移除時被保護。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Source-drain material needs protection during sacrificial-layer removal.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"源汲極需要在犧牲層移除時被保護。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"Source-drain material needs protection during sacrificial-layer removal. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}},{"id":"a020-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-22"],"title":"片內差異","titleEn":"Map across-wafer differences","objective":"完成「片內差異」的量測規劃，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for map across-wafer differences, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片內差異。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：成分、厚度及缺陷需在一致座標下比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map across-wafer differences. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Compare composition, thickness and defects in shared coordinates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「成分、厚度及缺陷需在一致座標下比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Compare composition, thickness and defects in shared coordinates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「片內差異」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map across-wafer differences and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片內差異」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for map across-wafer differences: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-23-k1","title":"片內差異的原理","titleEn":"Map across-wafer differences principle","text":"成分、厚度及缺陷需在一致座標下比較。","textEn":"Compare composition, thickness and defects in shared coordinates."},{"id":"a020-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片內差異」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map across-wafer differences?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","成分、厚度及缺陷需在一致座標下比較。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Compare composition, thickness and defects in shared coordinates.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"成分、厚度及缺陷需在一致座標下比較。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"Compare composition, thickness and defects in shared coordinates. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}},{"id":"a020-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-epi","v8a-sige","v8a-selective"],"prerequisiteIds":["a020-v8-23"],"title":"SiGe 模組交接","titleEn":"Complete the SiGe handoff","objective":"完成「SiGe 模組交接」的工程驗收單，把選擇性磊晶、晶面、活化接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for complete the sige handoff, connecting relevant limits in selective epitaxy, facets and activated contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SiGe 模組交接。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：選擇性、活化、應變與接觸需求需共同驗收。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Complete the SiGe handoff. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Accept selectivity, activation, strain and contact requirements jointly. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇性、活化、應變與接觸需求需共同驗收。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Accept selectivity, activation, strain and contact requirements jointly. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「SiGe 模組交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for complete the sige handoff and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SiGe 模組交接」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for complete the sige handoff: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a020-v8-24-k1","title":"SiGe 模組交接的原理","titleEn":"Complete the SiGe handoff principle","text":"選擇性、活化、應變與接觸需求需共同驗收。","textEn":"Accept selectivity, activation, strain and contact requirements jointly."},{"id":"a020-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","textEn":"Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SiGe 模組交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating complete the sige handoff?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","選擇性、活化、應變與接觸需求需共同驗收。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Accept selectivity, activation, strain and contact requirements jointly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"選擇性、活化、應變與接觸需求需共同驗收。 奈米片源汲極不只提供載子，也把機械應力與電流接入多層通道，需檢查逐層端點連接。","explanationEn":"Accept selectivity, activation, strain and contact requirements jointly. Nanosheet source-drain provides carriers, stress and current to several channels, requiring per-layer endpoint connectivity checks."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a021","title":"平面 CMOS 製程整合","titleEn":"Planar CMOS process integration","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解井區、接面及互補電路連通，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["CMOS 功能與隔離","閘與接面","接觸及互連","電路與良率"],"labelsEn":["CMOS function and isolation","Gates and junctions","Contacts and interconnects","Circuit and yield"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a021-stage01","order":1,"title":"CMOS 功能與隔離","titleEn":"CMOS function and isolation","description":"在「CMOS 功能與隔離」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cmos function and isolation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a021-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"互補反相器","titleEn":"Draw a complementary inverter","objective":"完成「互補反相器」的因果圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw a complementary inverter, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：互補反相器。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：NMOS 與 PMOS 的連接決定靜態邏輯功能。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw a complementary inverter. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: NMOS and PMOS connectivity determines static logic function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「NMOS 與 PMOS 的連接決定靜態邏輯功能。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: NMOS and PMOS connectivity determines static logic function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「互補反相器」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw a complementary inverter and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「互補反相器」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw a complementary inverter: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-01-k1","title":"互補反相器的原理","titleEn":"Draw a complementary inverter principle","text":"NMOS 與 PMOS 的連接決定靜態邏輯功能。","textEn":"NMOS and PMOS connectivity determines static logic function."},{"id":"a021-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「互補反相器」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw a complementary inverter?","options":["NMOS 與 PMOS 的連接決定靜態邏輯功能。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["NMOS and PMOS connectivity determines static logic function.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"NMOS 與 PMOS 的連接決定靜態邏輯功能。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"NMOS and PMOS connectivity determines static logic function. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-01"],"title":"井區與基板","titleEn":"Assign wells and substrate","objective":"完成「井區與基板」的對照表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assign wells and substrate, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：井區與基板。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：不同極性元件需要適當的井及本體接點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign wells and substrate. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Different polarities need appropriate wells and body contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同極性元件需要適當的井及本體接點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different polarities need appropriate wells and body contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「井區與基板」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign wells and substrate and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「井區與基板」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assign wells and substrate: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-02-k1","title":"井區與基板的原理","titleEn":"Assign wells and substrate principle","text":"不同極性元件需要適當的井及本體接點。","textEn":"Different polarities need appropriate wells and body contacts."},{"id":"a021-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「井區與基板」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign wells and substrate?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","不同極性元件需要適當的井及本體接點。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Different polarities need appropriate wells and body contacts.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同極性元件需要適當的井及本體接點。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"Different polarities need appropriate wells and body contacts. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-02"],"title":"遮罩層次","titleEn":"Map mask hierarchy","objective":"完成「遮罩層次」的敏感度草圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map mask hierarchy, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遮罩層次。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：不同遮罩分別定義主動區、閘、接觸與配線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map mask hierarchy. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Separate masks define active areas, gates, contacts and wiring. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同遮罩分別定義主動區、閘、接觸與配線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Separate masks define active areas, gates, contacts and wiring. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「遮罩層次」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map mask hierarchy and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遮罩層次」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map mask hierarchy: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-03-k1","title":"遮罩層次的原理","titleEn":"Map mask hierarchy principle","text":"不同遮罩分別定義主動區、閘、接觸與配線。","textEn":"Separate masks define active areas, gates, contacts and wiring."},{"id":"a021-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遮罩層次」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map mask hierarchy?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","不同遮罩分別定義主動區、閘、接觸與配線。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Separate masks define active areas, gates, contacts and wiring."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同遮罩分別定義主動區、閘、接觸與配線。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"Separate masks define active areas, gates, contacts and wiring. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-03"],"title":"隔離與寄生","titleEn":"Map isolation and parasitics","objective":"完成「隔離與寄生」的故障判別表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for map isolation and parasitics, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離與寄生。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：隔離不足可能產生原電路圖未畫出的路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map isolation and parasitics. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Insufficient isolation can create paths absent from the intended schematic. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離不足可能產生原電路圖未畫出的路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Insufficient isolation can create paths absent from the intended schematic. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「隔離與寄生」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map isolation and parasitics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離與寄生」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for map isolation and parasitics: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-04-k1","title":"隔離與寄生的原理","titleEn":"Map isolation and parasitics principle","text":"隔離不足可能產生原電路圖未畫出的路徑。","textEn":"Insufficient isolation can create paths absent from the intended schematic."},{"id":"a021-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離與寄生」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map isolation and parasitics?","options":["隔離不足可能產生原電路圖未畫出的路徑。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Insufficient isolation can create paths absent from the intended schematic.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隔離不足可能產生原電路圖未畫出的路徑。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"Insufficient isolation can create paths absent from the intended schematic. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-04"],"title":"閂鎖路徑","titleEn":"Trace latch-up paths","objective":"完成「閂鎖路徑」的量測規劃，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace latch-up paths, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閂鎖路徑。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：寄生雙極路徑取決於井與基板電阻及接點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace latch-up paths. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Parasitic bipolar paths depend on well and substrate resistance and contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「寄生雙極路徑取決於井與基板電阻及接點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Parasitic bipolar paths depend on well and substrate resistance and contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「閂鎖路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace latch-up paths and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閂鎖路徑」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace latch-up paths: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-05-k1","title":"閂鎖路徑的原理","titleEn":"Trace latch-up paths principle","text":"寄生雙極路徑取決於井與基板電阻及接點。","textEn":"Parasitic bipolar paths depend on well and substrate resistance and contacts."},{"id":"a021-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閂鎖路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace latch-up paths?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","寄生雙極路徑取決於井與基板電阻及接點。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Parasitic bipolar paths depend on well and substrate resistance and contacts.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"寄生雙極路徑取決於井與基板電阻及接點。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"Parasitic bipolar paths depend on well and substrate resistance and contacts. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-05"],"title":"熱順序約束","titleEn":"Order thermal constraints","objective":"完成「熱順序約束」的工程驗收單，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for order thermal constraints, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱順序約束。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：高溫步驟會改變已形成的摻雜及薄膜。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Order thermal constraints. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: High-temperature steps modify existing dopants and films. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高溫步驟會改變已形成的摻雜及薄膜。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-temperature steps modify existing dopants and films. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「熱順序約束」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for order thermal constraints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱順序約束」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for order thermal constraints: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-06-k1","title":"熱順序約束的原理","titleEn":"Order thermal constraints principle","text":"高溫步驟會改變已形成的摻雜及薄膜。","textEn":"High-temperature steps modify existing dopants and films."},{"id":"a021-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","textEn":"An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱順序約束」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating order thermal constraints?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","高溫步驟會改變已形成的摻雜及薄膜。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","High-temperature steps modify existing dopants and films."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高溫步驟會改變已形成的摻雜及薄膜。 反相器功能來自互補拉高與拉低路徑，井與本體接點則協助維持電位及抑制寄生作用。","explanationEn":"High-temperature steps modify existing dopants and films. An inverter uses complementary pull-up and pull-down paths, while wells and body ties maintain potentials and suppress parasitics."}}]},{"id":"a021-stage02","order":2,"title":"閘與接面","titleEn":"Gates and junctions","description":"在「閘與接面」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for gates and junctions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a021-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-06"],"title":"閘介電層","titleEn":"Assess gate dielectric","objective":"完成「閘介電層」的因果圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess gate dielectric, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘介電層。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：閘電容、漏電與可靠度是不同需求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess gate dielectric. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Gate capacitance, leakage and reliability are distinct needs. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘電容、漏電與可靠度是不同需求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate capacitance, leakage and reliability are distinct needs. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「閘介電層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess gate dielectric and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘介電層」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess gate dielectric: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-07-k1","title":"閘介電層的原理","titleEn":"Assess gate dielectric principle","text":"閘電容、漏電與可靠度是不同需求。","textEn":"Gate capacitance, leakage and reliability are distinct needs."},{"id":"a021-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘介電層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess gate dielectric?","options":["閘電容、漏電與可靠度是不同需求。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Gate capacitance, leakage and reliability are distinct needs.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閘電容、漏電與可靠度是不同需求。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Gate capacitance, leakage and reliability are distinct needs. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}},{"id":"a021-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-07"],"title":"閘長轉移","titleEn":"Track gate-length transfer","objective":"完成「閘長轉移」的對照表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for track gate-length transfer, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘長轉移。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：光阻尺寸與最終電性通道長度不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track gate-length transfer. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Resist dimensions differ from final electrical channel length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光阻尺寸與最終電性通道長度不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Resist dimensions differ from final electrical channel length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「閘長轉移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track gate-length transfer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘長轉移」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for track gate-length transfer: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-08-k1","title":"閘長轉移的原理","titleEn":"Track gate-length transfer principle","text":"光阻尺寸與最終電性通道長度不同。","textEn":"Resist dimensions differ from final electrical channel length."},{"id":"a021-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘長轉移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track gate-length transfer?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","光阻尺寸與最終電性通道長度不同。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Resist dimensions differ from final electrical channel length.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光阻尺寸與最終電性通道長度不同。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Resist dimensions differ from final electrical channel length. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}},{"id":"a021-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-08"],"title":"延伸接面","titleEn":"Place source-drain extensions","objective":"完成「延伸接面」的敏感度草圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for place source-drain extensions, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：延伸接面。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：淺延伸接面在電場與串聯電阻間取捨。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Place source-drain extensions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Shallow extensions trade electric-field control against series resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「淺延伸接面在電場與串聯電阻間取捨。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Shallow extensions trade electric-field control against series resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「延伸接面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for place source-drain extensions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「延伸接面」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for place source-drain extensions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-09-k1","title":"延伸接面的原理","titleEn":"Place source-drain extensions principle","text":"淺延伸接面在電場與串聯電阻間取捨。","textEn":"Shallow extensions trade electric-field control against series resistance."},{"id":"a021-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「延伸接面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating place source-drain extensions?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","淺延伸接面在電場與串聯電阻間取捨。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Shallow extensions trade electric-field control against series resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"淺延伸接面在電場與串聯電阻間取捨。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Shallow extensions trade electric-field control against series resistance. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}},{"id":"a021-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-09"],"title":"側壁間隔層","titleEn":"Define sidewall spacers","objective":"完成「側壁間隔層」的故障判別表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define sidewall spacers, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：側壁間隔層。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：間隔層把後續接面位置與閘邊緣分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define sidewall spacers. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Spacers separate later junction placement from gate edges. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「間隔層把後續接面位置與閘邊緣分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Spacers separate later junction placement from gate edges. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「側壁間隔層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define sidewall spacers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「側壁間隔層」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define sidewall spacers: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-10-k1","title":"側壁間隔層的原理","titleEn":"Define sidewall spacers principle","text":"間隔層把後續接面位置與閘邊緣分開。","textEn":"Spacers separate later junction placement from gate edges."},{"id":"a021-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「側壁間隔層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define sidewall spacers?","options":["間隔層把後續接面位置與閘邊緣分開。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Spacers separate later junction placement from gate edges.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"間隔層把後續接面位置與閘邊緣分開。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Spacers separate later junction placement from gate edges. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}},{"id":"a021-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-10"],"title":"重摻雜接面","titleEn":"Define heavily doped junctions","objective":"完成「重摻雜接面」的量測規劃，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define heavily doped junctions, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重摻雜接面。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：低電阻源汲極仍需維持接面隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define heavily doped junctions. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Low-resistance source-drain regions still need junction isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低電阻源汲極仍需維持接面隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low-resistance source-drain regions still need junction isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「重摻雜接面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define heavily doped junctions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重摻雜接面」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define heavily doped junctions: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-11-k1","title":"重摻雜接面的原理","titleEn":"Define heavily doped junctions principle","text":"低電阻源汲極仍需維持接面隔離。","textEn":"Low-resistance source-drain regions still need junction isolation."},{"id":"a021-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重摻雜接面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define heavily doped junctions?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","低電阻源汲極仍需維持接面隔離。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Low-resistance source-drain regions still need junction isolation.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低電阻源汲極仍需維持接面隔離。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Low-resistance source-drain regions still need junction isolation. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}},{"id":"a021-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-11"],"title":"活化退火","titleEn":"Integrate activation anneals","objective":"完成「活化退火」的工程驗收單，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for integrate activation anneals, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化退火。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活化收益需與橫向擴散造成的通道縮短比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Integrate activation anneals. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Activation gain must be compared with lateral-diffusion channel shortening. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化收益需與橫向擴散造成的通道縮短比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation gain must be compared with lateral-diffusion channel shortening. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「活化退火」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for integrate activation anneals and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化退火」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for integrate activation anneals: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-12-k1","title":"活化退火的原理","titleEn":"Integrate activation anneals principle","text":"活化收益需與橫向擴散造成的通道縮短比較。","textEn":"Activation gain must be compared with lateral-diffusion channel shortening."},{"id":"a021-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","textEn":"Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化退火」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating integrate activation anneals?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","活化收益需與橫向擴散造成的通道縮短比較。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Activation gain must be compared with lateral-diffusion channel shortening."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活化收益需與橫向擴散造成的通道縮短比較。 側壁間隔使源汲極處理與閘邊緣形成幾何關聯，但橫向擴散仍會改變電性有效通道長度。","explanationEn":"Activation gain must be compared with lateral-diffusion channel shortening. Spacers geometrically relate junction processing to gate edges, but lateral diffusion still changes electrical channel length."}}]},{"id":"a021-stage03","order":3,"title":"接觸及互連","titleEn":"Contacts and interconnects","description":"在「接觸及互連」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contacts and interconnects, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a021-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-12"],"title":"矽化物形成","titleEn":"Assess silicide formation","objective":"完成「矽化物形成」的因果圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess silicide formation, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：矽化物形成。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：導電接觸反應也會消耗表面矽。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess silicide formation. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Conductive contact reactions also consume surface silicon. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「導電接觸反應也會消耗表面矽。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Conductive contact reactions also consume surface silicon. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「矽化物形成」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess silicide formation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「矽化物形成」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess silicide formation: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-13-k1","title":"矽化物形成的原理","titleEn":"Assess silicide formation principle","text":"導電接觸反應也會消耗表面矽。","textEn":"Conductive contact reactions also consume surface silicon."},{"id":"a021-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「矽化物形成」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess silicide formation?","options":["導電接觸反應也會消耗表面矽。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Conductive contact reactions also consume surface silicon.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導電接觸反應也會消耗表面矽。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Conductive contact reactions also consume surface silicon. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-13"],"title":"接觸孔位置","titleEn":"Place contact openings","objective":"完成「接觸孔位置」的對照表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for place contact openings, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸孔位置。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：接觸需落在目標區且避免碰到閘。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Place contact openings. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Contacts must land on targets while avoiding gates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸需落在目標區且避免碰到閘。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contacts must land on targets while avoiding gates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接觸孔位置」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for place contact openings and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸孔位置」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for place contact openings: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸孔位置的原理","titleEn":"Place contact openings principle","text":"接觸需落在目標區且避免碰到閘。","textEn":"Contacts must land on targets while avoiding gates."},{"id":"a021-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸孔位置」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating place contact openings?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","接觸需落在目標區且避免碰到閘。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Contacts must land on targets while avoiding gates.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸需落在目標區且避免碰到閘。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Contacts must land on targets while avoiding gates. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-14"],"title":"介電層平坦化","titleEn":"Plan dielectric planarization","objective":"完成「介電層平坦化」的敏感度草圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for plan dielectric planarization, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介電層平坦化。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：台階形貌會傳遞到後續微影對焦。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan dielectric planarization. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Topography propagates into later lithography focus requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「台階形貌會傳遞到後續微影對焦。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Topography propagates into later lithography focus requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「介電層平坦化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan dielectric planarization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介電層平坦化」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for plan dielectric planarization: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-15-k1","title":"介電層平坦化的原理","titleEn":"Plan dielectric planarization principle","text":"台階形貌會傳遞到後續微影對焦。","textEn":"Topography propagates into later lithography focus requirements."},{"id":"a021-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介電層平坦化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan dielectric planarization?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","台階形貌會傳遞到後續微影對焦。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Topography propagates into later lithography focus requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"台階形貌會傳遞到後續微影對焦。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Topography propagates into later lithography focus requirements. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-15"],"title":"第一層配線","titleEn":"Route first-level metal","objective":"完成「第一層配線」的故障判別表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for route first-level metal, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：第一層配線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：電源與訊號連接需對應原始反相器網表。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Route first-level metal. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Power and signal connections must match the inverter netlist. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電源與訊號連接需對應原始反相器網表。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Power and signal connections must match the inverter netlist. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「第一層配線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for route first-level metal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「第一層配線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for route first-level metal: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-16-k1","title":"第一層配線的原理","titleEn":"Route first-level metal principle","text":"電源與訊號連接需對應原始反相器網表。","textEn":"Power and signal connections must match the inverter netlist."},{"id":"a021-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「第一層配線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating route first-level metal?","options":["電源與訊號連接需對應原始反相器網表。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Power and signal connections must match the inverter netlist.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電源與訊號連接需對應原始反相器網表。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Power and signal connections must match the inverter netlist. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-16"],"title":"通孔連通","titleEn":"Verify via connectivity","objective":"完成「通孔連通」的量測規劃，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for verify via connectivity, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：通孔連通。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：幾何重疊不能代替電性連通測試。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Verify via connectivity. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Geometric overlap does not replace electrical continuity tests. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何重疊不能代替電性連通測試。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Geometric overlap does not replace electrical continuity tests. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「通孔連通」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for verify via connectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「通孔連通」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for verify via connectivity: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-17-k1","title":"通孔連通的原理","titleEn":"Verify via connectivity principle","text":"幾何重疊不能代替電性連通測試。","textEn":"Geometric overlap does not replace electrical continuity tests."},{"id":"a021-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「通孔連通」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating verify via connectivity?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","幾何重疊不能代替電性連通測試。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Geometric overlap does not replace electrical continuity tests.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何重疊不能代替電性連通測試。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Geometric overlap does not replace electrical continuity tests. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}},{"id":"a021-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-17"],"title":"天線效應","titleEn":"Trace antenna charging","objective":"完成「天線效應」的工程驗收單，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace antenna charging, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：天線效應。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：長導線在製程中可把電荷集中到薄閘介電層。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace antenna charging. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Long conductors can collect process charge onto thin gate dielectrics. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「長導線在製程中可把電荷集中到薄閘介電層。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Long conductors can collect process charge onto thin gate dielectrics. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「天線效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace antenna charging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「天線效應」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace antenna charging: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-18-k1","title":"天線效應的原理","titleEn":"Trace antenna charging principle","text":"長導線在製程中可把電荷集中到薄閘介電層。","textEn":"Long conductors can collect process charge onto thin gate dielectrics."},{"id":"a021-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","textEn":"Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「天線效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace antenna charging?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","長導線在製程中可把電荷集中到薄閘介電層。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Long conductors can collect process charge onto thin gate dielectrics."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長導線在製程中可把電荷集中到薄閘介電層。 接觸與互連把元件接成電路；元件 I-V 合格仍可能因開路、短路或過高寄生而無法工作。","explanationEn":"Long conductors can collect process charge onto thin gate dielectrics. Contacts and interconnects form the circuit; good device I-V can coexist with circuit failure from opens, shorts or parasitics."}}]},{"id":"a021-stage04","order":4,"title":"電路與良率","titleEn":"Circuit and yield","description":"在「電路與良率」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for circuit and yield, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a021-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-18"],"title":"轉移特性","titleEn":"Read inverter transfer curves","objective":"完成「轉移特性」的因果圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for read inverter transfer curves, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：轉移特性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：切換點取決於兩種元件的相對驅動能力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read inverter transfer curves. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Switching point depends on relative device strengths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「切換點取決於兩種元件的相對驅動能力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Switching point depends on relative device strengths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「轉移特性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read inverter transfer curves and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「轉移特性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for read inverter transfer curves: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-19-k1","title":"轉移特性的原理","titleEn":"Read inverter transfer curves principle","text":"切換點取決於兩種元件的相對驅動能力。","textEn":"Switching point depends on relative device strengths."},{"id":"a021-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「轉移特性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read inverter transfer curves?","options":["切換點取決於兩種元件的相對驅動能力。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Switching point depends on relative device strengths.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"切換點取決於兩種元件的相對驅動能力。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Switching point depends on relative device strengths. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}},{"id":"a021-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-19"],"title":"靜態功耗","titleEn":"Measure static power","objective":"完成「靜態功耗」的對照表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure static power, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：靜態功耗。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：理想互補邏輯仍有實際漏電與過渡導通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure static power. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Ideal complementary logic still has real leakage and transition conduction. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「理想互補邏輯仍有實際漏電與過渡導通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ideal complementary logic still has real leakage and transition conduction. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「靜態功耗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure static power and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「靜態功耗」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure static power: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-20-k1","title":"靜態功耗的原理","titleEn":"Measure static power principle","text":"理想互補邏輯仍有實際漏電與過渡導通。","textEn":"Ideal complementary logic still has real leakage and transition conduction."},{"id":"a021-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「靜態功耗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure static power?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","理想互補邏輯仍有實際漏電與過渡導通。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Ideal complementary logic still has real leakage and transition conduction.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想互補邏輯仍有實際漏電與過渡導通。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Ideal complementary logic still has real leakage and transition conduction. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}},{"id":"a021-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-20"],"title":"延遲與負載","titleEn":"Relate delay to load","objective":"完成「延遲與負載」的敏感度草圖，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for relate delay to load, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：延遲與負載。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：相同元件在不同負載電容下有不同延遲。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 用簡化充電模型 t≈CΔV/I 比較相同電流下負載電容加倍的延遲；再列實際反相器中電流不是常數的限制。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate delay to load. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Identical devices have different delays under different capacitive loads. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Use t≈CΔV/I to compare delay when capacitance doubles at fixed current. Then state the limitation that current is not constant in a real inverter.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同元件在不同負載電容下有不同延遲。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Identical devices have different delays under different capacitive loads. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「延遲與負載」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate delay to load and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「延遲與負載」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for relate delay to load: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-21-k1","title":"延遲與負載的原理","titleEn":"Relate delay to load principle","text":"相同元件在不同負載電容下有不同延遲。","textEn":"Identical devices have different delays under different capacitive loads."},{"id":"a021-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「延遲與負載」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate delay to load?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","相同元件在不同負載電容下有不同延遲。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Identical devices have different delays under different capacitive loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同元件在不同負載電容下有不同延遲。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Identical devices have different delays under different capacitive loads. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}},{"id":"a021-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-21"],"title":"製程角落","titleEn":"Compare process corners","objective":"完成「製程角落」的故障判別表，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare process corners, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：製程角落。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：典型值不能代表快慢與失配的組合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare process corners. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Typical values do not represent fast, slow and mismatch combinations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「典型值不能代表快慢與失配的組合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Typical values do not represent fast, slow and mismatch combinations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「製程角落」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare process corners and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「製程角落」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare process corners: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-22-k1","title":"製程角落的原理","titleEn":"Compare process corners principle","text":"典型值不能代表快慢與失配的組合。","textEn":"Typical values do not represent fast, slow and mismatch combinations."},{"id":"a021-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「製程角落」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare process corners?","options":["典型值不能代表快慢與失配的組合。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Typical values do not represent fast, slow and mismatch combinations.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"典型值不能代表快慢與失配的組合。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Typical values do not represent fast, slow and mismatch combinations. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}},{"id":"a021-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-22"],"title":"失效定位","titleEn":"Localize circuit failures","objective":"完成「失效定位」的量測規劃，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for localize circuit failures, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：失效定位。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：電路失效需回連到元件、接觸或互連證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Localize circuit failures. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Circuit failures need device, contact or interconnect evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電路失效需回連到元件、接觸或互連證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Circuit failures need device, contact or interconnect evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「失效定位」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for localize circuit failures and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「失效定位」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for localize circuit failures: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-23-k1","title":"失效定位的原理","titleEn":"Localize circuit failures principle","text":"電路失效需回連到元件、接觸或互連證據。","textEn":"Circuit failures need device, contact or interconnect evidence."},{"id":"a021-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「失效定位」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating localize circuit failures?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","電路失效需回連到元件、接觸或互連證據。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Circuit failures need device, contact or interconnect evidence.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電路失效需回連到元件、接觸或互連證據。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Circuit failures need device, contact or interconnect evidence. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}},{"id":"a021-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v8a-highk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a021-v8-23"],"title":"整合流程審查","titleEn":"Review the integrated flow","objective":"完成「整合流程審查」的工程驗收單，把井區、接面及互補電路連通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review the integrated flow, connecting relevant limits in wells, junctions and complementary-circuit connectivity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：整合流程審查。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：步驟可單獨合格仍可能在相互作用後失敗。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review the integrated flow. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Individually acceptable steps can fail through integration interactions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「步驟可單獨合格仍可能在相互作用後失敗。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Individually acceptable steps can fail through integration interactions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「整合流程審查」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review the integrated flow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「整合流程審查」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review the integrated flow: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a021-v8-24-k1","title":"整合流程審查的原理","titleEn":"Review the integrated flow principle","text":"步驟可單獨合格仍可能在相互作用後失敗。","textEn":"Individually acceptable steps can fail through integration interactions."},{"id":"a021-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","textEn":"Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「整合流程審查」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review the integrated flow?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","步驟可單獨合格仍可能在相互作用後失敗。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Individually acceptable steps can fail through integration interactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"步驟可單獨合格仍可能在相互作用後失敗。 負載電容充放電需要有限電流；延遲改善須同時考慮驅動、負載、電壓及切換條件。","explanationEn":"Individually acceptable steps can fail through integration interactions. Finite current charges load capacitance; delay improvements depend on drive, load, voltage and switching conditions."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a022","title":"鰭式電晶體製造","titleEn":"FinFET fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["鰭幾何與靜電","鰭與隔離","三維閘與接觸","變異與電路"],"labelsEn":["Fin geometry and electrostatics","Fins and isolation","3D gates and contacts","Variation and circuits"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a022-stage01","order":1,"title":"鰭幾何與靜電","titleEn":"Fin geometry and electrostatics","description":"在「鰭幾何與靜電」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for fin geometry and electrostatics, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a022-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"三面閘控制","titleEn":"Draw three-sided gate control","objective":"完成「三面閘控制」的因果圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw three-sided gate control, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：三面閘控制。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：閘對鰭側壁與頂面的控制不同於平面元件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw three-sided gate control. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Gate control over fin sides and top differs from planar devices. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘對鰭側壁與頂面的控制不同於平面元件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate control over fin sides and top differs from planar devices. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「三面閘控制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw three-sided gate control and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「三面閘控制」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw three-sided gate control: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-01-k1","title":"三面閘控制的原理","titleEn":"Draw three-sided gate control principle","text":"閘對鰭側壁與頂面的控制不同於平面元件。","textEn":"Gate control over fin sides and top differs from planar devices."},{"id":"a022-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「三面閘控制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw three-sided gate control?","options":["閘對鰭側壁與頂面的控制不同於平面元件。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Gate control over fin sides and top differs from planar devices.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閘對鰭側壁與頂面的控制不同於平面元件。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Gate control over fin sides and top differs from planar devices. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}},{"id":"a022-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-01"],"title":"有效通道寬","titleEn":"Estimate effective channel width","objective":"完成「有效通道寬」的對照表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for estimate effective channel width, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：有效通道寬。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：有效寬度與鰭高、鰭寬及鰭數相關。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂矩形鰭：高 30、寬 8 個單位。用 2H+W 比較一鰭與二鰭幾何有效寬度，再列各面遷移率、接觸及電容使電流不等比例的原因。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate effective channel width. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Effective width relates to fin height, fin width and fin count. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical rectangular fin: height 30 and width 8 units. Use 2H+W to compare one and two fins, then explain nonproportional current from face mobility, contacts and capacitance.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「有效寬度與鰭高、鰭寬及鰭數相關。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Effective width relates to fin height, fin width and fin count. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「有效通道寬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate effective channel width and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「有效通道寬」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for estimate effective channel width: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-02-k1","title":"有效通道寬的原理","titleEn":"Estimate effective channel width principle","text":"有效寬度與鰭高、鰭寬及鰭數相關。","textEn":"Effective width relates to fin height, fin width and fin count."},{"id":"a022-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「有效通道寬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate effective channel width?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","有效寬度與鰭高、鰭寬及鰭數相關。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Effective width relates to fin height, fin width and fin count.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有效寬度與鰭高、鰭寬及鰭數相關。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Effective width relates to fin height, fin width and fin count. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}},{"id":"a022-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-02"],"title":"鰭數量化","titleEn":"Assess quantized drive sizing","objective":"完成「鰭數量化」的敏感度草圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess quantized drive sizing, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭數量化。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：整數鰭數限制連續調整元件驅動能力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess quantized drive sizing. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Integer fin counts constrain continuous drive sizing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「整數鰭數限制連續調整元件驅動能力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Integer fin counts constrain continuous drive sizing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「鰭數量化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess quantized drive sizing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭數量化」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess quantized drive sizing: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-03-k1","title":"鰭數量化的原理","titleEn":"Assess quantized drive sizing principle","text":"整數鰭數限制連續調整元件驅動能力。","textEn":"Integer fin counts constrain continuous drive sizing."},{"id":"a022-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭數量化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess quantized drive sizing?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","整數鰭數限制連續調整元件驅動能力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Integer fin counts constrain continuous drive sizing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"整數鰭數限制連續調整元件驅動能力。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Integer fin counts constrain continuous drive sizing. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}},{"id":"a022-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-03"],"title":"鰭間距","titleEn":"Budget fin pitch","objective":"完成「鰭間距」的故障判別表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget fin pitch, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭間距。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：更小間距也增加填充與隔離困難。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget fin pitch. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Smaller pitch also increases fill and isolation difficulty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更小間距也增加填充與隔離困難。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Smaller pitch also increases fill and isolation difficulty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「鰭間距」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget fin pitch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭間距」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget fin pitch: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-04-k1","title":"鰭間距的原理","titleEn":"Budget fin pitch principle","text":"更小間距也增加填充與隔離困難。","textEn":"Smaller pitch also increases fill and isolation difficulty."},{"id":"a022-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭間距」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget fin pitch?","options":["更小間距也增加填充與隔離困難。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Smaller pitch also increases fill and isolation difficulty.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更小間距也增加填充與隔離困難。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Smaller pitch also increases fill and isolation difficulty. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}},{"id":"a022-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-04"],"title":"短通道指標","titleEn":"Choose short-channel metrics","objective":"完成「短通道指標」的量測規劃，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose short-channel metrics, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：短通道指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：導通電流需與關斷漏電及汲極耦合一起比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose short-channel metrics. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Compare on-current with off-leakage and drain coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「導通電流需與關斷漏電及汲極耦合一起比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Compare on-current with off-leakage and drain coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「短通道指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose short-channel metrics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「短通道指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose short-channel metrics: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-05-k1","title":"短通道指標的原理","titleEn":"Choose short-channel metrics principle","text":"導通電流需與關斷漏電及汲極耦合一起比較。","textEn":"Compare on-current with off-leakage and drain coupling."},{"id":"a022-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「短通道指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose short-channel metrics?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","導通電流需與關斷漏電及汲極耦合一起比較。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Compare on-current with off-leakage and drain coupling.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"導通電流需與關斷漏電及汲極耦合一起比較。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Compare on-current with off-leakage and drain coupling. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}},{"id":"a022-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-05"],"title":"版圖測試車","titleEn":"Lay out a test vehicle","objective":"完成「版圖測試車」的工程驗收單，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for lay out a test vehicle, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：版圖測試車。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：不同鰭數與密度需要可比較測試結構。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Lay out a test vehicle. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Fin count and density variants need comparable test structures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同鰭數與密度需要可比較測試結構。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fin count and density variants need comparable test structures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「版圖測試車」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for lay out a test vehicle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「版圖測試車」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for lay out a test vehicle: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-06-k1","title":"版圖測試車的原理","titleEn":"Lay out a test vehicle principle","text":"不同鰭數與密度需要可比較測試結構。","textEn":"Fin count and density variants need comparable test structures."},{"id":"a022-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","textEn":"For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「版圖測試車」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating lay out a test vehicle?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","不同鰭數與密度需要可比較測試結構。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Fin count and density variants need comparable test structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同鰭數與密度需要可比較測試結構。 對近矩形鰭，三面控制的幾何寬度約隨兩倍鰭高加鰭寬改變；實際電性還受各面遷移率影響。","explanationEn":"Fin count and density variants need comparable test structures. For a near-rectangular fin, geometric gated width scales roughly as twice height plus width; face-dependent mobility also matters."}}]},{"id":"a022-stage02","order":2,"title":"鰭與隔離","titleEn":"Fins and isolation","description":"在「鰭與隔離」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for fins and isolation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a022-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-06"],"title":"鰭圖案轉移","titleEn":"Track fin pattern transfer","objective":"完成「鰭圖案轉移」的因果圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for track fin pattern transfer, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭圖案轉移。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：硬遮罩與蝕刻偏差會累積到最終鰭寬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track fin pattern transfer. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Hard-mask and etch biases accumulate into final fin width. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「硬遮罩與蝕刻偏差會累積到最終鰭寬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Hard-mask and etch biases accumulate into final fin width. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「鰭圖案轉移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track fin pattern transfer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭圖案轉移」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for track fin pattern transfer: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-07-k1","title":"鰭圖案轉移的原理","titleEn":"Track fin pattern transfer principle","text":"硬遮罩與蝕刻偏差會累積到最終鰭寬。","textEn":"Hard-mask and etch biases accumulate into final fin width."},{"id":"a022-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭圖案轉移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track fin pattern transfer?","options":["硬遮罩與蝕刻偏差會累積到最終鰭寬。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Hard-mask and etch biases accumulate into final fin width.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"硬遮罩與蝕刻偏差會累積到最終鰭寬。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Hard-mask and etch biases accumulate into final fin width. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}},{"id":"a022-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-07"],"title":"鰭側壁角","titleEn":"Measure fin taper","objective":"完成「鰭側壁角」的對照表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure fin taper, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭側壁角。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：上下寬度差會改變電場與有效截面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure fin taper. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Top-bottom width differences alter fields and effective cross-section. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「上下寬度差會改變電場與有效截面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Top-bottom width differences alter fields and effective cross-section. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「鰭側壁角」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure fin taper and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭側壁角」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure fin taper: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-08-k1","title":"鰭側壁角的原理","titleEn":"Measure fin taper principle","text":"上下寬度差會改變電場與有效截面。","textEn":"Top-bottom width differences alter fields and effective cross-section."},{"id":"a022-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭側壁角」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure fin taper?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","上下寬度差會改變電場與有效截面。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Top-bottom width differences alter fields and effective cross-section.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上下寬度差會改變電場與有效截面。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Top-bottom width differences alter fields and effective cross-section. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}},{"id":"a022-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-08"],"title":"鰭粗糙度","titleEn":"Map fin roughness","objective":"完成「鰭粗糙度」的敏感度草圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map fin roughness, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭粗糙度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：邊緣起伏可轉為局部通道寬度變異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map fin roughness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Edge fluctuations translate into local channel-width variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊緣起伏可轉為局部通道寬度變異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Edge fluctuations translate into local channel-width variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「鰭粗糙度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map fin roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭粗糙度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map fin roughness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-09-k1","title":"鰭粗糙度的原理","titleEn":"Map fin roughness principle","text":"邊緣起伏可轉為局部通道寬度變異。","textEn":"Edge fluctuations translate into local channel-width variation."},{"id":"a022-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭粗糙度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map fin roughness?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","邊緣起伏可轉為局部通道寬度變異。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Edge fluctuations translate into local channel-width variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣起伏可轉為局部通道寬度變異。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Edge fluctuations translate into local channel-width variation. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}},{"id":"a022-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-09"],"title":"隔離填充","titleEn":"Inspect isolation fill","objective":"完成「隔離填充」的故障判別表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect isolation fill, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離填充。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：鰭間填充要避免空洞與不均應力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect isolation fill. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Inter-fin fill must avoid voids and nonuniform stress. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鰭間填充要避免空洞與不均應力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Inter-fin fill must avoid voids and nonuniform stress. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「隔離填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect isolation fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離填充」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect isolation fill: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-10-k1","title":"隔離填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect isolation fill principle","text":"鰭間填充要避免空洞與不均應力。","textEn":"Inter-fin fill must avoid voids and nonuniform stress."},{"id":"a022-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect isolation fill?","options":["鰭間填充要避免空洞與不均應力。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Inter-fin fill must avoid voids and nonuniform stress.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鰭間填充要避免空洞與不均應力。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Inter-fin fill must avoid voids and nonuniform stress. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}},{"id":"a022-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-10"],"title":"隔離回蝕","titleEn":"Control isolation recess evidence","objective":"完成「隔離回蝕」的量測規劃，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for control isolation recess evidence, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離回蝕。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：回蝕高度決定暴露鰭高。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Control isolation recess evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Isolation recess defines exposed fin height. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回蝕高度決定暴露鰭高。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation recess defines exposed fin height. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「隔離回蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for control isolation recess evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離回蝕」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for control isolation recess evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-11-k1","title":"隔離回蝕的原理","titleEn":"Control isolation recess evidence principle","text":"回蝕高度決定暴露鰭高。","textEn":"Isolation recess defines exposed fin height."},{"id":"a022-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離回蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating control isolation recess evidence?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","回蝕高度決定暴露鰭高。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Isolation recess defines exposed fin height.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回蝕高度決定暴露鰭高。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Isolation recess defines exposed fin height. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}},{"id":"a022-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-11"],"title":"鰭切割","titleEn":"Define fin cuts","objective":"完成「鰭切割」的工程驗收單，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for define fin cuts, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭切割。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：切割位置決定哪些鰭區實際連通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define fin cuts. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Fin cuts define actual connectivity between fin regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「切割位置決定哪些鰭區實際連通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fin cuts define actual connectivity between fin regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「鰭切割」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define fin cuts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭切割」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for define fin cuts: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-12-k1","title":"鰭切割的原理","titleEn":"Define fin cuts principle","text":"切割位置決定哪些鰭區實際連通。","textEn":"Fin cuts define actual connectivity between fin regions."},{"id":"a022-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","textEn":"Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭切割」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define fin cuts?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","切割位置決定哪些鰭區實際連通。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Fin cuts define actual connectivity between fin regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"切割位置決定哪些鰭區實際連通。 鰭寬、側壁角與隔離回蝕高度共同定義通道截面，三者量測應配準到同一位置。","explanationEn":"Fin cuts define actual connectivity between fin regions. Fin width, taper and isolation recess jointly define the channel section and need co-registered measurements."}}]},{"id":"a022-stage03","order":3,"title":"三維閘與接觸","titleEn":"3D gates and contacts","description":"在「三維閘與接觸」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for 3d gates and contacts, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a022-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-12"],"title":"三維介電覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess 3D dielectric coverage","objective":"完成「三維介電覆蓋」的因果圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess 3d dielectric coverage, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：三維介電覆蓋。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：頂部膜厚合格不代表側壁合格。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess 3D dielectric coverage. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Acceptable top thickness does not prove sidewall coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂部膜厚合格不代表側壁合格。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptable top thickness does not prove sidewall coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「三維介電覆蓋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess 3d dielectric coverage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「三維介電覆蓋」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess 3d dielectric coverage: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-13-k1","title":"三維介電覆蓋的原理","titleEn":"Assess 3D dielectric coverage principle","text":"頂部膜厚合格不代表側壁合格。","textEn":"Acceptable top thickness does not prove sidewall coverage."},{"id":"a022-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「三維介電覆蓋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess 3d dielectric coverage?","options":["頂部膜厚合格不代表側壁合格。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable top thickness does not prove sidewall coverage.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂部膜厚合格不代表側壁合格。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Acceptable top thickness does not prove sidewall coverage. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}},{"id":"a022-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-13"],"title":"替換閘腔","titleEn":"Inspect replacement-gate cavities","objective":"完成「替換閘腔」的對照表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect replacement-gate cavities, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：替換閘腔。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：窄腔需容納介電層、功函數層與填充金屬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect replacement-gate cavities. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Narrow cavities must accommodate dielectric, work-function and fill layers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「窄腔需容納介電層、功函數層與填充金屬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Narrow cavities must accommodate dielectric, work-function and fill layers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「替換閘腔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect replacement-gate cavities and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「替換閘腔」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect replacement-gate cavities: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-14-k1","title":"替換閘腔的原理","titleEn":"Inspect replacement-gate cavities principle","text":"窄腔需容納介電層、功函數層與填充金屬。","textEn":"Narrow cavities must accommodate dielectric, work-function and fill layers."},{"id":"a022-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「替換閘腔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect replacement-gate cavities?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","窄腔需容納介電層、功函數層與填充金屬。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Narrow cavities must accommodate dielectric, work-function and fill layers.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"窄腔需容納介電層、功函數層與填充金屬。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Narrow cavities must accommodate dielectric, work-function and fill layers. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}},{"id":"a022-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-14"],"title":"源汲極磊晶","titleEn":"Shape source-drain epitaxy","objective":"完成「源汲極磊晶」的敏感度草圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for shape source-drain epitaxy, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極磊晶。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：相鄰鰭磊晶合併會改變接觸形貌。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Shape source-drain epitaxy. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Coalesced epitaxy across fins changes contact geometry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相鄰鰭磊晶合併會改變接觸形貌。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Coalesced epitaxy across fins changes contact geometry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「源汲極磊晶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for shape source-drain epitaxy and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極磊晶」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for shape source-drain epitaxy: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-15-k1","title":"源汲極磊晶的原理","titleEn":"Shape source-drain epitaxy principle","text":"相鄰鰭磊晶合併會改變接觸形貌。","textEn":"Coalesced epitaxy across fins changes contact geometry."},{"id":"a022-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極磊晶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating shape source-drain epitaxy?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","相鄰鰭磊晶合併會改變接觸形貌。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Coalesced epitaxy across fins changes contact geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相鄰鰭磊晶合併會改變接觸形貌。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Coalesced epitaxy across fins changes contact geometry. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}},{"id":"a022-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-15"],"title":"間隔層覆蓋","titleEn":"Check spacer coverage","objective":"完成「間隔層覆蓋」的故障判別表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for check spacer coverage, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：間隔層覆蓋。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：側壁針孔可能造成閘與接觸漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check spacer coverage. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Sidewall pinholes can create gate-contact leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「側壁針孔可能造成閘與接觸漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sidewall pinholes can create gate-contact leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「間隔層覆蓋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check spacer coverage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「間隔層覆蓋」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for check spacer coverage: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-16-k1","title":"間隔層覆蓋的原理","titleEn":"Check spacer coverage principle","text":"側壁針孔可能造成閘與接觸漏電。","textEn":"Sidewall pinholes can create gate-contact leakage."},{"id":"a022-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「間隔層覆蓋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check spacer coverage?","options":["側壁針孔可能造成閘與接觸漏電。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall pinholes can create gate-contact leakage.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"側壁針孔可能造成閘與接觸漏電。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Sidewall pinholes can create gate-contact leakage. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}},{"id":"a022-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-16"],"title":"接觸落點","titleEn":"Assess contact landing","objective":"完成「接觸落點」的量測規劃，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess contact landing, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸落點。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：接觸窗口與磊晶形貌共同限制有效面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess contact landing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Contact windows and epitaxial shape jointly limit effective area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸窗口與磊晶形貌共同限制有效面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contact windows and epitaxial shape jointly limit effective area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接觸落點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess contact landing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸落點」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess contact landing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-17-k1","title":"接觸落點的原理","titleEn":"Assess contact landing principle","text":"接觸窗口與磊晶形貌共同限制有效面積。","textEn":"Contact windows and epitaxial shape jointly limit effective area."},{"id":"a022-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸落點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess contact landing?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","接觸窗口與磊晶形貌共同限制有效面積。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Contact windows and epitaxial shape jointly limit effective area.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸窗口與磊晶形貌共同限制有效面積。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Contact windows and epitaxial shape jointly limit effective area. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}},{"id":"a022-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-17"],"title":"串聯電阻","titleEn":"Separate series resistance","objective":"完成「串聯電阻」的工程驗收單，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for separate series resistance, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：串聯電阻。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：鰭增加的理想電流可能受接觸限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate series resistance. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Ideal current gains from fins can be contact limited. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鰭增加的理想電流可能受接觸限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ideal current gains from fins can be contact limited. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「串聯電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate series resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「串聯電阻」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for separate series resistance: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-18-k1","title":"串聯電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate series resistance principle","text":"鰭增加的理想電流可能受接觸限制。","textEn":"Ideal current gains from fins can be contact limited."},{"id":"a022-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","textEn":"Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「串聯電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate series resistance?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","鰭增加的理想電流可能受接觸限制。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Ideal current gains from fins can be contact limited."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鰭增加的理想電流可能受接觸限制。 三維閘堆疊增加側壁及角落界面，單一平面監控片不能完全代表成核、覆蓋與填充。","explanationEn":"Ideal current gains from fins can be contact limited. Three-dimensional gates add sidewall and corner interfaces; one planar monitor cannot fully represent nucleation, coverage and fill."}}]},{"id":"a022-stage04","order":4,"title":"變異與電路","titleEn":"Variation and circuits","description":"在「變異與電路」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for variation and circuits, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a022-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-18"],"title":"鰭高統計","titleEn":"Analyze fin-height distributions","objective":"完成「鰭高統計」的因果圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for analyze fin-height distributions, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鰭高統計。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：平均鰭高不足以評估局部驅動差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze fin-height distributions. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean fin height is insufficient for local drive variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均鰭高不足以評估局部驅動差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean fin height is insufficient for local drive variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「鰭高統計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze fin-height distributions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鰭高統計」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for analyze fin-height distributions: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-19-k1","title":"鰭高統計的原理","titleEn":"Analyze fin-height distributions principle","text":"平均鰭高不足以評估局部驅動差異。","textEn":"Mean fin height is insufficient for local drive variation."},{"id":"a022-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鰭高統計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze fin-height distributions?","options":["平均鰭高不足以評估局部驅動差異。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Mean fin height is insufficient for local drive variation.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均鰭高不足以評估局部驅動差異。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Mean fin height is insufficient for local drive variation. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}},{"id":"a022-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-19"],"title":"閾值分布","titleEn":"Measure threshold distributions","objective":"完成「閾值分布」的對照表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure threshold distributions, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值分布。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：幾何、功函數及陷阱皆可能造成分布展寬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure threshold distributions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Geometry, work function and traps can broaden distributions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何、功函數及陷阱皆可能造成分布展寬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Geometry, work function and traps can broaden distributions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「閾值分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure threshold distributions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值分布」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure threshold distributions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-20-k1","title":"閾值分布的原理","titleEn":"Measure threshold distributions principle","text":"幾何、功函數及陷阱皆可能造成分布展寬。","textEn":"Geometry, work function and traps can broaden distributions."},{"id":"a022-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure threshold distributions?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","幾何、功函數及陷阱皆可能造成分布展寬。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Geometry, work function and traps can broaden distributions.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何、功函數及陷阱皆可能造成分布展寬。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Geometry, work function and traps can broaden distributions. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}},{"id":"a022-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-20"],"title":"自熱效應","titleEn":"Assess fin self-heating","objective":"完成「自熱效應」的敏感度草圖，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess fin self-heating, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自熱效應。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：狹窄熱路徑可提高通道溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess fin self-heating. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Narrow heat paths can elevate channel temperature. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「狹窄熱路徑可提高通道溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Narrow heat paths can elevate channel temperature. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「自熱效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess fin self-heating and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自熱效應」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess fin self-heating: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-21-k1","title":"自熱效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess fin self-heating principle","text":"狹窄熱路徑可提高通道溫度。","textEn":"Narrow heat paths can elevate channel temperature."},{"id":"a022-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自熱效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess fin self-heating?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","狹窄熱路徑可提高通道溫度。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Narrow heat paths can elevate channel temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"狹窄熱路徑可提高通道溫度。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Narrow heat paths can elevate channel temperature. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}},{"id":"a022-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-21"],"title":"寄生電容","titleEn":"Budget parasitic capacitance","objective":"完成「寄生電容」的故障判別表，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget parasitic capacitance, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：寄生電容。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：較高鰭可能同時提高驅動及寄生負載。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget parasitic capacitance. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Taller fins can increase both drive and parasitic loading. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較高鰭可能同時提高驅動及寄生負載。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Taller fins can increase both drive and parasitic loading. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「寄生電容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget parasitic capacitance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「寄生電容」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget parasitic capacitance: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-22-k1","title":"寄生電容的原理","titleEn":"Budget parasitic capacitance principle","text":"較高鰭可能同時提高驅動及寄生負載。","textEn":"Taller fins can increase both drive and parasitic loading."},{"id":"a022-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「寄生電容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget parasitic capacitance?","options":["較高鰭可能同時提高驅動及寄生負載。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Taller fins can increase both drive and parasitic loading.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"較高鰭可能同時提高驅動及寄生負載。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Taller fins can increase both drive and parasitic loading. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}},{"id":"a022-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-22"],"title":"標準元件密度","titleEn":"Assess cell-level density","objective":"完成「標準元件密度」的量測規劃，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess cell-level density, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：標準元件密度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：元件縮小不保證配線後標準元件同比縮小。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess cell-level density. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Device scaling does not guarantee equal cell scaling after routing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元件縮小不保證配線後標準元件同比縮小。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Device scaling does not guarantee equal cell scaling after routing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「標準元件密度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess cell-level density and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「標準元件密度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess cell-level density: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-23-k1","title":"標準元件密度的原理","titleEn":"Assess cell-level density principle","text":"元件縮小不保證配線後標準元件同比縮小。","textEn":"Device scaling does not guarantee equal cell scaling after routing."},{"id":"a022-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「標準元件密度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess cell-level density?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","元件縮小不保證配線後標準元件同比縮小。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Device scaling does not guarantee equal cell scaling after routing.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"元件縮小不保證配線後標準元件同比縮小。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Device scaling does not guarantee equal cell scaling after routing. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}},{"id":"a022-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-ald","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a022-v8-23"],"title":"FinFET 整合驗收","titleEn":"Accept FinFET integration","objective":"完成「FinFET 整合驗收」的工程驗收單，把鰭形貌、三面閘及量化驅動中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept finfet integration, connecting relevant limits in fin geometry, three-sided gates and quantized drive to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：FinFET 整合驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：靜電、電阻、變異與標準元件效能需一起審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept FinFET integration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review electrostatics, resistance, variability and cell performance jointly. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「靜電、電阻、變異與標準元件效能需一起審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review electrostatics, resistance, variability and cell performance jointly. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「FinFET 整合驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept finfet integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「FinFET 整合驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept finfet integration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a022-v8-24-k1","title":"FinFET 整合驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept FinFET integration principle","text":"靜電、電阻、變異與標準元件效能需一起審查。","textEn":"Review electrostatics, resistance, variability and cell performance jointly."},{"id":"a022-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","textEn":"Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「FinFET 整合驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept finfet integration?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","靜電、電阻、變異與標準元件效能需一起審查。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Review electrostatics, resistance, variability and cell performance jointly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜電、電阻、變異與標準元件效能需一起審查。 鰭數是整數，所以標準元件驅動尺寸不是任意連續變數；元件庫需把此量化與配線限制一起設計。","explanationEn":"Review electrostatics, resistance, variability and cell performance jointly. Fin count is integer, so cell drive is not continuously adjustable; libraries must combine this quantization with routing constraints."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a023","title":"環繞閘極奈米片電晶體","titleEn":"Gate-all-around nanosheet transistors","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["奈米片堆疊","內間隔與源汲極","釋放與環繞閘","每層及電路驗證"],"labelsEn":["Nanosheet stacks","Inner spacers and source-drain","Release and wraparound gate","Per-sheet and circuit validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a023-stage01","order":1,"title":"奈米片堆疊","titleEn":"Nanosheet stacks","description":"在「奈米片堆疊」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for nanosheet stacks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a023-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"環繞閘拓撲","titleEn":"Draw the gate-all-around topology","objective":"完成「環繞閘拓撲」的因果圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw the gate-all-around topology, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：環繞閘拓撲。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：閘須包覆通道四周而非只有上表面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw the gate-all-around topology. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: The gate surrounds the channel rather than covering only its top. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘須包覆通道四周而非只有上表面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The gate surrounds the channel rather than covering only its top. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「環繞閘拓撲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw the gate-all-around topology and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「環繞閘拓撲」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw the gate-all-around topology: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-01-k1","title":"環繞閘拓撲的原理","titleEn":"Draw the gate-all-around topology principle","text":"閘須包覆通道四周而非只有上表面。","textEn":"The gate surrounds the channel rather than covering only its top."},{"id":"a023-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「環繞閘拓撲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw the gate-all-around topology?","options":["閘須包覆通道四周而非只有上表面。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["The gate surrounds the channel rather than covering only its top.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閘須包覆通道四周而非只有上表面。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"The gate surrounds the channel rather than covering only its top. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}},{"id":"a023-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-01"],"title":"堆疊層角色","titleEn":"Assign stack-layer roles","objective":"完成「堆疊層角色」的對照表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assign stack-layer roles, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：堆疊層角色。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：通道層與可移除犧牲層需分開標示。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign stack-layer roles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Channel layers and removable sacrificial layers need separate labels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「通道層與可移除犧牲層需分開標示。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Channel layers and removable sacrificial layers need separate labels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「堆疊層角色」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign stack-layer roles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「堆疊層角色」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assign stack-layer roles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-02-k1","title":"堆疊層角色的原理","titleEn":"Assign stack-layer roles principle","text":"通道層與可移除犧牲層需分開標示。","textEn":"Channel layers and removable sacrificial layers need separate labels."},{"id":"a023-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「堆疊層角色」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign stack-layer roles?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","通道層與可移除犧牲層需分開標示。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Channel layers and removable sacrificial layers need separate labels.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通道層與可移除犧牲層需分開標示。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"Channel layers and removable sacrificial layers need separate labels. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}},{"id":"a023-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-02"],"title":"片寬與驅動","titleEn":"Relate sheet width and drive","objective":"完成「片寬與驅動」的敏感度草圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for relate sheet width and drive, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片寬與驅動。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：較寬通道增加驅動但也改變電容與機械穩定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate sheet width and drive. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Wider sheets change drive, capacitance and mechanical stability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較寬通道增加驅動但也改變電容與機械穩定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wider sheets change drive, capacitance and mechanical stability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「片寬與驅動」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate sheet width and drive and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片寬與驅動」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for relate sheet width and drive: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-03-k1","title":"片寬與驅動的原理","titleEn":"Relate sheet width and drive principle","text":"較寬通道增加驅動但也改變電容與機械穩定。","textEn":"Wider sheets change drive, capacitance and mechanical stability."},{"id":"a023-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片寬與驅動」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate sheet width and drive?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","較寬通道增加驅動但也改變電容與機械穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Wider sheets change drive, capacitance and mechanical stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"較寬通道增加驅動但也改變電容與機械穩定。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"Wider sheets change drive, capacitance and mechanical stability. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}},{"id":"a023-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-03"],"title":"層間距預算","titleEn":"Budget inter-sheet spacing","objective":"完成「層間距預算」的故障判別表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget inter-sheet spacing, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：層間距預算。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：間距需容納介電、功函數及閘金屬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂間隙預算：片間距 20 個單位，兩側各需介電 2、功函數層 3；算中間剩餘填充空間，再讓每側功函數層各增加 1 單位檢查裕度。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget inter-sheet spacing. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Spacing must fit dielectric, work-function and gate metal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical gap budget: spacing 20 units, each face needs dielectric 2 and work-function metal 3. Calculate remaining fill space and test margin after increasing each face’s work-function layer by 1 unit.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「間距需容納介電、功函數及閘金屬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Spacing must fit dielectric, work-function and gate metal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「層間距預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget inter-sheet spacing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「層間距預算」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget inter-sheet spacing: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-04-k1","title":"層間距預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget inter-sheet spacing principle","text":"間距需容納介電、功函數及閘金屬。","textEn":"Spacing must fit dielectric, work-function and gate metal."},{"id":"a023-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「層間距預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget inter-sheet spacing?","options":["間距需容納介電、功函數及閘金屬。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Spacing must fit dielectric, work-function and gate metal.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"間距需容納介電、功函數及閘金屬。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"Spacing must fit dielectric, work-function and gate metal. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}},{"id":"a023-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-04"],"title":"底部隔離","titleEn":"Define bottom isolation","objective":"完成「底部隔離」的量測規劃，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define bottom isolation, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部隔離。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：底部寄生通道不能因上層環繞閘而自動消失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define bottom isolation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Bottom parasitic conduction does not vanish merely because upper sheets are gated. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「底部寄生通道不能因上層環繞閘而自動消失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bottom parasitic conduction does not vanish merely because upper sheets are gated. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「底部隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define bottom isolation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部隔離」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define bottom isolation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-05-k1","title":"底部隔離的原理","titleEn":"Define bottom isolation principle","text":"底部寄生通道不能因上層環繞閘而自動消失。","textEn":"Bottom parasitic conduction does not vanish merely because upper sheets are gated."},{"id":"a023-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define bottom isolation?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","底部寄生通道不能因上層環繞閘而自動消失。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Bottom parasitic conduction does not vanish merely because upper sheets are gated.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"底部寄生通道不能因上層環繞閘而自動消失。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"Bottom parasitic conduction does not vanish merely because upper sheets are gated. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}},{"id":"a023-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-05"],"title":"堆疊均勻性","titleEn":"Map stack uniformity","objective":"完成「堆疊均勻性」的工程驗收單，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for map stack uniformity, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：堆疊均勻性。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：各層厚度偏差可形成不同電性通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map stack uniformity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Layer-thickness variation can create electrically different channels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「各層厚度偏差可形成不同電性通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Layer-thickness variation can create electrically different channels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「堆疊均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map stack uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「堆疊均勻性」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for map stack uniformity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-06-k1","title":"堆疊均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Map stack uniformity principle","text":"各層厚度偏差可形成不同電性通道。","textEn":"Layer-thickness variation can create electrically different channels."},{"id":"a023-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","textEn":"Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「堆疊均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map stack uniformity?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","各層厚度偏差可形成不同電性通道。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Layer-thickness variation can create electrically different channels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各層厚度偏差可形成不同電性通道。 奈米片有效通道寬與片周長及片數相關，但片間空間同時限制閘金屬體積。","explanationEn":"Layer-thickness variation can create electrically different channels. Effective channel width relates to sheet perimeter and count, while inter-sheet spacing limits gate-metal volume."}}]},{"id":"a023-stage02","order":2,"title":"內間隔與源汲極","titleEn":"Inner spacers and source-drain","description":"在「內間隔與源汲極」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for inner spacers and source-drain, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a023-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-06"],"title":"源汲極凹槽","titleEn":"Define source-drain recess","objective":"完成「源汲極凹槽」的因果圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define source-drain recess, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極凹槽。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：凹槽會暴露各片端點並設定後續磊晶區域。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define source-drain recess. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: The recess exposes sheet ends and defines subsequent epitaxial regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「凹槽會暴露各片端點並設定後續磊晶區域。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The recess exposes sheet ends and defines subsequent epitaxial regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「源汲極凹槽」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define source-drain recess and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極凹槽」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define source-drain recess: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-07-k1","title":"源汲極凹槽的原理","titleEn":"Define source-drain recess principle","text":"凹槽會暴露各片端點並設定後續磊晶區域。","textEn":"The recess exposes sheet ends and defines subsequent epitaxial regions."},{"id":"a023-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極凹槽」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define source-drain recess?","options":["凹槽會暴露各片端點並設定後續磊晶區域。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["The recess exposes sheet ends and defines subsequent epitaxial regions.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"凹槽會暴露各片端點並設定後續磊晶區域。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"The recess exposes sheet ends and defines subsequent epitaxial regions. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}},{"id":"a023-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-07"],"title":"犧牲層側向凹蝕","titleEn":"Recess sacrificial layers laterally","objective":"完成「犧牲層側向凹蝕」的對照表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for recess sacrificial layers laterally, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：犧牲層側向凹蝕。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：凹蝕深度決定內間隔層的可用長度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Recess sacrificial layers laterally. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Lateral recess determines available inner-spacer length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「凹蝕深度決定內間隔層的可用長度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lateral recess determines available inner-spacer length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「犧牲層側向凹蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for recess sacrificial layers laterally and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「犧牲層側向凹蝕」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for recess sacrificial layers laterally: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-08-k1","title":"犧牲層側向凹蝕的原理","titleEn":"Recess sacrificial layers laterally principle","text":"凹蝕深度決定內間隔層的可用長度。","textEn":"Lateral recess determines available inner-spacer length."},{"id":"a023-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「犧牲層側向凹蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating recess sacrificial layers laterally?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","凹蝕深度決定內間隔層的可用長度。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Lateral recess determines available inner-spacer length.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"凹蝕深度決定內間隔層的可用長度。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"Lateral recess determines available inner-spacer length. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}},{"id":"a023-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-08"],"title":"內間隔填充","titleEn":"Inspect inner-spacer fill","objective":"完成「內間隔填充」的敏感度草圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect inner-spacer fill, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：內間隔填充。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：空洞或不完整保護會影響後續釋放。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect inner-spacer fill. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Voids or incomplete protection affect later release. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「空洞或不完整保護會影響後續釋放。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Voids or incomplete protection affect later release. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「內間隔填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect inner-spacer fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「內間隔填充」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect inner-spacer fill: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-09-k1","title":"內間隔填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect inner-spacer fill principle","text":"空洞或不完整保護會影響後續釋放。","textEn":"Voids or incomplete protection affect later release."},{"id":"a023-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「內間隔填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect inner-spacer fill?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","空洞或不完整保護會影響後續釋放。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Voids or incomplete protection affect later release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"空洞或不完整保護會影響後續釋放。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"Voids or incomplete protection affect later release. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}},{"id":"a023-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-09"],"title":"端點清潔","titleEn":"Assess sheet-end cleaning","objective":"完成「端點清潔」的故障判別表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess sheet-end cleaning, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：端點清潔。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：清潔需保留薄通道端點與間隔層。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess sheet-end cleaning. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Cleaning must preserve thin channel ends and spacers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清潔需保留薄通道端點與間隔層。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Cleaning must preserve thin channel ends and spacers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「端點清潔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess sheet-end cleaning and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「端點清潔」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess sheet-end cleaning: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-10-k1","title":"端點清潔的原理","titleEn":"Assess sheet-end cleaning principle","text":"清潔需保留薄通道端點與間隔層。","textEn":"Cleaning must preserve thin channel ends and spacers."},{"id":"a023-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「端點清潔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess sheet-end cleaning?","options":["清潔需保留薄通道端點與間隔層。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Cleaning must preserve thin channel ends and spacers.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清潔需保留薄通道端點與間隔層。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"Cleaning must preserve thin channel ends and spacers. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}},{"id":"a023-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-10"],"title":"源汲極合併","titleEn":"Assess source-drain coalescence","objective":"完成「源汲極合併」的量測規劃，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess source-drain coalescence, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極合併。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同高度成長前緣合併可能產生缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess source-drain coalescence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Growth fronts at different heights can merge with defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同高度成長前緣合併可能產生缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Growth fronts at different heights can merge with defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「源汲極合併」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess source-drain coalescence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極合併」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess source-drain coalescence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-11-k1","title":"源汲極合併的原理","titleEn":"Assess source-drain coalescence principle","text":"不同高度成長前緣合併可能產生缺陷。","textEn":"Growth fronts at different heights can merge with defects."},{"id":"a023-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極合併」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess source-drain coalescence?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","不同高度成長前緣合併可能產生缺陷。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Growth fronts at different heights can merge with defects.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同高度成長前緣合併可能產生缺陷。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"Growth fronts at different heights can merge with defects. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}},{"id":"a023-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-11"],"title":"應變傳遞","titleEn":"Trace strain transfer","objective":"完成「應變傳遞」的工程驗收單，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace strain transfer, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應變傳遞。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：各層受拘束與支撐不同，應變可能不相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace strain transfer. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Different constraints and supports can give layers different strain. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「各層受拘束與支撐不同，應變可能不相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different constraints and supports can give layers different strain. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「應變傳遞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace strain transfer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應變傳遞」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace strain transfer: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-12-k1","title":"應變傳遞的原理","titleEn":"Trace strain transfer principle","text":"各層受拘束與支撐不同，應變可能不相同。","textEn":"Different constraints and supports can give layers different strain."},{"id":"a023-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","textEn":"Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應變傳遞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace strain transfer?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","各層受拘束與支撐不同，應變可能不相同。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Different constraints and supports can give layers different strain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各層受拘束與支撐不同，應變可能不相同。 內間隔在源汲極與可移除犧牲層間提供保護，使後續釋放能避免破壞電流進入端。","explanationEn":"Different constraints and supports can give layers different strain. Inner spacers protect the source-drain from removable sacrificial layers, preserving current-entry regions during release."}}]},{"id":"a023-stage03","order":3,"title":"釋放與環繞閘","titleEn":"Release and wraparound gate","description":"在「釋放與環繞閘」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for release and wraparound gate, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a023-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-12"],"title":"犧牲層選蝕","titleEn":"Assess sacrificial-layer selectivity","objective":"完成「犧牲層選蝕」的因果圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess sacrificial-layer selectivity, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：犧牲層選蝕。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：需要移除犧牲層而盡量保留通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess sacrificial-layer selectivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Sacrificial material must be removed while preserving channels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需要移除犧牲層而盡量保留通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sacrificial material must be removed while preserving channels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「犧牲層選蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess sacrificial-layer selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「犧牲層選蝕」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess sacrificial-layer selectivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-13-k1","title":"犧牲層選蝕的原理","titleEn":"Assess sacrificial-layer selectivity principle","text":"需要移除犧牲層而盡量保留通道。","textEn":"Sacrificial material must be removed while preserving channels."},{"id":"a023-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「犧牲層選蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess sacrificial-layer selectivity?","options":["需要移除犧牲層而盡量保留通道。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Sacrificial material must be removed while preserving channels.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"需要移除犧牲層而盡量保留通道。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"Sacrificial material must be removed while preserving channels. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}},{"id":"a023-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-13"],"title":"釋放完整性","titleEn":"Check release completeness","objective":"完成「釋放完整性」的對照表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for check release completeness, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：釋放完整性。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：入口已開不代表最深處已完全釋放。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check release completeness. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: An open entrance does not prove complete release at depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「入口已開不代表最深處已完全釋放。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An open entrance does not prove complete release at depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「釋放完整性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check release completeness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「釋放完整性」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for check release completeness: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-14-k1","title":"釋放完整性的原理","titleEn":"Check release completeness principle","text":"入口已開不代表最深處已完全釋放。","textEn":"An open entrance does not prove complete release at depth."},{"id":"a023-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「釋放完整性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check release completeness?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","入口已開不代表最深處已完全釋放。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","An open entrance does not prove complete release at depth.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口已開不代表最深處已完全釋放。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"An open entrance does not prove complete release at depth. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}},{"id":"a023-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-14"],"title":"通道塌陷","titleEn":"Inspect sheet collapse","objective":"完成「通道塌陷」的敏感度草圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect sheet collapse, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：通道塌陷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：釋放後支撐及表面力可能改變幾何。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect sheet collapse. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Support and surface forces can change geometry after release. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「釋放後支撐及表面力可能改變幾何。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Support and surface forces can change geometry after release. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「通道塌陷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect sheet collapse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「通道塌陷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect sheet collapse: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-15-k1","title":"通道塌陷的原理","titleEn":"Inspect sheet collapse principle","text":"釋放後支撐及表面力可能改變幾何。","textEn":"Support and surface forces can change geometry after release."},{"id":"a023-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「通道塌陷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect sheet collapse?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","釋放後支撐及表面力可能改變幾何。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Support and surface forces can change geometry after release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"釋放後支撐及表面力可能改變幾何。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"Support and surface forces can change geometry after release. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}},{"id":"a023-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-15"],"title":"環繞介電層","titleEn":"Inspect wraparound dielectric","objective":"完成「環繞介電層」的故障判別表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect wraparound dielectric, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：環繞介電層。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：四面及片間都需要連續介電覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect wraparound dielectric. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Continuous dielectric is needed around sheets and between layers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「四面及片間都需要連續介電覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Continuous dielectric is needed around sheets and between layers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「環繞介電層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect wraparound dielectric and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「環繞介電層」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect wraparound dielectric: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-16-k1","title":"環繞介電層的原理","titleEn":"Inspect wraparound dielectric principle","text":"四面及片間都需要連續介電覆蓋。","textEn":"Continuous dielectric is needed around sheets and between layers."},{"id":"a023-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「環繞介電層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect wraparound dielectric?","options":["四面及片間都需要連續介電覆蓋。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Continuous dielectric is needed around sheets and between layers.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"四面及片間都需要連續介電覆蓋。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"Continuous dielectric is needed around sheets and between layers. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}},{"id":"a023-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-16"],"title":"功函數金屬","titleEn":"Budget work-function metal","objective":"完成「功函數金屬」的量測規劃，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for budget work-function metal, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：功函數金屬。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：最窄間隙決定材料堆疊可用空間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget work-function metal. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: The narrowest gap limits available stack space. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「最窄間隙決定材料堆疊可用空間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The narrowest gap limits available stack space. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「功函數金屬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget work-function metal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「功函數金屬」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for budget work-function metal: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-17-k1","title":"功函數金屬的原理","titleEn":"Budget work-function metal principle","text":"最窄間隙決定材料堆疊可用空間。","textEn":"The narrowest gap limits available stack space."},{"id":"a023-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「功函數金屬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget work-function metal?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","最窄間隙決定材料堆疊可用空間。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The narrowest gap limits available stack space.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最窄間隙決定材料堆疊可用空間。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"The narrowest gap limits available stack space. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}},{"id":"a023-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-17"],"title":"閘填充空洞","titleEn":"Locate gate-fill voids","objective":"完成「閘填充空洞」的工程驗收單，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate gate-fill voids, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘填充空洞。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：片間金屬不連續可能影響閘控制及電阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate gate-fill voids. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Discontinuous inter-sheet metal can affect gate control and resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片間金屬不連續可能影響閘控制及電阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Discontinuous inter-sheet metal can affect gate control and resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「閘填充空洞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate gate-fill voids and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘填充空洞」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate gate-fill voids: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-18-k1","title":"閘填充空洞的原理","titleEn":"Locate gate-fill voids principle","text":"片間金屬不連續可能影響閘控制及電阻。","textEn":"Discontinuous inter-sheet metal can affect gate control and resistance."},{"id":"a023-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","textEn":"Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘填充空洞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate gate-fill voids?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","片間金屬不連續可能影響閘控制及電阻。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Discontinuous inter-sheet metal can affect gate control and resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"片間金屬不連續可能影響閘控制及電阻。 釋放讓通道失去原先的連續支撐，也暴露更多表面；機械穩定與表面損傷需要同步驗證。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous inter-sheet metal can affect gate control and resistance. Release removes continuous support and exposes more surface, requiring simultaneous checks of mechanical stability and surface damage."}}]},{"id":"a023-stage04","order":4,"title":"每層及電路驗證","titleEn":"Per-sheet and circuit validation","description":"在「每層及電路驗證」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for per-sheet and circuit validation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a023-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-18"],"title":"每層電性差","titleEn":"Assess per-sheet differences","objective":"完成「每層電性差」的因果圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess per-sheet differences, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：每層電性差。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：總電流合格可能掩蓋某一層失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess per-sheet differences. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Acceptable total current can hide one failed layer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「總電流合格可能掩蓋某一層失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptable total current can hide one failed layer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「每層電性差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess per-sheet differences and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「每層電性差」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess per-sheet differences: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-19-k1","title":"每層電性差的原理","titleEn":"Assess per-sheet differences principle","text":"總電流合格可能掩蓋某一層失效。","textEn":"Acceptable total current can hide one failed layer."},{"id":"a023-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「每層電性差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess per-sheet differences?","options":["總電流合格可能掩蓋某一層失效。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current can hide one failed layer.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總電流合格可能掩蓋某一層失效。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"Acceptable total current can hide one failed layer. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}},{"id":"a023-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-19"],"title":"短通道控制","titleEn":"Assess short-channel control","objective":"完成「短通道控制」的對照表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess short-channel control, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：短通道控制。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：更完整閘包覆仍需確認接面與接觸寄生。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess short-channel control. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: More complete gate coverage still requires junction and contact checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更完整閘包覆仍需確認接面與接觸寄生。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: More complete gate coverage still requires junction and contact checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「短通道控制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess short-channel control and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「短通道控制」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess short-channel control: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-20-k1","title":"短通道控制的原理","titleEn":"Assess short-channel control principle","text":"更完整閘包覆仍需確認接面與接觸寄生。","textEn":"More complete gate coverage still requires junction and contact checks."},{"id":"a023-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「短通道控制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess short-channel control?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","更完整閘包覆仍需確認接面與接觸寄生。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","More complete gate coverage still requires junction and contact checks.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更完整閘包覆仍需確認接面與接觸寄生。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"More complete gate coverage still requires junction and contact checks. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}},{"id":"a023-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-20"],"title":"寄生電容預算","titleEn":"Budget parasitic capacitance","objective":"完成「寄生電容預算」的敏感度草圖，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget parasitic capacitance, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：寄生電容預算。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：內間隔厚度與介電常數改變閘源汲耦合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget parasitic capacitance. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Inner-spacer thickness and permittivity change gate-source/drain coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「內間隔厚度與介電常數改變閘源汲耦合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Inner-spacer thickness and permittivity change gate-source/drain coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「寄生電容預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget parasitic capacitance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「寄生電容預算」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget parasitic capacitance: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-21-k1","title":"寄生電容預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget parasitic capacitance principle","text":"內間隔厚度與介電常數改變閘源汲耦合。","textEn":"Inner-spacer thickness and permittivity change gate-source/drain coupling."},{"id":"a023-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「寄生電容預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget parasitic capacitance?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","內間隔厚度與介電常數改變閘源汲耦合。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Inner-spacer thickness and permittivity change gate-source/drain coupling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"內間隔厚度與介電常數改變閘源汲耦合。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"Inner-spacer thickness and permittivity change gate-source/drain coupling. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}},{"id":"a023-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-21"],"title":"熱路徑","titleEn":"Trace heat pathways","objective":"完成「熱路徑」的故障判別表，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for trace heat pathways, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱路徑。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：堆疊層的散熱路徑不同於平面通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace heat pathways. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Stacked-sheet heat paths differ from planar-channel paths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「堆疊層的散熱路徑不同於平面通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stacked-sheet heat paths differ from planar-channel paths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「熱路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace heat pathways and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱路徑」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for trace heat pathways: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-22-k1","title":"熱路徑的原理","titleEn":"Trace heat pathways principle","text":"堆疊層的散熱路徑不同於平面通道。","textEn":"Stacked-sheet heat paths differ from planar-channel paths."},{"id":"a023-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace heat pathways?","options":["堆疊層的散熱路徑不同於平面通道。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Stacked-sheet heat paths differ from planar-channel paths.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"堆疊層的散熱路徑不同於平面通道。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"Stacked-sheet heat paths differ from planar-channel paths. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}},{"id":"a023-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-22"],"title":"片寬設計組","titleEn":"Compare sheet-width variants","objective":"完成「片寬設計組」的量測規劃，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare sheet-width variants, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片寬設計組。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：公平比較需相同漏電目標與工作電壓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sheet-width variants. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Fair comparison needs matched leakage targets and supply voltage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「公平比較需相同漏電目標與工作電壓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fair comparison needs matched leakage targets and supply voltage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「片寬設計組」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sheet-width variants and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片寬設計組」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare sheet-width variants: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-23-k1","title":"片寬設計組的原理","titleEn":"Compare sheet-width variants principle","text":"公平比較需相同漏電目標與工作電壓。","textEn":"Fair comparison needs matched leakage targets and supply voltage."},{"id":"a023-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片寬設計組」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sheet-width variants?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","公平比較需相同漏電目標與工作電壓。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Fair comparison needs matched leakage targets and supply voltage.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公平比較需相同漏電目標與工作電壓。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"Fair comparison needs matched leakage targets and supply voltage. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}},{"id":"a023-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a023-v8-23"],"title":"GAA 整合審查","titleEn":"Review GAA integration","objective":"完成「GAA 整合審查」的工程驗收單，把片間釋放、環繞閘及逐層差異中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review gaa integration, connecting relevant limits in inter-sheet release, wraparound gates and layer variation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：GAA 整合審查。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：須同時交付釋放、覆蓋、接觸與變異證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review GAA integration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Provide release, coverage, contact and variability evidence together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「須同時交付釋放、覆蓋、接觸與變異證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Provide release, coverage, contact and variability evidence together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「GAA 整合審查」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review gaa integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「GAA 整合審查」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review gaa integration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a023-v8-24-k1","title":"GAA 整合審查的原理","titleEn":"Review GAA integration principle","text":"須同時交付釋放、覆蓋、接觸與變異證據。","textEn":"Provide release, coverage, contact and variability evidence together."},{"id":"a023-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","textEn":"Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「GAA 整合審查」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review gaa integration?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","須同時交付釋放、覆蓋、接觸與變異證據。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Provide release, coverage, contact and variability evidence together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"須同時交付釋放、覆蓋、接觸與變異證據。 總電流是多片通道貢獻之和，因此單片退化可能被其他通道遮蔽；需要逐層或敏感測試結構。","explanationEn":"Provide release, coverage, contact and variability evidence together. Total current sums sheet contributions, so other sheets can mask one degraded channel; use per-layer or sensitive test structures."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a024","title":"互補式堆疊電晶體研究流程","titleEn":"Complementary FET research process flows","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["互補堆疊架構","中介隔離","上下層接觸","研究驗證"],"labelsEn":["Complementary stacked architecture","Middle dielectric isolation","Top and bottom contacts","Research validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a024-stage01","order":1,"title":"互補堆疊架構","titleEn":"Complementary stacked architecture","description":"在「互補堆疊架構」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for complementary stacked architecture, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a024-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"垂直互補配置","titleEn":"Draw vertical complementary stacking","objective":"完成「垂直互補配置」的因果圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw vertical complementary stacking, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：垂直互補配置。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：CFET 堆疊 n 與 p 元件，不只是多片同極性通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw vertical complementary stacking. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: CFET stacks n and p devices, not merely multiple same-polarity channels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「CFET 堆疊 n 與 p 元件，不只是多片同極性通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: CFET stacks n and p devices, not merely multiple same-polarity channels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「垂直互補配置」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw vertical complementary stacking and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「垂直互補配置」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw vertical complementary stacking: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-01-k1","title":"垂直互補配置的原理","titleEn":"Draw vertical complementary stacking principle","text":"CFET 堆疊 n 與 p 元件，不只是多片同極性通道。","textEn":"CFET stacks n and p devices, not merely multiple same-polarity channels."},{"id":"a024-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「垂直互補配置」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw vertical complementary stacking?","options":["CFET 堆疊 n 與 p 元件，不只是多片同極性通道。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["CFET stacks n and p devices, not merely multiple same-polarity channels.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"CFET 堆疊 n 與 p 元件，不只是多片同極性通道。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"CFET stacks n and p devices, not merely multiple same-polarity channels. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}},{"id":"a024-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-01"],"title":"單體與順序整合","titleEn":"Compare monolithic and sequential integration","objective":"完成「單體與順序整合」的對照表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare monolithic and sequential integration, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：單體與順序整合。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：單次堆疊加工與先後形成元件有不同熱限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare monolithic and sequential integration. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Single-stack and sequential device formation have different thermal constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單次堆疊加工與先後形成元件有不同熱限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Single-stack and sequential device formation have different thermal constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「單體與順序整合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare monolithic and sequential integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「單體與順序整合」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare monolithic and sequential integration: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-02-k1","title":"單體與順序整合的原理","titleEn":"Compare monolithic and sequential integration principle","text":"單次堆疊加工與先後形成元件有不同熱限制。","textEn":"Single-stack and sequential device formation have different thermal constraints."},{"id":"a024-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「單體與順序整合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare monolithic and sequential integration?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","單次堆疊加工與先後形成元件有不同熱限制。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Single-stack and sequential device formation have different thermal constraints.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單次堆疊加工與先後形成元件有不同熱限制。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"Single-stack and sequential device formation have different thermal constraints. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}},{"id":"a024-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-02"],"title":"標準元件高度","titleEn":"Budget standard-cell height","objective":"完成「標準元件高度」的敏感度草圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget standard-cell height, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：標準元件高度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：移除平面 n-p 間距不代表所有配線空間消失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 畫平面互補元件與 CFET 兩個相同輸入輸出的反相器；在每圖標出上下或左右源汲極、閘、VDD、VSS 與輸出。用連通性而非外形證明功能一致。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget standard-cell height. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Removing lateral n-p separation does not eliminate routing space needs. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Draw planar and CFET inverters with identical inputs and outputs. Mark source-drain, gates, VDD, VSS and output on each. Establish equivalent function through connectivity rather than shape.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「移除平面 n-p 間距不代表所有配線空間消失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removing lateral n-p separation does not eliminate routing space needs. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「標準元件高度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget standard-cell height and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「標準元件高度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget standard-cell height: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-03-k1","title":"標準元件高度的原理","titleEn":"Budget standard-cell height principle","text":"移除平面 n-p 間距不代表所有配線空間消失。","textEn":"Removing lateral n-p separation does not eliminate routing space needs."},{"id":"a024-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「標準元件高度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget standard-cell height?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","移除平面 n-p 間距不代表所有配線空間消失。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Removing lateral n-p separation does not eliminate routing space needs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除平面 n-p 間距不代表所有配線空間消失。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"Removing lateral n-p separation does not eliminate routing space needs. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}},{"id":"a024-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-03"],"title":"頂底通道分工","titleEn":"Assign top and bottom channels","objective":"完成「頂底通道分工」的故障判別表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assign top and bottom channels, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：頂底通道分工。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：兩層元件需要可辨識的電性及接觸測試。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign top and bottom channels. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Both device tiers need distinguishable electrical and contact tests. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩層元件需要可辨識的電性及接觸測試。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Both device tiers need distinguishable electrical and contact tests. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「頂底通道分工」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign top and bottom channels and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「頂底通道分工」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assign top and bottom channels: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-04-k1","title":"頂底通道分工的原理","titleEn":"Assign top and bottom channels principle","text":"兩層元件需要可辨識的電性及接觸測試。","textEn":"Both device tiers need distinguishable electrical and contact tests."},{"id":"a024-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「頂底通道分工」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign top and bottom channels?","options":["兩層元件需要可辨識的電性及接觸測試。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Both device tiers need distinguishable electrical and contact tests.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩層元件需要可辨識的電性及接觸測試。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"Both device tiers need distinguishable electrical and contact tests. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}},{"id":"a024-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-04"],"title":"共同閘選項","titleEn":"Assess common-gate options","objective":"完成「共同閘選項」的量測規劃，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess common-gate options, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：共同閘選項。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：共享閘連接仍需設定兩種元件的閾值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess common-gate options. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Common gate connectivity still needs separate threshold setting for both polarities. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「共享閘連接仍需設定兩種元件的閾值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Common gate connectivity still needs separate threshold setting for both polarities. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「共同閘選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess common-gate options and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「共同閘選項」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess common-gate options: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-05-k1","title":"共同閘選項的原理","titleEn":"Assess common-gate options principle","text":"共享閘連接仍需設定兩種元件的閾值。","textEn":"Common gate connectivity still needs separate threshold setting for both polarities."},{"id":"a024-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「共同閘選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess common-gate options?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","共享閘連接仍需設定兩種元件的閾值。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Common gate connectivity still needs separate threshold setting for both polarities.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共享閘連接仍需設定兩種元件的閾值。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"Common gate connectivity still needs separate threshold setting for both polarities. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}},{"id":"a024-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-05"],"title":"垂直節距","titleEn":"Budget vertical pitch","objective":"完成「垂直節距」的工程驗收單，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for budget vertical pitch, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：垂直節距。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：更小垂直距離會加劇隔離與加工空間限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget vertical pitch. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Smaller vertical spacing tightens isolation and processing constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更小垂直距離會加劇隔離與加工空間限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Smaller vertical spacing tightens isolation and processing constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「垂直節距」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget vertical pitch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「垂直節距」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for budget vertical pitch: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-06-k1","title":"垂直節距的原理","titleEn":"Budget vertical pitch principle","text":"更小垂直距離會加劇隔離與加工空間限制。","textEn":"Smaller vertical spacing tightens isolation and processing constraints."},{"id":"a024-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","textEn":"CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「垂直節距」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget vertical pitch?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","更小垂直距離會加劇隔離與加工空間限制。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Smaller vertical spacing tightens isolation and processing constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更小垂直距離會加劇隔離與加工空間限制。 CFET 以垂直方向取代部分平面 n-p 間距，但其面積收益取決於可實現的接觸與標準元件佈線。","explanationEn":"Smaller vertical spacing tightens isolation and processing constraints. CFET replaces some lateral n-p spacing vertically, but area benefits depend on realizable contacts and cell routing."}}]},{"id":"a024-stage02","order":2,"title":"中介隔離","titleEn":"Middle dielectric isolation","description":"在「中介隔離」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for middle dielectric isolation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a024-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-06"],"title":"中介層角色","titleEn":"Assign middle-layer function","objective":"完成「中介層角色」的因果圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assign middle-layer function, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：中介層角色。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：中介介電層隔離上下閘而非代替全部元件隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign middle-layer function. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Middle dielectric isolates tier gates rather than all device isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中介介電層隔離上下閘而非代替全部元件隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Middle dielectric isolates tier gates rather than all device isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「中介層角色」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign middle-layer function and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「中介層角色」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assign middle-layer function: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-07-k1","title":"中介層角色的原理","titleEn":"Assign middle-layer function principle","text":"中介介電層隔離上下閘而非代替全部元件隔離。","textEn":"Middle dielectric isolates tier gates rather than all device isolation."},{"id":"a024-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「中介層角色」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign middle-layer function?","options":["中介介電層隔離上下閘而非代替全部元件隔離。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Middle dielectric isolates tier gates rather than all device isolation.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中介介電層隔離上下閘而非代替全部元件隔離。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Middle dielectric isolates tier gates rather than all device isolation. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}},{"id":"a024-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-07"],"title":"中介隔離順序","titleEn":"Compare isolation ordering","objective":"完成「中介隔離順序」的對照表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare isolation ordering, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：中介隔離順序。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：先做隔離或先做源汲極凹槽會改變加工邊界。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare isolation ordering. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Isolation-first and recess-first sequences change processing boundaries. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「先做隔離或先做源汲極凹槽會改變加工邊界。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation-first and recess-first sequences change processing boundaries. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「中介隔離順序」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare isolation ordering and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「中介隔離順序」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare isolation ordering: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-08-k1","title":"中介隔離順序的原理","titleEn":"Compare isolation ordering principle","text":"先做隔離或先做源汲極凹槽會改變加工邊界。","textEn":"Isolation-first and recess-first sequences change processing boundaries."},{"id":"a024-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「中介隔離順序」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare isolation ordering?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","先做隔離或先做源汲極凹槽會改變加工邊界。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Isolation-first and recess-first sequences change processing boundaries.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先做隔離或先做源汲極凹槽會改變加工邊界。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Isolation-first and recess-first sequences change processing boundaries. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}},{"id":"a024-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-08"],"title":"內間隔共整合","titleEn":"Co-integrate inner spacers","objective":"完成「內間隔共整合」的敏感度草圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for co-integrate inner spacers, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：內間隔共整合。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：中介隔離與內間隔需避免彼此破壞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Co-integrate inner spacers. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Middle isolation and inner spacers must survive each other's processing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中介隔離與內間隔需避免彼此破壞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Middle isolation and inner spacers must survive each other's processing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「內間隔共整合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for co-integrate inner spacers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「內間隔共整合」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for co-integrate inner spacers: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-09-k1","title":"內間隔共整合的原理","titleEn":"Co-integrate inner spacers principle","text":"中介隔離與內間隔需避免彼此破壞。","textEn":"Middle isolation and inner spacers must survive each other's processing."},{"id":"a024-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「內間隔共整合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating co-integrate inner spacers?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","中介隔離與內間隔需避免彼此破壞。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Middle isolation and inner spacers must survive each other's processing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中介隔離與內間隔需避免彼此破壞。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Middle isolation and inner spacers must survive each other's processing. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}},{"id":"a024-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-09"],"title":"上下材料選擇性","titleEn":"Assess tier-material selectivity","objective":"完成「上下材料選擇性」的故障判別表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess tier-material selectivity, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：上下材料選擇性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：加工一層時另一層仍需要保護。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess tier-material selectivity. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Processing one tier requires protecting the other. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「加工一層時另一層仍需要保護。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Processing one tier requires protecting the other. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「上下材料選擇性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess tier-material selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「上下材料選擇性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess tier-material selectivity: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-10-k1","title":"上下材料選擇性的原理","titleEn":"Assess tier-material selectivity principle","text":"加工一層時另一層仍需要保護。","textEn":"Processing one tier requires protecting the other."},{"id":"a024-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「上下材料選擇性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess tier-material selectivity?","options":["加工一層時另一層仍需要保護。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Processing one tier requires protecting the other.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"加工一層時另一層仍需要保護。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Processing one tier requires protecting the other. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}},{"id":"a024-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-10"],"title":"選擇性磊晶","titleEn":"Inspect tier-selective epitaxy","objective":"完成「選擇性磊晶」的量測規劃，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect tier-selective epitaxy, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性磊晶。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：底層與頂層有不同的可達性與成核表面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect tier-selective epitaxy. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Top and bottom tiers differ in accessibility and seed surfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「底層與頂層有不同的可達性與成核表面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Top and bottom tiers differ in accessibility and seed surfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「選擇性磊晶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect tier-selective epitaxy and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性磊晶」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect tier-selective epitaxy: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-11-k1","title":"選擇性磊晶的原理","titleEn":"Inspect tier-selective epitaxy principle","text":"底層與頂層有不同的可達性與成核表面。","textEn":"Top and bottom tiers differ in accessibility and seed surfaces."},{"id":"a024-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性磊晶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect tier-selective epitaxy?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","底層與頂層有不同的可達性與成核表面。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Top and bottom tiers differ in accessibility and seed surfaces.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"底層與頂層有不同的可達性與成核表面。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Top and bottom tiers differ in accessibility and seed surfaces. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}},{"id":"a024-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-11"],"title":"低熱預算源汲極","titleEn":"Assess low-budget source-drain formation","objective":"完成「低熱預算源汲極」的工程驗收單，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess low-budget source-drain formation, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：低熱預算源汲極。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：降低熱暴露仍需維持活化與接觸品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess low-budget source-drain formation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Reduced thermal exposure must preserve activation and contact quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「降低熱暴露仍需維持活化與接觸品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reduced thermal exposure must preserve activation and contact quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「低熱預算源汲極」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess low-budget source-drain formation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「低熱預算源汲極」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess low-budget source-drain formation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-12-k1","title":"低熱預算源汲極的原理","titleEn":"Assess low-budget source-drain formation principle","text":"降低熱暴露仍需維持活化與接觸品質。","textEn":"Reduced thermal exposure must preserve activation and contact quality."},{"id":"a024-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","textEn":"Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「低熱預算源汲極」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess low-budget source-drain formation?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","降低熱暴露仍需維持活化與接觸品質。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Reduced thermal exposure must preserve activation and contact quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"降低熱暴露仍需維持活化與接觸品質。 中介隔離讓上下閘可具有不同材料與閾值設定；其形成順序又會影響後續源汲極的可達性。","explanationEn":"Reduced thermal exposure must preserve activation and contact quality. Middle isolation supports different tier-gate materials and thresholds; its sequence also affects source-drain accessibility."}}]},{"id":"a024-stage03","order":3,"title":"上下層接觸","titleEn":"Top and bottom contacts","description":"在「上下層接觸」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for top and bottom contacts, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a024-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-12"],"title":"前側底層接觸","titleEn":"Trace frontside bottom contacts","objective":"完成「前側底層接觸」的因果圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace frontside bottom contacts, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前側底層接觸。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：底層接觸需穿越或繞過上層結構。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace frontside bottom contacts. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Bottom contacts from the front must pass or bypass upper structures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「底層接觸需穿越或繞過上層結構。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bottom contacts from the front must pass or bypass upper structures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「前側底層接觸」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace frontside bottom contacts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前側底層接觸」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace frontside bottom contacts: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-13-k1","title":"前側底層接觸的原理","titleEn":"Trace frontside bottom contacts principle","text":"底層接觸需穿越或繞過上層結構。","textEn":"Bottom contacts from the front must pass or bypass upper structures."},{"id":"a024-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前側底層接觸」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace frontside bottom contacts?","options":["底層接觸需穿越或繞過上層結構。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Bottom contacts from the front must pass or bypass upper structures.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底層接觸需穿越或繞過上層結構。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Bottom contacts from the front must pass or bypass upper structures. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}},{"id":"a024-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-13"],"title":"背側底層接觸","titleEn":"Trace backside bottom contacts","objective":"完成「背側底層接觸」的對照表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace backside bottom contacts, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背側底層接觸。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：背側連接另需鍵合、薄化與對準模組。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace backside bottom contacts. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Backside access adds bonding, thinning and alignment modules. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背側連接另需鍵合、薄化與對準模組。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside access adds bonding, thinning and alignment modules. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「背側底層接觸」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace backside bottom contacts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背側底層接觸」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace backside bottom contacts: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-14-k1","title":"背側底層接觸的原理","titleEn":"Trace backside bottom contacts principle","text":"背側連接另需鍵合、薄化與對準模組。","textEn":"Backside access adds bonding, thinning and alignment modules."},{"id":"a024-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背側底層接觸」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace backside bottom contacts?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","背側連接另需鍵合、薄化與對準模組。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Backside access adds bonding, thinning and alignment modules.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"背側連接另需鍵合、薄化與對準模組。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Backside access adds bonding, thinning and alignment modules. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}},{"id":"a024-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-14"],"title":"源汲極隔離","titleEn":"Assess source-drain isolation","objective":"完成「源汲極隔離」的敏感度草圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess source-drain isolation, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極隔離。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：上下源汲極電性隔離與閘隔離是不同條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess source-drain isolation. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Source-drain tier isolation differs from gate isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「上下源汲極電性隔離與閘隔離是不同條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source-drain tier isolation differs from gate isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「源汲極隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess source-drain isolation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極隔離」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess source-drain isolation: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-15-k1","title":"源汲極隔離的原理","titleEn":"Assess source-drain isolation principle","text":"上下源汲極電性隔離與閘隔離是不同條件。","textEn":"Source-drain tier isolation differs from gate isolation."},{"id":"a024-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess source-drain isolation?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","上下源汲極電性隔離與閘隔離是不同條件。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Source-drain tier isolation differs from gate isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上下源汲極電性隔離與閘隔離是不同條件。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Source-drain tier isolation differs from gate isolation. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}},{"id":"a024-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-15"],"title":"堆疊接觸電阻","titleEn":"Separate tier contact resistance","objective":"完成「堆疊接觸電阻」的故障判別表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate tier contact resistance, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：堆疊接觸電阻。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：總串聯電阻會掩蓋頂底接觸差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate tier contact resistance. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Total series resistance can hide tier-contact differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「總串聯電阻會掩蓋頂底接觸差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Total series resistance can hide tier-contact differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「堆疊接觸電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate tier contact resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「堆疊接觸電阻」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate tier contact resistance: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-16-k1","title":"堆疊接觸電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate tier contact resistance principle","text":"總串聯電阻會掩蓋頂底接觸差異。","textEn":"Total series resistance can hide tier-contact differences."},{"id":"a024-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「堆疊接觸電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate tier contact resistance?","options":["總串聯電阻會掩蓋頂底接觸差異。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Total series resistance can hide tier-contact differences.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總串聯電阻會掩蓋頂底接觸差異。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Total series resistance can hide tier-contact differences. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}},{"id":"a024-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-16"],"title":"垂直佈線擁塞","titleEn":"Map vertical routing congestion","objective":"完成「垂直佈線擁塞」的量測規劃，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for map vertical routing congestion, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：垂直佈線擁塞。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：器件面積縮小可能把瓶頸轉移到接觸與配線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map vertical routing congestion. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Smaller devices can move bottlenecks into contacts and routing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「器件面積縮小可能把瓶頸轉移到接觸與配線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Smaller devices can move bottlenecks into contacts and routing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「垂直佈線擁塞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map vertical routing congestion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「垂直佈線擁塞」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for map vertical routing congestion: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-17-k1","title":"垂直佈線擁塞的原理","titleEn":"Map vertical routing congestion principle","text":"器件面積縮小可能把瓶頸轉移到接觸與配線。","textEn":"Smaller devices can move bottlenecks into contacts and routing."},{"id":"a024-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「垂直佈線擁塞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map vertical routing congestion?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","器件面積縮小可能把瓶頸轉移到接觸與配線。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Smaller devices can move bottlenecks into contacts and routing.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"器件面積縮小可能把瓶頸轉移到接觸與配線。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Smaller devices can move bottlenecks into contacts and routing. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}},{"id":"a024-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-17"],"title":"對準誤差傳播","titleEn":"Propagate alignment error","objective":"完成「對準誤差傳播」的工程驗收單，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for propagate alignment error, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：對準誤差傳播。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：不同模組的錯位需轉到同一三維座標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Propagate alignment error. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Module misalignments must be expressed in a common 3D frame. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同模組的錯位需轉到同一三維座標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Module misalignments must be expressed in a common 3D frame. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「對準誤差傳播」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for propagate alignment error and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「對準誤差傳播」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for propagate alignment error: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-18-k1","title":"對準誤差傳播的原理","titleEn":"Propagate alignment error principle","text":"不同模組的錯位需轉到同一三維座標。","textEn":"Module misalignments must be expressed in a common 3D frame."},{"id":"a024-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","textEn":"Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「對準誤差傳播」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating propagate alignment error?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","不同模組的錯位需轉到同一三維座標。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Module misalignments must be expressed in a common 3D frame."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同模組的錯位需轉到同一三維座標。 底層前側接觸與背側接觸各有不同加工模組，不能只比較導線長度而忽略隔離及薄化成本。","explanationEn":"Module misalignments must be expressed in a common 3D frame. Frontside and backside bottom contacts need different modules; wire-length comparisons alone miss isolation and thinning costs."}}]},{"id":"a024-stage04","order":4,"title":"研究驗證","titleEn":"Research validation","description":"在「研究驗證」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for research validation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a024-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-18"],"title":"分層 I-V 測試","titleEn":"Test tier-resolved I-V","objective":"完成「分層 I-V 測試」的因果圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for test tier-resolved i-v, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分層 I-V 測試。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：只有合併輸出無法確認每層獨立功能。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Test tier-resolved I-V. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Combined output alone cannot establish each tier's function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只有合併輸出無法確認每層獨立功能。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Combined output alone cannot establish each tier's function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「分層 I-V 測試」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for test tier-resolved i-v and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分層 I-V 測試」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for test tier-resolved i-v: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-19-k1","title":"分層 I-V 測試的原理","titleEn":"Test tier-resolved I-V principle","text":"只有合併輸出無法確認每層獨立功能。","textEn":"Combined output alone cannot establish each tier's function."},{"id":"a024-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分層 I-V 測試」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating test tier-resolved i-v?","options":["只有合併輸出無法確認每層獨立功能。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Combined output alone cannot establish each tier's function.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只有合併輸出無法確認每層獨立功能。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"Combined output alone cannot establish each tier's function. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}},{"id":"a024-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-19"],"title":"反相器轉移曲線","titleEn":"Assess inverter transfer","objective":"完成「反相器轉移曲線」的對照表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess inverter transfer, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：反相器轉移曲線。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。本步反相器轉移曲線一律為自訂教學模型；在圖上標示假想 VDD 與輸入輸出，不將曲線歸屬為 imec 實測資料。判讀依據：互補特性需由完整電路連接與轉移曲線驗證。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess inverter transfer. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. All inverter transfer curves in this exercise are hypothetical teaching models. Label the assumed VDD, input and output; do not attribute these curves to imec measurements. Interpretation: Complementarity needs circuit connectivity and transfer-curve evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「互補特性需由完整電路連接與轉移曲線驗證。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Complementarity needs circuit connectivity and transfer-curve evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：上下層各自都有正常的電晶體電流曲線，就足以證明接成反相器後的轉移曲線正確。 應回到「反相器轉移曲線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Valid transistor current curves for both tiers alone prove that the connected inverter has a correct transfer curve. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess inverter transfer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「反相器轉移曲線」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess inverter transfer: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-20-k1","title":"反相器轉移曲線的原理","titleEn":"Assess inverter transfer principle","text":"互補特性需由完整電路連接與轉移曲線驗證。","textEn":"Complementarity needs circuit connectivity and transfer-curve evidence."},{"id":"a024-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「反相器轉移曲線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess inverter transfer?","options":["上下層各自都有正常的電晶體電流曲線，就足以證明接成反相器後的轉移曲線正確。","互補特性需由完整電路連接與轉移曲線驗證。","轉移曲線只要穿過輸入與輸出皆為 VDD/2 的點，就不必再檢查轉換斜率或雜訊容限。"],"optionsEn":["Valid transistor current curves for both tiers alone prove that the connected inverter has a correct transfer curve.","Complementarity needs circuit connectivity and transfer-curve evidence.","A transfer curve crossing the point where input and output both equal VDD/2 needs no further slope or noise-margin assessment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"互補特性需由完整電路連接與轉移曲線驗證。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"Complementarity needs circuit connectivity and transfer-curve evidence. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}},{"id":"a024-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-20"],"title":"自熱與交互加熱","titleEn":"Assess mutual heating","objective":"完成「自熱與交互加熱」的敏感度草圖，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess mutual heating, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自熱與交互加熱。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：一層發熱可能改變另一層的電性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess mutual heating. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Heating one tier can alter the other's electrical behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「一層發熱可能改變另一層的電性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Heating one tier can alter the other's electrical behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「自熱與交互加熱」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess mutual heating and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自熱與交互加熱」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess mutual heating: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-21-k1","title":"自熱與交互加熱的原理","titleEn":"Assess mutual heating principle","text":"一層發熱可能改變另一層的電性。","textEn":"Heating one tier can alter the other's electrical behavior."},{"id":"a024-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自熱與交互加熱」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess mutual heating?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","一層發熱可能改變另一層的電性。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Heating one tier can alter the other's electrical behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一層發熱可能改變另一層的電性。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"Heating one tier can alter the other's electrical behavior. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}},{"id":"a024-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-21"],"title":"研究展示與量產","titleEn":"Separate demonstration from production","objective":"完成「研究展示與量產」的故障判別表，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate demonstration from production, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：研究展示與量產。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：單一功能測試車不等於量產良率證明。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate demonstration from production. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A functional test vehicle is not evidence of production yield. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一功能測試車不等於量產良率證明。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A functional test vehicle is not evidence of production yield. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「研究展示與量產」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate demonstration from production and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「研究展示與量產」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate demonstration from production: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-22-k1","title":"研究展示與量產的原理","titleEn":"Separate demonstration from production principle","text":"單一功能測試車不等於量產良率證明。","textEn":"A functional test vehicle is not evidence of production yield."},{"id":"a024-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「研究展示與量產」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate demonstration from production?","options":["單一功能測試車不等於量產良率證明。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["A functional test vehicle is not evidence of production yield.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一功能測試車不等於量產良率證明。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"A functional test vehicle is not evidence of production yield. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}},{"id":"a024-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-22"],"title":"跨節點比較","titleEn":"Compare research generations","objective":"完成「跨節點比較」的量測規劃，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare research generations, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：跨節點比較。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同研究必須對齊幾何、偏壓及抽取定義。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare research generations. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Cross-study comparisons need matched geometry, bias and extraction definitions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同研究必須對齊幾何、偏壓及抽取定義。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Cross-study comparisons need matched geometry, bias and extraction definitions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「跨節點比較」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare research generations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「跨節點比較」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare research generations: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-23-k1","title":"跨節點比較的原理","titleEn":"Compare research generations principle","text":"不同研究必須對齊幾何、偏壓及抽取定義。","textEn":"Cross-study comparisons need matched geometry, bias and extraction definitions."},{"id":"a024-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「跨節點比較」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare research generations?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","不同研究必須對齊幾何、偏壓及抽取定義。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Cross-study comparisons need matched geometry, bias and extraction definitions.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同研究必須對齊幾何、偏壓及抽取定義。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"Cross-study comparisons need matched geometry, bias and extraction definitions. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}},{"id":"a024-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-cfet","v8a-scaling","v8a-sige","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a024-v8-23"],"title":"CFET 證據地圖","titleEn":"Assemble a CFET evidence map","objective":"完成「CFET 證據地圖」的工程驗收單，把上下互補層、中介隔離及分層接觸中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assemble a cfet evidence map, connecting relevant limits in complementary tiers, middle isolation and tier contacts to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：CFET 證據地圖。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：隔離、雙極性、接觸、電路與重現性需分層報告。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assemble a CFET evidence map. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Report isolation, both polarities, contacts, circuits and repeatability separately. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離、雙極性、接觸、電路與重現性需分層報告。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report isolation, both polarities, contacts, circuits and repeatability separately. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「CFET 證據地圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assemble a cfet evidence map and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「CFET 證據地圖」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assemble a cfet evidence map: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a024-v8-24-k1","title":"CFET 證據地圖的原理","titleEn":"Assemble a CFET evidence map principle","text":"隔離、雙極性、接觸、電路與重現性需分層報告。","textEn":"Report isolation, both polarities, contacts, circuits and repeatability separately."},{"id":"a024-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","textEn":"After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「CFET 證據地圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assemble a cfet evidence map?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","隔離、雙極性、接觸、電路與重現性需分層報告。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Report isolation, both polarities, contacts, circuits and repeatability separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離、雙極性、接觸、電路與重現性需分層報告。 研究測試車展示功能後，仍需更多樣本驗證變異、存活率與可靠度，才能建立製造成熟度證據。","explanationEn":"Report isolation, both polarities, contacts, circuits and repeatability separately. After functional test-vehicle demonstrations, further samples are needed for variability, survival and reliability evidence."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a026","title":"埋入式電源軌整合","titleEn":"Buried power-rail integration","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電源路徑","埋入軌幾何","接觸與熱歷程","電源及可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Power pathways","Buried-rail geometry","Contacts and thermal history","Power and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a026-stage01","order":1,"title":"電源路徑","titleEn":"Power pathways","description":"在「電源路徑」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for power pathways, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a026-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"電源與訊號分離","titleEn":"Separate power and signals","objective":"完成「電源與訊號分離」的因果圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate power and signals, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電源與訊號分離。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：埋入式軌改變電源位置，訊號仍需獨立連通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate power and signals. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Buried rails relocate power while signals still need separate connectivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋入式軌改變電源位置，訊號仍需獨立連通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried rails relocate power while signals still need separate connectivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「電源與訊號分離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate power and signals and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電源與訊號分離」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate power and signals: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-01-k1","title":"電源與訊號分離的原理","titleEn":"Separate power and signals principle","text":"埋入式軌改變電源位置，訊號仍需獨立連通。","textEn":"Buried rails relocate power while signals still need separate connectivity."},{"id":"a026-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電源與訊號分離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate power and signals?","options":["埋入式軌改變電源位置，訊號仍需獨立連通。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Buried rails relocate power while signals still need separate connectivity.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋入式軌改變電源位置，訊號仍需獨立連通。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Buried rails relocate power while signals still need separate connectivity. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}},{"id":"a026-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-01"],"title":"正面與背面入口","titleEn":"Compare front and back access","objective":"完成「正面與背面入口」的對照表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare front and back access, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：正面與背面入口。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：有埋入軌不代表必然由背面供電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare front and back access. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Buried rails do not necessarily imply backside delivery. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「有埋入軌不代表必然由背面供電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried rails do not necessarily imply backside delivery. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「正面與背面入口」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare front and back access and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「正面與背面入口」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare front and back access: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-02-k1","title":"正面與背面入口的原理","titleEn":"Compare front and back access principle","text":"有埋入軌不代表必然由背面供電。","textEn":"Buried rails do not necessarily imply backside delivery."},{"id":"a026-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「正面與背面入口」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare front and back access?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","有埋入軌不代表必然由背面供電。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Buried rails do not necessarily imply backside delivery.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有埋入軌不代表必然由背面供電。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Buried rails do not necessarily imply backside delivery. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}},{"id":"a026-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-02"],"title":"電流回路","titleEn":"Trace the complete current loop","objective":"完成「電流回路」的敏感度草圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace the complete current loop, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電流回路。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：VDD 與回流路徑都貢獻元件壓降。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the complete current loop. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Both supply and return contribute to device voltage drop. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「VDD 與回流路徑都貢獻元件壓降。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Both supply and return contribute to device voltage drop. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「電流回路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the complete current loop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電流回路」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace the complete current loop: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-03-k1","title":"電流回路的原理","titleEn":"Trace the complete current loop principle","text":"VDD 與回流路徑都貢獻元件壓降。","textEn":"Both supply and return contribute to device voltage drop."},{"id":"a026-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電流回路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the complete current loop?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","VDD 與回流路徑都貢獻元件壓降。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Both supply and return contribute to device voltage drop."],"answer":2,"explanation":"VDD 與回流路徑都貢獻元件壓降。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Both supply and return contribute to device voltage drop. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}},{"id":"a026-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-03"],"title":"標準元件軌道","titleEn":"Budget cell tracks","objective":"完成「標準元件軌道」的故障判別表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget cell tracks, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：標準元件軌道。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：釋出的配線軌道需經實際佈線才能確認收益。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget cell tracks. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Released tracks need routing verification to establish benefits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「釋出的配線軌道需經實際佈線才能確認收益。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Released tracks need routing verification to establish benefits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「標準元件軌道」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget cell tracks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「標準元件軌道」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget cell tracks: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-04-k1","title":"標準元件軌道的原理","titleEn":"Budget cell tracks principle","text":"釋出的配線軌道需經實際佈線才能確認收益。","textEn":"Released tracks need routing verification to establish benefits."},{"id":"a026-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「標準元件軌道」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget cell tracks?","options":["釋出的配線軌道需經實際佈線才能確認收益。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Released tracks need routing verification to establish benefits.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"釋出的配線軌道需經實際佈線才能確認收益。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Released tracks need routing verification to establish benefits. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}},{"id":"a026-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-04"],"title":"埋入深度","titleEn":"Choose a depth study","objective":"完成「埋入深度」的量測規劃，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose a depth study, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋入深度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：更深軌會改變隔離、加工難度與接觸長度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose a depth study. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Deeper rails change isolation, process difficulty and contact length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更深軌會改變隔離、加工難度與接觸長度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Deeper rails change isolation, process difficulty and contact length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「埋入深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose a depth study and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋入深度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose a depth study: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-05-k1","title":"埋入深度的原理","titleEn":"Choose a depth study principle","text":"更深軌會改變隔離、加工難度與接觸長度。","textEn":"Deeper rails change isolation, process difficulty and contact length."},{"id":"a026-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋入深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose a depth study?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","更深軌會改變隔離、加工難度與接觸長度。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Deeper rails change isolation, process difficulty and contact length.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更深軌會改變隔離、加工難度與接觸長度。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Deeper rails change isolation, process difficulty and contact length. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}},{"id":"a026-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-05"],"title":"軌截面積","titleEn":"Assess rail cross-section","objective":"完成「軌截面積」的工程驗收單，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess rail cross-section, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軌截面積。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：電阻與可用截面及材料電阻率一起相關。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess rail cross-section. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Resistance depends on available cross-section and material resistivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電阻與可用截面及材料電阻率一起相關。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Resistance depends on available cross-section and material resistivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「軌截面積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess rail cross-section and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軌截面積」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess rail cross-section: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-06-k1","title":"軌截面積的原理","titleEn":"Assess rail cross-section principle","text":"電阻與可用截面及材料電阻率一起相關。","textEn":"Resistance depends on available cross-section and material resistivity."},{"id":"a026-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","textEn":"A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軌截面積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess rail cross-section?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","電阻與可用截面及材料電阻率一起相關。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Resistance depends on available cross-section and material resistivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電阻與可用截面及材料電阻率一起相關。 埋入軌是一種局部供電結構；電源從正面或背面進入是另一個設計維度，需以完整回路判定。","explanationEn":"Resistance depends on available cross-section and material resistivity. A buried rail is a local power structure; frontside or backside entry is a separate design dimension requiring a complete loop."}}]},{"id":"a026-stage02","order":2,"title":"埋入軌幾何","titleEn":"Buried-rail geometry","description":"在「埋入軌幾何」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for buried-rail geometry, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a026-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-06"],"title":"隔離溝槽","titleEn":"Draw isolation trenches","objective":"完成「隔離溝槽」的因果圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw isolation trenches, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：隔離溝槽。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：電源金屬需與不應導通的矽區隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw isolation trenches. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Power metal must be isolated from unintended silicon connections. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電源金屬需與不應導通的矽區隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Power metal must be isolated from unintended silicon connections. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「隔離溝槽」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw isolation trenches and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「隔離溝槽」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw isolation trenches: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-07-k1","title":"隔離溝槽的原理","titleEn":"Draw isolation trenches principle","text":"電源金屬需與不應導通的矽區隔離。","textEn":"Power metal must be isolated from unintended silicon connections."},{"id":"a026-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「隔離溝槽」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw isolation trenches?","options":["電源金屬需與不應導通的矽區隔離。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Power metal must be isolated from unintended silicon connections.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電源金屬需與不應導通的矽區隔離。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Power metal must be isolated from unintended silicon connections. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}},{"id":"a026-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-07"],"title":"介電襯層","titleEn":"Inspect dielectric liners","objective":"完成「介電襯層」的對照表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect dielectric liners, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介電襯層。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：局部針孔可能形成電源到基板漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect dielectric liners. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Local liner pinholes can create rail-to-substrate leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部針孔可能形成電源到基板漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local liner pinholes can create rail-to-substrate leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「介電襯層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect dielectric liners and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介電襯層」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect dielectric liners: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-08-k1","title":"介電襯層的原理","titleEn":"Inspect dielectric liners principle","text":"局部針孔可能形成電源到基板漏電。","textEn":"Local liner pinholes can create rail-to-substrate leakage."},{"id":"a026-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介電襯層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect dielectric liners?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","局部針孔可能形成電源到基板漏電。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Local liner pinholes can create rail-to-substrate leakage.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部針孔可能形成電源到基板漏電。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Local liner pinholes can create rail-to-substrate leakage. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}},{"id":"a026-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-08"],"title":"金屬填充","titleEn":"Assess metal fill","objective":"完成「金屬填充」的敏感度草圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess metal fill, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬填充。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：入口封口可能掩蓋軌內空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess metal fill. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Premature opening closure can hide voids inside rails. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「入口封口可能掩蓋軌內空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Premature opening closure can hide voids inside rails. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「金屬填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess metal fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬填充」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess metal fill: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-09-k1","title":"金屬填充的原理","titleEn":"Assess metal fill principle","text":"入口封口可能掩蓋軌內空洞。","textEn":"Premature opening closure can hide voids inside rails."},{"id":"a026-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess metal fill?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","入口封口可能掩蓋軌內空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Premature opening closure can hide voids inside rails."],"answer":2,"explanation":"入口封口可能掩蓋軌內空洞。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Premature opening closure can hide voids inside rails. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}},{"id":"a026-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-09"],"title":"軌頂封裝","titleEn":"Define rail capping","objective":"完成「軌頂封裝」的故障判別表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define rail capping, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軌頂封裝。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：封蓋須在後續元件製程中維持隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define rail capping. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Rail caps must preserve isolation during later device processing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「封蓋須在後續元件製程中維持隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rail caps must preserve isolation during later device processing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「軌頂封裝」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define rail capping and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軌頂封裝」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define rail capping: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-10-k1","title":"軌頂封裝的原理","titleEn":"Define rail capping principle","text":"封蓋須在後續元件製程中維持隔離。","textEn":"Rail caps must preserve isolation during later device processing."},{"id":"a026-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軌頂封裝」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define rail capping?","options":["封蓋須在後續元件製程中維持隔離。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Rail caps must preserve isolation during later device processing.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"封蓋須在後續元件製程中維持隔離。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Rail caps must preserve isolation during later device processing. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}},{"id":"a026-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-10"],"title":"金屬熱相容","titleEn":"Assess thermal compatibility","objective":"完成「金屬熱相容」的量測規劃，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess thermal compatibility, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬熱相容。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：早期埋入金屬必須承受後續前段熱歷程。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermal compatibility. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Early buried metal must survive subsequent front-end thermal history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「早期埋入金屬必須承受後續前段熱歷程。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Early buried metal must survive subsequent front-end thermal history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「金屬熱相容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermal compatibility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬熱相容」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess thermal compatibility: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-11-k1","title":"金屬熱相容的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermal compatibility principle","text":"早期埋入金屬必須承受後續前段熱歷程。","textEn":"Early buried metal must survive subsequent front-end thermal history."},{"id":"a026-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬熱相容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermal compatibility?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","早期埋入金屬必須承受後續前段熱歷程。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Early buried metal must survive subsequent front-end thermal history.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"早期埋入金屬必須承受後續前段熱歷程。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Early buried metal must survive subsequent front-end thermal history. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}},{"id":"a026-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-11"],"title":"形貌回復","titleEn":"Restore surface planarity","objective":"完成「形貌回復」的工程驗收單，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for restore surface planarity, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：形貌回復。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：埋軌上方台階會影響後續元件圖案。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Restore surface planarity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Topography above rails affects later device patterning. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋軌上方台階會影響後續元件圖案。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Topography above rails affects later device patterning. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「形貌回復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for restore surface planarity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「形貌回復」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for restore surface planarity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-12-k1","title":"形貌回復的原理","titleEn":"Restore surface planarity principle","text":"埋軌上方台階會影響後續元件圖案。","textEn":"Topography above rails affects later device patterning."},{"id":"a026-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","textEn":"Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「形貌回復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating restore surface planarity?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","埋軌上方台階會影響後續元件圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Topography above rails affects later device patterning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋軌上方台階會影響後續元件圖案。 金屬截面縮小提高電流密度，襯層則減少可用導體面積；幾何與隔離預算需聯合評估。","explanationEn":"Topography above rails affects later device patterning. Smaller metal cross-sections increase current density, while liners reduce usable conductor area; assess geometry and isolation together."}}]},{"id":"a026-stage03","order":3,"title":"接觸與熱歷程","titleEn":"Contacts and thermal history","description":"在「接觸與熱歷程」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contacts and thermal history, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a026-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-12"],"title":"軌接觸落點","titleEn":"Place rail contacts","objective":"完成「軌接觸落點」的因果圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for place rail contacts, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軌接觸落點。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：通孔需要可靠落在軌上並維持周圍隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Place rail contacts. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Vias must land reliably on rails while preserving surrounding isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「通孔需要可靠落在軌上並維持周圍隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Vias must land reliably on rails while preserving surrounding isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「軌接觸落點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for place rail contacts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軌接觸落點」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for place rail contacts: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-13-k1","title":"軌接觸落點的原理","titleEn":"Place rail contacts principle","text":"通孔需要可靠落在軌上並維持周圍隔離。","textEn":"Vias must land reliably on rails while preserving surrounding isolation."},{"id":"a026-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軌接觸落點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating place rail contacts?","options":["通孔需要可靠落在軌上並維持周圍隔離。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Vias must land reliably on rails while preserving surrounding isolation.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"通孔需要可靠落在軌上並維持周圍隔離。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Vias must land reliably on rails while preserving surrounding isolation. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}},{"id":"a026-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-13"],"title":"接觸電阻分解","titleEn":"Separate contact resistance","objective":"完成「接觸電阻分解」的對照表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate contact resistance, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸電阻分解。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：通孔金屬、界面與軌本體是不同電阻來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate contact resistance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Via metal, interfaces and rail body contribute separate resistances. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「通孔金屬、界面與軌本體是不同電阻來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Via metal, interfaces and rail body contribute separate resistances. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接觸電阻分解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate contact resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸電阻分解」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate contact resistance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸電阻分解的原理","titleEn":"Separate contact resistance principle","text":"通孔金屬、界面與軌本體是不同電阻來源。","textEn":"Via metal, interfaces and rail body contribute separate resistances."},{"id":"a026-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸電阻分解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate contact resistance?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","通孔金屬、界面與軌本體是不同電阻來源。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Via metal, interfaces and rail body contribute separate resistances.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通孔金屬、界面與軌本體是不同電阻來源。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Via metal, interfaces and rail body contribute separate resistances. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}},{"id":"a026-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-14"],"title":"熱應力傳遞","titleEn":"Trace thermal stress","objective":"完成「熱應力傳遞」的敏感度草圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace thermal stress, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱應力傳遞。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：埋軌與矽熱膨脹差可影響鄰近通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace thermal stress. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Rail-silicon expansion mismatch can affect nearby channels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋軌與矽熱膨脹差可影響鄰近通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rail-silicon expansion mismatch can affect nearby channels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「熱應力傳遞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace thermal stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱應力傳遞」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace thermal stress: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-15-k1","title":"熱應力傳遞的原理","titleEn":"Trace thermal stress principle","text":"埋軌與矽熱膨脹差可影響鄰近通道。","textEn":"Rail-silicon expansion mismatch can affect nearby channels."},{"id":"a026-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱應力傳遞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace thermal stress?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","埋軌與矽熱膨脹差可影響鄰近通道。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Rail-silicon expansion mismatch can affect nearby channels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋軌與矽熱膨脹差可影響鄰近通道。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Rail-silicon expansion mismatch can affect nearby channels. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}},{"id":"a026-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-15"],"title":"漏電測試","titleEn":"Test rail leakage","objective":"完成「漏電測試」的故障判別表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for test rail leakage, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：漏電測試。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：低軌電阻不能證明介電隔離完整。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Test rail leakage. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Low rail resistance does not establish dielectric isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低軌電阻不能證明介電隔離完整。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low rail resistance does not establish dielectric isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「漏電測試」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for test rail leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「漏電測試」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for test rail leakage: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-16-k1","title":"漏電測試的原理","titleEn":"Test rail leakage principle","text":"低軌電阻不能證明介電隔離完整。","textEn":"Low rail resistance does not establish dielectric isolation."},{"id":"a026-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「漏電測試」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating test rail leakage?","options":["低軌電阻不能證明介電隔離完整。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Low rail resistance does not establish dielectric isolation.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低軌電阻不能證明介電隔離完整。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Low rail resistance does not establish dielectric isolation. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}},{"id":"a026-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-16"],"title":"軌間短路","titleEn":"Locate inter-rail shorts","objective":"完成「軌間短路」的量測規劃，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for locate inter-rail shorts, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軌間短路。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：相鄰供電與回流軌需要獨立絕緣驗證。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate inter-rail shorts. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Adjacent supply and return rails need isolation verification. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相鄰供電與回流軌需要獨立絕緣驗證。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adjacent supply and return rails need isolation verification. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「軌間短路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate inter-rail shorts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軌間短路」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for locate inter-rail shorts: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-17-k1","title":"軌間短路的原理","titleEn":"Locate inter-rail shorts principle","text":"相鄰供電與回流軌需要獨立絕緣驗證。","textEn":"Adjacent supply and return rails need isolation verification."},{"id":"a026-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軌間短路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate inter-rail shorts?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","相鄰供電與回流軌需要獨立絕緣驗證。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Adjacent supply and return rails need isolation verification.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相鄰供電與回流軌需要獨立絕緣驗證。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Adjacent supply and return rails need isolation verification. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}},{"id":"a026-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-17"],"title":"接觸鏈測試","titleEn":"Use contact chains","objective":"完成「接觸鏈測試」的工程驗收單，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for use contact chains, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸鏈測試。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：長鏈可放大接觸缺陷但不易定位單一失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Use contact chains. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Chains amplify contact defects but may not locate one failure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「長鏈可放大接觸缺陷但不易定位單一失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chains amplify contact defects but may not locate one failure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接觸鏈測試」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for use contact chains and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸鏈測試」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for use contact chains: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-18-k1","title":"接觸鏈測試的原理","titleEn":"Use contact chains principle","text":"長鏈可放大接觸缺陷但不易定位單一失效。","textEn":"Chains amplify contact defects but may not locate one failure."},{"id":"a026-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","textEn":"Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸鏈測試」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating use contact chains?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","長鏈可放大接觸缺陷但不易定位單一失效。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Chains amplify contact defects but may not locate one failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長鏈可放大接觸缺陷但不易定位單一失效。 埋在前段的金屬會遭遇後續熱處理，選材需同時考慮擴散、應力及介電相容而非只看低電阻。","explanationEn":"Chains amplify contact defects but may not locate one failure. Metal buried early encounters later heating, so selection needs diffusion, stress and dielectric compatibility beyond low resistance."}}]},{"id":"a026-stage04","order":4,"title":"電源及可靠度","titleEn":"Power and reliability","description":"在「電源及可靠度」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for power and reliability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a026-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-18"],"title":"直流壓降","titleEn":"Compute DC drop","objective":"完成「直流壓降」的因果圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compute dc drop, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：直流壓降。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：串聯路徑的壓降需依局部電流分段計算。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂串聯供電：三段電阻 1、3、6 個單位且電流為 2；逐段算 I×R，再比較只把最小段與最大段各減半的總改善。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compute DC drop. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Series drop should be computed with each segment's local current. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical series supply: resistances 1,3,6 units and current 2. Calculate each I×R drop and compare halving only the smallest versus largest segment.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「串聯路徑的壓降需依局部電流分段計算。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Series drop should be computed with each segment's local current. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「直流壓降」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compute dc drop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「直流壓降」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compute dc drop: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-19-k1","title":"直流壓降的原理","titleEn":"Compute DC drop principle","text":"串聯路徑的壓降需依局部電流分段計算。","textEn":"Series drop should be computed with each segment's local current."},{"id":"a026-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「直流壓降」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compute dc drop?","options":["串聯路徑的壓降需依局部電流分段計算。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Series drop should be computed with each segment's local current.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"串聯路徑的壓降需依局部電流分段計算。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Series drop should be computed with each segment's local current. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}},{"id":"a026-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-19"],"title":"動態下陷","titleEn":"Assess transient droop","objective":"完成「動態下陷」的對照表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess transient droop, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：動態下陷。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：相同直流電阻可能有不同寄生及瞬態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess transient droop. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal DC resistance can coexist with different parasitics and transients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同直流電阻可能有不同寄生及瞬態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal DC resistance can coexist with different parasitics and transients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「動態下陷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess transient droop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「動態下陷」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess transient droop: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-20-k1","title":"動態下陷的原理","titleEn":"Assess transient droop principle","text":"相同直流電阻可能有不同寄生及瞬態。","textEn":"Equal DC resistance can coexist with different parasitics and transients."},{"id":"a026-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「動態下陷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess transient droop?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","相同直流電阻可能有不同寄生及瞬態。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Equal DC resistance can coexist with different parasitics and transients.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同直流電阻可能有不同寄生及瞬態。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Equal DC resistance can coexist with different parasitics and transients. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}},{"id":"a026-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-20"],"title":"電遷移","titleEn":"Assess electromigration","objective":"完成「電遷移」的敏感度草圖，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess electromigration, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電遷移。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：電流密度與溫度共同影響金屬可靠度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess electromigration. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Current density and temperature jointly affect metal reliability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電流密度與溫度共同影響金屬可靠度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Current density and temperature jointly affect metal reliability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「電遷移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess electromigration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電遷移」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess electromigration: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-21-k1","title":"電遷移的原理","titleEn":"Assess electromigration principle","text":"電流密度與溫度共同影響金屬可靠度。","textEn":"Current density and temperature jointly affect metal reliability."},{"id":"a026-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電遷移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess electromigration?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","電流密度與溫度共同影響金屬可靠度。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Current density and temperature jointly affect metal reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電流密度與溫度共同影響金屬可靠度。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Current density and temperature jointly affect metal reliability. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}},{"id":"a026-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-21"],"title":"局部熱點","titleEn":"Locate rail hotspots","objective":"完成「局部熱點」的故障判別表，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for locate rail hotspots, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：局部熱點。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：接觸狹窄處可能同時集中電流與熱。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate rail hotspots. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Narrow contacts can concentrate both current and heat. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸狹窄處可能同時集中電流與熱。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Narrow contacts can concentrate both current and heat. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「局部熱點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate rail hotspots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「局部熱點」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for locate rail hotspots: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-22-k1","title":"局部熱點的原理","titleEn":"Locate rail hotspots principle","text":"接觸狹窄處可能同時集中電流與熱。","textEn":"Narrow contacts can concentrate both current and heat."},{"id":"a026-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「局部熱點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate rail hotspots?","options":["接觸狹窄處可能同時集中電流與熱。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Narrow contacts can concentrate both current and heat.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸狹窄處可能同時集中電流與熱。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Narrow contacts can concentrate both current and heat. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}},{"id":"a026-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-22"],"title":"電路收益比較","titleEn":"Compare circuit benefit","objective":"完成「電路收益比較」的量測規劃，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare circuit benefit, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電路收益比較。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：面積收益需與功耗、延遲及良率一起評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare circuit benefit. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Area benefits need power, delay and yield assessment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「面積收益需與功耗、延遲及良率一起評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Area benefits need power, delay and yield assessment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「電路收益比較」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare circuit benefit and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電路收益比較」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare circuit benefit: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-23-k1","title":"電路收益比較的原理","titleEn":"Compare circuit benefit principle","text":"面積收益需與功耗、延遲及良率一起評估。","textEn":"Area benefits need power, delay and yield assessment."},{"id":"a026-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電路收益比較」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare circuit benefit?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","面積收益需與功耗、延遲及良率一起評估。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Area benefits need power, delay and yield assessment.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積收益需與功耗、延遲及良率一起評估。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Area benefits need power, delay and yield assessment. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}},{"id":"a026-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-bpr","v8a-scaling","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a026-v8-23"],"title":"埋軌放行","titleEn":"Release buried-rail integration","objective":"完成「埋軌放行」的工程驗收單，把埋軌隔離、熱相容及壓降中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release buried-rail integration, connecting relevant limits in rail isolation, thermal compatibility and voltage drop to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋軌放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：電性、隔離、熱相容與可佈線性需全部有證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release buried-rail integration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Electrical, isolation, thermal compatibility and routability all need evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電性、隔離、熱相容與可佈線性需全部有證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Electrical, isolation, thermal compatibility and routability all need evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「埋軌放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release buried-rail integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋軌放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release buried-rail integration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a026-v8-24-k1","title":"埋軌放行的原理","titleEn":"Release buried-rail integration principle","text":"電性、隔離、熱相容與可佈線性需全部有證據。","textEn":"Electrical, isolation, thermal compatibility and routability all need evidence."},{"id":"a026-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","textEn":"Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋軌放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release buried-rail integration?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","電性、隔離、熱相容與可佈線性需全部有證據。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Electrical, isolation, thermal compatibility and routability all need evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性、隔離、熱相容與可佈線性需全部有證據。 壓降減少可能釋出電壓裕度，但電流密度、熱點及電遷移仍需獨立驗證長期穩定性。","explanationEn":"Electrical, isolation, thermal compatibility and routability all need evidence. Reduced drop can free voltage margin, but current density, hotspots and electromigration need separate lifetime validation."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a027","title":"次二奈米邏輯製程研究","titleEn":"Sub-2-nm logic process research","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["節點與比較基準","元件及圖案","電源及互連","研究證據"],"labelsEn":["Nodes and comparison baselines","Devices and patterning","Power and interconnects","Research evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a027-stage01","order":1,"title":"節點與比較基準","titleEn":"Nodes and comparison baselines","description":"在「節點與比較基準」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for nodes and comparison baselines, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a027-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"節點名稱","titleEn":"Interpret node names","objective":"完成「節點名稱」的因果圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for interpret node names, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：節點名稱。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：節點名稱不是任何單一實體幾何的直接量測。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret node names. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: A node name is not a direct measurement of one physical dimension. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「節點名稱不是任何單一實體幾何的直接量測。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A node name is not a direct measurement of one physical dimension. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「節點名稱」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret node names and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「節點名稱」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for interpret node names: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-01-k1","title":"節點名稱的原理","titleEn":"Interpret node names principle","text":"節點名稱不是任何單一實體幾何的直接量測。","textEn":"A node name is not a direct measurement of one physical dimension."},{"id":"a027-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「節點名稱」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret node names?","options":["節點名稱不是任何單一實體幾何的直接量測。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A node name is not a direct measurement of one physical dimension.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"節點名稱不是任何單一實體幾何的直接量測。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"A node name is not a direct measurement of one physical dimension. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}},{"id":"a027-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-01"],"title":"幾何參數表","titleEn":"Build a geometry table","objective":"完成「幾何參數表」的對照表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for build a geometry table, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：幾何參數表。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：閘長、閘節距、金屬節距與元件高度各自不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a geometry table. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Gate length, gate pitch, metal pitch and cell height are distinct. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘長、閘節距、金屬節距與元件高度各自不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate length, gate pitch, metal pitch and cell height are distinct. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「幾何參數表」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a geometry table and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「幾何參數表」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for build a geometry table: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-02-k1","title":"幾何參數表的原理","titleEn":"Build a geometry table principle","text":"閘長、閘節距、金屬節距與元件高度各自不同。","textEn":"Gate length, gate pitch, metal pitch and cell height are distinct."},{"id":"a027-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「幾何參數表」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a geometry table?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","閘長、閘節距、金屬節距與元件高度各自不同。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Gate length, gate pitch, metal pitch and cell height are distinct.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘長、閘節距、金屬節距與元件高度各自不同。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"Gate length, gate pitch, metal pitch and cell height are distinct. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}},{"id":"a027-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-02"],"title":"工作負載基準","titleEn":"Choose workload baselines","objective":"完成「工作負載基準」的敏感度草圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for choose workload baselines, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：工作負載基準。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：效能比較需要相同工作負載與限制條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose workload baselines. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Performance comparisons require matched workloads and constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「效能比較需要相同工作負載與限制條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Performance comparisons require matched workloads and constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「工作負載基準」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose workload baselines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「工作負載基準」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for choose workload baselines: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-03-k1","title":"工作負載基準的原理","titleEn":"Choose workload baselines principle","text":"效能比較需要相同工作負載與限制條件。","textEn":"Performance comparisons require matched workloads and constraints."},{"id":"a027-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「工作負載基準」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose workload baselines?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","效能比較需要相同工作負載與限制條件。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Performance comparisons require matched workloads and constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"效能比較需要相同工作負載與限制條件。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"Performance comparisons require matched workloads and constraints. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}},{"id":"a027-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-03"],"title":"功耗效能面積","titleEn":"Separate PPA metrics","objective":"完成「功耗效能面積」的故障判別表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate ppa metrics, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：功耗效能面積。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：功耗、效能與面積通常不能同時單獨最佳化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自行建立三個候選架構的正規化 PPA 表，包含一個低功耗但面積較大方案；標明全部是假設，找出 Pareto 不被支配集合而非加總不相容單位。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate PPA metrics. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Power, performance and area generally cannot be independently optimized together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Create hypothetical normalized PPA data for three architectures including a low-power, larger-area option. Identify the nondominated Pareto set rather than adding incompatible units.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「功耗、效能與面積通常不能同時單獨最佳化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Power, performance and area generally cannot be independently optimized together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「功耗效能面積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate ppa metrics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「功耗效能面積」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate ppa metrics: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-04-k1","title":"功耗效能面積的原理","titleEn":"Separate PPA metrics principle","text":"功耗、效能與面積通常不能同時單獨最佳化。","textEn":"Power, performance and area generally cannot be independently optimized together."},{"id":"a027-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「功耗效能面積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate ppa metrics?","options":["功耗、效能與面積通常不能同時單獨最佳化。","總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Power, performance and area generally cannot be independently optimized together.","Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"功耗、效能與面積通常不能同時單獨最佳化。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"Power, performance and area generally cannot be independently optimized together. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}},{"id":"a027-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-04"],"title":"模型與量測","titleEn":"Classify evidence types","objective":"完成「模型與量測」的量測規劃，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for classify evidence types, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：模型與量測。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：模擬預測、單元展示與量產數據不可混稱。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify evidence types. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Predictions, test demonstrations and production data are distinct evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「模擬預測、單元展示與量產數據不可混稱。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Predictions, test demonstrations and production data are distinct evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「模型與量測」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify evidence types and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「模型與量測」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for classify evidence types: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-05-k1","title":"模型與量測的原理","titleEn":"Classify evidence types principle","text":"模擬預測、單元展示與量產數據不可混稱。","textEn":"Predictions, test demonstrations and production data are distinct evidence."},{"id":"a027-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「模型與量測」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify evidence types?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","模擬預測、單元展示與量產數據不可混稱。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Predictions, test demonstrations and production data are distinct evidence.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模擬預測、單元展示與量產數據不可混稱。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"Predictions, test demonstrations and production data are distinct evidence. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}},{"id":"a027-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-05"],"title":"不確定度帳本","titleEn":"Create an uncertainty ledger","objective":"完成「不確定度帳本」的工程驗收單，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for create an uncertainty ledger, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：不確定度帳本。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：公開缺失參數須標記未知，不能補成廠商規格。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Create an uncertainty ledger. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Missing public parameters remain unknown rather than invented specifications. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「公開缺失參數須標記未知，不能補成廠商規格。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Missing public parameters remain unknown rather than invented specifications. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。 應回到「不確定度帳本」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact. Revisit assumptions and sampling for create an uncertainty ledger and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「不確定度帳本」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for create an uncertainty ledger: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-06-k1","title":"不確定度帳本的原理","titleEn":"Create an uncertainty ledger principle","text":"公開缺失參數須標記未知，不能補成廠商規格。","textEn":"Missing public parameters remain unknown rather than invented specifications."},{"id":"a027-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","textEn":"Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「不確定度帳本」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating create an uncertainty ledger?","options":["總電流合格就證明每個通道都完整。","頂面膜厚代表所有側壁與底部厚度。","公開缺失參數須標記未知，不能補成廠商規格。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable total current proves every channel is intact.","Top thickness represents all sidewall and bottom thicknesses.","Missing public parameters remain unknown rather than invented specifications."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公開缺失參數須標記未知，不能補成廠商規格。 節點比較需要明確 PPA、工作負載及幾何基準，商業名稱與研究預測不可直接充當性能證據。","explanationEn":"Missing public parameters remain unknown rather than invented specifications. Node comparisons require explicit PPA, workload and geometry baselines; commercial names and projections are not performance evidence."}}]},{"id":"a027-stage02","order":2,"title":"元件及圖案","titleEn":"Devices and patterning","description":"在「元件及圖案」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for devices and patterning, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a027-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-06"],"title":"奈米片選項","titleEn":"Compare nanosheet options","objective":"完成「奈米片選項」的因果圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare nanosheet options, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：奈米片選項。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：寬度可調與堆疊製程限制需一起比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare nanosheet options. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Width flexibility must be weighed against stack-processing limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「寬度可調與堆疊製程限制需一起比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Width flexibility must be weighed against stack-processing limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「奈米片選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare nanosheet options and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「奈米片選項」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare nanosheet options: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-07-k1","title":"奈米片選項的原理","titleEn":"Compare nanosheet options principle","text":"寬度可調與堆疊製程限制需一起比較。","textEn":"Width flexibility must be weighed against stack-processing limits."},{"id":"a027-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「奈米片選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare nanosheet options?","options":["寬度可調與堆疊製程限制需一起比較。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Width flexibility must be weighed against stack-processing limits.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"寬度可調與堆疊製程限制需一起比較。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"Width flexibility must be weighed against stack-processing limits. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}},{"id":"a027-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-07"],"title":"Forksheet 選項","titleEn":"Assess forksheet options","objective":"完成「Forksheet 選項」的對照表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess forksheet options, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：Forksheet 選項。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：介電牆改變 n-p 間距與閘加工空間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess forksheet options. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A dielectric wall changes n-p separation and gate-processing space. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介電牆改變 n-p 間距與閘加工空間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A dielectric wall changes n-p separation and gate-processing space. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「Forksheet 選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess forksheet options and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「Forksheet 選項」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess forksheet options: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-08-k1","title":"Forksheet 選項的原理","titleEn":"Assess forksheet options principle","text":"介電牆改變 n-p 間距與閘加工空間。","textEn":"A dielectric wall changes n-p separation and gate-processing space."},{"id":"a027-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「Forksheet 選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess forksheet options?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","介電牆改變 n-p 間距與閘加工空間。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","A dielectric wall changes n-p separation and gate-processing space.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"介電牆改變 n-p 間距與閘加工空間。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"A dielectric wall changes n-p separation and gate-processing space. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}},{"id":"a027-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-08"],"title":"CFET 選項","titleEn":"Assess CFET options","objective":"完成「CFET 選項」的敏感度草圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess cfet options, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：CFET 選項。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：垂直互補可省平面面積但增加上下接觸難題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess CFET options. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Vertical complementarity saves lateral area but complicates tier contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「垂直互補可省平面面積但增加上下接觸難題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Vertical complementarity saves lateral area but complicates tier contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「CFET 選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess cfet options and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「CFET 選項」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess cfet options: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-09-k1","title":"CFET 選項的原理","titleEn":"Assess CFET options principle","text":"垂直互補可省平面面積但增加上下接觸難題。","textEn":"Vertical complementarity saves lateral area but complicates tier contacts."},{"id":"a027-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「CFET 選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess cfet options?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","垂直互補可省平面面積但增加上下接觸難題。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Vertical complementarity saves lateral area but complicates tier contacts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"垂直互補可省平面面積但增加上下接觸難題。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"Vertical complementarity saves lateral area but complicates tier contacts. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}},{"id":"a027-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-09"],"title":"通道材料","titleEn":"Compare channel materials","objective":"完成「通道材料」的故障判別表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare channel materials, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：通道材料。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高遷移率材料仍需可用介面與接觸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare channel materials. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: High-mobility materials still require workable interfaces and contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高遷移率材料仍需可用介面與接觸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-mobility materials still require workable interfaces and contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「通道材料」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare channel materials and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「通道材料」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare channel materials: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-10-k1","title":"通道材料的原理","titleEn":"Compare channel materials principle","text":"高遷移率材料仍需可用介面與接觸。","textEn":"High-mobility materials still require workable interfaces and contacts."},{"id":"a027-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「通道材料」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare channel materials?","options":["高遷移率材料仍需可用介面與接觸。","幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["High-mobility materials still require workable interfaces and contacts.","Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高遷移率材料仍需可用介面與接觸。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"High-mobility materials still require workable interfaces and contacts. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}},{"id":"a027-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-10"],"title":"圖案化分解","titleEn":"Decompose patterning needs","objective":"完成「圖案化分解」的量測規劃，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for decompose patterning needs, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案化分解。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：曝光解析度、套刻及缺陷率是不同限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Decompose patterning needs. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Resolution, overlay and defectivity are distinct patterning limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「曝光解析度、套刻及缺陷率是不同限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Resolution, overlay and defectivity are distinct patterning limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「圖案化分解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for decompose patterning needs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案化分解」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for decompose patterning needs: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-11-k1","title":"圖案化分解的原理","titleEn":"Decompose patterning needs principle","text":"曝光解析度、套刻及缺陷率是不同限制。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defectivity are distinct patterning limits."},{"id":"a027-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案化分解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating decompose patterning needs?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","曝光解析度、套刻及缺陷率是不同限制。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Resolution, overlay and defectivity are distinct patterning limits.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"曝光解析度、套刻及缺陷率是不同限制。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"Resolution, overlay and defectivity are distinct patterning limits. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}},{"id":"a027-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-11"],"title":"High-NA 邊界","titleEn":"Assess High-NA boundaries","objective":"完成「High-NA 邊界」的工程驗收單，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess high-na boundaries, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：High-NA 邊界。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：高數值孔徑改變成像條件但不自動解決全部整合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess High-NA boundaries. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Higher numerical aperture changes imaging but does not solve all integration issues. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高數值孔徑改變成像條件但不自動解決全部整合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher numerical aperture changes imaging but does not solve all integration issues. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。 應回到「High-NA 邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess high-na boundaries and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「High-NA 邊界」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess high-na boundaries: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-12-k1","title":"High-NA 邊界的原理","titleEn":"Assess High-NA boundaries principle","text":"高數值孔徑改變成像條件但不自動解決全部整合。","textEn":"Higher numerical aperture changes imaging but does not solve all integration issues."},{"id":"a027-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","textEn":"Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「High-NA 邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess high-na boundaries?","options":["幾何完整即可省略漏電量測。","接觸面積加倍必定使全部串聯電阻減半。","高數值孔徑改變成像條件但不自動解決全部整合。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity eliminates the need for leakage measurements.","Doubling contact area must halve all series resistance.","Higher numerical aperture changes imaging but does not solve all integration issues."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高數值孔徑改變成像條件但不自動解決全部整合。 架構改變會同時影響靜電、電容與加工可達性，單項通道指標的改善不等於整合方案更優。","explanationEn":"Higher numerical aperture changes imaging but does not solve all integration issues. Architecture changes electrostatics, capacitance and process access; improving one channel metric does not prove a better integrated solution."}}]},{"id":"a027-stage03","order":3,"title":"電源及互連","titleEn":"Power and interconnects","description":"在「電源及互連」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for power and interconnects, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a027-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-12"],"title":"接觸瓶頸","titleEn":"Locate contact bottlenecks","objective":"完成「接觸瓶頸」的因果圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for locate contact bottlenecks, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸瓶頸。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：通道改善可能被增加的存取電阻抵銷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate contact bottlenecks. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Channel improvements can be offset by access resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「通道改善可能被增加的存取電阻抵銷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Channel improvements can be offset by access resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「接觸瓶頸」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate contact bottlenecks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸瓶頸」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for locate contact bottlenecks: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-13-k1","title":"接觸瓶頸的原理","titleEn":"Locate contact bottlenecks principle","text":"通道改善可能被增加的存取電阻抵銷。","textEn":"Channel improvements can be offset by access resistance."},{"id":"a027-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸瓶頸」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate contact bottlenecks?","options":["通道改善可能被增加的存取電阻抵銷。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Channel improvements can be offset by access resistance.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"通道改善可能被增加的存取電阻抵銷。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Channel improvements can be offset by access resistance. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}},{"id":"a027-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-13"],"title":"局部配線材料","titleEn":"Compare local interconnect materials","objective":"完成「局部配線材料」的對照表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare local interconnect materials, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：局部配線材料。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：窄線電阻不可只套用塊材電阻率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare local interconnect materials. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Narrow-line resistance cannot be inferred from bulk resistivity alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「窄線電阻不可只套用塊材電阻率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Narrow-line resistance cannot be inferred from bulk resistivity alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「局部配線材料」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare local interconnect materials and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「局部配線材料」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare local interconnect materials: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-14-k1","title":"局部配線材料的原理","titleEn":"Compare local interconnect materials principle","text":"窄線電阻不可只套用塊材電阻率。","textEn":"Narrow-line resistance cannot be inferred from bulk resistivity alone."},{"id":"a027-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「局部配線材料」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare local interconnect materials?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","窄線電阻不可只套用塊材電阻率。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Narrow-line resistance cannot be inferred from bulk resistivity alone.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"窄線電阻不可只套用塊材電阻率。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Narrow-line resistance cannot be inferred from bulk resistivity alone. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}},{"id":"a027-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-14"],"title":"背面供電","titleEn":"Assess backside power","objective":"完成「背面供電」的敏感度草圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess backside power, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背面供電。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：正背面分工可減少擁塞但增加薄化及接觸模組。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess backside power. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Front-back separation can reduce congestion but adds thinning and contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「正背面分工可減少擁塞但增加薄化及接觸模組。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Front-back separation can reduce congestion but adds thinning and contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「背面供電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess backside power and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背面供電」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess backside power: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-15-k1","title":"背面供電的原理","titleEn":"Assess backside power principle","text":"正背面分工可減少擁塞但增加薄化及接觸模組。","textEn":"Front-back separation can reduce congestion but adds thinning and contacts."},{"id":"a027-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背面供電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess backside power?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","正背面分工可減少擁塞但增加薄化及接觸模組。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Front-back separation can reduce congestion but adds thinning and contacts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"正背面分工可減少擁塞但增加薄化及接觸模組。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Front-back separation can reduce congestion but adds thinning and contacts. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}},{"id":"a027-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-15"],"title":"熱路徑","titleEn":"Budget thermal pathways","objective":"完成「熱路徑」的故障判別表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget thermal pathways, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱路徑。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高密度與垂直堆疊會改變局部熱阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget thermal pathways. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Density and vertical stacking change local thermal resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高密度與垂直堆疊會改變局部熱阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Density and vertical stacking change local thermal resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「熱路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget thermal pathways and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱路徑」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget thermal pathways: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-16-k1","title":"熱路徑的原理","titleEn":"Budget thermal pathways principle","text":"高密度與垂直堆疊會改變局部熱阻。","textEn":"Density and vertical stacking change local thermal resistance."},{"id":"a027-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget thermal pathways?","options":["高密度與垂直堆疊會改變局部熱阻。","節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["Density and vertical stacking change local thermal resistance.","The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高密度與垂直堆疊會改變局部熱阻。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Density and vertical stacking change local thermal resistance. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}},{"id":"a027-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-16"],"title":"標準元件協同","titleEn":"Co-design standard cells","objective":"完成「標準元件協同」的量測規劃，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for co-design standard cells, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：標準元件協同。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：元件截面需與可實際連線的元件庫一起評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Co-design standard cells. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Device sections need evaluation with routable cell libraries. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元件截面需與可實際連線的元件庫一起評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Device sections need evaluation with routable cell libraries. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「標準元件協同」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for co-design standard cells and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「標準元件協同」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for co-design standard cells: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-17-k1","title":"標準元件協同的原理","titleEn":"Co-design standard cells principle","text":"元件截面需與可實際連線的元件庫一起評估。","textEn":"Device sections need evaluation with routable cell libraries."},{"id":"a027-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「標準元件協同」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating co-design standard cells?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","元件截面需與可實際連線的元件庫一起評估。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","Device sections need evaluation with routable cell libraries.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"元件截面需與可實際連線的元件庫一起評估。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Device sections need evaluation with routable cell libraries. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}},{"id":"a027-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-17"],"title":"SRAM 不同需求","titleEn":"Separate SRAM constraints","objective":"完成「SRAM 不同需求」的工程驗收單，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for separate sram constraints, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SRAM 不同需求。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：記憶體單元的穩定裕度不同於單純邏輯延遲。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate SRAM constraints. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Memory-cell stability differs from logic-delay optimization. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「記憶體單元的穩定裕度不同於單純邏輯延遲。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Memory-cell stability differs from logic-delay optimization. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。 應回到「SRAM 不同需求」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: The node name is a measured physical gate length. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate sram constraints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SRAM 不同需求」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for separate sram constraints: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-18-k1","title":"SRAM 不同需求的原理","titleEn":"Separate SRAM constraints principle","text":"記憶體單元的穩定裕度不同於單純邏輯延遲。","textEn":"Memory-cell stability differs from logic-delay optimization."},{"id":"a027-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","textEn":"As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SRAM 不同需求」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate sram constraints?","options":["節點名稱就是實體閘長的量測值。","模擬最佳值可直接當成量產良率。","記憶體單元的穩定裕度不同於單純邏輯延遲。"],"optionsEn":["The node name is a measured physical gate length.","The best simulation value directly represents production yield.","Memory-cell stability differs from logic-delay optimization."],"answer":2,"explanation":"記憶體單元的穩定裕度不同於單純邏輯延遲。 當接觸與互連占比增加，通道縮放對電路效能的改善可能遞減，需要由元件跨到配線協同設計。","explanationEn":"Memory-cell stability differs from logic-delay optimization. As contacts and interconnects contribute more, channel-scaling gains can diminish, requiring device-routing co-design."}}]},{"id":"a027-stage04","order":4,"title":"研究證據","titleEn":"Research evidence","description":"在「研究證據」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for research evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a027-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-18"],"title":"變異來源","titleEn":"Build a variability budget","objective":"完成「變異來源」的因果圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for build a variability budget, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：變異來源。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：幾何、材料與隨機缺陷需分開估算。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a variability budget. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Geometry, materials and stochastic defects need separate estimates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何、材料與隨機缺陷需分開估算。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Geometry, materials and stochastic defects need separate estimates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「變異來源」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a variability budget and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「變異來源」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for build a variability budget: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-19-k1","title":"變異來源的原理","titleEn":"Build a variability budget principle","text":"幾何、材料與隨機缺陷需分開估算。","textEn":"Geometry, materials and stochastic defects need separate estimates."},{"id":"a027-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「變異來源」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a variability budget?","options":["幾何、材料與隨機缺陷需分開估算。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Geometry, materials and stochastic defects need separate estimates.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何、材料與隨機缺陷需分開估算。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"Geometry, materials and stochastic defects need separate estimates. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}},{"id":"a027-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-19"],"title":"可靠度範圍","titleEn":"Define reliability conditions","objective":"完成「可靠度範圍」的對照表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for define reliability conditions, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：可靠度範圍。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：加速壓力試驗須有可解釋的外推模型。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define reliability conditions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Accelerated stress tests need an interpretable extrapolation model. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「加速壓力試驗須有可解釋的外推模型。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Accelerated stress tests need an interpretable extrapolation model. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「可靠度範圍」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define reliability conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「可靠度範圍」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for define reliability conditions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-20-k1","title":"可靠度範圍的原理","titleEn":"Define reliability conditions principle","text":"加速壓力試驗須有可解釋的外推模型。","textEn":"Accelerated stress tests need an interpretable extrapolation model."},{"id":"a027-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「可靠度範圍」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define reliability conditions?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","加速壓力試驗須有可解釋的外推模型。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Accelerated stress tests need an interpretable extrapolation model.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加速壓力試驗須有可解釋的外推模型。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"Accelerated stress tests need an interpretable extrapolation model. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}},{"id":"a027-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-20"],"title":"良率與成本","titleEn":"Connect yield and cost","objective":"完成「良率與成本」的敏感度草圖，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for connect yield and cost, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：良率與成本。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：較小裸晶不保證每顆良品成本較低。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect yield and cost. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Smaller dies do not guarantee lower cost per good die. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較小裸晶不保證每顆良品成本較低。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Smaller dies do not guarantee lower cost per good die. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「良率與成本」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect yield and cost and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「良率與成本」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for connect yield and cost: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-21-k1","title":"良率與成本的原理","titleEn":"Connect yield and cost principle","text":"較小裸晶不保證每顆良品成本較低。","textEn":"Smaller dies do not guarantee lower cost per good die."},{"id":"a027-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「良率與成本」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect yield and cost?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","較小裸晶不保證每顆良品成本較低。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","Smaller dies do not guarantee lower cost per good die."],"answer":2,"explanation":"較小裸晶不保證每顆良品成本較低。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"Smaller dies do not guarantee lower cost per good die. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}},{"id":"a027-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-21"],"title":"路線圖日期","titleEn":"Version roadmap claims","objective":"完成「路線圖日期」的故障判別表，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for version roadmap claims, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：路線圖日期。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：研究路線圖是有日期的預測而非交貨承諾。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Version roadmap claims. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Roadmaps are dated projections rather than delivery commitments. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「研究路線圖是有日期的預測而非交貨承諾。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Roadmaps are dated projections rather than delivery commitments. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「路線圖日期」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for version roadmap claims and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「路線圖日期」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for version roadmap claims: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-22-k1","title":"路線圖日期的原理","titleEn":"Version roadmap claims principle","text":"研究路線圖是有日期的預測而非交貨承諾。","textEn":"Roadmaps are dated projections rather than delivery commitments."},{"id":"a027-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「路線圖日期」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating version roadmap claims?","options":["研究路線圖是有日期的預測而非交貨承諾。","單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["Roadmaps are dated projections rather than delivery commitments.","One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"研究路線圖是有日期的預測而非交貨承諾。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"Roadmaps are dated projections rather than delivery commitments. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}},{"id":"a027-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-22"],"title":"公平比較矩陣","titleEn":"Build a fair comparison matrix","objective":"完成「公平比較矩陣」的量測規劃，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for build a fair comparison matrix, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：公平比較矩陣。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：只選各方案最佳單點會掩蓋共同限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a fair comparison matrix. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Selecting each option's best isolated metric hides common constraints. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只選各方案最佳單點會掩蓋共同限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Selecting each option's best isolated metric hides common constraints. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「公平比較矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a fair comparison matrix and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「公平比較矩陣」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for build a fair comparison matrix: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-23-k1","title":"公平比較矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Build a fair comparison matrix principle","text":"只選各方案最佳單點會掩蓋共同限制。","textEn":"Selecting each option's best isolated metric hides common constraints."},{"id":"a027-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「公平比較矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a fair comparison matrix?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","只選各方案最佳單點會掩蓋共同限制。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Selecting each option's best isolated metric hides common constraints.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只選各方案最佳單點會掩蓋共同限制。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"Selecting each option's best isolated metric hides common constraints. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}},{"id":"a027-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-scaling","v8a-cfet","v8a-backside"],"prerequisiteIds":["a027-v8-23"],"title":"研究提案交付","titleEn":"Deliver a research proposal","objective":"完成「研究提案交付」的工程驗收單，把比較基準、架構權衡及證據成熟度中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for deliver a research proposal, connecting relevant limits in comparison baselines, architecture tradeoffs and evidence maturity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：研究提案交付。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：提出可量測假說、對照組及失敗判準才可檢驗。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Deliver a research proposal. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: A testable proposal needs measurable hypotheses, controls and failure criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提出可量測假說、對照組及失敗判準才可檢驗。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A testable proposal needs measurable hypotheses, controls and failure criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。 應回到「研究提案交付」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer. Revisit assumptions and sampling for deliver a research proposal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「研究提案交付」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for deliver a research proposal: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a027-v8-24-k1","title":"研究提案交付的原理","titleEn":"Deliver a research proposal principle","text":"提出可量測假說、對照組及失敗判準才可檢驗。","textEn":"A testable proposal needs measurable hypotheses, controls and failure criteria."},{"id":"a027-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","textEn":"Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「研究提案交付」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating deliver a research proposal?","options":["單一中層截面可代表所有堆疊層。","低電阻可自動證明介電隔離完整。","提出可量測假說、對照組及失敗判準才可檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["One middle-layer section represents every stacked layer.","Low resistance automatically proves dielectric isolation.","A testable proposal needs measurable hypotheses, controls and failure criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"提出可量測假說、對照組及失敗判準才可檢驗。 模擬、測試結構與量產資料的抽樣範圍不同，研究結論應附樣本、偏壓、模型假設及可重現條件。","explanationEn":"A testable proposal needs measurable hypotheses, controls and failure criteria. Simulations, test structures and production data sample different scopes; state samples, bias, model assumptions and reproducibility conditions."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a028","title":"奈米片內側間隔層製作","titleEn":"Nanosheet inner-spacer fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["間隔層功能","側向凹蝕","填充與回蝕","釋放保護"],"labelsEn":["Spacer functions","Lateral recess","Fill and etchback","Protection during release"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a028-stage01","order":1,"title":"間隔層功能","titleEn":"Spacer functions","description":"在「間隔層功能」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for spacer functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a028-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"內外間隔差別","titleEn":"Separate inner and outer spacers","objective":"完成「內外間隔差別」的因果圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate inner and outer spacers, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：內外間隔差別。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：內間隔位於片間端部，外間隔位於閘外側。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate inner and outer spacers. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Inner spacers occupy inter-sheet ends while outer spacers flank the gate. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「內間隔位於片間端部，外間隔位於閘外側。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Inner spacers occupy inter-sheet ends while outer spacers flank the gate. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「內外間隔差別」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate inner and outer spacers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「內外間隔差別」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate inner and outer spacers: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-01-k1","title":"內外間隔差別的原理","titleEn":"Separate inner and outer spacers principle","text":"內間隔位於片間端部，外間隔位於閘外側。","textEn":"Inner spacers occupy inter-sheet ends while outer spacers flank the gate."},{"id":"a028-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「內外間隔差別」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate inner and outer spacers?","options":["內間隔位於片間端部，外間隔位於閘外側。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Inner spacers occupy inter-sheet ends while outer spacers flank the gate.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"內間隔位於片間端部，外間隔位於閘外側。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Inner spacers occupy inter-sheet ends while outer spacers flank the gate. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}},{"id":"a028-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-01"],"title":"閘源汲隔離","titleEn":"Trace gate-source/drain isolation","objective":"完成「閘源汲隔離」的對照表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace gate-source/drain isolation, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘源汲隔離。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：內間隔同時影響電隔離及後續選蝕保護。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace gate-source/drain isolation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Inner spacers affect electrical isolation and later selective-etch protection. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「內間隔同時影響電隔離及後續選蝕保護。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Inner spacers affect electrical isolation and later selective-etch protection. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘源汲隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace gate-source/drain isolation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘源汲隔離」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace gate-source/drain isolation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-02-k1","title":"閘源汲隔離的原理","titleEn":"Trace gate-source/drain isolation principle","text":"內間隔同時影響電隔離及後續選蝕保護。","textEn":"Inner spacers affect electrical isolation and later selective-etch protection."},{"id":"a028-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘源汲隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace gate-source/drain isolation?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","內間隔同時影響電隔離及後續選蝕保護。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Inner spacers affect electrical isolation and later selective-etch protection.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"內間隔同時影響電隔離及後續選蝕保護。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Inner spacers affect electrical isolation and later selective-etch protection. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}},{"id":"a028-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-02"],"title":"寄生電容","titleEn":"Estimate parasitic coupling","objective":"完成「寄生電容」的敏感度草圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for estimate parasitic coupling, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：寄生電容。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：介電常數與實際幾何共同決定耦合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 以平行板近似 C∝kA/d 做相對比較：固定面積，將 k 降為 0.8、間距降為 0.8；求電容比，說明低 k 與幾何縮放可能互相抵銷。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate parasitic coupling. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Permittivity and actual geometry jointly determine coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Use relative C∝kA/d at fixed area: both k and spacing become 0.8 of their initial values. Compute the ratio and explain cancellation between lower k and geometric scaling.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介電常數與實際幾何共同決定耦合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Permittivity and actual geometry jointly determine coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「寄生電容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate parasitic coupling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「寄生電容」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for estimate parasitic coupling: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-03-k1","title":"寄生電容的原理","titleEn":"Estimate parasitic coupling principle","text":"介電常數與實際幾何共同決定耦合。","textEn":"Permittivity and actual geometry jointly determine coupling."},{"id":"a028-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「寄生電容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate parasitic coupling?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","介電常數與實際幾何共同決定耦合。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Permittivity and actual geometry jointly determine coupling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電常數與實際幾何共同決定耦合。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Permittivity and actual geometry jointly determine coupling. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}},{"id":"a028-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-03"],"title":"間隔長度","titleEn":"Budget spacer length","objective":"完成「間隔長度」的故障判別表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for budget spacer length, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：間隔長度。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：太短增加耦合風險，太長可能增加存取電阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget spacer length. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Short spacers increase coupling risk while long spacers can add access resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「太短增加耦合風險，太長可能增加存取電阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Short spacers increase coupling risk while long spacers can add access resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「間隔長度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget spacer length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「間隔長度」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for budget spacer length: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-04-k1","title":"間隔長度的原理","titleEn":"Budget spacer length principle","text":"太短增加耦合風險，太長可能增加存取電阻。","textEn":"Short spacers increase coupling risk while long spacers can add access resistance."},{"id":"a028-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「間隔長度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget spacer length?","options":["太短增加耦合風險，太長可能增加存取電阻。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Short spacers increase coupling risk while long spacers can add access resistance.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"太短增加耦合風險，太長可能增加存取電阻。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Short spacers increase coupling risk while long spacers can add access resistance. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}},{"id":"a028-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-04"],"title":"片間可達性","titleEn":"Assess inter-sheet access","objective":"完成「片間可達性」的量測規劃，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess inter-sheet access, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片間可達性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同層的反應物到達及產物排出可能不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess inter-sheet access. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Reactant access and product removal can differ by layer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同層的反應物到達及產物排出可能不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reactant access and product removal can differ by layer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「片間可達性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess inter-sheet access and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片間可達性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess inter-sheet access: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-05-k1","title":"片間可達性的原理","titleEn":"Assess inter-sheet access principle","text":"不同層的反應物到達及產物排出可能不同。","textEn":"Reactant access and product removal can differ by layer."},{"id":"a028-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片間可達性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess inter-sheet access?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","不同層的反應物到達及產物排出可能不同。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Reactant access and product removal can differ by layer.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同層的反應物到達及產物排出可能不同。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Reactant access and product removal can differ by layer. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}},{"id":"a028-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-05"],"title":"源汲端點保護","titleEn":"Mark protected sheet ends","objective":"完成「源汲端點保護」的工程驗收單，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for mark protected sheet ends, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲端點保護。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：間隔形成不能消耗有效通道端點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Mark protected sheet ends. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Spacer formation must preserve functional channel ends. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「間隔形成不能消耗有效通道端點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Spacer formation must preserve functional channel ends. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「源汲端點保護」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for mark protected sheet ends and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲端點保護」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for mark protected sheet ends: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-06-k1","title":"源汲端點保護的原理","titleEn":"Mark protected sheet ends principle","text":"間隔形成不能消耗有效通道端點。","textEn":"Spacer formation must preserve functional channel ends."},{"id":"a028-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","textEn":"Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲端點保護」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating mark protected sheet ends?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","間隔形成不能消耗有效通道端點。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Spacer formation must preserve functional channel ends."],"answer":2,"explanation":"間隔形成不能消耗有效通道端點。 內間隔在閘與源汲極間提供電性及化學屏障，其長度與介電常數共同影響寄生電容。","explanationEn":"Spacer formation must preserve functional channel ends. Inner spacers form electrical and chemical barriers between gate and source-drain; length and permittivity jointly affect parasitic capacitance."}}]},{"id":"a028-stage02","order":2,"title":"側向凹蝕","titleEn":"Lateral recess","description":"在「側向凹蝕」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for lateral recess, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a028-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-06"],"title":"凹蝕選擇比","titleEn":"Define recess selectivity","objective":"完成「凹蝕選擇比」的因果圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define recess selectivity, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：凹蝕選擇比。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：犧牲材料去除量需與通道損失一起量測。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define recess selectivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Measure sacrificial removal together with channel loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「犧牲材料去除量需與通道損失一起量測。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Measure sacrificial removal together with channel loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「凹蝕選擇比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define recess selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「凹蝕選擇比」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define recess selectivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-07-k1","title":"凹蝕選擇比的原理","titleEn":"Define recess selectivity principle","text":"犧牲材料去除量需與通道損失一起量測。","textEn":"Measure sacrificial removal together with channel loss."},{"id":"a028-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「凹蝕選擇比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define recess selectivity?","options":["犧牲材料去除量需與通道損失一起量測。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Measure sacrificial removal together with channel loss.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"犧牲材料去除量需與通道損失一起量測。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Measure sacrificial removal together with channel loss. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}},{"id":"a028-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-07"],"title":"側向深度分布","titleEn":"Map recess-depth distributions","objective":"完成「側向深度分布」的對照表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for map recess-depth distributions, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：側向深度分布。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：平均凹蝕深度會掩蓋頂底片差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map recess-depth distributions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Mean recess depth can hide top-bottom differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均凹蝕深度會掩蓋頂底片差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean recess depth can hide top-bottom differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「側向深度分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map recess-depth distributions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「側向深度分布」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for map recess-depth distributions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-08-k1","title":"側向深度分布的原理","titleEn":"Map recess-depth distributions principle","text":"平均凹蝕深度會掩蓋頂底片差異。","textEn":"Mean recess depth can hide top-bottom differences."},{"id":"a028-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「側向深度分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map recess-depth distributions?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均凹蝕深度會掩蓋頂底片差異。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean recess depth can hide top-bottom differences.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均凹蝕深度會掩蓋頂底片差異。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Mean recess depth can hide top-bottom differences. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}},{"id":"a028-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-08"],"title":"凹角形狀","titleEn":"Inspect recessed corners","objective":"完成「凹角形狀」的敏感度草圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect recessed corners, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：凹角形狀。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：圓角與尖角會改變後續填充截面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect recessed corners. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Rounded and sharp corners produce different fill geometries. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「圓角與尖角會改變後續填充截面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rounded and sharp corners produce different fill geometries. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「凹角形狀」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect recessed corners and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「凹角形狀」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect recessed corners: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-09-k1","title":"凹角形狀的原理","titleEn":"Inspect recessed corners principle","text":"圓角與尖角會改變後續填充截面。","textEn":"Rounded and sharp corners produce different fill geometries."},{"id":"a028-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「凹角形狀」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect recessed corners?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","圓角與尖角會改變後續填充截面。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Rounded and sharp corners produce different fill geometries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圓角與尖角會改變後續填充截面。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Rounded and sharp corners produce different fill geometries. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}},{"id":"a028-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-09"],"title":"薄層粗糙","titleEn":"Check thin-layer roughness","objective":"完成「薄層粗糙」的故障判別表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for check thin-layer roughness, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：薄層粗糙。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：粗糙度相對於目標間隔長度可能不可忽略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check thin-layer roughness. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Roughness may be significant relative to spacer length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粗糙度相對於目標間隔長度可能不可忽略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Roughness may be significant relative to spacer length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「薄層粗糙」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check thin-layer roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「薄層粗糙」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for check thin-layer roughness: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-10-k1","title":"薄層粗糙的原理","titleEn":"Check thin-layer roughness principle","text":"粗糙度相對於目標間隔長度可能不可忽略。","textEn":"Roughness may be significant relative to spacer length."},{"id":"a028-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「薄層粗糙」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check thin-layer roughness?","options":["粗糙度相對於目標間隔長度可能不可忽略。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Roughness may be significant relative to spacer length.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"粗糙度相對於目標間隔長度可能不可忽略。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Roughness may be significant relative to spacer length. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}},{"id":"a028-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-10"],"title":"過蝕風險","titleEn":"Assess overetch","objective":"完成「過蝕風險」的量測規劃，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess overetch, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：過蝕風險。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：延長處理以清除最慢位置會增加其他區域損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess overetch. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Extending treatment for the slowest region increases loss elsewhere. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「延長處理以清除最慢位置會增加其他區域損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Extending treatment for the slowest region increases loss elsewhere. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「過蝕風險」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess overetch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「過蝕風險」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess overetch: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-11-k1","title":"過蝕風險的原理","titleEn":"Assess overetch principle","text":"延長處理以清除最慢位置會增加其他區域損失。","textEn":"Extending treatment for the slowest region increases loss elsewhere."},{"id":"a028-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「過蝕風險」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess overetch?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","延長處理以清除最慢位置會增加其他區域損失。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Extending treatment for the slowest region increases loss elsewhere.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"延長處理以清除最慢位置會增加其他區域損失。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Extending treatment for the slowest region increases loss elsewhere. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}},{"id":"a028-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-11"],"title":"圖案負載","titleEn":"Compare pattern loading","objective":"完成「圖案負載」的工程驗收單，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare pattern loading, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案負載。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：密集與稀疏結構需分別驗證凹蝕。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare pattern loading. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Dense and sparse structures need separate recess validation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「密集與稀疏結構需分別驗證凹蝕。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dense and sparse structures need separate recess validation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「圖案負載」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare pattern loading and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案負載」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare pattern loading: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-12-k1","title":"圖案負載的原理","titleEn":"Compare pattern loading principle","text":"密集與稀疏結構需分別驗證凹蝕。","textEn":"Dense and sparse structures need separate recess validation."},{"id":"a028-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","textEn":"Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案負載」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare pattern loading?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","密集與稀疏結構需分別驗證凹蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Dense and sparse structures need separate recess validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"密集與稀疏結構需分別驗證凹蝕。 各層凹蝕的平均深度及最差偏差都重要，局部過深會改變存取長度，過淺則減少保護裕度。","explanationEn":"Dense and sparse structures need separate recess validation. Mean and worst-layer recess matter: excessive recess alters access length while shallow recess reduces protection margin."}}]},{"id":"a028-stage03","order":3,"title":"填充與回蝕","titleEn":"Fill and etchback","description":"在「填充與回蝕」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for fill and etchback, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a028-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-12"],"title":"低介電材料","titleEn":"Compare low-k materials","objective":"完成「低介電材料」的因果圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare low-k materials, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：低介電材料。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：低介電常數不保證機械與化學耐受。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare low-k materials. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Low permittivity does not guarantee mechanical or chemical robustness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低介電常數不保證機械與化學耐受。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low permittivity does not guarantee mechanical or chemical robustness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「低介電材料」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare low-k materials and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「低介電材料」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare low-k materials: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-13-k1","title":"低介電材料的原理","titleEn":"Compare low-k materials principle","text":"低介電常數不保證機械與化學耐受。","textEn":"Low permittivity does not guarantee mechanical or chemical robustness."},{"id":"a028-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「低介電材料」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare low-k materials?","options":["低介電常數不保證機械與化學耐受。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Low permittivity does not guarantee mechanical or chemical robustness.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低介電常數不保證機械與化學耐受。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"Low permittivity does not guarantee mechanical or chemical robustness. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}},{"id":"a028-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-13"],"title":"共形沉積","titleEn":"Assess conformal deposition","objective":"完成「共形沉積」的對照表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess conformal deposition, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：共形沉積。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：厚度共形還需檢查成分共形。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess conformal deposition. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Thickness conformality also needs compositional conformality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度共形還需檢查成分共形。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness conformality also needs compositional conformality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「共形沉積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess conformal deposition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「共形沉積」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess conformal deposition: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-14-k1","title":"共形沉積的原理","titleEn":"Assess conformal deposition principle","text":"厚度共形還需檢查成分共形。","textEn":"Thickness conformality also needs compositional conformality."},{"id":"a028-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「共形沉積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess conformal deposition?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","厚度共形還需檢查成分共形。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Thickness conformality also needs compositional conformality.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度共形還需檢查成分共形。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"Thickness conformality also needs compositional conformality. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}},{"id":"a028-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-14"],"title":"腔口封閉","titleEn":"Predict opening closure","objective":"完成「腔口封閉」的敏感度草圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for predict opening closure, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：腔口封閉。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：入口較快成長可能留下隱藏空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Predict opening closure. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Faster entrance growth can trap hidden voids. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「入口較快成長可能留下隱藏空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Faster entrance growth can trap hidden voids. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「腔口封閉」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for predict opening closure and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「腔口封閉」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for predict opening closure: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-15-k1","title":"腔口封閉的原理","titleEn":"Predict opening closure principle","text":"入口較快成長可能留下隱藏空洞。","textEn":"Faster entrance growth can trap hidden voids."},{"id":"a028-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「腔口封閉」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating predict opening closure?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","入口較快成長可能留下隱藏空洞。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Faster entrance growth can trap hidden voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"入口較快成長可能留下隱藏空洞。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"Faster entrance growth can trap hidden voids. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}},{"id":"a028-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-15"],"title":"回蝕選擇性","titleEn":"Check etchback selectivity","objective":"完成「回蝕選擇性」的故障判別表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for check etchback selectivity, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：回蝕選擇性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：需去除外部材料而保留凹槽中的內間隔。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check etchback selectivity. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: External material must be removed while retaining recessed spacers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需去除外部材料而保留凹槽中的內間隔。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: External material must be removed while retaining recessed spacers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「回蝕選擇性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check etchback selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「回蝕選擇性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for check etchback selectivity: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-16-k1","title":"回蝕選擇性的原理","titleEn":"Check etchback selectivity principle","text":"需去除外部材料而保留凹槽中的內間隔。","textEn":"External material must be removed while retaining recessed spacers."},{"id":"a028-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「回蝕選擇性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check etchback selectivity?","options":["需去除外部材料而保留凹槽中的內間隔。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["External material must be removed while retaining recessed spacers.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"需去除外部材料而保留凹槽中的內間隔。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"External material must be removed while retaining recessed spacers. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}},{"id":"a028-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-16"],"title":"片端殘留","titleEn":"Inspect sheet-end residue","objective":"完成「片端殘留」的量測規劃，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect sheet-end residue, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片端殘留。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：端點殘留可阻礙源汲極磊晶成長。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect sheet-end residue. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Endpoint residues can obstruct source-drain epitaxy. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「端點殘留可阻礙源汲極磊晶成長。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Endpoint residues can obstruct source-drain epitaxy. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「片端殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect sheet-end residue and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片端殘留」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect sheet-end residue: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-17-k1","title":"片端殘留的原理","titleEn":"Inspect sheet-end residue principle","text":"端點殘留可阻礙源汲極磊晶成長。","textEn":"Endpoint residues can obstruct source-drain epitaxy."},{"id":"a028-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片端殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect sheet-end residue?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","端點殘留可阻礙源汲極磊晶成長。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Endpoint residues can obstruct source-drain epitaxy.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"端點殘留可阻礙源汲極磊晶成長。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"Endpoint residues can obstruct source-drain epitaxy. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}},{"id":"a028-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-17"],"title":"介電針孔","titleEn":"Locate dielectric pinholes","objective":"完成「介電針孔」的工程驗收單，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate dielectric pinholes, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介電針孔。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：單一缺口可能成為後續蝕刻侵入路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate dielectric pinholes. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: A single opening can become a later etchant-access path. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一缺口可能成為後續蝕刻侵入路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A single opening can become a later etchant-access path. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「介電針孔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate dielectric pinholes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介電針孔」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate dielectric pinholes: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-18-k1","title":"介電針孔的原理","titleEn":"Locate dielectric pinholes principle","text":"單一缺口可能成為後續蝕刻侵入路徑。","textEn":"A single opening can become a later etchant-access path."},{"id":"a028-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","textEn":"Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介電針孔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate dielectric pinholes?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","單一缺口可能成為後續蝕刻侵入路徑。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","A single opening can become a later etchant-access path."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一缺口可能成為後續蝕刻侵入路徑。 沉積與回蝕必須形成內部保留、外部清除的幾何選擇性，不能只憑全面膜厚判定成功。","explanationEn":"A single opening can become a later etchant-access path. Deposition and etchback must retain recessed material while clearing exposed surfaces; blanket thickness cannot establish success."}}]},{"id":"a028-stage04","order":4,"title":"釋放保護","titleEn":"Protection during release","description":"在「釋放保護」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for protection during release, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a028-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-18"],"title":"犧牲層釋放","titleEn":"Assess release survival","objective":"完成「犧牲層釋放」的因果圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess release survival, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：犧牲層釋放。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：內間隔需承受犧牲層移除的化學環境。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess release survival. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Inner spacers must survive sacrificial-layer removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「內間隔需承受犧牲層移除的化學環境。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Inner spacers must survive sacrificial-layer removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「犧牲層釋放」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess release survival and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「犧牲層釋放」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess release survival: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-19-k1","title":"犧牲層釋放的原理","titleEn":"Assess release survival principle","text":"內間隔需承受犧牲層移除的化學環境。","textEn":"Inner spacers must survive sacrificial-layer removal."},{"id":"a028-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「犧牲層釋放」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess release survival?","options":["內間隔需承受犧牲層移除的化學環境。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Inner spacers must survive sacrificial-layer removal.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"內間隔需承受犧牲層移除的化學環境。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"Inner spacers must survive sacrificial-layer removal. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}},{"id":"a028-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-19"],"title":"源汲極侵蝕","titleEn":"Detect source-drain attack","objective":"完成「源汲極侵蝕」的對照表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for detect source-drain attack, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極侵蝕。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：源汲極縮減可反映內間隔保護失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Detect source-drain attack. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Source-drain loss can indicate failed spacer protection. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「源汲極縮減可反映內間隔保護失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source-drain loss can indicate failed spacer protection. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「源汲極侵蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for detect source-drain attack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極侵蝕」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for detect source-drain attack: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-20-k1","title":"源汲極侵蝕的原理","titleEn":"Detect source-drain attack principle","text":"源汲極縮減可反映內間隔保護失效。","textEn":"Source-drain loss can indicate failed spacer protection."},{"id":"a028-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極侵蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating detect source-drain attack?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","源汲極縮減可反映內間隔保護失效。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Source-drain loss can indicate failed spacer protection.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"源汲極縮減可反映內間隔保護失效。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"Source-drain loss can indicate failed spacer protection. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}},{"id":"a028-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-20"],"title":"電容量測","titleEn":"Measure coupling capacitance","objective":"完成「電容量測」的敏感度草圖，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for measure coupling capacitance, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電容量測。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：比較需控制重疊面積及電性偏壓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure coupling capacitance. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Comparisons need matched overlap area and bias. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較需控制重疊面積及電性偏壓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Comparisons need matched overlap area and bias. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「電容量測」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure coupling capacitance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電容量測」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for measure coupling capacitance: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-21-k1","title":"電容量測的原理","titleEn":"Measure coupling capacitance principle","text":"比較需控制重疊面積及電性偏壓。","textEn":"Comparisons need matched overlap area and bias."},{"id":"a028-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電容量測」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure coupling capacitance?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","比較需控制重疊面積及電性偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Comparisons need matched overlap area and bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較需控制重疊面積及電性偏壓。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"Comparisons need matched overlap area and bias. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}},{"id":"a028-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-21"],"title":"存取電阻","titleEn":"Assess access resistance","objective":"完成「存取電阻」的故障判別表，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess access resistance, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：存取電阻。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：降低電容的改動可能增加非閘控區電阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess access resistance. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Capacitance reduction can increase ungated access resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「降低電容的改動可能增加非閘控區電阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Capacitance reduction can increase ungated access resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「存取電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess access resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「存取電阻」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess access resistance: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-22-k1","title":"存取電阻的原理","titleEn":"Assess access resistance principle","text":"降低電容的改動可能增加非閘控區電阻。","textEn":"Capacitance reduction can increase ungated access resistance."},{"id":"a028-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「存取電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess access resistance?","options":["降低電容的改動可能增加非閘控區電阻。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Capacitance reduction can increase ungated access resistance.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低電容的改動可能增加非閘控區電阻。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"Capacitance reduction can increase ungated access resistance. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}},{"id":"a028-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-22"],"title":"逐層截面","titleEn":"Inspect every sheet level","objective":"完成「逐層截面」的量測規劃，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect every sheet level, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：逐層截面。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：單一中層截面不能代表整個堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect every sheet level. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: One middle-level section cannot represent the full stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一中層截面不能代表整個堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One middle-level section cannot represent the full stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「逐層截面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect every sheet level and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「逐層截面」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect every sheet level: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-23-k1","title":"逐層截面的原理","titleEn":"Inspect every sheet level principle","text":"單一中層截面不能代表整個堆疊。","textEn":"One middle-level section cannot represent the full stack."},{"id":"a028-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「逐層截面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect every sheet level?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","單一中層截面不能代表整個堆疊。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","One middle-level section cannot represent the full stack.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一中層截面不能代表整個堆疊。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"One middle-level section cannot represent the full stack. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}},{"id":"a028-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sparc","v8a-selective","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a028-v8-23"],"title":"間隔模組放行","titleEn":"Release the spacer module","objective":"完成「間隔模組放行」的工程驗收單，把側向凹蝕、低介電填充及釋放保護中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the spacer module, connecting relevant limits in lateral recess, low-k fill and release protection to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：間隔模組放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：尺寸、覆蓋、低電容及釋放後存活須共同成立。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the spacer module. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Dimensions, coverage, capacitance and post-release survival must all hold. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「尺寸、覆蓋、低電容及釋放後存活須共同成立。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dimensions, coverage, capacitance and post-release survival must all hold. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「間隔模組放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the spacer module and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「間隔模組放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the spacer module: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a028-v8-24-k1","title":"間隔模組放行的原理","titleEn":"Release the spacer module principle","text":"尺寸、覆蓋、低電容及釋放後存活須共同成立。","textEn":"Dimensions, coverage, capacitance and post-release survival must all hold."},{"id":"a028-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","textEn":"A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「間隔模組放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the spacer module?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","尺寸、覆蓋、低電容及釋放後存活須共同成立。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Dimensions, coverage, capacitance and post-release survival must all hold."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺寸、覆蓋、低電容及釋放後存活須共同成立。 低介電常數材料若在釋放中受損，可能形成源汲極侵蝕路徑，因此電容收益需以化學存活為前提。","explanationEn":"Dimensions, coverage, capacitance and post-release survival must all hold. A low-k material damaged during release may expose source-drain to attack, so capacitance benefits require chemical survival."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a029","title":"源汲極接觸電阻控制","titleEn":"Source-drain contact resistance control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電阻分解","界面與摻雜","幾何及量測","整合及壽命"],"labelsEn":["Resistance decomposition","Interface and doping","Geometry and measurement","Integration and lifetime"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a029-stage01","order":1,"title":"電阻分解","titleEn":"Resistance decomposition","description":"在「電阻分解」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for resistance decomposition, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a029-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"電阻與比接觸電阻","titleEn":"Separate resistance and resistivity","objective":"完成「電阻與比接觸電阻」的因果圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate resistance and resistivity, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電阻與比接觸電阻。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：接觸電阻與比接觸電阻的單位不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate resistance and resistivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Contact resistance and specific contact resistivity have different units. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸電阻與比接觸電阻的單位不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contact resistance and specific contact resistivity have different units. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「電阻與比接觸電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate resistance and resistivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電阻與比接觸電阻」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate resistance and resistivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-01-k1","title":"電阻與比接觸電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate resistance and resistivity principle","text":"接觸電阻與比接觸電阻的單位不同。","textEn":"Contact resistance and specific contact resistivity have different units."},{"id":"a029-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電阻與比接觸電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate resistance and resistivity?","options":["接觸電阻與比接觸電阻的單位不同。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Contact resistance and specific contact resistivity have different units.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸電阻與比接觸電阻的單位不同。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance and specific contact resistivity have different units. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}},{"id":"a029-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-01"],"title":"通道與存取路徑","titleEn":"Separate channel and access paths","objective":"完成「通道與存取路徑」的對照表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate channel and access paths, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：通道與存取路徑。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：總電阻包含通道、源汲極、界面及金屬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate channel and access paths. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Total resistance includes channel, source-drain, interfaces and metal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「總電阻包含通道、源汲極、界面及金屬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Total resistance includes channel, source-drain, interfaces and metal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「通道與存取路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate channel and access paths and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「通道與存取路徑」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate channel and access paths: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-02-k1","title":"通道與存取路徑的原理","titleEn":"Separate channel and access paths principle","text":"總電阻包含通道、源汲極、界面及金屬。","textEn":"Total resistance includes channel, source-drain, interfaces and metal."},{"id":"a029-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「通道與存取路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate channel and access paths?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","總電阻包含通道、源汲極、界面及金屬。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Total resistance includes channel, source-drain, interfaces and metal.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總電阻包含通道、源汲極、界面及金屬。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Total resistance includes channel, source-drain, interfaces and metal. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}},{"id":"a029-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-02"],"title":"電流擁擠","titleEn":"Draw current crowding","objective":"完成「電流擁擠」的敏感度草圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for draw current crowding, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電流擁擠。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：電流未必均勻穿過整個幾何接觸面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw current crowding. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Current need not cross the geometric contact area uniformly. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電流未必均勻穿過整個幾何接觸面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Current need not cross the geometric contact area uniformly. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「電流擁擠」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw current crowding and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電流擁擠」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for draw current crowding: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-03-k1","title":"電流擁擠的原理","titleEn":"Draw current crowding principle","text":"電流未必均勻穿過整個幾何接觸面積。","textEn":"Current need not cross the geometric contact area uniformly."},{"id":"a029-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電流擁擠」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw current crowding?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","電流未必均勻穿過整個幾何接觸面積。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Current need not cross the geometric contact area uniformly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電流未必均勻穿過整個幾何接觸面積。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Current need not cross the geometric contact area uniformly. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}},{"id":"a029-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-03"],"title":"傳輸長度","titleEn":"Interpret transfer length","objective":"完成「傳輸長度」的故障判別表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for interpret transfer length, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：傳輸長度。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：接觸長度超過傳輸長度後收益可能減弱。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret transfer length. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Benefits can diminish when contact length exceeds transfer length. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸長度超過傳輸長度後收益可能減弱。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Benefits can diminish when contact length exceeds transfer length. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「傳輸長度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret transfer length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「傳輸長度」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for interpret transfer length: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-04-k1","title":"傳輸長度的原理","titleEn":"Interpret transfer length principle","text":"接觸長度超過傳輸長度後收益可能減弱。","textEn":"Benefits can diminish when contact length exceeds transfer length."},{"id":"a029-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「傳輸長度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret transfer length?","options":["接觸長度超過傳輸長度後收益可能減弱。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Benefits can diminish when contact length exceeds transfer length.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸長度超過傳輸長度後收益可能減弱。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Benefits can diminish when contact length exceeds transfer length. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}},{"id":"a029-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-04"],"title":"接觸能障","titleEn":"Draw contact barriers","objective":"完成「接觸能障」的量測規劃，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for draw contact barriers, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸能障。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：能障高度與穿隧機制共同影響接觸電性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw contact barriers. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Barrier height and tunneling jointly affect contact behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「能障高度與穿隧機制共同影響接觸電性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Barrier height and tunneling jointly affect contact behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「接觸能障」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw contact barriers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸能障」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for draw contact barriers: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-05-k1","title":"接觸能障的原理","titleEn":"Draw contact barriers principle","text":"能障高度與穿隧機制共同影響接觸電性。","textEn":"Barrier height and tunneling jointly affect contact behavior."},{"id":"a029-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸能障」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw contact barriers?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","能障高度與穿隧機制共同影響接觸電性。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Barrier height and tunneling jointly affect contact behavior.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"能障高度與穿隧機制共同影響接觸電性。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Barrier height and tunneling jointly affect contact behavior. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}},{"id":"a029-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-05"],"title":"公平基準","titleEn":"Choose comparison baselines","objective":"完成「公平基準」的工程驗收單，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for choose comparison baselines, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：公平基準。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：比較需使用相同面積定義與摻雜狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose comparison baselines. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Comparisons need matching area definitions and doping conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較需使用相同面積定義與摻雜狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Comparisons need matching area definitions and doping conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「公平基準」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose comparison baselines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「公平基準」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for choose comparison baselines: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-06-k1","title":"公平基準的原理","titleEn":"Choose comparison baselines principle","text":"比較需使用相同面積定義與摻雜狀態。","textEn":"Comparisons need matching area definitions and doping conditions."},{"id":"a029-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","textEn":"Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「公平基準」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose comparison baselines?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","比較需使用相同面積定義與摻雜狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Comparisons need matching area definitions and doping conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較需使用相同面積定義與摻雜狀態。 接觸電流可集中在入口附近，傳輸長度將片電阻與界面電阻相連，幾何面積不一定全都有效。","explanationEn":"Comparisons need matching area definitions and doping conditions. Contact current can crowd near edges; transfer length connects sheet and interface resistance, so not all geometric area is effective."}}]},{"id":"a029-stage02","order":2,"title":"界面與摻雜","titleEn":"Interface and doping","description":"在「界面與摻雜」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for interface and doping, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a029-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-06"],"title":"表面氧化殘留","titleEn":"Assess residual oxide","objective":"完成「表面氧化殘留」的因果圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess residual oxide, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面氧化殘留。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：薄殘留層也可能顯著增加界面電阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess residual oxide. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Even thin residual layers can significantly increase interface resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「薄殘留層也可能顯著增加界面電阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Even thin residual layers can significantly increase interface resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「表面氧化殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess residual oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面氧化殘留」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess residual oxide: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-07-k1","title":"表面氧化殘留的原理","titleEn":"Assess residual oxide principle","text":"薄殘留層也可能顯著增加界面電阻。","textEn":"Even thin residual layers can significantly increase interface resistance."},{"id":"a029-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面氧化殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess residual oxide?","options":["薄殘留層也可能顯著增加界面電阻。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Even thin residual layers can significantly increase interface resistance.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄殘留層也可能顯著增加界面電阻。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"Even thin residual layers can significantly increase interface resistance. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}},{"id":"a029-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-07"],"title":"活化載子","titleEn":"Measure active carriers","objective":"完成「活化載子」的對照表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure active carriers, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化載子。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：高化學濃度不保證高活化載子濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure active carriers. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: High chemical doping does not guarantee high active carrier density. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高化學濃度不保證高活化載子濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High chemical doping does not guarantee high active carrier density. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「活化載子」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure active carriers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化載子」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure active carriers: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-08-k1","title":"活化載子的原理","titleEn":"Measure active carriers principle","text":"高化學濃度不保證高活化載子濃度。","textEn":"High chemical doping does not guarantee high active carrier density."},{"id":"a029-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化載子」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure active carriers?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","高化學濃度不保證高活化載子濃度。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","High chemical doping does not guarantee high active carrier density.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高化學濃度不保證高活化載子濃度。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"High chemical doping does not guarantee high active carrier density. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}},{"id":"a029-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-08"],"title":"界面反應相","titleEn":"Inspect reacted phases","objective":"完成「界面反應相」的敏感度草圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect reacted phases, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面反應相。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：反應後相組成會改變電阻與材料消耗。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect reacted phases. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Reacted phases alter resistance and material consumption. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應後相組成會改變電阻與材料消耗。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reacted phases alter resistance and material consumption. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「界面反應相」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect reacted phases and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面反應相」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect reacted phases: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-09-k1","title":"界面反應相的原理","titleEn":"Inspect reacted phases principle","text":"反應後相組成會改變電阻與材料消耗。","textEn":"Reacted phases alter resistance and material consumption."},{"id":"a029-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面反應相」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect reacted phases?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","反應後相組成會改變電阻與材料消耗。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Reacted phases alter resistance and material consumption."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應後相組成會改變電阻與材料消耗。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"Reacted phases alter resistance and material consumption. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}},{"id":"a029-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-09"],"title":"金屬選擇","titleEn":"Compare contact metals","objective":"完成「金屬選擇」的故障判別表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare contact metals, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬選擇。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：低塊材電阻率不保證低半導體接觸電阻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare contact metals. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Low bulk metal resistivity does not ensure low semiconductor contact resistance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低塊材電阻率不保證低半導體接觸電阻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low bulk metal resistivity does not ensure low semiconductor contact resistance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「金屬選擇」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare contact metals and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬選擇」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare contact metals: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-10-k1","title":"金屬選擇的原理","titleEn":"Compare contact metals principle","text":"低塊材電阻率不保證低半導體接觸電阻。","textEn":"Low bulk metal resistivity does not ensure low semiconductor contact resistance."},{"id":"a029-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬選擇」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare contact metals?","options":["低塊材電阻率不保證低半導體接觸電阻。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk metal resistivity does not ensure low semiconductor contact resistance.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低塊材電阻率不保證低半導體接觸電阻。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"Low bulk metal resistivity does not ensure low semiconductor contact resistance. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}},{"id":"a029-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-10"],"title":"界面清潔等待","titleEn":"Track clean-to-metal delay","objective":"完成「界面清潔等待」的量測規劃，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track clean-to-metal delay, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面清潔等待。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：清潔後再氧化會改變接觸前的界面狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track clean-to-metal delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Reoxidation after cleaning changes the pre-metal interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清潔後再氧化會改變接觸前的界面狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reoxidation after cleaning changes the pre-metal interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「界面清潔等待」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track clean-to-metal delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面清潔等待」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track clean-to-metal delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-11-k1","title":"界面清潔等待的原理","titleEn":"Track clean-to-metal delay principle","text":"清潔後再氧化會改變接觸前的界面狀態。","textEn":"Reoxidation after cleaning changes the pre-metal interface."},{"id":"a029-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面清潔等待」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track clean-to-metal delay?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","清潔後再氧化會改變接觸前的界面狀態。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Reoxidation after cleaning changes the pre-metal interface.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔後再氧化會改變接觸前的界面狀態。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"Reoxidation after cleaning changes the pre-metal interface. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}},{"id":"a029-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-11"],"title":"退火窗口","titleEn":"Assess contact annealing","objective":"完成「退火窗口」的工程驗收單，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess contact annealing, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：退火窗口。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：接觸改善需與擴散、粗糙化及相變權衡。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess contact annealing. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Contact improvement must be balanced against diffusion, roughening and phase changes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸改善需與擴散、粗糙化及相變權衡。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contact improvement must be balanced against diffusion, roughening and phase changes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「退火窗口」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess contact annealing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「退火窗口」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess contact annealing: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-12-k1","title":"退火窗口的原理","titleEn":"Assess contact annealing principle","text":"接觸改善需與擴散、粗糙化及相變權衡。","textEn":"Contact improvement must be balanced against diffusion, roughening and phase changes."},{"id":"a029-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","textEn":"High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「退火窗口」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess contact annealing?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","接觸改善需與擴散、粗糙化及相變權衡。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Contact improvement must be balanced against diffusion, roughening and phase changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸改善需與擴散、粗糙化及相變權衡。 高活化濃度可縮窄能障，但界面氧化、反應相與粗糙度仍可能主導接觸傳輸。","explanationEn":"Contact improvement must be balanced against diffusion, roughening and phase changes. High active doping can narrow barriers while oxide, reacted phases and roughness can still dominate transport."}}]},{"id":"a029-stage03","order":3,"title":"幾何及量測","titleEn":"Geometry and measurement","description":"在「幾何及量測」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for geometry and measurement, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a029-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-12"],"title":"TLM 長度陣列","titleEn":"Lay out a TLM array","objective":"完成「TLM 長度陣列」的因果圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for lay out a tlm array, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：TLM 長度陣列。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：不同間距的電阻斜率與截距提供不同資訊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂長接觸 TLM：總電阻對間距的直線截距為 20 Ω。於兩接觸相同且寄生已去除假設下，求單接觸電阻；說明未有寬度與片電阻時不能直接得到比接觸電阻。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Lay out a TLM array. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Resistance slope and intercept across spacings provide different information. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical long-contact TLM: resistance-versus-spacing intercept is 20 Ω. With equal contacts and removed parasitics, find one contact resistance; explain why width and sheet resistance are still needed for specific contact resistivity.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同間距的電阻斜率與截距提供不同資訊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Resistance slope and intercept across spacings provide different information. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「TLM 長度陣列」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for lay out a tlm array and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「TLM 長度陣列」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for lay out a tlm array: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-13-k1","title":"TLM 長度陣列的原理","titleEn":"Lay out a TLM array principle","text":"不同間距的電阻斜率與截距提供不同資訊。","textEn":"Resistance slope and intercept across spacings provide different information."},{"id":"a029-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「TLM 長度陣列」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating lay out a tlm array?","options":["不同間距的電阻斜率與截距提供不同資訊。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Resistance slope and intercept across spacings provide different information.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同間距的電阻斜率與截距提供不同資訊。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Resistance slope and intercept across spacings provide different information. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}},{"id":"a029-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-13"],"title":"四端 Kelvin","titleEn":"Design Kelvin measurements","objective":"完成「四端 Kelvin」的對照表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for design kelvin measurements, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：四端 Kelvin。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：四端配置可降低探針及引線電阻干擾。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design Kelvin measurements. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Four-terminal configurations reduce probe and lead resistance influence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「四端配置可降低探針及引線電阻干擾。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Four-terminal configurations reduce probe and lead resistance influence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「四端 Kelvin」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design kelvin measurements and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「四端 Kelvin」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for design kelvin measurements: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-14-k1","title":"四端 Kelvin的原理","titleEn":"Design Kelvin measurements principle","text":"四端配置可降低探針及引線電阻干擾。","textEn":"Four-terminal configurations reduce probe and lead resistance influence."},{"id":"a029-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「四端 Kelvin」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design kelvin measurements?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","四端配置可降低探針及引線電阻干擾。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Four-terminal configurations reduce probe and lead resistance influence.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"四端配置可降低探針及引線電阻干擾。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Four-terminal configurations reduce probe and lead resistance influence. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}},{"id":"a029-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-14"],"title":"CTLM 幾何修正","titleEn":"Inspect circular TLM geometry","objective":"完成「CTLM 幾何修正」的敏感度草圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect circular tlm geometry, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：CTLM 幾何修正。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：圓形電流展開不能直接套用直線幾何公式。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect circular TLM geometry. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Radial current spreading needs geometry-specific treatment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「圓形電流展開不能直接套用直線幾何公式。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Radial current spreading needs geometry-specific treatment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「CTLM 幾何修正」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect circular tlm geometry and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「CTLM 幾何修正」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect circular tlm geometry: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-15-k1","title":"CTLM 幾何修正的原理","titleEn":"Inspect circular TLM geometry principle","text":"圓形電流展開不能直接套用直線幾何公式。","textEn":"Radial current spreading needs geometry-specific treatment."},{"id":"a029-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「CTLM 幾何修正」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect circular tlm geometry?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","圓形電流展開不能直接套用直線幾何公式。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Radial current spreading needs geometry-specific treatment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圓形電流展開不能直接套用直線幾何公式。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Radial current spreading needs geometry-specific treatment. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}},{"id":"a029-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-15"],"title":"面積抽取誤差","titleEn":"Propagate area error","objective":"完成「面積抽取誤差」的故障判別表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for propagate area error, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：面積抽取誤差。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：面積誤差可直接污染比接觸電阻判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Propagate area error. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Area errors directly affect extracted specific contact resistivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「面積誤差可直接污染比接觸電阻判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Area errors directly affect extracted specific contact resistivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「面積抽取誤差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for propagate area error and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「面積抽取誤差」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for propagate area error: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-16-k1","title":"面積抽取誤差的原理","titleEn":"Propagate area error principle","text":"面積誤差可直接污染比接觸電阻判讀。","textEn":"Area errors directly affect extracted specific contact resistivity."},{"id":"a029-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「面積抽取誤差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating propagate area error?","options":["面積誤差可直接污染比接觸電阻判讀。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Area errors directly affect extracted specific contact resistivity.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面積誤差可直接污染比接觸電阻判讀。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Area errors directly affect extracted specific contact resistivity. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}},{"id":"a029-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-16"],"title":"邊緣與側壁","titleEn":"Include sidewall contacts","objective":"完成「邊緣與側壁」的量測規劃，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for include sidewall contacts, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊緣與側壁。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：環繞接觸的有效面積不只頂面投影。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include sidewall contacts. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Wraparound contact area exceeds top-view projection alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「環繞接觸的有效面積不只頂面投影。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wraparound contact area exceeds top-view projection alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「邊緣與側壁」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include sidewall contacts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊緣與側壁」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for include sidewall contacts: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-17-k1","title":"邊緣與側壁的原理","titleEn":"Include sidewall contacts principle","text":"環繞接觸的有效面積不只頂面投影。","textEn":"Wraparound contact area exceeds top-view projection alone."},{"id":"a029-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊緣與側壁」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include sidewall contacts?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","環繞接觸的有效面積不只頂面投影。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Wraparound contact area exceeds top-view projection alone.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"環繞接觸的有效面積不只頂面投影。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Wraparound contact area exceeds top-view projection alone. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}},{"id":"a029-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-17"],"title":"低值量測極限","titleEn":"Assess low-resistance limits","objective":"完成「低值量測極限」的工程驗收單，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess low-resistance limits, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：低值量測極限。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：儀器零點及寄生可能主導極低電阻讀值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess low-resistance limits. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Offsets and parasitics can dominate very low resistance readings. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「儀器零點及寄生可能主導極低電阻讀值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Offsets and parasitics can dominate very low resistance readings. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「低值量測極限」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess low-resistance limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「低值量測極限」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess low-resistance limits: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-18-k1","title":"低值量測極限的原理","titleEn":"Assess low-resistance limits principle","text":"儀器零點及寄生可能主導極低電阻讀值。","textEn":"Offsets and parasitics can dominate very low resistance readings."},{"id":"a029-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","textEn":"TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「低值量測極限」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess low-resistance limits?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","儀器零點及寄生可能主導極低電阻讀值。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Offsets and parasitics can dominate very low resistance readings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"儀器零點及寄生可能主導極低電阻讀值。 TLM 的斜率與截距需在適當模型下分離片電阻及接觸貢獻，短接觸與有限幾何會改變抽取。","explanationEn":"Offsets and parasitics can dominate very low resistance readings. TLM slope and intercept separate sheet and contact contributions within an appropriate model; finite and short contacts affect extraction."}}]},{"id":"a029-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合及壽命","titleEn":"Integration and lifetime","description":"在「整合及壽命」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for integration and lifetime, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a029-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-18"],"title":"溫度依賴","titleEn":"Measure temperature dependence","objective":"完成「溫度依賴」的因果圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for measure temperature dependence, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度依賴。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：溫度趨勢可協助辨識不同傳輸機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure temperature dependence. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Temperature trends can help distinguish transport mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溫度趨勢可協助辨識不同傳輸機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Temperature trends can help distinguish transport mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「溫度依賴」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure temperature dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度依賴」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for measure temperature dependence: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-19-k1","title":"溫度依賴的原理","titleEn":"Measure temperature dependence principle","text":"溫度趨勢可協助辨識不同傳輸機制。","textEn":"Temperature trends can help distinguish transport mechanisms."},{"id":"a029-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度依賴」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure temperature dependence?","options":["溫度趨勢可協助辨識不同傳輸機制。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Temperature trends can help distinguish transport mechanisms.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"溫度趨勢可協助辨識不同傳輸機制。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"Temperature trends can help distinguish transport mechanisms. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}},{"id":"a029-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-19"],"title":"電流非線性","titleEn":"Inspect current nonlinearity","objective":"完成「電流非線性」的對照表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect current nonlinearity, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電流非線性。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：單點電阻可能掩蓋非歐姆接觸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect current nonlinearity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A single resistance value can hide non-ohmic behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單點電阻可能掩蓋非歐姆接觸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A single resistance value can hide non-ohmic behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「電流非線性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect current nonlinearity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電流非線性」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect current nonlinearity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-20-k1","title":"電流非線性的原理","titleEn":"Inspect current nonlinearity principle","text":"單點電阻可能掩蓋非歐姆接觸。","textEn":"A single resistance value can hide non-ohmic behavior."},{"id":"a029-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電流非線性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect current nonlinearity?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","單點電阻可能掩蓋非歐姆接觸。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","A single resistance value can hide non-ohmic behavior.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單點電阻可能掩蓋非歐姆接觸。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"A single resistance value can hide non-ohmic behavior. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}},{"id":"a029-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-20"],"title":"分布與尾端","titleEn":"Report distributions and tails","objective":"完成「分布與尾端」的敏感度草圖，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for report distributions and tails, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分布與尾端。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：少數高電阻接觸可能限制整體良率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report distributions and tails. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A small high-resistance tail can limit overall yield. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「少數高電阻接觸可能限制整體良率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A small high-resistance tail can limit overall yield. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「分布與尾端」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report distributions and tails and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分布與尾端」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for report distributions and tails: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-21-k1","title":"分布與尾端的原理","titleEn":"Report distributions and tails principle","text":"少數高電阻接觸可能限制整體良率。","textEn":"A small high-resistance tail can limit overall yield."},{"id":"a029-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分布與尾端」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report distributions and tails?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","少數高電阻接觸可能限制整體良率。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","A small high-resistance tail can limit overall yield."],"answer":2,"explanation":"少數高電阻接觸可能限制整體良率。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"A small high-resistance tail can limit overall yield. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}},{"id":"a029-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-21"],"title":"熱與電流老化","titleEn":"Assess thermal and current aging","objective":"完成「熱與電流老化」的故障判別表，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess thermal and current aging, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱與電流老化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：初始低阻不能替代長時間穩定性驗證。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermal and current aging. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Initially low resistance cannot replace long-term stability checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始低阻不能替代長時間穩定性驗證。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initially low resistance cannot replace long-term stability checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「熱與電流老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermal and current aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱與電流老化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess thermal and current aging: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-22-k1","title":"熱與電流老化的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermal and current aging principle","text":"初始低阻不能替代長時間穩定性驗證。","textEn":"Initially low resistance cannot replace long-term stability checks."},{"id":"a029-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱與電流老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermal and current aging?","options":["初始低阻不能替代長時間穩定性驗證。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Initially low resistance cannot replace long-term stability checks.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始低阻不能替代長時間穩定性驗證。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"Initially low resistance cannot replace long-term stability checks. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}},{"id":"a029-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-22"],"title":"元件效能歸因","titleEn":"Attribute device gains","objective":"完成「元件效能歸因」的量測規劃，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for attribute device gains, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：元件效能歸因。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：需把接觸改變與通道遷移率改變分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Attribute device gains. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Separate contact changes from channel-mobility changes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需把接觸改變與通道遷移率改變分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Separate contact changes from channel-mobility changes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「元件效能歸因」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for attribute device gains and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「元件效能歸因」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for attribute device gains: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-23-k1","title":"元件效能歸因的原理","titleEn":"Attribute device gains principle","text":"需把接觸改變與通道遷移率改變分開。","textEn":"Separate contact changes from channel-mobility changes."},{"id":"a029-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「元件效能歸因」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating attribute device gains?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","需把接觸改變與通道遷移率改變分開。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Separate contact changes from channel-mobility changes.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"需把接觸改變與通道遷移率改變分開。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"Separate contact changes from channel-mobility changes. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}},{"id":"a029-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-sige","v8a-scaling","v8a-epi"],"prerequisiteIds":["a029-v8-23"],"title":"接觸改善報告","titleEn":"Report contact improvement","objective":"完成「接觸改善報告」的工程驗收單，把活化、界面及比接觸電阻抽取中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for report contact improvement, connecting relevant limits in activation, interfaces and specific contact-resistivity extraction to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸改善報告。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：方法、幾何、活化、分布及可靠度都需可追溯。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report contact improvement. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Method, geometry, activation, distributions and reliability must be traceable. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「方法、幾何、活化、分布及可靠度都需可追溯。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Method, geometry, activation, distributions and reliability must be traceable. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「接觸改善報告」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report contact improvement and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸改善報告」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for report contact improvement: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a029-v8-24-k1","title":"接觸改善報告的原理","titleEn":"Report contact improvement principle","text":"方法、幾何、活化、分布及可靠度都需可追溯。","textEn":"Method, geometry, activation, distributions and reliability must be traceable."},{"id":"a029-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","textEn":"Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸改善報告」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report contact improvement?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","方法、幾何、活化、分布及可靠度都需可追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Method, geometry, activation, distributions and reliability must be traceable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"方法、幾何、活化、分布及可靠度都需可追溯。 低阻尾端與高阻尾端對統計的影響不同，報告中位數、分布及失效比例比只展示最低值更能描述批次。","explanationEn":"Method, geometry, activation, distributions and reliability must be traceable. Distribution tails matter differently; median, spread and failure fraction characterize a lot better than its minimum resistance alone."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a030","title":"自我對準接觸孔製程","titleEn":"Self-aligned contact processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["接觸與套刻","選擇性蝕刻","清潔及填充","電性與缺陷"],"labelsEn":["Contacts and overlay","Selective etching","Cleaning and fill","Electrical behavior and defects"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a030-stage01","order":1,"title":"接觸與套刻","titleEn":"Contacts and overlay","description":"在「接觸與套刻」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contacts and overlay, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a030-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"自對準的含義","titleEn":"Define self-alignment","objective":"完成「自對準的含義」的因果圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define self-alignment, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自對準的含義。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：自對準利用材料或結構邊界而非完全取消套刻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define self-alignment. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Self-alignment uses material or structural boundaries rather than eliminating overlay. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「自對準利用材料或結構邊界而非完全取消套刻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Self-alignment uses material or structural boundaries rather than eliminating overlay. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「自對準的含義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define self-alignment and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自對準的含義」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define self-alignment: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-01-k1","title":"自對準的含義的原理","titleEn":"Define self-alignment principle","text":"自對準利用材料或結構邊界而非完全取消套刻。","textEn":"Self-alignment uses material or structural boundaries rather than eliminating overlay."},{"id":"a030-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自對準的含義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define self-alignment?","options":["自對準利用材料或結構邊界而非完全取消套刻。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Self-alignment uses material or structural boundaries rather than eliminating overlay.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"自對準利用材料或結構邊界而非完全取消套刻。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"Self-alignment uses material or structural boundaries rather than eliminating overlay. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}},{"id":"a030-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-01"],"title":"接觸目標區","titleEn":"Mark contact targets","objective":"完成「接觸目標區」的對照表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for mark contact targets, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸目標區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：接觸需連到源汲極且避開閘金屬。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Mark contact targets. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Contacts must reach source-drain while avoiding gate metal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸需連到源汲極且避開閘金屬。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contacts must reach source-drain while avoiding gate metal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「接觸目標區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for mark contact targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸目標區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for mark contact targets: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-02-k1","title":"接觸目標區的原理","titleEn":"Mark contact targets principle","text":"接觸需連到源汲極且避開閘金屬。","textEn":"Contacts must reach source-drain while avoiding gate metal."},{"id":"a030-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸目標區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating mark contact targets?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","接觸需連到源汲極且避開閘金屬。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Contacts must reach source-drain while avoiding gate metal.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸需連到源汲極且避開閘金屬。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"Contacts must reach source-drain while avoiding gate metal. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}},{"id":"a030-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-02"],"title":"閘帽與間隔層","titleEn":"Assign caps and spacers","objective":"完成「閘帽與間隔層」的敏感度草圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assign caps and spacers, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘帽與間隔層。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：閘帽與間隔層共同提供蝕刻保護。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign caps and spacers. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Gate caps and spacers jointly provide etch protection. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘帽與間隔層共同提供蝕刻保護。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate caps and spacers jointly provide etch protection. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘帽與間隔層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign caps and spacers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘帽與間隔層」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assign caps and spacers: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-03-k1","title":"閘帽與間隔層的原理","titleEn":"Assign caps and spacers principle","text":"閘帽與間隔層共同提供蝕刻保護。","textEn":"Gate caps and spacers jointly provide etch protection."},{"id":"a030-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘帽與間隔層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign caps and spacers?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","閘帽與間隔層共同提供蝕刻保護。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Gate caps and spacers jointly provide etch protection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閘帽與間隔層共同提供蝕刻保護。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"Gate caps and spacers jointly provide etch protection. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}},{"id":"a030-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-03"],"title":"套刻容忍圖","titleEn":"Draw overlay-tolerance maps","objective":"完成「套刻容忍圖」的故障判別表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for draw overlay-tolerance maps, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：套刻容忍圖。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：幾何容忍需同時計入孔寬與保護層剩餘量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂一維落點：目標區寬 40、孔寬 20 單位；先求完全落入的中心偏移上限，再討論為何選擇性保護只能改變部分失效邊界。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw overlay-tolerance maps. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Tolerance includes opening width and remaining protective material. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical 1D landing: target width 40 and opening width 20 units. Find the center-offset limit for full landing, then explain why selective protection changes only some failure boundaries.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何容忍需同時計入孔寬與保護層剩餘量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Tolerance includes opening width and remaining protective material. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「套刻容忍圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw overlay-tolerance maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「套刻容忍圖」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for draw overlay-tolerance maps: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-04-k1","title":"套刻容忍圖的原理","titleEn":"Draw overlay-tolerance maps principle","text":"幾何容忍需同時計入孔寬與保護層剩餘量。","textEn":"Tolerance includes opening width and remaining protective material."},{"id":"a030-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「套刻容忍圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw overlay-tolerance maps?","options":["幾何容忍需同時計入孔寬與保護層剩餘量。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Tolerance includes opening width and remaining protective material.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何容忍需同時計入孔寬與保護層剩餘量。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"Tolerance includes opening width and remaining protective material. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}},{"id":"a030-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-04"],"title":"縱橫比","titleEn":"Assess aspect ratio","objective":"完成「縱橫比」的量測規劃，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess aspect ratio, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：縱橫比。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：深窄孔的傳輸與底部去除不同於平面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess aspect ratio. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Transport and bottom removal in deep holes differ from planar surfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「深窄孔的傳輸與底部去除不同於平面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Transport and bottom removal in deep holes differ from planar surfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「縱橫比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess aspect ratio and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「縱橫比」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess aspect ratio: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-05-k1","title":"縱橫比的原理","titleEn":"Assess aspect ratio principle","text":"深窄孔的傳輸與底部去除不同於平面。","textEn":"Transport and bottom removal in deep holes differ from planar surfaces."},{"id":"a030-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「縱橫比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess aspect ratio?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","深窄孔的傳輸與底部去除不同於平面。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Transport and bottom removal in deep holes differ from planar surfaces.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深窄孔的傳輸與底部去除不同於平面。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"Transport and bottom removal in deep holes differ from planar surfaces. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}},{"id":"a030-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-05"],"title":"材料選擇比","titleEn":"Define material selectivity","objective":"完成「材料選擇比」的工程驗收單，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for define material selectivity, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：材料選擇比。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：高選擇比仍需知道保護層可接受損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define material selectivity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: High selectivity still requires an allowable protection-layer loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高選擇比仍需知道保護層可接受損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High selectivity still requires an allowable protection-layer loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「材料選擇比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define material selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「材料選擇比」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for define material selectivity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-06-k1","title":"材料選擇比的原理","titleEn":"Define material selectivity principle","text":"高選擇比仍需知道保護層可接受損失。","textEn":"High selectivity still requires an allowable protection-layer loss."},{"id":"a030-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","textEn":"Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「材料選擇比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define material selectivity?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","高選擇比仍需知道保護層可接受損失。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","High selectivity still requires an allowable protection-layer loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高選擇比仍需知道保護層可接受損失。 自對準保護來自材料選擇性及結構重疊，套刻偏移仍可能縮小落點或增加角落暴露。","explanationEn":"High selectivity still requires an allowable protection-layer loss. Self-alignment relies on material selectivity and overlap; overlay shifts can still reduce landing area or expose corners."}}]},{"id":"a030-stage02","order":2,"title":"選擇性蝕刻","titleEn":"Selective etching","description":"在「選擇性蝕刻」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for selective etching, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a030-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-06"],"title":"離子方向性","titleEn":"Assess ion directionality","objective":"完成「離子方向性」的因果圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess ion directionality, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離子方向性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：方向性有助向下去除但仍可能傷害角落。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess ion directionality. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Directionality helps downward removal but can still damage corners. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「方向性有助向下去除但仍可能傷害角落。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Directionality helps downward removal but can still damage corners. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「離子方向性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess ion directionality and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離子方向性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess ion directionality: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-07-k1","title":"離子方向性的原理","titleEn":"Assess ion directionality principle","text":"方向性有助向下去除但仍可能傷害角落。","textEn":"Directionality helps downward removal but can still damage corners."},{"id":"a030-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離子方向性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess ion directionality?","options":["方向性有助向下去除但仍可能傷害角落。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Directionality helps downward removal but can still damage corners.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向性有助向下去除但仍可能傷害角落。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"Directionality helps downward removal but can still damage corners. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}},{"id":"a030-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-07"],"title":"原子層蝕刻循環","titleEn":"Decompose an ALE cycle","objective":"完成「原子層蝕刻循環」的對照表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for decompose an ale cycle, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：原子層蝕刻循環。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：表面改質與移除需作為分開的作用理解。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Decompose an ALE cycle. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Surface modification and removal are distinct operations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面改質與移除需作為分開的作用理解。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface modification and removal are distinct operations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「原子層蝕刻循環」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for decompose an ale cycle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「原子層蝕刻循環」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for decompose an ale cycle: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-08-k1","title":"原子層蝕刻循環的原理","titleEn":"Decompose an ALE cycle principle","text":"表面改質與移除需作為分開的作用理解。","textEn":"Surface modification and removal are distinct operations."},{"id":"a030-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「原子層蝕刻循環」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating decompose an ale cycle?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","表面改質與移除需作為分開的作用理解。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Surface modification and removal are distinct operations.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面改質與移除需作為分開的作用理解。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"Surface modification and removal are distinct operations. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}},{"id":"a030-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-08"],"title":"底部殘留","titleEn":"Inspect bottom residue","objective":"完成「底部殘留」的敏感度草圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect bottom residue, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部殘留。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：孔已打開不代表接觸界面完全清潔。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect bottom residue. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: An open hole does not prove a clean contact interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「孔已打開不代表接觸界面完全清潔。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An open hole does not prove a clean contact interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「底部殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect bottom residue and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部殘留」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect bottom residue: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-09-k1","title":"底部殘留的原理","titleEn":"Inspect bottom residue principle","text":"孔已打開不代表接觸界面完全清潔。","textEn":"An open hole does not prove a clean contact interface."},{"id":"a030-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect bottom residue?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","孔已打開不代表接觸界面完全清潔。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","An open hole does not prove a clean contact interface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔已打開不代表接觸界面完全清潔。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"An open hole does not prove a clean contact interface. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}},{"id":"a030-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-09"],"title":"角落保護","titleEn":"Measure corner loss","objective":"完成「角落保護」的故障判別表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for measure corner loss, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：角落保護。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：平均間隔厚度不能代表最薄角落。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure corner loss. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Mean spacer thickness does not represent the thinnest corner. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均間隔厚度不能代表最薄角落。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean spacer thickness does not represent the thinnest corner. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「角落保護」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure corner loss and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「角落保護」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for measure corner loss: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-10-k1","title":"角落保護的原理","titleEn":"Measure corner loss principle","text":"平均間隔厚度不能代表最薄角落。","textEn":"Mean spacer thickness does not represent the thinnest corner."},{"id":"a030-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「角落保護」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure corner loss?","options":["平均間隔厚度不能代表最薄角落。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Mean spacer thickness does not represent the thinnest corner.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均間隔厚度不能代表最薄角落。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"Mean spacer thickness does not represent the thinnest corner. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}},{"id":"a030-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-10"],"title":"微負載","titleEn":"Compare microloading","objective":"完成「微負載」的量測規劃，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for compare microloading, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：微負載。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同孔密度及尺寸可能有不同清除時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare microloading. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Hole density and size can cause different clearing times. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同孔密度及尺寸可能有不同清除時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Hole density and size can cause different clearing times. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「微負載」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare microloading and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「微負載」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for compare microloading: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-11-k1","title":"微負載的原理","titleEn":"Compare microloading principle","text":"不同孔密度及尺寸可能有不同清除時間。","textEn":"Hole density and size can cause different clearing times."},{"id":"a030-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「微負載」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare microloading?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","不同孔密度及尺寸可能有不同清除時間。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Hole density and size can cause different clearing times.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同孔密度及尺寸可能有不同清除時間。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"Hole density and size can cause different clearing times. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}},{"id":"a030-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-11"],"title":"終點與過蝕","titleEn":"Separate endpoint and overetch","objective":"完成「終點與過蝕」的工程驗收單，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for separate endpoint and overetch, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：終點與過蝕。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：最慢孔清除所需過蝕會消耗其他位置保護層。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate endpoint and overetch. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Overetch for slow holes consumes protection elsewhere. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「最慢孔清除所需過蝕會消耗其他位置保護層。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Overetch for slow holes consumes protection elsewhere. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「終點與過蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate endpoint and overetch and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「終點與過蝕」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for separate endpoint and overetch: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-12-k1","title":"終點與過蝕的原理","titleEn":"Separate endpoint and overetch principle","text":"最慢孔清除所需過蝕會消耗其他位置保護層。","textEn":"Overetch for slow holes consumes protection elsewhere."},{"id":"a030-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","textEn":"Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「終點與過蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate endpoint and overetch?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","最慢孔清除所需過蝕會消耗其他位置保護層。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Overetch for slow holes consumes protection elsewhere."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最慢孔清除所需過蝕會消耗其他位置保護層。 方向性蝕刻控制形狀，材料選擇性控制保護層損失，兩種能力需要分開量化。","explanationEn":"Overetch for slow holes consumes protection elsewhere. Directional etching controls shape while selectivity controls protective-layer loss; quantify these capabilities separately."}}]},{"id":"a030-stage03","order":3,"title":"清潔及填充","titleEn":"Cleaning and fill","description":"在「清潔及填充」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cleaning and fill, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a030-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-12"],"title":"蝕刻後殘留","titleEn":"Classify post-etch residues","objective":"完成「蝕刻後殘留」的因果圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for classify post-etch residues, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：蝕刻後殘留。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：聚合物與金屬殘留可能需要不同判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify post-etch residues. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Polymer and metal residues need different interpretation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「聚合物與金屬殘留可能需要不同判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Polymer and metal residues need different interpretation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「蝕刻後殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify post-etch residues and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「蝕刻後殘留」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for classify post-etch residues: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-13-k1","title":"蝕刻後殘留的原理","titleEn":"Classify post-etch residues principle","text":"聚合物與金屬殘留可能需要不同判讀。","textEn":"Polymer and metal residues need different interpretation."},{"id":"a030-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「蝕刻後殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify post-etch residues?","options":["聚合物與金屬殘留可能需要不同判讀。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Polymer and metal residues need different interpretation.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"聚合物與金屬殘留可能需要不同判讀。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Polymer and metal residues need different interpretation. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}},{"id":"a030-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-13"],"title":"源汲極損失","titleEn":"Measure source-drain loss","objective":"完成「源汲極損失」的對照表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure source-drain loss, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：源汲極損失。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：底部清潔不能以過度消耗目標材料為代價。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure source-drain loss. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Bottom cleaning must not excessively consume target material. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「底部清潔不能以過度消耗目標材料為代價。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bottom cleaning must not excessively consume target material. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「源汲極損失」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure source-drain loss and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「源汲極損失」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure source-drain loss: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-14-k1","title":"源汲極損失的原理","titleEn":"Measure source-drain loss principle","text":"底部清潔不能以過度消耗目標材料為代價。","textEn":"Bottom cleaning must not excessively consume target material."},{"id":"a030-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「源汲極損失」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure source-drain loss?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","底部清潔不能以過度消耗目標材料為代價。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Bottom cleaning must not excessively consume target material.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"底部清潔不能以過度消耗目標材料為代價。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Bottom cleaning must not excessively consume target material. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}},{"id":"a030-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-14"],"title":"襯層厚度預算","titleEn":"Budget liner thickness","objective":"完成「襯層厚度預算」的敏感度草圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget liner thickness, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：襯層厚度預算。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：襯層會消耗孔內可用導體截面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget liner thickness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Liners consume available conductor cross-section. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「襯層會消耗孔內可用導體截面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Liners consume available conductor cross-section. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「襯層厚度預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget liner thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「襯層厚度預算」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget liner thickness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-15-k1","title":"襯層厚度預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget liner thickness principle","text":"襯層會消耗孔內可用導體截面。","textEn":"Liners consume available conductor cross-section."},{"id":"a030-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「襯層厚度預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget liner thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","襯層會消耗孔內可用導體截面。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Liners consume available conductor cross-section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"襯層會消耗孔內可用導體截面。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Liners consume available conductor cross-section. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}},{"id":"a030-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-15"],"title":"接觸填充","titleEn":"Inspect contact fill","objective":"完成「接觸填充」的故障判別表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect contact fill, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸填充。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：早期封口可留下中空接觸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect contact fill. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Premature closure can leave hollow contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「早期封口可留下中空接觸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Premature closure can leave hollow contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「接觸填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect contact fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸填充」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect contact fill: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-16-k1","title":"接觸填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect contact fill principle","text":"早期封口可留下中空接觸。","textEn":"Premature closure can leave hollow contacts."},{"id":"a030-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect contact fill?","options":["早期封口可留下中空接觸。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Premature closure can leave hollow contacts.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"早期封口可留下中空接觸。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Premature closure can leave hollow contacts. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}},{"id":"a030-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-16"],"title":"平坦化隔離","titleEn":"Assess planarization isolation","objective":"完成「平坦化隔離」的量測規劃，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess planarization isolation, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：平坦化隔離。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：表面殘金屬可能連接原本分開的接觸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess planarization isolation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Residual surface metal can bridge separate contacts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面殘金屬可能連接原本分開的接觸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual surface metal can bridge separate contacts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「平坦化隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess planarization isolation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「平坦化隔離」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess planarization isolation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-17-k1","title":"平坦化隔離的原理","titleEn":"Assess planarization isolation principle","text":"表面殘金屬可能連接原本分開的接觸。","textEn":"Residual surface metal can bridge separate contacts."},{"id":"a030-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「平坦化隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess planarization isolation?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","表面殘金屬可能連接原本分開的接觸。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Residual surface metal can bridge separate contacts.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面殘金屬可能連接原本分開的接觸。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Residual surface metal can bridge separate contacts. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}},{"id":"a030-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-17"],"title":"阻障完整性","titleEn":"Assess barrier continuity","objective":"完成「阻障完整性」的工程驗收單，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess barrier continuity, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：阻障完整性。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：低電阻填充仍需防止材料向鄰近區擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess barrier continuity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Low-resistance fill still needs diffusion containment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低電阻填充仍需防止材料向鄰近區擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low-resistance fill still needs diffusion containment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「阻障完整性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess barrier continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「阻障完整性」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess barrier continuity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-18-k1","title":"阻障完整性的原理","titleEn":"Assess barrier continuity principle","text":"低電阻填充仍需防止材料向鄰近區擴散。","textEn":"Low-resistance fill still needs diffusion containment."},{"id":"a030-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","textEn":"Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「阻障完整性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess barrier continuity?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","低電阻填充仍需防止材料向鄰近區擴散。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Low-resistance fill still needs diffusion containment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低電阻填充仍需防止材料向鄰近區擴散。 接觸襯層可保護界面卻消耗導體截面，填充完成後仍需檢查空洞與實際連通面積。","explanationEn":"Low-resistance fill still needs diffusion containment. Contact liners protect interfaces but consume conductor area; inspect voids and actual connected area after filling."}}]},{"id":"a030-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性與缺陷","titleEn":"Electrical behavior and defects","description":"在「電性與缺陷」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for electrical behavior and defects, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a030-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-18"],"title":"開路與高阻","titleEn":"Separate opens and high resistance","objective":"完成「開路與高阻」的因果圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate opens and high resistance, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：開路與高阻。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：完全開路與部分接觸不良需要不同診斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate opens and high resistance. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Complete opens and partial contact failure need different diagnosis. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「完全開路與部分接觸不良需要不同診斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Complete opens and partial contact failure need different diagnosis. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「開路與高阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate opens and high resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「開路與高阻」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate opens and high resistance: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-19-k1","title":"開路與高阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate opens and high resistance principle","text":"完全開路與部分接觸不良需要不同診斷。","textEn":"Complete opens and partial contact failure need different diagnosis."},{"id":"a030-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「開路與高阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate opens and high resistance?","options":["完全開路與部分接觸不良需要不同診斷。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Complete opens and partial contact failure need different diagnosis.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"完全開路與部分接觸不良需要不同診斷。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Complete opens and partial contact failure need different diagnosis. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}},{"id":"a030-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-19"],"title":"閘接觸短路","titleEn":"Test gate-contact shorts","objective":"完成「閘接觸短路」的對照表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for test gate-contact shorts, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘接觸短路。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：源汲極導通不代表與閘保持隔離。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Test gate-contact shorts. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Source-drain continuity does not prove gate isolation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「源汲極導通不代表與閘保持隔離。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Source-drain continuity does not prove gate isolation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閘接觸短路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for test gate-contact shorts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘接觸短路」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for test gate-contact shorts: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-20-k1","title":"閘接觸短路的原理","titleEn":"Test gate-contact shorts principle","text":"源汲極導通不代表與閘保持隔離。","textEn":"Source-drain continuity does not prove gate isolation."},{"id":"a030-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘接觸短路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating test gate-contact shorts?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","源汲極導通不代表與閘保持隔離。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Source-drain continuity does not prove gate isolation.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"源汲極導通不代表與閘保持隔離。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Source-drain continuity does not prove gate isolation. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}},{"id":"a030-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-20"],"title":"接觸鏈統計","titleEn":"Analyze contact-chain statistics","objective":"完成「接觸鏈統計」的敏感度草圖，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for analyze contact-chain statistics, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸鏈統計。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：長鏈失效機率與單接點良率相關。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze contact-chain statistics. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Chain failure probability depends on individual contact yield. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「長鏈失效機率與單接點良率相關。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chain failure probability depends on individual contact yield. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「接觸鏈統計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze contact-chain statistics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸鏈統計」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for analyze contact-chain statistics: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-21-k1","title":"接觸鏈統計的原理","titleEn":"Analyze contact-chain statistics principle","text":"長鏈失效機率與單接點良率相關。","textEn":"Chain failure probability depends on individual contact yield."},{"id":"a030-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸鏈統計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze contact-chain statistics?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","長鏈失效機率與單接點良率相關。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Chain failure probability depends on individual contact yield."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長鏈失效機率與單接點良率相關。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Chain failure probability depends on individual contact yield. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}},{"id":"a030-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-21"],"title":"截面與電性對照","titleEn":"Correlate sections and electrical data","objective":"完成「截面與電性對照」的故障判別表，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for correlate sections and electrical data, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：截面與電性對照。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：截面位置需與實際失效位置匹配。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Correlate sections and electrical data. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Cross-sections must match actual electrical failure locations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「截面位置需與實際失效位置匹配。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Cross-sections must match actual electrical failure locations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「截面與電性對照」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for correlate sections and electrical data and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「截面與電性對照」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for correlate sections and electrical data: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-22-k1","title":"截面與電性對照的原理","titleEn":"Correlate sections and electrical data principle","text":"截面位置需與實際失效位置匹配。","textEn":"Cross-sections must match actual electrical failure locations."},{"id":"a030-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「截面與電性對照」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating correlate sections and electrical data?","options":["截面位置需與實際失效位置匹配。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-sections must match actual electrical failure locations.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"截面位置需與實際失效位置匹配。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Cross-sections must match actual electrical failure locations. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}},{"id":"a030-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-22"],"title":"設計窗口","titleEn":"Build a design-process window","objective":"完成「設計窗口」的量測規劃，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for build a design-process window, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：設計窗口。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：孔寬、套刻及保護層損失需共同取交集。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a design-process window. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Opening width, overlay and protection loss define a joint window. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「孔寬、套刻及保護層損失需共同取交集。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Opening width, overlay and protection loss define a joint window. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「設計窗口」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a design-process window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「設計窗口」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for build a design-process window: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-23-k1","title":"設計窗口的原理","titleEn":"Build a design-process window principle","text":"孔寬、套刻及保護層損失需共同取交集。","textEn":"Opening width, overlay and protection loss define a joint window."},{"id":"a030-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「設計窗口」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a design-process window?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","孔寬、套刻及保護層損失需共同取交集。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Opening width, overlay and protection loss define a joint window.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔寬、套刻及保護層損失需共同取交集。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Opening width, overlay and protection loss define a joint window. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}},{"id":"a030-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ale","v8a-selective","v8a-sparc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a030-v8-23"],"title":"SAC 放行","titleEn":"Accept self-aligned contacts","objective":"完成「SAC 放行」的工程驗收單，把套刻容忍、間隔保護及接觸導通中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept self-aligned contacts, connecting relevant limits in overlay tolerance, spacer protection and contact continuity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SAC 放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：導通、隔離、填充及套刻裕度必須一起驗證。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept self-aligned contacts. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Continuity, isolation, fill and overlay margin need joint validation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「導通、隔離、填充及套刻裕度必須一起驗證。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Continuity, isolation, fill and overlay margin need joint validation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「SAC 放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept self-aligned contacts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SAC 放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept self-aligned contacts: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a030-v8-24-k1","title":"SAC 放行的原理","titleEn":"Accept self-aligned contacts principle","text":"導通、隔離、填充及套刻裕度必須一起驗證。","textEn":"Continuity, isolation, fill and overlay margin need joint validation."},{"id":"a030-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","textEn":"Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SAC 放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept self-aligned contacts?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","導通、隔離、填充及套刻裕度必須一起驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Continuity, isolation, fill and overlay margin need joint validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導通、隔離、填充及套刻裕度必須一起驗證。 導通、閘隔離及鄰孔隔離是不同電路條件；一種接觸鏈測試不能取代所有漏電與短路檢查。","explanationEn":"Continuity, isolation, fill and overlay margin need joint validation. Continuity, gate isolation and neighbor isolation are different conditions; one chain test cannot replace all leakage and short checks."}}]}],"subcategory":"devices","subcategoryTitle":"先進電晶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Advanced transistors"},{"id":"a031","title":"深紫外光阻塗佈","titleEn":"Deep-ultraviolet photoresist coating","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["光阻與基板","塗佈流動","缺陷及膜厚","曝光交接"],"labelsEn":["Resist and substrate","Coating flow","Defects and thickness","Exposure handoff"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a031-stage01","order":1,"title":"光阻與基板","titleEn":"Resist and substrate","description":"在「光阻與基板」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for resist and substrate, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a031-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"曝光波長匹配","titleEn":"Match exposure wavelength","objective":"完成「曝光波長匹配」的因果圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for match exposure wavelength, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：曝光波長匹配。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：DUV 光阻須以相應波長資料選擇，不能以外觀判斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Match exposure wavelength. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: DUV resist selection needs wavelength-specific data, not appearance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「DUV 光阻須以相應波長資料選擇，不能以外觀判斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: DUV resist selection needs wavelength-specific data, not appearance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「曝光波長匹配」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for match exposure wavelength and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「曝光波長匹配」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for match exposure wavelength: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-01-k1","title":"曝光波長匹配的原理","titleEn":"Match exposure wavelength principle","text":"DUV 光阻須以相應波長資料選擇，不能以外觀判斷。","textEn":"DUV resist selection needs wavelength-specific data, not appearance."},{"id":"a031-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「曝光波長匹配」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating match exposure wavelength?","options":["DUV 光阻須以相應波長資料選擇，不能以外觀判斷。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["DUV resist selection needs wavelength-specific data, not appearance.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"DUV 光阻須以相應波長資料選擇，不能以外觀判斷。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"DUV resist selection needs wavelength-specific data, not appearance. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-01"],"title":"樹脂溶劑分工","titleEn":"Separate resin and solvent","objective":"完成「樹脂溶劑分工」的對照表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate resin and solvent, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：樹脂溶劑分工。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：溶劑影響流動與乾燥，樹脂影響成膜及顯影。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate resin and solvent. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Solvent affects flow and drying; resin affects film formation and development. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶劑影響流動與乾燥，樹脂影響成膜及顯影。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Solvent affects flow and drying; resin affects film formation and development. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「樹脂溶劑分工」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate resin and solvent and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「樹脂溶劑分工」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate resin and solvent: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-02-k1","title":"樹脂溶劑分工的原理","titleEn":"Separate resin and solvent principle","text":"溶劑影響流動與乾燥，樹脂影響成膜及顯影。","textEn":"Solvent affects flow and drying; resin affects film formation and development."},{"id":"a031-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「樹脂溶劑分工」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate resin and solvent?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","溶劑影響流動與乾燥，樹脂影響成膜及顯影。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Solvent affects flow and drying; resin affects film formation and development.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶劑影響流動與乾燥，樹脂影響成膜及顯影。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"Solvent affects flow and drying; resin affects film formation and development. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-02"],"title":"黏度與固含量","titleEn":"Compare viscosity and solids","objective":"完成「黏度與固含量」的敏感度草圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare viscosity and solids, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：黏度與固含量。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：相同黏度不保證乾膜厚度相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare viscosity and solids. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Equal viscosity does not guarantee equal dry thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同黏度不保證乾膜厚度相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal viscosity does not guarantee equal dry thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「黏度與固含量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare viscosity and solids and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「黏度與固含量」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare viscosity and solids: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-03-k1","title":"黏度與固含量的原理","titleEn":"Compare viscosity and solids principle","text":"相同黏度不保證乾膜厚度相同。","textEn":"Equal viscosity does not guarantee equal dry thickness."},{"id":"a031-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「黏度與固含量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare viscosity and solids?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","相同黏度不保證乾膜厚度相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","Equal viscosity does not guarantee equal dry thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同黏度不保證乾膜厚度相同。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"Equal viscosity does not guarantee equal dry thickness. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-03"],"title":"基板濕潤性","titleEn":"Assess substrate wetting","objective":"完成「基板濕潤性」的故障判別表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess substrate wetting, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基板濕潤性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：表面能不匹配可能造成退潤與露底。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess substrate wetting. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Surface-energy mismatch can cause dewetting and bare patches. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面能不匹配可能造成退潤與露底。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface-energy mismatch can cause dewetting and bare patches. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「基板濕潤性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess substrate wetting and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基板濕潤性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess substrate wetting: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-04-k1","title":"基板濕潤性的原理","titleEn":"Assess substrate wetting principle","text":"表面能不匹配可能造成退潤與露底。","textEn":"Surface-energy mismatch can cause dewetting and bare patches."},{"id":"a031-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基板濕潤性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess substrate wetting?","options":["表面能不匹配可能造成退潤與露底。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Surface-energy mismatch can cause dewetting and bare patches.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面能不匹配可能造成退潤與露底。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"Surface-energy mismatch can cause dewetting and bare patches. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-04"],"title":"附著促進","titleEn":"Assess adhesion promotion","objective":"完成「附著促進」的量測規劃，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess adhesion promotion, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：附著促進。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：附著處理要與基板材料及光阻化學相容。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess adhesion promotion. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Adhesion treatment must match substrate and resist chemistry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「附著處理要與基板材料及光阻化學相容。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adhesion treatment must match substrate and resist chemistry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「附著促進」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess adhesion promotion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「附著促進」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess adhesion promotion: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-05-k1","title":"附著促進的原理","titleEn":"Assess adhesion promotion principle","text":"附著處理要與基板材料及光阻化學相容。","textEn":"Adhesion treatment must match substrate and resist chemistry."},{"id":"a031-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「附著促進」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess adhesion promotion?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","附著處理要與基板材料及光阻化學相容。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Adhesion treatment must match substrate and resist chemistry.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"附著處理要與基板材料及光阻化學相容。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"Adhesion treatment must match substrate and resist chemistry. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-05"],"title":"塗佈前溫度","titleEn":"Record precoat temperature","objective":"完成「塗佈前溫度」的工程驗收單，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for record precoat temperature, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：塗佈前溫度。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：材料溫度改變黏度與揮發。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Record precoat temperature. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Material temperature changes viscosity and evaporation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料溫度改變黏度與揮發。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Material temperature changes viscosity and evaporation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「塗佈前溫度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for record precoat temperature and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「塗佈前溫度」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for record precoat temperature: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-06-k1","title":"塗佈前溫度的原理","titleEn":"Record precoat temperature principle","text":"材料溫度改變黏度與揮發。","textEn":"Material temperature changes viscosity and evaporation."},{"id":"a031-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","textEn":"Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「塗佈前溫度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating record precoat temperature?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","材料溫度改變黏度與揮發。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","Material temperature changes viscosity and evaporation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料溫度改變黏度與揮發。 旋塗的流動受黏度、離心效應與溶劑揮發共同影響，材料換批後應重新確認曲線而非只沿用轉速。","explanationEn":"Material temperature changes viscosity and evaporation. Spin flow depends on viscosity, centrifugal effects and evaporation; a material-lot change requires curve verification beyond reusing speed."}}]},{"id":"a031-stage02","order":2,"title":"塗佈流動","titleEn":"Coating flow","description":"在「塗佈流動」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for coating flow, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a031-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-06"],"title":"滴液位置","titleEn":"Assess dispense position","objective":"完成「滴液位置」的因果圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess dispense position, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：滴液位置。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：偏心滴液可造成初始覆蓋不均。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess dispense position. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Off-center dispensing can cause uneven initial coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「偏心滴液可造成初始覆蓋不均。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Off-center dispensing can cause uneven initial coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「滴液位置」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess dispense position and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「滴液位置」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess dispense position: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-07-k1","title":"滴液位置的原理","titleEn":"Assess dispense position principle","text":"偏心滴液可造成初始覆蓋不均。","textEn":"Off-center dispensing can cause uneven initial coverage."},{"id":"a031-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「滴液位置」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess dispense position?","options":["偏心滴液可造成初始覆蓋不均。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Off-center dispensing can cause uneven initial coverage.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏心滴液可造成初始覆蓋不均。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"Off-center dispensing can cause uneven initial coverage. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-07"],"title":"靜態與動態滴液","titleEn":"Compare static and dynamic dispense","objective":"完成「靜態與動態滴液」的對照表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare static and dynamic dispense, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：靜態與動態滴液。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：兩種滴液方式改變鋪展與材料利用率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare static and dynamic dispense. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: The two dispense modes alter spreading and material utilization. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩種滴液方式改變鋪展與材料利用率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The two dispense modes alter spreading and material utilization. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「靜態與動態滴液」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare static and dynamic dispense and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「靜態與動態滴液」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare static and dynamic dispense: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-08-k1","title":"靜態與動態滴液的原理","titleEn":"Compare static and dynamic dispense principle","text":"兩種滴液方式改變鋪展與材料利用率。","textEn":"The two dispense modes alter spreading and material utilization."},{"id":"a031-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「靜態與動態滴液」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare static and dynamic dispense?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","兩種滴液方式改變鋪展與材料利用率。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","The two dispense modes alter spreading and material utilization.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩種滴液方式改變鋪展與材料利用率。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"The two dispense modes alter spreading and material utilization. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-08"],"title":"加速度歷程","titleEn":"Design acceleration comparisons","objective":"完成「加速度歷程」的敏感度草圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for design acceleration comparisons, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：加速度歷程。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：轉速終值相同不代表鋪展歷程相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design acceleration comparisons. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Equal final speed does not imply equal spreading history. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「轉速終值相同不代表鋪展歷程相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal final speed does not imply equal spreading history. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「加速度歷程」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design acceleration comparisons and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「加速度歷程」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for design acceleration comparisons: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-09-k1","title":"加速度歷程的原理","titleEn":"Design acceleration comparisons principle","text":"轉速終值相同不代表鋪展歷程相同。","textEn":"Equal final speed does not imply equal spreading history."},{"id":"a031-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「加速度歷程」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design acceleration comparisons?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","轉速終值相同不代表鋪展歷程相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Equal final speed does not imply equal spreading history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉速終值相同不代表鋪展歷程相同。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"Equal final speed does not imply equal spreading history. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-09"],"title":"旋轉與膜厚","titleEn":"Analyze spin-thickness trends","objective":"完成「旋轉與膜厚」的故障判別表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for analyze spin-thickness trends, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：旋轉與膜厚。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：經驗膜厚關係僅在指定材料與範圍內適用。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 僅作經驗模型練習：假設 h∝ω^-1/2；把轉速加倍，求相對膜厚，再列黏度、揮發及加速度改變時必須重新校準的原因。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze spin-thickness trends. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Empirical spin-thickness relations apply only within specified materials and ranges. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Empirical model exercise only: assume h∝ω^-1/2. Double speed and calculate relative thickness, then state why viscosity, evaporation and acceleration changes require recalibration.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「經驗膜厚關係僅在指定材料與範圍內適用。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Empirical spin-thickness relations apply only within specified materials and ranges. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「旋轉與膜厚」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze spin-thickness trends and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「旋轉與膜厚」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for analyze spin-thickness trends: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-10-k1","title":"旋轉與膜厚的原理","titleEn":"Analyze spin-thickness trends principle","text":"經驗膜厚關係僅在指定材料與範圍內適用。","textEn":"Empirical spin-thickness relations apply only within specified materials and ranges."},{"id":"a031-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「旋轉與膜厚」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze spin-thickness trends?","options":["經驗膜厚關係僅在指定材料與範圍內適用。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Empirical spin-thickness relations apply only within specified materials and ranges.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"經驗膜厚關係僅在指定材料與範圍內適用。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"Empirical spin-thickness relations apply only within specified materials and ranges. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-10"],"title":"揮發與排風","titleEn":"Assess evaporation and exhaust","objective":"完成「揮發與排風」的量測規劃，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess evaporation and exhaust, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：揮發與排風。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：氣流改變溶劑蒸發並可能形成徑向差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess evaporation and exhaust. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Airflow changes solvent evaporation and can produce radial differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氣流改變溶劑蒸發並可能形成徑向差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Airflow changes solvent evaporation and can produce radial differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「揮發與排風」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess evaporation and exhaust and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「揮發與排風」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess evaporation and exhaust: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-11-k1","title":"揮發與排風的原理","titleEn":"Assess evaporation and exhaust principle","text":"氣流改變溶劑蒸發並可能形成徑向差異。","textEn":"Airflow changes solvent evaporation and can produce radial differences."},{"id":"a031-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「揮發與排風」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess evaporation and exhaust?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","氣流改變溶劑蒸發並可能形成徑向差異。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","Airflow changes solvent evaporation and can produce radial differences.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣流改變溶劑蒸發並可能形成徑向差異。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"Airflow changes solvent evaporation and can produce radial differences. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}},{"id":"a031-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-11"],"title":"邊珠形成","titleEn":"Inspect edge-bead formation","objective":"完成「邊珠形成」的工程驗收單，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for inspect edge-bead formation, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊珠形成。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：邊緣厚膜會影響後續接觸、污染及曝光可用區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect edge-bead formation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Edge beads affect downstream contact, contamination and usable exposure area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊緣厚膜會影響後續接觸、污染及曝光可用區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Edge beads affect downstream contact, contamination and usable exposure area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「邊珠形成」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect edge-bead formation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊珠形成」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for inspect edge-bead formation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-12-k1","title":"邊珠形成的原理","titleEn":"Inspect edge-bead formation principle","text":"邊緣厚膜會影響後續接觸、污染及曝光可用區。","textEn":"Edge beads affect downstream contact, contamination and usable exposure area."},{"id":"a031-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","textEn":"The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊珠形成」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect edge-bead formation?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","邊緣厚膜會影響後續接觸、污染及曝光可用區。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Edge beads affect downstream contact, contamination and usable exposure area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣厚膜會影響後續接觸、污染及曝光可用區。 液膜在鋪展與乾燥間轉換，前段加速度及排風因此可能改變最終厚度，即使終轉速不變。","explanationEn":"Edge beads affect downstream contact, contamination and usable exposure area. The film transitions from spreading to drying, so acceleration and exhaust can alter final thickness even at fixed final speed."}}]},{"id":"a031-stage03","order":3,"title":"缺陷及膜厚","titleEn":"Defects and thickness","description":"在「缺陷及膜厚」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for defects and thickness, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a031-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-12"],"title":"邊珠去除","titleEn":"Define edge-bead removal evidence","objective":"完成「邊珠去除」的因果圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define edge-bead removal evidence, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊珠去除。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：去除寬度需兼顧邊緣潔淨與有效面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define edge-bead removal evidence. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Removal width balances edge cleanliness and usable area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去除寬度需兼顧邊緣潔淨與有效面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removal width balances edge cleanliness and usable area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「邊珠去除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define edge-bead removal evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊珠去除」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define edge-bead removal evidence: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-13-k1","title":"邊珠去除的原理","titleEn":"Define edge-bead removal evidence principle","text":"去除寬度需兼顧邊緣潔淨與有效面積。","textEn":"Removal width balances edge cleanliness and usable area."},{"id":"a031-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊珠去除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define edge-bead removal evidence?","options":["去除寬度需兼顧邊緣潔淨與有效面積。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Removal width balances edge cleanliness and usable area.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"去除寬度需兼顧邊緣潔淨與有效面積。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Removal width balances edge cleanliness and usable area. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}},{"id":"a031-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-13"],"title":"背面污染","titleEn":"Inspect backside contamination","objective":"完成「背面污染」的對照表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect backside contamination, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背面污染。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：背面光阻可轉移到吸盤與後續晶圓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect backside contamination. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Backside resist can transfer to chucks and later wafers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背面光阻可轉移到吸盤與後續晶圓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside resist can transfer to chucks and later wafers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「背面污染」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect backside contamination and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背面污染」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect backside contamination: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-14-k1","title":"背面污染的原理","titleEn":"Inspect backside contamination principle","text":"背面光阻可轉移到吸盤與後續晶圓。","textEn":"Backside resist can transfer to chucks and later wafers."},{"id":"a031-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背面污染」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect backside contamination?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","背面光阻可轉移到吸盤與後續晶圓。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Backside resist can transfer to chucks and later wafers.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"背面光阻可轉移到吸盤與後續晶圓。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Backside resist can transfer to chucks and later wafers. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}},{"id":"a031-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-14"],"title":"氣泡缺陷","titleEn":"Identify bubbles","objective":"完成「氣泡缺陷」的敏感度草圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify bubbles, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣泡缺陷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：氣泡與固體粒子需分開建立缺陷類別。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify bubbles. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Bubbles and solid particles require separate defect classes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氣泡與固體粒子需分開建立缺陷類別。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bubbles and solid particles require separate defect classes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「氣泡缺陷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify bubbles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣泡缺陷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify bubbles: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-15-k1","title":"氣泡缺陷的原理","titleEn":"Identify bubbles principle","text":"氣泡與固體粒子需分開建立缺陷類別。","textEn":"Bubbles and solid particles require separate defect classes."},{"id":"a031-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣泡缺陷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify bubbles?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","氣泡與固體粒子需分開建立缺陷類別。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Bubbles and solid particles require separate defect classes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣泡與固體粒子需分開建立缺陷類別。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Bubbles and solid particles require separate defect classes. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}},{"id":"a031-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-15"],"title":"放射條紋","titleEn":"Interpret radial striations","objective":"完成「放射條紋」的故障判別表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for interpret radial striations, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：放射條紋。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：條紋應與旋轉、氣流及乾燥條件對照。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret radial striations. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Striations should be compared with rotation, airflow and drying conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「條紋應與旋轉、氣流及乾燥條件對照。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Striations should be compared with rotation, airflow and drying conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「放射條紋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret radial striations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「放射條紋」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for interpret radial striations: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-16-k1","title":"放射條紋的原理","titleEn":"Interpret radial striations principle","text":"條紋應與旋轉、氣流及乾燥條件對照。","textEn":"Striations should be compared with rotation, airflow and drying conditions."},{"id":"a031-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「放射條紋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret radial striations?","options":["條紋應與旋轉、氣流及乾燥條件對照。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Striations should be compared with rotation, airflow and drying conditions.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"條紋應與旋轉、氣流及乾燥條件對照。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Striations should be compared with rotation, airflow and drying conditions. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}},{"id":"a031-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-16"],"title":"台階覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess topographic coverage","objective":"完成「台階覆蓋」的量測規劃，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess topographic coverage, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：台階覆蓋。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：平面均勻膜不保證台階角落也有足夠厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess topographic coverage. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Uniform planar films do not guarantee sufficient corner coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平面均勻膜不保證台階角落也有足夠厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Uniform planar films do not guarantee sufficient corner coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「台階覆蓋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess topographic coverage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「台階覆蓋」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess topographic coverage: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-17-k1","title":"台階覆蓋的原理","titleEn":"Assess topographic coverage principle","text":"平面均勻膜不保證台階角落也有足夠厚度。","textEn":"Uniform planar films do not guarantee sufficient corner coverage."},{"id":"a031-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「台階覆蓋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess topographic coverage?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平面均勻膜不保證台階角落也有足夠厚度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Uniform planar films do not guarantee sufficient corner coverage.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平面均勻膜不保證台階角落也有足夠厚度。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Uniform planar films do not guarantee sufficient corner coverage. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}},{"id":"a031-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-17"],"title":"膜厚地圖","titleEn":"Construct thickness maps","objective":"完成「膜厚地圖」的工程驗收單，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for construct thickness maps, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：膜厚地圖。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：平均膜厚與片內非均勻性須同時報告。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Construct thickness maps. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Report mean thickness and within-wafer nonuniformity together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均膜厚與片內非均勻性須同時報告。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report mean thickness and within-wafer nonuniformity together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「膜厚地圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for construct thickness maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「膜厚地圖」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for construct thickness maps: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-18-k1","title":"膜厚地圖的原理","titleEn":"Construct thickness maps principle","text":"平均膜厚與片內非均勻性須同時報告。","textEn":"Report mean thickness and within-wafer nonuniformity together."},{"id":"a031-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","textEn":"Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「膜厚地圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating construct thickness maps?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","平均膜厚與片內非均勻性須同時報告。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Report mean thickness and within-wafer nonuniformity together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均膜厚與片內非均勻性須同時報告。 邊珠、背面殘留與氣泡具有不同空間形態，缺陷分類應保留位置而不只計算總數。","explanationEn":"Report mean thickness and within-wafer nonuniformity together. Edge beads, backside residues and bubbles have different spatial signatures; retain locations rather than only total defect counts."}}]},{"id":"a031-stage04","order":4,"title":"曝光交接","titleEn":"Exposure handoff","description":"在「曝光交接」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for exposure handoff, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a031-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-18"],"title":"光學常數","titleEn":"Check optical constants","objective":"完成「光學常數」的因果圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for check optical constants, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光學常數。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：膜厚反演需要適用波長的折射率模型。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check optical constants. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thickness extraction needs refractive-index models valid at the measurement wavelength. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「膜厚反演需要適用波長的折射率模型。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness extraction needs refractive-index models valid at the measurement wavelength. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「光學常數」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check optical constants and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光學常數」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for check optical constants: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-19-k1","title":"光學常數的原理","titleEn":"Check optical constants principle","text":"膜厚反演需要適用波長的折射率模型。","textEn":"Thickness extraction needs refractive-index models valid at the measurement wavelength."},{"id":"a031-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光學常數」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check optical constants?","options":["膜厚反演需要適用波長的折射率模型。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness extraction needs refractive-index models valid at the measurement wavelength.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜厚反演需要適用波長的折射率模型。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Thickness extraction needs refractive-index models valid at the measurement wavelength. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}},{"id":"a031-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-19"],"title":"反射與底層","titleEn":"Assess substrate reflectivity","objective":"完成「反射與底層」的對照表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess substrate reflectivity, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：反射與底層。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：基板反射會改變光阻內部曝光分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess substrate reflectivity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Substrate reflection changes exposure distribution within resist. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「基板反射會改變光阻內部曝光分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Substrate reflection changes exposure distribution within resist. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「反射與底層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess substrate reflectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「反射與底層」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess substrate reflectivity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-20-k1","title":"反射與底層的原理","titleEn":"Assess substrate reflectivity principle","text":"基板反射會改變光阻內部曝光分布。","textEn":"Substrate reflection changes exposure distribution within resist."},{"id":"a031-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「反射與底層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess substrate reflectivity?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","基板反射會改變光阻內部曝光分布。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","Substrate reflection changes exposure distribution within resist.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板反射會改變光阻內部曝光分布。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Substrate reflection changes exposure distribution within resist. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}},{"id":"a031-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-20"],"title":"底部抗反射層","titleEn":"Assess bottom antireflection layers","objective":"完成「底部抗反射層」的敏感度草圖，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess bottom antireflection layers, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部抗反射層。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：抗反射層需與光阻及後續蝕刻相容。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess bottom antireflection layers. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Antireflection layers must match resist and subsequent etching. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「抗反射層需與光阻及後續蝕刻相容。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Antireflection layers must match resist and subsequent etching. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「底部抗反射層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess bottom antireflection layers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部抗反射層」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess bottom antireflection layers: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-21-k1","title":"底部抗反射層的原理","titleEn":"Assess bottom antireflection layers principle","text":"抗反射層需與光阻及後續蝕刻相容。","textEn":"Antireflection layers must match resist and subsequent etching."},{"id":"a031-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部抗反射層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess bottom antireflection layers?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","抗反射層需與光阻及後續蝕刻相容。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Antireflection layers must match resist and subsequent etching."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抗反射層需與光阻及後續蝕刻相容。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Antireflection layers must match resist and subsequent etching. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}},{"id":"a031-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-21"],"title":"軟烤前等待","titleEn":"Assess delay before softbake","objective":"完成「軟烤前等待」的故障判別表，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess delay before softbake, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軟烤前等待。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：等待會改變溶劑殘留及流動。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess delay before softbake. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Delay changes solvent content and flow. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「等待會改變溶劑殘留及流動。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Delay changes solvent content and flow. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「軟烤前等待」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess delay before softbake and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軟烤前等待」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess delay before softbake: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-22-k1","title":"軟烤前等待的原理","titleEn":"Assess delay before softbake principle","text":"等待會改變溶劑殘留及流動。","textEn":"Delay changes solvent content and flow."},{"id":"a031-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軟烤前等待」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess delay before softbake?","options":["等待會改變溶劑殘留及流動。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Delay changes solvent content and flow.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"等待會改變溶劑殘留及流動。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Delay changes solvent content and flow. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}},{"id":"a031-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-22"],"title":"膜厚與焦深","titleEn":"Connect thickness and focus budget","objective":"完成「膜厚與焦深」的量測規劃，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for connect thickness and focus budget, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：膜厚與焦深。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：過厚或不均勻的膜會增加圖案轉移的不確定度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect thickness and focus budget. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Excessive or uneven thickness increases pattern-transfer uncertainty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「過厚或不均勻的膜會增加圖案轉移的不確定度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Excessive or uneven thickness increases pattern-transfer uncertainty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「膜厚與焦深」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect thickness and focus budget and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「膜厚與焦深」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for connect thickness and focus budget: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-23-k1","title":"膜厚與焦深的原理","titleEn":"Connect thickness and focus budget principle","text":"過厚或不均勻的膜會增加圖案轉移的不確定度。","textEn":"Excessive or uneven thickness increases pattern-transfer uncertainty."},{"id":"a031-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「膜厚與焦深」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect thickness and focus budget?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","過厚或不均勻的膜會增加圖案轉移的不確定度。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","Excessive or uneven thickness increases pattern-transfer uncertainty.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過厚或不均勻的膜會增加圖案轉移的不確定度。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Excessive or uneven thickness increases pattern-transfer uncertainty. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}},{"id":"a031-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-spin","v8a-resist","v8a-antireflect","v8a-car"],"prerequisiteIds":["a031-v8-23"],"title":"DUV 塗佈交接","titleEn":"Release the DUV coating","objective":"完成「DUV 塗佈交接」的工程驗收單，把塗佈流動、邊珠、膜厚與缺陷中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the duv coating, connecting relevant limits in coating flow, edge bead, thickness and defects to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：DUV 塗佈交接。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：膜厚、邊緣、背面及缺陷證據須一起交給曝光端。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the DUV coating. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thickness, edge, backside and defect evidence must accompany exposure handoff. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「膜厚、邊緣、背面及缺陷證據須一起交給曝光端。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness, edge, backside and defect evidence must accompany exposure handoff. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「DUV 塗佈交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the duv coating and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「DUV 塗佈交接」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the duv coating: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a031-v8-24-k1","title":"DUV 塗佈交接的原理","titleEn":"Release the DUV coating principle","text":"膜厚、邊緣、背面及缺陷證據須一起交給曝光端。","textEn":"Thickness, edge, backside and defect evidence must accompany exposure handoff."},{"id":"a031-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","textEn":"Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「DUV 塗佈交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the duv coating?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","膜厚、邊緣、背面及缺陷證據須一起交給曝光端。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Thickness, edge, backside and defect evidence must accompany exposure handoff."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜厚、邊緣、背面及缺陷證據須一起交給曝光端。 光阻膜厚與底層反射共同決定內部光場，塗佈端與曝光端需要共用光學堆疊版本。","explanationEn":"Thickness, edge, backside and defect evidence must accompany exposure handoff. Resist thickness and underlying reflection determine the internal optical field; coating and exposure should share the stack version."}}]}],"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography"},{"id":"a032","title":"光阻烘烤與顯影控制","titleEn":"Photoresist bake and development control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["烘烤機制","曝光後反應","顯影傳輸","圖案驗收"],"labelsEn":["Bake mechanisms","Post-exposure reaction","Development transport","Pattern acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a032-stage01","order":1,"title":"烘烤機制","titleEn":"Bake mechanisms","description":"在「烘烤機制」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for bake mechanisms, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a032-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"軟烤與 PEB","titleEn":"Separate softbake and PEB","objective":"完成「軟烤與 PEB」的因果圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate softbake and peb, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：軟烤與 PEB。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：除溶劑與曝光後反應是不同功能。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate softbake and PEB. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Solvent removal and post-exposure reaction serve different functions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「除溶劑與曝光後反應是不同功能。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Solvent removal and post-exposure reaction serve different functions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「軟烤與 PEB」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate softbake and peb and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「軟烤與 PEB」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate softbake and peb: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-01-k1","title":"軟烤與 PEB的原理","titleEn":"Separate softbake and PEB principle","text":"除溶劑與曝光後反應是不同功能。","textEn":"Solvent removal and post-exposure reaction serve different functions."},{"id":"a032-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「軟烤與 PEB」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate softbake and peb?","options":["除溶劑與曝光後反應是不同功能。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Solvent removal and post-exposure reaction serve different functions.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"除溶劑與曝光後反應是不同功能。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Solvent removal and post-exposure reaction serve different functions. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}},{"id":"a032-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-01"],"title":"熱板與片溫","titleEn":"Separate hotplate and wafer temperature","objective":"完成「熱板與片溫」的對照表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate hotplate and wafer temperature, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱板與片溫。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：設定溫度不能等同於光阻瞬間溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate hotplate and wafer temperature. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Setpoint does not equal instantaneous resist temperature. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「設定溫度不能等同於光阻瞬間溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Setpoint does not equal instantaneous resist temperature. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「熱板與片溫」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate hotplate and wafer temperature and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱板與片溫」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate hotplate and wafer temperature: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-02-k1","title":"熱板與片溫的原理","titleEn":"Separate hotplate and wafer temperature principle","text":"設定溫度不能等同於光阻瞬間溫度。","textEn":"Setpoint does not equal instantaneous resist temperature."},{"id":"a032-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱板與片溫」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate hotplate and wafer temperature?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","設定溫度不能等同於光阻瞬間溫度。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Setpoint does not equal instantaneous resist temperature.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設定溫度不能等同於光阻瞬間溫度。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Setpoint does not equal instantaneous resist temperature. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}},{"id":"a032-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-02"],"title":"殘留溶劑","titleEn":"Assess residual solvent","objective":"完成「殘留溶劑」的敏感度草圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess residual solvent, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：殘留溶劑。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：溶劑殘留會影響顯影與材料力學行為。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess residual solvent. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Residual solvent affects development and mechanical behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶劑殘留會影響顯影與材料力學行為。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual solvent affects development and mechanical behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「殘留溶劑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess residual solvent and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「殘留溶劑」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess residual solvent: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-03-k1","title":"殘留溶劑的原理","titleEn":"Assess residual solvent principle","text":"溶劑殘留會影響顯影與材料力學行為。","textEn":"Residual solvent affects development and mechanical behavior."},{"id":"a032-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「殘留溶劑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess residual solvent?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","溶劑殘留會影響顯影與材料力學行為。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","Residual solvent affects development and mechanical behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溶劑殘留會影響顯影與材料力學行為。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Residual solvent affects development and mechanical behavior. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}},{"id":"a032-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-03"],"title":"接觸熱阻","titleEn":"Assess thermal contact","objective":"完成「接觸熱阻」的故障判別表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess thermal contact, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸熱阻。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：晶圓翹曲與背面污染會改變熱接觸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thermal contact. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Wafer bow and backside contamination alter thermal contact. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「晶圓翹曲與背面污染會改變熱接觸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Wafer bow and backside contamination alter thermal contact. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「接觸熱阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thermal contact and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸熱阻」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess thermal contact: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-04-k1","title":"接觸熱阻的原理","titleEn":"Assess thermal contact principle","text":"晶圓翹曲與背面污染會改變熱接觸。","textEn":"Wafer bow and backside contamination alter thermal contact."},{"id":"a032-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸熱阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thermal contact?","options":["晶圓翹曲與背面污染會改變熱接觸。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Wafer bow and backside contamination alter thermal contact.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶圓翹曲與背面污染會改變熱接觸。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Wafer bow and backside contamination alter thermal contact. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}},{"id":"a032-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-04"],"title":"升溫與冷卻","titleEn":"Include heating and cooling","objective":"完成「升溫與冷卻」的量測規劃，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for include heating and cooling, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：升溫與冷卻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：化學反應不一定只發生在名義保溫時間內。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include heating and cooling. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Chemical reaction need not occur only during nominal dwell. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「化學反應不一定只發生在名義保溫時間內。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chemical reaction need not occur only during nominal dwell. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「升溫與冷卻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include heating and cooling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「升溫與冷卻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for include heating and cooling: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-05-k1","title":"升溫與冷卻的原理","titleEn":"Include heating and cooling principle","text":"化學反應不一定只發生在名義保溫時間內。","textEn":"Chemical reaction need not occur only during nominal dwell."},{"id":"a032-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「升溫與冷卻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include heating and cooling?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","化學反應不一定只發生在名義保溫時間內。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Chemical reaction need not occur only during nominal dwell.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"化學反應不一定只發生在名義保溫時間內。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Chemical reaction need not occur only during nominal dwell. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}},{"id":"a032-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-05"],"title":"烘烤均勻性","titleEn":"Map bake uniformity","objective":"完成「烘烤均勻性」的工程驗收單，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for map bake uniformity, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：烘烤均勻性。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：微小溫差可能經反應敏感度放大為尺寸差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map bake uniformity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Small temperature differences can amplify into dimensional variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「微小溫差可能經反應敏感度放大為尺寸差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Small temperature differences can amplify into dimensional variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「烘烤均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map bake uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「烘烤均勻性」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for map bake uniformity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-06-k1","title":"烘烤均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Map bake uniformity principle","text":"微小溫差可能經反應敏感度放大為尺寸差。","textEn":"Small temperature differences can amplify into dimensional variation."},{"id":"a032-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","textEn":"Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「烘烤均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map bake uniformity?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","微小溫差可能經反應敏感度放大為尺寸差。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","Small temperature differences can amplify into dimensional variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"微小溫差可能經反應敏感度放大為尺寸差。 軟烤調整溶劑與薄膜狀態，PEB 驅動曝光後反應；兩者的合格結果應以各自的物理目的定義。","explanationEn":"Small temperature differences can amplify into dimensional variation. Softbake adjusts solvent and film state while PEB drives post-exposure reaction; accept each against its own physical purpose."}}]},{"id":"a032-stage02","order":2,"title":"曝光後反應","titleEn":"Post-exposure reaction","description":"在「曝光後反應」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for post-exposure reaction, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a032-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-06"],"title":"曝光後等待","titleEn":"Track post-exposure delay","objective":"完成「曝光後等待」的因果圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for track post-exposure delay, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：曝光後等待。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：等待時間會改變酸遷移及污染中和機會。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track post-exposure delay. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Delay changes acid transport and opportunities for contaminant neutralization. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「等待時間會改變酸遷移及污染中和機會。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Delay changes acid transport and opportunities for contaminant neutralization. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「曝光後等待」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track post-exposure delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「曝光後等待」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for track post-exposure delay: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-07-k1","title":"曝光後等待的原理","titleEn":"Track post-exposure delay principle","text":"等待時間會改變酸遷移及污染中和機會。","textEn":"Delay changes acid transport and opportunities for contaminant neutralization."},{"id":"a032-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「曝光後等待」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track post-exposure delay?","options":["等待時間會改變酸遷移及污染中和機會。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Delay changes acid transport and opportunities for contaminant neutralization.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"等待時間會改變酸遷移及污染中和機會。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Delay changes acid transport and opportunities for contaminant neutralization. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}},{"id":"a032-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-07"],"title":"化學放大反應","titleEn":"Trace chemical amplification","objective":"完成「化學放大反應」的對照表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace chemical amplification, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：化學放大反應。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：光生酸可催化多次反應而非只對應單一光子事件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace chemical amplification. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Photoacid can catalyze multiple reactions rather than one event per photon. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光生酸可催化多次反應而非只對應單一光子事件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Photoacid can catalyze multiple reactions rather than one event per photon. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「化學放大反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace chemical amplification and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「化學放大反應」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace chemical amplification: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-08-k1","title":"化學放大反應的原理","titleEn":"Trace chemical amplification principle","text":"光生酸可催化多次反應而非只對應單一光子事件。","textEn":"Photoacid can catalyze multiple reactions rather than one event per photon."},{"id":"a032-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「化學放大反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace chemical amplification?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","光生酸可催化多次反應而非只對應單一光子事件。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","Photoacid can catalyze multiple reactions rather than one event per photon.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光生酸可催化多次反應而非只對應單一光子事件。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Photoacid can catalyze multiple reactions rather than one event per photon. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}},{"id":"a032-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-08"],"title":"酸擴散長度","titleEn":"Assess acid diffusion length","objective":"完成「酸擴散長度」的敏感度草圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess acid diffusion length, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：酸擴散長度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：更長反應時間也可能增加影像模糊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂一維擴散模型 L=√(2Dt)，固定 D 且時間增加四倍；求 L 的比例，再說明實際 PEB 中反應及淬熄為何使此模型不完整。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess acid diffusion length. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Longer reaction time can also increase image blur. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical 1D diffusion L=√(2Dt): hold D fixed and quadruple time. Find the L ratio and explain why reaction and quenching make this incomplete for actual PEB.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更長反應時間也可能增加影像模糊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Longer reaction time can also increase image blur. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「酸擴散長度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess acid diffusion length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「酸擴散長度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess acid diffusion length: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-09-k1","title":"酸擴散長度的原理","titleEn":"Assess acid diffusion length principle","text":"更長反應時間也可能增加影像模糊。","textEn":"Longer reaction time can also increase image blur."},{"id":"a032-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「酸擴散長度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess acid diffusion length?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","更長反應時間也可能增加影像模糊。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Longer reaction time can also increase image blur."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更長反應時間也可能增加影像模糊。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Longer reaction time can also increase image blur. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}},{"id":"a032-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-09"],"title":"表面中和","titleEn":"Assess surface neutralization","objective":"完成「表面中和」的故障判別表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess surface neutralization, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面中和。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：空氣鹼性污染可能改變上表面反應。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess surface neutralization. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Airborne bases can change reactions near the top surface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「空氣鹼性污染可能改變上表面反應。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Airborne bases can change reactions near the top surface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「表面中和」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess surface neutralization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面中和」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess surface neutralization: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-10-k1","title":"表面中和的原理","titleEn":"Assess surface neutralization principle","text":"空氣鹼性污染可能改變上表面反應。","textEn":"Airborne bases can change reactions near the top surface."},{"id":"a032-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面中和」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess surface neutralization?","options":["空氣鹼性污染可能改變上表面反應。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Airborne bases can change reactions near the top surface.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"空氣鹼性污染可能改變上表面反應。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Airborne bases can change reactions near the top surface. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}},{"id":"a032-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-10"],"title":"基底界面反應","titleEn":"Inspect substrate-interface reaction","objective":"完成「基底界面反應」的量測規劃，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect substrate-interface reaction, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基底界面反應。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：底層化學狀態會影響底部光阻輪廓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect substrate-interface reaction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Underlying chemistry affects the resist profile near the bottom. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「底層化學狀態會影響底部光阻輪廓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Underlying chemistry affects the resist profile near the bottom. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「基底界面反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect substrate-interface reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基底界面反應」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect substrate-interface reaction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-11-k1","title":"基底界面反應的原理","titleEn":"Inspect substrate-interface reaction principle","text":"底層化學狀態會影響底部光阻輪廓。","textEn":"Underlying chemistry affects the resist profile near the bottom."},{"id":"a032-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基底界面反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect substrate-interface reaction?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","底層化學狀態會影響底部光阻輪廓。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","Underlying chemistry affects the resist profile near the bottom.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"底層化學狀態會影響底部光阻輪廓。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Underlying chemistry affects the resist profile near the bottom. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}},{"id":"a032-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-11"],"title":"PEB 視窗","titleEn":"Build a PEB window","objective":"完成「PEB 視窗」的工程驗收單，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for build a peb window, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：PEB 視窗。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：反應完成度、尺寸及粗糙度需共同取捨。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a PEB window. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Reaction completion, dimensions and roughness need joint tradeoffs. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應完成度、尺寸及粗糙度需共同取捨。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reaction completion, dimensions and roughness need joint tradeoffs. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「PEB 視窗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a peb window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「PEB 視窗」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for build a peb window: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-12-k1","title":"PEB 視窗的原理","titleEn":"Build a PEB window principle","text":"反應完成度、尺寸及粗糙度需共同取捨。","textEn":"Reaction completion, dimensions and roughness need joint tradeoffs."},{"id":"a032-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","textEn":"Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「PEB 視窗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a peb window?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","反應完成度、尺寸及粗糙度需共同取捨。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Reaction completion, dimensions and roughness need joint tradeoffs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應完成度、尺寸及粗糙度需共同取捨。 酸催化與酸擴散同時發生，較完全的去保護可能伴隨較大的影像模糊，需要聯合量測。","explanationEn":"Reaction completion, dimensions and roughness need joint tradeoffs. Acid catalysis and diffusion occur together; more complete deprotection can accompany more blur, requiring joint measurements."}}]},{"id":"a032-stage03","order":3,"title":"顯影傳輸","titleEn":"Development transport","description":"在「顯影傳輸」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for development transport, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a032-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-12"],"title":"正負型溶解","titleEn":"Separate positive and negative tone","objective":"完成「正負型溶解」的因果圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate positive and negative tone, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：正負型溶解。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：顯影保留區由材料反應與顯影化學共同決定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate positive and negative tone. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Remaining regions depend on both resist chemistry and developer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「顯影保留區由材料反應與顯影化學共同決定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Remaining regions depend on both resist chemistry and developer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「正負型溶解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate positive and negative tone and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「正負型溶解」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate positive and negative tone: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-13-k1","title":"正負型溶解的原理","titleEn":"Separate positive and negative tone principle","text":"顯影保留區由材料反應與顯影化學共同決定。","textEn":"Remaining regions depend on both resist chemistry and developer."},{"id":"a032-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「正負型溶解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate positive and negative tone?","options":["顯影保留區由材料反應與顯影化學共同決定。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Remaining regions depend on both resist chemistry and developer.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顯影保留區由材料反應與顯影化學共同決定。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Remaining regions depend on both resist chemistry and developer. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}},{"id":"a032-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-13"],"title":"顯影液相容","titleEn":"Review developer compatibility","objective":"完成「顯影液相容」的對照表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for review developer compatibility, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：顯影液相容。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：不同光阻不能直接共用同一顯影條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review developer compatibility. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Different resists cannot automatically share developer conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同光阻不能直接共用同一顯影條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different resists cannot automatically share developer conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「顯影液相容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review developer compatibility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「顯影液相容」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for review developer compatibility: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-14-k1","title":"顯影液相容的原理","titleEn":"Review developer compatibility principle","text":"不同光阻不能直接共用同一顯影條件。","textEn":"Different resists cannot automatically share developer conditions."},{"id":"a032-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「顯影液相容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review developer compatibility?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","不同光阻不能直接共用同一顯影條件。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Different resists cannot automatically share developer conditions.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同光阻不能直接共用同一顯影條件。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Different resists cannot automatically share developer conditions. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}},{"id":"a032-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-14"],"title":"溶解速率","titleEn":"Compare dissolution rates","objective":"完成「溶解速率」的敏感度草圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare dissolution rates, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溶解速率。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：曝光與未曝光區速率差決定圖案對比。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare dissolution rates. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Rate contrast between exposed and unexposed regions determines image contrast. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「曝光與未曝光區速率差決定圖案對比。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rate contrast between exposed and unexposed regions determines image contrast. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「溶解速率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare dissolution rates and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溶解速率」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare dissolution rates: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-15-k1","title":"溶解速率的原理","titleEn":"Compare dissolution rates principle","text":"曝光與未曝光區速率差決定圖案對比。","textEn":"Rate contrast between exposed and unexposed regions determines image contrast."},{"id":"a032-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溶解速率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare dissolution rates?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","曝光與未曝光區速率差決定圖案對比。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Rate contrast between exposed and unexposed regions determines image contrast."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曝光與未曝光區速率差決定圖案對比。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Rate contrast between exposed and unexposed regions determines image contrast. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}},{"id":"a032-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-15"],"title":"液膜更新","titleEn":"Assess puddle renewal","objective":"完成「液膜更新」的故障判別表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess puddle renewal, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：液膜更新。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：顯影產物累積會改變局部傳輸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess puddle renewal. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Accumulated dissolution products change local transport. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「顯影產物累積會改變局部傳輸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Accumulated dissolution products change local transport. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「液膜更新」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess puddle renewal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「液膜更新」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess puddle renewal: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-16-k1","title":"液膜更新的原理","titleEn":"Assess puddle renewal principle","text":"顯影產物累積會改變局部傳輸。","textEn":"Accumulated dissolution products change local transport."},{"id":"a032-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「液膜更新」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess puddle renewal?","options":["顯影產物累積會改變局部傳輸。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Accumulated dissolution products change local transport.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顯影產物累積會改變局部傳輸。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Accumulated dissolution products change local transport. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}},{"id":"a032-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-16"],"title":"暗蝕損失","titleEn":"Measure dark erosion","objective":"完成「暗蝕損失」的量測規劃，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for measure dark erosion, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：暗蝕損失。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：未曝光保留區也可能在顯影中變薄。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure dark erosion. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Unexposed retained regions can also thin during development. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「未曝光保留區也可能在顯影中變薄。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Unexposed retained regions can also thin during development. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「暗蝕損失」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure dark erosion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「暗蝕損失」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for measure dark erosion: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-17-k1","title":"暗蝕損失的原理","titleEn":"Measure dark erosion principle","text":"未曝光保留區也可能在顯影中變薄。","textEn":"Unexposed retained regions can also thin during development."},{"id":"a032-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「暗蝕損失」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure dark erosion?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","未曝光保留區也可能在顯影中變薄。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Unexposed retained regions can also thin during development.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未曝光保留區也可能在顯影中變薄。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Unexposed retained regions can also thin during development. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}},{"id":"a032-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-17"],"title":"沖洗終止","titleEn":"Define rinse termination","objective":"完成「沖洗終止」的工程驗收單，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for define rinse termination, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沖洗終止。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：沖洗改變反應與溶解產物移除，需納入時間線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define rinse termination. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Rinsing affects reaction termination and product removal and belongs in the timeline. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沖洗改變反應與溶解產物移除，需納入時間線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rinsing affects reaction termination and product removal and belongs in the timeline. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「沖洗終止」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define rinse termination and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沖洗終止」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for define rinse termination: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-18-k1","title":"沖洗終止的原理","titleEn":"Define rinse termination principle","text":"沖洗改變反應與溶解產物移除，需納入時間線。","textEn":"Rinsing affects reaction termination and product removal and belongs in the timeline."},{"id":"a032-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","textEn":"Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沖洗終止」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define rinse termination?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","沖洗改變反應與溶解產物移除，需納入時間線。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Rinsing affects reaction termination and product removal and belongs in the timeline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沖洗改變反應與溶解產物移除，需納入時間線。 顯影產物移除受局部傳質限制，厚膜或細孔的清除不能由平面大開口結果直接預測。","explanationEn":"Rinsing affects reaction termination and product removal and belongs in the timeline. Product removal depends on local transport, so thick-film or small-hole clearance cannot follow directly from large planar openings."}}]},{"id":"a032-stage04","order":4,"title":"圖案驗收","titleEn":"Pattern acceptance","description":"在「圖案驗收」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for pattern acceptance, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a032-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-18"],"title":"底部殘膠","titleEn":"Identify scum","objective":"完成「底部殘膠」的因果圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify scum, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：底部殘膠。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：上方開口不代表底部已完全清除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify scum. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: An opening at the top does not prove complete bottom clearance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「上方開口不代表底部已完全清除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An opening at the top does not prove complete bottom clearance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「底部殘膠」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify scum and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「底部殘膠」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify scum: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-19-k1","title":"底部殘膠的原理","titleEn":"Identify scum principle","text":"上方開口不代表底部已完全清除。","textEn":"An opening at the top does not prove complete bottom clearance."},{"id":"a032-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「底部殘膠」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify scum?","options":["上方開口不代表底部已完全清除。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["An opening at the top does not prove complete bottom clearance.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上方開口不代表底部已完全清除。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"An opening at the top does not prove complete bottom clearance. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}},{"id":"a032-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-19"],"title":"側壁角度","titleEn":"Measure sidewall angle","objective":"完成「側壁角度」的對照表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure sidewall angle, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：側壁角度。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：頂視尺寸相同可能有不同底部尺寸。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure sidewall angle. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal top-view dimensions can hide different bottom dimensions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂視尺寸相同可能有不同底部尺寸。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal top-view dimensions can hide different bottom dimensions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「側壁角度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure sidewall angle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「側壁角度」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure sidewall angle: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-20-k1","title":"側壁角度的原理","titleEn":"Measure sidewall angle principle","text":"頂視尺寸相同可能有不同底部尺寸。","textEn":"Equal top-view dimensions can hide different bottom dimensions."},{"id":"a032-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「側壁角度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure sidewall angle?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","頂視尺寸相同可能有不同底部尺寸。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","Equal top-view dimensions can hide different bottom dimensions.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂視尺寸相同可能有不同底部尺寸。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"Equal top-view dimensions can hide different bottom dimensions. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}},{"id":"a032-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-20"],"title":"圖案倒塌","titleEn":"Assess pattern collapse","objective":"完成「圖案倒塌」的敏感度草圖，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess pattern collapse, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案倒塌。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：高細長圖案在乾燥中可能受毛細力破壞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pattern collapse. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Slender patterns can fail under capillary forces during drying. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高細長圖案在乾燥中可能受毛細力破壞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Slender patterns can fail under capillary forces during drying. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「圖案倒塌」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pattern collapse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案倒塌」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess pattern collapse: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-21-k1","title":"圖案倒塌的原理","titleEn":"Assess pattern collapse principle","text":"高細長圖案在乾燥中可能受毛細力破壞。","textEn":"Slender patterns can fail under capillary forces during drying."},{"id":"a032-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案倒塌」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pattern collapse?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","高細長圖案在乾燥中可能受毛細力破壞。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Slender patterns can fail under capillary forces during drying."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高細長圖案在乾燥中可能受毛細力破壞。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"Slender patterns can fail under capillary forces during drying. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}},{"id":"a032-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-21"],"title":"尺寸偏差歸因","titleEn":"Attribute CD bias","objective":"完成「尺寸偏差歸因」的故障判別表，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for attribute cd bias, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：尺寸偏差歸因。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：曝光、PEB 與顯影都可能造成最終尺寸偏差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Attribute CD bias. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Exposure, PEB and development can all cause final CD bias. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「曝光、PEB 與顯影都可能造成最終尺寸偏差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Exposure, PEB and development can all cause final CD bias. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「尺寸偏差歸因」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for attribute cd bias and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「尺寸偏差歸因」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for attribute cd bias: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-22-k1","title":"尺寸偏差歸因的原理","titleEn":"Attribute CD bias principle","text":"曝光、PEB 與顯影都可能造成最終尺寸偏差。","textEn":"Exposure, PEB and development can all cause final CD bias."},{"id":"a032-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「尺寸偏差歸因」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating attribute cd bias?","options":["曝光、PEB 與顯影都可能造成最終尺寸偏差。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Exposure, PEB and development can all cause final CD bias.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝光、PEB 與顯影都可能造成最終尺寸偏差。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"Exposure, PEB and development can all cause final CD bias. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}},{"id":"a032-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-22"],"title":"曝光烘烤矩陣","titleEn":"Design a dose-bake matrix","objective":"完成「曝光烘烤矩陣」的量測規劃，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for design a dose-bake matrix, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：曝光烘烤矩陣。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：交叉實驗可辨識劑量與熱歷程交互作用。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design a dose-bake matrix. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: A crossed study can identify dose-thermal-history interactions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「交叉實驗可辨識劑量與熱歷程交互作用。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A crossed study can identify dose-thermal-history interactions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「曝光烘烤矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design a dose-bake matrix and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「曝光烘烤矩陣」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for design a dose-bake matrix: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-23-k1","title":"曝光烘烤矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Design a dose-bake matrix principle","text":"交叉實驗可辨識劑量與熱歷程交互作用。","textEn":"A crossed study can identify dose-thermal-history interactions."},{"id":"a032-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「曝光烘烤矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design a dose-bake matrix?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","交叉實驗可辨識劑量與熱歷程交互作用。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","A crossed study can identify dose-thermal-history interactions.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交叉實驗可辨識劑量與熱歷程交互作用。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"A crossed study can identify dose-thermal-history interactions. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}},{"id":"a032-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-softbake","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v8a-acid"],"prerequisiteIds":["a032-v8-23"],"title":"光阻圖案交接","titleEn":"Release the resist pattern","objective":"完成「光阻圖案交接」的工程驗收單，把軟烤、酸擴散、溶解與輪廓中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the resist pattern, connecting relevant limits in softbake, acid diffusion, dissolution and profiles to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光阻圖案交接。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：線寬、輪廓、殘膠及薄膜損失需共同符合要求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the resist pattern. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Width, profile, scum and retained-film loss must jointly meet requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「線寬、輪廓、殘膠及薄膜損失需共同符合要求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Width, profile, scum and retained-film loss must jointly meet requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「光阻圖案交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the resist pattern and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光阻圖案交接」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the resist pattern: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a032-v8-24-k1","title":"光阻圖案交接的原理","titleEn":"Release the resist pattern principle","text":"線寬、輪廓、殘膠及薄膜損失需共同符合要求。","textEn":"Width, profile, scum and retained-film loss must jointly meet requirements."},{"id":"a032-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","textEn":"CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光阻圖案交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the resist pattern?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","線寬、輪廓、殘膠及薄膜損失需共同符合要求。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Width, profile, scum and retained-film loss must jointly meet requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線寬、輪廓、殘膠及薄膜損失需共同符合要求。 尺寸、底部殘膠與側壁角是互補圖案指標；頂視 CD 合格仍可能無法完成後續蝕刻轉移。","explanationEn":"Width, profile, scum and retained-film loss must jointly meet requirements. CD, bottom scum and sidewall angle are complementary; acceptable top-view CD can still fail later etch transfer."}}]}],"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography"},{"id":"a033","title":"化學放大型光阻設計","titleEn":"Chemically amplified resist design","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["配方功能分工","光化學及擴散","圖案與隨機性","整合及材料評估"],"labelsEn":["Formulation functions","Photochemistry and diffusion","Patterning and stochasticity","Integration and material assessment"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a033-stage01","order":1,"title":"配方功能分工","titleEn":"Formulation functions","description":"在「配方功能分工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for formulation functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a033-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"放大機制定義","titleEn":"Define amplification","objective":"完成「放大機制定義」的因果圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define amplification, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：放大機制定義。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：光生催化劑可啟動多次溶解度改變反應。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define amplification. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: A photogenerated catalyst can initiate multiple solubility-changing reactions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光生催化劑可啟動多次溶解度改變反應。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A photogenerated catalyst can initiate multiple solubility-changing reactions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「放大機制定義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define amplification and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「放大機制定義」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define amplification: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-01-k1","title":"放大機制定義的原理","titleEn":"Define amplification principle","text":"光生催化劑可啟動多次溶解度改變反應。","textEn":"A photogenerated catalyst can initiate multiple solubility-changing reactions."},{"id":"a033-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「放大機制定義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define amplification?","options":["光生催化劑可啟動多次溶解度改變反應。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["A photogenerated catalyst can initiate multiple solubility-changing reactions.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光生催化劑可啟動多次溶解度改變反應。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"A photogenerated catalyst can initiate multiple solubility-changing reactions. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}},{"id":"a033-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-01"],"title":"樹脂保護基","titleEn":"Assign protecting groups","objective":"完成「樹脂保護基」的對照表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assign protecting groups, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：樹脂保護基。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：保護基轉換使樹脂對顯影液的親和改變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign protecting groups. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Protecting-group conversion changes resin affinity to developer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「保護基轉換使樹脂對顯影液的親和改變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Protecting-group conversion changes resin affinity to developer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「樹脂保護基」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign protecting groups and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「樹脂保護基」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assign protecting groups: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-02-k1","title":"樹脂保護基的原理","titleEn":"Assign protecting groups principle","text":"保護基轉換使樹脂對顯影液的親和改變。","textEn":"Protecting-group conversion changes resin affinity to developer."},{"id":"a033-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「樹脂保護基」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign protecting groups?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","保護基轉換使樹脂對顯影液的親和改變。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Protecting-group conversion changes resin affinity to developer.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護基轉換使樹脂對顯影液的親和改變。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"Protecting-group conversion changes resin affinity to developer. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}},{"id":"a033-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-02"],"title":"光酸產生劑","titleEn":"Assign photoacid generators","objective":"完成「光酸產生劑」的敏感度草圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assign photoacid generators, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光酸產生劑。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：PAG 吸收、產酸與相容性須同時評估。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign photoacid generators. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: PAG absorption, acid generation and compatibility need joint evaluation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「PAG 吸收、產酸與相容性須同時評估。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: PAG absorption, acid generation and compatibility need joint evaluation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「光酸產生劑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign photoacid generators and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光酸產生劑」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assign photoacid generators: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-03-k1","title":"光酸產生劑的原理","titleEn":"Assign photoacid generators principle","text":"PAG 吸收、產酸與相容性須同時評估。","textEn":"PAG absorption, acid generation and compatibility need joint evaluation."},{"id":"a033-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光酸產生劑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign photoacid generators?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","PAG 吸收、產酸與相容性須同時評估。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","PAG absorption, acid generation and compatibility need joint evaluation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"PAG 吸收、產酸與相容性須同時評估。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"PAG absorption, acid generation and compatibility need joint evaluation. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}},{"id":"a033-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-03"],"title":"淬熄劑作用","titleEn":"Assign quencher functions","objective":"完成「淬熄劑作用」的故障判別表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assign quencher functions, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：淬熄劑作用。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：淬熄劑限制酸反應也可能降低感度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign quencher functions. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Quenchers limit acid activity but can reduce sensitivity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「淬熄劑限制酸反應也可能降低感度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Quenchers limit acid activity but can reduce sensitivity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「淬熄劑作用」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign quencher functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「淬熄劑作用」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assign quencher functions: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-04-k1","title":"淬熄劑作用的原理","titleEn":"Assign quencher functions principle","text":"淬熄劑限制酸反應也可能降低感度。","textEn":"Quenchers limit acid activity but can reduce sensitivity."},{"id":"a033-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「淬熄劑作用」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign quencher functions?","options":["淬熄劑限制酸反應也可能降低感度。","相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Quenchers limit acid activity but can reduce sensitivity.","Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淬熄劑限制酸反應也可能降低感度。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"Quenchers limit acid activity but can reduce sensitivity. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}},{"id":"a033-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-04"],"title":"溶劑與成膜","titleEn":"Choose film-formation evidence","objective":"完成「溶劑與成膜」的量測規劃，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose film-formation evidence, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溶劑與成膜。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：溶液均勻不保證乾膜成分分布均勻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose film-formation evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: A uniform solution does not guarantee uniform dry-film composition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶液均勻不保證乾膜成分分布均勻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A uniform solution does not guarantee uniform dry-film composition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「溶劑與成膜」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose film-formation evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溶劑與成膜」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose film-formation evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-05-k1","title":"溶劑與成膜的原理","titleEn":"Choose film-formation evidence principle","text":"溶液均勻不保證乾膜成分分布均勻。","textEn":"A uniform solution does not guarantee uniform dry-film composition."},{"id":"a033-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溶劑與成膜」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose film-formation evidence?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","溶液均勻不保證乾膜成分分布均勻。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","A uniform solution does not guarantee uniform dry-film composition.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶液均勻不保證乾膜成分分布均勻。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"A uniform solution does not guarantee uniform dry-film composition. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}},{"id":"a033-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-05"],"title":"波長相容","titleEn":"Assess wavelength compatibility","objective":"完成「波長相容」的工程驗收單，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess wavelength compatibility, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：波長相容。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：材料吸收需配合目標曝光波長與膜厚。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess wavelength compatibility. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Absorption must match exposure wavelength and film thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料吸收需配合目標曝光波長與膜厚。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Absorption must match exposure wavelength and film thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。 應回到「波長相容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess wavelength compatibility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「波長相容」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess wavelength compatibility: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-06-k1","title":"波長相容的原理","titleEn":"Assess wavelength compatibility principle","text":"材料吸收需配合目標曝光波長與膜厚。","textEn":"Absorption must match exposure wavelength and film thickness."},{"id":"a033-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","textEn":"Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「波長相容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess wavelength compatibility?","options":["相同最終轉速一定得到相同膜厚分布。","軟烤與 PEB 可視為相同化學步驟。","材料吸收需配合目標曝光波長與膜厚。"],"optionsEn":["Equal final spin speed always gives equal thickness maps.","Softbake and PEB are the same chemical step.","Absorption must match exposure wavelength and film thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料吸收需配合目標曝光波長與膜厚。 化學放大將光吸收與多次催化轉換連起來，但產酸效率、淬熄及溶解反應決定有效增益。","explanationEn":"Absorption must match exposure wavelength and film thickness. Chemical amplification links absorption to multiple catalytic conversions, while acid yield, quenching and dissolution set effective gain."}}]},{"id":"a033-stage02","order":2,"title":"光化學及擴散","titleEn":"Photochemistry and diffusion","description":"在「光化學及擴散」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for photochemistry and diffusion, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a033-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-06"],"title":"吸收深度","titleEn":"Estimate absorption depth","objective":"完成「吸收深度」的因果圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for estimate absorption depth, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：吸收深度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：過強吸收可能造成上下層反應不均。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate absorption depth. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Excessive absorption can produce through-film reaction gradients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「過強吸收可能造成上下層反應不均。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Excessive absorption can produce through-film reaction gradients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「吸收深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate absorption depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「吸收深度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for estimate absorption depth: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-07-k1","title":"吸收深度的原理","titleEn":"Estimate absorption depth principle","text":"過強吸收可能造成上下層反應不均。","textEn":"Excessive absorption can produce through-film reaction gradients."},{"id":"a033-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「吸收深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate absorption depth?","options":["過強吸收可能造成上下層反應不均。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Excessive absorption can produce through-film reaction gradients.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"過強吸收可能造成上下層反應不均。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Excessive absorption can produce through-film reaction gradients. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}},{"id":"a033-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-07"],"title":"酸產生統計","titleEn":"Assess acid-generation statistics","objective":"完成「酸產生統計」的對照表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess acid-generation statistics, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：酸產生統計。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：微小區域的光子與分子事件具有隨機性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess acid-generation statistics. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Photon and molecular events are stochastic in small volumes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「微小區域的光子與分子事件具有隨機性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Photon and molecular events are stochastic in small volumes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「酸產生統計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess acid-generation statistics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「酸產生統計」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess acid-generation statistics: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-08-k1","title":"酸產生統計的原理","titleEn":"Assess acid-generation statistics principle","text":"微小區域的光子與分子事件具有隨機性。","textEn":"Photon and molecular events are stochastic in small volumes."},{"id":"a033-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「酸產生統計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess acid-generation statistics?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","微小區域的光子與分子事件具有隨機性。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","Photon and molecular events are stochastic in small volumes.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"微小區域的光子與分子事件具有隨機性。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Photon and molecular events are stochastic in small volumes. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}},{"id":"a033-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-08"],"title":"反應與擴散","titleEn":"Separate reaction and diffusion","objective":"完成「反應與擴散」的敏感度草圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate reaction and diffusion, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：反應與擴散。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：反應速率與擴散係數控制不同影像特徵。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate reaction and diffusion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Reaction rate and diffusivity control different image characteristics. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反應速率與擴散係數控制不同影像特徵。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reaction rate and diffusivity control different image characteristics. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「反應與擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate reaction and diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「反應與擴散」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate reaction and diffusion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-09-k1","title":"反應與擴散的原理","titleEn":"Separate reaction and diffusion principle","text":"反應速率與擴散係數控制不同影像特徵。","textEn":"Reaction rate and diffusivity control different image characteristics."},{"id":"a033-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「反應與擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate reaction and diffusion?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","反應速率與擴散係數控制不同影像特徵。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Reaction rate and diffusivity control different image characteristics."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應速率與擴散係數控制不同影像特徵。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Reaction rate and diffusivity control different image characteristics. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}},{"id":"a033-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-09"],"title":"PEB 敏感度","titleEn":"Measure PEB sensitivity","objective":"完成「PEB 敏感度」的故障判別表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for measure peb sensitivity, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：PEB 敏感度。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高溫敏感度可能放大熱板不均造成的尺寸差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure PEB sensitivity. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Strong temperature sensitivity can amplify hotplate-related CD variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高溫敏感度可能放大熱板不均造成的尺寸差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Strong temperature sensitivity can amplify hotplate-related CD variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「PEB 敏感度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure peb sensitivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「PEB 敏感度」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for measure peb sensitivity: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-10-k1","title":"PEB 敏感度的原理","titleEn":"Measure PEB sensitivity principle","text":"高溫敏感度可能放大熱板不均造成的尺寸差。","textEn":"Strong temperature sensitivity can amplify hotplate-related CD variation."},{"id":"a033-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「PEB 敏感度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure peb sensitivity?","options":["高溫敏感度可能放大熱板不均造成的尺寸差。","曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Strong temperature sensitivity can amplify hotplate-related CD variation.","Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高溫敏感度可能放大熱板不均造成的尺寸差。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Strong temperature sensitivity can amplify hotplate-related CD variation. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}},{"id":"a033-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-10"],"title":"酸中和競爭","titleEn":"Analyze acid-neutralization competition","objective":"完成「酸中和競爭」的量測規劃，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for analyze acid-neutralization competition, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：酸中和競爭。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：淬熄與去保護反應競爭決定有效反應範圍。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze acid-neutralization competition. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Quenching competes with deprotection to set the effective reaction region. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「淬熄與去保護反應競爭決定有效反應範圍。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Quenching competes with deprotection to set the effective reaction region. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「酸中和競爭」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze acid-neutralization competition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「酸中和競爭」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for analyze acid-neutralization competition: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-11-k1","title":"酸中和競爭的原理","titleEn":"Analyze acid-neutralization competition principle","text":"淬熄與去保護反應競爭決定有效反應範圍。","textEn":"Quenching competes with deprotection to set the effective reaction region."},{"id":"a033-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「酸中和競爭」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze acid-neutralization competition?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","淬熄與去保護反應競爭決定有效反應範圍。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","Quenching competes with deprotection to set the effective reaction region.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淬熄與去保護反應競爭決定有效反應範圍。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Quenching competes with deprotection to set the effective reaction region. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}},{"id":"a033-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-11"],"title":"自由體積影響","titleEn":"Assess free-volume effects","objective":"完成「自由體積影響」的工程驗收單，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess free-volume effects, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自由體積影響。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：材料狀態會影響分子擴散而非只有溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess free-volume effects. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Material state influences molecular diffusion beyond temperature alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料狀態會影響分子擴散而非只有溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Material state influences molecular diffusion beyond temperature alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。 應回到「自由體積影響」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess free-volume effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自由體積影響」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess free-volume effects: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-12-k1","title":"自由體積影響的原理","titleEn":"Assess free-volume effects principle","text":"材料狀態會影響分子擴散而非只有溫度。","textEn":"Material state influences molecular diffusion beyond temperature alone."},{"id":"a033-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","textEn":"Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自由體積影響」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess free-volume effects?","options":["曝光劑量相同就能排除所有尺寸差。","頂視開口就證明孔底完全沒有殘膠。","材料狀態會影響分子擴散而非只有溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal dose rules out every dimensional difference.","A top-view opening proves no bottom scum.","Material state influences molecular diffusion beyond temperature alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料狀態會影響分子擴散而非只有溫度。 擴散長度與反應速率是不同參數，藉獨立圖案或時間實驗才能避免把反應加快誤判為酸移動更遠。","explanationEn":"Material state influences molecular diffusion beyond temperature alone. Diffusion length and reaction rate are different parameters; independent spatial or time experiments avoid confusing faster reaction with farther transport."}}]},{"id":"a033-stage03","order":3,"title":"圖案與隨機性","titleEn":"Patterning and stochasticity","description":"在「圖案與隨機性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for patterning and stochasticity, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a033-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-12"],"title":"感度解析度粗糙度","titleEn":"Compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness","objective":"完成「感度解析度粗糙度」的因果圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：感度解析度粗糙度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：降低曝光劑量不保證同時提升解析度與粗糙度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 以理想 Poisson 事件模型比較平均事件數 100 與 25 的相對波動 1/√N；說明這是光子統計類比，不能直接當成實際缺陷率。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Lower dose does not guarantee better resolution and roughness together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Use an ideal Poisson model to compare relative fluctuation 1/√N for mean counts 100 and 25. Explain that this photon-statistics analogy is not an actual defect-rate prediction.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「降低曝光劑量不保證同時提升解析度與粗糙度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lower dose does not guarantee better resolution and roughness together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「感度解析度粗糙度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「感度解析度粗糙度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-13-k1","title":"感度解析度粗糙度的原理","titleEn":"Compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness principle","text":"降低曝光劑量不保證同時提升解析度與粗糙度。","textEn":"Lower dose does not guarantee better resolution and roughness together."},{"id":"a033-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「感度解析度粗糙度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sensitivity-resolution-roughness?","options":["降低曝光劑量不保證同時提升解析度與粗糙度。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose does not guarantee better resolution and roughness together.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低曝光劑量不保證同時提升解析度與粗糙度。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Lower dose does not guarantee better resolution and roughness together. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}},{"id":"a033-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-13"],"title":"溶解對比","titleEn":"Measure dissolution contrast","objective":"完成「溶解對比」的對照表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure dissolution contrast, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溶解對比。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：去保護比例與實際溶解速率需以資料連結。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure dissolution contrast. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Deprotection fraction needs empirical connection to dissolution rate. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去保護比例與實際溶解速率需以資料連結。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Deprotection fraction needs empirical connection to dissolution rate. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「溶解對比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure dissolution contrast and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溶解對比」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure dissolution contrast: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-14-k1","title":"溶解對比的原理","titleEn":"Measure dissolution contrast principle","text":"去保護比例與實際溶解速率需以資料連結。","textEn":"Deprotection fraction needs empirical connection to dissolution rate."},{"id":"a033-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溶解對比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure dissolution contrast?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","去保護比例與實際溶解速率需以資料連結。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Deprotection fraction needs empirical connection to dissolution rate.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"去保護比例與實際溶解速率需以資料連結。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Deprotection fraction needs empirical connection to dissolution rate. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}},{"id":"a033-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-14"],"title":"線邊粗糙","titleEn":"Assess line-edge roughness","objective":"完成「線邊粗糙」的敏感度草圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess line-edge roughness, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：線邊粗糙。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：粗糙度需指定量測長度、濾波及取樣。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess line-edge roughness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Roughness requires specified evaluation length, filtering and sampling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粗糙度需指定量測長度、濾波及取樣。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Roughness requires specified evaluation length, filtering and sampling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「線邊粗糙」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess line-edge roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「線邊粗糙」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess line-edge roughness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-15-k1","title":"線邊粗糙的原理","titleEn":"Assess line-edge roughness principle","text":"粗糙度需指定量測長度、濾波及取樣。","textEn":"Roughness requires specified evaluation length, filtering and sampling."},{"id":"a033-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「線邊粗糙」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess line-edge roughness?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","粗糙度需指定量測長度、濾波及取樣。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Roughness requires specified evaluation length, filtering and sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粗糙度需指定量測長度、濾波及取樣。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Roughness requires specified evaluation length, filtering and sampling. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}},{"id":"a033-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-15"],"title":"缺孔與橋接","titleEn":"Classify missing and bridged features","objective":"完成「缺孔與橋接」的故障判別表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for classify missing and bridged features, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺孔與橋接。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：平均線寬可能掩蓋離散圖案失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify missing and bridged features. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Mean linewidth can conceal discrete pattern failures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均線寬可能掩蓋離散圖案失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean linewidth can conceal discrete pattern failures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「缺孔與橋接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify missing and bridged features and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺孔與橋接」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for classify missing and bridged features: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-16-k1","title":"缺孔與橋接的原理","titleEn":"Classify missing and bridged features principle","text":"平均線寬可能掩蓋離散圖案失效。","textEn":"Mean linewidth can conceal discrete pattern failures."},{"id":"a033-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺孔與橋接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify missing and bridged features?","options":["平均線寬可能掩蓋離散圖案失效。","較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Mean linewidth can conceal discrete pattern failures.","Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均線寬可能掩蓋離散圖案失效。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Mean linewidth can conceal discrete pattern failures. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}},{"id":"a033-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-16"],"title":"配方相分離","titleEn":"Inspect phase separation","objective":"完成「配方相分離」的量測規劃，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect phase separation, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：配方相分離。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：添加物分布不均可形成局部反應差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect phase separation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Nonuniform additive distribution can create local reaction differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「添加物分布不均可形成局部反應差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nonuniform additive distribution can create local reaction differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「配方相分離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect phase separation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「配方相分離」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect phase separation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-17-k1","title":"配方相分離的原理","titleEn":"Inspect phase separation principle","text":"添加物分布不均可形成局部反應差異。","textEn":"Nonuniform additive distribution can create local reaction differences."},{"id":"a033-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「配方相分離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect phase separation?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","添加物分布不均可形成局部反應差異。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Nonuniform additive distribution can create local reaction differences.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"添加物分布不均可形成局部反應差異。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Nonuniform additive distribution can create local reaction differences. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}},{"id":"a033-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-17"],"title":"顯影膨潤","titleEn":"Assess development swelling","objective":"完成「顯影膨潤」的工程驗收單，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess development swelling, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：顯影膨潤。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：溶劑進入膜內可能先改變形貌再溶解。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess development swelling. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Solvent ingress can change morphology before dissolution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶劑進入膜內可能先改變形貌再溶解。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Solvent ingress can change morphology before dissolution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。 應回到「顯影膨潤」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess development swelling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「顯影膨潤」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess development swelling: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-18-k1","title":"顯影膨潤的原理","titleEn":"Assess development swelling principle","text":"溶劑進入膜內可能先改變形貌再溶解。","textEn":"Solvent ingress can change morphology before dissolution."},{"id":"a033-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","textEn":"Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「顯影膨潤」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess development swelling?","options":["較低劑量必定同時改善解析度與粗糙度。","平均線寬合格即可忽略橋接與缺孔。","溶劑進入膜內可能先改變形貌再溶解。"],"optionsEn":["Lower dose must improve resolution and roughness together.","Acceptable mean width permits ignoring bridges and missing holes.","Solvent ingress can change morphology before dissolution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溶劑進入膜內可能先改變形貌再溶解。 平均化學反應與少量事件的隨機分布需分開看，低曝光劑量可能增加局部缺陷的不確定度。","explanationEn":"Solvent ingress can change morphology before dissolution. Separate average chemistry from sparse-event statistics; low dose can increase uncertainty in local defect formation."}}]},{"id":"a033-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合及材料評估","titleEn":"Integration and material assessment","description":"在「整合及材料評估」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for integration and material assessment, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a033-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-18"],"title":"蝕刻耐受","titleEn":"Assess etch resistance","objective":"完成「蝕刻耐受」的因果圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess etch resistance, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：蝕刻耐受。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：高感度材料仍需要足夠圖案轉移耐受。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess etch resistance. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Sensitive materials still need sufficient pattern-transfer durability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高感度材料仍需要足夠圖案轉移耐受。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sensitive materials still need sufficient pattern-transfer durability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「蝕刻耐受」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess etch resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「蝕刻耐受」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess etch resistance: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-19-k1","title":"蝕刻耐受的原理","titleEn":"Assess etch resistance principle","text":"高感度材料仍需要足夠圖案轉移耐受。","textEn":"Sensitive materials still need sufficient pattern-transfer durability."},{"id":"a033-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「蝕刻耐受」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess etch resistance?","options":["高感度材料仍需要足夠圖案轉移耐受。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Sensitive materials still need sufficient pattern-transfer durability.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高感度材料仍需要足夠圖案轉移耐受。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Sensitive materials still need sufficient pattern-transfer durability. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}},{"id":"a033-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-19"],"title":"逸氣與殘留","titleEn":"Review outgassing and residue","objective":"完成「逸氣與殘留」的對照表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for review outgassing and residue, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：逸氣與殘留。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：曝光或加熱釋出物可能影響設備與介面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review outgassing and residue. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Exposure or thermal outgassing can affect equipment and interfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「曝光或加熱釋出物可能影響設備與介面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Exposure or thermal outgassing can affect equipment and interfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「逸氣與殘留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review outgassing and residue and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「逸氣與殘留」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for review outgassing and residue: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-20-k1","title":"逸氣與殘留的原理","titleEn":"Review outgassing and residue principle","text":"曝光或加熱釋出物可能影響設備與介面。","textEn":"Exposure or thermal outgassing can affect equipment and interfaces."},{"id":"a033-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「逸氣與殘留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review outgassing and residue?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","曝光或加熱釋出物可能影響設備與介面。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","Exposure or thermal outgassing can affect equipment and interfaces.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"曝光或加熱釋出物可能影響設備與介面。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Exposure or thermal outgassing can affect equipment and interfaces. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}},{"id":"a033-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-20"],"title":"保存與老化","titleEn":"Assess storage aging","objective":"完成「保存與老化」的敏感度草圖，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess storage aging, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：保存與老化。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：配方性能需附批次、儲存條件及使用時點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess storage aging. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Performance needs lot, storage conditions and time-of-use metadata. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「配方性能需附批次、儲存條件及使用時點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Performance needs lot, storage conditions and time-of-use metadata. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「保存與老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess storage aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「保存與老化」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess storage aging: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-21-k1","title":"保存與老化的原理","titleEn":"Assess storage aging principle","text":"配方性能需附批次、儲存條件及使用時點。","textEn":"Performance needs lot, storage conditions and time-of-use metadata."},{"id":"a033-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「保存與老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess storage aging?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","配方性能需附批次、儲存條件及使用時點。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Performance needs lot, storage conditions and time-of-use metadata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配方性能需附批次、儲存條件及使用時點。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Performance needs lot, storage conditions and time-of-use metadata. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}},{"id":"a033-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-21"],"title":"組成實驗設計","titleEn":"Design mixture experiments","objective":"完成「組成實驗設計」的故障判別表，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for design mixture experiments, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：組成實驗設計。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：配方比例互相耦合，不能當作完全獨立變數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design mixture experiments. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Composition fractions are coupled rather than fully independent variables. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「配方比例互相耦合，不能當作完全獨立變數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Composition fractions are coupled rather than fully independent variables. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「組成實驗設計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design mixture experiments and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「組成實驗設計」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for design mixture experiments: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-22-k1","title":"組成實驗設計的原理","titleEn":"Design mixture experiments principle","text":"配方比例互相耦合，不能當作完全獨立變數。","textEn":"Composition fractions are coupled rather than fully independent variables."},{"id":"a033-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「組成實驗設計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design mixture experiments?","options":["配方比例互相耦合，不能當作完全獨立變數。","顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Composition fractions are coupled rather than fully independent variables.","Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"配方比例互相耦合，不能當作完全獨立變數。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Composition fractions are coupled rather than fully independent variables. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}},{"id":"a033-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-22"],"title":"資料與配方邊界","titleEn":"Distinguish model from proprietary recipe","objective":"完成「資料與配方邊界」的量測規劃，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for distinguish model from proprietary recipe, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：資料與配方邊界。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：公開原理能支持假說，但不能補出未公開配方。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish model from proprietary recipe. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Public principles support hypotheses but do not reveal proprietary formulations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「公開原理能支持假說，但不能補出未公開配方。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Public principles support hypotheses but do not reveal proprietary formulations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「資料與配方邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish model from proprietary recipe and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「資料與配方邊界」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for distinguish model from proprietary recipe: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-23-k1","title":"資料與配方邊界的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish model from proprietary recipe principle","text":"公開原理能支持假說，但不能補出未公開配方。","textEn":"Public principles support hypotheses but do not reveal proprietary formulations."},{"id":"a033-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「資料與配方邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish model from proprietary recipe?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","公開原理能支持假說，但不能補出未公開配方。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","Public principles support hypotheses but do not reveal proprietary formulations.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開原理能支持假說，但不能補出未公開配方。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Public principles support hypotheses but do not reveal proprietary formulations. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}},{"id":"a033-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-car","v8a-acid","v8a-pag","v8a-resist","v8a-peb","v8a-develop"],"prerequisiteIds":["a033-v8-23"],"title":"光阻材料評估","titleEn":"Deliver a resist assessment","objective":"完成「光阻材料評估」的工程驗收單，把PAG、淬熄、反應擴散與隨機性中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for deliver a resist assessment, connecting relevant limits in pag, quenching, reaction-diffusion and stochasticity to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光阻材料評估。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：需用相同曝光、顯影及蝕刻基準比較候選材料。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Deliver a resist assessment. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Compare candidate materials with matched exposure, development and etch baselines. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「需用相同曝光、顯影及蝕刻基準比較候選材料。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Compare candidate materials with matched exposure, development and etch baselines. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。 應回到「光阻材料評估」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Developer compatibility follows directly from color. Revisit assumptions and sampling for deliver a resist assessment and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光阻材料評估」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for deliver a resist assessment: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a033-v8-24-k1","title":"光阻材料評估的原理","titleEn":"Deliver a resist assessment principle","text":"需用相同曝光、顯影及蝕刻基準比較候選材料。","textEn":"Compare candidate materials with matched exposure, development and etch baselines."},{"id":"a033-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","textEn":"Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光阻材料評估」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating deliver a resist assessment?","options":["顯影液相容性可由顏色直接判斷。","增加酸擴散永遠只會改善圖案。","需用相同曝光、顯影及蝕刻基準比較候選材料。"],"optionsEn":["Developer compatibility follows directly from color.","More acid diffusion can only improve patterns.","Compare candidate materials with matched exposure, development and etch baselines."],"answer":2,"explanation":"需用相同曝光、顯影及蝕刻基準比較候選材料。 候選配方的解析度、粗糙度、感度及蝕刻耐受需在同一基準下比較，不能混用不同最佳條件宣稱全面勝出。","explanationEn":"Compare candidate materials with matched exposure, development and etch baselines. Compare resolution, roughness, sensitivity and etch resistance on the same baseline rather than mixing best conditions to claim universal superiority."}}]}],"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography"},{"id":"a034","title":"極紫外金屬氧化物光阻研究","titleEn":"EUV metal-oxide resist research","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究吸收與反應路徑、塗膜與表面、曝光與統計、轉移與驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: absorption and reaction, coating and surfaces, exposure and statistics, transfer and validation. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["吸收與反應路徑","塗膜與表面","曝光與統計","轉移與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Absorption and reaction","Coating and surfaces","Exposure and statistics","Transfer and validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a034-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"吸收與反應路徑","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction","description":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","descriptionEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists.","steps":[{"id":"a034-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出光子到溶解度的因果鏈","titleEn":"Trace photons to changed solubility","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Absorption and chemical conversion are different events.","instruction":"畫出光子到溶解度的因果鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace photons to changed solubility. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Absorption and chemical conversion are different events.","observation":"吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Absorption and chemical conversion are different events. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出光子到溶解度的因果鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace photons to changed solubility\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Absorption and chemical conversion are different events.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。","textEn":"Absorption and chemical conversion are different events."},{"id":"a034-v8-01-k2","title":"吸收與反應路徑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction: principle and limits","text":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","textEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出光子到溶解度的因果鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace photons to changed solubility\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。"],"optionsEn":["Absorption and chemical conversion are different events.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸收與化學轉換不是同一事件。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Absorption and chemical conversion are different events. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}},{"id":"a034-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-01"],"title":"比較有機與金屬氧化物光阻的元素角色","titleEn":"Compare elemental roles in organic and metal-oxide resists","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料分類不能單獨預測感度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material class alone does not predict sensitivity.","instruction":"比較有機與金屬氧化物光阻的元素角色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「材料分類不能單獨預測感度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare elemental roles in organic and metal-oxide resists. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material class alone does not predict sensitivity.","observation":"材料分類不能單獨預測感度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material class alone does not predict sensitivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較有機與金屬氧化物光阻的元素角色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料分類不能單獨預測感度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare elemental roles in organic and metal-oxide resists\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material class alone does not predict sensitivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料分類不能單獨預測感度。","textEn":"Material class alone does not predict sensitivity."},{"id":"a034-v8-02-k2","title":"吸收與反應路徑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction: principle and limits","text":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","textEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較有機與金屬氧化物光阻的元素角色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare elemental roles in organic and metal-oxide resists\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","材料分類不能單獨預測感度。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。"],"optionsEn":["Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Material class alone does not predict sensitivity.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料分類不能單獨預測感度。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Material class alone does not predict sensitivity. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}},{"id":"a034-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-02"],"title":"分開金屬核心與配體的功能","titleEn":"Separate metal-core and ligand functions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions.","instruction":"分開金屬核心與配體的功能。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate metal-core and ligand functions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions.","observation":"配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開金屬核心與配體的功能」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate metal-core and ligand functions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。","textEn":"Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions."},{"id":"a034-v8-03-k2","title":"吸收與反應路徑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction: principle and limits","text":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","textEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開金屬核心與配體的功能」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate metal-core and ligand functions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。"],"optionsEn":["Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配體會改變成膜及曝光後反應。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Ligands affect film formation and post-exposure reactions. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}},{"id":"a034-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-03"],"title":"以假設吸收係數計算厚度衰減","titleEn":"Calculate attenuation using an assumed absorption coefficient","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film.","instruction":"以假設吸收係數計算厚度衰減。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設均勻膜的吸收係數 α=0.020 nm⁻¹、厚度 t=20 nm、入射光子數 100。計算 T=exp(-αt)=0.6703，約 67.0 個等效光子穿透、33.0 個被吸收；厚度改為 40 nm 時吸收比例為 55.1%。比較吸收增加與實際化學轉換兩件事，不能由此計算單獨宣告感度或缺陷率。","instructionEn":"Calculate attenuation using an assumed absorption coefficient. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a uniform-film absorption coefficient α=0.020 nm⁻¹, thickness t=20 nm and 100 incident equivalent photons. T=exp(-αt)=0.6703 gives 67.0 transmitted and 33.0 absorbed. At 40 nm, absorption becomes 55.1%. Separate increased absorption from chemical conversion; this calculation alone establishes neither sensitivity nor defect rate.","observation":"Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n結果須有 33.0% 與 55.1%，並註明反應產率尚未量測。","observationEn":"Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 33.0% and 55.1%, explicitly noting that reaction yield is unmeasured.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以假設吸收係數計算厚度衰減」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：結果須有 33.0% 與 55.1%，並註明反應產率尚未量測。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate attenuation using an assumed absorption coefficient\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 33.0% and 55.1%, explicitly noting that reaction yield is unmeasured.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。","textEn":"Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film."},{"id":"a034-v8-04-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設均勻膜的吸收係數 α=0.020 nm⁻¹、厚度 t=20 nm、入射光子數 100。計算 T=exp(-αt)=0.6703，約 67.0 個等效光子穿透、33.0 個被吸收；厚度改為 40 nm 時吸收比例為 55.1%。比較吸收增加與實際化學轉換兩件事，不能由此計算單獨宣告感度或缺陷率。","textEn":"Assume a uniform-film absorption coefficient α=0.020 nm⁻¹, thickness t=20 nm and 100 incident equivalent photons. T=exp(-αt)=0.6703 gives 67.0 transmitted and 33.0 absorbed. At 40 nm, absorption becomes 55.1%. Separate increased absorption from chemical conversion; this calculation alone establishes neither sensitivity nor defect rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以假設吸收係數計算厚度衰減」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate attenuation using an assumed absorption coefficient\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。"],"optionsEn":["Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Beer–Lambert 模型須標明均勻薄膜假設。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Beer–Lambert modeling assumes a uniform film. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設均勻膜的吸收係數 α=0.020 nm⁻¹、厚度 t=20 nm、入射光子數 100。計算 T=exp(-αt)=0.6703，約 67.0 個等效光子穿透、33.0 個被吸收；厚度改為 40 nm 時吸收比例為 55.1%。比較吸收增加與實際化學轉換兩件事，不能由此計算單獨宣告感度或缺陷率。","textEn":"Assume a uniform-film absorption coefficient α=0.020 nm⁻¹, thickness t=20 nm and 100 incident equivalent photons. T=exp(-αt)=0.6703 gives 67.0 transmitted and 33.0 absorbed. At 40 nm, absorption becomes 55.1%. Separate increased absorption from chemical conversion; this calculation alone establishes neither sensitivity nor defect rate.","check":"結果須有 33.0% 與 55.1%，並註明反應產率尚未量測。","checkEn":"Report 33.0% and 55.1%, explicitly noting that reaction yield is unmeasured."}},{"id":"a034-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-04"],"title":"將曝光反應與烘烤反應分欄","titleEn":"Separate exposure and bake reactions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Post-exposure history can alter final solubility.","instruction":"將曝光反應與烘烤反應分欄。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate exposure and bake reactions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Post-exposure history can alter final solubility.","observation":"後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Post-exposure history can alter final solubility. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將曝光反應與烘烤反應分欄」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate exposure and bake reactions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Post-exposure history can alter final solubility.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。","textEn":"Post-exposure history can alter final solubility."},{"id":"a034-v8-05-k2","title":"吸收與反應路徑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction: principle and limits","text":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","textEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將曝光反應與烘烤反應分欄」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate exposure and bake reactions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。"],"optionsEn":["Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Post-exposure history can alter final solubility.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"後曝光歷程可能改變最終溶解度。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Post-exposure history can alter final solubility. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}},{"id":"a034-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-05"],"title":"建立配方批次與量測追溯表","titleEn":"Build a formulation-batch measurement ledger","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner.","instruction":"建立配方批次與量測追溯表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a formulation-batch measurement ledger. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner.","observation":"批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立配方批次與量測追溯表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a formulation-batch measurement ledger\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。","textEn":"Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner."},{"id":"a034-v8-06-k2","title":"吸收與反應路徑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and reaction: principle and limits","text":"金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","textEn":"Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立配方批次與量測追溯表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a formulation-batch measurement ledger\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。"],"optionsEn":["Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner."],"answer":2,"explanation":"批次差異不能全歸因於曝光機。 金屬氧化物光阻的吸收、配體反應與不溶化必須分開驗證。","explanationEn":"Batch variation cannot all be attributed to the scanner. Absorption, ligand reactions and insolubilization require separate evidence in metal-oxide resists."}}]},{"id":"a034-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"塗膜與表面","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces","description":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","descriptionEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together.","steps":[{"id":"a034-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-06"],"title":"繪製中心到邊緣的膜厚取樣網格","titleEn":"Map center-to-edge film-thickness sampling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity.","instruction":"繪製中心到邊緣的膜厚取樣網格。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map center-to-edge film-thickness sampling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity.","observation":"單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製中心到邊緣的膜厚取樣網格」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map center-to-edge film-thickness sampling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。","textEn":"One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity."},{"id":"a034-v8-07-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製中心到邊緣的膜厚取樣網格」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map center-to-edge film-thickness sampling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單點膜厚無法證明晶圓均勻性。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"One thickness point cannot establish wafer uniformity. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}},{"id":"a034-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-07"],"title":"比較兩種底層上的接觸角證據","titleEn":"Compare wetting evidence on two underlayers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface energy influences wetting and defects.","instruction":"比較兩種底層上的接觸角證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare wetting evidence on two underlayers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface energy influences wetting and defects.","observation":"表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface energy influences wetting and defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較兩種底層上的接觸角證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare wetting evidence on two underlayers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface energy influences wetting and defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。","textEn":"Surface energy influences wetting and defects."},{"id":"a034-v8-08-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較兩種底層上的接觸角證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare wetting evidence on two underlayers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Surface energy influences wetting and defects.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面能會影響潤濕與缺陷。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"Surface energy influences wetting and defects. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}},{"id":"a034-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-08"],"title":"用空白片分辨顆粒與圖案缺陷","titleEn":"Distinguish particles from pattern defects using blanks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream.","instruction":"用空白片分辨顆粒與圖案缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish particles from pattern defects using blanks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream.","observation":"曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用空白片分辨顆粒與圖案缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish particles from pattern defects using blanks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。","textEn":"Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream."},{"id":"a034-v8-09-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用空白片分辨顆粒與圖案缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish particles from pattern defects using blanks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曝光前缺陷可在後續被放大。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"Pre-exposure defects can be amplified downstream. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}},{"id":"a034-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-09"],"title":"對照曝光前後的光譜變化","titleEn":"Compare spectra before and after exposure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment.","instruction":"對照曝光前後的光譜變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare spectra before and after exposure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment.","observation":"光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對照曝光前後的光譜變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare spectra before and after exposure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。","textEn":"Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment."},{"id":"a034-v8-10-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對照曝光前後的光譜變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare spectra before and after exposure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。","相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment.","Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光譜改變需要對應可辨識的化學訊號。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"Spectral changes need an identifiable chemical assignment. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}},{"id":"a034-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-10"],"title":"規畫金屬污染與交叉污染監控","titleEn":"Plan metal and cross-contamination monitoring","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity.","instruction":"規畫金屬污染與交叉污染監控。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan metal and cross-contamination monitoring. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity.","observation":"成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫金屬污染與交叉污染監控」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan metal and cross-contamination monitoring\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。","textEn":"Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity."},{"id":"a034-v8-11-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫金屬污染與交叉污染監控」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan metal and cross-contamination monitoring\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"成像材料的金屬含量也構成整合問題。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"Metal content creates an integration issue as well as an imaging opportunity. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}},{"id":"a034-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-11"],"title":"建立膜厚與顯影殘留的對照圖","titleEn":"Relate film thickness to development residue","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility.","instruction":"建立膜厚與顯影殘留的對照圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate film thickness to development residue. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility.","observation":"殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立膜厚與顯影殘留的對照圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate film thickness to development residue\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。","textEn":"Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility."},{"id":"a034-v8-12-k2","title":"塗膜與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Coating and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","textEn":"Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立膜厚與顯影殘留的對照圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate film thickness to development residue\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同厚度就表示化學組成相同。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal chemical composition.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘留可能來自不完全溶解或底層相容性。 薄膜厚度與組成會同時影響吸收、顆粒及顯影結果。","explanationEn":"Residue can reflect incomplete dissolution or underlayer compatibility. Film thickness and composition affect absorption, particles and development together."}}]},{"id":"a034-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"曝光與統計","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics","description":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","descriptionEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges.","steps":[{"id":"a034-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-12"],"title":"設計劑量與焦距的二維矩陣","titleEn":"Design a dose–focus matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: An optimum point is not a broad process window.","instruction":"設計劑量與焦距的二維矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Design a dose–focus matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: An optimum point is not a broad process window.","observation":"最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"An optimum point is not a broad process window. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計劑量與焦距的二維矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Design a dose–focus matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"An optimum point is not a broad process window.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。","textEn":"An optimum point is not a broad process window."},{"id":"a034-v8-13-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計劑量與焦距的二維矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Design a dose–focus matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。"],"optionsEn":["An optimum point is not a broad process window.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"最佳單點不等於具有寬製程窗口。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"An optimum point is not a broad process window. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}},{"id":"a034-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-13"],"title":"分別標記正負光阻的保留區","titleEn":"Mark retained regions for positive and negative tones","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism.","instruction":"分別標記正負光阻的保留區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark retained regions for positive and negative tones. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism.","observation":"顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分別標記正負光阻的保留區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark retained regions for positive and negative tones\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。","textEn":"Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism."},{"id":"a034-v8-14-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分別標記正負光阻的保留區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark retained regions for positive and negative tones\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。"],"optionsEn":["Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"顯影後保留區取決於反應與顯影機制。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"Retention depends on reaction and development mechanism. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}},{"id":"a034-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-14"],"title":"量測邊緣粗糙度並標示取樣長度","titleEn":"Measure edge roughness with a stated sampling length","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling.","instruction":"量測邊緣粗糙度並標示取樣長度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure edge roughness with a stated sampling length. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling.","observation":"粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測邊緣粗糙度並標示取樣長度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure edge roughness with a stated sampling length\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。","textEn":"Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling."},{"id":"a034-v8-15-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測邊緣粗糙度並標示取樣長度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure edge roughness with a stated sampling length\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粗糙度數值受量測頻寬與取樣影響。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"Roughness values depend on bandwidth and sampling. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}},{"id":"a034-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-15"],"title":"統計斷線與橋接的個別發生率","titleEn":"Count breaks and bridges separately","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The two defect types can have different dose trends.","instruction":"統計斷線與橋接的個別發生率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Count breaks and bridges separately. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The two defect types can have different dose trends.","observation":"兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The two defect types can have different dose trends. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「統計斷線與橋接的個別發生率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Count breaks and bridges separately\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The two defect types can have different dose trends.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。","textEn":"The two defect types can have different dose trends."},{"id":"a034-v8-16-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「統計斷線與橋接的個別發生率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Count breaks and bridges separately\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。","只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。"],"optionsEn":["The two defect types can have different dose trends.","Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種缺陷可能對劑量有不同趨勢。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"The two defect types can have different dose trends. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}},{"id":"a034-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-16"],"title":"為零缺陷樣本計算統計上限","titleEn":"Estimate an upper bound for zero observed defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate.","instruction":"為零缺陷樣本計算統計上限。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate an upper bound for zero observed defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate.","observation":"零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為零缺陷樣本計算統計上限」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate an upper bound for zero observed defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。","textEn":"Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate."},{"id":"a034-v8-17-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為零缺陷樣本計算統計上限」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate an upper bound for zero observed defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。"],"optionsEn":["Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"零觀察不等於真實發生率為零。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"Zero observations do not imply a zero true rate. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}},{"id":"a034-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-17"],"title":"比較相同線寬下的不同曝光條件","titleEn":"Compare exposure conditions at matched linewidth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding.","instruction":"比較相同線寬下的不同曝光條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare exposure conditions at matched linewidth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding.","observation":"同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較相同線寬下的不同曝光條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare exposure conditions at matched linewidth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。","textEn":"Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding."},{"id":"a034-v8-18-k2","title":"曝光與統計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and statistics: principle and limits","text":"平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","textEn":"Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較相同線寬下的不同曝光條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare exposure conditions at matched linewidth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只看平均線寬即可排除罕見缺陷。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。"],"optionsEn":["Mean linewidth alone rules out rare defects.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同線寬比較可減少幾何混淆。 平均線寬不能取代斷線與橋接等罕見事件的統計。","explanationEn":"Matched linewidth reduces geometric confounding. Mean linewidth cannot replace rare-event statistics for breaks and bridges."}}]},{"id":"a034-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"轉移與驗證","titleEn":"Transfer and validation","description":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","descriptionEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels.","steps":[{"id":"a034-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-18"],"title":"追蹤光阻到硬罩的尺寸偏差","titleEn":"Trace dimensional bias from resist to hard mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness.","instruction":"追蹤光阻到硬罩的尺寸偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace dimensional bias from resist to hard mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness.","observation":"蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤光阻到硬罩的尺寸偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace dimensional bias from resist to hard mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。","textEn":"Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness."},{"id":"a034-v8-19-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤光阻到硬罩的尺寸偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace dimensional bias from resist to hard mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"蝕刻可能放大或縮小原始粗糙度。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"Etching can amplify or reduce initial roughness. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}},{"id":"a034-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-19"],"title":"檢查薄光阻的遮罩消耗預算","titleEn":"Check the consumption budget of a thin resist mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance.","instruction":"檢查薄光阻的遮罩消耗預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check the consumption budget of a thin resist mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance.","observation":"薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查薄光阻的遮罩消耗預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check the consumption budget of a thin resist mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。","textEn":"Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance."},{"id":"a034-v8-20-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查薄光阻的遮罩消耗預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check the consumption budget of a thin resist mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄膜提升圖案穩定性仍須滿足轉移耐受性。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"Thin films still require sufficient transfer resistance. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}},{"id":"a034-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-20"],"title":"將蛇形線導通對應至斷線位置","titleEn":"Relate serpentine continuity to break locations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電性測試與影像提供互補證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence.","instruction":"將蛇形線導通對應至斷線位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「電性測試與影像提供互補證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate serpentine continuity to break locations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence.","observation":"電性測試與影像提供互補證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將蛇形線導通對應至斷線位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電性測試與影像提供互補證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate serpentine continuity to break locations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電性測試與影像提供互補證據。","textEn":"Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence."},{"id":"a034-v8-21-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將蛇形線導通對應至斷線位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate serpentine continuity to break locations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","電性測試與影像提供互補證據。"],"optionsEn":["A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性測試與影像提供互補證據。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"Electrical tests and images provide complementary evidence. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}},{"id":"a034-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-21"],"title":"將梳狀漏電對應至橋接位置","titleEn":"Relate comb leakage to bridge locations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity.","instruction":"將梳狀漏電對應至橋接位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate comb leakage to bridge locations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity.","observation":"橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將梳狀漏電對應至橋接位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate comb leakage to bridge locations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。","textEn":"The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity."},{"id":"a034-v8-22-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將梳狀漏電對應至橋接位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate comb leakage to bridge locations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。","光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity.","A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"橋接缺陷的危害取決於網路連接。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"The impact of a bridge depends on network connectivity. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}},{"id":"a034-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-22"],"title":"比較研究展示與可量產證據","titleEn":"Distinguish research demonstrations from production evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local yield is not whole-product yield.","instruction":"比較研究展示與可量產證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish research demonstrations from production evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local yield is not whole-product yield.","observation":"局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local yield is not whole-product yield. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較研究展示與可量產證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish research demonstrations from production evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local yield is not whole-product yield.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。","textEn":"Local yield is not whole-product yield."},{"id":"a034-v8-23-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較研究展示與可量產證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish research demonstrations from production evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Local yield is not whole-product yield.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部良率不能代表整個產品的良率。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"Local yield is not whole-product yield. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}},{"id":"a034-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mor","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a034-v8-23"],"title":"提出包含化學、圖形與電性的材料審查","titleEn":"Review chemistry, pattern and electrical evidence together","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料選擇應由多層證據支持。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence.","instruction":"提出包含化學、圖形與電性的材料審查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「材料選擇應由多層證據支持。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review chemistry, pattern and electrical evidence together. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence.","observation":"材料選擇應由多層證據支持。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提出包含化學、圖形與電性的材料審查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料選擇應由多層證據支持。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review chemistry, pattern and electrical evidence together\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a034-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料選擇應由多層證據支持。","textEn":"Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence."},{"id":"a034-v8-24-k2","title":"轉移與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transfer and validation: principle and limits","text":"光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","textEn":"Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提出包含化學、圖形與電性的材料審查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review chemistry, pattern and electrical evidence together\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光阻影像正常即可保證互連導通。","吸收更多就必定具有較低缺陷。","材料選擇應由多層證據支持。"],"optionsEn":["A good resist image guarantees conductive interconnects.","Greater absorption necessarily guarantees fewer defects.","Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料選擇應由多層證據支持。 光阻圖案、硬罩圖案與金屬電性是不同驗證層次。","explanationEn":"Material selection needs multiple levels of evidence. Resist patterns, hard-mask patterns and metal electrical behavior are distinct validation levels."}}]}]},{"id":"a035","title":"光罩電子束寫入","titleEn":"Electron-beam mask writing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究資料與尺度、束流與定位、劑量與拼接、光罩驗收；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: data and scale, beam and placement, dose and stitching, mask acceptance. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["資料與尺度","束流與定位","劑量與拼接","光罩驗收"],"labelsEn":["Data and scale","Beam and placement","Dose and stitching","Mask acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a035-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"資料與尺度","titleEn":"Data and scale","description":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","descriptionEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction.","steps":[{"id":"a035-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"將晶圓目標依縮小倍率轉成光罩座標","titleEn":"Convert wafer targets into mask coordinates using reduction","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales.","instruction":"將晶圓目標依縮小倍率轉成光罩座標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Convert wafer targets into mask coordinates using reduction. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales.","observation":"光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將晶圓目標依縮小倍率轉成光罩座標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Convert wafer targets into mask coordinates using reduction\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。","textEn":"Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales."},{"id":"a035-v8-01-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將晶圓目標依縮小倍率轉成光罩座標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Convert wafer targets into mask coordinates using reduction\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。"],"optionsEn":["Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光罩與晶圓座標必須註明尺度。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Mask and wafer coordinates require explicit scales. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}},{"id":"a035-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-01"],"title":"檢查版圖多邊形的自交與空隙","titleEn":"Check layout polygons for self-intersections and gaps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Topology errors can become printable defects.","instruction":"檢查版圖多邊形的自交與空隙。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check layout polygons for self-intersections and gaps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Topology errors can become printable defects.","observation":"資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Topology errors can become printable defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查版圖多邊形的自交與空隙」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check layout polygons for self-intersections and gaps\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Topology errors can become printable defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。","textEn":"Topology errors can become printable defects."},{"id":"a035-v8-02-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查版圖多邊形的自交與空隙」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check layout polygons for self-intersections and gaps\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。"],"optionsEn":["Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","Topology errors can become printable defects.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料拓樸錯誤可能形成可印缺陷。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Topology errors can become printable defects. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}},{"id":"a035-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-02"],"title":"將曲線分割成允許的寫入圖元","titleEn":"Fracture curves into allowed writing primitives","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fracturing affects edge error and writing time.","instruction":"將曲線分割成允許的寫入圖元。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Fracture curves into allowed writing primitives. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fracturing affects edge error and writing time.","observation":"資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fracturing affects edge error and writing time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將曲線分割成允許的寫入圖元」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Fracture curves into allowed writing primitives\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fracturing affects edge error and writing time.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。","textEn":"Fracturing affects edge error and writing time."},{"id":"a035-v8-03-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將曲線分割成允許的寫入圖元」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Fracture curves into allowed writing primitives\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。"],"optionsEn":["Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Fracturing affects edge error and writing time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"資料分割會影響邊緣誤差與寫入時間。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Fracturing affects edge error and writing time. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}},{"id":"a035-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-03"],"title":"比較可變形束與多束寫入資料流","titleEn":"Compare variable-shaped and multibeam data flows","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平行化改變資料與校正需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Parallelism changes data and calibration demands.","instruction":"比較可變形束與多束寫入資料流。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「平行化改變資料與校正需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare variable-shaped and multibeam data flows. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Parallelism changes data and calibration demands.","observation":"平行化改變資料與校正需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Parallelism changes data and calibration demands. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較可變形束與多束寫入資料流」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平行化改變資料與校正需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare variable-shaped and multibeam data flows\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Parallelism changes data and calibration demands.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平行化改變資料與校正需求。","textEn":"Parallelism changes data and calibration demands."},{"id":"a035-v8-04-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較可變形束與多束寫入資料流」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare variable-shaped and multibeam data flows\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平行化改變資料與校正需求。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。"],"optionsEn":["Parallelism changes data and calibration demands.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平行化改變資料與校正需求。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Parallelism changes data and calibration demands. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}},{"id":"a035-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-04"],"title":"建立關鍵圖形的寫入優先檢查清單","titleEn":"Prioritize critical patterns for writing checks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions.","instruction":"建立關鍵圖形的寫入優先檢查清單。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Prioritize critical patterns for writing checks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions.","observation":"接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立關鍵圖形的寫入優先檢查清單」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Prioritize critical patterns for writing checks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。","textEn":"Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions."},{"id":"a035-v8-05-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立關鍵圖形的寫入優先檢查清單」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Prioritize critical patterns for writing checks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。"],"optionsEn":["Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接點與線端可能比大面積區更敏感。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Contacts and line ends may be more sensitive than broad regions. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}},{"id":"a035-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-05"],"title":"追蹤設計版號到光罩工作單","titleEn":"Trace design revision into the mask job","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable.","instruction":"追蹤設計版號到光罩工作單。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace design revision into the mask job. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable.","observation":"幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤設計版號到光罩工作單」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace design revision into the mask job\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。","textEn":"Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable."},{"id":"a035-v8-06-k2","title":"資料與尺度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and scale: principle and limits","text":"光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤設計版號到光罩工作單」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace design revision into the mask job\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。"],"optionsEn":["Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何正確但版號錯誤仍是不合格。 光罩寫入誤差經投影縮小後仍參與晶圓邊緣位置誤差。","explanationEn":"Correct geometry with the wrong revision is still unacceptable. Mask-writing errors remain part of wafer edge-placement error after projection reduction."}}]},{"id":"a035-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"束流與定位","titleEn":"Beam and placement","description":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","descriptionEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics.","steps":[{"id":"a035-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-06"],"title":"分別估算束流與駐留時間的劑量","titleEn":"Estimate dose from beam current and dwell time","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Dose is charge divided by exposed area.","instruction":"分別估算束流與駐留時間的劑量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設某圖元曝光面積為 100 μm²、所需總電荷為 0.20 nC、束流為 1.0 nA。先換算 100 μm²=10⁻⁶ cm²，再得面劑量 200 μC/cm²，理想駐留總時間 Q/I=0.20 s。另有 0.10 s 載台與資料開銷時，總時間是 0.30 s；不可把理想束流時間當作整體吞吐量。","instructionEn":"Estimate dose from beam current and dwell time. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Dose is charge divided by exposed area.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a 100 μm² exposed area, total charge 0.20 nC and beam current 1.0 nA. Convert the area to 10⁻⁶ cm²: dose is 200 μC/cm² and ideal beam time Q/I is 0.20 s. With 0.10 s of stage and data overhead, total time is 0.30 s; beam time alone is not throughput.","observation":"劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n確認面積換算、200 μC/cm² 與 0.30 s，分開曝光和開銷。","observationEn":"Dose is charge divided by exposed area. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nCheck the area conversion, 200 μC/cm² and 0.30 s, separating exposure and overhead.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分別估算束流與駐留時間的劑量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：確認面積換算、200 μC/cm² 與 0.30 s，分開曝光和開銷。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate dose from beam current and dwell time\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Dose is charge divided by exposed area.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Check the area conversion, 200 μC/cm² and 0.30 s, separating exposure and overhead.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。","textEn":"Dose is charge divided by exposed area."},{"id":"a035-v8-07-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設某圖元曝光面積為 100 μm²、所需總電荷為 0.20 nC、束流為 1.0 nA。先換算 100 μm²=10⁻⁶ cm²，再得面劑量 200 μC/cm²，理想駐留總時間 Q/I=0.20 s。另有 0.10 s 載台與資料開銷時，總時間是 0.30 s；不可把理想束流時間當作整體吞吐量。","textEn":"Assume a 100 μm² exposed area, total charge 0.20 nC and beam current 1.0 nA. Convert the area to 10⁻⁶ cm²: dose is 200 μC/cm² and ideal beam time Q/I is 0.20 s. With 0.10 s of stage and data overhead, total time is 0.30 s; beam time alone is not throughput."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分別估算束流與駐留時間的劑量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate dose from beam current and dwell time\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。"],"optionsEn":["Dose is charge divided by exposed area.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"劑量是電荷除以曝光面積。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"Dose is charge divided by exposed area. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設某圖元曝光面積為 100 μm²、所需總電荷為 0.20 nC、束流為 1.0 nA。先換算 100 μm²=10⁻⁶ cm²，再得面劑量 200 μC/cm²，理想駐留總時間 Q/I=0.20 s。另有 0.10 s 載台與資料開銷時，總時間是 0.30 s；不可把理想束流時間當作整體吞吐量。","textEn":"Assume a 100 μm² exposed area, total charge 0.20 nC and beam current 1.0 nA. Convert the area to 10⁻⁶ cm²: dose is 200 μC/cm² and ideal beam time Q/I is 0.20 s. With 0.10 s of stage and data overhead, total time is 0.30 s; beam time alone is not throughput.","check":"確認面積換算、200 μC/cm² 與 0.30 s，分開曝光和開銷。","checkEn":"Check the area conversion, 200 μC/cm² and 0.30 s, separating exposure and overhead."}},{"id":"a035-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-07"],"title":"以法拉第杯量測概念檢查電流漂移","titleEn":"Use a Faraday-cup model to assess current drift","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Current drift produces time-dependent dose error.","instruction":"以法拉第杯量測概念檢查電流漂移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use a Faraday-cup model to assess current drift. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Current drift produces time-dependent dose error.","observation":"電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Current drift produces time-dependent dose error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以法拉第杯量測概念檢查電流漂移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use a Faraday-cup model to assess current drift\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Current drift produces time-dependent dose error.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。","textEn":"Current drift produces time-dependent dose error."},{"id":"a035-v8-08-k2","title":"束流與定位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Beam and placement: principle and limits","text":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","textEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以法拉第杯量測概念檢查電流漂移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use a Faraday-cup model to assess current drift\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Current drift produces time-dependent dose error.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電流漂移會造成曝光量的時間偏差。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"Current drift produces time-dependent dose error. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}},{"id":"a035-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-08"],"title":"繪製載台誤差與偏轉誤差的分工","titleEn":"Separate stage and deflection errors","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources.","instruction":"繪製載台誤差與偏轉誤差的分工。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate stage and deflection errors. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources.","observation":"大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製載台誤差與偏轉誤差的分工」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate stage and deflection errors\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。","textEn":"Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources."},{"id":"a035-v8-09-k2","title":"束流與定位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Beam and placement: principle and limits","text":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","textEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製載台誤差與偏轉誤差的分工」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate stage and deflection errors\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大行程定位與小視場偏轉具有不同誤差來源。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"Long-range positioning and field deflection have different error sources. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}},{"id":"a035-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-09"],"title":"以標記網格擬合旋轉與縮放","titleEn":"Fit rotation and scale from a mark grid","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The model needs sufficient independent marks.","instruction":"以標記網格擬合旋轉與縮放。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Fit rotation and scale from a mark grid. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The model needs sufficient independent marks.","observation":"至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The model needs sufficient independent marks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以標記網格擬合旋轉與縮放」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Fit rotation and scale from a mark grid\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The model needs sufficient independent marks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。","textEn":"The model needs sufficient independent marks."},{"id":"a035-v8-10-k2","title":"束流與定位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Beam and placement: principle and limits","text":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","textEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以標記網格擬合旋轉與縮放」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Fit rotation and scale from a mark grid\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。","較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。"],"optionsEn":["The model needs sufficient independent marks.","A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"至少需要足夠獨立標記約束模型。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"The model needs sufficient independent marks. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}},{"id":"a035-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-10"],"title":"比較熱漂移前後的座標殘差","titleEn":"Compare coordinate residuals before and after thermal drift","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift.","instruction":"比較熱漂移前後的座標殘差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare coordinate residuals before and after thermal drift. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift.","observation":"慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較熱漂移前後的座標殘差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare coordinate residuals before and after thermal drift\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。","textEn":"One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift."},{"id":"a035-v8-11-k2","title":"束流與定位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Beam and placement: principle and limits","text":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","textEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較熱漂移前後的座標殘差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare coordinate residuals before and after thermal drift\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"慢漂移不會由單次校正永久消除。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"One calibration does not permanently remove slow drift. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}},{"id":"a035-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-11"],"title":"檢查絕緣基板充電造成的偏移","titleEn":"Assess displacement caused by insulating-substrate charging","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Charging alters trajectories and local exposure.","instruction":"檢查絕緣基板充電造成的偏移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess displacement caused by insulating-substrate charging. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Charging alters trajectories and local exposure.","observation":"充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Charging alters trajectories and local exposure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查絕緣基板充電造成的偏移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess displacement caused by insulating-substrate charging\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Charging alters trajectories and local exposure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。","textEn":"Charging alters trajectories and local exposure."},{"id":"a035-v8-12-k2","title":"束流與定位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Beam and placement: principle and limits","text":"束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","textEn":"Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查絕緣基板充電造成的偏移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess displacement caused by insulating-substrate charging\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較小束斑必定代表較高吞吐量。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller beam spot necessarily means higher throughput.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","Charging alters trajectories and local exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"充電會改變電子軌跡與局部曝光。 束斑尺寸、位置與電流穩定度是不同性能量。","explanationEn":"Charging alters trajectories and local exposure. Spot size, position and current stability are distinct metrics."}}]},{"id":"a035-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"劑量與拼接","titleEn":"Dose and stitching","description":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","descriptionEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models.","steps":[{"id":"a035-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-12"],"title":"畫出前向與背向散射的作用範圍","titleEn":"Sketch forward- and backscatter ranges","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Proximity effects span different spatial scales.","instruction":"畫出前向與背向散射的作用範圍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch forward- and backscatter ranges. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Proximity effects span different spatial scales.","observation":"鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Proximity effects span different spatial scales. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出前向與背向散射的作用範圍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch forward- and backscatter ranges\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Proximity effects span different spatial scales.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。","textEn":"Proximity effects span different spatial scales."},{"id":"a035-v8-13-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出前向與背向散射的作用範圍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch forward- and backscatter ranges\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。"],"optionsEn":["Proximity effects span different spatial scales.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鄰近效應包含不同空間尺度。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Proximity effects span different spatial scales. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}},{"id":"a035-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-13"],"title":"為密集與孤立圖形比較劑量修正","titleEn":"Compare dose correction for dense and isolated features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy.","instruction":"為密集與孤立圖形比較劑量修正。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dose correction for dense and isolated features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy.","observation":"相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為密集與孤立圖形比較劑量修正」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dose correction for dense and isolated features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。","textEn":"Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy."},{"id":"a035-v8-14-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為密集與孤立圖形比較劑量修正」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dose correction for dense and isolated features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同直接劑量不代表相同總沉積能量。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Equal direct dose does not imply equal deposited energy. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}},{"id":"a035-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-14"],"title":"量測跨寫入場的接縫","titleEn":"Measure seams across writing fields","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting.","instruction":"量測跨寫入場的接縫。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure seams across writing fields. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting.","observation":"場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測跨寫入場的接縫」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure seams across writing fields\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。","textEn":"Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting."},{"id":"a035-v8-15-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測跨寫入場的接縫」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure seams across writing fields\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"場內尺寸與跨場拼接需分開報告。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Within-field size and across-field stitching need separate reporting. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}},{"id":"a035-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-15"],"title":"比較單次與多次分攤曝光","titleEn":"Compare single-pass and divided-pass writing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time.","instruction":"比較單次與多次分攤曝光。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare single-pass and divided-pass writing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time.","observation":"多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單次與多次分攤曝光」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare single-pass and divided-pass writing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。","textEn":"Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time."},{"id":"a035-v8-16-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單次與多次分攤曝光」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare single-pass and divided-pass writing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。","平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time.","Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次曝光能平均部分誤差但增加時間。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Multiple passes can average some errors while adding time. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}},{"id":"a035-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-16"],"title":"估算圖元數與移動時間的吞吐量","titleEn":"Estimate throughput from shot count and movement overhead","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Beam current alone cannot predict throughput.","instruction":"估算圖元數與移動時間的吞吐量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate throughput from shot count and movement overhead. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Beam current alone cannot predict throughput.","observation":"吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Beam current alone cannot predict throughput. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算圖元數與移動時間的吞吐量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate throughput from shot count and movement overhead\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Beam current alone cannot predict throughput.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。","textEn":"Beam current alone cannot predict throughput."},{"id":"a035-v8-17-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算圖元數與移動時間的吞吐量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate throughput from shot count and movement overhead\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","Beam current alone cannot predict throughput.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask."],"answer":1,"explanation":"吞吐量不能只用束流大小推算。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Beam current alone cannot predict throughput. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}},{"id":"a035-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-17"],"title":"保留寫入中斷後的接續驗證紀錄","titleEn":"Plan verification after a writing interruption","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure.","instruction":"保留寫入中斷後的接續驗證紀錄。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan verification after a writing interruption. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure.","observation":"中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「保留寫入中斷後的接續驗證紀錄」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan verification after a writing interruption\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。","textEn":"Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure."},{"id":"a035-v8-18-k2","title":"劑量與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dose and stitching: principle and limits","text":"局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","textEn":"Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「保留寫入中斷後的接續驗證紀錄」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan verification after a writing interruption\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均劑量相同即可忽略拼接。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean dose makes stitching irrelevant.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中斷前後可能有漂移與重複曝光。 局部散射與跨場拼接需分別建模。","explanationEn":"Interruptions can introduce drift and repeated exposure. Local scattering and field stitching require separate models."}}]},{"id":"a035-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"光罩驗收","titleEn":"Mask acceptance","description":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","descriptionEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification.","steps":[{"id":"a035-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-18"],"title":"對照顯影前後的線寬偏差","titleEn":"Compare linewidth bias introduced by development","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry.","instruction":"對照顯影前後的線寬偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare linewidth bias introduced by development. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry.","observation":"電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對照顯影前後的線寬偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare linewidth bias introduced by development\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。","textEn":"Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry."},{"id":"a035-v8-19-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對照顯影前後的線寬偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare linewidth bias introduced by development\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。"],"optionsEn":["Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電子束寫入不是最終光罩幾何的唯一來源。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Beam writing is not the sole source of final mask geometry. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}},{"id":"a035-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-19"],"title":"檢查光罩蝕刻造成的邊緣位移","titleEn":"Assess edge displacement from mask etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias.","instruction":"檢查光罩蝕刻造成的邊緣位移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess edge displacement from mask etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias.","observation":"蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查光罩蝕刻造成的邊緣位移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess edge displacement from mask etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。","textEn":"Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias."},{"id":"a035-v8-20-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查光罩蝕刻造成的邊緣位移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess edge displacement from mask etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。"],"optionsEn":["One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"蝕刻偏差須與曝光偏差分離。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Etch bias must be separated from exposure bias. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}},{"id":"a035-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-20"],"title":"建立全片定位誤差向量圖","titleEn":"Create a full-mask placement-error vector map","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors.","instruction":"建立全片定位誤差向量圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Create a full-mask placement-error vector map. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors.","observation":"全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立全片定位誤差向量圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Create a full-mask placement-error vector map\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。","textEn":"Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors."},{"id":"a035-v8-21-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立全片定位誤差向量圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Create a full-mask placement-error vector map\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。"],"optionsEn":["One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"全片系統誤差可能與局部隨機誤差並存。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Global systematic errors can coexist with local random errors. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}},{"id":"a035-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-21"],"title":"將光罩缺陷送入可印性判讀","titleEn":"Evaluate mask defects for printability","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally.","instruction":"將光罩缺陷送入可印性判讀。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Evaluate mask defects for printability. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally.","observation":"可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將光罩缺陷送入可印性判讀」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Evaluate mask defects for printability\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。","textEn":"Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally."},{"id":"a035-v8-22-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將光罩缺陷送入可印性判讀」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Evaluate mask defects for printability\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。","只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。"],"optionsEn":["Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally.","One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可見缺陷不一定同樣影響晶圓圖形。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Visible defects do not all affect wafer patterns equally. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}},{"id":"a035-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-22"],"title":"建立修補後再次量測的關卡","titleEn":"Define remeasurement gates after repair","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repair can modify neighboring regions.","instruction":"建立修補後再次量測的關卡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define remeasurement gates after repair. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repair can modify neighboring regions.","observation":"修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repair can modify neighboring regions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立修補後再次量測的關卡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define remeasurement gates after repair\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repair can modify neighboring regions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。","textEn":"Repair can modify neighboring regions."},{"id":"a035-v8-23-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立修補後再次量測的關卡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define remeasurement gates after repair\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。"],"optionsEn":["One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Repair can modify neighboring regions.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"修補本身可能改變鄰近區域。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Repair can modify neighboring regions. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}},{"id":"a035-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-maskrepair","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a035-v8-23"],"title":"交付資料、曝光與量測的完整鏈結","titleEn":"Deliver a linked data-writing-metrology record","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Traceability links anomalies to their sources.","instruction":"交付資料、曝光與量測的完整鏈結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a linked data-writing-metrology record. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Traceability links anomalies to their sources.","observation":"追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Traceability links anomalies to their sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付資料、曝光與量測的完整鏈結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a linked data-writing-metrology record\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Traceability links anomalies to their sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a035-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。","textEn":"Traceability links anomalies to their sources."},{"id":"a035-v8-24-k2","title":"光罩驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask acceptance: principle and limits","text":"光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","textEn":"A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付資料、曝光與量測的完整鏈結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a linked data-writing-metrology record\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只測一個位置即可批準全片光罩。","把晶圓尺寸直接當作光罩尺寸。","追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。"],"optionsEn":["One measured site is sufficient to accept a whole mask.","Use wafer dimensions directly as mask dimensions.","Traceability links anomalies to their sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"追溯性讓異常能回到對應來源。 光罩幾何合格仍須驗證實際成像。","explanationEn":"Traceability links anomalies to their sources. A geometrically acceptable mask still needs imaging verification."}}]}]},{"id":"a036","title":"光罩缺陷檢測與修補","titleEn":"Photomask defect inspection and repair","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究缺陷與成像、定位與分類、修補策略、再驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: defects and imaging, localization and classification, repair strategy, requalification. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["缺陷與成像","定位與分類","修補策略","再驗證"],"labelsEn":["Defects and imaging","Localization and classification","Repair strategy","Requalification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a036-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"缺陷與成像","titleEn":"Defects and imaging","description":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","descriptionEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability.","steps":[{"id":"a036-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把透明、遮光與相位缺陷分欄","titleEn":"Separate clear, opaque and phase defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：三者對光場的作用不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The three classes affect the optical field differently.","instruction":"把透明、遮光與相位缺陷分欄。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「三者對光場的作用不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate clear, opaque and phase defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: The three classes affect the optical field differently.","observation":"三者對光場的作用不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The three classes affect the optical field differently. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把透明、遮光與相位缺陷分欄」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「三者對光場的作用不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate clear, opaque and phase defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The three classes affect the optical field differently.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"三者對光場的作用不同。","textEn":"The three classes affect the optical field differently."},{"id":"a036-v8-01-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把透明、遮光與相位缺陷分欄」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate clear, opaque and phase defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["三者對光場的作用不同。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["The three classes affect the optical field differently.","All small particles are negligible.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"三者對光場的作用不同。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"The three classes affect the optical field differently. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}},{"id":"a036-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-01"],"title":"比較光罩缺陷與晶圓重複缺陷","titleEn":"Compare mask defects with repeating wafer defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask defects can repeat across dies.","instruction":"比較光罩缺陷與晶圓重複缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare mask defects with repeating wafer defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask defects can repeat across dies.","observation":"光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask defects can repeat across dies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光罩缺陷與晶圓重複缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare mask defects with repeating wafer defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask defects can repeat across dies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。","textEn":"Mask defects can repeat across dies."},{"id":"a036-v8-02-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光罩缺陷與晶圓重複缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare mask defects with repeating wafer defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["All small particles are negligible.","Mask defects can repeat across dies.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光罩缺陷可能在多個晶粒重複。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"Mask defects can repeat across dies. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}},{"id":"a036-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-02"],"title":"標記多層膜下方與吸收層缺陷","titleEn":"Distinguish buried multilayer from absorber defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：缺陷深度改變修補可行性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Defect depth changes repair feasibility.","instruction":"標記多層膜下方與吸收層缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「缺陷深度改變修補可行性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish buried multilayer from absorber defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Defect depth changes repair feasibility.","observation":"缺陷深度改變修補可行性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Defect depth changes repair feasibility. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記多層膜下方與吸收層缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「缺陷深度改變修補可行性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish buried multilayer from absorber defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Defect depth changes repair feasibility.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"缺陷深度改變修補可行性。","textEn":"Defect depth changes repair feasibility."},{"id":"a036-v8-03-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記多層膜下方與吸收層缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish buried multilayer from absorber defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","缺陷深度改變修補可行性。"],"optionsEn":["All small particles are negligible.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Defect depth changes repair feasibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"缺陷深度改變修補可行性。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"Defect depth changes repair feasibility. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}},{"id":"a036-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-03"],"title":"畫出缺陷位置相對於線端的關係","titleEn":"Locate defects relative to line ends","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations.","instruction":"畫出缺陷位置相對於線端的關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Locate defects relative to line ends. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations.","observation":"相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出缺陷位置相對於線端的關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Locate defects relative to line ends\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。","textEn":"Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations."},{"id":"a036-v8-04-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出缺陷位置相對於線端的關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Locate defects relative to line ends\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations.","All small particles are negligible.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同缺陷在不同圖形位置可有不同危害。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"Identical defects can have different impacts at different pattern locations. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}},{"id":"a036-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-04"],"title":"比較光強缺陷與相位缺陷的空中像","titleEn":"Compare intensity- and phase-defect aerial images","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast.","instruction":"比較光強缺陷與相位缺陷的空中像。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare intensity- and phase-defect aerial images. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast.","observation":"相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光強缺陷與相位缺陷的空中像」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare intensity- and phase-defect aerial images\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。","textEn":"Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast."},{"id":"a036-v8-05-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光強缺陷與相位缺陷的空中像」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare intensity- and phase-defect aerial images\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["All small particles are negligible.","Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相位擾動可在外觀不明顯時影響成像。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"Phase perturbations can affect imaging without obvious surface contrast. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}},{"id":"a036-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-05"],"title":"定義缺陷分級需要的證據","titleEn":"Define evidence for defect disposition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Size is not the only disposition metric.","instruction":"定義缺陷分級需要的證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define evidence for defect disposition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Size is not the only disposition metric.","observation":"缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Size is not the only disposition metric. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All small particles are negligible.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義缺陷分級需要的證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define evidence for defect disposition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Size is not the only disposition metric.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。","textEn":"Size is not the only disposition metric."},{"id":"a036-v8-06-k2","title":"缺陷與成像的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and imaging: principle and limits","text":"缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","textEn":"Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義缺陷分級需要的證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define evidence for defect disposition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。"],"optionsEn":["All small particles are negligible.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Size is not the only disposition metric."],"answer":2,"explanation":"缺陷尺寸不是唯一分級指標。 缺陷分類須同時包括幾何、相位與可印性。","explanationEn":"Size is not the only disposition metric. Defect classification must include geometry, phase and printability."}}]},{"id":"a036-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"定位與分類","titleEn":"Localization and classification","description":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","descriptionEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate.","steps":[{"id":"a036-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-06"],"title":"建立檢查座標到修補座標的轉換","titleEn":"Transform inspection coordinates into repair coordinates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：工具間座標需共同標記校準。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks.","instruction":"建立檢查座標到修補座標的轉換。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「工具間座標需共同標記校準。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Transform inspection coordinates into repair coordinates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks.","observation":"工具間座標需共同標記校準。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立檢查座標到修補座標的轉換」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「工具間座標需共同標記校準。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Transform inspection coordinates into repair coordinates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"工具間座標需共同標記校準。","textEn":"Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks."},{"id":"a036-v8-07-k2","title":"定位與分類的原理與限制","titleEn":"Localization and classification: principle and limits","text":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立檢查座標到修補座標的轉換」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Transform inspection coordinates into repair coordinates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["工具間座標需共同標記校準。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","修補深度越大越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Deeper repair is always more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"工具間座標需共同標記校準。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Coordinate transfer needs shared calibration marks. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}},{"id":"a036-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-07"],"title":"比較 die-to-die 與 die-to-database 檢查","titleEn":"Compare die-to-die and die-to-database inspection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：比較基準不同會改變可見異常。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different references reveal different anomalies.","instruction":"比較 die-to-die 與 die-to-database 檢查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「比較基準不同會改變可見異常。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare die-to-die and die-to-database inspection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different references reveal different anomalies.","observation":"比較基準不同會改變可見異常。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different references reveal different anomalies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 die-to-die 與 die-to-database 檢查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「比較基準不同會改變可見異常。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare die-to-die and die-to-database inspection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different references reveal different anomalies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"比較基準不同會改變可見異常。","textEn":"Different references reveal different anomalies."},{"id":"a036-v8-08-k2","title":"定位與分類的原理與限制","titleEn":"Localization and classification: principle and limits","text":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 die-to-die 與 die-to-database 檢查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare die-to-die and die-to-database inspection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","比較基準不同會改變可見異常。","修補深度越大越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Different references reveal different anomalies.","Deeper repair is always more reliable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較基準不同會改變可見異常。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Different references reveal different anomalies. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}},{"id":"a036-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-08"],"title":"計算缺陷偵測的漏檢與誤報率","titleEn":"Calculate miss and false-alarm rates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Higher sensitivity can increase review burden.","instruction":"計算缺陷偵測的漏檢與誤報率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設盲測標準片有 100 處已知缺陷及 100 處已知正常區。檢查器找出 90 處真缺陷，但將 5 處正常區誤報。列出 TP=90、FN=10、FP=5、TN=95；漏檢率為 10%，誤報率為 5%。若只報告 95 次警報，無法得知靈敏度；並須說明此結果只適用於標準片所涵蓋的缺陷尺寸與類型。","instructionEn":"Calculate miss and false-alarm rates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Higher sensitivity can increase review burden.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): A hypothetical blind standard contains 100 known defects and 100 clean sites. Inspection detects 90 true defects and falsely flags 5 clean sites: TP=90, FN=10, FP=5, TN=95. The miss rate is 10% and false-positive rate 5%. Reporting 95 alarms alone cannot establish sensitivity. The result applies only to the defect sizes and classes represented by the standard.","observation":"提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付四格表、10% 與 5%，不可用警報總數代替辨識性能。","observationEn":"Higher sensitivity can increase review burden. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nSubmit the confusion matrix, 10% and 5%; do not substitute alarm count for detection performance.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算缺陷偵測的漏檢與誤報率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付四格表、10% 與 5%，不可用警報總數代替辨識性能。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate miss and false-alarm rates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Higher sensitivity can increase review burden.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Submit the confusion matrix, 10% and 5%; do not substitute alarm count for detection performance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。","textEn":"Higher sensitivity can increase review burden."},{"id":"a036-v8-09-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設盲測標準片有 100 處已知缺陷及 100 處已知正常區。檢查器找出 90 處真缺陷，但將 5 處正常區誤報。列出 TP=90、FN=10、FP=5、TN=95；漏檢率為 10%，誤報率為 5%。若只報告 95 次警報，無法得知靈敏度；並須說明此結果只適用於標準片所涵蓋的缺陷尺寸與類型。","textEn":"A hypothetical blind standard contains 100 known defects and 100 clean sites. Inspection detects 90 true defects and falsely flags 5 clean sites: TP=90, FN=10, FP=5, TN=95. The miss rate is 10% and false-positive rate 5%. Reporting 95 alarms alone cannot establish sensitivity. The result applies only to the defect sizes and classes represented by the standard."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算缺陷偵測的漏檢與誤報率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate miss and false-alarm rates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","修補深度越大越可靠。","提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。"],"optionsEn":["No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Deeper repair is always more reliable.","Higher sensitivity can increase review burden."],"answer":2,"explanation":"提高靈敏度可能增加複查負擔。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Higher sensitivity can increase review burden. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設盲測標準片有 100 處已知缺陷及 100 處已知正常區。檢查器找出 90 處真缺陷，但將 5 處正常區誤報。列出 TP=90、FN=10、FP=5、TN=95；漏檢率為 10%，誤報率為 5%。若只報告 95 次警報，無法得知靈敏度；並須說明此結果只適用於標準片所涵蓋的缺陷尺寸與類型。","textEn":"A hypothetical blind standard contains 100 known defects and 100 clean sites. Inspection detects 90 true defects and falsely flags 5 clean sites: TP=90, FN=10, FP=5, TN=95. The miss rate is 10% and false-positive rate 5%. Reporting 95 alarms alone cannot establish sensitivity. The result applies only to the defect sizes and classes represented by the standard.","check":"交付四格表、10% 與 5%，不可用警報總數代替辨識性能。","checkEn":"Submit the confusion matrix, 10% and 5%; do not substitute alarm count for detection performance."}},{"id":"a036-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-09"],"title":"對重複掃描評估缺陷位置再現性","titleEn":"Assess defect-position repeatability by rescanning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：定位再現性限制局部修補。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Localization repeatability limits local repair.","instruction":"對重複掃描評估缺陷位置再現性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「定位再現性限制局部修補。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess defect-position repeatability by rescanning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Localization repeatability limits local repair.","observation":"定位再現性限制局部修補。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Localization repeatability limits local repair. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對重複掃描評估缺陷位置再現性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「定位再現性限制局部修補。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess defect-position repeatability by rescanning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Localization repeatability limits local repair.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"定位再現性限制局部修補。","textEn":"Localization repeatability limits local repair."},{"id":"a036-v8-10-k2","title":"定位與分類的原理與限制","titleEn":"Localization and classification: principle and limits","text":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對重複掃描評估缺陷位置再現性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess defect-position repeatability by rescanning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["定位再現性限制局部修補。","檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","修補深度越大越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Localization repeatability limits local repair.","No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Deeper repair is always more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"定位再現性限制局部修補。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Localization repeatability limits local repair. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}},{"id":"a036-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-10"],"title":"分辨顆粒污染與圖形本體缺損","titleEn":"Distinguish contamination from pattern damage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments.","instruction":"分辨顆粒污染與圖形本體缺損。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish contamination from pattern damage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments.","observation":"清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分辨顆粒污染與圖形本體缺損」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish contamination from pattern damage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。","textEn":"Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments."},{"id":"a036-v8-11-k2","title":"定位與分類的原理與限制","titleEn":"Localization and classification: principle and limits","text":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分辨顆粒污染與圖形本體缺損」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish contamination from pattern damage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。","修補深度越大越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments.","Deeper repair is always more reliable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔與修補不是可互換的處置。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Cleaning and repair are not interchangeable treatments. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}},{"id":"a036-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-11"],"title":"為不確定缺陷建立複查分流","titleEn":"Route uncertain defects for further review","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result.","instruction":"為不確定缺陷建立複查分流。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Route uncertain defects for further review. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result.","observation":"不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為不確定缺陷建立複查分流」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Route uncertain defects for further review\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。","textEn":"Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result."},{"id":"a036-v8-12-k2","title":"定位與分類的原理與限制","titleEn":"Localization and classification: principle and limits","text":"檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為不確定缺陷建立複查分流」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Route uncertain defects for further review\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["檢查未報警就等於沒有任何缺陷。","修補深度越大越可靠。","不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。"],"optionsEn":["No inspection alarm proves there are no defects.","Deeper repair is always more reliable.","Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不確定性應保留而非強迫二分。 檢查的靈敏度與誤報率有取捨。","explanationEn":"Uncertainty should be retained rather than forced into a binary result. Inspection sensitivity trades against false-positive rate."}}]},{"id":"a036-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"修補策略","titleEn":"Repair strategy","description":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","descriptionEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects.","steps":[{"id":"a036-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-12"],"title":"對遮光多餘區規畫局部移除","titleEn":"Plan local removal for excess opaque material","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removal must avoid intended features.","instruction":"對遮光多餘區規畫局部移除。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan local removal for excess opaque material. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removal must avoid intended features.","observation":"移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removal must avoid intended features. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對遮光多餘區規畫局部移除」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan local removal for excess opaque material\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removal must avoid intended features.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。","textEn":"Removal must avoid intended features."},{"id":"a036-v8-13-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對遮光多餘區規畫局部移除」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan local removal for excess opaque material\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。","修補深度越大越可靠。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。"],"optionsEn":["Removal must avoid intended features.","Deeper repair is always more reliable.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"移除不得侵入應保留的圖形。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Removal must avoid intended features. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}},{"id":"a036-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-13"],"title":"對缺少吸收層的區域規畫局部添加","titleEn":"Plan local addition where absorber is missing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements.","instruction":"對缺少吸收層的區域規畫局部添加。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan local addition where absorber is missing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements.","observation":"添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對缺少吸收層的區域規畫局部添加」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan local addition where absorber is missing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。","textEn":"Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements."},{"id":"a036-v8-14-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對缺少吸收層的區域規畫局部添加」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan local addition where absorber is missing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["修補深度越大越可靠。","添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。"],"optionsEn":["Deeper repair is always more reliable.","Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase."],"answer":1,"explanation":"添加層需滿足光學及幾何要求。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Added material must meet optical and geometric requirements. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}},{"id":"a036-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-14"],"title":"畫出電子束與前驅物的作用區","titleEn":"Sketch the beam–precursor interaction region","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region.","instruction":"畫出電子束與前驅物的作用區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch the beam–precursor interaction region. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region.","observation":"反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出電子束與前驅物的作用區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch the beam–precursor interaction region\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。","textEn":"Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region."},{"id":"a036-v8-15-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出電子束與前驅物的作用區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch the beam–precursor interaction region\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["修補深度越大越可靠。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。","反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。"],"optionsEn":["Deeper repair is always more reliable.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應區域由束流與表面分子共同決定。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Beam exposure and surface molecules jointly define the reaction region. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}},{"id":"a036-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-15"],"title":"檢查修補殘留與暈圈效應","titleEn":"Inspect repair residue and halo effects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：修補區外也可能受影響。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area.","instruction":"檢查修補殘留與暈圈效應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「修補區外也可能受影響。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect repair residue and halo effects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area.","observation":"修補區外也可能受影響。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查修補殘留與暈圈效應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「修補區外也可能受影響。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect repair residue and halo effects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"修補區外也可能受影響。","textEn":"Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area."},{"id":"a036-v8-16-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查修補殘留與暈圈效應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect repair residue and halo effects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["修補區外也可能受影響。","修補深度越大越可靠。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。"],"optionsEn":["Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area.","Deeper repair is always more reliable.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"修補區外也可能受影響。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Effects may extend beyond the intended repair area. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}},{"id":"a036-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-16"],"title":"比較修補與圖形位移避讓方案","titleEn":"Compare repair with pattern-shift avoidance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair.","instruction":"比較修補與圖形位移避讓方案。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare repair with pattern-shift avoidance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair.","observation":"埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較修補與圖形位移避讓方案」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare repair with pattern-shift avoidance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。","textEn":"Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair."},{"id":"a036-v8-17-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較修補與圖形位移避讓方案」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare repair with pattern-shift avoidance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["修補深度越大越可靠。","埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。"],"optionsEn":["Deeper repair is always more reliable.","Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase."],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋藏缺陷不一定適合直接修補。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Buried defects are not always suitable for direct repair. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}},{"id":"a036-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-17"],"title":"建立停止修補的判定條件","titleEn":"Define repair stop criteria","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反覆處置可能累積損傷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repeated intervention can accumulate damage.","instruction":"建立停止修補的判定條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「反覆處置可能累積損傷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define repair stop criteria. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repeated intervention can accumulate damage.","observation":"反覆處置可能累積損傷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repeated intervention can accumulate damage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「修補深度越大越可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Deeper repair is always more reliable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立停止修補的判定條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反覆處置可能累積損傷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define repair stop criteria\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repeated intervention can accumulate damage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反覆處置可能累積損傷。","textEn":"Repeated intervention can accumulate damage."},{"id":"a036-v8-18-k2","title":"修補策略的原理與限制","titleEn":"Repair strategy: principle and limits","text":"添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","textEn":"Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立停止修補的判定條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define repair stop criteria\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["修補深度越大越可靠。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。","反覆處置可能累積損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Deeper repair is always more reliable.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","Repeated intervention can accumulate damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反覆處置可能累積損傷。 添加與移除材料的修補有不同副作用。","explanationEn":"Repeated intervention can accumulate damage. Additive and subtractive repair have different side effects."}}]},{"id":"a036-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"再驗證","titleEn":"Requalification","description":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","descriptionEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image.","steps":[{"id":"a036-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-18"],"title":"量測修補後邊緣位置","titleEn":"Measure post-repair edge placement","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements.","instruction":"量測修補後邊緣位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure post-repair edge placement. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements.","observation":"尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測修補後邊緣位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure post-repair edge placement\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。","textEn":"Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements."},{"id":"a036-v8-19-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測修補後邊緣位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure post-repair edge placement\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","All small particles are negligible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"尺寸恢復與位置恢復是不同要求。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Restoring size and restoring position are distinct requirements. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}},{"id":"a036-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-19"],"title":"以工作波長檢查空中像","titleEn":"Evaluate aerial images at the operating wavelength","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Printability verification should match imaging conditions.","instruction":"以工作波長檢查空中像。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Evaluate aerial images at the operating wavelength. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Printability verification should match imaging conditions.","observation":"可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Printability verification should match imaging conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以工作波長檢查空中像」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Evaluate aerial images at the operating wavelength\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Printability verification should match imaging conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。","textEn":"Printability verification should match imaging conditions."},{"id":"a036-v8-20-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以工作波長檢查空中像」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Evaluate aerial images at the operating wavelength\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外觀平整即代表相位正確。","可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","Printability verification should match imaging conditions.","All small particles are negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可印性驗證應對應實際成像條件。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Printability verification should match imaging conditions. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}},{"id":"a036-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-20"],"title":"比較焦距掃描中的修補表現","titleEn":"Compare repair performance through focus","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Passing one focus point does not establish a process window.","instruction":"比較焦距掃描中的修補表現。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare repair performance through focus. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Passing one focus point does not establish a process window.","observation":"單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Passing one focus point does not establish a process window. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較焦距掃描中的修補表現」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare repair performance through focus\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Passing one focus point does not establish a process window.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。","textEn":"Passing one focus point does not establish a process window."},{"id":"a036-v8-21-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較焦距掃描中的修補表現」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare repair performance through focus\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外觀平整即代表相位正確。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","All small particles are negligible.","Passing one focus point does not establish a process window."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一焦點合格不能保證製程窗口。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Passing one focus point does not establish a process window. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}},{"id":"a036-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-21"],"title":"檢查修補區與鄰近圖形的相互作用","titleEn":"Check repair interaction with neighboring patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling.","instruction":"檢查修補區與鄰近圖形的相互作用。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check repair interaction with neighboring patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling.","observation":"局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查修補區與鄰近圖形的相互作用」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check repair interaction with neighboring patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。","textEn":"Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling."},{"id":"a036-v8-22-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查修補區與鄰近圖形的相互作用」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check repair interaction with neighboring patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。","外觀平整即代表相位正確。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling.","A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","All small particles are negligible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部修補也可能改變鄰近光學耦合。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Local repair can change neighboring optical coupling. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}},{"id":"a036-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-22"],"title":"追蹤光罩清潔後的再驗證","titleEn":"Plan requalification after mask cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning can change residue and surface condition.","instruction":"追蹤光罩清潔後的再驗證。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan requalification after mask cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning can change residue and surface condition.","observation":"清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning can change residue and surface condition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤光罩清潔後的再驗證」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan requalification after mask cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning can change residue and surface condition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。","textEn":"Cleaning can change residue and surface condition."},{"id":"a036-v8-23-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤光罩清潔後的再驗證」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan requalification after mask cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外觀平整即代表相位正確。","清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","Cleaning can change residue and surface condition.","All small particles are negligible."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔可能改變殘留與表面狀態。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Cleaning can change residue and surface condition. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}},{"id":"a036-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskrepair","v8b-maskqual","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a036-v8-23"],"title":"完成可追溯的缺陷關閉報告","titleEn":"Complete a traceable defect-closure report","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria.","instruction":"完成可追溯的缺陷關閉報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Complete a traceable defect-closure report. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria.","observation":"關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「外觀平整即代表相位正確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A smooth appearance proves correct phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「完成可追溯的缺陷關閉報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Complete a traceable defect-closure report\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a036-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。","textEn":"Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria."},{"id":"a036-v8-24-k2","title":"再驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Requalification: principle and limits","text":"修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","textEn":"Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「完成可追溯的缺陷關閉報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Complete a traceable defect-closure report\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外觀平整即代表相位正確。","所有小顆粒都一定可忽略。","關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth appearance proves correct phase.","All small particles are negligible.","Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"關閉缺陷需要前後證據與接受條件。 修補成功以成像及定位證據判定，不只看修補區照片。","explanationEn":"Closure needs before/after evidence and acceptance criteria. Repair success requires imaging and placement evidence, not merely a repair image."}}]}]},{"id":"a037","title":"相位移光罩工程","titleEn":"Phase-shift mask engineering","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究振幅與相位、光罩結構、成像窗口、量測與整合；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: amplitude and phase, mask structures, imaging window, metrology and integration. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["振幅與相位","光罩結構","成像窗口","量測與整合"],"labelsEn":["Amplitude and phase","Mask structures","Imaging window","Metrology and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a037-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"振幅與相位","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase","description":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","descriptionEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities.","steps":[{"id":"a037-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"以複數平面表示兩束等振幅光","titleEn":"Represent equal-amplitude fields in the complex plane","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相位差決定相長或相消干涉。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference.","instruction":"以複數平面表示兩束等振幅光。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「相位差決定相長或相消干涉。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Represent equal-amplitude fields in the complex plane. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference.","observation":"相位差決定相長或相消干涉。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以複數平面表示兩束等振幅光」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相位差決定相長或相消干涉。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Represent equal-amplitude fields in the complex plane\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相位差決定相長或相消干涉。","textEn":"Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference."},{"id":"a037-v8-01-k2","title":"振幅與相位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase: principle and limits","text":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","textEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以複數平面表示兩束等振幅光」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Represent equal-amplitude fields in the complex plane\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相位差決定相長或相消干涉。","只需把兩束光強相加。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。"],"optionsEn":["Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference.","Simply add the two intensities.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相位差決定相長或相消干涉。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Phase difference controls constructive or destructive interference. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}},{"id":"a037-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-01"],"title":"計算零與半週期相位差的合成強度","titleEn":"Calculate intensity at zero and half-cycle phase difference","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：理想反相等振幅場可相消。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel.","instruction":"計算零與半週期相位差的合成強度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「理想反相等振幅場可相消。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設兩束相干光的振幅皆為 1。相位差 0 時，I=|1+1|²=4；相位差 π 時，I=|1-1|²=0。若第二束振幅僅 0.8，反相後 I=|1-0.8|²=0.04，便不是完全黑暗。畫出複數向量，說明相位正確仍需要振幅匹配；此為兩束光模型，不是完整投影系統。","instructionEn":"Calculate intensity at zero and half-cycle phase difference. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume coherent fields with amplitudes 1 and 1. At phase difference 0, I=|1+1|²=4; at π, I=|1-1|²=0. If the second amplitude is 0.8, opposing fields give I=|1-0.8|²=0.04 rather than complete darkness. Draw complex vectors and explain why phase alone is insufficient without amplitude matching. This is a two-field model, not a complete projection system.","observation":"理想反相等振幅場可相消。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n須得到 4、0、0.04，不能直接相加兩束強度。","observationEn":"Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nObtain 4, 0 and 0.04 without directly adding intensities.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算零與半週期相位差的合成強度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「理想反相等振幅場可相消。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：須得到 4、0、0.04，不能直接相加兩束強度。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate intensity at zero and half-cycle phase difference\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Obtain 4, 0 and 0.04 without directly adding intensities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"理想反相等振幅場可相消。","textEn":"Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel."},{"id":"a037-v8-02-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設兩束相干光的振幅皆為 1。相位差 0 時，I=|1+1|²=4；相位差 π 時，I=|1-1|²=0。若第二束振幅僅 0.8，反相後 I=|1-0.8|²=0.04，便不是完全黑暗。畫出複數向量，說明相位正確仍需要振幅匹配；此為兩束光模型，不是完整投影系統。","textEn":"Assume coherent fields with amplitudes 1 and 1. At phase difference 0, I=|1+1|²=4; at π, I=|1-1|²=0. If the second amplitude is 0.8, opposing fields give I=|1-0.8|²=0.04 rather than complete darkness. Draw complex vectors and explain why phase alone is insufficient without amplitude matching. This is a two-field model, not a complete projection system."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算零與半週期相位差的合成強度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate intensity at zero and half-cycle phase difference\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把兩束光強相加。","理想反相等振幅場可相消。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。"],"optionsEn":["Simply add the two intensities.","Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque."],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想反相等振幅場可相消。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Ideal equal-amplitude opposing fields can cancel. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設兩束相干光的振幅皆為 1。相位差 0 時，I=|1+1|²=4；相位差 π 時，I=|1-1|²=0。若第二束振幅僅 0.8，反相後 I=|1-0.8|²=0.04，便不是完全黑暗。畫出複數向量，說明相位正確仍需要振幅匹配；此為兩束光模型，不是完整投影系統。","textEn":"Assume coherent fields with amplitudes 1 and 1. At phase difference 0, I=|1+1|²=4; at π, I=|1-1|²=0. If the second amplitude is 0.8, opposing fields give I=|1-0.8|²=0.04 rather than complete darkness. Draw complex vectors and explain why phase alone is insufficient without amplitude matching. This is a two-field model, not a complete projection system.","check":"須得到 4、0、0.04，不能直接相加兩束強度。","checkEn":"Obtain 4, 0 and 0.04 without directly adding intensities."}},{"id":"a037-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-02"],"title":"比較振幅減半與強度減半","titleEn":"Distinguish halved amplitude from halved intensity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：強度與振幅平方成正比。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Intensity scales with amplitude squared.","instruction":"比較振幅減半與強度減半。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「強度與振幅平方成正比。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish halved amplitude from halved intensity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Intensity scales with amplitude squared.","observation":"強度與振幅平方成正比。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Intensity scales with amplitude squared. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較振幅減半與強度減半」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「強度與振幅平方成正比。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish halved amplitude from halved intensity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Intensity scales with amplitude squared.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"強度與振幅平方成正比。","textEn":"Intensity scales with amplitude squared."},{"id":"a037-v8-03-k2","title":"振幅與相位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase: principle and limits","text":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","textEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較振幅減半與強度減半」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish halved amplitude from halved intensity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把兩束光強相加。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","強度與振幅平方成正比。"],"optionsEn":["Simply add the two intensities.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Intensity scales with amplitude squared."],"answer":2,"explanation":"強度與振幅平方成正比。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Intensity scales with amplitude squared. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}},{"id":"a037-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-03"],"title":"繪製二元光罩邊緣的模糊像","titleEn":"Sketch blurred edges from a binary mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges.","instruction":"繪製二元光罩邊緣的模糊像。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch blurred edges from a binary mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges.","observation":"繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製二元光罩邊緣的模糊像」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch blurred edges from a binary mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。","textEn":"Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges."},{"id":"a037-v8-04-k2","title":"振幅與相位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase: principle and limits","text":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","textEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製二元光罩邊緣的模糊像」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch blurred edges from a binary mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。","只需把兩束光強相加。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。"],"optionsEn":["Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges.","Simply add the two intensities.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque."],"answer":0,"explanation":"繞射限制圖形轉移的陡峭度。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Diffraction limits the sharpness of transferred edges. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}},{"id":"a037-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-04"],"title":"加入相位反轉區觀察暗線","titleEn":"Add a phase-reversal region and inspect the dark line","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip.","instruction":"加入相位反轉區觀察暗線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Add a phase-reversal region and inspect the dark line. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip.","observation":"暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「加入相位反轉區觀察暗線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Add a phase-reversal region and inspect the dark line\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。","textEn":"Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip."},{"id":"a037-v8-05-k2","title":"振幅與相位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase: principle and limits","text":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","textEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「加入相位反轉區觀察暗線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Add a phase-reversal region and inspect the dark line\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把兩束光強相加。","暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。"],"optionsEn":["Simply add the two intensities.","Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暗線可由干涉形成而非遮光形成。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Interference can create a dark line without an opaque strip. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}},{"id":"a037-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-05"],"title":"列出簡化干涉模型的限制","titleEn":"List limits of a simplified interference model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination.","instruction":"列出簡化干涉模型的限制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List limits of a simplified interference model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination.","observation":"實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把兩束光強相加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply add the two intensities.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出簡化干涉模型的限制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List limits of a simplified interference model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。","textEn":"Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination."},{"id":"a037-v8-06-k2","title":"振幅與相位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Amplitude and phase: principle and limits","text":"強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","textEn":"Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出簡化干涉模型的限制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List limits of a simplified interference model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把兩束光強相加。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。"],"optionsEn":["Simply add the two intensities.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination."],"answer":2,"explanation":"實際成像還包含孔徑、偏振與照明。 強度來自複數光場相加後取模平方，不能直接相加强度。","explanationEn":"Real imaging also includes aperture, polarization and illumination. Intensity is the squared magnitude of summed complex fields, not a direct sum of intensities."}}]},{"id":"a037-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"光罩結構","titleEn":"Mask structures","description":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","descriptionEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts.","steps":[{"id":"a037-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-06"],"title":"畫出交替式光罩的相位分配","titleEn":"Assign phases in an alternating mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology.","instruction":"畫出交替式光罩的相位分配。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assign phases in an alternating mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology.","observation":"相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出交替式光罩的相位分配」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assign phases in an alternating mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。","textEn":"Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology."},{"id":"a037-v8-07-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出交替式光罩的相位分配」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assign phases in an alternating mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。"],"optionsEn":["Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相位標記必須與圖形拓樸相容。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Phase labels must be compatible with pattern topology. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}},{"id":"a037-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-07"],"title":"找出封閉迴圈中的相位衝突","titleEn":"Find phase conflicts in closed loops","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment.","instruction":"找出封閉迴圈中的相位衝突。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Find phase conflicts in closed loops. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment.","observation":"並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「找出封閉迴圈中的相位衝突」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Find phase conflicts in closed loops\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。","textEn":"Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment."},{"id":"a037-v8-08-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「找出封閉迴圈中的相位衝突」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Find phase conflicts in closed loops\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。"],"optionsEn":["Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"並非每個任意圖形都能直接交替著色。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Not every arbitrary layout permits simple alternating phase assignment. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}},{"id":"a037-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-08"],"title":"比較衰減式吸收層的透射與相位","titleEn":"Compare transmission and phase of an attenuating film","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Attenuated masks retain finite transmission.","instruction":"比較衰減式吸收層的透射與相位。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare transmission and phase of an attenuating film. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Attenuated masks retain finite transmission.","observation":"衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Attenuated masks retain finite transmission. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較衰減式吸收層的透射與相位」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare transmission and phase of an attenuating film\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Attenuated masks retain finite transmission.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。","textEn":"Attenuated masks retain finite transmission."},{"id":"a037-v8-09-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較衰減式吸收層的透射與相位」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare transmission and phase of an attenuating film\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。"],"optionsEn":["Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Attenuated masks retain finite transmission."],"answer":2,"explanation":"衰減式光罩仍有有限透光。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Attenuated masks retain finite transmission. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}},{"id":"a037-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-09"],"title":"以折射率與厚度估算相位差","titleEn":"Estimate phase difference from index and thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Phase delay depends on wavelength and material.","instruction":"以折射率與厚度估算相位差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate phase difference from index and thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Phase delay depends on wavelength and material.","observation":"相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Phase delay depends on wavelength and material. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以折射率與厚度估算相位差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate phase difference from index and thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Phase delay depends on wavelength and material.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。","textEn":"Phase delay depends on wavelength and material."},{"id":"a037-v8-10-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以折射率與厚度估算相位差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate phase difference from index and thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。","所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。"],"optionsEn":["Phase delay depends on wavelength and material.","Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相位延遲同時依賴波長與材料。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Phase delay depends on wavelength and material. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}},{"id":"a037-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-10"],"title":"標出製造厚度偏差造成的相位誤差","titleEn":"Map thickness error into phase error","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue.","instruction":"標出製造厚度偏差造成的相位誤差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map thickness error into phase error. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue.","observation":"厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標出製造厚度偏差造成的相位誤差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map thickness error into phase error\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。","textEn":"Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue."},{"id":"a037-v8-11-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標出製造厚度偏差造成的相位誤差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map thickness error into phase error\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。"],"optionsEn":["Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度均勻性會成為光學均勻性問題。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Thickness uniformity becomes an optical-uniformity issue. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}},{"id":"a037-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-11"],"title":"比較石英蝕刻與薄膜型結構","titleEn":"Compare etched-quartz and thin-film structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks.","instruction":"比較石英蝕刻與薄膜型結構。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare etched-quartz and thin-film structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks.","observation":"不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較石英蝕刻與薄膜型結構」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare etched-quartz and thin-film structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。","textEn":"Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks."},{"id":"a037-v8-12-k2","title":"光罩結構的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mask structures: principle and limits","text":"交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","textEn":"Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較石英蝕刻與薄膜型結構」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare etched-quartz and thin-film structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有相位移光罩都完全不透光。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every phase-shift mask is completely opaque.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同結構需要不同蝕刻及清潔驗證。 交替式與衰減式相位移光罩具有不同振幅與相位配置。","explanationEn":"Different structures require different etch and cleaning checks. Alternating and attenuated phase-shift masks use different amplitude and phase layouts."}}]},{"id":"a037-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"成像窗口","titleEn":"Imaging window","description":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","descriptionEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus.","steps":[{"id":"a037-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-12"],"title":"對密集與孤立線比較成像對比","titleEn":"Compare imaging contrast for dense and isolated lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally.","instruction":"對密集與孤立線比較成像對比。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare imaging contrast for dense and isolated lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally.","observation":"一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對密集與孤立線比較成像對比」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare imaging contrast for dense and isolated lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。","textEn":"One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally."},{"id":"a037-v8-13-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對密集與孤立線比較成像對比」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare imaging contrast for dense and isolated lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。"],"optionsEn":["One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一種相位配置不會同等改善所有圖形。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"One phase scheme does not improve every pattern equally. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}},{"id":"a037-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-13"],"title":"繪製線寬對焦距的曲線","titleEn":"Plot linewidth versus focus","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window.","instruction":"繪製線寬對焦距的曲線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plot linewidth versus focus. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window.","observation":"離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製線寬對焦距的曲線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plot linewidth versus focus\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。","textEn":"Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window."},{"id":"a037-v8-14-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製線寬對焦距的曲線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plot linewidth versus focus\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。"],"optionsEn":["Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase."],"answer":1,"explanation":"離焦靈敏度是製程窗口的一部分。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"Defocus sensitivity is part of the process window. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}},{"id":"a037-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-14"],"title":"建立劑量與焦距共同容許區","titleEn":"Construct a joint dose–focus acceptance region","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns.","instruction":"建立劑量與焦距共同容許區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Construct a joint dose–focus acceptance region. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns.","observation":"窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立劑量與焦距共同容許區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Construct a joint dose–focus acceptance region\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。","textEn":"A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns."},{"id":"a037-v8-15-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立劑量與焦距共同容許區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Construct a joint dose–focus acceptance region\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。"],"optionsEn":["Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"窗口要同時滿足多個圖形的尺寸要求。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"A window must satisfy size limits for multiple patterns. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}},{"id":"a037-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-15"],"title":"檢查旁瓣是否跨過光阻閾值","titleEn":"Check whether sidelobes cross the resist threshold","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Optical sidelobes can print unintended features.","instruction":"檢查旁瓣是否跨過光阻閾值。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check whether sidelobes cross the resist threshold. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Optical sidelobes can print unintended features.","observation":"光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Optical sidelobes can print unintended features. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查旁瓣是否跨過光阻閾值」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check whether sidelobes cross the resist threshold\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Optical sidelobes can print unintended features.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。","textEn":"Optical sidelobes can print unintended features."},{"id":"a037-v8-16-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查旁瓣是否跨過光阻閾值」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check whether sidelobes cross the resist threshold\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。","最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。"],"optionsEn":["Optical sidelobes can print unintended features.","Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學旁瓣可能產生非預期圖形。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"Optical sidelobes can print unintended features. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}},{"id":"a037-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-16"],"title":"比較不同照明對相位邊界的影響","titleEn":"Compare illumination effects on phase boundaries","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Illumination changes how phase interference is used.","instruction":"比較不同照明對相位邊界的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare illumination effects on phase boundaries. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Illumination changes how phase interference is used.","observation":"照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Illumination changes how phase interference is used. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同照明對相位邊界的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare illumination effects on phase boundaries\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Illumination changes how phase interference is used.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。","textEn":"Illumination changes how phase interference is used."},{"id":"a037-v8-17-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同照明對相位邊界的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare illumination effects on phase boundaries\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。"],"optionsEn":["Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Illumination changes how phase interference is used.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase."],"answer":1,"explanation":"照明條件會改變相位干涉的利用方式。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"Illumination changes how phase interference is used. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}},{"id":"a037-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-17"],"title":"評估線端與拐角的修正需求","titleEn":"Assess correction needs at line ends and corners","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions.","instruction":"評估線端與拐角的修正需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess correction needs at line ends and corners. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions.","observation":"一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估線端與拐角的修正需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess correction needs at line ends and corners\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。","textEn":"One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions."},{"id":"a037-v8-18-k2","title":"成像窗口的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging window: principle and limits","text":"相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","textEn":"Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估線端與拐角的修正需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess correction needs at line ends and corners\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最佳焦點改善代表所有焦距都改善。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Better best-focus imaging proves improvement at every focus.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一維線條結果不能直接推廣至二維圖形。 相位移改善取決於圖形、照明與焦距。","explanationEn":"One-dimensional line results do not automatically extend to two dimensions. Phase-shift benefits depend on pattern, illumination and focus."}}]},{"id":"a037-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測與整合","titleEn":"Metrology and integration","description":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","descriptionEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements.","steps":[{"id":"a037-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-18"],"title":"分別驗證透射率與相位角","titleEn":"Verify transmission and phase angle separately","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other.","instruction":"分別驗證透射率與相位角。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Verify transmission and phase angle separately. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other.","observation":"兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分別驗證透射率與相位角」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Verify transmission and phase angle separately\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。","textEn":"Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other."},{"id":"a037-v8-19-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分別驗證透射率與相位角」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Verify transmission and phase angle separately\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","只需把兩束光強相加。"],"optionsEn":["Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","Simply add the two intensities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩者皆會改變成像但不互相替代。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"Both affect imaging but do not substitute for each other. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}},{"id":"a037-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-19"],"title":"量測圖形定位與相位邊界偏差","titleEn":"Measure placement and phase-boundary offsets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry.","instruction":"量測圖形定位與相位邊界偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure placement and phase-boundary offsets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry.","observation":"相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測圖形定位與相位邊界偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure placement and phase-boundary offsets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。","textEn":"The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry."},{"id":"a037-v8-20-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測圖形定位與相位邊界偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure placement and phase-boundary offsets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。","只需把兩束光強相加。"],"optionsEn":["Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry.","Simply add the two intensities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相位邊界位置本身是關鍵幾何量。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"The phase-boundary position is itself a critical geometry. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}},{"id":"a037-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-20"],"title":"建立修補後的空中像比較","titleEn":"Compare aerial images before and after repair","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repair can restore shape without restoring phase.","instruction":"建立修補後的空中像比較。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare aerial images before and after repair. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repair can restore shape without restoring phase.","observation":"修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repair can restore shape without restoring phase. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立修補後的空中像比較」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare aerial images before and after repair\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repair can restore shape without restoring phase.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。","textEn":"Repair can restore shape without restoring phase."},{"id":"a037-v8-21-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立修補後的空中像比較」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare aerial images before and after repair\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","只需把兩束光強相加。","修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。"],"optionsEn":["Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","Simply add the two intensities.","Repair can restore shape without restoring phase."],"answer":2,"explanation":"修補可能恢復外形卻未恢復相位。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"Repair can restore shape without restoring phase. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}},{"id":"a037-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-21"],"title":"追蹤清潔造成的光學變化","titleEn":"Track optical changes caused by cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles.","instruction":"追蹤清潔造成的光學變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track optical changes caused by cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles.","observation":"光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤清潔造成的光學變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track optical changes caused by cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。","textEn":"Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles."},{"id":"a037-v8-22-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤清潔造成的光學變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track optical changes caused by cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。","幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","只需把兩束光強相加。"],"optionsEn":["Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles.","Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","Simply add the two intensities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學性能需要跨清潔循環追蹤。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"Optical performance needs tracking across cleaning cycles. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}},{"id":"a037-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-22"],"title":"比較光罩端與晶圓端驗收","titleEn":"Compare mask-side and wafer-side acceptance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements.","instruction":"比較光罩端與晶圓端驗收。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare mask-side and wafer-side acceptance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements.","observation":"光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光罩端與晶圓端驗收」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare mask-side and wafer-side acceptance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。","textEn":"Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements."},{"id":"a037-v8-23-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光罩端與晶圓端驗收」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare mask-side and wafer-side acceptance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。","只需把兩束光強相加。"],"optionsEn":["Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements.","Simply add the two intensities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光罩量測必須能連結晶圓成像需求。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"Mask metrology must link to wafer imaging requirements. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}},{"id":"a037-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-psm","v8b-psmibm","v8b-maskqual","v8b-comp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a037-v8-23"],"title":"提交相位配置與成像窗口設計審查","titleEn":"Review phase assignment and imaging window together","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold.","instruction":"提交相位配置與成像窗口設計審查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review phase assignment and imaging window together. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold.","observation":"設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提交相位配置與成像窗口設計審查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review phase assignment and imaging window together\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a037-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。","textEn":"Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold."},{"id":"a037-v8-24-k2","title":"量測與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Metrology and integration: principle and limits","text":"光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","textEn":"Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提交相位配置與成像窗口設計審查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review phase assignment and imaging window together\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何厚度相同就必定相位相同。","只需把兩束光強相加。","設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。"],"optionsEn":["Equal geometric thickness necessarily means equal phase.","Simply add the two intensities.","Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設計可印性與光罩可製造性需共同成立。 光學相位、透射率與幾何位置須分別量測。","explanationEn":"Printability and mask manufacturability must both hold. Optical phase, transmission and geometric placement require separate measurements."}}]}]},{"id":"a038","title":"光學鄰近修正","titleEn":"Optical proximity correction","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究成像誤差、模型校準、局部修正、窗口驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: imaging error, model calibration, local correction, window validation. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["成像誤差","模型校準","局部修正","窗口驗證"],"labelsEn":["Imaging error","Model calibration","Local correction","Window validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a038-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"成像誤差","titleEn":"Imaging error","description":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","descriptionEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets.","steps":[{"id":"a038-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"疊合設計輪廓與模擬晶圓輪廓","titleEn":"Overlay target and simulated wafer contours","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Edge-placement error requires common coordinates.","instruction":"疊合設計輪廓與模擬晶圓輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Overlay target and simulated wafer contours. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Edge-placement error requires common coordinates.","observation":"邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Edge-placement error requires common coordinates. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「疊合設計輪廓與模擬晶圓輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Overlay target and simulated wafer contours\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Edge-placement error requires common coordinates.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。","textEn":"Edge-placement error requires common coordinates."},{"id":"a038-v8-01-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「疊合設計輪廓與模擬晶圓輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Overlay target and simulated wafer contours\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。"],"optionsEn":["Edge-placement error requires common coordinates.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣位置誤差需以共同座標計算。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"Edge-placement error requires common coordinates. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}},{"id":"a038-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-01"],"title":"分開線端縮短與拐角圓化","titleEn":"Separate line-end shortening from corner rounding","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者需要不同的局部修正。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The two effects need different local corrections.","instruction":"分開線端縮短與拐角圓化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「兩者需要不同的局部修正。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate line-end shortening from corner rounding. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The two effects need different local corrections.","observation":"兩者需要不同的局部修正。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The two effects need different local corrections. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開線端縮短與拐角圓化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者需要不同的局部修正。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate line-end shortening from corner rounding\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The two effects need different local corrections.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者需要不同的局部修正。","textEn":"The two effects need different local corrections."},{"id":"a038-v8-02-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開線端縮短與拐角圓化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate line-end shortening from corner rounding\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","兩者需要不同的局部修正。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。"],"optionsEn":["Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","The two effects need different local corrections.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩者需要不同的局部修正。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"The two effects need different local corrections. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}},{"id":"a038-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-02"],"title":"比較密集線與孤立線偏差","titleEn":"Compare dense- and isolated-line bias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鄰近環境改變成像。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Neighboring geometry changes imaging.","instruction":"比較密集線與孤立線偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「鄰近環境改變成像。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dense- and isolated-line bias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Neighboring geometry changes imaging.","observation":"鄰近環境改變成像。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Neighboring geometry changes imaging. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較密集線與孤立線偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鄰近環境改變成像。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dense- and isolated-line bias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Neighboring geometry changes imaging.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鄰近環境改變成像。","textEn":"Neighboring geometry changes imaging."},{"id":"a038-v8-03-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較密集線與孤立線偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dense- and isolated-line bias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","鄰近環境改變成像。"],"optionsEn":["Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Neighboring geometry changes imaging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鄰近環境改變成像。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"Neighboring geometry changes imaging. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}},{"id":"a038-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-03"],"title":"定義邊緣評估點與正負方向","titleEn":"Define edge-evaluation points and sign conventions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable.","instruction":"定義邊緣評估點與正負方向。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define edge-evaluation points and sign conventions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable.","observation":"一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義邊緣評估點與正負方向」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define edge-evaluation points and sign conventions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。","textEn":"Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable."},{"id":"a038-v8-04-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義邊緣評估點與正負方向」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define edge-evaluation points and sign conventions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。"],"optionsEn":["Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一致符號讓修正方向可判讀。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"Consistent signs make correction direction interpretable. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}},{"id":"a038-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-04"],"title":"檢查光阻閾值對輪廓的影響","titleEn":"Inspect contour sensitivity to resist threshold","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The optical image is not the final developed contour.","instruction":"檢查光阻閾值對輪廓的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect contour sensitivity to resist threshold. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: The optical image is not the final developed contour.","observation":"光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The optical image is not the final developed contour. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查光阻閾值對輪廓的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect contour sensitivity to resist threshold\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The optical image is not the final developed contour.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。","textEn":"The optical image is not the final developed contour."},{"id":"a038-v8-05-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查光阻閾值對輪廓的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect contour sensitivity to resist threshold\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。"],"optionsEn":["Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","The optical image is not the final developed contour.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學像不是最終顯影輪廓。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"The optical image is not the final developed contour. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}},{"id":"a038-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-05"],"title":"建立微影與蝕刻偏差分帳","titleEn":"Separate lithographic and etch bias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation.","instruction":"建立微影與蝕刻偏差分帳。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate lithographic and etch bias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation.","observation":"混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立微影與蝕刻偏差分帳」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate lithographic and etch bias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。","textEn":"Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation."},{"id":"a038-v8-06-k2","title":"成像誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Imaging error: principle and limits","text":"OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","textEn":"OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立微影與蝕刻偏差分帳」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate lithographic and etch bias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。"],"optionsEn":["Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"混合偏差會使補償失去可追溯性。 OPC 修正光罩以補償成像及製程偏差，不是任意更改電路目標。","explanationEn":"Mixed biases obscure the origin of compensation. OPC modifies masks to compensate imaging and process bias, not to arbitrarily alter circuit targets."}}]},{"id":"a038-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"模型校準","titleEn":"Model calibration","description":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","descriptionEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented.","steps":[{"id":"a038-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-06"],"title":"選擇涵蓋線寬與間距的校準圖形","titleEn":"Choose calibration patterns spanning widths and spaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Models need representative pattern environments.","instruction":"選擇涵蓋線寬與間距的校準圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose calibration patterns spanning widths and spaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Models need representative pattern environments.","observation":"模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Models need representative pattern environments. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選擇涵蓋線寬與間距的校準圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose calibration patterns spanning widths and spaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Models need representative pattern environments.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。","textEn":"Models need representative pattern environments."},{"id":"a038-v8-07-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選擇涵蓋線寬與間距的校準圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose calibration patterns spanning widths and spaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。"],"optionsEn":["Models need representative pattern environments.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Every edge can be corrected independently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模型需要涵蓋代表性圖形環境。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Models need representative pattern environments. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}},{"id":"a038-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-07"],"title":"保留未參與擬合的驗證圖形","titleEn":"Hold out patterns from fitting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Independent data can reveal overfitting.","instruction":"保留未參與擬合的驗證圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Hold out patterns from fitting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Independent data can reveal overfitting.","observation":"獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Independent data can reveal overfitting. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「保留未參與擬合的驗證圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Hold out patterns from fitting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Independent data can reveal overfitting.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。","textEn":"Independent data can reveal overfitting."},{"id":"a038-v8-08-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「保留未參與擬合的驗證圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Hold out patterns from fitting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。"],"optionsEn":["Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Independent data can reveal overfitting.","Every edge can be corrected independently."],"answer":1,"explanation":"獨立資料可揭露過度擬合。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Independent data can reveal overfitting. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}},{"id":"a038-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-08"],"title":"比較量測噪聲與模型殘差","titleEn":"Compare measurement noise with model residuals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘差不全是模型失準。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residuals are not entirely model error.","instruction":"比較量測噪聲與模型殘差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「殘差不全是模型失準。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare measurement noise with model residuals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residuals are not entirely model error.","observation":"殘差不全是模型失準。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residuals are not entirely model error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較量測噪聲與模型殘差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘差不全是模型失準。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare measurement noise with model residuals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residuals are not entirely model error.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘差不全是模型失準。","textEn":"Residuals are not entirely model error."},{"id":"a038-v8-09-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較量測噪聲與模型殘差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare measurement noise with model residuals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","殘差不全是模型失準。"],"optionsEn":["Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Every edge can be corrected independently.","Residuals are not entirely model error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘差不全是模型失準。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Residuals are not entirely model error. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}},{"id":"a038-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-09"],"title":"檢查參數相關性與可辨識性","titleEn":"Check parameter correlation and identifiability","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同參數可能產生相似預測。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different parameters can produce similar predictions.","instruction":"檢查參數相關性與可辨識性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同參數可能產生相似預測。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check parameter correlation and identifiability. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different parameters can produce similar predictions.","observation":"不同參數可能產生相似預測。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different parameters can produce similar predictions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查參數相關性與可辨識性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同參數可能產生相似預測。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check parameter correlation and identifiability\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different parameters can produce similar predictions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同參數可能產生相似預測。","textEn":"Different parameters can produce similar predictions."},{"id":"a038-v8-10-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查參數相關性與可辨識性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check parameter correlation and identifiability\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同參數可能產生相似預測。","訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。"],"optionsEn":["Different parameters can produce similar predictions.","Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Every edge can be corrected independently."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同參數可能產生相似預測。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Different parameters can produce similar predictions. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}},{"id":"a038-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-10"],"title":"建立量測條件與模型版號鏈結","titleEn":"Link measurement conditions to model revision","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：混用不同製程資料會污染校準。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration.","instruction":"建立量測條件與模型版號鏈結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「混用不同製程資料會污染校準。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Link measurement conditions to model revision. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration.","observation":"混用不同製程資料會污染校準。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立量測條件與模型版號鏈結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「混用不同製程資料會污染校準。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Link measurement conditions to model revision\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"混用不同製程資料會污染校準。","textEn":"Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration."},{"id":"a038-v8-11-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立量測條件與模型版號鏈結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Link measurement conditions to model revision\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","混用不同製程資料會污染校準。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。"],"optionsEn":["Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration.","Every edge can be corrected independently."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混用不同製程資料會污染校準。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Mixing process conditions contaminates calibration. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}},{"id":"a038-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-11"],"title":"標示模型無法外推的圖形","titleEn":"Mark patterns outside validated coverage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation.","instruction":"標示模型無法外推的圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark patterns outside validated coverage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation.","observation":"未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標示模型無法外推的圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark patterns outside validated coverage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。","textEn":"Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation."},{"id":"a038-v8-12-k2","title":"模型校準的原理與限制","titleEn":"Model calibration: principle and limits","text":"校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","textEn":"Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標示模型無法外推的圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark patterns outside validated coverage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["訓練誤差低就足以證明預測準確。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。"],"optionsEn":["Low training error alone proves predictive accuracy.","Every edge can be corrected independently.","Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未涵蓋圖形應增加驗證而非直接外推。 校準集與驗證集須分離，且模型應記錄適用圖形範圍。","explanationEn":"Uncovered patterns need added validation rather than blind extrapolation. Calibration and validation sets must be separate and model pattern coverage documented."}}]},{"id":"a038-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"局部修正","titleEn":"Local correction","description":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","descriptionEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field.","steps":[{"id":"a038-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-12"],"title":"以線端延伸減少縮短","titleEn":"Use line-end extension to reduce shortening","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Extension must respect neighboring spaces.","instruction":"以線端延伸減少縮短。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use line-end extension to reduce shortening. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Extension must respect neighboring spaces.","observation":"延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Extension must respect neighboring spaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以線端延伸減少縮短」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use line-end extension to reduce shortening\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Extension must respect neighboring spaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。","textEn":"Extension must respect neighboring spaces."},{"id":"a038-v8-13-k2","title":"局部修正的原理與限制","titleEn":"Local correction: principle and limits","text":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","textEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以線端延伸減少縮短」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use line-end extension to reduce shortening\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Extension must respect neighboring spaces.","Every edge can be corrected independently.","Only best focus requires verification."],"answer":0,"explanation":"延伸量須檢查鄰近空間。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Extension must respect neighboring spaces. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}},{"id":"a038-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-13"],"title":"比較加入與不加入角落修正的輪廓","titleEn":"Compare contours with and without corner correction","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours.","instruction":"比較加入與不加入角落修正的輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare contours with and without corner correction. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours.","observation":"修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較加入與不加入角落修正的輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare contours with and without corner correction\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。","textEn":"Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours."},{"id":"a038-v8-14-k2","title":"局部修正的原理與限制","titleEn":"Local correction: principle and limits","text":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","textEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較加入與不加入角落修正的輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare contours with and without corner correction\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every edge can be corrected independently.","Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours.","Only best focus requires verification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"修正效益須以晶圓輪廓評估。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Correction benefit is evaluated on wafer contours. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}},{"id":"a038-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-14"],"title":"測試次解析輔助圖形的可印性","titleEn":"Test whether subresolution assist features print","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Assists should improve main features without printing extra features.","instruction":"測試次解析輔助圖形的可印性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Test whether subresolution assist features print. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Assists should improve main features without printing extra features.","observation":"輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Assists should improve main features without printing extra features. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「測試次解析輔助圖形的可印性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Test whether subresolution assist features print\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Assists should improve main features without printing extra features.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。","textEn":"Assists should improve main features without printing extra features."},{"id":"a038-v8-15-k2","title":"局部修正的原理與限制","titleEn":"Local correction: principle and limits","text":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","textEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「測試次解析輔助圖形的可印性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Test whether subresolution assist features print\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Every edge can be corrected independently.","Only best focus requires verification.","Assists should improve main features without printing extra features."],"answer":2,"explanation":"輔助圖形應改善主圖形而不形成額外圖形。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Assists should improve main features without printing extra features. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}},{"id":"a038-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-15"],"title":"逐次更新邊緣並觀察誤差收斂","titleEn":"Update edges iteratively and track error convergence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過大更新可能振盪。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Oversized updates can cause oscillation.","instruction":"逐次更新邊緣並觀察誤差收斂。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「過大更新可能振盪。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：設目標晶圓邊緣 x=100 nm，初始模擬位置 x=94 nm。採用局部線性教學模型：4 倍縮小光罩的邊緣移動 +8 nm，晶圓邊緣只移動 +2 nm。一次修正後位置為 96 nm，帶符號誤差由 -6 nm 變為 -4 nm。不要把光罩 +8 nm 直接加到晶圓；實際 OPC 須重新模擬鄰近耦合，不能永遠沿用此固定斜率。","instructionEn":"Update edges iteratively and track error convergence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Oversized updates can cause oscillation.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Let the wafer target edge be x=100 nm and the initial prediction x=94 nm. In a local linear teaching model with 4× mask reduction, moving a mask edge +8 nm shifts the wafer edge only +2 nm. The new prediction is 96 nm and signed error changes from -6 to -4 nm. Do not add mask displacement directly to the wafer. Real OPC needs neighborhood resimulation instead of assuming this slope always holds.","observation":"過大更新可能振盪。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付修正前後 -6 nm 與 -4 nm，以及光罩／晶圓尺度標記。","observationEn":"Oversized updates can cause oscillation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport -6 nm and -4 nm with explicit mask/wafer scale labels.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「逐次更新邊緣並觀察誤差收斂」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過大更新可能振盪。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付修正前後 -6 nm 與 -4 nm，以及光罩／晶圓尺度標記。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Update edges iteratively and track error convergence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Oversized updates can cause oscillation.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report -6 nm and -4 nm with explicit mask/wafer scale labels.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過大更新可能振盪。","textEn":"Oversized updates can cause oscillation."},{"id":"a038-v8-16-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"設目標晶圓邊緣 x=100 nm，初始模擬位置 x=94 nm。採用局部線性教學模型：4 倍縮小光罩的邊緣移動 +8 nm，晶圓邊緣只移動 +2 nm。一次修正後位置為 96 nm，帶符號誤差由 -6 nm 變為 -4 nm。不要把光罩 +8 nm 直接加到晶圓；實際 OPC 須重新模擬鄰近耦合，不能永遠沿用此固定斜率。","textEn":"Let the wafer target edge be x=100 nm and the initial prediction x=94 nm. In a local linear teaching model with 4× mask reduction, moving a mask edge +8 nm shifts the wafer edge only +2 nm. The new prediction is 96 nm and signed error changes from -6 to -4 nm. Do not add mask displacement directly to the wafer. Real OPC needs neighborhood resimulation instead of assuming this slope always holds."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「逐次更新邊緣並觀察誤差收斂」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Update edges iteratively and track error convergence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["過大更新可能振盪。","每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Oversized updates can cause oscillation.","Every edge can be corrected independently.","Only best focus requires verification."],"answer":0,"explanation":"過大更新可能振盪。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Oversized updates can cause oscillation. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"設目標晶圓邊緣 x=100 nm，初始模擬位置 x=94 nm。採用局部線性教學模型：4 倍縮小光罩的邊緣移動 +8 nm，晶圓邊緣只移動 +2 nm。一次修正後位置為 96 nm，帶符號誤差由 -6 nm 變為 -4 nm。不要把光罩 +8 nm 直接加到晶圓；實際 OPC 須重新模擬鄰近耦合，不能永遠沿用此固定斜率。","textEn":"Let the wafer target edge be x=100 nm and the initial prediction x=94 nm. In a local linear teaching model with 4× mask reduction, moving a mask edge +8 nm shifts the wafer edge only +2 nm. The new prediction is 96 nm and signed error changes from -6 to -4 nm. Do not add mask displacement directly to the wafer. Real OPC needs neighborhood resimulation instead of assuming this slope always holds.","check":"交付修正前後 -6 nm 與 -4 nm，以及光罩／晶圓尺度標記。","checkEn":"Report -6 nm and -4 nm with explicit mask/wafer scale labels."}},{"id":"a038-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-16"],"title":"比較局部成本與全區成本","titleEn":"Compare local and regional objective values","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local improvement can worsen neighbors.","instruction":"比較局部成本與全區成本。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare local and regional objective values. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local improvement can worsen neighbors.","observation":"局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local improvement can worsen neighbors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較局部成本與全區成本」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare local and regional objective values\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local improvement can worsen neighbors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。","textEn":"Local improvement can worsen neighbors."},{"id":"a038-v8-17-k2","title":"局部修正的原理與限制","titleEn":"Local correction: principle and limits","text":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","textEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較局部成本與全區成本」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare local and regional objective values\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Every edge can be corrected independently.","Local improvement can worsen neighbors.","Only best focus requires verification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部改善可能惡化鄰近圖形。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Local improvement can worsen neighbors. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}},{"id":"a038-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-17"],"title":"檢查最小光罩特徵限制","titleEn":"Check minimum mask-feature constraints","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Computed solutions must remain writable.","instruction":"檢查最小光罩特徵限制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check minimum mask-feature constraints. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Computed solutions must remain writable.","observation":"計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Computed solutions must remain writable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every edge can be corrected independently.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查最小光罩特徵限制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check minimum mask-feature constraints\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Computed solutions must remain writable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。","textEn":"Computed solutions must remain writable."},{"id":"a038-v8-18-k2","title":"局部修正的原理與限制","titleEn":"Local correction: principle and limits","text":"局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","textEn":"Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查最小光罩特徵限制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check minimum mask-feature constraints\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每一條邊緣都可以完全獨立修正。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。"],"optionsEn":["Every edge can be corrected independently.","Only best focus requires verification.","Computed solutions must remain writable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"計算解仍需能被光罩設備寫入。 局部邊緣移動會改變鄰近區域的光場。","explanationEn":"Computed solutions must remain writable. Moving one edge alters the neighboring optical field."}}]},{"id":"a038-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"窗口驗證","titleEn":"Window validation","description":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","descriptionEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints.","steps":[{"id":"a038-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-18"],"title":"掃描焦距與劑量下的輪廓","titleEn":"Sweep contours across focus and dose","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point.","instruction":"掃描焦距與劑量下的輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sweep contours across focus and dose. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point.","observation":"製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「掃描焦距與劑量下的輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sweep contours across focus and dose\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。","textEn":"Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point."},{"id":"a038-v8-19-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「掃描焦距與劑量下的輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sweep contours across focus and dose\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。"],"optionsEn":["Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point.","Only best focus requires verification.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask."],"answer":0,"explanation":"製程窗口驗證需超出最佳點。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"Window validation must extend beyond the nominal point. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}},{"id":"a038-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-19"],"title":"以最壞邊緣誤差補充平均誤差","titleEn":"Supplement mean error with worst-edge error","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Averages can hide localized fatal defects.","instruction":"以最壞邊緣誤差補充平均誤差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Supplement mean error with worst-edge error. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Averages can hide localized fatal defects.","observation":"平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Averages can hide localized fatal defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以最壞邊緣誤差補充平均誤差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Supplement mean error with worst-edge error\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Averages can hide localized fatal defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。","textEn":"Averages can hide localized fatal defects."},{"id":"a038-v8-20-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以最壞邊緣誤差補充平均誤差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Supplement mean error with worst-edge error\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。"],"optionsEn":["Only best focus requires verification.","Averages can hide localized fatal defects.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均值可掩蓋局部致命缺陷。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"Averages can hide localized fatal defects. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}},{"id":"a038-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-20"],"title":"檢查橋接與斷線熱點","titleEn":"Inspect bridge and break hotspots","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：功能失效與連通性有關。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Functional failure depends on connectivity.","instruction":"檢查橋接與斷線熱點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「功能失效與連通性有關。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect bridge and break hotspots. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Functional failure depends on connectivity.","observation":"功能失效與連通性有關。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Functional failure depends on connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查橋接與斷線熱點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「功能失效與連通性有關。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect bridge and break hotspots\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Functional failure depends on connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"功能失效與連通性有關。","textEn":"Functional failure depends on connectivity."},{"id":"a038-v8-21-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查橋接與斷線熱點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect bridge and break hotspots\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","功能失效與連通性有關。"],"optionsEn":["Only best focus requires verification.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","Functional failure depends on connectivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功能失效與連通性有關。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"Functional failure depends on connectivity. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}},{"id":"a038-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-21"],"title":"比較修正前後的光罩資料量","titleEn":"Compare mask-data volume before and after correction","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：精細修正可能提高寫入成本。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fine correction can increase writing cost.","instruction":"比較修正前後的光罩資料量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「精細修正可能提高寫入成本。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare mask-data volume before and after correction. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fine correction can increase writing cost.","observation":"精細修正可能提高寫入成本。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fine correction can increase writing cost. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較修正前後的光罩資料量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「精細修正可能提高寫入成本。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare mask-data volume before and after correction\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fine correction can increase writing cost.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"精細修正可能提高寫入成本。","textEn":"Fine correction can increase writing cost."},{"id":"a038-v8-22-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較修正前後的光罩資料量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare mask-data volume before and after correction\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["精細修正可能提高寫入成本。","只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。"],"optionsEn":["Fine correction can increase writing cost.","Only best focus requires verification.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask."],"answer":0,"explanation":"精細修正可能提高寫入成本。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"Fine correction can increase writing cost. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}},{"id":"a038-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-22"],"title":"將光罩量測回饋到 OPC 模型","titleEn":"Feed mask metrology back into the OPC model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction.","instruction":"將光罩量測回饋到 OPC 模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Feed mask metrology back into the OPC model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction.","observation":"實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將光罩量測回饋到 OPC 模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Feed mask metrology back into the OPC model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。","textEn":"Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction."},{"id":"a038-v8-23-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將光罩量測回饋到 OPC 模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Feed mask metrology back into the OPC model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。"],"optionsEn":["Only best focus requires verification.","Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實際光罩偏差會影響晶圓預測。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"Actual mask bias affects wafer prediction. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}},{"id":"a038-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a038-v8-23"],"title":"提交可製造且有窗口的修正版圖","titleEn":"Submit a manufacturable correction with validated window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing.","instruction":"提交可製造且有窗口的修正版圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Submit a manufacturable correction with validated window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing.","observation":"良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有最佳焦點需要驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Only best focus requires verification.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提交可製造且有窗口的修正版圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Submit a manufacturable correction with validated window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a038-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。","textEn":"A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing."},{"id":"a038-v8-24-k2","title":"窗口驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window validation: principle and limits","text":"OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","textEn":"OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提交可製造且有窗口的修正版圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Submit a manufacturable correction with validated window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有最佳焦點需要驗證。","直接把最終晶圓圖形複製到光罩即可。","良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。"],"optionsEn":["Only best focus requires verification.","Directly copy target wafer geometry onto the mask.","A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"良好修正需兼顧成像與製造。 OPC 必須在製程窗口內驗證，並符合光罩製造限制。","explanationEn":"A sound correction balances imaging and manufacturing. OPC needs process-window verification and mask-manufacturing constraints."}}]}]},{"id":"a039","title":"反向微影計算","titleEn":"Inverse lithography computation","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究反問題定義、最佳化設計、可製造性、穩健驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: inverse problem, optimization design, manufacturability, robust validation. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["反問題定義","最佳化設計","可製造性","穩健驗證"],"labelsEn":["Inverse problem","Optimization design","Manufacturability","Robust validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a039-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"反問題定義","titleEn":"Inverse problem","description":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","descriptionEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions.","steps":[{"id":"a039-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義目標輪廓與可修改的光罩區","titleEn":"Define target contours and editable mask regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反問題需先界定設計自由度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms.","instruction":"定義目標輪廓與可修改的光罩區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「反問題需先界定設計自由度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define target contours and editable mask regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms.","observation":"反問題需先界定設計自由度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義目標輪廓與可修改的光罩區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反問題需先界定設計自由度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define target contours and editable mask regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反問題需先界定設計自由度。","textEn":"An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms."},{"id":"a039-v8-01-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義目標輪廓與可修改的光罩區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define target contours and editable mask regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反問題需先界定設計自由度。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。"],"optionsEn":["An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反問題需先界定設計自由度。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"An inverse problem requires defined design freedoms. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}},{"id":"a039-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-01"],"title":"建立從光罩到光阻的前向模型","titleEn":"Construct a mask-to-resist forward model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy.","instruction":"建立從光罩到光阻的前向模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Construct a mask-to-resist forward model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy.","observation":"反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立從光罩到光阻的前向模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Construct a mask-to-resist forward model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。","textEn":"Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy."},{"id":"a039-v8-02-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立從光罩到光阻的前向模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Construct a mask-to-resist forward model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。"],"optionsEn":["The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反演品質受前向模型準確度限制。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"Inversion quality is limited by forward-model accuracy. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}},{"id":"a039-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-02"],"title":"比較像素與曲線兩種參數化","titleEn":"Compare pixel and contour parameterization","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：參數化影響解空間與計算需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Parameterization affects the solution space and computation.","instruction":"比較像素與曲線兩種參數化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「參數化影響解空間與計算需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare pixel and contour parameterization. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Parameterization affects the solution space and computation.","observation":"參數化影響解空間與計算需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Parameterization affects the solution space and computation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較像素與曲線兩種參數化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「參數化影響解空間與計算需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare pixel and contour parameterization\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Parameterization affects the solution space and computation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"參數化影響解空間與計算需求。","textEn":"Parameterization affects the solution space and computation."},{"id":"a039-v8-03-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較像素與曲線兩種參數化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare pixel and contour parameterization\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","參數化影響解空間與計算需求。"],"optionsEn":["The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","Parameterization affects the solution space and computation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"參數化影響解空間與計算需求。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"Parameterization affects the solution space and computation. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}},{"id":"a039-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-03"],"title":"選擇邊緣誤差或影像誤差目標","titleEn":"Choose edge-error or image-error objectives","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different objectives can favor different solutions.","instruction":"選擇邊緣誤差或影像誤差目標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose edge-error or image-error objectives. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different objectives can favor different solutions.","observation":"不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different objectives can favor different solutions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選擇邊緣誤差或影像誤差目標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose edge-error or image-error objectives\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different objectives can favor different solutions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。","textEn":"Different objectives can favor different solutions."},{"id":"a039-v8-04-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選擇邊緣誤差或影像誤差目標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose edge-error or image-error objectives\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。"],"optionsEn":["Different objectives can favor different solutions.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同成本函數可能偏好不同解。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"Different objectives can favor different solutions. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}},{"id":"a039-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-04"],"title":"畫出非唯一解的簡化示例","titleEn":"Sketch a simplified nonunique solution example","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Similar wafer images can arise from different masks.","instruction":"畫出非唯一解的簡化示例。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch a simplified nonunique solution example. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Similar wafer images can arise from different masks.","observation":"相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Similar wafer images can arise from different masks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出非唯一解的簡化示例」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch a simplified nonunique solution example\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Similar wafer images can arise from different masks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。","textEn":"Similar wafer images can arise from different masks."},{"id":"a039-v8-05-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出非唯一解的簡化示例」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch a simplified nonunique solution example\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。"],"optionsEn":["The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","Similar wafer images can arise from different masks.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相似晶圓像可來自不同光罩。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"Similar wafer images can arise from different masks. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}},{"id":"a039-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-05"],"title":"保留電路連通性的不可改條件","titleEn":"Preserve noneditable circuit-connectivity constraints","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Improved printability must preserve circuit intent.","instruction":"保留電路連通性的不可改條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Preserve noneditable circuit-connectivity constraints. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Improved printability must preserve circuit intent.","observation":"可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Improved printability must preserve circuit intent. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「保留電路連通性的不可改條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Preserve noneditable circuit-connectivity constraints\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Improved printability must preserve circuit intent.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。","textEn":"Improved printability must preserve circuit intent."},{"id":"a039-v8-06-k2","title":"反問題定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Inverse problem: principle and limits","text":"反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","textEn":"Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「保留電路連通性的不可改條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Preserve noneditable circuit-connectivity constraints\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。"],"optionsEn":["The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","Improved printability must preserve circuit intent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可印性改善不能破壞電路意圖。 反向微影從目標晶圓輪廓求光罩，通常存在多種候選解。","explanationEn":"Improved printability must preserve circuit intent. Inverse lithography solves for masks from target wafer contours and can admit multiple solutions."}}]},{"id":"a039-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"最佳化設計","titleEn":"Optimization design","description":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","descriptionEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern.","steps":[{"id":"a039-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-06"],"title":"用有限差分估算邊緣移動梯度","titleEn":"Estimate an edge-movement gradient by finite differences","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise.","instruction":"用有限差分估算邊緣移動梯度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate an edge-movement gradient by finite differences. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise.","observation":"步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用有限差分估算邊緣移動梯度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate an edge-movement gradient by finite differences\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。","textEn":"Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise."},{"id":"a039-v8-07-k2","title":"最佳化設計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optimization design: principle and limits","text":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","textEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用有限差分估算邊緣移動梯度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate an edge-movement gradient by finite differences\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。"],"optionsEn":["Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture."],"answer":0,"explanation":"步長太小會放大量測或數值噪聲。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Too small a step amplifies measurement or numerical noise. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}},{"id":"a039-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-07"],"title":"比較兩個初始解的收斂路徑","titleEn":"Compare convergence from two initial masks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local optimization can depend on initialization.","instruction":"比較兩個初始解的收斂路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare convergence from two initial masks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local optimization can depend on initialization.","observation":"局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local optimization can depend on initialization. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較兩個初始解的收斂路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare convergence from two initial masks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local optimization can depend on initialization.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。","textEn":"Local optimization can depend on initialization."},{"id":"a039-v8-08-k2","title":"最佳化設計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optimization design: principle and limits","text":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","textEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較兩個初始解的收斂路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare convergence from two initial masks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。"],"optionsEn":["A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","Local optimization can depend on initialization.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部最佳化可能依賴初始條件。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Local optimization can depend on initialization. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}},{"id":"a039-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-08"],"title":"加入平滑正則項並觀察圖形","titleEn":"Add smoothing regularization and inspect the mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Smoothing trades against imaging freedom.","instruction":"加入平滑正則項並觀察圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：比較兩個假想候選光罩，使用無因次成本 J=E²+λP。A 的 E=2、P=16；B 的 E=3、P=1。λ=0 時 J_A=4、J_B=9，選 A；λ=1 時 J_A=20、J_B=10，選 B。求交叉點 λ=1/3。說明 P 是本例定義的複雜度罰項，並非真實光罩寫入成本；權重改變會改變最佳解。","instructionEn":"Add smoothing regularization and inspect the mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Smoothing trades against imaging freedom.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Compare hypothetical masks with dimensionless cost J=E²+λP. A has E=2, P=16; B has E=3, P=1. At λ=0, costs are 4 and 9, favoring A; at λ=1, costs are 20 and 10, favoring B. The crossover is λ=1/3. P is an illustrative complexity penalty, not actual mask-writing cost. Changing weights changes the preferred solution.","observation":"平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n須算出 4/9、20/10 及 λ=1/3，並交代罰項定義。","observationEn":"Smoothing trades against imaging freedom. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nCalculate 4/9, 20/10 and λ=1/3, stating the penalty definition.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「加入平滑正則項並觀察圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：須算出 4/9、20/10 及 λ=1/3，並交代罰項定義。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Add smoothing regularization and inspect the mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Smoothing trades against imaging freedom.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Calculate 4/9, 20/10 and λ=1/3, stating the penalty definition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。","textEn":"Smoothing trades against imaging freedom."},{"id":"a039-v8-09-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"比較兩個假想候選光罩，使用無因次成本 J=E²+λP。A 的 E=2、P=16；B 的 E=3、P=1。λ=0 時 J_A=4、J_B=9，選 A；λ=1 時 J_A=20、J_B=10，選 B。求交叉點 λ=1/3。說明 P 是本例定義的複雜度罰項，並非真實光罩寫入成本；權重改變會改變最佳解。","textEn":"Compare hypothetical masks with dimensionless cost J=E²+λP. A has E=2, P=16; B has E=3, P=1. At λ=0, costs are 4 and 9, favoring A; at λ=1, costs are 20 and 10, favoring B. The crossover is λ=1/3. P is an illustrative complexity penalty, not actual mask-writing cost. Changing weights changes the preferred solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「加入平滑正則項並觀察圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Add smoothing regularization and inspect the mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。"],"optionsEn":["A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Smoothing trades against imaging freedom."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平滑程度與成像自由度有取捨。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Smoothing trades against imaging freedom. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"比較兩個假想候選光罩，使用無因次成本 J=E²+λP。A 的 E=2、P=16；B 的 E=3、P=1。λ=0 時 J_A=4、J_B=9，選 A；λ=1 時 J_A=20、J_B=10，選 B。求交叉點 λ=1/3。說明 P 是本例定義的複雜度罰項，並非真實光罩寫入成本；權重改變會改變最佳解。","textEn":"Compare hypothetical masks with dimensionless cost J=E²+λP. A has E=2, P=16; B has E=3, P=1. At λ=0, costs are 4 and 9, favoring A; at λ=1, costs are 20 and 10, favoring B. The crossover is λ=1/3. P is an illustrative complexity penalty, not actual mask-writing cost. Changing weights changes the preferred solution.","check":"須算出 4/9、20/10 及 λ=1/3，並交代罰項定義。","checkEn":"Calculate 4/9, 20/10 and λ=1/3, stating the penalty definition."}},{"id":"a039-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-09"],"title":"檢查更新步長對振盪的影響","titleEn":"Check update-step effects on oscillation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality.","instruction":"檢查更新步長對振盪的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check update-step effects on oscillation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality.","observation":"成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查更新步長對振盪的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check update-step effects on oscillation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。","textEn":"Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality."},{"id":"a039-v8-10-k2","title":"最佳化設計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optimization design: principle and limits","text":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","textEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查更新步長對振盪的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check update-step effects on oscillation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。","成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。"],"optionsEn":["Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality.","A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture."],"answer":0,"explanation":"成本下降速度不等於最終解品質。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Fast cost reduction does not guarantee final solution quality. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}},{"id":"a039-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-10"],"title":"分開訓練圖形與盲測圖形","titleEn":"Separate training and blind-test patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias.","instruction":"分開訓練圖形與盲測圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate training and blind-test patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias.","observation":"盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開訓練圖形與盲測圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate training and blind-test patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。","textEn":"Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias."},{"id":"a039-v8-11-k2","title":"最佳化設計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optimization design: principle and limits","text":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","textEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開訓練圖形與盲測圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate training and blind-test patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。"],"optionsEn":["A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"盲測有助於發現模型與最佳化偏誤。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Blind testing helps reveal model and optimization bias. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}},{"id":"a039-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-11"],"title":"記錄每次迭代的限制違反","titleEn":"Record constraint violations at each iteration","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost.","instruction":"記錄每次迭代的限制違反。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Record constraint violations at each iteration. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost.","observation":"可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄每次迭代的限制違反」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Record constraint violations at each iteration\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。","textEn":"Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost."},{"id":"a039-v8-12-k2","title":"最佳化設計的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optimization design: principle and limits","text":"目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","textEn":"The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄每次迭代的限制違反」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Record constraint violations at each iteration\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成本下降就表示所有限制都滿足。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["A lower cost proves all constraints are satisfied.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可行性應與成本值一起追蹤。 目標函數與正則化共同決定求得的圖形。","explanationEn":"Feasibility should be tracked alongside cost. The objective and regularization jointly determine the resulting pattern."}}]},{"id":"a039-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"可製造性","titleEn":"Manufacturability","description":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","descriptionEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands.","steps":[{"id":"a039-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-12"],"title":"設定最小曲率半徑與間距","titleEn":"Set minimum curvature radius and spacing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask writability constrains fine curvature.","instruction":"設定最小曲率半徑與間距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Set minimum curvature radius and spacing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask writability constrains fine curvature.","observation":"光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask writability constrains fine curvature. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設定最小曲率半徑與間距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Set minimum curvature radius and spacing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask writability constrains fine curvature.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。","textEn":"Mask writability constrains fine curvature."},{"id":"a039-v8-13-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設定最小曲率半徑與間距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Set minimum curvature radius and spacing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。"],"optionsEn":["Mask writability constrains fine curvature.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光罩可寫入性限制細小曲率。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Mask writability constrains fine curvature. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}},{"id":"a039-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-13"],"title":"將曲線轉成寫入資料並比較輪廓","titleEn":"Convert curves to writing data and compare contours","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Data discretization introduces additional edge error.","instruction":"將曲線轉成寫入資料並比較輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Convert curves to writing data and compare contours. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Data discretization introduces additional edge error.","observation":"資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Data discretization introduces additional edge error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將曲線轉成寫入資料並比較輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Convert curves to writing data and compare contours\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Data discretization introduces additional edge error.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。","textEn":"Data discretization introduces additional edge error."},{"id":"a039-v8-14-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將曲線轉成寫入資料並比較輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Convert curves to writing data and compare contours\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。"],"optionsEn":["More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Data discretization introduces additional edge error.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料離散化會引入新的邊緣誤差。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Data discretization introduces additional edge error. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}},{"id":"a039-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-14"],"title":"估算多束寫入的資料吞吐需求","titleEn":"Estimate data throughput for multibeam writing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities.","instruction":"估算多束寫入的資料吞吐需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate data throughput for multibeam writing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities.","observation":"光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算多束寫入的資料吞吐需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate data throughput for multibeam writing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。","textEn":"Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities."},{"id":"a039-v8-15-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算多束寫入的資料吞吐需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate data throughput for multibeam writing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。"],"optionsEn":["More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities."],"answer":2,"explanation":"光罩計算與寫入能力必須相容。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Mask computation must be compatible with writer capabilities. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}},{"id":"a039-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-15"],"title":"比較曲線區與直線區的量測取樣","titleEn":"Compare metrology sampling on curves and straight edges","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density.","instruction":"比較曲線區與直線區的量測取樣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare metrology sampling on curves and straight edges. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density.","observation":"曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較曲線區與直線區的量測取樣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare metrology sampling on curves and straight edges\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。","textEn":"Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density."},{"id":"a039-v8-16-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較曲線區與直線區的量測取樣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare metrology sampling on curves and straight edges\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。","曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。"],"optionsEn":["Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density.","More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests."],"answer":0,"explanation":"曲線量測需要足夠的方向與密度。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Curve metrology needs adequate orientations and density. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}},{"id":"a039-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-16"],"title":"加入光罩製造偏差再模擬","titleEn":"Resimulate with mask-fabrication bias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error.","instruction":"加入光罩製造偏差再模擬。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Resimulate with mask-fabrication bias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error.","observation":"理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「加入光罩製造偏差再模擬」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Resimulate with mask-fabrication bias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。","textEn":"Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error."},{"id":"a039-v8-17-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「加入光罩製造偏差再模擬」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Resimulate with mask-fabrication bias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。"],"optionsEn":["More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests."],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想光罩解需要考慮實體製作誤差。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Ideal mask solutions must account for fabrication error. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}},{"id":"a039-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-17"],"title":"評估小缺陷修補的可行區","titleEn":"Evaluate feasible repair regions for small defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fine complex patterns can complicate repair.","instruction":"評估小缺陷修補的可行區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Evaluate feasible repair regions for small defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fine complex patterns can complicate repair.","observation":"極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fine complex patterns can complicate repair. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估小缺陷修補的可行區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Evaluate feasible repair regions for small defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fine complex patterns can complicate repair.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。","textEn":"Fine complex patterns can complicate repair."},{"id":"a039-v8-18-k2","title":"可製造性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Manufacturability: principle and limits","text":"曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","textEn":"Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估小缺陷修補的可行區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Evaluate feasible repair regions for small defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曲線越複雜就一定越容易製造。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。"],"optionsEn":["More complex curves are necessarily easier to manufacture.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","Fine complex patterns can complicate repair."],"answer":2,"explanation":"極細複雜圖形可能增加修補難度。 曲線光罩可改善自由度，也增加資料與量測要求。","explanationEn":"Fine complex patterns can complicate repair. Curvilinear masks add freedom and increase data and metrology demands."}}]},{"id":"a039-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"穩健驗證","titleEn":"Robust validation","description":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","descriptionEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors.","steps":[{"id":"a039-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-18"],"title":"把多個焦距點加入成本函數","titleEn":"Include several focus points in the objective","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting.","instruction":"把多個焦距點加入成本函數。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Include several focus points in the objective. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting.","observation":"多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把多個焦距點加入成本函數」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Include several focus points in the objective\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。","textEn":"Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting."},{"id":"a039-v8-19-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把多個焦距點加入成本函數」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Include several focus points in the objective\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。"],"optionsEn":["Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多條件最佳化可避免名目點過度最佳化。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"Multi-condition optimization reduces nominal-point overfitting. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}},{"id":"a039-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-19"],"title":"比較劑量偏差下的邊緣誤差分布","titleEn":"Compare edge-error distributions under dose shifts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean.","instruction":"比較劑量偏差下的邊緣誤差分布。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare edge-error distributions under dose shifts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean.","observation":"尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較劑量偏差下的邊緣誤差分布」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare edge-error distributions under dose shifts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。","textEn":"Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean."},{"id":"a039-v8-20-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較劑量偏差下的邊緣誤差分布」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare edge-error distributions under dose shifts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。"],"optionsEn":["Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾端誤差比平均值更能顯示局部風險。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"Tail errors reveal local risk better than the mean. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}},{"id":"a039-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-20"],"title":"用獨立模型交叉檢查熱點","titleEn":"Cross-check hotspots with an independent model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias.","instruction":"用獨立模型交叉檢查熱點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Cross-check hotspots with an independent model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias.","observation":"相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用獨立模型交叉檢查熱點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Cross-check hotspots with an independent model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。","textEn":"Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias."},{"id":"a039-v8-21-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用獨立模型交叉檢查熱點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Cross-check hotspots with an independent model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。"],"optionsEn":["Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同模型自我驗證可能漏掉共同偏誤。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"Self-validation with one model can miss shared bias. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}},{"id":"a039-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-21"],"title":"建立計算成本與可印性比較表","titleEn":"Compare computational cost with printability","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit.","instruction":"建立計算成本與可印性比較表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare computational cost with printability. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit.","observation":"更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立計算成本與可印性比較表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare computational cost with printability\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。","textEn":"More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit."},{"id":"a039-v8-22-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立計算成本與可印性比較表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare computational cost with printability\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。","名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。"],"optionsEn":["More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit.","Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更昂貴的求解需要可量測的收益。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"More expensive optimization needs measurable benefit. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}},{"id":"a039-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-22"],"title":"標記尚未取得晶圓證據的主張","titleEn":"Mark claims lacking wafer evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement.","instruction":"標記尚未取得晶圓證據的主張。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark claims lacking wafer evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement.","observation":"模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記尚未取得晶圓證據的主張」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark claims lacking wafer evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。","textEn":"Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement."},{"id":"a039-v8-23-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記尚未取得晶圓證據的主張」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark claims lacking wafer evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。"],"optionsEn":["Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模擬改善不是晶圓實測改善。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"Simulated improvement is not measured wafer improvement. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}},{"id":"a039-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-jeol","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a039-v8-23"],"title":"交付光罩、模型與窗口的版本封包","titleEn":"Deliver versioned mask, model and process window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints.","instruction":"交付光罩、模型與窗口的版本封包。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver versioned mask, model and process window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints.","observation":"可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付光罩、模型與窗口的版本封包」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver versioned mask, model and process window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a039-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。","textEn":"Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints."},{"id":"a039-v8-24-k2","title":"穩健驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Robust validation: principle and limits","text":"單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","textEn":"A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付光罩、模型與窗口的版本封包」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver versioned mask, model and process window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目條件合格即可省略擾動測試。","反問題永遠只有唯一光罩解。","可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。"],"optionsEn":["Passing nominal conditions removes the need for perturbation tests.","The inverse problem always has one unique mask solution.","Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可重現性需要完整的輸入與限制。 單一條件的最佳解未必對焦距、劑量及光罩誤差穩健。","explanationEn":"Reproducibility needs complete inputs and constraints. A single-condition optimum may be fragile to focus, dose and mask errors."}}]}]},{"id":"a040","title":"浸潤式微影製程","titleEn":"Immersion lithography processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究光學與液體、表面與液體介面、掃描與誤差、微影整合；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: optics and liquid, surface and liquid interfaces, scanning and error, lithographic integration. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["光學與液體","表面與液體介面","掃描與誤差","微影整合"],"labelsEn":["Optics and liquid","Surface and liquid interfaces","Scanning and error","Lithographic integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a040-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"光學與液體","titleEn":"Optics and liquid","description":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","descriptionEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space.","steps":[{"id":"a040-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"用 NA=n sinθ 比較乾式與浸潤式","titleEn":"Compare dry and immersion imaging using NA=n sinθ","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture.","instruction":"用 NA=n sinθ 比較乾式與浸潤式。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dry and immersion imaging using NA=n sinθ. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture.","observation":"折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用 NA=n sinθ 比較乾式與浸潤式」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dry and immersion imaging using NA=n sinθ\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。","textEn":"Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture."},{"id":"a040-v8-01-k2","title":"光學與液體的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optics and liquid: principle and limits","text":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","textEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用 NA=n sinθ 比較乾式與浸潤式」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dry and immersion imaging using NA=n sinθ\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。"],"optionsEn":["Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"折射率與入射角共同決定數值孔徑。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Index and ray angle jointly determine numerical aperture. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}},{"id":"a040-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-01"],"title":"計算固定波長下的相對解析度","titleEn":"Calculate relative resolution at fixed wavelength","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed.","instruction":"計算固定波長下的相對解析度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Calculate relative resolution at fixed wavelength. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed.","observation":"Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算固定波長下的相對解析度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate relative resolution at fixed wavelength\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。","textEn":"Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed."},{"id":"a040-v8-02-k2","title":"光學與液體的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optics and liquid: principle and limits","text":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","textEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算固定波長下的相對解析度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate relative resolution at fixed wavelength\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Rayleigh 比較須固定其餘模型係數。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Rayleigh comparisons require other model factors to remain fixed. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}},{"id":"a040-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-02"],"title":"比較解析度與焦深的縮放","titleEn":"Compare resolution and depth-of-focus scaling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity.","instruction":"比較解析度與焦深的縮放。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設波長、k₁、k₂ 都固定，只把 NA 從 1.00 改為 1.35。由 CD∝1/NA，CD 比值為 0.741；由 DOF∝1/NA²，焦深比值為 0.549。若原假想 CD=100 nm、DOF=200 nm，新值約為 74.1 nm、109.7 nm。這是相對縮放示例，不能視為特定掃描機的保證尺寸。","instructionEn":"Compare resolution and depth-of-focus scaling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Hold wavelength, k₁ and k₂ fixed while changing NA from 1.00 to 1.35. CD∝1/NA gives a ratio of 0.741; DOF∝1/NA² gives 0.549. Hypothetical initial CD=100 nm and DOF=200 nm become approximately 74.1 nm and 109.7 nm. These are scaling examples, not scanner performance guarantees.","observation":"提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n同時報告解析度改善與焦深縮小，不可只選前者。","observationEn":"Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport both improved resolution and reduced depth of focus.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較解析度與焦深的縮放」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：同時報告解析度改善與焦深縮小，不可只選前者。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare resolution and depth-of-focus scaling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report both improved resolution and reduced depth of focus.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。","textEn":"Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity."},{"id":"a040-v8-03-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設波長、k₁、k₂ 都固定，只把 NA 從 1.00 改為 1.35。由 CD∝1/NA，CD 比值為 0.741；由 DOF∝1/NA²，焦深比值為 0.549。若原假想 CD=100 nm、DOF=200 nm，新值約為 74.1 nm、109.7 nm。這是相對縮放示例，不能視為特定掃描機的保證尺寸。","textEn":"Hold wavelength, k₁ and k₂ fixed while changing NA from 1.00 to 1.35. CD∝1/NA gives a ratio of 0.741; DOF∝1/NA² gives 0.549. Hypothetical initial CD=100 nm and DOF=200 nm become approximately 74.1 nm and 109.7 nm. These are scaling examples, not scanner performance guarantees."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較解析度與焦深的縮放」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare resolution and depth-of-focus scaling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"提高 NA 通常使焦深更敏感。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Higher NA generally tightens depth-of-focus sensitivity. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設波長、k₁、k₂ 都固定，只把 NA 從 1.00 改為 1.35。由 CD∝1/NA，CD 比值為 0.741；由 DOF∝1/NA²，焦深比值為 0.549。若原假想 CD=100 nm、DOF=200 nm，新值約為 74.1 nm、109.7 nm。這是相對縮放示例，不能視為特定掃描機的保證尺寸。","textEn":"Hold wavelength, k₁ and k₂ fixed while changing NA from 1.00 to 1.35. CD∝1/NA gives a ratio of 0.741; DOF∝1/NA² gives 0.549. Hypothetical initial CD=100 nm and DOF=200 nm become approximately 74.1 nm and 109.7 nm. These are scaling examples, not scanner performance guarantees.","check":"同時報告解析度改善與焦深縮小，不可只選前者。","checkEn":"Report both improved resolution and reduced depth of focus."}},{"id":"a040-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-03"],"title":"畫出鏡頭、液體與晶圓的光路","titleEn":"Sketch the lens–liquid–wafer optical path","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：液體介面不能從光路中省略。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path.","instruction":"畫出鏡頭、液體與晶圓的光路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「液體介面不能從光路中省略。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch the lens–liquid–wafer optical path. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path.","observation":"液體介面不能從光路中省略。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出鏡頭、液體與晶圓的光路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「液體介面不能從光路中省略。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch the lens–liquid–wafer optical path\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"液體介面不能從光路中省略。","textEn":"Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path."},{"id":"a040-v8-04-k2","title":"光學與液體的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optics and liquid: principle and limits","text":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","textEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出鏡頭、液體與晶圓的光路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch the lens–liquid–wafer optical path\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["液體介面不能從光路中省略。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。"],"optionsEn":["Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"液體介面不能從光路中省略。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Liquid interfaces cannot be omitted from the optical path. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}},{"id":"a040-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-04"],"title":"檢查氣泡造成的局部折射變化","titleEn":"Assess local refraction caused by a bubble","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption.","instruction":"檢查氣泡造成的局部折射變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess local refraction caused by a bubble. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption.","observation":"氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查氣泡造成的局部折射變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess local refraction caused by a bubble\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。","textEn":"Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption."},{"id":"a040-v8-05-k2","title":"光學與液體的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optics and liquid: principle and limits","text":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","textEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查氣泡造成的局部折射變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess local refraction caused by a bubble\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣泡會破壞均勻介質假設。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Bubbles violate the uniform-medium assumption. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}},{"id":"a040-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-05"],"title":"列出折射率隨溫度變化的誤差鏈","titleEn":"Trace temperature-dependent index into imaging error","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal stability becomes optical stability.","instruction":"列出折射率隨溫度變化的誤差鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace temperature-dependent index into imaging error. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal stability becomes optical stability.","observation":"熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal stability becomes optical stability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出折射率隨溫度變化的誤差鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace temperature-dependent index into imaging error\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal stability becomes optical stability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。","textEn":"Thermal stability becomes optical stability."},{"id":"a040-v8-06-k2","title":"光學與液體的原理與限制","titleEn":"Optics and liquid: principle and limits","text":"浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","textEn":"Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出折射率隨溫度變化的誤差鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace temperature-dependent index into imaging error\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Thermal stability becomes optical stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱穩定性會變成光學穩定性。 浸潤提高晶圓側成像介質折射率，數值孔徑需依所定義空間計算。","explanationEn":"Thermal stability becomes optical stability. Immersion raises the wafer-side imaging-medium refractive index; NA must be defined in the appropriate optical space."}}]},{"id":"a040-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面與液體介面","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces","description":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","descriptionEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process.","steps":[{"id":"a040-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-06"],"title":"比較有頂層與無頂層的介面","titleEn":"Compare coated and uncoated resist interfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions.","instruction":"比較有頂層與無頂層的介面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare coated and uncoated resist interfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions.","observation":"保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較有頂層與無頂層的介面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare coated and uncoated resist interfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。","textEn":"A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions."},{"id":"a040-v8-07-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較有頂層與無頂層的介面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare coated and uncoated resist interfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。"],"optionsEn":["A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保護層會改變接觸、溶出及光學條件。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"A protective layer changes contact, leaching and optical conditions. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}},{"id":"a040-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-07"],"title":"以接觸角示意液體潤濕","titleEn":"Illustrate wetting with contact-angle measurements","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning.","instruction":"以接觸角示意液體潤濕。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Illustrate wetting with contact-angle measurements. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning.","observation":"靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以接觸角示意液體潤濕」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Illustrate wetting with contact-angle measurements\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。","textEn":"Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning."},{"id":"a040-v8-08-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以接觸角示意液體潤濕」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Illustrate wetting with contact-angle measurements\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。"],"optionsEn":["The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靜態接觸角不能完全代表動態掃描。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"Static contact angles do not fully describe dynamic scanning. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}},{"id":"a040-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-08"],"title":"建立光阻成分溶出的檢查表","titleEn":"Plan checks for resist-component leaching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces.","instruction":"建立光阻成分溶出的檢查表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan checks for resist-component leaching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces.","observation":"溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立光阻成分溶出的檢查表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan checks for resist-component leaching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。","textEn":"Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces."},{"id":"a040-v8-09-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立光阻成分溶出的檢查表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan checks for resist-component leaching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。"],"optionsEn":["The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溶出可能影響液體與光學表面。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"Leaching can affect liquid and optical surfaces. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}},{"id":"a040-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-09"],"title":"分辨水痕與曝光圖形缺陷","titleEn":"Distinguish watermarks from pattern defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence.","instruction":"分辨水痕與曝光圖形缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish watermarks from pattern defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence.","observation":"缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分辨水痕與曝光圖形缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish watermarks from pattern defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。","textEn":"Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence."},{"id":"a040-v8-10-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分辨水痕與曝光圖形缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish watermarks from pattern defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。","頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence.","The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷外觀需結合曝光前後位置。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"Defect appearance needs before/after spatial evidence. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}},{"id":"a040-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-10"],"title":"檢查晶圓邊緣液體管理","titleEn":"Assess liquid management at wafer edges","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions.","instruction":"檢查晶圓邊緣液體管理。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess liquid management at wafer edges. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions.","observation":"邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查晶圓邊緣液體管理」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess liquid management at wafer edges\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。","textEn":"Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions."},{"id":"a040-v8-11-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查晶圓邊緣液體管理」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess liquid management at wafer edges\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。"],"optionsEn":["The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior."],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣幾何改變液體邊界條件。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"Edge geometry changes liquid boundary conditions. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}},{"id":"a040-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-11"],"title":"規畫顆粒與液體潔淨度取樣","titleEn":"Plan particle and liquid-cleanliness sampling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface.","instruction":"規畫顆粒與液體潔淨度取樣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan particle and liquid-cleanliness sampling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface.","observation":"過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「頂層完全不影響光阻反應。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫顆粒與液體潔淨度取樣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan particle and liquid-cleanliness sampling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。","textEn":"Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface."},{"id":"a040-v8-12-k2","title":"表面與液體介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Surface and liquid interfaces: principle and limits","text":"液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","textEn":"Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫顆粒與液體潔淨度取樣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan particle and liquid-cleanliness sampling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["頂層完全不影響光阻反應。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。"],"optionsEn":["The topcoat cannot affect resist behavior.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過濾性能不代表表面完全無顆粒。 液體、頂層與光阻的相容性是成像條件的一部分。","explanationEn":"Filtration performance does not prove a particle-free surface. Compatibility among liquid, topcoat and resist is part of the imaging process."}}]},{"id":"a040-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"掃描與誤差","titleEn":"Scanning and error","description":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","descriptionEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects.","steps":[{"id":"a040-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-12"],"title":"追蹤掃描方向與缺陷條紋","titleEn":"Relate scan direction to defect streaks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects.","instruction":"追蹤掃描方向與缺陷條紋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate scan direction to defect streaks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects.","observation":"方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤掃描方向與缺陷條紋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate scan direction to defect streaks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。","textEn":"Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects."},{"id":"a040-v8-13-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤掃描方向與缺陷條紋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate scan direction to defect streaks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。"],"optionsEn":["Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向性缺陷可提供液體或運動線索。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Directional defects can reveal fluid or motion effects. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}},{"id":"a040-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-13"],"title":"比較加速段與等速段的液體介面","titleEn":"Compare liquid interfaces during acceleration and steady motion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：暫態條件可能不同於穩態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transient conditions can differ from steady state.","instruction":"比較加速段與等速段的液體介面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「暫態條件可能不同於穩態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare liquid interfaces during acceleration and steady motion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transient conditions can differ from steady state.","observation":"暫態條件可能不同於穩態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transient conditions can differ from steady state. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較加速段與等速段的液體介面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「暫態條件可能不同於穩態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare liquid interfaces during acceleration and steady motion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transient conditions can differ from steady state.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"暫態條件可能不同於穩態。","textEn":"Transient conditions can differ from steady state."},{"id":"a040-v8-14-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較加速段與等速段的液體介面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare liquid interfaces during acceleration and steady motion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","暫態條件可能不同於穩態。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。"],"optionsEn":["Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","Transient conditions can differ from steady state.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫態條件可能不同於穩態。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Transient conditions can differ from steady state. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}},{"id":"a040-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-14"],"title":"將焦點地圖與晶圓翹曲疊合","titleEn":"Overlay focus maps with wafer bow","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Substrate topography consumes focus budget.","instruction":"將焦點地圖與晶圓翹曲疊合。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Overlay focus maps with wafer bow. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Substrate topography consumes focus budget.","observation":"基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Substrate topography consumes focus budget. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將焦點地圖與晶圓翹曲疊合」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Overlay focus maps with wafer bow\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Substrate topography consumes focus budget.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。","textEn":"Substrate topography consumes focus budget."},{"id":"a040-v8-15-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將焦點地圖與晶圓翹曲疊合」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Overlay focus maps with wafer bow\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。"],"optionsEn":["Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Substrate topography consumes focus budget."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基板形貌會消耗焦點預算。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Substrate topography consumes focus budget. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}},{"id":"a040-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-15"],"title":"拆解工具間套刻誤差","titleEn":"Decompose tool-to-tool overlay error","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多機混用需要交叉匹配。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Using several tools requires cross-matching.","instruction":"拆解工具間套刻誤差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「多機混用需要交叉匹配。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Decompose tool-to-tool overlay error. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Using several tools requires cross-matching.","observation":"多機混用需要交叉匹配。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Using several tools requires cross-matching. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「拆解工具間套刻誤差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多機混用需要交叉匹配。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Decompose tool-to-tool overlay error\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Using several tools requires cross-matching.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多機混用需要交叉匹配。","textEn":"Using several tools requires cross-matching."},{"id":"a040-v8-16-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「拆解工具間套刻誤差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Decompose tool-to-tool overlay error\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多機混用需要交叉匹配。","速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。"],"optionsEn":["Using several tools requires cross-matching.","Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多機混用需要交叉匹配。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Using several tools requires cross-matching. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}},{"id":"a040-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-16"],"title":"比較曝光前量測與曝光中控制","titleEn":"Compare pre-exposure measurement with in-exposure control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Feedforward and feedback address different timescales.","instruction":"比較曝光前量測與曝光中控制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare pre-exposure measurement with in-exposure control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Feedforward and feedback address different timescales.","observation":"前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Feedforward and feedback address different timescales. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較曝光前量測與曝光中控制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare pre-exposure measurement with in-exposure control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Feedforward and feedback address different timescales.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。","textEn":"Feedforward and feedback address different timescales."},{"id":"a040-v8-17-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較曝光前量測與曝光中控制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare pre-exposure measurement with in-exposure control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。"],"optionsEn":["Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","Feedforward and feedback address different timescales.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process."],"answer":1,"explanation":"前饋與回饋處理不同時間尺度。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Feedforward and feedback address different timescales. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}},{"id":"a040-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-17"],"title":"建立液體溫度與焦點漂移的關聯","titleEn":"Relate liquid temperature to focus drift","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources.","instruction":"建立液體溫度與焦點漂移的關聯。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate liquid temperature to focus drift. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources.","observation":"相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「速度提高不會改變液體狀態。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立液體溫度與焦點漂移的關聯」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate liquid temperature to focus drift\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。","textEn":"Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources."},{"id":"a040-v8-18-k2","title":"掃描與誤差的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scanning and error: principle and limits","text":"動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","textEn":"Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立液體溫度與焦點漂移的關聯」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate liquid temperature to focus drift\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["速度提高不會改變液體狀態。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。"],"optionsEn":["Higher speed cannot affect liquid behavior.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相關性仍需排除其他漂移來源。 動態液體管理會連結掃描速度、溫度與缺陷。","explanationEn":"Correlation still requires excluding other drift sources. Dynamic liquid management couples scan speed, temperature and defects."}}]},{"id":"a040-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"微影整合","titleEn":"Lithographic integration","description":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","descriptionEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation.","steps":[{"id":"a040-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-18"],"title":"建立劑量焦距矩陣並檢查線端","titleEn":"Build a dose–focus matrix including line ends","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout.","instruction":"建立劑量焦距矩陣並檢查線端。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a dose–focus matrix including line ends. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout.","observation":"一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立劑量焦距矩陣並檢查線端」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a dose–focus matrix including line ends\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。","textEn":"One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout."},{"id":"a040-v8-19-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立劑量焦距矩陣並檢查線端」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a dose–focus matrix including line ends\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。"],"optionsEn":["One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一維線寬不能代表所有版圖。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"One-dimensional linewidth does not represent every layout. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}},{"id":"a040-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-19"],"title":"比較浸潤單次與多重圖案化","titleEn":"Compare immersion single exposure with multipatterning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces.","instruction":"比較浸潤單次與多重圖案化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare immersion single exposure with multipatterning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces.","observation":"多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較浸潤單次與多重圖案化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare immersion single exposure with multipatterning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。","textEn":"Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces."},{"id":"a040-v8-20-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較浸潤單次與多重圖案化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare immersion single exposure with multipatterning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。"],"optionsEn":["The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多重圖案化加入套刻與製程介面。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"Multipatterning adds overlay and process interfaces. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}},{"id":"a040-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-20"],"title":"追蹤光阻到硬罩的轉移偏差","titleEn":"Track resist-to-hard-mask transfer bias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification.","instruction":"追蹤光阻到硬罩的轉移偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track resist-to-hard-mask transfer bias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification.","observation":"曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤光阻到硬罩的轉移偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track resist-to-hard-mask transfer bias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。","textEn":"Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification."},{"id":"a040-v8-21-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤光阻到硬罩的轉移偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track resist-to-hard-mask transfer bias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曝光品質需延伸到圖案轉移驗證。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"Exposure quality must extend into pattern-transfer verification. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}},{"id":"a040-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-21"],"title":"比較晶圓中心與邊緣缺陷密度","titleEn":"Compare center and edge defect densities","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions.","instruction":"比較晶圓中心與邊緣缺陷密度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare center and edge defect densities. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions.","observation":"空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較晶圓中心與邊緣缺陷密度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare center and edge defect densities\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。","textEn":"Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions."},{"id":"a040-v8-22-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較晶圓中心與邊緣缺陷密度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare center and edge defect densities\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。","解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。"],"optionsEn":["Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions.","The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"空間取樣不能只挑最佳區域。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"Spatial sampling must not select only favorable regions. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}},{"id":"a040-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-22"],"title":"分析吞吐量與良率的共同限制","titleEn":"Analyze throughput and yield together","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise.","instruction":"分析吞吐量與良率的共同限制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Analyze throughput and yield together. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise.","observation":"更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分析吞吐量與良率的共同限制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Analyze throughput and yield together\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。","textEn":"Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise."},{"id":"a040-v8-23-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分析吞吐量與良率的共同限制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Analyze throughput and yield together\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。"],"optionsEn":["The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更快曝光若增加缺陷未必提升有效產出。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"Faster exposure may not increase useful output if defects rise. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}},{"id":"a040-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-lenses","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a040-v8-23"],"title":"交付光學、液體與量測整合圖","titleEn":"Deliver an integrated optics–fluid–metrology diagram","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process.","instruction":"交付光學、液體與量測整合圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver an integrated optics–fluid–metrology diagram. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process.","observation":"浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The smallest resolved line proves the best process.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付光學、液體與量測整合圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver an integrated optics–fluid–metrology diagram\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a040-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。","textEn":"Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process."},{"id":"a040-v8-24-k2","title":"微影整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Lithographic integration: principle and limits","text":"解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","textEn":"Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付光學、液體與量測整合圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver an integrated optics–fluid–metrology diagram\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["解析線寬最小就代表製程最好。","浸潤只要把晶圓浸水即可。","浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。"],"optionsEn":["The smallest resolved line proves the best process.","Immersion simply requires submerging a wafer.","Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浸潤微影是多子系統協同工程。 解析度、套刻與缺陷率必須同時驗證。","explanationEn":"Immersion lithography is a coordinated multisystem process. Resolution, overlay and defect rate require joint validation."}}]}]},{"id":"a041","title":"極紫外曝光製程整合","titleEn":"EUV exposure process integration","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究系統與圖形、材料與光罩、窗口與缺陷、電性與整合；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: system and patterns, materials and masks, window and defects, electrical integration. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["系統與圖形","材料與光罩","窗口與缺陷","電性與整合"],"labelsEn":["System and patterns","Materials and masks","Window and defects","Electrical integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a041-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"系統與圖形","titleEn":"System and patterns","description":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","descriptionEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors.","steps":[{"id":"a041-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出光源至晶圓的反射路徑","titleEn":"Sketch the reflective source-to-wafer path","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput.","instruction":"畫出光源至晶圓的反射路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：在假設的四面反射鏡教學光路中，每面能量反射率皆為 0.70，且忽略其他損失。總傳輸比例為 0.70⁴=0.2401；100 單位入射能量只剩 24.01 單位。若其中一面因污染變成 0.60，剩餘為 0.70³×0.60=20.58，較原來降低 14.3%。本例鏡數與反射率不是任何 EUV 機台規格。","instructionEn":"Sketch the reflective source-to-wafer path. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): In a hypothetical four-mirror path, each mirror has energy reflectivity 0.70 and other losses are ignored. Total transmission is 0.70⁴=0.2401, leaving 24.01 of 100 incident energy units. If one mirror falls to 0.60, the result is 0.70³×0.60=20.58, a 14.3% relative decrease. Mirror count and reflectivities are not specifications of any EUV scanner.","observation":"EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n用乘積得到 24.01 與 20.58，不可把反射率直接相加。","observationEn":"Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nUse products to obtain 24.01 and 20.58; do not add reflectivities.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出光源至晶圓的反射路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：用乘積得到 24.01 與 20.58，不可把反射率直接相加。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch the reflective source-to-wafer path\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Use products to obtain 24.01 and 20.58; do not add reflectivities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。","textEn":"Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput."},{"id":"a041-v8-01-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"在假設的四面反射鏡教學光路中，每面能量反射率皆為 0.70，且忽略其他損失。總傳輸比例為 0.70⁴=0.2401；100 單位入射能量只剩 24.01 單位。若其中一面因污染變成 0.60，剩餘為 0.70³×0.60=20.58，較原來降低 14.3%。本例鏡數與反射率不是任何 EUV 機台規格。","textEn":"In a hypothetical four-mirror path, each mirror has energy reflectivity 0.70 and other losses are ignored. Total transmission is 0.70⁴=0.2401, leaving 24.01 of 100 incident energy units. If one mirror falls to 0.60, the result is 0.70³×0.60=20.58, a 14.3% relative decrease. Mirror count and reflectivities are not specifications of any EUV scanner."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出光源至晶圓的反射路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch the reflective source-to-wafer path\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern."],"answer":0,"explanation":"EUV 光路各反射介面都影響能量。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"Each reflecting interface affects EUV throughput. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"在假設的四面反射鏡教學光路中，每面能量反射率皆為 0.70，且忽略其他損失。總傳輸比例為 0.70⁴=0.2401；100 單位入射能量只剩 24.01 單位。若其中一面因污染變成 0.60，剩餘為 0.70³×0.60=20.58，較原來降低 14.3%。本例鏡數與反射率不是任何 EUV 機台規格。","textEn":"In a hypothetical four-mirror path, each mirror has energy reflectivity 0.70 and other losses are ignored. Total transmission is 0.70⁴=0.2401, leaving 24.01 of 100 incident energy units. If one mirror falls to 0.60, the result is 0.70³×0.60=20.58, a 14.3% relative decrease. Mirror count and reflectivities are not specifications of any EUV scanner.","check":"用乘積得到 24.01 與 20.58，不可把反射率直接相加。","checkEn":"Use products to obtain 24.01 and 20.58; do not add reflectivities."}},{"id":"a041-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-01"],"title":"分配光源穩定度與晶圓劑量責任","titleEn":"Separate source stability from wafer-dose control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Source output is not absorbed wafer dose.","instruction":"分配光源穩定度與晶圓劑量責任。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate source stability from wafer-dose control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Source output is not absorbed wafer dose.","observation":"光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Source output is not absorbed wafer dose. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分配光源穩定度與晶圓劑量責任」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate source stability from wafer-dose control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Source output is not absorbed wafer dose.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。","textEn":"Source output is not absorbed wafer dose."},{"id":"a041-v8-02-k2","title":"系統與圖形的原理與限制","titleEn":"System and patterns: principle and limits","text":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","textEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分配光源穩定度與晶圓劑量責任」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate source stability from wafer-dose control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。"],"optionsEn":["EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","Source output is not absorbed wafer dose.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光源輸出不是晶圓上吸收劑量。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"Source output is not absorbed wafer dose. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}},{"id":"a041-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-02"],"title":"標出真空、污染與維護的介面","titleEn":"Mark vacuum, contamination and maintenance interfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability.","instruction":"標出真空、污染與維護的介面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark vacuum, contamination and maintenance interfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability.","observation":"污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標出真空、污染與維護的介面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark vacuum, contamination and maintenance interfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。","textEn":"Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability."},{"id":"a041-v8-03-k2","title":"系統與圖形的原理與限制","titleEn":"System and patterns: principle and limits","text":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","textEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標出真空、污染與維護的介面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark vacuum, contamination and maintenance interfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"污染會改變反射率及製程穩定性。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"Contamination can alter reflectivity and process stability. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}},{"id":"a041-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-03"],"title":"比較線空間與接觸孔的成像目標","titleEn":"Compare line-space and contact-hole targets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different patterns have different failure modes.","instruction":"比較線空間與接觸孔的成像目標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare line-space and contact-hole targets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different patterns have different failure modes.","observation":"不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different patterns have different failure modes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較線空間與接觸孔的成像目標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare line-space and contact-hole targets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different patterns have different failure modes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。","textEn":"Different patterns have different failure modes."},{"id":"a041-v8-04-k2","title":"系統與圖形的原理與限制","titleEn":"System and patterns: principle and limits","text":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","textEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較線空間與接觸孔的成像目標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare line-space and contact-hole targets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Different patterns have different failure modes.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同圖形有不同的失敗模式。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"Different patterns have different failure modes. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}},{"id":"a041-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-04"],"title":"建立目標邊緣位置誤差預算","titleEn":"Build a target edge-placement-error budget","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation.","instruction":"建立目標邊緣位置誤差預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a target edge-placement-error budget. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation.","observation":"尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立目標邊緣位置誤差預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a target edge-placement-error budget\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。","textEn":"Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation."},{"id":"a041-v8-05-k2","title":"系統與圖形的原理與限制","titleEn":"System and patterns: principle and limits","text":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","textEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立目標邊緣位置誤差預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a target edge-placement-error budget\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。"],"optionsEn":["EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尺寸、位置及轉移誤差需共同分配。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"Size, placement and transfer errors need joint allocation. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}},{"id":"a041-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-05"],"title":"選擇可比的 DUV 或 EUV 對照流程","titleEn":"Choose a comparable DUV or EUV reference flow","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：公平比較需一致設計目標。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A fair comparison needs matching design targets.","instruction":"選擇可比的 DUV 或 EUV 對照流程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「公平比較需一致設計目標。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose a comparable DUV or EUV reference flow. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: A fair comparison needs matching design targets.","observation":"公平比較需一致設計目標。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A fair comparison needs matching design targets. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選擇可比的 DUV 或 EUV 對照流程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「公平比較需一致設計目標。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose a comparable DUV or EUV reference flow\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A fair comparison needs matching design targets.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"公平比較需一致設計目標。","textEn":"A fair comparison needs matching design targets."},{"id":"a041-v8-06-k2","title":"系統與圖形的原理與限制","titleEn":"System and patterns: principle and limits","text":"EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","textEn":"EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選擇可比的 DUV 或 EUV 對照流程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose a comparable DUV or EUV reference flow\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","公平比較需一致設計目標。"],"optionsEn":["EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","A fair comparison needs matching design targets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公平比較需一致設計目標。 EUV 以反射式光學與真空路徑成像，材料與光罩都參與成像誤差。","explanationEn":"A fair comparison needs matching design targets. EUV uses reflective optics and vacuum paths; materials and masks both contribute imaging errors."}}]},{"id":"a041-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"材料與光罩","titleEn":"Materials and masks","description":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","descriptionEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection.","steps":[{"id":"a041-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-06"],"title":"檢查多層光罩與吸收層的功能","titleEn":"Distinguish multilayer and absorber functions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently.","instruction":"檢查多層光罩與吸收層的功能。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish multilayer and absorber functions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently.","observation":"反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查多層光罩與吸收層的功能」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish multilayer and absorber functions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。","textEn":"Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently."},{"id":"a041-v8-07-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查多層光罩與吸收層的功能」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish multilayer and absorber functions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。"],"optionsEn":["Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反射式光罩與透射式光罩機制不同。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Reflective and transmissive masks operate differently. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}},{"id":"a041-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-07"],"title":"比較光罩三維效應的方向性","titleEn":"Compare orientation dependence of mask 3D effects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：斜入射可造成方向相關成像。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging.","instruction":"比較光罩三維效應的方向性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「斜入射可造成方向相關成像。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare orientation dependence of mask 3D effects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging.","observation":"斜入射可造成方向相關成像。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光罩三維效應的方向性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「斜入射可造成方向相關成像。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare orientation dependence of mask 3D effects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"斜入射可造成方向相關成像。","textEn":"Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging."},{"id":"a041-v8-08-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光罩三維效應的方向性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare orientation dependence of mask 3D effects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","斜入射可造成方向相關成像。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斜入射可造成方向相關成像。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Oblique incidence can produce orientation-dependent imaging. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}},{"id":"a041-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-08"],"title":"評估光罩保護膜的光學代價","titleEn":"Assess optical costs of a pellicle","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Particle protection also affects energy and heat.","instruction":"評估光罩保護膜的光學代價。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess optical costs of a pellicle. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Particle protection also affects energy and heat.","observation":"防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Particle protection also affects energy and heat. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估光罩保護膜的光學代價」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess optical costs of a pellicle\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Particle protection also affects energy and heat.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。","textEn":"Particle protection also affects energy and heat."},{"id":"a041-v8-09-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估光罩保護膜的光學代價」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess optical costs of a pellicle\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Particle protection also affects energy and heat."],"answer":2,"explanation":"防顆粒保護也會影響能量與熱。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Particle protection also affects energy and heat. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}},{"id":"a041-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-09"],"title":"比較不同底層對光阻的影響","titleEn":"Compare underlayer effects on resist behavior","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer.","instruction":"比較不同底層對光阻的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare underlayer effects on resist behavior. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer.","observation":"底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同底層對光阻的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare underlayer effects on resist behavior\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。","textEn":"Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer."},{"id":"a041-v8-10-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同底層對光阻的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare underlayer effects on resist behavior\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。","最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。"],"optionsEn":["Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer.","The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底層可影響反應與圖案轉移。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Underlayers affect reactions and pattern transfer. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}},{"id":"a041-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-10"],"title":"建立薄光阻與硬罩的厚度分工","titleEn":"Allocate thickness between resist and hard mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer.","instruction":"建立薄光阻與硬罩的厚度分工。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Allocate thickness between resist and hard mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer.","observation":"薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立薄光阻與硬罩的厚度分工」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Allocate thickness between resist and hard mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。","textEn":"Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer."},{"id":"a041-v8-11-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立薄光阻與硬罩的厚度分工」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Allocate thickness between resist and hard mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄光阻需要可行的後續轉移。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Thin resist requires a viable downstream transfer. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}},{"id":"a041-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-11"],"title":"追蹤塗佈到曝光的等待歷程","titleEn":"Track delay history between coating and exposure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Time history can change material state.","instruction":"追蹤塗佈到曝光的等待歷程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track delay history between coating and exposure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Time history can change material state.","observation":"時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Time history can change material state. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤塗佈到曝光的等待歷程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track delay history between coating and exposure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Time history can change material state.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。","textEn":"Time history can change material state."},{"id":"a041-v8-12-k2","title":"材料與光罩的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and masks: principle and limits","text":"光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","textEn":"Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤塗佈到曝光的等待歷程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track delay history between coating and exposure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["最薄光阻一定最適合所有圖形。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest resist is best for every pattern.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Time history can change material state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間歷程可能改變材料狀態。 光阻厚度、吸收、粗糙度與轉移耐受性需共同選擇。","explanationEn":"Time history can change material state. Resist thickness, absorption, roughness and transfer resistance require joint selection."}}]},{"id":"a041-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"窗口與缺陷","titleEn":"Window and defects","description":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","descriptionEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions.","steps":[{"id":"a041-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-12"],"title":"建立焦距劑量矩陣的取樣順序","titleEn":"Design sampling order for a focus–dose matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Randomized order helps separate drift.","instruction":"建立焦距劑量矩陣的取樣順序。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Design sampling order for a focus–dose matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Randomized order helps separate drift.","observation":"隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Randomized order helps separate drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立焦距劑量矩陣的取樣順序」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Design sampling order for a focus–dose matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Randomized order helps separate drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。","textEn":"Randomized order helps separate drift."},{"id":"a041-v8-13-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立焦距劑量矩陣的取樣順序」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Design sampling order for a focus–dose matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。"],"optionsEn":["Randomized order helps separate drift.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隨機化順序有助於分離漂移。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"Randomized order helps separate drift. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}},{"id":"a041-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-13"],"title":"分開密集區與孤立區的尺寸偏差","titleEn":"Separate dense and isolated dimensional bias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns.","instruction":"分開密集區與孤立區的尺寸偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate dense and isolated dimensional bias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns.","observation":"同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開密集區與孤立區的尺寸偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate dense and isolated dimensional bias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。","textEn":"One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns."},{"id":"a041-v8-14-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開密集區與孤立區的尺寸偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate dense and isolated dimensional bias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。"],"optionsEn":["Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一劑量不保證所有圖形相同表現。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"One dose does not guarantee equal behavior for all patterns. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}},{"id":"a041-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-14"],"title":"計算缺失接觸孔的發生率","titleEn":"Calculate missing-contact incidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness.","instruction":"計算缺失接觸孔的發生率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Calculate missing-contact incidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness.","observation":"接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算缺失接觸孔的發生率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate missing-contact incidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。","textEn":"Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness."},{"id":"a041-v8-15-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算缺失接觸孔的發生率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate missing-contact incidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。"],"optionsEn":["Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸孔缺失與線條粗糙度不可互換。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"Missing contacts are not interchangeable with line roughness. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}},{"id":"a041-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-15"],"title":"比較斷線與橋接的劑量趨勢","titleEn":"Compare dose trends for breaks and bridges","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another.","instruction":"比較斷線與橋接的劑量趨勢。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dose trends for breaks and bridges. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another.","observation":"提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較斷線與橋接的劑量趨勢」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dose trends for breaks and bridges\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。","textEn":"Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another."},{"id":"a041-v8-16-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較斷線與橋接的劑量趨勢」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dose trends for breaks and bridges\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。","套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another.","Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高劑量可能改善一種缺陷卻惡化另一種。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"Increasing dose can improve one defect class while worsening another. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}},{"id":"a041-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-16"],"title":"將光罩重複缺陷與隨機缺陷分群","titleEn":"Separate repeating mask defects from stochastic defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：空間重複性可提示系統來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source.","instruction":"將光罩重複缺陷與隨機缺陷分群。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「空間重複性可提示系統來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate repeating mask defects from stochastic defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source.","observation":"空間重複性可提示系統來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將光罩重複缺陷與隨機缺陷分群」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「空間重複性可提示系統來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate repeating mask defects from stochastic defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"空間重複性可提示系統來源。","textEn":"Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source."},{"id":"a041-v8-17-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將光罩重複缺陷與隨機缺陷分群」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate repeating mask defects from stochastic defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","空間重複性可提示系統來源。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。"],"optionsEn":["Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"空間重複性可提示系統來源。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"Spatial repetition can indicate a systematic source. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}},{"id":"a041-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-17"],"title":"為檢查面積不足的零缺陷結果加註","titleEn":"Qualify zero-defect results with inadequate inspected area","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size.","instruction":"為檢查面積不足的零缺陷結果加註。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Qualify zero-defect results with inadequate inspected area. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size.","observation":"稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為檢查面積不足的零缺陷結果加註」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Qualify zero-defect results with inadequate inspected area\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。","textEn":"Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size."},{"id":"a041-v8-18-k2","title":"窗口與缺陷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window and defects: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","textEn":"Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為檢查面積不足的零缺陷結果加註」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Qualify zero-defect results with inadequate inspected area\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻合格就不會發生隨機斷線。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。"],"optionsEn":["Good overlay prevents stochastic breaks.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size."],"answer":2,"explanation":"稀有事件結論需要足夠樣本量。 隨機缺陷、尺寸與套刻是不同合格條件。","explanationEn":"Rare-event conclusions need sufficient sample size. Stochastic defects, dimensions and overlay are distinct acceptance conditions."}}]},{"id":"a041-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性與整合","titleEn":"Electrical integration","description":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","descriptionEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation.","steps":[{"id":"a041-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-18"],"title":"對照顯影後與蝕刻後圖形","titleEn":"Compare post-development and post-etch patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transfer can change defect visibility.","instruction":"對照顯影後與蝕刻後圖形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare post-development and post-etch patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transfer can change defect visibility.","observation":"圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transfer can change defect visibility. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對照顯影後與蝕刻後圖形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare post-development and post-etch patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transfer can change defect visibility.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。","textEn":"Transfer can change defect visibility."},{"id":"a041-v8-19-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對照顯影後與蝕刻後圖形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare post-development and post-etch patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。"],"optionsEn":["Transfer can change defect visibility.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"圖案轉移可能改變缺陷可見性。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Transfer can change defect visibility. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}},{"id":"a041-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-19"],"title":"以電阻鏈驗證通孔連接","titleEn":"Verify via connectivity using resistance chains","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance.","instruction":"以電阻鏈驗證通孔連接。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Verify via connectivity using resistance chains. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance.","observation":"形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以電阻鏈驗證通孔連接」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Verify via connectivity using resistance chains\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。","textEn":"Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance."},{"id":"a041-v8-20-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以電阻鏈驗證通孔連接」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Verify via connectivity using resistance chains\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。"],"optionsEn":["Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"形貌完整不代表接觸電阻合格。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Intact morphology does not prove acceptable contact resistance. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}},{"id":"a041-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-20"],"title":"以梳狀結構驗證線間隔離","titleEn":"Verify line isolation with comb structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging.","instruction":"以梳狀結構驗證線間隔離。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Verify line isolation with comb structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging.","observation":"漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以梳狀結構驗證線間隔離」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Verify line isolation with comb structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。","textEn":"Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging."},{"id":"a041-v8-21-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以梳狀結構驗證線間隔離」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Verify line isolation with comb structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。"],"optionsEn":["Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電能揭露影像未辨識的連接。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Leakage can reveal connections missed by imaging. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}},{"id":"a041-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-21"],"title":"比較單次與多次曝光的誤差累積","titleEn":"Compare error accumulation for single and multiple exposure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor.","instruction":"比較單次與多次曝光的誤差累積。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare error accumulation for single and multiple exposure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor.","observation":"工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單次與多次曝光的誤差累積」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare error accumulation for single and multiple exposure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。","textEn":"Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor."},{"id":"a041-v8-22-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單次與多次曝光的誤差累積」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare error accumulation for single and multiple exposure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。","減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。"],"optionsEn":["Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor.","Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"工序數與失敗機會相關但非唯一因素。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Step count affects failure opportunities but is not the only factor. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}},{"id":"a041-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-22"],"title":"記錄研究良率與產品良率的範圍","titleEn":"State the scope of research and product yield","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：測試載具結果不可無條件外推。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally.","instruction":"記錄研究良率與產品良率的範圍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「測試載具結果不可無條件外推。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"State the scope of research and product yield. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally.","observation":"測試載具結果不可無條件外推。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄研究良率與產品良率的範圍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「測試載具結果不可無條件外推。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"State the scope of research and product yield\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"測試載具結果不可無條件外推。","textEn":"Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally."},{"id":"a041-v8-23-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄研究良率與產品良率的範圍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"State the scope of research and product yield\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","測試載具結果不可無條件外推。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。"],"optionsEn":["Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"測試載具結果不可無條件外推。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Test-vehicle results cannot be extrapolated unconditionally. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}},{"id":"a041-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-euv","v8b-pattern","v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a041-v8-23"],"title":"提出具缺陷、尺寸與電性證據的整合評審","titleEn":"Review integration with defect, dimensional and electrical evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types.","instruction":"提出具缺陷、尺寸與電性證據的整合評審。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review integration with defect, dimensional and electrical evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types.","observation":"整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提出具缺陷、尺寸與電性證據的整合評審」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review integration with defect, dimensional and electrical evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a041-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。","textEn":"Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types."},{"id":"a041-v8-24-k2","title":"電性與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical integration: principle and limits","text":"單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","textEn":"Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提出具缺陷、尺寸與電性證據的整合評審」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review integration with defect, dimensional and electrical evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["減少曝光次數即可保證產品良率增加。","EUV 可直接套用透射玻璃鏡頭。","整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。"],"optionsEn":["Fewer exposures guarantee improved product yield.","EUV can directly use transmitting glass lenses.","Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types."],"answer":2,"explanation":"整合成熟度需要多種獨立證據。 單次曝光減少工序的效益仍需以整合良率驗證。","explanationEn":"Integration maturity requires several independent evidence types. Benefits from fewer exposures still require integrated-yield validation."}}]}]},{"id":"a043","title":"雙重圖案化製程","titleEn":"Double-patterning lithography","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究分解與配色、曝光與轉移、誤差分配、整合比較；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: decomposition and coloring, exposure and transfer, error allocation, integration comparison. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["分解與配色","曝光與轉移","誤差分配","整合比較"],"labelsEn":["Decomposition and coloring","Exposure and transfer","Error allocation","Integration comparison"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a043-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"分解與配色","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring","description":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","descriptionEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately.","steps":[{"id":"a043-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"將密集線分成兩種顏色","titleEn":"Split dense lines into two colors","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern.","instruction":"將密集線分成兩種顏色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Split dense lines into two colors. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern.","observation":"每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將密集線分成兩種顏色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Split dense lines into two colors\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。","textEn":"Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern."},{"id":"a043-v8-01-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將密集線分成兩種顏色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Split dense lines into two colors\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。","只需把曝光時間加倍。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。"],"optionsEn":["Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern.","Simply double the exposure time.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個子集合的間距可大於最終間距。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"Each subset can have larger pitch than the final pattern. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}},{"id":"a043-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-01"],"title":"在鄰接圖找出奇數迴圈","titleEn":"Find odd cycles in a conflict graph","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors.","instruction":"在鄰接圖找出奇數迴圈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Find odd cycles in a conflict graph. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors.","observation":"某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「在鄰接圖找出奇數迴圈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Find odd cycles in a conflict graph\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。","textEn":"Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors."},{"id":"a043-v8-02-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「在鄰接圖找出奇數迴圈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Find odd cycles in a conflict graph\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把曝光時間加倍。","某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。"],"optionsEn":["Simply double the exposure time.","Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某些圖形不能只用兩色無衝突分解。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"Some patterns cannot be conflict-free with two colors. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}},{"id":"a043-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-02"],"title":"標記必須切割的版圖區域","titleEn":"Mark layout regions requiring stitches","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stitch points can add local failure risk.","instruction":"標記必須切割的版圖區域。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark layout regions requiring stitches. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stitch points can add local failure risk.","observation":"切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stitch points can add local failure risk. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記必須切割的版圖區域」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark layout regions requiring stitches\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stitch points can add local failure risk.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。","textEn":"Stitch points can add local failure risk."},{"id":"a043-v8-03-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記必須切割的版圖區域」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark layout regions requiring stitches\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把曝光時間加倍。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。"],"optionsEn":["Simply double the exposure time.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Stitch points can add local failure risk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"切割點可能增加局部失敗風險。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"Stitch points can add local failure risk. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}},{"id":"a043-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-03"],"title":"比較 LELE 與側壁雙重圖案化","titleEn":"Compare LELE with spacer double patterning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者的線形成方式不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They form lines by different mechanisms.","instruction":"比較 LELE 與側壁雙重圖案化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩者的線形成方式不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare LELE with spacer double patterning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: They form lines by different mechanisms.","observation":"兩者的線形成方式不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They form lines by different mechanisms. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 LELE 與側壁雙重圖案化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者的線形成方式不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare LELE with spacer double patterning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They form lines by different mechanisms.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者的線形成方式不同。","textEn":"They form lines by different mechanisms."},{"id":"a043-v8-04-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 LELE 與側壁雙重圖案化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare LELE with spacer double patterning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩者的線形成方式不同。","只需把曝光時間加倍。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。"],"optionsEn":["They form lines by different mechanisms.","Simply double the exposure time.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩者的線形成方式不同。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"They form lines by different mechanisms. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}},{"id":"a043-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-04"],"title":"寫出最終線寬與間距目標","titleEn":"State final linewidth and spacing targets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：圖案密度不等於線寬。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pattern density is not linewidth.","instruction":"寫出最終線寬與間距目標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「圖案密度不等於線寬。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"State final linewidth and spacing targets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pattern density is not linewidth.","observation":"圖案密度不等於線寬。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pattern density is not linewidth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「寫出最終線寬與間距目標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「圖案密度不等於線寬。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"State final linewidth and spacing targets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pattern density is not linewidth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"圖案密度不等於線寬。","textEn":"Pattern density is not linewidth."},{"id":"a043-v8-05-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「寫出最終線寬與間距目標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"State final linewidth and spacing targets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把曝光時間加倍。","圖案密度不等於線寬。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。"],"optionsEn":["Simply double the exposure time.","Pattern density is not linewidth.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圖案密度不等於線寬。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"Pattern density is not linewidth. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}},{"id":"a043-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-05"],"title":"畫出兩組光罩與共同座標","titleEn":"Draw both masks in shared coordinates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：分解後仍須保留電路連通性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity.","instruction":"畫出兩組光罩與共同座標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「分解後仍須保留電路連通性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw both masks in shared coordinates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity.","observation":"分解後仍須保留電路連通性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只需把曝光時間加倍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Simply double the exposure time.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出兩組光罩與共同座標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「分解後仍須保留電路連通性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw both masks in shared coordinates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"分解後仍須保留電路連通性。","textEn":"Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity."},{"id":"a043-v8-06-k2","title":"分解與配色的原理與限制","titleEn":"Decomposition and coloring: principle and limits","text":"雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","textEn":"Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出兩組光罩與共同座標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw both masks in shared coordinates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只需把曝光時間加倍。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","分解後仍須保留電路連通性。"],"optionsEn":["Simply double the exposure time.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分解後仍須保留電路連通性。 雙重圖案化把難以單次解析的圖形拆成可處理的子集合。","explanationEn":"Decomposition must preserve circuit connectivity. Double patterning partitions patterns into subsets that can be processed separately."}}]},{"id":"a043-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"曝光與轉移","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer","description":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","descriptionEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models.","steps":[{"id":"a043-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-06"],"title":"追蹤第一組光阻到硬罩","titleEn":"Trace first-pattern resist into the hard mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The first pattern must survive the second process.","instruction":"追蹤第一組光阻到硬罩。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace first-pattern resist into the hard mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: The first pattern must survive the second process.","observation":"第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The first pattern must survive the second process. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤第一組光阻到硬罩」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace first-pattern resist into the hard mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The first pattern must survive the second process.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。","textEn":"The first pattern must survive the second process."},{"id":"a043-v8-07-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤第一組光阻到硬罩」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace first-pattern resist into the hard mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["The first pattern must survive the second process.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一組圖形必須能承受第二組製程。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"The first pattern must survive the second process. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}},{"id":"a043-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-07"],"title":"標出第一組保護與平坦化需求","titleEn":"Mark first-pattern protection and planarization needs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：既有地形會影響第二次微影。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Existing topography affects the second lithography.","instruction":"標出第一組保護與平坦化需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「既有地形會影響第二次微影。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark first-pattern protection and planarization needs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Existing topography affects the second lithography.","observation":"既有地形會影響第二次微影。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Existing topography affects the second lithography. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標出第一組保護與平坦化需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「既有地形會影響第二次微影。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark first-pattern protection and planarization needs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Existing topography affects the second lithography.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"既有地形會影響第二次微影。","textEn":"Existing topography affects the second lithography."},{"id":"a043-v8-08-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標出第一組保護與平坦化需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark first-pattern protection and planarization needs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","既有地形會影響第二次微影。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Existing topography affects the second lithography.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"既有地形會影響第二次微影。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"Existing topography affects the second lithography. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}},{"id":"a043-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-08"],"title":"安排第二組對位標記位置","titleEn":"Plan second-pattern alignment marks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Marks must remain detectable after later films.","instruction":"安排第二組對位標記位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan second-pattern alignment marks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Marks must remain detectable after later films.","observation":"標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Marks must remain detectable after later films. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「安排第二組對位標記位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan second-pattern alignment marks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Marks must remain detectable after later films.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。","textEn":"Marks must remain detectable after later films."},{"id":"a043-v8-09-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「安排第二組對位標記位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan second-pattern alignment marks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。"],"optionsEn":["All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","Marks must remain detectable after later films."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標記須在後續薄膜後仍可辨識。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"Marks must remain detectable after later films. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}},{"id":"a043-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-09"],"title":"比較先蝕刻與凍結光阻策略","titleEn":"Compare intermediate etch with resist-freeze strategies","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料相容性會限制流程選擇。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material compatibility constrains flow selection.","instruction":"比較先蝕刻與凍結光阻策略。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「材料相容性會限制流程選擇。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare intermediate etch with resist-freeze strategies. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material compatibility constrains flow selection.","observation":"材料相容性會限制流程選擇。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material compatibility constrains flow selection. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較先蝕刻與凍結光阻策略」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料相容性會限制流程選擇。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare intermediate etch with resist-freeze strategies\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material compatibility constrains flow selection.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料相容性會限制流程選擇。","textEn":"Material compatibility constrains flow selection."},{"id":"a043-v8-10-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較先蝕刻與凍結光阻策略」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare intermediate etch with resist-freeze strategies\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料相容性會限制流程選擇。","所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["Material compatibility constrains flow selection.","All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料相容性會限制流程選擇。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"Material compatibility constrains flow selection. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}},{"id":"a043-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-10"],"title":"檢查兩組圖形合併後的缺口","titleEn":"Inspect gaps after merging both patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：各組合格不保證合併後連通。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity.","instruction":"檢查兩組圖形合併後的缺口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「各組合格不保證合併後連通。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect gaps after merging both patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity.","observation":"各組合格不保證合併後連通。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查兩組圖形合併後的缺口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「各組合格不保證合併後連通。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect gaps after merging both patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"各組合格不保證合併後連通。","textEn":"Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity."},{"id":"a043-v8-11-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查兩組圖形合併後的缺口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect gaps after merging both patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","各組合格不保證合併後連通。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各組合格不保證合併後連通。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"Each subset passing does not guarantee merged connectivity. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}},{"id":"a043-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-11"],"title":"追蹤清潔對第一組線條的侵蝕","titleEn":"Track cleaning damage to first-pattern lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss.","instruction":"追蹤清潔對第一組線條的侵蝕。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track cleaning damage to first-pattern lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss.","observation":"重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤清潔對第一組線條的侵蝕」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track cleaning damage to first-pattern lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。","textEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss."},{"id":"a043-v8-12-k2","title":"曝光與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and transfer: principle and limits","text":"兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","textEn":"Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤清潔對第一組線條的侵蝕」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track cleaning damage to first-pattern lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有雙重圖案化都沒有套刻需求。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。"],"optionsEn":["All double patterning eliminates overlay requirements.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複清潔可能累積尺寸損失。 兩次微影與側壁自對準是不同流程，不能混用誤差模型。","explanationEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate dimensional loss. Two-exposure lithography and spacer self-alignment are different flows with different error models."}}]},{"id":"a043-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"誤差分配","titleEn":"Error allocation","description":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","descriptionEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently.","steps":[{"id":"a043-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-12"],"title":"畫出套刻偏移造成的交替間距","titleEn":"Sketch alternating spaces caused by overlay shift","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相對位移會產生間距交替。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Relative displacement produces alternating spacing.","instruction":"畫出套刻偏移造成的交替間距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「相對位移會產生間距交替。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：設兩組交錯線條在完美對位時的左右間隙皆為 40 nm。第二組向右偏移 5 nm，而線寬不變，則左右間隙變成 45 nm 與 35 nm，平均仍為 40 nm。若最小間隙要求為 36 nm，這組圖形不合格，即使平均間隙完全正確。畫出帶方向的套刻向量與兩個間隙。","instructionEn":"Sketch alternating spaces caused by overlay shift. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Relative displacement produces alternating spacing.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Two interleaved line sets have 40 nm gaps on both sides at ideal alignment. Shift the second set 5 nm right without changing widths: gaps become 45 and 35 nm while their mean remains 40 nm. A 36 nm minimum-gap requirement is violated despite the correct mean. Draw the signed overlay vector and both gaps.","observation":"相對位移會產生間距交替。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 45/35 nm 與不合格理由，明確指出平均值盲點。","observationEn":"Relative displacement produces alternating spacing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 45/35 nm and the failure reason, identifying the mean-value blind spot.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出套刻偏移造成的交替間距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相對位移會產生間距交替。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 45/35 nm 與不合格理由，明確指出平均值盲點。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch alternating spaces caused by overlay shift\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Relative displacement produces alternating spacing.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 45/35 nm and the failure reason, identifying the mean-value blind spot.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相對位移會產生間距交替。","textEn":"Relative displacement produces alternating spacing."},{"id":"a043-v8-13-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"設兩組交錯線條在完美對位時的左右間隙皆為 40 nm。第二組向右偏移 5 nm，而線寬不變，則左右間隙變成 45 nm 與 35 nm，平均仍為 40 nm。若最小間隙要求為 36 nm，這組圖形不合格，即使平均間隙完全正確。畫出帶方向的套刻向量與兩個間隙。","textEn":"Two interleaved line sets have 40 nm gaps on both sides at ideal alignment. Shift the second set 5 nm right without changing widths: gaps become 45 and 35 nm while their mean remains 40 nm. A 36 nm minimum-gap requirement is violated despite the correct mean. Draw the signed overlay vector and both gaps."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出套刻偏移造成的交替間距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch alternating spaces caused by overlay shift\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相對位移會產生間距交替。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Relative displacement produces alternating spacing.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","The fewest-step scheme is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相對位移會產生間距交替。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"Relative displacement produces alternating spacing. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"設兩組交錯線條在完美對位時的左右間隙皆為 40 nm。第二組向右偏移 5 nm，而線寬不變，則左右間隙變成 45 nm 與 35 nm，平均仍為 40 nm。若最小間隙要求為 36 nm，這組圖形不合格，即使平均間隙完全正確。畫出帶方向的套刻向量與兩個間隙。","textEn":"Two interleaved line sets have 40 nm gaps on both sides at ideal alignment. Shift the second set 5 nm right without changing widths: gaps become 45 and 35 nm while their mean remains 40 nm. A 36 nm minimum-gap requirement is violated despite the correct mean. Draw the signed overlay vector and both gaps.","check":"交付 45/35 nm 與不合格理由，明確指出平均值盲點。","checkEn":"Report 45/35 nm and the failure reason, identifying the mean-value blind spot."}},{"id":"a043-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-13"],"title":"把兩組線寬偏差分別加入模型","titleEn":"Add linewidth bias for each subset separately","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Common and differential biases have different consequences.","instruction":"把兩組線寬偏差分別加入模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Add linewidth bias for each subset separately. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Common and differential biases have different consequences.","observation":"共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Common and differential biases have different consequences. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把兩組線寬偏差分別加入模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Add linewidth bias for each subset separately\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Common and differential biases have different consequences.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。","textEn":"Common and differential biases have different consequences."},{"id":"a043-v8-14-k2","title":"誤差分配的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error allocation: principle and limits","text":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","textEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把兩組線寬偏差分別加入模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Add linewidth bias for each subset separately\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","Common and differential biases have different consequences.","The fewest-step scheme is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共同偏差與差分偏差後果不同。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"Common and differential biases have different consequences. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}},{"id":"a043-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-14"],"title":"比較系統偏移與隨機偏移","titleEn":"Compare systematic and random displacement","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets.","instruction":"比較系統偏移與隨機偏移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare systematic and random displacement. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets.","observation":"可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較系統偏移與隨機偏移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare systematic and random displacement\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。","textEn":"Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets."},{"id":"a043-v8-15-k2","title":"誤差分配的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error allocation: principle and limits","text":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","textEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較系統偏移與隨機偏移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare systematic and random displacement\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。"],"optionsEn":["Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可補償誤差與不可預測誤差需分帳。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"Correctable and unpredictable errors need separate budgets. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}},{"id":"a043-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-15"],"title":"計算最小間距的最壞條件","titleEn":"Calculate worst-case minimum spacing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing.","instruction":"計算最小間距的最壞條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Calculate worst-case minimum spacing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing.","observation":"平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算最小間距的最壞條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate worst-case minimum spacing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。","textEn":"Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing."},{"id":"a043-v8-16-k2","title":"誤差分配的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error allocation: principle and limits","text":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","textEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算最小間距的最壞條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate worst-case minimum spacing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。","兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing.","Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","The fewest-step scheme is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均間距可能掩蓋最小間距不足。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"Mean spacing can hide insufficient minimum spacing. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}},{"id":"a043-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-16"],"title":"評估切割點的重疊容忍度","titleEn":"Assess overlap tolerance at a stitch","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin.","instruction":"評估切割點的重疊容忍度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess overlap tolerance at a stitch. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin.","observation":"切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估切割點的重疊容忍度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess overlap tolerance at a stitch\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。","textEn":"A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin."},{"id":"a043-v8-17-k2","title":"誤差分配的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error allocation: principle and limits","text":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","textEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估切割點的重疊容忍度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess overlap tolerance at a stitch\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin.","The fewest-step scheme is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"切割接縫需要額外連通裕量。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"A stitched seam needs extra connectivity margin. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}},{"id":"a043-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-17"],"title":"為兩組曝光建立分群統計","titleEn":"Build separate statistics for both exposures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：分群可揭露工具或製程差異。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Grouping can reveal tool or process differences.","instruction":"為兩組曝光建立分群統計。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「分群可揭露工具或製程差異。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build separate statistics for both exposures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Grouping can reveal tool or process differences.","observation":"分群可揭露工具或製程差異。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Grouping can reveal tool or process differences. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Correct mean placement prevents local errors.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為兩組曝光建立分群統計」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「分群可揭露工具或製程差異。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build separate statistics for both exposures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Grouping can reveal tool or process differences.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"分群可揭露工具或製程差異。","textEn":"Grouping can reveal tool or process differences."},{"id":"a043-v8-18-k2","title":"誤差分配的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error allocation: principle and limits","text":"相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","textEn":"Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為兩組曝光建立分群統計」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build separate statistics for both exposures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩次曝光平均位置正確就不會有局部錯誤。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","分群可揭露工具或製程差異。"],"optionsEn":["Correct mean placement prevents local errors.","The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Grouping can reveal tool or process differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分群可揭露工具或製程差異。 相對位置、線寬與側壁厚度具有不同的誤差傳遞方式。","explanationEn":"Grouping can reveal tool or process differences. Relative placement, linewidth and spacer thickness propagate errors differently."}}]},{"id":"a043-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合比較","titleEn":"Integration comparison","description":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","descriptionEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results.","steps":[{"id":"a043-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-18"],"title":"以蛇形線檢查接縫斷線","titleEn":"Check stitched breaks using serpentine lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups.","instruction":"以蛇形線檢查接縫斷線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check stitched breaks using serpentine lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups.","observation":"電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以蛇形線檢查接縫斷線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check stitched breaks using serpentine lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。","textEn":"Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups."},{"id":"a043-v8-19-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以蛇形線檢查接縫斷線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check stitched breaks using serpentine lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","只需把曝光時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups.","The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Simply double the exposure time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻異常需回溯到圖案群組。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Resistance anomalies need tracing to pattern groups. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}},{"id":"a043-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-19"],"title":"以梳狀結構檢查間距短路","titleEn":"Check spacing shorts using comb structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：橋接風險集中於最小間距。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing.","instruction":"以梳狀結構檢查間距短路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「橋接風險集中於最小間距。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check spacing shorts using comb structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing.","observation":"橋接風險集中於最小間距。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以梳狀結構檢查間距短路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「橋接風險集中於最小間距。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check spacing shorts using comb structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"橋接風險集中於最小間距。","textEn":"Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing."},{"id":"a043-v8-20-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以梳狀結構檢查間距短路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check spacing shorts using comb structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","橋接風險集中於最小間距。","只需把曝光時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing.","Simply double the exposure time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"橋接風險集中於最小間距。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Bridge risk concentrates at minimum spacing. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}},{"id":"a043-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-20"],"title":"比較雙重與單次 EUV 的介面數","titleEn":"Compare interfaces in double patterning and single EUV","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks.","instruction":"比較雙重與單次 EUV 的介面數。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare interfaces in double patterning and single EUV. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks.","observation":"減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較雙重與單次 EUV 的介面數」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare interfaces in double patterning and single EUV\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。","textEn":"Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks."},{"id":"a043-v8-21-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較雙重與單次 EUV 的介面數」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare interfaces in double patterning and single EUV\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","只需把曝光時間加倍。","減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。"],"optionsEn":["The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Simply double the exposure time.","Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"減少介面可能減少誤差來源但引入不同材料風險。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Fewer interfaces can reduce error sources while introducing different material risks. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}},{"id":"a043-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-21"],"title":"建立工序、檢查與返工成本表","titleEn":"Tabulate process, inspection and rework costs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Exposure count is not the only cost driver.","instruction":"建立工序、檢查與返工成本表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Tabulate process, inspection and rework costs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Exposure count is not the only cost driver.","observation":"曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Exposure count is not the only cost driver. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立工序、檢查與返工成本表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Tabulate process, inspection and rework costs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Exposure count is not the only cost driver.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。","textEn":"Exposure count is not the only cost driver."},{"id":"a043-v8-22-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立工序、檢查與返工成本表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Tabulate process, inspection and rework costs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。","步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","只需把曝光時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Exposure count is not the only cost driver.","The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Simply double the exposure time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝光次數不是成本的唯一來源。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Exposure count is not the only cost driver. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}},{"id":"a043-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-22"],"title":"標記不可沿用到任意版圖的規則","titleEn":"Mark rules that do not transfer to arbitrary layouts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rule validity depends on layout and flow.","instruction":"標記不可沿用到任意版圖的規則。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark rules that do not transfer to arbitrary layouts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rule validity depends on layout and flow.","observation":"規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rule validity depends on layout and flow. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記不可沿用到任意版圖的規則」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark rules that do not transfer to arbitrary layouts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rule validity depends on layout and flow.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。","textEn":"Rule validity depends on layout and flow."},{"id":"a043-v8-23-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記不可沿用到任意版圖的規則」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark rules that do not transfer to arbitrary layouts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。","只需把曝光時間加倍。"],"optionsEn":["The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Rule validity depends on layout and flow.","Simply double the exposure time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"規則有效範圍取決於圖形與流程。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Rule validity depends on layout and flow. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}},{"id":"a043-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-multipattern","v8b-saqp","v8b-comp","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a043-v8-23"],"title":"交付兩組圖案的整合驗收","titleEn":"Deliver integrated acceptance for both pattern subsets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior.","instruction":"交付兩組圖案的整合驗收。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver integrated acceptance for both pattern subsets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior.","observation":"驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fewest-step scheme is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付兩組圖案的整合驗收」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver integrated acceptance for both pattern subsets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a043-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。","textEn":"Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior."},{"id":"a043-v8-24-k2","title":"整合比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration comparison: principle and limits","text":"圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","textEn":"Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付兩組圖案的整合驗收」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver integrated acceptance for both pattern subsets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["步驟最少的方案永遠最佳。","只需把曝光時間加倍。","驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。"],"optionsEn":["The fewest-step scheme is always best.","Simply double the exposure time.","Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗收需涵蓋單組與合併後性能。 圖案化方案應同時比較版圖限制、步數與電性結果。","explanationEn":"Acceptance must cover subsets and their combined behavior. Patterning schemes need comparison of layout constraints, step count and electrical results."}}]}]},{"id":"a044","title":"自我對準四重圖案化","titleEn":"Self-aligned quadruple patterning","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究骨架與倍增、第一輪側壁、第二輪與切割、誤差與電性；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: mandrels and multiplication, first spacer cycle, second cycle and cuts, errors and electrical tests. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["骨架與倍增","第一輪側壁","第二輪與切割","誤差與電性"],"labelsEn":["Mandrels and multiplication","First spacer cycle","Second cycle and cuts","Errors and electrical tests"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a044-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"骨架與倍增","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication","description":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","descriptionEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement.","steps":[{"id":"a044-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出最初骨架與最終四倍線群","titleEn":"Draw initial mandrels and final fourfold line sets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：骨架週期與最終節距不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mandrel period differs from final pitch.","instruction":"畫出最初骨架與最終四倍線群。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「骨架週期與最終節距不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：設理想骨架節距為 160 nm；每輪側壁倍增恰好使規則線群節距減半。第一輪為 80 nm，第二輪為 40 nm。這並不表示最終線寬是 40 nm：若目標線寬為 15 nm，名目間隙應為 25 nm。另標記切割光罩的位置需求，避免把四倍線密度誤解為完整電路已完成。","instructionEn":"Draw initial mandrels and final fourfold line sets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mandrel period differs from final pitch.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume an ideal 160 nm mandrel pitch and each spacer multiplication exactly halves regular-line pitch. The first cycle gives 80 nm and the second 40 nm. Final linewidth is not therefore 40 nm: a 15 nm line leaves a nominal 25 nm gap. Also mark cut-mask placement requirements so fourfold line density is not mistaken for a completed circuit.","observation":"骨架週期與最終節距不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n須區分 160→80→40 nm 節距、15 nm 線寬及 25 nm 間隙。","observationEn":"Mandrel period differs from final pitch. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nDistinguish 160→80→40 nm pitch, 15 nm width and 25 nm gap.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出最初骨架與最終四倍線群」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「骨架週期與最終節距不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：須區分 160→80→40 nm 節距、15 nm 線寬及 25 nm 間隙。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw initial mandrels and final fourfold line sets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mandrel period differs from final pitch.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Distinguish 160→80→40 nm pitch, 15 nm width and 25 nm gap.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"骨架週期與最終節距不同。","textEn":"Mandrel period differs from final pitch."},{"id":"a044-v8-01-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"設理想骨架節距為 160 nm；每輪側壁倍增恰好使規則線群節距減半。第一輪為 80 nm，第二輪為 40 nm。這並不表示最終線寬是 40 nm：若目標線寬為 15 nm，名目間隙應為 25 nm。另標記切割光罩的位置需求，避免把四倍線密度誤解為完整電路已完成。","textEn":"Assume an ideal 160 nm mandrel pitch and each spacer multiplication exactly halves regular-line pitch. The first cycle gives 80 nm and the second 40 nm. Final linewidth is not therefore 40 nm: a 15 nm line leaves a nominal 25 nm gap. Also mark cut-mask placement requirements so fourfold line density is not mistaken for a completed circuit."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出最初骨架與最終四倍線群」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw initial mandrels and final fourfold line sets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["骨架週期與最終節距不同。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。"],"optionsEn":["Mandrel period differs from final pitch.","SAQP means exposing four times.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines."],"answer":0,"explanation":"骨架週期與最終節距不同。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Mandrel period differs from final pitch. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"設理想骨架節距為 160 nm；每輪側壁倍增恰好使規則線群節距減半。第一輪為 80 nm，第二輪為 40 nm。這並不表示最終線寬是 40 nm：若目標線寬為 15 nm，名目間隙應為 25 nm。另標記切割光罩的位置需求，避免把四倍線密度誤解為完整電路已完成。","textEn":"Assume an ideal 160 nm mandrel pitch and each spacer multiplication exactly halves regular-line pitch. The first cycle gives 80 nm and the second 40 nm. Final linewidth is not therefore 40 nm: a 15 nm line leaves a nominal 25 nm gap. Also mark cut-mask placement requirements so fourfold line density is not mistaken for a completed circuit.","check":"須區分 160→80→40 nm 節距、15 nm 線寬及 25 nm 間隙。","checkEn":"Distinguish 160→80→40 nm pitch, 15 nm width and 25 nm gap."}},{"id":"a044-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-01"],"title":"用不同顏色追蹤各代材料","titleEn":"Color-code each material generation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material identity determines selective-removal order.","instruction":"用不同顏色追蹤各代材料。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Color-code each material generation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material identity determines selective-removal order.","observation":"材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material identity determines selective-removal order. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用不同顏色追蹤各代材料」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Color-code each material generation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material identity determines selective-removal order.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。","textEn":"Material identity determines selective-removal order."},{"id":"a044-v8-02-k2","title":"骨架與倍增的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication: principle and limits","text":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","textEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用不同顏色追蹤各代材料」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Color-code each material generation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。"],"optionsEn":["SAQP means exposing four times.","Material identity determines selective-removal order.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料身分決定選擇性移除次序。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Material identity determines selective-removal order. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}},{"id":"a044-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-02"],"title":"比較 SADP 與 SAQP 的輪數","titleEn":"Compare cycle counts in SADP and SAQP","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources.","instruction":"比較 SADP 與 SAQP 的輪數。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare cycle counts in SADP and SAQP. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources.","observation":"增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 SADP 與 SAQP 的輪數」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare cycle counts in SADP and SAQP\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。","textEn":"Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources."},{"id":"a044-v8-03-k2","title":"骨架與倍增的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication: principle and limits","text":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","textEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 SADP 與 SAQP 的輪數」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare cycle counts in SADP and SAQP\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。"],"optionsEn":["SAQP means exposing four times.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"增加一輪也增加介面與誤差來源。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Another cycle adds interfaces and error sources. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}},{"id":"a044-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-03"],"title":"列出骨架線寬與側壁厚度的幾何關係","titleEn":"Relate mandrel width to spacer thickness geometrically","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions.","instruction":"列出骨架線寬與側壁厚度的幾何關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate mandrel width to spacer thickness geometrically. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions.","observation":"節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出骨架線寬與側壁厚度的幾何關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate mandrel width to spacer thickness geometrically\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。","textEn":"Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions."},{"id":"a044-v8-04-k2","title":"骨架與倍增的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication: principle and limits","text":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","textEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出骨架線寬與側壁厚度的幾何關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate mandrel width to spacer thickness geometrically\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。"],"optionsEn":["Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions.","SAQP means exposing four times.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines."],"answer":0,"explanation":"節距倍增不是任意厚度都能達成。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Pitch multiplication requires compatible dimensions. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}},{"id":"a044-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-04"],"title":"標記需要保留及刪除的最終線","titleEn":"Mark retained and deleted final lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Regular line arrays still need circuit topology.","instruction":"標記需要保留及刪除的最終線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark retained and deleted final lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Regular line arrays still need circuit topology.","observation":"規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Regular line arrays still need circuit topology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記需要保留及刪除的最終線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark retained and deleted final lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Regular line arrays still need circuit topology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。","textEn":"Regular line arrays still need circuit topology."},{"id":"a044-v8-05-k2","title":"骨架與倍增的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication: principle and limits","text":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","textEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記需要保留及刪除的最終線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark retained and deleted final lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。"],"optionsEn":["SAQP means exposing four times.","Regular line arrays still need circuit topology.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"規則線群仍需轉成電路拓樸。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Regular line arrays still need circuit topology. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}},{"id":"a044-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-05"],"title":"建立每層選擇性蝕刻矩陣","titleEn":"Build a layer-selectivity matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material discrimination enables repeated transfer.","instruction":"建立每層選擇性蝕刻矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a layer-selectivity matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material discrimination enables repeated transfer.","observation":"可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material discrimination enables repeated transfer. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"SAQP means exposing four times.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立每層選擇性蝕刻矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a layer-selectivity matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material discrimination enables repeated transfer.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。","textEn":"Material discrimination enables repeated transfer."},{"id":"a044-v8-06-k2","title":"骨架與倍增的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mandrels and multiplication: principle and limits","text":"SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","textEn":"SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立每層選擇性蝕刻矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a layer-selectivity matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。"],"optionsEn":["SAQP means exposing four times.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Material discrimination enables repeated transfer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可分辨材料是多輪轉移的基礎。 SAQP 利用兩輪側壁圖形倍增，線位置由多道沉積與蝕刻共同決定。","explanationEn":"Material discrimination enables repeated transfer. SAQP uses two spacer multiplication cycles; deposition and etch jointly determine line placement."}}]},{"id":"a044-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"第一輪側壁","titleEn":"First spacer cycle","description":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","descriptionEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours.","steps":[{"id":"a044-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-06"],"title":"檢查第一輪沉積的側壁覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect first-cycle sidewall coverage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness.","instruction":"檢查第一輪沉積的側壁覆蓋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect first-cycle sidewall coverage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness.","observation":"頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查第一輪沉積的側壁覆蓋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect first-cycle sidewall coverage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。","textEn":"Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness."},{"id":"a044-v8-07-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查第一輪沉積的側壁覆蓋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect first-cycle sidewall coverage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。"],"optionsEn":["Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂部膜厚不能代表側壁膜厚。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Top thickness does not establish sidewall thickness. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}},{"id":"a044-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-07"],"title":"畫出方向性回蝕後的側壁","titleEn":"Draw spacers after directional etchback","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity.","instruction":"畫出方向性回蝕後的側壁。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw spacers after directional etchback. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity.","observation":"底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出方向性回蝕後的側壁」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw spacers after directional etchback\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。","textEn":"Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity."},{"id":"a044-v8-08-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出方向性回蝕後的側壁」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw spacers after directional etchback\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"底部殘留會改變相鄰線連通性。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Bottom residue can alter neighboring-line connectivity. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}},{"id":"a044-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-08"],"title":"比較骨架移除前後的支撐","titleEn":"Compare support before and after mandrel removal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable.","instruction":"比較骨架移除前後的支撐。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare support before and after mandrel removal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable.","observation":"細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較骨架移除前後的支撐」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare support before and after mandrel removal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。","textEn":"Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable."},{"id":"a044-v8-09-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較骨架移除前後的支撐」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare support before and after mandrel removal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細長側壁可能因機械作用失穩。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Slender spacers can become mechanically unstable. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}},{"id":"a044-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-09"],"title":"量測第一輪的交替間距","titleEn":"Measure alternating spacing after the first cycle","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking.","instruction":"量測第一輪的交替間距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure alternating spacing after the first cycle. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking.","observation":"骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測第一輪的交替間距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure alternating spacing after the first cycle\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。","textEn":"Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking."},{"id":"a044-v8-10-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測第一輪的交替間距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure alternating spacing after the first cycle\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。","沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。"],"optionsEn":["Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking.","Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"骨架寬度誤差可形成節距游移。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Mandrel-width error can produce pitch walking. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}},{"id":"a044-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-10"],"title":"追蹤側壁圓角向硬罩轉移","titleEn":"Trace spacer corner shape into the hard mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contour shape affects subsequent line placement.","instruction":"追蹤側壁圓角向硬罩轉移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace spacer corner shape into the hard mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contour shape affects subsequent line placement.","observation":"輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contour shape affects subsequent line placement. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤側壁圓角向硬罩轉移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace spacer corner shape into the hard mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contour shape affects subsequent line placement.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。","textEn":"Contour shape affects subsequent line placement."},{"id":"a044-v8-11-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤側壁圓角向硬罩轉移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace spacer corner shape into the hard mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Contour shape affects subsequent line placement.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輪廓形狀會影響後續線位置。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Contour shape affects subsequent line placement. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}},{"id":"a044-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-11"],"title":"記錄第一輪中心與邊緣均勻性","titleEn":"Record center-to-edge uniformity in the first cycle","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle.","instruction":"記錄第一輪中心與邊緣均勻性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Record center-to-edge uniformity in the first cycle. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle.","observation":"晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄第一輪中心與邊緣均勻性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Record center-to-edge uniformity in the first cycle\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。","textEn":"Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle."},{"id":"a044-v8-12-k2","title":"第一輪側壁的原理與限制","titleEn":"First spacer cycle: principle and limits","text":"側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","textEn":"Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄第一輪中心與邊緣均勻性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Record center-to-edge uniformity in the first cycle\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["沉積越厚就一定得到越細的線。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker deposition necessarily produces finer lines.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶圓內不均勻會傳入下一輪。 側壁厚度控制與方向性蝕刻共同決定保留輪廓。","explanationEn":"Within-wafer nonuniformity propagates to the next cycle. Spacer thickness and directional etch jointly determine retained contours."}}]},{"id":"a044-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"第二輪與切割","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts","description":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","descriptionEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits.","steps":[{"id":"a044-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-12"],"title":"把第一輪圖形改作第二輪骨架","titleEn":"Use first-cycle patterns as second-cycle mandrels","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input.","instruction":"把第一輪圖形改作第二輪骨架。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use first-cycle patterns as second-cycle mandrels. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input.","observation":"上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把第一輪圖形改作第二輪骨架」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use first-cycle patterns as second-cycle mandrels\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。","textEn":"One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input."},{"id":"a044-v8-13-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把第一輪圖形改作第二輪骨架」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use first-cycle patterns as second-cycle mandrels\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Every line necessarily has the same error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上一輪輸出即下一輪輸入。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"One cycle's output becomes the next cycle's input. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}},{"id":"a044-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-13"],"title":"檢查第二輪厚度對最終線寬的影響","titleEn":"Assess second-cycle thickness effects on final width","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Later thickness control can directly set linewidth.","instruction":"檢查第二輪厚度對最終線寬的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess second-cycle thickness effects on final width. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Later thickness control can directly set linewidth.","observation":"後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Later thickness control can directly set linewidth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查第二輪厚度對最終線寬的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess second-cycle thickness effects on final width\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Later thickness control can directly set linewidth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。","textEn":"Later thickness control can directly set linewidth."},{"id":"a044-v8-14-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查第二輪厚度對最終線寬的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess second-cycle thickness effects on final width\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Later thickness control can directly set linewidth.","Every line necessarily has the same error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"後段厚度控制可能直接決定線寬。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"Later thickness control can directly set linewidth. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}},{"id":"a044-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-14"],"title":"疊合兩輪造成的節距游移","titleEn":"Superpose pitch walking from both cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：誤差可依線群具有週期結構。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups.","instruction":"疊合兩輪造成的節距游移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「誤差可依線群具有週期結構。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Superpose pitch walking from both cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups.","observation":"誤差可依線群具有週期結構。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「疊合兩輪造成的節距游移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「誤差可依線群具有週期結構。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Superpose pitch walking from both cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"誤差可依線群具有週期結構。","textEn":"Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups."},{"id":"a044-v8-15-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「疊合兩輪造成的節距游移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Superpose pitch walking from both cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","誤差可依線群具有週期結構。"],"optionsEn":["Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Every line necessarily has the same error.","Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups."],"answer":2,"explanation":"誤差可依線群具有週期結構。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"Errors can form periodic patterns across line groups. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}},{"id":"a044-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-15"],"title":"規畫切割光罩的容許窗口","titleEn":"Plan the cut-mask acceptance window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections.","instruction":"規畫切割光罩的容許窗口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan the cut-mask acceptance window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections.","observation":"切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫切割光罩的容許窗口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan the cut-mask acceptance window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。","textEn":"Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections."},{"id":"a044-v8-16-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫切割光罩的容許窗口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan the cut-mask acceptance window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。","自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections.","Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Every line necessarily has the same error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"切割套刻會影響線端及殘留連接。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"Cut overlay affects line ends and residual connections. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}},{"id":"a044-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-16"],"title":"比較 EUV 切割與多次 DUV 切割","titleEn":"Compare EUV cuts with multiple DUV cuts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements.","instruction":"比較 EUV 切割與多次 DUV 切割。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare EUV cuts with multiple DUV cuts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements.","observation":"切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 EUV 切割與多次 DUV 切割」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare EUV cuts with multiple DUV cuts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。","textEn":"Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements."},{"id":"a044-v8-17-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 EUV 切割與多次 DUV 切割」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare EUV cuts with multiple DUV cuts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements.","Every line necessarily has the same error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"切割方案改變步數與套刻要求。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"Cut strategies change step count and overlay requirements. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}},{"id":"a044-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-17"],"title":"檢查切割後是否留下短支線","titleEn":"Inspect short stubs after cutting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk.","instruction":"檢查切割後是否留下短支線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect short stubs after cutting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk.","observation":"殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查切割後是否留下短支線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect short stubs after cutting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。","textEn":"Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk."},{"id":"a044-v8-18-k2","title":"第二輪與切割的原理與限制","titleEn":"Second cycle and cuts: principle and limits","text":"自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","textEn":"Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查切割後是否留下短支線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect short stubs after cutting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自對準代表完全不需要切割對位。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。"],"optionsEn":["Self-alignment eliminates all cut alignment.","Every line necessarily has the same error.","Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘留支線可能改變寄生與短路風險。 自對準線條仍需要切割或阻擋圖形定義電路。","explanationEn":"Residual stubs can affect parasitics and shorting risk. Self-aligned lines still need cuts or blocks to define circuits."}}]},{"id":"a044-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"誤差與電性","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests","description":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","descriptionEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors.","steps":[{"id":"a044-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-18"],"title":"逐群統計四組線寬與間距","titleEn":"Measure widths and spaces by all four line groups","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors.","instruction":"逐群統計四組線寬與間距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure widths and spaces by all four line groups. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors.","observation":"混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「逐群統計四組線寬與間距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure widths and spaces by all four line groups\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。","textEn":"Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors."},{"id":"a044-v8-19-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「逐群統計四組線寬與間距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure widths and spaces by all four line groups\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。"],"optionsEn":["Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors.","Every line necessarily has the same error.","SAQP means exposing four times."],"answer":0,"explanation":"混合平均可能掩蓋系統性交替誤差。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Pooled averages can hide systematic alternating errors. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}},{"id":"a044-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-19"],"title":"把側壁粗糙度與硬罩粗糙度對照","titleEn":"Compare spacer and hard-mask roughness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum.","instruction":"把側壁粗糙度與硬罩粗糙度對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare spacer and hard-mask roughness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum.","observation":"轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把側壁粗糙度與硬罩粗糙度對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare spacer and hard-mask roughness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。","textEn":"Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum."},{"id":"a044-v8-20-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把側壁粗糙度與硬罩粗糙度對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare spacer and hard-mask roughness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。"],"optionsEn":["Every line necessarily has the same error.","Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum.","SAQP means exposing four times."],"answer":1,"explanation":"轉移可能改變粗糙度頻譜。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Transfer can alter the roughness spectrum. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}},{"id":"a044-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-20"],"title":"用金屬電阻比較不同線群","titleEn":"Compare line-group resistance after metallization","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Similar images can hide different conducting areas.","instruction":"用金屬電阻比較不同線群。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare line-group resistance after metallization. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Similar images can hide different conducting areas.","observation":"相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Similar images can hide different conducting areas. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用金屬電阻比較不同線群」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare line-group resistance after metallization\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Similar images can hide different conducting areas.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。","textEn":"Similar images can hide different conducting areas."},{"id":"a044-v8-21-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用金屬電阻比較不同線群」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare line-group resistance after metallization\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。"],"optionsEn":["Every line necessarily has the same error.","SAQP means exposing four times.","Similar images can hide different conducting areas."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相似影像可能有不同有效導電面積。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Similar images can hide different conducting areas. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}},{"id":"a044-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-21"],"title":"檢查切割區的漏電與開路","titleEn":"Check leakage and opens at cut regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：線體與線端需要不同電性載具。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles.","instruction":"檢查切割區的漏電與開路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「線體與線端需要不同電性載具。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check leakage and opens at cut regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles.","observation":"線體與線端需要不同電性載具。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查切割區的漏電與開路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「線體與線端需要不同電性載具。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check leakage and opens at cut regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"線體與線端需要不同電性載具。","textEn":"Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles."},{"id":"a044-v8-22-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查切割區的漏電與開路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check leakage and opens at cut regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線體與線端需要不同電性載具。","所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。"],"optionsEn":["Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles.","Every line necessarily has the same error.","SAQP means exposing four times."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線體與線端需要不同電性載具。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Line bodies and ends need different electrical vehicles. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}},{"id":"a044-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-22"],"title":"比較 SAQP 與單次成像的完整預算","titleEn":"Compare complete SAQP and single-image budgets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation.","instruction":"比較 SAQP 與單次成像的完整預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare complete SAQP and single-image budgets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation.","observation":"自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 SAQP 與單次成像的完整預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare complete SAQP and single-image budgets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。","textEn":"Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation."},{"id":"a044-v8-23-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 SAQP 與單次成像的完整預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare complete SAQP and single-image budgets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。"],"optionsEn":["Every line necessarily has the same error.","Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation.","SAQP means exposing four times."],"answer":1,"explanation":"自對準收益須扣除新增製程變異。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Self-alignment gains must account for added process variation. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}},{"id":"a044-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-saqp","v8b-multipattern","v8b-pattern","v8b-euvyield"],"prerequisiteIds":["a044-v8-23"],"title":"交付可追溯的四代圖形流程","titleEn":"Deliver a traceable four-generation pattern flow","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Each transfer needs input and output evidence.","instruction":"交付可追溯的四代圖形流程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a traceable four-generation pattern flow. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Each transfer needs input and output evidence.","observation":"每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Each transfer needs input and output evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有線條誤差必然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every line necessarily has the same error.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付可追溯的四代圖形流程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a traceable four-generation pattern flow\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Each transfer needs input and output evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a044-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。","textEn":"Each transfer needs input and output evidence."},{"id":"a044-v8-24-k2","title":"誤差與電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Errors and electrical tests: principle and limits","text":"四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","textEn":"Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付可追溯的四代圖形流程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a traceable four-generation pattern flow\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有線條誤差必然完全相同。","SAQP 就是連續曝光四次。","每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。"],"optionsEn":["Every line necessarily has the same error.","SAQP means exposing four times.","Each transfer needs input and output evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每道轉移都需有輸入與輸出證據。 四倍密度不表示所有線寬、間距與端點誤差自動一致。","explanationEn":"Each transfer needs input and output evidence. Fourfold density does not automatically equalize widths, spaces or end errors."}}]}]},{"id":"a045","title":"導向自組裝圖案化","titleEn":"Directed self-assembly patterning","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究自組裝原理、引導模板、缺陷與轉移、整合選擇；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: self-assembly principles, guiding templates, defects and transfer, integration choices. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["自組裝原理","引導模板","缺陷與轉移","整合選擇"],"labelsEn":["Self-assembly principles","Guiding templates","Defects and transfer","Integration choices"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a045-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"自組裝原理","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles","description":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","descriptionEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation.","steps":[{"id":"a045-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分開區塊相分離與宏觀混合","titleEn":"Distinguish microphase separation from macroscopic mixing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation.","instruction":"分開區塊相分離與宏觀混合。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish microphase separation from macroscopic mixing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation.","observation":"共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開區塊相分離與宏觀混合」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish microphase separation from macroscopic mixing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。","textEn":"Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation."},{"id":"a045-v8-01-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開區塊相分離與宏觀混合」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish microphase separation from macroscopic mixing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。"],"optionsEn":["Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation.","Self-assembly needs no placement template.","The same material orders identically at every thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共價連接限制兩區塊完全分離。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"Covalent linkage prevents complete block separation. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}},{"id":"a045-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-01"],"title":"以組成比例比較柱狀與層狀相","titleEn":"Compare cylinder and lamellar phases by composition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相態取決於材料與組成條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Morphology depends on material and composition.","instruction":"以組成比例比較柱狀與層狀相。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「相態取決於材料與組成條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare cylinder and lamellar phases by composition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Morphology depends on material and composition.","observation":"相態取決於材料與組成條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Morphology depends on material and composition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以組成比例比較柱狀與層狀相」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相態取決於材料與組成條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare cylinder and lamellar phases by composition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Morphology depends on material and composition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相態取決於材料與組成條件。","textEn":"Morphology depends on material and composition."},{"id":"a045-v8-02-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以組成比例比較柱狀與層狀相」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare cylinder and lamellar phases by composition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","相態取決於材料與組成條件。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。"],"optionsEn":["Self-assembly needs no placement template.","Morphology depends on material and composition.","The same material orders identically at every thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相態取決於材料與組成條件。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"Morphology depends on material and composition. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}},{"id":"a045-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-02"],"title":"標示自然週期與模板週期","titleEn":"Mark natural and guiding periods","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：模板需與材料尺度相容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Guides must be compatible with the material length scale.","instruction":"標示自然週期與模板週期。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「模板需與材料尺度相容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark natural and guiding periods. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Guides must be compatible with the material length scale.","observation":"模板需與材料尺度相容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Guides must be compatible with the material length scale. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標示自然週期與模板週期」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「模板需與材料尺度相容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark natural and guiding periods\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Guides must be compatible with the material length scale.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"模板需與材料尺度相容。","textEn":"Guides must be compatible with the material length scale."},{"id":"a045-v8-03-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標示自然週期與模板週期」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark natural and guiding periods\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","模板需與材料尺度相容。"],"optionsEn":["Self-assembly needs no placement template.","The same material orders identically at every thickness.","Guides must be compatible with the material length scale."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模板需與材料尺度相容。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"Guides must be compatible with the material length scale. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}},{"id":"a045-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-03"],"title":"比較高χ材料與較低χ材料的目標","titleEn":"Compare high-χ and lower-χ material goals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control.","instruction":"比較高χ材料與較低χ材料的目標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare high-χ and lower-χ material goals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control.","observation":"提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較高χ材料與較低χ材料的目標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare high-χ and lower-χ material goals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。","textEn":"Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control."},{"id":"a045-v8-04-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較高χ材料與較低χ材料的目標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare high-χ and lower-χ material goals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。"],"optionsEn":["Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control.","Self-assembly needs no placement template.","The same material orders identically at every thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高分離強度仍需處理界面與動力學。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"Stronger segregation still requires interface and kinetic control. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}},{"id":"a045-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-04"],"title":"畫出缺陷能量與退火動力學的分工","titleEn":"Separate defect energetics from annealing kinetics","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time.","instruction":"畫出缺陷能量與退火動力學的分工。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate defect energetics from annealing kinetics. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time.","observation":"最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出缺陷能量與退火動力學的分工」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate defect energetics from annealing kinetics\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。","textEn":"The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time."},{"id":"a045-v8-05-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出缺陷能量與退火動力學的分工」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate defect energetics from annealing kinetics\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。"],"optionsEn":["Self-assembly needs no placement template.","The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time.","The same material orders identically at every thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最低能態不保證在有限時間內到達。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"The lowest-energy state may not be reached in finite time. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}},{"id":"a045-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-05"],"title":"區分密度倍增與任意電路成形","titleEn":"Distinguish density multiplication from arbitrary circuitry","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern.","instruction":"區分密度倍增與任意電路成形。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish density multiplication from arbitrary circuitry. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern.","observation":"規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-assembly needs no placement template.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分密度倍增與任意電路成形」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish density multiplication from arbitrary circuitry\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。","textEn":"Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern."},{"id":"a045-v8-06-k2","title":"自組裝原理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-assembly principles: principle and limits","text":"區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","textEn":"Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分密度倍增與任意電路成形」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish density multiplication from arbitrary circuitry\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Self-assembly needs no placement template.","The same material orders identically at every thickness.","Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern."],"answer":2,"explanation":"規則自組裝不直接產生所有電路圖形。 區塊共聚物的自組裝有固有尺度，但仍需模板設定位置與方向。","explanationEn":"Regular self-assembly does not directly generate every circuit pattern. Block-copolymer self-assembly has a natural scale but still needs guides for placement and orientation."}}]},{"id":"a045-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"引導模板","titleEn":"Guiding templates","description":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","descriptionEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering.","steps":[{"id":"a045-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-06"],"title":"比較化學引導與地形引導","titleEn":"Compare chemical and topographic guidance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者以不同邊界條件定位。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They guide through different boundary conditions.","instruction":"比較化學引導與地形引導。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「兩者以不同邊界條件定位。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare chemical and topographic guidance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: They guide through different boundary conditions.","observation":"兩者以不同邊界條件定位。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They guide through different boundary conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較化學引導與地形引導」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者以不同邊界條件定位。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare chemical and topographic guidance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They guide through different boundary conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者以不同邊界條件定位。","textEn":"They guide through different boundary conditions."},{"id":"a045-v8-07-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較化學引導與地形引導」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare chemical and topographic guidance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩者以不同邊界條件定位。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["They guide through different boundary conditions.","The same material orders identically at every thickness.","One micrograph proves zero defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩者以不同邊界條件定位。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"They guide through different boundary conditions. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}},{"id":"a045-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-07"],"title":"標記中性層與選擇性潤濕層","titleEn":"Mark neutral and preferential wetting layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface preference can change block orientation.","instruction":"標記中性層與選擇性潤濕層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark neutral and preferential wetting layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface preference can change block orientation.","observation":"表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface preference can change block orientation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記中性層與選擇性潤濕層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark neutral and preferential wetting layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface preference can change block orientation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。","textEn":"Surface preference can change block orientation."},{"id":"a045-v8-08-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記中性層與選擇性潤濕層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark neutral and preferential wetting layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["The same material orders identically at every thickness.","Surface preference can change block orientation.","One micrograph proves zero defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面偏好可能改變區塊方向。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"Surface preference can change block orientation. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}},{"id":"a045-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-08"],"title":"量測模板線寬對排列的影響","titleEn":"Assess guide-width effects on ordering","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Guide-size error propagates into ordering.","instruction":"量測模板線寬對排列的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess guide-width effects on ordering. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Guide-size error propagates into ordering.","observation":"模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Guide-size error propagates into ordering. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測模板線寬對排列的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess guide-width effects on ordering\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Guide-size error propagates into ordering.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。","textEn":"Guide-size error propagates into ordering."},{"id":"a045-v8-09-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測模板線寬對排列的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess guide-width effects on ordering\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。"],"optionsEn":["The same material orders identically at every thickness.","One micrograph proves zero defects.","Guide-size error propagates into ordering."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模板尺寸誤差會傳入自組裝結果。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"Guide-size error propagates into ordering. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}},{"id":"a045-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-09"],"title":"比較薄膜厚度與自然週期的比例","titleEn":"Compare film thickness with natural period","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation.","instruction":"比較薄膜厚度與自然週期的比例。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare film thickness with natural period. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation.","observation":"厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較薄膜厚度與自然週期的比例」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare film thickness with natural period\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。","textEn":"Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation."},{"id":"a045-v8-10-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較薄膜厚度與自然週期的比例」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare film thickness with natural period\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。","只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation.","The same material orders identically at every thickness.","One micrograph proves zero defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度不相容可能引起缺陷或方向改變。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"Incompatible thickness can cause defects or reorientation. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}},{"id":"a045-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-10"],"title":"建立退火條件的對照矩陣","titleEn":"Build an annealing-condition comparison matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering.","instruction":"建立退火條件的對照矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build an annealing-condition comparison matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering.","observation":"熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立退火條件的對照矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build an annealing-condition comparison matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。","textEn":"Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering."},{"id":"a045-v8-11-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立退火條件的對照矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build an annealing-condition comparison matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["The same material orders identically at every thickness.","Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering.","One micrograph proves zero defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"熱史與溶劑史可能產生不同排列。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"Thermal and solvent histories can produce different ordering. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}},{"id":"a045-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-11"],"title":"追蹤模板邊界附近的排列","titleEn":"Track ordering near guide boundaries","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Boundary behavior can differ from the interior.","instruction":"追蹤模板邊界附近的排列。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track ordering near guide boundaries. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Boundary behavior can differ from the interior.","observation":"邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Boundary behavior can differ from the interior. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The same material orders identically at every thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤模板邊界附近的排列」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track ordering near guide boundaries\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Boundary behavior can differ from the interior.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。","textEn":"Boundary behavior can differ from the interior."},{"id":"a045-v8-12-k2","title":"引導模板的原理與限制","titleEn":"Guiding templates: principle and limits","text":"表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","textEn":"Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤模板邊界附近的排列」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track ordering near guide boundaries\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要材料相同，所有厚度都形成相同排列。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。"],"optionsEn":["The same material orders identically at every thickness.","One micrograph proves zero defects.","Boundary behavior can differ from the interior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊界效應可能不同於內部區域。 表面化學、侷限幾何與薄膜厚度共同控制排列。","explanationEn":"Boundary behavior can differ from the interior. Surface chemistry, confinement and film thickness jointly control ordering."}}]},{"id":"a045-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"缺陷與轉移","titleEn":"Defects and transfer","description":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","descriptionEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics.","steps":[{"id":"a045-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-12"],"title":"將位錯、橋接與缺失線分開","titleEn":"Separate dislocations, bridges and missing lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms.","instruction":"將位錯、橋接與缺失線分開。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate dislocations, bridges and missing lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms.","observation":"不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將位錯、橋接與缺失線分開」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate dislocations, bridges and missing lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。","textEn":"Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms."},{"id":"a045-v8-13-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","textEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將位錯、橋接與缺失線分開」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate dislocations, bridges and missing lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。"],"optionsEn":["Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms.","One micrograph proves zero defects.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同缺陷代表不同失敗機制。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Different defect classes indicate different failure mechanisms. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}},{"id":"a045-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-13"],"title":"估算檢查面積與罕見缺陷信賴區間","titleEn":"Relate inspected area to rare-defect confidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims.","instruction":"估算檢查面積與罕見缺陷信賴區間。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設對 10⁶ 個獨立且同分布的自組裝位置檢查，未發現缺陷。以零事件近似 95% 上限 3/N，得到 p<約 3×10⁻⁶；不是 p=0。若空間群聚讓有效獨立樣本數只剩 10⁵，上限變為約 3×10⁻⁵。畫出分散與群聚取樣，說明需先驗證獨立性。","instructionEn":"Relate inspected area to rare-defect confidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Inspect 10⁶ hypothetical independent, identically distributed assembly sites and observe no defects. The approximate zero-event 95% upper bound 3/N is about 3×10⁻⁶, not zero. If spatial clustering reduces effective independent samples to 10⁵, the bound becomes about 3×10⁻⁵. Sketch dispersed and clustered sampling and explain the independence requirement.","observation":"樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付兩個上限與獨立性限制，不宣稱零缺陷製程。","observationEn":"Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport both bounds and the independence limitation without claiming a defect-free process.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算檢查面積與罕見缺陷信賴區間」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付兩個上限與獨立性限制，不宣稱零缺陷製程。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate inspected area to rare-defect confidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report both bounds and the independence limitation without claiming a defect-free process.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。","textEn":"Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims."},{"id":"a045-v8-14-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設對 10⁶ 個獨立且同分布的自組裝位置檢查，未發現缺陷。以零事件近似 95% 上限 3/N，得到 p<約 3×10⁻⁶；不是 p=0。若空間群聚讓有效獨立樣本數只剩 10⁵，上限變為約 3×10⁻⁵。畫出分散與群聚取樣，說明需先驗證獨立性。","textEn":"Inspect 10⁶ hypothetical independent, identically distributed assembly sites and observe no defects. The approximate zero-event 95% upper bound 3/N is about 3×10⁻⁶, not zero. If spatial clustering reduces effective independent samples to 10⁵, the bound becomes about 3×10⁻⁵. Sketch dispersed and clustered sampling and explain the independence requirement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算檢查面積與罕見缺陷信賴區間」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate inspected area to rare-defect confidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。"],"optionsEn":["One micrograph proves zero defects.","Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"樣本面積限制可聲稱的缺陷率。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Sample area limits supportable defect-rate claims. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設對 10⁶ 個獨立且同分布的自組裝位置檢查，未發現缺陷。以零事件近似 95% 上限 3/N，得到 p<約 3×10⁻⁶；不是 p=0。若空間群聚讓有效獨立樣本數只剩 10⁵，上限變為約 3×10⁻⁵。畫出分散與群聚取樣，說明需先驗證獨立性。","textEn":"Inspect 10⁶ hypothetical independent, identically distributed assembly sites and observe no defects. The approximate zero-event 95% upper bound 3/N is about 3×10⁻⁶, not zero. If spatial clustering reduces effective independent samples to 10⁵, the bound becomes about 3×10⁻⁵. Sketch dispersed and clustered sampling and explain the independence requirement.","check":"交付兩個上限與獨立性限制，不宣稱零缺陷製程。","checkEn":"Report both bounds and the independence limitation without claiming a defect-free process."}},{"id":"a045-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-14"],"title":"比較模板缺陷與自組裝缺陷位置","titleEn":"Compare guide-defect and assembly-defect locations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spatial association helps trace origins.","instruction":"比較模板缺陷與自組裝缺陷位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare guide-defect and assembly-defect locations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spatial association helps trace origins.","observation":"空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Spatial association helps trace origins. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較模板缺陷與自組裝缺陷位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare guide-defect and assembly-defect locations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spatial association helps trace origins.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。","textEn":"Spatial association helps trace origins."},{"id":"a045-v8-15-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","textEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較模板缺陷與自組裝缺陷位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare guide-defect and assembly-defect locations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。"],"optionsEn":["One micrograph proves zero defects.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Spatial association helps trace origins."],"answer":2,"explanation":"空間關聯有助於追蹤來源。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Spatial association helps trace origins. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}},{"id":"a045-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-15"],"title":"設計移除單一區塊後的檢查","titleEn":"Plan inspection after removing one block","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Selective removal can damage retained blocks.","instruction":"設計移除單一區塊後的檢查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan inspection after removing one block. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Selective removal can damage retained blocks.","observation":"選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Selective removal can damage retained blocks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計移除單一區塊後的檢查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan inspection after removing one block\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Selective removal can damage retained blocks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。","textEn":"Selective removal can damage retained blocks."},{"id":"a045-v8-16-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","textEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計移除單一區塊後的檢查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan inspection after removing one block\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。","單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。"],"optionsEn":["Selective removal can damage retained blocks.","One micrograph proves zero defects.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇性移除也可能傷害保留區塊。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Selective removal can damage retained blocks. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}},{"id":"a045-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-16"],"title":"比較浸潤強化前後的輪廓","titleEn":"Compare contours before and after infiltration strengthening","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions.","instruction":"比較浸潤強化前後的輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare contours before and after infiltration strengthening. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions.","observation":"強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較浸潤強化前後的輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare contours before and after infiltration strengthening\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。","textEn":"Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions."},{"id":"a045-v8-17-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","textEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較浸潤強化前後的輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare contours before and after infiltration strengthening\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。"],"optionsEn":["One micrograph proves zero defects.","Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"強化改善耐受性但可能改變尺寸。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Strengthening can improve resistance while changing dimensions. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}},{"id":"a045-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-17"],"title":"追蹤聚合物到硬罩的缺陷","titleEn":"Trace defects from polymer into the hard mask","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transfer can change defect size and visibility.","instruction":"追蹤聚合物到硬罩的缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace defects from polymer into the hard mask. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transfer can change defect size and visibility.","observation":"轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transfer can change defect size and visibility. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One micrograph proves zero defects.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤聚合物到硬罩的缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace defects from polymer into the hard mask\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transfer can change defect size and visibility.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。","textEn":"Transfer can change defect size and visibility."},{"id":"a045-v8-18-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","textEn":"Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤聚合物到硬罩的缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace defects from polymer into the hard mask\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單張顯微照片足以證明零缺陷。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。"],"optionsEn":["One micrograph proves zero defects.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Transfer can change defect size and visibility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉移會改變缺陷大小與可見度。 漂亮的局部排列不能替代大面積缺陷統計。","explanationEn":"Transfer can change defect size and visibility. Attractive local ordering does not replace large-area defect statistics."}}]},{"id":"a045-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合選擇","titleEn":"Integration choices","description":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","descriptionEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure.","steps":[{"id":"a045-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-18"],"title":"比較線條與接觸孔縮小的用途","titleEn":"Compare line patterning with contact-hole shrinking","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria.","instruction":"比較線條與接觸孔縮小的用途。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare line patterning with contact-hole shrinking. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria.","observation":"不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較線條與接觸孔縮小的用途」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare line patterning with contact-hole shrinking\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。","textEn":"Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria."},{"id":"a045-v8-19-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較線條與接觸孔縮小的用途」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare line patterning with contact-hole shrinking\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。"],"optionsEn":["Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Self-assembly needs no placement template."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同用途需要不同模板與驗收。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"Different uses require different guides and acceptance criteria. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}},{"id":"a045-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-19"],"title":"把自組裝位置誤差加入套刻預算","titleEn":"Include assembly-placement error in overlay budgets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement.","instruction":"把自組裝位置誤差加入套刻預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Include assembly-placement error in overlay budgets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement.","observation":"自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把自組裝位置誤差加入套刻預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Include assembly-placement error in overlay budgets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。","textEn":"Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement."},{"id":"a045-v8-20-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把自組裝位置誤差加入套刻預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Include assembly-placement error in overlay budgets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。"],"optionsEn":["Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement.","Self-assembly needs no placement template."],"answer":1,"explanation":"自然週期精準不代表絕對位置正確。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"Accurate natural pitch does not prove absolute placement. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}},{"id":"a045-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-20"],"title":"用電性結構檢查殘留橋接","titleEn":"Check residual bridges with electrical structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Morphological and electrical results may differ.","instruction":"用電性結構檢查殘留橋接。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check residual bridges with electrical structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Morphological and electrical results may differ.","observation":"形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Morphological and electrical results may differ. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用電性結構檢查殘留橋接」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check residual bridges with electrical structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Morphological and electrical results may differ.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。","textEn":"Morphological and electrical results may differ."},{"id":"a045-v8-21-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用電性結構檢查殘留橋接」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check residual bridges with electrical structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。"],"optionsEn":["Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Self-assembly needs no placement template.","Morphological and electrical results may differ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"形貌與電性結果可能不完全一致。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"Morphological and electrical results may differ. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}},{"id":"a045-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-21"],"title":"比較 DSA 與 EUV 補充關係","titleEn":"Compare DSA as a complement to EUV","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography.","instruction":"比較 DSA 與 EUV 補充關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare DSA as a complement to EUV. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography.","observation":"自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 DSA 與 EUV 補充關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare DSA as a complement to EUV\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。","textEn":"Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography."},{"id":"a045-v8-22-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 DSA 與 EUV 補充關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare DSA as a complement to EUV\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。","聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。"],"optionsEn":["Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography.","Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Self-assembly needs no placement template."],"answer":0,"explanation":"自組裝可協助圖案化而非必然取代微影。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"Self-assembly can assist rather than necessarily replace lithography. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}},{"id":"a045-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-22"],"title":"記錄實驗展示的尺寸與材料範圍","titleEn":"Document demonstration dimensions and material scope","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：研究展示只支持所測條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A demonstration supports only tested conditions.","instruction":"記錄實驗展示的尺寸與材料範圍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「研究展示只支持所測條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Document demonstration dimensions and material scope. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A demonstration supports only tested conditions.","observation":"研究展示只支持所測條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A demonstration supports only tested conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄實驗展示的尺寸與材料範圍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「研究展示只支持所測條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Document demonstration dimensions and material scope\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A demonstration supports only tested conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"研究展示只支持所測條件。","textEn":"A demonstration supports only tested conditions."},{"id":"a045-v8-23-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄實驗展示的尺寸與材料範圍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Document demonstration dimensions and material scope\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","研究展示只支持所測條件。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。"],"optionsEn":["Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","A demonstration supports only tested conditions.","Self-assembly needs no placement template."],"answer":1,"explanation":"研究展示只支持所測條件。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"A demonstration supports only tested conditions. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}},{"id":"a045-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-dsa","v8b-dsahigh","v8b-sis","v8b-pattern"],"prerequisiteIds":["a045-v8-23"],"title":"提交模板、材料與缺陷證據鏈","titleEn":"Deliver a guide–material–defect evidence chain","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence.","instruction":"提交模板、材料與缺陷證據鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a guide–material–defect evidence chain. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence.","observation":"可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提交模板、材料與缺陷證據鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a guide–material–defect evidence chain\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a045-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。","textEn":"Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence."},{"id":"a045-v8-24-k2","title":"整合選擇的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration choices: principle and limits","text":"移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","textEn":"Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提交模板、材料與缺陷證據鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a guide–material–defect evidence chain\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["聚合物圖案可直接等同最終金屬線。","自組裝完全不需要任何定位模板。","可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。"],"optionsEn":["Polymer patterns are equivalent to final metal lines.","Self-assembly needs no placement template.","Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可整合性需要位置、缺陷與轉移共同證據。 移除一個區塊及圖案轉移可能改變原始自組裝結構。","explanationEn":"Integrability needs combined placement, defect and transfer evidence. Removing one block and transferring patterns can change the original self-assembled structure."}}]}]},{"id":"a046","title":"奈米壓印微影","titleEn":"Nanoimprint lithography","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究模板與樹脂、填充與對位、固化與脫模、缺陷與轉移；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: template and resin, filling and alignment, curing and release, defects and transfer. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["模板與樹脂","填充與對位","固化與脫模","缺陷與轉移"],"labelsEn":["Template and resin","Filling and alignment","Curing and release","Defects and transfer"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a046-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"模板與樹脂","titleEn":"Template and resin","description":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","descriptionEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography.","steps":[{"id":"a046-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"比較模板接觸與光學投影的資訊傳遞","titleEn":"Compare information transfer by contact and projection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology.","instruction":"比較模板接觸與光學投影的資訊傳遞。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare information transfer by contact and projection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology.","observation":"接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較模板接觸與光學投影的資訊傳遞」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare information transfer by contact and projection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。","textEn":"Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology."},{"id":"a046-v8-01-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較模板接觸與光學投影的資訊傳遞」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare information transfer by contact and projection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸轉移仍需光學或其他對位量測。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Contact transfer still needs optical or other alignment metrology. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}},{"id":"a046-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-01"],"title":"畫出模板凹凸與最終光阻極性","titleEn":"Relate template relief to final resist polarity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer.","instruction":"畫出模板凹凸與最終光阻極性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate template relief to final resist polarity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer.","observation":"凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出模板凹凸與最終光阻極性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate template relief to final resist polarity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。","textEn":"Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer."},{"id":"a046-v8-02-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出模板凹凸與最終光阻極性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate template relief to final resist polarity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"凸凹關係須在圖案轉移前釐清。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Relief polarity must be clarified before transfer. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}},{"id":"a046-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-02"],"title":"標記模板主模與複製模的關係","titleEn":"Distinguish master templates from replicas","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Replication adds layers to defect traceability.","instruction":"標記模板主模與複製模的關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish master templates from replicas. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Replication adds layers to defect traceability.","observation":"複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Replication adds layers to defect traceability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記模板主模與複製模的關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish master templates from replicas\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Replication adds layers to defect traceability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。","textEn":"Replication adds layers to defect traceability."},{"id":"a046-v8-03-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記模板主模與複製模的關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish master templates from replicas\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。"],"optionsEn":["Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Replication adds layers to defect traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"複製會增加缺陷追溯層次。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Replication adds layers to defect traceability. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}},{"id":"a046-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-03"],"title":"比較線條、孔洞與大面積區的填充","titleEn":"Compare filling of lines, holes and broad regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local pattern density changes resin demand.","instruction":"比較線條、孔洞與大面積區的填充。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare filling of lines, holes and broad regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local pattern density changes resin demand.","observation":"局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local pattern density changes resin demand. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較線條、孔洞與大面積區的填充」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare filling of lines, holes and broad regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local pattern density changes resin demand.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。","textEn":"Local pattern density changes resin demand."},{"id":"a046-v8-04-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較線條、孔洞與大面積區的填充」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare filling of lines, holes and broad regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Local pattern density changes resin demand.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部圖形密度改變樹脂需求。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Local pattern density changes resin demand. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}},{"id":"a046-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-04"],"title":"列出樹脂黏度與潤濕的角色","titleEn":"Identify the roles of viscosity and wetting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：填充不只取決於施加力量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Filling depends on more than applied force.","instruction":"列出樹脂黏度與潤濕的角色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「填充不只取決於施加力量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify the roles of viscosity and wetting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Filling depends on more than applied force.","observation":"填充不只取決於施加力量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Filling depends on more than applied force. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出樹脂黏度與潤濕的角色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「填充不只取決於施加力量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify the roles of viscosity and wetting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Filling depends on more than applied force.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"填充不只取決於施加力量。","textEn":"Filling depends on more than applied force."},{"id":"a046-v8-05-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出樹脂黏度與潤濕的角色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify the roles of viscosity and wetting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","填充不只取決於施加力量。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","Filling depends on more than applied force.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"填充不只取決於施加力量。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Filling depends on more than applied force. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}},{"id":"a046-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-05"],"title":"建立模板耐用度與清潔的評估項","titleEn":"Define template-durability and cleaning measures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime.","instruction":"建立模板耐用度與清潔的評估項。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define template-durability and cleaning measures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime.","observation":"清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立模板耐用度與清潔的評估項」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define template-durability and cleaning measures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。","textEn":"Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime."},{"id":"a046-v8-06-k2","title":"模板與樹脂的原理與限制","titleEn":"Template and resin: principle and limits","text":"奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","textEn":"Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立模板耐用度與清潔的評估項」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define template-durability and cleaning measures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。"],"optionsEn":["Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime."],"answer":2,"explanation":"清潔效率不能脫離表面壽命評估。 奈米壓印以模板與樹脂的接觸轉移圖形，與投影微影機制不同。","explanationEn":"Cleaning efficacy must be assessed with surface lifetime. Nanoimprint transfers patterns through template–resin contact, unlike projection lithography."}}]},{"id":"a046-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"填充與對位","titleEn":"Filling and alignment","description":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","descriptionEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control.","steps":[{"id":"a046-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-06"],"title":"依局部圖案體積規畫滴液分布","titleEn":"Plan droplets using local pattern volume","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers.","instruction":"依局部圖案體積規畫滴液分布。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設模板凹槽總體積 100 μm³，壓印區面積 1000 μm²，目標殘留層厚度 0.020 μm。理想所需樹脂體積為 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³。若滴入 140 μm³且完全填充、沒有流出或收縮，殘留層為 (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm，即 40 nm。實際還需評估氣泡、收縮與局部密度，不能只用總體積保證均勻。","instructionEn":"Plan droplets using local pattern volume. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume 100 μm³ of template-cavity volume, 1000 μm² imprint area and a target 0.020 μm residual layer. Ideal resin volume is 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³. Dispensing 140 μm³ with complete filling and no outflow or shrinkage yields (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm, or 40 nm, residual thickness. Bubbles, shrinkage and local density still matter; total volume does not guarantee uniformity.","observation":"均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n算出 120 μm³與 40 nm，並列出體積守恆假設。","observationEn":"Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nCalculate 120 μm³ and 40 nm and state the volume-conservation assumptions.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「依局部圖案體積規畫滴液分布」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：算出 120 μm³與 40 nm，並列出體積守恆假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan droplets using local pattern volume\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Calculate 120 μm³ and 40 nm and state the volume-conservation assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。","textEn":"Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers."},{"id":"a046-v8-07-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設模板凹槽總體積 100 μm³，壓印區面積 1000 μm²，目標殘留層厚度 0.020 μm。理想所需樹脂體積為 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³。若滴入 140 μm³且完全填充、沒有流出或收縮，殘留層為 (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm，即 40 nm。實際還需評估氣泡、收縮與局部密度，不能只用總體積保證均勻。","textEn":"Assume 100 μm³ of template-cavity volume, 1000 μm² imprint area and a target 0.020 μm residual layer. Ideal resin volume is 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³. Dispensing 140 μm³ with complete filling and no outflow or shrinkage yields (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm, or 40 nm, residual thickness. Bubbles, shrinkage and local density still matter; total volume does not guarantee uniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「依局部圖案體積規畫滴液分布」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan droplets using local pattern volume\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻滴液未必得到均勻殘留層。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Uniform droplets need not yield uniform residual layers. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設模板凹槽總體積 100 μm³，壓印區面積 1000 μm²，目標殘留層厚度 0.020 μm。理想所需樹脂體積為 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³。若滴入 140 μm³且完全填充、沒有流出或收縮，殘留層為 (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm，即 40 nm。實際還需評估氣泡、收縮與局部密度，不能只用總體積保證均勻。","textEn":"Assume 100 μm³ of template-cavity volume, 1000 μm² imprint area and a target 0.020 μm residual layer. Ideal resin volume is 100+1000×0.020=120 μm³. Dispensing 140 μm³ with complete filling and no outflow or shrinkage yields (140-100)/1000=0.040 μm, or 40 nm, residual thickness. Bubbles, shrinkage and local density still matter; total volume does not guarantee uniformity.","check":"算出 120 μm³與 40 nm，並列出體積守恆假設。","checkEn":"Calculate 120 μm³ and 40 nm and state the volume-conservation assumptions."}},{"id":"a046-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-07"],"title":"追蹤兩滴樹脂合流的氣泡風險","titleEn":"Track bubble risk where droplets merge","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：被困氣體會造成未填滿區。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Trapped gas can create unfilled regions.","instruction":"追蹤兩滴樹脂合流的氣泡風險。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「被困氣體會造成未填滿區。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track bubble risk where droplets merge. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Trapped gas can create unfilled regions.","observation":"被困氣體會造成未填滿區。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Trapped gas can create unfilled regions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤兩滴樹脂合流的氣泡風險」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「被困氣體會造成未填滿區。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track bubble risk where droplets merge\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Trapped gas can create unfilled regions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"被困氣體會造成未填滿區。","textEn":"Trapped gas can create unfilled regions."},{"id":"a046-v8-08-k2","title":"填充與對位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Filling and alignment: principle and limits","text":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","textEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤兩滴樹脂合流的氣泡風險」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track bubble risk where droplets merge\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","被困氣體會造成未填滿區。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。"],"optionsEn":["More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Trapped gas can create unfilled regions.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"被困氣體會造成未填滿區。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Trapped gas can create unfilled regions. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}},{"id":"a046-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-08"],"title":"比較接觸時間與填充完成度","titleEn":"Compare contact time with fill completeness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way.","instruction":"比較接觸時間與填充完成度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare contact time with fill completeness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way.","observation":"更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較接觸時間與填充完成度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare contact time with fill completeness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。","textEn":"Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way."},{"id":"a046-v8-09-k2","title":"填充與對位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Filling and alignment: principle and limits","text":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","textEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較接觸時間與填充完成度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare contact time with fill completeness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。","更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。"],"optionsEn":["More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更短時間可能增加缺陷但非線性關係。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Shorter time can increase defects in a nonlinear way. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}},{"id":"a046-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-09"],"title":"畫出模板與晶圓的對位標記","titleEn":"Draw template and wafer alignment marks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns.","instruction":"畫出模板與晶圓的對位標記。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw template and wafer alignment marks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns.","observation":"多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出模板與晶圓的對位標記」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw template and wafer alignment marks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。","textEn":"Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns."},{"id":"a046-v8-10-k2","title":"填充與對位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Filling and alignment: principle and limits","text":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","textEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出模板與晶圓的對位標記」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw template and wafer alignment marks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。","樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。"],"optionsEn":["Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns.","More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層製造仍需對準既有圖形。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Multilayer manufacturing still needs alignment to existing patterns. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}},{"id":"a046-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-10"],"title":"把晶圓變形加入套刻模型","titleEn":"Include wafer deformation in overlay models","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation.","instruction":"把晶圓變形加入套刻模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Include wafer deformation in overlay models. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation.","observation":"剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把晶圓變形加入套刻模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Include wafer deformation in overlay models\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。","textEn":"Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation."},{"id":"a046-v8-11-k2","title":"填充與對位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Filling and alignment: principle and limits","text":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","textEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把晶圓變形加入套刻模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Include wafer deformation in overlay models\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。"],"optionsEn":["More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剛體位移不足以描述所有形變。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Rigid displacement cannot describe every deformation. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}},{"id":"a046-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-11"],"title":"比較局部圖案密度與殘留層厚度","titleEn":"Compare local density with residual-layer thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residual-layer differences propagate into etching.","instruction":"比較局部圖案密度與殘留層厚度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare local density with residual-layer thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residual-layer differences propagate into etching.","observation":"殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residual-layer differences propagate into etching. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More resin always improves filling and uniformity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較局部圖案密度與殘留層厚度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare local density with residual-layer thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residual-layer differences propagate into etching.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。","textEn":"Residual-layer differences propagate into etching."},{"id":"a046-v8-12-k2","title":"填充與對位的原理與限制","titleEn":"Filling and alignment: principle and limits","text":"填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","textEn":"Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較局部圖案密度與殘留層厚度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare local density with residual-layer thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["樹脂越多就一定填充越完整且均勻。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。","殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。"],"optionsEn":["More resin always improves filling and uniformity.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","Residual-layer differences propagate into etching."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘留層差異會傳入後續蝕刻。 填充速度與殘留層均勻性需同時控制。","explanationEn":"Residual-layer differences propagate into etching. Filling speed and residual-layer uniformity require joint control."}}]},{"id":"a046-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"固化與脫模","titleEn":"Curing and release","description":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","descriptionEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues.","steps":[{"id":"a046-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-12"],"title":"區分光固化與熱壓印的能量途徑","titleEn":"Distinguish photocuring from thermal imprinting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets.","instruction":"區分光固化與熱壓印的能量途徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish photocuring from thermal imprinting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets.","observation":"不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分光固化與熱壓印的能量途徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish photocuring from thermal imprinting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。","textEn":"Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets."},{"id":"a046-v8-13-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分光固化與熱壓印的能量途徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish photocuring from thermal imprinting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。"],"optionsEn":["Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","A small template defect affects only one imprint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同機制有不同材料與熱預算。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Different mechanisms have different materials and thermal budgets. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}},{"id":"a046-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-13"],"title":"檢查固化前後的體積收縮","titleEn":"Assess volume shrinkage during curing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress.","instruction":"檢查固化前後的體積收縮。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess volume shrinkage during curing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress.","observation":"收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查固化前後的體積收縮」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess volume shrinkage during curing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。","textEn":"Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress."},{"id":"a046-v8-14-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查固化前後的體積收縮」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess volume shrinkage during curing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["固化後可以忽略脫模力。","收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。"],"optionsEn":["Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress.","A small template defect affects only one imprint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"收縮可能改變尺寸與應力。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Shrinkage can alter dimensions and stress. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}},{"id":"a046-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-14"],"title":"畫出脫模方向與高深寬比結構","titleEn":"Relate release direction to high-aspect-ratio features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Release forces can damage fine structures.","instruction":"畫出脫模方向與高深寬比結構。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate release direction to high-aspect-ratio features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Release forces can damage fine structures.","observation":"脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Release forces can damage fine structures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出脫模方向與高深寬比結構」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate release direction to high-aspect-ratio features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Release forces can damage fine structures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。","textEn":"Release forces can damage fine structures."},{"id":"a046-v8-15-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出脫模方向與高深寬比結構」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate release direction to high-aspect-ratio features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["固化後可以忽略脫模力。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。"],"optionsEn":["Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Release forces can damage fine structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"脫模受力可能損傷細小結構。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Release forces can damage fine structures. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}},{"id":"a046-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-15"],"title":"比較抗黏附表面使用前後","titleEn":"Compare anti-adhesion surfaces before and after use","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface condition changes with use history.","instruction":"比較抗黏附表面使用前後。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare anti-adhesion surfaces before and after use. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface condition changes with use history.","observation":"表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface condition changes with use history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較抗黏附表面使用前後」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare anti-adhesion surfaces before and after use\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface condition changes with use history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。","textEn":"Surface condition changes with use history."},{"id":"a046-v8-16-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較抗黏附表面使用前後」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare anti-adhesion surfaces before and after use\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。","固化後可以忽略脫模力。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。"],"optionsEn":["Surface condition changes with use history.","Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","A small template defect affects only one imprint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面狀態會隨使用歷程改變。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Surface condition changes with use history. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}},{"id":"a046-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-16"],"title":"檢查模板污染對下一次壓印的影響","titleEn":"Assess template contamination in the next imprint","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：污染可在連續晶粒中複製。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contamination can replicate across successive dies.","instruction":"檢查模板污染對下一次壓印的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「污染可在連續晶粒中複製。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess template contamination in the next imprint. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contamination can replicate across successive dies.","observation":"污染可在連續晶粒中複製。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contamination can replicate across successive dies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查模板污染對下一次壓印的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「污染可在連續晶粒中複製。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess template contamination in the next imprint\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contamination can replicate across successive dies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"污染可在連續晶粒中複製。","textEn":"Contamination can replicate across successive dies."},{"id":"a046-v8-17-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查模板污染對下一次壓印的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess template contamination in the next imprint\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["固化後可以忽略脫模力。","污染可在連續晶粒中複製。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。"],"optionsEn":["Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","Contamination can replicate across successive dies.","A small template defect affects only one imprint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"污染可在連續晶粒中複製。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Contamination can replicate across successive dies. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}},{"id":"a046-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-17"],"title":"為脫模異常設計停止與複查條件","titleEn":"Define stop-and-review criteria for release anomalies","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage.","instruction":"為脫模異常設計停止與複查條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define stop-and-review criteria for release anomalies. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage.","observation":"持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「固化後可以忽略脫模力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為脫模異常設計停止與複查條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define stop-and-review criteria for release anomalies\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。","textEn":"Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage."},{"id":"a046-v8-18-k2","title":"固化與脫模的原理與限制","titleEn":"Curing and release: principle and limits","text":"固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","textEn":"Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為脫模異常設計停止與複查條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define stop-and-review criteria for release anomalies\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["固化後可以忽略脫模力。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Release force becomes irrelevant after curing.","A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"持續壓印可能擴大模板損傷。 固化與脫模會引入收縮、應力及黏附問題。","explanationEn":"Continuing to imprint can amplify template damage. Curing and release can introduce shrinkage, stress and adhesion issues."}}]},{"id":"a046-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"缺陷與轉移","titleEn":"Defects and transfer","description":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","descriptionEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks.","steps":[{"id":"a046-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-18"],"title":"將未填充、顆粒與脫模缺陷分類","titleEn":"Classify nonfill, particle and release defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Defect classification guides corrective action.","instruction":"將未填充、顆粒與脫模缺陷分類。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Classify nonfill, particle and release defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Defect classification guides corrective action.","observation":"缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Defect classification guides corrective action. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將未填充、顆粒與脫模缺陷分類」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Classify nonfill, particle and release defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Defect classification guides corrective action.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。","textEn":"Defect classification guides corrective action."},{"id":"a046-v8-19-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將未填充、顆粒與脫模缺陷分類」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Classify nonfill, particle and release defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。"],"optionsEn":["Defect classification guides corrective action.","A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷分類有助於選擇改善方向。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"Defect classification guides corrective action. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}},{"id":"a046-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-19"],"title":"量測殘留層開口後的尺寸","titleEn":"Measure dimensions after residual-layer opening","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls.","instruction":"量測殘留層開口後的尺寸。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure dimensions after residual-layer opening. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls.","observation":"開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測殘留層開口後的尺寸」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure dimensions after residual-layer opening\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。","textEn":"Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls."},{"id":"a046-v8-20-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測殘留層開口後的尺寸」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure dimensions after residual-layer opening\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。"],"optionsEn":["A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開口蝕刻也可能侵蝕圖形側壁。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"Opening etch can also erode pattern sidewalls. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}},{"id":"a046-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-20"],"title":"比較模板輪廓與最終硬罩輪廓","titleEn":"Compare template and final hard-mask contours","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases.","instruction":"比較模板輪廓與最終硬罩輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare template and final hard-mask contours. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases.","observation":"接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較模板輪廓與最終硬罩輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare template and final hard-mask contours\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。","textEn":"Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases."},{"id":"a046-v8-21-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較模板輪廓與最終硬罩輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare template and final hard-mask contours\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。"],"optionsEn":["A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸複製仍有多道尺寸偏差。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"Contact replication still accumulates dimensional biases. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}},{"id":"a046-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-21"],"title":"建立模板使用次數與缺陷趨勢","titleEn":"Trend defects against template use count","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：壽命評估需要序列資料。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Lifetime assessment needs sequential data.","instruction":"建立模板使用次數與缺陷趨勢。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「壽命評估需要序列資料。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trend defects against template use count. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Lifetime assessment needs sequential data.","observation":"壽命評估需要序列資料。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Lifetime assessment needs sequential data. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立模板使用次數與缺陷趨勢」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「壽命評估需要序列資料。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trend defects against template use count\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Lifetime assessment needs sequential data.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"壽命評估需要序列資料。","textEn":"Lifetime assessment needs sequential data."},{"id":"a046-v8-22-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立模板使用次數與缺陷趨勢」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trend defects against template use count\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["壽命評估需要序列資料。","模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。"],"optionsEn":["Lifetime assessment needs sequential data.","A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壽命評估需要序列資料。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"Lifetime assessment needs sequential data. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}},{"id":"a046-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-22"],"title":"比較吞吐、缺陷與套刻的共同窗口","titleEn":"Compare the joint throughput–defect–overlay window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity.","instruction":"比較吞吐、缺陷與套刻的共同窗口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare the joint throughput–defect–overlay window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity.","observation":"單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較吞吐、缺陷與套刻的共同窗口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare the joint throughput–defect–overlay window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。","textEn":"One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity."},{"id":"a046-v8-23-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較吞吐、缺陷與套刻的共同窗口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare the joint throughput–defect–overlay window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。"],"optionsEn":["A small template defect affects only one imprint.","One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一性能優勢不能代表整體成熟度。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"One performance advantage does not establish overall maturity. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}},{"id":"a046-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-nil","v8b-pattern","v8b-maskmetro","v8b-nil2018"],"prerequisiteIds":["a046-v8-23"],"title":"交付有代表性圖形的壓印驗證報告","titleEn":"Deliver imprint validation across representative patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Validation must cover density and shape diversity.","instruction":"交付有代表性圖形的壓印驗證報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver imprint validation across representative patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Validation must cover density and shape diversity.","observation":"驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Validation must cover density and shape diversity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A small template defect affects only one imprint.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付有代表性圖形的壓印驗證報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver imprint validation across representative patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Validation must cover density and shape diversity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a046-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。","textEn":"Validation must cover density and shape diversity."},{"id":"a046-v8-24-k2","title":"缺陷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and transfer: principle and limits","text":"模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","textEn":"Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付有代表性圖形的壓印驗證報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver imprint validation across representative patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["模板上的小缺陷只會影響一次。","奈米壓印只靠提高投影鏡頭 NA。","驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。"],"optionsEn":["A small template defect affects only one imprint.","Nanoimprint works by increasing projection-lens NA.","Validation must cover density and shape diversity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗證需涵蓋密度與形狀多樣性。 模板重複使用使顆粒與缺陷複製成為重要風險。","explanationEn":"Validation must cover density and shape diversity. Template reuse makes particles and replicated defects important risks."}}]}]},{"id":"a047","title":"電子束直接寫入","titleEn":"Electron-beam direct writing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究資料與束斑、曝光與散射、對位與拼接、顯影與驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: data and spot, exposure and scattering, alignment and stitching, development and validation. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["資料與束斑","曝光與散射","對位與拼接","顯影與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Data and spot","Exposure and scattering","Alignment and stitching","Development and validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a047-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"資料與束斑","titleEn":"Data and spot","description":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","descriptionEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time.","steps":[{"id":"a047-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把設計版圖轉成可寫入圖元","titleEn":"Convert layout into writable primitives","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Conversion must preserve scale and topology.","instruction":"把設計版圖轉成可寫入圖元。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Convert layout into writable primitives. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Conversion must preserve scale and topology.","observation":"資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Conversion must preserve scale and topology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把設計版圖轉成可寫入圖元」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Convert layout into writable primitives\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Conversion must preserve scale and topology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。","textEn":"Conversion must preserve scale and topology."},{"id":"a047-v8-01-k2","title":"資料與束斑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and spot: principle and limits","text":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","textEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把設計版圖轉成可寫入圖元」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Convert layout into writable primitives\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。"],"optionsEn":["Conversion must preserve scale and topology.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料轉換須保留尺度與拓樸。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Conversion must preserve scale and topology. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}},{"id":"a047-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-01"],"title":"比較正型與負型電子束光阻","titleEn":"Compare positive- and negative-tone e-beam resists","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光阻極性改變保留區域。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Resist tone changes the retained region.","instruction":"比較正型與負型電子束光阻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「光阻極性改變保留區域。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare positive- and negative-tone e-beam resists. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Resist tone changes the retained region.","observation":"光阻極性改變保留區域。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Resist tone changes the retained region. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較正型與負型電子束光阻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光阻極性改變保留區域。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare positive- and negative-tone e-beam resists\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Resist tone changes the retained region.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光阻極性改變保留區域。","textEn":"Resist tone changes the retained region."},{"id":"a047-v8-02-k2","title":"資料與束斑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and spot: principle and limits","text":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","textEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較正型與負型電子束光阻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare positive- and negative-tone e-beam resists\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","光阻極性改變保留區域。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。"],"optionsEn":["Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Resist tone changes the retained region.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光阻極性改變保留區域。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Resist tone changes the retained region. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}},{"id":"a047-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-02"],"title":"依最小圖形選擇取樣格點","titleEn":"Choose a sampling grid for the smallest features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error.","instruction":"依最小圖形選擇取樣格點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose a sampling grid for the smallest features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error.","observation":"格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「依最小圖形選擇取樣格點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose a sampling grid for the smallest features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。","textEn":"Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error."},{"id":"a047-v8-03-k2","title":"資料與束斑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and spot: principle and limits","text":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","textEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「依最小圖形選擇取樣格點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose a sampling grid for the smallest features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"格點量化會引入邊緣位置誤差。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Grid quantization introduces edge-placement error. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}},{"id":"a047-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-03"],"title":"估算曝光面積與總電荷","titleEn":"Estimate exposed area and total charge","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Total charge is area dose multiplied by area.","instruction":"估算曝光面積與總電荷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate exposed area and total charge. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Total charge is area dose multiplied by area.","observation":"總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Total charge is area dose multiplied by area. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算曝光面積與總電荷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate exposed area and total charge\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Total charge is area dose multiplied by area.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。","textEn":"Total charge is area dose multiplied by area."},{"id":"a047-v8-04-k2","title":"資料與束斑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and spot: principle and limits","text":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","textEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算曝光面積與總電荷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate exposed area and total charge\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。"],"optionsEn":["Total charge is area dose multiplied by area.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總電荷由面劑量與面積決定。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Total charge is area dose multiplied by area. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}},{"id":"a047-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-04"],"title":"分開曝光時間與載台等待時間","titleEn":"Separate beam time from stage overhead","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Writing throughput includes non-exposure time.","instruction":"分開曝光時間與載台等待時間。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設完整曝光面積為 1 mm²=0.01 cm²、面劑量 100 μC/cm²、束流 1 nA。總電荷為 1 μC，理想束流時間為 1000 s。再加 120 s 載台與資料開銷，總時間為 1120 s，約 18.7 min。這只是單一曝光面積的電荷帳本；不代表特定光阻配方或機台吞吐量。","instructionEn":"Separate beam time from stage overhead. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Writing throughput includes non-exposure time.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a fully exposed area of 1 mm²=0.01 cm², dose 100 μC/cm² and current 1 nA. Total charge is 1 μC and ideal beam time 1000 s. Adding 120 s of stage/data overhead gives 1120 s, about 18.7 min. This is a charge ledger for one area, not a resist recipe or tool-throughput claim.","observation":"寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付面積換算、1 μC 與 1120 s，勿漏掉非曝光開銷。","observationEn":"Writing throughput includes non-exposure time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nShow the area conversion, 1 μC and 1120 s without omitting non-exposure overhead.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開曝光時間與載台等待時間」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付面積換算、1 μC 與 1120 s，勿漏掉非曝光開銷。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate beam time from stage overhead\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Writing throughput includes non-exposure time.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Show the area conversion, 1 μC and 1120 s without omitting non-exposure overhead.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。","textEn":"Writing throughput includes non-exposure time."},{"id":"a047-v8-05-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設完整曝光面積為 1 mm²=0.01 cm²、面劑量 100 μC/cm²、束流 1 nA。總電荷為 1 μC，理想束流時間為 1000 s。再加 120 s 載台與資料開銷，總時間為 1120 s，約 18.7 min。這只是單一曝光面積的電荷帳本；不代表特定光阻配方或機台吞吐量。","textEn":"Assume a fully exposed area of 1 mm²=0.01 cm², dose 100 μC/cm² and current 1 nA. Total charge is 1 μC and ideal beam time 1000 s. Adding 120 s of stage/data overhead gives 1120 s, about 18.7 min. This is a charge ledger for one area, not a resist recipe or tool-throughput claim."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開曝光時間與載台等待時間」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate beam time from stage overhead\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。"],"optionsEn":["Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Writing throughput includes non-exposure time.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"寫入吞吐量包含非曝光時間。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Writing throughput includes non-exposure time. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設完整曝光面積為 1 mm²=0.01 cm²、面劑量 100 μC/cm²、束流 1 nA。總電荷為 1 μC，理想束流時間為 1000 s。再加 120 s 載台與資料開銷，總時間為 1120 s，約 18.7 min。這只是單一曝光面積的電荷帳本；不代表特定光阻配方或機台吞吐量。","textEn":"Assume a fully exposed area of 1 mm²=0.01 cm², dose 100 μC/cm² and current 1 nA. Total charge is 1 μC and ideal beam time 1000 s. Adding 120 s of stage/data overhead gives 1120 s, about 18.7 min. This is a charge ledger for one area, not a resist recipe or tool-throughput claim.","check":"交付面積換算、1 μC 與 1120 s，勿漏掉非曝光開銷。","checkEn":"Show the area conversion, 1 μC and 1120 s without omitting non-exposure overhead."}},{"id":"a047-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-05"],"title":"設定小片樣品的座標原點","titleEn":"Define the coordinate origin for a small sample","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation.","instruction":"設定小片樣品的座標原點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define the coordinate origin for a small sample. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation.","observation":"樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設定小片樣品的座標原點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define the coordinate origin for a small sample\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。","textEn":"Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation."},{"id":"a047-v8-06-k2","title":"資料與束斑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Data and spot: principle and limits","text":"電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","textEn":"Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設定小片樣品的座標原點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define the coordinate origin for a small sample\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。"],"optionsEn":["Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樣品座標與機台座標需要轉換。 電子束直寫直接在基板定義圖形，通常需在解析度與時間間取捨。","explanationEn":"Sample and instrument coordinates need transformation. Electron-beam direct writing patterns substrates directly, usually trading resolution against time."}}]},{"id":"a047-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"曝光與散射","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering","description":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","descriptionEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose.","steps":[{"id":"a047-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-06"],"title":"畫出前向散射與背向散射","titleEn":"Sketch forward and backscattering","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure.","instruction":"畫出前向散射與背向散射。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch forward and backscattering. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure.","observation":"基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出前向散射與背向散射」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch forward and backscattering\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。","textEn":"The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure."},{"id":"a047-v8-07-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出前向散射與背向散射」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch forward and backscattering\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基板會影響長程鄰近曝光。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"The substrate affects long-range proximity exposure. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}},{"id":"a047-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-07"],"title":"比較薄厚光阻中的束斑展寬","titleEn":"Compare beam broadening in thin and thick resists","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability.","instruction":"比較薄厚光阻中的束斑展寬。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare beam broadening in thin and thick resists. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability.","observation":"厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較薄厚光阻中的束斑展寬」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare beam broadening in thin and thick resists\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。","textEn":"Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability."},{"id":"a047-v8-08-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較薄厚光阻中的束斑展寬」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare beam broadening in thin and thick resists\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度會改變散射與後續轉移能力。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"Thickness changes scattering and transfer capability. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}},{"id":"a047-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-08"],"title":"建立密集與孤立圖形的劑量矩陣","titleEn":"Build dose matrices for dense and isolated features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pattern environment can change optimum dose.","instruction":"建立密集與孤立圖形的劑量矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build dose matrices for dense and isolated features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pattern environment can change optimum dose.","observation":"圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pattern environment can change optimum dose. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立密集與孤立圖形的劑量矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build dose matrices for dense and isolated features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pattern environment can change optimum dose.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。","textEn":"Pattern environment can change optimum dose."},{"id":"a047-v8-09-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立密集與孤立圖形的劑量矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build dose matrices for dense and isolated features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。"],"optionsEn":["Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Pattern environment can change optimum dose."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圖形環境會改變最佳劑量。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"Pattern environment can change optimum dose. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}},{"id":"a047-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-09"],"title":"檢查大面積曝光對小間隙的影響","titleEn":"Assess broad exposure next to a narrow gap","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Proximity energy can close a narrow gap.","instruction":"檢查大面積曝光對小間隙的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess broad exposure next to a narrow gap. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Proximity energy can close a narrow gap.","observation":"鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Proximity energy can close a narrow gap. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查大面積曝光對小間隙的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess broad exposure next to a narrow gap\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Proximity energy can close a narrow gap.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。","textEn":"Proximity energy can close a narrow gap."},{"id":"a047-v8-10-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查大面積曝光對小間隙的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess broad exposure next to a narrow gap\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。","每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Proximity energy can close a narrow gap.","Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鄰近沉積能量可能使間隙封閉。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"Proximity energy can close a narrow gap. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}},{"id":"a047-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-10"],"title":"比較導電與絕緣樣品的充電","titleEn":"Compare charging on conducting and insulating samples","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：充電可使束流偏轉。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Charging can deflect the beam.","instruction":"比較導電與絕緣樣品的充電。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「充電可使束流偏轉。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare charging on conducting and insulating samples. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Charging can deflect the beam.","observation":"充電可使束流偏轉。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Charging can deflect the beam. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較導電與絕緣樣品的充電」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「充電可使束流偏轉。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare charging on conducting and insulating samples\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Charging can deflect the beam.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"充電可使束流偏轉。","textEn":"Charging can deflect the beam."},{"id":"a047-v8-11-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較導電與絕緣樣品的充電」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare charging on conducting and insulating samples\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","充電可使束流偏轉。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Charging can deflect the beam.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"充電可使束流偏轉。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"Charging can deflect the beam. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}},{"id":"a047-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-11"],"title":"評估導電保護層的相容性","titleEn":"Assess compatibility of a conductive coating","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist.","instruction":"評估導電保護層的相容性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess compatibility of a conductive coating. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist.","observation":"抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估導電保護層的相容性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess compatibility of a conductive coating\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。","textEn":"Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist."},{"id":"a047-v8-12-k2","title":"曝光與散射的原理與限制","titleEn":"Exposure and scattering: principle and limits","text":"電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","textEn":"Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估導電保護層的相容性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess compatibility of a conductive coating\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個位置收到的能量只來自該點束流。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。"],"optionsEn":["Each location receives energy only from its own beam exposure.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抑制充電措施也須可移除且不破壞光阻。 電子散射使局部沉積能量不同於名目劑量。","explanationEn":"Charge suppression must be removable without harming resist. Electron scattering makes deposited energy differ from nominal dose."}}]},{"id":"a047-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"對位與拼接","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching","description":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","descriptionEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors.","steps":[{"id":"a047-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-12"],"title":"以多個標記擬合平移旋轉","titleEn":"Fit translation and rotation using several marks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mark geometry determines identifiable errors.","instruction":"以多個標記擬合平移旋轉。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Fit translation and rotation using several marks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mark geometry determines identifiable errors.","observation":"標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mark geometry determines identifiable errors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以多個標記擬合平移旋轉」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Fit translation and rotation using several marks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mark geometry determines identifiable errors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。","textEn":"Mark geometry determines identifiable errors."},{"id":"a047-v8-13-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以多個標記擬合平移旋轉」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Fit translation and rotation using several marks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。"],"optionsEn":["Mark geometry determines identifiable errors.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"標記配置決定可辨識的誤差類型。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"Mark geometry determines identifiable errors. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}},{"id":"a047-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-13"],"title":"檢查標記辨識的訊號與損傷","titleEn":"Assess alignment-mark signal and damage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist.","instruction":"檢查標記辨識的訊號與損傷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess alignment-mark signal and damage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist.","observation":"辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查標記辨識的訊號與損傷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess alignment-mark signal and damage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。","textEn":"Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist."},{"id":"a047-v8-14-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查標記辨識的訊號與損傷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess alignment-mark signal and damage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。"],"optionsEn":["Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"辨識曝光可能影響附近光阻。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"Mark-detection exposure can affect nearby resist. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}},{"id":"a047-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-14"],"title":"把大圖形跨場放置並檢查接縫","titleEn":"Place a large pattern across fields and inspect seams","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：連續設計可能被寫入場切割。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A continuous design can be divided by writing fields.","instruction":"把大圖形跨場放置並檢查接縫。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「連續設計可能被寫入場切割。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Place a large pattern across fields and inspect seams. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: A continuous design can be divided by writing fields.","observation":"連續設計可能被寫入場切割。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A continuous design can be divided by writing fields. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把大圖形跨場放置並檢查接縫」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「連續設計可能被寫入場切割。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Place a large pattern across fields and inspect seams\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A continuous design can be divided by writing fields.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"連續設計可能被寫入場切割。","textEn":"A continuous design can be divided by writing fields."},{"id":"a047-v8-15-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把大圖形跨場放置並檢查接縫」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Place a large pattern across fields and inspect seams\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","連續設計可能被寫入場切割。"],"optionsEn":["Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","A continuous design can be divided by writing fields."],"answer":2,"explanation":"連續設計可能被寫入場切割。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"A continuous design can be divided by writing fields. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}},{"id":"a047-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-15"],"title":"比較掃描順序造成的時間漂移","titleEn":"Compare temporal drift under different write orders","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Write order changes the spatial expression of drift.","instruction":"比較掃描順序造成的時間漂移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare temporal drift under different write orders. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Write order changes the spatial expression of drift.","observation":"序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Write order changes the spatial expression of drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較掃描順序造成的時間漂移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare temporal drift under different write orders\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Write order changes the spatial expression of drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。","textEn":"Write order changes the spatial expression of drift."},{"id":"a047-v8-16-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較掃描順序造成的時間漂移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare temporal drift under different write orders\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。","拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。"],"optionsEn":["Write order changes the spatial expression of drift.","Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"序列順序會改變漂移的空間分布。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"Write order changes the spatial expression of drift. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}},{"id":"a047-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-16"],"title":"量測第一層到第二層的套刻","titleEn":"Measure overlay from the first to the second layer","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：層間對位須獨立驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interlayer registration needs independent validation.","instruction":"量測第一層到第二層的套刻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「層間對位須獨立驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure overlay from the first to the second layer. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interlayer registration needs independent validation.","observation":"層間對位須獨立驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interlayer registration needs independent validation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測第一層到第二層的套刻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「層間對位須獨立驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure overlay from the first to the second layer\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interlayer registration needs independent validation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"層間對位須獨立驗證。","textEn":"Interlayer registration needs independent validation."},{"id":"a047-v8-17-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測第一層到第二層的套刻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure overlay from the first to the second layer\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","層間對位須獨立驗證。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。"],"optionsEn":["Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Interlayer registration needs independent validation.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"層間對位須獨立驗證。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"Interlayer registration needs independent validation. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}},{"id":"a047-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-17"],"title":"分開全域與局部座標殘差","titleEn":"Separate global and local coordinate residuals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Global correction cannot remove every local distortion.","instruction":"分開全域與局部座標殘差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate global and local coordinate residuals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Global correction cannot remove every local distortion.","observation":"全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Global correction cannot remove every local distortion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開全域與局部座標殘差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate global and local coordinate residuals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Global correction cannot remove every local distortion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。","textEn":"Global correction cannot remove every local distortion."},{"id":"a047-v8-18-k2","title":"對位與拼接的原理與限制","titleEn":"Alignment and stitching: principle and limits","text":"場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","textEn":"Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開全域與局部座標殘差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate global and local coordinate residuals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["拼接合格就表示層間套刻合格。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。"],"optionsEn":["Good stitching proves good interlayer overlay.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Global correction cannot remove every local distortion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"全域修正不能消除所有局部變形。 場內定位、跨場拼接與層間套刻是不同誤差。","explanationEn":"Global correction cannot remove every local distortion. Within-field placement, field stitching and interlayer overlay are distinct errors."}}]},{"id":"a047-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"顯影與驗證","titleEn":"Development and validation","description":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","descriptionEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions.","steps":[{"id":"a047-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-18"],"title":"對照顯影時間與保留尺寸","titleEn":"Relate development history to retained dimensions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image.","instruction":"對照顯影時間與保留尺寸。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate development history to retained dimensions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image.","observation":"顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對照顯影時間與保留尺寸」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate development history to retained dimensions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。","textEn":"Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image."},{"id":"a047-v8-19-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對照顯影時間與保留尺寸」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate development history to retained dimensions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顯影不是單純的圖像顯現。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"Development is not merely revealing an unchanged image. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}},{"id":"a047-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-19"],"title":"檢查細長圖形倒塌與殘留","titleEn":"Inspect collapse and residue in slender patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution.","instruction":"檢查細長圖形倒塌與殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect collapse and residue in slender patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution.","observation":"機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查細長圖形倒塌與殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect collapse and residue in slender patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。","textEn":"Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution."},{"id":"a047-v8-20-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查細長圖形倒塌與殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect collapse and residue in slender patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械穩定性也限制可用解析度。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"Mechanical stability also limits useful resolution. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}},{"id":"a047-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-20"],"title":"比較抬離用與蝕刻用截面","titleEn":"Compare lift-off and etch-mask profiles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One resist profile may not suit both applications.","instruction":"比較抬離用與蝕刻用截面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare lift-off and etch-mask profiles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: One resist profile may not suit both applications.","observation":"相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One resist profile may not suit both applications. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較抬離用與蝕刻用截面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare lift-off and etch-mask profiles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One resist profile may not suit both applications.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。","textEn":"One resist profile may not suit both applications."},{"id":"a047-v8-21-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較抬離用與蝕刻用截面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare lift-off and etch-mask profiles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。"],"optionsEn":["Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","One resist profile may not suit both applications."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同光阻輪廓未必適合兩種用途。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"One resist profile may not suit both applications. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}},{"id":"a047-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-21"],"title":"評估顯微量測本身的曝光效應","titleEn":"Assess exposure effects caused by electron microscopy","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：量測可能改變敏感材料。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Measurement can modify sensitive materials.","instruction":"評估顯微量測本身的曝光效應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「量測可能改變敏感材料。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess exposure effects caused by electron microscopy. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Measurement can modify sensitive materials.","observation":"量測可能改變敏感材料。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Measurement can modify sensitive materials. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估顯微量測本身的曝光效應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「量測可能改變敏感材料。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess exposure effects caused by electron microscopy\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Measurement can modify sensitive materials.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"量測可能改變敏感材料。","textEn":"Measurement can modify sensitive materials."},{"id":"a047-v8-22-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估顯微量測本身的曝光效應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess exposure effects caused by electron microscopy\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測可能改變敏感材料。","曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Measurement can modify sensitive materials.","Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測可能改變敏感材料。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"Measurement can modify sensitive materials. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}},{"id":"a047-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-22"],"title":"以獨立量測驗證最小尺寸","titleEn":"Verify minimum dimensions with independent measurement","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence.","instruction":"以獨立量測驗證最小尺寸。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Verify minimum dimensions with independent measurement. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence.","observation":"儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以獨立量測驗證最小尺寸」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Verify minimum dimensions with independent measurement\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。","textEn":"An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence."},{"id":"a047-v8-23-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以獨立量測驗證最小尺寸」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Verify minimum dimensions with independent measurement\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器解析度聲明不是樣品尺寸證據。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"An instrument-resolution claim is not sample-dimension evidence. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}},{"id":"a047-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-jeol","v8b-nisttools","v8b-maskmetro"],"prerequisiteIds":["a047-v8-23"],"title":"交付資料、劑量與套刻的實驗紀錄","titleEn":"Deliver data, dose and overlay records","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history.","instruction":"交付資料、劑量與套刻的實驗紀錄。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver data, dose and overlay records. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history.","observation":"重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「曝光後尺寸不會再改變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dimensions cannot change after exposure.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付資料、劑量與套刻的實驗紀錄」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver data, dose and overlay records\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a047-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。","textEn":"Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history."},{"id":"a047-v8-24-k2","title":"顯影與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Development and validation: principle and limits","text":"顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","textEn":"Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付資料、劑量與套刻的實驗紀錄」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver data, dose and overlay records\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝光後尺寸不會再改變。","束斑直徑就是最終可製作線寬。","重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。"],"optionsEn":["Dimensions cannot change after exposure.","Beam diameter equals the final manufacturable linewidth.","Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重現直寫需要完整設計與歷程。 顯影與圖案轉移可能改變原始曝光尺寸。","explanationEn":"Reproducing direct writing needs complete design and history. Development and transfer can alter exposure-defined dimensions."}}]}]},{"id":"a048","title":"套刻誤差量測與補償","titleEn":"Overlay metrology and compensation","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究向量與標記、誤差模型、量測品質、補償與驗證；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: vectors and marks, error models, measurement quality, correction and validation. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["向量與標記","誤差模型","量測品質","補償與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Vectors and marks","Error models","Measurement quality","Correction and validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a048-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"向量與標記","titleEn":"Vectors and marks","description":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","descriptionEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth.","steps":[{"id":"a048-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出上下兩層的相對位置向量","titleEn":"Draw relative-placement vectors between two layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions.","instruction":"畫出上下兩層的相對位置向量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw relative-placement vectors between two layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions.","observation":"套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出上下兩層的相對位置向量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw relative-placement vectors between two layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。","textEn":"Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions."},{"id":"a048-v8-01-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出上下兩層的相對位置向量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw relative-placement vectors between two layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。"],"optionsEn":["Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","One translation corrects every distortion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"套刻需要共同座標與方向定義。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"Overlay needs common coordinates and sign conventions. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}},{"id":"a048-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-01"],"title":"把接觸孔偏移映射成落點風險","titleEn":"Map contact-hole offset into landing risk","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：容忍度取決於上下層幾何。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry.","instruction":"把接觸孔偏移映射成落點風險。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「容忍度取決於上下層幾何。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map contact-hole offset into landing risk. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry.","observation":"容忍度取決於上下層幾何。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把接觸孔偏移映射成落點風險」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「容忍度取決於上下層幾何。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map contact-hole offset into landing risk\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"容忍度取決於上下層幾何。","textEn":"Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry."},{"id":"a048-v8-02-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把接觸孔偏移映射成落點風險」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map contact-hole offset into landing risk\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","容忍度取決於上下層幾何。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。"],"optionsEn":["Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry.","One translation corrects every distortion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"容忍度取決於上下層幾何。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"Tolerance depends on both layers' geometry. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}},{"id":"a048-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-02"],"title":"比較影像式與繞射式標記","titleEn":"Compare image-based and diffraction-based marks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Marks respond differently to process asymmetry.","instruction":"比較影像式與繞射式標記。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare image-based and diffraction-based marks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Marks respond differently to process asymmetry.","observation":"不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Marks respond differently to process asymmetry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較影像式與繞射式標記」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare image-based and diffraction-based marks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Marks respond differently to process asymmetry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。","textEn":"Marks respond differently to process asymmetry."},{"id":"a048-v8-03-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較影像式與繞射式標記」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare image-based and diffraction-based marks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。"],"optionsEn":["Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","One translation corrects every distortion.","Marks respond differently to process asymmetry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同標記對製程非對稱的反應不同。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"Marks respond differently to process asymmetry. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}},{"id":"a048-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-03"],"title":"標記量測圖形與產品圖形的距離","titleEn":"Mark distances between metrology and product features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：標記區不一定代表產品區。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Metrology marks may not represent device regions.","instruction":"標記量測圖形與產品圖形的距離。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「標記區不一定代表產品區。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark distances between metrology and product features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Metrology marks may not represent device regions.","observation":"標記區不一定代表產品區。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Metrology marks may not represent device regions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記量測圖形與產品圖形的距離」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「標記區不一定代表產品區。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark distances between metrology and product features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Metrology marks may not represent device regions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"標記區不一定代表產品區。","textEn":"Metrology marks may not represent device regions."},{"id":"a048-v8-04-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記量測圖形與產品圖形的距離」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark distances between metrology and product features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["標記區不一定代表產品區。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。"],"optionsEn":["Metrology marks may not represent device regions.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","One translation corrects every distortion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"標記區不一定代表產品區。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"Metrology marks may not represent device regions. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}},{"id":"a048-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-04"],"title":"分開晶圓級與場內套刻","titleEn":"Separate wafer-level and within-field overlay","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種尺度需要不同取樣。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The two scales need different sampling.","instruction":"分開晶圓級與場內套刻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「兩種尺度需要不同取樣。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate wafer-level and within-field overlay. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: The two scales need different sampling.","observation":"兩種尺度需要不同取樣。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The two scales need different sampling. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開晶圓級與場內套刻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種尺度需要不同取樣。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate wafer-level and within-field overlay\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The two scales need different sampling.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種尺度需要不同取樣。","textEn":"The two scales need different sampling."},{"id":"a048-v8-05-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開晶圓級與場內套刻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate wafer-level and within-field overlay\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","兩種尺度需要不同取樣。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。"],"optionsEn":["Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","The two scales need different sampling.","One translation corrects every distortion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩種尺度需要不同取樣。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"The two scales need different sampling. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}},{"id":"a048-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-05"],"title":"建立套刻與邊緣位置誤差的關係","titleEn":"Relate overlay to edge-placement error","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Edge error also includes dimensions and shape.","instruction":"建立套刻與邊緣位置誤差的關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate overlay to edge-placement error. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Edge error also includes dimensions and shape.","observation":"邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Edge error also includes dimensions and shape. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立套刻與邊緣位置誤差的關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate overlay to edge-placement error\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Edge error also includes dimensions and shape.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。","textEn":"Edge error also includes dimensions and shape."},{"id":"a048-v8-06-k2","title":"向量與標記的原理與限制","titleEn":"Vectors and marks: principle and limits","text":"套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","textEn":"Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立套刻與邊緣位置誤差的關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate overlay to edge-placement error\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","One translation corrects every distortion.","Edge error also includes dimensions and shape."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣誤差還包括尺寸與形狀。 套刻是兩層圖形相對位置，不等於單層線寬。","explanationEn":"Edge error also includes dimensions and shape. Overlay is relative placement between layers, not single-layer linewidth."}}]},{"id":"a048-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"誤差模型","titleEn":"Error models","description":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","descriptionEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models.","steps":[{"id":"a048-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-06"],"title":"由向量圖辨識平移分量","titleEn":"Identify translation from a vector map","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A consistent shift can indicate global translation.","instruction":"由向量圖辨識平移分量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify translation from a vector map. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A consistent shift can indicate global translation.","observation":"一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A consistent shift can indicate global translation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由向量圖辨識平移分量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify translation from a vector map\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A consistent shift can indicate global translation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。","textEn":"A consistent shift can indicate global translation."},{"id":"a048-v8-07-k2","title":"誤差模型的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error models: principle and limits","text":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","textEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由向量圖辨識平移分量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify translation from a vector map\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。"],"optionsEn":["A consistent shift can indicate global translation.","One translation corrects every distortion.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一致方向偏移可能來自全域位移。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"A consistent shift can indicate global translation. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}},{"id":"a048-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-07"],"title":"由切向殘差辨識旋轉","titleEn":"Identify rotation from tangential residuals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rotational displacement grows with distance.","instruction":"由切向殘差辨識旋轉。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify rotation from tangential residuals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rotational displacement grows with distance.","observation":"旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rotational displacement grows with distance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由切向殘差辨識旋轉」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify rotation from tangential residuals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rotational displacement grows with distance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。","textEn":"Rotational displacement grows with distance."},{"id":"a048-v8-08-k2","title":"誤差模型的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error models: principle and limits","text":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","textEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由切向殘差辨識旋轉」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify rotation from tangential residuals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。"],"optionsEn":["One translation corrects every distortion.","Rotational displacement grows with distance.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"旋轉誤差隨距離增加位移。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"Rotational displacement grows with distance. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}},{"id":"a048-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-08"],"title":"由放射殘差辨識縮放","titleEn":"Identify scale from radial residuals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：倍率誤差不是固定平移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Magnification error is not constant translation.","instruction":"由放射殘差辨識縮放。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「倍率誤差不是固定平移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：在簡化一維例中，x=-1 mm 的套刻位移為 +1 nm，x=+1 mm 為 +3 nm。擬合 Δx=t+s x，得到平移 t=2 nm、縮放 s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm。若 x=0 的保留點實測為 +4 nm，模型預測只有 +2 nm，殘差 +2 nm 提醒你兩個校準點不足以證明完整形變模型。","instructionEn":"Identify scale from radial residuals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Magnification error is not constant translation.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): In a one-dimensional example, overlay displacement is +1 nm at x=-1 mm and +3 nm at x=+1 mm. Fitting Δx=t+s x gives translation t=2 nm and scale s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm. If a held-out point at x=0 measures +4 nm, the model predicts only +2 nm and residual is +2 nm. Two calibration points do not establish a complete distortion model.","observation":"倍率誤差不是固定平移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n需有 2 nm、1 ppm 及保留點 +2 nm 殘差。","observationEn":"Magnification error is not constant translation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 2 nm, 1 ppm and the held-out +2 nm residual.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由放射殘差辨識縮放」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「倍率誤差不是固定平移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：需有 2 nm、1 ppm 及保留點 +2 nm 殘差。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify scale from radial residuals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Magnification error is not constant translation.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 2 nm, 1 ppm and the held-out +2 nm residual.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"倍率誤差不是固定平移。","textEn":"Magnification error is not constant translation."},{"id":"a048-v8-09-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"在簡化一維例中，x=-1 mm 的套刻位移為 +1 nm，x=+1 mm 為 +3 nm。擬合 Δx=t+s x，得到平移 t=2 nm、縮放 s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm。若 x=0 的保留點實測為 +4 nm，模型預測只有 +2 nm，殘差 +2 nm 提醒你兩個校準點不足以證明完整形變模型。","textEn":"In a one-dimensional example, overlay displacement is +1 nm at x=-1 mm and +3 nm at x=+1 mm. Fitting Δx=t+s x gives translation t=2 nm and scale s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm. If a held-out point at x=0 measures +4 nm, the model predicts only +2 nm and residual is +2 nm. Two calibration points do not establish a complete distortion model."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由放射殘差辨識縮放」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify scale from radial residuals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","倍率誤差不是固定平移。"],"optionsEn":["One translation corrects every distortion.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Magnification error is not constant translation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"倍率誤差不是固定平移。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"Magnification error is not constant translation. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"在簡化一維例中，x=-1 mm 的套刻位移為 +1 nm，x=+1 mm 為 +3 nm。擬合 Δx=t+s x，得到平移 t=2 nm、縮放 s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm。若 x=0 的保留點實測為 +4 nm，模型預測只有 +2 nm，殘差 +2 nm 提醒你兩個校準點不足以證明完整形變模型。","textEn":"In a one-dimensional example, overlay displacement is +1 nm at x=-1 mm and +3 nm at x=+1 mm. Fitting Δx=t+s x gives translation t=2 nm and scale s=1 nm/mm=1 ppm. If a held-out point at x=0 measures +4 nm, the model predicts only +2 nm and residual is +2 nm. Two calibration points do not establish a complete distortion model.","check":"需有 2 nm、1 ppm 及保留點 +2 nm 殘差。","checkEn":"Report 2 nm, 1 ppm and the held-out +2 nm residual."}},{"id":"a048-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-09"],"title":"比較 X 與 Y 不同縮放","titleEn":"Compare anisotropic X and Y scaling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：非等向變形需要分方向係數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients.","instruction":"比較 X 與 Y 不同縮放。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「非等向變形需要分方向係數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare anisotropic X and Y scaling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients.","observation":"非等向變形需要分方向係數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 X 與 Y 不同縮放」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「非等向變形需要分方向係數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare anisotropic X and Y scaling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"非等向變形需要分方向係數。","textEn":"Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients."},{"id":"a048-v8-10-k2","title":"誤差模型的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error models: principle and limits","text":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","textEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 X 與 Y 不同縮放」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare anisotropic X and Y scaling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["非等向變形需要分方向係數。","只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients.","One translation corrects every distortion.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"非等向變形需要分方向係數。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"Anisotropic distortion needs separate directional coefficients. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}},{"id":"a048-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-10"],"title":"檢查高階模型是否過度擬合","titleEn":"Check higher-order models for overfitting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：增加係數也會增加資料需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: More coefficients require more data.","instruction":"檢查高階模型是否過度擬合。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「增加係數也會增加資料需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check higher-order models for overfitting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: More coefficients require more data.","observation":"增加係數也會增加資料需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"More coefficients require more data. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查高階模型是否過度擬合」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「增加係數也會增加資料需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check higher-order models for overfitting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"More coefficients require more data.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"增加係數也會增加資料需求。","textEn":"More coefficients require more data."},{"id":"a048-v8-11-k2","title":"誤差模型的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error models: principle and limits","text":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","textEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查高階模型是否過度擬合」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check higher-order models for overfitting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","增加係數也會增加資料需求。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。"],"optionsEn":["One translation corrects every distortion.","More coefficients require more data.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加係數也會增加資料需求。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"More coefficients require more data. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}},{"id":"a048-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-11"],"title":"保留未參與擬合的量測位置","titleEn":"Reserve measurement sites from fitting","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：保留點可測試模型外推。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Held-out sites test model generalization.","instruction":"保留未參與擬合的量測位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「保留點可測試模型外推。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Reserve measurement sites from fitting. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Held-out sites test model generalization.","observation":"保留點可測試模型外推。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Held-out sites test model generalization. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One translation corrects every distortion.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「保留未參與擬合的量測位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「保留點可測試模型外推。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Reserve measurement sites from fitting\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Held-out sites test model generalization.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"保留點可測試模型外推。","textEn":"Held-out sites test model generalization."},{"id":"a048-v8-12-k2","title":"誤差模型的原理與限制","titleEn":"Error models: principle and limits","text":"平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","textEn":"Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「保留未參與擬合的量測位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Reserve measurement sites from fitting\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只加一個平移量即可修正所有形變。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","保留點可測試模型外推。"],"optionsEn":["One translation corrects every distortion.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Held-out sites test model generalization."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保留點可測試模型外推。 平移、旋轉、縮放與高階形變需用適當模型區分。","explanationEn":"Held-out sites test model generalization. Translation, rotation, scale and higher-order deformation need suitable models."}}]},{"id":"a048-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"量測品質","titleEn":"Measurement quality","description":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","descriptionEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations.","steps":[{"id":"a048-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-12"],"title":"以重複量測估計再現性","titleEn":"Estimate repeatability from repeated measurement","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：重複性不代表對真值的準確度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth.","instruction":"以重複量測估計再現性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「重複性不代表對真值的準確度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate repeatability from repeated measurement. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth.","observation":"重複性不代表對真值的準確度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以重複量測估計再現性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「重複性不代表對真值的準確度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate repeatability from repeated measurement\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"重複性不代表對真值的準確度。","textEn":"Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth."},{"id":"a048-v8-13-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以重複量測估計再現性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate repeatability from repeated measurement\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["重複性不代表對真值的準確度。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。"],"optionsEn":["Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Zero calibration residual means no risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複性不代表對真值的準確度。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"Repeatability is not accuracy relative to truth. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}},{"id":"a048-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-13"],"title":"比較晶圓旋轉前後的工具偏差","titleEn":"Compare tool bias before and after wafer rotation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects.","instruction":"比較晶圓旋轉前後的工具偏差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare tool bias before and after wafer rotation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects.","observation":"旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較晶圓旋轉前後的工具偏差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare tool bias before and after wafer rotation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。","textEn":"Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects."},{"id":"a048-v8-14-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較晶圓旋轉前後的工具偏差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare tool bias before and after wafer rotation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。"],"optionsEn":["Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects.","Zero calibration residual means no risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"旋轉量測可協助分離工具與樣品效應。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"Rotated measurements help separate tool and sample effects. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}},{"id":"a048-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-14"],"title":"檢查標記被薄膜覆蓋後的訊號","titleEn":"Inspect mark signals after film coverage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：對比變化可能造成量測偏差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contrast changes can cause metrology bias.","instruction":"檢查標記被薄膜覆蓋後的訊號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「對比變化可能造成量測偏差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect mark signals after film coverage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contrast changes can cause metrology bias.","observation":"對比變化可能造成量測偏差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contrast changes can cause metrology bias. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查標記被薄膜覆蓋後的訊號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「對比變化可能造成量測偏差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect mark signals after film coverage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contrast changes can cause metrology bias.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"對比變化可能造成量測偏差。","textEn":"Contrast changes can cause metrology bias."},{"id":"a048-v8-15-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查標記被薄膜覆蓋後的訊號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect mark signals after film coverage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","對比變化可能造成量測偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Contrast changes can cause metrology bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對比變化可能造成量測偏差。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"Contrast changes can cause metrology bias. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}},{"id":"a048-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-15"],"title":"分析非對稱蝕刻造成的標記位移","titleEn":"Analyze apparent mark shift from asymmetric etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：量測中心不一定等於設計中心。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The measured center need not equal the design center.","instruction":"分析非對稱蝕刻造成的標記位移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「量測中心不一定等於設計中心。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Analyze apparent mark shift from asymmetric etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The measured center need not equal the design center.","observation":"量測中心不一定等於設計中心。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The measured center need not equal the design center. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分析非對稱蝕刻造成的標記位移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「量測中心不一定等於設計中心。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Analyze apparent mark shift from asymmetric etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The measured center need not equal the design center.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"量測中心不一定等於設計中心。","textEn":"The measured center need not equal the design center."},{"id":"a048-v8-16-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分析非對稱蝕刻造成的標記位移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Analyze apparent mark shift from asymmetric etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測中心不一定等於設計中心。","量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。"],"optionsEn":["The measured center need not equal the design center.","Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Zero calibration residual means no risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測中心不一定等於設計中心。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"The measured center need not equal the design center. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}},{"id":"a048-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-16"],"title":"比較不同工具的交叉匹配","titleEn":"Compare cross-matching between metrology tools","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：工具間偏差會污染製程比較。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons.","instruction":"比較不同工具的交叉匹配。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「工具間偏差會污染製程比較。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare cross-matching between metrology tools. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons.","observation":"工具間偏差會污染製程比較。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同工具的交叉匹配」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「工具間偏差會污染製程比較。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare cross-matching between metrology tools\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"工具間偏差會污染製程比較。","textEn":"Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons."},{"id":"a048-v8-17-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同工具的交叉匹配」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare cross-matching between metrology tools\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","工具間偏差會污染製程比較。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。"],"optionsEn":["Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons.","Zero calibration residual means no risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"工具間偏差會污染製程比較。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"Inter-tool bias can contaminate process comparisons. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}},{"id":"a048-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-17"],"title":"用不確定度區間評估邊界結果","titleEn":"Assess borderline results using uncertainty intervals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty.","instruction":"用不確定度區間評估邊界結果。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess borderline results using uncertainty intervals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty.","observation":"接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「量測工具不會產生系統偏差。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用不確定度區間評估邊界結果」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess borderline results using uncertainty intervals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。","textEn":"Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty."},{"id":"a048-v8-18-k2","title":"量測品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Measurement quality: principle and limits","text":"標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","textEn":"Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用不確定度區間評估邊界結果」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess borderline results using uncertainty intervals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測工具不會產生系統偏差。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。"],"optionsEn":["Metrology tools cannot introduce systematic bias.","Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接近限值的結果不能忽略量測不確定度。 標記偏差、工具偏差與真實套刻會混合在觀測值中。","explanationEn":"Near-limit results require measurement uncertainty. Mark bias, tool bias and true overlay combine in observations."}}]},{"id":"a048-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"補償與驗證","titleEn":"Correction and validation","description":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","descriptionEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals.","steps":[{"id":"a048-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-18"],"title":"把可修正係數轉成曝光補償","titleEn":"Translate correctable coefficients into exposure compensation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls.","instruction":"把可修正係數轉成曝光補償。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Translate correctable coefficients into exposure compensation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls.","observation":"補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把可修正係數轉成曝光補償」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Translate correctable coefficients into exposure compensation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。","textEn":"Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls."},{"id":"a048-v8-19-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把可修正係數轉成曝光補償」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Translate correctable coefficients into exposure compensation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls.","Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補償自由度受曝光機控制能力限制。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"Correction freedom is limited by scanner controls. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}},{"id":"a048-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-19"],"title":"區分批次前饋與批次後回饋","titleEn":"Distinguish lot feedforward from post-lot feedback","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者使用不同時間點資訊。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They use information available at different times.","instruction":"區分批次前饋與批次後回饋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「兩者使用不同時間點資訊。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish lot feedforward from post-lot feedback. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: They use information available at different times.","observation":"兩者使用不同時間點資訊。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They use information available at different times. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分批次前饋與批次後回饋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者使用不同時間點資訊。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish lot feedforward from post-lot feedback\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They use information available at different times.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者使用不同時間點資訊。","textEn":"They use information available at different times."},{"id":"a048-v8-20-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分批次前饋與批次後回饋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish lot feedforward from post-lot feedback\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","兩者使用不同時間點資訊。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Zero calibration residual means no risk.","They use information available at different times.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩者使用不同時間點資訊。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"They use information available at different times. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}},{"id":"a048-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-20"],"title":"比較補償前後的保留點殘差","titleEn":"Compare held-out residuals before and after correction","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：真正改善應出現在獨立資料。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Real improvement should appear in independent data.","instruction":"比較補償前後的保留點殘差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「真正改善應出現在獨立資料。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare held-out residuals before and after correction. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Real improvement should appear in independent data.","observation":"真正改善應出現在獨立資料。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Real improvement should appear in independent data. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較補償前後的保留點殘差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「真正改善應出現在獨立資料。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare held-out residuals before and after correction\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Real improvement should appear in independent data.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"真正改善應出現在獨立資料。","textEn":"Real improvement should appear in independent data."},{"id":"a048-v8-21-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較補償前後的保留點殘差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare held-out residuals before and after correction\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","真正改善應出現在獨立資料。"],"optionsEn":["Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","Real improvement should appear in independent data."],"answer":2,"explanation":"真正改善應出現在獨立資料。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"Real improvement should appear in independent data. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}},{"id":"a048-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-21"],"title":"檢查局部最大誤差而非只看均值","titleEn":"Check local maximum error rather than only the mean","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion.","instruction":"檢查局部最大誤差而非只看均值。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check local maximum error rather than only the mean. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion.","observation":"均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查局部最大誤差而非只看均值」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check local maximum error rather than only the mean\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。","textEn":"A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion."},{"id":"a048-v8-22-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查局部最大誤差而非只看均值」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check local maximum error rather than only the mean\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。","校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion.","Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均值接近零仍可能有大幅散布。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"A near-zero mean can coexist with wide dispersion. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}},{"id":"a048-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-22"],"title":"將套刻結果連結到電性載具","titleEn":"Link overlay results to electrical test structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance.","instruction":"將套刻結果連結到電性載具。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Link overlay results to electrical test structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance.","observation":"幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將套刻結果連結到電性載具」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Link overlay results to electrical test structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。","textEn":"Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance."},{"id":"a048-v8-23-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將套刻結果連結到電性載具」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Link overlay results to electrical test structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。"],"optionsEn":["Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何誤差需對應功能容忍度。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"Geometric error must relate to functional tolerance. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}},{"id":"a048-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-maskmetro","v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a048-v8-23"],"title":"交付模型係數與不確定度報告","titleEn":"Deliver model coefficients and uncertainty","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations.","instruction":"交付模型係數與不確定度報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver model coefficients and uncertainty. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations.","observation":"可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero calibration residual means no risk.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付模型係數與不確定度報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver model coefficients and uncertainty\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a048-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。","textEn":"Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations."},{"id":"a048-v8-24-k2","title":"補償與驗證的原理與限制","titleEn":"Correction and validation: principle and limits","text":"補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","textEn":"Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付模型係數與不確定度報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver model coefficients and uncertainty\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["校準資料殘差為零就表示沒有風險。","線寬合格就能證明套刻合格。","可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。"],"optionsEn":["Zero calibration residual means no risk.","Passing linewidth proves acceptable overlay.","Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可追溯補償需要資料、模型及限制。 補償必須用保留位置或下一批次驗證，不能只看擬合殘差。","explanationEn":"Traceable correction needs data, model and limitations. Correction needs held-out sites or a subsequent lot, not only fit residuals."}}]}]},{"id":"a049","title":"曝光焦距與劑量控制","titleEn":"Exposure focus and dose control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究焦點劑量定義、窗口量測、感測與補償、變異與接受；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: focus and dose, window measurement, sensing and correction, variation and acceptance. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["焦點劑量定義","窗口量測","感測與補償","變異與接受"],"labelsEn":["Focus and dose","Window measurement","Sensing and correction","Variation and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a049-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"焦點劑量定義","titleEn":"Focus and dose","description":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","descriptionEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours.","steps":[{"id":"a049-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義名目焦點與離焦符號","titleEn":"Define nominal focus and defocus signs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：焦點需有一致的參考面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Focus needs a consistent reference plane.","instruction":"定義名目焦點與離焦符號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「焦點需有一致的參考面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define nominal focus and defocus signs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Focus needs a consistent reference plane.","observation":"焦點需有一致的參考面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Focus needs a consistent reference plane. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義名目焦點與離焦符號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「焦點需有一致的參考面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define nominal focus and defocus signs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Focus needs a consistent reference plane.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"焦點需有一致的參考面。","textEn":"Focus needs a consistent reference plane."},{"id":"a049-v8-01-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義名目焦點與離焦符號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define nominal focus and defocus signs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["焦點需有一致的參考面。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。"],"optionsEn":["Focus needs a consistent reference plane.","Focus and dose are the same control variable.","One pattern represents every layout."],"answer":0,"explanation":"焦點需有一致的參考面。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Focus needs a consistent reference plane. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}},{"id":"a049-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-01"],"title":"分開入射劑量與吸收劑量","titleEn":"Separate incident and absorbed dose","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料吸收會改變有效能量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material absorption changes effective energy.","instruction":"分開入射劑量與吸收劑量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「材料吸收會改變有效能量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate incident and absorbed dose. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material absorption changes effective energy.","observation":"材料吸收會改變有效能量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material absorption changes effective energy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開入射劑量與吸收劑量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料吸收會改變有效能量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate incident and absorbed dose\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material absorption changes effective energy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料吸收會改變有效能量。","textEn":"Material absorption changes effective energy."},{"id":"a049-v8-02-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開入射劑量與吸收劑量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate incident and absorbed dose\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","材料吸收會改變有效能量。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。"],"optionsEn":["Focus and dose are the same control variable.","Material absorption changes effective energy.","One pattern represents every layout."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料吸收會改變有效能量。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Material absorption changes effective energy. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}},{"id":"a049-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-02"],"title":"畫出劑量變化的光阻閾值輪廓","titleEn":"Sketch resist-threshold contours under dose change","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone.","instruction":"畫出劑量變化的光阻閾值輪廓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch resist-threshold contours under dose change. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone.","observation":"劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出劑量變化的光阻閾值輪廓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch resist-threshold contours under dose change\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。","textEn":"Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone."},{"id":"a049-v8-03-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出劑量變化的光阻閾值輪廓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch resist-threshold contours under dose change\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。"],"optionsEn":["Focus and dose are the same control variable.","One pattern represents every layout.","Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"劑量改變可能使線寬增或減，取決於極性。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Dose can increase or decrease width depending on tone. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}},{"id":"a049-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-03"],"title":"比較密集線與接觸孔的焦點反應","titleEn":"Compare focus response of dense lines and contacts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同圖形有不同敏感度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Patterns have different sensitivities.","instruction":"比較密集線與接觸孔的焦點反應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同圖形有不同敏感度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare focus response of dense lines and contacts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Patterns have different sensitivities.","observation":"不同圖形有不同敏感度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Patterns have different sensitivities. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較密集線與接觸孔的焦點反應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同圖形有不同敏感度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare focus response of dense lines and contacts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Patterns have different sensitivities.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同圖形有不同敏感度。","textEn":"Patterns have different sensitivities."},{"id":"a049-v8-04-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較密集線與接觸孔的焦點反應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare focus response of dense lines and contacts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同圖形有不同敏感度。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。"],"optionsEn":["Patterns have different sensitivities.","Focus and dose are the same control variable.","One pattern represents every layout."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同圖形有不同敏感度。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Patterns have different sensitivities. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}},{"id":"a049-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-04"],"title":"把晶圓表面高度轉成焦點預算","titleEn":"Translate surface height into focus budget","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部地形會消耗可用焦深。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local topography consumes available depth of focus.","instruction":"把晶圓表面高度轉成焦點預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部地形會消耗可用焦深。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Translate surface height into focus budget. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local topography consumes available depth of focus.","observation":"局部地形會消耗可用焦深。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local topography consumes available depth of focus. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把晶圓表面高度轉成焦點預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部地形會消耗可用焦深。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Translate surface height into focus budget\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local topography consumes available depth of focus.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部地形會消耗可用焦深。","textEn":"Local topography consumes available depth of focus."},{"id":"a049-v8-05-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把晶圓表面高度轉成焦點預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Translate surface height into focus budget\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","局部地形會消耗可用焦深。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。"],"optionsEn":["Focus and dose are the same control variable.","Local topography consumes available depth of focus.","One pattern represents every layout."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部地形會消耗可用焦深。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Local topography consumes available depth of focus. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}},{"id":"a049-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-05"],"title":"列出材料、曝光與顯影的混淆變因","titleEn":"List material, exposure and development confounders","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose.","instruction":"列出材料、曝光與顯影的混淆變因。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List material, exposure and development confounders. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose.","observation":"線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Focus and dose are the same control variable.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出材料、曝光與顯影的混淆變因」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List material, exposure and development confounders\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。","textEn":"Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose."},{"id":"a049-v8-06-k2","title":"焦點劑量定義的原理與限制","titleEn":"Focus and dose: principle and limits","text":"焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","textEn":"Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出材料、曝光與顯影的混淆變因」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List material, exposure and development confounders\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。"],"optionsEn":["Focus and dose are the same control variable.","One pattern represents every layout.","Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線寬漂移不一定只由劑量造成。 焦距與劑量影響不同但會共同改變顯影輪廓。","explanationEn":"Linewidth drift need not be caused only by dose. Focus and dose have distinct effects that jointly change developed contours."}}]},{"id":"a049-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"窗口量測","titleEn":"Window measurement","description":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","descriptionEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints.","steps":[{"id":"a049-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-06"],"title":"規畫二維焦距劑量矩陣","titleEn":"Plan a two-dimensional focus–dose matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Joint sweeps reveal interactions.","instruction":"規畫二維焦距劑量矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan a two-dimensional focus–dose matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Joint sweeps reveal interactions.","observation":"兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Joint sweeps reveal interactions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫二維焦距劑量矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan a two-dimensional focus–dose matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Joint sweeps reveal interactions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。","textEn":"Joint sweeps reveal interactions."},{"id":"a049-v8-07-k2","title":"窗口量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window measurement: principle and limits","text":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","textEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫二維焦距劑量矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan a two-dimensional focus–dose matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。"],"optionsEn":["Joint sweeps reveal interactions.","One pattern represents every layout.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩變量聯合掃描能揭露交互作用。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"Joint sweeps reveal interactions. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}},{"id":"a049-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-07"],"title":"用 Bossung 曲線比較線寬隨焦距","titleEn":"Compare linewidth through focus with Bossung curves","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity.","instruction":"用 Bossung 曲線比較線寬隨焦距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare linewidth through focus with Bossung curves. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity.","observation":"曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用 Bossung 曲線比較線寬隨焦距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare linewidth through focus with Bossung curves\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。","textEn":"Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity."},{"id":"a049-v8-08-k2","title":"窗口量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window measurement: principle and limits","text":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","textEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用 Bossung 曲線比較線寬隨焦距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare linewidth through focus with Bossung curves\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。"],"optionsEn":["One pattern represents every layout.","Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"曲線形狀提供焦點與敏感度資訊。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"Curve shape informs focus and sensitivity. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}},{"id":"a049-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-08"],"title":"為線寬與缺陷分別畫合格區","titleEn":"Draw separate acceptance regions for width and defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects.","instruction":"為線寬與缺陷分別畫合格區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw separate acceptance regions for width and defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects.","observation":"尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為線寬與缺陷分別畫合格區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw separate acceptance regions for width and defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。","textEn":"Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects."},{"id":"a049-v8-09-k2","title":"窗口量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window measurement: principle and limits","text":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","textEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為線寬與缺陷分別畫合格區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw separate acceptance regions for width and defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。"],"optionsEn":["One pattern represents every layout.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺寸合格不代表缺陷合格。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"Passing dimensions does not imply passing defects. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}},{"id":"a049-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-09"],"title":"求多種圖形窗口的交集","titleEn":"Intersect process windows for several patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The common window can be narrower than an individual one.","instruction":"求多種圖形窗口的交集。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設線條 A 的合格焦距範圍為 [-40,40] nm、正規化劑量 [0.90,1.10]；接觸孔 B 為 [-20,30] nm、劑量 [0.95,1.05]，並先忽略交互作用。共同窗口為 [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05]，幾何中心是焦距 +5 nm、劑量 1.00。點 (+35 nm,1.00) 對 A 合格卻對共同窗口不合格。","instructionEn":"Intersect process windows for several patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The common window can be narrower than an individual one.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume line A passes at focus [-40,40] nm and normalized dose [0.90,1.10]; contact B passes at [-20,30] nm and [0.95,1.05], initially ignoring interactions. Their common window is [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05], with geometric center (+5 nm,1.00). The point (+35 nm,1.00) passes A but fails the common window.","observation":"共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付交集與 +5 nm/1.00 中心，並說明矩形與忽略交互作用假設。","observationEn":"The common window can be narrower than an individual one. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport the intersection and +5 nm/1.00 center, stating rectangular-window and no-interaction assumptions.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「求多種圖形窗口的交集」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付交集與 +5 nm/1.00 中心，並說明矩形與忽略交互作用假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Intersect process windows for several patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The common window can be narrower than an individual one.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report the intersection and +5 nm/1.00 center, stating rectangular-window and no-interaction assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。","textEn":"The common window can be narrower than an individual one."},{"id":"a049-v8-10-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設線條 A 的合格焦距範圍為 [-40,40] nm、正規化劑量 [0.90,1.10]；接觸孔 B 為 [-20,30] nm、劑量 [0.95,1.05]，並先忽略交互作用。共同窗口為 [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05]，幾何中心是焦距 +5 nm、劑量 1.00。點 (+35 nm,1.00) 對 A 合格卻對共同窗口不合格。","textEn":"Assume line A passes at focus [-40,40] nm and normalized dose [0.90,1.10]; contact B passes at [-20,30] nm and [0.95,1.05], initially ignoring interactions. Their common window is [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05], with geometric center (+5 nm,1.00). The point (+35 nm,1.00) passes A but fails the common window."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「求多種圖形窗口的交集」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Intersect process windows for several patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。","只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。"],"optionsEn":["The common window can be narrower than an individual one.","One pattern represents every layout.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共同窗口可能比單圖形窗口更窄。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"The common window can be narrower than an individual one. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設線條 A 的合格焦距範圍為 [-40,40] nm、正規化劑量 [0.90,1.10]；接觸孔 B 為 [-20,30] nm、劑量 [0.95,1.05]，並先忽略交互作用。共同窗口為 [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05]，幾何中心是焦距 +5 nm、劑量 1.00。點 (+35 nm,1.00) 對 A 合格卻對共同窗口不合格。","textEn":"Assume line A passes at focus [-40,40] nm and normalized dose [0.90,1.10]; contact B passes at [-20,30] nm and [0.95,1.05], initially ignoring interactions. Their common window is [-20,30]×[0.95,1.05], with geometric center (+5 nm,1.00). The point (+35 nm,1.00) passes A but fails the common window.","check":"交付交集與 +5 nm/1.00 中心，並說明矩形與忽略交互作用假設。","checkEn":"Report the intersection and +5 nm/1.00 center, stating rectangular-window and no-interaction assumptions."}},{"id":"a049-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-10"],"title":"比較插值與外推的可信範圍","titleEn":"Compare confidence in interpolation and extrapolation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable.","instruction":"比較插值與外推的可信範圍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare confidence in interpolation and extrapolation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable.","observation":"未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較插值與外推的可信範圍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare confidence in interpolation and extrapolation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。","textEn":"Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable."},{"id":"a049-v8-11-k2","title":"窗口量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window measurement: principle and limits","text":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","textEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較插值與外推的可信範圍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare confidence in interpolation and extrapolation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。"],"optionsEn":["One pattern represents every layout.","Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未量測邊界外不應直接宣告合格。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"Untested regions beyond the measured boundary should not be declared acceptable. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}},{"id":"a049-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-11"],"title":"檢查矩陣掃描期間的漂移","titleEn":"Check drift during the matrix sweep","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects.","instruction":"檢查矩陣掃描期間的漂移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check drift during the matrix sweep. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects.","observation":"時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One pattern represents every layout.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查矩陣掃描期間的漂移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check drift during the matrix sweep\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。","textEn":"Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects."},{"id":"a049-v8-12-k2","title":"窗口量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Window measurement: principle and limits","text":"製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","textEn":"A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查矩陣掃描期間的漂移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check drift during the matrix sweep\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只用一種圖形即可代表所有版圖。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。"],"optionsEn":["One pattern represents every layout.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間漂移可假裝成焦距或劑量效應。 製程窗口是多個圖形與限制的交集。","explanationEn":"Temporal drift can mimic focus or dose effects. A process window is the intersection of multiple patterns and constraints."}}]},{"id":"a049-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"感測與補償","titleEn":"Sensing and correction","description":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","descriptionEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging.","steps":[{"id":"a049-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-12"],"title":"畫出表面高度到鏡頭焦點的前饋鏈","titleEn":"Sketch height-to-focus feedforward","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Latency and spatial registration affect compensation.","instruction":"畫出表面高度到鏡頭焦點的前饋鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch height-to-focus feedforward. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Latency and spatial registration affect compensation.","observation":"量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Latency and spatial registration affect compensation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出表面高度到鏡頭焦點的前饋鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch height-to-focus feedforward\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Latency and spatial registration affect compensation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。","textEn":"Latency and spatial registration affect compensation."},{"id":"a049-v8-13-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出表面高度到鏡頭焦點的前饋鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch height-to-focus feedforward\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。"],"optionsEn":["Latency and spatial registration affect compensation.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測延遲與空間對應會影響補償。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Latency and spatial registration affect compensation. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}},{"id":"a049-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-13"],"title":"比較晶圓翹曲與局部台階","titleEn":"Compare wafer bow with local steps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different spatial scales require different correction capability.","instruction":"比較晶圓翹曲與局部台階。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare wafer bow with local steps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different spatial scales require different correction capability.","observation":"不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different spatial scales require different correction capability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較晶圓翹曲與局部台階」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare wafer bow with local steps\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different spatial scales require different correction capability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。","textEn":"Different spatial scales require different correction capability."},{"id":"a049-v8-14-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較晶圓翹曲與局部台階」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare wafer bow with local steps\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。"],"optionsEn":["A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","Different spatial scales require different correction capability.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同空間尺度需要不同補償能力。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Different spatial scales require different correction capability. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}},{"id":"a049-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-14"],"title":"檢查光源漂移到劑量控制的回路","titleEn":"Trace source drift through the dose-control loop","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift.","instruction":"檢查光源漂移到劑量控制的回路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace source drift through the dose-control loop. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift.","observation":"回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查光源漂移到劑量控制的回路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace source drift through the dose-control loop\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。","textEn":"Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift."},{"id":"a049-v8-15-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查光源漂移到劑量控制的回路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace source drift through the dose-control loop\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。"],"optionsEn":["A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回路頻寬限制可抑制的漂移。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Loop bandwidth limits suppressible drift. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}},{"id":"a049-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-15"],"title":"用監控片分離工具與材料批次差異","titleEn":"Use monitor wafers to separate tool and material variation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：對照材料可減少歸因混淆。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity.","instruction":"用監控片分離工具與材料批次差異。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「對照材料可減少歸因混淆。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use monitor wafers to separate tool and material variation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity.","observation":"對照材料可減少歸因混淆。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用監控片分離工具與材料批次差異」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「對照材料可減少歸因混淆。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use monitor wafers to separate tool and material variation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"對照材料可減少歸因混淆。","textEn":"Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity."},{"id":"a049-v8-16-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用監控片分離工具與材料批次差異」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use monitor wafers to separate tool and material variation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["對照材料可減少歸因混淆。","高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。"],"optionsEn":["Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity.","A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對照材料可減少歸因混淆。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Reference materials reduce attribution ambiguity. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}},{"id":"a049-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-16"],"title":"比較曝光前量測與曝光後量測","titleEn":"Compare pre- and post-exposure metrology","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：前饋與結果驗證互相補充。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other.","instruction":"比較曝光前量測與曝光後量測。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「前饋與結果驗證互相補充。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare pre- and post-exposure metrology. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other.","observation":"前饋與結果驗證互相補充。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較曝光前量測與曝光後量測」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「前饋與結果驗證互相補充。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare pre- and post-exposure metrology\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"前饋與結果驗證互相補充。","textEn":"Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other."},{"id":"a049-v8-17-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較曝光前量測與曝光後量測」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare pre- and post-exposure metrology\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","前饋與結果驗證互相補充。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。"],"optionsEn":["A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control."],"answer":1,"explanation":"前饋與結果驗證互相補充。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Feedforward and outcome verification complement each other. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}},{"id":"a049-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-17"],"title":"建立異常感測訊號的複查程序","titleEn":"Plan review for anomalous sensor signals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes.","instruction":"建立異常感測訊號的複查程序。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan review for anomalous sensor signals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes.","observation":"感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立異常感測訊號的複查程序」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan review for anomalous sensor signals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。","textEn":"Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes."},{"id":"a049-v8-18-k2","title":"感測與補償的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sensing and correction: principle and limits","text":"焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","textEn":"Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立異常感測訊號的複查程序」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan review for anomalous sensor signals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高度感測器讀值就等於光阻最佳焦點。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。"],"optionsEn":["A height-sensor reading equals the resist best focus.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"感測故障不能直接當成製程變化。 焦點控制需要表面高度、工具狀態與實際成像的鏈結。","explanationEn":"Sensor faults must not be mistaken for process changes. Focus control needs links among surface height, tool state and imaging."}}]},{"id":"a049-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"變異與接受","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance","description":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","descriptionEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability.","steps":[{"id":"a049-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-18"],"title":"把焦距劑量散布疊在窗口上","titleEn":"Overlay focus–dose variation on the window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails.","instruction":"把焦距劑量散布疊在窗口上。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Overlay focus–dose variation on the window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails.","observation":"名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把焦距劑量散布疊在窗口上」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Overlay focus–dose variation on the window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。","textEn":"A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails."},{"id":"a049-v8-19-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把焦距劑量散布疊在窗口上」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Overlay focus–dose variation on the window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。"],"optionsEn":["A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Focus and dose are the same control variable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"名目點位於窗口內仍可能有尾端超限。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"A nominal point inside the window can still have out-of-limit tails. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}},{"id":"a049-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-19"],"title":"比較最大裕量與最佳尺寸兩種設定","titleEn":"Compare maximum-margin and best-dimension settings","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最佳單點不一定最穩健。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The best nominal point need not be the most robust.","instruction":"比較最大裕量與最佳尺寸兩種設定。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「最佳單點不一定最穩健。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare maximum-margin and best-dimension settings. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The best nominal point need not be the most robust.","observation":"最佳單點不一定最穩健。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The best nominal point need not be the most robust. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較最大裕量與最佳尺寸兩種設定」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最佳單點不一定最穩健。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare maximum-margin and best-dimension settings\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The best nominal point need not be the most robust.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最佳單點不一定最穩健。","textEn":"The best nominal point need not be the most robust."},{"id":"a049-v8-20-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較最大裕量與最佳尺寸兩種設定」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare maximum-margin and best-dimension settings\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","最佳單點不一定最穩健。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","The best nominal point need not be the most robust.","Focus and dose are the same control variable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最佳單點不一定最穩健。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"The best nominal point need not be the most robust. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}},{"id":"a049-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-20"],"title":"檢查晶圓邊緣與中心的不同窗口","titleEn":"Compare edge and center windows","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：空間差異可能限制全片合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance.","instruction":"檢查晶圓邊緣與中心的不同窗口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「空間差異可能限制全片合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare edge and center windows. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance.","observation":"空間差異可能限制全片合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查晶圓邊緣與中心的不同窗口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「空間差異可能限制全片合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare edge and center windows\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"空間差異可能限制全片合格。","textEn":"Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance."},{"id":"a049-v8-21-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查晶圓邊緣與中心的不同窗口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare edge and center windows\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","空間差異可能限制全片合格。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Focus and dose are the same control variable.","Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"空間差異可能限制全片合格。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"Spatial differences can limit whole-wafer acceptance. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}},{"id":"a049-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-21"],"title":"追蹤跨批次的焦點與劑量趨勢","titleEn":"Trend focus and dose across lots","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：慢漂移需要長時間監控。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Slow drift needs long-term monitoring.","instruction":"追蹤跨批次的焦點與劑量趨勢。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「慢漂移需要長時間監控。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trend focus and dose across lots. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Slow drift needs long-term monitoring.","observation":"慢漂移需要長時間監控。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Slow drift needs long-term monitoring. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤跨批次的焦點與劑量趨勢」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「慢漂移需要長時間監控。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trend focus and dose across lots\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Slow drift needs long-term monitoring.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"慢漂移需要長時間監控。","textEn":"Slow drift needs long-term monitoring."},{"id":"a049-v8-22-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤跨批次的焦點與劑量趨勢」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trend focus and dose across lots\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["慢漂移需要長時間監控。","平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。"],"optionsEn":["Slow drift needs long-term monitoring.","An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Focus and dose are the same control variable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"慢漂移需要長時間監控。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"Slow drift needs long-term monitoring. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}},{"id":"a049-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-22"],"title":"將窗口結果傳入套刻與蝕刻審查","titleEn":"Pass window results into overlay and etch reviews","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin.","instruction":"將窗口結果傳入套刻與蝕刻審查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Pass window results into overlay and etch reviews. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin.","observation":"微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將窗口結果傳入套刻與蝕刻審查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Pass window results into overlay and etch reviews\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。","textEn":"Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin."},{"id":"a049-v8-23-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將窗口結果傳入套刻與蝕刻審查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Pass window results into overlay and etch reviews\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin.","Focus and dose are the same control variable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"微影窗口只是整合窗口的一部分。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"Lithographic margin is only part of integration margin. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}},{"id":"a049-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-duv","v8b-comp","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a049-v8-23"],"title":"交付包含條件與取樣範圍的控制計畫","titleEn":"Deliver controls with conditions and sampling scope","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Control plans need explicit applicability limits.","instruction":"交付包含條件與取樣範圍的控制計畫。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver controls with conditions and sampling scope. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Control plans need explicit applicability limits.","observation":"控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Control plans need explicit applicability limits. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付包含條件與取樣範圍的控制計畫」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver controls with conditions and sampling scope\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Control plans need explicit applicability limits.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a049-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。","textEn":"Control plans need explicit applicability limits."},{"id":"a049-v8-24-k2","title":"變異與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Variation and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","textEn":"Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付包含條件與取樣範圍的控制計畫」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver controls with conditions and sampling scope\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均線寬不變就表示控制正常。","焦距與劑量是完全相同的控制量。","控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged mean linewidth proves healthy control.","Focus and dose are the same control variable.","Control plans need explicit applicability limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制計畫需要清楚的適用範圍。 平均值合格不能保證整片晶圓或長時間穩定。","explanationEn":"Control plans need explicit applicability limits. Acceptable averages do not prove whole-wafer or long-term stability."}}]}]},{"id":"a050","title":"微影隨機缺陷分析","titleEn":"Lithographic stochastic-defect analysis","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究事件與機率、取樣與量測、來源分離、設計與接受；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: events and probability, sampling and metrology, source separation, design and acceptance. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology","v3-media-bc42a1134319"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["事件與機率","取樣與量測","來源分離","設計與接受"],"labelsEn":["Events and probability","Sampling and metrology","Source separation","Design and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"lithography","subcategoryTitle":"光阻、光罩與微影","subcategoryTitleEn":"Resists, masks and lithography","stages":[{"id":"a050-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"事件與機率","titleEn":"Events and probability","description":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","descriptionEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions.","steps":[{"id":"a050-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"區分線邊粗糙度與離散失敗事件","titleEn":"Distinguish line-edge roughness from discrete failures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics.","instruction":"區分線邊粗糙度與離散失敗事件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish line-edge roughness from discrete failures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics.","observation":"連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分線邊粗糙度與離散失敗事件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish line-edge roughness from discrete failures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。","textEn":"Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics."},{"id":"a050-v8-01-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分線邊粗糙度與離散失敗事件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish line-edge roughness from discrete failures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。"],"optionsEn":["Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續變異與罕見事件需要不同指標。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Continuous variation and rare failures need different metrics. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-01"],"title":"定義斷線、橋接與缺孔的判準","titleEn":"Define breaks, bridges and missing-hole criteria","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons.","instruction":"定義斷線、橋接與缺孔的判準。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define breaks, bridges and missing-hole criteria. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons.","observation":"分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義斷線、橋接與缺孔的判準」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define breaks, bridges and missing-hole criteria\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。","textEn":"Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons."},{"id":"a050-v8-02-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義斷線、橋接與缺孔的判準」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define breaks, bridges and missing-hole criteria\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。"],"optionsEn":["Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分類一致性是跨批次比較前提。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Consistent classification enables cross-lot comparisons. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-02"],"title":"以簡化泊松模型估算光子波動","titleEn":"Estimate photon fluctuations with a simple Poisson model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises.","instruction":"以簡化泊松模型估算光子波動。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate photon fluctuations with a simple Poisson model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises.","observation":"相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以簡化泊松模型估算光子波動」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate photon fluctuations with a simple Poisson model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。","textEn":"Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises."},{"id":"a050-v8-03-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以簡化泊松模型估算光子波動」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate photon fluctuations with a simple Poisson model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。"],"optionsEn":["Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相對波動隨平均事件數增加而下降。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Relative fluctuation decreases as mean event count rises. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-03"],"title":"列出泊松獨立性假設的限制","titleEn":"List limits of Poisson independence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions.","instruction":"列出泊松獨立性假設的限制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List limits of Poisson independence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions.","observation":"材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出泊松獨立性假設的限制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List limits of Poisson independence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。","textEn":"Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions."},{"id":"a050-v8-04-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出泊松獨立性假設的限制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List limits of Poisson independence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。"],"optionsEn":["Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料聚集與空間相關會破壞簡化假設。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Material clustering and spatial correlation violate simple assumptions. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-04"],"title":"分開單特徵失敗率與單位面積缺陷率","titleEn":"Separate per-feature probability from areal defect density","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同分母不能直接互換。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different denominators are not interchangeable.","instruction":"分開單特徵失敗率與單位面積缺陷率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「不同分母不能直接互換。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate per-feature probability from areal defect density. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different denominators are not interchangeable.","observation":"不同分母不能直接互換。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different denominators are not interchangeable. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開單特徵失敗率與單位面積缺陷率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同分母不能直接互換。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate per-feature probability from areal defect density\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different denominators are not interchangeable.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同分母不能直接互換。","textEn":"Different denominators are not interchangeable."},{"id":"a050-v8-05-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開單特徵失敗率與單位面積缺陷率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate per-feature probability from areal defect density\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","不同分母不能直接互換。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。"],"optionsEn":["Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","Different denominators are not interchangeable.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同分母不能直接互換。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Different denominators are not interchangeable. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-05"],"title":"畫出缺陷到電路失效的連結","titleEn":"Map defects into circuit failures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Not every defect causes the same functional consequence.","instruction":"畫出缺陷到電路失效的連結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map defects into circuit failures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Not every defect causes the same functional consequence.","observation":"不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Not every defect causes the same functional consequence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出缺陷到電路失效的連結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map defects into circuit failures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Not every defect causes the same functional consequence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。","textEn":"Not every defect causes the same functional consequence."},{"id":"a050-v8-06-k2","title":"事件與機率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Events and probability: principle and limits","text":"隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","textEn":"Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出缺陷到電路失效的連結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map defects into circuit failures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。"],"optionsEn":["Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Not every defect causes the same functional consequence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不是每個缺陷都造成相同功能後果。 隨機缺陷研究需定義事件、觀測機會與獨立性假設。","explanationEn":"Not every defect causes the same functional consequence. Stochastic-defect analysis requires events, opportunities and independence assumptions."}}]},{"id":"a050-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"取樣與量測","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology","description":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","descriptionEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions.","steps":[{"id":"a050-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-06"],"title":"計算零缺陷樣本的近似上限","titleEn":"Calculate an approximate upper bound after zero defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count.","instruction":"計算零缺陷樣本的近似上限。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設 N=100000 個獨立、同分布機會皆無缺陷。精確單側 95% 二項上限為 p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵，近似 3/N=3.0×10⁻⁵。若報告 p=0，便超出資料支持範圍。另說明漏檢與空間相關會破壞此計算的假設；此範例沒有實際晶圓良率數據。","instructionEn":"Calculate an approximate upper bound after zero defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): For N=100000 independent identically distributed opportunities with zero defects, the exact one-sided 95% binomial upper bound is p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵; 3/N approximates it as 3.0×10⁻⁵. Reporting p=0 exceeds the evidence. Missed detections and spatial correlation violate assumptions; the example contains no measured wafer-yield data.","observation":"在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n精確值與近似值需一致至約 0.15%，並列出至少一個假設。","observationEn":"For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nExact and approximate values should agree within about 0.15%; state at least one assumption.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算零缺陷樣本的近似上限」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：精確值與近似值需一致至約 0.15%，並列出至少一個假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate an approximate upper bound after zero defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Exact and approximate values should agree within about 0.15%; state at least one assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。","textEn":"For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count."},{"id":"a050-v8-07-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設 N=100000 個獨立、同分布機會皆無缺陷。精確單側 95% 二項上限為 p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵，近似 3/N=3.0×10⁻⁵。若報告 p=0，便超出資料支持範圍。另說明漏檢與空間相關會破壞此計算的假設；此範例沒有實際晶圓良率數據。","textEn":"For N=100000 independent identically distributed opportunities with zero defects, the exact one-sided 95% binomial upper bound is p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵; 3/N approximates it as 3.0×10⁻⁵. Reporting p=0 exceeds the evidence. Missed detections and spatial correlation violate assumptions; the example contains no measured wafer-yield data."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算零缺陷樣本的近似上限」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate an approximate upper bound after zero defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。"],"optionsEn":["For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Photon count alone determines every defect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在獨立事件假設下，95%上限約為3除以樣本數。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"For independent opportunities, the approximate 95% upper bound is 3 divided by sample count. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設 N=100000 個獨立、同分布機會皆無缺陷。精確單側 95% 二項上限為 p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵，近似 3/N=3.0×10⁻⁵。若報告 p=0，便超出資料支持範圍。另說明漏檢與空間相關會破壞此計算的假設；此範例沒有實際晶圓良率數據。","textEn":"For N=100000 independent identically distributed opportunities with zero defects, the exact one-sided 95% binomial upper bound is p=1-0.05^(1/N)=2.9957×10⁻⁵; 3/N approximates it as 3.0×10⁻⁵. Reporting p=0 exceeds the evidence. Missed detections and spatial correlation violate assumptions; the example contains no measured wafer-yield data.","check":"精確值與近似值需一致至約 0.15%，並列出至少一個假設。","checkEn":"Exact and approximate values should agree within about 0.15%; state at least one assumption."}},{"id":"a050-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-07"],"title":"比較兩組不等樣本數的缺陷率","titleEn":"Compare rates from unequal sample sizes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Raw counts alone cannot rank risk.","instruction":"比較兩組不等樣本數的缺陷率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare rates from unequal sample sizes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Raw counts alone cannot rank risk.","observation":"原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Raw counts alone cannot rank risk. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較兩組不等樣本數的缺陷率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare rates from unequal sample sizes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Raw counts alone cannot rank risk.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。","textEn":"Raw counts alone cannot rank risk."},{"id":"a050-v8-08-k2","title":"取樣與量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology: principle and limits","text":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較兩組不等樣本數的缺陷率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare rates from unequal sample sizes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。"],"optionsEn":["More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Raw counts alone cannot rank risk.","Photon count alone determines every defect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原始缺陷數不能直接代表風險高低。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"Raw counts alone cannot rank risk. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-08"],"title":"設計覆蓋不同晶圓區域的取樣","titleEn":"Sample across different wafer regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity.","instruction":"設計覆蓋不同晶圓區域的取樣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sample across different wafer regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity.","observation":"只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計覆蓋不同晶圓區域的取樣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sample across different wafer regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。","textEn":"Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity."},{"id":"a050-v8-09-k2","title":"取樣與量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology: principle and limits","text":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計覆蓋不同晶圓區域的取樣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sample across different wafer regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。"],"optionsEn":["More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Photon count alone determines every defect.","Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只抽中心會漏掉空間非均勻。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"Center-only sampling misses spatial nonuniformity. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-09"],"title":"估計檢查工具的漏檢比例","titleEn":"Estimate the inspection false-negative rate","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Observed rate can be lower than the true rate.","instruction":"估計檢查工具的漏檢比例。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate the inspection false-negative rate. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Observed rate can be lower than the true rate.","observation":"觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Observed rate can be lower than the true rate. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估計檢查工具的漏檢比例」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate the inspection false-negative rate\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Observed rate can be lower than the true rate.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。","textEn":"Observed rate can be lower than the true rate."},{"id":"a050-v8-10-k2","title":"取樣與量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology: principle and limits","text":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估計檢查工具的漏檢比例」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate the inspection false-negative rate\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。","增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。"],"optionsEn":["Observed rate can be lower than the true rate.","More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Photon count alone determines every defect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"觀察缺陷率可能低於真實缺陷率。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"Observed rate can be lower than the true rate. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-10"],"title":"比較人工複查與自動分類一致性","titleEn":"Compare manual review with automated classification","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：分類器偏差會影響統計。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Classifier bias affects statistics.","instruction":"比較人工複查與自動分類一致性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「分類器偏差會影響統計。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare manual review with automated classification. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Classifier bias affects statistics.","observation":"分類器偏差會影響統計。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Classifier bias affects statistics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較人工複查與自動分類一致性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「分類器偏差會影響統計。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare manual review with automated classification\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Classifier bias affects statistics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"分類器偏差會影響統計。","textEn":"Classifier bias affects statistics."},{"id":"a050-v8-11-k2","title":"取樣與量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology: principle and limits","text":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較人工複查與自動分類一致性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare manual review with automated classification\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","分類器偏差會影響統計。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。"],"optionsEn":["More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Classifier bias affects statistics.","Photon count alone determines every defect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分類器偏差會影響統計。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"Classifier bias affects statistics. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}},{"id":"a050-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-11"],"title":"把量測噪聲從粗糙度中區分","titleEn":"Distinguish metrology noise from roughness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness.","instruction":"把量測噪聲從粗糙度中區分。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish metrology noise from roughness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness.","observation":"量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把量測噪聲從粗糙度中區分」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish metrology noise from roughness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。","textEn":"Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness."},{"id":"a050-v8-12-k2","title":"取樣與量測的原理與限制","titleEn":"Sampling and metrology: principle and limits","text":"缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","textEn":"Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把量測噪聲從粗糙度中區分」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish metrology noise from roughness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["增加放大倍率就不需要增加取樣面積。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["More magnification removes the need for larger sampled area.","Photon count alone determines every defect.","Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測噪聲可提高表觀粗糙度。 缺陷檢查的靈敏度與檢查面積會限制統計結論。","explanationEn":"Measurement noise can inflate apparent roughness. Inspection sensitivity and inspected area limit statistical conclusions."}}]},{"id":"a050-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"來源分離","titleEn":"Source separation","description":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","descriptionEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution.","steps":[{"id":"a050-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-12"],"title":"以相同線寬比較不同劑量條件","titleEn":"Compare doses at matched linewidth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometry changes confound dose-only effects.","instruction":"以相同線寬比較不同劑量條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare doses at matched linewidth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometry changes confound dose-only effects.","observation":"幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometry changes confound dose-only effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以相同線寬比較不同劑量條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare doses at matched linewidth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometry changes confound dose-only effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。","textEn":"Geometry changes confound dose-only effects."},{"id":"a050-v8-13-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以相同線寬比較不同劑量條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare doses at matched linewidth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。"],"optionsEn":["Geometry changes confound dose-only effects.","Photon count alone determines every defect.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何改變會混淆純劑量效應。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"Geometry changes confound dose-only effects. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}},{"id":"a050-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-13"],"title":"分別繪製橋接與斷線的趨勢","titleEn":"Plot bridge and break trends separately","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They can respond oppositely to process changes.","instruction":"分別繪製橋接與斷線的趨勢。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plot bridge and break trends separately. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: They can respond oppositely to process changes.","observation":"兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They can respond oppositely to process changes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分別繪製橋接與斷線的趨勢」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plot bridge and break trends separately\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They can respond oppositely to process changes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。","textEn":"They can respond oppositely to process changes."},{"id":"a050-v8-14-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分別繪製橋接與斷線的趨勢」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plot bridge and break trends separately\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。"],"optionsEn":["Photon count alone determines every defect.","They can respond oppositely to process changes.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩者可能對製程調整反向回應。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"They can respond oppositely to process changes. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}},{"id":"a050-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-14"],"title":"比較光阻、底層與蝕刻三個因素","titleEn":"Compare resist, underlayer and etch factors","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources.","instruction":"比較光阻、底層與蝕刻三個因素。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare resist, underlayer and etch factors. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources.","observation":"多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光阻、底層與蝕刻三個因素」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare resist, underlayer and etch factors\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。","textEn":"Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources."},{"id":"a050-v8-15-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光阻、底層與蝕刻三個因素」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare resist, underlayer and etch factors\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。"],"optionsEn":["Photon count alone determines every defect.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多因素對照有助於分離整合來源。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"Multifactor controls help isolate integration sources. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}},{"id":"a050-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-15"],"title":"檢查缺陷是否以光罩位置重複","titleEn":"Check whether defects repeat at mask coordinates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins.","instruction":"檢查缺陷是否以光罩位置重複。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check whether defects repeat at mask coordinates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins.","observation":"重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查缺陷是否以光罩位置重複」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check whether defects repeat at mask coordinates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。","textEn":"Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins."},{"id":"a050-v8-16-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查缺陷是否以光罩位置重複」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check whether defects repeat at mask coordinates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。","所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。"],"optionsEn":["Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins.","Photon count alone determines every defect.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複缺陷可能屬於系統來源。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"Repeating defects can indicate systematic origins. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}},{"id":"a050-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-16"],"title":"量測缺陷的空間自相關","titleEn":"Measure spatial autocorrelation of defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Clustering reduces effective independent sample size.","instruction":"量測缺陷的空間自相關。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure spatial autocorrelation of defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Clustering reduces effective independent sample size.","observation":"群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Clustering reduces effective independent sample size. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測缺陷的空間自相關」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure spatial autocorrelation of defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Clustering reduces effective independent sample size.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。","textEn":"Clustering reduces effective independent sample size."},{"id":"a050-v8-17-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測缺陷的空間自相關」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure spatial autocorrelation of defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。"],"optionsEn":["Photon count alone determines every defect.","Clustering reduces effective independent sample size.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield."],"answer":1,"explanation":"群聚會減少有效獨立樣本數。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"Clustering reduces effective independent sample size. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}},{"id":"a050-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-17"],"title":"比較顯影後與蝕刻後的缺陷演化","titleEn":"Compare defect evolution through etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Etching can amplify, remove or create defects.","instruction":"比較顯影後與蝕刻後的缺陷演化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare defect evolution through etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Etching can amplify, remove or create defects.","observation":"蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Etching can amplify, remove or create defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Photon count alone determines every defect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較顯影後與蝕刻後的缺陷演化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare defect evolution through etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Etching can amplify, remove or create defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。","textEn":"Etching can amplify, remove or create defects."},{"id":"a050-v8-18-k2","title":"來源分離的原理與限制","titleEn":"Source separation: principle and limits","text":"光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","textEn":"Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較顯影後與蝕刻後的缺陷演化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare defect evolution through etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有缺陷都只由光子數決定。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Photon count alone determines every defect.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Etching can amplify, remove or create defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"蝕刻可放大、移除或新增缺陷。 光子、材料與圖形變異會共同影響缺陷，不能單一歸因。","explanationEn":"Etching can amplify, remove or create defects. Photon, material and pattern variation jointly affect defects and preclude simple attribution."}}]},{"id":"a050-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"設計與接受","titleEn":"Design and acceptance","description":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","descriptionEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures.","steps":[{"id":"a050-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-18"],"title":"用蛇形線連結斷線與開路","titleEn":"Link line breaks to opens using serpentine structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology.","instruction":"用蛇形線連結斷線與開路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Link line breaks to opens using serpentine structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology.","observation":"電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用蛇形線連結斷線與開路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Link line breaks to opens using serpentine structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。","textEn":"Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology."},{"id":"a050-v8-19-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用蛇形線連結斷線與開路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Link line breaks to opens using serpentine structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性載具驗證形貌的功能意義。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Electrical vehicles test the functional meaning of morphology. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}},{"id":"a050-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-19"],"title":"用叉狀結構連結橋接與漏電","titleEn":"Link bridges to leakage using fork structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：漏電位置需與影像座標對應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Leakage needs registration to image coordinates.","instruction":"用叉狀結構連結橋接與漏電。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「漏電位置需與影像座標對應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Link bridges to leakage using fork structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Leakage needs registration to image coordinates.","observation":"漏電位置需與影像座標對應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Leakage needs registration to image coordinates. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用叉狀結構連結橋接與漏電」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「漏電位置需與影像座標對應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Link bridges to leakage using fork structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Leakage needs registration to image coordinates.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"漏電位置需與影像座標對應。","textEn":"Leakage needs registration to image coordinates."},{"id":"a050-v8-20-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用叉狀結構連結橋接與漏電」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Link bridges to leakage using fork structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","漏電位置需與影像座標對應。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。"],"optionsEn":["Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Leakage needs registration to image coordinates.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏電位置需與影像座標對應。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Leakage needs registration to image coordinates. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}},{"id":"a050-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-20"],"title":"以簡化獨立模型估算多特徵良率","titleEn":"Estimate many-feature yield with an independent model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events.","instruction":"以簡化獨立模型估算多特徵良率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate many-feature yield with an independent model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events.","observation":"Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以簡化獨立模型估算多特徵良率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate many-feature yield with an independent model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。","textEn":"Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events."},{"id":"a050-v8-21-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以簡化獨立模型估算多特徵良率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate many-feature yield with an independent model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。"],"optionsEn":["Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Y=(1-p)^N 依賴獨立且同分布假設。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Y=(1-p)^N assumes independent identically distributed events. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}},{"id":"a050-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-21"],"title":"比較模型良率與實測載具良率","titleEn":"Compare modeled yield with measured vehicle yield","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures.","instruction":"比較模型良率與實測載具良率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare modeled yield with measured vehicle yield. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures.","observation":"差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較模型良率與實測載具良率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare modeled yield with measured vehicle yield\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。","textEn":"Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures."},{"id":"a050-v8-22-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較模型良率與實測載具良率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare modeled yield with measured vehicle yield\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。","影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。"],"optionsEn":["Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures.","Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"差異可能顯示相關性或未分類失敗。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Differences can indicate correlation or unclassified failures. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}},{"id":"a050-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-22"],"title":"設計兼顧劑量與吞吐的接受條件","titleEn":"Define acceptance balancing dose and throughput","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost.","instruction":"設計兼顧劑量與吞吐的接受條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define acceptance balancing dose and throughput. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost.","observation":"提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計兼顧劑量與吞吐的接受條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define acceptance balancing dose and throughput\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。","textEn":"Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost."},{"id":"a050-v8-23-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計兼顧劑量與吞吐的接受條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define acceptance balancing dose and throughput\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。"],"optionsEn":["Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"提高劑量的收益需同時評估成本。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Dose benefits must be evaluated alongside cost. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}},{"id":"a050-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-stochastic","v8b-euvyield","v8b-pattern","v8b-metrology"],"prerequisiteIds":["a050-v8-23"],"title":"交付帶信賴區間與限制的缺陷報告","titleEn":"Deliver a defect report with confidence intervals and limits","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison.","instruction":"交付帶信賴區間與限制的缺陷報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a defect report with confidence intervals and limits. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison.","observation":"明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付帶信賴區間與限制的缺陷報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a defect report with confidence intervals and limits\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a050-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。","textEn":"Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison."},{"id":"a050-v8-24-k2","title":"設計與接受的原理與限制","titleEn":"Design and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","textEn":"Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付帶信賴區間與限制的缺陷報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a defect report with confidence intervals and limits\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["影像缺陷率可以直接等同整顆晶片良率。","零觀察缺陷就表示缺陷率為零。","明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。"],"optionsEn":["Image defect rate directly equals whole-chip yield.","Zero observed defects means zero defect probability.","Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明確分母與不確定度才使結果可比較。 研究結果必須連結實際圖形與電性失效。","explanationEn":"Explicit denominators and uncertainty enable comparison. Research findings must link to actual patterns and electrical failures."}}]}]},{"id":"a051","title":"反應式離子蝕刻","titleEn":"Reactive-ion etching","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究電漿與表面、輪廓與選擇性、端點與均勻性、損傷與轉移；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: plasma and surface, profile and selectivity, endpoint and uniformity, damage and transfer. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電漿與表面","輪廓與選擇性","端點與均勻性","損傷與轉移"],"labelsEn":["Plasma and surface","Profile and selectivity","Endpoint and uniformity","Damage and transfer"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a051-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"電漿與表面","titleEn":"Plasma and surface","description":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","descriptionEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes.","steps":[{"id":"a051-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出電子、離子與中性自由基","titleEn":"Draw electrons, ions and neutral radicals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Particle populations have different energies and directionality.","instruction":"畫出電子、離子與中性自由基。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw electrons, ions and neutral radicals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Particle populations have different energies and directionality.","observation":"粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Particle populations have different energies and directionality. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出電子、離子與中性自由基」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw electrons, ions and neutral radicals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Particle populations have different energies and directionality.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。","textEn":"Particle populations have different energies and directionality."},{"id":"a051-v8-01-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出電子、離子與中性自由基」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw electrons, ions and neutral radicals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Particle populations have different energies and directionality.","RIE is purely physical bombardment.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"粒子族群具有不同能量與方向性。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Particle populations have different energies and directionality. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}},{"id":"a051-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-01"],"title":"分開體電漿與基板鞘層","titleEn":"Separate bulk plasma from substrate sheath","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鞘層電場會加速離子。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sheath fields accelerate ions.","instruction":"分開體電漿與基板鞘層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「鞘層電場會加速離子。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate bulk plasma from substrate sheath. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sheath fields accelerate ions.","observation":"鞘層電場會加速離子。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sheath fields accelerate ions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開體電漿與基板鞘層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鞘層電場會加速離子。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate bulk plasma from substrate sheath\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sheath fields accelerate ions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鞘層電場會加速離子。","textEn":"Sheath fields accelerate ions."},{"id":"a051-v8-02-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開體電漿與基板鞘層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate bulk plasma from substrate sheath\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","鞘層電場會加速離子。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["RIE is purely physical bombardment.","Sheath fields accelerate ions.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鞘層電場會加速離子。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Sheath fields accelerate ions. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}},{"id":"a051-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-02"],"title":"比較化學蝕刻與物理濺射","titleEn":"Compare chemical etching with physical sputtering","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可揮發產物有利於材料移除。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Volatile products facilitate material removal.","instruction":"比較化學蝕刻與物理濺射。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「可揮發產物有利於材料移除。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare chemical etching with physical sputtering. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Volatile products facilitate material removal.","observation":"可揮發產物有利於材料移除。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Volatile products facilitate material removal. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較化學蝕刻與物理濺射」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可揮發產物有利於材料移除。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare chemical etching with physical sputtering\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Volatile products facilitate material removal.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可揮發產物有利於材料移除。","textEn":"Volatile products facilitate material removal."},{"id":"a051-v8-03-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較化學蝕刻與物理濺射」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare chemical etching with physical sputtering\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","可揮發產物有利於材料移除。"],"optionsEn":["RIE is purely physical bombardment.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Volatile products facilitate material removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可揮發產物有利於材料移除。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Volatile products facilitate material removal. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}},{"id":"a051-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-03"],"title":"繪製離子入射方向分布","titleEn":"Sketch ion-incidence angular distributions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：角度分布影響側壁與底部。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms.","instruction":"繪製離子入射方向分布。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「角度分布影響側壁與底部。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch ion-incidence angular distributions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms.","observation":"角度分布影響側壁與底部。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製離子入射方向分布」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「角度分布影響側壁與底部。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch ion-incidence angular distributions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"角度分布影響側壁與底部。","textEn":"Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms."},{"id":"a051-v8-04-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製離子入射方向分布」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch ion-incidence angular distributions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["角度分布影響側壁與底部。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms.","RIE is purely physical bombardment.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"角度分布影響側壁與底部。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Angular distributions affect sidewalls and bottoms. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}},{"id":"a051-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-04"],"title":"標記掩膜、目標膜與停止層","titleEn":"Mark mask, target film and stop layer","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：各材料均可能被製程消耗。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Every material can be consumed by the process.","instruction":"標記掩膜、目標膜與停止層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「各材料均可能被製程消耗。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark mask, target film and stop layer. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Every material can be consumed by the process.","observation":"各材料均可能被製程消耗。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Every material can be consumed by the process. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記掩膜、目標膜與停止層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「各材料均可能被製程消耗。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark mask, target film and stop layer\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Every material can be consumed by the process.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"各材料均可能被製程消耗。","textEn":"Every material can be consumed by the process."},{"id":"a051-v8-05-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記掩膜、目標膜與停止層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark mask, target film and stop layer\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","各材料均可能被製程消耗。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["RIE is purely physical bombardment.","Every material can be consumed by the process.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各材料均可能被製程消耗。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Every material can be consumed by the process. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}},{"id":"a051-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-05"],"title":"建立不涉及實際機台配方的參數地圖","titleEn":"Build a parameter map without operating recipes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Power, pressure and temperature are coupled.","instruction":"建立不涉及實際機台配方的參數地圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a parameter map without operating recipes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Power, pressure and temperature are coupled.","observation":"功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Power, pressure and temperature are coupled. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"RIE is purely physical bombardment.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立不涉及實際機台配方的參數地圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a parameter map without operating recipes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Power, pressure and temperature are coupled.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。","textEn":"Power, pressure and temperature are coupled."},{"id":"a051-v8-06-k2","title":"電漿與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and surface: principle and limits","text":"RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","textEn":"Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立不涉及實際機台配方的參數地圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a parameter map without operating recipes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。"],"optionsEn":["RIE is purely physical bombardment.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Power, pressure and temperature are coupled."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功率、壓力與溫度彼此耦合。 RIE 的化學反應與離子轟擊共同決定蝕刻結果。","explanationEn":"Power, pressure and temperature are coupled. Chemical reactions and ion bombardment jointly determine RIE outcomes."}}]},{"id":"a051-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"輪廓與選擇性","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity","description":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","descriptionEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone.","steps":[{"id":"a051-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-06"],"title":"由蝕刻前後厚度計算平均速率","titleEn":"Calculate mean rate from thickness change","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平均速率需註明實際作用時間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mean rate needs the effective process time.","instruction":"由蝕刻前後厚度計算平均速率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「平均速率需註明實際作用時間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Calculate mean rate from thickness change. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mean rate needs the effective process time.","observation":"平均速率需註明實際作用時間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mean rate needs the effective process time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由蝕刻前後厚度計算平均速率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平均速率需註明實際作用時間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate mean rate from thickness change\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mean rate needs the effective process time.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平均速率需註明實際作用時間。","textEn":"Mean rate needs the effective process time."},{"id":"a051-v8-07-k2","title":"輪廓與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","textEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由蝕刻前後厚度計算平均速率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate mean rate from thickness change\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均速率需註明實際作用時間。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。"],"optionsEn":["Mean rate needs the effective process time.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均速率需註明實際作用時間。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Mean rate needs the effective process time. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}},{"id":"a051-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-07"],"title":"以兩材料速率計算選擇比","titleEn":"Calculate selectivity from two material rates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：選擇比依材料對與條件定義。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions.","instruction":"以兩材料速率計算選擇比。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「選擇比依材料對與條件定義。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設 20 s 內目標膜減少 100 nm、掩膜減少 10 nm。速率分別為 5.0 與 0.50 nm/s，選擇比為 10。若保持同速率再延長 4 s，目標膜多移除 20 nm、掩膜多損失 2 nm。說明此線性外推只適用於本假想穩態區間，不能忽略停止層與負載改變。","instructionEn":"Calculate selectivity from two material rates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume target loss of 100 nm and mask loss of 10 nm in 20 s. Rates are 5.0 and 0.50 nm/s, giving selectivity 10. Four extra seconds at the same rates remove 20 nm more target and 2 nm more mask. This linear extrapolation applies only to the hypothetical steady interval and cannot ignore stop layers or loading changes.","observation":"選擇比依材料對與條件定義。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 5.0、0.50、10、20 nm 與 2 nm，分清速率和選擇比。","observationEn":"Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 5.0, 0.50, 10, 20 nm and 2 nm, distinguishing rates from selectivity.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以兩材料速率計算選擇比」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「選擇比依材料對與條件定義。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 5.0、0.50、10、20 nm 與 2 nm，分清速率和選擇比。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate selectivity from two material rates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 5.0, 0.50, 10, 20 nm and 2 nm, distinguishing rates from selectivity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"選擇比依材料對與條件定義。","textEn":"Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions."},{"id":"a051-v8-08-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設 20 s 內目標膜減少 100 nm、掩膜減少 10 nm。速率分別為 5.0 與 0.50 nm/s，選擇比為 10。若保持同速率再延長 4 s，目標膜多移除 20 nm、掩膜多損失 2 nm。說明此線性外推只適用於本假想穩態區間，不能忽略停止層與負載改變。","textEn":"Assume target loss of 100 nm and mask loss of 10 nm in 20 s. Rates are 5.0 and 0.50 nm/s, giving selectivity 10. Four extra seconds at the same rates remove 20 nm more target and 2 nm more mask. This linear extrapolation applies only to the hypothetical steady interval and cannot ignore stop layers or loading changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以兩材料速率計算選擇比」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate selectivity from two material rates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","選擇比依材料對與條件定義。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。"],"optionsEn":["The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching."],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇比依材料對與條件定義。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Selectivity is defined for a material pair and conditions. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設 20 s 內目標膜減少 100 nm、掩膜減少 10 nm。速率分別為 5.0 與 0.50 nm/s，選擇比為 10。若保持同速率再延長 4 s，目標膜多移除 20 nm、掩膜多損失 2 nm。說明此線性外推只適用於本假想穩態區間，不能忽略停止層與負載改變。","textEn":"Assume target loss of 100 nm and mask loss of 10 nm in 20 s. Rates are 5.0 and 0.50 nm/s, giving selectivity 10. Four extra seconds at the same rates remove 20 nm more target and 2 nm more mask. This linear extrapolation applies only to the hypothetical steady interval and cannot ignore stop layers or loading changes.","check":"交付 5.0、0.50、10、20 nm 與 2 nm，分清速率和選擇比。","checkEn":"Report 5.0, 0.50, 10, 20 nm and 2 nm, distinguishing rates from selectivity."}},{"id":"a051-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-08"],"title":"比較垂直與橫向蝕刻量","titleEn":"Compare vertical and lateral removal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：方向性不能只由深度判斷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Depth alone does not establish anisotropy.","instruction":"比較垂直與橫向蝕刻量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「方向性不能只由深度判斷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare vertical and lateral removal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Depth alone does not establish anisotropy.","observation":"方向性不能只由深度判斷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Depth alone does not establish anisotropy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較垂直與橫向蝕刻量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「方向性不能只由深度判斷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare vertical and lateral removal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Depth alone does not establish anisotropy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"方向性不能只由深度判斷。","textEn":"Depth alone does not establish anisotropy."},{"id":"a051-v8-09-k2","title":"輪廓與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","textEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較垂直與橫向蝕刻量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare vertical and lateral removal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。","方向性不能只由深度判斷。"],"optionsEn":["The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.","Depth alone does not establish anisotropy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"方向性不能只由深度判斷。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Depth alone does not establish anisotropy. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}},{"id":"a051-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-09"],"title":"檢查光阻消耗與硬罩剩餘","titleEn":"Check resist consumption and hard-mask remainder","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：掩膜預算會限制可達深度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mask budget limits achievable depth.","instruction":"檢查光阻消耗與硬罩剩餘。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「掩膜預算會限制可達深度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check resist consumption and hard-mask remainder. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mask budget limits achievable depth.","observation":"掩膜預算會限制可達深度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mask budget limits achievable depth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查光阻消耗與硬罩剩餘」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「掩膜預算會限制可達深度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check resist consumption and hard-mask remainder\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mask budget limits achievable depth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"掩膜預算會限制可達深度。","textEn":"Mask budget limits achievable depth."},{"id":"a051-v8-10-k2","title":"輪廓與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","textEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查光阻消耗與硬罩剩餘」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check resist consumption and hard-mask remainder\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["掩膜預算會限制可達深度。","蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。"],"optionsEn":["Mask budget limits achievable depth.","The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching."],"answer":0,"explanation":"掩膜預算會限制可達深度。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Mask budget limits achievable depth. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}},{"id":"a051-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-10"],"title":"比較密集與孤立圖形速率","titleEn":"Compare dense and isolated pattern rates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部負載會改變反應物供應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local loading changes reactant supply.","instruction":"比較密集與孤立圖形速率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部負載會改變反應物供應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dense and isolated pattern rates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local loading changes reactant supply.","observation":"局部負載會改變反應物供應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local loading changes reactant supply. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較密集與孤立圖形速率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部負載會改變反應物供應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dense and isolated pattern rates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local loading changes reactant supply.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部負載會改變反應物供應。","textEn":"Local loading changes reactant supply."},{"id":"a051-v8-11-k2","title":"輪廓與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","textEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較密集與孤立圖形速率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dense and isolated pattern rates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","局部負載會改變反應物供應。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。"],"optionsEn":["The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Local loading changes reactant supply.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部負載會改變反應物供應。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Local loading changes reactant supply. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}},{"id":"a051-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-11"],"title":"辨識側壁聚合物與底部殘留","titleEn":"Distinguish sidewall polymer from bottom residue","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue.","instruction":"辨識側壁聚合物與底部殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish sidewall polymer from bottom residue. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue.","observation":"有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「辨識側壁聚合物與底部殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish sidewall polymer from bottom residue\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。","textEn":"Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue."},{"id":"a051-v8-12-k2","title":"輪廓與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","textEn":"Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「辨識側壁聚合物與底部殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish sidewall polymer from bottom residue\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻最快就一定具有最好選擇性。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。","有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。"],"optionsEn":["The fastest etch necessarily has the best selectivity.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.","Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"有益鈍化與有害殘留需要分辨。 速率、方向性與選擇性是不同指標，不能以單一速率排名。","explanationEn":"Useful passivation must be distinguished from harmful residue. Rate, directionality and selectivity are distinct and cannot be ranked by rate alone."}}]},{"id":"a051-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"端點與均勻性","titleEn":"Endpoint and uniformity","description":"電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","descriptionEn":"Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness.","steps":[{"id":"a051-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-12"],"title":"畫出 OES 訊號與層間界面","titleEn":"Relate OES signals to layer interfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：發光強度不是直接膜厚。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Emission intensity is not direct thickness.","instruction":"畫出 OES 訊號與層間界面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「發光強度不是直接膜厚。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate OES signals to layer interfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Emission intensity is not direct thickness.","observation":"發光強度不是直接膜厚。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Emission intensity is not direct thickness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出 OES 訊號與層間界面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「發光強度不是直接膜厚。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate OES signals to layer interfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Emission intensity is not direct thickness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"發光強度不是直接膜厚。","textEn":"Emission intensity is not direct thickness."},{"id":"a051-v8-13-k2","title":"端點與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","textEn":"Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出 OES 訊號與層間界面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate OES signals to layer interfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光強度不是直接膜厚。","亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。","側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Emission intensity is not direct thickness.","Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.","Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"發光強度不是直接膜厚。 電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","explanationEn":"Emission intensity is not direct thickness. Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}},{"id":"a051-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-13"],"title":"比較時間停止與端點停止","titleEn":"Compare timed and endpoint-controlled stopping","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets.","instruction":"比較時間停止與端點停止。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare timed and endpoint-controlled stopping. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets.","observation":"端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較時間停止與端點停止」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare timed and endpoint-controlled stopping\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。","textEn":"Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets."},{"id":"a051-v8-14-k2","title":"端點與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","textEn":"Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較時間停止與端點停止」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare timed and endpoint-controlled stopping\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。","端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。","側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.","Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets.","Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"端點控制仍需延遲與過蝕刻預算。 電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","explanationEn":"Endpoint control still needs latency and overetch budgets. Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}},{"id":"a051-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-14"],"title":"以深度地圖檢查晶圓均勻性","titleEn":"Check wafer uniformity using depth maps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單點端點不能保證全片同時完成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One endpoint does not guarantee simultaneous wafer completion.","instruction":"以深度地圖檢查晶圓均勻性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「單點端點不能保證全片同時完成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check wafer uniformity using depth maps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: One endpoint does not guarantee simultaneous wafer completion.","observation":"單點端點不能保證全片同時完成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One endpoint does not guarantee simultaneous wafer completion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \