plicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation.","observation":"基板溫度改變反應與鈍化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立晶圓背面熱接觸的誤差鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「基板溫度改變反應與鈍化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace backside thermal-contact errors\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"基板溫度改變反應與鈍化。","textEn":"Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation."},{"id":"a051-v8-18-k2","title":"端點與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","textEn":"Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立晶圓背面熱接觸的誤差鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace backside thermal-contact errors\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["亮度下降一定代表所有區域已蝕刻完成。","側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","基板溫度改變反應與鈍化。"],"optionsEn":["Falling brightness proves every region has finished etching.","Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基板溫度改變反應與鈍化。 電漿端點是間接訊號，需對應實際剩餘膜厚。","explanationEn":"Substrate temperature changes reaction and passivation. Plasma endpoint is an indirect signal requiring correlation with remaining thickness."}}]},{"id":"a051-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"損傷與轉移","titleEn":"Damage and transfer","description":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","descriptionEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks.","steps":[{"id":"a051-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-18"],"title":"檢查微溝槽與底部角落","titleEn":"Inspect microtrenching and bottom corners","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies.","instruction":"檢查微溝槽與底部角落。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect microtrenching and bottom corners. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies.","observation":"局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查微溝槽與底部角落」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect microtrenching and bottom corners\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。","textEn":"Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies."},{"id":"a051-v8-19-k2","title":"損傷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Damage and transfer: principle and limits","text":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查微溝槽與底部角落」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect microtrenching and bottom corners\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。","側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。"],"optionsEn":["Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies.","Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","RIE is purely physical bombardment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部離子軌跡會形成輪廓異常。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"Local ion trajectories can produce profile anomalies. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}},{"id":"a051-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-19"],"title":"比較充電前後的元件電性","titleEn":"Compare device electrical behavior after charging exposure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces.","instruction":"比較充電前後的元件電性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare device electrical behavior after charging exposure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces.","observation":"電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較充電前後的元件電性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare device electrical behavior after charging exposure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。","textEn":"Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces."},{"id":"a051-v8-20-k2","title":"損傷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Damage and transfer: principle and limits","text":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較充電前後的元件電性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare device electrical behavior after charging exposure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。"],"optionsEn":["Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces.","RIE is purely physical bombardment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電漿可造成介電層或介面損傷。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"Plasma can damage dielectrics or interfaces. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}},{"id":"a051-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ri